===============\n\n  5D-TimeBank is an additional command for AmiExpress,\n  it allows saving and restoring daily download bytes\n  and minutes of time for every user.\n\n@endnode\n@node ChildDoc2 "Requirements"\n\n  5D-TimeBank - Requirements\n  ==========================\n\n  o  an Amiga (or compatible - DRACO)\n  o  an AmiExpress-compatible BBS-program\n\n@endnode\n@node ChildDoc3 "Installation"\n\n  5D-TimeBank - Installation (for AmiExpress)\n  ===========================================\n\n  Simply copy the directories in this archive into your bbs-\n  directory.\n\n@endnode\n@node ChildDoc4 "History"\n\n  5D-TimeBank - History\n  =====================\n\n  v0.01 - [RELEASE I]\n\n@endnode\n@node ChildDoc5 "Greetings"\n\n  Greetings\n  =========\n\n  The Addict - Airworx - Celator - Conan&Newton\n  Cyber Master - Deathknight - Enzo - Hydra\n  Gilthanas - Lealand Gount - Mad Doc - Mad Force\n  Mad Man - Maverick - MouseBuster - Muad''Dib\n  Nero - Nors - Playmate - R/\\! - Rainmain\n  Rebel MC - Rush - Scarface - Snow - Steel\n  Thunder - Webster - Whiz!\n\n@endnode\n@node ChildDoc6 "How to contact 5D"\n\n  You can write a message to ''SvEN tHE CREAToR'' at the following boards:\n\n  o  Digital Suicide\n  o  Warez Unlimited\n  o  World of Elite\n\n  ... and several more\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',11057,1,0,NULL,NULL,'5d_tb001','scan',1780048351);
