 "5D-ZippySearch Installation"\nCopy all files which are in the archive bbs directory\nto your bbs directory.\n\nContents of archive:\n===================\n\nBBS/\n    Commands/\n        BBSCmd/\n            Z.info\n    Doors/\n        5D-ZippySearch/\n            5D-ZippySearch\n            5D-ZippySearch.info\n            5D-ZippySearch.Guide\n\n===================\n\n@endnode\n@node Greetings "5D-ZippySearch Greetings"\nGreetings go to:\n\n           Celator ........... Thank you for helping me with /X!\n           ByteAndi ............ For helping me to learn coding!\n           Prophet .................... For being a nice friend!\n           Snow ...................... Sing mehr lieder, leader!\n           Airworx ................. Continue work as Co Leader!\n           Delta-X ................. When you will merry Murdoc?\n           Strider ........ We should spread our standard again!\n\nSorry to all people I forgot but as you know my brain isn''t so well! hehe\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',19303,4,1,'Z','Doors/5D-ZippySearch','5d_zs001','scan',1780048358);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('5d_zs002','5D!ZS002.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/5D!ZS002.LHA','5D-ZippySearch','XIM','5D-ZippySearch',NULL,'sTc','5D','\  .........             ____      / \ :::::      ________  _\_ _|___ / \:::::..... \____   \_|   \__  \_',replace('  ____________________________________\n  \  .........             ____      /\n   \ :::::      ________  _\_ _|___ /\n    \:::::..... \____   \_|   \__  \_\n     \     :::::    |    ||    |    |\n     ::::: :::::    |    ||    |    |\n oS! ::::::::::''    |____||____|____|pR!De\n....... \ 5th dYNASTY pRESENTS / .........\n:                                      /X:\n:  5D-ZippySearch II v0.02 ©1995 by sTc  :\n:........................................:\n','\n',char(10)),'reference-board.txt',replace(replace('              W h e r e   t h e   w a r e z   c o m e   f r o m\r\n                                               __                /\_____:\r\n__/\__________________________________________|  \______________/  \    |__\r\n\_   ___________  _______ ________  \__   ___ |   _______  _______  \_  l  \\r\n__\____  \    _l   \    |  \     |___/     |  !    \   _l   \   _| __/\____ \_\r\n\_____    \___\     \___|   \___ !   \__   |_____   \__\     \__\    \____   /\r\n -mNT\_____/---\_____/--l____/-\______/\   |----\____/--\_____/--\____/--\__/\r\n                                        \__|\r\n\r\n- -- --> F A i R L i G H T   S W E D i S H   H E A D Q U A R T E R S <-- -- -\r\n\r\n           reference-board is back 2017 after more than 20 years in coma!\r\n\r\n                        Running on AmiExpress TelNet\r\n\r\n                    Connect to: reference-board.zapto.org:1541\r\n\r\n                    or: www.brysk.se/reference-board/index.htm\r\n               \n              UPLOAD DATE: 01-04-18  TIME: 18:59:49  ON NODE: 1\n','\r',char(13)),'\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',12748,2,1,'Z','Doors/5D-ZippySearch','5d_zs002','scan',1780048351);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('5d_zs008','5D!ZS008.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/5D!ZS008.LHA','5D-ZippySearch','XIM','5D-ZippySearch',NULL,'sTc/5D','5D','__5TH|_    |                  (/X-Tool) __\   __     |YNASTY _\     \|     |_ ____ ______ ___',replace('         ._____.\n    __5TH|_    |                  (/X-Tool)\n  __\   __     |YNASTY\n _\     \|     |_ ____ ______ ___\n \_\     \     |____ _______ _____ PRESENTS\n    \__________|\n 5D-ZippySearch II v0.08 (C)1996 by sTc/5D\n \n    Very fast, virtual string entering,\n    viewing, tagging, low memory usage.\n \n','\n',char(10)),'5D-ZippySearch.guide',replace('@database 5D-ZippySearch Documentation\n\nCopyright ©1996 sTc\n\n@remark $VER: (April 8 1996, 0:00)\n@remark AmigaGuide database for the 5D-ZippySearch Documentation\n\n@node MAIN "5D-ZippySearch Documentation"\n       ._____.\n  __5TH|_    |    ._____. ___________ ________. _______ ___.           ._____.\n__\\   __     |____|_    |_\\   _    ___\\____   |_\\  ___/__  |___    ____|_    |\n\\     \\|    _/     /    |     /    \\     _    |\\_____   /  ___/___/     /    |\n \\     \\    \\     /_    |____/    / \\    \\    |    /   /   \\     \\     /_    |\n  \\__________\\_____     |   /____/   \\________|_______/|__________\\_____     |\n                  |_____|pHS!                                          |_____|\n\n                                                     ... No Fear of Fun!\n\n    5D-ZippySearch.Guide - Contents\n    ===============================\n\n    1) @{" Introduction " Link ChildDoc1}\n    2) @{" Requirements " Link ChildDoc2}\n    3) @{" Installation " Link ChildDoc3}\n    4) @{" Tooltypes " Link ChildDoc7}\n    4) @{" History " Link ChildDoc4}\n    5) @{" Greetings " Link ChildDoc5}\n    6) @{" How to contact 5D " Link ChildDoc6}\n\n@endnode\n@node ChildDoc1 "Introduction"\n\n  5D-ZippySearch - Introduction\n  =============================\n\n  5D-ZippySearch is a replacement for the ''Z''-command\n  of AmiExpress. So it searchs for a user-defined string\n  in the current conf''s file dirs.\n\n@endnode\n@node ChildDoc2 "Requirements"\n\n  5D-ZippySearch - Requirements\n  =============================\n\n  o  an Amiga (or compatible - DRACO)\n  o  an AmiExpress-compatible BBS-program\n\n@endnode\n@node ChildDoc3 "Installation"\n\n  5D-ZippySearch - Installation (for AmiExpress)\n  ==============================================\n\n  Simply copy the directories in this archive into your bbs-\n  directory.\n\n@endnode\n@node ChildDoc4 "History"\n\n  5D-ZippySearch - History\n  ========================\n\n  v0.01 - [RELEASE II]\n  v0.02 - Increased speed of searching through the dirs\n          by adding intelligent buffering\n  v0.03 - Increased speed of searching through the dirs\n          by using 100% assembler-routine\n        - Added wildcard-support\n        - Added SEARCH-STRING highlighting\n        - Added VIRTUAL lineinput for search string and flag\n          string entering\n        - Added HOLD scan\n        - Fixed mem-allocation-bug (didn''t work if file-\n          length longer than largest memory block)\n        - Fixed stack-destroying-bug\n  v0.04 - Fixed argument-bug\n        - Added reverse scanmode (if more than one dir is\n          scanned, they are scanned in reverse order)\n        - Added cursor-tagging\n        - Program-icon added for choosing default-scanmode\n        - Added asynchronous i/o (special thanks to Crayor!)\n  v0.05 - Increased speed of searching through the dirs\n          by optimising assembler routine\n        - Reduced memory usage to 32kB\n  v0.06 - Fixed little search bug\n  v0.07 - Fixed Estring-bug (Estrings and normal strings\n          were changed what might have destroyed the output)\n        - Added flag altering\n        - Added several tooltypes\n        - Added buffer size tooltype\n  v0.08 - Fixed argument-bug\n        - Increased speed of searching through the dirs\n\n@endnode\n@node ChildDoc5 "Greetings"\n\n  Greetings\n  =========\n\n  Airworx - Celator - Conan&Newton - Crayor\n  Deathknight - Dres! - Enzo - Gilthanas\n  Leland Gaunt - Mad Doc - Mad Force - Mad Man\n  Maverick - MouseBuster - Muad''Dib - Nero\n  Playmate - R/\\! - Radavi - Rainmain\n  Rebel MC - Rush - Snow - Steel - Thunder\n  Webster - Whirlwind - Whiz!\n  ___\n  \\_/ Special thanks go to R/\! & Whirlwind & Webster & Radavi\n   o                       & Crayor for the asynch-i/o routine!\n\n@endnode\n@node ChildDoc6 "How to contact 5D"\n\n  You can write a message to ''SvEN tHE CREAToR'' at the following boards:\n\n  o Death Row\n  o Masturbation Station\n  o Punishment Inc.\n\n  ... and several more\n\n  Or leave E-Mail to: [email removed]\n\n@endnode\n@node ChildDoc7 "Tooltypes"\n\n  5D-ZippySearch - Tooltypes\n  ==========================\n\n  HOLD_LEVEL=<level>                   - Minimum level needed for\n                                         scanning the sysop hold\n                                         e.g. HOLD_LEVEL=255\n  CM_<command>=<NORMAL|REVERSE|ASK>    - Turn on reverse/normal/ask\n                                         mode for commands\n                                         e.g. CM_ZR=REVERSE\n  BUFFER_SIZE=<size>                   - Adjust buffer size\n                                         note: 2 buffers of this size\n                                         are allocated\n                                         e.g. BUFFER_SIZE=16384\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',19103,2,1,'Z','Doors/5D-ZippySearch','5d_zs008','scan',1780048351);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('5d_zs011','5D!ZS011.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/5D!ZS011.LHA','5D-ZippySearch','XIM','5D-ZippySearch',NULL,'sTc/5D','5D','_____ ___|  \   __ /  __//       \ /  |___ ...._\____/____|_   /   |   \...............',replace(replace('                __\r\n      _____ ___|  \   __\r\n     /  __//       \ /  |___\r\n...._\____/____|_   /   |   \...............\r\n:::/      \  \ |   /         \::::::::::::::\r\n::/           \|  /           \:[ dYNASTY ]:\r\n::\___________/|__\_____|     /:::::::::::::\r\n.---------------[ sTEEL]|____/-------------.\r\n|      5D-ZippySearch v0.11 by sTc/5D      |\r\n|      This is the AmiExpress version      |\r\n`------------------------------------------''\r\n--/\-- pASSED tHRU ENTROPY BBS --/\--\r\n    \r\n','\r',char(13)),'\n',char(10)),'5D-ZippySearch.guide',replace('@database 5D-ZippySearch Documentation\n\nCopyright ©1996 sTc\n\n@remark $VER: (October 12 1996, 12:00)\n@remark AmigaGuide database for the 5D-ZippySearch Documentation\n\n@node MAIN "5D-ZippySearch Documentation"\n       ._____.\n  __5TH|_    |    ._____. ___________ ________. _______ ___.           ._____.\n__\\   __     |____|_    |_\\   _    ___\\____   |_\\  ___/__  |___    ____|_    |\n\\     \\|    _/     /    |     /    \\     _    |\\_____   /  ___/___/     /    |\n \\     \\    \\     /_    |____/    / \\    \\    |    /   /   \\     \\     /_    |\n  \\__________\\_____     |   /____/   \\________|_______/|__________\\_____     |\n                  |_____|pHS!                                          |_____|\n\n                                                     ... No Fear of Fun!\n\n    5D-ZippySearch.Guide - Contents\n    ===============================\n\n    1) @{" Introduction " Link ChildDoc1}\n    2) @{" Requirements " Link ChildDoc2}\n    3) @{" Installation " Link ChildDoc3}\n    4) @{" Tooltypes " Link ChildDoc7}\n    4) @{" History " Link ChildDoc4}\n    5) @{" Greetings " Link ChildDoc5}\n    6) @{" How to contact 5D " Link ChildDoc6}\n\n@endnode\n@node ChildDoc1 "Introduction"\n\n  5D-ZippySearch - Introduction\n  =============================\n\n  5D-ZippySearch is a replacement for the ''Z''-command\n  of AmiExpress. It searches for a user-defined string\n  in the current conf''s file dirs.\n\n@endnode\n@node ChildDoc2 "Requirements"\n\n  5D-ZippySearch - Requirements\n  =============================\n\n  o  an Amiga (or compatible - DRACO)\n  o  AmiExpress v3.x+\n\n@endnode\n@node ChildDoc3 "Installation"\n\n  5D-ZippySearch - Installation (for AmiEx)\n  =========================================\n\n  Simply copy the directories in this archive into your bbs-\n  directory.\n\n@endnode\n@node ChildDoc4 "History"\n\n  5D-ZippySearch - History\n  ========================\n\n  v0.01 - [RELEASE II]\n  v0.02 - Increased speed of searching through the dirs\n          by adding intelligent buffering\n  v0.03 - Increased speed of searching through the dirs\n          by using 100% assembler-routine\n        - Added wildcard-support\n        - Added SEARCH-STRING highlighting\n        - Added VIRTUAL lineinput for search string and flag\n          string entering\n        - Added HOLD scan\n        - Fixed mem-allocation-bug (didn''t work if file-\n          length longer than largest memory block)\n        - Fixed stack-destroying-bug\n  v0.04 - Fixed argument-bug\n        - Added reverse scanmode (if more than one dir is\n          scanned, they are scanned in reverse order)\n        - Added cursor-tagging\n        - Program-icon added for choosing default-scanmode\n        - Added asynchronous i/o (special thanks to Crayor!)\n  v0.05 - Increased speed of searching through the dirs\n          by optimising assembler routine\n        - Reduced memory usage to 32kB\n  v0.06 - Fixed little search bug\n  v0.07 - Fixed Estring-bug (Estrings and normal strings\n          were changed what might have destroyed the output)\n        - Added flag altering\n        - Added several tooltypes\n        - Added buffer size tooltype\n  v0.08 - Fixed argument-bug\n        - Increased speed of searching through the dirs\n  v0.09 - Added ''C''lear command\n  v0.10 - FAME version created\n  v0.11 - Added ''L''ocal download command\n        - Fixed backscan to handle longer file\n          descriptions (especially the ones with\n          much ANSI code in it)\n\n@endnode\n@node ChildDoc5 "Greetings"\n\n  Greetings\n  =========\n\n  Airworx - ByteAndi - Celator - Clyde Radcliff\n  Conan&Newton - Crayor - Deathknight - Dres! - Enzo - Freeman -\n  Flozzy - Gilthanas - Leland Gaunt - Mad Doc - Mad Force\n  Mad Man - Maverick - MouseBuster - Muad''Dib - Nero\n  Playmate - R/\\! - Radavi - Rainmain\n  Rebel MC - Rush - Snow - Speed - Splash\n  Steel - Stringray - Strider - Thunder - Tom/HLM\n  Webster - Whirlwind - Whiz!\n  ___\n  \\_/ Special thanks go to R/\\!, Lector, Whirlwind, Webster\n   o             & Crayor for the asynch-i/o routine!\n\n@endnode\n@node ChildDoc6 "How to contact 5D"\n\n  You can write a message to ''SvEN tHE CREAToR'' at the following boards:\n\n  o Broadway BBS\n  o Death Row\n  o Masturbation Station\n  o Punishment Inc.\n  o Terminal FuckUp!\n\n  ... and several more\n\n  Or leave E-Mail to: [email removed]\n\n@endnode\n@node ChildDoc7 "Tooltypes"\n\n  5D-ZippySearch - Tooltypes\n  ==========================\n\n  HOLD_LEVEL=<level>                   - Minimum level needed for\n                                         scanning the sysop hold\n                                         e.g. HOLD_LEVEL=255\n  CM_<command>=<NORMAL|REVERSE|ASK>    - Turn on reverse/normal/ask\n                                         mode for commands\n                                         e.g. CM_ZR=REVERSE\n  BUFFER_SIZE=<size>                   - Adjust buffer size\n                                         note: 2 buffers of this size\n                                         are allocated\n                                         e.g. BUFFER_SIZE=16384\n  LOCALDL_LEVEL=<level>                - Minimum level needed\n                                         for local download\n                                         e.g. LOCALDL_LEVEL=255\n  DOCALDL_PATH=<path>                  - Default path for\n                                         local download\n                                         e.g. LOCALDL_PATH=RAM:\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',23232,1,1,'Z','Doors/5D-ZippySearch','5d_zs011','scan',1780048351);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('5d_add12','5D-ADD12.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/5D-ADD12.LHA','ConfigABTL','XIM','Amigaguide',NULL,'BOBO!','5D','______  __  / ____  \___  \  _____  ___  / \/  /  /  /  /  /  /  ¬  /\_  \ /  //  /  / /  /  /\__  /  /  /  /  /  /  //  /_\__  /',replace('5tH_/\____/\_ __/\__ _/\__ _/\_____/\__/\_ _\n______  __  / ____  \___  \  _____  ___  /\n \/  /  /  /  /  /  /  ¬  /\_  \ /  //  /  /\n /  /  /\__  /  /  /  /  /  /  //  /_\__  /\n/___  /___  /__/  /__/  /___  //  //___  /__\n____ /_ __ /____ /____ / ___ /__ /_ ___ //\nbIS\/    \/    \/    \/    \/  \/     \/\n  ADDBBSTOLOGOFF V1.2 - CODED BY BOBO!\n','\n',char(10)),'Addbbstologoff.Guide',replace('@database\n@node Main "AddBBStoLogoff v1.2 - Documentation by RAJ-BAN"\n\n @{"What is Addbbstologoff?    " link Whatisit      }  ---------------------------------------------\n @{"Features                   " link Features      }  ) Add Board to Logoff v1.2 (Second Release) (\n @{"Disclaimer                 " link Disclaimer    }  --------------Date: 25-May-1993--------------\n @{"What, Where and Why        " link whatwherewhy  }\n @{"Installation The Door      " link installation  }             Copyright © 1993 - Bobo!\n @{"Updating from v1.1 to v1.2 " link update1112    }    The East BBS +46-8-940614, +46-8-PRiVATE!\n @{"Output Example (Noansi)    " link outputex      }\n @{"Other utils/doors in work  " link otherutils    }       Doc typed at 27-Jan-1993 by RaJ-Ban\n @{"Final Notes from BOBO      " link finalnotes    }   Traders Nation +46-176-55202, +46-176-19228\n @{"Don''t touch my arexx script" link donottouch    } ----------------------------------------------\n @{"Credits, Greetings etc.    " link credz         } )   An highly optimized AmiExpress Door !    (\n @{"Updates of AddBBStologoff  " link updates       } ----------------------------------------------\n\n          Call this boards for lastest updates and newest wares!:\n -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    The East BBS #1 +46-8-940614   or  Traders Nation #1  +46-176-55202\n    The East BBS #2 +46-8-PRiVATE  or  Traders Nation #2  +46-176-19228\n@endnode\n@node Whatisit "What is AddBBStoLogoff?"\n\n                     ___ What is AddBBStologoff ? ___\n                     \(============================)/\n\n This is a Door which allows Users (Sysops) to add their own BBS advertise\n to a Logoff-screen. How many times haven''t you got the Question about\n putting other boards to the Logoff-screen ? And they will keep asking\n over and over again until you finally put it there. Too lazy or to Busy\n to do that ? Well here''s the solution. No need to bother sysops, Users\n can handle all that by themselves (if the got the right access.).\n As Sysop you are able to enter how many boards you want in the logoff\n and you can also include a Header file to be displayed. It also allows\n some sysop editing.\n@endnode\n@node Features "Features"\n   Features:\n   ---------\n · The one and only Door of this kind. Very nice to let Users add\n   Their boards to the logoff themselves!\n · Very fast (for beeing a Arexx door) even on a plain 68000 system!\n · Build in config editor, you really don''t need this doc.\n · Build in Help ! (what can I say... Why are you reading?)\n · Lots of securitychecks. So if something goes wrong, check the errorlog\n   and notify BoBo!\n · Multinode Copatible !\n@endnode\n@node Disclaimer "Disclaimer"\n                           ___ Disclaimer ___\n                           \(==============)/\n\n This Door is programmed in Arexx (at the moment) would not cause any\n problems. But as always theres no guarantee that it wont cause any damage.\n Anyway I, Bobo, take no responsibilities for what this door may cause to\n your Harddisc or Software. But I (and some other BBS''s) have been running\n this Door for about 4 weeks and NO Problem has accured. Bugreports and\n other suggestions are wanted, please look at the end of this document !\n This Door is CALLWARE. If you find it Useful and keep using it, call my\n BBS (perhaps to check for updates ?). Soon a version in C will be released,\n but i haven''t got the C power to do that yet.\n@endnode\n@node whatwherewhy "What, Where and Why"\n                        ___ What, Where and Why ___\n                        \(=======================)/\n\n This package should incloude the following:\n\n File with Full Path                       Size   Description\n -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n Doors:Arexx/Addbbs/Addbbstologoff.Rexx    29224  The Main Program.\n Doors:Arexx/Addbbs/Addbbstologoff.Doc     15242  You are looking on it.\n Doors:Arexx/Addbbs/Addbbstologoff.Guide   21801  Amiga Guide Doc.\n Doors:Arexx/Addbbs/Addbbstologoff.Update   4092  What has been Changed!\n Doors:Arexx/Addbbs/OutputEx.Txt            2066  Output Example (Noansi)\n Doors:Arexx/Addbbs/OutputEx.Txt.gr         2660  Output Example (Ansi)\n Doors:Arexx/Addbbs/ConfigABTL             46072  CLI config program.\n S:Addbbstologoff.Header                     705  Example Header included.\n S:Addbbstologoff.Help                      2364  Text for Online-Help.\n -----------------------------------------------------------------------\n If the filesizes doesn''t match, Call my BBS for a new copy. Someone may\n have altered the code, and that could mean a backdoor.\n@endnode\n@node installation "Installation The Door"\n                       ___ Installation The Door ___\n                       \(=========================)/\n\n As a registered AmiExpress you know how to install a AREXX type door in\n your system. If not, check the AE doc and try to understand the rest.\n First of all, make a dir in your DOORS:Arexx/ called ADDBBS or whatever\n you like. Copy the main program (and the doc) into that directory. Copy\n the Header and Help file to your S: dir. Now edit your BBS.cmd or the\n CustomCommands for older versions, located in your BBS:Command/ dir\n You should add something like this to your BBS.cmd file...\n\n -Cut Here-----------------------------------------------\n *ADDBBS   RM020Doors:Arexx/Addbbs/Addbbstologoff.rexx\n -Cut Here--|--------------------------------------------\n\n Addbbstologoff.Header\n ---------------------\n Now make a file called Addbbstologoff.Header or what ever you want it\n to be named (you can change it in the config). And in there you can have\n a logo for your board etc etc. Normally goes to the S: dir. (Look at\n the included one)\n\n Addbbstologoff.Config\n ---------------------\n To make a configfile, you can either use the included CLI configuration\n program (But since it''s arexx compiled, it wont work on all amigas), or\n you can use the inbuild one in the door. To use the inbuild one, install\n the door in your bbs.cmd, and go into your local node and run it. Go into\n S)ysopcommands, then M)ake/edit config. The configeditor looks like this:\n\n *) Version of Addbbstologoff........(1.2)\n 1) Maxboards in logoffscreen........(10)\n 2) Seclevel to addboard.............(20)\n 3) Seclevel to access sysopcommands.(255)\n 4) Write log to callerslog..........(YES)\n 5) Check for duplicate board........(YES)\n 6) Headerfile.......................(S:Addbbstologoff.Header)\n 7) Helpfile.........................(S:Addbbstologoff.Help)\n 8) Outputfile.......................(BBS:Node1/Logoff.Txt)\n S) Save, quit and use this config...(Save)\n Q) Quit and use old config..........(Nosave)\n X) Quit and use this config.........(Nosave)\n\n (1) ''Maxboards'' is the maximum numbers of boards to have on the logoffscreen.\n For example, you have chosen 10, there will never be more than 10 boards in\n your logoff. Because when someone adds the 11th board, board number 1 will\n get deleted, and the new board will get added at the bottom.\n\n (2) ''Addboard'' is the lowest security level you''ll need to Add a board to\n the logoff (You maybe don''t want some lamers to add boards by them selves).\n\n (3) ''SysopCommands'' is the lowest seclevel you''ll need to access the sysop\n (cosysop) menu. There you''ll have these options....\n D)elete logoffscreen: Delete the logoff screen and reset all boards.\n M)ake/Edit config   : Edit the S:Addbbstologoff.Config\n E)dit Board         : Edit one of the boards that are added to the\n                        logoff screen.\n R)emove Board       : Remove boards from logoffscreen.\n\n (4) ''Log'' is if the door should write to callerslog when a user is using\n the door (You can for example see who have added wich board and so on).\n\n (5) ''Duplicate check'' is if the door should check for duplicate boards.\n If it finds a duplicate board it won''t add anotherone !\n\n (6) ''Headerfile'' is the file, with full path, you want to put over the\n boards. Example, you maybe want a logo for your bbs/group name or something\n like that to be showed at the same screen (look at the included one).\n\n (7) ''Helpfile'' is the helpfile, with full path, thats used when a user uses\n online help. (Please don''t change the helptext)\n\n (8) ''Outputfile'' is the output file of the Door (with full path). The\n outputfile can be BBS:Screens/Logoff.txt or the BBS:NodeX/Logoff.txt file \n etc etc. If you are using Random-logoffs, just give the outputfile a correct\n number. You are now able to use the some outputfile for ALL nodes.\n@endnode\n@node update1112 "Updating from v1.1 to v1.2"\n                ___ Updating from version 1.1 to 1.2 ___\n                \(====================================)/\n The only thing you need to do, is to replace the old helpfile, docfile,\n updates and the arexx source with the new ones. You ALSO need to make a \n new configfile. Use the CLI version (Arexx Compiled), or the inbuild one.\n@endnode\n@node outputex "Output Example"\n                          ___ Output Example ___\n                          \(==================)/\n\n           [=> T H A N K   Y O U   F O R   C A L L I N G <=]\n             .       .       .          .        .       .       .\n          __/|___ __/|___.__/|_________/|_    __/|___ __/|___ __/|__\/_\n          \  _   \\  _   |\  _   \      _/    \  _   \\  _   \\  _   \\n   _ __ __/  |___//  |___|/  |___/\__/ _|__ __/__/   // _/   //  |___/\n  \\\\_\\_   __|_/   ___/|\___   \  / \\\\_\\____   </  \   < \___   \\n        /    |   \   |   |/   \   \/    |   /    \   \   \   \/   \   \\n        \  ______/___| __|______  /____ |   \______  /_____  /______  /\n  =======\/==========|/=========\/=====\|==========\/======\/===cgr=\/===\n\n    Y O U   C A N   A L S O   T R Y   T H E S E   C O O L   B O A R D S\n                                                                               \nAddbbstologoff v1.2! - Scripted in 1992/93 by [-bObO-] - East BBS +46-8-940614!\n\nLast user added: CaT                            Last updated: 05-20-93 20:38:33\n.--+------------------+-----------------+-------------------------------------.\n|Nd| Boardname        | Phone           | Comment                             |\n+--+------------------+-----------------+-------------------------------------+\n|04| CENTRESOFT!      | +46-18-463380   | NEMESIS EHQ! NEWEST AMI/CON/ST!     |\n|01| > 7:th Heaven <  | +46-8-53192192  | DECADE DIST SITE - WRD EHQ - 16k8   |\n|01| NEMESiS SYSTEMS! | +46-8-58038503! | SKiLLiON/EUE MEMBER BOARD - ELWooD! |\n|01| · the  SLAmmER · | +46-8-623·01·96 | /X · 68030/40Mhz · 16800 DS · INDY· |\n|01| FiNAL PHASE      | +46-8-7547760   | 1.7Gb of PC & CONSOLES NEWEST WAREZ |\n|01| UnderCover       | +46-8-54023405  | /X v2.39 , HST , AMIGA ELiTE ...... |\n|01| Speedhunters     | +46-174-34111   | EliTE · PORNO · KEWL · WRD WHQ!!    |\n|01| ·» Dyers Eve «·  | (·) PRiVATE (·) | FAiRLiGHT PC SWEDEN HEADQUARTER !!  |\n|02| Traders Nation   | +46-176-55202   | NoDE 2: +46-176-19228 NEW PC/AMiGA  |\n|01| Hall Of FAME     | +46[0]910-26665 | 18.82 MIPS 16.8K DS 0-1 DAY WAREZ!  |\n`--+------------------+-----------------+-------------------------------------''\n\n This is an example output from my board. As you see, we have a header\n above, and a maximum of 10 boards. (And ofcaurse, the ansi version looks\n much better!)\n@endnode\n@node otherutils "Other utils/doors in work"\n                     ___ Other utils/doors in work ___\n                     \(=============================)/\n\n File Checker........:The best Fcheck utility ever for Amiexpress. Will\n                      be released soon in C. Fast and good!\n Multisysoppage......:With this utility, users are able to choice wich\n                      sysop they want to page (if you are more than one\n                      sysop on the system.)\n Remoteshell.........:The old cool remoteshell that was removed from\n                      Amie 2.0+ is now back. The same old remoteshell\n                      where you can do whatever you like. (Format hehe)\n Ultimate Usermessage:The most powerful usermessage utility ever done\n                      for amie. With alot of commands and options.\n Node Information....:A new nodeinformation door, that shows alot of\n                      informations about the users on the other nodes.\n Last Files..........:The best utility to show the last files in the\n                      area.\n@endnode\n@node finalnotes "Final Notes !"\n                           ___ FINAL NOTES ! ___\n                           \(=================)/\n\n The arexx source\n ----------------\n I have decided to release this door uncompiled for those who wants to check\n and learn from my nice and clean source. But this means that the door is\n very easy to put a backdoor in. So PLEASE, check the source with CED or\n something before running it. Or call my board for a full copy of it to be\n 100% sure. If you want to compile this you have to do it yourself. I haven''t\n tested it, so do it on your own risk. Since this door is totaly optimized,\n this will run fast, even on 68000 cards.\n\n And remember, it''s LAME to rip others hard work. If you want to do something,\n do it yourself, this is mine and mine only source! If you want to use some\n part of the source it''s ok, if you give me some credits for it!\n\n Well, you maybe have seen that this version (1.2) has been in work a quite\n long time. But i wanted it to be GOOD, and errorfree before releasing it!\n I ONLY make quility doors. And i hope this is enough for you. And i give\n you RAJ-BAN, a big thanx for writing this documentation for me. Call his\n board!\n\n This door have one of the best error securitychecks. If somewhing goes wrong,\n the door will write to the errorlog (Doors:Errorlog), and then AUTOMATICLY\n force the user to leave a comment to the sysop. The door will write ALL sort\n of errors in the errorlog, included missing configfile, missing tools\n (C:Delete, C:Copy), and missing libraries etc etc. The Door will also tell\n the user who''s using it if an errorlog exists, and then tell him to inform\n the sysop to check what''s wrong.\n                                               Signed [-bObO-] of [-iNSANE-]\n@endnode\n@node donottouch "Don''t touch my arexx script"\n Don''t touch my arexx script\n ---------------------------\n Don''t change anything in the source, becouse i have spent quite a lot of\n time making this program for you. I hate lamer stealing others hard work,\n and not even mentioning the original Coder !\n So, if you want to see any changes, please call my board, and i''ll make\n the improvments you want!\n@endnode\n@node credz "The Credz etc."\n The Credz etc.\n --------------\n Programming and Idea by:  Bobo/East BBS\n Some Doc improvements by: RaJ-Ban/Traders Nation\n\n If you have any trouble installing or running this door, you may\n either call my board, or some of my beta testers for help. Also call\n for the latest Updates and new wares!\n\n  Name:             Sysop:         Phone Number:     Speed:   Supports:\n ==========================================================================\n  The East BBS #1   BOBO/INSANE    +46-8-940614      16.8k    AM/PC/ST/CON\n  The East BBS #2   BOBO/INSANE    +46-8-PRiVATE     14.4k    AM/PC/ST/CON\n  Wastelands        NiGHTSHADE/INS +46-8-157472      16.8k    AMiGA / CON\n  Traders Nation #1 RaJ-BaN        +46-176-55202     16.8k    AMiGA/PC/SNES\n  Traders Nation #2 RaJ-BaN        +46-176-19228     16.8k    AMiGA/PC/SNES\n  Crazy World       SLASH          +46-8-6054434     16.8k    AMiGA/PC/CON\n  Dope House #1     RICHI/FLT      +46-8-6031041     14.4k    AMiGA ONLY\n  Dope House #2     RICHI/FLT      +46-8-6031042     14.4k    AMiGA ONLY\n ==========================================================================\n\n I''m looking for more beta testers (multinode). Please leave me a comment\n either on my board or somewhere i have an account.\n\n Some greetings from [-bObO-] go''es to:\n --------------------------------------\n Raj-Ban/Indy, Slash/Indy, Richi/Fairlight, Nightshade/Ins, Necronomicon/Ins\n Elric/Quartex, Ministry/Quartex, Madness/Indy, X-Citing/Indy, Cruger/Shamen\n    Snuskbuske/Dual Crew, Zany/Noxius, Cevin Key/Elevation, Princip/Decade\n                 And ofcourse, all my friends that i missed.\n\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n                            That''s all folks...\n\n                  Call my board: +46-8-940614 (East BBS)\n\n                     For more cool doors and updates.\n\n              This documentation is copyrighted (C)''93 by RAJ-BAN!\n\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n@endnode\n@node updates "Updates!"\n\n @{"Updates, AddBBStoLogoff v1.0  " link 10 } (Was ONLY availible for BETA testers)\n @{"Updates, AddBBStoLogoff v1.1  " link 11 } (First release, a BETA version)\n @{"Updates, AddBBStoLogoff v1.2  " link 12 } (Second release, a 100% release)\n\n If you have any trouble installing or running this door, you may\n either call my board, or some of my beta testers for help. Also call\n for the latest Updates and new wares!\n\n  Name:             Sysop:         Phone Number:     Speed:   Supports:\n ==========================================================================\n  The East BBS #1   BOBO/INSANE    +46-8-940614      16.8k    AM/PC/ST/CON\n  The East BBS #2   BOBO/INSANE    +46-8-PRiVATE     14.4k    AM/PC/ST/CON\n  Wastelands        NiGHTSHADE/INS +46-8-157472      16.8k    AMiGA / CON\n  Traders Nation #1 RaJ-BaN        +46-176-55202     16.8k    AMiGA/PC/SNES\n  Traders Nation #2 RaJ-BaN        +46-176-19228     16.8k    AMiGA/PC/SNES\n  Crazy World       SLASH          +46-8-6054434     16.8k    AMiGA/PC/CON\n  Dope House #1     RICHI/FLT      +46-8-6031041     14.4k    AMiGA ONLY\n  Dope House #2     RICHI/FLT      +46-8-6031042     14.4k    AMiGA ONLY\n ==========================================================================\n@endnode\n@node 10 "Updates, AddBBStoLogoff v1.0"\nAddbbstologoff v1.0 (03-01-92 > 06-13-92) - [Only Availible for Betatesters]\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n03-01-92 <> This door was born.\n03-24-92 <> Added a mainmenu with the options Addboard, List Boards and\n            Sysop commands.\n04-05-92 <> Fixed a configfile (s:Addbbstologoff.Config)\n04-27-92 <> Rewritten the whole save part for faster saving.\n05-04-92 <> Added some nice ansi colours.\n05-24-92 <> Added two sysopcommands. M)ake/Edit config and D)elete logoff\n            screen.\n06-13-92 <> Added the option H)elp in the mainmenu. Now the user can get\n            online help when pressing ''H''\n@endnode\n@node 11 "Updates, AddBBStoLogoff v1.1"\nAddbbstologoff v1.1ßeta (08-21-92 > 02-02-93) - [First Release]\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n08-21-92 <> Added multinodesaving. When someone is saving, ABTL writes\n            a file called ''ENV:Doorstats'' with the nodenumber and username.\n            Then if some user on another node is trying to save, and found\n            that file, ABTL tells the user to try some other time.\n            (This means multinode boards can run this door without any\n            problems)\n08-29-92 <> Rewritten the save part (again..). Now it saves 40% faster!\n10-02-92 <> Fixed a new outputdesign. (hope you like it?!)\n11-14-92 <> Fixed the multinodesaving so it can handle unlimited nodes.\n12-05-92 <> Fixed a major bug when multinodesaving. Hope all bugs are\n            removed now!\n12-11-92 <> From now on, the documentation is written by Raj-Ban.\n01-15-93 <> Fixed a new way to save. Ex. if you have the maximum number\n            of boards on 10, and the user saves the 11th board, the board\n            at the top will get removed and the new board will come at\n            the bottom. Many have requested this sort of saving, here it is!\n01-21-93 <> Added two more sysopcommands. R)emove and E)dit boards.\n02-02-93 <> Now ABTL checks for duplicate boards when saving.\n@endnode\n@node 12 "Updates, AddBBStoLogoff v1.2"\nAddbbstologoff v1.2 (03-07-93 > 05-25-93) - [Second release]\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n03-07-93 <> Rewritten the whole sourcecode and removed all ansi codes.\n            Totaly new design is added. This looks much nicer now!\n03-28-93 <> You can now choice in the configfile if you want Duplicate check.\n04-04-93 <> Found a very ugly bug when multinodesaving. If a user added a\n            board, and it failed the duplicate check, ABTL didn''t delete\n            the doorstats file.\n04-13-93 <> Fixed a bug in remove and edit board. If you have removed all\n            boards, and try to remove another one the door would bug!\n04-15-93 <> This door is now programed for Insane.\n04-18-93 <> Fixed a prompt for online help. Now ABTL asks what command\n            the user want help with.\n04-19-93 <> Released it for my beta testers.\n04-20-93 <> The Uppercase fuction was really messed up. Didn''t work a shit.\n            Rewritten the whole uppercase fuction. Hope this works now.\n04-29-93 <> Added some nice ansi colors. Fixed some new lines.\n05-01-93 <> Added a configfile checker. ABTL now checks if the configfile is\n            valid or not.\n05-04-93 <> Added a menu for the Online help. From now on, the helpfile is\n            written by Guardian.\n05-20-93 <> Removed the last minibugs from the door. I think this is totaly\n            bugfree now.\n05-21-93 <> Decided to rewrite the online help routine. The last one was\n            not good, had no errorchecking or anything. This new one also\n            checks the helpfile so it''s for the right version of ABTL\n05-22-93 <> Decided to write the helpfile myself, since Guardian is to lazy.\n05-23-93 <> Found a little bug in the duplicate check. When the door\n            compared the boards, it didn''t uppercase them both.\n05-24-93 <> Written the documentation in Amiga Guide too. Hope this helps a\n            bit with the installation.\n05-25-93 <> Fixed a mini bug in the multinode saving. When ABTL had tryed to\n            save, the door jumped the to the mainmenu again.\n05-25-93 <> Fixed the nodenumber so you ONLY can write numbers now.\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',93978,7,0,NULL,NULL,'5d_add12','scan',1780048351);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('5d_af001','5D-AF001.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/5D-AF001.LHA','5D-AutoFree','XIM','5D-AutoFree',NULL,'SvEN','5D','______\     /__|      /___________\___  /___ \_____ \  _/   /     /__\   ____/  _ /_/   / _/  _/  \___  /\    /__/ \____ \_  \/___  /|',replace('      _______   _______           _______   \n______\     /__|      /___________\___  /___\n\_____ \  _/   /     /__\   ____/  _ /_/   /\n_/  _/  \___  /\    /__/ \____ \_  \/___  /|\n\ 5.\    / / /\ \_ / \    / _/  /  |   / / |\n|\______/___/_|\  /___\  /_____/___|____/Rpd\n`---------------\/-----\/----·presents·----''\n             5D-AutoFree v0.01\n   Coded by SvEN tHE CREAToR/5tH DyNASTY\n Makes files automatically free download if\nthey begin with a defineable string (''5D-'')!\n','\n',char(10)),'5D-AutoFree.Guide',replace('@database 5D-AutoFree Documentation\n@Author SvEN tHE CREAToR Of 5tH DyNASTY\n@Index Documentation\n\nCopyright © 1994 SvEN tHE CREAToR / 5tH DyNASTY\n\n@Remark $VER: 5D-AutoFree v0.01 by sTc/5D\n@Remark AmigaGuide database\n\n@node MAIN "5D-AutoFree Documentation © 1994 SvEN tHE CREAToR Of 5tH DyNASTY"\n                                                              :\n                                                       :      ¦             \n                   ________________  __________________¦      |\n            _______\_______       /  \             /   |      |______\n           |  __   _/     /______/____\  _     _  /    ¦      |  __  |\n           |  \/  _\________    \_\  / \/       \/     _      |  \/  |\n           |______\        /     / \/   |       |      /      |______|\n                   \___________ /       |_______|_____/       |Rpd!\n                              \/                     /________|\n                         :           :                                     :\n            ____   :     ¦     :     ¦      · 5 · T · H ·            :     ¦\n  __________\  /___¦    _|__/\ ¦     |_______ _______________________¦     |\n  \______   \\//   |    \____ \|     |   _   \\_____      /       /  |     |\n   /     \   \/    ¦     |   \ \     |   /    \/   /_____/    _  /   ¦     |\n _/       \   \_____     |    \ \_   |   _     \_____   \_     \/_____     |\n \       _/    /   /     |     \     |   /      /   /    /     |     /     |\n  \__________ /__________|     |\ ___|__/_____ /_______ /______|___________|\n            \/           |     ¦ \/          \/       \/\n                         ¦     :     · D · Y · N · A · S · T · Y ·\n                         :\n\n                        ##>>> P r E S E N T S <<<##\n\n                            5D-AutoFree v0.01\n\n                 Coded by SvEN tHE CREAToR of 5th Dynasty\n\n                           @{" Normal Documentation " Link Documentation}\n@endnode\n@node Documentation "5D-AutoFree Documentation"\n              _______________________________________________\n             |                                               |\n             | //                                            |\n             | /                                             |\n             |                                               |\n             |            @{" D e S C R I P T I O N " Link Description}           |\n             |                                               |\n             |           @{" I n S T A L L A T I O N " Link Installation}          |\n             |                                               |\n             |              @{" T o O L T Y P E S " Link Tooltypes}             |\n             |                                               |\n             |              @{" G r E E T I N G S " Link Greetings}             |\n             |                                               |\n             |                                             / |\n             |                                            // |\n             |_______________________________________________|\n\n@endnode\n@node Description "5D-AutoFree Description"\n5D-AutoFree has been coded by SvEN tHE CREAToR/5D!\n\n5D-AutoFree is a /X-Door which makes it possible to make files\nwhich have been uploaded and begin with a string like ''5D-'' to\nfree downloads automatically and add one line with a color which\ncan be defined by the sysop. The color and the auto free strings\ncan be simply defined in the icon of 5D-AutoFree.\n@endnode\n@node Installation "5D-AutoFree Installation"\nCopy all files which are in the archive bbs directory\nto your bbs directory.\n\nContents of archive:\n===================\n\nBBS/\n    Commands/\n        SYSCmd/\n            FILECHECK.info\n    Doors/\n        5D-AutoFree/\n            5D-AutoFree\n            5D-AutoFree.info\n            5D-AutoFree.Guide\n\n===================\n\n@endnode\n@node Greetings "5D-AutoFree Greetings"\nGreetings go to:\n\n           Celator ........... Thank you for helping me with /X!\n           ByteAndi ............ For helping me to learn coding!\n           Prophet .................... For being a nice friend!\n           Snow ...................... Sing mehr lieder, leader!\n           Airworx ................. Continue work as Co Leader!\n           Delta-X ................. When you will merry Murdoc?\n           Strider ........ We should spread our standard again!\n\nSorry to all people I forgot but as you know my brain isn''t so well! hehe\n\n@endnode\n@node Tooltypes "5D-AutoFree Tooltypes"\nYou can insert the following tooltypes in the icon\n  "Doors:5D-AutoFree/5D-AutoFree.info"\n\n===========\n\nFREE_COLOR=1;32                    - Ansi color string for the free download\n                                     description add line! If you don''t\n                                     want to use a color simply don''t insert\n                                     ''FREE_COLOR'' or put a '';'' before it!\nFREE_STR.1=5D-                     - If the file name begins with ''5D-''\n                                     the file will be maken free download!\nFREE_STR.2=FLT-                    - Same as above! The number of strings\n                                     can be as high as you want!\n\n===========\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',31424,6,0,NULL,NULL,'5d_af001','scan',1780048351);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('5d_amber','5D-AMBER.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/5D-AMBER.LHA',NULL,'XIM','5D-AMBER.EXE',NULL,'pROPHET/5D','5D',NULL,replace('5D-aMBERMOON cHARACTEReDITOR bY pROPHET/5D\n','\n',char(10)),'5D-AMBER.DOC',replace('\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\n                     5D-AMBERMOON EDITOR V1.0\n---------------------   FULL DOCUMENTATION -------------------------------\n\n                          CONTENTS :\n\n                .----------------------------------.                     \n                |Chapter1.............Requierements|\n                |Chapter2.............Functions    |\n                |Chpater3.............Credits      |\n                |Chpater4.............Greetings    |\n                |Chpater5.............Short note   |\n                ·----------------------------------·\n\n@chpater1[requierements]\n\n        To run AMBER ED 1.0 you need at least only 512Kb of memory\n        and only one disk drive (more are not supported).\n        Any OS x.x is supported.\n\n@chpater2[functions]\n\n       There are no special functions.....just type in the last\n       saved game ( REMEMBER,THE LAST SAVED GAME ) insert\n       AMBER_J (save game disk - must be AMBER_J it`s not only for\n       the prodigy version !) press RETURN and your character\n       will be optimized.That`s all.\n\n@chpater3[credits]\n\n               Full coding.................pROPHET/5D\n               Idea........................pROPHET/5D\n\n@chpater4[greetings]\n\n                       Greets fly out to :\n                    .---------------------.\n                    |oO     bRAWLER     Oo|\n               _____|oO     sKLEE       Oo|_____\n               \    |oO     rAPID       Oo|    /\n                \   |oO     dESERT      Oo|   /\n                 \  |oO     mURDOC      Oo|  /\n                  \ |oO    bYTEANDI     Oo| /\n                   \|oO      sNOW       Oo|/\n                   /|oO    aIRWORX      Oo|\\n                  / |oO  fRANK mAXWELL  Oo| \\n                 /  |oO    wOLFGANG     Oo|  \\n                /   |oO   sVEN (sTc)    Oo|   \\n               /    |oO     dONK        Oo|    \\n               \    |oO    pAMELA       Oo|    /\n                \   |oO    dELTA-X      Oo|   /\n                 \  |oO    X-wING       Oo|  /\n                  \_|oO     tURBO       Oo|_/\n                    ·---------------------·\n\n@chapter5[short note]\n\n         Remember,that this editor is optimizing only the first\n         character (your choosen one),`cause it`s boring to play\n         with a full optimized party (there`s no fun anymore).\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',37374,5,0,NULL,NULL,'5d_amber','scan',1780048351);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('5d_avl01','5D-AVL01.LZH','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/5D-AVL01.LZH','AVAIL','XIM','AVAIL',NULL,'PROPHET/5D','5D','5 \____\   / \     \____\   __/     /  /   \ T/   / \__   \  T  \  / \___ \   \/___    / H/   /   \     \ |   \    \ /  \   \      /',replace('  ____________________/\___________________\n5 \____\   / \     \____\   __/     /  /   \\n T/   / \__   \  T  \  / \___ \   \/___    /\nH/   /   \     \ |   \    \ /  \   \      /\n/________/     /_|    \/   \____\___\    /\n[===/_________/==|____/_____\RpD!/______/==]\n 5D-AVAIL v0.1 by PROPHET/5D SHELLuTIL\n','\n',char(10)),'5D-AVAIL01.DOC',replace('\n               +--------------------------------+\n               |   5D AVAIL v0.1 documentation  |\n               +--------------------------------+\n\n  5D Avail v0.1 is a simple AVAIL command replacement for OS2.0+ !\n  It shows all the memory (fast,chip and largest+total) and the\n  adressess of the dosbase,intuitionbase,gfxbase,expansionbase,execbase!\n\n  In later version i`ll change the complete look and add some new\n  features...................that`s all ......use it !\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',2866,3,1,'AVAIL','Doors/AVAIL','5d_avl01','scan',1780048351);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('5d_bch','5D-BCH.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/5D-BCH.LHA','5D-BaudCheck','XIM','5D-BaudCheck',NULL,NULL,'5D','______  __  / ____  \___  \  _____  ___  / \/  /  /  /  /  /  /  ¬  /\_  \ /  //  /  / /  /  /\__  /  /  /  /  /  /  //  /_\__  /',replace('5tH_/\____/\_ __/\__ _/\__ _/\_____/\__/\_ _\n______  __  / ____  \___  \  _____  ___  /\n \/  /  /  /  /  /  /  ¬  /\_  \ /  //  /  /\n /  /  /\__  /  /  /  /  /  /  //  /_\__  /\n/___  /___  /__/  /__/  /___  //  //___  /__\n____ /_ __ /____ /____ / ___ /__ /_ ___ //\nbIS\/    \/    \/    \/    \/  \/     \/\n     Baud rate detecter for ami/x\n','\n',char(10)),'5D-BaudCheck.guide',replace('@database 5D-BaudCheckDoc\n\nCopyright (c) 1993 SvEN tHE CREAToR / 5th Dynasty\n\n@Remark $VER: (October 9 1993, 15:30:00)\n@Remark AmigaGuide database for the 5D-BaudCheck Documentation\n\n@node MAIN "5D-BaudCheck Documentation (c)1993 SvEN tHE CREAToR of 5th Dynasty (October 9 1993, 15:30:00)"\n          ______    ______    ______    ______    ______    ______\n          \   ¬/    \   ¬/    \   ¬/    \   ¬/    \   ¬/    \   ¬/\n 5th ______\  /_ ____\  /______\  /______\  /______\  /______\  /_ ____\n    //     \\// |   \\\//     \\\//     \\\//     \\\//     \\\// |   \\\n   //       \/  |    \\/       \\/  |    \\/     ---\/       \\/  |    \\\n  /·         \___     ·\     |  ·\        ·\____    \\__      ·\___     ·\\n /·         | \        ·\    |   ·\ |      ·\        ·\ |      ·\        ·\\n \___________ /________ /____|___ /_|______ /________ / |______ /________ /\n            \/        \/        \/        \/        \/        \/    ·cj·\/\n\n                             >>> 5D-BaudCheck <<<\n\n                      Code & Design: SvEN tHE CREAToR/5D\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------- \n\n         >>> C·O·N·T·E·N·T·S  O·F  D·O·C·U·M·E·N·T·A·T·I·O·N <<<\n\n                         @{"      Introduction      " Link Cap01}\n                         @{"      Requirements      " Link Cap02}\n                         @{"      Installation      " Link Cap03}\n                         @{"       Tooltypes!       " Link Cap04}\n                         @{"       Greetings!       " Link Cap05}\n                         @{"   How to Contact me?   " Link Cap06}\n\n         ----------------------------------------------------------\n            Complete Docs for 5D-BaudCheck V0.01 [-5th Dynasty-]\n         ----------------------------------------------------------\n         The Documentation has been written by SvEN tHE CREAToR/5D.\n\n@endnode\n@node Cap01 "Introduction"\n  =======================================================================\n  5D-BaudCheck is a tool which allows the sysop to don''t allow users with\n  low baud connect to enter into the bbs except some users who have the\n  password to enter.\n  =======================================================================\n@endnode\n@node Cap02 "Requirements"\n  =======================================================================\n  To install 5D-BaudCheck you must have the following things:\n\n    Programm      Location            Description\n    ----------    --------            -----------\n    5D-BaudCheck  Doors:5D-BaudCheck  Main program\n\n  - an  Amiga Model (500/600/1000/1200/2000/2500/3000/4000/CDTV/CD³²)\n  - the installed Version of OS\2, OS\3, OS/432 or higher\n    (Soft-, Bit-, Hardware Version)\n  - the installed .INFO Files in the directories.\n  - AmiExpress V2.xx , v3.xx , v4.xx or higher.\n\n  =======================================================================\n@endnode\n@node Cap03 "How to install 5D-BaudCheck"\n  =======================================================================\n  To install 5D-BaudCheck you must have all Requirement which were\n  mentioned below. You need the following things.\n\n  --------------------------\n    Doors:5D-BaudCheck (dir)\n      ^^^ 5D-BaudCheck\n    BBS:Commands/SysCmd (dir)\n      ^^^ FRONTEND.info\n  --------------------------\n\n  Decruch the 5D-BaudCheck Archive. Go to your ''Doors:'' Directory\n  and make a Directory called ''5D-BaudCheck''. Copy ''5D-BaudCheck''\n  into the Directory. Go to your ''BBS:Commands/SysCmd'' Directory.\n  Copy ''FRONTEND.info'' into it.\n  =======================================================================\n@endnode\n@node Cap04 "Tooltype Informations..."\n  =======================================================================\n  - All tooltypes available in ''Doors:5D-BaudCheck/5D-BaudCheck.info''\n\n  LOW_BAUD=2400               - Allows you to set the baud rate at which\n                                5D-BaudCheck shall ask the user for the\n                                password. If he enters the wrong pw he\n                                will be logged out!\n  PASSWORD=LAMER_SUX          - Allows you to set the pw which will\n                                be asked if the baud rate is not high\n                                enough.\n  =======================================================================\n@endnode\n@node Cap05 "Greetings go to..."\n  =======================================================================\n\n              ···­­­> ALL MEMBERS OF 5TH DYNASTY <­­­···\n\n          .------------------------------------------------.\n          : And all people who I know and all who know me! :\n          `------------------------------------------------''\n\n  =======================================================================\n@endnode\n@node Cap06 "How to contact me..."\n  =======================================================================\n\n                   >>> CALL ALL 5TH DYNASTY HQS! <<<\n\n    .     /\_________  ______/\  /\______    /\_________  ______/\   .\n    .    _\______   .\ \______/ _\____   \  _\______   .\ \______/   .\n    :   /   _/ _/    \\/     .\/   __|   .\/   _/ _/    \\/     .\   :\n    |  /    \  \      \\      \\   \__    \\   \  \      \\      \\  |\n    +--\_____\__\       \____ //_____|     \\___\__\       \____ //--+\n    :            \  ____/    \/      |______/       \  ____/    \/   :\n    .             \/                                 \/              .\n               ___.\n              /  .|___    _______/\    /\______    ___________/\\n             /   ||   \  _\_  ____/_  _\____   \  _\_  __      /\n            /         .\/      /   .\/   __|   .\/     \______/\n           /      _    \\    _/     \\   \__    \\         .\\n           \______|     \\_________  /_____|     \\_______ //\n                  |______/         \/      |______/       \/\n\n               ···­­­>   \%\ 5TH DYNASTY GHQ \%\   <­­­···\n\n                        SYSOP: SvEN tHE CREAToR\n                        COSYS: Mr.Return\n                               Cee Jay\n\n                    -<>- CaLL: +49-(0)30-7424141 -<>-\n\n  =======================================================================\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',10138,1,0,NULL,NULL,'5d_bch','scan',1780048351);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('5d_bchck','5D-BCHCK.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/5D-BCHCK.LHA','5D-BaudCheck','XIM','5D-BaudCheck',NULL,NULL,'5D','______  __  / ____  \___  \  _____  ___  / \/  /  /  /  /  /  /  ¬  /\_  \ /  //  /  / /  /  /\__  /  /  /  /  /  /  //  /_\__  /',replace('5tH_/\____/\_ __/\__ _/\__ _/\_____/\__/\_ _\n______  __  / ____  \___  \  _____  ___  /\n \/  /  /  /  /  /  /  ¬  /\_  \ /  //  /  /\n /  /  /\__  /  /  /  /  /  /  //  /_\__  /\n/___  /___  /__/  /__/  /___  //  //___  /__\n____ /_ __ /____ /____ / ___ /__ /_ ___ //\nbIS\/    \/    \/    \/    \/  \/     \/\n     Baud rate detecter for ami/x\n','\n',char(10)),'5D-BaudCheck.guide',replace('@database 5D-BaudCheckDoc\n\nCopyright (c) 1993 SvEN tHE CREAToR / 5th Dynasty\n\n@Remark $VER: (October 9 1993, 15:30:00)\n@Remark AmigaGuide database for the 5D-BaudCheck Documentation\n\n@node MAIN "5D-BaudCheck Documentation (c)1993 SvEN tHE CREAToR of 5th Dynasty (October 9 1993, 15:30:00)"\n          ______    ______    ______    ______    ______    ______\n          \   ¬/    \   ¬/    \   ¬/    \   ¬/    \   ¬/    \   ¬/\n 5th ______\  /_ ____\  /______\  /______\  /______\  /______\  /_ ____\n    //     \\// |   \\\//     \\\//     \\\//     \\\//     \\\// |   \\\n   //       \/  |    \\/       \\/  |    \\/     ---\/       \\/  |    \\\n  /·         \___     ·\     |  ·\        ·\____    \\__      ·\___     ·\\n /·         | \        ·\    |   ·\ |      ·\        ·\ |      ·\        ·\\n \___________ /________ /____|___ /_|______ /________ / |______ /________ /\n            \/        \/        \/        \/        \/        \/    ·cj·\/\n\n                             >>> 5D-BaudCheck <<<\n\n                      Code & Design: SvEN tHE CREAToR/5D\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------- \n\n         >>> C·O·N·T·E·N·T·S  O·F  D·O·C·U·M·E·N·T·A·T·I·O·N <<<\n\n                         @{"      Introduction      " Link Cap01}\n                         @{"      Requirements      " Link Cap02}\n                         @{"      Installation      " Link Cap03}\n                         @{"       Tooltypes!       " Link Cap04}\n                         @{"       Greetings!       " Link Cap05}\n                         @{"   How to Contact me?   " Link Cap06}\n\n         ----------------------------------------------------------\n            Complete Docs for 5D-BaudCheck V0.01 [-5th Dynasty-]\n         ----------------------------------------------------------\n         The Documentation has been written by SvEN tHE CREAToR/5D.\n\n@endnode\n@node Cap01 "Introduction"\n  =======================================================================\n  5D-BaudCheck is a tool which allows the sysop to don''t allow users with\n  low baud connect to enter into the bbs except some users who have the\n  password to enter.\n  =======================================================================\n@endnode\n@node Cap02 "Requirements"\n  =======================================================================\n  To install 5D-BaudCheck you must have the following things:\n\n    Programm      Location            Description\n    ----------    --------            -----------\n    5D-BaudCheck  Doors:5D-BaudCheck  Main program\n\n  - an  Amiga Model (500/600/1000/1200/2000/2500/3000/4000/CDTV/CD³²)\n  - the installed Version of OS\2, OS\3, OS/432 or higher\n    (Soft-, Bit-, Hardware Version)\n  - the installed .INFO Files in the directories.\n  - AmiExpress V2.xx , v3.xx , v4.xx or higher.\n\n  =======================================================================\n@endnode\n@node Cap03 "How to install 5D-BaudCheck"\n  =======================================================================\n  To install 5D-BaudCheck you must have all Requirement which were\n  mentioned below. You need the following things.\n\n  --------------------------\n    Doors:5D-BaudCheck (dir)\n      ^^^ 5D-BaudCheck\n    BBS:Commands/SysCmd (dir)\n      ^^^ FRONTEND.info\n  --------------------------\n\n  Decruch the 5D-BaudCheck Archive. Go to your ''Doors:'' Directory\n  and make a Directory called ''5D-BaudCheck''. Copy ''5D-BaudCheck''\n  into the Directory. Go to your ''BBS:Commands/SysCmd'' Directory.\n  Copy ''FRONTEND.info'' into it.\n  =======================================================================\n@endnode\n@node Cap04 "Tooltype Informations..."\n  =======================================================================\n  - All tooltypes available in ''Doors:5D-BaudCheck/5D-BaudCheck.info''\n\n  LOW_BAUD=2400               - Allows you to set the baud rate at which\n                                5D-BaudCheck shall ask the user for the\n                                password. If he enters the wrong pw he\n                                will be logged out!\n  PASSWORD=LAMER_SUX          - Allows you to set the pw which will\n                                be asked if the baud rate is not high\n                                enough.\n  =======================================================================\n@endnode\n@node Cap05 "Greetings go to..."\n  =======================================================================\n\n              ···­­­> ALL MEMBERS OF 5TH DYNASTY <­­­···\n\n          .------------------------------------------------.\n          : And all people who I know and all who know me! :\n          `------------------------------------------------''\n\n  =======================================================================\n@endnode\n@node Cap06 "How to contact me..."\n  =======================================================================\n\n                   >>> CALL ALL 5TH DYNASTY HQS! <<<\n\n    .     /\_________  ______/\  /\______    /\_________  ______/\   .\n    .    _\______   .\ \______/ _\____   \  _\______   .\ \______/   .\n    :   /   _/ _/    \\/     .\/   __|   .\/   _/ _/    \\/     .\   :\n    |  /    \  \      \\      \\   \__    \\  