n\n\n                             RubberStamp V1.3\n                             ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n            Docs By Dark Angel (but blame Strobe for the code)\n\n\n                         I N T R O D U C T I O N \n\nOi  you!   yeah you...  you know that bloody timestamp door that bombs your\nbbs when it runs?  Well this ain''t it...  this WORKS :)))) B O N U S !\n\nErm...   i''m supposed to be serious now..  but instead i''ll tell you it''s a\nreally  funky  timestamp  replacement door for ALL machines, written in C++\n(fast) and completely system legal (for a change).\n\nYou can define how it looks, take it to parties, show it to your girlfriend\n(not included in this archive folks) and generally make your users think of\nyou as a demi god :*)\n\nInstall it... then tell me it''s shite alright ?\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nIt''s another eXCiTIng door from Strobe and Dark Angel of 976 Ev!L in Sunny\n                                 ENGLAND!\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n                         R E Q U I R E M E N T S \n\n\nAn  Amiga,  a  hardisk,  /X, sadistic tendancies, your Grandma''s teeth and a\nlittle  time  to  spare (about 30 seconds average).  Sysops of Phantasm may\nrequire a little more time, say a day or two ;*)\n\n\n                         I N S T A L L A T I O N \n\n                                 LOAD OPUS\n            Copy the files to the relevant dirs on your bbs... \n                                 FUCK OFF\n\n\n                        C O N F I G U R A T I O N \n\nTooltypes:\n-=-=-=-=-\n\nSTAMP\n\nThis tooltype defines the groovy look of the timestamp entry on the\nfilelisting for all remote callers to the bbs..  Dead simple and quite\nhonestly I don''t see any point in telling you about it :) So I''m lazy...\nshoot me!\n\nExample tooltype configuration:\n\nSTAMP=-+=[ @HOU:@MIN:@SEC ]--[ Node @NOD ]--[ @CPS CPS ]=+-\n\nBecomes:\n\n--[23:32]--[On Node #0]--[CPS: 4536]--\n\n\n                               -------------\nSTAMP.LOCAL\n\nThis very exciting and interesting tooltype defines the look of the local\nuploads to the bbs (e.g.  local node sysop).  Basically used when the CPS\nrate is Zero, nil, nothing, nada...  or less than 1 :)\n\nExample tooltype configuration:\n\nSTAMP.LOCAL=-+=[ @HOU:@MIN:@SEC ]--[ Node @NOD ]--[ SYSOP UL ]=+-\n\nBecomes:\n\n--[23:32]--[On Node #0]--[ SYSOP UL ]--\n\nTOOLTYPE NOTE:\n\nFor BOTH of these tooltypes the following applies:\n\n@HOU is the hour of the upload\n@MIN is the minute of the upload\n@SEC is the second (fucking hell this is smart) of the upload\n@NOD is the node the file was upped on\n@CPS is the cps rate reported by /X :*) [very acurate m8]\n\nANSI colour codes supported in the tooltypes so USE ''EM!\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n                          R E G I S T R A T I O M\n\nIt''s a good idea. It''s free. Just do it.\n\nSpecial registration competition!!!\n\nIf you can find out HOW to register this program then a registered copy\nwill be yours!!!\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n                            G R E E T I N G S \n\nHello to everyone on planet Earth from me, Dark Angel and Strobe (who''s\nwatching me type which is a real putoff y''know...  God I hate some\npeople...  btw I''m totally sane contrary to popular opinion on the\nscene)...\n\nHello to everyone not on planet Earth...  especially the guys from uranus -\ncos let''s face it you''ve got to have a sense of humour to come from a\nplanet named after your arse :)\n\n[Fuck me why did I ask this nutter to do the docs ;) - Strobe]\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',11458,2,0,NULL,NULL,'976rs13','scan',1780048365);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('a__fron','A!-FRON.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/A!-FRON.LHA','FrontEnd','XIM','frontend',NULL,NULL,'A!','_7______ ·\_ _7 ____/____   _7______   ·/ ._\_    \/   /_\_______  _/_ _\_    \/   /_. |       /___/|·      \/     Y       /___/  |',replace('   _________    _______        ____________\n  _7______ ·\_ _7 ____/____   _7______   ·/\n._\_    \/   /_\_______  _/_ _\_    \/   /_.\n|       /___/|·      \/     Y       /___/  |\nl________j   l_______/      l_______ _     |\n |                `----------'' -d!--------+''\n/\      a!-FrontStatus V1.3 For /X        |_                                \n¯| Shows BPS ^ Sysop Avail - Inc Preview! \/\n |    [vIäRsÅjÄvLAbRasÅnIaNArfANiNTE!]    |\n `-----------------------------------[cP]-''\n\n\n','\n',char(10)),'a!-FrontStatus.dOC',replace('\n[=/===/=/==[sEARCH¡NG fOR fR¡ENdSh¡P? - nO nEEd tO loOK fURTHER]==\=\===\=]\n              _________ ________________\n           .__\________Y_  __________  _\  _____________________\n   __  _   |:· _______///'' ¬       ¬T  ¬\\/______  _ ___,      ¬|   _  __\n .-\ \-\\--|   ¬''      |   :        |    \/    ¬'' :\\\__________|--//-/ /-.\n |         |           |   .        |             |            ¬\         |\n |         l___________l____________l_____________l______________\        |\n |                                                                        |\n |     [ /X 4.9 ^ a12Oo/o3O/5o/6 ^ 28k8 uSR ^ 1.7 Gb oF wARE^sPACE! ]     |\n |                                                                        |\n |                 [ dOM¡NAtOR : zUG/pROJEkT sERO ^ fLOW ]                |\n |   [ SlAVES : a!DS/fLW^pSE - f!N/pSE - RibE/pSE - m7G/fLW - zBR/fLW ]   |\n |                                                                        |\n |        [ nODE ¹ : +46-321-141o3 ^ nODE ² : +46-cOMM¡NG sOOn!! ]        |\n |                                                                        |\n |             [ aM¡GAEL¡tE ^ /X SUPPORt ^ CONSOlE ^ MOdUlES ]            |\n |             [ ASC¡¡ ^ bLONd pWR! ^ lEGAl StUFf ^ REQUEStS ]            |\n |                _____________________________ ______                    |\n |               |.··           _             ¬Y  ___/______              |\n |               |:             T_             |  ¬       ¬T              |\n `-/ /-//--------|.             | \            |           |-------\\-\ \-''\n   ¯¯  ¯         l______________l_\\_          l___________|        ¯  ¯¯\n                                    \___________|!CE\n \n[=\===\=\==[pROJEkT sERO WhQ ^ fLOW dlX hQ - coOL cREW! - wAREZ]==/=/===/=]\n\n\n\n\n           [  FrontStatus V1.3 Public By a!DS/pSE!^fLW in 1996 ]\n\n\n\n\n                            [- Introduction -]\n\n                     This door was coded using AmigaE!\n  I never planned to release a Public Version but Whattaheck, Here it is.\n\n\n\n                     [- Stuff Used While Developing -]\n\n                               General Snus\n                               RaveMeister 2\n                          Telepfhunken RC 870 CD\n                               Pfhilips RGB\n                                 USR 28k8\n                            Amiga 1200/o3O/5o/6\n\n\n\n\n                            [- Requierments -]\n\n       You will need a Amiga/Compatible and a /X / Clone BBS system\n\n       I haven''t tested this on earlier AmiExpress System Than 4.9.\n      I think it will work fine on Clones and earlier Versions of /X.\n                    Contact me on Acme^Inc for reports!\n\n\n\n\n                            [- Installation -]\n\n                           For Early /X systems:\n                           ---------------------\n\n           Copy the "DOORS" directory to your DOORS: directory.\n               Edit the bbs:commands/sys.cmd file and type:\n\nFRONTEND	XM005DOORS:a!dOoRS/a!-FrontStatus/FRONTEND\n                || |   |\n                || |   `---- Door Location \n		|| `-------- Lowest Access to use door    \n                |`---------- Multinode\n                `----------- DoorType \n\n\n                         For IconBased /X systems:\n                         -------------------------\n\n           Copy the "DOORS" directory to your DOORS: directory.\n           Copy the "COMMANDS" directory to your BBS: directory.\n\n                       It SHOULD work fine by now...\n\n\n\n                       [- Greetings in no order 2 -]\n\n\n          zUG - [maytag] - zABlER - Vlad - FENRiZ - iCE - GUffAW \n           logobyte - orchis - Tr!nitY - Dixy - LAdY jAY - 6pac \n             Xerxes - Aeroba - typhoon - RiBE - dEAMO - cOSMO\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',17688,7,0,NULL,NULL,'rnsc_fe4','scan',1780048365);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('a_aqwk24','A!AQWK24.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/A!AQWK24.LHA','AmiQWK','XIM','AmiQWK',NULL,NULL,NULL,'This is version 2.4 of the AmiQWK II QWKMail reader.  It fixes the work directory bug in version 2.3',replace(replace('AmiQWK 2.4 QWKMail reader for AmigaDOS 2.04+\r\n\r\nThis is version 2.4 of the AmiQWK II QWKMail \r\nreader.  It fixes the work directory bug in \r\nversion 2.3\r\n\r\n','\r',char(13)),'\n',char(10)),'AmiQWK.guide',replace('@database AmiQWK.guide\n\n@Master amiqwk.texi\n\n@Width 72\n\n\nThis is the AmigaGuide® file AmiQWK.guide, produced by Makeinfo-1.55 from \nthe input file amiqwk.texi.\n\n\n@Node Main "AmiQWK.guide"\n@Next "Introduction"\n\n\n\n\n\nChapters:\n\n @{" Introduction " Link "Introduction"} \n @{" Legal Stuff " Link "Legal Stuff"} \n @{" System Requirements " Link "System Requirements"} \n @{" Installation and Quick Setup " Link "Installation and Quick Setup"} \n @{" Using AmiQWK " Link "Using AmiQWK"} \n @{" Reading and Writing Messages " Link "Reading and Writing Messages"} \n @{" Configuration " Link "Configuration"} \n\nAppendixes:\n\n @{" Advanced QWK features " Link "Advanced QWK features"}            Adding, Dropping conferences, etc.\n @{" The Future of AmiQWK " Link "The Future of AmiQWK"}             What to look for in future versions.\n @{" Technical Support " Link "Technical Support"}                How to get technical support.\n @{" Acknowledgments " Link "Acknowledgments"}                  Some of the people who made `AmiQWK'' possible.\n @{" Index " Link "Index"}                            Concept Index.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Introduction" "AmiQWK.guide/Introduction"\n@Next "Legal Stuff"\n@Prev "Main"\n@Toc "Main"\n\nIntroduction\n************\n\n\n @{" About this manual " Link "About this manual"}    About the `AmiQWK II'' Manual.\n @{" What is QWKMail? " Link "What is QWKMail?"}     Description of QWKMail.\n @{" What is AmiQWK II? " Link "What is AmiQWK II?"}   Description of `AmiQWK II''.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "About this manual" "AmiQWK.guide/About this manual"\n@Next "What is QWKMail?"\n@Toc "Introduction"\n\nAbout this manual\n=================\n\n   This manual assumes that you have at least a basic knowledge of the\nAmiga operating system. If you are not familiar with the Amiga I,\nrecommend reading the ''Basic Operations'' chapter of your AmigaDOS\nmanual.\n\n   This manual was written in `Texinfo'', the GNU documentation format,\nand processed through `MakeGuide'' to generate ASCII, `AmigaGuide'', TeX,\nand PostScript versions.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "What is QWKMail?" "AmiQWK.guide/What is QWKMail?"\n@Next "What is AmiQWK II?"\n@Prev "About this manual"\n@Toc "Introduction"\n\nWhat is QWKMail?\n================\n\n   QWKMail is an offline message format. Using QWKMail allows you to\ncall a BBS, collect all waiting messages, transfer them to your\ncomputer, and read them after you have logged off of the BBS. You can\nthen read them with a QWK compatible message reader such as `AmiQWK''.\nNew messages can be edited with your favorite text editor. Some of the\nadvantages of using QWKMail include:\n\n   * Collecting all waiting messages into a QWKMail packet usually\n     takes only a fraction of the time it takes to read messages\n     online, resulting in lower phone bills.\n\n   * Since your replies are edited offline, you can take as much time\n     as you need to enter and reply to messages. You also have the\n     advantage of using tools that may not be available when using BBS\n     editors, such as spelling and grammar checkers.\n\n   * You can easily save or print messages for future reference.\n\n   The QWK format was created in 1987 by Mark ''Sparky'' Herring. It is\nbased on Clark Development Corp.''s `PC-Board'' Version 12.0 BBS message\nbase format.  The QWKMail format is now supported by most BBS programs\neither internally or by an external ''door'' program.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "What is AmiQWK II?" "AmiQWK.guide/What is AmiQWK II?"\n@Prev "What is QWKMail?"\n@Toc "Introduction"\n\nWhat is AmiQWK II?\n==================\n\n   `AmiQWK II'' is a full featured QWKMail offline message reader for the\nCommodore Amiga computer. My goals for `AmiQWK'' are (in no particular\norder)\n\n   * To be the most stable and compatible QWKMail reader available for\n     the Commodore Amiga computer.\n\n   * To be the most full featured QWKMail reader for the Commodore Amiga\n     computer.\n\n   * To take advantage of features found Release 2 and higher of the\n     Amiga operating system.\n\n   * To be easy to use.\n\n   * To be highly configurable.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Legal Stuff" "AmiQWK.guide/Legal Stuff"\n@Next "System Requirements"\n@Prev "Introduction"\n@Toc "Main"\n\nLegal Stuff\n***********\n\n\n @{" About Shareware " Link "About Shareware"}      About the shareware concept.\n @{" Registration " Link "Registration"}         How to register `AmiQWK''.\n @{" Warranty " Link "Warranty"}             Warranty information.\n @{" Copyright " Link "Copyright"}            Copyright information.\n @{" Distribution " Link "Distribution"}         Distribution information.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "About Shareware" "AmiQWK.guide/About Shareware"\n@Next "Registration"\n@Toc "Legal Stuff"\n\nAbout Shareware\n===============\n\n   `AmiQWK II'' is released under the concept of Shareware. This means\nthat you are granted a license to use `AmiQWK II'' for a period of 30\ndays after the initial use. After 30 days you must either register the\nprogram or discontinue its use. See @{"Registration" Link "Registration"}, for more details.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Registration" "AmiQWK.guide/Registration"\n@Next "Warranty"\n@Prev "About Shareware"\n@Toc "Legal Stuff"\n\nRegistration\n============\n\n   To register `AmiQWK'', fill out the registration form (filename\n`Registration.form'') and send it along with your payment to the address\non the registration form. You will receive a 16 digit registration key\nbased on your name. Enter this number into the ''Register'' window of the\nconfiguration editor and `AmiQWK II'' will generate a keyfile\n(`AmiQWK.KEY'') that will remove the shareware registration notices.\n\n   Recommended method of payment is a check drwan from a U.S. bank or a\nmoney order in US dollars. (I can no longer accept personal checks\ndrawn from Canadian banks due to a change in bank policy.) Cash is\naccepted (US Funds only), however you send cash at your own risk.\n\n   AmiQWK users in New Zealand and Australia can register through my\nNew Zealand distributor. See the registration form (filename\n`registration.form'' for more details.\n\n   The registration key will work with all minor revisions of `AmiQWK\nII''.  (i.e. all versions up to, but not including, 3.0) When a new\nmajor revision becomes available, registered `AmiQWK II'' users will be\neligible for reduced cost updates.\n\n   Most registrations are processed within 2 working days. If a network\naddress is given, I will send your registration key via email in\naddition to postal mail.\n\n   Group registrations and site licenses are available, Contact the\nauthor for details. See @{"Technical Support" Link "Technical Support"}.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Warranty" "AmiQWK.guide/Warranty"\n@Next "Copyright"\n@Prev "Registration"\n@Toc "Legal Stuff"\n\nWarranty\n========\n\n   THIS PRODUCT IS PROVIDED "AS-IS" WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND. ALL\nRISKS AND DAMAGES, INCIDENTAL OR OTHERWISE, ARISING FROM THE USE,\nMISUSE, OR INABILITY TO USE THIS PROGRAM ARE ENTIRELY THE\nRESPONSIBILITY OF THE USER.  THE AUTHOR DOES NOT MAKE ANY GUARANTEES OR\nREPRESENTATIONS REGARDING THE CORRECTNESS, RELIABILITY, ACCURACY,\nCURRENTNESS, ETC. OF THIS PROGRAM. THE AUTHOR WILL NOT ACCEPT\nRESPONSIBILITY FOR ANY DAMAGE OR LOSSES RESULTING FORM THE USE, MISUSE,\nOR INABILITY TO USE THIS PRODUCT.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Copyright" "AmiQWK.guide/Copyright"\n@Next "Distribution"\n@Prev "Warranty"\n@Toc "Legal Stuff"\n\nCopyright\n=========\n\n   The `AmiQWK II'' software and documentation are copyright (C)\n1992,1993 Jim Dawson. All rights reserved.\n\n   `AmigaGuide'', `AmigaGuide.info'', `amigaguide.library'' (C) Copyright\n1992 Commodore-Amiga, Inc. All Rights Reserved. Reproduced and\ndistributed under license from Commodore.\n\n   `ReqTools'' and `reqtools.library'' are Copyright (C) Nico François.\n\n   All product names used in this document are trademarks of their\nrespective owners.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Distribution" "AmiQWK.guide/Distribution"\n@Prev "Copyright"\n@Toc "Legal Stuff"\n\nDistribution\n============\n\n   Regardless of the method of distribution, `AmiQWK II'' is NOT and\nnever has been public domain.\n\n   `AmiQWK II'' may be distributed freely, providing the following\ncriteria are met:\n\n   * Distribution is limited to the original shareware distribution\n     only. None of the files in the `AmiQWK II'' distribution archive\n     may be modified or omitted.\n\n   * No material gain may be realized from the distribution of `AmiQWK\n     II'', other than a small amount to cover distribution materials.\n\n   * `AmiQWK II'' may be included in freely distributable software\n     libraries, including the Fred Fish collection.\n\n   * `AmiQWK II'' may not be bundled with any hardware or software\n     product without prior written consent from Jim Dawson.\n\n   * Registration numbers for `AmiQWK'', and the key file that `AmiQWK\n     II'' generates from them (`AmiQWK.KEY'') may not be distributed.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "System Requirements" "AmiQWK.guide/System Requirements"\n@Next "Installation and Quick Setup"\n@Prev "Legal Stuff"\n@Toc "Main"\n\nSystem Requirements\n*******************\n\n\n @{" Hardware Requirements " Link "Hardware Requirements"} \n @{" Software Requirements " Link "Software Requirements"} \n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Hardware Requirements" "AmiQWK.guide/Hardware Requirements"\n@Next "Software Requirements"\n@Toc "System Requirements"\n\nHardware Requirements\n=====================\n\n   `AmiQWK'' requires the following hardware:\n\n   * Amiga computer.\n\n   * 512KB RAM. (1MB or more recommended.)\n\n   * Floppy drive (Second floppy drive or hard drive highly\n     recommended.)\n\n   * Printer. (if you want to print messages.)\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Software Requirements" "AmiQWK.guide/Software Requirements"\n@Prev "Hardware Requirements"\n@Toc "System Requirements"\n\nSoftware Requirements\n=====================\n\n   `AmiQWK'' requires the following software:\n\n   * Workbench 2.04 (V37) or higher.\n\n   * A text editor that can save ASCII text without any formatting\n     info. (ED and MEMACS that come with Workbench are fine.)\n\n   * Any archivers you plan to use. (`ZIP'', `LHA/LHArc'', `ZOO'', and\n     `ARC'' are currently supported)\n\n   * `reqtools.library''. (included with `AmiQWK II'' distribution\n     archive.)\n\n   * `amigaguide.library''. (included with `AmiQWK II'' distribution\n     archive, only required for online help.)\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Installation and Quick Setup" "AmiQWK.guide/Installation and Quick Setup"\n@Next "Using AmiQWK"\n@Prev "System Requirements"\n@Toc "Main"\n\nInstallation and Quick Setup\n****************************\n\n   To install `AmiQWK'', just double-click on the ''Install_AQ2'' icon.\nThis will copy the `reqtools.library'' and `amigaguide.library'' to your\n`libs:'' directory. If newer versions of either library are already\npresent, the library will not be copied.\n\n   Once the libraries have been installed, run `AmiQWK'' by\ndouble-clicking on it''s icon or by typing `AmiQWK'' from the `CLI''.\n\n   Once `AmiQWK'' is running, you will need to configure it to work on\nyour system. Click on the gadget labeled ''Config `AmiQWK''...'' or type\n''C'' (1) to bring up the configuration editor window.\n\n   The configuration editor window has 9 gadgets, the first 6 of which\nwhen clicked on will bring up a configuration sub-window. The remaining\n3 gadgets are used to save the configuration to disk, use the\nconfiguration without saving, and to cancel changes you have made to\nthe configuration. The following describes only the most basic\nconfiguration options needed to get `AmiQWK'' running, See\n@{"Configuration" Link "Configuration"}, for a more detailed description of all of the\nconfiguration options.\n\n`Operation''\n     Change the ''Editor'' string gadget to whatever editor you use.\n     About the only restrictions on the editor are that it must save\n     text in plain ASCII format (with no formatting codes) and that it\n     does not detach itself from the CLI process that spawned it. Here\n     are some examples:\n\n    `CygnusEd''\n          `c:ed -sticky'' (See @{"CygnusEd Notes" Link "CygnusEd Notes"}.)\n\n    `TurboText''\n          `c:ttx WAIT''\n\n    `Ed (AmigaDos)''\n          `c:ed''\n\n    `MEmacs (AmigaDos)''\n          `sys:tools/memacs''\n\n    `GoldEd''\n          `c:ed sticky''\n\n     See @{"Operation window" Link "Operation window"}, for more information.\n\n`Replies''\n     The default configuration for replies should not need to be\n     changed for most applications. See @{"Replies window" Link "Replies window"}, for more\n     information.\n\n`Paths''\n     In the Paths window you tell `AmiQWK'' where it should look for and\n     store certain files.\n\n    `Packet Dir''\n          This is where `AmiQWK'' should look for mail packets. This is\n          normally the same directory your term program uses for\n          downloads.\n\n    `Reply Dir''\n          This is where `AmiQWK'' stores replies. This is normally the\n          same directory your term program uses for uploads.\n\n    `Work Dir''\n          This is where `AmiQWK'' creates its work directory. If you\n          have enough memory, you might want to change this to `RAM:''\n          for best performance. If you leave it blank `AmiQWK'' will\n          create the work directory in the `AmiQWK'' program directory.\n\n     See @{"Paths window" Link "Paths window"}, for more information.\n\n`Archivers''\n     You will probably not need to change anything in the Archivers\n     window.  See @{"Archivers window" Link "Archivers window"}, for more information.\n\n`Graphics''\n     You will probably not need to make changes in the Graphics window\n     to get `AmiQWK'' to work. See @{"Graphics window" Link "Graphics window"}, for more information.\n\n`Register''\n     Enter your name in the gadget labeled ''Your Name''. If you have\n     registered, enter your registration key number in the\n     ''Registration Key'' gadget, otherwise leave it blank. See\n     @{"Register window" Link "Register window"}, for more information.\n\n   Once you have your configuration set, click on the ''Save'' gadget of\nthe ''Config'' window to save it to disk. If you think you messed up\nsomewhere and want to start again from scratch, click on ''Cancel''. If\nyou want to try out your configuration before you save it, click on\n''Use''.\n\n   ---------- Footnotes ----------\n\n   (1)  Most actions in `AmiQWK'' can be accomplished by using either\nthe mouse or the keyboard. Whenever a keyboard shortcut exists it will\nusually have the shortcut key underlined.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Using AmiQWK" "AmiQWK.guide/Using AmiQWK"\n@Next "Reading and Writing Messages"\n@Prev "Installation and Quick Setup"\n@Toc "Main"\n\nUsing AmiQWK\n************\n\n\n @{" Starting AmiQWK " Link "Starting AmiQWK"} \n @{" Select Packet window " Link "Select Packet window"} \n @{" Registered To " Link "Registered To"} \n @{" Open Packet... " Link "Open Packet..."} \n @{" Config AmiQWK... " Link "Config AmiQWK..."} \n @{" About AmiQWK... " Link "About AmiQWK..."} \n @{" Rename Packet... " Link "Rename Packet..."} \n @{" HELP!!!... " Link "HELP!!!..."} \n @{" Delete Packet... " Link "Delete Packet..."} \n @{" Quit and Exit... " Link "Quit and Exit..."} \n @{" Opening a packet " Link "Opening a packet"} \n @{" Select item to read window " Link "Select item to read window"} \n @{" Text Viewer " Link "Text Viewer"} \n @{" ANSI Viewer " Link "ANSI Viewer"} \n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Starting AmiQWK" "AmiQWK.guide/Starting AmiQWK"\n@Next "Select Packet window"\n@Toc "Using AmiQWK"\n\nStarting AmiQWK\n===============\n\n   Before you use `AmiQWK'', You will need to download a QWKMail packet\nfrom your favorite BBS. Consult the online documentation for the BBS\nQWK mailer (or, if all else fails, the system operator) for\ninstructions on how to download a QWKMail packet. `AmiQWK'' will run\nwithout any packets, but you won''t be able to do much with it.\n\n     *TIP:* Do *NOT* use Zmodem Resume mode when downloading QWKMail\n     packets.\n     \n     Since most BBSes use the same filename for packets every time, if you\n     already have a QWK packet in your downloads directory your term program will\n     think you are trying to resume an aborted transfer, and the new packet will\n     be appended to the old one instead of creating a new file.\n\n   Once you have a QWKMail packet, start `AmiQWK'' by double clicking\nthe `AmiQWK'' icon or typing ''`AmiQWK'''' from the CLI. `AmiQWK'' will open\na custom, public screen (named ''AMIQWK'') with a window titled ''Select\nPacket''. (If you haven''t registered yet, a window will appear reminding\nyou to register before the ''Select Packet'' window (See\n@{"Select Packet window" Link "Select Packet window"}.) appears, as well as several other places in the\nprogram.) See @{"Registration" Link "Registration"}, for more details about registering `AmiQWK''.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Select Packet window" "AmiQWK.guide/Select Packet window"\n@Next "Registered To"\n@Prev "Starting AmiQWK"\n@Toc "Using AmiQWK"\n\nSelect Packet window\n====================\n\n   From the Select Packet window, you can open a QWKMail packet for\nreading, delete or rename packets, enter the configuration editor, and\nget information about the program. The Select Packet window has the\nfollowing gadgets:\n\n`Registered To''\n     Name of the registered user. See @{"Registered To" Link "Registered To"}.\n\n`Open Packet...''\n     Open a packet for reading. See @{"Open Packet..." Link "Open Packet..."}.\n\n`Config AmiQWK...''\n     Open the configuration editor. See @{"Main Configuration Window" Link "Main Configuration Window"}.\n\n`About AmiQWK...''\n     Displays version, and copyright information, as well as how to get\n     technical support and where to send your registration fees. See\n     @{"About AmiQWK..." Link "About AmiQWK..."}.\n\n`Rename Packet...''\n     Rename or move a packet. See @{"Rename Packet..." Link "Rename Packet..."}.\n\n`HELP!!!...''\n     Get online help. See @{"HELP!!!..." Link "HELP!!!..."}.\n\n`Delete Packet...''\n     Delete a packet. See @{"Delete Packet..." Link "Delete Packet..."}.\n\n`Quit and Exit...''\n     Exit program. See @{"Quit and Exit..." Link "Quit and Exit..."}.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Registered To" "AmiQWK.guide/Registered To"\n@Next "Open Packet..."\n@Prev "Select Packet window"\n@Toc "Using AmiQWK"\n\nRegistered To\n=============\n\n   This read only text gadget displays the name of the person who has\nregistered this copy of `AmiQWK'', or ''** UNREGISTERED EVALUATION COPY\n**'' if `AmiQWK'' cannot process the registration key. This gadget is\nread-only. See @{"Registration" Link "Registration"}, for more information on registering\n`AmiQWK''.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Open Packet..." "AmiQWK.guide/Open Packet..."\n@Next "Config AmiQWK..."\n@Prev "Registered To"\n@Toc "Using AmiQWK"\n\nOpen Packet...\n==============\n\n   When the ''Open Packet...'' gadget is selected, `AmiQWK'' opens a file\nrequester for you to select the mail packet to be opened. See\n@{"Opening a packet" Link "Opening a packet"}, for more information.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Config AmiQWK..." "AmiQWK.guide/Config AmiQWK..."\n@Next "About AmiQWK..."\n@Prev "Open Packet..."\n@Toc "Using AmiQWK"\n\nConfig AmiQWK...\n================\n\n   Clicking on this gadget opens the configuration editor. See\n@{"Main Configuration Window" Link "Main Configuration Window"}, for more information.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "About AmiQWK..." "AmiQWK.guide/About AmiQWK..."\n@Next "Rename Packet..."\n@Prev "Config AmiQWK..."\n@Toc "Using AmiQWK"\n\nAbout AmiQWK...\n===============\n\n   This gadget opens a window containing version and copyright\ninformation, and where to send registrations, bug reports, suggestions,\netc.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Rename Packet..." "AmiQWK.guide/Rename Packet..."\n@Next "HELP!!!..."\n@Prev "About AmiQWK..."\n@Toc "Using AmiQWK"\n\nRename Packet...\n================\n\n   This gadget opens a file requester to select a file to be renamed.\nOnce a file is selected, another file requester is opened to select the\nnew file name.\n\n   A file can be moved by using the rename function. Just enter a\ndifferent path in the ''Rename File As...'' file requester. You can even\n''Rename'' a file to another volume.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "HELP!!!..." "AmiQWK.guide/HELP!!!..."\n@Next "Delete Packet..."\n@Prev "Rename Packet..."\n@Toc "Using AmiQWK"\n\nHELP!!!...\n==========\n\n   This gadget brings up `AmigaGuide'' help for the Packet Selection\nwindow. You can get help for most windows by pressing the ''HELP'' key.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Delete Packet..." "AmiQWK.guide/Delete Packet..."\n@Next "Quit and Exit..."\n@Prev "HELP!!!..."\n@Toc "Using AmiQWK"\n\nDelete Packet...\n================\n\n   This gadget opens a file requester to select a file to be deleted.\nOnce a file is selected another requester will appear to ask for\nconfirmation before deleting the file.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Quit and Exit..." "AmiQWK.guide/Quit and Exit..."\n@Next "Opening a packet"\n@Prev "Delete Packet..."\n@Toc "Using AmiQWK"\n\nQuit and Exit...\n================\n\n   Click on this gadget to exit the program. Unless ''Ask Before Exit''\nin the Operations config window (See @{"Operation window" Link "Operation window"}.) is turned off\nyou will be asked for confirmation before `AmiQWK'' closes.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Opening a packet" "AmiQWK.guide/Opening a packet"\n@Next "Select item to read window"\n@Prev "Quit and Exit..."\n@Toc "Using AmiQWK"\n\nOpening a packet\n================\n\n   When ''Open Packet...'' is selected from the ''Select Packet'' window, a\nfile requester will appear to select the packet to open. Once a packet\nis selected, `AmiQWK'' closes the ''Select Packet'' window, extracts the\nmail packet into the work directory (automatically determining what\nmethod was used to compress the packet) as well as the reply packet, if\nit exists. The extraction procedure takes place in a CLI window that\nappears on the `AmiQWK'' screen. (assuming you haven''t changed the spawn\nwindow specifications in the Operations configuration window. (See\n@{"Operation window" Link "Operation window"}.))\n\n   Once the packet is extracted, `AmiQWK'' will scan the packet,\nbuilding lists of conferences and messages. This may take a while if\nyou are reading a large packet. If index files are not present in the\npacket or if the number of messages in the messages.dat file does not\nmatch the number of message indexes, `AmiQWK'' will attempt to generate\nthe indexes itself. (note that the indexes are not saved back to the\npacket, as `AmiQWK'' can generate the indexes very quickly.) Once the\npacket has been processed, the ''Select item to read'' window will open.\nSee @{"Select item to read window" Link "Select item to read window"}.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Select item to read window" "AmiQWK.guide/Select item to read window"\n@Next "Text Viewer"\n@Prev "Opening a packet"\n@Toc "Using AmiQWK"\n\nSelect item to read window\n==========================\n\n   This window gives important information about the packet and the BBS\nthat it came from, and has several gadgets for selecting various parts\nof the mail packet for reading. (note that some of the gadgets may be\ndisabled if the corresponding item is not available in the packet.)\nThere is also a menu which can be used to generate requests to add,\ndrop, or reset conferences (assuming that the QWK packer that generated\nthe packet can process these requests, otherwise the menu items will be\ndisabled.)\n\n   The following information about the packet and the BBS it came from\nis displayed on the left part of the window.\n\n`Packet:''\n     The filename of the packet (not including path).\n\n`BBS:''\n     The name of the BBS that the packet came from.\n\n`Location:''\n     The location of the BBS.\n\n`Sysop:''\n     The name of the system operator of the BBS.\n\n`Phone:''\n     Primary phone number of the BBS.\n\n`Packet ID:''\n     Packet identifier for generating reply packets.\n\n`Time:''\n     Time that the packet was created.\n\n`Date:''\n     Date that the packet was created.\n\n`User Name:''\n     Name of the person who downloaded the packet.\n\n   And on the right are the following gadgets. Note that some of them\nmay be disabled if they are not available.\n\n`''Hello'' File...''\n     Displays welcome text using the internal text viewer. (See\n     @{"Text Viewer" Link "Text Viewer"}.) Usually is the login and welcome screen from the\n     BBS, but may contain other information.\n\n`Bulletins...''\n     Display bulletin file(s) using the internal text viewer. (See\n     @{"Text Viewer" Link "Text Viewer"}.) A file requester will be opened to select which file\n     to read. The bulletin files are named ''BLT-x.y'' where ''x'' is the\n     conference the bulletin came from and ''y'' is the actual number of\n     the bulletin. (i.e. BLT-3.1 indicates that it is the first\n     bulletin in conference 3.) Bulletins are usually only included if\n     they have been updated since the last time you called the BBS.\n     Select ''Cancel'' on the file requester to return to the ''Select\n     item to read'' window.\n\n`News...''\n     Display the News file using the internal text viewer. (See\n     @{"Text Viewer" Link "Text Viewer"}.) This file can contain anything the sysop chooses.\n     Usually this file, like bulletins, is only included if it has been\n     updated since the last mail packet was downloaded.\n\n`Read Mail...''\n     Read messages. (See @{"Reading Messages" Link "Reading Messages"}.)\n\n`New Files...''\n     Displays a list of files recently posted to the BBS using the\n     internal text viewer. (See @{"Text Viewer" Link "Text Viewer"}.)\n\n`''Goodbye'' Text''\n     Displays logout text using the internal text viewer. (See\n     @{"Text Viewer" Link "Text Viewer"}.) Usually this is the text that the BBS displays to\n     users logging off of the system, however it may contain other\n     information.\n\n`Close Packet...''\n     Closes the packet currently being read and returns to the Select\n     Packet window. (See @{"Select Packet window" Link "Select Packet window"}.) If there are any\n     replies, they will be packed into a reply packet for uploading.\n\n`Exit AmiQWK...''\n     Exit program. Unless ''Ask Before Exit'' in the Operations config\n     window is turned off (See @{"Operation window" Link "Operation window"}.) you will be asked for\n     confirmation before `AmiQWK'' closes. If there are any replies,\n     they will be packed into a reply packet for uploading.\n\n   And finally, there is a menu named ''Conference''. It will contain the\nfollowing menu items, however these items may be disabled if the QWK\npacker cannot handle these requests.\n\n`Add Conference''\n     Add a conference to your list of active conferences. A window will\n     appear listing all conferences that don''t have any messages in\n     them (if they have messages, you must already be subscribed to\n     that conference.) once a conference is selected, you will be asked\n     for confirmation before the add conference request is generated.\n\n`Drop Conference''\n     Remove a conference from your list of active conferences. A window\n     will appear listing all conferences. Once a conference is\n     selected, you will be asked for confirmation before the drop\n     conference request is generated.\n\n`Reset Pointer''\n     Reset last read pointer within a conference. A window will appear\n     listing all conferences. Once a conference is selected you will be\n     asked to enter a new last read message number. Once a last read\n     message number is selected, you will be asked for confirmation\n     before the reset request is generated.  See @{"Advanced QWK features" Link "Advanced QWK features"},\nfor more details on Adding, Dropping, and Reseting conferences.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Text Viewer" "AmiQWK.guide/Text Viewer"\n@Next "ANSI Viewer"\n@Prev "Select item to read window"\n@Toc "Using AmiQWK"\n\nText Viewer\n===========\n\n   `AmiQWK'' has a built-in text viewer for reading text files included\nin the QWKMail packet, such as the Hello, Goodbye, News, Bulletins, and\nrecent uploads files. ANSI display sequences are filtered out before\nthe text is displayed. (Note that if the text uses ANSI cursor\npositioning codes, the text may be jumbled. However most ANSI text uses\nonly color codes.)\n\n   The following keys control movement in the text and message viewers:\n\nKeypad 8, Up Arrow\n     Scroll up one line of text.\n\nKeypad 2, Down Arrow\n     Scroll down one line of text.\n\nKeypad 9\n     Scroll up one page of text.\n\nKeypad 3 Space Bar\n     Scroll down one page of text.\n\nKeypad 7\n     Move to start of text.\n\nKeypad 1\n     Move to end of text.\n\n   In addition to the above keys, you can move through the current text\nby using the scroll bar at the bottom of the screen. (unless the scroll\nbar is disabled in the Operations configuration window. (See\n@{"Operation window" Link "Operation window"}.)\n\n   The following keys (and their corresponding menu items in the\n''Commands'' menu) also perform functions:\n\nQ\n     Quit reading text and return to the ''Select item to read'' window.\n     See @{"Select item to read window" Link "Select item to read window"}.\n\nP\n     Print the current text. See @{"Printing Text and Messages" Link "Printing Text and Messages"}.\n\nS\n     Save the current text. See @{"Saving Text and Messages" Link "Saving Text and Messages"}.\n\nA\n     ANSI display of the current message. See @{"ANSI Viewer" Link "ANSI Viewer"}.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "ANSI Viewer" "AmiQWK.guide/ANSI Viewer"\n@Prev "Text Viewer"\n@Toc "Using AmiQWK"\n\nANSI Viewer\n===========\n\n   The ANSI viewer will display the current message or text on a virtual\nterminal, as if it were being viewed on a terminal screen while\nconnected to a BBS. ANSI display sequences allow for changing the color\nof the text and background, cursor position, etc.\n\n   The ANSI viewer will correctly display most IBM-PC ANSI sequences.\nANSI is displayed on it''s own custom 16 color screen, the palette is\nhard-coded to match the default IBM-PC display.\n\n   The ANSI viewer uses the same font as is used for normal message\ntext.\n\n   When in the ANSI viewer the following functions are available:\n\nP\n     Pause the display. Display will be suspended until another key is\n     pressed.\n\nQ\n     Quit ANSI display and return to message or text reader.\n\nA\n     Display ANSI text again.\n\n0-9\n     Change display speed. 0 is fastest (no delay), 9 is slowest (max.\n     delay).\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Reading and Writing Messages" "AmiQWK.guide/Reading and Writing Messages"\n@Next "Configuration"\n@Prev "Using AmiQWK"\n@Toc "Main"\n\nReading and Writing Messages\n****************************\n\n\n @{" Reading Messages " Link "Reading Messages"} \n @{" Entering and re-editing new messages " Link "Entering and re-editing new messages"} \n @{" Writing messages and BBS Etiquette " Link "Writing messages and BBS Etiquette"} \n @{" Conference Window " Link "Conference Window"} \n @{" Message Index window " Link "Message Index window"} \n @{" Saving Text and Messages " Link "Saving Text and Messages"} \n @{" Printing Text and Messages " Link "Printing Text and Messages"} \n @{" New Tagline window " Link "New Tagline window"} \n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Reading Messages" "AmiQWK.guide/Reading Messages"\n@Next "Entering and re-editing new messages"\n@Toc "Reading and Writing Messages"\n\nReading Messages\n================\n\n   When ''Read Mail...'' is selected from the ''Select item to read''\nwindow, (See @{"Select item to read window" Link "Select item to read window"}.) the ''Select item to read''\nwindow is closed and you will enter the message reader.\n\n   When you first enter the message reader, the ''Select Conference''\nwindow (See @{"Conference Window" Link "Conference Window"}.) will appear for you to select the\nconference you want to start reading from. It will default to the first\nconference with messages other than the ''Replies'' conference. When you\nhave selected a conference, `AmiQWK'' will start displaying messages.\n\n   The message reader is divided into two sections. The top section\ncontains header information and several gadgets, and the bottom section\ncontains the message text.\n\n   The following header information is present in the header at the top\nof the screen:\n\nFrom:\n     Sender of the message.\n\nTo:\n     Person the message is addressed to.\n\nSubj:\n     Subject of the message.\n\nDate:\n     Date the message was entered.\n\nTime:\n     Time the message was entered.\n\nConference:\n     Name and number of the conference the message is in.\n\nMessage:\n     Message number, Number of this message out of the total available\n     in this conference, and the total number of messages in this\n     conference.  this packet.\n\nReply To:\n     Number of the message that this message is a reply to. (or blank\n     if it isn''t a reply to another message.)\n\nPRIVATE\n     If displayed, this message is tagged as being Private, usually\n     readable only by the sender, receiver, and system operator.\n\nREAD\n     If displayed, this message has already been read.\n\nPERSONAL\n     If displayed, this message is addressed to you personally.\n\n   In addition, there are six gadgets in the upper right of the screen.\n`Index''\n     Opens the Message Index window, to select a message to read. See\n     @{"Message Index window" Link "Message Index window"}.\n\n`Conf.''\n     Opens the Conference window, to select which conference to read.\n     See @{"Conference Window" Link "Conference Window"}.\n\n`Reply''\n     Reply to the current message. See\n     @{"Entering and re-editing new messages" Link "Entering and re-editing new messages"}.\n\n`Help''\n     Call up the `AmigaGuide'' help for the message viewer.\n\n`<<''\n     Read the previous message.\n\n`>>''\n     Read the next message.\n\n   At the bottom of the screen is the message text. There is a scroll\nbar at the bottom (unless the scroll bar is disabled in the Operations\nconfiguration window.) which can be used to move through the message\nusing the mouse. The following keys can also be used to move through\nthe message.\n\nKeypad 8, Up Arrow\n     Scroll up one line of message.\n\nKeypad 2, Down Arrow\n     Scroll down one line of message.\n\nKeypad 9\n     Scroll up one page of message.\n\nKeypad 3, Space Bar\n     Scroll down one page of message.\n\nKeypad 7\n     Move to start of message.\n\nKeypad 1\n     Move to end of message.\n\nKeypad 4, Left Arrow\n     Read the previous message in the current conference.\n\nKeypad 6, Right Arrow, RETURN\n     Read the next message in the current conference.\n\nSPACE BAR\n     Move forward 1 page. If the end of the message is passed the next\n     message is read.\n\n   The following keys also perform functions:\n\nA\n     ANSI display of the current message. See @{"ANSI Viewer" Link "ANSI Viewer"}.\n\nC\n     Open Conference window to select a new conference. See\n     @{"Conference Window" Link "Conference Window"}.\n\nE\n     Re-edit Reply. (only works in ''Replies'' conference.) See\n     @{"Entering and re-editing new messages" Link "Entering and re-editing new messages"}.\n\nI\n     Open Message Index window to select which message to read in the\n     current conference. See @{"Message Index window" Link "Message Index window"}.\n\nK\n     Kill (delete) the current message. (Only works in ''Replies''\n     conference.)\n\nN\n     Enter a new message. See @{"Entering and re-editing new messages" Link "Entering and re-editing new messages"}.\n\nP\n     Print the current message. See @{"Printing Text and Messages" Link "Printing Text and Messages"}.\n\nQ, ESC\n     Exit message reader and return to the ''Select item to read''\n     window. See @{"Select item to read window" Link "Select item to read window"}.\n\nR\n     Reply to the current message. See\n     @{"Entering and re-editing new messages" Link "Entering and re-editing new messages"}.\n\nS\n     Save the current message to disk. See @{"Saving Text and Messages" Link "Saving Text and Messages"}.\n\nT\n     Add a new tagline to the tagline file. See @{"New Tagline window" Link "New Tagline window"}.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Entering and re-editing new messages" "AmiQWK.guide/Entering and re-editing new messages"\n@Next "Writing messages and BBS Etiquette"\n@Prev "Reading Messages"\n@Toc "Reading and Writing Messages"\n\nEntering and re-editing new messages\n====================================\n\n   When you select ''Reply'' or ''New message'' when reading messages, the\n''New Message'' window is opened for information about the message. (such\nas who it is to, subject, etc.) and your editor is opened for you to\nenter your your message. (Note that you can alter the order the order\nin which the new message window is opened. You can configure `AmiQWK''\nto edit the message first then open the new message window, Open the\nnew message window then edit the message, or open the new message\nwindow both before and after the message is edited (the default). See\n@{"Replies window" Link "Replies window"}, for more information.)\n\n   If you are replying to an existing message, the original message\nwill be quoted in the new message text, with the quote prefix you\nselected in the Replies configuration window prefixed to each line. See\n@{"Replies window" Link "Replies window"}.  When re-editing messages the text will be sent to the\neditor as-is.\n\n`To''\n     This is the person the message is addressed to. If you are\n     replying to an existing message, this will default to the sender\n     of the message you are replying to. If it is a new message, this\n     field will be blank. This field is limited to 25 characters.\n\n`From''\n     This is normally your name. You can change this field, however\n     most QWKMail systems will not allow messages to be posted unless\n     this field matches your name. This field is limited to 25\n     characters due to constraints of the QWKMail format.\n\n`Subject''\n     This is the subject of the message. If you are replying to an\n     existing message this field will default to the subject of the\n     original message.  (with an optional ''RE:'' prefix, provided that\n     ''RE: prefix for reply subject'' is turned on in the ''Replies''\n     configuration window and the subject doesn''t already have a ''RE:''\n     prefix.) Otherwise this field is left blank so you can enter\n     whatever you want here. This field is limited to 25 characters due\n     to constraints of the QWKMail format.\n\n`Conference''\n     This is the conference you want the message to be posted to. It\n     defaults to the conference you are currently reading messages in.\n     You can enter the conference number in the integer string gadget,\n     or you can click on the ''Conference'' button and the Conference\n     window will appear for you to select a conference. (See\n     @{"Conference Window" Link "Conference Window"}.) The name of the conference will appear to the\n     right of the conference number gadget. `AmiQWK'' will check the\n     selected conference number against a list of conferences to make\n     sure you have selected a valid conference.\n\n`Public Status''\n     This is a cycle gadget that can be either set to ''Public'' or\n     ''Private''. A ''public'' message will be visible to everyone, while a\n     ''Private'' message is usually only visible to the sender, the\n     person who it is addressed to, and the system operator. Note that\n     not all conferences support private messages.\n\n`Return Receipt''\n     Tells the BBS to generate a return receipt message when this\n     message is received. This function is available only if it is\n     supported by the QWK mailer. Note that asking for a ''Return\n     Receipt'' will prefix the Subject field with ''RRR''.\n\n`Tagline''\n     This is a short one-line message that is appended to the end of\n     your message. You can select a tagline from the list gadget, or\n     type one into the string gadget below it. (If you enter a new\n     tagline, it will be appended to your tagline file for future use.)\n     Taglines are disabled when re-editing messages.\n\n`Select Another Tagline''\n     If you don''t like the tagline that `AmiQWK'' has selected for you,\n     click on this gadget and a new one will be selected.\n\n`OK''\n     Accept the current settings.\n\n`Cancel''\n     Cancel the new message.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Writing messages and BBS Etiquette" "AmiQWK.guide/Writing messages and BBS Etiquette"\n@Next "Conference Window"\n@Prev "Entering and re-editing new messages"\n@Toc "Reading and Writing Messages"\n\nWriting messages and BBS Etiquette\n==================================\n\n   When writing a message, Keep in mind that others will have to read\nit.  There are certain things that you can do to\n\n   * Avoid typing in all caps. Messages that are in all caps can be\n     difficult to read on some monitors.\n\n   * When entering a reply, quote only the relevant information.\n\n   * Try to keep your paragraphs short, and insert a blank line between\n     paragraphs.\n\n   * Try to keep on the subject and don''t post messages to areas where\n     they don''t belong.\n\n   Also remember that many BBSes are connected to BBS networks such as\nFidonet and Usenet. Additional rules may apply to network message\nareas, such as high and low ASCII characters (ASCII 0-31 and 128-255)\nand ANSI escape sequences may not be permitted, etc. If you are in\ndoubt as to what is and isn''t permitted in a certain conference, ask\nthe system operator or the network conference moderator for guidelines.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Conference Window" "AmiQWK.guide/Conference Window"\n@Next "Message Index window"\n@Prev "Writing messages and BBS Etiquette"\n@Toc "Reading and Writing Messages"\n\nConference Window\n=================\n\n   The Conference window is used to select a conference. It consists of\na list gadget listing all available conferences, and an OK and a cancel\ngadget.\n\n`Conference List''\n     Lists all available conferences by name and number, with the total\n     number of messages in each conference. You can select a conference\n     by double-clicking on the desired line of the conference or by\n     selecting a conference and clicking on the ''OK'' gadget.\n\n`OK''\n     Accept the currently selected conference and close the Conference\n     window.\n\n`Cancel''\n     Closes the Conference window and discards any conference selection.\n\n   You can also control the Conference window with the keyboard.\n\nC, Q, ESC\n     Closes the Conference window and discards any conference selection.\n\nO, ENTER\n     Accept the currently selected conference and close the Conference\n     window.\n\nKeypad 8, Up Arrow\n     Scroll up through the conference list.\n\nKeypad 2, Down Arrow\n     Scroll down through the conference list.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Message Index window" "AmiQWK.guide/Message Index window"\n@Next "Saving Text and Messages"\n@Prev "Conference Window"\n@Toc "Reading and Writing Messages"\n\nMessage Index window\n====================\n\n   The Message Index window  is used to select a message from within a\nconference. It consists of a list gadget listing all available messages,\nand an OK and a cancel gadget. The operation of the Message Index\nwindow is nearly identical to the Conference window.\n\n`message List''\n     Lists all available messages, by the To, From, Subject fields. The\n     following flags are present as well:\n\n    `*''\n          The message is addressed to you personally.\n\n    `R''\n          This message has been read.\n\n    `P''\n          This message is marked as being Private.\n\n     You can select a message by double-clicking on the desired line of\n     the message list, or by picking the desired conference with either\n     the mouse or keyboard and then clicking on the ''OK'' gadget.\n\n`OK''\n     Accept the currently selected message and close the Message Index\n     window.\n\n`Cancel''\n     Closes the Message Index window and discards any message selection.\n\n   You can also control the message window with the keyboard.\n\nC, Q, ESC\n     Closes the Message Index window and discards any message selection.\n\nO, ENTER\n     Accept the currently selected message and close the Message Index\n     window.\n\nKeypad 8, Up Arrow\n     Scroll up through the message list.\n\nKeypad 2, Down Arrow\n     Scroll down through the message list.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Saving Text and Messages" "AmiQWK.guide/Saving Text and Messages"\n@Next "Printing Text and Messages"\n@Prev "Message Index window"\n@Toc "Reading and Writing Messages"\n\nSaving Text and Messages\n========================\n\n   When you select ''Save'', A file requester will open for you to select\nthe file name to save the text or message to. If the file you selected\nalready exists the new text or message will be appended to the end of\nthe existing file. If you are saving a message the contents of the\nheader will be saved as well.\n\n   The default path and/or directory for the saved text can be set in\nthe ''Paths'' window of the config editor. See @{"Paths window" Link "Paths window"}.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Printing Text and Messages" "AmiQWK.guide/Printing Text and Messages"\n@Next "New Tagline window"\n@Prev "Saving Text and Messages"\n@Toc "Reading and Writing Messages"\n\nPrinting Text and Messages\n==========================\n\n   When you select ''Print'', the current text or message will be sent to\nthe printer. If you are printing a message the contents of the header\nwill be printed as well.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "New Tagline window" "AmiQWK.guide/New Tagline window"\n@Prev "Printing Text and Messages"\n@Toc "Reading and Writing Messages"\n\nNew Tagline window\n==================\n\n   The New Tagline window is used to enter a new tagline into the\ntaglines list file. It consists of three gadgets:\n\n`Tagline''\n     A string gadget to enter the new tagline into.\n\n`OK''\n     Close the New Tagline window and save the new tagline to the\n     tagline list file.\n\n`Cancel''\n     Close the New Tagline window and discard the new tagline.\n\n   One idea for those of you who like to steal taglines. Use a text\nsnapping program such as PowerSnap to cut taglines out of messages\nusing the mouse and then paste them into the New Tagline window.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Configuration" "AmiQWK.guide/Configuration"\n@Next "Advanced QWK features"\n@Prev "Reading and Writing Messages"\n@Toc "Main"\n\nConfiguration\n*************\n\n\n @{" Main Configuration Window " Link "Main Configuration Window"} \n @{" Operation window " Link "Operation window"} \n @{" CygnusEd Notes " Link "CygnusEd Notes"} \n @{" Replies window " Link "Replies window"} \n @{" Paths window " Link "Paths window"} \n @{" Archivers window " Link "Archivers window"} \n @{" Graphics window " Link "Graphics window"} \n @{" Register window " Link "Register window"} \n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Main Configuration Window" "AmiQWK.guide/Main Configuration Window"\n@Next "Operation window"\n@Toc "Configuration"\n\nMain Configuration Window\n=========================\n\n   The configuration editor consists of a main configuration window and\nseveral sub-windows. The main Configuration window has the following\ngadgets:\n\n`Operation''\n     Opens the Operation configuration window. The Operation window is\n     used to configure the general operation of `AmiQWK''. See\n     @{"Operation window" Link "Operation window"}.\n\n`Replies''\n     Opens the Replies configuration window. The Relies window is used\n     to configure how replies and new messages are processed. See\n     @{"Replies window" Link "Replies window"}.\n\n`Paths''\n     Opens the Paths configuration window. The Paths window is used to\n     tell `AmiQWK'' where it should look for and store files. See\n     @{"Paths window" Link "Paths window"}.\n\n`Archivers''\n     Opens the Archivers configuration window. The Archivers window is\n     used to specify which compression programs are used and their\n     command line options.  See @{"Archivers window" Link "Archivers window"}.\n\n`Graphics''\n     Opens the Graphics configuration window. The Graphics window is\n     used to specify which screen mode the `AmiQWK'' screen should open\n     in, the font that should be used for text displays, the screen\n     palette, etc. See @{"Graphics window" Link "Graphics window"}.\n\n`Register''\n     Opens the Registration configuration window. The Register window\n     is used to enter your registration key when you register `AmiQWK''.\n     See @{"Register window" Link "Register window"}.\n\n`Save''\n     Accepts the current configuration and saves it to disk and return\n     to the ''Select Packet'' window. See @{"Select Packet window" Link "Select Packet window"}.\n\n`Use''\n     Accepts the current configuration and returns you to the ''Select\n     Packet'' window See @{"Select Packet window" Link "Select Packet window"}. but does not save the new\n     configuration to disk. If the new configuration is not saved to\n     disk before exiting the program the new configuration will be lost.\n\n`Cancel''\n     Discard all changes to the configuration and return to the ''Select\n     Packet'' window. See @{"Select Packet window" Link "Select Packet window"}.\n\n   The configuration is saved in a file named ''Config.AQ'' in the same\ndirectory that `AmiQWK'' is located in.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Operation window" "AmiQWK.guide/Operation window"\n@Next "CygnusEd Notes"\n@Prev "Main Configuration Window"\n@Toc "Configuration"\n\nOperation window\n================\n\n   The Operation window is used to configure the general operation of\n`AmiQWK''.\n\n`Scroll bar in text window''\n     If this checkbox gadget is selected, a scroll bar will appear at\n     the bottom of the text and message windows. This scroll bar can be\n     used to move around the displayed text using the mouse.\n\n`Tab Size''\n     This slider gadget specifies the number of spaces between tab\n     stops.\n\n`Ask before Exit''\n     If this checkbox is selected, `AmiQWK'' will ask for confirmation\n     before exiting. Otherwise it will exit without asking first.\n\n`After Read''\n     This cycle gadget is used to tell `AmiQWK'' what to do with a\n     packet after you read it. It can be set to:\n\n    `No Action''\n          Nothing is done to the packet after you read it.\n\n    `Rename Packet''\n          You will be presented with a file requester to change the\n          name of the packet after you read it.\n\n    `Delete Packet.''\n          You will be asked if you want to delete the packet after you\n          read it.\n\n    `Ask''\n          You will be presented with a requester asking if you want to\n          Rename, Delete, or take no action at all on the packet after\n          you have read it.\n\n`Packet Search Pattern Match''\n     This is the pattern that `AmiQWK'' should use when looking for mail\n     packets.  It should normally be something like ''#?.Q#?'' as packet\n     names normally end with ''.QWK'' and some term programs may change\n     the extension if a duplicate file is downloaded.\n\n`Editor''\n     This is the command line used to start your editor for editing\n     messages. Be sure to specify any command line switches you need\n     here as well. The file name will be appended to the end of this\n     string.\n\n     Keep in mind that your text editor must NOT detach itself from the\n     process that started it.\n\n     Here are some example editor strings for various editors.\n\n    `CygnusEd''\n          `c:ed -sticky'' (See @{"CygnusEd Notes" Link "CygnusEd Notes"}.)\n\n    `TurboText''\n          `c:ttx WAIT''\n\n    `Ed''\n          `c:ed''\n\n    `MEmacs''\n          `sys:tools/memacs''\n\n    `GoldEd''\n          `c:ed sticky''\n\n     If you are using `CygnusEd'', See @{"CygnusEd Notes" Link "CygnusEd Notes"}.\n\n`Workbench to front on edit''\n     If this checkbox is selected, `AmiQWK'' will pull the workbench\n     screen to front when the editor is started. This is useful if you\n     are using an editor that opens on the workbench screen but does\n     not pull it to the front for you, such as the ''ed'' program that\n     comes with Workbench.\n\n`Spawn Window''\n     This string gadget is used to set the console specifications for\n     the spawn window for extracting packets and packing replies. See\n     your AmigaDos manual for more information on console\n     specifications. If you want the spawn window to open on the\n     `AmiQWK'' screen, make sure that ''SCREENAMIQWK'' appears somewhere\n     on this line.\n\n`Requesters''\n     Allows you to choose between ASL and `ReqTools'' file, font, and\n     screenmode requesters. (note that `AmiQWK'' will use the `ReqTools''\n     screenmode requester if you are using version 37 of ASL.library,\n     because ASL.library v37 does not have a screenmode selector.)\n\n`Use''\n     Use the current settings and return to the main configuration\n     window. See @{"Main Configuration Window" Link "Main Configuration Window"}.\n\n`Cancel''\n     Discard changes and return to the main configuration window. See\n     @{"Main Configuration Window" Link "Main Configuration Window"}.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "CygnusEd Notes" "AmiQWK.guide/CygnusEd Notes"\n@Next "Replies window"\n@Prev "Operation window"\n@Toc "Configuration"\n\nCygnusEd Notes\n==============\n\n   If you are using `CygnusEd'' version 2.12 or earlier, you may have\ntrouble getting `CygnusEd'' to open without detaching itself from it''s\nparent process due to a bug in the `ED'' activator program. If you are\nusing `CygnusEd'' 2.12, there are three options open to you.\n\n   * You can upgrade to a newer version of `CygnusEd''.\n\n   * You can get a third party replacement for the ''`ED'''' activator\n     program.  There are at least two in the public domain. At least\n     one of them will be available from the `AmiQWK'' support BBS at all\n     times. See @{"Technical Support" Link "Technical Support"}.\n\n   * You can use the included `CygnusEd'' starter script. (filename\n     ''StartCed'', set the ''Editor'' gadget in the ''Operation'' window of\n     the config editor to ''`StartCed'''' if you use this script. You may\n     also need to specify the full path to the `StartCed'' script.)\n\n   For best results, you will probably want to ''hot-start'' `CygnusEd''\nfrom the `s:user-startup'' file. See your `CygnusEd'' program for details\non ''hot-starting''.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Replies window" "AmiQWK.guide/Replies window"\n@Next "Paths window"\n@Prev "CygnusEd Notes"\n@Toc "Configuration"\n\nReplies window\n==============\n\n`Edit Header''\n     This cycle gadget has three settings. It controls when the message\n     editor and the ''New Message'' window are opened.\n\n    `Before Edit''\n          Edit message header in the ''New Message'' window before\n          editing the message text.\n\n    `After Edit''\n          Edit message header in the ''New Message'' window after editing\n          the message text.\n\n    `Before and After Edit''\n          Edit message header in the ''New Message'' window both before\n          and after editing the message text.\n\n`Quote Prefix''\n     This string is prefixed before each line of quoted text when\n     replying to a message.\n\n`Header Info in replies''\n     If this checkbox is selected, the information in the message\n     header will be included in the message text of a reply. Has no\n     effect on new messages.  (i.e. not a reply to an existing message.)\n\n`RE: prefix for reply subject''\n     If this checkbox is selected, the subject field of the new message\n     will be prefixed with ''RE:'' unless it already has a ''RE:'' prefix.\n\n`Trunc/Wrap reply text''\n     Specifies if quoted text in a reply is to be truncated or word\n     wrapped.\n\n`Col.''\n     Specifies column that quoted text in a reply is to be truncated or\n     word wrapped at.\n\n`Use''\n     Use the current settings and return to the main configuration\n     window. See @{"Main Configuration Window" Link "Main Configuration Window"}.\n\n`Cancel''\n     Discard changes and return to the main configuration window. See\n     @{"Main Configuration Window" Link "Main Configuration Window"}.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Paths window" "AmiQWK.guide/Paths window"\n@Next "Archivers window"\n@Prev "Replies window"\n@Toc "Configuration"\n\nPaths window\n============\n\n   The paths window is used to tell `AmiQWK'' where it should look for\nand store files. To the right of each path string gadget is a\n''pickfile'' button, which will open a file requester to select the\ndesired path. You can either type the path into the string gadget or\nselect the path from the file requester.\n\n`Packet Directory''\n     Tells `AmiQWK'' where it should look for mail packets. This should\n     be set to the downloads directory your terminal program uses.\n\n`Reply Directory''\n     Tells `AmiQWK'' where it should store reply packets. This should be\n     set to the uploads directory your terminal program uses.\n\n`Work Directory''\n     Tells `AmiQWK'' where it should create it''s work directory. If you\n     have enough memory, this should be set to `RAM:'' for best\n     performance. If this field is left blank, `AmiQWK'' will create\n     it''s work directory in the directory in the same directory as the\n     `AmiQWK'' executable file.\n\n`Saved Text''\n     Default path and/or filename for saved text. You can enter a\n     complete path with filename, just a filename (the files will be\n     saved to the `AmiQWK'' directory unless you specify a path when you\n     save messages or text files) or just a path (you will need to make\n     sure that the path name ends with a '':'' or a ''/'', otherwise\n     `AmiQWK'' will think that the last part of the path is actually a\n     file name.)\n\n`Use''\n     Use the current settings and return to the main configuration\n     window. See @{"Main Configuration Window" Link "Main Configuration Window"}.\n\n`Cancel''\n     Discard changes and return to the main configuration window. See\n     @{"Main Configuration Window" Link "Main Configuration Window"}.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Archivers window" "AmiQWK.guide/Archivers window"\n@Next "Graphics window"\n@Prev "Paths window"\n@Toc "Configuration"\n\nArchivers window\n================\n\n   The Archivers window is used to specify the command line strings for\nthe file compression/extraction programs. Currently `AmiQWK'' supports\n`LHA/LHArc'', `ZIP'', `ZOO'', and `ARC'' compression. The filename and\ndestination directory will be appended to the command line strings.\n\n`Use''\n     Use the current settings and return to the main configuration\n     window. See @{"Main Configuration Window" Link "Main Configuration Window"}.\n\n`Cancel''\n     Discard changes and return to the main configuration window. See\n     @{"Main Configuration Window" Link "Main Configuration Window"}.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Graphics window" "AmiQWK.guide/Graphics window"\n@Next "Register window"\n@Prev "Archivers window"\n@Toc "Configuration"\n\nGraphics window\n===============\n\n   The Graphics window is used to specify the general appearance of\n`AmiQWK''.\n\n`Screen Mode''\n     The name of the screen mode that `AmiQWK'' opens on. (Read only,\n     use the ''Select Screen Mode'' gadget to select a screen mode.)\n\n`Width''\n     The width of the `AmiQWK'' screen in pixels. (Read only)\n\n`Height''\n     The height of the `AmiQWK'' screen in pixels. (Read only)\n\n`Select Screen Mode''\n     Select a screen mode for `AmiQWK'' using the ASL or `ReqTools''\n     screenmode requester. (If you are using version 37 of ASL.library,\n     the `ReqTools'' screenmode requester will be used.) You can also\n     specify the number of colors the `AmiQWK'' screen uses. (I\n     recommend using 4 colors. At this time `AmiQWK'' does not use more\n     than four colors except for the ANSI display screen, which is hard\n     coded to use a 16 color screen.)\n\n`Shanghai''\n     If this checkmark is selected, the `AmiQWK'' screen will be opened\n     in ''Shanghai'' mode. If this option is set, older applications that\n     would normaly open on the Workbench screen instead open on the\n     default public screen, which may or may not be the Workbench\n     screen.\n\n`PopPubScreen''\n     If this checkmark is selected, the `AmiQWK'' screen will be opened\n     in ''PopPubScreen'' mode. This will cause the AmiQWK screen to ''pop''\n     to the front whenever a window is opened on the AmiQWK screen.\n\n`Edit Palette''\n     Change the color palette `AmiQWK'' uses using the `ReqTools''\n     palette requester.\n\n`Select Font''\n     Select the font `AmiQWK'' uses for message text and the ANSI\n     display, using the ASL or `ReqTools'' font requester. The selected\n     font and size will appear to the right of the ''Select Font''\n     gadget. I recommend using an IBM-PC style font as many packets\n     will contain characters that only appear properly when viewed with\n     an IBM-PC style font.\n\n`Use''\n     Use the current settings and return to the main configuration\n     window. See @{"Main Configuration Window" Link "Main Configuration Window"}.\n\n`Cancel''\n     Discard changes and return to the main configuration window. See\n     @{"Main Configuration Window" Link "Main Configuration Window"}.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Register window" "AmiQWK.guide/Register window"\n@Prev "Graphics window"\n@Toc "Configuration"\n\nRegister window\n===============\n\n   The Register window is used generate a registration keyfile. When you\nregister you will be given a 16 digit registration number which should\nbe entered into this window.\n\n`Your Name''\n     Enter your name into this gadget. It must be entered exactly as it\n     was specified on your registration form as the registration key is\n     matched against this field.\n\n`Registration Key''\n     Enter your 16 digit registration number in this gadget.\n\n`Status''\n     Registration status. Will either be a registration serial number\n     or ''** UNREGISTERED EVALUATION COPY **'' if a valid registration\n     key is not present.\n\n`Use''\n     Save your registration key to disk and return to the main\n     configuration window. See @{"Main Configuration Window" Link "Main Configuration Window"}.\n\n`Cancel''\n     Discard changes and return to the main configuration window. See\n     @{"Main Configuration Window" Link "Main Configuration Window"}.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Advanced QWK features" "AmiQWK.guide/Advanced QWK features"\n@Next "The Future of AmiQWK"\n@Prev "Configuration"\n@Toc "Main"\n\nAdvanced QWK features\n*********************\n\n   Some BBSes allow for adding, dropping, and resetting of conferences,\ndownloading files attached to messages, and other functions by sending\nmessages to the BBS via a QWKmail packet. If the BBS supports these\nfeatures a file named DOOR.ID will be included in the QWKMail packet\nthat will tell `AmiQWK'' what functions are available and how to process\na request.\n\n   For example, if you had a packet from a Wildcat! BBS and had `AmiQWK''\ngenerate a request to add conference #25, `AmiQWK'' would generate a\nmessage with the following header information:\n\n   FROM: <your name>\nTO: TOMCAT\nSUBJ: ADD\nCONFERENCE 25\nIf you decide to abort the request, just enter the ''Replies'' conference\nand ''Kill'' the request message. (See @{"Reading Messages" Link "Reading Messages"}.)\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "The Future of AmiQWK" "AmiQWK.guide/The Future of AmiQWK"\n@Next "Technical Support"\n@Prev "Advanced QWK features"\n@Toc "Main"\n\nThe Future of AmiQWK\n********************\n\n   `AmiQWK III''will be a complete rewrite of the existing code. Some of\nthe features I plan on adding are:\n\n   * A whole new multi-window, multi-packet environment.\n        - Any number of packets can be opened at a time, limited only by\n          available memory.\n\n   * Database of services\n        - New messages can be created even if no packet is present.\n\n        - Replies can be sent to a different service than the packet is\n          from.\n\n   * Sorting\n        - Conferences by Name or Number.\n\n        - Messages by To, From, Subject, Message Number, etc.\n\n   * String search for message by to:, from:, subject:, message text.\n\n   * Improvement of quote system.\n        - Quote prefix may contain initials, first name of the person\n          who''se text is quoted, etc.\n\n   * Tagline manager\n        - Edit, Delete, Sort, Find tagline functions.\n\n        - multiple tagline files can be maintained. (such as a file\n          containing only Star Trek quotes, etc.)\n\n        - A true ''Steal Tagline'' function.\n\n   * Database of BBS and packet information\n        - Keep a record of which packets have been read, etc.\n\n        - Keep record of conferences and other information about the\n          packets a BBS generates, so that a reply packet can be\n          generated even if no packet exists for the BBS.\n\n        - Keep a address book of people you regularly send messages to,\n          including network addresses, phone and fax numbers, etc.\n\n        - Keep a ''Twit'' list. Ignore messages with certain topics or\n          from/to persons listed.\n\n   * ''Blue Wave'' and ''QWK-II'' packet support.\n\n   * Possible UUCP, TCP/IP, Fidonet, and FAX interfaces.\n\n   * UUEncode/UUDecode support.\n\n   * PGP (Pretty Good Privacy) support.\n\n   * ''Text Variables'' for inserting information into text, such as who\n     the message is to/from, etc.\n\n   * ARexx Interface\n\n   If there is a feature you would like to see in a future version, let\nme know about it, even if I listed it already. If I get a lot of\nrequests I may move it to a higher position on the list.\n\n   Remember, The future of `AmiQWK'' depends on YOU! Send in your\nregistration as soon as possible.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Technical Support" "AmiQWK.guide/Technical Support"\n@Next "Acknowledgments"\n@Prev "The Future of AmiQWK"\n@Toc "Main"\n\nTechnical Support\n*****************\n\n   Technical support for `AmiQWK'' is available through the following:\n\nElectronic Mail\n    INTERNET\n          [email removed]\nPostal Mail\n     Jim Dawson\n     509 S. Madison St.\n     Marion, IL. 62959\n     USA\n\nBBS\n     The Hackers Guild II BBS\n     (618)997-2591 300-14,400 BPS USR HST/v.32/v.32bis.\n     Full Duplex, 8 data bits, 1 stop bit, no parity.\n     24 Hrs, 7 Days. (Ex. Fidonet Zone Mail Hour.) You can download\n     from the AmiQWK file area on your first call.\n\n   For fastest and most reliable way to get technical support is to\ncall The Hackers Guild II BBS directly.\n\n   When asking for help, please give as complete description of your\nproblem as possible, as well as a complete description of your system\nand any software that might also be running at the same time as\n`AmiQWK''. The more information I have the faster I can suggest a\nsolution to your problem.\n\n   I will personally post new versions of AmiQWK to The Hackers Guild\nII BBS, Aminet FTP sites, and new versions will be submitted to Fred\nFish for inclusion in his library of freely distributable software.\nUsers of Fidonet mailers can FREQ the latest version of AmiQWK by\nrequesting ''AMIQWK'' from 1:2290/42.0 (or 618-997-2591 if you don''t have\na Fidonet nodelist.)\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Acknowledgments" "AmiQWK.guide/Acknowledgments"\n@Next "Index"\n@Prev "Technical Support"\n@Toc "Main"\n\nAcknowledgments\n***************\n\n   Special thanks go to:\n\n`Jefferey Foy''\n     For information on the QWKMail format and MSBIN-IEEE conversion\n     routines.\n\n`Greg Hewgill''\n     For specifications of the DOOR.ID file.\n\n`Patrick Y. Lee''\n     For his excellent document on the QWKMail format.\n\n`Marcus Trisdale''\n     For his ANSI display code.\n\n`Jan van den Baard''\n     For his GadToolsBox GUI builder program.\n\n`Nico François''\n     For `reqtools.library''\n\n`Commodore Business Machines''\n     for `AmigaGuide.library'' and for making the Amiga computer.\n\n`Robert J Chassell and Richard M. Stallman''\n     for the Texinfo documentation format.\n\n`Reinhard Spisser and Sebastiano Vigna''\n     for `MakeGuide''.\n\n`Chris Hurley, Guy Bartoli, Dave Birdsong, Dennis Jann, Mike Soucy,''\n`Kipling Cooper, Steve Stewart, and Matt Weatherford''\n     for Beta Testing `AmiQWK''\n\n   And of course, everyone who has sent in registrations.\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Index" "AmiQWK.guide/Index"\n@Prev "Acknowledgments"\n@Toc "Main"\n\nIndex\n*****\n\n@Index "Index"\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',180539,4,0,NULL,NULL,'a_aqwk24','scan',1780048365);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ab_shell','AB-SHELL.LZH','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/AB-SHELL.LZH','DOS','XIM','DOS',NULL,NULL,'AB','V (_) /| \|: :|  \ \ Ya Face !_ V /.| \\| ||/\/. \ With... (_)!/ || //| ||\ ||__ BONEHEADs''...',replace('_) _   /\ .   ./\|\ Hammers\nV (_) /| \|: :|  \ \ Ya Face\n!_ V /.| \\| ||/\/. \ With...\n(_)!/ || //| ||\ ||__ BONEHEADs''...\n:V / _|| \\| || \||~~ DOS ShELL v1.6k\n.!/ __ | // × |\ \: / w/TOOL-ED\n / / | | /| ~ |/ / /  (ICON Editor)\n~~~  ~\|/ .\_/.\/|/ All ya need & it''s\n       :Døk      :  system SAFE!\n','\n',char(10)),'BoneSHELL.Guide',replace('@database ABUSE BONEHEADSHELL\n@Author BµSH DøKTøR\n@Index Documentation\n\nCopyright © 1994 BONEHeAD / ABUSE\n\n@Remark $VER: BONEHEADSHELL v 1.6k by Bonehead / /.BUSE\n@Remark AmigaGuide database\n\n@node MAIN "BONEHEADSHELL Documentation © 1994 Bonehead//.BUSE"\n           .\n          /|.           /\\n         / ||\  . .    /./    PRESENTS!  :\n        /  || \/| |\  / |\\n       / : ||  \| | \/ /| \      BONEHeAD''s DOS SHELL w/ TOOL-ED!\n      / /| ||:\ \ | / / |  \\n     / / | || / / | \ \ | \ \             Version 1.6K\n    / /  | || \ \ | |\ \| |\_\\n   / /___| ||:/ / | | \ | |_.           Coded by BONEHeAD\n  /  ____  ||  /| | | / | __|\n /    / |  || / ~~~ |/ /| | __         For /X 3.xx and UP!\n/____/  |  ||/:\___// / | |/ /\n:       |  |: . Døk/ /  | / /       DOX typed by the BµSH DøKTøR\n        :\ |       \/   |  /\n          \|            | /\n           :            |/ @{" Normal Documentation " Link Documentation}\n                        :\n@endnode\n@node Documentation "BONEHEAD SHELL Documentation"\n           .\n          /|.           /\\n         / ||\  . .    /./      @{" D e s c r i p t i o n " Link Description}\n        /  || \/| |\  / |\\n       / : ||  \| | \/ /| \     @{" I n s t a l l a t i o n " Link Installation}\n      / /| ||:\ \ | / / |  \\n     / / | || / / | \ \ | \ \   @{" T o o l t y p e s " Link Tooltypes} \n    / /  | || \ \ | |\ \| |\_\\n   / /___| ||:/ / | | \ | |_.   @{" G r e e t i n g s " Link Greetings}\n  /  ____  ||  /| | | / | __|\n /    / |  || / ~~~ |/ /| | __  @{" C o n t a c t s " Link Contacts}\n/____/  |  ||/:\___// / | |/ /\n:       |  |: . Døk/ /  | / /\n        :\ |       \/   |  /\n          \|            | /\n           :            |/\n                        :\n@endnode\n@node Description "BONEHEAD SHELL Description"\nBONEHEAD SHELL has been coded by BONEHEAD / /.BUSE!\n\n    Description - Are you sick of these bullshit Shell utilities\n                  for REMOTE sysop work on /X ? Want to edit a ICON?\n                  Paranoid & afraid of getting your''re bbs hacked?\n\n        Enter...  BONEHEAD SHELL.  Quick, easy, PW protected,\n                  Edit ICONS, more...\n\n This basically sets the SHELL up so only Sysops / Co-Sysops can access\nthe remote shell of the BBS. You can also, remotely edit bbs ICONS. Kool!\n\n How Does it Work ?\n \n Easy= JUST LIKE YOUR OLD SHELL ...It does Everything Possible.\n       The only diffrence is when you UPLOAD / DOWNLOAD you Must\n       type the Complete PATH and Filename.\n  \n        Example Upload = Upload BBS:commands/bbscmd/( The file/s you send\n                                                      will be placed in\n                                                      the BBSCMD dir. )\n\n        Example Download = Download BBS:DOORS/YAMAMA.TXT\n                                                (This will Download\n                                                  YAMAMA.txt)\n  \n  \n                 [ Simple Egh - Well Thats The IDEA ]\n\nTo EDIT a ICON remotely, just type  TOOL-ED {path for Icon} {no .info needed}\n\n        Example = TOOL-ED DH0:BBS/access/ACS.255.info\n\n   There are no Fuckin Backdoors and NO ONE but Levels 255 can access!\n PLUS! No one can format your hard drive... the command is coded out. It''s\n also password protected, (of course).\n -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\nContents of archive:\n===================\n\n\n            BONESHELL.Guide\n            BONESHELL.Guide.info\n            DOS\n            DOS.info\n            DOS.HLP\n\n\n===================\n\n      @{" Main Menu " Link Documentation}\n\n@endnode\n@node Installation "BONEHEAD SHELL Installation"\n\n     INSTALLATION =\n\n  Copy these into place...\n\n DOS.info to...\n\n  BBS/Commands/\n        BBSCmd/\n            DOS.info\n\n And the rest to...(you should make a DIR in DOORS called SHELL)\n\n      Doors/\n          SHELL/\n              DOS\n              DOS.HLP\n              BONESHELL.Guide\n              BONESHELL.GUIDE.info\n\n    Edit the DOS.info icon and put in your password... \n    Then just go over to the main prompt and type  '' DOS ''\n    Here are the commands...\n\n        EXIT = TO EXIT THE DOS SHELL.\n        UP   = TO  UPLOAD A FILE TO THE SYSTEM (INCLUDE PATH)\n        DOWN = TO DOWNLOAD A FILE FROM THE SYSTEM (INCLUDE PATH/FILE_NAME)\n        TOOL-ED = CHANGE / ADD TOOL TYPES ON SYSTEM ICONS \n        <dos commands> most all CLI command \n        HELP = GETS YOU THE COMMANDS\n \n    You are now in a Honest to good TRUE 100% Working Shell ..\n  With no fuckin This and Thats .......\n\n    Thanks to Bonehead we can have easier things to use like this .\n\n\n      @{" Main Menu " Link Documentation}\n\n@endnode\n@node Tooltypes "BONEHEAD SHELL Tooltypes"\nYou can insert the following tooltypes in the icons in\nBBS:Commands/BBSCmd/DOS\n\n===========\n\nLOCATION=Doors:SHELL/DOS           - Location of the Door\nSTACK=10000                        - Stack of the Door\nPRIORITY=2                         - Priority of the Door\nPASSWORD=22254                     - Password for the Door\nMULTINODE=YES\nACCESS=255\nTYPE=XIM\n\n===========\n\n      @{" Main Menu " Link Documentation}\n\n@endnode\n@node Greetings "BONEHEAD SHELL Greetings"\n\n   GREETs GoINg OuT To All oUR ElIte HoMMies In The Scene !\n\n       CARDINAL ..     SHaDOWREAPER      Frantic- Abuse leader in jail now!\n\n       ACOMA           Del & KickFace    Pack Rat / Devil''s Den\n\n       ENERGY          KrOnIOn           Prodigy\n\n       /\/orske        Gazzer            White Knight\n\n       The Legend / R/\D/\R ( We miss ya Rich )\n\n       MOTION - Especially Donald if he is still the leader\n\n          And all The Rest of You Modem Whore''s !\n           -----------------------------------\n\n             DOX typed up by the BµSH DøKTøR\n\n\n      From Bonehead\n  \n         SUCK MY BIG DISK - Oh and Hi To EveryOne !\n\n      @{" Main Menu " Link Documentation}\n\n@endnode\n@node Contacts "BONEHEAD SHELL Contacts"\nBONEHEAD SHELL has been coded by BONEHEAD / /.BUSE!\n      /\   ____  __          .\n     /  \  \  / / //\  /\   /^\   Call NOW!\n    / /\ \ / / / //  \/  \ /   \\n   / /  \// /_/ // /\ \/\ \  /\_\ Sysop: /\/\IX/\/\ASTER\n  / /    / __  // /__\ \ \ \/___\n / /    / / / // ______ \ \ \__ \     .   If ya don''t know the number, ASK!\n/ /    / / / // /  \ \/ / / /  \ \   /|.           /\\n\ \   / / / // /    \/ / / /.  / /  / ||\  . .    /./\n \ \ / /__\/ \ \    / /\/ / |\/ /  /  || \/| |\  / |\\n  \ \\// /    \/    \/\  /  |  /  / : ||  \| | \/ /| \\n   \ \/ /              \/Døk| /  / /| ||:\ \ | / / |  \\n    \  /    ______ ____     |/  / / | || / / | \ \ | \ \\n     \/     \  __ \\  _\    :  / /  | || \ \ | |\ \| |\_\\n             \ \ \ \\ \_      / /___| ||:/ / | | \ | |_.\n              \ \ \ \\  \    /  ____  ||  /| | | / | __|\n               \ \/  \\ \   /    / |  || / ~~~ |/ /| | __\n                \____/ \/  /____/  |  ||/:\___// / | |/ /\n                           :       |  |: .    / /  | / /\n                                   :\ |       \/   |  /\n                                     \|            | /\n                                      :            |/\n          @{" Main Menu " Link Documentation}      :\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),'{"LOCATION":"Doors:SHELL/DOS","STACK":"10000","PRIORITY":"2","ACCESS":"255","TYPE":"XIM"}','auto-added',18558,1,0,NULL,NULL,'ab_shell','scan',1780048365);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('abc_cbv4','ABC-CBV4.LZH','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ABC-CBV4.LZH',NULL,'XIM','CONFBULL.exe',NULL,':','ABC','(___  / . . ___ _____)__  __.  /  .___  ___/ |  _  \ | | \ _ ¬|  ¬\ _  \¬|  \  | ¬|  ___) |  l__/ l_l_/__  l_  / l__/ l__/___  l_____\',replace(' __________________/\_______________________\n(___  / . . ___ _____)__  __.  /  .___  ___/\n|  _  \ | | \ _ ¬|  ¬\ _  \¬|  \  | ¬|  ___)\n|  l__/ l_l_/__  l_  / l__/ l__/___  l_____\\n`--'' `--''tGø  `--''¬\/--'' `--''     `--''      \n ConfBull v4.2 By : Rad! For /X & S-EXPRESS\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ \n','\n',char(10)),'CONFBULL.doc',replace('       _________________________/\____________________________\n      (____   /  .  .  ____ ______)___   ___.   /  .____  ___/\n      |   _   \  |  |  \ __  ¬|  ¬\  _   \ ¬|   \  |  ¬|  ___)\n      |   l___/  l__l__/___   l_  /  l___/  l___/___   l_____\\n      `---''  `---''        `---''¬\/---''  `---''tGø   `---''\n.-------------------------------------------------------------------.\n!                                                                   |\n|             Multi-Conference Bulletin Displayer v4.2              |\n|                                                                   |\n|                            By : Rad!                              |\n|                                                                   |\n|                For /X v2.x & 3.x  © 1994 AMbiANCE                 |\n|                                                                   !\n`-------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\nREASON FOR THIS DOOR\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n	I''ve installed a few other bulletin doors in the past, and I\nhave noticed that one thing is missing from each of them. It might not\nalways be the same thing, but it definately pissed me off. That is why\nI''ve taken the time to write this little update of my old Confbull.\n(It was release under my old group fF iNC, which is now AMbiANCE)\nA few things I''ve updated in this version are :\n\n	1. Individual updating of bulletins\n	2. Improved speed of updating bulletins by 50%\n	3. Removed senseless config file for maximum speed\n	4. Included a quick online help and better output\n	5. New compressed version usable by all 680x0 users\n\nINSTALATION FOR /X 3.x USERS\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n	Note - The comments on the files tell you where to put them on\n               your hd.\n\n	1. Copy all main program files to a directory titled :\n	   > BBS:DOORS/RAD/\n	\n2. Copy the "B.info" to your bbscmd directory\n	3. Assign BULLETINS: to your directory where you will\n	   keep your bulletins.\n	   (All the bulletins should go into one directory)\n	4. Make an updating script for each of your bulletins\n	   (I have included an example of this in the mainfile dir)\n	5. Make sure you have a bulletins menu in the bulletin directory\n	   (I have included an example of this in the mainfile dir)\n	6. Load up /X and run it from the main menu!\n\nINSTALATION FOR /X 2.x USERS\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n	1. Follow rules for 3.x users\n	2. Instead of adding the "B.info" to the bbscmd, make sure\n	   you have added the proper info to the bbscommands text\n	   indicating this door is an AREXX module\n	3. Load up /X and run it from the main menu!\n\nINSTALATION FOR S-EXPRESS USERS\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n	1. Follow rules for /X 3.x and 2.x (I think S-EXPRESS is the same?)\n	   (I really don''t care for S-EXPRESS so I''m sorry for this!)\n\nINFORMATION ON UPDATING SEQUENCES\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n	You should create a file for each bulletin you wish to be updated\nwhen a user selects it. There should be two options on your bulletin.\nAn ANSI and ASCII output. Make the command string for ANSI in a file titled\n\n> BULL<x>.a\n\n	The <x> meaning the bulletin number, the "a" symbolizing the ANSI\nupdate of this bulletin. An example of the update would be :\n\nUTILS:TBAR >BBS:SCREENS/BULLETINS/BULL1.TXT.GR UPLD BBS:USER.DATA 015 5\n\nThis would update my ThrashBar Bulletin #1 for users using ansi mode.\nThe reason for two seperate update strings is to speed up the updating.\nSo instead of updating BOTH ANSI and ASCII, we update just the one\nwhich will be shown to the user.\n\n	Now you should make an option for the ASCII output of the bulletin.\nStart by calling the file :\n\n> BULL<x>.n\n\n	The <x> again being the bulletin to display, and the "n" symbolizing\nthe ASCII updating of this bulletin. An example would be :\n\nUTILS:TBAR >BBS:SCREENS/BULLETINS/BULL1.TXT UPLD BBS:USER.DATA 015 5 -A\n\nThis would update the ASCII output of ThrashBar.\n\n	There are some exceptions to this method. If your bulletin doesn''t\noffer a .GR option, default it to .TXT and make the update file titled :\n\n> BULL<x>.n\n\n	My util will default to the "n" if no "a" is found in the bulletins\ndirectory for that bulletin. If no update files are found for a bulletin,\nit will NOT update the bulletin. This works well if you display bulletins\nsuch as WEEKTOP by Byteandi, which requires updating after each logoff only!\n\nOk, that seems like all I need to cover here!\n\nGREETS FLY OUT TO THE FOLLOWING GROUPS\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nLsd, Digital, Insane, Nexus, Mystic, Dcs, Logic, 5d, Fairlight, Nut & Bolt,\nParadox, God, Origine, Crystal, Lego, Doodles & Shock, Delirium, Prodigy,\nEquinox, Quartex, Trsi, Lemon, Kefrens, Medellin, Skid Row, and all others\nwhich I have sadly missed!\n\nSPECIAL CONGRADULATIONS GO TO\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nfADEONE/lEGO : You have done the BEST artworks I have ever seen... If anybody\nknowing this mate reads this, PLEASE give him my regards for his GREAT job.\nI use his works to make my friends on the PC sad that they don''t own an AMIGA!\n\nSUPPORT FOR THIS PRODUCTION\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nDJ rAd! (HINT HINT) Mega Lo Mania\nD.M.S.              S.O.S.\nEOAD                Love''s The Feeling!\n\nThat''s all mates!\n\nAnybody interested in joining AMbiANCE, contact me (Rad!) on my bbs,\n(MEGA LO MANIA) at +1-812-944-6866, NUP = BUBBY)\n\n __________________/\_______________________\n(___  / . . ___ _____)__  __.  /  .___  ___/\n|  _  \ | | \ _ ¬|  ¬\ _  \¬|  \  | ¬|  ___)\n|  l__/ l_l_/__  l_  / l__/ l__/___  l_____\\n`--'' `--''tGø  `--''¬\/--'' `--''     `--''      \n ConfBull v4.2 By : Rad! For /X & S-EXPRESS\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ \n\n[EOF]\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',27185,4,0,NULL,NULL,'abc_cbv4','scan',1780048365);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ac__be1o','AC!-BE1O.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/AC!-BE1O.LHA',NULL,'XIM','_____|_____________ ____|____________|_ __',NULL,NULL,'AC!','|\___ |  _  / __/._/__ . |  _   / _   |    : |  _/ :  / /  |  l   / | :  / _/  _}--:s   | |__l__l_(  \__l_____/____l_(   \______|c   |',replace(' _____|_____________ ____|____________|_ __\n|\___ |  _  / __/._/__ . |  _   / _   |    :\n|  _/ :  / /  |  l   / | :  / _/  _}--:s   |\n|__l__l_(  \__l_____/____l_(   \______|c   |\n|--------\__/---------------\___/----------|\n|    ·BRILLIANCE· BBS-STYLE ·2fAST/aC!·    |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'reference-board.txt',replace(replace('              W h e r e   t h e   w a r e z   c o m e   f r o m\r\n                                               __                /\_____:\r\n__/\__________________________________________|  \______________/  \    |__\r\n\_   ___________  _______ ________  \__   ___ |   _______  _______  \_  l  \\r\n__\____  \    _l   \    |  \     |___/     |  !    \   _l   \   _| __/\____ \_\r\n\_____    \___\     \___|   \___ !   \__   |_____   \__\     \__\    \____   /\r\n -mNT\_____/---\_____/--l____/-\______/\   |----\____/--\_____/--\____/--\__/\r\n                                        \__|\r\n\r\n- -- --> F A i R L i G H T   S W E D i S H   H E A D Q U A R T E R S <-- -- -\r\n\r\n           reference-board is back 2017 after more than 20 years in coma!\r\n\r\n                        Running on AmiExpress TelNet\r\n\r\n                    Connect to: reference-board.zapto.org:1541\r\n\r\n                    or: www.brysk.se/reference-board/index.htm\r\n               \n              UPLOAD DATE: 01-04-18  TIME: 18:52:17  ON NODE: 1\n','\r',char(13)),'\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,12361,2,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048365);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ac__bs1o','AC!-BS1O.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/AC!-BS1O.LHA','installer','XIM','Installer',NULL,'mOGUe!/aRTcORE!','AC!','__\__  \_______ _   /________  \_______ ___/ _/   /__   / \__/__   /  /   /__   /__/__ _    / _/ _/   \  _/__/_ /   / _/ _/ \',replace('  _____      _ ______    _ ____     _ ______\n__\__  \_______ _   /________  \_______ ___/\n   _/   /__   / \__/__   /  /   /__   /__/__\n  _    / _/ _/   \  _/__/_ /   / _/ _/ \    \n__/___/ _   \_____\ \    /____/ _   \_____ _\n.----\__\    /---\______/----\__\    /Rpd!-.\n|        \  /                    \  /      |\n|         \/   aRTcORE! BR­NGS    \/       |\n|                                          |\n|    BOARD STYLE V1.o BY mOGUe!/aRTcORE!   |\n|                                          |\n','\n',char(10)),'002..TXT',replace('INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ac092','AC092.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/AC092.LHA','ac','XIM','ac','0.92',NULL,NULL,'für AmiExpress von KICKSTART',replace('ArchivChecker v0.92\n  für AmiExpress\n  von KICKSTART\n','\n',char(10)),'ac.doc',replace('\n\n                          ArchivChecker v0.92\n\n                            für AmiExpress\n\n                             von KICKSTART\n                       [32m _______________________[m\n                       [32m \   __/\_  _/ __/ __/ /\n                         \__ /  / // __/ __/ /__\n                          \_/   \/ \__/\__/\___/[m\n\n             Call STEEL WHQ `THE RED RAIN'' +49-30-691-72-51\n                or out EURO HQ `KLONDYKE'' +46-83-693-93\n\n[33mGERMAN DOC[m\n\nFor the english Doc look some pages down!\n\n[4mFiles im Archiv:[m\n\n         AC       Hauptprogramm\n         AC.Dok   Dieses File\n         AC.DEFS  Defines-File [Sollte ins S:-Dir kopiert werden!]\n\n[4mAllgemeines[m\n\nAC vergleicht das Extension des angegebenen Filenames mit den Extensions\naus dem Defs-File.  Findet er das Extension in dem Defs-File wieder wird\nder volle Filename (mit Path) an den Stellen in der Commandline (Siehe\nDefsfile) eingesetzt an denne ein `*'' (Stern) steht.  Danach wird die\nCommandline mit hilfe der LVOExecute() Funktion aus der Doslibrary\naufgerufen.\n\n\n\n[4mDas Defs-File[m\n\nDas Defs-File [AC.Defs] wird vom AC bei jedem Aufruf aus dem S:-Directory\nnachgeladen.  Der Aufbau des Files sieht folgendermaßen aus:\n\n<extension>\n<commandline>\n<extension>\n<commandline>\n .\n .\n . [etc]\n\n`<Extension>'' kann ein beliebig langer Text sein der mit dem Ende des\nFilenames den AC als Parameter übergeben bekommt verglichen wird.  Stimmt\nder mit dem Ende des Filenames überein wird die `<commandline>'' dadrunter\nausgeführt.  Hier kann man als Joker der Stern (`*'') benutzen.  An der\nStelle wird dann jedesmal der Filename (mit Path und Extension) eingesetzt.\nDie ganze Commandline mit nachher eingesetztem Filename sollte allerdings\nnicht länger als 256 Zeichen sein.\n\nReicht die eine Zeile als Commandline nicht aus kann in der Zeile einfach\neine Batchdatei aufgerufen werden der dann der Stern (später dann der\nFilename) als Parameter übergeben wird (siehe dazu das Commodore\nDos-Handbuch!).\n\n\n\n[4mEinbinden in AmiExress[m\n\nAls Filename wird bei der Parameterübergabe immer das letzte Stück (vom\nEnde bis zum letzten Space) genommen.  AmiExpress z.B.  übergibt den\nCheckern für dem Filename immer noch `-n t'' das hiermit einfach\nübersprungen wird.  Mann kann aber auch nur den Filename angeben.  Hier ein\npaar Beispiele:\n\nAC -n t files:game.dms\nAC files:-s-kick.wrp\nAC güllegülle dh1:master.lzh\n\n\n[33mENGLISH DOC[m\n\n\nFiles in the -s-ac Archiv:\n\n         AC       Mainprogram\n         AC.Doc   This helpfile\n         AC.DEFS  Defines-File [please copy this into the s:-directory]\n\n\n[4mOverview[m\n\nAC compares the extension of the filename that is given ac by the parameter\nstring with the extensions in the `.defs''-file.  Every extension in the\ndefs-file has a commandline, too.  And if AC find the parameter-extension\nagain in the defs-file the commandline would execute by the Dos library\nfunction LVOExecute().  Before all `*''-wildcards in the commandline will\nchange to the AC-parameterstring.\n\n\n[4mThe Defs-File[m\n\nAfter you start AC it will load the file `AC.Defs'' from the S:-Dir. You can\ninsert your own extensions at the end of the defsfile like this example:\n\n<extension>\n<commandline>\n<extension>\n<commandline>\n .\n .\n . [and so on]\n\n<extension> is your extension that would compared with the extension of the\nparameterstring. The <commandline> is a programname und a parameterstring\nincluding the star-wildcard.\n\nExample for a little defsfile:\n\n.lzh\nlharc a * s:mybox.txt\n\nIf you now start AC with the parameterstring `bbs:uploads/jrcomm.lzh''\nAC will execute `lharc a bbs:uploads/jrcomm.lzh s:mybox.txt''. So you can\nadd a text from AmiExpress to Lzh-Archives.\n\nIs one commandline not enougth you kann start in the one line a batchfile\nwith the star [the filename] is given as parameter. (see into the Commodore\nAmigaDos book. You can use the `.key''-command in batchfiles.)\n\n[4mInsert AC into AmiExpress[m\n\nAC use from the parameterstring only the last part as filename. Because\nAmiExpress execute the filechecker with `<progname> -n t <filename>''. You\ncan give AC before the filename much other shit. AC will only take the last\npart as filename!\n\nNext some examples again:\n\ncommandline                        filename\n\nAC -n t files:game.dms          -> files:games\nAC files:-s-kick.wrp            -> files:-s-kick.wrp\nAC shitfuck dh1:master.lzh      -> dh1:master.lzh\n\n\n\n                                               [32mKick/Steel[m - Berlin 4/91\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',5339,4,0,NULL,NULL,'ac092','scan',1780048365);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('acc_v100','ACC-V100.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ACC-V100.LHA',NULL,'XIM','PRESENTS : ACCOUNT ED','1.00',NULL,'ACC',NULL,replace('PRESENTS : ACCOUNT ED V1.00\n','\n',char(10)),'AccEd.Doc',replace('\n      //\      //\         //\  //\_   //\ //\_    //\____     //\____\n      \\ \     \\/     //\ \\/  \\_ \  \\/ \\_ \   \\__   \    \\___  \\n     //\\ \   //\ //\ // ///\  //\_\/ //\ //\ \ \ //\ \\  /   //\__/  /\n    // /\\ \ // /// ///  \/ ///\\_ \ // /// ///  \/ / // /   // ___  /\n   //  \_/  \/  \/  \/   /  \/  \/  \/  \/  \/   /  \//  \  //  \ /  \  \n   \\_______/\__/\______/\__/\______/\__/\______/\__/\\__/  \\__/\\__/[SNAP] \n\n                          PRESENTS : ACCOUNT ED V1.00\n\n Introduction to Division A Account Ed!\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n Well, hello Sysop''s!				DATE: 08-28-92 TIME: 16:32:42\n\n This is The Leading One / Division A writing on another doc!\n\n I''m here again to give ya'' another usefull util releaving you from some\n of the more boring sides of beeing a Sysop!\n\n First of ALL I want to thank everyone who has supported me when I have been\n coding on my doors!\n\n Second I want to tell you that this util has been under development in 2\n months and is QUALITY SOFTWARE, it''s has been carefully tested against bugs\n & *VERY* optimized since the real version 1.00 (This is actually version\n V1.08, but since I decided from the start that I would release a HIGH QUALITY\n door it took some time as I said. The first version took only 2 days to\n finish, but I wanted to make the fasted AREXX PROGRAM AVAILABLE!)\n\n Use this door at YOUR own risk, it hasn''t caused any problems on my bbs for\n the past 2 months and it WILL NEVER do it cause i''ve tested it to it''s edges\n and that''s for YOUR SAFETY!\n\n This is a HIGH SECURETY PERFORMANCE DOOR which CAN log everything what your\n users does and you can cut off almost any function that you don''t think is\n aproperiate for your Cosysop!\n\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n Here''s the main features :)\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n ° This door is 100% compatible with the built in account editor\n ° It logs if any one LOOKS at an account or WRITES an account\n ° It does not use the built in callerslog if a hacker deletes it you stand\n   there like a fool.. You can chose any name you like!\n ° It have features like that you can PRINT an account\n ° You can branch 1 account forward or backward or 10 at a time\n ° It fully supports the numeric keyboard so you can save & exit from there\n ° It creates bulletins with which persons who have access to conference X\n ° It creates a securety bulletin where YOU can chose which securety levels\n   You would like to look at, etc 20-255, Ed will then list all users who\n   have access between 20-255 + which confs they have access to\n ° It features a global conference access upgrader which can either take or\n   give access to a specific conference for ALL USERS and if you which you\n   can state if you want it to give access to etc conf 9 to all users who\n   have access 30-40 or so (it''s the best one I''ve ever seen)\n ° Someone who uses the door can NOT give anyone higher status than he has\n   got so you cosysop with acc 230 can give himself acc 255 :)\n ° It features 9 presets (AmiEx built in editor 6 presets)\n ° You can search for a name in any way if you just now a bit of the name\n   trype that and it will find it (Wildcards) etc you have a user called\n   The Silencer (Hi! :) and you only remember the part of the called called\n   ''ncer'' (Strange..), well just write ncer as a name and Account Ed will find\n   the user! You don''t have to use ANY ''*'' Ed won''t work if you use it!\n ° If you use the ''N'' command look at new users and jumps of the account\n   reading to read a normal account ED remembers where you where so it will\n   look for the next new user if you use the ''N'' command again!\n ° This util will NOT damage your USER.DATA in *ANY WAY* and have NO BACKDOORS!\n   like other user.data utils like tarheels ...\n ° All information about you user.data was extracted by me (The Leading One)\n ° You can put a securety level for changing data in the account editor like\n   the commands similar to (A-T) so your cosysop ONLY can use presets and\n   READ account (Yeah) for uppgrading new users and NOT fooling around!\n ° You can put in a securety level for using the GLOBAL Conf acc upgrader!\n ° It''s programmed in AREXX for reliable and user friendly code\n\n And that''s 18 VERY REASONABLE reasons for YOU to atleast TRY this door out!\n \n Yours, The Leading One of Division A\n\n PS! The next door I will release is called Member and is made especially\n     for Division A DS!\n\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n Other doors available from Division A Doors:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n Quest		- A Questionary door for new users with a sysop meny USE IT!\n Sysop Uploader - The best Sysop upload util available\n File Comment   - Adds a file comment ANY WHERE in you filelistening\n Division A Vote- The voting door with the coolest functions made for Equinox Top 20\n Connect	- Emulates an AmiExpress board as an advertisment! Pretty cool\n Account Ed	- An Account Editor for high securety and fast upgrades\n Node Activities- A Who door, who is on the nodes ?\n News mag	- If you want a paper on your board this is it!\n Members	- Comming Soon!\n\n All doors available & FREE DOWNLOAD on Insanety +46(0)589-10780\n All World Releases are made thru my board so call it! 8)\n\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n Instalation VERY Inportant\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n This is going to be step by step instructions so hold on.\n\n 1. First put this in your custom command file with a text editor\n\n    1*        Rm255Doors:Arexx/Account/AccED.rexx\n\n 2. Make an assign called Doors:, make a dir in doors called Arexx and\n    make a dir in Arexx called Account. You must do this otherwise the\n    door wont work! And it''s smart to do so becouse all my other doors\n    also needs this path and the dir called Arexx!\n\n 3. Load the arexx source into a text editor and look att the top where\n    there are a bunch of comments (/* XXX */)\n\n    UserFile	 = ''BBS:User.Data''\n\n    This is the name of your user.data file! If you want to test all the\n    functions in Account Ed and don''t want to ruin your user.data, just\n    make a copy of your and rename it and enter that name instead and you\n    can test it and assure yourself that this door is completly harmless!\n\n    UserKeys	 = ''BBS:User.Keys''\n\n    This is the name of your user.keys file, since Account Ed NEVER writes\n    anything to that file you don''t have to make a backup of that file or\n    something like that\n\n    Enable   	 = 255\n\n    This is the securety a user has got to have if he wants to change \n    anything in the account except using the presets to upgrade users.\n    Very usefull if you don''t think your cosysops should change peoples\n    uploads / download bytes or things like that\n\n    Thus, these commands are always avaible for a user even if the user\n    doesn''t have the enable status:\n\n    A = Change name\n    B = Change location\n    J = Change autorejoin conference\n    T = Change timelimit\n\n    The rest of the commands from C-S are ONLY available if a user has got\n    the enable status or higher\n\n    Log      	 = 2\n\n    This parameter tells Account Ed how much it should log what happens in\n    the door. These are the values you can use:\n\n    1 = Make logfile ONLY when someone reads an account\n    2 = Make logfile ONLY when someone saves an account (like the built in ed)\n    3 = Make logfile when someone either reads or saves an account\n    4 = Logfile turned OFF\n\n    ChangeAcc	 = 255\n\n    This is the access needed by a user to have the opertunety to use the\n    Global Access upgrader function. If a user has got that status he may\n    remove ALL users access to a certain conference so beware\n\n    Printer	 = ''On''\n\n    If you don''t have a Printer or don''t want anyone to print out an account\n    on your printer change that to Off. If it''s on your or the person using\n    Account Ed could print out the account they''re watching\n\n    LPos	 = 100 * 231\n\n    If you have many users and know that you never deletes anyone under the\n    slotnumber 100 for an example you just set the left value to 100, then\n    Account Ed then searches for new users it automatically starts to search\n    from user 100. 231 is an constant and should NOT be changed if you want\n    the search for new user function to work properly\n\n 4. Save the source and put it in DOORS:Arexx/Account/AccEd.Rexx\n\n 5. Now you have to set up your presets file! This is how the preset file\n    should look like:\n\n    First your should state how many presets you are going to have minimum\n    0 and maximum 9\n\n    1\n\n    And then you have to write what the first preset should be in this\n    form! Do not add the comment that i Will add.\n\n    30		-> Securety Level\n    1		-> Ratio Type, 0 = Free Dl, 1 = Bytes & Files and so on\n    3		-> Ul/Dl ratio 1/3\n    1000000	-> Daily bytes limit\n    XX___XXX	-> Conference access! You may use - instead of _ if you like\n    3600	-> Time limit in secounds\n\n    A preset file could look like this:\n\n       _____ Number of presets\n      /\n    2\n    5\n    1\n    2\n    100000\n    X________\n    1200\n    3600\n    30\n    1\n    3\n    400000\n\n    Well that''s all about that and I hope that you''ll manage to fix that.\n\n 6. Save the preset file as DOORS:Arexx/Account/AccEd.Presets\n\n 7. Login to your BBS and write 1 at the prompt!\n\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n How to use the Account Editor\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n These commands are avaible when you have choosed an account and loaded it:\n\n On the numeric pad:\n\n * - Save account\n / - Exit account editing\n . - Print account\n + - Move one account forward\n - - Move one account backward\n [ - Move ten accounts forward\n ] - Move ten accounts backward\n\n On the regular keyboard:\n\n Del - Delete account\n 0   - Reactivate\n 1-9 - Presets\n A-T - Change info in the account, showed when account editing\n TAB - Exit\n\n Shift-~ = Save account\n Shift-X = Exit\n\n The commands has been placed so it should be VERY fast and easy to look at\n an account and change! There for most of the commands are available at the\n numeric PAD!\n\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n Files Included in the Package\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n Account/       Bytes\n\n AccEd.Rexx	21694\n AccEd.History	  217\n AccEd.Doc	13047\n AccEd.Presets	  155\n AccEd.Log	   80\n Division	 2294\n\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n Disclaimer\n ~~~~~~~~~~~\n I (The Leading One/Division A) take no resonibilities what so ever for what\n this util may cause (It should not cause any thing atleast not on my board)\n or for the usefullness of it.\n\n THIS PROGRAM IS NOT PD, IF YOU USE IT YOU HAVE TO CALL MY BOARD AS A PAYMENT\n +46(0)589-10780. THIS SOFTWARE GOES UNDER THE NAME: ''CALLWARE''\n\n When I spread this util there where no Backdoors, but if you want my utils\n backdoor free, free download and 1st in the world then call my board!\n\n This package may ONLY be redistrubated in it''s origanally form. And NOT\n included in the AmiExpress(tm) package without MY permission.\n\n If the AmiEx development team want me to make more doors for their package,\n then please give me more info personally, like how to address and get data\n from AmiEx using Assembler! That info is REALLY hard to get I''ve tried!!!\n\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n Well that''s all about the program! DO NOT CHANGE ANYTHING IN THE SOURCE\n becouse I have spent quite a lot of time developening this program and\n it does not seam fair that you change something and then write that\n it''s you who have made this util! So please call my board and I will make\n the improvments you want! ALSO CALL ME FOR ANY REASON! Or.. If you simple\n want to join Division A... :)\n\n And what is life without being greeted ?\n\n Spirit 	/ Psychotic\n Phoenix	/ Psychotic\n Neuromancer	/ Cytax\n Harakiri	/ Triad\n Tropic		/ Division A\n GelyHead	/ The Eternal Genises\n Pripps		/ X-Trade\n Ice		/ The Silents (For not installing my doors :)\n D-Zire		/ The Silents\n The Silencer   / Equinox\n Rioter		/ Equinox\n Dream Warrior	/ Phenomena\n Bareface	/ Basstech\n Maltese Falcon / AmiEx Development Team (For Keeping up da'' good work!)\n ByteMaster	/ AmiEx Development Team (For making an almost useable prg..:)\n Cool Falco	/ Humm For making nice doors!\n\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n More doors ahead! Signed: The Leading One / DIVISION A\n\n PS! Sorry for my bad english, but I would like to se an American or an\n                               English man write swedish... Hahahaha :) DS!\n\n                   Call My BOARD: +46(0)589-10780 (INSANETY)\n\n                         (Division A Doors Support BBS)\n\n            Or... Call HARDCORE Division A WHQ +46(0)19-123460 (HST)\n\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n                  .:. DVA .:. In Hoc Signo Vinces .:. DVA .:.\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,18107,6,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048365);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('acc_v103','ACC-V103.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ACC-V103.LHA',NULL,'XIM','PRESENTS : ACCOUNT ED','1.03',NULL,'ACC',NULL,replace('PRESENTS : ACCOUNT ED V1.03\n','\n',char(10)),'AccEd.Doc',replace('                     _      ___    _______        ______   _\n 2.30+     /\    /\ | \  /\/  \\  /      /\    /\/\     \ / \        Major\n Door     /  \  // \|  \/  \   \\/ _____// \  /  \ \/\  \\|  \       Hacker\n For     /|   \//   \   \   \   \\  |  //   \/  //  \    \\   \      Proof\n Your    \|   //    /  //        /  | //  __/  //    __   /  //__    Update!\n Safety   \  /     /| //|  |\  _/|  | \       //|   /|   /| /    \\n           \______/ |_/ |__| \__\|__|  \______/ |__/ |__/ |______/ DLS\n       \n                         PRESENTS : ACCOUNT ED V1.03\n\n Introduction to Virtual Account Ed!\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n Well, Hello Sysop''s ''n Hackers!!		DATE: 03-27-93 TIME: 21:02:36\n\n This is Delusion / Virtual writing on another doc!\n\n I''m here again to give ya'' another usefull util releaving you from some\n of the more boring sides of beeing a Sysop!\n\n First of ALL I want to thank everyone who has supported me when I have been\n coding on my doors and to Kid Curry / Endless Piracy and D-Zire / Silents\n for pointing out the need of an real 2.30+ update! This door only works on\n 2.30+ AmiExpress. If you only have 1.1w+ then use Account Ed V1.03\n\n Second I wan''t to tell you that this util has been under development in 6\n months and is QUALITY SOFTWARE, it''s has been carefully tested against bugs\n & *VERY* optimized since the real version 1.00 (This is actually version\n V1.03, but since I decided from the start that I would release a HIGH QUALITY\n door it took some time as I said. The first version took only 2 days to\n finish, but I wanted to make the fasted AREXX PROGRAM AVAILABLE!)\n\n Use this door at YOUR own risk, it hasn''t caused any problems on my bbs for\n the past 6 months and it WILL NEVER do it cause I''ve tested it to it''s edges\n and that''s for YOUR SAFETY!\n\n This is a HIGH SECURETY PERFORMANCE DOOR which CAN log everything what your\n users does and you can cut off almost any function that you don''t think is\n aproperiate for your Cosysop. You can also withdraw the access for this\n door between two predefined time periods like between 24.00 and 08.00!\n\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n Here''s the main features :)\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n ° This door is 100% compatible with the built in account editor\n ° It is compatible with the Quest Door programmed by me so you whenever\n   you watch an account just press a butten and you''ll get that users\n   questionary at your screen. Very usefull when upgrading new users!!!\n ° Built in help page in the account editor for fast help\n ° It logs if any one LOOKS at an account or WRITES an account\n ° It does not use the built in callerslog if a hacker deletes it you stand\n   there like a fool.. You can chose any name you like!\n ° But, it''s adds a line to the callerslog saying "Account Editing..."\n ° It checks if the user in on a predefined list with user who should have\n   access to account ed!\n ° You can withdraw the access to the acount editor between to time periods\n   so no one can account ed between 24.00 and 08.00 for instance\n ° It have features like that you can PRINT an account to your PRINTER\n ° You can branch 1 account forward or backward or 10 at a time\n ° It fully supports the numeric keyboard so you can save & exit from there\n ° It creates bulletins with which persons who have access to conference X\n ° It creates a securety bulletin where YOU can chose which securety levels\n   You would like to look at, etc 20-255, Ed will then list all users who\n   have access between 20-255 + which confs they have access to\n ° It features a global conference access upgrader which can either take or\n   give access to a specific conference for ALL USERS and if you which you\n   can state if you want it to give access to etc conf 9 to all users who\n   have access 30-40 or so (it''s the best one I''ve ever seen)\n ° Someone who uses the door can NOT give anyone higher status than he has\n   got so you cosysop with acc 230 can give himself acc 255 :)\n ° You can specify a conf that no one can give access to! :) Like member conf!\n ° It features 9 presets (AmiEx built in editor 6 presets)\n ° You can give each preset an description which will be displayed\n ° Every time you save an account it cleans up the mess amiex has done!\n ° You can search for a name in any way if you just now a bit of the name\n   trype that and it will find it (Wildcards) etc you have a user called\n   The Silencer (Hi! :) and you only remember the part of the called called\n   ''ncer'' (Strange..), well just write ncer as a name and Account Ed will find\n   the user! You don''t have to use ANY ''*'' Ed won''t work if you use it!\n ° If you use the ''N'' command and then exit the account you can continue\n   where you started if you choose ''N'' again ...\n ° This util will NOT damage your USER.DATA in *ANY WAY* and have NO BACKDOORS!\n   like other user.data utils as tarheels ...\n ° All information about you user.data was extracted by me (Delusion)\n ° You can put a securety level for changing data in the account editor like\n   the commands similar to (A-T) so your cosysop ONLY can use presets and\n   READ account (Yeah) for uppgrading new users and NOT fooling around!\n ° You can put in a securety level for using the GLOBAL Conf acc upgrader!\n ° It''s programmed in AREXX for reliable and user friendly code\n\n And that''s 26 VERY REASONABLE reasons for YOU to atleast TRY this door out!\n \n Yours, Delusion of Virtual\n\n All hackers are gonna hate you for installing this door! I promise!\n\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n Other doors available from Virtual Doors Productions: (VTL)\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n Quest		 - A Questionary door for new users with a sysop meny USE IT!\n Sysop Uploader  - The best Sysop upload util available\n File Comment    - Adds a file comment ANY WHERE in you filelistening\n Virtual Vote    - The voting door with the coolest functions made for Equinox Top 20\n Connect	 - Emulates an AmiExpress board as an advertisment! Pretty cool\n Account Ed	 - An Account Editor for high securety and fast upgrades\n Node Activities - A Who door, who is on the nodes ?\n News mag	 - If you want a paper on your board this is it!\n Log Viewer	 - Views log files for the above programs backwards!\n Config Ed	 - Edit your Config files online or remote...\n Virtual Chart   - A Complement door to Virtual Vote, for disk mags etc\n LastCallers Util- The best lastcallers util around which makes 3 output bulls\n DirXCleaner     - Deletes all your old files both on hd and in dir\n MailServer(DNET)- Echo Mail Program for /X to register call my board!\n Members	 - Comming Soon!\n\n All doors available & FREE DOWNLOAD on INSANiTY +46(0)589-10780\n All World Releases are made thruogh my board so call it! 8)\n\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n Instalation VERY Important\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n This is going to be step by step instructions so hold on.\n\n 1. First put this in your BBS:Commands/BBS.cmd file with a text editor\n\n    1*        Rm230Doors:Arexx/Account/AccED.rexx\n\n 2. Make an assign called Doors:, make a dir in doors called Arexx and\n    make a dir in Arexx called Account. You must do this otherwise the\n    door wont work! And it''s smart to do so becouse all my other doors\n    also needs this path and the dir called Arexx!\n\n 3. Load the arexx source into a text editor and look att the top where\n    there are a bunch of comments (/* XXX */)\n\n    UserFile	 = ''BBS:User.Data''\n\n    This is the name of your user.data file! If you want to test all the\n    functions in Account Ed and don''t want to ruin your user.data, just\n    make a copy of your and rename it and enter that name instead and you\n    can test it and assure yourself that this door is completly harmless!\n\n    UserKeys	 = ''BBS:User.Keys''\n\n    This is the name of your user.keys file, since Account Ed NEVER writes\n    anything to that file you don''t have to make a backup of that file or\n    something like that\n\n    Enable   	 = 255\n\n    This is the securety a user has got to have if he wants to change \n    anything in the account except using the presets to upgrade users.\n    Very usefull if you don''t think your cosysops should change peoples\n    uploads / download bytes or things like that\n\n    Thus, these commands are always avaible for a user even if the user\n    doesn''t have the enable status:\n\n    A = Change name\n    B = Change location\n    J = Change autorejoin conference\n    T = Change timelimit\n\n    The rest of the commands from C-S are ONLY available if a user has got\n    the enable status or higher\n\n    Log      	 = 2\n\n    This parameter tells Account Ed how much it should log what happens in\n    the door. These are the values you can use:\n\n    1 = Make logfile ONLY when someone reads an account\n    2 = Make logfile ONLY when someone saves an account (like the built in ed)\n    3 = Make logfile when someone either reads or saves an account\n    4 = Logfile turned OFF\n\n    ChangeAcc	 = 255\n\n    This is the access needed by a user to have the opertunety to use the\n    Global Access upgrader function. If a user has got that status he may\n    remove ALL users access to a certain conference so beware\n\n    Printer	 = ''On''\n\n    If you don''t have a Printer or don''t want anyone to print out an account\n    on your printer change that to Off. If it''s on your or the person using\n    Account Ed could print out the account they''re watching\n\n    NewSlot	 = 100\n\n    If you have many users and know that you never deletes anyone under the\n    slotnumber 100 for an example you just set the left value to 100, then\n    Account Ed then searches for new users it automatically starts to search\n    from user 100.\n\n    NotAccC	 = 5\n\n    If you ie have cosysops from another group and have an area for your\n    group that you don''t want your cosysops to give themselves access to\n    just enter the number of that conference here. On my board Virtual\n    has got the conference 5, so I don''t want any outsiders in there so I set\n    my Not Access To Conference to 5, simple ehh? On the other hand if you\n    don''t have a restricted area just set that value to 0 and anything else!\n\n 4. Save the source and put it in DOORS:Arexx/Account/AccEd.Rexx\n\n 5. Now you have to set up your presets file! This is how the preset file\n    should look like:\n\n        Type of file ratio  Dayly download bytes    Account Ed Version Number\n                          \              |                        |\n        Securety Level     \ File Ratio  |    Dayly time limit    |\n                      \     \    |       |                   |    |\n      Number of Presets|     |   |       | Conference Access |    |\n     /                 |     |   |       |        \          |    |\n    6----------------------------------------------------------1.03\n    | Lamer          | 5   | 1 | 2 | 100000   | X________ | 1200  |\n    | PD User        | 20  | 1 | 3 | 500000   | X_X__X_X_ | 3600  |\n    | Elite User     | 30  | 1 | 3 | 2500000  | X_XX_X_X_ | 3600  |\n    | Elite User +   | 40  | 1 | 4 | 5000000  | X_XX_X_X_ | 4800  |\n    | Virtual Member | 50  | 1 | 5 | 10000000 | X_XXXX_X_ | 7200  |\n    | Proud CoSysop  | 230 | 0 | 5 | 10000000 | XXXXXXXXX | 14400 |\n    2359-------------------------------------------------------0730\n  / | Delusion Sauna Fox D-Zire                                   | \\n |  ---------------------------------------------------------------  |\n |                             \                                     |\n Start time for locking out     Certified users to use  End time for locking\n users from Account Ed          Account Ed              out users from AccEd\n\n    Well that''s all about that and I hope that you''ll manage to fix that.\n    You should load the actual preset file supplied within this archive\n    to your values and save it. Do not snap this one becouse the positions\n    are not right! :)\n\n 6. Save the preset file as DOORS:Arexx/Account/AccEd.Presets\n\n 7. Login to your BBS and write 1 at the prompt!\n\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n How to use the Account Editor\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n These commands are avaible when you have choosed an account and loaded it:\n\n On the numeric pad:\n\n * - Save account\n / - Show users questionary\n . - Print account\n + - Move one account forward\n - - Move one account backward\n [ - Move ten accounts forward\n ] - Move ten accounts backward\n\n On the regular keyboard:\n\n Del - Delete account\n 0   - Reactivate\n 1-9 - Presets\n A-T - Change info in the account, showed when account editing\n TAB - Exit\n\n Shift-~ = Save account\n Shift-X = Exit\n\n The commands has been placed so it should be VERY fast and easy to look at\n an account and change! There for most of the commands are available at the\n numeric PAD!\n\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n Disclaimer\n ~~~~~~~~~~~\n I (Delusion/Virtual) take no resonibilities what so ever for what\n this util may cause (It should not cause any thing atleast not on my board)\n or for the usefullness of it.\n\n THIS PROGRAM IS NOT PD, IF YOU USE IT YOU HAVE TO CALL MY BOARD AS A PAYMENT\n +46(0)589-10780. THIS SOFTWARE GOES UNDER THE NAME: ''CALLWARE''\n\n When I spread this util there where no Backdoors, but if you want my utils\n backdoor free, free download and 1st in the world then call my board!\n\n This package may ONLY be redistrubated in it''s origanally form. And NOT\n included in the AmiExpress(tm) package without MY permission.\n\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n Well that''s all about the program! DO NOT CHANGE ANYTHING IN THE SOURCE\n becouse I have spent quite a lot of time developening this program and\n it does not seam fair that you change something and then write that\n it''s you who have made this util! So please call my board and I will make\n the improvments you want! ALSO CALL ME FOR ANY REASON! Or.. If you simple\n want to join Virtual... :)\n\n And what is life without being greeted ?\n\n Spirit 	/ Psychotic\n Phoenix	/ Psychotic\n Fox            / 2000 AD\n GelyHead	/ The Eternal Genises\n Ice		/ The Silents\n D-Zire		/ The Silents\n Norad          / Anarchy\n The Silencer   / Equinox (Any more cool doors comming!?)\n Rioter		/ Equinox (I hope your game is great)\n Dream Warrior	/ Phenomena\n Maltese Falcon / AmiEx Development Team (For Keeping up da'' good work, but\n                                          don''t let it go to your head!)\n Joseph Hodge	/ AmiEx Development Team (For making an almost useable prg..:)\n Cool Falco	/ For making nice doors!\n\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n More doors ahead! Signed: Delusion / Virtual\n\n PS! Sorry for my bad english, but I would like to se an American or an\n                               English man write swedish... Hahahaha :) DS!\n\n    Call My Board NOW: +46(0)589-10780 (INSANiTY) Dual Standard VTL EHQ\n\n                         (Virtual Doors Support BBS)\n\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n                  .:. VTL .:. In Hoc Signo Vinces .:. VTL .:.\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,25528,9,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048365);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('acc_v105','ACC-V105.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ACC-V105.LHA',NULL,'XIM','PRESENTS : ACCOUNT ED','1.05',NULL,'ACC',NULL,replace('PRESENTS : ACCOUNT ED V1.05\n','\n',char(10)),'AccEd.Doc',replace('\n                 »» From The Worlds No.1 /X Door Makers ««\n\n         °        °        °   °      °    °       °   °   °    °\n      °    ° __°   __° __° ______ °_  __° __ °__° ______° __ °     °\n   °    °   /~~\° /~~\/~~\/~~ _~~\/~\/~~\/~~\/~~\/~~ _~~\/~~\ 93'' °   °\n      °  ° /   / /   /   /  ¬\/  / _____/  _/\  /  /\/  /  _/ °   °\n     °    /\  /\/   /\  /   \  _/  _/  /   /   /      _/\  /_  ° °   °\n   °   °  \_ ¬ /   /  _/\  //  /  /  °/  _/   /   /\  /  _/  \°    °\n      °    \__  __/___/\__/ \_/\_/ °  \____/\/\__/___/_  ____/ © DLS\n   °  "  " """\/"""""""""" ° """" °  ° """"    """"""""\/"""""" "  "  °\n      °    °    °       °      °      °    °     °       ° °    °  °\n        °    °     °  °     °      °      °   °     °     °   °\n         V·i·r·t·u·a·l P·r·e·s·e·n·t·s A·c·c·o·u·n·t E·d V·1·.·0·5\n\n                                 Starring\n\n                     Delusion of Virtual as Programmer\n\n  /\  __________________/\/\_________________/\___________ _  _  _   _    _\n /  \/\n	Introduction, Preface\n    \n	Finaly I''ve rewritten this 6 months old documentation and given\n	it a new look that should be far more easier to read and get some\n	hints from. This is revision V1.05 and you might have to take a\n	closer look at some upgraded fascillities that is not compatible\n	with V1.04 & V1.03, but here we go from the begining so hang on ..\n\n	Account Editor (Short name AccED) is a so called ARexx Door for\n	the /X 2.35+ package and will interfer as an AIM (Arexx Interface\n        Module). If you use this door you can make the security on your\n	board even higher with the high security features of this door.\n\n	The source is not compiled and should be rather easy for an ARexx\n	programmer to take a look at, which you also should do if you\n	wan''t to be sure there is no backdoors provided with the source\n	from one in the row of people who got it before you. To be sure\n	wether there is a backdoor or not you should call my board INSANiTY\n	which is the official distrubtion site for my doors and my /X\n	echo mail package which is available for a nominal fee. I''m right\n	now doing a major update on that program so it can aproximatly\n	be delivered first at May. ßeta versions will be available sooner.\n\n  /\  __________________/\/\_________________/\___________ _  _  _   _    _\n /  \/\n	What will AccED do for you?\n\n	Account Ed is designed with high security in mind and I think my\n	door is the first one that can lock out a user at a specific time\n	period, ie between 24.00 and 08.00 in the morning if you think\n	that no one should access the account editor then.\n\n	It also checks if a person got the right name from a list of\n	persons alloved to use the account editor. This works in the same\n	way as Maltese Falcons Remote Shell and Sysop Download utils.\n\n	Every entry in the user data that someone who is in Account ED\n	look at will be reported and logged in a speciall Account ED log\n	file. It will also add comments if someone read or wrote an account\n	and if you print an account. Yes, you could actually print an account\n	to your printer using the printer settings from your Amiga DOS.\n	This feature is really my favorite, if you are going to delete an\n	user you could easily print the users account before selecting\n	delete and store it somewhere for no good but anyway ..\n\n	You can lock certain functions in the account editor for your\n	cosysops so they only could use the 6 pre defined presets, no\n	I''m joking .. 6 presets, NO! the 9 pre defined presets with a\n	comment which you can write so the cosysop knows what each preset\n	stands for and for which users they are meant. Nice ehh!?\n\n	Like the MCP (Master Control Program) by Bryce, you can give and\n	take access for a conference for all your users, so if you close\n	a conference you easily can delete all users access to it or if\n	you simple have started a new area. But.. wouldn''t it be nice to\n	go a litle bit further and include one more nice feature into that\n	powerfull command? Yes! You can define between which two access\n	levels a user must be so you could give/take access from users who\n	only has got the security level 30 to 40 ie.\n\n	As the need to check for a user that you by mistake has given a too\n	high security level even grows stronger the more hackers there\n	are around I''ve included the feature to get a list of all users\n	between to certain security levels so you could use 200 to 255 or\n	if you simple wan''t a whole userlist you type 1 to 255 ..\n	This section of Account ED also includes the possibility to get\n	a list of all users who has got access to a certain conference for\n	instance your groups member conference 5!\n\n	Back to the main account editor there are some major line ups if\n	you compare to the built in editor. First of all the design is\n	made to be easy to overview and fast to get some particular\n	information about one user. The built in one was so messy that I\n	had a hard time to understand my own account with the download /\n	upload cps and location put like a joke on the screen. This is\n	should be easy to read and each function has got new letters\n	becouse the old ones was worn out and not well placed. I hope\n	you''ll soon learn the new keys!\n\n	The help page inside the account editor is for easy access to\n	the most common functions inside the editor. You simple press\n	a key and you can view it at the same time as the account is on\n	the same page so you easily could compare and so on. If you\n	have used my Questionary Door called Quest (last version V1.09)\n	this program is fully compatible with Quest. Anytime when you\n	are reading a persons account you could press a key and get that\n	users questionary on your screen. Very usefull if you upgrade\n	first time users.. I think you remeber yourself loading a text-\n	editor with your Answers file and trying to upgrade that poor\n	users account, but how did your cosysops manage!? I guess that\n	they didn''t and the security with new users failed on your board!\n\n	Ever wanted a function that writes a letter very fast to your\n	users and saying that they should upload and shows the users\n	stats with uploaded/download bytes & file, calls and message?\n	Well it''s built in into Account ED!\n\n	Another thing that can make you nervs popp up is then you have\n	to delete old recieved messages from users who has not choosen\n	delete then they''ve replied letters and all those EALL messages\n	that you new users hate.. Account ED has a built in function\n	which scanns your msgbase and deletes old mail and asks what\n	you want to do with the EALL messages!!\n\n	You can give a speciall access level for viewing the passwords\n	of all acounts, if you do not have this security level Account ED\n	will prompt Not Displayed as a password. You can choose if the\n	password default should be shown to the ones with the security\n	level or they have to press a special key combination for the\n	password to appear. Usefull if you have some friends beside you!\n\n	What about security for your groups conference then? Well as this\n	program has been around a while I''ve thought of that too, so you\n	could specify a conference to which no one could give access!\n	This means that your cosysop not can give himself access to your\n	groups member area!!\n\n	Ok I see that you are beginning to understand why I developed\n	this new account editor, so I will now give you only one more\n	reason to use it. If you sometimes have an upload competion on\n	your board you know how anyoing it is to give that poor winner\n	his rewareded upload credits, it usually means that you have\n	to run down the stairs to get a pocket calculator and then\n	enter his new upload bytes. But you could stop doing that\n	already today if you use this account editor with built in\n	calculator which can add and sub from a users account. You just\n	choose the field you wan''t to change and use the upper case of\n	the letter instead and you will be asked if you wan''t to sub or\n	add and how many bytes. This works for all fields that has got\n	to do with upload, download and limits.\n\n	Oh, sorry I forgot to tell you one thing. In the /X account editor\n	when you choose ie to change the users uploaded creds it clears\n	that field and you have to try to remember what there was standing.\n	My account editor will not remove anything that you don''t write\n	over and when you move the cursor with the backspace key it won''t\n	remove any letters from the screen, but just in memory so you\n	easily could remeber what was standing there before and you then\n	can write over it!\n\n	These is more features than many doors together can''t even handle!\n	So you''d better take a closer look or you''ll regret it!\n\n  /\  __________________/\/\_________________/\___________ _  _  _   _    _\n /  \/\n	Instalation ..\n\n	Snap the following row to your BBS:Commands/BBS.Cmd file:\n\n	*1        Rm230Doors:Arexx/Account/AccEd.rexx\n\n	This will let all users with security level 230 and higher access\n	the account editor if their names are in the allowed user list.\n\n	When you have managed to do that it would be time to move the\n	Account ED package to your Doors:Arexx/ path, which is the path\n	all my doors requires so you better not put it elsewhere.\n\n	Previous user must note that there should be 3 new directories inside\n	the Account/ direcotry called: QuestApp, QuestDel and QuestQst.\n	if you are previous running Quest and has got it in the\n	Doors:Arexx/Quest/ dir you should move your questions from the answers\n	dir to the QuestApp dir in the Account directory. Otherwise Account ED\n	can''t get the questionaries! (More info in the Quest doc file)\n\n	After doing that you should edit the AccEd.Presets file which\n	shall contain your personal presets and comments. I will only\n	give a brief explenation on how that file works, you have to\n	find out the rest by yourself!\n\n	The 7 present at the left top edge is the numbers of presets you\n	are going to have. To add one for instance add the number to 8\n	and enter the new values under the 7:th preset. 2359 and 0730 is the\n	time period when no one has got access to Account ED. The names\n	located under the presets is all users who are allowed to use\n	the account editor.\n\n	  Comment         SecL  RaT Rat Aut  Bytelimit ConfAccess  TimeLim  Computers\n	7--------------------------------------------------------------1.05-------------------\nPreset1	| Lamer          | 5   | 1 | 2 | 1 | 100000   | X________ | 1200  | Amiga 500        |\nPreset2 | PD User        | 20  | 1 | 3 | 2 | 500000   | X_X__X_X_ | 3600  | Amiga 500+       |\nPreset3 | Elite User     | 30  | 1 | 3 | 4 | 2500000  | X_XX_X_X_ | 3600  | Amiga 600        |\nPreset4	| Elite Trader   | 40  | 1 | 3 | 7 | 5000000  | X_X__XXX_ | 4800  | Amiga 1000       |\nPreset5	| Virtual Member | 50  | 1 | 0 | 4 | 10000000 | X_XXXX_X_ | 7200  | Amiga 1200       |\nPreset6	| Virtual Member | 50  | 1 | 0 | 7 | 10000000 | X_X_XXXX_ | 7200  | Amiga 2000       |\nPreset7	| Proud CoSysop  | 230 | 0 | 0 | 7 | 10000000 | X_XX_XXXX | 14400 | Amiga 3000       |\nPreset8	|                |     |   |   |   |          |           |       | Amiga 4000       |\nPreset9	|                |     |   |   |   |          |           |       | PC Com 286       |\n	2359-----------------------------------------------------------0730 PC Com 386       |\n	| Delusion Sauna Fox D-Zire                                       | PC Com 486       |\n	------------------------------------------------------------------- PC Com 586       |\n	| UserData Path    | BBS:User.Data      | Enable Seclevel  |  255 | Atari 1040       |\n	| UserKeys Path    | BBS:User.Keys      | ChangeAcc Seclev |  255 | Other            |\n	| Write Note Path  | BBS:Conf-7         | MsgBaseClean Sec |  255 |                  |\n	| AccED Password   | Transworld         | See Users Pass   |  255 |                  |\n	| DeleteQuest Pass | Bobolink           | Show Users Pass  |  Off |                  |\n	| Recieve App Mail | Delusion           | Print Account    |   On |                  |\n	| AccountED Colour | [0m               | Search New Users |  300 |                  |\n	| Log Status AccED | 4                  | Members Conf     |    5 |                  |\n	| Reserved Nothing |                    | Kickout After X  |    5 |------------------|\n	| Reserved Nothing |                    | Questionary      |    4 | AccountED © 1993 |\n	| AutoAccess Quest | No                 | MustEnter No Ret |  Yes | Delusion of VTL! |\n	--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n	In previous preset files the computer list was in this form:\n	Amiga 500¬Amiga 1000¬ and so on, now it should stand in descending\n	order in the column which says computers.\n\n	Under the names with the persons who has got access to Account\n	(Delusion Sauna Fox D-Zire) is all the configuration datas for both\n	Quest and Account ED, all values who has got to do with Quest is\n	explained separately in the Quest Doc so here comes the explanations:\n\n	UserData Path	- The path on you harddrive where your userdata is\n\n	UserData Keys	- The path on you harddrive where your userkeys is\n\n	Write Note Path - This is the path to the conference where you wan''t\n			  the warning notes made in Account ED to come\n			  This should be a path to one of your 9 conferences\n\n	AccED Password	- If you wan''t to enter a password to use Account ED\n			  you should enter a password here, if this line\n			  is empty Account Ed wont ask you for a password\n\n	DeleteQuestPass - This is the password a user has to enter if he\n			  want''s to delete a users questionary (application)\n\n	AccountEdColour - This is the colour in which all data in the AccED\n			  will be displayed in\n\n	Log Status AccEd- Maybe you don''t wan''t to log every action taken in\n			  Account ED, then you should change the Log variabel.\n			  Here is what the different numbers means:\n\n			  1, Log only when an account is read\n			  2, Log only when an account is saved\n			  3, Log both read and save\n			  4, Log both read and save, but not then sysop does it!\n			  0, Log nothing\n\n	Enable Seclevel	- This is the security level a user has got to have to\n			  change anything in a users account than the name,\n			  location and autorejoin conference. A user with\n			  lower status than the enable status can however use\n			  the nine presets, which is the meaning that the user\n			  should use instead. I recomend that you lower your\n			  cosysops security level to 230 and keep yours at 255.\n			  They can not logon your password becouse a user can\n			  not look at the slot number 1 and they can not give\n			  anyone higher security level than they self got, so\n			  a cosysop with 230 can not give himself security\n			  level 255 and play sysop which is the case with the\n			  built in account editor!\n\n	ChangeAcc Seclev- This is the access level a user has got to have if\n			  he want''s to give or take access from all users for\n			  a certain conference.	I explained that command in\n			  the features so read more about it there!\n\n	MsgBaseClean Sec- The access level required to use the built in\n			  message base cleaner, to delete old recieved mail\n\n	See Users Pass	- If you do not have this access level or higher you\n			  won''t be able	to se different users passwords when\n			  using the account editor. Have you sometime asked\n			  yourself the question, why should my cosysop se\n			  other users passwords, then he just should upgrade\n			  users accounts!?\n\n	Show Users Pass - This option works like this.. If a user has got the\n			  requested security level entered at SeePass the user\n			  will then be able to se another users password, but\n			  if this option is turned Off your user has to	push\n			  Shift+C to see the password and edit it. If he\n			  doesn''t there	will only stand Not Displayed. If you\n			  have choosed to let your cosysops view the users\n			  passwords, but don''t wan''t them to see them by\n			  defualt you should choose Off, if you always wan''t\n			  to see the password you should choose On and the\n			  passwords will be displayed if you have SeePass\n			  security level.\n\n	Print Account	- If you do not own a printer you should deffinently\n			  chose Off as a printer option, or if you don''t wan''t\n			  anyone to print an account.\n\n	Search New Users- This one is made to increase the speed when searching\n			  for new users. If you know that you will never get a\n			  new user with the slot number under 300, then choose\n			  300 and the Account Editor will start to search for\n			  new users beginning at the slot number 300!\n\n	Members Conf	- As my board is Virtual European HeadQuarter and main\n			  board for all our comming productions and so on in\n			  our special member area, I found it very anoying\n			  with cosysops giving them selves access to that\n			  conference just of curiosity. That problem has now\n			  been eliminated with this feature letting the sysop\n			  specify a conference where no one can give themselves\n			  access too. The only way to give a user access to\n			  conference is to use the built in /X editor on the F6\n			  key when someone is currently online!\n\n	This is how it could look. Do not snap this one, use the supplied\n	one in this archive called AccEd.Presets. Please note that everything\n	is position dependant, all configuration parameters must stand between\n	a | and a | so it could look like this |         BBS:User.Data | or\n	| BBS:User.Data.          | it doesn''t matter.\n\n	If you have any questions concerning this rather complicated config\n	file, don''t be afraid to call my board and ask!\n\n	You should now be finished with the instalation.\n\n  /\  __________________/\/\_________________/\___________ _  _  _   _    _\n /  \/\n	Greetings\n\n	My regards has to go to the folowing people in no order.\n\n	D-Zire of Silents		»» Thanx all time m8\n	The Silencer of Equinox		»» Looking forward to your netmailprg\n	Quaz of Addonic			»» Do you really think ADC is the right?\n	Ice of Silents			»» When does you start to use LaC again?\n	Kid Curry of Endless Piracy	»» Could use your support again!\n	Norad of Anarchy		»» Thanx for using my LastCallersUtil!\n	Fox of 2000 AD			»» For being my cool cosysop\n	Nightshade of Priority		»» I will soon make C doors, then..!\n	Rioter of Equinox		»» Articles comming soon for your mag\n	Kaka of Virtual			»» My /X door developer companion\n	It of Cryptoburners		»» Thanx for comments and calling me!\n	Micro Pal of Alcatraz		»» Looking forward to your slide show\n\n  /\  __________________/\/\_________________/\___________ _  _  _   _    _\n /  \/\n	Final words\n\n	This util has been developed and updated under a very long period.\n	The first version was made for /X 1.1x so you could imagine.\n	6 months ago I thought this was the best account editor available,\n	well it actually was the only replacement editor available. Now 6\n	months later I still thinks this one is the best, compared to the\n	built in.. There are no opponents nowadays either and I can only\n	say thank you! Becouse with that you all have proved that there\n	is no need for another one than this and I will continue to update\n	this one to even fit your needs in the future. Maybe there will\n	come a C version later this year, but no promises. It depends on\n	how much time I can spare for producing this account editor.\n \n	I hope you will get very much use of this util, or you won''t se\n	if it helps or not becouse your board will not be hacked (hope\n	fully), but if your board doesn''t get hacked you can thank this\n	util and your other utils like them from Maltese Falcon!\n\n	These are some other doors that I''ve made, Quest, Sysop Uploader,\n	File Comment, Virtual Vote, Connect, Node Activities, News mag,\n	Log Viewer, Config Ed, Virtual Chart, LastCallers Util, DirXCleaner\n	MailServer (DNET), Members and Password Fail!\n\n	If I get the chance I hope to have a chat with you at a party,\n	maybe Computer Crossroads or at European Computer Conference,\n	invitation text to the last party is supplied within this archive!\n	I would be gratefull if you called my board and come with complaints,\n	ideas or whatever you may come up with on all my doors!\n\n	This program is Copyright Delusion of Virtual and may not be sold in\n	any form or made profitable on without the permission of the author.\n\n	Yours, Delusion of Virtual, Sat 1 May 1993\n \n        Can be reached at, INSANiTY +46(0)589-10780, DualStandard\n\n  /\  __________________/\/\_________________/\___________ _  _  _   _    _\n /  \/                                                   A DLS Dezign Prod 93''\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,44512,7,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048365);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('acc','ACC.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ACC.LHA','Access','XIM','Access',NULL,'TarHeel',NULL,'by TarHeel',replace('Access 1.0\nby TarHeel\n','\n',char(10)),'Access.Doc',replace('\n                                Access 1.0\n                                by TarHeel \n\n    ''Access''  what a name haha, I couldn''t think of anything else to call it\n so rename it to whatever turns you on.  grin.  Access rewrites the dir1-9\n file to show how many times a file has been accessed (downloaded).  It does\n demand a few things which are explained below.  It should be real easy to\n use,  simply place it in your c: dir   next  place a line in the script\n file that express executes at logoff    \n                                         run access\n\n that is it.  The program has no arguments.  It is quite smart really, besides\n I HATE programs that demand a lot of arguments when it is NOT necessary and\n the programmer could have figured it out himself if he is worth his salt. \n\n What the program does is this.  First it checks your configuration file. This\n file must be named   config1  or  config2  or config3   anything other then\n that the program will exit out.  (Yes I know this can be done different but\n that will be done in the next version of it.)    Here it gains the information\n the program needs for the different conference paths.  Next the proggie will\n read the last block of the callerslog and see which file(s) have been \n downloaded. LIMIT IS 30 FILES max.  The reason for the limit is because of\n the A500 problem (that NO ONE admits to).  After isolating the file names\n the program will scan the upload dir1 to find a match, once doing so the \n program will next search for the   Sent by:  (which MUST be Present) line.\n Once finding it the proggie checks to see if there has been previous \n Accesses and if so increments them by one.  if not then it will insert the\n line \n                   Downloaded 1 time\n                       or\n                   Downloaded 10 times      (if previously accessed)\n\n Thats about it.  I''m hoping that in explaining how this program works in\n fairly good detail it will give other programmers a idea on how to proceed\n with their utilities and make them MORE user friendly.  Programmers keep\n in mind that too many args to your utils does nothing but show how new\n you are to the game.  If you have to have args use relative words not this\n -L -E  Bullshit,  that don''t cut it plus  use toupper() so the command line\n is not cap sensitive!!   Remember the people that use your stuff are not\n the ones that programmed it.  I''m sure you know what I mean by that!\n      Any how enough of that.  I''m sure this proggie will have a bug or two\n it has only been tested on my machine and so far works great but I''m the\n one that programmed it.  grin.   So if any of you guys that love to make\n proggies fail  well here is your chance.  Report all bugs to my BBS.\n\n\n Program requirements!!!     READ THIS - Most Important !!!!!!!!!!!!!\n^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n\n  The program WILL NOT work unless the following conditions are met.\n \n    1.  Sent by:  Must Be Functional within the configuration file. and\n        The dir listing must be as express writes it.  One util that groups\n        all the files uploaded by one person and only puts one Sent by:\n        cannot be run with access.  (the util is nice but)\n\n    2.  Your callerslog must be active in your configuration file.  This\n        means you must have a callerslog.\n\n    3.  Access must reside with in the c: dir or the script must give the\n        full path name to it.\n\n    4.  You must have a Amiga!\n\n    5.  You must have my BBS number on you logoff.txt and logoff.txt.gr\n        files.  If not well the proggie won''t run.   (I know this is vane\n        but business is slow in this far corner of the world.  Of course\n        you could always write your own proggie.)\n\n    6.  You MUST be a registered owner of AmiExpress.  Well I guess the \n        proggie will work if you aren''t  but IT is going to be my PUSH\n        to get people to register for Express.  Now all you people in\n        Modem Wonderland that has been out there for a while should know\n        that I pretty well mean business when I make a statement.  So all\n        you cool people that are using Express and haven''t paid for it, \n        Buy It NOW!   To all the super cool Elite types or ones that think\n        they are, you can at least buy the program that helps you to trade\n        illegal programs.  Keep in mind that this is going to be my pet\n        project and if you haven''t heard of me well start asking questions\n        then.\n\n-------\n\n   Multi - Nodes ??\n\n        Not a clue what would happen there.   As I get some time I will check\n  into it and see what I come up with.   I plan on revising this proggie \n  anyhow so will add something along those lines.   Now If I had a new 2500\n  then it would have been done correctly to begin with.  (anyone have one\n  cheap??  hehe.  or will trade programming.  I haven''t really run across\n  anything I can''t program!)\n\n\n------\n\n     As stated above business is slow here so if you are looking for new\n stuff (util wise)  Call me.  Also  I''m looking for all the files I can\n get (grin).  Special attention is paid here for files containing C source\n code.   A recent mechanical HD problem destroyed almost all of my collection\n sniff sniff.   (it was the drives fault really!!) \n\n   Also included in the archive is a dir1 listing to show how it looks like\n after the proggie has done its thing.\n\n\n\n      The Association!   (206)-384-2591\n              Tender is Tarheel\n\n\n\n   PS   -  Hopefully I kept my standard in explaining things horribly and\n           keeping the spelling at the first grade level.                    \n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',17145,4,0,NULL,NULL,'acc','scan',1780048365);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('accpw','ACCPW.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ACCPW.LHA',NULL,'XIM','Account Edit Password Door',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,replace('Account Edit Password Door\n','\n',char(10)),'1.doc',replace('	\nAccount Edit PW Protection 1.0\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nAll files goes in Doors:1/\nChange the PASSWORD in 1-env to your own choice.\nALL letters in the PW is case sensitive.\nAdd filenote Restricted to the 1-envfile so it can''t be VS''ed or DS''ed.\n	\nAdd this to your customcommands file:\n	\n*1        RS255DOORS:1/1.rexx\n	\nOk thats all you have to do to make your system a little bit safer.\n	\n-Skalman, Valhalla +46-(0)54-566657\n	\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,2939,2,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048365);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('acct10','ACCT10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ACCT10.LHA','accountant','XIM','accountant',NULL,'ByteMaster',NULL,'Written by ByteMaster',replace('Accountant, version 1.0\nWritten by ByteMaster\n','\n',char(10)),'Accountant.Doc',replace('                           /X Accountant, version 1.0\n                              Written by ByteMaster\n                  /X Developement Team - The Silent Achievers\n                  -------------------------------------------\n\nThe /X Accountant is a door I put together for those sysops out there who\nenjoy the income of a subscriber based BBS. This door should help maintain\nMegaByte Purchases and also keep track days for a suscribed user.\n\nThe door is fairly easy to operate once installed.\n\nRequirements: AmiExpress 2.1+\n\nModule Type: X\n\nProgram Logic: \n     1) AutoAdds user to account as active current date.\n     2) Searches for user name in a file called accountant.cfg in the \n        program directory. If found will load the account editor, \n        otherwise:\n\n          a) If established ACCOUNTANT account, the user stats will be\n             updated. \n\n          b) user stats will be displayed.\n\n          c) returns to AmiExpress.\n\n     3) If user name was found in accountant.cfg then the account editor\n        will be brought up for editing accounts,\n\n        NOTE: Accountant.cfg is a file you create in the directory where\n              the Accountant is located. This file should have a list\n              of users authorised to use the editor.\n\n        NOTE: Everyone with access to the ACCOUNTANT will automatically\n              be assigned an account, which means the Sysop has an account\n              as well. \n\n     ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n     THE FOLLOWING ASSUMES THAT THE ACCOUNT EDITOR MODE IS ACTIVE BASED\n     ON ABOVE CRITERIA.\n     ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n     4) ACCOUNTANT Displays a list of commands:\n\n        a. A)dd - This allows you to add accounts to the ACCOUNTANT.\n                  If the account requested already exists then that\n                  account will be loaded.\n                  The account that is added will be ACTIVE current date.\n\n                  If you choose this option by mistake. Just press return\n                  at the name prompt and nothing will be changed.\n\n        b. S)ave- This saves the CURRENT account to the database. You\n                  must choose this option for each account that you change\n                  in order to retain the changes.\n\n        c. L)ookFor- This option will search for a specified account\n                     by name. There is no wildcards in this feature at\n                     this time.\n\n        d. N)ext- This option Loads the next account. If you have\n                  changed a prior account, make sure to save it first.\n                  If you are at the last account in the database then\n                  the first account will be loaded. This is sort of a\n                  Wrapping feature.\n\n        e. P)rior- This option Loads the account prior to the current\n                   on being displayed. If you have changed the current\n                   account, make sure you save it prior to selecting \n                   this option.\n\n        f. R)ecord- This is probably a bad name to use for a command, this\n                    command will update the user account History with the\n                    current TERMS''s information, then it will reset the\n                    TERM data and make the account INACTIVE. \n\n                    NOTE: Once the account is inactive the account is \n                          considered available for reuse, so if you\n                          plan on adding a new TERM for the USER do it now\n                          before the data gets overwitten by another account.\n        \n        g. Q)uit- Exits the ACCOUNTANT. Make sure you have saved any desired\n                  changes before choosing this option.\n\n        h. commands a-k are self explanatory. NOTE that you cannot change the\n                    accounts number of Days Remaining at this time.\n\n        ------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nACCOUNT UPDATE LOGIC:\n\n        1) If the account is active and there is megabytes purchased then the\n           program will subtract the number of megabytes downloaded from the\n           express account and add it to the number of megabytes used for the\n           ACCOUNTANT.\n\n           ie:\n\n           ACCOUNTANT: ByteMaster purchased 10 Meg\n\n           EXPRESS: ByteMaster has downloaded 15 Meg\n\n           ACCOUNTANT: Adds 10 Megs to the amount used and subtracts\n                       10 Megs from the EXPRESS download bytes for that account.\n\n        2) If the account has purchased a certain number of days, then the\n           accountant will display the number of 24Hours remaining for that\n           account. Keep in mind that the program will not delete EXPRESS\n           accounts and it will not make an ACCOUNTANT account INACTIVE, this is\n           true even if the user goes over the number of days purchased.\n\n        3) The ACCOUNTANT account is saved.\n\n\nRECOMMENDATIONS:\n\n    It is recommended that this door be invoked via an MCI ~CC command from \na Bull.txt. Keep in mind that the accounts only auto update when the user\nenters the door.\n\n\nWell that''s about it, if there is any problems you know how to get in touch\nwith me,. This door is v1.0 so I am sure there will be alot of modifications\nto it once I get some feedback.. Currently I can see the following needs\nadded:\n\n  1) ASCII list of accounts feature.\n  2) Auto Account Delete\n  3) Statistics utility for the ACCOUNTANT\n\n\nWell like I said I am open to suggestions, with your feedback this could turn\nout to be a very nice and much needed door. \n\n\nByteMaster - Light Speed Technologies, ByteMaster''s BBS,/X WHQ(PD) 703-639-6114\n\n                                                                                  ','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',25849,5,0,NULL,NULL,'acct10','scan',1780048365);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('acd_acde','ACD-ACDE.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ACD-ACDE.LHA','AccessDenied','XIM','AccessDenied',NULL,NULL,'ACD','/.\  / _   / _   / ___/  ___/  ___/ / | \/  |__/  |__/  ___\___  \___ \ /  _  \  |  \  |  \     /  |  /  |  \',replace('      _    _____________________________\n     /.\  / _   / _   / ___/  ___/  ___/\n    / | \/  |__/  |__/  ___\___  \___ \ \n   /  _  \  |  \  |  \     /  |  /  |  \\n  (___|   \_____\_____\____\_____\_____/\n   <--`----\ ----- D E N I E D ----->[pF]\n::::::::::::::::: PrEsEnTs :::::::::::::::::\n............ AcCeSs DeNiEd V0.9b ...........\n A Usefull EnCryption/De WoRks On DMS / LHA\n      And All Other Dos Type Files ','\n',char(10)),'AccessDenied.Guide',replace('@database "Access Denied V0.9ß"\n@AUTHOR "Exile - Pink Floyd"\n@(C) "Access Denied"\n@Ver$ "Access Denied V0.9ß    \n@HEIGHT 30\n@Node MAIN "Access Denied"\n                                                                  \n       .:::::::. .:::::::. .:::::::. ::::::::: .:::::::. .:::::::.\n       ::::::::: ::::::::: ::::::::: ::::::::: ::::::::: :::::::::\n       :::: :::: ::::  ::: ::::  ::: ::::      ::::      ::::     \n       ::::::::: ::::      ::::      :::::::    ·:::::.   ·:::::. \n       :::: :::: ::::  ::: ::::  ::: ::::            :::       :::\n       :::: :::: ::::::::: ::::::::: ::::::::: ::::::::: :::::::::\n       :::: :::: ·:::::::· ·:::::::· ::::::::: ·:::::::· ·:::::::·\n                                                                  \n       :::::::.  ::::::::: :::  :::: ::::::::: ::::::::: :::::::. \n       ::::::::: ::::::::: :::: :::: ::::::::: ::::::::: :::::::::\n       :::: :::: ::::      :::::::::   :::::   ::::      :::: ::::\n       :::: :::: :::::::   :::::::::   :::::   :::::::   :::: ::::\n       :::: :::: ::::      :::::::::   :::::   ::::      :::: ::::\n       ::::::::: ::::::::: :::: :::: ::::::::: ::::::::: :::::::::\n       ::::::::· ::::::::: ::::  ::: ::::::::: ::::::::: ::::::::·\n             _ __ ___ ________________________________ __ _ _\n                     Y    .--------------------.\n                     :    |   @{"  Disclaimer  " link "Disc"}  |\n.                    .    :   @{" Requirements " link "Req"}  : \n..                   .    :   @{" Installation " link "Inst"}  :   \n....                      .   @{" How it works " link "What"}  .\n.............             `--------------------''\n..................\n..........................\n.............................................................................\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "Disc"\n@toc "Disc"\n\n                              What is it ???\n Well this is the first version of Access Denied which basically is a small\n Encryption Program\n\n WARNING - DO NOT LOSE YA PASSWORDS AS IF YOU DECRYPT A FILE WITH THE WRONG\n           PASSWORDS THE FILE WILL THEN ENCRYPT ITSELF AGAIN WITH THE NEW\n           PASSWORDS AND THE OLD SO FILE WILL BE ENCRYPTED TWICE !!!!!!!!!\n\n\n                             @{" Main Menu " link "MAIN"}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "Req" "Requirements"\n@toc "Req"\n\n               Any Amiga (600,1200,3000,4000,4000T,5000(?)....\n\n                            @{" BACK TO MAIN MENU? " link "MAIN"}\n\n@endnode\n@node "Inst" "Installation - "\n@toc "Inst"\n                         \n                           HAHA What Installation.\n\n                            @{" BACK TO MAIN MENU? " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n@node "What" "---> What it does: <---"\n@toc "What"\n\n    This File Encryption Program Has Been Tested on DMS / LHA files aswell\n    as ordinary dos files with no Crashes or corruptions to date ,\n    We take no responsibilty with Loss of data or damage caused by use\n    or misuse of this Program  YOU HAVE BEEN WARNED !!!!!\n               \n < 1 >  Select File - No Explaination Needed\n\n < 2 >  Enter Passwords - Enter Two Passwords Pressing Return On Each Line\n        N.B   Must Be 6 Characters NO MORE NO LESS\n\n < 3 >  Encrypt / Decrypt - Now you have entered your passwords click this\n        gadget to Encrypt the file , The file will be save in the same \n        place as the Selected file but the new file will have the Extension\n        .EPF this is so as not to confuse you in what files have been done.\n\n < 4 >  Follow The same Procedure to Decrypt the file but any extensions\n        like .DMS .LHA will not be returned to the file ( This May be\n        cured in the next release of this program ). \n  \n < 5 >  The EXE button is still in progress if this program is used will\n        try to finish the EXE part in the next version \n \n                            @{" CLICK ME PLEASE !" link "CallNow"}\n@endnode\n@node "CallNow" "CallNow....."\n@toc "CallNow"\n\n        . \n        :                                                  \n        | \n   _ __ ________________________________________________________\n        \_________     /       /       /       /       /       /\\n        |\__/    /    /  _____/  _____/  _____/  _    /  _    / / \n        .  /   __    /  /\___/  /\___/       /\   \  /\   \  / /          \n        . /    /    /  /_/__/  /_/__/  _____/  \_  \/  \_  \/ /   \n         /    /    /       /       /       /       /       /\/          \n        /____/____/_______/_______/_______/_______/_______/ /     \n   __   \____\____\_______\_______\_______\_______\_______\/       __\n  /\_\                                                            /_/\\n  \/_/~°¤~°¤~°¤~°¤ dA SySoP GeEzEr Is PiNk FlOyD! ~°¤~°¤~°¤~°¤~°¤~\_\/\n   _______________________________________________________        __   __\n   \____       \         \       /  \    \       \        \      / /\ / /\\n    \__/        \   _____/      /   /___ /   ____/         \    / / // / /\n-[pF]-/    /    /       /          /    /       /     /    /\  / / // / /\n     /    /    /   ____/          /    /   ____/     /    / / /_/ //_/ /\n    /         /       /    /     /    /       /          / / _\_\/_\_\/\n   /_________/\______/\___/_____/____/\______/\_________/ / /_/\ /_/\\n   \_________\/\_____\/\__\_____\____\/\_____\/\________\/  \_\/ \_\/\n  +----------------------------------------------------------+\n  | dA TeAm CoNsIsTs Of »»«« SqUeAkY - MiNi MaStEr - BiGnOsE |\n  +----------------------------------------------------------+                                                                       \n  >>>                                                           <<<\n            DoOdS CaLl DiS BbS oN +44 (0)1 843 AsK ElItE\n\n                                 @{" ATDT ! " link "MAIN"}\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',11479,4,0,NULL,NULL,'acd_acde','scan',1780048365);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('aclea15','ACLEA15.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ACLEA15.LHA','AEClean','XIM','AEClean','1.5',NULL,NULL,NULL,replace('AEClean v1.5  WB2.0 ONLY!\n','\n',char(10)),'AEClean.doc',replace('                    _____ ______________________________\n                    \\   \\\_____//\__/\\_\\ __ //\____/\n---------/\---------// /\ // /_/ \\ \  // // __// /_/---------/\-------------\n---------\/--------// /_/// /_____\\ \// //  \// /___---------\/-------------\n                   \\/___\\____//___\//_//_/\_\\____/                Nameless\n\n \n                  - -- ---=*)> PRESENTS: <(*=--- -- -\n \n                   *** AEClean v1.5  WB2.0 ONLY! ***\n\n       AmiExpress Utility to help U ''cleanup'' inactive accounts\n\n\nThis little utility will allow you to list all your inactive accounts\nquickly.  If you also select the WARNing and MESSage switches it''ll create\na neatly formatted stdio output which you can redirect to a file and then\npost on your board to alert the ones who are calling that their friends\nmay be loosing their accounts. You can even add it to your logoff script\nto constantly alert users (when they logon that people are about to loose\ntheir accounts because of inactivity).\n\nI originally wrote this program with lots of features to even tell you\nwhat users weren''t uploading... but to do that I also had to read in\nthe BBS:Nodex/Callerslog file and I DIDN''T want to keep a long one of\nthose on my board (well maybe 1 months worth)! so I made this version\nto strictly READ (No writing involved!) your BBS:User.Data file and\nfigure out all the information...\n\nI should mention, this program does NOT delete those accounts, it only\nTELLS YOU that certain users havn''t called in X nr of days. YOU have to\ndelete them when you feel that they'' probably wont ever call back or\nwhatever...\n\nAdditonal feature of v1.1 and up.  If you have an ''AEClean.exclude'' text\nfile with user names of those you wish exclude them from the list, it\nwill, else it wont exclude anyone! Note: this file should be located in\nyour current dir, OR your BBS: directory OR your S: directory. It will\nsearch for the file in that order. Lastly, this new feature renders this\nutility FOR USE WITH WB2.0 ONLY (don''t even try it under 1.3 hehe).\n\n\n                           /========\\n                           ) SYNTAX (\n                           \========/\n\n\nSyntax is as follows:\n\n   AEClean <days> [WARN] [MESS] [NOANSI] [NONRS] [NODAYS] [CLS] [DEL=x]\n\nWhere:\n\n<days> is a MANDATORY number which represents the number of days back in\n       time to find out who hasn''t called. Without the nr you just get help.\n\n            -< OPTIONAL SWITCHES ON/OFF >-\n\n[CLS]    turns ON the issuing of a screen clear at start of output\n[WARN]   turns ON the warning borders\n[NONRS]  turns OFF the numbers before the users names\n[NOANSI] turns OFF ANSI colors for warning & message\n[NODAYS] turns OFF the printing of UserX ''hasnt called in X days'' text\n[MESS]   turns ON a text message for easy AE message creation\n\n[DEL=x]  Changes default message to indicate you''ll delete user after x days\n         instead of the <days>/2 normally printed (only when MESS swich is on)\n\nNote: The MESSage switch will print a message which will warn the users\n      that you''ll delete them after 1/2 the value of days passes. I did\n      this cause I wanted it that way for my board! I issue a 60 day\n      warning and then delete them after 90 days!\n\nTo redirect output to file use ''>''. Ie.. AEClean >ram:test 30 WARN MESS\n\n\n                         /============\\n                         ) SAMPLE USE (\n                         \============/\n\n\nAt any Shell/Cli type:  AEClean 60 WARN MESS\n\nWill probably give you an output that looks something like this...\n\n +--------------------------------------------------------------------+ \n       WARNING     WARNING     WARNING     WARNING     WARNING \n +--------------------------------------------------------------------+ \n   The following users have failed to call the BBS in over 60\n   days and will be deleted from the board after another 30 days\n   of inactivity. Please mention it to them if you know them.\n\n       (1) Blue hasn''t called in 79 days\n       (2) John hasn''t called in 73 days\n       (3) Snake hasn''t called in 72 days\n       (4) Phantom hasn''t called in 60 days\n +--------------------------------------------------------------------+ \n       WARNING     WARNING     WARNING     WARNING     WARNING \n +--------------------------------------------------------------------+ \n\nNOTICE!!! Version 1.4 and up now sorts output by showing WORST CALLERS\nFIRST... thanx to the guy who suggested this, I forgot you''re handle\nit''s been so long since ya called my board ... hehehe....\n\nTo get the names without anything else, you can enter the following:\n\n  AEClean 60 NONRS NODAYS\n\nand your output for the above data should look something like this:\n\n       Blue\n       John\n       Snake\n       Phantom\n\nOf course, you can always type: ''AEClean'' by itself for help with syntax.\n\n\n                /==================================\\n                ) SAMPLE USE (AS A LOGON BULLETIN) (\n                \==================================/\n\nInsert this line in your logoff script...\n\n  AEClean >BBS:Bull.txt 60 WARN MESS CLS\n\n\n\n                        /==================\\n                        ) REVISION HISTORY (\n                        \==================/\n\n    v1.0 => 06-May-92 - INITIAL RELEASE\n\n    v1.1 => 23-May-92\n          - Previous version DID NOT check to see if the account was inactive,\n            therefore it would always list old accounts active or not (at\n            least until it was overwritten by a new user). Ooops. Bug fixed!\n          - If a user called and did not completely log on, the user.data file\n            will store all his info but will not update the LAST CALLED date,\n            therefore these users would have showed up as ''... hasn''t called\n            in 8000+ days'' (since the date variable is 0 it counts all the days\n            since 01-01-70 and echos this number). NOW these users will show\n            up as "... has an incomplete account" (unless the NODAYS option is\n            used).\n          - Added an option to exclude certain users via. a ''AEClean.exclude''\n            file. Type only 1 name per line, Currently AEClean will look in\n            your current dir, then your BBS: dir then your S: directory for\n            this file - if it doesn''t find it it will continue on (thinking\n            you dont want to exclude anyone).\n          - Added a ''NONE - All users in good standing!'' output for cases\n            where ALL users had called within the nr of days. \n          - Reduced size of code by 10%.\n\n    v1.2 => 04-Jul-92\n          - Added the CLS option to allow faster operation when used as a\n            bulletin [cause it clears screen first and doesn''t have to resort\n            to scrolling the display...]\n\n    v1.3 => 02-Aug-92\n          - Had some illegal memory accesses'' DAMN - thanx to the enforcer,\n            I managed to eliminate ''em all...\n          - Minor touchups: added version string, changed group name (again),\n            disabled ctrl-c handling, reformated source code...\n\n    v1.4 => 10-Nov-92\n          - Recompiled with SAS-C v6.0\n          - Now sorts the output by the WORST to BEST callers (ie.. The guy\n            who hasn''t called in 100 days would be shown first, 99 next etc..\n          - Added DEL=x (note: no spaces) to override default message and\n            indicate you''ll delete user after x number of days instead...\n          - Fixed date algorithm to prevent huge numbers if you got a user who\n            might be calling from far into the future (hehe) Thanx ''Saxon of\n            Shining 8'' for pointing that out to me... The problem was I was\n            using the user with the most recent date in the user.data file\n            as todays date instead of calculating it from the system date...\n\n    v1.5 => 11-Nov-92\n          - Wooops, my date function was listing users + 1 day from input\n            and off by a few hours (big deal huh), well - thought I''d fix\n            it since it was a quickie... hehe\n\n               \n                        /==============\\n                        ) RELEASE INFO (\n                        \==============/\n\nLastly, I am running this under workbench v2.1  AND I KNOW IT WON''T WORK\nunder WB1.3. For more info, requests, the latest warez, etc... call my\nboard - Snarfs Pub (407) 267-8155.......\n\nLater, Nameless\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',12146,5,0,NULL,NULL,'aclea15','scan',1780048365);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('acp_sr10','ACP-SR10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ACP-SR10.LHA','ACP-Strip','XIM','ACP-Strip',NULL,NULL,'ACP',NULL,replace('ACP-Strip 1.0 - Fast Logfile Stripper\n\n','\n',char(10)),'ACP-Strip.doc',replace('\n      __\n     ///  ACP-Strip 1.0\n__  ///   (C)opyright by ACP-Developement 1/95\n\\\///  \n \XX/     Public Domain\n\n1. Preface\n\nACP-Strip is public domain, meaning that you can use and spread the\nprogram as long the archive contents stay unchanged. \nArchive contents must be:\n\n ACP-Strip                     10940 Bytes\n ACP-Strip.c                    2088 Bytes\n ACP-Strip.doc                  1873 Bytes\n\nMinimum archive size must be    9102 Bytes\n\nYou are using ACP-Strip on your own risk. I cannot be held responsible\nfor any damage caused by ACP-Strip. This includes system crashes, bugs\nin the program or this documentation.\n\n2. The purpose of this program...\n\n...is to strip logiles, or even other textfiles.\n\nACP-Strip has one special feature: It won''t cut the lines in the middle, so\nthe stripped length will never reach the User-input exactly.\n\n3. Installation:\n\nSimply copy ACP-Strip to C:, or somewhere else you like.\n\n4. How to use:\n\nStart ACP-Strip without without any options, it''s selfexplaining.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nACP-Strip V1.0  (C)1995 by ACP-Development\n\nUsage: ACP-Strip <filename> <length>\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nFurther you can use ACP-Strip with Cron-Programs like Event! or TPTCron.\n\n5. Bugs\n\nNone known.\n\n6. History\n\n 0.1-0.9  Internal Revisions\n     1.0  First Public Release\n\n7. Authors\n\nACP-Strip was written by Michael Gredenberg and the Docfile was written by\nPeter Augustin. Design & Betatestting also done by Peter Augustin.\nThanx are going out to the readers of AMIGA.AUS ;)\n\nContact the ACP-Developent at:\n\nP.O.Box 98\n1097 Vienna\n\nor send a netmail to:\n\nMichael Gredenberg       FaaastLane BBS\n2:310/72.13@fidonet      +43 1 876-1-678 \n39:23/5.1@amiganet       v32.bis 14400bps\n\nPeter Augustin           Amiga Crackpoint\n2:310/72.88@fidonet      +43 2252 46519 USR V.34\n39:23/5@amiganet         +43 2252 82615 ISDN 64k\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',11222,4,0,NULL,NULL,'acp_sr10','scan',1780048365);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('acp_st10','ACP-ST10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ACP-ST10.LHA','ACP-Strip','XIM','ACP-Strip',NULL,NULL,'ACP',NULL,replace('ACP-Strip 1.0 - Fast Logfile Stripper\n\n','\n',char(10)),'ACP-Strip.doc',replace('\n      __\n     ///  ACP-Strip 1.0\n__  ///   (C)opyright by ACP-Developement 1/95\n\\\///  \n \XX/     Public Domain\n\n1. Preface\n\nACP-Strip is public domain, meaning that you can use and spread the\nprogram as long the archive contents stay unchanged. \nArchive contents must be:\n\n ACP-Strip                     10940 Bytes\n ACP-Strip.c                    2088 Bytes\n ACP-Strip.doc                  1873 Bytes\n\nMinimum archive size must be    9102 Bytes\n\nYou are using ACP-Strip on your own risk. I cannot be held responsible\nfor any damage caused by ACP-Strip. This includes system crashes, bugs\nin the program or this documentation.\n\n2. The purpose of this program...\n\n...is to strip logiles, or even other textfiles.\n\nACP-Strip has one special feature: It won''t cut the lines in the middle, so\nthe stripped length will never reach the User-input exactly.\n\n3. Installation:\n\nSimply copy ACP-Strip to C:, or somewhere else you like.\n\n4. How to use:\n\nStart ACP-Strip without without any options, it''s selfexplaining.\n\n--------------------------------------------------\nACP-Strip V1.0  (C)1995 by ACP-Development\n\nUsage: ACP-Strip <filename> <length>\n--------------------------------------------------\n\nFurther you can use ACP-Strip with Cron-Programs like Event! or TPTCron.\n\n5. Bugs\n\nNone known.\n\n6. History\n\n 0.1-0.9  Internal Revisions\n     1.0  First Public Release\n\n7. Authors\n\nACP-Strip was written by Michael Gredenberg and the Docfile was written by\nPeter Augustin. Design & Betatestting also done by Peter Augustin.\nThanx are going out to the readers of AMIGA.AUS ;)\n\nContact the ACP-Developent at:\n\nP.O.Box 98\n1097 Vienna\n\nor send a netmail to:\n\nMichael Gredenberg       FaaastLane BBS\n2:310/72.13@fidonet      +43 1 876-1-678 \n39:23/5.1@amiganet       v32.bis 14400bps\n\nPeter Augustin           Amiga Crackpoint\n2:310/72.88@fidonet      +43 2252 46519 USR V.34\n39:23/5@amiganet         +43 2252 82615 ISDN 64k\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',12751,5,0,NULL,NULL,'acp_st10','scan',1780048365);
