hael Gredenberg       FaaastLane BBS\n2:310/72.13@fidonet      +43 1 876-1-678 \n39:23/5.1@amiganet       v32.bis 14400bps\n\nPeter Augustin           Amiga Crackpoint\n2:310/72.88@fidonet      +43 2252 46519 USR V.34\n39:23/5@amiganet         +43 2252 82615 ISDN 64k\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,2592,2,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048365);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('acs_br40','ACS-BR40.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ACS-BR40.LHA',NULL,'XIM','Baudrate.EXE',NULL,NULL,'ACS','|  /   \     /     /  ___/  ____/ _____/ | | /  :_ \ \_/\  \_/\  __/\____  \____  \ | _/   _/  \_\  \_ \  \_:   \_ :   \_ :   \_',replace('.---_/\_____/\____/\____/\_____/\_____/\-.\n|  /   \     /     /  ___/  ____/ _____/ |\n| /  :_ \ \_/\  \_/\  __/\____  \____  \ |\n_/   _/  \_\  \_ \  \_:   \_ :   \_ :   \_\n\    |    /    /     /     /      /   M@!/\n|\___|___/____/_____/_____/______/______/|\n| <-- - -->> DaniSh DIviSi@n <<-- - -->  |\n`----------------------------------------''\n|->>Accumilated BaudRate Control  V4.0<<-|\n|   Counting All your Callers Baudrate   |\n|       NEW UPDATE, NEW FEATURES!!       |\nO--------------------------->Tuff Brain<-O\n','\n',char(10)),'Baudrate.doc',replace('			Accumilated BaudRate Control  V4.0\n			----------------------------------\n\n\nWelcome to Accumilated Baudrate Control (ABC)    -> NEW UPDATE!!!! <-\n\nWith this little utils you can se how many of your callers are running ex. with \na 2400 baud modem. \n\nThe program inclose thise baud rate connection:\n\n300\n600\n1200\n2400\n4800\n7200\n9600\n12200\n14400\n16800\n19200\n21600\n24000\n26400\n28800\n\nYou can also se, when a last callers has called with the baud rate. \n(A date will be displayed for each baud rate)\n\n\nHOW TO INSTALL:\n---------------\n\nTo install this program, you MUST make a dir called BAUDRATE in you DOORS \ndirectory.\n\nAn example:\n\nMakedir doors:BAUDRATE\n\nAfter that, you must copy BAUDRATE.EXE and BAUDRATE.CFG file to doors:Baudrate/\n\nAfter that, you have to edit the BAUDRATE.CFG file to adjust the Patch for\nBulletins. (Default is BBS:NORMAL/BULLETINS/BULL21.TXT.GR), and then \ntype YES for show the list to all the users, or NO for no list to the \nusers.\n\nIf you don''t wanna have the program to make a bulletins, then\njust DELETE the BAUDRATE.CFG file!!!! (If you delete the BAUDRATE.CFG file,\nthe list will be displayed for each user who log''s on.)\n\nThere is a lot of alternative how to run this /X utils. My suggestion is\nyou use the FRONTEND.INFO file and copy it from this LHA packet to your \nBBS:commands/syscmd directory!!!\n\n\nHOW TO RESET THE PROGRAM\n------------------------\n\nWhen you want to Reset the data in this program, you have to delete the file\ncalled BAUDRATE.DATA in your doors:baudrate Dir.\n\nAfter you have deleted the BAUDRATE.DATA file, and the next user log''s on,\nthen the program will write LAST RESET: XX/XX/XX (after what the date is that\nday)\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\nBugs report and new ideas are welcome....\n\nNOTE: IF you are having problems install this program, you can give me \na call. Look at the bottum for futher informations!!!!!\n\n> Tuff Brain / A((E$$ <\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n\nO----------------------------------------------------------------------------O\n|                 ___             ___     ___  ___  ___                      |\n|                /__/ /  / /\/\  /__/    /__/ /__/ /__                       | \n|               /    /__/ /   / /  /    /__/ /__/ ___/  Member Of A((E$$ DK  |\n|                                                                            |\n|		           PHONE +45 43 54 06 64                             |\n|                                                                            |\n| RUNNING /X 3.36, USRobotics 28K8 Dual Standard, 950 MB Quantum HD,         |\n| Open 24 hrs.                                                               |\n|                                                                            |\n|                            SYSop: Tuff Brain                               |\nO----------------------------------------------------------------------------O\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',91378,7,0,NULL,NULL,'acs_br40','scan',1780048365);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('acs_comp','ACS-COMP.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ACS-COMP.LHA','Compressor','XIM','Compressor',NULL,NULL,'ACS','.__|     |     |     |  ___|     |     |__. |  |  |  |  |__|  |__|  _/_|  `--|  `--|  |2 |  |  .  |  l  |  l  |  l  |--,  |--,  |  |F',replace('   ._____._____._____._____._____._____.\n.__|     |     |     |  ___|     |     |__.\n|  |  |  |  |__|  |__|  _/_|  `--|  `--|  |2\n|  |  .  |  l  |  l  |  l  |--,  |--,  |  |F\n`--l__|  l__   l__   l__   l__   l__   |--''\n      `--''  `--''  `--''  `--''  `--''  `--''\n  FileList Compressor v1.0 ©1995 WiZE/aCCESs\n  ------------------------------------------\n  Strip Your FileLists - Speed Up Your Duper\n\n','\n',char(10)),'Compressor.Doc',replace('---====================================================================---\n  FileList Compressor Version 1.0 Coded By : WiZE^Access     15-FEB-1995\n---====================================================================---\n\n\nBoth this program and its source are freely distributable, but remain Copyright\n                                    \n                           (c) Wize/Access 1995.\n\n\n---==========================================================================---\n\n\nIntroduction\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n     Ever wanted to boost up your DupeChecker? Then this util might be\n\n      your solution. It strips all the date and description from the\n\n          /X FileLists into a file that contains only FileNames.\n\n\n\n   FileList Compressor v1.0 is a 100% C program, for maximum efficiency.\n\n\nSystem Requirements\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n        A500(+), A600, A1200, A2000, A2500, A3000, A4000\n                       With KickStart 2.0 or higher.\n\n         (tested on A4000 25MHz and 6MB of RAM and KICKSTART 40.55\n                              -> works fine)\n\n            (tested on A2000 G-Force 40MHz and 8 MB 32 Bit RAM\n                              -> works fine)\n\n          (tested on A2000 1MB RAM no accelerator with KICK 2.05\n                              -> works fine)\n\n           (tested on A 500 3MB RAM with KICK 1.3 and KICK 2.05\n                              -> works fine)\n\n\n\nUsage from the Shell\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nPROMPT> Compressor (executable 4900 bytes) FileList OutPutFile\n\n\nEXAMPLE: Compressor bbs:amiga/dir1 ram:New.dir1\n\n\n\nFuture improvements\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n                            Mainly more speed.\n\n\nNote :\n~~~~~~\n\nThese improvements will mostly depend on the needs of Compressor users.\n\n\n\nAuthor:\n~~~~~~~\n\nComments, suggestions, bug reports, flames, gifts, postbombs, etc...\nare welcome.\n\n\n                                 WiZE/aCS\n\ncontact:\n                           cLASH oF tHE cHAMPONS\n\n                         NODE 1 ++46 854 086 9 28\n                         NODE 2 ++46 854 061 3 85\n\n\n\nFileList Compressorwas written with:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n	SAS/C v6.50\n\n\n\nLicense\n~~~~~~~\n\n        Compressor v1.0 and (hereinafter "Files") and their related\ndocumentation, utilities and examples (c) Copyright 1995 ACCESS All Rights\n                                 Reserved.\n\nThese Files and their related documentation, utilities and examples are\n                                 provided\n\n                                  "AS-IS"\n\n       and subject to change without notice; no warranties are made.\n\n\n                       All use is at your own risk.\n                No liability or responsibility is assumed.\n\n\nSpecific Files from the archive may be reproduced and distributed separately\n       under license subject to agreement with the following terms:\n\n\n1.   The Files may be reproduced but may not be modified in any way.\n\n2.   The Files may only be distributed as an integral part of a software\n     product solely for Commodore Amiga computers.\n\n3.   The related documentation, utilities, and examples provided by\n     ACCESS may not be reproduced or distributed, in whole or in part,\n     except as part of a complete and unmodified archive as provided by\n     ACCESS.\n\n4.   Licensee shall hold ACCESS harmless from any and all claims, damages\n     and liabilities resulting from or arising out of its use or distribution\n     of the Files.\n\n5.   All copies of ACCESS`s software product containing the Files and\n     of ACCESS`s product documentation related there to must include\n     the following copyright notice:\n\n\nThese Files and their related documentation, utilities and examples are provided\n\n\n6.   Such technical information as is contained in the Files (and any\n     product thereof) or in the related documentation, utilities, and\n     examples may not be exported in contravention of the laws and\n     regulations of Sweden.\n\n7.   ACCESS may terminate this license at any time, with or without cause.\n     This license hereunder will automatically terminate upon any breach\n     of these terms and conditions.  Upon any such termination,\n     ACCESS shall destroy all copies of the Files and the related\n     documentation, utilities, and examples in its possession.\n\n\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',5473,2,0,NULL,NULL,'acs_comp','scan',1780048365);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('acs_frt','ACS-FRT.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ACS-FRT.LHA','NewFront','XIM','._____._____._____._____._____._____.',NULL,NULL,'ACS','.__|     |     |     |  ___|     |     |__. |  |  |  |  |__|  |__|  _/_|  `--|  `--|  |2 |  |  .  |  l  |  l  |  l  |--,  |--,  |  |F',replace('   ._____._____._____._____._____._____.\n.__|     |     |     |  ___|     |     |__.\n|  |  |  |  |__|  |__|  _/_|  `--|  `--|  |2\n|  |  .  |  l  |  l  |  l  |--,  |--,  |  |F\n`--l__|  l__   l__   l__   l__   l__   |--''\n      `--''  `--''  `--''  `--''  `--''  `--''\n      NewFront v1.0 ©1995 WiZE/aCCESs\n  ----------------------------------------\n      A plain and simple FrontEnd door\n\n','\n',char(10)),'NewFront.Doc',replace('---====================================================================---\n       NewFront Version v1.0 Coded By : WiZE^Access     15-FEB-1995\n---====================================================================---\n\n\nBoth this program and its source are freely distributable, but remain Copyright\n                                    \n                           (c) Wize/Access 1995.\n\n\n---==========================================================================---\n\n\nIntroduction\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n First this program is made for use with AmiExpress Bulletin Board System.\n\n       NewFront is a simple and nice looking FrontEnd door for /X 3+\n\n\n         NewFront 1.0 is a 100% C program, for maximum efficiency.\n\n\nSystem Requirements\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n        A500(+), A600, A1200, A2000, A2500, A3000, A4000\n                       With KickStart 2.0 or higher.\n\n         (tested on A4000 25MHz and 6MB of RAM and KICKSTART 40.55\n                              -> works fine)\n\n            (tested on A2000 G-Force 40MHz and 8 MB 32 Bit RAM\n                              -> works fine)\n\n          (tested on A2000 1MB RAM no accelerator with KICK 2.05\n                              -> works fine)\n\n           (tested on A 500 3MB RAM with KICK 1.3 and KICK 2.05\n                              -> works fine)\n\n\nInstallation\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nFor use with /X:\n\nIn the archive is an /X-example included\n\n Copy all file`s from the archive ` BBS: ` to your BBS: (DIR)\n\n\n\nFuture improvements\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n                               None planed.\n\n\n\nNote :\n~~~~~~\n\nimprovements will mostly depend on the needs of NewFront users.\n\n\n\nAuthor:\n~~~~~~~\n\nComments, suggestions, bug reports, flames, gifts, postbombs, etc...\nare welcome.\n\n\n                                 WiZE/aCS\n\ncontact:\n                           cLASH oF tHE cHAMPONS\n\n                         NODE 1 ++46 854 086 9 28\n                         NODE 2 ++46 854 061 3 85\n\n\n\nNewFront v1.0 was written with:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n	SAS/C v6.50\n\n\n\nLicense\n~~~~~~~\n\n         NewFront v1.0 and (hereinafter "Files") and their related\ndocumentation, utilities and examples (c) Copyright 1995 ACCESS All Rights\n                                 Reserved.\n\nThese Files and their related documentation, utilities and examples are\n                                 provided\n\n                                  "AS-IS"\n\n       and subject to change without notice; no warranties are made.\n\n\n                       All use is at your own risk.\n                No liability or responsibility is assumed.\n\n\nSpecific Files from the archive may be reproduced and distributed separately\n       under license subject to agreement with the following terms:\n\n\n1.   The Files may be reproduced but may not be modified in any way.\n\n2.   The Files may only be distributed as an integral part of a software\n     product solely for Commodore Amiga computers.\n\n3.   The related documentation, utilities, and examples provided by\n     ACCESS may not be reproduced or distributed, in whole or in part,\n     except as part of a complete and unmodified archive as provided by\n     ACCESS.\n\n4.   Licensee shall hold ACCESS harmless from any and all claims, damages\n     and liabilities resulting from or arising out of its use or distribution\n     of the Files.\n\n5.   All copies of ACCESS`s software product containing the Files and\n     of ACCESS`s product documentation related there to must include\n     the following copyright notice:\n\n\nThese Files and their related documentation, utilities and examples are provided\n\n\n6.   Such technical information as is contained in the Files (and any\n     product thereof) or in the related documentation, utilities, and\n     examples may not be exported in contravention of the laws and\n     regulations of Sweden.\n\n7.   ACCESS may terminate this license at any time, with or without cause.\n     This license hereunder will automatically terminate upon any breach\n     of these terms and conditions.  Upon any such termination,\n     ACCESS shall destroy all copies of the Files and the related\n     documentation, utilities, and examples in its possession.\n\n\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,7551,2,0,NULL,NULL,'acs_frt_newfront','scan',1780048365);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('acs_hack','ACS_HACK.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ACS_HACK.LHA','Ami-Hacker','XIM','Ami-Hacker',NULL,'Cray-1','ACS','/ _  |  .  |  .  |  ___|  ___)  ___) / __  |  |--|  |--|  _)_|___  |___  | _/  `|  |  ''  |  ''  |  `  |  `  |  `  |',replace('      __________________________________    \n     / _  |  .  |  .  |  ___|  ___)  ___)   \n    / __  |  |--|  |--|  _)_|___  |___  |   \n  _/  `|  |  ''  |  ''  |  `  |  `  |  `  |   \n  `----`--`-----`-----`-----`-----`-----''®  \n:-::::::::::::::BRiNGS:YA!:::::::::kKiD::-: \n\n       AMI-EXPRESS --- PASSWORD HACKER\n       ===============================\n  Hacks Out PassWords From User.data ,Unix\n   Style. Works On ALL Currently Used /X\n    Versions. Written in ASM By Cray-1\n','\n',char(10)),'Hacker.Guide',replace('@DATABASE "Default"\n@NODE "MAIN" "Main Help Menu."\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\n                  @{"-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-="}	 __________________________________  \n                  @{"       What Is It?      " LINK "1"}      / _  |  .  |  .  |  ___|  ___)  ___)   \n                  @{"      Installation      " LINK "2"}     / __  |  |--|  |--|  _)_|___  |___  |\n                  @{"-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-="}   _/  `|  |  ''  |  ''  |  `  |  `  |  `  |\n                  @{"     Dictionary File    " LINK "DICT"}   `----`--`-----`-----`-----`-----`-----''® \n                  @{"     Users      File    " LINK "USERS"}       Ami-Express Password Hacker V1.0\n                  @{"     Output     File    " LINK "OUTPUT"}      ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n                  @{"-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-="}             By Cray-1 of A((eSS\n                  @{"       Bench Marks      " LINK "SPEED"}\n                  @{" Technical Information  " LINK "TECH"}        Coming Soon To A BBS Near You...\n                  @{"        SYSOPS!         " LINK "SYSOPS" }\n                  @{"-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-="}\n                  @{"         Bugs           " LINK "BUGS"}                   Dizzer II\n                  @{"-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-="}                   ~~~~~~~~~\n                  @{"      Greetings!        " LINK "Greetings"}\n\n         Call The Edge Of Chaos +44 (0)41 644 5588\n                         A((eSS UK HQ                          \n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "Greetings" "Greetings"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\n                    Greetings Go To The Following:\n                    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n            Sophocles    - Send Me Your Internet Address!\n            Renegade     - Epitaph = "Leave It With Me."\n            Cobra        - Teach me to Crack.! :)\n            AnF!         - Working Hard At Uni.? (I Hope Not!)\n            Sasha        - Send Me Some Funky Tapes Dude!\n            Slash        - Lost Your Address Dude! ;(\n            LSD	         - Hi Guys!\n            Jomas!       - The Turbos Are A GREAT idea!\n            Ex4          - Hope You Guys Aren''t Pissed off About this.\n            Paradox      - Still A Force To Rival With.\n            Silver Fox   - Where Are U Dude?\n            KeyBoard Kid - Where Would We Be With U Guys?          \n            CRS+Crew     - How Are Things?\n            MaG          - Run Out Of Boards To Call Yet?          \n\n            Hi! To EveryOne I Have Forgotten, U Know Who U Are!\n\n         You Can Conntact Me and The Guys At @{"The Edge Of Chaos..." SYSTEM "Eoc.Exe"}\n                 \n                What Out For Dizzer II Coming To A BBS Soon\n                               Near You.\n\n                 It Might Just Be ''Something WonderFUL''.\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "BUGS" "BUGS"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\nBUGS\n~~~~\n\n  Few BUGS as Such. One Might Be That Although, It Checks\n  To See If The FileNames You Have Given It Exist, It \n  Doesn''t Check to See If They Are Valid Files. So Carefull\n  What You Feed it. Sorry About This But For Speed It Was\n  Written In ASM and Checking For Shit Like That is A Hassle\n  And Prob. Would Have Slowed It Down.\n\n This Is The First PUBLIC Release of This Product And Prob. The Last!\n\n      Get In Touch With me To Discuss Suggestions Or Critisisms\n                Source Code Availible On Request.\n\n      My INTERNET Accounts Are Temp. DEAD. but I Can Be Found On\n         The Edge Of Chaos BBS , Or Any Other Elite IN The UK.\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "2" "How Do I Install This?"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\nInstallation\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n   If You Are Reading This Then I Am Not Sure You Are \n   The Sort Of Person That Needs A Password Hacker.\n\n Simply Drag The Icon To The Place You Would Like The \n Program To  Reside  ON Your  HardDisk, (Or Floppy!!)\n And  Double  Click On it To Run It.\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "1" "What Does It Do?"\n@TOC "MAIN"\nFIRSTLY!\n~~~~~~~~\n   My Bad Spelling Is Because Of The Hasty Writting Of This\n   Guide. (I Have No Fancy Guide Writter, However If Someone\n   Has Written A Good One, Please Send Me it! :))\n\n   Right Anyone That Has Hacked out Passwords On A UNIX System\n   can Skip This Part.\n\n   Firstly For All Sysop''s Dont Worry, You Need To Have A Valid\n   USER.DATA File To Do Any Hacking. The Program Takes A Valid\n   Dictionary File Full Of Words, And The User.Data File, And\n   Once Run Tells You Which Users Have Which Passwords, In The\n   Dictionary.\n\n   Simple huh?\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "DICT" "Dictionary File Format."\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\n    The Dictionary File Is A Straight ASCII Dictionary.\n    Words Should  Be Separated From  Each Other  With A \n    CR. \n\n    Dictionarys, Can Be As Large As Your Availible Memory.\n    However The Word Length Of The Dictionary Must be Under\n    256  Characters. I Shouldn''t  Think This  To Be A Major \n    Problem. Since There Are No Words With 256+ Characters!\n\n\n    On A UNIX System, The Place The Dictionary Is Stored is\n                        USR/DICT/WORDS   \n          This Is Public, So Access Should Be Easy.\n\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE "USERS" "The Users File Format."\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\n     Right This is The Triacky One. The Users File is\n     a USER.DATA File From Any Ami-Express BBS. \n     Again It Can Be As Large As Your Memory Allows, Since\n     each user is 232 bytes, you would have to have a lot \n     of users to fill the average memory!\n\n     Getting The USER.DATA File From An Ami-Express BBS Is \n     Fairly Hard. Its Hard-Coded Into Express No To Give The\n     Thing Out. And Trying To Get Your Average Sysop To Part\n     With His is A Challange. Thats Why This Is More User To\n     Sysops Than Users.\n\n   See Also Sysops README!\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "OUTPUT" "The OutPut File Generated"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n          \n   Nothing Special Just Some Passwords.\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "SYSOPS" "Warning! Readme!"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\n    Right Once The Novelty Of Finding Out Your Own Users Passwords\n    Has Worn Off. You Might Start To Think......\n\n            "Shit Someone Might Try To Hack Me Now...."\n\n    The Answer To This is "YES!!!" but, The Answer To This Has\n    Always Been Yes. It Just Takes A Thing Like This To Remind Sysops\n    That They Should Always Be on There Gaurd. Anyone Could Write A \n    Backdoor. The Trouble is Nowadays, The Sportsman ships Outa it.\n    People Dont Just Want To hack They Want To Fuck''n Format!!!!\n\n   I Sure As Hell Would Preffer My Passwords Hacked Out That My BBS\n   LOW-LEVEL  Formatted!  Remember  Passwords Can Be  Changed, Data \n   Cant Be Un-Formatted.\n\n   This Util. Has TWO Distinct Advantages,\n   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n     1) The Lame Backdoor Writters Will Target User.Data, \n        Instead Of Targeting Your HD.\n     2) You Might Actually Notice That Your BBS Is Under Threat.\n\n  As Well As These It Does do Its Job Quite Well, So If  You Happen\n  To "Stumble" Across Someones USER.DATA, You Will Have A Few \n  Passwords in A Few Mins. For Sure.\n\nSYSOPS THAT DONT PROGRAM -- READ THIS!!\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n   Right  Just Quickly To Show You How To Spot A Backdrop In A \n   Lame Door. First the Easy Things, Eg. Check The Size of The\n   File With The Crew That Released It. Stuff Like That.\n\n   Right Run SNOOPDOS!\n\n If You See It Even Touch Your USER.DATA Then Go To The Next Step.\n\n  If It Looks Normal, Then You Might Want To Go Through It With\n  A HEX Editor  Anyway To  Check For  References To USER.DATA, \n  Remember The  File May  Be Crunched  so Un-Chunch It First!!\n\n If It Does Touch The USER.DATA , Even if It Is Something That Is\n Meant To, (eg. An Account Editor ) it Is Worth Dissassembling it.\n\n     Grab A Copy of Resource Or Something. And Dissassemble It. \n  Right Near The Bottom Of The Listing There Should Be A Line Like\n\nlbc00023    dc.b ''bbs:user.data'',0\n\n  or Something, There Should Be A Label, (If Dissassembled In Resource)\n  or you may have to work out the offset from the nearest label.\n \nLook For A Reference To The Label or The Offset From The Previous Label\nIn The Code.\n\nProb. Something Like This\n\n		move.l	#lbc00023,d1\n  Right What You Are Looking For Is This, And Also A Line VERY NEAR,\n  That Says:\n                jsr	-$1E(a6)\n\n		tst	d0	<< or Something Like \n		beq	fail	<<   This\n\n                move.l	d0,SOMEWHERE!!! <This Will Be a Label\n		\n*** The One To Watch Out For Which means They Are Nicking Your,\n    Passwords, Would Be After This .. Something Like This.\n\n                move.l	#SOMEWHERE!!!,a0\n\nLABEL		move.l	100(a0),d0\n		move.l	d0,SOMETHING!!\n		addq	#232,a0\n		bra	LABEL\n\n  Right it will BE Covered Up This Other Stuff Around It. But That \n  is What it will be. The jsr is the open. It Opens The USER.DATA\n  file. The SOMEWHERE!!! is just some label to an address in memory.\n  the line move.l 100(a0),d0 means, MOVE 100 bytes From What is in a0\n  into d0, and The User.Data file is in a0 so 100 bytes from the\n  start of the users file is the password.\n  the addq #232,a0 just means go to the next user.\n\n   If Something Like This is In The Source Code, Then Be Very CareFull\n About Using That Door, Dont Use it until You Have Confirmed its Origin\n    and perhaps ask the authors why it needs to Access The Passwords.\n\nAnymore Help Needed Just Contact me Cray-1 at The Edge of Chaos.\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "TECH" "Technical Information"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\n The Way The Hack Works, Is It Uses That Crypt Routine From\n /X, And Encrypts The Words In The Dictionary, And Compares\n Them Against The Encrypted Password. \n\nIt Intionally Doesnt Print The Passwords Of Deleted Users.\n\nTo 2-Cool Who Originally Wrote The Crypt Routine, Its Good,\nIn Fact The Original Password Can NOT Be Decypted, Because\nData Is Lost In The Crypt Proccess.\n\n Its A Hell Of A Lot More Secure Than Joe Hodges Original \n                     Ascii Passwords!\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "SPEED" "System Bench Marks"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\n    I Havn''t Tested It One Many Systems, but Compared With\n    A Simillar Program For Unix Systems its FAST.\n\n    On My A1200, 68030 Running 40Mhz With 68882 AND 4 \n    Megs of 32 Bit FAST and 4 Megs 16 Bit Fast\n\n    The Hacker Was Able To Do A Dictionary File of 1 Megabyte\n    With A Users File Of 255 Users, in 12 Mins.\n\n    I Think Thats About 3 Seconds Per User.\n\nOf Course This Speed Is Due Mainly To 2-Cool''s Most Exellent\nCrypt Routine That He Did For Joe Hodge.\n@ENDNODE\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',29225,5,0,NULL,NULL,'acs_hack','scan',1780048372);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('acs_ip10','ACS-IP10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ACS-IP10.LHA','telnetd','XIM','telnetd',NULL,'DANSKEN/ACS','ACS','! QUICK DOX - HOWTO SETUP TELNET NODES!    ! +------------------------------------------+ !      LAME RELEASE BY DANSKEN/ACS         !',replace('+------------------------------------------+\n! QUICK DOX - HOWTO SETUP TELNET NODES!    !\n+------------------------------------------+\n!      LAME RELEASE BY DANSKEN/ACS         !\n+------------------------------------------+\n!   THIS IS FOR AMIEXPRESS 3.38+ ONLY!     !\n+------------------------------------------+\n','\n',char(10)),'mastrb8.txt',replace(replace('STILL GOING STRONG in 2014!\r\n\r\n                ___         ._            _______             ·\r\n   /\  _________)  \________| \___________)__   /_________:__ :________\r\n  /  \/\  __  \    ____ ___/|  \______  \_  / _/___  \_ ____/ ¦__ \___ \\r\n /   /  \ \__  \___  \  |   |   \  _/  __/ /    /\__  \  |¦   | /  \_|  \\r\n/  \/    \_ \   \ !   \_|   !    \_\    \_     /   \   \ ||   |·    /|   \_\r\n\___|     ___\  /__    /l________ /_\    /__  /_____\  / |¦   |    /_|    /\r\n    l____/-A×E\/  \___/_!       \/   \  /   \/       \/__|:   ¦__ /  l___/\r\n       ______            _____        \/      :    ____   ·   : \/\r\n    ___)     \___________)    \__________:___ ¦____)   \__________\r\n    \    _______     _______    \___    ____/ |\_____   \______   \\r\n   /\___   \/        |    _)    \/       ¦    |/    |    \    |    \\r\n _/    !    \        |    \      \_      |    |     !     \   |     \\r\n \______     \___    |_____\      /___   |    ¦            \  |      \_\r\n       \______/ \____!      \    /   \___|    :________     \_|       /\r\n                             \  /        ¦    ·       \______/|      /\r\n   YOUVE HEARD ABOUT IT!      \/         :    ·               l_____/\r\n       \r\n         MASTURBATiON STATiON AMIGA/PC/CONSOLE/ASCII-ANSI/C64        \r\n               Telnet: bbs.masturbationstationbbs.com\r\n\r\n           UPLOAD DATE: 09-11-15  TIME: 17:53:25  ON NODE: 2\r\n\r\n  UPLOADER: Black Beard            LOCATION: mASTURBATIONSTATIONBBS.COM\r\n\r\n','\r',char(13)),'\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',26407,2,0,NULL,NULL,'acs_ip10','scan',1780048365);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('acs_lh3','ACS-LH3.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ACS-LH3.LHA','lha','XIM','LhaChecker',NULL,NULL,'ACS','_____ _____ _____ _____ _____ _____ |~   ¬Y~   ¬Y~   ¬Y~ ___Y~   ¬Y~   ¬| |  T  |  T__|  T__|  ___|_ \__|_ \__|',replace('  \n   _____ _____ _____ _____ _____ _____ \n  |~   ¬Y~   ¬Y~   ¬Y~ ___Y~   ¬Y~   ¬|\n  |  T  |  T__|  T__|  ___|_ \__|_ \__|\n  |     |  | ¬|  | ¬|  l  |¬\   |¬\  B|\n  !  !  !  !  !  !  !     !     !    g!\n  ·  ·  :  .  ·  ·  :     :     ·    n:\n  :            Bring''s ya             :\n  -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n     ·» Super LhA Checker v3.0 «·\n \n','\n',char(10)),'LhaCHECKER.Doc',replace('---====================================================================---\n   SUPER_LHA_CHECKER Version 3.0 Coded By : WiZE^Access     28-FEB-1995\n---====================================================================---\n\n\nBoth this program and its source are freely distributable, but remain Copyright\n                                    \n                           (c) Wize/Access 1995.\n\n\n---==========================================================================---\n\n\nIntroduction\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n     First this program is made for use with an Bulletin Board System,\n               but of course you can use it also from Shell.\n\n\n Super_Lha_Checker by WIZE/ACCESS is an Shell-Utility to process all kinds\n                       of LHA LZH LZA RUN archives.\n\n You may Add, Strip comercial''s from/to the archive. And test integrity of\n                                 archive.\n\n                 And that''s not all ... Special features :\n\n                     - ABILITY TO VIEW THE FILE_ID.DIZ\n\n               - ABILITY TO ADD A LINER INTO THE FILE_ID.DIZ\n\n                 - ABILITY TO SET IT''S OWN WORK DIRECTORY\n\n        - ABILITY TO SET A SELECTIVE NUMBER OF KILOBYTES AS BUFFER\n\n        - ABILITY TO TURN ON/OFF THE TESTING, STRIPPING AND ADDING.\n\n           - ABILITY TO EXECUTE A SCRIPT BEFORE EXECUTING ITSELF\n\n                        - ABILITY TO SET LHA''S PATH\n\n\n    Super_Lha_Checker v3.0 is a 100% C program, for maximum efficiency.\n\n\nSystem Requirements\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n        A500(+), A600, A1200, A2000, A2500, A3000, A4000\n                       With KickStart 2.0 or higher.\n\n         (tested on A4000 25MHz and 6MB of RAM and KICKSTART 40.55\n                              -> works fine)\n\n            (tested on A2000 G-Force 40MHz and 8 MB 32 Bit RAM\n                              -> works fine)\n\n          (tested on A2000 1MB RAM no accelerator with KICK 2.05\n                              -> works fine)\n\n           (tested on A 500 3MB RAM with KICK 1.3 and KICK 2.05\n                              -> works fine)\n\n\nInstallation\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nFor use with /X:\n\nIn the archive is an /X-example included\n\n Copy all file`s from the archive ` BBS:FCHECK/ ` to your BBS:FCHECK (DIR)\n        Copy LhaChecker ( executable 5540 bytes ) to your c: (DIR)\n\n\nUsage from the Shell\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nPROMPT> LhaChecker (executable 5540 bytes) Archive\n\n\n\nConfigure C:LhaChecker.Info:\n\n\nADD=YES/NO		- Turn file added on/off.\n\nSTRIP=YES/NO		- Turn file stripping on/off.\n\nCHECK=YES/NO		- Turn archive testing on/off.\n\nWORK=DH0:		- Set your own Work Space. In this case DH0:.\n\nSCRIPT=Scriptfile	- The path+name of the script file to execute\n                          upon execution of lhachecker.\n			  For example Doors:LhaChecker/ISTRIP.batch\n\nFILEID_ADD=             - The line to insert after the description.\n                          i.e:\n                          _________________ _/\_______/\__|\___  /\\n			  \____ \  __\_.  /_\__/___  \__/ / \  \/  \\n			   |  /  \ \ / | /  |  | _/ _/  |/|  \   /  \\n			   | /   /  /  |/   |  | \  \|  | |   \\/    \\n			   |    /\_____|____|  |__\  \__|_____/||    /\n			  :|___/------------|__|---\__/D!-------|___/:\n			  ··   VALHALLA : BEFORE THE WAR! - [1/6]   ··\n          The Tag-Liner ------------------------> [Leeched From COTC!]\n\nBUFFER=64		- The number of I/O KiloBytes to use while testing\n                          the archive. The higher - the faster.\n\nLHA=ram:LhA		- Path to LhA. Usefull if you want it resident. \n                          (if you want resident just make LHA=LhA)\n			  (and then ''Resident c:Lha Pure'' in user-startup)\n\n\nChanges since v2.1:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nThe checker caused a Guru if the config file was not found.  !!FIXED!!\n\nEven if you had set it to CHECK, it didn''t!.  !!FIXED!!\n\nIf the File_ID.Diz didn''t exist, and LhaCheck v2.1 tried to view it, it\nwould have created a empty description.  !!FIXED!!\n\nNew Design (again).  !!ADDED!!\n\nSmoother code made it just about 400bytes larger than before.\nAnd still i have added/changed many things. Should be somewhat quicker now!\n\n\nFuture improvements\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n Random selected files to be inserted, to make it more difficult to strip.\n   Skip the external LhA by Stefan Boberg and make my own LhA routines.\n                      Realtime output in AmiExpress.\n\n\n\nNote :\n~~~~~~\n\nThese improvements will mostly depend on the needs of Lha_Checker users.\n\n\n\nAuthor:\n~~~~~~~\n\nComments, suggestions, bug reports, flames, gifts, postbombs, etc...\nare welcome.\n\n\n                                 WiZE/aCS\n\n                          NODE 1 ++46 854 086 928\n                          NODE 2 ++46 854 061 385\n\n\n\nSuper_Lha_Checker was written with:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n	SAS/C v6.50\n\n\n\nLicense\n~~~~~~~\n\n     Super_Lha_Checker 3.0 and (hereinafter "Files") and their related\ndocumentation, utilities and examples (c) Copyright 1995 ACCESS All Rights\n                                 Reserved.\n\nThese Files and their related documentation, utilities and examples are\n                                 provided\n\n                                  "AS-IS"\n\n       and subject to change without notice; no warranties are made.\n\n\n                       All use is at your own risk.\n                No liability or responsibility is assumed.\n\n\nSpecific Files from the archive may be reproduced and distributed separately\n       under license subject to agreement with the following terms:\n\n\n1.   The Files may be reproduced but may not be modified in any way.\n\n2.   The Files may only be distributed as an integral part of a software\n     product solely for Commodore Amiga computers.\n\n3.   The related documentation, utilities, and examples provided by\n     ACCESS may not be reproduced or distributed, in whole or in part,\n     except as part of a complete and unmodified archive as provided by\n     ACCESS.\n\n4.   Licensee shall hold ACCESS harmless from any and all claims, damages\n     and liabilities resulting from or arising out of its use or distribution\n     of the Files.\n\n5.   All copies of ACCESS`s software product containing the Files and\n     of ACCESS`s product documentation related there to must include\n     the following copyright notice:\n\n\nThese Files and their related documentation, utilities and examples are provided\n\n\n6.   Such technical information as is contained in the Files (and any\n     product thereof) or in the related documentation, utilities, and\n     examples may not be exported in contravention of the laws and\n     regulations of Sweden.\n\n7.   ACCESS may terminate this license at any time, with or without cause.\n     This license hereunder will automatically terminate upon any breach\n     of these terms and conditions.  Upon any such termination,\n     ACCESS shall destroy all copies of the Files and the related\n     documentation, utilities, and examples in its possession.\n\n\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',44620,4,0,NULL,NULL,'acs_lh3','scan',1780048365);
