G AND ADDING.\n\n           - ABILITY TO EXECUTE A SCRIPT BEFORE EXECUTING ITSELF\n\n                        - ABILITY TO SET LHA''S PATH\n\n\n    Super_Lha_Checker v2.1 is a 100% C program, for maximum efficiency.\n\n\nSystem Requirements\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n        A500(+), A600, A1200, A2000, A2500, A3000, A4000\n                       With KickStart 2.0 or higher.\n\n         (tested on A4000 25MHz and 6MB of RAM and KICKSTART 40.55\n                              -> works fine)\n\n            (tested on A2000 G-Force 40MHz and 8 MB 32 Bit RAM\n                              -> works fine)\n\n          (tested on A2000 1MB RAM no accelerator with KICK 2.05\n                              -> works fine)\n\n           (tested on A 500 3MB RAM with KICK 1.3 and KICK 2.05\n                              -> works fine)\n\n\nInstallation\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nFor use with /X:\n\nIn the archive is an /X-example included\n\n Copy all file`s from the archive ` BBS:FCHECK/ ` to your BBS:FCHECK (DIR)\n        Copy LhaChecker ( executable 5104 bytes ) to your c: (DIR)\n\n\nUsage from the Shell\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nPROMPT> LhaChecker (executable 5104 bytes) Archive\n\n\n\nConfigure Doors:LhaChecker/LhaChecker.Info:\n\n\nADD=YES/NO		- Turn file added on/off.\n\nSTRIP=YES/NO		- Turn file stripping on/off.\n\nCHECK=YES/NO		- Turn archive testing on/off.\n\nWORK=DH0:		- Set your own Work Space. In this case DH0:.\n\nSCRIPT=Scriptfile	- The path+name of the script file to execute\n                          upon execution of lhachecker.\n			  For example Doors:LhaChecker/ISTRIP.batch\n\nFILEID_ADD=             - The line to insert after the description.\n                          i.e:\n                          _________________ _/\_______/\__|\___  /\\n			  \____ \  __\_.  /_\__/___  \__/ / \  \/  \\n			   |  /  \ \ / | /  |  | _/ _/  |/|  \   /  \\n			   | /   /  /  |/   |  | \  \|  | |   \\/    \\n			   |    /\_____|____|  |__\  \__|_____/||    /\n			  :|___/------------|__|---\__/D!-------|___/:\n			  ··   VALHALLA : BEFORE THE WAR! - [1/6]   ··\n         The file Liner ------------------------> [Leeched From COTC!]\n\nBUFFER=64		- The number of I/O KiloBytes to use while testing\n                          the archive. The higher - the faster.\n\nLHA=ram:LhA		- Path to LhA. Usefull if you want it resident. \n\n\n\n\nFuture improvements\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n Random selected files to be inserted, to make it more difficult to strip.\n   Skip the external LhA by Stefan Boberg and make my own LhA routines.\n                      Realtime output in AmiExpress.\n\n\n\nNote :\n~~~~~~\n\nThese improvements will mostly depend on the needs of Lha_Checker users.\n\n\n\nAuthor:\n~~~~~~~\n\nComments, suggestions, bug reports, flames, gifts, postbombs, etc...\nare welcome.\n\n\n                                 WiZE/aCS\n\ncontact:\n                           cLASH oF tHE cHAMPONS\n\n                         NODE 1 ++46 854 086 9 28\n                         NODE 2 ++46 854 061 3 85\n\n\n\nSuper_Lha_Checker was written with:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n	SAS/C v6.50\n\n\n\nLicense\n~~~~~~~\n\n     Super_Lha_Checker 2.1 and (hereinafter "Files") and their related\ndocumentation, utilities and examples (c) Copyright 1995 ACCESS All Rights\n                                 Reserved.\n\nThese Files and their related documentation, utilities and examples are\n                                 provided\n\n                                  "AS-IS"\n\n       and subject to change without notice; no warranties are made.\n\n\n                       All use is at your own risk.\n                No liability or responsibility is assumed.\n\n\nSpecific Files from the archive may be reproduced and distributed separately\n       under license subject to agreement with the following terms:\n\n\n1.   The Files may be reproduced but may not be modified in any way.\n\n2.   The Files may only be distributed as an integral part of a software\n     product solely