INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ata30','ATA30.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ATA30.LHA','AmiTextAdder','XIM','AmiTextAdder','3.0',NULL,NULL,NULL,replace('<---------> AmiTextAdder V3.0 <--------->\n','\n',char(10)),'AmiTextAdder.guide',replace('@database "AmiTextAdder.guide"\n@width 79\n@height 22\n\n@Node Main "AmiTextAdder V3.0 - ATA_Guide"\n    <-----------------------> AmiTextAdder V3.0 <----------------------->\n\n          (C) 1993 This version is public domain and may be freely\n              copied unless nothing in the program is changed.\n\n   Release Date: 25-JUNE-1993      Release #   : 3       Release Ver.: 3.0\n\n\n                             @{"   UPDATE NOTES    " Link UpdateNote}\n                             @{"  HOW TO UPGRADE   " Link HowUpdate}\n                             @{"QUICK INSTALLATION " Link QuickInstall}\n                             @{"     OVERVIEW      " Link Overview}\n                             @{"SUPPORTED BBSPROG. " Link MultiSupport}\n                             @{"   CLI/AMI USAGE   " Link AtaUsage}\n                             @{"  INSTALLING ATA   " Link Install}\n                             @{" INSTRUCTION VIEW  " Link InstructV}\n                             @{"     COMMANDS      " Link Commands}\n                             @{"   WHY USING ATA   " Link WhyUse}\n                             @{"     HISTORY       " Link History}\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node UpdateNote "UPDATE NOTES"\n\nUPDATE NOTES\n\nAmiTextAdder V3.0 is an update from V2.1. The changes this time is mostly\nnew keywords, and corrected textstrings. No extra function to be found in\nthis version, but the code is ofcourse improved. That is one good reason\nto update any old version.\n@EndNode\n\n@Node HowUpdate "HOW TO UPDATE FROM V2.1"\n\nHOW TO UPDATE FROM V2.1\n\nThe update from V2.1 to V3.0 is very simple. Exchange the AmiTextAdder\nprogram only. But to be up to date with new keywords we recommend you to\nread the history how to update your keywords.\n@EndNode\n\n@Node QuickInstall "QUICK INSTALLATION"\n\nQUICK INSTALLATION\n\nDue to the fact that many Sysops don''t like to read and install it with\nall commands etc. Therfore I have made a quick installation directory.\nJust select one of the archived directories matching your AmiExpress version\nand copy these file to your harddisk, and your system is on. This quick\ninstallation will take about 10 seconds. Scan the commands so you know which\nfunctions are available. You mind find many of these great.\n\nATA will show a @{"Error Description" Link Errors} if something fails. Try\nto correct it before reporting it as a bug.\n@EndNode\n\n@Node OverView "OVERVIEW"\n\nAmiTextAdder is a @{"AmiExpress" Link AmiExpress} designed software for adding textfiles\nto uploaded files. It''s configurable and should fit all needs.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node AmiExpress "AmiExpress"\n\nAmiExpress is a copyrighted bbs program, by Joseph Hodge. A easy but useful\nbbs program. This program is mainly designed for AmiExpress but may be used\nwith many others.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node MultiSupport "SUPPORTED BBSPROGRAMS"\n\nAmiTextAdder V3.0 works perfect with following BBS programs.\n\n- AmiExpress, all newer versions.\n- XenoLink, all versions.\n- CNet, all versions.\n\nThis documentation only covers AmiExpress, if using it for another\nbbs-program, you have to set it up yourself.\n@endnode\n\n@node AtaUsage "CLI, OR AMIEXPRESS USE?"\n\nAmiTextAdder can be used as a @{"CLI" Link INCLI} command, or it may be used in a Extended\nfilecheck, available in AmiExpress.\nThe difference?. Well, for the program it doesn''t matter, the only difference\nis that using it in a extended filecheck, the program name and path parms\nwill be supplied. This means it will append/insert your textfiles automatic.\n\nIf you want to add it manually, you have to supply all parameters by your\nown. This program can be used instead of the CLI command JOIN, since ATA\nhave more functions.\n@endnode\n\n@node Install "HOW TO INSTALL ATA?"\n\nIf you want to set it up fast, and don''t care how it works, you should read\nthe chapter called @{"QUICK INSTALLATION" Link QuickInstall}.\nFor interested users, we''ll hereby do a manually installation, which is much\nbetter since you''ll learn how to set up the system as you like.\n\nAmiTextAdder is used as a Filechecker. This means that the program will\nrun for every uploaded textfile. In a directory called BBS:FCHECK/ there\nshould be a number of files, all named like the last endnote. For example\nfiles could be named as TXT, CAP, etc. To set up the program, you need an\ntexteditor to write the following text.\nIf you don''t want to write this yourself, or you need some examples, you\ncan find preconfigured files in the archived listing.\nThe function of the external checkers should be found in your update\nmanual, when registering your AmiExpress.\nAn example of a file could be @{"BBS:FCHECK/TXT" Link FcheckTXT}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node FcheckTXT "BBS:FCHECK/TXT"\n\n------> CUT HERE <------\n@{"C:AmiTextAdder" link LINE_1}\n@{"APPEND s:text NEWLINEMODE 1 SHOWINFO SETLIMIT 2000 TO" link LINE_2}\n@{"Linking Failure..." link LINE_3}\n@{"Linking Failure..." link LINE_4}\n------> CUT HERE <------\n\n@endnode\n\n@node LINE_1 "Line Number 1"\n\nLINE NUMBER 1\n\nThe full path and filename of the AmiTextAdder program.\nA good place is C:, or your AmiExpress utilities directory.\nDo not send the output to any device. Example ">NIL:". This will cause\nproblems, since this is what AmiExpress does.\n@endnode\n\n@node LINE_2 "Line Number 2"\n\nLINE NUMBER 2\n\nThe command line, (ie. instructions).\nabove. Suggested is to end the line with TO or @{"WORKFILE" link WorkFile}.\n@endnode\n\n@node LINE_3 "Line Number 3"\n\nLINE NUMBER 3\n\nA configurable error message, that AmiExpress will\ndisplay if something failures. You can write a message here yourself,\nor just write as shown above. Please note that you are limited to 1 line.\n@endnode\n\n@node LINE_3 "Line Number 3"\n\nLINE NUMBER 3\n\nThis line must be here if using AmiExpress V2.x versions. Otherwise this\nline isn''t used.\n@endnode\n\n@node INCLI "CLI USE"\n\nA CLI use of the program with equal usage may look like this:\nAmiTextAdder APPEND s:text NEWLINEMODE 1 SHOWINFO SETLIMIT 2000 @{"TO" link WorkFile} ram:Linktothis.txt\n@endnode\n\n@node InstructV "INSTRUCTION-VIEW"\n\nRunning program without arguments, or using ''?'', will result in a look\nlike this:\n\n--------------> CUT HERE <--------------\n\nAmiTextAdder V3.0 by Kazar/Comax  © JUNE 1993\nTextfile Appender/Inserter For AmiExpress.\n\n@{"WORKFILE=TO/A/K" Link WorkFile}, APPEND=AFTER/A/K, INSERT=BEFORE/A/K, SHOWINFO/S,\nNOPROGRESS/S, NEWLINEMODE/K, SETLIMIT/N, TYPE=VIEWEXTERNAL/K:\n\n--------------> CUT HERE <--------------\n@endnode\n\n@node WorkFile "WORKFILE/TO"\n\nWORKFILE/TO\n\nThis command MUST be placed at the end of the command line if using\nAmiExpress. Due to AmiExpress internal programming. All other commands may\n be placed in random order.\nIf using ATA from CLI/SHELL, even WORKFILE command may be placed selective.\nIf using AmiExpress, end the second line as shown with "WORKFILE".\nYou may ignore the WORKFILE command, since AmiTextAdder will use any\nfiledescription without headercommand as WORKFILE, but to stay compatible\nwith further releases you should use the WORKFILE command.\n@endnode\n\n@node Commands "COMMANDS"\n\nCOMMANDS\n\nAmiTextAdder V3.0 supports @{"MULTI-APPENDINGS" link Multi}. This means that you can\ndeclare up to 50 files to be added to a single WorkFile.\nAmiTextAdder needs at least one append file to work.\n\nATA V3.0 Commandlistning:\n\nAFTER/      : Appends file after WorkFile. (This is the normal\nAPPEND        way, and the fastest. If requested memory to allocate\n              appendfile fails, the program will instead add one line\n              at the time. Maximum is 50 different appendfiles.\nBEFORE/     : Appends file before WorkFile. If requested memory\nINSERT        fails, the program will add one line at the time.\n              Also here the number of declarations is limited to 50.\n\n@{"SHOWINFO" link ShowInfo}    : Selects external information to be view when appending.\n              Further information later in the documentation.\nNOPROGRESS  : Disables task information about what the program is currently\n              working with. Removes texts like "Appending" etc.\n@{"NEWLINEMODE" link Nmodes} : Enables Newline information, and specifies the mode.\n              Read more about available modes for this feature.\nSETLIMIT    : Will display (type) the uploaded file at AmiExpress window, for\n              both user and sysop. ATA has a size argument.\n              SETLIMIT 2000, will display all uploaded files under\n              2000 bytes of size. A value around 2000 is recommended.\n              Ofcourse if you don''t like it, don''t use it.\n@{"VIEWEXTERNAL" link ViewE}: A very popular function. Enables a preconfigured textfile\n              to be shown before actual appending.\nWORKFILE/   : The WORKFILE TO append/insert to. Argument should not be used\nTO            if running under AmiExpress.\n@endnode\n\n@node Errors "GENERAL INFORMATION/ERROR"\n\nMessages when problem occurs consist of 2 types.\nThe first is named WARNING:, and means that the program will continue the\nwork even thought the problem.\nThe second is named ERROR:, and will terminate the operation direct.\n@endnode\n\n@node WhyUse "WHY USING ATA?"\n\nWhy using ATA, instead of other linkers?\n\n* ATA has a number of different ways to link files.\n* Date structure is equal the one used by AmiExpress. A well known format\n  for all.\n* Supports external messages, showable filecontest, progress indicator and\n  many other powerful functions.\n* ATA is a multi-file adder. It can add up to 50 different files to one\n  same file.\n* Works with all kickstarts from 1.2 and higher.\n* Designed following CBM-AMIGA-DOS lines of a high class command format.\n* Supports MC68000-68040 without any problems.\n* Can be breaked under progress using CTRL-C.\n* @{"Inserts uploaded date" link InsertDate} in appending files.\n* All errormessages will be shown on AmiExpress window.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node InsertDate "DATE FUNCTION"\n\nWriting a string called "%ATA_time" in the appendfile, will declare that\nyou want the actual upload date to be inserted there.\nThe date position text is case sensitivity, so write it exactly like\ndescribed above.\nExample of a line in the appendfile could look like this:\n\nUploaded "%ATA_time" at xxxxxxxx, +46-xxx-xxxxx\n\nAnd the result may look like this:\n\nUploaded "Sun Jul 26 23:43:52 1992" at xxxxxxxx, +46-xxx-xxxxx\n@endnode\n\n@node ViewE "VIEW EXTERNAL FILE"\n\nVIEW EXTERNAL FILE\n\nEenables a textfile to be shown before the actual appending.\nThis is a completely sysop designed message, and could consist of a thank\nfor the upload or something like that. This file could use ansi codes, since\nAmiExpress will filter them out if not using ANSI.\n@endnode\n\n@node ShowInfo "FILE INFORMATION"\n\nViews the uploaded filename, length, and current date/time.\nOther information will be added to this option in future releases so\ndo use this option.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Multi "ATA - THE MULTI ADDER"\n\nAmiTextAdder now supports up to 50 declarations of appending files. This\nmeans that you can specify 50 different files to be added to the same\nWorkFile.\n\nExample of a BBS:FCHECK/XXX file:\n------> CUT HERE <------\nC:AmiTextAdder\nAPPEND s:text1 APPEND s:text5 INSERT c:Textfile.txt APPEND doc/Ap_text NEWLINEMODE 2 SHOWINFO SETLIMIT 2000 TO xxxx\nLinking Failure...\nLinking Failure...\n------> CUT HERE <------\nThis will cause the program to append: "s:text1" & "s:text5" & "doc/Ap_text"\nafter WorkFile, and "c:Textfile.txt" will be inserted before the file xxxxxx.\n@endnode\n\n@node Nmodes "ALL NEWLINEMODES"\n\nNEWLINEMODE specifies the mode for the display. These modes are available\nand should be specified after this keyword.\n\n"1" - Normal view. Add "." for all newlines.\n"2" - Updated view, will delete all "." when appending is done.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node History "HISTORY"\n\n       Available versions and their history of changes/improvements.\n\n                            @{"AmiTextAdder V3.0" link AE30}\n\n                            @{"AmiTextAdder V2.1" link AE21}\n\n                            @{"AmiTextAdder V2.0" link AE20}\n\n                            @{"AmiTextAdder V1.0" link AE10}\n@endnode\n\n@node AE30 "AmiTextAdder V3.0"\n\n««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»\nAmiTextAdder V3.0\n\n*  Internal changes.\n*  Keyword APPEND now equals AFTER. APPEND will later on surely be the\n   only keyword recognized.\n*  Keyword INSERT now equals BEFORE. INSERT will later on surely be the\n   only keyword recognized.\n*  Keyword TYPE now equals VIEWEXTERNAL. A shortened keyword.\n*  Keyword DISPLAYLIMIT replaced with SETLIMIT.\n*  Keyword ORIGINALFILE replaced with TO. WORKFILE keyword is still\n   recognized, and will surely stay that way.\n*  History rewritten (ie. corrected).\n*  Documentation totally rewritten.\n*  Added a quick installation in the doc.\n\n««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»\n@endnode\n\n@node AE21 "AmiTextAdder V2.1"\n\n««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»\nAmiTextAdder V2.1\n\n*  Now support 2 modes of Newlinedisplays, refer to documentation.\n*  NEWLINE command replaced with NEWLINEMODE, since you now can select\n   different modes.\n*  Removed all MEWLINE displays in Organizing file mode.\n*  Modified progress text when using BEFORE. Previosly it stood\n   "Appending", but that wasn''t the correct text, since the program\n   doesn''t append it. Rewritten to "Inserting".\n*  Modified textstring shown, if workfile is empty.\n*  Corrected the command line information. All keywords now have their\n   right flags.\n*  Fixed a LARGE BUG in all previous versions. DISPLAYLIMIT command didn''t\n   care about the limit specified. It showed the file always if\n   DISPLAYLIMIT command was specified.\n*  Internal Changes.\n*  HighBit ascii-chars now handled correctly.\n\n««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»\n\n@endnode\n\n@node AE20 "AmiTextAdder V2.0"\n\n««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»\nAmiTextAdder V2.0\n\n*  Exchanged stringtexts when typing uploaded file, unnecessary text\n   removed.\n*  Improved error handling. Reports when missing, unknown and illegal use\n   of commands.\n*  "Organized" message now moved to correct location. Before this message\n   was typed before all organizing was done.\n*  ATA now pre-process all appendfiles to see if they exist before\n   trying to append the first.\n*  Reference to ''appendTO file'' should be WORKFILE. Original file is a\n   misleading label, but due to compatibility the program supports both\n   declarations.\n*  Added ability to use C:VERSION to ATA, and receive name and version\n   number of the program. Using additional command FULL/S will also display\n   internal release date.\n*  ATA is now supporting MULTI-ADD. You can now declare up to 50\n   different append files, due to the new command format. Before you\n   could only use 1.\n*  Options and commands titles are gone. ATA is now using OS2.0 language.\n*  Output now looks much better then before. Newline_codes removed, for\n   better outlook when MULTI-ADDING files.\n*  ATA now checks if a command is declared twice, and will then terminate\n   the action and leave a message.\n*  Internal Changes. Better program structure.\n*  Corrected textstrings. Missing words inserted, and textstrings are\n   re-constructed.\n*  Fixed so "%ATA_time" don''t add returncode. Meaning you can continue\n   the line after a %ATA_time declaration.\n*  Re-programmed to fit the OS2.0 command language.\n\n««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»\n\n@endnode\n\n@node AE10 "AmiTextAdder V1.0"\n\n««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»\nAmiTextAdder V1.0\n\n*  First release. No known bugs.\n\n««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»\n\n@endnode\n\n','\n',char(10)),'{"TYPE":"VIEWEXTERNAL/K:"}','auto-added',34521,9,0,NULL,NULL,'ata30','scan',1780048410);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ata_v20','ATA_V20.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ATA_V20.LHA','AmiTextAdder','XIM','AmiTextAdder','2.0',NULL,'ATA',NULL,replace('<----> AmiTextAdder V2.0 <---->\n','\n',char(10)),'AmiTextAdder.guide',replace('@database "AmiTextAdder.guide"\n@width 79\n@height 21\n\n@Node Main "AmiTextAdder V2.0 - ATA_Guide Version 2.12"\n \n      <-----------------------> AmiTextAdder V2.0 <----------------------->\n\n           (C) 1992 This version is public domain and may be freely\n               copied unless nothing in the program is changed.\n\n                      Elite BBS:  DEFCON-1 +46-501-51495\n                               Written By: KAZAR\n\n                              @{"   YES!!, UPDATE   " Link UpdateNote}\n                              @{"  HOW TO UPGRADE   " Link HowUpdate}\n                              @{" PROBLEMS, SUPPORT " Link ProbSupport}\n                              @{"     OVERVIEW      " Link Overview}\n                              @{"   MULTI PROGRAM   " Link MultiSupport}\n                              @{"   CLI/AMI USAGE   " Link AtaUsage}\n                              @{"  INSTALLING ATA   " Link Install}\n                              @{" INSTRUCTION VIEW  " Link InstructV}\n                              @{"     COMMANDS      " Link Commands}\n                              @{"   WHY USING ATA   " Link WhyUse}\n                              @{"     HISTORY       " Link History}\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node UpdateNote "Yes!!, AmiTextAdder is updated"\n\nWell, well folks. The second release of ATA, AmiTextAdder. This version\nhas been called 2.0, since it supports CBM-AMIGA standard command language.\nIt''s now simply the best there is. Step inside the new cave, and see the\nlight. Versions expected to be released was, V1.07 and V1.4. But since I\nre-programmed in CBM-AMIGA standard, I released it as 2.0. The program is\ndeveloped using OS2.0 and the layout is very alike CBM-AMIGA. But, since\nthere might be people using older kickstart versions, this program works\njust as good on a 1.2-1.3, as an 2.0.\n                                        / Signed KAZAR, the Programmer.\n@EndNode\n\n@Node HowUpdate "HOW TO UPDATE FROM V1.0"\n\nIf you have been using AmiTextAdder V1.0, and want to update to V2.0\nyou need to change your command line (2) totally. This new powerful version\nuses the high-class CBM-AMIGA DOS standard format, and will remain that\nduring all new versions.\nThe things to change is more difficult then rewrite the whole command line.\nTherefor we suggest that you read this documentation, and set up your\nAmiTextAdder from the beginning.\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node ProbSupport "PROBLEMS-SUPPORT"\n\nIf you have trouble using AmiTextAdder, or any other program by me, call\nthe support BBS: +46-501-51495. Also if having suggestions, remarks,\ncomplains and news about any of my software. You''ll be able to chat with\nme personal and leave messages. You will also get access to the SUPPORT\narea.\n\nATA will show a @{"Error Description" Link Errors} if something fails. Try\nto correct it before reporting it as a bug.\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node OverView "OVERVIEW"\n\nAmiTextAdder is a @{"AmiExpress" Link AmiExpress} designed software for adding textfiles\nto uploaded files. It''s configurable and should fit all needs.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node AmiExpress "AmiExpress"\n\nAmiExpress is a copyrighted bbs program, by Joseph Hodge. A easy but useful\nbbs program. This program is mainly designed for AmiExpress but may be used\nwith many others.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node MultiSupport "MULTI-PROGRAM-SUPPORT"\n\nAmiTextAdder V2.0 works perfect using these BBS programs.\n\n- AmiExpress, all newer versions.\n- XenoLink, all versions.\n- CNet, all versions.\n\n(Please note that the program surely supports much more, but I haven''t\n tested so many BBS-programs. Do leave me a note on which program it works\n with, and on which it doesn''t.)\n\n@endnode\n\n@node AtaUsage "CLI, OR AMIEXPRESS USE?"\n\nAmiTextAdder can be used either in @{"CLI" Link INCLI}, or in FCheck procedure. Why should\nyou use it in CLI then?. Perhaps you like to join a file by own purpose,\nand not just a boardaddy . This program is so usable that you could exchange\nit with the C: command Join. If using ATA from CLI, all commands should be\nwritten after the program name, like a normally C: program. If you should use\nAmiTextAdder as an autoadder in AmiExpress, the commands should be written at\nline 2, in the extended FCHECK/xxx file. Detailed information later on.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Install "HOW TO INSTALL ATA?"\n\nAmiTextAdder is a external AmiExpress checker. All checkers are located\nin a directory called BBS:FCHECK/ The file to be saved in that directory\nis the name of the endnote, example TXT. AmiExpress will execute the\nfilename when someone uploads a .xxx file. This program is ideal for\ndocumentations, captures and other textbased uploads.\nPreconfigured files should be located in the arched listing, named TXT,\nCAP, DOX and DOC.\n The function of the external checkers should be found in your update\nmanual, when registering your AmiExpress. \nThe fact that running a board without registration is immoral, but I''ll\nexplain the FCheck routine anyway.\nAn example of a file could be @{"BBS:FCHECK/TXT" Link FcheckTXT}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node FcheckTXT "BBS:FCHECK/TXT"\n\n------> CUT HERE <------\n@{"C:AmiTextAdder" link LINE_1}\n@{"AFTER s:text NEWLINE SHOWINFO DISPLAYLIMIT 2000 WORKFILE" link LINE_2}\n@{"Linking Failure..." link LINE_3}\n------> CUT HERE <------\n\n@endnode\n\n@node LINE_1 "Line Number 1"\n\nThe full path and filename of the AmiTextAdder program.\nEasily placed in C: or your AmiExpress program directory.\nDon''t send output to NIL: via >NIL:, since this will cause problems for\nAmiExpress, due to that AmiExpress saves the output to a tempfile, and\nthen displays it... Never use ''>''.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node LINE_2 "Line Number 2"\n\nThe command line, needed for the program. Example as\nabove. If writing @{"WORKFILE" link WorkFile}, this MUST! be the last command on the line.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node LINE_3 "Line Number 3"\n\nLine number 3 is a configurable error message, that AmiExpress will\ndisplay if something failures. You can write a message here yourself,\nor just write as shown above. Please note that you are limited to 1 line.\nThis procedure can be done with all types of textbased uploads.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node INCLI "CLI USE"\n\nA CLI use of the program with equal usage may look like this:\nAmiTextAdder AFTER s:text NEWLINE SHOWINFO DISPLAYLIMIT 2000 @{"WORKFILE" link WorkFile} ram:Linktothis.txt\n\n@endnode\n\n@node InstructV "INSTRUCTION-VIEW"\n\nRunning program without arguments, or using ''?'', will result in a look\nlike this:\n\n--------------> CUT HERE <--------------\nAmiTextAdder V2.0  by Kazar  ©1992\nFlexible/Configurable Textfile Adder For AmiExpress.\n\nSupport BBS: Defcon-1: +46-501-51495, ELITE.\n\n@{"WORKFILE=ORIGINALFILE/M" Link WorkFile}, AFTER/K/A, BEFORE/K/A, SHOWINFO/S, NOPROGRESS/S, NEW\nLINE/S, DISPLAYLIMIT/N/K, VIEWEXTERNAL/K:\n--------------> CUT HERE <--------------\n\n@endnode\n\n@node WorkFile "WORKFILE/ORIGINALFILE"\n\nThis command MUST be placed at the end of the command line if using\nAmiExpress. Due to internal programming. All other commands may be placed\nin random order.\nIf using ATA from CLI/SHELL, even WORKFILE command may be placed selective.\nIf using AmiExpress, end the second line as shown with "WORKFILE".\nYou may ignore the WORKFILE command, since AmiTextAdder will use any\nfiledescription without headercommand as WORKFILE, but to stay compatible\nwith further releases you should use the WORKFILE command.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Commands "COMMANDS"\n\nAmiTextAdder V2.0 supports @{"MULTI-APPENDINGS" link Multi}. This means that you can\ndeclare up to 50 files to be added to a single WorkFile. \nAmiTextAdder needs at least one append file to work.\n\nATA V2.0 Commandlistning:\n\nAFTER       : Appends file after WorkFile. (This is the normal\n              way, and the fastest. If requested memory to allocate\n              appendfile fails, the program will instead add one line\n              at the time. Maximum is 50 different appendfiles.\nBEFORE      : Appends file before WorkFile. If requested memory\n              fails, the program will add one line at the time.\n              Also here the number of declarations is limited to 50.\n\n@{"SHOWINFO" link ShowInfo}    : Selectrs external information to be view when appending.\n              Further information later in the documentation.\nNOPROGRESS  : Disables task information about what the program is currently\n              working with. Removes texts like "Appending" etc.\nNEWLINE     : Enables Newline indicator. Will add a dot (.) for every\n              line added to WorkFile.\nDISPLAYLIMIT: Will display (type) the uploaded file at AmiExpress window, for\n              both user and sysop. ATA has a size argument.\n              DISPLAYLIMIT 2000, will display all uploaded files under\n              2000 bytes of size. A value around 2000 is recommended.\n              Ofcourse if you don''t like it, don''t use it.\n@{"VIEWEXTERNAL" link ViewE}: A very popular function. Enables a preconfigured textfile\n              to be shown before actual appending.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Errors "GENERAL INFORMATION/ERROR"\n\nMessages when problem occurs consist of 2 types.\nThe first is named WARNING:, and means that the program will continue the\nwork even thought the problem.\nThe second is named ERROR:, and will terminate the operation direct.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node WhyUse "WHY USING ATA?"\n\nWhy using ATA, instead of other linkers?\n\n* ATA has a number of different ways to link files.\n* Date structure is equal the one used by AmiExpress. A well known format\n  for all.\n* Supports external messages, showable filecontest, progress indicator and\n  many other powerful functions.\n* ATA is a multi-file adder. It can add up to 50 different files to one\n  same file.\n* Works with all kickstarts from 1.2 and higher.\n* Designed following CBM-AMIGA-DOS lines of a high class command format.\n* Supports MC68000-68040 without any problems.\n* Can be breaked under progress using CTRL-C.\n* @{"Inserts uploaded date" link InsertDate} in appending files.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node InsertDate "DATE FUNCTION"\n\nWriting a string called "%ATA_time" in the appendfile, will declare that\nyou want the actual upload date to be inserted there.\nThe date position text is case sensitivity, so write it exactly like\ndescribed above.\nExample of a line in the appendfile could look like this:\n\nUploaded "%ATA_time" at DEFCON-1, +46-501-51495\n\nAnd the result may look like this:\n\nUploaded "Sun Jul 26 23:43:52 1992" at DEFCON 1, +46-501-51495\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ViewE "VIEW EXTERNAL FILE"\n\nEnables a textfile to be shown before the actual appending.\nThis is a completely sysop designed message, and could consist of a thank\nfor the upload or something like that. This file could use ansi codes, since\nAmiExpress will filter them out if not using Ansi.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ShowInfo "FILE INFORMATION"\n\nViews the uploaded filename, length, and current date/time.\nOther information will be added to this option in future releases so\ndo use this option.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Multi "ATA - THE MULTI ADDER"\n\nAmiTextAdder now supports up to 50 declarations of appending files. This\nmeans that you can specify 50 different files to be added to the same\nWorkFile.\n\nExample of a BBS:FCHECK/XXX file:\n------> CUT HERE <------\nc:AmiTextAdder\nAFTER s:text1 AFTER s:text5 BEFORE c:Textfile.txt AFTER doc/Ap_text NEWLINE SHOWINFO DISPLAYLIMIT 2000 WORKFILE\nLinking Failure...\n------> CUT HERE <------\nThis will cause the program to append: "s:text1" & "s:text5" & "doc/Ap_text"\nafter WorkFile, and "c:Textfile.txt" will be inserted before the WorkFile.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node History "HISTORY"\n\n««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»\nAmiTextAdder V2.0\n\n*  Exchanged stringtexts when typing uploaded file, unnecessary text\n   removed.\n*  Improved error handling. Reports when missing, unknown and illegal use\n   of commands.\n*  "Organized" message now moved to correct location. Before this message\n   was typed before all organizing was done.\n*  ATA now pre-process all appendfiles to see if they exist before\n   trying to append the first.\n*  Reference to ''appendTO file'' should be WORKFILE. Original file is a\n   misleading label, but due to compatibility the program supports both\n   declarations.\n*  Added ability to use C:VERSION to ATA, and receive name and version\n   number of the program. Using additional command FULL/S will also display\n   internal release date.\n*  ATA is now supporting MULTI-ADD. You can now declare up to 50\n   different append files, due to the new command format. Before you\n   could only use 1.\n*  Options and commands titles are gone. ATA is now using OS2.0 language.\n*  Output now looks much better then before. Newline_codes removed, for\n   better outlook when MULTI-ADDING files.\n*  ATA now checks if a command is declared twice, and will then terminate\n   the action and leave a message.\n*  Internal Changes. Better program structure.\n*  Corrected textstrings. Missing words inserted, and textstrings are\n   re-constructed.\n*  Fixed so "%ATA_time" don''t add returncode. Meaning you can continue\n   the line after a %ATA_time declaration.\n*  Re-programmed to fit the OS2.0 command language.\n\n««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»\nAmiTextAdder V1.0\n\n*  First release. No known bugs.\n\n««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««««»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»»\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',32462,10,0,NULL,NULL,'ata_v20','scan',1780048410);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('atc_mc11','ATC-MC11.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ATC-MC11.LHA','MultiComment','XIM','_______  [ aTOMIC /X iNNOVATiON PRESENT ]',NULL,NULL,'ATC','_\____  \________ ______       _____ _______ \    _   \______/_\___  \  ____\___/____    \ .\_______/    |   _   |__\/    |   |   /____/',replace(replace(' _______  [ aTOMIC /X iNNOVATiON PRESENT ]\r\n_\____  \________ ______       _____ _______\r\n\    _   \______/_\___  \  ____\___/____    \\r\n.\_______/    |   _   |__\/    |   |   /____/\r\n:     nK/_____|_______|  /_____|___|________|\r\n| ---------------------------------------- :\r\n| MULTI COMMENT v1.1 - CAPTAIN CAVEMAN/pSD |\r\n|  FASTER! - MORE OPTIONS - BETTER DESIGN  |\r\n`--( pSYCHAD pRODUCTS gLOBALLY rELEASED )--''\r\n','\r',char(13)),'\n',char(10)),'MultiComment.guide',replace('@database MultiComment.Doc\n\n(c) 1994 by Captain Caveman /X Design\n\n@Remark $VER: MultiComment 1.1 AmigaGuide docs (30-Oct-94)\n@Remark AmigaGuide DataBase "MultiComment v1.1"\n\n@node MAIN " MultiComment v1.1 (c) 1994 by Captain Caveman /X Design! "\n\n         @{"Captain Caveman" LINK CONT} proudly presents another fine @{"/X" LINK AMIX} door:\n\n          _____________ ___/\  ______/\  ___________/\_/\  _________/\\n         /       /     \\_   \/   __   \/   _/  _____/   \/  ___   __/\n        //  |___//  |   \//       \//       \|| __/ \//   \  \ ||  |\n     :://   |   |   |    \  \  /   \  \  /   \   ''   \  \     \||  |::\n    .::\________|________/__|\/|_  /__|\/|_  /_____  /__|\____/|___|::.\n    :::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\/::::::::\/::::::\/[CC]::::::::::::::\n\n          MultiComment v1.1 (c) 1994 by Captain Caveman /X Design!\n\n                          @{" What is MultiComment? " LINK WHAT}\n                          @{"     Requirements      " LINK REQU}\n                          @{"     Installation      " LINK INST}\n                          @{"      How to Use       " LINK HOWT}\n                          @{"      ToolTypes        " LINK TOOL}\n                          @{"      Arguments        " LINK ARGU}\n                          @{"      Greetings!       " LINK GREE}\n                          @{"     Contact Info      " LINK CONT}\n                          @{"    Version History    " LINK HIST}\n@endnode\n@node WHAT " What is Ratio Report? "\n                           ---------------------\n                           What is MultiComment?\n                           ---------------------\n\n          MultiComment is a XIM door created for all @{"Ami-Express" LINK AMIX}\n       BBS''s. It is designed as a replacement for the rather useless\n                     "Comment to Sysop" default door.\n\n      This door (as the name suggests) allows you to send comments to\n     the sysop, cosysops or *ANYBODY* the sysop chooses to include in\n                 the tooltypes with the touch of a button!\n\n   This door was created to be the most configurable and most attractive\n       commenter available, and also for programming practice! It is\n      written in C, using SAS/Lattice C version 6.2. This means it is\n                      faster than other ARexx doors.\n\n\n                            @{" Return to Title " LINK MAIN}\n@endnode\n@node REQU " Requirements "\n                              -------------\n                              Requirements:\n                              -------------\n\n                    To run MultiComment, you will need:\n\n              1. An @{"Amiga!" LINK AMIGA} It should be run on every @{"Amiga!" LINK AMIGA}\n\n              2. @{"AmiExpress." LINK AMIX} Minimum /X 2.x\n\n              3. The following files contained in this archive:\n\n                     - MultiComment            (Mainfile)\n                     - MultiComment.info       (Icon)\n                     - C.info                  (Icon)\n\n\n                            @{" Return to Title " LINK MAIN}\n@endnode\n@node INST "Installation"\n                       -----------------------------\n                       Installation of MultiComment:\n                       -----------------------------\n\n       Double click the install icon!  Make sure you set the default\n  tooltype to wherever your Installer program is (the one that came with\n   Workbench of course!).  It assumes you have the installer program in\n      the SYS:  directory by default.  If you don''t have it, or can''t\n         be bothered changing 1 line in the default tooltypes, try\n                           this longwinded way:\n\n   1. Copy the directory named: MultiComment into your Doors: directory.\n\n  2a. If you use /X3.x copy the C.info in your: BBS:Commands/BBSCMD/\n\n  2b. If you use /X2.x copy the following to your: BBS:Commands/BBS.CMD\n\n\n------------------Cut here------------------\nC         XM001DOORS:MultiComment/MultiComment\n------------------Cut here------------------\n\n\n                            @{" Return to Title " LINK MAIN}\n@endnode\n@node HOWT " How to use MultiComment "\n                         ------------------------\n                         How to use MultiComment:\n                         ------------------------\n\n          Simply copy the C.info file into the correct directory\n              and then type C from within @{"Ami-Express" NODE AMIX}.\n\n      The door should load and display a list of all sysops, cosysops\n           and friends that the sysop inserted in the tooltypes!\n\n\n                            @{" Return to Title " LINK MAIN}\n\n@endnode\n@node GREE " Greetings fly out to the following: "\n                          ---------------------\n                          Greetings must go to:\n                          ---------------------\n\n                                The Rookie\n                              Streetfighter\n                                 Overdose\n                               Dream Master\n                                Bad Kamma\n                                  Reaper\n                               Van-Hellsong\n\n     Huge thanks must go to Frantic for the 4k intro included in this\n                                 archive!\n\n            and all other @{"Amiga" LINK AMIGA} enthusiasts around the world!\n\n\n                            @{" Return to Title " LINK MAIN}\n@endnode\n@node AMIGA "Amiga"\n                            ------------------\n                            Amiga - Any model!\n                            ------------------\n\n      The most amazing computer ever created! The only machine with\n     standard stereo sound, amazing graphics, and FULL MULTITASKING!\n\n\n             Try doing that on your crappy IBM or Apple Mac!\n\n\n            Actually, try even running a BBS on one! Dream on!\n\n\n                            @{" Return to Title " LINK MAIN}\n@endnode\n@node CONT " Contacting Captain Caveman! "\n                       ---------------------------\n                       Contacting Captain Caveman!\n                       ---------------------------\n\n     This program and documentation was created by Captain Caveman on\n            a 2 meg Amiga 1200 on Thursday, 1st September 1994!\n\n       To contact me for bug reports, suggestions, ideas or general\n        slander, leave mail to Captain Caveman on any major BBS in\n                          Auckland, New Zealand!\n\n           (Try Marantz, Stoned Immaculate or even the Village).\n\n\n                            @{" Return to Title " LINK MAIN}\n@endnode\n@node AMIX " Ami-Express "\n                              --------------\n                              Ami-Express /X\n                              --------------\n\n     The most common BBS program in the world! Great for programming\n                  doors, and very powerful BBS software!\n\n\n                            @{" Return to Title " LINK MAIN}\n@endnode\n@node TOOL " ToolTypes Used "\n                      -----------------------------\n                      ToolTypes used in MultiComment\n                      -----------------------------\n\n     Click once on the Doors:MultiComment/MultiComment.info icon, and\n    press the Right "Amiga" key and "I" or select Information from the\n       Icon menu in Workbench. A list of tooltypes will appear that\n                              you can alter:\n\n    DEFAULT_SYSOP - This is the sysop selected if the user just hits\n                    "Return" in the program\n           PROMPT - This text will be displayed while waiting for the\n                    user to choose a sysop/cosysop\n       ANSI_TITLE - Brings up an ANSI title, just put brackets around it\n                    if you don''t want it to appear (why not!)\n        ANIMATION - Animates the title ANSI if SHOW_TITLE is set, again\n                    bracket this if you don''t want it animated\n           NAME.1 - The name of the first sysop to appear in the\n                    list (25 characters shown)\n           DESC.1 - Description of the sysop! (Max. 44 characters)\n           NAME.2 - Name of sysop #2!\n           DESC.2 - Description of sysop #2!\n           NAME.3 - Name of sysop #3!\n           DESC.3 - Description of sysop #3!\n\n    If any of the description tooltypes are missing, the computer will\n         insert default comments that come with the MultiComment.\n\n     The default sysop will appear in white in the program, so if the\n       user just hits "Return", the sysop in white will be selected!\n\n         The computer will only accept the first 25 characters of\n      a name, any extras will be ignored. The comment can be up to 44\n                     characters before being chopped!\n\n                            @{" Return to Title " LINK MAIN}\n@endnode\n@node ARGU " Arguments "\n                                 ---------\n                                 Arguments\n                                 ---------\n\n               MultiComment can be called by simply typing:\n\n                                     C\n\n      If you pass if a "?" switch, a list of greetings will appear:\n\n                                    C ?\n\n\n                            @{" Return to Title " LINK MAIN}\n@endnode\n\n@node HIST " Version History "\n                              ---------------\n                              Version History\n                              ---------------\n\n   v0.9 - Beta test version, never released.\n\n   v1.0 - Released 2nd September 1994.\n        - Animation added!\n        - Prints a list of greetings if you pass it "-H" in the\n          command line.\n        - Bug fixed where if the user hit "Return", the default sysop\n          would not be printed on the screen.\n\n   v1.1 - Released 30th October 1994.\n        - Changed compiler to SAS C v6.51!\n        - Changed the greetings list argument to "?" instead of "-H"\n        - Fixed bug in the non-animated ascii title.\n        - HUGE speed increase in reading the icon tooltypes!\n\n                            @{" Return to Title " LINK MAIN}\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,32400,3,0,NULL,NULL,'atc_mc11_multicomment','scan',1780048410);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('atc_qst1','ATC-QST1.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ATC-QST1.LHA',NULL,'XIM','_______  [ aTOMIC /X iNNOVATiON PRESENT ]',NULL,'CAPTAIN','ATC','_\____  \________ ______       _____ _______ \    _   \______/_\___  \  ____\___/____    \ .\_______/    |   _   |__\/    |   |   /____/',replace(replace(' _______  [ aTOMIC /X iNNOVATiON PRESENT ]\r\n_\____  \________ ______       _____ _______\r\n\    _   \______/_\___  \  ____\___/____    \\r\n.\_______/    |   _   |__\/    |   |   /____/\r\n:     nK/_____|_______|  /_____|___|________|\r\n| ---------------------------------------- :\r\n|   QUICK STATS v1.0 - WRITTEN BY CAPTAIN  |\r\n| CAVEMAN/PSD! FOR USE WITH /X 3.x TO 4.x! |\r\n`--( pSYCHAD pRODUCTS gLOBALLY rELEASED )--''\r\n','\r',char(13)),'\n',char(10)),'QuickStats.txt',replace('~\n[0mINSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('atc_rr16','ATC-RR16.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ATC-RR16.LHA','RatioReport','XIM','_______  [ aTOMIC /X iNNOVATiON PRESENT ]',NULL,NULL,'ATC','_\____  \________ ______       _____ _______ \    _   \______/_\___  \  ____\___/____    \ .\_______/    |   _   |__\/    |   |   /____/',replace(replace(' _______  [ aTOMIC /X iNNOVATiON PRESENT ]\r\n_\____  \________ ______       _____ _______\r\n\    _   \______/_\___  \  ____\___/____    \\r\n.\_______/    |   _   |__\/    |   |   /____/\r\n:     nK/_____|_______|  /_____|___|________|\r\n| ---------------------------------------- :\r\n| RATIO REPORT v1.6 - CAPTAIN CAVEMAN/pSD! |\r\n|   A MUST FOR ALL *GOOD* TRADING BOARDS   |\r\n`--( pSYCHAD pRODUCTS gLOBALLY rELEASED )--''\r\n','\r',char(13)),'\n',char(10)),'RatioReport.guide',replace('@database RatioReport.Doc\n\n(c) 1994 by Captain Caveman /X Design\n\n@Remark $VER: RatioReport 1.6 AmigaGuide docs (30-Aug-94)\n@Remark AmigaGuide DataBase "RatioReport v1.6"\n\n@node MAIN " RatioReport v1.6 (c) 1994 by Captain Caveman /X Design! "\n\n         @{"Captain Caveman" LINK CONT} proudly presents his first ever @{"/X" LINK AMIX} door:\n\n  _______  ____________   ___    ____________________  ___ _______________\n  \____  \/   \__  __/ | /   \   \____  \  ___/____  \/   \\____  \__  __/\n   |  /  / _|  \|  ||  |/  |  \   |  /  /  _/ \|  |  /  |  \|  /  / |  |\n  :|  \  \ \_   \  ||  /   |   \::|  \  \  |   \  __/   |   \  \  \:|  |:\n .:|__|\  \_|___/__||__\_______/::|__|\  \______\_|:\_______/__|\__\|__|:.\n :::::::\__/[CC]:::::::::::::::::::::::\__/:::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\n\n          RatioReport v1.6 (c) 1994 by Captain Caveman /X Design!\n\n                          @{" What is RatioReport? " LINK WHAT}\n                          @{"    Requirements      " LINK REQU}\n                          @{"    Installation      " LINK INST}\n                          @{"     How to Use       " LINK HOWT}\n                          @{"     ToolTypes        " LINK TOOL}\n                          @{"     Greetings!       " LINK GREE}\n                          @{"    Contact Info      " LINK CONT}\n                          @{"   Version History    " LINK HIST}\n@endnode\n@node WHAT " What is Ratio Report? "\n                          ---------------------\n                          What is Ratio Report?\n                          ---------------------\n\n          Ratio Report is a XIM door created for all @{"Ami-Express" LINK AMIX}\n       BBS''s. It brings up a title and displays some information to\n         the user about the state of their uploads and downloads.\n\n     This door was created to be the most configurable Ratio Reporter\n      available, and also for programming practice! It is written in\n       C, using SAS/Lattice C version 6.2. This means it is faster\n                         than other ARexx doors.\n\n\n                            @{" Return to Title " LINK MAIN}\n@endnode\n@node REQU " Requirements "\n                              -------------\n                              Requirements:\n                              -------------\n\n                    To run Ratio Report, you will need:\n\n              1. An @{"Amiga!" LINK AMIGA} It should be run on every @{"Amiga!" LINK AMIGA}\n\n              2. @{"AmiExpress." LINK AMIX} Minimum /X 2.x\n\n              3. The following files contained in this archive:\n\n                     - RatioReport        (Mainfile)\n                     - RatioReport.info   (Icon for Doors dir)\n                     - Ratio.info         (Icon for Commands dir)\n\n\n                            @{" Return to Title " LINK MAIN}\n@endnode\n@node INST "Installation"\n                       ----------------------------\n                       Installation of RatioReport:\n                       ----------------------------\n\n   1. Copy the directory named: RatioReport into your Doors: directory.\n\n  2a. If u use /X3.x copy the Ratio.info in your: BBS:Commands/BBSCMD/\n\n  2b. If u use /X2.x copy the following to your: BBS:Commands/BBS.CMD\n\n\n------------------Cut here------------------\nRATIO     XM010DOORS:RatioReport/RatioReport\n------------------Cut here------------------\n\n\n                            @{" Return to Title " LINK MAIN}\n@endnode\n@node HOWT " How to use Ratio Report "\n                         ------------------------\n                         How to use Ratio Report:\n                         ------------------------\n\n     Use the install script provided with this archive! Make sure you\n       have the Commodore Installer utility in your SYS: directory!\n       If you don''t, simply change the default tool to wherever the\n                     Installer is located on your system!\n\n           Or bung the Ratio.info file into the correct directory\n              and then type "RATIO" from within @{"Ami-Express" NODE AMIX}.\n\n    The door should load and display the information about the user''s\n                        uploading and downloading!\n\n  Alternatively, run it before calling the download command, so the user\n                     feels guilty about their ratio!\n\n               Also, type "RATIO ?" for a list of greetings!\n\n\n                            @{" Return to Title " LINK MAIN}\n\n@endnode\n@node GREE " Greetings fly out to the following: "\n                          ---------------------\n                          Greetings must go to:\n                          ---------------------\n\n                                The Rookie\n                                 Homicide\n                                 Overdose\n                               Van-Hellsong\n                                Supertouch\n                               Dream Master\n                                Bad Kamma\n                                Skeptical\n                                  Alpine\n                                   Ceer\n                                  Reaper\n\n     Huge thanks must go to Frantic for the 3k intro included in this\n       archive! I''ve finally gotten around to changing your graphics\n                               aswell dude!\n\n            and all other @{"Amiga" LINK AMIGA} enthusiasts around the world!\n\n\n                            @{" Return to Title " LINK MAIN}\n@endnode\n@node AMIGA "Amiga"\n                            ------------------\n                            Amiga - Any model!\n                            ------------------\n\n      The most amazing computer ever created! The only machine with\n     standard stereo sound, amazing graphics, and FULL MULTITASKING!\n\n\n             Try doing that on your crappy IBM or Apple Mac!\n\n\n            Actually, try even running a BBS on one! Dream on!\n\n\n                            @{" Return to Title " LINK MAIN}\n@endnode\n@node CONT " Contacting Captain Caveman! "\n                       ---------------------------\n                       Contacting Captain Caveman!\n                       ---------------------------\n\n   The original program and documentation was created by Captain Caveman\n           on a 2 meg Amiga 1200 on Thursday, 25th August 1994!\n\n       To contact me for bug reports, suggestions, ideas or general\n        slander, leave mail to Captain Caveman on any major BBS in\n                          Auckland, New Zealand!\n\n           Try Marantz, Stoned Immaculate or even the Village.\n\n\n                            @{" Return to Title " LINK MAIN}\n@endnode\n@node AMIX " Ami-Express "\n                              --------------\n                              Ami-Express /X\n                              --------------\n\n     The most common BBS program in the world! Great for programming\n                  doors, and very powerful BBS software!\n\n      And of course, everybody who uses it has a registered copy! ;-)\n\n\n                            @{" Return to Title " LINK MAIN}\n@endnode\n@node TOOL " ToolTypes Used "\n                      -----------------------------\n                      ToolTypes used in RatioReport\n                      -----------------------------\n\n   Click once on the Doors:RatioReport/RatioReport.info icon, and press\n    Right "Amiga" key and "I" or select Information from the Icon menu\n    in Workbench. A list of tooltypes will appear that you can alter:\n\n         ANSI_TITLE - This will bring up an 8 colour Ansi screen as\n                      the title. If you do NOT want the ansi appearing\n                      then put brackets around the word (as in the CBM\n                      style guidelines)\n          ANIMATION - If ANSI_TITLE is found and ANIMATION is also found\n                      the title will be animated!\n          TITLELINE - If ANSI_TITLE is not found, you can insert your\n                      own title line here which will be displayed at the\n                      top of the screen!\n               DULL - This is shown if the user hasn''t traded more\n                      than 100000 bytes (a dull user!)\n              LEECH - Text displayed if ratio is worse than 1:20\n         RATIO1TO20 - Text displayed if ratio is better than 1:20\n         RATIO1TO15 - Text displayed if ratio is better than 1:15\n         RATIO1TO10 - Text displayed if ratio is better than 1:10\n          RATIO1TO5 - Text displayed if ratio is better than 1:5\n          RATIO1TO3 - Text displayed if ratio is better than 1:3\n          RATIO1TO1 - Text displayed if ratio is better than 1:1\n          RATIO2TO1 - Text displayed if ratio is better than 2:1\n          RATIO3TO1 - Text displayed if ratio is better than 3:1\n              ELITE - Text displayed if ratio is better than 5:1\n              EQUAL - This text is shown if the user has downloaded\n                      the same number of bytes as uploaded. This is\n                      only shown if the user has traded (uploaded or\n                      downloaded something)\n\n    The ratio is Uploads:Downloads, so a ratio of 1:5 means for every\n                1 meg of uploads, the user leeches 5 megs!\n\n     If the ratio falls between these, it will be rounded DOWN. So a\n        user that uploads 1 meg for every 17 megs leeched will get\n                       the RATIO1TO20 comment only.\n\n   If any of these tooltypes are missing, the computer will insert the\n        default comments that come with the RatioReport.info icon.\n\n    The computer will only accept the first 60 characters, any extras\n                             will be ignored.\n\n\n                            @{" Return to Title " LINK MAIN}\n@endnode\n@node HIST " Version History "\n                              ---------------\n                              Version History\n                              ---------------\n\n   v0.9 - Beta test version, never released.\n\n   v1.0 - Released 25th August 1994.\n        - Two versions of docs included, one for users of AmigaGuide\n          (RatioReportWB2.guide) and one for users of Multiview\n          (RatioReport.guide).\n\n   v1.1 - Released 26th August 1994.\n        - Bug found where the red ASCII was appearing as white during a\n          remote logon, now fixed.\n        - History added to docs!\n\n   v1.2 - Released 30th August 1994.\n        - New tooltype added, EQUAL for when the user appears to have\n          downloaded their own files!\n        - Colour of title ASCII should always be red now, bug finally\n          fixed!\n\n   v1.3 - Released 18th September 1994.\n        - New tooltype added, RATIO1TO15 for people who are in between\n          the 1:20 and 1:10 ratio\n        - Sped up icon reading! Instead of setting up the array each\n          time, checking for the file/directory extension, and then\n          searching, I now lock the file and then unlock it at the end.\n          This should be about 5 times faster for reading tooltypes!\n        - Added ANIMATION and ANSI_TITLE features to make it more like\n          my other /X utility, MultiComment!\n        - Greetings page added, simply type "RATIO ?" at the prompt\n          for a quick list of greetings!\n        - Decided not to include Multiview docs anymore, I may however\n          release a utility to convert AmigaGuide docs to Multiview\n          format and vice versa (if there''s enough support for it!)\n\n   v1.4 - Released 20th September 1994\n        - Added non-stop text commands so the text wouldn''t pause\n        - Changed tooltypes to behave as in the Commodore style\n          guidelines\n\n   v1.5 - Released 24th September 1994\n        - Fixed bug in non-stop text where the "More (y/n/ns)" requester\n          appeared. This bug seems to occur due to /X and not my code!\n\n   v1.6 - Released 30th September 1994\n        - Added TITLELINE option for people who don''t want ANY ascii\n          so they can write whatever they want! Suggested by cANaAN!\n\n\n                            @{" Return to Title " LINK MAIN}\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,29024,3,0,NULL,NULL,'atc_rr16_ratioreport','scan',1780048410);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('atc_stvt','ATC-STVT.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ATC-STVT.LHA',NULL,'XIM','VOTE.X',NULL,NULL,'ATC','__\___ \|       /  _  \/  \/  \/  \    __/_ __/  |  \___/   |   \_\  /  \   \   |   | \_______|____\\_________/_\/____\__|\______|',replace('hMC____  _____________  /\  __  / _|______  \n__\___ \|       /  _  \/  \/  \/  \    __/_ \n   __/  |  \___/   |   \_\  /  \   \   |   |\n\_______|____\\_________/_\/____\__|\______|\n|pSYCHE/dVS pRESENTS tHE sUPER^tRADER vOTE|\n| dOOR v1.0!  aLL uSA sYSOPS mUST iNSTALL |\n| iF tHEY wANT tO bE iNCLUDED iN tHE nEXT |\n|  vOTING cHARTS oF aTOMIC sUPER^tRADER!  |\n`-----------------------------------------''       \n','\n',char(10)),'VOTE.DOC',replace('\n            -<( Super Trader v1.0 by Psyche/Devious Dezigns )>-\n\n                              (Quick Docs!)\n\n\n      This  door  was  quickly made so there are no special funtions or such\n but  it  does  the  job  required.   All  you  have to do is copy the doors\n directory  and  the Vote.info in the bbscmd.  Its that simple..  To restart\n Super  Trader, just delete the contents in the files ANSWERS and USERS, but\n dont  delete  the actual files as the door looks for them..  anyways I will\n make a new version in the future with mote functions, but for now cya!  and\n have fun!\n\n pSYCHE/dVS!\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',11795,4,0,NULL,NULL,'atc_stvt','scan',1780048410);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('atc_fdup','ATC_FDUP.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ATC_FDUP.LHA',NULL,'XIM','._______ __________________________________.',NULL,NULL,'ATC','_\____  \________ ______       _____ ______| \    _   \______/_\___  \  ____\___/____    \ |\_______/    |   _   |__\/    |   |   /____/',replace('._______ __________________________________.\n_\____  \________ ______       _____ ______|\n\    _   \______/_\___  \  ____\___/____    \\n|\_______/    |   _   |__\/    |   |   /____/\n|     nK/_____|_______|  /_____|___|________|\n| ---------------------------------------- |\n| UPDATE FOR BOBO/MST FILEDESCRIPTION DOOR |\n`-----( aLL sYSOPS sHOULD iNSTALL iT )-----''   \n','\n',char(10)),'reference-board.txt',replace(replace('              W h e r e   t h e   w a r e z   c o m e   f r o m\r\n                                               __                /\_____:\r\n__/\__________________________________________|  \______________/  \    |__\r\n\_   ___________  _______ ________  \__   ___ |   _______  _______  \_  l  \\r\n__\____  \    _l   \    |  \     |___/     |  !    \   _l   \   _| __/\____ \_\r\n\_____    \___\     \___|   \___ !   \__   |_____   \__\     \__\    \____   /\r\n -mNT\_____/---\_____/--l____/-\______/\   |----\____/--\_____/--\____/--\__/\r\n                                        \__|\r\n\r\n- -- --> F A i R L i G H T   S W E D i S H   H E A D Q U A R T E R S <-- -- -\r\n\r\n           reference-board is back 2017 after more than 20 years in coma!\r\n\r\n                        Running on AmiExpress TelNet\r\n\r\n                    Connect to: reference-board.zapto.org:1541\r\n\r\n                    or: www.brysk.se/reference-board/index.htm\r\n               \n              UPLOAD DATE: 01-04-18  TIME: 19:56:46  ON NODE: 0\n','\r',char(13)),'\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,12980,6,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048410);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('atc_rr17','ATC_RR17.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ATC_RR17.LHA','RATIOREP','XIM','RATIOREP',NULL,NULL,'ATC','hMC____  _____________  /\  __  / _|______ __\___ \|       /  _  \/  \/  \/  \    __/_ __/  |  \___/   |   \_\  /  \   \   |   |',replace('                                 · :\nhMC____  _____________  /\  __  / _|______\n__\___ \|       /  _  \/  \/  \/  \    __/_\n   __/  |  \___/   |   \_\  /  \   \   |   |\n\_______|____\\_________/_\/____\__|\______|\ncAPTAIN cAVEMAN / pSYCHAD & aTOMIC /X dESIGN\n    present... RATIO REPORT version 1.7\n-+---------÷-------------÷----------------+-\n','\n',char(10)),'reference-board.txt',replace(replace('              W h e r e   t h e   w a r e z   c o m e   f r o m\r\n                                               __                /\_____:\r\n__/\__________________________________________|  \______________/  \    |__\r\n\_   ___________  _______ ________  \__   ___ |   _______  _______  \_  l  \\r\n__\____  \    _l   \    |  \     |___/     |  !    \   _l   \   _| __/\____ \_\r\n\_____    \___\     \___|   \___ !   \__   |_____   \__\     \__\    \____   /\r\n -mNT\_____/---\_____/--l____/-\______/\   |----\____/--\_____/--\____/--\__/\r\n                                        \__|\r\n\r\n- -- --> F A i R L i G H T   S W E D i S H   H E A D Q U A R T E R S <-- -- -\r\n\r\n           reference-board is back 2017 after more than 20 years in coma!\r\n\r\n                        Running on AmiExpress TelNet\r\n\r\n                    Connect to: reference-board.zapto.org:1541\r\n\r\n                    or: www.brysk.se/reference-board/index.htm\r\n               \n              UPLOAD DATE: 01-04-18  TIME: 19:56:45  ON NODE: 0\n','\r',char(13)),'\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',23014,9,0,NULL,NULL,'atc_rr17','scan',1780048410);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('atc_sr10','ATC_SR10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ATC_SR10.LHA',NULL,'XIM','._______ __________________________________.',NULL,'dRAKAR/aTC/tRSI/mTH','ATC','_\____  \________ ______       _____ ______| \    _   \______/_\___  \  ____\___/____    \ |\_______/    |   _   |__\/    |   |   /____/',replace('._______ __________________________________.\n_\____  \________ ______       _____ ______|\n\    _   \______/_\___  \  ____\___/____    \\n|\_______/    |   _   |__\/    |   |   /____/\n|     nK/_____|_______|  /_____|___|________|\n| ---------------------------------------- |\n| STATUS REVIEW v1. BY dRAKAR/aTC/tRSI/mTH |\n`-----( qUICK sCRIPT bUT nICE dESIGN )-----''   \n','\n',char(10)),'STATSREV.DOC',replace('                                                          ·\n      _             ·                     /\          ·   :              _\n       \\_  _______ :____________________/  \  ____  /   _|_________  _//\n_ _  _______\___   \|       __     _    |    \/    \/    \     ____/____  _ _\n __\/__\    ___/    |/      |      |    |   \  /    \     \    |     |__\/__\n   \/   \___________|_      |\__________|____\/______\    |\_________|  \/\n                   /        |                    /        |  hMC\n                  ·         :                   ·         :\n                            .                             .\n\n                   status review version 1.0 docs...\n\n                   \n                   installation...\n\n                   ok.. well,  basically  i  made  this \n                   door  nice  and quickly for one main\n                   reason,  there  aren''t  enough  nice \n                   looking  stat doors around.   anyway\n                   this  was just made with  help  from\n                   mci  coding, so all  you  have to do\n                   is  make it  display the  screen  at\n                   the ''s'' command.  \n                   \n                   future plans...\n\n                   i am currently  working  on the code\n                   for a door to match the stats review\n                   script.  its gonna be a stats editer\n                   door, in similar design.   also i am\n                   working on a more animated and betta\n                   version of the review door.\n\n                   last words...\n\n                   if you want to contact me  for mail\n                   or  shit  about  bugs  in any of my \n                   doors, then mail me on masturbation\n                   station... greets to all members of\n                   atomic, myth, trsi,  prestige,  and\n                   crux...\n\n\n                   drakar/trsi&atomic&myth...\n\n                   \n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,4591,3,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048410);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('atl_page','ATL-PAGE.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ATL-PAGE.LHA',NULL,'XIM','________________________',NULL,NULL,'ATL','________________________ |         |          / _/  PRESENtS THiS |   ---   |         /  |   NEW AMiX DooR',replace('\n ________________________\n|         |          / _/  PRESENtS THiS\n|   ---   |         /  |   NEW AMiX DooR\n|         |___   __/   |__ CALLED\n|    |    |  |   \ |   |  \     DZYPAGE\n|    |    |  |    \|   |   \\n|    |    |  |     \        \ ThIS iS V1.0!\nl____|    |  |_   _/___    _/ dA FiRST\nDiZY!`----''   `---''   `----''  rElEASE!!\n','\n',char(10)),'Dzypage.DOC',replace('ReAdMe fILE AND RULES FoR DZYPAGE :\n\n1.I TAKE NO RESPONSABILITY WHATSOEVER IF ANYTHING AT ALL CRASHES ETC. !!!!!!!!!!\n2.IF YOU DONT KNOW HOW TO INSTALL THIS - THEN DONT USE IT!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n3.YOU ALSO NEED SOME REXX STUFF TO uSe THiS!!!!!!!!\n4.WANT ME (DiZY) tO MAkE YoU SoME AsCiI? lEAVE mE a nOTE oN ElECTRONiC ConFuSioN oR CyClOnE ZoNe or MEnTaL iNSAnITy oR PhEnOmEnA oR SkY ToWeR EtC. !!\n\nGiGA-GrEEtZ tO: JoShUa,WeBsTeR,MeNaCe,Mr.nOBrAiN,KrALlE,\nmR.OrIoN,SoFTLiNE aNd AlL dA FriEnDlY GuYZ i KnOW! :)\n                                \n                               _/\   ___/\\n   ______/\ ______________/\  /   \ /    .\\n  |       .\\_    ./       .\/    .Y      \\\n  |     .  \\|____/         \\    !|       \\\n  |    ||   \\___ \  ___     \\   :!       //\n  |    !|    \\ .\ \/     ____/__ .: ______/\n  |    :!     \\ \\/    ./  .\ |   . .\\n  |    .:     //  \\   //    \\|  .   \\\n  |     .    //   //          \\       \\\n  l_____    _/____/_____      _/___    _/\n       `----''[DiZY!]   `------''   `----''\n..SIGNING OFF!\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,3259,3,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048410);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('atm_gr10','ATM-GR10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ATM-GR10.LHA',NULL,'XIM','_____  _____________  /\  __  / _|______',NULL,NULL,'ATM','__\___ \|       /  _  \/  \/  \/  \    __/_ \  __/  |  \___/   |   \_\  /  \   \   |   | hMC_____|____\\_________/_\/____\__|\______|',replace('  _____  _____________  /\  __  / _|______\n__\___ \|       /  _  \/  \/  \/  \    __/_\n\  __/  |  \___/   |   \_\  /  \   \   |   |\nhMC_____|____\\_________/_\/____\__|\______|\n[(----------------------------------------)]\n  aTOMiC! PRESENT THE GAMES REViEW iSSUE 1\n[(----------------------------------------)]\n','\n',char(10)),'ATM-GR10.TXT',replace(replace('\r\n               _                                                 _\r\n              (_)-----------------------------------------------(_)\r\n               |::::''                                            |\r\n               |::     ATOMiC PRESENT....      . _ __  ____  _ _ |_\r\n       _\______:_________________________ _____:_____\ \__/ /____:____/_\r\n       __\___   _/_____  _____\_   _   _/ \_   :   _/ \____/ \_   ___/__\r\n   _ _/    ___    \_ |    | _/     |     \_   \_/    \_     \_    l     \_\_\r\n   \ \_____________/ |    : \_____________/____:______/_____ /___________/ /\r\n               |.    :    .                    .           \/   .|\r\n               |:.   .         Copywright Atomic 1995 (C)      .:|\r\n               |::. .  .                                 .  ..:::|\r\n              (_)-adk!------------------------------------------(_)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n \r\n                                    /\\r\n     _________      ______   ____  /  \  __________  ________\r\n    /   _____/______\__   \_/  _ \/ _  \/   ___   /__\   ___/___\r\n  _/    \_     \   ___/    |    \  /    \   \____/ |  \____    /\r\n  \____________|\__________|_____\/______\_________|__________/\r\n                                         ·\r\n                                     ·   :                   ______\r\n       _______ _ ___________________/    | __________  _____|      |\r\n    ___\___   \_  ___   /_         /     |/   ___   /_/     /\     |\r\n   /     _/   _/  \____/ |        /     _/    \____/ |    _/  \_   |\r\n  /______\     \_________|\______/      \____________|______/\     | hMC\r\n          \_____/               /        :                    \____|\r\n                               ·         .\r\n \r\n              ( THE aTOMiC 1995 / 1996 GAMES REViEW )\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n@BEGIN_TEXT\r\n\r\n                                             __\r\n     ____________________.· 1995 / 1996! ·.__\/_______________\r\n    |     | |     |                         \/\/ |     | |    |\r\n    |_____|_|     |.----------------------------.|     | |____|\r\n     _____  |     ||      ·) JELLY BOY! (·      ||     |\r\n    |     | |     |`----------------------------''|     |\r\n    |_____|_|_____|__\/__.· GAMES REViEW ·.______|_____|\r\n                    \/\/\r\n\r\n\r\n Jelly Boy is a might-morphing sweetie who''s found himself  trapped\r\n in a deadly sweet factory.  To escape, he''s going  to  need  every\r\n ounce of his bendy changeability, as well as someneat footwork  to\r\n avoid the security guards and survive the hazards which  block his\r\n way - which are made even worse, of course,  by  numerous  blocked\r\n exits and locked doors.\r\n \r\n This is where Jelly Boy''s  morph-ability  comes in handy.  As long\r\n he''s collected the right  pick-ups,  our  hero can change into any\r\n one  of  27 different shapes and objects (ranging from a submarine\r\n to and umbrella).  Buth there''s always a logical reason for him to\r\n change into certain  shapes  to solve certain puzzles, so a bit of\r\n laterial thinking should see your right!\r\n \r\n \r\n                                             __\r\n     ____________________.· 1995 / 1996! ·.__\/_______________\r\n    |     | |     |                         \/\/ |     | |    |\r\n    |_____|_|     |.----------------------------.|     | |____|\r\n     _____  |     ||      ·) MR. NUTZ 2 (·      ||     |\r\n    |     | |     |`----------------------------''|     |\r\n    |_____|_|_____|__\/__.· GAMES REViEW ·.______|_____|\r\n                    \/\/\r\n \r\n \r\n Oceans toothy, bushy-tailed terror is back.  While holidays at the\r\n beautiful resort  that is Planet Peanut, our heroes relaxation  is\r\n spoiled byt he appearance of a villainouse gang of space  chickens\r\n which  is,  or  course,  and  excuse  for  a colorful romp through\r\n gameplay heaven.  Destined to become a classic!\r\n \r\n \r\n                                             __\r\n     ____________________.· 1995 / 1996! ·.__\/_______________\r\n    |     | |     |                         \/\/ |     | |    |\r\n    |_____|_|     |.----------------------------.|     | |____|\r\n     _____  |     ||     ·) PUTTY SQUAD! (·     ||     |\r\n    |     | |     |`----------------------------''|     |\r\n    |_____|_|_____|__\/__.· GAMES REViEW ·.______|_____|\r\n                    \/\/\r\n \r\n \r\n The  world''s  most unlikely  hero makes his return in Putty Squad!\r\n Throughout his  new  adventure,  our  blue  blob  hero  encounters\r\n enemies as varied  as  Terminator  Carrots,  Demonic  Dentures and\r\n Bombing Bees.  This one is shaping up to be a real winner.\r\n \r\n \r\n                                             __\r\n     ____________________.· 1995 / 1996! ·.__\/_______________\r\n    |     | |     |                         \/\/ |     | |    |\r\n    |_____|_|     |.----------------------------.|     | |____|\r\n     _____  |     ||      ·) FLiNSTONES (·      ||     |\r\n    |     | |     |`----------------------------''|     |\r\n    |_____|_|_____|__\/__.· GAMES REViEW ·.______|_____|\r\n                    \/\/\r\n \r\n \r\n Fred Flintone is beleaguered by problems he really shouldn''t have!\r\n Not least of these is the fact that his boss hates him and he''s in\r\n danger  of  losing his job.  So, in order to get away from it all,\r\n Fred packs up his  Loin-cloth  and sets off on a quest - which, of\r\n course is where you come in.\r\n \r\n Taking control of Fred, you guide  him  through  eight  levels  of\r\n serious   platform   action.    The  scenarios  which  await  your\r\n exploration  range from Fred''s work-place, the streets of Bedrock.\r\n The Flinstone family  home  and  even  the race-track on the other\r\n side  of  town.   No  prizes for guessing what he might have to do\r\n there.\r\n \r\n Making life much harder  are the usual perils you''d expect to find\r\n in Cretaceous times: Pterodactyls swoop, giant frogs leap and huge\r\n nameless dinosaurs wander  around - its up to you whether you want\r\n to use them or avoid them.\r\n \r\n You can rely on your trusty  club  to  smash  many  of  them  into\r\n nothingness, but this won''t work with all the foes you meet - some\r\n will require a little more brain power than that.  This is where a\r\n bit  of  thought  comes in.   Maybe,  just maybe, there are secret\r\n passages, even locations and even special power-ups you''ll miss!\r\n \r\n \r\n                                             __\r\n     ____________________.· 1995 / 1996! ·.__\/_______________\r\n    |     | |     |                         \/\/ |     | |    |\r\n    |_____|_|     |.----------------------------.|     | |____|\r\n     _____  |     ||   ·) EUROFiGHTER 2000 (·   ||     |\r\n    |     | |     |`----------------------------''|     |\r\n    |_____|_|_____|__\/__.· GAMES REViEW ·.______|_____|\r\n                    \/\/\r\n \r\n \r\n The next military masterpiece from the chaps at D.I.D will be this\r\n awesome sequel to the best-selling fight and fight simulator, TFX!\r\n Eurofighter 2000 will  feature  a flight  model that  was produced\r\n with the help of both aircraft manafacturers and realworld pilots!\r\n Watch the skies....\r\n \r\n \r\n                                             __\r\n     ____________________.· 1995 / 1996! ·.__\/_______________\r\n    |     | |     |                         \/\/ |     | |    |\r\n    |_____|_|     |.----------------------------.|     | |____|\r\n     _____  |     ||     ·) GREEN LATERN (·     ||     |\r\n    |     | |     |`----------------------------''|     |\r\n    |_____|_|_____|__\/__.· GAMES REViEW ·.______|_____|\r\n                    \/\/\r\n \r\n \r\n Super heroes don''t come much bigger that  this -  as  Ocean  bring\r\n the classic DC comics character to life on the amiga.\r\n \r\n \r\n \r\n@END_TEXT\r\n  \r\n           _  _ _  ___  __ _\r\n                 \ \_/ /_____ ______ ______________________\r\n             _    \___/ \_   \    _/ \_  ______/\_   _   _/    _\r\n            (_) _/     \_   \ \    \_     ___/_/     |     \_ (_)\r\n                \_______/____\ \    /_____|   \_____________/ adk!\r\n    .-- - ----  --- --- ---- -\____/ --- -:-- - -------- --- ---- ----.\r\n    |                                                                 |\r\n    |   If you would like to know some information or cheats for a    |\r\n    |   game coming up or that you have already, just ring our new    |\r\n    |   ATOMiC GAMES HOTLiNE on +64-9-535-2133  or message  dRAkAR    |\r\n    |   on almost any scene board!  Special thanks fly out to  the    |\r\n    |   following people for helping out in issue one:  dRAkAR/iHS    |\r\n    |   For the content, aCiD kID/sHT/wL!  and  hOMiCiDE/aTM!  for    |\r\n    |   the design work.  Following issues will be in amiga code!!    |\r\n    |                                                                 |\r\n    `--- ---- ----- --- -- ---- ----- --- ---- --- ----- -- ---- -----''\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','\r',char(13)),'\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,7170,6,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048410);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('atx_chat','ATX-CHAT.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ATX-CHAT.LHA',NULL,'XIM','Z1.EXE',NULL,NULL,'ATX','sLa/_  I  \I  \      / Y  \___  \__  \ Y  / / I  I   \   \/ \_/  _   \ I  / I   \  / /  _  I       /   \   I   /    \ I   /  \',replace('    /\_.__ ./\______/\_ /\____/\___/\__ _/\\nsLa/_  I  \I  \      / Y  \___  \__  \ Y  /\n  / I  I   \   \/ \_/  _   \ I  / I   \  /\n /  _  I       /   \   I   /    \ I   /  \\n/   I  I__I\__/\___/\__I__/__I\__\___/_I  \\n\___I__I======[ P.R.E.S.E.N.T.S ]======I___\\n New 32 NODE mutichat version 3.0 !!\n','\n',char(10)),'Dago.TXT',replace('\n\n\n\n\n\n .=[*][+][*][+]`=[*][+][*][+]`=[*][+][*][+]`=[*][+][*][+]`=[*][+][*][+][*]=.\n[*    | __                                                      __  |    *]\n +]   ; \/+-=->   NoW cAlL tHe OrGaNiZeD CrIme cAlL fAsT   <-=-+\/  ;   [+\n[*    >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>DAGOBERTS-REVANGE<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<     *]\n `-=>         :                :   BBS                        :Dagobert<=-`\n >>>> //////////////////////////////\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ <<<<<<<\n .-=>  -  <-+-:AmIgA 2000 - 360 Mb OnLiNe - 68030/25MhZ - CoOl:-+->    <=-`\n[*    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\//////////////////////////////       *]\n[+    *YoUr OpErAtOrS aRe: Dagobert - cosy:TKK/Butthead/Blackcat *       +]\n[+    *        For other Conferences :.....................      *       +]\n[+    *                  Right hand is :TKK                      *       +]\n[+    ************************************************************       +]\n[+    -          __   NoDe0 +49 208-XXX-XXX  16.8 Zyxel  __         -    +]\n*]  AMI-ExPrEsSS      NoDe1 +49 208-XXX-XXX  14.4 USR-D.S Ami-ExPrEsSS   [*\n+]     -              NoDe2 +49 208-XXX-XXX  16.8 Zyxel             -    [+\n[+   .:-*- AsK onLy ElItEs foR da NuMber aNd tHe SyStem PasSword -*-:.   +]\n *]_  _  _  _    _  _  _  _    _  _  _  _    _  _  _  _    _  _  _  _  _[*\n.=[*][+][*][+]`=[*][+][*][+]`=[*][+][*][+]`=[*][+][*][+]`=[*][+][*][+][*]=.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',17292,10,0,NULL,NULL,'atx_chat','scan',1780048410);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('atx_dmsa','ATX-DMSA.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ATX-DMSA.LHA','Append','XIM','Append','1.0',NULL,'ATX',NULL,replace('Dms Track+Text Appender V1.0!\n','\n',char(10)),'Append.doc',replace('                    ___  ____ ________   _  ___  __  _  _   \n                   (__ \(___ \\_   ___)_( )|  _)/  \( \/ )  \n                   / /\ \| |\ \ | | |  _  || | / /\ \\  /   \n                  / /_ \ \ | \ \| | | | | || | \ \/ //  \_  \n                  \___)(_/_) (_/(_) (_) (_)(_)  \__/(_/\__) \n                - -- ---=-==-===> PRESENT: <===-==-=--- -- -\n                       Dms Track+Text Appender V1.0! \n                - -- ---=-==-==================-==-=--- -- -\n                       Coded by I.O for ICE/Anthrox! \n\n  This Util was coded for all you Trainer Guys out there who still use\n  Multiple Dms files for your trainers and fixes.. Its simple to use and\n  has been thoroughly tested (over 100 trainers!) Works for both the old\n  and new DMS!  Its a fairly old util (almost a year old) but works pretty\n  well!   \n\nQuick Dox:\n\n  Track_Append <Dest File> [Text <File>] <Source Files> [Text <File>]\n\n  Dest File     : Final Output File (eg. Cooltrnr.dms)\n  Text          : Optional Text append\n  File          : Name of text file (eg. anthrox.txt)\n  Source File(s): Name(s) of Dms file(s) to append (eg. 1.dms 2.dms 3.dms)\n\nExample:\n\n  O.k. Say you want to dms up tracks 0,49,76-79 and wanted "anthrox.txt" \n  as the Frontend-text and "bbs.txt" as the End-Text and the Final file\n  to be called "shithot.dms" this is what you would do.\n\n  Note:  .dms may be ommitted!\n         \n\n  1> First Dms the tracks required.\n\n    Dms read file1 low 0 high 0 nozero\n    Dms read file2 low 49 high 49 nozero\n    Dms read file3 low 76 high 79 nozero\n\n  2> Type in the arguments.\n\n    TRACK_APPEND shithot TEXT anthrox.txt file1 file2 file3 text bbs.txt\n \n  3> Write it to a disk to test.\n\n  4> Spread the Fucka!\n\n  NOTE: Some CrunchMode combinations will cause a CRC error.. So just stick \n        with one Cmode and all should be fine!\n\n                                            Signed:\n                                          Ice/Anthrox\n\n  Any Problems, Leave a message to me on any of these cool boards!\n\n  Call these cool Anthrox Boards:\n\n                     Martyrium WHQ   - +1-713-460-8217\n                     Fastrax USHQ    - +1-201-939-4543 \n                     Enterprise OZHQ - +61-3-312-5747\n\n  and all other Atx boards around the globe!\n\n  Call these other Cool Boards:\n \n                     Reign In Blood   - +1-212-409-5306\n                     Edge of Insanity - +1-708-499-4370\n                     Danse Macabre    - +1-713-324-2139\n\n  Greetings to the Following:  Hydro,Manx,Wintermute,Kirk,BlackCat,Vindex\n                               Voyager+family, Skol,Mymurth,Thargoid\n                               and all other ATX dudes out there!\n                               Micro,Ram,Assimilator,Warduke,Wormeater\n                               And all who I have forgotten!\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',14971,7,0,NULL,NULL,'atx_dmsa','scan',1780048410);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('atx_mess','ATX-MESS.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ATX-MESS.LHA','MESS','XIM','MESS',NULL,NULL,'ATX','\   \/    \       / |   |/       /  \ \/ / / _  \  /  \/  |_/  _   /  _/ __/    \  / /  \   \/   /   |/   |  /   \   \    //  \',replace('  __/\  _____________/|___  ________/\/\  /\\n  \   \/    \       / |   |/       /  \ \/ /\n  / _  \  /  \/  |_/  _   /  _/ __/    \  /\n /  \   \/   /   |/   |  /   \   \    //  \\n \___\  /___/\___|\___|__\___|\  /\   / /\ \\n- -- -\/=-==-===> PRESENT <===-\/-=\_/\/- \/\nMESSAGE SENDER !                JORDANJORDAN\n','\n',char(10)),'MESS.DOC',replace('         ANTHROX BRINGS YOU THIS TIME ** MESSAGE ADDER ** UTIL FOT /X \n         ------------------------------------------------------------\n                               \n       CODED BY I o for THE USS-ENTERPRISE BBS +61-3-312-5747 (SOON +1 412)\n\nDOCS + BETA TESTING BY KIRK/ATX\n\n1> WHATS IT DO?\n \n              Basically it will place a message at the bottom of your dir listing.\nIt has the feature to add this message to as many of your dir listings as you wish.\nIt will also convert your dir listing to upper case if you like.\n\n2> HOW IT ALL WORKS\n\n              Ok the programme is coded in 68000 making it is extremely fast\nso you can place it in your logoff batch, without a problem! It scans a config file\nyou create in the S: dir called mess.config. This config file tells the programme\nwhat dir to place the message in and wether you want the dir listing to be converted \nto upper case. Different messages can be added to each file listing.\n\n3> WHAT YOU NEED TO DO\n\n              1> Create a config file and place it in the S: dir \nThis config has the complete paths to the dir listing''s you wish to modify.\nIt also contains the file name of the file you wish to place in the listing and\na caps on/off option (below is an example of the one i use on my bbs)\n----------------------------- S:MESS.CONFIG -----------------------------------              \nCAPS ON = YES\nBBS:BRIDGE/DIR1 BBS:BRIDGE/BORDER.TXT\nBBS:ENGINE/DIR1 BBS:ENGINE/BORDER.TXT\nBBS:CARGO1/DIR1 BBS:CARGO1/BORDER.TXT\nBBS:CARGO2/DIR1 BBS:CARGO2/BORDER.TXT\nBBS:READY/DIR1 BBS:READY/BORDER.TXT\n*\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nThe border.txt is the file i place in the listing (more about this shortly).\nThe * at the end of the listing must remain there and shouldnot be deleted as\nthis marks the end of your confrences\n\n              2> The file MESS should be placed in your logoff batch.\nThis will scan the config and if files have been uploaded to a selected dir\nit will then shift the file (border.txt) to the bottom of the listing and will\nthen convert to upper case if you have selected that option.\n\n              3> You must create a text file you wish to place in the dir\nlisting. I have called mine border.txt (this can be named anything) \nOf course if you want a differnt message to be placed in differnt dir then\njust create differnt text files..\n\n------------------------- BBS:BRIDGE/BORDER.TXT ------------------------------\n[9m\n[42m>*<->*<->*<->*<->*<->*<->*<  MESSAGE FROM SYSOP  >*<->*<->*<->*<->*<->*<->*<[0m\n   FOR  ALL YOU PEOPLE OUT THERE WAITING FOR YOUR CONSOLE COPIERS  \n                       THERE HERE !!            \n                     \n\n  DONT FORGET TO USE THE MESSAGE BASE IN CONFRENCE 1 TO SELL UNWANTED GEAR\n[42m>*<->*<->*<->*<->*<->*<->*<  USS-ENTERPRISE BBS  >*<->*<->*<->*<->*<->*< I.O[0m\n[9m\n \n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nYou will notice the [9m at the start and end of the text file,these must not\nbe removed. as "MESS" looks for these to indicate the start and end of the file\nYou may have as many lines in the text file as you like\n\n4> NOTES + GREETS\n\n             We have allocated 300k of fastram for your dir listing.\n(this should be ample) if not suck my big Gutzo!\n\nHYDSTAR.....Hang in there we all love you!\nWINTERMUTE..Your a perverted barstard!\nPOT.........Samilog is number 1!\nVOYAGER.....Good to have you back in the team!\nWORMEATER...Good work son!\nTHRASH......Who are you ? talk to me!\nDREAMSCAPE..Bleeding bloddy barstards ahah nice chatting!\nVINDEX......Mega greetz!\nPOWS/TCB....Mega greetz! (i hope you like this one too)\nHOMEBOY.....YA IS YA REALLY BACK FROM DA DEAD?\nAND ALL MY FRIENDS AROUND THE GLOBE!\n\n\nFUCKINGS TO G.O.D FOR THE FAKER IDEA RIPP!                KIRK/ATX\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',28864,6,0,NULL,NULL,'atx_mess','scan',1780048410);
