|\n `:::::::::::::::|            | TONS OF ONLiNE MESSAGES AND MULTi-CHATS |\n  `::::::::::::::`------------+  NUP IS REQUIRED SO ASK WHOEVER POSTED  |\n   `::::::::::::::::::::::::::|    THIS ADVERT FOR THE NUMBER AND NUP   |\n    `:::::::::::::::::::::::::`-----------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',24415,5,0,NULL,NULL,'ax_mod_s','scan',1780048423);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ax_telnd','AX_TELND.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/AX_TELND.LHA',NULL,'XIM','telnetd.device',NULL,NULL,'AX','/ _ \|  \/  |_   _|  ___\ \ / / / /_\ \ .  . | | | | |__  \ V / |  _  | |\/| | | | |  __| /   \',replace('      ___ ___  ________ _______   __\n     / _ \|  \/  |_   _|  ___\ \ / /\n    / /_\ \ .  . | | | | |__  \ V / \n    |  _  | |\/| | | | |  __| /   \ \n    | | | | |  | |_| |_| |___/ /^\ \\n    \_| |_|_|  |_/\___/\____/\/   \/\n[------[ amiexpress.co.uk Presents ]-------]\n:                                          :\n.     Telnetd.device & amitcp setup        :\n.          for Amiexpress BBS              .\n.										   . 	\n:....:::   Visit Amiexpress.co.uk   :::....:\n\n','\n',char(10)),'help.txt',replace('On the WinUAE side of things, I imagine just bsdsocket.library needs to be checked. Though, other stuff like JIT and a ton of memory, etc etc are probably advisable if not needed. \r\rWith AmigaDOS, you need telnetd.device in devs: (the one I''m using reports version 1.-1..) Pretty sure it was from the amitcp.lha archive elsewhere on the forum. There''s a shareware version on Aminet, and that one isn''t it.. I''ll attach it to this message. You also (probably) need to mount the fifo-handler (38.4 is on Aminet, though isn''t that just a part of AmigaDOS? Huh.. anyhoo...)\r\rtelnetd.device needs to be configured with the file AmiTCP:db/telnetd-device.conf with the line "x y pacerate 19200 255.255.255.255" (assuming you want to allow all (255.255.255.255) ips access...) x is the port (telnet is 23) and y is the number of connections. (I haven''t tested past 3, but more might work..) pacerate is important for AmiExpress running on a fast WinUAE. It doesn''t seem necessary on (some) real Amiga(s). (I know of a guy running AmiX on a real Amiga and doesn''t need it..)\r\rAmiExpress just needs node(x)/serial/internal_unit.def tooltypes to be: serial.device=telnetd.device serial.baud=19200 serial.unit=x (x being node0, serial.unit=0; node1 serial.unit=1 etc) node(x)/modem/modem.def tooltypes: modem.init=ATM0S0=0 modem.reset=ATZ modem.ring=RING modem.answer=ATA modem.offhook=ATH1M0 These are important because telnetd.device ''emulates'' a modem with those Hayse commands.. And why pacerate is needed.. It sends a fast, unending string of ''RING <date>'' over and over.. AmiExpress sends ATA because of the ''RING'' etc.. Without pacerate, on a fast Amiga/WinUAE it goes so fast it clogs AmiExpress which just drops connection.. (my theory anyway).\r\rNote: internal_unit.def and modem.def can actually be named anything. AmiExpress just finds whatever file is in node(x)/modem or /serial\r\rTaken from:\rhttp://eab.abime.net/showthread.php?p=388479\rPosted By Paranoid','\r',char(13)),NULL,'auto-added',102723,2,0,NULL,NULL,'ax_telnd','scan',1780048423);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ays_sp10','AYS-SP10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/AYS-SP10.LHA',NULL,'XIM','S-CHAT.XIM',NULL,'SHATTERSTAR/ABYSS','AYS','RELEASED 25-12-93 @ 12:01 ABYSS :"HARD TO THE CORE!":',replace('[*> S-PAGE BY SHATTERSTAR/ABYSS <*]\n     RELEASED 25-12-93 @ 12:01     \n    ABYSS :"HARD TO THE CORE!":\n','\n',char(10)),'S-PAGE.DOC',replace('                          M E R R Y  C H R I S T M A S! \n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n                      [*> S-PAGE BY SHATTERSTAR/ABYSS <*]\n\n                           RELEASED 25-12-93 @ 12:01\n\n                          ABYSS :"HARD TO THE CORE!":\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n                            ****   Introduction! ****\n\n    Why another operator page door?     \n\n    Simple explanation!  The current existing operating page doors either did\n    not offer the features I wanted, or did not support the version of /X I\n    am running so I decided to coded my own.\n\n\n                               **** Features ****\n\n    - Coded in C!  No REXX stuff here! \n\n    - Coded with NO backdoors; however, I would not put it past some\n      asshole out there to append a virus to this executable (it will\n      run from the CLI but won''t do anything!) To be safe, SCAN these\n      files with VirusZ or whatever you use! I am not responsible for\n      anything that happends to your system since this door does nothing\n      else then what is described in this documentation file!\n\n    - Supports all processors from 68000 to 68040 (Special ''030'' version \n      enclosed in this archive).\n\n    - Defaults to comment to sysop when OPERATOR PAGE is disabled.\n\n    - Writes the page reasons to both the callers log and a special page \n      log that can be viewed with the correct security access (sysop \n      configurable with a seperate config file).\n\n      [No need to go through an entire callers log to see what someone wanted!]\n  \n    - The special log can be reset remotly. No text editors required!\n\n    - Carrier Detecting capability (no hangups resulting in lockups)\n\n    - Multiple Node Support (Hopefully! Not tested! But SHOULD work!)\n\n    - You can use your own text files for Operator Page On/Off/Aborted \n      Message(s) or if your a boring person, you can use the \n      use the internal defaults I have coded into the door.\n\n    - This door creates all of the files it will require for operation.\n\n\n                             ****  Installation! ****\n\n\n    1] Assign the root of the directory that will contain S-PAGE directory to\n       a volume called ABYSS! \n\n       Example of an assignment:\n \n       ASSIGN ABYSS: BBS:DOORS/   {Add this to your user.startup or whatever}\n\n    2] Copy the entire S-PAGE directory in this archive to the root of the \n       directory you have assigned as the volume ABYSS.\n\n    3] Add the following line to your BBS.CMD file (or CUSTOMCOMMANDS depending on\n       the version of /X you run [or creat A ICON for /X3.XX]):\n\n       >--] Start Snap \n       *O        XM010ABYSS:S-PAGE/S-PAGE.XIM\n       >--] Stop ^ Snap\n                   |> Make sure you SPECIFY ''X''.  This is not an Arexx door.\n\n    4] Edit the S-PAGE.CFG file located in the directory called S-PAGE in the\n       root of ABYSS (look at STEP 1 to see where this is).  The cfg file\n       consists of the following:\n\n                         --- S-PAGE.CFG BEGIN ---\n200	; Access Level Required to read and reset the private chat log. Must be\n    ; be in the format XXX. (i.e. security level of 30 is 030)\n                         ---  S-PAGE.CFG END  ---\n\n        Note: The only information read in is the first 3 characters!\n        All other text is ignored.\n\n\n                           ***   General Operation!  ***\n\n    The door basically operates in this manner.  \n\n    1. When an user tries to pages you, the door will check to see if the \n       operator page is enable.  \n\n    2. If it is not, the doop will display the text file called CHATOFF.TXT \n       to the user  and then passes the command for leaving a comment to the \n       sysop to express (if you are using a COMMENT door it will still work\n       with this door as well). If for some reason the text file CHATOFF.TXT \n       is missing, then the door will display the internal default message \n       coded into the door to the to the user. \n\n    3. Now if the operator page is enable, the door will display the text file\n       CHATON.TXT to the user and then prompt them to input a reason for paging\n       the sysop (4 characters mininum and 69 characters max entry is allowed).\n	   \n       If the user enters less then 3 characters for thier reason into the \n       door, it will display the text file ABORTED.TXT to the user and then \n       return to the main command line prompt of the bbs (You can use your\n       imagination on what o stick in the aborted text!) Also, as with \n       the CHATOFF.TXT text file,  if the CHATON.TXT text file is missing the \n       door will display the internal default text I have coded into it.  The \n       same also applies to the text file called ABORTED.TXT.\n\n\n                             **** Special Operation! ****\n\n    If you wish to use the special log that the door saves all the page \n    request to, you will need to create a file called S-PAGE.CFG and stick\n    it in the S-PAGE directory located in the root of ABYSS.  If you only\n    want to save the page reasons to the callers log, then do not create the\n    config file.  I have included a sample config file with this archive as \n    an example (use it if you like, it has been setup to allows users with an  \n    access level of 200+ to use this feature). If the config file is missing \n    the feature will just abort back to the main command menu of the bbs if \n    the user enters ''o l''.  When the log is viewed the user will be given the\n    option of resetting the log.\n\n    To view the special log, enter ''o l'' at the main bbs command prompt. You \n    MUST use LOWERCASE to view the log!  (Mabey in an update I''ll do a easy\n    conversion of the input to either uppercase or lowercase, but I feel lazy\n    at the moment.\n\n                           ****  Trouble Shooting! ****\n\n*   The door ASSUMES you have an ABYSS: assignment.  If you don''t then the\n    door will use all the internal defaults and the ''o l'' feature will be\n    diabled!  Also, all TEXT files can contain all the ansi color you want \n    and they MUST all reside in the S-PAGE directory located in the root of \n    ABYSS: (nice name huh?)\n\n*   This door should NOT crash! It has been tested for 2 months on my\n    bbs extensivily!  If it does crash, call my bbs and tell me what\n    the hell happened (and as they say at Microsoft Corporation "For\n    $79.95 we can offer a bug fix for that problem!" [just kidding]).\n\n*   The ''o l'' feature keep aborting. Is S-PAGE.CFG in the S-PAGE directory? \n    If it''s in your S: directory, go RE-READ the docs!\n\n\n                        ****  Future Enchancments! ****\n\n    - At some time in the next 3-4 months I might make an update to this\n      door if I get the urge to look ath the source code again; however,\n      if you have any superb ideas, please feel free to reach me at my bbs.\n\n\n                        **** Contact Information! ****\n\nIf you want to call and complain or make suggestions about this door, then\nfeel free to call my bbs.  The bbs ad will follow at the end of this archive.\nI also welcome coders to call and participate in the coders corner on my bbs!\n\n* NOTE: I will take request for special version of this door!  If you want\n        a custom version then contact me and we will discuss the details! \n\n\n                         **** Personal Greetings! ****\n\n        Special Greets to All My Friends in ABYSS and P:E:A:C:E!  \n\nSpecial Greetings extended to SMC & SKINDIVER for the excellent support a sysop\n                   can expect from a pair of co-sysops! \n\n  Special thanks to : Mack Lifeguard (Vegas huh? Are you a millionair yet?)\n                      Mst & DeCTon   (Cheese Pizza Kicks Ass!)\n                      Flyboy         (BRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRRR!)\n                      Greymalkin     (Where is your wardialer?)\n                      \n         Last but least! Thanks to all my users who took the time\n    to test this door out! I am sure those EALLS about getting deleted\n                   for not using it WOKE some of you up!\n\n -+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-\n                                               _ _.________.__.              \n                    ·                             |        |                 \n  .           __ . _!_____________________________|___.  \\|                 \n  :                 |                        .    :   |    |           !     \n _|/\_              | //      ·       .           :...|____|_ _.       :     \n  7: 7_____ _____ __|__ /\___ _____ _____ _____ /\ ___|_ __:__ _____ /\|__ _ \n  |  |~ _ ¬Y~ ___Y~ ___Y. _ ¬Y~ _ ¬Y~ _ ¬Y~ ___Y  Y~ _ ¬Y~ _ ¬Y~ _ ¬Y! 7     \n  |· |. | .|· |  |. _|_|: _ _|! | .|: _ .|¡ |  |: |. | :|. | :|. _ ·|· |___  \n  |! |: | .|¡ |  |: | ¬|  | ¬|· | .|: | ·|· |  |· |· |  |· | :|· | ·|. | ¬7  \n  |. |  | ·|. |  |· | !|. | ·|. | ·|· | ·|. |  |. |. | ·|· | :|  | :|. | ·|  \n  |  |__|  |__;  i___ ·|__| :|__|  |__|  |__;  |  |_____|· |__|! |__|___ .|__\n·-`--''  `--''        `--''  `--''  `--''  `--''     `--''   | `--''  `--''     `--''  \n  |              . _|      .   _          ·    .      |  :                |  \n  :       __ __ _:/ \____ ___ /¬\ _______ _______ ____|__|__ __ _.        :  \n                \________Y~  Y   Y~  _  ¬Y~  _  ¬Y~  _____/     __           \n                 |~  |___|·  _  :|¡  _  .|·  |  ·|____  ¬|     /_/\          \n     __          |:  |  ¬|.  |  ·|·  |  .|:  |  .|~  |  .|     \_\/          \n    /\_\         |!  |  .|:  |   |:  |   |.  |   |:  |  .|                   \n    \/_/         |·  |  :|   |  .|   |  :|   |  :|   |  :|                   \n                 |   |   |!  |  .|:  |  ·|.  |  .|.  |  .|                   \n        .___ _ __i____  ·|___|   |___|   |_______|.  ____|__ ___ _           \n                 |  |`---''   `---''   `---''   .   `---''|-Sd                   \n                 ·  |    .          ·             //  |  |                   \n      ·-- -- - --- -`---------------------------------''--- - - -·            \n                    :          +1 713 999 3640          ·\n \n CODER''S CONFERENCE - AX-EDIT BETA TEST SITE - ABYSS WHQ - P:E:A:C:E USHQ!\n\n              0-1 DAY WAREZ! - /X 2.39 - 530 MEGS - 96-14.4K\n\n OFFICIAL VOTE SITE FOR SWAP AND DANCE CHARTS! ALL ABYSS RELEASES ARE FREE!\n\n                SYSOP(S) : SHATTERSTAR, SMC, AND SKINDIVER!\n\n -+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',26134,10,0,NULL,NULL,'ays_sp10','scan',1780048423);
