INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('bk_ss152','BK-SS152.LZX','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/BK-SS152.LZX',NULL,'XIM','bk ss152',NULL,NULL,'BK',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,50247,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048428);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('bk_ss153','BK-SS153.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/BK-SS153.LHA','AmigaGuide','XIM','_|__  ___  __|_ |__/_ ___ ____ __ __ ___  2F',NULL,NULL,'BK','\___)(___\(___/ |   /(___\\   ''\ | /(___\ -. .------------------------------------------'' |            P r e s e n t s',replace('_|__  ___  __|_ |__/_ ___ ____ __ __ ___  2F\n\___)(___\(___/ |   /(___\\   ''\ | /(___\ -.\n.------------------------------------------''\n|            P r e s e n t s\n`------------------------------------------.\n    BK Sysdude Send v1.53 · Minor Update   |\n.------------------------------------------''\n| Features multiple-dir-sending, online help\n| selectable archive names, LHA/LZX/ZIP pack\n| and an `You sure you wanna send?'' request.\n`------------------------ - -- - - -  -- - -\n','\n',char(10)),'SS.guide',replace('@DATABASE "BK Sysdudesend.Guide"\n@master "Main"\n@NODE "Main" "BK Sysdude Send v1.53"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\n              _|__  ___  __|_ |__/_ ___ ____ __ __ ___  2F\n              l___)(___|(___/ |   /(___||   ''| | /(___| -.\n              .------------------------------------------''\n              |            P r e s e n t s\n              `---------------------------- --- -- - - - -\n\n                         BK Sysdude Send v1.53\n                             Aminet Version\n\n @{"      Explanation       " LINK "What"} .................. What is BK Sysdudesend ?\n @{"     Distribution!      " LINK "Distri"}.............. Read this too! Important info\n @{"          Why?          " LINK "Why"} ........... Why should I install this one ?\n @{"     Installation!      " LINK "How"} ........... How should I install this one ?\n @{"         Usage!         " LINK "Usage"} .............. How to use the bloody sucka!\n\n @{"        History!        " LINK "History"} ........ What has this thingy been through?\n @{"      Known bugs!       " LINK "Bugs"} .... Things you don''t have to bother me for\n @{"       Greetings        " LINK "LW"} ............. Other interesting information\n\n @{"      Bad Karma !       " LINK "BK"} ........ Who are they and what do they do ?\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "What" "What is this shit?"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\n                   What the bloody hell is Sysdudesend ?\n                 -======================================-\n\nYou might know the problem... Annoying users who want files that aren''t online\non the board. It happens all the time; Starting DOpus, searching through your\nHD (and it is a mess, right?), packing with LHA/LZX, finding the right dir to\nput your file in so the user can finally download the shitty thing.\n\nThis is the solution:\n\nBuy yarself a Magnum .44 and blow your head clean off... You are a lamer,\nthe lowest lowlife scum in the world. The world is far better of without you.\n(Aah.. I can still hear my teacher English saying that.. 8)\n\nNo, just kidding (in case you might haven''t figured that out by now).\n\n@{b}BK Sysdude Send @{ub}(short for Bad Karma Sysdude Send, if case you haven''t\nfigured that out by now) is a file sender (in case you haven''t figured\nthat out yet) with some really nice options (in case you haven''t figured\nthat out yet) and a real sexy look (you will not figure this one\nout), to give users files they want but you don''t have online!\n\nRight Right, I know you now are thinking ''Fuck you mate, all the bloody work\nto install some fucking crappy amos-doors'' but believe me, this one is worth\nit! (And it ISN''T amos!)\n\nJust read on to find out why...\n\n @{" Distribution " LINK "Distri"}\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "Distri" "How should I spread this thing ?"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\n                                 Distribution\n                               -==============-\n\nOkay, looks like this is going to be the only serious part in this doc :).\n\nWell, I enjoyed writing this door, but as you might know, there''s ALOT of \nwork coding such things and I don''t want my work to be worthless. That''s\nwhy I have decided to make Sysdudesend MAILWARE.\n\nThat''s right, you still don''t have to pay shit for using this program!\nJust don''t be lazy and let me know you are USING it! Just send me an\ne-mail or a letter or I don''t know what. (Letters can be sent to the\nPOBox mentioned in the @{" Bad Karma " LINK "BK"} part.\n\nOkay, look at it this way: the more e-mail I get (don''t touch that\nmassmail button, John) , the more encouraged I get for coding more\ndoors! So if you''d like to see some more BK doors coming from me,\nthen WRITE. Press that ''WRITE EMAIL MESSAGE'' button NOW!\n\nWell, what to write: Just say ''Hi I use it'', or if you have any\nsuggestions/bug reports -duh-/presents/17-year old sisters\nthen include them in the mail ;)\n\nOkay, thanks in advance to all e-mailers.\n\nMessages/Letters received so far:\n---------------------------------\n\n.----.---------------------------------------------------.-------------.\n| #  | Name of sender                                    | Receivedate |\n|----+---------------------------------------------------+-------------|\n| 01 | Gianluca Bivona                                   | 29-Jul-1996 |\n`----^---------------------------------------------------^-------------''\n\n @{" Why the bloody ''ell? " LINK "Why"}\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "Why" "Why should I use this shit"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\n                 Why the bloody hell should I use this one ?\n                -===========================================-\n\nWell, I haven''t got a clue.\n\n @{" Features " LINK "Features"}\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "Features" "Features of this shit"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\n                 What the bloody hell is this babe capable of?\n                -============================================-\n\nAha! All the nice thingies this door can do!\n\n *   AmiExpress v3.xx+ AND SigmaExpress compatible! [SELECTABLE]\n *   Password & Sysop-only protection               [SELECTABLE]\n *   Multiple File sending\n *   Multi Dir sending!\n *   Files-to-send overview                         [SELECTABLE]\n *   LZX & LHA packing of files\n     (With user-definable archive names & default packerpath)\n *   Online help at every point!\n *   Allows sending from RAM:\n     (Unlike some others who try to send from Ram Disk: !!)\n *   Extra security built in!\n\nYes! And what do you need to experience all these lovely things?\n\n * An Amiga\n * A Modem\n * A BBS-Program that ends on -express\n * A Kickstart 2.0 (do you know a nostalgic sysop running Kick 1.3??)\n * The ReqTools library (included in this archive)\n * The AEDoor.library   (also included, ain''t I a nice guy 8)\n\nThe ReqTools library is copyright by Nico François, but hey, who gives a\nfuck anyway, since Nico ditched his a4000 ?!?!\n\n  @{" How the bloody ''ell do I install this ??? " LINK "How"}\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "How" "How should I use this shit"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\n                   How the bloody hell should I use this ?\n                  -=======================================-\n\nWell, it''s very simple:\nFirst install it all. You can do it the easy way (Automatic) or the hard\nway. (If you want to be the local pain in the ass).\n\n@{b}Automatic Installation\n-----------------------@{ub}\n\nReally simple. Doubleclick the INSTALL_SYSDUDESEND icon & enjoy the computer\ndoing all the hard work!\n\n@{b}Manual Installation\n--------------------@{ub}\n\n @{"  Ami Express  " LINK "AXpress"}\n @{" Sigma Express " LINK "SXpress"}\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "AXpress" "Installation on Ami Express"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\n                   Installation on a AmiExpress system\n                  -===================================-\n\nThis one is real simple too (actually)! Just do this:\n\n * Look in the archive... There should be a drawer called COMMANDS in there.\n   Go into it. There is a subdrawer called BBSCMD and also enter that one.\n   Now copy the SS.info to you own BBS:Commands/BBSCmd drawer, adjust the\n   accesslevel (tooltype ACCESS=) and go!\n\n * Copy the BK drawer from the DOORS drawer in the archive to your own DOORS:\n\n * Adjust the configuration file using the @{"tooltypes" LINK "TT"}\n\n@{b}!*! NOTE !*!  YOU CANNOT PLACE THE DRAWER SOMEWHERE ELSE. THE DOOR IS HARDCODED\n              TO READ ALL FILES FROM THE DOORS:BK/Sysdudesend/ DIR!! @{ub}\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "SXpress" "Installation on Sigma Express"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\n                  Installation on a SigmaExpress system\n                 -=====================================-\n\nThis one is real simple too! Just do this:\n\n * Go to your BBS:COMMANDS drawer and locate the bbs.cmd file. Load it into an\n   editor and add the following line:\n\n       *SS       XM100DOORS:BK/SysdudeSend/SS.xim\n       | |       |  | `=> Filename\n       | |       |  `-==> Access level required to run the door\n       | |       `-=====> XM type of door (executable)\n       | `-=============> BBS command to start the door\n       `-===============> Command works on ALL nodes\n\n * Copy the BK drawer from the DOORS drawer in the archive to your own DOORS:\n\n * Adjust the configuration file using the @{"tooltypes" LINK "TT"}\n\n@{b}!*! NOTE !*!  YOU CANNOT PLACE THE DRAWER SOMEWHERE ELSE. THE DOOR IS HARDCODED\n              TO READ ALL FILES FROM THE DOORS:BK/Sysdudesend/ DIR!! @{ub}\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "TT" "Tooltypes for the installation procedure"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\nA list of all tooltypes and their explanation:\n\n@{b}PSW@{ub}            Here you can specify what password has to be used to start\n               the door. If not defined, the default password, 666 , will be\n               used.\n\n@{b}REQUESTER@{ub}      This is the alternative to the password routines.\n               If this tooltype is set, the password routine will be skipped,\n               and a visual protection will be ran. A requester will open;\n               This requester has to get closed within 4-5 seconds, or else\n               the door will quit. (This will prevent users from starting\n               the door and having the board hang the whole day!)\n               I prefer this method, because it is faster, and safer!\n               (Passwords are easily hacked, this will force the sysop to\n               be present!)\n\n@{b}DISPLAYFILES@{ub}   If this tooltype is set, Sysdudesend will first display\n               a list of the files that are about to get transmitted.\n               This will slowdown a bit, but will prevent you from\n               sending wrong files (cardlists etc 8)..\n\n@{b}PACKERPATH@{ub}     Here you can specify whether you want to use a default\n               packerpath or not. If you don''t specify a path, the files\n               will be packed into the currentdir. (This usually is\n               DH0: or DH0:WBStartup). If you want the files to be packed\n               somewhere else, this is the place to specify it. You can\n               enter pathnames here like RAM: or DH1:Pack/ or whatsoever.\n               When using subdirs, don''t forget the ending / !\n@{b}EXTRACONFIRM@{ub}   This tooltype has been added for the doubtfull people\n               out there. It gives you the chance to ABORT before sending.\n               @{i}Note: This tooltype is only valid when DISPLAYFILES is selected.\n                     You can''t abort the sending of packed archives@{ui}.\n\n @{" Usage " LINK "Usage"}\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "Usage" "Usage for this door"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\n                           Usage of Sysdudesend\n                          -====================-\n\nHow to use it:\n(Note: @{b}bold@{ub} text equals the door output at the explained stage)\n\nOn the menu prompt, you have to type SS to start the door\n(unless you renamed it). Depending on how you configured the door,\nyou will be prompted with a requester, begging to be closed, or\nyou will have to enter the password you specified in the tooltypes.\n\n@{bg highlight} BaD KaRMa @{bg text}@{fg highlight} Sysdude Send V1.53 @{bg highlight}@{fg text} By [-cR!SP-] in 1996 @{bg background}\n\nThe door will then prompt you with a filerequester, in which you can\nselect the files you want to send. Press OK to continue.\n\nNow AGAIN you will be prompted by another filerequester. This is the cewl\nthingy about the door. If you want to send MORE files (thus from other\ndirectories) then you can select them here (and you can keep on selecting!)\nIf you have selected all the files, just press OK (WITHOUT SELECTING A FILE!)\n\n@{b}Pack file? (y/N/?/a)@{ub}\n\nThe door will then ask you if you want to pack the files.\nIf you are sending an already packed file, select (n)o here.\n(Help is available here by pressing ? or H. You can abort with a/A)\nIf you press (n)o and you have defined the EXTRACONFIRM tooltype,\nthen you will be prompted whether you REALLY want to send the files\nor not. If you haven''t defined the EXTRACONFIRM tooltype, the\nsending will automatically start.\n\nNow, back to the packerthingy:\nIf you press (Y)es , you get the choise between LHA, LZX and ZIP.\n\n@{b}Please select the packer you want to use:\n (1) LHA/LZH\n (2) LZX\n (3) ZIP\n\nChoose: (1-3/?/a)@{ub}\n\nSelect the packer you want by pressing the number in front of it.\n(Help is available here by pressing ? or H and aborting is done with a/A)\n\n@{b}Please enter destination archivename : @{ub}\n\nThen, the door will ask you the archivename for the packer. Here you can enter\na name (with or without path/with or without archivetype extension)\n(eg: RAM:PACKED.LZX   or DH1:PACKED).\nIf you haven''t specified a default dir, the file will be packed into the\ncurrentdir (read @{"tooltypes" LINK "TT"} for more info). If you have\nspecified a default dir & the dir you entered here DIFFERS from the\ndefaultdir, you will be promped with the question if you want to\nuse the selected dir or the default dir.\n\n@{b}You selected a packing dir different from the defaultdir you specified.\nYou selected       : @{ub}<selected dirname>\n@{b}The default dir is : @{ub}<default dirname>\n@{b}Do you wish to use the default dir ? (Y/n)@{ub}\n\nPress Y here to use the default dir or N to use the selected dir\n\n@{b}Please wait while packing files...@{ub}\n\nThe files will be packed and send to the user using ZModem.\n\nVoila, the door quits with a ''ZMODEM DOWNLOAD SUCCESSFULL'' message!\n\n @{" Read me too!" LINK "LW"}\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "BUGS" "Know bugs"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\n                                Known Bugs\n                               -==========-\n\n * When using /X, the sending won''t work when the user has put his\n   setting to HYDRA. This is an internal /X bug!\n   (For /X users, i can only advice to use S!X, as it doesn''t have this\n    bug!).\n\n   When I get some updates of the /X (or S!X) doordocs that tell me how\n   to use external protocols, i will update BK-Sysdudesend to work with them!\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "History" "The making of .... "\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\n                                 History\n                               -=========-\n\n@{b}  v1.53       18.08.96          FOURTH PUBLIC RELEASE\n                                Some minor bugfixes here. Also added a new tooltype\n                                called EXTRACONFIRM.\n                                Also new is a memory allocated block for storing the\n                                filenames.@{ub}\n\n@{b}  v1.52        03.06.96         THIRD PUBLIC RELEASE\n                                Added new tooltype: PACKERPATH@{ub}\n\n  v1.51        02.06.96         Fixed a bug: BK-SS wouldn''t take the default value when RETURN was\n                                pressed on prompts\n  v1.50        24.04.96         Fixed another ZIP-bug. BK-SS would forget to delete the file after sending\n                                Added ''Abort'' option to menus\n                                Added online help\n\n  v1.13        02.04.96         SECOND PUBLIC RELEASE\n                                Fixed the extension buggy code: Now ANY extension may be entered.\n                                BK-SS will replace it by the filetypes extension.\n                                Fixed the ZIP-packing bug. Now it won''t hang the node anymore.\n                                Added ''Ram Disk:'' sending (failed because of space in ''Ram Disk:'')\n\n  v1.11        23.03.96         Added sysop-definable filenames option\n  v1.1         20.03.96         Fixing the layout (changed some colors)\n                                Smucking up the hotkey-code\n                                Added ZIP packing\n\n  v1.0         29.01.96         FIRST PUBLIC RELEASE\n\n  v0.93ß       15.01.96         INTERNAL RELEASE\n  v0.1ß        29.07.95         INTERNAL RELEASE\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "LW" "Last words from the author"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\n                =--------------------------------------------=\n                    This is a BaD KaRMa /X-Division product.\n                 All copyrights and that shit are irrelevant.\n                            Resistance is futile.\n                =--------------------------------------------=\n\n To contact me for any reason/bug reports/questions, try one of the\n following means:\n\n  * Call my  board @{b}Cybergarden@{ub} at +32-11-333703 (2ndz RD)\n  * On IRC,  check out #amielite to see if i''m there.\n  * E-Mail:  [email removed]                     (available now!)\n\n\n                                Greetings: (no order)\n                               -=====================-\n\n                 Crux / Flood / Hellfire / Outlaws / Purple Turtle\n\n                     @{b}Keep the scene alive dudes... you rock!@{ub}\n\n       Well some personal greetings go out to the following people:\n      -============================================================-\n\n-TCB!-       Dude, what''s up? Let us know when you are having your computer\n             fixed! Stay cewl!\n\nFRaNKy       Well, without you I wouldn''t have found some nasty bugs :))\n             Hope to see some more shit from you too :)\n\nRETI         For all his cool ansis and support on my board!\n\nMaLC0MN      For giving me the tip to change the door''s name from SYSOP SEND to\n             SYSDUDE send & for the hints/tips/moral support... Thnx!\n\nShane & SID  Yo dudes, we''ll get that CRUX demo division rocking soon!\n             Hope to get that intro working asap :))\n\nToxic        Keep up the good work & nail that little hacker scum! :)\n\nBoone        Yes! I started that Chippack and Yes! it''s going well :)\n             Still looking forward to hear some more mods dude!\n\nTrespass     Hi! Nice job on the intro & creator. Keep up the good work dude!\n\nEric The R.  Yo! This has been some time since we last chatted :).\n             Keep on running that board like hell & chat ya soon mate!\n\n#amielite    Keep on keeping cool dudez... you rule!\n\n@{i}Special Hi goes out to Gianluca Bivona for he was the first to send me an e-mail!\nThanks for the comments & help dude, you motivated me to continue this project!@{ui}\n\n @{" Bad Karma " LINK "BK"}\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "BK" "The BAD KARMA crew"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\n     .--------------- ------- --- -- - -- --- ------- ---------------.\n     |                                                               |\n     |  How To Get In Touch With bAD kARMA fOR :                     |\n     |                                                               |\n     |                   - Amiga/SNES/SEGA/GG/GB Backups             |\n     |                   - PSX/Saturn-Copies                         |\n     |                   - SNES/SEGA/GB/GG Backup-Units              |\n     |                   - Amiga/Console Support On *YOUR* BBS       |\n     |                   - Becoming A Member                         |\n     |                                                               |\n     |  IRC ............... : Channel #AmiElite                      |\n     |                        nicks  [FRaNKy] , [CRISP] , [TCB]      |\n     |  Leaders E-Mail .... : FRaNKy - [email removed]             |\n     |                        Crisp  - [email removed]              |\n     |  Regular Fan-Mail .. : Po Box 368                             |\n     |                        2800 Mechelen                          |\n     |                        Belgium                                |\n     |                                                               |\n     |                                                               |\n     |             Or Feel Free To Call Any Of Our Boards!           |\n     |                                                               |\n     |  WHO CARES..........[WHQ]......[4 NODES]........416-xxx-xxxx  |\n     |  DOXOLOGY...........[LHQ]......[2 NODES].......+32-16-xxxxxx  |\n     |  SKY TOWER..........[EHQ]......[6 NODES].......+45-748-xxxxx  |\n     |  METAL IMPACT.......[ HQ]......[5 NODES].......+32-15-xxxxxx  |\n     |  @{b}CYBER GARDEN.......[BHQ]......[2 NODES].......+32-11-xxxxxx@{ub}  |\n     |  NUCLEAR WASTE......[SHQ]......[2 NODES].......+46-xxx-xxxxx  |\n     |                                                               |\n     +--------------- ------- --- -- - -- --- ------- ---------------+\n     |                     bAD kARMA mEMBERS!                        |\n     |                                                               |\n     |  BIGOPHONE...............[-BELGIUM-]..................[JEAN]  |\n     |  BOONE...................[-SWEDEN!-]................[THOMAS]  |\n     |  CANDYMAN................[SCOTLAND!].................[STEVE]  |\n     |  @{b}CRISP...................[-BELGIUM-]...................[TIM]@{ub}  |\n     |  ENZO....................[-DENMARK-]..................[MIKE]  |\n     |  ERIC THE RED............[-CANADA!-]..................[ERIC]  |\n     |  FRANKY..................[-BELGIUM-].................[PETER]  |\n     |  MADBOY..................[-GREECE!-]................[KOSTAS]  |\n     |  MARWIC..................[-SWEDEN!-]...............[ANDREAS]  |\n     |  MALC0MN.................[-BELGIUM-]...............[KORNEEL]  |\n     |  MOSEZ...................[-BELGIUM-].................[STIJN]  |\n     |  NINO....................[-GERMANY-]..................[NINO]  |\n     |  PHANTOM.................[-BELGIUM-].................[CHRIS]  |\n     |  RETI....................[-BELGIUM-].................[FRANK]  |\n     |  TCB.....................[-BELGIUM-].................[DANNY]  |\n     |  TRESPASS................[AUSTRALIA]...................[DAN]  |\n     |  ZYNIX...................[-BELGIUM-]..................[TONY]  |\n     |                                                               |\n     `---------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n@ENDNODE\n','\n',char(10)),'{"ACCESS":")"}',NULL,120278,1,0,NULL,NULL,'bk_ss153','scan',1780048428);
