  g@@@]@@@@@@AM@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@@W.    !@@@WKWmW  -- M@@PV`     Ü\n    dA*@@W@@@@@A  ''**@8@@@@@@KV*@@7      V**WW@@mmWWMA ~f   .    |\n   dP,2Z*@@@@@@D     ''M@@@@@@fV- ''M   ,mmWm@@@@@@@@@''.      -   \ /\n ,mA @ \.M@@@@@@.       ''~Vf''''    ''    !~~M@@@M@@@~''~!           ·\n ,A- ]meWW@@@@@@@                           *@@@A~   ''           \n W`  d[@@@.Y@@@@W.                                        The Drøp Zøne !\n `   Am@@@W4@@@@@-              .                                \n     t@@A@@@@@@@M''              ! Y=.                     iF  µ aINT hERE\n    gfdM@@@@@@@@@                    `~`                         \n   d5WA]@@@@@@@@@s             ,.     ,.               µ aINT bEEN nøWHERE !!\n  ]@f []@@@@@@@@@@z.         V@@***N@mm@.       `c               \n     ''W@@@@@@@@@@@@W_                  *f     ,W  \.       fIND dA nµMBA\n      @@@@@@@@@@M@@@@m_                     , ''@. ''[             \n     d@M@@@@@W@P'' VM@@@Ws.                _-f !@- ,[          nØ nµP\n     @5g@@@@@@@f     V@@@@W_            g@@    W  /`             \n    ,b''~~**f ''@z       V@@D@Wmc___.   ,m@@@    ,g/         wALES fìNEST !\n .           ''*,       ''***~*''V@K[,z-*~VMA~~ ''~                 \n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',37107,7,0,NULL,NULL,'bstrip','scan',1780048435);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('btd_mc10','BTD-MC10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/BTD-MC10.LHA','MFM-Comment','XIM','MFM-Comment',NULL,'MFM/BETRAYED!','BTD','/////  \_   \ \_    \____  \..____/\  ___ _ _/    / __/__/    /   /   \:      \/ \    /    \_/    /  _/    /¦  B3TRAY3D!',replace('__ _ _/\___/\/\____/\_/\____  .             \n /////  \_   \ \_    \____  \..____/\  ___ _\n   _/    / __/__/    /   /   \:      \/     \n   \    /    \_/    /  _/    /¦  B3TRAY3D!  \n .:|\_________\____/______  /:|____/\  _____\n- -ø=slr==================\/==ø  PR3S\/3NTS:\n|¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯|\n|·MFM-Comment v1.0 by MFM/BETRAYED! for /X·|\n|Very easy to install,fast and good looking|\n|Auto Configuration/Built in Config-Editor!|\n|__________________________________________|\n \n','\n',char(10)),'MFM-Comment.doc',replace('                ------------------------------------------\n\n                     >>> bETRAYEd - we can''t die! <<<\n\n             bETRAYEd are back after some months of silence...\n\n  This time we present ''MFM-Comment v1.00'' for AmiExpress, Coded by MFM!\n\n                             Released 12-06-94\n\n                          (c)1994 MFM/bTd^iPl^SR\n\n                ------------------------------------------\n\n  >> Purpose:\n\n  This is a comment-door for /X and I suppose that you know how a comment-\n  door works!\n\n  >> Features:\n\n  · Fast\n  · Good Looking\n  · Auto Configuration\n  · Built in Configuration Editor\n  · Small code size\n  · It DOESN''T got a comment-counter :-) (Hi SiL)\n  · Built in check so that lamers can''t modify code/credits/version\n  · NO backdoors (Get it at an BETRAYED HQ/DIST to be 200% sure of no\n                  backdoors)\n  · Etc!\n\n  >> Sample output (WITHOUT fancy colors):\n\n  .----------------------------------------------------------------.\n  | [=] MFM-Cømment v1.0 [=] (c)1994 by MFM / BETRAYED ^ iPL ^ SR! |\n  +----------------------+-----------------------------------------+\n  | 1 MFM                | System Operator                         |\n  | 2 Rolemaster         | Amiga/Hacking                           |\n  `----------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n  Enter the number of the sysop you want to write to:\n\n  >> How to install:\n\n  Copy Commands/BBSCmd/C.Info to BBS:Commands/BBSCmd/C.Info\n  Copy Doors/bTd/MFM-Comment to BBS:Doors/bTd/MFM-Comment\n  Copy Libs/AEDoor.library to Libs:AEDoor.library\n\n  And MFM-Comment v1.0 is installed!\n\n  >> How to configure mfm-comment:\n\n  When you have installed MFM-Comment just load /X, login as sysop and\n  enter "C", this will start the configuration editor automagically! It\n  will look like this:\n\n                        ---------------------------\n\n  Some Board [1:NEW USERS] Menu (99997 mins. left): C\n  \n  Instructions for configure-mode!\n  ································\n  Enter all sysops/comments when prompted and then a configfile will\n  be automagically created! Max length for (co)sysop name is 18 chars\n  and 39 for (co)sysop comments. And the first name MUST be the sysops\n  because of logical reasons (See DOC). To cancel configuration\n  creation press enter on the "How many..." prompt.\n\n  How many sysops AND cosysops : 2\n  Sysop/CoSysop name: MFM\n  Comment           : System Operator\n  Sysop/CoSysop name: Rolemaster\n  Comment           : Amiga/Hacking\n  Configuration completed and saved!\n\n                        ---------------------------\n\n  Quite selfexplaining I think... The name of the config-file will be\n  "BBS:MFM-c.cfg" and the configuration editor will be started automagically\n  if this file doesn''t exist AND you got sysop access (255) (it will always\n  check that you have sysop access). You MUST enter the main sysop''s name\n  as the first name, as the door uses the internal C command instead of E for\n  the first sysop because C usually got lower access-level then E(Many LAME\n  comment-doors always uses E). To start the configuration editor even\n  when the config exists enter "C -c". You can also edit the config file\n  with any texteditor such as CygnusEd 3.5,  and it''s structure is exactly\n  the same as when you entered it in the built-in editor:\n\n  2                        <-- Number of sysops\n  MFM                      <-- First sysop''s name       \n  Ruler of the world       <-- Comment for first sysop\n  ROLEMASTER               <-- Second sysop''s name\n  Amiga, PC & Hacking      <-- Comment for second sysop\n\n  ## Easy eh?\n\n  >> Notes:\n\n  Sorry for lousy docfile but I *HATE* making docs and it was made in\n  a hurry...\n\n  >> How to contact the author:\n\n                  Post a message to MFM at these systems:\n\n    +46-26-124467      iNFiNiTE LiNK   (BETRAYED WHQ)   (NUP: IWILLUL)\n \n    +46-270-12138      REPULSE         (DOODLES^SHOCK)  (NUP: AMFETAMIN)\n    ++1-IT''S-PRi-VATE  CHAOTiC ENTiTY  (iNTERPOL WHQ)   (NO NUP)\n    ++1-IT''S-PRi-VATE  PSYCHO TERMiNAL (ENDLESS PiRACY) (GET THE NUP YOURSELF!)\n    ++1-IT''S-PRi-VATE  THE HOLE        (SKiD ROW USHQ)  (INVITE ONLY!)\n\n                       Or some other cool us-boards!\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',10212,4,0,NULL,NULL,'btd_mc10','scan',1780048435);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('bth_hc10','BTH-HC10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/BTH-HC10.LHA','HoldCheck','XIM','HoldCheck',NULL,NULL,'BTH','__/\____ _/   /_ _/\__ ___                ¦ ______   \   ___/__   /   / presents a XIM ¦ /  _¬ __/   /   /       / door to /X 4.+. ¦',replace('-bIS!       /\__      [ Kerosene/B÷thong ] ¦\n __/\____ _/   /_ _/\__ ___                ¦\n______   \   ___/__   /   / presents a XIM ¦\n /  _¬ __/   /   /       / door to /X 4.+. ¦\n/___¬   \ ___   /___/   / HoldChecker 1.0  ¦\n ______ /__ __ /______ /                   ¦\n      \/     \/      \/ A Total uniq door. ¦\n checks for hold uploads, and if its an    ¦\n hold upload then the door will write a    ¦\n message to sysop. Nice design.            ¦\n-  - --------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'HoldCheck.doc',replace('    ____.                      ____.\n    \  _|___ __________________\  _|___ _________ _____ .______________\n    /  __   \\_   _______   ____  __   \\_____   \\_   \|  ___  ______/\n   /    |    \    __|__/__  | /    |    \    |    \   \ \   \   \_    \\n  /     |     \   |      /  |/     |     \_  |     \   \ \   \_  |     \\n  \___________/_________/___|\_____|      /________/___|\     /________/\n- -- ------ -----------------------|_____/-skZ-----------\___/---- -- - -\n\n\n                    _/\_)  P R E S E N T S  (_/\_\n\n\n                           KeroPage  v1.0       \n\n                  ^ ^   By KeroSene / Bethong    ^ ^\n                   ^                              ^ \n\n\n                This program is freely distributed as\n                long as all files remain unmodified.\n                I will not take any reponsibility of\n                any problems that this program may cause.\n                (it shouldn''t cause any.)\n\n\n\n\nThis archive (bth-hc10.lha) should contain these files:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nName:                  Size:    Comment:\n\nDoors/Kero-HoldCheck/\n\n     HoldCheck         12536    The main file.\n     HoldCheck.info      888    The Icon Config File!\n     HoldCheck.doc      5209    This doc file...\n                            \nCommands/SYSCMDCmd/\n\n     EXAMINE×.info      1062    The icon file for checking the uploads.\n\n\n\n\nIMPORTENT!!!\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThis door is TOTALLY UNIQE! So you coders out there better not make a hold\nchecker only because the idea is cool. Its Copyright Kerosene/bTh.\n\n\n\n\nInstallation!\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nCopy all files from Doors/ and Commands/ to BBS: ... And then your\ninstallation is done....\n\n\n\n\nConFiGuration:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nHoldChecker.info:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nTooltypes: \nTO_NAME=<Sysops Name>, the users/cosysop/sysop that is going to recive the\nmesssage.\n\nREASON=<Reason>, the reason for the message.\n\ne.g:\n\nTO_NAME=KeroSene\nREASON=Another Hold Upload!\n\n\nWhat is it?!\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nIt''s a door made by KeroSene of B÷thong. Coded in C (SAS/C 6.55).\nIt checks for hold uploads. if the door finds a hold upload then it\nwill notify sysop by writing a msg.\n\n\n\n\nHistory!\n~~~~~~~~~\n0.1ß - Just a ßeta releze (non working shit).....\n\n0.2ß - New Output and it wont crash. (argh hate writing history).\n\n1.0  - First public releze.\n\n\n\n\n\n\nDo You Wan''t Me Something?\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nWrite a mess to me on Acid Attack or Future Entrance, and you will\nrecive a answer very fast!\n\n\n\n\n\nSpecial THANX to my ßeta testers!!!\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nAmon ·········· Cuckoo''s Nest\nDansken ······· Hall Of Fame\nVital ········· Future Entrance\n\n\n\nGreetings!\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nAmon/mst     ... Thanx for all ideas and ßeta testing!\n\nAquarius/otl ... Thanx for all the help with sending Olms etc.\n\nBiscrok/otl  ... Thanx for your logos!\n\nCray-1/acs   ... Thanx for the Includes, i''ll check the ansi colours!\n\nCrawl/ott    ... The nuker is coming =)...\n\nDansken/acs  ... Thanx for ßeta Testing my toolz, and some ideas!\n\nNeptune/otl  ... Thanx for all the structs & settings etc!\n\nRecall/ihs   ... Do you still suck as much as useal =).\n\nSkize!/led   ... Thanx for da logos!..\n\nTwister/ogn  ... Some cool ideas and ßeta testing!\n\nVital/tfa    ... Thanx for the help with the coding!\n\nVietCong/os! ... Thanx for da logos!?\n\nWingnut/sup  ... Yea sure, i''ll call your board..!\n\n\n\n\n               .:::.   M U S i C A L   S U P P O R T  .:::.\n\n\n\n                                 B-THONG     ^ ^\n                                              ^\n                        ^ ^    BAD RELiGON\n                         ^\n                              FAiTH NO MORE  ^ ^\n                                              ^\n                        ^ ^   MACHINE HEAD!\n                         ^\n                                  D:A:D      ^ ^\n                                              ^\n                        ^ ^      SLAYER!\n                         ^\n                                 PANTERA     ^ ^\n                                              ^\n                        ^ ^     NAiLBOMB!\n                         ^       \n                                BiOHAZARD    ^ ^\n                                              ^\n                        ^ ^     SEPULTURA                   \n                         ^\n       \n\n\n               .:::. C R E D I T S (Alphabetic Order) .:::.\n\n                            Amon/mst\n                            Aquarius/otl\n                            Bionic/ydl\n                            Biscrok/otl\n                            Boogeyman/gt\n                            Cray-1/acs\n                            Crawl/ott \n                            Dansken/acs\n                            Dildo/?\n                            Norad/led\n                            Punisher/dsr\n                            Skize/led\n                            Stryper/ydl\n                            Twister/ogn\n                            V-Cut/cls\n                            Vegas/otl\n                            Vietcong/os!\n                            Vital/tfa\n\n\n                   ^ ^   All who i forgotten   ^ ^\n                    ^                           ^\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',12546,1,0,NULL,NULL,'bth_hc10','scan',1780048435);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('bth_pa01','BTH-PA01.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/BTH-PA01.LHA','KeroPage','XIM','[KeroSene / Bethong ]----------[ KeroStats ]',NULL,NULL,'BTH','_____   _____   _____ _/     \_/     \_/  ¦  \_  Bethong presents ¦   --¦_/__   __/   ¦   |K',replace('[KeroSene / Bethong ]----------[ KeroStats ]\n  _____   _____   _____\n_/     \_/     \_/  ¦  \_  Bethong presents\n¦   --¦_/__   __/   ¦   |K\n|      ¦  ¦   | ¦       ¦r KeroPage v0.1ß\n¦   --¦¯\ |   ¦ |   ¦   :s\n:______/¯ ¦___: ¦___¦___¦  A Xim door to\n\n AmiExpress. A page door which let you to \n stop some user to page.\n[ GET THIS 100% BACKDOORED UTIL # NOW !! # ]\n','\n',char(10)),'KeroPage.doc',replace('         ____   _____   _____   _____   _____   _____   ____\n       _/    \_/     \_/     \_/  ¦  \_/     \_/     \_/    \_\n       ¦   -¦ ¦   ¦___¦__   __/   :   ¦  _¦_  |       :   ¦  /\n       |    -<     _¦_¦ |   ¦ ¦       ¦   ¦   ¦   ¦   ¦    ¯¯7\n       ¦__ -¦ ¦___¦   | ¦   | |___¦   ¦___    :___¦   |__¦   :\n          :___¦   :___¦ :___¦     :___¦   ¦___¦Krs:___¦  |___¦\n\n\n\n                       ::. P R E S E N T S .::\n\n\n                            KeroPage v0.1ß\n\n                    >>> By KeroSene / Bethong <<<\n\n\n                This program is freely distributed as\n                long as all files remain unmodified.\n                I will not take any reponsibility of\n                any problems that this program may cause.\n                (it shouldn''t cause any =))\n\n   I want to format all the boards! Install this tool to help me achive\n   my goal! hihajahjahahhhhaiahaiha!\n\nThis archive should contain these files:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nName:                  Size:    Comment:\n\nDoors/KeroPage/\n\n     KeroPage          ×××××    The main file.\n     KeroPage.doc      ×××××    This doc file...\n     denied.cfg            9    The Config file for KeroPage\n     denied.txt          274    The text for the "booked"....\n     \nCommands/BBSCmd/\n\n     O.info            ×××××    The icon file which will show Stats\n                                when you hit ''O''.\n\n\n\nInstallation!\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nCopy all files from Doors/ and Commands/ to BBS: ... And then your\ninstallation is done....\n\nConfigUration!\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nHow to configure the Pager... in the file denied.cfg you can add\nthe slot number of the user that you wan''t be able to page you!\nThen the file denied.txt will be shown.. And you can edit the file\nhow much as you like.....\n\nNo time for credz sorry!\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,20069,5,0,NULL,NULL,'bth_pa01_keropage','scan',1780048435);
