************\n\n*****************************************************************************\nTHIS TOOL IS INFESTED WITH - NAZI DEAMON v2 - BY CIRCLE OF POWER ! ! ! ! ! !\n*****************************************************************************\n\n*****************************************************************************\nTHIS TOOL IS INFESTED WITH - NAZI DEAMON v2 - BY CIRCLE OF POWER ! ! ! ! ! !\n*****************************************************************************\n\n*****************************************************************************\nTHIS TOOL IS INFESTED WITH - NAZI DEAMON v2 - BY CIRCLE OF POWER ! ! ! ! ! !\n*****************************************************************************\n\n*****************************************************************************\nTHIS TOOL IS INFESTED WITH - NAZI DEAMON v2 - BY CIRCLE OF POWER ! ! ! ! ! !\n*****************************************************************************\n\n*****************************************************************************\nTHIS TOOL IS INFESTED WITH - NAZI DEAMON v2 - BY CIRCLE OF POWER ! ! ! ! ! !\n*****************************************************************************\n\n*****************************************************************************\nTHIS TOOL IS INFESTED WITH - NAZI DEAMON v2 - BY CIRCLE OF POWER ! ! ! ! ! !\n*****************************************************************************\n\n*****************************************************************************\nTHIS TOOL IS INFESTED WITH - NAZI DEAMON v2 - BY CIRCLE OF POWER ! ! ! ! ! !\n*****************************************************************************\n\n*****************************************************************************\nTHIS TOOL IS INFESTED WITH - NAZI DEAMON v2 - BY CIRCLE OF POWER ! ! ! ! ! !\n*****************************************************************************\n\n*****************************************************************************\nTHIS TOOL IS INFESTED WITH - NAZI DEAMON v2 - BY CIRCLE OF POWER ! ! ! ! ! !\n*****************************************************************************\n\n*****************************************************************************\nTHIS TOOL IS INFESTED WITH - NAZI DEAMON v2 - BY CIRCLE OF POWER ! ! ! ! ! !\n*****************************************************************************\n\n*****************************************************************************\nTHIS TOOL IS INFESTED WITH - NAZI DEAMON v2 - BY CIRCLE OF POWER ! ! ! ! ! !\n*****************************************************************************\n\n*****************************************************************************\nTHIS TOOL IS INFESTED WITH - NAZI DEAMON v2 - BY CIRCLE OF POWER ! ! ! ! ! !\n*****************************************************************************\n\n*****************************************************************************\nTHIS TOOL IS INFESTED WITH - NAZI DEAMON v2 - BY CIRCLE OF POWER ! ! ! ! ! !\n*****************************************************************************\n\n*****************************************************************************\nTHIS TOOL IS INFESTED WITH - NAZI DEAMON v2 - BY CIRCLE OF POWER ! ! ! ! ! !\n*****************************************************************************\n\n*****************************************************************************\nTHIS TOOL IS INFESTED WITH - NAZI DEAMON v2 - BY CIRCLE OF POWER ! ! ! ! ! !\n*****************************************************************************\n\n*****************************************************************************\nTHIS TOOL IS INFESTED WITH - NAZI DEAMON v2 - BY CIRCLE OF POWER ! ! ! ! ! !\n*****************************************************************************\n\n\n\n\n\n\nThis archive should contain these files:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nName:                  Size:    Comment:\n\nKeroStats/Doors/KeroStats/\n\n     KeroStats         ×××××    The main file.\n     KeroStats.doc     ×××××    This file.\n     KeroStats.guide   ×××××    This file, but in amiga-guide format\n     S.look            ×××××    The look file.\n     S.info            ×××××    The config icon.\n\nKeroStats/Commands/\n\n     SysCmd/S.info     ×××××    The icon file which will show Stats\n                                when you login.\n     BBSCmd/S.info     ×××××    The icon file which will show Stats\n                                when you hit ''S''.\n\nKeroStats/MiscIcons/\n     FileStats.info    ×××××    The info file for FileStats.look\nKeroStats/MiscLooks/ \n     FileStats.look    ×××××    The look file, shows the filestats.\n\nInstallation!\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nCopy All files over to the right directorys, Doors/ to BBS:, Commands to BBS:\ni haven''t got any time to explain. \n\nToolTypes!\n~~~~~~~~~~~\nEXPERTMODE=<Your String>\n\nHow the output shall be when the user has Expert mode on.\n\nLAMERMODE=<Your String>\n\nHow the output shall be when the user has Expert mode off.\n\nRATIODSBLD=<Your String>\n\nHow the output shall be when the user has disabled ratio.\n\nRATIOTYPE.0=<Your String>\n\nHow the output shall be when the user has byte ratio.\n\nRATIOTYPE.1=<Your String>\n\nHow the output shall be when the user has bytes/file ratio.\n\nRATIOTYPE.2=<Your String>\n\nHow the output shall be when the user has file ratio.\n\nCHATON=<Your String>\n\nHow the output shall be when the chat-flag is on.\n\nCHATOFF=<Your String>\n\nHow the output shall be when the chat-flag is off.\n\nBEFORERATIO=<Your String>\n\nHow the output shall be when the ratio writes out.\n\nI.e:\nBEFORERATIO=1:\nthen the output will be:\n1:<Ratio Number>\n\n\nThe different commands!\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nA simple command looks like this:\n\n°UN8L\n^^^^^^\n|||||\n||||`-------> The text will be lefted, it can also be F, Free or R Righted.\n||||\n|||`--------> The OutPut strings length\n|||\n||`---------> The type of output, in this case the name of the user =)\n||\n|`----------> Pointing to the Userinfo. \n|\n`-----------> MetaChar\n\nand may output this: KeroSene\n\n\n°P7L\n^^^^\n||||\n|||`--------> The text will be lefted, it can also be F, Free or R Righted.\n|||\n||`---------> The OutPut strings length\n||\n|`----------> The type of output, in this case the programmers name =)\n|\n`-----------> MetaChar\n\nAnd WILL output this: KeroSen\n\n\nIf you are going to get the userinfo. Then it shall start with\n°U<Commmand><Length>L. U is the UserInfo. If you wan''t the Current date, time or\nthe programmers name. Then you shall NOT start with U.\nYou can also start with °U<Command>F, this will only allocate space for the length\nof the string.\n\nHere comes the different UserCommands!\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nCom:  Small Desc:               Long Desc:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n°UN - Alias/Name/Handle         The users handle.\n°UL - Location/Group            The users Location.\n°UB - PhoneNumber               The users PhoneNumber.\n°UR - SlotNumber                The users Slotnumber.\n°US - Security Level            The users Secerity Level.\n°UM - Messages Written          The number of messages the user has writen.\n°UT - Times Called              The number of logins.\n°UE - Laston Time/Date String   Last on string. i.e: Thu Apr 20 21:14:53 1995.\n°UU - Timeused (Minutes)        The total time that the user have used.\n°UI - Timelimit (Minutes)       The time limit.\n°UO - TimeTotal (Minutes)       The maximum time that the user has.\n°UX - Expertmode                Expert mode, configured in the Info file.\n°UD - Linelength                The linelenght that the user has.\n°UC - Computer                  The computer name =)\n°UA - AccessGroup               Name of it.\n°UP - ProtoCol                  The ProtoCol that the user has.\n×°UQ - Screen Clear              The Screen Clear flag, Defined in *.info.\n\n× Do not exists\nHere comes the different FileCommands!\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nCom:  Small Desc:               Long Desc:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n°FU - Uploads - Files           The number of Uploads in files.\n°FD - Downloads - Files         The number of Downloads in files.\n°FO - Bytesupload               The number of Uploads in bytes.\n°FW - Bytesdownload             The number of Downloads in bytes.\n°FL - DailyBytelimit            The maximum bytes/day.\n°FB - DailyByteDownloaded       The bytes/day downloaded.\n°FR - Ratio                     Ratio, may be a number or the Config i Info file.\n°FT - Ratiotype                 Ratiotype configured in Info file.\n°FC - Conference                The number of the conference.\n°FN - Conference name           The Name of the conference.\n°FP - Cps Up                    The Highest Cps.\n°FZ - Cps Down                  The Lowest Cps.\n\nHere comes the different SystemCommands!\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nCom:  Small Desc:               Long Desc:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n°SN - SystemName                The System name. Acp.info.\n°SS - Sysops Name               The Sysops name. Acp.info.\n°SD - Node Number               The node number which the user i logged in to.\n°SB - OnlineBaud                The Online-Baud.\n°SC - Chat-Flag                 The Chat Flag, Configured in Info file.\n×°SU - Chat-Flag-User            N/A (TheFlag = Avail for OLM/CHAT )\n°SV - /X Version                AmiExpress version.\n°ST - Total Systems Calls       The Total System Calls =)\n\nHere Comes the different Global Commands!\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nCom: Small Desc:               Long Desc:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n°T - The Current Time          The Current Time i.e 12:31:21\n°D - The Current Date          The current Date i.e 95-04-03\n°P - Programmers - Name        My Name =)\n°G - Programmers - Group       My Group =)\n°V - The Version number        The Version number of this Door.\n\nIf you don''t understand anything, delete the hole shit and carry on like\nnothing happend =]\n\nUsage!\n~~~~~~~\nThe name of the Command/BBSCmd/x.info must also have an existing look-file\nx.look, and a icon file. x.info.\n\nATTENTION!\n~~~~~~~~~~~\nIn your acp.info \n\nWhats New!\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nSome new commands, you can choose betwen F(Free) or L(Lefted) R(Righted)in\nthe look-file. If you have the command installed as S, then the Look File \nand Info file should be named S.Look, S.info. And lots of other shit to.\nThe BBS name is now clean...\n\nMore to come!\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nKeroWall     - A Normal wall, but i''ll Research of some cool features.\nKeroScript   - A easy script languane whick shall be used as a Newuser\n               Question shit. (Alomost ready =))\nKeroBBSAdder - Sorry about the name, but it shall be like bobo/mystic\n               AddBBSLogout, but NOT in arexx!\nKeroCA       - Conference Access checker (Hehe ask amon, his ideea) I have\n               started on this door so soooon you will be able to look at\n               it!\nKeroConfig   - Like the Internal W command, BUT more features. ( But the \n               fucking real name and Internet name are impossible, i don''t\n               have any struct for the file which name is user.misc =()\nKeroPage     - Almost like a normal pager... BUT this one alowes you to\n               skip some users from paging =) Started it...\n\nQuestion!\n~~~~~~~~~~\nAre i''m to egoistic?\nMaybe, but i must show that i Exists.\n\nSearching Members!\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nBethong searching members, Ascii artist, Coders, Traders, Dezigners, \nSysops & Boards Are you good at something above, Then You Are Welcome\nTo Join Bethong! \nWrite a mess to me on Cuckoo''s Nest or Future Entrance.\n\nDo You Wan''t Me Something?\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nWrite a mess to me on Cuckoo''s Nest or Future Entrance, and you will\nrecive a answer very fast!\n\nHistory!\n~~~~~~~~~\n0.1ß - The first ßeta version. All commands in a mess.\n\n0.2ß - Some systems commands. The Option F (Free) instead of L (Lefted)\n\n0.3ß - If you have the command installed as S, then the Look File and\n       Info file should be named S.Look, S.info.\n\n0.4ß - Easyier commands. More Commands. Some cleaner code. Unneeded\n       variabels was deleted.\n\n0.5ß - Som Commands were stupid so i fixed them =) Righted are also\n       exists!\n\nWell, do i releze a new version every day, hehe.\n\n\n                 ==-==( C - R - E - D - Z )==-==\n\n           AMON        - Sysop at Cuckoo''s Nest.\n           NORAD       - Sysop at Aces High.\n           ViTAL       - Sysop at Future Entrance.\n           TWiSTER     - Sysop at Flashback.\n           CLONE!      - Dezigner for some look files.\n\n*DO NOT RELESE THIS VERSION* ------------- *DO NOT RELESE THIS VERSION*\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                 .:::. G R E E T I N G S .:::.\n\n        AMON - ViTAL - DANSKEN - TWiSTER - SAVAGE - ZiN!\n        JURK - AQUARiUS - NORAD - FAX - NiGHTWiND - ODEN\n                TERMiNATOR - BOOGEYMAN - TOR\n                    NEPTUNE - CLONE! - NERO \n                   ALL MEMBERS iN BETHONG =)\n\n                 >>> All who i forgotten <<<\n\n\nAnd more will come!\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nJust look for da files who starts with bth- (Hehe)\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,25861,5,0,NULL,NULL,'bth_st05_kerostats','scan',1780048435);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('bth_wa02','BTH-WA02.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/BTH-WA02.LHA','KeroWall','XIM','KeroWall',NULL,NULL,'BTH','_____   _____   _____ _/     \_/     \_/  ¦  \_  Bethong presents ¦   --¦_/__   __/   ¦   |K',replace('[KeroSene / Bethong ]----------[ KeroStats ]\n  _____   _____   _____\n_/     \_/     \_/  ¦  \_  Bethong presents\n¦   --¦_/__   __/   ¦   |K\n|      ¦  ¦   | ¦       ¦r KeroWall v0.1ß\n¦   --¦¯\ |   ¦ |   ¦   :s\n:______/¯ ¦___: ¦___¦___¦  A Xim door to\n\n AmiExpress. A simple wall with some kewl \n featurse.......\n\n','\n',char(10)),'keroWall.Doc',replace('SIEG HEIL MEIN FHURER! \n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',20011,5,0,NULL,NULL,'bth_wa02','scan',1780048435);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('bull_21','BULL-21.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/BULL-21.LHA','Bulls','XIM','Bulls',NULL,NULL,'BULL','|               Show Bulletins Selectable  | ¦_/\___/\___/\___    for Every Conference  ¦ |\   /\ __/_  __/                          |',replace('+[ MYSTiC /X-DESiGN ]-----[ Bulls 2.1 ]----+\n|               Show Bulletins Selectable  |\n¦_/\___/\___/\___    for Every Conference  ¦\n|\   /\ __/_  __/                          |\n|/ Y \/_.¬\/  \  Added Features:           |\n/  | \\¬¦ \\  \\ o Cursor-Key Selection    |\n\__l_//___//__// o Use your Own Bull-Logo  ¦\n|dL!\/   \/  \/                            |\n+-[ EMPiRE/MYSTiC ]-[ XIM - /X 2.xx/3.xx ]-+\n','\n',char(10)),'Bulls.DOC',replace('\n                  ###### ###   ## ######  ### ######  ######              \n    _______|\     ###    #### ### ###  ## ### ###  ## ###       /|________\n   |         >    ####   ######## ######  ### ######  ####     <         |\n   | |¯¯¯¯¯|/     ###    ### # ## ###     ### #####   ###       \|¯¯¯¯¯| |\n   | |            ###### ###   ## ###     ### ### ##  ######           | |\n   | |_________________________________________________________________| |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |                             Bulls V2.1                              |\n   |                             ~~~~~~~~~~                              |\n   |                             TYPE:  XIM                              |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |                  ©1994 EMPiRE / MYSTiC /X-DESiGN                    |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |       LaSt OuTpOsT  +31-72-157682 & +31-72-201182  -  HOLLAND       |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |       AmixNet:  @NL0004   -   /X-Fido:  44:100/102     EMPiRE       |\n   |_____________________________________________________________________|\n\n===============================================================================\n\n PURPOSE:\n ~~~~~~~~\n  - Are You Getting Tired Changing 1 Bulletin and then Copying it to all\n    other Conferences, then This is the Tool for You!!\n    All Bulletins are now stored in 1 Directory so only one Bulletin\n    has to change to ''Show'' it in all conferences.\n\n  - This DOOR is a Alternative to the ''b'' command in /X 2.xx & /X 3.xx\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n REQUIREMENTS:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  /X 2.xx & /X 3.xx\n  It Won''t work with Ami Express 1.1x!!\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n INSTALLATION:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  - Copy the EmP_Tools Directory to DOORS:\n  - Edit DOORS:EmP_Tools/Bulls.CFG to your Needs.\n\n--start: cut here------------------------------------------------------------\nDUAL_LISTING       YES                 ; Use 2 Listings [YES/NO]                   \nCURSOR_KEYS        YES                 ; Use Cursors to select a Bull [YES/NO]\n[Init_END]====================================================================\nSystem Setup                                       ; bull1.txt\nTe Koop / For Sale                                 ; bull2.txt\n-                                                  ; bull3.txt Doesn''t Exist\nGameBoy & Nintendo Cards                           ; bull4.txt\nLastCallers & TopUps                               ; bull5.txt\n-                                                  ; bull6.txt Doesn''t Exist\n-                                                  ; bull7.txt Doesn''t Exist\nHST ASL & DS ASL Settings                          ; bull8.txt\nBBS Legal Disclaimer                               ; bull9.txt\nPrivate Bull #1                                    ; bull10.txt\nPrivate Bull #2                                    ; bull11.txt\nPrivate Bull #3                                    ; bull12.txt\nPrivate Bull #4                                    ; bull13.txt\nPrivate Bull #5                                    ; bull14.txt\nPrivate Bull #6                                    ; bull15.txt\nPrivate Bull #7                                    ; bull16.txt\nPrivate Bull #8                                    ; bull17.txt\nPrivate Bull #9                                    ; bull18.txt\nPrivate Bull #10                                   ; bull19.txt\n[BullNames_END]===============================================================\nXX------X----------                                ; Conference 1\nXX-X---XX----------                                ; Conference 2\nXX-XX--XX----------                                ; Conference 3\nXX-X---XX----------                                ; Conference 4\nXX-X---XX----------                                ; Conference 5\nXX-X---XX----------                                ; Conference 6\nXX-X---XX----------                                ; Conference 7\nXX------X----------                                ; Conference 8\nXX-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX                                ; Conference 9\nXX-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX                                ; Conference 10\n[CnfAccess_END]===============================================================\n[36m     ______________________  ______  ______________________________________\n     \____   \    /  \    /\ \    /\ \       \__    __\____\____   \       \\n     //  /   //  /   //  / / //  / / //  ____/\/   /\_//   //  /   /   /___/\\n    //     _//  /   //  /_/_//  /_/_//  __/_/ /   / ///   //  /   /\__   \__/\n  _//  /   //  /   //  /   //  /   //      / /   / ///   //  /   /   /   /\\n  \_______/\______/\______/\______/\______/ /\__/ / \___/\__/___/\______/ /\n   \______\/\_____\/\_____\/\_____\/\_____\/  \_\/   \__\/\_____\/\_____\/\n[34m  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n[Title_END]===================================================================\n--end: cut here--------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  - Init:\n    ~~~~~\n     Change to ''Y'' if you want 2 Output Lists otherwise change to ''N''.\n\n    BullNames\n    ~~~~~~~~~\n     These Are the Bulletin Names.\n     (1 List: Max 39 Chars, 2 Lists: Max 31 Chars)\n\n    CnfAccess:\n    ~~~~~~~~~~\n     Here you can Select which Bulletins can be Read in which Conference\n     for example:\n\n      Conference 1 is XX------X---------- then the following bulls are shown.\n\n                [1]  System Setup\n                [2]  For Sale\n                [9]  BBS Legal Disclaimer\n\n\n      Conference 4 is XX-X---XX---------- then the following bulls are shown.\n\n                [1]  System Setup\n                [2]  For Sale\n                [4]  GameBoy & Nintendo Cards\n                [8]  HST ASL & DS ASL Settings\n                [9]  BBS Legal Disclaimer\n\n    Title:\n    ~~~~~~\n     Bulletin Logo.\n     Keep in mind:  Max 20 Lines and 200 Chars/Line!\n     In Bulls.TXT are a few Logo Examples to choose from.\n\n\n  - If you have Fewer (or More) Conferences than the 10 above then you\n    can Leave them out (or put them in!).\n\n  - Create a Directory:  BBS:Bulletins\n    And copy all your Bulletins (from a Conference) to it.\n\n  AE 2.xx:\n  ~~~~~~~~\n  - Append/Join the BBS.cmd to BBS:Commands/BBS.cmd\n\n    Or add:            111111111122222222223333333333  <-- Position!\n              123456789012345678901234567890123456789\n\n              *B        XM001DOORS:EmP_Tools/Bulls\n\n  AE 3.xx:\n  ~~~~~~~~\n  - Copy B.info to BBS:Commands/BBScmd/\n\n    Or add to B.info ICON ToolType Info:\n\n      ACCESS=001\n      LOCATION=DOORS:EmP_Tools/Bulls\n      MULTINODE=YES\n      PRIORITY=0\n      STACK=50000\n      TYPE=XIM\n\n\n  - Don''t forget to Redirect Output Files from Others tools (in logOff.bat)\n    to BBS:bulletins and Not to the ''old'' BBS:Conference/Bulletins! \n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n USAGE:\n ~~~~~~\n  Just enter B on the MAIN screen in AmiExpress.\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n ERROR MESSAGES:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n  o ERROR:  Bulls 2.0 ONLY Works with /X 2.xx & /X 3.xx!!\n  `-------> Obvious\n\n  o ERROR:  BBS:Bulletins/bull{x}.txt Not Found !!\n  `-------> Bulletin {x} can''t be found in BBS:Bulletins\n\n  o ERROR:  DOORS:EmP_Tools/Bulls.CFG Not Found !!\n  `-------> Bulls.CFG can''t be found in DOORS:EmP_Tools\n\n  o ERROR:  UnKnown Keyword: XXXXXXXX in JoinCnf.CFG\n  |\n  `--> There must be 2 different KeyWords in the INIT part (Bulls.CFG)\n       Compare this with the original Bulls.CFG\n       Check that the KeyWords are:\n\n         DUAL_LISTINGS\n         CURSOR_KEYS\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n BUG REPORT & SUGGESTIONS:                                                                   \n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  It''s possible that a mistake will occure.... Nobody is Perfect.\n  If you have any Suggestions or Comments Please Leave a Message on my Board:\n\n   LaSt OuTpOsT  N1: +31-72-157682  N2: +31-72-201182  -  HOLLAND\n   ~~~~~~~~~~~~  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~     ~~~~~~~\n       AmixNet:  @NL0004   -   /X-Fido:  44:100/102   EMPiRE\n       ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~       ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~   ~~~~~~\n\n===============================================================================\n\n NOTE:\n ~~~~~\n  o This Program Has been tested on a /X 2.0 - 3.37 Configuration.\n\n  o If a User uses More lines then the sysop can see the Screen-Output on\n    the Sysop-side will be scrambled caused by the Ansi-Handling but on\n    the Users-side it will be ok!!\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n REGISTRATION:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  If YOU use this Program please let me know by Calling Last Outpost or\n  to send me a Message by NetMail @NL0004 - EMPiRE  Coz we want to know\n  how many Sysops are using our Tools!!!\n \n\n===============================================================================\n\n HISTORY:\n ~~~~~~~~\n  V0.1  11-07-92 - Internal Version\n\n  V1.0  02-03-93 - Release Version\n\n  V1.1  03-20-93 - Added The 2 OutputList Option\n                 - Added Support for .txt.gr Files\n                 - [Bulls.CFG CHANGED!]\n\n  V1.2  05-05-93 - Added ''Non-Stop'' Menu Showing, if you got too many Bulls\n                   then the irritating ''More (Y/n/ns)'' appeared... FIXED\n                 - Cleaned Up.\n        06-21-93 - Fixed a small Error found with the RexxDoorDebugger.\n\n  V2.0ß 01-01-94 - ReWritten to XIM!\n        01-13-94 - Better Bulls.CFG reading\n                 - Added some more Ansi Colors\n                 - Changed the Bulls.CFG layout (same layout as JoinCnf.CFG).\n                   It''s now also possible to use your Own Bulletin Logo\n                   [Bulls.CFG CHANGED!]\n        01-14-94 - Bug Report from JPS\n                    o When using Bull [00] it was possible to press different\n                      <SHIFT>-keys to show it.. FIXED\n        01-17-94 - When Bulls is run, it will ShowUp on the Server.\n        01-25-94 - Fixed the ''10-Node'' BUG\n\n  V2.0  01-29-94 - Release\n\n  V2.1ß 02-05-94 - Change the ''Full Use of 80 Chars/Line'' to 79 Chars/Line\n                   because some Terminals on Amiga/PC can''t handle the 80th\n                   character right (extra linefeeds)!\n        02-07-94 - Bug Report from B.O.B/CF & Enzo:\n                    o When using NON-Ansi the character color will change to\n                      Magenta when exiting/using Bulls.\n                      There were 2 ESC-chars after eachother in the command-\n                      line which /X doesn''t like... FIXED!\n        02-28-94 - Added Cursor-Key Support. To Include this the Bulls.CFG\n                   changed:\n                    o Bull0.txt support has been deleted, so change your\n                      Bull-Access!\n                 - [Bulls.CFG CHANGED!]\n        03-20-94 - Optimized some code.\n        03-24-94 - Added some Suggestions from SpeedDevil/Partek:\n                    o When starting Bulls the BullSelection >[]< will now\n                      be disabled until an ArrowKey is pressed or a Bull is \n                      selected.\n                    o After showing a Bulletin pressing <ENTER> will show\n                      the Bulletin-List again and not Quit Bulls anymore.\n                      So it''s now only possible to Quit Bulls in the\n                      Bulletin-List.\n\n  V2.1  04-13-94 - Release\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n EMPiRE /X DOORS/UTILS COLLECTION UNTIL NOW!:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  - AboStats V0.2                        AIM Door\n  - AE2PCE V1.0                          CLI Util\n  - AutoOnline V1.2                      XIM Door/Util\n  - Bulls V2.1                           XIM Door\n  - CheckDir V1.0                        CLI Util\n  - CheckNU V1.0                         XIM Door\n  - ConfAccess V1.1                      ServerUtil\n  - CopyDate V1.3                        CLI Util\n  - DlDir V2.0                           XIM Door\n  - DoorKIT 1.01                         XIM Doors/Includes\n  - DMenu V1.0                           AIM Door\n  - DutchNET V1.0  [AmiXnet]             AIM Door\n  - Front V2.0                           XIM Door\n  - JoinCnf V3.5                         XIM Door\n  - LastCalls & TopUps V1.2              LogOffUtil\n  - LastDL V0.1                          LogOffUtil\n  - LastUL V0.1                          LogOffUtil\n  - MakeFree V1.1                        AIM Door\n  - MemberList V1.0                      AIM Door\n  - MonthTopUp V2.0                      ServerUtil\n  - MultiNodeLastCaller V1.1             LogOffUtil\n  - Page V2.1                            XIM Door\n  - PMail V1.1                           AIM Door\n  - Remote Maintenance V1.3              AIM Door\n  - SceneTalk Voter V2.3                 AIM Door\n  - SceneTalk Voter V2.2 [Party]         CLI Door\n  - SecLevChk V1.0                       ServerUtil\n  - Sent FrondEnd 1.0  [Sent_FE]         XIM Door\n  - StripCR V1.0                         CLI Util\n  - SysopCommands V1.0                   AIM Door\n  - UserData Cleaner/Repair V2.0         ServerUtil\n  - UserStats V2.0                       ServerUtil\n  - UsrCnfAx V1.1                        CLI Util\n  - View & Check Archive/Text V1.7       AIM Door\n  - WhoNode V1.3                         AIM Door\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n THANX MUST GO TO ALL OFFICIAL BETA-TESTERS:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n   Tycoon/Mystic             [Channel X]\n   JPS                       [Red October]\n   Sal-One/TRSi              [BoonDocks]\n   Sharon/5D                 [The Unknown]\n   Blue Bird/Mystic          [Tau Ceti]\n   Easy Rider/Mystic         [Mamba]\n   Mega Fortress             [MF Enterprise]\n   Beast/Partek              [Sequencial]\n   SpeedDevil/Partek         [Rising Sun]\n   Galaxy                    [Ulixys]\n\n\n GREETZ/TNX GO TO:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n   Killraven/MST /X-DESiGN - For giving me sum Great Pointers/Sources on ''C''\n   CrackDown/MST /X-DESiGN - Nice Doors, Keep it up!\n   ByteAndi                - Tnx for all ya ''C'' Help & Sources!\n   JAF/G.O.D.              - For some good REXX ideas\n   Bad Sector/Hidden       - Still Using your Sort-Routine. It''s the Fastest!\n   B.O.B./CyberForce       - For (Mis)Using/Testing my tools! :)\n   Aragorn/Vision          - Tnx for Testing in the past\n   Camelot/Complex         - Tnx for Testing in the past\n   Telekinetic/T.F.A.      - Tnx for Testing in the past\n   Alcoholic               - Tnx for Testing in the past\n   Price/T.F.A.            - Great job on your {F}ull {S}creen {E}ditor!\n   Van Damme               - Nice Doors!!!\n   DR.G/IBB                - Hope to see Check''N Add work on a 040\n   SiGMA SEVEN             - Nice job on SiGMA-EXPRESS! Tempted to ''Convert''\n   911/Movement            - Tnx For ya Ansi Logo''s!! You''re the Greatest!\n   Mike                    - Tnx for calling!\n   Amicom/TRSi             - Tnx for calling!\n   SkIn                    - Tnx for ya Description Logo! Looks Great!!\n   Shadow Man/S8           - Nice Doors & Tnx for ya greetz! & Calling ofcoz\n   [MAZ!^PHAZE]            - Tnx for calling!\n   Shuyuki Tanaka          - Tnx for your Messages!\n   AGONY/cOmpLeX           - Tnx for calling!\n   HUMANOiD & jABBA /MST &\n    SCANDAL                - Tnx for calling!\n   LECTOR                  - Tnx for your NetMail\n   Koo Koo Ka Choo         - Tnx for calling!\n   TaRzAN                  - Tnx for your NetMail. Yezz 040 Speed Rulez!!\n   Crayor/Scx              - Tnx for calling!\n   Foxx''n''Lynxx            - Tnx for your BugReports!!!\n   ThE BiRD                - Tnx for your NetMail on UsrCnfAx\n   Dux                     - Tnx for your NetMail\n   dR.dRE!/fAITH           - Tnx for da greetz, Nice Doors btw\n   [-RUNT&SCOTTIE-]        - Tnx for calling!\n   sPAcEcAKe/aF            - Tnx for calling!\n   Freddy Kreuger/GOD      - Tnx for your NetMail on JoinCnf 3.2\n   MF1                     - Tnx for calling!\n   AtomiX/N.A.S.A          - Hope the ''C'' archive was sume help for ya!\n   MAD HARLEQUiN [ITPH01]  - Tnx for your Nice AmiXnet Messy''s\n   Mike Hoffren  [SF0001]  - Tnx for the BugReport on JoinCnf 3.3 [100+ Cnfs]\n   Galaxy/TFA              - Nice job on da SentCleaner\n   SvEN tHE CREAToR/5D     - ''Tnx'' for forcing me to use Cursor-Keys!\n   Diogenes/TPY/5D         - Tnx for calling and for your BugReport!\n\n   & Ofcoz to ALL MYSTiC Members all over the Globe!\n\n\n                        ______  __________________   