LLAND:          +31-72-157682  &  +31-72-201182             :HOLLAND\n\n','\n',char(10)),'{"ACCESS":"001","LOCATION":"DOORS:EmP_Tools/Bulls","PRIORITY":"0","STACK":"50000","TYPE":"XIM"}','auto-added',22351,1,0,NULL,NULL,'bull_21','scan',1780048435);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('bulls','BULLS.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/BULLS.LHA','bulls','XIM','Bulls',NULL,NULL,NULL,'____\        /___\   ____  /____/ ___/______ _     \l      _  \_______ ____\/       __l_________  __l__       l ___',replace('    __________   ___________     _____\n____\        /___\   ____  /____/ ___/______\n               _     \l      _  \_______\n____\/       __l_________  __l__       l ___\ng®m /________)   e^D \_____)   (_________)\n          «« m e g a s t y l e  »»\n               ...presents...\n \n                 Bulls v1.5\n \nNEW and IMPROVED Bulletin-viewer for /X+S!X.\n[ISDN]-÷ LEECHED FROM ZONE-ONE-BBS ÷-[ISDN] \n','\n',char(10)),'Bulls.GUIDE',replace('@database "mEGAZTYLE.guide"\n@node MAIN\n@title "                                              »«  m e g a s t y l e  »«  r u l e s  »«"\n@{b}\n                              @{u}m e g a s t y l e@{uu}\n\n                 ________   _________   _________     ______.\n           ______\      /___\  ___  /___\  ___  /_____\____ l____\n     ______\              _     l/    _    \l     _     __/     /_______\n.___(       \____\/     __l__  _______l_______  __l__   \l_____/        )___.\n|                /______)   (_____/        \____)   (____\                  |\n|                                                                           |\n| g®m      _____      ___.           .______   ___.       _________     e^D |\n|___  ____/ ___/______\  l___________|     /___\ _l_______\  ___  /____  ___|\n   (__\   \______   _    __/     _   l       _   \      _     l/      /__)\n       \__      l __l__  l     __l_______  __l_        _l_  _________/\n         (________)   (________)     \_____)  (________) (_____/ @{ub}\n\n\n\n@{fg shine}                  p r e s e n t s   a   n e w   d o o r :@{fg text}\n\n\n                      @{b}    @{bg shine}@{u}  B u l l s   1 . 5  @{bg back}@{ub}@{uu}\n\n\n\n\n              @{"           d o c u m e n t a t i o n           " link index}\n\n\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node index\n@title "                                             »» i n d e x ««"\n\n\n    @{u}                                                          @{uu}\n\n\n@{b}                                                               ½½½½½  ½½½½½\n                                                               ½½½½½  ½½½½½\n                                                               ½½½½½  ½½½½½\n                                                               ½½½½½  ½½½½½\n                                                               ½½½½½  ½½½½½\n         ____        __________          ____.   ___________   ½½½½½  ½½½½½\n________(___/________\ __     /__________\___l___\  ____   /__    `½½½½''\n                   _   l/       _      _____/  _      l/      ½½½½½½  ½½½½½½\n_____            __l___/      __l__    l     __l__  __________½½½½½½  ½½½½½½\n    (____________)    /_______)   (__________)   (_____/      ½½½½½½  ½½½½½½\n                                                              ½½½½½½  ½½½½½½\n                                                              ½½½½½½  ½½½½½½\n   @{fg shine} @{"            introduction             "  link introduction      }    @{fg text}                ½½½½½½  ½½½½½½\n@{fg shine}    @{"            installation             "  link installation      }          @{fg text}          ½½½½½½  ½½½½½½\n@{fg shine}    @{"              how 2 use              "  link how 2 use         }\n    @{"              copyright              "  link copyright         }\n    @{"          changes ÷ history          " link changes ÷ history  } @{ub} @{fg text}\n\n\n    @{u}                                                          @{uu}\n\n\n@endnode\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n@node introduction\n                                                                 .\n\n                                                                 :\n                                                                 :\n             __________________.______.      ________            :\n          ._(___)_.   ___     _|      l_____\\_     /____________:_ _\n          |       |----/      \        /     \   __/\      __    :\n          l_______|   /_______/        |-----/_______\____       :\n                              l________|(rLf)            /-------:-\n                                                                 :\n                                                                 :\n                                                                 :\n                                                                 .\n\n\nBulls v1.5 is a handy utility to show different bulletin-textfiles to the\nAmiExpress server. However, it does differ from other bulletin-viewers in\nseveral ways. More features included, and full support of the MCI-interface has\nbeen implanted to try to make this door the best around.\n\n\nThe main reason why I coded this door is that most of the other doors I''ve tried\nout have had a aweful design, bad cursor reading, poor display-routines and some\nvery-very (Sysop) unfriendly configuration possibilities.\n\n\nSince I didn''t like the ones I got hold of from others, I started to code\nsomething for my own sake. - And this is it! :)\n\n\nI''m currently working on Bulls v2.o which I hope will be even better than this\nversion. I coded this before I started on the Zippy-Search, so... Much can be\nimproved in future releases, and all registered users WILL notice the benefit\nof it! :)\n\n\n           - - - --- ------[ lizard of megastyle! ]------ --- - -  -\n\n@endnode\n\n\n\n\n\n\n@node installation\n\n .\n                                                                              .\n :\n :                                                                            :\n : __        _____ .___.   ______ __.              _________. ____________    :\n_:(__)_______\_ _/_|_  l___\__  // _l______.  _____\__  //  l____)_  _   /____:_\n :    | __    /_  _ /   /     _ // \     /_l__\__     _ //   /    |_    / ___ :\n_:____|--/   /-/  //    |--/____/----/__/ \     /--/____/    |____|/---/\--/  :\n :      /___/ /___/_____|(rLf)          \---/__/       l_____|            /___:_\n :                                                                            :\n :                        i n s t a l l a t i o n                             :\n .                                                                            :\n                                                                              .\n\n@{fg shine}To install...@{fg text}\n\n\n\nAll you have to do is to copy each of the files in this archive to its\nbelonging directory under "BBS:".\n\nThat''s all... (Simple isn''t it? :)\n\n\n\nConfiguration :\n---------------\n\nThere is only one way to configurate this door, and that is through the\nBulls.info icon. If you, from workbench, use information on this icon, you''ll\nsee several different Tooltype strings.\n\nFirst of all you''ll have to configurate where to locate your BullX.TXT-files.\nThis is done by changing the PATH followed with a "/" to the "BULLETINS_PATH="\ntooltype.\n\nThen you''ll have to state how many bulletin-lines to be included in the \nbulletin-list. Do not write more than the total amount of Bulletin-lines.\n\nUse the tooltype BULLETIN.x=<name> to declare the bulletin-lines, where "x"\nis the line-number and <name> is the name of the Bulletin-Door to be showned.\n\nThe tooltype CONFSHOW.x=<parameters> is used to set up in which conference the\nBulletin-Door is to be displayed in. Remember that the "x" is the line-number\nto the belonging Bulletin-Door. These parameters is set up like this:\n\n\nCONFSHOW.x=xxxxxxxxxxxxoxo....etc...etc..\n\n#confnr :  123456789012345...etc...etc..\n           000000000111111......etc...\n\nAs you can see, each "x" or "o" represent a conference-number. "x" means that\nthe Bulletin-Door will be displayed in this colume''s conference-nr. And "o" \nmeans that the Bulletin-Door will be suppressed in this conference, and will\nnot be displayed on the bulletin-list.\n\n2 simple examples to get your minds going crazy :\n\nCONFSHOW.1=xo  - Set up that Bulletin-Door #1 will be showned in Conf #1, but\n                 not in Conf #2.\n\nCONFSHOW.1=ox  - Set up that Bulletin-Door #1 will NOT be showned in Conf #1,\n                 but will be visible in Conf #2.\n\n\n\nHere is an example of how to set up this BULLS.INFO-icon :\n\n-------------------------- Cut Start Here! --------------------------\n\nBULLETINS_PATH=BBS:BULLETINS/\nANTBULLETINS=9\nBULLETIN.1=AMFETAMIN\nCONFSHOW.1=xxxxxxxxxxxxoxo\nBULLETIN.2=Quick-New\nCONFSHOW.2=oxxxxxxxxxxxoxo\n.\n.\n.\n.\n\n\n--------------------------- Cut End Here! ---------------------------\n\n\nThen you''ll have to make small bulletin-textfiles. These can include standard\nMCI-functions (~) aswell as ordinary text and ANSI-codes.\n\nEach Bulletin-file must have a filename like this "BULLx.TXT", where "x" is the\nmatching bulletin-line number. And the files must exist in the BULLETINS_PATH-\ndrawer. Otherwise none of the bulletins will be showned.\n\n\n\nHere is an example of how to set up such a "BULLx.TXT"-textfile :\n\n--------------------------------- cut start ---------------------------------\n\n~SS_BBS:Screens/Amfetamin.txt \n\n---------------------------------  cut end  ---------------------------------\n\nOr you can use : ~CC_BestUl to launch commands etc...\n\n\n\n Megastyle! is not to held responsible if this program should cause any damage\n to your computer or lead to loss of data. It is provided as is, and is being\n installed and used on your own risk. There is no installer-script provided\n together with the UNREGISTERED versions of the Megastyle! productions!\n\n\n@endnode\n\n\n\n\n\n@node how 2 use\n@title "                                              )>» h o w  2  u s e «<("\n\n                                      ½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½.\n                                     ½½½½½½½½         ½½½½½½½½\n      ____.            _________         _______      ½½½½½½½½\n   ___\ __l____________\       /_________\     /______½½½½½½½½\n   \    \___        _             _      /\           ½½½½½½½½\n    \______/      __l__    "    __l__           ___   ½½½½½½½½\n          /_______)   (_________)   (___________) /_  ½½½½½½½½\n                                                   |  ½½½½½½½½\n                ½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½''\n                ½½½½½½½½                           |    |\n                ½½½½½½½½                           |    |\n                ½½½½½½½½                           |    |\n                ½½½½½½½½      ._____      _____    |   _|________\n                ½½½½½½½½______|    /_____/ ___/____|___\  ____  /___\n                ½½½½½½½½      |       _  \_______   _       l/     /\n                ½½½½½½½½__    l     __l__       l __l__  _________/\n                ½½½½½½½½ (__________)   (_________)|  (____/\n                ½½½½½½½½                           |    |\n                ½½½½½½½½                           |    |\n                ½½½½½½½½  @{fg shine}   h o w       u s e  @{fg text}   |  ½½½½½½½½\n                ½½½½½½½½      @{fg shine}       2    @{fg text}         |  ½½½½½½½½\n                ½½½½½½½½                           |  ½½½½½½½½\n                ½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½\n\n\n\n     Just @{"Install" link installation} it and run it from /X or S!X.\n\nUse the command "B" at the main prompt, and you may include the correct\nBulletin-number to view a Bulletin-file right away.\n\n\n\n@endnode\n\n\n\n\n\n\n@node copyright\n            .\n\n            :\n            :                                      ________ _______ _  _\n           _:__________  _________________ ________\__   _//\n            :      ___/__\__    __      /\\\ __      /___ /       .\n          _ :_ ____        /___        /     \______/   /_________:_ _\n            :     /-------/ __/-------/\______|        ___________|\n            :     _________(___)__________    ________/       /   l_\n           _:____\\_     /       |    ___/____\__   _        /     /\n            :     \   __/\_______|   /_         /---/       /      |\n         - -:-----/_______\(rLf) \----/________/   /_______/_______|\n            :\n            :                 c o p y r i g h t\n            :\n            .\n\n\n\n                                 ---[%]---\n\n                    Zippy-Search is a Megastyle! production\n\n               Code, idea & design by   Lizard of TBL MGS!\n               Error-logo by            Magz of GRT MGS!\n               Tooltype read code by    Lizard of TBL MGS!\n               Bulletin logo            Jedi (Ex. MGS!)\n\n\n              \n\n                         Creds for this GUIDE file\n\n               Slapped together by      Lizard\n               Asciis by                Relief   of T! MGS! 5D\n                                        Grimlock of GRT E^D MGS!\n\n                                 ---[%]---\n\n\n\n                      Megastyle! does now consist of\n \n               Leader . . . . . . . . . Lizard\n               Code . . . . . . . . . . Lizard\n                                        Magz\n                                        Instant\n                                        Splash\n               AscII. . . . . . . . . . Relief\n                                        U-MAN\n                                        Grimlock!\n                                        Magz\n               Boards . . . . . . . . . Noiseless - WHQ         LIZARD\n                                        Genetic Waste           MAGZ\n                                        Ecstatica               INSTANT\n                                        Traders Paradise        U-MAN\n\n                                 ---[%]---\n\n\n\n\n\n\n   ............\n   ::        ::\n   ::        ::\n    .        ::\n   /_____    ::          ___________                                          .\n  /_     \//\____________\      ___/_______    _________\n //      \/        _     /     /_         /____\___    //                     :\n/--------/     .---/____/   .---/________         _    //                     :\n     -T!/______\  /_       _|  .______.  \-----/_______/                      :\n                  __\   __/____|_     l_          _______.     _____________  :\n   ::        ::   \  \__    _ _        /_____ ____\     _l_____\     _     /__:_\n   ::        ::    \--(/      /            _//          \        ____/____/  /:\n   ::        ::       /____________________ /      /\-----/_____/   /_________:_\n   ::        ::                           /_______/(rLf)                      :\n   ::........::                                                               :\n                                                                              :\n                        m e g a s t y l e    ¹ 9 9 6                          :\n                                                                              .\n\n@endnode\n\n\n\n\n\n\n@node changes ÷ history\n\n\n    ___.        __      ____    ___.      _____  ½½½½½½½½½½      .____\n  ._\ _l_______(_/_____/ __/____\  l______\   /__½½½½   ½½½______|   /_.\n  |   \__   _       _  \____  _    __/  _        ½½½½½½½''        l     |\n  |____l/  _l_     _l_     l _l_   l   _l_  "  __½½½½   ½½½½½_______  _l\n g®m   /___) (_____) (_______) (_______) (_____) ½½½½   ½½½½½   \_____)\n                                                 ½½½½   ½½½½½ e^D\n\n                               ...HISTORY...\n\n\n\nSome time ago : First Public-Release v1.o of the door. Ordinary Bull-viewer.\n\n29.03.96      : Bulls v1.5, added the conf-show option, and many other bugs\n                was removed. Better error-trap system included, and timeouts\n                fixed. (250 sec. before closing down the door. :)\n\n\n\n\n\nThanks to the following boards for helpful beta-testing of MegaStyle-products:\n«----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                             Genetic Waste (Magz)\n  Checkpoint (Kingpin)   -   Power Rage (Instant)   -   EveryWare (-Shade!)\n                           Bumble Bee Land (Baffle!)\n\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',36791,9,0,NULL,NULL,'vdk_vb10','scan',1780048435);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('bullv2','BULLV2.LZX','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/BULLV2.LZX',NULL,'XIM','Filenote',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'auto-added',27178,0,0,NULL,NULL,'bullv2','scan',1780048435);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('bullview','BULLVIEW.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/BULLVIEW.LHA',NULL,'XIM','exe.-l0S-eND0S-bBS-.exe',NULL,NULL,NULL,'replace "B"',replace('The one and only bulletin updater to\nreplace "B"\n','\n',char(10)),'NBullview.readme',replace('Short:    Real-time updated bulletins. (ARexx)\nUploader: Leo Davidson <[email removed]>\nAuthor:   Leo Davidson <[email removed]>\nType:     comm/amiex\n\nNBullview.lha - BullView v1.10 by P0T-NOoDLE. (ARexx)\n\n- THE FIRST (and one of the best?) real-time Bulletin Updater to replace "B".\n* When the user selects a bulletin, it updates it before showing it to them!\n* Can also display normal texts.\n* One set of bulletins global to all conferences.\n\n*** This archive is *not* *new*, I am just putting all the Gods''Gift utils\n*** on Aminet for everyone (and so that people can stop bothering me :-).\n\n .--------------------------------------------- ----- ---- --- -- -  -   -  |\n | Leo ''Nudel'' Davidson - Yr1 Computation - [email removed] |\n |  -   -  - -- --- ---- ----- ---------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',19539,6,0,NULL,NULL,'bullview','scan',1780048435);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('burner','BURNER.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/BURNER.LHA',NULL,'XIM','FILE BURNER by THE BONEHEAD/MOTION',NULL,'THE',NULL,'File Deleter For Ami X 2.xx and UP.',replace('FILE BURNER by THE BONEHEAD/MOTION\nFile Deleter For Ami X 2.xx and UP.\n','\n',char(10)),'BURNER.DOC',replace('\n BackRound -This utility was intially Created to be a Private Program\n            for the Co-Sysops at BONEHEADS BBS . Due to the Fact\n            that SOME SYSOPS ARE FORCED TO HAVE A JOB these days and\n            need to depend on they''re co-sysops to do the BBS Maintenece\n            for them sometimes. Well the BIG problem we had at the time\n            was HARD DRIVE SPACE and my Co-Sysops kept Bitching that \n            going through and deleting files was was a TASK and tied up\n            my BBS at the same time. Well so here is Where the Utility\n            comes in .. I sat down and wrote a lil arexx program that\n            would go through and delete the files quckly putting the \n            appropiate noticed on the file to let users know it is \n            OFFLINE. Well as the story goes it worked GREAT and My\n            co-sysops were in and out of the BBS in no time when\n            room had to be made on the H/D. Well the story should end \n             here but does not my Co''s were so impressed by the Utility\n             that they started showing it to they''re friends who run\n             other boards and then they liked it so much they would show\n             they''re friends(Probably 10 BBS run this Sucker Now) so I\n             decided to release this Program to the public ...Enjoy\n  \n                             BONEHEAD/MOTION - \n  \n                    Call Boneheads  BBS at -909 356 0787\n                              (MOTION USHQ)\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n  Instructions-\n\n   TYPE in BURNER at the main Prompt. You will be asked which Conference\n   you want to take files OFFLINE in. Pick a conference. You will Now be\n   prompted which date you want to delete to. Put in a date. Then the\n   program will go back to the Last deleted file in the Conference and\n   ask you if you want to delete the File. Hit Y / N / or Q for Quit\n   The program will then move foward each individual file and ask you\n   the same question so on and so on. When you are satisfied you have\n   made enough space in the H/D just hit Q for quit and it will tell \n   you to HOLD on While Cleaning Up ( It will be Properly Noting all\n   the files as Offline and deleting them ). Thats it Simple Egh ?\n\n      (NOTE - THIS PROGRAM USES HOT KEYS SO DO NOT HIT RETURN AFTER\n              YOU MAKE A CHOICE)\n\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\n                     FILE BURNER by THE BONEHEAD/MOTION \n\n                         For Ami X 2.xx and UP.\n\n  Simple to Install -\n\n   1- Add file Where You Put your BBS Utilities.\n\n   2-Then go to EDIT your custom Commands and Add This\n\n     Burner    RM255[PATH+Filename with No Space after the 5]\n\n     [Ex Burner   RM255dh0:doors/burner]\n\n     Make sure you count 11 spaces starting from Left edge of\n     the screen to RM in order to properly line the program up.\n\n                        \n     And just Execute at the main Prompt by Typing in BURNER\n\n     And Go at it.\n       \n             \n       NOTE - When First executed do not fear about what it is doing..\n              this is not a virus ! it will read your s:acp.start-up\n              to read your System Configuration Paths.\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,4629,2,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048435);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('bv','BV.LZX','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/BV.LZX',NULL,'XIM','WHEREFUNROLEZ.EXE',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'auto-added',20003,0,0,NULL,NULL,'bv','scan',1780048435);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('bytekill','BYTEKILL.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/BYTEKILL.LHA',NULL,'XIM','YeT aNoTHeR MYSTiC-ReLeaSe:',NULL,'ByteAndi/MsT',NULL,'BYTeKiLLeR V1.0 (/X NuKe eNHaNCeMeNT TooL) © 1993 BY ByteAndi/MsT',replace('        YeT aNoTHeR MYSTiC-ReLeaSe:\n              BYTeKiLLeR V1.0\n         (/X NuKe eNHaNCeMeNT TooL)\n           © 1993 BY ByteAndi/MsT\n','\n',char(10)),'ByteKiller.GUIDE',replace('@database ByTeKiLLeR.DoC\n(c)oPYRiGHT (c) 1993 BYTeaNDi/MST\n\n@Remark $VER: (SePTeMBeR 07 1993, 18:20:40)\n@Remark AmigaGuide DataBase Doc-File for the /X-TooL ByteKiller\n@Remark Spelling checked by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC\n\n@node MAIN "ByteKiller Documentation (c) 1993 ByteAndi/MST (MYSTiC /X-Design)"\n\n\n\n         __                      (/X-Design)                        __      \n         \/__________________________________________________ ______\/      \n        /\/    /         \/.  /   /  _____/    ____/____/    \/\    \/\\n   _ _|//_____/   /  /   //  /   / _ _   //   /\__/    /.  /___/\_____\\|_ _\n      |\\    /.  /__/   /___    /\/     /·   / / //   //  /   /\/     //|\n        \___//  /\_/   /\__/   /       /    / / /·   /   ·   / /______/\n           /___/ //___/ / /___/_______/____/ / /____/_______/ /A×E!\n           \___\/ \___\/  \___\_______\____\/  \____\_______\/\n\n                          YeT aNoTHeR MYSTiC-ReLeaSe:\n                                BYTeKiLLeR V1.0\n                           (/X NuKe eNHaNCeMeNT TooL)\n                             © 1993 BY ByteAndi/MsT\n\n                            @{"    I N D E X    " LINK INDEX}\n\n                    @{"  Members of (Mystic/X-Design)   "LINK X-Design}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node INDEX "I N D E X"\n\n\n\n          ·C·O·N·T·E·N·T·S··O·F··T·H·I·S··D·O·C·U·M·E·N·T·A·T·I·O·N·\n\n                        @{"    I N T R O D U C T I O N    " LINK INTRO}\n                        @{"    R E Q U I R E M E N T S    " LINK REQUIREMENTS}\n                        @{"    I N S T A L L A T I O N    " LINK INSTALLATION}\n                        @{"         O P T I O N S         " LINK OPTIONS}\n                        @{"       T O O L T Y P E S       " LINK TOOLTYPES}\n                        @{"       G R E E T I N G S       " LINK GREETINGS}\n                        @{"I N F O S  A B O U T  M O V E R" LINK MOVER}\n                        @{"    F U T U R E   P L A N S    " LINK FUTURE}\n\n          DoCFiLe WRiTTeN BY ByteAndi/MsT & SieGeL/MsT & KiLLrAvEn/MsT\n@endnode\n\n@node INTRO "INTRODUCTION"\n\n\n\n   Well, for a long time I used @{"NosNUKE" link NosNUKE} from Nosferatu, a great /X Nuker,\n   but from version 3.0 NosNUKE does not work 100% anymore!! I hate this!\n   So that means I have to wait for an update of NosNUKE, but until now\n   there is no update. So I decided to write my own personal Nuker.\n\n                           BYTEKiLLER V1.0 WAS BORN!\n\n   The first internal versions could only nuke files, but why not enabling\n   it to make files FreeDL, generate FakeFiles, MOVE files from one confe-\n   rence to another, give private comments to cool/lame uploaders, give\n   info about the user-activity in the ACP and Callerslog and to do a lot\n   more! Well, this is the version to solve all your problems!\n\n\n   Let''s start of with the @{"REQUIREMENTS" LINK REQUIREMENTS}.\n\n                                   @{" INDEX " LINK INDEX}\n@endnode\n\n@node NOSNUKE "INFOS ABOUT NOSNUKE FROM NOSFERATU"\n\nGREAT TOOL... Too bad version 3.0 doesn''t work 100%...\n\n                                   @{" INDEX " LINK INDEX}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node REQUIREMENTS "REQUIREMENTS FOR THIZ TOOL"\n\n   ************************************************************************\n   *       IMPORTANT NOTE! BYTEKiLLER V1.0 RUNS ONLY UNDER /X 3.XX!!      *\n   ************************************************************************\n\n   What do you need: · Ofcoz an Amiga :)\n                     · KickStart V37+\n                     · Working version of /X v3.xx\n                     · And some files to nuke :)\n\n   Let''s continue to the @{"installation" link Installation} and see what needs to be done...\n\n                                   @{" INDEX " LINK INDEX}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node INSTALLATION "INSTALLATION OF THIZ GREAT TOOL"\n\nThis Archive should contain the following files:\n \n                  1. BBS:COMMANDS/BBSCMD/NUKE.INFO\n                  2. DOORS:BYTEKILLER/BYTEKILLER\n                  3. DOORS:BYTEKILLER/BYTEKILLER.INFO\n                  4. BYTEKILLER.GUIDE [THIS! ;)]                 \n\n   1. NUKE.INFO\n   ~~~~~~~~~~~~\n   You can rename this icon to whatever you want, it is only used to call\n   the Nuker from /X. Make sure to set the stack higher than 4096 bytes,\n   20000 bytes is the default value.\n\n   2.BYTEKILLER\n   ~~~~~~~~~~~~\n   This is the actual executable program (XIM) and has a size of 39800 bytes.\n   Please copy it to the Doors:ByteKiller/ directory.\n\n   3.BYTEKILLER.INFO\n   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n   This is the icon for ByteKiller v1.0, DO NOT FORGET TO COPY IT to the\n   Doors:ByteKiller/ directory, or else the program fails!!!\n   \n   For a detailed description of the valid tooltypes, check out the\n   @{"TOOLTYPES" link ToolTypes} chapter. \n\n   4.BYTEKILLER.GUIDE\n   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n   The AmigaGuide Database you are still reading, copy anywhere... :)\n\n\n   Now follows a complete list of all @{"OPTIONS" LINK OPTIONS} from BYTEKILLER V1.00...\n\n                                   @{" INDEX " LINK INDEX}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node WICHTIG "IMPORTANT NOTE !!!"\n\n   This version does not support Ami-X v2.xx, but if a lot of people are\n   asking for a v2.xx version I will release it one day. If YOU want a\n   v2.xx version, contact me at @{"Diabolo BBS" LINK DIABOLO}.\n\n\n                                   @{" INDEX " LINK INDEX}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node OPTIONS "ALL COMMANDS AND OPTIONS FOR BYTEKILLER V1.00"\n\n   Options:\n   ~~~~~~~~\n   @{" F " LINK FREEDL} »»»»> To mark a file as a FreeDownload\n   @{" C " LINK GIVETAKE} »»»»> To give or take crediz to/from an user\n   @{" D " LINK DELETE} »»»»> The selected file will be deleted and a FakeFile will\n             be created. ByteKiller will show the uploader.\n   @{" M " LINK MOVE} »»»»> Move Files from one conference to another...the moved file\n             will be sorted by date in the new conference.\n   @{" N " LINK NEXTFILE} »»»»> If ByteKiller finds more entries with the pattern matching,\n             you are able to switch to the next file until you find the\n             file you want.\n   @{" Q " LINK QUIT} »»»»> To quit ByteKiller...(but why should you? :) )\n\n                                   ·N·O·T·E· \n\n   · If you enter a filename that doesn''t exist, ByteKiller will ask you if\n     you want to generate a FakeFile under that name.\n\n   · If you start ByteKiller without a filename, you will see a list of all\n     users that have been Nuked one or several times. This is an option you\n     can turn on or off (see @{"TOOLTYPES" link ToolTypes}).\n\n                                 @{" INDEX " LINK INDEX}\n@endnode\n\n@node FREEDL "MARK A FILE AS FREEDOWNLOAD"\n\n                              FREEDOWNLOAD (F)\n                              ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n   If you choose the F option, the selected file will be marked as a\n   FreeDownload. ByteKiller will change the bytes-info about the file\n   to FREE and will add the following comment to the description:\n\n                  <<< FREE DOWNLOAD >>> <<< FREE DOWNLOAD >>>\n\n                                  Nice eh? :)\n\n                                @{" OPTIONS " LINK OPTIONS}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node GIVETAKE "GIVE/TAKE BYTES TO/FROM AN USER"\n\n                          GIVE/TAKE BYTES (C)\n                          ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n   This is the Nuker part :)! With this option you can take or give bytes\n   to/from an user. All downloaders can get their downloaded bytes back\n   ofcoz.\n   \n   First ByteKiller will search for the uploader and if it finds him, it\n   will ask you wether you want to TAKE or GIVE bytes. The specified file\n   will NOT be deleted!\n\n   NOTE: Failed transfers are recognized and if such a file is to be found,\n         ByteKiller will ask you to continue nuking or continue searching\n         for the uploader.\n\n   If you have specified the @{"TOOLTYPE" LINK NUKERTOOLS} "EXTERN_COMMENT=YES" ByteKiller will\n   ask you to enter a private message (max. 5 lines) to the uploader. This\n   message will be appended to the ByteKiller message.\n\n   After this you can have ByteKiller returning credits to downloaders.\n\n   ByteKiller will now show you the comments which can replace the size-info\n   of the nuked file. You can specify up to 97 (!) comments, but if you still\n   think you need a comment which is not present, you can enter it live :).\n\n   See @{"TOOLTYPES" LINK TOOLTYPES} for more info about comments!\n\n   When this is done, you are asked to enter a comment for the file-\n   description itself. You can choose between a short or a long comment\n   line. Short comments are defined as default and are length-limited to\n   the file-description length.\n\n   Long comments take up a full line and are appended UNDER the description\n   of the file.\n\n   At this point, ByteKiller will show you the next file if you used pattern-\n   matching (*) and will ask you what to do with it (back to step 1).\n \n   If you didn''t use pattern-matching, you are prompted for a new filename\n   or to show you the list of all nuked users in this conference.\n\n                                @{" OPTIONS " LINK OPTIONS}\n@endnode\n\n@node DELETE "BYTEKILLER GUIDE - DELETE A FILE"\n\n                                   DELETE (D)\n                                   ~~~~~~~~~~\n\n   This function does the same as the @{" C " link GiveTake} function (Give/Take crediz), but\n   this time the fill WILL BE DELETED and a fake file will be created. So\n   take care of this function, ''caus deleted files are deleted!\n\n\n                                @{" OPTIONS " LINK OPTIONS}\n@endnode\n\n@node MOVE "BYTEKILLER GUIDE - MOVING A FILE"\n\n                                    MOVE (M)\n                                    ~~~~~~~~\n   When activated, ByteKiller will first show all conferences that\n   particular user (the one who uses the nuker) has access to. The current\n   conference number will be shown in green, the destination directories\n   will be displayed in plain white.\n   \n   You can simply select the destination conference by typing in the number\n   of the conference.\n   \n   The next steps are the same as with the @{" C " link GiveTake} function. But you cannot\n   enter a new description.\n\n   Read @{" MOVER " LINK MOVER} for more info about this part of ByteKiller.\n\n\n                                  @{" OPTIONS " LINK OPTIONS}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node NEXTFILE "BYTEKILLER GUIDE - NEXT FILE BY USING PATTERN MATCHING"\n\n                               NEXT FILE (N)\n                               ~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n   If you use the pattern matching possibilities and multiple files match\n   the pattern you entered, the next file will be shown and at your will :).\n\n\n                                  @{" OPTIONS " LINK OPTIONS}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node QUIT "BYTEKILLER GUIDE - QUIT THIZ TOOL..."\n\n\n                                    QUIT (Q)\n                                    ~~~~~~~~\n\n   One of the tougher parts of ByteKiller... it actually QUITS ByteKiller.\n   \n                           BUT WE WILL MEET AGAIN! :)\n\n\n                                  @{" OPTIONS " LINK OPTIONS}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node TOOLTYPES "BYTEKILLER GUIDE - ALL TOOLTYPE INFORMATION"\n\n                      User-Definitions for ByteKiller V1.00\n                      ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n   NUKER=<number>       = Specifies how many users have access to the nuker.\n\n   NUKER=ALL            = All users who have access to the nuker can use the\n                          nuker without PW-Protection.\n\n   NUKER.<Nr>=<User>    = Name of the User who has access to the nuker.\n                          <Nr>   is the NukerNumber ranging from 1 to ???\n                          <User> is the name of the user (must be the same\n                                 like his handle!)\n\n   NUKER_PW.<nr>=<PW>   = User-PW (Maximum 10 characters are allowed!)\n                          Specifies the private PW for the active user.\n\n   ACCESS_MOVE.<Nr>=YES = <Nr> is the NukerNumber of the user (NOT the\n                          slotnumber!), who has access to move files across\n                          conferences. To disable this option, delete this\n                          Tooltype or set it to "NO".\n\n   ACCESS_DEL.<Nr>=YES  = <Nr> is the NukerNumber of the user, who has access\n                          to delete files. To disable this option, delete\n                          this ToolType or set it to "NO".\n\n   ACCESS_FREE.<Nr>=YES = <Nr> is the NukerNumber of the user, who has access\n                          to mark a file as a Free Download. To disable this\n                          option, delete this ToolType or set it to "NO".\n\n   *************************************************************************\n                                IMPORTANT NOTE:\n                                ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n            THE LAST FIVE TOOLTYPES ARE ONLY USEFUL, IF THE TOOLTYPE\n                         "NUKER=ALL" IS DISABLED !!!!!\n   *************************************************************************\n\n   ACCESS_FREE=ALL      = Every user, who has access to the Nuker, could mark\n                          files as a FREE DOWNLOAD.\n\n   ACCESS_DEL=ALL       = Every user, who has access to the Nuker, could\n                          DELETE Files.\n\n   ACCESS_MOVE=ALL      = Every user, who has access to the Nuker, could MOVE\n                          files across conferences.\n\n                          @{"NUKER SPECIFIC TOOLTYPES" LINK NUKERTOOLS}\n@endnode\n\n@node NUKERTOOLS "BYTEKILLER GUIDE - NUKER SPECIFIC TOOLTYPES"}\n\n                            Nuker Specific ToolTypes\n                            ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n   EXTERN_COMMENT=YES    = Allows you to enter extra comments via the\n                           internal Ami-Express editor.\n\n   CREATE_DATAS=YES      = Create a Data-File for every conference with a\n                           list of all nuked users, nuked users'' bytes &\n                           files, and the date of the last Nuke of the users.\n                           If you want to write some Bulls for that Data-File\n                           leave a message on one of our /X DeSiGn Boards,\n                           i.e. @{" DIABOLO " LINK DIABOLO}.\n\n   NODE.<nr>=<PATH>      = Here you must specify per node where you have the\n                           callerlog. Specify the full path. For example:\n                           "BBS:NODE0/CALLERLOG". Make sure the number\n                           follow each other, so 0, 1, 2 etc.\n\n   USERDATA=<PATH>       = Specify the full path where you have your user-\n                           data. For example: "BBS:USER.DATA".\n\n   COMMENT.<Nr>=<COM>    = This is where you can specify upto 97 different\n                           comments which can be appended to the file-\n                           description after nuking the file.\n                           (NOTE: "OTHER" & "NONE" are specified internally).\n\n   SIZE.<Nr>=<COM>       = This is where you can specify upto 97 different\n                           comments which can replace the byte information\n                           of a nuked file.\n                           (NOTE: "OTHER" & "NONE" are specified internally).\n\n                                @{" INDEX " LINK INDEX}\n@endnode\n\n@node GREETINGS "GREETINGS..."\n\n                              ·G·R·E·E·T·I·N·G·S·\n\n  Many greetings to Empire and the other @{" Members of (Mystic/X-Design) "LINK X-Design}\n\n  Killraven, Fuzzy, Axe.....hmmmmm....I hope no more stress with AFL..\n  SieGeL...THX for that Nice Dox......\n\n  I hope this will show the Development Team what to do with /X !\n\n  Special greetings to Van Damme... I hope you will come next time with\n                                    a XIM, take a look at Empire!\n\n  To Bytemaster, we hope for more information about this Kewl Ami-Express!\n\n  Greetings to Genghis Khan, you are on the right Way...\n\n  THX to Spy because he helped me to learn C  and invested many Time\n  in my Doors\n\n  Many Many THX To All my Beta tester for BugReports, Hints and Tips\n  to install Options....in this Door....\n              _\n           _ //\n  Thanx to \X/ Amiga For Being The Best Computer Ever made ...\n\n  =======================================================================\n@endnode\n\n@node X-Design "New /X"\n\n                      ______  __________________\n               +-----/    \ \/ / __/_  __/ / __/----------+\n               |----/ / / /\  /\  /-/ /-/ / /----[ /X ]---|\n               |----\/ / /-/ /\  /-/ /-/ /\ \--[ DESiGN ]-|\n               +-----\/\/--\/--\/--\/--\/--\/-------------+\n               |                                          |\n               |   EMPiRE   -   BYTEANDi   -  CRACKDOWN   |\n               |   TYCOON   -   KiLLRAVEN  -   SiEGEL     |\n               |   FUZZY    -     SPY                     |\n               +------------------------------------------+\n\n                                @{" INDEX " LINK INDEX}\n\n@endnode\n@node DIABOLO "Advert"\n                        ·  :                 .     :     :\n-============-   \____ ¬V ¬V___ ¬V___ ¬V___ ¬V ¬|  |___ ¬|   MANAGEMENT\n MYSTIC           | ¬|  |  | ¬|  | ¬|  | ¬|  |  |  | ¬|  |   -========-\n      GHQ         |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |   ANDi/MST\n-============-    |  |  |  |     |    _|  |  |  |__|  |  |   SPY/MST\n                  |  |  |  |  |  |  | ¬|  |  |  | ¬|  |  |   FELDMAN\n-ELiTE oNLY-      |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |   FuZzY/MsT\n                  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |   SYSTEM\nCALL US NoW FoR   |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |   -====-\nTHE NEWEST AMiGA/ |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |   RUNS oN A3000\nPC&Console STUFF  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |   WiTH 25MHZ AND\nAND ALL MST-      |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |   AMiEX (REG.)\nRELEASES.         |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n                __|_____A__A__A__A_____A_____A_____A_____|D! SUPPoRTED BY\nWE oNLY ACCEPT    |     :  :     :     :     :     :     |   -==========-\n9600 - 16.800     :     ·  .     .           .     ·     :   M Y S T I C\nBAUD CoNNECTS.    .        .\n                         Node0  +49 (0) 30-6221994   HST\n                         Node1  +49 (0) 30-6212312   Zyxel\n                         Node0  +49 (0) 30-6218787   Dual\n\n                                @{" INDEX " LINK INDEX}\n@endnode\n\n@node MOVER "INFOS ABOUT THE MOVER"\n\n   This little routine is written by Spy/MST and ByteAndi/MST. It allows you\n   to move files without changing the filelist, moving the files from one\n   conference to another.\n\n   ByteKiller allows you to take upload-bytes from the upload, it is very\n   fast and a piece of powerful coding. Hope you enjoy it as much as we do!\n\n                             @{" INDEX " LINK INDEX}\n\n@endnode\n@node FUTURE "News about X-DeSign"\n\n   We are currently busy with:\n   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n   · Better Shell for /X ,looks like Cshell\n\n   · MultiChat\n\n   · SysopDownload with some kewl functions\n\n   · Some New Bulletins\n\n   · Newfiles (new Update) : Split in three Parts because scrolling\n                             of the FileList now via arrowkeys and more!\n\n   · BytekillerV1.1 using Big Boss Data Files to search for Uploader\n\n   · ConferenceScan (new update): Flagging files, better lay-out and\n                                  revolutionary new options!\n\n                    @{" Members of (Mystic/X-Design) "LINK X-Design}\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,54607,5,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048435);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('c_n_cs13','C&N-CS13.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/C&N-CS13.LHA','ConferenceSecurity','XIM','ConferenceSecurity',NULL,NULL,NULL,'·-================-· Conference Security V1.30 - /X 3.x ASM Door! Use on "J" / "<" / ">" and "G"',replace('    *CoNaN&NeWToN*\n ·-================-·\nConference Security V1.30 - /X 3.x ASM Door!\n       Use on "J" / "<" / ">" and "G"\n  Totally recoded and minor options added.\nProve to be uninstallable for Sysops :) hehe\n\nA major updated and easy to use V2.0 will be\n        released in the near future.    /C+N\n','\n',char(10)),'ConferenceSecurity.Guide',replace('@DATABASE Conference Security Documentation V1.00\n@NODE main "Conference Security Documentation V1.00"\n\n           /\                                _____.      /\\n      /\  /  \ ______    ______/\___________/    ¬!_____/  \  ______________\n     /  \/    \\    ¬\  /    ¬/                         |   \/            ¬/\n    /          \\     \/     /  ___________.      ._____!___/             /\n   /            \\     \    /_____.     ¬\ |      7    ¬\  ¬\       .____/_____\n  /    \  /      \\        /      7       \!      |      \   \      7        ¬/\n /      \/        \/      /|      !        \      !      /    \     !        /\n/________\         \     / |               /            /      \            /\n       /____________\   /  !______        /!___        /_______/___        /\n             ·A×E·\    /         \_______/    \_______/           \_______/\n                   \  /\n                    \/\n                         .oO· Conference Security ·Oo.\n\n         @{"Introduction              " LINK intro}         @{"Example Of A Configuration" LINK configex}\n         @{"Installation              " LINK install}         @{"Text vs. AmigaGuide       " LINK txtvsag}\n         @{"Join Conference        ''J''" LINK join}         @{"Note Worthy Features      " LINK features}\n         @{"Add Conference         ''>''" LINK add}         @{"Compability               " LINK comp}\n         @{"Sub Conference         ''<''" LINK sub}         @{"Disclaimer & Copyright    " LINK discopy}\n         @{"Logoff                 ''G''" LINK logoff}         @{"Contact The Creators      " LINK bloodstreet}\n         @{"Logoff Batch              " LINK batch}         @{"Mystic Boards             " LINK boards}\n         @{"Configuration             " LINK config}         @{"Credits And About         " LINK creds}\n\n               All Was Done by *CoNaN&NeWToN* For Mystic in 1993\n\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE intro "Introduction"\n\n   » Introduction «\n·-==================-·\n\nThis Door Gives You The Ability To Secure Certain Conferences From Hacking\nand Generally Keeping Your Private Conferences Safe.\nWorks With Normal or Relative Conferences.\nAlso Takes Account Of Stupid Sysops Who Give Multiple Access To The Same\nConferences.\n\nThere Are Certain Good Things In Having All The Conference Doors In One\nDoor, But Mostly More Security Arround The Conferences.\n\nThis Is An Assembler XIM Door! NOT REXX OR "C" SHIT!\n\nThe Door Can Be PowerPacker and Still Work From AmiExpress... Surprised?\n(But You Loose CPU Speed!)\n\nOnly Available For AmiX V3.x! (If Requested A 2.xx Version Can be Arranged.)\n\nI Would Like To Urge The AmiExpress Development Team To Be More Helpful\nTowards Un-Registered AmiExpress Developers Such As C+N.\nInstead Of Keeping People From Creating Good Doors, Lots Of People Are\nCreating Crap Doors... And Loads Of Them!!\n\nSo You Better Appreciate The Time Spent On These *CoNaN&NeWToN* Productions.\n\nIf You don''t Know The Names You Can Be Assured That 10 Years In The Scene\nIs Quite Impressive And That Our Experience In Programming Is More Than\nEnough To Make AmiExpress Assembler Tools.\n\nIf You Have Problems Installing This Door Contact Us...\n                        ...Or If You Just Want To Get In Touch With Us... :)\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE install "Installation"\n\n   » Installation «\n·-==================-·\n\nYou Should Have The Following Files Present...\nDoors:MST_ConfSec/\n  ConferenceSecurity         The XIM Door (Use For ALL 4 Commands)\n    Version 1.00             (Instruction Below)\n\n  ConferenceSecurity.info    The Configuration File! (AmiX 3.x Standard)\n    No Version?!             Use Wb.Info Or Dopus.\n\n  ConferenceSecurity.Exe     The Logoff.Batch File (Handling Safe Confs.)\n    Version 1.00             If You Use This Don''t Use ConfSecCleanUp.Exe Too!\n                             (Usage Information Below)\n\n  ConfSecCleanUp.Exe         Use In LogOff Batch If You Don''t Use The LogOff\n    Version 1.00             For Safe Conferences. (Usage Information Below)\n\n  ConferenceSecurity.Doc     Txt Documentation For This Door.\n    Version 1.00\n\n  ConferenceSecurity.Giude   AmigaGuide Documentation For This Door. (This?!)\n    Version 1.00\n\nCommands(/BBSCmd)\n  J.info                    Patches The JoinConference Command.J\n  <.info                    Patches The Fast Lower JoinConference Command.<\n  >.info                    Patches The Fast Higher JoinConference Command.>\n  G.info                    Patches The Logoff Command.G\n\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE join "Join Conference"\n\n   » Join Conference "J" «\n·-=========================-·\n\nWill Compute A Conference Menu For You If You Decide That Users Should\nOnly See The Conferences They Have Access To.\nSee Configuration For MenuTypes!\nChecks A Give Access Level And/Or A Password For The Conferences.\n\nParameters Will Ofcoz Be Recognized For Shortcuts!\n  "J <confnr.>"\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE add "Add Conference"\n\n   » Add Conference  ">" «\n·-=========================-·\n\nAdds 1 To The Current Conference. Checks For Access Level And Password.\nIt Goes Into Join Conference If Any Problem Accours. (See Above!)\n\nNo Parameters Will be Aknowledged! (At The Moment.) Any Ideas?\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE sub "Sub Conference"\n\n   » Sub Conference  "<" «\n·-=========================-·\n\nSubs 1 To The Current Conference. Checks For Access Level And Password.\nIt Goes Into Join Conference If Any Problem Accours. (See Above!)\n\nNo Parameters Will be Aknowledged! (At The Moment.) Any Ideas?\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE logoff "Logoff"\n\n   » Logoff          "G" «\n·-=========================-·\n\nChecks If You Are Login Off In A "Safe Conference" or If You Have To Move\nBefore You Can Logoff. If You Must Move, It Will Go Into Join Conference.\nIt Uses Also Needs A Run In The Logoff Batch To Ensure That "Alt-H" And\nF10 Actions To Do Not Break Any Security!\nHere Again It Will Check Password,Axx And Safe Conference Configurations.\n\nParameters Will Ofcoz Be Recognized For Shortcuts!\n  "G <safe confnr.>"\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE batch "Logoff Batch"\n\n   » Logoff Batch «\n·-==================-·\n\nTo Ensure That People Who Loose Carrier Can Not Auto-Join A "Safe Conference",\nIf An Account Should Get Hacked And The Foul Being Then Just "Happends" To\nAuto-Join A Restricted Conference.\n\nConfSecCleanUp.Exe\n  This One Only Delete The "PSWFAILSTATS@#" That The JoinConference Uses\n  To Control The Amount Of Password Failures.\nUsage:\n    ConfSecCleanUp.Exe          Deletes All "PSWFAILSTATS@#" In Env:\n                                Use In BBS Init.\n    ConfSecCleanUp.Exe <node>   Deletes The "PSWFAILSTATS@#" For The\n                                Node To Be Reset! Use In LogOff.Batch.\n\nConferenceSecurity.Exe\n  Changes The AutoJoin Conference In The User.Data If Something Needs\n  To Be changed.\nUsage:\n    ConferenceSecurity.Exe          Run All User.Data AutoJoin Conference.\n                                    Use In BBS Init.\n    ConferenceSecurity.Exe <node>   Runs User or All User.Data AutoJoin C.\n                                    Use In LogOff.Batch.\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE config "Configuration"\n\n   » Configuration «\n·-===================-·\n\nThe Configuration Must Be Placed In "Doors:"! (At Least For This Version)\n\nAmiX3.x Config.:\nIn Order To Maintain The Same "Style" As AmiX I Have Made The Configuration\nAs An .info File ("ConferenceSecurity.info").\nYou Can Use Dopus or Workbench To Alter .info Files.\n(The Door.info Should Ofcoz Be Made According To AmiX.Docs!)\n\nFollowing Things will be Recognized in the .info:\n\nPSW.<confnr.>=<password>     : User Required To Enter Password!\nCPSW.<confnr.>=<password>    : User Required To Enter Case Sensitive Psw!\nAXX.<confnr.>=<access level> : User Required To Have At Least Specified Axx.!\nHOT.<confnr.>                : User Can Not LogOff (AutoJoin) Conference!\nAXXFAIL=<access level>       : Users Access Level Dropped To, After Psw-Fail!\nMENUTYPE=<menu type>         : The Display You Use For Yar JoinConf.Menu\nCONFIRM=<confirm type>       : Confirm LogOff Configuration\nLIST.<confnr>=<listpathfile> : Check If you Name Is Allowed In Conference!\nDAY.<confnr>=<Day On/Off>    : Which Days Conference Can Be Joined.\nTIME.<confnr>=<HHMM>,<HHMM>  : Set Time Interval For Conference Join.\n                               Multiple Can Be Used For Same Conference.\n                               (Does Not Handle Over Midnights.\n                               Eg.: 2300,0100... Use 2300,2359 and 0000,0100)\nNAME.<confnr>=<xtra>|<conf name>\n                             : Will OverRide Confname In ConfConfig.Info.\n                               <xtra> Is For Add On''s!\n                               <conf name> Will Be Right Centered As Normal!\n                               <xtra> Will Be Left Centered!\n                               <xtra> With No <confname> Will Left Centre\n                               <xtra> And Right Centre The NodeConfig ConfName.\nNOPSWAXX=<access level>      : Users With Axx Level Equal Or Higher\n                               Do Not Have To EnTer Psw To Join Psw Confs.\nLOGO=<pathfile>              : You Can Show An Ansi Above The Conf List.\n                               (Only For Internal MenuType.)\nNET=<netnumber>              : First Net Mail Conference.\nNORM_COLUMNS=<column number> : Number Of Columns In Normal/Local Conference\n                               List. (Only For Internal MenuType.)\nNET_COLUMNS=<column number>  : Number Of Columns In Net Conference List.\n                               (Only For Internal MenuType.)\nDAYTIME_PRIVATE.<confnr.>    : Will Not Show Joinable Days And Times!\n\n<confnr.>        ranges from 1 to 999                           (AmiX3.x Limit)\n<password>       can be 32 Characters                              (Door Limit)\n<access level>   ranges from 1 to 255                           (AmiX Standard)\n<menu type>      There Are Three Different Types:\n  STANDARD       <Screens>JoinConf<access level>.<language>|.<gr>\n  AREA           <Screens>JoinConf.<area><access level>.<language>|.<gr>\n  INTERNAL       Will Calculate Internal Menus. No Bother Creating Files\n                 For Relative Conferences!!\n                 Can Be Immitated With ~MCI Codes Also!\n                 Faster Than The Above...!\n<confirm type>   Different Types\n  NONE           User Does Not Have To Confirm LogOff.\n  NOTEXPERT      User In Non Expert Mode Has To Confirm LogOff.\n  EXPERT         User In Expert Mode Has To Confirm LogOff.\n  ALL            User Has To Confirm LogOff.\n<listpathfile>   .info File Where You List The Names To A Give Conference.\n                 Conf2List(.info) Do Write .info In Your Config!!\n<HHMM>,<HHMM>    Start Time,End Time Of Interval.\n<Day On/Off>     Is Made Of 7 Chars. One For Each Day. "X" For Ok.\n                 First Char Is Sunday And Last Is Saturday.\n                 Eg.: DAY.3=X__X__X. Conference 3 Can Be Joined On Sundays\n                 Wednesdays And Saturdays Only!\n\nDefault "MenuType" Is "STANDARD".\nIf <Screens> Is Not In Your BBS:NodeX.info Then "BBS:Node<x>/" Is Default.\nDefault "Confirm" Is "NONE".\nDefault "Time" Is "0000,2359"\nDefault "Net" Conference Start Is 0 (Maining Only Local Conferences.)\nDefault "NORM_COLUMNS" and "NET_COLUMNS" Are 1. (Max 3 Columns.)\nAll Columns Are Auto Adjusted If There Is Enough Space.\n\nIf No "NOPSWAXX" Is Defined Then All Users Will Have To Enter Psw''s.\n(Ideal For Sysop''s Who Get Bored With Entering Psw!)\n\nAll Strings Can Use Upper or Lower Case, The Door Is Not Case Sensitive.\nExcept of course Case Sensitive Passwords.\n\nMost Options Are Maybe Pretty Weird But Try Them And You Will Maybe Find\nOut Their Purpose And Future Purposes For You.\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE configex "Example Of A Configuration"\n\n   » Example Of A Configuration «\n·-================================-·\n\nAXX.3=100                              : Access Level To Join Conf 3\nAXX.5=245                              : Access Level To Join Conf 5\nPSW.5=innersanctum                     : Password For Conf 5\nHOT.5                                  : No Logoff From Conf 1 And .Exe Run\n                                         Through For Security!\nAXXFAIL=100                            : Set Access Level Down After Password\n                                         Failure!\nMENUTYPE=Internal                      : Menutype. Fast Internal!\nHOT.1                                  : No Logoff From Conf 1 And .Exe Run\n                                         Through For Security!\nCPSW.4=DuLpErT                         : Case Password For Conf 4\nCONFIRM=NOTEXPERT                      : Logoff Confirm Type\nLIST.2=Doors:MST_ConfSec/Conf2List     : .info List Of Admited User In Conf 5\nLIST.5=Doors:MST_ConfSec/Conf5List     : .info List Of Admited User In Conf 5\nTIME.3=1100,1300                       : Tine Interval For Conference 3\nTIME.3=1930,2300                       : Tine Interval For Conference 3\nDAY.3=XXX_XXX                          : Days Open In Conference 3\nNOPSWAXX=255                           : Users With This Or Higher Access Level\n                                         Dont Have To Write A PSW!\nNAME.5=[UN0001]|Hard Core              : New Split! Name For Conf 5\nNAME.4=Crap Request                    : New Name For Conf 4\nNAME.2=Local|                          : Adds <Extr> And Keeps The Confname!!\n                                         Left And Right Centered Of Course.\nLOGO=Doors:MST_ConfSec/JoinConf.Logo   : Ansi Above The Internal Menutype Only!\nNET=4                                  : Net From Real! Conf 4\nNORM_COLUMNS=3                         : 3 Normal Conferences\nNET_COLUMNS=2                          : 2 Net Conferences\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE txtvsag "Text vs. AmigaGuide"\n\n   » Text vs. AmigaGuide «\n·-=========================-·\n\nI Examined An AmigaGuide File And Discovered The Structure.\nSo Instead Of Using Converters To Get Your Prefered Format I Have Desided\nTo Make One Of Each! Both Viewing Utilities Should Be Inluded In The\nDistribution Package.\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE features "Note Worthy Features"\n\n   » Note Worthy Features «\n·-==========================-·\n\nWell The Join Door Keeps Track Of Online Psw Failures So If 3 Failures Occur\nIn Da Same Conference User Can NOT Join Any Psw Conf.\nPeople May Abort Psw Check After 2 Failures, But The Door Keeps Track On\nFailures In (Env:PswFailStats@N) As Long As User Online!\nEnv:PswFailStats@N File Is Reset With One Of The Two Available .exe Files\nIn Your Logoff.Batch...)\n\nWill Enter Psw Failures In CallersLog.\n\nSupports Only 0-9 Nodes, And Will Ofcoz Be Updated If Joseph Hodge\nDesides To Make More Nodes Available. (And Even If He Doesn''t...)\nCan Handle Up To 1-999 Conferences, But I Seriously Doubt If It Will Be\nA Problem!\n\nSupports Also "Screens=<path>". And Confirm LogOff As Configured...\nFeatures For Netmail Boards.\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE comp "Compability"\n\n   » Compability «\n·-=================-·\n\nThis Door Should Work Fine With All Computers.\nAssembled With A A4000/68040/KS3.0 and tested on My Slow A500/68000/KS2.0.\nDoor Should Work On KS1.2/1.3 But AmiExpress Requires KS2.0+!\n\nCurrently This Door Only Works With AmiX3.x.\n\nUse Version <files> To Make Sure The Versions In This Doc Corresponds To The\nFiles In The Archive.\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE discopy "Disclaimer & Copyright"\n\n   » Disclaimer&Copyright «\n·-==========================-·\n\nThe Authors Of This AmiX Door Do Not Take Any Responsability For Any Loss\nOf Data Using This Or Any Other Products By Yours Truly.\nThis Door Is Copyright by C+N. This Means That This Door Should Be Spread\nIn It''s Original State.\n(No Files May Be Excluded Or Changed From The "Install" Archive.)\n\nThis Is Not Public Domain, Not Fee Can Be Taken For This Program!\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE bloodstreet "Contact *CoNaN&NeWToN* At Bloodstreet"\n\n   » Feedback «\n·-==============-·\n\nWell It Would Be Nice To Know If People Use Our Doors On Their Boards!\nSo Please Contact Us Just For Fun. Or For Suggestions And Stuff.\n\nOur Modem Handle Is "CoNaN&NeWToN" So If You See It Arround... :)\n                         _      .                   _\n                ________/¬\   __:     _____   _____/ \___________\n                \___       \./ ¬|___./    ¬\./    ¬\_____    ___/\n                  \__  _| __V.  |  ¬V.  |   V.  |   |.  |   __/\n                   \__ \_  ¬|¦  |  .|:  |   |:  |   |¦  |   _/\n                    |   |   |°  |  ¦|°  |   |¦  |   |°  |   |\n             _  _/\_A       A      °A       A°      A   |   A_/\_ _\n                     \_____/ \_____/ \_____/ \_____/ \_____/  _\n       _______________/¬\___/\________   ________/\__________/¬\_________\n       \____   ______/     ¬\______  ¬\./   ______/   ______/       ____/\n         \______   ¬|.   |   |. __|  __V.   _____|    _____|.   |  ____/\n          \_   |    |¦   |_  |: \__   ¬|¦   |    |.   |    |¦   |_____/\n           |   |    |°   | \_|¦   |   .|°   |    |¦   |    |°   |\n      _ _  A    ____A_   |   |°  _|   ¦|______   A°  ______A_   A  _ _\n         \/ \__/      \_/:    \_/ |   °|      \_/ \_/        \_/ \/\n                         :        _)  (_\n                                  \ sc /\n                                   \  /\n                                    \/\n\n      There is Only One Board In The World Where You Can Be Sure To Find\n             *CoNaN&NeWToN*. So Why Not Try Calling Bloodstreet...!\n                         +45-75-15-9284 <> +45-75-15-9286\n\n                        Net...AmiXnet : @DK0001 (MAiNLiNE)\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE boards "Mystic Boards Worldwide"\n\n   » Mystic Boards «\n·-===================-·\n                   .\n    _______     __/|__    _______________________.  /\______\n   _\  .. ¬\   /   ! ¬\  _\  ________.   .___.  ¬| /   .___/\n   \_  ||   \ /____.   \_\_____ ¬\___|   |___|   |/    |__Z___\n  /¬   ||  -\\    ¬!  -\\    ¬V -\\  | -!|   | -!|\    !¬  -// FuN RoOLeS !\n  \____!!_  _/\______  _/\_____  _/\ !___!   !___! \_____  _/  -^- -  - -^-\n   \___\_\_/\\/\____\_/\\/\___\_/\\/ !___!   !___!\/___/\_//\n+--------·\\/·------·\\/·-----·\\/·-------------------·\//·------------------+\n|DiGiTal CaNdY   ^ 3 NdZ aMiGa Whq! ^ -------- ÷ ------------- +1-5134713366 |\n|LaST ouTposT    ^ 2 NdZ aMiGa Ehq! ^ SneS Whq ÷ /X-DeSiGn EhQ +31-72157682  |\n|BoGuS ExCepT¿oN ^ 2 NdZ aMiGa UShq ^ -------- ÷ ------------- +1-2ø34378655 |\n|The RestaUrAnt  ^ 3 NdZ aMiGa UShq ^ -------- ÷ ------------- +1-6163637ø27 |\n|D¿aBoLo         ^ 3 NdZ aMiGa Ghq! ^ -------- ÷ /X-DeSiGn WhQ +49-3ø6218787 |\n|TrAdE ¿n CeNtEr ^ 1 Nd'' aMiGa Ghq! ^ IbM! EhQ ÷ /X-DeSiGn GhQ +49-7ø826ø611 |\n|TrAdE ¿n CeNtEr ^ 2 NdZ aMiGa iSDn ^ IbM! EhQ ÷ ------------- +49-7ø8292122ø|\n|NorTh star Land ^ 2 NdZ aMiGa Ghq! ^ -------- ÷ ------------- +49-304162261 |\n|CrY¿nG F¿eLdS   ^ 1 Nd'' aMiGa Ghq! ^ -------- ÷ ------------- +49-4ø6452525 |\n|THe Add¿cT¿oN   ^ 1 Nd'' aMiGa Ghq! ^ -------- ÷ ------------- +49-61ø231564 |\n|An¿mAlS         ^ 1 Nd'' aMiGa Chhq ^ -------- ÷ ------------- +41-53246782  |\n|MaMbA           ^ 1 Nd'' aMiGa Phq! ^ -------- ÷ ------------- +48-22367443  |\n|OuT oF SpAcE    ^ 1 Nd'' aMiGa Shq! ^ -------- ÷ ------------- +46-62o13141  |\n|ChAnNeL-X       ^ 2 NdZ aMiGa DisT ^ -------- ÷ /X-DeSiGn DhQ +31-229ø62244 |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------·A×E^MsT·-+\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE creds "Credits & About"\n\n   » Credits&About «\n·-===================-·\n\nThis Door Was Only Made So That People Can Feel More Secure In Their\nDaily Use Of Private or Restricted Conferences.\nAnd Because Their Seems To Be A Lack of Quality Asm Doors Out There!\nIt Has Been Thouroughly Tested And Should Not Contain Any Bugs.\nCreated With The Help From Arexx Port Stuff And An Asm Source Sent by\nSilverHawk!/Tarkus Team. Thx!\n\nI Had Some Support From The Following Things:\nMean The Cruel!, NeWToN The Money Sucking Hole!, Omar''s Video+Videos!\nA Wicked Metallica Tape...?? Some C64 Tunes...\n\nWell This Door Should Be 100% Mc680xx And Kickstart (1.x,2.x/3.x Compatible)\nBecause It Was Made On My A4000/040/25Mhz With Kick3.0...And My A500...\nAnd Tested on An A2000 With Kick2.0.\n\nBeware of Mc68040, Because I Found A Very Suspicious "Bug", The Code\nTested An Odd-LongAddress But The Mc68040 CAN DO THAT... So Now I Will Have\nTo Test My Code On My A500 For Such Tricky Bugs. A500 Is SO SLOW!!! ARGH!\n\nBETA-TESTING Done By Mean At BloodStreet.. Beware Of Psychotics Roaming!\n\nBut Should You Find Any Bugs, or If You Want To See Some Improvements On\nThis or Other Doors You Should Contact C+N:\n\nWe Can Be Contacted by Modem On:\nBloodStreet...+45-75-159-284 or Maybe On Any Other Mystic Hq...\nThe Before Mentioned Boards Will Maybe Be Running Our Newest Doors/Updates.\n\nLook Out For More Releases From C+N...\n\nGreets To The Following Dudes... Mystic Members Worldwide.\nAll In Tarkus Team - Droopy - BlackHawk - Tsl&Crionics - Detron\nPennywise - Candyman - Ramirez - Zawran&Cromer - Zeus - Mr. Beer\nFelix - Promax - Ozone&Xod - Tensor - Frostie - Dux - Weird Dream & Yobbo\nD-Siya - Flamestriker - Omar - Capital - Excessive Knight - MacroNit\nThe Old Rebels Tribe And Some More...\n\nSoon More AmiExpress Doors From The Hard Working Guys From Mystic /X Design!\n@ENDNODE\n','\n',char(10)),'{"TYPE":"<menu"}','auto-added',46504,14,0,NULL,NULL,'c_n_cs13','scan',1780048435);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('c_cardgm','C-CARDGM.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/C-CARDGM.LHA','13','XIM','13',NULL,'PROXIMA',NULL,'|     _______/    _  ¬\     _  ¬\   ¬|ZACK |     |/   ¬\    |/    \   |/    \   |____ |:    !     /    !     /   !     /   !   /',replace('  ____________________________________.\n |     _______/    _  ¬\     _  ¬\   ¬|ZACK \n |     |/   ¬\    |/    \   |/    \   |____ \n |:    !     /    !     /   !     /   !   / \n |__________/__________/_________/_______/\n------Your Home Entertainment Service-------\n            Card-Game by PROXIMA\n','\n',char(10)),'CardGame_English.Guide',replace('@database \n\n\n@node main "CardGame / PROXIMA"\n+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|									    |\n|            ****   ***   ****   ****    ****   ***   *   *  *****          |\n|           *      *   *  *   *  *   *  *      *   *  ** **  *		    |\n|           *      *****  ****   *   *  *  **  *****  * * *  ***            |\n|           *      *   *  *   *  *   *  *   *  *   *  *   *  *              |\n|            ****  *   *  *   *  ****    ****  *   *  *   *  *****          |\n|       							    PROXIMA |\n+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n\n\n		@{"Introduction" link intro}\n		@{"The game menu" link jeu}\n                @{"Installation" link install}\n                @{"Notes" link notes}\n		\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node intro "Introduction"\n\n\n		      	 	CARDGAME\n				+-+-+-+-\n\n	  As its name tell it, this game is a cardgame, relatively \n	not well known.\n	\n	The base system is to announce the number of pleats you think\n	you''ll can do with yours cards, and to do anything to realise\n	it...\n\n\n	Code : Emmanuel Létondor	\n			Adress -> 13 les bruyéres / 69380 Chessy\n			E-Mail -> [email removed]\n\n	Gfx :  Guillaume Labrosse\n			Adress -> Le clos du verger / 01600 Toussieux\n\n	       Fabrice Mazat\n			Adress -> Le perroux / 69380 Alix		\n	\n\n	Mod :  Thierry Rivier\n			Adress -> La roche / 69620 Letra\n@endnode\n\n@node install "Installation"\n\n	\n	That''s very simple:\n\n	In the disk, there are some files and directories :\n\n	- Create a folder (Ex:CardGame) in your game directory,\n	  and copy all the files in this new dir.\n\n	- Copy the content of each directory of the disk in the\n	  corresponding one in your HD, for each file who doesn''t\n	  exists yet. (BUT NOT THE S DIRECTORY)	\n\n	Note: As the disk is about to be full, we couldn''t put\n	      all the required utilities as multiview or more, but\n     	      you normally have them in your Sys:Utilities/ folder.\n	      	\n					Finished !\n						(Doesn''t need any ASSIGN)\n@endnode	\n\n\n@node notes "Notes"\n\n\n\n---------------------------+ General +-----------------------------\n\n   We must say that ;\n\n	We are not responsible of any software or hardware degradation\n	which could be due to this game utilisation.\n\n	(How? I don''t know, but...)\n	\n\n---------------------+ Program rights +----------------------------\n\n   This program is entierely FREEWARE, and you can do everything you\n   want with this package, since that the readme files are not modified\n   and that you don''t use musics or graphics in SHAREWARE/COMMERCIAL\n   products without the autors permission.\n	\n\n\n---------------------+ Creators notes +----------------------------\n\n   Notes from the Coder, E.L :\n   +-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+\n\n	I just want to give you some little precisions concerning the\n	game: \n	The cards'' rotation isn''t precalculated, and the computer\n	is playing as any other player (He doesn''t "see" the player \n	cards !)...\n\n	The counted time is increased only during the reflexions phases.\n	(Choice of number of pleats, choice of playing a card).\n\n\n   Notes from the Graphist G.L :\n   +-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+\n\n\n\n  Cherche codeur volontaire et courageux pour gestion de 400 vues d''un\npetit mec.\n  Plus sérieusement , cherche contacts cools et motivés (Codeurs , \ngraphistes , musiciens ) pour développer de nouveaux produits .\nMalgré les protestations du codeur, les amateurs sont aussi les\nbienvenus ( surtout les nanas comme le souffle le codeur ).\n\n\n   Notes du Graphiste F.M :\n   +-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-\n\nSearching for old stamps + If you are a pretty blond, i''m interested;\n\n\n   Notes from the Musician, T.R :\n   +-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-+-\n\n\n		The electro-orgasms were digitalised by the coder,\n		i must say that.\n		Contact me for musics.		\n\n@endnode\n\n@node jeu "The Menu/Game screens"\n\n\n	- Greetings, load of fonts.\n\n	- Menu, Start of the music "Melodance"\n	\n		Game ........ : Start the game\n		Briefing .... : Explications concerning the rules\n		Dos cartes .. : Choice of the cards back\n		Hall Of Fames : Best players (Automatically saved in S:)\n		Quitter ..... : Quit...\n\n\n	- Game screen\n\n	The computer is situated on the upper of the screen, and\n	the human player is on the bottom.\n	Each player has three numbers :\n\n	  * On the left, the number of pleats you must do to win. \n	    Yellow: You must do some pleats.\n	    Blue  : You musn''t do any more pleat.\n	    Red   : You have made too mutch pleats.\n\n	  * On the right :  E (+F)\n\n		 E: Number of points.\n		   (We doesn''t care of the actual deal)\n		 F: Change of the score since the previous deal.\n	Exemple : 60 (-6) means that we just loose 6 points\n		  and that we actually have 60 points.\n\n\n	The choose of the card to play is made with the arrows on the\n	keyboard, and Return or up arrow validates.\n\n	You can press ''ESCape'' pratically when you want during the game,\n	to get back to the menu.\n\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',518436,8,0,NULL,NULL,'c_cardgm','scan',1780048435);
