g-reports, please\012   contact me via one of the following ways:\012\012   BBS:     The Undiscovered     +31-2294-4442    (28k8)\012                                 +31-2294-1442    (28k8)\012                                 +31-2294-tRY!    (28k8)\012\012            Last Outpost         +31-72-157682    (28k8)\012                                 +31-72-201182    (28k8)\012\012                          or on one of the MYSTiC boards!\012\012                         Internet: [email removed]\012                              IRC: #Rave, #Amiga (Nick: KiLLraVeN)\012\012                             /XF-Net: 44:100/100.1\012                             NLA-Net: 14:100/102.1\012@EndNode\012\012@Node Ami-X "Ami-Express information, dude!"\012\012     - - - ­ ­ ­ [ PLEASE SUPPORT AMi-EXPRESS AND REGiSTER! ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012\012   As  a  programmer I know how much time Joseph Hodge must have put into\012   developing  Ami-Express.  You are now benefiting from his efforts, why\012   not  reward  his  work  and register NOW!  With registering you secure\012   yourself  of support and the further development of Ami-Express.  I am\012   not asking money for ConfScan, but you would do me a big favour if you\012   would register yourself!\012\012                           You can order your copy at\012\012                 LightSpeed Technology (USA)   +1-305-964-4263\012\012            Or check your local Ami-Express support board near you!\012\012                                    Thanks!\012\012@EndNode\012\012@Node History "How did it end up like this - /X-PoWeR! - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\012                        - - - ­ ­ ­ HiSTORY ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   2.6.06   07-Oct-94 New       : Incorporated a new search-routine that\012                                  makes ConfScan find a file about 200%\012                                  faster! With ''N S U'' and ''N T'' it finds\012                                  a file within 1 sec, ALWAYS! That is\012                                  dir-file-size INDEPENDENT!\012\012   2.6.03   24-Aug-94 Fixed     : ConfScan no longer crashes if you have dir-\012                                  files with size 0 in your conference.\012                                  *Reported by Jake at Last Outpost*\012\012            24-Aug-94 Fixed     : If you didn''t have RELATIVE_CONFERENCES,\012                                  ConfScan could screw things up. Fixed.\012                                  *Reported by Zed on Channel-X*\012\012            24-Aug-94 Improved  : A pause between conferences would also\012                                  cause a pause between dirs and that is not\012                                  what it is supposed to do. Now it works\012                                  without problems.\012                                  *Reported by Zed on Channel-X*\012\012            24-Aug-94 Fixed     : If you had the ''Clear Screen'' option on,\012                                  the screen would also be cleared at the\012                                  end of the list, showing only the final\012                                  stats, not cool. So I fixed that.\012                                  *Reported by Muad''Dib*\012\012            24-Aug-94 Improved  : The Config menu has got a new and better\012                                  interface and now has two sections:\012                                  environmental options and CS options. Also,\012                                  when the config menu is called from ''N'' or\012                                  ''F'', the environmental options will show\012                                  up first (instead of the CS options that\012                                  used to come up first).\012\012            24-Aug-94 Improved  : Wrote a few new help files that are shorter\012                                  and (hopefully) easier to read and better\012                                  to understand.\012\012            25-Aug-94 Fixed     : If you have the ClearScreen option set, it\012                                  will now also clear the screen the first\012                                  time.\012                                  *Reported by Arcade/MST*\012\012   2.6.02   11-Aug-94 Fixed     : Tagging and flagging of files was a mess!\012                                  Things got messed up, nothing went right.\012                                  This will fix it, make sure to REMOVE any\012                                  file in your ...ConfScan/Users directory.\012                                  *Reported by Me*\012\012   2.6.01   07-Aug-94 New       : ConfScan now saves all the files that a\012                                  user flags in the sub-directory users in\012                                  the ConfScan directory. They are stored\012                                  like User_x, where x is the slotnumber\012                                  of the user. This has the advantage that\012                                  users can logoff, call back and still\012                                  have those files flagged.\012                                  \012                                  If the directory ../Users does not exist,\012                                  ConfScan will create it for you.\012                                  \012                                  For now, this is not an option, I intend\012                                  to make at optionable for either the sysop\012                                  and user.\012                                  *Requested by several sysops*\012\012            07-Aug-94 New       : The flagged files are no longer saved in\012                                  text format, a structure is now used for\012                                  storage. This decreases readability (if\012                                  you ever read them 8-) ), but increases\012                                  speed.\012\012            07-Aug-94 Fixed     : ConfScan now also works under /X 4.x.\012\012   2.6.00   24-Jul-94 New       : When a dirfile is being copied (ie. you\012                                  have the copy-dirfiles turned on), the\012                                  user will see a percentage displaying the\012                                  progress of the copy (just like the scanning\012                                  routine).\012                                  This only happens when you have the USE-\012                                  PERCENTAGE option turned on.\012\012                      Improved  : Built in some more error information on \012                                  some parts of the program. Home usage only.\012\012   2.5.63   23-Jul-94 Fixed     : The ConfxCMD bug is gone. I just had to take\012                                  a closer look. Ami-Express gives the number\012                                  of the current conference MINUS 1. I knew\012                                  that, but forgot it later on in the routine.\012                                  *Reported by Zed at Channel-X*\012\012                      New       : From now on, registered versions are \012                                  available from me. Registered version do not\012                                  have special functions or hidden features,\012                                  they are just registered (shown at startup).\012                                  The only advantage is that you will most\012                                  likely get the current available version.\012\012                      Fixed     : MAJOR BUGFIX! For some incredibly STUPID\012                                  reason I forgot to check for hold access\012                                  with the ''F'' command 8-( My sincere apologies\012                                  for such a mistake, how could this slip\012                                  through all tests...\012                                  *Reported by TyCooN*\012                                  \012   2.5.62   16-Jul-94 Fixed     : It appears it still does not work properly.\012                                  Made a quick fix on-line 8-(\012                                  *Reported by Zed at Channel-X*\012\012   2.5.61   11-Jul-94 Fixed     : When installed as an ConfxCMD command, it\012                                  would look in the wrong Conference for the\012                                  icon information. Is fixed.\012                                  *Reported by Zed at Channel-X*\012\012                                  * R E L E A S E  V E R S i O N *\012\012   2.5.60   28-Jun-94 New       : ''N S G'' now works. It stands for "New Since\012                                  last logon Global" and does the same as\012                                  ''CS''.\012                                  *Requested by EMPiRE/MST*\012\012            30-Jun-94 Changed   : Removed the Beta testers registration info.\012            \012   2.5.59   26-Jun-94 Fixed     : Changed the header of ConfScan, ''cause\012                                  ArCaDe is now also a MYSTiC member.\012\012   2.5.58   20-Jun-94 New       : CTRL-C is now recognized at the flag/tag\012                                  prompt in ConfScan.\012                                  *Requested by Sal-One*\012\012                      Improved  : Made the tagging routine a little bit more\012                                  robust.\012\012   2.5.57   20-Jun-94 Fixed     : Any comments between P/N and the file date\012                                  are now shown with a blue background colour\012                                  from the P/N to the file date (no more spaces\012                                  between the comment and the file date).\012\012   2.5.56   18-Jun-94 Fixed     : The ''P'' bug is fixed.\012                                  *Reported by Tycoon/MYSTiC*\012\012                      Improved  : Replaced an Execute() routine with System().\012\012   2.5.55   15-Jun-94 Fixed     : I forgot to put a return (''\n'') after the\012                                  comment line in the callerslog.\012                                  *Reported (first) by Muad''Dib/5D*\012\012                      Fixed     : Replaced some of the ESC[M and ESC[K\012                                  commands with 79 spaces. I find this\012                                  *STUPiD* but there are still terminals\012                                  around (especialy on the MS-DOS platform\012                                  that DO NOT recognize them!! So incredibly\012                                  lame!\012\012                      Changed   : The task priority of ConfScan is now always\012                                  0. I used to adjust the priority to the\012                                  same as ACP, but that could slow the system\012                                  down if you had it above 0. This evens the\012                                  CPU time a bit if you have multiple nodes.\012\012                      Fixed     : The temporary files in T: were not removed\012                                  if you had ''CopyDirFiles'' activated.\012\012   2.5.54   13-Jun-94 Fixed     : The `FileHelp'' files for every conference\012                                  sometimes were not shown. Fixed it.\012                                  *Reported by EMPiRE/MYSTiC*\012\012                      Improved  : The user can now also enter values like\012                                  -5 or `T'' when ConfScan asks for a date\012                                  via a prompt.\012\012                      Fixed     : The ''N'' command wouldn''t show the existence\012                                  of the [H]old dir to people who had access\012                                  for it if ConfScan asked for it via the\012                                  prompt (Which directory...).\012\012                      Improved  : The output to the Callerslog is now modified\012                                  to "Directory Scan from (xx-xx-xx)" to gain\012                                  compatibility with some callerslog-scan-\012                                  programs.\012                                  *Requested by Sal-One/TRSi^ZENiTH*\012\012                      Fixed     : if you had used the ''P'' space and filesize\012                                  in the filedir (DiRx) for a comment (for\012                                  instance "DELETED!"), than the second ''E''\012                                  would not be shown. is fixed now.\012\012                      Fixed     : Text-files were not shown with the [V]iew\012                                  function (still a result of the multi-\012                                  langual stuff... sh*t).\012                                  *Reported by TyCooN/MYSTiC*\012\012                      Fixed     : The [V]iew option was not multi-node yet,\012                                  fixed that ofcourse.\012\012   2.5.53   06-Jun-94 Fixed     : Due to the new multi-langual stuff in \012                                  ConfScan, the [V]iew function failed in\012                                  locating the output of the [V]iew function.\012                                  *Reported by Just Another Freak*\012\012   2.5.52   05-Jun-94 Fixed     : The search routine failed sometimes if you\012                                  had banners in your dirfiles. This has now\012                                  been fixed.\012                                  *Reported by Tycoon/MYSTiC*\012\012   2.5.51   04-Jun-94 New       : At the prompt there now is a percentage\012                                  shown. it indicates how much of the files\012                                  have been shown already.\012                                  \012                      Improved  : Added credits for Pascal (Arcade).\012\012   2.5.50   02-Jun-94 Improved  : Searching routine has been sped up a\012                                  little bit. instead of the stack, i\012                                  now use some of the CPU''s registers.\012                                  Especially 030+ users will benefit\012                                  from this. if you don''t have an 030,\012                                  go buy one! :-)\012\012            03-Jun-94 Improved  : All ConfScan help files can now be made\012                                  multi-langual just like in Ami-Express\012                                  itself (with .TXT and .TXT.GR). it now\012                                  takes the ScreenTypes.info in account\012                                  when showing a textfile, meaning that\012                                  the helpfile filename is now built up\012                                  like this:\012                                  \012                                  ConfScan.<CMD>.Help<ACS>.<GROUP>\012                                  \012                                  Where CMD = Command name (f.i. CS)\012                                        ACS = Accesslevel, but if the\012                                              level is not found, the\012                                              <ACS> will be skipped.\012                                      GROUP = Language. Factory settings\012                                              are .TXT (Mono) and .TXT.GR\012                                              (Colour). But you can add\012                                              more types in the icon.\012                                  *Requested by AtomiX (Here you go ;) )*\012\012            03-Jun-94 Fixed     : The infamous ''f'' bug has been removed.\012                                  it only occured when you had the "Copy\012                                  DirFiles" option on (Sysop Prefs)...\012                                  *Reported by Brutus*\012\012            03-Jun-94 Fixed     : Starting a download from ConfScan no longer\012                                  causes Ami-Express to perform a fake log-\012                                  out if you said ''Goodbye after'', this time\012                                  the user will be kicked off the board.\012                                  THiS WiLL ONLY WORK WiTH VERSiON 3.38+ !!\012                                  *Reported by ->>Constrictor<<-*\012\012\012            03-Jun-94 Improved  : CONFSCAN NOW HAS GOT A FUCKiNG FAST ASM\012                                  SEARCH ROUTiNE AND KiCKS ASS! USUALLY\012                                  ALL DATES ARE FOUND WiTHiN 2-3 SECONDS!!\012                                  \012                                  *> ASM CODE WRiTTEN BY PASCAL EEFTiNCK <*\012                                  *> THANKS A LOT MAN! iT WORKS GREAT !! <*\012\012            04-Jun-94 New       : At the CS-Prompt (More) you can now enter\012                                  a ''P'' to manually override the Full Desc\012                                  mode giving you a full page of new files\012                                  instead of checking for broken file de-\012                                  scriptions. This works only for that time,\012                                  the next prompt will still use Full Desc\012                                  mode (unless you press ''P'' again).\012\012   2.5.49   27-May-94 Improved  : What do you know? it''s my birthday! :)\012                                  Never mind that, I did manage to fit in\012                                  something new anyway... if you now press\012                                  ''Q'' in the config menu (''N W'') nothing\012                                  will be saved.\012                                  *Requested by Muad''Dib/5D*\012                                  (Thanks for the tapez man :) ).\012\012            27-May-94 New/Fixed : You can now [V]iew files from the hold\012                                  dir (but ofcourse only if you have got\012                                  hold access).\012                                  *Reported by Muad''Dib/5D*\012\012            01-Jun-94 Fixed     : And once again I had to fix the date \012                                  routine ''cause June wasn''t recognized\012                                  correctly (stupid bug!!!). Sorry guyz.\012                                  *Reported by Muad''Dib/5D*\012\012   2.5.48   21-May-94 New       : The /-\ routine has been replaced by an\012                                  percentage routine. So instead of the /-\\012                                  pointer you get to see a percentage showing\012                                  how much of the dirfile has been scanned.\012                                  The config program has been changed as well\012                                  for this, I just renamed the "Busypointer"\012                                  field to "Use Percentage" so if you had the\012                                  Busypointer on, you will get the % now.\012                                  ** YOU SAW iT HERE FiRST! **\012\012            22-May-94 Fixed     : The ''F'' function wouldn''t recognize the\012                                  hold dir if you didn''t specify it at the\012                                  prompt. Now it does.\012\012   2.5.47   20-May-94 Improved  : Replaced some old routines with newer and\012                                  better ones. This is the finishing up part\012                                  before the release.\012\012   2.5.46   17-May-94 Fixed     : The ''F'' command wouldn''t show the FileHelp\012                                  file if you enter it without arguments.\012                                  *Reported by Tycoon/MYSTiC*\012\012                      Fixed     : if you had the ''always show full desc'' mode\012                                  on and you [V]iewed a file, ConfScan was \012                                  confused and tags went wrong. is now fixed.\012                                  \012                      Improved  : if you have the ''Clear Screen'' flag on, the\012                                  screen will also be cleared at the start of\012                                  ConfScan, not after the first prompt.\012\012                      Fixed     : if you left the ''F'' command with enter you\012                                  would still get a line telling you that there\012                                  were 0 bytes and 0 files.\012\012   2.5.45   12-May-94 Fixed     : Bug in the ''prompt'' routine sometimes caused\012                                  for an infinite loop, the only way out was\012                                  the ''Q'' option. is now fixed.\012                                  *Reported by Brutus/Brutal Approach*\012\012                      Fixed     : Replaced some old stick-m-together routines\012                                  with the AddPart routine. This solves the\012                                  problem that ConfScan can''t find certain\012                                  files (such as dirfiles).\012                                  *Reported by Brutus/Brutal Approach*\012\012   2.5.44   10-May-94 Fixed     : Minor bug in the config menu is fixed.\012\012   2.5.43   10-May-94 Improved  : Radical change in the config menu! it now\012                                  consists of two menus instead of 1. You\012                                  can swap menus with ''Y''. Save/exit with ''Z''.\012\012                      New       : You can have ConfScan always show you the\012                                  full description of a file. That means that\012                                  if you get the `More'' prompt in the middle\012                                  of a file description, ConfScan will notice\012                                  this and show the next files until that \012                                  file is about to disappear from your screen\012                                  showing its full description. This is quite\012                                  a nice feature if you ask me ;-) Very nice\012                                  and USER CONFiGURABLE.\012\012                      New       : You can have ConfScan clear the screen\012                                  after every `More'' prompt. This is also\012                                  USER CONFiGURABLE. ConfScan will *NOT*\012                                  clear the screen when you are in non-stop\012                                  mode (either with the `ns'' argument or `n''\012                                  from the `More'' prompt).\012\012                      New       : You can have ConfScan show you just the\012                                  first line of file descriptions. This is\012                                  also USER CONFiGURABLE.\012\012                                  * New Preferences Structure, conversion *\012                                  * util required for sysops. Does NOT    *\012                                  * affect user config files!             *\012\012   2.5.42   06-May-94 Improved  : ConfScan now recognizes the new prefs that\012                                  the Config program saves. This asked for the\012                                  whole ''Config Menu'' part to be rewritten.\012\012                                  * NEW PREFS FORMAT FOR USERS! OLD CONFiG *\012                                        * FiLES NEED TO BE DELETED! *\012\012                      Fixed     : The "introfile" was shown with extra lines.\012                                  Also put an ESC[0m in front of the intro-\012                                  file to prevent colour leakage.\012\012                      Improved  : All parts of ConfScan have been updated with\012                                  the new prefs structure (phew).\012\012   2.5.41   03-May-94 Fixed     : The summary of the conferences with their\012                                  bytes and files could get messed up if you\012                                  had long conference names. This is now fixed\012                                  and set to 20 chars.\012                                  *Reported by Muad''Dib/5D*\012\012   2.5.40   01-May-94 Fixed     : Tagging the same files twice could happen\012                                  if user tagged, exited and tagged something\012                                  in the same list again. is fixed.\012\012                      Improved  : When you press ''C'' at the prompt, the screen\012                                  will be cleared and the last file with its\012                                  COMPLETE description will be shown. So that\012                                  means you will always get to see ALL file\012                                  descriptions if you keep using C.\012                                  *Requested by Easy Rider/MST/TRSi*\012\012   2.5.39   27-Apr-94 Removed   : When users use ''CS'' they no longer get\012                                  to see how many files/bytes were uploaded\012                                  in that conf. it was ugly :( Design rulez.\012                                  *Requested by Muad''Dib/5D & TyCooN/MST*\012\012   2.5.38   27-Apr-94 Fixed     : Memory bug fixed, thanks to Mungwall.\012                                  Now there are no Enforcer hits (there\012                                  never were) and no Mungwall hits.\012                                  *Crying by TyCooN/MST :)*\012\012   2.5.37   25-Apr-94 New       : When in multi-conference mode, accumulative\012                                  figures will be shown after each conference.\012\012                      New       : Added ''NS'' support. Many users wanted to be\012                                  able to have the file listing scroll by non\012                                  stop. if you enter ''ns'' after the command,\012                                  all the files will scroll non-stop. This \012                                  works for ALL commands (N, F and CS).\012\012                      New       : ConfScan can now give a small overview of\012                                  all conferences with their shown bytes and\012                                  number of files. To do this, you have to \012                                  meet a few conditions:\012                                  * Add a ''+'' after the CS-command\012                                    i.e. "CS +" or "CS T ns +"\012                                  * More than 1 conference needs to have new\012                                    files (so it doesn''t work with ''F'' or\012                                    ''N'' since that isn''t usefull).\012                                  * Access level of user is high enough, when\012                                    an user has got hold-access, he is able\012                                    to see the overview.\012\012   2.5.36   25-Apr-94 Fixed     : All returns (\n\r) are now done internally.\012                                  So any more ''Pause more/y/n'' are from now\012                                  on impossible. This way I circumvent the\012                                  3.38 ''problem''.\012\012                      Changed   : if there is no date on the appropriate\012                                  location, it will no longer be high-\012                                  lighted again. This should speed up the\012                                  display a bit.\012                                  *Requested by MKO!/PDX*\012\012   2.5.35   13-Apr-94 Improved  : Replaced all ''/X-DeSiGn'' logo''s with the\012                                  new /X-PoWeR! logo''s... too many people\012                                  were abusing the /X-DeSiGn trademark :(\012\012                      Fixed     : ConfScan would sometimes abusively take\012                                  dates in file descriptions as the file\012                                  date... :( Fixed now.\012\012   2.5.34   13-Apr-94 Fixed     : When pressing ''D'' while you were in tag-\012                                  mode, any file you flagged would not be\012                                  noticed... oops... fixed now.\012                                  *Reported by Tycoon/MYSTiC*\012\012                      Improved  : Sped up the output on your screen.\012\012   2.5.33   11-Apr-94 Fixed     : To prevent problems with NONSTOPTEXT, i\012                                  have taken care of the /n/r''s myself. This\012                                  eliminates occurances of ''(pause) etc.''.\012                                  \012                      Improved  : The ''F'' command doesn''t needlesly copy\012                                  itself to T: anymore unless you specify it\012                                  in the icon with COPY_DiRFiLES. This also\012                                  increases the ''F'' command.\012\012   2.5.32   06-Apr-94 New       : You can now directly start the Download\012                                  from ConfScan with the [D], this can be\012                                  done either at the prompt or when you''re\012                                  tagging.\012\012                      New       : You can now directly start KiLLER from\012                                  ConfScan with the [!], this can be done\012                                  done either at the prompt or when you''re\012                                  tagging.\012\012   2.5.31   03-Apr-94 Fixed     : Wooops, forgot to remove the extra space\012                                  in ''normal'' lines, this caused the first\012                                  line of descriptions to be one char to\012                                  the left.\012\012                      Fixed     : Comments with BossNuke and KiLLER are also\012                                  properly displayed again (nobody had noticed\012                                  it though :) ).\012\012   2.5.30   02-Apr-94 Improved  : No more extra space between the filename  \012                                  and the file status (N or P). That way a\012                                  sysop can simply grab the dirfile from\012                                  screen and insert it in his own dirfile\012                                  w/o having to edit it.\012                                  *Requested by some dudes at Last Outpost*\012\012   2.5.29   01-Apr-94 Fixed     : internal fix. Never mind.\012\012   2.5.28   01-Apr-94 New       : intergrated the bytes and files into the\012                                  last line (used to be: "READY SCANNiNG"\012                                  but now holds the number of bytes and files\012                                  shown).\012                                  *Requested by Empire/MST*\012\012   2.5.27   31-Mar-94 New       : When ConfScan is ready scanning, you get\012                                  to see the total amount of files and bytes\012                                  that an user got to see.\012                                  *Requested by Chaplin/PHUN*\012\012   2.5.26   30-Mar-94 Improved  : Better Config colours (CS W, N W etc.)\012\012   2.5.25   27-Mar-94 New       : For more flexibility, you can now select\012                                  your own colours for the file listing:\012                                  LiST.FiLE=xx   - File name\012                                  LiST.STATUS=xx - File status (P or N)\012                                  LiST.SiZE=xx   - File size\012                                  LiST.DATE=xx   - File date\012                                  LiST.DESC=xx   = File desc\012                                  xx = ANSi code (31=red, 32=green etc.)\012\012                      Improved  : The help on the ''More'' options is now\012                                  external, you now have 4 more helpfiles:\012                                  ConfScan.More_General.Help - General help\012                                  ConfScan.More_Tagging.Help - Tagging help\012                                  ConfScan.More_Killing.Help - Killing help\012                                  ConfScan.More_Viewing.Help - Viewing help\012                                  This is done because you can set access \012                                  levels for viewing and killing and you can\012                                  turn of Tagging. So those files will ONLY\012                                  be showed when an user has access.\012\012                      Improved  : To KiLL files you can now also press DEL\012                                  (this also goes when you are in TAG mode).\012\012                      Improved  : To quit ConfScan you can also press ESC.\012\012   2.5.24   26-Mar-94 Improved  : Replaced NO_BOSSNUKE and NO_KiLLER by one\012                                  tooltype: NO_NUKER_SUPPORT\012\012   2.5.23   25-Mar-94 New       : New tooltype: NO_BUSYPOiNTER. if you put\012                                  this in your icon you will NOT see a /-\\012                                  spinning after `Scanning...''. This will\012                                  speed up the searching though.\012\012   2.5.22   24-Mar-94 Fixed     : Put the COPY_DiRFiLES back because this\012                                  can be handy for multi-node systems!\012                                  *Requested by Muad''Dib/5D*\012\012   2.5.21   22-Mar-94 Fixed     : Search routine now has a few extra checks\012                                  to make sure it is a date we got and not\012                                  a date from within a description\012\012   2.5.20   22-Mar-94 Improved  : Searching for files is now almost 100%(!)\012                                  faster thanks to a routine from Tycoon of\012                                  MYSTiC. Thanks man! it really is fast now!\012                                  \012                                  This makes the tooltype COPY_DiRFiLES un-\012                                  usable. So scratch that one :)\012\012                      Fixed     : The `sscanf'' function in SAS/C sometimes\012                                  fucks up, replaced with my own routine.\012\012   2.5.19   19-Mar-94 Fixed     : Sometimes KiLLER wouldn''t recognize kills\012                                  made with ConfScan. That is now fixed.\012                                  This also fix the Download-bug (not seeing\012                                  tagged files).\012\012   2.5.18   16-Mar-94 Fixed     : Some internal changes. This fixes one of\012                                  the most hard-headed bugs! \012\012   2.5.22   11-Mar-94 New       : KiLLing of files is now possible when in\012                                  [T]ag mode with the [K].\012\012                      New       : Viewing of files is now possible when in\012                                  [T]ag mode with the [V].\012\012                      Fixed     : Changed the colours of the hgh-light mode,\012                                  instead of light blue background with blue\012                                  characters it is now a blue background with\012                                  white characters (red if you are on the\012                                  local node).\012\012   2.5.13   07-Mar-94 Fixed     : Replaced a real old routine with a more\012                                  modern one. Hope this fixes ''THE'' bug :(\012\012                      Fixed     : Esc[0m are now only given the before a\012                                  filename and not every line.\012                                  *Reported by EMPiRE/MST*\012\012   2.5.12   06-Mar-94 New       : Added support for my nuker, KiLLER.\012                                  KiLLER comment are shown with a light-blue\012                                  background and dark-blue foreground.\012                                  New tooltype: NO_KiLLER (if specified any\012                                  comments made with KiLLER will not be\012                                  high-lighted).\012\012                      Fixed     : Some bug fixes (internal).\012\012   2.5.08   22-Feb-94 New       : Cursorkeys can now be used when user\012                                  wants to [T]ag files. Old keys are\012                                  still supported though.\012\012                      New       : When Tagging a file with ''0'' the cursor\012                                  will jump to the next file.\012\012                      Fixed     : Minor bug fix.\012\012                      Improved  : Guide file was changed drastically to\012                                  make it better reading material. Setup\012                                  a bit different. Now with installation\012                                  instructions for 3 levels of skill of\012                                  the sysops (stupid, newby and veteran).\012\012   2.5.07   21-Feb-94 New       : Added a few tooltypes so the sysop can \012                                  decide which filetypes are not supported.\012                                  Tooltypes are:\012                                  NO_DMS_ViEW for .DMS files,\012                                  NO_LHA_ViEW for .LhA/LZH files,\012                                  NO_ZiP_ViEW for .ZiP files and\012                                  NO_TXT_ViEW for .TXT/DOC/ASC/NFO files.\012                                  *Requested by Muad''Dib* (Stupid DMS bug).\012\012   2.5.06   21-Feb-94 Fixed     : Minor bug fix (users who have just viewed\012                                  a file cannot tag files after that, makes\012                                  sense ofcourse since the screen is totally\012                                  messed up).\012\012   2.5.05   20-Feb-94 New       : File viewer built in. Supported files are:\012                                  DMS, LHA, LZH, ASC, TXT, DOC, NFO and ZiP.\012\012                      New       : New tooltype: ViEW_ACCESS. Here you can enter\012                                  the minimum access a user must have to be\012                                  able to [V]iew a file. When an user has got\012                                  no access, he will not be aware of the ViEW\012                                  option (it is not shown as an option).\012                                  Example: ViEW_ACCESS=100\012\012                      Change    : Changed the colours a little bit to get a\012                                  certain standard. Still not perfect though.\012\012   2.5.04   19-Feb-94 Fixed     : Some coloured file-descriptions would some-\012                                  times fuck up the rest of the file-listings\012                                  with colour. is now fixed.\012\012                      New       : Registration info added, special registered\012                                  version can now be made (for beta-testing\012                                  purposes).\012                                  \012                      Fixed     : Longer BossNuke descriptions are now detected\012                                  and properly processed.\012\012   2.5.03   19-Feb-94 Special   : Tailermade version for Muad''Dib/5D\012\012   2.5.02   12-Feb-94 New       : Added a tooltype: COPY_DiRFiLES. This tells\012                                  ConfScan to copy the dir-file (dirx) to T:\012                                  first and start scanning the file there.\012                                  *Requested by TyCooN/MST*\012\012   2.5.00   10-Feb-94 Fixed     : Date entries don''t fail anymore when you\012                                  were asked for a date.\012                                  *Report by Muad''Dib/5D*\012\012                      Fixed     : The hold dir is now accepted when asked\012                                  for a dir to scan.\012\012                      Fixed     : Display of nuked files Improved.\012\012                      New       : Added a ''Scanning...'' routine so you can\012                                  see that ConfScan is busy.\012                                  *Requested by many sysops*\012\012                      New       : Added support for Dir-Style by The Bird.\012                                  You can use this dir-styler now without\012                                  any problems.\012                                  *Requested by [-sAl-øNe!/TRS¡-]*\012\012   2.4.01   13-Jan-93 Fixed     : Did a final bug fix for the jump routine.\012                                  it failed if you were not running your\012                                  BBS with relative conferences. it is now\012                                  made that it can''t fail! (He said... :) )\012\012                      New       : I split up the Download part and the\012                                  scanning part of ConfScan. You know have a\012                                  separate download program.\012                                  \012                                  I also split up the helpfiles from within\012                                  ConfScan. This is all done for reasons of\012                                  SPEED. ConfScan will start up faster this\012                                  way. And you can now edit the help file\012                                  to your needs.\012\012   2.3.03   13-Jan-94 Fixed     : Memory bug fixed! Yes, finally! This was\012                                  a strange bug, but with the help of\012                                  Tycoon/MST it is now gone! No more memory\012                                  is being eaten everytime you use it!\012                                  *Reported by NORAD (Aces High BBS)*\012\012                      New       : A new tooltype in the ConfScan icon. if you\012                                  specify "NO_BOSSNUKE" all comments made\012                                  with BossNuke will NOT be highlighted.\012\012                      Fixed     : Updated the built-in docs so now the T\012                                  option is added.\012\012   2.3.01   03-Jan-94 Fixed     : Jump bug fixed. Seems to go okay now,\012                                  but if I get no bug-reports, I cannot\012                                  fix it! So if you got a problem with\012                                  it, CONTACT ME!\012                                  *Reported by EMPiRE/MST*\012\012   2.2.01   01-Jan-94 Fixed     : ''January'' bug fix! Stupid bug! :(\012                                  *Reported by Muad''Dib/5D & Tycoon/MST*\012                      Fixed     : -x days bug fixed. Now works 100%!\012                                  *Reported by Tycoon/MST*\012                      New/Fixed : ''f h'' is possible now\012                                  *Reported by Muad''Dib/5D*\012\012   2.1.02   26-Oct-93  New      : New option, `T'' will show the uploaded\012                                  files of [T]oday. it can be used instead\012                                  of `S'' or a date. Example: N T U, CS T.\012                                  *Requested by: sHARON/SCooPeX*\012                       Fixed    : Better BossNuke support, taglines of\012                                  BossNuke (`...<BoSSNuKe'') are now\012                                  displayed with a red background and yel-\012                                  low characters.\012\012\012   2.1.01   23-Oct-93  New      : File-counter, when you flag a file you\012                                  will see the actual number of files an\012                                  user has flagged sofar. if a user TAGS\012                                  his files, the number of files will be\012                                  shown at the bottom-right.\012                                  *Requested by: EMPiRE*\012                       Fixed    : File tagging Improved a little by allo-\012                                  cating a little bit more memory for it.\012\012\012   2.0.31   10-Oct-93  OFFiCiAL RELEASE OF VERSiON 2.0!\012                       Fixed    : Correct recognition of ''sent-by'' lines.\012\012   2.0.27   08-Oct-93  Fixed    : Config menu also recognizes conferences\012                                  without a file-base. They will not be\012                                  shown in the menu.\012\012   2.0.26   08-Oct-93  New/Fixed: Auto-recognition of mail conferences or\012                                   other conferences without a file-base,\012                                   the option in the icon to exclude certain\012                                   conferences from being scanned will stay\012                                   active.\012                                  `F'' command bug fixed (conferences without\012                                   file-base could cause problems.\012\012   2.0.23   07-Oct-93  New/Fixed: Nuker support added\012                                  Improved downloading command\012                                  F command included\012                                  Better help files\012                                  Changed file display a bit for tagging\012                                  Added BNF support ;)\012                                  Version information ($VER) Improved\012                                  Better "NO CARRiER" protection\012                                  Who information for /X added (i forgot!)\012\012   2.0.01 - 2.0.22     Beta-releases and all sorts of bug-fixing. See above.\012\012   2.0.00  20-Sep-93   MAJOR UPDATE! First beta-release!\012                       New options: Downloading included in program\012                                    N S U like behavior implemented\012                                    File flagging implemented\012                                    File tagging implemented\012                                    ANSi colour display\012                                    Lines between files possible\012                                    Returns between files possible\012                                    NewDates can be shown\012                                    Sentby''s can be filtered out\012                                    Special remarks in dir-listing are\012                                            shown high-lighted!\012                                    Clear Screen & Continue implemented\012                                    Skip conference implemented\012                                    Nonstop display this conference\012                                    Nonstop display all conferences\012                                    Bigger & Better config menu\012                                    Bigger & Better info for users\012                                    Download command can show all flagged\012                                        files from all conferences\012                                    AutoJump to next conference where user\012                                        has flagged files (also after DL)\012                                    Pause between conferences is now optional\012                                    CTRL-C is detected, program can be stopped\012\012   1.7     18-Sep-93   Bug-Fix: Dir-files still caused problems, is fixed!\012                       Bug-Fix: No more trouble when inserting an extra\012                                space after the conference numbers in the\012                                config menu.\012\012   1.6     11-Sep-93   Bug-Fix: Dir-files with lines longer than 150\012                       characters caused a guru :-(. The maximum is now set\012                       to 300 characters, that should be enough.\012\012   1.5     25-Aug-93   First public release\012\012   All  previous  information is either lost or not worth to be mentioned,\012   it''s  the usual stuff like "new option" and "fixed a bug".  Believe me,\012   you  don''t wanna know.  From now on the history file will be kept up to\012   date...\012\012@EndNode\012\012@Node Errors "What have you done wrong? - /X-PoWeR! - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\012              - - - ­ ­ ­ [ POSSiBLE ERROR MESSAGES ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   Since  nobody  is perfect, there is a slight chance an error may occur,\012   there are only a few possible errors, so here they are:\012\012   ­ "Couldn''t allocate memory! Too little memory?"\012\012     Do you have enough memory free to run ConfScan?  The program uses about\012     36Kb  of memory (largest block in once is 32Kb for copying files).  The\012     best  thing  you can do is reset and try again.  If it still fails, you\012     better  buy  a  memory  expansion...  If you have enough memory and you\012     still get this error, then please contact me.\012\012   ­ "Couldn''t open temporary file for output! Too little memory?"\012\012     ConfScan  uses a temporary file to store the files which will be showed\012     to  you  later,  this  temp  file  is in the T:  directory, do you have\012     enough  memory  left?   If your file-listings are really big, this file\012     can  be  become  quite large (if you have masses of new warez every day\012     (ofcourse  you  have  :-)).  Maybe the file is still present in T:  and\012     this  MiGHT  cause  the problem, check the T:  directory...  else reset\012     and try again.\012\012   ­ "Couldn''t open file: <name>"\012\012     For  some reason, ConfScan was not able to open the file <name>.  Maybe\012     it  was  in  use by another program?  Best thing to do is reset and try\012     again.   Another  possibility  is that you have not reserved some Ami-X\012     Net- mail area''s and ConfScan tries to open a dir file...\012\012   ­ "Couldn''t open icon.library!"\012\012     If  this  happens,  you better install the icon.libary, but this cannot\012     happen, ''cause /X 3.xx uses it also, so if the icon.library is missing,\012     Ami-X will not startup :-).\012\012   ­ "Error reading from input file during filecopy!"\012\012     It  seems that something went wrong while reading the input file during\012     a  file  copy.  File copies only occur while scanning and when you exit\012     the config menu.  Reset and try again.\012\012   ­ "Error writing to output file during filecopy!"\012\012     Something  went  wrong  while  writing to the output file during a file\012     copy.  This can only happen while scanning and when you exit the config\012     menu.  Reset and try again.\012\012   ­ "Couldn''t open your config file!"\012\012     For  some  reason ConfScan was not able to create your own config file!\012     This should always be possible, better reset and try again.\012\012   Well,  that''s  all  the  errors  ConfScan can create.  If you don''t get\012   ConfScan working on your system, just @{"give a me call" link Killraven} and i''ll make sure\012   it will work!\012\012@EndNode\012\012@Node Tagging "Tagging, the new way of flagging! - © KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\012                  - - - ­ ­ ­ [ TAGGiNG OF FiLES ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   Instead of having to type the filenames (or paste them with PowerSnap)\012   users  (and  you) can walk over the filenames with the cursor keys and\012   select them with spacebar or the ''0''.\012\012   The  idea  comes from some PC terminal programs (and not BBS programs!)\012   that  allow  their  users to let them ''walk'' over the files that are on\012   the screen and with one simple touch of the keyboard the file is marked\012   as  ''flagged''  (or  tagged in this case).  I have implemented this cool\012   method in my door! ConfScan was the FiRST to use this method. \012\012   If  the  user  wishes  to  TAG his files a small bar will appear on the\012   first  filename  that  is  on the screen after the last ''more'' shown on\012   screen.   With  the cursor keys on the numeric keypad the user can move\012   up  and  down over the filenames.  With the `0'' the user can select and\012   deselect  a  file.   A selected file can be recognized at the `*'' being\012   after the filename.\012\012   Flagging  and tagging can be used through each other, it doesn''t matter\012   if  you  flag first and then tag, it will work.  You might wonder if it\012   still works when the users has no colours on screen (no ANSi).  Yes, it\012   works, besides the bar there will also be a ''<'' sign after the filename\012   to point out the current filename.\012\012   This method works ofcourse with all ConfScan imitations (N, F and CS).\012\012   If  you  also are an /X Coder and you want to know more about how I did\012   it, just contact me at Channel-X and I will help you further.\012\012               ­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­\012               ATTENTiON! ATTENTiON! ATTENTiON! ATTENTiON!\012               ­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­\012\012   Before  you  all  start screaming and yellin'' that there is a bug in my\012   program,  you  can  tag  files that are displayed since the last ''more''\012   line  (or from the beginning if there was no ''more'').  This is done for\012   programmer''s  simplicity  ;) Maybe in the future it will be possible to\012   tag  all  files that are on screen, but that is more difficult than you\012   might think (multiple conferences on one screen and so forth).\012@EndNode\012\012@Node More "Gimme more! Gimme more! - By KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\012                  - - - ­ ­ ­ [ MORE OF CONFSCAN ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   All the help is put into separate files for your convenience.  This is\012   done  to  support  multiple screentypes (so you can have separate help\012   files  for  every  screentype  (=  language)).   Also, because you can\012   determine  access  levels  for  each  action,  separate help files are\012   needed.  So here they are:\012\012   ConfScan.More_General.Help.TXT ^ General Help, available to all\012   ConfScan.More_KiLLiNG.Help.TXT ^ Help for KiLLING of files\012   ConfScan.More_Tagging.Help.TXT ^ Help for Tagging files\012   ConfScan.More_Viewing.Help.TXT ^ Help for [V]iewing files\012\012                       In that order, their contents are:\012\012                         ^-^-^-^-[ B R E A K ]-^-^-^-^\012\012                              MORE ABOUT CONFSCAN\012 \012     [P] ^ Show a full page of files     [A] ^ Non Stop ALL conferences\012     [F] ^ Flag files                    [N] ^ Non Stop CURRENT conference\012     [C] ^ Clear Screen                  [S] ^ Skip current conference\012     [Q] ^ Quit ConfScan                 [D] ^ Start downloading\012\012                         ^-^-^-^-[ B R E A K ]-^-^-^-^\012\012                                 KiLLiNG FiLES \012 \012  [K] ^ KiLL FiLES\012 \012        Either in Tag mode or at the prompt. With ''K'' you can select files\012        that need to be KiLLED later on with KiLLER. The colour of the bar\012        will change if you are in tag mode.\012 \012  [!] ^ Start KiLLER (you will not return to ConfScan afterwards).\012\012                         ^-^-^-^-[ B R E A K ]-^-^-^-^\012\012                          TAGGiNG FiLES WiTH CONFSCAN\012 \012  [T] ^ Tag files\012 \012        Use cursor keys to move the bar over the screen. Press space to\012        select or deselect a file. An asterisk (*) will appear after it''s\012        name meaning it is selected and the colour of the bar will change.\012\012                         ^-^-^-^-[ B R E A K ]-^-^-^-^\012\012                                 ViEWiNG FiLES\012 \012  [V] ^ View Files\012 \012        Either at the prompt or when you are tagging, with ''V'' you will\012        get to view that file.\012 \012        Supported file types: DMS ^ Disk Masher  (Amiga Disk Archives)\012                              ZIP ^ Zip          (msdos File Archives)\012                              LHA ^ LhA(rc)      (Amiga File Archives)\012                              TXT/DOC/NFO/NF0    (Text files)\012\012@EndNode\012\012@Node Important "Update Information - © 1994 KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\012                - - - ­ ­ ­ [ UPDATE iNFORMATiON ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   Congratulations.    You''ve   found  ConfScan  2.6.06  of  ConfScan,  a\012   radically faster version of the ConfScan series.  It has a totally new\012   search  routine  that makes it possible to find files within 1 second!\012   If  you  were a previous user of ConfScan 2.x, you will most certainly\012   notice the difference, esspecially with large dir-files.\012\012   The  original  package still contains the old 2.6 version as they were\012   spread on all systems world-wide.  However, this archive also contains\012   a  file  called  "Beta_Version.LHA"  and  there you can find the 68000\012   version  of  the  version  with the improved search-routine.  There is\012   only  an  68000 version.  Once installed with the Installer script you\012   can simply copy that version over the installed version.\012\012   IMPORTANT! My internet address has changed: [email removed] !\012\012   I  am  working  on a new version (3.0) that will be totally different,\012   but  due to circumstances beyond my control this may take a while, but\012   you can count on a new version.\012\012   Until then... KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC (Sun Feb  5 15:57:26 1995)\012\012                - - - ­ ­ ­ [ UPDATE iNFORMATiON ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   Welcome  to  version  2.6  of  ConfScan.  This is just an intermediate\012   release,  to  fix  the problem with Ami-Express 4.xx.  I didn''t expect\012   this  version  of  Ami-Express to be released this soon.  My apologies\012   for the error I made (both in judgement as in programming).\012\012   A  few  days  ago  a  saw  a patch of ConfScan going around fixing the\012   problem  with  /X  4.x, but the patcher (I don''t know who did it and I\012   don''t care, really) also made it a 4.x door ONLY.  Now that isn''t what\012   I  had  in  mind!   I know that the patcher couldn''t do anything else,\012   because it was programmed that way (to check for just 1 version).\012\012   Anyway,  like  I said before, this version wasn''t to be released until\012   some  other options were build in, but it appears that there is a need\012   for  a  fixed  version (I figured that if you wanted a new version you\012   would  call  one  of  the MYSTiC boards, there you could get a patched\012   version).  So here it is!\012\012   A small overview of all changes since 2.5(.60):\012   \012   · Flagged  files  from  users  are now saved to a special directory in\012     the  ConfScan  directory  (.../Users/). This enables users to safely\012     log off and download the files at a later time. Several sysops asked\012     for this option.\012\012   · New ConfScan_DL door to read the new structure that ConfScan uses to\012     store  the  files.  It also has got a better look and some bugs were\012     fixed: ­ Non-relative Conference jumping now goes fine\012            ­ Files  entered  after  the  ''D'' command are now flagged and\012              recognized  (previously  ConfScan_DL  would inform you that\012              there  were no files in the current conference although you\012              had just flagged them with the ''D'' command).\012\012     New option: ­ If  you  add ''-r'' as the first argument after ''D'', you\012                   will  be  asked  if  you  want to delete (remove) your\012                   remaining  files.  This  is  just  a small work-around\012                   until my ''A'' command is finished.\012\012     Important : To get this working, ConfScan_DL needs to know where you\012                 have  stored ConfScan. If you install it with the script\012                 there  is  no problem. But if you have already installed\012                 it, add the tooltype ''CS_Location=<path>'' to your D.info\012                 or else it will fail.\012\012   · New Config menu layout and smarter interpretation of the menu.\012     If  you  call  the config menu with ''N'' or ''F'' you will get the menu\012     with  environmental  options  first  instead of the menu with the CS\012     options (as it was before this release).\012\012   · New  ConfScan_G  command with a LOT more options.  Help is available\012     via  ''G ?''  (the file is called ConfScan.G.Help.TXT).\012\012     New options involve: ­ View the remaining files\012                          ­ Remove the remaining files & log off\012                          ­ Download the remaining files\012\012     If  you enter a ''!'' after the ''G'' command, you will force it to just\012     shut up and log off 8-)\012\012     Important : To get this working, ConfScan_G needs  to know where you\012                 have  stored ConfScan. If you install it with the script\012                 there  is  no problem. But if you have already installed\012                 it, add the tooltype ''CS_Location=<path>'' to your G.info\012                 or else it will fail.\012\012   · Quite  a  lot of bugfixes, for a more complete description check the\012     @{"history" link History} part, but here are the main points:\012     ­ ConfScan now works fine from any dir, not just the BBSCmd/ dir.\012     ­ Hold access problem fixed (shame shame).\012     ­ Better error information/detection.\012     ­ A percentage is now shown when a dirfile is being copied.\012     ­ Clear Screen works better.\012     ­ Pause between conferences now works like it should work.\012     ­ Dirfiles if size 0 are handled correctly (skipped :) ).\012     ­ The RELATIVE_CONFERENCES bug is fixed. Non-relative conferences\012       are now supported.\012\012   · I  wrote  shorter  and  better  help files for the users. They don''t\012     need  (nor  are  they  interested  in) long textfiles explaining the\012     theory  behind  ConfScan.  Please use these instead of the old ones.\012\012   Well,  that''s  it  for  now.   Remember,  this is just an intermediate\012   release.   The  next  release  (3.0?)  will most likely have a new GUI\012   Config and the ability to set up your own set of command''s that can be\012   called  from  within  ConfScan.  Like I said before in the Guide, I am\012   interested in your suggestions, so contact me if you have some!\012   \012   I would like to take this oppertunity to thank all the people who made\012   suggestions  for  ConfScan,  and  in  particulair  Zed,  he''s  a great\012   beta-tester,  I could need more of his kind!  Thanks man, you are very\012   thourough and persistant :-)\012   \012   Further  more, school has begun again, so my other internet account is\012   also  active  again:   [email removed]  (yes,  my  first  name is\012   Robert). Write me if you feel bored or anything :-) Or you can find me\012   on IRC at #Rave or #Amiga under Killraven.\012\012   Goodbye & I hope you enjoy ConfScan!\012   \012   (Thu Aug 25 14:45:38 1994  -  Kewl,  one  year  exactly  after the 1st\012    release!)\012\012@EndNode\012\012@Node ConfScan_DL "Guide to ConfScan_DL - © 1994 KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\012\012                           Small Guide to ConfScan_DL\012                   for AmiExpress BBS together with ConfScan\012\012                            Program version: 2.6.02\012                Compilation Date/Time: Thu Aug 25 14:54:47 1994\012\012                           © 1994 by KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC\012\012                       ...part of the ConfScan Package...\012\012                              @{"    Introduction    " link DL_intro}\012\012                              @{"       Usage        " link DL_Usage}\012\012                              @{"    Configuration   " link DL_Configuration}\012\012                              @{"      History       " link DL_History}\012@EndNode\012\012@Node DL_intro "introduction to ConfScan_DL - © 1994 KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\012                    - - - ­ ­ ­ [ iNTRODUCTiON ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   ConfScan_DL  plays  a very important role inside the ConfScan package.\012   it  is  the  link  between all the flagged files and Ami-Express.  You\012   MUST install ConfScan_DL if you want to let users download files.  But\012   that''s not all.\012\012   It  is  great  ofcourse  that  you  now  can  flag files from multiple\012   conferences,  but what happens if you want to download them?  Nothing!\012   Ami-Express  is not capable to let users download files from different\012   conferences  at  once,  thus  I created ConfScan_DL.  ConfScan_DL lets\012   users  download files from multiple_conferences.  Unfortunately not at\012   once, but it is a great improvement compared to nothing 8-)\012\012   What  ConfScan_DL  does,  is flag the files for the conference that an\012   user  is in.  ConfScan_DL checks if there were files selected from the\012   current  conference  and  if there are files, they will be flagged and\012   the internal download command will be started.\012\012   Besides  flagging the files, ConfScan_DL can automatically jump to the\012   next conference where files are selected from.  This can be done right\012   after the download or (when there are no files selected in the current\012   conference)  straight  away.  Users can always ask for a list with all\012   the files they selected.\012\012   But  that  is  not  all!  Many sysops already have another command put\012   under  their  ''D''.  That makes it impossible to install ConfScan_DL as\012   well  under  the  ''D''  command.   But  I  found  out  that these doors\012   generally  do  the same thing:  check if the user may download or not.\012   There  are  lots  of varieties, node checkers, conference checkers and\012   even user checkers.  Well, ConfScan_DL has that built in!\012\012   With  ConfScan_DL you can exclude a node, a conference or even an user\012   from downloading.  This is done with a few tooltypes in the icon.  You\012   can  even  create  a list of people that actually CAN download in that\012   conference  or on that node, so anybody who is not in that list cannot\012   download.\012@EndNode\012\012@Node DL_Usage "How to use ConfScan_DL - © 1994 KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\012                                 ^-[ USAGE ]-^\012\012   I''ve  done  my  best  to  make  the  usage  of the DL door as easy and\012   convinient  as  possible.   If  a user has not used ConfScan, the user\012   will never even know the DL door is being used.\012\012   What  does the user see then?  Well, let''s assume an user has selected\012   five  files,  1 in conference 1, 2 in conference 2 and 2 in conference\012   4.   The  user is in conference 3 and wants to download (thus executes\012   the ''D'' command).  This is what will happen:\012\012   · ConfScan_DL will check wether downloads on this node are legal.\012     If they are not, ConfScan_DL will not allow downloads and will show\012     a text file or a brief message.\012\012   · ConfScan_DL will check wether downloads in this conference are legal.\012     If they are not, ConfScan_DL will not allow downloads and will show\012     a text file or a brief message.\012\012   · ConfScan_DL will check if the user is allowed to download at all.\012     If he is excluded from downloading in general (this can be done with\012     ConfScan_DL) than that user will either see a brief message telling\012     him to sod off or a textfile you can create.\012\012   At  this  point  the  user is allowed to download and ConfScan_DL will\012   check  for  files.  If it finds files it will say so, but in this case\012   it will say:\012\012  ConfScan v2.6 Download File Checker - (c) Copyright 1994 by KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC\012\012       Files flagged for this conference:   0    Skipped alien files:  5\012\012        Your remaining files have been saved. You can logoff safely and\012                 continue downloading another time if you like.\012\012      Would you like to see the list of still remaining files? [Y/n]\012\012\012   So  ConfScan_DL  does  notice  that  there  are  other  files flagged,\012   otherwise  it  will  not ask the user that last question.  Suppose the\012   user says "YES"...\012\012\012                     Files remaining in other conferences:\012                     `-----------------------------------''\012                      TRP-YZ2.DMS       in Conference   1\012                      CATFIX12.LHA      in Conference   2\012                      MDBLC004.LHA      in Conference   2\012                      AXFUNREG.DMS      in Conference   4\012                      BILL&TED.RUL      in Conference   5\012\012    Automatically join the next conference with remaining files? [Y/n]\012\012\012   The  last question offers the user to automatically jump (join) to the\012   next conference where files are flagged.  If the user want so, he will\012   be jumped to the next conference (with the installed ''J'' command).\012\012   There,  the  user can (and unfortunatelly must) select the ''D'' command\012   again.  Then he will see:\012\012  ConfScan v2.6 Download File Checker - (c) Copyright 1994 by KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC\012\012       Files flagged for this conference:   1    Skipped alien files:   4\012\012        Your remaining files have been saved. You can logoff safely and\012                 continue downloading another time if you like.\012\012      Would you like to see the list of still remaining files? [Y/n]\012\012   Well,  after  that  it  will be the same as shown above, but after the\012   download,  ConfScan_DL  will  jump  right  away to the next conference\012   where files were flagged (if the user wanted to ofcourse).\012\012   This  will  be  repeated  for  every  conference where files have been\012   flagged (or tagged).\012\012                 ^-[ HOW TO GET RiD OF SAVED FLAGGED FiLES ]-^\012\012   Sometimes  it  is desired to get rid of all those saved flagged files.\012   Normally  you  would  do  that  with  the  ''A'' command, but /X doesn''t\012   recognize  the  ConfScan  files.  So to work around this problem, I''ve\012   built in this option in the ''D'' command.\012\012   If  the  first  argument after the ''D'' command is ''-r'', a procedure to\012   remove  the flagged files will be started.  I.e.  ''D -r'' will give you\012   this:\012\012               °±² ConfScan_DL - Remove Personal Saved Files ²±°\012\012        Are you sure you want to remove your saved flagged files? [y/N]\012\012   If you are sure, press ''Y'' and you will get either\012\012                         Removed your personal file...\012\012   or, when it fails to remove it (for some dark reason):\012\012                      ERROR! FAiLED TO REMOVE YOUR FiLE!\012\012   If you want to remove files that are not there, you will get to see\012\012           You have no personal ConfScan file. Nothing to be removed.\012\012   I think of everything, don''t I? 8-)\012\012@EndNode\012\012@Node DL_Configuration "Configuration for ConfScan_DL - © 1994 KiLLraVen/MYSTiC"\012                            ^-[ CONFiGURATiON ]-^\012\012   ConfScan_DL  can be configured with the external configuration program\012   Config. You can install it with the Installer script.\012\012               ^-[ CONFSCAN_DL ]-^\012\012   The  ConfScan_DL  part  of  the  Config program can be reached via the\012   [ConfScan_DL] button in the main screen.  A new window will appear.\012\012   The  "ConfScan_DL  Preferences  window 1" is divided into three parts;\012   Node Restrictions, Baud Restrictions and Conference Restrictions.\012\012                        .---------------------------.\012       [ Graphical ]    |-----------+---------------|\012                        |  NODE     |  CONF    | T  |\012        [ Display ]     |  RESTR.   |  RESTR.  | E  |\012                        |           |          | X  |\012                        |           |          | T  |\012            ;-)         |           |          |    |\012                        +-----------+----------|    |\012                        | BAUD RESTRiCTiONS    |    |\012                        `---------------------------''\012\012   Every  time  a  user  wants  to  download, but you have restricted the\012   download  for  that  user, the user will get to see a (brief) message.\012   This  can  either  be  an internal message or a file that you specify.\012   This can be specified PER type of restriction.\012\012   The way you can specify this is universal to all type of restrictions:\012\012   o Internal message\012   o Show file\012\012   I think it speaks for itself.\012\012            ^-[ NODE RESTRiCTiONS ]-^\012\012   The  cycle  gadget  at the top of the window lets you walk through all\012   your  available  nodes.  Shift-Click to go one back. You might want to\012   install Cycle-To-Menu, it''s a very nifty and handy tool ;)\012\012          ^-[ CONFERENCE RESTRiCTiON ]-^\012\012   With  the cycle gadget at the top of the window you can (just like the\012   nodes)  switch  between conferences. Because some boards have a LOT of\012   conferences,  the  ''S''  button allows you to select the conference you\012   want more easily than the cycle gadget might.\012\012               ^-[ RESTRiCTiONS ]-^\012\012   Both  types  of  restrictions  can have the same sort of restrictions,\012   therefore,  the  following  explanation  are valid for either Node and\012   Conference restrictions. The explanation will talk about node, but you\012   can fill in Conference at any time.\012\012   No restrictions   ­ If   you   set  the  node''s  status  to  this,  no\012                       restriction will rest upon this node.  Downloading\012                       from this node will be no problem (unless you have\012                       a baud restriction).\012                       (Default)\012\012   No Downloads      ­ Downloading  from  that  node  will  be impossible\012                       unless  you  give  an  user  special  access  (see\012                       further on).\012\012   Accesslevel       ­ Only users with access level <x> or higher will be\012                       able  to  download  from  this node.  If you don''t\012                       specify  the  access  level  (in the string gadget\012                       behind  it),  the  access  level  will  be  0  and\012                       everybody will be able to download.\012\012   User list         ­ Only users that are present in an user list (ASCII\012                       format)  are  able to download from this node.  If\012                       an  user is not found (or the file does not exist)\012                       the  user  can  NOT  download.   You  can  enter a\012                       filename in the string gadget beneath it or select\012                       a file with the [Select] button.\012\012                       The  user list must consists of an ASCII file that\012                       is built up like this:\012\012                       [BOF]\012                       Tycoon/MYSTiC\012                       KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC\012                       ArCaDe/MYSTiC\012                       etc.\012                       etc.\012                       [EOF]\012\012             ^-[ BAUD RESTRiCTiON ]-^\012\012   Although  this  part  of the Config program looks to be separated from\012   the  Node  restrictions,  this  part will react to changes made in the\012   node  cycle gadget. In other words, any baud restrictions are made for\012   the currently visible node in the cycle gadget.\012\012   No restriction    ­ All baud rates are allowed to download.\012                       (Default)\012\012   Minimum baud      ­ This  is  the minimum baud required for an user to\012                       be able download.\012\012                ^-[ SAVE PREFS ]-^\012\012   The  ConfScan_DL  preferences  need  to  be  saved separately from the\012   ConfScan  preferences (well, not neccessarily but I programmed it this\012   way ;) ). Therefore save them from this window.\012\012   ConfScan_DL  preferences  will  be  saved in the Download command icon\012   (most  likely the D icon). The preferences will also be read from this\012   icon.\012\012                ^-[ MORE PREFS ]-^\012\012   Yes, there is more, see the next section.\012\012                ^-[ MAiN PREFS ]-^\012\012   This will take you back to the first window.\012\012   The  ConfScan_DL  icon  can  be  TOTALLY  configured  with  the Config\012   program, so use it to configure what you want.\012\012   For  you tooltype freaks out there, here is an explanation what Config\012   will save...\012\012   There  are  8  tooltypes for ConfScan_DL, but with these tooltypes you\012   can achieve a lot!  Here they are, followed by a brief explanation.\012\012   · NODE.x      = "NO" / Access level / Filename (with path)\012   · NODE.x.FAiL = iNTERNAL / Filename (with path)\012\012   · CONF.x      = "NO" / Access level / Filename (with path)\012   · CONF.x.FAiL = iNTERNAL / Filename (with path)\012\012   · USER.x      = ALWAYS/NEVER (where x is the slotnumber of the user)\012   · USER.x.FAiL = iNTERNAL / Filename (with path)\012\012   · AREA.name      = ALWAYS/NEVER (where name is the area name of the user)\012   · AREA.name.FiLE = iNTERNAL / Filename (with path)\012\012   First of all, x stands for a number.  So if you want to exclude node 3\012   from  downloading,  enter  NODE.3=NO  in  the  icon.   Or  if you want\012   conference  10  to  be  a  conference where users cannot download, you\012   enter CONF.10=NO in the icon.\012\012   After  NODE.x  or CONF.x you can enter 3 things.  You can either enter\012   "NO", an access level or a filename.  If you enter NO downloading from\012   that node or conference will be impossible, NOBODY can download.\012\012   If  you  enter  an  access  level, that means that downloading is only\012   allowed  when the access level of the user is EQUAL OR HiGHER THAN the\012   level you enter.  If his level is too low, than he can''t download from\012   that node/conference.\012\012   If you enter a filename, ConfScan_DL will open that file and checks if\012   that  file  holds  the  handle  of the user.  If it does, the user can\012   download, otherwise they will be disappointed.  The file must be build\012   up like this:\012\012   ---> CUT <---\012\012   KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC          (ofcourse without the spaces in front of it)\012   EMPiRE/MYSTiC\012   Pharaoh/SR\012   Muad''Dib/5D\012\012   ---> CUT <---\012\012   The  search  routine  is  case insensitive, so don''t worry about that.\012   The file can be placed anywhere because you have to enter the complete\012   path and filename after the NODE.x or CONF.x tooltype.\012\012\012   Ofcourse  it  is  possible to you want certain users to never download\012   (again) on your board or that you want certain users always to be able\012   to  download.   This  can be achieved with the USER.x tooltype.  The x\012   stands  for the number of the user in your user.data (his slotnumber).\012   After  that  you  can either enter NEVER (no download for this guy) or\012   ALWAYS (downloading will be no problem).\012\012   The  same  goes  for users with a certain AREA NAME.  This way you can\012   prevent  NEW users from downloading at all or any other range of users\012   with a particulair AREA NAME (the F option in the user editor).\012\012\012   Now, when ConfScan_DL sees that an user is not allowed to download, it\012   will display a message.  This can be either an internal one or one you\012   made  for him :). If you enter iNTERNAL after NODE.x.FAiL, CONF.x.FAiL\012   or USER.x.FAiL, the internal message will be send:\012\012                    -----[ NO DOWNLOADiNG ON THiS NODE! ]-----\012\012                    -----[ NO DOWNLOADiNG iN THiS CONF! ]-----\012\012                    -----[ NO DOWNLOADiNG FOR YOU DUDE! ]-----\012\012                    -----[ NO DOWNLOADiNG FOR YOU GEEK! ]-----\012\012                    -----[ NO DOWNLOADiNG AT xxxx BAUD! ]-----\012                    -----[ MiNiMAL REQUiRED: xxxx BAUD! ]-----\012\012                                       8-)\012\012   ...or  you  can enter a filename after the .FiLE and that file will be\012   shown instead, it''s just what you like.\012@EndNode\012\012@Node DL_History "The History Of ConfScan_DL - © 1994 KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\012                      - - - ­ ­ ­ HiSTORY ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   \012   2.6.02   25-Aug-94 New         : With the ''-r'' option, you can now \012                                    manually remove your saved tagged\012                                    files.\012\012   2.6.01   11-Aug-94 Improved    : Now recognizes the new structure from\012                                    ConfScan which is a bit smaller.\012\012   2.6.00   07-Aug-94 New         : Better layout, not so boring anymore.\012\012                      New         : It recognizes the new structure that\012                                    ConfScan uses.\012\012   2.5.09   06-Jun-94 Improved    : Optimized the source, this was mainly\012                                    possible thanks to Joe (/X 3.38). Output\012                                    is now almost 4Kb smaller!\012\012   2.5.08   18-May-94 New         : Is now able to read the slightly different\012                                    tooltypes that the Config program leaves\012                                    behind.\012\012   2.5.07   18-May-94 Fixed       : The user statistics are now saved in the\012                                    ENV: dir (by ConfScan) and are now read\012                                    correctly (was T:).\012\012   2.5.06   11-Mar-94 New         : New tooltype: AREA.code where <code> is\012                                    the conference access you have given an\012                                    user (the F option in the user editor).\012                                    it works just like USER.SLOTNUMBER, so\012                                    AREA.NEW=NEVER will prevent new users\012                                    from downloading. \012                                    \012                                    New tooltype: AREA.FiLE=<filename>\012                                    This file will be shown to users when\012                                    they want to download.\012\012   2.5.04   29-Mar-94 Improved    : After USER.SLOTNUMBER you can now enter\012                                    an argument, either NEVER or ALWAYS.\012                                    This way you can also grant users to\012                                    have override access to all restrictions\012                                    you may have put on other users. For\012                                    example: USER.2=ALWAYS, user #2 shall\012                                    always be able to download, no matter\012                                    what the restrictions in the D.info.\012                                    USER.2=NEVER means that he can NEVER\012                                    download.\012\012   2.5.02   26-Mar-94 Improved    : internal message will be shown unless\012                                    you specify NODE.FiLE, CONF.FiLE or\012                                    USER.FiLE in the icon. To show the in-\012                                    ternal message, simply delete that\012                                    tooltype entry (or put it between\012                                    brackets).\012\012                      New         : ConfScan_DL can now check for a baud-\012                                    rate per node. New tooltype:\012                                    BAUD.x=y - where x is node number and\012                                               y the minimum baud rate\012                                               (i.e. BAUD.0=9600).\012                                    *Requested by Pharaoh/SR*\012\012   2.5.01   25-Mar-94 Improved    : You can now also enter iNTERNAL after\012                                    NODE.FiLE, CONF.FiLE and USER.FiLE to\012                                    display an internal message instead of\012                                    a file.\012\012   2.5.00   25-Mar-94 New         : You can now exclude node''s conf''s and\012                                    even user''s from downloading. But also\012                                    allow certain users to download in/on\012                                    a conf/node. New tooltypes:\012                                    NODE.X=NO/ACSLEVEL/FiLENAME\012                                    CONF.X=NO/ACSLEVEL/FiLENAME\012                                    USER.X\012                                    NODE.FiLE=FiLENAME\012                                    CONF.FiLE=FiLENAME\012                                    USER.FiLE=FiLENAME\012                                    *Requested by Chaplin&Stony/PHUN*\012\012   2.4.00   10-Feb-94 Fixed       : Conference jumping bug fixed.\012\012   2.3.04   13-Jan-94 Improved    : ConfScan_DL is now a separate part of\012                                    the ConfScan package...\012@EndNode\012\012@Node Registration "Registration info - /X-PoWeR! - KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\012                    - - - ­ ­ ­ [ REGiSTRATiON ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   ConfScan may be considered FREE-WARE.  That means that you can do with\012   it  whatever you want, but DO NOT ALTER THE CODE, and YOU MAY NOT SELL\012   iT!\012\012   However,  special registered versions are available.  These version do\012   not differ from the (public) available versions except that registered\012   versions  notify  the user that it is in fact a registered version 8-)\012   Some  sysops  asked for one, so it now is possible.  Another advantage\012   is  that  you  will  most  likely  get  a  more  up to date version of\012   ConfScan.   ConfScan  is  always  under  development so by registering\012   yourself  you  will  get the most current version (plus updates if you\012   call regularly).\012\012                      - - - ­ ­ ­ [ SUPPORT ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   Only  major  updates/bugfixes  (like this one) will be released to the\012   masses,  however,  if you want to get updates on a regular basis (even\012   little fixes) you can register yourself and ask for the updates.\012\012   I  also  offer you support for ConfScan!  You can at Channel-X, or you\012   can  contact  me  via  internet,  AND ALL FOR NOTHiNG!  Here is how to\012   reach me:\012\012                    Channel-X      · +31-2290-62244\012                                     +31-2290-62535\012\012                    Last Outpost   · +31-7201-57682\012                                     +31-7202-01182\012\012                    Undiscovered   · +31-2294-4442\012                                     +31-2294-1442\012\012                                   Internet:\012                                   ~~~~~~~~~\012                         [email removed]\012\012\012   The only thing you WiLL NEVER EVER get is a ConfScan T-shirt... ;-)\012\012@EndNode\012\012@Node KiLLER "KiLLER - The New Way Of Nuking! - By KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\012                        - - - ­ ­ ­ [ KiLLER ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012                              YOUR DEADLY FRiEND!\012\012   KiLLER  is the new nuker that I am currently working on.  It will be a\012   totally  *NEW* way of nuking, no nuker is quite like it.  It will have\012   plenty  of  options  for  the  users,  a nice layout and ofcourse fast\012   performance.\012\012   KiLLER  can act like your average every day nuker (and that is exactly\012   how the currently spread versions work), but the new and coming KiLLER\012   will have some neat features:\012\012   ·  TRS,  Total Reverse System.  As a sysop you will be able to reverse\012   (undo) ANY action that has been performed with KiLLER.  KiLLER keeps a\012   log  that  records  all actions performed by KiLLER.  This way you can\012   easily undo any KiLLiNGS of cosysops and/or users.\012\012   ·  User  nuking!  Users are often the ones who tell you what files are\012   fake/lame/old/etc.   So  why  not  let them place comments in the file\012   directory  (dirx)?  KiLLER will let users KiLL files in the sense that\012   they  can  place  a comment, but will not actually deduct credits from\012   the uploader or remove the file.  When you, as sysop, start KiLLER the\012   next  time you will be informed of any user KiLLiNG and you can decide\012   wether this is a valid KiLLiNG or not.\012\012   · Fully GUi!  KiLLER will come with a GUi for the sysop, just like the\012   Config  program  of  ConfScan!   This will make KiLLiNG as easy and as\012   funny as playing BombMan!  But this will be made AFTER there is a full\012   and  working version of KiLLER/Ami-Express.  So this will take a while\012   (fall 94 I guess).\012\012   ·   Total  configuration  for  both  sysops  and  users  with  KiLLiNG\012   privileges.  Every question that KiLLER will ask can be pre-configured\012   so  you  can walk through KiLLER with [return]s as all default answers\012   are configurable.  Quiting will also be possible from any question!\012\012   ·  Logfile creator for logging all uploads and/or KiLLiNGS.  This will\012   speed  up  things  significantly!   At the moment KiLLER is capable of\012   reading BossNuke logfile, but this will (ofcourse) change.\012\012   ·  File moving ANYWHERE you want.  You will be able to move files from\012   ANY  dir  to  ANY  conference  in  ANY  dir,  or  copy  them  to other\012   conferences.  You name it, KiLLER can do it.\012\012              - - - ­ ­ ­ [ WHEN WiLL iT BE READY? ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   The  new  KiLLER  will  hopefully  be  ready this year, but due to the\012   enormous  extent  of the powers of KiLLER, it may well be that it will\012   not   be   ready   until  next  year  (really).   But  don''t  despair,\012   beta-version  will  be  put  out  to  selected  sysops,  so if you are\012   interested, contact your local MYSTiC board now (or contact me)!\012\012        - - - ­ ­ ­ [ WHAT GOOD DOES iT DO FOR ME KNOW? ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   At  this  point you have no benefit from it, asides from the fact that\012   you  can  start  a nuker from ConfScan (simply call it ''Killer'').  But\012   ConfScan is already capable of marking files to be ''KiLLED'' later on.\012\012   In the mean time, be patient, enjoy ConfScan and take care...\012\012@EndNode\012\012@Node SysopCommands "Special Sysop Commands - © 1994 KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\012                    - - - ­ ­ ­ [ ALL COMMANDS ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   Here  is a brief list of ALL arguments that ConfScan recognizes.  Some\012   arguments  require a certain access level, if not given, all users can\012   use the arguments.\012\012\012   N.B.:   The ''N'' command and ''CS'' command parse arguments the same way,\012   so  every  example  I give for ''N'' can also be applied to ''CS'' (unless\012   specified different).\012\012   <date> - N 06-26-94\012   ~~~~~~\012   This  will  make  ConfScan  search the current conference for the date\012   ''06-26-94''  in  the  upload  directory.   If  there  is  no  directory\012   specified, the upload dir file will be the default.\012\012   <-x>   - N -5\012   ~~~~\012   ConfScan  will  search  the  current conference for the date five days\012   back from TODAY.  So you can also read it as "show me the new files of\012   the last 5 days." And again in the upload dir file.\012\012   <S>    - N S\012   ~~~\012   This  is  the  normal  ''S''  argument  (Since  last  on).  It will make\012   ConfScan  search  for  the  date that the user was last on the system.\012   And in the upload dir file.\012\012   <T>    - N T\012   ~~~\012   The T comes from Today.  The date to search for will be set to today''s\012   date.   Needless  to  say this is done in the upload dir file although\012   you can specify another dir file.\012\012\012   <U>   - N S U\012   ~~~\012   The dir file to search in, is now set to the upload dir file.\012\012   <A>   - F A or N -10 A\012   ~~~\012   All dir files will be taken into account when searching for a date.\012\012   <H>   - CS H or N -5 H\012   ~~~\012   The hold dir file will be scanned for the given date.\012\012   <x>   - N 5 U or F 3\012   ~~~\012   The  ''x''  stands  for  any number and represents the number of the dir\012   file that will be the target to search the date in.\012\012\012   <NS>  - N S U NS or F A NS\012   ~~~~\012   NonStop  display  of  all  the  files,  no prompt will be given and no\012   pauses between conferences.  You will be able to break it with CTRL-C.\012\012\012   <+>   - CS +\012   ~~~\012   This  argument only works with the CS command.  If, after scanning, in\012   more  than  1  conference new files were found, a small report will be\012   displayed  on  screen  telling you how many bytes/files were upload in\012   the conferences with new files.  If there was only ONE conference with\012   new  files,  the  report  will  not be generated since you can see the\012   stats in the final bar when CS exits.\012\012   Not  every  user  can use this option, only users with Hold access (or\012   higher) can do this.\012\012\012   <A> or <G>  - N S G or N S A A\012   ~~~~~~~~~~\012   This  will  force  the  ''N''  command  to  act like ''CS''.  It will make\012   ConfScan  go  in  Multiple  Conference  mode.   In  other  words,  all\012   conferences will be scanned for new files.\012\012\012   All  of  these  arguments  can  be  combined, here are some daily used\012   examples:\012\012   CS NS +  - Scan  all dirs in all conferences for new files,  show them\012              nonstop and generate a report with the upload bytes/files.\012\012   CS T     - Scan  all  dirs in all conferences for new files,  uploaded\012              today.\012\012   CS -5 H  - What files were upload in the hold dirs the last 5 days?\012\012   N -5 NS  - Show  me  all  files  from  the last 5 days nonstop of this\012              conference (current conference).\012\012   F A NS   - Give me all files of all dirs NonStop.\012\012   N S G    - This is the same as ''CS'', it will show you  all  new  files\012              since  your  last  logon  from all upload dirs and from all\012              conferences.\012\012   N S A G  - This  is  the  same as ''CS A'', it will scan all dirs in all\012              conferences for new files since the last logon.\012@EndNode\012','\012',char(10)),'{"ACCESS":"100","LOCATION":"<path>''"}','auto-added',309498,2,0,NULL,NULL,'cnfscn26','scan',1780048448);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('com2b3','COM2B3.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/COM2B3.LHA','SaturnComment','XIM','SaturnComment',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,replace('SaturnComment\n','\n',char(10)),'SaturnComment.guide',replace('@database "SaturnComment Guide"\n@master Tempest:Doors/Saturn/Comment/SaturnComment.guide\n@$VER SaturnComment Guide 2.0\n@author "jUPiTER8!"\n@(c) "Copyright © 1996 by jUPiTER8!"\n@help "main"\n@index "main"\n\n@node "main" "Guide to SaturnComment"\n@next "legal"\n@font topaz.font 8\n\n                                                 /\\n                       ________________________ /  \ _                     ·\n  ___ ______________  |_______ ________   _____/___/__|_    ______________/_\n |  _/  _______    /_ |\_____¬\______ ¬\_/   ______    /___/  _______    /_ |\n |  \_____  \/   ___/_/   __/  /    /___/    /   /    /   \_____  \/   ___/_|\n | /    /   /    /   /    /   /    /   /    /   /    /   /    /   /    /   /|\n |/____    /____    /____    /____/__ /____    /____    /____    /____    / |\n |   /____/   /____/  |/____/    /       /____/   /____/   /____/kRm/____/  |\n |____________________|                               |_____________________|\n\n                                 presents\n\n                        @{b}S a t u r n   C o m m e n t@{ub}\n\n                                 v 2 . 0\n\n\n                 All code and design by @{b}jUPiTER8!@{ub}/Stardust\n\n   @{"                                                                        " link null}\n\n      @{"             Legal             " link legal}  @{"            History             " link history}\n      @{"          Introduction         " link introduction}  @{"             To do              " link todo}\n      @{"            Features           " link features}  @{"            Credits             " link credits}\n      @{"          Installation         " link installation}  @{"             Author             " link author}\n      @{"         Configuration         " link configuration}  @{"          Bug Reports           " link bugreports}\n      @{"             Usage             " link usage}  @{"           Greetings            " link greetings}\n\n   @{"                                                                        " link null}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "legal" "Legal"\n@next "introduction"\n@prev "main"\n@font topaz.font 8\n\n  This guide and the door may not be completely free of errors. I don''t take\n  any responsability for any damages it may cause. Use it at your own risk!\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "introduction" "Introduction to SaturnComment"\n@next "features"\n@prev "legal"\n@font topaz.font 8\n\n  SaturnComment is @{b}not@{ub} "just another comment-door", it''s @{b}the@{ub} comment-door!\n\n  Just take a quick look at all the @{"features" link features}!\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "features" "The features of SaturnComment"\n@next "installation"\n@prev "introduction"\n@font topaz.font 8\n\n  @{" · " link null} Coded in C - no slow ARexx crap!\n  @{" · " link null} Very nice design (If I may say so :))\n  @{" · " link null} Infinite number of sysops\n  @{" · " link null} Cursorkey selection\n  @{" · " link null} Numerical selection\n  @{" · " link null} Argument selection, IE "c 2" will skip select sysop number 2\n  @{" · " link null} Randomly selected comments\n  @{" · " link null} Shows how many messages each sysop has received\n       (This requires atleast Tempest 3.51 (July 26) or it will just show 0,\n       this is because the counter wasn''t actually implemented until that\n       date. So go and get an update, since it will look strange otherwise!)\n  @{" · " link null} Runs under Tempest! :)\n\n  So, don''t waste any time and @{"install" link installation} it quickly! :)\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "installation" "Installation of SaturnComment"\n@next "configuration"\n@prev "features"\n@font topaz.font 8\n\n  @{" 1 " link null} Put all the files in "Tempest:Doors/Saturn/Comment"\n       (or wherever you like, but the config-file must be in the same\n       directory).\n\n\n  @{" 2 " link null} Edit your "GlobalMenu.opt" and include this line:\n\n       [*,*,*,*,*] = C | T-DOOR | DOORS:Saturn/Comment/SaturnComment       \n\n \n  Now you need to @{"configure" link configuration} it.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "configuration" "Configuration of SaturnComment"\n@next "usage"\n@prev "installation"\n@font topaz.font 8\n\n  @{" 1 " link null} Edit the file "SaturnComment.config".\n\n       If the @{b}first@{ub} line contains the word "ANSIBAR", that is what\n       you are going to get. The non-ANSIBAR version is not only faster,\n       but in my opinion it''s very nice too! So I suggest that you try both\n       ways and decide which one you like best. To get the non-ANSIBAR\n       version just write "NO FUCKING BAR" or whatever you like, but don''t\n       include the word "ANSIBAR"!\n\n       At line @{b}two@{ub}, the real configuration begin. Every section\n       starts with @USERNAME, where you ofcourse put the sysops name.\n       The following lines should contain comments, one on each line.\n       The door will choose one randomly each time the door is started.\n       You mark the end of the comments with @END on the beginning of a\n       line. How long the comments can be depends on how long the longest\n       name of the sysops is.\n\n       Repeat those lines for all your (co)sysops.\n\n  Now learn how to @{"use" link usage} it!\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "usage" "Usage of SaturnComment"\n@next "history"\n@prev "configuration"\n@font topaz.font 8\n\n  After the door is started you just select the sysop of your choice\n  using the cursorkeys or numerical keys. Pressing shift while moving\n  up/down will move you to the start/end of the list, if you''re not\n  already there ofcourse.\n\n  You can also skip that selection by entering the sysop you want\n  directly at the main prompt in the bbs. Just enter "c 3" for instance,\n  and the door will jump to the message posting part directly.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "history" "History of SaturnComment"\n@next "todo"\n@prev "usage"\n@font topaz.font 8\n\n  @{" V1.0 " link nowhere} (960526) First public release.\n\n  @{" V1.1 " link nowhere} (960705) Changed width of output to 79 characters.\n                   Made the door post PERSONAL mail, instead of PRIVATE.\n\n  @{" V2.0 " link nowhere} (960805) Rewrote the whole door from scratch.\n                   Designed it totally differently.\n                   Rewrote these docs.\n                   Changed name and format of configuration file.\n                   Added random comments.\n                   Added numerical selection.\n                   Added argument selection.\n                   Made the door adjust the length of the comments according\n                     to the length of the sysop names.\n                   The door now shows how many messages each sysop has\n                     received.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "todo" "To do"\n@next "credits"\n@prev "history"\n@font topaz.font 8\n\n  Since I have never seen a comment-door that has any features this one\n  haven''t, I can''t think of anything.\n\n  @{"Contact me" link author} and give me ideas!\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "credits" "Credits"\n@next "author"\n@prev "todo"\n@font topaz.font 8\n\n  All code and design by me, @{"jUPiTER8!" link author}.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "author" "Author of SaturnComment"\n@next "bugreports"\n@prev "credits"\n@font topaz.font 8\n\n  @{b}jUPiTER8!@{ub}/@{b}Stardust@{ub} (STD)\n\n\n  You can contact me via e-mail on:\n\n  @{b}[email removed]@{ub}\n\n\n  Or leave mail to me at:\n\n  Infinite Power, Receiver, Stage Dive, Bumble Bee Land, Dawn of Eternity.\n\n\n  You can probably catch me on IRC too, under the nick "jUPiTER8".\n  I''m usually at #amielite on EFnet and in #tempest at Undernet.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "bugreports" "If you find bugs..."\n@next "greetings"\n@prev "author"\n@font topaz.font 8\n\n  If you find any bugs, please @{"contact" link author} me and tell me what''s wrong.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "greetings" "Greets!"\n@prev "bugreports"\n@font topaz.font 8\n\n  @{b}Skeleton@{ub} Waiting for 3.60... :)\n  @{b}Baffle@{ub}   Quit sleeping! :)\n\n  And ofcourse to everyone who betatested this door and\n  all other nice guys at @{b}#tempest@{ub} and @{b}#amielite@{ub}...\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',14930,4,0,NULL,NULL,'com2b3','scan',1780048448);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('comment','COMMENT.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/COMMENT.LHA','KC-Config','XIM','Comment',NULL,NULL,NULL,'control',replace('Best comment door around with cursor\ncontrol\n','\n',char(10)),'KiLLER-Comment.GUiDE',replace('@DATABASE "KiLLER-Comment.GUiDE"\n@REMARK	.-------------------------------------------------------.\n@REMARK  | This document should be read with AmigaGuide (OS 2.x) |\n@REMARK  | or MultiView (OS 3.x) or any other guide reader. Tnx. |\n@REMARK  `-------------------------------------------------------''\n@REMARK	$VER: KiLLER Comment 1.2.0\n@WIDTH 80\n@NODE MAIN "KiLLER Comment - MYSTiC 1994/1995 - © 1994/1995 KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n                            Guide to KiLLER Comment\n                     for Ami-Express Bulletin Board Systems\n\n                             Program version: 1.2.0\n                Compilation Date/Time: Thu Feb  2 15:23:39 1995\n\n                         © 1994/1995 by @{"KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC" link Contact}\n\n                   ... another fine MYSTiC /X production ...\n\n      @{" First words... " link WhatIs}    What/Why is KiLLER Comment?\n      @{" Features       " link Features}    What can it do?\n      @{" Installation   " link Install}    How to install KiLLER Comment on your BBS\n      @{" Usage /X       " link AmiUsage}    How things go with Ami-Express\n      @{" Usage Config   " link Config}    How to use the Config GUI\n      @{" History        " link History}    History of KiLLER Comment\n      @{" History Config " link HistoryGUI}    History of KiLLER Config\n      @{" Greetings      " link Greetings}    Greetings, messages and contact info\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE WhatIs "What/Why is KiLLER Comment? - © 1994/1995 KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n                         .---------------------------.\n                         |  What is KiLLER Comment?  |\n                         `---------------------------''\n\n   KiLLER Comment is number 1001 in the row of a [C]omment doors.  But this\n   is not just *a* comment door, otherwise I wouldn''t have made it.  I have\n   some profound reasons.\n\n   Despite  the  fact  that  there  must be over a 1000 different [C]omment\n   doors,  there  is not one comment door that suits my needs.  I have seen\n   plenty of them but to me they all look ugly, have static interfaces, are\n   as flexible as a log of wood and generally suck :-).\n\n   With  this mind I''ve tried to make KiLLER Comment as smart and pretty as\n   I  can  and  I  feel I have succeeded.  I have never seen a comment door\n   that  works  as  simple  as  this  one  with  a fair amount of so-called\n   ''intelligence'' and comes with a nice GUI.\n\n   What  is  this  ''intelligence'' I speak about you say?  Well, all comment\n   doors  sofar  weren''t  able  to see that if I typed "c kill" I wanted to\n   comment to "KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC" nor where they able to see that if I typed\n   "c  amiga" I wanted to comment to the Amiga co-sysop.  KiLLER Comment is\n   able to detect this!\n\n   Another  thing  is  security.   Every  new  user  was  able to see which\n   cosysops  you  had,  but  by giving every cosysop a security level, they\n   will  not see their names/jobs.  And if there is only one (co)sysop they\n   are  allowed  to  see,  they  will  not  even  see it is done via KiLLER\n   Comment.\n\n   Also,  per user in the [C]omment list there is a check wether he/she has\n   got access to the conference that KiLLER [C]omment is called from, so it\n   is impossible to write a person to someone in the wrong conference.\n\n   What I personally also dislike are comment doors that only fill like 25%\n   of  your  screen.   Not  that  you  should put a lot of nonsense in your\n   comment  door,  no,  but  KiLLER  Comment puts an extra line between the\n   names  of  the  (co-)sysops  if  that''s possible with the user''s maximum\n   numbers  of  lines  he  can  handle  on his screen.  It''s these kinds of\n   things I miss in those 13-in-a-dozen [C]omment doors.  That''s why I made\n   KiLLER Comment.\n\n   And  oh, just like I first introduced cursor control in ConfScan, KiLLER\n   comment also uses cursor control for selecting a user you can write to.\n\n   Anyway,  I  hope  you  will  enjoy KiLLER Comment as much as I will.  Go\n   check out the features if you want to know more.\n\n                                                          -KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE Features "Features of KiLLER Comment - © 1994/1995 KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n                        .------------------------------.\n                        |  Features of KiLLER Comment  |\n                        `------------------------------''\n\n   Although  the  list  of  features isn''t big, it''s enough for a [C]omment\n   door.  Remember, it''s only a [C]omment door.\n\n   » GUI Config\n\n   A small program comes with it to set it up the way you want it as easy\n   as possible.  It''s just click and save, you probably won''t even need the\n   keyboard but to fill in some personal info.\n\n   » Security\n\n   Users  with  low  access will not see all cosysops in the [C]omment list\n   (esspecially useful with new users).\n\n   » Known as\n\n   Very often your cosysops will have names that contain some sort of group\n   name  in  it  (like  KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC), but it''s not always that nice or\n   handy  to  have  that group name in the comment door (be it for cosmetic\n   reasons,  be  it  for  some  other reason).  That''s why you can enter an\n   alias  for  each of your cosysops (and for yourself ofcourse) which will\n   be used to display in the comment list.\n\n   » Info\n\n   For  every (co)sysop you can enter one line of information regarding why\n   he  is in the comment list.  This can be something like "Amiga Co-Sysop"\n   or "Takes care of users / files / lamers".\n\n   » Comments\n\n   Most  comment doors offer you the possibility to display a message after\n   the  user has selected someone to write to.  This is generally something\n   like  "<name>  says:   bla bla".  With KiLLER Comment you can make lines\n   like  this:   "And  there  goes another message to <name>" or "<name> is\n   cheering of joy!".\n   \n   An example file with fortune cookies has been supplied (Comments.ASCII).\n\n   » Cursor Control / Numeric entries / Default sysop\n\n   Selecting  a  user  can  be done with the cursor keys or by entering the\n   corresponding number.  A default sysop is also available (space).\n\n   » Comment Statistics\n\n   KiLLER  Comment  keeps record of the number of messages written to every\n   user  and  also knows when every user received his last message plus the\n   user  who  wrote  it to him.  So with this information it is possible to\n   create  some  nice  looking  statistics.  These statistics can be viewed\n   within /X or with the Config program.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE Install "How to install KiLLER Comment - © 1994/1995 KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n                      .----------------------------------.\n                      |  Installation of KiLLER Comment  |\n                      `----------------------------------''\n\n   KiLLER  Comment  can  be installed like any /X 3.x command, but please\n   take notice of these tooltypes:\n\n   "KC-Config.info" - The icon of the GUI config program\n   \n   · ACP_LOCATION=<path>      - Location of your ACP.info file.\n                                (eg. ACP_LOCATION=SYS:WBStartUp)\n\n   · KC_LOCATION=<path>       - Location of the /X version\n                                (eg. KC_LOCATION=DOORS:K-Comment)\n                                ** NOTE ** NOTE ** NOTE ** NOTE ** NOTE **\n                                 THIS SHOULD BE THE PATH TO THE DIRECTORY\n                                 AND SHOULD _NOT_ INCLUDE THE NAME OF THE\n                                 EXECUTABLE! DON''T FORGET THIS! (HI JAKE)\n                                ** NOTE ** NOTE ** NOTE ** NOTE ** NOTE **\n\n   · KC_VIEWER=<full name>    - External viewer for the Commentistics\n                                (eg. KC_VIEWER=C:PPMORE)\n\n   · PUB_SCREEN=<name>        - Optional(!) name of public screen that the\n                                config program will open on instead of the\n                                Workbench.\n                                (eg. PUB_SCREEN=ECS_PUB)\n\n   "C.info"          - The icon in your BBS command directory\n\n   · ACS_STATS=<level>        - The minimum level required to view the\n                                statiscal mumbo jumbo that KiLLER Comment\n                                is able to create for you (with ''C ?'').\n                                (eg. ACS_STATS=50)\n\n   · BBS_LOCATION=<path>      - This should be the path to your BBS:, or\n                                if you keep your USER.DATA located some-\n                                where else, the path to your USER.DATA.\n\n   · SEPARATOR_LINES          - An empty line is by default put  between\n                                two sysops if possible, but if you don''t\n                                like  that,  you can also have a line of\n                                ''-''s put between them.  To do so, simply\n                                this tooltype.\n\n   I  have  found  it  very  useful  to  put the Config program in my ACP\n   command list.  Maybe this can be useful for you too.\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE AmiUsage "Usage in Ami-Express - © 1994/1995 KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n                          .------------------------.\n                          |  Usage in Ami-Express  |\n                          `------------------------''\n\n                          ^-^  Selecting a user  ^-^\n\n   Once  installed, the usage of the [C]omment door is (and should be) real\n   easy.  You can simply start it with ''C'' and you will be presented with a\n   menu from which you can select a user to send some mail to.\n\n   However,  like I said in the first words, KiLLER comment is a bit smart.\n   If  you enter a parameter after the ''C'', you can skip the menu and still\n   select  the  person you want to write to.  For example, suppose you want\n   to write a message to "Muad''Dib".  We all know that this is a very lousy\n   name  to spell, so we can suffice by entering "C Muad" and Muad''Dib will\n   be selected.\n\n   However,  if  you''ve  got  another  cosysop  in  the  list that is named\n   Muad''Dab,  KiLLER  Comment  will  take  the first name that has the part\n   "muad"  in it.  This is just the way it goes, so if you want to write to\n   Muad''Dab  instead  of  Muad''Dib  you  have  to enter another string that\n   uniquely identifies Muad''Dab, for instance:  "C Dab" :)\n\n   Another  way to select a user is entering his or her appropriate number.\n   If  you  know  that Muad''Dib is number 2 in the list, you can suffice by\n   entering  "C 2".   And  if  you  know that Muad''Dab is number 5, you can\n   enter  "C 5"  to  write  to Muad''Dab.  Real easy.  If you enter a number\n   that does not exist, you will be presented with the menu again.\n\n   But  that''s not all, let''s say you got separate sysops (or cosysops) for\n   different  conferences;  Amiga,  SNES  and  PC.  And suppose you want to\n   write  to  the Amiga cosysop, you can simply enter "C Amiga" or "C Ami".\n   Make  sure  the  length  of  the  string  after  the  "C"  is at least 3\n   characters,  otherwise  it will be marked as ambigious and the menu will\n   be  prompted.   And  yes,  that means that "C PC" will NOT work (haha!).\n   But  hey,  there  are  3  other  ways of selecting that sysop.  So don''t\n   despair (or enter "C p PC" if the text is "Cosysop PC").\n\n                           ^-^  Commentistics  ^-^\n\n   The  commentistics  can be viewed by entering a question mark behind the\n   "C".  Couldn''t be more simple.  Just enter "C ?" and you will be able to\n   view  all  sorts  of  statistic mumbo jumbo on your screen.  Once you''ve\n   seen the first screen, you can go to the next screen by pressing any key\n   BUT Q, ESC can CTRL-C.  Than the screen will be cleared in a fashionable\n   style and the last page will be shown, containing the times and names of\n   users who wrote last to the users in the Comment list.\n\n                           ^-^  Syntax Summary  ^-^\n\n   For all you folks that didn''t bother to read the upper texts, here''s the\n   brief list of all commands:\n\n   C        - A menu will be shown from which you can select a user\n\n   C <text> - The  <text> will be compared to the names of the users in the\n              list  and  if  that fails, it will be compared to the info of\n              each user in the list. This comparing is case insensitive.\n\n   C <#>    - The corresponding name with the number will be selected.\n\n   C ?      - The commentistics will be shown.\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE Config "The Config Editor - © 1994/1995 KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n                             .-----------------.\n                             |  Config Editor  |\n                             `-----------------''\n\n   KiLLER  Comment  comes  with  a  full C= compliant Guided User Interface\n   (commonly  known  as  GUI).  With this Configuration Editor you are able\n   to setup KiLLER Comment the way YOU want.\n\n   When  you  start  the  Config  Editor for the first time, the sysop will\n   automatically  added as the first entry in the list of users that can be\n   commented  to.   There  should  at  least  be  ONE  entry in the list or\n   otherwise the user can''t comment to anybody :-)\n\n   Okay,  I  think it is best if I just tell you what every button does and\n   how to do things.  Here we go...\n\n   » Known As\n\n   You  can  enter an alias for every user that is in the list.  By default\n   the  alias  is  the  same  as  their real name in /X but you are free to\n   change  it.  KiLLER Comment will still know their real name, don''t worry\n   about that.  This function can be handy if you got a cosysop with a name\n   like [-Bad Boy^Lamers-R-Us^I-Suck-] but you don''t want to have that damn\n   ugly handle in your comment door.  Fill in whatever you like.\n\n   » Info\n\n   As  usual  you are able to enter one line of text that somehow describes\n   why  this  user  is put in the list of ''commenteers'' :) You can put info\n   like "Amiga Cosysop" in here or "Nuking is my nick-name!".  You are free\n   to  use  any colours in it, just enter them in the gadget like you would\n   do  in  a  text  file.   If pressing the ESC removes the cursor from the\n   gadget,  you  need to TURN OF THE TEXT-FILTER OPTION IN YOUR PREFERENCES\n   FROM YOUR AMIGA (Prefs/IControl)!!\n\n   Although  you  can only have like 34 chars on screen for info about that\n   user,  the  Config  Editor  takes 80 chars.  You are responsible for the\n   length  of  the  text.   If you put 80 chars of text in it, it will look\n   like a mess on screen in Ami-Express.\n\n   » Comments\n\n   A  comment is a line of text that is shown to the user who just selected\n   somebody.   This  can  be  a  message  like  "Muad''Dib says:  Thanks for\n   nothing!"  or  "You can hear Muad''Dib shout with joy.".  Or you can show\n   him fortune cookie (max.  1 line!).  An example file has been included.\n\n   This gadget wants a full path plus filename to a file that contains such\n   messages.   This can be a different file for every user or the same file\n   for all users.  The lines in the text file can contain anything you like\n   where you can use ''%s'' to represent the name of the choosen user.\n\n   Examples:   %s says: Thanks for your mail bud.\n               You can hear %s scream with joy.\n               %s is overwhelmed with tears by your gesture.\n               Who is General Failure and why is he reading my hard drive?\n\n   Be creative!\n\n   With  the  [S]  button  you  can select a file via a file-requester than\n   rather typing in its full name.\n\n   » Req. Acs\n\n   For  security  reasons,  you  are able to set a minimum access level for\n   every  user in the comment list.  This way you are able to have multiple\n   cosysops and not let all the users know what they all do.\n\n   Imagine  you''ve got a cosysop for the Amiga section, SNES section and PC\n   section.   You''ve  got  a lot of Amiga users, but you don''t want them to\n   know  that  you  got  a  PC  section.   If  they would use the ''C'' door,\n   normally  they  would  see  that  you  got a cosysop for the PC section.\n   "What  PC  section?"  they will think.  Or even worse, new users who use\n   the door can easily spot your conferences.  But not with KiLLER Comment,\n   just  make  sure that the Amiga users have a lower access level than the\n   PC users.\n\n   It''s  not  perfect yet, but it''s a start.  I am thinking of a better way\n   to secure this (it''s possible, I just have to work it out a bit more).\n\n   By  the  way,  cosysops  with  "C"  access  will  also NOT see the other\n   cosysop(s) (not even in the Commentistics).\n\n   » Commentistics\n\n   Not  only in Ami-Express, but also in the Config Editor, you are able to\n   look  up  the statistics that KiLLER Comment can create.  The statistics\n   are  put  into  a  file  and that file is shown to you with the external\n   viewer  you specified.  For your information, that file is always called\n   T:KC_Commentistics,  does  NOT  contain  any  ANSI  codes and is removed\n   afterwards.\n\n   » Add / Del\n\n   Adding  a  user  to  the  list is quite easy, select Add and you will be\n   presented  with  a  list  of all your users in your USER.DATA.  This may\n   take  a  while,  depending on your type (read:  speed) of computer, hard\n   drive  and number of users in your USER.DATA.  A new user will always be\n   inserted at the END of the list.\n\n   To  remove  a user from the list, make it the active user (its name will\n   be  shown  below the listview) and press Del.  Easy as peanuts.  The new\n   current user will be the last user in the list.\n\n   You can not remove all users from the list.  A protection has been built\n   in  so please try to do so :) It''s impossible to remove them all because\n   to who should the users in your system comment to?\n\n   » Up / Down\n\n   With  those  gadgets  you  are  able to determine the order in which the\n   users  will  appear a) in the list and b) on screen in Ami-Express.  The\n   most upper user will be the default sysop!\n\n   To  move  a user, make it the current one by selecting it and then press\n   either up or down (repeatively if neccessary).\n\n   » Save\n\n   Guess what?\n\n   » &\n   \n   Sorry? What did you say? :)\n\n   » Quit\n\n   You  guessed  it.   By  the  way,  there  is  NO  warning if you changed\n   something and did not save it before quitting.\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE Greetings "Greetings go to... - © KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n                            .-------------------.\n                            |  Greetings to...  |\n                            `-------------------''\n\n                            In no specific order:\n\n            Muad''Dib/DLT ^ Motive Power/MST ^ QuartZ/MST ^ Jabbah \n\n            Exotic ^ UFOk/MST ^ Easy Rider/MST ^ I-GO/MW ^ Galaxy\n\n        bObO/MST ^ Famous''O''Hara ^ Zed ^ Green Beret/MST ^ Arcade/MST\n\n                     ... and to all my other friends ...\n\n\n   If you want to contact me, read @{"this!" link Contact}\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE Contact "How to get in touch with me - © KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n                             - ------------------.\n                            |  Contacting me...  |\n                            `------------------ - \n\n       For FAST response (preferred) please contact me on Internet:\n\n                               [email removed]\n\n                    ( [email removed] -- backup )\n\n                       - - -- --- ------- --- -- - -\n\n                 I can be reached on the following boards:\n\n                The Undiscovered       +31-2294-1442 (USR 28k8)\n                                       +31-2294-4442 (USR 28k8)\n                                       +31-2294-tRY! (USR 28k8)\n\n                Last Outpost           +31-72-201182 (USR 28k8)\n                                       +31-72-157682 (USR 28k8)\n\n         I know, you have to call The Netherlands for it, but it''s\n            the only boards I call on a frequent basis, sorry.\n\n                       - - -- --- ------- --- -- - -\n\n        You can also find me on IRC once in a while on the channels\n                     #amigascne, #amiga and #megawatt\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE History "History of KiLLER Comment - © 1994/1995 KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n\n   1.2.0    03-02-95    Fixed the version numbers in the executable ;)\n                        REPORTED BY: MOTiVE POWER\n                        \n                        You can now enter an asterisk behind the name of\n                        the person you want to write to (ie. C MUAD*).\n                        REQUESTED BY: MUAD''DiB\n                        \n                        Made the percentage bar in the commentistics a\n                        relative one, like in KiLLER-Baud. The user with\n                        the most messages will always have 100% and the\n                        rest will be a relative representation to that\n                        user.\n\n   1.1.0    26-12-94    KiLLER [C]omment now checks wether the persons in\n                        the [C]omment list have access to the current conf\n                        that KC is called from. If not, that person will\n                        not be put in the list.\n                        REQUESTED BY: QuartZ\n\n   1.0.5    02-11-94    You can now have lines used as a separator on screen\n                        instead of a blank line.\n                        New tooltype: SEPARATOR_LINES\n                        REQUESTED BY: JAKE\n\n   1.0.4    20-10-94    Added an access level check. If a user does not have\n                        the minimal required access to actually see a cosysop\n                        in the Comment list, than that user will not see\n                        that cosysop. See also @{"History Gui" link HistoryGUI}.\n                        REQUESTED BY: TYCOON/MYSTiC & MUAD''DiB\n\n            20-10-94    The program now attempts to write messages with the\n                        external "E" door (if any). This makes it more\n                        flexible for sysop, allowing them to have external\n                        "E" doors installed, like the one from 5D and the\n                        external one from Tycoon/MYSTiC (/X-Fido).\n                        REQUESTED BY: TYCOON/MYSTiC\n\n   1.0.3    15-10-94    A bug in the "Commentistics" routine caused a guru\n                        when there were users with no messages. A division\n                        by zero was the result -> guru :( Fixed that.\n\n   1.0.0    14-10-94    First initial release to friends.\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE HistoryGUI "History of KiLLER Config Editor - © 1994/1995 KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n\n   1.0.3    14-02-95    Fixed a bug that caused all users with a name\n                        shorter than 4 characters to be left out of the\n                        user-list when you wanted to add a user.\n                        REPORTED BY: PHANTOM/OVERLORDS\n\n   1.0.2    20-10-94    Restyled the GUI bit. I removed the "Show Comments"\n                        gadget because I found it not useful. Removed the\n                        code also (ofcoz, but you never know who reads\n                        this :) ).\n\n            20-10-94    New option: [ Req. Acs ] (Required Access)\n                        You can set a minimum access level per user in the\n                        list. Users with an access level lower than that\n                        level will NOT see him in the [C]omment door.\n                        This enables you to let even new users use this\n                        door and not reveal to them that you (for instance)\n                        have an Amiga cosysop and/or SNES cosysop and/or\n                        PC cosysop.\n                        REQUESTED BY: TYCOON/MYSTIC & MUAD''DIB/DLT\n\n            20-10-94    New option: [ Clear Statistical Data ]\n                        With this option you can clear all statistical data\n                        that is kept for every user. This means that the\n                        total # of msg-s, last msg date and user will be set\n                        to 0 (or None).\n\n            20-10-94    Another restyle: [ Save ][ & ][ Quit ]\n                        Save -> Saves the (new) prefs\n                        &    -> Save and Quit\n                        Quit -> Quit the program\n\n            20-10-94    Another restyle: I changed the placed of the [ Add ]\n                        [ Del ] [ Up ] [ Down ] a bit, to make it a bit more\n                        logical.\n\n   1.0.1    14-10-94    First bug found in 3 secs by Muad''Dib :) If you\n                        selected "Commentistics" from the GUI Config and\n                        there were no messages written yet, a crash was\n                        the result (division by zero). Fixed it.\n\n   1.0.0    14-10-94    First initial release to friends.\n@ENDNODE\n','\n',char(10)),'{"LOCATION":"<path>"}','auto-added',61567,5,0,NULL,NULL,'trsi_c13_2','scan',1780048448);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('compare','COMPARE.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/COMPARE.LHA','Compare','XIM','Compare',NULL,'Thomas',NULL,'\.       /  >---,___ Y .--''      ./ \.  ,------<  /    j `----.  ./Allways ___    \.---------'' /--''`------''./  _on the',replace('    __________.---------, ,---,________\n    \.       /  >---,___ Y .--''      ./\n      \.  ,------<  /    j `----.  ./Allways\n ___    \.---------'' /--''`------''./  _on the\n \ / //-'' \.     / _/          ./ `-//\ line\n  Y  \\----.\____\/___________/,----\\/  for\n _|_//__||_/  \»»>>>---<<<««/  \       you!\n|_|--,____( <> )=Spacecakes( <> )\n__(<>)_____\__/>)___________\__/____________\nCompare 1.05 by Thomas Smistad & K.Galåen\nReleased by spacecakes/frumps. 07.10.95..\n','\n',char(10)),'Compare.DOC',replace('\n\n                                    Compare\n                                      by\n                        Thomas Smistad & Kjetil Galåen\n\n        This program is UnderWare, which means that if you often use it \n        you should consider mailing us money to by our girls new underware,\n        and who knows, maybe you will receve a registered version of\n        our update. \n\nCopying:\n        You may distribute this program as long as all the files in this \n        archive is distributed and unchanged, and nobody ( except us ;) \n        makes profit from it unless we have been contacted and given you\n        our approval.\n\nDescription:\n\n        Compare is a program which compares to files, and print the\n        differences with offset to cli. It is written in assembler,\n        and the routines are very fast.\n\nUsage:\n        Compare <filename1> <filename2>\n\n        This means that you should type the name of the program,\n        followed by the names of the two files you want compared.\n        Example follows.\n\n        If you would like the output written to a file, just redirect it \n        by writing "> device:name". This is useful not only because is \n        stores your output, but if you expect many differences to \n        occur, it is much faster than typing it all to cli.\n\n\nExample:\n        To compare the following two files, ram:test1 and ram:test2,\n        type this in cli:\n\n        Compare ram:test1 ram:test2 >ram:temp\n\n        This will give you the output file temp in ram, looking somewhat \n        like this:\n\n                                File1:          File2:\n                Offset          hex  ascii      hex  ascii\n\n                $00000000       $32  ''2''        $33  ''3''\n                $000000a3       $01  ''.''        $20  '' ''\n\n                Number of differences: $00000002\n\n        The offset equals the number of bytes from the start of the file\n        to the difference. Hex is the content of the byte in the file, and\n        ascii is the ascii presentation of the same number. The number of\n        differences is given in hex ( we didn''t care to convert it to\n        decimal, sorry, but it will be included in a future\n        version ;) .\n        \n\n\nKnown problems:\n\n   - If the files you compare are shifted in propotion to each other,\n     the program doesn''t recognize this. This will give you the rest of the\n     file as differences. ( This will show in the hex/ascii column, but you \n     will get very big difference files ) .\n\n   - This program does not accept quotation marks.\n\n   - This program will not work form an icon.\n\n\nFuture improvements:\n\n   - We will print the "number of differences" in decimal, not hex.\n\n   - Make the program  accept quotation marks.\n\n   - Detect position shifting.\n\n\n\n\n\n      We will not be held responsible for any missuse of this program..\n\n      This program has been tested on an Amiga 500+ with fastram, and an\n      Amiga 1200 with a 030, FPU and fastram, and works perfectly, if you\n      should find any bugs though, we appreciate it if you contact us so\n      that we can fix it.\n\n          Thomas Smistad          Kjetil Galåen\n          Casper Lundes vei 4b    Kolsåsen 11e\n          N-7078  SAUPSTAD        N-7079  FLATÅSEN\n          NORWAY                  NORWAY\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',14098,2,0,NULL,NULL,'compare','scan',1780048448);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('conf','CONF.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/CONF.LHA','JoinCnf','XIM','JoinCnf','3.6',NULL,NULL,NULL,replace('empire JoinCnf V3.6 \n','\n',char(10)),'JoinCnf.doc',replace('\n                  ###### ###   ## ######  ### ######  ######              \n    _______|\     ###    #### ### ###  ## ### ###  ## ###       /|________\n   |         >    ####   ######## ######  ### ######  ####     <         |\n   | |¯¯¯¯¯|/     ###    ### # ## ###     ### #####   ###       \|¯¯¯¯¯| |\n   | |            ###### ###   ## ###     ### ### ##  ######           | |\n   | |_________________________________________________________________| |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |                            JoinCnf V3.6                             |\n   |                            ~~~~~~~~~~~~                             |\n   |                             TYPE:  XIM                              |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |                   ©1994  EMPiRE / MYSTiC /X-PoWeR!                  |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |       LaSt OuTpOsT  +31-72-157682 & +31-72-201182  -  HOLLAND       |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |       AmixNet:  @NL0004   -   /X-Fido:  44:100/102     EMPiRE       |\n   |_____________________________________________________________________|\n\n===============================================================================\n\n PURPOSE:\n ~~~~~~~~\n  o This DOOR is a alternative to the ''j'' command in /X 3.xx\n\n  o At the moment i''m using 36 Conferences and I don''t want Users\n    to ''See'' Conferences where they don''t have Access to, like the Private\n    Conferences.\n\n  o SplitUp between the File and the NetMail Conferences (optional)\n\n  o Passwords Checking for Access to Private Conferences.\n    If a User fails to enter the right Conference Password it will be Logged\n    in DOORS:Doors.LOG and/or he/she will be Kicked-Off (optional)\n\n  o Cursor-Key control for Conference selecting.\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n REQUIREMENTS:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  Ami Express 3.xx\n  It Doesn''t work with Ami Express 1.1x or 2.xx!!\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n INSTALLATION:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  o Copy the EmP_Tools Directory to DOORS:\n  o Make sure ENV: exists! (standard with OS2.x+)\n  o Merge your NodeX/JoinConf.txt with my DOORS:EmP_Tools/JoinCnf.CFG and\n    Edit it to your Needs. (Check the Existing JoinCnf.CFG!)\n\n JoinCnf.CFG LayOut:\n\n##[ start: cut here ]#########################################################\nLOGFILE            Doors:Doors.LOG  ; Log File Name for Password Failures\nDUAL_LISTING       YES              ; Use 2 Listings [YES/NO]\nCURRENT_CNF        YES              ; Show Current Conferences [YES/NO]\nCNF_NAMES          NO               ; Use Names from ConfConfig.info Icon [/X 3.x]\nPASSWORD_LEVEL     255              ; Password Protection Below Level\nNETMAIL_STARTCNF   18               ; First NetMail Conference Number\nDROP_DTR           3                ; Drop Carrier after 3 Password Failures\nCURSOR_KEYS        YES              ; Use the Cursors to select a Cnf [YES/NO]\n[Init_END] ====================================================================\nCNF_NAME.1 =...................... NEW USER\nCNF_NAME.2 =......................... AMiGA\nCNF_NAME.3 =............... AMiGA <OUTPOST>\nCNF_NAME.4 =................ SNES <OUTPOST>\nCNF_NAME.5 =........ MEGADRIVE/MS <OUTPOST>\nCNF_NAME.6 =............. GAMEBOY <OUTPOST>\nCNF_NAME.7 =........... GAME GEAR <OUTPOST>\nCNF_NAME.8 =........... PC-ENGINE <OUTPOST>\nCNF_NAME.9 =................ LYNX <OUTPOST>\nCNF_NAME.10=.................. PC <OUTPOST>\nCNF_NAME.11=................. C64 <OUTPOST>\nCNF_NAME.12=...................... REQUESTS\nCNF_NAME.13=.................... /X SUPPORT\nCNF_NAME.14=. EmP & /X DESiGN BeTaTeST SiTe\nCNF_NAME.15=.............. MYSTiC <PRiVATE>\nCNF_PASS.15=PASSWORD\nCNF_NAME.16=.............. MYSTiC SCENETALK\nCNF_PASS.16=PASSWORD\nCNF_NAME.17=...................... ROM BASE\nCNF_NAME.18=[AX0001]. /X Net Administration\nCNF_NAME.19=[LS0001]......... C Programming\nCNF_NAME.20=[LS0002]....... ASM Programming\nCNF_NAME.21=[LS0003]...... REXX Programming\nCNF_NAME.22=[PN0001]............ Pirate NET\nCNF_NAME.23=[HLT001]............. DuTCH NeT\nCNF_NAME.24=[PFT001].......... Amiga Topics\nCNF_NAME.26=[MOV001].......... Movie Topics\nCNF_NAME.27=[AA0001]........... ANSI Topics\nCNF_NAME.28=[WBS001]............ Buy & Sell\nCNF_NAME.29=[CHBX01]............ ChatterBox\n[Cnf_END]=====================================================================\n  [36m___/\  ___/\  ___/\  ___/\ ___/\  ___/\  ___/\  ___/\  ___/\  ___/\  ___/\\n  \[35m_ [36m. \ \_ . \ \_ . \ \  __\\  __\ \_ . \ \  __\ \_ . \ \  . \ \  __\ \  __\\n  [35m/  |__\/  |  \/  |  \/  ._l/  ._l_/  |__\/  ._l_/  |  \/  |__\/  ._l_/__.  \\n /   ¡   \  ¡   \  |   \  | /   ¡   \  .   \  ¡   \  |   \  ¡   \  ¡   \  ¡   \\n [34m\_____  /______/__¡_  /__¡ \_____  /__¡_  /____  /__¡_  /____  /____  /____  /\n-------\/------------\/-----------\/-----\/-----\/[Ð!]-\/-----\/-----\/-----\/-\n\n[Title_END]===================================================================\n\n[34m---------------------------[  [36mNETMAIL CONFERENCES  [34m]---------------------------[0m\n\n[NetMail_END]==================================================================\n\n[34m-------------------------------------------------------------------------------[0m\n[CurCnf_END]==================================================================\n[34m-------------------------------------------------------------------------------[0m\n[EndTitle_END]================================================================\n##[ end: cut here ]###########################################################\n\n\n\n  - If ''CNF_NAMES'' is set to YES then the CNF_NAME.xx is taken from\n    the BBS:ConfConfig.info Icon [/X 3.x].\n    This makes the CNF_NAME.xx in JoinCnf.CFG obsolete.\n    It''s also possible to Mix this with the Names from JoinCnf.CFG, first\n    the Names from BBS:ConfConfig.info or s:Acp.Startup are read and then\n    the names from JoinCnf.CFG are written over the old ones.\n  - CNF_NAME.x can''t be longer the 80 Characters.\n  - CNF_PASS.x can''t be longer the 40 Characters.\n\n\n[Init_END] ====================================================================\nCNF_NAME.2 =........... AMiGA PUBLIC DOMAIN\nCNF_PASS.15=PASSWORD\nCNF_PASS.16=PASSWORD\nCNF_NAME.18=[AX0001]. /X Net Administration\nCNF_NAME.19=[LS0001]......... C Programming\nCNF_NAME.20=[LS0002]....... ASM Programming\nCNF_NAME.21=[LS0003]...... REXX Programming\nCNF_NAME.22=[PN0001]............ Pirate NET\nCNF_NAME.23=[HLT001]............. DuTCH NeT\nCNF_NAME.24=[PFT001].......... Amiga Topics\n[Cnf_END]=====================================================================\n\n\n  - If you don''t want to Use the ''PASSWORD_LEVEL'' Option then set is to a\n    value greater than 255, this way Everyone has to enter the Private \n    Conference Password.\n\n  - For now I expect that all Conferences above ''NETMAIL_STARTCNF'' are\n    NetMail Conferences so if this isn''t the case or you don''t want to use\n    the File/NetMail Splitup then set NETMAIL_STARTCNF to 0\n\n  - Set ''DROP_DTR'' to the number of Password-tries before the User is Kicked.\n    He/she will not be able to use JoinCnf until ENV:JC-PWFAIL.{SLotNr} has\n    been deleted (for example after a SystemReset).\n    Use ''0'' to disable this option.\n\n  - Set ''CURSOR_KEYS'' to ''YES'' if you want to use the Cursor-Keys to select a\n    Conference. Keep in mind that it only will work if the Output-Screen\n    ''fits'' in the Users TerminalScreen!\n    Set it to ''NO'' to disable this option.\n\n  AE 3.xx:\n  ~~~~~~~~\n  - Copy J.info,<.info & >.info to BBS:Commands/BBScmd/\n\n    Or add to J.info, <.info & >.info ICON ToolType Info:\n\n      ACCESS=001\n      LOCATION=DOORS:EmP_Tools/JoinCnf\n      MULTINODE=YES\n      PRIORITY=0\n      STACK=50000\n      TYPE=XIM\n\n  - If you want ''Relative Conferences'' then you add the following to\n    BBS:CONFCONFIG.INFO IconToolType Info: \n\n      RELATIVE_CONFERENCES\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n USAGE:\n ~~~~~~\n  Just enter J, < or > on the MAIN screen in AmiExpress.\n\n  Selecting > x or < x  will make JoinCnf jump x Conferences Up or Down.\n\n===============================================================================\n\n ERROR MESSAGES:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n  o ERROR:  DOORS:EmP_Tools/JoinCnf.CFG Not Found !!!\n  |\n  `--> JoinCnf.CFG can''t be found in DOORS:EmP_Tools !?\n\n  o ERROR:  BBS:ConfConfig Not Found !!!\n  |\n  `--> BBS:ConfConfig can''t be found in BBS:\n\n  o ERROR:  JoinCnf 3.0 ONLY Works with /X 3.xx!!\n  |\n  `--> Obvious\n\n  o ERROR:  UnKnown Keyword: XXXXXXXX in JoinCnf.CFG\n  |\n  `--> There must be 8 different KeyWords in the INIT part (JoinCnf.CFG)\n       Compare this with the original JoinCnf.CFG\n       Check that the KeyWords are:\n\n         LOGFILE\n         DUAL_LISTINGS\n         CURRENT_CNF\n         CNF_NAMES\n         PASSWORD_LEVEL\n         NETMAIL_STARTCNF\n         DROP_DTR\n         CURSOR_KEYS\n\n  o ERROR:  CNF_NAME part of JoinCnf.CFG is NOT Valid!!\n  |\n  `--> Check that all CNF_NAME.xx are correct and that xx is a Valid Conf.\n       The Line has to start with CNF_NAME.xx=  (example: CNF_NAME.1 =)\n\n  o ERROR:  CNF_PASS part of JoinCnf.CFG is NOT Valid!!\n  |\n  `--> Check that all CNF_PASS.x are correct and that x is a Valid Conference.\n       The Line has to start with CNF_PASS.xx=  (example: CNF_PASS.1 =)\n\n  o ERROR:  BBS:Access/AREA.x Not Found!!\n  |\n  `--> An User got an ConferencesAccess (x) that doesn''t exist (anymore)!!\n\n  o ERROR:  ToolType NCONFS doesn''t Exist in BBS:ConfConfig.info!!\n  |\n  `--> Should/Will never happen... /X Wouldn''t have started!\n\n  o ERROR:  CNF_PASS.x in JoinCnf.CFG is LONGER then 40 Characters!!!\n  |\n  `--> Edit CNF_PASS.x password to a smaller one (< 40 Characters)!\n\n  o ERROR:  Only 100 Conferences are Supported for now!!!\n  |\n  `--> Contact EMPiRE and Blackmail/Bribe him in making a ''Bigger'' version.\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n BUG REPORT & SUGGESTIONS:                                                                   \n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  It''s possible that a mistake will occur.... Nobody is Perfect.\n  If you have any Suggestions or Comments Please Leave a Message on my Board:\n\n   LaSt OuTpOsT  N1: +31-72-157682  N2: +31-72-201182  -  HOLLAND\n   ~~~~~~~~~~~~  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~     ~~~~~~~\n   AmixNet:  @NL0004\n   /X-Fido:  44:100/102\n   UUCP   :  [email removed]\n\n===============================================================================\n\n NOTE:\n ~~~~~\n  o This Program Has been tested on a /X 2.0 - /X 3.38 Configuration.\n  o If you don''t use Conference Passwords then the < and > references are\n    not necessary and can be left out if you want, because the internal\n    < and > are always a bit faster.\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n REGISTRATION:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  If YOU use this Program please let me know by Calling Last Outpost or\n  to send me a Message by NetMail @NL0004 - EMPiRE  Coz I want to know\n  how many Sysops are using my Tools!!!\n \n\n===============================================================================\n\n HISTORY:\n ~~~~~~~~\n  V1.0  07-05-92 - Release Version\n\n  V1.1  07-15-92 - Improved Password Checking\n\n  V1.2  07-28-92 - The internal j(oin) command can be changed.\n                 - Relative Conferences: ConfAccess _______X_ -> j 1 !!!\n\n  V1.3  07-29-92 - Made ''Relative Conferences'' selectable. Default OFF\n                 - Improved Conference selection.\n\n  V1.4  08-03-92 - Default ''Relative Conferences'' is YES. As it''s now Default\n                   in /X 2.1 [1 Aug''92]\n                 - Moved ''Relative Conferences'' to the Config file\n                   [ JoinCnf.CFG CHANGED! ]\n                 - Bug Removed:\n                    o The Door Failed when e.g ''J 1abcd'' was entered.\n                    o Minor Bug removed in the Password Protection.\n\n  V1.5  08-23-92 - Changed the ColorLayout a bit.\n\n  V1.6  09-11-92 - Request Update for THC/DESiRE: 2 Conference Lists.\n                   [ JoinCnf.CFG CHANGED! ]\n\n  V1.7  10-21-92 - Small Improvements.\n\n  V1.8  01-23-93 - Small Improvements in the 2 Conference Lists.\n\n  V1.9  01-25-93 - Bug Report from JPS (Tnx!):\n                    o 1 Cnf List Failed, 1 Line of Code was Accidentally\n                      Killed from the Source.... \n\n  V1.10 02-22-93 - Changed Layout a bit\n\n  V2.ß  04-22-93 - /X 3.1 UPDATE!!! - It''s Still BETA coz I Just got /X 3.1\n                   2 Hours ago!\n        04-29-93 - Added < and > Support because of Password Protection\n        05-03-93 - Better Error Checking (''Fool'' Proof?!)\n        05-04-93 - Changed whole Config (JoinCnf.CFG) Layout!!\n                   [ JoinCnf.CFG CHANGED! ]\n                 - Added ''Current Confererence'' Option\n        05-06-93 - Bug Report from Aragorn/Vision (Tnx!):\n                    o Rexx claims that 2a,2b,.. exist between 1 to 20 (dec)\n\n  V2.0  05-09-93 - Release Version\n\n  V2.1  05-10-93 - Minor Update. The date in Doors.LOG file was wrong.\n        05-20-93 - Added ''Password Level'', this way the Sysop/CoSysop doesn''t\n                   need to enter a Conferences Password eachtime he Joins\n                   that Conference. (Thanx to Alcoholic for the Idea!!)\n                   [ JoinCnf.CFG CHANGED! ]\n        05-27-93 - Fixed the UpperCase Problem in JoinCnf.CFG and all used\n                   Icon Files [/X 3.x]\n\n  V2.2  06-18-93 - Updated the ''<'' & ''>'' code.\n        06-21-93 - Fixed a small Error found with the RexxDoorDebugger.\n        06-28-93 - Added the ErrorMessages in the doc.\n\n  V2.3  07-23-93 - Better Error handling\n\n  V3.ß1 08-10-93 - At last the XIM Version! Rexx is a thing of the Past!\n                 - Changed ALL References from AIM to XIM !!!\n                 - Keywords ''NRSPACES'', ''RELATIVE_CONFERENCE'', ''NCONFS'' are\n                   deleted from JoinCnf.CFG (Obsolete) because they are now\n                   ''read'' from the BBS:ConfConfig.info [/X 3.x] or\n                   s:ACP.Startup [/X 2.xx]\n                   [ JoinCnf.CFG CHANGED! ]\n\n  V3.ß2 08-13-93 - Keyword ''NRLINES'' is deleted from JoinCnf.CFG.\n                 - Keyword ''NETMAIL_STARTCNF'' added to JoinCnf.CFG\n                   If there are NetMail Conferences then the Conference\n                   showing can be split in 2 (Files & Netmail).\n                 - Renamed Keyword ''2_LISTINGS'' to ''DUAL_LISTING''\n                   [ JoinCnf.CFG CHANGED! ]\n                 - Included Optimized 030 Version!\n\n  V3.ß3 08-15-93 - Added the ''LOGFILE'' Option. Password Failures on Private\n                   Conferences will be logged in DOORS:Doors.LOG (default)\n                 - Added the ''CNF_NAMES'' Keyword (was ''CONFCONFIG_NAMES'')\n                   Now ConferenceNames from BBS:ConfConfig tooltype [/X 3.x]\n                   (or s:ACP.Startup [/X 2.xx]) and CNF_NAME.xx from\n                   JoinCnf.CFG can be Mixed in the Output.\n\n  V3.ß4 08-23-93 - Optimized the code and it''s now about 2 kb smaller\n                 - Bug Report from Beast (Tnx!):\n                    o JoinCnf failed completely when the OLD ''LOADCONFIG''\n                      option in ACP.Startup was used [/X 2.xx]\n                 - DEBUG OPTION: enter !% as Conference and you get some info\n                                 when all goes wrong.\n\n  V3.0  08-26-93 - Release Version.\n                 - All Debug routines removed.\n                 - Optimized 030 Version Included.\n\n  V3.1  09-04-93 - Bug Reports from ByteAndi/MST:\n                    o The Last conference couldn''t be joined when Not using\n                      ''RELATIVE_CONFERENCE'' (only happend in the Menu)\n        09-05-93 -  o Sometimes when only entering ''J'' a Conference would be\n                      joined. This is due to a BUG in /X... Fixed for now!\n        09-11-93 - Release Version.\n\n  V3.2  10-02-93 - /X 3.11 Update... AE Returned a different VersionNumber\n                   then in previous versions... this made JoinCnf think that\n                   it wasn''t /X 3.xx but /X 2.xx... FIXED!\n\n  V3.3ß 10-09-93 - Bug Report from ByteAndi/MST:\n                    o Conference Passwords bigger than 80 Chars would Halted\n                      the system! The maximum CNF_PASS size is now 40 Chars.\n                 - Updated some more code. Needs Lesser memory to run.\n                 - Better Error checking.\n        10-14-93 - Bug Report from Sal1/TRSI:\n                    o /X 2.xx & NOT using ''RELATIVE_CONFERENCE'' still failed.\n                      Should be fixed now!\n                 - When the KeyWord ''LOADCONFIG'' is used in the Acp.Startup\n                   [/X 2.xx] then the ''Current Conference'' Option will be\n                   Disabled! \n                 - Some more Code-Optimizing.\n\n  V3.3  12-01-93 - Release Version\n                 - Included an Optimized 020 Version for A1200/A4000 Users.\n                 - Just replace the Old JoinCnf with the New One!\n\n  V3.4ß 01-16-93 - Bug Report from Sal1/TRSI:\n                    o When Using /X 3.20+ & ''NETMAIL_STARTCNF  0'' & Not Using\n                      ''RELATIVE_CONFERENCE'' the Conferences were not shown.\n                 - Added ''DROP_DTR'' option, it Drops the Carrier of the\n                   User after he/she fails to enter the Right Password for\n                   a number of times. After this he/she won''t be able to use\n                   JoinCnf until the file ENV:JC_PWFAIL.{SlotNr} doesn''t exist\n                   anymore (for example after a systemreset). When he tries\n                   he will be Kicked-Off right away!\n        01-17-94 - Bug Report from Mike Hoffren:\n                    o Using 108 Conferences will Crash the System!\n                      In the past it was ''Only'' possible to use 100 Confs,\n                      I never thought there would be more than that!\n                      It''s been Fixed to 256 Conferences for now\n                 - When JoinCnf is run, it will ShowUp on the Server.\n        01-21-94 - Change the Command-Line a bit.\n                 - JoinCnf will now make Use of the full 80 Chars/Line, this\n                   means that LayOut of JoinCnf.CFG Changed a bit!\n                   [ JoinCnf.CFG CHANGED! ]\n        01-25-94 - Fixed the ''10-Node'' BUG. Using Node 10+ would result in\n                   JoinCnf thinking it was started from Node 1.... FIXED!\n\n  V3.4  01-29-94 - Release Version.\n\n  V3.5ß 02-01-94 - Change the ''Full Use of 80 Chars/Line'' to 79 Chars/Line\n                   because some Terminals on Amiga/PC can''t handle the 80th\n                   character on the right (extra linefeeds)!\n                   [ JoinCnf.CFG CHANGED! ]\n                 - Took out all 100+ Conferencing coz /X-Fido is on it''s way\n                   now (so no need for 100+ Conferences) and otherwise the\n                   Code becomes too big! A 100+ Version Can be REQUESTED!\n        02-06-94 - Changed the CommandLine-Input so only Numbers can be\n                   selected.\n                 - Added some BETA-Code to use the Cursor-Keys to select a\n                   Conference. The only BIG problem exists when there are too\n                   many Conferences and the Screen starts scrolling....\n        02-09-94 - Updated the Cursor-Key Code so it''s now possible to Use\n                   Cursor-Keys only if the JoinCnf output-screen fits in the\n                   Users terminalscreen (without scrolling). If it doesn''t\n                   ''fit'' then the Cursor-Keys are disabled otherwise it would\n                   mess up the screen!\n                 - Added the ''CURSOR_KEYS'' KeyWord, when it''s ''NO'' then there\n                   will never be made use of ANSI when using the Cursors.\n                   When the KeyWord is ''YES'' or is leftout then ANSI is used\n                   when the JoinCnf-Screen ''fits'' in the Users TerminalScreen.\n                   [ JoinCnf.CFG CHANGED! ]\n                 - Note: For now the Cursor-Code works only with Relative\n                         Conferences.\n        02-16-94 - Fixed a Small Bug in the Password Handling.\n        02-20-94 - Fixed the Non-Relative Conferences problems so now it will\n                   work on ANY /X 2.xx or 3.xx configuration.\n        02-21-94 - Fixed a Bug in printing the Command-Line to Screen. It\n                   failed when there where Non-Even FileConfs & NetMailConfs.\n                 - Changed the Cursor-Handling. The ''jump'' from FileConf to \n                   NetMailConf has been changed.\n        03-08-94 - Optimized the Cursor-Key Routine.\n\n  V3.5  03-13-94 - Release Version.\n\n  V3.6ß 04-11-94 - Added the ''Q'' to the CommandLine on Tycoon''s Request:\n                    o Pressing ''Q'' will now Exit JoinCnf Immediately, even\n                      when a Conference is selected.\n        04-14-94 - Killed all sscanf''s in the Source coz of Bugs in the\n                   SAS Compiler and this way JoinCnf gets 2 kb smaller!\n        04-17-94 - After a long talk with ByteMaster I managed to kill some\n                   obsolete code, this will make JoinCnf startup Faster!\n                 - Added an New CommandLine Option: \n                    ''> 4''  will Join: Current Conference + 4 (if it Exists)\n                    ''< 9''  will Join: Current Conference - 9 (if it Exists)\n                    ''< -2'' will Join: Current Conference + 2 (if it Exists)\n                 - ReCompiled with the Latest AE.Includes\n        06-28-94 - Fixed some code that can cause random guru''s (SAS C Bug!)\n                 - Removed ALL /X 2.xx support because of the new AE.Includes\n                   JoinCnf won''t work on any /X version before /X 3.38, if\n                   you still have not upgraded then this is the time to do it!\n\n  V3.6  07-01-94 - Release Version.\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n EMPiRE /X DOORS/UTILS COLLECTION UNTIL NOW!:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  - AboStats V0.2                        AIM Door\n  - AE2PCE V1.0                          CLI Util\n  - AutoOnline V1.3                      XIM Door/Util\n  - Bulls V2.2                           XIM Door\n  - CheckDir V1.0                        CLI Util\n  - CheckNU V1.0                         XIM Door\n  - ConfAccess V1.1                      ServerUtil\n  - CopyDate V1.3                        CLI Util\n  - DlDir V2.1                           XIM Door\n  - DoorKIT 1.01                         XIM Doors/Includes\n  - DMenu V1.0                           AIM Door\n  - DutchNET V1.0  [AmiXnet]             AIM Door\n  - Front V2.0                           XIM Door\n  - JoinCnf V3.6                         XIM Door\n  - LastCalls & TopUps V1.2              LogOffUtil\n  - LastDL V0.1                          LogOffUtil\n  - LastUL V0.1                          LogOffUtil\n  - MakeFree V1.1                        AIM Door\n  - MemberList V1.0                      AIM Door\n  - MonthTopUp V2.0                      ServerUtil\n  - MultiNodeLastCaller V1.1             LogOffUtil\n  - Page V2.1                            XIM Door\n  - PMail V1.1                           AIM Door\n  - Remote Maintenance V1.3              AIM Door\n  - SceneTalk Voter V2.3                 AIM Door\n  - SceneTalk Voter V2.2 [Party]         CLI Door\n  - SecLevChk V1.0                       ServerUtil\n  - Sent FrondEnd 1.0  [Sent_FE]         XIM Door\n  - StripCR V1.0                         CLI Util\n  - SysopCommands V1.0                   AIM Door\n  - UserData Cleaner/Repair V2.0         ServerUtil\n  - UserStats V2.0                       ServerUtil\n  - UsrCnfAx V1.1                        CLI Util\n  - View & Check Archive/Text V1.7       AIM Door\n  - WhoNode V1.3                         AIM Door\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n THANX MUST GO TO ALL OFFICIAL BETA-TESTERS:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n   Tycoon/Mystic /X-PoWeR!   [Channel X]\n   JPS                       [Red October]\n   Sal-One/TRSi              [BoonDocks]\n   Blue Bird/Mystic          [Tau Ceti]\n   Beast/Partek              [Sequencial]\n   SpeedDevil/Partek         [Rising Sun]\n   Galaxy                    [Ulixys]\n\n\n GREETZ/TNX GO TO:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n   Killraven/MST /X-PoWeR! - For giving me sum Great Pointers/Sources on ''C''\n   ByteAndi/TRSI           - Tnx for all ya ''C'' Help & Sources!\n   Easy Rider/Mystic       - hope ya are back soon!\n   JAF/G.O.D.              - For some good REXX ideas\n   Bad Sector/Hidden       - Still Using your Sort-Routine. It''s the Fastest!\n   B.O.B./CyberForce       - For (Mis)Using/Testing my tools! :)\n   Aragorn/Vision          - Tnx for Testing\n   Camelot/Complex         - Tnx for Testing\n   Sharon/5D               - Tnx for Testing\n   Telekinetic/T.F.A.      - Tnx for Testing\n   Alcoholic               - Tnx for Testing\n   Price/T.F.A.            - Great job on your {F}ull {S}creen {E}ditor!\n   Van Damme               - Nice Doors!!!\n   DR.G/IBB                - Hope to see Check''N Add work on a 040\n   SiGMA SEVEN             - Nice job on SiGMA-EXPRESS! Tempted to ''Convert''\n   911/Movement            - Tnx For ya Ansi Logo''s!! You''re the Greatest!\n   Mike                    - Tnx for calling!\n   Amicom/TRSi             - Tnx for calling!\n   THC/Legend              - Tnx for Beta-Testing!\n   Mega Fortress           - Tnx for Beta-Testing!\n   SkIn                    - Tnx for ya Description Logo! Looks Great!!\n   Shadow Man/S8           - Nice Doors & Tnx for ya greetz! & Calling ofcoz\n   [MAZ!^PHAZE]            - Tnx for calling!\n   Shuyuki Tanaka          - Tnx for your Messages!\n   AGONY/cOmpLeX           - Tnx for calling!\n   HUMANOiD & jABBA /MST &\n    SCANDAL                - Tnx for calling!\n   LECTOR                  - Tnx for your NetMail\n   Koo Koo Ka Choo         - Tnx for calling!\n   TaRzAN                  - Tnx for your NetMail. Yezz 040 Speed Rulez!!\n   Crayor/Scx              - Tnx for calling!\n   Foxx''n''Lynxx            - Tnx for your BugReports!!!\n   ThE BiRD                - Tnx for your NetMail on UsrCnfAx\n   Dux                     - Tnx for your NetMail\n   dR.dRE!/fAITH           - Tnx for da greetz, Nice Doors btw\n   [-RUNT&SCOTTIE-]        - Tnx for calling!\n   sPAcEcAKe/aF            - Tnx for calling!\n   Freddy Kreuger/GOD      - Tnx for your NetMail on JoinCnf 3.2\n   MF1                     - Tnx for calling!\n   AtomiX/N.A.S.A          - Hope the ''C'' archive was sume help for ya!\n   MAD HARLEQUiN [ITPH01]  - Tnx for your Nice AmiXnet Messy''s\n   Mike Hoffren  [SF0001]  - Tnx for the BugReport on JoinCnf 3.3 [100+ Cnfs]\n   Galaxy/TFA              - Nice job on da SentCleaner\n   SvEN tHE CREAToR/5D     - ''Tnx'' for forcing me to use Cursor-Keys!\n   Diogenes/TPY/5D         - Tnx for calling and for your BugReport!\n   L.A.Style               - Tnx For Calling/Beta-Testing!\n\n   & Ofcoz to ALL MYSTiC Members all over the Globe!\n\n                        ______  __________________                            \n.----------------+-----/    \ \/ / __/_  __/ / __/----------+----------------.\n|                |----/ / / /\  /\  /-/ /-/ / /----[ /X ]---|                |\n|       /\    /\ |-EmP\/ / /-/ /\  /-/ /-/ /\ \--[ PoWeR! ]-|       /\    /\ |\n|      /C \  /!/ +-----\/\/--\/--\/--\/--\/--\/-------------+      /C \  /!/ |\n|     /i/\ \/R/  |                                          |     /i/\ \/R/  |\n|    /T/  \ E/   |   EMPiRE   -   KiLLRAVEN  -   TYCOON     |    /T/  \ E/   |\n|   /S/   /W \   |                                          |   /S/   /W \   |\n|  /Y/   /O/\ \  |   RE/Y\o   -   INCOGNiTO  -   HARDBYTE   |  /Y/   /O/\ \  |\n| /M/   /P/  \ \ |                                          | /M/   /P/  \ \ |\n| \/    \/    \/ |                   BoBo                   | \/    \/    \/ |\n|                |                                          |                |\n`----------------+----------[  MYSTiC /X PoWeR!  ]----------+----------------''\n\n\n \n\n                       ____ _________ _________ ________ _____\n            MYSTiC    /   / \\  /    \\\  /   _\\\  /   \\\  /     MYSTiC\n                     /   /   \\/   /\ \\\/   /___\\/__   \\\/\n         CONSOLE    /   / /\  /   __   \ \____   \   /   /      AMIGA\n                   /   /_/  \/   / /   /_____/   /  /   /\n       WORLD-HQ    \________X___/ /___/\________/   \__/      EURO-HQ\n      ____ _________ ________ _________ _________ _________ ________ _____\n     /    \\\  /   / \\  /   \\\  /    \\\  /    \\\  /   _\\\  /   \\\  /\n    /   /\ \\\/   / /\\\/__   \\\/   /\ \\\/   /\ \\\/   /___\\/__   \\\/\n   /   / /  \/   / /  \   /   / /   _____\/   / /  \ \____   \   /   /\n  /   /_/   /   /_/   /  /   / /   /     /   /_/   /_____/   /  /   /\n  \________X_________/   \__/  \__/      \________/\________/   \__/\n\n\nAMIGA - SNES - MEGADRIVE - GAMEBOY - GAMEGEAR - PC ENGINE - LYNX NEOGEO - C64\n\n4.5 Gb ONLINE             SYSOP:  EMPiRE / MYSTiC               4.5 Gb ONLINE\n\nHOLLAND:              +31-72-157682  &  +31-72-201182               :HOLLAND\n\n','\n',char(10)),'{"ACCESS":"001","LOCATION":"DOORS:EmP_Tools/JoinCnf","PRIORITY":"0","STACK":"50000","TYPE":"XIM"}','auto-added',44471,4,0,NULL,NULL,'mst_jc40','scan',1780048448);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('confsc26','CONFSC26.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/CONFSC26.LHA','ConfScan','XIM','AmigaGuide',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\__ ¬\/¬\\__ ¬Y \__  __\_____¬\__ ¬\__    ¬\ /¬      \/\  l  /\   ¬\/    ¬\/¬\__/¬  \__/ /   \  /  \ \   /  \    \      \   ¬\   / ¬\',replace('_____  _ _____ ____________________________ \n\__ ¬\/¬\\__ ¬Y \__  __\_____¬\__ ¬\__    ¬\\n /¬      \/\  l  /\   ¬\/    ¬\/¬\__/¬  \__/\n/   \  /  \ \   /  \    \      \   ¬\   / ¬\\n\___/\/    \___/    \_   \_____/     \_____/\n|----(______)-(___________)-(_________)ppx-|\n| CONFERENCE SCAN v2.6 - iNTERMEDiATE REL. |\n+------------------------------------------+\n| o Ami-Express 3.38+ and 4.x Compatible!  |\n| o Remembers flagged files after log off! |\n| o Much more! Read inside!                |\n`-----------------------[KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC]-''\n','\n',char(10)),'ConfScan.Guide',replace('@DATABASE "ConfScan.GUiDE"\012@REMARK .------------------------------------------------------------------.\012@REMARK | This document is written in AmigaGUiDE format, so please read it |\012@REMARK | with AmigaGUiDE or your favourite guide reader.... ciao now...   |\012@REMARK `------------------------------------------------------------------''\012@REMARK $VER: ConfScan v2.6.06\012@WiDTH 80\012@NODE MAiN "Guide to ConfScan v2.6.06 - /X-PoWeR! - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\012                               Guide to ConfScan\012                     for Ami-Express Bulletin Board Systems\012\012                          Program version: 2.6.06\012              Compilation Date/Time: Oct 7th 1994 - 23:21:06\012\012                         © 1993-94 by @{"KiLLRaVeN/MYSTiC" link Killraven}\012                          ASM Coding by ArCaDe/MYSTiC\012\012                ... another fine MYSTiC /X PoWeR! production...\012\012                 @{"      READ THiS FiRST FOR THE LATEST iNFO!     " link Important}\012\012                 @{"    Introduction    " link introduction}      @{" History of ConfScan " link History}\012                 @{"     Features!      " link     Features}      @{"    Known Bugs       " link Bugs}\012                 @{"    Requirements    " link Requirements}      @{" Possible error msgs " link Errors}\012                 @{"    Installation    " link installation}      @{" Future improvements " link Future}\012                 @{"    Configuration   " link Configuration}      @{"     Greetings       " link Greetings}\012                 @{"  Usage (by users)  " link        Usage}      @{"  Registered users!  " link Registration}\012\012                 @{"    ConfScan_DL     " link ConfScan_DL }      @{"     KiLLER iNFO     " link KiLLER}\012@EndNode\012\012@Node Introduction "Introduction to ConfScan - /X-PoWeR! - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\012                     - - ­ ­ ­ [ iNTRODUCTiON ] ­ ­ ­ - -\012\012   Welcome to ConfScan!\012\012   ConfScan  was  written  during a period of 1 year and has become quite\012   a  powerful  program  with  many possibilities and great potential.  I\012   have spent a lot of time programming and testing it so I hope you will\012   like it and use it with pleasure.\012\012   A little bit of history...\012\012   At first ConfScan was merely meant as a small util that enabled sysops\012   to  easily  check  what  was uploaded in all the different conferences\012   without  having  to  join them one by one.  The very first version did\012   nothing  more  than  that.  That was version 1.0.  It was never really\012   released but to a few friends.\012\012   Nowadays ConfScan can perform a much greater task than just displaying\012   some  filenames  on  the  screen.  ConfScan can now be used to control\012   some  main  parts  of  the  bulletin  board  system Ami-Express.  With\012   ConfScan  you  can  scan for new files, view them from within ConfScan\012   and you can even Nuke files with ConfScan.  Usage of ConfScan has been\012   made as intuitive as possible and should be very easy to use.\012\012   ConfScan  is  an  intelligent program, detecting the options for every\012   user  using  ConfScan, not showing options that they don''t have access\012   for.   ConfScan  also recognizes Ami-X Net conferences that usually do\012   not have file bases, as a result these conferences without a file base\012   are not shown in the config menu (''CS W'').\012\012   ConfScan  comes  with  a  highly user friendly GUi Config program!  No\012   more  tooltypes  to fill in by the sysop!  Just start the program from\012   the CLi or Workbench and CLiCK the options you want and save''m!\012\012   ConfScan  is  made  in a way that you don''t have to repeat information\012   that  is  already known is other files or icons.  ConfScan knows where\012   to find it and will use it.  But in my opinion that is something every\012   program  should  support.   Besides that, if you have any problem with\012   ConfScan  you  can  always reach me for support, I am offering support\012   for all registered sysops of Ami-Express, FOR FREE!\012\012   But  not only for you, the sysop, ConfScan is a must.  Your users will\012   also  appreciate  it  since  ConfScan  allows users to tag their files\012   instead  of  flagging them (but they can still flag files if they want\012   to  ofcourse)  and  ConfScan  enabled  them  to  download  files  from\012   different   conferences  without  having  them  to  jump  through  the\012   conferences  by  theirselves.   in  the  near  future, it will also be\012   possible  to  download all files from all conferences in one time!  So\012   look out for the coming version!\012\012   ConfScan also offers your users a large configurability.  ConfScan has\012   a Config Menu built in so they can easily adjust their preferences.\012\012   A seperate Download door enables you to put restrictions on downloads.\012   With  the  GUi  Config  program  you can easily exclude conferences or\012   nodes from downloading.  You can put accesslevels on nodes/conferences\012   or  even  use userlists for download access on nodes/conferences.  And\012   all  this  information is again saved by the Config program, so you do\012   not have to fill in any tooltypes (GUi Config does that for you).\012\012   if  this  sounds  like  a  useful  program in your ears, check out the\012   @{"features" link features} to find out more.  Or at least start the GUi Config.\012\012                                                        @{"-KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC" link Killraven}\012\012@EndNode\012\012@Node Requirements "What DO you need? - /X-PoWeR! - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\012                   - - - ­ ­ ­ [ REQUiREMENTS ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   The  requirements can differ a lot since you can setup ConfScan anyway\012   you  like,  but  if  you  want to use ConfScan to the fullest you need\012   this:\012\012   · @{" Ami-Express BBS " link Ami-X} version 3.38+ (/X 4.x is supported)\012   \012     YOU NEED VERSiON 3.38 OR HiGHER TO RUN THiS PROGRAM, PLEASE OBTAiN\012     THE LATEST VERSiON FROM YOUR DEALER (SEE "AMi-EXPRESS BBS").\012\012   · @{" Clean dir files " link CleanDir}\012\012   For the support of [V]iewing files you need to have in your C: dir\012   · DMS\012   · LHA\012   · UNZiP\012\012   If you want to be able to nuke files with ConfScan you need to have\012\012   · @{" KiLLER " link KiLLER}\012\012   installed on your system.\012\012@EndNode\012\012@Node CleanDir "VERY iMPORTANT! READ THiS! - By KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\012                 - - - ­ ­ ­ [ CLEAN DiR FiLES ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   This  may sound obvious, but to get the most out of ConfScan, you need\012   to  have  clean  dir files.  So no taglines or any other alien text in\012   your dir files.\012\012   There is one exception on the other hand, there is one program you are\012   allowed to use to alter your dir file and that is DirStyle by The Bird\012   of  TRSi.   Support  for this dirstyler is built in to ConfScan.  This\012   was  done  after a request from Sal-One/TRSi.  If you have a dirstyler\012   that  you  would like to have support for, contact me and maybe we can\012   work something out.\012\012   Nukers on the other hand cause no problems.  You are free to use them,\012   even better, there is support for two nukers:  BossNuke and KiLLER.\012\012   "What  can  go  wrong  if I use a dirstyler?" you might wonder.  Well,\012   there  is  one thing that can go wrong; file-tagging.  ConfScan uses a\012   algorithm  to  recognize  filenames in the dir-file.  But if you use a\012   dirstyler  that  puts text where normally filenames are, ConfScan will\012   see that text as a filename.\012\012   If  you  still want to use that dirstyler, you can turn of the tagging\012   with the Config program (see @{"Configuration" link Configuration}).\012@EndNode\012\012@Node Installation "How to get it working - /X-PoWeR! - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\012                    - - - ­ ­ ­ [ iNSTALLATiON ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   To install ConfScan, simply double-click on the install-ConfScan icon.\012\012   Installation  will  proceed  with  the  C=  installer.   Help has been\012   provided  in  the  installer  program,  so  no  need  to  repeat  that\012   information in here.\012\012   What can you do with the installer? The installer script will:\012\012   · Allow  you  to  install  the  ConfScan  main  executable  (ConfScan\012     itself).  You can choose either for the 68000 or 680x0 version.\012\012   · Allow you to install the ConfScan_DL Download door that  is  needed\012     for Ami-Express to recognize any flagged/tagged  files.   This  one\012     comes in just one flavour, 68000.\012\012   · Allow you to install the ConfScan_G door which checks if users have\012     flagged  files  still  not  downloaded  before they logoff (a small\012     patch for the original ''G'' door, nothing special).\012\012   · Allow  you to install the help files that come with ConfScan.  Such\012     files are needed to give help to users that use ConfScan.  They can\012     get  access  to  these  files  by putting a question mark after the\012     command (ie.  `N ?'').\012\012   · Allow  you to install the fully GUi Configuration program (Config).\012     This  program  will  allow  you  to  mold ConfScan to your personal\012     needs.   Here you can set all pre-defined preferences, such as ANSi\012     support,  show  new  dates  etc.   etc.  But this is also the place\012     where  you  can  set  download restrictions and exclude conferences\012     from being scanned.  And much more!\012\012   · Allow you to install this guide. You are reading it now.\012\012   · Let  you  choose  as  which  command  you  can to install ConfScan.\012     ConfScan  can  act like 3 different commands, `N'', `F'' and `CS''.  I\012     suggest  you install it as all 3 functions, but if you want you can\012     skip the `CS'' door ''cause it is built-in in `N'' also.\012\012   · Let  you  select the place where you want to install ConfScan.  The\012     default  destination  is  "DOORS:" but you are free to put it where\012     you  want  (the  destination  will  be  put  in  the  command icons\012     afterwards).   Remember,  a directory `ConfScan'' will be created in\012     that directory!\012\012   · Let  you  select  the  name  of  the  command  that the ConfScan_DL\012     download  door will be installed under.  I strongly suggest you put\012     it under the ''D'' cause otherwise users will not be able to download\012     anything ;)\012\012   · Let  you select the place where you want to install the Ami-Express\012     commands.\012     (Default: BBS:Commands/BBSCmd/).\012\012   · Let you set the minimum level required to use any of the ConfScan\012     related commands.\012     (Default: 20).\012\012   · Let  you  set the priority ConfScan will get when executed (only if\012     you  are  an  expert user).  If you are running a multinode system,\012     please  set  it  to 0, otherwise users on the other nodes will have\012     hindrance  from  it  if  you  give  it +1.  Systems with 1 node can\012     easily set it to +1 or +5 for maximum performance.\012     (Default: 0).\012\012   · Ask for the directory where you keep your ACP.info.  This is needed\012     for the Config program.\012\012   · Start the Config program for you so you can configure ConfScan.\012\012   All  commands will get a stack of 50,000 and will be set to multinode.\012   As ConfScan is written in C and ASM, it will be installed as a XiM.\012   \012   If  you want ConfScan installed under another name than `CS'', you will\012   have  to  do  it by hand.  But you can still use the installer.  After\012   installation,  simply rename the CS.info icon in your BBS:Commands/...\012   directory  to  whatever  you  want  (for example, `SCAN'').  This will,\012   however,  force  you  to rename some of the help files as well (rename\012   every file that has ".CS." in it to ".SCAN.").\012@EndNode\012\012@Node Configuration "Config - For easy configuration - KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\012                  - - - ­ ­ ­ [ CONFiGURATiON ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   ConfScan  comes  with an external configuration program called Config.\012   It  is  fully  GUi  so  no more stupid textfiles to create or icons to\012   fill.   Just  start  the  program  and  away  you  are.  Here are some\012   guidelines where you can find some stuff and what it all means.\012\012\012              ^-[ ACCESS LEVELS ]-^\012\012   Hold Access       ­ Every user with an access level equal to or higher\012                       than  the  value  you enter here, is able to watch\012                       the contents of the hold dirs.\012                       (Default:  250).\012\012   View Access       ­ Every  user with an access level >= than the value\012                       you  enter  here,  is  able to view files that are\012                       shown  in  the  dir  file.   You can specify which\012                       filetypes   are  supported  via  the  View  prefs.\012                       (Default:  20).\012\012   KiLL Access       ­ Every  user with an access level >= than the value\012                       you  enter  here,  is  able  to  flag/tag files as\012                       KiLLER  targets.  This is for usage with the nuker\012                       @{"''KiLLER''" link KiLLER}.\012                       (Default:  250).\012\012                ^-[ iNTRO FiLE ]-^\012\012   Intro file        ­ The  filename that you can specify here (either by\012                       entering the filename in the text box or selecting\012                       it  with ''S'') will be the name of the file that is\012                       shown at every startup of ConfScan.  At the moment\012                       you  can enter no variables (such as time/date and\012                       place).\012                       (Default:  <none>).\012\012         ^-[ DEFAULT USER PREFERENCES ]-^\012\012   These are the values that are used if an user does not have his or her\012   own private configuration for ConfScan.\012\012   ANSi Colours      ­ This  option  turns the colours on or off when the\012                       files  are  showed  in your screen.  You can setup\012                       those colours via the `Colours'' button.\012                       (Default: Off)\012\012   Show Sent-by      ­ By  default,  ConfScan  will  filter  out any file\012                       description  lines  that  start  with  ''Sent by:''.\012                       They  are  usually not interesting for users.  But\012                       with  the  latest File_iD''s and SentBy''s you don''t\012                       know what to expect anymore.\012                       (Default: Off)\012\012   Show New Dates    ­ Every time a new date is detected, a little banner\012                       will be displayed informing you of the new date.\012                       (Default: Off)\012\012   Clear Screen      ­ After  *every*  prompt, the screen will be cleared\012                       if  you  turn  this option on.  This speeds up the\012                       display  on  screen  quite  a  bit, esspecially on\012                       local nodes, try it.\012                       (Default: Off)\012\012   Lines b/files     ­ Some  users  find  it  usefull  to have a line put\012                       between all the files.  This does the trick.\012                       (Default: Off)\012\012   Pause b/confs     ­ This   will   put  a  pause  banner  between  each\012                       conference that has got new files.\012                       (Default: Off)\012\012   Return b/files    ­ Some  users  find it usefull to have an empty line\012                       between  all  the  files.  If you''ve got the time,\012                       use  it,  it  makes  it  easier  to detect all the\012                       different files.\012                       (Default: Off)\012\012   One line per file ­ If  you  turn  this on, just the first line of the\012                       file description will be shown.  Very handy if you\012                       want to tag a lot of files FAST.\012                       (Default: Off)\012\012   Always full desc. ­ This   will   prevent   file  descriptions  to  be\012                       displayed broken on your screen.  Turn this on and\012                       from  *every*  file you will always get to see the\012                       entire   file   description.   This  mode  can  be\012                       overridden with the [P] at the flag-prompt.\012                       (Default: Off)\012\012   Future expansion  ­ Guess what? Not used.\012\012               ^-[ SYSOP PREFS ]-^\012\012   This  is  where you set all the internal preferences ConfScan will use\012   while operating.  It more or less controls the engine of ConfScan.\012\012   Copy dirfiles     ­ With  multiple node systems, this is a must!  This\012                       will   first  copy  your  dirfile  to  T:   before\012                       searching   it  for  a  file  date.   This  allows\012                       multinode support.\012                       (Default: Off)\012\012   Callerslog        ­ Every  time ConfScan is started and this option is\012                       activated,  it  will  be logged in the callerslog.\012                       (Default: Off)\012\012   Use Percentage    ­ A  nice feature of ConfScan is, that it is capable\012                       of  showing  a  percentage  (%)  on  screen  while\012                       searching  the  dirfiles.  If you don''t want this,\012                       turn this option off.\012                       (Default: On)\012\012   Nuker Support     ­ ConfScan  is  also able to recognize comments made\012                       with   nukers.   Currently  supported  nukers  are\012                       BossNuke  and  KiLLER.   But any comment placed on\012                       the  spot where normally the file-size is, will be\012                       seen  as  a nuker comment.  Any nuker comment will\012                       be  display  with a dark-blue background and white\012                       characters.   If  you  don''t  want that to happen,\012                       turn this off.\012                       (Default: On)\012\012   Allow Tagging     ­ @{"Tagging" link Tagging}  is  a  thing  of the day, ConfScan had it\012                       first!   If,  for some reason, you don''t want your\012                       users to tag files, turn it off.\012\012                       Another  reason  why  you want to turn this option\012                       OFF  is  because you use a @{"dirstyler" link CleanDir} that confuses\012                       ConfScan in it''s file-recognition algorithm.\012                       (Default: On)\012\012           ^-[ iGNORED CONFERENCES ]-^\012\012   Any  conference you put in this listview will NOT be seen by ConfScan.\012   That  means  that  it will not scan the conference for new files (CS),\012   not will it be shown when the users wants to set his/her config.\012\012   You  can  add  a conference with "Add Conf", a list will appear of all\012   your conference and simply click on the one you want to add.\012\012   To remove a conference, select the one you want to remove and click on\012   "Del Conf".  Izze simple.\012\012                 ^-[ COLOURS ]-^\012\012   If  you  click  on  the [Colours] button, you will get a new window in\012   which you can enter the colours for the file listing.\012\012   The  values  you  can enter are ANSi ESC colour codes, here is a brief\012   display of all colours:\012\012             BLACK = 30 - RED    = 31 - GREEN = 32 - YELLOW = 33\012             DBLUE = 34 - PURPLE = 35 - LBLUE = 36 - WHiTE  = 0\012\012   Filename          ­ Colour of the filenames.\012                       (Default: 36)\012\012   Status            ­ Colour of the file status (P = Passed, etc.).\012                       (Default: 35)\012\012   File Size         ­ Size of the file (no, really?).\012                       (Default: 33)\012\012   File Date         ­ Date of the file (no kidding?).\012                       (Default: 31)\012\012   Description       ­ Colour that will be used for the file description.\012                       Mind  you  that  this ESC sequence will be sent at\012                       the  start  of  the  file description.  That means\012                       that  if  there is an ANSi colour code in the file\012                       description, the remainder of the file description\012                       will  be  in  THAT  colour  code  and not that you\012                       specify here.\012                       (Default: 0)\012\012                       NOTE:   Although ESC[37m is also the ANSi code for\012                       white,  Ami-Express fails to handle this correctly\012                       cause  the  local  node  will show RED (while your\012                       users  will  actually  have  white).  But by using\012                       ESC[0m you can circumvent this problem.\012\012                ^-[ ViEW PREFS ]-^\012\012   This  is  where  you  can specify which filetypes are allowed to view.\012   Currently supported filetypes are:\012\012   DMS               ­ Files  that  have  DMS  as  a file extension.  The\012                       action  that  is  performed on these files is "DMS\012                       ViEW <filename>".\012                       (Default: On)\012\012   LHA               ­ These  are  files  that  have  LHA  or  LZH  as an\012                       extension.   The action performed on such files is\012                       "LHA V <filename>".\012                       (Default: On)\012\012   Text files        ­ A whole range of extensions go for this file type:\012                       NFO,  NF0,  TXT,  DOC  and  ASC.   These files are\012                       simply  shown  to  them.   This  might  be the ONE\012                       filetype  you  want  to  turn  off  since the show\012                       routine will NOT abort display when it sees binary\012                       codes.\012                       (Default: On)\012\012   ZiP files         ­ Files with the extension ZiP will be attacked with\012                       an "ZiP -v <filename>" command and the result will\012                       be shown on screen.\012                       (Default: On)\012\012                 ^-[ SAVE iT! ]-^\012\012   To  save  all your settings, simply click on the [Save & Exit] button.\012   To quit without saving, close the window.\012\012      ^-[ WHAT ABOUT THAT OTHER BUTTON? ]-^\012\012   That  button  [ConfScan_DL]  lets  you setup some restrictions for the\012   download command.  See the @{"ConfScan_DL guide" link ConfScan_DL} for that!\012@EndNode\012\012@Node Features "Features of ConfScan - /X-PoWeR! - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\012                      - - - ­ ­ ­ [ FEATURES ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012 · GUi  Config  program that can be started from the CLi or Workbench for\012   easy configuration of ConfScan, a first for an /X-Tool!\012\012 · FAST searching with LOW memory consumption! Max. 60Kb per node!\012\012 · ConfScan  can  act  like `N'', `F'' and it''s own `CS''.  So you get three\012   programs for the download of one!  8-)\012\012 · ConfScan  can  show  you the full file descriptions always, so no more\012   broken file descriptions on your screen.  Fully user configurable.\012\012 · One  of the main features of ConfScan is ofcourse the fact that it can\012   scan  multiple  conferences in one time, this is unique!  No other dir\012   scanner is able to do that but ConfScan.\012\012 · Another  feature  is  the  file  @{"tagging" link Tagging}.  Although other dir scanners\012   provide  this  options  also,  ConfScan was the first to use it and it\012   kind of revolutionized the way of tagging/flagging files.\012\012 · Users  can  setup  ConfScan  to  their  own  personal  likings  via  a\012   preferences  menu they can call up with the ''W'' argument.  But this is\012   not  so special anymore.  Maybe the fact that it looks good and has no\012   overabundance  of  colours  in  it make it better than the other ones.\012   Also,  ConfScan recognizes conferences without a filebase and will not\012   even show them to users in the config menu.\012\012 · This is what the users can setup for theirselves:\012   ­ ANSi colour display\012   ­ Line between files\012   ­ Return between files\012   ­ Pause between conferences\012   ­ Show new dates\012   ­ Show sent-by (or not)\012   ­ Always show full descriptions\012   ­ Clear Screen after every prompt\012   ­ Show just the 1st line of a description\012\012 · Like I said above, ConfScan recognizes conferences without a filebase.\012   This is done to support Ami-X Net conferences (they usually don''t have\012   them). You don''t have to specify them, ConfScan is ''smart''.\012\012 · Scanning options; ConfScan has them, here you go:\012\012   ­ Scanning from a certain date\012   ­ Scanning from a number of days back\012   ­ Scanning from the day a user was last on\012   ­ Scanning from [t]oday\012   ­ Scanning in current conference or all conferences\012   ­ Scanning in upload dirs, all dirs or specified dir\012   ­ Scanning in hold dirs (special access-level required)\012   ­ Scanning in selected conferences (user configurable)\012   ­ Scanning with a byte- & filereport afterwards for users with\012     [H]old access (f.e. cosysops).\012   ­ Scanning non-stop\012\012 · Flagging  from  ALL  conferences is possible, ConfScan will keep track\012   itself  of all the files flagged and via the Download door, /X will be\012   informed about them (i.o.w.  they will be flagged).\012\012 · The  special  download  door  does  more  then just flag files for the\012   users.  It can automatically join the next conference where files were\012   flagged  by  the user.  This can be done straight away when they start\012   the download command in a conference where they have selected no files\012   or right after the downloading of files of that conference.\012\012   NOTE!       In  the near future, ConfScan will be able to send all the\012   ~~~~~       files  to  the  users  in  ONE  time.  This saves time and\012               trouble  for your users as well as for your board, it will\012               be  less  busy. \012\012 · With  @{"KiLLER" link KiLLER} installed, you can nuke files from within ConfScan.  Most\012   likely  you  will find a beta version of KiLLER inside and you will be\012   able  to  test it.  As soon as I''ve finished coding it, I will release\012   it  and  make  sure  you  can  still keep using it in cooperation with\012   ConfScan as well as a stand-alone program.\012\012   ALSO READ THE @{" HiSTORY " link History} iN THiS GUiDE FOR MORE iNFO ABOUT THESE\012   FEATURES!\012\012@EndNode\012\012@Node Usage "Usage by users (that includes you) - /X-PoWeR! - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\012                       - - - ­ ­ ­ [ USAGE ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   ConfScan  is  very  easy  to  use, despite of it''s army of options ;-)\012   ConfScan comes with a set of very clear help files that your users can\012   call  in for help with ''<command> ?''.  This goes for ''N'', ''F'', ''G'' and\012   ''CS''.   Here are they in plain ASCII.  Feel free to change them if you\012   want  to.   To  get  a  full  view  of all recognized command, see the\012   @{"ALL COMMAND LIST" link SysopCommands}.\012\012   All the help is put into separate files for your convenience.  This is\012   done  to  support  multiple screentypes (so you can have separate help\012   files  for  every  screentype  (=  language)).  They are called:\012\012                      N  - Command   : ConfScan.N.Help.TXT\012                      F  - Command   : ConfScan.F.Help.TXT\012                      G  - Command   : ConfScan.G.Help.TXT\012                      CS - Command   : ConfScan.CS.Help.TXT\012\012                       In that order, their contents are:\012\012                         ^-^-^-^-[ B R E A K ]-^-^-^-^\012\012                              ConfScan User Help \012 \012  N -x     Files from x days back        Extra options:\012  N <date> Files from <date> and on      ­­­­­­­­­­­­­­\012  N S U    Files since last logon        · Add ''NS'' for non stop display\012  N T U    Files since today             · Use CTRL-C to break program\012  N S G    Files since last logon        · Enter ''N W'' for to edit your own\012           from all conf''s (Global)        personal environment settings.\012 \012                              Environment Options\012 \012  · Select global conferences            · Put lines between files on screen\012  · Usage of ANSI colours in list        · Put return between files on screen\012  · Leave out sent-by''s                  · Pause between conferences (only used\012  · Display new date banner                when you scan globally)\012  · Clear the screen after prompt        · Display only first line of descr.\012 \012  · Show Full Descriptions is an option that will make sure you will always\012    get to see the full description of a file, and never will the description\012    of a file be broken on your screen. It is not the opposite of ''one line''!\012\012                          ^-^-^-^-[ B R E A K ]-^-^-^-^\012\012                               ConfScan User Help\012 \012  F        Pop up ''f'' menu               Extra options:\012  F <#>    Files from dir <#>            ­­­­­­­­­­­­­­\012  F U      Files from upload dir         · Add ''NS'' for non stop display\012  F A      Files from all dirs           · Use CTRL-C to break program\012  F H      Files from hold dir           · Enter ''F W'' for to edit your own\012           (access required)               personal environment settings.\012 \012                              Environment Options\012 \012  · Select global conferences            · Put lines between files on screen\012  · Usage of ANSI colours in list        · Put return between files on screen\012  · Leave out sent-by''s                  · Pause between conferences (only used\012  · Display new date banner                when you scan globally)\012  · Clear the screen after prompt        · Display only first line of descr.\012 \012  · Show Full Descriptions is an option that will make sure you will always\012    get to see the full description of a file, and never will the description\012    of a file be broken on your screen. It is not the opposite of ''one line''!\012\012                          ^-^-^-^-[ B R E A K ]-^-^-^-^\012\012                               ConfScan User Help\012 \012  CS -x     Files from x days back       Extra options:\012  CS <date> Files from <date> and on     ­­­­­­­­­­­­­­\012  CS A      Files from all dirs          · Add ''NS'' for non stop display\012  CS T      Files since today            · Use CTRL-C to break program\012  CS <#>    Files from dir <#>           · Enter ''CS W'' for to edit your own\012                                           personal environment settings.\012  CS scans globally for new files in     · Add ''+'' for a byte-report\012  the upload dir since last logon          (access required)\012  unless specified different (above).\012 \012                              Environment Options\012 \012  · Select global conferences            · Put lines between files on screen\012  · Usage of ANSI colours in list        · Put return between files on screen\012  · Leave out sent-by''s                  · Pause between conferences (only used\012  · Display new date banner                when you scan globally)\012  · Clear the screen after prompt        · Display only first line of descr.\012 \012  · Show Full Descriptions is an option that will make sure you will always\012    get to see the full description of a file, and never will the description\012    of a file be broken on your screen. It is not the opposite of ''one line''!\012\012                          ^-^-^-^-[ B R E A K ]-^-^-^-^\012\012                          ConfScan Goodbye Explanation\012 \012   Theory  Your sysop has installed ConfScan for scanning the dirfiles,\012           and ConfScan stores your flagged files in a different matter\012           then Ami-Express does (because ConfScan can remember flagged\012           files from multiple conferences and /X can''t). This also asks\012           for a different ''G'' command, this is it!\012 \012           This new commands does the same as the internal one, with a\012           few differences:\012 \012           ^ Ability to start downloading from ''G''\012           ^ Ability to view your remaining flagged files\012           ^ Ability to remove your remaining flagged files\012 \012 Practice  Once notified that you have remaining files, your options are:\012 \012           [G] ^ Goodbye, let me out!             To force ConfScan_G to\012           [L] ^ List the remaining files         just log off, enter a\012           [D] ^ Download remaining files         ''!'' after the G (''G !'').\012           [R] ^ Remove them & log off\012           [Q] ^ Quit, back to /X prompt          (c) ''94 KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC\012\012                          ^-^-^-^-[ B R E A K ]-^-^-^-^\012\012   SEE ALSO: @{"More options" link More}\012\012@EndNode\012\012@Node Future "Possible Future improvements - /X-PoWeR! - KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\012                - - - ­ ­ ­ [ FUTURE iMPROVEMENTS ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012 · Downloading  ALL  files  from  ALL  conferences  in ONE time.  This is\012   possible now thanks to the help of Joe Hodge (thanks Joe!).  Make sure\012   you  are  a  registered  sysop,  or  else you want be able to run that\012   version of ConfScan!  It will require /X 3.38+.\012\012 · Improved  file  tagging,  it can be annoying sometimes that you cannot\012   reach a file that is still on screen.  I will have to look into that.\012\012 · ''A'' command to alter/remove flagged files (multiple conferences ofcoz).\012\012 · ''Z''  command  to  search  in  multiple  conferences  and with ConfScan\012   interface.\012\012   Anyway,  if  you  have  suggestions,  make  sure  to  drop me a line at\012   Channel-X or at one of the other MYSTiC boards (in Holland preferably,\012   that''s where  I  am most).  By the way, you don''t need to have a\012   suggestion to call  the MYSTiC boards, you''re welcome at any time, open\012   24 hours a day and at your service!\012\012   Let me know what you think and what YOU think needs improvement!\012\012                            __                       /\\012    :        _ __  __Stz___|  \________/\___________/_ \______/\ _       ·\012   _¦_______ //  \/  \_/   |  \\_  ____  \           /__/      \\\ ______:_\012    |        //       \___   ___/____ \ //__/    |__/  .|   /___/_       |\012    |     ._/    \/   \\_|    \    \|  \/\_//    ||    ||  /      \_.    |\012    |  .:::\_____||_____/|_____\__________/______||_____|__________/:::. |\012   -+--      W O R L D W I D E   B U L L E T I N   B O A R D S !       --+--\012    |                                                                    |\012    |       MASTURBATiON STATiON - 7 NODES - WHQ! - 1-305-552-1192       |\012    |           LAST OUTPOST     - 2 NODES - EHQ! -  +31-721-57682       |\012    |             THE EAST       - 3 NODES - SCHQ -   +46-8-940614       |\012    |         FORBiDDEN ENTRY    - 3 NODES - CHQ! - 1-416-281-3912       |\012    |           TRADE LiNES      - 1 NODE! - CHQ! - 1-514-966-9569       |\012    |           UZi SUiCiDE      - 3 NODES - USHQ - 1-203-437-8655       |\012    |            CHANNEL X       - 2 NODES - DHQ! - +31-2290-62244       |\012    |           OUT OF SPACE     - 1 NODE! - SHQ! -  +46-620-13141       |\012    |         FORBiDDEN PLANET   - 2 NODES - IHQ! - +353-1-820-8489      |\012    |           ROCKA ROLLA      - 2 NODES - THQ! - +90-216-363-5742     |\012    |            TAU CETi        - 1 NODE! - ESHQ -   +34-34255620       |\012   -+--------------------------------------------------------------------+--\012    :                                                                    :\012\012@EndNode\012\012@Node Bugs "Known Bugs - /X-PoWeR! - Wild Stallions Shall Rule! 8-)"\012                    - - - ­ ­ ­ [ KNOWN BUGS ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   This  is  the  part  that  all  programmers hate, admitting that their\012   program contains bugs.  I''ll ease my mind with the thought that nobody\012   is  perfect  and  that  hopefully  due to a bug, I will once day get a\012   receipt  from  the bank saying that I''ve got $10 million on my account\012   8-) Here we go...\012\012   · When  you  are  at the end of a dir file (like 95%) and you only got\012     one  file  after  pressing  return,  you 