n\niF uSER gOT rATIO 0 tHEN dOOR wILL oFCOZ nOTICE tHAT ;)\ntHIS sETTINGS aRE aLSO tHE dEFAULT iF nO sETTINGS aRE fOUND!\n\n\naXXCHECK.aNSI:\n\ntHIS IS tHE fILE tHE dOOR sHOWS iF tHE uSER iS sETBACK!...\nyOU cAN cHANGE iT tO wHATeVER yOU wANT.. ;)\n\n*END OF DOC*\n\n\n\ntHNX gOES tO: dR. ICE\SEA fOR aLL hELP wITH tHIS E cODE!\n              wOOBER\aRCADE fOR tHE dESIGN!\n\noTHER gREETZ tO:aLL fRIENDS ,aLL pALS aT #aMIELITE,aMIGANO,#sID64\n\naNY qUESTIONS,iDEAS,bUGS?..cALL cHECKpOINT BBS oR eMAIL mE aT:[email removed]\n\n                      thundercat^digital corruption''98\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',9942,4,0,NULL,NULL,'dc_axx10','scan',1780048460);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dc_dgw','DC-DGW.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DC-DGW.LHA',NULL,'XIM','DIGI-WHO.EXE',NULL,'ItaL/DC^FRS','DC','_\_ \\__//  __/\__/\_ _//  \|  |_ |   \ \  \\  \  |  \_/ \/ "  \  / \ |_____/_  /\____|_  /_  /_|__/____/FuN',replace('    ___ ____ ______________ __  __\n   _\_ \\__//  __/\__/\_ _//  \|  |_ \n  |   \ \  \\  \  |  \_/ \/ "  \  / \\n  |_____/_  /\____|_  /_  /_|__/____/FuN\n.--v-^-v--\/^-v-^--^\/^-\/v-^---^-v-^---.\n| C · O · R · R · U · P · T · I · O · N |\n|-^--^--v-^-v-^--^--v-^---^-v-^--^-v-^--|\n|              Digi Who v1.o            |\n|             by  ItaL/DC^FRS           |\n|    Nice Looking Who Door for /X v4+   |\n`---------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'About.txt',replace('\n\n               StEPhEn KiNg''S\n        ______  ______  ______  _______  _______  ____ __  ___     \n      ___)    \__)    \__)    \__)     \__)  ___)__)  Y  \__) \_   \n      |-   |   |-   /  |-   /  |-   \   |-    ___)-   |   |-   |__ \n      |    |   |   ____|   ____|     \  |     \  |    |   |   /   |\n      l____l___l_______)_______)_trb____l______) l________l_______|\n           ______   ___ __  ___   ______  _______  _______  \n          __)    \___) Y  \__) \___)    \__)     \__)     \ \n          l___|   |-  _|_  |-   |-   |   |-   _(__|-   (___)\n              |   |   ___  |    |    |   |   (___ l___,    |\n              l___l____l___l____l____l___l________l________|\n\n            [ A1200 sLiM % fALcON/40/882 % 10 mB 32 bIt RaM ]\n                 [ 2.8 GigS hDD % oNLiNe cD % uSR v34+s ]\n\n                 [ tHA oNLy MaStER : It/\L oF FREEZERS! ]\n                [ Co-MaStERs : dWEEP % Eugene % d/\iSy % ]\n\n                   [ NodE 1: +90-216-36E Lite ] [ v34+ ]            \n                   [ NodE 2: +90-216-32E Lite ] [ v34+ ]\n\n       [ AmiGa ElitE % Pc ElitE % ModS % MidS % SaMPs % gRaPhiCs ]\n       [ AmiGA MuSiC StUFF % 64''eR StUFF % AtARi MuSiC % ReQuESt ]\n\n                [ x2 fOR MaJoRs % x3 fOR yOuR oWn MaJoRs ]\n\n                \n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',9665,2,0,NULL,NULL,'dc_dgw','scan',1780048460);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dc_ml13','DC-ML13.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DC-ML13.LHA','SX_MSG','XIM','SX_MSG',NULL,'DigitalCorruption','DC','dC! |  _ \_  |/    |/  |_  _/ ._ |   | zS!sE _ |  /  /  /  |_ /   |/  |  |/ |   |_  _ \\ |____/   \___/ \___|   |__/  |_____| //',replace('     ________| ____  __|_________|___\ndC! |  _ \_  |/    |/  |_  _/ ._ |   | zS!sE\n  _ |  /  /  /  |_ /   |/  |  |/ |   |_  _\n \\ |____/   \___/ \___|   |__/  |_____| //\n|¯      \____| \___|  \____| \_____|      ¯|\n|   · C Ø R R U P T ¡ Ø N    ¹ 9 9 8 ! ·   |\n|                                          |\n|  SX_MSG v1.3 Update - XIM MessageLister  |\n|     for SystemX by DigitalCorruption     |\n|_                                        _|\n //28.Mar.99_______________________[r]FoX\\\n','\n',char(10)),'SX_MSG.guide',replace('@database 67acfcc0-0\n@master AA-dev:BETA/SX_MSG/doors/ML/SX_MSG.guide\n@$VER: 1.0\n@remark Created with Heddley v1.1 (c) Edd Dumbill 1994\n\n@node "Main" "SX_MSG - The MessageBase Lister for SystemX"\n@next "intro"\n@prev "Main"\n\n    @{b}@{u}@{bg highlight}wELCOME tO SX_MSG 1.3 wRITTEn bY [r]FoX@{ub}@{uu}@{bg back} \n              \n     @{b}@{bg shine}XIM for SystemX by dIGITAL^cORRUPTION@{ub}@{bg back} \n          \n        @{b}dA dOCuMETa              \n        -----------               \n\n    @{"-[  iNTROdz  ]-" link "intro" 0}    about this\n    @{"-[  iNZTALL  ]-" link "install" 0}    installation\n    @{"-[   uSAGE   ]-" link "usage" 0}    usage of the MessageLister\n    @{"-[  fEATURe  ]-" link "features" 0}    fetaures\n    @{"-[   pLANs   ]-" link "plans" 0}    future plans       \n    @{"-[  cONTAcT  ]-" link "contact" 0}    contact & support    \n    @{"-[    S\X    ]-" link "sx" 0}    SystemX BBS software       \n    @{"-[  gREETZz  ]-" link "greetz" 0}    greezie   \n\n    A Messages Indexer for the only usage \n          with the XIM-port of the \n      System-X Bulletin Board Software\n@endnode\n\n@node "intro" "intro"\n@next "install"\n@prev "Main"\n \n @{b}@{bg highlight}Welcome to the MessageLister !@{ub}@{bg back}\n ------------------------------\n\n SX_MSG V1.3 is an XIM-Door for the usage with the \n @{"SystemX" link "sx" 0} BBS software only \n and cannot be used under other BBS programms!\n\n The MessageLister is nice to use with upcoming \n Fido software or other  Netwares for @{"SystemX" link "sx" 0},\n or simpley to make your Messagebases under SystemX most\n visible and easy in its handling of messages.\n\n This Door is a basic instrument, to give overview \n to all the configured MessageBases.\n It shows the existing MessageBases in a conference, \n total Msgs, new ones and a lot more...\n\n\n @{"<" link "Main" 0}  @{">" link "install" 0}  @{"Main" link "Main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "install" "install"\n@next "inst_MCI"\n@prev "intro"\n\n @{b}@{bg highlight}Installation:@{ub}@{bg back}\n -------------\n\n@{b}@{bg highlight} ! ALL NEW FEATURES OF THIS UPDATE RUN ONLY CORRECT ON !\n !    SYSTEMX v1.o6b [eSSeXX] BY DIGITAL CORRUPTION    !@{ub}@{bg back}\n\n The MessageLister gives you a powerfull handling \n for the MessageBases of SystemX. \n The Door is so advanced in its handling, that i use the\n other Message Commands  like `E` or `R` to it, too.\n You may give any Commandname you like. `ML` as Commandname \n runs fine here, including the fingerdynamics ;)\n\n @{bg fill}Now do it :@{bg back}\n\n - Copy all archive contents to SX:Doors/ML/ or any Directory\n   you like.\n\n - configure the Door call\n\n   + by @{"MCI-File" link "inst_MCI" 0}    \n   + as @{"XIM Door" link "inst_XIM" 0} \n   + as @{"MailScan" link "inst_MS" 0}   \n   + as @{"BaseBull" link "inst_BB" 0}\n \n - Restart SystemX, so the new settings will be activated\n\n Thats all.\n Now Login and call the Door in your selected way.\n While startup the Door shows you an Index about the installed\n MessageBases in the current Conference and a CommandPrompt,\n were you may enter yer actions.\n Check one of the scan-functions to see,\n if all Conferences/MessageBases\n are scanned for you. if not, so check your Conference Access.\n\n\n @{"<" link "intro" 0}  @{">" link "usage" 0}  @{"Main" link "Main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "usage" "usage"\n@next "features"\n@prev "install"\n \n @{b}@{bg highlight}How to use that shit ?@{ub}@{bg back}\n ----------------------\n\n After calling the MessageLister, first an ansi-header comes up\n (@{i}if the sysop @{ui}@{"calls the Door by MCI-File" link "inst_MCI" 0}) \n or the Door starts direcly with an overview of the installed \n MsgBases in the actual conference, you are.\n\n ex:                \n                  +- @{bg shine}current Conference Name@{bg back}\n                  |           \n                  |           +- @{bg shine}current Date/Time Last Call@{bg back}\n                  |           |                    |        \n                  |           |                    |\n                  *           *                    *\n MsgBases in New User  05-18-98 | 14:30:52 LastCall: 05-18-98 \n --------------------------------------------------------------\n (  1) - New Users Chat   [ 278/8]|----------------------------\n ---|-----|------------------|---|---\n    |     |                  |   |\n    |     |                  |   +- @{bg shine}Number of New Msgs@{bg back}\n    |     |                  +- @{bg shine}Number of total Msgs in this@{bg back}\n    |     |                     @{bg shine}MsgBase@{bg back}\n    |     +- @{bg shine}Name of the MsgBase@{bg back}    \n    +- @{bg shine}Number of the MsgBase in current Conference@{bg back}\n\n \n @{b}TitleBar Informations@{ub} : - current Conference Name\n                         - current Date\n                         - current Time\n                         - Last Call Date/Time\n\n          @{b}MsgBase List@{ub} : - Number of MsgBase\n                         - Name of MsgBase\n                         - Total Msgs in Base\n                         - Total New Msgs in Base\n\n After that a Commandprompt comes up and you are able \n to use the following commands:\n\n ex:\n\n @{b}@{bg highlight}MsgLister Commands: ?,CR,E,R,L,I,S,s,+,-,#,(New Users Chat) :@{ub}@{bg back} \n\n The name of the current MsgBase, you browse in, is shown \n in the parentieses on the Commandprompt were you enter the\n Commands you like to do.\n The CommandPrompt also accepts digits for the selected  \n MsgBase you like to join. (see `I`-command) \n\n @{bg highlight}The commands are :@{bg back}\n \n @{b}?@{ub}   - @{bg shine}View the Helpmenu@{bg back}\n                This shows a small menuansi, explaining, what\n                the commands are doing.\n\n @{b}??@{ub}  - @{bg shine}View an additional Helppage@{bg back}, with more explaination to\n                the commands.\n\n @{b}CR@{ub}  - @{bg shine}Press Return and the MsgLister will quit@{bg back}. The Door will\n                quit, if you enter any unknown command.\n\n @{b}E@{ub}   - @{bg shine}Enter a Msg@{bg back}\n                Here you join Enter Msg by SystemX. You have to\n                put the Reciver and the subject into a normal \n                way. Just enter a Msgs ...\n\n @{b}R@{ub}   - @{bg shine}Read a Msg <Argumment>@{bg back}\n                You may give an Digit Argument here for the Msg\n                you like to read.\n                For that, you write the Msgnumber you wich, \n                like `r 13` or `r32` \n\n @{b}L@{ub}   - @{bg shine}List Msgs <Argument>@{bg back}\n                This will list all Msgs Headers in the current\n                MsgBase.\n                If a Digit Argument is given to the `L`\n                command, the Messages are listed from the \n                MsgNumber <Argument> to Listend.\n                If no MsgNumber is given, the list starts at \n                Msg #1.\n\n                The List will inform you about:\n\n                   - Name of MsgBase\n                   - total Msgs in MsgBase\n                   - Msg number\n                   - Date/Time of Msg edit\n                   - Name of writer\n                   - Name of receiver\n                   - Replay Marker\n                   - New Marker\n                   - File Attached Marker\n                   - Msg Subject\n                   - `PRIVATE MSG` Flag\n                   - `DELETED` Flag\n\n                The Massage Markers are:\n\n                 @{bg fill}  > @{bg back} replayed\n                 @{bg fill} >> @{bg back} replayed twice\n                 @{bg fill}  * @{bg back} new Msg\n                 @{bg fill}  + @{bg back} file attached           \n\n @{b}I@{ub}   - @{bg shine}Index of MsgBases@{bg back} in the actual Conference.\n                This will show you the same, as you see at\n                startup the Door. If you enter a Number at the\n                CommandPrompt, you automatic join the selected\n                MsgBase(Nr.) and see the list of last Msgs in\n                the new joined MsgBase.\n\n @{b}S@{ub}   - @{bg shine}Scan for new Msgs@{bg back}. \n                This Mailscan searches for new Msgs for you\n                and let you choose btw. READ, QUIT, IGNORE \n                the new mail.\n                The Mailscan also accepts Msgs to \n                `all` and `eall`. \n                After that, you return the CommandPrompt.\n       \n    @{b}@{i}! If you call the Door with additional Argument `s`,\n    so only! Mailscan will be executed.\n \n              Ex:`ml s`. see @{"Calling SX_MSG" link "install" 0}\n\n    If you call the Door with additionaöl Argument `i`, \n    so only! the MsgBase Index is shown!@{ub}@{ui} \n\n s   - @{bg shine}scan for unreaded Msgs <Argument>@{bg back}  (see L.R.P.)\n       A short Index of unreaded Msgs will shown here in the\n       form of the Mailscan. \n       All Conferences, you have axx to, are scanned and all   \n       unreaded Msgs are visible and counted.\n\n       @{b}If you give the `s` Command an Argument `o`, all\n       unreaded Msgs will reset to OLD (read already).@{ub}\n       \n       @{b}This will not reset the flag for New Mail, \n       its for @{i}unreaded@{ui} ! @{ub}  \n\n @{b}+/-@{ub} - @{bg shine}browse to next/previous MsgBase@{bg back} in this Conference\n\n @{b}#@{ub}   - @{bg shine}List the last Msgs only@{bg back}\n                How many lines are listed, is given by the\n                usersettings ScreenLegth.\n                Only the last Messages will be listed as Header\n                List as same as the `L` command does.\n\n\n @{"<" link "install" 0}  @{">" link "features" 0}  @{"Main" link "Main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "features" "features"\n@next "plans"\n@prev "usage"\n       \n@{b} @{bg highlight}history/features:@{ub}@{bg back}\n -----------------\n         \n SX_MSG V1.3:\n         \n   10.2.98\n          - activ prompt, show current msgbase name\n          - msgbase selection with num. input direct at the\n            prompt, then readtopic->user.screenlenght->listend\n            only.\n          - msgread selection with argument `r 12` or `r12` \n            here join Msg Options of sx\n          - complete msgs indexlist or only the last ones will\n            shown number,date,time,from,to,reply,subject\n          - ascii found and colored :) now MCI-file does \n            clearscreen at beginning (optional), then logo,\n            then door or what ever you want\n          - some bugs fixed\n          - double listing the MessageBases\n            titelbarinfo: current conference name, current\n            time/date, last login, max msgs/new msgs in\n            current base\n   25.3.98\n          - bugfix - handles 256 MessageBases with maximal\n            10.000 Messages/MessageBase\n          - reply marker - shows, if the Message is answered  \n            if a msg is replyed more then 1 time, its a double\n            reply marker\n          - new nice looking helpmenu added\n          - private-flag added  :   + if msg is private\n                                      subject=`PRIVATE`\n                                    + private msg subject\n                                      visible for \n                                      writer and reciver\n          - delete-flag added   :   + deleted msgs have\n                                      `DELETED` in subject\n   3.4.98\n          - changed gfx-output a bit\n          - cut the timestring to 5 chars, swap time and date\n            output\n          - move the actualbase(baseindex) function to trash.\n            found XIMFunction(507,0,0) JH_MCI :) for current\n            msgbase at the prompt\n          - bugfix - change the current LRP\n          - new msgs are shown now ! flagged in baseindex and\n            subjectlist and how many of them.\n          - bugfix - cut the messagebasename to 12 chars, coz\n            output trouble\n          - optimised the code, i.e. done an argumentparsing\n            for SX_Function\n          - tuned the gfx a bit\n          - added a small and raw info\n   22.5.98\n          - added a Mailscan what shows unreaded and new mails\n            Mailscan let you choose between read the new msg,\n            do not read or quit mailscan. If you like to read\n            your new mail, Mailscan joins the msg automatic,\n            acceps `eall`,`all` and `username` to be active\n          - call the door with argument `s` for mailscan only !\n          - added an argument for `s` (scan for unreaded msgs,\n            named `o` to switch all msgs in all msgbases to\n            OLD.\n\n          - added an argument for `L` (Listview) were you can\n            give a msgnumb from what you like to view the list\n   28.5.98\n          - Mail/Msgscan has now a conference user access level\n            check. If the User has no access to any conference,\n\n            the mailscan breaks.\n          - an Informationpage was added with more detailed\n            explaination about the commands        \n   30.5.98\n          - if Users Screenlength <= 27 lines, the\n            informationpage switched to a second part\n          - optimised the source, killed lamershit. source: 54k\n            including all Ansis\n    1.6.98\n          - make the conference axx check more advanced. checks\n            now all confs for axx, does not break after noaxx\n            anymore. \n            Ex: Confaxx:  XXX_XX_X\n          - do some more small internal fixes, opts, gfx,\n            funcs,... only penouts\n    3.6.98\n          - bugfix - after Mailscan found new mail, the\n            CommandPrompt is ok now. fixed some penouts, too\n          - finish this Guide\n   20.3.99\n          - make very more code optimisations. source: 20k\n          - add prefix `i` to show the MsgBases of the actual\n            conference, only\n          - fix a bug in SX: Join.ANS was shown before you \n            really join the conference, so if you call Doors\n            from theJoin.ANS file, what are MsgBase specific,\n            you earn the data from last conf.\n            Now use ML as internal map command to call it in\n            Join.ANS like:\n            ~SX_MI\\17\\0| (execute internal map function)\n          - add a blue(Esc[34m)`+` as flag for fileattaches in \n            the Msg.\n\n   known Bugs:\n                        \n   - MailScan does not work 100%, sometimes new Msgs are\n     not found and any crap is typed and the LRP is set :(\n     I will fix this, when i include SX-Config->Doors->MailScan\n     in SystemX soon.\n\n\n @{"<" link "usage" 0}  @{">" link "plans" 0}  @{"Main" link "Main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "plans" "plans"\n@next "contact"\n@prev "features"\n\n @{b}@{bg highlight}Future Plans:@{ub}@{bg back}\n -------------\n\n go to the net :)\n check out the fido transfer, build a router, a sorter, \n a spooler with inbound/ and outbound/ in Mail:\n Implement this into SystemX. \n Results of such things can earliest be viewed in \n some months, coz there are a lot of other projects\n we are on, so please have patient :)\n\n next todo:\n               \n          - delete msg by nr. from subjectlist (SXFunction?) \n          - if a msg is replayed, add `re:` to the subject \n            WHILE REPLAYING\n            need implementaion in sx, too, or i do it in the ML\n          - \n          - \n          -                     \n    \n @{"<" link "features" 0}  @{">" link "contact" 0}  @{"Main" link "Main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "contact" "contact"\n@next "sx"\n@prev "plans"\n\n @{b}@{bg highlight}Contact:@{ub}@{bg back}\n --------\n\n All your suggestions, hints and comments are welcome.\n Bugreports are importand for me to know, so i can fix anywhat.\n \n There are serveral way`s to connect me : \n\n My BBS:\n -------\n +49(0)451/55220      Node #1 with 56ooo v.9o\n\n Internet:\n ---------\n\n  EMail : [email removed]\n              [email removed]\n\n    WWW : http://www.luebeck.netsurf.de/~clasen\n\n Feel free to write me. \n\n\n @{"<" link "plans" 0}  @{">" link "sx" 0}  @{"Main" link "Main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "sx" "sx"\n@next "greetz"\n@prev "contact"\n\n @{b}@{bg highlight}SystemX Bulletin Board System@{ub}@{bg back}\n -----------------------------\n\n@{b} SystemX@{ub} is a new Bulletin Board System in the Style of\n AmiExpress.\n\n The archive includes all needed files to run a full\n configurable Bulletin Board System. There are serveral\n utilities posted with the archives.\n\n @{bg shine}SX (eSSeXX) has a lot of features:@{bg back}\n\n        - Supports 7 door types:\n                        - AmiExpress (XIM)         \n                        - AmiExpress AREXX (AIM)    \n                        - DayDream                \n                        - DayDream AREXX                \n                        - Paragon/MAXsBBS          \n                        - Shell/Dos/STDIO               \n                        - FAME         \n        - full flexable Bulletin Board System\n        - up to 256 Conferences\n        - up to 256 Fileares per Conference\n        - up to 500 MsgBases per Conference\n        - Partially compatable with /X\n        - XPR protocol support (xpr#?modem.library)\n        - HydraCom/SModem support.\n        - comfortable GUI Config\n        - comfortable GUI UserEd\n        - lots of internal Functions \n        - supports MCI-Commands\n        - ARexx port ("SX-MCP")\n        - Line and Fullscreen Message Editor with \n          fileattachment\n        - easy CommandMenu creation\n        - full MCI-Code support on all ansis shown by SX\n        - nearly all is editable by the sysop\n        - ...\n\n The List is long ...\n \n\n SystemX is done by Digital Corruption.\n For contacting the Author of SystemX \n\n               @{bg shine}mailto: [email removed]@{bg back}\n\n or visit the SystemX Support Page at \n \n               @{bg shine}http://www.luebeck.netsurf.de/~clasen@{bg back}\n\n@{bg highlight}                SystemX is Freeware !                @{bg back}\n\n\n @{"<" link "contact" 0}  @{">" link "greetz" 0}  @{"Main" link "Main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "greetz" "greetz"\n@next "Main"\n@prev "sx"\n\n @{b}@{bg highlight}gREETz:@{ub}@{bg back}\n -------\n\n Greetings un unordered form:\n\n Get_Merry, Thaler, Obligator, Wolfman, Phantom, Jungle,\n Sal-One, Wizzler, Woober, Ramonster, Stark, Case, Zed, \n Trantor, Kunglao, Digiman, Gandalf, DiGITaLCoRRuPTiON,\n Rasta, Test, Shadow, Merlin, Badgirl, Raped,Prodigenator,\n Crusader, Wolfman, Jedi, Belzebuth, R19, Ubit, Shadow, \n GetMerry, ShenDC, SigmaSeven, Crazy, Lizard, Looney, torque \n WarPig, Kryten, Quasar, DC1, Holger&Olli :)\n #elitecafe, #amielite\n and many many more ...\n\n @{"<" link "sx" 0}  @{">" link "Main" 0}  @{"Main" link "Main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "inst_MCI" "inst_MCI"\n@next "inst_XIM"\n@prev "install"\n\n @{b}@{bg highlight}Call ML by MCI-File:@{ub}@{bg back}\n --------------------\n \n If you call the MessageLister by an MCI_File, you may handle\n the startup in serveral ways.\n How to use MCI-Files you can read in the SX-Guide.\n\n - open SXConfig -> Menus/Commands -> Main_Menu\n - add a new Command:\n\n   Command :  ML         /* the Command Name       */\n   ExtraNr.:   0         /* no Extra Number needet */\n   LowAxx  :  10         /* Low Axx for the ML     */ \n   HighAxx : 255         /* High Axx for the ML    */\n   Func.ID :  12         /* show Ansi              */\n   Door/String/File : SX:doors/ml/sx_msg.ans   /* path to the\n                                                  ML-Header  */\n\n - check the Part in the @{b}SX_MSG.ans@{ub} (AnsiHeader), were\n   the Door is called like `@{b}~SX_doors/ml/sx_msg.ans@{ub}`, \n   if its correct for you.\n\n Do not kill the `[2J` for clear Screen at the top of the file\n while editing with any AnsiEd !\n\n You may edit the HeaderFile like your whishes, a complete\n MCI-Command Reference for SystemX ca be found in the SX-Guide.\n\n Send me your own MessageLister Headeransi, i will spread it\n with the next update !!\n\n @{"< Install" link "install" 0}  @{">" link "inst_XIM" 0}  @{"Main" link "Main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "inst_XIM" "inst_XIM"\n@next "inst_MS"\n@prev "inst_MCI"\n\n @{b}@{bg highlight}Call ML as XIM:@{ub}@{bg back}\n ---------------\n\n If you call the MessageLister direct as XIM-Door, it will\n start without any preactions with the Index of the \n MessageBases in the current Conference.\n\n - call SXConfig -> Menus/Commands -> Main_Menu\n - add a new Command:\n\n  @{bg shine} Command : @{bg back} ML     ; Command Name       \n  @{bg fill} ExtraNr.: @{bg back}  0     ; no ExtraNr. needed \n  @{bg shine} LowAxx  : @{bg back} 10     ; LowAxx for the ML  \n  @{bg fill} Highxx  : @{bg back}255     ; HighAxx for the ML \n  @{bg shine} Func.ID : @{bg back}120     ; XIM-Door !         \n  @{bg fill} Door/String/File : @{bg back} sx:doors/ml/SX_MSG  ; the path to ML\n\n - Restart SystemX to activate the new Command.\n\n Now logon and check, if all went fine :)\n\n \n @{"< Install" link "install" 0}  @{">" link "inst_MS" 0}  @{"Main" link "Main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "inst_MS" "inst_MS"\n@next "inst_BB"\n@prev "inst_XIM"\n\n @{b}@{bg highlight}Call ML as MailScan:@{ub}@{bg back}\n --------------------\n\n If you Login to yer SystemX, the MessageLister has a nice\n Feature to @{b}scan for new Msgs@{ub}.\n If you call the MessageLister with an Argument `@{b}@{i}s@{ub}@{ui}`,\n only the MailScan function of the MessageLister will work.\n\n Example: `@{b}@{i}ml s@{ub}@{ui}`\n\n The MailScan found new Msgs for you, for `@{b}eall@{ub}` and for `@{b}all@{ub}`.\n If the MailScan found such Msg, you can select between\n \n -    @{b}Q@{ub} ...... Quit/Abort the Mailscan\n -    @{b}N@{ub} ...... No reading, but proceed scanning\n - @{b}CR/Y@{ub} ...... Read the new Msgs\n\n If you add a command for the Mailscan to the @{b}Internal Map@{ub} of\n SystemX, you can call it from MCI-Command @{bg shine}(~SX_MS\17\0|)@{bg back}\n from any ansi/ascii like in @{"BaseBull" link "inst_BB" 0} mode.\n\n @{"< Install" link "install" 0}  @{">" link "usage" 0}  @{"Main" link "Main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "inst_BB" "inst_BB"\n@next "install"\n@prev "inst_MS"\n\n @{b}@{bg highlight}Call ML as BaseBull:@{ub}@{bg back}\n @{b}--------------------@{ub}\n\n If you join any Conference in yer SystemX, the MessageLister\n has a nice Feature to show the Messagebases in the joined \n Conference.\n\n You have to edit a new command in @{b}SX-Config -> Internal Map@{ub}\n i.e. `MI`\n\n @{b}@{bg shine}in Door/String/File:@{ub}@{bg back} Doors:ML/SX_MSG\n @{b}@{bg shine}Mainline Arguments :@{ub}@{bg back} i\n\n Call the MessageLister with an Argument `@{b}i@{ub}`,\n the MessageLister will only show the MsgBases in the\n current Conference and nothing more.\n\n Example:      Enter following line to your Join.ANS\n\n               @{b}~SX_MI\17\0|@{ub}     ;SXFunction 17:\n                                 execute internal map function \n\n\n @{"< Install" link "inst_MS" 0}  @{">" link "usage" 0}  @{"Main" link "Main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',23919,3,0,NULL,NULL,'dc_ml13','scan',1780048460);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dc_x106b','DC-X106B.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DC-X106B.LHA','SX','XIM','SX',NULL,'DigitalCorruption.','DC','dC! |  _ \_  |/    |/  |_  _/ ._ |   | zS!sE _ |  /  /  /  |_ /   |/  |  |/ |   |_  _ \\ |____/   \___/ \___|   |__/  |_____| //',replace('     ________| ____  __|_________|___\ndC! |  _ \_  |/    |/  |_  _/ ._ |   | zS!sE\n  _ |  /  /  /  |_ /   |/  |  |/ |   |_  _\n \\ |____/   \___/ \___|   |__/  |_____| //\n|¯      \____| \___|  \____| \_____|      ¯|\n|   · C Ø R R U P T ¡ Ø N    ¹ 9 9 9 ! ·   |\n|                                          |\n|   System-X [eSSeXX] v1.o6b Updatefiles   |\n.Bulletin Board System by DigitalCorruption.\n|_                                        _|\n //.08.Apr.99.___________________.[r]FoX.\\\n','\n',char(10)),'Changes.GUIDE',replace('@database SXDoc\n@master sx:doc/changes.guide\n@remark Created with Heddley v1.1 (c) Edd Dumbill 1994\n\n@node "MAIN" "System-X BBS Software"\n\n -= System-X Changes =-\n\n Since System-X is born in the end of `96 lots of changes are\n done on this software.\n The BBS was under development by ZED for all versions \n up to the 1.05r2\n\n @{" Version 1.01    " link "101" 0}\n @{" Version 1.02    " link "102" 0}\n @{" Version 1.03    " link "103" 0}\n @{" Version 1.04    " link "104" 0}\n @{" Version 1.04fix " link "104f" 0}\n @{" Version 1.05    " link "105" 0}\n\n Then he leave the development and gave the sources \n out to aminet.\n I pick them up some weeks before and at that time i`m working\n more and more on the codes.\n\n @{"Version 1.06      " link "1.06" 0}\n Changes in the 1.06 are done carefully, coz the sources are \n new and i have to study the powerfull envoirement \n of the sources, before i do any bigger changes.\n \n @{"Version 1.06b     " link "106b" 0}                \n This version contains more changes to make some things \n running better.\n@endnode\n\n@node "101" "Version 1.01"\n -=[ 14-June-1997 ]============[ 1.00 -> 1.01 ]===============-\n\n        - TELNET callers no longer get a baud of 0\n        - Enforcer hits removed from SX and SX-Config \n          (thanks Skittle)\n        - Deleting Messages now possible\n        - Quoting Messages now possible\n        - Better DayDream Support \n          (WHO''s ONLINE doors work, SoulFront and \n           RealTimeWho tested!)\n        - SX-Config->Doors->FrontDoor feature now works \n          (tested with SoulFront)\n        - "C"onfig Button added to SX-MCP\n        - SX-Config->MCPPrefs Improved\n        - Delete/UnDelete now functional in online UserED\n        - If two new users logged in at once it would \n          screw up - fixed\n@endnode\n\n@node "102" "Version 1.02"\n -=[ 25-June-1997 ]============[ 1.01 -> 1.02 ]===============-\n\n        - Sent-by-Lines now work\n          (SX-Config->Confs "SentByLine"check boxes)\n\n        - Background upload checker included!\n          (You must enable it in each conference, SX-Config->Confs)\n\n        - Checks userbase when entering message\n\n        - FILE_ID.DIZ from ZIP now unpacks properly\n\n        - Doesn''t re-init modem when you open screen or press HELP\n                (this could hangup on a connecting caller)\n\n        - Pause after each screen now possible\n\n        - ibmcon.device included. This may be used in-place of\n          kalacon.device in your "Local Display" and "Display Modes"\n          config. It offers fast 2/8/16 color ANSI and some VT100 support.\n\n        - Checks for ansi''s in conference path, eg:\n\n                SX:Confs/Amiga/Commands.255.ANS\n                SX:Confs/Amiga/Commands.ANS\n                SX:Screens/Commands.255.ANS\n                SX:Screens/Commands.ANS\n\n                This would be the order in which it searches for the ansi.\n\n        - Two new functions added (17 and 18), See DOC/SXFunctions.\n\n        - It''s now possible to run a filechecker door. Refer to SX.Guide\n@endnode\n\n@node "103" "Version 1.03"\n -=[ 16-July-1997 ]============[ 1.02 -> 1.03 ]=========================-\n\n        - Screen Mode, Pens and Palette menu-options added.\n\n        - Time left moved to title bar in HH:MM:SS format\n\n        - Realname displayed in status bar (replaces time left)\n\n        - The "SX" button in the bottom-right corner does something.\n                (Try it when someone is online)\n\n        - Simple AREXX interface added to SX-MCP, see REXX/ dir or\n                SX.Guide for more information\n\n        - New Full Screen Editor available - SXEd 1.03!!\n                (Put "Doors:SXEd" into SX-Config->Doors->Message Editor\n                        and select the "XIM /X" type)\n\n        - File Attaching now possible (with SXEd only)\n\n        - "Disallow Attachments" CheckBOX added to SX-Config->\n                Conf/File/Msg->MessageBases.\n\n        - Entering a message to "ALL" or "SYSOP" works again! :)\n\n        - Full connect string logged (SX:Node%ld/CallersLog) for the\n                benefit of STopCPS.\n\n        - BGCheck Optimized\n\n        - Experimental FAME door support added.\n\n        - SX-MCP now has a Zoom gadget.\n\n        - Paragon door command 203 fixed (used to crash!)\n\n        - Some enforcer hits removed.\n\n        NOTE:        For AREXX doors, install rexxdoor (from AmiExpress)\n                into the DOORS: directory, *NOT* SX:Utils/ as previously\n                written in the docs.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "104" "Version 1.04"\n -=[ 27-September-1997 ]==========[ 1.03 -> 1.04 ]=======================-\n\n        - Online UserED Bug (Presets etc) fixed.\n\n        - Some new users would get marked as deleted - fixed\n\n        - Quoting Messages fixed\n\n        - You can now enter messages to "ALL" or "EALL" like /X\n\n        - It''s possible to run more than 1 filecheck door, see\n          "FileCheck Door - How?" in SX.Guide for more information.\n\n        - FullScreenEditor and BGCheck are now user configurable.\n          See function 99 and 100 or the "Bonus/" directory.\n\n        - SXEd (Message Editor) now allows international characters\n\n        - MoveFile door added (move between filedirs and/or confs)\n                (still alpha version, use at own risk)\n\n        - SX-MCP saves your away-flag and away-reason when you quit\n\n        - SX-MCP can shutdown all nodes when you click the close gadget\n\n        - SX-Config -> Main -> Inactivity Timeout now works. Set it\n          to a reasonable number, like 300. Set to zero to turn off.\n\n        - When viewing messages, the message header no-longer scrolls\n          away when the message is long.\n\n        - More: (C)ontinuous option now works\n\n        - Userlist no-longer shows deleted users\n\n        - "D <filename>" from menu works.\n\n        - FetchKey() DD-Door routine improved. Sick-Chat now works!\n\n        - ShowAnsi() routine is now a bit faster.\n\n        - SX now handles incomplete uploads and resuming much better.\n          It stores incomplete uploads away and asks the user if they\n          want to resume, next time they hit ''U''.\n\n        - Some door routines have been made more compatable with /X.\n          It''s now possible to run "JoinCnf 3.6 - EMPiRE" with SX!\n          (You must have a "J" command in your Internal-Map too!)\n\n        - If you double click on a node in SX-MCP, it will be launched.\n\n        - Ansi capture feature added (in the pulldown menus).\n\n        - Doesn''t allow uploads if space low.\n          (Check SX-Config -> Main -> Min Upload Space).\n\n        - You can change your (in SX:TXT/Strings.XXX)\n\n        [P]roceed, (D)isconnect after - (A)bort:\n\n                to:\n\n        [P]roceed, (E)dit Flags, (D)isconnect after, (C)hange Protocol - (A)bort:\n\n\n        Note:        If you have not fixed your STRINGS.XXX control codes yet,\n                refer to "Editing STRINGS.XXX" in SX.Guide or the BBS\n                may crash!!\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "104f" "1.04fixed"\n -=[ 03-October-1997 ]============[ 1.04 -> 1.04fix ]======================-\n\n        - It could sometimes lockup when opening screen - fixed\n\n        - SXEd had left/right arrows swapped - fixed\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "105" "1.05"\n -=[ XX-December-1997 ]==============[ 1.04 -> 1.05 ]======================-\n\n        - New auto inserts for stdio door execution:\n                        %t        timeleft (mins)\n                        %a        access level (security)\n\n        - MCI Code ~LF| now works (node number).\n\n        - When you give users a new access-preset, timeleft is changed too.\n          (Online UserED)\n\n        - MoveFile() routine fixed - faster and safer (used during upload).\n\n        - Local Uploading more than 1 file works again :)\n\n        - Delete button added to GUI-UserED\n\n        - New checkbox added to SX-Config->Conf/Msg/File->Edit Message Bases\n          "Ask Private". Will ask the user if they want the message to be\n          private. If ticked, this overrides "Private Area: " checkbox.\n\n        - Serial Device and DTE Speed can be left blank for local nodes\n          without crashing the node.\n\n        - ~NP| MCI code added - turns OFF "More? (y/n/c)" prompts.\n\n        - SX-Config -> "Local Display" touched up a bit.\n\n        - SX can(not) allow multiple logins (check SX-Config->"This Node")\n\n        - Local downloads now possible. Files copied to SysOp Download Path\n\n        - "R <number>" from menu is now possible.\n\n        - Upload.log loop bug seems to be fixed.\n\n        - It''s possible to run doors from within doors! eg: Run SXNUKE from\n          AquaScan just like on /X systems.\n\n        - BGCheck has been optimized and no longer requires c:move command.\n\n        - BB_CHATFLAG (142) XIM-Door command now works.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "1.06" "1.06"\n\n System-X 1.06 (eSSeXX)\n\n - change all version requests and strings to SX 1.06 (eSSeXX)\n - sx-config: nodeselection by a slider gadget now\n - sx-config: creating a new msgbase will create the related\n              Directory, too.\n - sx-config: change Mainconfig values for Min HD Space to KB\n              and the Timeout/Timeoutwarn to Minutes.              \n - sx-config: creating a new conference will create the needed Directo\n              and a Directory /Messages\n              creating a new MsgBase will create the needed Dirs, too.\n              (confpath/Messages/BaseX)\n              All that selectable with nice Reqtools requester, default\n              ok.\n - sx-config: creating a new Menu will create a default Command Prompt\n              too. You will be asked by a requester.\n - sx       : Inactivity Time Warning is ok now. Set the inactivity warn\n              minutes in sx-config, when the pre-alarm should run.\n - sx       : change SXFunction 15 (UserList) to more options:\n              Extranumber 0 : list handle, location, calls \n              Extranumber 1 : list relname, location, calls\n              Extranumber 2 : list handle, axx, location, calls, lasto\n              Extranumber 3 : list realname, axx, location, calls, las\n - sx-mcp   : doubleclick on the nodelist will bring up the nodescreen\n              to front now. This was only able, if the screen was already\n              open..\n - sx       : add SX:/TXT/OfflineHelp.ANS and bring the keys for\n              online and offline nodescreen up to date. \n - recompiled most additional utils and main`s for 020 and 000\n - began to pack the new updatearchives for 68000 and 68020, change\n   some ansi and some penouts.\n - writing the guide, day by day\n - sx-config: change some penouts, string output..\n - write an Installer for the BBS, includes some features, \n   i.e. create a StartBatch. \n - test installing, do preconfigs, ...\n@endnode\n\n@node "106b" "106b"\n\n System-X v1.06b (eSSeXX)\n\n - sx  : Commands given at LineInput() are stored in a table\n         now. Recall them with the up- and down arrowkeys like\n         in a shell.\n         passwords are removed from command recallbuffer \n\n - sx  : implement XIM-Function #517 JH_LOGONTYPE\n\n         msg->Data -1: no node avail\n                    0: awaiting call\n                    1: sysop login\n                    2: local login\n                    3: remote login\n     \n - sx  : change the JoinConference function a bit. Now join \n         first before Join.ans is typed/executed.\n\n - sx  : change Login credits to dIGITAL cORRUPTION\n\n - sx  : FileChecking: DupeFiles were not found. Fixed.\n\n - sx-config: fix a small gfx-bug\n@endnode\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',98982,5,0,NULL,NULL,'dc_x106b','scan',1780048460);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dc_x107i','DC-X107I.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DC-X107I.LHA','AmigaGuide','XIM','AmigaGuide',NULL,NULL,'DC','dC! |  _ \_  |/    |/  |_  _/ ._ |   | zS!sE _ |  /  /  /  |_ /   |/  |  |/ |   |_  _ \\ |____/   \___/ \___|   |__/  |_____| //',replace('     ________| ____  __|_________|___\ndC! |  _ \_  |/    |/  |_  _/ ._ |   | zS!sE\n  _ |  /  /  /  |_ /   |/  |  |/ |   |_  _\n \\ |____/   \___/ \___|   |__/  |_____| //\n|¯      \____| \___|  \____| \_____|      ¯|\n|   · C Ø R R U P T ¡ Ø N    ¹ 9 9 9 ! ·   |\n|                                          |\n|   S Y S T E M - X  v1.o7 (e S S e X X)   |\n|   Full Install Version of the SX 1.o7    |\n|_                                        _|\n //.04.OCT.99.____________________.DC`99.\\\n','\n',char(10)),'DC-X107i.readme',replace('Short:    System-X 1.07 (eSSeXX) Bulletin Board System - Full install archive\nUploader: [email removed]\nAuthor:   [r]FoX - Support: http://www.luebeck.netsurf.de/~clasen\nType:     comm/bbs\n\n  \n   System-X 1.07 (eSSeXX) Install archive \n   --------------------------------------\n\n   This archive contains the full install version of the \n   SX (eSSeXX) BBS software and all other needed files to run a\n   full AmiExpress styled Bulletin Board System.\n   \n   System-X is on the run and will be updated permanently !\n\n   ==================================================================\n\n   INSTALL NOTES\n\n   To install this software, use the supported Installer.\n\n   !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n   The installer does no versioncheck of any systemlibary`s so\n   plz check that up.\n   !!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n\n   Follow the instructions by the Installer. You have any time the\n   posibility, to abort the installation.\n   \n   If you like to install by hand, refer to the guide in the SX:Doc/\n   directory, chapter `Installation`.\n \n   Have a look at the guide and reset your computer.\n\n   Start the System-X BBS in your selected way and be a real \X op :)     \n  \n   ==================================================================\n\n   Developers Internal Changes\n	===========================\n\n	Note(s) on further developing:\n	------------------------------\n	* To check if a file exists, use the access() function, defined in stdio.h.\n  	This funtion basically does the same as: Lock() a file, check if lock!=0,\n  	and then UnLock() the file again.\n\n	v1.07 -> v1.08\n	==============\n\n	Changes, relevant for both users and delopers:\n	----------------------------------------------\n	* Added ~MN MCI-Command to display the current MessageBase number.\n	* JoinedBase.ANS is now displayed when a new MsgBase is joined\n\n	Changes, relevant for developers only:\n	--------------------------------------\n	* Bumped the version number\n	\n	Specified changes:\n	------------------\n	Source       Procedure/Function Change(s)\n	~~~~~~~~~~~~ ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n	ver.h        *                  - bumped version\n\n	showansi.c   MCIPS              - added ~MN command for current basenumber\n\n	msgs.c       GotoMsgArea        - added showansi("joinedbase")\n\n\n	v1.06 -> v1.07\n	==============\n\n	Changes, relevant for both users and delopers:\n	----------------------------------------------\n	* SX doesn''t go into an endless loop anymore if a door isn''t found.\n	* Wordwrapping added to chat!\n	* MCP now shows the correct activity when chat is finished.\n	* Added wildcard support to name-prompt (confirmation prompt is new string\n	  in Strings.ANS.\n	+ Change the Login-Wildcard procedure more direct\n	+ Update the Node-Screens ''About'' text\n	+ Update the crypted Welcome message\n	+ SX-Config changes up to 32 Nodes now\n	+ SX-MCP bumped version\n	+ Guides updated\n\n	Changes, relevant for developers only:\n	--------------------------------------\n	* Replaced all the version numbers into a macro, defined in ver.h\n	* The CallerLog() routine from prim.c is now in the log.c file.\n	* The LoadStrings() and FreeStrings() routines are now in configs.c\n	* Ver.c is renamed to Sysinfo.c, because the name confused me ;-)\n	+ SX-Config and SX-MCP got version-Macro, too\n	+ SX-Config can handle 32 nodes now again \n\n\n	Specified changes:\n	------------------\n	Source       Procedure/Function Change(s)\n	~~~~~~~~~~~~ ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n	sx.c         RunDoor            - checks if door parameter isn''t empty\n	                                - checks if specified door exists\n	                                  (both these things caused endless loops)\n             	 TestDoor           - replaced a bit of code\n	             main               - replaced version strings\n	             CheckWin           - replaced version string and ''About'' text\n	             Account            - added wildcard support for handle/name\n    	                             - comfirmation for name is now in Strings.ANS\n\n\n	door_xim.c   WaitForXIM         - added SX_MSGAREANUM command\n 	                                - replaced version string\n\n	showansi.c   MCIPS              - replaced version string\n	             *                  - removed LoadStrings() and FreeStrings()\n\n	chat&page.c  PageSysOp          - added some comments\n	             Chat               - rewrote the routine almost completely\n	                                - added wordwrapping\n	                                - MCP now displays correct activity after chat\n\n	prim.c       CallerLog          - removed this function from the source-code\n\n	log.c        *                  - added this file to the link-list\n\n	configs.c    *                  - added LoadStrings() and FreeStrings()\n\n\n	SX-Config\n	---------\n\n	sx-config.c	   *		- bumped version\n\n	sxconfig_gui.c	*		- changed the nodeslide value up to 32\n\n	mcpprefs.c	   *		- changed the visible nodelist slider up\n								  to 32 and check up the whole process\n\n\n  The development of System-X (eSSeXX) is going on !                 [r]FoX\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',887917,6,0,NULL,NULL,'ula_us10','scan',1780048460);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dc_xu101','DC-XU101.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DC-XU101.LHA','SX-Config','XIM','SX-Config',NULL,NULL,'DC','____¦____  (   _____/__  - ------------- _/     ___/ _/\_  T     ¬\_ ·  diGiTAL   · .-\     ¦/    7--7  l       / · cORRUPTiON ·',replace('        .________________\n    ____¦____  (   _____/__  - -------------\n  _/     ___/ _/\_  T     ¬\_ ·  diGiTAL   ·\n.-\     ¦/    7--7  l       / · cORRUPTiON ·\n|  \____.-----¦  ¦----.____/------- -  -   -\n|           SYSTEM-X 1.01 UPDATE\n|        BugFixes and new features.\n`-[15/06/97]---------------------------[Zed]\n','\n',char(10)),'Changes.GUIDE',replace('@database SXDoc\n@node MAIN "System-X BBS Software"\n                        -= System-X Changes =-\n\n                                @{" 1.01 " Link 101}\n\n@endnode\n@node 101 "Version 1.01"\n\n-=[ 20-June-1997 ]============[ 1.00 -> 1.01 ]=========================-\n\n	- TELNET callers no longer get a baud of 0\n\n	- Enforcer hits removed from SX and SX-Config (thanks Skittle)\n\n	- Deleting Messages now possible\n\n	- Quoting Messages now possible\n\n	- Better DayDream Support (WHO''s ONLINE doors work, SoulFront\n					and RealTimeWho tested!)\n\n	- SX-Config->Doors->FrontDoor feature now works (tested with\n					SoulFront)\n\n	- "C"onfig Button added to SX-MCP\n\n	- SX-Config->MCPPrefs Improved\n\n	- Delete/UnDelete now functional in online UserED\n\n	- If two new users logged in at once it would screw up - fixed\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',152462,4,0,NULL,NULL,'dc_xu101','scan',1780048460);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dc_xu102','DC-XU102.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DC-XU102.LHA','SX-Config','XIM','SX-Config',NULL,NULL,'DC','____¦____  (   _____/__  - ------------- _/     ___/ _/\_  T     ¬\_ ·  diGiTAL   · .-\     ¦/    7--7  l       / · cORRUPTiON ·',replace('        .________________\n    ____¦____  (   _____/__  - -------------\n  _/     ___/ _/\_  T     ¬\_ ·  diGiTAL   ·\n.-\     ¦/    7--7  l       / · cORRUPTiON ·\n|  \____.-----¦  ¦----.____/------- -  -   -\n|           SYSTEM-X 1.02 UPDATE\n|        BugFixes and new features.\n`-[25/06/97]---------------------------[Zed]\n','\n',char(10)),'Dev.GUIDE',replace('@database SXDEV\012@node MAIN "Developing Doors"\012\012		  DEVELOPING DOORS AND UTILS FOR SYSTEM-X\012\012		    @{" Structures associated with SX     " Link structs}\012		    @{" How the door port works in theory " Link port}\012		    @{" List of XIM functions available   " Link funcs}\012		    @{" Communication with MCP            " Link mcp}\012\012 .-----------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 | System-X uses the XIM door port as its primary door port. This means  |\012 | it''s compatable with AmiExpress. If you are intending to write a door |\012 | especially for System-X, use the XIM port, as it gives you the most   |\012 | power.                                                                |\012 `-----------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012 Note: if you find any developer/starter packs around for AmiExpress, they\012       will work just fine with System-X. There are examples for AmigaE\012       and heaps of ASM examples around. Developing doors for SX can also\012       be done using any of the other door types, but XIM is the best for\012       SX (has the most commands available).\012@endnode\012@node structs "Structures"\012\012The structures are all in ''C'' format, but in general:\012\012WORD, short		=	16 bit signed word\012UWORD			=	16 bit unsigned word\012int, long, LONG		=	32 bit signed word\012ULONG			=	32 bit unsigned word\012APTR			=	32 bit pointer\012\012Any fields with an asterix "*" infront of them are pointers!\012\012\012.---------------------------------------.\012| User.data or User structure in memory |\012`---------------------------------------''\012\012struct UserData {\012	char	Name[31],\012		Pass[9],\012		Location[30],\012		PhoneNumber[13];\012	USHORT	Slot_Number;\012	USHORT	Sec_Status,		/* access level */\012		Sec_Board,		/* unused	*/\012		Sec_Library,		/* unused       */\012		Sec_Bulletin,		/* unused	*/\012		Messages_Posted;\012	ULONG	NewSinceDate,\012		ConfRead1,\012		ConfRead2,\012		ConfRead3,\012		ConfRead4,\012		ConfRead5,\012		ConfRead6,\012		ConfRead7,\012		ConfRead8,\012		ConfRead9;\012	char	Conference_Access[10];\012	USHORT	Uploads,\012		Downloads,\012		ConfRJoin,\012		Times_Called;\012	long	Time_Last_On,\012		Time_Used,\012		Time_Limit,\012		Time_Left;\012	ULONG	Bytes_Download,\012		Bytes_Upload,\012		Daily_Bytes_Limit,\012		Daily_Bytes_Dld;\012	char	Expert;\012	ULONG	ConfYM1,\012		ConfYM2,\012		ConfYM3,\012		ConfYM4,\012		ConfYM5,\012		ConfYM6,\012		ConfYM7,\012		ConfYM8,\012		ConfYM9;\012	long    BeginLogCall;\012	UBYTE	Protocol,\012		UUCPA,\012		LineLength,\012		New_User;\012	};\012\012.---------------------------------------------.\012| User.Index or UserIndex structure in memory |\012`---------------------------------------------''\012\012struct UserIndexStruct\012{\012	char handle[31];\012	char realname[31];\012	UWORD misc;\012};\012\012\012.---------------------------.\012| User.SX file or in memory |\012`---------------------------''\012\012struct SXUserStruct\012{\012	UWORD byteratio;\012	UWORD fileratio;\012	ULONG flags;\012	UWORD freefiles;\012	ULONG freebytes;\012	ULONG ConfAccess[10];\012	UWORD lastfilearea;\012	char computer[24];\012	char sentbyline[46];\012	char password[16];\012	long firstcall;\012	char reserved[110];\012};\012\012\012.-----------------.\012| Prefs/Confs.DAT |\012`-----------------''\012\012struct ConfStruct\012{\012	char name[45];\012	char path[55];\012	char pass[16];\012	char filepath[52];\012	UWORD fileareas;\012	UWORD uploadarea;\012	UBYTE flf;\012	UBYTE flags;\012	char reserve[82];\012};\012\012\012.------------------.\012| Prefs/Serial.DAT |\012`------------------''\012\012struct SerialStruct\012{\012	char device[32];\012	WORD unit;\012	WORD misc;\012	long minrate;\012	long dcerate;\012	UBYTE sevenwire;\012	UBYTE shared;\012	char ring[16];\012	char connect[24];\012	char answer[16];\012	char initstr[48];\012};\012\012\012.-------------------.\012| SX:Prefs/Main.DAT |\012`-------------------''\012\012struct MainStruct\012{\012	char BBSName[64];\012	char BBSPath[64];\012	char BBSLoc[64];\012	char Sysop[64];\012	char DNPath[64];\012	char ULPath[64];\012	long nodes;\012};\012\012.---------------------------------------.\012| SX:LogFiles/Download.LOG & Upload.LOG |\012`---------------------------------------''\012\012struct XferLog\012{\012	UWORD	user_slot;\012	UBYTE	conf,\012		filearea;\012	char	filename[32];\012	long	size,\012		baud,\012		cps,\012		time;\012	UBYTE	node;\012	char	res[7];\012} Xfer;\012\012\012.-------------------------.\012| SX:LogFiles/Callers.LOG |\012`-------------------------''\012\012Note: this file has a UWORD at the top before the first structure, which\012is a pointer to the oldest entry in the log. (its a rotary log of 30)\012\012struct CallerLog\012{\012	UWORD	user_slot,\012		node;\012	long	time_login,\012		time_logout,\012		seconds_online,\012		bytes_uploaded,\012		bytes_downloaded;\012	UWORD	files_uploaded,\012		files_downloaded,\012		messages;\012	long	baud,\012		flags;\012	UBYTE	logout_mode;\012	char	res[25];\012};\012\012\012.----------------------------------------------------------------.\012| NODE STRUCTURE AS PASSED BY MCP-COMMAND-14 OR XIM-COMMAND-1505 |\012`----------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012struct node_struct\012{						/* offset DEC	*/\012	APTR next;				/*	0	*/\012	struct UserData *User;			/*	4	*/\012	struct UserIndexStruct *UserIndex;	/*	8	*/\012	struct SXUserStruct *SXUser;		/*	12	*/\012	char *action;				/*	16	*/\012	char *filename;				/*	20	*/\012	long baud;				/*	24	*/\012	long loginsecs;				/*	28	*/\012	UWORD number;				/*	32	*/\012	UBYTE actionnumber;			/*	34	*/\012	UBYTE active;				/*	35	*/\012	UBYTE useron;				/*	36	*/\012	UBYTE misc;				/*	37	*/\012};\012\012@endnode\012@node port "Door Port"\012\012There are two ways to program doors for System-X. One is to use\012AEDoor.library, which is very easy, and the other is to use exec\012messages, which gives more control. Below is explained the exec\012message style of programming doors.\012\012\012--- The message structure ---\012\012struct JHMessage\012{\012  struct Message Msg;   <----- msg structure\012  char String[200];     <----- info buffer\012  int Data;             <----- Read/Write & result indicator\012  int Command;          <----- Command sent from door.\012  int NODEID;           <----- reserved\012  int LineNum;          <----- reserved\012  unsigned long signal; <----- reserved\012  struct Process *task;\012  APTR *Semi;\012};\012\012\012The port name is AEDoorPort%d , where %d is the node number. General\012in ''C'' you''d do:\012\012--------------------------------------------------\012\012char portname[32];\012struct MsgPort *port;\012\012sprintf(portname, "AEDoorPort%d", atoi(argv[1]));\012port = FindPort(portname);\012\012--------------------------------------------------\012\012See the examples/ directory for more information.\012\012@endnode\012@node funcs "System-X XIM Functions"\012\012  The following list is a list of all System-X HOST Commands which\012  can be used in every program language to get/store information to the\012  AmiExpress Host Port. With this Command you can get Information\012  like BBSNAME, USERNAME etc. Click on the Buttons for more Information.\012\012    @{" JH_LI            <Func: 000> " Link Cap1101000}    @{" JH_REGISTER      <Func: 001> " Link Cap1101001}\012    @{" JH_SHUTDOWN      <Func: 002> " Link Cap1101002}    @{" JH_WRITE         <Func: 003> " Link Cap1101003}\012    @{" JH_SM            <Func: 004> " Link Cap1101004}    @{" JH_PM            <Func: 005> " Link Cap1101005}\012    @{" JH_HK            <Func: 006> " Link Cap1101006}    @{" JH_SG            <Func: 007> " Link Cap1101007}\012    @{" JH_SF            <Func: 008> " Link Cap1101008}    @{" JH_EF            <Func: 009> " Link Cap1101009}\012    @{" JH_CO            <Func: 010> " Link Cap1101010}    @{" JH_BBSNAME       <Func: 011> " Link Cap1101011}\012    @{" JH_SYSOP         <Func: 012> " Link Cap1101012}    @{" JH_FLAGFILE      <Func: 013> " Link Cap1101013}\012    @{" DT_NAME          <Func: 100> " Link Cap1101100}    @{" DT_PASSWORD      <Func: 101> " Link Cap1101101}\012    @{" DT_LOCATION      <Func: 102> " Link Cap1101102}    @{" DT_PHONENUMBER   <Func: 103> " Link Cap1101103}\012    @{" DT_SLOTNUMBER    <Func: 104> " Link Cap1101104}    @{" DT_ACCESSLEVEL   <Func: 105> " Link Cap1101105}\012    @{" DT_RATIOTYPE     <Func: 106> " Link Cap1101106}    @{" DT_RATIO         <Func: 107> " Link Cap1101107}\012    @{" DT_COMPTYPE      <Func: 108> " Link Cap1101108}    @{" DT_MESSAGESPOSTED<Func: 109> " Link Cap1101109}\012    @{" DT_UPLOADS       <Func: 110> " Link Cap1101110}    @{" DT_DOWNLOADS     <Func: 111> " Link Cap1101111}\012    @{" DT_TIMESCALLED   <Func: 112> " Link Cap1101112}    @{" DT_TIMELASTON    <Func: 113> " Link Cap1101109}\012    @{" DT_TIMEUSED      <Func: 114> " Link Cap1101114}    @{" DT_TIMELIMIT     <Func: 115> " Link Cap1101115}\012    @{" DT_TIMETOTAL     <Func: 116> " Link Cap1101116}    @{" DT_BYTESUPLOAD   <Func: 117> " Link Cap1101117}\012    @{" DT_BYTEDOWNLOAD  <Func: 118> " Link Cap1101118}    @{" DT_DAILYBYTELIMIT<Func: 119> " Link Cap1101119}\012    @{" DT_DAILYBYTEDLD  <Func: 120> " Link Cap1101120}    @{" DT_EXPERT        <Func: 121> " Link Cap1101121}\012    @{" DT_LINELENGTH    <Func: 122> " Link Cap1101122}    @{" ACTIVE_NODES     <Func: 123> " Link Cap1101123}\012    @{" DT_DUMP          <Func: 124> " Link Cap1101124}    @{" DT_TIMEOUT       <Func: 125> " Link Cap1101125}\012    @{" BB_CONFNAME      <Func: 126> " Link Cap1101126}    @{" BB_CONFLOCAL     <Func: 127> " Link Cap1101127}\012    @{" BB_LOCAL         <Func: 128> " Link Cap1101128}    @{" BB_STATUS        <Func: 129> " Link Cap1101129}\012    @{" BB_MAINLINE      <Func: 131> " Link Cap1101131}    @{" RETURNCOMMAND    <Func: 136> " Link Cap1101136}\012    @{" ZMODEMSEND       <Func: 137> " Link Cap1101137}    @{" ZMODEMRECEIVE    <Func: 138> " Link Cap1101138}\012    @{" SCREEN_ADDRESS   <Func: 139> " Link Cap1101139}    @{" BB_TASKPRI       <Func: 140> " Link Cap1101140}\012    @{" RAWSCREEN_ADDRESS<Func: 141> " Link Cap1101141}    @{" BB_CHATFLAG      <Func: 142> " Link Cap1101142}\012    @{" DT_STAMP_LASTON  <Func: 143> " Link Cap1101143}    @{" DT_STAMP_CTIME   <Func: 144> " Link Cap1101144}\012    @{" DT_CURR_TIME     <Func: 145> " Link Cap1101145}    @{" DT_CONFACCESS    <Func: 146> " Link Cap1101146}\012    @{" BB_NODEID        <Func: 149> " Link Cap1101149}    @{" BB_CALLERSLOG    <Func: 150> " Link Cap1101150}\012    @{" BB_UDLOG         <Func: 151> " Link Cap1101151}    @{" EXPRESS_VERSION  <Func: 152> " Link Cap1101152}\012    @{" BB_CHATSET       <Func: 162> " Link Cap1101162}    @{" ENVSTAT          <Func: 163> " Link Cap1101163}\012    @{" NODE_DEVICE      <Func: 503> " Link Cap1101503}    @{" NODE_UNIT        <Func: 504> " Link Cap1101504}\012    @{" NODE_BAUD        <Func: 505> " Link Cap1101505}    @{" JH_MCI           <Func: 507> " Link Cap1101507}\012    @{" PRV_COMMAND      <Func: 508> " Link Cap1101508}    @{" BB_CONFNUM       <Func: 510> " Link Cap1101510}\012    @{" BB_DROPDTR       <Func: 511> " Link Cap1101511}    @{" BB_GETTASK       <Func: 512> " Link Cap1101512}\012    @{" NODE_BAUDRATE    <Func: 516> " Link Cap1101516}    @{" BB_LOGONTYPE     <Func: 517> " Link Cap1101517}\012    @{" BB_SCRLEFT       <Func: 518> " Link Cap1101518}    @{" BB_SCRTOP        <Func: 519> " Link Cap1101519}\012    @{" BB_SCRWIDTH      <Func: 520> " Link Cap1101520}    @{" BB_SCRHEIGHT     <Func: 521> " Link Cap1101521}\012    @{" BB_PURGELIN      <Func: 522> " Link Cap1101522}    @{" BB_PURGELINESTART<Func: 523> " Link Cap1101523}\012    @{" BB_PURGELINEEND  <Func: 524> " Link Cap1101524}    @{" BB_NONSTOPTEXT   <Func: 525> " Link Cap1101525}\012    @{" BB_LINECOUNT     <Func: 526> " Link Cap1101526}    @{" DT_LANGUAGE      <Func: 527> " Link Cap1101527}\012    @{" DT_QUICKFLAG     <Func: 528> " Link Cap1101528}    @{" DT_GOODFILE      <Func: 529> " Link Cap1101529}\012\012    Below are functions that are System-X specific and DO NOT work under\012                     AmiExpress or any AmiExpress clones.\012\012    @{" SX_PS           <Func: 1500> " Link SX_PS}    @{" SX_USERPO       <Func: 1501> " Link SX_USERPO}\012    @{" SX_USERPO2      <Func: 1502> " Link SX_USERPO2}    @{" SX_USERPO3      <Func: 1503> " Link SX_USERPO3}\012    @{" SX_VER          <Func: 1504> " Link SX_VER}    @{" SX_NODES        <Func: 1505> " Link SX_NODES}\012    @{" SX_FUNCTION     <Func: 1506> " Link SX_FUNCTION}    @{" SX_CONF        <Func: 1508> " Link SX_CONF}\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101000 "JH_LI             <Func: 000>"\012\012JH_LI          Requests a string of information from the user with a\012               default string.\012\012               msg->Command = 0\012               msg->String  = default result string\012               msg->Data    = Maximum length of response.\012\012               msg->Data will be set to a -1 if a loss carrier or console\012               TIMEOUT occurs, otherwise MSG->Data will be 1\012\012               msg->String will be the response string from the user.\012(FUNCTION #: 0 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101001 "JH_REGISTER       <Func: 001>"\012\012JH_REGISTER    Registers a door or XIM with the current node.\012\012               msg->Command = 1\012\012               This must be the first command issued to the express node.\012               This increments the number of doors active for the current\012               node.\012(FUNCTION #: 1 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101002 "JH_SHUTDOWN       <Func: 002>"\012\012JH_SHUTDOWN   Tells the node that a door is shutting down, this decreases\012              the number of active doors indicator , which once at 0,\012              the AEDoorPort will close.\012\012              msg->Command = 2\012              msg->Data    = N/A\012(FUNCTION #: 2 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101003 "JH_WRITE          <Func: 003>"\012\012JH_WRITE        Allows you to send a text string to the user.\012\012                msg->Command = 3\012                msg->String  = text\012                msg->Data    = N/A\012(FUNCTION #: 3 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101004 "JH_SM             <Func: 004>"\012\012JH_SM           Allows you to send a text string to the user.\012\012                msg->Command = 4\012                msg->String  = text\012                msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012                if msg->Data = 1, then a CR/LF combination will be sent.\012(FUNCTION #: 4 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101005 "JH_PM             <Func: 005>"\012\012JH_PM           Allows you to prompt the user for a specified number of\012                characters.\012\012                msg->Command = 5\012                msg->String  = prompt string\012                msg->Data    = maximum response length.\012\012                if msg->Data = -1, then a loss carrier has occurred or a\012                TIMEOUT condition has occurred, otherwise msg->Data = 1.\012\012                msg->String will be the user response.\012(FUNCTION #: 5 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101006 "JH_HK              <Func: 006>"\012\012JH_HK           Allows you to get a 1 character response from the user.\012\012                msg->Command = 6\012                msg->String  = text\012                msg->Data    = N/A\012\012                if msg->Data = -1, then a loss carrier has occurred or a\012                TIMEOUT condition has occurred, otherwise msg->Data = 1.\012\012                msg->String will be the result string.\012(FUNCTION #: 6 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101007 "JH_SG             <Func: 007>"\012\012JH_SG           Allows you to display a text file to the user.\012\012                msg->Command = 7\012                msg->String  = part file name.\012                msg->Data    = N/A\012\012                ie:\012\012                msg->String = "BBS:Node1/Bull\012\012                This would try to display BBS:Node1/BULL.TXT\012                also takes into account language specifications.\012\012                This also searches for the access level patterns, ie:\012\012                Bull10.TXT, Bull100.TXT\012(FUNCTION #: 7 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101008 "JH_SF             <Func: 008>"\012\012JH_SF           Allows you to display a text file to the user.\012\012                msg->Command = 8\012                msg->String  = Complete pathname\012                msg->Data    = N/A\012\012                ie:\012\012                msg->String  = "BBS:Node1/BULL.TXT"\012\012                This would show the file if it exists.\012(FUNCTION #: 8 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101009 "JH_EF             <Func: 009>"\012\012JH_EF          Allows you to use the internal msgbase editor to edit your\012               own files.\012\012               msg->Command = 9\012               msg->String  = Complete pathname\012               msg->Data    = 0\012\012               if msg->Data = -1, then a loss carrier has occurred or a\012               TIMEOUT has occurred, otherwise msg->Data will be 1.\012(FUNCTION #: 9 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101010 "JH_CO             <Func: 010>"\012\012JH_CO          Allows you to send text string to the console only.\012\012               msg->Command = 10\012               msg->String  = text\012               msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012               if msg->Data = 1, then a CR/LF combination will be sent in\012               addition to the text.\012(FUNCTION #: 10 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101011 "JH_BBSNAME        <Func: 011>"\012\012JH_BBSNAME      Allows you to retrieve the BBS Name.\012\012                msg->Command = 11\012                msg->Data    = N/A\012\012                msg->String will be the BBS name.\012(FUNCTION #: 11 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101012 "JH_SYSOP          <Func: 012>"\012\012JH_SYSOP        Allows you to retrieve the Sysop''s Name.\012\012                msg->Command = 12\012                msg->Data    = N/A\012\012                msg->String will be the Sysop name.\012(FUNCTION #: 12 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101013 "JH_FLAGFILE       <Func: 013>"\012\012JH_FLAGFILE     Allows you to add files to the list of flagged files.\012\012                msg->Command = 13\012                msg->String  = FileName\012                msg->Data    = N/A\012\012                Adds the msg->String to the list of flagged files for\012                downloading purposes,\012\012                NOTE: The files must be in the download path for this to\012                      work.\012(FUNCTION #: 13 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101100 "DT_NAME           <Func: 100>"\012\012DT_NAME         Allows you to retrieve or change users name/handle\012\012                msg->Command = 100\012                msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012                if msg->Data = 1, then msg->String will be the name.\012                if msg->Data = 0, then name will be msg->String\012(FUNCTION #: 100 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101101 "DT_PASSWORD       <Func: 101>"\012\012DT_PASSWORD     Allows you to retrieve or change users password\012\012                msg->Command = 101\012                msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012                if msg->Data = 1, then msg->String will be the password.\012                if msg->Data = 0, then the password will be msg->String.\012(FUNCTION #: 101 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101102 "DT_LOCATION      <Func: 102>"\012\012DT_LOCATION     Allows you to retrieve or change users location\012\012                msg->Command = 102\012                msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012                if msg->Data = 1, then msg->String will be the location\012                if msg->Data = 0, then the location will be msg->String\012(FUNCTION #: 102 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101103 "DT_PHONENUMBER    <Func: 103>"\012\012DT_PHONENUMBER  Allows you to retrieve or change users phone number.\012\012               msg->Command = 103\012               msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012               if msg->Data = 1, then msg->String will be the phonenumber\012               if msg->Data = 0, ten phonenumber will be msg->String\012(FUNCTION #: 103 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101104 "DT_SLOTNUMBER     <Func: 104>"\012\012DT_SLOTNUMBER  Allows you to retrieve users slot number\012\012               msg->Command = 104\012               msg->Data    = 1\012\012               if msg->Data = 1, then msg->String will be the SLOTNUMBER.\012(FUNCTION #: 104 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101105 "DT_ACCESSLEVEL    <Func: 105>"\012\012DT_ACCESSLEVEL  Allows you to retrieve or change users access level.\012\012                msg->Command = 105\012                msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012                if msg->Data = 1, then msg->String will be ACCESSLEVEL.\012                if msg->Data = 0, then ACCESSLEVEL will be msg->String.\012(FUNCTION #: 105 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101106 "DT_RATIOTYPE      <Func: 106>"\012\012DT_RATIOTYPE    Allows you to retrieve or change users RatioType\012\012                msg->Command = 106\012                msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012                if msg->Data = 1, then msg->String will be RatioType.\012                if msg->Data = 0, then RatioType will be msg->String.\012(FUNCTION #: 106 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101107 "DT_RATIO          <Func: 107>"\012\012DT_RATIO        Allows you to retrieve or change users ratio\012\012                msg->Command = 107\012                msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012                if msg->Data = 1, then msg->String will be ratio.\012                if msg->Data = 0, then ratio will be msg->String.\012(FUNCTION #: 107 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101108 "DT_COMPTYPE       <Func: 108>"\012\012DT_COMPTYPE     Allows you to retrieve or change users ComputerTypes code\012\012                msg->Command = 108\012                msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012                if msg->Data = 1, then msg->String will be ComputerTypes.\012                if msg->Data = 0, then ComputerTypes will be msg->String.\012(FUNCTION #: 108 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101109 "DT_MESSAGESPOSTED <Func: 109>"\012\012DT_MESSAGESPOSTED Allows you to retrieve or change users MESSAGESPOSTED\012\012               msg->Command = 109\012               msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012               if msg->Data = 1, then msg->String will be MESSAGESPOSTED.\012               if msg->Data = 0, then MESSAGESPOSTED will be msg->String.\012(FUNCTION #: 109 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101110 "DT_UPLOADS        <Func: 110>"\012\012DT_UPLOADS      Allows you to retrieve or change number of UserUploads.\012\012                msg->Command = 110\012                msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012                if msg->Data = 1, then msg->String will be uploads.\012                if msg->Data = 0, then uploads will be msg->String.\012(FUNCTION #: 110 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101111 "DT_DOWNLOADS      <Func: 111>"\012\012DT_DOWNLOADS   Allows you to retrieve or change number of UserDownloads.\012\012                msg->Command = 111\012                msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012                if msg->Data = 1, then msg->String will be downloads.\012                if msg->Data = 0, then downloads will be msg->String.\012(FUNCTION #: 111 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101112 "DT_TIMESCALLED    <Func: 112>"\012\012DT_TIMESCALLED  Allows you to retrieve or change number of UserCalls.\012\012                msg->Command = 112\012                msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012                if msg->Data = 1, then msg->String will be TIMESCALLED.\012                if msg->Data = 0, then TIMESCALLED will be msg->String.\012(FUNCTION #: 112 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101113 "DT_TIMELASTON     <Func: 113>"\012\012DT_TIMELASTON   Allows you to retrieve or change time user last called.\012\012                msg->Command = 113\012                msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012                if msg->Data = 1, then msg->String will be TIMESCALLED.\012                if msg->Data = 0, then TIMESCALLED will be msg->String.\012\012                NOTE: This is not a date stamp, this is the number of\012                      seconds since January 19something.\012(FUNCTION #: 113 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101114 "DT_TIMEUSED       <Func: 114>"\012\012DT_TIMEUSED     Allows you to retrieve or change TIMEUSED today.\012\012                msg->Command = 114\012                msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012                if msg->Data = 1, then msg->String will be TIMEUSED.\012                if msg->Data = 0, then TIMEUSED will be msg->String.\012\012                NOTE: This is in seconds.\012(FUNCTION #: 114 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101115 "DT_TIMELIMIT      <Func: 115>"\012\012DT_TIMELIMIT    Allows you to retrieve or change TimeAllowed for a user.\012\012                msg->Command = 115\012                msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012                if msg->Data = 1, then msg->String will be TIMELIMIT.\012                if msg->Data = 0, then TIMELIMIT will be msg->String.\012\012                NOTE: Time in seconds.\012(FUNCTION #: 115 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101116 "DT_TIMETOTAL      <Func: 116>"\012\012DT_TIMETOTAL   Allows you to retrieve or change total time remaining.\012               for a user today.\012\012               msg->Command = 116\012               msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012               if msg->Data = 1, then msg->String will be time remaining.\012               if msg->Data = 0, then time remaining will be msg->String.\012\012               NOTE: Time in seconds.\012(FUNCTION #: 116 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101117 "DT_BYTESUPLOAD    <Func: 117>"\012\012DT_BYTESUPLOAD  Allows you to retrieve or change bytes uploads per user.\012\012                msg->Command = 117\012                msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012                if msg->Data = 1, then msg->String will be BYTESUPLOADED.\012                if msg->Data = 0, then BYTESUPLOADED will be msg->String.\012(FUNCTION #: 117 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101118 "DT_BYTEDOWNLOAD   <Func: 118>"\012\012DT_BYTEDOWNLOAD Allows you to retrieve or change bytes downloaded per\012                user.\012\012               msg->Command = 118\012               msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012               if msg->Data = 1, then msg->String will be BYTESDOWNLOADED.\012               if msg->Data = 0, then BYTESDOWNLOADED will be msg->String.\012(FUNCTION #: 118 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101119 "DT_DAILYBYTELIMIT <Func: 119>"\012\012DT_DAILYBYTELIMIT Allows you to retrieve or change a users daily byte\012                  download limit.\012\012                  msg->Command = 119\012                  msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012                  if msg->Data = 1, then msg->String will be bytelimit.\012                  if msg->Data = 0, then bytelimit will be msg->String.\012(FUNCTION #: 119 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101120 "DT_DAILYBYTEDLD   <Func: 120>"\012\012DT_DAILYBYTEDLD Allows you to retrieve or change daily bytes downloaded.\012\012                msg->Command = 120\012                msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012                if msg->Data = 1, then msg->String will be dailybytes.\012                if msg->Data = 0, then dailybytes will be msg->String.\012(FUNCTION #: 120 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101121 "DT_EXPERT         <Func: 121>"\012\012DT_EXPERT         Allows you to retrieve or change expert mode.\012\012                  msg->Command = 121\012                  msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012(FUNCTION #: 121 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101122 "DT_LINELENGTH     <Func: 122>"\012\012DT_LINELENGTH     Allows you to retrieve or change user LINELENGTH specs.\012\012                  msg->Command = 122\012                  msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012                  if msg->Data = 1, then msg->String will be LINELENGTH.\012                  if msg->Data = 0, then LINELENGTH will be msg->String.\012(FUNCTION #: 122 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101123 "ACTIVE_NODES      <Func: 123>"\012\012ACTIVE_NODES    Allows you to retrieve a string of active&inactive nodes.\012\012                msg->Command = 123\012                msg->Data    = N/A\012\012                msg->String will be a string 10 bytes in length, with\012                     ''X''s marking the active nodes.\012\012                NOTE: This command will surely be changing, the current\012                      limit is 9 nodes.\012(FUNCTION #: 123 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101124 "DT_DUMP           <Func: 124>"\012\012DT_DUMP           Allows you to dump the user''s data structure to a\012                  specified file.\012\012                  msg->Command = 124\012                  msg->String  = FileName\012(FUNCTION #: 124 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101125 "DT_TIMEOUT        <Func: 125>"\012\012DT_TIMEOUT       Allows you to retrieve or change the door TIMEOUT limit.\012\012                 msg->Command = 125\012                 msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012                 if msg->Data = 1, then msg->String will equal TIMEOUT.\012                 if msg->Data = 0, then TIMEOUT will equal msg->String.\012\012                 NOTE: This time is in seconds.\012(FUNCTION #: 125 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101126 "BB_CONFNAME       <Func: 126>"\012\012BB_CONFNAME       Allows you to retrieve or change the conference name.\012\012                  msg->Command = 126\012                  msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012                  if msg->Data = 1, then msg->String will be name.\012                  if msg->Data = 0, then name will be msg->String.\012(FUNCTION #: 126 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101127 "BB_CONFLOCAL      <Func: 127>"\012\012BB_CONFLOCAL    Allows you to retrieve or change the conference location.\012\012                msg->Command = 127\012                msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012                if msg->Data = 1, then msg->String will be location.\012                if msg->Data = 0, then location will be msg->String.\012(FUNCTION #: 127 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101128 "BB_LOCAL          <Func: 128>"\012\012BB_LOCAL          Allows you to retrieve the current BBS location.\012\012                  msg->Command = 128\012                  msg->Data    = N/A\012(FUNCTION #: 128 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101129 "BB_STATUS         <Func: 129>"\012\012BB_STATUS         Allows you to retrieve the current status of the node.\012\012                  msg->Command = 129\012                  msg->Data    = N/A\012\012                  msg->String will be ''OFFLINE'' or ''ONLINE'' depending on\012                  whether a user is logged onto the node.\012(FUNCTION #: 129 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101131 "BB_MAINLINE       <Func: 131>"\012\012BB_MAINLINE     Allows you to retrieve the menu prompt arguments prior to\012                the door being entered.\012\012                msg->Command = 131\012                msg->Data    = N/A\012\012                msg->String will be the menu prompt arguments.\012(FUNCTION #: 131 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101136 "RETURNCOMMAND     <Func: 136>"\012\012RETURNCOMMAND    Allows you to specify an internal command to be executed\012                 when the door is finished.\012\012                 msg->Command = 136\012                 msg->Data    = N/A\012\012                 command to be executed will be msg->String.\012(FUNCTION #: 136 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101137 "ZMODEMSEND        <Func: 137>"\012\012ZMODEMSEND      Allows you to send files to the user via Zmodem protocol.\012\012                msg->Command = 137\012                msg->String  = filename (complete pathname)\012                msg->Data    = N/A\012\012                result of transfer will be in msg->Data, where\012\012                if msg->Data = 1 , then transfer successful.\012                if msg->Data = -2, then user lost carrier.\012                if msg->Data = 0 , then transfer unsuccessful.\012(FUNCTION #: 137 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101138 "ZMODEMRECEIVE     <Func: 138>"\012\012ZMODEMRECEIVE    Allows you to receive batch uploads via Zmodem protocol.\012\012                 msg->Command = 138\012                 msg->String  = receive directory path\012                 msg->Data    = N/A\012\012                 result of transfer will be in msg->Data, where\012\012                 if msg->Data = 1 , then transfer successful.\012                 if msg->Data = -2, then user lost carrier.\012                 if msg->Data = 0,  then transfer unsuccessful.\012(FUNCTION #: 138 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101139 "SCREEN_ADDRESS    <Func: 139>"\012\012SCREEN_ADDRESS    Allows you to retrieve the screen address.\012\012                  msg->Command = 139\012                  msg->Data    = N/A\012\012                  msg->String will be a string containing the hexadecimal\012                  address of the Node screen.\012(FUNCTION #: 139 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101140 "BB_TASKPRI        <Func: 140>"\012\012BB_TASKPRI    Allows you to retrieve the priority the node is running at.\012\012              msg->Command = 140\012              msg->Data    = N/A\012\012              msg->String will contain the priority of the node.\012(FUNCTION #: 140 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101141 "RAWSCREEN_ADDRESS <Func: 141>"\012\012RAWSCREEN_ADDRESS Allows you to retrieve the screen address of the node.\012\012              msg->Command = 141\012              msg->Data    = N/A\012\012              msg->String will be a string containing the decimal address\012                   of the express node.\012(FUNCTION #: 141 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101142 "BB_CHATFLAG       <Func: 142>"\012\012BB_CHATFLAG       Allows you to retrieve the current chat setting.\012\012                  msg->Command = 142\012                  msg->Data    = N/A\012\012                  msg->String will be "ON" or "OFF".\012(FUNCTION #: 142 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101143 "DT_STAMP_LASTON   <Func: 143>"\012\012DT_STAMP_LASTON Allows you to retrieve a date string containing the date\012                of when the user last logged on.\012\012                msg->Command = 143\012                msg->Data    = N/A\012\012                msg->String will be the date string.\012(FUNCTION #: 143 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101144 "DT_STAMP_CTIME    <Func: 144>"\012\012DT_STAMP_CTIME    Allows you to retrieve a current time string.\012\012                  msg->Command = 144\012                  msg->Data    = N/A\012\012                  msg->String will be a current time string.\012(FUNCTION #: 144 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101145 "DT_CURR_TIME      <Func: 145>"\012\012DT_CURR_TIME     Allows you to retrieve the current time in seconds since\012                 January something.\012\012                 msg->Command = 145\012                 msg->Data    = N/A\012\012                 msg->String will be the current time.\012(FUNCTION #: 145 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101146 "DT_CONFACCESS     <Func: 146>"\012\012DT_CONFACCESS     Allows you to retrieve the users conference access.\012\012                  msg->Command = 146\012                  msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012                  if msg->Data = 1, then msg->String will be AREANAME.\012                  if msg->Data = 0, then AREANAME will be msg->String.\012\012(FUNCTION #: 146 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101149 "BB_NODEID         <Func: 149>"\012\012BB_NODEID         Allows you to retrieve the Node number for the current\012                  node\012\012                  msg->Command = 149\012                  msg->Data    = N/A\012\012                  msg->String will be the node number.\012(FUNCTION #: 149 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101150 "BB_CALLERSLOG     <Func: 150>"\012\012BB_CALLERSLOG     Allows you to add a line of text to the CALLERSLOG.\012\012                  msg->Command = 150\012                  msg->String  = text\012                  msg->Data    = N/A\012(FUNCTION #: 150 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101151 "BB_UDLOG          <Func: 151>"\012\012BB_UDLOG          Allows you to add a line of text to the UDLOG.\012\012                  msg->Command = 151\012                  msg->String  = text\012                  msg->Data    = N/A\012(FUNCTION #: 151 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101152 "EXPRESS_VERSION   <Func: 152>"\012\012EXPRESS_VERSION   Allows you to retrieve the current version string of\012                  express.\012\012                  msg->Command = 152\012                  msg->Data    = N/A\012(FUNCTION #: 152 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101162 "BB_CHATSET        <Func: 162>"\012\012BB_CHATSET     Allows you to retrieve or change the chat status.\012\012               msg->Command = 162\012               msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012               if msg->Data = 1, then msg->String will be current status.\012               if msg->Data = 0, then status will be msg->String.\012(FUNCTION #: 162 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101163 "ENVSTAT           <Func: 163>"\012\012ENVSTAT          Allows you to retrieve or change the current environment\012                 stat variable code.\012\012                 msg->Command = 163\012                 msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012                 if msg->Data = 1, then msg->String will be status.\012                 if msg->Data = 0, then status will be msg->String.\012(FUNCTION #: 163 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101503 "NODE_DEVICE       <Func: 503>"\012\012NODE_DEVICE       Allows you to retrieve the node device name.\012\012                  msg->Command = 503\012                  msg->Data    = N/A\012\012                  msg->String will be the device string.\012(FUNCTION #: 503 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101504 "NODE_UNIT         <Func: 504>"\012\012NODE_UNIT         Allows you to retrieve the node unit number.\012\012                  msg->Command = 504\012                  msg->Data    = N/A\012\012                  msg->String will be the current node number.\012(FUNCTION #: 504 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101505 "NODE_BAUD         <Func: 505>"\012\012NODE_BAUD    Allows you to retrieve the initialized baud rate of the node.\012\012             msg->Command = 505\012             msg->Data    = N/A\012\012             msg->String will be the INIT baud rate.\012(FUNCTION #: 505 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101507 "JH_MCI            <Func: 507>"\012\012JH_MCI            Allows you to send MCI text to express.\012\012                  msg->Command = 507\012                  msg->String  = text\012                  msg->Data    = N/A\012(FUNCTION #: 507 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101508 "PRV_COMMAND       <Func: 508>"\012\012PRV_COMMAND       Allows you to immediately execute an internal express\012                  menu command.\012\012                  msg->Command = 508\012                  msg->String  = commandstring\012                  msg->Data    = N/A\012(FUNCTION #: 508 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101510 "BB_CONFNUM        <Func: 510>"\012\012BB_CONFNUM     Allows you to retrieve the current conference number.\012\012               msg->Command = 510\012               msg->Data    = N/A\012\012               msg->String will be conference number ranging from 0 to 8.\012(FUNCTION #: 510 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101511 "BB_DROPDTR        <Func: 511>"\012\012BB_DROPDTR        Allows you to drop carrier on a user.\012\012                  msg->Command = 511\012                  msg->Data    = N/A\012(FUNCTION #: 511 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101512 "BB_GETTASK        <Func: 512>"\012\012BB_GETTASK        Finds the current nodes task address.\012\012                  msg->Command = 512\012                  msg->Data    = N/A\012\012                  msg->task will be the express task address.\012(FUNCTION #: 512 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101516 "NODE_BAUDRATE     <Func: 516>"\012\012NODE_BAUDRATE     Allows you to retrieve the current users connect rate\012\012                  msg->Command = 516\012                  msg->Data    = N/A\012\012                  msg->String will be the connect rate\012(FUNCTION #: 516 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101517 "BB_LOGONTYPE      <Func: 517>"\012\012BB_LOGONTYPE      Allows you to retrieve the LOGONTYPE.\012\012                  msg->Command = 517\012                  msg->Data    = N/A\012\012                  msg->Data will be:\012\012                  0 = AWAIT_LOGON\012                  1 = SYSOP_LOGON\012                  2 = LOCAL_LOGON\012                  3 = REMOTE_LOGON\012(FUNCTION #: 517 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101518 "BB_SCRLEFT        <Func: 518>"\012\012BB_SCRLEFT      Allows you to retrieve the screen coordinates.\012\012                msg->Command = 518\012                msg->Data    = N/A\012\012                msg->Data will be the Node''s Initial LEFTEDGE coordinate.\012(FUNCTION #: 518 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101519 "BB_SCRTOP         <Func: 519>"\012\012BB_SCRTOP        Allows you to retrieve the screen coordinates.\012\012                 msg->Command = 519\012                 msg->Data    = N/A\012\012                 msg->Data will be the Node''s Initial TOPEDGE coordinate.\012(FUNCTION #: 519 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101520 "BB_SCRWIDTH       <Func: 520>"\012\012BB_SCRWIDTH       Allows you to retrieve the screen coordinates.\012\012                  msg->Command = 520\012                  msg->Data    = N/A\012\012                  msg->Data will be the Node''s Initial screen height.\012(FUNCTION #: 520 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101521 "BB_SCRHEIGHT      <Func: 521>"\012\012BB_SCRHEIGHT      Allows you to retrieve the screen coordinates.\012\012                  msg->Command = 521\012                  msg->Data    = N/A\012\012                  msg->Data will be the Node''s Initial screen width.\012(FUNCTION #: 521 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101522 "BB_PURGELIN       <Func: 522>"\012\012BB_PURGELIN   Allows you to abort serial input.\012\012               msg->Command = 522\012               msg->Data    = N/A\012\012              aborts serial input and flushes the serial buffer and sends\012              a request for more input.\012(FUNCTION #: 522 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101523 "BB_PURGELINESTART <Func: 523>"\012\012BB_PURGELINESTART Allows you to CLEAR the serial buffer and request more\012                  serial input.\012\012                  msg->Command = 523\012                  msg->Data    = N/A\012(FUNCTION #: 523 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101524 "BB_PURGELINEEND   <Func: 524>"\012\012BB_PURGELINEEND   Allows you to CLEAR the serial buffer.\012\012                  msg->Command = 524\012                  msg->Data    = N/A\012(FUNCTION #: 524 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101525 "BB_NONSTOPTEXT    <Func: 525>"\012\012BB_NONSTOPTEXT    Allows you to change the NONSTOP text scrolling flag.\012\012                  msg->Command = 525\012                  msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012                  if msg->Data = 1, then display text will not pause.\012                  if msg->Data = 0, then display text will pause.\012(FUNCTION #: 525 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101526 "BB_LINECOUNT      <Func: 526>"\012\012BB_LINECOUNT   Allows you to retrieve or change the user''s current number\012               of lines viewed.\012\012               msg->Command = 526\012               msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012               if msg->Data = 1, then msg->String will be current line.\012               if msg->Data = 0, then current line will be msg->String.\012(FUNCTION #: 526 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101527 "DT_LANGUAGE       <Func: 527>"\012\012DT_LANGUAGE      Allows you to retrieve or change the current language\012                 specifications.\012\012                 msg->Command = 527\012                 msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012                 if msg->Data = 1, then msg->String will be language.\012                 if msg->Data = 0, then language will be msg->String.\012\012                NOTE: Languages need to be standardized, please what for\012                      guidelines.\012\012                ie:  Default language .TXT\012                     English          .ENG\012                     German           .GER\012\012                     note that this only effects the menus, bulletins &\012                     other screen text files.\012(FUNCTION #: 527 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101528 "DT_QUICKFLAG      <Func: 528>"\012\012DT_QUICKFLAG      Allows you to change the QUICKTEXT flag.\012\012                  msg->Command = 528\012                  msg->Data    = 1 or 0\012\012                  if msg->Data = 1, then the QuickFlag will be set.\012                  if msg->Data = 0, then the QuickFlag will not be set.\012(FUNCTION #: 528 )\012\012@endnode\012@node Cap1101529 "DT_GOODFILE       <Func: 529>"\012\012DT_GOODFILE       Allows you to set the results of a tested file after\012                  upload.\012\012                  msg->Command = 529\012                  msg->Data    = 1,0 or -1\012\012                  if msg->Data is 1, then the file was not tested.\012                  if msg->Data is 0, then the file passed the filetest.\012                  if msg->Data is -1, then the file failed the filetest.\012\012                  NOTE: This command is only useful with the SYSCmd door\012                  called FILECHECK.\012(FUNCTION #: 529 )\012\012@endnode\012@node SX_PS "System-X Only Print String"\012\012SX_PS		Prints a string to the console/serial port.\012\012		msg->Command = 1500\012		msg->Data    = pointer to a string\012\012\012		Note: no copying required and no length limit!\012\012\012(FUNCTION #: 1500 )\012@endnode\012@node SX_USERPO "Get UserStruct Pointer (UserData)"\012\012SX_USERPO	Gives you the pointer to the User structure\012\012		msg->Command = 1501\012\012\012		returns the pointer in msg->Data\012\012(FUNCTION #: 1501 )\012@endnode\012@node SX_USERPO2 "Get UserStruct Pointer (SXUser)"\012\012SX_USERPO2	Gives you the pointer to the SXUser structure\012\012		msg->Command = 1502\012\012\012		returns the pointer in msg->Data\012\012(FUNCTION #: 1502 )\012@endnode\012@node SX_USERPO3 "Get UserStruct Pointer (Index)"\012\012SX_USERPO3	Gives you the pointer to the User Index structure\012\012		msg->Command = 1503\012\012\012		returns the pointer in msg->Data\012\012(FUNCTION #: 1503 )\012@endnode\012\012@node SX_VER "Get the System-X version"\012\012SX_VER		Gives you the version of SX\012\012		msg->Command = 1504\012\012		returns it in msg->String, eg: "1.00"\012\012(FUNCTION #: 1504 )\012@endnode\012@node SX_NODES "Get a pointer to the node structures"\012\012SX_NODES	Get a pointer to the node structures\012\012		msg->Command = 1505\012\012		returns it in msg->Data\012\012		For more information, see MCP Communication/Command 14.\012\012(FUNCTION #: 1505 )\012@endnode\012@node mcp "MCP"\012\012Communication with MCP is available through standard EXEC-MESSAGES.\012\012The structure of the message is (you must allocate it)\012\012struct MCPMessage\012{\012	struct Message Msg;\012	UWORD command;\012	UWORD nodenum;\012	long data1;\012	long data2;\012	long data3;\012	long data4;\012	long data5;\012	long data6;\012};\012\012UWORD''s are 16-bit\012long''s are 32-bit\012\012\012If anything but an actual node wants to use this port, you must make\012nodenum equal 0 (zero) (that includes doors!).\012\012\012.------------------------.\012| MCP Commands Available |\012`------------------------''\012\012	Note: Commands 1 to 5 are PRIVATE!!\012\012\012	6 - MENU POINTER\012\012		Ask MCP to give you a pointer to a menu structure\012\012		themsg.command = 6\012		themsg.data1   = pointer to the menu you want\012					eg: "Main_Menu"\012\012		returns\012\012		themsg.data2   = the pointer you wanted\012		themsg.data3   = size of the struct in bytes\012\012\012\012	8 - MD5 ENCRYPTION\012\012		This will ask MCP to encrypt a string for you, using MD5.\012\012		themsg.command = 8\012		themsg.data1   = pointer to the string to encrypt\012		themsg.data2   = pointer to 16 bytes to put the result in\012\012\012	10 - QUERY SYSOP\012\012		Find out if the sysop is available\012\012		themsg.command = 10\012\012		returns\012\012		themsg.data1   = pointer to the reason for being away\012				(if NULL, the sysop is available)\012\012\012	12 - APPEND TO A FILE\012\012		themsg.command = 12\012		themsg.data1   = pointer to the filename string\012		themsg.data2   = pointer to the buffer to append\012		themsg.data3   = size of the append buffer\012\012\012	14 - GET A POINTER TO THE NODE INFORMATION CHAIN\012\012		themsg.command = 14\012\012		returns\012\012		themsg.data1   = the pointer to node 1''s structure\012				(use the NEXT field to browse through)\012\012		the struct is as follows\012\012		struct node_struct\012		{					/* offset DEC	*/\012			APTR next;			/*	0	*/\012			struct UserData *User;		/*	4	*/\012			struct UserIndexStruct *UserIndex;/*	8	*/\012			struct SXUserStruct *SXUser;	/*	12	*/\012			char *action;			/*	16	*/\012			char *filename;			/*	20	*/\012			long baud;			/*	24	*/\012			long loginsecs;			/*	28	*/\012			UWORD number;			/*	32	*/\012			UBYTE actionnumber;		/*	34	*/\012			UBYTE active;			/*	35	*/\012			UBYTE useron;			/*	36	*/\012			UBYTE misc;			/*	37	*/\012		};\012\012.--------------------------------------.\012| Example ''C'' program using MCP''s port |\012`--------------------------------------''\012\012struct MCPMessage\012{\012	struct Message Msg;\012	UWORD command;\012	UWORD nodenum;\012	long data1;\012	long data2;\012	long data3;\012	long data4;\012	long data5;\012	long data6;\012};\012struct MCPMessage themsg;\012struct MsgPort *MyPort, *MCPPort;\012\012	MCPPort = FindPort("SX-MCP");\012	if(MCPPort)\012	{\012		MyPort = CreateMsgPort();\012		if(MyPort)\012		{\012			themsg.Msg.mn_Length = sizeof(struct MCPMessage);\012			themsg.Msg.mn_ReplyPort = MyPort;\012			themsg.nodenum = 0;\012			themsg.command = 10;	/* 10 = QUERY SYSOP */\012			PutMsg(MCPPort, (struct Message *)&themsg);\012			WaitPort(MyPort);\012			DeleteMsgPort(MyPort);\012			if(themsg.data1)\012			{\012				PutStr("The Sysop is away because:\n\n");\012				PutStr((char *)themsg.data1);\012				PutStr("\n");\012			} else {\012				PutStr("The Sysop is available!\n");\012			}\012		}\012	}\012@endnode\012@node SX_FUNCTION "Execute an internal SX Function"\012\012SX_FUNCTION	Execute an internal SX Function (sxfunctions.doc)\012\012		msg->data = pointer to this structure:\012\012struct SXFuncStruct\012{\012	UWORD	id;\012	char	*string;\012	UWORD	extra;\012	UWORD	low;\012	UWORD	high;\012	char	*mainarg;\012	char	*execarg;\012} *SXFunc;\012\012		Must must allocate this structure and fill in all\012		the fields, then pass it through msg->data.\012\012(FUNCTION #: 1506 )\012@endnode\012@node SX_CONF "Obtain a pointer to the current Conference Struct"\012\012SX_CONF		Obtain a pointer to the current Conference Structure.\012\012\012		msg->Data will be the pointer to this struct:\012	\012struct ConfStruct\012{\012	char name[45];\012	char path[55];\012	char pass[16];\012	char filepath[52];\012	UWORD fileareas;\012	UWORD uploadarea;\012	UBYTE flf;\012	UBYTE flags;\012	char reserve[82];\012};\012\012(FUNCTION #: 1508 )\012@endnode\012','\012',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',177959,4,0,NULL,NULL,'dc_xu102','scan',1780048460);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dcall103','DCALL103.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DCALL103.LHA','guide','XIM','guide','1.03',NULL,NULL,NULL,replace('TransAmiga "Todays Callers" Script v1.03 \n','\n',char(10)),'trompete.txt',replace('\n\n\n\n\n ___(\·----------------------- ----  ---  --   -     -        - \n      \)       IN A WORLD OF DREAMS - IN A WORLD OF PASSION\n\n            THIS FILE DECIDED TO PASS ONE OF THE LAST AND REAL\n                 BULLETIN BOARD SYSTEMS IN CENTRAL EUROPE\n\n                     THE ONLY WAY TO SURVIVE - FAITH!       (\ ___\n          -      -    ---  --- ------- ----------------------·\)\n\n\n\n\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',14736,4,0,NULL,NULL,'dcall103','scan',1780048460);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dcd_xprt','DCD!XPRT.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DCD!XPRT.LHA',NULL,'XIM','pizza_taxi.exe',NULL,NULL,'DCD','·X·|    _   /_   ._/___ ·Digital·Corruption· .|    /   _|   l    |.      ._____. ._||________\_________||______|     |______.',replace('    _________ ______\n·X·|    _   /_   ._/___ ·Digital·Corruption·\n  .|    /   _|   l    |.      ._____.\n._||________\_________||______|     |______.\n|                                         _|\n|_   pRESENTS: Digi Expert! V1.o          \_\n_/        from ItaL/DC^FRS!                |\n|  kewl looking ''X'' Command replacement    |\n|    for Amiexpress 4.Xx bbs systems!      |\n|                                          |\n|_ [12-Oct-96]_                   [ItaL]_  |','\n',char(10)),'Ringelblume4.txt',replace('                 \n                                  ·     ·\n                               _ __\   /__ _\n                            _ _)\\  \ /  //(_ _\n                           -\   __\° X °/__   /-\n                    _ __ ___ ___)  \/_\/  (___ ___ __ _\n                   -\\\_\\__\\__  _ /¦\ _  __//__//_///-\n             ·         _.      \__)_¯_¯_(__/      ._         ·\n           _/          \|_       | | | | |       _|/          \_\n         __\ ___ _/\____\/__ __ _| | | | |_ __ __\/____/\_ ___ /__\n       _/   \  (_)  \   \/  /_/\\| |_|_| |//\_\  \/   /  (_)  /   \_\n       |                    \_\/ | | | | | \/_/                    |\n      _|                      __ | | | | | __                   _ _|_\n      \|_ _                   \/_| | | | |_\/                      |/\n       |                     · _)  ¯_¯_¯  (_ ·                     |\n       |  ·H2o!·              \\___ \ / ___//                      |\n       ¯\_______________________ _)  Y  (_ _______________________/¯\n                                 \___ ___/\n                                    (_)\n ','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',8592,4,0,NULL,NULL,'dcd_xprt','scan',1780048460);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dcn_f_x2','DCN!F-X2.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DCN!F-X2.LHA','dCN!FileID','XIM','DCN! FileID',NULL,'Derrow','DCN!F','_________________________________________  | ____ \_ ____/ _______) ________)   \___  \ | /  /  / __/_  \  \   \___  \   \_|  \ |   \|',replace('.-----------(dCN-/F·dEZiGN)----------------.\n_________________________________________  |\n____ \_ ____/ _______) ________)   \___  \ |\n/  /  / __/_  \  \   \___  \   \_|  \ |   \|\n_____/_____/______)__ /____/___ /___/_|    \\n|···················\/AdN!····\/······\____/\n| presents a FANTASTIC new kind of DOORS:  |\n|  dCN!FileID v2 pUBLiC vERSION fOR /X!    |\n|    cODED bY Derrow (dCN-/F·dEZiGN)       |\n`--- -- - - - - - - - - - [03-29-96] -- ---''\n','\n',char(10)),'dCN!FileID.guide',replace('@database Bytekiller.guide\n@author "sCANDiC (dCN-/F·dEZiGN)"\n@$VER: dCN!FileID.guide 2.0\n\n@NODE MAIN "dCN!FileID v2.0 dOCUMENTATION"\n\n                          @{fg shine}(@{fg text}Decision@{fg shine}-/@{fg text}F@{fg shine}·@{fg text}Dezign@{fg shine})\n           ____\n@{fg shine}    ______@{fg text}|@{fg shine}   _|________   _________     ________ _@{fg shine}_______  _____ _______\n@{fg text}    \\   @{fg shine}  _@{fg text}   \\       _@{fg shine}/___@{fg text}\\@{fg shine}_      / @{fg text}_  .\\     __@{fg shine}/@{fg text}  _ @{fg shine}  _ \\@{fg text}/  @{fg shine}  _@{fg text}/ @{fg shine}   __@{fg text}/@{fg shine}__\n@{fg text}     \\    /    \\   @{fg shine}   \\_.   / @{fg shine}    / (_@{fg text}) |     _@{fg shine}/ @{fg text}   _ @{fg shine}   \\@{fg text}  _   \\   @{fg shine} _@{fg text}/ @{fg shine}   |\n@{fg text}      \\________@{fg shine}|@{fg text}\\_______@{fg shine}|  /@{fg text}______@{fg shine}\\    @{fg text} |_____@{fg shine}|@{fg text}_____@{fg text}|  @{fg shine}   \\@{fg text}/_____\\_________@{fg shine}|\n@{fg shine}          _____      @{fg text}    \\@{fg shine}/           @{fg text}              |______@{fg shine}\\\n@{fg shine}  _______@{fg text}|  @{fg shine}   |________  _ _________@{fg text}· @{fg shine}  _____________   __________\n@{fg text}  \\    @{fg shine}  _    _@{fg text}/    @{fg shine} __@{fg text}/@{fg shine}__.@{fg shine}_        /_@{fg text}\\  \\    @{fg shine}  _    _\\__@{fg text}\\@{fg shine}_       /\n@{fg text}   \\     /    \\   @{fg shine}  _@{fg text}/   @{fg shine} |@{fg text}/ @{fg shine}      /.@{fg text}  \\@{fg shine}/ @{fg text}\\     \\    \\ @{fg shine}   /      / @{fg text}  ·Mo!/aL·\n@{fg text}    \\__________\\__________/_________@{fg shine}|@{fg text}______\\_____     \\ @{fg shine} /@{fg text}_______@{fg shine}\\\n                                       @{fg text}         |______\\@{fg shine}/\n           @{fg text}dCN!FileID v2.0 by Derrow @{fg shine}(@{fg fill}dCN@{fg shine}-/@{fg fill}F@{fg shine}·@{fg fill}dEZiGN@{fg shine})@{fg text} for @{"FAME" LINK FAME} and /X.\n\n               - @{fg fill}ENGLISH@{fg text} -                        - @{fg fill}GERMAN@{fg text} -\n\n           @{"    DISCLAIMER    " LINK E0}                 @{"     VORWORT     " LINK G0}\n           @{"   iNTRODUCTiON   " LINK E1}                 @{"   EINLEITUNG    " LINK G1}\n           @{"   rEQUIREMENTS   " LINK E2}                 @{" VORAUSSETZUNGEN " LINK G2}\n           @{"   iNSTALLATION   " LINK E3}                 @{"  iNSTALLATION   " LINK G3}\n\n           @{"   cONFIGURATION  " LINK E4}                 @{"  kONFIGURATION  " LINK G4}\n           @{"      hISTORY     " LINK E5}                 @{"   ENTWiCKLUNG   " LINK G5}\n           @{"    kNOWN bUGS    " LINK E6}                 @{"  bEKANNTE bUGS  " LINK G6}\n\n                             @{" hOW TO rEGISTER " LINK REGISTER}\n                             @{"    gREETINGS    " LINK GREET}\n                             @{"  aBOUT F.A.M.E. " LINK FAME}\n                         @{fg shine}->  @{fg text}@{"(dCN!-/F·dEZiGN) " LINK DCN!} @{fg shine} <-\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE G0 "VORWORT"\n\nBei den Produktionen von (dCN-/F·dEZiGN) handelt es sich um hoch-\nqualitative Programme für die Benutzung mit @{"FAME" LINK FAME} und /X.\n\nAlle Produkte von (dCN-/F·dEZiGN) sind Shareware! Das bedeutet es wird von \nvielen Produktionen eine frei verfügbare Version geben. Diese darf über \nalle bekannten Wege frei vertrieben werden (PD-Serien/Aminet/Mailboxen/etc...).\nEs ist erlaubt diese Versionen ohne zeitliche Limitation zu benutzen.\n\nDas Programm wird den Benutzern so zur Verfügung gestellt, wie es ist,\nohne jegliche Garantie oder Haftung irgendeiner Art, sei es ausdrücklich\noder implizit. Wer das Programm benutzt, erklärt sich damit einverstanden,\njegliches Risiko, das die Benutzung des Programms mit sich bringt,\nselbst zu tragen. Der Autor haftet in keinem Fall für Schäden, die\ndirekt oder indirekt durch den Gebrauch oder Mißbrauch des Programms\nentstanden sind.\n\nEs wird keinerlei Gewährleistung für die Funktion des Programmes übernommen.\n\nDie registrierten Versionen der Programme dürfen nur auf einem Rechner \ninstalliert sein und auch nur Zeitgleich auf einem Rechner ausgeführt werden.\nAusnahmeregelungen sind möglich, aber unbedingt schriftlich mit dem Autor\nzu verhanceln!\nDas Verbreiten von registrierten Versionen ist VERBOTEN!\n\nDas Programm sowie die Dokumentation dürfen unter keinen Umständen in\nirgendeiner Form verändert werden.\n\nDie Verwendung des Programms, der Dokumentation oder Teile davon für\nandere Projekte ist VERBOTEN!, soweit dies nicht schriftlich mit dem Autor\nverhandelt wurde.\n\nDer Autor behält sich das Recht vor, Änderungen an Programm und Dokumentation\nohne vorherige Ankündigung zu machen.\n\n\nJeder Verstoß gegen diese Regelungen wird strafrechtlich verfolgt.\n\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE E0 "DISCLAIMER"\n\nAll (dCN-/F·dEZiGN) productions are, without exceptions, high qualitiy \nprograms to be used with @{"FAME" LINK FAME} and /X.\n\nAlso, all (dCN-/F·dEZiGN) products are shareware ! This means, that most of\nour programs will be available on Aminet, PD-Series, BBS`s etc and may be \nfreely distributed. It is allowed to use these programs without any time \nlimitations.\n\nThis software is provided by the regents and contributors ``as is'''' and any \nexpress or implied warranties, including, but not limited to, the implied \nwarranties of merchantability and fitness for a particular purpose are \ndisclaimed. In no event shall the regents or contributors be liable for any \ndirect, indirect, incidental, special, exemplary, or consequential damages \n(including, but not limited to, procurement of substitute goods or services; \nloss of use, data, or profits; or business interruption) however caused and \non any theory of liability, whether in contract, strict liability, or tort \n(including negligence or otherwise) arising in any way out of the use of this \nsoftware, even if advised of the possibility of such damage.\n\n\nThe registered version of this program may only be used on one system. \nExceptions are only applied by a written permission to the author of this\nprogram.\n\nThe distribution of the registered version is NOT ALLOWED !!\n\nAlso it is not allowed to change this program and its documentation in any \nway.\n\nThis program and documentation may only be used in any other project if the \nauthor gave a written permission.\n\nThe author has all rights to change the program and the documentation without\nany announcements.\n\n\nAll offences to these rules will be followed by the law !!!!\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE E1 "iNTRODUCTiON"\n\nThis is a demoversion of dCN!FileID 2.0 by Derrow (dCN-/F·dEZiGN)!\ndCN!FileID is a XIM-Door which unpacks the FILE_ID.DIZ from the\nfollowing archives/files:\n\n- LHA\n- LZX\n- DMS\n- EXE\n- ZIP\n- TXT\n- GIF\n- MOD\n\nIf there isn`t a FILE_ID.DIZ available, it is possible to add one to the\narchive/file.\nThe main use of the program is for the BBS program @{"FAME" LINK FAME} and /X.\nBecause of its great flexibility, it may work with any other program.\nSee @{"iNSTALLATION" LINK E3} for more information.\n\n\nThis program offers, beside its normal functions, some special options:\n\n - Fully configurable and unlimited number of User Sentby-Line''s\n - Display of\n                FILE_ID.DIZ Date (LHA/LZX/ZIP)\n                FILE-CREATION-DATE (DMS)\n                Date of the newest file in the archiv (LHA/LZX/ZIP)\n                Date of the oldest file in the archiv (LHA/LZX/ZIP)\n - Upload Time\n - Upload Node\n\n - Stripping of FUCKING BBS-Addy''s from and in the FILE_ID.DIZ\n _ If a BBS-Addy was found in the FILE_ID.DIZ, then the stripped FILE_ID.DIZ\n   will be replaced in the File-Archiv, if defined.\n\n\ndCN!BYE is used to automatically log off after the upload.\ndCN!SENT is used to configure the SENTBY-Line for each user\nindividually. These settings will be used by dCN!FileID.\n\n\nTo set these options, use the Preferences-Editor.\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE g1 "EINLEITUNG"\n\nDies ist die Demoversion von dCN!FileID 2.0 von Derrow (dCN-/F·dEZiGN)!\ndCN!FileID ist ein XIM Door welches das auspacken der FILE_ID.DIZ aus\nfolgenden Dateitypen erlaubt.\n - LHA Archivdatei\n - LZX Archivdatei\n - DMS Archivdatei\n - EXE Amiga Ausführbare Programme\n - ZIP Archivdatei\n - TXT ASCII Datei\n - GIF Bilddatei\n - MOD Moduledatei (Protracker und kompatible)\n\nWenn die FILE_ID.DIZ nicht vorhanden ist kann diese ebenfalls in die\nDateien geschrieben werden.\nDieses Programm ist für den Betrieb mit dem Mailboxprogramm @{"FAME" LINK FAME} und /X vor-\ngesehen. es ist möglich das es sich. aufgrund seiner Flexibilität,\nauch mit vielen anderen Programmen verträgt. Näheres dazu ist bei\n@{"iNSTALLATION" LINK G3} nachzulesen.\n\nEbenfalls integriert sind folgende Funktionen:\n - Beliebig viele und voll konfigurierbare User Sentby-Lines.\n - Anzeigen von \n                FILE_ID.DIZ Datum (LHA/LZX/ZIP)\n                FILE-CREATION Datum (DMS)\n                Datum der neuesten Datei im Archiv (LHA/LZX/ZIP)\n                Datum der ältesten Datei im Archiv (LHA/LZX/ZIP)\n - Upload Zeit\n - Upload Node\n\n - Strippen von beschissenen BBS-Adds aus und in der FILE_ID.DIZ.\n - Wenn ein BBS-Addy in der FILE_ID.DIZ gefunden wurde, dann wird die\n   gestrippte FILE_ID.DIZ im File-Archiv erneuert, falls gewuenscht.\n\n\ndCN!BYE erlaubt das Automatische ausloggen nach dem Upload.\ndCN!SENT ermöglicht dem Benutzter, seine persönliche SENT-Line zu\nkonfigurieren und Einstellungen für das Verhalten von dCN!FileID\nzu abzuspeichern.\n\nDie Konfiguration erfolgt mit dem Preferences-Editor.\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n\n@NODE E2 "rEQUIREMENTS"\n\n@{fg fill}You need these things to run this program:@{fg text}\n\n\nAll you need is a really cool Amiga with operating system V2.x+ and about\n1 MB of free RAM and HD space.\n\nLast but not least, you need:\n\n/X V 3.x and higher.\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE G2 "VORAUSSETZUNGEN"\n\n@{fg fill}Folgendes wird für die einwandfreie Funktion der Programme benötigt:@{fg text}\n\nEinen Amiga :^)\nOS 2.0+\n1MB freies RAM\n1MB freien Festplattenspeicher\n/X V 3.x und hoeher\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n\n@NODE E3 "iNSTALLATION"\n\n@{fg fill}To install this fine piece of work, do the following:@{fg text}\n\nJust copy from C/\n               DMS\n               DMSDescript\n               EXEDescript\n               GIFDescript\n               Lha\n               LZX\n               ModuleDescript\n               UNDMS\n               UnZip\n               Zip\n...to SYS:C/\n\n          from Libs/\n                    FileID.library\n         ...to Libs:\n                    FileID.library\n\nIf there already exist some of these programs, check out the version\nnumber. It may happen that older versions of these programs will not work\n100% with dCN!FileID !!\n\n\nAnd now copy BBS/\n                  doors/\n                        dCN!FileID/\n                                   dCN!FileID.cfg\n                                   dCN!FileID\n                                   dCN!FileID.020+\n                                   dCN!FileID.strip\n                                   dCN!FileIDPrefs\n                                   dCN!FileIDPrefs.info\n                                   dCN!SENT\n                                   dCN!SENT.020+\n                                   dCN!BYE\n                  Commands/\n                           BBSCmd/\n                                   SENT.info\n                                   U.info\n                           SYSCmd/\n                                   EXAMINE.info\nto your "BBS:" assignment.\n\n\nIf you have a 68020+ processor in your fine Amiga, use the ".020" version !.\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE G3 "iNSTALLATION"\n\n@{fg fill}Zur Installation sind folgende Arbeitsschritte nötig:@{fg text}\n\nKopieren von C/\n               DMS\n               DMSDescript\n               EXEDescript\n               GIFDescript\n               Lha\n               LZX\n               ModuleDescript\n               UNDMS\n               UnZip\n               Zip\n...nach SYS:C/\n\n          von  Libs/\n                    FileID.library\n         ...zu Libs:\n                    FileID.library\n\nWenn die Programme, oder Teile davon, bereits installiert sind, ist die\nVersion zu überprüfen! Bei Abweichungen KANN es passieren, das einige\nFunktionen von dCN!FileID nicht 100%ig ausgeführt werden!!!\n\nKopieren von BBS/\n                  doors/\n                        dCN!FileID/\n                                   dCN!FileID.cfg\n                                   dCN!FileID\n                                   dCN!FileID.020+\n                                   dCN!FileID.strip\n                                   dCN!FileIDPrefs\n                                   dCN!FileIDPrefs.info\n                                   dCN!SENT\n                                   dCN!SENT.020+\n                                   dCN!BYE\n                  Commands/\n                           BBSCmd/\n                                   SENT.info\n                                   U.info\n                           SYSCmd/\n                                   EXAMINE.info\nin das "BBS:" Assign kopieren...\nDie ".020" Versionen sind NUR zu verwenden wenn eine 68020+ CPU\nim Rechner läuft!\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n\n@NODE G4 "KONFIGURATION"\n\nPreferences-Editor von FileID V2.0\n__________________________________\n\nDie Konfiguration zu dCN!FileID erfolgt komplett mit diesem Prefs-Programm.\n\nMit dem Editor werden die default werte und einige andere Settings\nfuer den FileID Extractor eingestellt.\n\n\nDie Erklaerung der Optionen:\n\n\n                  Default Settings fuer den User\n                  ______________________________\n\n\nMAXLINES             :  Maximale Anzahl der Zeilen, die als Description\n                        benutzt werden koennen oder sollen.\n\nTIME TO ASK ID       :  Die Zeit, wielang auf eine Eingabe nach dem\n                        ausgeben der File_id.diz gewartet werden soll.\n\nUSE FILE_ID          :  YES:  FileID wird benutz, ohne den User danach\n                              zu fragen.\n                        NO:   FileID wird nicht benutzt. Der User wird\n                              jedesmal aufgefordert eine Description\n                              einzugeben.\n                        ASK:  Der User wird jedesmal gefragt, ob er die\n                              File_id.diz-Description benutzen moechte.\n\nUSE TAGLINE          :  YES:  Sent-by Line des Users wird benutzt.\n                        NO:   Sent-by Line des Users wird nicht benutzt.\n                        ASK:  User wird gefragt, ob er die Sent-by Line\n                              benutzen moechte.\n\nUSE FULL-EDITOR      :  Damit wird eingestellt, ob der Fullscreen-Editor\n                        fuer die File-Description benutzt werden soll.\n                        (In der Unregistrierten Version nicht verfügbar)\n\nAUTODETECT LOGO      :  Automatische Erkennung eines Logos aufgrund des\n                        File-Namens.\n                        (In der Unregistrierten Version nicht verfügbar)\n\nLIST AVAIL-LOGOS     :  Vorhande Logos auflisten.\n                        (In der Unregistrierten Version nicht verfügbar)\n\n\n\n                  Settings fuer die Sent-by Lines\n                  _______________________________\n\n   Wenn eine der ESC-Code Sequencen geaendert werden soll, dann muss anstelle\n   des normalen "ESC"-Kommando-Startzeichens ein "@" verwendet werden, weil \n   es nicht moeglich ist, ein "ESC"-Code in einem Prefs-programm einzugeben.\n\n\n\nCYCLE BUTTON\nAPPEND SENTLINE      :  Umschalten zwischen den Sent-by Lines.\n\nEingabefeld\nAPPEND SENTLINE      :  Formatierung der Sent-by Line.\n\n                        Optionen:\n\n                           %F :  File_id.diz Datum\n                           %N :  Neuestes Datum eines Files in dem Archiv\n                           %O :  Aeltestes Datum eines Files in dem Archiv\n                           %# :  Node-Nr.\n                           %T :  Tagline (User-Tagline)\n                           %U :  Upload Time\n\nCYCLE BUTTON\nFID TEXT             :  Formatierung fuer das File_id.diz Datum, fuer\n                        File-Archive(LHA,LZH,LZX,ZIP).\n\n                        Optionen:\n\n                           %D :  Tag (numerisch)\n                           %M :  Monat (numerisch)\n                           %m :  Monat (namens-kuerzel)\n                           %Y :  Jahr (numerisch)\n\nCYCLE BUTTON\nFCD TEXT             :  Formatierung fuer das File-Creation Datum, fuer\n                        File-Archive(DMS).\n\n                        Optionen:\n\n                           %D :  Tag (numerisch)\n                           %M :  Monat (numerisch)\n                           %m :  Monat (namens-kuerzel)\n                           %Y :  Jahr (numerisch)\n\nCYCLE BUTTON\nNO_ID_TEXT           :  Formatierung fuer das File-Datum, fuer Files\n                        die kein Datum enthalten. (TXT,MOD,GIF)\n\nCYCLE BUTTON\nNEW_TEXT             :  Formatierung fuer das Neueste Datum eines Files\n                        in einem Archiv.\n\n\n                        Optionen:\n\n                           %D :  Tag (numerisch)\n                           %M :  Monat (numerisch)\n                           %m :  Monat (namens-kuerzel)\n                           %Y :  Jahr (numerisch)\n\nCYCLE BUTTON\nÔLD_TEXT             :  Formatierung fuer das Aelteste Datum eines Files\n                        in einem Archiv.\n\n                        Optionen:\n\n                           %D :  Tag (numerisch)\n                           %M :  Monat (numerisch)\n                           %m :  Monat (namens-kuerzel)\n                           %Y :  Jahr (numerisch)\n\nCYCLE BUTTON\nNO_NEW_TEXT          :  Formatierung fuer das neueste File-Datum, fuer\n                        Archive\n                        die keine Files enthalten, bei denen ein Datum\n                        vorhanden\n                        ist.\n\n\nCYCLE BUTTON\nNO_OLD_TEXT          :  Formatierung fuer das aelteste File-Datum, fuer\n                        Archive\n                        die keine Files enthalten, bei denen ein Datum\n                        vorhanden\n                        ist.\n\n\nCYCLE BUTTON\nUL_TIME_TEXT         :  Formatierung fuer den Upload Time String.\n\n                        Optionen:\n\n                           %H :  Stunden\n                           %M :  Minuten\n                           %S :  Sekunden\n\n\n\n\n            Settings fuer die Archiv-ADD/EXTRACT/REPLACE Commandos\n            ______________________________________________________\n\n\nCYCLE BUTTON\nARCHIV ADD COMMAND   :  Aufrufzeile um eine File_id.diz in ein Archiv\n                        dazuzupacken.\n\nCYCLE BUTTON\nARCHIV EXTRACT COMMAND: Aufrufzeile um eine File_id.diz aus einem Archiv\n                        zu entpacken.\n\nCYCLE BUTTON\nARCHIV REPLACE COMMAND: Aufrufzeile um eine File_id.diz in einem Archiv zu\n                        replacen.\n\nAuswahl-Button\nCommand Replace/Delete: Falls ein Packer keine Replace-Funktion\n                        unterstuetzt,\n                        sondern nur eine Delete-funktion, dann muss hier Delete\n                        ausgewaehlt werden.\n\n\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n\n@NODE E4 "cONFIGURATION"\n\n\nPreferences-Editor for FileID V2.0\n__________________________________\n\nThe configuration of dCN!FileID is completly followed by this Prefs-Program.\n\nThis editor is used to set the default settings and some other options\nfor the FileID Extractor.\n\n\nExplanation of the options:\n\n\n                  Default Settings for the User\n                  _____________________________\n\n\nMAXLINES             :  Maximum number of lines which are used for the\n                        description.\n\nTIME TO ASK ID       :  Time to wait for user input after the displaying\n                        of the FILE_ID.DIZ.\n\nUSE FILE_ID          :  YES:  FILE_ID will be used without asking the\n                              user.\n                        NO:   FILE_ID will NOT be used. The user will be\n                              prompted for a description each time.\n                        ASK:  User will be asked whether he should use\n                              the description or not.\n\nUSE TAGLINE          :  YES:  Sent-by Line of the User will be used.\n                        NO:   Sent-by Line of the User will NOT be used.\n                        ASK:  User will be asked whether to use the\n                              Sent-by Lne or not.\n\nUSE FULL-EDITOR      :  Check this to use the Fullscreen-Editor for the\n                        File-Description.\n                        (Only for registered users)\n\nAUTODETECT LOGO      :  Automatic detection of a group logo by checking\n                        the filename\n                        (Only for registered users)\n\nLIST AVAIL-LOGOS     :  List all available logos\n                        (Only for registered users)\n\n\n                  Settings for the Sent-by Lines\n                  ______________________________\n\n        If you want to change any of the ESC-Code sequences, then use\n     instead of the normal "ESC"-character-Introducer this character: "@",\n  because it is not possible to put an "ESC"-char-intr. in a Prefs-programm.\n\n\nCYCLE BUTTON\nAPPEND SENTLINE      :  Switch between the Sent-by Lines.\n\nTEXTENTRY\nAPPEND SENTLINE      :  Format of the Sent-by Line.\n\n                        Options:\n\n                           %F :  File_id.diz Date\n                           %N :  Newest date of a file in the archiv\n                           %O :  Oldest date of a file in the archiv\n                           %# :  Node-Nr.\n                           %T :  Tagline (User-Tagline)\n                           %U :  Upload Time\n\nCYCLE BUTTON\nFID TEXT             :  Format for the File_id.diz date, used by\n                        file-archives(LHA,LZH,LZX,ZIP).\n\n                        Options:\n\n                           %D :  Day (numeric)\n                           %M :  Month (numeric)\n                           %m :  Month (shortname)\n                           %Y :  Year (numeric)\n\nCYCLE BUTTON\nFCD TEXT             :  Format for the file-creation date, used by\n                        file-archive(DMS).\n\n                        Options:\n\n                           %D :  Day (numeric)\n                           %M :  Month (numeric)\n                           %m :  Month (shortname)\n                           %Y :  Year (numeric)\n\nCYCLE BUTTON\nNO_ID_TEXT           :  Format for the file-date, used for files\n                        which have no date. (TXT,MOD,GIF)\n\nCYCLE BUTTON\nNEW_TEXT             :  Format for the newest date of a file in an\n                        archiv.\n\n\n                        Options:\n\n                           %D :  Day (numeric)\n                           %M :  Month (numeric)\n                           %m :  Month (shortname)\n                           %Y :  Year (numeric)\n\nCYCLE BUTTON\nÔLD_TEXT             :  Format for the oldest date of a file in an\n                        archiv.\n\n                        Options:\n\n                           %D :  Day (numeric)\n                           %M :  Month (numeric)\n                           %m :  Month (shortname)\n                           %Y :  Year (numeric)\n\nCYCLE BUTTON\nNO_NEW_TEXT          :  Format for the newest file-date for archives\n                        which have no files with a date.\n\n\nCYCLE BUTTON\nNO_OLD_TEXT          :  Format for the oldest file-date for archives\n                        which have no files with a date.\n\n\nCYCLE BUTTON\nUL_TIME_TEXT         :  Format for the Upload Time String.\n\n                        Options:\n\n                           %H :  Hours\n                           %M :  Minutes\n                           %S :  Seconds\n\n\n\n\n            Settings for the Archiv-ADD/EXTRACT/REPLACE commands\n            ______________________________________________________\n\n\n\nCYCLE BUTTON\nARCHIV ADD COMMAND   :  Command line to add a File_id.diz to an archiv\n\nCYCLE BUTTON\nARCHIV EXTRACT COMMAND: Command line to extract a File_id.diz to an archiv\n\nCYCLE BUTTON\nARCHIV REPLACE COMMAND: Command line to replace a File_id.diz in an archiv\n\nSelect-Button\nCommand Replace/Delete: If a packer does not support a replace function,\n                        select Delete !\n\n\n\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n\n@NODE E5 "hISTORY"\n\n@{fg fill}The history...@{fg text}\n\nHundrets of BETA-releases were testet by sCANDiC!\nThousands of changes have been made to the program...\n\nIn the future, these changes will be posted in this section ! :^)\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE G5 "eNTWiCKLUNG"\n\n@{fg fill}Die Entwicklungsgeschichte...@{fg text}\n\nHunderte von BETA-Versionen wurden von sCANDiC getested!\nTausende von Änderungen haben die Programme erfahren...\n\nIn Zukunft werden diese Änderungen hier stehen! :^)\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE E6 "kNOWN bUGS"\n\n@{fg fill}Known bugs by using dCN!FileID...@{fg text}\n\nIn the /X Version of dCN!FileID, it can happen, that the Sent-by lines in \nthe File-Dir will fuck up, if you define a Sent-by line which has a \nlength over 200 characters including the ESC-Codes!\nThis is not realy a bug on dCN!FileID, more on /X itself.\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE G6 "bEKANNTE pROBLEME/BUGS"\n\n@{fg fill}Bekannte Probleme bei der benuetzung von dCN!FileID...@{fg text}\n\nBei der /X Version von dCN!FileID, kann es passieren, dass im File-Dir\ndie Sent-by Lines bescheuert aussehen, wenn eine Sent-by Line so definiert\nwird, dass Sie laenger als 200 Zeichen hat inclusive der ESC-Codes!\nDas ist nicht wirklich ein Bug von dCN!FileID, mehr ein Bug von /X selbst.\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE REGISTER "hOW TO rEGISTER"\n\n·         -( oNE oF eUROPES fASTEST aND mOST rESPECTED bOARDS! )-\n¦ _______________:______ _ ____ _ ___.    _ _________  _________________\n| \___._    \_   ¦     /  ____/____  l______   _____/_/_    \____._    /\n`-|   l/     /   :    /   \       /  /     /  ___/     /     \   l/  _/_.\n  l___/     /\_______/___________/________/___________/_______\__/     /|\n.----/_____/-Mo-------------------------------------------------/_____/-''\n|     ._____________ ___.   _ ___.     /\____________:________________\n|     | _  ______/  \   l______  l____/_ \_.   \     ¦     /______   /\n`-----| \__.___/     \  /     /  /     /  \|    \    :    /      \__/---.\n      l____|/_________\______/________/_________/\_______/________\     |\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------''\n|   sUPPORTiNG: aMiGA, pC, mAC, sNES , hPA! <-> eIGHT fUCKiN` fAST nODES!\n|	        	     4.5 gIG oNLINE !!!\n|               .t.o.t.a.l. .p.r.i.v.a.t.e. .s.y.s.t.e.m.!.\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------.\n sYS:dERROW/tRSI iNC. sTUFF:sAM vISION/hZN - dEFENS/hZN - iXXY/tRSI iNC.|\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------''\n|       nODE#1: +49- uSR 33.6!       <->       nODE#5: +49-iSDN!\n|       nODE#2: +49- uSR 33.6!       <->       nODE#6: +49-iSDN!\n|       nODE#3: +49- zYX 19.2!       <->       nODE#7: +49-iSDN!\n|       nODE#4: +49- zYX 16.8!       <->       nODE#8: +49-iSDN!\n`----------------------------------------------------------------------->\n  *** tRSI mEMBER hQ - hORIZON wHQ - tBI wHQ - mERLIN cHQ - fSW eHQ ***\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GREET "gREETINGS"\n\n@{fg fill}These are my personal greetings....\n@{fg text}\n\n\n               Strider/tRSi for the greatest BBS System ever! :)\n         sCANDiC/dCN^M!^PgS & Cthulhu/dCN for this nice documentation...\n                  SieGel/tRSi for his help and suggestions...\n           BloodRock/SDC for his great FAME.library & FileID.library\n           Mario/tRSi please return back online with your great BBS.\n                      Vampire/tRSi for good friendship...\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@node "FAME" "Informations about the FAME-System."\n\n                        @{b}Informations about FAME@{ub}\n\n FAME is at this time still under construction, but because of the fact\n that many people asked for FAME, it will be released until the end\n of february under the concept of shareware and will be available for\n everyone. At the begining not everything will be completly finished and\n because of this not everything you can already configure will work.\n The registered Versions have to work at least some days before they will\n be released for registered Users, but it''s still possible that these\n versions also make problems when using them. But as soon as you''ve\n reported those problems, they will be fixed!\n\n If some of the settings won''t work, it might be a bug but it''s also (more)\n possible that those functions are not implemented yet.\n\n Some of the internal functions are currently untested and it''s possible\n that they produce errors or problems, but please remember the complexity\n of FAME !\n\n If you have questions or problems with FAME, please turn on one of the\n FAME-Developers or ask Strider to solve your problems.\n\n\n@{b}@{u}What should FAME costs ?@{ub}@{uu}\n\n Registered Version:  110 USD / 150 DM\n Betatester Version:  145 USD / 200 DM\n\n\n@{b}@{u}What is included in the FAME-package ?@{ub}@{uu}\n\n Server, SystemEditor, MainPart, FAMEHydra.FIM, FAMEError.FIM\n\n FAME.library FAMEChat.FIM programmed by Bloodrock/tRSi\n\n FAMEFullEd.FIM, FAMEScript.FIM programmed by Beatnik/tRSi\n\n MUI UserEditor, FAMEDoorHelp.FIM, FAMEInfo programmed by SieGeL/tRSi\n\n Also some doors and tools from the FAME-Development-Team are included,\n but this doors are only unregistered Versions and have therefor some\n limitations. The registered Versions of those doors and the Informations\n how to get them are available here in the pUNISHMENT iNC. BBS.\n\n It could happen that some of the doors and tools listed here are currently\n missing because there are currently under development !\n\n\n@{b}@{u}Who creates FAME ?@{ub}@{uu}\n\n@{fg fill}Main programmer:@{fg text}\n\n - David ''Strider'' Wettig (tRSi) [email removed]\n\n@{fg fill}Additional programmer:@{fg text}\n\n - Oliver ''Bloodrock'' Lange (tRSi) [email removed]\n - Ulrich Arne ''Beatnik'' Jansen (tRSi) [email removed]\n - Sascha ''Siegel'' Pfalz (tRSi) [email removed]\n\n@{fg fill}FAME-Development-Team:@{fg text}\n\n - David ''Strider'' Wettig (tRSi) [email removed]\n - Oliver ''Bloodrock'' Lange (tRSi) [email removed]\n - Ulrich Arne ''Beatnik'' Jansen (tRSi) [email removed]\n - Sascha ''Siegel'' Pfalz (tRSi) [email removed]\n - Andreas ''ByteAndi'' Petermann (tRSi)\n - Dirk ''Spy'' Holzkampf (tRSi) [email removed]\n - Bodo ''Dr.Dre!'' Hoffmann (tRSi)\n\n\n@{b}@{u}Disclaimer:@{ub}@{uu}\n\n No warranties are given. We take no responsibility of any possible harm this\n product could do to your AMIGA system (not that it would but..).\n We give also no warranties to any dokuments or doors/tools included with\n FAME.\n You use FAME and all FAME related files at your own risk !\n\n Of course we take no responsibility when someone is using FAME for illegal\n terms.\n @{b}------------------------------------------------------------------[EOF]-----@{ub}\n@endnode\n\n@NODE dCN! "(dCN-/F·dEZiGN) in Future..."\n\n                     @{fg fill}Projects of (dCN·/F-dEZiGN) 1996\n                     @{fg shine}~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n@{fg fill}Project    Type            Features                          Status   Coder\n@{fg shine}~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n@{fg text}dCN!JOiN   Join-Conf Tool  Select Conference via Cursor      READY    Cthulhu\n                           Protect Conferences via Password   \ndCN!BULL   Bulletin-View   Select Bulletins via Cursor       WORKING  Cthulhu\n                           Lvl.-Axx/Conf-Axx related Bulls    \ndCN!STAT   UserStatus      Extern Designfiles                IDLE     Derrow\n                           User-Config for up to 48 designs \n                           Random designs                   \ndCN!WHO    WHO-Tool        Nice looking WHO-Door             IDLE     Derrow\n                           Maybe with configurable design     \ndCN!CHECK  Multi-Checker   Intelligent Checker for LHA/LZX   WORKING  RTM&Derrow\n                           DMS/ZIP/TXT with more than 20    \n                           Add- and Stripmodes              \ndCN!TOP    Multitop        Bulletins TOP-Generator with      IDLE     Cthulhu\n                           extern designs                   \ndCN!WEEK   Weektop         Global Weektop Tool with UL/DL    IDLE     Cthulhu\n                           Gives Creditz to Week-Top Upper  \n                           Writes EALL at the end of period \ndCN!EDIT   Filelist-ED     Editor for the Filelisting        WORKING  Derrow\n                           Supports ANSI and FILE ID 2.x    \n                           (ByteAndi) Features              \ndCN!LAST   LastCaller      LastCallers Tool fully            IDLE     Derrow\n                           User-Configureable               \n                           With WEEK-and GLOBAL Records     \ndCN!FREE   Free-DL Tool    Sets Files Free Download and      WORKING  Cthulhu\n                           writes EALL Message               \ndCN!ZIPPY  Zippy Search    Global Conferenvces Search        WORKING  TranceTip\n                           Reverse Filedir Scan\n                           Multiple Filescan\ndCN!FileID FILE_ID Proc.   BG-Check Module                   READY    Derrow\n                           Strip&Add File_Id-Lines\ndCN!DUPE   DupeChecker     BG-Check Dupechecker with         IDLE     TranceTip\n                           Support of different Conferences  \ndCN!NUKE   File-Nuker      File Nuker with many options      IDLE     Derrow\n\n\n                      @{fg fill}Members behind (dCN·/F-dEZiGN):\n                      @{fg shine}~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n                      @{fg text}sCANDiC    - Coordination & Design\n                      Cthulhu    - Coder\n                      RTM        - Coder\n                      Trancetip  - Coder\n                      Derrow     - Coder\n\n@{fg fill}...more projects to come! If you want any specials, suggest us!\n\n@{fg shine}If YOU are a really good BBS Tools Coder (NO LAME AREXX OR SUCH SHIT!) and want\n    to join (dCN-/F·dEZiGN) just contact any dECiSiON member worldwide!\n\n@ENDNODE\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'XIM-BBSCmd',377314,1,0,NULL,NULL,'dcn_fileid','scan',1780048460);
