 the names you use to call the doors (i.e.  "N").\nThe  second  row  is  the  decsription that MULTIDOOR will show when you\nselects  the doors.  This is all you have to do.  If you want to install\nanother  command  just name it like "DOORS:MULTIDOOR/MULTI_O.CFG".  Easy\nhuh?   But  don''t  forget  that  the  commands you want to use *MUST* be\ninstalled with it''s ICON in the BBSCMD directory.\n\nProgram Logic:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nIf  you  I.E.   install this door as the N command.  MultiDoor will look\nfor  the  file "Doors:MultiDoor/Multi_N.Cfg".  (Check the CONFIG part of\nthe  doc  for  more  info).   If it''s found, the door will try to locate\n"Doors:MultiDoor/Multi_N.Data".   If  that is found, the door will check\nfor  the  users config in it.  If the door finds it, it will execute the\ndoor  with  the  arguments  that  is sent to MultiDoor.  If not, it will\ndisplay  a  list of the doors he can select, and what he chooses will be\nadded  to the datafile!  After this the door will work FULLY transparent\nbeteween the command prompt and the choosed door.\n\nProgram History:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nv0.1 - First version.  This was called "MULTINEW" and could only be installed\n       on the N command.  The idea for this door came from Zcandaler and\n       ORGASMATRON!, and they wanted it almost at the same time..!  Cool eh?\n       Only released to beta testers and some others...\n\nv1.0 - Now showing a banner so the user understands that he can at any time\n       change door at this command with the -CFG option.  Also added the gr8\n       feature to make it installable on all commands.  Ideas by ORGASMATRON!\n       and myself!  =) Documenation totaly rewriten and improved by ORG*\n\nv1.1 - Fixed some internal bugs, and also fixed so that the user *HAVE TO* enter\n       something at the prompt.\n\nContact nIKE?!\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nCall INSTANT PLEASURE (+46-510-27660) or leave a message to any CRAZE or\nDELIGHT  member  and  tell  them  to  contact  me.   (My board has a NUP\ninstalled,  so u should better get that first!  =)).  If you want a door\npersonally  designed  or  have  some  ideas etc for doors, then u should\ncontact  me!   I don''t charge anything for the doors..  Although u could\ngive me a card or support my board or something =)..\n\nGreetings:\n~~~~~~~~~~\n     (« aLL cRZ/pSE ^ dELIGHT mEMBERS! · bOBO/mYSTIC · xERXES/fLT^mST »)\n    (« vEDDER/iNS · dANSKEN · aGAMEMNON/m22 · rIOTER/eQX · lOGiC/rBS »)\n  (« zCANDALER!/dPL · dR.dRE!/tRSi · aQUARIUS/oTL · sAVAGE/iNS · lOUIE/iNS »)\n (« kID cURRY/cLS · jUAN/tRSi · bOROMIR/tRSi · oRG*/x-TRADE · cYBERTRON/aFL »)\n (« eXIDOR · lUSSAR''N/rEBELS · mANTA/aC · dISC/rBS · hIJACKER/cLS · cASCADE »)\n (« uFO/oRIENT · aLL tHE oTHER fELLA''S i''VE fORGOT iN tHIS sHITTY dOC fILE! »)\n\n==============================================================================\n       And also ! Don`t forget to give these DELIGHT boards a ring !\n==============================================================================\n    DIGITAL EXTASY   [WHQ      HQ]   +1.201.345.4315 -  4 RINGDOWN\n    DOOM OF EXTASY   [European HQ]  +49.234.921.0347 -  3 RINGDOWN\n                                    +49.234.927.0480 -  2 ISDN RGDN\n    MAGIC BBS        [German   HQ]  +49.231.836.991  -  2 NODES\n                                    +49.231.833.906\n    DAWN RAID        [UK       HQ]  +44.1707.320.320 -  5 NODES\n                                    +44.1707.392.317            \n                                    +44.1707.392.453 -  3 RINGDOWN\n    THE UNDISCOVERED [NL       HQ]  +31.229.444.42   -  3 NODES\n                                    +31.229.414.42\n                                    +31.229.443.31\n    UNDERCOVER       [Swedish  HQ]  +46.854.023.405  -  2 NODES\n                                    +46.854.066.627    \n    EUROPE''S CHAOS   [ Dist Site ]  +49.461.302.80   -  4 NODES\n    THE KREMLIN      [ Dist Site ]   +7.095.125.5867 -  1 NODE\n==============================================================================\n                    AND OF COURSE THESE CRZ/PSE BOARDS\n==============================================================================\n            INSTANT PLEASURE *WHQ*  +46 510   27660  [1 Node! ]\n            EVERYWARE        *NHQ*  +47 639   54190  [2 Nodes!]\n            NUCLEAR WASTE    *SHQ*  +46 510   27173  [1 Node! ]\n==============================================================================\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',8434,2,0,NULL,NULL,'dlt_md10','scan',1780048479);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dlt_mq14','DLT-MQ14.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DLT-MQ14.LHA',NULL,'XIM','_/\____/\______/\_sCn__/\________/\_____/\_.',NULL,'Diogenes.','DLT','\____ \_______   /\ /__\______  \  \   ___\| |/  /  /  ___/  /__X    \  \_ \     \  \  /| /_____/_____/_____/______\_____\__\__\__\/ |',replace('_/\____/\______/\_sCn__/\________/\_____/\_.\n\____ \_______   /\ /__\______  \  \   ___\|\n|/  /  /  ___/  /__X    \  \_ \     \  \  /|\n/_____/_____/_____/______\_____\__\__\__\/ |\n\_____\_____\_____\______/_____/__/__/__/  |\n]------------------------------------------[\n|             M  A  S  Q  U  E             |\n| v1.4i: The PSEUDO INTELLIGENT Quest Door |\n| FAR BETTER than ''The Quest'' by Diogenes. |\n| !GUARANTEES *ABSOLUTE* LAMER PROTECTION! |\n`--------{ /X XIM by .\\YSTIF/DLT }--------''\n','\n',char(10)),'masque.doc',replace('                                                    ._____.\n     _____________________________   ______________ |     |_______________\n     \_______  \   ______/       /  (______)  ____/_|_   _| \_____  _____/\n     |      /   \_ ___)_\_   ___/___/      \_ \__     |  \_     |    |\n     |     /     / \      |  \     \        /   |     |   |     |    |\n     |__________/_________|_________\_____ /____|_____|___|_____|____|\n +-Mo!/f^I- - -- - -- - -- - -- - -- - --\/- -- - -- - - -- - -- - -- - -- -+\n\n                                P R E S E N T S\n\n                  ___ ___  _____  ,____  _____         _____\n                 (   |   )(_____l______)(____,)(_____l(____/,\n                  ------------------------------------------\n               v1.4k [1st Public Release] (c)''94 Mystif/Delight\n\n         The MOST POWERFUL New User Quest Door for /X 4.x, 3.x, (?)2.x\n             ~~~~ ~~~~~~~~\n_______________________________________________________________________________\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n                             The Purpose of Masque\n_______________________________________________________________________________\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n  I guess most of you have seen and most probably have installed ''The Quest'' by\n  Diogenes/SR. He called his production ''revolutionary'' and was absolutely\n  right in that, since it was a really amazing piece of coding. But the level\n  of interactivity introduced by ''The Quest'' was kinda low and it lacked some\n  features that I turned out to be in need of and the number of which kept\n  growing. And icon-tooltypes approach was very very muchly unwelcome. Thus\n  Masque was born...\n\n  * Script based, but you *dont* have to be a programmer to write your own\n    powerful scripts ranging from simple questionaires and up to those\n    ''one-wrong-step-and-you-are-deleted'' types for private systems\n\n  * Pseudo intelligence in answers analysis incorporating smartcards provides\n    literally unlimited power\n\n  * Points calculation and analysis for totally ''artificially'' controlled new\n    user validation - the deserving ones will automatically get the axx, while\n    lamers will be kicked to never come back\n\n  * Notification of the users about a new user''s arrival\n\n  * A jump to another script from within a scipt can be performed at any time\n    to offer multiple languages, local scene questions etc\n\n  * Backdoor free - a feature these days\n\n  * Many other extraordinary features too wild to describe\n\n  Though it will take quite a while to configure but the program is worth it!\n\n_______________________________________________________________________________\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n                               Installing Masque\n_______________________________________________________________________________\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n  Copy the files from this archive to their respective directories of your bbs:\n  Remember to create ''Answers'' dir in "doors:masque/" if none exists.\n  Note that ACCESS in masque.info in SYSCMD should be set to a low value, like\n  001 while in BBSCMD/MAS.info it should be the same as SYSOP_AXX in masque.cfg\n  (200 for example) since only sysop and cosysops should be able to launch it.\n  Then you must have a line in your JOIN.TXT:\n\n  ~CC_masque\n            ^---Space\n\n  And ofcoze don''t forget to edit masque.script and masque.cfg to suit your\n  personal needs. These files are vital for Masque'' proper functioning.\n\n  Sysop and cosysops can launch it from the main menu prompt the following way:\n    ''MAS''\n    ''MAS n''  search for new users since last logon\n    ''MAS s''  search for a particular users'' answers\n    ''MAS a''  answer the questionaire\n\n_______________________________________________________________________________\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n                            Configuration keywords\n_______________________________________________________________________________\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n                    Whenever '';'' is hit the rest of the line is considered to\n                    be a comment\n\n                    XXXX must be either FILE or TEXT. If you want a text file\n                    to be displayed, *DO* include the extention, for example:\n                    KICKASS_FILE "bbs:screens/FuckOff.txt"\n\n\n  SYSOP_ACCESS      Access required for a user to view other users'' answers\n  ------------      and to answer questions whether or not he has already\n                    answered them.\n                    Default is 250.\n\n  MAX_POINTS        Specifies how many points a user can get if he answers all\n  ----------        the questions correctly (correctly from the sysop''s point\n                    of view, offcoz). You gotta answer all the questions\n                    yourself and then substitute the value  with the number in\n                    the "points" field when you ''V''iew your own answers. Don''t\n                    forget to repeat the procedure every time you change the\n                    script. Actually it does not have to be the absolute\n                    maximum value; in this case a user can get more than 100%.\n\n                    Another way is to use automatic MAX_POINTS computation. In\n                    order to do that leave out this keyword in masque.cfg, but\n                    use ''ASK.M'' instead of ''ASK'' in masque.script whenever you\n                    want to grant any points for the question. This way\n                    MAX_POINTS is calculated by adding up M''s from all the\n                    ''ASK.M'' questions. (Shit, I really hope you catch my drift)\n                    However, you can use ''ASK'' (without .M) as well, when you\n                    dont want to grant points for a question. See ''ASK'' script\n                    keyword description later in the doc.\n\n  MAX_FAULTS        This makes the door drop dtr on the user after he answered\n  ----------        N times with a blank line or simply pressed return instead\n                    of providing an answer to a question. Provide a larger\n                    number to disable this option. Alternatively you can use\n                    ''ASK CR'', thus allowing users to answer with a blank line.\n                    Default is 255.\n\n  MUST_ANSWER_XXXX  A string or a text file which will be displayed to the user\n  ----------------  after each blank line for an answer.\n\n  KICKASS_XXXX      A string or an ansi text file to display before dropping\n  ------------      dtr when the user reaches the "MAX_FAULTS" limit.\n\n  PREVIOUS_FLAG     "CMD" if you want CMD_NAME to be launched when a kicked\n  -------------     user attempts to login, which is usually ''C''omment to sysop\n                    so that he can explain what the hell happened and provide\n                    excuses if he got any. "NO" if you want a kicked user to get\n                    lost. "YES" will tell the door to treat a kicked user as a\n                    new user.\n                    Default is "YES".\n\n  NO_PREVIOUS_XXXX  If PREVIOUS_FLAG is "NO" this string or ansi text file will\n  ----------------  be displayed before dropping dtr.\n\n  CMD_NAME          Menu command to execute when a kicked user comes back. In\n  --------          order to use this option PREVIOUS_FLAG must be "CMD".\n                    Default is ''c''\n\n  CMD_FRONT_XXXX    If PREVIOUS_FLAG is "CMD" this string or ansi text file\n  --------------    will be displayed right before CMD_NAME is launched.\n\n  CMD_TAIL_XXXX     If PREVIOUS_FLAG is "CMD" this is a string or a text file\n  -------------     to display right after CMD_NAME returns. Dtr will be\n                    dropped afterwards.\n\n  MAIL_USER         User to send a message to when a new user logs in. Message\n  ---------         will contain the number of points, access after answering\n                    all the questions and whether he was kicked. If MAIL_USER\n                    is EALL then a public message will be sent asking for any\n                    valuable info concerning the new user. No EALL message is\n                    sent if the user is kicked (Whats the use?)\n\n  MAIL_LOCATION     Location of the conference where you want the message sent\n  -------------     (eg: "bbs:Conf_2/")\n\n                    You can have multiple users notified, but remember that\n                    each MAIL_USER must be followed by his MAIL_LOCATION.\n\n\n  Here is an example of masque.cfg:\n  ---------------------------------\nSYSOP_ACCESS      200\nMAX_FAULTS        3\n;MAX_POINTS        15\nKICKASS_FILE      "bbs:screens/FuckOff.txt"\nMUST_ANSWER_TEXT  "ANSWER, You Little Ugly No Good... "\nPREVIOUS_FLAG     CMD\nCMD_FRONT_TEXT    "You didn''t Pass the Validation, What Excuses Have You Got?!?"\nCMD_TAIL_TEXT     "Don''t Expect Much from Sysop though..."\n;CMD_NAME          o\n;NO_PREVIOUS_TEXT  "You Were Told to Fuck off... So FUCK OFF!!!"\nMAIL_USER         Mystif\nMAIL_LOCATION     BBS:NEWUSERS/\nMAIL_USER         EALL\nMAIL_LOCATION     BBS:ELITE/\n\n_______________________________________________________________________________\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n                               Script keywords\n_______________________________________________________________________________\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n     Whenever '';'' is hit the rest of the line is considered to be a comment\n\n  PRINT "string"\n     Display a string of text to the user\n\n  SHOW "file"\n     Display an ansi text file to the user\n\n  KICKASS\n     Drop dtr\n\n  QUIT\n     Quit the questionaire\n\n  DOOR "name"\n     Immediately launch the specified door or internal menu command\n\n  POINTS [SET] N|MAX\n     Points manipulation.\n     Eg: ''POINTS 5''        Grant N points to the user\n         ''POINTS SET 100''  Set users'' points to 100\n         ''POINTS MAX''      Grant the M value from the last ''ASK.M''\n\n  ACCESS N\n     Change user''s access level to N\n\n  SCRIPT "ext"\n     Execution will proceed to "masque.ext" (which is your another script)\n\n  ASK[.M] [CR] "string"\n     Display a text string and wait for an answer. If you DONT use MAX_POINTS\n     in masque.cfg then the MAX_POINTS value is calculated during the\n     questioning procedure by adding together M''s of each asked question.\n     (eg: ''ASK.5 "blabla"'' will tell the door to increase MAX_POINTS by 5)\n     If CR is used then a blank line will be considered a valid answer.\n\n  IF [NOT] "string1" "string2" ... "string32"\n     If one of the strings is [not] found in the answer to the last ''ASK''ed\n     question then execution proceeds to the deeper level. Say, you want to\n     kick the user if he answered ''no'' on ''Will you support the board?'', then\n     you could use the following script fragment:\n\n     ASK "Will you support the board? "\n     IF "n*"\n       KICKASS\n     ^^----------------!!!These 2 spaces *ARE* IMPORTANT!!!\n\n  IF POINTS [NOT] MORE|EQUAL|LESS N|MAX\n     Same as the above one but instead of strings it compares the number of\n     points the user has managed to get so far with the N value, or with\n     MAX_POINTS. If points turn out to be less than 0, then points are set to 0\n\n  ELSE\n     If the corresponding IF statement was not satisfied then execution skips\n     to the lines following ELSE (if ELSE is present, offcoz)\n\n\n  An example of masque.script:\n  ----------------------------\nPRINT "Who the Hell Do You Think You Are?"\nASK " [1]: "\nIF Mystif                                    ;Hehehehe\n  ACCESS 30\n  DOOR "o"\n  QUIT\n\nPRINT "Identify the following abbreviations"\nASK.5 " [1] HLM: "\nIF "*hoodlum*"\n  POINTS MAX\nELSE\n  PRINT "Wrong"\nASK.5 " [2] CLS: "\nIF "*classic*"\n  POINTS MAX\nELSE\n  PRINT "Wrong"\n\nPRINT "CC Stands for... "\nASK.5 " [1]: "\nIF NOT "*Cal*Card*"\n  PRINT "Wrong"\n  ASK "Wrong, You Got One More Chance...: "\n  IF NOT "*Cal*Card*"\n    PRINT "Wrong again!"\n    ASK "The Very Last Chance...: "\n    IF NOT "*Cal*Card*"\n      PRINT "Nah..."\n      POINTS -5\n    ELSE\n      POINTS 1\n  ELSE\n    POINTS 3\nELSE\n  POINTS MAX\n  PRINT "Oh, Yeahhh!"\n\nPRINT "State Your Latest Wares (3 lines)"\nASK CR " [1]: "\nASK CR " [2]: "\nASK CR " [3]: "\n\nIF POINTS EQUAL MAX\n  SHOW "bbs:Screens/Yeppo.txt"\n  ACCESS 20\nELSE\n  IF POINTS NOT MORE 5\n    PRINT "You Are a Fucking Asshole Dude!"\n    KICKASS\n\n_______________________________________________________________________________\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n                           Greetings & Personal Info\n_______________________________________________________________________________\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n  Hellos go in no particular order to the following people:\n\n     Diogenes      awesome *original* idea\n     NightProwler  initial beta-testing and ideas\n     Muad''Dib      your reps were AMAZING! ;)\n     Tarzan        sorry for neverending leeching\n     Neil          hope to see you back one day\n     Gorefest\n     Morphus\n     Lightning\n     Rebel\n     Empire        i love your doors\n     Hornet\n\n  And all Delight members worldwide...\n\n\n  I can be reached on these great systems:\n    The Plastic Passion: +45-98238413\n    The Undiscovered:    +31-22944442\n\n  or on my own board\n    The Kremlin:      +7-(0)951255867\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,32872,7,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048479);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dlt_nw10','DLT-NW10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DLT-NW10.LHA',NULL,'XIM','__    ____  _     _',NULL,NULL,'DLT','CR/\ZE aND!       /\_\ __\ __________________  \/_/  ____________/\____ ____ _ / __  /  /_____  / ____/  /  /·  _ /',replace('                     __    ____  _     _    \n  CR/\ZE aND!       /\_\ __\                \n__________________  \/_/  ____________/\____\n ____ _ / __  /  /_____  / ____/  /  /·  _ /\n /  / //  ___/  /  /   \/  /  /     //   \/ \n/____ /_____/_____/_____\___ /__/__/______\.\nSk¡n\/---------- PRESENTS -\/--------------+\n(« nEW uSERS! v1.0 - cOOL! © nIKE/cRZ^dLT »)\n+------------------------------------------+\n------------------------------>[a·bAsE]<----\n','\n',char(10)),'NewUsers.Doc',replace('    ___________   ____________   _________      ___________    _____________\n.___\___      /_._\_____     /___\______  \ ____\_____    /____\___        /\n|      /_____/  |    _|/   _/__      _____ \      _______/____ ___/       /_\n|    _/         |    \        /      \      \     \          / __________/  \\n|_______________|_____\      /________\      \______________/________________\\n-mNt/aC!               \____/          \______\\n\n                                     &\n                  _     _ ___       ___\n                            /_  __ /__/\ _\n _ ___________________________     \__\/    _____________¦_________/\______\n ________   _ /  ___    /o   /___________  /·  ______/   |   \ _      o _ /\n __/    /   //    _____//   /    /       \//   /    /         \/       \\/\n  /________ /________ /_________/_________\_______ /_____|_____\_________\\n  \_______\/\_______\/\_________\____ ____/______\/\_____¦_____/_________/\n           \/        \/              Y.           \/     ·            Sk¡n\n                                     :o\n                                    +.\n\n                     Presents another /X^S!X^F!X Door\n\n                      -^(· NewUsers v1.1 by Nike ·)^-\n\nDescription:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\nListing new users on the board!\n\nFeatures:\n~~~~~~~~~\n* Door! Instead of the usual listers you''ll have to run in you''re logoff!\n* East to use!\n* Fast installation!\n* Speed is pretty ok!\n\nInstallation:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nUnarchive the file "NEWUSERS.LHA" to Ram: and start the installation proggy\nI''ve added to the main archive. This will do almost all the work!\n\nProgram History:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nV1.0 - First Release Ever!\n\nContact nIKE?!\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nCall INSTANT PLEASURE (+46-510-27660) or leave a message to any CRAZE or DELIGHT\nmember and tell them to contact me. (My board has a NUP installed, so u should\nbetter get that first! =)).\nIf you want a door personally designed or have some ideas etc for doors, then\nu should contact me! I don''t charge anything for the doors..\nAlthough u could give me a card or support my board or something =)..\n\nGreetings:\n~~~~~~~~~~\n     (« aLL cRAZE ^ dELIGHT mEMBERS! · bOBO/mYSTIC · xERXES/fLT^mST »)\n    (« vEDDER/iNS · dANSKEN · aGAMEMNON/m22 · rIOTER/eQX · lOGiC/rBS »)\n  (« zCANDALER!/dPL · dR.dRE!/tRSi · aQUARIUS/oTL · sAVAGE/iNS · lOUIE/iNS »)\n (« kID cURRY/cLS · jUAN/tRSi · bOROMIR/tRSi · oRG*/x-TRADE · cYBERTRON/aFL »)\n (« eXIDOR · lUSSAR''N/rEBELS · mANTA/aC · dISC · hIJACKER/cLS · cASCADE/aFL »)\n (« uFO/oRIENT · aLL tHE oTHER fELLA''S i''VE fORGOT iN tHIS sHITTY dOC fILE! »)\n\n==============================================================================\n       And also ! Don`t forget to give these DELIGHT boards a ring !\n==============================================================================\n            CHAOTIC ENTITY   *WHQ*  +1 610 489 5783  [Ringdown]\n            DOOM OF EXTASY   *EHQ*  +49 PRIVATE !!!  [Ringdown]\n            TOWER OF BABYLON *GHQ*  +49 PRIVATE !!!  [Ringdown]\n            UNDERCOVER       *SHQ*  +46 8 540 23405  [2 Nodes!]\n            DAWN RAID        *UKHQ* +44 707 320 320  [Ringdown]\n            THE UNDISCOVERED *DHQ*  +31 229 444 42   [2 Nodes!]\n            EUROPES CHAOS    *DST*  +49 461 311 458  [1 Node! ]\n            THE KREMLIN      *DST*  +7  951 255 867  [1 Node! ]\n==============================================================================\n                     AND OF COURSE THESE CRAZE BOARDS\n==============================================================================\n            INSTANT PLEASURE *WHQ*  +46 TOO ELITE!!  [1 Node! ]\n            CYBER FORCE      *SHQ*  +46 510   26683  [1 Node! ]\n            ALTERED STATE    *SHQ*  +46 TOO ELITE!!  [2 Nodes!]\n            NUCLEAR WASTE    *DST*  +46 510   27173  [1 Node! ]\n==============================================================================\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,7450,4,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048479);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dlt_ul11','DLT-UL11.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DLT-UL11.LHA','userlist','XIM','userlist',NULL,NULL,'DLT','CR/\ZE aND!       /\_\ __\ __________________  \/_/  ____________/\____ ____ _ / __  /  /_____  / ____/  /  /·  _ /',replace('                     __    ____  _     _\n  CR/\ZE aND!       /\_\ __\\n__________________  \/_/  ____________/\____\n ____ _ / __  /  /_____  / ____/  /  /·  _ /\n /  / //  ___/  /  /   \/  /  /     //   \/\n/____ /_____/_____/_____\___ /__/__/______\.\nSk¡n\/---------- PRESENTS -\/--------------+\n(« uSER lIST v1.1 - uPDATE © nIKE/cRZ^dLT »)\n+------------------------------------------+\n','\n',char(10)),'Userlist.Doc',replace('    ___________   ____________   _________      ___________    _____________\n.___\___      /_._\_____     /___\______  \ ____\_____    /____\___        /\n|      /_____/  |    _|/   _/__      _____ \      _______/____ ___/       /_\n|    _/         |    \        /      \      \     \          / __________/  \\n|_______________|_____\      /________\      \______________/________________\\n-mNt/aC!               \____/          \______\\n\n                                     &\n                  _     _ ___       ___\n                            /_  __ /__/\ _\n _ ___________________________     \__\/    _____________¦_________/\______\n ________   _ /  ___    /o   /___________  /·  ______/   |   \ _      o _ /\n __/    /   //    _____//   /    /       \//   /    /         \/       \\/\n  /________ /________ /_________/_________\_______ /_____|_____\_________\\n  \_______\/\_______\/\_________\____ ____/______\/\_____¦_____/_________/\n           \/        \/              Y.           \/     ·            Sk¡n\n                                     :o\n                                    +.\n\n                     ==)> Presents 2 ya in 1994! <(==\n\n                        -^(· User-List v1.0b ·)^-\n\nIntroduction:\n=============\nUserlister. Some new (?) options like Zippy search not found in other\ndoors (i think?)..\n\no Zippy Search for a user with Real Wildcards.\no "Realtime" userlisting instead of running another utility in your logoff\n  batch.\no Fast enuff\no Cool enuff (?)\no etc.\n\nInstallation:\n=============\nCopy the files as they are when u unpacked the archive.\n\nContact nIKE?!\n==============\nCall INSTANT PLEASURE (+46-510-27660) or leave a message to any CRAZE or DELIGHT\nmember and tell them to contact me. (My board has a NUP installed, so u should\nbetter get that first! =)).\nIf you want a door personally designed or have some ideas etc for doors, then\nu should contact me! I don''t charge anything for the doors..\nAlthough u could give me a card or support my board or something =)..\n\nHistory:\n========\nv1.0    - This version.\nv1.0b   - Fixed some few internal screwups, and made a real wildcard\n          search instead of a lame "*" wildcard option that wasn''t too good.\n\nGreetings:\n==========\n     (« aLL cRAZE ^ dELIGHT mEMBERS! · bOBO/mYSTIC · xERXES/fLT^mST »)\n    (« vEDDER/iNS · dANSKEN · aGAMEMNON/m22 · rIOTER/eQX · lOGiC/rBS »)\n  (« zCANDALER!/dPL · dR.dRE!/tRSi · aQUARIUS/oTL · sAVAGE/iNS · lOUIE/iNS »)\n (« kID cURRY/cLS · jUAN/tRSi · bOROMIR/tRSi · oRG*/x-TRADE · cYBERTRON/aFL »)\n (« eXIDOR · lUSSAR''N/rEBELS · mANTA/aC · dISC · hIJACKER/cLS · cASCADE/aFL »)\n (« uFO/oRIENT · aLL tHE oTHER fELLA''S i''VE fORGOT iN tHIS sHITTY dOC fILE! »)\n\nSince everybody else write like "musical support" and shit, i''ll write it too!\n==============================================================================\n             NiRVANA ^ GREEN DAY ^ VARiOUS MODULES ^ PEARL JAM\n==============================================================================\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',35900,4,0,NULL,NULL,'dlt_ul11','scan',1780048479);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dlt_wall','DLT-WALL.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DLT-WALL.LHA',NULL,'XIM','rexxsyslib.library',NULL,NULL,'DLT','\____ \_______   /\ /__\______  \  \   ___\| |/  /  /  ___/  /__X    \  \_ \     \  \  /| /_____/_____/_____/______\_____\__\__\__\/ |',replace('_/\____/\______/\_sCn__/\________/\_____/\_.\n\____ \_______   /\ /__\______  \  \   ___\|\n|/  /  /  ___/  /__X    \  \_ \     \  \  /|\n/_____/_____/_____/______\_____\__\__\__\/ |\n\     \     \     \      /     /  /  /  /  |\n|\     \     \     \    /     /  /  /  /   |\n|----wALL-dOOR-v.1.o-bY-vASCAL/dELIGHT!----|\nl__________________________________________j\n','\n',char(10)),'WALL.DOC',replace('                                    /\                .__\n    ___________________________    /  \_______________|  \_____________\n    \         \          /    /___/    \          /   |   \    __     /\n     \______   \   ___  /__  /    \____/_____    /_   |    \    \    /\n      |    /    \  \   /  / /     |    |   _/___/ |   _     \    \__/\n      |         /        /        |    |   \      |   |      \    \\n      |________/\_______/\_______/|____|\___.     |___|      /_____\\n                                            |_____|D! |_____/\n                           \n                ->  SYSTEM INFO V 2.1 BY VASCAL/DELIGHT  <-\n              -> BREAK AWAY BBS +49-471-503758 DELIGHT EHQ <-\n                       -> RELEASE DATE IS 05-22-94 <-\n       \n  \n  \nPurpose:\n~~~~~~~~\n        This is just another WALL DOOR that simply does\n        what all the other wall doors do as well but this\n        one seems to be a little shorter and better to \n        configurate ? Who knows ....\n\n \nRequirement:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\n        Any Amiga Modell\n        Any Amiexpress version\n        Any Workbench Version\n \n \nInstallation:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n        Make sure RPSTART is started. Copy all files into the dirs\n        they are supported from me. Now there is a file called \n        wall.dat in the DOORS:WALL directory. This file contains\n        15 lines. When you want the wall to show 10 lines then\n        just delete 5 of `em or if you want the wall to have 20\n        lines then just add 5 more - that`s how you define the\n        number of lines of the wall and I think tehre is no more\n        to configure .\n\n\n\n\n        AMIEX V1.XX :\n                     Install the same way described in the AMIEX V2.XX \n                     Section.\n \n        AMIEX V2.XX :\n                     ADD to your bbs:commands/CustomCommands\n\n---------------( cut here )-------------------\n\n*WALL      RM050DOORS:WALL/WALL\n\n---------------( cut here )-------------------\n\n        AMIEX V3.XX :\n                     Simply move the ICON WALL.INFO              \n                     to your BBS:COMMANDS/BBSCMD directory.\n   \n        \n   \nHistory:\n~~~~~~~~\n        V1.0: First release\n \n \nBugreport:\n~~~~~~~~~~\n        If you find any bugs in this Util contact me (VASCAL) under    \n        my account "VASCAL & SCAN" on any BBS you think I am on,\n        YOU CAN NOT RECH ME UNDER THE BREAK AWAY ANYMORE DUE IT WAS\n        BUSTED ... buhuuuuuuuu :-(\n\n\n          \nDisclaimer:\n~~~~~~~~~~~\n        This DOOR is CALLWARE that means if you install it then you have  \n        to give me a dizzy on your bbs hehehe 8-)\n  \n  \n  \n       \nGreets:\n~~~~~~~ First I great all the delight members, espacially SLICK and   \n        BLACKBIRD and SDD. Stay as you are dudes .\n        SLICK -> bist du im Urlaub ?\n        BLACKBIRD -> Yo u see I`m not 100% dead ...\n        NOOKMAN -> Ich call dich man am Wochenende\n        MCI -> Ich hab deine nummer nicht mehr ..\n\n        And the rest -> c u ..\n\n\n\nLast words:\n~~~~~~~~~~~\n        This door is an AREXX door but it is pretty fast - even on an \n        easy 68000. If you don`t think so just buy an 680X0 and don`t\n        blame me !\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',46511,2,0,NULL,NULL,'dlt_wall','scan',1780048479);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dlt_who','DLT-WHO.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DLT-WHO.LHA',NULL,'XIM','rexxsyslib.library',NULL,NULL,'DLT','\____ \_______   /\ /__\______  \  \   ___\| |/  /  /  ___/  /__X    \  \_ \     \  \  /| /_____/_____/_____/______\_____\__\__\__\/ |',replace('_/\____/\______/\_sCn__/\________/\_____/\_.\n\____ \_______   /\ /__\______  \  \   ___\|\n|/  /  /  ___/  /__X    \  \_ \     \  \  /|\n/_____/_____/_____/______\_____\__\__\__\/ |\n\     \     \     \      /     /  /  /  /  |\n|\     \     \     \    /     /  /  /  /   |\n|-[-wHO-dOOR-v1.o-bY-vASCAL/dELIGHT-1994-]-|\nl__________________________________________j\n','\n',char(10)),'WHO.DOC',replace('                                    /\                .__\n    ___________________________    /  \_______________|  \_____________\n    \         \          /    /___/    \          /   |   \    __     /\n     \______   \   ___  /__  /    \____/_____    /_   |    \    \    /\n      |    /    \  \   /  / /     |    |   _/___/ |   _     \    \__/\n      |         /        /        |    |   \      |   |      \    \\n      |________/\_______/\_______/|____|\___.     |___|      /_____\\n                                            |_____|D! |_____/\n                           \n                ->  WALL DOOR  V 2.1 BY VASCAL/DELIGHT  <-\n                       -> RELEASE DATE IS 05-24-94 <-\n       \n  \n  \nPurpose:\n~~~~~~~~\n        This door shows you wwhich nodes are active and who \n        else is online on that nodes. It also shows you ( the\n        user / caller ) what the guy on the other node is doing\n        at the moment.\n \nRequirement:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\n        Any Amiga Modell\n        Any Amiexpress version\n        Any Workbench Version\n \n \nInstallation:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n        Make sure RPSTART is started. Copy all files into the dirs\n        they are supported from me.                            \n\n\n\n        AMIEX V1.XX :\n                     Install the same way described in the AMIEX V2.XX \n                     Section.\n \n        AMIEX V2.XX :\n                     ADD to your bbs:commands/CustomCommands\n\n---------------( cut here )-------------------\n\n*WHO       RM050DOORS:WHO/WHO\n\n---------------( cut here )-------------------\n\n        AMIEX V3.XX :\n                     Simply move the ICON WHO.INFO              \n                     to your BBS:COMMANDS/BBSCMD directory.\n   \n        \n   \nHistory:\n~~~~~~~~\n        V1.0: First release\n \n \nBugreport:\n~~~~~~~~~~\n        If you find any bugs in this Util contact me (VASCAL) under    \n        my account "VASCAL & SCAN" on any BBS you think I am on,\n        YOU CAN NOT RECH ME UNDER THE BREAK AWAY ANYMORE DUE IT WAS\n        BUSTED ... buhuuuuuuuu :-(\n\n\n          \nDisclaimer:\n~~~~~~~~~~~\n        This DOOR is CALLWARE that means if you install it then you have  \n        to give me a dizzy on your bbs hehehe 8-)\n  \n  \n  \n       \nGreets:\n~~~~~~~ NO GREETZ IN THIS ONE.                                        \n\n\n\nLast words:\n~~~~~~~~~~~\n        This door is an AREXX door but it is pretty fast - even on an \n        easy 68000. If you don`t think so just buy an 680X0 and don`t\n        blame me !\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',48632,1,0,NULL,NULL,'dlt_who','scan',1780048479);
