Venger\n    Zendor - Mike - Luca - Abbe - Stuff - Broder - Zync - Zych - La Fayette\n     Axe - Nebraska - Eracore - Linus - Avalon - Nero - Dixy - Crux - Nuke\n   Fuze - Fix - Kain - Prospex - Canaima - Pripps - Hilbert - Mital - D-Zire\n        Jucke - Double - E-Go - Distler - Sy-Klone - Fazer - Zcandaler\n                  Beavis & Butthead - Renko - Juan - Guardian\n\nForgive me if I forgot someone. It''s not easy to remember everybody you know!\n\n[EOF]\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',59862,4,0,NULL,NULL,'dpl_ma10','scan',1780048488);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dpl_ma13','DPL_MA13.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DPL_MA13.LHA','Crunch','XIM','Crunch',NULL,'Tango/DPL','DPL','.\____ \   /   _____   /  /\___  \---------. |/   /  \ /   / ______/  /   \/   \        | /_______/___ /   / /   _/\________/  DUPLO |',replace(' ____/\_____/\___________________           \n.\____ \   /   _____   /  /\___  \---------.\n|/   /  \ /   / ______/  /   \/   \        |\n/_______/___ /   / /   _/\________/  DUPLO |\n|          \/__ / /_______\-Mo!            |\n¦-------------\/---------------------------¦\n|            P R E S E N T S :             |\n|        ModAdd v1.3, by Tango/DPL         |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'ModAdd.doc',replace('\n        .\n        :    :\n        :   /|\n        |  / | t A N G o                  _______\n        ._/  |___ _ ____________ _______ |      /_____________________\n       _ _   ___/____________   \     _ \|     /___________________   \\n        :    |     \      ______ \     \ \    / \______    |      |  . \_\n        :    l      \_    \    /  \_    \ \  /       |     |      ''     /\n      _ :_______     /_____\       /____|\  /______  `     |__________ /\n        |  -mNt\____/       \ ____/       \/      `--------''         \/\n        |                    \/                                      :\n        |                       o F   D U P L o                      |\n        |                                                            |\n        `---------------------- P R E S E N t S ----------------- - -''\n\n                                  ModAdd v1.3\n\n                             Idea by: The Big Byte\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                Important note!\n                               ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThis util is released under the concept of tradeware. If you like it and use\nit, upload some on my board. I will not take any responsability for whatever\nthis door does with your computer (It wont do anything but what it should, but\nyou never know what those lamers do!).\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                 What it does!\n                                ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThis /X-door/util will let you add strings of text to the samplenames in a\nmodule!\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                            Why use this one then!\n                           ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nWell, have you seen an util like this before? I''ve never seen one that can\nhandle both "*.mod" and "mod.*" files, but this one! If you want it to handle\nboth, it has to be installed as FILECHECK door, but can also be used as a\nstandard filecheck door for "*.mod" files.\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                 Installation!\n                                ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nIf you run /X 3.x, copy all files I''ve supplied and your set.\n\nIf you run /X 2.x or S-Express, insert the followin line to your\n"commands/sys.cmd" file.\n\n---( cut )---\nFILECHECK XM010DOORS:ModAdd/ModAdd.x\n---( cut )---\n\nIf you want to use it as a standard filechecker, you have to figure out how to\nistall it by yourself. The really big advantage with this program is if you use\nit as a FILECHECK door.\n\nHowever, either one of the above you choose, you must now edit your configfile!\nIt should be named "DOORS:ModAdd/ModAdd.cfg" and can ceep the following\noptions.\n\nCOMPRESS - This keyword tells the adder to compress the files with PowerPacker.\n           If this is going to work, you need "Libs:powerpacker.library" and\n           "C:crunch" available.\nXPK      - This tells the adder to decrunch XPK modules before adding to them!\nPP       - This tells the adder to decrunch PP modules before adding to them!\n           The two options above needs all libraries except "asl.library" and\n           "C:xup" to work!\n\nThe rest of the lines in the configfile should be the lines to add.\n"30-Total Inferno" means that the adder should add "Total Inferno" to\nsamplename nr. 30. Don''t forget the "-" between samplenr and the addstring, and\ndon''t try samplenr''s above 31, coz it wont work! :)\n\nIf you wish to use this util from SHELL, there are two ways. If ModAdd is\ncalled without options, it put''s up an asl-requester, with wich you can select\nmodules to add to. Otherwise, it can be run with "ModAdd.x a <modulename>" to\nadd to the module called <modulename>. I hope you understand how to put it in\n"BBS:FCheck" now.\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                 These are the ß-sites for all my doors/utils!\n                ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n           Disorder               Marwin             ++46-456-27511\n           Forbidden Dreams       Manta              ++46-411-12894\n           Total Inferno          Tango              ++46-42-234164\n           Twisted Society        The Big Byte       ++46-44-106144\n\nAll my utils should be free dl, otherwise tell me and I''ll kick that ß-tester.\nIf you want to ß-test my doors/utils, contact me and we''ll work something out.\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                  Greetings!\n                                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~\n    Melone - Krusty - Hoot - Marwin - Manta - The Big Byte - Norad - Venger\n    Zendor - Mike - Luca - Abbe - Stuff - Broder - Zync - Zych - La Fayette\n     Axe - Nebraska - Eracore - Linus - Avalon - Nero - Dixy - Crux - Nuke\n   Fuze - Fix - Kain - Prospex - Canaima - Pripps - Hilbert - Mital - D-Zire\n                  Jucke - Double - E-Go - Distler - Sy-Klone\n\nForgive me if I forgot someone. It''s not easy to remember everybody you know!\n\n[EOF]\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',90495,6,0,NULL,NULL,'dpl_ma13','scan',1780048488);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dpl_mc10','DPL_MC10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DPL_MC10.LHA','MessClean','XIM','LE-win5-96.exe',NULL,'Tango/DPL','DPL','.\____ \   /   _____   /  /\___  \---------. |/   /  \ /   / ______/  /   \/   \        | /_______/___ /   / /   _/\________/  DUPLO |',replace(' ____/\_____/\___________________\n.\____ \   /   _____   /  /\___  \---------.\n|/   /  \ /   / ______/  /   \/   \        |\n/_______/___ /   / /   _/\________/  DUPLO |\n|          \/__ / /_______\-Mo!            |\n¦-------------\/---------------------------¦\n|             PRESENTS ToDAY:              |\n|      MessClean v1.0 - by Tango/DPL       |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'MessClean.doc',replace('\n                                MessClean v1.0\n\n                       Another great util by Tango/DPL!\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n                              1. Prologue\n                              2. History\n                              3. Dox\n                              4. Next version(s)\n                              5. Greets\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n                                  1. Prologue\n                                  ~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nThe only reason why I made this litle util is that I, and many other sysops\nwith me are fed up with all these old recieved messages lying around the HD!\nThis util sets an end to those messages!\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n                                  2. History\n                                  ~~~~~~~~~~\nv1.0 - First version. Simply removed all recieved messages!\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n                                    3. Dox\n                                    ~~~~~~\nThis program is really simple to use!\n\nMessClean <Conf>\n\nis the only thing you need to write.\n\nEx.   MessClean BBS:Conf1\n\nRun it once every logoff or once a week or whatever! It removes all\nrecieved messages permanently, both from the HeaderFile and the dir.\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n                              4. Next version(s)\n                              ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nFor the future versions I''ve planned the following:\n\n* Deletion of all EALL/ALL messages after a given period.\n* Compression & optimizion of the HeaderFile. (Faster Mailscan!)\n* Charging of users. You can charge a user with 10kb for every letter he''s \n  forgot!\n\nIf you have any aditional features you think would be useful! Please contact me \non my board, Total Inferno, at ++46-42-234164.\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n                                   5. Greets\n                                   ~~~~~~~~~\nMy best wishes goes to the following dudes!\n\nAxe, Melone, Marwin, Krusty, Fix, Venger, Viper, Deathwish, The Big Byte, \nCateye, Luca, Double, Kain, Nebraska, Manta, Skin, and everybody else i know!\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',17565,6,0,NULL,NULL,'dpl_mc10','scan',1780048488);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dpl_mc11','DPL-MC11.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DPL-MC11.LHA','MessClean','XIM','MessClean',NULL,NULL,'DPL','.\____ \   /   _____   /  /\___  \---------. |/   /  \ /   / ______/  /   \/   \        | /_______/___ /   / /   _/\________/  DUPLO |',replace(' ____/\_____/\___________________           \n.\____ \   /   _____   /  /\___  \---------.\n|/   /  \ /   / ______/  /   \/   \        |\n/_______/___ /   / /   _/\________/  DUPLO |\n|          \/__ / /_______\-Mo!            |\n¦-------------\/---------------------------¦\n|            P R E S E N T S :             |\n|              MessClean v1.1              |\n|  The update we''ve all been waiting for!  |\n|   Now with ALL/EALL deletion, MsgBase    |\n|             compression etc!             |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'MessClean.doc',replace('\n        .\n        :    :\n        :   /|\n        |  / | t A N G o                  _______\n        ._/  |___ _ ____________ _______ |      /_____________________\n       _ _   ___/____________   \     _ \|     /___________________   \\n        :    |     \      ______ \     \ \    / \______    |      |  . \_\n        :    l      \_    \    /  \_    \ \  /       |     |      ''     /\n      _ :_______     /_____\       /____|\  /______  `     |__________ /\n        |  -mNt\____/       \ ____/       \/      `--------''         \/\n        |                    \/                                      :\n        |                       o F   D U P L o                      |\n        |                                                            |\n        `---------------------- P R E S E N t S ----------------- - -''\n\n                                MessClean v1.1\n\n                                 Idea by: Me!\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                Important note!\n                               ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThis util is released under the concept of tradeware. If you like it and use\nit, upload some on my board. I will not take any responsability for whatever\nthis door does with your computer (It wont do anything but what it should, but\nyou never know what those lamers do!).\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                 What it does!\n                                ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThis litle util cleans up your messagebase. Some sysops, including myself\nthinks it''s alot extra work to clean up the messagebases, so I made this litle\nutil to do the job for you.\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                               Why use thisone!\n                              ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nWell, for starters, it''s the only one I know of that does the job nice and\neasy. JH made one once, but it''s quite anoying to use, so I made this, and it\nworx gr8!\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                   History!\n                                  ~~~~~~~~~~\nV1.0 - Had the ability to strip messages that users had forgotten to delete\n       after recieve. Many sysops wants their HD clean from such shit,\n       including me. :)\nV1.1 - Totally rewritten, as I thought my old source was to complicated. This\n       MUST be even quicker! :)\n       Added the ability to compress the messagebase in an /X friendly way. I''m\n       by this not saying that all utils will work, coz I don''t know how\n       they''re written, but /X don''t complain. It depends on how the utils\n       handle the msgbase. If you run a netmail util other than /X-Net, don''t\n       run this util with the compress option on those confs.\n       Also added the ability to remove ALL/EALL messages when they get to old.\n       Added a MsgDate fix. Some utils post messages with a date way beyond the\n       real date. This is because the authors of these utils don''t know how to\n       get the date in /X format, so they put a 0 in that field. However, this\n       util fixes these messages and puts todays date on em, so you can be able\n       to use the ALL/EALL deleter. Fex WeekTop v1.0 wich I run, sets the date\n       to 0 and all these messages will be deleted if you don''t use the\n       fix-option.\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                    Usage!\n                                   ~~~~~~~~\nThis util should be run from SHELL or some batchfile only! It''s NOT an /X-door!\n\nUsage template:\n\nMessClean <ConfPath> [ALL=DAYS] [COMPRESS] [FIX]\n\nWell, not hard. ConfPath should be the path to the conference you wish to\nprocess, ie. "BBS:Conf1" or whatever.\n\nALL=DAYS is the ALL/EALL deletion. If you enter "ALL=5", all ALL/EALL messages\nolder than 5 days will be nuked! Watch it here! Some lame utils don''t write the\nright date when posting messages. Check it out before using this.\n\nIf the keyword COMPRESS is written, the util will compress the MsgBase as\nmentioned above. It''s not very advanced, but will strip your HeaderFile and\nspeed up msgscanning alot for users who hasn''t scanned in a long time, ie\nnewusers.\n\nIf the keyword FIX is written, the util will put the current time on all\nmessages with illegal time in the timefield. This will prevent ALL/EALL delete\nfrom deleting them instantly!\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                 These are the ß-sites for all my doors/utils!\n                ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n       Altered State Asylum #1       Juan               ++46-317-759378\n       Altered State Asylum #2       Juan               ++46-317-759376\n       Disorder                      Marwin             ++46-456-27511\n       Forbidden Dreams              Manta              ++46-411-12894\n       Total Inferno                 Tango              ++46-42-234164\n       Twisted Society               The Big Byte       ++46-44-106144\n\nAll my utils should be free dl, otherwise tell me and I''ll kick that ß-tester.\nIf you want to ß-test my doors/utils, contact me and we''ll work something out.\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                  Greetings!\n                                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~\n    Melone - Krusty - Hoot - Marwin - Manta - The Big Byte - Norad - Venger\n    Zendor - Mike - Luca - Abbe - Stuff - Broder - Zync - Zych - La Fayette\n     Axe - Nebraska - Eracore - Linus - Avalon - Nero - Dixy - Crux - Nuke\n   Fuze - Fix - Kain - Prospex - Canaima - Pripps - Hilbert - Mital - D-Zire\n         Jucke - Double - E-Go - Distler - Sy-Klone - Juan - Guardian\n\nForgive me if I forgot someone. It''s not easy to remember everybody you know!\n\n[EOF]\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',19572,10,0,NULL,NULL,'dpl_mc11','scan',1780048488);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dpl_mc12','DPL-MC12.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DPL-MC12.LHA','MessClean','XIM','MessClean',NULL,'All/Eall','DPL','.\____ \   /   _____   /  /\___  \---------. |/   /  \ /   / ______/  /   \/   \        | /_______/___ /   / /   _/\________/  DUPLO |',replace(' ____/\_____/\___________________           \n.\____ \   /   _____   /  /\___  \---------.\n|/   /  \ /   / ______/  /   \/   \        |\n/_______/___ /   / /   _/\________/  DUPLO |\n|          \/__ / /_______\-Mo!            |\n¦-------------\/---------------------------¦\n|            P R E S E N T S :             |\n|              MessClean v1.2              |\n|     Featuring, old message, All/Eall     |\n|    deletion, datebug fix and MsgBase     |\n|               compression.               |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'MessClean.doc',replace('\n        .\n        :    :\n        :   /|\n        |  / | t A N G o                  _______\n        ._/  |___ _ ____________ _______ |      /_____________________\n       _ _   ___/____________   \     _ \|     /___________________   \\n        :    |     \      ______ \     \ \    / \______    |      |  . \_\n        :    l      \_    \    /  \_    \ \  /       |     |      ''     /\n      _ :_______     /_____\       /____|\  /______  `     |__________ /\n        |  -mNt\____/       \ ____/       \/      `--------''         \/\n        |                    \/                                      :\n        |                       o F   D U P L o                      |\n        |                                                            |\n        `---------------------- P R E S E N t S ----------------- - -''\n\n                                MessClean v1.2\n\n                                 Idea by: Me!\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                Important note!\n                               ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThis util is released under the concept of tradeware. If you like it and use\nit, upload some on my board. I will not take any responsability for whatever\nthis door does with your computer (It wont do anything but what it should, but\nyou never know what those lamers do!).\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                 What it does!\n                                ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThis litle util cleans up your messagebase. Some sysops, including myself\nthinks it''s alot extra work to clean up the messagebases, so I made this litle\nutil to do the job for you.\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                               Why use thisone!\n                              ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nWell, for starters, it''s the only one I know of that does the job nice and\neasy. JH made one once, but it''s quite anoying to use, so I made this, and it\nworx gr8!\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                   History!\n                                  ~~~~~~~~~~\nV1.0 - Had the ability to strip messages that users had forgotten to delete\n       after recieve. Many sysops wants their HD clean from such shit,\n       including me. :)\nV1.1 - Totally rewritten, as I thought my old source was to complicated. This\n       MUST be even quicker! :)\n       Added the ability to compress the messagebase in an /X friendly way. I''m\n       by this not saying that all utils will work, coz I don''t know how\n       they''re written, but /X don''t complain. It depends on how the utils\n       handle the msgbase. If you run a netmail util other than /X-Net, don''t\n       run this util with the compress option on those confs.\n       Also added the ability to remove ALL/EALL messages when they get to old.\n       Added a MsgDate fix. Some utils post messages with a date way beyond the\n       real date. This is because the authors of these utils don''t know how to\n       get the date in /X format, so they put a 0 in that field. However, this\n       util fixes these messages and puts todays date on em, so you can be able\n       to use the ALL/EALL deleter. Fex WeekTop v1.0 wich I run, sets the date\n       to 0 and all these messages will be deleted if you don''t use the\n       fix-option.\nv1.2 - Added the ability to delete old messages, fex if a user wrote a message\n       to another 3 months ago and he never called again, etc. Rewrote the util\n       from scratch to increase the speed. Now all compression, deletion etc is\n       made in memory, giving the program a speed boost.\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                    Usage!\n                                   ~~~~~~~~\nThis util should be run from SHELL or some batchfile only! It''s NOT an /X-door!\n\nUsage template:\n\nMessClean <ConfPath> [ALL=DAYS] [OLD=DAYS] [COMPRESS] [FIX]\n\nWell, not hard. ConfPath should be the path to the conference you wish to\nprocess, ie. "BBS:Conf1" or whatever.\n\nRunning MessClean without any other args than the ConfPath simply deletes all\nrecieved messages from the messagebase.\n\nALL=DAYS is the ALL/EALL deletion. If you enter "ALL=5", all ALL/EALL messages\nolder than 5 days will be nuked! Watch it here! Some lame utils don''t write the\nright date when posting messages. Check it out before using this.\n\nOLD=DAYS let''s you delete messages after a period of time wether they''re\nrecieved ore not. "OLD=60" deletes messages after 60 days if they don''t get\nrecieved.\n\nIf the keyword COMPRESS is written, the util will compress the MsgBase as\nmentioned above. It''s not very advanced, but will strip your HeaderFile and\nspeed up msgscanning alot for users who hasn''t scanned in a long time, ie\nnewusers.\n\nIf the keyword FIX is written, the util will put the current time on all\nmessages with illegal time in the timefield. This will prevent ALL/EALL delete\nfrom deleting them instantly!\n\nNOTE! Unlike the lame attempt by Joseph Hodge to archive this, this util should\nbe able to be run when a user''s online. It locks the messagebase just like /X.\nIn fact I ripped these routines from the source of /X! :)\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                 These are the ß-sites for all my doors/utils!\n                ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n       Asylum Altered State #1       Juan               ++46-317-759378\n       Asylum Altered State #2       Juan               ++46-317-759376\n       Disorder                      Marwin             ++46-456-27511\n       Imagine                       Rille              ++46-42-135505\n       Total Inferno                 Tango              ++46-42-234164\n       Twisted Society               The Big Byte       ++46-44-106144\n\nAll my utils should be free dl, otherwise tell me and I''ll kick that ß-tester.\nIf you want to ß-test my doors/utils, contact me and we''ll work something out.\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                  Greetings!\n                                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~\n    Melone - Krusty - Hoot - Marwin - Manta - The Big Byte - Norad - Venger\n    Zendor - Mike - Luca - Abbe - Stuff - Broder - Zync - Zych - La Fayette\n     Axe - Nebraska - Eracore - Linus - Avalon - Nero - Dixy - Crux - Nuke\n   Fuze - Fix - Kain - Prospex - Canaima - Pripps - Hilbert - Mital - D-Zire\n        Jucke - Double - E-Go - Distler - Sy-Klone - Fazer - Zcandaler\n   Beavis & Butthead - Renko - Juan - Guardian - EaSy RiDeR - Wozzy - Suggs\n                            Rille - Fonus - Proctor\n\nForgive me if I forgot someone. It''s not easy to remember everybody you know!\n\n[EOF]\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',13705,2,0,NULL,NULL,'dpl_mc12','scan',1780048488);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dpl_mi10','DPL-MI10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DPL-MI10.LHA','ModInfo','XIM','LE-win5-96.exe',NULL,'Tango/DPL','DPL','.\____ \   /   _____   /  /\___  \---------. |/   /  \ /   / ______/  /   \/   \        | /_______/___ /   / /   _/\________/  DUPLO |',replace(' ____/\_____/\___________________           \n.\____ \   /   _____   /  /\___  \---------.\n|/   /  \ /   / ______/  /   \/   \        |\n/_______/___ /   / /   _/\________/  DUPLO |\n|          \/__ / /_______\-Mo!            |\n¦-------------\/---------------------------¦\n|            P R E S E N T S :             |\n|        ModInfo v1.0, by Tango/DPL        |\n| A moduleinfo util for your DOpus/DM/FM!  |\n`------------------------------------------''\n- -[ fLYING DRAGON ]- - -  --[ rEAL WHq ]- -\n','\n',char(10)),'lOSeNDOS.guide',replace('                   \n                     __  _ __  /\__ _  _ __/\  __ _  __\n                    _\/___   \/              \/   ___\/_\n              ......\/\  /........................\  /\/......\n             :         \/                          \/         :\n             :      .___             .___         .___        :\n             :   _ _|   \      ______|   \  ______|   \       :\n             :   \\\__   7___  \______   /  \__   ____/       :\n             :      /.   |   \__/.  l/   \___/_____   \__ _   :\n             :     /::.  |    _/::.       _/::.  l/    _///   :\n             :     \___________\___________\____________\     :\n             :___        .___        .___        .___         :___\n     _ ______|   \ ______|   \ ______|   \ ______|   \  ______|   \\n     \\\__   ____/ \______   / \______   / \______   /  \__   ____/\n        /.   ___|___/.   |   \__/.  _|   \__/.  l/   \___/_____   \__ _\n       /::.  l/   _/::.  |    _/::. \___  _/::.       _/::.  l/    _///\n       \_ _________\_____|_____\___________\___________\___________ \\n         Y   :                                                :[nM$]Y\n      .------''                                                `------.\n      :eXON/rIOT^jORMAS · gHANDY/gODS · rAHIEM/eSSENCE · cELIC/rEKTUM: \n      `------.                                                .------''\n             `------------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',17061,11,0,NULL,NULL,'dpl_mi10','scan',1780048488);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dpl_mv10','DPL_MV10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DPL_MV10.LHA','xup','XIM','LE-win5-96.exe',NULL,'Tango/DPL','DPL','.\____ \   /   _____   /  /\___  \---------. |/   /  \ /   / ______/  /   \/   \        | /_______/___ /   / /   _/\________/  DUPLO |',replace(' ____/\_____/\___________________           \n.\____ \   /   _____   /  /\___  \---------.\n|/   /  \ /   / ______/  /   \/   \        |\n/_______/___ /   / /   _/\________/  DUPLO |\n|          \/__ / /_______\-Mo!            |\n¦-------------\/---------------------------¦\n|            P R E S E N T S :             |\n|        ModView v1.0, by Tango/DPL        |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'ModView.doc',replace('\n        .\n        :    :\n        :   /|\n        |  / | t A N G o                  _______\n        ._/  |___ _ ____________ _______ |      /_____________________\n       _ _   ___/____________   \     _ \|     /___________________   \\n        :    |     \      ______ \     \ \    / \______    |      |  . \_\n        :    l      \_    \    /  \_    \ \  /       |     |      ''     /\n      _ :_______     /_____\       /____|\  /______  `     |__________ /\n        |  -mNt\____/       \ ____/       \/      `--------''         \/\n        |                    \/                                      :\n        |                       o F   D U P L o                      |\n        |                                                            |\n        `---------------------- P R E S E N t S ----------------- - -''\n\n                                 ModView v1.0\n\n                             Idea by: The Big Byte\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                Important note!\n                               ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThis util is released under the concept of tradeware. If you like it and use\nit, upload some on my board. I will not take any responsability for whatever\nthis door does with your computer (It wont do anything but what it should, but\nyou never know what those lamers do!).\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                 What it does!\n                                ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThis door displays some info about a choosen module!\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                            Why use this one then!\n                           ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nWell, it''s from me! :) I''ve seen many atempts to do this in my days as a sysop\nwith a module-area, but none have come up to my demands. This one does it''s job\nin a nice, quick way, and loox good too. You can even enter all modules you\nwanna show info about on the mainline, ie. "modview a.mod b.mod c.mod" and the\nviewer shows them one after the other.\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                 Installation!\n                                ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nIf you run /X 3.x, copy all files I''ve supplied and your set.\n\nIf you run /X 2.x or S-Express, insert the following line to your\n"commands/bbs.cmd" file.\n\n---( cut )---\nMODVIEW   XM020DOORS:ModView.x\n---( cut )---\n\nThe door needs all files in "c:" and "libs:" to run at it''s best, otherwise you\nwont be able to view XPK or PP modules. Sorry!\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                 These are the ß-sites for all my doors/utils!\n                ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n           Disorder               Marwin             ++46-456-27511\n           Forbidden Dreams       Manta              ++46-411-12894\n           Total Inferno          Tango              ++46-42-234164\n           Twisted Society        The Big Byte       ++46-44-106144\n\nAll my utils should be free dl, otherwise tell me and I''ll kick that ß-tester.\nIf you want to ß-test my doors/utils, contact me and we''ll work something out.\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                  Greetings!\n                                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~\n    Melone - Krusty - Hoot - Marwin - Manta - The Big Byte - Norad - Venger\n    Zendor - Mike - Luca - Abbe - Stuff - Broder - Zync - Zych - La Fayette\n     Axe - Nebraska - Eracore - Linus - Avalon - Nero - Dixy - Crux - Nuke\n   Fuze - Fix - Kain - Prospex - Canaima - Pripps - Hilbert - Mital - D-Zire\n                  Jucke - Double - E-Go - Distler - Sy-Klone\n\nForgive me if I forgot someone. It''s not easy to remember everybody you know!\n\n[EOF]\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',60864,6,0,NULL,NULL,'dpl_mv10','scan',1780048488);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dpl_n44f','DPL-N44F.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DPL-N44F.LHA',NULL,'XIM','Phreak.exe',NULL,'kAiN/dUPLO^dM0','DPL','....::::.....      :::: ::::.....  ....... :::: :::: :::: .....::::.:::· :::: :::: :::: ·:::.:::: :::: :::: ::::      :::: ·:::.:::·',replace('     ....           ........\n ....::::.....      :::: ::::.....  .......\n:::: :::: :::: .....::::.:::· :::: :::: ::::\n·:::.:::: :::: :::: ::::      :::: ·:::.:::·\n.-kRm-----·:::.:::·-----------::::... ..  .\n|\n|  NEW ORDER v4.40f - THE ASCii REQUESTER  ·\n|                                          :\n|      DEVELOPED BY kAiN/dUPLO^dM0 iN      ¦\n| CO-OPERATiON WiTH SOME OF THE BEST ASCii |\n|           ARTiSTS iN THE WORLD!          |\n|__________________________________________|\n','\n',char(10)),'NEWORDER.DOC',replace('\no----------------- -- -  -  -+( A DUPLO RELEASE )+-  -  - -- -----------------o\n|·                                                                           ·|\n|                                                                             |\n|                                                                             |\n|                                                                             |\n|                                                                             |\n¦                                                                             ¦\n¦                                                                             ¦\n:                                                                             :\n:                                                                             :\n.                                                                             .\n.                                                                             .\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n .---+( W E L C O M E · T O · T H E · D O C U M E N T A T i O N · F O R )+---.\n |°                                                    _ ______             °|\n |_________ ________ _____/\_   _________ ________   _____/___/_____ ________|\n \\______ ¬\______ ¬\__  / /¬\_ \__   _ ¬\______ ¬\_/   __________ ¬\______ ¬\_\n | /    /   /  \_____/  / /   /  /    /   /    /___/    /   /  \_____/    /___/\n |/    /   /    /   /    /   /  /    /   /    /   /    /   /    /   /    /   |\n /____/   /____    /____    /  /____    /____/_  /____    /____    /____/_   |\n |  /____/   /____/   /____/      /____/    /       /____/   /____/    /     |\n |                                                                           |\n ÷-----------------------+( V E R S i O N · 4 . 4 0 )+-----------------------÷\n |                                                                           |\n |        ··  o N E  ·  Features      ·  What Can NEW ORDER Do?    ··        |\n |        ··  T W o  ·  Credits       ·  Who Have Made NEW ORDER?  ··        |\n |        ··  THReE  ·  Installation  ·  How To Install NEW ORDER  ··        |\n |        ··  FoU R  ·  Operation     ·  How To Operate NEW ORDER  ··        |\n |        ··  F iVE  ·  Troubles      ·  Do You Have A Problem?    ··        |\n |        ··  S i X  ·  Greetings     ·  Greetings And Messages    ··        |\n |        ··  SEVEN  ·  Information   ·  Useless Information       ··        |\n |        ··  EiGHT  ·  The End!      ·  Some Final Words          ··        |\n |                                                                           |\n `---------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                                   Here\n\n                                    We\n\n                                    Go\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n ___ _ ____________________________________________:_\n|  _(_)_                                           |\n| (_(_)_) · no. oNE : fEATURES! ·              _ __|__________________________\n|___(_)______________________________________:_____|                          |\n                                             ¦       + nEW oRDER · v4.40f +   |\n                                             |________________________________|\n\n\n   Ok! Lets get To Business! New Order.. Hmm.. What Is It? First Of All,\n   It Is A Wonderful Popgroup! And Second, It Is A New Door By Kain!!\n   Oh Yeah, What About It? Kain Have Made Several Smashing Doors!?!?\n   Oh Yes I Have!! What Is So Special About This One Then?? Well, It Is\n   A Fully Working Ascii-Order Door! Better Than Every Other Released!\n\n   Just Check These Nice Features Out:\n\n   o  /X 3.x Design\n   o  Configured Via Icons.\n   o  Easy To Setup.\n   o  Makes Private Messages With The Orders To The Artist.\n   o  Artists Can Upload Their Asciis Through New Order.\n   o  New Order Put The File(s) In A Private Message To The Orderer.\n   o  It Can Put The File In Filelist For Public Download.\n      (This Is Up To The Artist, And Is Asked For Every Uled File.)\n   o  Uses Sent-By-Line In The Filelisting.\n      It Handles: SentBy V1.3 by LightSpeed Technologies (TCN)\n                  File Description (Version 1.0b) by Bobo/Mystic\n      It Will Probably Handle Later Versions Of These Programs Too.\n   o  Can Use Uploaded Ascii As Filedescription.\n   o  Coded In Arexx - NO Backdoors.\n   o  Goodlooking Design. (Thanks Karma)\n   o  Has Every Feature An Ascii-Artist Needs !!!!\n\n\n ___ _ ____________________________________________:_\n|  _(_)_                                           |\n| (_(_)_) · no. tWO : CREDiTS! ·               _ __|__________________________\n|___(_)______________________________________:_____|                          |\n                                             ¦       + nEW oRDER · v4.40f +   |\n                                             |________________________________|\n\n\n                                             _____\n          __________________________________/_ _ /__.__________/_______ _ _\n         /  __    / _____    /   ____/   .____\\\\__|   ___   /  _____////\n        /    /___/_  \   ___/   ___/__   |/    /    |    \___/____   \\n       /    /_     \  \    \    /_    \  /    /     |     \_/   _\    \\n      /_____________\__\    \__________\_____/______|______/___________\\n   .--------------------\____/dZG-------------------------/---------------.\n   |                                                                      |\n   |      Door                                                            |\n   |        Code       -  KAiN/DPL                                        |\n   |        Design     -  KAiN/DPL, KARMA/AL, DANZiG/AL                   |\n   |        Ideas      -  KAiN/DPL, KARMA,AL, DANZiG/AL, U-MAN/2kAD       |\n   |        Testing    -  KAiN/DPL, DANZiG/AL, KARMA/AL                   |\n   |                                                                      |\n   |      Docs                                                            |\n   |        Author     -  KAiN/DPL                                        |\n   |        Design     -  KARMA/AL, KAiN/DPL                              |\n   |        Ascii-art  -  KARMA/AL, DANZiG/AL, U-MAN/2kAD                 |\n   |                                                                      |\n   |   ----------------------------------------------------------------   |\n   |                                                                      |\n   |                      For Updates And Help Call                       |\n   |                                                                      |\n   |                  - Final Impact Or Serpent Hill -                    |\n   |                                                                      |\n   `----------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n\n ___ _ ____________________________________________:_\n|  _(_)_                                           |\n| (_(_)_) · no. tHREE : iNSTALLATiON! ·        _ __|__________________________\n|___(_)______________________________________:_____|                          |\n                                             ¦       + nEW oRDER · v4.40f +   |\n                                             |________________________________|\n\n\n  /X 2.xx Installation\n  ---------------------\n\n  - Register & Install /X 3.xx And Follow The /X 3.xx Installation !!\n\n  /X 3.xx Installation\n  ---------------------\n\n  - The New Order Dir Can Be Installed Wherever You Like But If You\n    Dont Install It In DOORS: Then You Must Add The PATH Tooltype To\n    Your BBS:Commands/BBSCmd/ORDER.info Icon. See Tooltypes Info !\n\n  - Anyway, Just Copy The NewOrder Directory And NEWORDER.info To DOORS:\n    (Or Wherever You Like To Install New Order!)\n\n  - Copy ORDER.info To BBS:Commands/BBScmd/ Or BBS:Commands/ConfXCmd/\n\n\n  Tooltypes For The NEWORDER.info\n  -------------------------------\n\n  ARTISTS=<num>           -  Number Of Artists That A User May Order From\n  ARTIST.<num>=<name>     -  Ascii-Artist''s Handle\n  COMMENT.<num>=<comment> -  Comment On The Artist (Group Etc...)\n  CONF=<conf-num>         -  Conference To Use (Your AsciiConference)\n\n  Tooltype For The BBS:Commands/BBSCmd/ORDER.info\n  -----------------------------------------------\n\n  PATH=<New Order Dir Path> - The Path Where You Keep Your New Order Dir.\n                              Note  If This Tooltype Is Not Set, New Order\n                              Will Use The DOORS: Directory.\n\n\n  Safety\n  ------\n\n  You Might Want To Make Backupcopies On:\n\n    CONF/MSGBASE/MAILSTATS\n    CONF/MSGBASE/HEADERFILE\n    CONF/DIRx (Your Upload-Dir-File)\n\n  Just As A Safety Precaution. These Are The Files That New Order Writes To.\n  Other System Files That New Order Uses Are (Read Only):\n\n    PATH/NEWORDER.info     -  To Read Which Conference To Use And To\n                              Get All Info On Artists.\n    BBS:CONFCONFIG.info    -  To Read Conference Path.\n    BBS:<CONF>.info        -  To Read What Dir Is Uploaddir, Path For Uploads.\n\n\n  Inside New Order\n  ----------------\n\n  New Order Will Need To Create A Couple Of Files On Your Harddisk In Order\n  To Work. All Files Are Stored In Your <path>/NEWORDER/ Dir.\n  So If You Still Would Like To Be A Friends To Your Ascii-Artists, Dont\n  Delete NEWORDER.xx Or NEWORDER.data. These Files Contains Both All The\n  Orders And Artist-Settings.\n  New Order Also Using Your T:-Assign As A Temporary Place For Uploades.\n\n ___ _ ____________________________________________:_\n|  _(_)_                                           |\n| (_(_)_) · no. fOUR : OPERATiON! ·            _ __|__________________________\n|___(_)______________________________________:_____|                          |\n                                             ¦       + nEW oRDER · v4.40f +   |\n                                             |________________________________|\n\n\n   Operating New Order\n   -------------------\n\n  Now When The Installation Is Correct Setup, Run The Door !\n\n  If Everything Is Working You Will Find A Nice Looking Menu With 3 Or 4\n  Option Depending On If You Are A User Or An Artist. Let''s Say You Are An\n  Artist Just To Explain All Options Just Once Since It Is Only One Option\n  (Read Orders) That Differs. Also There Are Two Hidden Commands.\n\n  Option 1   Write Order. Does Exactly What You Think It Does, Writes An Order\n  ========   To Selected Artist. If You Dont Find Any Artist To Send An Order\n             To, Then You Have Not Set The Tooltypes In Path/NEWORDER.info.\n             Just Go Back And Fix That.\n             If Everything Is Correct Then Just Select Who You Want Your\n             Ascii From. When This Is Done, Write A Description And Save It!\n\n             Exit (E) Will Quit New Order And <CR> Goes Back To Mainmenu.\n\n\n  Option 2   Read Orders. This Let The Artist Scan Through Orders Made To\n  ========   Him/Her And Choose What He/She Want To Do:\n\n        key   text      explaination\n        ===  ======= = =======================================================\n        (A)  Answer  - Lets The Artist Upload The Ascii(s) To The Orderer.\n                       New Order Will Put The Uploaded File(s) In A Private\n                       Message To The Orderer AND Put The File in The File-\n                       listing In The Ascii Conference. (New Order Asks The\n                       Artist For Every File If He/She Like To Put The File\n                       In Filelisting).\n\n        (D)  Del     - Simply Deletes The Selected Order.\n\n        (L)  Dl List - Lets The Artist Download A List With All Orders For Him.\n\n        (N)  New     - Jumps To The Last Order Read.\n\n        (M)  Main    - Jumps Back To Mainmenu.\n\n        (E)  Exit    - Exits New Order And Jumps Back To /X.\n\n        (R)  Reset   - Resets The Last-Read-Flag.\n\n       (-/+) -/+     - Goes To Previous/Next Order.\n\n     (1-999) #       - Goes To Order #\n\n        (?)  ?       - Shows Some Help.\n\n             Any Other Key Will Go To Next Order.\n\n             If The Artists Selects ANSWER He/She Will Be Asked To Upload The\n             Ascii(s). And If Everything Goes Right, He/She Then Have To Write\n             A Description For Every Uploaded Ascii. This Is The Description\n             That Will Be In The Letter And In The Filelisting.\n\n             If An Error Message Pops Up This Can Depend On Several Things:\n\n              -  Uploaded File Already Exists.\n              -  No File Has Actually Been Sent.\n              -  Uploader Loss Carrier.\n\n  Option Q/3 Quit. This Just Quits New Order.\n  ==========\n\n  Option C   Views Credits, Greetings And Some Other Info.\n  ========\n\n  Option X   This Is Not Shown In The Menu But It Turns Expert Mode ON/OFF.\n  ========   If Expert Mode Is On, The Menu Will Not Be Shown After Each\n             Command Made. This Is Only Available For Artists!\n\n\n  All Options But 3,C And X Can Be Used From The /X-Commandline.\n\n\n  If New Order Discovers That You Are Using A Newer Version Than v4.37 For\n  The First Time, It Automaticly Updates The Order-Files.\n\n\n ___ _ ____________________________________________:_\n|  _(_)_                                           |\n| (_(_)_) · no. fiVE : TROUBLE SHOOTiNG! ·     _ __|__________________________\n|___(_)______________________________________:_____|                          |\n                                             ¦       + nEW oRDER · v4.40f +   |\n                                             |________________________________|\n\n\n   Troubles ??\n   -----------\n\n  If New Order Won''t Work Properly This Can Depend On Several Things. The Only\n  Thing I Can Tell You For Sure Is That It Is YOU That Fucked Up, Not Me! =)\n\n   o New Order Won''t Start Properly - Check That All Tooltypes Is Set Right\n\n   o Uploading Can''t Be Done - Check That Your ULPATH Is Set Right\n\n   o An Error xxx Where xxx Is A Number - New Order Tries To Read/Write To\n     A File That Doesn''t Exist. This Error Message Should Not Pop Up If You\n     Have Installed /X & NEWORDER Correct.\n\n   o A Syntax xxx Where xxx Is A Number - Some Code Errors. Should Not Exist\n     Since We Have Tested New Order Several Times Before Releasing It.\n\n  If New Order Won''t Run Even If You Have Installed Everything Right, Then\n  Please Contact Me At Serpent Hill Or Final Impact! Find Out The Number!\n\n\n ___ _ ____________________________________________:_\n|  _(_)_                                           |\n| (_(_)_) · no. siX : GREETiNGS & MESSAGES! ·  _ __|__________________________\n|___(_)______________________________________:_____|                          |\n                                             ¦       + nEW oRDER · v4.40f +   |\n                                             |________________________________|\n\n\n--: GREEtiNGS! :----------------------------------------------------- -- -  -\n\n\n    Karma · Callis · U-Man · Danzig · Stain · Boromir · Sladoled · Hoot\n    Tango  · Krusty · Aquarius  · Ezco  · All The Other Duplo Members!!\n\n\n--: MESSaGES! :------------------------------------------------------ -- -  -\n\n\n    Karma   -  DAYBREAK!! It''ll be f*kking great !!\n\n    Callis  -  Hey.. So finally even you found a real life.. with jenny\n               i mean.. thats good.. keep her..\n\n    U-Man   -  bamse är världens starkaste björn!! på ALLT!!!! (??)\n\n    Ezco    -  tänka sig att du och jag ska gifta oss !!\n\n    Danzig  -  synd att du blev tvungen att stänga kyron dome !!\n               tack för all hjälp med betatesting !!\n\n    Stain   -  keep on rockin'' in the free world !!\n\n\n--: REGaRDS! :------------------------------------------------------- -- -  -\n\n\n    Aquarius · ByteAndi · Tango · The Silencer · Mack Lifeguard · Bobo!\n\n\n ___ _ ____________________________________________:_\n|  _(_)_                                           |\n| (_(_)_) · no. sEVEN : iNFORMATiON! ·         _ __|__________________________\n|___(_)______________________________________:_____|                          |\n                                             ¦       + nEW oRDER · v4.40f +   |\n                                             |________________________________|\n\n\n--: MUSiCAL SUPPORt! :----------------------------------------------- -- -  -\n\n\n       Hardy Nilsson · This Perfect Day · The Odd Numbers · Parasites\n       Allan Holdsworth · Toots Thielemans · Jaco Pastorius · Frente!\n       Nils Landgren  · Shreadhead  ·  Billie Holliday ·  Tribal Tech\n                    !!  J  A  M  i  R  O  Q  U  A  i  !!\n\n\n\n\n--: NON-MUSiCAL SUPPORt! :------------------------------------------- -- -  -\n\n\n         I Would Like To Thank Mom, Dad And My Family And All Other\n         People Who Made This Possible. Thanks Alot. God Bless You!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                  · THiS PRODUCTiON WAS BROUGHT TO YOU BY ·\n                              _\n        __________           / \     ___________ _______      _________\n      __\______   \  _______/   \  __\______    \      /___  /     ___/__\n     /        /    \/      /     \/       _/     \_   /    \/     /\     \\n   _/        /      \_    /       \_      \_______/  /      \_    \/      \_\n   \_________________/_____________/________|________________/_____________/\n  .---uMn/aC!---------------------------------------------------------------.\n  |  · CALL THESE BOARDS TO GET YOUR HANDS ON THE LATEST DUPLO RELEASES! ·  |\n -|-------------------------------------------------------------------------|-\n  |                                                                         |\n  |        fATAL cHAOS               +47-67591513     NORWEIGAN HQ          |\n  |        aSYLUM aLTERED sTATE #1   +46-317759378    SCANDINAVIAN HQ       |\n  |        aSYLUM aLTERED sTATE #2   +46-317759376    SCANDINAVIAN HQ       |\n  |        mETAL cONNEXTION #1       +45-74435949     EUROPEAN HQ           |\n  |        mETAL cONNEXTION #2       +45-RING-DOWN    EUROPEAN HQ           |\n  |        mETAL cONNEXTION #3       +45-RING-DOWN    EUROPEAN HQ           |\n  |        tOTAL iNFERNO             +46-42234164     SWEDISH HQ            |\n  |        fISTFUL oF sTEEL          +49-67235622     GERMAN HQ             |\n  |        dIVINE cONTACT            +358-313453706   FINNISH HQ            |\n  |        tOTAL eCLIPSE             +46-31572545     DIST.SITE             |\n  |                                                                         |\n  `-------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                                   Think\n\n                                   About\n\n                                    It!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                        · BLAME iT ON THE POPSTARS! ·\n\n                   ___________/\  _______________________/\\n             .-----\________    \/      _______________    \-----.\n             |      /     _/     \_    /\     \/     _/     \_   |\n             |    _/      \_______/    \/      \_    \_______/   |\n             | uMn\__________ __ _______________/________ __ _   |\n             |                                                   |\n             `--------------------» s T A r «--------------------''\n\n  ( kARMA/dYNAM0^aRCLiTE - kAiN/dUPLO^dYNAM0 - U-MAN/2OOOaD^sQUASH^aRT cORE )\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                                    Get\n\n                                     A\n\n                                   Life!!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCAPiTALiSTiC MESSAGE! --------------------------------------------------------+\n\n Make Sure You Get Your Hands On The Latest Productions From Two Of The Most\n                     Talented Guys In The Scene Today!\n\n\n                    FROM KARMA/ARCLiTE^dYNAM0^G''FORCE:\n\n                               · KiCKBACK ·\n\n         The New Fantastic Collection From Karma Is Finally Here!\n      Contains Various Group Banners For Both Amiga And Ascii Groups!\nFantastic Guest Art From Such Heroes As U-Man/ArtCore And Danzig/Arclite etc!\n  The First Work Released From One The True Masters Of The Ascii Scene In\n       Eight Months! Make Sure You Get It, It Was Worth Waiting For!\n\n\n            FROM U-MAN/2kAD^ARTCORE^UZi^SQUASH^dYNAM0^G''FORCE:\n\n                           · MiLLENiUM PART 1 ·\n\nThe Latest And As Always Outstanding Creation From This Hero Is Now Released!\n Includes Work Of Different Kinds That Will Make You Fall In Love Instantly!\n     Also Included Are Guest Art From Karma, Danzig, Shapechanger etc!\n     Get Your Hands On This One To See The Most Beautiful Ascii Logos\nYou Will Ever See In Your Lifetime, Made By One Of The Best (If Not THE Best)\n                        Ascii Painters Of All Time!\n\n\nAnd Don''t Forget To Look Out For The Co-Operation Production By Karma & U-Man\n                Which Will Be Released Sometime This Year!\n\n+------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n·                                                                             ·\n·                                                                             ·\n:                                                                             :\n:                                                                             :\n¦                                                                             ¦\n¦                                                                             ¦\n|                                                                             |\n|                                                                             |\n|                                                                             |\n|                                                                             |\n|                                                                             |\no----------------- -- -  -  -+( A DUPLO RELEASE )+-  -  - -- -----------------o\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',22287,5,0,NULL,NULL,'dpl_n44f','scan',1780048488);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dpl_no4r','DPL-NO4R.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DPL-NO4R.LHA',NULL,'XIM','....           ........',NULL,'kAiN/dUPLO^dM0','DPL','....::::.....      :::: ::::.....  ....... :::: :::: :::: .....::::.:::· :::: :::: :::: ·:::.:::: :::: :::: ::::      :::: ·:::.:::·',replace('     ....           ........\n ....::::.....      :::: ::::.....  .......\n:::: :::: :::: .....::::.:::· :::: :::: ::::\n·:::.:::: :::: :::: ::::      :::: ·:::.:::·\n.-kRm-----·:::.:::·-----------::::... ..  .\n|\n|  NEW ORDER v4.37r - THE ASCii REQUESTER  ·\n|                                          :\n|      DEVELOPED BY kAiN/dUPLO^dM0 iN      ¦\n| CO-OPERATiON WiTH SOME OF THE BEST ASCii |\n|           ARTiSTS iN THE WORLD!          |\n','\n',char(10)),'NEWORDER.DOC',replace('\no----------------- -- -  -  -+( A DUPLO RELEASE )+-  -  - -- -----------------o\n|·                                                                           ·|\n|                                                                             |\n|                                                                             |\n|                                                                             |\n|                                                                             |\n¦                                                                             ¦\n¦                                                                             ¦\n:                                                                             :\n:                                                                             :\n.                                                                             .\n.                                                                             .\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n .---+( W E L C O M E · T O · T H E · D O C U M E N T A T i O N · F O R )+---.\n |°                                                    _ ______             °|\n |_________ ________ _____/\_   _________ ________   _____/___/_____ ________|\n \\______ ¬\______ ¬\__  / /¬\_ \__   _ ¬\______ ¬\_/   __________ ¬\______ ¬\_\n | /    /   /  \_____/  / /   /  /    /   /    /___/    /   /  \_____/    /___/\n |/    /   /    /   /    /   /  /    /   /    /   /    /   /    /   /    /   |\n /____/   /____    /____    /  /____    /____/_  /____    /____    /____/_   |\n |  /____/   /____/   /____/      /____/    /       /____/   /____/    /     |\n |                                                                           |\n ÷-----------------------+( V E R S i O N · 4 . 3 7 )+-----------------------÷\n |                                                                           |\n |        ··  o N E  ·  Features      ·  What Can NEW ORDER Do?    ··        |\n |        ··  T W o  ·  Credits       ·  Who Have Made NEW ORDER?  ··        |\n |        ··  THReE  ·  Installation  ·  How To Install NEW ORDER  ··        |\n |        ··  FoU R  ·  Operation     ·  How To Operate NEW ORDER  ··        |\n |        ··  F iVE  ·  Troubles      ·  Do You Have A Problem?    ··        |\n |        ··  S i X  ·  Greetings     ·  Greetings And Messages    ··        |\n |        ··  SEVEN  ·  Information   ·  Useless Information       ··        |\n |        ··  EiGHT  ·  The End!      ·  Some Final Words          ··        |\n |                                                                           |\n `---------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                                   Here\n\n                                    We\n\n                                    Go\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n ___ _ ____________________________________________:_\n|  _(_)_                                           |\n| (_(_)_) · no. oNE : fEATURES! ·              _ __|__________________________\n|___(_)______________________________________:_____|                          |\n                                             ¦       + nEW oRDER · v4.37r +   |\n                                             |________________________________|\n\n\n   Ok! Lets get To Business! New Order.. Hmm.. What Is It? First Of All,\n   It Is A Wonderful Popgroup! And Second, It Is A New Door By Kain!!\n   Oh Yeah, What About It? Kain Have Made Several Smashing Doors!?!?\n   Oh Yes I Have!! What Is So Special About This One Then?? Well, It Is\n   A Fully Working Ascii-Order Door! Better Than Every Other Released!\n\n   Just Check These Nice Features Out:\n\n   o  /X 3.x Design\n   o  Configured Via Icons.\n   o  Easy To Setup.\n   o  Makes Private Messages With The Orders To The Artist.\n   o  Artists Can Upload Their Asciis Through New Order.\n   o  New Order Put The File(s) In A Private Message To The Orderer.\n   o  It Can Put The File In Filelist For Public Download.\n      (This Is Up To The Artist, And Is Asked For Every Uled File.)\n   o  Uses Sent-By-Line In The Filelisting.\n      It Handles: SentBy V1.3 by LightSpeed Technologies (TCN)\n                  File Description (Version 1.0b) by Bobo/Mystic\n      It Will Probably Handle Later Versions Of These Programs Too.\n   o  Can Use Uploaded Ascii As Filedescription.\n   o  Coded In Arexx - NO Backdoors.\n   o  Goodlooking Design. (Thanks Karma)\n\n\n ___ _ ____________________________________________:_\n|  _(_)_                                           |\n| (_(_)_) · no. tWO : CREDiTS! ·               _ __|__________________________\n|___(_)______________________________________:_____|                          |\n                                             ¦       + nEW oRDER · v4.37r +   |\n                                             |________________________________|\n\n\n                                             _____\n          __________________________________/_ _ /__.__________/_______ _ _\n         /  __    / _____    /   ____/   .____\\\\__|   ___   /  _____////\n        /    /___/_  \   ___/   ___/__   |/    /    |    \___/____   \\n       /    /_     \  \    \    /_    \  /    /     |     \_/   _\    \\n      /_____________\__\    \__________\_____/______|______/___________\\n   .--------------------\____/dZG-------------------------/---------------.\n   |                                                                      |\n   |      Door                                                            |\n   |        Code       -  KAiN/DPL                                        |\n   |        Design     -  KAiN/DPL, KARMA/AL, DANZiG/AL                   |\n   |        Ideas      -  KAiN/DPL, KARMA,AL, DANZiG/AL, U-MAN/2kAD       |\n   |        Testing    -  KAiN/DPL, DANZiG/AL, KARMA/AL                   |\n   |                                                                      |\n   |      Docs                                                            |\n   |        Author     -  KAiN/DPL                                        |\n   |        Design     -  KARMA/AL, KAiN/DPL                              |\n   |        Ascii-art  -  KARMA/AL, DANZiG/AL, U-MAN/2kAD                 |\n   |                                                                      |\n   |   ----------------------------------------------------------------   |\n   |                                                                      |\n   |                      For Updates And Help Call                       |\n   |                                                                      |\n   |                  - Final Impact Or Serpent Hill -                    |\n   |                                                                      |\n   `----------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n\n ___ _ ____________________________________________:_\n|  _(_)_                                           |\n| (_(_)_) · no. tHREE : iNSTALLATiON! ·        _ __|__________________________\n|___(_)______________________________________:_____|                          |\n                                             ¦       + nEW oRDER · v4.37r +   |\n                                             |________________________________|\n\n\n  /X 2.xx Installation\n  ---------------------\n\n  - Register & Install /X 3.xx And Follow The /X 3.xx Installation !!\n\n  /X 3.xx Installation\n  ---------------------\n\n  - The New Order Dir Can Be Installed Wherever You Like But If You\n    Dont Install It In DOORS: Then You Must Add The PATH Tooltype To\n    Your BBS:Commands/BBSCmd/ORDER.info Icon. See Tooltypes Info !\n\n  - Anyway, Just Copy The NewOrder Directory And NEWORDER.info To DOORS:\n    (Or Wherever You Like To Install New Order!)\n\n  - Copy ORDER.info To BBS:Commands/BBScmd/ Or BBS:Commands/ConfXCmd/\n\n\n  Tooltypes For The NEWORDER.info\n  -------------------------------\n\n  ARTISTS=<num>           -  Number Of Artists That A User May Order From\n  ARTIST.<num>=<name>     -  Ascii-Artist Handle\n  COMMENT.<num>=<comment> -  Comment On The Artist (Group Etc...)\n  CONF=<conf-num>         -  Conference To Use\n\n  Tooltype For The BBS:Commands/BBSCmd/ORDER.info\n  -----------------------------------------------\n\n  PATH=<New Order Dir Path> - The Path Where You Keep Your New Order Dir.\n                              Note  If This Tooltype Is Not Set, New Order\n                              Will Use The DOORS: Directory.\n\n\n  Safety\n  ------\n\n  You Might Want To Make Backupcopies On:\n\n    CONF/MSGBASE/MAILSTATS\n    CONF/MSGBASE/HEADERFILE\n    CONF/DIRx (Your Upload-Dir-File)\n\n  Just As A Safety Precaution. These Are The Files That New Order Writes To.\n  Other System Files That New Order Uses Are (Read Only):\n\n    PATH/NEWORDER.info     -  To Read Which Conference To Use And To\n                              Get All Info On Artists.\n    BBS:CONFCONFIG.info    -  To Read Conference Path.\n    BBS:<CONF>.info        -  To Read What Dir Is Uploaddir, Path For Uploads.\n\n\n ___ _ ____________________________________________:_\n|  _(_)_                                           |\n| (_(_)_) · no. fOUR : OPERATiON! ·            _ __|__________________________\n|___(_)______________________________________:_____|                          |\n                                             ¦       + nEW oRDER · v4.37r +   |\n                                             |________________________________|\n\n\n   Operating New Order\n   -------------------\n\n  Now When The Installation Is Correct Setup, Run The Door !\n\n  If Everything Is Working You Will Find A Nice Looking Menu With 3 Or 4\n  Option Depending On If You Are A User Or An Artist. Let''s Say You Are An\n  Artist Just To Explain All Options Just Once Since It Is Only One Option\n  (Read Orders) That Differs.\n\n  Option 1   Write Order. Does Exactly What You Think It Does, Writes An Order\n             To Selected Artist. If You Dont Find Any Artist To Send An Order\n             To, Then You Have Not Set The Tooltypes In Path/NEWORDER.info.\n             Just Go Back And Fix That.\n             If Everything Is Correct Then Just Select Who You Want Your\n             Ascii From. When This Is Done, Write A Description And Save It!\n\n  Option 2   Read Orders. This Let The Artist Scan Through Orders Made To\n             Him/Her And Choose What He/She Want To Do:\n\n             ANSWER  - Lets The Artist Upload The Ascii(s) To The Orderer.\n                       New Order Will Put The Uploaded File(s) In A Private\n                       Message To The Orderer AND Put The File in The File-\n                       listing In The Ascii Conference. (New Order Asks The\n                       Artist For Every File If He/She Like To Put The File\n                       In Filelisting).\n\n             DELETE  - Simply Deletes The Selected Order.\n\n             DL LIST - Lets The Artist Download A List With All Orders For Him.\n\n             QUIT    - Jumps Back To Mainmenu.\n\n             Any Other Key Will Go To Next Order.\n\n             If The Artists Selects ANSWER He/She Will Be Asked To Upload The\n             Ascii(s). And If Everything Goes Right, He/She Then Have To Write\n             A Description For Every Uploaded Ascii. This Is The Description\n             That Will Be In The Letter And In The Filelisting.\n\n             If An Error Message Pops Up This Can Depend On Several Things:\n\n              -  Uploaded File Already Exists.\n              -  No File Has Actually Been Sent.\n              -  Uploader Loss Carrier.\n\n  Option Q/3 Quit. This Just Quits New Order.\n\n  Option C   Views Credits, Greetings And Some Other Info.\n\n  Option X   This Is Not Shown In The Menu But It Turns Expert Mode ON/OFF.\n             If Expert Mode Is On, The Menu Will Not Be Shown After Each\n             Command Made. This Is Only Available For Artists!\n\n\n ___ _ ____________________________________________:_\n|  _(_)_                                           |\n| (_(_)_) · no. fiVE : TROUBLE SHOOTiNG! ·     _ __|__________________________\n|___(_)______________________________________:_____|                          |\n                                             ¦       + nEW oRDER · v4.37r +   |\n                                             |________________________________|\n\n\n   Troubles ??\n   -----------\n\n  If New Order Won''t Work Properly This Can Depend On Several Things. The Only\n  Thing I Can Tell You For Sure Is That It Is YOU That Fucked Up, Not Me! =)\n\n   o New Order Won''t Start Properly - Check That All Tooltypes Is Set Right\n\n   o Uploading Can''t Be Done - Check That Your ULPATH Is Set Right\n\n   o An Error xxx Where xxx Is A Number - New Order Tries To Read/Write To\n     A File That Doesn''t Exist. This Error Message Should Not Pop Up If You\n     Have Installed /X & NEWORDER Correct.\n\n   o A Syntax xxx Where xxx Is A Number - Some Code Errors. Should Not Exist\n     Since We Have Tested New Order Several Times Before Releasing It.\n\n  If New Order Won''t Run Even If You Have Installed Everything Right, Then\n  Please Contact Me At Kyron Dome, Traders Nation or Final Impact!\n\n\n ___ _ ____________________________________________:_\n|  _(_)_                                           |\n| (_(_)_) · no. siX : GREETiNGS & MESSAGES! ·  _ __|__________________________\n|___(_)______________________________________:_____|                          |\n                                             ¦       + nEW oRDER · v4.37r +   |\n                                             |________________________________|\n\n\n--: GREEtiNGS! :----------------------------------------------------- -- -  -\n\n\n    Karma · Callis · U-Man · Danzig · Stain · Boromir · Sladoled · Hoot\n    Tango  · Krusty · Aquarius  · Ezco  · All The Other Duplo Members!!\n\n\n--: MESSaGES! :------------------------------------------------------ -- -  -\n\n\n    Karma   -  CROCKPOT ! We Kick Butt ! Tintin !\n\n    Callis  -  Hej!! What''s shaking baby !?! Techno suger !! Tacka vet jag\n               neds atomic dustbin !!\n\n    U-Man   -  bamse är världens starkaste björn!! på ALLT!!!! (??)\n\n    Ezco    -  tänka sig att du och jag ska gifta oss !!\n\n    Danzig  -  synd att du blev tvungen att stänga kyron dome !!\n               tack för all hjälp med betatesting !!\n\n    Stain   -  keep on rockin'' in the free world !!\n\n\n--: REGaRDS! :------------------------------------------------------- -- -  -\n\n\n    Aquarius · ByteAndi · Tango · The Silencer · Mack Lifeguard · Bobo!\n\n\n ___ _ ____________________________________________:_\n|  _(_)_                                           |\n| (_(_)_) · no. sEVEN : iNFORMATiON! ·         _ __|__________________________\n|___(_)______________________________________:_____|                          |\n                                             ¦       + nEW oRDER · v4.37r +   |\n                                             |________________________________|\n\n\n--: MUSiCAL SUPPORt! :----------------------------------------------- -- -  -\n\n\n       Hardy Nilsson · This Perfect Day · The Odd Numbers · Parasites\n       Bad Religion · Green Day · No Fun At All · Neds Atomic Dustbin\n       Mother Earth · Jamiroquai ·  Galliano · the Lemonheads · Souls\n       !!     Crockpot     !!     Immodium     !!     Cherryl      !!\n\n\n--: NON-MUSiCAL SUPPORt! :------------------------------------------- -- -  -\n\n\n         I Would Like To Thank Mom, Dad And My Family And All Other\n         People Who Made This Possible. Thanks Alot. God Bless You!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                  · THiS PRODUCTiON WAS BROUGHT TO YOU BY ·\n                              _\n        __________           / \     ___________ _______      _________\n      __\______   \  _______/   \  __\______    \      /___  /     ___/__\n     /        /    \/      /     \/       _/     \_   /    \/     /\     \\n   _/        /      \_    /       \_      \_______/  /      \_    \/      \_\n   \_________________/_____________/________|________________/_____________/\n  .---uMn/aC!---------------------------------------------------------------.\n  |  · CALL THESE BOARDS TO GET YOUR HANDS ON THE LATEST DUPLO RELEASES! ·  |\n -|-------------------------------------------------------------------------|-\n  |                                                                         |\n  |        fATAL cHAOS               +47-67591513     NORWEIGAN HQ          |\n  |        aSYLUM aLTERED sTATE #1   +46-317759378    SCANDINAVIAN HQ       |\n  |        aSYLUM aLTERED sTATE #2   +46-317759376    SCANDINAVIAN HQ       |\n  |        mETAL cONNEXTION #1       +45-74435949     EUROPEAN HQ           |\n  |        mETAL cONNEXTION #2       +45-RING-DOWN    EUROPEAN HQ           |\n  |        mETAL cONNEXTION #3       +45-RING-DOWN    EUROPEAN HQ           |\n  |        tOTAL iNFERNO             +46-42234164     SWEDISH HQ            |\n  |        fISTFUL oF sTEEL          +49-67235622     GERMAN HQ             |\n  |        dIVINE cONTACT            +358-313453706   FINNISH HQ            |\n  |        tOTAL eCLIPSE             +46-31572545     DIST.SITE             |\n  |                                                                         |\n  `-------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                                   Think\n\n                                   About\n\n                                    It!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                        · BLAME iT ON THE POPSTARS! ·\n\n                   ___________/\  _______________________/\\n             .-----\________    \/      _______________    \-----.\n             |      /     _/     \_    /\     \/     _/     \_   |\n             |    _/      \_______/    \/      \_    \_______/   |\n             | uMn\__________ __ _______________/________ __ _   |\n             |                                                   |\n             `--------------------» s T A r «--------------------''\n\n  ( kARMA/dYNAM0^aRCLiTE - kAiN/dUPLO^dYNAM0 - U-MAN/2OOOaD^sQUASH^aRT cORE )\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                                    Get\n\n                                     A\n\n                                   Life!!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nCAPiTALiSTiC MESSAGE! --------------------------------------------------------+\n\n Make Sure You Get Your Hands On The Latest Productions From Two Of The Most\n                     Talented Guys In The Scene Today!\n\n\n                    FROM KARMA/ARCLiTE^dYNAM0^G''FORCE:\n\n                               · KiCKBACK ·\n\n         The New Fantastic Collection From Karma Is Finally Here!\n      Contains Various Group Banners For Both Amiga And Ascii Groups!\nFantastic Guest Art From Such Heroes As U-Man/ArtCore And Danzig/Arclite etc!\n  The First Work Released From One The True Masters Of The Ascii Scene In\n       Eight Months! Make Sure You Get It, It Was Worth Waiting For!\n\n\n            FROM U-MAN/2kAD^ARTCORE^UZi^SQUASH^dYNAM0^G''FORCE:\n\n                           · MiLLENiUM PART 1 ·\n\nThe Latest And As Always Outstanding Creation From This Hero Is Now Released!\n Includes Work Of Different Kinds That Will Make You Fall In Love Instantly!\n     Also Included Are Guest Art From Karma, Danzig, Shapechanger etc!\n     Get Your Hands On This One To See The Most Beautiful Ascii Logos\nYou Will Ever See In Your Lifetime, Made By One Of The Best (If Not THE Best)\n                        Ascii Painters Of All Time!\n\n\nAnd Don''t Forget To Look Out For The Co-Operation Production By Karma & U-Man\n                Which Will Be Released Sometime Next Year!\n\n+------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n·                                                                             ·\n·                                                                             ·\n:                                                                             :\n:                                                                             :\n¦                                                                             ¦\n¦                                                                             ¦\n|                                                                             |\n|                                                                             |\n|                                                                             |\n|                                                                             |\n|                                                                             |\no----------------- -- -  -  -+( A DUPLO RELEASE )+-  -  - -- -----------------o\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,16417,3,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048488);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dpl_pc10','DPL-PC10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DPL-PC10.LHA',NULL,'XIM','PWCommand.x',NULL,'Tango/DPL','DPL','.\____ \   /   _____   /  /\___  \---------. |/   /  \ /   / ______/  /   \/   \        | /_______/___ /   / /   _/\________/  DUPLO |',replace(' ____/\_____/\___________________           \n.\____ \   /   _____   /  /\___  \---------.\n|/   /  \ /   / ______/  /   \/   \        |\n/_______/___ /   / /   _/\________/  DUPLO |\n|          \/__ / /_______\-Mo!            |\n¦-------------\/---------------------------¦\n|            P R E S E N T S :             |\n|       PWCommand v1.0, by Tango/DPL       |\n|  Put a PW on sertain commands like the   |\n|   internal /X stuff. With this you may   |\n|  have diffrent PW''s for diffrent user.   |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'PWCommand.doc',replace('\n        .\n        :    :\n        :   /|\n        |  / | t A N G o                  _______\n        ._/  |___ _ ____________ _______ |      /_____________________\n       _ _   ___/____________   \     _ \|     /___________________   \\n        :    |     \      ______ \     \ \    / \______    |      |  . \_\n        :    l      \_    \    /  \_    \ \  /       |     |      ''     /\n      _ :_______     /_____\       /____|\  /______  `     |__________ /\n        |  -mNt\____/       \ ____/       \/      `--------''         \/\n        |                    \/                                      :\n        |                       o F   D U P L o                      |\n        |                                                            |\n        `---------------------- P R E S E N t S ----------------- - -''\n\n                                PWCommand v1.0\n\n                              Idea by: Double/DPL\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                Important note!\n                               ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThis util is released under the concept of tradeware. If you like it and use\nit, upload some on my board. I will not take any responsability for whatever\nthis door does with your computer (It wont do anything but what it should, but\nyou never know what those lamers do!).\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                   History!\n                                  ~~~~~~~~~~\nv1.0 - First release. Featuring diffrent PW''s for diffrent users and the\n       ability to decide wich users who should have axx to the command, thereby\n       eliminating lots of hack-atempts!\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                 Installation!\n                                ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nIf you run /X 3.x, copy all files I''ve supplied and your set.\n\nIf you run /X 2.x or S-Express, insert the followin line fex., to your\n"commands/bbs.cmd" file.\n\n---( cut )---\n1         XM001DOORS:PWCommand/PWCommand.x\n---( cut )---\n\nWhen you''ve installed the door you must create an icon/bbs.cmd entry for all\nfunctions you wish to have PW on. The edit their config files. If you want a PW\nat the user editor (1) make a file called "1.cfg". If you want one for the\nremote-shell, (0) make a file called "0.cfg" etc. These configfiles should be\nput in the same directory as "PWCommand.x" and should look as follows (except\nthe comments!).\n\n---( cut )---\n1            <- Command to be issued if access is granted.\nTango        <- First user who could use the door/command.\nMyPW         <- First user''s PW.\n-dOUBLE      <- Second user.....\nHisPW        <- Second user''s PW. And so on....\n---( cut )---\n\nIf the command issued on the first line is the same as the one that started the\ndoor the PWCommand door will call the internal /X command, otherwise any\ninternal/external command, ie. if you make a command with PW as "1" and you\nwant it to run the user-editor you would get a loop wich never ends, but this\nis not possible.\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                 These are the ß-sites for all my doors/utils!\n                ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n       Asylum Altered State #1       Juan               ++46-317-759378\n       Asylum Altered State #2       Juan               ++46-317-759376\n       Disorder                      Marwin             ++46-456-27511\n       Imagine                       Rille              ++46-42-135505\n       Total Inferno                 Tango              ++46-42-234164\n       Twisted Society               The Big Byte       ++46-44-106144\n\nAll my utils should be free dl, otherwise tell me and I''ll kick that ß-tester.\nIf you want to ß-test my doors/utils, contact me and we''ll work something out.\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                  Greetings!\n                                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~\n    Melone - Krusty - Hoot - Marwin - Manta - The Big Byte - Norad - Venger\n    Zendor - Mike - Luca - Abbe - Stuff - Broder - Zync - Zych - La Fayette\n     Axe - Nebraska - Eracore - Linus - Avalon - Nero - Dixy - Crux - Nuke\n   Fuze - Fix - Kain - Prospex - Canaima - Pripps - Hilbert - Mital - D-Zire\n        Jucke - Double - E-Go - Distler - Sy-Klone - Fazer - Zcandaler\n   Beavis & Butthead - Renko - Juan - Guardian - EaSy RiDeR - Wozzy - Suggs\n                            Rille - Fonus - Proctor\n\nForgive me if I forgot someone. It''s not easy to remember everybody you know!\n\n[EOF]\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',13628,2,0,NULL,NULL,'dpl_pc10','scan',1780048488);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dpl_scr2','DPL-SCR2.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DPL-SCR2.LHA',NULL,'XIM','OOS_EXECUTE.ME',NULL,NULL,'DPL','\\_____ ¬\__   / ______ ¬\__   / \__  _ ¬\_ /   /   /   /   /  _____/   /¬\_/   /   // /   /   /   /   /   /   /   /   /   /   /',replace(' ________ ______/\_______ ______ ________\n\\_____ ¬\__   / ______ ¬\__   / \__  _ ¬\_\n  /   /   /   /   /  _____/   /¬\_/   /   //\n /   /   /   /   /   /   /   /   /   /   /\n/___    /___    /___/_  /___    /___    /kRm\n÷--/___/---/___/---/-------/___/---/___/---\n:   KAiN PRESENTS ANOTHER OPERATOR PAGER   :\n:             SCREAMAGER II v1.0           :\n:..........................................:\n','\n',char(10)),'SCREAMAGER.doc',replace('                                      ·\n                                      ·\n                                      :\n                                      ¦\n                                      |\n                                      |\n                                      |\n                                      |\n                                     !¦!\n+------------------------------------¡!¡------------------------------------+\n|     _ __ ___________ ________/\ __________ ________  ___________          |\n|         \\_______  ¬\__     /  \_______  ¬\__     /_ \__    _  ¬\_ __ _   |\n| .---------/     /    /     /    /    ______/     / ¬\_/     /    //-----. |\n| |--------/     /    /     /    /     /----/     /    /     /    /-------| |\n| |·DUPLO·/     /    /     /    /     /    /     /    /     /    /·DUPLO!·| |\n| |------/_____     /_____     /\    /----/_____     /_____     /---------| |\n| `----------/_____/----/_____/--\  /kRm------/_____/----/_____/----------'' |\n|                                 \/                                        |\n+------------------------------------!¡!------------------------------------+\n                                     ¡¦¡\n                                      |\n                                      |\n                                      ¦\n                                      :\n                       :______________________________:\n                     ._|_ _                        _ _|_.\n                 -÷* | :                              : | *÷-\n                     |             pRESENTs             |\n                     |       aNOTHEr dOOr fOr /X        |\n                     |             cODEd bY             |\n                 -÷* |_:_ _                        _ _:_| *÷-\n                       |______________________________|\n                       :                              :\n                                      :\n                                      ¦\n                                      |\n                                      |\n                                      ¦\n                                      :\n                        ______\n                 ______/     /______/\  _______ ______/\\n                /    _/     /_______  \(_______) ______ \____\n               /    _     _/      _/   \        \/     \ \   \\n             _/      \     \_     \     \_       \_     \ \   \_\n             \________\     /______\     /________/______\     /\n                       \   /        \   /              uMn\   /\n                        \_/          \_/                   \_/\n\n                                      :\n                                      ¦\n                                      |\n                                      ¦\n                                      :\n\n                                 c A L L E d\n\n                                      :\n                                      ¦\n                                      :\n                   !¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯!\n                  -÷        S C R E A M A G E R    I I      ÷-\n                   ¡________________________________________¡\n                                      :\n                                      ¦\n                                      |\n                                      |\n                                      ¦\n                                      :\n        +-----------------------------+\n        |\n        |                     ÷tABLE oF cONTENTs÷\n        |\n        ¦ ·01············································cREDiTs·\n        : ·02······························wHy uSe tHIs pROGRAm?·\n        ¡ ·03································aBOUt sCREAMAGEr II·\n        : ·04·······································iNSTALLATiOn·\n        ¦ ·05··········································gREETiNGs·\n        | ·06········································fOr cONTACt·\n        |\n        |\n        +-----------------------------+\n                                      :\n                                      ¦\n                                      |\n              ¦                                                ¦\n            --+------------------×         ×-------------------+--\n              ¡                                                ¡\n     -  -- ---÷+ cREDiTs·cREDiTs·cREDiTs·cREDiTs·cREDiTs·cRED +÷--- --  -\n              !                                                !\n            --+------------------×         ×-------------------+--\n              ¦                                                ¦\n\n\n            cODe , dESiGn , dOCs      :     KAiN  /  DPL ^ DYNAMO\n\n            iDEAs , bETa tESTiNg      :        TANGO /  ASH ^ DPL\n                                      :              MARWIN / DPL\n                                      :               LiNUS / DPL\n\n            lOGOs, aSCii aRt          :            KARMA / AL^M12\n                                                     U-MAN / 2kAD\n\n            mORAl sUPPORt             :                       iDA\n                                                            HEFFA\n                                                        BRAiNPOOL\n\n                                      !\n                                      ¡\n\n              ¦                                                ¦\n            --+------------------×         ×-------------------+--\n              ¡                                                ¡\n     -  -- ---÷+ wHy uSe tHIs pROGRAm·wHy uSe tHIs pROGRAm·wH +÷--- --  -\n              !                                                !\n            --+------------------×         ×-------------------+--\n              ¦                                                ¦\n\n\n       tEn gOOd rEASOn wHy tO uSe a sCREAMAGEr II...\n\n       oNe   ·    iT CAN DO EVERYTHiNG THAT iS USEFUL iN A PAGER\n       tWo   ·    iT iS COOLER THAN ALL OTHER PAGERS\n      tHREe  ·    iT CAN MAKE MESSAGE\n      fOUr   ·    iT iS WRiTTEN BY ME                                _\n       fIVe  ·    iT CAN SiNG ALL GOOD POPSONGS                    _(_)_\n       sEx   ·    yES PLEASE                                  - --(_(_)_)-- -\n      sEVEn  ·    iT HAS COOLER DOCS THAN  OTHER DOCS               (_)\n      eIGHt  ·    yOU CAN LEAVE MESSAGE TO THE USER\n       nINe  ·    oPTiONABLE ''REASON FOR CHAT''\n       tEN   ·    tHERE ARE TEN GOOD REASONS FOR USiNG iT\n\n\n\n                                      !\n                                      ¡\n\n              ¦                                                ¦\n            --+------------------×         ×-------------------+--\n              ¡                                                ¡\n     -  -- ---÷+ aBOUt sCREAMAGEr · aBOUt sCREAMAGEr · aBOUt  +÷--- --  -\n              !                                                !\n            --+------------------×         ×-------------------+--\n              ¦                                                ¦\n\n\n    Screamager II is not an ordinary pagedoor !! It has alot of good\n    features that most pager dont have. For example, in SCREAMAGER II,\n    you can leave messages for yuor user that''ll popup when chat is OFF!!\n    You choose if that useless ''REASON TO CHAT'' shit should be there or\n    not. If sysop runs the door, a sysop-menu will popup where you can\n    edit message to user, toggle ''REASON FOR CHAT'', view message to user,\n    toggle chat, test users view, and actually quit SCREAMAGER II.\n\n    From the users side, it''s not much more than other pager, except that\n    this one looks better !! That''s just becoz it''s made by KAiN !!\n\n\n                                      !\n                                      ¡\n\n              ¦                                                ¦\n            --+------------------×         ×-------------------+--\n              ¡                                                ¡\n     -  -- ---÷+ iNSTALLATiOn·iNSTALLATiOn·iNSTALLATiOn·iNSTA +÷--- --  -\n              !                                                !\n            --+------------------×         ×-------------------+--\n              ¦                                                ¦\n\n\n\n    Well, every experienced sysop should know how to install this one but for\n    those who don''t know we''ll show you...\n\n     /X 2.xx Installation:\n     ---------------------\n\n    - Copy the SCREAMAGER directory to DOORS:\n    - Put the following line in BBS:Commands/BBS.CMD\n\n    ---------------- CUT HERE -----------------\n    *O        RM020DOORS:SCREAMAGER/SCREAM.rexx\n    ---------------- CUT HERE -----------------\n\n\n     /X 3.xx Installation:\n     ---------------------\n\n    - Copy the SCREAMAGER Directory to DOORS:\n    - Copy O.info to BBS:Commands/BBScmd/\n\n\n\n                                      !\n                                      ¡\n\n              ¦                                                ¦\n            --+------------------×         ×-------------------+--\n              ¡                                                ¡\n     -  -- ---÷+ gREETiNGs·rEGARDs·gREETiNGs·rEGARDs·gREETiNG +÷--- --  -\n              !                                                !\n            --+------------------×         ×-------------------+--\n              ¦                                                ¦\n\n                              pERSONAl gREETiNGs\n                             --------------------\n\n          KARMA÷CALLiS÷CORE÷U-MAN÷DANZiG÷TANGO÷HOOT÷KRUSTY÷MARWiN\n\n                                   rEGARDs\n                                  ---------\n\n                      MACK LiFEGUARD÷VAN DAMME÷DELUTiON\n\n\n                                   mESSAGEs\n                                  ----------\n\n             KARMA    -   he... WE ARE POPSTARS NOW !!!!\n             CALLiS   -   LiSTEN UP.. TECHNO SUCK !!!\n             CORE     -   I MiSS YOU..\n             U-MAN    -   THANKS ALOT FOR YOUR LOGOS AND STUFF..\n                          I''M ALMOST FiNiSHED WiTH NEW ORDER !!\n             DANZiG   -   PANG PANG.. WELCOME BACK !!\n             TANGO    -   I HOPE YOU''RE SATiSFiED WiTH THiS DOOR..\n             HOOT     -   öhhhh.. PEPS iS NOOOOOT COOL..\n             KRUSTY   -   YOU HAVE RED HAiR AND I HAVE DREADLOCKS..\n             MARWiN   -   THANKS FOR BETATESTiNG..\n             ALL      -   HEFFA RULES THE WORLD\n\n\n\n                                      !\n                                      ¡\n\n              ¦                                                ¦\n            --+------------------×         ×-------------------+--\n              ¡                                                ¡\n     -  -- ---÷+ fOr cONTACt·fOr cONTACt·fOr cONTACt·fOr cONT +÷--- --  -\n              !                                                !\n            --+------------------×         ×-------------------+--\n              ¦                                                ¦\n\n\n  For the latest updates and other /X-utils from Kain call these numbers:\n\n            -- Coast Link  +46-176-80568  Sysop: Danzig --\n\n          -- Total Inferno  +46-042-234164  Sysop: Tango --\n\n            -- Disorder  +46-0456-27511  Sysop: Marwin --\n\n\n\n                                      !\n                                      ¡\n\n              ¦                                                ¦\n            --+------------------×         ×-------------------+--\n              ¡                                                ¡\n     -  -- ---÷+                ·eNd oF fILe·                 +÷--- --  -\n              !                                                !\n            --+------------------×         ×-------------------+--\n              ¦                                                ¦\n\n\n\n                                     A\n                 ___________/\  _______________________/\\n           .-----\________    \/      _______________    \-----.\n           |      /     _/     \_    /\     \/     _/     \_   |\n           |    _/      \_______/    \/      \_    \_______/   |\n           | uMn\__________ __ _______________/________ __ _   |\n           |                                                   |\n           `--------------------» s T A r «--------------------''\n\n                   ( kARMA/M12&AL % kAiN/dPL % U-MAN/2kAd )\n\n\n\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',10604,3,0,NULL,NULL,'dpl_scr2','scan',1780048488);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dpl_sd10','DPL-SD10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DPL-SD10.LHA','StripDir','XIM','StripDir','1.0',NULL,'DPL',NULL,replace('StripDir v1.0\n','\n',char(10)),'StripDir.doc',replace('\n        .\n        :    :\n        :   /|\n        |  / | t A N G o                  _______\n        ._/  |___ _ ____________ _______ |      /_____________________\n       _ _   ___/____________   \     _ \|     /___________________   \\n        :    |     \      ______ \     \ \    / \______    |      |  . \_\n        :    l      \_    \    /  \_    \ \  /       |     |      ''     /\n      _ :_______     /_____\       /____|\  /______  `     |__________ /\n        |  -mNt\____/       \ ____/       \/      `--------''         \/\n        |                    \/                                      :\n        |                       o F   D U P L o                      |\n        |                                                            |\n        `---------------------- P R E S E N t S ----------------- - -''\n\n                                 StripDir v1.0\n\n                             Idea by: Scroud/Indie\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                Important note!\n                               ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThis util is released under the concept of tradeware. If you like it and use\nit, upload some on my board. I will not take any responsability for whatever\nthis door does with your computer (It wont do anything but what it should, but\nyou never know what those lamers do!).\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                   History!\n                                  ~~~~~~~~~~\nv1.0 - First (only?) version. No comments or special features!\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                    Usage!\n                                   ~~~~~~~~\nThe commandline parameters of StripDir is:\n\nStripDir <dirlist> [full]\n\nThe DIRLIST parameter is the full path to the list you want to strip! OBS! \nThere is no way to un-strip a list! ;)\n\nWhen I recieved the original idea from Scroud, he wanted the whole first line\nof every file to be saved. This way you can sometimes get a hint of what a\nfilename really is. However, I thought this was a litle stupid. I only wanted\nthe speed of a stripped dir-list. Therefor I added the FULL option. With this\noption set the stripper will only save the filename, upload date and filesize,\ncreating a somewhat smaller file.\n\nHere are some info''s about my dirlists before and after striping.\n\n        Normal size      Normal stripped      Full stripped\n        ~~~~~~~~~~~      ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~      ~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nDIR1     1257229        214571 (83% gain)    95133 (92% gain)\nDIR2      288286         40853 (86% gain)    16989 (94% gain)\n\nWell, the numbers speaks for themselves. If you only use your dir1 for the\ndupechecker you will gain HD-space and your dupechecker will fly!\n\nOBS! I only striped DIR2 to give you some more figures to look at. It''s not\nvery wise to strip the list of all warez actually existing in the conf, since\nall descs will be deleted!\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                 These are the ß-sites for all my doors/utils!\n                ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n       Asylum Altered State #1       Juan               ++46-317-759378\n       Asylum Altered State #2       Juan               ++46-317-759376\n       Disorder                      Marwin             ++46-456-27511\n       Imagine #1                    Rille              ++46-42-135504\n       Imagine #2                    Rille              ++46-42-135505\n       Total Inferno                 Tango              ++46-42-234164\n       Twisted Society               The Big Byte       ++46-44-106144\n\nAll my utils should be free dl, otherwise tell me and I''ll kick that ß-tester.\nIf you want to ß-test my doors/utils, contact me and we''ll work something out.\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                  Greetings!\n                                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~\n    Melone - Krusty - Hoot - Marwin - Manta - The Big Byte - Norad - Venger\n    Zendor - Mike - Luca - Abbe - Stuff - Broder - Zync - Zych - La Fayette\n     Axe - Nebraska - Eracore - Linus - Avalon - Nero - Dixy - Crux - Nuke\n   Fuze - Fix - Kain - Prospex - Canaima - Pripps - Hilbert - Mital - D-Zire\n        Jucke - Double - E-Go - Distler - Sy-Klone - Fazer - Zcandaler\n   Beavis & Butthead - Renko - Juan - Guardian - EaSy RiDeR - Wozzy - Suggs\n       Rille - Fonus - Nightshade - Borre - Scroud - Derek - Vega - Rix\n\nForgive me if I forgot someone. It''s not easy to remember everybody you know!\n\n[EOF]\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',7450,4,0,NULL,NULL,'dpl_sd10','scan',1780048488);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dpl_sp10','DPL-SP10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DPL-SP10.LHA',NULL,'XIM','SpeedPass.x',NULL,'Tango/DPL','DPL','.\____ \   /   _____   /  /\___  \---------. |/   /  \ /   / ______/  /   \/   \        | /_______/___ /   / /   _/\________/  DUPLO |',replace(' ____/\_____/\___________________           \n.\____ \   /   _____   /  /\___  \---------.\n|/   /  \ /   / ______/  /   \/   \        |\n/_______/___ /   / /   _/\________/  DUPLO |\n|          \/__ / /_______\-Mo!            |\n¦-------------\/---------------------------¦\n|            P R E S E N T S :             |\n|       SpeedPass v1.0, by Tango/DPL       |\n| Set NUP on certain connect speeds, such  |\n|  as 2400, 4800 etc. Fully configurable!  |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'SpeedPass.doc',replace('\n        .\n        :    :\n        :   /|\n        |  / | t A N G o                  _______\n        ._/  |___ _ ____________ _______ |      /_____________________\n       _ _   ___/____________   \     _ \|     /___________________   \\n        :    |     \      ______ \     \ \    / \______    |      |  . \_\n        :    l      \_    \    /  \_    \ \  /       |     |      ''     /\n      _ :_______     /_____\       /____|\  /______  `     |__________ /\n        |  -mNt\____/       \ ____/       \/      `--------''         \/\n        |                    \/                                      :\n        |                       o F   D U P L o                      |\n        |                                                            |\n        `---------------------- P R E S E N t S ----------------- - -''\n\n                                SpeedPass v1.0\n\n                              Idea by: Rille/SCX\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                Important note!\n                               ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThis util is released under the concept of tradeware. If you like it and use\nit, upload some on my board. I will not take any responsability for whatever\nthis door does with your computer (It wont do anything but what it should, but\nyou never know what those lamers do!).\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                   History!\n                                  ~~~~~~~~~~\nv1.0 - First release. Let you set a NUP''s for any connectspeeds. Supports\n       diffrent NUP''s for all connect speeds, and unlimited speeds/pw''s.\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                 Installation!\n                                ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nIf you run /X 3.x, copy all files I''ve supplied and you''re almost set.\n\nIf you run /X 2.x or S-Express, insert the followin line to your\n"commands/sys.cmd" file.\n\n---( cut )---\nSPEEDPW   XM001DOORS:SpeedPass/SpeedPass.x\n---( cut )---\n\nThe first thing you have to do is to edit the SpeedPass.x.info icon. There are\none special keyword wich you can use.\n\nATTEMPTS=3\n\nThis let the user guess 3 times at the pw before he''s kicked. Besides this you\nmay put any baudrate in the icon.\n\n2400=PassWord\n\nThis sets the 2400 password to "PassWord". The passwords are NOT case\nsensetive. You may add as many of these as you want.\n\nThe last thing to do is to put the following in fex your "GuestLogon.txt" in\norder to have the door run at every newuser logon.\n\n---( cut )---\n~\n~CC_SPEEDPW|\n---( cut )---\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                 These are the ß-sites for all my doors/utils!\n                ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n       Asylum Altered State #1       Juan               ++46-317-759378\n       Asylum Altered State #2       Juan               ++46-317-759376\n       Disorder                      Marwin             ++46-456-27511\n       Imagine                       Rille              ++46-42-135505\n       Total Inferno                 Tango              ++46-42-234164\n       Twisted Society               The Big Byte       ++46-44-106144\n\nAll my utils should be free dl, otherwise tell me and I''ll kick that ß-tester.\nIf you want to ß-test my doors/utils, contact me and we''ll work something out.\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                  Greetings!\n                                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~\n    Melone - Krusty - Hoot - Marwin - Manta - The Big Byte - Norad - Venger\n    Zendor - Mike - Luca - Abbe - Stuff - Broder - Zync - Zych - La Fayette\n     Axe - Nebraska - Eracore - Linus - Avalon - Nero - Dixy - Crux - Nuke\n   Fuze - Fix - Kain - Prospex - Canaima - Pripps - Hilbert - Mital - D-Zire\n        Jucke - Double - E-Go - Distler - Sy-Klone - Fazer - Zcandaler\n   Beavis & Butthead - Renko - Juan - Guardian - EaSy RiDeR - Wozzy - Suggs\n                            Rille - Fonus - Proctor\n\nForgive me if I forgot someone. It''s not easy to remember everybody you know!\n\n[EOF]\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',15816,3,0,NULL,NULL,'dpl_sp10','scan',1780048488);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dpl_st10','DPL_ST10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DPL_ST10.LHA','*','XIM','stfc100',NULL,'LinuS/DPL','DPL','_  _ ______ \____________/\_   /\____ : |Li! /   /  \  /  ____  \ /  /      \¦ |   /   /   / /  //  /  //__/   /   /|',replace('  _ _________  \n _  _ ______ \____________/\_   /\____ :\n  |Li! /   /  \  /  ____  \ /  /      \¦\n  |   /   /   / /  //  /  //__/   /   /| \n  ¦  /  _/   / /  //  ___/ \  \ _/   / ¦\n  :  \______/____//  / \______/_____/  :\n  +--------------/__/--(Presents)------+ \n  | StatisFaction V1.0      /X-DOOR!!! |\n  |         Coded by LinuS/DPL         |\n  `------------------------------1994--''\n','\n',char(10)),'stfc100.doc',replace('      _ __ ___________ ________/\ __________ ________  ___________\n          \\_______  ¬\__     /  \_______  ¬\__     /_ \__    _  ¬\_ __ _\n  .---------/     /    /     /    /    ______/     / ¬\_/     /    //-----.\n  |--------/     /    /     /    /     /----/     /    /     /    /-------|\n  |·DUPLO·/     /    /     /    /     /    /     /    /     /    /·DUPLO!·|\n  |------/_____     /_____     /\    /----/_____     /_____     /---------|\n  `----------/_____/----/_____/--\  /kRm------/_____/----/_____/----------''\n                                  \/\n\n\nHy and welcome to my Statisfaction door for Ur AMiexpress!\nFIRST one thing: I HATE TYPING DOCs!   ;)\n\nOk this door is really simple to install and use! You only need a working\nversion of amiexpress or S-express(!!) and a AEDOOR.LIBRARY!\nI only descripe the installation for amiex 2.x and S-express because I \n*HATE* the `icon-war` AMiex 3.x!\n\n\n\nWHAT DID the door do?!\n\nThats easy! This door shows the Stats of the logged on USER! THATS ALL!!\nI know really not good but I hate the output of the buildin stats of /X\nand S-epress! So I`ve coded this one with a nice output I think!\n\nYou could change the "STATS" logo if you want to! You have to save our\nfavorite ascii or something else at the s: directory with the name\nSTFC.TITLE thats all!\n\n\nhere is the bbs.cmd add line ;)\n\n+-+-+-+-+-+-+-CUT HERE\n\n*S        XM010DOORS:STFCv1.0/STFC100\n\n-+-+-+-+-+-+-+CUT again!\n\n\nThats all! The /X 3.x Users have to install made their own fucking Tool-\ntype! Have fun!!\n\n\n\nLiNuS/DPL`94    This is UPLOADWARE UL somthing at my BBS!! +49 6723 5622!\n\n\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',19383,5,0,NULL,NULL,'dpl_st10','scan',1780048488);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dpl_te10','DPL-TE10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DPL-TE10.LHA','TestLZX','XIM','TestLZX','1.0','Tango/DPL','DPL',NULL,replace('TestLZX v1.0, by Tango/DPL                  \n','\n',char(10)),'TestLZX.guide',replace('@database TestLZX\n@author Tango/Duplo\n@$VER: TestLZX.guide 1.0 (18.02.95)\n\n@node MAIN "TestLZX v1.0 Documentation"\n\n .           ________    ____.__   ______________.      _______\n `--.___ _ __\\_____  \\__/    |  \\__\\______  \\    |   __/  ___  \\\n  - |___\\\\\\\\__   |    \\__    |   \\__   _____/    |___\\__   |    \\_ _ ___.\n    `        |_____    /|_____    /|___  |  |_____    /|____     ////___| -\n    .------------\\____/-----\\____/---\\___|------\\____/-dNo\\_____/-------''\n    |\n    :                             PRESENTS:\n    .\n                      [- TestLZX v1.0, by Tango/DPL -]\n\n                      [- Contents of Documentation! -]\n\n                          @{"    Copyright Note    " Link Copyright}\n                          @{"   Archive Contents   " Link Archive}\n                          @{"     Installation     " Link Installation}\n                          @{"        History       " Link History}\n                          @{"    How to Reach Me   " Link Reach}\n                          @{"       Greetings      " Link Greetings}\n\n                                                            ©1995 - Tango/DPL\n@endnode\n\n@node Copyright "TestLZX v1.0 Documentation"\n\n                          Copyright ©1995 Tango/DPL\n\n The author of this product take no responseabilty for any lost, destroyed or\n                   corrupted data this product may cause.\n\nPermission is granted to freely distribute this product through any media for\n non-commercial purposes, as long as the release archive remains unmodified.\n@endnode\n\n@node Archive "TestLZX v1.0 Documentation"\n\nContents of DPL-TE10.LHA\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nfile_id.diz                467 bytes   Description file.\nTestLZX.guide             3397 bytes   This guide.\nFCheck/lzx.info            584 bytes   FCheck icon for /X 3.0+.\nUtils/TestLZX              900 bytes   The checker itself.\n@endnode\n\n@node Installation "TestLZX v1.0 Documentation"\n\nThe template for the checker is:\n\n   TestLZX FILE/A TEST/S ADD/K\n\nFILE  -  This is the name of the file to be checked. It must allways be\n         present for the checker to work! =)\nTEST  -  This switch specifies wether or not the file should be checked or\n         not.\nADD   -  With this keyword you can specify file(s) to be added to the\n         archive.\n\nLook at the example file, "FCheck/lzx.info" if you don''t know how to use this\nchecker. It shouldn''t be too hard to understand then.\n@endnode\n\n@node History "TestLZX v1.0 Documentation"\n\nv1.0  -  [RELEASE 1] This version. Features testing and adding to LZX-files!\n@endnode\n\n@node Reach "TestLZX v1.0 Documentation"\n\n                I''m frequently calling the following boards!\n\n             Aces High, Atlantic, Dragonlance, Far Out, Imagine,\n     Serpent Hill (as [KRUSTY&TANGO]), Undercover, Virtual Intelligence\n                               and White Room.\n\n You may also call my own board, Inferno, at ++46-42-234164. However, you''ll\n                        need an invitation to get in.\n@endnode\n\n@node Greetings "TestLZX v1.0 Documentation"\n\n              I want to greet the following persons, no order!\n\n  Melone, Krusty, Scroud, Hoot, Norad, Abbe, Eracore, Kain, Prospex, Jucke,\n    Double, Zcandaler, Renko, Juan, Ezco, Rille, Nightshade, Gryzor, Rix,\n                Demax, Dino, Christ, Taste, Dalamar, Aquarius\n\n                       Forgive me if I forgot someone!\n@endnode\n\n[EOF]\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',3036,1,0,NULL,NULL,'dpl_te10','scan',1780048488);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dpl_tl10','DPL_TL10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DPL_TL10.LHA','TaoList','XIM','TaoList',NULL,NULL,'DPL','.\____ \   /   _____   /  /\___  \---------. |/   /  \ /   / ______/  /   \/   \        | /_______/___ /   / /   _/\________/  DUPLO |',replace(' ____/\_____/\___________________           \n.\____ \   /   _____   /  /\___  \---------.\n|/   /  \ /   / ______/  /   \/   \        |\n/_______/___ /   / /   _/\________/  DUPLO |\n|          \/__ / /_______\-Mo!            |\n¦-------------\/---------------------------¦\n|            P R E S E N T S :             |\n|   TaoList v1.0, the fastest, smallest,   |\n| coolest & nicest userlister to this day! |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'TaoList.doc',replace('\n        .\n        :    :\n        :   /|\n        |  / | t A N G o                  _______\n        ._/  |___ _ ____________ _______ |      /_____________________\n       _ _   ___/____________   \     _ \|     /___________________   \\n        :    |     \      ______ \     \ \    / \______    |      |  . \_\n        :    l      \_    \    /  \_    \ \  /       |     |      ''     /\n      _ :_______     /_____\       /____|\  /______  `     |__________ /\n        |  -mNt\____/       \ ____/       \/      `--------''         \/\n        |                    \/                                      :\n        |                       o F   D U P L o                      |\n        |                                                            |\n        `---------------------- P R E S E N t S ----------------- - -''\n\n                                 TaoList v1.0\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                Important note!\n                               ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThis util is released under the concept of tradeware. If you like it and use\nit, upload some on my board. I will not take any responsability for whatever\nthis door does with your computer (It wont do anything but what it should, but\nyou never know what those lamers do!).\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                 What it does!\n                                ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThis simple litle program creats a userlist!\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                            Why use this one then!\n                           ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n                      * It''s the smallest on the market!\n                      * It''s fast!\n                      * It''s coded in pure C!\n                      * It''s free from backdoors!\n                      * It has a nice output!\n                      * It''s made by me! :)\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                 Installation!\n                                ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nCopy the program to a place where you can reach it, preferably BBS:Utils.\n\nInsert the following line in your logoffbatch and change it for your needs!\n\n---( cut )---\nTaoList BBS:user.data BBS:Conf1/Bulletins/Bull10.txt\n---( cut )---\n\nIf used in a SHELL-window you can skip the bulletin path and have an output in\nthe console window instead.\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                 These are the ß-sites for all my doors/utils!\n                ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n           Disorder               Marwin             ++46-456-27511\n           Forbidden Dreams       Manta              ++46-411-12894\n           Total Inferno          Tango              ++46-42-234164\n           Twisted Society        The Big Byte       ++46-44-106144\n\nAll my utils should be free dl, otherwise tell me and I''ll kick that ß-tester. \nIf you want to ß-test my doors/utils, contact me and we''ll work something out.\n\n«-----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                                  Greetings!\n                                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~\n    Melone - Krusty - Hoot - Marwin - Manta - The Big Byte - Norad - Venger\n    Zendor - Mike - Luca - Abbe - Stuff - Broder - Zync - Zych - La Fayette\n     Axe - Nebraska - Eracore - Linus - Avalon - Nero - Dixy - Crux - Nuke\n   Fuze - Fix - Kain - Prospex - Canaima - Pripps - Hilbert - Mital - D-Zire\n                  Jucke - Double - E-Go - Distler - Sy-Klone\n\nForgive me if I forgot someone. It''s not easy to remember everybody you know!\n\n[EOF]\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',14425,6,0,NULL,NULL,'dpl_tl10','scan',1780048488);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dpl_tm10','DPL-TM10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DPL-TM10.LHA',NULL,'XIM','TempAnsMover',NULL,NULL,'DPL',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'auto-added',16136,0,0,NULL,NULL,'dpl_tm10','scan',1780048488);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dpl_txad','DPL-TXAD.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DPL-TXAD.LHA','TxtAdder','XIM','TxtAdder',NULL,NULL,'DPL',NULL,replace('TXTADDER VERSION 3.3\n','\n',char(10)),'TxtAdder.doc',replace('\n                        TxtAdder V3.3 - by Tango/DPL''94\n\n[-----------------------------------------------------------------------------]\n\nThe history of TxtAdder V3.3\n\nThis TxtAdder is available to you for one simple reason! About half a year ago\nMarwin/Defiance asked me to do a TxtAdder for him. I made a quick one in pascal\nthat finaly was able to add one logo at front, at back or both at front and\nback. Marwin gave me a few hints how to make the program better, but I was too\nlazy to finnish it! :( The some months ago I learned C and after some weeks\nMarwin asked me once again to finnish my TxtAdder. Therefor I rewrote it in C\nand added a few cool options. First of all you''re able to add the current date\nto the textfile uploaded. "What''s so fucking special about that!?" I here you\nall scream, but! This is not the only feature! This txtadder in fact has a\nfeature wich I''ve never seen! It can add unlimited numbers of adds to the file.\nBut, more about that in the rest of the doc. At last I just want to say a _BIG_\nhello to Marwin, who''s one of my best friend on the scene!\n\n[-----------------------------------------------------------------------------]\n\nNormal documentation!\n\nFirst of all I just want to warn you a little. The errorchecking routines in\nthis program are not what they could be. If something happens it just exits\nsilently. It should not leave any files open or so, but try not to mess around\nwith the special files it creates!\n\nThe configfile, named "TxtAdder.cnf" shold look as follows! Remember, it will\n_NOT_ work with comments! The name of the configfile is "S:TxtAdder.cfg"\n(not changable, sorry!)\n\n-----< cut >----------\n1S:Board1.add\n3S:Board2.add\n-----< cut >----------\n^     ^\n|     |\n|     `----> This is the path and name of the file to add!\n|\n`----------> This tells the adder where to add the logo, 1 = FRONT, 2 = BOTH\n             and 3 = END.\n\nIn all textfiles exept the sourcefile the textadder will check for the string\n$DATE_STR (case sensetive) and will enter todays date over it. So, if you put\nthe string in a file you add the date will be exchanged with the string. Simple\neh!? I have included some sample files wich will work if you want to check the\nadder out.\n\n[-----------------------------------------------------------------------------]\n\nThe greets!\n\n   MARWIN         - Thanx for all the encouragement!\n   KRU5TY         - Thanx for the coolest ASCII-style ever!\n   MELONE         - One of my best friends and cool trader!\n   D0UBLE         - You Norweigan squit! ;)\n   MIKE           - Get to know this guy! He''s cool and very friendly!\n   THE BIG BYTE   - Thanx for all the help with my 030''s!\n\nTo everybody else - Call my board and upload some if ya like this util! The \n                    name and numba is:  ToTAL iNFERNo +46-42-234164!\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',7237,3,0,NULL,NULL,'dpl_txad','scan',1780048488);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dpl_un11','DPL_UN11.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DPL_UN11.LHA','UserNuke','XIM','UserNuke',NULL,'Tango/DPL','DPL','.\____ \   /   _____   /  /\___  \---------. |/   /  \ /   / ______/  /   \/   \        | /_______/___ /   / /   _/\________/  DUPLO |',replace(' ____/\_____/\___________________\n.\____ \   /   _____   /  /\___  \---------.\n|/   /  \ /   / ______/  /   \/   \        |\n/_______/___ /   / /   _/\________/  DUPLO |\n|          \/__ / /_______\-Mo!            |\n¦-------------\/---------------------------¦\n|             PRESENTS ToDAY:              |\n|       UserNuke v1.1 - by Tango/DPL       |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'Mea_culpa.txt',replace('  --------------------- DENMARKS FINEST BBS SYSTEM ------------------------\n  \n     QUARTEX DANISH HQ\n\n     T.E.K. DIST. SITE        /\   SYSOP : PENNYWISE    \n     ___  ___  ___________   /  \  ~~~~~ \n    /   \/   \ \  ________) /    \  COs  : MAC / T.E.K.\n   /          \/  ___)___  /   _  \ ~~~    DRIZZT / RED ARROWS\n  /     \/    \\         \/    /  \\        \n /     _/      \\_      //    _    \\  \n/______\_________/______/_____/      \_\n ~~~~~~ ~~~~~~~~~ ~~~~~~ ~~~~/________/\n                ANSI BY MARC  ~~~~~~~~                         /\\n               ___________  ___ ___    _______ ___________    /  \ \n AMIGA 0-DAYZ  \         / /   |   \  /      / \______    \  /    \   \n H.P.A. CONF   //   /___/\//   |   \\//     /__ /     \    \/   _  \   \n WARZONE     _//   /     \\_   |    \\_    /   X_     /____/    /  \\   \n SUPER NES   \             /   ¦      /  _/     /      ~\_     _    \\  \n /X CONF      \___________/__________/_________/_________/_____/      \_\n               ~~~~~~~~~~~ ~~~~~~~~~~ ~~~~~~~~~ ~~~~~~~~~ ~~~~/________/\n                DIAL + 45  75 12 70 52  FOR A DUAL CONNECTION  ~~~~~~~~\n                       ~~  ~~ ~~ ~~ ~~\n \n ---------------------- WHERE THE REAL ELITE COMES -----------------------\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',17034,4,0,NULL,NULL,'dpl_un11','scan',1780048488);
