INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dtc_sr1f','DTC-SR1F.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DTC-SR1F.LHA',NULL,'XIM','Sr10.x',NULL,'kRs!/DTC','DTC','============= |   \_   _/ __/ ============ DiGiTAl ChAoS | I> \| || (___ /X^DD  DiVSN ============= |____/|_| \___/ ============',replace('               ______________                \n============= |   \_   _/ __/ ============       \nDiGiTAl ChAoS | I> \| || (___ /X^DD  DiVSN\n============= |____/|_| \___/ ============                     \n             ..p.r.e.s.e.n.t.s..\n.----------------------------------------.\n|    SySTeM ReSeT  V1.0  by kRs!/DTC     |\n`----------------------------------------''	  \nSyStEM REbOotER TooL 4 /X aNd DaYDreAm BBS\nDiSplAys LaST SySTEm ReBooT - NiCE AnSIgfX\nPwPrOtECteD SySOp MOdE - FaST''n''EaZy 2 UsE\n-- AmIgaGUiDE DoC FiXeD In ThIS ReLEaSe --\n','\n',char(10)),'SR10.GuidE',replace('@DATABASE "Default"\n@NODE "MAIN" "SyStEm ReSEt  1.0"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n             .                          .\n             ¡\                         \\/.\n  _____/\____| \______/\_____/\  ___/\___\//\\n /  _____)   |  \   ____/    _ \/   . \_ \/  \           .-------.\n \______ \   i   \____. \____/  \_  i__/ ..   \_ .-------+-------+------.\n   /   /  \____.  /   i  \_/     /  ._)  ¡¡    / | D¡G¡TaL cHaOs |      |\n   \  /    /   i /        /\    /   i \_ ||   /  |     /X''n''DD D¡V¡S¡On |\n    \_____/\__  /\_______/  \  /\____  /_!|  /   `-------+-------+------''\n <---------. \_/ .-----------\/-----\_/--:l_/------------''       |\n           |     |                                               `--.\n         .-+-----+----.           .___/\____/\_____/\____/\______/\ |\n         | `-----''    |           ¡   _ \_  . \_ ____/   . \_    _ \`--.\n         | GfX:   LrY |           |   ___/  i__/___. \   i__/____/  \_ |\n         | cOdE:  kRs |           |  .  \   ._)    i  \_ ._)   /     / |\n     <---+------------+-------.   |  ¡   \_ i \_       / i \_  \    /  |\n         `------------''       |   l__|    /__  /______/___  /   \  /   |\n                              `------l___/--\_/----------\_/-----\/----''\n          \n @{" What iS It? " LINK "WHATIS"}  @{" InSTaLLaTioN " LINK "INSTALL"}  @{" D¡GiTaL ChAøS " LINK "DTC"}  @{" GrEetiNgS " LINK "GREETS"}  @{" CrEdItS " LINK "CREDS"}  \n\n           \n                                                             [ 24.4.95 ] \n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "WHATIS" "WhAT Is It?"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n(-) What Is It? (-)\n\nSySteM ResEt can be used in two different ways:  normal users can use it to\nsee  when your system has been last rebooted, while co/sysops can use it to\nreset the system from remote.\n\nWhat  does this tool do?  You (Da SySoP) run it, it asks you the magic word\n(Ie:   a  password),  it  asks  you  if  you  are  really  sure  and then..\nthree..two..one...   the  computer is reset and you loose the CARRIER.  You\ncan  wait  a few minutes, then you can try to call your board again, to see\nif it has been able to reboot and to get online again..  Great..  you could\nsay..  but you could also have some doubts about the utility of this tool..\nWell,  imagine  you are on holiday or however far from home and you have to\ncontrol  your  board from remote or (in the worst way =) you have to let it\nin  the  hands  of  your  cosysops..   Now,  if  there''s the need to change\nsomething  in the board configuration (modify some conferences, some access\npresets,  some  commands..)  what  do  you  do?   You  can enter the shell,\ndownload  the  config  files (if u''re using DayDream) or the icons of which\nyou  need  to  change  tooltypes  (/X),  you modify them and in the end you\nupload  them  again  in the right directories.  But at this time the system\nwon''t  see  the changes until it is rebooted..  But you''re from remote, you\ncan''t  press  CTRL-A-A or quit your board and restart it..  Here it is, you\nuse SySTeM ReSeT.  Okee?  `)\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "INSTALL" "InStAllATiON"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\n(-) InSTaLL''n''CoNfIguRe (-)\n\nFirst  of  all:   this  is an /X XIM DOOR but you can use it 100% also on a\nDayDream  system, you only need the DD-Xim V2.0 by DarkElf/Access.  I think\nthat  if  you''re  using  DayDream  you''ll have it, ''cause it''s great and it\nallows  you  to use many /X doors.  However, if you haven''t it you can find\nit on DTC boards (Another reason to call them =).\n\nThe  file  SR.CFG  is  read  when  the door is run and if it''s not found in\nDOORS:DTC/  path,  the  door  exits.  This file is made up of 2 lines:  the\npassword required to reset the system and the minimum access level required\nto  enter SySoP mODe.  I strongly suggest you to install also SRL.X in your\nS:USER-STARTUP,  so that SyTeM ReSeT will be able to display date''n''time of\nyour last system reboot.\n\n\n+++ /X INSTALLATION: +++\n\nJust  copy SR.CFG in DOORS:DTC/ but consider that this path is HARDCODED in\nthe  door  and  you  can''t  change  it.   Put the icon file (RESET.INFO) in\nBBSCMD.  Put SR.x wherever you want.\n\n\n+++ DayDream INSTALLATION: +++\n\nCopy  SR.CFG  in  DOORS:DTC/  then  add  the  new  command to your daydream\nconfiguration file, compile it and dream =)..\n\nExample:\n\nDOOR_COMMAND.. RESET\nDOOR_TYPE..... 1\nDOOR_SECURITY. 50\nDOOR_EXECUTE.. Doors:XIM %N DOORS:DTC/SR10/SR.x  \n+\n\nGive  System  Reset  a  standard access level (users will see only when you\nlast rebooted) and make sure you set a co/sysop level for the SySOp MoDe in\nSR.CFG).\n\nThat''s all guys!\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "DTC" "DiGiTal ChAOS"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\n                  /\             /\   ___\n                 // \           // \_|   |___   ___               __\n        _/\____  \  /  _/\_____ \  /         )_|.  |             /_/\\n        ).     \ /\/\  ).      \/\/\__   ___/  \|  !             \_\/\n        |: ___  \    \//  _____//   \|   |  _   \  | __\n _  /\__|¦ \ /   \    \   |   \      \   |  Y.   \ |/. \          /\\n  \/    |   Y    /    /   |    \     /   |__||    \ /   \__/\    /  \\n  __    |_____  /_  _/\_____   /_  _/|   |  |__  _/__  _/    \  /    \__ _\n /_/\         \/_ \/       \__/  \/   \ /      \/    \/       \/\n \_\/         /_/\             _/\_.   Y\n              \_\/    _/\____  )   ¦   :/\___  _______  _/\____\n                      ). _   \/.   !_  ). _  \/  ___  \/   _   \   /\\n    _  _ __    /\  __//  Y___//  _   \//  Y   \  \ /.  \_  Y___/__/  \  _ _\n           \  /  \/ /    |   )   Y.   \   _    \  Y/   / \_    )      \/\n            \/      \____  _/____||    \__Y     \___  /____  _/LrY    __\n                         \/      !__  _/  !__  _/   \/     \/        /_/\\n                                    \/       \/                      \_\/\n\n ÐIGITal CHA0$ iS LOOkInG fOR neW mEMbers ... WE nEED :\n\n                        [1-2] CoÐe®(s)\n             --!!!--->  [4-5] 7RaÐe®(S) (aMiGa)   <---!!!--    \n                        [1-2] MuSicIan(s)\n                        [1-2] SysTEm(s) FO® Ds\n\n                           @{" > Contacts < " LINK "POINT"} \n                          @{" ! MeMbEr LisT ! " LINK "MEMBERS"}\n                        @{" =)  SoFToGrApHy  (= " LINK "PRODS"}\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "POINT" "PoInT Of No ReTuRN"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n_____ ______ ___ ______ _______      __   __  +--------------------------+\n|    ¬¥     ¬¥  ¬¥     ¬¥      ¬\   (__) |-   |S¥SØP:  H a n t a r e X   |\n|: :  |:  ¡  |:  |:     |_     _/             |CØS¥S:  I c e   M c       |\n|°  _/|°  |  |°  |°  ¡  | ¥   ¥               |                          |\n|   | |   |  |   |   |  | |  °|     . :  __   |RµNN¡N''øN: a12oo/o3o/40Mhz|\nl__|| l______7___7___|__; l__||     |\| (__)  |           7MegsRAM-/X 4.7|\n   ::                        ::     :         |                          |\n    :                         :               | F®¡eNdly SySøP - Nø NµP  |\n :                                            |Ea$¥ RaT¡ø$ - Ø Day$ F¡Le$|\n |:_____ ______ _______ ___ __ ______ ______  | Amy & PC Conf. - H/P/A   |\n || __ ¬¥  __