INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('dtc_td15','DTC-TD15.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/DTC-TD15.LHA',NULL,'XIM','Td.X',NULL,'kRs!/DTC','DTC','============= |   \_   _/ _/  ============ DiGiTAl ChAoS | I> \| || (__  /X  DiViSiON ============= |____/|_| \___\ ============',replace('               ______________                  \n============= |   \_   _/ _/  ============       \nDiGiTAl ChAoS | I> \| || (__  /X  DiViSiON\n============= |____/|_| \___\ ============                     \n             ..p.r.e.s.e.n.t.s..\n.----------------------------------------.\n|    ToP DoWNlOAdS V1.5  by kRs!/DTC     |\n`----------------------------------------''	  \nDoWnLOaDs TopTen MaKer..JuSt hAvE a lOoK!!\nGrEaT ANSI looKinG.. IFFs ExAmpLEs InSidE.','\n',char(10)),'TD15.GuidE',replace('@DATABASE "Default"\n@NODE "MAIN" "ToP DoWnlOAdS 1.5"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n_____/\  ___/\  ___/\       __                            <     __\n\    _ \/     \/    _\_    (__)   - D¡G¡TaL ChAøS /X D¡V¡S¡øN  (__)\n \___/  \_ ¡   \_  ___/__       __\n   /     / |    /  |_/\\/______\\/..____/\.___.  /____ .___/\ .__/\____/\_\n   \    /      /   |   \/   \  \\/_¡___.  \   ¡|//    \¡  .  \¡    \  ___/\n    \  /\_____/\   | |  \_ _ \_ \/    /:   \_ |_/_  _  \_ i   \_ |  \___.\\n <---\/--------.\__| |   / Y  / /   ./ |    / |   \_Y   / .    / |   /  i \_\n   GfX: LrY    | |   l  /  ; /     //  |   /  l_   /;  /  ¡   /  l  /      /\n  cODE: kRs!   | l_____/\___/\_/\__/___|  /\___   /___/l__|  /l____/\_____/\n   VeR: 1.5    `-----------------------l_/-----\_/--------l_/-------------->\n            \n\n@{" (?) What it is? (?) " LINK "WHATIS"}                               @{" (/) InSTaLLaTioN (\) " LINK "INSTALL"}\n\n            @{" (*) D¡GiTaL ChAøS (*) " LINK "DTC"}       @{" (!) GrEtInGs (!) " LINK "GREETS"}\n                        \n                              @{" (C) CrEdItS (C) " LINK "CREDS"}\n\n                                                                 [ 23.2.95 ] \n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "WHATIS" "WhAT It Is?"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n(-) What it is? (-)\n\n*)  Top  Downloads is an /X utility that creates bullettins with the 9 most\ndownloaded  files  of  your  board,  or  of a particular conference of your\nboard.   It isn''t a XIM door, it''s a simple CLI program that you can run as\na  IIM  DOOR or in any other way you want (batch logoff files, other logoff\ndoors etc.)\n*)  It is based on the scanning of /X UDLOG and it''s very flexible allowing\nyou  to  create  separate  topten  bullettins  for  each conference, global\nbulletins  with  the  most  downloaded  files of your board (so of all your\nconferences) or also of only some particular conferences..\n*) Top Downloads generates simple (but very great looking =) ANSI bulletins\nthat  you  can  show  in your board in the way you prefer (as bulletins, as\nbull.txt of a conference, as the nodeX/bull.txt, as the sysop paging screen\n=).\n*)  I  have to say that I hadn''t ever seen a /X utility like this in the /X\nscene,  so,  10x  to  Mind Melter''s idea, I think I''ve made something quite\nnew.\n\nNothing else to say..  Let''s go to the InSTaLL''n''CoNfIguRe section..\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "INSTALL" "InStAllATiON"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n(-) InSTaLL''n''CoNfIguRe (-)\n\nFirst  of all create in DOORS:  a DTC directory (DOORS:DTC) that will store\nall  the TD.CFGx configuration files you''ll need to run Top Downloads.  You\ncan create as many TD.CFGx (x = 0,1,2,3 ecc.) as you want, considering that\neach  TD.CFGx  will  create  a different topten bullettin.  You can edit or\ncreate TD.CFGx with a simple ASCII editor (CED or Amigados'' Ed like).\nTop Downloads reads the TD.CFGx starting from TD.CFG0, so BE SURE IT ALWAYS\nEXISTS.   Then, if you want only one bulletin you only need the config file\nTD.CFG0\n\nThis is the format of TD.CFGx files:\n\nLine 1:  bbs:node0/udlog    <------ /X  Udlog  name  with  path.   \nLine 2:  bbs:node0/bull.txt <------ Output bulletin name with path.\n\nNow you have to tell the program which conferences have to be considered in\nthe topten making and how to identify them in the UDLOG.\nYou''ll  have to write two config lines per conference, writing in the first\nline  the  PATH TO THE DOWNLOAD DIR OF THECONFERENCE and in the second line\nthe CONFERENCE NAME THAT WILL BE USED IN THE BULLETIN..\nLike this: \n\nLine 3:  BBS:PICS/DOWNLOADS <------ Path to conference''s download dir.\nLine 4:  -* XXX PiCtUreS -* <------ Conference NAME showed in the bullettin\n\nIn this way you''ll have a topten bulletin only for the pictures conference,\nif  you  want a topten with other conferences simply add them in the config\nfile..\nLike this:\n\nLine 5:  BBS:PC/DOWNLOADS   <------ Path to conference''s download dir.\nLine 6:  wC =) MS-DOS Cw =) <------ Conference NAME showed in the bullettin\n\nAnd  so  on..   If  you  want  a  SINGLE GLOBAL TOPTEN BULLETIN FOR ALL THE\nCONFERENCES of your board add them all in one single config file..\n\nIf  on  the  contrary  you  want  SEPARATE  TOPTEN  BULLETINS FOR DIFFERENT\nCONFERENCES  just  make  different  TD.CFGx  files  putting  in  each one a\ndifferent output bulletin name and a different conference..  Simply..\nIsn''t it? =)\n\n***  IMPORTANT  *** The Path to conference''s download dir (Lines 3 and 5 in\nthis  example)  is  CASE  SENSITIVE  and  is  looked for in the UDLOG, so I\nsuggest  you  to  have  a look at your UDLOG and copy the PATHS as they are\nwritten.\n---------------------------- (Cut from UdLog) -----------------------------\n\n	Downloading DC0:DOWNLOAD/MANGA/lemon04.gif 64315 bytes\n                    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nIn this case you should write DC0:DOWNLOAD/MANGA/ in your config file.\n\nThen you have to decide when you want the bulletins created to be showed, I\nsuggest  you  to  show the global bulletin with all the conferences, during\nthe  logon procedure (bbs:NODEx/bull.txt), and the one-conference-bulletins\nat  the  joining  of  the  various  conferences  (NODEx/confname/bull.txt).\nObviously you can use the MCI ~SS_filename\n\nYou  can put the TD.X executable wherever you want, just run it when a user\nlog off from your system.  Do it with a logoff batch script, using a logoff\ndoor  or  with a MCI ~CC_TD into your logoff screen, but if you use the MCI\ncommand  be  sure  you  have  the  TD.INFO in the SYSCMD directory with the\ntooltype  TYPE=IIM.   If you want the topten updated once in a day run TD.X\nwith an event manager, it doesn''t matter..\n\nIn  the  end..   Consider  about  deleting or cutting your UDLOG sometimes,\nbecause  the  UDLOGSCANNINGFILELOCATINGSTRIPPING''n''SORTING  routine  of Top\nDownloads isn''t  very  fast  and if your Udlog is huge the program can take\nsome  minutes  to process it, even on fast machines..  (I''m sorry about it,\nbut it''s not my fault, processing the UDLOG takes a lot of time and I think\nit''s not possible to do much better..  =)\n\nThat''s all.. EnJoY ThE CøOLnEsS!! `)\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "DTC" "DiGiTal ChAOS"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\n                  /\             /\   ___\n                 // \           // \_|   |___   ___               __\n        _/\____  \  /  _/\_____ \  /         )_|.  |             /_/\\n        ).     \ /\/\  ).      \/\/\__   ___/  \|  !             \_\/\n        |: ___  \    \//  _____//   \|   |  _   \  | __\n _  /\__|¦ \ /   \    \   |   \      \   |  Y.   \ |/. \          /\\n  \/    |   Y    /    /   |    \     /   |__||    \ /   \__/\    /  \\n  __    |_____  /_  _/\_____   /_  _/|   |  |__  _/__  _/    \  /    \__ _\n /_/\         \/_ \/       \__/  \/   \ /      \/    \/       \/\n \_\/         /_/\             _/\_.   Y\n              \_\/    _/\____  )   ¦   :/\___  _______  _/\____\n                      ). _   \/.   !_  ). _  \/  ___  \/   _   \   /\\n    _  _ __    /\  __//  Y___//  _   \//  Y   \  \ /.  \_  Y___/__/  \  _ _\n           \  /  \/ /    |   )   Y.   \   _    \  Y/   / \_  