INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ecl_ex13','ECL_EX13.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ECL_EX13.LHA','c','XIM','Exorcist!.x',NULL,NULL,'ECL','Sysop : a very kewl FAKE door with sum oth functions (Award uploads, comment, etc.) I personally prefer this one instead of the',replace('Exorcist version 1.3 for /X\nSysop : a very kewl FAKE door with sum oth\nfunctions (Award uploads, comment, etc.)\nI personally prefer this one instead of the\nNosNuke.\n','\n',char(10)),'Exorcist!.doc',replace('      _ _______  _______        __    _ _______  _______  ______\n     / \\~~~~~~Y\\~~~~~~Y\     /~~\  /~\\~~~~~~Y\\~~~~~~Y\\~~~~~\\n    //  \\_____j \\_____j \    \___)//  \\___  j \\_____j \\_____)\n    \\  (____\\  (    \\  (     ____\\  (___/ /  (____\\  (___\n     \\  ~~_/ \\  \    \\  \    \~~~\\\  ~___/\___~~~~\\\  ~_/\n      \`   \_/\\`  \__/\\`  \__/\\\  \\`  \ ______)/   \\`  \__/\\n       \    ~  Y\   ~~  Y\   ~~  Y\`  Y\   Y~~~~~~      Y\   ~~  \\n        \______j \______j \______j \__j \__j____________j \______/\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n                                  present\n\n                                 EXORCIST!\n                            version 1.3, /X 2.3x\n\n                     (C) 1993  CFi & B/\Zz of Eclipse\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nTABLE OF CONTENTS\n----------------------------\n 1. PREFACE.......................................1\n 2. GETTING EXORCIST! TO WORK.....................2\n   2a. What does Exorcist! need to work...........2\n   2b. How to install Exorcist!...................2\n   2c. Configuring options in Exorcist!.cfg.......3 \n   2d. Starting Exorcist!.........................5\n 3. EXPELL (NUKE) FILES...........................5\n   3a What is expelling files.....................5\n   3b How do I use it.............................5\n   3c Tips on using the expell option.............7\n 4. AWARD FILES...................................7\n   4a What is awarding files......................7\n   4b How do I use it.............................7\n   4c Tips on using the award function............8\n 5. FREE FILES....................................8\n   5a What is freeing files.......................8\n   5b How do I use it.............................8\n   5c Tips on using the free function.............9\n 6. COMMENTING FILES..............................9\n   6a What is commenting files....................9\n   6b How do I use it.............................9\n   6c Tips on using the comment function.........10\n 7. RESURRECT OPTION.............................10\n   7a What is the resurrect option...............10\n   7b How do I use it............................10\n   7c Tips on using the resurrect option.........11\n 8. GENERAL INFORMATION..........................11\n   8a How does Exorcist! function................11\n   8b TroubleShooting............................12\n   8c Names and Addresses........................12\n   8d Disclaimer.................................13\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n1. PREFACE\n----------\nEverybody who owns or maintains a Bulletin Board System knows that not\nall uploads are of similar nature. Sometimes users upload things that have\nalready been uploaded. And sometimes users upload something of such value\nthat he ought to get more than his standard ratio for it. Also it would be\nnice to make files free-download without much fuss. To solve all these\nproblems and more, Eclipse made Exorcist!\nExorcist! is a /X utility that gives you the ability to perform certain \noperations on uploaded files. Although the most of the operations Exorcist!\ncan perform are also available in other programs (eg NosNUKE by Nosferatu),\nExorcist! combines a much higher speed (about 10 times faster than\nNosNUKE) with a greatly enhanced functionality. Exorcist! for instance\nsupports wildcards, multiple file selection, free-download option,\nmultiple access-level security and many more features.\nAlthough getting the grips with Exorcist! will probably not be as easy as\nwith simpler utilities like NosNUKE, its benefits will surely be worth the\neffort.\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\n2. GETTING EXORCIST! TO WORK\n----------------------------\n2a. What does Exorcist! need to work.\n\nAlthough Exorcist! is quite easy to get up and running, it demands certain\nthings of your system, and of your BBS.\nHardware Demands:\n- Exorcist! needs about a 120k of available RAM to work, as it enhances\n  it speed by searching out of RAM instead of from disk. Keep in mind that\n  using /X costs a lot of RAM (esp. multi-node) and Exorcist! only works as\n  an /X door.\n\nSoftware demands:\n- Exorcist! uses the UDlog or the Callerslog to search for uploaders and\n  downloaders. As it is possible in /X to disable/enable the UDlog or the\n  CallersLog you should check if one of these is enabled. If it is not,\n	Exorcist! will not be able to find uploaders and downloaders, making it\n  impossible to deduct or return credits. If you, in case of a disabled\n  UDlog or Callerslog , enable one of them, Exorcist! is only able to\n  find uploaders and downloaders whose actions are from a date later than\n  the date you enabled the log, as only those actions have been entered \n  in the log.\n- Exorcist must be able to access some files on your BBS-system. To tell\n  Exorcist! where he can find these files, you have to specify an option \n  in its config file: Exorcist!.cfg (see 2c.)\n- Exorcist! will work with most custom filelisters used on /X boards, but\n  as they are non-standard, Exorcist! can be incompatible with one. If you\n  use an incompatible filelister you can either use another one, or contact\n  us to see if we can make an adapted version that works with your \n  filelister.\n- As stated above, Exorcist! uses the UDlog to find uploaders and\n  downloaders, so you must be careful not to use any programs which alter\n  this log in a non-standard matter, or just plain wrong (like Freeleech). \n  Exorcist! can do strange things if you use such a program. \n  \n2b. How to install Exorcist!\n\nInstalling Exorcist! is about as easy as installing any other /X door,\nalthough Exorcist needs a config file with the right options specified to\nwork flawlessly.\n\nIn the Exorcist! package you will find the following files:\n - Exorcist!.x                : the 68000  version of Exorcist! for /X 2.3x\n - Exorcist!_030.x            : the 68020+ version of Exorcist! for /X 2.3x\n - Exorcist!.doc              : this file\n - Exorcist!.cfg              : a pre-defined config file\n - Exorcist!.update           : a list of changes made to each new version\n\nTo install Exorcist! you have to do the following:\n- Choose the version of Exorcist! which fits your configuration best.\n- Copy it to the place you prefer. Although it''s the easiest to copy it to\n  the to DOOR: assigned directory.\n- Copy the Exorcist!.cfg file in the same directory as the main program.\n  (We will describe possible alterations to this file later)\n- Make the following entry in your BBS.CMD file. This file is located in\n  the "BBS:Commands/" directory:\n  \n  [COMMAND]  XS[ACCESS][PATH]\n  \n  Where:\n  [COMMAND] : The command that must be typed in when logged on to your\n              bbs system to activate Exorcist!\n  [ACCESS]  : This is the lowest Accesslevel a person must have to be \n              able to use Exorcist!.\n  [PATH]    : This is the complete pathname (directory+filename) to where\n              you have copied the Exorcist! program file and the\n              Exorcist!.cfg config file.\n  Make sure that you put each part of the entry into the right column.\n  If you don''t this, everything might crash! (The exact format can be\n  found in your /X manual)  \n\n  An example entry is: EXORCIST  XS200DOORS:Exorcist!_030.x\n  Here you have to type EXORCIST to activate Exorcist!, you must have\n  Accesslevel 200 or higher, and the Exorcist! program file is located in\n  the to DOORS: assigned directory and is called Exorcist!_030.x (the\n  68020+ version for /X 2.3x)\n- Edit the config file to your needs. To see what options are available,\n  read the following sub-chapter.\n- You have now installed Exorcist! correctly.\n\n\n2c. Configuring options in Exorcist!.cfg\n\nTo configure Exorcist! to your likings and to have it functioning \noptimally, you have to edit the Exorcist!.cfg file.\nThis file contains all the currently active options. When adding an option,\nthink about these guidelines:\n- All options must be seperated by a linefeed.\n- If a line starts with a '';'', than that line will be seen as a comment\n  line. (EXAMPLE: ;This is a comment line)\n- You can use blank lines.\n- You may specify any number of spaces or tabs between the arguments\n  of a keyword, as long as all needed keywords are specified on the same\n  line. \n- All strings must be within quotation marks (")\n  This also implies that you cannot use the " character in strings.\n  (EXAMPLE: "HELLO", not ''HELLO'' or HELLO)\n\n\nThe following list contains all valid keywords for the Exorcist!.cfg file,\nmost of these options are optional, but if your board differs greatly from\nthe standard /X configuration, you''ll have to specify some options.\n\nSKIPNODE <number>[,<number>,...]\nLet''s you skip certain nodes in the search for the uploader. This option\ncan be useful to increase speed if you have a special sysop node, which\nyou don''t want to search. A good idea is also to specify all non-existing\nnodes upto 9 here.\nEXAMPLE: SKIPNODE 0,3,4,5,6,7,8,9\n\nSIZEMSG <1-8> <text[8]>\nYou can specify upto 8 custom size messages here. The message must be 8\ncharacters long. These messages will later be shown to you as optional\nsizedescriptors while expelling files. \nEXAMPLE: SIZEMSG 1 "ANCIENT!"\n\nDEFAULTSIZEMSG <number>\nHere you specify which size message should be used when the user selects\nan illegal size message. You can specify 1-8 for any of the with SIZEMSG\ndefined messages, 0 for no message, or 9 to let the user enter a\ncustom message. Default = 0.\nEXAMPLE: DEFAULTSIZEMSG 3\n\nEXPELLMSG <1-8> <text[50]>\nYou can specify upto 8 custom expell messages here. The message has a\nmaximum length of 50 characters. These messages will later be shown to\nyou as optional expell messages while expelling files.\nEXAMPLE: EXPELLMSG 1 "This one is old enough for the VIC-20"\n\nDEFAULTEXPELLMSG <number>\nHere you specify which expell message should be used when the user selects\nan illegal expell message. You can specify 1-8 for any of the with\nEXPELLMSG defined messages, 0 for no message, or 9 to let the user enter\na custom message. Default = 0.\nEXAMPLE: DEFAULTEXPELLMSG 1\n\nAWARDMSG <1-8> <text[50]> (0 = NONE, 9 = OTHER)\nYou can specify upto 8 custom award messages here. The message has a\nmaximum length of 50 characters. These messages will later be shown to\nyou as optional award messages while awarding files.\nEXAMPLE: AWARDMSG 2 ".oO WARE OF THE CENTURY Oo."\n\nDEFAULTAWARDMSG <number>\nHere you specify which award message should be used when the user selects\nan illegal award message. You can specify 1-8 for any of the with AWARDMSG\ndefined messages, 0 for no message, or 9 to let the user enter a custom\nmessage. Default = 0.\nEXAMPLE: DEFAULTAWARDMSG 2\n\nKEEPLOG\nSpecifying this command enables Exorcist! to keep a log file of all actions\nperformed. Note that a different logfile is kept for every node and that\nthese logfiles are kept in the BBS:node{x}/Exorcist!.log file, where {x} is\nthe node number. Remember to delete (parts of) the logfile now and then, as\nit keeps growing.\n\nSYSOPQUIET\nSpecifying this command disables Exorcist! to automatically send a message\nto the sysop. Normally the message is only send if the sysop is NOT the user.\n\nWILDCARDLEVEL <level>\nMake wildcards restricted to a certain accesslevel. \nDefault = 0 (This means that the standard level to enter the door is used).\nEXAMPLE: WILDCARDLEVEL 220 \n\nAWARDLEVEL <level>\nSet the minimal level required to award files. \nDefault = 0 (This means that the standard level to enter the door is used).\nEXAMPLE: AWARDLEVEL 220\n\nFREELEVEL <level>\nSet the minimal level required to make files freedownload. \nDefault = 0 (This means that the standard level to enter the door is used).\nEXAMPLE: FREELEVEL 220\n\nRESURRECTLEVEL <level>\nSet the minimal level required to resurrect (= un-nuke) files. \nDefault = 0 (This means that the standard level to enter the door is used).\nThis option only works in conjunction with the PROTECTFILES keyword!\nEXAMPLE RESURRECTLEVEL 250\n\nUSERDATAPATH <path>\nFull path including name, where user.data can be found. Default is\n"BBS:user.data". This option must be specified if your BBS has specified\nan user.data path in the acp.startup file. If you don''t specify this\nkeyword when needed, the users won''t be modified.\nEXAMPLE: USERDATAPATH "DH0:AMIX/userdata.ax"\n\nPROTECTFILES <path>\nSpecifying this means that Exorcist! will not delete the file that was \nexpelled. It will be moved to it the <path> specified and a directory with \nthe name of the file is created. \nThis option must be specified to be able to RESURRECT files.\nREMEMBER: All Expelled files will not be deleted! So you''ll have to\nclean up the directory specified now and then!\nEXAMPLE: PROTECTFILES "BBS:Resurrect/"\n(Exorcist! will not create the specified directory, so you must already\nhave created it for Exorcist!)\n\nCALLERSLOG\nThis option indicates that Exorcist! should use the callerslog instead of\nthe UDLog. This is handy if you don''t use the UDLog, the only disadvantage\nis that this option makes Exorcist! slower, since the Callerslog is\ngenerally larger than the UDLog.\n\nANONYMOUS\nSpecifying this means that the name of the user of Exorcist! will not be\ndisplayed with the messages specified.\n\n2d. Starting Exorcist!\n\nSince Exorcist! is a door you have to login to your BBS to be able to \nexecute Exorcist! If you are logged in, you have to type in the in your \nBBS.CMD file entered keyword. (If you don''t know this keyword, ask your\nsysop) Now Exorcist! will start.\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n3. EXPELL (NUKE) FILES\n----------------------\n3a. What is expelling files.\n\nIf some user has uploaded something you specifically do not want on your\nBBS, you can EXPELL the uploaded file. Doing this the following things\nhappen:\n- The file will be either deleted or moved to a non downloadable directory.\n- Instead of the file, a directory will be created with the same name as\n  the file. Since directory are not recognized by the system as files, it\n  now is impossible to download or upload the file (again). It is not\n  possible to expell a file twices.\n- You will get the opportunity to deduct the ''illegaly'' gained credits from\n  the uploader. It is also possible to multiply the deducted credits to\n  ''punish'' the uploader. \n- The number of uploads of the uploader will be reduced by 1 per file.\n- A comment will be added to the file in the file-dir about the expelling\n  of the file. (By whom, number of credits deducted, message etc.)\n- The credits of the people who downloaded the file can be returned.\n- There can be send messages to uploader, downloaders and the sysop of the\n  BBS, if he is not expelling the file himself.\n(Expelling Files is what NosNUKE calls NUKING files)\n\nAnother option is if you have seen a ''FAKE'' file(s) on another BBS. You can\nprotect your BBS from people uploading this/these file(s). \n\n3b. How do I use it.\n\nThere are two ways to use the expell option:\n\nTo use the EXPELL to expell existing files, do the following:\n- First you have to start Exorcist! See 2d for this. \nYou will now be confronted with the Exorcist! options, available to you. \n- Type E <ENTER> (You have chosen the Expell option)\nYou will now be able to enter the filename(s) of the file(s) you want to\nexpell.\n- Type a filename or pattern. If you have access to them,y ou can use \n  wildcards like *,?,#? here.\n- Press <ENTER>. You can now enter a second filename or pattern.\n- When you are finished entering filenames, just press <ENTER> on a blank\n  line.\nAfter you have entered the files, Exorcist! will search for them and will \nask you to confirm each file.\n- Enter a N for each file you don''t want to expell, any other key will\n  confirm to expell the file.\nIMPORTANT: Watch out! Do not confirm files that must NOT be expelled, as\n           there is no way back from this decision. This confirmation is\n           the only one!\n\nNow Exorcist! will search for the uploader(s) of the file(s). \nAfter this is done , you will be asked if messages to the uploaders should\nbe send.\n- Enter a Y if you want to send messages informing the uploader what is\n  expelled and how much credits are deducted. Otherwise enter a N.\n\nNow Exorcist! will clear the screen an build up the following information:\n  Top of the screen: Action you are performing.\n  First ''window''   : Uploader data, (Name,Place,Uploads,bytes etc.)\n  Second ''window''  : Left part: possible sizedescriptions, right part: \n                     possible expelldescriptions.\n  Underneath       : Current Filename to Expell (name+size)\n                     \nUnder this information there will be the following questions:\n"Deduct how many times credits"\n- Enter a number with which the filesize must be multiplied to get the\n  amount of bytes the uploader gets deducted from his uploaded bytes.\n  If you enter a ''0'' no credits will be deducted, the uploader keeps \n  its ''illegally'' gained upload bytes.\n  If you enter a ''1'' he just has uploaded the file for nothing.\n  If you enter a number higher than ''1'' you will punish the uploader by\n  deducting more credits than he has gained.\nThe next questions will be:\n"Choose a size description"\n- Enter a number from 0 to 9. \n  Here you choose the description that will\n  replace the filesize in the files list. The choices are displayed in the\n  left part of the second window. If you enter a ''0'' the size will stay. \n  If you enter a 9 you can enter your own description. This description\n  may not be longer than 8 characters.\n"Choose a expell description"\n- Enter a number from 0 to 9. \n  Here you choose the description that will be placed under the expelled\n  file along with your name. If you enter a ''0'' this description will not\n  be placed.\n  If you enter a 9 you can enter your own description. This description\n  may not be longer than 50 characters.\nNow Exorcist will show you what choices you have made and will ask you to\nconfirm these.\n- Enter Y or N.\n  If you enter N you will be asked the same questions again.\n\nNow Exorcist! will Expell the file. And, if specified,  add the file \ninformation to the message to the uploader. \nAfter this Exorcist! will ask you:\n"Return credits to downloaders (Y/n)"\n- Enter a Y if you want the downloaders of the expelled file to get their\n  spent credits back. (Download bytes will be reduced by the filesize and\n  one file is deducted from total downloaded files).\n  Otherwise specify a N.\nIf you answered yes to the previous question, Exorcist! will ask you:\n"Send messages to downloaders (Y/n)"\n- Enter a Y if you want messages sent to the downloaders, informing them\n  that the spent credits on the expelled files are returned. Otherwise\n  specify a N.\nExorcist! will return the credits and send the messages if specified.\nIf there are more files specified, the screen will be cleaned from the\nfilename down. And the same procedure for the next file will commence.\nAll files uploaded by one person will be treated after each other. And\nonly one message per uploader will be sent. After you have completed the\nprocedure for all files, Exorcist! will throw you back in the BBS.\n\n\nThe second option is to Expell non-existing files to prevent them from\nbeing uploaded:\n- Use the same procedure as you do when normally expelling files, \n  until the moment you have to enter the filenames.\n- Now enter the non-existing files you want te be ''expelled'',\nThe rest of the procedure will also be the same. BUT ofcourse uploader\nand downloader information will not be found, and question concerning these\nwill not be asked. EXCEPT ONE...Exorcist! will still ask you if messages to\nuploaders must be send...if you have only specified non-existing files, you\ncan type anything you want as an answer, as it will be ignored. Note also \nthat size and expell comments can not be made.\n\nYou can use both options of Expell together, expelling existing and\nnon-existing files in only one session.\n\n\n3c. Tips on using the expell option.\n\nThe following list contains some tips about when and how to use the expell\noption.\n- Don''t try to expell files with sending deduct messages to uploaders and \n  to expell files without sending deduct messages to uploaders in one \n  session, as this is impossible.\n- If Exorcist! says a file does not have an uploader, it doesn''t have to \n  mean that it not has an uploader. Exorcist! can''t just not find the\n  uploader int the UDlog.\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n4. AWARD FILES.\n---------------\n4a. What is awarding files.\n\nWhen you award an upload. You give the uploader extra credits for his\nupload. To be precise the award option does the following:\n- Multiply the number of bytes earned by uploading the file with a\n  specified amount and adding this to the uploader''s total bytes uploaded.\n- Append a specified description to the file.\n- Send a message to the uploader and, if option is enabled, to the sysop.\n\n\n4b. How do I use it.\n\n- First you have to start Exorcist! See 2d for this. \nYou will now be confronted with the Exorcist! options, available to you. \n- Type A <ENTER> (You have chosen the Award option)\nYou will now be able to enter the filename(s) of the file(s) you want to\naward.\n- Type a filename or pattern. If you have access to them,y ou can use \n  wildcards like *,?,#?,| here.\n- Press <ENTER>. You can now enter a second filename or pattern.\n- When you are finished entering filenames, just press <ENTER> on a blank\n  line.\nAfter you have entered the files, Exorcist! will search for them and will\nask you to confirm each file.\n- Enter a N for each file you don''t want to award, any other key will\n  confirm to award the file.\nIMPORTANT: Watch out to not confirm files that must NOT be awarded, as\n           there is no way back from this decision. This confirmation is\n           the only one!\n\nNow Exorcist! will search for the uploader(s) of the file(s). \nAfter this is done , You will be asked if messages to the uploaders should\nbe send.\n- Enter a Y if you want to send messages informing the uploader what is\n  awarded and how much credits are added. Otherwise enter a N.\n\nNow Exorcist! will clear the screen an build up the following information:\n  Top of the screen: Action you are performing.\n  First ''window''   : Uploader data, (Name,Place,Uploads,bytes etc.)\n  Second ''window''  : possible awarddescriptions.\n  Underneath       : Current Filename to award (name+size)\n                     \nUnder this information there will be the following questions:\n"Add how many times credits"\n- Enter a number with which the filesize must be multiplied to get the\n  amount of bytes the uploader gets awarded to his uploaded bytes.\n  If you enter a ''0'' no credits will be awarded, the uploader keeps \n  its gained upload bytes, this is a way to cancel the award!\n  If you enter a number higher than ''0'' you will award the uploader by\n  awarding credits.\nThe next questions will be:\n"Choose an award description"\n- Enter a number from 0 to 9. \n  Here you choose the description that will\n  replace the filesize in the files list. The choices are displayed in the\n  left part of the second window. If you enter a ''0'' no message will be\n  added. If you enter a 9 you can enter your own description. This\n  description may not be longer than 50 characters.\nNow Exorcist will show you what choices you have made and will ask you to\nconfirm these.\n- Enter Y or N.\n  If you enter N you will be asked the same questions again.\n\nNow Exorcist! will award the uploader, and place the description.\nAnd, if specified,  add the file information in the message to the \nuploader. \nIf there are more files specified, the screen will be cleared from \nthe filename downwards. Then the same procedure for the next file will\ncommence. All files uploaded by one person will be treated after each \nother. And only one message per uploader will be sent.\nAfter you have completed the procedure for all files. Exorcist! will throw\nyou back in the BBS.\n\n\n4c. Tips on using the award option.\n\n- YOU CANNOT AWARD YOUR OWN FILES! \n- If you have a lot of people who use Exorcist!, use the AWARDLEVEL option\n  in the config file. It is very easy to give a person almost a disabled\n  status, just by awarding a file of 1 MB 999 times (=1GB!!!). People could\n  get tempted...\n- If you only want to put a comment to a file, use the comment option, not\n  the award option!\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n5. FREE FILES.\n--------------\n5a. What is freeing files.\n\nUsing the FREE option, it is possible to make certain files\n''free-download''. It specifically does the following:\n- Making specified file free-download, using the /X standard.\n- Appending a standard FREE DOWNLOAD description to the file in the \n  file list.\n\n\n5b. How do I use it.\n- First you have to start Exorcist! See 2d for this. \nYou will now be confronted with the Exorcist! options, available to you. \n- Type F <ENTER> (You have chosen the Free option)\nYou will now be able to enter the filename(s) of the file(s) you want to\nfree.\n- Type a filename or pattern. If you have access to them, you can use \n  wildcards like *,?,#? here.\n- Press <ENTER>. You can now enter a second filename or pattern.\n- When you are finished entering filenames, just press <ENTER> on a blank\n  line.\nAfter you have entered the files, Exorcist! will search for them and will \nask you to confirm each file.\n- Enter a N for each file you don''t want to free any other key will\n  confirm to free the file.\nIMPORTANT: Watch out to not confirm files that must NOT be freed, as\n           there is no way back from this decision. This confirmation is\n           the only one!\n\nNow Exorcist! will clear the screen and will, for each file, put a message \non the screen that it is being freed.\nAfter that Exorcist! will throw you back in the BBS.\n\n\n5c. Tips on using the free option.\n\n- You can turn OFF the free-download of a file by deleting the F in its DOS\n  commentline. You also have to strip the free-download comment in the file\n  list, as people otherwise think a non free-download file IS free\n  download.\n- You can combine the free-download option with the award option. This will\n  add extra comments under the other comments in the file list. \n  REMEMBER: It is possible to resurrect an expelled file that was\n  previously made free-download and awarded. But all these actions will add\n  comments to the files list. Ultimatily making it impossible to really see\n  what happened to the file.\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n6. COMMENTING FILES.\n--------------------\n6a. What is commenting files.\n\nSometimes it''s useful if you have the ability to just append a one-line \ncomment to a certain file in the file list. You can use comment for this\npurpose.\n\n\n6b. How do I use it.\n\n- First you have to start Exorcist! See 2d for this. \nYou will now be confronted with the Exorcist! options, available to you. \n- Type C <ENTER> (You have chosen the Comment option)\nYou will now be able to enter the filename(s) of the file(s) you want to\naward.\n- Type a filename or pattern. If you have access to them,y ou can use \n  wildcards like *,?,#? here.\n- Press <ENTER>. You can now enter a second filename or pattern.\n- When you are finished entering filenames, just press <ENTER> on a blank\n  line.\nAfter you have entered the files, Exorcist! will search for them and will \nask you to confirm each file.\n- Enter a N for each file you don''t want to comment, any other key will\n  confirm to comment the file.\nIMPORTANT: Watch out to not confirm files that must NOT be comment, as\n           there is no way back from this decision. This confirmation is\n           the only one!\n\nNow Exorcist! will clear the screen and build up the following information:\n  Top of the screen: Action you are performing.\n  Underneath       : Current Filename to Comment (name+size)\n                     \nUnder this information there will be the following question:\n"Enter a comment:"\n- You can enter a comment This comment may not be longer than 50 \n  characters.\nNow Exorcist will show you what choice you have made and will ask you to\nconfirm it.\n- Enter Y or N.\n  If you enter N you will be asked the same question again.\n\nNow Exorcist! will append the entered comment to the file in the file list.\nAnd, if specified,  add the file information to the message to the \nuploader. \nAfter this Exorcist! will ask you:\nIf there are more files specified, the screen will be cleared from \nthe filename downwards. Then the same procedure for the next file will\ncommence. All files uploaded by one person will be treated after each \nother. And only one message per uploader will be sent.\nAfter you have completed the procedure for all files. Exorcist! will throw\nyou back in the BBS.\n\n\n6c. Tips on using the comment option.\n\n- You can put multiple line comments to a file in the file list, by\n  executing Exorcist! several times on the same file. \n  In this version it is not possible to add a multiple line comment or a\n  textfile to a file in the fileslist. This might be implemented in future\n  versions.\n- You cannot put comments to files which are no longer available on the\n  BBS.\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n7. THE RESURRECT OPTION.\n------------------------\n7a. What is the resurrect option.\n\nIf you have an expelled file that later turns out to be no ''FAKE'' file at\nall, you can use the Resurrect option. \nThis option will do the following:\n- It will delete the directory made instead of the expelled file in the\n  upload directory.\n- It will copy the original file from the path, specified with the\n  PROTECTFILES keyword (see 2c. PROTECTFILES) to the directory it was\n  expelled from. \n- The uploader gets back it''s deducted credits.\n- In the file list a comment that the file is resurrected will be appended\n  under the expell description. Also the filesize will be restored.\n- If enabled, messages will be sent to inform uploader and, if specified,\n  the sysop.\nREMEMBER: Resurrecting files is only possible if:\n* The PROTECTFILES keyword is specified in the config file (see 2c.)\n* There is a copy of the original file and a .ex! file in the resurrction\n  dir (see 2c.)\n* The UDlog has not been ''cleaned'' recently. \n* There is enough space on the drive the file was expelled from.\n\n7b. How do I use it.\n\n- First you have to start Exorcist! See 2d for this. \nYou will now be confronted with the Exorcist! options, available to you. \n- Type R <ENTER> (You have chosen the Resurrect option)\n  (If you cannot type R, you probably haven''t enabled the ResurrectOption. \n  (see 2c. PROTECTFILES)\nYou will now be able to enter the filename(s) of the file(s) you want to\nresurrect.\n- Type a filename or pattern. If you have access to them,y ou can use \n  wildcards like *,?,#? here.\n- Press <ENTER>. You can now enter a second filename or pattern.\n- When you are finished entering filenames, just press <ENTER> on a blank\n  line.\nAfter you have entered the files, Exorcist! will search for them and will \nask you to confirm each file.\n- Enter a N for each file you don''t want to resurrect, any other key will\n  confirm to resurrect the file.\nIMPORTANT: Watch out to not confirm files that must NOT be resurrected, as\n           there is no way back from this decision. This confirmation is\n           the only one!\n\nNow Exorcist! will search for the uploader(s) of the file(s). \nAfter it has done this, it will ask if messages to the uploaders should be\nsend.\n- Enter a Y if you want to send messages informing the uploader what is\n  resurrected and how much credits are returned. Otherwise enter a N.\n\nNow Exorcist! will clear the screen an build up the following information:\n  Top of the screen: Action you are performing.\n  ''window''         : Uploader data, (Name,Place,Uploads,bytes etc.)\n  Underneath       : Current Filename to resurrect (name+size)\n                     \nUnder this information there will be the following question:\n"Return credits to uploader (Y/n)"\n- Enter Y if you want to return the credits, otherwise enter N.\nNow Exorcist will show you what choices you have made and will ask you to\nconfirm these.\n- Enter Y or N.\n  If you enter N you will be asked the same questions again.\nNow Exorcist! will Resurrect the file. And, if specified, add the file\ninformation to the message to the uploader. \nExorcist! will return the credits and send the messages if specified.\nIf there are more files specified, the screen will be cleared from the\nfilename downwards. Then the same procedure for the next file will\ncommence. All files uploaded by one person will be treated after each \nother. And only one message per uploader will be sent.\nAfter you have completed the procedure for all files. Exorcist! will throw\nyou back in the BBS.\n\n\n7c. Tips on using the resurrect option.\n\n- Clean up the resurrection dir once in a while. Delete all files of which\n  you know it are fakes and their .ex! files.\n- Using resurrection slows down the expell option when deleting the\n  original. The original now must be moved, which takes time. \n- Resurrect will NOT deduct any credits from downloaders, as they probably\n  considered the file expelled, and continued to up/down with their new\n  downloaded bytes. Deducting can possibly bring some of them in serious\n  trouble. Maybe we will implement this option in later versions.\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n8. GENERAL INFORMATION.\n-----------------------\n8a. How does Exorcist! function.\n\nExorcist! uses several high-speed searching algorithms and real time user\nadjusting algorithms to work as fast as possible.\nExorcist! has been programmed modularly using the SAS/C v6 development\nsystem and was tested on several high-speed BBS''s in Holland.\n\nExorcist can create the following files:\n- If the KEEPLOG keyword is specified (see 2c.), then for every node there\n  will be a Exorcist!.log file\n- If the PROTECTFILES keyword is specified (see 2c.), then for every\n  expelled file the following files will be created in the resurection\n  directory: \n   - <filename>     : the original expelled file\n   - <filename>.ex! : the data file needed by exorcist! to resurrect the\n                      file.\n\n\n8b. TroubleShooting.\n\nThe following is a list of possible questions and problems, plus the\nanswers to solve them. If Exorcist! still not works after you followed the\ninstructions, send us a letter or a message. (See 8c.)\n\nP: Why won''t Exorcist! startup?\nS: - Is your accesslevel high enough?\n   - Are you logged in the BBS? (Exorcist! won''t start from DOS)\n   - Does the BBS.CMD file contain the right entry? (See 2b)\n   - Do you have enough memory left? (See 2a)\n   If you answered all the questions correctly and it still does not work,\n   install Exorcist! again and check again.\n\nP: Exorcist! says the config file is corrupt.\nS: Check if your config file is correct according to the rules in 2c.\n\nP: Exorcist! does not find a certain file.\nS: - Did you enter the name correctly?\n   - Is the file not (already) expelled?\n   - Is the file still present on the BBS? \n     (You can''t expell deleted files!)\n  \nP: Exorcist! does not find the (right) uploader,\nS: Not all uploaders can be found. Their upload action must (still) be in\n   the UDlog or the Callerslog. If one of these logs is deleted, no\n   uploaders can be found.\n   - Has the UDlog or the Callerslog been ''refreshed'' recently?\n   - Did you enter (per accident) a non-existing file?\n   - Do you use Freeleech or another Free-Download utility?\n     (These sometimes corrupt the UDlog!)\n\nP: I have entered the wrong description and confirmed it. What must I do?\nS: The file list is plain ASCII, it can be edited with any standard editor.\n   So change it to the right description yourself (or let the sysop do it)\n\nP: The credits are not added or substracted from up and downloaders\nS: Specify the right path to your user.data file in the config file \n   (see 2c. USERDATAPATH)\n\nP: When I use the program it only produces junk on my screen.\nS: Exorcist! uses ANSI-codes to fit all information on one screen of max.\n   25 lines. Use an ANSI compatible terminal emulation. You do not have to\n   enable ANSI when entering the BBS.\n\nP: I cannot find the option I want to use!\nS: If your accesslevel is not high enough to use an option, Exorcist! will\n   not even give you the opportunity to select the option.\n   - Is your accesslevel high enough?\n\n\nExorcist! has been written to finally get a fast and reliable program to do\nall those things essential for a good running BBS, but which were formerly\nonly possible with slow and nonfriendly programs. We hope you enjoy using\nExorcist!!\n\n8c. Names and Addresses.\n\nYou can contact us (CFi and B/\Zz) at:\n\n     Write to:\n     P.O. Box 11023\n     7502 LA ENSCHEDE\n     HOLLAND\n\n     Or leave mail at:\n     White House BBS (Eclipse DHQ)\n     ++31-85-517247\n\n\n8d. Disclaimer\n\nUse this software at your own risk. The authors will not be liable for\nany damage arising from the failure of this program to perform as described,\nor any destruction of other programs or data residing on a system\nattempting to run the program. While no damaging errors are known, the\nuser of this program uses it at his or her own risk.\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',57032,10,0,NULL,NULL,'ecl_ex13','scan',1780048498);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('eft_dwax','EFT-DWAX.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/EFT-DWAX.LHA',NULL,'XIM','______________________________    ______',NULL,'Hifi/Effect','EFT','\_  ___/  ____  ___/ ___/ ___/-._/      \_ )  _/    __/  __/   _/   `     \__    __/ /__     ___l____l___     ___     /______\be',replace(' ______________________________    ______\n \_  ___/  ____  ___/ ___/ ___/-._/      \_\n  )  _/    __/  __/   _/   `     \__    __/\n /__     ___l____l___     ___     /______\be\n  |`----''           `----''  `----''        |\n  |        DazWall v3.0 [RELEASE 1]       |\n  |          (AmiExpress Version)         |\n  |                                       |\n  | · Definately the *BEST* wall ever! ·  |\n  |                                       |\n  |                   Code by Hifi/Effect |\n  `--._________________________________.--''\n','\n',char(10)),'reference-board.txt',replace(replace('              W h e r e   t h e   w a r e z   c o m e   f r o m\r\n                                               __                /\_____:\r\n__/\__________________________________________|  \______________/  \    |__\r\n\_   ___________  _______ ________  \__   ___ |   _______  _______  \_  l  \\r\n__\____  \    _l   \    |  \     |___/     |  !    \   _l   \   _| __/\____ \_\r\n\_____    \___\     \___|   \___ !   \__   |_____   \__\     \__\    \____   /\r\n -mNT\_____/---\_____/--l____/-\______/\   |----\____/--\_____/--\____/--\__/\r\n                                        \__|\r\n\r\n- -- --> F A i R L i G H T   S W E D i S H   H E A D Q U A R T E R S <-- -- -\r\n\r\n           reference-board is back 2017 after more than 20 years in coma!\r\n\r\n                        Running on AmiExpress TelNet\r\n\r\n                    Connect to: reference-board.zapto.org:1541\r\n\r\n                    or: www.brysk.se/reference-board/index.htm\r\n               \n              UPLOAD DATE: 01-04-18  TIME: 20:35:32  ON NODE: 0\n','\r',char(13)),'\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,75165,1,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048498);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('eft_ps10','EFT-PS10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/EFT-PS10.LHA',NULL,'XIM','.----[ EFFECT ^ pUNICA pROJECTS! ^ /X ]----.',NULL,':','EFT','|                                   .----. | | Door    : pUNI sTATS             E|   /|D| | Version : 1.0                    F|  / |O|',replace('.----[ EFFECT ^ pUNICA pROJECTS! ^ /X ]----.\n|                                   .----. |\n| Door    : pUNI sTATS             E|   /|D|\n| Version : 1.0                    F|  / |O|\n| Done by : mSW/Effect             F| |  |O|\n| Info    : Cool status door       E| |. |R|\n|           for yar pleasure       C| || |S|\n|                                  T| |` | |\n| Released on: 14-09-1995           `-| /  |\n`-------------------------------------|/---''\n','\n',char(10)),'pUNI-sTATS.guide',replace('@database AquaPWFail\n@master temp:a/bbs/doors/eFFECT/pUNI-sTATS/pUNI-sTATS.guide\n@$VER: pUNI-sTATS.guide 1.0 (09.9.95)\n@author "-mSW / eFFECT^pUNICA pROJECTS"\n@(c) "mSW"\n@remark Created with Heddley v1.1 (c) Edd Dumbill 1994\n\n@node "MAIN" "pUNI-sTATS v1.0 Documentation"\n\n     _________    _________  _________  _________   ________ ______________\n    /¬       /   /¬       / /¬       / /¬       /  /¬    __/ \____    ____/\n   //  \____/   //  \____/ //  \____/ //  \____/  //    /       |¬    ¬|\n  //   ___/_   //   ___/  //   ___/  //   ___/_  //    /___/\   |     :|M\n /o        ¬\ /o  __|    /o  __|    /o        ¬\ \\         /   |     .|S\n \  ________/ \  /       \  /       \  ________/  \________/    |______|W\n  \/           \/         \/         \/\n\n                                 bRINGS yA\n\n          >>> pUNI-sTATUS v1.0 by mSW/eFFECT^pUNICA pROJECTS <<<\n\n                      [- Contents of Documentation -]\n\n                @{" Copyright Note " link "Copyright" 0}          @{"    History    " link "History" 0} \n                @{"Archive Contents" link "Archive" 0}          @{"How to Reach Me" link "ContactMe" 0} \n                @{"  Introduction  " link "Introduction" 0}          @{"  Other Tools  " link "Punica-Projects" 0} \n                @{"  Requirements  " link "Requirements" 0}          @{"   Greetings   " link "Greetings" 0} \n                @{"  Installation  " link "Installation" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "Copyright" "pUNI-sTATS v1.0 Documentation"\n\n\n                          .·····················.\n                         :  Copyright ©1995 mSW  :\n                          ·.....................·\n\n\n\n\n                Permission is granted to freely distribute\n              this product for non-commercial purposes only,\n                  as long as all files remain unmodified.\n@endnode\n\n@node "Archive" "pUNI-sTATS v1.0 Documentation"\n Archive (EFT-PS10.LHA) Contents\n ·······························\n\n Doors/Effect/pUNI-sTATS\n   pUNI-sTATS.rEXX     3839 bytes  The door itself.\n   pUNI-sTATS.gUIDE    6135 bytes  This AmigaGuide documentation.\n\n Commands/BBSCmd/\n   S.iNFO               842 bYTES  Command icon for /X 3.0+.\n   sTATS.iNFO           842 bYTES  Command icon for /X 3.0+.\n@endnode\n\n@node "Introduction" "pUNI-sTATS v1.0 Documentation"\n Introduction\n ············\n\n pUNI-sTATS is a Status Door. Well, I guess that ya all know what\n a status door does, so I will not go into it too deeply explaining.\n@endnode\n\n@node "Requirements" "pUNI-sTATS v1.0 Documentation"\n Requirements\n ············\n\n - An Amiga with OS 2.04 or higher.\n\n - AmiExpress, SigmaExpress or any compatible program.\n@endnode\n\n@node "Installation" "pUNI-sTATS v1.0 Documentation"\n Installation\n ············\n\n Just copy the ''pUNI-sTATS'' directory to ''Doors:'', and (for /X 3.0+)\n put the provided command icon ''S.info'' in your ''BBSCmd''\n drawer.\n@endnode\n\n@node "History" "pUNI-sTATS v1.0 Documentation"\n History\n ·······\n\n 0.5 (22-07-95) First beta ready.\n\n 1.0 (14-08-95) Written this guide file for ya to read.\n\n     (14-09-95) First release!\n@endnode\n\n@node "ContactMe" "pUNI-sTATS v1.0 Documentation"\n Contact Me!\n ···········\n\n    If you have any cool ideas for improvement of this tool, questions,\n    bug reports or whatever, contact me on one of the following boards:\n\n     @{"tHE-oASE" link "Punica Oase" 0} ................. mSW ............... +31-[0]3060-67278\n     ----------------------------------------------------------------\n     wILD pALMS ............... rADAVI ............ +31-[0]3060-Yess!\n     aTMOSPHERE ............... dELITE ............ +31-fASTER pLEASE\n     hIGHLANDER ............... hIFI .............. +31-eFFECT pOSSE!\n     pHANTOM .................. H&A ............... +31-eFFECT pOSSE!\n     tNT ...................... mINOR THREAT....... +31-eFFECT pOSSE!\n\n               oR aT aNY oTHER bIG sYSTEM iN tHE nETHERLANDS\n               ·············································\n@endnode\n\n@node "Punica-Projects" "pUNI-sTATS v1.0 Documentation"\n pUNICA pROJECTS\n ···············\n\n\n       fILE-nAME             tOOL nAME             wHAT iS iT\n    .································································.\n   : eFT-PS10.lHA          pUNI-sTATUS V1.0      a sTATUS dOOR fOR /X :\n    ·................................................................·\n@endnode\n\n@node "BetaTesters" "pUNI-sTATS v1.0 Documentation"\n Beta Testers\n ············\n\n\n\n                     mSW              @{"tHE oASE" link "Punica Oase" 0}\n                        rADAVI           wILD pALMS\n\n\n\n\n        Wanna B a Betatester of the to come Punica Projects Doors??\n\n              Leave A mail to MSW at one of the above systems\n@endnode\n\n@node "Greetings" "pUNI-sTATS v1.0 Documentation"\n Greetings\n ·········\n\n                Greetings must go to (in no special order):\n\n       HAWK/eFT ^ RADAVI/eFT ^ HIFI/eFT ^ H&A/eFT ^ MINOR THREAT/eFT\n                    THE RAVER/eFT ^ SGT-D/eFT ^ WHW/rYL\n         PLL/mTH ^ DELITE/mTH ^ TAKE/mTH ^ CREW ONE/mTH ^ THC/mTH\n              PROF B.ROM/pARTEK ^ MUAD''DIB/mST ^ SCARFACE/vSG\n               APOLLO/rYL ^ STIMPSON/MO[l]EN, ^ VETERAN/cOC\n                              PURPLE HAZE/sPD\n@endnode\n\n@node "Punica Oase" "pUNI-sTATS v1.0 Documentation"\n  \n       ----»> e F F E C T  w O R L D  h E A D Q U A R T E R S <«----\n \n                         ._____._____________________\n   - ---- --   -  -  tHE |  _  |___  \_______/ _____/   -------   -- -\n -  -- - - - -------     l_____l___\  \_____)  ___)__ --- - -  - -   -\n  -  - - -- -------       ==========\__\===\________/ -   - - -    -\n  \n               [·tHE hOUSEHOLD iS dEAD, lONG lIVE tHE oASE·]\n  \n      [·sYSOP : mSW/eFFECT/s^N/tB&TB/pP·] [·rADAVI/eFFECT/s&N/rOYAL·]\n            [·eUROPE''S bIGGEST sTRIPPED /X & aSCII cONFERENCE·]\n   [·mUSIC lIBRARY ^ aMIGA sTUFF ^ pC sCENE rELATED gOODIES ^ rEQUESTS·]\n     [·dIRTY mINDED pEOPLES fREEDOWNLOAD cONFERENCE ^ mUCH mUCH mORE·]\n  \n    [·aLL rUNNING oN aN oRDINARY COMMODORE 2000/030 wITH aN uSR 21k6!·]\n            [·mORE tHAN oNE gIGABYTE oF sPACE tO bE fILLED uP·]\n  \n       [·nODE#1 +31-[0]30-606-7278·] [·nODE#2 +31-[0]30-14k4blergh·]\n@endnode\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,6648,2,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048498);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('elt_sd27','ELT-SD27.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ELT-SD27.LHA','sysdl','XIM','IconEdit',NULL,'sPLASH/eLTECH','ELT','\__ _____  l__ _ ______  _____  _____  l __/ /  ___/_  |  \_ \_  \_  ___/_  |  \_  _  \_ /   |  _/  |  _/  |  _/  |  _/  |  _/  |   /',replace('___________. _ ________________________.____\n\__ _____  l__ _ ______  _____  _____  l __/\n /  ___/_  |  \_ \_  \_  ___/_  |  \_  _  \_\n/   |  _/  |  _/  |  _/  |  _/  |  _/  |   /\n\______!______!______!______!______!___liN^\n        .· eLteCh nOrWaY pReSeNT ·.\n      -= sYSOP dOWNLOAD v2.7 fOR /X =-\n           -= bY sPLASH/eLTECH =-\npErMAnENT vAcATIon - 44 1257 416994 eLT wHQ!\n','\n',char(10)),'SysDL.Guide',replace('@database "SysDL.Guide"\n@WIDTH 77\n@NODE Main "MAIN" "Welcome to SysopDL Documentation"\n          @@@@@*5W@@@WsW@@!********************!@@@@@@@WmZ**]@@@@[@@@@@@\n          5    ,@@@@@@@@@@                      @@@@@@@@@@s ]@@@@[     P   \n          9    ]@@@P  V@@@ ______,___.  ___.,__  @@@@  M@@@. ]@@@[     r \n          ''    ]@@@b   *** @@@@@@]@@@[i@@@@@W@@  @@@@  ]@@@b ]@@@[     e \n          r    ''@@@@Ws.    M@@@@*!M@@!@@@P ''M@@  @@@@  ]@@@W ]@@@[     a \n          e     ''M@@@@@Ws   M@@@b d@! @@@@s.''~~  @@@@  ]@@@@ ]@@@[     c \n          h       ''VM@@@@W  !@@@@_@A  !@@@@@W_   @@@@  ]@@@@ ]@@@[     h \n          c    ,__.  V@@@@[  M@@@@@!   ''*@@@@@W  @@@@  ]@@@D ]@@@[     e \n          a    ]@@b   @@@@[  !@@@@A   __. ~M@@@[ @@@@  d@@@! ]@@@[     r \n          e    ]@@@WmW@@@@!   M@@@!   @@W. d@@@[m@@@@mm@@@A iW@@@Wi    '' \n          r    ]@@A@@@@@@f    !@@A    @@A@@@@@A @@@@@@@@@f  ]@@@@@[    9 \n          P    2XX__XXXX______g@@L____XXL2XXXL__XXXXXXXL____2XXXXXL    5   \n          ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~T@A~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n                            ,@A`\n\n                         Sysop Download 2.7 (25/03-95)\n \n                               By Splash/ElTECH\n              \n                          @{"What is Sysop Download ?  " LINK "ABOUT"}   \n                          @{"This Version              " LINK "VERSION"}\n                          @{"Requirements.             " LINK "REQ"}                \n                          @{"Features.                 " LINK "FEATURES"}               \n                          @{"Installation.             " LINK "INSTA"}              \n                          @{"How to operate.           " LINK "USE"}              \n                          @{"Future Upgrades           " LINK "FUTURE"}\n                          @{"Credits                   " LINK "CREDS"}\n                          @{"Greetings.                " LINK "GREET"}                 \n                          @{"How to contact the Author " LINK "HOWTOCONTACT"}\n              \n@ENDNODE\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n@NODE "ABOUT" "What is Sysop Download ?"\n\nSysop DL is a door for all sysops that have lots of users who ask to download\nspesific files... Imagine how hard it is to pack the files and then upload it to \nyour board so that the user can download it..... But now..... The hard woork is \nover...... (I do know that good sysop download doors allready exist, but I think \nthat there are no other doors with the same @{"features" LINK "FEATURES"} as this :-)\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "REQ" "Requirements."\n\n\nA Commodore Amiga computer (Pese suxx :-), /X (I guess any version will do...) \n\nFor this door to work you should also have:\nreqtools.library and AEDoor.library in your LIBS:\n\nIf U want to use the lha packing feature, U must have lha in your path !\nA good place to have it is in C:\n\n\nIf you by any chance should have problems getting this door working, \nthen call me !\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "FEATURES" "Features."\n\n@{i}Features@{ui}\n                               \n\n* Fileselector for sysop to choose files from. \n* Online lha crunching (automatic if a directory is selected)  \n* Also includes a remote function (With PW protection) for cosysops.\n* NEW and gr8 DEZIGN\n* @{"File Completion" LINK "COMPLETE"} in REMOTE mode.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "INSTA" "Installation."\n\n\n                             \nJust copy the included files to the correct dirs, that''s it.... \nThe configuration can be found in the SysDL.info. Here you can choose the temp\ndir for lha crunching (The lha file will ofcoz be deleted after the transfer)\nThe password for remote function can also be edited here..\n\nSince the door will check if sysop is present or not (will check if the nodex \nscreen is active) there is no longer any use of the SYSPW TOOLTYPE.\nTo allow users to use the remote function you must have a tooltype called\n\nUSER.X=Username (Where x is a number)\n(This is not needed for the sysop who has automaticly access to this...)\nFor example like this:\nUSER.1=Preacher\nUSER.2=UnMad\n\nThe username is ofcoz NOT CASE SENSITIVE.\n\nCouldn''t be more simple.... (I think)\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "USE" "How to operate."\n\n                              \n\nWhen you first start the door U will be asked if U want to use the REMOTE \nfunction. This function is included for cosysops etc. ,so if you are local\n(In front of your computer :-) U should NOT use this. I''ll explain the \ndifference between the two modes:\n\nREMOTE\n------\nBefore getting axx to this mode you will have to enter a PW, so only people who\nknow the PW can use Sysop Download from remote. The PW can be changed in the \nSysDL.info. The default PW is ''Password''. The PW is NOT case sensetive!\nWhen entering this mode U will have to write the files/dirs U want to DL by hand.\nFor easy selecting of files you can use the @{"File Completion" LINK "COMPLETE"}\nU can select as many items as U like. When U are finished, just pressing return\nwill bring up a request of what U want to do. \nU can select between: Pack,Continue,Quit...\n\n*Pack will let you LHA pack your files before downloading.\n*Continue will download the files without packing.\n*Quit will Quit the door (Wow !)\n\nFILESELECTOR\n------------\nIf U select Continue from the first prompt, A Nice filerequester will pop up,\nand u can select your files or dirs. But before popping up it will check if the \nnodex screen is active, to see if the sysop is around. If not the requester will \nNOT pop up.  \nWhen U are finished, just press Download!, \nand on U go! U are then asked if U would like to Pack the files. If U want that \nthen select Pack, else select Continue.... (or Quit)\n\nSome people wanted me to include a PW routine BEFORE starting the \ndoor. But if you want this you can use the tooltype PASSWORD= i bbscmd/ds.info\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "FUTURE" "Future Upgrades & Address."\n@{i}Future@{ui}\n\nI got a good suggestion from Lizard/Spaceballs. He suggested that I included \nfileselecting by using the cursor keys in remote mode. This will probably be \nincluded in the next version.\n\n\nHere is my @{"address" link "HowToContact"}\n@endnode\n@node "HowToContact"\n\nI''m interested in joining a group with good traders. I''ve got one of the biggest \nboards i Norway, I code /X doors and other cool stuff. And I also trade a bit.\nI especially want to be a Norwegian HQ for a group, preferably a pretty big one.\n\nBut for any reason give me a call !\n \nHow to contact me:\n\n@{"Flame Strike" LINK "FLAME"} :+47 51631702\n\nOr snailmail: Splash/ElTECH\n              Lindeveien 69\n              N-4300 Sandnes\n              Norway\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "CREDS" "Credits."\n\nCode,Idea    - Splash/ElTECH\nDoor Design  - Shade\nGuide Design - Splash & Preacher/ElTECH\n\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE "GREET" "Greetings."\n\n\n                                  \n\n                         Greetings to all my friends ! \n\nSpecial greetings to: \n\nPreacher   - 4 being helpful and always comming up with new ideas.\nShade      - Gr8 DEZiGN man!\nDr. Ice    - 4 helping me with problems.\nLizard     - Gr8 tips about future upgrades (sorry that I''ve not included it in\n             this version, but you know, It''s not THAT easy.. :-)\nTrouble    - What''s up with your board ?? Have you quit the scene ??.....\n\nAND OFCOURSE ALL MEMBERS OF :\n\n             _______ /|   _______/\_______________    _____ \n            /~ ____// | __\___  ~__~/  _____/~   ~\  /~ ¡ ~\.  \n           //  __)_// |/ ~\  /  :| //  __) //   .__)//  |  \\\\n           \\     ~\\ ~   \\/   || \\     ~\\   : \\\\      / \  \n            \  ____/\______/\____|  \  ____/\____ // \. |__/  /\n             \/ .____/\______/\_____|\/ .TeTSUo__\/ / \/ ____/\n              \/                      \/          \/   \/ \n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "FLAME" "Flame Strike"\n\n \n \n ____/\____:_/\ ::______/\__.:____ ____.:/\_____\n \ _      ¬:.  Y.:.        ¬\:\_  Y   / :.     / SysOp:\n  \/   _____   | _________   \/  _ _  \   l___/  Splash/ElTECH\n  /    __) /   l/  \    l¬    \   Y    \  __)__\n  \    |   \   /    \   __    /   |    /  l    \ \n   \___!    \______ /\ __l___/\___l__ /_______ / CoSys:UnMad\n==================\/==\/============\/=======\/  \nElTECH HQ                                 ·   ..\n                   __/\_____:__/\__:_/\____ :   ·:_/| /\.:/\______\nRunning on:        \       ¬:.     ¬:   _  \¦   :   |/  \:.      /\n                    \  l_______  ____ __/  /|   ¦   l  _/   l___/\nA4ooo/o3o/25Mhz   __/\__ ¬\  /   Y /  \    \|   |   _   \_  __)__\n                  \    l   \/    |/   |\    /   |   \    /  l   ¬\\nUSRobotics HST DS  \______ /\ ___l\___l \  /¦   ¦___l\  /_______ /\n                   ======\/==\/==========\/=:   :=====\/=======\/\n                                            `---''\n                         Call +47 51631702 \n \n         Still growing! BIG /X Conference with 300++ files!\n\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE "COMPLETE" "How to use the filecompletion function."\n\n\nTo use this GREAT feature of SysDL is rater simple. First you MUST specify a\ndevice (or assign) to access. At the ''Filename 1:'' prompt you write fexs. ''Dh0:'',\nif you then Hit the TAB button you will be given a list of all DIRECTORIES found\nin the path. You can then continue by writing some chars of the entry you want, \nand then press TAB again. (If you fexs wanted to DL some fonts, you would type \n''fo'' and then press TAB. If there i more than ONE entry (or two including the \n.info file) you will again be given a list of entries fitting your ''filename''.\nAnd you select the entry (file or dir) by pressing RETURN ofcourse..\nEmpty line will let U finish.....\n\nThis might seem a bit hard but it''s MUCH more easy to use than it sounds like :-)\n\nSome usefull keys:\n\nPressing Ctrl+X will clear the input line \n\nREMOTE mode has got two different ''clear modes''. U can have automatic clearing of\ninput between filenames ON or OFF. (The default is ON) You can toggle this by \npressing Ctrl+a. If you have autoclear OFF the OLD filename will still be there \nwhen selecting the next file. This is nice if you are going to DL different files\nin the same dir. (less to write)\n\nUsing the TAB button will ONLY show DIRECTORIES if no start pattern of filename\nis suggested by user. If you for any reason want to list ALL entries in a dir\nyou can press ''?''.\n\nThat''s it.... If this was hard to understand then just give it a try and you''ll\nC how easy it is...\n \n@ENDNODE\n@NODE "VERSION" "What has happened since last version ?"\nExxon is dead and I have joined:\n                                   _\n                 _____________    / l_____________________________\n        ÷ ----- /   ____X    /___/   ___X   _____/  ____X    /   / ----- ÷\n               /   ___/_/   /   /   /   /  ___/_/   /   /  __   /\n              /    /   /   /   /   /   /   /   /   /   /   /   /\n             /    /   /   /   /   /   /   /   /       /   /   /\n     ÷ +---- \_______/   ____X_______/   ____X_______/   /___X ----+ ÷\n       |            \___/           \___/           \___/          |\n       |  . .                     _ __l! ___________ !l__ _        |\n       | _/\/\_  "More balls than     | Y    __     Y |            |\n       | (o_o_)   a Snooker Table!"   | l     ______l |            |\n       | /\ _/\____                   | |    |      | |            |\n       | \____/_ __}                  | |    l      | |            |\n                              ________| |___________l |________    |\n       |_ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ |               | _ _ _ _ _ _|\n                                      | (c) In!       |\n       ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯l_______________l¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n\nWhat is new with the door:\n\n*Found out that there was a bug when reading the keys, so when (P)ack was \nselected, it would just start downloading without packing... Tis worked fine in \nolder versions, but I guess I messed the source up a bit in version 2.6, but it''s\nfixed now anyway....\n\n*It is now possible to quit the door at ANY time by pressing Ctrl+C\n\nGuess that''s it......\n@ENDNODE\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',63089,2,0,NULL,NULL,'elt_sd27','scan',1780048498);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('elt_vd11','ELT-VD11.LZX','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ELT-VD11.LZX',NULL,'XIM','WHEREFUNROLEZ.EXE',NULL,NULL,'ELT',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'auto-added',46134,0,0,NULL,NULL,'elt_vd11','scan',1780048498);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('eltlsl11','ELTLSL11.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ELTLSL11.LHA','lsl','XIM','____ l_l_ ____ ___ _l_',NULL,NULL,NULL,'\__/,l\__,\__/,\__,\  )-- /X division! -- -. l                                     l ELTECH PRESENT : LoWER SPeeD LoGoN V1.1  l',replace('____ l_l_ ____ ___ _l_\n\__/,l\__,\__/,\__,\  )-- /X division! -- -.\n     l                                     l\n  ELTECH PRESENT : LoWER SPeeD LoGoN V1.1  l\n                                           ²\n Let only certain users on your BBS at Low !\n      connect speeds such as 96oo etc!     |\n                                           i\n<- -- -2F--------------- - -- -   -- ----- ''\n','\n',char(10)),'reference-board.txt',replace(replace('              W h e r e   t h e   w a r e z   c o m e   f r o m\r\n                                               __                /\_____:\r\n__/\__________________________________________|  \______________/  \    |__\r\n\_   ___________  _______ ________  \__   ___ |   _______  _______  \_  l  \\r\n__\____  \    _l   \    |  \     |___/     |  !    \   _l   \   _| __/\____ \_\r\n\_____    \___\     \___|   \___ !   \__   |_____   \__\     \__\    \____   /\r\n -mNT\_____/---\_____/--l____/-\______/\   |----\____/--\_____/--\____/--\__/\r\n                                        \__|\r\n\r\n- -- --> F A i R L i G H T   S W E D i S H   H E A D Q U A R T E R S <-- -- -\r\n\r\n           reference-board is back 2017 after more than 20 years in coma!\r\n\r\n                        Running on AmiExpress TelNet\r\n\r\n                    Connect to: reference-board.zapto.org:1541\r\n\r\n                    or: www.brysk.se/reference-board/index.htm\r\n               \n              UPLOAD DATE: 11-02-18  TIME: 06:51:31  ON NODE: 0\n','\r',char(13)),'\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,15977,2,0,NULL,NULL,'eltlsl11','scan',1780048498);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('emp_ao11','EMP-AO11.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/EMP-AO11.LHA','AutoOnline','XIM','AutoOnline',NULL,'Delete/Rename','EMP','|    Automatically Online Files to Any Cnf | ¦_/\___/\___/\___  when you''re NOT arround ¦ |\   /\ __/_  __/                          |',replace('+[ MYSTiC /X-DESiGN ]--[ Auto-Online 1.1 ]-+\n|    Automatically Online Files to Any Cnf |\n¦_/\___/\___/\___  when you''re NOT arround ¦\n|\   /\ __/_  __/                          |\n|/ Y \/_.¬\/  \  Added Features:           |\n/  | \\¬¦ \\  \\ o Delete/Rename Protection|\n\__l_//___//__// o Full FILE_ID.DIZ Support¦\n|dL!\/   \/  \/  o Better Error Handling   |\n+-[ EMPiRE & INCOGNiTO ]-[ XIM - /X 3.xx ]-+\n','\n',char(10)),'AutoOnline.DOC',replace('    _____________________________________________________________________\n   |                                                                     |\n   |                          AutoOnline V1.1                            |\n   |                          ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~                            |\n   |                             TYPE:  XIM                              |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |       EMPiRE / MYSTiC /X-DESiGN & INCOGNiTO / MYSTiC /X-DESiGN      |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |       LaSt OuTpOsT  +31-72-157682 & +31-72-201182  -   HOLLAND      |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |       AmixNet:  @NL0004   -   /X-Fido:  44:100/102      EMPiRE      |\n   |                                                                     |\n   `---------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n===============================================================================\n\n PURPOSE:\n ~~~~~~~~\n  With this DOOR/UTIL you will be able to Upload Group-Releases, Set the\n  Release Time & Date and it will put them Online Automatically at the\n  given Time/Date! This will be a BIG help for Sysops who got many releases\n  to Online.\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n REQUIREMENTS:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  - Ami Express 3.xx  (there won''t be a 2.xx Version... so UPGRADE NOW!)\n\n    XPR Support MUST be disabled for now UNTIL ByteMaster fixes a /X bug!\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n INSTALLATION:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  o Copy the EmP_Tools Directory to DOORS:\n  o Copy the Utils Directory to BBS:Utils\n  o Copy the c Directory to c:\n  o Copy AutoOnline.CFG to s:\n  o Add ''BBS:Utils/AutoOnline.EXE QUIET'' to your startup-sequence.\n\n  o AE 3.xx:\n    ~~~~~~~~\n    - Copy AO.info to BBS:Commands/BBScmd/\n      Or for More Safety to BBS:Commands/Conf{x}Cmd/\n      {x}=Private Conference Nr\n\n      Or add to AO.info ICON ToolType Info:\n\n        ACCESS=100\n        LOCATION=DOORS:EmP_Tools/AutoOnline\n        MULTINODE=YES\n        PRIORITY=0\n        STACK=50000\n        TYPE=XIM\n\n\n  o CONFIG FILE:  AutoOnline.CFG\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n    This file contains information used by both the /X-door and the\n    executable file. The first line must be the path (incl. name) of\n    the data file being used. The second line is the Time Difference between\n    local time and the CET time must be specified (local time minus CET time).\n\n    Example:\n\n      BBS:Utils/AutoOnline.DAT\n      0\n\n    If s:AutoOnline.CFG doesn''t exist it will be created with the above\n    information. (CET=0)\n\n\n  o DATA FILE:  AutoOnline.DAT\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n    The files to be released are stored in a data file (the name and location\n    of this file are specified in AutoOnline.CFG). The contents of\n    this file will be described using the following example:\n\n    01: EMP_JC33.LHA  12-01-93  18:00:00\n    02: BBS:CNF_MYSTiC/\n    03: BBS:CNF_AMiGA/\n    04:        ______  __________________           \n    05: .-----/    \ \/ / __/_  __/ / __/----------.\n    06: |----/ / / /\  /\  /-/ /-/ / /----[ /X ]---|\n    07: |-EmP\/ / /-/ /\  /-/ /-/ /\ \--[ DESiGN ]-|\n    08: +-----\/\/--\/--\/--\/--\/--\/-------------+\n    09: |                                          |\n    10: | AE DOOR: JoinCnf V3.3 - by EMPiRE/MYSTiC |\n    11: | - 2 Bugs Fixed & Faster  [XIM/2.xx/3.xx] |\n    12: |                                          |\n    13: `------------------------------------------''\n    14: *******************************************************************************\n\n    Line 01: Contains the Filename to be released, the release date\n             (MM-DD-YEAR) and the release time (HH:MM:SS).\n    Line 02: Specifies the Source Conference Path of the file.\n    Line 03: Specifies the Destination Conference Path of the file \n    Line 04:\n      to   : Description of the file. (May be less than 10 Lines!)\n    Line 13:\n    Line 14: marks the end of this record. (80 ''*'' Characters!)\n\n    There is no limit to the number of allowed records and the records may be\n    ordered randomly (the program scans the complete data file for the first\n    coming releases).\n\n===============================================================================\n\n USAGE:\n ~~~~~~\n  o AutoOnline (/X DOOR):\n\n    - Just enter AO on the MAIN screen in AmiExpress.\n\n    - Multiple Uploads are Allowed.\n\n    - In some cases it is possible to Upload an already existing file but\n      after Uploading AutoOnline will Ask you to Rename the File. This can\n      happen because AutoOnline doesn''t know the Destination-Conference yet!\n\n    - The Filename/Date/Time of ''Releases'' can be Renamed/Changed Online.\n\n    - If ''Releases'' are Deleted then they are MOVED to the HOLD directory of\n      the Source-Conference.\n\n    - It is NOT possible to start AutoOnline from a Conference without\n      FileDir(s).\n\n    - It is NOT possible to select a NETMAIL Conference without FileDir(s) as\n      ''Online'' Conference.\n\n    - It is Impossible/Useless to Select the Conference where the Files were\n      uploaded as Destination-Conference, because they are already there!\n\n    - Files that have been Deleted/Disappeared will Automatically be removed\n      from AutoOnline.DAT.\n\n    - All FilePaths are checked if there is enough DiskSpace to store the\n      Files. If none was found the Door will quit!\n\n    - When a ''Release'' already Exists in the Destination conference the\n      BackGround AutoOnline.EXE will replace the ''Online'' Time with ''FAILED''\n      in AutoOnline.DAT and won''t try to ''Online'' the File. This can happen\n      when the File was uploaded in the Destination-Conference prior to the\n      ''Online'' Date/Time. \n\n    - The User of the Door can only ''Online'' Files in Conferences where he\n      has Access.\n\n    - When AutoOnline.EXE is run Files older then the Current Date will be\n      onlined, so when for some reason the System-Date is changed to a time\n      in the future Files older then the New Date will be Onlined too!!\n      So be warned!\n\n\n  o AutoOnline.EXE (CLI UTIL):\n\n    The files are put online at the right time by a background process that\n    is started using the program AutoOnline.EXE. Normally this program is \n    started by the /X door, but it is also possible to start this program\n    from the CLI commandline.\n    The TaskPriority is set to -3 so there will NEVER be any SlowDown.\n \n    When no parameter is given the program checks the data file and starts\n    the background process. The other functions of the program can be called\n    by giving one of the following parameters:\n\n      PEND :   Shows the Next File that will be put ''Online''.\n      LIST :   Shows a list of all Files (incl. descriptions) to be put\n               ''Online'' in Release-Time order.\n      KILL :   Stops the Background-Process.\n      QUIET:   No Output to Current CLI-Window.\n\n===============================================================================\n\n ERROR MESSAGES:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n  o ERROR:  BBS:ConfConfig Not Found !!!\n  `-------> BBS:ConfConfig can''t be found\n\n  o ERROR:  AutoOnline 1.1 ONLY Works with /X 3.xx!!\n  `-------> Obvious\n\n  o ERROR:  There is NO FileDir Present in the Destination Conference!\n  `-------> Happens if a Destination Conference without a FileDir was chosen.\n\n  o ERROR:  No FileDirs Present in the Current Conference!\n  `-------> Happens if AutoOnline was started from a Conference without\n            a FileDir.\n\n  o ERROR:  ToolType NCONFS doesn''t Exist in BBS:ConfConfig.info!!\n  `-------> Should/Will never happen... /X Wouldn''t have started!\n\n  o ERROR:  Can''t Move File to HOLD Directory!\n  `-------> Error occurred while Moving a ''Deleted'' File to the Current\n            Conference Hold directory.\n\n  o ERROR:  FILENAME Can''t be Deleted\n  `-------> Error occurred while Deleting a File\n\n  o ERROR:  FILENAME Can''t be Renamed\n  `-------> Error occurred while Renaming a File\n\n  o ERROR:  Can''t find ANY DiskSpace in the CurrentConference Upload Paths\n  `-------> HardDisk FULL !! Get more HD-Space!\n\n  o ERROR:  Can''t Allocate enough Memory!\n  `-------> Not Enough Memory present to execute! Get more RAM!\n\n\n WARNING MESSAGES:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  o WARNING:  s:AutoOnline.CFG Not Found !! Creating Default ConfigFile!\n\n  o WARNING:  BBS:Utils/AutoOnline.DAT Not Found !! Creating Default DataFile!",\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n BUG REPORT & SUGGESTIONS:                                                                   \n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  It''s possible that a mistake will occure.... Nobody is Perfect.\n  If you have any Suggestions or Comments Please Leave a Message on my Board:\n\n   LaSt OuTpOsT  N1: +31-72-157682  N2: +31-72-201182  -  HOLLAND\n   ~~~~~~~~~~~~  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~     ~~~~~~~\n       AmixNet:  @NL0004   -   /X-Fido:  44:100/102   EMPiRE\n       ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~       ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~   ~~~~~~\n\n===============================================================================\n\n NOTE:\n ~~~~~\n  - This Program Has been tested on a /X 3.12 - 3.32 Configuration.\n\n  - This has been the BIGGEST Door (and DOC for that matter) I''ve (EMPiRE)\n    made until NOW, from the outside it doesn''t look too difficult but i had\n    my hands full with the Error, FileExistance, FileCopy and HD-FreeSpace\n    checking. So I don''t think ANYONE will top thiz one!\n\n  - AutoOnline (/X DOOR) always Waits until AutoOnline.EXE (CLI UTIL) has\n    finished so there will never be File I/O Conflicts.\n\n===============================================================================\n\n CREDITZ:\n ~~~~~~~~\n  - AutoOnline        (50172)  [/X DOOR]   ->  EMPiRE/MYSTiC /X-DESiGN\n\n  - AutoOnline.EXE    (29072)  [CLI UTIL]  ->  INCOGNiTO/MYSTiC /X-DESiGN\n\n  - DMSDescript v1.1  (16156)  [CLI UTIL]  ->  Re/Y\o/MYSTiC /X-DESiGN\n\n  - EXEDescript V1.0  (15684)  [CLI UTIL]  ->  Re/Y\o/MYSTiC /X-DESiGN\n\n  - TxtExtract V1.3   (10416)  [CLI UTIL]  ->  SPY/MYSTiC /X-DESiGN\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n REGISTRATION:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  If YOU use this Program please let me know by Calling Last Outpost or\n  to send me a Message by NetMail @NL0004 - EMPiRE  Coz we want to know\n  how many Sysops are using our Tools!!!\n\n \n===============================================================================\n\n HISTORY:\n ~~~~~~~~\n  V0.1  10-30-93 - First BETA Version for the BetaTesters.\n\n  V0.2  11-01-93 - Internal Beta Version.\n\n  V0.3  11-22-93 - Final Beta Version\n\n  V1.0  12-01-93 - Release Version\n\n  V1.1ß 12-05-93 - There is a BUG in /X when using External XPR Libraries. \n                   /X will GURU after Files are uploaded in AutoOnline. This\n                   seems te be a BUG in /X so Disable XPR until further notice.\n                 - Fixed an ANSI Error in the View-Ouput\n                 - Optimized some routines.\n        01-12-94 - Fixed a ''flag'' error.\n                 - Added FILE_ID.DIZ Support for LHA/LZH Uploads\n        01-13-94 - Added FILE_ID.DIZ Support for DMS/TXT/DOC/NFO/EXE Uploads\n        01-14-94 - Added AutoOnline.info, in it are the Users who can\n                   Re-Name/Time/Date & Delete Files\n        01-17-94 - When AutoOnline is run, it now will ShowUp on the Server.\n        01-19-94 - Support for the ''PLAYPEN'' option in the Node{x}.info\n                   It will now check the Path to the PlayPen Directory.\n        01-20-94 - Added Adding of FILE_ID.DIZ to LHA/LZH/DMS/TXT/DOC/NFO/EXE\n        01-25-94 - Fixed the ''10-Node'' BUG\n\n  V1.1  01-29-94 - Release Version\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n STILL TO DO:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  - File Checking after the Uploads.\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n EMPiRE /X DOORS/UTILS COLLECTION UNTIL NOW!:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  - AboStats V0.2                        AIM Door\n  - AutoOnline V1.1                      XIM Door/Util\n  - Bulls V2.0                           XIM Door\n  - CheckNU V1.0                         XIM Door\n  - ConfAccess V1.1                      ServerUtil\n  - CopyDate V1.3                        CLI Util\n  - DlDir V2.0                           XIM Door\n  - DoorKIT 1.01                         XIM Doors/Includes\n  - DMenu V1.0                           AIM Door\n  - DutchNET V1.0  [AmiXnet]             AIM Door\n  - Front V2.0                           XIM Door\n  - JoinCnf V3.4                         XIM Door\n  - LastCalls & TopUps V1.2              LogOffUtil\n  - LastDL V0.1                          LogOffUtil\n  - LastUL V0.1                          LogOffUtil\n  - MakeFree V1.1                        AIM Door\n  - MemberList V1.0                      AIM Door\n  - MonthTopUp V2.0                      ServerUtil\n  - MultiNodeLastCaller V1.1             LogOffUtil\n  - Page V2.0                            XIM Door\n  - PMail V1.1                           AIM Door\n  - Remote Maintenance V1.3              AIM Door\n  - SceneTalk Voter V2.3                 AIM Door\n  - SceneTalk Voter V2.2 [Party]         CLI Door\n  - SecLevChk V1.0                       ServerUtil\n  - Sent FrondEnd 1.0  [Sent_FE]         XIM Door\n  - SysopCommands V1.0                   AIM Door\n  - UserData Cleaner/Repair V2.0         ServerUtil\n  - UserStats V2.0                       ServerUtil\n  - UsrCnfAx V1.1                        CLI Util\n  - View & Check Archive/Text V1.7       AIM Door\n  - WhoNode V1.3                         AIM Door\n\n===============================================================================\n\n THANX MUST GO TO ALL OFFICIAL BETA-TESTERS:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n   Tycoon/Mystic             [Channel X]\n   ByteAndi/Mystic           [Diabolo]\n   JPS                       [Red October]\n   Sal-One/TRSi              [BoonDocks]\n   Sharon/Scx                [The Unknown]\n   Blue Bird/Mystic          [Tau Ceti]\n   Easy Rider/Mystic         [Mamba]\n   Mega Fortress             [MF Enterprise]\n   Beast/Partek              [Sequencial]\n   SpeedDevil/Partek         [Rising Sun]\n\n\n GREETZ/TNX GO TO:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n   ByteAndi/MST /X-DESiGN  - NewFiles is the best! And Tnx for all ya ''C''\n                             Help & Sources! You''re (almost) the Greatest!\n   Killraven/MST /X-DESiGN - For giving me sum Great Pointers/Sources on ''C''\n   CrackDown/MST /X-DESiGN - Nice Doors, Keep it up!\n   JAF/G.O.D.              - For some good REXX ideas\n   Bad Sector/Hidden       - Still Using your Sort-Routine. It''s the Fastest!\n   B.O.B./Paradox          - For (Mis)Using/Testing my tools!\n   Aragorn/Vision          - Tnx for Testing in the past\n   Camelot/Complex         - Tnx for Testing in the past\n   Telekinetic/T.F.A.      - Tnx for Testing in the past\n   Alcoholic               - Tnx for Testing in the past\n   Price/T.F.A.            - Great job on your {F}ull {S}creen {E}ditor!\n   Van Damme               - Nice Doors!!!\n   DR.G/IBB                - Hope to see Check''N Add work on a 040\n   SiGMA SEVEN             - Nice job on SiGMA-EXPRESS!\n   911/Movement            - Tnx For ya Ansi Logo''s!! You''re the Greatest!\n   Mike                    - Tnx for calling!\n   Amicom/TRSi             - Tnx for calling!\n   SkIn                    - Tnx for ya Description Logo! Looks Great!!\n   Shadow Man/S8           - Nice Doors & Tnx for ya greetz! & Calling ofcoz\n   [MAZ!^PHAZE]            - Tnx for calling!\n   Shuyuki Tanaka          - Tnx for your Messages!\n   AGONY/cOmpLeX           - Tnx for calling!\n   HUMANOiD & RU$tY/AFL    - Tnx for calling!\n   LECTOR                  - Tnx for your NetMail\n   Koo Koo Ka Choo         - Tnx for calling!\n   TaRzAN                  - Tnx for your NetMail. Yezz 040 Speed Rulez!!\n   Crayor/Scx              - Tnx for calling!\n   Foxx''n''Lynxx            - Tnx for your BugReports!!!\n   ThE BiRD                - Tnx for your NetMail on UsrCnfAx\n   Dux                     - Tnx for your NetMail\n   dR.dRE!/fAITH           - Tnx for da greetz, Nice Doors btw\n   [-RUNT&SCOTTIE-]        - Tnx for calling!\n   sPAcEcAKe/aF            - Tnx for calling!\n   Freddy Kreuger/GOD      - Tnx for your NetMail on JoinCnf 3.2\n   MF1                     - Tnx for calling!\n   AtomiX/N.A.S.A          - Hope the ''C'' archive was sume help for ya!\n   Mike Hoffren  [SF0001]  - Tnx for the BugReport on JoinCnf 3.3 [100+ Cnfs]\n\n\n   & Ofcoz to ALL MYSTiC Members all over the Globe!\n\n\n                        ______  __________________                            \n.----------------+-----/    \ \/ / __/_