--------+----------------.\n|                |----/ / / /\  /\  /-/ /-/ / /----[ /X ]---|                |\n|       /\    /\ |-EmP\/ / /-/ /\  /-/ /-/ /\ \--[ DESiGN ]-|       /\    /\ |\n|      /C \  /N/ +-----\/\/--\/--\/--\/--\/--\/-------------+      /C \  /N/ |\n|     /i/\ \/G/  |                                          |     /i/\ \/G/  |\n|    /T/  \ i/   |                                          |    /T/  \ i/   |\n|   /S/   /S \   |   EMPiRE   -   BYTEANDi   -  CRACKDOWN   |   /S/   /S \   |\n|  /Y/   /E/\ \  |   TYCOON   -   KiLLRAVEN  -   SiEGEL     |  /Y/   /E/\ \  |\n| /M/   /D/  \ \ |   FUZZY    -      SPY     -  INCOGNiTO   | /M/   /D/  \ \ |\n| \/    \/    \/ |   RE/Y\o   -     BoBo     -   HARDBYTE   | \/    \/    \/ |\n|                |                                          |                |\n`----------------+----------[  MYSTiC /X DESiGN  ]----------+----------------''\n\n \n\n                       ____ _________ _________ ________ _____\n            MYSTiC    /   / \\  /    \\\  /   _\\\  /   \\\  /     MYSTiC\n                     /   /   \\/   /\ \\\/   /___\\/__   \\\/\n         CONSOLE    /   / /\  /   __   \ \____   \   /   /      AMIGA\n                   /   /_/  \/   / /   /_____/   /  /   /\n       WORLD-HQ    \________X___/ /___/\________/   \__/      EURO-HQ\n      ____ _________ ________ _________ _________ _________ ________ _____\n     /    \\\  /   / \\  /   \\\  /    \\\  /    \\\  /   _\\\  /   \\\  /\n    /   /\ \\\/   / /\\\/__   \\\/   /\ \\\/   /\ \\\/   /___\\/__   \\\/\n   /   / /  \/   / /  \   /   / /   _____\/   / /  \ \____   \   /   /\n  /   /_/   /   /_/   /  /   / /   /     /   /_/   /_____/   /  /   /\n  \________X_________/   \__/  \__/      \________/\________/   \__/\n\n\n  AMIGA - SNES - MEGADRIVE - GAMEBOY - GAMEGEAR - PC ENGINE - LYNX - C64\n\n  3.5 Gb ONLINE          SYSOP:  EMPiRE / MYSTiC           3.5 Gb ONLINE\n\n  HOLLAND:          +31-72-157682  &  +31-72-201182             :HOLLAND\n\n','\n',char(10)),'{"ACCESS":"001","LOCATION":"DOORS:EmP_Tools/Bulls","PRIORITY":"0","STACK":"50000","TYPE":"XIM"}','auto-added',41660,8,0,NULL,NULL,'emp_bl20','scan',1780048498);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('emp_bl21','EMP-BL21.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/EMP-BL21.LHA','Bulls','XIM','Bulls',NULL,NULL,'EMP','|               Show Bulletins Selectable  | ¦_/\___/\___/\___    for Every Conference  ¦ |\   /\ __/_  __/                          |',replace('+[ MYSTiC /X-DESiGN ]-----[ Bulls 2.1 ]----+\n|               Show Bulletins Selectable  |\n¦_/\___/\___/\___    for Every Conference  ¦\n|\   /\ __/_  __/                          |\n|/ Y \/_.¬\/  \  Added Features:           |\n/  | \\¬¦ \\  \\ o Cursor-Key Selection    |\n\__l_//___//__// o Use your Own Bull-Logo  ¦\n|dL!\/   \/  \/                            |\n+-[ EMPiRE/MYSTiC ]-[ XIM - /X 2.xx/3.xx ]-+\n- sCANDAL! tHE nEW dIMENSION iN tHIS wORLD -\n','\n',char(10)),'Bulls.DOC',replace('\n                  ###### ###   ## ######  ### ######  ######              \n    _______|\     ###    #### ### ###  ## ### ###  ## ###       /|________\n   |         >    ####   ######## ######  ### ######  ####     <         |\n   | |¯¯¯¯¯|/     ###    ### # ## ###     ### #####   ###       \|¯¯¯¯¯| |\n   | |            ###### ###   ## ###     ### ### ##  ######           | |\n   | |_________________________________________________________________| |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |                             Bulls V2.1                              |\n   |                             ~~~~~~~~~~                              |\n   |                             TYPE:  XIM                              |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |                  ©1994 EMPiRE / MYSTiC /X-DESiGN                    |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |       LaSt OuTpOsT  +31-72-157682 & +31-72-201182  -  HOLLAND       |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |       AmixNet:  @NL0004   -   /X-Fido:  44:100/102     EMPiRE       |\n   |_____________________________________________________________________|\n\n===============================================================================\n\n PURPOSE:\n ~~~~~~~~\n  - Are You Getting Tired Changing 1 Bulletin and then Copying it to all\n    other Conferences, then This is the Tool for You!!\n    All Bulletins are now stored in 1 Directory so only one Bulletin\n    has to change to ''Show'' it in all conferences.\n\n  - This DOOR is a Alternative to the ''b'' command in /X 2.xx & /X 3.xx\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n REQUIREMENTS:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  /X 2.xx & /X 3.xx\n  It Won''t work with Ami Express 1.1x!!\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n INSTALLATION:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  - Copy the EmP_Tools Directory to DOORS:\n  - Edit DOORS:EmP_Tools/Bulls.CFG to your Needs.\n\n--start: cut here------------------------------------------------------------\nDUAL_LISTING       YES                 ; Use 2 Listings [YES/NO]                   \nCURSOR_KEYS        YES                 ; Use Cursors to select a Bull [YES/NO]\n[Init_END]====================================================================\nSystem Setup                                       ; bull1.txt\nTe Koop / For Sale                                 ; bull2.txt\n-                                                  ; bull3.txt Doesn''t Exist\nGameBoy & Nintendo Cards                           ; bull4.txt\nLastCallers & TopUps                               ; bull5.txt\n-                                                  ; bull6.txt Doesn''t Exist\n-                                                  ; bull7.txt Doesn''t Exist\nHST ASL & DS ASL Settings                          ; bull8.txt\nBBS Legal Disclaimer                               ; bull9.txt\nPrivate Bull #1                                    ; bull10.txt\nPrivate Bull #2                                    ; bull11.txt\nPrivate Bull #3                                    ; bull12.txt\nPrivate Bull #4                                    ; bull13.txt\nPrivate Bull #5                                    ; bull14.txt\nPrivate Bull #6                                    ; bull15.txt\nPrivate Bull #7                                    ; bull16.txt\nPrivate Bull #8                                    ; bull17.txt\nPrivate Bull #9                                    ; bull18.txt\nPrivate Bull #10                                   ; bull19.txt\n[BullNames_END]===============================================================\nXX------X----------                                ; Conference 1\nXX-X---XX----------                                ; Conference 2\nXX-XX--XX----------                                ; Conference 3\nXX-X---XX----------                                ; Conference 4\nXX-X---XX----------                                ; Conference 5\nXX-X---XX----------                                ; Conference 6\nXX-X---XX----------                                ; Conference 7\nXX------X----------                                ; Conference 8\nXX-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX                                ; Conference 9\nXX-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX                                ; Conference 10\n[CnfAccess_END]===============================================================\n[36m     ______________________  ______  ______________________________________\n     \____   \    /  \    /\ \    /\ \       \__    __\____\____   \       \\n     //  /   //  /   //  / / //  / / //  ____/\/   /\_//   //  /   /   /___/\\n    //     _//  /   //  /_/_//  /_/_//  __/_/ /   / ///   //  /   /\__   \__/\n  _//  /   //  /   //  /   //  /   //      / /   / ///   //  /   /   /   /\\n  \_______/\______/\______/\______/\______/ /\__/ / \___/\__/___/\______/ /\n   \______\/\_____\/\_____\/\_____\/\_____\/  \_\/   \__\/\_____\/\_____\/\n[34m  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n[Title_END]===================================================================\n--end: cut here--------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  - Init:\n    ~~~~~\n     Change to ''Y'' if you want 2 Output Lists otherwise change to ''N''.\n\n    BullNames\n    ~~~~~~~~~\n     These Are the Bulletin Names.\n     (1 List: Max 39 Chars, 2 Lists: Max 31 Chars)\n\n    CnfAccess:\n    ~~~~~~~~~~\n     Here you can Select which Bulletins can be Read in which Conference\n     for example:\n\n      Conference 1 is XX------X---------- then the following bulls are shown.\n\n                [1]  System Setup\n                [2]  For Sale\n                [9]  BBS Legal Disclaimer\n\n\n      Conference 4 is XX-X---XX---------- then the following bulls are shown.\n\n                [1]  System Setup\n                [2]  For Sale\n                [4]  GameBoy & Nintendo Cards\n                [8]  HST ASL & DS ASL Settings\n                [9]  BBS Legal Disclaimer\n\n    Title:\n    ~~~~~~\n     Bulletin Logo.\n     Keep in mind:  Max 20 Lines and 200 Chars/Line!\n     In Bulls.TXT are a few Logo Examples to choose from.\n\n\n  - If you have Fewer (or More) Conferences than the 10 above then you\n    can Leave them out (or put them in!).\n\n  - Create a Directory:  BBS:Bulletins\n    And copy all your Bulletins (from a Conference) to it.\n\n  AE 2.xx:\n  ~~~~~~~~\n  - Append/Join the BBS.cmd to BBS:Commands/BBS.cmd\n\n    Or add:            111111111122222222223333333333  <-- Position!\n              123456789012345678901234567890123456789\n\n              *B        XM001DOORS:EmP_Tools/Bulls\n\n  AE 3.xx:\n  ~~~~~~~~\n  - Copy B.info to BBS:Commands/BBScmd/\n\n    Or add to B.info ICON ToolType Info:\n\n      ACCESS=001\n      LOCATION=DOORS:EmP_Tools/Bulls\n      MULTINODE=YES\n      PRIORITY=0\n      STACK=50000\n      TYPE=XIM\n\n\n  - Don''t forget to Redirect Output Files from Others tools (in logOff.bat)\n    to BBS:bulletins and Not to the ''old'' BBS:Conference/Bulletins! \n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n USAGE:\n ~~~~~~\n  Just enter B on the MAIN screen in AmiExpress.\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n ERROR MESSAGES:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n  o ERROR:  Bulls 2.0 ONLY Works with /X 2.xx & /X 3.xx!!\n  `-------> Obvious\n\n  o ERROR:  BBS:Bulletins/bull{x}.txt Not Found !!\n  `-------> Bulletin {x} can''t be found in BBS:Bulletins\n\n  o ERROR:  DOORS:EmP_Tools/Bulls.CFG Not Found !!\n  `-------> Bulls.CFG can''t be found in DOORS:EmP_Tools\n\n  o ERROR:  UnKnown Keyword: XXXXXXXX in JoinCnf.CFG\n  |\n  `--> There must be 2 different KeyWords in the INIT part (Bulls.CFG)\n       Compare this with the original Bulls.CFG\n       Check that the KeyWords are:\n\n         DUAL_LISTINGS\n         CURSOR_KEYS\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n BUG REPORT & SUGGESTIONS:                                                                   \n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  It''s possible that a mistake will occure.... Nobody is Perfect.\n  If you have any Suggestions or Comments Please Leave a Message on my Board:\n\n   LaSt OuTpOsT  N1: +31-72-157682  N2: +31-72-201182  -  HOLLAND\n   ~~~~~~~~~~~~  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~     ~~~~~~~\n       AmixNet:  @NL0004   -   /X-Fido:  44:100/102   EMPiRE\n       ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~       ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~   ~~~~~~\n\n===============================================================================\n\n NOTE:\n ~~~~~\n  o This Program Has been tested on a /X 2.0 - 3.37 Configuration.\n\n  o If a User uses More lines then the sysop can see the Screen-Output on\n    the Sysop-side will be scrambled caused by the Ansi-Handling but on\n    the Users-side it will be ok!!\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n REGISTRATION:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  If YOU use this Program please let me know by Calling Last Outpost or\n  to send me a Message by NetMail @NL0004 - EMPiRE  Coz we want to know\n  how many Sysops are using our Tools!!!\n \n\n===============================================================================\n\n HISTORY:\n ~~~~~~~~\n  V0.1  11-07-92 - Internal Version\n\n  V1.0  02-03-93 - Release Version\n\n  V1.1  03-20-93 - Added The 2 OutputList Option\n                 - Added Support for .txt.gr Files\n                 - [Bulls.CFG CHANGED!]\n\n  V1.2  05-05-93 - Added ''Non-Stop'' Menu Showing, if you got too many Bulls\n                   then the irritating ''More (Y/n/ns)'' appeared... FIXED\n                 - Cleaned Up.\n        06-21-93 - Fixed a small Error found with the RexxDoorDebugger.\n\n  V2.0ß 01-01-94 - ReWritten to XIM!\n        01-13-94 - Better Bulls.CFG reading\n                 - Added some more Ansi Colors\n                 - Changed the Bulls.CFG layout (same layout as JoinCnf.CFG).\n                   It''s now also possible to use your Own Bulletin Logo\n                   [Bulls.CFG CHANGED!]\n        01-14-94 - Bug Report from JPS\n                    o When using Bull [00] it was possible to press different\n                      <SHIFT>-keys to show it.. FIXED\n        01-17-94 - When Bulls is run, it will ShowUp on the Server.\n        01-25-94 - Fixed the ''10-Node'' BUG\n\n  V2.0  01-29-94 - Release\n\n  V2.1ß 02-05-94 - Change the ''Full Use of 80 Chars/Line'' to 79 Chars/Line\n                   because some Terminals on Amiga/PC can''t handle the 80th\n                   character right (extra linefeeds)!\n        02-07-94 - Bug Report from B.O.B/CF & Enzo:\n                    o When using NON-Ansi the character color will change to\n                      Magenta when exiting/using Bulls.\n                      There were 2 ESC-chars after eachother in the command-\n                      line which /X doesn''t like... FIXED!\n        02-28-94 - Added Cursor-Key Support. To Include this the Bulls.CFG\n                   changed:\n                    o Bull0.txt support has been deleted, so change your\n                      Bull-Access!\n                 - [Bulls.CFG CHANGED!]\n        03-20-94 - Optimized some code.\n        03-24-94 - Added some Suggestions from SpeedDevil/Partek:\n                    o When starting Bulls the BullSelection >[]< will now\n                      be disabled until an ArrowKey is pressed or a Bull is \n                      selected.\n                    o After showing a Bulletin pressing <ENTER> will show\n                      the Bulletin-List again and not Quit Bulls anymore.\n                      So it''s now only possible to Quit Bulls in the\n                      Bulletin-List.\n\n  V2.1  04-13-94 - Release\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n EMPiRE /X DOORS/UTILS COLLECTION UNTIL NOW!:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  - AboStats V0.2                        AIM Door\n  - AE2PCE V1.0                          CLI Util\n  - AutoOnline V1.2                      XIM Door/Util\n  - Bulls V2.1                           XIM Door\n  - CheckDir V1.0                        CLI Util\n  - CheckNU V1.0                         XIM Door\n  - ConfAccess V1.1                      ServerUtil\n  - CopyDate V1.3                        CLI Util\n  - DlDir V2.0                           XIM Door\n  - DoorKIT 1.01                         XIM Doors/Includes\n  - DMenu V1.0                           AIM Door\n  - DutchNET V1.0  [AmiXnet]             AIM Door\n  - Front V2.0                           XIM Door\n  - JoinCnf V3.5                         XIM Door\n  - LastCalls & TopUps V1.2              LogOffUtil\n  - LastDL V0.1                          LogOffUtil\n  - LastUL V0.1                          LogOffUtil\n  - MakeFree V1.1                        AIM Door\n  - MemberList V1.0                      AIM Door\n  - MonthTopUp V2.0                      ServerUtil\n  - MultiNodeLastCaller V1.1             LogOffUtil\n  - Page V2.1                            XIM Door\n  - PMail V1.1                           AIM Door\n  - Remote Maintenance V1.3              AIM Door\n  - SceneTalk Voter V2.3                 AIM Door\n  - SceneTalk Voter V2.2 [Party]         CLI Door\n  - SecLevChk V1.0                       ServerUtil\n  - Sent FrondEnd 1.0  [Sent_FE]         XIM Door\n  - StripCR V1.0                         CLI Util\n  - SysopCommands V1.0                   AIM Door\n  - UserData Cleaner/Repair V2.0         ServerUtil\n  - UserStats V2.0                       ServerUtil\n  - UsrCnfAx V1.1                        CLI Util\n  - View & Check Archive/Text V1.7       AIM Door\n  - WhoNode V1.3                         AIM Door\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n THANX MUST GO TO ALL OFFICIAL BETA-TESTERS:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n   Tycoon/Mystic             [Channel X]\n   JPS                       [Red October]\n   Sal-One/TRSi              [BoonDocks]\n   Sharon/5D                 [The Unknown]\n   Blue Bird/Mystic          [Tau Ceti]\n   Easy Rider/Mystic         [Mamba]\n   Mega Fortress             [MF Enterprise]\n   Beast/Partek              [Sequencial]\n   SpeedDevil/Partek         [Rising Sun]\n   Galaxy                    [Ulixys]\n\n\n GREETZ/TNX GO TO:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n   Killraven/MST /X-DESiGN - For giving me sum Great Pointers/Sources on ''C''\n   CrackDown/MST /X-DESiGN - Nice Doors, Keep it up!\n   ByteAndi                - Tnx for all ya ''C'' Help & Sources!\n   JAF/G.O.D.              - For some good REXX ideas\n   Bad Sector/Hidden       - Still Using your Sort-Routine. It''s the Fastest!\n   B.O.B./CyberForce       - For (Mis)Using/Testing my tools! :)\n   Aragorn/Vision          - Tnx for Testing in the past\n   Camelot/Complex         - Tnx for Testing in the past\n   Telekinetic/T.F.A.      - Tnx for Testing in the past\n   Alcoholic               - Tnx for Testing in the past\n   Price/T.F.A.            - Great job on your {F}ull {S}creen {E}ditor!\n   Van Damme               - Nice Doors!!!\n   DR.G/IBB                - Hope to see Check''N Add work on a 040\n   SiGMA SEVEN             - Nice job on SiGMA-EXPRESS! Tempted to ''Convert''\n   911/Movement            - Tnx For ya Ansi Logo''s!! You''re the Greatest!\n   Mike                    - Tnx for calling!\n   Amicom/TRSi             - Tnx for calling!\n   SkIn                    - Tnx for ya Description Logo! Looks Great!!\n   Shadow Man/S8           - Nice Doors & Tnx for ya greetz! & Calling ofcoz\n   [MAZ!^PHAZE]            - Tnx for calling!\n   Shuyuki Tanaka          - Tnx for your Messages!\n   AGONY/cOmpLeX           - Tnx for calling!\n   HUMANOiD & jABBA /MST &\n    SCANDAL                - Tnx for calling!\n   LECTOR                  - Tnx for your NetMail\n   Koo Koo Ka Choo         - Tnx for calling!\n   TaRzAN                  - Tnx for your NetMail. Yezz 040 Speed Rulez!!\n   Crayor/Scx              - Tnx for calling!\n   Foxx''n''Lynxx            - Tnx for your BugReports!!!\n   ThE BiRD                - Tnx for your NetMail on UsrCnfAx\n   Dux                     - Tnx for your NetMail\n   dR.dRE!/fAITH           - Tnx for da greetz, Nice Doors btw\n   [-RUNT&SCOTTIE-]        - Tnx for calling!\n   sPAcEcAKe/aF            - Tnx for calling!\n   Freddy Kreuger/GOD      - Tnx for your NetMail on JoinCnf 3.2\n   MF1                     - Tnx for calling!\n   AtomiX/N.A.S.A          - Hope the ''C'' archive was sume help for ya!\n   MAD HARLEQUiN [ITPH01]  - Tnx for your Nice AmiXnet Messy''s\n   Mike Hoffren  [SF0001]  - Tnx for the BugReport on JoinCnf 3.3 [100+ Cnfs]\n   Galaxy/TFA              - Nice job on da SentCleaner\n   SvEN tHE CREAToR/5D     - ''Tnx'' for forcing me to use Cursor-Keys!\n   Diogenes/TPY/5D         - Tnx for calling and for your BugReport!\n\n   & Ofcoz to ALL MYSTiC Members all over the Globe!\n\n\n                        ______  __________________                            \n.----------------+-----/    \ \/ / __/_  __/ / __/----------+----------------.\n|                |----/ / / /\  /\  /-/ /-/ / /----[ /X ]---|                |\n|       /\    /\ |-EmP\/ / /-/ /\  /-/ /-/ /\ \--[ DESiGN ]-|       /\    /\ |\n|      /C \  /N/ +-----\/\/--\/--\/--\/--\/--\/-------------+      /C \  /N/ |\n|     /i/\ \/G/  |                                          |     /i/\ \/G/  |\n|    /T/  \ i/   |                                          |    /T/  \ i/   |\n|   /S/   /S \   |   EMPiRE   -   KiLLRAVEN  -   TYCOON     |   /S/   /S \   |\n|  /Y/   /E/\ \  |   SiEGEL   -   CRACKDOWN  -   FUZZY      |  /Y/   /E/\ \  |\n| /M/   /D/  \ \ |    SPY     -   INCOGNiTO  -   RE/Y\o     | /M/   /D/  \ \ |\n| \/    \/    \/ |    BoBo    -   HARDBYTE                  | \/    \/    \/ |\n|                |                                          |                |\n`----------------+----------[  MYSTiC /X DESiGN  ]----------+----------------''\n\n\n \n\n                       ____ _________ _________ ________ _____\n            MYSTiC    /   / \\  /    \\\  /   _\\\  /   \\\  /     MYSTiC\n                     /   /   \\/   /\ \\\/   /___\\/__   \\\/\n         CONSOLE    /   / /\  /   __   \ \____   \   /   /      AMIGA\n                   /   /_/  \/   / /   /_____/   /  /   /\n       WORLD-HQ    \________X___/ /___/\________/   \__/      EURO-HQ\n      ____ _________ ________ _________ _________ _________ ________ _____\n     /    \\\  /   / \\  /   \\\  /    \\\  /    \\\  /   _\\\  /   \\\  /\n    /   /\ \\\/   / /\\\/__   \\\/   /\ \\\/   /\ \\\/   /___\\/__   \\\/\n   /   / /  \/   / /  \   /   / /   _____\/   / /  \ \____   \   /   /\n  /   /_/   /   /_/   /  /   / /   /     /   /_/   /_____/   /  /   /\n  \________X_________/   \__/  \__/      \________/\________/   \__/\n\n\n  AMIGA - SNES - MEGADRIVE - GAMEBOY - GAMEGEAR - PC ENGINE - LYNX - C64\n\n  4 Gb ONLINE           SYSOP:  EMPiRE / MYSTiC              4 Gb ONLINE\n\n  HOLLAND:          +31-72-157682  &  +31-72-201182             :HOLLAND\n\n','\n',char(10)),'{"ACCESS":"001","LOCATION":"DOORS:EmP_Tools/Bulls","PRIORITY":"0","STACK":"50000","TYPE":"XIM"}','auto-added',29078,4,0,NULL,NULL,'emp_bl21','scan',1780048498);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('emp_bl22','EMP-BL22.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/EMP-BL22.LHA','Bulls','XIM','Bulls',NULL,NULL,'EMP','|               Show Bulletins Selectable  | ¦_/\___/\___/\___    for Every Conference  ¦ |\   /\ __/_  __/                          |',replace('+[ MYSTiC /X-PoWeR! ]-----[ Bulls 2.2 ]----+\n|               Show Bulletins Selectable  |\n¦_/\___/\___/\___    for Every Conference  ¦\n|\   /\ __/_  __/                          |\n|/ Y \/_.¬\/  \  Added Features:           |\n/  | \\¬¦ \\  \\ o Changed Prompt stuff    |\n\__l_//___//__// o Removed some ''C'' Bugs   ¦\n|dL!\/   \/  \/  o Faster Startup          |\n+-[ EMPiRE/MYSTiC ]----[ XIM - /X 3.38+ ]--+\n','\n',char(10)),'Bulls.DOC',replace('\n                  ###### ###   ## ######  ### ######  ######              \n    _______|\     ###    #### ### ###  ## ### ###  ## ###       /|________\n   |         >    ####   ######## ######  ### ######  ####     <         |\n   | |¯¯¯¯¯|/     ###    ### # ## ###     ### #####   ###       \|¯¯¯¯¯| |\n   | |            ###### ###   ## ###     ### ### ##  ######           | |\n   | |_________________________________________________________________| |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |                             Bulls V2.2                              |\n   |                             ~~~~~~~~~~                              |\n   |                             TYPE:  XIM                              |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |                  ©1994 EMPiRE / MYSTiC /X-PoWeR!                    |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |       LaSt OuTpOsT  +31-72-157682 & +31-72-201182  -  HOLLAND       |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |       AmixNet:  @NL0004   -   /X-Fido:  44:100/102     EMPiRE       |\n   |_____________________________________________________________________|\n\n===============================================================================\n\n PURPOSE:\n ~~~~~~~~\n  - Are You Getting Tired Changing 1 Bulletin and then Copying it to all\n    other Conferences, then This is the Tool for You!!\n    All Bulletins are now stored in 1 Directory so only one Bulletin\n    has to change to ''Show'' it in all conferences.\n\n  - This DOOR is a Alternative to the ''b'' command in /X 3.xx\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n REQUIREMENTS:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  /X 3.xx\n  It Won''t work with Ami Express 1.1x & 2.xx!!\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n INSTALLATION:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  - Copy the EmP_Tools Directory to DOORS:\n  - Edit DOORS:EmP_Tools/Bulls.CFG to your Needs.\n\n--start: cut here------------------------------------------------------------\nDUAL_LISTING       YES                 ; Use 2 Listings [YES/NO]                   \nCURSOR_KEYS        YES                 ; Use Cursors to select a Bull [YES/NO]\n[Init_END]====================================================================\nSystem Setup                                       ; bull1.txt\nTe Koop / For Sale                                 ; bull2.txt\n-                                                  ; bull3.txt Doesn''t Exist\nGameBoy & Nintendo Cards                           ; bull4.txt\nLastCallers & TopUps                               ; bull5.txt\n-                                                  ; bull6.txt Doesn''t Exist\n-                                                  ; bull7.txt Doesn''t Exist\nHST ASL & DS ASL Settings                          ; bull8.txt\nBBS Legal Disclaimer                               ; bull9.txt\nPrivate Bull #1                                    ; bull10.txt\nPrivate Bull #2                                    ; bull11.txt\nPrivate Bull #3                                    ; bull12.txt\nPrivate Bull #4                                    ; bull13.txt\nPrivate Bull #5                                    ; bull14.txt\nPrivate Bull #6                                    ; bull15.txt\nPrivate Bull #7                                    ; bull16.txt\nPrivate Bull #8                                    ; bull17.txt\nPrivate Bull #9                                    ; bull18.txt\nPrivate Bull #10                                   ; bull19.txt\n[BullNames_END]===============================================================\nXX------X----------                                ; Conference 1\nXX-X---XX----------                                ; Conference 2\nXX-XX--XX----------                                ; Conference 3\nXX-X---XX----------                                ; Conference 4\nXX-X---XX----------                                ; Conference 5\nXX-X---XX----------                                ; Conference 6\nXX-X---XX----------                                ; Conference 7\nXX------X----------                                ; Conference 8\nXX-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX                                ; Conference 9\nXX-XXXXXXXXXXXXXXXX                                ; Conference 10\n[CnfAccess_END]===============================================================\n[36m     ______________________  ______  ______________________________________\n     \____   \    /  \    /\ \    /\ \       \__    __\____\____   \       \\n     //  /   //  /   //  / / //  / / //  ____/\/   /\_//   //  /   /   /___/\\n    //     _//  /   //  /_/_//  /_/_//  __/_/ /   / ///   //  /   /\__   \__/\n  _//  /   //  /   //  /   //  /   //      / /   / ///   //  /   /   /   /\\n  \_______/\______/\______/\______/\______/ /\__/ / \___/\__/___/\______/ /\n   \______\/\_____\/\_____\/\_____\/\_____\/  \_\/   \__\/\_____\/\_____\/\n[34m  ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n[Title_END]===================================================================\n--end: cut here--------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  - Init:\n    ~~~~~\n     Change to ''Y'' if you want 2 Output Lists otherwise change to ''N''.\n\n    BullNames\n    ~~~~~~~~~\n     These Are the Bulletin Names.\n     (1 List: Max 39 Chars, 2 Lists: Max 31 Chars)\n\n    CnfAccess:\n    ~~~~~~~~~~\n     Here you can Select which Bulletins can be Read in which Conference\n     for example:\n\n      Conference 1 is XX------X---------- then the following bulls are shown.\n\n                [1]  System Setup\n                [2]  For Sale\n                [9]  BBS Legal Disclaimer\n\n\n      Conference 4 is XX-X---XX---------- then the following bulls are shown.\n\n                [1]  System Setup\n                [2]  For Sale\n                [4]  GameBoy & Nintendo Cards\n                [8]  HST ASL & DS ASL Settings\n                [9]  BBS Legal Disclaimer\n\n    Title:\n    ~~~~~~\n     Bulletin Logo.\n     Keep in mind:  Max 20 Lines and 200 Chars/Line!\n     In Bulls.TXT are a few Logo Examples to choose from.\n\n\n  - If you have Fewer (or More) Conferences than the 10 above then you\n    can Leave them out (or put them in!).\n\n  - Create a Directory:  BBS:Bulletins\n    And copy all your Bulletins (from a Conference) to it.\n\n\n  AE 3.xx:\n  ~~~~~~~~\n  - Copy B.info to BBS:Commands/BBScmd/\n\n    Or add to B.info ICON ToolType Info:\n\n      ACCESS=001\n      LOCATION=DOORS:EmP_Tools/Bulls\n      MULTINODE=YES\n      PRIORITY=0\n      STACK=50000\n      TYPE=XIM\n\n\n  - Don''t forget to Redirect Output Files from Others tools (in logOff.bat)\n    to BBS:bulletins and Not to the ''old'' BBS:Conference/Bulletins! \n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n USAGE:\n ~~~~~~\n  Just enter B on the MAIN screen in AmiExpress.\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n ERROR MESSAGES:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n  o ERROR:  Bulls 2.0 ONLY Works with /X 3.xx!!\n  `-------> Obvious\n\n  o ERROR:  BBS:Bulletins/bull{x}.txt Not Found !!\n  `-------> Bulletin {x} can''t be found in BBS:Bulletins\n\n  o ERROR:  DOORS:EmP_Tools/Bulls.CFG Not Found !!\n  `-------> Bulls.CFG can''t be found in DOORS:EmP_Tools\n\n  o ERROR:  UnKnown Keyword: XXXXXXXX in JoinCnf.CFG\n  |\n  `--> There must be 2 different KeyWords in the INIT part (Bulls.CFG)\n       Compare this with the original Bulls.CFG\n       Check that the KeyWords are:\n\n         DUAL_LISTINGS\n         CURSOR_KEYS\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n BUG REPORT & SUGGESTIONS:                                                                   \n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  It''s possible that a mistake will occure.... Nobody is Perfect.\n  If you have any Suggestions or Comments Please Leave a Message on my Board:\n\n   LaSt OuTpOsT  N1: +31-72-157682  N2: +31-72-201182  -  HOLLAND\n   ~~~~~~~~~~~~  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~     ~~~~~~~\n   AmixNet:  @NL0004\n   /X-Fido:  44:100/102\n   UUCP   :  [email removed]\n\n===============================================================================\n\n NOTE:\n ~~~~~\n  o This Program Has been tested on a /X 2.0 - 3.38 Configuration.\n\n  o If a User uses More lines then the sysop can see the Screen-Output on\n    the Sysop-side will be scrambled caused by the Ansi-Handling but on\n    the Users-side it will be ok!!\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n REGISTRATION:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  If YOU use this Program please let me know by Calling Last Outpost or\n  to send me a Message by NetMail @NL0004 - EMPiRE  Coz we want to know\n  how many Sysops are using our Tools!!!\n \n\n===============================================================================\n\n HISTORY:\n ~~~~~~~~\n  V0.1  11-07-92 - Internal Version\n\n  V1.0  02-03-93 - Release Version\n\n  V1.1  03-20-93 - Added The 2 OutputList Option\n                 - Added Support for .txt.gr Files\n                 - [Bulls.CFG CHANGED!]\n\n  V1.2  05-05-93 - Added ''Non-Stop'' Menu Showing, if you got too many Bulls\n                   then the irritating ''More (Y/n/ns)'' appeared... FIXED\n                 - Cleaned Up.\n        06-21-93 - Fixed a small Error found with the RexxDoorDebugger.\n\n  V2.0ß 01-01-94 - ReWritten to XIM!\n        01-13-94 - Better Bulls.CFG reading\n                 - Added some more Ansi Colors\n                 - Changed the Bulls.CFG layout (same layout as JoinCnf.CFG).\n                   It''s now also possible to use your Own Bulletin Logo\n                   [Bulls.CFG CHANGED!]\n        01-14-94 - Bug Report from JPS\n                    o When using Bull [00] it was possible to press different\n                      <SHIFT>-keys to show it.. FIXED\n        01-17-94 - When Bulls is run, it will ShowUp on the Server.\n        01-25-94 - Fixed the ''10-Node'' BUG\n\n  V2.0  01-29-94 - Release\n\n  V2.1ß 02-05-94 - Change the ''Full Use of 80 Chars/Line'' to 79 Chars/Line\n                   because some Terminals on Amiga/PC can''t handle the 80th\n                   character right (extra linefeeds)!\n        02-07-94 - Bug Report from B.O.B/CF & Enzo:\n                    o When using NON-Ansi the character color will change to\n                      Magenta when exiting/using Bulls.\n                      There were 2 ESC-chars after eachother in the command-\n                      line which /X doesn''t like... FIXED!\n        02-28-94 - Added Cursor-Key Support. To Include this the Bulls.CFG\n                   changed:\n                    o Bull0.txt support has been deleted, so change your\n                      Bull-Access!\n                 - [Bulls.CFG CHANGED!]\n        03-20-94 - Optimized some code.\n        03-24-94 - Added some Suggestions from SpeedDevil/Partek:\n                    o When starting Bulls the BullSelection >[]< will now\n                      be disabled until an ArrowKey is pressed or a Bull is \n                      selected.\n                    o After showing a Bulletin pressing <ENTER> will show\n                      the Bulletin-List again and not Quit Bulls anymore.\n                      So it''s now only possible to Quit Bulls in the\n                      Bulletin-List.\n \n  V2.1  04-13-94 - Release Version.\n\n  V2.2ß 04-18-94 - ReCompiled with the Latest AE.Includes.\n        04-24-94 - Fixed the Text-Showing Error when there is no ClearScreen\n                   code in the Bulletin.\n        05-21-94 - Changed a few things:\n                    when a bulletin is selected from command line (b 1) then\n                    Bulls will quit right away (when the bulletin doesn''t\n                    exist the Bulls menu will be shown)\n                 - Removed a small bug concerning the Commandline starting.\n                 - Killed all sscanf''s in the Source coz of Bugs in the\n                   SAS Compiler and this way Bulls gets 2 kb smaller!\n        06-21-94 - When a Bulletin is shown then the shown BulletinNr will be\n                   printed on the commandline (Request from Tycoon)\n                 - BugFix: When there where no Bulletins present in the\n                   current Conference it was still possible to enter a key.\n\n  V2.2  07-01-94 - Release Version.\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n EMPiRE /X DOORS/UTILS COLLECTION UNTIL NOW!:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  - AboStats V0.2                        AIM Door\n  - AE2PCE V1.0                          CLI Util\n  - AutoOnline V1.3                      XIM Door/Util\n  - Bulls V2.2                           XIM Door\n  - CheckDir V1.0                        CLI Util\n  - CheckNU V1.0                         XIM Door\n  - ConfAccess V1.1                      ServerUtil\n  - CopyDate V1.3                        CLI Util\n  - DlDir V2.1                           XIM Door\n  - DoorKIT 1.01                         XIM Doors/Includes\n  - DMenu V1.0                           AIM Door\n  - DutchNET V1.0  [AmiXnet]             AIM Door\n  - Front V2.0                           XIM Door\n  - JoinCnf V3.6                         XIM Door\n  - LastCalls & TopUps V1.2              LogOffUtil\n  - LastDL V0.1                          LogOffUtil\n  - LastUL V0.1                          LogOffUtil\n  - MakeFree V1.1                        AIM Door\n  - MemberList V1.0                      AIM Door\n  - MonthTopUp V2.0                      ServerUtil\n  - MultiNodeLastCaller V1.1             LogOffUtil\n  - Page V2.1                            XIM Door\n  - PMail V1.1                           AIM Door\n  - Remote Maintenance V1.3              AIM Door\n  - SceneTalk Voter V2.3                 AIM Door\n  - SceneTalk Voter V2.2 [Party]         CLI Door\n  - SecLevChk V1.0                       ServerUtil\n  - Sent FrondEnd 1.0  [Sent_FE]         XIM Door\n  - StripCR V1.0                         CLI Util\n  - SysopCommands V1.0                   AIM Door\n  - UserData Cleaner/Repair V2.0         ServerUtil\n  - UserStats V2.0                       ServerUtil\n  - UsrCnfAx V1.1                        CLI Util\n  - View & Check Archive/Text V1.7       AIM Door\n  - WhoNode V1.3                         AIM Door\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n THANX MUST GO TO ALL OFFICIAL BETA-TESTERS:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n   Tycoon/Mystic /X-PoWeR!   [Channel X]\n   JPS                       [Red October]\n   Sal-One/TRSi              [BoonDocks]\n   Blue Bird/Mystic          [Tau Ceti]\n   Beast/Partek              [Sequencial]\n   SpeedDevil/Partek         [Rising Sun]\n   Galaxy                    [Ulixys]\n\n\n GREETZ/TNX GO TO:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n   Killraven/MST /X-PoWeR! - For giving me sum Great Pointers/Sources on ''C''\n   ByteAndi/TRSI           - Tnx for all ya ''C'' Help & Sources!\n   Easy Rider/Mystic       - hope ya are back soon!\n   JAF/G.O.D.              - For some good REXX ideas\n   Bad Sector/Hidden       - Still Using your Sort-Routine. It''s the Fastest!\n   B.O.B./CyberForce       - For (Mis)Using/Testing my tools! :)\n   Aragorn/Vision          - Tnx for Testing\n   Camelot/Complex         - Tnx for Testing\n   Sharon/5D               - Tnx for Testing\n   Telekinetic/T.F.A.      - Tnx for Testing\n   Alcoholic               - Tnx for Testing\n   Price/T.F.A.            - Great job on your {F}ull {S}creen {E}ditor!\n   Van Damme               - Nice Doors!!!\n   DR.G/IBB                - Hope to see Check''N Add work on a 040\n   SiGMA SEVEN             - Nice job on SiGMA-EXPRESS! Tempted to ''Convert''\n   911/Movement            - Tnx For ya Ansi Logo''s!! You''re the Greatest!\n   Mike                    - Tnx for calling!\n   Amicom/TRSi             - Tnx for calling!\n   THC/Legend              - Tnx for Beta-Testing!\n   Mega Fortress           - Tnx for Beta-Testing!\n   SkIn                    - Tnx for ya Description Logo! Looks Great!!\n   Shadow Man/S8           - Nice Doors & Tnx for ya greetz! & Calling ofcoz\n   [MAZ!^PHAZE]            - Tnx for calling!\n   Shuyuki Tanaka          - Tnx for your Messages!\n   AGONY/cOmpLeX           - Tnx for calling!\n   HUMANOiD & jABBA /MST &\n    SCANDAL                - Tnx for calling!\n   LECTOR                  - Tnx for your NetMail\n   Koo Koo Ka Choo         - Tnx for calling!\n   TaRzAN                  - Tnx for your NetMail. Yezz 040 Speed Rulez!!\n   Crayor/Scx              - Tnx for calling!\n   Foxx''n''Lynxx            - Tnx for your BugReports!!!\n   ThE BiRD                - Tnx for your NetMail on UsrCnfAx\n   Dux                     - Tnx for your NetMail\n   dR.dRE!/fAITH           - Tnx for da greetz, Nice Doors btw\n   [-RUNT&SCOTTIE-]        - Tnx for calling!\n   sPAcEcAKe/aF            - Tnx for calling!\n   Freddy Kreuger/GOD      - Tnx for your NetMail on JoinCnf 3.2\n   MF1                     - Tnx for calling!\n   AtomiX/N.A.S.A          - Hope the ''C'' archive was sume help for ya!\n   MAD HARLEQUiN [ITPH01]  - Tnx for your Nice AmiXnet Messy''s\n   Mike Hoffren  [SF0001]  - Tnx for the BugReport on JoinCnf 3.3 [100+ Cnfs]\n   Galaxy/TFA              - Nice job on da SentCleaner\n   SvEN tHE CREAToR/5D     - ''Tnx'' for forcing me to use Cursor-Keys!\n   Diogenes/TPY/5D         - Tnx for calling and for your BugReport!\n   L.A.Style               - Tnx For Calling/Beta-Testing!\n\n   & Ofcoz to ALL MYSTiC Members all over the Globe!\n\n                        ______  __________________                            \n.----------------+-----/    \ \/ / __/_  __/ / __/----------+----------------.\n|                |----/ / / /\  /\  /-/ /-/ / /----[ /X ]---|                |\n|       /\    /\ |-EmP\/ / /-/ /\  /-/ /-/ /\ \--[ PoWeR! ]-|       /\    /\ |\n|      /C \  /!/ +-----\/\/--\/--\/--\/--\/--\/-------------+      /C \  /!/ |\n|     /i/\ \/R/  |                                          |     /i/\ \/R/  |\n|    /T/  \ E/   |   EMPiRE   -   KiLLRAVEN  -   TYCOON     |    /T/  \ E/   |\n|   /S/   /W \   |                                          |   /S/   /W \   |\n|  /Y/   /O/\ \  |   RE/Y\o   -   INCOGNiTO  -   HARDBYTE   |  /Y/   /O/\ \  |\n| /M/   /P/  \ \ |                                          | /M/   /P/  \ \ |\n| \/    \/    \/ |                   BoBo                   | \/    \/    \/ |\n|                |                                          |                |\n`----------------+----------[  MYSTiC /X PoWeR!  ]----------+----------------''\n\n\n \n\n                       ____ _________ _________ ________ _____\n            MYSTiC    /   / \\  /    \\\  /   _\\\  /   \\\  /     MYSTiC\n                     /   /   \\/   /\ \\\/   /___\\/__   \\\/\n         CONSOLE    /   / /\  /   __   \ \____   \   /   /      AMIGA\n                   /   /_/  \/   / /   /_____/   /  /   /\n       WORLD-HQ    \________X___/ /___/\________/   \__/      EURO-HQ\n      ____ _________ ________ _________ _________ _________ ________ _____\n     /    \\\  /   / \\  /   \\\  /    \\\  /    \\\  /   _\\\  /   \\\  /\n    /   /\ \\\/   / /\\\/__   \\\/   /\ \\\/   /\ \\\/   /___\\/__   \\\/\n   /   / /  \/   / /  \   /   / /   _____\/   / /  \ \____   \   /   /\n  /   /_/   /   /_/   /  /   / /   /     /   /_/   /_____/   /  /   /\n  \________X_________/   \__/  \__/      \________/\________/   \__/\n\n\nAMIGA - SNES - MEGADRIVE - GAMEBOY - GAMEGEAR - PC ENGINE - LYNX NEOGEO - C64\n\n4.5 Gb ONLINE             SYSOP:  EMPiRE / MYSTiC               4.5 Gb ONLINE\n\nHOLLAND:              +31-72-157682  &  +31-72-201182               :HOLLAND\n\n','\n',char(10)),'{"ACCESS":"001","LOCATION":"DOORS:EmP_Tools/Bulls","PRIORITY":"0","STACK":"50000","TYPE":"XIM"}','auto-added',22291,3,0,NULL,NULL,'emp_bl22','scan',1780048498);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('emp_ca10','EMP-CA10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/EMP-CA10.LHA','ConfAccess','XIM','ConfAccess','1.0','EMPiRE/[SBS]','EMP',NULL,replace('AE UTIL: ConfAccess V1.0   - by EMPiRE/[SBS]\n','\n',char(10)),'ConfAccess.doc',replace('\n                  ###### ###   ## ######  ### ######  ######              \n    _______|\     ###    #### ### ###  ## ### ###  ## ###       /|________\n   |         >    ####   ######## ######  ### ######  ####     <         |\n   | |¯¯¯¯¯|/     ###    ### # ## ###     ### #####   ###       \|¯¯¯¯¯| |\n   | |            ###### ###   ## ###     ### ### ##  ######           | |\n   | |_________________________________________________________________| |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |                          ConfAccess V1.0                            |\n   |                          ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~                            |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |                       BY EMPiRE / SUBMiSSiON                        |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |             LaSt OuTpOsT  +31-72-157682 & +31-72-201182             |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |       AmixNet:  @NL0004   -   /X-Fido:  44:100/102   [EMPiRE]       |\n   |_____________________________________________________________________|\n\n \n\n PURPOSE:\n ~~~~~~~~\n  I Made This tool after installing /X 3.1 when i found out that i had\n  28 different Conference Accesses and that''s a bit too much!\n  \n  With this Tool you can:\n\n    - Change/Rename Conference Access\n    - Move a Conference\n    - Merge a Conference Access with another Conference\n    - List All Users with Selected Conference Access\n    - Backup User.Data & User.Keys\n    - Create Conference List in RAM:\n\n\n REQUIREMENTS:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  - A Running RexxMast\n  - /X 3.x  (It won''t work with earlier /X Versions)\n\n\n INSTALLATION:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  - Copy All the Files to BBS:Utils/EmP :\n\n     BBS:Utils/EmP/ConfAccess\n     BBS:Utils/EmP/ConfAccess.doc\n\n  - Create a Backup Directory for the User.Data/User.Keys:\n\n     BBS:BACKUP\n\n  - Add the BBS:Utils/EmP Directory to your Path (Startup-Seqeunce)\n\n  - Add to BBS:ACP.info ICON ToolType Info:\n\n      BUTTON_NAME.<num>=ConfAccess\n      BUTTON_COMMAND.<num>=run >NIL: BBS:Utils/EmP/ConfAccess\n\n       <num>=1-15\n\n\n USAGE:\n ~~~~~~\n  - Server Usage:  Select <ConfAccess> Button\n  - CLI Usage   :  ConfAccess\n\n\n IMPORTANT:\n ~~~~~~~~~~\n  - ALWAYS make a BACKUP (option 3) BEFORE you SAVE the NEW\n    User.Data & User.Keys !!!\n\n\n BUG REPORT & SUGGESTIONS:                                                                   \n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  It''s possible that a mistake will occur.... Nobody is Perfect.\n  If you have any Suggestions or Comments Please Leave a Message on my Board:\n\n    LaSt OuTpOsT  +31-721-57682  -  HOLLAND    NETMAIL:  @NL0004\n    ~~~~~~~~~~~~  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~     ~~~~~~~    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n NOTE:\n ~~~~~\n  - This Tool works GREAT on a 68040 or higher. But on a 68000\n    it''s a bit slow! So be patient or buy a 020+!\n  - This Program Has been Made for use with a /X 3.6 Configuration. But it\n    will Work on ANY /X 3.x Setup.\n\n\n REGISTRATION (?!):\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  - If YOU use this Program please let me know by Calling Last Outpost or\n    to send me a Message by NetMail @NL0004 [EMPiRE] Coz I want to know\n    how many Sysops are using my Tools!!!\n\n\n HISTORY:\n ~~~~~~~~\n  V0.1  04-27-93  - First Beta Release\n                     I Made This tool after installing /X 3.1 when i found\n                     out that i had 28 different Conference Accesses and\n                     that''s a bit too much!\n  V0.2  04-08-93  - Cleaned up some code\n                  - Added ''Show Conferences Access'' Option\n  V0.3  05-16-93  - Beta Release Version\n                  - Better Layout\n  V0.4  05-20-93  - Added ConferencesList\n                  - Forced Delete of Protected Temp.Files\n        05-25-93  - Added ''Change Access'' depending on certain UserLevel\n  V1.0  06-21-93  - Added ''Create Conference List''\n                    This will make a txt file in ram (RAM:ConfAccess.txt)\n                    which will show all Conferences and their Access to them.\n        06-24-93  - Changed the Layout a bit\n                  - Updated the PAL/NTSC Window code\n                  - Removed all /X 2.xx related code because it''s useless for\n                    /X 2.xx\n                  - Added a ShortCut: ConfAccess NOCHK\n                    this way the User.Data/Uer.Keys will not be Checked.\n\n\n\n EMPiRE /X DOORS/UTILS COLLECTION UNTIL NOW!:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  - AboStats V0.2                        Door\n  - Bulls V1.2                           Door\n  - ConfAccess V1.0                      ServerUtil\n  - CopyDate V1.3                        Util\n  - DlDir V1.2                           Door\n  - DMenu V1.0                           Door\n  - DutchNET V1.0                        Door\n  - JoinCnf V2.2                         Door\n  - LastCalls & TopUps V1.2              Util\n  - MakeFree V1.1                        Door\n  - MemberList V1.0                      Door\n  - MonthTopUp V2.0                      ServerUtil\n  - MultiNodeLastCaller V1.1             Util\n  - Page V1.3                            Door\n  - PMail V1.1                           Door\n  - Remote Maintenance V1.3              Door\n  - SceneTalk Voter V2.1                 Door\n  - SecLevChk V1.0                       ServerUtil\n  - SysopCommands V1.0                   Door\n  - UserData Cleaner/Repair V1.4         ServerUtil\n  - UserStats V2.0                       ServerUtil\n  - UsrCnfAx V1.0                        Util\n  - View & Check Archive/Text V1.6       Door\n  - WhoNode V1.3                         Door\n\n\n THANX MUST GO TO ALL OFFICIAL BETA-TESTERS:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n   Aragorn/Vision           [Terminal Zone]\n   Camelot/Endless Piracy   [Chaos]\n   Telekinetic/T.F.A.       [Total Confusion]\n   Alcoholic                [Sticky Fingers]\n   Tycoon/Desire            [Channel X]\n   Mike                     [Global Chaos]\n   Amicom/TRSi              [Skara Brae]\n   JPS/Submission           [Red October]\n   Sal-One/TRSi             [BoonDocks]\n\n\n GREETZ/TNX GO TO:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n   JAF/G.O.D.          - For some good REXX ideas\n   Bad Sector/Hidden   - Still Using your Sort-Routine... It''s the Fastest!\n   Price/T.F.A.        - Great job on your {F}ull {S}creen {E}ditor!\n   Van Damme           - Nice Doors!!! Will call ya for a chat!\n   DR.G/IBB            - Hope to see Check''N Add work on a 040\n   SiGMA SEVEN         - Long time no ''See''\n   911/Movement        - Tnx For ya Ansi Logo''s!!\n   SkIn                - Tnx for ya Decription Logo! Looks Great!!\n   Shadow Man/S8       - Nice Doors & Tnx for ya greetz!\n   [MAZ!^PHAZE]        - Tnx for calling!\n   Shuyuki Tanaka      - Tnx for your Messages!\n   \n   & Ofcoz to ALL SUBMiSSiON Members all over the Globe!\n\n\n                       ____ _________ _________ ________ _____\n        AMIGA         /   / \\  /    \\\  /   _\\\  /   \\\  /     AMIGA\n       SNES          /   /   \\/   /\ \\\/   /___\\/__   \\\/     SNES\n      MEGADRIVE     /   / /\  /   __   \ \____   \   /   /       MEGADRIVE\n     GAMEBOY       /   /_/  \/   / /   /_____/   /  /   /       GAMEBOY\n    GAMEGEAR      /_________/___/ /___/_________/  /___/       GAMEGEAR\n      ____ _________ ________ _________ _________ _________ ________ _____\n     /    \\\  /   / \\  /   \\\  /    \\\  /    \\\  /   _\\\  /   \\\  /\n    /   /\ \\\/   / /\\\/__   \\\/   /\ \\\/   /\ \\\/   /___\\/__   \\\/\n   /   / /  \/   / /  \   /   / /   _____\/   / /  \ \____   \   /   /\n  /   /_/   /   /_/   /  /   / /   /     /   /_/   /_____/   /  /   /\n /_________/_________/  /___/ /___/     /_________/_________/  /___/\n\n\n                       SYSOP:  EMPiRE / SUBMiSSiON\n\n               HOLLAND:    +31-72-157682  &  +31-72-201182\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',9109,2,0,NULL,NULL,'emp_ca10','scan',1780048498);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('emp_cn10','EMP-CN10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/EMP-CN10.LHA','CheckNU','XIM','CheckNU',NULL,NULL,'EMP','¦_/\___/\___/\___                          ¦ |\   /\ __/_  __/   Checks NewUser Status  | |/ Y \/_.¬\/  \        for ''Lameness''      |',replace('+[ MYSTiC /X-DESiGN ]----[ CheckNU 1.0 ]---+\n¦_/\___/\___/\___                          ¦\n|\   /\ __/_  __/   Checks NewUser Status  |\n|/ Y \/_.¬\/  \        for ''Lameness''      |\n/  | \\¬¦ \\  \\ It will ''SetBack'' InActive|\n\__l_//___//__//  Users to a NewUser-Level ¦\n|dL!\/   \/  \/   after a number of Calls  |\n+-[ EMPiRE/MYSTiC ]------[ XIM - /X 3.xx ]-+\n','\n',char(10)),'CheckNU.DOC',replace('\n                  ###### ###   ## ######  ### ######  ######              \n    _______|\     ###    #### ### ###  ## ### ###  ## ###       /|________\n   |         >    ####   ######## ######  ### ######  ####     <         |\n   | |¯¯¯¯¯|/     ###    ### # ## ###     ### #####   ###       \|¯¯¯¯¯| |\n   | |            ###### ###   ## ###     ### ### ##  ######           | |\n   | |_________________________________________________________________| |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |                            CheckNU V1.0                             |\n   |                            ~~~~~~~~~~~~                             |\n   |                             TYPE:  XIM                              |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |                  ©1994 EMPiRE / MYSTiC /X-DESiGN                    |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |       LaSt OuTpOsT  +31-72-157682 & +31-72-201182  -  HOLLAND       |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |       AmixNet:  @NL0004   -   /X-Fido:  44:100/102     EMPiRE       |\n   |_____________________________________________________________________|\n\n===============================================================================\n\n PURPOSE:\n ~~~~~~~~\n  - Checks NewUser Status for Lameness:\n\n    (New) Users that have logged on a number of times and didn''t upload a\n    number of bytes and have a certain Level will be warned that their\n    account is not good enuf and that they have a number of logOn''s left\n    to Change this. After that if the User didn''t comply he is SetBack to\n    the NewUser Conference.\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\nOutput Messages:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n  MINLEVEL   15             \n  MINLOGON   10             \n  MAXLOGON   13             \n  MINBYTES   1000000        \n\n o Warning Message:\n\n ============================[   W A R N I N G   ]===========================\n                                                  \n               Your Account is BAD! You already logged on 10 Times\n\n                     Without even Uploading at least 1 Mb!\n \n                    You got 3 LogOn''s left to Change this!!\n\n                      Otherwise your Account here is GONE!!\n\n =[ 8 ]======================[   W A R N I N G   ]===========================\n\n\n\n o SetBack Message:\n\n ============================[   W A R N I N G   ]===========================\n\n \n     Your Account has been put back to a NEWUSER level coz of INACTIVITY.\n\n\n =[ 8 ]======================[   W A R N I N G   ]===========================\n\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n REQUIREMENTS:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  Ami Express 3.xx (there won''t be a 1.1x or 2.xx Version. So UPGRADE NOW!)\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n INSTALLATION:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  o Copy the EmP_Tools Directory to DOORS:\n    Edit it to your Needs. (Check the Existing CheckNU.CFG!)\n\n CheckNU.CFG LayOut:\n\n##[ start: cut here ]#########################################################\nMINLEVEL   15                   ; Levels equal/below MINLEVEL will be Checked\nMINLOGON   10                   ; Min. Nr of LogOns before Warning\nMAXLOGON   13                   ; Max. Nr of LogOns before NEWUSER SetBack\nMINBYTES   1000000              ; Min. Upload Bytes for Checking\nLOGFILE    BBS:SetBack.LOG      ; LogFile of Users who where SetBack\n##[ end: cut here ]###########################################################\n\n\n  AE 3.xx:\n  ~~~~~~~~\n  o Copy CheckNU.info BBS:Commands/SYScmd/\n\n    Or add to CheckNU.info ICON ToolType Info:\n\n      ACCESS=001\n      LOCATION=DOORS:EmP_Tools/CheckNU\n      MULTINODE=YES\n      PRIORITY=0\n      STACK=50000\n      TYPE=XIM\n\n  o This Door was designed to Start from a Bulletin this way the Door is\n    started with every User\n\n    as BBS:Bull.txt\n\n--[ start: cut here ]-------------------------\n~CC_FE_Sent\n--[ stop: cut here ]--------------------------\n\n    or with a txtfile (BBS:Bulletins/bull.txt)\n\n--[ start: cut here ]-------------------------\n~SS_BBS:Bulletins/bull.txt|~CC_FE_Sent\n--[ stop: cut here ]--------------------------\n    Example:\n\n    ~SS_BBS:Bulletins/bull.txt|~CC_CheckNU|~CC_Sent_FE|\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n NOTE:\n ~~~~~\n\n  o When a User is SetBack the Carrier will be dropped! There is no other way\n    because /X will let the User join the conference he was last in even\n    when he hasn''t got access to it anymore!\n\n  o Users that have been SetBack to the NewUser Conference will see the\n    Message again when the LogOn but the Carrier will not be dropped!\n    So the User can explain his MisBehaviour (or NOT).\n\n  o Keep in mind that if the Name of the NewUser Conference changes then\n    Users who were setback to the Old NewUser Conference are always Kicked\n    Off after the Message.\n\n  o In the LogFile contains:\n     - Date the User was SetBack\n     - UserName\n     - ConferenceAccess before the User was SetBack\n\n  o The LogFile will be Created if it doesn''t exist!\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n ERROR MESSAGES:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n  o ERROR:  CheckNU ONLY Works with /X 3.x!!\n  |\n  `--> Obvious\n\n  o ERROR:  DOORS:EmP_Tools/CheckNU.CFG Not Found !!!\n  |\n  `--> CheckNU.CFG can''t be found in DOORS:EmP_Tools !?\n\n  o ERROR:  BBS:ACCESS/Preset.1.info Not Found !!!\n  |\n  `--> BBS:ACCESS/Preset.1.info can''t be found\n\n  o ERROR:  BBS:Access/PRESET.1.info is NOT valid!\n  |         Can''t find IconToolType: PRESET.AREA\n  |\n  `--> Check BBS:Access/PRESET.1.info for Errors\n\n  o ERROR:  Can''t Open DoorFile\n  |\n  `--> For some reason the DoorFile can''t be Created or Written to!\n\n  o ERROR:  UnKnown Keyword: XXXXXXXX in CheckNU.CFG\n  |\n  `--> There must be 5 different lines in the INIT part (CheckNU.CFG)\n       Compare this with the original CheckNU.CFG\n       Check that the KeyWords are:\n\n         MINLEVEL\n         MINLOGON\n         MAXLOGON\n         MINBYTES\n         LOGFILE\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n BUG REPORT & SUGGESTIONS:                                                                   \n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  It''s possible that a mistake will occur.... Nobody is Perfect.\n  If you have any Suggestions or Comments Please Leave a Message on my Board:\n\n   LaSt OuTpOsT  N1: +31-72-157682  N2: +31-72-201182  -  HOLLAND\n   ~~~~~~~~~~~~  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~     ~~~~~~~\n       AmixNet:  @NL0004   -   /X-Fido:  44:100/102   EMPiRE\n       ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~       ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~   ~~~~~~\n\n===============================================================================\n\n /X NOTE:\n ~~~~~~~~\n  This Program Has been tested on a /X 2.0 - /X 3.32 Configuration.\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n REGISTRATION:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  If YOU use this Program please let me know by Calling Last Outpost or\n  to send me a Message by NetMail @NL0004 - EMPiRE  Coz I want to know\n  how many Sysops are using my Tools!!!\n \n\n===============================================================================\n\n HISTORY:\n ~~~~~~~~\n  V0.1  12-10-92 - First Beta Version.\n\n  V0.2  12-22-92 - Added a LogFile with all SetBack Users.\n                 - Added some more Ansi-Color\n        01-17-94 - When CheckNU is run, it will ShowUp on the Server.\n        01-25-94 - Fixed the ''10-Node'' BUG\n\n  V1.0  01-29-94 - Release Version\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n EMPiRE /X DOORS/UTILS COLLECTION UNTIL NOW!:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  - AboStats V0.2                        AIM Door\n  - AutoOnline V1.1                      XIM Door/Util\n  - Bulls V2.0                           XIM Door\n  - CheckNU V1.0                         XIM Door\n  - ConfAccess V1.1                      ServerUtil\n  - CopyDate V1.3                        CLI Util\n  - DlDir V2.0                           XIM Door\n  - DoorKIT 1.01                         XIM Doors/Includes\n  - DMenu V1.0                           AIM Door\n  - DutchNET V1.0  [AmiXnet]             AIM Door\n  - Front V2.0                           XIM Door\n  - JoinCnf V3.4                         XIM Door\n  - LastCalls & TopUps V1.2              LogOffUtil\n  - LastDL V0.1                          LogOffUtil\n  - LastUL V0.1                          LogOffUtil\n  - MakeFree V1.1                        AIM Door\n  - MemberList V1.0                      AIM Door\n  - MonthTopUp V2.0                      ServerUtil\n  - MultiNodeLastCaller V1.1             LogOffUtil\n  - Page V2.0                            XIM Door\n  - PMail V1.1                           AIM Door\n  - Remote Maintenance V1.3              AIM Door\n  - SceneTalk Voter V2.3                 AIM Door\n  - SceneTalk Voter V2.2 [Party]         CLI Door\n  - SecLevChk V1.0                       ServerUtil\n  - Sent FrondEnd 1.0  [Sent_FE]         XIM Door\n  - SysopCommands V1.0                   AIM Door\n  - UserData Cleaner/Repair V2.0         ServerUtil\n  - UserStats V2.0                       ServerUtil\n  - UsrCnfAx V1.1                        CLI Util\n  - View & Check Archive/Text V1.7       AIM Door\n  - WhoNode V1.3                         AIM Door\n\n===============================================================================\n\n THANX MUST GO TO ALL OFFICIAL BETA-TESTERS:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n   Tycoon/Mystic             [Channel X]\n   ByteAndi/Mystic           [Diabolo]\n   JPS                       [Red October]\n   Sal-One/TRSi              [BoonDocks]\n   Sharon/Scx                [The Unknown]\n   Blue Bird/Mystic          [Tau Ceti]\n   Easy Rider/Mystic         [Mamba]\n   Mega Fortress             [MF Enterprise]\n   Beast/Partek              [Sequencial]\n   SpeedDevil/Partek         [Rising Sun]\n\n\n GREETZ/TNX GO TO:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n   ByteAndi/MST /X-DESiGN  - NewFiles is the best! And Tnx for all ya ''C''\n                             Help & Sources! You''re (almost) the Greatest!\n   Killraven/MST /X-DESiGN - For giving me sum Great Pointers/Sources on ''C''\n   CrackDown/MST /X-DESiGN - Nice Doors, Keep it up!\n   JAF/G.O.D.              - For some good REXX ideas\n   Bad Sector/Hidden       - Still Using your Sort-Routine. It''s the Fastest!\n   B.O.B./Paradox          - For (Mis)Using/Testing my tools!\n   Aragorn/Vision          - Tnx for Testing in the past\n   Camelot/Complex         - Tnx for Testing in the past\n   Telekinetic/T.F.A.      - Tnx for Testing in the past\n   Alcoholic               - Tnx for Testing in the past\n   Price/T.F.A.            - Great job on your {F}ull {S}creen {E}ditor!\n   Van Damme               - Nice Doors!!!\n   DR.G/IBB                - Hope to see Check''N Add work on a 040\n   SiGMA SEVEN             - Nice job on SiGMA-EXPRESS!\n   911/Movement            - Tnx For ya Ansi Logo''s!! You''re the Greatest!\n   Mike                    - Tnx for calling!\n   Amicom/TRSi             - Tnx for calling!\n   SkIn                    - Tnx for ya Description Logo! Looks Great!!\n   Shadow Man/S8           - Nice Doors & Tnx for ya greetz! & Calling ofcoz\n   [MAZ!^PHAZE]            - Tnx for calling!\n   Shuyuki Tanaka          - Tnx for your Messages!\n   AGONY/cOmpLeX           - Tnx for calling!\n   HUMANOiD & RU$tY/AFL    - Tnx for calling!\n   LECTOR                  - Tnx for your NetMail\n   Koo Koo Ka Choo         - Tnx for calling!\n   TaRzAN                  - Tnx for your NetMail. Yezz 040 Speed Rulez!!\n   Crayor/Scx              - Tnx for calling!\n   Foxx''n''Lynxx            - Tnx for your BugReports!!!\n   ThE BiRD                - Tnx for your NetMail on UsrCnfAx\n   Dux                     - Tnx for your NetMail\n   dR.dRE!/fAITH           - Tnx for da greetz, Nice Doors btw\n   [-RUNT&SCOTTIE-]        - Tnx for calling!\n   sPAcEcAKe/aF            - Tnx for calling!\n   Freddy Kreuger/GOD      - Tnx for your NetMail on JoinCnf 3.2\n   MF1                     - Tnx for calling!\n   AtomiX/N.A.S.A          - Hope the ''C'' archive was sume help for ya!\n   MAD HARLEQUiN [ITPH01]  - Tnx for your Nice AmiXnet Messy''s\n   Mike Hoffren  [SF0001]  - Tnx for the BugReport on JoinCnf 3.3 [100+ Cnfs]\n   Galaxy/TFA              - Nice job on da SentCleaner\n\n\n   & Ofcoz to ALL MYSTiC Members all over the Globe!\n\n\n                        ______  __________________                            \n.----------------+-----/    \ \/ / __/_  __/ / __/----------+----------------.\n|                |----/ / / /\  /\  /-/ /-/ / /----[ /X ]---|                |\n|       /\    /\ |-EmP\/ / /-/ /\  /-/ /-/ /\ \--[ DESiGN ]-|       /\    /\ |\n|      /C \  /N/ +-----\/\/--\/--\/--\/--\/--\/-------------+      /C \  /N/ |\n|     /i/\ \/G/  |                                          |     /i/\ \/G/  |\n|    /T/  \ i/   |                                          |    /T/  \ i/   |\n|   /S/   /S \   |   EMPiRE   -   BYTEANDi   -  CRACKDOWN   |   /S/   /S \   |\n|  /Y/   /E/\ \  |   TYCOON   -   KiLLRAVEN  -   SiEGEL     |  /Y/   /E/\ \  |\n| /M/   /D/  \ \ |   FUZZY    -      SPY     -  INCOGNiTO   | /M/   /D/  \ \ |\n| \/    \/    \/ |   RE/Y\o   -     BoBo     -   HARDBYTE   | \/    \/    \/ |\n|                |                                          |                |\n`----------------+----------[  MYSTiC /X DESiGN  ]----------+----------------''\n\n \n\n                       ____ _________ _________ ________ _____\n            MYSTiC    /   / \\  /    \\\  /   _\\\  /   \\\  /     MYSTiC\n                     /   /   \\/   /\ \\\/   /___\\/__   \\\/\n         CONSOLE    /   / /\  /   __   \ \____   \   /   /      AMIGA\n                   /   /_/  \/   / /   /_____/   /  /   /\n       WORLD-HQ    \________X___/ /___/\________/   \__/      EURO-HQ\n      ____ _________ ________ _________ _________ _________ ________ _____\n     /    \\\  /   / \\  /   \\\  /    \\\  /    \\\  /   _\\\  /   \\\  /\n    /   /\ \\\/   / /\\\/__   \\\/   /\ \\\/   /\ \\\/   /___\\/__   \\\/\n   /   / /  \/   / /  \   /   / /   _____\/   / /  \ \____   \   /   /\n  /   /_/   /   /_/   /  /   / /   /     /   /_/   /_____/   /  /   /\n  \________X_________/   \__/  \__/      \________/\________/   \__/\n\n\n  AMIGA - SNES - MEGADRIVE - GAMEBOY - GAMEGEAR - PC ENGINE - LYNX - C64\n\n  3.5 Gb ONLINE          SYSOP:  EMPiRE / MYSTiC           3.5 Gb ONLINE\n\n  HOLLAND:          +31-72-157682  &  +31-72-201182             :HOLLAND\n\n','\n',char(10)),'{"ACCESS":"001","LOCATION":"DOORS:EmP_Tools/CheckNU","PRIORITY":"0","STACK":"50000","TYPE":"XIM"}','auto-added',40735,8,0,NULL,NULL,'emp_cn10','scan',1780048498);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('emp_dd20','EMP-DD20.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/EMP-DD20.LHA','DlDir','XIM','DlDir',NULL,NULL,'EMP','|              Download Selected FileDirs, | ¦_/\___/\___/\___  ''RealTime'' AllFiles     ¦ |\   /\ __/_  __/                          |',replace('+[ MYSTiC /X-DESiGN ]-----[ DlDir 2.0 ]----+\n|              Download Selected FileDirs, |\n¦_/\___/\___/\___  ''RealTime'' AllFiles     ¦\n|\   /\ __/_  __/                          |\n|/ Y \/_.¬\/  \  Added Features:           |\n/  | \\¬¦ \\  \\ o ReWritten to XIM!       |\n\__l_//___//__// o Better FileName Handling¦\n|dL!\/   \/  \/                            |\n+-[ EMPiRE/MYSTiC ]------[ XIM - /X 3.xx ]-+\n','\n',char(10)),'DlDir.DOC',replace('\n                  ###### ###   ## ######  ### ######  ######              \n    _______|\     ###    #### ### ###  ## ### ###  ## ###       /|________\n   |         >    ####   ######## ######  ### ######  ####     <         |\n   | |¯¯¯¯¯|/     ###    ### # ## ###     ### #####   ###       \|¯¯¯¯¯| |\n   | |            ###### ###   ## ###     ### ### ##  ######           | |\n   | |_________________________________________________________________| |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |                             DlDir V2.0                              |\n   |                             ~~~~~~~~~~                              |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |                         BY EMPiRE / MYSTiC                          |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |       LaSt OuTpOsT  +31-72-157682 & +31-72-201182  -  HOLLAND       |\n   |                                                                     |\n   |       AmixNet:  @NL0004   -   /X-Fido:  44:100/102   [EMPiRE]       |\n   |_____________________________________________________________________|\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n PURPOSE:\n ~~~~~~~~\n  Download (File)Dirs Online! It works like a ''RealTime'' AllFiles\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n REQUIREMENTS:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  - Ami Express 3.xx  (there won''t be a 2.xx Version... so UPGRADE NOW!)\n  - Make sure that LHA exists in your ''Path''\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n INSTALLATION:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  - Copy the EmP_Tools Directory to DOORS:\n\n\n  AE 3.xx:\n  ~~~~~~~~\n  - Copy DD.info to BBS:Commands/BBScmd/\n\n    Or add to DD.info ICON ToolType Info:\n\n      ACCESS=010\n      LOCATION=DOORS:EmP_Tools/DlDir\n      MULTINODE=YES\n      PRIORITY=0\n      STACK=50000\n      TYPE=XIM\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n USAGE:\n ~~~~~~\n  Just enter DD <FileDirs> on the MAIN screen in AmiExpress.\n\n  For Example:  DD 1 2 ABC 4 -> This will Download Dir1, Dir2 & Dir4\n                                and will Skip DirABC\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n BUG REPORT & SUGGESTIONS:                                                                   \n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  It''s possible that a mistake will occur.... Nobody is Perfect.\n  If you have any Suggestions or Comments Please Leave a Message on my Board:\n\n     LaSt OuTpOsT  N1: +31-72-157682  N2: +31-72-201182  -  HOLLAND\n     ~~~~~~~~~~~~  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~     ~~~~~~~\n        AmiXnet:  @NL0004   -   /X-Fido:  44:100/102   [EMPiRE]\n        ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~       ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~   ~~~~~~~~\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n NOTE:\n ~~~~~\n  o This Program Has been tested on a /X 3.32 Configuration.\n    But it will work on Any /X 3.xx System.\n\n  o The OutPut FileName has been changed to this format:\n\n     FileName:  03181423.LHA\n                _ _ _ _ \n                | | | |\n                | | | `---------> Seconds\n                | | `-----------> Minutes\n                | `-------------> Day\n                `---------------> Conference Number\n\n     If there are more then 100 Conferences then the first character\n     becomes a ''A''....''J''.\n\n  o To know from Which board you got the Dirs a Text-File will be added\n    with the following information:\n\n      [email removed]:\n\n       BBS       :  LaST ouTPoST\n       CONFERENCE:  SNES <OUTPOST>\n       DATE      :  01-29-94\n\n  o I''ve been thinking about adding a Global Conference Downloader but I\n    think it''s a bit useless becoz overhere the Archive would be about\n    4 Mb in size!\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n REGISTRATION:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  If YOU use this Program please let me know by Calling Last Outpost or\n  to send me a Message on AmiXnet @NL0004 [EMPiRE] Coz I want to know\n  how many Sysops are using my Tools!!!\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n HISTORY:\n ~~~~~~~~\n  V1.0  02-24-93 - First Release\n\n  V1.1  04-01-93 - Release Version\n                 - Changed the Name of the DL-File\n\n  V1.2  04-20-93 - Added NonStop Txt Showing\n        05-11-93 - /X 3.x Compatible\n        06-01-93 - Command Line Usage is now Possible! (dd 1 2 4)\n        06-12-93 - Release Version\n\n  V1.3  06-21-93 - Fixed a small Error found with the RexxDoorDebugger.\n\n  V2.0ß 01-17-94 - Rewritten to XIM\n        01-18-94 - Added a Better OutPut FileName\n        01-25-94 - Fixed the ''10-Node'' BUG.\n        01-27-94 - Added the BBS InfoFile to the Archive.\n\n  V2.0  01-29-94 - Release Version\n\n\n===============================================================================\n\n EMPiRE /X DOORS/UTILS COLLECTION UNTIL NOW!:\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  - AboStats V0.