INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('etp_r10','ETP-R10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ETP-R10.LHA','ElRead_Amix','XIM','68CKSZ',NULL,'Amix/Sigma','ETP','_\ _)  /__\ _)/ _|  |_\   \(__)\   \ / _/-/ /_| _/-/ /\_  _//   /\__/ /__/ \ \ / /  / \ / /  /  | \___/  /  |',replace('_____ ___  ____ __.___ ____  _______\n _\ _)  /__\ _)/ _|  |_\   \(__)\   \\n/ _/-/ /_| _/-/ /\_  _//   /\__/ /__/\n\ \ / /  / \ / /  /  | \___/  /  | \n____|\__/\___|___/|  |___|/___|__| products\n<-------(st!/-----|__\-----------------/\\->\n \n            Electrip Reader v1.0\n      Amix/Sigma/Tempest/Fame versions\n \n<-----------//\ releasedate: 29-Apr-1997 \->\n','\n',char(10)),'ElRead.doc',replace('putt fila i logoffbatch. datafila blir lagt/oppdatert i bbs:. vet ikke om\nsigma og tempest bruker bbs:, men bbs: må være assignet til ''main'' bbs dirren.\n\nhadde ikke tid til å legge inn destination på datafila :)\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',29434,3,0,NULL,NULL,'etp_r10','scan',1780048504);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ex2_3_18','EX2_3_18.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/EX2_3_18.LHA','Ex!_Task_2_000','XIM','Ex!_CreateSLog',NULL,NULL,'EX2','|      Exorcist! v3.0  PUBLIC BETA 18      | |       /X v2.3x & S-Express version       | +------------------------------------------+',replace('+------------------------------------------+\n|      Exorcist! v3.0  PUBLIC BETA 18      |\n|       /X v2.3x & S-Express version       |\n+------------------------------------------+\n««« FEEL THE POWER OF THIS AWESOME NUKER »»»\n','\n',char(10)),'Ex!_Sysop.guide',replace('@DATABASE "Ex!_Sysop.guide"\n\n@NODE Main "Exorcist! v3.0 - ©1993-1994 SkidRow"\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n                                 EXORCIST!\n                             The File Expeller\n                                   v3.0\n\n                   (c) 1993-1994  CFi & B/\Zz of SkidRow\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n	Table of contents:\n\n	@{" Preface     " link exsg_1} Introduction to Exorcist!\n	@{" Changes     " link exsg_2} Changes in v3.0 compared to v2.1\n	@{" Installing  " link exsg_3} How to get Exorcist! working on your system\n	@{" Configuring " link exsg_4} How to configure Exorcist! to your wishes\n	@{" Access/     " link exsg_5} How to give access to Exorcist! for /X v3.xx\n	@{" Contact     " link exsg_6} How to contact the authors\n	@{" Disclaimer  " link exsg_7} Read this!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE exsg_1 "Exorcist! v3.0 - Preface"\n\nEverybody who owns or maintains a BBS, knows that not all uploads are of\nsimilar nature. Sometimes users upload things that have already been\nuploaded. And sometimes users upload something of such value that he ought\nto get more than his standard ratio for it. Also it would be nice to make\nfiles free-download without much fuss. To solve all these problems and more,\nSkidRow made Exorcist!\n\nExorcist! is a /X utility that gives you the ability to perform certain\noperations on uploaded files. Although the most of the operations Exorcist!\ncan perform are also available in other programs (eg NosNUKE or BossNUKE),\nExorcist! combines a high speed with a greatly enhanced functionality. \n\nAlthough getting the grips with Exorcist! will probably not be as easy as\nwith simpler utilities like NosNUKE or BossNUKE, its benefits will surely\nbe worth the effort.\n\nExorcist! has been written to finally get a fast and reliable program to\ndo all those things essential for running a good BBS, but which were\nformerly only possible with slow and non friendly programs. We hope you\nenjoy using Exorcist!!\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE exsg_2 "Exorcist! v3.0 - Changes"\n\nThe new version 3.0 has several new major options compared to v2.1:\n\n- @{"Background task" link exsg_3_2}   : A background task was added to Exorcist!, to\n                      provide the service of performing all actions\n                      asked for, whether the resources for that action\n                      are available at that moment or not.\n- @{"Speedlog" link exsg_3_1}          : Exorcist! uses a fast uploader search algorithm \n                      using a special log. Under normal conditions\n                      uploaders will be found within 0.1 secs.\n- Comment editor    : Exorcist! now uses a full screen editor to add or\n                      edit comments in the filedir.\n- Edit file comment : Exorcist! gives you the possibility to edit the \n                      filecomments in the filedir.\n- Inter-conf moving : Exorcist! can move files (including comments) from\n                      one conference to another.\n- Fully configurable: Exorcist! comments and messages can be COMPLETELY edited \n                      to your wishes.\n- ASCII std comments: Exorcist! can read standard ascii files to use as default\n                      standard comments.\n- Improved filecmt  : Exorcist! now has the ability to handle any filedir\n                      utilities additions. Lines upto 160 chars and/or\n                      lines containing ANSI codes will be handled\n                      the right way.\n\nOther options are improved and bugfixed:\n\n- Exorcist! can now find uploaders who logged in the day before 0:00 and\n  uploaded their files after 0:00.\n- Major crash bug when searching uploaders and comments has been fixed.\n- Award command has been split in the award and deduct commands.\n- several small bugs were removed.\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE exsg_3 "Exorcist! v3.0 - Installing"\nHow to install Exorcist!:\n\nExorcist! uses a CBM Installer compatible install script.\nTo install Exorcist! just doubleclick the Install_Ex! icon in the\ndirectory to which Exorcist! was extracted.\n\nDuring the installation process some questions are asked:\n\n  - Select BBS directory          \n      Here you must select the directory in which your bbs is located.\n\n  - Select directory for Exorcist!\n      Here you must select an existing directory. Exorcist! will be\n      installed into this directory.\n\n  - Do you want to add Exorcist! to ... \n      If you select yes here, an entry will be added to the bbs.cmd file\n      or the BBSCmd dir, so that Exorcist! can be started from /X. It\n      is adviced to keep the access level as low as possible, since there\n      are better ways to give access to Exorcist!\n\n  - Do you want to install the @{"speedlog" link exsg_3_1}?\n      If you select yes here, the speedlog will be installed on your system.\n      The speedlog will be installed as the FRONTEND door, if your system\n      already contains a FRONTEND door, then this door should be renamed\n      to FRONTEND2, so that the speedlog door can automatically start it.\n\n  - Install the @{"background task" link exsg_3_2} permanently?\n      If you want to use the speedlog, you MUST install the background task\n      permanently. Otherwise you have the choice of installing the\n      background permanently, or having Exorcist! start the background task\n      at each use. Installing the background task permanently has the\n      advantage that Exorcist! will startup much faster!\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE exsg_3_1 "What is the speedlog?"\n\nThe speedlog is a new feature for this release, and has been added to\nExorcist! to improve the search speed for uploaders and downloaders\neven more. The only way to use speedlog is to install it via the\ninstaller script of Exorcist!.\n\nThe speedlog consists of a file called ''Ex!_SpeedLog'' and a door called\n''Ex!_UpdateSLog.x'' both are in the directory where Exorcist! is located.\nThe Ex!_UpdateSLog.x door is automaticaly executed when a user logs in,\nand will transparently update the speedlog, without the online user\nnoticing anything.\n\nThe speedlog will be kept in RAM during the time that Ex!_Task is active,\nso that the maximum search speed can be obtained. The one minor\ndisadvantage of speedlog is that you will have to spend 16KB memory to\nkeep the speedlog in memory.\n\nA speed indication: on a system with a normal taskload, Exorcist! will\nbe able to find uploaders/downloaders within 0.1 sec out of the speedlog.\n\nNOTE for users of speedlog: \n  Due to the fact that /X will not execute the FRONTEND door when\n  a sysop login (F1) is performed, you may not perform a sysop login\n  on any node where uploads and/or downloads take place. It is adviced\n  the use a special private sysop node for this, and remember that on\n  this node no uploading or downloading may take place.\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE exsg_3_2 "What is the background task?"\n\nThe background task was added to Exorcist! because in previous releases\nof Exorcist! problems with updating user records and mailheaders appeared.\n\nTo get rid of these problems the background task was introduced. The\nbackground task is a small program that runs at priority 0, so that it will\nnot take away any processor time from /X.\n\nWhen there is any time left on the system, and the needed resources are\navailable, the background task will perform all changes that are needed due\nto actions performed in Exorcist! The one huge advantage over previous\nversions of Exorcist! is the fact that ANY action you specify will ALWAYS\nbe performed!\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE exsg_4 "Exorcist! v3.0 - Configuring"\n\nStarting with this revision, Exorcist! will use the ini.library for\nprocessing its configuration file called ''Exorcist!.ini''. Due to a bug\nin ini.library the Exorcist!.ini file must exist in the same directory\nas Exorcist!, or else an endless loop will occur.\n\nThe format of the Exorcist!.ini file is as followed. The file is a normal\nASCII file, and the only demand is that the file starts with '';INI''.\n\nFurthermore the file consist of sections, which start which the section\nname between [ ] brackets (eg. [Paths]). Each section can contain multiple\nvariables, of which none is needed, Exorcist! will run OK, even if you have\na completely empty Exorcist!.ini file.\n\nEach variable is placed on one line. There cannot be more than one variable\non a line! The format for the variable line is <varname>=<value>, where you\nmay not place white spaces between the <varname> and the ''='', or between the\n''='' and the <value>.\n\nIf a line starts with '';'' or ''*'' it is considered a commentline. \nif you use a '';'' on a normal line, then the rest of that line is considered\nto be a comment. Although it is not needed, it is best to place the <value>\ninbetween ''"'' signs, if it is a string, to make sure that no unwanted spaces\nare included in the <value> string.\n\nExample:\n\n[Paths]\nStats="BBS:Ex!_Stats"                 ;this is the path to the stats file\n\n\n	Possible Sections:\n\n	@{"[ActionStrings]" link exsg_4_1} The action strings placed in the filedir\n	@{"[Comments]     " link exsg_4_2} Options for added commentlines\n	@{"[Levels]       " link exsg_4_3} Access levels for actions (for /X v2.3x only)\n	@{"[Messages]     " link exsg_4_4} Options and layout for messages send\n	@{"[Misc]         " link exsg_4_5} Miscellaneous options\n	@{"[Paths]        " link exsg_4_6} Paths to important files\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE exsg_4_1 "Configuring - ActionStrings"\n@TOC exsg_4\n\nPossible variables are:\n\nAward_L     : This string defines the action string for awarding when using\n              large comments. use %d for times credits.\n\nDeduct_L    : This string defines the action string for deducting when using\n              large comments. use %d for times credits.\n\nExpell_L    : This string defines the action string for expelling when using\n              large comments. use %d for times credits.\n\nFree_L      : This string defines the action string used when a file is made\n              free downloadable using large comments.\n\nResurrect_L : This string defines the action string used when a file is\n              resurrected using large comments.\n\n\nFree_S      : This string defines the action string used when a file is made\n              free downloadable using small comments. (max 14 chars)\n\nResurrect_S : This string defines the action string used when a file is\n              resurrected using small comments. (max 14 chars)\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE exsg_4_2 "Configuring - Comments"\n@TOC exsg_4\n\nLineStart   : This is the string that is placed at the beginning of each\n              Exorcist! commentline to identify it as an Exorcist! comment\n              line. You may NOT use an empty string here!\n\nLineEnd     : This is the string that is placed at the end of each\n              Exorcist! commentline to identify it as an Exorcist! comment\n              line. You may NOT use an empty string here!\n\nSmallCmt    : This specifies if smallcomments may be used.\n              specify "YES" if all added comments should be small comments.\n              specify "NO"  if all added comments should be large comments.\n              specify "ASK" if you want to let the user choose.\n\nStripCmt    : This specifies if Exorcist! commentlines must be removed when\n              resurrecting files. Specify YES or NO. Note that this option\n              will not work when you want to remove commentlines which have\n              other LineEnds than the current LineEnd.\n\nMaxCmtLines : This specifies the maximum number of Exorcist! commentlines\n              that may be added. 0 to 8 are valid.\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE exsg_4_3 "Configuring - Levels"\n@TOC exsg_4\n\nAward     : This specifies the level needed to award files.\n            Valid range = 0-255.\n\nComment   : This specifies the level needed to comment files.\n            Valid range = 0-255.\n\nDeduct    : This specifies the level needed to deduct files.\n            Valid range = 0-255.\n\nEditCmt   : This specifies the level needed to edit filecomments.\n            Valid range = 0-255.\n\nExpell    : This specifies the level needed to expell files.\n            Valid range = 0-255.\n\nFree      : This specifies the level needed to make files freedownload.\n            Valid range = 0-255.\n\nMoveFiles : This specifies the level needed to use the file mover.\n            Valid range = 0-255.\n\nResurrect : This specifies the level needed to resurrect files.\n            Valid range = 0-255.\n\n\nAnonymous : This specifies the level needed to stay anonymous.\n            Valid range = 0-255.\n\nWildcard  : This specifies the level needed to use wildcard.\n            Valid range = 0-255.\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE exsg_4_4 "Configuring - Messages"\n@TOC exsg_4\n\nUploader         : Send a message to the uploader(s) of the file(s).\n                   Valid are "YES", "NO" and "ASK".\n\nDownloader       : Send a message to the downloader(s) of a file.\n                   Valid are "YES", "NO" and "ASK".\n\nSysop            : Send a duplicate of each message to the sysop.\n                   Valid are "YES" and "NO". \n\nPublic           : Make the messages that are sent public.\n                   Valid are "YES" and "NO". \n\n\nAnonymous        : String placed in the sender field when the user wants\n                   to remain anonymous.\n\nSubject          : String placed in the subject field.\n\nHeader           : Header string for the message. %s is the action.\n                   Max length = 1024.\n\nAction_Award     : Actionstring for awarded files.\n                   Max length = 30.\n\nAction_Comment   : Actionstring for commented files.\n                   Max length = 30.\n\nAction_Create    : Actionstring for created files.\n                   Max length = 30.\n\nAction_Deduct    : Actionstring for deducted credits.\n                   Max length = 30.\n\nAction_Edit      : Actionstring for edited file comments.\n                   Max length = 30.\n\nAction_Expell    : Actionstring for expelled files.\n                   Max length = 30.\n\nAction_Free      : Actionstring for files made freedownloadable.\n                   Max length = 30.\n\nAction_Move      : Actionstring for for moved files.\n                   Max length = 30.\n\nAction_Resurrect : Actionstring for resurrected files.\n                   Max length = 30.\n\nAction_Return    : Actionstring for returned credits.\n                   Max length = 30.\n\nFiles            : String used for each file. max length = 256\n                 : Valid format codes are:                   length\n                 : %FN = FileName                             (12)\n                 : %FS = FileSize                             ( 7)\n                 : %FC = FileComment                          (??)\n                 : %SC = SizeComment                          (10)\n                 : %TI = Times awarded or deducted            ( 3)\n                 : %TO = Total bytes (= FileSize * Times)     (10)\n                 : %BT = Byte Type (= "u/l" or "d/l")         ( 3)\n                 : %AC = Action (= "given" or "taken")        ( 5)\n\nFiles_NoTotal    : String used for each file. max length = 256\n                 : This string is used when no user credits are added or\n                 : deducted. Valid format codes are:\n                 : %FN,%FS,%FC,%SC are allowed\n\nResult           : String used to terminate the message.\n                 : Max length = 1024.\n                 : valid format codes are:                   length\n                 : %PB = Previous bytes                       (10)\n                 : %PF = Previous files                       ( 5)\n                 : %CB = Current bytes                        (10)\n                 : %CF = Current files                        ( 5)\n                 : %TB = Total bytes                          (10)\n                 : %TF = Total files                          ( 5)\n                 : %TY = Type (= "uploaded" or "downloaded")  (10)\n                 : %BT = Byte Type (= "u/l" or "d/l")         ( 3)\n                 : %AC = Action (= "given" or "taken")        ( 5)\n\nResult_NoTotal   : String used to terminate the message.\n                 : This string is used when no user credits are added or\n                 : deducted. No format codes are allowed!\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE exsg_4_5 "Configuring - Misc"\n@TOC exsg_4\n\nKeepLog             : This option enables the Ex!_Log in each conference\n                    : directory. In this log all actions performed in\n                    : Exorcist! will be noted.\n                    : Valid are "YES" and "NO".\n\nKeepStats           : This option enables the stats file for statistics\n                    : about how often users were expelled, awarded\n                    : or deducted.\n                    : The format of the stats file is public, so that\n                    : other utilities can make use of it.\n                    : The format is for each user is:\n                    :\n                    : struct  Ex_Stats\n                    :   {\n                    :   ULONG Award_Bytes;\n                    :   ULONG Deduct_Bytes;\n                    :   ULONG Expell_Bytes;\n                    :   UWORD Award_Files;\n                    :   UWORD Deduct_Files;\n                    :   UWORD Expell_Files;\n                    :   };\n                    :\n                    : The file consist of a number of these structures\n                    : packed back to back. Accessing of a certain user\n                    : means:\n                    : Search(File,(UserSlot-1)*sizeof(struct Ex_Stats),\n                    :        OFFSET_BEGINNING);\n\nIndividualReturning : This option allows individual returning of credits\n                    : to downloaders.\n                    : "YES" means that individual returning will always be on.\n                    : "NO"  means that individual returning is not possible.\n                    : "ASK" lets the user decide which option to use.\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE exsg_4_6 "Configuring - Paths"\n@TOC exsg_4\n\nAcp       : Path to acp.info. Must end with '':'' or ''/'' (for /X v3.xx only)\n\nUserData  : Path to user.data. Must include the filename (for /X v2.3x only)\n\nStats     : Path to file containing the Exorcist! stats. Make sure\n          : that this file is also accessible for other utils.\n          : Must include the filename.\n\nResurrect : Path to directory where expelled files will go.\n          : Must end with '':'' or ''/''.\n          : NOTE: if you remove this entry, Resurrect will be disabled,\n          :       and all files you expell are deleted instead of moved!\n\nAwardCmt  : Path to file containing standard award comments.\n          : Must include the filename.\n\nDeductCmt : Path to file containing standard deduct comments.\n          : Must include the filename.\n\nExpellCmt : Path to file containing standard expell comments.\n          : Must include the filename.\n\nLogosCmt  : Path to file containing standard logos.\n          : Must include the filename.\n\nSizeCmt   : Path to file containing standard size comments.\n          : Must include the filename.\n\nThe format of the standard comment files is as follows:\n\nEach line means a standard commentline.\nIf a line starts with '';'' then that line is considered to be a commentline.\nIf a line starts with ''@'' then that line is considered to be an ID-line.\nThis ID will be used in the editor to select the commentline that follows\nthe ID line.\nIf a line ends with ''@'' then this line will be linked with the next\nline into a multi-line standard comment.\n\nexample:\n\n;This is a commentline\nstandard comment #1\n\@ID\nstandard comment #2a@\nstandard comment #2b\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE exsg_5 "Exorcist! v3.0 - Access for /X v3.xx"\n\nExorcist! for /X v3.xx makes use of the standard access system as\ndescribed in the /X docs. The new tooltypes that can be added are:\n\n  - EX!.AWARD     : Let the user award credits to other users\n  - EX!.COMMENT   : Let the user comment files\n  - EX!.DEDUCT    : Let the user deduct credits from other users\n  - EX!.EDITCMT   : Let the user edit file comments\n  - EX!.EXPELL    : Let the user expell files\n  - EX!.FREE      : Let the user make files free download\n  - EX!.MOVEFILE  : Let the user do cross conference file moving\n  - EX!.RESURRECT : Let the user resurrect files\n  - EX!.ANONYMOUS : Let the user perform his actions anonymously\n  - EX!.WILDCARD  : Let the user use wildcards when selecting files\n\nJust add these to the .info for a level or a single person, so that\nExorcist! can determine which users have access.\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n\n@NODE exsg_6 "Exorcist! v3.0 - Contacting the authors"\n\nYou can contact us (CFi and B/\Zz) at:\n\n     Write to:\n     P.O. Box 11023\n     7502 LA ENSCHEDE\n     HOLLAND\n\n     Or Call These Boards:\n     DøøMBaSe    (SkidRow)\n       +31-(0)10-2731172\n     ThE sCORE   (SkidRow)\n       +31-0575-044-471\n\n     /X-NetMail:\n     Eclipse DHQ@NL0002\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE exsg_7 "Exorcist! v3.0 - Disclaimer"\n\nDisclaimer:\n\nUse this software at your own risk. The authors will not be liable for\nany damage arising from the failure of this program to perform as described,\nor any destruction of other programs or data residing on a system\nattempting to run the program. While no damaging errors are known, the\nuser of this program uses it at his or her own risk.\nYou may spread the original, unchanged archive for non-commercial purposes.\nPD companies may not spread this product for anything more than the actual\ncopying costs, and only with written permission of one of the authors.\n\nThis program is GiftWare!\nIf you use this program often, a gift would be appreciated by the @{"authors" link exsg_6}!\n\n@ENDNODE\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',91132,4,0,NULL,NULL,'ex2_3_18','scan',1780048504);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ex3_3_18','EX3_3_18.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/EX3_3_18.LHA','Ex!_Task_3_000','XIM','Ex!_CreateSLog',NULL,NULL,'EX3','|      Exorcist! v3.0  PUBLIC BETA 18      | |             /X v3.xx version             | +------------------------------------------+',replace('+------------------------------------------+\n|      Exorcist! v3.0  PUBLIC BETA 18      |\n|             /X v3.xx version             |\n+------------------------------------------+\n««« FEEL THE POWER OF THIS AWESOME NUKER »»»\n','\n',char(10)),'Ex!_Sysop.guide',replace('@DATABASE "Ex!_Sysop.guide"\n\n@NODE Main "Exorcist! v3.0 - ©1993-1994 SkidRow"\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n                                 EXORCIST!\n                             The File Expeller\n                                   v3.0\n\n                   (c) 1993-1994  CFi & B/\Zz of SkidRow\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n	Table of contents:\n\n	@{" Preface     " link exsg_1} Introduction to Exorcist!\n	@{" Changes     " link exsg_2} Changes in v3.0 compared to v2.1\n	@{" Installing  " link exsg_3} How to get Exorcist! working on your system\n	@{" Configuring " link exsg_4} How to configure Exorcist! to your wishes\n	@{" Access/     " link exsg_5} How to give access to Exorcist! for /X v3.xx\n	@{" Contact     " link exsg_6} How to contact the authors\n	@{" Disclaimer  " link exsg_7} Read this!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE exsg_1 "Exorcist! v3.0 - Preface"\n\nEverybody who owns or maintains a BBS, knows that not all uploads are of\nsimilar nature. Sometimes users upload things that have already been\nuploaded. And sometimes users upload something of such value that he ought\nto get more than his standard ratio for it. Also it would be nice to make\nfiles free-download without much fuss. To solve all these problems and more,\nwe made Exorcist!\n\nExorcist! is a /X utility that gives you the ability to perform certain\noperations on uploaded files. Although the most of the operations Exorcist!\ncan perform are also available in other programs (eg NosNUKE or BossNUKE),\nExorcist! combines a high speed with a greatly enhanced functionality. \n\nAlthough getting the grips with Exorcist! will probably not be as easy as\nwith simpler utilities like NosNUKE or BossNUKE, its benefits will surely\nbe worth the effort.\n\nExorcist! has been written to finally get a fast and reliable program to\ndo all those things essential for running a good BBS, but which were\nformerly only possible with slow and non friendly programs. We hope you\nenjoy using Exorcist!!\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE exsg_2 "Exorcist! v3.0 - Changes"\n\nThe new version 3.0 has several new major options compared to v2.1:\n\n- @{"Background task" link exsg_3_2}   : A background task was added to Exorcist!, to\n                      provide the service of performing all actions\n                      asked for, whether the resources for that action\n                      are available at that moment or not.\n- @{"Speedlog" link exsg_3_1}          : Exorcist! uses a fast uploader search algorithm \n                      using a special log. Under normal conditions\n                      uploaders will be found within 0.1 secs.\n- Comment editor    : Exorcist! now uses a full screen editor to add or\n                      edit comments in the filedir.\n- Edit file comment : Exorcist! gives you the possibility to edit the \n                      filecomments in the filedir.\n- Inter-conf moving : Exorcist! can move files (including comments) from\n                      one conference to another.\n- Fully configurable: Exorcist! comments and messages can be COMPLETELY edited \n                      to your wishes.\n- ASCII std comments: Exorcist! can read standard ascii files to use as default\n                      standard comments.\n- Improved filecmt  : Exorcist! now has the ability to handle any filedir\n                      utilities additions. Lines upto 160 chars and/or\n                      lines containing ANSI codes will be handled\n                      the right way.\n\nOther options are improved and bugfixed:\n\n- Exorcist! can now find uploaders who logged in the day before 0:00 and\n  uploaded their files after 0:00.\n- Major crash bug when searching uploaders and comments has been fixed.\n- Award command has been split in the award and deduct commands.\n- several small bugs were removed.\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE exsg_3 "Exorcist! v3.0 - Installing"\nHow to install Exorcist!:\n\nExorcist! uses a CBM Installer compatible install script.\nTo install Exorcist! just doubleclick the Install_Ex! icon in the\ndirectory to which Exorcist! was extracted.\n\nDuring the installation process some questions are asked:\n\n  - Select BBS directory          \n      Here you must select the directory in which your bbs is located.\n\n  - Select directory for Exorcist!\n      Here you must select an existing directory. Exorcist! will be\n      installed into this directory.\n\n  - Do you want to add Exorcist! to ... \n      If you select yes here, an entry will be added to the bbs.cmd file\n      or the BBSCmd dir, so that Exorcist! can be started from /X. It\n      is adviced to keep the access level as low as possible, since there\n      are better ways to give access to Exorcist!\n\n  - Do you want to install the @{"speedlog" link exsg_3_1}?\n      If you select yes here, the speedlog will be installed on your system.\n      The speedlog will be installed as the FRONTEND door, if your system\n      already contains a FRONTEND door, then this door should be renamed\n      to FRONTEND2, so that the speedlog door can automatically start it.\n\n  - Install the @{"background task" link exsg_3_2} permanently?\n      If you want to use the speedlog, you MUST install the background task\n      permanently. Otherwise you have the choice of installing the\n      background permanently, or having Exorcist! start the background task\n      at each use. Installing the background task permanently has the\n      advantage that Exorcist! will startup much faster!\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE exsg_3_1 "What is the speedlog?"\n\nThe speedlog is a new feature for this release, and has been added to\nExorcist! to improve the search speed for uploaders and downloaders\neven more. The only way to use speedlog is to install it via the\ninstaller script of Exorcist!.\n\nThe speedlog consists of a file called ''Ex!_SpeedLog'' and a door called\n''Ex!_UpdateSLog.x'' both are in the directory where Exorcist! is located.\nThe Ex!_UpdateSLog.x door is automaticaly executed when a user logs in,\nand will transparently update the speedlog, without the online user\nnoticing anything.\n\nThe speedlog will be kept in RAM during the time that Ex!_Task is active,\nso that the maximum search speed can be obtained. The one minor\ndisadvantage of speedlog is that you will have to spend 16KB memory to\nkeep the speedlog in memory.\n\nA speed indication: on a system with a normal taskload, Exorcist! will\nbe able to find uploaders/downloaders within 0.1 sec out of the speedlog.\n\nNOTE for users of speedlog: \n  Due to the fact that /X will not execute the FRONTEND door when\n  a sysop login (F1) is performed, you may not perform a sysop login\n  on any node where uploads and/or downloads take place. It is adviced\n  the use a special private sysop node for this, and remember that on\n  this node no uploading or downloading may take place.\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE exsg_3_2 "What is the background task?"\n\nThe background task was added to Exorcist! because in previous releases\nof Exorcist! problems with updating user records and mailheaders appeared.\n\nTo get rid of these problems the background task was introduced. The\nbackground task is a small program that runs at priority 0, so that it will\nnot take away any processor time from /X.\n\nWhen there is any time left on the system, and the needed resources are\navailable, the background task will perform all changes that are needed due\nto actions performed in Exorcist! The one huge advantage over previous\nversions of Exorcist! is the fact that ANY action you specify will ALWAYS\nbe performed!\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE exsg_4 "Exorcist! v3.0 - Configuring"\n\nStarting with this revision, Exorcist! will use the ini.library for\nprocessing its configuration file called ''Exorcist!.ini''. Due to a bug\nin ini.library the Exorcist!.ini file must exist in the same directory\nas Exorcist!, or else an endless loop will occur.\n\nThe format of the Exorcist!.ini file is as followed. The file is a normal\nASCII file, and the only demand is that the file starts with '';INI''.\n\nFurthermore the file consist of sections, which start which the section\nname between [ ] brackets (eg. [Paths]). Each section can contain multiple\nvariables, of which none is needed, Exorcist! will run OK, even if you have\na completely empty Exorcist!.ini file.\n\nEach variable is placed on one line. There cannot be more than one variable\non a line! The format for the variable line is <varname>=<value>, where you\nmay not place white spaces between the <varname> and the ''='', or between the\n''='' and the <value>.\n\nIf a line starts with '';'' or ''*'' it is considered a commentline. \nif you use a '';'' on a normal line, then the rest of that line is considered\nto be a comment. Although it is not needed, it is best to place the <value>\ninbetween ''"'' signs, if it is a string, to make sure that no unwanted spaces\nare included in the <value> string.\n\nExample:\n\n[Paths]\nStats="BBS:Ex!_Stats"                 ;this is the path to the stats file\n\n\n	Possible Sections:\n\n	@{"[ActionStrings]" link exsg_4_1} The action strings placed in the filedir\n	@{"[Comments]     " link exsg_4_2} Options for added commentlines\n	@{"[Levels]       " link exsg_4_3} Access levels for actions (for /X v2.3x only)\n	@{"[Messages]     " link exsg_4_4} Options and layout for messages send\n	@{"[Misc]         " link exsg_4_5} Miscellaneous options\n	@{"[Paths]        " link exsg_4_6} Paths to important files\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE exsg_4_1 "Configuring - ActionStrings"\n@TOC exsg_4\n\nPossible variables are:\n\nAward_L     : This string defines the action string for awarding when using\n              large comments. use %d for times credits.\n\nDeduct_L    : This string defines the action string for deducting when using\n              large comments. use %d for times credits.\n\nExpell_L    : This string defines the action string for expelling when using\n              large comments. use %d for times credits.\n\nFree_L      : This string defines the action string used when a file is made\n              free downloadable using large comments.\n\nResurrect_L : This string defines the action string used when a file is\n              resurrected using large comments.\n\n\nFree_S      : This string defines the action string used when a file is made\n              free downloadable using small comments. (max 14 chars)\n\nResurrect_S : This string defines the action string used when a file is\n              resurrected using small comments. (max 14 chars)\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE exsg_4_2 "Configuring - Comments"\n@TOC exsg_4\n\nLineStart   : This is the string that is placed at the beginning of each\n              Exorcist! commentline to identify it as an Exorcist! comment\n              line. You may NOT use an empty string here!\n\nLineEnd     : This is the string that is placed at the end of each\n              Exorcist! commentline to identify it as an Exorcist! comment\n              line. You may NOT use an empty string here!\n\nSmallCmt    : This specifies if smallcomments may be used.\n              specify "YES" if all added comments should be small comments.\n              specify "NO"  if all added comments should be large comments.\n              specify "ASK" if you want to let the user choose.\n\nStripCmt    : This specifies if Exorcist! commentlines must be removed when\n              resurrecting files. Specify YES or NO. Note that this option\n              will not work when you want to remove commentlines which have\n              other LineEnds than the current LineEnd.\n\nMaxCmtLines : This specifies the maximum number of Exorcist! commentlines\n              that may be added. 0 to 8 are valid.\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE exsg_4_3 "Configuring - Levels"\n@TOC exsg_4\n\nAward     : This specifies the level needed to award files.\n            Valid range = 0-255.\n\nComment   : This specifies the level needed to comment files.\n            Valid range = 0-255.\n\nDeduct    : This specifies the level needed to deduct files.\n            Valid range = 0-255.\n\nEditCmt   : This specifies the level needed to edit filecomments.\n            Valid range = 0-255.\n\nExpell    : This specifies the level needed to expell files.\n            Valid range = 0-255.\n\nFree      : This specifies the level needed to make files freedownload.\n            Valid range = 0-255.\n\nMoveFiles : This specifies the level needed to use the file mover.\n            Valid range = 0-255.\n\nResurrect : This specifies the level needed to resurrect files.\n            Valid range = 0-255.\n\n\nAnonymous : This specifies the level needed to stay anonymous.\n            Valid range = 0-255.\n\nWildcard  : This specifies the level needed to use wildcard.\n            Valid range = 0-255.\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE exsg_4_4 "Configuring - Messages"\n@TOC exsg_4\n\nUploader         : Send a message to the uploader(s) of the file(s).\n                   Valid are "YES", "NO" and "ASK".\n\nDownloader       : Send a message to the downloader(s) of a file.\n                   Valid are "YES", "NO" and "ASK".\n\nSysop            : Send a duplicate of each message to the sysop.\n                   Valid are "YES" and "NO". \n\nPublic           : Make the messages that are sent public.\n                   Valid are "YES" and "NO". \n\n\nAnonymous        : String placed in the sender field when the user wants\n                   to remain anonymous.\n\nSubject          : String placed in the subject field.\n\nHeader           : Header string for the message. %s is the action.\n                   Max length = 1024.\n\nAction_Award     : Actionstring for awarded files.\n                   Max length = 30.\n\nAction_Comment   : Actionstring for commented files.\n                   Max length = 30.\n\nAction_Create    : Actionstring for created files.\n                   Max length = 30.\n\nAction_Deduct    : Actionstring for deducted credits.\n                   Max length = 30.\n\nAction_Edit      : Actionstring for edited file comments.\n                   Max length = 30.\n\nAction_Expell    : Actionstring for expelled files.\n                   Max length = 30.\n\nAction_Free      : Actionstring for files made freedownloadable.\n                   Max length = 30.\n\nAction_Move      : Actionstring for for moved files.\n                   Max length = 30.\n\nAction_Resurrect : Actionstring for resurrected files.\n                   Max length = 30.\n\nAction_Return    : Actionstring for returned credits.\n                   Max length = 30.\n\nFiles            : String used for each file. max length = 256\n                 : Valid format codes are:                   length\n                 : %FN = FileName                             (12)\n                 : %FS = FileSize                             ( 7)\n                 : %FC = FileComment                          (??)\n                 : %SC = SizeComment                          (10)\n                 : %TI = Times awarded or deducted            ( 3)\n                 : %TO = Total bytes (= FileSize * Times)     (10)\n                 : %BT = Byte Type (= "u/l" or "d/l")         ( 3)\n                 : %AC = Action (= "given" or "taken")        ( 5)\n\nFiles_NoTotal    : String used for each file. max length = 256\n                 : This string is used when no user credits are added or\n                 : deducted. Valid format codes are:\n                 : %FN,%FS,%FC,%SC are allowed\n\nResult           : String used to terminate the message.\n                 : Max length = 1024.\n                 : valid format codes are:                   length\n                 : %PB = Previous bytes                       (10)\n                 : %PF = Previous files                       ( 5)\n                 : %CB = Current bytes                        (10)\n                 : %CF = Current files                        ( 5)\n                 : %TB = Total bytes                          (10)\n                 : %TF = Total files                          ( 5)\n                 : %TY = Type (= "uploaded" or "downloaded")  (10)\n                 : %BT = Byte Type (= "u/l" or "d/l")         ( 3)\n                 : %AC = Action (= "given" or "taken")        ( 5)\n\nResult_NoTotal   : String used to terminate the message.\n                 : This string is used when no user credits are added or\n                 : deducted. No format codes are allowed!\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE exsg_4_5 "Configuring - Misc"\n@TOC exsg_4\n\nKeepLog             : This option enables the Ex!_Log in each conference\n                    : directory. In this log all actions performed in\n                    : Exorcist! will be noted.\n                    : Valid are "YES" and "NO".\n\nKeepStats           : This option enables the stats file for statistics\n                    : about how often users were expelled, awarded\n                    : or deducted.\n                    : The format of the stats file is public, so that\n                    : other utilities can make use of it.\n                    : The format is for each user is:\n                    :\n                    : struct  Ex_Stats\n                    :   {\n                    :   ULONG Award_Bytes;\n                    :   ULONG Deduct_Bytes;\n                    :   ULONG Expell_Bytes;\n                    :   UWORD Award_Files;\n                    :   UWORD Deduct_Files;\n                    :   UWORD Expell_Files;\n                    :   };\n                    :\n                    : The file consist of a number of these structures\n                    : packed back to back. Accessing of a certain user\n                    : means:\n                    : Search(File,(UserSlot-1)*sizeof(struct Ex_Stats),\n                    :        OFFSET_BEGINNING);\n\nIndividualReturning : This option allows individual returning of credits\n                    : to downloaders.\n                    : "YES" means that individual returning will always be on.\n                    : "NO"  means that individual returning is not possible.\n                    : "ASK" lets the user decide which option to use.\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE exsg_4_6 "Configuring - Paths"\n@TOC exsg_4\n\nAcp       : Path to acp.info. Must end with '':'' or ''/'' (for /X v3.xx only)\n\nUserData  : Path to user.data. Must include the filename (for /X v2.3x only)\n\nStats     : Path to file containing the Exorcist! stats. Make sure\n          : that this file is also accessible for other utils.\n          : Must include the filename.\n\nResurrect : Path to directory where expelled files will go.\n          : Must end with '':'' or ''/''.\n          : NOTE: if you remove this entry, Resurrect will be disabled,\n          :       and all files you expell are deleted instead of moved!\n\nAwardCmt  : Path to file containing standard award comments.\n          : Must include the filename.\n\nDeductCmt : Path to file containing standard deduct comments.\n          : Must include the filename.\n\nExpellCmt : Path to file containing standard expell comments.\n          : Must include the filename.\n\nLogosCmt  : Path to file containing standard logos.\n          : Must include the filename.\n\nSizeCmt   : Path to file containing standard size comments.\n          : Must include the filename.\n\nThe format of the standard comment files is as follows:\n\nEach line means a standard commentline.\nIf a line starts with '';'' then that line is considered to be a commentline.\nIf a line starts with ''@'' then that line is considered to be an ID-line.\nThis ID will be used in the editor to select the commentline that follows\nthe ID line.\nIf a line ends with ''@'' then this line will be linked with the next\nline into a multi-line standard comment.\n\nexample:\n\n;This is a commentline\nstandard comment #1\n\@ID\nstandard comment #2a@\nstandard comment #2b\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE exsg_5 "Exorcist! v3.0 - Access for /X v3.xx"\n\nExorcist! for /X v3.xx makes use of the standard access system as\ndescribed in the /X docs. The new tooltypes that can be added are:\n\n  - EX!.AWARD     : Let the user award credits to other users\n  - EX!.COMMENT   : Let the user comment files\n  - EX!.DEDUCT    : Let the user deduct credits from other users\n  - EX!.EDITCMT   : Let the user edit file comments\n  - EX!.EXPELL    : Let the user expell files\n  - EX!.FREE      : Let the user make files free download\n  - EX!.MOVEFILE  : Let the user do cross conference file moving\n  - EX!.RESURRECT : Let the user resurrect files\n  - EX!.ANONYMOUS : Let the user perform his actions anonymously\n  - EX!.WILDCARD  : Let the user use wildcards when selecting files\n\nJust add these to the .info for a level or a single person, so that\nExorcist! can determine which users have access.\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n\n@NODE exsg_6 "Exorcist! v3.0 - Contacting the authors"\n\nYou can contact us (CFi and B/\\Zz) at:\n\n     Write to:\n     P.O. Box 11023\n     7502 LA ENSCHEDE\n     HOLLAND\n\n     Or Call These Boards:\n     DooMBaSe  : \n        +31-10-2731172\n     ThE sCORE :\n        +31-0575-044-471\n     /X-NetMail:\n     Eclipse DHQ@NL0002\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE exsg_7 "Exorcist! v3.0 - Disclaimer"\n\nDisclaimer:\n\nUse this software at your own risk. The authors will not be liable for\nany damage arising from the failure of this program to perform as described,\nor any destruction of other programs or data residing on a system\nattempting to run the program. While no damaging errors are known, the\nuser of this program uses it at his or her own risk.\nYou may spread the original, unchanged archive for non-commercial purposes.\nPD companies may not spread this product for anything more than the actual\ncopying costs, and only with written permission of one of the authors.\n\nThis program is GiftWare!\nIf you use this program often, a gift would be appreciated by the @{"authors" link exsg_6}!\n\n@ENDNODE\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',94236,4,0,NULL,NULL,'ex3_3_18','scan',1780048504);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('exc_af91','EXC-AF91.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/EXC-AF91.LHA',NULL,'XIM','aMPfIX',NULL,'sLAC/eXcelence','EXC',':  _ ________________|      /_ _________ : ¦ _ _______   /\     |     /______     / ¦ |   /    \/  /  \_       _/  /   \  __/  |',replace('      /X-iNNOVATiON    _______            ·\n :  _ ________________|      /_ _________ :\n ¦ _ _______   /\     |     /______     / ¦\n |   /    \/  /  \_       _/  /   \  __/  |\n | _/      \_/\_ /         \ /     \/  \_ |\n | \___________//     |_____\\__________/ |\n l_____________/______|AdN________________|\n         ·pRESENTS· ·yOU· ·tODAY·\n      aMPfIX 0.91 bY sLAC/eXcelence\n   nOW yOU cAN dISPLAY a hEADER uSING dA\n      lASTCALLER >aMPHETAMiN 2.0< !\n','\n',char(10)),'aMPfIX.doc',replace('\n\n                                ______\n                      .         \  _ /         .\n                  - --+----------\ //----------+-- -\n _            .-------'' _______   \/        _  `-------._______\n_\///\_______ |  ______|      /\_______     //\_______ |     _//\_______\n \///  _____/_|__\_    |    _//  _____/___. //  _____/_|___. |/   _____/_____.\n  /   ___/    :  /_    _     \_  \        l/   ___/        | /   ___/        |\n /____________:_//     |______/___________/________________|/_/\_____________|\n             _|\_______|-Mo!                       __  |     //  _____/_____\n  __/\__     \|_                                  /\_\ l____/    \          |\n  \ QQ /      \/                                  \/_/ |aC!/_/\_____________|\n  /_\/_\      | \       eXCELENCE - /X-iNNOVATiON      |    //  _____/_____.\n    \/        | \\                                 _   |   /   ___/        |\n          - --+------------------------------------\/--''  /________________|\n              ·\n\n\n                       E·X·P·R·E·S·S · D·E·S·I·G·N                                                     :\n\n                                 PRESENTS\n\n               aMPfIX 0.91 coded by sLAC/·e÷X÷C÷E÷L÷E÷N÷C÷e·\n\n  \n\n\nWHAT''S THE USE OF THIS TOOL ?\n-----------------------------\n\n        this tool makes it possible to use a >LASTCALLER< ansi-header\n        with the lascaller-util >AMFETAMIN 2.0< by The Silencer/TDS.\n        DO NOT USE IT WITH AN OTHER LASTCALLER UTIL !!!\n\nCONTENTS OF THIS ARCHIVE:\n-------------------------\n  \n        aMPfIX                      1132\n        aMPfIX.020+                 1132\n        aMPfIX.doc                  2757\n        EXAMPLE.IFF                28264\n        SOURCE.EXE                 15912   (from where it comes)\n        \nHOW TO INTALL:\n--------------\n\n        just copy the >aMPfIX< in your BBS:UTILS/ direktory and edit\n        your logoff-batch file ...\n\n<---------------------------------- CUT ------------------------------->\n\n BBS:UTILS/aMPfIX <AMFETAMIN OUTPUT-FILE> <HEADER-FILE> <OUTPUT-FILE>\n\n<---------------------------------- CUT ------------------------------->\n\n        <AMFETAMIN OUTPUT-FILE>   the file AMFETAMIN placed in with\n                                  full path\n\n        <HEADER-FILE>             the file where your header placed\n                                  in with full path\n        \n 	<OUTPUT-FILE>             the path & filename where aMPfIX\n                                  should place the output\n\n\n\n...thats all dudez......wish you much phun with diz tool!\n\n\n\n\n\n\nGREETINGS:\n----------\n\n			sCANDIC/eXC lEADER\n 			mONTY/eXC^bP\n			mICK/eXC\n			mOGUE!/sCX^aC!\n			-sLIME/bP\n			MR.B!G/sCX\n			JOJO/sCX\n			mario/t.r.s.i.\n			dOg/afl\n			eCS/t.r.s.i.\n			Spellfire/t.r.s.i. cONSOLE\n			','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',42483,1,0,NULL,NULL,'exc_af91','scan',1780048504);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('exc_dox2','EXC_DOX2.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/EXC_DOX2.LHA','eXc_DOWN','XIM','___________          __ __',NULL,'sHadoW!','EXC','|  ___\____ |   _____|  |  |_____ |____  |  / |  |  __ |  |  |     | -----|   /  | /  |--| \___|>   <|  |__|-----',replace('      ___________          __ __\n     |  ___\____ |   _____|  |  |_____\n     |____  |  / |  |  __ |  |  |     |\n-----|   /  | /  |--| \___|>   <|  |__|-----\n-----|      |    |--|     |  |  |  |  |-----\n     |______|____|  |_____|__|__|_____|\n____________________________________________\n   eXc_dOWN v2.00 bY sHadoW!  [xIM dOOR]\n    fREE cONFIGURABLE wITH 32 fUNCTIONs\n¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n   eXclusiVe iS a sUBGROUP oF 5tH dYNASTY\n','\n',char(10)),'eXc_DOWN.guide',replace('@database eXc_dOWN Documentation\n\nCopyright ©1996 sTc\n\n@remark $VER: (September 29 1996, 15:00)\n@remark AmigaGuide database for the eXc_dOWN Documentation\n\n@node MAIN "eXc_dOWN Documentation"\n              __        __           __     _____          __\n   _______   /  |____  /  |      ___|  \   /  __/_   __   /  |___   _______\n  /  ____/_ /   |    \/   |____ /   |   \ _\____  \ /  \ /   |   \ /  ____/_\n /  ______/_\_      _/    |    /    |    /      \  /    /    |    /  ______/_\n/         /         /         /     |   /         /    /     |   /           \\n\_________\_____|   \_________\_________\_________\____\_________\___________/\n                |_____/[-S7E3L-]\n\n              > eXclusive is a sub-group of 5th Dynasty <\n       ._____.\n  __5TH|_    |    ._____. ___________ ________. _______ ___.           ._____.\n__\   __     |____|_    |_\   _    ___\____   |_\  ___/__  |___    ____|_    |\n\     \|    _/     /    |     /    \     _    |\_____   /  ___/___/     /    |\n \     \    \     /_    |____/    / \    \    |    /   /   \     \     /_    |\n  \__________\_____     |   /____/   \________|_______/|__________\_____     |\n                  |_____|pHS!                                          |_____|\n\n                                                     ... No Fear of Fun!\n\n       eXc_dOWN.Guide - Contents\n    ===============================\n\n    1) @{" Introduction " Link ChildDoc1}\n    2) @{" Requirements " Link ChildDoc2}\n    3) @{" Installation " Link ChildDoc3}\n    4) @{" Commands  " Link ChildDoc4}\n    5) @{" History " Link ChildDoc5}\n    6) @{" Greetings " Link ChildDoc6}\n    7) @{" How to contact 5D and eXc" Link ChildDoc7}\n\n@endnode\n@node ChildDoc1 "Introduction"\n\n     eXc_dOWN - Introduction\n  =============================\n\n  eXc_dOWN is a replacement for the ''D''-command\n  of AmiExpress. It will show the status before download!\n\n@endnode\n@node ChildDoc2 "Requirements"\n\n     eXc_dOWN - Requirements\n  =============================\n\n  o  an Amiga (or compatible - DRACO)\n  o  an AmiExpress-compatible BBS-program\n\n@endnode\n@node ChildDoc3 "Installation"\n\n     eXc_dOWN - Installation (for AmiExpress)\n  ==============================================\n\n  Simply copy the directories in this archive into your bbs-\n  directory.\n\n@endnode\n@node ChildDoc4 "Commands"\n\n     eXc_dOWN dESIGN cOMMANDS\n  ==============================\n\n   Okay guys you have 32 information !\n   For every piece of information must be 20 chars reserved !\n   Look at the config !\n\n   01.  %UN  = USERNAME\n   02.  %UL  = USERLOCATION\n   03.  %UP  = USERPHONENUMBER\n   04.  %US  = USERSLOTNUMBER\n   05.  %UE  = USEREDITOR\n   06.  %LV  = ACCESLEVEL\n   07.  %CA  = CONFACCS\n   08.  %BN  = BBSNAME\n   09.  %SN  = SYSOPNAME\n   10.  %EV  = EXPRESS VERSION\n   11.  %AC  = CONFNAME\n   12.  %TL  = TIME TOTAL\n   13.  %TU  = TIME USED\n   14.  %TR  = TIME LIMIT\n   15.  %LO  = LAST ON\n   16.  %BU  = BYTES UPLOAD\n   17.  %BD  = BYTES DOWNLOAD\n   18.  %FU  = FILES UPLOAD\n   19.  %FD  = FILES DOWNLOAD\n   20.  %RA  = RATIO\n   21.  %RT  = RATIOTYPE\n   22.  %MP  = MESSAGEPOSTED\n   23.  %XF  = XFERPROTOCOL\n   24.  %SA  = SYSOPAVAIL\n   25.  %DB  = DAILYBYTES\n   26.  %XM  = EXPERTMODE\n   27.  %TC  = TIMESCALLED\n   28.  %LI  = LINES\n   29.  %DE  = NODE DEVICE\n   30.  %OB  = TAMPON ohhh no ONLINE BAUD\n   31.  %OR  = ONLINE BAUDRATE\n   32.  %CP  = UP/DOWN CPS\n\n@endnode\n@node ChildDoc5 "History"\n\n     eXc_dOWN - History\n  ========================\n\n  v1.00 Never released version - for eXc only !!\n  v2.00 This version\n\n@endnode\n@node ChildDoc6 "Greetings"\n\n  Greetings\n  =========\n\n  aIRWORX      tHX  fOR tESTING mY fIRST fAME tOOLS!\n  rYAN         cOOL tRADING\n  sTEEL        bRING mORE gUYS !\n  sTc          tHANKS fOR sOME hELP\n  sNOW         tHANKS fOR bETA tESTING\n  sERAPH       tHANKS fOR cOOL iDEAS\n  [tHUNDER]    gREETS uNKNOWN\n  lF           cHANGE tO fAME\n  zANOK        cOOL bBS\n  sHADOWER     iT`S fOR yOU (dISSY????)\n  eNZO         cALL yA sOON\n  rADIOSITY    gREETS fROM sNoW: uSE iT\n  sTRIDER      cOOL bBS sYTEM bUT iMPLEMENT mORE lIKE pROTOCOLS\n  dR dRE!      cOOL dOORS bUT wHY COMMERCIALIZE tHE sCENE ?\n  sIEGEL       tHE sAME tO yOU !!\n\n@endnode\n@node ChildDoc7 "How to contact 5D and eXc"\n\n  You can write a message to ''sHadoW!'' at the following boards:\n\n  o aNTARCTICA            5D lEADING HQ\n  o dIGITAL sUICIDE       5D wHQ\n  o tERMINAL fUCKUP!      5D gHQ\n  o oNE eIGHT sEVEN       5D dHQ\n  o sKY tOWER             5D dKHQ\n  o nEEDFUL tHINGS        5D uSHQ\n  o aNOTHER uNIVERSE      5D uSHQ\n  o Death Row\n  o wASTED lANDS\n  o fLYING dRAGON\n  o tRADERS pARADISE\n\n  ... and several more\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,16076,2,0,NULL,NULL,'exc_dox2_exc_down','scan',1780048504);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('exc_wal1','EXC_WAL1.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/EXC_WAL1.LHA','eXc_WALL','XIM','eXc_WALL',NULL,'wAsI^qUASI','EXC','__)      ¬\__)  \   ¬\__)       ¬\ \    \_____\     \    \    \______\ \     __\__\_____\   /\    \_______',replace('   ________   ________   _________\n __)      ¬\__)  \   ¬\__)       ¬\\n \    \_____\     \    \    \______\\n  \     __\__\_____\   /\    \_______\n  s\    \     \     \¯¯¯¯\    \     ¬\\n   H\    \     \     \    \    \      \\n    d\    \     \     \    \    \      \\n     !\_________/\_____\___/\__________/\n____________________________________________\n^ eXc-wAlL by wAsI^qUASI eXclusivE /X dEv. ^\n¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n[=cHECKED!=========================pASSED!=]\n','\n',char(10)),'eXc_WALL.doc',replace('\n                              eXc_WALL\n                            by wASI^QUASi\n\n                    <o> Produced by Exclusive <o>\n\nJust this little piece of information: eXc_WALL is a real wall.\nThat means you can type char-by-char whereever on the wall where\nyou want. Just this little handycap: you''ve a limit of 104 chars.\nThe decreasing amount of chars will be shown by a decreasing\nnumber of blocks that will disappear every 4 chars.\nTo make your text good looking you can adjust the writing color\nby choosing one of seven colors. Another helpy point is the\nreal-time clock in the upper right corner that will update every\nsecond.\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',9719,5,0,NULL,NULL,'exc_wal1','scan',1780048504);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('exc_wal2','EXC_WAL2.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/EXC_WAL2.LHA','eXc_WALL','XIM','eXc_WALL',NULL,'wAsI^qUASI','EXC','__)      ¬\__)  \   ¬\__)       ¬\  /X-fAME \    \_____\     \    \    \______\  DESIGN \     __\__\_____\   /\    \_______',replace('   ________   ________   _________\n __)      ¬\__)  \   ¬\__)       ¬\  /X-fAME\n \    \_____\     \    \    \______\  DESIGN\n  \     __\__\_____\   /\    \_______\n  s\    \     \     \¯¯¯¯\    \     ¬\\n   H\    \     \     \    \    \      \\n    d\    \     \     \    \    \      \\n     !\_________/\_____\___/\__________/\n____________________________________________\n      ^ eXc-wAlL 1.01 by wAsI^qUASI ^\n¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n[========================( fLYING DRAGN )==]\n','\n',char(10)),'eXc_WALL.doc',replace('\n                              eXc_WALL\n                            by wASI^QUASi\n\n                    <o> Produced by Exclusive <o>\n\nJust this little piece of information: eXc_WALL is a real wall.\nThat means you can type char-by-char whereever on the wall where\nyou want. Just this little handycap: you''ve a limit of 104 chars.\nThe decreasing amount of chars will be shown by a decreasing\nnumber of blocks that will disappear every 4 chars.\nTo make your text good looking you can adjust the writing color\nby choosing one of seven colors. Another helpy point is the\nreal-time clock in the upper right corner that will update every\nsecond.\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',13053,3,0,NULL,NULL,'exc_wal1','scan',1780048504);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('exe_phr','EXE&PHR.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/EXE&PHR.LHA','CONFIG','XIM','CONFIG',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,replace('FAIRLIGHT PRESENTS: R.R.R.MULTI TOOL FOR /X\n','\n',char(10)),'reference-board.txt',replace(replace('              W h e r e   t h e   w a r e z   c o m e   f r o m\r\n                                               __                /\_____:\r\n__/\__________________________________________|  \______________/  \    |__\r\n\_   ___________  _______ ________  \__   ___ |   _______  _______  \_  l  \\r\n__\____  \    _l   \    |  \     |___/     |  !    \   _l   \   _| __/\____ \_\r\n\_____    \___\     \___|   \___ !   \__   |_____   \__\     \__\    \____   /\r\n -mNT\_____/---\_____/--l____/-\______/\   |----\____/--\_____/--\____/--\__/\r\n                                        \__|\r\n\r\n- -- --> F A i R L i G H T   S W E D i S H   H E A D Q U A R T E R S <-- -- -\r\n\r\n           reference-board is back 2017 after more than 20 years in coma!\r\n\r\n                        Running on AmiExpress TelNet\r\n\r\n                    Connect to: reference-board.zapto.org:1541\r\n\r\n                    or: www.brysk.se/reference-board/index.htm\r\n               \n              UPLOAD DATE: 01-04-18  TIME: 19:35:34  ON NODE: 0\n','\r',char(13)),'\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',24571,1,0,NULL,NULL,'exe_phr','scan',1780048504);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('explorer','EXPLORER.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/EXPLORER.LHA','ExPlOrEr','XIM','ExPlOrEr',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Känner igen massor av olika filer',replace('Kollar vad det är för sortes fil\nKänner igen massor av olika filer\n','\n',char(10)),'ReAdMe.gUiDe',replace('@database "Explorer.Guide"\n\n; Detta Documet Får Ej Ändras om du ändrar det i alla fall\n; så kommer du att bli bommbad med Bommber Virus (Ha Ha Ha!!) Ehh?\n\n@node main "Explorer 0.1"\n\n	                    Explorer v0.1\n\nDetta är en Lamer Version av Explorer. Tycker du att du behöver något \nsånt här program så sicka 50 Kr till @{"Peter Lindberg" Link addr} \nså får du den registrerade versionen.\nEller Håll utkick efter Vers 1.0\n\nReg Vers\n	* Känner igen 500 filer till\n	* Kann Packa up filer\n	* Kann Rippa saker ut ur filer du just scanat (Music/Samplingar/Bild)\n	* 60% till 70% snabbare\n	* Kan scana via devices (Plocka ut filer ur Icke-Dos-Diskar)\n\nNote: Denna version är bara en test version \n      nästa version kommer (helt klart) att vara MYCKET bättre\n						--Watch Out--\n\n@{"Wath Is This?" Link ab}\n@{"Vilken knapp får jag inte trycka på" Link us}\n@endnode\n\n@Node ab\n\n\nDetta är ett program som Ska känna igen\nCa \n   380 Fil Exsistioner\n   180 Filer\n+  545 Banners\n-------\n  1105 Filer\n\nDetta dock bara den oregistrerade version\nDen reistrerade versionen känner igen dubbelt så mycket\n\nOm inte programet funkar som det borde så ska du veta att det\nhar bara testats på min A1200 68030/28 Mhz 10 Meg Ram/80 Meg Hd\n\n@{"Usage" Link us}\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node addr\n----------- Adresser ----------\n\nDet lättaste sättet att få kotakt med mig är Via -High Way- BBs\n\nOm det är något du vill fråga så lämmna ett medelande på\nDMZ BBs/-High Way- BBs eller DaGcEnTRaL 9o²1o (code name Foxy)\n\n(jag har metdvetet låtit bli att skriva in min addres mga att \njag är nästan aldrig hemma (Studerar på dagarna party på helgerna))\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node us\n\nTangenter:\n<F1>     On/Off Prefix scan\n<F2>     On/Off File scan\n<F3>     On/Off Log File (Ram:Logfile)\n<F4>     On/Off Banner Scan (Banner=Reklam)\n<Space>  Om du vill scana en hel låda\n<Return> Om du vill bara scana EN fil\n<Shift>  Om du vill pausa En Låd-Scaning\n<Amiga>+<A>=Swap Screens\n\nTryck in <Shift> Tangenten vid start (När "Explorer" Skylten \nkommer up) så blir det en Hi-Laced Skärm!\n\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------\n* Om programet inte vill starta kolla att du har\n	1. Tillräklit med minne (500 Kb) Ledigt\n	2. "Data 7","Data 8","Data 9" Filerna I samma Låda-\n	   Och att programet är startat från den lådan\n\n* Om programet quitar mitt i en scan så är filen "uptagen"\n\n* Om det inte går att he på Banner scan så saknas filer\n"Banner" Ska vara i samma låda som Explorer\n------------------------------------------------------------\n\n@EndNode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',71946,6,0,NULL,NULL,'explorer','scan',1780048504);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ext_st1z','EXT-ST1Z.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/EXT-ST1Z.LHA','Random','XIM','Random',NULL,NULL,'EXT','÷ Sorry to those who dl the bugged version!÷ ÷ Will _NEVER_ happen again!               ÷',replace('÷ Ecsta-Stat Buggfixed version 1.0Z ÷\n÷ Sorry to those who dl the bugged version!÷\n÷ Will _NEVER_ happen again!               ÷\n','\n',char(10)),'Ecsta-Stat.GuiDe',replace('@database Ecsta-Stat.GuiDe\n@$VER: Ecsta-Stat v1.04m By Instant/Independant - Guide File\n@node MAIN "Ecsta-Stat v1.04m (c) 07/95 Instant/Independant"\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                                Ecsta-Stat\n\n                              Version: 1.04m\n                                    By\n                            Instant/Independant\n\n\n    DISCLAIMER: The Author Takes no responsibility for any damage this\n      may cause you, your family, your pets, your friends, your house\n    your neighbourhood, your machine, any inventory in your house, your\n          country, your state or anything else you may think of.\n\n  tO EnCourage further development of any ECSTA-TOOLS programme ($1), and\nthe development of ''UNPROFOR (Working Title) - The Strategy Game for Amiga'' ($5)\n     Please send the money to me, see CONTACTS for further information\n\n\n@endnode\n@node CONTENTS "Ecsta-Stat v1.04 (c) 07/95 Instant/Independant"\n                 Welcome to my First Ami Express Release!\n      This is a fast and featurefull STATUS programme, which replaces\n     the internal ''S'' command, and any other ''S'' command you may have!\n\n   Anyway: Press any of THEESE buttons to go to the corresponding page!\n\n                          @{" Installation " link "Install"}\n                          @{" Contact " link "Contact"}\n                          @{" History " link "history"}\n                          @{" Other " link "OTHER"}\n\n\n\n\nCopyright 19(c)95 Ecstatica BBS\n@endnode\n@node INSTALL "Installation Info for Ecsta-Stat v1.04 by Instant"\n                     How do you install this utility?\n                     ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                       UNARCHIVE ME-U.lha FROM BBS:\n         and everything will be placed where it should be placed!\n\n\n                  The Files that will be unarchived are:\n\n\n		Ecsta-Stat.rexx - Main Programme\n		Ecsta-Stat.Gui  - GUI\n		Cookies		- CookieFile\n		Random		- Randomize Programme\n\n             Theese files will be placed in a directory called\n                      ''DOORS:ECSTA-TOOLS/ECSTA-STAT/''\n\n\n           Also You Can Place ME in bbs:docs or the Above path.\n\n            To Add A Cookie or ten, just edit the COOKIE file!\n\n\n\nCopyright 19(c)95 Ecstatica BBS\n@endnode\n@node HISTORY "In 1963 JKF Was Shot, in 1988 The Berlin Wall Crumbled, in 1991 Saddam Got his Ass Kicked!, In 1995 Instant Released Ecsta Stat"\nHISTORY\n-------\nVersion 0.99 - Added Everything (NEVER RELEASED)\nVersion 1.00 - Added Ansi BackGround (UNRELEASED)\nVersion 1.01 - Added Cookie File (UNRELEASED)\nVersion 1.02 - Added Guide File (UNRELEASED)\nVersion 1.03 - Made Installation Script (UNRELEASED)\nVersion 1.04 - LHAed The Whole Thing and Sent it away for a beta release (Release #0.99)\nVersion 1.04m- Added ANSI and ASCII logo,Made Cookie Work (Release #1)\n\n@Endnode\n@node CONTACT "First you turn left at 1st, then proceed allong west avenue for 30 blocks, when you come to a roadsight turn left and then right"\nCONTACT\n-------\nTo Contact The Author For Registration, Flames,  or Fan-Mail :)\ndo any of the following\n---\n\nVia Internet\n	Email : [email removed]\n        WWW   : http://powertech.no/~terjeba/ - Leave a Message in the GUestbook\n	IRC   : #amiga, #amiga!, #warez, #compuwar\n\nVia Modem\n  	     Ecstatica : +474U2FINDOUT - The Home of Ecsta-Tools\n	Bumble Bee Land: +474U2FINDOUT - Name: Instant (NUP,SYSPW)\n	 Basic Instinct: +474U2FINDOUT - Name: Instant\n	        OutPost: +46CANTBEBOTHERED2TYPETHEMIN - Name: Instant\n\nVia snailMail\n		Terje Alexander Barth\n		Fredtunveien 18\n		1370 Asker\n		Norway\n\n- Please send $1 if you REALLY Like this programme and want me to further develop it :)\n- Please send $5 or more if you would like the Game ''UN - Conflict Jugoslavia''\n  to be furhter developed!\n@ENDNODE\n@node OTHER\n\n             Other Usefull utilities to be released by me are\n             ------------------------------------------------\n\nEcsta-Req    	- Requester for ASCII, AREXX and "STUFF"\nEcsta-Chat	- Chat Door\nEcsta-DS	- Local/Sysop Download Door\nEcsta-Who	- Who Door\nEcsta-Front	- FrontDoor\nEcsta-Desert	- Strategy Game for /X\n@ENDNODE\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',50323,3,0,NULL,NULL,'ext_st1z','scan',1780048504);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ext107','EXT107.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/EXT107.LHA','Filenote','XIM','FILENOTE','1.07',NULL,NULL,'-------------------------------------------- use this pack for the newest update !!! ATTENTION: requires /X3.38+ or any tool',replace('         EXTERMINATE v1.07 BETA\n--------------------------------------------\n use this pack for the newest update !!!\n ATTENTION: requires /X3.38+ or any tool\n that allows multiple examine-calls like\n anthrox dupe check, conftop or similar!!!\n','\n',char(10)),'Exterminate_1.00.doc',replace('\n\n             EXTERMINATE! 1.00ß - by DELTAFORCE /X-pression\n           --------------------------------------------------\n\n1. Exterminate! checkt den FILENAMEN des files, das gerade geuploadet wurde,\nund kann anhand bestimmter File-Merkmale (meinsten am File-Beginn wie "DLM_", \n"5D-" etc. erkennen, um was für einen release es sich handelt.\n\nMan hat nun die möglichkeit, diese Files entweder zu nuken oder sie Free \nDownload zu setzen, z.B. bei releases der eigenen Group.\n\nDas Pack besteht aus folgenden Teilen:\n\n             BBS:COMMANDS/SYSCmd/EXAMINE1.info\n\n             DOORS:EXTERMINATE!/EXTERMINATE!.x\n \n             DOORS:EXTERMINATE/EXTERMINATE!.info\n\ndie Files werden einfach in die entsprechenden Verzeichnisse kopiert und\nschon ist das Tool betriebsbereit. In dem untersten file (EXTERMINATE!.info)\nsind die Tooltypes enthalten, mit denen das Tool gesteuert wird:\n\n1.       CRAP.x=APL*\n\nDies bedeutet, das sämtliche Files, die mit APL beginnen, genuked werden,\nder Stern fungiert hier also als ganz normale Wildcard und kann nach belieben\ngesetzt werden. Will man also alle Files von 5D und von APOLLO nuken, so gibt\nman\n       CRAP.1=APL*\n       CRAP.2=5D*\n\netc. an.\n\n\n2.\n         COMMENT.1=no AP(R)OLLO crap allowed!\n\nHier kann man die comments anbgeben, die dann unter das genukte file gesetzt\nwerden. Der comment darf max. 26 chars lang sein, ist er grösser, wird er auf\n26 chars abgekürzt. Der comment wird AUTOMATISCH zentriert, also direkt nach\ndem "=" mit dem comment anfangen! Wird dieser Tooltype nicht gesetzt, so wird\n"this is lame crap!" als standard-comment verwendet.\n\n\n3.       ID.1=this is a lame apollo-pseudo-release!\n\nIn dieser Zeile kann man eine bis zu 40 Zeichen lange erklärung angeben, \ndie dem uploader angezeigt wird, wenn sein File genuked wird. Sie einzugeben,\nist unbedingt empfehlenswert, wird dieeser ToolType nicht gesetzt, wird\n"restricted file!!!" verwendet. \n\n\n4.        DEDUCT.1=2\n\nHier kann man für jeden Filetyp angeben, wie oft er genukd werden soll, will \nman z.B,m das 5D-crap -2, apollo-sachen jedoch -5 genuked werden, so gibt man\nan:\n          DEDUCT.1=5\n          DEDUCT.2=2\n\netc. Wird der Tooltype nicht gesetzt, so wird immer -1 genuked!\n\n============================================================================\n\nDie folgenden Tooltypes beziehen sich auf die FREE DOWNLOAD functions:\n\n1.        FREE.1=DLM*\n          FREE.2=AI_*\n\nDies ist das Pendant zu CRAP.x, hier werden also files angegebn, die FREE \nDL gesetzt werden sollen. \n\n\n2.        FREE_COMMENT=!! FREEDDOWNLOAD !!\n\nHier kann man angeben, welcher comment unter die FreeDL-Files gesetzt werden\nsoll, default ist hier: "!! FREE DOWNLOAD !!"\n\n\n\nWichtig ist in jedem Fall, die Tooltypes DURCHLAUFEND zu numerieren, so würde\n\n         CRAP.1=BIMSE*\n         CRAP.2=BUMSE*\n         CRAP.4=ALDI*\n\nnur bis zu CRAP.2 ausgelesen werden!!!!!\n\n\n\n                                      viel Spaß, DELTAFORCE/DLM\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',14788,1,0,NULL,NULL,'st_sfl11','scan',1780048504);
