     rexxmast >nil:\n\n                      *do not 4get to copy the libs*\n\n      IF YOU DONT GET THE INSTALLATION JUST *CLOSE* YOUR BBS!DUMMASS!\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "menu3" "What does it require?"\n@toc "menu"\n\n\n                     =WHAT ABOUT THE REQUIREMENTS???=\n\n                       AMIGA 5oo-4ooo (68ooo-68o4o)\n\n                     AMIEXRESS V3.2X+ (C)LIGHTSPEED 94\n\n                 TWO LIBRARIES (SUPPORTED IN THIS PACKAGE)\n\n                 SOME COMMANDS (SUPPORTED IN THIS PACKAGE)\n\n\n\n\n      This Program will run On *ANY* Machine!Execpt PeeCee Clowns :)\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "menu4" "Credits!"\n@toc "menu"\n\n                               =THE CREdZ!=\n\n                   Coding - Jordan & Silencio/Interactive\n                         Guide - Jordan Interactive\n\n                            CygnusEd - ASDG Inc\n                          Rexx - C=Commodore Inc\n                         Amiexpress - Joseph Hodge\n                      RpStart - Dineen Edwards Group\n\n                     Greets to all IA MEMBERS ^ to...\n                 Deltaforce/Blue/Coroplex/Ceterus/Sigma Seven\n          Dr.Dre/Siegel/Byteandi/Floppyhans/Kaoz/GEM/Slaze/Exocet\n        Scottie/Maz/Hamster/Irata and all I learned to know through\n                         all the years in scene :)\n\n\n                            @{" BACK TO MAIN MENU? " link "MAIN"}\n\n@endnode\n@node "menu5" "Support"\n@toc "menu"\n\nINSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('fix_alie','FIX-ALIE.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/FIX-ALIE.LHA','aLiEn!','XIM','aLiEn!',NULL,NULL,'FIX','_________(_)___|    /  :  WE FIX · U PLAY  : \_   ____/ \   |  _/---·-------------------: :|   ___/   \  _   \_      /X DIVISION     :',replace('          _    ._____  .-------------------.\n_________(_)___|    /  :  WE FIX · U PLAY  :\n\_   ____/ \   |  _/---·-------------------:\n:|   ___/   \  _   \_      /X DIVISION     :\n:l____| \___/  |____/    pRESENTS todAY!   :\n`---------\____|---------------------------''\n               aLiEn sTrIp v0.1\n       LHA-sTriPPeR wItH aNsI-AnaLySe\n','\n',char(10)),'alien.doc',replace('          _    ._____  .-------------------.\n_________(_)___|    /  :  WE FIX · U PLAY  :\n\_   ____/ \   |  _/---·-------------------:\n:|   ___/   \  _   \_      /X DIVISION     :\n:l____| \___/  |____/    pRESENTS todAY!   :\n`---------\____|---------------------------''\n               aLiEn sTrIp v0.1\n       LHA-sTriPPeR wItH aNsI-AnaLySe\n\nyO! sYsOps\n\nFirst This Version is a Public Release for everyone!\n\nyoops another fucking Lha stripper ?\n\nYoop but one of the Best \n\nsimply copy all dirs to your BBS:  \n\n\n\n\nCall our Boards WW:\n\n                    SHQ - Bananas in Pyjamas +46-ELITE-KNOWS\n\n                    DHQ - Dope House         +31-ELITE-KNOWS\n\n                    GHQ - Running Wild       +49-ELITE-KNOWS\n\n                    WHQ - Leviathan           +1-713-ELITE\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n               - --*-- -   Fixes which Works for Life   - --*-- -\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n@BEGIN_FILE_ID.DIZ          _    ._____  .-------------------.\n_________(_)___|    /  :  WE FIX · U PLAY  :\n\_   ____/ \   |  _/---·-------------------:\n:|   ___/   \  _   \_      /X DIVISION     :\n:l____| \___/  |____/    pRESENTS todAY!   :\n`---------\____|---------------------------''\n               aLiEn sTrIp v0.1\n       LHA-sTriPPeR wItH aNsI-AnaLySe\n@END_FILE_ID.DIZ\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',24245,18,0,NULL,NULL,'fix_alie','scan',1780048515);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('fl041','FL041.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/FL041.LHA',NULL,'XIM','fl.x','0.41',NULL,NULL,'Author : SPOCK / TRSI Requirements : AmigaDOS2.0 & AmiExpress 2+',replace('FreeLeech v0.41 (Door) for AmiExpress.\nAuthor : SPOCK / TRSI\nRequirements : AmigaDOS2.0 & AmiExpress 2+\n','\n',char(10)),'fl.doc',replace('\n                   FreeLeech v0.41 (Door) for AmiExpress\n                   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n                Author : SPOCK / TRSI ([email removed])\n              Requirements : AmigaDOS2.0 & AmiExpress 2.(33?)\n\n                       Account Preferences (Fl.prefs)\n                       ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nPrefs  file  should be in the same directory as the prg.  All options can be\ndefined in two ways, either by using the shorter keyword or the longer.  For\nexample:  ''U = Spock'' vs.  ''User = Spock''\n\nU=User/A/K\n~~~~~~~~~~\nUser/Account  name  or  "Everybody!".   Should  be defined for every line in\npreferences.   If user name contains spaces, use quotes (").  When only this\noption  is  defined for user he/she may freeleech always.  All the following\noptions limit freeleeching.\n\nST=StartTime/K, ET=EndTime/K\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nAllowed  FreeLeech  Times.   If these aren''t defined user may freeleech 24h.\nNone or both should be defined.\n\nSD=StartDate/K, ED=EndDate/K\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nFreeLeech  period.   NEW:   Should  be  entered  in  Canadien  format,  like\n20-02-93.   None, both or other can be defined.  If none, user may freeleech\nalways.   If only StartDate is defined, user may freeleech from that date to\neternity.  If only EndDate is defined, user may freeleech until that date.\n\nDL=DayLimit/K/N\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nDefines how old stuff user may freeleech.  If not defined user may freeleech\nanything.\n\nML=MbLimit/K/N\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nDefines  maximum  freeleech Mbytes (1 = 1024*1024).  If not defined user may\nfreeleech as much as he dares or has time.\n\nFC=FreeConf/K/N/M\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nList  of  conferences  where  user  may  freeleech.  If not defined user may\nfreeleech in every conference.  Example :  ''FC = 1 2 3 4''.  Don''t use quotes\non this one!\n\n\n                         Miscellanous Notes & Bugs\n                         ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n*BUG* : If user losts carrier while freeleeching all bytes and files that were\n	flagged will be added to his status. This is becouse AmiExpress zmodem\n	(door implementation) doesn''t think it''s important to let door know\n	which files were actually sent OK. This could be fixed with semi-kludge\n	if somebody wanted.\n*FOO* : SuperUsers may use ''?'' too see all accounts\n*FOO* : Maximum size for path+filenames that can be send once is 200 bytes.\n	However freeleech lets you flag as much as you want, but will send\n	them ''in pieces of 200'', so the transfer will break for a moment.\n*FOO* : Possible ''*'' before user name in user status means that the user may\n	freeleech at the moment. This was added for debugging reasons, but\n	isn''t worth removing IMHO.\n\n                             FreeLeech History\n                             ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nFreeleech v0.4 -> v0.41\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n*NEW* : SuperUser -flag (see Prefs). At the moment this means only that the user\n	may use the ''?'' command.\n*NEW* : The account list shows also users'' the amount of files freeleeched and\n	freeleech conferences.\n*FIX* : Minor display bug, ''left'' was always 0.0 (Crom)\n*FOO* : DateFormat changed from AmigaDOS format (12-Jan-92) to Canadien (12-01-92)\n	to save space in display and becouse it''s easier to use.\n\nFreeleech v0.3 -> v0.4\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n*NEW*: ANSI Colors, MbLimit, Everybody! Account\n*FIX*: Callerslog & Udlog ''Bug'', ENV:STATS@\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',10483,2,0,NULL,NULL,'fl041','scan',1780048515);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('fld_ap10','FLD-AP10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/FLD-AP10.LHA',NULL,'XIM','fLOoD /X-dIViSiON',NULL,NULL,'FLD','______________           ____ _____/  ____/______/___________\_  \ _/          ____/\_       \_ _____/   \',replace('          fLOoD /X-dIViSiON\n        ______________           ____\n  _____/  ____/______/___________\_  \\n_/          ____/\_       \_ _____/   \\n\__._________/_____________/_________._\\n...:         p r e s e n t s         :..\n:                                      :\n:            DirDowner  v1.0           :\n:The BEST - 9 configurable packers, 99 :\n:       Filedirs, nice design etc.     :\n:          Released 26/11/1995         :\n:......................................:\n','\n',char(10)),'lOSeNDOS.guide',replace('                   \n                     __  _ __  /\__ _  _ __/\  __ _  __\n                    _\/___   \/              \/   ___\/_\n              ......\/\  /........................\  /\/......\n             :         \/                          \/         :\n             :      .___             .___         .___        :\n             :   _ _|   \      ______|   \  ______|   \       :\n             :   \\\__   7___  \______   /  \__   ____/       :\n             :      /.   |   \__/.  l/   \___/_____   \__ _   :\n             :     /::.  |    _/::.       _/::.  l/    _///   :\n             :     \___________\___________\____________\     :\n             :___        .___        .___        .___         :___\n     _ ______|   \ ______|   \ ______|   \ ______|   \  ______|   \\n     \\\__   ____/ \______   / \______   / \______   /  \__   ____/\n        /.   ___|___/.   |   \__/.  _|   \__/.  l/   \___/_____   \__ _\n       /::.  l/   _/::.  |    _/::. \___  _/::.       _/::.  l/    _///\n       \_ _________\_____|_____\___________\___________\___________ \\n         Y   :                                                :[nM$]Y\n      .------''                                                `------.\n      :eXON/rIOT^jORMAS · gHANDY/gODS · rAHIEM/eSSENCE · cELIC/rEKTUM: \n      `------.                                                .------''\n             `------------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,13082,6,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048515);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('fld_chat','FLD-CHAT.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/FLD-CHAT.LHA','8','XIM','8',NULL,'Genius)_____|','FLD','._)  _/__)   /  ._)  _ (_._)  _ (_._)  _ \ |    ._/   _/___|    /   |    /   |    /  \ |____| |___\    |________|________|__      |',replace('  _____  _____    ______   ______   _____\n._)  _/__)   /  ._)  _ (_._)  _ (_._)  _ \\n|    ._/   _/___|    /   |    /   |    /  \\n|____| |___\    |________|________|__      |\n|By Genius)_____| Spli7chat v1.0 !! )______|\n|                                          |\n|The ULTIMATE splitscreen chatter, graphic |\n|interface, capture, commands executed from|\n|chat, userdefinable designs, and more!!!  |\n|            For /X or S!X systems         |\n`[22-Aug-96]--------------------------[248]''\n','\n',char(10)),'Spli7Chat.guide',replace('@DATABASE "SPLI7CHAT v1.0 FULL DOC/GUIDE"\n@NODE "MAIN" "Spli7Chat V1.0 Guide"\n\n     _\n   ._)\  _______________________________.\n   |   \/                               |\n   |  .....................             |       f · L · O · o · D\n   |  :       @{fg shine}   ________ @{fg text}:             |\n   |  : @{fg shine} _______/  _____/_:___________ @{fg text} |          /X division @{fg shine}   _____ @{fg text}\n@{fg shine}  _@{fg text}|@{fg shine}__:_/   ___/__ \_        \_  __   \_@{fg text}|@{fg shine}____________     ________\_   \\n@{fg shine}_/           ____/____________/  \          /   __   \___/   ______/    \\n\_____________/           @{fg text}:@{fg shine} \______________/    \       \________________\ @{fg text}\n      :                   :..  .........|.@{fg shine}\________________/@{fg text}(rLf)/-T   ...\n      :             .....   :  :        |:.    .....                ...:.:\n      :       ......:   :...:..:        | :     :  :...........     :\n    ..:.......:.............:           | :.....:           :.:.....:...\n....:         :                         |____:_______________________:__ _\n:.:           .                          ....:                       :....\n:                                        :.........presents..........::\n:\n:                @{fg shine}  SPLI7CHAT - coded by Genius / FLD    ©mP!1996 @{fg text}\n:          \n:.................................................................. . .\n\n@{fg shine}\n                        R E A D   t h i s   g u i d e\n@{fg text}\nIt''s a quite complex door, and mabye you won''t get parts of the installation\n            etc. if you don''t read this... so make me happy, ok?!\n@{fg shine}\n              _________________________________________________\n             _)                                               (_ \n            ! @{fg text}  o                                          O@{fg shine}    !@{fg text}\n\n       @{"                      General information                       " LINK "General"}    \n\n       @{"                           Features                             " LINK "Features"}    \n\n       @{"                         Installation                           " LINK "Installation"}    \n\n       @{"                    How to make new designs                     " LINK "Designs"}    \n\n       @{"                        How to register                         " LINK "Register"}    \n\n       @{"                      Bugreports/updates                        " LINK "BUGS"}    \n\n       @{"                       Features to come                         " LINK "Future Features"}    \n\n       @{"                        Greetings ect.                          " LINK "Greets"}    \n@{fg shine}            .                                                   .\n            |_ @{fg text} O                                         o@{fg shine}    _|\n              )_______________________________________________(\n\n@{fg text}\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "General" "General Information"\n\n\n                     @{b}      .:General information:.       @{ub}                  \n@{fg shine}\n                         (___                   ___)\n                            /___________________\\n\n@{fg text}\n  1st of all, if they are included in your package, look at the screenshots\n     (the pictures descripe the door alot better than I can in words! 8)\n\n    Tired of your users always are writing slower than you, and it pisses\n                                  you off?\n\n     Ever wanted to be able to write at the same time as your user while\n                                  in chat?\n\n     Ever wanted to (like on Cnet) execute commands directly from chat?\n\n        Ever wanted a splitscreen chatter, but found that the few in\n                            existence were CRAP?\n\n       Ever felt like a normal chat was just too boring with the same\n                        design / style all the time?\n\n@{fg shine}\n  @{b}    Well, then you got the right door now, this product is BRILLIANT! @{ub}\n@{fg text}\n\n    The biggest door I''ve EVER written (and i''ve written quite a few now)\n     The source is far over 1500 lines and the compiled door fills over \n           110K !!! the is one massive block of superb doorstuff!\n\n   Check out the screenshots.. and you''ll know that this baby is fiine! 8)\n\n\n    The biggest door I''ve EVER written (and i''ve writte quite a few now)\n     The sourcer is far over 1500 lines and the compiled door fill over \n            80K !!! the is one massive block of superb doorstuff!\n\n   Check out the screenshots.. and you''ll know that this baby is fiine! 8)\n\n\n\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "Features" "Features"\n\n\n                              @{b}  .:Features:.   @{ub}                            \n@{fg shine}\n                         (___                   ___)\n                            /___________________\\n@{fg text}\n                   GUI directly on your /X or S!X screen!\n\n            SYSOP to USER splitscreen chatter with double-cursors\n\n         You can execute commands (like from the mainmenu) by typing\n      in the chatter /command for example :     /s    show your status\n       all commands works, incl. up/downloading exept for G (goodbye)\n       Both sysop and user can use this feature! After the command are\n                 executed the bbs returns to the chatting...\n\n      You can make your OWN designs, and even change to another design\n                             while chatting!!!!\n\n        Very flexible configuration of the designs, you can even make\n      a side-by-side chat or a "normal" over-and-under chattype.. only\n                           YOU set the limits! 8)\n\n   The chatter remembers EACH users longest chat/ total chats / total time\n   in chat ect. lots of stuff, and you can create TOP10 chatter bulletins\n                   with the util included in the package!\n\n      The chatter can also display REALTIME and CHATTIME (and lots more\n    features) WHILE chatting, so you can always see for how long you have\n                               been chatting!\n\n                            Online configuration!\n\n                      DEL clears the current chatwindow\n\n   Capture feature! When capture is activated ( using the on-screen GUI )\n    is remembers and saves everything written by user and sysop, AND it''s\n     all being saved in a seperate capture-file for each user. That way\n    it''s easy and fast to locate a specific chat, if you wan''t to recall\n                    what you and your user talked about!\n\n\n\n        @{b}     Massive code and testing - this baby is fiiine! 8) @{ub}\n\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "Installation" "Installation"\n\n\n                            @{b}  .:Installation:. @{ub}                            \n@{fg shine}\n                         (___                   ___)\n                            /___________________\\n@{fg text}\n\n     There''s icons with the package ( in Installstuff/ ) just copy them\n          to the right dirs.. you know the drill, you are a sysop!\n\n    I also supplied you with a @{fg shine}CHATSTART.txt@{fg text} for your BBS:NODEx/ so when\n   your pager starts a chat or you press F1..  spli7chat is automatically\n                                  started!\n\n  You might change your CHATEND.txt to something, like a logo or something\n  I use a big logo that sais C''YA L8R (save a bit of time, typing it every\n                               time myself 8)\n\n   If you want to RESET the stats (like the topchatters ect.) just delete\n    all files in the dir called "DATA/"  that way, the chatter starts as\n                      if it was opened the first time!\n\n\n    The first thing I suggest you do, it start it up - and press the gui\n     button: CONFIG   ... then make some hotkeys for you personal use...\n                    The two other "checkmark boxes" are:\n\n\n     @{fg shine}  Autocapture@{fg text} - well of''coz turn capture on at every chat-start!\n\n    @{fg shine}   AutoDesign@{fg text} -  checks if the users have less than 24 lines (like\n                     most PC terminal programs have, and uses the internal\n                     chatdesign (works even if the user have only 23 lines)\n                     The chatter STILL remembers you farvorite design\n                     and uses that one, when a user comes with enough lines.\n\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "Designs" "How to make new designs"\n\n\n                     @{b}    .:How to make new designs:.  @{ub}                     \n@{fg shine}\n                         (___                   ___)\n                            /___________________\\n\n@{fg text}\n   Make the design (the background) with any ansi editor, (like PROAnsi or\n   HyperANSI), then save it in DESIGNS/ with the number you desire + .txt\n                                in the end...\n\n   Now make a new textfile with the configuration for the design, for the\n    commands you can use, just look in one of the many supplied examples!\n                          and save it as number.cfg\n\n  Start up the chatter and press TAB, the type the number.. c if it works!\n\n\n   Heres just a bit of tips if you are not really into all the ansi stuff\n                                 and codes..\n\n\n         ESC[y;xH    Will place the cursor at location x,y on your\n                     screen... example:   ESC[14;2H\n\n         ESC[3xm     Change pen colour (x = colour 0-7)\n                     example ESC[33m\n\n         ESC[4xm     Change background colour, like pen...\n\n         ESC[0m      Changes to normal writing style.. (like a reset\n                     of the colour ect)\n\n         ESC[1m      bold writing (4=underline 3=itallic etc.)\n\n         ESC[32;41m  the ; conbines to codes to make the ansi command\n                     fill less space...\n\n\n     NOTE! due to some wierd bug/fault i amiexpress, colour 0 and 7 are\n  swapped on the sysop''s screen, I deal with this by replacing ALL ESC[37m\n   with ESC[0m (white colour) in my ansi screens, mabye this will work for\n                   you too, if not - just don''t do it ! 8)\n\n  @{b}   Should be enough to get you started! try and learn - the best way! @{b}\n\n\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "Register" "How to register"\n\n\n                         @{b}    .:How to register:.  @{ub}                         \n@{fg shine}\n                         (___                   ___)\n                            /___________________\\n@{fg text}\n\n\n@{fg shine}       Very important! Very important! Very important! Very important! @{fg text}\n\n\n\n                    @{b}     Registration is 100% FREE!@{ub}\n\n  No money is involved! - why not? becoz'' doors SHOULD be free! that''s why!\n\n     All you gotta do is call @{" my board " LINK "ADD"} and say "Hello m8, I would like a\n   registered copy of spli7chat!" and I''ll make you a keyfile you can download!\n\n  And if you want to, I''ll keep your net-adress ect. and contact you, if I make\n                                updates ect.\n\n\n@{fg shine}       Very important! Very important! Very important! Very important! @{fg text}\n\n\n\n\n    So, theres really NO reason NOT to reg. this door... i understand if\n   you are not living in denmark, the phonecosts ect. so therefor there''s\n   NO LIMITATIONS in the unregistered version, the ONLY difference between\n       it and a regged one, is your name in it! - and you saying that\n                              you like my work!\n\n    But I would like to know how many uses this door, and what they think\n    about it.. the more feedback i get, the more i''ll do to make it even\n                                   better!\n\n    It would also be EXCELENT if you would take the time to write a small\n   letter to me, over fidonet (u can find my fido adress another place in\n  this document) Just type a few words about weather you like this product\n   or mabye you have some ideas.. everything will be greatly appriciated!\n\n\n\n@{b}                                   Thanx!@{ub}\n\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "BUGS" "Bug reports"\n\n\n@{b}                           .:Bugreports/updates:.                          @{ub}\n@{fg shine}\n                         (___                   ___)\n                            /___________________\\n\n@{fg text}\n     This door have been tested a lot by myself and some betatesters, so\n     there should NOT be bugs in.. But if you come accross something you\n       think is a bug, you may contact me at one of my net-adresses or\n                 through my board (or any danish FLOOD site)\n\n                            @{" HOW TO CONTACT ME? " LINK "ADD"}                       \n\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "Future Features" "Features to come"\n\n\n                         @{b}   .:Features to come:. @{ub}                          \n@{fg shine}\n                         (___                   ___)\n                            /___________________\\n@{fg text}                    \n\n                  @{fg shine}  o @{fg text} Bulletin creator tool\n                       did''nt have time to make on for this version!\n\n                  @{fg shine}  o @{fg text} -MABYE- some color handling\n                       for user aswell as sysop...\n\n                  @{fg shine}  o @{fg text} Mabye a DESIGN editor, so you don''t\n                       have to make the .cfg file yourself\n\n                  @{fg shine}  o @{fg text} Fullauto coffee-maker ;)\n\n                  @{fg shine}  o @{fg text} mabye a SPEAK mode??  good idea??\n\n                  @{fg shine}  o @{fg text} Your ideas... I''m open for any suggestions!\n\n\n\n\n\n                            @{" HOW TO CONTACT ME? " LINK "ADD"}                       \n\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "Greets" "Greetings"\n\n               @{fg shine}                                ·\n                          .---------------------\-.\n                          |·                     \|\n                          :                       \ \n                          |                       |\\n                          :    @{fg text}  .:gREETS:.  @{fg shine}     :~\n                         _|        ______         |\n                         \:                       :\n                          \                       |\n                          :\                     ,:\n                          `/----------------------''\n                          ·   @{fg text}                     \n\n\n       CoOL /X cOdERS:.          mENACE^fld · Chrome^fld · Jawlog^fld\n\n       CoOL sYSdEViLS:.          Lionheart^fld · Cybersoul \n                                 Chevy · 2PAC · Seahawk etc.\n\n       sPECIAL gREETS:.          Melomaniac, Sundown\n                                 and ALL flood, plaztique, twilight, \n                                 vodka and hamstarz members! 8)\n\n\n                           @{fg shine}   - gENiUS / fLOOD@{fg text}\n                /\________________________________ __ _ _  _\n               ·\n\n\n\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "ADD" "How to contact me"\n\n\n                       @{b}    .: How to contact me :.@{ub}\n@{fg shine}\n                         (___                   ___)\n                            /___________________\\n\n@{fg text}\n              \n                                                                           \n                   @{fg shine}.-----------.@{fg text}                                           \n   .--^----·-------@{fg shine}|\  __.__  /|@{fg text}-----^^--------.  .-----------------^--.   \n   |·              @{fg shine}| \ \ ! / / :@{fg text}              ·|  |·                  ·!   \n   |@{fg shine}______________ |  \ \_/ /  : ______________@{fg text}|  | hAMSTARZ   wORLDhQ |   \n   |@{fg shine}\_____       ·)| `_\___/_'' |(·      ______/@{fg text}|  :                    |   \n_ _|_@{fg shine}¯\         // | (_\`-''/_) : \\         /¯@{fg text}_|__| pLAZTiQUE  wORLDhQ |   \n\\\_  @{fg shine} \____   ((__|  ¯¯| .¯¯  |__))  _____/ @{fg text}  __/|                    |   \n   |·  @{fg shine} ¯\___   ·--| .  : :    |--·  ____/¯ @{fg text}   |  ! tWiLiGHT      dKhQ |   \n   |:.  @{fg shine}  ¯\_      `(_  `^'' __)''      _/¯  @{fg text}   _|_ _                    |   \n   |:::. @{fg shine}   \____   /|   "  ¯:\    ___/  @{fg text}      _/// nD1   +45-39902992 |   \n   |:::::. @{fg shine}  ¯¯\_  _)|__·_.__|(_   _/¯ @{fg text}        |  . nD2   +45-private! |   \n   |:::::::.@{fg shine}    `--'' || : | || `---'' @{fg text}    ·©mP!·|  | nD3   +45-telnetnd |   \n   :·················@{fg shine}`^-^-^-^''@{fg text}·················:  | nD4   +45-telnetnd |   \n   |@{fg shine}._________________________________________.@{fg text}|  | nD5   +45-telnetnd :   \n   |@{fg shine}|__ _____!  |  .  |  ____  _  )  ______!  |@{fg text}| _|_                   |   \n   |@{fg shine}|  \  |  \  |  |  |  --''|  _  |  |  |  \  |@{fg text}| \_                    |   \n   |@{fg shine}`-----^-----^--^--^-----^--\__!-----^-----''@{fg text}|  | sYS: gENiUS/fLD   _|__ \n   |@{fg shine}   :  |_____________  _________________:  |@{fg text}|  |      ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯    __/ \n   |@{fg shine}.__|_ |  ____  .  | \/  _____ |  _  )  |  |@{fg text}|  |                    |   \n   |@{fg shine}| __/ |  --''|  |  |·  / |  _/ |  _  |    -:@{fg text}|  | aMY & el¡7e   oNLY_|_ _\n   |@{fg shine}`-----^-----''--^--''-\/--^-----^--\__!--^--''@{fg text}|  |·                   _///\n   `---·---^^--^-------------------^-----------''  `--·-------^^-^------''   \n\n                                     ...\n\n        @{fg shine}       Well, this is the quickest way.. call my board!\n\n       If you don''t want to do THAT.. well, you can mail me at one of\n                               there adresses:@{fg text}\n\n\n                      @{"  Email......... not availble!  " LINK "Idiot!"}\n\n                      @{"  Fidonet....... 2:236/112.5    " LINK "Idiot!"}\n\n                      @{"  Amiganet...... 39:141/145.5   " LINK "Idiot!"}\n\n                      @{"  HOAnet........ 10:1/26.5      " LINK "Idiot!"}\n\n                      @{"  Scenenet...... 245:3/0.5      " LINK "Idiot!"}\n\n                      @{"  IRC/Internet.. #amielite      " LINK "Idiot!"}\n\n\n          @{fg shine}     Or leave a messy at one of FLOODs danish sites!@{fg text}\n\n\n\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "Idiot!" "Idiot!"\n\n\n HEY! are you stupid?!.. U can''t use Amigaguide for that! \n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',69945,3,0,NULL,NULL,'fld_chat','scan',1780048515);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('fld_crdd','FLD-CRDD.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/FLD-CRDD.LHA',NULL,'XIM','DirDowner.xim',NULL,NULL,'FLD','______________           ____ _____/  ____/______/___________\_  \ _/          ____/\_       \_ _____/   \',replace('          fLOoD /X-dIViSiON\n        ______________           ____\n  _____/  ____/______/___________\_  \\n_/          ____/\_       \_ _____/   \\n\__._________/_____________/_________._\\n...:         p r e s e n t s         :..\n:                                      :\n:            DirDowner  v1.0           :\n:The BEST - 9 configurable packers, 99 :\n:       Filedirs, nice design etc.     :\n:          Released 26/11/1995         :\n:...................................[1]:\n[02-02-96]-[n!]»(H¡DDeN PØWeR!)«[n!]-[14:51]\n[03-02-96]-diGiTAL^HAREm-[fTP&33.6k]-[02:38]\n','\n',char(10)),'DirDowner.doc',replace('     _\n   ._)\  _______________________________.\n   |   \/                               |\n   |  .....................             |       f · L · O · o · D\n   |  :          ________ :             |\n   |  :  _______/  _____/_:___________  |          /X division    _____\n  _|__:_/   ___/__ \_        \_  __   \_|____________     ________\_   \\n_/           ____/____________/  \          /   __   \___/   ______/    \\n\_____________/           : \______________/    \       \________________\\n      :                   :..  .........|.\________________/(rLf)/-T   ...\n      :             .....   :  :        |:.    .....                ...:.:\n      :       ......:   :...:..:        | :     :  :...........     :\n    ..:.......:.............:           | :.....:           :.:.....:...\n....:         :                         |____:_______________________:__ _\n:.:           .                          ....:                       :....\n:                                        :.........presents..........::\n:\n:           DirDowner v1.0  by  Chrome / fLOoD /X\n:          \n:......................................................................... . .\n\n\n\n\n· Disclaimer:\n\n    The author cannot be held responsible for ANY damage caused by the\n    use of this program, such as loss of data, damage to hardware etc.\n           The use of this program is ENTIRELY on your own risk!\n   This door may be distributed freely, as long as all files in original\n                         archive remains intact...\n            I guarantee, that this door is 100% backdoor free!\n\n\n Ok, now we got that settled, let me introduce you to the very best\ndirlist-downloader EVER made for /X...\n This door supports upto 99 filedirs pr. conference and upto 9\nconfigurable packers, so your PC-users can choose for example ZIP\nor ARJ, while your Amiga users can use LhA or LZX as they wish...\nIt''s ALL up to you to decide which packers should be available!\n(Oh yeah, and for the sake of not being so boring, I did NOT include\n9 packers in this archive! Come on, who haven''t got AEdoor.library!?\nStop adding useless files just to get more credits!)\n\nOk, enough bragging, lets move on to:\n\n\n\n· Installation:\n\nOn /X:\n Just copy the files into their proper directories, and make sure the\naccess level in the DD.info (in bbs:commands/bbscmd) is what you want\nit to be (security)... \n\nOn S!X:\n Just do as you normally install doors, but to get this running, you\nmust have an icon to go with your conference dir, that contains the\ntooltype ''NDIRS''. An example: You have a conference in bbs:files/warez/\nwith two filedirs. Then you would need to add bbs:files/warez.info,\nthis icon would contain NDIRS=2. This is all you need!\n\n\n\n And then we reach the important part:\n\n\n· Configuration:\n\n You can setup the packers in the Dirdowner.info icon which MUST be\nplaced in the same dir as the door itself, using the following\ntooltypes:\n\n Packer.x  :  The packer syntax, using %a as where the tempfile\n              should be placed in the syntax, and %f for where\n              the files to be packed is placed in the syntax.\n              Example: You wish to use LhA, and it''s syntax goes\n              sumthing like:\n              LhA a <Destination> <Source files>\n              you would make it like this in the DirDowner.info:\n              Packer.1=LhA a %a %f\n              And it would run Just ok!\n              Note, that after what you write in the Packer.x-tooltype,\n              the door automatically adds a ''>NIL:'' so you don''t have\n              to worry about this.\n\n Text.x    :  The text displayed to the user...\n              Usually the name of the packer ;)\n\n Ext.x     :  The extension the packer adds... F.x LhA adds .Lha\n              to it''s dest file and so it would be:\n              Ext.x=.LhA\n\nIf only one packer is present in the Dirdowner.info, the user will\nnot be asked which packer he wants to use (quite obvious, eh?)\nand YES, this door checks to see if user has lost carrier on a query!\n That''s all! The Tempfile will be called DL<date><month>,\nif for example someone downloads a filelist on the 25. of November,\nthe packed file will be DL25NOV.xxx  (.xxx is specified in ext.x!)\n\n\n\n· NOTE:\n\n Upon launch, the door tries to delete files in bbs:nodex/work/ called\ndl#?, this is because if a dl-file already would exist with the same\nfilenames in it, LhA or similar packers would not pack the new files\nin the dldir file... And this would suck pretty much if the sysop\nwould have to check bbs:nodex/work/ for old dldir-files in order\nto make the door work. Ofcoz, when the dldir-file has been sent\n(or attempted to be sent) the dldir-file is automatically deleted,\nso it doesnt take up space (just in case someone runs his bbs: from\na diskdrive ;)\n\n So far, the door only supports 9 nodes... Don''t know if this is enough,\nbut if ya need a version running with 10+ nodes, call my board and\ntell me, and I will fix it for you!\n\n If something goes wrong, the door either displays a message saying\n»error in input«, then it''s the users fault (as always ;) but if\nyou/he get a message saying »please notify sysop« then check your\nDirdowner.info that ALL tooltypes are present and correct typed.\nIf this is ok, Snoopdos may help you quite a lot here...\nBut ofcoz, if everything else fails, blame it on the user 8)\n\nIf the user selects a filelist for the upload dir, the door simply\nassumes the upload dir to be the last dir... Ie if you have specified\nNDIRS=20 (in your conference .info!) and the user selects the upload\ndir, the file packed will be DIR20.\n\n\n\n· How to contact me:\n\n If you have any bugreports, new ideas for improvements or want to\nrequest a door for your board, the easiest way is to call my board:\n-> Volvo''s Inn:  +45 8660 0051\nOr you could leave a msg for me at one of our DK boards, or any\nother elite board in Denmark ;)\n\n\n\n· Greetings:\n\n Greetings, Hi''s and respects must go to these randomly picked people:\n\n · mESH! - Jawlog - Pride - Screem - Azlan - Scqeech - Dizy - Json ·\n· Relief - Wenix - Jet Z - Zwoolock - Bird - Adonis - Melanc - Rodex ·\n· Nashua - SkyWalker - Black Death - Platoon - All FLD and OTL members ·\n· TrickTrax -  And to all I forgot! ·\n\n\n\n                                       - Chrome / FLD ^ OTL\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',9260,5,0,NULL,NULL,'fld_crdd','scan',1780048515);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('fld_ff10','FLD-FF10.LZX','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/FLD-FF10.LZX',NULL,'XIM','fld ff10',NULL,NULL,'FLD',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,29096,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048515);
