INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ihs_uc11','IHS-UC11.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/IHS-UC11.LHA','usercheck','XIM','usercheck',NULL,'pSYCHoTROn/iHS','IHS','¦   __________________  _ .:::::::::::::::.¦ ¦.-.\__  /  /  /  ___/ /\\               ::¦ ¦¦ :/  \/  _  /__   /./\// INHUMANS<----.::¦',replace('.------------------------------------------.\n¦   __________________  _ .:::::::::::::::.¦\n¦.-.\__  /  /  /  ___/ /\\               ::¦\n¦¦ :/  \/  _  /__   /./\// INHUMANS<----.::¦\n¦¦ .\   \  /  \  \  \¦\//  .------------''::¦\n¦:   \  /\/\  /\/\  /¦ Y   `---->PRESENTS::¦\n¦`----\/»WLK\/----\/-'' `---------------->::¦\n¦                                        ::¦\n¦   A New /X Door Called UserCheck v1.1  ::¦\n¦        Coded by pSYCHoTROn/iHS         ::¦\n¦.::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::''¦\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'usercheck.guide',replace('@database 081b7650-0\n@master sc:usercheck/usercheck.guide\n@remark Created with Heddley v1.0 (c) Edd Dumbill 1994\n\n@node "Main" "UserCheck v1.0"\n           ___ ___.---.__.---.__.--.__      _______ ___.---.______\n          (___Y _¬\   ¦ _l_  | ¬|  ¦ ¬\ __ /   __ ¬Y _¬\   ¦ ____/__\n         _|  ¬\  \ \  | \__  |  |  | _ \\//\   `/  |  \ \  |_______¬\__\n        (_)    \  \ \ |  T   |  ¯  |  \ \/  \  T   |   \ \ |     l   \/\n          l_____\__\  |__|   |_____|   \  /  \_|   |____\  |_________/\n            :       \_|  l___|     `----\/l___\l___|     \_|       :\n            :..................................................xCz.:\n\n                       I * N * H * U * M * A * N * S                \n\n                                                                        \n                                 PRESENTS:\n                                 \n                                 \n                               KICKUSER V1.0\n                                                                        \n                              \n                             @{"WHAT IS THIS SHIT:" link "What" 0}\n                                     \n                             @{"   INSTALLATION:  " link "Install" 0}\n                                \n                             @{"    GREETZ TO:    " link "Greetz" 0}             \n                                 \n                                \n                                  \n\n                                        \n@endnode\n\n@node "What" "What is this?"\n@next "Install"\n@prev "Main"\nSome of you probably wonder what this is? This door checks that the new user\nuploads at least x meg in y days.... if he hasn''t done this he will get his\naxx lowered.. He will also get a mess who tells him to send a message to the\nsysop and explain why he hasn''t uploaded enough .. The message looks like\nthis!\n\n.-------------------------------------------------------------------. \n| READ THIS! READ THIS! READ THIS! READ THIS! READ THIS! READ THIS! |\n`-------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n   You have NOT managed uploading xxxxxxxx bytes in xxxx days!!\n   This board does not support inactive users , and you seem\n   to be one of them.\n   If you wanna get your old access back , then mail the sysop\n   and give him a damned good reason for lettin you in again!\n\n.-------------------------------------------------------------------. \n| READ THIS! READ THIS! READ THIS! READ THIS! READ THIS! READ THIS! |\n`-------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\nYou have also some gonfigurasions to helps you to choose the rules for the\nnewuser on your board\n\n1. What conference the door should send the message. \n2. How many kilobytes the user must upload. \n3. How long time he have got to upload. \n4. What access to user should get when he is kicked. \n5. Which users how should not be effectedby this door.\n\nTo make this gonfiguration yop type USERCHECK CONFIG at the /X promt.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "Install" "istallalation"\n@next "greetz"\n@prev "What"\nWhen you have decided to install this door for your board you copy the\nusercheck drawer to bbs:door and the Usercheck.info to your\nBBS:Commands/BBSCmd/ drawer. Then add the line "~CC_USERCHECK" to all your\nbull.txt files in your bbs:node drawers. When you are finished type Usercheck\nconfig at your /X prompt.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "greetz" "Greetz to"\n@prev "install"\nI like to say thanx to the following guys:\n\nWedlock/iHS «-» The ascii god.\n\nBiztro/iHS  «-» For nice ideas.\n\nRecall/iHS  «-» Great IHS leader.\n\nNIKE/TRSI   «-» GREATEST SYSOP EVER AND CODING HELP\n\nZORRO/BFG   «-» You''re always a helping hand.\n\n\n@endnode\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',25103,6,0,NULL,NULL,'ihs_uc11','scan',1780048545);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ihs_ul11','IHS_UL11.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/IHS_UL11.LHA',NULL,'XIM','Ul-Logoff.X',NULL,'tANGO/lED^iHS^pTL','IHS','_____ _____ _____ _____  ___________.::::. | | |  \| | |_| | | | |  \/  |  _  |  ::.|   ! | | \ | |  _  | |_| | |\/| |  _  | \·::::. ¦',replace('.--- -- -  -÷i÷N÷H÷U÷M÷A÷N÷S÷-        - ---.\n_____ _____ _____ _____  ___________.::::. |\n| |  \| | |_| | | | |  \/  |  _  |  ::.|   !\n| | \ | |  _  | |_| | |\/| |  _  | \·::::. ¦\n|_|_|\__|_| |_|_____|_|  |_|_| |_|_|.._.:: :\n             p R E S E N T S     RcL·::::· ·\n                                            \n    uL-lOGOFF v1.1 bY tANGO/lED^iHS^pTL    .\n.                                         ::\n¦:.                                    ..::¦\n`- -                         -  -- --- ----''\n','\n',char(10)),'Ul-Logoff.guide',replace('@database 00325fa0-0\n@master BBS:misc/ihs/work/Ul-Logoff.guide\n@$VER: Ul-Logoff.x 1.1 (13.9.95)\n@author "tANGO/iHS^lED^pTL"\n@(c) "1995 by tANGO/iHS^lED^pTL"\n@remark Created with Heddley v1.1 (c) Edd Dumbill 1994\n\n@node "Main" "No title"\n\n\n                  _ __         ____\n   _____      ______  |__ ____|_   |___  ___  _______      ______ _____\n _:_____: ___|     /  |  \\     /   |   \\/   \\_\\____  \\____|     /  ___/___\n \\       |   \\    /   .   \\_  /    |  _  /   \\_  _/   \\_  \\    /_____    /\n  \\______|____\\__/____|    /_______|___\\/_____/__\\     /___\\__/_________/\n <--------------------|___/--------------------uMn\\___/------------------>\n\n                                  pRESENTS\n\n                               uL-lOGOFF v1.1\n\n                            bY tANGO/iHS^lED^pTL\n\n\n                               @{" iNTRODUCTION " link "introduction" 0}\n                               @{" rEQUIREMENTS " link "requirement" 0}\n                               @{" iNSTALLATION " link "installation" 0}\n                               @{"   hISTORY    " link "history" 0}\n                               @{"  gREETINGS   " link "greetings" 0}\n                               @{" hOW tO rEACH " link "howtoreach" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "introduction" "iNTRODUCTION"\n\n                                 iNTRODUCTION\n                                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThis is not the first door that lets you log off after an upload... Though,\nit''s the first one that completely melts into /X. You don''t need to run it\nwith an MCI command, it replaces the U command completely... Choosing\ngoodbye after upload will really hang you up after you''ve uploaded, and\nbefore all the filechecking. If you just choose start, or use RZ you will be\nasked if you want to log off after the upload is complete. What more is\nthere to it? This is the first door I''ve seen so far that solves this\nproblem in a nice and easy way. There''s simply now reason not to run it!\n\nThis door is, like all my other doors and utils, written in C. No lame arexx\nhere... It''s fast and good looking... Simply pure quality!\n@endnode\n\n@node "requirement" "rEQUIREMENTS"\n\n                                rEQUIREMENTS\n                                ~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThis door requires you to run /X v3.x+ on an Amiga! :)\n@endnode\n\n@node "installation" "iNSTALLATION"\n\n                                iNSTALLATION\n                                ~~~~~~~~~~~~\nEverything is set up for you... Simply copy the files to the correct\ndirectories.\n\nPlease note that if you already run doors as EXAMINE, fex file_id or\ndreamchart doors, you''ll have to rename some icons. I''ve installed this door\nas EXAMINE and have moved all the other EXAMINE doors one step forward, ie\n\n   EXAMINE  -> EXAMINE1\n   EXAMINE1 -> EXAMINE2\n\nand so on... This way you will get the logoff question before any file_id''s\nare processed. It''s not needed though. You may as well run it after all the\nother EXAMINE doors. If you want to do it this way, reanme the EXAMINE icon i\nsupplied.\n\nIf you want to you can add the following to you logoff batch as well.\n\n   delete ENV:UL-Logoff.<node> QUIET\n\nIf you skip this, the door won''t ask the user if he wants to hang up or not if\nhe just called and uploaded then hanged up, called again and used RZ. If he\nused U he would get the question again. This happens because there''s no other\nway to detect if the user loged off or not.\n@endnode\n\n@node "history" "hISTORY"\n\n                                  hISTORY\n                                  ~~~~~~~\nv1.0  -  First beta version. Not realeased other than to some of my friends.\n\nv1.1  -  Added a function to check if the user had uploads to resume. If he\n         had the normal upload routine will be called. This is needed\n         because there''s no way to resume an upload if /X doesn''t do it it''s\n         way.\n         Added a function to show and check the upload space. While i was\n         beta-testing v1.0, some of my users asked if there was room on the\n         HD, so I fixed the problem.\n@endnode\n\n@node "greetings" "gREETINGS"\n\n                                 gREETINGS\n                                 ~~~~~~~~~\nI know I''m bound to forget someone if I write a long greetings list.\nTherefor I won''t do it... Feel greeted if you know me. Here are some special\nones that I want to share with you though!\n\n       Cathleen, La Fayette, Exeron & Maniac, DJ Gizmo, Christ, Abbe\n       TBB, Scroud & Melone, Rille, Rioter, Overlord, Hiway & Route66\n                              Visitor & Recall\n\nPlease forgive me if I forgot someone! :)\n@endnode\n\n@node "howtoreach" "hOW tO rEACH"\n\n                                hOW tO rEACH\n                                ~~~~~~~~~~~~\nIf you want to get in contact with me, write me a message on my board,\nInferno, on any board in the 042, 0431, 0435 or 0418 areas in sweden or on\none of the following boards,\n\n              Bitchboard, Ace of spades, Skyline, Last resort\n\nor write an e-mail to [email removed]\n@endnode\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',18841,5,0,NULL,NULL,'ihs_ul11','scan',1780048545);
