irements  <- " link REQUIREMENTS }\n                          @{" ->  Installation  <- " link INSTALLATION }\n                          @{" ->   The Future   <- " link THE_FUTURE }\n                          @{" ->    Epilogue    <- " link EPILOGUE }\n                          @{" ->     Credits    <- " link CREDITS }\n@endnode\n\n@node INTRODUCTION\n@title "sKAN^4^sTATUs · cODED bY mARX/iNSANE!"\n+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+\n\nIntroduction:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nsKAN^4^sTATUs V1.02 features:\n\n** 100% M680x0 ASM-code (faaaaaaast!)\n** VERY cool dezign (Hiya cLUSTER!)\n\nsKAN^4^sTATUs V1.02 does NOT feature:\n\n** Configuration abilities upto 99% (YET!)\n\n\n\nYepp! I''m back! This time with another cool release... sKAN^4^sTATUs V1.02!\nAlthough none of my projects start without the goal in mind of making them\nNO.1 in whatever /X cathegory of tools they might belong to, this one can\nreally make you scratch your head. It is as simple as a alternative to the\n1000 status-doors already available! Now, WHAT makes this one so special?\nWell, at this stage of development, almost nothing! At least, if you ignore\nthe VERY COOL DEZIGN (which you really can''t ignore, can you? ;) The real\nadvantage of this baby, is... the forthcoming features! (Read ''THE FUTURE''!)\nI have sum great fockin'' plans for this one (as always...) and you''re gonna\nsee the kind of features that nobody ever seen in a goddam status-door!\n\nA status-door has one task, and that is to display relevant information to\nthe user. It is also very easy to code such a door. Since it''s considered\nbeing the first door one codes, many people have done their own version.\nNow, the amount of information doesn''t grow with newer versions of /X.\nSo, the only significant change from door to door is... the design!\n\n+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+\n@endnode\n\n@node REQUIREMENTS\n@title "sKAN^4^sTATUs · cODED bY mARX/iNSANE!"\n+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+\n\nRequirements:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nsKAN^4^sTATUs V1.02 requires:\n\n** AmiExpress 3.xx      (Doesn''t everybody have it?)\n** Kickstart 2+         (Doesn''t everybody have it?)\n** Motorola 68020+      (Doesn''t everybody have it?)\n\n+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+\n@endnode\n\n@node INSTALLATION\n@title "sKAN^4^sTATUs · cODED bY mARX/iNSANE!"\n+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+\n\nInstallation:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nVery easy! All you need is the executable itself. Simply modify the\nBBS:Commands/BBSCmd/S.info to point to skAN^4^sTATUs.\n\n... and you''re READY TO GO!\n\n+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+\n@endnode\n\n@node THE_FUTURE\n@title "sKAN^4^sTATUs · cODED bY mARX/iNSANE!"\n+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+\n\nThe Future:\n~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nCurrently, I''m busy surviving the military service. Although I have great\nplans for this baby, that must be taken into consideration. The goal is to\nmake it independent of the traditional hardcoded design. That means that YOU\nwill be able to create design-files for it. Only your imagination will be\nyour obstacle!\n\nNow imagine yourself that YOU can design your own status-door. Cool, huh?\nWell, that''s the point! It''s existance will eliminate every need of\nalternative status-doors!\n\nIn short, I''m gonna take this baby so far...... aaaaaaaaarrrrrrrgh!\n\n+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+\n@endnode\n\n@node EPILOGUE\n@title "sKAN^4^sTATUs · cODED bY mARX/iNSANE!"\n+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+\n\nEpilogue:\n~~~~~~~~~\n\nThis is my second /X-util that I release and I hope it won''t be the last.\nIt''s a small project and I hope you find it useful and easy to use.\nIf you for any reason feel the need of contacting me (Bugs? NAH! :)) please\ndo so! I can be reached at most groovy bulletine board systems (the majority\nof them are located in Stockholm/Sweden).\nJust write me a msg at any of these:\n\n\n\n** Insanitary [iNS WHQ]         Sysop:  cLUSTER/iNS\n** Asylum     [iNS SHQ]         Sysop:  jUAN/iNS^tRSI\n\n** Flashback                    Sysop:  tWiSTeR/oGN^dCS\n** Undercover                   Sysop:  DeMaX/dLT^rYL\n** Instant Pleasure             Sysop:  nIKE/tRSI^cRZ\n\n\n\nmARX/iNSANE signing off...\n\n+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+\n@endnode\n\n@node CREDITS\n@title "sKAN^4^sTATUs · cODED bY mARX/iNSANE!"\n+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+\n\nCredits:\n~~~~~~~~\n\nCoding & Developing.................:   mARX/iNSANE\nDesign & ßeta-testing...............:   cLUSTER/iNSANE\nSuggestions, Ideas & /X Help........:   nIKE/tRSI^cRZ\n\nßeta-testers (alpha order):\n\nFlashback               (at least for a couple of hours, huh mate? ;))\nInsanitary              (as always!)\nInstant Pleasure        (sum people like to piss others off ;))\nPalladium               (curiosity killed the shark ;))\n\nsKAN^4^sTATUs was developed on a A4000/030 with 14Mb RAM and OS3.0!\n\n+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+:+\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',11895,5,0,NULL,NULL,'ins_s4s1','scan',1780048553);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ins_sb27','INS-SB27.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/INS-SB27.LHA',NULL,'XIM','kRm_____:  .______________.  :______',NULL,NULL,'INS','-_/ _/  \ _/  _______ _/  \ _/  ___/-------- \_ \_  \\\____ \_  _ \_  \\\_  _/_. iNSANE |  |  |\ |  !  |  |  |  |\ |  !  | ------',replace('kRm_____:  .______________.  :______        \n-_/ _/  \ _/  _______ _/  \ _/  ___/--------\n \_ \_  \\\____ \_  _ \_  \\\_  _/_. iNSANE \n  |  |  |\ |  !  |  |  |  |\ |  !  | ------ \n  ¦  l__|  l__   l__|  l__|  l__   |  1994  \n--:  ·--l__|--\__|--l__|--l__|--\__|--------\n[SBULL V2.7] [RELEASE 5] FROM NiGHTSHADE/iNS\nTHIS BULLETINE SYSTEM GIVE YOU MANY FEATURES\n * FASTER DISPLAYS * ONLINE UPDATED BULLS * \n * BUILT IN CFG EDITOR * STATESTICS FUNCT*  \n  * INCLUDED A RESIDENT VERSION TO RAPE *   \n','\n',char(10)),'SBull27r5.guide',replace('@database "NSDoor"\n\n@Node Main "Door"\n@Title "Manual By NiGHTSHADE                  Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n              /\       ___.                    ___.\n            _/  \____ |   |_________/\ ______ |   | _________\n            \___|    \|   \    __  /  \\_    \|   |/   _____/\n         Mb /   |     \   |\___  \/  | \|     \   /   __/ \\n           /    |   \     |   /   \  _  \   \    /    |    \\n          /     |___|\    |_______/  |___\__|\   \__________\\n     *---/______|-----\___|----/_____|--------\___|---------------*\n     |         SBull V2.7 [Release 5] Amiga-Guide manual          |\n     |     EallWare Copyright (c) 1994, 95 By NiGHTSHADE/iNS!     |\n     *------------------------------------------------------------*\n            @{" What is this Door     " Link "What"}  @{" Archive Contents      " Link "Archive"}\n            @{" What is EallWare      " Link "Eall"}  @{" Door Installations    " Link "Install"}\n            @{" Door Usages           " Link "DoorUsage"}  @{" Door History          " Link "History"}\n            @{" Door Beta Testers     " Link "Beta"}  @{" The Greetings         " Link "Greetings"}\n            @{" Contact NiGHTSHADE    " Link "ContactNS"}  @{" Other Tools from NS!  "Link "Other"}\n            @{"            - Some Sample Outputs! -            " Link "Outputs"}\n     *------------------------------------------------------------*\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "What"\n@Title "What is SBull                         Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n\n SBull are designed and developed by NiGHTSHADE/iNS to give the sysop\n maximum confort and minimum harddrive fragmention.\n\n   * Simpe to install.\n   * Built in @{"Configuration editor" Link "CFGS"} (As always :)) - No damn budget version!\n   * @{"Online bulletine update" Link "OBU"} (to shorten LONG loggoff scripts) to minimize\n     time loss and hard drive fragmention!\n   * FASTER output than /X itself!\n     Old Display Routine : 500 Displays took 67 secs.\n     New Display Routine : 500 Displays took 24 secs.\n   * 50 Posts @{"runtime history" Link "Runtime"}.\n   * @{"Statestics" Link "STATSS"} recorder (Displays stats about the door)\n   * Works like /X''s @{"internal bulls" Link "Internal"} but is nicer!\n   * Better speed than all to me known ''bullies''.\n   * Should work on ALL OS and CPU''s.\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "RunTime"\n@Title "Runtime History..                     Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n\n What is "Runtime History !?"\n============================================================================\n\n  Runtime  history  is a smart routine wich prevents a user who uses sbull\n  to  update  the same  bulletine many times in a row it would just update\n  it once the simply display the result,  this option is reseted each time\n  the door is exited.\n\n============================================================================\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "OBU"\n@Title "Online Updated Bulls..                Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n\n What is online updated bulls and how does it work !?\n============================================================================\n\n  Online  updated  bulls is a routine included in this door,  it have many\n  avantages  against  the traditional way of creating/update bulletines in\n  the Ami Express board system. The routine (if enabled) simply checks for\n  a file named Bull<no>.s if that file exists it will execute the file who\n  is supposed to create the Bull<no>.TXT or Bull<no>.TXT.GR.\n  Those  script  updated  bulletines shortens the loggoff script execution\n  time by typical 60-70% and ofcouse it also stops to much HD fragmention.\n\n============================================================================\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Internal"\n@Title "Emulates...                           Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n\n Like the internal bulls !?\n============================================================================\n\n  I have puted some efforts to "emulate" the standard way of /X to display\n  bulletines,  but you might have select or will select some option(s) who\n  makes this emulation less nice... Like the Wait For Return option...\n\n============================================================================\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Archive"\n@Title "The Archive Contents                  Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n\n This Archive should contain :\n============================================================================\nSBull27r5.020                  - The 020+ optimized version.\nSBull27r5.0x0                  - The unoptimized version for all MC680x0\nSBull27r5.020.res              - The Resident 020+ optimized version.\nSBull27r5.0x0.res              - The Resident unoptimized version for all\n                                 lovely motorolas (MC680x0)\nSmartBull27b4.guide            - Guess!\n============================================================================\n@EndNode\n\n@node "Eall"\n@Title "What is Eallware                      Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n\n What is eallware !?\n============================================================================\n\n    When you install the door you are supposed to post a eall messy with\n    the add i have included,  this is what eall ware is. I don''t want to\n    force you to do so (i can by coding it in the door but why should i)\n    so instead i hope you who is sysop on a board that you self consider\n    good and fast have atleast 1 minute to give back (post the eall msg)\n    for the hours that i have spendt making and tested this door for you\n    and they are atleast 10.. freely translated it''s 0.001666666666 % in\n    exchange.... not to much to ask for i guess.... If you don''t i might\n    don''t code more doors for you and focus my talent on other things...\n\n    If  you are a user on a board that have SBull 2.7+ installed and you\n    can''t find any Wastelads eall then the sysop consider his board LAME\n    or he is COMPLETLY IMORRAL! and don''t give a shit back to people who\n    just  tries  to  help him (like i did to born this door) and you who\n    might trade there so stop the support and support someone that don''t\n    for sure talks shit behind you''re back or abusses you''re time/money!\n\n============================================================================\n@EndNode\n\n@node "Install"\n@Title "The /X ToolTypes Information          Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n\n  - THIS PART IS TAKEN FROM THE ORGiNAL /X AMIGA GUIDE AND ARE MODIFIED -\n  =======================================================================\n  <module>.INFO        - This ICON defines a MODULE for /X. The Name of\n                         the <module> should be the same as the executing\n                         in MainMenu prompt, and should be in one of the\n                         three Directories. This icon should be placed\n                         in the BBS:Commands/BBSCmd directory.\n\n     The following directorys are placed under the <BBS Path>:Commands/\n     path.\n\n     a> BBSCmd     - Modules in this directory are allowed to be\n                     executed from any menu prompt or MCI text file.\n\n     b> SYSCmd     - Modules in this directory are only accessible by\n                     MCI text files and internal BBS operations.\n\n     c> CONF(x)    - Modules in this directory are allowed to be\n                     executed from conference (x) menu prompt or from\n                     any MCI text file in conference (x).\n     d> Node(x)    - Modules in this directory are allowed to be\n                     executed from node (x) menu prompts or from any\n                     MCI text file in Node (x).\n  - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n  The ToolTypes of the <module(s)> :\n\n  ACCESS= <numb>       - tells /X the access level required to run this\n                         module. This option is ignored for internal\n                         Module options.\n\n  INTERNAL= <command>  - Specifies if you want to have this Module the\n                         same as a internal AmiExpress command. if you\n                         choose this option you don`t need the following\n                         tool types.\n\n  LOCATION= <string>   - Specifies the path to the door.\n\n  MULTINODE=YES        - Tells /X if the module may be simultaneously\n                         accessed from other nodes, this door is multinode\n                         compatible. Options for this tool type\n                         are <YES/NO>. This is a Multinode door.\n\n  PASSWORD= <string>   - Force the user to enter password before executing\n                         this module. This option is case sensetive wich\n                         means that "OK" and "Ok" is''nt the same.\n                         If you want the ''Bulls!'' command to be protected then\n                         use this tooltype.\n\n  PRIORITY=SAME        - Let''s you set the priority of the door. If you use\n                         PRIORITY=SAME, it will use the same Priority\n                         that express uses. For best result of the door use\n                         the ''SAME'' option.\n\n  QUICKMODE            - This simply tells AmiExpress not to run the Module\n                         in question if the user has logged onto the BBS\n                         using the QUICK LOGON option.\n                         tooltype.\n\n  STACK=4096           - tells /X the stacksize to use when launching this\n                         module. Default is 4096. This door requires\n                         atleast 4096 bytes of stack.\n\n  TYPE=XIM               - tells /X which type of module it is to support:\n                         XIM = /X Standard Module, this door is a XIM door.\n\n  TRAPON               - This makes LOGON Output go to a Log for Error\n                         Checking, you don''t need this option, just\n                         fragments youre hd a lot!\n  =======================================================================\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "DoorUsage"\n@Title "Door Usage                            Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n\n How to use the SBull Door :\n============================================================================\n\n  Step 1 : Install the door (refere to the main /X manual)\n  Step 2 : Setup the bulls (See below)\n  Step 3 : Enter the door and configurate it (See below)\n  Step 4 : Ready to rock''n roll!\n\n\n\n  Step 2 How to make bulls! :\n\n     First of all you have to consider if you want to use local (conferance\n     specific bulletines) or the more exclusive global bulletines, once you\n     have decided that it''s time to create youre bulletine(s).\n\n     For local bulletines :\n\n      First create a directory named : {confpath}/Bulletins this directory\n      is  where  the door will search for bulletine''s/scripts and even for\n      the menu file (please make a real nice one so they dont think i have\n      designed it :)).\n      All  of  the below files in this local install instruction should be\n      placed in this directory ({confpath}/Bulletins).\n\n      Secound create youre bulletine menu file (named ''BullHelp.TXT'') this\n      txt file will be displayed each time the door is executed and if the\n      user enters ''?''.\n\n      The third step is to create the bulletine scripts(if you want them!)\n      and they should be labeled ''BULL<no!>.s'' and this script file should\n      create the bulletine ''BULL<no!>.(txt||txt.gr).\n      The alternative for this option is to let the loggoff scripts create\n      all the bulletine''s, but  keep in  mind that some of the bulletine''s\n      have to be created from there like updating Last Callers for example\n\n     For GLOBAL bulletines :\n\n      First create a directory labeled {BBSPATH}/Bulletins, this directory\n      is  where  the door will search for bulletine''s/scripts and even for\n      the menu file (please make a real nice one so they dont think i have\n      designed it :)).\n      All  of the below files in this global install instruction should be\n      placed in this directory {BBSpath}/Bulletins (Normaly BBS: i Guess)\n\n      Secound create youre bulletine menu file (named ''BullHelp.TXT'') this\n      txt file will be displayed each time the door is executed and if the\n      user enters ''?''.\n\n      The third step is to create the bulletine scripts(if you want them!)\n      and they should be labeled ''BULL<no!>.s'' and this script file should\n      create the bulletine ''BULL<no!>.(txt||txt.gr).\n      The alternative for this option is to let the loggoff scripts create\n      all the bulletine''s, but  keep in  mind that some of the bulletine''s\n      have to be created from there like updating Last Callers for example\n\n\n  Step 3 How to configure :\n\n\n    * IF YOU USED A OLD VERSION SBULL THEN DELETE THE DATA FILE \n      OR I CANT TAKE THE RESPONCIBILITY OF WHAT COULD HAPPEN!\n    If you run it the first time then the CFG will appear direct (if you have\n    the exact sysop name). \n    Enter the door and press ''C'' (not shown on the prompt!) then\n    the configuration  menu will appear (if you have the master\n    sysop name!), here are the menu commands :\n\n.---------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n|        SBULL V2.7 [RELEASE 5] CONFIG Jan 28 1995 BY NiGHTSHADE/InS        |\n+-------------------------------------.-------------------------------------+\n|@{" [B]ulletine type              [GLO] " Link "BullT"}|@{" [C]lear Screen on new bull    [YES] " Link "Cls"}|\n|@{" [F]ast Ansi Output (By Ansi)  [YES] " Link "FaAsi"}|@{" [L]ocal Usage Counter         [YES] " Link "LUC"}|\n|@{" [U]pdated Script Bulls        [YES] " Link "USB"}|@{" [W]ait for return             [NO!] " Link "WFR"}|\n|@{" [R]outine for display         [NS!] " Link "RFD"}|@{" [V]iew status (Alow user)     [YES] " Link "VS"}|\n+-------------------------------------+-------------------------------------+\n|@{" [S]ave Config And Exit              " Link "SCAE"}|@{" [D]efault Config Profile            " Link "DCP"}|\n|@{" [P]rompt Change (When Wait is on)   " Link "PC"}|@{" [Q]uit Without Save                 " Link "QWS"}|\n`-------------------------------------^-------------------------------------''\n\n[@{"                DISPLAYS ALL OF THE ABOVE CONFIGS IN A ROW!                " Link "ALL"}]\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "BullT"\n@Title "Door Usage                            Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n============================================================================\n\n       [B]ulletine type            - The bulltine type to use in this conf\n                                     there are 3 types   (Default = DIS) :\n                                                      [DIS] Disabled\n                                                      [GLO] Global Bulls\n                                                      [LOC] Locale bulls\n\n============================================================================\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Cls"\n@Title "Door Usage                            Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n============================================================================\n\n       [C]lear Screen on new bull  - Should the door clears screens when a\n                                     new bulletine shows up(Default : YES)\n\n============================================================================\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "FaAsi"\n@Title "Door Usage                            Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n============================================================================\n\n       [F]ast Ansi Output          - Should  the  door send a special ansi\n                                     sequence  to  disable  the cursor and\n                                     save lots of blitts-.. Not recomended\n                                     in a PC conf.         (Default : No!)\n\n============================================================================\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "LUC"\n@Title "Door Usage                            Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n============================================================================\n\n       [L]ocal Usage Counter       - Enables  the statestics,   this is''nt\n                                     100%  implented  yet  but in the next\n                                     version.              (Default : Yes)\n\n============================================================================\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "USB"\n@Title "Door Usage                            Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n============================================================================\n\n       [U]pdated Script Bulls      - Allow .s scripts to be executed,   if\n                                     this  options  is''nt enabled the good\n                                     benefits  from onlline udates will be\n                                     all washed away....   (Default is On)\n\n============================================================================\n@EndNode\n\n\n@Node "WFR"\n@Title "Door Usage                            Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n============================================================================\n\n       [W]ait for return           - Should the user press ''RETURN!'' after\n                                     each bulletine he/she displays  (this\n                                     options prompt is designable -  Check\n                                     opt. ''p''             (Default is OFF)\n\n============================================================================\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "RFD"\n@Title "Door Usage                            Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n============================================================================\n\n       [R]outine for display       - Allows you to change the display type\n                                     this door should use, the SLOW /X org\n                                     or the fast Nightshade version.\n\n============================================================================\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "VS"\n@Title "Door Usage                            Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n============================================================================\n\n       [V]iew status (Alow user)   - If  you  want the users to be able to\n                                     display  the  status screen where the\n                                     various door stats is displayed.\n\n============================================================================\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "SCAE"\n@Title "Door Usage                            Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n============================================================================\n\n       [S]ave Config And Exit      - Saves the door configuration and quit\n\n============================================================================\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "DCP"\n@Title "Door Usage                            Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n============================================================================\n\n       [D]efault Config Profile    - Return to the standard config profile\n\n============================================================================\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "PC"\n@Title "Door Usage                            Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n============================================================================\n\n       [P]rompt Change             - Changes the prompt in the ''w'' option!\n\n============================================================================\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "QWS"\n@Title "Door Usage                            Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n============================================================================\n\n       [Q]uit Without Save!        - Quits the door without saving the CFG\n\n============================================================================\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "ALL"\n@Title "All Config Options                    Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n\n============================================================================\n\n       [B]ulletine type            - The bulltine type to use in this conf\n                                     there are 3 types   (Default = DIS) :\n                                                      [DIS] Disabled\n                                                      [GLO] Global Bulls\n                                                      [LOC] Locale bulls\n\n============================================================================\n\n       [C]lear Screen on new bull  - Should the door clears screens when a\n                                     new bulletine shows up(Default : YES)\n\n============================================================================\n\n       [F]ast Ansi Output          - Should  the  door send a special ansi\n                                     sequence  to  disable  the cursor and\n                                     save lots of blitts-.. Not recomended\n                                     in a PC conf.         (Default : No!)\n\n============================================================================\n\n       [L]ocal Usage Counter       - Enables  the statestics,   this is''nt\n                                     100%  implented  yet  but in the next\n                                     version.              (Default : Yes)\n\n============================================================================\n\n       [U]pdated Script Bulls      - Allow .s scripts to be executed,   if\n                                     this  options  is''nt enabled the good\n                                     benefits  from onlline udates will be\n                                     all washed away....   (Default is On)\n\n============================================================================\n\n       [W]ait for return           - Should the user press ''RETURN!'' after\n                                     each bulletine he/she displays  (this\n                                     options prompt is designable -  Check\n                                     opt. ''p''             (Default is OFF)\n\n============================================================================\n\n       [R]outine for display       - Allows you to change the display type\n                                     this door should use, the SLOW /X org\n                                     or the fast Nightshade version.\n\n============================================================================\n\n       [V]iew status (Alow user)   - If  you  want the users to be able to\n                                     display  the  status screen where the\n                                     various door stats is displayed.\n\n============================================================================\n\n       [S]ave Config And Exit      - Saves the door configuration and quit\n\n============================================================================\n\n       [D]efault Config Profile    - Return to the standard config profile\n\n============================================================================\n\n       [P]rompt Change             - Changes the prompt in the ''w'' option!\n\n============================================================================\n\n       [Q]uit Without Save!        - Quits the door without saving the CFG\n\n============================================================================\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "History"\n@Title "Smart Bull History                    Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n\n  Program History - Changes / New features\n============================================================================\n\n   V1.0 b1 - NiGHTSHADE (??-???-??) No Public Version\n              * Wrote the first version who was as configurable as\n                a rock just for my own board (Wastelands) without\n                the powerfull ''Auto Update'' script executer.\n\n   V1.1 b1 - NiGHTSHADE (??-???-??) No Public Version\n              * Rewrote the whole thing.\n              * Added the ''Global'' mode.\n\n   V1.2 r1 - NiGHTSHADE (??-???-??) [Release 1]\n              * Added a faster output routine for slightly speedup.\n              * Fixed some ansi buggs.\n\n   V1.5 b1 - NiGHTSHADE (??-???-??) No Public Version\n              * Rewrote *MUCH* (I guess 70%) of the code.\n              * Optimized a little.\n\n   V1.7 r2 - NiGHTSHADE (??-???-??) [Release 2]\n              * Made it to Emulate the ''B'' command as good as\n                possible (Thanx to Dansken for the idea!).\n\n   V2.0 r3 - NiGHTSHADE (??-???-??) [Release 3]\n              * Rewrote Aprox. 30% of the code.\n              * Optimized even more. (From 7 KB to 3.9 KB with my new\n                way to code /X doors using new startupcode ect.\n\n   V2.1 b1 - NiGHTSHADE (21-Jul-94) No Public Version\n              * Fixed the 50 last used bulls so the door woun''t    [21-Jul-94]\n                auto-update a bull twice untill exited.            [21-Jul-94]\n\n   V2.2 b1 - NiGHTSHADE (12-Aug-94) No Public Version\n              * Optimized a little.                                [09-Aug-94]\n              * Changed some ansi.                                 [12-Aug-94]\n\n   V2.3 r4 - NiGHTSHADE (04-Dec-94) [Release 4]\n              * Rewrote the 50 last.                               [01-Dec-94]\n              * Rewrote the file check for LO/GL mode.             [03-Dec-94]\n\n   V2.4 b1 - NiGHTSHADE (07-Dec-94) No Public Version\n              * Added a simple CFG part.                           [07-Dec-94]\n              * Added configurable cls.                            [07-Dec-94]\n\n   V2.5 b1- NiGHTSHADE (02-Jan-95) No Public Version\n              * Recovered after new year!                          [01-Jan-95]\n              * Hates the Version Steps!                           [01-Jan-95]\n              * Added the FAST ansi.                               [02-Jan-95]\n              * Improved cfg save/load routines.                   [02-Jan-95]\n              * Better Door startup.                               [02-Jan-95]\n\n   V2.6 b1 - NiGHTSHADE (07-Jan-95) No Public Version\n              * Fixed a minibugg, it wound dispaly bull 8!         [07-Jan-95]\n                (Thanx to Distler/ISDN for the bugg report)        [07-Jan-95]\n\n   V2.7 b1 - NiGHTSHADE (20-Jan-95) No Public Version.\n              * Rewrote much code to make it more flexible.        [18-Jan-95]\n              * Added the BULL type for each conf.                 [19-Jan-95]\n              * Added the Script update in the config.             [19-Jan-95]\n              * Added the wait for return option(cfg!).            [19-Jan-95]\n              * Added the possibility to change the wait for       [20-Jan-95]\n                return prompt.                                     [20-Jan-95]\n              * Changed the name of the door to ''SBULL'' sounds     [20-Jan-95]\n                nicer i guess.                                     [20-Jan-95]\n\n   V2.7 b2 - NiGHTSHADE (22-Jan-95) No Public Version\n              * Fixed some layouts in the CFG part.                [22-Jan-95]\n              * Changed the type of bullread                       [22-Jan-95]\n\n   V2.7 b3 - NiGHTSHADE (24-Jan-95) No Public Version\n              * Added and fixed some of the CFG stuff              [24-Jan-95]\n\n   V2.7 b4 - NiGHTSHADE (26-Jan-95) Nu Public Version (But soon!)\n              * Coded a internal display command (_FASTER_) than   [26-Jan-95]\n                than /X''s intrenal due to the fact that /X check   [26-Jan-95]\n                for GR/TXT in a stupid way! (The way many other    [26-Jan-95]\n                doors uses (due to lazyness))                      [26-Jan-95]\n              * Added line counter in the new view mode            [26-Jan-95]\n                (thanx to Ezco for the report)                     [26-Jan-95]\n              * Tested the display routines under the exact same   [26-Jan-95]\n                system and i was happy to se the results :         [26-Jan-95]\n                Old Display Routine : 500 Displays took 67 secs.   [26-Jan-95]\n                New Display Routine : 500 Displays took 24 secs.   [26-Jan-95]\n              * Added the display routine modes in the cfg         [26-Jan-95]\n              * Added the screen mode in use to the status line.   [26-Jan-95]\n              * Finally fixed the statestics function.             [26-Jan-95]\n              * Added a config switch for the stats function       [26-Jan-95]\n                (Thanx to Spider for the idea!)                    [26-Jan-95]\n\n   V2.7 R5 - NiGHTSHADE (28-Jan-95) Release 5 (Time : 05:20 ARGH!) \n              * Fixed a ''bugg'' in the new display routine, the     [28-Jan-95]\n                display looks nice localy but not through          [28-Jan-95]\n                the serial.. Forgotten that /X needs both CR/LF    [28-Jan-95]\n                Thanx to TBB for the report!                       [28-Jan-95]\n              * Tested it by null modem (the board was down 1 hr!) [28-Jan-95]\n              * Decided to create a new type of ware like          [28-Jan-95]\n                free ware, shareware ect... This tool goes under   [28-Jan-95]\n                EALL ware... it means if you use it and have a     [28-Jan-95]\n                good board then you should post my add as EALL!    [28-Jan-95]\n              * Added some simple ansi in the Status screen        [28-Jan-95]\n              * Added some other infos in the Status screen        [28-Jan-95]\n              * Fixed resident datas                               [28-Jan-95]\n              * Changed the startup routine slightly, can now      [28-Jan-95]\n                handles up to 255 nodes.                           [28-Jan-95]\n              * Tested everything with enforcer active - No hits   [28-Jan-95]\n              * No buggs reported for my beta crew and i have''nt   [28-Jan-95]\n                found anny myself under my hard testings           [28-Jan-95]\n              * Yet another litre of coffe (soon i might will take [28-Jan-95]\n                a half kg of coffe for registration :))            [28-Jan-95]\n\n   Vx.x xx - Future enchantments (??-???-??)\n              * Better layout.\n              * Cursor support if anyone would like it!\n \n============================================================================\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Beta"\n@Title "The cool Beta crew!                   Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n\n.---------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n|      OFFICIAL BETA SITES LIST FOR THE NIGHTSHADE /X DOORS/TOOLS           |\n+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| HALL OF FAME      +46-910-26665    DANSKEN/ACCESS          USR 28800 EVT. |\n| NAPALM            +46-8-894595     BLAST/SSP               ACX 28800 VFC  |\n| SERPENT HILL      +46-8-FIND IT    ECZO/TRIS^DPL         2*USR 28800 EVT. |\n| TWISTED SOCIETY   +46-44-106144    TBB/iNFLECT             USR 21600 DS   |\n| UNDERGROUND       +46-16-424911    ViKiNG/iNDEPENDENT      USR 21600 DS   |\n+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|  PLEASE GIVE THOOSE DUDES A CALL - THEY ARE REALLY AWESOME IN MANY WAYS!  |\n`---------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "ContactNS"\n@Title "Contact NiGHTSHADE                    Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n\n___/\  _______________________________________________________________ _\n  /  \/\\n /   /  \        \\\\\\\                  [×] THE PLACE THAT ROCKS [*]\n \ PARTY \       |^ ^  \\\n  ON DUDE/      _|_ ___  |          \          {+} WASTELANDS {-}\n   \/\  /      (o(.Y.)   o)         _\__\n      \/       /(__) ^  \\         (__''_)     [] STAFF ROOSTER! []\n              (______/   ))_      _|_cOl|\n              //\ `-''   //  \   _/ __)-(_)       NiGHTSHADE/iNS\n             ((  \  _  //    \ /\  |---(_)         cASE/dCS!\n             /\\  \___//      Y  \ `---(_)\n  ____ ____ /  \\   |// ___ . `   \/\n / __ |    Y    \\__// |___||     /           FAST AMIGA & CONSOLE\n/ /(__|    '' .   (__)  |   ||\___/         [WHY NUP - LAMERS DEL''ED!]\n\_)   |______|      o  `---''|\n             |      ¦       |              NoDe #1 +46(8)157472 28k8!\n             |      °       |                   #2 cOMMINg sOOn!\n             |              |\n_ _______________________________________________________________/\  ___\n                                                               - --\/\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Greetings"\n@Title "The good things...                    Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n\n MY GREETINGS MUST GO TO (A-Z ORDER) :\n============================================================================\n\n  * ANTISOCIAL                  - HOPE INSPERATIONS ARE GAINING LEVELS!\n  * BENNY                       - GOOD''OL FRIENDS OF MiNE!\n  * BOBO                        - RUNNING LOW ON IDEAS !?\n  * BLAST                       - KEEP CODING AND YOU WILL KILL US :))\n  * CENTURION/PREMIERE          - FASTEST IN EUROPE !?\n  * CLUSTER/INS                 - INSANE IN THE BRAIN :)\n  * CASE/DCS!                   - MY KiLLING CO-RAVER!\n  * CYCLONE                     - KEEP LEECHING DUDE!\n  * DANSKEN/ACS                 - SKELLEFTEA''S MANIAC NO.1!\n  * DANZIG                      - YOURE ASCII ARE GOOD!\n  * DISTLER                     - AT THE DAMN MILITARY SERVICE.\n                                  HOPE THAT YOU WILL GET BACK IN ST!\n                                  DAMN LAME TO LOCK YOU OUT I THINK (AND\n                                  MANY ONES WITH ME - ST ON THE LOOSE!)\n  * EVERSLICK                   - NO TRADING NO MORE !?\n  * EZCO                        - WORKING HARD I GUESS !?\n  * GAZ                         - GOOD CONSOLE SUPPORT M8!\n  * ICON                        - NO CONSOLE SPEED!?\n  * JADE                        - HAVE YOU DIED !?\n  * LIGHTSPEED TECH.            - GUESS ? - FOR /X OFCOUSE.\n  * LINEBACKER                  - I WILL CALL ''THE MANSION'' SOME DAY AGAIN!\n  * LOOBY/INS                   - PROGRAMING MANIAC.\n  * MARX                        - NiGHT CHATTER NO.1.\n  * METAL/INS                   - CODES A LOT (NO RESULT ??)\n  * MR.COKE                     - KEEP CODING MY ''MINI-INTRO''. ZZZZZZ...\n  * NECROPHILIAC                - CHAT YOU AS ALWAYS!\n  * NECRONOMICON                - HOPFULLY WITH WORKING HD !\n  * PRINCIP/INS^CLS!?           - HELP WITH MODEMS AGAIN :)\n  * RAD                         - TO BAD YOU KILLED ''MEGA LO MANIA''!\n  * SAVAGE                      - GOOD SUPPORTER!\n  * SHAPECHANGER                - REAL GOOD ASCII...\n  * SHOCKER                     - ALWAYS MANY REQUESTS!\n  * SNIPER                      - HAVE YOU DIED SINCE THE FEKKE!\n  * SPIDER                      - KILLES MY SPARE TIME!\n  * TBB/INFEKT                  - MY BEST BETA TESTER!\n  * vIETCONg                    - STILL PROBBS WITH THE CPS !?\n  * WARHAMMES                   - NO SPEED FOR ME AT YOURE BOARD!\n  * WARLOCK                     - FOR BORROWING THIS COMPUTER.\n  * WESTBAM                     - KiLLING TRADER\n  * XCLUZIWE/DD·STYLE^XWR       - THANX FOR THE ''BETA'' LOGGO!\n  * ZANOK                       - ONE DAY BACK I HOPE!\n\n============================================================================\n\n I know i have forgotten a dozzen or 2 and i''m terribe sorry for that.\n\n============================================================================\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Other"\n@Title "Other tools i have made for you       Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n              /\       ___.                    ___.\n            _/  \____ |   |_________/\ ______ |   | _________\n            \___|    \|   \    __  /  \\_    \|   |/   _____/\n         Mb /   |     \   |\___  \/  | \|     \   /   __/ \\n           /    |   \     |   /   \  _  \   \    /    |    \\n          /     |___|\    |_______/  |___\__|\   \__________\\n    *>---/______|-----\___|----/_____|--------\___|---------------<*\n\n    AmiExpress Proffesional Doors Available To You From NiGHTSHADE!\n\n«········································································»\n\n  [Cool Wall]\n\n   Cool Wall are designed and developed to give the user a chanse to\n   type a comment so the next user(s) can read it and type a comment\n   to,  i have seen walls on other boards but they are offen slow or\n   have sick design.\n\n    * Fast and Nice.\n    * Built in, Simple to use Configuration Editor & Data reseter.\n    * Fast Statestics function. (Writed how many times).\n    * Better speed than all to me known ''walls''.\n    * Works on ALL OS and CPU''s (If not - Contact me).\n\n«········································································»\n\n  [MComment ]\n\n   MComment is a replacement for borring built in ''C'' command,\n   it gives you the following avantages :\n\n    * Up to 6 (or 8) Sysops/Cosysops in the ''C'' menu.\n    * Built in, Simple to use Configuration Editor.\n    * Cool & Fast Statestics function. (Ohh just 2 mails in 240 days?! :))\n    * Better preformance than all to me known ''C'' replacers.\n    * Works on ALL OS and CPU''s (If not - Contact me).\n\n«········································································»\n\n  [Smart DSF] \n\n   SmartDSF is a replacement for the ''DS'' command,\n   it gives you the following avantages :\n\n    * Requester selected files (multiple if wanted!).\n    * Uses ASL because everybody have it (and if you\n      like the REQTools.library better, my guesses are\n      that you have patched the ASL.library).\n    * If a file was unsuccefully downloaded the door asks\n      if you want to try again, continue with the next or\n      abort the zmodem batch transfer. (According to my\n      knowledge NO ''DS'' door offers this, not even\n      Ami Express itself!).\n    * Displays all files and there sizes before sent.\n    * Estimates the transfer time in secounds.\n    * 680x0+ and a 68020+ optimized version included.\n    * Better preformance than all to me known ''DS'' replacers.\n    * Works on ALL OS and CPU''s (If not - Contact me). \n\n«········································································»\n\n   [Smart Show]\n\n    SmartShow is a door developed to display a TXT file eg.\n    like a door list or a member list for a group.\n    it will bring the following to youre system :\n\n     * Simple configurator (Just use from CLI!).\n     * Request selector for the TXT file to show.\n     * Fast Statestics function (Displays No. of usages).\n     * Reliable & Fast.\n     * Works on ALL OS and CPU''s (If not - Contact me).\n\n«········································································»\n\n   [Status Scan]\n\n    Status Scan is a replacement for the ''S'' command i have seen\n    to many ones who are SLOW or have bad design and decided to\n    code one my self (to easy indeead but who cares !?) when the\n    result stops at 2.7 KB (When others might take up to 10 KB?)\n\n     * __FAST__\n     * Nice\n     * Reliable\n     * Small.\n\n«········································································»\n\n   [Youre idea !?]\n\n    Dial me and well can chat about them!\n\n«········································································»\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Outputs"\n@Title "Some Sample Outputs                   Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n\n Take a look at the below screen shots without colour (The dude is CRAZY :)\n============================================================================\n\n                       @{"  The Main Screen        " Link "MAINS"}\n                       @{"  The Config Screen      " Link "CFGS"}\n                       @{"  The Statestics Screen  " Link "STATSS"}\n\n============================================================================\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "MAINS"\n@Title "MainScreen Sample                     Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n                    __________\n      _ _ __________\___     /_  _______    _______     __________ _ _\n       \\\\_____._     /    /  \/      /___/      /____/   ______////\n           /    |/   _/    /    \     /    \     /    \______   \\n         _/     |\    \_  /      \_  /      \_  /      \_   /    \_\n.-----uMn\_____________/__________/__________/__________/_________/aC!------.\n|                                                                           |\n| [o1] LAST 10 VERY HAPPY USERS!              [o2] USERS LIST               |\n| [o3] TOP BYTE UPLOADERS                     [o4] TOP BYTE LEECHERS        |\n| [o5] TOP FILE UPLOADERS                     [o6] TOP FILE LEECHERS        |\n| [o7] TOP MSGS WRITERS                       [o8] THE WEEKLY STATESTICS    |\n| [o9] THE SYSTEM RECORDS!                                                  |\n|                                                                           |\n ---------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n[SBULL V2.7] [RELEASE 5] BY NiGHTSHADE/iNS      DiAL WASTELANDS [+46(8)157472]\nWhich Bulletin (?)=List, (S)=Status, (Enter)=none?\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "CFGS"\n@Title "Config Screen Sample                  Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n\n\n.---------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n|        SBULL V2.7 [RELEASE 5] CONFIG Jan 28 1995 BY NiGHTSHADE/InS        |\n+-------------------------------------.-------------------------------------+\n|@{" [B]ulletine type              [GLO] " Link "BullT"}|@{" [C]lear Screen on new bull    [YES] " Link "Cls"}|\n|@{" [F]ast Ansi Output (By Ansi)  [YES] " Link "FaAsi"}|@{" [L]ocal Usage Counter         [YES] " Link "LUC"}|\n|@{" [U]pdated Script Bulls        [YES] " Link "USB"}|@{" [W]ait for return             [NO!] " Link "WFR"}|\n|@{" [R]outine for display         [NS!] " Link "RFD"}|@{" [V]iew status (Alow user)     [YES] " Link "VS"}|\n+-------------------------------------+-------------------------------------+\n|@{" [S]ave Config And Exit              " Link "SCAE"}|@{" [D]efault Config Profile            " Link "DCP"}|\n|@{" [P]rompt Change (When Wait is on)   " Link "PC"}|@{" [Q]uit Without Save                 " Link "QWS"}|\n`-------------------------------------^-------------------------------------''\n\n[@{"                DISPLAYS ALL OF THE ABOVE CONFIGS IN A ROW!                " Link "ALL"}]\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "STATSS"\n@Title "Statestics Screen Sample              Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n\n\n                      .------------------------------.\n [CoDING NiGHTSHADE]  | SBULL V2.7 [RELEASE 5] STATS |  [!MY BETA TESTERS!]\n                      |------------------------------|\n [DESIGN NiGHTSHADE]  | Total door usages : 00000074 |  [.......TBB/iNFECT]\n [......DANSKEN/ACS]  | Total bull disps  : 00000169 |  [......DiSTLER/HNY]\n [........METAL/iNS]  | Total CLI updates : 00000042 |  [......DANSKEN/ACS]\n [.......TBB/iNFECT]  |------------------------------|  [........BLAST/SSP]\n [.PLAYBOY MAGAZINE]  |  [WASTELANDS [+46-8-157472]  |  [...........VIKING]\n                      `------------------------------''\n\n\n[SBULL V2.7] [RELEASE 5] BY NiGHTSHADE/iNS      DiAL WASTELANDS [+46(8)157472]\nWhich Bulletin (?)=List, (S)=Status, (Enter)=none?\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Hidden"\n@Title "The hidden part                       Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n\n Woow... youre a hacker, you have found the hidden part in this manual..\n feel proud and take a extra beer next time at the pub/disco!\n\n@EndNode\n','\n',char(10)),'{"ACCESS":"<numb>","LOCATION":"<string>","PRIORITY":"SAME","STACK":"4096","TYPE":"XIM"}',NULL,56718,6,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048553);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ins_sd13','INS-SD13.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/INS-SD13.LHA',NULL,'XIM','kRm_____:  .______________.  :______',NULL,'ZOLTRIX','INS','-_/ _/  \ _/  _______ _/  \ _/  ___/-------- \_ \_  \\\____ \_  _ \_  \\\_  _/_. iNSANE |  |  |\ |  !  |  |  |  |\ |  !  | ------',replace('kRm_____:  .______________.  :______\n-_/ _/  \ _/  _______ _/  \ _/  ___/--------\n \_ \_  \\\____ \_  _ \_  \\\_  _/_. iNSANE\n  |  |  |\ |  !  |  |  |  |\ |  !  | ------\n  ¦  l__|  l__   l__|  l__|  l__   |  1995\n.-:  ·--l__|--\__|--l__|--l__|--\__|-------.\n| NiGHTSHADE BRINGS SMART-DSF V1.3 /X DOOR |\n| WHO IS A COMPLEMENT TO THE ''DS'' COMMAND! |\n| FEATURE : REQ SELECTION, Z-RESUME & MORE |\n|   ** LOOK AT THIS DOOR OR LOOSE IT! **   |\n`------------------------------------------''\nIMPORTED BY ZOLTRIX TRD/LSD/PFL/976/HF/ACS','\n',char(10)),'SmartDSF.guide',replace('@DataBase "SmartDSF"\n@Author "Nightshade & Cluster"\n@Node Main "SmartDSF"\n@Title "SmartDSF Amiga-Guide Manual            Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n              /\       ___.                    ___.\n            _/  \____ |   |_________/\ ______ |   | _________\n            \___|    \|   \    __  /  \\_    \|   |/   _____/\n         Mb /   |     \   |\___  \/  | \|     \   /   __/ \\n           /    |   \     |   /   \  _  \   \    /    |    \\n          /     |___|\    |_______/  |___\__|\   \__________\\n     *---/______|-----\___|----/_____|--------\___|---------------*\n     |  SmartDSF V1.3 Copyright (c) 1995 By NiGHTSHADE of INSANE  |\n     |         Amiga-Guide Documentation By NiGHTSHADE & CLUSTER  |\n     *------------------------------------------------------------*\n\n                         @{" What is SmartDSF     " Link "What"}\n                         @{" Archive Contents     " Link "Archive"}\n                         @{" Program Usage        " Link "Usage"}\n                         @{" Program History      " Link "History"}\n                         @{" Program Beta Testers " Link "Beta"}\n                         @{" My Greetings         " Link "Greetings"}\n                         @{" Contact NiGHTSHADE   " Link "ContactNS"}\n\n===========================================================================\n@EndNode\n\n\n\n@Node "What"\n@Title "What is SmartDSF                      Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n===========================================================================\n\n SmartDSF is a replacement for the ''DS'' command,\n it gives you the following advantages :\n\n   * Uses Requester when choosing files (multiple if wanted!).\n\n   * Uses the ASL Library because of the standard.\n     (for those of you who likes the REQTools Requesters better,\n     my guesses are that you''ve allready patched the ASL.library).\n\n   * If a file was unsuccessfully downloaded the door asks\n     if you wish to try again, continue with the next file or\n     abort the zmodem batch transfer. (According to my knowledge,\n     NO ''DS'' door offers this, not even AmiExpress itself!).\n\n   * Displays all tagged files and their sizes before transfer.\n\n   * Estimated time calculation included and will be shown in Mins & Secs.\n\n   * 680x0 -> 68040 optimized versions included.\n\n   * Resident code version also available for the sysops with lotsa memory.\n\n   * Better performance than all so far known ''DS'' replacments.\n\n   * Works on ALL OS (Even old 1.3) and CPU''s.\n\n===========================================================================\n@EndNode\n\n\n\n@Node "Usage"\n@Title "How to use SmartDSF                   Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n===========================================================================\n\n Consult the /X main manual when you install this door.\n ======================================================\n\n *DO NOT* forget to include the PASSWORD=<PASS> tooltype in your DS icon\n or else all users will have access to the door and could accidently hang\n your board.\n\n I have included a sample icon, where you just have to adjust the path and\n the password tooltype to get it all setup.  (NOTE: pw is cAsE sensitive!)\n\n===========================================================================\n@EndNode\n\n\n\n@Node "History"\n@Title "SmartDSF History                      Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n===========================================================================\n\n   Program History - Changes / New features\n   ========================================\n\n   V1.0   - NiGHTSHADE (02-Dec-94) No Public Version\n   =================================================\n             * Wrote the first version who only had the\n               simple req-send options.\n\n\n   V1.2b1 - NiGHTSHADE (03-Dec-94) Beta 1\n   =================================================\n             * Added the displaying of files before transfer.\n             * Added the continue/abort option if transfer failed.\n             * Added the retry option if transfer failed.\n             * Added the Est. Transfertime calc. shown before filetransfers.\n             * Layout Improvements.\n\n   V1.3r2 - NIGHTSHADE (07 May 1995) Release\n   =================================================\n             * Changed the layout of the program.\n             * CPS Calculator added.\n             * Added Est. Transfertime calculation in mins & secs.\n             * Speedup of the filecounter with approx 20%.\n\n\n   Vx.x   - Future enchantments (??-???-??)\n   ========================================\n             * Requester On/Off Configuration.\n             * Statistics function.\n             * Own password handler.\n             * Byte deductor (For the files/bytes)\n               if the sysop wants to!\n             * Log DS actions routines.\n             * Faster display routines.\n\n===========================================================================\n@EndNode\n\n\n\n@Node "Beta"\n@Title "The cool Beta crew!                   Dia