      :eXON/rIOT^jORMAS · gHANDY/gODS · rAHIEM/eSSENCE · cELIC/rEKTUM: \n      `------.                                                .------''\n             `------------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',19383,6,0,NULL,NULL,'lsd_aec1','scan',1780048575);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('lsd_aer','LSD-AER.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/LSD-AER.LHA','aereg106','XIM','aereg106',NULL,NULL,'LSD','\_/  \_-Sd\_/~  ______/  \_  ¬\_\__\\ |:   7____|_____   ¬|:   |   ·7 |!   |~  ¬|~  ¬|   !|·   |   !| pRESENTS',replace('_¦_/\     _____________/\_____ :___ __ _ _\n\_/  \_-Sd\_/~  ______/  \_  ¬\_\__\\\n |:   7____|_____   ¬|:   |   ·7\n |!   |~  ¬|~  ¬|   !|·   |   !| pRESENTS\n l_____    :|_________|.   _____;_________\n  ¦    `----''         `----''    ¦\nAE-Register v1.06-Now Can re-registers all\nnew /X version of /X4.x(tested to /X4.3)\n','\n',char(10)),'aereg106.doc',replace('      Read All About It On....\n\n          ____    __     __     _  __    ____  _____\n         /       /      /      /  /     / __  /\n        / _/    /  __  / _\   /        / __    /\n       /       /      /   /  /  \     /       /\n      /\n                       ___________\n                      /               Sysop: John Yaya\n                        \     /       1-414-964-7434   \n                         \   /        Ami-X Latest (REG.)\n                          >           AMIGA CONSOLE DOCS H/P\n                         /   \        USR DS 21.6''s\n                       _/ ____\ _     3 NODES RINGDOWN\n                      /               LSD USHQ\n*****************************************************************************\n\n\n                           -¿- LSd Presents -¿-\n\n                     AERegister (Public) Version 1.06\n                       Written & Updated by mUB/LSD!\n\n\nRelease Notes:\n--------------\n\nThis tool is an update to the original (and the best!) Ami-Express automatic\nre-registering tool. This latest version can re-register ALL versions of\nAmi-Express from /X3.3 through to /X4.x (Tested upto /X4.3). Therefore this\ntool will allow you to register any version you can find within this version\nspan...\n\nIt works by scanning through the Ami-Express code dissassembling and seeking \nout and removing all ''known'' Ami-Express registration techniques. It does this\nhowever in an ''intellegent'' way in that it is not restricted to one single \nversion of /X. It does not take into account version dependant ''global'' data \nreferences and so continues to work right across the spectrum of releases of \nAmi-Express`s... even the beta testing versions!\n\nThis release is long in coming because we where not even going to release it\nagain (see below for reasons why!) but after the complete BOTCH of everyone\nelses crack attempts at /X3.x we decided to do the right thing and release it\nonce again for the world to use. Too many nerving stories of ''backdoor'' fucked\nversions.. use this, grab a copy from a friend (if you can manage get it from\nsomeone who has registered?? A harder job that cracking it .. hehe ).. and be \nsafe..\n\n\n\nWhy Release it so late?\n-----------------------\n\nWell its been released so late because firstly we could not originally even\nbe bothered to waste five minutes with a disk-monitor. When we seen how shit\nit was we thoughed.. "What the FU%^ is this??" To be honest I thoughed it was\na fake........ my quote ''You gotta be kidding.. is this the /X4.x that you`ve\ngotta pay $55 for an update to?? Please tell me your WINDING ME UP?????????''\nI wouldn`t pay one dime..\n\nI think calling this minor update ''Version 4.x'' is a complete JOKE! The code\nis still laced with bugs, badly implemented ideas, awful code and pathetic\ncoding practices (the "goto`s" in the source are great for readability.. NOT!)\nOkay lets look at what you get for your money...\n\n1.	HYDRA.. (well fuck me .. this bi-directional protocol is in the PD \n(the Complete fucking source to it!) All that was needed was for the /X \ncoders to change the logfile output so that /X kept track of the file\ntransfers (oh.. and changing 1 line to make the thing open in serial shared\nmode... ) How difficult..(NOT!) must have taken them all of 5 mins, then\nwhat goes and happens to the executable size?? It storms over the 300k\nbarrier and ends up fucking 320k.. WHAT A JOKE.. Why did they not implement\nHydra as a external module? Just using a Semaphore to pass information\nbetween each other?? Ah well...\n\n2.	QWK-MAIL REPLIES.. This should have been implemented when they 1st\nadded QWK-Downloading.. again. boy this is hard stuff.. (NOT) QWK is pretty\nlame anyway...\n\n3.	TEXT-CONFIGURATION.. hahahahahahahahaha How very pathetic they are...\nReverting back to /X2.x style configuration because their icon system is\nso great (wonder why?? Icons are just so really cool and fast so why should \nthey need to do this??? heheh) Even then they have made editing the damn\nconfiguration harder than programming the fucking thing probably was... Why \nthe fuck use braces {}}}}}} FUCKING HELL... NOT EVERYONE IS A C-PROGRAMMER !\nEven the original /X2.x configration was better... and where is this ''all \nsinging all dancing'' configuration editor that has been promised???\n\n4.	NEW PROTECTION... Oh dear another really really crap copy-protection\nwhy the fuck do they really bother with it?? I mean EVERY time it gets \nremoved anyway... they could at least make it a bit more interesting.. a \nchallege??  The thing is now, I`m not even sure if most people can even\nbe bothered to install /X updates anymore...... (BANG! There goes another\nmeg of fast..and for what?)\n\n5.	And possibly a few other insignificant little things and 1,00000`s\nof bugfixes and probably some new bugs added (spagetti coding rules.. its the\nif it works don`t mess with it motto... Professionalism at it highest..)\n\n\n\n\n\nWhy even use /X?\n----------------			\n\nTo be honest you`d be far better of running S-Express.. I`ve heard from a \nfew people that the new version of S-Express due out soon will sport the\nfollowing features...\n\n1. Full Bi-directional Hydra support..\n2. Unlimited conferences\n3. Encrypted Password support\n4. Full Compatibility with /X3.x & /X4.x ''user.data'' & ''user.keys'' for\n   easy conversion from /X to S!X\n5. Every single bit of text within S-Express will be changable by sysops\n   so that every BBS running S!X can look different!\n\nand much much more.. so in our opinion your better off with S!X than\n/X4.x.. save your money.. get drunk... get laid... buy some food... buy\na 28.8... get some cc`s... but DON`T waste your hard earned money on \nregistering to /X4.x... you`ll  be sorry... (MARK MY WORDS!!!!!!!!!!!!!)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nend.\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',15270,5,0,NULL,NULL,'lsd_aer','scan',1780048575);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('lsd_ano','LSD_ANO.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/LSD_ANO.LHA',NULL,'XIM','LE-win5-96.exe',NULL,NULL,'LSD',': _____.__/\:____   ____  ____   )/ideo    : | \__  | / \\__  \ /  _ \/ _  \  (--oo)    | :   \  | \__/  \  \  ___/ //  /   \_-/     :',replace('.------------------------------------------.\n: _____.__/\:____   ____  ____   )/ideo    :\n| \__  | / \\__  \ /  _ \/ _  \  (--oo)    |\n:   \  | \__/  \  \  ___/ //  /   \_-/     :\n|    \ : /  |  /  / /  /  /  /    /\/asty  |\n:     \_/|__|____/____/\____/ -[Presents]- :\n|        ______    ______________          |\n:      .:\    /\  /   ________   \::.      :\n|    .:::/   /_/__\__   \/   /   /\:::.    |\n:  .::::/   /   /   /   /   /   / /:::::.  :\n|.::::::\______/\______/_______/ /::::::::.|\n:::::::::\_____\/\_____\_______\/[P]::::::::\n| VNAnounce v1.0 Only 100% Anounce Door    |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'VN_Anounce.doc',replace('\n   VN_Anounce v1.0/LSD\n\n   Here is the only Anounce door that has ever worked 100%\n\nR$-John :) LowLife 3\n   The problem i had was all anounce doors used to lockup at 1 stage\n   or another so i mythered Nasty like mad man with an axe, until\n   he wrote somthing that would work Even if Hydra is in use.\n\n   He told me to fuckoff lots of times told me to stop fuking bugging\n   him, he threatened to format my hardrive & i know he would do that\n   as he realy is a nastybastard. he threatened to stuff lastnights \n   beefcurry leftovers into my floppys, cut the ribbon on my keyboard\n   hackup the fonelines into the house. all sorts of things until\n   fianaly he had heard enough and wrote this little door.\n   ALSO to view what Nasty LooksLike View the icon for the commands\n\n)/ideo /\/asty/LSD\n\n   All this door does is Launch the Internal door OLM\n   To anounce logins/logoffs & Uploads\n   i''m not as bad as R$- seems to think..... Plus if i had threatened to\n   do any of the above i would have done it NO FUCKIN Second chances!\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',12813,6,0,NULL,NULL,'lsd_ano','scan',1780048582);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('lsd_areg','LSD-AREG.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/LSD-AREG.LHA','AERegister','XIM','ACP',NULL,'mUb/lSD.','LSD','| | | __Y   |    pRESENTS:-  aE-rEGISTER | |_|__ | | | Auto Cracks & re-register all |   Y   |   | versions of /X V3.xx+ Tested',replace(' _   ___ ___\n| | | __Y   |    pRESENTS:-  aE-rEGISTER\n| |_|__ | | | Auto Cracks & re-register all\n|   Y   |   | versions of /X V3.xx+ Tested\n|   |   |   | upto V3.32 Supplied with\n|   |   |   | UnRegistered version of /X 3.32\n|___|___|mUb| & Setup.            bY mUb/lSD.\n','\n',char(10)),'AEUP331.guide',replace('@database AmiexDoc\n\nCopyright (c) 1994 LightSpeed Technologies Inc.\nAll Rights Reserved\n\n@Remark $VER: (Jan 02 1994, 09:06:01)\n@Remark AmigaGuide for the /X Update 3.31\n\n@node MAIN "/X Update 3.31 (c)1992-1994 LightSpeed Technologies Inc."\n               .: U P D A T E  D O C U M E N T A T I O N :.\n\n             The following is a list of changes to version 3.31\n             of AmiExpress.\n                     @{" MultiComm Port               " Link Update01}\n                     @{" Program Execution            " Link Update02}\n                     @{" MCI Commands                 " Link Update03}\n                     @{" Internal Zmodem Protocol     " Link Update04}\n                     @{" XPR Protocols                " Link Update05}\n                     @{" Custom Commands              " Link Update06}\n                     @{" Message Base                 " Link Update07}\n                     @{" AmiXnet Updates              " Link Update08}\n                  ------------------------------------  \n  \n  Documentation written by: \n  Joseph Hodge\n  LightSpeed Technologies Developement\n\n  Copyright (c) 1994 LightSpeed Technologies Inc.  All Rights Reserved.\n  Any copy or illegal distribution of this Documentation is prohibited.\n\n@endnode\n@node Update01 "MultiComm Port"\n  =======================================================================\n  Following is a list of changes to the MultiComm Port\n\n  Since version 3.30 of AmiExpress we have increased the Maximum Number\n  of Nodes that ACP can handle. ACP can now handle a maximum of 32 Nodes.\n\n  This change involved changing the internal MultiComm structure to handle\n  32 nodes vs 9 nodes. This change means that the old NewChat and some of\n  the older Online Message Send Modules may not work any longer. We have\n  released an update to the NewChat door so that it will handle the 32\n  node configuration.\n\n@endnode\n@node Update02 "Program Execution"\n  =======================================================================\n  \n  Since version 3.30 of AmiExpress you now have the ability to make\n  AmiExpress resident. Doing this should speed up program execution\n  and also conserve memory. \n\n  Making AmiExpress resident:\n\n  1. change all nodestart tooltypes in the NODE icons to reflect the\n     following:\n     \n     NODESTART=express\n \n  2. Update your s:user-startup script by adding the following after\n     your BBS Assignment:\n\n     RESIDENT EXPRESS BBS:EXPRESS\n\n\n@endnode\n@node Update03 "MCI Commands"\n  =======================================================================\n  Following is a list of changes to the MCI Commands\n\n  I have modified the ~CC command to allow the execution of MENU PROMPT\n  commands. This will allow you to run the internal WHO command from any\n  MCI text. Simply add this MCI command to your MCI Text File:\n\n  ~CC_WHO\n\n  NOTE: It is important to realise that most MENU COMMANDS should only\n        be run from the MENU PROMPT. For Instance , forcing the READING\n        of mail at the FRONTEND of express would not be wise because the\n        BBS does not know who is logging onto the system. So use your\n        own judgement on these matters. \n\n@endnode\n@node Update04 "Internal Zmodem Protocol"\n  ===========================================================================\n  Following is a list of changes to the Internal Zmodem Protocol \n\n  I added the tooltype ''HDTRANSBUFFER'', this tooltype is for the node icons.\n\n  HDTRANSBUFFER allows you to change the buffer size from serial to harddisk.\n  This option is a better alternative than using a RAMPEN because it works\n  on a file by file basis, whereas the RAMPEN method has to wait until all\n  uploads are complete.\n\n  HDTRANSBUFFER has the following syntax:\n\n  HDTRANSBUFFER=<buffers>\n\n      You may specifiy as many buffers as you like. The number of buffers\n      default to 8 if this tooltype is not used. Here is a formula for\n      determining how much memory will be allocated for transfers when the\n      node is started:\n\n      ((buffers+2)*1024)*2\n                         ^----- This is required due to the double buffering.\n\n      ie:\n \n      HDTRANSBUFFER=20 would require 45,056 bytes of memory\n\n      1. ((20+2)*1024)*2\n      2. (22*1024)*2\n      3. (22528)*2\n      4. 45056\n\n    Version 3.30 a bug was introduced with this HDTRANSBUFFER addition.\n  AmiExpress was not freeing the memory it allocated for the buffers. This\n  is the primary reason for releasing this version.\n\n@endnode\n@node Update05 "XPR Protocols"\n  =======================================================================\n  Following is a list of changes to the XPR Protocols Interface:\n\n  We have temporarily removed the XPR interface and placed it in a SYSCMD.\n  We will most likely put this back into AmiExpress in a month or so. \n\n  One of the important changes to AmiExpress besides this is now all batch\n  Protocol Icons must contain the tooltype AE_BATCH instead of BATCH.\n\n@endnode\n@node Update06 "Custom Commands"\n  =======================================================================\n  \n  I added the tooltype ''QUICKMODE'' for the module icons. This tooltype\n  simply tells AmiExpress not to run the Module in question if the user\n  has logged onto the sysop using the QUICK logon option.\n\n@endnode\n@node Update07 "Message Base"\n  =======================================================================\n  \n  Since Version 3.30 the message base has been modified to re-display\n  the original message if a reply to a message was aborted.\n\n@endnode\n@node Update08 "AmiXnet Updates"\n  =======================================================================\n  \n  Due to the expansion of the Net, including more sales and increased\n  volume of mail, we realized the need for a more optimized method of\n  packing netmail. AmiXnet currently recalculates the MailRoute for\n  every net mail conference when it is packing mail and unpacking mail.\n  This in itself is not efficient. Therefore I modified all of the NETMAIL\n  utilities to recognize pre computed mailroutes, this greatly speeds up\n  the mail packing process for those with only one Node Id.\n\n  In order to invoke the optimized method of packing mail you will need to\n  do the following:\n\n  1. Modify the scripts that run MRUPDATE with an additional commandline\n     option ''AUTOUPDATE''. AUTOUPDATE should be the last commandline option\n     to MRUPDATE. This will force MRUPDATE to create pre-calculated \n     mailroutes when new maps come down the net.\n\n  2. Create a directory in BBS:AmiXnet named your node id. For instance I\n     have a directory called:\n\n     BBS:AmiXnet/703001 because 703001 is my nodeid.\n\n  Once you have done the above, the next time mail is packed the netutils\n  will create pre-computed route files and place them into the newly \n  created directory.\n\n  NOTE: ONLY DO THIS IF YOU HAVE ONLY 1 NODE ID. THERE IS A COUPLE OF\n        BBSs WITH MULTIPLE NODE IDS, THIS OPTION WILL NOT WORK FOR THEM\n        AT THE MOMENT. I HOPE IN THE NEAR FUTURE I WILL HAVE THIS SOLVED.\n\n\n  \n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',468793,6,0,NULL,NULL,'lsd_areg','scan',1780048575);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('lsd_bw20','LSD-BW20.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/LSD-BW20.LHA',NULL,'XIM','Wall.XIM',NULL,NULL,'LSD','_/¦  _/\___/\          lSD pRESENTS       ¦ \ |  \ __/\ .\    bRICK wALL vERSION 2.o  | / |_ /_.¬\/ | \                           |',replace('<--. ------------- ------------------------+\n _/¦  _/\___/\          lSD pRESENTS       ¦\n \ |  \ __/\ .\    bRICK wALL vERSION 2.o  |\n / |_ /_.¬\/ | \                           |\n/  l ¬\ ¦  \ l  \   wALL dOOR fOR /X 4.x   |\n\____ /___ /___ /                          ¦\n<- -\/---\/- -\/[-dL!-]- --------------- --+\n','\n',char(10)),'BrickWall.Guide',replace('@DATABASE National Lottery Guide\n@AUTHOR Harv\n@(C) 1995 Grand Admiral n Harv\n\n@NODE MAIN\n@TITLE "LSD''s Brick Wall Version 2.0 for /X 4.x"\n\n                        __/|    ____/\__ ____/\\n                       !o  |   !o       Vo    .\\\n                      |||  |___|:  |____||  |  \\\\:-\n                   -:|||:  |   |___    :|:  |   .\\\n                      ||.  |   |sc |   o|.  |    /\n                       |______ |________| ______/\n                       ~~~~~~~\|PRESENTS|/~~~~~~\n                         BRICK WALL VERSION 2.0\n                       \n  @{" Installation " LINK INSTALLATION} Its Easy           @{" Tooltypes    " LINK TOOLTYPES} Very Important\n  @{" Setting Up   " LINK SETUP} Running It         @{" Supp. Files  " LINK FILES} Storage Area \n  @{" Disclaimer   " LINK DISCLAIMER} Not our Fault!     @{" History      " LINK HISTORY} History is Crap!\n  @{" Distribution " LINK DISTRIBUTION} Get it Upped       @{" New Features " LINK NEW} Suprise Suprise!\n  @{" LSD Plug     " LINK LSD} Kewl               @{" Specials     " LINK SPECIAL} Inbuilt User Commands\n  @{" What Is It?  " LINK TELLMEMORE} Doh!               @{" Banner Files " LINK BANNERS} Bricks and Banners\n  @{" Ami Express  " LINK AMIEXP} /X Wassat???       @{" Credits      " LINK CREDITS} Hi Kids :)))\n  @{" Other Doors  " LINK OTHERSTUFF} Grab Em Too        @{" Authors      " LINK AUTHORS} Its Us, Again\n  @{" Registration " LINK REGISTER} Go on, Please      @{" Support      " LINK SUPPORT} Why not Call\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE INSTALLATION\n@TITLE "How To Install Lottery..."\n\n Installation\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~\n Installation is VERY simple, all you have to do is copy the "BBS:" dir\n into your "BBS:", I was always joubious about this, so check it first if\n ya like, we don''t mind.\n\n Once this has been done, you should really read the @{"ToolTypes" LINK TOOLTYPES} section\n in the docs to choice your configuartion options. There are quite a few \n to choose from too, its fuckin feature packed is this version.\n\n Once you have done all these, it should be ready to use, give it a try\n anyway, also it might be an idea to choose your @{"Banners" LINK BANNERS}, i.e the look\n of the wall.\n\n Manual Installation\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n What!!!!!. You want to Install it manually, TOOOOOOL, thats what you are,\n well, okay, if you insist. Right first thing, erm, you DO HAVE /X on your\n system don''t you. Ok, right then, in the "DOORS" assign first make a dir\n called "LSD-Toolz", you may already have this if you have installed any\n of our doors before, anyway, and in that directory you should then make\n another directory called "LSD-Wall", the directories mentioned have to \n called this, this is the way the programs have been wrote so don''t\n fuckin complain.... ok, then, assuming you have unarchived all of the\n shit out of the origional archive, copy the "LSD-Toolz/LSD-Wall" dir\n into the one youve just made, copying the storage directory is entirly\n optional but has some nice banners and bricks for you to fuck around \n with.\n\n The next thing you need to do is copy the "COMMANDS/BBSCMD/WALL>INFO"\n into your own directory of the same title, and thats it, go for it.\n wouldn''t it have been easier to copy the job lot though, oh well, \n there are some akward people around I guess :)))) !!\n\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE SETUP\n@TITLE "Setup the BrickWall"\n\n Setting Up BrickWall\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n Well, all ya need to do is Setup your @{"Banners" LINK BANNERS} and then configure\n your @{"ToolTypes" LINK TOOLTYPES} and away you go, also, don''t forget to setup your\n BBSCBD/Wall.Info Icon, I.e Access Levels, Names etc... Easy as pi$$ eh??\n\n IMPORTANT:  Make sure that there is a file called "Lock.Wall" in the wall\n             directory. It is needed to lock other users from writing on the\n             wall at the same time as you are. Its just a text file which\n             has the message "DO NOT DELETE"\n\n\n For banning people, there is a file called "Banned.Wall". In here you put\n the user''s name and the reason why they are banned, eg..\n\n Fred Bloggs\n This is a LAME NAME\n Harv\n Just a lame fuck\n >>Bo<<\n Ultra Fat Fuck\n\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE DISCLAIMER\n@TITLE "Disclaimer"\n\n Disclaimer\n ~~~~~~~~~~\n Well, all we can say is, we have tested this and found all the bugs, and \n got rid of them, to the best of our knowledge there are no bugs. However,\n any damage caused to your system by this door is not our fault. This is\n no cause for alarm. This is hardly going to happen, its a fuckin /X door\n for gods sake :).\n\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE DISTRIBUTION\n\n Distribution\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~\n Distrubution of LSD''s BrickWall is completley legal, in fact we would be \n very happy if you would pass it round your friends and other BBS''s you \n call as the further it goes, the more people know how kewl it is.\n\n There is no registered version, this version is completley uncrippled and\n the full release, it is completley free, and therefore illegal to charge\n anyone, apart from the price of a floppy disk maybe. But don''t go sckanin\n all your m8y''s, cos thats not nice.\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE LSD\n\n\n             /\_____         ____________________________/\           \n            /      |        /                /             \\n           /       |_______/         l______/|              \ \n          /        l       \_______        \ |       l       \\n          \                /      l        / |               /\n           \______________/\______________/  l______________/   \n\n WOOOOOOOOOOOOOOOW Extreme closeup of unfeasably large LSD Logo, ott or\n wot.... ask Axen and he''ll tell you otherwise. \n@ENDNODE\n@NODE TELLMEMORE\n@TITLE "Tell Me More..."\n\n What Does It Do?!\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n WHAT! I can''t beleive you clicked on this button... You don''t know what it\n does, Wassat??? oh sorry, you were just browsing the docs to look for \n sarcastic comments like this one. I bet Grand Admiral is gonna love me for\n writing these docs (Not). oh well, on with the show.\n\n This is a graffiti Wall for /X, ya must have seen the sort before, or so\n you thought, you have never seen a wall like this, it does ya normal stuff\n such as anonymous, blame, edit. But all these features have been optimised\n and have been improved, i.e, arrow key editing, switch on and offable \n blame, edit, view, the lot. It even has its own custom command set, such\n as:\n \n  <** AREA **> is full of Twats who shag sheep.\n\n This example would then print up, if you logged on the BBS and were from\n Bradford..\n\n Bradford is full of twats who shag sheep.\n\n Kewl eh, read more about that in the @{"Specials" LINK SPECIAL} section. Some very nice\n features indeed :).\n\n Well there ya go, my round up of What BrickWall 2.0 is! \n\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE AMIEXP\n@TITLE "You Need This!"\n\n What Does It Need?!\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n Well, BrickWall 2.0 was coded with /X 4.x as the target but it may work \n on other versions, I dunno much about /X version 3.x so I couldn''t tell\n ya. Thats all it needs. And of course WB 2.x. But ya wouldn''t be running \n /X without it would ya??\n\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE OTHERSTUFF\n@TITLE "Other LSD Doors To Watch Out For..."\n\n Other LSD Doors To Watch Out For...\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n    Why not check out these other kewl doors written by us?\n\n      Lottery - A Kewl BBS game to let your users bet credz, Version 2.0\n                is already been worked on. Which will let you set a time\n                for the computer to automatically draw the lottery for\n                you, i.e generate the numers. Version 2.0 will be done \n                >>Bo<< has finished his tour of every Pie Shop in \n                Bradford and the rest of West Yorkshire.\n    \n        FList - A new door that allows users to download a file list of\n                conferences. Multiple conferences can be flagged together\n                with specific directories. They are then archived up in\n                users preference and sent to him. The door also has a unique\n                AmigaGuide facility for Amiga users that packages the lists\n                into one text file dividing confs and dirs up into nodes\n                and creating a menu for the lists automatically - it will\n                also add your bbs logo to the file for you!\n                Users flag confs and dirs using cursor keys for simplicity!\n\n All these doors can be found (or will be found soon) on all kewl bbses\n including of course 13th Hour and all LSD boards.\n\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE REGISTER\n@TITLE "How To Register"\n\n Registration\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~\n Haha, its free, no registration in this version but ya can send is some \n money if you want anyway, we don''t mind honest. Hang on, i have an idea.\n\n Right, this is not registerware its >>Bo<< Abuse ware, just log on any\n LSD BBS and send abusive mail to >>Bo<<. The best abusive message wins\n a registered copy of FList and Lottery, this is serious, I mean it, so\n go for it, Sorry >>Bo<< m8y, I couldn''t resist, why do you think I jumped\n at the chance to do these docs for Grand Admiral, hahahahaha. \n\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE SUPPORT\n@TITLE "Many Thanx for the Support..."\n\n Beta Testers\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~\n Cheerz >>Bo<< and Harv for testing it for me, it works dunnit??, Yup,\n kewl.. Well then peeps, Enjoy.\n\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE CREDITS\n@TITLE "Credits!"\n\n Credits\n ~~~~~~~\n  Many thanx goto the following in no particular order :-\n\n       PriSoner\n       Venom\n       Tango n Dan (Keep tekkin the Tablets m8y)\n       Ace\n       Harv (Hehe I get to thank myself, thats THANK btw)\n       Grand Admiral (FOR WRITING THIS KEWL PROGGY, AUTHOR DUDE)\n       Axen (Yo M8y get your phone fixed or buy a new one)\n       TheMainMan (Cheerz for being so amusing m8y, love it :))\n       Jim! Sorry about the BBS m8y, it was kewl, :( Dearly Miss it!\n       All LSD Mebers\n       My Mum (cheerz for the cups of tea whilst writing these docs)\n       My A Level Results (NOT)\n\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE AUTHORS\n@TITLE "Who DunnIt?!"\n\n Authors\n ~~~~~~~\n Well Grand Admiral did ALL the coding for this one. Well done m8y. But I\n did some Ansi Graphics, I.e those Kewl LSD Bricks and Banners. >>Bo<< did\n some Ansi as well, and so did Grand Admiral. \n\n If ya Get anymore kewl Ansi Let us know. Design some and mail it to us!!\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE TOOLTYPES\n@TITLE "Everyones a Tooltype :)"\n\n ToolType Configuration\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n What I could say about Tooltypes, But thats another Story. On with it..\n Here is a List of the Tooltypes and a description of what they are used\n for (btw "WallPrefs.Info" this is the list) :-\n\n USERVIEWANON     -  This will let the User view who has really written \n                     something on the wall under the Anonymous Handle.\n\n USERALAIS        -  This will let the User view who has really written\n                     something on the wall under someone elses Handle.\n\n ANONCOLOUR       -  This changes the colour when someone write under the\n                     anonymous name. I.e 6 would be Cyan. So if all the\n                     other names were in green and the anonymous was in\n                     cyan, the gutless wonders would stick out a mile off.\n\n                     VALID OPTIONS ARE\n\n                     0 BLACK\n                     1 RED\n                     2 GREEN\n                     3 YELLOW\n                     4 BLUE\n                     5 PURPLE\n                     6 CYAN\n                     7 WHITE\n\n NAMECOLOUR       -  This is basically the same as the last, except this\n                     is for when people use their ordinary names.\n\n                     VALID OPTIONS ARE SAME AS ABOVE\n\n USERMSGCOLOUR    -  You can set this tooltype with a number, (Ansi Pen)\n\n                     VALID OPTIONS ARE SAME AS ABOVE\n\n SYSOPMSGCOLOUR   -  This is the same as above, define two different \n                     colours for user and sysop and the sysop messages will\n                     stand out. Bracket it and the sysop can choose his/her\n                     colour.\n\n                     VALID OPTIONS ARE SAME AS ABOVE\n\n CHOOSECOLOUR     -  This lets the user choose there colours instead of\n                     you defining them. Bracket this for it to loose its \n                     effect.\n\n USERANON         -  This lets you turn off and on the user anonymous \n                     facility. Bracket this and it will loose its effect.\n\n NOMESSAGE        -  This lets you define the message when no one wants to\n                     write anything. \n\n                     VALID OPTION IS A STRING OF TEXT\n\n SPECIALCOMMAND   -  This turns on and off the ability to use Special \n                     Commands. See @{"Specials" LINK SPECIALS} for details.\n\n USERONNODE       -  This will tell the user that someone else is on\n                     another node writing on the wall and they will have to\n                     wait. Remarking this, the user will just get a message\n                     saying that the wall is busy.\n\n Thats it for the tooltypes, easy eh? just do the normal tooltypey things\n with em, you''ll soon get the hang of it.\n\n \n@ENDNODE\n@NODE FILES\n@TITLE "In the Storage Area"\n\n Storage Area\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~\n Put all your wall designs in here, youll already find a generous selection\n in here. But add some more if you like. Build up a big collection. Any kewl\n ones ya do, send em to us. We would like to see em and use in future \n releases.\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE HISTORY\n@TITLE "Bahhh Humbug, Zoink!!"\n\n History\n ~~~~~~~\n APRIL 1995    -   Released under Imperial Software as ImpWall 1.3. Just\n                   like NastyWall only faster.\n \n AUGUST 1995   -   This Release. Wow what a long history.\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE NEW\n@TITLE "New Features, Wow show em Bob"\n\n New Features\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~\n The new features in this version are as follows :-\n\n Special Commands\n Tooltype Configuration of Anonymous etc..\n Better Colour Handling Tooltypes.\n Configurable Bricks.\n Configurable Banners.\n Configurable Bannanas (Just Wondered if you were paying Attention).\n Arrow Key Usablity for Editing.\n Better editing and deleting features.\n faster, a lot faster.\n\n So get em enjoyed. Anymore features ya want adding goto the @{"Support" LINK SUPPORT} section\n and mail us on one of the mentioned BBS''s.\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE SPECIAL\n@TITLE "Special COmmand"\n\n Special Commands\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n These can be a lot of Fun, Here we go :-\n\n <** USER **>       -  This will print the name of the user online in the\n                       message.\n                       This command can also be used if the user selected\n                       change name.\n\n <** AREA **>       -  This does the same but with location instead of name.\n\n <** PASS **>       -  This does the same with password, don''t worry about\n                       this one, only the user whats logged on sees it, it\n                       doesn''t store the password in the wall data file.\n\n <** FONE **>        -  This does the same but with PhoneNumber, again it \n                       doesn''t store it anywhere so don''t worry.\n\n Right ill give ya some examples shall I?? \n\n <** USER **> is a big piece of shit.\n Hey <** USER **>, i know your password, is it <** PASS **>.\n For a good time call <** FONE **>\n\n Kewl eh???\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE BANNERS\n@TITLE "Bricks and Banners may clog up my Ansi Editor but >>Bo<< is still fat."\n\n Banners ''n'' Bricks\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n Right, to use your banners and brick on the wall, you have to stick to \n the following rules :-\n\n Banner Headerfile is no more than 5 Lines Long\n Banner TailerFile is no more than 5 lines Long\n Bricks for the wall are no more than 64 Lines Long.\n \n To use them on the wall, rename the files of your choice as follows :-\n\n Banner Header File        =  TopBanner.Wall\n\n Banner Tailer File        =  BottomBanner.Wall\n\n Bricks File               =  Wall.Wall\n\n And thats it, Happy Wall Designing.\n@ENDNODE\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',32500,11,0,NULL,NULL,'lsd_bw20','scan',1780048575);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('lsd_bw22','LSD-BW22.LZX','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/LSD-BW22.LZX',NULL,'XIM','Wall.XIM',NULL,NULL,'LSD',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'auto-added',32168,0,0,NULL,NULL,'lsd_bw22','scan',1780048575);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('lsd_bw23','LSD-BW23.LZX','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/LSD-BW23.LZX',NULL,'XIM','lsd bw23',NULL,NULL,'LSD',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,97951,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048575);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('lsd_ckex','LSD-CKEX.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/LSD-CKEX.LHA','CheckExe','XIM','CheckExe',NULL,NULL,'LSD','.:\    /\  /   ________   \::. .:::/   /_/__\__   \/   /   /\:::. .::::/   /   /   /   /   /   / /:::::.',replace('         ______    ______________           \n       .:\    /\  /   ________   \::.       \n     .:::/   /_/__\__   \/   /   /\:::.     \n   .::::/   /   /   /   /   /   / /:::::.   \n .::::::\______/\______/_______/ /::::::::. \n:::::::::\_____\/\_____\_______\/[P]::::::::\n ::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\n  ::::::::::EXECUATABLE CHECKER:::::::::::\n   :::::::::SHAGRATT  /  L.S.D ::::::::::\n    ::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\n','\n',char(10)),'CheckExe.doc',replace('                      _______     _______________________    \n                     -\_    ¬|===/    ______________    ¬\==-\n                       |     |  / /\  |_____|    ¬| \_    \\n                     -=|     |==\/  \___   ¬\     |=/     /=-\n                      .|     |__/_   \/     /     |/     /\n                     -|___________\________/|_____/     /===-\n                        -=-=-=-=-\/-=-PRESENT-=-\______/\n\n              C H E C K   E X E   V E R S I O N   1 . 0   B E T A\n\n\n              The first ever Amiga Executable Hunk Checker v 1.0ß \n\n                       Written by:        Shagratt/LSD\n                       Docs by:           Doc/Doc''s House\n                       Beta testing by:   Doc/Doc''s House\n                       Design by:         Shagratt and Doc\n\n\nHow many times have you had a "supposedly good executable" that FAILED to\nwork and you were left frustrated spending hours trying to figure out if it\nwas an error you''ve made, just a "fake" to frustrate you, or there was some\nproblem with the file you could not detect?\n\nThe entire credit for this must go to the folks at LSD, particularly Shagratt \nwho took my very "fuzzy ideas" and coded them into a solidly working util \nwhich everyone can NOW use.\n    \n    \n                         W H A T   D O E S   I T   D O   ?\n    \nCLI/SHELL Usage:\n    \n    Merely tell it:  Checkexe <Filename>.  Checkexe will then happily\n    go about checking the structures to see if it is really a "exe"\n    command, show you all the HUNKS, tell you what kind of memory\n    requirements are needed, and then report if the file is OK.  Here\n    is an example of it checking ITSELF: checkexe <checkexe>\n\n              Executable Hunk Checker v 1.0ß - Written by Shagratt/LSD\n                                                                             \n              PROGRAM IS PACKED WITH "CrunchMania R/N/[H]"\n\n              CHECKING HUNKS..            \n                            \n              Hunk_Header  ($3f3).......  \n              Hunk_Code    ($3e9)....     \n              Hunk_Reloc32 ($3ec).......  \n              Hunk_End     ($3f2)..       \n              Hunk_BSS     ($3eb)....     \n\n              Memory usage:    Chipmem: 0k\n                             Publicmem: 6k\n                               Fastmem: 0k\n                            \n              FILE OK  \n\n\nBBS USAGE:\n\n    Checkexe can be used with Ami-Express/Tempest/C-Net/XenoLing (in fact\n    any BBS software!) as is.  I am most familiar with Ami-Express and its \n    "FCcheck" and will use this as an example how it works;\n    CD BBS:FCheck\n    <Filename>= EXE\n\n    checkexe           ; This is LINE #1, or your <Command>\n                       ; BLANK...LINE 2,  or your <Args>  Sorry...NONE YET!\n    CHECK FAILED - NO HUNK HEADER       ;LINES # 3 - ??? Error warnings\n    CHECK FAILED - BAD HUNK STRUCTURE   \n    WARNING: Program needs FASTMEM\n    WARNING: Program needs 1MB of CHIPMEM\n    WARNING: Program needs over 1MB of memory\n    WARNING: Program will have CHIPMEM problems, kill all externals\n\n    ****NOTE****  Lines 5-8 are "Optionals", but I suggest you use and\n                  force such files to your HOLD DIR so you can add such\n                  "Warnings" to the file descriptions.\n    =======================================================================\n    Again, CHECKEXE is for use with ".exe" commands.  These are commands\n    which will execute, or "run" on your system.  Files such as texts,\n    docs, .dms files or others ARE NOT EXECUTABLE.   \n    \n    ****PAY ATTENTION TO ME PLEASE****  "What is an executable?"\n\n    Many people are "confused" about what IS/IS NOT considered "exe".\n    Most folks consider only their commands in the C:, SYSTEM:, or\n    TOOLS: directories as executables.  These are files which you can\n    either enter their names from a CLI/SHELL or run clicking on their\n    associated icons.   THESE ARE NOT *ALL* the types of "executables"\n    which exist!  The following are other types of files which\n    Amiga DOS considers "executable", although not ''all possibilities'':\n    \n    LIBS: -  libraries such as: decrunch.library\n    L:    -  handlers such as: aux-handler\n    REXX: -  compiled RPSTART REXX such as: DCI "Door" for Ami-Express\n\n    ''Rule of Thumb''....."compiled" files may/may not be ''executable''\n                   .....file not compiled MAY NOT (normally) be! \n\nCOMPRESSED FILES:\n\n    Checkexe makes use of the DECRUNCH.LIBRARY!  If a file has been\n    compressed with any known "cruncher", checkexe will report the type\n    of compression as was shown above in the CLI/SHELL example.  This \n    is a bonus feature which Shagratt added to help everyone identify\n    all types of files, so they can be "uncrunched" with DLD in case\n    you have specific problems.\n\n    NOTE: If you do not wish to use this option, do not have \n          decrunch.library in your libs: directory.  CHECKEXE will \n          still work correctly, but without this option!\n\n\nMEMORY USAGE:\n\n    Another useful feature is the report on memory usage, eg;\n\n              Memory usage:    Chipmem: 604k\n                             Publicmem: 12k\n                               Fastmem: 0k\n\n    This report tells us that the .exe file it has just checked needs 1meg\n    of CHIP memory to be executed.  A useful feature i`m sure you`ll agree!\n\n\nWHAT IT CAN`T DO:\n\n    If a file has been passed by CHECKEXE, there is still a chance it \n    will not work.  Sadly there is no way to detect bad programming!\n\n\nDOCUMENTATION/TESTING\n\n    This documentation was written by "Doc", Doc''s House from notes\n    given me in "ßeta" directly from Shagratt with his permission to\n    write them during testing.  \n    \n    "BLATANT ADVERTISING"---  Doc''s House +1 614-855-3114, is a special\n    BBS system to assist Sysops, PR Groups, and Programmers.  We are\n    specialists in DESIGN/DEVELOPMENT/TESTING.  If you ever want an\n    great util idea to work on, "Free" help with DESIGNS/DEVELOPMENT,\n    or a good forum to release quality utils that will give them\n    good descriptions and PUBLICITY.........give us a call.\n\n    Ohhhh....and a phone call to support people such as the LSD Group,\n             Shagratt, and others who spend COUNTLESS HOURS slaving\n             in the micro-world of "bytes" and "bug-reports" bringing\n             you these utils to express your thanks is VERY APPRECIATED!\n\n\nIMPORTANT MESSAGE:\n\n    Because of online checking, the executable file MUST have the suffix\n    ".exe", so if you release a production onto the boards, PLEASE ENSURE \n    it has this suffix (eg; "LSD-lard.exe" "TSL-cool.exe", "ASI-hot.exe"\n    etc.).\n    \n    SYSOPS PLEASE ENFORCE THIS IF YOU ARE TO USE THIS CHECKER!\n\n\nDISTRIBUTION:\n\n    This tool is Public Domain, it has a maximum distribution charge of\n    One pound and fifty pence (Or your countries equivelant), this includes\n    media, postage and all other overheads.  \n\n    The GNU General Public License, Version 2, June 1991 is made a part of\n    this agreement as if contained herein.\n\n    LSD® is a Service Mark of "Leisure Software Development"®, a group of \n    associated talented individual programmers, designers, bulletin\n    board operators and public information specialists promoting the\n    Amiga computer and products therefor.  Our specialty is specialized\n    programming, utilities and projects for its enhanced usage. \n\n\nBUG REPORTS:\n\n    If you find any problems with this tool, or have an idea to make it\n    more powerful then contact either Doc on Docs House BBS or Pazza\n    of LSD on any LSD BBS.  The message will get passed on to Shagratt.\n\n\nCALL THESE BOARDS:\n\n\n                             SKULLBUGGERY (WHQ)\n                    4 Node >> +1 706 650 1417 << RINGDOWN\n                              +1 706 868 9783\n                              +1 706 868 9467\n                              +1 706 PRI VATE\n\n                               SYSOP: BIKER\n                          COSYSOP: D-MAN, SKYLARK\n                              1.5 GIG ONLINE,\n                          16800 HST, AMI-EXPRESS\n\n\n                             CARNIVAL (USHQ)\n                             +1 414 392 3761\n                             +1 414 392 3794\n       \n                          SYSOP: Eddie The Head\n                        COSYSOP: D-MAN, FISH, MUB\n                            14400 HST, C-Net\n\n\n                             THE HOLE (USHQ)\n                  2 Node >> +1 419 899 2754 << RingDown \n              \n                              SYSOP: Oleman\n                             COSYSOP: D-Man\n                         16800 HST, AMI-EXPRESS\n\n\n                       DIABOLICAL SABOTAGE (USHQ)\n                             +1 717 266 6436\n                             +1 717 266 6300\n                             +1 717 266 1940\n\n                           SYSOP: Dr Vinculum\n                      COSYSOP: D-MAN, FISH, PHIDEAUX\n                16800/14400 DUAL STANDARD HST, AMI-EXPRESS\n\n\n                          STYLETRON (Dis-Site)\n                            +1 916 366 0592\n\n                             SYSOP: MALCAR\n                            COSYSOP: D-MAN\n                        16800 HST, AMI-EXPRESS\n\n\n                           SECOM CITY (EHQ)\n                 3 Node >> +49 308 034 262 << RingDown\n                           +49 308 039 806\n                           +49 308 039 132 \n\n                            SYSOP: CRAYOR\n                        COSYSOP: D-MAN, DEXON\n                        16800 HST, AMI-EXPRESS\n\n                   \n                        MILLENIA (UK Dis-Site)\n                            +44 91 2843142\n                            +44 91 2840484\n\n                            SYSOP: Kitaro\n                           COSYSOP: D-MAN\n                       16800 HST, AMI-EXPRESS\n\nAnd don`t forget to call our friends BBS - DOCS HOUSE, number given earlier!\n\nend.\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',24091,2,0,NULL,NULL,'lsd_ckex','scan',1780048575);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('lsd_ds15','LSD-DS15.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/LSD-DS15.LHA','donate','XIM','donate',NULL,NULL,'LSD',NULL,replace('Donating User Door Version 1.5\n','\n',char(10)),'donate.doc',replace('               .. _ __ ___ _____  _____ _____ ___ __ _ ... \n               ... ___ __ _\   / /  __//___  \ _ __ ___ .. \n               .. _ __ ___ /  /  \   \ /  /\  \ ___ __ _ . \n               . ___ __ _ /  /__ _\_  \  /_/  /_ __ ___ .. \n                .. _ __ ___\____//_____/______/___ __ _ ...\n                       Present a door for /X V2.33+ \n                   Donation Stats V1.5 by SuBhUmAnZ/LSD\n                    Handles Pay leech Accounts for ya!\n                             The Documention!\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nI TAKE NO RESPONSIBILIY FOR BACKDOORS, OR FUCKED DATA BY THE USE OF THIS \nPROGRAM.  I DID NOT PUT ANY BACK DOORS IN THE CODE.  HOPEFULLY NO ONE \nDECIDES TO DO SO!  IF YOUR NOT SURE, GET IT FROM AN LSD BOARD!\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWell lets see, first copy all the files into a DOORS:donate/ directory.  Next,\nedit your bbs.cmd file and insert the following....\n\n-----------CUT HERE----------- \ndonate    XM020DOORS:donate/donate\n-----------CUT HERE-----------\n\n....or if you have 3.x put the following in an icon called donate.info....\n\nACCESS=020\nLOCATION=Doors:donate/donate\nMULTINODE=YES\nPRIORITY=0\nSTACK=50000\nTYPE=XIM\n\n\n\nAdd it to you logon bullentins.  You must do this so it automatically can \nhandle the pay leeches.  I do it by using BBS:Nodex/BULL20.TXT and using \nMCI commands to display it.  Example follows....\n \n----------CUT HERE-----------\n~SS_s:lastcall.txt            <---- Displays the lastcallers file\n~SP                           <---- Pauses for keypress\n~CC_with                      <---- Runs my with door\n~CC_donate                    <---- Runs this door  MUST SETUP THIS WAY!\n----------CUT HERE----------\n\nThis makes it automatic upon login.  Which is necessay to handle the accounts!\n\nDescription of DONATE.USERS file:\n--------------------------------\n\n----------CUT HERE----------\n* Donating Users Layout.  Read the DOCS!!!!!!  Return after EVERY ENTRY!\nsirrom                        1993/06/12   <---  Users start on line 2\nThe Senator                   1993/05/31     You can enter as many as\nMephastopheles                1993/05/31     you like.  Hit Return after\nVoodoo Kid                    1993/05/31     every entry.\nrandito                       1993/05/31\nhannibal                      1993/05/31\notto patch                    1993/05/31\n\n----------CUT HERE----------\n\nLines 2 to infinity is where you user names go.  Note the format, it is very \nimportant.  It goes as follows....\n\n\nUSER NAME  Columns 1-30       Expiration Date Column 31-40 format YYYY/MM/DD\nsirrom                        1993/06/12 \n\n\n\nNote that the user name is not case sensitive so you can enter it in all \nlower case or whatever....\n\n\nDescription of door:\n--------------------\n\nI wrote this door to handle my pay leeches automatically, (admit it, you have\na few that help pay the phone bills!) instead of the manual writing the shit \ndown method.  Makes the user have a disabled ratio for the time that he/she \nhas donated.  After the time is up, it resets his/her Ratio, Download files, \nand Download bytes to his/her original stats from the Donate.stats File.  The\nDoor also keeps a log of everone that has expired in the file Donate.log. \n\n\nMAKE SURE A USER EXPIRES BEFORE SETTING THEM UP AGAIN UNLESS YOU DON''T REALLY\nCARE ABOUT THE DONATE.LOG OR THEIR STATS BEING RESET TO WHAT THEY USED TO BE!\n\nYou can use a pack program on the user.data if ya want cause this program \ndoes not use the SLOT number to keep the stats of the user.  It uses the\nuser name.\n\n\nIf you have any suggestions or would really like to see something added, \ncontact me on a LSD BBS.  Some BBS''s that i hang out on are, Diabolical \nSabotage, Skull Buggery, Mass Media, Tempest Thunderstorm, and /X World HQ.   \n\nGreets to:   (In no perticular order)\nALL the LSD members, including..... \nDr Vinculum (My other partner in crime around here)\nPazza (I have to greet him he is the leader...:) )\nFish (Fucking trader from hell!)\nD-Man (I believe he really is GOD :) )\nVan Damme (The master of doors)\nRed Alert (The master of H/P! Sorry i missed ya in my wall release.)\nBytemaster (The man behind the BBS) \nMaltese Falcon (/X support team..Gr8 Friend & Excellent Coder! :) ) \nRacer-X (Friend from the CCI days :) )\nRoach (Long time friend and chum :) )\n.44 Magnum (Just plain k00l...)\nGambit (The best gamer around, i sed gamer not lamer :) )\n\nLSD is the k00lest of the k00l thanx for all the support guys.....\n\nALL MY USERS, you also know who you are!\nand anyone else i forgot........\n\nAnd i send a big wet kiss to Jen in Maine!\n \nL8r, \n-SuBhUmAnZ/LSD\n \n','\n',char(10)),'{"ACCESS":"020","LOCATION":"Doors:donate/donate","PRIORITY":"0","STACK":"50000","TYPE":"XIM"}','auto-added',13268,1,0,NULL,NULL,'lsd_ds15','scan',1780048575);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('lsd_ds20','LSD-DS20.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/LSD-DS20.LHA','donate','XIM','LE-win5-96.exe',NULL,'SuBhUmAnZ/LSD','LSD','\   / /  __//     \ Present a door for /  /  \   \ /  /\  \   /X V2.33+ /  /__ _\_  \  /_/  /Donation Stats V2.0',replace(' _____  _____ _____ \n \   / /  __//     \ Present a door for \n /  /  \   \ /  /\  \   /X V2.33+\n/  /__ _\_  \  /_/  /Donation Stats V2.0\n\____//_____/______/ by SuBhUmAnZ/LSD\n    Handles Pay leech Accounts for ya!\n     Now with Remote Sysop Commands!','\n',char(10)),'lOSeNDOS.guide',replace('                   \n                     __  _ __  /\__ _  _ __/\  __ _  __\n                    _\/___   \/              \/   ___\/_\n              ......\/\  /........................\  /\/......\n             :         \/                          \/         :\n             :      .___             .___         .___        :\n             :   _ _|   \      ______|   \  ______|   \       :\n             :   \\\__   7___  \______   /  \__   ____/       :\n             :      /.   |   \__/.  l/   \___/_____   \__ _   :\n             :     /::.  |    _/::.       _/::.  l/    _///   :\n             :     \___________\___________\____________\     :\n             :___        .___        .___        .___         :___\n     _ ______|   \ ______|   \ ______|   \ ______|   \  ______|   \\n     \\\__   ____/ \______   / \______   / \______   /  \__   ____/\n        /.   ___|___/.   |   \__/.  _|   \__/.  l/   \___/_____   \__ _\n       /::.  l/   _/::.  |    _/::. \___  _/::.       _/::.  l/    _///\n       \_ _________\_____|_____\___________\___________\___________ \\n         Y   :                                                :[nM$]Y\n      .------''                                                `------.\n      :eXON/rIOT^jORMAS · gHANDY/gODS · rAHIEM/eSSENCE · cELIC/rEKTUM: \n      `------.                                                .------''\n             `-------------------