   cODE bY BiLBo BaGGIns/MOTION^REDNEX\012\012                      @{"          iNTRODUCTION          " link "intro" 0} \012                      @{"          iNSTALLATION          " link "install" 0} \012                      @{"          fUTURE pLANS          " link "plans" 0} \012                      @{"           bUG rEPORT           " link "bugs" 0} \012                      @{"             gREETS             " link "greets" 0} \012                      @{"         tOOLS oVERVIEW         " link "tools" 0} \012                      @{"          mOTION iNFOS          " link "motion" 0}\012                      @{"              eXIT              " quit}\012@endnode\012\012@node "intro" "-^-> iNTRODUCTION -^-"\012@next "install"\012@prev "main"\012\012  BB-Olm is a internode message sender and announcer for Tempest.\012\012  Features:\012  - send internode messages\012  - annouce users logon and logoff\012  - messages are queued till receiver is idle\012  - muting still works\012  - fast\012  - coded in C\012\012  The Archive contains 4 programs:\012  BB-Olm         Send internode message to another node.\012  BB-AnnounceIn  Announce Users Logon (send internode messages to every\012                 node). \012  BB-AnnounceOff Announce Users Logoff (send internode messages to every\012                 node).\012  BB-OlmSender   Sends message to a node (needed by BB-Olm and BB-Announce).\012\012\012                            @{" bACK tO mAIN mENU " link "main" 0}\012@endnode\012\012@node "install" "-^- iNSTALLATION -^-"\012@next "plans"\012@prev "intro"\012\012  Installation of BB-OlmSender:\012  -----------------------------\012\012  Copy BB-OlmSender to Tempest:Utils/\012\012  Usage:\012  BB-OlmSender <TempestDir>\012  Option:\012  <TempestDir>  Name of the Directory where your Tempest is\012\012  Edit your startup-sequence or user-startup:\012  -------------------------> cut here <-------------------------\012  runback Tempest:Utils/BB-OlmSender Tempest:\012  -------------------------> cut here <-------------------------\012\012\012  Installation of BB-Olm:\012  -----------------------\012\012  Copy BB-Olm to Tempest:Doors/\012\012  Edit your *.opt file(s):\012  -------------------------> cut here <-------------------------\012  [10,*,*,*,*]   = olm  |T-DOOR|Tempest:DOORS/BB-Olm\012  -------------------------> cut here <-------------------------\012\012\012  Installation of BB-AnnounceIn:\012  ------------------------------\012\012  Copy BB-AnnounceIn(.cfg) to Tempest:Doors/\012\012  Edit your Text-Welcome(.ansi) file(s):\012  -------------------------> cut here <-------------------------\012  ~TD(Doors:BB-AnnounceIn)\012  -------------------------> cut here <-------------------------\012\012  Edit your BB-AnnounceIn.cfg file:\012  -------------------------> cut here <-------------------------\012  NO                          ;Do you want to be asked to Announce? (YES/NO)\012  -------------------------> cut here <-------------------------\012\012\012  Installation of BB-AnnounceOff:\012  -------------------------------\012\012  Copy BB-AnnounceOff(.cfg) to Tempest:Doors/\012\012  Edit your Text-Logoff(.ansi) file(s):\012  -------------------------> cut here <-------------------------\012  ~TD(Doors:BB-AnnounceOff)\012  -------------------------> cut here <-------------------------\012  It looks better when you put the screenclear from your Text-Logoff behind\012  the door.\012\012  Edit your BB-AnnounceOff.cfg file:\012  -------------------------> cut here <-------------------------\012  NO                          ;Do you want to be asked to Announce? (YES/NO)\012  -------------------------> cut here <-------------------------\012\012\012                            @{" bACK tO mAIN mENU " link "MAIN" 0}\012@endnode\012\012@node "plans" "-^- fUTURE pLANS -^-"\012@next "bugs"\012@prev "install"\012\012  Make a option to send a internode messsage to every node.\012\012\012                            @{" bACK tO mAIN mENU " 