INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('m_sans01','M!SANS01.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/M!SANS01.LHA',NULL,'XIM','_____________________________________',NULL,'BiLBo',NULL,'/        /     /  ___/___/     /     /\ // /  /  // /  // /  //  // /  // /  / / // /  /  // /  // /  //  // /  // /  / /',replace('    _____________________________________\n   /        /     /  ___/___/     /     /\\n  // /  /  // /  // /  //  // /  // /  / /\n // /  /  // /  // /  //  // /  // /  / /\n/__/__/__/_____/__/__/___/_____/__/__/ /\n\__\__\__\_____\_____\___\_____\__\__\/[B]\n+pReSeNtZ   ->SendAnswer v0.1<-   /X ToOl+\n+ Door that sends the NewUserAnswers as  +\n+ to every user and asks for refs.       +\n+ No quest door, uses /X routine.        +\n+ for S!X & /X   by BiLBo BaGGIns/MoTioN +\n','\n',char(10)),'SendAnswer.guide',replace('@database "MoTiOn - Send Answer V0.1"\n@AUTHOR "The aDDiCt"                 \n@(C) "BiLBo BaGGIns/Motion"                  \n@Ver$ "Send Answer V0.1 (10-03-94)"\n@HEIGHT 30\n@Node MAIN "--> Main Menu <--"\n\n  .%%%................%%%....%%%..........%%/\%%.%%%......%%%....%..%....%%\n .%%.%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%.%%%%%%.%%%%%%%%%%%%/  \%%%.%%%%%%%%.%%%%%%%%%%%%%%.\n %%/(_________________/(_____/(___________(____)%/(______%%|\___%.____.%%.%\n %%\                 /      ~\\             /  |//      ~\%|.   \|   ~|%%%.\n .%%\  /\           //   |:   \\  ..   .   /   |/    |    \||    \    |%%%%\n  .%%\/            //    |.    \_/||   |\_/|   |     |.    \|         |%%%.\n ..%%|.  (\   /)   \\          /%%|:   |%%|:   |\          /:   \     |%%. \n ..%%||   \\_//     \____.    /%%%|_   |%%|.___|%\__.     /|.   |\    |%%%.\n ====||    \==\\   /=====|_  /======\__|==|/========|__._/=|____|=\___|====\n %%%%|______\..\\//%%%%%%%%)/%%%%%%%%%%%%%:%%%%%%%%%%%%Y%%%%%%%%%%%:%%%%%%%\n %%%%%%%%%%\/%%%\/%%%%%%%%%°%%%%%%%%%%%%%%.%%%%%%%%%%%%:%%%%%%%%%%%.%%°Adi·\n   ·%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%°·····°%%%°··········°%%%°·········°%%°········°%°··\n        +-------------------» PRESENTS IN 1994 «-------------------+\n\n\n                              Send Answer V0.1\n\n                         done by  @{"BiLBo BaGGIns/MoTioN" link "coder"}\n\n                            guide by @{"tHe aDDiCt" link "guider"} \n\n                           +-------------------+\n                           |  @{"   Features   " link "Intro"}  |              \n                           |  @{" Installation " link "Install"}  |              \n                           |  @{" Instructions " link "Instr"}  |             \n                           |  @{"   Greetings  " link "Greet"}  |\n                           |  @{"  Last Words  " link "Last"}  |            \n                           |  @{"   CaLL NoW   " link "Call"}  |\n                           +-------------------+\n\n@endnode\n@Node coder "--> BiLBo BaGGIns/MoTioN <--"\n\n That`s me, the coder of that util. If you found any bugs or know any\n improvements please contact me. Also contact me if you wanna have a special\n version for your BBS.\n I changed my handle from Bilbo to BiLBo BaGGins. But not on all BBS, so\n if you wanna contact me better mail to Bilbo*.\n I have double accounts with Sisko so you can although try Sisko*.\n\n\n                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n@Node guider "--> tHe aDDiCt <--"\n\n Yeahhh that`s me, tHe aDDiCt. The machine who made this guide.\n\n\n                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n@Node Intro "--> Features <--"\n\n I was not happy with all the quest doors avaible. All these doors wher big\n and used there own format. I wanted a door, that uses the internal /X\n routines. So I wrote Send Answer. It tooks the Answers from a user out of\n the TempAns file and writes a mail to the sysop with it. It then writes a\n mail to all Users, that a new User is in.\n\n * Mails the Answers to the Sysop\n * Mails an eall to all Users, that a new User is in\n * compiled AREXX for more speed\n * no backdoors\n * if you`ve got no CoProc contact me and you get a working version\n   for your system\n\n\n                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n@Node Install "--> Installation <--"\n\n Extract the whole User Answer Shower archive to your RAM.\n\n\n /X2.x: Append the following Line to your\n        BBS:Commands/BBS.CMD File:\n        ---------------------->> Cut Here <<--------------------------\n        sendanswer    RM200DOORS:Answer/SendAnswer.exe\n        ---------------------->> Cut Here <<--------------------------\n\n /X3.x: For installing on that systems make your own Icon and place it\n        in your BBS:Commands/BBS.CMD drawer.\n\n\n Edit your SendAnswer.cfg file:\n >BBS:Lamer\n Enter here the path and name of the Conference where the mails should be\n posted.\n\n \n Edit your SendAnswer.txt:\n example:\n                               Nice to have you in\n                   Your answers will be send to the Sysop now\n This file will be shown when the door starts\n\n Edit your joined.txt file(s):\n ~CC_sendanswer\n This will start the door when the user answered the questions.\n\n Copy the rexxsupport.library to your Libs directory.\n\n Be sure, that you have the following files: (otherwise the door won`t work)\n\n * TempAns in the BBS:NodeX dirs\n * the correct path of the New User Conference in the SendAnswer.cfg file\n\n\n                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n@Node Instr "--> Instruction <--"\n\n Nothing to say everything will be done automatically.\n\n\n                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n\n@Node Plans "--> Future Plans <--"\n\n * maybe convert it to C when I have time\n\n\n                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n@node Greet "---> Greetings <---"\n\n                              Greetings go to\n          Andy/MoTioN...........thx for the great help in coding\n          Sisko/MoTioN..........greatest account killing leecher\n          Spider/Osiris.................thx for help in coding C\n          Incubus/GOD.......................keep on trading dude\n          \X/arhawk/Logic................Strip`n Add is the best\n          Eazy-e/Taurus...........................PC user now !?\n          Schwabenpower/MoTioN............cewl long chats hehehe\n          tHe aDDiCt.....................................machine\n          Striker/TRZ..............................Sisko rulez!!\n                     and all the rest I have forgotten\n\n           Thanx for the help on releasing this door must go to\n          Andy/MoTioN.............................help in coding\n          tHe aDDiCt..................................guide file\n          Sisko/MOTioN...............................betatesting\n\n\n                                 @{" WOW ! " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n\n@Node Last "---> Last Words <---"\n\n                      Other MoTioN /X tools avaible:\n\n Multi-Diz....................New DIZ system for all files.............Andy\n News In All Conferences......Showing `n s u` in all conferences.......Andy\n On-Line-Message..............Sending online message...................Andy\n OnLineBulletinsUpdater.......Updating bulls if ya wanna se it.........Andy\n PlaY-PeN-PaRt-UpLoAD-MoVeR...Moves files after a system crash.........Andy\n LHADo........................LHA-Checker/Stripper/Adder................BBC\n Textstripper.................Text-Stripper/Adder.......................BBC\n Dream Status.................Status door.............................Bilbo\n StarTrek.....................Star Trek comment door..................Bilbo\n Frontstatus..................Frontend door...........................Bilbo\n Userlist.....................Creates userlist bulletin...............Bilbo\n FileIDAdd....................Add your line to FileID.........BiLBo BaGGins\n User Answer Shower...........Shows the new user answers......BiLBo BaGGins\n SendAnswer...................Sends User Answer to Sysop......BiLBo BaGGins\n\n                      MoTioN -  The Force that moves\n\n\n                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n\n@Node Call "---> Call Now <---"\n\n                          MoTioN boards worldwide:\n\n DEEP SPACE NINE     WHQ        #1: +49-7-Ask-For-IT V32.bis   Sisko\n                          2 Ndz RD: +49-7-Ask-For-IT DST 21.6\n                          2 Ndz RD: +49-7-Ask-For-IT ISDN\n SANITARIUM          GHQ        #1: +49-8-Ask-For-IT DST       jMS\n                                #2: +49-8-Ask-For-IT DST\n                                #3: +49-8-Ask-For-IT V32.bis\n WILD MARIA          GHQ        #1: +49-7-Ask-For-IT V32.bis   Joe Cool\n                                #2: +49-7-Ask-For-IT V32.bis\n PARANOID ILLUSION  USHQ        #1:  +1-203-859-0335 DST       Buzz\n\n\n                                  @{" ATDT !" link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,36576,6,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048589);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('m_st0_1','M_ST0_1.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/M_ST0_1.LHA',NULL,'XIM','startrek.exe',NULL,'Bilbo/MTN',NULL,'/        /     /  ___/___/     /     /\ // /  /  // /  // /  //  // /  // /  / / // /  /  // /  // /  //  // /  // /  / /',replace('    _____________________________________\n   /        /     /  ___/___/     /     /\\n  // /  /  // /  // /  //  // /  // /  / /\n // /  /  // /  // /  //  // /  // /  / /\n/__/__/__/_____/__/__/___/_____/__/__/ /\n\__\__\__\_____\_____\___\_____\__\__\/[B]\n+-+-+-+- pReSeNtZ aNoThEr /X ToOl -+-+-+-+\n+      Star Trek V0.1 by Bilbo/MTN       +\n+ Star Trek Door for all Express Systems +','\n',char(10)),'startrek.guide',replace('@database "MoTiOn - Star Trek V0.1"\n@AUTHOR "The aDDiCt"                 \n@(C) "Bilbo/Motion"                  \n@Ver$ "Star Trek V0.1 (01-04-94)   \n@HEIGHT 30\n@Node MAIN "--> Main Menu <--"\n\n  .%%%................%%%....%%%..........%%/\%%.%%%......%%%....%..%....%%\n .%%.%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%.%%%%%%.%%%%%%%%%%%%/  \%%%.%%%%%%%%.%%%%%%%%%%%%%%.\n %%/(_________________/(_____/(___________(____)%/(______%%|\___%.____.%%.%\n %%\                 /      ~\\             /  |//      ~\%|.   \|   ~|%%%.\n .%%\  /\           //   |:   \\  ..   .   /   |/    |    \||    \    |%%%%\n  .%%\/            //    |.    \_/||   |\_/|   |     |.    \|         |%%%.\n ..%%|.  (\   /)   \\          /%%|:   |%%|:   |\          /:   \     |%%. \n ..%%||   \\_//     \____.    /%%%|_   |%%|.___|%\__.     /|.   |\    |%%%.\n ====||    \==\\   /=====|_  /======\__|==|/========|__._/=|____|=\___|====\n %%%%|______\..\\//%%%%%%%%)/%%%%%%%%%%%%%:%%%%%%%%%%%%Y%%%%%%%%%%%:%%%%%%%\n %%%%%%%%%%\/%%%\/%%%%%%%%%°%%%%%%%%%%%%%%.%%%%%%%%%%%%:%%%%%%%%%%%.%%°Adi·\n   ·%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%°·····°%%%°··········°%%%°·········°%%°········°%°··\n        +-------------------» PRESENTS IN 1994 «-------------------+\n\n\n                               Star Trek V0.1\n\n                           done by  @{"Bilbo/MoTioN" link "coder"}\n\n                            guide by @{"tHe aDDiCt" link "guider"} \n\n                           +-------------------+\n                           |  @{"   Features   " link "Intro"}  |              \n                           |  @{" Installation " link "Install"}  |              \n                           |  @{" Instructions " link "Instr"}  |             \n                           |  @{"   Greetings  " link "Greet"}  |\n                           |  @{"  Last Words  " link "Last"}  |            \n                           |  @{"   CaLL NoW   " link "Call"}  |\n                           +-------------------+\n\n@endnode\n@Node coder "--> Bilbo/MoTioN <--"\n\n That`s me, the coder of that door. If you found any bugs or know any\n improvements please contact me. Also contact me if you wanna have a special\n version for your BBS.\n\n\n                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n@Node guider "--> tHe aDDiCt <--"\n\n Yeahhh that`s me, tHe aDDiCt. The cewl dude who made this guide.\n\n\n                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n@Node Intro "--> Features <--"\n\n * displays random comment\n * add as many comments as you want\n * running on all Express Versions (/X 2.xx-3.xx & Sigma Express)\n * no backdoors\n * compiled AREXX\n * tested over monthes\n\n\n                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n@Node Install "--> Installation <--"\n\n Extract the whole Star Trek archiv to you assigned doors dir.\n\n /X2.x: Append the following Line to your\n        BBS:Commands/BBS.CMD File:\n        ---------------------->> Cut Here <<--------------------------\n        *STARTREK     RM010DOORS:StarTrek/StarTrek.exe\n        ---------------------->> Cut Here <<--------------------------\n\n /X3.x: For installing on that systems make your own Icon and place it\n        in your BBS:Commands/BBS.CMD drawer.\n\n Copy the rexxsupport.library to your assigned LIBS: dir.\n\n StarTrek.CFG - The Config File:\n Here are the comments. Add your own comments here. One comment one line\n\n Be sure, that you have the following files: (otherwise the door won`t work)\n * LIBS:rexxsupport.library\n * Doors:StarTrek/StarTrek.cfg\n\n\n                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n@Node Instr "--> Instruction <--"\n\n On dEEP sPACE nINE the door is displayed in the Nodex/Bull10.TXT. With\n the MCI command ~CC_startrek|, but you can also display it in the\n Conf/Bull10.TXT or wherever you want. (Cewl if you have a StarTrek\n Conference!)\n\n\n                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n\n@Node Plans "--> Future Plans <--"\n\n * no more at the moment\n\n\n                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n@node Greet "---> Greetings <---"\n\n                              Greetings go to\n          Andy/MoTioN...........thx for the great help in coding\n          Sisko/MoTioN................greatest friend and tester\n          Spider/Osiris.........where are the Osiris releases ??\n          Incubus/GOD............................keep on trading\n          \X/arhawk/Logic................Strip`n Add is the best\n          Eazy-e/Taurus..............................let`s party\n          Schwabenpower/MoTioN............cewl long chats hehehe\n          tHe aDDiCt.....................................machine\n                     and all the rest I have forgotten\n\n           Thanx for the help on releasing this door must go to\n          Andy/MoTioN.............................help in coding\n          tHe aDDiCt..................................guide file\n\n                           and to my betatester\n              Sisko/MoTioN, jMS/MoTioN, Schwabenpower/MoTioN\n\n\n                                 @{" WOW ! " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n\n@Node Last "---> Last Words <---"\n\n                      Other MoTioN /X tools avaible:\n\n Multi-Diz....................New DIZ system for all files.............Andy\n News In All Conferences......Showing `n s u` in all conferences.......Andy\n On-Line-Message..............Sending online message...................Andy\n OnLineBulletinsUpdater.......Updating bulls if ya wanna se it.........Andy\n PlaY-PeN-PaRt-UpLoAD-MoVeR...Moves files after a system crash.........Andy\n LHADo........................LHA-Checker/Stripper/Adder................BBC\n Textstripper.................Text-Stripper/Adder.......................BBC\n Dream Status.................Status door.............................Bilbo\n StarTrek.....................Star Trek comment door..................Bilbo\n\n                      MoTioN -  The Force that moves\n\n\n                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n\n@Node Call "---> Call Now <---"\n\n                          MoTioN boards worldwide:\n\n FASTWAY             WHQ  6 Ndz RD: +49-714-129-0036 DST 21.6  Andy\n                          2 Ndz RD: +49-714-129-3050 ISDN\n DEEP SPACE NINE     EHQ        #1: +49-715-290-2518 V32.bis   Sisko\n                          2 Ndz RD: +49-715-290-2507 DST 21.6\n                          2 Ndz RD: +49-715-293-8240 ISDN\n GATEWAY TO HELL     GHQ        #1: +49-712-147-8470 DST 16.8  Dragon\n                                #2: +49-712-144-696  DST 16.8\n                          2 Ndz RD: +49-712-194-1590 ISDN\n BLIND DATE          GHQ        #1: +49-714-151-252  HST       Psycho\n                                #2: +49-714-151-759  V32.bis\n SANITARIUM          GHQ        #1: +49-816-566-642  DST       jMS\n                                #2: +49-816-566-738  V32.bis\n SNAKE BITE          GHQ        #1: +49-713-422-682  DST       Schwabenpower\n PARANOID ILLUSION  USHQ        #1:  +1-203-859-0335 DST       Buzz\n\n\n                                  @{" ATDT !" link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',24170,2,0,NULL,NULL,'m_st0_1','scan',1780048634);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('m_stra01','M!STRA01.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/M!STRA01.LHA',NULL,'XIM','_  _    ___ ________   ___    ___',NULL,'gONZALEZ/m!',NULL,'/ \/ \  /   \__  __\_> /   \  /   \ /  \/ \\/  | \\/ .\/ .\/  | \\/  | \\ ::/   ||  \\  |  \\  \\  \\  |  \\  |  \\::',replace('     _  _    ___ ________   ___    ___\n    / \/ \  /   \__  __\_> /   \  /   \\n   /  \/ \\/  | \\/ .\/ .\/  | \\/  | \\\n::/   ||  \\  |  \\  \\  \\  |  \\  |  \\::\n::\ __||___/______/___/___/______/__|__ /::\n===\|=========P=R=E=S=E=N=T=S======[B]|/===\n= /X3.x only    sTRIP bBS aDDIES 0.1      =\n=     bY gONZALEZ/m! & jOE cOOL/m!        =\n===========================================\n','\n',char(10)),'sTRIPADDS.guide',replace('@database "MoTiOn - (-sTRIP bBS aDDIES 0.1-)"\n@AUTHOR "jOE cOOl"                 \n@(C) "gONZALEZ/mOTION & jOE cOOL/mOTION"                  \n@Ver$ "(-sTRIP bBS aDDIES 0.1-) (20-06-94)"\n@HEIGHT 30\n@Node MAIN "(-Main Menu-)"\n\n _____________________________________________________________________\n MoTioN-MoTioN-MoTioN-MoTioN-MoTioN-MoTioN-MoTioN-MoTioN-MoTioN-MoTioN\n ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n            _    _    ____   ______ ____  ____    _____  \n           / \\__/ \\  /    \\ / _  _ \\\\  / /    \\  /  _  \\  \n          /   __  .\\/   | .\\\\// .\\\\//\\/\\/   | .\\/   |  .\\  \n         /    ||   \\\\   |  \\\\/   \\\\/   \\\\   |  \\\\   |   \\\\  \n         \\ ___||____/_______/\\____/\\____/_______/___|___ /  \n          \\| -------] the force that moves: M! [------ |/  \n  \n _____________________________________________________________________\n MoTioN-MoTioN-MoTioN-MoTioN-MoTioN-MoTioN-MoTioN-MoTioN-MoTioN-MoTioN\n ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n\n     +-------------------» PRESENTS IN 1994 «-------------------+\n\n\n                        (-sTRIP bBS aDDIES 0.1-)\n           \n                    by  @{"(-gONZALEZ & jOE cOOL-)" link "coder"}\n                        @{"(-     Features      -)" link "Intro"}                \n                        @{"(-   Installation    -)" link "Install"}                \n                        @{"(-   Instructions    -)" link "Instr"}              \n                        @{"(-    Greetings      -)" link "Greet"}  \n                        @{"(-    Last Words     -)" link "Last"}              \n                        @{"(-     CaLL NoW      -)" link "Call"}  \n                        \n\n@endnode\n@Node coder "(-gONZALEZ & jOE cOOL-)"\n\n Yes, here we are. We checked this Util on a\n A4000/40 /X 3.37 and\n A4000/40 /X 3.38 Board and never found any bug.\n But if you find one or think this tool could be made\n better so just contact us (Gonzalez & Joe Cool)\n or any other Motion Member.\n\n\n\n                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n@Node Intro "(-     Features      -)"\n\n We thought that some boring bbs-addies in the File_Id.Diz \n should be stripped. So that your Filelist will be \n complete without any BBS-addy. \n This tool will clean the File_id.diz before being added \n in your filelist.\n \n * no Backdoors\n * /3.x only\n \n  \n\n\n                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n@Node Install "(-   Installation    -)"\n\n Extract the whole BBS-Addies Stripper to your RAM.\n\n  /X2.x:    sORRY tHIS dOOR dOESN''T wORK oN /X2.x\n\n  /X3.x: 1) Rename your old Examine.info in Syscmd-Drawer\n            to Examin1.info\n         2) Copy the 0-Byte Examin1.info from RAM:Commands/BBSCMD/\n	    to bbs:Commands/BBSCMD/\n         3) Copy then Examin1.info from RAM:COMMANDS/SYSCMD/\n            to bbs:Commands/BBSCMD/\n         4) Copy sTRIPADDS.rEXX to DOORS:FILEID/\n         5) Copy sTRIPADDS.cHECK to DOORS:FILEID/\n         6) Copy sTRIPADDS.sTRIP to DOORS:FILEID/\n\n    *** Complete ***\n\n \n                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n@Node Instr "(- Instruction -)"\n\n  1)  If you wanna have other Files to be checked you have\n      to Edit the sTRIPADDS.cHECK\n\n          cut\n   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n   lha lzh\n   LHA x "{#}" FILE_ID.DIZ T: >NIL:\n   LHA d "{#}" FILE_ID.DIZ >NIL:\n   lha a "{#}" t:FILE_ID.DIZ >NIL:\n   txt doc dok dox nfo\n   FileIDExtract TxtExtract "{#}" TO T:FILE_ID.DIZ >NIL:\n   FileIDExtract TxtDelete "{#}" >nil:\n   FileIDExtract TxtAdd "{#}" TEXT T:FILE_ID.DIZ >NIL:\n   zip\n   UNZIP -x "{#}" FILE_ID.DIZ -d T: >NIL:\n   ZIP -d "{#}" FILE_ID.DIZ >NIL:\n   ZIP -9 "{#}" t:FILE_ID.DIZ >NIL:\n   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n          cut\n\n   e.g.\n   1) lha lzh\n   2) LHA x "{#}" FILE_ID.DIZ T: >NIL:\n   3) LHA d "{#}" FILE_ID.DIZ >NIL:\n   4) lha a "{#}" t:FILE_ID.DIZ >NIL:\n   1) The Files  x.lha and y.lzh will be checked\n   2) The Command to get the File_Id.Diz\n   3) The Command to delete the File_ID.Diz\n   4) The Command to save the new File_ID.Diz\n\n  2)  You have to edit your sTRIPADDS.sTRIP\n\n          cut\n   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n   bBS\n   Fastest!\n   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n          cut\n \n   Now all lines which include this Addys will be deleted\n\n\n\n                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n\n@Node Plans "(- Future Plans -)"\n\n * We wanna code some more useful /X-Tools\n   but next time they will be coded in C\n\n\n                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n@node Greet "(- Greetings -)"\n\n\n\n                              Greetings go to\n          BBC/MoTioN...............thx for your "Chaos-ASM-Kurs" \n          Andy/MoTioN...................biggest greetings to you\n          Sisko/MoTioN..............................Hello to you\n          Incubus/GOD.......................keep on trading dude\n          \\X/arhawk/Logic................Strip`n Add is the best\n          tHe aDDiCt/5D.....................say thanx to Hillary\n          Calypso/GOD...............I think we have to call more\n                     and all the rest I have forgotten\n\n\n\n                                 @{" WOW ! " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n\n@Node Last "(- Last Words -)"\n\n                      Other MoTioN /X tools avaible:\n\n Multi-Diz....................New DIZ system for all files.............Andy\n News In All Conferences......Showing `n s u` in all conferences.......Andy\n On-Line-Message..............Sending online message...................Andy\n OnLineBulletinsUpdater.......Updating bulls if ya wanna se it.........Andy\n PlaY-PeN-PaRt-UpLoAD-MoVeR...Moves files after a system crash.........Andy\n LHADo........................LHA-Checker/Stripper/Adder................BBC\n Textstripper.................Text-Stripper/Adder.......................BBC\n Dream Status.................Status door.............................Bilbo\n StarTrek.....................Star Trek comment door..................Bilbo\n Frontstatus..................Frontend door...........................Bilbo\n Userlist.....................Creates userlist bulletin...............Bilbo\n FileIDAdd....................Add your line to FileID.........BiLBo BaGGins\n User Answer Shower...........Shows the new user answers......BiLBo BaGGins\n SendAnswer...................Sends User Answer to Sysop......BiLBo BaGGins\n sTRIP bBS aDDIES.............Stripps ADDs in File_id.DIZ.gONZALEZ&jOE cOOL\n rEALOG.......................Callerslog Viewer....................gONZALEZ\n nEW uSERS aNSWER.............Shows New Users Answers..............jOE cOOL\n pAGER........................Sysop Pager..........................jOE cOOL\n oPEN.........................Another Open Door....................jOE cOOL\n cOMMENT......................Another Comment Door.................jOE cOOL\n                     \n                      MoTioN -  The Force that moves\n\n\n                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n\n@Node Call "(- Call Now -)"\n\n                          MoTioN boards worldwide:\n\n DEEP SPACE NINE     WHQ        #1: +49-7-Ask-For-IT V32.bis   Sisko\n                          2 Ndz RD: +49-7-Ask-For-IT DST 21.6\n                          2 Ndz RD: +49-7-Ask-For-IT ISDN\n SANITARIUM          GHQ        #1: +49-8-Ask-For-IT DST       jMS\n                                #2: +49-8-Ask-For-IT DST\n                                #3: +49-8-Ask-For-IT V32.bis\n WILD MARIA          GHQ        #1: +49-7-Ask-For-IT V32.bis   Joe Cool\n                                #2: +49-7-Ask-For-IT V32.bis\n PARANOID ILLUSION  USHQ        #1:  +1-203-859-0335 DST       Buzz\n\n\n                                  @{" ATDT !" link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,5951,3,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048589);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('m_tpca07','M!TPCA07.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/M!TPCA07.LHA','BB-TopCa','XIM','BB-TopCa',NULL,'Door/Util',NULL,'./ _\ __ ___|      /gZ! |   \\ //_  l_____/_ - --------------------- l____\\//____/_____/    . m o t i o n .',replace('  __        ._______\n./ _\ __ ___|      /gZ!\n|   \\ //_  l_____/_ - ---------------------\nl____\\//____/_____/    . m o t i o n .\n- ----\/------------------------------------\n               BB-TopCa v0.7\nCallers Door/Util with many options and low\nmemory usage. All designs are extern in\ndatafiles. So you can make your own designs\nfor it now.\n- ------------------- Code: BiLBo BaGGins/M!\n','\n',char(10)),'BB-TopCa.guide',replace('@database BB-TopCa\n@master Coding:Sources/C/Tempest/BB-TopCa/BB-TopCa.guide\n@$VER: 0.7 (09-16-95)\n@author "BiLBo BaGGins/MoTioN"\n@(c) "1995 MoTioN"\n@help "main"\n@wordwrap\n@font topaz.font 8\n@index main\n@index main\n@remark Created with Heddley v1.1 (c) Edd Dumbill 1994\n\n@node "main" "Guide to BB-TopCa v0.7 by BiLBo BaGGins/MoTioN"\n@next "intro"\n\n     _____              ________________________________  ____________\n    |     \  ___________\_______   ___________/         \_\______     \_\n    |     _\/_      /         \     |/       /     |    \\      /    _ /\n    | Mo!  \/    _ /     |    \\    /________\___________/_____/     //\n    |______/     //\___________/----''                         /______/\n          /______/\n                        -^-  Tempest Inovations  -^-\n\n                               BB-TopCa v0.7\n\n                          Code: BiLBo BaGGins/MoTioN\n\n                      @{"          Introduction          " link "intro" 0} \n                      @{"          Installation          " link "install" 0} \n                      @{"          Future Plans          " link "plans" 0} \n                      @{"           Bug Report           " link "bugs" 0} \n                      @{"             Greets             " link "greets" 0} \n                      @{"          Motion Infos          " link "motion" 0}\n                      @{"              Exit              " quit}\n@endnode\n\n@node "intro" "-^- Introduction -^-"\n@next "install"\n@prev "main"\n\n  BB-TopCa is a TopCaller door/util for Tempest with many options. You can\n  make your own designs for it in different ansi types.\n\n  Features:\n  - external designs\n  - very low memory usage (for TopTenCallers <10K with a userbase of 500)\n  - startable as door and util\n  - many options that make it easy to run in the Text-Welcome\n\n\n                            @{" Back to main menu " link "main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "install" "-^- Installation -^-"\n@next "plans"\n@prev "intro"\n\n  Installation:\n  -------------\n\n  Copy BB-TopCa#? to Doors:\n\n\n  Start as a Door:\n\n  Edit the Text-Welcome files(s):\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n  ~TD(Doors:BB-TopCa)\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n\n  Edit the Bulletins.opt file:\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n  [20-,*,*,*,*] =6   |T-DOOR|Tempest:Doors/BB-TopCa\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n\n\n  Start as a Util:\n\n  Edit the Logoff-x.bat files(s):\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n  Doors:BB-TopCa\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n\n  Edit the Bulletins.opt file:\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n  [20-,*,*,*,*] =6   |PRINT|Tempest:Bulletins/TopCaller.txt\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n\n\n  Edit the BB-TopUl.cfg file:\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n  15                                  // Number of entries to be displayed\n  1                                   // Rows (1 <= Rows >= 2 )\n  2                                   // Number of designs\n  0                                   // Screenclear at start (0=Yes, 1=No)\n  0                                   // Pause at end (0=Yes, 1=No)\n  0                                   // Show nonstop (0=Yes, 1=No)\n  0                                   // File (0=New, 1=Append)\n  0                                   // Ansitype (0=Normal, 1=Amiga, 2=Ibm)\n  Tempest:Accounts.data               // Name of the Accounts.data\n  T:Text.txt                          // Name of the outputfile\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n  1.line: The number of users you want to have displayed\n  2.line: The rows you want to have.\n          1 for displaying it in 1 row\n          2 for displaying it in 2 rows\n  3.line: The number of the design you want to have.\n  4.line: If you want a screenclear before displaying\n          0 for Yes\n          1 for No\n  5.line: If you want to have a Pause-Prompt after displaying\n          0 for Yes\n          1 for No\n  6.line: If you want to have it shown nonstop         (only needed by Util)\n          0 for Yes\n          1 for No\n          That is very important if you join some Bulletins to one. As the\n          Nonstop command is a Toggle, you would turn it on/off everytime.\n  7.line: Type of filecreation                        (only needed by Util)\n          0 for creating a new file\n          1 for appending it to an existing file.\n          With that you can join it to an existing file. For example you\n          first create a Lastcaller Bulletin as Text-Welcome, you can than\n          easy append the TopUploaders to it.\n  8.line: Type of ansi you want to have                (only needed by Util)\n          0 for Normal\n          1 for Amiga\n          2 for Ibm\n  8.line: Path and Name of the Accounts.data           (only needed by Util)\n  9.line: Path and Name of the outputfile              (only needed by Util)\n\n\n\n  External designs:\n  -----------------\n\n  The designs are stored in the BB-TopCa.output.x(.ansi|.amiga|.ibm) files.\n  Where x is the number of the design. The output-files must be in the same\n  directory as BB-TopCa.\n  The Door first looks for the ansitype of the User and than tries to open\n  the belonging output-file. If it doesn`t find it, it tries to open the\n  normal output-file without any extension (BB-TopCa.output.x).\n  Than it reads the lines from it, looks for keywords, inserts the belonging\n  datas and displays them.\n\n  You can easily make your own designs. Just make one in your favourite\n  ANSI-Editor and place keywords where you want to have the nodedatas.\n	The keywords look like this: @HANDLE=====....[\n                                    /        |  \\n                                  1/        2|  3\\n\n  1. The beginning of the keyword (e.g.: ''@HANDLE====='' for the handle).\n  2. Fillers. With that you can fill it as long as you want to have the\n     inserted data. You can fill with a character that you want (except ''[''\n     and '']'').\n  3. The ending of the keyword (e.g.: ''['' for inserting from the left side).\n     The last character defines if the data is insterted from the left (''['')\n     or the right ('']'') side.\n\n\n  Structure of the output-files:\n  There are all the lines of the design. The lines that are shown at the\n  top, the userline and the lines at the end.\n  The lines are always placed between two keylines.\n  Top lines between ''@BEGIN_TOP_x'' and ''@END_TOP_x'' (unlimited lines).\n  Line for the users between ''@BEGIN_LINE_x'' and ''@END_LINE_x'' (one line).\n  End lines between ''@BEGIN_END_x'' and ''@END_END_x'' (unlimited lines).\n  Where x is the number of rows.\n\n  Keywords for the user line (1 row):\n  ''@N''            for entry number\n  ''@HANDLE=====''  for Handle\n  ''@LOCATION===''  for Location\n  ''@CALL==''       for Calls\n\n  Keywords for the user line (2 rows):\n  ''@N''            for entry number     (left side)\n  ''@HANDLE=====''  for Handle           (left side)\n  ''@CALL==''       for Calls           (left side)\n  ''@n''            for entry number    (right side)\n  ''@handle=====''  for Handle          (right side)\n  ''@call==''       for Calls           (right side)\n\n  Keywords for the end lines:\n  ''@CALL''         for total Calls\n  ''@MSGS''         for total Messages\n  ''@FIUL''         for total Files uploaded\n  ''@FIDL''         for total Files downloaded\n  ''@MBUL''         for total MBytes uploaded\n  ''@MBDL''         for total MBytes downloaded\n\n\n                            @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "plans" "-^- Future Plans -^-"\n@next "bugs"\n@prev "install"\n\n  Make more keywords for more datas. If you know some improvments contact\n  me and I will try to insert them.\n\n\n                            @{" Back to main menu " link "main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "bugs" "-^- Bug Report -^-"\n@next "greets"\n@prev "plans"\n\n  I hope there are no bugs in it, but nobody is perfect. So don`t hesitate\n  and tell me any bug you find. I can only remove bugs that I know.\n\n\n                            @{" Back to main menu " link "main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "greets" "-^- Greetings flow out to -^-"\n@next "motion"\n@prev "bugs"\n\n                        my personal Greetings go to\n                        ¯ ¯¯ ¯¯¯ ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯ ¯¯¯ ¯¯ ¯\n  2fast  Agent  AMO/ORS  APEX  Aquarius/OTL   BBC/M!   Ben/M!   Bezzzerk/M!\n  Calypso/GOD      Castor/PDX      Deathknight/PSG       Demax^Agressor/DLT\n  Dr. Dre/TRSI   Duke/M!    Echo&Guido    ECS/TRSI    E.F.A./M!    Fnord/M!\n  Fury/M!   Intercode/BB   JAF    Joker    Juan/TRSI    Kingpin    Logic/M!\n  Mario/TRSI     Marky&Power/BLH     Mogue/AC     Mr.Solo/RNX     Pitch/RBS\n  Playmate/M!   Princip/M!   Profex    Relief/oS    Rhetor/M!    sCANDIC/M!\n  Schwabenpower/M!   Shane/CRX   Shapechanger/DeZIGN   Sisko/M!    Skeleton\n  Skywalker    sNIKE    Spider/ORS    Striker    Tango/OGN    The Addict/M!\n  Tom/FLT            Treach/AC            Vampire/TRSI             Zinko/PB\n\n                        all MoTioN members worldwide\n                      and all the rest I have forgotten\n\n\n                            @{" Back to main menu " link "main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "motion" "-^- MoTioN Informations -^-"\n@prev "greets"\n\n                       the crazy ones behind MoTioN are \n                       ¯ ¯¯ ¯¯¯ ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯ ¯¯¯ ¯¯ ¯\n               BBC · Ben · Bezzzerk · BiLBo BaGGins · Bloodwolf\n              Bowen · Disque Bleu · Duke · E.F.A. · Fnord · Fury\n                KiNGPin · lOGIC · pLaYmAte · ¶r¡nçe Øf Th¡eves\n               pRINCIP · Rhetor · RTD · sCANDIC · SchwabenPower\n                    sISKO · tHE aDDICT · tRAITOR · Wendigo\n\n\n                       call our crazy boards worldwide\n                       ¯ ¯¯ ¯¯¯ ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯ ¯¯¯ ¯¯ ¯\n             WHQ....Mortuary................+1-aSK-fOR-iT!...6nDZ\n             EHQ....Deep Space Nine........+49-aSK-fOR-iT!...6nDZ\n             GHQ....FastFileSystem.........+49-aSK-fOR-iT!...9nDZ\n             SWIHQ..Dial Hard..............+41-aSK-fOR-iT!...5nDZ\n             SHQ....Interchange............+46-aSK-fOR-iT!...3nDZ\n             OZHQ...Dark Sun...............+61-aSK-fOR-iT!...3nDZ\n             DKHQ...Northern Palace........+45-aSK-fOR-iT!...3nDZ\n             NHQ....Checkpoint.............+47-aSK-fOR-iT!...2nDZ\n\n\n                            @{" Back to main menu " link "main" 0}\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),'{"LOCATION":"==''"}','auto-added',19728,5,0,NULL,NULL,'m_tpca07','scan',1780048589);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('m_tpdl07','M!TPDL07.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/M!TPDL07.LHA','BB-TopDl','XIM','BB-TopDl',NULL,'Door/Util',NULL,'./ _\ __ ___|      /gZ! |   \\ //_  l_____/_ - --------------------- l____\\//____/_____/    . m o t i o n .',replace('  __        ._______\n./ _\ __ ___|      /gZ!\n|   \\ //_  l_____/_ - ---------------------\nl____\\//____/_____/    . m o t i o n .\n- ----\/------------------------------------\n               BB-TopDl v0.7\nDownloader Door/Util with many options and\nlow memory usage. All designs are extern in\ndatafiles. So you can make your own designs\nfor it now.\n- ------------------- Code: BiLBo BaGGins/M!\n','\n',char(10)),'BB-TopDl.guide',replace('@database BB-TopDl\n@master Coding:Sources/C/Tempest/BB-TopDl/BB-TopDl.guide\n@$VER: 0.7 (09-16-95)\n@author "BiLBo BaGGins/MoTioN"\n@(c) "1995 MoTioN"\n@help "main"\n@wordwrap\n@font topaz.font 8\n@index main\n@index main\n@remark Created with Heddley v1.1 (c) Edd Dumbill 1994\n\n@node "main" "Guide to BB-TopDl v0.7 by BiLBo BaGGins/MoTioN"\n@next "intro"\n\n     _____              ________________________________  ____________\n    |     \  ___________\_______   ___________/         \_\______     \_\n    |     _\/_      /         \     |/       /     |    \\      /    _ /\n    | Mo!  \/    _ /     |    \\    /________\___________/_____/     //\n    |______/     //\___________/----''                         /______/\n          /______/\n                        -^-  Tempest Inovations  -^-\n\n                               BB-TopDl v0.7\n\n                          Code: BiLBo BaGGins/MoTioN\n\n                      @{"          Introduction          " link "intro" 0} \n                      @{"          Installation          " link "install" 0} \n                      @{"          Future Plans          " link "plans" 0} \n                      @{"           Bug Report           " link "bugs" 0} \n                      @{"             Greets             " link "greets" 0} \n                      @{"          Motion Infos          " link "motion" 0}\n                      @{"              Exit              " quit}\n@endnode\n\n@node "intro" "-^- Introduction -^-"\n@next "install"\n@prev "main"\n\n  BB-TopDl is a TopDownloader door/util for Tempest with many options. You\n  can make your own designs for it in different ansi types.\n\n  Features:\n  - external designs\n  - very low memory usage (for TopTenDownloaders <10K with a userbase of\n    500)\n  - startable as door and util\n  - many options that make it easy to run in the Text-Welcome\n\n\n                            @{" Back to main menu " link "main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "install" "-^- Installation -^-"\n@next "plans"\n@prev "intro"\n\n  Installation:\n  -------------\n\n  Copy BB-TopDl#? to Doors:\n\n\n  Start as a Door:\n\n  Edit the Text-Welcome files(s):\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n  ~TD(Doors:BB-TopDl)\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n\n  Edit the Bulletins.opt file:\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n  [20-,*,*,*,*] =4   |T-DOOR|Tempest:Doors/BB-TopDl\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n\n\n  Start as a Util:\n\n  Edit the Logoff-x.bat files(s):\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n  Doors:BB-TopDl\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n\n  Edit the Bulletins.opt file:\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n  [20-,*,*,*,*] =4   |PRINT|Tempest:Bulletins/TopDownloader.txt\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n\n\n  Edit the BB-TopDl.cfg file:\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n  15                                  // Number of entries to be displayed\n  1                                   // Rows (1 <= Rows >= 2 )\n  2                                   // Number of designs\n  0                                   // Screenclear at start (0=Yes, 1=No)\n  0                                   // Pause at end (0=Yes, 1=No)\n  0                                   // Show nonstop (0=Yes, 1=No)\n  0                                   // File (0=New, 1=Append)\n  0                                   // Ansitype (0=Normal, 1=Amiga, 2=Ibm)\n  Tempest:Accounts.data               // Name of the Accounts.data\n  T:Text.txt                          // Name of the outputfile\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n  1.line: The number of users you want to have displayed\n  2.line: The rows you want to have.\n          1 for displaying it in 1 row\n          2 for displaying it in 2 rows\n  3.line: The number of the design you want to have.\n  4.line: If you want a screenclear before displaying\n          0 for Yes\n          1 for No\n  5.line: If you want to have a Pause-Prompt after displaying\n          0 for Yes\n          1 for No\n  6.line: If you want to have it shown nonstop         (only needed by Util)\n          0 for Yes\n          1 for No\n          That is very important if you join some Bulletins to one. As the\n          Nonstop command is a Toggle, you would turn it on/off everytime.\n  7.line: Type of filecreation                        (only needed by Util)\n          0 for creating a new file\n          1 for appending it to an existing file.\n          With that you can join it to an existing file. For example you\n          first create a Lastcaller Bulletin as Text-Welcome, you can than\n          easy append the TopDownloaders to it.\n  8.line: Type of ansi you want to have                (only needed by Util)\n          0 for Normal\n          1 for Amiga\n          2 for Ibm\n  8.line: Path and Name of the Accounts.data           (only needed by Util)\n  9.line: Path and Name of the outputfile              (only needed by Util)\n\n\n\n  External designs:\n  -----------------\n\n  The designs are stored in the BB-TopDl.output.x(.ansi|.amiga|.ibm) files.\n  Where x is the number of the design. The output-files must be in the same\n  directory as BB-TopDl.\n  The Door first looks for the ansitype of the User and than tries to open\n  the belonging output-file. If it doesn`t find it, it tries to open the\n  normal output-file without any extension (BB-TopDl.output.x).\n  Than it reads the lines from it, looks for keywords, inserts the belonging\n  datas and displays them.\n\n  You can easily make your own designs. Just make one in your favourite\n  ANSI-Editor and place keywords where you want to have the nodedatas.\n	The keywords look like this: @HANDLE=====....[\n                                    /        |  \\n                                  1/        2|  3\\n\n  1. The beginning of the keyword (e.g.: ''@HANDLE====='' for the handle).\n  2. Fillers. With that you can fill it as long as you want to have the\n     inserted data. You can fill with a character that you want (except ''[''\n     and '']'').\n  3. The ending of the keyword (e.g.: ''['' for inserting from the left side).\n     The last character defines if the data is insterted from the left (''['')\n     or the right ('']'') side.\n\n\n  Structure of the output-files:\n  There are all the lines of the design. The lines that are shown at the\n  top, the userline and the lines at the end.\n  The lines are always placed between two keylines.\n  Top lines between ''@BEGIN_TOP_x'' and ''@END_TOP_x'' (unlimited lines).\n  Line for the users between ''@BEGIN_LINE_x'' and ''@END_LINE_x'' (one line).\n  End lines between ''@BEGIN_END_x'' and ''@END_END_x'' (unlimited lines).\n  Where x is the number of rows.\n\n  Keywords for the user line (1 row):\n  ''@N''            for entry number\n  ''@HANDLE=====''  for Handle\n  ''@LOCATION===''  for Location\n  ''@DLBYTES====''  for downloaded Bytes\n  ''@DLFI''         for downloaded Files\n  ''@CALL''         for Calls\n  ''@MSGS''         for Messages\n  ''@RATI''         for Ratio (6 chars)\n\n  Keywords for the user line (2 rows):\n  ''@N''            for entry number     (left side)\n  ''@HANDLE=====''  for Handle           (left side)\n  ''@DLBYTES====''  for downloaded Bytes   (left side)\n  ''@DLFI''         for downloaded Files   (left side)\n  ''@R''            for Ratio (6 chars)  (left side)\n  ''@n''            for entry number    (right side)\n  ''@handle=====''  for Handle          (right side)\n  ''@dlbytes====''  for downloaded Bytes  (right side)\n  ''@dlfi''         for downloaded Files  (right side)\n  ''@r''            for Ratio (6 chars) (right side)\n\n  Keywords for the end lines:\n  ''@CALL''         for total Calls\n  ''@MSGS''         for total Messages\n  ''@FIUL''         for total Files uploaded\n  ''@FIDL''         for total Files downloaded\n  ''@MBUL''         for total MBytes uploaded\n  ''@MBDL''         for total MBytes downloaded\n\n\n                            @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "plans" "-^- Future Plans -^-"\n@next "bugs"\n@prev "install"\n\n  Make more keywords for more datas. If you know some improvments contact\n  me and I will try to insert them.\n\n\n                            @{" Back to main menu " link "main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "bugs" "-^- Bug Report -^-"\n@next "greets"\n@prev "plans"\n\n  I hope there are no bugs in it, but nobody is perfect. So don`t hesitate\n  and tell me any bug you find. I can only remove bugs that I know.\n\n\n                            @{" Back to main menu " link "main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "greets" "-^- Greetings flow out to -^-"\n@next "motion"\n@prev "bugs"\n\n                        my personal Greetings go to\n                        ¯ ¯¯ ¯¯¯ ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯ ¯¯¯ ¯¯ ¯\n  2fast  Agent  AMO/ORS  APEX  Aquarius/OTL   BBC/M!   Ben/M!   Bezzzerk/M!\n  Calypso/GOD      Castor/PDX      Deathknight/PSG       Demax^Agressor/DLT\n  Dr. Dre/TRSI   Duke/M!    Echo&Guido    ECS/TRSI    E.F.A./M!   