INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('m_tpul07','M!TPUL07.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/M!TPUL07.LHA','BB-TopUl','XIM','BB-TopUl',NULL,'Door/Util',NULL,'./ _\ __ ___|      /gZ! |   \\ //_  l_____/_ - --------------------- l____\\//____/_____/    . m o t i o n .',replace('  __        ._______\n./ _\ __ ___|      /gZ!\n|   \\ //_  l_____/_ - ---------------------\nl____\\//____/_____/    . m o t i o n .\n- ----\/------------------------------------\n               BB-TopUl v0.7\nUploader Door/Util with many options and low\nmemory usage. All designs are extern in\ndatafiles. So you can make your own designs\nfor it now.\n- ------------------- Code: BiLBo BaGGins/M!\n','\n',char(10)),'BB-TopUl.guide',replace('@database BB-TopUl\n@master Coding:Sources/C/Tempest/BB-TopUl/BB-TopUl.guide\n@$VER: 0.7 (09-16-95)\n@author "BiLBo BaGGins/MoTioN"\n@(c) "1995 MoTioN"\n@help "main"\n@wordwrap\n@font topaz.font 8\n@index main\n@index main\n@remark Created with Heddley v1.1 (c) Edd Dumbill 1994\n\n@node "main" "Guide to BB-TopUl v0.7 by BiLBo BaGGins/MoTioN"\n@next "intro"\n\n     _____              ________________________________  ____________\n    |     \  ___________\_______   ___________/         \_\______     \_\n    |     _\/_      /         \     |/       /     |    \\      /    _ /\n    | Mo!  \/    _ /     |    \\    /________\___________/_____/     //\n    |______/     //\___________/----''                         /______/\n          /______/\n                        -^-  Tempest Inovations  -^-\n\n                               BB-TopUl v0.7\n\n                          Code: BiLBo BaGGins/MoTioN\n\n                      @{"          Introduction          " link "intro" 0} \n                      @{"          Installation          " link "install" 0} \n                      @{"          Future Plans          " link "plans" 0} \n                      @{"           Bug Report           " link "bugs" 0} \n                      @{"             Greets             " link "greets" 0} \n                      @{"          Motion Infos          " link "motion" 0}\n                      @{"              Exit              " quit}\n@endnode\n\n@node "intro" "-^- Introduction -^-"\n@next "install"\n@prev "main"\n\n  BB-TopUl is a TopUploader door/util for Tempest with many options. You can\n  make your own designs for it in different ansi types.\n\n  Features:\n  - external designs\n  - very low memory usage (for TopTenUploaders <10K with a userbase of 500)\n  - startable as door and util\n  - many options that make it easy to run in the Text-Welcome\n\n\n                            @{" Back to main menu " link "main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "install" "-^- Installation -^-"\n@next "plans"\n@prev "intro"\n\n  Installation:\n  -------------\n\n  Copy BB-TopUl#? to Doors:\n\n\n  Start as a Door:\n\n  Edit the Text-Welcome files(s):\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n  ~TD(Doors:BB-TopUl)\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n\n  Edit the Bulletins.opt file:\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n  [20-,*,*,*,*] =3   |T-DOOR|Tempest:Doors/BB-TopUl\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n\n\n  Start as a Util:\n\n  Edit the Logoff-x.bat files(s):\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n  Doors:BB-TopUl\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n\n  Edit the Bulletins.opt file:\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n  [20-,*,*,*,*] =3   |PRINT|Tempest:Bulletins/TopUploader.txt\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n\n\n  Edit the BB-TopUl.cfg file:\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n  15                                  // Number of entries to be displayed\n  1                                   // Rows (1 <= Rows >= 2 )\n  2                                   // Number of designs\n  0                                   // Screenclear at start (0=Yes, 1=No)\n  0                                   // Pause at end (0=Yes, 1=No)\n  0                                   // Show nonstop (0=Yes, 1=No)\n  0                                   // File (0=New, 1=Append)\n  0                                   // Ansitype (0=Normal, 1=Amiga, 2=Ibm)\n  Tempest:Accounts.data               // Name of the Accounts.data\n  T:Text.txt                          // Name of the outputfile\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n  1.line: The number of users you want to have displayed\n  2.line: The rows you want to have.\n          1 for displaying it in 1 row\n          2 for displaying it in 2 rows\n  3.line: The number of the design you want to have.\n  4.line: If you want a screenclear before displaying\n          0 for Yes\n          1 for No\n  5.line: If you want to have a Pause-Prompt after displaying\n          0 for Yes\n          1 for No\n  6.line: If you want to have it shown nonstop         (only needed by Util)\n          0 for Yes\n          1 for No\n          That is very important if you join some Bulletins to one. As the\n          Nonstop command is a Toggle, you would turn it on/off everytime.\n  7.line: Type of filecreation                        (only needed by Util)\n          0 for creating a new file\n          1 for appending it to an existing file.\n          With that you can join it to an existing file. For example you\n          first create a Lastcaller Bulletin as Text-Welcome, you can than\n          easy append the TopUploaders to it.\n  8.line: Type of ansi you want to have                (only needed by Util)\n          0 for Normal\n          1 for Amiga\n          2 for Ibm\n  8.line: Path and Name of the Accounts.data           (only needed by Util)\n  9.line: Path and Name of the outputfile              (only needed by Util)\n\n\n\n  External designs:\n  -----------------\n\n  The designs are stored in the BB-TopUl.output.x(.ansi|.amiga|.ibm) files.\n  Where x is the number of the design. The output-files must be in the same\n  directory as BB-TopUl.\n  The Door first looks for the ansitype of the User and than tries to open\n  the belonging output-file. If it doesn`t find it, it tries to open the\n  normal output-file without any extension (BB-TopUl.output.x).\n  Than it reads the lines from it, looks for keywords, inserts the belonging\n  datas and displays them.\n\n  You can easily make your own designs. Just make one in your favourite\n  ANSI-Editor and place keywords where you want to have the nodedatas.\n	The keywords look like this: @HANDLE=====....[\n                                    /        |  \\n                                  1/        2|  3\\n\n  1. The beginning of the keyword (e.g.: ''@HANDLE====='' for the handle).\n  2. Fillers. With that you can fill it as long as you want to have the\n     inserted data. You can fill with a character that you want (except ''[''\n     and '']'').\n  3. The ending of the keyword (e.g.: ''['' for inserting from the left side).\n     The last character defines if the data is insterted from the left (''['')\n     or the right ('']'') side.\n\n\n  Structure of the output-files:\n  There are all the lines of the design. The lines that are shown at the\n  top, the userline and the lines at the end.\n  The lines are always placed between two keylines.\n  Top lines between ''@BEGIN_TOP_x'' and ''@END_TOP_x'' (unlimited lines).\n  Line for the users between ''@BEGIN_LINE_x'' and ''@END_LINE_x'' (one line).\n  End lines between ''@BEGIN_END_x'' and ''@END_END_x'' (unlimited lines).\n  Where x is the number of rows.\n\n  Keywords for the user line (1 row):\n  ''@N''            for entry number\n  ''@HANDLE=====''  for Handle\n  ''@LOCATION===''  for Location\n  ''@ULBYTES====''  for uploaded Bytes\n  ''@ULFI''         for uploaded Files\n  ''@CALL''         for Calls\n  ''@MSGS''         for Messages\n  ''@RATI''         for Ratio (6 chars)\n\n  Keywords for the user line (2 rows):\n  ''@N''            for entry number     (left side)\n  ''@HANDLE=====''  for Handle           (left side)\n  ''@ULBYTES====''  for uploaded Bytes   (left side)\n  ''@ULFI''         for uploaded Files   (left side)\n  ''@R''            for Ratio (6 chars)  (left side)\n  ''@n''            for entry number    (right side)\n  ''@handle=====''  for Handle          (right side)\n  ''@ulbytes====''  for uploaded Bytes  (right side)\n  ''@ulfi''         for uploaded Files  (right side)\n  ''@r''            for Ratio (6 chars) (right side)\n\n  Keywords for the end lines:\n  ''@CALL''         for total Calls\n  ''@MSGS''         for total Messages\n  ''@FIUL''         for total Files uploaded\n  ''@FIDL''         for total Files downloaded\n  ''@MBUL''         for total MBytes uploaded\n  ''@MBDL''         for total MBytes downloaded\n\n\n                            @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "plans" "-^- Future Plans -^-"\n@next "bugs"\n@prev "install"\n\n  Make more keywords for more datas. If you know some improvments contact\n  me and I will try to insert them.\n\n\n                            @{" Back to main menu " link "main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "bugs" "-^- Bug Report -^-"\n@next "greets"\n@prev "plans"\n\n  I hope there are no bugs in it, but nobody is perfect. So don`t hesitate\n  and tell me any bug you find. I can only remove bugs that I know.\n\n\n                            @{" Back to main menu " link "main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "greets" "-^- Greetings flow out to -^-"\n@next "motion"\n@prev "bugs"\n\n                        my personal Greetings go to\n                        ¯ ¯¯ ¯¯¯ ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯ ¯¯¯ ¯¯ ¯\n  2fast  Agent  AMO/ORS  APEX  Aquarius/OTL   BBC/M!   Ben/M!   Bezzzerk/M!\n  Calypso/GOD      Castor/PDX      Deathknight/PSG       Demax^Agressor/DLT\n  Dr. Dre/TRSI   Duke/M!    Echo&Guido    ECS/TRSI    E.F.A./M!    Fnord/M!\n  Fury/M!   Intercode/BB   JAF    Joker    Juan/TRSI    Kingpin    Logic/M!\n  Mario/TRSI     Marky&Power/BLH     Mogue/AC     Mr.Solo/RNX     Pitch/RBS\n  Playmate/M!   Princip/M!   Profex    Relief/oS    Rhetor/M!    sCANDIC/M!\n  Schwabenpower/M!   Shane/CRX   Shapechanger/DeZIGN   Sisko/M!    Skeleton\n  Skywalker    sNIKE    Spider/ORS    Striker    Tango/OGN    The Addict/M!\n  Tom/FLT            Treach/AC            Vampire/TRSI             Zinko/PB\n\n                        all MoTioN members worldwide\n                      and all the rest I have forgotten\n\n\n                            @{" Back to main menu " link "main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "motion" "-^- MoTioN Informations -^-"\n@prev "greets"\n\n                       the crazy ones behind MoTioN are \n                       ¯ ¯¯ ¯¯¯ ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯ ¯¯¯ ¯¯ ¯\n               BBC · Ben · Bezzzerk · BiLBo BaGGins · Bloodwolf\n              Bowen · Disque Bleu · Duke · E.F.A. · Fnord · Fury\n                KiNGPin · lOGIC · pLaYmAte · ¶r¡nçe Øf Th¡eves\n               pRINCIP · Rhetor · RTD · sCANDIC · SchwabenPower\n                    sISKO · tHE aDDICT · tRAITOR · Wendigo\n\n\n                       call our crazy boards worldwide\n                       ¯ ¯¯ ¯¯¯ ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯ ¯¯¯ ¯¯ ¯\n             WHQ....Mortuary................+1-aSK-fOR-iT!...6nDZ\n             EHQ....Deep Space Nine........+49-aSK-fOR-iT!...6nDZ\n             GHQ....FastFileSystem.........+49-aSK-fOR-iT!...9nDZ\n             SWIHQ..Dial Hard..............+41-aSK-fOR-iT!...5nDZ\n             SHQ....Interchange............+46-aSK-fOR-iT!...3nDZ\n             OZHQ...Dark Sun...............+61-aSK-fOR-iT!...3nDZ\n             DKHQ...Northern Palace........+45-aSK-fOR-iT!...3nDZ\n             NHQ....Checkpoint.............+47-aSK-fOR-iT!...2nDZ\n\n\n                            @{" Back to main menu " link "main" 0}\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),'{"LOCATION":"==''"}','auto-added',19414,4,0,NULL,NULL,'m_tpul07','scan',1780048589);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('m_uas11','M!UAS11.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/M!UAS11.LHA',NULL,'XIM','_____________________________________',NULL,'BiLBo',NULL,'/        /     /  ___/___/     /     /\ // /  /  // /  // /  //  // /  // /  / / // /  /  // /  // /  //  // /  // /  / /',replace('    _____________________________________\n   /        /     /  ___/___/     /     /\\n  // /  /  // /  // /  //  // /  // /  / /\n // /  /  // /  // /  //  // /  // /  / /\n/__/__/__/_____/__/__/___/_____/__/__/ /\n\__\__\__\_____\_____\___\_____\__\__\/[B]\n+pReSeNtZ >UserAnswerShower v1.1< /X ToOl+\n+ Door that shows a users new users      +\n+ answers out of the TempAns or Answer   +\n+ files                                  +\n+ running on all /X Systems              +\n+                by BiLBo BaGGIns/MoTioN +\n','\n',char(10)),'Answer.guide',replace('@database "MoTiOn - User Answer Shower V1.1"\n@AUTHOR "The aDDiCt"                 \n@(C) "BiLBo BaGGIns/Motion"                  \n@Ver$ "User Answer Shower V1.1 (10-03-94)"\n@HEIGHT 30\n@Node MAIN "--> Main Menu <--"\n\n  .%%%................%%%....%%%..........%%/\%%.%%%......%%%....%..%....%%\n .%%.%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%.%%%%%%.%%%%%%%%%%%%/  \%%%.%%%%%%%%.%%%%%%%%%%%%%%.\n %%/(_________________/(_____/(___________(____)%/(______%%|\___%.____.%%.%\n %%\                 /      ~\\             /  |//      ~\%|.   \|   ~|%%%.\n .%%\  /\           //   |:   \\  ..   .   /   |/    |    \||    \    |%%%%\n  .%%\/            //    |.    \_/||   |\_/|   |     |.    \|         |%%%.\n ..%%|.  (\   /)   \\          /%%|:   |%%|:   |\          /:   \     |%%. \n ..%%||   \\_//     \____.    /%%%|_   |%%|.___|%\__.     /|.   |\    |%%%.\n ====||    \==\\   /=====|_  /======\__|==|/========|__._/=|____|=\___|====\n %%%%|______\..\\//%%%%%%%%)/%%%%%%%%%%%%%:%%%%%%%%%%%%Y%%%%%%%%%%%:%%%%%%%\n %%%%%%%%%%\/%%%\/%%%%%%%%%°%%%%%%%%%%%%%%.%%%%%%%%%%%%:%%%%%%%%%%%.%%°Adi·\n   ·%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%°·····°%%%°··········°%%%°·········°%%°········°%°··\n        +-------------------» PRESENTS IN 1994 «-------------------+\n\n\n                          User Answer Shower V1.1\n\n                         done by  @{"BiLBo BaGGIns/MoTioN" link "coder"}\n\n                            guide by @{"tHe aDDiCt" link "guider"} \n\n                           +-------------------+\n                           |  @{"   Features   " link "Intro"}  |              \n                           |  @{" Installation " link "Install"}  |              \n                           |  @{" Instructions " link "Instr"}  |             \n                           |  @{"   Greetings  " link "Greet"}  |\n                           |  @{"  Last Words  " link "Last"}  |            \n                           |  @{"   CaLL NoW   " link "Call"}  |\n                           +-------------------+\n\n@endnode\n@Node coder "--> BiLBo BaGGIns/MoTioN <--"\n\n That`s me, the coder of that util. If you found any bugs or know any\n improvements please contact me. Also contact me if you wanna have a special\n version for your BBS.\n I changed my handle from Bilbo to BiLBo BaGGins. But not on all BBS, so\n if you wanna contact me better mail to Bilbo*.\n\n\n                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n@Node guider "--> tHe aDDiCt <--"\n\n Yeahhh that`s me, tHe aDDiCt. The machine who made this guide.\n\n\n                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n@Node Intro "--> Features <--"\n\n Some days ago other members meant that we should release something now, so\n I wrote the docs to this util now. I coded the util over a month ago but\n never released it coz I was to busy to write the docs. I invested all my\n time in learning C, so all my new doors/utils will be in C now.\n\n * enter users handle and the doors searches for his New User Answers\n   and display them\n * displays TempAnswers on a node you want\n * running on all /X Systems I think\n * no backdoors\n * compiled AREXX (if you have no CoProz contact me and you get a running\n   version for your system)\n\n\n                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n@Node Install "--> Installation <--"\n\n Extract the whole User Answer Shower archive to your assigned doors dir.\n\n /X2.x: Append the following Line to your\n        BBS:Commands/BBS.CMD File:\n        ---------------------->> Cut Here <<--------------------------\n        answer        RM200DOORS:Answer/Answer.exe\n        ---------------------->> Cut Here <<--------------------------\n\n /X3.x: For installing on that systems make your own Icon and place it\n        in your BBS:Commands/BBS.CMD drawer.\n\n Copy the rexxsupport.library to your Libs directory.\n\n Be sure, that you have the following files: (otherwise the door won`t work)\n\n * TempAns in the BBS:NodeX dirs\n * Answers in the BBS:NodeX dirs\n\n                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n@Node Instr "--> Instruction <--"\n\n When you started the door, you will be asked if you wanna see a Tempans\n file of a node or search for a User in the Answer files(s).\n If you choosed `t` for the TempAns file, the door will ask for the node.\n When you entered it it will display it.\n If you choosed `a` for, the door will ask for the users handle. When you\n entered it, it will ask from which node he should start to search. Enter\n the node and the door will search and display the answers if found.\n\n\n                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n\n@Node Plans "--> Future Plans <--"\n\n * maybe convert it to C when I have time\n\n\n                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n@node Greet "---> Greetings <---"\n\n                              Greetings go to\n          Andy/MoTioN...........thx for the great help in coding\n          Sisko/MoTioN..........greatest account killing leecher\n          Spider/Osiris.................thx for help in coding C\n          Incubus/GOD.......................keep on trading dude\n          \X/arhawk/Logic................Strip`n Add is the best\n          Eazy-e/Taurus...........................PC user now !?\n          Schwabenpower/MoTioN............cewl long chats hehehe\n          tHe aDDiCt.....................................machine\n                     and all the rest I have forgotten\n\n           Thanx for the help on releasing this door must go to\n          Andy/MoTioN.............................help in coding\n          tHe aDDiCt..................................guide file\n          Sisko/MOTioN...............................betatesting\n\n\n                                 @{" WOW ! " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n\n@Node Last "---> Last Words <---"\n\n                      Other MoTioN /X tools avaible:\n\n Multi-Diz....................New DIZ system for all files.............Andy\n News In All Conferences......Showing `n s u` in all conferences.......Andy\n On-Line-Message..............Sending online message...................Andy\n OnLineBulletinsUpdater.......Updating bulls if ya wanna se it.........Andy\n PlaY-PeN-PaRt-UpLoAD-MoVeR...Moves files after a system crash.........Andy\n LHADo........................LHA-Checker/Stripper/Adder................BBC\n Textstripper.................Text-Stripper/Adder.......................BBC\n Dream Status.................Status door.............................Bilbo\n StarTrek.....................Star Trek comment door..................Bilbo\n Frontstatus..................Frontend door...........................Bilbo\n Userlist.....................Creates userlist bulletin...............Bilbo\n FileIDAdd....................Add your line to FileID.........BiLBo BaGGins\n User Answer Shower...........Shows the new user answers......BiLBo BaGGins\n\n                      MoTioN -  The Force that moves\n\n\n                           @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n\n@Node Call "---> Call Now <---"\n\n                          MoTioN boards worldwide:\n\n DEEP SPACE NINE     WHQ        #1: +49-7-Ask-For-IT V32.bis   Sisko\n                          2 Ndz RD: +49-7-Ask-For-IT DST 21.6\n                          2 Ndz RD: +49-7-Ask-For-IT ISDN\n SANITARIUM          GHQ        #1: +49-8-Ask-For-IT DST       jMS\n                                #2: +49-8-Ask-For-IT V32.bis\n WILD MARIA          GHQ        #1: +49-7-Ask-For-IT V32.bis   Joe Cool\n                                #2: +49-7-Ask-For-IT V32.bis\n PARANOID ILLUSION  USHQ        #1:  +1-203-859-0335 DST       Buzz\n\n\n                                  @{" ATDT !" link "MAIN"}\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,22754,2,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048589);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('m_wall02','M!WALL02.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/M!WALL02.LHA','BB-Wall','XIM','BB-Wall',NULL,NULL,NULL,'|        |     |  l_ \__/     |     | .__|  |  |  |  |  |  _/_|  |  |  |  |  |___. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  l  |  |  |  |  |  |   |',replace('   .________._____.__.  _________._____.\n   |        |     |  l_ \__/     |     |\n.__|  |  |  |  |  |  _/_|  |  |  |  |  |___.\n|  |  |  |  |  |  |  l  |  |  |  |  |  |   |\n!2Fl__|__|  l_____l__   l__l_____l__|  |___!\n|        `--''        `--''           `--''   |\n|               BB-Wall v0.2               |\n| Nice, little Wall for Tempest.           |\n| Code:BiLBo BaGGins/M!                    |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'BB-Wall.guide',replace('@database BB-Wall\n@master Coding:Sources/C/Tempest/BB-Wall/BB-Wall.guide\n@$VER: 0.2 (07-25-95)\n@author "BiLBo BaGGins/MoTioN"\n@(c) "1995 MoTioN"\n@help "main"\n@wordwrap\n@font topaz.font 8\n@index main\n@index main\n@remark Created with Heddley v1.1 (c) Edd Dumbill 1994\n\n@node "main" "Guide to BB-Wall v0.2 by BiLBo BaGGins/MoTioN"\n@next "intro"\n\n     _____              ________________________________  ____________\n    |     \  ___________\_______   ___________/         \_\______     \_\n    |     _\/_      /         \     |/       /     |    \\      /    _ /\n    | Mo!  \/    _ /     |    \\    /________\___________/_____/     //\n    |______/     //\___________/----''                         /______/\n          /______/\n                        -^-  Tempest Inovations  -^-\n\n                                BB-Wall v0.2\n\n                          cODE: BiLBo BaGGins/MoTioN\n\n                      @{"          iNTRODUCTION          " link "intro" 0} \n                      @{"          iNSTALLATION          " link "install" 0} \n                      @{"          fUTURE pLANS          " link "plans" 0} \n                      @{"           bUG rEPORT           " link "bugs" 0} \n                      @{"             gREETS             " link "greets" 0} \n                      @{"          mOTION iNFOS          " link "motion" 0}\n                      @{"              eXIT              " quit}\n@endnode\n\n@node "intro" "-^- iNTRODUCTION -^-"\n@next "install"\n@prev "main"\n\n  BB-Wall is a nice, little wall for Tempest. It looks exactly like the\n  great one on /X from my friend Calypso.\n\n  Features:\n  - handles up to 10 lines\n  - random color\n  - anonymous posting possible\n\n\n                            @{" bACK tO mAIN mENU " link "main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "install" "-^- iNSTALLATION -^-"\n@next "plans"\n@prev "intro"\n\n  Copy BB-Frontend(.#?) to Doors:\n\n\n  Edit your Text-Welcome file(s):\n  -------------------------> cut here <-------------------------\n  ~TD(Doors:BB-Wall)\n  -------------------------> cut here <-------------------------\n\n\n                            @{" bACK tO mAIN mENU " link "MAIN" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "plans" "-^- fUTURE pLANS -^-"\n@next "bugs"\n@prev "install"\n\n  No more improvments planned at the moment.\n\n\n                            @{" bACK tO mAIN mENU " link "main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "bugs" "-^- buG rEPORT -^-"\n@next "greets"\n@prev "plans"\n\n  It`s running now for some months on DS9 and I found no bugs. If you find\n  any or know some improvments contact me.\n\n\n                            @{" bACK tO mAIN mENU " link "main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "greets" "-^- gREETINGS fLOW oUT tO -^-"\n@next "motion"\n@prev "bugs"\n\n                        mY pERSONAL gREETINGS gO tO\n                        ¯ ¯¯ ¯¯¯ ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯ ¯¯¯ ¯¯ ¯\n\n   2fast · Agent · AMO/ORS · Aquarius/OTL · BBC/M! · Ben/M! · Bezzzerk/M!\n    Calypso/GOD · Castor/PDX · Deathknight/PSG · Dr. Dre/TRSI · Duke/M!\n   ECS/TRSI · E.F.A./M! · Fnord/M! · Fury/M! · Intercode/BB · JAF · Joker\n  Juan/TRSI · Kingpin · Logic/M! · Mario/TRSI · Marky&Power/BLH · Mogue/AC\n        Mr.Solo/RNX ·  Playmate/M! · Princip/M! · Profex · Rhetor/M!\n  Schwabenpower/M! · Shane/CRX · Shapechanger/DeZIGN · Sisko/M! · Skeleton\n    Skywalker · sNIKE · Spider/ORS · Striker · Tango/OGN · The Addict/M!\n                     Tom/FLT · Treach/AC · Vampire/TRSI\n\n                        aLL MoTioN mEMBERS wORLDWIDE\n                      aND aLL tHE rEST I hAVE fORGOTTEN\n\n\n                            @{" bACK tO mAIN mENU " link "main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "motion" "-^- MoTioN iNFORMATIONS -^-"\n@prev "greets"\n\n                       tHE cRAZY oNES bEHIND mOTION aRE \n                       ¯ ¯¯ ¯¯¯ ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯ ¯¯¯ ¯¯ ¯\n          BBC · Ben · Bezzzerk · BiLBo BaGGins · Bloodwolf · Bowen\n             Disque Bleu · Duke · Fnord · Fury · KiNGPin · lOGIC\n       pLaYmAte · Prince of Thieves · pRINCIP · Radar L0VE · rED aLERT\n               Rhetor · RTD · SchwabenPower · sISKO · Wendigo\n\n\n                       cALL oUR cRAZY bOARDS wORLDWIDE\n                       ¯ ¯¯ ¯¯¯ ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯ ¯¯¯ ¯¯ ¯\n             WHQ....Mortuary................+1-aSK-fOR-iT!...6nDZ\n             EHQ....Deep Space Nine........+49-aSK-fOR-iT!...6nDZ\n             SWIHQ..Dial Hard..............+41-aSK-fOR-iT!...5nDZ\n             SHQ....Interchange............+46-aSK-fOR-iT!...3nDZ\n             GHQ....The Addiction..........+49-aSK-fOR-iT!...3nDZ\n             OZHQ...Dark Sun...............+61-aSK-fOR-iT!...3nDZ\n             DKHQ...Northern Palace........+45-aSK-fOR-iT!...3nDZ\n             NHQ....Checkpoint.............+47-aSK-fOR-iT!...2nDZ\n\n\n                            @{" bACK tO mAIN mENU " link "main" 0}\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',13957,5,0,NULL,NULL,'m_wall02','scan',1780048589);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('m_who05','M!WHO05.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/M!WHO05.LHA','BB-Wh','XIM','BB-Wh',NULL,NULL,NULL,'./ _\ __ ___|      /gZ! |   \\ //_  l_____/_ - --------------------- l____\\//____/_____/    . m o t i o n .',replace('  __        ._______\n./ _\ __ ___|      /gZ!\n|   \\ //_  l_____/_ - ---------------------\nl____\\//____/_____/    . m o t i o n .\n- ----\/------------------------------------\n                BB-Who v0.5\nWho, Wh and Whm doors for Tempest. All\ndesigns are extern in datafiles. So you can\nmake your own designs for it now.\n- ------------------- Code: BiLBo BaGGins/M!\n','\n',char(10)),'BB-Who.guide',replace('@database BB-Who\n@master Coding:Sources/C/Tempest/BB-Who/BB-Who.guide\n@$VER: 0.5 (09-17-95)\n@author "BiLBo BaGGins/MoTioN"\n@(c) "1995 MoTioN"\n@help "main"\n@wordwrap\n@font topaz.font 8\n@index main\n@index main\n@remark Created with Heddley v1.1 (c) Edd Dumbill 1994\n\n@node "main" "Guide to BB-Who v0.5 by BiLBo BaGGins/MoTioN"\n@next "intro"\n\n     _____              ________________________________  ____________\n    |     \  ___________\_______   ___________/         \_\______     \_\n    |     _\/_      /         \     |/       /     |    \\      /    _ /\n    | Mo!  \/    _ /     |    \\    /________\___________/_____/     //\n    |______/     //\___________/----''                         /______/\n          /______/\n                        -^-  Tempest Inovations  -^-\n\n                                BB-Who v0.5\n\n                          Code: BiLBo BaGGins/MoTioN\n\n                      @{"          Introduction          " link "intro" 0} \n                      @{"          Installation          " link "install" 0} \n                      @{"          Future Plans          " link "plans" 0} \n                      @{"           Bug Report           " link "bugs" 0} \n                      @{"             Greets             " link "greets" 0} \n                      @{"          Motion Infos          " link "motion" 0}\n                      @{"              Exit              " quit}\n@endnode\n\n@node "intro" "-^- Introduction -^-"\n@next "install"\n@prev "main"\n\n  BB-Who is a who door for Tempest.\n\n  Features:\n  - shows Node, Name, Location, Baud, Activity, Time, Conference\n  - external designs\n\n\n  BB-Wh is a wh door for Tempest.\n\n  Features:\n  - shows Node, Name, Location and Action\n  - external designs\n\n\n  BB-Whm is a monitoring wh door for Tempest.\n\n  Features:\n  - shows Node, Name, Location and Action\n  - external designs\n  - monitoring\n\n\n                            @{" Back to main menu " link "main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "install" "-^- Installation -^-"\n@next "plans"\n@prev "intro"\n\n  Copy BB-Wh#? to Doors:\n\n\n  Edit the BB-Wh#?.cfg file:\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n  4                            // Number of Design\n  Y                            // Screenclear at start - (Y)es, (N)o\n  --------------------------> cut here <--------------------------\n\n  1.line: The number of the design you want to have.\n  2.line: If you want a screenclear before displaying\n          Y for Yes\n          N for No\n\n\n  Edit your GlobalMenu.opt file(s):\n  -------------------------> cut here <-------------------------\n  [30-,*,*,*,*]   = who    |T-DOOR|DOORS:BB-Who\n  [30-,*,*,*,*]   = wh     |T-DOOR|DOORS:BB-Wh\n  [30-,*,*,*,*]   = whm    |T-DOOR|DOORS:BB-Whm\n  -------------------------> cut here <-------------------------\n\n\n\n  External designs:\n  -----------------\n\n  The designs are stored in the BB-Wh#?.output.x(.ansi|.amiga|.ibm) files.\n  Where x is the number of the design. The output-files must be in the\n  same directory as BB-Wh#?.\n  The Door first looks for the ansitype of the User and than tries to open\n  the belonging output-file. If it doesn`t find it, it tries to open the\n  normal output-file without any extension (BB-Wh#?.output.x).\n  Than it reads the lines from it, looks for keywords, inserts the belonging\n  datas and displays them.\n\n  You can easily make your own designs. Just make one in your favourite\n  ANSI-Editor and place keywords where you want to have the nodedatas.\n	The keywords look like this: @HANDLE=====....[\n                                    /        |  \\n                                  1/        2|  3\\n\n  1. The beginning of the keyword (e.g.: ''@HANDLE====='' for the handle).\n  2. Fillers. With that you can fill it as long as you want to have the\n     inserted data. You can fill with a character that you want (except ''[''\n     and '']'').\n  3. The ending of the keyword (e.g.: ''['' for inserting from the left side).\n     The last character defines if the data is insterted from the left (''['')\n     or the right ('']'') side.\n\n\n  Structure of the output-files:\n  There are all the lines of the design. The lines that are shown at the\n  top, the borders for the nodes, the nodelines and the lines at the end.\n  The lines are always placed between two keylines.\n  Top lines between ''@BEGIN_TOP'' and ''@END_TOP'' (unlimited lines).\n  Borderline for nodes between ''@BEGIN_BORDER'' and ''@END_BORDER'' (one line,\n  only used in BB-Who).\n  Lines for the nodes between ''@BEGIN_LINE'' and ''@END_LINE'' (two lines in\n  BB-Who and one line in BB-Wh/BB-Whm).\n  End lines between ''@BEGIN_END'' and ''@END_END'' (unlimited lines).\n\n\n  Keywords for the BB-Who lines:\n  ''@N''                                   for the node number.\n  ''@C''                                   for the conference number.\n  ''@LOG''                                 for the login time.\n  ''@BAU''                                 for the connect baud.\n  ''@HANDLE=====''                         for the username.\n  ''@LOCATION===''                         for the userlocation\n  ''@ACTIVITYU=========================='' for the upload activity.\n  ''@ACTIVITYD=========================='' for the download activity.\n\n\n  Keywords for the BB-Wh/BB-Whm lines:\n  ''@N''                                   for the node number.\n  ''@HANDLE=====''                         for the username.\n  ''@LOCATION===''                         for the userlocation.\n  ''@ACTIVITY===''                         for the activity.\n\n\n                            @{" Back to main menu " link "MAIN" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "plans" "-^- Future Plans -^-"\n@next "bugs"\n@prev "install"\n\n  Make more keywords for more datas. If you know some improvments contact\n  me and I will try to insert them.\n\n\n                            @{" Back to main menu " link "main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "bugs" "-^- Bug Report -^-"\n@next "greets"\n@prev "plans"\n\n  I hope there are no bugs in it, but nobody is perfect. So don`t hesitate\n  and tell me any bug you find. I can only remove bugs that I know.\n\n\n                            @{" Back to main menu " link "main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "greets" "-^- Greetings flow out to -^-"\n@next "motion"\n@prev "bugs"\n\n                        my personal Greetings go to\n                        ¯ ¯¯ ¯¯¯ ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯ ¯¯¯ ¯¯ ¯\n  2fast  Agent  AMO/ORS  APEX  Aquarius/OTL   BBC/M!   Ben/M!   Bezzzerk/M!\n  Calypso/GOD      Castor/PDX      Deathknight/PSG       Demax^Agressor/DLT\n  Dr. Dre/TRSI   Duke/M!    Echo&Guido    ECS/TRSI    E.F.A./M!    Fnord/M!\n  Fury/M!   Intercode/BB   JAF    Joker    Juan/TRSI    Kingpin    Logic/M!\n  Mario/TRSI     Marky&Power/BLH     Mogue/AC     Mr.Solo/RNX     Pitch/RBS\n  Playmate/M!   Princip/M!   Profex    Relief/oS    Rhetor/M!    sCANDIC/M!\n  Schwabenpower/M!   Shane/CRX   Shapechanger/DeZIGN   Sisko/M!    Skeleton\n  Skywalker    sNIKE    Spider/ORS    Striker    Tango/OGN    The Addict/M!\n  Tom/FLT            Treach/AC            Vampire/TRSI             Zinko/PB\n\n                        all MoTioN members worldwide\n                      and all the rest I have forgotten\n\n\n                            @{" Back to main menu " link "main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "motion" "-^- MoTioN Informations -^-"\n@prev "greets"\n\n                       the crazy ones behind MoTioN are \n                       ¯ ¯¯ ¯¯¯ ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯ ¯¯¯ ¯¯ ¯\n               BBC · Ben · Bezzzerk · BiLBo BaGGins · Bloodwolf\n              Bowen · Disque Bleu · Duke · E.F.A. · Fnord · Fury\n                KiNGPin · lOGIC · pLaYmAte · ¶r¡nçe Øf Th¡eves\n               pRINCIP · Rhetor · RTD · sCANDIC · SchwabenPower\n                    sISKO · tHE aDDICT · tRAITOR · Wendigo\n\n\n                       call our crazy boards worldwide\n                       ¯ ¯¯ ¯¯¯ ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯ ¯¯¯ ¯¯ ¯\n             WHQ....Mortuary................+1-aSK-fOR-iT!...6nDZ\n             EHQ....Deep Space Nine........+49-aSK-fOR-iT!...6nDZ\n             GHQ....FastFileSystem.........+49-aSK-fOR-iT!...9nDZ\n             SWIHQ..Dial Hard..............+41-aSK-fOR-iT!...5nDZ\n             SHQ....Interchange............+46-aSK-fOR-iT!...3nDZ\n             OZHQ...Dark Sun...............+61-aSK-fOR-iT!...3nDZ\n             DKHQ...Northern Palace........+45-aSK-fOR-iT!...3nDZ\n             NHQ....Checkpoint.............+47-aSK-fOR-iT!...2nDZ\n\n\n                            @{" Back to main menu " link "main" 0}\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),'{"LOCATION":"==''"}','auto-added',32523,4,0,NULL,NULL,'m_who05','scan',1780048589);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('m22_dd10','M22-DD10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/M22-DD10.LHA','DIZDATE','XIM','_______:__ _________ ________________ __ _',NULL,NULL,'M22','| ______| _ \______ ¬\_   _________________ |\\__   \/¬\_/   _____/__|__               | |  /   __   /    / \______ ¬\_ M·o·M·E·N·t :',replace(' _______:__ _________ ________________ __ _\n| ______| _ \______ ¬\_   _________________\n|\\__   \/¬\_/   _____/__|__               |\n|  /   __   /    / \______ ¬\_ M·o·M·E·N·t :\n| /    /   /____    /   _____/     2·2     :\n|/____/   /kRm/____/    /   /______________|\n|__ /____/_______ /____    /__________ __ _\n|       :            /____/                |\n|        DizDate v1.0 for AMIEXPRESS       :\n:  Adds a line after description with date .\n.     of FILE_ID.DIZ in ZIP/LHA-files.\n   -------------- -- -          ------ -- -','\n',char(10)),'DIZDATE.DOC',replace('DizDate v1.0 by Agamemnon / Moment 22\n-------------------------------------\n\nThis is a XIM-door for AmiExpress, should work on all versions.\nYou must have a FileId-door installed as \nbbs:commands/syscmd/examine.info to be able to run DizDate. \nTested FileId-utils are ByteAndi''s and Bobo''s.\n\nThis is what DizDate does:\n\n---- CUT ----\n\nOX-OPUS1.ZIP N1031626  10-17-94    OPUS AND BILL : ON THE ROAD AGAIN  [o1/o4]\n                                     ____________________________ _ _  ___\n                                 ZD!/    __  :  __   __/  |    \ | | \/ __\\n                                   /  :  \/  |  \/   \/  /~\ |\ \  :  \__ ~\\n                                 ÕÔ   §   \      \«   \     \«-§ \     \«ø  ¾\n                                  \_______/______/____/_____/____/_____/____/\n                                  ­:::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::­\n                                 /÷÷ E ÷÷ X ÷÷ C ÷÷ H ÷÷ A ÷÷ N ÷÷ G ÷÷ E ÷÷÷\n                                 >>> Snuskis / DCS <<< - >>> GURU''S DREAM <<<\nDizDate adds this line ->        -( FILE_ID.DIZ 10/14/94 )-( UL : 01:20:47 )-\n\n---- CUT ----\n\nSo you can find out how old the uploads really are by checking the date\nFILE_ID.DIZ was created.\n\nInstallation\n------------\nDIZDATE       -> DOORS:\nDIZDATE.INFO  -> DOORS:\nEXAMINE1.INFO -> BBS:COMMANDS/SYSCMD/ \n\n*NOTE* If EXAMINE1.INFO for some reason already exist put\nDizDate as EXAMINE2.INFO.\n\nConfiguration\n-------------\n\nEdit the tooltypes in DOORS:DIZDATE.INFO:\n\nLHA = Y/N         - Check Diz on LHA-files? Requires LHA in C:.\n \nZIP = Y/N         - ZIP-files? Requires UNZIP in C:.\n\nNODIZLINE = Y/N   - If it is an unknown file, like DMS or TXT where DizDate\n                    can''t extract any FILE_ID.DIZ it prints UNKNOWN in\n                    the added line, or if you select N, no line will\n                    be added for unknown files.\n\nProblems? Bugs?\n---------------\n\nCall Infinite Power +46-[0]171-67461 & +46-[0]171-57868 NUP=PROKTOLOG and\nleave mail to AGAMEMNON.\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,15480,5,0,NULL,NULL,'m22_dd10_dizdate','scan',1780048589);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('m22_ga11','M22-GA11.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/M22-GA11.LHA','GetAnswer','XIM','GetAnswer',NULL,NULL,'M22','\_  _  _ ¬\\   _ ¬\ \   _ ¬\.-------------. /   / /   /_\__/  / _\__/  /|  MOMENT 22  | /   / /   // _____/_/ _____/_|   PROUDLY   |',replace(' __________ _______  _______\n \_  _  _ ¬\\   _ ¬\ \   _ ¬\.-------------.\n /   / /   /_\__/  / _\__/  /|  MOMENT 22  |\n/   / /   // _____/_/ _____/_|   PROUDLY   |\n\  /\/\  //   \/   /   \/   /|  PRESENTS!  |\n \/    \/ \_______/\_______/ `-------------''\n.------------------------------------------.\n|              GetAnswer v1.1              |\n|  A fast, small and cool util to look on  |\n|    new user answers from /X. XIM-door    |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'GetAnswer.doc',replace('                                GetAnswer v1.1\n                                ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n                          By Agamemnon / Moment 22\n\nThis is a useful door so sysops and cosysops can look on\nnew user''s answers, just install as a XIM-door.\n\nYou can use AmigaDOS wildcards (*,?,#?,~ etc) when you search\nafter a username.\n\nCall INFINITE POWER at +46-[0]171-67461, and -57868 for updates.\n ','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',11752,1,1,'ga','Doors/GetAnswer','m22_ga11','scan',1780048589);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('m22_lc10','M22-LC10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/M22-LC10.LHA','LastCallers','XIM','LastCallers',NULL,NULL,'M22','\_  _  _ ¬\\   _ ¬\ \   _ ¬\.-------------. /   / /   /_\__/  / _\__/  /|  MOMENT 22  | /   / /   // _____/_/ _____/_|   PROUDLY   |',replace(' __________ _______  _______\n \_  _  _ ¬\\   _ ¬\ \   _ ¬\.-------------.\n /   / /   /_\__/  / _\__/  /|  MOMENT 22  |\n/   / /   // _____/_/ _____/_|   PROUDLY   |\n\  /\/\  //   \/   /   \/   /|  PRESENTS!  |\n \/    \/ \_______/\_______/ `-------------''\n.------------------------------------------.\n|             LastCallers v1.0             |\n| A fast, small and cool lastcallers util  |\n|that makes different lists for each access|\n`------------------------------------------''\n>MAYDAY.. MAYDAY.. INTRUDERS ENTER MEN-TEL!»\n','\n',char(10)),'LastCallers.doc',replace('                              LastCallers v1.0\n                              ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n                          By Agamemnon / Moment 22\n\nUSAGE: LastCallers <node> <status[-status]> <datafile> <bullfile>\n\nwhere <datafile> is a unique file for different statuslevels. \nFor example, if you want a LastCallers-list that only shows\nPD-users with statuslevel 20-30 you can use:\n\nLastCallers <node> 20-30 s:lastcallers2030.dat bbs:nodex/bull.txt\n\nand a separate list for Elite-users with level 50:\n\nLastCallers <node> 50 s:lastcallers50.dat bbs:nodex/bull50.txt\n\nCall INFINITE POWER at +46-[0]171-67461, and -57868 for updates.\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',22127,6,0,NULL,NULL,'m22_lc10','scan',1780048589);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('m22_tl12','M22-TL12.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/M22-TL12.LHA','TopList','XIM','TopList',NULL,NULL,'M22','\_  _  _ ¬\\   _ ¬\ \   _ ¬\.-------------. /   / /   /_\__/  / _\__/  /|  MOMENT 22  | /   / /   // _____/_/ _____/_|   PROUDLY   |',replace(' __________ _______  _______\n \_  _  _ ¬\\   _ ¬\ \   _ ¬\.-------------.\n /   / /   /_\__/  / _\__/  /|  MOMENT 22  |\n/   / /   // _____/_/ _____/_|   PROUDLY   |\n\  /\/\  //   \/   /   \/   /|  PRESENTS!  |\n \/    \/ \_______/\_______/ `-------------''\n.------------------------------------------.\n|               TopList v1.2               |\n| A fast, small and cool toplist util that |\n|can make different toplist for each access|\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'TopList.doc',replace('                                TopList v1.2\n                                ~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n                          By Agamemnon / Moment 22\n\nUSAGE: TopList <status[-status]> <UL/DL> <filepath> <amount>\n\nWell, I don''t have to explain all the arguments coz it''s very simple.\n\nCall INFINITE POWER at +46-[0]171-67461, and -57868 for updates.\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',10889,2,0,NULL,NULL,'m22_tl12','scan',1780048589);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mad_vhs','MAD-VHS.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MAD-VHS.LHA','LhA','XIM','LE-win5-96.exe',NULL,NULL,'MAD','/\  /\   _   ____  \_/ __ \   _  \     / /  \/  \_(_)  \ \ \   _ \ \/\ (_)  \ O / / /\  /\  ___  / / /  // /   / ___  / _/',replace('       ______________   __________________\n  /\  /\   _   ____  \_/ __ \   _  \     /\n /  \/  \_(_)  \ \ \   _ \ \/\ (_)  \ O / \n/ /\  /\  ___  / / /  // /   / ___  / _/  \n\ \ \/ / /  / /  \/  / \ \__/ /  / / /    \n \/    \/   \/\_____/¯¯¯\____/   \  /     \n          ->RELEASES TODAY<-      ¯¯ \n     -> VHS ORDERING DOOR v3.00 <-\n        "Every Sysops Dream"\nFeatures like: Upload Movielist,offers,tips\nDownload Orderlogs,Special VHS SYSOP MENU\nORDER ON LINE,Complete Explaining DOC,\n      User Download MOVIE LIST\n_\n"Never have to Bother The Sysop Again"\n Exept When Installing IT\n','\n',char(10)),'lOSeNDOS.guide',replace('                   \n                     __  _ __  /\__ _  _ __/\  __ _  __\n                    _\/___   \/              \/   ___\/_\n              ......\/\  /........................\  /\/......\n             :         \/                          \/         :\n             :      .___             .___         .___        :\n             :   _ _|   \      ______|   \  ______|   \       :\n             :   \\\__   7___  \______   /  \__   ____/       :\n             :      /.   |   \__/.  l/   \___/_____   \__ _   :\n             :     /::.  |    _/::.       _/::.  l/    _///   :\n             :     \___________\___________\____________\     :\n             :___        .___        .___        .___         :___\n     _ ______|   \ ______|   \ ______|   \ ______|   \  ______|   \\n     \\\__   ____/ \______   / \______   / \______   /  \__   ____/\n        /.   ___|___/.   |   \__/.  _|   \__/.  l/   \___/_____   \__ _\n       /::.  l/   _/::.  |    _/::. \___  _/::.       _/::.  l/    _///\n       \_ _________\_____|_____\___________\___________\___________ \\n         Y   :                                                :[nM$]Y\n      .------''                                                `------.\n      :eXON/rIOT^jORMAS · gHANDY/gODS · rAHIEM/eSSENCE · cELIC/rEKTUM: \n      `------.                                                .------''\n             `------------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',62776,5,0,NULL,NULL,'mad_vhs','scan',1780048589);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mafia','MAFIA.LZH','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MAFIA.LZH',NULL,'XIM','MafiaDoor Source (ASM).',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,replace('MafiaDoor Source (ASM).\n','\n',char(10)),'uzi.txt',replace('                                            .---------------------------.\n    _______.-----------------._______/|     |     4NODEZ  RiNGDOWN      |\n    \_     |     .------     |________|.....| 73 GiG OF AMiGA CoNSoLE PC|\n   .:|     |     |     ______|        |:::::|  uZiSUiCiDE.sERVEBBS.ORG  |\n  .::|     |     |     |     |        |-----+-----.      TELNET         |\n .:::|           |     |     |       :|     |     |                     |\n.::::\___________|___________|________|     `-----+---------------------''\n:::::::::::::::::|                                | 24HR 7DAY STATiC iP! \n_________________|___________/|__________________/|______________________\n\_     ______    |     _______|          |_____________      _/    _____/\n_|_____    |     |     |      |    |_____|        |   |      |     ___|_ \n|     |    |     |     |      |    |     |        |   |      |     |    |\n|     |    |     |     |     :|          |       :|   |      |     |    |\n|__________|_____|_____|______|__________|________|__________|__________|\n:::::::::::::::::|            |                                         |\n`::::::::::::::::|            |ALWAYS THE LATEST VERSION oF AMi-EXPRESS |\n `:::::::::::::::|            | TONS OF ONLiNE MESSAGES AND MULTi-CHATS |\n  `::::::::::::::`------------+  NUP IS REQUIRED SO ASK WHOEVER POSTED  |\n   `::::::::::::::::::::::::::|    THIS ADVERT FOR THE NUMBER AND NUP   |\n    `:::::::::::::::::::::::::`-----------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,65451,5,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048589);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mailqueu','MAILQUEU.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MAILQUEU.LHA','MailQueue','XIM','MailQueue',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Upload to aminet on 20.2 to : comm/net ->> [Synergy] - [4 Nodez!] - [Synergy] <<- FiLe_iD.aBuSE - eVERYwARE · nORWaYs FiNEsT!!',replace('Monitor number of msgs in SMTPSpool\nUpload to aminet on 20.2 to : comm/net\n ->> [Synergy] - [4 Nodez!] - [Synergy] <<- \nFiLe_iD.aBuSE - eVERYwARE · nORWaYs FiNEsT!!','\n',char(10)),'MailQueue.doc',replace('\n MAILQUEUE, written by Kai Iske January 13. 1995\n            This is PUBLIC DOMAIN; you may do with it whatever you like\n\nIf you change/republish/delete/sell the program or do anything similar, please\nbe so kind to keep my name within the program and all the other files, even\nthough you`re not obliged to, as for the definition of Public Domain\n\nThis is just a little program to use with the INetUtils for AmiTCP/AS225,\nespecially for your SMTPSpool directory. The program will monitor all queued\nfiles within the SMTPSpool directory and display the number of messages in a\nsmall window, you may position somewhere on your Workbench. As soon as a\nmessage is queued/deleted, the information will be updated.\n\nMAILQUEUE was written using SAS 6.5....\n\nMAILQUEUE requires netsupport.library, which can be found on AmiNet\n          or on several other sources. This library is not contained\n          in the distribution of MAILQUEUE. It can be found as\n          /pub/aminet/comm/net/NSP*.*\n\n!!! MailQueue requires OS 2.x and up to run, MailQueue is PURE !!!\n\n\n\n----------------------\nWhat does MAILQUEUE???\n----------------------\n\n\nIt  will  simply  monitor  all  files  starting with "D." (the name all queued\nmessages  start  with), located in your SMTPSpool directory.  As stated above,\ninformation will be shown in a window, how much messages are queued.\n\n  MailQueue WINX/N,WINY/N,OPENNOW/S\n\nNOTE: You must have either SMTPSpoolDir defined as Environment variable or have\n      it set in your config file (usually uulib:Config)\n\nExplanation\n\n  WINX      - Specifies the X position of the information window (default 0)\n  WINY      - Specifies the Y position of the information window (default 0)\n  OPENNOW   - Normally, MailQueue won`t open the window on startup\n              if there aren`t any messages queued. If you prefer to have\n              the window opened, even if there aren`t any message, when\n              starting MailQueue, supply this parameter\n  ZEROCLOSE - Tells MailQueue to close the window, as soon as there aren`t\n              any messages queued, anymore\n  ONLYWB    - Will cause MailQueue to only open it`s window on Workbench\n  SENDMAIL  - This is for UUCP sendmail compatibility. Sendmail produces\n              two D.#? files per mail. This switch causes MailQueue\n              to only display half the amount of matching files, thus\n              showing the correct number of queued mails.\n\nExamples\n\n  MailQueue 10 10 OPENNOW\n\n  Will open the window at 10/10 on your Workbench Screen\n\n\n---------------------------\nHow to install MAILQUEUE???\n---------------------------\n\nSimply copy it to a directory within you search path (eg. AmiTCP:Bin)\n\n\n\n\n------------\nVersion 37.0\n------------\n  - initial release\n\n\n------------\nVersion 37.1\n------------\n  - Added new ONLYWB option, whichs causes the program\n    to only open it`s window, on Workbench\n  - MailQueue wasn`t really pure, as it used to set up LibBases\n    as globals (well, technically wasn`t pure ;)). Changed.\n    (Reported by : WShell users)\n  - Whoops, wrong version string contained in executable ;)\n  - Added ZEROCLOSE option to hide the Queue window when no messages are\n    queued. (This was done by Greg Patterson; thanks Greg)\n\n\n------------\nVersion 37.2\n------------\n  - Added SendMail switch, which acts as a SENDMAIL compatible\n    switch. SendMail creates two D.#? entries for one mail.\n    The SendMail switch causes MailQueue to halve the number\n    of files found, in order to show the number of mails\n    (Requested by : <[email removed]>)\n\n\nHope you like it, if not, delete it......\n\n\n\nSo long,\n\n     Kai\n\n\n\n\n --- Kai Iske\n Brucknerstrasse 18, 63452 Hanau, Germany, Tel.: +49-(0)6181-850181\n Z-Net     : [email removed]  Fido: Kai Iske, 2:244/6302.11\n internet  : [email removed]             IRC:kiske\n                   CompuServe: Kai Iske, 100524,1201\n ---- Life sucks ----\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',14474,2,0,NULL,NULL,'mailqueu','scan',1780048589);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('manswers','MANSWERS.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MANSWERS.LHA',NULL,'XIM','exe.-l0S-eND0S-bBS-.exe',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,replace('Search and displays users answers text\n','\n',char(10)),'AnswerReader.Doc',replace('\nAnswers Reader v1.02 for Hydro and Sweet Thing!\nBy P0T-NOoDLE, August 1994 -> May 1995.\n\n\n\nQuick Docs:\n\nThis will search your BBS:Node??/Answers files for a given user''s answers...\n\nIt''ll work for upto 99 nodes.\n\nThe door is multinode OK, XIM type,uses very little stack, and can be made\nresident.\n\nOn the commandline prompt you can give the door the name of the user you are\nlooking for - if you don''t you will be prompted for it.\n\nIt''ll check for any name that begins with the name you give, eg give "Hydro"\nand "Hydro", "Hydro!", and "Hydro The Cunt" will all be found...\n\nWhile searching you can press ^C to abort the search.\n\nIt does NOT load the whole answers file(s) into memory, so you don''t have to\nworry if you answers files are 5 meg or something (they''ll take ages, but\nyou won''t run out of memory because of them).\n	Sorry, it''s not the fasted search routine in the world, but it was\nthe easiest way to make it work without loading the whole file into memory\nand without using complex routines like in Super-DupeCheck...\n\n		Enjoy!\n\nv1.00 -> v1.01: Stupid bug in search routine removed.\n                Made the searching anim jumping dot thing animate less often.\nv1.01 -> v1.02: Now asks if you want to continue seaching in case there is\n                more than one entry for the given user name...\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',10398,5,0,NULL,NULL,'manswers','scan',1780048589);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('man_dj01','MAN_DJ01.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MAN_DJ01.LHA','j','XIM','j',NULL,NULL,'MAN','/   /_/   /_ \  _/__ __ \ WiLD THiNG''s /   / /   /  \      /  / /__ ___    _____ \________/___/_____//___/  //  /uNr/  __/',replace('   ____  ____ _ ____ _____\n  /   /_/   /_ \  _/__ __ \ WiLD THiNG''s\n /   / /   /  \      /  / /__ ___    _____\n \________/___/_____//___/  //  /uNr/  __/\n   /___  ____/      /      //  /____\  \\n    /    /  /______/______//______/_____\\n   /____/   Mannassas & FeaR presents\n                DoSJoiN v0.1\n         Join command for the CLI \n   /X v3.x util <-> Kick > 2.x required\n','\n',char(10)),'dosjoin.doc',replace('     ____  ____  ___ __ _______ _____________________   _____________\n    /    /\    \/   \  :       \        /     :      : /    /       /\n   //           \___/  :___     \   ___/ ____ : ____ :/    /___    /____\n   \            /   \      \ /  /    /:       :      :        /   /    /\n    \____/\____/\___/______/___/____/ :_______:______:_______/________/\n\n                               DoSJoin v0.1\n                      written by WiLD THiNG/Mannassas\n                      \nThis tiny tool is for lazy sysops like me, it the join conference command\nfor the CLI.\n\nExample:\nj 5  works as cd <path to conf 5>\n\n\n  For any ideas OR bug reports write TO WiLD THiNG at one of our boards:\n\n\n[--> CRaZY WoRLD  PHQ  SySoP: JaRRi/Mannassas          ++48-2-6636797 <--]\n[--> DiXie        WHQ  SySoP: WiLD THiNG/Mannassas     ++48-71-575825 <--]\n[--> LiFe         PHQ  SySoP: RaBoCoST/Mannassas       ++48-22-118628 <--]\n[--> Vacant       PCHQ SySoP: ZyRioN/Mannassas         ++48-42-871766 <--]\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',5230,5,0,NULL,NULL,'man_dj01','scan',1780048589);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('man_dj02','MAN_DJ02.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MAN_DJ02.LHA',NULL,'XIM','LE-win5-96.exe',NULL,NULL,'MAN','/   /_/   /_ \  _/__ __ \ WiLD THiNG''s /   / /   /  \      /  / /__ ___    _____ \________/___/_____//___/  //  /uNr/  __/',replace('   ____  ____ _ ____ _____\n  /   /_/   /_ \  _/__ __ \ WiLD THiNG''s\n /   / /   /  \      /  / /__ ___    _____\n \________/___/_____//___/  //  /uNr/  __/\n   /___  ____/      /      //  /____\  \\n    /    /  /______/______//______/_____\\n   /____/   Mannassas & FeaR presents\n.------------ DOSJoin v0.2 ---------------.\n|     Join conf command for yer CLI       |\n|     BUGFIXED & LIST CONFS OPTION        |\n|   /X 3.x DOS Util - Kick >2.x required  |\n`-----------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'lOSeNDOS.guide',replace('                   \n                     __  _ __  /\__ _  _ __/\  __ _  __\n                    _\/___   \/              \/   ___\/_\n              ......\/\  /........................\  /\/......\n             :         \/                          \/         :\n             :      .___             .___         .___        :\n             :   _ _|   \      ______|   \  ______|   \       :\n             :   \\\__   7___  \______   /  \__   ____/       :\n             :      /.   |   \__/.  l/   \___/_____   \__ _   :\n             :     /::.  |    _/::.       _/::.  l/    _///   :\n             :     \___________\___________\____________\     :\n             :___        .___        .___        .___         :___\n     _ ______|   \ ______|   \ ______|   \ ______|   \  ______|   \\n     \\\__   ____/ \______   / \______   / \______   /  \__   ____/\n        /.   ___|___/.   |   \__/.  _|   \__/.  l/   \___/_____   \__ _\n       /::.  l/   _/::.  |    _/::. \___  _/::.       _/::.  l/    _///\n       \_ _________\_____|_____\___________\___________\___________ \\n         Y   :                                                :[nM$]Y\n      .------''                                                `------.\n      :eXON/rIOT^jORMAS · gHANDY/gODS · rAHIEM/eSSENCE · cELIC/rEKTUM: \n      `------.                                                .------''\n             `------------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',6543,5,0,NULL,NULL,'man_dj02','scan',1780048589);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('man_wl03','MAN_WL03.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MAN_WL03.LHA','wildlist','XIM','wildlist',NULL,NULL,'MAN','/   /_/   /_ \  _/__ __ \ WiLD THiNG''s /   / /   /  \      /  / /__ ___    _____ \________/___/_____//___/  //  /uNr/  __/',replace('   ____  ____ _ ____ _____\n  /   /_/   /_ \  _/__ __ \ WiLD THiNG''s\n /   / /   /  \      /  / /__ ___    _____\n \________/___/_____//___/  //  /uNr/  __/\n   /___  ____/      /      //  /____\  \\n    /    /  /______/______//______/_____\\n   /____/ [--> Mannassas <--] presents\n              WiLDLiST v0.3\n  /X v3.x XIM Door - Kick >2.x required\nDownload all filelists from all conferences\n    the user has axxess to in one file\n         --+=# BuGFiXeD #=+--\n','\n',char(10)),'wildlist.guide',replace('@database WiLDist.guide\n\n@node MAIN "WiLDLiST v0.3 DoX (c) 01/94  WiLD THiNG/Mannassas"\n\n                          [---> Mannassas <---]                           \n                              presents the\n     ____  ____  ___ __ _______ _____________________   _____________\n    /    /\    \/   \  :       \        /     :      : /    /       /\n   //           \___/  :___     \   ___/ ____ : ____ :/    /___    /____\n   \            /   \      \ /  /    /:       :      :        /   /    /\n    \____/\____/\___/______/___/____/ :_______:______:_______/________/\n                                 SeRieS\n   ====================================================================\n                              WiLD LiST v0.3\n                     (c) 01/94 by WiLD THiNG/Mannassas\n   ====================================================================\n              @{" Introduction        " link "introduction"} @{" Greetings         " link "greets"}\n              @{" Installation        " link "installation"} @{" Contact           " link "contact"}\n              @{" other WiLDTooLS     " link "tools"} @{" History           " link "history"}\n              @{" future improvements " link "future"}\n@endnode\n\n@node introduction\n\nHere  we  go with the new version, so first a litte story, it took me now 3\ndays  to  code  this  little  shit  (it''s  my  first door in E so shut up),\nyesterday  I was happy to have it working and so I send the ßeta version to\nEasy  Rider  at Mamba BBS, well just as he told me he send it forth I found\nit  had  a  serious  bug,  it put the wrong conferences together, SORRY FOR\nTHIS, should have seen it.\n\n\nSo  WiLD  LiST  puts  all  dir-files  from all conferences the user has got\naccess  to  one  file  and  packs  it with lha and then sends it to him.  I\nwonder  why  all the file list download doors I have seen from other people\nalways  did  it  so  stupidly  and just packed them from one conference and\nalways in hundreds of dir files.\n\n                                           [---> WiLD THiNG/Mannassas <---]\n\n\nPS:Isn''t there anybody who wants to write those stupid docs for my doors ??\nOnce heard that only bad coders write good docs, so one day I''ll maybe be a\ngood one, coz my docs are already now cruel :-)\n\n@endnode\n@node future\n                 -======================================-\n                           Future Improvements\n                 -======================================-\n· no config file will be needed - conf locations will be read from the\n  confconfig tooltypes\n· sort of confs\n· I''ll hire somebody as doc writer, coz it''s so boring\n\n@endnode\n\n@node history\n                 -======================================-\n                               H I S T O R Y\n                 -======================================-\n\nv0.1  - rel 26-Jan-94   - first ßeta release\n        ca. 07:00\nv0.2  - rel 26-Jan-94   - packs the LIST now, adds your logo TO\n        ca. 23:00         the list\n\nv0.3  - rel 27-Jan-94   - fixed that bug with the wrong conferences\n                          and spent some hours at this stupid doc,\n                          fixed a bug: forgot to free the mem after a\n                          pattern matching :-)\n\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node installation\n                 -======================================-\n                               Installation:\n                 -======================================-\n                   You will need /X v3.x and Kick > 2.x\n\nCopy  the  files  to  the right dirs and that''s it and change the config to\nsuit your needs, BUT remember you MUST have all your conferences there.  Oh\nalmost forgot it it needs da AEDoor.Library.\n\nUm  by  the  way  :-) the first line in the config file is the full path to\nyour bbs-logo which will be added to the list.\n\nBy  the way, I was to lazy to sort the confs, so they will be packed in the\norder you entered them in the ACCESS/AREA.xxxxxx.info\n\n@endnode\n\n                                           \n@node greets\n                 -======================================-\n                           Special thanx for ...\n                 -======================================-\n\nZiPPER/Yodel    : THX for all\nZielu/Mad Elks  : thx for yer bug reports\nJarri/Mannassas : ...lots of good ideas\nuNReaL/FeaR     : ...all the KeWL ASCII''s\nEasy Rider/MST  : ...your critics and ideas and yer fast distribution :-)\nWouter van Oortmerssen : ... Amiga E compiler, it''s the BEST\nBig C & Amiga   : ... the best computer\nSiNTAX/WøT      : ...your examples were the first thing I saw in E and I\n                  loved it\n                  \n\n\n                 -======================================-\n                       Greetings go to(in no order)\n                 -======================================-\n\n                       all Mannassas & FeaR members\nTic., R19, Dragon/Motion, Vince, Andy/Motion, Sunset, Donald/Motion, Vince,\nWild  Child/Taurus, (Milchbubi, Tekknonase, Kinderschaender von Bottrop :-)\n-> haddu selber gesagt) and all others who know me...\n\nLogic           : hey yer checkers  are da best \nEmpire/Mystic   : well you see, finally got away from that arexx stuff\n\n\n                 -======================================-\n                              Fuckings go to\n                 -======================================-\nPolish telecom (TPSA): fucked up assholes\nall you stupid lamers here that even can''t do a simple file description\nZonderkommando       : fuck yerself ye bloody nazis\nTERMOS               : yer a bunch of lamers\n\n@endnode\n\n@node contact\n                *** For any improvement or bug reports ***\n             *** write to WiLD THiNG at one of our boards ***\n\n   __________                                   _____\n..(_    ____ \...______......______.....___....(    / /\  _____  /\........\n.../   /    \ \ /   _  \    /  /  /..../   ).../   / /  \ \   / /  \...... \n../   /     / //   / \  \  /  /  /.....)   \../   /_(    \_) (_/    )....  \n./   /      \//   /   \  \/  /  /...../    (_/   /   \             /....   \n(   (        /\  /     \  \ /  /...../          / __  \           /....    \n.\   \______/  \ \_____/   \\  \..../   /)     / (__)  )    _    /....     \n..\            /           / \  \../   /.\    /\      /.\  /.\  /....      \n...\__________/\__________/\_/\_/ /   /..(___/..\____/...\/...\/....       \n.................................(___/.............................\n\n                             oNe oF ouR BoaRDZ\n\n[--> <--------------------------------------------------------------> <--]\n[--> CRaZY WoRLD  PHQ  SySoP: JaRRi/Mannassas          ++48-2-6636797 <--]\n[--> DiXiE        WHQ  SySoP: WiLD THiNG/Mannassas     ++48-71-575825 <--]\n[--> LiFe         PHQ  SySoP: RaBoCoST/Mannassas       ++48-22-118628 <--]\n[--> Vacant       PCHQ SySoP: ZyRioN/Mannassas         ++48-42-871766 <--]\n[--> <--------------------------------------------------------------> <--]\n                    DiXiE new user pw is ''Mason-Dixon''\n\nIf you would like to join us as a coder, grafician, musician, trader or sysop\ncontact us at one of our boards or one of our @{"members" link "members"}.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node tools\n                          LooK ouT FoR THe oTHeR \n      ____  ____  ___ __ _______ _____________________   _____________\n     /    /\    \/   \  :       \        /     :      : /    /       /\n    //           \___/  :___     \   ___/ ____ : ____ :/    /___    /____\n    \            /   \      \ /  /    /:       :      :        /   /    /\n     \____/\____/\___/______/___/____/ :_______:______:_______/________/\n\n\n[----- NAME ------|------ DESCRIPTION -------|------- FEATURES ---------------]\n WiLDRead v0.13   | file/archive/log viewer  | text search\n                  | AIM door                 | file/arc info\n                  |                          | next/prev. page\n                  |                          | page selection\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDNeW v0.4     | new user questionaire    | multilanguage\n                  | AIM door                 | baud checking for questions\n                  |                          | multiple answers\n                  |                          | text comments (internal ed)\n                  |                          | sysop review of new users\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDBull v0.2    | global bulletins         | scroll bar selection\n                  | AIM door                 | all bulls in one dir\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDMenu v0.1    | multi level menus        | all menus in one file\n                  | AIM door                 |\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDKick v0.1    | unwanted users kick out  | show  msg to user & hang up\n                  | AIM door                 |\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDVote v0.9    | vote door                | configurable user add/delete\n                  | AIM door                 | of topics and itemz\n                  |                          | download of result file\n                  |                          | result output with graph bars\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDLiST v0.3    | file LIST dl             | download all filelists from\n                  | XIM door                 | conferences the user has \n                  |                          |  access TO in one file\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n\n@endnode\n\n@node members\n\n                    FEAR & MANNASSAS OFFICIAL MEMBERLIST\n                                 08-Jan-94\n\n 			  FEAR - AMIGA POLAND\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDARK ANGEL      -       CODER		- Ex.INVESTATION\nHUDSON          -       MUSICIAN	- EX.DDF\nJABO            -       TRADER		- EX.INVESTATION\nMEPHISTO        -       MUSICIAN	- EX.INVESTATION\nSHADE           -       PROGRAMMER\nTEES            -       GRAPHICIAN	- EX.EQUINOX\nTHANATOS        -       PROGRAMMER\nTHE TRADER      -       SWAPPER,CHIEF	- EX.INVESTATION\n\n 			   FEAR - AMIGA GERMANY\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nALEC EMPIRE	-	MUSICIAN,SWAPPER - EX.IRIS\n\n 			   FEAR - AMIGA BAHRAIN\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n		EXOTIC		-	SWAPPER\n\n 			   FEAR - AMIGA ENGLAND\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n		KING TUT	-	SWAPPER\n\n 			   FEAR - AMIGA DENMARK\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n		FOXTROT 	-	SWAPPER\n\n 			   FEAR - AMIGA JORDANIA\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n		BASSAM 		-	SWAPPER\n\n 			     FEAR - PC POLAND\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nJASPER		-	CODER	\nUNREAL		-	CODER	- EX.INVESTATION\nGaMmA           -       PROGRAMER\nDiScOvEr        -       PROGRAMER\nMr. NoName      -       CODER\nFrOdO           -       CODER\n\n\n\n                          Mannassas - subgroup of Fear\n                                Polish division:\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n                     WiLD THiNG      sysop - /X coder\n                     Crazy Squaw     gfx\n                     Rabocost        animations - sysop\n                     Gollum          trader - coder\n                     Spec            trader\n                     Kajtek          gfx\n                     lEVY            /X coder\n                     Jarri           sysop\n                     ZyRiOn          sysop - coder\n                     Trocek          trader - coder\n                     Seb McKein      trader\n        \n                                German division:\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n                        KC              trader - sfx\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n@endnode\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',19681,5,0,NULL,NULL,'man_wl03','scan',1780048589);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('man_wn03','MAN_WN03.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MAN_WN03.LHA',NULL,'XIM','_  ____        __  _ _  __  __  _  __',NULL,NULL,'MAN','/ \/  / \  /\  / / / / \/ _\/ _\/ \/  \ /     / _ \/  \/ /\/ / // / / / / // /\/ / /\_/\_/ \/_/\__/\__/_/ \ \ \ \/_/ \ \',replace('    _  ____        __  _ _  __  __  _  __\n   / \/  / \  /\  / / / / \/ _\/ _\/ \/  \\n  /     / _ \/  \/ /\/ / // / / / / // /\/\n / /\_/\_/ \/_/\__/\__/_/ \ \ \ \/_/ \ \\n \/        -= presents =- /_/ /_/    /_/\n+*+.+*+ WiLDNew v0.2  MuLTiLaNGuaGe +*+.+*+\n:           New User questionaire døør\n','\n',char(10)),'WiLDNeW.doc',replace('\n                |\n              --+--\n                |                    /\       /\\n      /\     __      /\        _    /  \_    /  \/\                     /\\n     /  \   /  \    /  \      / \  /   / \  /   /  \  /\______ /\_____ /  \  /\______\n    /    \ /    |  /    \    /   \/   /   \/   /    \/       //      //    \/       /\n   /      /     | /   _  \  /        /        /   _ /   ____//   ___//   _ /   ____/\n  /              /   / \  \/        /        /   / \\   \    \   \  /   / \\   \\n /    /\  /\    /   _____ /   /\   /   /\   /   ____ \   \    \   \/    ___ \   \\n/    /  \/  \  /   /     /   /  \_/   /  \_/   /  _   \   \_   \   \   / _   \   \\n\___/        \_\__/      \__/     \__/     \__/  / \__/   / \__/   /__/ / \__/   /\n  ______________________________________________/        /        /    /        /\n  \_____________________________________________________/\_______/     \_______/\n \n                                 presents:\n\n===========================================================================\n                        WiLDNeW v0.3 Multilanguage\n                          written by WiLD THiNG\n===========================================================================\nThis  is a new questionaire door for new users, it can give some answers or\ncomments on the questions and you can have your questinairs in ANSI and you\ncan have different questions for different baud-rates.  Furthermore you can\nask  new  questions on specified answers (you should now say WOW, no ?  na,\nmaybe   next   time). \n\n Now  you  can  have  your  questions in whatever language you want, i have\nsupplied  with  this  release  an English, Polish and German one, but don''t\nforget that the user will probably answer in the language he has been asked\nif you don''t tell him otherwise.\n\nThe  filled in questionaires will be saved in the WiLDTools/WiLDNew/answers\ndirectory with the user name as filename.\n\n\nConfig file:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\n(doors:WiLDTools//WiLDNeW/WiLDNew.cfg)\nYes here you must declare which languages you want to have, and the names\nof the quest files \neg.: \n==== cut here ====\nEnglish quest.eng\nPolski quest.pol\nDeutsch quest.ger \n==== cut here ====\nand whatever you want...\n\nWiLDNew will ask which language the user prefers.\n\nhere  are the recognition chars for the quest file, they have to be at the\nbeginning of every line:\n\n- print out line\n? Ask question\n§ Ask question which user MUST Answer \n^ Check answer \n+ Call the editor and let the user write you a comment, that \n        comment will be saved in .../answers/username.com\n=xxxxx ask user with specified baud rate where xxxxx is the rate\n%xxxxx show line only to user calling at xxxxx baud\n\nYou can combine the answer checking with a new question:\n\n?Have you ever heard of WiLDTools ?             - ask question\n^yes                                            - if entered "yes" then\n§Why not ?                                      - user must answer why\n?Is there anything you want to tell me ?\n^yes\n+                                               - if the answer is\n                                                  yes - start the\n                                                  editor\n\nLook at the example config file to see some possibilities :)\n\n\nInstallation:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nTo  install  on  /X 3.x just run the WNinst script.  Don''t forget to assign\ndoors:    properly. Now add to yer joined.txt ~CC_WNew, and in da first\nline only ~ . That''s it...\n\nhave phun...\n\nFor  any  bug reports, improvements or if you''d like me to write a door for\nyou  contact  me  at my board Dixie ++49-71-575825 or write me a message at\nTatooine    (Taurus    WHQ   ++49-711-456672)   or   Mamba   (Mystic   PHQ\n++48-22-367443).\n\n\nHistory:\n~~~~~~~~\nv0.1    First Version\nv0.2    added Multilanguage option\n\n\n\nOther available WiLDTools:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nWiLDDoors       Select your Door via Scrollbar (beta release)\nWiLDBull        Select bulletins via scrollbar\nWiLDMenu        Helps to keep your menus all in one file for all axxlevels\nWiLDRead        great file/archive/callerslog viewer with many features\nWiLDcompress    Arexx compression tool\nWiLDtxtadd      Adds your logos to uploaded text files\nWiLDCheck       Upload checker, checks for file_id.diz files in archives\n                and uses them as description (beta release)\n\nplanned WiLDTools:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nWiLDWheel       Whell of fortune - small game \n\n                Anything YOU want me to write for you (almost)\n\n\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|                      CaLL NoW oNe oF ouR BoaRDS                         |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|Dixie WHQ      Sysop: WiLD THiNG   ++48-71-575825  24oo-168oo v42b       |\n|LiFE  PHQ      Sysop: Rabocost     ++48-22-118628  24oo-144oo DUAL  22-8h|\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n                        \n\nFinally I can''t hold back to send out sum greetz:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nEazy-E            : Will we meet again som'' time ?\nR19/ex-Mannassas  : cum back ye traitor :-), and get yer board workin''\nEasy Rider/Mystic : Thx for yer ideas. I''m workin'' on that upload door...\nSchlegi           : Man, what''s yer HD doin'' ?\nEmpire/Mystic     : Thx for yer help, I''m hard workin'' on that C stuff\nZiPPER/Yodel      : How is it goin'' up there in Sweden ?\nAndy/Motion       : Sorry, can''t call your board now\nWild Child/Taurus : Com'' on tell yer sex-hungry lovers to write their\n                    letters to you and not to me, I HATE it\nViNCE             : Call me anytime, BUT CALL\nTIC.              : You were the best at Havanna,\n                    leave me a mail at Tatooine\nDonald/Motion     : Thx for all yer help at my beginning\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nand some more simple greetz go to:\n\nAXE/Mystic,  Giants/tYt,  Mc  Boe,  Incubus/Motion, Justice, Dragon/Motion,\nFLASHLiGHT,  Fnord,  Scotty,  Neuromancer,  Jarri,  Jabo,  SiR Jack and all\nothers who know uz...\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,12005,5,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048589);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('man_wv09','MAN_WV09.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MAN_WV09.LHA',NULL,'XIM','/\  /\  /\  /\  /\  -=( Mannassas )=-',NULL,NULL,'MAN','/  \/  \/  \/  \/ /  °°° /X Design °°° / /\__/\ \/\ \/\  /       brings you \/      \/  \/  \/ [-> WiLD Vote v0.9 <-]',replace('   /\  /\  /\  /\  /\  -=( Mannassas )=-  \n  /  \/  \/  \/  \/ /  °°° /X Design °°°  \n / /\__/\ \/\ \/\  /       brings you   \n \/      \/  \/  \/ [-> WiLD Vote v0.9 <-]\n The ultimate multi-function /X Vote door\n  uSeR aDD & DeLeTe & ReVieW & MaNY MoRe\n','\n',char(10)),'wildvote.guide',replace('@database WiLDVote.doc \n\n@node MAIN "WiLDVote v0.9 DoX (c) 01/94  WiLD THiNG/Mannassas"\n\n                           [---> Mannassas <---]\n                               presents the\n      ____  ____  ___ __ _______ _____________________   _____________\n     /    /\    \/   \  :       \        /     :      : /    /       /\n    //           \___/  :___     \   ___/ ____ : ____ :/    /___    /____\n    \            /   \      \ /  /    /:       :      :        /   /    /\n     \____/\____/\___/______/___/____/ :_______:______:_______/________/\n                                  SeRieS\n     ====================================================================\n                               WiLD VoTe v0.9\n                   written 01/94 by WiLD THiNG/Mannassas\n     ====================================================================\n\n                              C O N T E N T S\n              @{" Features            " link "overview"}    @{" Preface           " link "preface"}\n              @{" Installation        " link "installation"}    @{" Greetings         " link "greets"}\n              @{" Future improvements " link "improvements"}    @{" Contact           " link "contact"}\n              @{" other WiLDTooLS     " link "tools"}    @{" History           " link "history"}\n                                \n                                 \n\n@endnode\n@node preface\nWell,  I  wrote  this  door  so far in 3 days from scratch, but I think the\nresult isn''t as bad as it seems, if you don''t like my door, then don''t tell\nme it''s bullshit or something like that, but tell me WHY you don''t like it.\n  This is the first amigaguide doc for one of my WiLDTools, but we should\nuse all that fine features that the best computer ever made has, remember\n          ---------> oNLy aMiGa MaKeS iT ALL PoSSiBLe <----------\n\nbye and keep da warez rollin''\n\n\n                    08/01/94 [---> WiLD THiNG - Mannassas - DiXiE BBS <---]\n@endnode\n\n@node overview\n                          --- F E A T U R E S ---\n\n· scans for new topics at login and lists them\n· everyone can add/delete topics and items to vote on (access level\n  depending, differs on every topic if a user can add items or not)\n· creates complete result list for free download at wish\n· users votes will be stored, so he can look where he voted on and change\n  his vote - everyone can vote only once\n· results are shown sorted with percentage and graph bars\n· info who and when somebody created a topic and optional long description\n· optional logs to callerslog\n\n\n              *** THIS DOOR DOESN''T CONTAIN ANY BACKDOORS ***\n\nThe  only  ''hidden''  function  is  the  command ''q'' which will exit without\nsaving(for access higher than 250)\n\n@endnode\n\n@node installation\n                      --- I N S T A L L A T I O N --\n\nBecause  this  is just a beta release you''ll have to create the first topic\nby  hand  or  change  the  one  in  the arc.  There has to be a file called\ntems.WV in the Doors:WildTools/Wildvote/ directory which contains:\n\n                     first line  - number of topics\n                     second line - name of the topics\n                     third line  - access level needed to add item\n\nin the Doors:WildTools/Wildvote/tems/ directory are the files with the\nvotes and the names of each topic their names are the numbers of the\ntopic. e.g: file 1(KeWLeST BBS):\n=== cut here ===\nDiXiE   <------- name of the item\n4       <------- number of votes\nMamba\n4\nCrazy World\n4\n=== cut here ===\nIf  you  want  WiLDVote  to  be started automatically at every logon and to\ncheck  if  a  user hasn''t voted on a topic yet you''ll have to use two names\nfor  it,  for  the auto-start it MUST be ''WVC'' for the other anything else.\nNow put the ~CC_WVC command to your bull.txt.\nThe  problem  is  that  WiLDVote shouldn''t be used at more than one node at\nonce  but  as  WiLDVote has two different names there might be some problem\nwith the stats files.\nWV is an AIM type door, MULTINODE=NO\n\nHave a look at the WiLDVote.cfg file, here the access levels for the\ndifferent actions are defined.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node improvements\n                    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n                    The complete version will contain:\n                    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n    - item deletion\n    - installation routine\n    - list of voters\n\n@endnode\n\n@node history\n                    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n                                 History:\n                    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n- v0.3          completely rewrote it after the old version was gone after\n                a HD crash\n- v0.4          added review with sorting\n- v0.5          first public beta release\n                Review improved with graph bars, access checking for\n                delete/add\n- v0.6          access checking for each topic\n- v0.7          improved vote scanning: now topics are shown at login,\n                topic menu  shown in two rows\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n                         v0.8 - released 08-Jan-94\ngrafical  output  improvements,  made  scan  routine look nicer, added save\nprogress  indicator,  searches  for  duplicate  items,  checks  now if item\nalready  exists,  removed  some  minor  bugs,  now  info  option  with long\ndescription possibility, configurable callerslog option\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nv0.9 - released\nagain improved the design a bit and made it more compact, updated helpfile,\nresult download  option as ANSI file\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nAll  of the WiLDTools are first released at DiXiE BBS and then at Mamba and\nCrazy World.\n\nIf you want beta - test my tools @{"call me" link "contact"}.\n@endnode\n\n@node greets\n                          ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n                           Special thanx for ...\n                          ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nZiPPER/Yodel    : THX for all\nZielu/Mad Elks  : thx for yer bug reports\nJarri/Mannassas : ...lots of good ideas\nuNReaL/FeaR     : ...all the KeWL ASCII''s\n\n                    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n                       Greetings go to(in no order)\n                    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nEasy  Rider/Mystic,  Empire/Mystic,  EaZy-E/Taurus,  AXE/Mystic, Tic., R19,\nDragon/Motion, Vince, Andy/Motion, Sunset and all others who know uz...\n\n                             ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n                              Fuckings go to\n                             ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nPolish telecom (TPSA): fucked up assholes\nall you stupid lamers here that even can''t do a simple file description\n\nPS.: If I forgot you, leave me a messy at @{"one of our boards" link "contact"}\n@endnode\n\n@node contact\n                *** For any improvement or bug reports ***\n             *** write to WiLD THiNG at one of our boards ***\n\n   __________                                   _____\n..(_    ____ \...______......______.....___....(    / /\  _____  /\........\n.../   /    \ \ /   _  \    /  /  /..../   ).../   / /  \ \   / /  \...... \n../   /     / //   / \  \  /  /  /.....)   \../   /_(    \_) (_/    )....  \n./   /      \//   /   \  \/  /  /...../    (_/   /   \             /....   \n(   (        /\  /     \  \ /  /...../          / __  \           /....    \n.\   \______/  \ \_____/   \\  \..../   /)     / (__)  )    _    /....     \n..\            /           / \  \../   /.\    /\      /.\  /.\  /....      \n...\__________/\__________/\_/\_/ /   /..(___/..\____/...\/...\/....       \n.................................(___/.............................\n\n                             oNe oF ouR BoaRDZ\n\n[--> <--------------------------------------------------------------> <--]\n[--> CRaZY WoRLD  PHQ  SySoP: JaRRi/Mannassas          ++48-2-6636797 <--]\n[--> DiXiE        WHQ  SySoP: WiLD THiNG/Mannassas     ++48-71-575825 <--]\n[--> LiFe         PHQ  SySoP: RaBoCoST/Mannassas       ++48-22-118628 <--]\n[--> Vacant       PCHQ SySoP: ZyRioN/Mannassas         ++48-42-871766 <--]\n[--> <--------------------------------------------------------------> <--]\n\nIf you would like to join us as a coder, grafician, musician, trader or sysop\ncontact us at one of our boards or one of our @{"members" link "members"}.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node tools\n                          LooK ouT FoR THe oTHeR \n      ____  ____  ___ __ _______ _____________________   _____________\n     /    /\    \/   \  :       \        /     :      : /    /       /\n    //           \___/  :___     \   ___/ ____ : ____ :/    /___    /____\n    \            /   \      \ /  /    /:       :      :        /   /    /\n     \____/\____/\___/______/___/____/ :_______:______:_______/________/\n\n\n[----- NAME ------|------ DESCRIPTION -------|------- FEATURES ---------------]\n WiLDRead v0.13   | file/archive/log viewer  | text search\n                  |                          | file/arc info\n                  |                          | next/prev. page\n                  |                          | page selection\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDNeW v0.4     | new user questionaire    | multilanguage\n                  |                          | baud checking for questions\n                  |                          | multiple answers\n                  |                          | text comments (internal ed)\n                  |                          | sysop review of new users\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDBull v0.2    | global bulletins         | scroll bar selection\n                  |                          | all bulls in one dir\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDMenu v0.1    | multi level menus        | all menus in one file\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDKick v0.1    | unwanted users kick out  | show  msg to user & hang up\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDList v0.1    | global filelist dl       | packs filelists from all confs\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n\n@endnode\n\n@node members\n\n                    FEAR & MANNASSAS OFFICIAL MEMBERLIST\n                                 08-Jan-94\n\n 			  FEAR - AMIGA POLAND\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDARK ANGEL      -       CODER		- Ex.INVESTATION\nHUDSON          -       MUSICIAN	- EX.DDF\nJABO            -       TRADER		- EX.INVESTATION\nMEPHISTO        -       MUSICIAN	- EX.INVESTATION\nSHADE           -       PROGRAMMER\nTEES            -       GRAPHICIAN	- EX.EQUINOX\nTHANATOS        -       PROGRAMMER\nTHE TRADER      -       SWAPPER,CHIEF	- EX.INVESTATION\n\n 			   FEAR - AMIGA GERMANY\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nALEC EMPIRE	-	MUSICIAN,SWAPPER - EX.IRIS\n\n 			   FEAR - AMIGA BAHRAIN\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n		EXOTIC		-	SWAPPER\n\n 			   FEAR - AMIGA ENGLAND\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n		KING TUT	-	SWAPPER\n\n 			   FEAR - AMIGA DENMARK\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n		FOXTROT 	-	SWAPPER\n\n 			   FEAR - AMIGA JORDANIA\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n		BASSAM 		-	SWAPPER\n\n 			     FEAR - PC POLAND\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nJASPER		-	CODER	\nUNREAL		-	CODER	- EX.INVESTATION\nGaMmA           -       PROGRAMER\nDiScOvEr        -       PROGRAMER\nMr. NoName      -       CODER\nFrOdO           -       CODER\n\n\n\n                          Mannassas - subgroup of Fear\n                                Polish division:\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n                     WiLD THiNG      sysop - /X dezign - chief\n                     Crazy Squaw     gfx\n                     Rabocost        animations - sysop\n                     Gollum          trader - coder\n                     Spec            trader - sfx\n                     Kajtek          gfx\n                     lEVY            /X dezign\n                     Jarri           sysop\n                     ZyRiOn          sysop - coder\n                     Trocek          trader - coder\n        \n                                German division:\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n                        KC              trader - sfx\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n@endnode\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,20960,5,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048589);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mapus132','MAPUS132.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MAPUS132.LHA',NULL,'XIM','MaPuS.132',NULL,'Eniac',NULL,'|  _____/\  __________  ___  /\____        | |  \____  \/  _¬\___ ¬\/ |¬\/  ___/--------| |   |  ..  \     \  __/  |  \___ ¬\  v1.32 |',replace('.------------------------------------------.\n|  _____/\  __________  ___  /\____        |\n|  \____  \/  _¬\___ ¬\/ |¬\/  ___/--------|\n|   |  ..  \     \  __/  |  \___ ¬\  v1.32 |\n|   |__||__/__|__/__| \_____/_____/--------|\n| <------( DMS checker By Eniac )--------> |\n`--------------------------------------mk--''\n','\n',char(10)),'MAPUS.GUIDE',replace('@database MaPuSDoc\n\nCopyright (c) 1993-94 by Caton\nAll Rights Reserved\n\n@Remark $VER: MaPuS Dox AmigaGuide format 1.5 (6.5.94) by Caton\n\n@node MAIN "MaPuS"\n\nSelect language please:\n\n                    @{" ITALIANO " Link ITA}      -      @{" ENGLISH " Link ENG}\n            /\\\n           /  \\\n     ______\\__/___________  _______ _______  ____\n     \\_____/  \\________   \\/       \\\\_     \\|    |\n     .    /    \\|   _|/   /   _/\\   \\|           |<<----------------+\n     :   /      \\   \\_    \\   \\_/    \\           |                  |\n        /        \\   |\\    \\_        /    \\      |                  |\n     :  \\________/   | \\____/_______/|    |\\_____|                  |\n     |          |____|______   ______|____|________                 |\n     |                \\_    |  \\_        \\ \\__    / ______          |\n     |                 |    |Mb |  _/|    \\  /   /\\|    _/          |\n     |                 |    |___|  \\__     \\/   /  \\    |           |\n     |                 |    /   \\    |\\     \\_          |           |\n     |                 |________/    | \\_____/___/\\     |           |\n     `--------------------------|____|-------------\\____|-----------''\n\n                                 PRESENTS:\n\n               .------------------------------------------.\n               |  _____/\\  __________  ___  /\\____        |\n               |  \\____  \\/  _¬\\___ ¬\\/ |¬\\/  ___/--------|\n               |   |  ..  \\     \\  __/  |  \\___ ¬\\        |\n               |   |__||__/__|__/__| \\_____/_____/--------|\n               | <------( DMS checker By Eniac )--------> |\n               `--------------------------------------mk--''\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ITA "Istruzioni di ''MaPuS''."\n\n                             @{b}INDICE GENERALE:@{ub}\n\n@{" ATTENZIONE " Link Cap01}\n@{" INTRODUZIONE A MaPuS " Link Cap02}\n@{" PERCHE'' USARE MaPuS E NON UN ALTRO CHECKER? " Link Cap03}\n@{" COME FUNZIONA " Link Cap04}\n@{" ESEMPI " Link Cap05}\n@{" USO DI MaPuS CON AMIEXPRESS o DLG " Link AXuso}\n@{" GLOSSARIO " Link Cap06}\n@{" UPDATES DEL MaPuS " Link Cap07}\n@{" FUTURI SVILUPPI " Link Cap08}\n@{" RINGRAZIAMENTI " Link Cap09}\n@{" COME CONTATTARCI " Link Cap10}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap01 "ATTENZIONE:"\n\n\nE''  stato  deciso  di  immettere  questo  programma  nel  Pubblico Dominio,\nimponendo l''opzione dello Shareware qualora venisse usato regolarmente.\n\nQuindi se lo hai installato nella tua BBS o lo utilizzi di routine, faresti\nbene a registrarti per premiare il lavoro di chi lo sviluppa.\n\nLa  cifra  di  registrazione  (simbolica) e` di 15$ o 15000 Lire da spedire\ninclusa  nella  busta  o  come cheque o come vaglia postale al seguente\nindirizzo:\n\n                             Antonino Pintaudi\n                                P.O. Box 11\n                         98125 Contesse (Messina)\n                                  ITALIA\n\nL''archivio originale MaPuS???.LHA (in cui ???  e` il numero della versione)\nnon puo'' essere modificato.  Non possono essere aggiunti o tolti file salvo\nle normali "pubblicita''" delle BBS.\n\nLa lista dei file che contiene l''archivio originale e` la seguente:\n\n---\nbbs/fcheck/DMS                      ;Configurazione per @{"AmiExpress" Link AXuso}\nbbs/fcheck/DMS.Info                 ;Configurazione per @{"AmiExpress v3.+" Link AXuso}\nbin/MaPuS.???                       ;Eseguibile (??? sta per n. di ver.)\nDLGConfig/Batch/UPLOAD1.BATCH       ;/\nDLGConfig/Text/Banner.displayme     ;| Files necessari per @{"DLG" Link AXuso}\nDLGConfig/Text/PreDesc.txt          ;\\\ndoc/MaPuS.GUIDE                     ;Istruzioni in formato AmigaGuide\nlibs/arp.library                    ;arp.library V39.1\nIRONLAW.txt.Displayme               ;/ Pubblicita'' di\nread.i                              ;\\ @{"IRON LAW BBS" Link Cap10}\n---\n\nIn  caso  avessi  qualche  tua proposta per migliorare il programma (ad es.\nuno  script  per  il  tuo  programma  di BBS) DEVI contattare l''autore, che\nincludera''  (con  i  dovuti ringraziamenti) il tuo lavoro in ogni revisione\ndel programma.\n\nNessuno  e` responsabile in alcun modo degli eventuali (e remoti) danni che\nMaPuS potrebbe arrecare al tuo sistema.\n\nMaPuS e` stato scritto totalmente in @{i}Assembly@{ui}!\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap02 "INTRODUZIONE A MaPuS:"\n\n\nCos''e`  MaPuS?   MaPuS  e`  la soluzione ideale per il trattamento dei file\nDMS.    Puoi   manipolarli   come  piu''  ti  aggrada.   Puoi  controllarli,\naggiungere,  rimuovere e creare @{"front, tail e track banner" Link Cap06}; tutto in un\nmodo alquanto funzionale.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap03 "PERCHE'' USARE MaPuS E NON UN ALTRO CHECKER?"\n\n\nSemplice.   Alcuni  checker  non funzionano perfettamente su tutti i files,\naltri  non  ti  forniscono  le  informazioni in modo completo, e nessuno ti\npermette  di  creare  e aggiungere banner.  MaPuS puo'' essere usato con una\n@{"BBS"  Link AXuso} o nei tuoi file @{"script" Link Cap05} o semplicemente per  @{"testare i file DMS" Link Cap04}.\nMaPuS e` garantito al 100% su queste funzioni.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap04 "COME FUNZIONA:"\n\nSe invochi MaPuS con solo il suo nome ti fornira'' la sintassi:\n\nMaPuS [-<options>] FileName[.DMS] [DestFile]\n\nOpzioni:\n\n@{" Operazioni sui front banner " Link FrontOpt}\n@{" Operazioni sui track banner " Link TrackOpt}\n@{" Operazioni sui tail banner " Link TailOpt}\n            @{" Varie " Link VarieOpt}\n\nSe invochi MaPuS con il solo nome file sorgente, questo sara'' controllato e\nti verranno mostrate alcune informazioni sullo stato.\n\nLa specifica del file sorgente puo'' contenere le wildcards * o ? o #?.\n\n@{b}NOTA: Ad ogni revisione di MaPuS ricordati di ricreare il MaPuS.cfg@{ub}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node FrontOpt "Operazioni sui front banner:"\n\n\n\n\n\n@{" a " Link Opta} aggiunge un front banner.\n@{" r " Link Optr} rimuove i front banner.\n@{" m " Link Optm} crea un front banner.\n\n\n\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node TrackOpt "Operazioni sui track banner:"\n\n\n\n\n@{" t " Link Opta} aggiunge un track banner.\n@{" k " Link Optr} rimuove i track banner.\n@{" n " Link Optm} crea un track banner.\n\n\n\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node TailOpt "Operazioni sui tail banner:"\n\n\n\n\n@{" A " Link Opta} aggiunge un tail banner.\n@{" R " Link Optr} rimuove i tail banner.\n@{" M " Link Optm} crea un tail banner.\n\n\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Opta "Aggiungi banner:"\n\n\nDevi  fornire  il  "FileName"  sorgente  (con o senza l''estenzione .DMS) ed\nopzionalmente un file destinazione "DestFile".\n\nMaPuS  testera''  il  file  ed  aggiungera''  il  banner al file destinazione\n(creando  quindi una copia del file sorgente) o direttamente al sorgente in\ncaso mancasse il destinazione.\n\nQualora  non  fornissi  alcun  nome  di  file  come parametro, apparira'' un\nrequester ARP, che ti permettera'' di sceglierne uno.\n\n@{b}NOTA:@{ub} Se devi creare il file destinazione in RAM: usa l''opzione @{"s" Link VarieOpt}.\n\nIl  "FileName" puo'' essere privo di estensione, ma e` indispensabile che la\nscriva tu per il file destinazione.\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Optr "Rimuovi i banner:"\n\n\nSpecifica   come   parametri   il  nome  del  file  sorgente  e  di  quello\ndestinazione.   MaPuS,  dopo aver testato il file sorgente, creera'' un file\ndestinazione privo dei banner.  Se non hai specificato il file destinazione\ni banner verranno "strippati" direttamente dal file sorgente.\n\nQualora  mancasse  anche  quest''ultimo,  apparira''  un requester ARP che ti\npermettera'' di sceglierlo.\n\n@{b}NOTA:@{ub} Se usi la RAM: specifica l''opzione @{"s" Link VarieOpt}.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Optm "Crea i banner:"\n\n\nSpecifica  il  nome  del  file  di  testo  da  usare come banner o se no ti\napparira''  un  requester  che  ti permettera'' di sceglierlo.  MaPuS creera''\nnella  S:   un  file  chiamato  "MaPuS.cfg", che ti permettera'' di usare le\nopzioni di adding.\n\nIl formato del file testo e`:  64 colonne (return compreso) per 16 linee.\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node VarieOpt "Opzioni varie:"\n\n@{b} s @{ub}  -  Non  controllare  lo  spazio disponibile.  Indispensabile se\n        lavori nella RAM:  che e` sempre piena al 100%.\n\n@{b} v @{ub}  -  Visualizza delle informazioni sul file DMS, ma non testarlo.\n\n@{b} d @{ub}  -  Metti la data di upload nel track banner da aggiungere.\n\n@{b} g @{ub}  -  Visualizza alcuni ringraziamenti.\n\n@{b} u @{ub}  -  Per scegliere, in ogni caso, il file DMS da un requester ARP.\n\n@{b} f @{ub}  -  Visualizza dettagliate informazioni su ogni traccia del file\n        DMS.\n\n@{b} c @{ub}  -  Restituisce un codice di ritorno di 15 in caso di fallito\n        checking.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap05 "ESEMPI:"\n\n\n1) Controlla un file:\n In questo esempio immaginiamo di avere un file nella tua directory DL:\nchiamato TEST.DMS e che tu voglia controllarlo.\n\nMaPuS dl:TEST.dms o MaPuS dl:TEST\n\nsara''  controllato  e  ti verranno mostrate alcune informazioni sullo stato\ndello stesso.\n\n2) Crea un @{"tail banner" Link TailOpt}:\n\nMaPuS -M \n\n3) Aggiungi un @{"front banner" Link FrontOpt} e rimuovi i @{"tail" Link TailOpt} e @{"track banner" Link TrackOpt}:\n\nMaPuS -AskR dl:TEST[.dms] ram:newTEST.dms\n\n(Nota l''opzione @{"s" Link VarieOpt} per la ram:)\n\n4) Testa tutti i file di una directory:\n\nMaPuS dl:*.dms ovvero MaPuS dl:#?.dms\n\n@endnode\n\n@node AXuso "Uso con /X o DLG:"\n\n\nSe vuoi usare MaPuS con AmiExpress usa lo script incluso: @{b}bbs/fcheck/DMS@{ub}\n\n<----- CONTENUTO DEL FILE: ---------- CUT ------------------------------->\nMaPuS\n\nError\n<------------------------------------ CUT ------------------------------->\n\nNOTA: La seconda linea contiene le opzioni per il MaPuS.\n\n@{b} RICORDA: @{ub} Il file deve contenere esclusivamente queste 3 linee!\n\n  Se  possiedi  una  versione  superiore  alla  3.0  di  AmiExpress  piazza\nsemplicemente  il file incluso nell''archivio - "DMS.info" - nella directory\nBBS:FCheck.\n\nInclusi nell''archivio i file necessari per l''uso di MaPuS con DLG:\n\nDLGConfig/Batch/UPLOAD1.BATCH\nDLGConfig/Text/Banner.displayme\nDLGConfig/Text/PreDesc.txt\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap06 "GLOSSARIO:"\n\n@{"Tail Banner" Link TailOpt}:  e` il testo che sara'' aggiunto in coda al file DMS.\n              (e` l''ultimo che verra'' mostrato nella scompattazione)\n\n@{"Front Banner" Link FrontOpt}: e` il testo che sara'' aggiunto in fronte al file DMS.\n              (e` il primo che verra'' mostrato nella scompattazione)\n\n@{"Track Banner" Link TrackOpt}: e` la traccia zero che sara'' mostrata come se fosse un testo.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap07 "UPDATES DEL MaPuS:"\n\n0.** Versioni sperimentali mai rilasciate.\n\n0.84 Prima versione pubblica. Per mia decisione tutte le versioni pubbliche\n     da ora in poi non implementeranno l''opzione @{"-k" Link TrackOpt}.\n \n0.85 Prima versione registrata, rilasciata a chi ne faceva richiesta\n     chiamando @{"IRON LAW BBS" Link Cap10}.\n \n0.86-0.91 Versioni private\n     Sistemati alcuni bug, fra cui l''opzione @{"-k" Link TrackOpt} che corrompeva l''archivio\n     se vi erano un track banner e subito dopo un front banner.\n\n0.92 Versione pubblica.\n     Implementata l''opzione @{"-f" Link VarieOpt}.  Se specificata mostra informazioni\n     dettagliate su ogni traccia del file DMS.\n\n0.93 Versione registrata.\n \n0.94 Versione mai rilasciata.\n \n0.95 Versione Shareware.\n     Sistemato un bug il quale non faceva funzionare l''opzione @{"-f" Link VarieOpt} se\n     il file era selezionato dal requester.\n \n0.96 Versione Shareware.\n     Su segnalazione di Felix rimosso un bug per il quale MaPuS non poteva\n     essere reso residente. Sistemate alcune piccolezze.\n\n0.97 Versione registrata.\n\n0.98-0.99 Versioni private.\n\n1.00 Versione Shareware, non completa a causa della MANCANZA totale di\n     registrazioni!\n     Chi desidera la versione completa deve versare la quota di\n     registrazione o contattare @{"IRON LAW BBS" Link Cap10}.\n     Aggiunta delle wildcards (*,?,#?).  Velocizzata la routine di\n     stripping,  in alcuni casi e` piu'' veloce del 200%!!!  Creata la guide\n     che contiene sia le istruzioni in italiano che in inglese, modificata\n     la struttura dell''archivio.\n\n1.01 Versione registrata.\n\n1.02-1.09 Versioni private.\n\n1.10 Versione rilasciata allo SMAU 1993.  Aggiunta la possibilita'' di\n     inserire la data di upload (utile per le BBS) nei track banner\n     (opzione @{"-d" Link VarieOpt}).  Ora l''esecuzione di MaPuS puo'' essere bloccata con\n     CTRL-C (solo dopo il test).\n\n1.11 Versione registrata.\n\n1.12 Sistemata l''opzione @{"-t" Link Trackopt}. Per un bug nella 1.10 quest''opzione\n     non funzionava correttamente su 68000.\n\n1.13 Versione registrata.\n\n1.14 Sistemati due problemi:\n     1) Se il nome del file conteneva il carattere "-", MaPuS\n        non interpretava correttamente la linea di comando.\n     2) A volte l''add di un track banner corrompeva l''archivio.\n\n1.15 Versione registrata.\n\n1.16 Rimossi due bug:\n     1) Qualora durante il check di un file venisse premuto CTRL-C il\n        programma faceva bloccare il sistema.\n     2) Piccolo problema con la command line.\n     Ora le informazioni che da'' MaPuS sono compatibili con il DMS V1.51+.\n     Modifiche alla guide, eliminati i doc in formato ASCII.\n\n1.17 Versione registrata.  (I_I)\n\n1.18-1.29 Versioni Private mai rilasciate.\n          Nota: ho visto girare una versione 1.20. Questa versione non e`\n          mai stata creata da me, percio'' sconsiglio l''utilizzo.\n\n1.30 Sistemati alcuni bug: ora il checking di un file vuoto non produce\n     problemi.\n\n     Aggiunto il supporto delle virgolette: ora il nome del file\n     puo'' contenere spazi, se fra virgolette.\n\n1.31 Versione registrata.\n\n1.32 Implementata l''opzione @{"-c" Link VarieOpt} per far restituire un codice di ritorno di 15\n     in caso di fallito checking (su segnalazione di Jay Ruyle).\n\n1.33 Versione registrata.\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap08 "FUTURI SVILUPPI:"\n\n- MaPuS potra'' prendere da un file la lista dei file su cui operare.\n\n- Utilizzo di un migliore requester, mantenendo la compatibilita'' con il SO\n  1.3.\n\n- View dei banner.\n\n- Script per fallimento o riuscita del test (utile per BBS).\n\n- Aggiunta della data al tail e al front banner.\n\n- Possibilita'' di rendere random la scelta del banner da aggiungere (ottimo\n  per le BBS).\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap09 "RINGRAZIAMENTI:"\n\n\n\nMolte grazie a (in ordine alfabetico):\n\nAlex,  /\\rc, Atomos, Batblaster, Blulight, Caton, Crier, Deus, Doc, Doctor\nRevenge,  DR.Dream/FTH,  DR.G,  Exodus,  Fashion Light, Felix, Gandalf/FTH,\nGhost,  GiapDJ,  Godfather,  Guile, Highlander, Høøk/FTH, Jay Ruyle, Joseph\nHodge  (/X  author), Kenshiro, Kris, Laurent, Leo, LoneWolf, Mad Harlequin,\nMad Lemming, MAUI BBS (2:335/602@fidonet), /\\/\\aster T/4WD, Metalbasher!,\nMF  the  Best,  Modem  Boy,  Mondrian,  MR.IRQ,  MR.Swapper,  /\\/ightmare,\n/\\/ikita/4WD,  Nosferatu, Pier, Pixie, Polaris, Pork, Pows, Randy, Sauzer,\nSeven  /\\/\\, Shady, Splatter, T-Rexx, The Outlaw, Top, Tron/RPK, Warrior,\nWoodelf, tutti i miei utenti, e tutti coloro che dimentico...\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap10 "CONTATTI:"\n\nPuoi contattarci (in Matrix) ai seguenti indirizzi:\n\n2:335/602.15@fidonet\n39:102/1.15@amiganet\[email removed]\nEniac@ITPH06\n\no via posta "classica" a:\n\n                             Antonino Pintaudi\n                                P.O. Box 11\n                         98125 Contesse (Messina)\n                                  ITALIA\n\n\nOPPURE CHIAMA:\n            /\\\n           /  \\\n     ______\\__/___________  _______ _______  ____\n     \\_____/  \\________   \\/       \\\\_     \\|    |\n     .    /    \\|   _|/   /   _/\\   \\|           |<<----------------+\n     :   /      \\   \\_    \\   \\_/    \\           | ++39-(0)90-881378|\n        /        \\   |\\    \\_        /    \\      |                  |\n     :  \\________/   | \\____/_______/|    |\\_____|  SYSOP: Crier    |\n     |          |____|______   ______|____|________                 |\n     |                \\_    |  \\_        \\ \\__    / ______          |\n     | 16800 HST       |    |Mb |  _/|    \\  /   /\\|    _/          |\n     | AmiExpress      |    |___|  \\__     \\/   /  \\    |           |\n     |                 |    /   \\    |\\     \\_          |           |\n     |                 |________/    | \\_____/___/\\     |    24/24h |\n     `--------------------------|____|-------------\\____|-----------''\n\n\nATTENZIONE: NUOVO NUMERO!! ++39-(0)90-881378.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ENG "MaPuS dox:"\n\n                             @{b}GENERAL INDEX:@{ub}\n\n@{" WARNING " Link Cap01E}\n@{" INTRODUCING MaPuS " Link Cap02E}\n@{" WHY SHOULD YOU USE MaPuS AND NOT ANOTHER CHECKER? " Link Cap03E}\n@{" HOW DOES IT WORK " Link Cap04E}\n@{" EXAMPLES " Link Cap05E}\n@{" AMIEXPRESS OR DLG USING OF MaPuS" Link AXusoE}\n@{" GLOSSARY " Link Cap06E}\n@{" MaPuS'' UPDATES " Link Cap07E}\n@{" FUTURE FEATURES " Link Cap08E}\n@{" GREETINGS " Link Cap09E}\n@{" CONTACTS " Link Cap10E}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap01E "PAY ATTENTION:"\n\n\nMaPuS is Shareware, you must register yourself if you use it regularly.\n\nThe registration charge is 15$. You can send it enclosed on the envelope\nor as cheque at the following address:\n\n\n                             Antonino Pintaudi\n                                P.O. Box 11\n                         98125 Contesse (Messina)\n                                  ITALY\n\nThe  original  archive  MaPuS???.LHA  (???  is the version number) can''t be\nmodified.  You can''t add or remove files except BBS advertisements.\n\nThe archive files list is the following:\n\n---\nbbs/fcheck/DMS                       ;@{"AmiExpress" Link AXusoE} config\nbbs/fcheck/DMS.info                  ;@{"AmiExpress v3.+" Link AXusoE} config\nbin/MaPuS.???                        ;Executable program (??? =n. of version)\nDLGConfig/Batch/UPLOAD1.BATCH        ;/\nDLGConfig/Text/Banner.displayme      ;| @{"DLG" Link AXusoE} Config\nDLGConfig/Text/PreDesc.txt           ;\\\ndoc/MaPuS.GUIDE                      ;AmigaGuide ITALIAN & ENGLISH dox.\nlibs/arp.library                     ;arp.library V39.1\nIRONLAW.txt.Displayme                ;/ @{"IRON LAW BBS" Link Cap10E}\nread.i                               ;\\   addings\n---\n\n   If  you  want  to include any your proposition for MaPuS in the archive,\nyou MUST contact the author; he''ll include your work into the next versions\nand he will thank you.\n\nNO-ONE  is  responsable  of  (remote) damages that MaPuS can create to your\nsystem.\n\nMaPuS is written entirely in @{i}Assembly@{ui}!\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap02E "INTRODUCING MaPuS:"\n\n\nWhat  is  MaPuS?  MaPuS is the ultimate solution for DMS files.  You can do\nall  you  want  on  these  files.  You can check them, make, remove and add\ntail, track, front banners; all in a good and functional way.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap03E "WHY SHOULD YOU USE MaPuS AND NOT ANOTHER CHECKER?"\n\n\nSimple.   Some  doesn''t  work perfectly on all files, others don''t give you\nall  informations  about the file, and no-one lets you add your text files.\nMaPuS can be used with a @{"BBS" Link AXusoE} or into your @{"script files"\nLink  Cap05E} or simply to @{"check" Link Cap04E}\nyour DMS files.  MaPuS is 100% tested for these functions.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap04E "HOW DOES IT WORK:"\n\nIf you invoke MaPuS with only his name, you''ll get the syntax:\n\nMaPuS [-<options>] FileName[.DMS] [DestFile]\n\nOptions:\n\n@{" Operations on front banners " Link FrontOptE}\n@{" Operations on track banners " Link TrackOptE}\n@{" Operations on tail banners " Link TailOptE}\n        @{" Other options " Link VarieOptE}\n\n\nIf you invoke MaPuS with the source file name only, the file will be tested\nand are printed on the screen many informations about it.\n\nYou can also specify wildcards in source file name:  *, ?, #?.\n\n@{b}Please update your MaPuS.cfg on every revision of MaPuS.@{ub}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node FrontOptE "Operations on front banners:"\n\n\n\n\n\n@{" a " Link OptaE} add a front banner.\n@{" r " Link OptrE} remove front banners.\n@{" m " Link OptmE} make a front banner.\n\n\n\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node TrackOptE "Operations on track banners:"\n\n\n\n\n@{" t " Link OptaE} add a track banner.\n@{" k " Link OptrE} remove track banners.\n@{" n " Link OptmE} make a track banner.\n\n\n\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node TailOptE "Operations on tail banners:"\n\n\n\n\n@{" A " Link OptaE} add a tail banner.\n@{" R " Link OptrE} remove tail banners.\n@{" M " Link OptmE} make a tail banner.\n\n\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node OptaE "Add a banner:"\n\n\nSpecify  source  "FileName"  (with  or  without .DMS extention) and, if you\nwant, a destination file "DestFile".\n\nMaPuS  will  test  that  file  and  add  the  banner to the destination one\n(making,  so,  a  copy  of  the  source  file) or if the destination is not\nspecified to the source file directly.\n\nIf the source file name were absent, an ARP requester would appear.\n\n@{b}NOTE:@{ub} If you want to create the destination file in RAM: use the @{"s" Link VarieOptE} option.\n\n"FileName"  can  be  without  extention,  but  you MUST write the extention\nyourself in the destination file name.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node OptrE "Remove banners:"\n\nPass  source FileName and/or DestFile name and MaPuS will search and remove\nfront  banners and report to you operation results.  If no destination file\nwere specified, the banners would be stripped to the source file directly.\n\nIf you don''t specify FileName, an ARP requester will appear.\n\n@{b}NOTE:@{ub} If you use the RAM: specify the @{"s" Link VarieOpt} option.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node OptmE "Create banners:"\n\n\nPass  the  text  file  name  or a requester will appear and it will let you\nselect  a  filename  as  banner.   MaPuS  will  place in S:  a file, called\n"MaPuS.cfg".  Now you can add it to your DMS files.\n\nText file format is:  64 colums (with linefeed) for 16 lines.\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node VarieOptE "Other options:"\n\n@{b} s @{ub}  -  Don''t check free space. You should use it if you work with RAM:\n\n@{b} v @{ub}  -  View DMS file informations only, and don''t check it.\n\n@{b} d @{ub}  -  Add to track banners the uploading date.\n\n@{b} g @{ub}  -  Show some greetings.\n\n@{b} u @{ub}  -  Use an ARP requester to select the DMS file.\n\n@{b} f @{ub}  -  Show informations about every track of the DMS file.\n\n@{b} c @{ub}  -  Activate return codes. If the checking fails a return code of\n        15 will be returned.\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap05E "EXAMPLES:"\n\n1) Check a file:\n In this example I will suppose that you''ve a file in your DL: directory\ncalled TEST.DMS and you want to test it.\n\nType: MaPuS DL:TEST or MaPuS dl:TEST.dms\n\nit will be tested and you''ll get some infos about the file.\n\n2) Make a @{"tail banner" Link TailOptE}:\n\nType: MaPuS -M\n\n3) Add a @{"front banner" Link FrontOptE} and remove @{"tail" Link TailOptE} and @{"track banners" Link TrackOptE}:\n\nType: MaPuS -AskR dl:TEST.dms ram:newTEST.dms\n\n(Note @{"s" Link VarieOptE} option for RAM:)\n\n4) Test all files of a directory:\n\nMaPuS dl:*.dms or MaPuS dl:#?.dms\n\n@endnode\n\nCiao...\n\n@node AXusoE "/X or DLG using:"\n\n\nIf you want to use MaPuS with AmiExpress have a look at: @{b}bbs/fcheck/DMS@{ub}\n\n<----- THERE''s THE CONTENTS OF THE FILE ---------- CUT HERE ------------->\nMaPuS\n\nError\n<------------------------------------------------- CUT HERE ------------->\n\nNOTE: the 2nd line contains the options for MaPuS.\n\n@{b} REMEMBER: @{ub} The file must contains these 3 lines only!\n\nIf you''ve AmiExpress v3+ place file "DMS.info" into BBS:FCheck directory.\n\nThe  scripts  to  use  MaPuS with DLG are included in the archive, and they\nare:\n\nDLGConfig/Batch/UPLOAD1.BATCH\nDLGConfig/Text/Banner.displayme\nDLGConfig/Text/PreDesc.txt\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap06E "GLOSSARY:"\n\n@{"Tail Banner" Link TailOptE}: it''s a text file that will be appended to the end of file.\n             (it''s the last text that will be displayed unpacking)\n\n@{"Front Banner" Link FrontOptE}: it''s a text file that will be appended to the front of file.\n              (it''s the first text that will be displayed unpacking)\n\n@{"Track Banner" Link TrackOptE}: it''s the zero-track that will displayed as text file.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap07E "MaPuS UPDATES:"\n\n0.** Sperimental versions never released.\n\n0.84 First public version.  For our decision, public versions don''t\n     implement @{"-k" Link TrackOptE} command.\n\n0.85 First registered version, got if you''ve called @{"IRON LAW BBS" Link Cap10E}.\n\n0.86-0.91 Private versions.\n     Fixed some bugs: Before @{"-k" Link TrackOptE} command corrupted archives if there were\n     track and front banner.\n\n0.92 Public version.\n     New  option @{"-f" Link VarieOptE}.  If you specify it, MaPuS will show you informations\n     about every track.\n\n0.93 Registered version.\n\n0.94 Sperimental version never released.\n\n0.95 Shareware version.\n     Fixed a bug in @{"-f" Link VarieOptE} option (the infos were not displayed if the file\n     had been selected from requester).\n\n0.96 Shareware version.\n     Fixed a bug. Now MaPuS can be resident. Thanks to Felix for bug\n     reporting.\n\n0.97 Registered version.\n\n0.98-0.99 Private versions.\n\n1.00 Shareware version, not 100% beacause no one has registered his copy of\n     MaPuS! If you want the complete version you must pay the registration\n     fee or call @{"IRON LAW BBS" Link Cap10E}.\n     Wildcards added (*,?,#?).  Speeded up stripping routine.\n     Docs  are  now  also  in Amiga-Guide format, that contains english and\n     italian ones. Archive structure modified.\n\n1.01 Registered version.\n\n1.02-1.09 Private versions.\n\n1.10 Special version released at SMAU 1993.  Added the uploading date\n     (useful for BBS) on track banners (use @{"-d" Link VarieOptE} option).  Now you can stop\n     MaPuS with CTRL-C (after the test).\n\n1.11 Registered version.\n\n1.12 Fixed a problem in @{"-t" Link TrackoptE} option. A bug made 1.10 not working on 68000\n     systems.\n\n1.13 Registered version.\n\n1.14 Fixed two problems:\n     1) If the filename started with a minus character the command line\n        parsing didn''t worked.\n     2) Sometimes the track banners adding did corrupt the archive.\n\n1.15 Registered version.\n\n1.16 Fixed two bugs:\n     1) If CTRL-C was pressed during a file check, the program crashed the\n        system.\n     2) Small command line bug.\n     Now MaPuS informations are compatible with DMS V1.51+.\n     Guide corrected, ASCII docs deleted.\n\n1.17 Registered version.\n\n1.18-1.29 Private, not released, versions.\n         Note: I saw a "1.20" version. This version hasn''t been created by us,\n         you shouldn''t use it..\n\n1.30 Fixed some bugs: now an empty file checking doesn''t do problems.\n\n     Now supporting "": file name can contain spaces, if between "".\n\n1.31 Registered version.\n\n1.32 Added return codes with @{"-c" Link VarieOptE} option. It  returns a code of 15 if the\n     checking fails. Signaled by Jay Ruyle.\n\n1.33 Registered version.\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap08E "FUTURE FEATURES:"\n\n\n- MaPuS will take the file list to operate over from a text file.\n\n- Use of a better requester.\n\n- Banner display.\n\n- Scripts for failed or successful tests (useful for BBSes).\n\n- Date adding on tail and front banners.\n\n- MaPuS will select a random banner to add.\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap09E "GREETINGS:"\n\nMany thanks go to (alphabetic order):\n\nAlex,  /\\rc, Atomos, Batblaster, Blulight, Caton, Crier, Deus, Doc, Doctor\nRevenge,  DR.Dream/FTH,  DR.G,  Exodus,  Fashion Light, Felix, Gandalf/FTH,\nGhost,  GiapDJ,  Godfather,  Guile, Highlander, Høøk/FTH, Jay Ruyle, Joseph\nHodge  (/X  author), Kenshiro, Kris, Laurent, Leo, LoneWolf, Mad Harlequin,\nMad Lemming, MAUI BBS (2:335/602@fidonet), /\\/\\aster T/4WD, Metalbasher!,\nMF  the  Best,  Modem  Boy,  Mondrian,  MR.IRQ,  MR.Swapper,  /\\/ightmare,\n/\\/ikita/4WD,  Nosferatu, Pier, Pixie, Polaris, Pork, Pows, Randy, Sauzer,\nSeven  /\\/\\, Shady, Splatter, T-Rexx, The Outlaw, Top, Tron/RPK, Warrior,\nWoodelf, all my users, all friends and all the ones I forget...\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap10E "CONTACTS:"\n\n\nYou can contact us (via NetMail) at these addresses:\n\n2:335/602.15@fidonet\n39:102/1.15@amiganet\[email removed]\nEniac@ITPH06\n\nor via "old" mail at:\n\n                             Antonino Pintaudi\n                                P.O. Box 11\n                         98125 Contesse (Messina)\n                                  ITALIA\n\nOR CALL:\n            /\\\n           /  \\\n     ______\\__/___________  _______ _______  ____\n     \\_____/  \\________   \\/       \\\\_     \\|    |\n     .    /    \\|   _|/   /   _/\\   \\|           |<<----------------+\n     :   /      \\   \\_    \\   \\_/    \\           | ++39-(0)90-881378|\n        /        \\   |\\    \\_        /    \\      |                  |\n     :  \\________/   | \\____/_______/|    |\\_____|  SYSOP: Crier    |\n     |          |____|______   ______|____|________                 |\n     |                \\_    |  \\_        \\ \\__    / ______          |\n     | 16800 HST       |    |Mb |  _/|    \\  /   /\\|    _/          |\n     | AmiExpress      |    |___|  \\__     \\/   /  \\    |           |\n     |                 |    /   \\    |\\     \\_          |           |\n     |                 |________/    | \\_____/___/\\     |    24/24h |\n     `--------------------------|____|-------------\\____|-----------''\n\n\nWARNING: NEW NUMBER: ++39-(0)90-881378\n\n@endnode\n\nWhere you''re looking in????\nFINE!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',40489,5,0,NULL,NULL,'mapus132','scan',1780048589);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mapus133','MAPUS133.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MAPUS133.LHA',NULL,'XIM','mapus.133',NULL,'Eniac',NULL,'|  _____/\  __________  ___  /\____        | |  \____  \/  _¬\___ ¬\/ |¬\/  ___/--------| |   |  ..  \     \  __/  |  \___ ¬\  v1.33 |',replace('.------------------------------------------.\n|  _____/\  __________  ___  /\____        |\n|  \____  \/  _¬\___ ¬\/ |¬\/  ___/--------|\n|   |  ..  \     \  __/  |  \___ ¬\  v1.33 |\n|   |__||__/__|__/__| \_____/_____/--------|\n| <------( DMS checker By Eniac )--------> |\n`--------------------------------------mk--''\n','\n',char(10)),'MAPUS.GUIDE',replace('@database MaPuSDoc\n\nCopyright (c) 1993-94 by Caton\nAll Rights Reserved\n\n@Remark $VER: MaPuS Dox AmigaGuide format 1.5 (6.5.94) by Caton\n\n@node MAIN "MaPuS"\n\nSelect language please:\n\n                    @{" ITALIANO " Link ITA}      -      @{" ENGLISH " Link ENG}\n            /\\\n           /  \\\n     ______\\__/___________  _______ _______  ____\n     \\_____/  \\________   \\/       \\\\_     \\|    |\n     .    /    \\|   _|/   /   _/\\   \\|           |<<----------------+\n     :   /      \\   \\_    \\   \\_/    \\           |                  |\n        /        \\   |\\    \\_        /    \\      |                  |\n     :  \\________/   | \\____/_______/|    |\\_____|                  |\n     |          |____|______   ______|____|________                 |\n     |                \\_    |  \\_        \\ \\__    / ______          |\n     |                 |    |Mb |  _/|    \\  /   /\\|    _/          |\n     |                 |    |___|  \\__     \\/   /  \\    |           |\n     |                 |    /   \\    |\\     \\_          |           |\n     |                 |________/    | \\_____/___/\\     |           |\n     `--------------------------|____|-------------\\____|-----------''\n\n                                 PRESENTS:\n\n               .------------------------------------------.\n               |  _____/\\  __________  ___  /\\____        |\n               |  \\____  \\/  _¬\\___ ¬\\/ |¬\\/  ___/--------|\n               |   |  ..  \\     \\  __/  |  \\___ ¬\\        |\n               |   |__||__/__|__/__| \\_____/_____/--------|\n               | <------( DMS checker By Eniac )--------> |\n               `--------------------------------------mk--''\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ITA "Istruzioni di ''MaPuS''."\n\n                             @{b}INDICE GENERALE:@{ub}\n\n@{" ATTENZIONE " Link Cap01}\n@{" INTRODUZIONE A MaPuS " Link Cap02}\n@{" PERCHE'' USARE MaPuS E NON UN ALTRO CHECKER? " Link Cap03}\n@{" COME FUNZIONA " Link Cap04}\n@{" ESEMPI " Link Cap05}\n@{" USO DI MaPuS CON AMIEXPRESS o DLG " Link AXuso}\n@{" GLOSSARIO " Link Cap06}\n@{" UPDATES DEL MaPuS " Link Cap07}\n@{" FUTURI SVILUPPI " Link Cap08}\n@{" RINGRAZIAMENTI " Link Cap09}\n@{" COME CONTATTARCI " Link Cap10}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap01 "ATTENZIONE:"\n\n\nE''  stato  deciso  di  immettere  questo  programma  nel  Pubblico Dominio,\nimponendo l''opzione dello Shareware qualora venisse usato regolarmente.\n\nQuindi se lo hai installato nella tua BBS o lo utilizzi di routine, faresti\nbene a registrarti per premiare il lavoro di chi lo sviluppa.\n\nLa  cifra  di  registrazione  (simbolica) e` di 15$ o 15000 Lire da spedire\ninclusa  nella  busta  o  come cheque o come vaglia postale al seguente\nindirizzo:\n\n                             Antonino Pintaudi\n                                P.O. Box 11\n                         98125 Contesse (Messina)\n                                  ITALIA\n\nL''archivio originale MaPuS???.LHA (in cui ???  e` il numero della versione)\nnon puo'' essere modificato.  Non possono essere aggiunti o tolti file salvo\nle normali "pubblicita''" delle BBS.\n\nLa lista dei file che contiene l''archivio originale e` la seguente:\n\n---\nbbs/fcheck/DMS                      ;Configurazione per @{"AmiExpress" Link AXuso}\nbbs/fcheck/DMS.Info                 ;Configurazione per @{"AmiExpress v3.+" Link AXuso}\nbin/MaPuS.???                       ;Eseguibile (??? sta per n. di ver.)\nDLGConfig/Batch/UPLOAD1.BATCH       ;/\nDLGConfig/Text/Banner.displayme     ;| Files necessari per @{"DLG" Link AXuso}\nDLGConfig/Text/PreDesc.txt          ;\\\ndoc/MaPuS.GUIDE                     ;Istruzioni in formato AmigaGuide\nlibs/arp.library                    ;arp.library V39.1\nIRONLAW.txt.Displayme               ;/ Pubblicita'' di\nread.i                              ;\\ @{"IRON LAW BBS" Link Cap10}\n---\n\nIn  caso  avessi  qualche  tua proposta per migliorare il programma (ad es.\nuno  script  per  il  tuo  programma  di BBS) DEVI contattare l''autore, che\nincludera''  (con  i  dovuti ringraziamenti) il tuo lavoro in ogni revisione\ndel programma.\n\nNessuno  e` responsabile in alcun modo degli eventuali (e remoti) danni che\nMaPuS potrebbe arrecare al tuo sistema.\n\nMaPuS e` stato scritto totalmente in @{i}Assembly@{ui}!\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap02 "INTRODUZIONE A MaPuS:"\n\n\nCos''e`  MaPuS?   MaPuS  e`  la soluzione ideale per il trattamento dei file\nDMS.    Puoi   manipolarli   come  piu''  ti  aggrada.   Puoi  controllarli,\naggiungere,  rimuovere e creare @{"front, tail e track banner" Link Cap06}; tutto in un\nmodo alquanto funzionale.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap03 "PERCHE'' USARE MaPuS E NON UN ALTRO CHECKER?"\n\n\nSemplice.   Alcuni  checker  non funzionano perfettamente su tutti i files,\naltri  non  ti  forniscono  le  informazioni in modo completo, e nessuno ti\npermette  di  creare  e aggiungere banner.  MaPuS puo'' essere usato con una\n@{"BBS"  Link AXuso} o nei tuoi file @{"script" Link Cap05} o semplicemente per  @{"testare i file DMS" Link Cap04}.\nMaPuS e` garantito al 100% su queste funzioni.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap04 "COME FUNZIONA:"\n\nSe invochi MaPuS con solo il suo nome ti fornira'' la sintassi:\n\nMaPuS [-<options>] FileName[.DMS] [DestFile]\n\nOpzioni:\n\n@{" Operazioni sui front banner " Link FrontOpt}\n@{" Operazioni sui track banner " Link TrackOpt}\n@{" Operazioni sui tail banner " Link TailOpt}\n            @{" Varie " Link VarieOpt}\n\nSe invochi MaPuS con il solo nome file sorgente, questo sara'' controllato e\nti verranno mostrate alcune informazioni sullo stato.\n\nLa specifica del file sorgente puo'' contenere le wildcards * o ? o #?.\n\n@{b}NOTA: Ad ogni revisione di MaPuS ricordati di ricreare il MaPuS.cfg@{ub}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node FrontOpt "Operazioni sui front banner:"\n\n\n\n\n\n@{" a " Link Opta} aggiunge un front banner.\n@{" r " Link Optr} rimuove i front banner.\n@{" m " Link Optm} crea un front banner.\n\n\n\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node TrackOpt "Operazioni sui track banner:"\n\n\n\n\n@{" t " Link Opta} aggiunge un track banner.\n@{" k " Link Optr} rimuove i track banner.\n@{" n " Link Optm} crea un track banner.\n\n\n\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node TailOpt "Operazioni sui tail banner:"\n\n\n\n\n@{" A " Link Opta} aggiunge un tail banner.\n@{" R " Link Optr} rimuove i tail banner.\n@{" M " Link Optm} crea un tail banner.\n\n\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Opta "Aggiungi banner:"\n\n\nDevi  fornire  il  "FileName"  sorgente  (con o senza l''estenzione .DMS) ed\nopzionalmente un file destinazione "DestFile".\n\nMaPuS  testera''  il  file  ed  aggiungera''  il  banner al file destinazione\n(creando  quindi una copia del file sorgente) o direttamente al sorgente in\ncaso mancasse il destinazione.\n\nQualora  non  fornissi  alcun  nome  di  file  come parametro, apparira'' un\nrequester ARP, che ti permettera'' di sceglierne uno.\n\n@{b}NOTA:@{ub} Se devi creare il file destinazione in RAM: usa l''opzione @{"s" Link VarieOpt}.\n\nIl  "FileName" puo'' essere privo di estensione, ma e` indispensabile che la\nscriva tu per il file destinazione.\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Optr "Rimuovi i banner:"\n\n\nSpecifica   come   parametri   il  nome  del  file  sorgente  e  di  quello\ndestinazione.   MaPuS,  dopo aver testato il file sorgente, creera'' un file\ndestinazione privo dei banner.  Se non hai specificato il file destinazione\ni banner verranno "strippati" direttamente dal file sorgente.\n\nQualora  mancasse  anche  quest''ultimo,  apparira''  un requester ARP che ti\npermettera'' di sceglierlo.\n\n@{b}NOTA:@{ub} Se usi la RAM: specifica l''opzione @{"s" Link VarieOpt}.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Optm "Crea i banner:"\n\n\nSpecifica  il  nome  del  file  di  testo  da  usare come banner o se no ti\napparira''  un  requester  che  ti permettera'' di sceglierlo.  MaPuS creera''\nnella  S:   un  file  chiamato  "MaPuS.cfg", che ti permettera'' di usare le\nopzioni di adding.\n\nIl formato del file testo e`:  64 colonne (return compreso) per 16 linee.\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node VarieOpt "Opzioni varie:"\n\n@{b} s @{ub}  -  Non  controllare  lo  spazio disponibile.  Indispensabile se\n        lavori nella RAM:  che e` sempre piena al 100%.\n\n@{b} v @{ub}  -  Visualizza delle informazioni sul file DMS, ma non testarlo.\n\n@{b} d @{ub}  -  Metti la data di upload nel track banner da aggiungere.\n\n@{b} g @{ub}  -  Visualizza alcuni ringraziamenti.\n\n@{b} u @{ub}  -  Per scegliere, in ogni caso, il file DMS da un requester ARP.\n\n@{b} f @{ub}  -  Visualizza dettagliate informazioni su ogni traccia del file\n        DMS.\n\n@{b} c @{ub}  -  Restituisce un codice di ritorno di 15 in caso di fallito\n        checking.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap05 "ESEMPI:"\n\n\n1) Controlla un file:\n In questo esempio immaginiamo di avere un file nella tua directory DL:\nchiamato TEST.DMS e che tu voglia controllarlo.\n\nMaPuS dl:TEST.dms o MaPuS dl:TEST\n\nsara''  controllato  e  ti verranno mostrate alcune informazioni sullo stato\ndello stesso.\n\n2) Crea un @{"tail banner" Link TailOpt}:\n\nMaPuS -M \n\n3) Aggiungi un @{"front banner" Link FrontOpt} e rimuovi i @{"tail" Link TailOpt} e @{"track banner" Link TrackOpt}:\n\nMaPuS -AskR dl:TEST[.dms] ram:newTEST.dms\n\n(Nota l''opzione @{"s" Link VarieOpt} per la ram:)\n\n4) Testa tutti i file di una directory:\n\nMaPuS dl:*.dms ovvero MaPuS dl:#?.dms\n\n@endnode\n\n@node AXuso "Uso con /X o DLG:"\n\n\nSe vuoi usare MaPuS con AmiExpress usa lo script incluso: @{b}bbs/fcheck/DMS@{ub}\n\n<----- CONTENUTO DEL FILE: ---------- CUT ------------------------------->\nMaPuS\n\nError\n<------------------------------------ CUT ------------------------------->\n\nNOTA: La seconda linea contiene le opzioni per il MaPuS.\n\n@{b} RICORDA: @{ub} Il file deve contenere esclusivamente queste 3 linee!\n\n  Se  possiedi  una  versione  superiore  alla  3.0  di  AmiExpress  piazza\nsemplicemente  il file incluso nell''archivio - "DMS.info" - nella directory\nBBS:FCheck.\n\nInclusi nell''archivio i file necessari per l''uso di MaPuS con DLG:\n\nDLGConfig/Batch/UPLOAD1.BATCH\nDLGConfig/Text/Banner.displayme\nDLGConfig/Text/PreDesc.txt\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap06 "GLOSSARIO:"\n\n@{"Tail Banner" Link TailOpt}:  e` il testo che sara'' aggiunto in coda al file DMS.\n              (e` l''ultimo che verra'' mostrato nella scompattazione)\n\n@{"Front Banner" Link FrontOpt}: e` il testo che sara'' aggiunto in fronte al file DMS.\n              (e` il primo che verra'' mostrato nella scompattazione)\n\n@{"Track Banner" Link TrackOpt}: e` la traccia zero che sara'' mostrata come se fosse un testo.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap07 "UPDATES DEL MaPuS:"\n\n0.** Versioni sperimentali mai rilasciate.\n\n0.84 Prima versione pubblica. Per mia decisione tutte le versioni pubbliche\n     da ora in poi non implementeranno l''opzione @{"-k" Link TrackOpt}.\n \n0.85 Prima versione registrata, rilasciata a chi ne faceva richiesta\n     chiamando @{"IRON LAW BBS" Link Cap10}.\n \n0.86-0.91 Versioni private\n     Sistemati alcuni bug, fra cui l''opzione @{"-k" Link TrackOpt} che corrompeva l''archivio\n     se vi erano un track banner e subito dopo un front banner.\n\n0.92 Versione pubblica.\n     Implementata l''opzione @{"-f" Link VarieOpt}.  Se specificata mostra informazioni\n     dettagliate su ogni traccia del file DMS.\n\n0.93 Versione registrata.\n \n0.94 Versione mai rilasciata.\n \n0.95 Versione Shareware.\n     Sistemato un bug il quale non faceva funzionare l''opzione @{"-f" Link VarieOpt} se\n     il file era selezionato dal requester.\n \n0.96 Versione Shareware.\n     Su segnalazione di Felix rimosso un bug per il quale MaPuS non poteva\n     essere reso residente. Sistemate alcune piccolezze.\n\n0.97 Versione registrata.\n\n0.98-0.99 Versioni private.\n\n1.00 Versione Shareware, non completa a causa della MANCANZA totale di\n     registrazioni!\n     Chi desidera la versione completa deve versare la quota di\n     registrazione o contattare @{"IRON LAW BBS" Link Cap10}.\n     Aggiunta delle wildcards (*,?,#?).  Velocizzata la routine di\n     stripping,  in alcuni casi e` piu'' veloce del 200%!!!  Creata la guide\n     che contiene sia le istruzioni in italiano che in inglese, modificata\n     la struttura dell''archivio.\n\n1.01 Versione registrata.\n\n1.02-1.09 Versioni private.\n\n1.10 Versione rilasciata allo SMAU 1993.  Aggiunta la possibilita'' di\n     inserire la data di upload (utile per le BBS) nei track banner\n     (opzione @{"-d" Link VarieOpt}).  Ora l''esecuzione di MaPuS puo'' essere bloccata con\n     CTRL-C (solo dopo il test).\n\n1.11 Versione registrata.\n\n1.12 Sistemata l''opzione @{"-t" Link Trackopt}. Per un bug nella 1.10 quest''opzione\n     non funzionava correttamente su 68000.\n\n1.13 Versione registrata.\n\n1.14 Sistemati due problemi:\n     1) Se il nome del file conteneva il carattere "-", MaPuS\n        non interpretava correttamente la linea di comando.\n     2) A volte l''add di un track banner corrompeva l''archivio.\n\n1.15 Versione registrata.\n\n1.16 Rimossi due bug:\n     1) Qualora durante il check di un file venisse premuto CTRL-C il\n        programma faceva bloccare il sistema.\n     2) Piccolo problema con la command line.\n     Ora le informazioni che da'' MaPuS sono compatibili con il DMS V1.51+.\n     Modifiche alla guide, eliminati i doc in formato ASCII.\n\n1.17 Versione registrata.  (I_I)\n\n1.18-1.29 Versioni Private mai rilasciate.\n          Nota: ho visto girare una versione 1.20. Questa versione non e`\n          mai stata creata da me, percio'' sconsiglio l''utilizzo.\n\n1.30 Sistemati alcuni bug: ora il checking di un file vuoto non produce\n     problemi.\n\n     Aggiunto il supporto delle virgolette: ora il nome del file\n     puo'' contenere spazi, se fra virgolette.\n\n1.31 Versione registrata.\n\n1.32 Implementata l''opzione @{"-c" Link VarieOpt} per far restituire un codice di ritorno di 15\n     in caso di fallito checking (su segnalazione di Jay Ruyle).\n\n1.33 Versione registrata.\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap08 "FUTURI SVILUPPI:"\n\n- MaPuS potra'' prendere da un file la lista dei file su cui operare.\n\n- Utilizzo di un migliore requester, mantenendo la compatibilita'' con il SO\n  1.3.\n\n- View dei banner.\n\n- Script per fallimento o riuscita del test (utile per BBS).\n\n- Aggiunta della data al tail e al front banner.\n\n- Possibilita'' di rendere random la scelta del banner da aggiungere (ottimo\n  per le BBS).\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap09 "RINGRAZIAMENTI:"\n\n\n\nMolte grazie a (in ordine alfabetico):\n\nAlex,  /\\rc, Atomos, Batblaster, Blulight, Caton, Crier, Deus, Doc, Doctor\nRevenge,  DR.Dream/FTH,  DR.G,  Exodus,  Fashion Light, Felix, Gandalf/FTH,\nGhost,  GiapDJ,  Godfather,  Guile, Highlander, Høøk/FTH, Jay Ruyle, Joseph\nHodge  (/X  author), Kenshiro, Kris, Laurent, Leo, LoneWolf, Mad Harlequin,\nMad Lemming, MAUI BBS (2:335/602@fidonet), /\\/\\aster T/4WD, Metalbasher!,\nMF  the  Best,  Modem  Boy,  Mondrian,  MR.IRQ,  MR.Swapper,  /\\/ightmare,\n/\\/ikita/4WD,  Nosferatu, Pier, Pixie, Polaris, Pork, Pows, Randy, Sauzer,\nSeven  /\\/\\, Shady, Splatter, T-Rexx, The Outlaw, Top, Tron/RPK, Warrior,\nWoodelf, tutti i miei utenti, e tutti coloro che dimentico...\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap10 "CONTATTI:"\n\nPuoi contattarci (in Matrix) ai seguenti indirizzi:\n\n2:335/602.15@fidonet\n39:102/1.15@amiganet\[email removed]\nEniac@ITPH06\n\no via posta "classica" a:\n\n                             Antonino Pintaudi\n                                P.O. Box 11\n                         98125 Contesse (Messina)\n                                  ITALIA\n\n\nOPPURE CHIAMA:\n            /\\\n           /  \\\n     ______\\__/___________  _______ _______  ____\n     \\_____/  \\________   \\/       \\\\_     \\|    |\n     .    /    \\|   _|/   /   _/\\   \\|           |<<----------------+\n     :   /      \\   \\_    \\   \\_/    \\           | ++39-(0)90-881378|\n        /        \\   |\\    \\_        /    \\      |                  |\n     :  \\________/   | \\____/_______/|    |\\_____|  SYSOP: Crier    |\n     |          |____|______   ______|____|________                 |\n     |                \\_    |  \\_        \\ \\__    / ______          |\n     | 16800 HST       |    |Mb |  _/|    \\  /   /\\|    _/          |\n     | AmiExpress      |    |___|  \\__     \\/   /  \\    |           |\n     |                 |    /   \\    |\\     \\_          |           |\n     |                 |________/    | \\_____/___/\\     |    24/24h |\n     `--------------------------|____|-------------\\____|-----------''\n\n\nATTENZIONE: NUOVO NUMERO!! ++39-(0)90-881378.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ENG "MaPuS dox:"\n\n                             @{b}GENERAL INDEX:@{ub}\n\n@{" WARNING " Link Cap01E}\n@{" INTRODUCING MaPuS " Link Cap02E}\n@{" WHY SHOULD YOU USE MaPuS AND NOT ANOTHER CHECKER? " Link Cap03E}\n@{" HOW DOES IT WORK " Link Cap04E}\n@{" EXAMPLES " Link Cap05E}\n@{" AMIEXPRESS OR DLG USING OF MaPuS" Link AXusoE}\n@{" GLOSSARY " Link Cap06E}\n@{" MaPuS'' UPDATES " Link Cap07E}\n@{" FUTURE FEATURES " Link Cap08E}\n@{" GREETINGS " Link Cap09E}\n@{" CONTACTS " Link Cap10E}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap01E "PAY ATTENTION:"\n\n\nMaPuS is Shareware, you must register yourself if you use it regularly.\n\nThe registration charge is 15$. You can send it enclosed on the envelope\nor as cheque at the following address:\n\n\n                             Antonino Pintaudi\n                                P.O. Box 11\n                         98125 Contesse (Messina)\n                                  ITALY\n\nThe  original  archive  MaPuS???.LHA  (???  is the version number) can''t be\nmodified.  You can''t add or remove files except BBS advertisements.\n\nThe archive files list is the following:\n\n---\nbbs/fcheck/DMS                       ;@{"AmiExpress" Link AXusoE} config\nbbs/fcheck/DMS.info                  ;@{"AmiExpress v3.+" Link AXusoE} config\nbin/MaPuS.???                        ;Executable program (??? =n. of version)\nDLGConfig/Batch/UPLOAD1.BATCH        ;/\nDLGConfig/Text/Banner.displayme      ;| @{"DLG" Link AXusoE} Config\nDLGConfig/Text/PreDesc.txt           ;\\\ndoc/MaPuS.GUIDE                      ;AmigaGuide ITALIAN & ENGLISH dox.\nlibs/arp.library                     ;arp.library V39.1\nIRONLAW.txt.Displayme                ;/ @{"IRON LAW BBS" Link Cap10E}\nread.i                               ;\\   addings\n---\n\n   If  you  want  to include any your proposition for MaPuS in the archive,\nyou MUST contact the author; he''ll include your work into the next versions\nand he will thank you.\n\nNO-ONE  is  responsable  of  (remote) damages that MaPuS can create to your\nsystem.\n\nMaPuS is written entirely in @{i}Assembly@{ui}!\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap02E "INTRODUCING MaPuS:"\n\n\nWhat  is  MaPuS?  MaPuS is the ultimate solution for DMS files.  You can do\nall  you  want  on  these  files.  You can check them, make, remove and add\ntail, track, front banners; all in a good and functional way.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap03E "WHY SHOULD YOU USE MaPuS AND NOT ANOTHER CHECKER?"\n\n\nSimple.   Some  doesn''t  work perfectly on all files, others don''t give you\nall  informations  about the file, and no-one lets you add your text files.\nMaPuS can be used with a @{"BBS" Link AXusoE} or into your @{"script files"\nLink  Cap05E} or simply to @{"check" Link Cap04E}\nyour DMS files.  MaPuS is 100% tested for these functions.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap04E "HOW DOES IT WORK:"\n\nIf you invoke MaPuS with only his name, you''ll get the syntax:\n\nMaPuS [-<options>] FileName[.DMS] [DestFile]\n\nOptions:\n\n@{" Operations on front banners " Link FrontOptE}\n@{" Operations on track banners " Link TrackOptE}\n@{" Operations on tail banners " Link TailOptE}\n        @{" Other options " Link VarieOptE}\n\n\nIf you invoke MaPuS with the source file name only, the file will be tested\nand are printed on the screen many informations about it.\n\nYou can also specify wildcards in source file name:  *, ?, #?.\n\n@{b}Please update your MaPuS.cfg on every revision of MaPuS.@{ub}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node FrontOptE "Operations on front banners:"\n\n\n\n\n\n@{" a " Link OptaE} add a front banner.\n@{" r " Link OptrE} remove front banners.\n@{" m " Link OptmE} make a front banner.\n\n\n\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node TrackOptE "Operations on track banners:"\n\n\n\n\n@{" t " Link OptaE} add a track banner.\n@{" k " Link OptrE} remove track banners.\n@{" n " Link OptmE} make a track banner.\n\n\n\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node TailOptE "Operations on tail banners:"\n\n\n\n\n@{" A " Link OptaE} add a tail banner.\n@{" R " Link OptrE} remove tail banners.\n@{" M " Link OptmE} make a tail banner.\n\n\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node OptaE "Add a banner:"\n\n\nSpecify  source  "FileName"  (with  or  without .DMS extention) and, if you\nwant, a destination file "DestFile".\n\nMaPuS  will  test  that  file  and  add  the  banner to the destination one\n(making,  so,  a  copy  of  the  source  file) or if the destination is not\nspecified to the source file directly.\n\nIf the source file name were absent, an ARP requester would appear.\n\n@{b}NOTE:@{ub} If you want to create the destination file in RAM: use the @{"s" Link VarieOptE} option.\n\n"FileName"  can  be  without  extention,  but  you MUST write the extention\nyourself in the destination file name.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node OptrE "Remove banners:"\n\nPass  source FileName and/or DestFile name and MaPuS will search and remove\nfront  banners and report to you operation results.  If no destination file\nwere specified, the banners would be stripped to the source file directly.\n\nIf you don''t specify FileName, an ARP requester will appear.\n\n@{b}NOTE:@{ub} If you use the RAM: specify the @{"s" Link VarieOpt} option.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node OptmE "Create banners:"\n\n\nPass  the  text  file  name  or a requester will appear and it will let you\nselect  a  filename  as  banner.   MaPuS  will  place in S:  a file, called\n"MaPuS.cfg".  Now you can add it to your DMS files.\n\nText file format is:  64 colums (with linefeed) for 16 lines.\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node VarieOptE "Other options:"\n\n@{b} s @{ub}  -  Don''t check free space. You should use it if you work with RAM:\n\n@{b} v @{ub}  -  View DMS file informations only, and don''t check it.\n\n@{b} d @{ub}  -  Add to track banners the uploading date.\n\n@{b} g @{ub}  -  Show some greetings.\n\n@{b} u @{ub}  -  Use an ARP requester to select the DMS file.\n\n@{b} f @{ub}  -  Show informations about every track of the DMS file.\n\n@{b} c @{ub}  -  Activate return codes. If the checking fails a return code of\n        15 will be returned.\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap05E "EXAMPLES:"\n\n1) Check a file:\n In this example I will suppose that you''ve a file in your DL: directory\ncalled TEST.DMS and you want to test it.\n\nType: MaPuS DL:TEST or MaPuS dl:TEST.dms\n\nit will be tested and you''ll get some infos about the file.\n\n2) Make a @{"tail banner" Link TailOptE}:\n\nType: MaPuS -M\n\n3) Add a @{"front banner" Link FrontOptE} and remove @{"tail" Link TailOptE} and @{"track banners" Link TrackOptE}:\n\nType: MaPuS -AskR dl:TEST.dms ram:newTEST.dms\n\n(Note @{"s" Link VarieOptE} option for RAM:)\n\n4) Test all files of a directory:\n\nMaPuS dl:*.dms or MaPuS dl:#?.dms\n\n@endnode\n\nCiao...\n\n@node AXusoE "/X or DLG using:"\n\n\nIf you want to use MaPuS with AmiExpress have a look at: @{b}bbs/fcheck/DMS@{ub}\n\n<----- THERE''s THE CONTENTS OF THE FILE ---------- CUT HERE ------------->\nMaPuS\n\nError\n<------------------------------------------------- CUT HERE ------------->\n\nNOTE: the 2nd line contains the options for MaPuS.\n\n@{b} REMEMBER: @{ub} The file must contains these 3 lines only!\n\nIf you''ve AmiExpress v3+ place file "DMS.info" into BBS:FCheck directory.\n\nThe  scripts  to  use  MaPuS with DLG are included in the archive, and they\nare:\n\nDLGConfig/Batch/UPLOAD1.BATCH\nDLGConfig/Text/Banner.displayme\nDLGConfig/Text/PreDesc.txt\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap06E "GLOSSARY:"\n\n@{"Tail Banner" Link TailOptE}: it''s a text file that will be appended to the end of file.\n             (it''s the last text that will be displayed unpacking)\n\n@{"Front Banner" Link FrontOptE}: it''s a text file that will be appended to the front of file.\n              (it''s the first text that will be displayed unpacking)\n\n@{"Track Banner" Link TrackOptE}: it''s the zero-track that will displayed as text file.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap07E "MaPuS UPDATES:"\n\n0.** Sperimental versions never released.\n\n0.84 First public version.  For our decision, public versions don''t\n     implement @{"-k" Link TrackOptE} command.\n\n0.85 First registered version, got if you''ve called @{"IRON LAW BBS" Link Cap10E}.\n\n0.86-0.91 Private versions.\n     Fixed some bugs: Before @{"-k" Link TrackOptE} command corrupted archives if there were\n     track and front banner.\n\n0.92 Public version.\n     New  option @{"-f" Link VarieOptE}.  If you specify it, MaPuS will show you informations\n     about every track.\n\n0.93 Registered version.\n\n0.94 Sperimental version never released.\n\n0.95 Shareware version.\n     Fixed a bug in @{"-f" Link VarieOptE} option (the infos were not displayed if the file\n     had been selected from requester).\n\n0.96 Shareware version.\n     Fixed a bug. Now MaPuS can be resident. Thanks to Felix for bug\n     reporting.\n\n0.97 Registered version.\n\n0.98-0.99 Private versions.\n\n1.00 Shareware version, not 100% beacause no one has registered his copy of\n     MaPuS! If you want the complete version you must pay the registration\n     fee or call @{"IRON LAW BBS" Link Cap10E}.\n     Wildcards added (*,?,#?).  Speeded up stripping routine.\n     Docs  are  now  also  in Amiga-Guide format, that contains english and\n     italian ones. Archive structure modified.\n\n1.01 Registered version.\n\n1.02-1.09 Private versions.\n\n1.10 Special version released at SMAU 1993.  Added the uploading date\n     (useful for BBS) on track banners (use @{"-d" Link VarieOptE} option).  Now you can stop\n     MaPuS with CTRL-C (after the test).\n\n1.11 Registered version.\n\n1.12 Fixed a problem in @{"-t" Link TrackoptE} option. A bug made 1.10 not working on 68000\n     systems.\n\n1.13 Registered version.\n\n1.14 Fixed two problems:\n     1) If the filename started with a minus character the command line\n        parsing didn''t worked.\n     2) Sometimes the track banners adding did corrupt the archive.\n\n1.15 Registered version.\n\n1.16 Fixed two bugs:\n     1) If CTRL-C was pressed during a file check, the program crashed the\n        system.\n     2) Small command line bug.\n     Now MaPuS informations are compatible with DMS V1.51+.\n     Guide corrected, ASCII docs deleted.\n\n1.17 Registered version.\n\n1.18-1.29 Private, not released, versions.\n         Note: I saw a "1.20" version. This version hasn''t been created by us,\n         you shouldn''t use it..\n\n1.30 Fixed some bugs: now an empty file checking doesn''t do problems.\n\n     Now supporting "": file name can contain spaces, if between "".\n\n1.31 Registered version.\n\n1.32 Added return codes with @{"-c" Link VarieOptE} option. It  returns a code of 15 if the\n     checking fails. Signaled by Jay Ruyle.\n\n1.33 Registered version.\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap08E "FUTURE FEATURES:"\n\n\n- MaPuS will take the file list to operate over from a text file.\n\n- Use of a better requester.\n\n- Banner display.\n\n- Scripts for failed or successful tests (useful for BBSes).\n\n- Date adding on tail and front banners.\n\n- MaPuS will select a random banner to add.\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap09E "GREETINGS:"\n\nMany thanks go to (alphabetic order):\n\nAlex,  /\\rc, Atomos, Batblaster, Blulight, Caton, Crier, Deus, Doc, Doctor\nRevenge,  DR.Dream/FTH,  DR.G,  Exodus,  Fashion Light, Felix, Gandalf/FTH,\nGhost,  GiapDJ,  Godfather,  Guile, Highlander, Høøk/FTH, Jay Ruyle, Joseph\nHodge  (/X  author), Kenshiro, Kris, Laurent, Leo, LoneWolf, Mad Harlequin,\nMad Lemming, MAUI BBS (2:335/602@fidonet), /\\/\\aster T/4WD, Metalbasher!,\nMF  the  Best,  Modem  Boy,  Mondrian,  MR.IRQ,  MR.Swapper,  /\\/ightmare,\n/\\/ikita/4WD,  Nosferatu, Pier, Pixie, Polaris, Pork, Pows, Randy, Sauzer,\nSeven  /\\/\\, Shady, Splatter, T-Rexx, The Outlaw, Top, Tron/RPK, Warrior,\nWoodelf, all my users, all friends and all the ones I forget...\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap10E "CONTACTS:"\n\n\nYou can contact us (via NetMail) at these addresses:\n\n2:335/602.15@fidonet\n39:102/1.15@amiganet\[email removed]\nEniac@ITPH06\n\nor via "old" mail at:\n\n                             Antonino Pintaudi\n                                P.O. Box 11\n                         98125 Contesse (Messina)\n                                  ITALIA\n\nOR CALL:\n            /\\\n           /  \\\n     ______\\__/___________  _______ _______  ____\n     \\_____/  \\________   \\/       \\\\_     \\|    |\n     .    /    \\|   _|/   /   _/\\   \\|           |<<----------------+\n     :   /      \\   \\_    \\   \\_/    \\           | ++39-(0)90-881378|\n        /        \\   |\\    \\_        /    \\      |                  |\n     :  \\________/   | \\____/_______/|    |\\_____|  SYSOP: Crier    |\n     |          |____|______   ______|____|________                 |\n     |                \\_    |  \\_        \\ \\__    / ______          |\n     | 16800 HST       |    |Mb |  _/|    \\  /   /\\|    _/          |\n     | AmiExpress      |    |___|  \\__     \\/   /  \\    |           |\n     |                 |    /   \\    |\\     \\_          |           |\n     |                 |________/    | \\_____/___/\\     |    24/24h |\n     `--------------------------|____|-------------\\____|-----------''\n\n\nWARNING: NEW NUMBER: ++39-(0)90-881378\n\n@endnode\n\nWhere you''re looking in????\nFINE!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',35870,2,0,NULL,NULL,'mapus133','scan',1780048589);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mapus134','MAPUS134.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MAPUS134.LHA',NULL,'XIM','MaPuS.134',NULL,'Eniac',NULL,'|  _____/\  __________  ___  /\____        | |  \____  \/  _¬\___ ¬\/ |¬\/  ___/--------| |   |  ..  \     \  __/  |  \___ ¬\  v1.34 |',replace('.------------------------------------------.\n|  _____/\  __________  ___  /\____        |\n|  \____  \/  _¬\___ ¬\/ |¬\/  ___/--------|\n|   |  ..  \     \  __/  |  \___ ¬\  v1.34 |\n|   |__||__/__|__/__| \_____/_____/--------|\n| <------( DMS checker By Eniac )--------> |\n''--------------------------------------mk--''\n','\n',char(10)),'MaPuS.guide',replace('@database MaPuSDoc\n\nCopyright (c) 1993-94-95 by Caton\nAll Rights Reserved\n\n@Remark $VER: MaPuS Dox AmigaGuide format 1.6 (4.10.95) by Caton\n\n@node MAIN "MaPuS"\n\nSelect language please:\n\n                    @{" ITALIANO " Link ITA}      -      @{" ENGLISH " Link ENG}\n\n\n               .------------------------------------------.\n               |  _____/\  __________  ___  /\____        |\n               |  \____  \/  _¬\___ ¬\/ |¬\/  ___/--------|\n               |   |  ..  \     \  __/  |  \___ ¬\        |\n               |   |__||__/__|__/__| \_____/_____/--------|\n               | <------( DMS checker By Eniac )--------> |\n               `--------------------------------------mk--''\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ITA "Istruzioni di ''MaPuS''."\n\n                             @{b}INDICE GENERALE:@{ub}\n\n@{" ATTENZIONE " Link Cap01}\n@{" INTRODUZIONE A MaPuS " Link Cap02}\n@{" PERCHE'' USARE MaPuS E NON UN ALTRO CHECKER? " Link Cap03}\n@{" COME FUNZIONA " Link Cap04}\n@{" ESEMPI " Link Cap05}\n@{" USO DI MaPuS CON AMIEXPRESS o DLG " Link AXuso}\n@{" GLOSSARIO " Link Cap06}\n@{" UPDATES DEL MaPuS " Link Cap07}\n@{" FUTURI SVILUPPI " Link Cap08}\n@{" RINGRAZIAMENTI " Link Cap09}\n@{" COME CONTATTARCI " Link Cap10}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap01 "ATTENZIONE:"\n\n\nE''  stato  deciso  di  immettere  questo  programma  nel  Pubblico Dominio,\nimponendo l''opzione dello Shareware qualora venisse usato regolarmente.\n\nQuindi se lo hai installato nella tua BBS o lo utilizzi di routine, faresti\nbene a registrarti per premiare il lavoro di chi lo sviluppa.\n\nLa  cifra  di  registrazione  (simbolica) e` di 15$ o 15000 Lire da spedire\ninclusa  nella  busta  o  come cheque o come vaglia postale al seguente\nindirizzo:\n\n                             Antonino Pintaudi\n                                P.O. Box 11\n                         98125 Contesse (Messina)\n                                  ITALIA\n\nL''archivio originale MaPuS???.LHA (in cui ???  e` il numero della versione)\nnon puo'' essere modificato.  Non possono essere aggiunti o tolti file salvo\nle normali "pubblicita''" delle BBS.\n\nLa lista dei file che contiene l''archivio originale e` la seguente:\n\n---\nbbs/fcheck/DMS                      ;Configurazione per @{"AmiExpress" Link AXuso}\nbbs/fcheck/DMS.Info                 ;Configurazione per @{"AmiExpress v3.+" Link AXuso}\nbin/MaPuS.???                       ;Eseguibile (??? sta per n. di ver.)\nbin/MAPUS_NOTE.TXT                  ;Informazioni su questa versione\nDLGConfig/Batch/UPLOAD1.BATCH       ;/\nDLGConfig/Text/Banner.displayme     ;| Files necessari per @{"DLG" Link AXuso}\nDLGConfig/Text/PreDesc.txt          ;\\ndoc/MaPuS.GUIDE                     ;Istruzioni in formato AmigaGuide\nlibs/arp.library                    ;arp.library V39.1\nMAPUS.LHA                           ;Copia di BackUp di questo archivio\n---\n\nIn  caso  avessi  qualche  tua proposta per migliorare il programma (ad es.\nuno  script  per  il  tuo  programma  di BBS) DEVI contattare l''autore, che\nincludera''  (con  i  dovuti ringraziamenti) il tuo lavoro in ogni revisione\ndel programma.\n\nNessuno  e` responsabile in alcun modo degli eventuali (e remoti) danni che\nMaPuS potrebbe arrecare al tuo sistema.\n\nMaPuS e` stato scritto totalmente in @{i}Assembly@{ui}!\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap02 "INTRODUZIONE A MaPuS:"\n\n\nCos''e`  MaPuS?   MaPuS  e`  la soluzione ideale per il trattamento dei file\nDMS.    Puoi   manipolarli   come  piu''  ti  aggrada.   Puoi  controllarli,\naggiungere,  rimuovere e creare @{"front, tail e track banner" Link Cap06}; tutto in un\nmodo alquanto funzionale.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap03 "PERCHE'' USARE MaPuS E NON UN ALTRO CHECKER?"\n\n\nSemplice.   Alcuni  checker  non funzionano perfettamente su tutti i files,\naltri  non  ti  forniscono  le  informazioni in modo completo, e nessuno ti\npermette  di  creare  e aggiungere banner.  MaPuS puo'' essere usato con una\n@{"BBS"  Link AXuso} o nei tuoi file @{"script" Link Cap05} o semplicemente per  @{"testare i file DMS" Link Cap04}.\nMaPuS e` garantito al 100% su queste funzioni.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap04 "COME FUNZIONA:"\n\nSe invochi MaPuS con solo il suo nome ti fornira'' la sintassi:\n\nMaPuS [-<options>] FileName[.DMS] [DestFile]\n\nOpzioni:\n\n@{" Operazioni sui front banner " Link FrontOpt}\n@{" Operazioni sui track banner " Link TrackOpt}\n@{" Operazioni sui tail banner " Link TailOpt}\n            @{" Varie " Link VarieOpt}\n\nSe invochi MaPuS con il solo nome file sorgente, questo sara'' controllato e\nti verranno mostrate alcune informazioni sullo stato.\n\nLa specifica del file sorgente puo'' contenere le wildcards * o ? o #?.\n\n@{b}NOTA: Ad ogni revisione di MaPuS ricordati di ricreare il MaPuS.cfg@{ub}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node FrontOpt "Operazioni sui front banner:"\n\n\n\n\n\n@{" a " Link Opta} aggiunge un front banner.\n@{" r " Link Optr} rimuove i front banner.\n@{" m " Link Optm} crea un front banner.\n\n\n\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node TrackOpt "Operazioni sui track banner:"\n\n\n\n\n@{" t " Link Opta} aggiunge un track banner.\n@{" k " Link Optr} rimuove i track banner.\n@{" n " Link Optm} crea un track banner.\n\n\n\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node TailOpt "Operazioni sui tail banner:"\n\n\n\n\n@{" A " Link Opta} aggiunge un tail banner.\n@{" R " Link Optr} rimuove i tail banner.\n@{" M " Link Optm} crea un tail banner.\n\n\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Opta "Aggiungi banner:"\n\n\nDevi  fornire  il  "FileName"  sorgente  (con o senza l''estenzione .DMS) ed\nopzionalmente un file destinazione "DestFile".\n\nMaPuS  testera''  il  file  ed  aggiungera''  il  banner al file destinazione\n(creando  quindi una copia del file sorgente) o direttamente al sorgente in\ncaso mancasse il destinazione.\n\nQualora  non  fornissi  alcun  nome  di  file  come parametro, apparira'' un\nrequester ARP, che ti permettera'' di sceglierne uno.\n\n@{b}NOTA:@{ub} Se devi creare il file destinazione in RAM: usa l''opzione @{"s" Link VarieOpt}.\n\nIl  "FileName" puo'' essere privo di estensione, ma e` indispensabile che la\nscriva tu per il file destinazione.\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Optr "Rimuovi i banner:"\n\n\nSpecifica   come   parametri   il  nome  del  file  sorgente  e  di  quello\ndestinazione.   MaPuS,  dopo aver testato il file sorgente, creera'' un file\ndestinazione privo dei banner.  Se non hai specificato il file destinazione\ni banner verranno "strippati" direttamente dal file sorgente.\n\nQualora  mancasse  anche  quest''ultimo,  apparira''  un requester ARP che ti\npermettera'' di sceglierlo.\n\n@{b}NOTA:@{ub} Se usi la RAM: specifica l''opzione @{"s" Link VarieOpt}.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Optm "Crea i banner:"\n\n\nSpecifica  il  nome  del  file  di  testo  da  usare come banner o se no ti\napparira''  un  requester  che  ti permettera'' di sceglierlo.  MaPuS creera''\nnella  S:   un  file  chiamato  "MaPuS.cfg", che ti permettera'' di usare le\nopzioni di adding.\n\nIl formato del file testo e`:  64 colonne (return compreso) per 16 linee.\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node VarieOpt "Opzioni varie:"\n\n@{b} s @{ub}  -  Non  controllare  lo  spazio disponibile.  Indispensabile se\n        lavori nella RAM:  che e` sempre piena al 100%.\n\n@{b} v @{ub}  -  Visualizza delle informazioni sul file DMS, ma non testarlo.\n\n@{b} d @{ub}  -  Metti la data di upload nel track banner da aggiungere.\n\n@{b} g @{ub}  -  Visualizza alcuni ringraziamenti.\n\n@{b} u @{ub}  -  Per scegliere, in ogni caso, il file DMS da un requester ARP.\n\n@{b} f @{ub}  -  Visualizza dettagliate informazioni su ogni traccia del file\n        DMS.\n\n@{b} c @{ub}  -  Restituisce un codice di ritorno di 15 in caso di fallito\n        checking.\n\n@{b} i @{ub}  -  Esclude alcuni reports.\n\n@{b} I @{ub}  -  Esclude altri reports.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap05 "ESEMPI:"\n\n\n1) Controlla un file:\n In questo esempio immaginiamo di avere un file nella tua directory DL:\nchiamato TEST.DMS e che tu voglia controllarlo.\n\nMaPuS dl:TEST.dms o MaPuS dl:TEST\n\nsara''  controllato  e  ti verranno mostrate alcune informazioni sullo stato\ndello stesso.\n\n2) Crea un @{"tail banner" Link TailOpt}:\n\nMaPuS -M \n\n3) Aggiungi un @{"front banner" Link FrontOpt} e rimuovi i @{"tail" Link TailOpt} e @{"track banner" Link TrackOpt}:\n\nMaPuS -AskR dl:TEST[.dms] ram:newTEST.dms\n\n(Nota l''opzione @{"s" Link VarieOpt} per la ram:)\n\n4) Testa tutti i file di una directory:\n\nMaPuS dl:*.dms ovvero MaPuS dl:#?.dms\n\n@endnode\n\n@node AXuso "Uso con /X o DLG:"\n\n\nSe vuoi usare MaPuS con AmiExpress usa lo script incluso: @{b}bbs/fcheck/DMS@{ub}\n\n<----- CONTENUTO DEL FILE: ---------- CUT ------------------------------->\nMaPuS\n\nError\n<------------------------------------ CUT ------------------------------->\n\nNOTA: La seconda linea contiene le opzioni per il MaPuS.\n\n@{b} RICORDA: @{ub} Il file deve contenere esclusivamente queste 3 linee!\n\n  Se  possiedi  una  versione  superiore  alla  3.0  di  AmiExpress  piazza\nsemplicemente  il file incluso nell''archivio - "DMS.info" - nella directory\nBBS:FCheck.\n\nInclusi nell''archivio i file necessari per l''uso di MaPuS con DLG:\n\nDLGConfig/Batch/UPLOAD1.BATCH\nDLGConfig/Text/Banner.displayme\nDLGConfig/Text/PreDesc.txt\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap06 "GLOSSARIO:"\n\n@{"Tail Banner" Link TailOpt}:  e` il testo che sara'' aggiunto in coda al file DMS.\n              (e` l''ultimo che verra'' mostrato nella scompattazione)\n\n@{"Front Banner" Link FrontOpt}: e` il testo che sara'' aggiunto in fronte al file DMS.\n              (e` il primo che verra'' mostrato nella scompattazione)\n\n@{"Track Banner" Link TrackOpt}: e` la traccia zero che sara'' mostrata come se fosse un testo.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap07 "UPDATES DEL MaPuS:"\n\n0.** Versioni sperimentali mai rilasciate.\n\n0.84 Prima versione pubblica. Per mia decisione tutte le versioni pubbliche\n     da ora in poi non implementeranno l''opzione @{"-k" Link TrackOpt}.\n \n0.85 Prima versione registrata, rilasciata a chi ne faceva richiesta\n     chiamando @{"DELTA CITY BBS" Link Cap10}.\n \n0.86-0.91 Versioni private\n     Sistemati alcuni bug, fra cui l''opzione @{"-k" Link TrackOpt} che corrompeva l''archivio\n     se vi erano un track banner e subito dopo un front banner.\n\n0.92 Versione pubblica.\n     Implementata l''opzione @{"-f" Link VarieOpt}.  Se specificata mostra informazioni\n     dettagliate su ogni traccia del file DMS.\n\n0.93 Versione registrata.\n \n0.94 Versione mai rilasciata.\n \n0.95 Versione Shareware.\n     Sistemato un bug il quale non faceva funzionare l''opzione @{"-f" Link VarieOpt} se\n     il file era selezionato dal requester.\n \n0.96 Versione Shareware.\n     Su segnalazione di Felix rimosso un bug per il quale MaPuS non poteva\n     essere reso residente. Sistemate alcune piccolezze.\n\n0.97 Versione registrata.\n\n0.98-0.99 Versioni private.\n\n1.00 Versione Shareware, non completa a causa della MANCANZA totale di\n     registrazioni!\n     Chi desidera la versione completa deve versare la quota di\n     registrazione o contattare @{"DELTA CITY BBS" Link Cap10}.\n     Aggiunta delle wildcards (*,?,#?).  Velocizzata la routine di\n     stripping,  in alcuni casi e` piu'' veloce del 200%!!!  Creata la guide\n     che contiene sia le istruzioni in italiano che in inglese, modificata\n     la struttura dell''archivio.\n\n1.01 Versione registrata.\n\n1.02-1.09 Versioni private.\n\n1.10 Versione rilasciata allo SMAU 1993.  Aggiunta la possibilita'' di\n     inserire la data di upload (utile per le BBS) nei track banner\n     (opzione @{"-d" Link VarieOpt}).  Ora l''esecuzione di MaPuS puo'' essere bloccata con\n     CTRL-C (solo dopo il test).\n\n1.11 Versione registrata.\n\n1.12 Sistemata l''opzione @{"-t" Link Trackopt}. Per un bug nella 1.10 quest''opzione\n     non funzionava correttamente su 68000.\n\n1.13 Versione registrata.\n\n1.14 Sistemati due problemi:\n     1) Se il nome del file conteneva il carattere "-", MaPuS\n        non interpretava correttamente la linea di comando.\n     2) A volte l''add di un track banner corrompeva l''archivio.\n\n1.15 Versione registrata.\n\n1.16 Rimossi due bug:\n     1) Qualora durante il check di un file venisse premuto CTRL-C il\n        programma faceva bloccare il sistema.\n     2) Piccolo problema con la command line.\n     Ora le informazioni che da'' MaPuS sono compatibili con il DMS V1.51+.\n     Modifiche alla guide, eliminati i doc in formato ASCII.\n\n1.17 Versione registrata.  (I_I)\n\n1.18-1.29 Versioni Private mai rilasciate.\n          Nota: ho visto girare una versione 1.20. Questa versione non e`\n          mai stata creata da me, percio'' sconsiglio l''utilizzo.\n\n1.30 Sistemati alcuni bug: ora il checking di un file vuoto non produce\n     problemi.\n\n     Aggiunto il supporto delle virgolette: ora il nome del file\n     puo'' contenere spazi, se fra virgolette.\n\n1.31 Versione registrata.\n\n1.32 Implementata l''opzione @{"-c" Link VarieOpt} per far restituire un codice di ritorno di 15\n     in caso di fallito checking (su segnalazione di Jay Ruyle).\n\n1.33 Versione registrata.\n\n1.34 Correzione di qualche bug. Nuove opzioni @{"-i e -I" Link VarieOpt}.\n\n1.35 Versione registrata.\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap08 "FUTURI SVILUPPI:"\n\n- MaPuS potra'' prendere da un file la lista dei file su cui operare.\n\n- Utilizzo di un migliore requester, mantenendo la compatibilita'' con il SO\n  1.3.\n\n- View dei banner.\n\n- Script per fallimento o riuscita del test (utile per BBS).\n\n- Aggiunta della data al tail e al front banner.\n\n- Possibilita'' di rendere random la scelta del banner da aggiungere (ottimo\n  per le BBS).\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap09 "RINGRAZIAMENTI:"\n\n\n\nMolte grazie a (in ordine alfabetico):\n\nAlex,  /\rc,  Atomos, Batblaster, Blulight, Caton, Crier, Deus, Doc, Doctor\nRevenge,  DR.Dream/FTH,  DR.G,  Exodus,  Fashion Light, Felix, Gandalf/FTH,\nGhost,  GiapDJ,  Godfather,  Guile, Highlander, Høøk/FTH, Jay Ruyle, Joseph\nHodge  (/X  author), Kenshiro, Kris, Laurent, Leo, LoneWolf, Mad Harlequin,\nMad  Lemming,  MAUI BBS (2:335/602@fidonet), /\/\aster T/4WD, Metalbasher!,\nMF   the  Best,  Modem  Boy,  Mondrian,  MR.IRQ,  MR.Swapper,  /\/ightmare,\n/\/ikita/4WD,  Nosferatu,  Pier, Pixie, Polaris, Pork, Pows, Randy, Sauzer,\nSeven  /\/\,  Shady,  Splatter, T-Rexx, The Outlaw, Top, Tron/RPK, Warrior,\nWoodelf, tutti i miei utenti, e tutti coloro che dimentico...\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap10 "CONTATTI:"\n\nPuoi contattarci (in Matrix) ai seguenti indirizzi:\n\n2:335/[email removed]\n\no via posta "classica" a:\n\n                             Antonino Pintaudi\n                                P.O. Box 11\n                         98125 Contesse (Messina)\n                                  ITALIA\n\n\noppure chiamando la *NUOVA* BBS di supporto:\n\n                              Delta City BBS\n                            +39-(0)931-760203\n                   [ Lasciare un messaggio ad "Eniac" ]\n@endnode\n\n@node ENG "MaPuS dox:"\n\n                             @{b}GENERAL INDEX:@{ub}\n\n@{" WARNING " Link Cap01E}\n@{" INTRODUCING MaPuS " Link Cap02E}\n@{" WHY SHOULD YOU USE MaPuS AND NOT ANOTHER CHECKER? " Link Cap03E}\n@{" HOW IT WORKS " Link Cap04E}\n@{" EXAMPLES " Link Cap05E}\n@{" USING OF MaPuS WITH AMIEXPRESS OR DLG " Link AXusoE}\n@{" GLOSSARY " Link Cap06E}\n@{" MaPuS UPDATES " Link Cap07E}\n@{" FUTURE FEATURES " Link Cap08E}\n@{" GREETINGS " Link Cap09E}\n@{" CONTACTS " Link Cap10E}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap01E "PAY ATTENTION:"\n\n\nMaPuS is Shareware, you must register yourself if you use it regularly.\n\nThe registration charge is 15$. You can send it enclosed on the envelope\nor as cheque at the following address:\n\n\n                             Antonino Pintaudi\n                                P.O. Box 11\n                         98125 Contesse (Messina)\n                                  ITALY\n\nThe  original  archive  MaPuS???.LHA  (???  is the version number) can''t be\nmodified.  You can''t add or remove files except BBS advertisements.\n\nThe archive files list is the following:\n\n---\nbbs/fcheck/DMS                       ;@{"AmiExpress" Link AXusoE} config\nbbs/fcheck/DMS.info                  ;@{"AmiExpress v3.+" Link AXusoE} config\nbin/MaPuS.???                        ;Executable program (??? =n. of version)\nbin/MAPUS_NOTE.TXT                   ;Info about this version\nDLGConfig/Batch/UPLOAD1.BATCH        ;/\nDLGConfig/Text/Banner.displayme      ;| @{"DLG" Link AXusoE} Config\nDLGConfig/Text/PreDesc.txt           ;\\ndoc/MaPuS.GUIDE                      ;AmigaGuide ITALIAN & ENGLISH dox.\nlibs/arp.library                     ;arp.library V39.1\nMAPUS.LHA                            ;BackUp copy of this archive\n---\n\n   If  you  want  to include any your proposition for MaPuS in the archive,\nyou MUST contact the author; he''ll include your work into the next versions\nand he will thank you.\n\nNO-ONE  is  responsable  of  (remote) damages that MaPuS can create to your\nsystem.\n\nMaPuS is written entirely in @{i}Assembly@{ui}!\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap02E "INTRODUCING MaPuS:"\n\n\nWhat  is  MaPuS?  MaPuS is the ultimate solution for DMS files.  You can do\nall  you  want  on  these  files.  You can check them, make, remove and add\ntail, track, front banners; all in a good and functional way.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap03E "WHY SHOULD YOU USE MaPuS AND NOT ANOTHER CHECKER?"\n\n\nSimple.   Some  doesn''t  work perfectly on all files, others don''t give you\nall  informations  about the file, and no-one lets you add your text files.\nMaPuS can be used with a @{"BBS" Link AXusoE} or into your @{"script files"\nLink  Cap05E} or simply to @{"check" Link Cap04E}\nyour DMS files.  MaPuS is 100% tested for these functions.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap04E "HOW DOES IT WORK:"\n\nIf you invoke MaPuS with only his name, you''ll get the syntax:\n\nMaPuS [-<options>] FileName[.DMS] [DestFile]\n\nOptions:\n\n@{" Operations on front banners " Link FrontOptE}\n@{" Operations on track banners " Link TrackOptE}\n@{" Operations on tail banners " Link TailOptE}\n        @{" Other options " Link VarieOptE}\n\n\nIf you invoke MaPuS with the source file name only, the file will be tested\nand are printed on the screen many informations about it.\n\nYou can also specify wildcards in source file name:  *, ?, #?.\n\n@{b}Please update your MaPuS.cfg on every revision of MaPuS.@{ub}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node FrontOptE "Operations on front banners:"\n\n\n\n\n\n@{" a " Link OptaE} add a front banner.\n@{" r " Link OptrE} remove front banners.\n@{" m " Link OptmE} make a front banner.\n\n\n\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node TrackOptE "Operations on track banners:"\n\n\n\n\n@{" t " Link OptaE} add a track banner.\n@{" k " Link OptrE} remove track banners.\n@{" n " Link OptmE} make a track banner.\n\n\n\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node TailOptE "Operations on tail banners:"\n\n\n\n\n@{" A " Link OptaE} add a tail banner.\n@{" R " Link OptrE} remove tail banners.\n@{" M " Link OptmE} make a tail banner.\n\n\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node OptaE "Add a banner:"\n\n\nSpecify  source  "FileName"  (with  or  without .DMS extention) and, if you\nwant, a destination file "DestFile".\n\nMaPuS  will  test  that  file  and  add  the  banner to the destination one\n(making,  so,  a  copy  of  the  source  file) or if the destination is not\nspecified to the source file directly.\n\nIf the source file name were absent, an ARP requester would appear.\n\n@{b}NOTE:@{ub} If you want to create the destination file in RAM: use the @{"s" Link VarieOptE} option.\n\n"FileName"  can  be  without  extention,  but  you MUST write the extention\nyourself in the destination file name.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node OptrE "Remove banners:"\n\nPass  source FileName and/or DestFile name and MaPuS will search and remove\nfront  banners and report to you operation results.  If no destination file\nwere specified, the banners would be stripped to the source file directly.\n\nIf you don''t specify FileName, an ARP requester will appear.\n\n@{b}NOTE:@{ub} If you use the RAM: specify the @{"s" Link VarieOpt} option.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node OptmE "Create banners:"\n\n\nPass  the  text  file  name  or a requester will appear and it will let you\nselect  a  filename  as  banner.   MaPuS  will  place in S:  a file, called\n"MaPuS.cfg".  Now you can add it to your DMS files.\n\nText file format is:  64 colums (with linefeed) for 16 lines.\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node VarieOptE "Other options:"\n\n@{b} s @{ub}  -  Don''t check free space. You should use it if you work with RAM:\n\n@{b} v @{ub}  -  View DMS file informations only, and don''t check it.\n\n@{b} d @{ub}  -  Add to track banners the uploading date.\n\n@{b} g @{ub}  -  Show some greetings.\n\n@{b} u @{ub}  -  Use an ARP requester to select the DMS file.\n\n@{b} f @{ub}  -  Show informations about every track of the DMS file.\n\n@{b} c @{ub}  -  Activate return codes. If the checking fails a return code of\n        15 will be returned.\n\n@{b} i @{ub}  -  Don''t show informations.\n\n@{b} I @{ub}  -  Don''t show other informations.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap05E "EXAMPLES:"\n\n1) Check a file:\n In this example I will suppose that you''ve a file in your DL: directory\ncalled TEST.DMS and you want to test it.\n\nType: MaPuS DL:TEST or MaPuS dl:TEST.dms\n\nit will be tested and you''ll get some infos about the file.\n\n2) Make a @{"tail banner" Link TailOptE}:\n\nType: MaPuS -M\n\n3) Add a @{"front banner" Link FrontOptE} and remove @{"tail" Link TailOptE} and @{"track banners" Link TrackOptE}:\n\nType: MaPuS -AskR dl:TEST.dms ram:newTEST.dms\n\n(Note @{"s" Link VarieOptE} option for RAM:)\n\n4) Test all files of a directory:\n\nMaPuS dl:*.dms or MaPuS dl:#?.dms\n\n@endnode\n\nCiao...\n\n@node AXusoE "/X or DLG using:"\n\n\nIf you want to use MaPuS with AmiExpress have a look at: @{b}bbs/fcheck/DMS@{ub}\n\n<----- THERE''s THE CONTENTS OF THE FILE ---------- CUT HERE ------------->\nMaPuS\n\nError\n<------------------------------------------------- CUT HERE ------------->\n\nNOTE: the 2nd line contains the options for MaPuS.\n\n@{b} REMEMBER: @{ub} The file must contains these 3 lines only!\n\nIf you''ve AmiExpress v3+ place file "DMS.info" into BBS:FCheck directory.\n\nThe  scripts  to  use  MaPuS with DLG are included in the archive, and they\nare:\n\nDLGConfig/Batch/UPLOAD1.BATCH\nDLGConfig/Text/Banner.displayme\nDLGConfig/Text/PreDesc.txt\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap06E "GLOSSARY:"\n\n@{"Tail Banner" Link TailOptE}: it''s a text file that will be appended to the end of file.\n             (it''s the last text that will be displayed unpacking)\n\n@{"Front Banner" Link FrontOptE}: it''s a text file that will be appended to the front of file.\n              (it''s the first text that will be displayed unpacking)\n\n@{"Track Banner" Link TrackOptE}: it''s the zero-track that will displayed as text file.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap07E "MaPuS UPDATES:"\n\n0.** Sperimental versions never released.\n\n0.84 First public version.  For our decision, public versions don''t\n     implement @{"-k" Link TrackOptE} command.\n\n0.85 First registered version, got if you''ve called @{"DELTA CITY BBS" Link Cap10E}.\n\n0.86-0.91 Private versions.\n     Fixed some bugs: Before @{"-k" Link TrackOptE} command corrupted archives if there were\n     track and front banner.\n\n0.92 Public version.\n     New  option @{"-f" Link VarieOptE}.  If you specify it, MaPuS will show you informations\n     about every track.\n\n0.93 Registered version.\n\n0.94 Sperimental version never released.\n\n0.95 Shareware version.\n     Fixed a bug in @{"-f" Link VarieOptE} option (the infos were not displayed if the file\n     had been selected from requester).\n\n0.96 Shareware version.\n     Fixed a bug. Now MaPuS can be resident. Thanks to Felix for bug\n     reporting.\n\n0.97 Registered version.\n\n0.98-0.99 Private versions.\n\n1.00 Shareware version, not 100% beacause no one has registered his copy of\n     MaPuS! If you want the complete version you must pay the registration\n     fee or call @{"DELTA CITY BBS" Link Cap10E}.\n     Wildcards added (*,?,#?).  Speeded up stripping routine.\n     Docs  are  now  also  in Amiga-Guide format, that contains english and\n     italian ones. Archive structure modified.\n\n1.01 Registered version.\n\n1.02-1.09 Private versions.\n\n1.10 Special version released at SMAU 1993.  Added the uploading date\n     (useful for BBS) on track banners (use @{"-d" Link VarieOptE} option).  Now you can stop\n     MaPuS with CTRL-C (after the test).\n\n1.11 Registered version.\n\n1.12 Fixed a problem in @{"-t" Link TrackoptE} option. A bug made 1.10 not working on 68000\n     systems.\n\n1.13 Registered version.\n\n1.14 Fixed two problems:\n     1) If the filename started with a minus character the command line\n        parsing didn''t worked.\n     2) Sometimes the track banners adding did corrupt the archive.\n\n1.15 Registered version.\n\n1.16 Fixed two bugs:\n     1) If CTRL-C was pressed during a file check, the program crashed the\n        system.\n     2) Small command line bug.\n     Now MaPuS informations are compatible with DMS V1.51+.\n     Guide corrected, ASCII docs deleted.\n\n1.17 Registered version.\n\n1.18-1.29 Private, not released, versions.\n         Note: I saw a "1.20" version. This version hasn''t been created by us,\n         you shouldn''t use it..\n\n1.30 Fixed some bugs: now an empty file checking doesn''t do problems.\n\n     Now supporting "": file name can contain spaces, if between "".\n\n1.31 Registered version.\n\n1.32 Added return codes with @{"-c" Link VarieOptE} option. It  returns a code of 15 if the\n     checking fails. Signaled by Jay Ruyle.\n\n1.33 Registered version.\n\n1.34 Bug fixes. New options @{"-i and -I" Link VarieOptE}.\n\n1.35 Registered version.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap08E "FUTURE FEATURES:"\n\n\n- MaPuS will take the file list to operate over from a text file.\n\n- Use of a better requester.\n\n- Banner display.\n\n- Scripts for failed or successful tests (useful for BBSes).\n\n- Date adding on tail and front banners.\n\n- MaPuS will select a random banner to add.\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap09E "GREETINGS:"\n\nMany thanks go to (alphabetic order):\n\nAlex,  /\rc,  Atomos, Batblaster, Blulight, Caton, Crier, Deus, Doc, Doctor\nRevenge,  DR.Dream/FTH,  DR.G,  Exodus,  Fashion Light, Felix, Gandalf/FTH,\nGhost,  GiapDJ,  Godfather,  Guile, Highlander, Høøk/FTH, Jay Ruyle, Joseph\nHodge  (/X  author), Kenshiro, Kris, Laurent, Leo, LoneWolf, Mad Harlequin,\nMad  Lemming,  MAUI BBS (2:335/602@fidonet), /\/\aster T/4WD, Metalbasher!,\nMF   the  Best,  Modem  Boy,  Mondrian,  MR.IRQ,  MR.Swapper,  /\/ightmare,\n/\/ikita/4WD,  Nosferatu,  Pier, Pixie, Polaris, Pork, Pows, Randy, Sauzer,\nSeven  /\/\,  Shady,  Splatter, T-Rexx, The Outlaw, Top, Tron/RPK, Warrior,\nWoodelf, all my users, all friends and all the ones I forget...\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Cap10E "CONTACTS:"\n\n\nYou can contact us (via NetMail) at these addresses:\n\n2:335/[email removed]\n\nor via "old" mail at:\n\n                             Antonino Pintaudi\n                                P.O. Box 11\n                         98125 Contesse (Messina)\n                                  ITALIA\n\n\nor calling the *NEW* support BBS:\n\n                              Delta City BBS\n                            +39-(0)931-760203\n                      [ Leave a message to "Eniac" ]\n@endnode\n\nWhere you''re looking in????\nFINE!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',71866,3,0,NULL,NULL,'mapus134','scan',1780048589);
