 DATE: 12-22-17  TIME: 18:25:44  ON NODE: 1\n','\r',char(13)),'\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,8034,2,0,NULL,NULL,'mdb_at10_mdb_amitest','scan',1780048589);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mdb_cu15','MDB-CU15.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MDB-CU15.LHA','MDB-ConfUpdater','XIM','DMSDescript',NULL,NULL,'MDB','|  _____/\ _____/\  _____/\       THe      | |  \  _  / \  ___/ /  / \  \  GRaVeDiGGeRS | |  /\/ | \  \/ \  /  /\_/\  \              |',replace('.------------------------------------------.\n|  _____/\ _____/\  _____/\       THe      |\n|  \  _  / \  ___/ /  / \  \  GRaVeDiGGeRS |\n|  /\/ | \  \/ \  /  /\_/\  \              |\n| / /__|  \ /  /  \  \   /  / /X DeSiGn    |\n| \____/  / \  \   \__\ /  /  100% pure    |\n|      \_/   \_/        \_/   XIM-assembly |\n| >> Conference Updater 1.5Beta <<         |\n| >> - Inserting - Viewing - Copying - <<  |\n| * oTM * MDB PRoDuCTioNS * BBS DEATHsimple|\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'ConfUpdater.GUIDE',replace('@database MDB-ConferenceUpdater 1.1\n\nCopyright (C) 1994 (MDB Productionc/OTM The Gravediggers) \nAll Rights Reserved\n\n@Remark $VER: Version V1.1 (13 Mrt 1994)\n@Remark AmigaGuide database for the ConferenceUpdater 1.1\n\n@node MAIN "MDB-ConferenceUpdater 1.1 AmigaGuide Document (C) 1994 (MDB Productions)"\n\n                         _____/\   ______/\  _____/\ \n                        /  / \  \  \  ___  \ \  ___ \\n                       /  /\_/\  \ /\/| /  / /\/ /  /\n                       \  \   /  //   |/  / /  |/   \\n                        \__\ /  / \___   /  \__|_   /\n                             \_/      \_/        \_/ \n\n                   MDB Productions  iS PRouD To PReSeNT :\n\n                  C O N F E R E N C E - U P D A T E R 1.1\n\n          ·:·C·O·N·T·E·N·T·S··O·F··D·O·C·U·M·E·N·T·A·T·I·O·N·:·\n\n                             @{"  INTRODUCTION  " LINK PART_01}\n                             @{"  REQUIREMENTS  " LINK PART_02}\n                             @{"  INSTALLATION  " LINK PART_03}\n                             @{"   TOOL-TYPES   " LINK PART_04}\n                             @{"    CHANGES!    " LINK PART_05}\n                             @{"     ADVERT     " LINK PART_06}\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_01 "Introduction"\n\nFor sysops it''s hard to keep their conferences up to date. This door\nchecks if the files stated in the catalogs still exist. If they don''t\nexists anymore, the filesize in the catalog will be changed to a text\nlike ''OFFLINE'', ''DELETED'' or something simular.\n\nThe door is very smart, so the less installation you have to do. It\nchecks the following icons BBS:CONFCONFIG and CONF<num>. Lets enjoy\nthis one.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_02 "Requirements"\n\nWhat U need to run it...\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n - an Amigamodel (A500/A600/A1200/A2000/A3000/A4000) with Kickstart 2.04++\n\n - the installed /X-Software (V3.20+) in the drawer BBS:\n\nNow let''s go on by explaining the @{"Installation" LINK PART_03}...\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_03 "Installation for ConfUpdater 1.1"\n\nHow to install it to your /X-System...\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nFirst make a Drawer into Doors: called ''MDB-ConfUpdater'' and copy the Files\n - ''MDB-ConfUpdater''\n - ''MDB-ConfUpdater.INFO''\ninto it.\n\nSecond copy the Icon ''CU.INFO'' into the BBSCmd Drawer.\n\nThats all there is. Simple he!\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_04 "ToolTypes for ConfUpdater 1.1"\n\n                                ToolTypes\n                                ~~~~~~~~~\n\n                    @{" TOOLTYPES FOR MDB-ConfUpdater 1.1" LINK PART_04_LC}\n\n                    @{" TOOLTYPES FOR CU                 " LINK PART_04_LO}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_04_LC "ToolTypes for MDB-ConfUpdater 1.1\n\n                 ToolTypes for MDB-ConfUpdater 1.1\n                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nDELETE.num=<string>             - The DELETE.num tooltype specifies the text\n                                  that will be passed to your catalogs. The\n                                  maximum string length is 8 characters. Do\n                                  not overide this one. The maximum of\n                                  DELETE.num is 9.\n                                  Eg. DELETE.1=OFFLINE\n\nDESTINATION=<path>              - This tooltype specifies where the DIR<num>\n                                  catalogs will be stored. It is a backup-\n                                  mechanism, so you have to move them your\n                                  self to active them. The catalogs will be\n                                  be stored as CONF<num>_DIR<num>. The path\n                                  must end with a '':'' or a ''/'' like:\n                                  DESTINATION=RAM: or\n                                  DESTINATION=Work:Tmp/\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_04_LO "ToolTypes For CU"\n\n                       ToolTypes for CU\n                       ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nACCESS=<acs.level>              - This tooltype specifies the access level\n                                  that the user must have to run the door.\n                                  Eg. ACCESS=200\n\nLOCATION=<filename>             - This tooltype specifies where the Door\n                                  is located.\n                                  Eg. LOCATION=Doors:MDB-ConfUpdater/MDB-ConfUpdater\n\nMULTINODE=<YES|NO>              - This tooltype specifies if the Door may\n                                  started in different nodes.\n                                  Eg. MULTINODE=YES\n\nPRIORITY=<num>                  - This tooltype specifies the AmigaDos\n                                  priority when the Door is executed.\n                                  Eg. PRIORITY=2\n\nSTACK=<size>                    - This tooltype specifies the Door stack.\n                                  Eg. STACK=8096\n\nTYPE=<AIM|SIM|TIM|XIM>          - This tooltype specifies the Door-type.\n                                  This Door is written in 100% pure\n                                  Assembly so TYPE=XIM\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_05 "Changes"\n\n1.1 (13 Mar 1994) \n    - The term ''catalog'' changed to ''dir'' for better understanding\n      for some persons.\n    - Using ANSI-codes instead of CSI-codes. The screens must work\n      remote now!\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_06 "Death Simple ... OTM The GraveDiggers"\n\n/X 3.3+    :+                   WELCOME TO                            /X 3.3+\n          .::.       ____________  ______________._          .+.\n         .:+.       |__  \  ____/ / _ \      _/  | \         .:.\n   AscII  +::+.     |  \  \  .)\_/     \/   | |  |  \       ::+.    AscII\n \  B Y  /   :.     |  /   \ |  |   :   \   | |  _   \     :+:.  \   B Y   /\n _\ MSW /_          |______/\___|\__|___/\__| |__|___/     .     _\  MSW  /_ \n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-         -=-            -=-=-=-=-             -=-=-=-=-=--=-=-\n.°*DEATH                                                             DEATH*°.\n   SIMPLE*°.                                                      .°*SIMPLE\n=-=-=-               -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-            -=-=-          -=-=-=   -=-=-\n                ___/\____/\  __ _/\  /\_____/\__      /\____\n-24 HoUrS      /     \____/ /  Y   \/___  _ \  |     /  .  |    ..::.\n-chataBle     /   ___/    \/   :    \  / ___/  |__  /   |__|     +::.+\n-SysOp        \___   \____ \___ ____ \/  |\  __|  \/_    __/   .+::+\n-CeWl Area''s  /   \__/    \/   Y    \/\__| \/      \ \__/  \   .:\n              \  ___/\____/\___|__  /__  |  \______ \____  /\n               \/                 \/   \/          \/    \/ +31-(0)2152-68786\n\n    __/\__ __ ___ _ _ _   :-)   2 OPERATOR 2  (-:      ___ __ __ __/\__\n    \ Oo /__ ______ _ _       ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~          __ __ __\ oO /\n    /_--_\__ ___ __ __       2-)  COSYSOP  (-2        __ ____ _ _/_--_\\n      \/                                                           \/\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),'{"ACCESS":"<acs.level>","LOCATION":"<filename>","PRIORITY":"<num>","STACK":"<size>","TYPE":"<AIM|SIM|TIM|XIM>"}','auto-added',53644,5,0,NULL,NULL,'mdb_cu15','scan',1780048589);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mdb_cu18','MDB-CU18.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MDB-CU18.LHA','MDB-ConfUpdater','XIM','DMSDescript',NULL,NULL,'MDB','|  _____/\   ______/\  _____/\  (c) 1994   | | /  / \  \  \  ___  \ \  ___ \ PRoDuCTioNS| |/  /\_/\  \ /\/| /  / /\/ /  /            |',replace('.------------------------------------------.\n|  _____/\   ______/\  _____/\  (c) 1994   |\n| /  / \  \  \  ___  \ \  ___ \ PRoDuCTioNS|\n|/  /\_/\  \ /\/| /  / /\/ /  /            |\n|\  \   /  //   |/  / /  |/   \ 100% PuRe  |\n| \__\ /__/ \______/  \__|____/ XiM /X DooR|\n|                                          |\n| $VER: ConferenceUpdater 1.8 (02-Jun-1994)|\n|                                          |\n|  MDB PRoDuCTioNS * NiGHTCRaWLER * ViDuR  |\n`------------------------------------------''\n>MAYDAY.. MAYDAY.. INTRUDERS ENTER MEN-TEL!<\n','\n',char(10)),'ConfUpdater.GUIDE',replace('@database MDB-ConferenceUpdater 1.8\n\nCopyright (C) 1994 (MDB Productions)\nAll Rights Reserved\n\n@Remark $VER: Version V1.8 (02 Jun 1994)\n@Remark AmigaGuide database for the ConferenceUpdater 1.8\n\n@node MAIN "MDB-ConferenceUpdater 1.8 AmigaGuide Document (C) 1994 (MDB Productions)"\n\n                         _____/\   ______/\  _____/\ \n                        /  / \  \  \  ___  \ \  ___ \\n                       /  /\_/\  \ /\/| /  / /\/ /  /\n                       \  \   /  //   |/  / /  |/   \\n                        \__\ /  / \___   /  \__|_   /\n                             \_/      \_/        \_/ \n\n                   MDB Productions  iS PRouD To PReSeNT :\n\n                  C O N F E R E N C E - U P D A T E R 1.8\n\n          ·:·C·O·N·T·E·N·T·S··O·F··D·O·C·U·M·E·N·T·A·T·I·O·N·:·\n\n                             @{"  INTRODUCTION  " LINK PART_01}\n                             @{"  REQUIREMENTS  " LINK PART_02}\n                             @{"  INSTALLATION  " LINK PART_03}\n                             @{"   TOOL-TYPES   " LINK PART_04}\n                             @{"    COMMANDS    " LINK PART_05}\n                             @{"    CHANGES!    " LINK PART_06}\n                             @{"     ADVERT     " LINK PART_07}\n                             @{"      HELP      " LINK PART_08}\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_01 "Introduction"\n\nFor sysops it''s hard to keep their conferences up to date. This door\nchecks if the files stated in the catalogs still exist. If they don''t\nexists anymore, the filesize in the catalog will be changed to a text\nlike ''OFFLINE'', ''DELETED'' or something simular.\n\nThe door is very smart, so the less installation you have to do. It\nchecks the following icons BBS:CONFCONFIG and CONF<num>. Lets enjoy\nthis one.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_02 "Requirements"\n\nWhat U need to run it...\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n - an Amigamodel (A500/A600/A1200/A2000/A3000/A4000) with Kickstart 2.04++\n\n - the installed /X-Software (V3.20+) in the drawer BBS:\n\nNow let''s go on by explaining the @{"Installation" LINK PART_03}...\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_03 "Installation for ConfUpdater 1.8"\n\nHow to install it to your /X-System...\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nFirst make a Drawer into Doors: called ''MDB-ConfUpdater'' and copy the Files\n - ''MDB-ConfUpdater''\n - ''MDB-ConfUpdater.INFO''\ninto it.\n\nSecond copy the Icon ''CU.INFO'' into the BBSCmd Drawer.\n\nLast bu not least you have to copy some tools into the C Drawer, coz\nthe insert-option need them to extract the FILE_ID.DIZ. These files are:\n - ''DMSDescript''\n - ''EXEDescript''\n - ''TxtExtract''\n\nThats all there is. Simple he!\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_04 "ToolTypes for ConfUpdater 1.8"\n\n                                ToolTypes\n                                ~~~~~~~~~\n\n                    @{" TOOLTYPES FOR MDB-ConfUpdater 1.8" LINK PART_04_LC}\n\n                    @{" TOOLTYPES FOR CU                 " LINK PART_04_LO}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_04_LC "ToolTypes for MDB-ConfUpdater 1.8\n\n                 ToolTypes for MDB-ConfUpdater 1.8\n                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nDELETE.num=<string>             - The DELETE.num tooltype specifies the text\n                                  that will be passed to your catalogs. The\n                                  maximum string length is 8 characters. Do\n                                  not overide this one. The maximum of\n                                  DELETE.num is 9.\n                                  Eg. DELETE.1=OFFLINE\n\nDESTINATION=<path>              - This tooltype specifies where the DIR<num>\n                                  catalogs will be stored. It is a backup-\n                                  mechanism, so you have to move them your\n                                  self to active them. The catalogs will be\n                                  be stored as CONF<num>_DIR<num>. The path\n                                  must end with a '':'' or a ''/'' like:\n                                  DESTINATION=RAM: or\n                                  DESTINATION=Work:Tmp/\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_04_LO "ToolTypes For CU"\n\n                       ToolTypes for CU\n                       ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nACCESS=<acs.level>              - This tooltype specifies the access level\n                                  that the user must have to run the door.\n                                  Eg. ACCESS=200\n\nLOCATION=<filename>             - This tooltype specifies where the Door\n                                  is located.\n                                  LOCATION=Doors:MDB-ConfUpdater/MDB-ConfUpdater\n                                  !!! DO NOT CHANGE THIS ONE !!!\n\nMULTINODE=<YES|NO>              - This tooltype specifies if the Door may\n                                  started in different nodes.\n                                  Eg. MULTINODE=YES\n\nPRIORITY=<num>                  - This tooltype specifies the AmigaDos\n                                  priority when the Door is executed.\n                                  Eg. PRIORITY=2\n\nSTACK=<size>                    - This tooltype specifies the Door stack.\n                                  Eg. STACK=8096\n\nTYPE=<AIM|SIM|TIM|XIM>          - This tooltype specifies the Door-type.\n                                  This Door is written in 100% pure\n                                  Assembly so TYPE=XIM\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_05 "Commands"\n\nStart the door by useing the CU-command, and will get the main menu.\n\n@{" A "} Shows some litte information about the authors.\n\n@{" D "} In a conference you can use different DIRs. The maximum is\n    stated in the CONF<num> icon in the tooltype NDIRS. By \n    startup this value will be used as working DIR. This option\n    allows you to change the dirnumber you are working with.\n\n@{" U "} THE CONFERENCE UPDATE. This one scans your current dir (as\n    mentions with option D). If a entry in your dir doesn''t\n    exists anymore, a action will take place:\n       1. change the filesize in a message like ''DELETED''\n       2. delete the entry.\n    Which one will depant of your option (1-0).\n\n@{" Q "} Don''t try.\n\n@{" I "} This one scans all your update dirs. If there is a file \n    which is not present in the current dir, the file will\n    be added to this dir.\n\n@{" V "} A previously processed dir can be viewed with this option.\n\n@{" B "} We always say, safety first. Therefore an updated dir is\n    placed in a directory according the DESTINATION tooltype.\n    But if you want, you can the bring the processed dir only.\n    Safety first, so a backup will be made of your actual dir\n    in the bbs.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_06 "Changes"\n\n1.8 (02 Jun May 1994)\n    - All functions recognise the Exorcist commands! Nice he!\n      Thanxs to RubiX from TFA for mentioning.\n\n1.7 (02 Jun May 1994)\n    - Viewer changed, now it uses de DT_LINELENGTH function and\n      correctly displays the text options in stead of the filesize\n      (the last char wasn''t displayed).\n\n1.6 (29 May 1994)\n    - Some maincoding changes, faster and better!\n    - The DIRs will be re-read after each DLPATH is scanned by\n      the Insert-option. No duplicate entries any more!\n    - Now the door uses the online BBS dir by the Insert-option\n      if you answer is NO to the question if you like to use the\n      previously processed dir.\n    - Handles empty dirs (0 bytes or doesn''t exist) correcty by\n      the Insert-option.\n\n1.5 (20 May 1994)\n    - Scans download directories 1 to 9 and insert new files to\n      the DIR.\n    - View the processed dir.\n    - Brings the processed dir online.\n    - Default startup for directory changed from DIR1 to NDIRS as\n      stated in CONF<num>.INFO\n    - Delete an entry in the dir if the file doesn''t exists.\n    - A lot more, I already forgot them.\n\n1.4 (16 May 1994) Never released\n    \n1.3 (16 Mar 1994)\n    - Faster screenhandling.\n    - New action available, directory occurences will be deleted when\n      the file is not available.\n\n1.2 (14 Mar 1994)\n    - Returncode $a removed. This value meant LINE DOWN in stead\n      of NEW LINE in ANSI-codes.\n\n1.1 (13 Mar 1994) \n    - The term ''catalog'' changed to ''dir'' for better understanding\n      for some persons.\n    - Using ANSI-codes instead of CSI-codes. The screens must work\n      remote now!\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_07 "Death Simple ... OTM The GraveDiggers"\n\n/X 3.3+    :+                   WELCOME TO                            /X 3.3+\n          .::.       ____________  ______________._          .+.\n         .:+.       |__  \  ____/ / _ \      _/  | \         .:.\n   AscII  +::+.     |  \  \  .)\_/     \/   | |  |  \       ::+.    AscII\n \  B Y  /   :.     |  /   \ |  |   :   \   | |  _   \     :+:.  \   B Y   /\n _\ MSW /_          |______/\___|\__|___/\__| |__|___/     .     _\  MSW  /_ \n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-         -=-            -=-=-=-=-             -=-=-=-=-=--=-=-\n.°*DEATH                                                             DEATH*°.\n   SIMPLE*°.                                                      .°*SIMPLE\n=-=-=-               -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-            -=-=-          -=-=-=   -=-=-\n                ___/\____/\  __ _/\  /\_____/\__      /\____\n-24 HoUrS      /     \____/ /  Y   \/___  _ \  |     /  .  |    ..::.\n-chataBle     /   ___/    \/   :    \  / ___/  |__  /   |__|     +::.+\n-SysOp        \___   \____ \___ ____ \/  |\  __|  \/_    __/   .+::+\n-CeWl Area''s  /   \__/    \/   Y    \/\__| \/      \ \__/  \   .:\n              \  ___/\____/\___|__  /__  |  \______ \____  /\n               \/                 \/   \/          \/    \/ +31-(0)2152-68786\n\n    __/\__ __ ___ _ _ _   :-)   2 OPERATOR 2  (-:      ___ __ __ __/\__\n    \ Oo /__ ______ _ _       ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~          __ __ __\ oO /\n    /_--_\__ ___ __ __       2-)  COSYSOP  (-2        __ ____ _ _/_--_\\n      \/                                                           \/\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_08 "Help me please"\nCan somebody help me with the following feature:\nI like to implent a break-option useing CTRL-C keys. But how can I prog\nthis feature in assembler??? If you now how, please contact me and tell\nme how to do it, or better give me a some source coding?\n\nContact me directy:\n   MDB Productions\n   PWA-park 93\n   3905 CC  Veenendaal\n   The Netherlands\n   +31-(0)8385-29239\n\nOr leave a messy at our board\n   Death Simple\n   +31-(0)2152-68786\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),'{"ACCESS":"<acs.level>","LOCATION":"<filename>","PRIORITY":"<num>","STACK":"<size>","TYPE":"<AIM|SIM|TIM|XIM>"}','auto-added',46497,2,0,NULL,NULL,'mdb_cu18','scan',1780048589);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mdb_cu19','MDB-CU19.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MDB-CU19.LHA','MDB-ConfUpdater','XIM','DMSDescript',NULL,NULL,'MDB','|  _____/\   ______/\  _____/\  (c) 1994   | | /  / \  \  \  ___  \ \  ___ \ PRoDuCTioNS| |/  /\_/\  \ /\/| /  / /\/ /  /            |',replace('.------------------------------------------.\n|  _____/\   ______/\  _____/\  (c) 1994   |\n| /  / \  \  \  ___  \ \  ___ \ PRoDuCTioNS|\n|/  /\_/\  \ /\/| /  / /\/ /  /            |\n|\  \   /  //   |/  / /  |/   \ 100% PuRe  |\n| \__\ /__/ \______/  \__|____/ XiM /X DooR|\n|                                          |\n| $VER: ConferenceUpdater 1.9 (05-Jun-1994)|\n| >>>>>>>>Now including dir sort! <<<<<<<< |\n|                                          |\n|  MDB PRoDuCTioNS * NiGHTCRaWLER * ViDuR  |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'ConfUpdater.GUIDE',replace('@database MDB-ConferenceUpdater 1.9\n\nCopyright (C) 1994 (MDB Productions)\nAll Rights Reserved\n\n@Remark $VER: Version V1.9 (05 Jun 1994)\n@Remark AmigaGuide database for the ConferenceUpdater 1.9\n\n@node MAIN "MDB-ConferenceUpdater 1.9 AmigaGuide Document (C) 1994 (MDB Productions)"\n\n                         _____/\   ______/\  _____/\ \n                        /  / \  \  \  ___  \ \  ___ \\n                       /  /\_/\  \ /\/| /  / /\/ /  /\n                       \  \   /  //   |/  / /  |/   \\n                        \__\ /  / \___   /  \__|_   /\n                             \_/      \_/        \_/ \n\n                   MDB Productions  iS PRouD To PReSeNT :\n\n                  C O N F E R E N C E - U P D A T E R 1.9\n\n          ·:·C·O·N·T·E·N·T·S··O·F··D·O·C·U·M·E·N·T·A·T·I·O·N·:·\n\n                             @{"  INTRODUCTION  " LINK PART_01}\n                             @{"  REQUIREMENTS  " LINK PART_02}\n                             @{"  INSTALLATION  " LINK PART_03}\n                             @{"   TOOL-TYPES   " LINK PART_04}\n                             @{"    COMMANDS    " LINK PART_05}\n                             @{"    CHANGES!    " LINK PART_06}\n                             @{"     ADVERT     " LINK PART_07}\n                             @{"      HELP      " LINK PART_08}\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_01 "Introduction"\n\nFor sysops it''s hard to keep their conferences up to date. This door\nchecks if the files stated in the catalogs still exist. If they don''t\nexists anymore, the filesize in the catalog will be changed to a text\nlike ''OFFLINE'', ''DELETED'' or something simular.\n\nThe door is very smart, so the less installation you have to do. It\nchecks the following icons BBS:CONFCONFIG and CONF<num>. Lets enjoy\nthis one.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_02 "Requirements"\n\nWhat U need to run it...\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n - an Amigamodel (A500/A600/A1200/A2000/A3000/A4000) with Kickstart 2.04++\n\n - the installed /X-Software (V3.20+) in the drawer BBS:\n\nNow let''s go on by explaining the @{"Installation" LINK PART_03}...\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_03 "Installation for ConfUpdater 1.9"\n\nHow to install it to your /X-System...\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nFirst make a Drawer into Doors: called ''MDB-ConfUpdater'' and copy the Files\n - ''MDB-ConfUpdater''\n - ''MDB-ConfUpdater.INFO''\ninto it.\n\nSecond copy the Icon ''CU.INFO'' into the BBSCmd Drawer.\n\nLast bu not least you have to copy some tools into the C Drawer, coz\nthe insert-option need them to extract the FILE_ID.DIZ. These files are:\n - ''DMSDescript''\n - ''EXEDescript''\n - ''TxtExtract''\n\nThats all there is. Simple he!\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_04 "ToolTypes for ConfUpdater 1.9"\n\n                                ToolTypes\n                                ~~~~~~~~~\n\n                    @{" TOOLTYPES FOR MDB-ConfUpdater 1.9" LINK PART_04_LC}\n\n                    @{" TOOLTYPES FOR CU                 " LINK PART_04_LO}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_04_LC "ToolTypes for MDB-ConfUpdater 1.9\n\n                 ToolTypes for MDB-ConfUpdater 1.9\n                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nDELETE.num=<string>             - The DELETE.num tooltype specifies the text\n                                  that will be passed to your catalogs. The\n                                  maximum string length is 8 characters. Do\n                                  not overide this one. The maximum of\n                                  DELETE.num is 9.\n                                  Eg. DELETE.1=OFFLINE\n\nDESTINATION=<path>              - This tooltype specifies where the DIR<num>\n                                  catalogs will be stored. It is a backup-\n                                  mechanism, so you have to move them your\n                                  self to active them. The catalogs will be\n                                  be stored as CONF<num>_DIR<num>. The path\n                                  must end with a '':'' or a ''/'' like:\n                                  DESTINATION=RAM: or\n                                  DESTINATION=Work:Tmp/\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_04_LO "ToolTypes For CU"\n\n                       ToolTypes for CU\n                       ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nACCESS=<acs.level>              - This tooltype specifies the access level\n                                  that the user must have to run the door.\n                                  Eg. ACCESS=200\n\nLOCATION=<filename>             - This tooltype specifies where the Door\n                                  is located.\n                                  LOCATION=Doors:MDB-ConfUpdater/MDB-ConfUpdater\n                                  !!! DO NOT CHANGE THIS ONE !!!\n\nMULTINODE=<YES|NO>              - This tooltype specifies if the Door may\n                                  started in different nodes.\n                                  Eg. MULTINODE=YES\n\nPRIORITY=<num>                  - This tooltype specifies the AmigaDos\n                                  priority when the Door is executed.\n                                  Eg. PRIORITY=2\n\nSTACK=<size>                    - This tooltype specifies the Door stack.\n                                  Eg. STACK=8096\n\nTYPE=<AIM|SIM|TIM|XIM>          - This tooltype specifies the Door-type.\n                                  This Door is written in 100% pure\n                                  Assembly so TYPE=XIM\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_05 "Commands"\n\nStart the door by useing the CU-command, and will get the main menu.\n\n@{" A "} Shows some litte information about the authors.\n\n@{" D "} In a conference you can use different DIRs. The maximum is\n    stated in the CONF<num> icon in the tooltype NDIRS. By \n    startup this value will be used as working DIR. This option\n    allows you to change the dirnumber you are working with.\n\n@{" U "} THE CONFERENCE UPDATE. This one scans your current dir (as\n    mentions with option D). If a entry in your dir doesn''t\n    exists anymore, a action will take place:\n       1. change the filesize in a message like ''DELETED''\n       2. delete the entry.\n    Which one will depant of your option (1-0).\n\n@{" Q "} Don''t try.\n\n@{" I "} This one scans all your update dirs. If there is a file \n    which is not present in the current dir, the file will\n    be added to this dir.\n\n@{" V "} A previously processed dir can be viewed with this option.\n\n@{" B "} We always say, safety first. Therefore an updated dir is\n    placed in a directory according the DESTINATION tooltype.\n    But if you want, you can the bring the processed dir only.\n    Safety first, so a backup will be made of your actual dir\n    in the bbs.\n\n@{" S "} Sorts the dir by date, filename.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_06 "Changes"\n\n1.9 (05 Jun May 1994)\n    - The dir can now be sorted! It''s even possible to make all\n      files with current date; nice for the ''N S U'' command.\n      Be aware for look a likes, I just saw one from noCtyre/Mystic!!!\n    - Dir viewer works remote now!\n\n1.8 (02 Jun May 1994)\n    - All functions recognise the Exorcist commands! Nice he!\n      Thanxs to RubiX from TFA for mentioning.\n\n1.7 (02 Jun May 1994)\n    - Viewer changed, now it uses de DT_LINELENGTH function and\n      correctly displays the text options in stead of the filesize\n      (the last char wasn''t displayed).\n\n1.6 (29 May 1994)\n    - Some maincoding changes, faster and better!\n    - The DIRs will be re-read after each DLPATH is scanned by\n      the Insert-option. No duplicate entries any more!\n    - Now the door uses the online BBS dir by the Insert-option\n      if you answer is NO to the question if you like to use the\n      previously processed dir.\n    - Handles empty dirs (0 bytes or doesn''t exist) correcty by\n      the Insert-option.\n\n1.5 (20 May 1994)\n    - Scans download directories 1 to 9 and insert new files to\n      the DIR.\n    - View the processed dir.\n    - Brings the processed dir online.\n    - Default startup for directory changed from DIR1 to NDIRS as\n      stated in CONF<num>.INFO\n    - Delete an entry in the dir if the file doesn''t exists.\n    - A lot more, I already forgot them.\n\n1.4 (16 May 1994) Never released\n    \n1.3 (16 Mar 1994)\n    - Faster screenhandling.\n    - New action available, directory occurences will be deleted when\n      the file is not available.\n\n1.2 (14 Mar 1994)\n    - Returncode $a removed. This value meant LINE DOWN in stead\n      of NEW LINE in ANSI-codes.\n\n1.1 (13 Mar 1994) \n    - The term ''catalog'' changed to ''dir'' for better understanding\n      for some persons.\n    - Using ANSI-codes instead of CSI-codes. The screens must work\n      remote now!\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_07 "Death Simple ... OTM The GraveDiggers"\n\n/X 3.3+    :+                   WELCOME TO                            /X 3.3+\n          .::.       ____________  ______________._          .+.\n         .:+.       |__  \  ____/ / _ \      _/  | \         .:.\n   AscII  +::+.     |  \  \  .)\_/     \/   | |  |  \       ::+.    AscII\n \  B Y  /   :.     |  /   \ |  |   :   \   | |  _   \     :+:.  \   B Y   /\n _\ MSW /_          |______/\___|\__|___/\__| |__|___/     .     _\  MSW  /_ \n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-         -=-            -=-=-=-=-             -=-=-=-=-=--=-=-\n.°*DEATH                                                             DEATH*°.\n   SIMPLE*°.                                                      .°*SIMPLE\n=-=-=-               -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-            -=-=-          -=-=-=   -=-=-\n                ___/\____/\  __ _/\  /\_____/\__      /\____\n-24 HoUrS      /     \____/ /  Y   \/___  _ \  |     /  .  |    ..::.\n-chataBle     /   ___/    \/   :    \  / ___/  |__  /   |__|     +::.+\n-SysOp        \___   \____ \___ ____ \/  |\  __|  \/_    __/   .+::+\n-CeWl Area''s  /   \__/    \/   Y    \/\__| \/      \ \__/  \   .:\n              \  ___/\____/\___|__  /__  |  \______ \____  /\n               \/                 \/   \/          \/    \/ +31-(0)2152-68786\n\n    __/\__ __ ___ _ _ _   :-)   2 OPERATOR 2  (-:      ___ __ __ __/\__\n    \ Oo /__ ______ _ _       ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~          __ __ __\ oO /\n    /_--_\__ ___ __ __       2-)  COSYSOP  (-2        __ ____ _ _/_--_\\n      \/                                                           \/\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_08 "Help me please"\nCan somebody help me with the following feature:\nI like to implent a break-option useing CTRL-C keys. But how can I prog\nthis feature in assembler??? If you now how, please contact me and tell\nme how to do it, or better give me a some source coding?\n\nContact me directy:\n   MDB Productions\n   PWA-park 93\n   3905 CC  Veenendaal\n   The Netherlands\n   +31-(0)8385-29239\n\nOr leave a messy at our board\n   Death Simple\n   +31-(0)2152-68786\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),'{"ACCESS":"<acs.level>","LOCATION":"<filename>","PRIORITY":"<num>","STACK":"<size>","TYPE":"<AIM|SIM|TIM|XIM>"}','auto-added',47414,2,0,NULL,NULL,'mdb_cu19','scan',1780048589);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mdb_lc16','MDB-LC16.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MDB-LC16.LHA','MDB-LastCallers','XIM','MDB-LastCallers',NULL,NULL,'MDB','|  _____/\   ______/\  _____/\  (c) 1994   | | /  / \  \  \  ___  \ \  ___ \ PRoDuCTioNS| |/  /\_/\  \ /\/| /  / /\/ /  /            |',replace('.------------------------------------------.\n|  _____/\   ______/\  _____/\  (c) 1994   |\n| /  / \  \  \  ___  \ \  ___ \ PRoDuCTioNS|\n|/  /\_/\  \ /\/| /  / /\/ /  /            |\n|\  \   /  //   |/  / /  |/   \ 100% PuRe  |\n| \__\ /__/ \______/  \__|____/ SiM /X DooR|\n|                                          |\n| $VER: Last Callers 1.6 (04-Jun-1994)     |\n| Some main coding enhanced!               |\n|                                          |\n|  MDB PRoDuCTioNS * NiGHTCRaWLER * ViDuR  |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'MDB-LastCallers.GUIDE',replace('@database MDB-LastCallers 1.6\n\nCopyright (C) 1994 (MDB Productionc) \nAll Rights Reserved\n\n@Remark $VER: Version V1.6 (Mrt 01 1994)\n@Remark AmigaGuide database for the LastCallers 1.6\n\n@node MAIN "MDB-LastCallers 1.6 AmigaGuide Document (C) 1994 (MDB Productions)"\n\n                         _____/\   ______/\  _____/\ \n                        /  / \  \  \  ___  \ \  ___ \\n                       /  /\_/\  \ /\/| /  / /\/ /  /\n                       \  \   /  //   |/  / /  |/   \\n                        \__\ /  / \___   /  \__|_   /\n                             \_/      \_/        \_/ \n\n                   MDB Productions  iS PRouD To PReSeNT :\n\n                        L A S T C A L L E R 1.6\n\n          ·:·C·O·N·T·E·N·T·S··O·F··D·O·C·U·M·E·N·T·A·T·I·O·N·:·\n\n                             @{"  INTRODUCTION  " LINK PART_01}\n                             @{"  REQUIREMENTS  " LINK PART_02}\n                             @{"  INSTALLATION  " LINK PART_03}\n                             @{"   TOOL-TYPES   " LINK PART_04}\n                             @{"    CHANGES!    " LINK PART_05}\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_01 "Introduction"\n\nA saw a lot of LastCaller doors and scripts, but I always though\n''huh, I could do this better!''. Thats why I wrote this door.Nowadays\nit is a SIM module, coz I had to scan the CallersLog in Node(1) and\nI had also running some statistics.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_02 "Requirements"\n\nWhat U need to run it...\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n - an Amigamodel (A500/A600/A1200/A2000/A3000/A4000) with Kickstart 2.04++\n\n - the installed /X-Software (V3.20++)\n\nNow let''s go on by explaining the @{"Installation" LINK PART_03}...\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_03 "Installation for MDB-LastCallers 1.6"\n\nHow to install it to your /X-System...\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nFirst make a Drawer into Doors: called ''MDB-LastCallers'' and copy the Files\n - ''MDB-LASTCALLERS''\n - ''MDB-LASTCALLERS.INFO''\n - ''FOOTER.TXT''\n - ''HEADER.TXT''\ninto it.\n\nSecond copy the Icon ''LOGOFF1.INFO'' into the SYSCmd Drawer.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_04 "ToolTypes for MDB-LastCallers 1.6"\n\n                                ToolTypes\n                                ~~~~~~~~~\n\n                    @{" TOOLTYPES FOR MDB-LASTCALLERS 1.6" LINK PART_04_LC}\n\n                    @{" TOOLTYPES FOR LOGOFF<n>          " LINK PART_04_LO}\n\n                    @{" THE LOGOFF SCRIPT                " LINK PART_04_SC}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_04_LC "ToolTypes for MDB-LastCallers 1.6\n\n                 ToolTypes for MDB-LastCallers 1.6\n                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nBULL=<filename>                 - This ToolType specifies the output-file.\n                                  /X calls this one a BULL. Include this\n                                  in your login-Bull so that every caller\n                                  sees the last 10 callers.\n                                  Eg. BULL=BBS:LastCallers.txt\n\nHEADER=<filename>               - The header tooltype specifies which file\n                                  will be joined before the LastCallers info.\n                                  Eg. FOOTER=Doors:MDB-LastCallers/Header.txt\n\nFOOTER=<filename>               - The footer tooltype specifies which file\n                                  will be joined behind the LastCallers info.\n                                  Eg. FOOTER=Doors:MDB-LastCallers/Footer.txt\n\nCALLERSLOG=<filename>           - This tooltypes indicates which log must be\n                                  be scanned.\n                                  Eg. CALLERSLOG=BBS:Node1/CallersLog\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_04_LO "ToolTypes For LogOff<x>"\n\n                       ToolTypes for LogOff<x>"\n                       ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nAs noted in Chapter @{"Introduction" LINK PART_01}, this Door is a SIM\nmodule. The script must be called when a user is signing off, e.g. if\nhe/she is running in node 1, then you must have ''LOGOFF1.INFO'' in your\nSYSCmd Drawer.\n\nLOCATION=<filename>             - This tooltype specifies where the script\n                                  is located.\n                                  Eg. LOCATION=BBS:Node1/Logoff.script\n\nMULTINODE=<YES|NO>              - This tooltype specifies if the Door may\n                                  started in different nodes.\n                                  Eg. MULTINODE=YES\n\nPRIORITY=<n>                    - This tooltype specifies the AmigaDos\n                                  priority when the Door is executed.\n                                  Eg. PRIORITY=2\n\nSTACK=<n>                       - This tooltype specifies the Door stack.\n                                  Eg. STACK=8096\n\nTYPE=<AIM|SIM|TIM|XIM>          - This tooltype specifies the Door-type.\n                                  This Door is a script so TYPE=SIM\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_04_SC "The LogOff script"\n\nThe script file is needed, coz here you can tell which batch jobs you want\nto run. In this case you are only interested in the last callers, so you\nmake in file LOGOFF.SCRIPT in your NODE<num> Drawer. It look likes the\nfollowing example:\n\n^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^CUT HERE ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\nDoors:MDB-LastCallers/MDB-LastCallers\n^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^CUT HERE ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n\nAnd then you have to change the attribute bytes of this script:\n SET THE S BIT FOR SCRIPT with Dopus or with C:PROTECT\nDO NOT FORGET THIS ONE, ELSE IT WON''T WORK!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_05 "Changes"\n\n1.6  (03 Jun 1994)\n  - Some coding enhanced.\n\n0.05 (01 Mrt 1994)\n - SIM module instead of real XIM.\n\n0.04 (27 Feb 1994)\n - Icon based.\n\n0.03 (?? ???? 1004)\n - Should run on all processors now.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ADVERT "Death Simple ... OTM The GraveDiggers"\n\n/X 3.3+    :+                   WELCOME TO                            /X 3.3+\n          .::.       ____________  ______________._          .+.\n         .:+.       |__  \  ____/ / _ \      _/  | \         .:.\n   AscII  +::+.     |  \  \  .)\_/     \/   | |  |  \       ::+.    AscII\n \  B Y  /   :.     |  /   \ |  |   :   \   | |  _   \     :+:.  \   B Y   /\n _\ MSW /_          |______/\___|\__|___/\__| |__|___/     .     _\  MSW  /_ \n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-         -=-            -=-=-=-=-             -=-=-=-=-=--=-=-\n.°*DEATH                                                             DEATH*°.\n   SIMPLE*°.                                                      .°*SIMPLE\n=-=-=-               -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-            -=-=-          -=-=-=   -=-=-\n                ___/\____/\  __ _/\  /\_____/\__      /\____\n-24 HoUrS      /     \____/ /  Y   \/___  _ \  |     /  .  |    ..::.\n-chataBle     /   ___/    \/   :    \  / ___/  |__  /   |__|     +::.+\n-SysOp        \___   \____ \___ ____ \/  |\  __|  \/_    __/   .+::+\n-CeWl Area''s  /   \__/    \/   Y    \/\__| \/      \ \__/  \   .:\n              \  ___/\____/\___|__  /__  |  \______ \____  /\n               \/                 \/   \/          \/    \/ +31-(0)2152-68786\n\n    __/\__ __ ___ _ _ _   :-)   2 OPERATOR 2  (-:      ___ __ __ __/\__\n    \ Oo /__ ______ _ _       ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~          __ __ __\ oO /\n    /_--_\__ ___ __ __       2-)  COSYSOP  (-2        __ ____ _ _/_--_\\n      \/                                                           \/\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),'{"LOCATION":"<filename>","PRIORITY":"<n>","STACK":"<n>","TYPE":"<AIM|SIM|TIM|XIM>"}','auto-added',17027,7,0,NULL,NULL,'mdb_lc16','scan',1780048589);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mdb_zs10','MDB-ZS10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MDB-ZS10.LHA','MDB-Search','XIM','LE-win5-96.exe',NULL,NULL,'MDB','|  _____/\   ______/\  _____/\  (c) 1994   | | /  / \  \  \  ___  \ \  ___ \ PRoDuCTioNS| |/  /\_/\  \ /\/| /  / /\/ /  /            |',replace('.------------------------------------------.\n|  _____/\   ______/\  _____/\  (c) 1994   |\n| /  / \  \  \  ___  \ \  ___ \ PRoDuCTioNS|\n|/  /\_/\  \ /\/| /  / /\/ /  /            |\n|\  \   /  //   |/  / /  |/   \ 100% PuRe  |\n| \__\ /__/ \______/  \__|____/ XiM /X DooR|\n|                                          |\n| $VER: Zippy Search 1.0 (29-May-1994)     |\n| Scans all conferences like ConferenceScan|\n|                                          |\n|  MDB PRoDuCTioNS * NiGHTCRaWLER * ViDuR  |\n`------------------------------------------''\nWHOOOMMMP THERE iT iS - MEN-TEL 4 PReSiDENT!\n','\n',char(10)),'ZippySearch.GUIDE',replace('	@database MDB-ZippySearch 1.0\n\nCopyright (C) 1994 (MDB Productions)\nAll Rights Reserved\n\n@Remark $VER: Version V1.0 (29 May 1994)\n@Remark AmigaGuide database for the ZippySearch 1.0\n\n@node MAIN "MDB-ZippySearch 1.0 AmigaGuide Document (C) 1994 (MDB Productions)"\n\n                         _____/\   ______/\  _____/\ \n                        /  / \  \  \  ___  \ \  ___ \\n                       /  /\_/\  \ /\/| /  / /\/ /  /\n                       \  \   /  //   |/  / /  |/   \\n                        \__\ /  / \___   /  \__|_   /\n                             \_/      \_/        \_/ \n\n                   MDB Productions  iS PRouD To PReSeNT :\n\n                      Z I P P Y - S E A R C H E R 1.0\n\n          ·:·C·O·N·T·E·N·T·S··O·F··D·O·C·U·M·E·N·T·A·T·I·O·N·:·\n\n                             @{"  INTRODUCTION  " LINK PART_01}\n                             @{"  REQUIREMENTS  " LINK PART_02}\n                             @{"  INSTALLATION  " LINK PART_03}\n                             @{"   TOOL-TYPES   " LINK PART_04}\n                             @{"    COMMANDS    " LINK PART_05}\n                             @{"    CHANGES!    " LINK PART_06}\n                             @{"     ADVERT     " LINK PART_07}\n                             @{"      HELP      " LINK PART_08}\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_01 "Introduction"\n\nSometimes it is hard to find a file in a BBS, especially if there are\nmany conferences. All ZippySearches that I have found only scans the\nconference you are joined. There I decided to code a new ZippySearcher\nthat actually scans all conferences you have access to.\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_02 "Requirements"\n\nWhat U need to run it...\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n - an Amigamodel (A500/A600/A1200/A2000/A3000/A4000) with Kickstart 2.04++\n\n - the installed /X-Software (V3.20+) in the drawer BBS:\n\nNow let''s go on by explaining the @{"Installation" LINK PART_03}...\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_03 "Installation for ZippySearcher 1.0"\n\nHow to install it to your /X-System...\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nFirst make a Drawer into Doors: called ''MDB-Search'' and copy the Files\n - ''MDB-Search''\n - ''MDB-Search.INFO''\ninto it.\n\nSecond copy the Icon ''Z.INFO'' into the BBSCmd Drawer.\n\nThats all there is. Simple he!\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_04 "ToolTypes for ZippySearcher 1.0"\n\n                                ToolTypes\n                                ~~~~~~~~~\n\n                    @{" TOOLTYPES FOR MDB-Search 1.0" LINK PART_04_LC}\n\n                    @{" TOOLTYPES FOR Z             " LINK PART_04_LO}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_04_LC "ToolTypes for MDB-Search 1.0\n\n                 ToolTypes for MDB-Search 1.0\n                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nActually there no tooltypes, perhaps in feature releases.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_04_LO "ToolTypes For Z"\n\n                       ToolTypes for Z\n                       ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nACCESS=<acs.level>              - This tooltype specifies the access level\n                                  that the user must have to run the door.\n                                  Eg. ACCESS=10\n\nLOCATION=<filename>             - This tooltype specifies where the Door\n                                  is located.\n                                  LOCATION=Doors:MDB-Search/MDB-Search\n                                  !!! DO NOT CHANGE THIS ONE !!!\n\nMULTINODE=<YES|NO>              - This tooltype specifies if the Door may\n                                  started in different nodes.\n                                  Eg. MULTINODE=YES\n\nPRIORITY=<num>                  - This tooltype specifies the AmigaDos\n                                  priority when the Door is executed.\n                                  Eg. PRIORITY=2\n\nSTACK=<size>                    - This tooltype specifies the Door stack.\n                                  Eg. STACK=8096\n\nTYPE=<AIM|SIM|TIM|XIM>          - This tooltype specifies the Door-type.\n                                  This Door is written in 100% pure\n                                  Assembly so TYPE=XIM\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_05 "Commands"\n\nStart the door by useing the Z-command, and will get the main menu.\n\n@{" S "} Toggles between ''All conferences'' and ''Current conference''\n    to scan.\n\n@{" D "} Toggles between ''All dirs'' and ''Upload dirs only'' to scan.\n\n@{" Z "} Enter the string you like to find. Okay, its not case sensitive.\n\n@{" G "} Go searching the string.\n\n@{" A "} Shows some litte information about the authors.\n\n@{" Q "} Don''t try.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_06 "Changes"\n\n1.0 (29 May 1994)\n    - First release.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_07 "Death Simple ... OTM The GraveDiggers"\n\n/X 3.3+    :+                   WELCOME TO                            /X 3.3+\n          .::.       ____________  ______________._          .+.\n         .:+.       |__  \  ____/ / _ \      _/  | \         .:.\n   AscII  +::+.     |  \  \  .)\_/     \/   | |  |  \       ::+.    AscII\n \  B Y  /   :.     |  /   \ |  |   :   \   | |  _   \     :+:.  \   B Y   /\n _\ MSW /_          |______/\___|\__|___/\__| |__|___/     .     _\  MSW  /_ \n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-         -=-            -=-=-=-=-             -=-=-=-=-=--=-=-\n.°*DEATH                                                             DEATH*°.\n   SIMPLE*°.                                                      .°*SIMPLE\n=-=-=-               -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-            -=-=-          -=-=-=   -=-=-\n                ___/\____/\  __ _/\  /\_____/\__      /\____\n-24 HoUrS      /     \____/ /  Y   \/___  _ \  |     /  .  |    ..::.\n-chataBle     /   ___/    \/   :    \  / ___/  |__  /   |__|     +::.+\n-SysOp        \___   \____ \___ ____ \/  |\  __|  \/_    __/   .+::+\n-CeWl Area''s  /   \__/    \/   Y    \/\__| \/      \ \__/  \   .:\n              \  ___/\____/\___|__  /__  |  \______ \____  /\n               \/                 \/   \/          \/    \/ +31-(0)2152-68786\n\n    __/\__ __ ___ _ _ _   :-)   2 OPERATOR 2  (-:      ___ __ __ __/\__\n    \ Oo /__ ______ _ _       ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~          __ __ __\ oO /\n    /_--_\__ ___ __ __       2-)  COSYSOP  (-2        __ ____ _ _/_--_\\n      \/                                                           \/\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_08 "Help me please"\nCan somebody help me with the following feature:\nI like to implent a break-option useing CTRL-C keys. But how can I prog\nthis feature in assembler??? If you now how, please contact me and tell\nme how to do it, or better give me a some source coding?\n\nContact me directy:\n   MDB Productions\n   PWA-park 93\n   3905 CC  Veenendaal\n   The Netherlands\n   +31-(0)8385-29239\n\nOr leave a messy at our board\n   Death Simple\n   +31-(0)2152-68786\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),'{"ACCESS":"<acs.level>","LOCATION":"<filename>","PRIORITY":"<num>","STACK":"<size>","TYPE":"<AIM|SIM|TIM|XIM>"}','auto-added',17690,7,0,NULL,NULL,'mdb_zs10','scan',1780048589);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mdb_zs12','MDB-ZS12.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MDB-ZS12.LHA','MDB-Search','XIM','MDB-Search',NULL,NULL,'MDB','|  _____/\   ______/\  _____/\  (c) 1994   | | /  / \  \  \  ___  \ \  ___ \ PRoDuCTioNS| |/  /\_/\  \ /\/| /  / /\/ /  /            |',replace('.------------------------------------------.\n|  _____/\   ______/\  _____/\  (c) 1994   |\n| /  / \  \  \  ___  \ \  ___ \ PRoDuCTioNS|\n|/  /\_/\  \ /\/| /  / /\/ /  /            |\n|\  \   /  //   |/  / /  |/   \ 100% PuRe  |\n| \__\ /__/ \______/  \__|____/ XiM /X DooR|\n|                                          |\n| $VER: Zippy Search 1.2 (02-Jun-1994)     |\n| Scans all conferences like ConferenceScan|\n|                                          |\n|  MDB PRoDuCTioNS * NiGHTCRaWLER * ViDuR  |\n`------------------------------------------''\n[04-02-96]=diGiTAL^HAREm=[fTP&33.6k]-[03:19]\n','\n',char(10)),'reference-board.txt',replace(replace('              W h e r e   t h e   w a r e z   c o m e   f r o m\r\n                                               __                /\_____:\r\n__/\__________________________________________|  \______________/  \    |__\r\n\_   ___________  _______ ________  \__   ___ |   _______  _______  \_  l  \\r\n__\____  \    _l   \    |  \     |___/     |  !    \   _l   \   _| __/\____ \_\r\n\_____    \___\     \___|   \___ !   \__   |_____   \__\     \__\    \____   /\r\n -mNT\_____/---\_____/--l____/-\______/\   |----\____/--\_____/--\____/--\__/\r\n                                        \__|\r\n\r\n- -- --> F A i R L i G H T   S W E D i S H   H E A D Q U A R T E R S <-- -- -\r\n\r\n           reference-board is back 2017 after more than 20 years in coma!\r\n\r\n                        Running on AmiExpress TelNet\r\n\r\n                    Connect to: reference-board.zapto.org:1541\r\n\r\n                    or: www.brysk.se/reference-board/index.htm\r\n               \n              UPLOAD DATE: 11-30-18  TIME: 13:15:52  ON NODE: 0\n','\r',char(13)),'\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',15475,7,0,NULL,NULL,'mdb_zs12','scan',1780048589);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mdbcu113','MDBCU113.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MDBCU113.LHA','MDB-ConfUpdater','XIM','DMSDescript',NULL,NULL,NULL,'|  _____/\   ______/\  _____/\  (c) 1994   | | /  / \  \  \  ___  \ \  ___ \ PRoDuCTioNS| |/  /\_/\  \ /\/| /  / /\/ /  /            |',replace('.------------------------------------------.\n|  _____/\   ______/\  _____/\  (c) 1994   |\n| /  / \  \  \  ___  \ \  ___ \ PRoDuCTioNS|\n|/  /\_/\  \ /\/| /  / /\/ /  /            |\n|\  \   /  //   |/  / /  |/   \ 100% PuRe  |\n| \__\ /__/ \______/  \__|____/ XiM /X DooR|\n|                                          |\n| $VER:ConferenceUpdater 1.13 (12-Jun-1994)|\n|                                          |\n|  MDB PRoDuCTioNS * NiGHTCRaWLER * ViDuR  |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'ConfUpdater.GUIDE',replace('@database MDB-ConferenceUpdater 1.13\n\nCopyright (C) 1994 (MDB Productions)\nAll Rights Reserved\n\n@Remark $VER: Version V1.13 (12-Jun-1994)\n@Remark AmigaGuide database for the ConferenceUpdater 1.13\n\n@node MAIN "MDB-ConferenceUpdater 1.13 AmigaGuide Document (C) 1994 (MDB Productions)"\n\n                         _____/\   ______/\  _____/\ \n                        /  / \  \  \  ___  \ \  ___ \\n                       /  /\_/\  \ /\/| /  / /\/ /  /\n                       \  \   /  //   |/  / /  |/   \\n                        \__\ /  / \___   /  \__|_   /\n                             \_/      \_/        \_/ \n\n                   MDB Productions  iS PRouD To PReSeNT :\n\n                  C O N F E R E N C E - U P D A T E R 1.13\n\n          ·:·C·O·N·T·E·N·T·S··O·F··D·O·C·U·M·E·N·T·A·T·I·O·N·:·\n\n                             @{"  INTRODUCTION  " LINK PART_01}\n                             @{"  REQUIREMENTS  " LINK PART_02}\n                             @{"  INSTALLATION  " LINK PART_03}\n                             @{"   TOOL-TYPES   " LINK PART_04}\n                             @{"    COMMANDS    " LINK PART_05}\n                             @{"    CHANGES!    " LINK PART_06}\n                             @{"     ADVERT     " LINK PART_07}\n                             @{"      HELP      " LINK PART_08}\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_01 "Introduction"\n\nFor sysops it''s hard to keep their conferences up to date. This door\nchecks if the files stated in the catalogs still exist. If they don''t\nexists anymore, the filesize in the catalog will be changed to a text\nlike ''OFFLINE'', ''DELETED'' or something simular.\n\nThe door is very smart, so the less installation you have to do. It\nchecks the following icons BBS:CONFCONFIG and CONF<num>. Lets enjoy\nthis one.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_02 "Requirements"\n\nWhat U need to run it...\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n - an Amigamodel (A500/A600/A1200/A2000/A3000/A4000) with Kickstart 2.04++\n\n - the installed /X-Software (V3.20+) in the drawer BBS:\n\nNow let''s go on by explaining the @{"Installation" LINK PART_03}...\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_03 "Installation for ConfUpdater 1.13"\n\nHow to install it to your /X-System...\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nFirst make a Drawer into Doors: called ''MDB-ConfUpdater'' and copy the Files\n - ''MDB-ConfUpdater''\n - ''MDB-ConfUpdater.INFO''\ninto it.\n\nSecond copy the Icon ''CU.INFO'' into the BBSCmd Drawer.\n\nLast bu not least you have to copy some tools into the C Drawer, coz\nthe insert-option need them to extract the FILE_ID.DIZ. These files are:\n - ''DMSDescript''\n - ''EXEDescript''\n - ''TxtExtract''\n\nThats all there is. Simple he!\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_04 "ToolTypes for ConfUpdater 1.13"\n\n                                ToolTypes\n                                ~~~~~~~~~\n\n                    @{" TOOLTYPES FOR MDB-ConfUpdater 1.13" LINK PART_04_LC}\n\n                    @{" TOOLTYPES FOR CU                  " LINK PART_04_LO}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_04_LC "ToolTypes for MDB-ConfUpdater 1.13\n\n                 ToolTypes for MDB-ConfUpdater 1.13\n                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nDELETE.num=<string>             - The DELETE.num tooltype specifies the text\n                                  that will be passed to your catalogs. The\n                                  maximum string length is 8 characters. Do\n                                  not overide this one. The maximum of\n                                  DELETE.num is 9.\n                                  Eg. DELETE.1=OFFLINE\n\nDESTINATION=<path>              - This tooltype specifies where the DIR<num>\n                                  catalogs will be stored. It is a backup-\n                                  mechanism, so you have to move them your\n                                  self to active them. The catalogs will be\n                                  be stored as CONF<num>_DIR<num>. The path\n                                  must end with a '':'' or a ''/'' like:\n                                  DESTINATION=RAM: or\n                                  DESTINATION=Work:Tmp/\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_04_LO "ToolTypes For CU"\n\n                       ToolTypes for CU\n                       ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nACCESS=<acs.level>              - This tooltype specifies the access level\n                                  that the user must have to run the door.\n                                  Eg. ACCESS=200\n\nLOCATION=<filename>             - This tooltype specifies where the Door\n                                  is located.\n                                  LOCATION=Doors:MDB-ConfUpdater/MDB-ConfUpdater\n                                  !!! DO NOT CHANGE THIS ONE !!!\n\nMULTINODE=<YES|NO>              - This tooltype specifies if the Door may\n                                  started in different nodes.\n                                  Eg. MULTINODE=YES\n\nPRIORITY=<num>                  - This tooltype specifies the AmigaDos\n                                  priority when the Door is executed.\n                                  Eg. PRIORITY=2\n\nSTACK=<size>                    - This tooltype specifies the Door stack.\n                                  Eg. STACK=8096\n\nTYPE=<AIM|SIM|TIM|XIM>          - This tooltype specifies the Door-type.\n                                  This Door is written in 100% pure\n                                  Assembly so TYPE=XIM\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_05 "Commands"\n\nStart the door by useing the CU-command, and will get the main menu.\n\n@{" A "} Shows some litte information about the authors.\n\n@{" D "} In a conference you can use different DIRs. The maximum is\n    stated in the CONF<num> icon in the tooltype NDIRS. By \n    startup this value will be used as working DIR. This option\n    allows you to change the dirnumber you are working with.\n\n@{" U "} THE CONFERENCE UPDATE. This one scans your current dir (as\n    mentions with option D). If a entry in your dir doesn''t\n    exists anymore, a action will take place:\n       1. change the filesize in a message like ''DELETED''\n       2. delete the entry.\n    Which one will depant of your option (1-0).\n\n@{" Q "} Don''t try.\n\n@{" I "} This one scans all your update dirs. If there is a file \n    which is not present in the current dir, the file will\n    be added to this dir.\n\n@{" V "} A previously processed dir can be viewed with this option.\n\n@{" B "} We always say, safety first. Therefore an updated dir is\n    placed in a directory according the DESTINATION tooltype.\n    But if you want, you can the bring the processed dir only.\n    Safety first, so a backup will be made of your actual dir\n    in the bbs.\n\n@{" S "} Sorts the dir by date, filename.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_06 "Changes"\n\n1.13 (12-Jun-1993(\n    - New version number introduced, coz of the many releases.\n    - Dir-viewer enhanced.\n    - Now scans 9 conferences in stead of only 4. Coz my bbs\n      has only 4 confs, I never discovered it!\n    - Buf fixed. In some cases an updated dir wasn''t closed, now\n      it does (I think).\n    - Endmessages adapted for all cases: insert, update and delete.\n\n1.9 (05-Jun-1994)\n    - The dir can now be sorted! It''s even possible to make all\n      files with current date; nice for the ''N S U'' command.\n      Be aware for look a likes, I just saw one from noCtyre/Mystic!!!\n    - Dir viewer works remote now!\n\n1.8 (02-Jun-1994)\n    - All functions recognise the Exorcist commands! Nice he!\n      Thanxs to RubiX from TFA for mentioning.\n\n1.7 (02-Jun-1994)\n    - Viewer changed, now it uses de DT_LINELENGTH function and\n      correctly displays the text options in stead of the filesize\n      (the last char wasn''t displayed).\n\n1.6 (29-May-1994)\n    - Some maincoding changes, faster and better!\n    - The DIRs will be re-read after each DLPATH is scanned by\n      the Insert-option. No duplicate entries any more!\n    - Now the door uses the online BBS dir by the Insert-option\n      if you answer is NO to the question if you like to use the\n      previously processed dir.\n    - Handles empty dirs (0 bytes or doesn''t exist) correcty by\n      the Insert-option.\n\n1.5 (20-May-1994)\n    - Scans download directories 1 to 9 and insert new files to\n      the DIR.\n    - View the processed dir.\n    - Brings the processed dir online.\n    - Default startup for directory changed from DIR1 to NDIRS as\n      stated in CONF<num>.INFO\n    - Delete an entry in the dir if the file doesn''t exists.\n    - A lot more, I already forgot them.\n\n1.4 (16-May-1994) Never released\n    \n1.3 (16-Mar-1994)\n    - Faster screenhandling.\n    - New action available, directory occurences will be deleted when\n      the file is not available.\n\n1.2 (14-Mar-1994)\n    - Returncode $a removed. This value meant LINE DOWN in stead\n      of NEW LINE in ANSI-codes.\n\n1.1 (13-Mar-1994) \n    - The term ''catalog'' changed to ''dir'' for better understanding\n      for some persons.\n    - Using ANSI-codes instead of CSI-codes. The screens must work\n      remote now!\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_07 "Death Simple ... OTM The GraveDiggers"\n\n/X 3.3+    :+                   WELCOME TO                            /X 3.3+\n          .::.       ____________  ______________._          .+.\n         .:+.       |__  \  ____/ / _ \      _/  | \         .:.\n   AscII  +::+.     |  \  \  .)\_/     \/   | |  |  \       ::+.    AscII\n \  B Y  /   :.     |  /   \ |  |   :   \   | |  _   \     :+:.  \   B Y   /\n _\ MSW /_          |______/\___|\__|___/\__| |__|___/     .     _\  MSW  /_ \n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-         -=-            -=-=-=-=-             -=-=-=-=-=--=-=-\n.°*DEATH                                                             DEATH*°.\n   SIMPLE*°.                                                      .°*SIMPLE\n=-=-=-               -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-            -=-=-          -=-=-=   -=-=-\n                ___/\____/\  __ _/\  /\_____/\__      /\____\n-24 HoUrS      /     \____/ /  Y   \/___  _ \  |     /  .  |    ..::.\n-chataBle     /   ___/    \/   :    \  / ___/  |__  /   |__|     +::.+\n-SysOp        \___   \____ \___ ____ \/  |\  __|  \/_    __/   .+::+\n-CeWl Area''s  /   \__/    \/   Y    \/\__| \/      \ \__/  \   .:\n              \  ___/\____/\___|__  /__  |  \______ \____  /\n               \/                 \/   \/          \/    \/ +31-(0)2152-68786\n\n    __/\__ __ ___ _ _ _   :-)   2 OPERATOR 2  (-:      ___ __ __ __/\__\n    \ Oo /__ ______ _ _       ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~          __ __ __\ oO /\n    /_--_\__ ___ __ __       2-)  COSYSOP  (-2        __ ____ _ _/_--_\\n      \/                                                           \/\n\n@endnode\n\n@node PART_08 "Help me please"\nCan somebody help me with the following feature:\nI like to implent a break-option useing CTRL-C keys. But how can I prog\nthis feature in assembler??? If you now how, please contact me and tell\nme how to do it, or better give me a some source coding?\n\nContact me directy:\n   MDB Productions\n   PWA-park 93\n   3905 CC  Veenendaal\n   The Netherlands\n   +31-(0)8385-29239\n\nOr leave a messy at our board\n   Death Simple\n   +31-(0)2152-68786\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),'{"ACCESS":"<acs.level>","LOCATION":"<filename>","PRIORITY":"<num>","STACK":"<size>","TYPE":"<AIM|SIM|TIM|XIM>"}','auto-added',43017,2,0,NULL,NULL,'mdbcu113','scan',1780048589);
