INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mgs_log','MGS-LOG.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MGS-LOG.LHA','log-shrink','XIM','log-shrink',NULL,NULL,'MGS','____\        /___\   ____  /____/ ___/______ _     \l      _  \_______ ____\/       __l_________  __l__       l ___',replace('    __________   ___________     _____\n____\        /___\   ____  /____/ ___/______\n               _     \l      _  \_______\n____\/       __l_________  __l__       l ___\ng®m /________)   e^D \_____)   (_________)\n          «« m e g a s t y l e  »»\n               ...presents...\n \n              Log-Shrink v1.o!\n \nThe best way to shorten down your HUGE logs!\n','\n',char(10)),'Log-Shrink.GUIDE',replace('@database "mEGAZTYLE.guide"\n@node MAIN\n@title "                                              »«  m e g a s t y l e  »«  r u l e s  »«"\n@{b}\n                              @{u}m e g a s t y l e@{uu}\n\n                 ________   _________   _________     ______.\n           ______\      /___\  ___  /___\  ___  /_____\____ l____\n     ______\              _     l/    _    \l     _     __/     /_______\n.___(       \____\/     __l__  _______l_______  __l__   \l_____/        )___.\n|                /______)   (_____/        \____)   (____\                  |\n|                                                                           |\n| g®m      _____      ___.           .______   ___.       _________     e^D |\n|___  ____/ ___/______\  l___________|     /___\ _l_______\  ___  /____  ___|\n   (__\   \______   _    __/     _   l       _   \      _     l/      /__)\n       \__      l __l__  l     __l_______  __l_        _l_  _________/\n         (________)   (________)     \_____)  (________) (_____/ @{ub}\n\n\n\n@{fg shine}                  p r e s e n t s   a   n e w   d o o r :@{fg text}\n\n\n                @{b}    @{bg shine}@{u}  L o g - S h r i n k   1 . o  @{bg back}@{ub}@{uu}\n\n\n\n\n              @{"           d o c u m e n t a t i o n           " link index}\n\n\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node index\n@title "                                             »» i n d e x ««"\n\n\n    @{u}                                                          @{uu}\n\n\n@{b}                                                               ½½½½½  ½½½½½\n                                                               ½½½½½  ½½½½½\n                                                               ½½½½½  ½½½½½\n                                                               ½½½½½  ½½½½½\n                                                               ½½½½½  ½½½½½\n         ____        __________          ____.   ___________   ½½½½½  ½½½½½\n________(___/________\ __     /__________\___l___\  ____   /__    `½½½½''\n                   _   l/       _      _____/  _      l/      ½½½½½½  ½½½½½½\n_____            __l___/      __l__    l     __l__  __________½½½½½½  ½½½½½½\n    (____________)    /_______)   (__________)   (_____/      ½½½½½½  ½½½½½½\n                                                              ½½½½½½  ½½½½½½\n                                                              ½½½½½½  ½½½½½½\n   @{fg shine} @{"            introduction             "  link introduction      }    @{fg text}                ½½½½½½  ½½½½½½\n@{fg shine}    @{"            installation             "  link installation      }          @{fg text}          ½½½½½½  ½½½½½½\n@{fg shine}    @{"              how 2 use              "  link how 2 use         }\n    @{"              copyright              "  link copyright         }\n    @{"          changes ÷ history          " link changes ÷ history  } @{ub} @{fg text}\n\n\n    @{u}                                                          @{uu}\n\n\n@endnode\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n@node introduction\n                                                                 .\n\n                                                                 :\n                                                                 :\n             __________________.______.      ________            :\n          ._(___)_.   ___     _|      l_____\\_     /____________:_ _\n          |       |----/      \        /     \   __/\      __    :\n          l_______|   /_______/        |-----/_______\____       :\n                              l________|(rLf)            /-------:-\n                                                                 :\n                                                                 :\n                                                                 :\n                                                                 .\n\n\nEver discovered that some of the applications you''re using just seems to append\nand append and append to the log-files without erasing the old data?\n\nWell, I just noticed that my AmiExpress Callerslog was over 2MB long once, and\ndecided to make a utility that could keep the length of that particular file\ndown to a resonable level without loosing any important data.\n\nI then started to code on this little program that can be used on any log-file\nin text-format generated by any application for the Amiga. My main goal was to\nmake a fast and system-friendly door, which I could trust wouldn''t screw up my\nsystem totally.\n\n\nThis door does that, it reduce the length of any (text-)file to a desired\namount of bytes, from within the file till the end of the file.\n\nThis way you won''t lose the last entries in the file, and discard the old \nentries on the top of the file.\n\n\n\n                                 Enjoy it! :)\n\n\n\n           - - - --- ------[ lizard of megastyle! ]------ --- - -  -\n\n\n     This program should be 100% systemfriendly coded. If any error should\n    occure, then the program should managed to shutdown without causing any\n                             damage to the system.\n\n\n\n\n@endnode\n\n\n\n\n\n\n@node installation\n\n .\n                                                                              .\n :\n :                                                                            :\n : __        _____ .___.   ______ __.              _________. ____________    :\n_:(__)_______\_ _/_|_  l___\__  // _l______.  _____\__  //  l____)_  _   /____:_\n :    | __    /_  _ /   /     _ // \     /_l__\__     _ //   /    |_    / ___ :\n_:____|--/   /-/  //    |--/____/----/__/ \     /--/____/    |____|/---/\--/  :\n :      /___/ /___/_____|(rLf)          \---/__/       l_____|            /___:_\n :                                                                            :\n :                        i n s t a l l a t i o n                             :\n .                                                                            :\n                                                                              .\n\n @{fg shine}To install...@{fg text}\n\n\n\n All you have to do is to copy the main executable file in this archive to\n whatever directory you wish. I would advice SYS:C/.\n\n\n Also, if you wish to use it together with AmiExpress v3.x+, then you should\n write a command-line into your logoff-script for each node.\n\n\n That''s all... (Simple isn''t it? :)\n\n\n\n\n Functionality :\n\n\n   Log-shrink <Path+Filename> <Size>\n\n   <Path+Filename> is the source-file to be shrinked.\n   <Size> is a number in bytes to dedicate how big the logfile should be...\n\n\n\n If there is spaces in the filename, use "''s marks to indicate start and the end\n of the complete path+filename.\n\n\n\n Remember : This shrinker will cut from within the file -> end of file. \n            So... You won''t miss your last entries in the file. :)\n\n\n@endnode\n\n\n\n\n\n@node how 2 use\n@title "                                              )>» h o w  2  u s e «<("\n\n                                      ½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½½.\n                                     ½½½½½½½½         ½½½½½½½½\n      ____.            _________         _______      ½½½½½½½½\n   ___\ __l____________\       /_________\     /______½½½½½½½½\n   \    \___        _             _  