INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mgs_nst','MGS-NST.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MGS-NST.LHA','node-status','XIM','node-status',NULL,NULL,'MGS','_\_/    / _  __  ______ _______/__  ___    / | _ \  /     /  __/__/   /_ _   /   ___   / |__\ \/ /___/_____________/____/____//___/',replace(' ___     _______________________ _ _________\n_\_/    / _  __  ______ _______/__  ___    /\n| _ \  /     /  __/__/   /_ _   /   ___   /\n|__\ \/ /___/_____________/____/____//___/\n    \  /                   .------------.\n     \/  Node-Status v1.2 -÷-  styLE!   ¡\n                           `------------÷\nNice /X-door to report your BBS-activity|\nat logon. Good configurations options.  |\n -[31.O5.95]------ ---- ---------·LZD·--''\n','\n',char(10)),'_Node-Status.guide',replace('@database "Node-Status.Guide"\n@WIDTH 77\n@INDEX "MAIN"\n@NODE Main "MAIN" "Welcome to the Node-Status Documentation!"\n                                                   __.       \n______ ______________ ______ ________    _________/ _|_____/\______ _ __________\n ____ V _________   // ____/_______  \  _\  ______   _  __/  \  __/_________   /\n |   \_/   |   _/  //  \___  |   _/   \/  \___   \   |___     \ \      /  _/  /\n |    |    |  ____/_     |   |   _     /    _/   /   |   \    /  \_   /  ____/_\n |____|    |_______/_________:___\    /_________/____|_______/_______/________/\n      |____|                      \  /                       \n      :   _____                    \/\n           ____\__________\n            ____\_______  )\n                 \/     ) ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                        ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯ ·g·i·v·e·s·  ·y·o·u·\n\n                                                   \n                        .-------------- -       - ---.\n                        |                          ¯7|\n                        |                            :\n                        :      NODE-STATUS v1.1      .\n                        ·\n                        ·             by\n                                                     ·\n                        ·  Magnar Harestad (Lizard)  :\n                        :·                           |\n                        |l_                          |\n                        `----- -       - ------------''\n\n\n                            Release date : 31.05.95\n\n                       @{"What is Node-Status v1.0?       " LINK "ABOUT"}   \n                       @{"Requirements to run this door   " LINK "REQUIRE"}   \n                       @{"How to install Node-Status...   " LINK "INSTALL"}   \n                       @{"Who''s done what ?               " LINK "CREDITS"}   \n                       @{"The official mGs-Greetings!     " LINK "GREETINGS"}   \n                       @{"Info about MegaStyle.           " LINK "INFO"}   \n                       @{"How to contact MEGASTyLE!       " LINK "CONTACT"}\n@ENDNODE\n\n\n\n;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\n@NODE "ABOUT" "What is Node-Status ?"\n                                                               @{" Go back.. " Link MAIN}\n\nNode-status v1.0 is a small utility to show which node you''re logged onto.\nIt also report the baudrate of the connection and the current status on each\nof the other available nodes.\n\nNode-Status can also be used to display a logo-textfile (with MCI-support)\nto the users together with the node-status report.\n\n\nThe main reason why I coded this door is that most of the doors available lacks\na good design, and do not have any textfile support.\n\nI also included a Clear-Screen argument for those who wants to get rid of that\n"modem-report" message from AmiExpress at the top of the screen.\n\n\nThe door is also in my opinion more powerful than other doors available. \nFirst of all, it has a very nice tool-type support. This is very important when\nyou want a correct node baudrate directly out from each individual node-icon. \nNo incorrect-status from the /X-port is being used for this purpose. \n\n\n\nFinally,\n\n\nThis utility is coded in Amiga-E with inline-ASM for maximal speed-performance!\n@ENDNODE\n\n\n\n;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\n@NODE "REQUIRE" "Requirements to run this door."\n                                                               @{" Go back.. " Link MAIN}\n\n\nYou will need a computer with OS 2.x, or higher, and any version of AmiExpress.\nHowever, AmiExpress v4.xx++ is preferred.\n\n\nNode-Status also requires the AEDoor.Library present in LIBS:. You can find this\nlibrary in the LIBS-directory in this package.\n\nIf this library is not present for some reason in this package, then give my\nboard a call and I''ll gladly give it to you.\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n\n\n;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\n@NODE "INSTALL" "How to do the installation..."\n                                                               @{" Go back.. " Link MAIN}\n\nAll you have to do is to copy each of the files in this archive to its\nbelonging directory under "BBS:".\n\nThat''s all... (Simple isn''t it? :)\n\n\n\nConfiguration :\n---------------\n\nThere is only one way to configurate this door, and that is through the\nNode-Status.info icon. If you, from workbench, use information on this icon,\nyou''ll see two Tooltype choices in use. These are : \n\n\nCLEAR_SCREEN=YES\nSHOW_LOGO=YES\n\n\nThese choices can be toggled by writing YES or NO. (Not case-sensitive)\n\n\nThe first one will clear the screen right after the modem-handshake is over,\nand the second one will show the textfile : "Node-status.Logo".\n\n\n* The logo-textfile must be placed in the same directory as the main-program.\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n\n\n;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\n@NODE "CREDITS" "Credits for this MEGASTYLE production:"\n                                                               @{" Go back.. " Link MAIN}\n\n\n                             The credits goes to :\n                            «=-------------------=»\n\n\n\n             Magnar Harestad, Lizard of Megastyle and Spaceballs!\n\n\n\n\n                        For doing the following things:\n                       «-------------------------------»\n\n                                    Coding\n                                   Designing\n                                 ANSI-Drawning\n                                Guide-Designing\n                             AsC²-art and designs\n                            Writing this guide-text\n\n\n\n\n(Splash, it seems like you''re not the only one doing everything by yourself! :)\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n\n\n;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\n@NODE "GREETINGS" "The Official MeGaSTyLe GrEeTiNgS:"\n                                                               @{" Go back.. " Link MAIN}\n\n   _________ \n    _______ )  ·M·e·g·a·S·t·y·l·e·  ·s·e·n·d·s·  ·g·r·e·e·t·i·n·g·  ·t·o·\n           )¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n           ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n\n    Spaceballs, Eltech, Andromeda, CNCD, Parallax, Complex, Virtual dreams,\nStone Arts, Rebels, TRSI, Scoopex, Avalon, Aquarious, Access, Prestige, Skid Row\n\n                   And to all the other /X-coders out there!\n\n\n________ \n ______ ) ·L·i·z·a·r·d·  ·s·e·n·d·s·  ·s·p·e·c·i·a·l·  ·g·r·e·e·t·i·n·g·  ·t·o·\n       )¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n       ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n\nSplash  : Your SysDl looks REALLY impressive! - Nice going, m8!\nDr. Ice : Thx for all the help you have given me regarding Amiga-E.\nWoober  : Keep on doing those Asc²... But think about cOLoUrS Too!\nJedi    : Welcome to MegaStyle, m8!\nShorty  : G-shade and texturemapped vectors forever? :)\nKingpin : Thanks for the bug-report on this first beta-release!\nShade   : Still afraid of busts? ;)))))))\nRaz     : Love your intro, man. Flames rulE!\nMr.Z    : Where are you? Your lines are down... :''-(\nBaffle  : Is your board up?\nStratos : to bad that you decided to leave. No hard feelings.\nFake    : Get a decent modem, and get that board on the air!\nChris   : Nice haircut! :) And what''s up in Bergen?\n\n\nAnd a nice''n''lovelY fucking to this SHI-member :\n\nKurt H. : GO''N''HANG YOURSELF!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!! (lamEr!)\n@ENDNODE\n\n\n\n;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\n@NODE "INFO" "About MegaStyle..."\n                                                               @{" Go back.. " Link MAIN}\n\nMegastyle is a new AmiExpress-Support group formed by Lizard of Spaceballs in\nthe middle of may 1995.\n\nOur main goal is to support all the /X-boards out there with the best doors\naround. We try hard to make our products as system-friendly as possible and\nwith unique configuration possibilities.\n\n\nWe want to be the leading /X-development group in the future, and therefore\nneed more skilled coders and ANSI-artist to make our products even better!\n\n\n\nIf you''re interesting in teaming up, then take a look at the contact-info.\n\n\n\n\nThanks to the following boards for helpful beta-testing of MegaStyle-products:\n«----------------------------------------------------------------------------»\n\n                            Dr. Feelgood (Science)\n   Checkpoint (Kingpin)   -   Total Panic (Jedi)   -   Flame-Strike (Splash)\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n\n\n;-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\n@NODE "CONTACT" "How to contact MegaStyle!"\n                                                               @{" Go back.. " Link MAIN}\n\n\n                              How to contact us :\n                         ·