nyour BBS etc. The easy part:)\n\nMAIL READ:\nAs  you  know,  any incoming mail contains a shitload of crap and\ninformation as a header. It also contains your email  address.  I\nhave  added  a  routine  that removes most of this when a user is\nonline reading their mail. It takes a complete  email  and  scans\nthrough  until  it  finds  the  string: "X-Mailer:" ...thereafter\nshowing the rest of the file,  nothing  beforehand.  So,  if  you\nhave  users on your BBS that you don''t much care for...well, they\nwill  never  get  to see your (*) email address. Plus, the screen\ndoesn''t become cluttered up with unwanted information.\n\n(*) Remember all mails  returned  to  BBS  users  are  originally\naddressed  to  YOU.  You''ll  soon  see.  If  you scan a .PVT file\ndirectly from YAM you''ll see  all  the  information  in  the  YAM\nheader that is cut out when viewing through Ami-Express.\n\nKILL:\nI agonised over this for days. Finally came  up  with  this  lame\nidea  for  deleting  mail.  It  deletes all current mail for that\nuser. They have chances to download etc. It will ask whether  the\nuser wants to KILL the mail yet (or not). It works just fine  and\nI see no reason to update it in the future. Slouch. Beer burp.\n\nABOUT + INFORMATION:\nSimple text files to add flair. Puh. Spit.\n\n------------------------------------------\n\nIf  the door is in use then no other node can access their email,\nhaving  to  wait until user1 is finished. Simultaneous use of YAM\nscanning etc could result in World War IV.\nOr so I theorise.\n\nWhat happened to WW3?\nProbably occurred, between me writing this and you reading this.\nWe''ll see. Always be prepared.\n\nAnyway, Def-Base tells me that it is possible to  make  the  door\nmultinode  friendly,  but  I haven''t got around to that yet. He''s\nsmarter than the average bear, + I''m still trying to understand.\n\n:P\n\n------------------------------------------\n\nRead mail options:\n\nDownload:  Let  you  download  the  current  file.  A  counter is\ncurrently running that makes each new download:\n\n YourMail1\n YourMail2\n YourMail3  ...etc...\n\n...so files don''t overwrite each other at the user''s end.\nCan''t remember if NCOMM etc overwrite in that way.\nBut I programmed it in anyway :)\n\nREPLY:  Accesses  the  text  editor,  already supplying the email\naddress of current-read email. Simple.\n\nFILE  ATTACH has been re-installed, as I was bored. As to whether\nit functions correctly, I don''t know. Seems fine to me. Test.\n\nEXTRAZ:\n       mosearch.info  (*)\n       cumail.txt\n       nomail.txt\n       logonsearch.rexx\n       scanit.rexx\n\n(*) Info file goes in usual BBS:commands/bbscmd. The other  files\nare  left  where  they are. Two txt files can be changed to suit,\nload up into suitable ANSI/TEXT editor.\n\n(*) Add: ~CC_MOSEARCH ...to your logon script. You know how.\n    Shows whether the logged-on user has email or not.\n    Will load YAM if not already loaded. Beware!\n\nAnd that''s about it.\nAs usual, all ideas/abuse appreciated.\n@endnode\n@node "auth" "Contact"\nContact:   [email removed]\n\nBBS        Wormhole/JaDe: Digital Candy\n           JaDe         : 13th Hour\n           Moriarty     : Havok\n\nIRC:       Peace4U/[-JaDe-]/WoRmHoLe\n           #England            - undernet.org\n           #Am!ga              - stealth.net\n           #100%FullOnSexPics  - :)\n@endnode\n@node "file" "Files"\nWhen   program  runs  it  loads  (if  not  already  loaded)  YAM,\nsearching for it in the usual YAM: assign.\n@endnode\n@node "fina" "Jerry Springer''s Final Thought..."\nYAM courtesy of Marcel Beck.\nFine program. Fine.\n@endnode\n@node "inst" "Getting this fecker to work..."\nJust put all files where they should be. Phhhhhh.\nRexxMast and RPstart must be running.\nCheck AEDocs for RPstart instructions.\n\nMost important: Find ''Folder.cfg'' and load into  a  text  editor,\nchanging  the number 4 to any desired folder of YAM that you wish\nto store all BBS-Emails. 0 -  3  are  Incoming,  Outgoing,  Sent,\nArchived.  Custom folders begin at 4. Please consult YAM guide on\nhow to achieve multiple orgasms. Erm, folders.\n\nMAKE SURE that all files go where I say they  should.  You  might\nthink  it  okay that you have ''waitforport'' etc in your SYS:REXXC\ndirectory, but Mo-Mail wants it in C: (for my personal ease),  it\nwon''t go searching for it. It doesn''t give a feck.\n@endnode\n@node "Bugs" "Those feckin crawlies..."\nYAM  looks  for  aliases:  If  a  user  tries  to enter a non-net\naddress when writing an email it will store this as an  error  in\nYAM,  so  next  time you open the YAM icon it will show a list of\nerror messages. Just clear these and cancel  any  other  unwanted\nwindows.  If  YAM is left un(?)iconified then this will leave the\nsystem hanging when a user endters a stupid address. A  real  net\naddress is something with ''@'' in it. Etc.\n\nMo-Email,  as  said before, kicks YAM into HIDE mode, so don''t be\nfuckin'' around with it. It ain''t no toy:P\n\nAlso: You might wanna change your ''realname'' config in  YAM  main\nprogram,  as  all  emails sent out contain your address - for all\nreturned mail/replies etc. Change it  to  something  like  ''Email\nUser'', or some lame crap like that. Further explaination on this\nis beyond me right now, new headache.\n@endnode\n@node "upda" "Something new..?"\nIf  a  file  called  ''NOATTACH''  exists in ''doors:email/'' then it will\nremove the ''Attach a  file?''  routine  from  Mo-Mail.  Mo-Mail  simply\nlooks  for  this file, doesn''t matter what the file contains. It could\nbe a hardcore sex pic for all Mo cares.\n\nTANGo:  Saved  the day with some excellent ansi. Mo-Mail was literally\nnaked without it. Thank you:)\n\nGreetz:\nWell, there are far too many to name here. If  I  haven''t  added  your\nname  then  mail  me  and  I''ll  put  it  up in lights. Once again I''m\nfighting another bitch headache, shocking, so here''s goes:\n\n Sn0zZ (welcome back m8;) Good time''s are uh-head)\n Def-Base (Saves the day again and again. He''s Batman in real life)\n TANGo (Man, you saved me from a fate worse than, erm, ansi-ridicule)\n Cool96 (Yer right, stay on stealth. Fuck the pussies)\n StoneCold (Brave man, beta''ing this door. He shows no fear)\n Ade (Digital Candy is doin'' just fine. Keep goin'';)\n Ace (13th Hour and the previous (DC) are my second homes)\n\nAlso to Blueboy, Trazer, Marsh, and a bucketload more;)\nWell, I know I''ve forgotten a heap of people. Apologeeeeeezuschrist.\n\nFuckin''s and slaggin''s:\nBuZz^MnC (A man who ejaculates constantly)\nCache-DtL (Or was it OtL? It seemed to change the other night)\n\nI don''t think I have any other enemies.\nIf untrue, mail me;)\n@endnode\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',62062,5,0,NULL,NULL,'momail17','scan',1780048612);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('momail20','MOMAIL20.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MOMAIL20.LHA','8','XIM','10',NULL,NULL,NULL,':mO-mAIL v2.00- sAFRA 1999 - BETA TEST DOOR: +------------------------------------------+ :>>>>> Requires YAM 2.0p7 and /X 4.12 <<<<<:',replace('.------------------------------------------.\n:mO-mAIL v2.00- sAFRA 1999 - BETA TEST DOOR:\n+------------------------------------------+\n:>>>>> Requires YAM 2.0p7 and /X 4.12 <<<<<:\n:>>> AmiExpress Email Door - 100% AREXX <<<:\n+------------------------------------------+\n|  Mo-Mail is PD. Do what you wish with it |\n+------------------------------------------+\n|  THIS VERSION FOR USERS WITH A STATIC IP :\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'Mo-Email.Guide',replace('@database Mo-Email.Guide\n@$VER: Mo-E-Mail (v1.03)\n@author "Safra"\n\n@node "Main" "mO-eMAIL dOCS"\n\n              @{b}==============================================\n               mO-eMAIL - v2.00 - STATIC IP VERSION - sAFRA\n              ==============================================@{ub}\n\n              @{" Introduction                  " link "Intr"}  -  mO-eMAIL!\n              @{" System Specs                  " link "spec"}  -     nEEDS!\n              @{" Installation                  " link "inst"}  -        gO!\n              @{" Important                     " link "Impo"}  -      vERY!\n              @{" Author                        " link "auth"}  -   cONTACT!\n              @{" Files                         " link "file"}  -     cHECK!\n              @{" Known Bugs                    " link "bugs"}  -   rECHECK!\n              @{" Final                         " link "fina"}  -   tHE eND!\n\n              @{" READ ME                       " link "upda"}  -    pLEASE!\n              @{b}==============================================\n              [AREXX-DOOR-AREXX-DOOR--AREXX-DOOR-AREXX-DOOR]\n              ==============================================@{ub}\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "Intr" "Introduction"\nForever ago I wanted an email door for ?Express. Nothing was  out\nthere  aside  from  a custom door by RRR. This wasn''t public so I\nstarted on this little effort.\n\nThe original MoMail17.lha can go piss in a lake for all  I  care.\nI  have  now  changed a few things in it so anyone using a STATIC\nIP gains. Hopefully. The original door was  for  temp-assigned-IP\ninternet  users - using some godforsaken programming to allow the\nBBS to have ''unlimited email  addresses''.  It  could  still  work\nproperly,  but  lack  of feedback and patience forced me to ditch\nit. Too bad.\n\nAnyhows,  this  new  version  is  for people at Demon Net etc. Or\nperhaps Freeserve (which is free, shockingly):\n\n [email removed]\n [email removed]\n\nYou know the score.\n\n@endnode\n@node "spec" "Specifications"\nMo-Email is currently running on my:  A1200 (68020) (68882 fpu)\n                                      10 Meg RAM\n                                      85 Meg Drive (still)\n                                      /X version 4.12\n                                      YAM 2.00 Preview 7\n\nWhether this will work on other versions of /X, I have no idea.\nWill it work on other systems? Fame/S!x/DayDream? I don''t know.\nYou tell me.\n\n@endnode\n@node "Impo" "Important!"\n\n<--------------------------------------------------------------->\nBEGIN OLD DOCS: MAY NOW NOT APPLY TO YAM 2.00:\n\nIn  order  for  users  to  delete  their  mail,  you  MUST UNtick\n''CONFIRM BEFORE DELETION'' in your YAM prefs/config.  Also  cancel\n''GET MAIL ON STARTUP''...as I am not sure whether this interferes\nwith the program, should a  user  be  the  one  to  load  YAM.  I\nbelieve  it  causes  no  hassle  when YAM is in HIDE mode. YAM is\ntold to go HIDE its ass when Mo-Email is run.\n\nIt  would  be  wise to put YAM in WBSTARTUP, else the program has\nto be loaded when a  user  tries  to  access  Mo-Mail.  It  needs\nloading only once, but once is enough to piss off a user.\n<--------------------------------------------------------------->\n\nBEGIN NEW DOCS: How other things work:\n\nThe  tailer  that  is  added  to  an outgoing email contains your\npersonal tag: (doors:email/signature.txt). Change  this  to  suit\nyour BBS etc. The easy part:)\n\nAnyone on the BBS using split names will become hyphenated:\n\n IE: ''The Count'' becomes ''The-Count''\n\nElse they do not have a valid email address.\nThough I''m sure I''m wrong.\nSee also: KNOWN BUGS\n\nAs  you  know,  any incoming mail contains a shitload of crap and\ninformation as a header.\n\nI have added a routine that removes most of this when a  user  is\nonline reading their mail. It takes a complete  email  and  scans\nthrough  until it finds the string: "Content-Type:" ...thereafter\nshowing the rest of the file, nothing beforehand.\n\nKILL:\nI agonised over this for days. Finally came  up  with  this  lame\nidea  for  deleting  mail.  It  deletes all current mail for that\nuser. They have chances to download etc. It will ask whether  the\nuser wants to KILL the mail yet (or not). It works just fine  and\nI see no reason to update it ever.\n\nABOUT + INFORMATION:\nSimple text files to add fun and frolics.\n\nIf  the door is in use then no other node can access their email,\nhaving  to  wait until user1 is finished. Simultaneous use of YAM\nscanning etc could result in hassle. Or so I theorise.\n\nRead mail options:\n\nDownload:  Let  you  download  the  current  file.  A  counter is\ncurrently running that makes each new download:\n\n YourMail1\n YourMail2\n YourMail3  ...etc...\n\n...so files don''t overwrite each other at the user''s end.\nCan''t remember if NCOMM etc overwrite in that way.\nBut I programmed it in anyway :)\n\nREPLY:  Accesses  the  text  editor,  already supplying the email\naddress of current-read email. Simple.\n\nFILE-ATTACH is currently disabled.\n\nEXTRAZ:\n       mosearch.info  (*)\n       cumail.txt\n       nomail.txt\n       logonsearch.rexx\n       scanit.rexx\n\n(*) Info file goes in usual BBS:commands/bbscmd. The other  files\nare  left  where  they are. Two txt files can be changed to suit,\nload up into suitable ANSI/TEXT editor.\n\n(*) Add: ~CC_MOSEARCH ...to your logon script. You know how.\n    Shows whether the logged-on user has email or not.\n    Will load YAM if not already loaded. Beware!\n\nAnd that''s about it.\nAs usual, all ideas/abuse appreciated.\n@endnode\n@node "auth" "Contact"\nContact:   [email removed]\nBBS:       (UK) 01536-744-639 (After 10pm please)\n@endnode\n@node "file" "Files"\nWhen   program  runs  it  loads  (if  not  already  loaded)  YAM,\nsearching for it in the usual YAM: assign.\n@endnode\n@node "fina" "Jerry Springer''s Final Thought..."\nYAM courtesy of Marcel Beck - 1995/1999.\nSuperb program. Truly.\n\nAscII courtesy of TANGo.\n\n@endnode\n@node "inst" "Getting this fecker to work..."\nJust put all files where they should be. Phhhhhh.\nRexxMast and RPstart must be running.\nCheck AEDocs for RPstart instructions.\n\nMost important: Find ''Folder.cfg'' and load into  a  text  editor,\nchanging  the number 4 to any desired folder of YAM that you wish\nto store all BBS-Emails. 0 -  3  are  Incoming,  Outgoing,  Sent,\nArchived.  Custom folders begin at 4. Please consult YAM guide on\nhow to achieve multiple orgasms. Erm, folders.\n\nVery important: Find ''Domain.cfg'' and change it to your domain.\nIf your email address is ''[email removed]'' then your\nDomain.cfg will be ''welcome.demon.co.uk''\n\nMAKE SURE that all files go where I say they  should.  You  might\nthink  it  okay that you have ''waitforport'' etc in your SYS:REXXC\ndirectory, but Mo-Mail wants it in C: (for my personal ease),  it\nwon''t go searching for it. It doesn''t give a feck.\n\nWhere files should be:\n\n libs:rexxsyslib.library\n C:rx\n C:waitforport\n C:delete\n C:wait\n C:makedir\n C:dir\n C:list\n\nYou  as the sysop will have to send the mail. If anyone out there\nhas the luxury of 24/7 net connects then basically  someone  with\na    high    enough   level  of  axs  on  the  BBS  can  begin  a\ndirect-from-the-net mail check. Otherwise, it''s up  to  sysop  to\ngather all mail etc.\n\nA  script/program  could  be  created  that will send YAM(Miami?)\nonline once a day. This would of course have nothing to  do  with\n/X or MoMail. Totally independant. I''m not writing it.\n\nIf anyone does, then MoMail needs tweaking to show  that  YAM  is\ncurrently running a mail call.\n\nYes, I have put little thought into this. Cough.\n\n@endnode\n@node "Bugs" "Those feckin crawlies..."\n\nMOMAIL  will  do a pathetic check on any entered email address to\ncheck for validity. If it does NOT contain a ''@''  then  the  user\nwill not proceed further. NOT  implemented  is  a  check  to  see\nwhether a user has entered a duff-space name:\n\n IE: [email removed] org\n\n(Space between ''com'' and ''org'')\n\n...Or  something  similar.  If YAM is not hidden then a requester\nwill pop up to tell the  Amiga  owner  that  somebody  fucked  up\nsomewhere.  If  YAM is hidden then everything should be cool, and\nthe user simply loses out. Not sure entirely.\n\nIf YAM is not running when MOMAIL begins then it  will  load  the\nYAM as follows:\n\nrun etc: ''YAM:YAM PREFSFILE=YAM:.config MAILDIR=YAM: NOCHECK HIDE''\n\nPREFSFILE=the main config for your YAM program\nMAILDIR=the directory that holds all your incoming/etc folders.\n\nRemember: The current setup needs FOLDER 4 TO BE CALLED ''BBS''\nRemember: Folders begin at ''0''.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "upda" "BETA"\nTHIS IS A BETA VERSION\nI TAKE NO RESPONSIBILITY FOR ANY DAMAGE CAUSED\nYOU USE AT YOUR OWN RISK\n\nAnd...etc.\n@endnode\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',45434,5,0,NULL,NULL,'momail20','scan',1780048612);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mover','MOVER.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MOVER.LHA','Mover','XIM','MOVER Mover','1.3',NULL,NULL,NULL,replace('Mover v1.3\n','\n',char(10)),'lOSeNDOS.guide',replace('                   \n                     __  _ __  /\__ _  _ __/\  __ _  __\n                    _\/___   \/              \/   ___\/_\n              ......\/\  /........................\  /\/......\n             :         \/                          \/         :\n             :      .___             .___         .___        :\n             :   _ _|   \      ______|   \  ______|   \       :\n             :   \\\__   7___  \______   /  \__   ____/       :\n             :      /.   |   \__/.  l/   \___/_____   \__ _   :\n             :     /::.  |    _/::.       _/::.  l/    _///   :\n             :     \___________\___________\____________\     :\n             :___        .___        .___        .___         :___\n     _ ______|   \ ______|   \ ______|   \ ______|   \  ______|   \\n     \\\__   ____/ \______   / \______   / \______   /  \__   ____/\n        /.   ___|___/.   |   \__/.  _|   \__/.  l/   \___/_____   \__ _\n       /::.  l/   _/::.  |    _/::. \___  _/::.       _/::.  l/    _///\n       \_ _________\_____|_____\___________\___________\___________ \\n         Y   :                                                :[nM$]Y\n      .------''                                                `------.\n      :eXON/rIOT^jORMAS · gHANDY/gODS · rAHIEM/eSSENCE · cELIC/rEKTUM: \n      `------.                                                .------''\n             `------------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'XIM-BBSCmd',27397,5,0,NULL,NULL,'mover_mover','scan',1780048612);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mover_16','MOVER_16.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MOVER_16.LHA',NULL,'XIM','MOVE FiLES! AMiEXPRESS UTiLS!',NULL,NULL,'MOVER',NULL,replace('MOVE FiLES! AMiEXPRESS UTiLS!\n','\n',char(10)),'uzi.txt',replace('                                            .---------------------------.\n    _______.-----------------._______/|     |     4NODEZ  RiNGDOWN      |\n    \_     |     .------     |________|.....| 73 GiG OF AMiGA CoNSoLE PC|\n   .:|     |     |     ______|        |:::::|  uZiSUiCiDE.sERVEBBS.ORG  |\n  .::|     |     |     |     |        |-----+-----.      TELNET         |\n .:::|           |     |     |       :|     |     |                     |\n.::::\___________|___________|________|     `-----+---------------------''\n:::::::::::::::::|                                | 24HR 7DAY STATiC iP! \n_________________|___________/|__________________/|______________________\n\_     ______    |     _______|          |_____________      _/    _____/\n_|_____    |     |     |      |    |_____|        |   |      |     ___|_ \n|     |    |     |     |      |    |     |        |   |      |     |    |\n|     |    |     |     |     :|          |       :|   |      |     |    |\n|__________|_____|_____|______|__________|________|__________|__________|\n:::::::::::::::::|            |                                         |\n`::::::::::::::::|            |ALWAYS THE LATEST VERSION oF AMi-EXPRESS |\n `:::::::::::::::|            | TONS OF ONLiNE MESSAGES AND MULTi-CHATS |\n  `::::::::::::::`------------+  NUP IS REQUIRED SO ASK WHOEVER POSTED  |\n   `::::::::::::::::::::::::::|    THIS ADVERT FOR THE NUMBER AND NUP   |\n    `:::::::::::::::::::::::::`-----------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,5889,5,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048612);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('movfil03','MOVFIL03.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MOVFIL03.LHA',NULL,'XIM','move files older than xx days to a other',NULL,NULL,NULL,'dir..',replace('move files older than xx days to a other\ndir..\n','\n',char(10)),'MoveFiles.doc',replace('        ____    __  _____  __  ____   _  _    __   __ ____\n        )(\ \  _)(_ )__ / _)(_ )(\ \ _)\/(_  _)(_  \/ )__(_\n        )(_)/  )/\(  _)/  )/\( )(_)/ )/\/\(  )/\(  /\ \) \(\n        )( )\ /(\/)\ )/__ \\// )( )\ )\  /( /(\/)\ )( /)_//\n        \/ \/ \/  \//___(  \/  \/ \/ \/  \/ \/  \/ \/ )__/\n\n               - -- ---=*)> PRESENTS: <(*=--- -- -\n \n                      *** MoveFiles v0.3 ***\n\n        AmiExpress Utility to move files older than X  days!\n           Coded by Nameless, beta tested by Dalai Lama\n\n\nWell, if you''re getting tired of constantly filling up your BBS:Conf/Upload\ndirectory with uploads, this program will quickly MOVE the files X nr of days\nold, and older, from your upload directory to an archive path (From which ya\ncan move ''em offline to tape...) and at the same time update your\nBBS:Conf/DirX files to reflect that they''re no longer RECENT uploads.\n\nAll Parameters are set in a CONFIG file. The name of which is passed as an\nargument to this program. I recommend you name the config file(s) the same\nas your BBS:Conference to make it easy for ya to move those files (ya just\ntype ''MoveFiles BBS:ConfName'' and it''ll move the older stuff...\n\n\n*** COMMAND SYNTAX ***\n\n\n  MoveFiles  ConfigFile[.mfcnfg]  [QUICK]\n\n\nWHERE:\n\nConfigFile  Is the name of the config file with the following options,\n            If you don''t understand - see the SAMPLE.MFCnfg file included.\n            Note: the .mfcnfg is optional (it WILL append it if u didn''t)\n\n   NR_DAYS_OLD   xxx   <-(the number of days of files you want to keep)\n   SRC_DIR_TXT   xxx   <-(source BBS:Conf/DirX text file path&name)\n   SRC_PATH      xxx   <-(source BBS:Conf/Upload directory path)\n   DEST_DIR_TXT  xxx   <-(destination BBS:Conf/DirX text file path&name)\n   DEST_PATH     xxx   <-(destination archive dir path to move files to)\n\n\n[QUICK]    Is an optional switch which turns OFF verbose mode (avoids the\n           detailed info during run). With QUICK you will just be told\n           to wait while processing, and It''ll probably be slightly quicker.\n\n\n*** CONSIDERATIONS ***\n\n\nThere is an assumptions that was made in doing this utility, which has to do\nwith your source & destination BBS:Conf/DirX text files. Most of you have been\nmodifyin'' the heck out of yours so I thought ya ought to know:\n\n  This utility assumes ALL DATES are in order from oldest (top) to newest\n  (bottom) in both the source & destination text files. This version does\n  not sort these files (maybe a later version will).  Failure to keep your\n  dates in this order will prevent this utility from working correctly (It''ll\n  stop copying when it finds a date closer to the X number of days you\n  specified). Note: there''s a util called ''Arrange'' by AirWolf which will\n  sort your DirX files (just in case you''ve been mixing the dates up...)\n\nINVALID dates in the date field (you know - like the word ''DELETED!'' instead\nof ''03-04-92'') are OK (YES OK!) - This program will just ignore that line as\neven having legit file. You got that? No date, No file will be moved. Dates\nare pretty important - hehe.\n\nI also wanted to mention that header lines (at the top of the DirX file) are\nok, as long as you don''t have a valid date in the date field - then It''ll\nthink that line contains an actual filename to process.  When this program\nupdates the DirX files, it should ignore the headers.\n\nAnother thing to keep in mind is, IF it can''t MOVE any of the upload files,\nthen it won''t bother to try to update your DirX files. What I mean by that\nis the program MUST succeed in actually transfering 1 file from your source\nto your destination THEN it will update your dest DirX file with ALL of the\nolder files which were (OR were supposed to be) moved.\n\n\n*** REVISION HISTORY ***\n\n\nv0.1 - 5/12/92 - Initial release...beta for dalai lama to test out... bugs?\n                 hmmm, none that I''m aware of in the brief time I checked\n                 it out!\nv0.2 - 5/13/92 - Rewrote copy function - 300% faster yeah! Changed link opts,\n                 Eliminated ALL stdio functions for Amiga2.0.lib functions\n                 Eliminated redundant functions, reduced size by 5K! I did\n                 increase allocated buffer size, if you dont have at least\n                 the memory to hold your source DirX text file + 100k this\n                 program may choke and run out of memory. beta test release.\nv0.3 - 5/17/92 - Fixed a bug which caused dest file to be deleted before\n                 checking to see if source file existed. Also fixed bug with\n                 memory alignment, changed malloc() to exec.library\n                 AllocVec(). Reduced size another 1K. Added a skip of DirX\n                 re-writes if no files were moved. Removed opening of\n                 dos.library, done by link to c.o. Other minor cleanups...\n                 ----->>>  Initial ''RaZorMaID GRouP'' release!  <<<---\n\n\n*** PLANNED/POSSIBLE IMPROVEMENTS ***\n\n\no  Had a suggestion to check for an ''*'' character right after the date (you\n   know ... MM-DD-YY* ... and if it exists to delete that file from the upload\n   dir and the text file without bothering to transering it.  Would make it\n   easy to identify and get rid of ''lame'' files, as well as those already\n   backed up.\n\no  Had another suggestion to sort the DirX file (That would eliminate one of\n   the current limitations - see above ''assumptions...''). If you know you''re\n   DirX file dates aren''t sorted correctly by date - just use the Arrange Util\n   by AirWolf. (if you can find it - hehe).\n\n\n*** RELEASE INFO & COMMENTS ***\n\n\nLast week, I was asked by a friend to code this utility, I havn''t seen another\nutility like this, so I figured a quick ''C'' util would do it. I''ve spent a lot\nof time assuring the safety (making sure NO DAMAGE) will come to any of your\nfiles during run (I think this program is 80% error handling and 20% actual\ncode - hehe), but still, run at your own risk!. Anyway, I''d like to mention, I\ndo have the SAS C v5.1b SOURCE code available for ANYONE who wishes to examine\nit (make sure it''s ok), re-compile it..., or even modify it to suit their own\nneeds. Just call my board, Snarfs Pub (407)267-8155, and leave me a message\nthat ya want the code.\n\nLastly, I am running this under workbench v2.04, And I CAN''T guarantee that\nit''ll work under 1.3 - but I''m pretty sure it will. USE AT YOUR OWN RISK!\n\nLater dudes, Nameless\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,14094,3,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048612);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mres202','MRES202.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MRES202.LHA','MultiResetPrefs','XIM','MultiReset','2.02',NULL,NULL,'Reset Enhancer... [iSDN][-] lEEChEd fRoM gOd''s hArEm [-][16.8]',replace('Multi Reset V2.02 \nReset Enhancer...\n[iSDN][-] lEEChEd fRoM gOd''s hArEm [-][16.8]\n','\n',char(10)),'MultiReset.doc',replace('MultiReset 2.02                  Documentation                  16-Jun-1995\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nIntroduction\n\n   Sometimes  he''s very needful, the reset.  Pressing CTRL+AMIGA+AMIGA your\n   computer reboots.  But must be this procedure so stupid.\n   There  are many things that we can do here.  Multireset will show you an\n   other  way.  It can play samples, showing IFF-pictures and clear all the\n   vectors (i.e.  KickTag, KickMem and so on..).\n\n   One problem has left:  Multireset don''t run on older machines, like A500\n   and many A2000.\n\nInstallation and setup\n\n   At  first copy the MultiResetPrefs-program to your PREFS-directory.  The\n   MultiReset-program  should be copied to the WBStartup-directory.  Before\n   using  MultiReset you must run the prefs-program.  It will open a little\n   window with many gadgets where you can configure the reset-style:\n\n   (Gfx)                - the full path of the picture that multireset\n                          shows. If the gadget is empty no picture will\n                          be displayed. You can use all resulutions but\n                          IFF files only. (see screen-gadget)\n   (Sfx)                - the full path of the sample that multireset\n                          plays. You can use IFF or RAW samples here.\n   (Dos)                - Here you can enter a dos-command (with\n                          parameters) that will be executed before\n                          showing the picture and playing the sample.\n   (Log)                - Here you can specify an file for the MultiReset\n                          log.\n   (Noopen)             - If active the Open()-routine will be patched, so\n                          that all open-calls with newfile mode would\n                          be ignored.\n   (Nowrite)            - If active the Write()-routine will be patched,\n                          so that all write-calls are impossible.\n   (Nowait)             - No delay after playing the sample\n   (Time)               - variable delaytime from 0 to 10 s \n   (Norexx)             - Ignore messages to the rexx-port\n   (Userscreen)         - If this gadget is active, multireset will\n                          show the picture on an own sreen. Now you can\n                          use HAM, EHB or HAM8 formats. Is the\n                          gadget disabled, you should only use pictures\n                          in the depth of your workbenchscreen.\n   (Workbench)          - Switch the workbenchscreen to front.\n   (Coldcapute)         - Clears the Coldcapture-vector.\n   (Coolcapture)        - Clears the Coolcapture-vector.\n   (KickTag)            - Clears the Kicktag-vector.\n   (KickMem)            - Clears the Kickmem-vector.\n   (PicPos)             - It will open a window in the size of the\n                          selected picture. You can move around it and\n                          so fix the position on the workbenchsreen.\n                          If you enter ''-1'' for the X or Y coordinate\n                          the picture will be automatically centered in\n                          the corresponding direction.\n   (VecPos)             - Same as PicPos, but for the little window\n                          that shows the vectors. Only useful when at\n                          least one vector should be cleared.\n\n   Now  you  can use a second way to reset your machine with MultiReset.  I\n   have  added  a  simply rexxport that understand 3 commands:\n\n   RESET        - will do the reset with all options\n   RESET QUICK  - will do the reset immediately, without picture and sample\n   REMOVE       - removes MultiReset out of the memory\n\n   The  rexxport  is  named  ''MultiReset''.  A reset via Arexx can look like\n   this:\n\n   address ''MultiReset'';RESET \n\nHistory    \n\n   V 1.3  - first public release\n   V 1.4  - default path for sfx, fgx and dos-string\n   V 1.5  - internal release\n   V 1.6  - saving prefswindow positions\n   V 1.7  - bug fix: updateing gadgets\n          - patch Open() and Write()\n          - logfile\n   V 1.8  - delay can be switched on or off\n   V 1.9  - Prefs now saved in ENVARC:\n          - Rexx-Port added\n   V 2.0  - MUI-Interface\n   V 2.01 - new Arexx-command REMOVE\n          - bug fix: actions will be done if gadgets released\n   V 2.02 - variable delaytime (0-10s)\n\nAbout program and author\n\n   This  little program is giftware.  If you like it, send me a litte gift.\n   If there are any bugs or improvements, send also to:\n\n   eMail    : [email removed]\n   SnailMail: Frank Fenn\n              Raabestrasse 7\n              (Germany) Berlin\n              10405\n   Phone    : +49-30-39979430 (7:00 am - 3:30 pm)\n\nThanx to\n\n   Stefan Stuntz          - for his great MUI-package\n   Wouter van Oortmerssen - for the E-language\n   [email removed]   - for bugreports and hints\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',74791,3,0,NULL,NULL,'mres202','scan',1780048612);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mrl_ws','MRL_WS.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MRL_WS.LHA','GetPubName','XIM','GetPubName',NULL,NULL,'MRL','\ __/\\//()\\  \ __/\ \ / __) >< ||//_ / __)//\\ /____\//\\|/___/____\___/',replace(' ______  _  _   _______ \n \ __/\\//()\\  \ __/\ \\n / __) >< ||//_ / __)//\\\n/____\//\\|/___/____\___/  \nThe RimFire (901)382-8303\n -+=*   Presents    *=+-\n     Where is Sysop\n\nThis is a program to let a\nuser know where the sysop is \nwork on the sysop''s computer.\n','\n',char(10)),'SW_LRM.DOC',replace('INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mscanfix','MSCANFIX.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MSCANFIX.LHA','MagicScan','XIM','MagicConvert',NULL,'Faktor/Independent',NULL,'##      MagicScan Beta Version - Fix!     ## ## -------------------------------------- ## ##        -- For AmiExpress 4.xx --       ##',replace('############################################\n##      MagicScan Beta Version - Fix!     ##\n## -------------------------------------- ##\n##        -- For AmiExpress 4.xx --       ##\n##                                        ##\n## Major bug removed - Don''t use the old! ##\n## ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~ ##\n##  Copyright (c) by Faktor/Independent   ##\n############################################\n','\n',char(10)),'1.FileDUPE.Txt',replace('\n                               Nu var du dum!\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',54917,11,0,NULL,NULL,'mscanfix','scan',1780048612);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mscanv10','MSCANV10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MSCANV10.LHA','MScanner','XIM','+---------------------------------------+',NULL,'|',NULL,'| MDD`s mESSAGE bASE sCANNER V1.0 A nEW | | aND fIRST rELEASED /X dOOR wRITTEN bY | | mAGIC dRUMMER!. rEAD tHE dOC-fILE fOR |',replace('  +---------------------------------------+\n  | MDD`s mESSAGE bASE sCANNER V1.0 A nEW |\n  | aND fIRST rELEASED /X dOOR wRITTEN bY |\n  | mAGIC dRUMMER!. rEAD tHE dOC-fILE fOR |\n  | fULL iNFORMATION aBOUT tHIS kEWL tOOL |\n  +---------------------------------------+\n  |  aNOTHER fAST aSSEMBLER dOOR bY MDD!  |\n  +---------------------------------------+\n','\n',char(10)),'MScanner.Doc',replace('     +----------------------------------------------------------+\n     | MDD`S MESSAGE BASE SCANNER V1.0 WRITTEN BY MAGIC DRUMMER |\n     +----------------------------------------------------------+\n\n     Use my new /XDoor to Scan for TXT`S in all Msg-Bases!!\n     This helps the LAZY Sysop`s to clean up there MSG BASES\n     OLD and LAME EALLS like on the NIRVANA BBS or BOONDOCKS!!!\n\n     +---------------+\n     | tHE fEATURES: |\n     +---------------+\n\n->   The whole Programm is written in 680XX Assembler (High Performance)\n->   This Door will not use the intern /XMessage Functions -->> more Speed\n->   You can search for texts in the Message Header and in the Message\n     Text (body)\n->   You can use this tool to scan for EALL Msg`s and Delete them (Sysop)\n->   If you search in the Msg Text all Found Txt`s will be Highlited!\n     (need ANSI Modus!)\n->   The Programm shows you the real amount of ONLINE Msg`s\n\n     +---------------+\n     | iNSTALLATION: |\n     +---------------+\n\n1.   move the Directory ''Doors/MsgScanner/'' in your Doors: Directory\n     3 Files! ''RMail'' , ''MScanner'' , ''MScanner.Doc''\n2.   move the files in Directory ''BBSCMD'' in your ''BBS:Commands/BBSCMD/''\n     Directory (2 Files,  R.info and RS.info )\n3.   Thats All .... easy, isnt`t it?  enjoy!\n\n     +-------------+\n     | hOW tO uSE: |\n     +-------------+\n\n1.   SIMPLY TYPE ''RS + <CR>'' to run the DOOR\n     OR DIRECT   ''RS <SEARCHTEXT> + <CR>''\n\n2.   Enter your Text to search at the Prompt\n     e.g "bBs-aDds" , "MAGIC DRUMMER" (spaces allowed)\n         "the" , "1"\n     You can enter simply everything you like from 1 up to 20 letters\n\n3.   Then you will ask for ''MsgText'' or ''MsgHeader''\n     this figures out were you wish to search in\n\n     Hit ''1'' for "MsgTexts"  (or just <CR>)\n     hit ''2'' for "MsgHeader"\n\n     If you choose Msgtexts (1) my program will search your <SEARCHTEXT>\n     in the body of the text..\n     In this options all found txt`s will be HIGHLITED\n\n     MsgHeader (2) will search your <SEARCHTEXT> in the message header..\n     (message from, message to, and subject)  -> Giga Fast!!\n\n4.   ''MDD`s MsgScanner'' will show you after that some useful values:\n\n     First message             :     23		-> The first Online Msg\n     Last message              :   2251		-> The last Online Msg\n     Total active messages     :    752		-> All Online Msg`s\n\n     You will get another Prompt were you can Enter the ScanStart\n     for the search algorythm\n\n     MsgNumber to Start,<CR>=1 :                -> Hit Return to start from\n						-> the First available Mail\n						-> Or any other Number\n						-> between First and Last\n						-> Msg!\n\n     ''MDD`s MsgScanner'' will start Scanning for your choosen txt in the\n     choosen area after this\n\n5.   Options when ''MDD`s MsgScanner'' find a Msg:\n\n\n  a) Hit ''Q''    to.. guess what..  Quit!!\n\n  b) Hit ''D''    to Delete the Mail		-> This only works if you\n						-> Wrote this mail, or the\n						-> Mail is addressed to you\n						-> or you are the SYSOP!\n  c) Hit ''<CR>'' to continue Scanning\n\n->   iMPORTANT nOTE:\n     ---------------\n->   ONLY THE REAL SYSOP CAN DELETE REALLY ALL MAILS!\n->   THAT WILL NOT DEPEND ON THE LEVEL.. ONLY THE USER IN\n->   SLOT 0 CAN SCAN IN PRIVATE MAILS AND DELETE THEM\n\n     +----------------------+\n     | uSEFUL tIPS & tRICKS |\n     +----------------------+\n\n->   to make this programm more faster DELETE old Mails!!\n->   you can speed up your whole Msg Base when you do the\n     following 4 Steps (also speeds up the normal /X Msg Functions!!)\n\n   1.copy your  ''BBS:ConfName/MsgBase/HeaderFile''      to RAM:\n   2.Rename the ''BBS:ConfName/MsgBase/HeaderFile''\n     to         ''BBS:ConfName/MsgBase/HeaderFile.old''\n   3.copy the   ''RAM:HeaderFile'' back to your\n                 ''BBS:ConfName/MsgBase/'' Directory\n   4.Delte the  ''BBS:ConfName/MsgBase/HeaderFile.old''\n\n->   This is like to Optimize Your Harddrive..\n->   You can do this with other files too!!\n     e.g ''BBS:User.Data''\n          ''BBS:User.Keys''\n          ''BBS:NodeX/Callerslog''\n           ...\n\n     +-------------------------------------------------+\n     | tHE eND & cREDITS & gREETINGS & cONTACT aDDRESS |\n     +-------------------------------------------------+\n\n->   Finally you have Reached the END of this little Document\n\n->   I want to sent out some other credits to ...\n\n     BitBug   -> Thx for helping me to Style this tool and bugreport!\n     Amicom   -> Beta Testing (only 2 days ! haha)\n             -> "Mann alle stunde ne neue Version?? codest du in easy C" ?\n\n->   Some Greetings fly to ...\n\n     Bitbug     -> "wer issn Toyax?"\n     Byteandi   -> "iss doch tutti!!"\n     Starscream -> "Simply the best i know!"\n     Apollo     -> "CO-Sysop on my BBS!"\n     Maximilien -> "nice time with you!, force the Paradox boards\n                    to use this GREAT TOOL!!"\n\n->   Contact Address\n\n     Reach me for bugreport or just for a nice chat on Hack Reaktor\n     6 Nodes , 16.8 DS , ISDN , Amiga , Console , IBM , H/P\n\n     Dial : +49-(0)89-650-044\n\n     or leave mail to ''MAGIC DRUMMER'' on any cool BBS all over the GLOBE\n\n     e.g. House of Coolness\n          Mirage\n          Gates of Asgad\n          ...\n-------------------------------------------------------------tHE END!-------\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,11635,3,0,NULL,NULL,'mscanv10_mscanner','scan',1780048612);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('msg_sear','MSG-SEAR.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MSG-SEAR.LHA','SearchMsg','XIM','SearchMsg',NULL,NULL,'MSG',NULL,replace('Message base search..\n','\n',char(10)),'SearchMsg.Doc',replace('SearchMsg 3.0\n-------------\n\nSearchMsg, XIM door, now works for both netmail and and regular conferences.\n\n-------------\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',17671,6,0,NULL,NULL,'msg_sear','scan',1780048612);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('msgrescu','MSGRESCU.LZH','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MSGRESCU.LZH','MsgRescue','XIM','MsgRescue',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,replace('MessageBase repair Util\n','\n',char(10)),'MsgRescue.doc',replace('****************************************************************************\n*                                                                          *\n*                 MsgRescue V1.0 By Bryce! of Horizon 1991                 *\n*                                                                          *\n*                    Util that rescues a crashed MsgBase                   *\n*                                                                          *\n****************************************************************************\n\n                    User''s Manual for the MsgTop utility.\n\n\n1. Introduction\n\n   Nothing much to tell about this util. It speaks for itself. \n   You have probably as a sysop got the message ''MsgBase ERROR!\n   Please notify Sysop!" lots of times, but most of the time\n   it''s just a minor problem, but without the proper tools,\n   there''s nothing to do except reset the whole MsgBase. UNTIL NOW!\n   Most of the time it is just the MailStats file that has been\n   crashed, and this file only contains a little info about the\n   actual HeaderFile. This util reconstructs and recalculates\n   a new MailStats file, and you won''t need to reset the MsgBase.\n\n\n2. How to get started\n\n   The usage of the MsgRescue util looks like this:\n\n   MsgRescue [HeaderFile] [MailStats]\n\n   These two files are the data files placed in the MsgBase directory\n   in your conference directory. Let''s say your Elite Conference is\n   called ''Elite'', and is placed in the BBS: directory. The command-\n   line would the look like this:\n\n   MsgRescue BBS:Elite/MsgBase/HeaderFile BBS:Elite/MsgBase/MailStats\n\n   Short and sweet!\n\n3. Hints\n\n   You might want to put this util in the logoff script, if you\n   got time for it, and the chance of your MsgBase being crashed\n   is almost equal to zero.\n\n\n4. Aftertouch\n\n   First of all I want to thank a couple of people:\n\n   BamBam           - Let get the conference going!\n   Ted/Defjam       - Thanx for all the debugging help!\n   SpaZm/Fairlight  - A source of inspiration!\n   Mogwai/Defjam    - How''s that new BBS program comming?\n   The Baron/Defjam - Hope you''ll be able to take some time off soon.\n\n   And then for some greetings: (in NO order at all)\n\n   Prisoner of Wife, Bigfoot, In Decent, Cydric, Jabbah, Zin, BamBam,\n   Damage, Porta, Capricorn, Strider, Conqueror, Jetaza, Judge Dredd,\n   Raistlin, Winter Mute, Black Shadow, Blaizer, Irata, Spike,\n   Highlander, Archangel, Zcandaler, Splatt, Mr.Trax, The UnderTaker...\n\n   (Sorry, if I''ve forgotten someone.)\n\n   And of course to all HORIZON members!\n\n\n6. Credits and other Information\n\n   Programmed in Manx Aztec ''C'' for reliable and system-friendly code.\n\n   Programming:       Bryce! - Horizon\n\n   This util has been tested, and works 100% on: KickStart 1.2, 1.3, 2.0.\n   It has also been tested on various RAM set-ups, such as; 1 Mb chip, \n   0.5 Mb chip, 0.5 Mb chip & 0.5 Mb fast, 0.5 Mb chip & 4 Mb fast, 1 Mb \n   chip and 2 Mb fast, 1 Mb chip & 1 Mb fast, 2 Mb chip & 4 Mb 32 bit fast,\n   and this worked 100%. Processors tested with this util includes: 68000 \n   7.14 Mhz, 68030 25 MHz, and 68882 25 MHz, and no problems occured with \n   this either.\n\n   You can reach me (Bryce!), or check out my utils at my beta-testers:\n\n   The MainFrame   - Horizon EHQ   - +46-303-67301\n   DownTown        - Classic HQ    - +31-575029313\n   Marityrium      - Classic USHQ  -  713-666-4093\n   The Graveyard   - Agile UKHQ    - +44-915160560\n   West BBS        - Defjam SHQ    - +46-31-311879\n   Total Eclipse   - Aurora HQ     - +46-31-572545\n\n   Or try these util-making friends of mine''s boards:\n\n   Streets of Fire - Defjam SHQ    - +46-755-61537\n   Spaztic BBS     - Fairlight PHQ -  407-639-9123\n\n   Ok, I think that''s just about it, I guess... So, I''ll just let you\n   carry on with installing this great util, and say goodbye. See you\n   in the next production.\n\n                                 ...Bryce! ''91\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',7629,3,0,NULL,NULL,'msgrescu','scan',1780048612);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('msgtop','MSGTOP.LZH','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MSGTOP.LZH','MsgTop','XIM','MsgTop',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,replace('Top Message Writer\n','\n',char(10)),'MsgTop.doc',replace('****************************************************************************\n*                                                                          *\n*                  MsgTop V1.0 By Bryce! of Horizon 1991                   *\n*                                                                          *\n*                        Top Message Writers Util                          *\n*                                                                          *\n****************************************************************************\n\n                    User''s Manual for the MsgTop utility.\n\n\n1. Introduction\n\n   This utility is for you, sysops, who would like to stimulate users\n   to write more messages. It looks like a regular Top Uploaders list\n   but it shows who''s been writing the most messages. It''s very simple\n   to use so there should be no problems. It also displays some other\n   info like; the total amount of messages written, number of users,\n   and so on. I think you''ll enjoy it!\n\n2. How to get started\n\n   The of the MsgTop Util looks like this:\n\n   MsgTop [User.Data] [OutputFile] [-g/-n] [IncludeFile/-n]\n\n   The User.Data argument is of course the full path to your user.data\n   file. The OutputFile argument is the full path to where you want the\n   result to go. The -g or -n argument is for ANSI graphics or not. \n   (-g for ANSI and -n for NO ANSI). The next argument is the include-\n   file. This a textfile which will be included in the actual result-\n   file. Replace this with -n if you don''t want an includefile.\n\n   Here''s an example: \n   \n   Your user.data file is in BBS: and you would like the output to\n   be in BBS:Elite/Bulletins/Bull5.txt. You would also like ANSI\n   graphics, and an include file which is called ''Head'' and is \n   placed in the S: directory. The commandline would then look\n   like this:\n\n   MsgTop BBS:User.Data BBS:Elite/Bulletins/Bull5.txt -g s:Head\n\n   Pretty simple, eh?\n\n\n3. Hints\n\n   The only hint I can give, is that older versions of AmiExpress\n   doesn''t save info about how many messages a user has written,\n   so make sure you are using the newest version available.\n   (I run it with AmiExpress v1.0 Oct 31 1990, myself and that\n   works fine!)\n\n\n5. Aftertouch\n\n   First of all I want to thank a couple of people:\n\n   BamBam           - Let get the conference going!\n   Ted/Defjam       - Thanx for all the debugging help!\n   SpaZm/Fairlight  - A source of inspiration!\n   Mogwai/Defjam    - How''s that new BBS program comming?\n   The Baron/Defjam - Hope you''ll be able to take some time off soon.\n\n   And then for some greetings: (in NO order at all)\n\n   Prisoner of Wife, Bigfoot, In Decent, Cydric, Jabbah, Zin, BamBam,\n   Damage, Porta, Capricorn, Strider, Conqueror, Jetaza, Judge Dredd,\n   Raistlin, Winter Mute, Black Shadow, Blaizer, Irata, Spike,\n   Highlander, Archangel, Zcandaler, Splatt, Mr.Trax, The UnderTaker...\n\n   (Sorry, if I''ve forgotten someone.)\n\n   And of course to all HORIZON members!\n\n\n6. Credits and other Information\n\n   Programmed in Manx Aztec ''C'' for reliable and system-friendly code.\n\n   Programming:       Bryce! - Horizon\n\n   This util has been tested, and works 100% on: KickStart 1.2, 1.3, 2.0.\n   It has also been tested on various RAM set-ups, such as; 1 Mb chip, \n   0.5 Mb chip, 0.5 Mb chip & 0.5 Mb fast, 0.5 Mb chip & 4 Mb fast, 1 Mb \n   chip and 2 Mb fast, 1 Mb chip & 1 Mb fast, 2 Mb chip & 4 Mb 32 bit fast,\n   and this worked 100%. Processors tested with this util includes: 68000 \n   7.14 Mhz, 68030 25 MHz, and 68882 25 MHz, and no problems occured with \n   this either.\n\n   You can reach me (Bryce!), or check out my utils at my beta-testers:\n\n   The MainFrame   - Horizon EHQ   - +46-303-67301\n   DownTown        - Classic HQ    - +31-575029313\n   Marityrium      - Classic USHQ  -  713-666-4093\n   The Graveyard   - Agile UKHQ    - +44-915160560\n   West BBS        - Defjam SHQ    - +46-31-311879\n   Total Eclipse   - Aurora HQ     - +46-31-572545\n\n   Or try these util-making friends of mine''s boards:\n\n   Streets of Fire - Defjam SHQ    - +46-755-61537\n   Spaztic BBS     - Fairlight PHQ -  407-639-9123\n\n   Ok, I think that''s just about it, I guess... So, I''ll just let you\n   carry on with installing this great util, and say goodbye. See you\n   in the next production.\n\n                                 ...Bryce! ''91\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',9787,3,0,NULL,NULL,'msgtop','scan',1780048612);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mst_aeh2','MST-AEH2.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MST-AEH2.LHA',NULL,'XIM','______  ___/\____/\____/\__  ·  /\__       ·',NULL,NULL,'MST','_____ \/  /  /  /  ___/__  \/  / _  \.aXY! : ¦  / \_  /\_   /\_  \   /  /  /  /__/      ¦ `-/  /  /  /  /  /  /  /  /  /  /  /-------''',replace('______  ___/\____/\____/\__  ·  /\__       ·\n_____ \/  /  /  /  ___/__  \/  / _  \.aXY! :\n¦  / \_  /\_   /\_  \   /  /  /  /__/      ¦\n`-/  /  /  /  /  /  /  /  /  /  /  /-------''\n /  /  /  /  /  /  /  /  /  /  /  / PRESENTS\n/__/  /\__  /\__  /--/  /  /\__  /--------->\n  /__/  /__/  /__/  /__/  ·  /__/  ..IN 1996\n.------------------------------------------.\n|aE-hELP v1.1b eXPRESS v3+ hELP dOOR [XIM] :\n: rEMOTE oUTPUT bUGS fIXED!! tRESPASS/MST  |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'aMI-hELP.Guide',replace('@DATABASE "aMI-hELP.GUiDE"\n@REMARK	.-------------------------------------------------------.\n@REMARK  | This document should be read with AmigaGuide (OS 2.x) |\n@REMARK  | or MultiView (OS 3.x) or any other guide reader. Tnx. |\n@REMARK  `-------------------------------------------------------''\n@REMARK	$VER: aMI-hELP 1.1.b\n@WIDTH 80\n@NODE MAIN "aMI-hELP - MYSTiC /X pOWER 1996 - © 1996 tRESPASS/mYSTiC"\n                              Guide to aMI-hELP\n                     for Ami-Express Bulletin Board Systems\n\n                             Program version: 1.1.b\n                Compilation Date/Time: Sun Jan 14 13:42:11 1996\n\n                           © 1996 by @{"tRESPASS/mYSTiC" link Contact}\n\n                   ... another fine MYSTiC /X production ...\n\n      @{" First words... " link WhatIs}    What/Why is aMI-hELP?\n      @{" Features       " link Features}    What does it do?\n      @{" Installation   " link Install}    How to install aMI-hELP on your BBS\n      @{" Usage /X       " link AmiUsage}    How to operate with Ami-Express\n      @{" History        " link History}    Bugs/Fixs/Beta Testers     \n      @{" Greetings      " link Greetings}    Greetings, messages and contact info\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE WhatIs "What/Why is aMI-hELP? - © 1996 tRESPASS/mYSTiC"\n                         .---------------------------.\n                         |      What is aMI-hELP     |\n                         `---------------------------''\n\n   aMI-hELP is only the second Ami-Express help door I have seen. This door\n   is not just the same as the other one by ?? of ?? I cannot even remember\n   This Help door is Brilliant! (even if I do say so myself :-))\n\n   The ansi output is excellent with a Guest mYSTiC ansi from @{"pAINT/cLIQUE" link Contact}\n   a brilliant up-and-coming ascii artist.\n\n   Now I guess You may be wondering why I wrote such a door as aMI-hELP.!!\n   Buggered if I know!  No. There really was a reason. To use Express\n   naturally It requires a high level of inteligance. Some people namely\n   the leechers on your board simply dont have this inteligance level \n   required. So I wrote this for them leechers.\n\n   Also it is for people who are new to express so they can pick it up\n   quicker than of normal useage.\n\n   aMI-hELP is coded in 1oo% ASM POWER for fastest reactions to Your push\n   of a button :))\n\n   I wrote this door in a couple of days. the most time consumming part \n   was to add in all the help texts arrgh! was that boreing!, but I am\n   happy with the final results of this fine mYSTiC door and I hope You\n   enjoy its use??\n  \n   (Not that Youll need it) :))\n                                                      \n                                                       -tRESPASS/mYSTiC\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE Features "Features of aMI-hELP - © 1996 tRESPASS/mYSTiC"\n                        .------------------------------.\n                        |     Features of aMI-hELP     |\n                        `------------------------------''\n\n   Well It is fairly hard to make a features list for a Help door. But\n   I will do my best.\n\n                             Its a mYSTiC door RARAR!\n                             \n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE Install "How to install aMI-hELP - © 1996 tRESPASS/mYSTiC"\n                      .----------------------------------.\n                      |       Installation aMI-hELP      |\n                      `----------------------------------''\n\n              aMI-hELP  can  be installed like any /X 3.x+ command.\n\n                              copy ram:bbs/#? bbs:\n\n                 assuming You have unpacked the archive to ram:\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE AmiUsage "Usage in Ami-Express - © 1996 tRESPASS/mYSTiC"\n                          .------------------------.\n                          |  Usage in Ami-Express  |\n                          `------------------------''\n\n  To start Ami-Help from the bbs command line type h or Help and press\n  return. this will give you a menu looking similar to a bbs main menu\n  the greatness here is that now you can choose your command.\n\n      [G] for example and the follwing will pop up on the screen \n\n                       cOMMAND [G] - Goodbye/Logoff\n\n          this will be followed by a descriptve summary of the command\n          [G] and what it does. EG: Files still flagged etc etc!\n\n     This way Your users are not getting confused about flagged files!!!\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE History "The history of AE-Help © 1996 tRESPASS/mYSTiC"\n                        \n            \n      First Release 7th Jan 1995 aMI-hELP 1.0.b - Bug in remote output\n                               -  Thanks @{"cOMPUTEK" link Contact} for picking this up. \n                       \n      Second Release 14th Jan 1995 aMI-hELP 1.1.b - No known bugs    \n\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Greetings "Greetings go to... - © tRESPASS/mYSTiC"\n                            .-------------------.\n                            |  Greetings to...  |\n                            `-------------------''\n\n                       ALL MYSTiC MEMBERS WORLD-WIDE!\n                       ALL CLIQUE MEMBERS WORLD-WIDE!\n                      ALL INTENSITY MEMBERS WORLD-WIDE\n\n      mAGE/cLIQUE      -    I hope to see CC back very quickly\n      pANTERA/cLIQUE   -    Happy new year and things will be good in ''96\n      bODYcOUNT/cLIQUE -    sNIFF sNIFF whats that smell on Your finger?\n      sMASH/uSX        -    Tell me part 4 of Your plan please\n      pSYCHE/dVS/hF    -    Your a good guy, I hope to keep chatting to You.\n      rOADrUNNER/dVS   -    You should be more like your Organiser\n      pAINT/cLiQUE     -    Your ascii kicks! Soon some cool logos??\n      nIKE/tRSI        -    Cant wait to get back to iRC cuz!\n      fURY/pSG         -    No!! My modem isnt a 300baud! haha!\n      kURGAN/hONEY     -    Mate! What can I say.. Speak soon!\n      mADbOY/iNTENSITY -    Bloody Greeks!!\n      Maud''ib/rYL/hLM  -    hLM hQ Now hey. More nice warez for me to leech.\n      cYBERwULF/qTX    -    Been cool surfin with You.\n      \n            hAPPY nEW yEAR''S tO aLL i KNOW bUT fORGOT tO sAY hI tO!!\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE Contact "How to get in touch with me - © tRESPASS/mYSTiC"\n                             - ------------------.\n                            |  Contacting me...  |\n                            `------------------ - \n\n                 I can be reached on the following boards:\n\n                       - - -- --- ------- --- -- - -\n\n                The Undiscovered       +31-2294-1442   (USR 28k8)\n                                       +31-2294-4442   (USR 28k8)\n                                       +31-2294-tRY!   (USR 28k8)\n                \n                Dark Sun               +61-pRIVATE     (USR 28k8)\n                                       +61-pRIVATE     (USR 28k8)\n                                       +61-pRIVATE     (USR 28k8)\n\n                Death Row              +1-8o1-476-9o68 (USR 28k8) \n                                       +1-8o1-479-4678 (USR 28k8)\n                                       +1-8o1-476-8916 (USR 28k8)\n                                       +1-8o1-479-o267 (USR 28k8)\n                                       \n                TerraFirma             +61-9-2473025   (USR 16k8)                    \n\n                Wakeing Grounds        +61-8-2673144   (V-FAST28k8)\n             \n                The Slammer            +46-8-6230196   (USR 28k8)\n                                       +46-8-6231366   (USR 28k8)\n                \n                \n@ENDNODE         \n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,28219,5,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048612);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mst_bk13','MST-BK13.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MST-BK13.LHA','ByteKiller','XIM','ByteKillHandler',NULL,'(Mystic/X-DeSign)','MST','+---/    \ \/ / __/_  __/ / __/------------+ |--/ / / /\  /\  /-/ /-/ / /---ByteAndi----| |--\/ / /-/ /\  /-/ /-/ /\ \-----MsT-------|',replace('     ______  __________________             \n+---/    \ \/ / __/_  __/ / __/------------+\n|--/ / / /\  /\  /-/ /-/ / /---ByteAndi----|\n|--\/ / /-/ /\  /-/ /-/ /\ \-----MsT-------|\n+---\/\/--\/--\/--\/--\/--\/------X-DeSign-+\n|Bytekiller V1.3 with FAKE and NUKE OPTION |\n| ONE OF THE FASTES UP-DOWNLOADER SEARCHER |\n|       CONF_ACCOUNTING SUPPORTED          |\n|      written by (Mystic/X-DeSign)        |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'ByteKiller.guide',replace('@database Bytekiller.doc\n\nCopyright (c) 1993 by ByteAndi/MsT\n\n@Remark $VER: (December 28 1993, 14:30:00)\n@Remark AmigaGuide DataBase "Bytekiller" DoCuMeNTaTioN\n\n@node MAIN "BytekillerV1.3 DoCFiLe (c) 1993 BY ByteAndi/MsT (MYSTiC/X-DeSiGN)"\n _________________  ________________/\__________________    (/X-DeSiGN)\n \______________ _\/   /   /   ____// _____/___/___    /__________________|\n |.      /  /  / //___   //___   ./.  /   /   /   /___/.                 .|\n ||     /  /  / ./   /  ./   /  //   /   /   /   /   //      Presents    ||\n |:    /  /  /  /   /   /   /   /   /   /   /   /  //     Here And TodaY :|\n |____/  /  /  /   /   /   /   /   /_ _/   /   /  ./______________________|\n |:::/__/__/__/______ /______ /____ / /__ /______ /...:::::::::::::::Sk!n:|\n                    \/      \/    \/    \/      \/\n \n                      Bytekiller V1.3 by ByteAndi/MsT \n\n      --+-C-O-N-T-E-N-S--O-F--T-H-I-S--D-O-C-U-M-E-N-T-A-T-I-O-N-+--\n                \n      @{" I N T R O D U C T I O N " LINK C1}            @{" R E Q U I R E M E N T S " LINK C2}\n      @{" I N S T A L L A T I O N " LINK C3}            @{"    G R E E T I N G S    " LINK C4}\n      @{"    T O O L T Y P E S    " LINK C5}            @{"      C H A N G E S      " LINK C6}\n\n                      @{"S O M E  P R I V A T  W O R D S" LINK C7}\n\n\n      DoCFiLe WRiTTeN BY Axe/Mst & ByteAndi/MsT (c) BY (MYSTiC/X-DeSiGN)\n\n@endnode\n\n@node C2 "R E Q U I R E M E N T S..."\n\n                                  BYTEKILLER v1.3\n                              \nPackage of MST-BK13.lha :\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n         \n         doors:Bytekiller/Bytekiller                /X tool for NUKING\n                         /Bytekiller.info           .info for configuration\n                         /BytekillHandler           BytekillHandler as cli-tool\n                         /FakeMessage/              dir for UserComments\n                         /Bulls/                    dir for BullCreator\n         \n                                    /X 3.+ Version Reg.\n\n\n@endnode\n@node C1 "I N T R O D U C T I O N..."\n         \n     What BYTEKILLER is able to :\n     ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n     \n     CREAT FAKE-FILE :\n     ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n     If BYTEKILLER don`t find the Name of the File what you have insert,\n     he Ask if you want creat the File as FakeFile!\n\n     FREEDOWNLOAD :\n     ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n     BYTEKILLER can make some FreeDownloads if you Want!\n\n     FAKING :\n     ~~~~~~~~\n     BYTEKILLER makes it for normal people possible to FAKE files (means\n     they can write a comment to a file telling it is fake or old or...)\n     just like in the old AMIFAKER from TRSI.\n     \n     The sysop is able to search for those comments by using function "F"\n     of BKv1.3 and is able to nuke those files. The user can be given\n     a definated percent of the nuked files as upload bytes by the sysop.\n     \n     NUKING :\n     ~~~~~~~~\n     Function "I" of BKv1.3 makes it possible to type in as many files\n     as the computer allows. Now it is possible to nuke files with autonuke\n     mode (especially for nuking multiple disk releases in a amazing time or\n     giving 2* credits for majors ...) or in single mode or even make\n     FREEDOWNLOAD. To make a autonuke mode possible the tooltype "AUTONUKE" is\n     required.\n\n     Bytekiller Suports the CONF_ACCOUNTING for User !\n     \n     If the NewFiles V2.5 is out, you can Flag there Files to Nuke it with \n     the Bytekiller V1.3, BosNuke will insert the Same Option, so don`t be\n     worry if you mostly Like BosNuke!\n\n     Furthermore it is possible to make all nuke comments in the filelisting\n     in different colors and styles. So it is for example possible to\n     place a comment in "italic with green text on blue background"\n     thats simply generated with "3;44;32".\n     \n     Special greetins to Dr.Dre! for this idea and Remo of Mystic for the\n     configurating idea.\n     \n     Why using Bytekiller and not "%§+/&" :\n     ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n      WELL AFTER YOU SAW IT ONE TIME YOU WILL KNOW WHY ! IT IS THE FUCKING \n\n                                  B.E.S.T. !\n\n\n@endnode\n@node C3 "I N S T A L L A T I O N ..."\n\nSETTING UP :\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nThe Bytekillhandler in the archive should be started in the logoffscript\nof each of the nodes.\n\nEXAMPLE:\n\nBytekillHandler <path of callerslog of node>\n\nThis program makes sure that this nuker will find the uploader in a faster\nperiode than BOSSNUKE without the need of being started in a FILECHECK.INFO.\nEither this program generates a datafile that take space on your HD away !\n\nIt just writes behind every file the usernumber of the uploader what makes\nthis nuker to the fastest in finding the uploader.\n\n\nCopy the Directory of Bytekiller in your Doors: Directory and start \nBytekiller as XIM Door!\n\n@endnode\n@node C5 "T O O L T Y P E S ..."\n\n                      @{"         NUKER            " LINK NUKER}\n                      @{"      NUKER.<Number>      " LINK NUKER.<Number>}\n                      @{"      NUKER_PW.<1-x>      " LINK NUKER_PW.<1-x>}\n                      @{"   ACCESS_FREE.<Nummer>   " LINK ACCESS_FREE.<Nummer>}\n                      @{"    ACCESS_DEL.<Nummer>   " LINK ACCESS_FREE.<Nummer>}\n                      @{"       NODE.<0-x>         " LINK NODE.<0-x>}\n                      @{"    COMMENT.<1-998>       " LINK COMMENT.<1-998>}\n                      @{"     SIZE.<1-998>         " LINK SIZE.<1-998>}\n                      @{"     EXTERN_COMMENT       " LINK EXTERN_COMMENT}\n                      @{"      CREATE_DATAS        " LINK CREATE_DATAS}\n                      @{"        AUTONUKE          " LINK AUTONUKE}\n                      @{"     GREAT_MESSAGE        " LINK GREAT_MESSAGE}\n                      @{"     SHORT_MESSAGE        " LINK SHORT_MESSAGE}\n                      @{"        BOSSDATA          " LINK BOSSDATA}\n                      @{"    USER_FAKE_MESSAGE     " LINK USER_FAKE_MESSAGE}\n                      @{"     ACCOUNT_PER_CONF     " LINK ACCOUNT_PER_CONF}\n                      @{"       TAKE_COLOR         " LINK TAKE_COLOR}\n                      @{"       USER_COLOR         " LINK USER_COLOR}\n                      @{"       FREE_COLOR         " LINK FREE_COLOR}\n                      @{"       GIVE_COLOR         " LINK GIVE_COLOR}\n\n@endnode\n@node NUKER "NUKER ..."\n\n                 NUKER=<what amount of Nuker or "ALL"> \n\n         If this is ALL, all user with a level selected in \n         "bbs:commands/bbscmd/nuke.info" can start the nuker !\n   But "USER_FAKE_MESSAGE=<percent>" is not possible anymore in this case !\n\n@endnode\n@node NUKER.<Number> "NUKER.<Number> ..."\n\n                        NUKER.<Number>=<NukerName>\n\n    Is "NUKER=<1-x>" selected, so everyone allowed to nuke must get a number\n    and at "NUKERNAME" must be his user name !\n\n@endnode\n\n@node NUKER_PW.<1-x> "NUKER_PW.<1-x>...."\n\n                         NUKER_PW.<1-x>=<Password>\n\n             If available it will ask for a personell password !\n             Not needed.\n@endnode\n\n\n@node ACCESS_FREE.<Nummer> "NUKER.<Number> ..."\n\n                          ACCESS_FREE.<Nummer>\n                          ACCESS_DEL.<Nummer>\n\nTo allow a special user to delete and make FreeDownload files.\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n                            ACCESS_FREE\n                            ACCESS_DEL\n\nallows all users with his Name in the .info File to delete files or make \nthem freedownload \n\nit is only possible to use one of these tooltypes.\n\nper user "ACCESS_FREE.<Nummer>" or for ALL users in the List "ACCESS_FREE"\n\n@endnode\n@node NODE.<0-x> "NODE.<0-x>..."\n\n                     NODE.<0-x>=<full path for Callerslog> \n\nAll nodes with callerslog or udlog path. The nodes must be writen from\n"0-x", if "NODE0" is local node you have to write for NODE1 :\n\nNODE.0=<full path for Callerslog>\n\n@endnode\n@node COMMENT.<1-998> "COMMENT.<1-998>...."\n\n                  COMMENT.<1-998>=<Comments for the Filelisting>\n\n           There are 1-998 different comments possible you can type.\n           The options NONE and OTHER are done by the nuker himself.\n\n@endnode\n@node SIZE.<1-998> "SIZE.<1-998>...."\n\n            SIZE.<1-998>=<Comments for the Size in the List>\n\n              Same as COMMENT just for the BYTECOMMENTS\n\n@endnode\n@node EXTERN_COMMENT "EXTERN_COMMENT......"\n\n\n                            EXTERN_COMMENT\n\n   allows 5 more lines for the uploader that will be in the nukermessage.\n\n               !!!  NOT POSSIBLE IN AUTONUKE MODE.  !!!\n\n@endnode\n@node CREATE_DATAS "CREATE_DATAS....."\n\n                           CREATE_DATAS\n\nThis will create extern datafiles with the users who got nuked and allows\nthe nuker to see the list of the nuked user.\n\nIt is possible to make bulls out of these datas.\n\n               Please use " BuLLCReaToR V1.0 " by Siegel/mst\n\n@endnode\n@node AUTONUKE "AUTONUKE....."\n\n                             AUTONUKE\n\nThis allows to nuke alot of files at one time (WILDCARDS, after 3 letters\nalways allowed)\n\nIn this mode all needed options will be asked by the nuker and used on\nall the files after.\n\n@endnode\n@node GREAT_MESSAGE "GREAT_MESSAGE......"\n\n                            GREAT_MESSAGE\n\nWrites a big message to the up/down-loader in old NOSNUKE style with more\ninformations.\n\n@endnode\n@node SHORT_MESSAGE "SHORT_MESSAGE...."\n\n                             SHORT_MESSAGE \n\n          Writes messages in Old BOSNUKE format with more informations.\n\n@endnode\n@node BOSSDATA "BOSSDATA....."\n\n                               BOSSDATA\n\nIf you still don´t trust my filehandler you can use the old one from bosnuke\nand let udlog.x as filecheck.info work.\n\n@endnode\n@node USER_FAKE_MESSAGE "USER_FAKE_MESSAGE........."\n\n                        USER_FAKE_MESSAGE=<1-100%>\n\nAllows user to write a message in filelisting and for that getting (IF the\nfile gets nuked) a percent <1-100%> of bytes of the nuked file. There will\nbe no message writeen to the user about that. Only the first user that\nnoticed the fake will get credits.\n\n@endnode\n@node ACCOUNT_PER_CONF "ACCOUNT_PER_CONF...."\n\n                           ACCOUNT_PER_CONF\n\n     If one or more user got ConfAccounting you will need this tooltype.\n\n@endnode\n@node TAKE_COLOR "TAKE_COLOR...."\n\n                            TAKE_COLOR=36       \n\nWill show a comments with option "TAKEN" in a special color. Here blue.\n\n@endnode\n@node USER_COLOR "USER_COLOR......"\n\n                            USER_COLOR=44       \n\nSame as take_color just for the USER COMMENTS.\n\n@endnode\n@node FREE_COLOR "FREE_COLOR......"\n\n                            FREE_COLOR=3;31     \n\n      Same as take_color but will show FREEDOWNLOAD in special colors\n      Here red and italic.\n\n@endnode\n@node GIVE_COLOR "GIVE_COLOR....."\n\n                            GIVE_COLOR=3;44;32\n\n    Same again but for option "GIVEN" here italic, blue background and \n    green letters.\n@endnode\n\n@node C6 "Changes....."\n\n\n            I have removed the Mover Option, because the programm is \n            now to Complex to include this option again!\n\n            Changes by the Uploader Search, \n            three-Way search : BOSDATA, Bytekillhandler and Callerslog!\n            I think Bytekiller is in ALL ways The Fastes UP-DownLoader searcher!\n\n            Changes by the msgroutine....to many sysops Fake`s in her\n            msgbase!\n\n            Installed AutoNuke and Faker modus\n\n            Installed the option to Add Colors in the DirListing\n\n            Install two options for the Messages to the Up-Downloader\n\n            I have changed the menu options because some sysops have written\n            that they are to stupid to understand the options!\n\n\n@endnode\n@node C4 "Greetings To EveryOne"\n\n                               -G-R-E-E-T-I-N-G-S-\n\n  Many Greetings to Empire and the Other @{" Member from (Mystic/X-Design) "LINK MSTMEMBER}\n\n  Killraven, Fuzzy, Axe....\n\n  THX to Spy because he helped me to learn C  and invested many \n  Time in my Doors\n\n  Many Many THX To All my Beta tester for BugReports, Hints and Tips\n  to install Options....in that Door...\n\n  To All Friends over the Globe wich Knows us!\n\n             //\n  Thanx to \X/ Amiga For Being The Best Computer Ever made ...\n\n\n\n\n            And some other wonderfull Ami-Express Tool Programmers ...\n\n                                 @{" 5th  Dynasty " Link 5thDynasty}\n\n                            And Last But Not Least ...\n\n             All Ex-Members Of AFL That We Have Met Over The Years...\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node 5thDynasty\n\n\n               5th______  ___  __  ___   _____  _. ___  ___\n               \\__   \\  \\/  /_|  |/___\\ / ___/_/ |_\\  \\/  /\n                |  |  \\_/ _/__\\  |  /  |___  \\_   _/\\_/ _/\n                |  |  ||  ||  \\\\_| /   |     ||   |  |  |\n                |  |  ||  ||  |\\_| \\_  |SNOW ||   |  |  |\n                |_____||__||__|__|__|__|_____||___|  |__|\n\nIf you want to program something yourself ... just ask us for the source and we\nwill see what we can do ... Will probable give you the source with\ndocumentation included so you know what you see in it ...\n\nP.S.: Nothing Personal ... Just nice to have some people around who can\nprogram as good as other people already did ... Always nice to have people\naround who want to give you their sources ...\n\n@endnode\n\n\n@node MSTMEMBER "ALL MEMBERS FROM (MYSTIC/X-DESIGN)"\n\n                      ______  __________________          \n               +-----/    \ \/ / __/_  __/ / __/----------+\n               |----/ / / /\  /\  /-/ /-/ / /----[ /X ]---|\n               |----\/ / /-/ /\  /-/ /-/ /\ \--[ DESiGN ]-|\n               +-----\/\/--\/--\/--\/--\/--\/-------------+\n               |                                          |\n               |   EMPiRE   -   @{"BYTEANDi" LINK DIABOLO}   -  CRACKDOWN  |\n               |   TYCOON   -   KiLLRAVEN  -   SiEGEL     |\n               |   FUZZY    -     SPY      - Re/Y\o       |\n               +------------------------------------------+\n@endnode\n@node DIABOLO "Advert"\n                        ·  :                 .     :     :\n-============-   \____ ¬V ¬V___ ¬V___ ¬V___ ¬V ¬|  |___ ¬|   MANAGEMENT\n(Mystic/X-Design) | ¬|  |  | ¬|  | ¬|  | ¬|  |  |  | ¬|  |   -========-\n      WHQ         |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |   ANDi/MST\n-============-    |  |  |  |     |    _|  |  |  |__|  |  |   SPY/MST\n                  |  |  |  |  |  |  | ¬|  |  |  | ¬|  |  |   FELDMAN\n-ELiTE oNLY-      |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |   FuZzY/MsT\n                  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |   Wolfmann/TRSI\nCALL US NoW FoR   |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |   -====-\nTHE NEWEST AMiGA/ |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |   RUNS oN A3000\nPC&Console STUFF  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |   WiTH 25MHZ AND\nAND ALL MST-      |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |   AMiEX (REG.)\nRELEASES.         |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n                __|_____A__A__A__A_____A_____A_____A_____|D! SUPPoRTED BY\nWE oNLY ACCEPT    |     :  :     :     :     :     :     |   -==========-\n9600 - 16.800     :     ·  .     .           .     ·     :   M Y S T I C\nBAUD CoNNECTS.    .        .                                      \n                         Node0  +49 (0) 30-6221994   HST\n                         Node1  +49 (0) 30-6212312   Zyxel\n                         Node2  +49 (0) 30-6218787   Dual\n\n@endnode\n\n@node C7 "S O M E  P R I V A T  W O R D S..."\n\n    I Invest here many Times to Code the Best Doors what I can for You,\n    and all Doors where be tested on Some Month in many Boards, but we don`t\n    can Find All small BUGS, so PLEASE don`t write me any think, How Lame\n    my Doors because a Little Fake, or while the /X Author have changed any \n    in his /X Code! If you find any than Contact me on the /X WHQ or in \n    the 4 AM BBS from Flatliner and I will fix the BUGS so Fast as I can!\n\n    If you Like the (Mystic/X-Design) Doors or have any suggestions about \n    other Doors, than please leave a Mail!\n\n                           Byteandi (Mystic/X-Design)\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',49987,5,1,'bk','Doors/bytekiller','mst_bk13','scan',1780048612);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mst_bk14','MST-BK14.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MST-BK14.LHA','Bytekiller','XIM','ByteKillHandler',NULL,'(Mystic/X-DeSign)','MST','+---/    \ \/ / __/_  __/ / __/------------+ |--/ / / /\  /\  /-/ /-/ / /---ByteAndi----| |--\/ / /-/ /\  /-/ /-/ /\ \-----MsT-------|',replace('     ______  __________________             \n+---/    \ \/ / __/_  __/ / __/------------+\n|--/ / / /\  /\  /-/ /-/ / /---ByteAndi----|\n|--\/ / /-/ /\  /-/ /-/ /\ \-----MsT-------|\n+---\/\/--\/--\/--\/--\/--\/------X-DeSign-+\n|Bytekiller V1.4 with FAKE and NUKE OPTION |\n|           UPDATE without BUG             |\n|      written by (Mystic/X-DeSign)        |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'ByteKiller.guide',replace('@database Bytekiller.doc\n\nCopyright (c) 1993 by ByteAndi/MsT\n\n@Remark $VER: (December 28 1993, 14:30:00)\n@Remark AmigaGuide DataBase "Bytekiller" DoCuMeNTaTioN\n\n@node MAIN "BytekillerV1.4 DoCFiLe (c) 1993 BY ByteAndi/MsT (MYSTiC/X-DeSiGN)"\n _________________  ________________/\__________________    (/X-DeSiGN)\n \______________ _\/   /   /   ____// _____/___/___    /__________________|\n |.      /  /  / //___   //___   ./.  /   /   /   /___/.                 .|\n ||     /  /  / ./   /  ./   /  //   /   /   /   /   //      Presents    ||\n |:    /  /  /  /   /   /   /   /   /   /   /   /  //     Here And TodaY :|\n |____/  /  /  /   /   /   /   /   /_ _/   /   /  ./______________________|\n |:::/__/__/__/______ /______ /____ / /__ /______ /...:::::::::::::::Sk!n:|\n                    \/      \/    \/    \/      \/\n \n                      Bytekiller V1.4 by ByteAndi/MsT \n\n      --+-C-O-N-T-E-N-S--O-F--T-H-I-S--D-O-C-U-M-E-N-T-A-T-I-O-N-+--\n                \n      @{" I N T R O D U C T I O N " LINK C1}            @{" R E Q U I R E M E N T S " LINK C2}\n      @{" I N S T A L L A T I O N " LINK C3}            @{"    G R E E T I N G S    " LINK C4}\n      @{"    T O O L T Y P E S    " LINK C5}            @{"      C H A N G E S      " LINK C6}\n\n                      @{"S O M E  P R I V A T  W O R D S" LINK C7}\n\n\n      DoCFiLe WRiTTeN BY Axe/Mst & ByteAndi/MsT (c) BY (MYSTiC/X-DeSiGN)\n\n@endnode\n\n@node C2 "R E Q U I R E M E N T S..."\n\n                                  BYTEKILLER v1.4\n                              \nPackage of MST-BK13.lha :\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n         \n         doors:Bytekiller/Bytekiller                /X tool for NUKING\n                         /Bytekiller.info           .info for configuration\n                         /BytekillHandler           BytekillHandler as cli-tool\n                         /FakeMessage/              dir for UserComments\n                         /Bulls/                    dir for BullCreator\n         \n                                    /X 3.+ Version Reg.\n\n\n@endnode\n@node C1 "I N T R O D U C T I O N..."\n         \n     What BYTEKILLER is able to :\n     ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n     \n     CREAT FAKE-FILE :\n     ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n     If BYTEKILLER don`t find the Name of the File what you have insert,\n     he Ask if you want creat the File as FakeFile!\n\n     FREEDOWNLOAD :\n     ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n     BYTEKILLER can make some FreeDownloads if you Want!\n\n     FAKING :\n     ~~~~~~~~\n     BYTEKILLER makes it for normal people possible to FAKE files (means\n     they can write a comment to a file telling it is fake or old or...)\n     just like in the old AMIFAKER from TRSI.\n     \n     The sysop is able to search for those comments by using function "F"\n     of BKv1.4 and is able to nuke those files. The user can be given\n     a definated percent of the nuked files as upload bytes by the sysop.\n     \n     NUKING :\n     ~~~~~~~~\n     Function "I" of BKV1.4 makes it possible to type in as many files\n     as the computer allows. Now it is possible to nuke files with autonuke\n     mode (especially for nuking multiple disk releases in a amazing time or\n     giving 2* credits for majors ...) or in single mode or even make\n     FREEDOWNLOAD. To make a autonuke mode possible the tooltype "AUTONUKE" is\n     required.\n\n     Bytekiller Suports the CONF_ACCOUNTING for User !\n     \n     If the NewFiles V2.5 is out, you can Flag there Files to Nuke it with \n     the Bytekiller V1.4, BosNuke will insert the Same Option, so don`t be\n     worry if you mostly Like BosNuke!\n\n     Furthermore it is possible to make all nuke comments in the filelisting\n     in different colors and styles. So it is for example possible to\n     place a comment in "italic with green text on blue background"\n     thats simply generated with "3;44;32".\n     \n     Special greetins to Dr.Dre! for this idea and Remo of Mystic for the\n     configurating idea.\n     \n     Why using Bytekiller and not "%§+/&" :\n     ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n      WELL AFTER YOU SAW IT ONE TIME YOU WILL KNOW WHY ! IT IS THE FUCKING \n\n                                  B.E.S.T. !\n\n\n@endnode\n@node C3 "I N S T A L L A T I O N ..."\n\nSETTING UP :\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nThe Bytekillhandler in the archive should be started in the logoffscript\nof each of the nodes.\n\nEXAMPLE:\n\nBytekillHandler <path of callerslog of node>\n\nThis program makes sure that this nuker will find the uploader in a faster\nperiode than BOSSNUKE without the need of being started in a FILECHECK.INFO.\nEither this program generates a datafile that take space on your HD away !\n\nIt just writes behind every file the usernumber of the uploader what makes\nthis nuker to the fastest in finding the uploader.\n\n\nCopy the Directory of Bytekiller in your Doors: Directory and start \nBytekiller as XIM Door!\n\n@endnode\n@node C5 "T O O L T Y P E S ..."\n\n                      @{"         NUKER            " LINK NUKER}\n                      @{"      NUKER.<Number>      " LINK NUKER.<Number>}\n                      @{"      NUKER_PW.<1-x>      " LINK NUKER_PW.<1-x>}\n                      @{"   ACCESS_FREE.<Nummer>   " LINK ACCESS_FREE.<Nummer>}\n                      @{"    ACCESS_DEL.<Nummer>   " LINK ACCESS_FREE.<Nummer>}\n                      @{"       NODE.<0-x>         " LINK NODE.<0-x>}\n                      @{"    COMMENT.<1-998>       " LINK COMMENT.<1-998>}\n                      @{"     SIZE.<1-998>         " LINK SIZE.<1-998>}\n                      @{"     EXTERN_COMMENT       " LINK EXTERN_COMMENT}\n                      @{"      CREATE_DATAS        " LINK CREATE_DATAS}\n                      @{"        AUTONUKE          " LINK AUTONUKE}\n                      @{"     GREAT_MESSAGE        " LINK GREAT_MESSAGE}\n                      @{"     SHORT_MESSAGE        " LINK SHORT_MESSAGE}\n                      @{"        BOSSDATA          " LINK BOSSDATA}\n                      @{"    USER_FAKE_MESSAGE     " LINK USER_FAKE_MESSAGE}\n                      @{"     ACCOUNT_PER_CONF     " LINK ACCOUNT_PER_CONF}\n                      @{"       TAKE_COLOR         " LINK TAKE_COLOR}\n                      @{"       USER_COLOR         " LINK USER_COLOR}\n                      @{"       FREE_COLOR         " LINK FREE_COLOR}\n                      @{"       GIVE_COLOR         " LINK GIVE_COLOR}\n\n@endnode\n@node NUKER "NUKER ..."\n\n                 NUKER=<what amount of Nuker or "ALL"> \n\n         If this is ALL, all user with a level selected in \n         "bbs:commands/bbscmd/nuke.info" can start the nuker !\n   But "USER_FAKE_MESSAGE=<percent>" is not possible anymore in this case !\n\n@endnode\n@node NUKER.<Number> "NUKER.<Number> ..."\n\n                        NUKER.<Number>=<NukerName>\n\n    Is "NUKER=<1-x>" selected, so everyone allowed to nuke must get a number\n    and at "NUKERNAME" must be his user name !\n\n@endnode\n\n@node NUKER_PW.<1-x> "NUKER_PW.<1-x>...."\n\n                         NUKER_PW.<1-x>=<Password>\n\n             If available it will ask for a personell password !\n             Not needed.\n@endnode\n\n\n@node ACCESS_FREE.<Nummer> "NUKER.<Number> ..."\n\n                          ACCESS_FREE.<Nummer>\n                          ACCESS_DEL.<Nummer>\n\nTo allow a special user to delete and make FreeDownload files.\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n                            ACCESS_FREE\n                            ACCESS_DEL\n\nallows all users with his Name in the .info File to delete files or make \nthem freedownload \n\nit is only possible to use one of these tooltypes.\n\nper user "ACCESS_FREE.<Nummer>" or for ALL users in the List "ACCESS_FREE"\n\n@endnode\n@node NODE.<0-x> "NODE.<0-x>..."\n\n                     NODE.<0-x>=<full path for Callerslog> \n\nAll nodes with callerslog or udlog path. The nodes must be writen from\n"0-x", if "NODE0" is local node you have to write for NODE1 :\n\nNODE.0=<full path for Callerslog>\n\n@endnode\n@node COMMENT.<1-998> "COMMENT.<1-998>...."\n\n                  COMMENT.<1-998>=<Comments for the Filelisting>\n\n           There are 1-998 different comments possible you can type.\n           The options NONE and OTHER are done by the nuker himself.\n\n@endnode\n@node SIZE.<1-998> "SIZE.<1-998>...."\n\n            SIZE.<1-998>=<Comments for the Size in the List>\n\n              Same as COMMENT just for the BYTECOMMENTS\n\n@endnode\n@node EXTERN_COMMENT "EXTERN_COMMENT......"\n\n\n                            EXTERN_COMMENT\n\n   allows 5 more lines for the uploader that will be in the nukermessage.\n\n               !!!  NOT POSSIBLE IN AUTONUKE MODE.  !!!\n\n@endnode\n@node CREATE_DATAS "CREATE_DATAS....."\n\n                           CREATE_DATAS\n\nThis will create extern datafiles with the users who got nuked and allows\nthe nuker to see the list of the nuked user.\n\nIt is possible to make bulls out of these datas.\n\n               Please use " BuLLCReaToR V1.0 " by Siegel/mst\n\n@endnode\n@node AUTONUKE "AUTONUKE....."\n\n                             AUTONUKE\n\nThis allows to nuke alot of files at one time (WILDCARDS, after 3 letters\nalways allowed)\n\nIn this mode all needed options will be asked by the nuker and used on\nall the files after.\n\n@endnode\n@node GREAT_MESSAGE "GREAT_MESSAGE......"\n\n                            GREAT_MESSAGE\n\nWrites a big message to the up/down-loader in old NOSNUKE style with more\ninformations.\n\n@endnode\n@node SHORT_MESSAGE "SHORT_MESSAGE...."\n\n                             SHORT_MESSAGE \n\n          Writes messages in Old BOSNUKE format with more informations.\n\n@endnode\n@node BOSSDATA "BOSSDATA....."\n\n                               BOSSDATA\n\nIf you still don´t trust my filehandler you can use the old one from bosnuke\nand let udlog.x as filecheck.info work.\n\n@endnode\n@node USER_FAKE_MESSAGE "USER_FAKE_MESSAGE........."\n\n                        USER_FAKE_MESSAGE=<1-100%>\n\nAllows user to write a message in filelisting and for that getting (IF the\nfile gets nuked) a percent <1-100%> of bytes of the nuked file. There will\nbe no message writeen to the user about that. Only the first user that\nnoticed the fake will get credits.\n\n@endnode\n@node ACCOUNT_PER_CONF "ACCOUNT_PER_CONF...."\n\n                           ACCOUNT_PER_CONF\n\n     If one or more user got ConfAccounting you will need this tooltype.\n\n@endnode\n@node TAKE_COLOR "TAKE_COLOR...."\n\n                            TAKE_COLOR=36       \n\nWill show a comments with option "TAKEN" in a special color. Here blue.\n\n@endnode\n@node USER_COLOR "USER_COLOR......"\n\n                            USER_COLOR=44       \n\nSame as take_color just for the USER COMMENTS.\n\n@endnode\n@node FREE_COLOR "FREE_COLOR......"\n\n                            FREE_COLOR=3;31     \n\n      Same as take_color but will show FREEDOWNLOAD in special colors\n      Here red and italic.\n\n@endnode\n@node GIVE_COLOR "GIVE_COLOR....."\n\n                            GIVE_COLOR=3;44;32\n\n    Same again but for option "GIVEN" here italic, blue background and \n    green letters.\n@endnode\n\n@node C6 "Changes....."\n\n\nBytekillerV1.3\n\n            I have removed the Mover Option, because the programm is \n            now to Complex to include this option again!\n\n            Changes by the Uploader Search, \n            three-Way search : BOSDATA, Bytekillhandler and Callerslog!\n            I think Bytekiller is in ALL ways The Fastes UP-DownLoader searcher!\n\n            Changes by the msgroutine....to many sysops Fake`s in her\n            msgbase!\n\n            Installed AutoNuke and Faker modus\n\n            Installed the option to Add Colors in the DirListing\n\n            Install two options for the Messages to the Up-Downloader\n\n            I have changed the menu options because some sysops have written\n            that they are to stupid to understand the options!\n\nBytekillerV1.4\n\n            removed the Bug in the Fake from list Option!\n\n\n\n@endnode\n@node C4 "Greetings To EveryOne"\n\n                               -G-R-E-E-T-I-N-G-S-\n\n  Many Greetings to Empire and the Other @{" Member from (Mystic/X-Design) "LINK MSTMEMBER}\n\n  Killraven, Fuzzy, Axe....\n\n  THX to Spy because he helped me to learn C  and invested many \n  Time in my Doors\n\n  Many Many THX To All my Beta tester for BugReports, Hints and Tips\n  to install Options....in that Door...\n\n  To All Friends over the Globe wich Knows us!\n\n             //\n  Thanx to \X/ Amiga For Being The Best Computer Ever made ...\n\n\n\n\n            And some other wonderfull Ami-Express Tool Programmers ...\n\n                                 @{" 5th  Dynasty " Link 5thDynasty}\n\n                            And Last But Not Least ...\n\n             All Ex-Members Of AFL That We Have Met Over The Years...\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node 5thDynasty\n\n\n               5th______  ___  __  ___   _____  _. ___  ___\n               \\__   \\  \\/  /_|  |/___\\ / ___/_/ |_\\  \\/  /\n                |  |  \\_/ _/__\\  |  /  |___  \\_   _/\\_/ _/\n                |  |  ||  ||  \\\\_| /   |     ||   |  |  |\n                |  |  ||  ||  |\\_| \\_  |SNOW ||   |  |  |\n                |_____||__||__|__|__|__|_____||___|  |__|\n\nIf you want to program something yourself ... just ask us for the source and we\nwill see what we can do ... Will probable give you the source with\ndocumentation included so you know what you see in it ...\n\nP.S.: Nothing Personal ... Just nice to have some people around who can\nprogram as good as other people already did ... Always nice to have people\naround who want to give you their sources ...\n\n@endnode\n\n\n@node MSTMEMBER "ALL MEMBERS FROM (MYSTIC/X-DESIGN)"\n\n                      ______  __________________          \n               +-----/    \ \/ / __/_  __/ / __/----------+\n               |----/ / / /\  /\  /-/ /-/ / /----[ /X ]---|\n               |----\/ / /-/ /\  /-/ /-/ /\ \--[ DESiGN ]-|\n               +-----\/\/--\/--\/--\/--\/--\/-------------+\n               |                                          |\n               |   EMPiRE   -   @{"BYTEANDi" LINK DIABOLO}   -  CRACKDOWN  |\n               |   TYCOON   -   KiLLRAVEN  -   SiEGEL     |\n               |   FUZZY    -     SPY      - Re/Y\o       |\n               +------------------------------------------+\n@endnode\n@node DIABOLO "Advert"\n                        ·  :                 .     :     :\n-============-   \____ ¬V ¬V___ ¬V___ ¬V___ ¬V ¬|  |___ ¬|   MANAGEMENT\n(Mystic/X-Design) | ¬|  |  | ¬|  | ¬|  | ¬|  |  |  | ¬|  |   -========-\n      WHQ         |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |   ANDi/MST\n-============-    |  |  |  |     |    _|  |  |  |__|  |  |   SPY/MST\n                  |  |  |  |  |  |  | ¬|  |  |  | ¬|  |  |   FELDMAN\n-ELiTE oNLY-      |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |   FuZzY/MsT\n                  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |   Wolfmann/TRSI\nCALL US NoW FoR   |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |   -====-\nTHE NEWEST AMiGA/ |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |   RUNS oN A3000\nPC&Console STUFF  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |   WiTH 25MHZ AND\nAND ALL MST-      |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |   AMiEX (REG.)\nRELEASES.         |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n                __|_____A__A__A__A_____A_____A_____A_____|D! SUPPoRTED BY\nWE oNLY ACCEPT    |     :  :     :     :     :     :     |   -==========-\n9600 - 16.800     :     ·  .     .           .     ·     :   M Y S T I C\nBAUD CoNNECTS.    .        .                                      \n                         Node0  +49 (0) 30-6221994   HST\n                         Node1  +49 (0) 30-6212312   Zyxel\n                         Node2  +49 (0) 30-6218787   Dual\n\n@endnode\n\n@node C7 "S O M E  P R I V A T  W O R D S..."\n\n    I Invest here many Times to Code the Best Doors what I can for You,\n    and all Doors where be tested on Some Month in many Boards, but we don`t\n    can Find All small BUGS, so PLEASE don`t write me any think, How Lame\n    my Doors because a Little Fake, or while the /X Author have changed any \n    in his /X Code! If you find any than Contact me on the /X WHQ or in \n    the 4 AM BBS from Flatliner and I will fix the BUGS so Fast as I can!\n\n    If you Like the (Mystic/X-Design) Doors or have any suggestions about \n    other Doors, than please leave a Mail!\n\n                           Byteandi (Mystic/X-Design)\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',48223,5,1,'bk','Doors/bytekiller','mst_bk14','scan',1780048612);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mst_bstt','MST-BSTT.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MST-BSTT.LHA',NULL,'XIM','LE-win5-96.exe',NULL,NULL,'MST',NULL,replace('-\n','\n',char(10)),'lOSeNDOS.guide',replace('                   \n                     __  _ __  /\__ _  _ __/\  __ _  __\n                    _\/___   \/              \/   ___\/_\n              ......\/\  /........................\  /\/......\n             :         \/                          \/         :\n             :      .___             .___         .___        :\n             :   _ _|   \      ______|   \  ______|   \       :\n             :   \\\__   7___  \______   /  \__   ____/       :\n             :      /.   |   \__/.  l/   \___/_____   \__ _   :\n             :     /::.  |    _/::.       _/::.  l/    _///   :\n             :     \___________\___________\____________\     :\n             :___        .___        .___        .___         :___\n     _ ______|   \ ______|   \ ______|   \ ______|   \  ______|   \\n     \\\__   ____/ \______   / \______   / \______   /  \__   ____/\n        /.   ___|___/.   |   \__/.  _|   \__/.  l/   \___/_____   \__ _\n       /::.  l/   _/::.  |    _/::. \___  _/::.       _/::.  l/    _///\n       \_ _________\_____|_____\___________\___________\___________ \\n         Y   :                                                :[nM$]Y\n      .------''                                                `------.\n      :eXON/rIOT^jORMAS · gHANDY/gODS · rAHIEM/eSSENCE · cELIC/rEKTUM: \n      `------.                                                .------''\n             `------------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',71035,7,0,NULL,NULL,'mst_bstt','scan',1780048612);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mst_ca12','MST-CA12.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MST-CA12.LHA',NULL,'XIM','LE-win5-96.exe',NULL,NULL,'MST','|__ ______\   \____  /   /_________|____ /   |  \   /   /___/_/  ___/______/  ___/__ /        \___  /____  \   \   /    \  \    /',replace('  .--------[____ mYSTIC ____]--------.\n  |__ ______\   \____  /   /_________|____\n /   |  \   /   /___/_/  ___/______/  ___/__\n/        \___  /____  \   \   /    \  \    /\n\___\/   /____/    /  /______/_____/______/\n  | /___/   \________/AdN!          _|_\n  |                                 \_/\n  |  cALLERSLOG 1.2 fOR lOGIC bBS    |\n  | 100% fIXED - iNC iFF sCREENsHOT  |\n  |                                  |\n  `-[LoGIC DeVELOPeMENT]-[/X cOMPAT]-''\n-//-[fLYING DraGON-//-HF^iFT^dLT^oTL^rEA-\\-\n','\n',char(10)),'lOSeNDOS.guide',replace('                   \n                     __  _ __  /\__ _  _ __/\  __ _  __\n                    _\/___   \/              \/   ___\/_\n              ......\/\  /........................\  /\/......\n             :         \/                          \/         :\n             :      .___             .___         .___        :\n             :   _ _|   \      ______|   \  ______|   \       :\n             :   \\\__   7___  \______   /  \__   ____/       :\n             :      /.   |   \__/.  l/   \___/_____   \__ _   :\n             :     /::.  |    _/::.       _/::.  l/    _///   :\n             :     \___________\___________\____________\     :\n             :___        .___        .___        .___         :___\n     _ ______|   \ ______|   \ ______|   \ ______|   \  ______|   \\n     \\\__   ____/ \______   / \______   / \______   /  \__   ____/\n        /.   ___|___/.   |   \__/.  _|   \__/.  l/   \___/_____   \__ _\n       /::.  l/   _/::.  |    _/::. \___  _/::.       _/::.  l/    _///\n       \_ _________\_____|_____\___________\___________\___________ \\n         Y   :                                                :[nM$]Y\n      .------''                                                `------.\n      :eXON/rIOT^jORMAS · gHANDY/gODS · rAHIEM/eSSENCE · cELIC/rEKTUM: \n      `------.                                                .------''\n             `------------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',29726,11,0,NULL,NULL,'mst_ca12','scan',1780048612);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mst_cf22','MST_CF22.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MST_CF22.LHA',NULL,'XIM','LE-win5-96.exe',NULL,NULL,'MST','.---/    \ \/ / __/_  __/ / __/------------. |--/ / / /\  /\  /-/ /-/ / /---Bobo--------| |--\/ / /-/ /\  /-/ /-/ /\ \----Mystic-----|',replace('     ______  __________________\n.---/    \ \/ / __/_  __/ / __/------------.\n|--/ / / /\  /\  /-/ /-/ / /---Bobo--------|\n|--\/ / /-/ /\  /-/ /-/ /\ \----Mystic-----|\n|---\/\/--\/--\/--\/--\/--\/-----/X-Design-|\n|-----AND LOOBY INSANE /X DEVELOPMENT------|\n|..Conference Top Uploaders (Version 2.2)..|\n|.The Ultimate Weektop Tool for Amiexpress.|\n|.....Features: Online Updating, Fast!.....|\n|...Works without Conference Accounting!...|\n|.Inbuilt Config Program for Easy Install!.|\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'Conftop.Doc',replace('   ____ _________________   _______________________ _ _______________\n --\__ Y ____ __________/---\_____ ___ ______ ____// \\__ ________  /----\n    / \ / \/_____\/   \  /X  /   Y \/  _)__/_____\/   \/  l_ \/  Y  \ \n   /   Y   \    ! \    \    /    !  \      \    ! \    \      \  |   \\n --\___|_  /____  /__  /----\_____  /____  /____  /__  /____  /__|_  /---\n         \/     \/   \/           \/     \/     \/   \/     \/   ML\/\n          W·E  P·R·O·D·U·C·E  F·O·R  Y·O·U·R  C·O·M·F·O·R·T !\n\n                    PRESENTS A NEW MAJOR PRODUCT >:\n\n   Conference Top Uploaders v2.2 (Door) for Amiexpress BBS (Release 1)\n   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n         Authers: BOBO & LOOBY   Favourite Board: The East BBS\n          Door Requirements: AmigaDOS2.0 & Amiexpress 2.(33?)\n\n                 This documentation is written by BOBO!\n\n  Program history and example outputs/scripts come in seperate files with\n                          the release archive.\n\n\n           Notable features on Conference Top Uploaders...\n           ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n        * Built in Config Program (Easy to set up and modify)\n        * Works without conference accounting.\n        * Configable: Write message to EALL or other user when reseting.\n        * Configable: Write bulletine when reseting.\n        * AmiExpress compatible with all amiexpress versions above 2.33.\n        * Online Updating.\n        * Multi-node compatible.\n        * Very FAST!\n        * Special Optimized Versions for all CPU types (000/010/020/030/040)\n        * Lot''s of secuirty checks. Nothing can go wrong!\n\n   Conference Top Uploaders have been tested on the following setups\n                  without any sort of problems.. :\n\n       A2000 (68030/50Mhz) OS 2.0 - Amiexpress v3.32 (BOBO/MYSTIC)\n       A3000 (68030/25Mhz) OS 3.0 - Amiexpress v3.12 (SLASH/MAGIC 12)\n       A3000 (68030/25Mhz) OS 2.0 - Amiexpress v3.32 (BYTEANDI/MYSTIC)\n       A3000 (68030/25Mhz) OS 2.0 - Amiexpress v3.12 (UFFE)\n       A4000 (68030/25Mhz) OS 3.0 - S-Express v0.33  (CEVIN KEY)\n       A4000 (68040/25Mhz) OS 3.0 - Amiexpress v3.18 (NIGHTSHADE)\n\n           More beta-testers wanted for future versions.\n\n     Suggestions, Ideas and bug reports are welcome and wanted!\n\n\n     The complete release Archive (MST-CT21.LHA) should contents\n     ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nConftop/Conftop.000           38332 bytes   All-processors version.\nConftop/Conftop.020           38300 bytes   Optimized version for 020 or better.\nConftop/Conftop.Doc           17508 bytes   This document file.\nConftop/Conftop.Update         5097 bytes   Update file.\nConftop/Conftop.Output         1820 bytes   Conftop Output Example.\nCommands/BBSCmd/Conftop.info    417 bytes   Command icon for /X 3.xx+.\nCommands/SYSCmd/FileCheck.info 1082 bytes   Command icon for /X 3.xx+.\nCommands/BBS.Cmd                516 bytes   Command file for /X 2.xx.\nCommands/SYS.Cmd                 50 bytes   Command file for /X 2.xx.\nConf2/Bull20.txt                 50 bytes   Example Bullbatch file.\nConftop.Playpen                  40 bytes   Example Playpen file.\n\n\n                         BackGround & Purpose\n                         ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nConfTop was orginally written becouse it didn''t exists any good door to count\nuploads in a optinal conference under a choosen number of days. I orginally\ngot this idea from the WeekTop utility by AirWolf that counted the total uploads\nin all conferences under a week. But since users started to ask me to code\nsomething to count uploads in a special conference, i started coding this tool. \nThe first version was coded in Arexx, and was pretty slow.\nNow it''s here, Coded in pure C and FAST!\n\nAs the sysop you are able to choose the interval (number of days), how many\nrows (Uploaders) you want to show, and if you want to write any mail when\nreseting. You can also choose if you want to write a bulletine. You may also \nhave a headerfile/Tailerfile and a exclude-file for one or all conferences.\nThis are explained later in this document.\n\nSince this door runs often, the computer of the board should be rather fast.\nA 68000 Amiga is probably too slow to have any use for this tool, but on 020+''s\nit should run fast enough.\n\n\n                  To install Conference Top Uploaders\n                  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nTo install conftop on your amiexpress system, copy all necessary files into\nan optional directory.\n\nNOTE: IF YOU HAVE EXTERNAL PLAYPEN DIRECTORIES, YOU MUST MAKE A SPECIAL FILE.\n      PLEASE READ LATER IN THIS DOCUMENT HOW TO DO IT!\n\nInstallation for amiexpress 3.0+ sysops:\n\nCopy the included icon (Conftop.info) into the BBSCmd/ directory, and copy\n(Filecheck.info) into SYSCmd/ directory. If you already have a filecheck.info\n(for Bossnuke or whatever), copy it to BBSCmd/ and name it (Filechk.info) and\nit will be launched after conftop have run.\n\nNOTE: Remember to edit the path in Conftop.info and Filecheck.info, if you\n      DO NOT put conftop in Doors:Amiexpress/Conftop/Conftop.X\n\n------------------------------------- END OF AMIEXPRESS 3.0+ INSTALLATION\n\nInstallation for amiexpress 2.xx sysops:\n\nAdd this line to your BBS.CMD (or Customcommands).  (Use the included)\n\n----Cut Here-----------------------------------------\n*CONFTOP  XM010Doors:Amiexpress/Conftop/Conftop.x\n----Cut Here-----------------------------------------\n ^^^^^^^    ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n   |         |                 |> Filename of the door with full path.\n   |         |>Accesslevel required to use door.\n   |>The command that will invoke door.\n\nAdd this line to your SYS.CMD (or Customcommands).  (Use the included)\n\n----Cut Here-----------------------------------------\nFILECHECK XM010Doors:Amiexpress/Conftop/Conftop.x\n----Cut Here-----------------------------------------\n\nIf you want to launch a door after (on amiexpress 2.xx), you must do a fake-\nfile named (BBS:Commands/BBSCmd/FileChk.info). You can just make it 0 bytes,\nit doesn''t mather. If conftop founds that file, it will try to start a door\ncalled "FileChk" so you must enter this line in your BBS.Cmd (or Customcommands):\n\n----Cut Here-----------------------------------------\nFILECHK   XM010Doors:DUPECHECK.X\n----Cut Here-----------------------------------------\n\n------------------------------------- END OF AMIEXPRESS 2.xx INSTALLATION\n\nNow, logon your local node and simply type: (Conftop -CFG). This will let you\ninto the configuration program where you can control everything.\n(NOTE: Secuirty level 255 required for accessing Configuration menu)\n\nWhen you have installed conftop into a conference with the config program,\nyou must load your texteditor (CED), and edit your bullbatch file in that\nconference. (Ex BULL20.TXT or whatever)\n(Use the included)\n\n-------( Cut Here )----------------------------\n~\nUpdating CONFTOP, please wait ~N ..\n~CC_Conftop\n-------( Cut Here )----------------------------\n\n\n                          Configuration\n                          ~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nWhen you have installed conftop in your board (as described above), you must\njoin the conference you want to run conftop in. Enter "CONFTOP -CFG" and it\nwill let you entering the configuration program......\n\n»thE EaSt BBS« [2:»CoMmOdOrE aMiGa«] Menu (60 mins. left): CONFTOP -CFG\n\nA big configuration screen will be shown...\n\n.----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| Conference Top Uploaders -- Configuration Editor -- Security 255 Required! |\n|--------------------------------------v-------------------------------------|\n| 1) Number of Days : (   7)           | S) Save config.                     |\n| 2) Number of Rows : (  10)           | L) Load config.                     |\n| 3) Show Statistics: ( Yes)           | R) Remove conftop from conference.  |\n| 4) Mail User      : (EALL          ) | A) About conference top uploaders.  |\n| 5) Bulletin file  : (BBS2:Bulletins) | E) Edit users in datafile.          |\n|                                      |                                     |\n| Next reset: Fri Jan 07 00:00:00 1994 | Date     : Thu Dec 30 22:26:55 1993 |\n|--------------------------------------^-------------------------------------|\n| Please select (1,2,3,4,S,L,R,A,E) ?                                        |\n|----------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Configuration File not found. Using defaults...                            |\n`----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\nNow make the changes you want to do in the config.\n\n( 1) - Change the interval (1-99). Conftop will always run continuos, which\n       means after the choosen interval, conftop will start over and run\n       again.\n( 2) - Change the number rows (1-99). This is how many uploaders you want to\n       show when a user is joining a conference.\n( 3) - Change if you want to show statistics after conftop have reseted.\n       It will show the top uploader last period and the record uploader.\n( 4) - Change who you want to send a message to, or if you don''t want to send\n       any message at all. The message will be written public from user number\n       one (Often the sysop).\n( 5) - Change the name and path to the bulletine file that will be written each\n       time conftop resets. Write ''NONE'' to not make any bulletine.\n( S) - Save the config.\n( L) - Loads the config.\n( R) - Removes (uninstall) conftop from this conference. All datafiles are\n       are removed.\n( A) - About conftop screen.\n( E) - Let''s you go to the user editor. The following screen will be shown:\n\n.----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n|     Conference Top Uploaders -- Configuration Editor -- User Editor!       |\n|--------------------------------------v-------------------------------------|\n| 1) Username:                         | A) Add a user to datafile.          |\n| 2) Location:                         | R) Remove a user from datafile.     |\n| 3) Bytes   :                         | E) Edit a user in datafile.         |\n| 4) Files   :                         | L) List all users in datafile.      |\n|                                      | Q) Quit back to menu.               |\n| S) Save datafile with all changes.   |                                     |\n|                                      | Users in datafile: (  0)            |\n|--------------------------------------^-------------------------------------|\n| Please select (A,R,E,L,Q,S) ?                                              |\n|----------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| Awaiting Command...                                                        |\n`----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n( A) - Add a user to datafile.\n( R) - Remove a user from datafile.\n( E) - Edit a user in datafile.\n( L) - List all users in datafile.\n( Q) - Quit back to the mainmenu.\n( S) - Save all your changes.\n\nNOTE: The commands ''R,E & L'' are disabled when no users exists in datafile.\n\n\n     WE ARE VERY SORRY FOR HOLDING CONFTOP FROM RELEASE SOO LONG TIME,\n        BUT WE WANTED IT TO BE THE BEST CONFERENCE WEEKTOP UTILITY\n               AVAILIBLE FOR AMIEXPRESS BBS!  NOW USE IT!!\n\n\n     How to run conftop if you have external playpen directories\n     ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nIf you don''t have your playpen directories located in your NodeX directory,\nyou MUST make a file called "CONFTOP.PLAYPEN" and put it in BBS:\n\nIn this file you should enter which nodes who have external playpen dirs >:\n\n-------( Cut Here )----------------------------\nNODE1 RAM:PLAYPEN1/\nNODE2 RAM:PLAYPEN2/\nNODE3 HD0:PLAYPEN3/\n-------( Cut Here )----------------------------\n\nThis means that if a user is uploading at node 1, conftop will search in\nRAM:PLAYPEN1/ for the file. If the node is not listed, or the this file\ndoesn''t exists, conftop will search in the normal BBS:NodeX/Playpen/ dir.\n\nNOTE: DON''T REMEMBER TO ENTER THE SLASH OR COLON AT THE END!\n\n\n                   How to exclude users from conftop\n                   ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nConftop will always search for a exclude file..\n\n· Conftop.Exclude - with users to exclude from Conftop.\n\nThat file are first searched for in the conference path (ex BBS:Elite/), and\nif it is not found, it will search in BBS:. If the user is found in exclude\nfile, conftop will not update him in the datafile when he upload files.\n\n\n                          Use a Header/Tailer\n                          ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nConftop will always search for a headerfile/tailerfile ..\n\n· Conftop.Header - for display before the output, and\n· Conftop.Tailer - for display after the output.\n\nThese files are first looked for in the conference path (ex BBS:Elite/), and\nif it is not found, it will search in BBS:. If no headerfile is found, a\nclear-screen (CTRL-L) is sent so it displays quicker/nicer.\n\nNOTE: When you are using a own headerfile, don''t forget the clear-screen at\n      the top!\n\n\n                         In futher versions\n                         ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nIn futher versions, Conftop will be run via icons. All information will be\nstored there, which means that the program size will be ALOT smaller! (Since\nthe config prg can be removed). You will also be able to configable a start-\ndate for use if you are going to use conftop in competions. Conftop will also\nbe more optimized, and i have a new design that maybe will be used.\n\nMore ideas wanted for future releases! Call my board today!\n\n\n                            Contact me\n                            ~~~~~~~~~~\nTo contact me, or to contact Mystic/X-Design, or if you have any suggestions\nor bug reports or anything else, call my board or Mystic /X WHQ and leave me\na message.\n\nBoardname             Phonenumber         Cputype        Sysop         Nodes\n==============================================================================\nThe East BBS #1       +46-8940614         68030/50Mhz    BOBO/MYSTIC   3 Nodes\nThe East BBS #2       +46-8940615         68030/50Mhz    BOBO/MYSTIC   3 Nodes\nThe East BBS #3       +46-8940919         68030/50Mhz    BOBO/MYSTIC   3 Nodes\nDiabolo #1            +49-306218787       68030/25Mhz    ANDY/MYSTIC   3 Nodes\nDiabolo #2            +49-306221994       68030/25Mhz    ANDY/MYSTIC   3 Nodes\nDiabolo #3            +49-306212312       68030/25Mhz    ANDY/MYSTIC   3 Nodes\n\n                             Greetings\n                             ~~~~~~~~~\nGreetings to: Looby, Nightshade, Pacific/2000 AD, Cruger/Skidrow, Dee/Delight\n              Agressor, Reactor/MST, Rhys/FLT, Screwball, Distler\n\nMany thanx to Looby and Nightshade who helped me to learn C and spended many\nhours helping me. Without you guys this door wouldn''t exists!\n\nMany thanx to Byteandi/Mystic and Remo/Mystic for all help and support.\n\nAnd many many thanx to all my beta testers for bug-reports, suggestions and\nhints & tips to improve this door.\n\n\n                    All members of (Mystic/X-Design)\n                    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n                        ______  __________________\n.----------------+-----/    \ \/ / __/_  __/ / __/----------+----------------.\n|                |----/ / / /\  /\  /-/ /-/ / /----[ /X ]---|                |\n|       /\    /\ |-EmP\/ / /-/ /\  /-/ /-/ /\ \--[ DESiGN ]-|       /\    /\ |\n|      /C \  /N/ +-----\/\/--\/--\/--\/--\/--\/-------------+      /C \  /N/ |\n|     /i/\ \/G/  |                                          |     /i/\ \/G/  |\n|    /T/  \ i/   |                                          |    /T/  \ i/   |\n|   /S/   /S \   |   EMPiRE   -   BYTEANDi   -  CRACKDOWN   |   /S/   /S \   |\n|  /Y/   /E/\ \  |   TYCOON   -   KiLLRAVEN  -   SiEGEL     |  /Y/   /E/\ \  |\n| /M/   /D/  \ \ |   FUZZY    -      SPY     -  INCOGNiTO   | /M/   /D/  \ \ |\n| \/    \/    \/ |   RE/Y\o   -     BOBO!    -   HARDBYTE   | \/    \/    \/ |\n|                |                                          |                |\n`----------------+----------[  MYSTiC /X DESiGN  ]----------+----------------''\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  ____/\____/\ ______/\_____  ___/\_______/\_______/\_______/\_____\n -\____ ____  Y  ____ _____/ML\__ ___________  ____ _________ ____/------\n    /    \/___|_  \/  __)___   /  __)___/___Y_  \/______ \/    \\n   /      \\____   \  |     \ /   |     \\____   \     |  \     \ B.B.S.\n   \      /   T    /  !     / \   !     /   T    /     !  /     /\n ---\____/\___|___/\_______/   \_______/\___|___/\_______/\____/---------\n.---------v-----------------------------------------------v-------------.\n| NODE (1):+46-8-940614 - NODE (2) +46-8-940615 - NODE (3).+46-8-940919 |\n|         .                                               :             |\n|  ...:.:..:..  MyStIc: FuN & FriEnDshIp! - NoThInG ElSe! ..:..:.:...   |\n`-v-----------------------v-------------------------------------------v-''\n  :____ _________________ : _______________________ _ _______________ :\n -.\__ Y ____ __________/-.-\_____ ___ ______ ____// \\__ ________  /-.--\n  . / \ / \/_____\/   \  /X  /   Y \/  _)__/_____\/   \/  l_ \/  Y  \ .\n   /   Y   \    ! \    \    /    !  \      \    ! \    \      \  |   \\n --\___|_  /____  /__  /----\_____  /____  /____  /__  /____  /__|_  /---\n         \/     \/   \/           \/     \/     \/   \/     \/   ML\/\n          W·E  P·R·O·D·U·C·E  F·O·R  Y·O·U·R  C·O·M·F·O·R·T !\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',51378,3,0,NULL,NULL,'mst_cf22','scan',1780048628);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mst_cf23','MST-CF23.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MST-CF23.LHA','Usereditor','XIM','Conftop000.x',NULL,NULL,'MST','\   /\ | /\ __/\ . /\ |\ . /| BOBO/MYSTiC | / V \/_. \/_.¬\/_| \/ |/ |_\|     AND     | /  |  \¬|  \¬¦  \¬|  \ |  ¦ ¬\LOOBY/iNSANE!|',replace(' _/\___/¦___/\___/\___/¦_/\__.-------------.\n \   /\ | /\ __/\ . /\ |\ . /| BOBO/MYSTiC |\n / V \/_. \/_.¬\/_| \/ |/ |_\|     AND     |\n/  |  \¬|  \¬¦  \¬|  \ |  ¦ ¬\LOOBY/iNSANE!|\n\__¦  /__  /__  / ¦__/_¦___  /  PRESENTS:  |\n.---\/---\/---\/-/X-Power!-\/^-------------|\n|:.Conference Top Uploaders (Version 2.3).:|\n|:The Ultimate Weektop-Tool for Amiexpress:|\n|:Bug-Fixed and alot of new options added!:|\n|:100% Compatible with S-Express & /X2.33+:|\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'Conftop.Guide',replace('@DATABASE Conftop.Guide\n@$VER: Guide for Conftop v2.3 (3rd May 1994)\n\n@REMARK Copyright (c) 1994 Mystic.\n@REMARK All Rights Reserved.\n@REMARK Main Program by Bobo/Mystic and Looby/Insane.\n@REMARK Document and Update files by Bobo/Mystic.\n\n@REMARK You need MultiView, Amigaguide or any other GUIDE viewer.\n\n@NODE MAIN "Conftop: Contents."\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    Conference Top Uploaders (Version 2.3) [RELEASE 2] - 3rd May 1994\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n          @{"[ Background and Purpose ]" Link Background}      @{"[ Available Tooltypes ]" Link Config}\n          @{"[    Notable Features    ]" Link Features  }      @{"[   Program History   ]" Link Tooltypes}\n          @{"[  Install into Express  ]" Link Install   }      @{"[  Thanks and Greets  ]" Link Greets}\n          @{"[  Configurate Conftop   ]" Link History   }\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\n            Copyright (c) 1994 by Bobo/Mystic and Looby/Insane\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n Example Outputs/Scripts come in seperate files with the release archive.\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Background "Conftop: Background and Purpose"\n[------------( Background and Purpose )-----------------------------------]\n\nConftop was orginally written becouse it didn''t exists any good Conftop\nutility when i needed one. I first tested Van Dammes Conftop utility, but\nit was slow and i didn''t get it working correctly so i started coding my\nown. The first version was coded in arexx and was pretty slow, so i decided\nto recode it in C which is much faster.\n\nAs the sysop you can specify the interval (number of days), how many rows,\nand if you want to write a message when reseting. You may also have a\nheaderfile/tailerfile and a exclude-files for one or all conferences.\nAll this functions are explained later in this document.\n\nConftop can now be made resident. I really recommend you to do this, since\nit will speed this door up quite much, specially on 68000-68020 computers!\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Features "Conftop: Notable Features"\n[------------( Notable Features )-----------------------------------------]\n\nSeveral reasons to use Conference Top Uploaders:\n\n* Written entirely in C for fast code.\n* Works without conference accounting.\n* Configable: Write message to optional user when reseting.\n* Can be made resident.\n* Can run other filecheck doors after.\n* Can display header/tailer files, different ones for each conference, \n  as well as global ones for all conferences.\n* Checks for private uploads.\n* Special optimized versions for all CPU types.\n* Online updating.\n* 32-Node compatable. (Actually how many nodes you want)\n* Using Icons (/X3.x Standard Nowadays), but should work fine with /X2.x\n  and Sigma Express.\n* Can use a global datafile for all conferences and/or seperate ones for\n  individual conferences.\n* Allows skipping update if specific user is named (by username or slot)\n\nConftop only allow one door to be started after. If this isn''t enough,\ni recommend you to use S-Dupecheck by Pot-Noodle or Dupecheck by Byteandi.\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Install "Conftop: Install into Express"\n[------------( Install into Express )-------------------------------------]\n\nThis door should be installed as your standard FileCheck door.\nOn /X3.x you have you have to edit (or create) the filecheck.info in\nyour Syscmd directory. On /X2.x and SExpress you have to edit the\nSYS.Cmd in the usual way. Remember to give this door a low access level\n(Like "001") and make it multinode. The door is an XIM type ofcourse!\n\nAlso, for added speed, you may make the door resident with your normal\n"resident" command (CLI: "Resident Conftop.x PURE"). But if you do, make\nsure that Express runs just the doorfilename, without its path. On /X3.x\nyou also need the tooltype RESIDENT in the icon.\n\nYou also need a icon in your bbscmd directory. Just copy your created\nfilecheck icon into you bbscmd dir and name it CONFTOP.INFO.\nOn /X2.x, just snap the line you just entered in sys.cmd and insert it\ninto your bbs.cmd file and rename FILECHECK to CONFTOP.\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Config "Conftop: How to configurate conftop"\n[------------( How to configurate conftop )-------------------------------]\n\nWhile you''re reading this section it may be a good idea to view the example\nicons that came with the archive.\n\nThe whole way to configurate conftop is totaly changed. I am now using\nicons since it is the standard nowadays. You have one icon for global\ndata in doors: (eg all tooltypes you want to be available for all\nconferences) and you have one icon in each conference you want to run\nconftop in. Read the next chapter to see available tooltypes.\n\nThe only thing you need to do to install conftop into a conference is to\ncreate a iconfile in the specific conference path and put the tooltype\nDAYS in it. (EG DAYS=7 or DAYS=WEEKLY)\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Tooltypes "Conftop: Available Tooltypes"\n[------------( Available Tooltypes )--------------------------------------]\n\nHere are the available tooltypes.\n\n[*] - Can be used both in the global and the local icon.\n[-] - Can only be used in the global icon (Doors:Conftop.info)\n[!] - Can only be used in the local icon (<confpath>/Conftop.info)\n\nTooltype-Name:                    Description:\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDAYS=<days/weekly>            [!] This tooltype specifies the interval of\n                                  conftop. You can put it to WEEKLY if you\n                                  want to run conftop weekly (Monday->Sunday)\n                                  EG: DAYS=WEEKLY,DAYS=14\n\nROWS=<# rows>                 [*] This tooltype specifies how many rows/lines\n                                  with users you want to display.\n                                  EG: ROWS=10\n\nMAILUSER=<username>           [*] This tooltype specifies which user you\n                                  want to write a message to when conftop is\n                                  reseting. If this tooltype is not specified\n                                  at all, no message will be written.\n                                  EG: MAILUSER=EALL\n\nBULLFILE=<bulletinefile>      [*] This tooltype specifies where you want to\n                                  write the bulletin file to when reseting.\n                                  If this tooltype is not specified at all,\n                                  no bulletine will be written.\n                                  EG: BULLFILE=BBS:Bulletins/Bull1.txt\n\nSHARE_DATA=<confpath>         [!] If this tooltype is specified, all other\n                                  tooltypes will be disabled. This allows\n                                  a conference to be run at another confs\n                                  datafile/icon. Eg: SHARE_DATA=BBS:Conf1/\n\nSHOW_RESETDATE                [*] This tooltype specifies if you want to\n                                  show the complete resetdate instaid of\n                                  showing eg: Day (1/7).\n\nNEXTDOOR=<doorname>           [*] This tooltype specifies which door that\n                                  should be started after conftop have run.\n                                  EG: NEXTDOOR=DUPECHECK\n\nCONFNAME=<cnfname>            [!] If this tooltype is specified, conftop\n                                  will use this conference name instaid of\n                                  using the one in Confconfig.info file.\n                                  EG: CONFNAME=Amiga Elite\n\nEXCLUDE_<num>=<user/slot>     [*] This tooltype specifies which users that\n                                  you want to exclude from conftop.\n                                  You can enter both username and slotnumber\n                                  EG: EXCLUDE_1=BOBO,EXCLUDE_2=165\n\nPLAYPEN_<node>=<dir>          [-] This tooltype is only needed if you don''t\n                                  have your playpen directories located in\n                                  BBS:NodeX/Playpen/. If they don''t, you\n                                  must type your external playpen dir here.\n                                  EG: PLAYPEN_1=HD2:PLAYPEN/\n\nMIN_LIMIT=<bytes>             [*] If this tooltype is specifed, only users\n                                  above the limit of <size> bytes will be\n                                  displayed.\n\nSKIP_EMPTY_LINES              [*] If this tooltype is specified, conftop will\n                                  not output any empty lines. Eg if ROWS=10\n                                  and only 1 user have uploaded, conftop\n                                  will not fill the other 9 lines up.\n\nFROMUSER                      [*] Here you can specify a own user the message\n                                  will be written from. Default is the SYSOP.\n\nSUBJECT                       [*] Here you can specify a own subject for the\n                                  message. Default is "Results from Conftop"\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE History "Conftop: Program History"\n[------------( Program History )------------------------------------------]\n\n{ + }-New feature(s)         { - }-Removed feature\n{ * }-changed feature        { ! }-fixed feature (Bug)\n{ # }-Information            { ? }-let me know if this work\n\nConftop v1.0 (09-18-93 > 10-15-93) - [Private version for my board]\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nFirst version, coded in Arexx by Bobo\n\n09-18-93 { + } I started coding this door.\n - ^^ -  { + } Main source for updating uploads in datafiles.\n - ^^ -  { + } Showing output in conference routine coded.\n09-19-93 { + } Now using a configfile.\n09-20-93 { + } Now showing total upload stats at the bottom.\n09-22-93 { # } Optimized the sourcecode :> Now: 6502 Before: 7523\n09-23-93 { * } Now using a own sort routine instaid of using WB''s SORT.\n               Also abit useless code removed (Now size: 6229)\n - ^^ -  { # } Optimized the sourcecode :> Now: 5687 Before: 6229\n10-01-93 { ! } You can now choose how many uploaders you want in a conference.\n10-02-93 { * } Now using a own showfile routine instaid of using amiexpress''s\n               that is abit slow.\n - ^^ -  { + } Now configuable playpen paths in configfile.\n - ^^ -  { + } Now changing stat to ''Joining a conf'' when running from\n               Bull20.txt, and ''Uploading'' when running from Filecheck.\n - ^^ -  { ? } Crashed sometimes on A4000/040. Changed some init codes. I\n               *think* it works now.\n10-03-93 { # } Optimized the sourcecode :> Now: 5439 Before: 6012\n               (Alot of useless code & routines removed)\n10-07-93 { + } Now you can launch a door after conftop in filecheck.\n         { # } ^ NOTE: All type of Doors without AREXX doors works ^\n10-10-93 { ! } Didnot give the launched door the right filename.\n10-11-93 { * } Changed the output design abit. Now some more chars for\n               username and location.\n - ^^ -  { + } Recoded the source so i was able to compile it.\n\nConftop v1.1 (10-16-93 > 11-02-93) - [Only Available for Betatesters]\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nStill coded in Arexx. First beta-version.\n\n10-16-93 { # } Since Nightshade didn''t want to waste his time on coding\n               this door in C, i decided to update it abit.\n - ^^ -  { * } Now 50% faster when joining a conference. Conftop are now\n               sorting & updating when you have uploaded a file.\n - ^^ -  { ? } Fixed for multinode systems. Tell me if this works!?\n10-17-93 { ! } Didn''t create a new datafile if it didn''t exists one.\n10-23-93 { ! } ALOT of bugs found in the compiled version. Rewritten alot\n               of functions to make it work 100%!\n\nConftop v2.0 (11-02-93 > 12-11-93) - [Only Available for Betatesters]\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nTalked abit with Looby, and we started to make conftop coded in C.\n\n11-02-93 { + } LOOBY: Coded the mainprogram.\n11-05-93 { + } BOBO : Coded the message structure to write messages.\n11-10-93 { * } LOOBY: Datafile now in binery.\n11-13-93 { + } BOBO : Now displaying total uploads and you can launch a\n                      door after.\n11-15-93 { + } BOBO : Coded a new object file, since the one we used was\n                      to old, and didnot support filechecking.\n                      Many thanx to Byteandi for all help!\n11-20-93 { + } LOOBY: New reset routine that shows ex. Day: (1/7).\n11-24-93 { + } BOBO : Now showing statistics.\n11-25-93 { + } BOBO : Displaying statistics is now configuable in the\n                      configfile.\n\nConftop v2.1 (12-11-93 > 02-05-94) - [Only Available for Betatesters]\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nRecoded conftop. Now more optimized and faster. The code size is now\nabout 20k less then old version.\n\n12-11-93 { * } BOBO : Started recoding and optimize conftop.\n - ^^ -  { * } BOBO : Totaly new configuration program coded.\n12-15-93 { + } BOBO : Now using SAS/C 6.50. Coool..\n12-18-93 { ! } BOBO : Now an 100% working send message routine.\n12-25-93 { ! } LOOBY: Now an 100% working fixbytes routine.\n12-27-93 { ! } LOOBY: Now an 100% working sort routine.\n12-28-93 { ! } BOBO : Now locking msgbase correctly.\n01-13-94 { * } BOBO : Some new design improvments.\n01-17-94 { * } BOBO : Changed each line to 78 chars, since pc only support max\n                      79 chars / line.  Before: 80 chars / line.\n01-19-94 { ! } BOBO : Now starting filecheck when user is found in excludefile.\n01-29-94 { ! } LOOBY: New sort routine (again!). Optimized and a tiny bug fixed.\n01-31-94 { * } LOOBY: New fixbytes routine (again!). Optimized!\n02-05-94 { ! } LOOBY: Sort routine bugfixed (again!!)\n\nConftop v2.2 (02-05-94) - [First Public Release Version]\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nFirst Public release version!\n\nConftop v2.3 (02-20-94 > 04-19-94) - [Public Release Version]\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n02-20-94 { * } BOBO : New design used. Tell me what you think about it!\n - ^^ -  { * } BOBO : Optimized abit. Some useless routines removed.\n02-24-94 { ! } BOBO : Conftop did not start the filechecking if a user was\n                      found in the excludefile. FIXED!\n - ^^ -  { * } BOBO : The file: Conftop.Stats is no longer needed. It is\n                      saved in the Conftop.Data file.\n02-25-94 { * } BOBO : Now you can make Conftop resident.\n02-26-94 { * } BOBO : The files: Conftop.Playpen & Conftop.Exclude is no\n                      longer needed. It is saved in the iconfile.\n02-27-94 { * } BOBO : Saved 8 bytes to much for each user in the datafile - FIXED!\n03-01-94 { * } BOBO : Removed as much global data as possible from the code.\n                      Conftop now requires less memory then before.\n - ^^ -  { ! } BOBO : Conftop was leaking memory at afew places. Most when\n                      a error occured. I think i found the most of them, but \n                      please report if you found some more.\n - ^^ -  { + } BOBO : A new option (tooltype) available. You can now have two\n                      or more conferences running on the same datafile. The\n                      tooltype in the infofile is called:\n                      SHARE_DATA_CNF<conf#>=<conftop datafile>\n\n                      EG: SHARE_DATA_CNF1=BBS:Elite/Conftop.Data\n                      - This would make so all uploads in conference one\n                        will be tranfered to the datafile in bbs:elite/\n - ^^ -  { * } BOBO : Updated the config program. Now more simple, and not as\n                      big as the last one. No user-editor is available in this\n                      configprg, so i hope someone will code a external editor\n                      for conftop.\n03-02-94 { * } BOBO : Coded a convert program to convert the old datafiles to\n                      the new format.\n - ^^ -  { + } BOBO : A new option (tooltype) available. You can now select\n                      what door you want to start after conftop.\n                      NEXTDOOR=<doorname>  EG: NEXTDOOR=FILECHK\n                      - This would try to start a door called FILECHK.\n                        You must have it in BBSCMD/\n03-05-94 { * } BOBO : Conftop is now totaly running on icons. The whole cfg-\n                      program is removed. You must now have a icon in each\n                      conference named: Conftop.info. The following tooltypes\n                      is available: DAYS,ROWS,MAILUSER,BULLFILE.\n - ^^ -  { ! } BOBO : Conftop did bug sometimes when it was made resident.\n                      This problem is fixed!\n03-06-94 { + } BOBO : Now if a error occur, it will be written to the callerslog.\n03-07-94 { + ) BOBO : New tooltypes in conficon: SHARE_DATA,EXCLUDE_<num>\n - ^^ -  { + } BOBO : New tooltypes in doorsicon: PLAYPEN_<node>,EXCLUDE_<num>\n                      NEXTDOOR. More will be available!\n03-08-94 { + } BOBO : New tooltype in conficon: CONFNAME=<name>. If this\n                      tooltype is specifed, it will use this conference name\n                      instaid of reading it from CONFCONFIG.INFO\n03-10-94 { + } BOBO : New tooltype in conficon: SHOW_RESETDATE. If this tooltype\n                      is specified the complete resetdate will be shows instaid\n                      of eg: Day (1/7).\n03-11-94 { ! } BOBO : Fixed quite many bugs in the convert program and maked it\n                      safer.\n03-13-94 { + } BOBO : New tooltype in conficon: MIN_LIMIT=<size>. If this\n                      tooltype is specifed, only users above the <size> will\n                      be displayed.  Thanx to DR. G/4WD for the idea!\n03-15-94 { + } BOBO : Coded a USEREDITOR so you can edit users in the datafiles.\n03-21-94 { ! } BOBO : Fixed the NONSTOP bug.  Thanx to REMO/MST for the report.\n03-22-94 { + } BOBO : You can now press CTRL+X in the usereditor to erase all\n                      the input.\n03-23-94 { * } BOBO : You can now have the tooltypes MIN_LIMIT, BULLFILE,\n                      and SHOW_RESETDATE in the global icon.\n03-24-94 { * } BOBO : If Conftop couldn''t write the message/bulletine, a error\n                      will be written to the callerslog.\n03-26-94 { ! } BOBO : Now using the tooltypes CONFNAME and MIN_LIMIT when \n                      writing message/bulletine.\n03-29-94 { * } BOBO : New Dataformat. You can now change the number of days\n                      whenever you want without to reset.  Thanx to RAJ-BAN\n                      for the idea/suggestion.\n - ^^ -  { * } BOBO : Now writing: Day (1/7 - Final Results) when conftop\n                      is writing mail/bulletine.  Thanx to MOOCHER/FLT for\n                      the sugguestion.\n - ^^ -  { ! } BOBO : Now using a own routine to display the header/tailer\n                      files. Max 300 chars/line.\n03-30-94 { ! } BOBO : Misspelling fixed (Availible->Available)\n - ^^ -  { + } BOBO : Now you can use both the slot-number and the\n                      username at the tooltype EXCLUDE_<num>.\n03-31-94 { + } BOBO : You can now enter DAYS=WEEKLY and conftop will always\n                      run from Monday->Sunday.\n04-02-94 { + } BOBO : New tooltype available: SKIP_EMPTY_LINES. If this\n                      tooltype is specified, conftop will not output empty\n                      lines.\n04-05-94 { ! } BOBO : Forgot to send the carrage return in my displayfile\n                      routine.  Thanx to Dee/Delight for the bugreport!\n - ^^ -  { + } BOBO : New tooltype: FROMUSER. Here you can specify a own\n                      user the message should be written from.\n - ^^ -  { + } BOBO : New tooltype: SUBJECT. Here you can specify a own\n                      subject for the message.\n04-07-94 { ! } BOBO : Conftop read the config two times each time a user\n                      was joining a conference or uploading a file.\n04-12-94 { * } BOBO : Changed, fixed and updated the WEEKLY feature.\n                      Please report if this work correctly now!\n04-16-94 { + } BOBO : Conftop now checks if the upload is private. If it is\n                      conftop will skip the update.\n04-19-94 { - } BOBO : Registration routines removed.\n                      Final size: 25976 (Source: 33123 with comments)\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Greets "Conftop: Thanks and Greets"\n[------------( Thanks and Greets )----------------------------------------]\n\nGreetings to: Pacific/2000 AD, Looby/Insane, Dee/Delight, Agressor/Anthrox,\n              Reactor/Mystic, Easy Rider/Mystic, Ufok/Mystic, Screwball!\n\nMany thanx to Byteandi/TRSI and Remo/Mystic for all help and support!\n\nAnd many many thanx to all my beta testers for bug-reports, suggestions and\nhints & tips to improve this door.\n@ENDNODE\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',82431,7,0,NULL,NULL,'mst_cf23','scan',1780048612);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mst_cl10','MST-CL10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MST-CL10.LHA','MST-CLOCK','XIM','LE-win5-96.exe',NULL,'SIEGEL/MST','MST','_/  v  \__/ ! \  /  _____.   ._(__)/  . \ \_ _:_ ______  \/\___  \ |   | |  \_  |_/\ _/  \ /  \_  v  __   v   \|   | |    _ |   \',replace('   _____    ___    _____________.__. ____   \n _/  v  \__/ ! \  /  _____.   ._(__)/  . \  \n \_ _:_ ______  \/\___  \ |   | |  \_  |_/\ \n_/  \ /  \_  v  __   v   \|   | |    _ |   \\n\    v    /  ___/\    ___/!___! !___/__-   /\n-\___:___/___/-ã!-\___/---------------\___/-\n--------------------------------------------\nRELEASED : /X-CLOCK V1.0 BY SIEGEL/MST\n','\n',char(10)),'MST-CLOCK.GUIDE',replace('@database mst-clock.guide\n\n@node Main "MST-CLOCK V1.0 - /X uTiL WRiTTeN BY SieGeL/MsT"\n\n             /\____________.__  _______________________   ________\n            /   ._.____    |  \/    ________ _     /___)_/   .___/\n          _/    | |    \___.   \____.   \_|   \___/          |______\n          \     | |     /  |    /   |    /|    |  |   ____   ¦     /\n           \ ___l_l___ /______ /_______ / |    |  l___ | \________/\n            \/       \/      \/       \/  l____|      \!·A×E·\n\n                                \n                                /X - D e S i G N \n\n                    iS BaCK WiTH aNoTHeR PRoDuCTioN CaLLeD :\n\n                                 /X CLoCK V1.0\n \n                CoDiNG & DoCS BY SieGeL/MsT - GFX BY A×E/MST\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\n                              @{" INTRODUCTION " Link partone}\n                              @{" REQUIREMENTS " Link parttwo}\n                              @{" INSTALLATION " Link partthree}\n                              @{" GREETINGS... " Link partfour}\n@endnode\n\n@node partone "Why I wrote it...."\n\n                           REASONS FOR THIS TOOL\n                           ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nWell, everybody knows the /X-Clock "S-Watch"..it''s a fine Clock, but it has \na fatal mistake : It''s ARexx! AND COMPILED !!! WHAT A LAMELESS !!!! My A4000 \ndon''t like compiled Arexx-Scripts...everytime it crashes...and that''s the\nreason why I wrote it new completly in Fast C! All functions from "S-WATCH"\nare included and a bit more...the clock will tell U, how many time you have\non this BBS,how many u are used ...blablabla....:)\n\nI don''t want to write so much shit here, so let''s get started with the\n@{"Requirements" Link parttwo} and so on....\n\n@endnode\n\n@node parttwo "Requirements for thiz Tool..."\n\n                              REQUIREMENTS\n                              ~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nYou need an Amiga :) with Kickstart V37++ , a full working Amiex V2.XX or\n\nhigher and the Library "icon.library" in yar LIBS: Drawer...but this will\n\nbe no prob, coz diz Library is included with the original Commodore Disks.\n\nAt Least, you''ll need an Icon in ur DOORS: Drawer called "MST-CLOCK.INFO"!\n\nBut thiz Icon will be descripted in the @{"Installation" Link partthree} Part of this Doc-File.\n\nLook there for more infos...\n\n@endnode\n\n@node partthree "Installation of thiz Tool..."\n\n                             INSTALLATION\n                             ~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nHere I will describe how to install the Clock for /X V2.xx & V3.xx...first\nthe Installations for the different Amiex-Versions :\n\n\n V2.XX\n~~~~~~~\nWell, get a Texteditor and put the following Line into your BBS.CMD File:\n\n----CUT HERE----\n*T        XM001DOORS:MST-CLOCK\n----CUT HERE----\n\nI don''t explain the XM001... coz I think you know how to install doors in \nur BBS....if u do not, FUCK OFF !!!!\n\n\n V3.XX\n~~~~~~~\nCopy the Icon "T.INFO" from this Archive to your BBS:COMMANDS/BBS.CMD \nDrawer and change the Tooltypes for your own settings,i.e. ACCESS=150 usw.\n\nNow, copy the Files "MST-CLOCK" and "MST-CLOCK.INFO" to yar DOORS: Drawer.\n\nIMPORTANT NOTE:DON''T FORGET TO COPY THE MST-CLOCK.INFO FILE INTO DOORS:, \n               OTHERWISE THE TOOL WON''T WORK !!!!\n\nIn the Iconfile are two Tooltypes :\n\n   1) LOCATION=str     Where `str` is the Location, you are livin'', i.e.\n                       LOCATION=BeRLiN/GeRMaNY \n                       `str` can be 40 characters long, if the length from\n                       str is greater than 40, all following characters\n                       were cutted off...so don''t be suprised....:)\n\n   2) GMT=x            In this Tooltype, you must (!) enter your Difference\n                       between the Greenwich MeanTime (GMT) and your \n                       Country...i.e. for Germany the GMT is +1...it''s not\n                       neccessary to write a +, but if you livin'' in L.A.\n                       for example, your GMT-Time is -8..and here you must\n                       enter the `-` sign, otherwise the Program things, ur\n                       GMT-Time is +8...silly, but who cares...:)\n\n\nAnd that''s all for installation...easy he ?? Now enjoy thiz Fast Clock and \nI hope you don''t came too late to one of you dates anymore...:)\n\nThe last thing I should write down are the @{"GREETINGS..." Link partfour}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node partfour "Greetings and Adverts..."\n\n                                GReeTiNGS\n                                ~~~~~~~~~\n\n  aXe/MsT         - THX FoR HeLPiNG WiTH THe GFX...iT''S CeWL !\n  aRGoN/MsT       - KeeP oN TRaDiN'' MaN !\n  BYTeaNDi/MsT    - C RuLeZ !!! We aRe oN THe RiGHT WaY !\n  SPY/MsT         - CeWL TaLKiNG oN THe LaST MeeTiNG...\n  eMPiRe/MsT      - uR TooLS aRe GreaT ! WaiTiNG FoR MoRe ReLeaSeS....:)\n  KiLLRaVeN/MsT   - WHY u ReLeaSe SHiTTY aReXX-TooLS ? TRY C...\n  FuZZY/MsT       - WHeRe aRe uR ReLeaSeS ???\n  eaSY RiDeR/MsT  - i''LL LeaRN PoLiSH SooN...:)\n  WoLFGaNG/iNDY   - THX FoR TeSTiNG MY TooLS\n  STRiDeR/SHaDeS  - HoPe To See No MoRe aReXX-TooLS iN THe FuTuRe...:)\n  SK¡N & aMBLiN   - You aRe THe ReaL ASC¡¡-GoDS !!!!\n\nFoR @{"CoNTaCT" Link contact} CaLL DiaBoLo-BBS /X-DeSiGN WHQ aND LeaVe a MeSSi To SieGeL/MsT\n\n@endnode\n\n@node contact "KALL DIZ OR DIE !!!!!"\n\n                         ·  :                 .     :     :\n -============-   \____ ¬V ¬V___ ¬V___ ¬V___ ¬V ¬|  |___ ¬| MANAGEMENT\n  MYSTIC           | ¬|  |  | ¬|  | ¬|  | ¬|  |  |  | ¬|  | -========-\n       GHQ         |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | ANDi/MST\n -============-    |  |  |  |     |    _|  |  |  |__|  |  | SPY/MST\n                   |  |  |  |  |  |  | ¬|  |  |  | ¬|  |  | FELDMAN\n -ELiTE oNLY-      |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | FuZzY/MsT\n                   |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | SYSTEM\n CALL US NoW FoR   |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | -====-\n THE NEWEST AMiGA/ |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | RUNS oN A3000\n PCSTUFF           |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | WiTH 25MHZ AND\n AND ALL MST-      |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  | AMiEX (REG.)\n RELEASES.         |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n                 __|_____A__A__A__A_____A_____A_____A_____| SUPPoRTET BY\n WE oNLY ACCEPT    |     :  :     :     :     :     :D!   | -==========-\n 9600 - 16.800     :     ·  .     .           .     ·     : M Y S T I C\n BAUD CoNNECTS.    .        .                                      \n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),'{"ACCESS":"150","LOCATION":"str"}','auto-added',22407,5,0,NULL,NULL,'mst_cl10','scan',1780048619);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mst_cm11','MST-CM11.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MST-CM11.LHA','Chat-O-Meter','XIM','Chat-O-Meter','1.1',NULL,'MST',NULL,replace('Chat-o-Meter v1.1 TOP Chatter list for /X\n','\n',char(10)),'Chat-O-Meter.GUIDE',replace('@DATABASE "Chat-O-Meter.GUIDE"\n@REMARK .------------------------------------------------------------------.\n@REMARK | This document is written in AmigaGUIDE format, so please read it |\n@REMARK | with AmigaGUIDE or your favourite guide reader.... ciao now...   |\n@REMARK `------------------------------------------------------------------''\n@REMARK $VER: Chat-O-Meter v1.1\n@WIDTH 80\n@NODE MAIN "Guide to Chat-O-Mter - By KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n\n      ____:        ____:     ________        :__       :________________\n     /    |_____  /    |_____\__     |_______|  \_____ (__________     /\n    /     |     \/     |       /     ___________      \/     \    |___/_\n  _/    \   /    \_____       /\_____      \___/      /       \   |     \\n  \______\_/      \_____     /     _________/\       /\______ /__________\\n =-=-=-=-=-|_______\=-=\____/\_____/=-=-=-=-=-\_____/=-=-=-=\/[Sy-K!]-=-=-=\n\n                     -=-( KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC BrInGs YoU )-=-\n\n                         >»»»> CHAT-O-METER 1.0 <««««<\n\n                               @{"+-Introduction-+" link introduction }\n                               @{"+-Installation-+" link installation }\n                               @{"+-Requirements-+" link requirements }\n                               @{"+-----Usage----+" link usage}\n   \n                               @{"+----History---+" link History }\n                               @{"+----Contact---+" link Contact }\n                               @{"+----Greetz!---+" link Greetinx }\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Introduction "Welcome to Chat-O-Meter! - By KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n\n                      -%- Introduction to Chat-O-Meter -%-\n\n   Welcome  to  another  /X-DeSiGn production!  This time a not-so-serious\n   utility.  Chat-O-Meter is a small program that `watches'' your chats and\n   records  how  long  you  have  chatted.   Every  time  a chat is ended,\n   Chat-O-Meter will display how long you have chatted and if this chat is\n   worth being recorded in the Top Ten Chats!\n\n   Also,  the  total  number  of  chats held and the total time chatted is\n   recorded  in this file.  This file is a text-file so it can be shown as\n   a  bulletin  if  ya  like  or  display it after every chat (with an MCI\n   command).\n\n   That is all Chat-O-Meter does. I hope you like it :)\n\n                              @{" EXAMPLE-OUTPUT " link Example}\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Requirements "What do you need to have - By KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n\n                             -%- Requirements -%-\n\n   This is my first release for both /X 2.xx and 3.xx so enjoy it!\n\n   Requirements:  » Ami-Express v2.xx or v3.xx\n                  » A big mouth (for real long chats! :))\n                  » Users with an even bigger mouth!\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Installation "How do I install it? - By KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n\n                            -%- Installation -%-\n\n   Okay, for the fast sysops with /X 3.xx:\n\n   - Make a dir called Doors:Chat-O-Meter and copy `Chat-O-Meter'' in it\n   - Copy the `Chat-O-Meter.info'' file to your SysCmd directory\n   - Edit your StartChat.TXT & EndChat.TXT and make sure `Chat-O-Meter''\n     is called at the start and end of the chat\n   - That''s it\n\n   Fast sysops with /X 2.xx:\n\n   - Make a dir called Doors:Chat-O-Meter and copy `Chat-O-Meter'' in it\n   - Edit your `bbs.cmd'' like this:\n     *CHAT-O-METER XM020Doors:Chat-O-Meter/Chat-O-Meter\n   - Edit your StartChat.TXT & EndChat.TXT and make sure `Chat-O-Meter''\n     is called at the start and end of the chat\n   - That''s it\n\n                       And Now For The Slow Ones... :)\n\n   For both versions:\n\n   » Make a directory called `Doors:Chat-O-Meter''\n   » Copy the program called `Chat-O-Meter'' to this directory\n     (spell the name correct!)\n   » Now you have to edit your `STARTCHAT.TXT'' and `ENDCHAT.TXT'' which\n     can both be found in your BBS:NODEx/ directory. Make sure this is\n     put into it:\n     \n     ~CC_CHAT-O-METER\n     \n   This  should  be  put  in  BOTH  files!  If you didn''t have those files\n   already,  make  sure  to put in any welcome word was well, ''cause Ami-X\n   doesn''t  display  `This is xxxx, how can I help you?'' any longer if you\n   have those files!\n\n   If you want to have the scores file shown after every chat, this can be\n   done with the MCI commands.\n\n   * For /X 2.xx sysops: *\n\n   - Edit your `bbs.cmd'' like this:\n\n     *CHAT-O-METER XM020Doors:Chat-O-Meter/Chat-O-Meter\n\n   * For /X 3.xx sysops: *\n\n   - Copy the `Chat-O-Meter.info'' file to your SysCmd directory\n\n   You are done! Enjoy!\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Usage "Some info about Chat-O-Meter - By KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n\n                             -%- Usage Info -%-\n\n   Chat-O-Meter works like this:\n\n   Every  time  it is started it checks your T:  directory to see if there\n   is  a  @{"specific  file" link file}  present.   If  it  isn''t, it will be created and\n   Chat-O-Meter will exit at once.\n\n   If  it  is  present,  that  means  that  you  have  ended  a  chat  and\n   Chat-O-Meter  will  read  that file, delete it and create a new Top Ten\n   file called `Chat-O-Top.TXT'' in the Doors:Chat-O-Meter/ directory.\n\n   So  to show the Top Ten Chats, all you need to do is display that file.\n   It  already includes a CLS code, so the screen is cleared for ya.  It''s\n   real simple actually.  That is all there is to be said.\n@EndNode\n\n@Node file "The ENV: file... - By KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n\n   This  file  is called `ENV:Chat-O-Meter@x'' where the `x'' stands for the\n   number  of  the  node you are on!  If, per accident, you get to see the\n   results of the chat at the BEGINNING of a chat, get out of the chat and\n   remove the file in the ENV:  directory and all will be okay!  @EndNode\n\n@EndNode\n@Node History "The Making Of... - By KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n\n                               -%- History -%-\n\n   23-Oct-93   1.1   Implemented safety-procedure so when user drops\n                     carrier in chat the Chat-O-Top doesn''t get mixed up.\n                     Released at: 27-Oct-93\n\n   17-Oct-93   1.0   First release to friends.\n\n   From here it can only grow...\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Contact "To get in contact with me - By KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n                               -%- Contact -%-\n\n                            I can be reached at:\n\n               Channel-X - Node 1 - +31-2290-62244 - 14k4DS/TD\n               Channel-X - Node 2 - +31-2290-62535 - 16k8DS/TD\n               \n                                    or at\n\n               Last Outpost - Node 1 - +31-72-157682 - 16k8DS\n               Last Outpost - Node 2 - +31-72-201182 - 16k8DS\n\n                                    or at\n\n               The Undiscovered - Node 1 - +31-2294-4442 - 14k4SUP\n\n                                    or at\n\n                          INTERNET: [email removed]\n                       /X-FIDO NET: 44:100/100.1\n                           NLA NET: 14:100/102.1\n                           BOS NET: 99:999/4.1\n                           AMY NET: 39:151/201.1\n\n                               Bye for now...\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Greetinx "Greetings to people I know - By KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n                              -%- Greetinx -%-\n\n   Big hello''s fly to:\n   \n   HardByte/MST   - What would life be without a tv? (Hé, that rhymes :))\n   \n   Tycoon/MST     - Pre-exams suck major...\n   \n   Byteandi/MST   - You are a very sportive kinda guy! I like that!\n\n   Siegel/MST     - Nice little tools! What are your plans?\n\n   Spy/MST        - Memory ain''t that hard, is it?\n\n   Easy Rider/MST - You dirty you! Too bad I lost that message!\n\n   Muad''Dib/ATX   - USR Rulez My Man... only elite :))\n   \n   Dick Jansen    - Love ya... :)\n   \n   Yhatware       - Rave Is The Best! Rave The City III is KeWl!\n\n   Coca Cola Kid  - Earth calling CCK?\n   \n   Cable          - Do you think you will beat me? Never!\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Example "This Is How It Looks In B/W - By KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n             ___\n    ______  /  /_____________      ____      _________________________________\n    \___  \/  /  / __ \__   /     /    \     \_____   / _____   / ____/  __  /\n    /  /__/ __  /     / /  / /\  /  /  / /\  /  / /  /  __/ /  /  __//  /  \/\n   /  /  /  /  /  /  / /  /  \/ /  /  /  \/ /  / /  /  /__ /  /  /__/  /\n   \____/\_/  /\_/\_/  \_/      \____/      \_/\/\_/\____//  /\____/\_/\n           \_/                                            \_/\n                                BEST 10 CHATTERS \n \n      1. KiLLraVeN               2 hours,  2 mins and 24 secs!  (21-Oct-93)\n      2. Cable                   1 hours, 31 mins and 11 secs!  (13-Oct-93)\n      3. Blackout                1 hours, 20 mins and 49 secs!  (15-Sep-93)\n      4. Muad''Dib                1 hours, 11 mins and 39 secs!  (19-Oct-93)\n      5. Lightning               0 hours, 57 mins and 16 secs!  (31-May-93)\n      6. Fingernail              0 hours, 44 mins and 10 secs!  (24-Jan-93)\n      7. KiLLraVeN               0 hours, 38 mins and  7 secs!  (16-Dec-92)\n      8. The Cheese              0 hours, 31 mins and 56 secs!  (12-Apr-93)\n      9. Wild Life               0 hours, 29 mins and 24 secs!  (11-Feb-93)\n     10. HardByte                0 hours, 17 mins and 53 secs!  (01-Nov-92)\n \n         Total # of chats: 4325!         Total chat time:   416:06:47!\n \n         Chat-O-Meter WaS DoNe In 1993 By KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC (/X DeSiGn)\n\n        [ Hehehe.. this example is frauded... look at the dates :) ]\n@EndNode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',22671,5,0,NULL,NULL,'mst_cm11','scan',1780048619);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mst_cm20','MST-CM20.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MST-CM20.LHA','Chat-O-Meter','XIM','Chat-O-Meter',NULL,NULL,'MST','.-\_  \/  _/   __/______\/___/-------------. | /   \/   \______  \_  \/  \_   mYSTIC!   | :/     \____/   _____/___    / /X dIVISION .',replace('  __/\  __________ _ ___  /\__              \n.-\_  \/  _/   __/______\/___/-------------.\n| /   \/   \______  \_  \/  \_   mYSTIC!   |\n:/     \____/   _____/___    / /X dIVISION .\n/_______\-\_____/--sTZ--l___/--------------:\n| KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC BRiNGS: CHAT-O-METER v2 |\n| *CREATES BULLETiN ABOUT YOUR CHAT-TiMES* :\n: o Cool Layout (StZ!) o Sysop Chat Top 10 |\n| o Hide chat & more   o User Statistics   :\n: o Conversion util to upgrade from v1.x!  |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'Chat-O-Meter.Guide',replace('@DATABASE "Chat-O-Meter.GUiDE"\n@REMARK  .-------------------------------------------------------.\n@REMARK  | This document should be read with AmigaGuide (OS 2.x) |\n@REMARK  | or MultiView (OS 3.x) or any other guide reader. Tnx. |\n@REMARK  `-------------------------------------------------------''\n@REMARK  $VER: Chat-O-Meter 2.0.9\n@WIDTH 80\n@NODE MAIN "KiLLER Comment - MYSTiC 1994 - © 1994 KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n                            Guide to Chat-O-Meter\n                 for Ami-Express 3.38+ Bulletin Board Systems\n\n                            Program version: 2.0.9\n               Compilation Date/Time: Sun Dec 25 14:00:09 1994\n\n                        © 1994/1995 by @{"KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC" link Contact}\n\n                   ... another fine MYSTiC /X production ...\n\n                       @{"       UPDATE iNFORMATiON!       " link WhatsNew}\n\n      @{" Welcome Sysop! " link WhatIs}    What is Chat-O-Meter?\n      @{" Features       " link Features}    What can it do?\n      @{" Installation   " link Install}    How to install Chat-O-Meter\n      @{" Conversion     " link Conversion}    How to convert your old 1.x bulletin to 2.x\n      @{" Example 1      " link BullExample}    Example output the bulletin of Chat-O-Meter\n      @{" Example 2      " link ExitChatExample}    Example output when you exit a chat\n      @{" History        " link History}    History of Chat-O-Meter\n      @{" Greetings      " link Greetings}    Greetings, messages and contact info\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE WhatIs "What is Chat-O-Meter - © KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n                          - -----------------------.\n                         |  What Is Chat-O-Meter?  |\n                         `----------------------- -\n\n   Chat-O-Meter  is  a  small tool that keeps track of all your chats, in\n   particulair  the  length  of  all  your  chats  with users.  With this\n   information it is able to create a nice looking @{"bulletin" link BullExample} that displays\n   a Top Ten of all times.\n\n   Besides  that,  it  also saves the times of the chats per user. At the\n   end  of  every  chat,  the  user  gets  to  see  his  or  her personal\n   information such as the overall score and total number of chats he/she\n   was engaged in.\n\n   This  only  takes up a small amount of time and hardly any disk space.\n   The  creation of the bulletin only takes up about 1 sec (on a standard\n   machine,  it''s  even  quicker  on 020+ systems) and the file size of a\n   file that holds 400 users is about 3.5Kb.\n\n   Chat-O-Meter  also  is giftware, do with it what you want, but you may\n   not  sell  it.  Distribution on AmiNet is allowed, but distribution on\n   PD  series  is  forbidden  (I  don''t  like  people  making money of my\n   products).\n\n   Anyway,  this  version has been totally rewritten from scratch and now\n   has a cool logo made by Stezothetic, so enjoy it!\n\n                                                        @{"-KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC" link Contact}\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE WhatsNew "What''s New in version 2.0 - © KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n                           - --------------------.\n                          |  New in version 2.0  |\n                          `-------------------- -\n\n   The  previous  version ( 1.2 ) was released over one year ago (October\n   1993)  and  to tell you the truth, the coding was lousy and it was not\n   that  sysop  friendly.   But  do  not  despair,  this version has been\n   totally rewritten (from scratch!) and is much smarter and has got some\n   nice new options.  Better forget all about the previous version :-)\n\n   It  has  to  be  said  that I would have never created this version if\n   Quartz  hadn''t  asked  for  it  AND if Stezothetic hadn''t made such an\n   awesome logo.  It seems people use my tools after all :-)\n\n   First  of  all,  the best improvement is that it is now able to detect\n   wether you started or ended a chat.  So if you were a previous user of\n   Chat-O-Meter,  the  times  of  deleting  the  old data file before you\n   started another chat are over :) Lost carriers are no problem anymore.\n\n   Another  *BIG* improvement is the @{"new layout" link BullExample}, done by Stezo (Stz).  It\n   now  has  got a really great logo and nice colours.  You''ll love it, I\n   do!  Many thanks to Stezothetic for creating the logo!\n\n   What  also  new is, is the fact that a record is kept of all chats per\n   user.   One  file is kept that contains all information about ALL your\n   chats ever (since you started to use CoM ofcoz) per user.  I will also\n   create  a  door/tool that creates a nice bulletin out of that one.  If\n   you  think  this  is  nonsense, you are able to turn it off so no data\n   file will be created.\n\n   The  previous  version also did not set the ENV:  variable of AMi-X to\n   the right value, so users that performed a ''who'' saw that the user you\n   were  chatting  with was ''using a door''.  This has been fixed.  But if\n   you  liked  that ''feature'' of Chat-O-Meter, it is still able to hide a\n   chat. Privacy above all (nope, there is no PGP function :) ).\n\n   That''s it.  I hope you''ll like it, it''s one of those nice little doors\n   that  makes  just  the  difference  between your board and your follow\n   sysops'' boards.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE Features "Features of Chat-O-Meter - © KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n                      - ------------------------------.\n                     |  Features of Chat-O-Meter 2.0  |\n                     `------------------------------ -\n\n   ­ Creates a bulletin wherever you want (configurable)\n\n   ­ Very nice/cool layout thanks to Stezothetic (Stz)\n\n   ­ Ability to hide a chat from other users\n\n   ­ Fast creation of data files and bulletin\n   \n   ­ Small data files (308 bytes and 2 bytes/user)\n   \n   ­ Keeps track of sysop chats, but also user chats. That is,\n     a record is kept per user with his/her personal total chat\n     time and total number of chats.\n     \n   ­ At the end of a chat, a small bulletin is shown stating the\n     latest statistics. See @{"example" link ExitChatExample}.\n     This is configurable (Quiet mode is available).\n     \n   ­ Configurable ''Show Bulletin [ Y/n ]'' when user has entered\n     the Chat-O-Meter Top Ten.\n     \n   ­ Configurable stripping of plural words ( 1 mIN instead of 1 mINS)\n\n   ­ Easy to use\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE ExitChatExample "Exit Chat Example - © KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n\n   Every time you exit a chat, you will get to see this small bulletin.\n\n :                                                                         :\n-O-------------------------------------------------------------------------O-\n :  /X MYSTiC       Chat-O-Meter v2.0  by  KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC     /X MYSTiC  :\n ¡                                                                         .\n :  tHIS cHAT:  0:00:11 -O- oVERALL tIME: 0002:07:44 -O- cHAT #: 187       ¡\n .         yOUR oVERALL sCORE: 0000:12:46 -O- yOUR cHAT #: 132             :\n .                                                                         |\n :   sORRY dUDE, nO Chat-O-Meter tOP tIME tODAY, tRY aGAIN sOON, oKAY?!    :\n-O-------------------------------------------------------------------------O-\n :                                                                         :\n\n   However,   when   you   specify   that   you  don''t  want  a  userfile\n   (NO_USERFILE), you will get this as output:\n\n :                                                                         :\n-O-------------------------------------------------------------------------O-\n :  /X MYSTiC       Chat-O-Meter v2.0  by  KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC     /X MYSTiC  :\n ¡                                                                         .\n :  tHIS cHAT:  0:00:02 -O- oVERALL tIME: 0002:07:49 -O- cHAT #: 190       ¡\n .                                                                         |\n :   sORRY dUDE, nO Chat-O-Meter tOP tIME tODAY, tRY aGAIN sOON, oKAY?!    :\n-O-------------------------------------------------------------------------O-\n :                                                                         :\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE Install "Installation of Chat-O-Meter - © KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n                      - -----------------------------.\n                     |  How to install Chat-O-Meter  |\n                     `----------------------------- -\n\n   First  of  all, you can put the executable (Chat-O-Meter) anywhere you\n   like.   The  data  files  will  be  created in that same directory.  I\n   suggest  you  put it in DOORS:Chat-O-Meter/ but hey, it''s up to you (I\n   just  hate  it  when people hard code a path in their program, haven''t\n   they heard of the PROGDIR:  assign?).\n\n   Secondly,  Chat-O-Meter  needs  to be started with an MCI command from\n   the  STARTCHAT.TXT  and  ENDCHAT.TXT  files  that can be found in your\n   BBS:NODEx/   directory.    Two   icons   have   been  supplied  called\n   `Chat_Start.info''  and  `Chat_End.info''.   I recommend you put them in\n   your  BBS:Commands/SYSCmd/  directory,  as  is  standard with commands\n   started with an MCI command.\n\n   For  those sysops who don''t know how to implement Chat-O-Meter in your\n   STARTCHAT.TXT  and  ENDCHAT.TXT,  make  sure the text files contain at\n   least the following lines:\n\n                 STARTCHAT.TXT           ENDCHAT.TXT\n                 -------------           -----------\n                 ~                       ~\n                 ~CC_CHAT_START          ~CC_CHAT_END\n\n   It  doesn''t  matter wether you''ve got a logo in those files.  Just put\n   the text in there somewhere.\n\n   Once you have copied the icons to your BBS:Commands/SYSCmd/ directory,\n   check out the following tooltypes:\n\n   Chat_Start.info\n   ---------------\n   STACK=50000          ; Keep it this high, everything is done on stack\n   There are no more tooltypes for this icon.\n   \n   Chat_End.info\n   -------------\n   CHAT_END             : This  is how Chat-O-Meter recognizes the end of\n                          a chat. Make sure it is in this icon!\n\n   BULLETIN=            : This  is where you can specify how the bulletin\n                          should be called and where it should be created\n                          (i.e. BULLETIN=BBS:Bulletins/Chat-O-Meter.TXT)\n\n   DONT_ASK             : Normally,  whenever  a user gets in the Top Ten\n                          of Chat-O-Meter,  he/she  will  be asked wether\n                          the  Chat-O-Meter  bulletin  should be shown to\n                          them. However, if you specify this tooltype, no\n                          questions  will  be  asked  and nothing will be\n                          shown.\n\n   DONT_TRUNC           : By  default  all plural ''s''-es will be removed.\n                          So  for  example:  1 hOURS  becomes 1 hOUR  and\n                          1 sECS  becomes  1 sEC.  However,  if you think\n                          that  ruins  the  bulletin (cosmetically),  you\n                          can  override  it  by specifying this tooltype.\n                          All plural ''s''-es will be left alone.\n\n   QUIET                : Whenever  a chat is ended,  a small bulletin is\n                          shown  with  the  latest  statistics about that\n                          chat.  However,  if  you do not want this to be\n                          shown,  specify this tooltype and the user will\n                          even know you are using Chat-O-Meter.  No,  not\n                          even a copyright message ;-)\n\n   NO_USERFILE          : This  version  of  Chat-O-Meter  creates a file\n                          that  contains  all  chat information about the\n                          users,   one  by  one.  So  Chat-O-Meter  knows\n                          from  every  user,  how long he/she has chatted\n                          and  how many times you have chatted with them.\n                          It  doesn''t  take  up  much space,  with around\n                          400  users  you will get a file of about 3.5KB.\n                          If  you  feel  this  is  useless or you have no\n                          need  for  this,  insert this tooltype and that\n                          file   will  not  be  created  plus  the  small\n                          bulletin at the end of a chat will be smaller.\n\n   That are all tooltypes for this moment.  When you are done setting the\n   tooltypes  you  are ready with the installation of Chat-O-Meter.  Have\n   fun and chat your head off!  :-)\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE BullExample "Bulletin Example Output - Design by Stezothetic!"\n\n   ASCII  never looks good in AmigaGuide or MultiView, but you''ll get the\n   idea anyway I hope.\n   \n   If  you  might wonder why there are multiple entries for one user, the\n   Chat-O-Meter  Top  Ten  is  sorted  by  the length of the chat, and it\n   doesn''t matter wether a user is present several times in it.\n   \n   This  is  not because I am to lazy to built in that check, but suppose\n   you have a chat of 5 hours with somebody.  The next time you chat with\n   him,  you  have a chat of 7 hours.  Does this mean I should just erase\n   that  5  hour  chat and mention the 7 hour chat?  I think not, that is\n   not  fair.   A  5  hour chat is just as cool as a 7 hour chat and they\n   both deserve to be mentioned.\n\n .                          _  __           /        __  _      ·          .\n-O-_____   ___.___  ___________ //\___   / ·   ______\  .        \ _      -O-\n :/  __/__/   |  ¬\/   _ ¬\____\/____/  · /   /  __ ¬\ -:---------\/-----. :\n_/   |   ¬\_  _    \_  _   \_  \/  ¬\_ / / /_/   \/   \_| >cHAT·O·mETER< | :\n\_____     /__|     /__|    /___     //_/ / \_____     /`----------------'' H\n-:---l____/---l____/---l___//\-l____/-\_\/-------l____/------ ---  --   -  ¡_\n H                       __/  \  ___  ___________  /\_________    _______  \/\n | .------------------.  \_    \/  ¬\/  __ ¬\____\/____/  __ ¬\___\____ ¬\_H\n ¡ :   ·/X mYSTIC!·   :  /     \/    \_ \____/__ \/  ¬\_  \____/__   \/  _/:\n :_`---------------- - _/       \_____/___     /__     /____     /___/    \_\n \/ -  -- --- ---------\_________/--Stz--\____/--l____/----\____/----\_____/-\n :                                                                         |\n !   o1. Muad''Dib             01 hOUR , 20 mINS aND 51 sECS  (22-dEC-94)   :\n |   o2. Muad''Dib             00 hOURS, 25 mINS aND 15 sECS  (22-dEC-94)   :\n O   o3. TyCooN/MYSTiC        00 hOURS, 03 mINS aND 04 sECS  (24-dEC-94)   ¡\n |   o4. TyCooN/MYSTiC        00 hOURS, 01 mIN  aND 51 sECS  (22-dEC-94)   O\n H   o5. KiLLRaVeN/MYSTIC     00 hOURS, 01 mIN  aND 22 sECS  (21-dEC-94)   |\n :   o6. TyCooN/MYSTiC        00 hOURS, 00 mINS aND 59 sECS  (24-dEC-94)   H\n H   o7. TyCooN/MYSTiC        00 hOURS, 00 mINS aND 51 sECS  (22-dEC-94)   :\n ¡   o8. KiLLRaVeN/MYSTIC     00 hOURS, 00 mINS aND 34 sECS  (21-dEC-94)   ·\n_:   o9. KiLLRaVeN/MYSTIC     00 hOURS, 00 mINS aND 32 sECS  (21-dEC-94)   :_\n\:   1o. KiLLRaVeN/MYSTIC     00 hOURS, 00 mINS aND 29 sECS  (22-dEC-94)   :/\n \                                                                         /\n :\        tOTAL # oF cHATS: 190         tOTAL cHAT tIME:    2:07:49      /:\n-O-\---------------------------------------------------------------------/-O-\n :  ·                                                                   ·  :\n\n           (Ghee, I chat a lot with myself don''t you think? :-) )\n\n      The design was done totally by Stezothetic, many thanks for that!\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE History "History of Chat-O-Meter - Amazing... :)"\n                  - -------------------------------------.\n                 |  History: Something that once was...  |\n                 `------------------------------------- -\n\n   22-Jan-95   1.0.1    Fixed CoM-Convert; it now reads the name of the\n                        user from the correct place.\n\n   04-Jan-95   1.0.0    Completed CoM-Convert and restyled it.\n\n   03-Jan-95   1.0.0    Created CoM-Convert.\n\n   25-Dec-94   2.0.9    Chat-O-Meter can also run in silent mode now.\n                        New tooltype: QUIET\n\n   25-Dec-94   2.0.8    Merry X-Mas :) Made some internal changes, removed\n                        the stack-check (smaller executable).\n\n   24-Dec-94   2.0.7    Found the bug that caused the strange resets.\n                        I adjusted the wrong variable... sigh... it\n                        should be fixed now.\n\n   24-Dec-94   2.0.6    Allocated memory for some structures by myself\n                        instead of allocating them on the stack. Hope\n                        to have fixed the strange guru''s.\n\n   24-Dec-94   2.0.5ß   Special version for Muad''Dib with DEBUG info.\n\n   24-Dec-94   2.0.5    Tried to fix a bug that caused strange resets on\n                        Muad''Dibs machine (040) and weird crashes on my\n                        own system (total freeze and I had to turn my\n                        computer off for at least one minute!).\n\n   24-Dec-94   2.0.4    Fixed a bug that caused the bulletin only the be\n                        updated in the event of a new entry in the Top\n                        Ten. The Total Chat Time was never updated.\n                        *Reported by Quartz*\n\n   23-Dec-94   2.0.3    Built in the User file, now a record is kept of\n                        every user. A new bulletin perhaps.\n                        New tooltype: NO_USERFILE\n                        \n                        Altered the output after the chat again, now also\n                        contains info about the user him/herself.\n\n   22-Dec-94   2.0.2    Altered the output a bit and made some minor\n                        internal changes that caused a smaller executable.\n\n   21-Dec-94   2.0.1    Altered the output after a chat.\n\n   21-Dec-94   2.0.0    Totally rewrote it from scratch:\n                        - END_CHAT tooltype fixes the problem with lost\n                          carriers and then starting a chat again causing\n                          the start of the chat being the end of a chat.\n                          (Never mind if you don''t get it, it''s fixed!)\n                        *Requested by Quartz*\n\n                        New layout from Stezothetic implemented.\n                        *Thanks to Stezothetic*\n\n   26-Oct-93   1.2      Output file is now sysop-configurable. Now you can\n                        have it saved anywhere you like!\n                        Released: 30-Oct-93\n\n   23-Oct-93   1.1      Implemented safety-procedure so when user drops\n                        carrier in chat the Chat-O-Top doesn''t get mixed up.\n                        Released at: 27-Oct-93\n\n   17-Oct-93   1.0      First release to friends.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE Greetings "Greetings and thanks - © 1994/1995 KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n                            - --------------------.\n                           |  Greetings & Thanks  |\n                           `-------------------- -\n\n   A *BIG* THANKS TO STEZOTHETIC (Stz) FOR CREATING THE DESiGN, THANKS MATE!\n\n   Also thanks to Quartz for stimulating me to create this version.\n\n                                      :\n                                     -O-\n                                      :\n\n   Muad''Dib       -  Finally 3 nodes kicking on 28k8!\n   \n   Quartz         -  Logos make me program :)\n   \n   Stezothetic    -  You''re in the army... nooohow...\n   \n   I-GO           -  Johnnies and Anitas zuigen!\n   \n   Wishbringer    -  Faces... (no, not faeces ;-) )\n   \n   Motive Power   -  War is a fucking tough game!\n   \n   bObO           -  We need to talk ( :) )\n   \n   Zed            -  I hope you like this tool mate.\n   \n   Undertaker     -  Your modules kick ass, nobody can beat you!\n   \n   Arcade         -  Some times are rough, some are tough...\n   \n   MYSTiC Members -  Love you all :-)\n   \n                       ... and everybody I forgot ...\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE Contact "How to get in touch with me - © KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n                             - ------------------.\n                            |  Contacting me...  |\n                            `------------------ - \n\n       For FAST response (preferred) please contact me on Internet:\n\n                               [email removed]\n\n                    ( [email removed] -- backup )\n\n                       - - -- --- ------- --- -- - -\n\n                 I can be reached on the following boards:\n\n                       - - -- --- ------- --- -- - -\n\n                The Undiscovered       +31-2294-1442 (USR 28k8)\n                                       +31-2294-4442 (USR 28k8)\n                                       +31-2294-tRY! (USR 28k8)\n\n                Last Outpost           +31-72-201182 (USR 28k8)\n                                       +31-72-157682 (USR 28k8)\n\n         I know, you have to call The Netherlands for it, but it''s\n            the only boards I call on a frequent basis, sorry.\n\n                       - - -- --- ------- --- -- - -\n\n        You can also find me on IRC once in a while on the channels\n                   #amigascne, #amiga, #rave and #megawatt\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE Conversion "How to convert your old bulletin - © 1995 KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n                           - ---------------------.\n                          |  Bulletin Conversion  |\n                          `--------------------- -\n\n   For  sysops  that  used  Chat-O-Meter  1.x, there is a special program\n   called  "CoM-Convert"  that allows you to convert your old bulletin to\n   the  new  data  file  that  Chat-O-Meter  2.0  uses.  If you are not a\n   previous user of Chat-O-Meter, you can skip this part.\n\n   To  convert  it,  simply  start  the  program  "CoM-Convert"  from the\n   directory  where  you  have Chat-O-Meter 2.0 installed.  The data file\n   will be created in the directory where you started "CoM-Convert".\n\n   Once  you  have  started the program, a file requester will pop up and\n   you  must select the old bulletin.  Press `OK'' and you will get to see\n   the names (plus additional info) from that bulletin.\n\n   After that, the program will exit (`Ready.'') and you can find the data\n   file  called  `Chat-O-Meter.Data''  in that same directory.  Move it if\n   you  have  to.  The new bulletin will not be created yet!  To do this,\n   you  have  to  start Chat-O-Meter 2.0 from /X (start and end a chat is\n   sufficient).\n\n   That''s it, easy a as a fiddle.\n\n   NOTE : To use this tool, you must have req-tools installed.\n\n   NOTE¹: There  is *NO* check whether the file you feed to "CoM-Convert"\n          really  is an old bulletin from 1.x.  You can even cheat if you\n          want to ;-)\n\n   NOTE²: To  all beta-testers, this conversion util takes in account any\n          old  `Chat-O-Meter.Data'' file.  That is, it doesn''t recalculate\n          a new Top-Ten (it simply converts the old one), but it does ADD\n          the  old  `Total Chat Time''  to the new time and that also goes\n          for the total number of chats.\n@ENDNODE\n','\n',char(10)),'{"STACK":"50000"}','auto-added',42549,2,0,NULL,NULL,'mst_cm20','scan',1780048619);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mst_com2','MST-COM2.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MST-COM2.LHA',NULL,'XIM','Z1.EXE',NULL,NULL,'MST','.-\_  \/  _/   __/______\/___/-------------. | /   \/   \______  \_  \/  \_   mYSTIC!   | :/     \____/   _____/___    / /X dIVISION .',replace('  __/\  __________ _ ___  /\__              \n.-\_  \/  _/   __/______\/___/-------------.\n| /   \/   \______  \_  \/  \_   mYSTIC!   |\n:/     \____/   _____/___    / /X dIVISION .\n/_______\-\_____/--sTZ--l___/--------------:\n| KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC BRiNGS: CHAT-O-METER v2 |\n| *CREATES BULLETiN ABOUT YOUR CHAT-TiMES* :\n: o Cool Layout (StZ!) o Sysop Chat Top 10 |\n| o Hide chat & more   o User Statistics   :\n: o Conversion util to upgrade from v1.x!  |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'Dago.TXT',replace(' .=[*][+][*][+]`=[*][+][*][+]`=[*][+][*][+]`=[*][+][*][+]`=[*][+][*][+][*]=.\n[*    | __                                                      __  |    *]\n +]   ; \/+-=->   NoW cAlL tHe OrGaNiZeD CrIme cAlL fAsT   <-=-+\/  ;   [+\n[*    >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>DAGOBERTS-REVANGE<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<     *]\n `-=>         :                :   BBS                        :Dagobert<=-`\n >>>> //////////////////////////////\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ <<<<<<<\n .-=> <-+-:AmIgA 2000 -8MB- 700 Mb OnLiNe - 68030/28MhZ - CoOl:-+->    <=-`\n[*    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\//////////////////////////////       *]\n[+    *YoUr OpErAtOrS aRe: Dagobert - cosy:TKK/Butthead/Blackcat *       +]\n[+    *        For other Conferences :.....................      *       +]\n[+    *                  Right hand is :TKK                      *       +]\n[+    ************************************************************       +]\n[+    \               NoDe0 +49 208-ask-ask  16.8 Zyxel          /       +]\n*]     \              NoDe1 +49 208-ask-ask  14.4 USR-D.S       /        [*\n+]      \             NoDe2 +49 208-ask-ask  16.8 Zyxel        /         [+\n+]       \            Node3 +49 208-ask-ask  ||:| V32bis      /          [+\n+]        \           Node4 +49 208-!!!-!!!  PRIVAT          /           ]+\n[+         **************************************************            +]\n+]        /    AMIGA-TOOLS-PORNO-X/Tools-CONSOLE-PEEeCEEe    \           [+\n[+       ------------------------------------------------------          +]\n+]        \________________JUST_FOR_FUN_!!___________________/           [+\n+[    ===============================================================    +]\n+]    """""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""    +]\n[+   .:-*- AsK onLy ElItEs foR da NuMber aNd tHe SyStem PasSword -*-:.   +]\n+]    """""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""    +]\n[+    ===============================================================    [+\n *]_  _  _  _    _  _  _  _    _  _  _  _    _  _  _  _    _  _  _  _  _[*\n.=[*][+][*][+]`=[*][+][*][+]`=[*][+][*][+]`=[*][+][*][+]`=[*][+][*][+][*]=.\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',19987,11,0,NULL,NULL,'mst_com2','scan',1780048619);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mst_cs1','MST-CS1.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MST-CS1.LHA','ConferenceSecurity','XIM','AmigaGuide',NULL,NULL,'MST','_/  v  \__/ ! \  /  _____.   ._(__)/  . \ \_ _:_ ______  \/\___  \ |   | |  \_  |_/\ _/  \ /  \_  v  __   v   \|   | |    _ |   \',replace('   _____    ___    _____________.__. ____   \n _/  v  \__/ ! \  /  _____.   ._(__)/  . \  \n \_ _:_ ______  \/\___  \ |   | |  \_  |_/\ \n_/  \ /  \_  v  __   v   \|   | |    _ |   \\n\    v    /  ___/\    ___/!___! !___/__-   /\n-\___:___/___/-ã!-\___/---------------\___/-\n--------------------------------------------\n','\n',char(10)),'ConferenceSecurity.Guide',replace('@DATABASE Conference Security Documentation V1.00\n@NODE main "Conference Security Documentation V1.00"\n\n           /\                                _____.      /\\n      /\  /  \ ______    ______/\___________/    ¬!_____/  \  ______________\n     /  \/    \\    ¬\  /    ¬/                         |   \/            ¬/\n    /          \\     \/     /  ___________.      ._____!___/             /\n   /            \\     \    /_____.     ¬\ |      7    ¬\  ¬\       .____/_____\n  /    \  /      \\        /      7       \!      |      \   \      7        ¬/\n /      \/        \/      /|      !        \      !      /    \     !        /\n/________\         \     / |               /            /      \            /\n       /____________\   /  !______        /!___        /_______/___        /\n             ·A×E·\    /         \_______/    \_______/           \_______/\n                   \  /\n                    \/\n                         .oO· Conference Security ·Oo.\n\n         @{"Introduction              " LINK intro}         @{"Example Of A Configuration" LINK configex}\n         @{"Installation              " LINK install}         @{"Text vs. AmigaGuide       " LINK txtvsag}\n         @{"Join Conference        ''J''" LINK join}         @{"Note Worthy Features      " LINK features}\n         @{"Add Conference         ''>''" LINK add}         @{"Compability               " LINK comp}\n         @{"Sub Conference         ''<''" LINK sub}         @{"Disclaimer & Copyright    " LINK discopy}\n         @{"Logoff                 ''G''" LINK logoff}         @{"Contact The Creators      " LINK bloodstreet}\n         @{"Logoff Batch              " LINK batch}         @{"Mystic Boards             " LINK boards}\n         @{"Configuration             " LINK config}         @{"Credits And About         " LINK creds}\n\n               All Was Done by *CoNaN&NeWToN* For Mystic in 1993\n\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE intro "Introduction"\n\n   » Introduction «\n·-==================-·\n\nThis Door Gives You The Ability To Secure Certain Conferences From Hacking\nand Generally Keeping Your Private Conferences Safe.\nWorks With Normal or Relative Conferences.\nAlso Takes Account Of Stupid Sysops Who Give Multiple Access To The Same\nConferences.\n\nThere Are Certain Good Things In Having All The Conference Doors In One\nDoor, But Mostly More Security Arround The Conferences.\n\nThis Is An Assembler XIM Door! NOT REXX OR "C" SHIT!\n\nThe Door Can Be PowerPacker and Still Work From AmiExpress... Surprised?\n(But You Loose CPU Speed!)\n\nOnly Available For AmiX V3.x! (If Requested A 2.xx Version Can be Arranged.)\n\nI Would Like To Urge The AmiExpress Development Team To Be More Helpful\nTowards Un-Registered AmiExpress Developers Such As C+N.\nInstead Of Keeping People From Creating Good Doors, Lots Of People Are\nCreating Crap Doors... And Loads Of Them!!\n\nSo You Better Appreciate The Time Spent On These *CoNaN&NeWToN* Productions.\n\nIf You don''t Know The Names You Can Be Assured That 10 Years In The Scene\nIs Quite Impressive And That Our Experience In Programming Is More Than\nEnough To Make AmiExpress Assembler Tools.\n\nIf You Have Problems Installing This Door Contact Us...\n                        ...Or If You Just Want To Get In Touch With Us... :)\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE install "Installation"\n\n   » Installation «\n·-==================-·\n\nYou Should Have The Following Files Present...\nDoors:MST_ConfSec/\n  ConferenceSecurity         The XIM Door (Use For ALL 4 Commands)\n    Version 1.00             (Instruction Below)\n\n  ConferenceSecurity.info    The Configuration File! (AmiX 3.x Standard)\n    No Version?!             Use Wb.Info Or Dopus.\n\n  ConferenceSecurity.Exe     The Logoff.Batch File (Handling Safe Confs.)\n    Version 1.00             If You Use This Don''t Use ConfSecCleanUp.Exe Too!\n                             (Usage Information Below)\n\n  ConfSecCleanUp.Exe         Use In LogOff Batch If You Don''t Use The LogOff\n    Version 1.00             For Safe Conferences. (Usage Information Below)\n\n  ConferenceSecurity.Doc     Txt Documentation For This Door.\n    Version 1.00\n\n  ConferenceSecurity.Giude   AmigaGuide Documentation For This Door. (This?!)\n    Version 1.00\n\nCommands(/BBSCmd)\n  J.info                    Patches The JoinConference Command.J\n  <.info                    Patches The Fast Lower JoinConference Command.<\n  >.info                    Patches The Fast Higher JoinConference Command.>\n  G.info                    Patches The Logoff Command.G\n\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE join "Join Conference"\n\n   » Join Conference "J" «\n·-=========================-·\n\nWill Compute A Conference Menu For You If You Decide That Users Should\nOnly See The Conferences They Have Access To.\nSee Configuration For MenuTypes!\nChecks A Give Access Level And/Or A Password For The Conferences.\n\nParameters Will Ofcoz Be Recognized For Shortcuts!\n  "J <confnr.>"\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE add "Add Conference"\n\n   » Add Conference  ">" «\n·-=========================-·\n\nAdds 1 To The Current Conference. Checks For Access Level And Password.\nIt Goes Into Join Conference If Any Problem Accours. (See Above!)\n\nNo Parameters Will be Aknowledged! (At The Moment.) Any Ideas?\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE sub "Sub Conference"\n\n   » Sub Conference  "<" «\n·-=========================-·\n\nSubs 1 To The Current Conference. Checks For Access Level And Password.\nIt Goes Into Join Conference If Any Problem Accours. (See Above!)\n\nNo Parameters Will be Aknowledged! (At The Moment.) Any Ideas?\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE logoff "Logoff"\n\n   » Logoff          "G" «\n·-=========================-·\n\nChecks If You Are Login Off In A "Safe Conference" or If You Have To Move\nBefore You Can Logoff. If You Must Move, It Will Go Into Join Conference.\nIt Uses Also Needs A Run In The Logoff Batch To Ensure That "Alt-H" And\nF10 Actions To Do Not Break Any Security!\nHere Again It Will Check Password,Axx And Safe Conference Configurations.\n\nParameters Will Ofcoz Be Recognized For Shortcuts!\n  "G <safe confnr.>"\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE batch "Logoff Batch"\n\n   » Logoff Batch «\n·-==================-·\n\nTo Ensure That People Who Loose Carrier Can Not Auto-Join A "Safe Conference",\nIf An Account Should Get Hacked And The Foul Being Then Just "Happends" To\nAuto-Join A Restricted Conference.\n\nConfSecCleanUp.Exe\n  This One Only Delete The "PSWFAILSTATS@#" That The JoinConference Uses\n  To Control The Amount Of Password Failures.\nUsage:\n    ConfSecCleanUp.Exe          Deletes All "PSWFAILSTATS@#" In Env:\n                                Use In BBS Init.\n    ConfSecCleanUp.Exe <node>   Deletes The "PSWFAILSTATS@#" For The\n                                Node To Be Reset! Use In LogOff.Batch.\n\nConferenceSecurity.Exe\n  Changes The AutoJoin Conference In The User.Data If Something Needs\n  To Be changed.\nUsage:\n    ConferenceSecurity.Exe          Run All User.Data AutoJoin Conference.\n                                    Use In BBS Init.\n    ConferenceSecurity.Exe <node>   Runs User or All User.Data AutoJoin C.\n                                    Use In LogOff.Batch.\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE config "Configuration"\n\n   » Configuration «\n·-===================-·\n\nThe Configuration Must Be Placed In "Doors:"! (At Least For This Version)\n\nAmiX3.x Config.:\nIn Order To Maintain The Same "Style" As AmiX I Have Made The Configuration\nAs An .info File ("ConferenceSecurity.info").\nYou Can Use Dopus or Workbench To Alter .info Files.\n(The Door.info Should Ofcoz Be Made According To AmiX.Docs!)\n\nFollowing Things will be Recognized in the .info:\n\nPSW.<confnr.>=<password>     : User Required To Enter Password!\nCPSW.<confnr.>=<password>    : User Required To Enter Case Sensitive Psw!\nAXX.<confnr.>=<access level> : User Required To Have At Least Specified Axx.!\nHOT.<confnr.>                : User Can Not LogOff (AutoJoin) Conference!\nAXXFAIL=<access level>       : Users Access Level Dropped To, After Psw-Fail!\nMENUTYPE=<menu type>         : The Display You Use For Yar JoinConf.Menu\nCONFIRM=<confirm type>       : Confirm LogOff Configuration\nLIST.<confnr>=<listpathfile> : Check If you Name Is Allowed In Conference!\nDAY.<confnr>=<Day On/Off>    : Which Days Conference Can Be Joined.\nTIME.<confnr>=<HHMM>,<HHMM>  : Set Time Interval For Conference Join.\n                               Multiple Can Be Used For Same Conference.\n                               (Does Not Handle Over Midnights.\n                               Eg.: 2300,0100... Use 2300,2359 and 0000,0100)\nNAME.<confnr>=<xtra>|<conf name>\n                             : Will OverRide Confname In ConfConfig.Info.\n                               <xtra> Is For Add On''s!\n                               <conf name> Will Be Right Centered As Normal!\n                               <xtra> Will Be Left Centered!\n                               <xtra> With No <confname> Will Left Centre\n                               <xtra> And Right Centre The NodeConfig ConfName.\nNOPSWAXX=<access level>      : Users With Axx Level Equal Or Higher\n                               Do Not Have To EnTer Psw To Join Psw Confs.\nLOGO=<pathfile>              : You Can Show An Ansi Above The Conf List.\n                               (Only For Internal MenuType.)\nNET=<netnumber>              : First Net Mail Conference.\nNORM_COLUMNS=<column number> : Number Of Columns In Normal/Local Conference\n                               List. (Only For Internal MenuType.)\nNET_COLUMNS=<column number>  : Number Of Columns In Net Conference List.\n                               (Only For Internal MenuType.)\nDAYTIME_PRIVATE.<confnr.>    : Will Not Show Joinable Days And Times!\n\n<confnr.>        ranges from 1 to 999                           (AmiX3.x Limit)\n<password>       can be 32 Characters                              (Door Limit)\n<access level>   ranges from 1 to 255                           (AmiX Standard)\n<menu type>      There Are Three Different Types:\n  STANDARD       <Screens>JoinConf<access level>.<language>|.<gr>\n  AREA           <Screens>JoinConf.<area><access level>.<language>|.<gr>\n  INTERNAL       Will Calculate Internal Menus. No Bother Creating Files\n                 For Relative Conferences!!\n                 Can Be Immitated With ~MCI Codes Also!\n                 Faster Than The Above...!\n<confirm type>   Different Types\n  NONE           User Does Not Have To Confirm LogOff.\n  NOTEXPERT      User In Non Expert Mode Has To Confirm LogOff.\n  EXPERT         User In Expert Mode Has To Confirm LogOff.\n  ALL            User Has To Confirm LogOff.\n<listpathfile>   .info File Where You List The Names To A Give Conference.\n                 Conf2List(.info) Do Write .info In Your Config!!\n<HHMM>,<HHMM>    Start Time,End Time Of Interval.\n<Day On/Off>     Is Made Of 7 Chars. One For Each Day. "X" For Ok.\n                 First Char Is Sunday And Last Is Saturday.\n                 Eg.: DAY.3=X__X__X. Conference 3 Can Be Joined On Sundays\n                 Wednesdays And Saturdays Only!\n\nDefault "MenuType" Is "STANDARD".\nIf <Screens> Is Not In Your BBS:NodeX.info Then "BBS:Node<x>/" Is Default.\nDefault "Confirm" Is "NONE".\nDefault "Time" Is "0000,2359"\nDefault "Net" Conference Start Is 0 (Maining Only Local Conferences.)\nDefault "NORM_COLUMNS" and "NET_COLUMNS" Are 1. (Max 3 Columns.)\nAll Columns Are Auto Adjusted If There Is Enough Space.\n\nIf No "NOPSWAXX" Is Defined Then All Users Will Have To Enter Psw''s.\n(Ideal For Sysop''s Who Get Bored With Entering Psw!)\n\nAll Strings Can Use Upper or Lower Case, The Door Is Not Case Sensitive.\nExcept of course Case Sensitive Passwords.\n\nMost Options Are Maybe Pretty Weird But Try Them And You Will Maybe Find\nOut Their Purpose And Future Purposes For You.\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE configex "Example Of A Configuration"\n\n   » Example Of A Configuration «\n·-================================-·\n\nAXX.3=100                              : Access Level To Join Conf 3\nAXX.5=245                              : Access Level To Join Conf 5\nPSW.5=innersanctum                     : Password For Conf 5\nHOT.5                                  : No Logoff From Conf 1 And .Exe Run\n                                         Through For Security!\nAXXFAIL=100                            : Set Access Level Down After Password\n                                         Failure!\nMENUTYPE=Internal                      : Menutype. Fast Internal!\nHOT.1                                  : No Logoff From Conf 1 And .Exe Run\n                                         Through For Security!\nCPSW.4=DuLpErT                         : Case Password For Conf 4\nCONFIRM=NOTEXPERT                      : Logoff Confirm Type\nLIST.2=Doors:MST_ConfSec/Conf2List     : .info List Of Admited User In Conf 5\nLIST.5=Doors:MST_ConfSec/Conf5List     : .info List Of Admited User In Conf 5\nTIME.3=1100,1300                       : Tine Interval For Conference 3\nTIME.3=1930,2300                       : Tine Interval For Conference 3\nDAY.3=XXX_XXX                          : Days Open In Conference 3\nNOPSWAXX=255                           : Users With This Or Higher Access Level\n                                         Dont Have To Write A PSW!\nNAME.5=[UN0001]|Hard Core              : New Split! Name For Conf 5\nNAME.4=Crap Request                    : New Name For Conf 4\nNAME.2=Local|                          : Adds <Extr> And Keeps The Confname!!\n                                         Left And Right Centered Of Course.\nLOGO=Doors:MST_ConfSec/JoinConf.Logo   : Ansi Above The Internal Menutype Only!\nNET=4                                  : Net From Real! Conf 4\nNORM_COLUMNS=3                         : 3 Normal Conferences\nNET_COLUMNS=2                          : 2 Net Conferences\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE txtvsag "Text vs. AmigaGuide"\n\n   » Text vs. AmigaGuide «\n·-=========================-·\n\nI Examined An AmigaGuide File And Discovered The Structure.\nSo Instead Of Using Converters To Get Your Prefered Format I Have Desided\nTo Make One Of Each! Both Viewing Utilities Should Be Inluded In The\nDistribution Package.\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE features "Note Worthy Features"\n\n   » Note Worthy Features «\n·-==========================-·\n\nWell The Join Door Keeps Track Of Online Psw Failures So If 3 Failures Occur\nIn Da Same Conference User Can NOT Join Any Psw Conf.\nPeople May Abort Psw Check After 2 Failures, But The Door Keeps Track On\nFailures In (Env:PswFailStats@N) As Long As User Online!\nEnv:PswFailStats@N File Is Reset With One Of The Two Available .exe Files\nIn Your Logoff.Batch...)\n\nWill Enter Psw Failures In CallersLog.\n\nSupports Only 0-9 Nodes, And Will Ofcoz Be Updated If Joseph Hodge\nDesides To Make More Nodes Available. (And Even If He Doesn''t...)\nCan Handle Up To 1-999 Conferences, But I Seriously Doubt If It Will Be\nA Problem!\n\nSupports Also "Screens=<path>". And Confirm LogOff As Configured...\nFeatures For Netmail Boards.\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE comp "Compability"\n\n   » Compability «\n·-=================-·\n\nThis Door Should Work Fine With All Computers.\nAssembled With A A4000/68040/KS3.0 and tested on My Slow A500/68000/KS2.0.\nDoor Should Work On KS1.2/1.3 But AmiExpress Requires KS2.0+!\n\nCurrently This Door Only Works With AmiX3.x.\n\nUse Version <files> To Make Sure The Versions In This Doc Corresponds To The\nFiles In The Archive.\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE discopy "Disclaimer & Copyright"\n\n   » Disclaimer&Copyright «\n·-==========================-·\n\nThe Authors Of This AmiX Door Do Not Take Any Responsability For Any Loss\nOf Data Using This Or Any Other Products By Yours Truly.\nThis Door Is Copyright by C+N. This Means That This Door Should Be Spread\nIn It''s Original State.\n(No Files May Be Excluded Or Changed From The "Install" Archive.)\n\nThis Is Not Public Domain, Not Fee Can Be Taken For This Program!\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE bloodstreet "Contact *CoNaN&NeWToN* At Bloodstreet"\n\n   » Feedback «\n·-==============-·\n\nWell It Would Be Nice To Know If People Use Our Doors On Their Boards!\nSo Please Contact Us Just For Fun. Or For Suggestions And Stuff.\n\nOur Modem Handle Is "CoNaN&NeWToN" So If You See It Arround... :)\n                         _      .                   _\n                ________/¬\   __:     _____   _____/ \___________\n                \___       \./ ¬|___./    ¬\./    ¬\_____    ___/\n                  \__  _| __V.  |  ¬V.  |   V.  |   |.  |   __/\n                   \__ \_  ¬|¦  |  .|:  |   |:  |   |¦  |   _/\n                    |   |   |°  |  ¦|°  |   |¦  |   |°  |   |\n             _  _/\_A       A      °A       A°      A   |   A_/\_ _\n                     \_____/ \_____/ \_____/ \_____/ \_____/  _\n       _______________/¬\___/\________   ________/\__________/¬\_________\n       \____   ______/     ¬\______  ¬\./   ______/   ______/       ____/\n         \______   ¬|.   |   |. __|  __V.   _____|    _____|.   |  ____/\n          \_   |    |¦   |_  |: \__   ¬|¦   |    |.   |    |¦   |_____/\n           |   |    |°   | \_|¦   |   .|°   |    |¦   |    |°   |\n      _ _  A    ____A_   |   |°  _|   ¦|______   A°  ______A_   A  _ _\n         \/ \__/      \_/:    \_/ |   °|      \_/ \_/        \_/ \/\n                         :        _)  (_\n                                  \ sc /\n                                   \  /\n                                    \/\n\n      There is Only One Board In The World Where You Can Be Sure To Find\n             *CoNaN&NeWToN*. So Why Not Try Calling Bloodstreet...!\n                         +45-75-15-9284 <> +45-75-15-9286\n\n                        Net...AmiXnet : @DK0001 (MAiNLiNE)\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE boards "Mystic Boards Worldwide"\n\n   » Mystic Boards «\n·-===================-·\n                   .\n    _______     __/|__    _______________________.  /\______\n   _\  .. ¬\   /   ! ¬\  _\  ________.   .___.  ¬| /   .___/\n   \_  ||   \ /____.   \_\_____ ¬\___|   |___|   |/    |__Z___\n  /¬   ||  -\\    ¬!  -\\    ¬V -\\  | -!|   | -!|\    !¬  -// FuN RoOLeS !\n  \____!!_  _/\______  _/\_____  _/\ !___!   !___! \_____  _/  -^- -  - -^-\n   \___\_\_/\\/\____\_/\\/\___\_/\\/ !___!   !___!\/___/\_//\n+--------·\\/·------·\\/·-----·\\/·-------------------·\//·------------------+\n|DiGiTal CaNdY   ^ 3 NdZ aMiGa Whq! ^ -------- ÷ ------------- +1-5134713366 |\n|LaST ouTposT    ^ 2 NdZ aMiGa Ehq! ^ SneS Whq ÷ /X-DeSiGn EhQ +31-72157682  |\n|BoGuS ExCepT¿oN ^ 2 NdZ aMiGa UShq ^ -------- ÷ ------------- +1-2ø34378655 |\n|The RestaUrAnt  ^ 3 NdZ aMiGa UShq ^ -------- ÷ ------------- +1-6163637ø27 |\n|D¿aBoLo         ^ 3 NdZ aMiGa Ghq! ^ -------- ÷ /X-DeSiGn WhQ +49-3ø6218787 |\n|TrAdE ¿n CeNtEr ^ 1 Nd'' aMiGa Ghq! ^ IbM! EhQ ÷ /X-DeSiGn GhQ +49-7ø826ø611 |\n|TrAdE ¿n CeNtEr ^ 2 NdZ aMiGa iSDn ^ IbM! EhQ ÷ ------------- +49-7ø8292122ø|\n|NorTh star Land ^ 2 NdZ aMiGa Ghq! ^ -------- ÷ ------------- +49-304162261 |\n|CrY¿nG F¿eLdS   ^ 1 Nd'' aMiGa Ghq! ^ -------- ÷ ------------- +49-4ø6452525 |\n|THe Add¿cT¿oN   ^ 1 Nd'' aMiGa Ghq! ^ -------- ÷ ------------- +49-61ø231564 |\n|An¿mAlS         ^ 1 Nd'' aMiGa Chhq ^ -------- ÷ ------------- +41-53246782  |\n|MaMbA           ^ 1 Nd'' aMiGa Phq! ^ -------- ÷ ------------- +48-22367443  |\n|OuT oF SpAcE    ^ 1 Nd'' aMiGa Shq! ^ -------- ÷ ------------- +46-62o13141  |\n|ChAnNeL-X       ^ 2 NdZ aMiGa DisT ^ -------- ÷ /X-DeSiGn DhQ +31-229ø62244 |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------·A×E^MsT·-+\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE creds "Credits & About"\n\n   » Credits&About «\n·-===================-·\n\nThis Door Was Only Made So That People Can Feel More Secure In Their\nDaily Use Of Private or Restricted Conferences.\nAnd Because Their Seems To Be A Lack of Quality Asm Doors Out There!\nIt Has Been Thouroughly Tested And Should Not Contain Any Bugs.\nCreated With The Help From Arexx Port Stuff And An Asm Source Sent by\nSilverHawk!/Tarkus Team. Thx!\n\nI Had Some Support From The Following Things:\nMean The Cruel!, NeWToN The Money Sucking Hole!, Omar''s Video+Videos!\nA Wicked Metallica Tape...?? Some C64 Tunes...\n\nWell This Door Should Be 100% Mc680xx And Kickstart (1.x,2.x/3.x Compatible)\nBecause It Was Made On My A4000/040/25Mhz With Kick3.0...And My A500...\nAnd Tested on An A2000 With Kick2.0.\n\nBeware of Mc68040, Because I Found A Very Suspicious "Bug", The Code\nTested An Odd-LongAddress But The Mc68040 CAN DO THAT... So Now I Will Have\nTo Test My Code On My A500 For Such Tricky Bugs. A500 Is SO SLOW!!! ARGH!\n\nBETA-TESTING Done By Mean At BloodStreet.. Beware Of Psychotics Roaming!\n\nBut Should You Find Any Bugs, or If You Want To See Some Improvements On\nThis or Other Doors You Should Contact C+N:\n\nWe Can Be Contacted by Modem On:\nBloodStreet...+45-75-159-284 or Maybe On Any Other Mystic Hq...\nThe Before Mentioned Boards Will Maybe Be Running Our Newest Doors/Updates.\n\nLook Out For More Releases From C+N...\n\nGreets To The Following Dudes... Mystic Members Worldwide.\nAll In Tarkus Team - Droopy - BlackHawk - Tsl&Crionics - Detron\nPennywise - Candyman - Ramirez - Zawran&Cromer - Zeus - Mr. Beer\nFelix - Promax - Ozone&Xod - Tensor - Frostie - Dux - Weird Dream & Yobbo\nD-Siya - Flamestriker - Omar - Capital - Excessive Knight - MacroNit\nThe Old Rebels Tribe And Some More...\n\nSoon More AmiExpress Doors From The Hard Working Guys From Mystic /X Design!\n@ENDNODE\n','\n',char(10)),'{"TYPE":"<menu"}','auto-added',68675,8,0,NULL,NULL,'mst_cs1','scan',1780048619);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mst_cs16','MST-CS16.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MST-CS16.LHA','ConfScan','XIM','ConfScan',NULL,NULL,'MST','_/  v  \__/ ! \  /  _____.   ._(__)/  . \ \_ _:_ ______  \/\___  \ |   | |  \_  |_/\ _/  \ /  \_  v  __   v   \|   | |    _ |   \',replace('   _____    ___    _____________.__. ____   \n _/  v  \__/ ! \  /  _____.   ._(__)/  . \  \n \_ _:_ ______  \/\___  \ |   | |  \_  |_/\ \n_/  \ /  \_  v  __   v   \|   | |    _ |   \\n\    v    /  ___/\    ___/!___! !___/__-   /\n-\___:___/___/-ã!-\___/---------------\___/-\n--------------------------------------------\n          WORLD CLOCK VERSION1.6\n','\n',char(10)),'ConfScan.GUIDE',replace('@DATABASE "ConfScan.GUIDE"\n@REMARK .------------------------------------------------------------------.\n@REMARK | This document is written in AmigaGUIDE format, so please read it |\n@REMARK | with AmigaGUIDE or your favourite guide reader.... tnx m8...     |\n@REMARK `------------------------------------------------------------------''\n@WIDTH 80\n@NODE MAIN "Guide to ConfScan v1.6 - /X DeSiGn - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n.----------.                  .--------..---------.\n|   ____   |                  |   _____||   ______|\n|  |    |__|.-------..-------.|  |      |  |______ .-------..-------..-------.\n|  |        |   _   ||   _   ||  |__    |         ||   ____||   _   ||   _   |\n|  |        |  | |  ||  | |  ||     |   `------.  ||  |     |  `-''  ||  | |  |\n|  |    .--.|  | |  ||  | |  ||  .--''          |  ||  |     |   _   ||  | |  |\n|  |____|  ||  |_|  ||  | |  ||  |       ______|  ||  |____ |  | |  ||  | |  |\n|          ||       ||  | |  ||  | v1.6 |         ||       ||  | |  ||  | |  |\n`----------''`-------''`--'' `--''`--'' °°°° `---------''`-------''`--'' `--''`--'' `--''\n                           © 1993 by KiLLRaVeN/MYSTiC\n\n                ... another fine MYSTiC /X DeSiGn production...\n\n  ----Start----» @{"    Introduction    " link Introduction}  .-» @{" History of ConfScan " link History}\n                 @{"     Features!      " link     Features}  |   @{"     BugReports      " link BugReports}\n                 @{"    Requirements    " link Requirements}  |   @{" Possible error msgs " link Errors}\n                 @{"    Installation    " link Installation}  |   @{" Future improvements " link Future}\n                 @{"  Usage (by users)  " link        Usage}--''   @{"    Registration     " link Registration}---.\n                                                                   |\n                                 @{"  Greetings  " link Greetings} «-------------------''\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Introduction "Introduction to ConfScan - /X DeSiGn - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n\n                      ----------( INTRODUCTION )----------\n                                  °°°°°°°°°°°°\n             _________________________________________________________\n       O----/\____\_____\____\____\__________\_________\____\_________\-O\n       :   / /    /     /    /    /    ______/         /    /         / :\n       |  / / _  /     /    /    /____      /    /    /    /    _____/  |\n       | / /   \  _   /____     /    /     /    /____/    /    /    /   |\n       |/ /    /\/   /    /    /    /     /    /  / /    /    /    /    |\n       :\/____/     /_________/__________/    /  / /    /_________/  CD!:\n       O----\/_____/-------------------\/____/---\/____/----------------O\n\n\n   Yezz...  here it is, the ultimate tool for scanning conferences without\n   having  to  join them again and again.  It offers comfortable usage and\n   for  you, the sysop, happy @{"users" link users} ''cause they don''t have to keep joinin''\n   conferences any longer!\n\n   It  does  not  only  scan for new files in all conferences, it can also\n   scan  from  a  certain  date, scan from a numbers of days back.  And it\n   also supports hold directories...\n\n   Anyway,  check  out  the  @{"features" link Features} and I''m sure you will be thrilled to\n   install this door on your system...  happy scanning!\n\n                                                        @{"-KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC" link Killraven}\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Requirements "What DO you need? - /X DeSiGn - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n\n                      ----------( REQUIREMENTS )----------\n                                  °°°°°°°°°°°°\n   Okay, here are the requirements to use this door:\n\n   ­ @{"Ami-Express BBS version 3.x" link Ami-X} (sorry, no 2.xx support, upgrade!)\n   ­ @{"Users" link users}\n   ­ @{"Files" link files}\n\n   Nothing to worry about I hope... (for you)...\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Installation "How to get it working - /X DeSiGn - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n\n                      ----------( INSTALLATION )----------\n                                  °°°°°°°°°°°°\n\n   Easier done than said...  let''s see...  it is real simple, all you have\n   to  do  is copy the supplied icon to your BBS:Commands/BBSCmd/ and fill\n   in the correct tooltypes in the icon, they are:\n\n   ACCESS=020                       ­ Change if ya like\n   LOCATION=DOORS:ConfScan/ConfScan ­ Change if ya like\n   MULTINODE=YES                    ­ Ofcourse it is...\n   PRIORITY=0                       ­ Change if ya like (not neccesary)\n   STACK=50000                      ­ Should be more than enough\n   TYPE=XIM                         ­ We want speed! No slow Rexx!\n\n   ----  ConfScan Tooltypes  ----   ­ Just a comment line, discard it.\n   HOLD_ACCESS=250                  ­ Change  if  ya  like. All @{"users" link users} with\n                                      this accesslevel or higher  are able\n                                      to scan the HOLD dirs.\n\n   ---- Reserved Conferences ----   ­ Just a comment line, discard it.\n   CONF.x                           ­ Put  here  any conference (or confe-\n                                      rences)  that  you  don''t want to be\n                                      scanned  by  ConfScan. You MUST fill\n                                      in   your  mail-conferences  without\n                                      filebase,   other   conferences  are\n                                      optional... for example, if you want\n                                      conference  8  to  be  reserved just\n                                      enter CONF.8 below the comment line.\n\n   A  special  030  version  is also supplied, I suggest you use it if you\n   have  a  030+  board ''cause it scans a bit faster than the 000 version.\n   Just copy the 030 version over the 000 version and you''re done.\n\n   Okay, well, if you''ve done that, you are nearly finished.  All you have\n   to  do  know  is  copy  the program itself (''ConfScan'') to the path you\n   supplied in the icon and after that...  TADA!  Installation complete!\n\n   All  user-config  files  will  be stored in the same directory that the\n   program is in.  The files look like:  ConfScan_UserData.usernumber.  So\n   your  own  config will be "ConfScan_UserData.0" and it will contain the\n   numbers of the conferences you DO NOT want to see...\n\n   NOTE: Maybe  you  want to change the name of the command in /X for your\n         own  convenience  (let''s  say you want to call it SCAN instead of \n         CS), that is okay, the program will work just fine. But if you do\n         so, remember that  the help page will still talk about CS instead\n         of SCAN. Just wanted you to know...\n\n   Well, enough technical information, go enjoy the program!\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Features "Features of ConfScan - /X DeSiGn - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n                        ----------( FEATURES )----------\n                                    °°°°°°°°\n                       Yo ho ho, here are the features...\n\n                                  Easy To Use\n                                  °°°°°°°°°°°\n   ConfScan  is  very  flexible in use and even the dumbest user should be\n   able  to  use  it.   A  help  page is included in the program which can\n   easily be accessed with ''CS ?'' just like in AmigaDOS.\n\n                                 Fast Searching\n                                 °°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n   Scanning  the  directories  goes supersonic thanks to C programming and\n   searching in RAM instead of harddisk.\n\n                              Good Looking Layout\n                              °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n   He?  What can I say?  It just looks good and is informative and uses no\n   high ansi (so even for you, the sysop, it looks good :-)).\n\n                              Security Guaranteed\n                              °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n   There  is  a DOUBLE security in ConfScan.  First of all, a user will be\n   checked  for his conference access, and second, you can reserve certain\n   conferences  of  being  scanned!   So  no  worry  about that, all works\n   relatively  so  @{"users" link users} will not see conferences they are not supposed to\n   see.\n\n                               User Configurable\n                               °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n   Every  user  can  setup his own private config file.  This file will be\n   located  in the same directory as the ConfScan program is in.  The user\n   is able to config which conferences he doesn''t want to see and which he\n   does  want  to  see.   Again,  the is very easy to use (select multiple\n   conferences to turn on/off).  And it looks good too!  ;-)\n\n                              Multi-Node supported\n                              °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n   Not  one  important file will be locked while ConfScan does its job, so\n   that  means  no  waiting on the other node or /X complaining ''cause the\n   conference-dir is locked.\n\n                               Ami-X Net Support\n                               °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n   Most  Ami-X Net conferences don''t have file bases in them, to make sure\n   that  ConfScan  doesn''t  try to scan this conferences (it will cause an\n   error  and the program will abort), you must enter them in the ConfScan\n   info file that comes along with this program.\n\n   And  if you do have Ami-X net conferences with file bases, no problemo,\n   ConfScan will scan them (ofcourse).\n\n                                Scanning options\n                                °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n   ConfScan can scan a lot and in many ways... here they are:\n\n   ­ Scanning from a certain date\n   ­ Scanning from a number of days back\n   ­ Scanning from the day a user was last on\n   ­ Scanning in upload dirs or in all dirs\n   ­ Scanning in hold dirs (special access-level used)\n\n\n   Well,  if  this  doesn''t  convince  you to start using ConfScan, than I\n   don''t  know  what  will.  This door should enlarge the activity on your\n   board  ''cause  @{"users" link users} are losing less time on scanning and so your board\n   is  easier to reach...  I can go on like this, but you are smart enough\n   to see the advantages...\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Usage "Usage by users (that includes you) - /X DeSiGn - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n\n                         ----------( USAGE )-----------\n                                     °°°°°\n\n   Simplicity itself, you can use the program like this:\n\n   CS [option 1] [option 2]\n       ^          ^\n       |          |-------» A(ll)      Scan All dirs\n       |          `-------» U(pload)   Scan Upload dirs\n       |\n       |------------------» S(ince)    Sets  the  date to scan from to the\n       |                               date  the  user  was  last  on your\n       |                               system.\n       |------------------» MM/DD/YY   Sets the date to scan from, it must\n       |                               be in the /X format.\n       |------------------» -X         Sets  the  date  to  scan from to X\n       |                               days back.\n       |------------------» W          With this option the user can create\n       |                               his/her own configuration file.\n       `------------------» ?          Shows the information page.\n\n   If  you  do not use option 1, option 2 becomes option 1...  get it?  So\n   you can use the option 2 commands also as option 1 commands.\n\n   And if you do not specify any option at all, the default values will be\n   taken, which are:  option 1 = S and option 2 = U.\n\n   Okay, it''s example time! Here are some examples you can learn from:\n\n   CS                      ­ Scans for files since you were last on the\n                             board in the upload directory of conferences.\n   CS S U                  ­ Does exactly the same\n   CS U                    ­ Yep, also the same\n\n   CS -5                   ­ Scans for files that are 5 days old in the\n                             upload directory of conferences\n   CS -5 A                 ­ Scans for files that are 5 days old in all\n                             directories of conferences\n\n   CS 08-26-93 A           ­ Scans for files since the 26th of August 1993\n                             in all directories of conferences\n\n   CS H                    ­ Scans for files since you were last on in the\n                             hold directory of conferences.\n\n   CS W                    ­ Let''s you configure ConfScan...\n\n   CS ?                    ­ Show''s you the information page...\n\n   Looks  real easy, doesn''t it?  It is!  Just install it and you''ll never\n   want to miss it again!\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Future "You want more? You animal! - /X DeSiGn - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n\n                  ----------( FUTURE IMPROVEMENTS )----------\n                              °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n\n   Future improvements will be:\n\n   ­ ANSI Display of files (not just black and white)\n   ­ Flagging Files\n   ­ Detecting CTRL-C\n   \n\n   Anyway,  if  you  have  suggestions,  make  sure  to  drop me a line at\n   Channel-X or at one of the other MYSTiC boards (in Holland preferably,\n   that''s where  I  am most).  By the way, you don''t need to have a\n   suggestion to call  the MYSTiC boards, you''re welcome at any time, open\n   24 hours a day and at your service!\n\n   Let me know what you think and what YOU think needs improvement!\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node BugReports "BugReport (Doodlebug Invasion part III) - /X DeSiGn - Written by Guess Who?"\n\n                      ----------( BUG REPORTS )----------\n                                  °°°°°°°°°°°\n\n   Bug reports can be left at one of the MYSTiC /X DeSiGn Boards:\n   \n         Channel-X      +31-2290-62244 (14k4DS)    I''m CoSysop here, so this\n                        +31-2290-62535 (16k8DS)    is where I am most.\n                        \n         Diabolo        +49-30-6218787 (14k4DS)    /X DeSiGn WHQ\n         Last Outpost   +31-72-201182  (16k8DS)    /X DeSiGn DHQ\n                        +31-72-157682  (16k8DS)\n         EuroNode       +49-7131963823 (14k4)      /X DeSiGn GHQ (5 Nodez)\n         Trade''n''Centre +49-708260611  (14k4DS)    /X DeSiGn GHQ\n                        +49-7082921220 (14k4DS)    /X DeSiGn GHQ\n\n                        Other ways to reach me:         \n\n                       /X-FIDO NET: 44:100/100.1\n                           NLA NET: 14:100/102.1\n                           BOS NET: 99:999/4.2\n                           AMY NET: 39:151/201.2\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Greetings "Greetinx Alien, I Want To Speak To Your Leader! - /X DeSiGn (no, really!)"\n\n                       ----------( GREETINGS )----------\n                                   °°°°°°°°°\n\n   So, you wanted to know if you were on the greetings-list eh?  Well, the\n   lucky winners are:\n\n\n   ByteAndi/MsT      Pfooi, I have a lot of trouble getting your includes\n                     to work, but I am rewritting them for myself and for\n                     all other /X DeSiGn Members ofcourse...\n\n   Siegle/MsT        Friendship ROoLez!\n   \n   Axe/MsT           Global eh? Hope so...\n   \n   Tycoon/MsT        Thanks for your help man!\n   \n   Empire/MsT        What happened man? You''re so quiet :-)\n   \n   Pitagora          Thanks for the bug-report, this should fix your\n                     problem.\n\n\n        ... and all my friends on the BosNet/Ami-X Fido mailing systems!\n\n\n                And here are the numbers you are diein'' to call:\n\n               ___\n             _/   ¬\                   - -^o^·M·Y·S·T·i·C·^o^- -\n            /      .¬\\n           /._/\\_\ \ \         HeY SuCkeR CaLL dIz KeWL BoArDs, ToO !\n_ ________(( _/\__\\ \<_____________________________________________________ _\n          /\/__.  \_.  \\n         <__ \ø\\__Y\\  \\n      ____<   ¯¯___///  /  ReD ocToBeR     -^- 3 NoDeS Ehq! -÷- +31-1ø4165552\n     /ø   Y       .//  /   LaST ouTposT    -^- 2 NoDeS Dhq! -^- +31-72157682\n    //    |_  ÷---|` ./    BoGuS ExCepT¿oN -^- 3 NoDeS UShq -^- +1-2034378655\n   /`      /\__  ^/\ |     ThE ResTaUrAnT  -^- 4 NoDeS Whq  -÷- +1-616363ø271\n  /.    .  [_  \_/  \!     EuRoNoDe        -^- 8 NoDeS Ghq! -÷- +49-7131963823\n.//   _/     \_/ ~\  ·     DiAbOlO         -^- 3 NoDeS Ghq! -÷- +49-3ø6218787\n|(    |        ,   \       TrAdE ¿n CeNtEr -^- 2 NoDeS Ghq! -÷- +49-7ø826ø611\n|!    | (   . /    ))      NoRtH StAr LaNd -^- 2 NoDeS Ghq! -^- +49-3ø4162261\n|·    | ø    Y    //  _    tHe Add¿cT¿oN   -^- 1 NoDe'' Ghq! -^- +49-610231564\n|  _  | !    |   / \ (%)   CrY¿nG F¿eLdS   -^- 1 NoDe'' Ghq! -÷- +49-406452525\n| |_| | |    !  ` /"XI_I_  An¿mAlS         -^- 1 NoDe'' Chhq -^- +41-53246782\n!_| |_! !    ·\  ` [____¬\ OuT oF SpAcE    -^- 1 NoDe'' Shq! -÷- +46-62o13141\n/!! !!\ ·      \_  [____ ( ¿nTerPooL       -^- 1 NoDe'' Shq! -÷- +46-34683652\n)     ( ._   _.  \_[_____/__________________________________________________ _\n\_____/   \_/      |÷aXe÷|\n                   X_____X\n\n\n                      ToTaLL MaDNeSS by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC!\n                (Excuse my corny jokes, but FuN RoOlez Ya KnOw!)\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Users "You don''t know what users are? And you''re a sysop?!?!"\n\n   Users: People who are constantly trying to fill up your precious\n          harddisk space with stuff hoping you will get to see that\n          most annoying requester "Volume BBS: is full" and come to\n          the conclusion you just missed the release of the year...\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Killraven "What are you looking for? My DNA structure?"\n\n   Ah, you want to know more about me, well.... okay, I''ll show you a \n   picture of me when I was reaaaaly young:\n\n                  ·\n           ·      ·\n         ·          ·       See the one with the real def hair? That''s\n            ·  · ·    ·     me,  and this picture was taken when I was\n          ·  · ^·     ·     still a reserve recrute at Spermazoid...\n               |     ·\n        ·   ·    ·· ·       (those were the hours... exciting as ever!)\n           ·  ·     ·\n               · · ·\n\n   Enough stupidity... get back to business...\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Ami-X "Ami-Express Information, dude!"\n\n                    Please support Ami-Express and register!\n                    °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n\n                           You can order your copy at\n\n                 LightSpeed Technology (USA)   +1-305-964-4263\n\n\n            Or check your local Ami-Express support board near you!\n\n                                    Thanks!\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Files "What? You need help with that too?!"\n\n   Hé!  Keep your fingers of you brother''s system!  Go play with Barbie or\n   Playmobil!  Don''t touch your brothers computer!\n\n   Go  away  or I''ll tell your brother when he''s back and oooohhh...  does\n   he  know  where  to find ya...  if you only knew what he did to some of\n   his @{"users" link users}...  boy o boy!\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node History "How did it end up like this - /X DeSiGn - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n\n                      ----------( HISTORY )---------\n                                  °°°°°°°\n   1.6   11-Sep-93   Bug-Fix: Dir-files with lines longer than 150\n                     characters caused a guru :-(. The maximum is now set\n                     to 300 characters, that should be enough.\n\n   1.5   25-Aug-93   First public release\n\n   All  previous  information is either lost or not worth to be mentioned,\n   it''s  the usual stuff like "new option" and "fixed a bug".  Believe me,\n   you  don''t wanna know.  From now on the history file will be kept up to\n   date...\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Errors "What have you done wrong? - /X DeSiGn - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n\n                  ----------( POSSIBLE ERRORS )---------\n                              °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n\n   Since  nobody  is perfect, there is a slight chance an error may occur,\n   there are only a few possible errors, so here they are:\n\n   ­ "Couldn''t allocate memory! Too little memory?"\n\n     Do you have enough memory free to run ConfScan?  The program uses about\n     36Kb  of memory (largest block in once is 32Kb for copying files).  The\n     best  thing  you can do is reset and try again.  If it still fails, you\n     better  buy  a  memory  expansion...  if you have enough memory and you\n     still get this error, then please contact me.\n\n   ­ "Couldn''t open temporary file for output! Too little memory?"\n\n     ConfScan  uses a temporary file to store the files which will be showed\n     to  you  later,  this  temp  file  is in the T:  directory, do you have\n     enough  memory  left?   If your file-listings are really big, this file\n     can  be  become  quite large (if you have masses of new warez every day\n     (ofcourse  you  have  :-)).  Maybe the file is still present in T:  and\n     this  MIGHT  cause  the problem, check the T:  directory...  else reset\n     and try again.\n\n   ­ "Couldn''t open file: <name>"\n\n     For  some reason, ConfScan was not able to open the file <name>.  Maybe\n     it  was  in  use by another program?  Best thing to do is reset and try\n     again.   Another  possibility  is that you have not reserved some Ami-X\n     Net- mail area''s and ConfScan tries to open a dir file...\n\n   ­ "Couldn''t open icon.library!"\n\n     If  this  happens,  you better install the icon.libary, but this cannot\n     happen, ''cause /X 3.xx uses it also, so if the icon.library is missing,\n     Ami-X will not startup :-).\n\n   ­ "Error reading from input file during filecopy!"\n\n     It  seems that something went wrong while reading the input file during\n     a  file  copy.  File copies only occur while scanning and when you exit\n     the config menu.  Reset and try again.\n\n   ­ "Error writing to output file during filecopy!"\n\n     Something  went  wrong  while  writing to the output file during a file\n     copy.  This can only happen while scanning and when you exit the config\n     menu.  Reset and try again.\n\n   ­ "Couldn''t open your config file!"\n\n     For  some  reason ConfScan was not able to create your own config file!\n     This should always be possible, better reset and try again.\n\n   Well,  that''s  all  the  errors  ConfScan can create.  If you don''t get\n   ConfScan  working  on your system, just give me call and I''ll make sure\n   it will work!\n\n   /X DeSiGn Support Centre: +31-72-157682 & +31-72-201182 «» 24 Hrs Service\n   °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n   KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC HangOut: +31-2290-62244 & +31-2290-62535 (14k4/16k8/USR)\n   °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Registration "Don''t worry, it costs nothing! - /X DeSiGn - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n\n                   ----------( REGISTRATION )----------\n                               °°°°°°°°°°°°\n\n                      DON''T WORRY, IT COSTS NOTHING!\n\n   Since  I don''t believe in shareware (I know myself :-)) this program is\n   free  to  use.   Spread it as much as you can and tell all your friends\n   about  it.  You may not SELL it to other people, if you catch you do it\n   I will burn your house down!\n\n   What I would like you to do is call @{"Channel-X" link Channel-X} and tell me you are using\n   it.   That  way I know how many people are using it (this encourages me\n   to keep updating ConfScan).\n\n   So I''ll be hearing from you!\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Channel-X "COMMERCIAL MODE <ON> - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n\n                                                 /\        /\\n      ² NØÐE $¥$TEM  ² µ$R Ð$  µPTØ ¹6.8K!  /  \      /  \\n   _____________________________________________\   \    /   /\n  /  ____________________________________________\   \  /   / $¥$Ø¶: T¥ÇØØN\n /  /   / /  / // ___  // / / // / / // ____// /  \   \/   /\n/  /   / /__/ // /__/ //  \/ //  \/ // /_   / /    \  /   /   ÇØ: K¿££®ÆVEN\n\  \  / ___  // ___  // /\  // /\  // __/  / /      \/   /\n \  \/ /  / // /  / // / / // / / // /___ / /___    /   /\    ÆM¿GÆ/ÇØN$Ø£E\n  \  \/__/_//_/__/_//_/_/_//_/_/_//_____//_____/_K!/   /  \\n   \______________________________________________/   /\   \ +³¹-²²9°-6²²44\n                                                 /   /  \   \+³¹-²²9°-6²5³5\n      HØME ØF ÆMI-X F¿ÐØ  MÆN¥ NETMÆ¿L ÆREÆS  \  /    \  /\n                                                  \/      \/\n\n\n@EndNode\n','\n',char(10)),'{"ACCESS":"020","LOCATION":"DOORS:ConfScan/ConfScan","PRIORITY":"0","STACK":"50000","TYPE":"XIM"}','auto-added',57378,6,0,NULL,NULL,'mst_cs16','scan',1780048619);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mst_cs17','MST-CS17.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MST-CS17.LHA','ConfScan','XIM','ConfScan',NULL,NULL,'MST','_/  v  \__/ ! \  /  _____.   ._(__)/  . \ \_ _:_ ______  \/\___  \ |   | |  \_  |_/\ _/  \ /  \_  v  __   v   \|   | |    _ |   \',replace('   _____    ___    _____________.__. ____   \n _/  v  \__/ ! \  /  _____.   ._(__)/  . \  \n \_ _:_ ______  \/\___  \ |   | |  \_  |_/\ \n_/  \ /  \_  v  __   v   \|   | |    _ |   \\n\    v    /  ___/\    ___/!___! !___/__-   /\n-\___:___/___/-ã!-\___/---------------\___/-\n--------------------------------------------\n','\n',char(10)),'ConfScan.GUIDE',replace('@DATABASE "ConfScan.GUIDE"\n@REMARK .------------------------------------------------------------------.\n@REMARK | This document is written in AmigaGUIDE format, so please read it |\n@REMARK | with AmigaGUIDE or your favourite guide reader.... tnx m8...     |\n@REMARK `------------------------------------------------------------------''\n@WIDTH 80\n@NODE MAIN "Guide to ConfScan v1.7 - /X DeSiGn - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n.----------.                  .--------..---------.\n|   ____   |                  |   _____||   ______|\n|  |    |__|.-------..-------.|  |      |  |______ .-------..-------..-------.\n|  |        |   _   ||   _   ||  |__    |         ||   ____||   _   ||   _   |\n|  |        |  | |  ||  | |  ||     |   `------.  ||  |     |  `-''  ||  | |  |\n|  |    .--.|  | |  ||  | |  ||  .--''          |  ||  |     |   _   ||  | |  |\n|  |____|  ||  |_|  ||  | |  ||  |       ______|  ||  |____ |  | |  ||  | |  |\n|          ||       ||  | |  ||  | v1.7 |         ||       ||  | |  ||  | |  |\n`----------''`-------''`--'' `--''`--'' °°°° `---------''`-------''`--'' `--''`--'' `--''\n                           © 1993 by KiLLRaVeN/MYSTiC\n\n                ... another fine MYSTiC /X DeSiGn production...\n\n  ----Start----» @{"    Introduction    " link Introduction}  .-» @{" History of ConfScan " link History}\n                 @{"     Features!      " link     Features}  |   @{"     BugReports      " link BugReports}\n                 @{"    Requirements    " link Requirements}  |   @{" Possible error msgs " link Errors}\n                 @{"    Installation    " link Installation}  |   @{" Future improvements " link Future}\n                 @{"  Usage (by users)  " link        Usage}--''   @{"    Registration     " link Registration}---.\n                                                                   |\n                                 @{"  Greetings  " link Greetings} «-------------------''\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Introduction "Introduction to ConfScan - /X DeSiGn - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n\n                      ----------( INTRODUCTION )----------\n                                  °°°°°°°°°°°°\n             _________________________________________________________\n       O----/\____\_____\____\____\__________\_________\____\_________\-O\n       :   / /    /     /    /    /    ______/         /    /         / :\n       |  / / _  /     /    /    /____      /    /    /    /    _____/  |\n       | / /   \  _   /____     /    /     /    /____/    /    /    /   |\n       |/ /    /\/   /    /    /    /     /    /  / /    /    /    /    |\n       :\/____/     /_________/__________/    /  / /    /_________/  CD!:\n       O----\/_____/-------------------\/____/---\/____/----------------O\n\n\n   Yezz...  here it is, the ultimate tool for scanning conferences without\n   having  to  join them again and again.  It offers comfortable usage and\n   for  you, the sysop, happy @{"users" link users} ''cause they don''t have to keep joinin''\n   conferences any longer!\n\n   It  does  not  only  scan for new files in all conferences, it can also\n   scan  from  a  certain  date, scan from a numbers of days back.  And it\n   also supports hold directories...\n\n   Anyway,  check  out  the  @{"features" link Features} and I''m sure you will be thrilled to\n   install this door on your system...  happy scanning!\n\n                                                        @{"-KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC" link Killraven}\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Requirements "What DO you need? - /X DeSiGn - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n\n                      ----------( REQUIREMENTS )----------\n                                  °°°°°°°°°°°°\n   Okay, here are the requirements to use this door:\n\n   ­ @{"Ami-Express BBS version 3.x" link Ami-X} (sorry, no 2.xx support, upgrade!)\n   ­ @{"Users" link users}\n   ­ @{"Files" link files}\n\n   Nothing to worry about I hope... (for you)...\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Installation "How to get it working - /X DeSiGn - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n\n                      ----------( INSTALLATION )----------\n                                  °°°°°°°°°°°°\n\n   Easier done than said...  let''s see...  it is real simple, all you have\n   to  do  is copy the supplied icon to your BBS:Commands/BBSCmd/ and fill\n   in the correct tooltypes in the icon, they are:\n\n   ACCESS=020                       ­ Change if ya like\n   LOCATION=DOORS:ConfScan/ConfScan ­ Change if ya like\n   MULTINODE=YES                    ­ Ofcourse it is...\n   PRIORITY=0                       ­ Change if ya like (not neccesary)\n   STACK=50000                      ­ Should be more than enough\n   TYPE=XIM                         ­ We want speed! No slow Rexx!\n\n   ----  ConfScan Tooltypes  ----   ­ Just a comment line, discard it.\n   HOLD_ACCESS=250                  ­ Change  if  ya  like. All @{"users" link users} with\n                                      this accesslevel or higher  are able\n                                      to scan the HOLD dirs.\n\n   ---- Reserved Conferences ----   ­ Just a comment line, discard it.\n   CONF.x                           ­ Put  here  any conference (or confe-\n                                      rences)  that  you  don''t want to be\n                                      scanned  by  ConfScan. You MUST fill\n                                      in   your  mail-conferences  without\n                                      filebase,   other   conferences  are\n                                      optional... for example, if you want\n                                      conference  8  to  be  reserved just\n                                      enter CONF.8 below the comment line.\n\n   A  special  020  version  is also supplied, I suggest you use it if you\n   have  a  020+  board ''cause it scans a bit faster than the 000 version.\n   Just copy the 020 version over the 000 version and you''re done.\n\n   Okay, well, if you''ve done that, you are nearly finished.  All you have\n   to  do  know  is  copy  the program itself (''ConfScan'') to the path you\n   supplied in the icon and after that...  TADA!  Installation complete!\n\n   All  user-config  files  will  be stored in the same directory that the\n   program is in.  The files look like:  ConfScan_UserData.usernumber.  So\n   your  own  config will be "ConfScan_UserData.0" and it will contain the\n   numbers of the conferences you DO NOT want to see...\n\n   NOTE: Maybe  you  want to change the name of the command in /X for your\n         own  convenience  (let''s  say you want to call it SCAN instead of \n         CS), that is okay, the program will work just fine. But if you do\n         so, remember that  the help page will still talk about CS instead\n         of SCAN. Just wanted you to know...\n\n   Well, enough technical information, go enjoy the program!\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Features "Features of ConfScan - /X DeSiGn - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n                        ----------( FEATURES )----------\n                                    °°°°°°°°\n                       Yo ho ho, here are the features...\n\n                                  Easy To Use\n                                  °°°°°°°°°°°\n   ConfScan  is  very  flexible in use and even the dumbest user should be\n   able  to  use  it.   A  help  page is included in the program which can\n   easily be accessed with ''CS ?'' just like in AmigaDOS.\n\n                                 Fast Searching\n                                 °°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n   Scanning  the  directories  goes supersonic thanks to C programming and\n   searching in RAM instead of harddisk.\n\n                              Good Looking Layout\n                              °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n   He?  What can I say?  It just looks good and is informative and uses no\n   high ansi (so even for you, the sysop, it looks good :-)).\n\n                              Security Guaranteed\n                              °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n   There  is  a DOUBLE security in ConfScan.  First of all, a user will be\n   checked  for his conference access, and second, you can reserve certain\n   conferences  of  being  scanned!   So  no  worry  about that, all works\n   relatively  so  @{"users" link users} will not see conferences they are not supposed to\n   see.\n\n                               User Configurable\n                               °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n   Every  user  can  setup his own private config file.  This file will be\n   located  in the same directory as the ConfScan program is in.  The user\n   is able to config which conferences he doesn''t want to see and which he\n   does  want  to  see.   Again,  the is very easy to use (select multiple\n   conferences to turn on/off).  And it looks good too!  ;-)\n\n                              Multi-Node supported\n                              °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n   Not  one  important file will be locked while ConfScan does its job, so\n   that  means  no  waiting on the other node or /X complaining ''cause the\n   conference-dir is locked.\n\n                               Ami-X Net Support\n                               °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n   Most  Ami-X Net conferences don''t have file bases in them, to make sure\n   that  ConfScan  doesn''t  try to scan this conferences (it will cause an\n   error  and the program will abort), you must enter them in the ConfScan\n   info file that comes along with this program.\n\n   And  if you do have Ami-X net conferences with file bases, no problemo,\n   ConfScan will scan them (ofcourse).\n\n                                Scanning options\n                                °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n   ConfScan can scan a lot and in many ways... here they are:\n\n   ­ Scanning from a certain date\n   ­ Scanning from a number of days back\n   ­ Scanning from the day a user was last on\n   ­ Scanning in upload dirs or in all dirs\n   ­ Scanning in hold dirs (special access-level used)\n\n\n   Well,  if  this  doesn''t  convince  you to start using ConfScan, than I\n   don''t  know  what  will.  This door should enlarge the activity on your\n   board  ''cause  @{"users" link users} are losing less time on scanning and so your board\n   is  easier to reach...  I can go on like this, but you are smart enough\n   to see the advantages...\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Usage "Usage by users (that includes you) - /X DeSiGn - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n\n                         ----------( USAGE )-----------\n                                     °°°°°\n\n   Simplicity itself, you can use the program like this:\n\n   CS [option 1] [option 2]\n       ^          ^\n       |          |-------» A(ll)      Scan All dirs\n       |          `-------» U(pload)   Scan Upload dirs\n       |\n       |------------------» S(ince)    Sets  the  date to scan from to the\n       |                               date  the  user  was  last  on your\n       |                               system.\n       |------------------» MM/DD/YY   Sets the date to scan from, it must\n       |                               be in the /X format.\n       |------------------» -X         Sets  the  date  to  scan from to X\n       |                               days back.\n       |------------------» W          With this option the user can create\n       |                               his/her own configuration file.\n       `------------------» ?          Shows the information page.\n\n   If  you  do not use option 1, option 2 becomes option 1...  get it?  So\n   you can use the option 2 commands also as option 1 commands.\n\n   And if you do not specify any option at all, the default values will be\n   taken, which are:  option 1 = S and option 2 = U.\n\n   Okay, it''s example time! Here are some examples you can learn from:\n\n   CS                      ­ Scans for files since you were last on the\n                             board in the upload directory of conferences.\n   CS S U                  ­ Does exactly the same\n   CS U                    ­ Yep, also the same\n\n   CS -5                   ­ Scans for files that are 5 days old in the\n                             upload directory of conferences\n   CS -5 A                 ­ Scans for files that are 5 days old in all\n                             directories of conferences\n\n   CS 08-26-93 A           ­ Scans for files since the 26th of August 1993\n                             in all directories of conferences\n\n   CS H                    ­ Scans for files since you were last on in the\n                             hold directory of conferences.\n\n   CS W                    ­ Let''s you configure ConfScan...\n\n   CS ?                    ­ Show''s you the information page...\n\n   Looks  real easy, doesn''t it?  It is!  Just install it and you''ll never\n   want to miss it again!\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Future "You want more? You animal! - /X DeSiGn - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n\n                  ----------( FUTURE IMPROVEMENTS )----------\n                              °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n\n   Okay, a new version is on stack! It is being tested right now, and\n   it includes the following new options:\n   \n                         >> ANSI Colour Display <<\n                          >> CTRL-C Detecting <<\n                            >> File Flagging <<\n                             >> Downloading <<\n   \n                            >> & MUCH MORE! <<\n   \n   So just wait and sit tight, ''cause it will be a MAJOR UPDATE! So\n   watch out for version 2.0!\n\n   Anyway,  if  you  have  suggestions,  make  sure  to  drop me a line at\n   Channel-X or at one of the other MYSTiC boards (in Holland preferably,\n   that''s where  I  am most).  By the way, you don''t need to have a\n   suggestion to call  the MYSTiC boards, you''re welcome at any time, open\n   24 hours a day and at your service!\n\n   Let me know what you think and what YOU think needs improvement!\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node BugReports "BugReport (Doodlebug Invasion part III) - /X DeSiGn - Written by Guess Who?"\n\n                      ----------( BUG REPORTS )----------\n                                  °°°°°°°°°°°\n\n   Bug reports can be left at one of the MYSTiC /X DeSiGn Boards:\n\n                   .\n    _______     __/|__    _______________________.  /\______\n   _\  .. ¬\   /   ! ¬\  _\  ________.   .___.  ¬| /   .___/\n   \_  ||   \ /____.   \_\_____ ¬\___|   |___|   |/    |__Z___\n  /¬   ||  -\\    ¬!  -\\    ¬V -\\  | -!|   | -!|\    !¬  -// FuN RoOLeS !\n  \____!!_  _/\______  _/\_____  _/\ !___!   !___! \_____  _/  -^- -  - -^-\n   \___\_\_/\\/\____\_/\\/\___\_/\\/ !___!   !___!\/___/\_//\n+--------·\\/·------·\\/·-----·\\/·-------------------·\//·------------------+\n|LaST ouTposT    ^ 2 NdZ aMiGa Ehq! ^ SneS Whq ÷ /X-DeSiGn EhQ +31-72157682  |\n|D¿aBoLo         ^ 3 NdZ aMiGa Ghq! ^ -------- ÷ /X-DeSiGn WhQ +49-3ø6218787 |\n|TrAdE ¿n CeNtEr ^ 1 Nd'' aMiGa Ghq! ^ IbM! EhQ ÷ /X-DeSiGn GhQ +49-7ø826ø611 |\n|ChAnNeL-X       ^ 2 NdZ aMiGa DisT ^ -------- ÷ /X-DeSiGn DhQ +31-229ø62244 |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------·A×E^MsT·-+\n  \n                        Other ways to reach me:         \n\n                       /X-FIDO NET: 44:100/100.1\n                           NLA NET: 14:100/102.1\n                           BOS NET: 99:999/4.1\n                           AMY NET: 39:151/201.1\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Greetings "Greetinx Alien, I Want To Speak To Your Leader! - /X DeSiGn (no, really!)"\n\n                       ----------( GREETINGS )----------\n                                   °°°°°°°°°\n\n   So, you wanted to know if you were on the greetings-list eh?  Well, the\n   lucky winners are:\n\n\n   ByteAndi/MsT      Your include file works now, the problem was the old\n                     library (.o). So all is okay now.\n\n   Axe/MsT           ......\n   \n   Tycoon/MsT        Thanks for your help man!\n   \n   Empire/MsT        ISDN RoOlez!\n   \n   Pitagora          This will take care of it! Thanks for upload the dir-\n                     file so I could check it out. L8r...\n\n\n        ... and all my friends on the BosNet/Ami-X Fido mailing systems!\n\n                   .\n    _______     __/|__    _______________________.  /\______\n   _\  .. ¬\   /   ! ¬\  _\  ________.   .___.  ¬| /   .___/\n   \_  ||   \ /____.   \_\_____ ¬\___|   |___|   |/    |__Z___\n  /¬   ||  -\\    ¬!  -\\    ¬V -\\  | -!|   | -!|\    !¬  -// FuN RoOLeS !\n  \____!!_  _/\______  _/\_____  _/\ !___!   !___! \_____  _/  -^- -  - -^-\n   \___\_\_/\\/\____\_/\\/\___\_/\\/ !___!   !___!\/___/\_//\n+--------·\\/·------·\\/·-----·\\/·-------------------·\//·------------------+\n|DiGiTal CaNdY   ^ 3 NdZ aMiGa Whq! ^ -------- ÷ ------------- +1-5134713366 |\n|LaST ouTposT    ^ 2 NdZ aMiGa Ehq! ^ SneS Whq ÷ /X-DeSiGn EhQ +31-72157682  |\n|BoGuS ExCepT¿oN ^ 2 NdZ aMiGa UShq ^ -------- ÷ ------------- +1-2ø34378655 |\n|The RestaUrAnt  ^ 3 NdZ aMiGa UShq ^ -------- ÷ ------------- +1-6163637ø27 |\n|D¿aBoLo         ^ 3 NdZ aMiGa Ghq! ^ -------- ÷ /X-DeSiGn WhQ +49-3ø6218787 |\n|TrAdE ¿n CeNtEr ^ 1 Nd'' aMiGa Ghq! ^ IbM! EhQ ÷ /X-DeSiGn GhQ +49-7ø826ø611 |\n|TrAdE ¿n CeNtEr ^ 2 NdZ aMiGa iSDn ^ IbM! EhQ ÷ ------------- +49-7ø8292122ø|\n|CrY¿nG F¿eLdS   ^ 1 Nd'' aMiGa Ghq! ^ -------- ÷ ------------- +49-4ø6452525 |\n|THe Add¿cT¿oN   ^ 1 Nd'' aMiGa Ghq! ^ -------- ÷ ------------- +49-61ø231564 |\n|An¿mAlS         ^ 1 Nd'' aMiGa Chhq ^ -------- ÷ ------------- +41-53246782  |\n|MaMbA           ^ 1 Nd'' aMiGa Phq! ^ -------- ÷ ------------- +48-22367443  |\n|OuT oF SpAcE    ^ 1 Nd'' aMiGa Shq! ^ -------- ÷ ------------- +46-62o13141  |\n|ChAnNeL-X       ^ 2 NdZ aMiGa DisT ^ -------- ÷ /X-DeSiGn DhQ +31-229ø62244 |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------·A×E^MsT·-+\n\n                      ToTaLL MaDNeSS by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC!\n                (Excuse my corny jokes, but FuN RoOlez Ya KnOw!)\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Users "You don''t know what users are? And you''re a sysop?!?!"\n\n   Users: People who are constantly trying to fill up your precious\n          harddisk space with stuff hoping you will get to see that\n          most annoying requester "Volume BBS: is full" and come to\n          the conclusion you just missed the release of the year...\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Killraven "What are you looking for? My DNA structure?"\n\n   Ah, you want to know more about me, well.... okay, I''ll show you a \n   picture of me when I was reaaaaly young:\n\n                  ·\n           ·      ·\n         ·          ·       See the one with the real def hair? That''s\n            ·  · ·    ·     me,  and this picture was taken when I was\n          ·  · ^·     ·     still a reserve recrute at Spermazoid...\n               |     ·\n        ·   ·    ·· ·       (those were the hours... exciting as ever!)\n           ·  ·     ·\n               · · ·\n\n   Enough stupidity... get back to business...\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Ami-X "Ami-Express Information, dude!"\n\n                    Please support Ami-Express and register!\n                    °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n\n                           You can order your copy at\n\n                 LightSpeed Technology (USA)   +1-305-964-4263\n\n\n            Or check your local Ami-Express support board near you!\n\n                                    Thanks!\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Files "What? You need help with that too?!"\n\n   Hé!  Keep your fingers of you brother''s system!  Go play with Barbie or\n   Playmobil!  Don''t touch your brothers computer!\n\n   Go  away  or I''ll tell your brother when he''s back and oooohhh...  does\n   he  know  where  to find ya...  if you only knew what he did to some of\n   his @{"users" link users}...  boy o boy!\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node History "How did it end up like this - /X DeSiGn - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n\n                      ----------( HISTORY )---------\n                                  °°°°°°°\n\n   1.7   18-Sep-93   Bug-Fix: Dir-files still caused problems, is fixed!\n                     Bug-Fix: No more trouble when inserting an extra\n                              space after the conference numbers in the\n                              config menu.\n\n   1.6   11-Sep-93   Bug-Fix: Dir-files with lines longer than 150\n                     characters caused a guru :-(. The maximum is now set\n                     to 300 characters, that should be enough.\n\n   1.5   25-Aug-93   First public release\n\n   All  previous  information is either lost or not worth to be mentioned,\n   it''s  the usual stuff like "new option" and "fixed a bug".  Believe me,\n   you  don''t wanna know.  From now on the history file will be kept up to\n   date...\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Errors "What have you done wrong? - /X DeSiGn - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n\n                  ----------( POSSIBLE ERRORS )---------\n                              °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n\n   Since  nobody  is perfect, there is a slight chance an error may occur,\n   there are only a few possible errors, so here they are:\n\n   ­ "Couldn''t allocate memory! Too little memory?"\n\n     Do you have enough memory free to run ConfScan?  The program uses about\n     36Kb  of memory (largest block in once is 32Kb for copying files).  The\n     best  thing  you can do is reset and try again.  If it still fails, you\n     better  buy  a  memory  expansion...  if you have enough memory and you\n     still get this error, then please contact me.\n\n   ­ "Couldn''t open temporary file for output! Too little memory?"\n\n     ConfScan  uses a temporary file to store the files which will be showed\n     to  you  later,  this  temp  file  is in the T:  directory, do you have\n     enough  memory  left?   If your file-listings are really big, this file\n     can  be  become  quite large (if you have masses of new warez every day\n     (ofcourse  you  have  :-)).  Maybe the file is still present in T:  and\n     this  MIGHT  cause  the problem, check the T:  directory...  else reset\n     and try again.\n\n   ­ "Couldn''t open file: <name>"\n\n     For  some reason, ConfScan was not able to open the file <name>.  Maybe\n     it  was  in  use by another program?  Best thing to do is reset and try\n     again.   Another  possibility  is that you have not reserved some Ami-X\n     Net- mail area''s and ConfScan tries to open a dir file...\n\n   ­ "Couldn''t open icon.library!"\n\n     If  this  happens,  you better install the icon.libary, but this cannot\n     happen, ''cause /X 3.xx uses it also, so if the icon.library is missing,\n     Ami-X will not startup :-).\n\n   ­ "Error reading from input file during filecopy!"\n\n     It  seems that something went wrong while reading the input file during\n     a  file  copy.  File copies only occur while scanning and when you exit\n     the config menu.  Reset and try again.\n\n   ­ "Error writing to output file during filecopy!"\n\n     Something  went  wrong  while  writing to the output file during a file\n     copy.  This can only happen while scanning and when you exit the config\n     menu.  Reset and try again.\n\n   ­ "Couldn''t open your config file!"\n\n     For  some  reason ConfScan was not able to create your own config file!\n     This should always be possible, better reset and try again.\n\n   Well,  that''s  all  the  errors  ConfScan can create.  If you don''t get\n   ConfScan  working  on your system, just give me call and I''ll make sure\n   it will work!\n\n   KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC HangOut: +31-2290-62244 & +31-2290-62535 (14k4/16k8/USR)\n   °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n                Or call one of the MYSTiC /X DeSiGn Boards!\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Registration "Don''t worry, it costs nothing! - /X DeSiGn - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n\n                   ----------( REGISTRATION )----------\n                               °°°°°°°°°°°°\n\n                      DON''T WORRY, IT COSTS NOTHING!\n\n   Since  I don''t believe in shareware (I know myself :-)) this program is\n   free  to  use.   Spread it as much as you can and tell all your friends\n   about  it.  You may not SELL it to other people, if you catch you do it\n   I will burn your house down!\n\n   What I would like you to do is call @{"Channel-X" link Channel-X} and tell me you are using\n   it.   That  way I know how many people are using it (this encourages me\n   to keep updating ConfScan).\n\n   So I''ll be hearing from you!\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Channel-X "COMMERCIAL MODE <ON> - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n\n                                                 /\        /\\n      ² NØÐE $¥$TEM  ² µ$R Ð$  µPTØ ¹6.8K!  /  \      /  \\n   _____________________________________________\   \    /   /\n  /  ____________________________________________\   \  /   / $¥$Ø¶: T¥ÇØØN\n /  /   / /  / // ___  // / / // / / // ____// /  \   \/   /\n/  /   / /__/ // /__/ //  \/ //  \/ // /_   / /    \  /   /   ÇØ: K¿££®ÆVEN\n\  \  / ___  // ___  // /\  // /\  // __/  / /      \/   /\n \  \/ /  / // /  / // / / // / / // /___ / /___    /   /\    ÆM¿GÆ/ÇØN$Ø£E\n  \  \/__/_//_/__/_//_/_/_//_/_/_//_____//_____/_K!/   /  \\n   \______________________________________________/   /\   \ +³¹-²²9°-6²²44\n                                                 /   /  \   \+³¹-²²9°-6²5³5\n      HØME ØF ÆMI-X F¿ÐØ  MÆN¥ NETMÆ¿L ÆREÆS  \  /    \  /\n                                                  \/      \/\n\n\n@EndNode\n','\n',char(10)),'{"ACCESS":"020","LOCATION":"DOORS:ConfScan/ConfScan","PRIORITY":"0","STACK":"50000","TYPE":"XIM"}','auto-added',56897,7,0,NULL,NULL,'mst_cs17','scan',1780048619);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mst_cs22','MST-CS22.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MST-CS22.LHA','ConfScan','XIM','ConfScan',NULL,'KiLLraVeN','MST','\____\/____  | ____ _____ ____ \\___    \ /   \/  \_____ \/____ \/  \/   \/  |___/ /    ||   \_  /  \_  /  \_  \_   \_ |vol\_',replace(' _____  ______|\__________/\____ ________  \n \____\/____  | ____ _____ ____ \\___    \ \n  /   \/  \_____ \/____ \/  \/   \/  |___/ \n /    ||   \_  /  \_  /  \_  \_   \_ |vol\_\n+\____||____/______/______/___/____/______/+\n| ConfScan v2.2 - 1994 Update By KiLLraVeN |\n| January-bug fixed and new options added! |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'ConfScan.GUIDE',replace('@DATABASE "ConfScan.GUIDE"\n@REMARK .------------------------------------------------------------------.\n@REMARK | This document is written in AmigaGUIDE format, so please read it |\n@REMARK | with AmigaGUIDE or your favourite guide reader.... ciao now...   |\n@REMARK `------------------------------------------------------------------''\n@REMARK $VER: ConfScan v2.2.0\n@WIDTH 80\n@NODE MAIN "Guide to ConfScan v2.2 - /X DeSiGn - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n.----------.                  .--------..---------.\n|o  ____   | © & ® & TM & (c) |o  _____||o  ______| Anybody for a cool logo?\n|| |    |__|.-------..-------.|| |      || |______ .-------..-------..-------.\n|| |        |o  _   ||o  _   ||| |__    ||        ||o  ____||o  _   ||o  _   |\n|| |        || | |  ||| | |  |||    |   `------.  ||| |     || `-''  ||| | |  |\n|| |    .--.|| | |  ||| | |  ||| .--''          |  ||| |     ||  _   ||| | |  |\n|| |____|  ||| |_|  ||| | |  ||| |       ______|  ||| |____ || | |  ||| | |  |\n||         |||      ||| | |  ||| | v2.2 |         |||      ||| | |  ||| | |  |\n`----------''`-------''`--'' `--''`--'' °°°° `---------''`-------''`--'' `--''`--'' `--''\n                         © 1993-94 by KiLLRaVeN/MYSTiC\n\n                ... another fine MYSTiC /X DeSiGn production...\n\n                 @{"    Introduction    " link Introduction}  .-» @{" History of ConfScan " link History}\n                 @{"     Features!      " link     Features}  |   @{"     BugReports      " link BugReports}\n                 @{"    Requirements    " link Requirements}  |   @{" Possible error msgs " link Errors}\n                 @{"    Installation    " link Installation}  |   @{" Future improvements " link Future}\n                 @{"  Usage (by users)  " link        Usage}--''   @{"     Greetings       " link Greetings}\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Introduction "Introduction to ConfScan - /X DeSiGn - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n\n                      ----------( INTRODUCTION )----------\n                                  °°°°°°°°°°°°\n         __                                                         __\n         \/__________________________________________________ ______\/     \n        /\/    /         \/.  /   /  _____/    ____/____/    \/\    \/\\n   _ _!//_____/   /  /   //  /   / _ _   //   /\__/    /.  /___/\_____\\!_ _\n      |\\    /.  /__/   /___    /\/     /·   / / //   //  /   /\/     //|\n        \___//  /\_/   /\__/   /       /    / / /·   /   ·   / /______/\n           /___/ //___/ / /___/_______/____/ / /____/_______/ /A×E!\n           \___\/ \___\/  \___\_______\____\/  \____\_______\/\n\n\n   You  found  it!  This is the ultimate tool for scanning conferences for\n   new  files.  "Ha!" I hear you shout, "so what''s new about that, I got a\n   truckload  full  of that sh*t!" Ah well, I bet that NONE of those doors\n   offer the same possibilities and flexibility like this door does.\n\n   "That''s  what  they all say!" Sure, but did they please you?  Were they\n   right?   Or  did  you  still look for that one door that would make you\n   totally  happy  and  would  give  your users the most pleasant tool for\n   scanning files and downloading files?  Look no further.\n\n   With  this  tool  users  can scan for new files in ALL conferences they\n   have  access  to  with  one  single  command.   With one single command\n   knowing  what  is new on your board, with one single command knowing if\n   someone  left  you  a private file (yes, hold dirs are supported).  But\n   that''s  not  all,  a  special frontdoor gives your users the ability to\n   automatically jump to the next conference where they have files flagged\n   after downloading the files from the previous conference.\n\n   And  all  of this with lots of options users can turn off or on.  Those\n   options  include:   ANSI  colour  display,  Removal  of sentby''s, lines\n   between files, returns between files, new dates between days and more.\n\n   But  the  most revolutionary of all has yet to come.  Because with this\n   version  of  ConfScan  it  is possible to @{"TAG files" link Tagging} instead of flagging\n   them!  Yes, you heard it right, TAGging files!\n\n   And  again  this  is  not all, but I''ve been rambling enough, if I have\n   tickled  your  curiousity,  go check out the @{"features" link Features} and I am sure you\n   will be another happy user of ConfScan!\n\n                                                        @{"-KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC" link Killraven}\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Requirements "What DO you need? - /X DeSiGn - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n\n                      ----------( REQUIREMENTS )----------\n                                  °°°°°°°°°°°°\n   Okay, here are the requirements to use this door:\n\n   ­ @{"Ami-Express BBS version 3.x" link Ami-X} (sorry, no 2.xx support, upgrade!)\n   ­ @{"Users" link users}\n   ­ Files\n   ­ @{"CLEAN DIR FILES!" link CleanDir}\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node CleanDir "VERY IMPORTANT! READ THIS! - By KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n\n             ­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­\n               WARNING * WARNING * WARNING * WARNING * WARNING\n             ­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­\n\n   When  beta-testing  on some boards I found out that ConfScan might fail\n   in  recognizing  files  now  and  then  if  you do not have a clean dir\n   listing.   What  I  mean  with  that is, that if you use something like\n   DirStyler  or  any  other program that changes your dir listing itself,\n   ConfScan may not be able to correctly identify files, dates etc.\n\n   This  only  goes  for  dir  listings  with  something  IN  FRONT OF THE\n   DESCRIPTION!  So, for example, this would cause problems:\n\n PROGRAM.DMS  N   5635  12-06-92  Best Program you have ever seen! Get it!\n DL: 15 TIMES NOW DUDE!           [MISTRAL]--------[NODE 2]-------[1902CPS]\n\n                           But this one wouldn''t:\n\n PROGRAM.DMS  N   5635  12-06-92  Best Program you have ever seen! Get it!\n                                  [MISTRAL]--------[NODE 2]-------[1902CPS]\n\n   Why? Well, ConfScan sticks to these rules for recognizing a file:\n\n   1) Position 1 is NOT a space\n   2) Position 1 is NOT a return (empty line)\n   3) Position 1 is NOT an escape code\n   4) Positions 13, 23, 32 & 33 are spaces\n\n   You  see that I do reckon with some dir listing mutators, because it is\n   allowed to have something like\n\n   =============================== 27 Sept 1993 ============================\n\n   in  your  dir  listings.   But  the first example would cause a problem\n   cause it fits all rules!  So be careful!\n\n   NOTICE: If your dir files contain ANSI codes, chances are that\n   ~~~~~~~ ConfScan will fail. But now you can get rid of that other\n           door that creates the ANSI ''cause ConfScan does it for you\n           now!\n\n   As  a  result  of  an eventuel failing file recognition the TAG routine\n   will also fail ''cause it takes non-files as file and will allow user to\n   actually  tag  them.   But  if you still want to use ConfScan (and that\n   still  is  possible but the file tagging will not work correct) you can\n   turn  the  tagging  of with an option in the icon file (NO_TAGGING) but\n   for more info about that, go see the @{"installation" link Installation} part.\n\n   So to make sure ConfScan will work properly:\n   \n             ­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­\n             ¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!   USE CLEAN DIR FILES!   ¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!¡!\n             ­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­\n\n   By the way, Nukers are allowed! They cause no trouble whatsoever!\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Installation "How to get it working - /X DeSiGn - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n\n                      ----------( INSTALLATION )----------\n                                  °°°°°°°°°°°°\n   Okay,  this  can  take  some  time, so please read everything with your\n   greatest  attention, and I know how much you hate installing doors so I\n   will be as clear as I can so you can do it as quick as possible.\n\n   ConfScan  comes  in  two  versions:   000  and 020.  If you have a 020+\n   processor, just copy the 020 version over the 000 version and delete it\n   again.   I  suggest  you copy it to:  Doors:ConfScan/ but that is up to\n   you.  Just remember where you have put it.\n\n   ConfScan is able to act as 4 different programs! ConfScan performs as:\n   » `N''    - N S U like behavior, multiple confs supported with N S U A!\n   » `F''    - Complete dir-listings (just like the good old `F'')\n   » `CS''   - Does the same as `N'' but this time the usage is a little bit\n              different.  I  prefer to use CS above N S U ''cause CS can be\n              started  without any further arguments and it just starts to\n              do its job. Check out what you like...\n   » `D''    - It  acts  like  a frontdoor to the real download command, b4\n              the  real download door is started, it flags the right files\n              for the current conference and can jump (also after download)\n              to the next conference with flagged files.  The internal `D''\n              command is used for up & downloading. No worry.\n\n   You  don''t  need to stick to these names.  The `CS'' and `D'' part can be\n   given  ANY  name.   So if you want to give the download command another\n   name  than  `D'',  you  are free to do so (but it would ''cause confusion\n   under your users).\n\n   All programs need ofcourse an icon of their own, but you do not have to\n   create every icon one by one.  If you install one icon correct, you can\n   use it for `N'', `CS'' and `F''.  Only the `D'' icon differs from the rest.\n\n   I  suggest  you install the program as all 4 functions, but if you want\n   you can skip the `CS'' door ''cause it is built-in in `N'' also.\n\n   Okay, let''s install the `N'' icon, this one can be used for `CS'' and `F''\n   (or any other name).\n\n   Valid tooltypes are:\n\n   ACCESS=020                       ­ Change if ya like\n\n   LOCATION=DOORS:ConfScan/ConfScan ­ Why change?\n\n   MULTINODE=YES                    ­ Ofcourse it is...\n\n   PRIORITY=0                       ­ Change if ya like (not neccesary)\n\n   STACK=50000                      ­ Should be more than enough\n\n   TYPE=XIM                         ­ A real C door ofcoz ;)\n\n   ----( ConfScan Options )----     ­ Just a comment line, discard it.\n\n   HOLD_ACCESS=250                  ­ Change  if  ya  like. All @{"users" link users} with\n                                      this accesslevel or higher  are able\n                                      to scan the HOLD dirs.\n\n   CALLERSLOG                       ­ If you specify this keyword, every\n                                      time ConfScan is started, it will be\n                                      noted in the Callerslog.\n\n   NO_TAGGING                       ­ Turn this option ON if you have dir\n                                      files that are mutated by dir stylers\n                                      or any other program that fysically\n                                      changes the dir files. For more info\n                                      about WHEN you need to turn this option\n                                      on, read the @{"requirements" link CleanDir}!\n\n                                      When you activate the NO_TAGGING flag, \n                                      users can NOT tag files! So be carefull!\n\n   INTRO_FILE=<filename>            ­ It is possible to have ConfScan display\n                                      a file before the list of files. Here\n                                      you can put your BBS ID or whatever.\n                                      It can be any length and you can use\n                                      as much ANSI as you like. With the\n                                      filename, you need to feel in the\n                                      complete path.\n\n   As sysop you can determine what the default values of ConfScan are, you\n   can  decide wether the first time they start ConfScan the listings will\n   be  showed  in  colour, with lines in it and the newdate.  Or any other\n   combination.   If  you  specify  them,  then  that  will be the default\n   values.  If you put the values between braces `('' they will NOT be seen\n   as activated.\n\n   DEFAULT_ANSI                     ­ ANSI colours will be default\n                                      Filename  will be light-blue\n                                      FileCheck will be dark-blue\n                                      FileSize  will be yellow\n                                      FileDate  will be red\n                                      FileDesc  will be white\n\n   DEFAULT_LINES                    ­ Lines between files will be default\n\n   DEFAULT_RETURNS                  ­ Return between files will be default\n\n   DEFAULT_PAUSE                    ­ Pause between conferences (if the users\n                                      scans in all conferences) will be\n                                      default\n\n   DEFAULT_NEWDATE                  ­ In the listing any new date will be\n                                      shown (centered, with colour)\n\n   DEFAULT_SENTBY                   ­ Sentby''s will be showed default\n\n   ----( Excluded Confs Below )---- ­ Just a comment line, discard it.\n\n   CONF.x                           ­ Put  here  any conference (or confe-\n                                      rences)  that  you  don''t want to be\n                                      scanned  by  ConfScan.\n                                      NOTE: It is no longer need to fill in\n                                            your mail conferences here any\n                                            more. They are recognized now\n                                            by ConfScan. BUT! Filling them\n                                            in increases the speed of CS\n                                            a bit, so if you got the time,\n                                            fill them in anyway!\n\n   That  are  all  valid  tooltypes until now.  Fill it to your liking and\n   copy  it  to BBS:Commands/BBSCmd/...  rename and copy this icon for the\n   other functions as well (if you like).\n\n   All  user-config  files  will  be stored in the same directory that the\n   program is in.  The files look like:  ConfScan_UserData.usernumber.  So\n   your  own  config will be "ConfScan_UserData.1" and it will contain the\n   numbers  of  the conferences you DO NOT want to see and the differences\n   between the default-settings.  It can be read with a text-editor of you\n   like.  The file will have as a comment the name of that user.\n\n\n                     ----( DOWNLOAD COMMAND )----\n                           °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n\n   To  let  Ami-Express  communicate  with  ConfScan,  a  special DOWNLOAD\n   command  is  needed,  ''cause Ami-Express itself can only remember files\n   flagged   from   ONE   conference   and  not  (like  ConfScan)  several\n   conferences.\n\n   I recommend you to install it as `D'', but if you wish you can rename it\n   to  anything  you  want,  but  make  sure  you install it correct!  The\n   supplied  icon  will  have  the  right values if you copied the program\n   `ConfScan'' to your DOORS:ConfScan/ directory.  If not, you need to edit\n   the tooltypes:\n\n   ACCESS=020                       ­ Change if ya like\n\n   LOCATION=DOORS:ConfScan/ConfScan ­ Why change?\n\n   MULTINODE=YES                    ­ Ofcourse it is...\n\n   PRIORITY=0                       ­ Change if ya like (not neccesary)\n\n   STACK=50000                      ­ Should be more than enough\n\n   TYPE=XIM                         ­ Cool C Code (CCC)\n\n   ----( ConfScan Options )----     ­ Another comment line, discard\n\n   DOWNLOAD_COMMAND                 ­ This will inform ConfScan that this\n                                      is the DOWNLOAD command, so if you\n                                      want to rename `D'' to something\n                                      else, put this value in the icon and\n                                      it will work.\n\n   Okay, that ends the installation. A final remark:\n   \n   ­ Do not change your default settings once you have installed and users\n   have been using the door.  That way you will mix up the settings of the\n   users,  ''cause  in  the  config file only the points of difference have\n   been saved so when you first had LINES as a default but the user didn''t\n   want  it  and  you turned the default off again, the user would get the\n   lines again...  if you don''t understand it, don''t worry.  Just remember\n   to NOT change them.\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Features "Features of ConfScan - /X DeSiGn - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n\n                        ----------( FEATURES )----------\n                                    °°°°°°°°\n\n   This  is  the  part  where  I need you to convince how badly you are in\n   need for this door :) So relax and let me talk you into it, okay?\n\n                                  Easy To Use\n                                  °°°°°°°°°°°\n   ConfScan  is  very  flexible in use and even the dumbest user should be\n   able  to  use  it.   A  help  page is included in the program which can\n   easily be accessed with `CS ?'' or `N ?'', just like in AmigaDOS.\n\n                                 Fast Searching\n                                 °°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n   Scanning  the  directories  goes supersonic thanks to C programming and\n   searching in RAM instead of harddisk.\n\n                              Good Looking Layout\n                              °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n   He?  What can I say?  It just looks good and is informative and uses no\n   high  ansi  (so even for you, the sysop, it looks good :-)).  In future\n   releases  it  may  be  possible to layout your own directory, but until\n   then you''re stuck with mine.\n\n                              Security Guaranteed\n                              °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n   There  is  a DOUBLE security in ConfScan.  First of all, a user will be\n   checked  for his conference access, and second, you can reserve certain\n   conferences  of  being  scanned!   So  no  worry  about that, all works\n   relatively  so  @{"users" link users} will not see conferences they are not supposed to\n   see.\n\n                               User Configurable\n                               °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n   Every  user  can  setup his own private config file.  This file will be\n   located  in the same directory as the ConfScan program is in.  The user\n   is able to config which conferences he doesn''t want to see and which he\n   does  want  to  see. Also many other options like ''lines between files''\n   can be turned on/off.  Again,  the is very easy to use (select multiple\n   conferences to turn on/off) and looks good.\n\n                              Multi-Node supported\n                              °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n   Not  one  important file will be locked while ConfScan does its job, so\n   that  means  no  waiting on the other node or /X complaining ''cause the\n   conference-dir is locked.\n\n                               Ami-X Net Support\n                               °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n   From  this version on, ConfScan will detect wether a conference has got\n   a  file  base  or not.  If the user wants to scan a conference that has\n   got  not  file base a message will appear pointing out that the current\n   file base has got no file base.  This will NOT happen if the user scans\n   ALL  conferences  (either  with  `N S U A'' or `CS''), then ConfScan will\n   simply skip that conference.\n\n   And  if you do have Ami-X net conferences with file bases, no problemo,\n   ConfScan will scan them (ofcourse).\n\n                                Scanning options\n                                °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n   ConfScan can scan a lot and in many ways... here they are:\n\n   ­ Scanning from a certain date\n   ­ Scanning from a number of days back\n   ­ Scanning from the day a user was last on\n   ­ Scanning in current conference or all conferences\n   ­ Scanning in upload dirs or in all dirs\n   ­ Scanning in hold dirs (special access-level used)\n\n                                  Flagging\n                                  °°°°°°°°\n   From version 2.0 it is possible to flag files from all conferences.  It\n   doesn''t  matter  in  which conference an user is, he can flag the files\n   and  download  them later without any problems (if you install ConfScan\n   as a `D'' door as well ofcoz).\n\n                                   Tagging\n                                   °°°°°°°\n   Also  from  version  2.0  files can be TAGGED instead of being flagged.\n   This  idea  is stolen from some pc terminal programs.  The user can now\n   walk  over  the files with a ''cursor'' in the form of a coloured bar (or\n   `<''  if in non- colourmode).  With the numeric keyboard the user can go\n   up  a  file,  down  a file, select the file or deselect the file.  Real\n   cool,  I  think.   I hope that more doors will use this method, it''s so\n   easy in use.\n\n                                 Downloading\n                                 °°°°°°°°°°°\n   ConfScan  is  even  able  to  perform  as a download front-door.  This,\n   ofcoz,  is  needed  to check wether an user had selected files from the\n   current  conference  he/she  is in.  But that''s not all, if the program\n   detects  flagged  files  but not in the current conference, the program\n   will  ask  the user is he/she wants to auto-jump to the next conference\n   with  flagged  files!  This also happens when an user has files flagged\n   other  than  in  the  current  dir  and  the program will join the next\n   conference AFTER downloading the files of the current conference.\n\n   Well,  if  this  doesn''t  convince  you to start using ConfScan, than I\n   don''t  know  what  will.  This door should enlarge the activity on your\n   board  ''cause  @{"users" link users} are losing less time on scanning and so your board\n   is  easier to reach...  I can go on like this, but you are smart enough\n   to see the advantages...\n\n                                  2.0+ Features\n                                  °°°°°°°°°°°°°\n\n   » @{"`N S U''" link NSU} like behavior possible, but still can be used as @{"`CS''" link CS}\n\n   » @{"`F''" link F} function also included in the program\n\n   » Can also act as frontdoor for the @{"DOWNLOAD COMMAND" link download} so that files\n     flagged from Conference 1 can also be downloaded when the download\n     command is given in Conference 5.\n\n   » Flagging of files is now possible\n     \n   » @{"Tagging of files" link Tagging} is now possible!\n\n   » @{"ANSI display" link AnsiDisplay} of files is possible\n\n   » Lines between files are possible\n   \n   » Returns between files are possible\n   \n   » Pausing between conferences is now optional\n   \n   » Showing SentBy''s is also optional\n   \n   » Clear displays of new date is now possible\n   \n   » CTRL-C is detected, so it is possible to break the program.\n   \n   » Intelligent @{"`More'' option" link More}\n\n   » Lots of help for the users to get to know ConfScan (about 8K of the\n     program is dox-only).\n\n   » @{"BNF support" link BNF}\n   \n   » Improved "No Carrier" checking!\n\n   » Automatic recognition of conferences with no file base in them.\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Usage "Usage by users (that includes you) - /X DeSiGn - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n\n                         ----------( USAGE )-----------\n                                     °°°°°\n\n   Although this program is very easy to use, it has lots of options and to\n   get it working at its best, you better check out all the possibilities:\n \n   + Scanning in ONE/ALL conferences   (Conferences Can Be Turned On/Off)\n   + Scanning in ALL/UPLOAD dirs       (Upload Dir Is Default)\n \n   + Scanning from a given date        (i.e. 09-25-93)\n   + Scanning from a # of days back    (i.e. -10 = 10 Days Back)\n   + Scanning from last on system      (N S U Like, Also Default Value)\n \n   + File Flagging (also in ALL mode)  (Normal Way)\n   + File Tagging  (also in ALL mode)  (''New'' Method Done By KLR/MST)\n \n   + ANSI Colourful display of files   (User Configurable)\n   + Lines between files               (User Configurable)\n   + Return between files              (User Configurable)\n   + Show sentby''s                     (User Configurable)\n   + Show New Dates in listing         (User Configurable)\n   + Pause between conf. (in ALL mode) (User configurable)\n \n   + Nonstop display of CURRENT conf.  (One Of The `More'' Options)\n   + Nonstop display of ALL conf.      (One Of The `More'' Options)\n   + Clear screen and continue listing (One Of The `More'' Options)\n \n   + CTRL-C Detecting                  (Anytime During Execution)\n   + Your own private config           (With The `W'' Option)\n \n                     ----( Options in the CONFIG MENU )----\n \n   + Turn conferences on/off that will be scanned when you want to scan\n     all conferences for new files. Files with a `*'' in front of their\n     name will be scanned. Turning on/off goes by entering the number\n     or character in front. You can enter more then one characters/#''s\n     at a time.\n \n   + Turn ANSI display          on/off  + Turn Pause between conf. on/off\n   + Turn LINES between files   on/off  + Turn `NewDate'' display   on/off\n   + Turn RETURNS between files on/off  + Turn `SentBy'' display    on/off\n\n\n   Instructions for the `CS'' command:\n   °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n   ConfScan works like this: ConfScan [opt1] [opt2]\n                                       ^     ^\n                                       |     |\n   S - Since last on (default)---------+     +-(default)- Show UPLOAD dirs - U\n   DATE - Show from date --------------+     `-------------- Show ALL dirs - A\n   -X - Show from x days back ---------+  If you skip opt1 but fill in opt2,\n   W - CONFIG MENU --------------------''  opt1 is loaded with default value.\n \n   Examples: ConfScan -10............Shows files from UL dir from 10 days back\n             ConfScan S A............Shows files from ALL dir from last on BBS\n    In ALL   ConfScan A...............................The same as ConfScan S A\n    conf''s   ConfScan ...............Shows files from UL dirs from last on BBS\n             ConfScan W................GO TO CONFIG MENU & ADJUST PREFERENCES!\n \n\n   Instructions for the `N'' command:\n   °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n   ConfScan works like this: N [opt1] [opt2] [opt3]\n                                ^      ^      ^\n                                |      |      |\n   S - Since last on -----------+      |      `------ Show ALL conferences - A\n   DATE - Since date -----------+      +-------(default)- Show UPLOAD dirs - U\n   -X - Since x days back ------+      `-------------------- Show ALL dirs - A\n   W - CONFIG MENU -------------''\n \n   Examples: N S U...........................Shows the new files since last on\n             N -10....................Shows the files from 10 days back and up\n             N 09-25-93...................Shows the files from 09-25-93 and up\n \n             N S U A..........Shows the new files since last on from ALL conf.\n             N -10 U A........Shows the files from 10 days back from ALL conf.\n             N S A A...Shows the files since last on in ALL dirs and ALL conf.\n             N 09-20-93 A A....Shows the files from 09-20-93 in ALL dirs/conf.\n \n             N W..................................GETS YOU IN THE CONFIG MENU!\n                 This is where you can deselect conferences from being scanned\n                                     and turn on/off some options of ConfScan.\n\n   Instructions for the `F'' command:\n   °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n   ConfScan works like this: F [option]\n                                ^\n                                |    Important:\n    X - Shows file listing X ---+    If you enter an incorrent number or\n    A - Shows all dirs ---------+    you do not fill in any number, you\n    U - Shows the upload dirs --+    will get a menu first.\n    W - Config menu ------------''\n  \n\n   With  `<progname> ?'' the user can view these some docs in colour.  The\n   program  will  detect  with  which  command  it  is called and show the\n   correct usage information, don''t worry ;)\n\n   SEE ALSO: @{"More options" link More}\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Future "You want more? You animal! - /X DeSiGn - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n\n                  ----------( FUTURE IMPROVEMENTS )----------\n                              °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n\n   Here  are  some  ideas  for  future  version I have, I''m thinking about\n   including them but I don''t want to overload the program, so let me know\n   what you think!\n\n   ­ Sysop can setup the colours ConfScan will use to show the files\n     and new date etcetera.\n\n   ­ Sysop can FORCE users to have an option turned ON or OFF. For\n     instance, no LINES between files. Or always ANSI display on.\n\n   ­ Subject sensitive help (a la Amiga Guide)\n\n   ­ Individual messages shown to user(s) when starting a download\n\n   What I want to implement for sure is:\n   \n   ­ Sysop can scan for files that have been nuked (or special access)\n\n   Anyway,  if  you  have  suggestions,  make  sure  to  drop me a line at\n   Channel-X or at one of the other MYSTiC boards (in Holland preferably,\n   that''s where  I  am most).  By the way, you don''t need to have a\n   suggestion to call  the MYSTiC boards, you''re welcome at any time, open\n   24 hours a day and at your service!\n\n   Let me know what you think and what YOU think needs improvement!\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node BugReports "BugReport (Doodlebug Invasion part III) - /X DeSiGn - Written by Guess Who?"\n\n                      ----------( BUG REPORTS )----------\n                                  °°°°°°°°°°°\n\n   If  you  think  you  have  found  a  bug, please fill in the bug report\n   document and send it to one of these boards, Channel-X preferred!\n\n                   .\n    _______     __/|__    _______________________.  /\______\n   _\  .. ¬\   /   ! ¬\  _\  ________.   .___.  ¬| /   .___/\n   \_  ||   \ /____.   \_\_____ ¬\___|   |___|   |/    |__Z___\n  /¬   ||  -\\    ¬!  -\\    ¬V -\\  | -!|   | -!|\    !¬  -// FuN RoOLeS !\n  \____!!_  _/\______  _/\_____  _/\ !___!   !___! \_____  _/  -^- -  - -^-\n   \___\_\_/\\/\____\_/\\/\___\_/\\/ !___!   !___!\/___/\_//\n+--------·\\/·------·\\/·-----·\\/·-------------------·\//·------------------+\n|LaST ouTposT    ^ 2 NdZ aMiGa Ehq! ^ SneS Whq ÷ /X-DeSiGn EhQ +31-72157682  |\n|D¿aBoLo         ^ 3 NdZ aMiGa Ghq! ^ -------- ÷ /X-DeSiGn WhQ +49-3ø6218787 |\n|TrAdE ¿n CeNtEr ^ 1 Nd'' aMiGa Ghq! ^ IbM! EhQ ÷ /X-DeSiGn GhQ +49-7ø826ø611 |\n|ChAnNeL-X       ^ 2 NdZ aMiGa DisT ^ -------- ÷ /X-DeSiGn DhQ +31-229ø62244 |\n+------------------------------------------------------------------·A×E^MsT·-+\n  \n                        Other ways to reach me:         \n\n                       /X-FIDO NET: 44:100/100.1\n                           NLA NET: 14:100/102.1\n                           BOS NET: 99:999/4.1\n                           AMY NET: 39:151/201.1\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Greetings "Greetinx Alien, I Want To Speak To Your Leader! - /X DeSiGn (no, really!)"\n\n                       ----------( GREETINGS )----------\n                                   °°°°°°°°°\n\n   ­ ByteAndi/MST       Cool door mate, FILE_ID finally made it on\n                        the Amiga! Let''s keep those fine /X prods\n                        coming...\n\n   ­ Remo/MST           Thanks for debugging my coming project...\n\n   ­ Pharaoh/SR         Nice chat man... you got that new modem yet?\n\n   ­ Muad''Dib/5D        Lamer, cry baby! Here''s the fix, you bono...\n\n   ­ Lightning/5D       When are you gonna do some cool ANSIs?\n\n   ­ Tycoon/MST         Soon the two CDROMS will be on-line, coool!\n\n   ­ CBA/TRC            Wat ben je toch lame he?\n\n   ­ Domino/TRSi        I still have got your videotape man, when are\n                        you gonna get it?\n\n   ­ Flame/TRSi         Sorry dude, we sold the Bacardi to a pub ;)\n\n   ­ Sababba            Bliep, tuuuut...\n\n              and to all the guyz I met at the Party III!   \n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Users "You don''t know what users are? And you''re a sysop?!?!"\n\n   Users: People who are constantly trying to fill up your precious\n          harddisk space with stuff hoping you will get to see that\n          most annoying requester "Volume BBS: is full" and come to\n          the conclusion you just missed the release of the year...\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Killraven "What are you looking for? My DNA structure?"\n\n\n\n\n               < EXTREMELY STUPID JOKE REMOVED   -ED. >\n\n\n\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Ami-X "Ami-Express Information, dude!"\n\n                    Please support Ami-Express and register!\n                    °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n\n                           You can order your copy at\n\n                 LightSpeed Technology (USA)   +1-305-964-4263\n\n\n            Or check your local Ami-Express support board near you!\n\n                                    Thanks!\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Files "What? You need help with that too?!"\n\n   Hé!  Keep your fingers of you brother''s system!  Go play with Barbie or\n   Playmobil!  Don''t touch your brothers computer!\n\n   Go  away  or I''ll tell your brother when he''s back and oooohhh...  does\n   he  know  where  to find ya...  if you only knew what he did to some of\n   his @{"users" link users}...  boy o boy!\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node History "How did it end up like this - /X DeSiGn - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n\n                      ----------( HISTORY )---------\n                                  °°°°°°°\n\n   2.2.01   01-Jan-93 Fixed     : ''January'' bug fix! Stupid bug! :(\n                                  *Reported by Muad''Dib/5D & Tycoon/MST*\n                      Fixed     : -x days bug fixed. Now works 100%!\n                                  *Reported by Tycoon/MST*\n                      New/Fixed : ''f h'' is possible now\n                                  *Reported by Muad''Dib/5D*\n\n   2.1.02   26-Oct-93  New      : New option, `T'' will show the uploaded\n                                  files of [T]oday. It can be used instead\n                                  of `S'' or a date. Example: N T U, CS T.\n                                  *Requested by: sHARON/SCooPeX*\n                       Fixed    : Better BossNuke support, taglines of\n                                  BossNuke (`...<BoSSNuKe'') are now\n                                  displayed with a red background and yel-\n                                  low characters.\n\n\n   2.1.01   23-Oct-93  New      : File-counter, when you flag a file you\n                                  will see the actual number of files an\n                                  user has flagged sofar. If a user TAGS\n                                  his files, the number of files will be\n                                  shown at the bottom-right.\n                                  *Requested by: EMPiRE*\n                       Fixed    : File tagging improved a little by allo-\n                                  cating a little bit more memory for it.\n\n\n   2.0.31   10-Oct-93  OFFICIAL RELEASE OF VERSION 2.0!\n                       Fixed    : Correct recognition of ''sent-by'' lines.\n\n   2.0.27   08-Oct-93  Fixed    : Config menu also recognizes conferences\n                                  without a file-base. They will not be\n                                  shown in the menu.\n\n   2.0.26   08-Oct-93  New/Fixed: Auto-recognition of mail conferences or\n                                   other conferences without a file-base,\n                                   the option in the icon to exclude certain\n                                   conferences from being scanned will stay\n                                   active.\n                                  `F'' command bug fixed (conferences without\n                                   file-base could cause problems.\n\n   2.0.23   07-Oct-93  New/Fixed: Nuker support added\n                                  Improved downloading command\n                                  F command included\n                                  Better help files\n                                  Changed file display a bit for tagging\n                                  Added BNF support ;)\n                                  Version information ($VER) improved\n                                  Better "NO CARRIER" protection\n                                  Who information for /X added (I forgot!)\n\n   2.0.01 - 2.0.22     Beta-releases and all sorts of bug-fixing. See above.\n\n   2.0.00  20-Sep-93   MAJOR UPDATE! First beta-release!\n                       New options: Downloading included in program\n                                    N S U like behavior implemented\n                                    File flagging implemented\n                                    File tagging implemented\n                                    ANSI colour display\n                                    Lines between files possible\n                                    Returns between files possible\n                                    NewDates can be shown\n                                    Sentby''s can be filtered out\n                                    Special remarks in dir-listing are\n                                            shown high-lighted!\n                                    Clear Screen & Continue implemented\n                                    Skip conference implemented\n                                    Nonstop display this conference\n                                    Nonstop display all conferences\n                                    Bigger & Better config menu\n                                    Bigger & Better info for users\n                                    Download command can show all flagged\n                                        files from all conferences\n                                    AutoJump to next conference where user\n                                        has flagged files (also after DL)\n                                    Pause between conferences is now optional\n                                    CTRL-C is detected, program can be stopped\n\n   1.7     18-Sep-93   Bug-Fix: Dir-files still caused problems, is fixed!\n                       Bug-Fix: No more trouble when inserting an extra\n                                space after the conference numbers in the\n                                config menu.\n\n   1.6     11-Sep-93   Bug-Fix: Dir-files with lines longer than 150\n                       characters caused a guru :-(. The maximum is now set\n                       to 300 characters, that should be enough.\n\n   1.5     25-Aug-93   First public release\n\n   All  previous  information is either lost or not worth to be mentioned,\n   it''s  the usual stuff like "new option" and "fixed a bug".  Believe me,\n   you  don''t wanna know.  From now on the history file will be kept up to\n   date...\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Errors "What have you done wrong? - /X DeSiGn - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n\n                  ----------( POSSIBLE ERRORS )---------\n                              °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n\n   Since  nobody  is perfect, there is a slight chance an error may occur,\n   there are only a few possible errors, so here they are:\n\n   ­ "Couldn''t allocate memory! Too little memory?"\n\n     Do you have enough memory free to run ConfScan?  The program uses about\n     36Kb  of memory (largest block in once is 32Kb for copying files).  The\n     best  thing  you can do is reset and try again.  If it still fails, you\n     better  buy  a  memory  expansion...  if you have enough memory and you\n     still get this error, then please contact me.\n\n   ­ "Couldn''t open temporary file for output! Too little memory?"\n\n     ConfScan  uses a temporary file to store the files which will be showed\n     to  you  later,  this  temp  file  is in the T:  directory, do you have\n     enough  memory  left?   If your file-listings are really big, this file\n     can  be  become  quite large (if you have masses of new warez every day\n     (ofcourse  you  have  :-)).  Maybe the file is still present in T:  and\n     this  MIGHT  cause  the problem, check the T:  directory...  else reset\n     and try again.\n\n   ­ "Couldn''t open file: <name>"\n\n     For  some reason, ConfScan was not able to open the file <name>.  Maybe\n     it  was  in  use by another program?  Best thing to do is reset and try\n     again.   Another  possibility  is that you have not reserved some Ami-X\n     Net- mail area''s and ConfScan tries to open a dir file...\n\n   ­ "Couldn''t open icon.library!"\n\n     If  this  happens,  you better install the icon.libary, but this cannot\n     happen, ''cause /X 3.xx uses it also, so if the icon.library is missing,\n     Ami-X will not startup :-).\n\n   ­ "Error reading from input file during filecopy!"\n\n     It  seems that something went wrong while reading the input file during\n     a  file  copy.  File copies only occur while scanning and when you exit\n     the config menu.  Reset and try again.\n\n   ­ "Error writing to output file during filecopy!"\n\n     Something  went  wrong  while  writing to the output file during a file\n     copy.  This can only happen while scanning and when you exit the config\n     menu.  Reset and try again.\n\n   ­ "Couldn''t open your config file!"\n\n     For  some  reason ConfScan was not able to create your own config file!\n     This should always be possible, better reset and try again.\n\n   Well,  that''s  all  the  errors  ConfScan can create.  If you don''t get\n   ConfScan  working  on your system, just give me call and I''ll make sure\n   it will work!\n\n   KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC HangOut: +31-2290-62244 & +31-2290-62535 (14k4/16k8/USR)\n   °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n                Or call one of the MYSTiC /X DeSiGn Boards!\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Channel-X "COMMERCIAL MODE <ON> - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\n\n                                                 /\        /\\n      ² NØÐE $¥$TEM  ² µ$R Ð$  µPTØ ¹6.8K!  /  \      /  \\n   _____________________________________________\   \    /   /\n  /  ____________________________________________\   \  /   / $¥$Ø¶: T¥ÇØØN\n /  /   / /  / // ___  // / / // / / // ____// /  \   \/   /\n/  /   / /__/ // /__/ //  \/ //  \/ // /_   / /    \  /   /   ÇØ: K¿££®ÆVEN\n\  \  / ___  // ___  // /\  // /\  // __/  / /      \/   /\n \  \/ /  / // /  / // / / // / / // /___ / /___    /   /\    ÆM¿GÆ/ÇØN$Ø£E\n  \  \/__/_//_/__/_//_/_/_//_/_/_//_____//_____/_K!/   /  \\n   \______________________________________________/   /\   \ +³¹-²²9°-6²²44\n                                                 /   /  \   \+³¹-²²9°-6²5³5\n      HØME ØF ÆMI-X F¿ÐØ  MÆN¥ NETMÆ¿L ÆREÆS  \  /    \  /\n                                                  \/      \/\n\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Download "Download FrontDoor - By KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n\n                    ----( Download FrontDoor )----\n                          °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n\n   From  this  version  on  it  is  possible  to  flag and tag files, this\n   ofcourse  asks  for  a  special door that notifies the download command\n   which  files  need to be downloaded ''cause Ami-X can only download from\n   one conference at a time.\n\n   This  is  where ConfScan comes in again.  It searches for flagged files\n   in the current conference and flags them for the user.  Any files given\n   after  the  `D''  command  will be flagged also.  If there are any other\n   files flagged in other conferences the user can choose to view them and\n   the  files  will  be shown with their name and in which conference they\n   are.\n\n   Another  function  of  the  door  is,  that  it  can  jump  to the next\n   conference  where  files  are  flagged.  This can be done at any point,\n   meaning  that  it will jump to the next conference AFTER files from the\n   current  conference  are  downloaded  or  straight away if there are no\n   files flagged in the current conference.\n\n   Unfortunately  this can also ''cause some problems for users and perhaps\n   you,  the  sysop.   If  an  user chooses to jump to the next conference\n   after  downloading but then decides to say ''Goodbye after download'' the\n   user  will  not  be  thrown off the BBS after downloading!  Instead the\n   user  will  be  joined  to  the  next  conference!   A warning has been\n   implemented  in  the  program  so  the  users  will be notified of this\n   ''problem'' beyond my control.\n\n   If  you  do  not  wish to use my frontdoor as a replacement for the `D''\n   command  then you can always install it under an under name.  Just make\n   sure  that  in  the  associated  icon  the tooltype DOWNLOAD_COMMAND is\n   given.\n\n   But  why  would  you  want  to  do  so,  ''cause if an user has not used\n   ConfScan  before  downloading,  he  (or  she) will never now there is a\n   frontdoor.   So  users  will not know it is there unless they have used\n   ConfScan one way or the other (with `CS'' or `F'' or `N'').\n\n   A brief overview:\n\n     » After downloading files from a certain conference, the user can\n       choose to automatically jump to the next conference where files\n       are flagged (ofcoz only when there are other files).\n\n     » The download command can show all files that are flagged and with\n       the number of the conference where they are located.\n\n     » The download command can have ANY name, `D'' is recommended, but\n       any name is accepted (read the installation part for more info).\n\n     » Users who do not use the CS door, and you (the sysop) decide not to\n       install it as ''N S U'', will never notice that the frontdoor is there.\n\n   I you have any wishes concerning this part, contact me at Channel-X.\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node Tagging "Tagging, the new way of flagging! - © KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n\n                         ----( Tagging of Files )----\n                               °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n\n   For  the  first  time  in Ami-Express history it is now possible to TAG\n   files instead of FLAGging them.  What does that mean?  The method ain''t\n   new to PC users, but it is to Amiga dedicated users ;-)\n\n   The  idea  comes from some PC terminal programs (and not BBS programs!)\n   that  allow  their  users to let them ''walk'' over the files that are on\n   the screen and with one simple touch of the keyboard the file is marked\n   as  ''flagged''  (or  tagged in this case).  I have implemented this cool\n   method in my door!\n\n   If  the  user  wishes  to  TAG his files a small bar will appear on the\n   first  filename  that  is  on the screen after the last ''more'' shown on\n   screen.   With  the cursor keys on the numeric keypad the user can move\n   up  and  down over the filenames.  With the `0'' the user can select and\n   deselect  a  file.   A selected file can be recognized at the `*'' being\n   after the filename.\n\n   Flagging  and tagging can be used through each other, it doesn''t matter\n   if  you  flag first and then tag, it will work.  You might wonder if it\n   still works when the users has no colours on screen (no ANSI).  Yes, it\n   works, besides the bar there will also be a ''<'' sign after the filename\n   to point out the current filename.\n\n   This method works ofcourse with all ConfScan imitations (N, F and CS).\n\n   If  you  also are an /X Coder and you want to know more about how I did\n   it, just contact me at Channel-X and I will help you further.\n\n             ­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­\n              ATTENTION! ATTENTION! ATTENTION! ATTENTION!\n             ­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­\n\n   Before  you  all  start screaming and yellin'' that there is a bug in my\n   program,  you  can  tag  files that are displayed since the last ''more''\n   line  (or from the beginning if there was no ''more'').  This is done for\n   programmer''s  simplicity  ;) Maybe in the future it will be possible to\n   tag  all  files that are on screen, but that is more difficult than you\n   might think (multiple conferences on one screen and so forth).\n\n   It''s just that you know... I am working on it though.\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node NSU "N S U like behavior of ConfScan - By KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n\n                          ----( N S U ConfScan )----\n                                °°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n\n   ConfScan can now be used as a total replacement of the `N'' command.  It\n   functions  100% like it and more!  With this command users can scan for\n   new  files  in  the current conference but also in ALL conferences with\n   one simple command.\n\n   Here is a snapshot from the help-file in ConfScan itself:\n\n                       --( snip.. snip.. snip... )--\n\n   ConfScan works like this: N [opt1] [opt2] [opt3]\n                                ^      ^      ^\n                                |      |      |\n   S - Since last on -----------+      |      `------ Show ALL conferences - A\n   DATE - Since date -----------+      +-------(default)- Show UPLOAD dirs - U\n   -X - Since x days back ------+      `-------------------- Show ALL dirs - A\n   W - CONFIG MENU -------------''\n \n   Examples: N S U...........................Shows the new files since last on\n             N -10....................Shows the files from 10 days back and up\n             N 09-25-93...................Shows the files from 09-25-93 and up\n \n             N S U A..........Shows the new files since last on from ALL conf.\n             N -10 U A........Shows the files from 10 days back from ALL conf.\n             N S A A...Shows the files since last on in ALL dirs and ALL conf.\n             N 09-20-93 A A....Shows the files from 09-20-93 in ALL dirs/conf.\n \n             N W..................................GETS YOU IN THE CONFIG MENU!\n\n                       --( snip.. snip.. snip... )--\n\n   It''s  all rather logic, everything that you were used to do with `N'' is\n   possible but now you can do more.  A third option has been included for\n   activating the @{"ALL mode" link AllMode}.\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node CS "The original mode - By KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n\n                           ----( CS Mode... )----\n                                 °°°°°°°°°°\n\n   This  is  the  original program mode like it was before v2.0.  It still\n   works  that  way  but  now  has some fancy nancy stuff attached such as\n   colour display, new dates etc.  etc.\n\n   A snapshot from the on-line help in ConfScan:\n\n                       --( snip.. snip.. snip... )--\n\n   ConfScan works like this: ConfScan [opt1] [opt2]\n                                       ^     ^\n                                       |     |\n   S - Since last on (default)---------+     +-(default)- Show UPLOAD dirs - U\n   DATE - Show from date --------------+     `-------------- Show ALL dirs - A\n   -X - Show from x days back ---------+  If you skip opt1 but fill in opt2,\n   W - CONFIG MENU --------------------''  opt1 is loaded with default value.\n \n   Examples: ConfScan -10............Shows files from UL dir from 10 days back\n             ConfScan S A............Shows files from ALL dir from last on BBS\n    In ALL   ConfScan A...............................The same as ConfScan S A\n    conf''s   ConfScan ...............Shows files from UL dirs from last on BBS\n             ConfScan W................GO TO CONFIG MENU & ADJUST PREFERENCES!\n\n                       --( snip.. snip.. snip... )--\n\n   See,  the  basic works.  On the place of `ConfScan'' you need to fill in\n   the name you gave it on your system (`CS'' I hope).\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node F "F-Imitation by ConfScan - By KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n\n                        ----( The F in ConFscan )----\n                              °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n\n   If  ConfScan  can  act  like  `N'',  then it is only logical it can also\n   function as `F'', well it can and it goes a little something like this:\n\n                       --( snip.. snip.. snip... )--\n\n   ConfScan works like this: F [option]\n                               ^\n                               |    Important:\n   X - Shows file listing X ---+    If you enter an incorrent number or\n   A - Shows all dirs ---------+    you do not fill in any number, you\n   U - Shows the upload dirs --+    will get a menu first.\n   W - Config menu ------------''\n\n                       --( snip.. snip.. snip... )--\n\n   Just like the good old `F''...  the same file will be shown as with good\n   old  `F''.  But it will not generate an error if the user enters a wrong\n   file  number, it will simply come up with the menu and ask for it again\n   (and he ain''t gettin'' out before he gives me a correct number!  ;)\n\n   NOTE: There is no ALL mode in this part. That can also be achieved\n         with `N'' or `CS''.\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node AllMode "The ALL mode in ConfScan - By KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n\n                         ----( The ALL mode... )----\n                               °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n\n   The  ALL  mode  is the mode in which ConfScan performs the action(s) on\n   ALL  conferences  an  user has activated (from the range of conferences\n   the user has access to).\n\n   Examples of instructions to get ConfScan in the ALL mode are:\n\n   N S U A     New Files Since Last On in UL dirs from all conferences\n   CS          New Files Since Last On in UL dirs from all conferences \n   CS H        New Files Since Last On in HOLD dirs from all conferences\n   N S H A     New Files Since Last On in HOLD dirs from all conferences\n   N -10 U A   New Files From 10 Days Back in UL dirs from all conferences\n   CS -10      New Files From 10 Days Back in UL dirs from all conferences\n   \n   This also shows why I prefer the `CS'' command above the `N'' ;-)....\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node AnsiDisplay "It''s a colourful world... - By KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n\n                          ----( ANSI Display )----\n                                °°°°°°°°°°°°\n\n   For  your  pleasure  you  can  now  watch  dir listings in full 24-bits\n   colour!  NOT!  But you can still watch it in 3-bits colour (8 cols) and\n   that should work also.  A view of the colours used:\n\n   0---------|---------|---------|---------|---------|--------|------etc.\n\n   Fido72.lha    P 105298  05-13-93 Update Fido V0.72\n   ^             ^ ^       ^        ^\n   |             | |       |        `--------------» Standard white colour\n   |             | |       `-----------------------»            Bloody red\n   |             | `-------------------------------»         Golden yellow\n   |             `---------------------------------»          Mystery blue\n   `-----------------------------------------------»     Devine light blue\n\n   And  you  might  not have noticed it, but from now on there is only ONE\n   space  between  the  file-date  and  description!   That  was neccesary\n   because  of the tagging method.  Some space was needed to place the `*''\n   after  the  filename and that was the only way.  But I don''t think many\n   people  will  notice  it.   Don''t  worry,  this is only the case on the\n   screen, the dir files themself are not affected.\n\n   Another point worth mentioning is that ConfScan recognizes remarks that\n   have been put on the spot of the file-size and file-date.  Such remarks\n   can  be  put there with ByteKiller or NosNuke or by hand.  Such remarks\n   are  shown  with  a high-lighted background so the user will KNOW it is\n   there.  This can be of a big help for users to easily detect fake files\n   or free downloads.\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node More "Gimme more! Gimme more! - By KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n\n                        ----( More Of ConfScan )----\n                              °°°°°°°°°°°°°°°°\n\n   The  `More''  options  of  ConfScan are (ofcoz?) the options an user has\n   when he''s in the file listing and having a screen full of files.\n\n   I have implemented full support for the numeric keyboard, so it can all\n   be  done  with  one  single hand.  But for those A600 users I have also\n   kept the standard way, no worry.\n\n   There he can decide to:\n\n   F or . - Flag files manually\n   T or 0 - Tag files the simple way ;)\n   \n   C or 5 - Clear the screen and continue to watch the list\n   N or ( - Nonstop watch the list of the current conference\n   A or ) - Nonstop watch the lists of all conferences\n   S or * - Skip the current conference and go on (in @{"ALL mode" link AllMode} only)\n\n   Q - Quit and go back in Ami-X\n   \n@EndNode\n\n@Node BNF "BNF - What the hell is it? - By KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\n\n                           ----( BNF Support )----\n                                 °°°°°°°°°°°\n\n   I can hear you think "what is BNF?" Well, ofcourse it''s an abbreviation\n   and  it stands for Backus-Naur Form.  In fact, this is only a difficult\n   term to describe how I have documented the use of the door.\n\n   The BNF goes like this:\n\n   [...]    - Argument that MAY be used for the program to work\n   <...>    - Argument that MUST be used for the program to work\n   (...)    - Multiple arguments can be filled in and can be used in\n              conjunction with [] and <>...\n              \n   There  is  more,  but  I  won''t bother you with that.  Just remeber the\n   above and you''ll be fine.\n\n@EndNode\n','\n',char(10)),'{"ACCESS":"020","LOCATION":"DOORS:ConfScan/ConfScan","PRIORITY":"0","STACK":"50000","TYPE":"XIM"}','auto-added',82430,5,0,NULL,NULL,'mst_cs22','scan',1780048619);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mst_cs25','MST-CS25.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MST-CS25.LHA','ConfScan','XIM','AmigaGuide',NULL,'Tag/Flag','MST','|                           ~~~~~~~~~~~~~  | ¦_/\___/\___/\___    MAJOR UPDATE OF THE   | |\   /\ __/_  __/  BEST CONFERENCE SCANNER |',replace('+-[ MYSTiC /X-PoWeR! ]----[ ConfScan 2.5 ]-+\n|                           ~~~~~~~~~~~~~  |\n¦_/\___/\___/\___    MAJOR UPDATE OF THE   |\n|\   /\ __/_  __/  BEST CONFERENCE SCANNER |\n|/ Y \/_.¬\/  \                            |\n/  | \\¬¦ \\  \\ o GUI Config Program (WB) |\n\__l_//___//__// o ASM Routines for speed! ¦\n|dL!\/   \/  \/  o Tag/Flag/View/KiLL files|\n+-[ KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC]---[ XiM - /X 3.38+ ]-+\n','\n',char(10)),'ConfScan.Guide',replace('@DATABASE "ConfScan.GUiDE"\012@REMARK .------------------------------------------------------------------.\012@REMARK | This document is written in AmigaGUiDE format, so please read it |\012@REMARK | with AmigaGUiDE or your favourite guide reader.... ciao now...   |\012@REMARK `------------------------------------------------------------------''\012@REMARK $VER: ConfScan v2.5.60\012@WiDTH 80\012@NODE MAiN "Guide to ConfScan v2.5.60 - /X-PoWeR! - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\012                               Guide to ConfScan\012                     for Ami-Express Bulletin Board Systems\012\012                          Program version: 2.5.60\012              Compilation Date/Time: Thu Jun 30 14:23:06 1994\012\012                         © 1993-94 by @{"KiLLRaVeN/MYSTiC" link Killraven}\012                          ASM Coding by ArCaDe/MYSTiC\012\012                ... another fine MYSTiC /X PoWeR! production...\012\012                 @{"      You already run ConfScan? => Read Me!    " link important}\012                 @{"    Introduction    " link introduction}      @{" History of ConfScan " link History}\012                 @{"     Features!      " link     Features}      @{"     BugReports      " link BugReports}\012                 @{"    Requirements    " link Requirements}      @{" Possible error msgs " link Errors}\012                 @{"    Installation    " link installation}      @{" Future improvements " link Future}\012                 @{"    Configuration   " link Configuration}      @{"     Greetings       " link Greetings}\012                 @{"  Usage (by users)  " link        Usage}      @{"  Register... NOT!!  " link Registration}\012\012                 @{"    ConfScan_DL     " link ConfScan_DL }      @{"     KiLLER iNFO     " link KiLLER}\012@EndNode\012\012@Node Introduction "Introduction to ConfScan - /X-PoWeR! - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\012                     - - ­ ­ ­ [ iNTRODUCTiON ] ­ ­ ­ - -\012\012   Welcome to ConfScan!\012\012   ConfScan  was  written  during a period of 1 year and has become quite\012   a  powerful  program  with  many possibilities and great potential.  I\012   have spent a lot of time programming and testing it so I hope you will\012   like it and use it with pleasure.\012\012   A little bit of history...\012\012   At first ConfScan was merely meant as a small util that enabled sysops\012   to  easily  check  what  was uploaded in all the different conferences\012   without  having  to  join them one by one.  The very first version did\012   nothing  more  than  that.  That was version 1.0.  It was never really\012   released but to a few friends.\012\012   Nowadays ConfScan can perform a much greater task than just displaying\012   some  filenames  on  the  screen.  ConfScan can now be used to control\012   some  main  parts  of  the  bulletin  board  system Ami-Express.  With\012   ConfScan  you  can  scan for new files, view them from within ConfScan\012   and you can even Nuke files with ConfScan.  Usage of ConfScan has been\012   made as intuitive as possible and should be very easy to use.\012\012   ConfScan  is  an  intelligent program, detecting the options for every\012   user  using  ConfScan, not showing options that they don''t have access\012   for.   ConfScan  also recognizes Ami-X Net conferences that usually do\012   not have file bases, as a result these conferences without a file base\012   are not shown in the config menu (''CS W'').\012\012   ConfScan  comes  with  a  highly user friendly GUi Config program!  No\012   more  tooltypes  to fill in by the sysop!  Just start the program from\012   the CLi or Workbench and CLiCK the options you want and save''m!\012\012   ConfScan  is  made  in a way that you don''t have to repeat information\012   that  is  already known is other files or icons.  ConfScan knows where\012   to find it and will use it.  But in my opinion that is something every\012   program  should  support.   Besides that, if you have any problem with\012   ConfScan  you  can  always reach me for support, I am offering support\012   for all registered sysops of Ami-Express, FOR FREE!\012\012   But  not only for you, the sysop, ConfScan is a must.  Your users will\012   also  appreciate  it  since  ConfScan  allows users to tag their files\012   instead  of  flagging them (but they can still flag files if they want\012   to  ofcourse)  and  ConfScan  enabled  them  to  download  files  from\012   different   conferences  without  having  them  to  jump  through  the\012   conferences  by  theirselves.   in  the  near  future, it will also be\012   possible  to  download all files from all conferences in one time!  So\012   look out for the coming version!\012\012   ConfScan also offers your users a large configurability.  ConfScan has\012   a Config Menu built in so they can easily adjust their preferences.\012\012   A seperate Download door enables you to put restrictions on downloads.\012   With  the  GUi  Config  program  you can easily exclude conferences or\012   nodes from downloading.  You can put accesslevels on nodes/conferences\012   or  even  use userlists for download access on nodes/conferences.  And\012   all  this  information is again saved by the Config program, so you do\012   not have to fill in any tooltypes (GUi Config does that for you).\012\012   if  this  sounds  like  a  useful  program in your ears, check out the\012   @{"features" link features} to find out more.  Or at least start the GUi Config.\012\012                                                        @{"-KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC" link Killraven}\012\012@EndNode\012\012@Node Requirements "What DO you need? - /X-PoWeR! - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\012                   - - - ­ ­ ­ [ REQUiREMENTS ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   The  requirements can differ a lot since you can setup ConfScan anyway\012   you  like,  but  if  you  want to use ConfScan to the fullest you need\012   this:\012\012   · @{" Ami-Express BBS " link Ami-X} version 3.38+\012   \012     YOU NEED VERSiON 3.38 OR HiGHER TO RUN THiS PROGRAM, PLEASE OBTAiN\012     THE LATEST VERSiON FROM YOUR DEALER (SEE "AMi-EXPRESS BBS").\012\012   · @{" Clean dir files " link CleanDir}\012\012   For the support of [V]iewing files you need to have in your C: dir\012   · DMS\012   · LHA\012   · UNZiP\012\012   If you want to be able to nuke files with ConfScan you need to have\012\012   · @{" KiLLER " link KiLLER}\012\012   installed on your system.\012\012@EndNode\012\012@Node CleanDir "VERY iMPORTANT! READ THiS! - By KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\012                 - - - ­ ­ ­ [ CLEAN DiR FiLES ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   This  may sound obvious, but to get the most out of ConfScan, you need\012   to  have  clean  dir files.  So no taglines or any other alien text in\012   your dir files.\012\012   There is one exception on the other hand, there is one program you are\012   allowed to use to alter your dir file and that is DirStyle by The Bird\012   of  TRSi.   Support  for this dirstyler is built in to ConfScan.  This\012   was  done  after a request from Sal-One/TRSi.  If you have a dirstyler\012   that  you  would like to have support for, contact me and maybe we can\012   work something out.\012\012   Nukers on the other hand cause no problems.  You are free to use them,\012   even better, there is support for two nukers:  BossNuke and KiLLER.\012\012   "What  can  go  wrong  if I use a dirstyler?" you might wonder.  Well,\012   there  is  one thing that can go wrong; file-tagging.  ConfScan uses a\012   algorithm  to  recognize  filenames in the dir-file.  But if you use a\012   dirstyler  that  puts text where normally filenames are, ConfScan will\012   see that text as a filename.\012\012   If  you  still want to use that dirstyler, you can turn of the tagging\012   with the Config program (see @{"Configuration" link Configuration}).\012@EndNode\012\012@Node Installation "How to get it working - /X-PoWeR! - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\012                    - - - ­ ­ ­ [ iNSTALLATiON ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   To install ConfScan, simply double-click on the install-ConfScan icon.\012\012   Installation  will  proceed  with  the  C=  installer.   Help has been\012   provided  in  the  installer  program,  so  no  need  to  repeat  that\012   information in here.\012\012   What can you do with the installer? The installer script will:\012\012   · Allow  you  to  install  the  ConfScan  main  executable  (ConfScan\012     itself).  You can choose either for the 68000 or 680x0 version.\012\012   · Allow you to install the ConfScan_DL Download door that  is  needed\012     for Ami-Express to recognize any flagged/tagged  files.   This  one\012     comes in just one flavour, 68000.\012\012   · Allow you to install the ConfScan_G door which checks if users have\012     flagged  files  still  not  downloaded  before they logoff (a small\012     patch for the original ''G'' door, nothing special).\012\012   · Allow  you to install the help files that come with ConfScan.  Such\012     files are needed to give help to users that use ConfScan.  They can\012     get  access  to  these  files  by putting a question mark after the\012     command (ie.  `N ?'').\012\012   · Allow  you to install the fully GUi Configuration program (Config).\012     This  program  will  allow  you  to  mold ConfScan to your personal\012     needs.   Here you can set all pre-defined preferences, such as ANSi\012     support,  show  new  dates  etc.   etc.  But this is also the place\012     where  you  can  set  download restrictions and exclude conferences\012     from being scanned.  And much more!\012\012   · Allow you to install this guide. You are reading it now.\012\012   · Let  you  choose  as  which  command  you  can to install ConfScan.\012     ConfScan  can  act like 3 different commands, `N'', `F'' and `CS''.  I\012     suggest  you install it as all 3 functions, but if you want you can\012     skip the `CS'' door ''cause it is built-in in `N'' also.\012\012   · Let  you  select the place where you want to install ConfScan.  The\012     default  destination  is  "DOORS:" but you are free to put it where\012     you  want  (the  destination  will  be  put  in  the  command icons\012     afterwards).   Remember,  a directory `ConfScan'' will be created in\012     that directory!\012\012   · Let  you  select  the  name  of  the  command  that the ConfScan_DL\012     download  door will be installed under.  I strongly suggest you put\012     it under the ''D'' cause otherwise users will not be able to download\012     anything ;)\012\012   · Let  you select the place where you want to install the Ami-Express\012     commands.\012     (Default: BBS:Commands/BBSCmd/).\012\012   · Let you set the minimum level required to use any of the ConfScan\012     related commands.\012     (Default: 20).\012\012   · Let  you  set the priority ConfScan will get when executed (only if\012     you  are  an  expert user).  If you are running a multinode system,\012     please  set  it  to 0, otherwise users on the other nodes will have\012     hindrance  from  it  if  you  give  it +1.  Systems with 1 node can\012     easily set it to +1 or +5 for maximum performance.\012     (Default: 0).\012\012   · Ask for the directory where you keep your ACP.info.  This is needed\012     for the Config program.\012\012   · Start the Config program for you so you can configure ConfScan.\012\012   All  commands will get a stack of 50,000 and will be set to multinode.\012   As ConfScan is written in C and ASM, it will be installed as a XiM.\012   \012   If  you want ConfScan installed under another name than `CS'', you will\012   have  to  do  it by hand.  But you can still use the installer.  After\012   installation,  simply rename the CS.info icon in your BBS:Commands/...\012   directory  to  whatever  you  want  (for example, `SCAN'').  This will,\012   however,  force  you  to rename some of the help files as well (rename\012   every file that has ".CS." in it to ".SCAN.").\012@EndNode\012\012@Node Configuration "Config - For easy configuration - KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\012                  - - - ­ ­ ­ [ CONFiGURATiON ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   ConfScan  comes  with an external configuration program called Config.\012   It  is  fully  GUi  so  no more stupid textfiles to create or icons to\012   fill.   Just  start  the  program  and  away  you  are.  Here are some\012   guidelines where you can find some stuff and what it all means.\012\012\012              ^-[ ACCESS LEVELS ]-^\012\012   Hold Access       ­ Every user with an access level equal to or higher\012                       than  the  value  you enter here, is able to watch\012                       the contents of the hold dirs.\012                       (Default:  250).\012\012   View Access       ­ Every  user with an access level >= than the value\012                       you  enter  here,  is  able to view files that are\012                       shown  in  the  dir  file.   You can specify which\012                       filetypes   are  supported  via  the  View  prefs.\012                       (Default:  20).\012\012   KiLL Access       ­ Every  user with an access level >= than the value\012                       you  enter  here,  is  able  to  flag/tag files as\012                       KiLLER  targets.  This is for usage with the nuker\012                       @{"''KiLLER''" link KiLLER}.\012                       (Default:  250).\012\012                ^-[ iNTRO FiLE ]-^\012\012   Intro file        ­ The  filename that you can specify here (either by\012                       entering the filename in the text box or selecting\012                       it  with ''S'') will be the name of the file that is\012                       shown at every startup of ConfScan.  At the moment\012                       you  can enter no variables (such as time/date and\012                       place).\012                       (Default:  <none>).\012\012         ^-[ DEFAULT USER PREFERENCES ]-^\012\012   These are the values that are used if an user does not have his or her\012   own private configuration for ConfScan.\012\012   ANSi Colours      ­ This  option  turns the colours on or off when the\012                       files  are  showed  in your screen.  You can setup\012                       those colours via the `Colours'' button.\012                       (Default: Off)\012\012   Show Sent-by      ­ By  default,  ConfScan  will  filter  out any file\012                       description  lines  that  start  with  ''Sent by:''.\012                       They  are  usually not interesting for users.  But\012                       with  the  latest File_iD''s and SentBy''s you don''t\012                       know what to expect anymore.\012                       (Default: Off)\012\012   Show New Dates    ­ Every time a new date is detected, a little banner\012                       will be displayed informing you of the new date.\012                       (Default: Off)\012\012   Clear Screen      ­ After  *every*  prompt, the screen will be cleared\012                       if  you  turn  this option on.  This speeds up the\012                       display  on  screen  quite  a  bit, esspecially on\012                       local nodes, try it.\012                       (Default: Off)\012\012   Lines b/files     ­ Some  users  find  it  usefull  to have a line put\012                       between all the files.  This does the trick.\012                       (Default: Off)\012\012   Pause b/confs     ­ This   will   put  a  pause  banner  between  each\012                       conference that has got new files.\012                       (Default: Off)\012\012   Return b/files    ­ Some  users  find it usefull to have an empty line\012                       between  all  the  files.  If you''ve got the time,\012                       use  it,  it  makes  it  easier  to detect all the\012                       different files.\012                       (Default: Off)\012\012   One line per file ­ If  you  turn  this on, just the first line of the\012                       file description will be shown.  Very handy if you\012                       want to tag a lot of files FAST.\012                       (Default: Off)\012\012   Always full desc. ­ This   will   prevent   file  descriptions  to  be\012                       displayed broken on your screen.  Turn this on and\012                       from  *every*  file you will always get to see the\012                       entire   file   description.   This  mode  can  be\012                       overridden with the [P] at the flag-prompt.\012                       (Default: Off)\012\012   Future expansion  ­ Guess what? Not used.\012\012               ^-[ SYSOP PREFS ]-^\012\012   This  is  where you set all the internal preferences ConfScan will use\012   while operating.  It more or less controls the engine of ConfScan.\012\012   Copy dirfiles     ­ With  multiple node systems, this is a must!  This\012                       will   first  copy  your  dirfile  to  T:   before\012                       searching   it  for  a  file  date.   This  allows\012                       multinode support.\012                       (Default: Off)\012\012   Callerslog        ­ Every  time ConfScan is started and this option is\012                       activated,  it  will  be logged in the callerslog.\012                       (Default: Off)\012\012   Use Percentage    ­ A  nice feature of ConfScan is, that it is capable\012                       of  showing  a  percentage  (%)  on  screen  while\012                       searching  the  dirfiles.  If you don''t want this,\012                       turn this option off.\012                       (Default: On)\012\012   Nuker Support     ­ ConfScan  is  also able to recognize comments made\012                       with   nukers.   Currently  supported  nukers  are\012                       BossNuke  and  KiLLER.   But any comment placed on\012                       the  spot where normally the file-size is, will be\012                       seen  as  a nuker comment.  Any nuker comment will\012                       be  display  with a dark-blue background and white\012                       characters.   If  you  don''t  want that to happen,\012                       turn this off.\012                       (Default: On)\012\012   Allow Tagging     ­ @{"Tagging" link Tagging}  is  a  thing  of the day, ConfScan had it\012                       first!   If,  for some reason, you don''t want your\012                       users to tag files, turn it off.\012\012                       Another  reason  why  you want to turn this option\012                       OFF  is  because you use a @{"dirstyler" link CleanDir} that confuses\012                       ConfScan in it''s file-recognition algorithm.\012                       (Default: On)\012\012           ^-[ iGNORED CONFERENCES ]-^\012\012   Any  conference you put in this listview will NOT be seen by ConfScan.\012   That  means  that  it will not scan the conference for new files (CS),\012   not will it be shown when the users wants to set his/her config.\012\012   You  can  add  a conference with "Add Conf", a list will appear of all\012   your conference and simply click on the one you want to add.\012\012   To remove a conference, select the one you want to remove and click on\012   "Del Conf".  Izze simple.\012\012                 ^-[ COLOURS ]-^\012\012   If  you  click  on  the [Colours] button, you will get a new window in\012   which you can enter the colours for the file listing.\012\012   The  values  you  can enter are ANSi ESC colour codes, here is a brief\012   display of all colours:\012\012             BLACK = 30 - RED    = 31 - GREEN = 32 - YELLOW = 33\012             DBLUE = 34 - PURPLE = 35 - LBLUE = 36 - WHiTE  = 0\012\012   Filename          ­ Colour of the filenames.\012                       (Default: 36)\012\012   Status            ­ Colour of the file status (P = Passed, etc.).\012                       (Default: 35)\012\012   File Size         ­ Size of the file (no, really?).\012                       (Default: 33)\012\012   File Date         ­ Date of the file (no kidding?).\012                       (Default: 31)\012\012   Description       ­ Colour that will be used for the file description.\012                       Mind  you  that  this ESC sequence will be sent at\012                       the  start  of  the  file description.  That means\012                       that  if  there is an ANSi colour code in the file\012                       description, the remainder of the file description\012                       will  be  in  THAT  colour  code  and not that you\012                       specify here.\012                       (Default: 0)\012\012                       NOTE:   Although ESC[37m is also the ANSi code for\012                       white,  Ami-Express fails to handle this correctly\012                       cause  the  local  node  will show RED (while your\012                       users  will  actually  have  white).  But by using\012                       ESC[0m you can circumvent this problem.\012\012                ^-[ ViEW PREFS ]-^\012\012   This  is  where  you  can specify which filetypes are allowed to view.\012   Currently supported filetypes are:\012\012   DMS               ­ Files  that  have  DMS  as  a file extension.  The\012                       action  that  is  performed on these files is "DMS\012                       ViEW <filename>".\012                       (Default: On)\012\012   LHA               ­ These  are  files  that  have  LHA  or  LZH  as an\012                       extension.   The action performed on such files is\012                       "LHA V <filename>".\012                       (Default: On)\012\012   Text files        ­ A whole range of extensions go for this file type:\012                       NFO,  NF0,  TXT,  DOC  and  ASC.   These files are\012                       simply  shown  to  them.   This  might  be the ONE\012                       filetype  you  want  to  turn  off  since the show\012                       routine will NOT abort display when it sees binary\012                       codes.\012                       (Default: On)\012\012   ZiP files         ­ Files with the extension ZiP will be attacked with\012                       an "ZiP -v <filename>" command and the result will\012                       be shown on screen.\012                       (Default: On)\012\012                 ^-[ SAVE iT! ]-^\012\012   To  save  all your settings, simply click on the [Save & Exit] button.\012   To quit without saving, close the window.\012\012      ^-[ WHAT ABOUT THAT OTHER BUTTON? ]-^\012\012   That  button  [ConfScan_DL]  lets  you setup some restrictions for the\012   download command.  See the @{"ConfScan_DL guide" link ConfScan_DL} for that!\012@EndNode\012\012@Node Features "Features of ConfScan - /X-PoWeR! - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\012                      - - - ­ ­ ­ [ FEATURES ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012 · GUi  Config  program that can be started from the CLi or Workbench for\012   easy configuration of ConfScan, a first for an /X-Tool!\012\012 · FAST searching with LOW memory consumption! Max. 60Kb per node!\012\012 · ConfScan  can  act  like `N'', `F'' and it''s own `CS''.  So you get three\012   programs for the download of one!  8-)\012\012 · ConfScan  can  show  you the full file descriptions always, so no more\012   broken file descriptions on your screen.  Fully user configurable.\012\012 · One  of the main features of ConfScan is ofcourse the fact that it can\012   scan  multiple  conferences in one time, this is unique!  No other dir\012   scanner is able to do that but ConfScan.\012\012 · Another  feature  is  the  file  @{"tagging" link Tagging}.  Although other dir scanners\012   provide  this  options  also,  ConfScan was the first to use it and it\012   kind of revolutionized the way of tagging/flagging files.\012\012 · Users  can  setup  ConfScan  to  their  own  personal  likings  via  a\012   preferences  menu they can call up with the ''W'' argument.  But this is\012   not  so special anymore.  Maybe the fact that it looks good and has no\012   overabundance  of  colours  in  it make it better than the other ones.\012   Also,  ConfScan recognizes conferences without a filebase and will not\012   even show them to users in the config menu.\012\012 · This is what the users can setup for theirselves:\012   ­ ANSi colour display\012   ­ Line between files\012   ­ Return between files\012   ­ Pause between conferences\012   ­ Show new dates\012   ­ Show sent-by (or not)\012   ­ Always show full descriptions\012   ­ Clear Screen after every prompt\012   ­ Show just the 1st line of a description\012\012 · Like I said above, ConfScan recognizes conferences without a filebase.\012   This is done to support Ami-X Net conferences (they usually don''t have\012   them). You don''t have to specify them, ConfScan is ''smart''.\012\012 · Scanning options; ConfScan has them, here you go:\012\012   ­ Scanning from a certain date\012   ­ Scanning from a number of days back\012   ­ Scanning from the day a user was last on\012   ­ Scanning from [t]oday\012   ­ Scanning in current conference or all conferences\012   ­ Scanning in upload dirs, all dirs or specified dir\012   ­ Scanning in hold dirs (special access-level required)\012   ­ Scanning in selected conferences (user configurable)\012   ­ Scanning with a byte- & filereport afterwards for users with\012     [H]old access (f.e. cosysops).\012   ­ Scanning non-stop\012\012 · Flagging  from  ALL  conferences is possible, ConfScan will keep track\012   itself  of all the files flagged and via the Download door, /X will be\012   informed about them (i.o.w.  they will be flagged).\012\012 · The  special  download  door  does  more  then just flag files for the\012   users.  It can automatically join the next conference where files were\012   flagged  by  the user.  This can be done straight away when they start\012   the download command in a conference where they have selected no files\012   or right after the downloading of files of that conference.\012\012   NOTE!       In  the near future, ConfScan will be able to send all the\012   ~~~~~       files  to  the  users  in  ONE  time.  This saves time and\012               trouble  for your users as well as for your board, it will\012               be  less  busy. \012\012 · With  @{"KiLLER" link KiLLER} installed, you can nuke files from within ConfScan.  Most\012   likely  you  will find a beta version of KiLLER inside and you will be\012   able  to  test it.  As soon as I''ve finished coding it, I will release\012   it  and  make  sure  you  can  still keep using it in cooperation with\012   ConfScan as well as a stand-alone program.\012\012   ALSO READ THE @{" HiSTORY " link History} iN THiS GUiDE FOR MORE iNFO ABOUT THESE\012   FEATURES!\012\012@EndNode\012\012@Node Usage "Usage by users (that includes you) - /X-PoWeR! - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\012                       - - - ­ ­ ­ [ USAGE ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012                                @{"ALL COMMAND LIST" link SysopCommands}\012\012                   >(this is a copy of the user help files)<\012\012   Although this program is very easy to use, it has lots of options and to\012   get it working at its best, you better check out all the possibilities:\012 \012   + Scanning in ONE/ALL conferences   (Conferences Can Be Turned On/Off)\012   + Scanning in ALL/UPLOAD dirs       (Upload Dir is Default)\012 \012   + Scanning from a given date        (i.e. 09-25-93)\012   + Scanning from a # of days back    (i.e. -10 = 10 Days Back)\012   + Scanning from last on system      (N S U Like, Also Default Value)\012   + Scanning from Today               (i.e. N T U)\012 \012   + File Flagging (also in ALL mode)  (Normal Way)\012   + File Tagging  (also in ALL mode)  (`New'' Method Done By KLR/MST)\012 \012   + ANSi Colourful display of files   (User Configurable)\012   + Lines between files               (User Configurable)\012   + Return between files              (User Configurable)\012   + Show sentby''s                     (User Configurable)\012   + Show New Dates in listing         (User Configurable)\012   + Pause between conf. (in ALL mode) (User Configurable)\012 \012   + Nonstop display of CURRENT conf.  (One Of The `More'' Options)\012   + Nonstop display of ALL conf.      (One Of The `More'' Options)\012   + Clear screen and continue listing (One Of The `More'' Options)\012 \012   + CTRL-C Detecting                  (Anytime During Execution)\012   + Your own private config           (With The `W'' Option)\012 \012     iF YOU USE `CONFSCAN'' FOR FLAGGiNG FiLES YOU CAN AUTOJUMP TO THE NEXT \012        CONFERENCE WHERE YOU HAVE FiLES FLAGGED! ALSO AFTER DOWNLOADiNG! \012 \012                     ----[ Options in the CONFiG MENU ]----\012 \012   + Turn conferences on/off that will be scanned when you want to scan\012     all conferences for new files. Files with a `*'' in front of their\012     name will be scanned. Turning on/off goes by entering the number\012     or character in front. You can enter more then one characters/#''s\012     at a time.\012 \012   + Turn ANSi display          on/off  + Turn PAUSE between conf. on/off\012   + Turn LiNES between files   on/off  + Turn `NewDate'' display   on/off\012   + Turn RETURNS between files on/off  + Turn `SentBy'' display    on/off\012 \012                           ----[ ConfScan Usage ]----\012 \012   NOTE: This explanation talks about `ConfScan'', but there you need to fill\012   ~~~~~ in the name the sysop gave it!\012 \012   ConfScan works like this: ConfScan [opt1] [opt2]\012                                       ^     ^\012                                       |     |\012   S - Since last on (default) --------+     +-(default)- Show UPLOAD dirs - U\012   DATE - Show from date --------------+     `-------------- Show ALL dirs - A\012   -X - Show from x days back ---------+  if you skip opt1 but fill in opt2,\012   W - CONFiG MENU --------------------+  opt1 is loaded with default value.\012   T - Since Today --------------------''\012 \012   Examples: ConfScan -10............Shows files from UL dir from 10 days back\012             ConfScan S A...........Shows files from ALL dirs from last on BBS\012    in ALL   ConfScan A...............................The same as ConfScan S A\012    conf''s   ConfScan ...............Shows files from UL dirs from last on BBS\012             ConfScan W................GO TO CONFiG MENU & ADJUST PREFERENCES!\012\012\012                  - - - ­ ­ ­ [ THE `N'' COMMAND ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012\012   ConfScan works like this: N [opt1] [opt2] [opt3]\012                                ^      ^      ^\012                                |      |      |\012   S - Since last on -----------+      |      `------ Show ALL conferences - A\012   DATE - Since date -----------+      +-------(default)- Show UPLOAD dirs - U\012   -X - Since x days back ------+      `-------------------- Show ALL dirs - A\012   W - CONFiG MENU -------------+\012   T - Since today -------------''\012 \012   Examples: N S U...........................Shows the new files since last on\012             N -10....................Shows the files from 10 days back and up\012             N 09-25-93...................Shows the files from 09-25-93 and up\012             N T U..............................Shows the new files from today\012 \012             N S U A..........Shows the new files since last on from ALL conf.\012             N -10 U A........Shows the files from 10 days back from ALL conf.\012             N S A A...Shows the files since last on in ALL dirs and ALL conf.\012             N 09-20-93 A A....Shows the files from 09-20-93 in ALL dirs/conf.\012             N T U A.............Shows the new files from today from ALL conf.\012             N W..................................GETS YOU iN THE CONFiG MENU!\012\012\012                  - - - ­ ­ ­ [ THE `F'' COMMAND ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012\012  ConfScan works like this: F [option]\012                              ^\012                              |    important:\012  X - Shows file listing X ---+    if you enter an incorrect number or\012  A - Shows all dirs ---------+    you do not fill in any number, you\012  U - Shows the upload dirs --+    will get a menu first.\012  H - Shows the hold dirs ----+\012  W - Config menu ------------''\012\012\012   With  `<progname> ?''  the user can view these some docs in colour.  The\012   program  will  detect  with  which  command  it  is called and show the\012   correct usage information, don''t worry ;)\012\012   SEE ALSO: @{"More options" link More}\012\012@EndNode\012\012@Node Future "Possible Future improvements - /X-PoWeR! - KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\012                - - - ­ ­ ­ [ FUTURE iMPROVEMENTS ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012 · Downloading  ALL  files  from  ALL  conferences  in ONE time.  This is\012   possible now thanks to the help of Joe Hodge (thanks Joe!).  Make sure\012   you  are  a  registered  sysop,  or  else you want be able to run that\012   version of ConfScan!  It will require /X 3.38+.\012\012 · Improved  file  tagging,  it can be annoying sometimes that you cannot\012   reach a file that is still on screen.  I will have to look into that.\012\012 · ''A'' command to alter/remove flagged files (multiple conferences ofcoz).\012\012 · ''Z''  command  to  search  in  multiple  conferences  and with ConfScan\012   interface.\012\012   Anyway,  if  you  have  suggestions,  make  sure  to  drop me a line at\012   Channel-X or at one of the other MYSTiC boards (in Holland preferably,\012   that''s where  I  am most).  By the way, you don''t need to have a\012   suggestion to call  the MYSTiC boards, you''re welcome at any time, open\012   24 hours a day and at your service!\012\012   Let me know what you think and what YOU think needs improvement!\012\012                            __                       /\\012    :        _ __  __Stz___|  \________/\___________/_ \______/\ _       ·\012   _¦_______ //  \/  \_/   |  \\_  ____  \           /__/      \\\ ______:_\012    |        //       \___   ___/____ \ //__/    |__/  .|   /___/_       |\012    |     ._/    \/   \\_|    \    \|  \/\_//    ||    ||  /      \_.    |\012    |  .:::\_____||_____/|_____\__________/______||_____|__________/:::. |\012   -+--      W O R L D W I D E   B U L L E T I N   B O A R D S !       --+--\012    |                                                                    |\012    |       MASTURBATiON STATiON - 5 NODES - WHQ! - 1-305-552-1192       |\012    |           LAST OUTPOST     - 2 NODES - EHQ! -  +31-721-57682       |\012    |         FORBiDDEN ENTRY    - 3 NODES - CHQ! - 1-416-281-3912       |\012    |             NO LiMiT       - 1 NODE! - GHQ! - +49-46-PRiVATE       |\012    |         TRADE iN CENTER    - 3 NODES - GHQ! - +49-708-260611       |\012    |          SATANiC REALMS    - 2 NODES - OZHQ -  +61-522-41302       |\012    |             THE EAST       - 3 NODEA - PHQ! -   +46-8-840614       |\012    |           BLOOD STREET     - 2 NODES - SCHQ -  +45-751-59284       |\012    |           OUT OF SPACE     - 1 NODE! - SHQ! -  +46-620-13141       |\012    |           UZi SUiCiDE      - 3 NODES - USHQ - 1-203-437-8655       |\012    |            TAU CETi        - 1 NODE! - ESHQ -   +34-34255620       |\012    |            CHANNEL X       - 2 NODES - DiST - +31-2290-62244       |\012    |         SHOTOKAN PALACE    - 2 NODES - DiST -  +32-227-00407       |\012   -+--------------------------------------------------------------------+--\012    :                                                                    :\012\012@EndNode\012\012@Node BugReports "BugReport (Doodlebug invasion part iii) - /X-PoWeR! - Written by Guess Who?"\012\012                    - - - ­ ­ ­ [ BUG REPORTS ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   If you''ve found a bug, make sure to @{"contact" link Killraven} me at Channel-X !!!!! I can\012   not fix bugs if >YOU< don''t report them! Don''t think somebody else will\012   report any bugs, ''cause you all think somebody else will do so.\012\012   Call Channel-X -=> +31-2290-62244 or +31-2290-62535\012\012                        Other ways to reach me:         \012\012                   [email removed] (internet)\012\012                       /X-FiDO NET: 44:100/100.1\012                           NLA NET: 14:100/102.1\012                           BOS NET: 99:999/4.1\012                           AMY NET: 39:151/201.1\012\012@EndNode\012\012@Node Greetings "Greetinx Alien, I Want To Speak To Your Leader! - /X-PoWeR! (no, really!)"\012\012                     - - - ­ ­ ­ [ GREETiNGS ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012                         ALL MYSTiC MEMBERS WORLD-WiDE!\012\012   ­ Tycoon/MST         Thanks for the support and help...\012\012   ­ EMPiRE/MST         Who are you gonna call?\012\012   ­ Axe/MST            Ain''t life a bitch?\012\012  