bug-reports, please\012   contact me via one of the following ways:\012\012   BBS:     Channel-X            +31-2290-62535   (16k8)   /X-PoWeR! EHQ\012                                 +31-2290-62244   (14k4)   /X-Fido   WHQ\012\012            Last Outpost         +31-72-157682    (16k8)   /X-PoWeR! WHQ\012                                 +31-72-201182    (16k8)   MYSTiC    EHQ\012\012                          or on one of the MYSTiC boards!\012\012                         Internet: [email removed]\012                              IRC: #Rave, #Amiga (Nick: Killraven)\012\012                             /XF-Net: 44:100/100.1\012                             NLA-Net: 14:100/102.1\012@EndNode\012\012@Node Ami-X "Ami-Express information, dude!"\012\012     - - - ­ ­ ­ [ PLEASE SUPPORT AMi-EXPRESS AND REGiSTER! ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012\012   As  a  programmer I know how much time Joseph Hodge must have put into\012   developing  Ami-Express.  You are now benefiting from his efforts, why\012   not  reward  his  work  and register NOW!  With registering you secure\012   yourself  of support and the further development of Ami-Express.  I am\012   not asking money for ConfScan, but you would do me a big favour if you\012   would register yourself!\012\012                           You can order your copy at\012\012                 LightSpeed Technology (USA)   +1-305-964-4263\012\012                                      or\012\012                 Channel-X (HOL)               +31-229-062-535\012\012\012            Or check your local Ami-Express support board near you!\012\012                                    Thanks!\012\012@EndNode\012\012@Node History "How did it end up like this - /X-PoWeR! - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\012                        - - - ­ ­ ­ HiSTORY ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   2.6.03   24-Aug-94 Fixed     : ConfScan no longer crashes if you have dir-\012                                  files with size 0 in your conference.\012                                  *Reported by Jake at Last Outpost*\012\012            24-Aug-94 Fixed     : If you didn''t have RELATIVE_CONFERENCES,\012                                  ConfScan could screw things up. Fixed.\012                                  *Reported by Zed on Channel-X*\012\012            24-Aug-94 Improved  : A pause between conferences would also\012                                  cause a pause between dirs and that is not\012                                  what it is supposed to do. Now it works\012                                  without problems.\012                                  *Reported by Zed on Channel-X*\012\012            24-Aug-94 Fixed     : If you had the ''Clear Screen'' option on,\012                                  the screen would also be cleared at the\012                                  end of the list, showing only the final\012                                  stats, not cool. So I fixed that.\012                                  *Reported by Muad''Dib*\012\012            24-Aug-94 Improved  : The Config menu has got a new and better\012                                  interface and now has two sections:\012                                  environmental options and CS options. Also,\012                                  when the config menu is called from ''N'' or\012                                  ''F'', the environmental options will show\012                                  up first (instead of the CS options that\012                                  used to come up first).\012\012            24-Aug-94 Improved  : Wrote a few new help files that are shorter\012                                  and (hopefully) easier to read and better\012                                  to understand.\012\012            25-Aug-94 Fixed     : If you have the ClearScreen option set, it\012                                  will now also clear the screen the first\012                                  time.\012                                  *Reported by Arcade/MST*\012\012   2.6.02   11-Aug-94 Fixed     : Tagging and flagging of files was a mess!\012                                  Things got messed up, nothing went right.\012                                  This will fix it, make sure to REMOVE any\012                                  file in your ...ConfScan/Users directory.\012                                  *Reported by Me*\012\012   2.6.01   07-Aug-94 New       : ConfScan now saves all the files that a\012                                  user flags in the sub-directory users in\012                                  the ConfScan directory. They are stored\012                                  like User_x, where x is the slotnumber\012                                  of the user. This has the advantage that\012                                  users can logoff, call back and still\012                                  have those files flagged.\012                                  \012                                  If the directory ../Users does not exist,\012                                  ConfScan will create it for you.\012                                  \012                                  For now, this is not an option, I intend\012                                  to make at optionable for either the sysop\012                                  and user.\012                                  *Requested by several sysops*\012\012            07-Aug-94 New       : The flagged files are no longer saved in\012                                  text format, a structure is now used for\012                                  storage. This decreases readability (if\012                                  you ever read them 8-) ), but increases\012                                  speed.\012\012            07-Aug-94 Fixed     : ConfScan now also works under /X 4.x.\012\012   2.6.00   24-Jul-94 New       : When a dirfile is being copied (ie. you\012                                  have the copy-dirfiles turned on), the\012                                  user will see a percentage displaying the\012                                  progress of the copy (just like the scanning\012                                  routine).\012                                  This only happens when you have the USE-\012                                  PERCENTAGE option turned on.\012\012                      Improved  : Built in some more error information on \012                                  some parts of the program. Home usage only.\012\012   2.5.63   23-Jul-94 Fixed     : The ConfxCMD bug is gone. I just had to take\012                                  a closer look. Ami-Express gives the number\012                                  of the current conference MINUS 1. I knew\012                                  that, but forgot it later on in the routine.\012                                  *Reported by Zed at Channel-X*\012\012                      New       : From now on, registered versions are \012                                  available from me. Registered version do not\012                                  have special functions or hidden features,\012                                  they are just registered (shown at startup).\012                                  The only advantage is that you will most\012                                  likely get the current available version.\012\012                      Fixed     : MAJOR BUGFIX! For some incredibly STUPID\012                                  reason I forgot to check for hold access\012                                  with the ''F'' command 8-( My sincere apologies\012                                  for such a mistake, how could this slip\012                                  through all tests...\012                                  *Reported by TyCooN*\012                                  \012   2.5.62   16-Jul-94 Fixed     : It appears it still does not work properly.\012                                  Made a quick fix on-line 8-(\012                                  *Reported by Zed at Channel-X*\012\012   2.5.61   11-Jul-94 Fixed     : When installed as an ConfxCMD command, it\012                                  would look in the wrong Conference for the\012                                  icon information. Is fixed.\012                                  *Reported by Zed at Channel-X*\012\012                                  * R E L E A S E  V E R S i O N *\012\012   2.5.60   28-Jun-94 New       : ''N S G'' now works. It stands for "New Since\012                                  last logon Global" and does the same as\012                                  ''CS''.\012                                  *Requested by EMPiRE/MST*\012\012            30-Jun-94 Changed   : Removed the Beta testers registration info.\012            \012   2.5.59   26-Jun-94 Fixed     : Changed the header of ConfScan, ''cause\012                                  ArCaDe is now also a MYSTiC member.\012\012   2.5.58   20-Jun-94 New       : CTRL-C is now recognized at the flag/tag\012                                  prompt in ConfScan.\012                                  *Requested by Sal-One*\012\012                      Improved  : Made the tagging routine a little bit more\012                                  robust.\012\012   2.5.57   20-Jun-94 Fixed     : Any comments between P/N and the file date\012                                  are now shown with a blue background colour\012                                  from the P/N to the file date (no more spaces\012                                  between the comment and the file date).\012\012   2.5.56   18-Jun-94 Fixed     : The ''P'' bug is fixed.\012                                  *Reported by Tycoon/MYSTiC*\012\012                      Improved  : Replaced an Execute() routine with System().\012\012   2.5.55   15-Jun-94 Fixed     : I forgot to put a return (''\n'') after the\012                                  comment line in the callerslog.\012                                  *Reported (first) by Muad''Dib/5D*\012\012                      Fixed     : Replaced some of the ESC[M and ESC[K\012                                  commands with 79 spaces. I find this\012                                  *STUPiD* but there are still terminals\012                                  around (especialy on the MS-DOS platform\012                                  that DO NOT recognize them!! So incredibly\012                                  lame!\012\012                      Changed   : The task priority of ConfScan is now always\012                                  0. I used to adjust the priority to the\012                                  same as ACP, but that could slow the system\012                                  down if you had it above 0. This evens the\012                                  CPU time a bit if you have multiple nodes.\012\012                      Fixed     : The temporary files in T: were not removed\012                                  if you had ''CopyDirFiles'' activated.\012\012   2.5.54   13-Jun-94 Fixed     : The `FileHelp'' files for every conference\012                                  sometimes were not shown. Fixed it.\012                                  *Reported by EMPiRE/MYSTiC*\012\012                      Improved  : The user can now also enter values like\012                                  -5 or `T'' when ConfScan asks for a date\012                                  via a prompt.\012\012                      Fixed     : The ''N'' command wouldn''t show the existence\012                                  of the [H]old dir to people who had access\012                                  for it if ConfScan asked for it via the\012                                  prompt (Which directory...).\012\012                      Improved  : The output to the Callerslog is now modified\012                                  to "Directory Scan from (xx-xx-xx)" to gain\012                                  compatibility with some callerslog-scan-\012                                  programs.\012                                  *Requested by Sal-One/TRSi^ZENiTH*\012\012                      Fixed     : if you had used the ''P'' space and filesize\012                                  in the filedir (DiRx) for a comment (for\012                                  instance "DELETED!"), than the second ''E''\012                                  would not be shown. is fixed now.\012\012                      Fixed     : Text-files were not shown with the [V]iew\012                                  function (still a result of the multi-\012                                  langual stuff... sh*t).\012                                  *Reported by TyCooN/MYSTiC*\012\012                      Fixed     : The [V]iew option was not multi-node yet,\012                                  fixed that ofcourse.\012\012   2.5.53   06-Jun-94 Fixed     : Due to the new multi-langual stuff in \012                                  ConfScan, the [V]iew function failed in\012                                  locating the output of the [V]iew function.\012                                  *Reported by Just Another Freak*\012\012   2.5.52   05-Jun-94 Fixed     : The search routine failed sometimes if you\012                                  had banners in your dirfiles. This has now\012                                  been fixed.\012                                  *Reported by Tycoon/MYSTiC*\012\012   2.5.51   04-Jun-94 New       : At the prompt there now is a percentage\012                                  shown. it indicates how much of the files\012                                  have been shown already.\012                                  \012                      Improved  : Added credits for Pascal (Arcade).\012\012   2.5.50   02-Jun-94 Improved  : Searching routine has been sped up a\012                                  little bit. instead of the stack, i\012                                  now use some of the CPU''s registers.\012                                  Especially 030+ users will benefit\012                                  from this. if you don''t have an 030,\012                                  go buy one! :-)\012\012            03-Jun-94 Improved  : All ConfScan help files can now be made\012                                  multi-langual just like in Ami-Express\012                                  itself (with .TXT and .TXT.GR). it now\012                                  takes the ScreenTypes.info in account\012                                  when showing a textfile, meaning that\012                                  the helpfile filename is now built up\012                                  like this:\012                                  \012                                  ConfScan.<CMD>.Help<ACS>.<GROUP>\012                                  \012                                  Where CMD = Command name (f.i. CS)\012                                        ACS = Accesslevel, but if the\012                                              level is not found, the\012                                              <ACS> will be skipped.\012                                      GROUP = Language. Factory settings\012                                              are .TXT (Mono) and .TXT.GR\012                                              (Colour). But you can add\012                                              more types in the icon.\012                                  *Requested by AtomiX (Here you go ;) )*\012\012            03-Jun-94 Fixed     : The infamous ''f'' bug has been removed.\012                                  it only occured when you had the "Copy\012                                  DirFiles" option on (Sysop Prefs)...\012                                  *Reported by Brutus*\012\012            03-Jun-94 Fixed     : Starting a download from ConfScan no longer\012                                  causes Ami-Express to perform a fake log-\012                                  out if you said ''Goodbye after'', this time\012                                  the user will be kicked off the board.\012                                  THiS WiLL ONLY WORK WiTH VERSiON 3.38+ !!\012                                  *Reported by ->>Constrictor<<-*\012\012\012            03-Jun-94 Improved  : CONFSCAN NOW HAS GOT A FUCKiNG FAST ASM\012                                  SEARCH ROUTiNE AND KiCKS ASS! USUALLY\012                                  ALL DATES ARE FOUND WiTHiN 2-3 SECONDS!!\012                                  \012                                  *> ASM CODE WRiTTEN BY PASCAL EEFTiNCK <*\012                                  *> THANKS A LOT MAN! iT WORKS GREAT !! <*\012\012            04-Jun-94 New       : At the CS-Prompt (More) you can now enter\012                                  a ''P'' to manually override the Full Desc\012                                  mode giving you a full page of new files\012                                  instead of checking for broken file de-\012                                  scriptions. This works only for that time,\012                                  the next prompt will still use Full Desc\012                                  mode (unless you press ''P'' again).\012\012   2.5.49   27-May-94 Improved  : What do you know? it''s my birthday! :)\012                                  Never mind that, I did manage to fit in\012                                  something new anyway... if you now press\012                                  ''Q'' in the config menu (''N W'') nothing\012                                  will be saved.\012                                  *Requested by Muad''Dib/5D*\012                                  (Thanks for the tapez man :) ).\012\012            27-May-94 New/Fixed : You can now [V]iew files from the hold\012                                  dir (but ofcourse only if you have got\012                                  hold access).\012                                  *Reported by Muad''Dib/5D*\012\012            01-Jun-94 Fixed     : And once again I had to fix the date \012                                  routine ''cause June wasn''t recognized\012                                  correctly (stupid bug!!!). Sorry guyz.\012                                  *Reported by Muad''Dib/5D*\012\012   2.5.48   21-May-94 New       : The /-\ routine has been replaced by an\012                                  percentage routine. So instead of the /-\\012                                  pointer you get to see a percentage showing\012                                  how much of the dirfile has been scanned.\012                                  The config program has been changed as well\012                                  for this, I just renamed the "Busypointer"\012                                  field to "Use Percentage" so if you had the\012                                  Busypointer on, you will get the % now.\012                                  ** YOU SAW iT HERE FiRST! **\012\012            22-May-94 Fixed     : The ''F'' function wouldn''t recognize the\012                                  hold dir if you didn''t specify it at the\012                                  prompt. Now it does.\012\012   2.5.47   20-May-94 Improved  : Replaced some old routines with newer and\012                                  better ones. This is the finishing up part\012                                  before the release.\012\012   2.5.46   17-May-94 Fixed     : The ''F'' command wouldn''t show the FileHelp\012                                  file if you enter it without arguments.\012                                  *Reported by Tycoon/MYSTiC*\012\012                      Fixed     : if you had the ''always show full desc'' mode\012                                  on and you [V]iewed a file, ConfScan was \012                                  confused and tags went wrong. is now fixed.\012                                  \012                      Improved  : if you have the ''Clear Screen'' flag on, the\012                                  screen will also be cleared at the start of\012                                  ConfScan, not after the first prompt.\012\012                      Fixed     : if you left the ''F'' command with enter you\012                                  would still get a line telling you that there\012                                  were 0 bytes and 0 files.\012\012   2.5.45   12-May-94 Fixed     : Bug in the ''prompt'' routine sometimes caused\012                                  for an infinite loop, the only way out was\012                                  the ''Q'' option. is now fixed.\012                                  *Reported by Brutus/Brutal Approach*\012\012                      Fixed     : Replaced some old stick-m-together routines\012                                  with the AddPart routine. This solves the\012                                  problem that ConfScan can''t find certain\012                                  files (such as dirfiles).\012                                  *Reported by Brutus/Brutal Approach*\012\012   2.5.44   10-May-94 Fixed     : Minor bug in the config menu is fixed.\012\012   2.5.43   10-May-94 Improved  : Radical change in the config menu! it now\012                                  consists of two menus instead of 1. You\012                                  can swap menus with ''Y''. Save/exit with ''Z''.\012\012                      New       : You can have ConfScan always show you the\012                                  full description of a file. That means that\012                                  if you get the `More'' prompt in the middle\012                                  of a file description, ConfScan will notice\012                                  this and show the next files until that \012                                  file is about to disappear from your screen\012                                  showing its full description. This is quite\012                                  a nice feature if you ask me ;-) Very nice\012                                  and USER CONFiGURABLE.\012\012                      New       : You can have ConfScan clear the screen\012                                  after every `More'' prompt. This is also\012                                  USER CONFiGURABLE. ConfScan will *NOT*\012                                  clear the screen when you are in non-stop\012                                  mode (either with the `ns'' argument or `n''\012                                  from the `More'' prompt).\012\012                      New       : You can have ConfScan show you just the\012                                  first line of file descriptions. This is\012                                  also USER CONFiGURABLE.\012\012                                  * New Preferences Structure, conversion *\012                                  * util required for sysops. Does NOT    *\012                                  * affect user config files!             *\012\012   2.5.42   06-May-94 Improved  : ConfScan now recognizes the new prefs that\012                                  the Config program saves. This asked for the\012                                  whole ''Config Menu'' part to be rewritten.\012\012                                  * NEW PREFS FORMAT FOR USERS! OLD CONFiG *\012                                        * FiLES NEED TO BE DELETED! *\012\012                      Fixed     : The "introfile" was shown with extra lines.\012                                  Also put an ESC[0m in front of the intro-\012                                  file to prevent colour leakage.\012\012                      Improved  : All parts of ConfScan have been updated with\012                                  the new prefs structure (phew).\012\012   2.5.41   03-May-94 Fixed     : The summary of the conferences with their\012                                  bytes and files could get messed up if you\012                                  had long conference names. This is now fixed\012                                  and set to 20 chars.\012                                  *Reported by Muad''Dib/5D*\012\012   2.5.40   01-May-94 Fixed     : Tagging the same files twice could happen\012                                  if user tagged, exited and tagged something\012                                  in the same list again. is fixed.\012\012                      Improved  : When you press ''C'' at the prompt, the screen\012                                  will be cleared and the last file with its\012                                  COMPLETE description will be shown. So that\012                                  means you will always get to see ALL file\012                                  descriptions if you keep using C.\012                                  *Requested by Easy Rider/MST/TRSi*\012\012   2.5.39   27-Apr-94 Removed   : When users use ''CS'' they no longer get\012                                  to see how many files/bytes were uploaded\012                                  in that conf. it was ugly :( Design rulez.\012                                  *Requested by Muad''Dib/5D & TyCooN/MST*\012\012   2.5.38   27-Apr-94 Fixed     : Memory bug fixed, thanks to Mungwall.\012                                  Now there are no Enforcer hits (there\012                                  never were) and no Mungwall hits.\012                                  *Crying by TyCooN/MST :)*\012\012   2.5.37   25-Apr-94 New       : When in multi-conference mode, accumulative\012                                  figures will be shown after each conference.\012\012                      New       : Added ''NS'' support. Many users wanted to be\012                                  able to have the file listing scroll by non\012                                  stop. if you enter ''ns'' after the command,\012                                  all the files will scroll non-stop. This \012                                  works for ALL commands (N, F and CS).\012\012                      New       : ConfScan can now give a small overview of\012                                  all conferences with their shown bytes and\012                                  number of files. To do this, you have to \012                                  meet a few conditions:\012                                  * Add a ''+'' after the CS-command\012                                    i.e. "CS +" or "CS T ns +"\012                                  * More than 1 conference needs to have new\012                                    files (so it doesn''t work with ''F'' or\012                                    ''N'' since that isn''t usefull).\012                                  * Access level of user is high enough, when\012                                    an user has got hold-access, he is able\012                                    to see the overview.\012\012   2.5.36   25-Apr-94 Fixed     : All returns (\n\r) are now done internally.\012                                  So any more ''Pause more/y/n'' are from now\012                                  on impossible. This way I circumvent the\012                                  3.38 ''problem''.\012\012                      Changed   : if there is no date on the appropriate\012                                  location, it will no longer be high-\012                                  lighted again. This should speed up the\012                                  display a bit.\012                                  *Requested by MKO!/PDX*\012\012   2.5.35   13-Apr-94 Improved  : Replaced all ''/X-DeSiGn'' logo''s with the\012                                  new /X-PoWeR! logo''s... too many people\012                                  were abusing the /X-DeSiGn trademark :(\012\012                      Fixed     : ConfScan would sometimes abusively take\012                                  dates in file descriptions as the file\012                                  date... :( Fixed now.\012\012   2.5.34   13-Apr-94 Fixed     : When pressing ''D'' while you were in tag-\012                                  mode, any file you flagged would not be\012                                  noticed... oops... fixed now.\012                                  *Reported by Tycoon/MYSTiC*\012\012                      Improved  : Sped up the output on your screen.\012\012   2.5.33   11-Apr-94 Fixed     : To prevent problems with NONSTOPTEXT, i\012                                  have taken care of the /n/r''s myself. This\012                                  eliminates occurances of ''(pause) etc.''.\012                                  \012                      Improved  : The ''F'' command doesn''t needlesly copy\012                                  itself to T: anymore unless you specify it\012                                  in the icon with COPY_DiRFiLES. This also\012                                  increases the ''F'' command.\012\012   2.5.32   06-Apr-94 New       : You can now directly start the Download\012                                  from ConfScan with the [D], this can be\012                                  done either at the prompt or when you''re\012                                  tagging.\012\012                      New       : You can now directly start KiLLER from\012                                  ConfScan with the [!], this can be done\012                                  done either at the prompt or when you''re\012                                  tagging.\012\012   2.5.31   03-Apr-94 Fixed     : Wooops, forgot to remove the extra space\012                                  in ''normal'' lines, this caused the first\012                                  line of descriptions to be one char to\012                                  the left.\012\012                      Fixed     : Comments with BossNuke and KiLLER are also\012                                  properly displayed again (nobody had noticed\012                                  it though :) ).\012\012   2.5.30   02-Apr-94 Improved  : No more extra space between the filename  \012                                  and the file status (N or P). That way a\012                                  sysop can simply grab the dirfile from\012                                  screen and insert it in his own dirfile\012                                  w/o having to edit it.\012                                  *Requested by some dudes at Last Outpost*\012\012   2.5.29   01-Apr-94 Fixed     : internal fix. Never mind.\012\012   2.5.28   01-Apr-94 New       : intergrated the bytes and files into the\012                                  last line (used to be: "READY SCANNiNG"\012                                  but now holds the number of bytes and files\012                                  shown).\012                                  *Requested by Empire/MST*\012\012   2.5.27   31-Mar-94 New       : When ConfScan is ready scanning, you get\012                                  to see the total amount of files and bytes\012                                  that an user got to see.\012                                  *Requested by Chaplin/PHUN*\012\012   2.5.26   30-Mar-94 Improved  : Better Config colours (CS W, N W etc.)\012\012   2.5.25   27-Mar-94 New       : For more flexibility, you can now select\012                                  your own colours for the file listing:\012                                  LiST.FiLE=xx   - File name\012                                  LiST.STATUS=xx - File status (P or N)\012                                  LiST.SiZE=xx   - File size\012                                  LiST.DATE=xx   - File date\012                                  LiST.DESC=xx   = File desc\012                                  xx = ANSi code (31=red, 32=green etc.)\012\012                      Improved  : The help on the ''More'' options is now\012                                  external, you now have 4 more helpfiles:\012                                  ConfScan.More_General.Help - General help\012                                  ConfScan.More_Tagging.Help - Tagging help\012                                  ConfScan.More_Killing.Help - Killing help\012                                  ConfScan.More_Viewing.Help - Viewing help\012                                  This is done because you can set access \012                                  levels for viewing and killing and you can\012                                  turn of Tagging. So those files will ONLY\012                                  be showed when an user has access.\012\012                      Improved  : To KiLL files you can now also press DEL\012                                  (this also goes when you are in TAG mode).\012\012                      Improved  : To quit ConfScan you can also press ESC.\012\012   2.5.24   26-Mar-94 Improved  : Replaced NO_BOSSNUKE and NO_KiLLER by one\012                                  tooltype: NO_NUKER_SUPPORT\012\012   2.5.23   25-Mar-94 New       : New tooltype: NO_BUSYPOiNTER. if you put\012                                  this in your icon you will NOT see a /-\\012                                  spinning after `Scanning...''. This will\012                                  speed up the searching though.\012\012   2.5.22   24-Mar-94 Fixed     : Put the COPY_DiRFiLES back because this\012                                  can be handy for multi-node systems!\012                                  *Requested by Muad''Dib/5D*\012\012   2.5.21   22-Mar-94 Fixed     : Search routine now has a few extra checks\012                                  to make sure it is a date we got and not\012                                  a date from within a description\012\012   2.5.20   22-Mar-94 Improved  : Searching for files is now almost 100%(!)\012                                  faster thanks to a routine from Tycoon of\012                                  MYSTiC. Thanks man! it really is fast now!\012                                  \012                                  This makes the tooltype COPY_DiRFiLES un-\012                                  usable. So scratch that one :)\012\012                      Fixed     : The `sscanf'' function in SAS/C sometimes\012                                  fucks up, replaced with my own routine.\012\012   2.5.19   19-Mar-94 Fixed     : Sometimes KiLLER wouldn''t recognize kills\012                                  made with ConfScan. That is now fixed.\012                                  This also fix the Download-bug (not seeing\012                                  tagged files).\012\012   2.5.18   16-Mar-94 Fixed     : Some internal changes. This fixes one of\012                                  the most hard-headed bugs! \012\012   2.5.22   11-Mar-94 New       : KiLLing of files is now possible when in\012                                  [T]ag mode with the [K].\012\012                      New       : Viewing of files is now possible when in\012                                  [T]ag mode with the [V].\012\012                      Fixed     : Changed the colours of the hgh-light mode,\012                                  instead of light blue background with blue\012                                  characters it is now a blue background with\012                                  white characters (red if you are on the\012                                  local node).\012\012   2.5.13   07-Mar-94 Fixed     : Replaced a real old routine with a more\012                                  modern one. Hope this fixes ''THE'' bug :(\012\012                      Fixed     : Esc[0m are now only given the before a\012                                  filename and not every line.\012                                  *Reported by EMPiRE/MST*\012\012   2.5.12   06-Mar-94 New       : Added support for my nuker, KiLLER.\012                                  KiLLER comment are shown with a light-blue\012                                  background and dark-blue foreground.\012                                  New tooltype: NO_KiLLER (if specified any\012                                  comments made with KiLLER will not be\012                                  high-lighted).\012\012                      Fixed     : Some bug fixes (internal).\012\012   2.5.08   22-Feb-94 New       : Cursorkeys can now be used when user\012                                  wants to [T]ag files. Old keys are\012                                  still supported though.\012\012                      New       : When Tagging a file with ''0'' the cursor\012                                  will jump to the next file.\012\012                      Fixed     : Minor bug fix.\012\012                      Improved  : Guide file was changed drastically to\012                                  make it better reading material. Setup\012                                  a bit different. Now with installation\012                                  instructions for 3 levels of skill of\012                                  the sysops (stupid, newby and veteran).\012\012   2.5.07   21-Feb-94 New       : Added a few tooltypes so the sysop can \012                                  decide which filetypes are not supported.\012                                  Tooltypes are:\012                                  NO_DMS_ViEW for .DMS files,\012                                  NO_LHA_ViEW for .LhA/LZH files,\012                                  NO_ZiP_ViEW for .ZiP files and\012                                  NO_TXT_ViEW for .TXT/DOC/ASC/NFO files.\012                                  *Requested by Muad''Dib* (Stupid DMS bug).\012\012   2.5.06   21-Feb-94 Fixed     : Minor bug fix (users who have just viewed\012                                  a file cannot tag files after that, makes\012                                  sense ofcourse since the screen is totally\012                                  messed up).\012\012   2.5.05   20-Feb-94 New       : File viewer built in. Supported files are:\012                                  DMS, LHA, LZH, ASC, TXT, DOC, NFO and ZiP.\012\012                      New       : New tooltype: ViEW_ACCESS. Here you can enter\012                                  the minimum access a user must have to be\012                                  able to [V]iew a file. When an user has got\012                                  no access, he will not be aware of the ViEW\012                                  option (it is not shown as an option).\012                                  Example: ViEW_ACCESS=100\012\012                      Change    : Changed the colours a little bit to get a\012                                  certain standard. Still not perfect though.\012\012   2.5.04   19-Feb-94 Fixed     : Some coloured file-descriptions would some-\012                                  times fuck up the rest of the file-listings\012                                  with colour. is now fixed.\012\012                      New       : Registration info added, special registered\012                                  version can now be made (for beta-testing\012                                  purposes).\012                                  \012                      Fixed     : Longer BossNuke descriptions are now detected\012                                  and properly processed.\012\012   2.5.03   19-Feb-94 Special   : Tailermade version for Muad''Dib/5D\012\012   2.5.02   12-Feb-94 New       : Added a tooltype: COPY_DiRFiLES. This tells\012                                  ConfScan to copy the dir-file (dirx) to T:\012                                  first and start scanning the file there.\012                                  *Requested by TyCooN/MST*\012\012   2.5.00   10-Feb-94 Fixed     : Date entries don''t fail anymore when you\012                                  were asked for a date.\012                                  *Report by Muad''Dib/5D*\012\012                      Fixed     : The hold dir is now accepted when asked\012                                  for a dir to scan.\012\012                      Fixed     : Display of nuked files Improved.\012\012                      New       : Added a ''Scanning...'' routine so you can\012                                  see that ConfScan is busy.\012                                  *Requested by many sysops*\012\012                      New       : Added support for Dir-Style by The Bird.\012                                  You can use this dir-styler now without\012                                  any problems.\012                                  *Requested by [-sAl-øNe!/TRS¡-]*\012\012   2.4.01   13-Jan-93 Fixed     : Did a final bug fix for the jump routine.\012                                  it failed if you were not running your\012                                  BBS with relative conferences. it is now\012                                  made that it can''t fail! (He said... :) )\012\012                      New       : I split up the Download part and the\012                                  scanning part of ConfScan. You know have a\012                                  separate download program.\012                                  \012                                  I also split up the helpfiles from within\012                                  ConfScan. This is all done for reasons of\012                                  SPEED. ConfScan will start up faster this\012                                  way. And you can now edit the help file\012                                  to your needs.\012\012   2.3.03   13-Jan-94 Fixed     : Memory bug fixed! Yes, finally! This was\012                                  a strange bug, but with the help of\012                                  Tycoon/MST it is now gone! No more memory\012                                  is being eaten everytime you use it!\012                                  *Reported by NORAD (Aces High BBS)*\012\012                      New       : A new tooltype in the ConfScan icon. if you\012                                  specify "NO_BOSSNUKE" all comments made\012                                  with BossNuke will NOT be highlighted.\012\012                      Fixed     : Updated the built-in docs so now the T\012                                  option is added.\012\012   2.3.01   03-Jan-94 Fixed     : Jump bug fixed. Seems to go okay now,\012                                  but if I get no bug-reports, I cannot\012                                  fix it! So if you got a problem with\012                                  it, CONTACT ME!\012                                  *Reported by EMPiRE/MST*\012\012   2.2.01   01-Jan-94 Fixed     : ''January'' bug fix! Stupid bug! :(\012                                  *Reported by Muad''Dib/5D & Tycoon/MST*\012                      Fixed     : -x days bug fixed. Now works 100%!\012                                  *Reported by Tycoon/MST*\012                      New/Fixed : ''f h'' is possible now\012                                  *Reported by Muad''Dib/5D*\012\012   2.1.02   26-Oct-93  New      : New option, `T'' will show the uploaded\012                                  files of [T]oday. it can be used instead\012                                  of `S'' or a date. Example: N T U, CS T.\012                                  *Requested by: sHARON/SCooPeX*\012                       Fixed    : Better BossNuke support, taglines of\012                                  BossNuke (`...<BoSSNuKe'') are now\012                                  displayed with a red background and yel-\012                                  low characters.\012\012\012   2.1.01   23-Oct-93  New      : File-counter, when you flag a file you\012                                  will see the actual number of files an\012                                  user has flagged sofar. if a user TAGS\012                                  his files, the number of files will be\012                                  shown at the bottom-right.\012                                  *Requested by: EMPiRE*\012                       Fixed    : File tagging Improved a little by allo-\012                                  cating a little bit more memory for it.\012\012\012   2.0.31   10-Oct-93  OFFiCiAL RELEASE OF VERSiON 2.0!\012                       Fixed    : Correct recognition of ''sent-by'' lines.\012\012   2.0.27   08-Oct-93  Fixed    : Config menu also recognizes conferences\012                                  without a file-base. They will not be\012                                  shown in the menu.\012\012   2.0.26   08-Oct-93  New/Fixed: Auto-recognition of mail conferences or\012                                   other conferences without a file-base,\012                                   the option in the icon to exclude certain\012                                   conferences from being scanned will stay\012                                   active.\012                                  `F'' command bug fixed (conferences without\012                                   file-base could cause problems.\012\012   2.0.23   07-Oct-93  New/Fixed: Nuker support added\012                                  Improved downloading command\012                                  F command included\012                                  Better help files\012                                  Changed file display a bit for tagging\012                                  Added BNF support ;)\012                                  Version information ($VER) Improved\012                                  Better "NO CARRiER" protection\012                                  Who information for /X added (i forgot!)\012\012   2.0.01 - 2.0.22     Beta-releases and all sorts of bug-fixing. See above.\012\012   2.0.00  20-Sep-93   MAJOR UPDATE! First beta-release!\012                       New options: Downloading included in program\012                                    N S U like behavior implemented\012                                    File flagging implemented\012                                    File tagging implemented\012                                    ANSi colour display\012                                    Lines between files possible\012                                    Returns between files possible\012                                    NewDates can be shown\012                                    Sentby''s can be filtered out\012                                    Special remarks in dir-listing are\012                                            shown high-lighted!\012                                    Clear Screen & Continue implemented\012                                    Skip conference implemented\012                                    Nonstop display this conference\012                                    Nonstop display all conferences\012                                    Bigger & Better config menu\012                                    Bigger & Better info for users\012                                    Download command can show all flagged\012                                        files from all conferences\012                                    AutoJump to next conference where user\012                                        has flagged files (also after DL)\012                                    Pause between conferences is now optional\012                                    CTRL-C is detected, program can be stopped\012\012   1.7     18-Sep-93   Bug-Fix: Dir-files still caused problems, is fixed!\012                       Bug-Fix: No more trouble when inserting an extra\012                                space after the conference numbers in the\012                                config menu.\012\012   1.6     11-Sep-93   Bug-Fix: Dir-files with lines longer than 150\012                       characters caused a guru :-(. The maximum is now set\012                       to 300 characters, that should be enough.\012\012   1.5     25-Aug-93   First public release\012\012   All  previous  information is either lost or not worth to be mentioned,\012   it''s  the usual stuff like "new option" and "fixed a bug".  Believe me,\012   you  don''t wanna know.  From now on the history file will be kept up to\012   date...\012\012@EndNode\012\012@Node Errors "What have you done wrong? - /X-PoWeR! - Written by KiLLrAvEn/MYSTiC"\012              - - - ­ ­ ­ [ POSSiBLE ERROR MESSAGES ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   Since  nobody  is perfect, there is a slight chance an error may occur,\012   there are only a few possible errors, so here they are:\012\012   ­ "Couldn''t allocate memory! Too little memory?"\012\012     Do you have enough memory free to run ConfScan?  The program uses about\012     36Kb  of memory (largest block in once is 32Kb for copying files).  The\012     best  thing  you can do is reset and try again.  If it still fails, you\012     better  buy  a  memory  expansion...  If you have enough memory and you\012     still get this error, then please contact me.\012\012   ­ "Couldn''t open temporary file for output! Too little memory?"\012\012     ConfScan  uses a temporary file to store the files which will be showed\012     to  you  later,  this  temp  file  is in the T:  directory, do you have\012     enough  memory  left?   If your file-listings are really big, this file\012     can  be  become  quite large (if you have masses of new warez every day\012     (ofcourse  you  have  :-)).  Maybe the file is still present in T:  and\012     this  MiGHT  cause  the problem, check the T:  directory...  else reset\012     and try again.\012\012   ­ "Couldn''t open file: <name>"\012\012     For  some reason, ConfScan was not able to open the file <name>.  Maybe\012     it  was  in  use by another program?  Best thing to do is reset and try\012     again.   Another  possibility  is that you have not reserved some Ami-X\012     Net- mail area''s and ConfScan tries to open a dir file...\012\012   ­ "Couldn''t open icon.library!"\012\012     If  this  happens,  you better install the icon.libary, but this cannot\012     happen, ''cause /X 3.xx uses it also, so if the icon.library is missing,\012     Ami-X will not startup :-).\012\012   ­ "Error reading from input file during filecopy!"\012\012     It  seems that something went wrong while reading the input file during\012     a  file  copy.  File copies only occur while scanning and when you exit\012     the config menu.  Reset and try again.\012\012   ­ "Error writing to output file during filecopy!"\012\012     Something  went  wrong  while  writing to the output file during a file\012     copy.  This can only happen while scanning and when you exit the config\012     menu.  Reset and try again.\012\012   ­ "Couldn''t open your config file!"\012\012     For  some  reason ConfScan was not able to create your own config file!\012     This should always be possible, better reset and try again.\012\012   Well,  that''s  all  the  errors  ConfScan can create.  If you don''t get\012   ConfScan working on your system, just @{"give a me call" link Killraven} and i''ll make sure\012   it will work!\012\012@EndNode\012\012@Node Tagging "Tagging, the new way of flagging! - © KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\012                  - - - ­ ­ ­ [ TAGGiNG OF FiLES ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   Instead of having to type the filenames (or paste them with PowerSnap)\012   users  (and  you) can walk over the filenames with the cursor keys and\012   select them with spacebar or the ''0''.\012\012   The  idea  comes from some PC terminal programs (and not BBS programs!)\012   that  allow  their  users to let them ''walk'' over the files that are on\012   the screen and with one simple touch of the keyboard the file is marked\012   as  ''flagged''  (or  tagged in this case).  I have implemented this cool\012   method in my door! ConfScan was the FiRST to use this method. \012\012   If  the  user  wishes  to  TAG his files a small bar will appear on the\012   first  filename  that  is  on the screen after the last ''more'' shown on\012   screen.   With  the cursor keys on the numeric keypad the user can move\012   up  and  down over the filenames.  With the `0'' the user can select and\012   deselect  a  file.   A selected file can be recognized at the `*'' being\012   after the filename.\012\012   Flagging  and tagging can be used through each other, it doesn''t matter\012   if  you  flag first and then tag, it will work.  You might wonder if it\012   still works when the users has no colours on screen (no ANSi).  Yes, it\012   works, besides the bar there will also be a ''<'' sign after the filename\012   to point out the current filename.\012\012   This method works ofcourse with all ConfScan imitations (N, F and CS).\012\012   If  you  also are an /X Coder and you want to know more about how I did\012   it, just contact me at Channel-X and I will help you further.\012\012               ­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­\012               ATTENTiON! ATTENTiON! ATTENTiON! ATTENTiON!\012               ­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­­\012\012   Before  you  all  start screaming and yellin'' that there is a bug in my\012   program,  you  can  tag  files that are displayed since the last ''more''\012   line  (or from the beginning if there was no ''more'').  This is done for\012   programmer''s  simplicity  ;) Maybe in the future it will be possible to\012   tag  all  files that are on screen, but that is more difficult than you\012   might think (multiple conferences on one screen and so forth).\012@EndNode\012\012@Node More "Gimme more! Gimme more! - By KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\012                  - - - ­ ­ ­ [ MORE OF CONFSCAN ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   All the help is put into separate files for your convenience.  This is\012   done  to  support  multiple screentypes (so you can have separate help\012   files  for  every  screentype  (=  language)).   Also, because you can\012   determine  access  levels  for  each  action,  separate help files are\012   needed.  So here they are:\012\012   ConfScan.More_General.Help.TXT ^ General Help, available to all\012   ConfScan.More_KiLLiNG.Help.TXT ^ Help for KiLLING of files\012   ConfScan.More_Tagging.Help.TXT ^ Help for Tagging files\012   ConfScan.More_Viewing.Help.TXT ^ Help for [V]iewing files\012\012                       In that order, their contents are:\012\012                         ^-^-^-^-[ B R E A K ]-^-^-^-^\012\012                              MORE ABOUT CONFSCAN\012 \012     [P] ^ Show a full page of files     [A] ^ Non Stop ALL conferences\012     [F] ^ Flag files                    [N] ^ Non Stop CURRENT conference\012     [C] ^ Clear Screen                  [S] ^ Skip current conference\012     [Q] ^ Quit ConfScan                 [D] ^ Start downloading\012\012                         ^-^-^-^-[ B R E A K ]-^-^-^-^\012\012                                 KiLLiNG FiLES \012 \012  [K] ^ KiLL FiLES\012 \012        Either in Tag mode or at the prompt. With ''K'' you can select files\012        that need to be KiLLED later on with KiLLER. The colour of the bar\012        will change if you are in tag mode.\012 \012  [!] ^ Start KiLLER (you will not return to ConfScan afterwards).\012\012                         ^-^-^-^-[ B R E A K ]-^-^-^-^\012\012                          TAGGiNG FiLES WiTH CONFSCAN\012 \012  [T] ^ Tag files\012 \012        Use cursor keys to move the bar over the screen. Press space to\012        select or deselect a file. An asterisk (*) will appear after it''s\012        name meaning it is selected and the colour of the bar will change.\012\012                         ^-^-^-^-[ B R E A K ]-^-^-^-^\012\012                                 ViEWiNG FiLES\012 \012  [V] ^ View Files\012 \012        Either at the prompt or when you are tagging, with ''V'' you will\012        get to view that file.\012 \012        Supported file types: DMS ^ Disk Masher  (Amiga Disk Archives)\012                              ZIP ^ Zip          (msdos File Archives)\012                              LHA ^ LhA(rc)      (Amiga File Archives)\012                              TXT/DOC/NFO/NF0    (Text files)\012\012@EndNode\012\012@Node Important "Update Information - © 1994 KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\012                - - - ­ ­ ­ [ UPDATE iNFORMATiON ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   Welcome  to  version  2.6  of  ConfScan.  This is just an intermediate\012   release,  to  fix  the problem with Ami-Express 4.xx.  I didn''t expect\012   this  version  of  Ami-Express to be released this soon.  My apologies\012   for the error I made (both in judgement as in programming).\012\012   A  few  days  ago  a  saw  a patch of ConfScan going around fixing the\012   problem  with  /X  4.x, but the patcher (I don''t know who did it and I\012   don''t care, really) also made it a 4.x door ONLY.  Now that isn''t what\012   I  had  in  mind!   I know that the patcher couldn''t do anything else,\012   because it was programmed that way (to check for just 1 version).\012\012   Anyway,  like  I said before, this version wasn''t to be released until\012   some  other options were build in, but it appears that there is a need\012   for  a  fixed  version (I figured that if you wanted a new version you\012   would  call  one  of  the MYSTiC boards, there you could get a patched\012   version).  So here it is!\012\012   A small overview of all changes since 2.5(.60):\012   \012   · Flagged  files  from  users  are now saved to a special directory in\012     the  ConfScan  directory  (.../Users/). This enables users to safely\012     log off and download the files at a later time. Several sysops asked\012     for this option.\012\012   · New ConfScan_DL door to read the new structure that ConfScan uses to\012     store  the  files.  It also has got a better look and some bugs were\012     fixed: ­ Non-relative Conference jumping now goes fine\012            ­ Files  entered  after  the  ''D'' command are now flagged and\012              recognized  (previously  ConfScan_DL  would inform you that\012              there  were no files in the current conference although you\012              had just flagged them with the ''D'' command).\012\012     New option: ­ If  you  add ''-r'' as the first argument after ''D'', you\012                   will  be  asked  if  you  want to delete (remove) your\012                   remaining  files.  This  is  just  a small work-around\012                   until my ''A'' command is finished.\012\012     Important : To get this working, ConfScan_DL needs to know where you\012                 have  stored ConfScan. If you install it with the script\012                 there  is  no problem. But if you have already installed\012                 it, add the tooltype ''CS_Location=<path>'' to your D.info\012                 or else it will fail.\012\012   · New Config menu layout and smarter interpretation of the menu.\012     If  you  call  the config menu with ''N'' or ''F'' you will get the menu\012     with  environmental  options  first  instead of the menu with the CS\012     options (as it was before this release).\012\012   · New  ConfScan_G  command with a LOT more options.  Help is available\012     via  ''G ?''  (the file is called ConfScan.G.Help.TXT).\012\012     New options involve: ­ View the remaining files\012                          ­ Remove the remaining files & log off\012                          ­ Download the remaining files\012\012     If  you enter a ''!'' after the ''G'' command, you will force it to just\012     shut up and log off 8-)\012\012     Important : To get this working, ConfScan_G needs  to know where you\012                 have  stored ConfScan. If you install it with the script\012                 there  is  no problem. But if you have already installed\012                 it, add the tooltype ''CS_Location=<path>'' to your G.info\012                 or else it will fail.\012\012   · Quite  a  lot of bugfixes, for a more complete description check the\012     @{"history" link History} part, but here are the main points:\012     ­ ConfScan now works fine from any dir, not just the BBSCmd/ dir.\012     ­ Hold access problem fixed (shame shame).\012     ­ Better error information/detection.\012     ­ A percentage is now shown when a dirfile is being copied.\012     ­ Clear Screen works better.\012     ­ Pause between conferences now works like it should work.\012     ­ Dirfiles if size 0 are handled correctly (skipped :) ).\012     ­ The RELATIVE_CONFERENCES bug is fixed. Non-relative conferences\012       are now supported.\012\012   · I  wrote  shorter  and  better  help files for the users. They don''t\012     need  (nor  are  they  interested  in) long textfiles explaining the\012     theory  behind  ConfScan.  Please use these instead of the old ones.\012\012   Well,  that''s  it  for  now.   Remember,  this is just an intermediate\012   release.   The  next  release  (3.0?)  will most likely have a new GUI\012   Config and the ability to set up your own set of command''s that can be\012   called  from  within  ConfScan.  Like I said before in the Guide, I am\012   interested in your suggestions, so contact me if you have some!\012   \012   I would like to take this oppertunity to thank all the people who made\012   suggestions  for  ConfScan,  and  in  particulair  Zed,  he''s  a great\012   beta-tester,  I could need more of his kind!  Thanks man, you are very\012   thourough and persistant :-)\012   \012   Further  more, school has begun again, so my other internet account is\012   also  active  again:   [email removed]  (yes,  my  first  name is\012   Robert). Write me if you feel bored or anything :-) Or you can find me\012   on IRC at #Rave or #Amiga under Killraven.\012\012   Goodbye & I hope you enjoy ConfScan!\012   \012   (Thu Aug 25 14:45:38 1994  -  Kewl,  one  year  exactly  after the 1st\012    release!)\012\012@EndNode\012\012@Node ConfScan_DL "Guide to ConfScan_DL - © 1994 KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\012\012                           Small Guide to ConfScan_DL\012                   for AmiExpress BBS together with ConfScan\012\012                            Program version: 2.6.02\012                Compilation Date/Time: Thu Aug 25 14:54:47 1994\012\012                           © 1994 by KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC\012\012                       ...part of the ConfScan Package...\012\012                              @{"    Introduction    " link DL_intro}\012\012                              @{"       Usage        " link DL_Usage}\012\012                              @{"    Configuration   " link DL_Configuration}\012\012                              @{"      History       " link DL_History}\012@EndNode\012\012@Node DL_intro "introduction to ConfScan_DL - © 1994 KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\012                    - - - ­ ­ ­ [ iNTRODUCTiON ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   ConfScan_DL  plays  a very important role inside the ConfScan package.\012   it  is  the  link  between all the flagged files and Ami-Express.  You\012   MUST install ConfScan_DL if you want to let users download files.  But\012   that''s not all.\012\012   It  is  great  ofcourse  that  you  now  can  flag files from multiple\012   conferences,  but what happens if you want to download them?  Nothing!\012   Ami-Express  is not capable to let users download files from different\012   conferences  at  once,  thus  I created ConfScan_DL.  ConfScan_DL lets\012   users  download files from multiple_conferences.  Unfortunately not at\012   once, but it is a great improvement compared to nothing 8-)\012\012   What  ConfScan_DL  does,  is flag the files for the conference that an\012   user  is in.  ConfScan_DL checks if there were files selected from the\012   current  conference  and  if there are files, they will be flagged and\012   the internal download command will be started.\012\012   Besides  flagging the files, ConfScan_DL can automatically jump to the\012   next conference where files are selected from.  This can be done right\012   after the download or (when there are no files selected in the current\012   conference)  straight  away.  Users can always ask for a list with all\012   the files they selected.\012\012   But  that  is  not  all!  Many sysops already have another command put\012   under  their  ''D''.  That makes it impossible to install ConfScan_DL as\012   well  under  the  ''D''  command.   But  I  found  out  that these doors\012   generally  do  the same thing:  check if the user may download or not.\012   There  are  lots  of varieties, node checkers, conference checkers and\012   even user checkers.  Well, ConfScan_DL has that built in!\012\012   With  ConfScan_DL you can exclude a node, a conference or even an user\012   from downloading.  This is done with a few tooltypes in the icon.  You\012   can  even  create  a list of people that actually CAN download in that\012   conference  or on that node, so anybody who is not in that list cannot\012   download.\012@EndNode\012\012@Node DL_Usage "How to use ConfScan_DL - © 1994 KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\012                                 ^-[ USAGE ]-^\012\012   I''ve  done  my  best  to  make  the  usage  of the DL door as easy and\012   convinient  as  possible.   If  a user has not used ConfScan, the user\012   will never even know the DL door is being used.\012\012   What  does the user see then?  Well, let''s assume an user has selected\012   five  files,  1 in conference 1, 2 in conference 2 and 2 in conference\012   4.   The  user is in conference 3 and wants to download (thus executes\012   the ''D'' command).  This is what will happen:\012\012   · ConfScan_DL will check wether downloads on this node are legal.\012     If they are not, ConfScan_DL will not allow downloads and will show\012     a text file or a brief message.\012\012   · ConfScan_DL will check wether downloads in this conference are legal.\012     If they are not, ConfScan_DL will not allow downloads and will show\012     a text file or a brief message.\012\012   · ConfScan_DL will check if the user is allowed to download at all.\012     If he is excluded from downloading in general (this can be done with\012     ConfScan_DL) than that user will either see a brief message telling\012     him to sod off or a textfile you can create.\012\012   At  this  point  the  user is allowed to download and ConfScan_DL will\012   check  for  files.  If it finds files it will say so, but in this case\012   it will say:\012\012  ConfScan v2.6 Download File Checker - (c) Copyright 1994 by KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC\012\012       Files flagged for this conference:   0    Skipped alien files:  5\012\012        Your remaining files have been saved. You can logoff safely and\012                 continue downloading another time if you like.\012\012      Would you like to see the list of still remaining files? [Y/n]\012\012\012   So  ConfScan_DL  does  notice  that  there  are  other  files flagged,\012   otherwise  it  will  not ask the user that last question.  Suppose the\012   user says "YES"...\012\012\012                     Files remaining in other conferences:\012                     `-----------------------------------''\012                      TRP-YZ2.DMS       in Conference   1\012                      CATFIX12.LHA      in Conference   2\012                      MDBLC004.LHA      in Conference   2\012                      AXFUNREG.DMS      in Conference   4\012                      BILL&TED.RUL      in Conference   5\012\012    Automatically join the next conference with remaining files? [Y/n]\012\012\012   The  last question offers the user to automatically jump (join) to the\012   next conference where files are flagged.  If the user want so, he will\012   be jumped to the next conference (with the installed ''J'' command).\012\012   There,  the  user can (and unfortunatelly must) select the ''D'' command\012   again.  Then he will see:\012\012  ConfScan v2.6 Download File Checker - (c) Copyright 1994 by KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC\012\012       Files flagged for this conference:   1    Skipped alien files:   4\012\012        Your remaining files have been saved. You can logoff safely and\012                 continue downloading another time if you like.\012\012      Would you like to see the list of still remaining files? [Y/n]\012\012   Well,  after  that  it  will be the same as shown above, but after the\012   download,  ConfScan_DL  will  jump  right  away to the next conference\012   where files were flagged (if the user wanted to ofcourse).\012\012   This  will  be  repeated  for  every  conference where files have been\012   flagged (or tagged).\012\012                 ^-[ HOW TO GET RiD OF SAVED FLAGGED FiLES ]-^\012\012   Sometimes  it  is desired to get rid of all those saved flagged files.\012   Normally  you  would  do  that  with  the  ''A'' command, but /X doesn''t\012   recognize  the  ConfScan  files.  So to work around this problem, I''ve\012   built in this option in the ''D'' command.\012\012   If  the  first  argument after the ''D'' command is ''-r'', a procedure to\012   remove  the flagged files will be started.  I.e.  ''D -r'' will give you\012   this:\012\012               °±² ConfScan_DL - Remove Personal Saved Files ²±°\012\012        Are you sure you want to remove your saved flagged files? [y/N]\012\012   If you are sure, press ''Y'' and you will get either\012\012                         Removed your personal file...\012\012   or, when it fails to remove it (for some dark reason):\012\012                      ERROR! FAiLED TO REMOVE YOUR FiLE!\012\012   If you want to remove files that are not there, you will get to see\012\012           You have no personal ConfScan file. Nothing to be removed.\012\012   I think of everything, don''t I? 8-)\012\012@EndNode\012\012@Node DL_Configuration "Configuration for ConfScan_DL - © 1994 KiLLraVen/MYSTiC"\012                            ^-[ CONFiGURATiON ]-^\012\012   ConfScan_DL  can be configured with the external configuration program\012   Config. You can install it with the Installer script.\012\012               ^-[ CONFSCAN_DL ]-^\012\012   The  ConfScan_DL  part  of  the  Config program can be reached via the\012   [ConfScan_DL] button in the main screen.  A new window will appear.\012\012   The  "ConfScan_DL  Preferences  window 1" is divided into three parts;\012   Node Restrictions, Baud Restrictions and Conference Restrictions.\012\012                        .---------------------------.\012       [ Graphical ]    |-----------+---------------|\012                        |  NODE     |  CONF    | T  |\012        [ Display ]     |  RESTR.   |  RESTR.  | E  |\012                        |           |          | X  |\012                        |           |          | T  |\012            ;-)         |           |          |    |\012                        +-----------+----------|    |\012                        | BAUD RESTRiCTiONS    |    |\012                        `---------------------------''\012\012   Every  time  a  user  wants  to  download, but you have restricted the\012   download  for  that  user, the user will get to see a (brief) message.\012   This  can  either  be  an internal message or a file that you specify.\012   This can be specified PER type of restriction.\012\012   The way you can specify this is universal to all type of restrictions:\012\012   o Internal message\012   o Show file\012\012   I think it speaks for itself.\012\012            ^-[ NODE RESTRiCTiONS ]-^\012\012   The  cycle  gadget  at the top of the window lets you walk through all\012   your  available  nodes.  Shift-Click to go one back. You might want to\012   install Cycle-To-Menu, it''s a very nifty and handy tool ;)\012\012          ^-[ CONFERENCE RESTRiCTiON ]-^\012\012   With  the cycle gadget at the top of the window you can (just like the\012   nodes)  switch  between conferences. Because some boards have a LOT of\012   conferences,  the  ''S''  button allows you to select the conference you\012   want more easily than the cycle gadget might.\012\012               ^-[ RESTRiCTiONS ]-^\012\012   Both  types  of  restrictions  can have the same sort of restrictions,\012   therefore,  the  following  explanation  are valid for either Node and\012   Conference restrictions. The explanation will talk about node, but you\012   can fill in Conference at any time.\012\012   No restrictions   ­ If   you   set  the  node''s  status  to  this,  no\012                       restriction will rest upon this node.  Downloading\012                       from this node will be no problem (unless you have\012                       a baud restriction).\012                       (Default)\012\012   No Downloads      ­ Downloading  from  that  node  will  be impossible\012                       unless  you  give  an  user  special  access  (see\012                       further on).\012\012   Accesslevel       ­ Only users with access level <x> or higher will be\012                       able  to  download  from  this node.  If you don''t\012                       specify  the  access  level  (in the string gadget\012                       behind  it),  the  access  level  will  be  0  and\012                       everybody will be able to download.\012\012   User list         ­ Only users that are present in an user list (ASCII\012                       format)  are  able to download from this node.  If\012                       an  user is not found (or the file does not exist)\012                       the  user  can  NOT  download.   You  can  enter a\012                       filename in the string gadget beneath it or select\012                       a file with the [Select] button.\012\012                       The  user list must consists of an ASCII file that\012                       is built up like this:\012\012                       [BOF]\012                       Tycoon/MYSTiC\012                       KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC\012                       ArCaDe/MYSTiC\012                       etc.\012                       etc.\012                       [EOF]\012\012             ^-[ BAUD RESTRiCTiON ]-^\012\012   Although  this  part  of the Config program looks to be separated from\012   the  Node  restrictions,  this  part will react to changes made in the\012   node  cycle gadget. In other words, any baud restrictions are made for\012   the currently visible node in the cycle gadget.\012\012   No restriction    ­ All baud rates are allowed to download.\012                       (Default)\012\012   Minimum baud      ­ This  is  the minimum baud required for an user to\012                       be able download.\012\012                ^-[ SAVE PREFS ]-^\012\012   The  ConfScan_DL  preferences  need  to  be  saved separately from the\012   ConfScan  preferences (well, not neccessarily but I programmed it this\012   way ;) ). Therefore save them from this window.\012\012   ConfScan_DL  preferences  will  be  saved in the Download command icon\012   (most  likely the D icon). The preferences will also be read from this\012   icon.\012\012                ^-[ MORE PREFS ]-^\012\012   Yes, there is more, see the next section.\012\012                ^-[ MAiN PREFS ]-^\012\012   This will take you back to the first window.\012\012   The  ConfScan_DL  icon  can  be  TOTALLY  configured  with  the Config\012   program, so use it to configure what you want.\012\012   For  you tooltype freaks out there, here is an explanation what Config\012   will save...\012\012   There  are  8  tooltypes for ConfScan_DL, but with these tooltypes you\012   can achieve a lot!  Here they are, followed by a brief explanation.\012\012   · NODE.x      = "NO" / Access level / Filename (with path)\012   · NODE.x.FAiL = iNTERNAL / Filename (with path)\012\012   · CONF.x      = "NO" / Access level / Filename (with path)\012   · CONF.x.FAiL = iNTERNAL / Filename (with path)\012\012   · USER.x      = ALWAYS/NEVER (where x is the slotnumber of the user)\012   · USER.x.FAiL = iNTERNAL / Filename (with path)\012\012   · AREA.name      = ALWAYS/NEVER (where name is the area name of the user)\012   · AREA.name.FiLE = iNTERNAL / Filename (with path)\012\012   First of all, x stands for a number.  So if you want to exclude node 3\012   from  downloading,  enter  NODE.3=NO  in  the  icon.   Or  if you want\012   conference  10  to  be  a  conference where users cannot download, you\012   enter CONF.10=NO in the icon.\012\012   After  NODE.x  or CONF.x you can enter 3 things.  You can either enter\012   "NO", an access level or a filename.  If you enter NO downloading from\012   that node or conference will be impossible, NOBODY can download.\012\012   If  you  enter  an  access  level, that means that downloading is only\012   allowed  when the access level of the user is EQUAL OR HiGHER THAN the\012   level you enter.  If his level is too low, than he can''t download from\012   that node/conference.\012\012   If you enter a filename, ConfScan_DL will open that file and checks if\012   that  file  holds  the  handle  of the user.  If it does, the user can\012   download, otherwise they will be disappointed.  The file must be build\012   up like this:\012\012   ---> CUT <---\012\012   KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC          (ofcourse without the spaces in front of it)\012   EMPiRE/MYSTiC\012   Pharaoh/SR\012   Muad''Dib/5D\012\012   ---> CUT <---\012\012   The  search  routine  is  case insensitive, so don''t worry about that.\012   The file can be placed anywhere because you have to enter the complete\012   path and filename after the NODE.x or CONF.x tooltype.\012\012\012   Ofcourse  it  is  possible to you want certain users to never download\012   (again) on your board or that you want certain users always to be able\012   to  download.   This  can be achieved with the USER.x tooltype.  The x\012   stands  for the number of the user in your user.data (his slotnumber).\012   After  that  you  can either enter NEVER (no download for this guy) or\012   ALWAYS (downloading will be no problem).\012\012   The  same  goes  for users with a certain AREA NAME.  This way you can\012   prevent  NEW users from downloading at all or any other range of users\012   with a particulair AREA NAME (the F option in the user editor).\012\012\012   Now, when ConfScan_DL sees that an user is not allowed to download, it\012   will display a message.  This can be either an internal one or one you\012   made  for him :). If you enter iNTERNAL after NODE.x.FAiL, CONF.x.FAiL\012   or USER.x.FAiL, the internal message will be send:\012\012                    -----[ NO DOWNLOADiNG ON THiS NODE! ]-----\012\012                    -----[ NO DOWNLOADiNG iN THiS CONF! ]-----\012\012                    -----[ NO DOWNLOADiNG FOR YOU DUDE! ]-----\012\012                    -----[ NO DOWNLOADiNG FOR YOU GEEK! ]-----\012\012                    -----[ NO DOWNLOADiNG AT xxxx BAUD! ]-----\012                    -----[ MiNiMAL REQUiRED: xxxx BAUD! ]-----\012\012                                       8-)\012\012   ...or  you  can enter a filename after the .FiLE and that file will be\012   shown instead, it''s just what you like.\012@EndNode\012\012@Node DL_History "The History Of ConfScan_DL - © 1994 KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\012                      - - - ­ ­ ­ HiSTORY ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   \012   2.6.02   25-Aug-94 New         : With the ''-r'' option, you can now \012                                    manually remove your saved tagged\012                                    files.\012\012   2.6.01   11-Aug-94 Improved    : Now recognizes the new structure from\012                                    ConfScan which is a bit smaller.\012\012   2.6.00   07-Aug-94 New         : Better layout, not so boring anymore.\012\012                      New         : It recognizes the new structure that\012                                    ConfScan uses.\012\012   2.5.09   06-Jun-94 Improved    : Optimized the source, this was mainly\012                                    possible thanks to Joe (/X 3.38). Output\012                                    is now almost 4Kb smaller!\012\012   2.5.08   18-May-94 New         : Is now able to read the slightly different\012                                    tooltypes that the Config program leaves\012                                    behind.\012\012   2.5.07   18-May-94 Fixed       : The user statistics are now saved in the\012                                    ENV: dir (by ConfScan) and are now read\012                                    correctly (was T:).\012\012   2.5.06   11-Mar-94 New         : New tooltype: AREA.code where <code> is\012                                    the conference access you have given an\012                                    user (the F option in the user editor).\012                                    it works just like USER.SLOTNUMBER, so\012                                    AREA.NEW=NEVER will prevent new users\012                                    from downloading. \012                                    \012                                    New tooltype: AREA.FiLE=<filename>\012                                    This file will be shown to users when\012                                    they want to download.\012\012   2.5.04   29-Mar-94 Improved    : After USER.SLOTNUMBER you can now enter\012                                    an argument, either NEVER or ALWAYS.\012                                    This way you can also grant users to\012                                    have override access to all restrictions\012                                    you may have put on other users. For\012                                    example: USER.2=ALWAYS, user #2 shall\012                                    always be able to download, no matter\012                                    what the restrictions in the D.info.\012                                    USER.2=NEVER means that he can NEVER\012                                    download.\012\012   2.5.02   26-Mar-94 Improved    : internal message will be shown unless\012                                    you specify NODE.FiLE, CONF.FiLE or\012                                    USER.FiLE in the icon. To show the in-\012                                    ternal message, simply delete that\012                                    tooltype entry (or put it between\012                                    brackets).\012\012                      New         : ConfScan_DL can now check for a baud-\012                                    rate per node. New tooltype:\012                                    BAUD.x=y - where x is node number and\012                                               y the minimum baud rate\012                                               (i.e. BAUD.0=9600).\012                                    *Requested by Pharaoh/SR*\012\012   2.5.01   25-Mar-94 Improved    : You can now also enter iNTERNAL after\012                                    NODE.FiLE, CONF.FiLE and USER.FiLE to\012                                    display an internal message instead of\012                                    a file.\012\012   2.5.00   25-Mar-94 New         : You can now exclude node''s conf''s and\012                                    even user''s from downloading. But also\012                                    allow certain users to download in/on\012                                    a conf/node. New tooltypes:\012                                    NODE.X=NO/ACSLEVEL/FiLENAME\012                                    CONF.X=NO/ACSLEVEL/FiLENAME\012                                    USER.X\012                                    NODE.FiLE=FiLENAME\012                                    CONF.FiLE=FiLENAME\012                                    USER.FiLE=FiLENAME\012                                    *Requested by Chaplin&Stony/PHUN*\012\012   2.4.00   10-Feb-94 Fixed       : Conference jumping bug fixed.\012\012   2.3.04   13-Jan-94 Improved    : ConfScan_DL is now a separate part of\012                                    the ConfScan package...\012@EndNode\012\012@Node Registration "Registration info - /X-PoWeR! - KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\012                    - - - ­ ­ ­ [ REGiSTRATiON ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   ConfScan may be considered FREE-WARE.  That means that you can do with\012   it  whatever you want, but DO NOT ALTER THE CODE, and YOU MAY NOT SELL\012   iT!\012\012   However,  special registered versions are available.  These version do\012   not differ from the (public) available versions except that registered\012   versions  notify  the user that it is in fact a registered version 8-)\012   Some  sysops  asked for one, so it now is possible.  Another advantage\012   is  that  you  will  most  likely  get  a  more  up to date version of\012   ConfScan.   ConfScan  is  always  under  development so by registering\012   yourself  you  will  get the most current version (plus updates if you\012   call regularly).\012\012                      - - - ­ ­ ­ [ SUPPORT ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   Only  major  updates/bugfixes  (like this one) will be released to the\012   masses,  however,  if you want to get updates on a regular basis (even\012   little fixes) you can register yourself and ask for the updates.\012\012   I  also  offer you support for ConfScan!  You can at Channel-X, or you\012   can  contact  me  via  internet,  AND ALL FOR NOTHiNG!  Here is how to\012   reach me:\012\012                    Channel-X      · +31-2290-62244\012                                     +31-2290-62535\012\012                    Last Outpost   · +31-7201-57682\012                                     +31-7202-01182\012\012                    Undiscovered   · +31-2294-4442\012                                     +31-2294-1442\012\012                                   Internet:\012                                   ~~~~~~~~~\012                         [email removed]\012\012\012   The only thing you WiLL NEVER EVER get is a ConfScan T-shirt... ;-)\012\012@EndNode\012\012@Node KiLLER "KiLLER - The New Way Of Nuking! - By KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\012                        - - - ­ ­ ­ [ KiLLER ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012                              YOUR DEADLY FRiEND!\012\012   KiLLER  is the new nuker that I am currently working on.  It will be a\012   totally  *NEW* way of nuking, no nuker is quite like it.  It will have\012   plenty  of  options  for  the  users,  a nice layout and ofcourse fast\012   performance.\012\012   KiLLER  can act like your average every day nuker (and that is exactly\012   how the currently spread versions work), but the new and coming KiLLER\012   will have some neat features:\012\012   ·  TRS,  Total Reverse System.  As a sysop you will be able to reverse\012   (undo) ANY action that has been performed with KiLLER.  KiLLER keeps a\012   log  that  records  all actions performed by KiLLER.  This way you can\012   easily undo any KiLLiNGS of cosysops and/or users.\012\012   ·  User  nuking!  Users are often the ones who tell you what files are\012   fake/lame/old/etc.   So  why  not  let them place comments in the file\012   directory  (dirx)?  KiLLER will let users KiLL files in the sense that\012   they  can  place  a comment, but will not actually deduct credits from\012   the uploader or remove the file.  When you, as sysop, start KiLLER the\012   next  time you will be informed of any user KiLLiNG and you can decide\012   wether this is a valid KiLLiNG or not.\012\012   · Fully GUi!  KiLLER will come with a GUi for the sysop, just like the\012   Config  program  of  ConfScan!   This will make KiLLiNG as easy and as\012   funny as playing BombMan!  But this will be made AFTER there is a full\012   and  working version of KiLLER/Ami-Express.  So this will take a while\012   (fall 94 I guess).\012\012   ·   Total  configuration  for  both  sysops  and  users  with  KiLLiNG\012   privileges.  Every question that KiLLER will ask can be pre-configured\012   so  you  can walk through KiLLER with [return]s as all default answers\012   are configurable.  Quiting will also be possible from any question!\012\012   ·  Logfile creator for logging all uploads and/or KiLLiNGS.  This will\012   speed  up  things  significantly!   At the moment KiLLER is capable of\012   reading BossNuke logfile, but this will (ofcourse) change.\012\012   ·  File moving ANYWHERE you want.  You will be able to move files from\012   ANY  dir  to  ANY  conference  in  ANY  dir,  or  copy  them  to other\012   conferences.  You name it, KiLLER can do it.\012\012              - - - ­ ­ ­ [ WHEN WiLL iT BE READY? ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   The  new  KiLLER  will  hopefully  be  ready this year, but due to the\012   enormous  extent  of the powers of KiLLER, it may well be that it will\012   not   be   ready   until  next  year  (really).   But  don''t  despair,\012   beta-version  will  be  put  out  to  selected  sysops,  so if you are\012   interested, contact your local MYSTiC board now (or contact me)!\012\012        - - - ­ ­ ­ [ WHAT GOOD DOES iT DO FOR ME KNOW? ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   At  this  point you have no benefit from it, asides from the fact that\012   you  can  start  a nuker from ConfScan (simply call it ''Killer'').  But\012   ConfScan is already capable of marking files to be ''KiLLED'' later on.\012\012   In the mean time, be patient, enjoy ConfScan and take care...\012\012@EndNode\012\012@Node SysopCommands "Special Sysop Commands - © 1994 KiLLraVeN/MYSTiC"\012                    - - - ­ ­ ­ [ ALL COMMANDS ] ­ ­ ­ - - -\012\012   Here  is a brief list of ALL arguments that ConfScan recognizes.  Some\012   arguments  require a certain access level, if not given, all users can\012   use the arguments.\012\012\012   N.B.:   The ''N'' command and ''CS'' command parse arguments the same way,\012   so  every  example  I give for ''N'' can also be applied to ''CS'' (unless\012   specified different).\012\012   <date> - N 06-26-94\012   ~~~~~~\012   This  will  make  ConfScan  search the current conference for the date\012   ''06-26-94''  in  the  upload  directory.   If  there  is  no  directory\012   specified, the upload dir file will be the default.\012\012   <-x>   - N -5\012   ~~~~\012   ConfScan  will  search  the  current conference for the date five days\012   back from TODAY.  So you can also read it as "show me the new files of\012   the last 5 days." And again in the upload dir file.\012\012   <S>    - N S\012   ~~~\012   This  is  the  normal  ''S''  argument  (Since  last  on).  It will make\012   ConfScan  search  for  the  date that the user was last on the system.\012   And in the upload dir file.\012\012   <T>    - N T\012   ~~~\012   The T comes from Today.  The date to search for will be set to today''s\012   date.   Needless  to  say this is done in the upload dir file although\012   you can specify another dir file.\012\012\012   <U>   - N S U\012   ~~~\012   The dir file to search in, is now set to the upload dir file.\012\012   <A>   - F A or N -10 A\012   ~~~\012   All dir files will be taken into account when searching for a date.\012\012   <H>   - CS H or N -5 H\012   ~~~\012   The hold dir file will be scanned for the given date.\012\012   <x>   - N 5 U or F 3\012   ~~~\012   The  ''x''  stands  for  any number and represents the number of the dir\012   file that will be the target to search the date in.\012\012\012   <NS>  - N S U NS or F A NS\012   ~~~~\012   NonStop  display  of  all  the  files,  no prompt will be given and no\012   pauses between conferences.  You will be able to break it with CTRL-C.\012\012\012   <+>   - CS +\012   ~~~\012   This  argument only works with the CS command.  If, after scanning, in\012   more  than  1  conference new files were found, a small report will be\012   displayed  on  screen  telling you how many bytes/files were upload in\012   the conferences with new files.  If there was only ONE conference with\012   new  files,  the  report  will  not be generated since you can see the\012   stats in the final bar when CS exits.\012\012   Not  every  user  can use this option, only users with Hold access (or\012   higher) can do this.\012\012\012   <A> or <G>  - N S G or N S A A\012   ~~~~~~~~~~\012   This  will  force  the  ''N''  command  to  act like ''CS''.  It will make\012   ConfScan  go  in  Multiple  Conference  mode.   In  other  words,  all\012   conferences will be scanned for new files.\012\012\012   All  of  these  arguments  can  be  combined, here are some daily used\012   examples:\012\012   CS NS +  - Scan  all dirs in all conferences for new files,  show them\012              nonstop and generate a report with the upload bytes/files.\012\012   CS T     - Scan  all  dirs in all conferences for new files,  uploaded\012              today.\012\012   CS -5 H  - What files were upload in the hold dirs the last 5 days?\012\012   N -5 NS  - Show  me  all  files  from  the last 5 days nonstop of this\012              conference (current conference).\012\012   F A NS   - Give me all files of all dirs NonStop.\012\012   N S G    - This is the same as ''CS'', it will show you  all  new  files\012              since  your  last  logon  from all upload dirs and from all\012              conferences.\012\012   N S A G  - This  is  the  same as ''CS A'', it will scan all dirs in all\012              conferences for new files since the last logon.\012@EndNode\012','\012',char(10)),'{"ACCESS":"100","LOCATION":"<path>''"}','auto-added',275548,5,0,NULL,NULL,'mst_cs26','scan',1780048619);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mst_csf2','MST-CSF2.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MST-CSF2.LHA','ConfScan_DL','XIM','ConfScan_DL',NULL,NULL,'MST','________   ____     ________/__\_ _______ _\__  _  \__\  /__ _/ __/_ _   /_/_\__   / /   /  /   /  _/  /_\__   / \  /  \_ _/__/_',replace('                                /\          \n   ________   ____     ________/__\_ _______\n  _\__  _  \__\  /__ _/ __/_ _   /_/_\__   /\n /   /  /   /  _/  /_\__   / \  /  \_ _/__/_\n/   /  / __/___   /   _/  /   \/    / \    /\n\__/__/__\    /  /_______/_____\___/______/|\n`---------\_____/-( aMi-X )-----------Rpd!-''\n       fiX fOR tHE mST-CS26.LHA fiLE!       \n  bOTH cONFsCAN_DL & cONFsCAN_G aRE fiXED!  \n','\n',char(10)),'Dago.TXT',replace(' .=[*][+][*][+]`=[*][+][*][+]`=[*][+][*][+]`=[*][+][*][+]`=[*][+][*][+][*]=.\n[*    | __                                                      __  |    *]\n +]   ; \/+-=->   NoW cAlL tHe OrGaNiZeD CrIme cAlL fAsT   <-=-+\/  ;   [+\n[*    >>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>DAGOBERTS-REVANGE<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<<     *]\n `-=>         :                :   BBS                        :Dagobert<=-`\n >>>> //////////////////////////////\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\ <<<<<<<\n .-=> <-+-:AmIgA 2000 -8MB- 700 Mb OnLiNe - 68030/28MhZ - CoOl:-+->    <=-`\n[*    \\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\\//////////////////////////////       *]\n[+    *YoUr OpErAtOrS aRe: Dagobert - cosy:TKK/Butthead/Blackcat *       +]\n[+    *        For other Conferences :.....................      *       +]\n[+    *                  Right hand is :TKK                      *       +]\n[+    ************************************************************       +]\n[+    \               NoDe0 +49 208-ask-ask  16.8 Zyxel          /       +]\n*]     \              NoDe1 +49 208-ask-ask  14.4 USR-D.S       /        [*\n+]      \             NoDe2 +49 208-ask-ask  16.8 Zyxel        /         [+\n+]       \            Node3 +49 208-ask-ask  ||:| V32bis      /          [+\n+]        \           Node4 +49 208-!!!-!!!  PRIVAT          /           ]+\n[+         **************************************************            +]\n+]        /    AMIGA-TOOLS-PORNO-X/Tools-CONSOLE-PEEeCEEe    \           [+\n[+       ------------------------------------------------------          +]\n+]        \________________JUST_FOR_FUN_!!___________________/           [+\n+[    ===============================================================    +]\n+]    """""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""    +]\n[+   .:-*- AsK onLy ElItEs foR da NuMber aNd tHe SyStem PasSword -*-:.   +]\n+]    """""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""""    +]\n[+    ===============================================================    [+\n *]_  _  _  _    _  _  _  _    _  _  _  _    _  _  _  _    _  _  _  _  _[*\n.=[*][+][*][+]`=[*][+][*][+]`=[*][+][*][+]`=[*][+][*][+]`=[*][+][*][+][*]=.\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',38670,9,0,NULL,NULL,'mst_csf2','scan',1780048619);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mst_csfx','MST-CSFX.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MST-CSFX.LHA','ConfScan_DL','XIM','ConfScan_DL',NULL,'KLR/mST','MST','______  ___\__   /_____________/_ \_________ \____ \/ ____/ _/   / ____/   _ /__/____   / _/   \  /   \___   /___  \_   \/   \_ _/__/_',replace('           _______              /\          \n______  ___\__   /_____________/_ \_________\n\____ \/ ____/ _/   / ____/   _ /__/____   /\n_/   \  /   \___   /___  \_   \/   \_ _/__/_\n\     \/     / /  /  _/   /   |     / \    /\n|\ ___||____/____/_______/____|____/_____ /|\n`-\/------( aMi-X ^ diViSiOn )------Rpd!\/-''\ncONFsCAN_DL aND cONFsCAN_G uPDATE by KLR/mST\n (uSE mST-CS26.LHA fOR a cOMPLETE cONFsCAN) \n','\n',char(10)),'ConfScan_DL.2603.ReadMe',replace('                         _________\n            _____  ______\___  __/_____________________ __________\n           _\____\/____.    /  \  _______________   /__))   .____/__\n           \     \/    |_  /  _/\______  \_     \__/   \_   l      /\n            \____||    |/_____\___________/______\______/_________/\n                  l____|-Mo!\n\n                          ^-[  ConfScan_DL uPDATE! ]-^\n\n   Murphy struck again! Three hours before the official release date,\n   a bug was discovered in the ConfScan_DL door, damn! It''s not a big\n   bug, but a bug is a bug. (Period).\n   \n   The  bug was,  that if you had files flagged with ConfScan and you\n   would  enter  a  few filenames after the `D'' command, the internal\n   `D'' command would not be started...  <sigh>... I fixed it ofcourse\n   and I hope you didn''t even notice it ;-)\n\n   For those of you who hate reading big docs and/or update files:\n\n   o This version allows users to manually remove their outstanding\n     files (remaining flagged files) with the ''-r'' option.\n\n   o Don''t forget to put ''CS_Location=<path>'' in your D.info!\n\n   To  install  it,  simply  copy  it  over the old ConfScan_DL after\n   installation with the script that came with MST-CS26.LHA!\n\n                       That''s it! Enjoy the new ConfScan!\n\n                              ø KiLLraVeN/mYSTiC ø\n                          ( Sat Aug 27 17:21:05 1994 )\n','\n',char(10)),'{"LOCATION":"<path>''"}','auto-added',28556,4,0,NULL,NULL,'mst_csfx','scan',1780048619);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('mst_dmex','MST-DMEX.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/MST-DMEX.LHA','DMSDescript','XIM','DMSDescript',NULL,NULL,'MST','+---/    \ \/ / __/_  __/ / __/------------+ |--/ / / /\  /\  /-/ /-/ / /---Re/Y\o------| |--\/ / /-/ /\  /-/ /-/ /\ \----Mystic-----|',replace('     ______  __________________\n+---/    \ \/ / __/_  __/ / __/------------+\n|--/ / / /\  /\  /-/ /-/ / /---Re/Y\o------|\n|--\/ / /-/ /\  /-/ /-/ /\ \----Mystic-----|\n+---\/\/--\/--\/--\/--\/--\/-----/X-DeSign-+\n| DMSDescript 1.1 & EXEDescript 1.0 Utils  |\n|   Adding, Deleting, Viewing, Changing    |\n| File_ID.Diz To A DMS-Archive Or An Exe-  |\n|  File ! Can Be Used For Any Executable!  |\n+------------------------------------------+\n','\n',char(10)),'DMS-EXEDescript.guide',replace('@database DMSDescript-EXEDescriptDoc\n\nCopyright (C) 1993 TekLords/Mystic/X-DeSign, Belgium, LI\nAll Rights Reserved\n\n@Remark $VER: Version V1.0 (Jan 13 1994, 14:24:21)\n@Remark AmigaGuide database for the DMSDescript-EXEDescript Documentation\n\n@node MAIN "DMSDescript-EXEDescript AmigaGuide Document (C) 1993 TekLords/Mystic/X-DeSign (Jan 13 1994, 14:24:21)"\n\n                                :                                          \n   ________               :     ¦                    /\\                    \n   \\       \\  ____________¦    _|_ ___________ _____/_ \\_ _ __________ __ _\n    \\______ \\/ __ _ _/    |    \\\\\\\\\\_       /\\\\\\_    /__/\\\\\\\\__      //_///\n     /     \\  /     \\     |    _/   /______/     _  /   \\    _/     /      \n   _/       \\/       \\_____   _\\______    \\_      \\/     \\_  \\_____/\\_     \n   \\        ||        /   /   \\      /     /      |       /          /     \n    \\ ______||______ /_________\\_________ /_______|_____ /_________ /      \n     \\/            \\/                   \\/             \\/     Rpd!\\/ \n                              (MYSTiC/X-DeSiGN) \n\n\n              .: C O N T E N T S  O F  D O C U M E N T A T I O N :.\n              ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n                         @{"        Introduction        " Link Part01}\n                         @{"        Requirements        " Link Part02}\n                         @{"   How To Use These Utils   " Link Part03}\n                         @{"         Greetings          " Link Part04}\n\n                Docs done by @{" Re/Y\o/TekLords/Mystic/X-DeSign " Link Diabolo}.\n                       Install And Enjoy The Program ...\n@endnode\n@node Part01 "Introduction To DMSDescript-EXEDescript by Re/Y\o/TLS/MST "\n\n                              .: Introduction :.\n                              ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nWell it is very easy ... DMSDescript-EXEDescript can be used to make life\neasier for the once that want to add, remove, extract the FileDescription to\nDMS-Archives and to EXEcutables ... They can be used from Shell,\nDiskmaster2.x, DirOpus, or any other DirUtil ...\n\n@endnode\n@node Part02 "Requirements"\n\n                              .: Requirements :.\n                              ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nAll you need is an ©Amiga, DMSDescript, EXEDescript ... Some Archives ...\nIf you find any BUGS or have some SUGGESTIONS please leave me a messy ... You\nwill most certainly be able to find me at @{" Diabolo " Link Diabolo}.\n\n\n@endnode\n@node Part03 "How To Install DMSDescript-EXEDescript by Re/Y\o/TLS/MST"\n\n                            .:Installation Guide:.\n                            ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nThe Program runs on most amiga configurations ... there shouldn''t be much\nlimitations ... except not enough diskspace ... not enough ram ... but it\ndoesn''t consume much itself ... it''s just the archives that might consume\nsome space ...\nJust copy the programs where you like them to be and where they can be found\nby FileID v1.3+ ...\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nDMSDescript v1.1 By Re/Y\\o(/Y\\ystic/X-DeSign)\n\n\nUsage: DMSDescript <a|x|d> [<Description>] <DMS Archive>\n       a Add FileDescription\n       x Extract FileDescription\n       d Delete FileDescription\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nEXEDescript v1.0 By Re/Y\\o(/Y\\ystic/X-DeSign)\n\n\nUsage: EXEDescript <a|x|d> [<Description>] <Executable>\n       a Add FileDescription\n       x Extract FileDescription\n       d Delete FileDescription\n\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nThe Description will only be used in case of ''a'' and ''x'' i.e. Add a description\nto an archive or extract it from one ...\n\nThere is not much to say about it ... just that the description does not need\nto be named File_ID.Diz ... doesn''t matter what name it has ...\n\n@endnode\n@node Part04 "Greetings To EveryOne"\n\n\n\n               First Of All I Want To Greet Some Betatesters ...\n\n                               @{"     Andi/MST     " Link Diabolo}\n                               @{"     Spy/MST      " Link Paralysis}\n                               @{"    SieGel/MST    " Link Diabolo}\n                               @{" Genghis Khan/TLS " Link WOK}\n                               @{"       Uli        " Link FlyingSaucer}\n                               @{"     Scorpio      " Link LastDesire}\n                               @{"    Ken & Ryu     " Link ShotokanPalace}\n                               @{"      Pigeon      " Link Universe}\n\n               Yankee Rose           -=+=- /\\ltern/\\te Re/\\ality\n               ARGON/MST             -=+=- *||MATROSE ARGON||*\n               Foxx''n''Lynxx          -=+=- </\\/> ZigZag Corp <\\/\\>\n               - GALAXY -            -=+=- Call ULIXYS BBS (ISDN)\n               STB                   -=+=- NoWHeRe\n               RHYS/FAIRLIGHT        -=+=- > > F A I R L I G H T < <\n               Mike                  -=+=- GL0BAL CHA0S BBS\n               [-AmiCom/PDX]         -=+=- SKARA BRAE ISDN\n               SPEEDLOCK             -=+=- Lighthouse 6 NDS -THHG-\n               THE SiLENCER/TRSi     -=+=- »»»[ T R S i ]«««\n                THE CHAMP            -=+=- <*>RANDOM ACCESS<*>\n               dR.dRE!               -=+=- -=====Faith=====-\n               FuZzY/MsT             -=+=- (MySTiC /X-DeSiGN)\n               DELTAFORCE            -=+=- // MEN-TEL BBS //\n               SATAN                 -=+=- {SHINING 8}\n               EMPiRE                -=+=- -÷M÷Y÷S÷T÷i÷C÷-\n               [-bObO-]              -=+=- [» MYSTiC/X-DESiGN «]\n\n                               @{"      Amiga       " Link Amiga}\n\n               Secondly All The Members Of Mystic & TekLords ...\n\n                                 @{"    Mystic    " Link Mystic}\n                                 @{"   TekLords   " Link TekLords}\n\n                            And Last But Not Least ...\n\n        All Ex- And Still-Members Of AFL That I Have Met Over The Years...\n\n        Don''t Shoot Me If I Forgot You ... There Are So Many People I Have\n        To Thank For Testing ... That I Probably Forgot To Mention Here ...\n\n@endnode\n@node Diabolo  "Diabolo -=- Mystic/X-DeSign WHQ -=-"\n\n\n                        ·  :                 .     :     :\n-============-   \\____ ¬V ¬V___ ¬V___ ¬V___ ¬V ¬|  |___ ¬|   MANAGEMENT\n (Mystic/X-Design)| ¬|  |  | ¬|  | ¬|  | ¬|  |  |  | ¬|  |   -========-\n      WHQ         |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |   ANDi/MST\n-============-    |  |  |  |     |    _|  |  |  |__|  |  |   SPY/MST\n                  |  |  |  |  |  |  | ¬|  |  |  | ¬|  |  |   FELDMAN\n-ELiTE oNLY-      |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |   FuZzY/MsT\n                  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |   Wolfmann/TRSI\nCALL US NoW FoR   |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |   (-FaZ! & tERMi-)\nTHE NEWEST AMiGA/ |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |     -====-\nPCSTUFF           |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |