\n\nBlade/NoCrack                                      @{" Main Menu " Link main}\n@endnode\n@node t2 " Requirements"\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nLHACHECK requires:\n\n - Kick2.0 or higher\n - LHA1.5 or higher\n - an LHA/LHZ archive to test :)\n\n\n\n That''s it!                                          @{" Main Menu " Link main}\n@endnode\n@node t3 " Installation "\n\nFILES NEEDED :\n¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\nLHACHECK        The Program itselfs must be in the C: Directory\n\nLHA.KILL        List of TextNames followed by <CR>\n                These BBS Ads will be removed from the archive\n                (WildCards permitted)\n\nLHA.ADD         List of TextNames followed by <CR>\n                These BBS Ads will be added to the archive\n                (WildCards permitted)\n\n\nINSTALLATION IN /X :\n¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\nCopy LHA.INFO/LZH.INFO/LZA.INFO/RUN.INFO/SFX.INFO in your FCheck Directory\n(normally BBS:FCHECK)\nIf you only got /X2.xx use LHACHECK as any other LHA/LZH-Checker\n(NO CHECKOPTIONS! Only Checker=C:LHACHECK)\n\n\nINSTALLATION IN FASTCALL :\n¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\nIn Fastcall you have to insert following line in\n"MB:BOXDATEN/UPLOAD.BAT":\n\n LHACHECK $LF KILL\n\n\nINSTALLATION IN OTHER BBS-SYSTEMS :\n¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\nLook in your BBS-Manual how to install an extern program.\nFor BBS-Systems that doesn''t check LHA/LZH-Checker text output, i have\ninserted the "KILL"-Option which will delete the file if its corrupt.\n\n\nCLI-USAGE:      LHACHECK <archive> [KILL]\n\n\nThat''s all!                                          @{" Main Menu " Link main}\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',11064,3,0,NULL,NULL,'nc_lchk','scan',1780048634);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('nchat11','NCHAT11.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/NCHAT11.LHA','NodeSysopChat','XIM','NodeSysopChat',NULL,'Spy/tRSi',NULL,'\_____ \___  \___  \/  __ \  \   _____/\ \\____   /  /  / _/___  \/  /\ ____/\\/ \\___ /  /     /\__/  /  / /___/\\/',replace(' ___________________  __________________\n \_____ \___  \___  \/  __ \  \   _____/\\n  \\____   /  /  / _/___  \/  /\ ____/\\/\n    \\___ /  /     /\__/  /  / /___/\\/\n      \__/__/__/__/\_____/__/ /\___\/\n         \\_\\_\\_\/\____\\_\/  NL\n                 PRESENTS\n                NChat V1.1ß\n     A /X-iNNOVATiON TOOL BY Spy/tRSi\n    WHICH ALLOWS A  SYSOP CHAT BETWEEN\n   2 NODES, SAME AS THE F1 CONSOLE CHAT\n    WITH DROPPING CARRIER ON THE OTHER\n                  NODE !\n','\n',char(10)),'NodeSysopChat.english.doc',replace('\n                  NodeSysopChat V1.1ß (c) by Spy/tRSi&ILa\n                      translated by Cindarella/SR&ILa\n\n\n    For questions and ideas:\n\n    p/\R/\LySiS:  Node 1-3 : +49 (0)30 721 60 71 - USR DUAL V.FAST 28800\n                  Node 4   : +49 (0)30 722 60 65 - USR DUAL V.FAST 28800\n\n\n    Did you ever get nerves, that it`s only possible to get somebody in \n    the chat by the console ? Don`t worry...Now you have NCHAT !!!\n\n\n    NCHAT is a tool, which allows (Co-) Sysops to chat from one node to \n    another. "YES" that`s right !!! NCHAT emulates the possibility to \n    start a Sysop-Chat from another node, as like as the Sysop is sitting\n    in front of the console and pushes F1. That it works, you need several\n    nodes. :)\n\n\n    NCHAT gives you the possibility to start NCHAT whenever you want \n    (as long as a user is online). You can also drop a user out the bbs,\n    as like as the (Co-) Sysop is sitting in front the console. The user,\n    that you want to chat with, must call via modem. It`s not possible to\n    use NCHAT with local nodes. That`s not useful, because in this case you \n    you have still the "operator page". :)\n    I`m still working on the "Account-Editing", that`s why this is "only"\n    a ß-version.\n\n\n    NCHAT is easy to install. Just put the 3 files "NodeSysopChat",\n    "NodeSysopChat.start.txt" and "NodeSysopChat.end.txt" in a directory.\n    Install "NodeSysopChat" as a XIM-Door, and change the 2 text files\n    "NodeSysopChat.start.txt" and "NodeSysopChat.end.txt" like you want\n    and now start it. :)\n\n\n    "NodeSysopChat.start.txt" is shown at the beginning from NCHAT,\n    "NodeSysopChat.end.txt" at the end from NCHAT, also like startchat.txt\n    and endchat.txt at the normal sysopchat. Both text-files must stand\n    in the same directory then the door. In the file "NodeSysopChat.start.txt"\n    you can see with the symbol "§" at the beginning of the chat the name of\n    the (Co-) Sysop, which just used NCHAT.\n\n\n    If you are in the chat, you have 2 commands. With CTRL-C you can end the\n    chat. CTRL-F shows you more functions.\n\n    \n    1. D - With "D" you can drop a user on another node\n\n    2. E - That is going to be the account-editing\n\n    3. S - Gives you the possibility to do something in the bbs between\n           you are still in the chat. During this time the use is on ice.\n\n    4. Q - With "Q" you can quit the menue\n\n\n    Other functions will follow in the other versions, because I have to do \n    something in the future.\n\n\n    So, I think that`s all what you have to know about NCHAT....\n    Have fun and in case if you find mistakes or if you have new ideas,\n    please call my bbs.\n\n\n\n                                    F.O.R.\n\n         _______  _______  _______  _______  _______\n               / /      / /      / /      / /      /   /\n              / /      / /      / /      / /      /   /                   _______\n      _______/ /______/ /______/ /      / /      /   /_______  ________  /\n     /        /      / /      / /      / /      /   /       / /       / /______\n    /        /      / /      / /      / /      /   /       / /       /        /\n   /_______ /______/ /______/ /______/ /______/   /_______/ /_______/ _______/\n                                                           /\n                                                          /\n                                                         /\n\n                                   C.A.L.L.\n\n\n     _______  ______ ______  ______  __      __  __ ________ _____ ________\n     \.  _ ~\|     ~|\.   ~\|     ~||.~|    |  || ~|\.     ~\\   ~\\.     ~\\n     |\\ ___/|  __ .||\\ __/|  __ .||| |    |  || .| \\ ____/|\  _/ \\ ____/\n     | \/\   |  __ |||.\/  ||  __ |||| |___ |_    || _\/_ .\ |.\/|  _\/_ .\\n     ||   \  |  || :||| |  ||  || :||: \  .\/ \__ ||/      \\||  | /      \\\n     |:___/  |__||_:||:_|__||__||__||:__\ //\_____:|\_______/|:__| \_______/\n      .            .  .              .   \/       .           .     -FuZzY-\n                                     .            .\n                   .  .                                       .\n     ·-----------> AMIEXPRESS V3.36 / AMIGA 3000 / 24 H ONLINE <-----------·\n     |                                                                     |\n     |                   U.S.Robotics V.FAST CLASS Rulez                   |\n     |                                                                     |\n     |      PORT             NUMBER   MODEM   SPEED      NODETYPE          |\n     ·---+-------------------------------------------------------------+---·\n       D | NODE 1: +49(0)30 721 6071 USR DUAL 28800 RINGDOWN NODE 1-3! | C\n       I | NODE 2: +49(0)30 721 6072 USR DUAL 28800 DIRECT LINE ACCESS | A\n       A | NODE 3: +49(0)30 721 6073 USR DUAL 28800 DIRECT LINE ACCESS | L\n       L | NODE 4: +49(0)30 722 6065 USR DUAL 28800 DIRECT LINE ACCESS | L\n     ·---+-------------------------------------------------------------+---·\n     |                                                                     |\n     |        G . I . V . E       I . T       A       R . I . N . G        |\n     |                                                                     |\n     ·--> SUPPORTING !PD-SOFTWARE ONLY! FOR: AMIGA, ATARI, IBM-PC & MAC <--·\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',19582,1,0,NULL,NULL,'nchat11','scan',1780048634);
