INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('netcon14','NETCON14.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/NETCON14.LHA',NULL,'XIM','NetControl.exe',NULL,'ThE',NULL,'Controls the whole /Xnet Transfers Done by ThE BiRD - /X Development Team. .------------------------------------------.',replace('  NetControl 1.04 -Utility- For 3.20+ only\n    Controls the whole /Xnet Transfers\n  Done by ThE BiRD - /X Development Team.\n.------------------------------------------.\n|/X Development Team - The Silent Achievers|\n|Utility for Ami-Express v3.20+&/XNet v5.1+|\n`------------------------------------------''\n UPDATE ONLY USEFULL FOR /XNet v5.1+ Users\n÷( ''nOTHA gREAT wARE fROM bUMBLE bEE lAND )÷','\n',char(10)),'NetControl.doc',replace('       .----------------------------------------------------------.\n       |       /X Net Controler V1.04 - Written by The Bird       |\n       |        /X Development Team - The Silent Achievers        |\n       `----------------------------------------------------------''\n\n                             UPDATE FROM v1.02\n\n                              DOCUMENTATION:\n                              ~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nWhat is NetControl for ?\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nFirst of all Netcontrol is a TOTAL replacement for the orginal /Xnet Scripts\nin your AMIXNET/SCRIPTS/ directory. This utility will solve ALL problems\nwith the daily /Xnet transfers. It will totally control your nettransfers,\nso this scripts will not look so unproffesional for AmiExpress.\n \nRequirements\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThe minimum requirements for running this Utility is a full installed \nAmiExpress v3.20+ and a fully installed /Xnet v5.1+ version. If you are not\na proud owner of this two things or if you are not registered now for /Xnet5.1\nthis utility will be totally useless for you, because many things changed in\nthe release of /Xnet v5.1+\n\nAdditional Requirements:\n-----------------------\nAmiExpress v3.20+                ->\nAcp Server v3.20+                ->\nNetPack v5.1+                    ->\nNetMerge v6.2+                   ->\nMRUpdate v1.8+                   -> if you don`t own one of this\nMSGReceipts v1.1+                -> Utilities with the correct\nTERM v2.9+                       -> version number or higher then\nTaskTime v1.1+                   -> this utility will not work 100%\nDisplayRoute v1.2+               -> get all Utilities before using it.\n\nOriginal WB Commandos needed:\n---------------------------- \nC:run\nC:dir\nC:delete\nC:copy\nC:Type\n\nFunctions\n~~~~~~~~~\nThe functions for this utility are very simple. First of all you have 2\ndifferent functions which this utility works on. You can start this utility\nso that it will call out for you every day at a specified time and will\ntransfer all mails automatically. And the second function is the MANUAL\nfunction. This one is for people which don`t want to let the computer call out\nbecause of high phonebills. So you can transfer mails when ever you want by\nhand and then this utility will convert all mails automatically into your\nmessagesbases.\n \nConfiguration\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThe configuration of this utility is very very easy. You just have to insert\nthe following syntax in your CLI:\n \n1> NetControl.exe CONFIG\n\nThen this utility will prompt you for inserting some informations about your\nconfigurated Express and /Xnet. Answer this question correctly step by step and\nyou will get no problem with the later automatically running of this program.\nYou will also be prompted for inserting information of the NETIDs you want to\ncall. If you are prompted for the phonenumber just insert the whole number\nwith the land & countrycode.\n \nThe other things in the configuration are very easy to manage.\n \nAutomatical CALLING:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nIf you want the NetControl automatically transfer netmails every day ,you just\nhave to start the NetControl once at your startup-sequence to be sure it`s\n100% running if your system crashs or you make a reset.\n\nGoto your favourite Texteditor and insert the following into your own\nstartup-sequence:\n \n------ cut here -------\nUTILS:NetControl.exe START\n------ cut here -------\n\nThis will initate the Tasktime at every RESET. In this example here\nit`s important to have the "NetControl.exe" program located in the UTILS:\ndirectory.\n\nFrom now on NetControl will suspend your choosen /Xnode at your favourite time\nyou inserted in the configuration. Then it will pack all needed netmails to\ntransfer and call all HostIds you inserted in the CONFIG. After the transfer\nit will decrunch(merge) all downloaded netmails from your HOST and will\nautomatically post it in the different Conferences. This procedure will be\nstarted again every day at the same time you choose in the Config.\n\nManual Transfers:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThis function was included because if you call out a HOST BBS which is far\naway from you which will result high phonebills.\nTo use this function you have to do the following step by step.\n \n1. Exit the /X Node you want to call out\n2. Take a Shell and start the NetControl program as follows:\n \n   1> NetControl.exe LOCAL\n\n3. Wait until NetControl will prompt you for transfering /XNetMails.\n4. Start now your favourite Terminalprogram.\n5. Call your HOST BBS you want to transfer mail.\n6. Wait until the prompt "ANSI Graphics (Y/n)?"\n7. Insert now "!--NET--!" or "@--NET--@" and press return\n8. Now you will be prompted to insert your NETID.\n9. Follow this prompt and insert your own NETID with the "@".\n10.Now you will prompted to insert your own NetPassword you choose for this\n   HOST BBS.\n11.Insert this password and wait until you will be prompted to press\n   return to receive the newest netmail.\n12.Receive your mail and then you will be prompted if you have netmail to\n   transfer or not.\n13.Transfer now all NetMailFiles NetControl will list you.\n14.If you are ready with uploading all Netmails just go back in the Shell \n   where NetControl was started and press return for telling NetControl that\n   you are ready with all Transfers.\n\nFrom now on NetControl will do all work alone and will post all netmessages in\nit`s conferences.\nIf you have a second or more HOST BBS`s Netcontrol will go to the next HOST BBS\nand will start at step 3 again.\n\nSingle-Host BBS calling\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nAnother included function is the Single BBS Calling. With this function you can\nchoose one HOST BBS you want to call automatical. This is usefull if this BBS\nwas busy at the specified time you called it autmatically.\n \nTo use this function you just have to open a shell and then insert the\nfollowing commands while /X is Awaiting Connect on that Node you choose at the\nNetControl Config.\n \n1> NetControl.exe <NetID>\n \nYou have to insert the whole netid with "@" instead of <NetID>. Then /X will \nstart suspending and call this BBS automatically.\n \nHelp-Screen\n~~~~~~~~~~~\nTo Open a help screen you have to start NetControl like this:\n \n1> NetControl.exe ?\n \nThen the following screen will appear:\n \n.----------------------------------------------------------.\n|       /X Net Controler v1.04 - Written by The Bird       |\n|        /X Development Team - The Silent Achievers        |\n`----------------------------------------------------------''\n\n This is a utility for AmiExpress 3.20+ & /XNet 5.1+ only!\n Copyright (c)`93 LightSpeed Technologies.\n\n Usage: NetControl [START]   - Initate TaskTime in Startup-Sequence\n        NetControl [CONFIG]  - Start the Configuration program\n        NetControl [LOCAL]   - Activate the manual Nettransfer\n        NetControl [@NETID]  - Allows you to call only ONE NETcontact\n\nThis screen will list all options you have with NetControl on one page.\n \nChanges to v1.01\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nAfter the v1.00 Release i found some bugs in the Manual Transfer Routine\nand so i have to release v1.01 were all bugs are removed and some\ncosmetic changes was made to the Manual Transfer. Now the Utility shows\nyou the Password, your NetID and wheter you have to transfer mail or not.\nHope you like that little improvements. For any further bug reports please\nwrite a message in the AX0001 Conference to The Bird@GR0004 and tell me\nall bugs.. or directly call my BBS +49-711-776380.\n\nChanges to v1.02\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nAfter the v1.01 release i found some major bugs in the manual transfer\nagain. I removed that bugs now and all should work fine. \n\nChanges to v1.04\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nAnd again fixed some bugs in the Utility and added some cosmentic changes\nand converted the code to the new /X v3.20+ standard /Xnet. A Major Bug\nwas removed which don`t transfer ALL Needed Netmails for Uploading to\nthe HOST BBS. NEED A NEW CONFIG !!!\n\nHistory & Greetings\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nAs a history i just want to say that the idea of this utility was born on the\nnerving SCRIPTS released with the /Xnet. I searched of a better way to manage\nthis transfers and i hopely found it.\n \nAnd i hope you like this Utility which is only usefull for the registered\n/Xnet v5.1+ users. But i think of an version for the older /Xnets.\n \nMy Greetings go out to many people, but as now i only want to name some:\n \nAndy of Fastway BBS\nJoseph Hodge (ByteMaster)\nThe Outlaw\n\nand to all BetaTesters and Distributors of AmiExpress.\n \nIf you are not a USER of AmiExpress and you want to register for it. Call the\nfollowing bbs`s in you local area. There you can get AmiExpress and it`s\nutilities.\n \n\n              The Last! Amiga BBS - USA ----- 1-305-456-0126\n              7th Heaven ---------- HOLLAND - +31-0703815656\n              Heart of Nowhere ---- ITALY --- +39-2-97291781\n              Image World --------- FINLAND -+358-71-2626775\n              Metal Decade -------- GERMANY - +49-711-776380\n              Global Chaos -------- GERMANY -- +49-8231-1068\n              The Addiction ------- GERMANY - +49-6102-31564\n\n\nThis program was written by the German Distributor & BetaTester "THE BIRD" \nwhichs BBS is called Metal Decade.\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',40370,6,0,NULL,NULL,'netcon14','scan',1780048634);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('netcon15','NETCON15.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/NETCON15.LHA',NULL,'XIM','NetControl.exe',NULL,'ThE',NULL,'Controls the whole /Xnet Transfers Done by ThE BiRD - /X Development Team. .------------------------------------------.',replace('  NetControl 1.05 -Utility- For 3.20+ only\n    Controls the whole /Xnet Transfers\n  Done by ThE BiRD - /X Development Team.\n.------------------------------------------.\n|/X Development Team - The Silent Achievers|\n|Utility for Ami-Express v3.20+&/XNet v5.1+|\n`------------------------------------------''\n  BUGFIXED and AUTOUPDATE FUNCTION ON !!!\n','\n',char(10)),'NetControl.doc',replace('       .----------------------------------------------------------.\n       |       /X Net Controler V1.05 - Written by The Bird       |\n       |        /X Development Team - The Silent Achievers        |\n       `----------------------------------------------------------''\n\n                             UPDATE FROM v1.04\n\n                              DOCUMENTATION:\n                              ~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nWhat is NetControl for ?\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nFirst of all Netcontrol is a TOTAL replacement for the orginal /Xnet Scripts\nin your AMIXNET/SCRIPTS/ directory. This utility will solve ALL problems\nwith the daily /Xnet transfers. It will totally control your nettransfers,\nso this scripts will not look so unproffesional for AmiExpress.\n \nRequirements\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThe minimum requirements for running this Utility is a full installed \nAmiExpress v3.20+ and a fully installed /Xnet v5.1+ version. If you are not\na proud owner of this two things or if you are not registered now for /Xnet5.1\nthis utility will be totally useless for you, because many things changed in\nthe release of /Xnet v5.1+\n\nAdditional Requirements:\n-----------------------\nAmiExpress v3.20+                ->\nAcp Server v3.20+                ->\nNetPack v5.1+                    ->\nNetMerge v6.2+                   ->\nMRUpdate v1.8+                   -> if you don`t own one of this\nMSGReceipts v1.1+                -> Utilities with the correct\nTERM v2.9+                       -> version number or higher then\nTaskTime v1.1+                   -> this utility will not work 100%\nDisplayRoute v1.2+               -> get all Utilities before using it.\n\nOriginal WB Commandos needed:\n---------------------------- \nC:run\nC:dir\nC:delete\nC:copy\nC:Type\n\nFunctions\n~~~~~~~~~\nThe functions for this utility are very simple. First of all you have 2\ndifferent functions which this utility works on. You can start this utility\nso that it will call out for you every day at a specified time and will\ntransfer all mails automatically. And the second function is the MANUAL\nfunction. This one is for people which don`t want to let the computer call out\nbecause of high phonebills. So you can transfer mails when ever you want by\nhand and then this utility will convert all mails automatically into your\nmessagesbases.\n \nConfiguration\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThe configuration of this utility is very very easy. You just have to insert\nthe following syntax in your CLI:\n \n1> NetControl.exe CONFIG\n\nThen this utility will prompt you for inserting some informations about your\nconfigurated Express and /Xnet. Answer this question correctly step by step and\nyou will get no problem with the later automatically running of this program.\nYou will also be prompted for inserting information of the NETIDs you want to\ncall. If you are prompted for the phonenumber just insert the whole number\nwith the land & countrycode.\n \nThe other things in the configuration are very easy to manage.\n \nAutomatical CALLING:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nIf you want the NetControl automatically transfer netmails every day ,you just\nhave to start the NetControl once at your startup-sequence to be sure it`s\n100% running if your system crashs or you make a reset.\n\nGoto your favourite Texteditor and insert the following into your own\nstartup-sequence:\n \n------ cut here -------\nUTILS:NetControl.exe START\n------ cut here -------\n\nThis will initate the Tasktime at every RESET. In this example here\nit`s important to have the "NetControl.exe" program located in the UTILS:\ndirectory.\n\nFrom now on NetControl will suspend your choosen /Xnode at your favourite time\nyou inserted in the configuration. Then it will pack all needed netmails to\ntransfer and call all HostIds you inserted in the CONFIG. After the transfer\nit will decrunch(merge) all downloaded netmails from your HOST and will\nautomatically post it in the different Conferences. This procedure will be\nstarted again every day at the same time you choose in the Config.\n\nManual Transfers:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThis function was included because if you call out a HOST BBS which is far\naway from you which will result high phonebills.\nTo use this function you have to do the following step by step.\n \n1. Exit the /X Node you want to call out\n2. Take a Shell and start the NetControl program as follows:\n \n   1> NetControl.exe LOCAL\n\n3. Wait until NetControl will prompt you for transfering /XNetMails.\n4. Start now your favourite Terminalprogram.\n5. Call your HOST BBS you want to transfer mail.\n6. Wait until the prompt "ANSI Graphics (Y/n)?"\n7. Insert now "!--NET--!" or "@--NET--@" and press return\n8. Now you will be prompted to insert your NETID.\n9. Follow this prompt and insert your own NETID with the "@".\n10.Now you will prompted to insert your own NetPassword you choose for this\n   HOST BBS.\n11.Insert this password and wait until you will be prompted to press\n   return to receive the newest netmail.\n12.Receive your mail and then you will be prompted if you have netmail to\n   transfer or not.\n13.Transfer now all NetMailFiles NetControl will list you.\n14.If you are ready with uploading all Netmails just go back in the Shell \n   where NetControl was started and press return for telling NetControl that\n   you are ready with all Transfers.\n\nFrom now on NetControl will do all work alone and will post all netmessages in\nit`s conferences.\nIf you have a second or more HOST BBS`s Netcontrol will go to the next HOST BBS\nand will start at step 3 again.\n\nSingle-Host BBS calling\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nAnother included function is the Single BBS Calling. With this function you can\nchoose one HOST BBS you want to call automatical. This is usefull if this BBS\nwas busy at the specified time you called it autmatically.\n \nTo use this function you just have to open a shell and then insert the\nfollowing commands while /X is Awaiting Connect on that Node you choose at the\nNetControl Config.\n \n1> NetControl.exe <NetID>\n \nYou have to insert the whole netid with "@" instead of <NetID>. Then /X will \nstart suspending and call this BBS automatically.\n \nHelp-Screen\n~~~~~~~~~~~\nTo Open a help screen you have to start NetControl like this:\n \n1> NetControl.exe ?\n \nThen the following screen will appear:\n \n.----------------------------------------------------------.\n|       /X Net Controler v1.05 - Written by The Bird       |\n|        /X Development Team - The Silent Achievers        |\n`----------------------------------------------------------''\n\n This is a utility for AmiExpress 3.20+ & /XNet 5.1+ only!\n Copyright (c)`93 LightSpeed Technologies.\n\n Usage: NetControl [START]   - Initate TaskTime in Startup-Sequence\n        NetControl [CONFIG]  - Start the Configuration program\n        NetControl [LOCAL]   - Activate the manual Nettransfer\n        NetControl [@NETID]  - Allows you to call only ONE NETcontact\n\nThis screen will list all options you have with NetControl on one page.\n \nChanges to v1.01\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nAfter the v1.00 Release i found some bugs in the Manual Transfer Routine\nand so i have to release v1.01 were all bugs are removed and some\ncosmetic changes was made to the Manual Transfer. Now the Utility shows\nyou the Password, your NetID and wheter you have to transfer mail or not.\nHope you like that little improvements. For any further bug reports please\nwrite a message in the AX0001 Conference to The Bird@GR0004 and tell me\nall bugs.. or directly call my BBS +49-711-776380.\n\nChanges to v1.02\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nAfter the v1.01 release i found some major bugs in the manual transfer\nagain. I removed that bugs now and all should work fine. \n\nChanges to v1.04\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nAnd again fixed some bugs in the Utility and added some cosmentic changes\nand converted the code to the new /X v3.20+ standard /Xnet. A Major Bug\nwas removed which don`t transfer ALL Needed Netmails for Uploading to\nthe HOST BBS. NEED A NEW CONFIG !!!\n\nChanges to v1.05\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nFixed several Bugs and included the new "AUTOUPDATE" in the MRUpdate\nexecution, that will fix problems with the BBS:AMIXNET/<NetiD>/<NetConf>.bin\nfiles some people don`t know. But make sure to start MRUpdate one time with\nthe AUTOUPDATE option on.\n\nHistory & Greetings\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nAs a history i just want to say that the idea of this utility was born on the\nnerving SCRIPTS released with the /Xnet. I searched of a better way to manage\nthis transfers and i hopely found it.\n \nAnd i hope you like this Utility which is only usefull for the registered\n/Xnet v5.1+ users. But i think of an version for the older /Xnets.\n \nMy Greetings go out to many people, but as now i only want to name some:\n \nAndy of Fastway BBS\nJoseph Hodge (ByteMaster)\nThe Outlaw\n\nand to all BetaTesters and Distributors of AmiExpress.\n \nIf you are not a USER of AmiExpress and you want to register for it. Call the\nfollowing bbs`s in you local area. There you can get AmiExpress and it`s\nutilities.\n \n\n              The Last! Amiga BBS - USA ----- 1-305-456-0126\n              7th Heaven ---------- HOLLAND - +31-0703815656\n              Heart of Nowhere ---- ITALY --- +39-2-97291781\n              Image World --------- FINLAND -+358-71-2626775\n              Metal Decade -------- GERMANY - +49-711-776380\n              Global Chaos -------- GERMANY -- +49-8231-1068\n              The Addiction ------- GERMANY - +49-6102-31564\n\n\nThis program was written by the German Distributor & BetaTester "THE BIRD" \nwhichs BBS is called Metal Decade.\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',31764,3,0,NULL,NULL,'netcon15','scan',1780048634);
