INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ns__ss10','NS!-SS10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/NS!-SS10.LHA','Logoff','XIM','Logoff',NULL,'NiGHTSHADE/iNS^DPL','NS!','|  [sMARTSHOw V1.0] BY NiGHTSHADE/iNS^DPL  | | DiSPLAYS A TXT, REQ CFG & FAST-RELIABLE! | |  RELEASED 18-JAN-95 20:56 AT WASTELANDS  |',replace('.------------------------------------------.\n|  [sMARTSHOw V1.0] BY NiGHTSHADE/iNS^DPL  |\n| DiSPLAYS A TXT, REQ CFG & FAST-RELIABLE! |\n|  RELEASED 18-JAN-95 20:56 AT WASTELANDS  |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'SmartShow10R1.guide',replace('@database "NSDoor"\n\n@Node Main "Door"\n@Title "Manual By NiGHTSHADE/iNS^DpL          Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n\n\nSmartShow V1.0 [RELEASE 1] Amiga-Guide manual\nCopyright (c) 1995 By NiGHTSHADE/InS^DpL\n\n @{" What is this Door     " Link "What"}\n @{" Archive Contents      " Link "Archive"}\n @{" Door Usage            " Link "Usage"}\n @{" Door Installations    " Link "Install"}\n @{" Door Beta Crew        " Link "Beta"}\n @{" Program History       " Link "History"}\n @{" The Greetings         " Link "Greetings"}\n @{" Contact NiGHTSHADE    " Link "ContactNS"}\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "What"\n@Title "What is SmartShow                     Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n\n SmartShow is a door developed to display a TXT file eg.\n like a door list or a member list for a group.\n it will bring the following to youre system :\n\n   * Simple configurator (Just use from CLI!).\n   * Request selector for the TXT file to show.\n   * Fast Statestics function (Displays No. of usages).\n   * Reliable & Fast.\n   * Works on ALL OS and CPU''s (If not - Contact me).\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Archive"\n@Title "The Archive Contents                  Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n\n This Archive should contain :\n\n- -- START -- -\n  SmartShow10R1.0x0             - The Main Door\n  SmartShowCfg10.0x0            - The CLI Cfg util.\n  SmartShow10R1.ContactMe       - My Addy (Please make eall :))\n  SmartShow10R1.DistSite        - Another one so you wount miss it :))\n- --  END  -- -\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Usage"\n@Title "Usage                                 Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n\n    How do i use the :\n\n @{" The Door it self       " Link "DoorUsage"}\n @{" The CLI configurator   " Link "CliUsage"}\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "CliUsage"\n@Title "CLI Usage                             Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n\nSmartShow-CliConfig V1.0 [RELEASE 1] by NiGHTSHADE.\nAll rights reserved. Not for commercial use.\n\n  Usage : SmartShowCfg10.0x0 <Command>\n\n  Where <Command> is one of:\n\n  File    Selects a file by ASL.\n  Reset   Resets the statestics.\n  Remove  Remove the data file.\n\n\n@EndNode\n@Node "DoorUsage"\n@Title "Door Usage                            Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n\n How to use it :\n\n   * To simple, just enters it and it will display the TXT file seclected\n     from the CLI configurator - If not it will displays a error message.\n   * At the bottom line to the right is the total no. of usages of the door.\n\n@EndNode\n\n\n@Node "History"\n@Title "History                               Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n\n  Program History - Changes / New features\n\n   V1.0   [-BETA! 1-] - NiGHTSHADE (08-Dec-94)\n             * Beginned with it.\n             * Splited the program in 2 parts\n               - The CFG and the DOOR.\n             * Added FILE, REMOVE & the RESET arguments to Cfg.      [Cli!]\n             * Changed my msg.port routine                           [Door]\n\n   V1.0   [Release 1] - NiGHTSHADE (18-Jan-95)\n             * Changed some ansi                                     [Door]\n             * Speeded things up                                     [Door]\n             * Changed output routine                                [Cli!]\n             * No Buggs reported or found.\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "ContactNS"\n@Title "Contact NiGHTSHADE/InS^DpL            Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n\n___/\  _______________________________________________________________ _\n  /  \/\\n /   /  \        \\\\\\\                  [×] THE PLACE THAT ROCKS [*]\n \ PARTY \       |^ ^  \\\n  ON DUDE/      _|_ ___  |          \          {+} WASTELANDS {-}\n   \/\  /      (o(.Y.)   o)         _\__\n      \/       /(__) ^  \\         (__''_)     [] STAFF ROOSTER! []\n              (______/   ))_      _|_cOl|\n              //\ `-''   //  \   _/ __)-(_)     NiGHTSHADE/DPL^iNS\n             ((  \  _  //    \ /\  |---(_)         cASE/dCS!\n             /\\  \___//      Y  \ `---(_)\n  ____ ____ /  \\   |// ___ . `   \/\n / __ |    Y    \\__// |___||     /           FAST AMIGA & CONSOLE\n/ /(__|    '' .   (__)  |   ||\___/         [WHY NUP - LAMERS DEL''ED!]\n\_)   |______|      o  `---''|\n             |      ¦       |              NoDe #1 FiND iT 28k8!\n             |      °       |                   #2 cOMMINg sOOn!\n             |              |\n_ _______________________________________________________________/\  ___\n                                                               - --\/\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Beta"\n@Title "The cool Beta crew!                   Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n\n.---------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n|      OFFICIAL BETA SITES LIST FOR THE NIGHTSHADE /X DOORS/TOOLS           |\n+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| HALL OF FAME      +46-910-26665    DANSKEN/ACCESS          USR 28800 DS   |\n| NAPALM            +46-8-894595     BLAST/SSP               ACX 28800 VFC  |\n| TWISTED SOCIETY   +46-44-106144    TBB/iNFLECT             USR 21600 DS   |\n| UNDERGROUND       +46-16-424911    ViKiNG/iNDEPENDENT      USR 21600 DS   |\n+---------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|  PLEASE GIVE THOOSE DUDES A CALL - THEY ARE REALLY AWESOME IN MANY WAYS!  |\n`---------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "Greetings"\n@Title "The good things...                    Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n\n\n MY GREETINGS MUST GO TO (A-Z ORDER) :\n\n  * ANTISOCIAL                  - HOPE INSPERATIONS ARE GAINING LEVELS!\n  * BOBO                        - RUNNING LOW ON IDEAS !?\n  * BLAST                       - KEEP CODING AND YOU WILL KILL US :))\n  * CENTURION/PREMIERE          - FASTEST IN EUROPE !?\n  * CLUSTER/INS                 - KEEPS INSANITUARY ROOLING.\n  * CASE/DCS!                   - MY KiLLING CO-RAVER!\n  * CYCLONE                     - KEEP LEECHING DUDE!\n  * DANSKEN/ACS                 - SKELLEFTEA''S MANIAC NO.1!\n  * DANZIG                      - YOURE ASCII ARE GOOD!\n  * DISTLER/ISDN                - AT THE DAMN MILITARY SERVICE.\n                                  HOPE THAT YOU WILL GET BACK IN ST!\n                                  DAMN LAME TO LOCK YOU OUT I THINK (AND\n                                  MANY ONES WITH ME - ST ON THE LOOSE!)\n  * EVERSLICK                   - NO TRADING NO MORE !?\n  * EZCO                        - WORKING HARD I GUESS !?\n  * GAZ                         - GOOD CONSOLE SUPPORT M8!\n  * ICON                        - NO CONSOLE SPEED!?\n  * JADE                        - HAVE YOU DIED !?\n  * LIGHTSPEED TECH.            - GUESS ? - FOR /X OFCOUSE.\n  * LINEBACKER                  - I WILL CALL ''THE MANSION'' SOME DAY AGAIN!\n  * LOOBY/INS                   - PROGRAMING MANIAC.\n  * METAL/INS                   - CODES A LOT (NO RESULT ??)\n  * MR.COKE                     - KEEP CODING MY ''MINI-INTRO''. ZZZZZZ...\n  * NECROPHILIAC                - CHAT YOU AS ALWAYS!\n  * NECRONOMICON                - HOPFULLY WITH WORKING HD !\n  * PRINCIP/INS^CLS!?           - HELP WITH MODEMS AGAIN :)\n  * RAD                         - TO BAD YOU KILLED ''MEGA LO MANIA''!\n  * SAVAGE                      - GOOD SUPPORTER!\n  * SHAPECHANGER                - REAL GOOD ASCII...\n  * SHOCKER                     - ALWAYS MANY REQUESTS!\n  * SNIPER                      - THANX FOR THE SUPPORT!\n  * SPIDER                      - KILLES MY SPARE TIME!\n  * TBB/INFEKT                  - MY BEST BETA TESTER!\n  * WARHAMMES/iSDN              - NO SPEED FOR ME AT YOURE BOARD!\n  * WARLOCK                     - FOR BORROWING THIS COMPUTER.\n  * WESTBAM                     - KiLLING TRADER\n  * XCLUZIWE/DD·STYLE^XWR       - THANX FOR THE ''BETA'' LOGGO!\n  * ZANOK                       - ONE DAY BACK I HOPE!\n\n I know i have forgotten a dozzen or 2 and i''m terribe sorry for that.\n ---------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n@EndNode\n\n@node "Install"\n@Title "The /X ToolTypes Information          Dial Wastelands [+46(8)157472]"\n\n  * Please install this command as ''DOORS'' so ALL /X board will user DOORS\n    instead of things like DOORLIST, LIST, WHAT & DOOR... It is better for\n    all of us /X freaks if we have standards.\n\n  - THIS PART IS TAKEN FROM THE ORGiNAL /X AMIGA GUIDE AND ARE MODIFIED -\n  =======================================================================\n  <module>.INFO        - This ICON defines a MODULE for /X. The Name of\n                         the <module> should be the same as the executing\n                         in MainMenu prompt, and should be in one of the\n                         three Directories. This icon should be placed\n                         in the BBS:Commands/BBSCmd directory.\n\n     The following directorys are placed under the <BBS Path>:Commands/\n     path.\n\n     a> BBSCmd     - Modules in this directory are allowed to be\n                     executed from any menu prompt or MCI text file.\n\n     b> SYSCmd     - Modules in this directory are only accessible by\n                     MCI text files and internal BBS operations.\n\n     c> CONF(x)    - Modules in this directory are allowed to be\n                     executed from conference (x) menu prompt or from\n                     any MCI text file in conference (x).\n     d> Node(x)    - Modules in this directory are allowed to be\n                     executed from node (x) menu prompts or from any\n                     MCI text file in Node (x).\n  - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n  The ToolTypes of the <module(s)> :\n\n  ACCESS= <numb>       - tells /X the access level required to run this\n                         module. This option is ignored for internal\n                         Module options.\n\n  INTERNAL= <command>  - Specifies if you want to have this Module the\n                         same as a internal AmiExpress command. if you\n                         choose this option you don`t need the following\n                         tool types.\n\n  LOCATION= <string>   - Specifies the location of the Module.\n\n  MULTINODE=YES        - Tells /X if the module may be simultaneously\n                         accessed from other nodes, this door is multinode\n                         compatible. Options for this tool type\n                         are <YES/NO>.\n\n  PASSWORD= <string>   - Force the user to enter password before executing\n                         this module. This option is case sensetive wich\n                         means that "OK" and "Ok" is''nt the same.\n                         If you want the ''C'' command to be protected then\n                         use this tooltype.\n\n  PRIORITY=SAME        - Let''s you set the priority of the door. If you use\n                         PRIORITY=SAME, it will use the same Priority\n                         that express uses. For best result of the door use\n                         the ''SAME'' option.\n\n  QUICKMODE            - This simply tells AmiExpress not to run the Module\n                         in question if the user has logged onto the BBS\n                         using the QUICK LOGON option.\n                         If you want all the users to be able to use this\n                         door then disable this option by removing the\n                         tooltype.\n\n  STACK=4096           - tells /X the stacksize to use when launching this\n                         module. Default is 4096. This door requires\n                         4096 bytes of stack.\n\n  TYPE=XIM               - tells /X which type of module it is to support:\n                         XIM = /X Standard Module, this door is a XIM door.\n\n  TRAPON               - This makes LOGON Output go to a Log for Error\n                         Checking, you don''t need this option, just\n                         fragments youre hd a lot!\n  =======================================================================\n@EndNode\n','\n',char(10)),'{"ACCESS":"<numb>","LOCATION":"<string>","PRIORITY":"SAME","STACK":"4096","TYPE":"XIM"}','auto-added',96320,15,0,NULL,NULL,'otl_lo10','scan',1780048643);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ns_lb10','NS_LB10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/NS_LB10.LHA',NULL,'XIM','LogonBatch.xim',NULL,'AtomiX','NS','|::::\°  __   \°  __   \°    __ \°  __   \| |::::/   //   /  /_/   /    /  \/  /_/   /| |:::/   //   /   _    /\___    /   _    /:|',replace('|::::____________________________________:|\n|::::\°  __   \°  __   \°    __ \°  __   \|\n|::::/   //   /  /_/   /    /  \/  /_/   /|\n|:::/   //   /   _    /\___    /   _    /:|\n|::/   //   /   //   /    /   /   //   /::|\n|::\__//___/\__//___/\_______/\__//___/:::|\n|:::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::|\n|::: Logon Batch Version 1.0 by AtomiX :::|\n|:::: for AmiExpress /X 2.x and higher :::|\n|:::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::|\n`-----------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'LogonBatch.guide',replace('@DATABASE "DoorMenu.guide"\n\n@WIDTH 80\n@NODE MAIN "NaSa PrEsEnTs"\n\n                          Logon Batch V1.0 \n               written by AtomiX Sun Feb 27 10:09:01 1994\n \n            @{"    Copyright Note    " LINK COPRIGHT} -1- @{"   Urheberechte    " LINK URHEBERECHT}\n            @{"    Product Info      " LINK Produkt } -2- @{"   Produkt Info''s  " LINK PRODUKT}\n            @{"    Installation      " LINK INSTALL } -3- @{"   Installation    " LINK INSTALLATION}\n            @{"    Bug Report        " LINK BUG     } -4- @{"   FehlerReporte   " LINK FEHLER}\n            @{"                    Some Hello''s               " LINK HIHO}\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE COPRIGHT\n@TITLE "Copyrighted"\n\n - AmiExpress is Copyrighted(?) by LightSpeed Technologies\n\n - MultView , AmigaGuide , is Copyrighted by C=\n\n - This Tool is Callware ,who installing my Doors CAN call me\n   i''m intresting which people are installing my Tools/Doors\n   +49 5723 74340 \n\n								@{"Main Menu" LINK MAIN}\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE URHEBERECHT\n@Urheberechte\n\n - AmiExpress ist Urheberechtlich geschützt von LightSpeedTechnologies(?)\n\n - MultiView , Amiga Guide , ist Urheberechtlich geschützt von Commodore\n\n - Dieses Programm ist Callware, wer dieses Programm Installiert möchte\n   sich bitte bei der CHAOS LINE melden, weil es mich intressiert\n   welche Leute meine Programme Installieren ..\n\n								@{"Main Menu" LINK MAIN}\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PRODUkT\n@TITLE "Product Informations"\n\n     Logon Batch have the same Function''s as the normaly Logoff.batch\n\n     BBS:NODEx/Logon.Batch    {if not exists BBS:BATCH/Logon.Batch}\n     \n     Dont forget to set the Archive bit for Script\n\n     example :\n\n     "protect BBS:NODEx/LOGON.BATCH +s"\n     "protect BBS:BATCH/LOGON.BATCH +s"\n\n\n								@{"Main Menu" LINK MAIN}\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE INSTALL\n@TITLE "Logon Batch 1.0 - Installation"\n\n * INSTALLATION *\n\n - Copy all file to BBS:Doors/<or where you like it>\n\n\n AE 3.xx Installation\n --------------------\n\n  - Copy Open.info to BBS:Commands/SYSCmd/\n\n    Or add to FRONTEND.info:\n\n      ACCESS=001\n      LOCATION=BBS:DOORS/LogonBatch/LogonBatch.xim\n      MULTINODE=YES\n      PRIORITY=0\n		STACK=15000\n      TYPE=XIM\n\n\n								@{"Main Menu" LINK MAIN}\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE INSTALLATION\n@TITLE "LogonBatch - Installation"\n\n * INSTALLATION *\n\n - Kopieren Sie alle Files in folgenden Pfad \n\n   "BBS:DOORS/"\n\n   AE 3.xx Installation\n   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n - Kopieren Sie das "FrontEnd.info zu "BBS:COMMANDS/SYSCMD/"\n\n   Oder fügen Sie folgende Befehle in "FRONTEND.info" ein\n\n      ACCESS=001\n      LOCATION=BBS:DOORS/LogonBatch/LogonBatch.xim\n      MULTINODE=YES\n      PRIORITY=0\n		STACK=15000\n      TYPE=XIM\n\n\n								@{"Main Menu" LINK MAIN}\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE BUG\n@TITLE "Bug Reports"\n\n BUG REPORT & SUGGESTIONS\n ------------------------\n\n   It''s possible that a mistake will occur.... nobody is perfect.\n   If you have any suggestions or comments please leave a message\n   to the programmer or Sysop on the N.A.S.A World Headquarters\n   CHAOS LINE\n\n   in the Future you can reach me on the Chaos Line in the Fido Net\n  \n     Chaos Line  +49-5723-74340  United Germany\n     ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n								@{"Main Menu" LINK MAIN}\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE FEHLER\n@TITLE "Fehler Report"\n\n Fehler Reporte & Vorschläge\n ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n\n   Es ist möglich das Fehler passieren ... niemand ist perfekt.\n   Wenn Sie vorschläge oder Fehler Reporte zu unseren Tools haben\n   dann rufen sie unser Hauptquatier an und hinterlassen Sie eine\n   Nachricht zu denn Programmierer oder zu dem Sysop\n\n   ein weiterhin haben wir immer die neusten Fred Fish Disketten\n   und AmiExpress Utilities Online (Etwas Werbung muss ja sein)\n\n   Demnächst ist die Chaos Line auch über das Fido Netz ereichbar\n\n\n     Chaos Line  +49-5723-74340  United Germany\n     ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n								@{"Main Menu" LINK MAIN}\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE HIHO\n@TITLE "THE GREETINGS"\n\n  Greetings must go to the followings guys\n\n  Dr.Dre     - Nice chats with you\n  ByteAndi   - File ID is cool but need some modifications\n  Empire     - Thx for your help with coding C\n  Oldman     - I hope the Private Message V1.0ß is now encrypting correct\n  Highlander - nice chats,and don''t drink and Trade\n  No Limit   - thx for Support\n  Flake      - Virus Workshop Rules\n  MCC J.     - for making the paint for UI 107\n  MCloud     - you are a nice guy ,great idea''s Ghost Chat is in work\n  Yeggman    - nice trading, better times will come soon\n  Jee        - no comment\n  Doc Whoo   - i catch you soon for a mega chat\n  bAsTaRd    - keep it cool baby\n  Big Boss   - ohh no New User Stop on Mirage (snief)\n  Sigma Seven- nice Message routine in S Express,i call you in some days\n  Nero       - Nice board in Sweden\n  Aquarius   - Fast Tools...\n  Flashlight - 298 User''s Deleted oh wooow , learn C\n  Outlaw     - Thanks for the fast help\n  Diabolika  - I see you soon on the CeBit ''94\n  Stefanie   - Thank you for Moral Support..\n\n	and simply all they i have forgotten here\n\n								@{"Main Menu" LINK MAIN}\n@ENDNODE\n','\n',char(10)),'{"ACCESS":"001","LOCATION":"BBS:DOORS/LogonBatch/LogonBatch.xim","PRIORITY":"0","STACK":"15000","TYPE":"XIM"}','auto-added',18347,6,0,NULL,NULL,'ns_lb10','scan',1780048643);
