   If you have any suggestions or comments please leave a message\n   to the programmer or Sysop on the N.A.S.A World Headquarters\n   CHAOS LINE\n\n   in the Future you can reach me on the Chaos Line in the Fido Net\n  \n     Chaos Line  +49-5723-74340  United Germany\n     ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n								@{"Main Menu" LINK MAIN}\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE FEHLER\n@TITLE "Fehler Report"\n\n Fehler Reporte & Vorschläge\n ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n\n   Es ist möglich das Fehler passieren ... niemand ist perfekt.\n   Wenn Sie vorschläge oder Fehler Reporte zu unseren Tools haben\n   dann rufen sie unser Hauptquatier an und hinterlassen Sie eine\n   Nachricht zu denn Programmierer oder zu dem Sysop\n\n   ein weiterhin haben wir immer die neusten Fred Fish Disketten\n   und AmiExpress Utilities Online (Etwas Werbung muss ja sein)\n\n   Demnächst ist die Chaos Line auch über das Fido Netz ereichbar\n\n\n     Chaos Line  +49-5723-74340  United Germany\n     ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n								@{"Main Menu" LINK MAIN}\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE HIHO\n@TITLE "THE GREETINGS"\n\n  Greetings must go to the followings guys\n\n  Dr.Dre     - Nice chats with you\n  ByteAndi   - File ID is cool but need some modifications\n  Empire     - Thx for your help with coding C\n  Oldman     - I hope the Private Message V1.0ß is now encrypting correct\n  Highlander - nice chats,and don''t drink and Trade\n  No Limit   - thx for Support\n  Flake      - Virus Workshop Rules\n  MCC J.     - for making the paint for UI 107\n  MCloud     - you are a nice guy ,great idea''s Ghost Chat is in work\n  Yeggman    - nice trading, better times will come soon\n  Jee        - no comment\n  Doc Whoo   - i catch you soon for a mega chat\n  bAsTaRd    - keep it cool baby\n  Big Boss   - ohh no New User Stop on Mirage (snief)\n  Sigma Seven- nice Message routine in S Express,i call you in some days\n  Nero       - Nice board in Sweden\n  Aquarius   - Fast Tools...\n  Flashlight - 298 User''s Deleted oh wooow , learn C\n  Outlaw     - Thanks for the fast help\n  Diabolika  - I see you soon on the CeBit ''94\n  Stefanie   - Thank you for Moral Support..\n\n	and simply all they i have forgotten here\n\n								@{"Main Menu" LINK MAIN}\n@ENDNODE\n','\n',char(10)),'{"ACCESS":"250","LOCATION":"DOORS:SystemControl/SystemControl.xim","PRIORITY":"0","STACK":"15000","TYPE":"XIM"}','auto-added',17060,6,0,NULL,NULL,'ns_sc10','scan',1780048643);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ns14','NS14.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/NS14.LHA',NULL,'XIM','LE-win5-96.exe','1.4',NULL,NULL,'[iSDN][-÷ lEEChEd fRoM gOd''s hArEm ÷-][16.8]',replace('New Stuff v1.4 for AmiExpress BBS software.\n[iSDN][-÷ lEEChEd fRoM gOd''s hArEm ÷-][16.8]\n','\n',char(10)),'lOSeNDOS.guide',replace('                   \n                     __  _ __  /\__ _  _ __/\  __ _  __\n                    _\/___   \/              \/   ___\/_\n              ......\/\  /........................\  /\/......\n             :         \/                          \/         :\n             :      .___             .___         .___        :\n             :   _ _|   \      ______|   \  ______|   \       :\n             :   \\\__   7___  \______   /  \__   ____/       :\n             :      /.   |   \__/.  l/   \___/_____   \__ _   :\n             :     /::.  |    _/::.       _/::.  l/    _///   :\n             :     \___________\___________\____________\     :\n             :___        .___        .___        .___         :___\n     _ ______|   \ ______|   \ ______|   \ ______|   \  ______|   \\n     \\\__   ____/ \______   / \______   / \______   /  \__   ____/\n        /.   ___|___/.   |   \__/.  _|   \__/.  l/   \___/_____   \__ _\n       /::.  l/   _/::.  |    _/::. \___  _/::.       _/::.  l/    _///\n       \_ _________\_____|_____\___________\___________\___________ \\n         Y   :                                                :[nM$]Y\n      .------''                                                `------.\n      :eXON/rIOT^jORMAS · gHANDY/gODS · rAHIEM/eSSENCE · cELIC/rEKTUM: \n      `------.                                                .------''\n             `------------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',15681,5,0,NULL,NULL,'ns14','scan',1780048643);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('nsa_sec','NSA_SEC.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/NSA_SEC.LHA','SEC','XIM','SEC',NULL,NULL,'NSA','(|          ___     ____    ___         |) |)         / . \   / __/   / _ \        (| (:        /  |  \ /\__  \ /  .  \       :)',replace('|========================================|\n(|          ___     ____    ___         |)\n|)         / . \   / __/   / _ \        (|\n(:        /  |  \ /\__  \ /  .  \       :)\n|)        \__|__/ \_____/ \__|__/       (|\n(|                                      |)\n|==4/6/97===[ Security  v1.00 ]==========|\n(|                                      |)\n|)   Professional Security System For   (|\n(|     MAX''s BBS/MAX''s Professional     |)\n|)                                      (|\n','\n',char(10)),'Security.Guide',replace('@database Security.guide\n@author "Niki Murkett"\n@(C) "© 1997 NSA Designs"\n\n@node main "NSA Security By Niki Murkett"\n\n     o*¤°¬°¤*o,¸_¸,o*¤°¬°¤*o,¸_¸,o*¤°¬°¤*o,¸_¸,o*¤°¬°¤*o,¸_¸,o*¤°¬°¤*o\n\n     _   _ ____   ___     ____  _____ ____ _   _ ____  ___ _______   __\n    | \ | / ___| / _ \   / ___|| ____/ ___| | | |  _ \|_ _|_   _\ \ / /\n    |  \| \___ \| |_| |  \___ \|  _|| |   | | | | |_) || |  | |  \ V / \n    | |\  |___) |  _  |   ___) | |__| |___| |_| |  _ < | |  | |   | |  \n    |_| \_|____/|_| |_|  |____/|_____\____|\___/|_| \_\___| |_|   |_|  \n     \n\n     o*¤°¬°¤*o,¸_¸,o*¤°¬°¤*o,¸_¸,o*¤°¬°¤*o,¸_¸,o*¤°¬°¤*o,¸_¸,o*¤°¬°¤*o\n\n\n                                 Version 1.00\n\n\n                         @{"        Introduction       " link intro}\n                         @{"     System Requirements   " link sysreq}\n\n                         @{"        Installation       " link inst}\n                         @{"           Usage           " link inuse}\n\n                         @{" Copyright, Credz & Greetz " link copy}\n                         @{"        Distribution       " link dist}\n                         @{"         Disclaimer        " link disc}\n\n\n                         @{"MAX''s BBS Professional Info" link maxpro}\n\nThis program requires a NSA keyfile to operate.  More information in the \ndoor!\n\n                        ______   /|  _____/\ _______/\\n                        \  \  \ | |  \  ___/ \       /\n                         \  \  \| |   \/ \    \_/\  /\n--------Released-By------/  /\    |--__\  \---/ _/ /-----Designs--------------\n                        /__/  \   / /__   /   \// /\n                               \_/     \_/     /_/\n\n\n\n\n@endnode\n@node intro "Introduction"\n\nNSA Security was originally written by me for a mate''s BBS to keep his \nprivate sections VERY private :)\n\nThe spec was simple, if a user isn''t on the list then they shouldn''t even\nget to a password screen on anything that could give the game away!\n\nAs a result, NSA Secure was born nearly 1 year ago :)  It has simple to\nuse configs & a selection of ways to put a nosey user off finding out\nwhat it''s protecting :)\n\n@endnode\n@node sysreq "System Requirements"\n\nYou need to be running MAX''s BBS (any version should do!) and have something\nyou want to hide! (Usually seems to be porn or warez nowadays :/ )\n\nYou must have the NSAkeyfile.key file in your S: directory for this door \nto run (Like most NSA doors)...\n\nYo ucan obtain 1 FREE(!!!) by calling Redrum BBS, or by emailing your \ndetails to [email removed] :)\n(See the door for more info!)\n\n@endnode\n@node inst "Installation & Configs"\n\nThe easy bit :^)... Just use the following:-\n\n	Lha X NSA_Secure.Lha Doors:\n	\nThis will work for any system that has Doors: assigned to where the BBS has\nit''s doors..\n\nYou will need the NSAkeyfile.key in S: for this program to work.\nThis is FREE!!!!!!!!..  Run the door for more info :)\n\nA director called SEC will be created in Doors: for the program.\n\nThe reason why the door & dir are called SEC is to allow longer path names\nfor the config files :)\n\nRunning\n~~~~~~~\n\nExecution under MAX''s BBS 1.54 or /X\ Pro v1 - v1.70\nIn the menu editor set.\n\nKey:   Function:  Extra:    Lo Acc:    Hi Acc:	  Filename/Name/Dest/Path:\n ''       34	    0 	      100	10000	  Doors:Sec/Sec ConfigFile\n\nConfigFile is the full path and name of your config file!\ne.g.  \nDoors:Sec/Sec S:MyWarez.config\nDoors:Sec/Sec Work:Private.text\n\nYou may have as many config files for as many parts of the BBS that you\nrequire :)))))\n\n\nConfig File\n~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nThe config file can be located ANYWHERE on you HD!!!\n\nIt''s in the following format:-\n\nLine 1	- The menu number to jump to on a successful entry :)\nLine 2	- The ANSI file to display for the password entry display.\nLine 3	- Action to be taken if user is not on access list.  See below.\nLines 4+  User/Password list!\n	  Just have the first line for user name & second for password for\n	  as many users as you want to give access to :)))))\n	  \n	  Names & Passwords are not case-sensitive :)\n\n\nLook at the configs supplied for help :)\n\n\nActions (Line 3)\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nIf a user isn''t on your access list then you probably don''t even want them \nto know anything about it :))))\n\nTherefore, NSA Security supports 3 differant ways to throwing a user off\nthe trail! :)\n\n\nMethod 1 - The fake error message <G>\n	   Simply have line 3 contain a fake error message for an imaginary\n	   door program!\n	   e.g.\n	   Error! Sysop Upload Door FAILED!  Return code (68).\n	   \nMethod 2 - Menu Jumping! :)))))\n	   Simply have the first char of the line as a : and then have a\n	   menu to jump to if the user doesn''t have access!\n	   It''s usually best to make a user jump to a normal logout menu \n	   or the furthest part of the BBS & if they ask, just say it''s a \n	   menu jumper :) heheheheh <EG>\n	   e.g.\n	   :23\n	   \nNumber 3 - The Larch..  ..  Seriously...\n\nMethod 3 - The ANSI display! :)))\n	   If you have the first char to be a < then NSA Security will just\n	   display an ansi file, then quit.\n	   You could have this ansi as a statistics file with normal \n	   auto-inserts so peeps wouldn''t think anything about it :)\n	   e.g.\n	   <BBS:Text/Statistics.text\n\nThe password prompt appears at ANSI co-ordinate 31,13.  This can not be\nchanged in the current release!\n\n\nYou can also have NSA Secure running in the maindoor.text file :)\nThis gives you the ability for having 1 main menu for elite users & 1 for\nnormal users! :))))\n\n\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node inuse "Using NSA Security when started :))))))"\n\nWhen the door is started, it loads up one of the configs specified and\nscans it to see if the user is on it.\n\nIf they are then they get 3 chances to enter the correct password to gain\naccess to your private menu.\n\nALL actions are logged to a file called Security.log in Doors:Sec/\n\nIf the user isn''t on the list they they will be delt with according to\nline 3 of the config file :)))))\n\n\nIt''s up to you what you use this door for, either for members file sections,\nsysop menu, porn, warez etc etc...  I don''t really care!\n\nAll I can say is if you have illegal files, you still stand the chance of\nbeing busted & having all of your gear confiscated!\n\n\nI think that''s about it now :)))))))))))))\n\n(Read the credz & greetz :))) )\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node copy "Copyright, Credz & Greetz"\n\nNSA Security is Copyright © 1997 NSA Designs\n\n	Main Coding:  Niki Murkett\n\n\nContacting Niki Murkett:-\n \nEmail [email removed]\n\nURL: Http://www.geocities.com/SiliconValley/Lakes/8748\n\nThe web page has only just been arranged as of 4-June-97 so the pages won''t\neven be on the server for a few days yet!!!\n\n\nEcho net:\n\n	FLuFFy NeT	888:100/0	- UK HOME!\n\nFLuFFy NeT is a very friendly mail network covering the UK, Ireland, Holland\nand now Australia!\n\nAmong other things, MOST of the worlds top MAX''s door coders are already\nconnected!..  If you want to know anything to do with MAX''s, then join up :)\n \nIt''s also a pretty good laff :)\n\n\n\nSupport BBS''s!\n\nRedrum BBS - Node 1: +44 [0]1635 826720  24Hrz, Max Speed 33.6K\n           - Node 2: +44 [0]1635 827203  24Hrz, Max Speed 14.4K\n           - Node 3: +44 [0]1635 PRIVATE - Publicly online soon!\n				 SysOp: Niki Murkett (N!k!^NSA)\n				 \nsUB-bASS   - Node 1: +44 [0]1473 412842  24Hrz, Max Speed 14.4K\n				 SysOp: Techn!x\n\ncRANBERRY  - Node 1: +44 [0]1488 608698  24Hrz W/E ONLY!, Max Speed 14.4K\n				 Sysop: Leigh Russ (Perk^NSA)\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\n\nGreetz to...\n\nJacknife, !n5ane, Perk, Dr. X, Ghandi, Skittle, Roger Wilco, Mos, Luigi, \nOzz, Bradman, Techn!x and all the others I forget about when writing \ngreetz :)\n\nAlso to Steve Clack for very long chats :) & Glen Martin from GREMLiNS BBS\nfor being the only person I know nutty enough to call half way round the\nworld for a chat :))))  (Just foned me again a few mins ago :))) )\n\n\n@endnode\n@node dist "Distribution"\n\nThis program & related doc files are copyright!\n\nDo what you want with it tho :)\n\nSpread it around the world a few times :)\n\n@endnode\n@node disc "Disclaimer"\n\nUsual stuff applies, u use it at your own risk etc. etc.\n\nJust don''t blame me if it shags up your BBS, gets your wife pregnant, \nruns the dog over, turns the moon blue etc...\n\nIt is very safe tho :)\n\n@endnode\n\n@node maxpro "MAX''s BBS Professional - The future of BBS''s!"\n\nThere are 3 versions of MAX''s BBS Professional available...\n\nv1.00	- PD evaluation copy - Crashes at midnight\nv1.66	- Registered ONLY..  New look, cleaner & faster than v1.00\nv1.70	- Look below at the feature list!\n\n                  MAX''s BBS Professional features list :)\n\nAlready in MAX''s Pro v1.70\n\nTrue Os2.04/os3.x screens & windows  (interleaved under os3.x)\nAll screens are named public ones.  Format:  MAXsBBS?  where ? is the node \n	number!\nNew look gadgets\nVery FAST!  Uses under 4% CPU time on a slow 030 :)  0.60% when idle!\nScript based File_id/.readme/$Ver: file detection\nBanner adding/stripping, virus checking & credit docking :)\nFree Download support\nNew 250 line message editor! :)\nNew MAX''s commands!\nAltered Paragon protocol.  Doors won''t lock up on 2+ local logins!\nBefore/After mail import scripts for Freq servers, traptoss etc etc.\nANSI/RIP support\nScreen colour locking on os3.0 - Stops hisoft basic doors screwing things up!\nAnimated login intro :)\nAdvanced door port structure\nAmi-Express door emulation!!!  Run LSD-Wall on MAX''s pro :))))))\n\n\nBeing added before release...\n\nTrapdoor/GMS/Telnet Spawnable\nPlug-in support..  External progs can become part of max''s!\n\n\n\nCurrent project size:	approx 7,000 lines pure asm\n			     + 2,000 lines asm in config editor!\n			     \n\nThe file handler is THE most powerful available for ANY BBS system!!!!!!\n\nEven supports colour file_id''s!!!..  Also checks the file format so you\ncan add a script to nuke imcomplete pictures for example! :) Or limit\nvirus checking to certain file types..  The list is endless :)\n\n\nRegistration costs:\n\nPro v1.66	- £3 uk...  Grab the file MAXsPro.lha from the aminet or\n		  any decent BBS for the reg form...\nPro v1.70	- £15 uk..  More expensive, but has MUCH better features!\n		  Not available as of writing..  Contact me for more info!\n		  \n\nUK Registration Site is Redrum BBS, Australian registration site will be\nGREMLiNS BBS (Currently being arranged at time of door release!)\n\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',56486,4,0,NULL,NULL,'nsa_sec','scan',1780048643);
