INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ntr_st11','NTR-ST11.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/NTR-ST11.LHA','RPSTaRT','XIM','RPSTaRT',NULL,NULL,'NTR','/~¯ \\ ___/  / \\ ___/__ \\/~¯  \\   \\ /  /  /__/__ /   / ¬\  \  _/_ /   / /  /\ /__/__/___ ,/____/_ //___\  ¯¬\___/_/__/ /',replace('    __/\_________/\________/\  ___/\___/\\n   /~¯ \\ ___/  / \\ ___/__ \\/~¯  \\   \\\n  /  /  /__/__ /   / ¬\  \  _/_ /   / /  /\\n /__/__/___ ,/____/_ //___\  ¯¬\___/_/__/ /\n \__\__\___\/\____\_\/\____\___/\__\_\__\/\n  ~~~~~~~~~~\/~~~~~~~\/~~~~~\__\/~~~~~~~~\n    [ NEUTRON /X iNSPiRATiON BRINGS YA ]\n\n    NEUTRON STATUS DOOR PUBLIC RELEASE\n\n[ RELEASED AT COSMIC CIRCUS - NEUTRON WHQ! ]\n','\n',char(10)),'NTR-STAT.guide',replace('@DataBase Neutron Status Dox\n\nCopyright (c) 1995 Gravedancer of Neutron\n\n@Remark $VER: Neutron Status v1.o public\n@Remark AmigaGuide database for the Status Dox\n\n@node MAIN "Neutron Status Dox (c)1995 Gravedancer of Neutron"\n\n      ______                      ____ _ _____________________\n      \____ \___________________,/   /_________  \_____ \____ \_____\n        /  \ \    \_  _____/    /   /    /  __/ _/    /  \   \ \    \_\n       /    \ \    /,____)__ __/   /   \/   \   \_   /    \   \ \-gD /\n      /______\____/_________\_____/_____\____\___/________/____\____/\n\n                     [. nEUTRON - /X - iNSPiRATiON .]\n\n               [. bRINGS yA a bRAND nEW sTATUS dOOR fOR /X .]\n\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------- \n\n         >>> C·O·N·T·E·N·T·S  O·F  D·O·C·U·M·E·N·T·A·T·I·O·N <<<\n\n                         @{"      Introduction      " Link Cap01}\n                         @{"      Requirements      " Link Cap02}\n                         @{"      Installation      " Link Cap03}\n                         @{"       Greetings!       " Link Cap05}\n                         @{"   How to Contact me?   " Link Cap06}\n                         @{"        Credits         " Link Cap10}\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------\n                     Complete Docs for Neutron Status!\n         ---------------------------------------------------------\n       The Documentation has been written by Gravedancer of Neutron\n\n@endnode\n@node Cap01 "Introduction"\n  =======================================================================\n\nthis is just another try to make a good status door ... more to come !!!!!!!!!\n\n  =======================================================================\n@endnode\n@node Cap02 "Requirements"\n  =======================================================================\n\n           To install Status you must have the following things:\n\n  - an  Amiga Model (500/600/1000/1200/2000/2500/3000/4000/CDTV/CD³²)\n  - the installed Version of OS\2, OS\3 or higher\n    (Soft- or Hardware Version)\n  - AmiExpress V2.xx , v3.xx or higher. And surely S-Express hehe.\n\n  =======================================================================\n@endnode\n@node Cap03 "How to install NTR-STATS:"\n  =======================================================================\n\nfirst  copy  all in  c to c:, all from libs to libs:, all from doors to doors:\nand   all   from commands/bbscmd  to  your  bbs:commands/bbscmd  directory ...\nthen start rpstart in your user-startup. the next  step  depends  on  the fact\nwhether you are already using an rms door or not ... if not just  copy s to s:\nbut if you run another rms''ed door load up your editor and add the  lines from\nmy       rms.config     to      your     rms.config      ...     thats all ...\n\n  =======================================================================\n@endnode\n@node Cap05 "Greetings go to the following guys:"\n  =======================================================================\n\nfirst of all i''d like to greet all the great names in /X programming like ...\n\n                               Dr.Dre!/tRSi\n                               ByteAndi/tRSi\n                                SieGeL/tRSi\n                                 Spy/tRSi\n                               Delta-X/tRSi\n                                 2fAST/aVT\n                               kNUCKLES/aVT\n                                 sTc/TaSK\n                                CALYPSO/GOD\n\n          next i''d like to say hello to the best ascii heroes ...\n\n                          mOGUe!/P¡MoK^-aRTcORE!\n                            2fAST/aC!^nEON^hLM\n                   mR.vAIN/bONZAI/SUNFLEX ¡NC/aRT-cORE!\n                       aLL oTHER mEMBAS oF aRT-cORE\n\n                and last but not least the real greetz ...\n\n                          GENERAT¡ON/nTR^pDY^iLS\n                                  DAN/nTR\n                                M¡CK/bP^dCN\n                              MAGNET¡C/bP^dCN\n                              eCS^mARIO/tRS¡\n                              sPELLF¡RE/tRS¡\n                           dJ mELLOWNOISE/¡NFECT\n                               dONALD/sHOOT\n\n          [. hOPE tO sEE yA sOON oN tHE cOSM¡C c¡RCUS mEET¡NG .]\n\n  =======================================================================\n@endnode\n@node Cap06 "How to contact me:"\n  =======================================================================\n\nyou can find me on this nice bbs ...\n\n                                                         /\\n________________________________________________ _______/ \\________________\n\_______       \________   /  _________________ Y _____/   \\______        /\n  /     \______/_      /   \________    \      \_/     \____/      \______/_\n /-gD   /        \    /     \      7     \      7      |   /       /        \\n \________________\_________/____________/______l______|___\_________________\\n\n_________________/\______________________________________,____________________\n\_______        / \\___________     \_____       \_      /    _/  ___________/\n  /     \______/_  \\/      __/    _/     \______/_     /      \_______    \\n /      /        \__/       \       \_    /        \  _/        \     7     \\n \________________\ |________\_______/______________\___________/___________/\n              ______|\n\n            [«» nEUTRON! wHQ «» pRODIGY gHQ «» iLLUSION eHQ «»]\n\n                  «[» sYSOP : gENERATION/nTR^pDY^iLS «]»\n\n         »[« eCS & mARIO xXx 2fAST xXx cAOS xXx dAN xXx mR.bIG »]«\n\n  =======================================================================\n@endnode\n@node Cap10 "The Credits"\n\n  =======================================================================\n\n                      Main Idea, Programming : Gravedancer/nTR\n                                 Betatesting : Generation/nTR^pDY^iLS\n\nThings that i used/needed to produce this kind of software ...\n\n ... a kuhl computer ( A12oO - 6MB - 68882/40 - installed /X )\n  ... CygnusED Professional V3.5 © 1987-1993 CygnusSoft Software\n   ... bottles of milk and coke\n    ... the music from prodigy and some really kuhl dj''s\n     ... the fun that i had while playing biing !\n\n  =======================================================================\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',50036,3,0,NULL,NULL,'ntr_st11','scan',1780048650);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('numb_l10','NUMB-L10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/NUMB-L10.LHA','FastLHA','XIM','FastLHA',NULL,'NIKE!/NUMB','NUMB','|        /                    _ _ |       /                    | \ / \|      /   .:    ____ _______|__\___',replace('     ._________                             \n     |        /                    _     \n   _ |       /                    | \   \n  / \|      /   .:    ____ _______|__\___\n_/  \\_    /:    ::  /  _ Y ___  ______  \\n\    \    /::....::_/    \ /     \|   /   \_\n \____\  / ·::::::·\      Y_______X________/\n       \/           \_____|mes&wc!         \n(==============[PRESENTS]==================)\n(« FastLhaChecker v1.O by NIKE!/NUMB ''95! »)\n(==========================================)\n','\n',char(10)),'FastLhacheck''o.Doc',replace('                        ._________\n                        |        /                    _\n                      _ |       /                    | \\n                     / \|      /   .:    ____ _______|__\___\n                   _/  \\_    /:    ::  /  _ Y ___  ______  \\n                   \    \    /::....::_/    \ /     \|   /   \_\n                    \____\  / ·::::::·\      Y_______X________/\n                          \/           \_____|mes&wc!\n                   [==] Takes ya from da back with! [==]\n\n                    -> fASTlHAcHECK''o v1.O by nIKE! <-\n\n         (Sorry for the lame doc, but i had 60 minutes to fix it)\n\nThe program checks for the BBS:FCHECK/<filetype>.INFO icon, if it fails to\nfind it, it will quit.. Coz the config is in that icon.. so for instance, if\nyou have it on LZH you must have LZH.info WITH CONFIG TOOLTYPES or the shit\nwill probably make something DUMB happen.. ;).. actually i don''t know what will\nhappen, and i will prevent usage if something like that happens.. well..\n\nCopy the main program to somewhere where you want to have it..\nCopy your stripfile (as all strippers it has one!) to S:LHACHECK.OMIT\nEdit a file called S:LHACHECK.ADD and include all the files (with path)\nthat should be added to the LHA archives.. (These will ALWAYS be added, even\nif you have reversed or randomized adds..)\n\nThat''s the first part.. the second part are these damn tooltypes.. ;)\n\nSTRIP=YES            ; This will turn on STRIPPING of adds\nADD=YES              ; This will turn on ADDING (S:LHACHECK.ADD)\n                       THIS MUST BE TURNED ON TO USE REVERSED/RANDOM ADDS!\nCHECK=YES            ; Turns on filechecking.\nREVERSE=YES          ; Turns on making a file called the same as the uploaded\n                       file..\nREVADD=S:EyeCandy!   ; Filename for the reversed add.. will be copied to T: and\n                       renamed..\nRANDOM=YES           ; Random filenames for the adds.. \nRANDIR=S:RandomDir   ; The util will list all files in this dir to the memory\n                       and select X number of files and rename them to something\n                       randomly..\nRANNUM=4             ; This will add 4 random adds.. Defaults to 1\n\nI hope u understand.. i''ve included an example file..\n\n                      Greetings to da deserving ones!\n\nTo join NUMB (A group consisting of members of SPB·LSD·DLT·TRSI·CRZ·ETC) then\ncontact mESSiAH on any fast elite board or call CHECKPOiNT!\n\n                +47-515-931-23 (2 NODES 28k8 DS RINGDOWN!)\n\n                           To contact the coder:\n      Any fast elite board in Europe, and the major ones in The U.S.\n                 My Own board in sweden (INSTANT PLEASURE)\n              FidoNet: 2:203/701.5     WasteNet: 55:100/704.5\n                      InterNet: [email removed]\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',15995,3,0,NULL,NULL,'numb_l10','scan',1780048650);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('nusermsg','NUSERMSG.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/NUSERMSG.LHA',NULL,'XIM','exe.-l0S-eND0S-bBS-.exe',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,replace('USER MESSAGE DOOR (NOT A WALL)\n','\n',char(10)),'usermsg.doc',replace('Usermsg door for AmiExpress!!  "OH NO NOT ANOTHER ONE" well when I\nfirst wrote and release it there was only a lame WALL door out so shut\nup!! Anyhow mine doesn''t have the problem a lot of reacent doors have of\nlooking like dog shit!...\n\nInstallation is simple as shit. Edit the top of USERMSG.REXX to alter\nthe output file. The rest is as normal and I''m not explaining how\nto run a BBS, you should know that!.\n\nIf you wanna see what the output looks like before you waste that time\ninstalling it, look in ATX_UTILS and type USERMSG.DOOR or whatever...\n\nSorry that the ARexx is unreadble but its easier to update when its\nmade modular (Well sort of modular!). IF your some paranoid idiot, search\nfor the words FORMAT or DELETE or USERDATA or whatever, you wont find any\nshit in there... Or replace every ";" with a CR... Uptoyou!\n\n\n\nHistory:-\n\nv2 (I think) Released with P0T-TRIX.DMS\nv2.03 - this one - No works out the size of the user''s screen using what\n        they''ve set their lines/screen to.\n        Also fixed something... FUck I dont remember... Who cares???\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',10006,5,0,NULL,NULL,'nusermsg','scan',1780048650);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('nva_low1','NVA-LOW1.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/NVA-LOW1.LHA','nova-low','XIM','nova-low',NULL,NULL,'NVA',':::   ::: :::   ::: :::   ::: :::   ::: ::::  ::: :::   ::: :::   ::: :::   ::: ::::: ::: :::   ::: :::   ::: :::::::::',replace(':::   :::  :::::::  :::   :::  :::::::\n:::   ::: :::   ::: :::   ::: :::   :::\n::::  ::: :::   ::: :::   ::: :::   :::\n::::: ::: :::   ::: :::   ::: :::::::::\n::: ::::: :::   ::: :::   ::: :::   :::\n:::  :::: :::   :::  ::: :::  :::   :::\n:::   :::  :::::::    :::::   :::   :::\n      L O G O F F   W A L L  1.1b\nReviseD rx code /\/ New SysOp functions\n','\n',char(10)),'NoVa-LoW.GUIDE',replace('@DATABASE "NoVa-LoW documentation"\n\n@NODE MAIN "NoVa-LoW documentation"\n\n       ******   ****     ********     ****    ****   ************\n       *******  ****    ****  ****    ****    ****   ****    ****\n       ******** ****   ****    ****   ****    ****   ****    ****\n       **** ********   ****    ****   ****    ****   ************\n       ****  *******   ****    ****   *****  *****   ****    ****\n       ****   ******    ****  ****     **********    ****    ****\n       ****    *****     ********       ********             ****\n       ***                               ******               ***\n       **                                                      **\n       *                                                        *\n              NovA-LoW  v1.1b (c) StooKie / FreElAnCe 1996\n\n               AnoTher KewL Rx /X Door  4 /X Versions 4.++\n\n           @{"What is it" Link 0.1.}   @{"InstallIng" Link 0.2.}  @{"Bugz" Link 0.3.}  @{"GreeTingZ" Link 0.4.}\n\n                  @{"Sysop" Link 0.5.}                      @{"ToDo" Link 0.6.}\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE 0. "index"\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE 0.1. "What is it"\n\n What IS it ???\n ==============\n\n  HAviNg Run a BBs for a while i''ve been lookIng for sommit a BIT different\n from the Usual bbs log off screen doorz !!! All there seem''d to be was\n a load of add bbs''s to logoff !! this was getting a bit boring coz every\n bbs had one and they all mostly look''d the same to me !! aha ! idea !\n Peeps like to slag others off on a wall ! why not a wall wid a difference\n A logoff wall ! ya don''t know whats on it till it''s too late ! arghhhh\n someone diss''d ya and it''s to late to get back it em ! SHIT wait till\n the next call and get ya own back on em ! big time ! and they won''t know\n till they have log''d off and it''s too late for them to do anything bout it\n\n the door is installed under the "G" logoff key ! it''s simple to understand\n and use ! even the lame "KID" can use it without worry !\n\n check out the nova-low1.iff and the nova-low3.iff if ya wann have a quick\n butchers at it b4 ya think bout installin it to ya setup\n\n\n IMPORTANT INFO !\n ----------------\n\n this door has been optimized for speed " as everyone knows rexx ain''t the\n fastest of languages " so to run the door correct then the "G".info must\n only run the rexx script <Doors:NvA/NoVa-low/runit> if you don''t run it\n this way it will instantly lock up !!!!!\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE 0.2. "Installing"\n\n InsTaLlInG NoVa Logoff WaLl....\n ===============================\n\n CopY The UsuALl Shit froM Dis ArchIve To your /X setup\n\n  " BBs:commands/bbscnd/g.info   to YoUr BBS:commands/bbscmd "\n\n  " BBS:DOORS/Nva/NoVa-LoW   To youR DooRs:Nva/ "\n    If YA don''t have a NVA dir in doors: den MAke One !!!\n\n\n IMPORTANT INFO !\n ----------------\n\n this door has been optimized for speed " as everyone knows rexx ain''t the\n fastest of languages " so to run the door correct then the "G".info must\n only run the rexx script <Doors:NvA/NoVa-low/runit> if you don''t run it\n this way it will instantly lock up !!!!!\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE 0.3. "bugz"\n\n KnoWn BuGz....\n ==============\n\n Arghhh The OnlY Bloody Bug In Here ShouLd Be ThiS On >> /\\o//\ <<\n  Unfortunatly If Ya fiNd One !then Mail ME and lemme know what\n  Happend !! BTW if a node Locks up whilst they were in NoVa-low\n  Then The File " ENV:NVA_doorlock " will not be deleted !!! and no one\n  else will be able to use the door ! If ThiS HappEns Then Ya Will HAve\n  to Delete The file by hand !!!\n\n  Thanx to Def BAse for pointing this small niggling little bug ! ermmm\n  but none of my rx doors seem to wanna run on a ks 3.1 system ! i aint\n  had time or a chance to find out why ! if anyone knows why this is\n  happening then pleaze enlighten me to save time in the longrun !\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE 0.4. "greetingz"\n\n GreeTinGz\n =========\n\n In No Order !!\n\n    P..K           Ain''t ya got that Other 100 meg In acTion Yet\n    SCARAB         24 hrz ! what a fukin laff ! NEVER ! hullo ! DEAD !\n    Def BasE       Ya Got  A liFe Now ! heheh YA Got /X ! WikEd\n    SkuTTer        ya gotta be dead ! not a fuckin peep out a ya\n    SimBa          YA got it Sorted Yet M8 ! What YA think to dis 1 den ?\n    GiZmO          i''ll HAve Ta BEll YA nxt time i''m at The PyraMid\n    ZyKe           ! shit ! ya still alive after all diz time ?\n\n    Any 1 else i 4 got to mention !!! catch yaz bout\n\n  If YA WaNNa ConTaX ME YA cAn GEt ME AT The :->\n\n  The PyrAmiD 01289 304426 9pm-6am weekdayz 24hrz weekendz   14k4\n  Da EleCtrOn 01289 331822 6pm-8am weekdayz 24hrz weeKEndZ   28k8\n\n  BTW FUk Da Speling Mistackes ! coz i ate Doing Dox !!!!!\n  and can''t be pissed to check 4 dem !!\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n\n\n@NODE 0.5. "Sysop"\n\n SysOp CommanDz ....\n ===================\n\n HokAY ! a special sysop screen has now been add''d to the logoff wall\n it will auto enable the sysop commands for any user that has a security\n access of 250 +  " check nova-low2.iff for a quick view of the screen"\n\n this menu is about the same as the user menu ! it explaines it''s self\n on screen !   2 new commands will appear !\n\n (V)iew logoff wall ! can''t guess what that does ??\n\n (K)ill a messy on the wall ! ! remove the lame bbs plug that some newby\n sysop has left on the wall ! then it ask''s what message ya wanna\n remove. type in the numba then it''s deleted and will show ya the new\n saved logoff screen !\n\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n\n@NODE 0.6. "todo"\n\n ThinGs To Do ....\n =================\n\n If AnyoNe Likes The Door I miGhT Think about Changing things about and\n  adding odds and ends If ya have any ideas for adding to the door\n  lemme know and i''l see what i can do !!!\n\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',29377,1,0,NULL,NULL,'nva_low1','scan',1780048650);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('nvx_avl1','NVX-AVL1.LZX','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/NVX-AVL1.LZX',NULL,'XIM','"FILE_ID.DIZ"',NULL,NULL,'NVX',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'auto-added',17234,0,0,NULL,NULL,'nvx_avl1','scan',1780048650);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('nvx_awai','NVX-AWAI.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/NVX-AWAI.LHA','V-Await','XIM','V-Await',NULL,NULL,'NVX','\_____    \     /   \___  / ___/ tGø/aC!/.   /    /.   /    /.   _   \ //   /    //   /    //   /    /',replace('       ________________________________\n       \_____    \     /   \___  / ___/\ntGø/aC!/.   /    /.   /    /.   _   \\n      //   /    //   /    //   /    /\n     /____/    /\________/____/    /\n         /____/              /    /\n   { V-AWAiT v1.O1 - VENOM / NERVE AXiS }\nAn AwaitScreen replacement, Needs SAmiLog!\n','\n',char(10)),'awaitscreen.txt',replace('~\n~CC_V-AWAIT|\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',14298,1,0,NULL,NULL,'nvx_awai','scan',1780048650);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('nvx_dc21','NVX-DC21.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/NVX-DC21.LHA',NULL,'XIM','DirChecker.000',NULL,'VENOM/NERVE','NVX','(  /(__/_\   ''/___\(__/_   (___\`_\\_,|`---. «------------------------------------------'' V-DIRCHECKER V2.01 BY VENOM/NERVE AXIS 96',replace(' ___ ___ ____       ___     ___  _  _ . ___\n(  /(__/_\   ''/___\(__/_   (___\`_\\_,|`---.\n«------------------------------------------''\n  V-DIRCHECKER V2.01 BY VENOM/NERVE AXIS 96\nFAME & /X Clone utility to compare BBS file\nlistings and upload directories for any\nduplicate entries and missing files/entries.\n-------------------------------[tGø/-T!]---»\n','\n',char(10)),'DirChecker.Guide',replace('@DATABASE "DirChecker.Guide"\n@NODE Main "DirChecker"\n\n                                   ::]%[:: n e r v e   a x i s ::]%[::\n                                                  .\n                                               · /-------- -- -\n -  - ----------------------------------------/ /  code: venom/nerve axis\n          door: v-dirchecker 2.o1            / /------------------ -- -  -\n         -  - -- ---------------------------/ /\n                                           /\n\n             :::]%[::: fame util release :::]%[:::\n\n\n                @{"  " LINK "Intro"} Intro        - What the hell is this?\n                @{"  " LINK "Install"} Installation - Where to shove it :)\n                @{"  " LINK "Usage"} Usage        - How to make it go *PING*\n                @{"  " LINK "History"} History      - I always hated history!\n                @{"  " LINK "Credits"} Credits      - Who made it?\n                @{"  " LINK "Contact"} Contact      - Really wanna talk to him?\n                @{"  " LINK "FAME"} FAME         - The nicest system around\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Intro "Introduction"\n\n                                  ..\n                             .---:  :---------.\n                             |   ····         |\n                            [%] iNTRODUCTiON [%]\n                             |         ....   |\n                             `---------:  :---''\n                                        ··\n\nA  small  CLI  utility  for  sysops  that  goes  through  a directory on the\n         hard-drive and the relevant bbs file listing and outputs:\n\n	· duplicate entries in the directory listing\n	· files in the listing but not on the hard-drive\n	· files on the hard-drive but not in the listing\n\nThese are output to the cli window as standard and leaves it up to you as to\nwhether  you  want  to  remove  it.   Basically this was created to clean up\ndirectories on a BBS because we''d had a couple of duplicate files sneak past\nus  on  13th  Hour  due  to old files being deleted by mistake or duplicates\n                    popping up when they weren''t wanted.\n\nThis  version is approximately 3 times faster than version 1.00 so obviously\nwe  recommend  this  one  instead :) On a test listing of one meg it took 10\nseconds  to  check  and output all relevant information, while version v1.00\n                              took 27 seconds.\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Install "Installation"\n\n                                  ..\n                             .---:  :---------.\n                             |   ····         |\n                            [%] iNSTALLATiON [%]\n                             |         ....   |\n                             `---------:  :---''\n                                        ··\n\nJust  copy  this  to  any  directory  you  store  your bbs utilities and run\nwhenever  you  wish.  There are two versions, a standard version and the 020\nversion. Rename the command to "dirchecker" and put it wherever. Simple eh?\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Usage "Usage"\n\n                               ..\n                          .---:  :--------------.\n                          |   ····              |\n                         [%] USiNG THE PROGRAM [%]\n                          |              ....   |\n                          `--------------:  :---''\n                                          ··\n\nOpen a shell window and type:\n\n                          dirchecker <dir> <list>\n\nDir is the directory on the hard-drive you wish to check.\nList is the listing on the hard-drive you wish to check.\n\nIf you run dirchecker without any parameters it will tell you that parameters\n          are required and give a quick rundown of how to use it.\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE History "History"\n                                ..\n                           .---:  :------------.\n                           |   ····            |\n                          [%] PROGRAM HiSTORY [%]\n                           |            ....   |\n                           `------------:  :---''\n                                         ··\n\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n01-Jan-96	V1.oo\n\nFirst public release.\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n06-Sep-96	V2.oo\n\nComplete re-write of version 1.oo, now approx 3 times faster.\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n09-Sep-06	V2.o1\n\nChanged output to put quotes round filenames as some files with spaces\nat the end were found. Now you can see if there are any spaces.\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Credits "Credits"\n\n                                ..\n                           .---:  :-------------.\n                           |   ····             |\n                          [%] CREDiTS & GREETS [%]\n                           |             ....   |\n                           `-------------:  :---''\n                                          ··\n\n                                  All Work\n\n                      Code & Mountain Dew - Venom/Nvx\n                      Docs & Gloom Deluxe - TANGo/Nvx\n\n\n              Quick Hellos From Venom To These Lovely People\n\n Hybrid, Reflex, MDR, Mic Flair, Bill, Video Nasty, Icon, MrFrapp, Memo, MrZ\n   Biggles, Delta TX, Ghostrider, Strider, Dr.Dre, Sigel, Derrow, Mad Dan,\n  Scouser, Narcosis, Neelix, Ordyne, Sidewinder, Stainless Steel Rat, Raoul\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Contact "Contact"\n\n                               ..\n                          .---:  :---------------.\n                          |   ····               |\n                         [%] CONTACT THE AUTHOR [%]\n                          |               ....   |\n                          `---------------:  :---''\n                                           ··\n\n                             1 3 t h   H O U R\n\n                    Nerve Axis UKHQ · Twisted Dist Site\n\n                      + 4 4   0 1 7 0 4   5 0 5 8 4 5\n\n                    33k6 Courier Power - 2 Node Ringdown\n      \n                Ace ^ Venom ^ TANGo ^ Biggles ^ Crash ^ Zone\n\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE FAME "About FAME"\n\n@{b}@{u}What should FAME costs ?@{ub}@{uu}\n\n Registered Version:  110 USD / 150 DM\n Betatester Version:  145 USD / 200 DM\n\n\n@{b}@{u}What is included in the FAME-package ?@{ub}@{uu}\n\n Server, SystemEditor, MainPart, FAMEHydra.FIM, FAMEError.FIM\n\n FAME.library FAMEChat.FIM programmed by Bloodrock/tRSi\n\n FAMEFullEd.FIM, FAMEScript.FIM programmed by Beatnik/tRSi\n\n MUI UserEditor, FAMEDoorHelp.FIM, FAMEInfo programmed by SieGeL/tRSi\n\n Also some doors and tools from the FAME-Development-Team are included,\n but this doors are only unregistered Versions and have therefor some\n limitations. The registered Versions of those doors and the Informations\n how to get them are available here in the pUNISHMENT iNC. BBS.\n\n It could happen that some of the doors and tools listed here are currently\n missing because there are currently under development !\n\n\n@{b}@{u}Who creates FAME ?@{ub}@{uu}\n\n@{fg fill}Main programmer:@{fg text}\n\n - David ''Strider'' Wettig (tRSi) [email removed]\n\n@{fg fill}Additional programmer:@{fg text}\n\n - Oliver ''Bloodrock'' Lange (tRSi) [email removed]\n - Ulrich Arne ''Beatnik'' Jansen (tRSi) [email removed]\n - Sascha ''Siegel'' Pfalz (tRSi) [email removed]\n\n@{fg fill}FAME-Development-Team:@{fg text}\n\n - David ''Strider'' Wettig (tRSi) [email removed]\n - Oliver ''Bloodrock'' Lange (tRSi) [email removed]\n - Ulrich Arne ''Beatnik'' Jansen (tRSi) [email removed]\n - Sascha ''Siegel'' Pfalz (tRSi) [email removed]\n - Andreas ''ByteAndi'' Petermann (tRSi)\n - Dirk ''Spy'' Holzkampf (tRSi) [email removed]\n - Bodo ''Dr.Dre!'' Hoffmann (tRSi) [email removed]\n@ENDNODE\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',11866,1,0,NULL,NULL,'nvx_dc21','scan',1780048650);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('nvx_dl05','NVX_DL05.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/NVX_DL05.LHA','ud-info','XIM','ud-info',NULL,'OrdYnE','NVX','______  \|  Y |  /\__| Y  \__/\ /\__  /\___ MaF| \/\ \  : |_/    |   __/\_ Y _/ \/ |    \     |\__   :   /  /  :  \PreSents',replace('______/\ .__ _.__  __._ /\\n______  \|  Y |  /\__| Y  \__/\ /\__  /\___\nMaF| \/\ \  : |_/    |   __/\_ Y _/ \/\n   |    \     |\__   :   /  /  :  \PreSents\n   !    |\    |  \   |  / _/   |   \\n___:    : \___|___\____/__\____|    \_/\  _\n<>=­    í----------------------`-----''--\/-\n       dOWNLOAD iNFORMATiONS V0.5\n    a cOOL XIM dOOR fOR aMI-EXPRESS\n  sHOWS uSER hIS sTATS/bAUD rATE/cONF\n      aLSO hAS cOOL cOOKiE oUTPUT\n     bY OrdYnE / vEnOm  nERVE aXiS\n','\n',char(10)),'ud-info.Doc',replace('\n\n_______________.___  ______  _\n\____  ____/   |  ¬\/  __ ¬\_\ -  -- --- ----------------------------.\n_/   \/  ¬\_   _    \_ \____/__           ×X× ·T·H·E· ·E·D·G·E· ×X×  í\n\_____     /___|     /___     /           ×X× A NERVE AXiS BBS! ×X×  !\n-:---l____/----l____/---\____/--- --- -- -  ×X× 01226  289303 ×X×    |\n !                                                                   !\n :                         ______ _ _______   ______ _ _______       :\n !  ×X× NERVE AXiS! ×X×   /  __ ¬\_  ____ ¬\_/  ___/__    __  \_     |\n O                       /   \____/__   /   /   |    ¬\_  \____/__   ¦\n ¡                       \_____     /______/_____      /_ __     /   !\n ¦            - -- --- -------\____/------------l_____/----\____/------\n !                                                                   |\n ¦       STAFF:  [OrdYnE/NVX]    [EPSiLON/NVX]    [ToD/NVX]          !\n |                                                                   !\n : × AMiGA ONLY PD × GAMES × DEMOS × MODS × /XPRESS DOORS × UTiLS ×  ¦\n |   ×X× 68030 P0WER ×X× 900 MEGABYTE 0NLiNE ×X× 28×8dS USR ×X×      !\n `-------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n\n°¤ðÇð¤°¬¯¬°¤ðÇð¤°¬¯¬°¤ðÇð¤°¬¯¬°¤ðÇð¤°¬¯¬°¤ðÇð¤°¬¯¬°¤ðÇð¤°¬¯¬°¤ðÇð¤°¬¯¬°¤ðÇð¤°\n\n        ____  _____ _____  ___________. __________\n      _/    \|   ___ __ ¬\_\____ ¬\_  |/    / __ ¬\_\n      \     \\   ¬\_ \____/__ \/  _/  ·    /  \____/__\n       \____|\_____/___     /_/    \______/_ ___     /\n                      \____/  \_____/          \____/ ___ _ __\n                                      _____________  /       /______\n                                      \_____  ¬\   \/   /___/    __/__\n                                       /   |    \_     /    \______  ¬\_\n                                       \___|     /     \_____/    _____/\n                                           l____/  /\___\ \________/\n                                             _ ___/\n\n\n\n\n\n--^-- --- dOWNLOAD iNFORMATiONS v0.5 bY OrdYnE & vEnOm / nERVE aXiS --- -^--\n\n\n\n\nwHOT iS dOWNLOAD iNFORMATiONS ?\n\nDownload informations is just a small XIM door for /X-Press \nto show users there current status..eg amount of upload / downloads\nthey have made and the ammount of time they have left + other stuff..\n\n\n\n\niNSTALATION :\n\nJust copy the insluded files into the realative directorys and have all\nthe ushual crap installed to run XIM doors\n\nMake Shure You Put The DOWNLOADMSG.TXT in Each conf you want to run it from\n\n\n\n\nCookie File :\n\nThis door also runs a cookie file that can be edited by you to include\nwhot you like.Its called Pea-Soup\n\n\n\n \nGreetings :\n\nGreetings go to..\n     Epsilon (thanx for the cookie help)\n      Mdr , Discordia , Rocky , Gromit , Fury , Tod , Crash! ,\nFlo , Nik , Mark Panther , Cosy , No5 , Sasha , Chrono And everyone else\nwho hates me!.\n\n\n *** A BIG THANX TO VEMON FOR THE CONVERSION FROM REXX TO C ! ***\n\n\nHistory :\n\nV 0.1b  : First attempt in rexx by Ordyne\nV 0.2b  : Look of the door changed\nV 0.3b  : Cookie added\nV 0.4b  : Slight Changes in Look again (still in rexx)\nV 0.5   : First Release Version  * Converted into C by Venom *\n\n\n\nCheck the output of this door in the ilbm file included!!!\n\nright go and install it!\n\n\n--^-- --- dOWNLOAD iNFORMATiONS v0.5 bY OrdYnE & vEnOm / nERVE aXiS --- -^--\n\n\n        ____  _____ _____  ___________. __________\n      _/    \|   ___ __ ¬\_\____ ¬\_  |/    / __ ¬\_\n      \     \\   ¬\_ \____/__ \/  _/  ·    /  \____/__\n       \____|\_____/___     /_/    \______/_ ___     /\n                      \____/  \_____/          \____/ ___ _ __\n                                      _____________  /       /______\n                                      \_____  ¬\   \/   /___/    __/__\n             ×X× TRY THESE ×X×         /   |    \_     /    \______  ¬\_\n                                       \___|     /     \_____/    _____/\n         ×X× NERVE AXiS BOARDS ×X×         l____/  /\___\ \________/\n                                             _ ___/\n\n        .-------------------.--------------.-------.-------------.\n        ¦     BOARD NAME    ¦    NUMBER    ¦ON-LINE¦    SYSOP    ¦\n        |-------------------.--------------.-------.-------------|\n        ! tHE edGE          ¦ 01226-289303 ¦ 24 Hr ¦ OrdYnE      !\n        ¦ TRiCK 0R TREAT II ¦ 01733-391797 ¦ 24 Hr ¦ ZiPZiPPY    :\n        ¦ P0WER PLANT       ¦ 01299-431590 ¦ 24 Hr ¦ CHANCER     !\n        : 13th HOUR         ¦ 01704-505845 ¦ 24 Hr ¦ ACE + VENOM ¦\n        `--------------------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',14003,3,0,NULL,NULL,'nvx_dl05','scan',1780048650);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('nvx_lc10','NVX-LC10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/NVX-LC10.LHA',NULL,'XIM','LE-window6.12',NULL,'VENOM/NERVE','NVX','(  /(__/_\   ''/___\(__/_   (___\`_\\_,|`---. «------------------------------------------'' V-LASTCALLERS V1.00 BY VENOM/NERVE AXIS 96',replace(' ___ ___ ____       ___     ___  _  _ . ___\n(  /(__/_\   ''/___\(__/_   (___\`_\\_,|`---.\n«------------------------------------------''\n V-LASTCALLERS V1.00 BY VENOM/NERVE AXIS 96\nFAME util that produces:\n· last callers with up to 20 users\n· weekly statistics\n· system records\n· mini callers log\n-------------------------------[tGø/-T!]---»\n','\n',char(10)),'LastCallers.Guide',replace('@DATABASE "LastCallers.Guide"\n@NODE Main "LastCallers"\n\n                                   ::]%[:: n e r v e   a x i s ::]%[::\n                                                  .\n                                               · /-------- -- -\n -  - ----------------------------------------/ /  code: venom/nerve axis\n          util: v-lastcallers v1.oo          / /------------------ -- -  -\n         -  - -- ---------------------------/ /\n                                           /\n\n             :::]%[::: fame util release :::]%[:::\n\n\n                @{"  " LINK "Intro"} Intro        - What the hell is this?\n                @{"  " LINK "Install"} Installation - Where to shove it :)\n                @{"  " LINK "Usage"} Usage        - How to make it go *PING*\n                @{"  " LINK "Credits"} Credits      - Who made it?\n                @{"  " LINK "Contact"} Contact      - Really wanna talk to him?\n                @{"  " LINK "FAME"} FAME         - The nicest system around\n                @{"  " LINK "Structures"} Structures   - Want to use my data files?\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Intro "Introduction"\n\n                                  ..\n                             .---:  :---------.\n                             |   ····         |\n                            [%] iNTRODUCTiON [%]\n                             |         ....   |\n                             `---------:  :---''\n                                        ··\n\nA  dinky good looking little FAME lastcallers utility that will produce the\nfollowing outputs:\n\n	· last callers with up to 20 users\n	· weekly statistics\n	· system records\n	· mini callers log\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Install "Installation"\n\n                                  ..\n                             .---:  :---------.\n                             |   ····         |\n                            [%] iNSTALLATiON [%]\n                             |         ....   |\n                             `---------:  :---''\n                                        ··\n\nPut V-LastCallers into a directory within your DOORS:  assign.  The obvious\nchoice would be a dir called "V-LASTCALLERS" or something similar :)\n\nPut the 3 header files in the same dir as the program, the files are:\n\n	· LCHeader.TXT - Last Callers header file\n	· WSHeader.TXT - Week Stats header file\n	· RSHeader.TXT - Record Stats header file\n\nThe program will look in PROGDIR: for all it''s header/data files.\n\nTo make the lastcallers door update at every logoff put a copy of the\nLastCallers.Script file in FAME:Node{x}/NodeBatches/LogoffBatches/\nwhere {x} is the number of your modem node(s).\n\nSo if you have 2 modem nodes then put a copy of the script in each one.\n\nIf the script is missing then it should look like...\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------\n.key node\n.bra {\n.ket }\n\nDOORS:V-TOOLS/V-LastCallers/LastCallers {node} 10 SCREENS:BULLS/VLC_LASTCALLERS.TXT SCREENS:BULLS/VLC_WEEKSTATS.TXT SCREENS:BULLS/VLC_RECORDSTATS.TXT FAME:Mini_Callers.Log\n------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nobviously the paths will be different for your system.\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Usage "Usage"\n\n                               ..\n                          .---:  :--------------.\n                          |   ····              |\n                         [%] USiNG THE PROGRAM [%]\n                          |              ....   |\n                          `--------------:  :---''\n                                          ··\n\nUsage: LastCallers <node> <lines> <LCFile> <WSFile> <RSFile> <MCLFile>\n\n<node>    : the node to update for\n<lines>   : the number of users in the LastCallers output file\n<LCFile>  : filename to save LastCallers bulletin as\n<WSFile>  : filename to save WeeklyStats bulletin as\n<RSFile>  : filename to save RecordStats bulletin as\n<MCLFile> : filename to save MiniCallersLog as\n\ne.g.\n\nLastCallers 1 10 BULLS:LAST10 BULLS:WEEKLY BULLS:RECORDS FAME:MINI.LOG\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Structures "Structures"\n\n                                ..\n                           .---:  :-------.\n                           |   ····       |\n                          [%] STRUCTURES [%]\n                           |       ....   |\n                           `-------:  :---''\n                                    ··\n\nTo  allow  other  programmers  to  re-use  the  data files stored here, the\nfollowing  structures have been included.  At time of writing FAME does not\nwrite  details  of  messages  written/comments  to sysop, therefore certain\nitems in the structure are marked as *NOT USED*, if FAME starts writing the\ndetails to the callerslog these items will be filled.\n\n\n                  @{"  " LINK "LastCallers.DAT"} LastCallers.DAT - 20 Last Callers\n                  @{"  " LINK "Days.DAT"} Days.DAT        - Last weeks stats\n                  @{"  " LINK "Records.DAT"} Records.DAT     - System Records\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE LastCallers.DAT "LastCallers.DAT"\n\nStructure of an entry in LastCallers.DAT - there are 20 of these in the\nfile, the first is the latest logoff.\n\nstruct CLStats\n{\n    int     nodenumber,         // Node number\n            logontype;          // Type of logon             *DEFINES BELOW*\n    char    logondate[9],       // Date in fomat MM-DD-YY\n            logontime[9];       // Time in format HH:MM:SS\n    int     userslot;           // FAME slot number\n    char    username[32],       // FAME User name\n            userloc[32],        // FAME User location\n            logoffdate[9],      // Date in fomat MM-DD-YY\n            logofftime[9];      // Time in format HH:MM:SS\n    int     timeon,             // Time online in mins\n            logofftype,         // Type of logoff            *DEFINES BELOW*\n            speed,              // Connect speed (baud rate)\n            confjoins,          // Number of confs joined, inc auto-rejoin\n            fileviews,          // Number of files viewed (menu command V)\n            pwfails,            // Number of password fails, inc system & NUP\n            dirscans,           // Number of dir scans inc newfiles scans\n            msgwrite,           // Number of messages written.    *NOT USED*\n            msgread,            // Number of times cmd R used.    *NOT USED*\n            pages,              // Number of times the sysop was paged\n            comments,           // Number of times cmd C used.    *NOT USED*\n            ealls,              // Number of EALLs written        *NOT USED*\n            newuser,            // Is the user a newuser        0=NO 1=YES\n            sysopchats,         // Number of times user chatted to sysop\n            changestats,        // Number of times command W was used\n            sys_accountedits,   // SYSOP - Number of times cmd ''1'' was used\n            sys_clogviews,      // SYSOP - Number of times cmd ''2'' was used\n            sys_udlogviews,     // SYSOP - Number of times cmd ''3'' was used\n            sys_doorlogviews,   // SYSOP - Number of times cmd ''4'' was used\n            sys_listedits,      // SYSOP - Number of times cmd ''5'' was used\n            sys_fileedits,      // SYSOP - Number of times cmd ''6'' was used\n            sys_doslists,       // SYSOP - Number of times cmd ''7'' was used\n            sys_dosdirs,        // SYSOP - Number of times cmd ''8'' was used\n            sys_dosinfos,       // SYSOP - Number of times cmd ''9'' was used\n            sys_shells,         // SYSOP - Number of times ''SHELL'' was used\n            ul_files,           // Number of files uploaded\n            ul_kbytes,          // Size of uploads (in KB)\n            dl_files,           // Number of files downloaded\n            dl_kbytes;          // Size of downloads (in KB)\n    char    sparespace[40];     // Space for later expansion\n};\n\n/*----------------------( Defines for type of logon )----------------------*/\n#define LOGON_UNKNOWN    0                          // Fallback value\n#define LOGON_MODEM      1                          // Normal modem connect\n#define LOGON_RELOGON    2                          // ReLogon (RL from menu)\n#define LOGON_SYSOP      3                          // F1 or SF1\n#define LOGON_LOCAL      4                          // F2 or SF2\n/*--------------------( Defines for type of logoff )-----------------------*/\n#define LOGOFF_UNKNOWN   0                          // Fallback value\n#define LOGOFF_NORMAL    1                          // Normal (G from menu)\n#define LOGOFF_TIMEOUT   2                          // Door & Node timeout\n#define LOGOFF_RELOGON   3                          // ReLogon (RL from menu)\n#define LOGOFF_KICK      4                          // User kicked (F10)\n#define LOGOFF_TIMELIM   5                          // User timelimit reached\n#define LOGOFF_CARRIER   6                          // User lost carrier\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Days.DAT "Days.DAT"\n\nStructure of an entry in Days.DAT - there are 8 records in the file.\nThe first is the current day and is still being filled with each call,\nthe second is yesterday, the third is the day before yesterday etc etc\n\nstruct DayStats\n{\n    char    lastupdate[9];      // Date of last update (MM-DD-YY)\n    int     calls,              // Number of calls\n            mins,               // Number of mins in use\n            confjoins,          // Number of join confs (inc auto-rejoin)\n            fileviews,          // Number of files viewed (menu command V)\n            pwfails,            // Number of password fails, inc system & NUP\n            dirscans,           // Number of dir scans inc newfiles scans\n            msgwrite,           // Number of messages written.    *NOT USED*\n            msgread,            // Number of times cmd R used.    *NOT USED*\n            pages,              // Number of times the sysop was paged\n            comments,           // Number of times cmd C used.    *NOT USED*\n            ealls,              // Number of EALLs written        *NOT USED*\n            newusers,           // Number of new users\n            sysopchats,         // Number of times user chatted to sysop\n            changestats,        // Number of times command W was used\n            sys_accountedits,   // SYSOP - Number of times cmd ''1'' was used\n            sys_clogviews,      // SYSOP - Number of times cmd ''2'' was used\n            sys_udlogviews,     // SYSOP - Number of times cmd ''3'' was used\n            sys_doorlogviews,   // SYSOP - Number of times cmd ''4'' was used\n            sys_listedits,      // SYSOP - Number of times cmd ''5'' was used\n            sys_fileedits,      // SYSOP - Number of times cmd ''6'' was used\n            sys_doslists,       // SYSOP - Number of times cmd ''7'' was used\n            sys_dosdirs,        // SYSOP - Number of times cmd ''8'' was used\n            sys_dosinfos,       // SYSOP - Number of times cmd ''9'' was used\n            sys_shells,         // SYSOP - Number of times ''SHELL'' was used\n            ul_files,           // Number of files uploaded\n            ul_kbytes,          // Size of uploads (in KB)\n            dl_files,           // Number of files downloaded\n            dl_kbytes,          // Size of downloads (in KB)\n            lostcarriers;       // Number of lost carriers\n    char    sparespace[36];     // Space for later expansion\n};\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Records.DAT "Records.DAT"\n\nStructure of the system records file, the dates are in standard C format\n(number of seconds since Jan 1st 1970 or whatever it is).\n\nstruct SystemRecords\n{\n    int     calls,              calls_date,             // Number of calls\n            mins,               mins_date,              // Number of mins in use\n            confjoins,          confjoins_date,         // Number of join confs (inc auto-rejoin)\n            fileviews,          fileviews_date,         // Number of files viewed (menu command V)\n            pwfails,            pwfails_date,           // Number of password fails, inc system & NUP\n            dirscans,           dirscans_date,          // Number of dir scans inc newfiles scans\n            msgwrite,           msgwrite_date,          // Number of messages written.    *NOT USED*\n            msgread,            msgread_date,           // Number of times cmd R used.    *NOT USED*\n            pages,              pages_date,             // Number of times the sysop was paged\n            comments,           comments_date,          // Number of times cmd C used.    *NOT USED*\n            ealls,              ealls_date,             // Number of EALLs written        *NOT USED*\n            newusers,           newusers_date,          // Number of new users\n            sysopchats,         sysopchats_date,        // Number of times user chatted to sysop\n            changestats,        changestats_date,       // Number of times command W was used\n            sys_accountedits,   sys_accountedits_date,  // SYSOP - Number of times cmd ''1'' was used\n            sys_clogviews,      sys_clogviews_date,     // SYSOP - Number of times cmd ''2'' was used\n            sys_udlogviews,     sys_udlogviews_date,    // SYSOP - Number of times cmd ''3'' was used\n            sys_doorlogviews,   sys_doorlogviews_date,  // SYSOP - Number of times cmd ''4'' was used\n            sys_listedits,      sys_listedits_date,     // SYSOP - Number of times cmd ''5'' was used\n            sys_fileedits,      sys_fileedits_date,     // SYSOP - Number of times cmd ''6'' was used\n            sys_doslists,       sys_doslists_date,      // SYSOP - Number of times cmd ''7'' was used\n            sys_dosdirs,        sys_dosdirs_date,       // SYSOP - Number of times cmd ''8'' was used\n            sys_dosinfos,       sys_dosinfos_date,      // SYSOP - Number of times cmd ''9'' was used\n            sys_shells,         sys_shells_date,        // SYSOP - Number of times ''SHELL'' was used\n            ul_files,           ul_files_date,          // Number of files uploaded\n            ul_kbytes,          ul_kbytes_date,         // Size of uploads (in KB)\n            dl_files,           dl_files_date,          // Number of files downloaded\n            dl_kbytes,          dl_kbytes_date,         // Size of downloads (in KB)\n            lostcarriers,       lostcarriers_date;      // Number of lost carriers\n    char    sparespace[32];                             // Space for later expansion\n};\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Credits "Credits"\n\n                                ..\n                           .---:  :-------------.\n                           |   ····             |\n                          [%] CREDiTS & GREETS [%]\n                           |             ....   |\n                           `-------------:  :---''\n                                          ··\n\n                                  All Work\n\n                      Code & Mountain Dew - Venom/Nvx\n                      Docs & Gloom Deluxe - TANGo/Nvx\n\n\n              Quick Hellos From Venom To These Lovely People\n\n Hybrid, Reflex, MDR, Mic Flair, Bill, Video Nasty, Icon, MrFrapp, Memo, MrZ\n   Biggles, Delta TX, Ghostrider, Strider, Dr.Dre, Sigel, Derrow, Mad Dan,\n  Scouser, Narcosis, Neelix, Ordyne, Sidewinder, Stainless Steel Rat, Raoul\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Contact "Contact"\n\n                               ..\n                          .---:  :---------------.\n                          |   ····               |\n                         [%] CONTACT THE AUTHOR [%]\n                          |               ....   |\n                          `---------------:  :---''\n                                           ··\n\n                             1 3 t h   H O U R\n\n                    Nerve Axis UKHQ · Twisted Dist Site\n\n                      + 4 4   0 1 7 0 4   5 0 5 8 4 5\n\n                    33k6 Courier Power - 2 Node Ringdown\n      \n                Ace ^ Venom ^ TANGo ^ Biggles ^ Crash ^ Zone\n\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE FAME "About FAME"\n\n@{b}@{u}What should FAME costs ?@{ub}@{uu}\n\n Registered Version:  110 USD / 150 DM\n Betatester Version:  145 USD / 200 DM\n\n\n@{b}@{u}What is included in the FAME-package ?@{ub}@{uu}\n\n Server, SystemEditor, MainPart, FAMEHydra.FIM, FAMEError.FIM\n\n FAME.library FAMEChat.FIM programmed by Bloodrock/tRSi\n\n FAMEFullEd.FIM, FAMEScript.FIM programmed by Beatnik/tRSi\n\n MUI UserEditor, FAMEDoorHelp.FIM, FAMEInfo programmed by SieGeL/tRSi\n\n Also some doors and tools from the FAME-Development-Team are included,\n but this doors are only unregistered Versions and have therefor some\n limitations. The registered Versions of those doors and the Informations\n how to get them are available here in the pUNISHMENT iNC. BBS.\n\n It could happen that some of the doors and tools listed here are currently\n missing because there are currently under development !\n\n\n@{b}@{u}Who creates FAME ?@{ub}@{uu}\n\n@{fg fill}Main programmer:@{fg text}\n\n - David ''Strider'' Wettig (tRSi) [email removed]\n\n@{fg fill}Additional programmer:@{fg text}\n\n - Oliver ''Bloodrock'' Lange (tRSi) [email removed]\n - Ulrich Arne ''Beatnik'' Jansen (tRSi) [email removed]\n - Sascha ''Siegel'' Pfalz (tRSi) [email removed]\n\n@{fg fill}FAME-Development-Team:@{fg text}\n\n - David ''Strider'' Wettig (tRSi) [email removed]\n - Oliver ''Bloodrock'' Lange (tRSi) [email removed]\n - Ulrich Arne ''Beatnik'' Jansen (tRSi) [email removed]\n - Sascha ''Siegel'' Pfalz (tRSi) [email removed]\n - Andreas ''ByteAndi'' Petermann (tRSi)\n - Dirk ''Spy'' Holzkampf (tRSi) [email removed]\n - Bodo ''Dr.Dre!'' Hoffmann (tRSi) [email removed]\n@ENDNODE\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',47420,6,0,NULL,NULL,'nvx_lc10','scan',1780048650);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('nvx_rem2','NVX-REM2.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/NVX-REM2.LHA','dirsizer','XIM','REXXDOOR',NULL,NULL,'NVX','(  //__/_\   ''/___\/__/_  (___\`_\\_ |`---. + --- ---------------------------------\_| |    REM Version 1.2a / Real E-Mail      |',replace(' ___ ___ ____       ___    ___  _  _ . ___  \n(  //__/_\   ''/___\/__/_  (___\`_\\_ |`---. \n + --- ---------------------------------\_| \n |    REM Version 1.2a / Real E-Mail      | \n | An E-Mail door for FAME / Ami-Express  | \n |            nEEDS: mUI & yAM            | \n |     1st Public Release - 12/01/97      |\n `----------------------------------------'' \n','\n',char(10)),'bbstag.txt',replace('\n\n   E-MAIL SENT VIA "La Luna BBS" running FAME/AMIGA 2000/28/17/030/2node \n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',30057,5,0,NULL,NULL,'nvx_rem2','scan',1780048650);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('nvx_rem5','NVX-REM5.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/NVX-REM5.LHA','dirsizer','XIM','REXXDOOR',NULL,NULL,'NVX','(  //__/_\   ''/___\/__/_  (___\`_\\_ |`---. + --- ---------------------------------\_| |    REM Version 1.5 / Real E-Mail       |',replace(' ___ ___ ____       ___    ___  _  _ . ___ \n(  //__/_\   ''/___\/__/_  (___\`_\\_ |`---.\n + --- ---------------------------------\_|\n |    REM Version 1.5 / Real E-Mail       |\n | An E-Mail door for FAME & Ami-Express  |\n |            nEEDS: mUI & yAM            |\n `----------------------------------------''','\n',char(10)),'REMAIL.DOC',replace('\n           REMail - Real E-Mailer for FAME / /X BBS Systems v1.5\n          -------------------------------------------------------\n\nAnyway, I won''t go into great detail about the installation, cause I havent\ngot the time to write docs, and this is only an alpha version mainly for\ntesting.  If it fucks up you HD / E-Mail DONT blame me. You have been warned!\n\nRequirements:	YAM v1.2+ (Yet Another Mailer) available from Aminet\n		MUI v3.1+ (For YAM) available from Aminet\n		\n		Amiga OS 2+\n		Ami-Express system 3.9+\n		FAME BBS system 1.23b+\n\n		A valid Internet account!!!\n\n		The REMail archive named: NVX-REM5.lha\n\n		contents:-\n\n		  Personal:REMail/fame/doors/REMail/c (dir)\n     		  	dirsizer                         \n     		  Personal:REMail/fame/doors/REMail/docs (dir)\n       			REMail.doc                       \n  		  bbsaddress.cfg                   bbstag.txt\n  		  REMail.aim                       title.txt\n\n\nUsing YAM as your E-Mail interface, REMail allows you to utilise YAM\nthrough an Ami-Express or FAME BBS.\n\nThere are 2 door commands which should be called:\n		\n		EMAIL\n		EMAILS\n\nThey should both be placed in the BBSCMD drawer.\n\nEMAIL calls the REMail programme from the bbs which allows users to write/read\nemail as it comes in through YAM, as per normal.\n\nEMAILS actually checks incoming mail to the specified user when they logon.\n\nEMAILS should be called in a bull.txt script:-\n\n-----cut------\n\n~CC_EMAILS\n\n-----cut------\n\nBoth door commands are set as AIM and should have a stack of 10000.\n\n\nThe file BBSTAG.txt contains the tagline which is added to the end of every\nemail sent from your BBS.\n\neg:\n\n   E-MAIL SENT VIA "La Luna BBS" running FAME/AMIGA 2000/28/17/030/2node \n\n\nThe file TITLE.txt contains the header for REMail.\n\neg:\n         _________        ____    ____    ______      _____   _____\n        |      ___|      |    \__/    |__\_____ \__ _/_____\_|     |\n        |     /___   __  |            |      __    |         |     |\n        |      __/  |__| |    |\/|    |       /    |         |     |___\n        |_________|      |____|  |____|____________|_________l_________|\n\n\nThe most important file BBSADDRESS.cfg should contain your E-Mail address.\n\neg:\n\[email removed]\n\nCopy the DIRSIZER file in /C/ to your own C: directory. Thanx go out\nto Venom/NVX for this HANDY little tool! \n\nAdd an assign to your user-startup assigning REMAIL: to the correct path of \nthe REMAIL.AIM file!\n\nOk, i believe that''s it, and hopefully it will all work! Well it does on my\nBBS ok. sort of..!! :-)\n\nThis is only a temporary measusre to offer users the chance of having e-mail\non the BBS they connect to, as there are no public email doors released yet!\n\nAny problems, contact me below, or E-Mail [email removed]\n\n                             .l.a.  .l.u.n.a.\n           _____    ____          _____    ____ __:_____________\n          /    /___/    \        /    /___/   /   |   _    /    \\n         /    /   //     \      /    /   /  _/|   |   /   //     \\n     tGø/________/        \    /________/         |__/   /        \\n                 ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯             ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯  /____\¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n\n           68o3o/28/17mb [%] 96oo-288oo [%] baud locked @ 1152oo\n\n                     free email service · cool ratios\n\n                   system operators are neelix & epsilon\n                      zone - crash - venom - maverick\n\n                 running latest fame · instant validation\n\n         node 1: +44 (o)12o6 5o1835     node 2: +44 (o)12o6 5o38oo\n\n         node 3: dynamic ^ telnet       node 4: dynamic ^ telnet\n\n                  .l.a.  .l.u.n.a. - a.n. n.v.x. u.k.h.q.\n\n\nThanx to Venom for the Idea, and to all the NVX guys and \nother testers that have supported me over the last few months! :-)\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',33922,6,0,NULL,NULL,'nvx_rem5','scan',1780048650);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('nvx_ud11','NVX-UD11.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/NVX-UD11.LHA',NULL,'XIM','UDClean.000',NULL,'VENOM/NERVE','NVX','(  /(__/_\   ''/___\(__/_   (___\`_\\_,|`---. «------------------------------------------'' V-UDCLEAN V1.01 BY VENOM/NERVE AXIS 96',replace(' ___ ___ ____       ___     ___  _  _ . ___\n(  /(__/_\   ''/___\(__/_   (___\`_\\_,|`---.\n«------------------------------------------''\n   V-UDCLEAN V1.01 BY VENOM/NERVE AXIS 96\n  FAME utility to check userdata for users\n  who haven''t called over x number of days\n This ver recognises deleted users properly\n-------------------------------[tGø/-T!]---»\n','\n',char(10)),'UDClean.Guide',replace('@DATABASE "UDClean.Guide"\n@NODE Main "UDCLean"\n\n                                   ::]%[:: n e r v e   a x i s ::]%[::\n                                                  .\n                                               · /-------- -- -\n -  - ----------------------------------------/ /  code: venom/nerve axis\n          door: v-udclean v1.oo              / /------------------ -- -  -\n         -  - -- ---------------------------/ /\n                                           /\n\n             :::]%[::: fame util release :::]%[:::\n\n\n                @{"  " LINK "Intro"} Intro        - What the hell is this?\n                @{"  " LINK "Install"} Installation - Where to shove it :)\n                @{"  " LINK "Usage"} Usage        - How to make it go *PING*\n                @{"  " LINK "Credits"} Credits      - Who made it?\n                @{"  " LINK "Contact"} Contact      - Really wanna talk to him?\n                @{"  " LINK "FAME"} FAME         - The nicest system around\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Intro "Introduction"\n\n                                  ..\n                             .---:  :---------.\n                             |   ····         |\n                            [%] iNTRODUCTiON [%]\n                             |         ....   |\n                             `---------:  :---''\n                                        ··\n\nFAME  util  to  check number of inactive users over x number of days.  This\nallows  the  sysop  to maintain a steady userbase and delete accounts where\n                              they see fit :)\n\nThis version checks the Deleted_Or_Not flag properly so won''t re-list any\nusers that have already been deleted.\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Install "Installation"\n\n                                  ..\n                             .---:  :---------.\n                             |   ····         |\n                            [%] iNSTALLATiON [%]\n                             |         ....   |\n                             `---------:  :---''\n                                        ··\n\nJust  copy  this  to  any  directory  you  store  your bbs utilities and run\nwhenever  you  wish.  There are two versions, a standard version and the 020\nversion. Rename the command to "udclean" and put it wherever.  Simple eh? :)\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Usage "Usage"\n\n                               ..\n                          .---:  :--------------.\n                          |   ····              |\n                         [%] USiNG THE PROGRAM [%]\n                          |              ....   |\n                          `--------------:  :---''\n                                          ··\n\nUsage: UDClean <userdata> <days> <header> <footer> [<ignore>]\n\nExample: UDClean FAME:user.data 90 Header.txt Footer.txt Ignore.txt\n\nThe  ignore  file  is a list of users that you wish to ignore no matter how\nmany  days it has been since their last call, perhaps members of your group\n    who are at university or don''t have regular access to a modem etc.\n\nYou  can  use  it  as a bulletin or just from the cli to keep an eye on who\n              isn''t supporting your board on a regular basis.\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Credits "Credits"\n\n                                ..\n                           .---:  :-------------.\n                           |   ····             |\n                          [%] CREDiTS & GREETS [%]\n                           |             ....   |\n                           `-------------:  :---''\n                                          ··\n\n                                  All Work\n\n                      Code & Mountain Dew - Venom/Nvx\n                      Docs & Gloom Deluxe - TANGo/Nvx\n\n\n              Quick Hellos From Venom To These Lovely People\n\n Hybrid, Reflex, MDR, Mic Flair, Bill, Video Nasty, Icon, MrFrapp, Memo, MrZ\n   Biggles, Delta TX, Ghostrider, Strider, Dr.Dre, Sigel, Derrow, Mad Dan,\n  Scouser, Narcosis, Neelix, Ordyne, Sidewinder, Stainless Steel Rat, Raoul\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Contact "Contact"\n\n                               ..\n                          .---:  :---------------.\n                          |   ····               |\n                         [%] CONTACT THE AUTHOR [%]\n                          |               ....   |\n                          `---------------:  :---''\n                                           ··\n\n                             1 3 t h   H O U R\n\n                    Nerve Axis UKHQ · Twisted Dist Site\n\n                      + 4 4   0 1 7 0 4   5 0 5 8 4 5\n\n                    33k6 Courier Power - 2 Node Ringdown\n      \n                Ace ^ Venom ^ TANGo ^ Biggles ^ Crash ^ Zone\n\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE FAME "About FAME"\n\n@{b}@{u}What should FAME costs ?@{ub}@{uu}\n\n Registered Version:  110 USD / 150 DM\n Betatester Version:  145 USD / 200 DM\n\n\n@{b}@{u}What is included in the FAME-package ?@{ub}@{uu}\n\n Server, SystemEditor, MainPart, FAMEHydra.FIM, FAMEError.FIM\n\n FAME.library FAMEChat.FIM programmed by Bloodrock/tRSi\n\n FAMEFullEd.FIM, FAMEScript.FIM programmed by Beatnik/tRSi\n\n MUI UserEditor, FAMEDoorHelp.FIM, FAMEInfo programmed by SieGeL/tRSi\n\n Also some doors and tools from the FAME-Development-Team are included,\n but this doors are only unregistered Versions and have therefor some\n limitations. The registered Versions of those doors and the Informations\n how to get them are available here in the pUNISHMENT iNC. BBS.\n\n It could happen that some of the doors and tools listed here are currently\n missing because there are currently under development !\n\n\n@{b}@{u}Who creates FAME ?@{ub}@{uu}\n\n@{fg fill}Main programmer:@{fg text}\n\n - David ''Strider'' Wettig (tRSi) [email removed]\n\n@{fg fill}Additional programmer:@{fg text}\n\n - Oliver ''Bloodrock'' Lange (tRSi) [email removed]\n - Ulrich Arne ''Beatnik'' Jansen (tRSi) [email removed]\n - Sascha ''Siegel'' Pfalz (tRSi) [email removed]\n\n@{fg fill}FAME-Development-Team:@{fg text}\n\n - David ''Strider'' Wettig (tRSi) [email removed]\n - Oliver ''Bloodrock'' Lange (tRSi) [email removed]\n - Ulrich Arne ''Beatnik'' Jansen (tRSi) [email removed]\n - Sascha ''Siegel'' Pfalz (tRSi) [email removed]\n - Andreas ''ByteAndi'' Petermann (tRSi)\n - Dirk ''Spy'' Holzkampf (tRSi) [email removed]\n - Bodo ''Dr.Dre!'' Hoffmann (tRSi) [email removed]\n@ENDNODE\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',16002,2,0,NULL,NULL,'nvx_ud11','scan',1780048650);
