  |  _|___|  | |   |\    /    (___|   |__|  2\\n\   |   _  _|\  /|   |_  |   ~  \|   :_ |_|   |_\  /|    |_: |  __|_    /\n 2  |_____|  :\/ |_____| |___|__||_____||_______|\/ |______| |______|  2\n 2\   |      :::  __    /          \ /          \    __  :::      |   /2\n -/   |_/\  _:::_/\ \__/   T H E    X    T H E   \__/ /\_:::_  /\_|   \-\n 0        \/ / \ \/_/     O M E N  / \  O M E N     \_\/ / \ \/        0\n/7 __________\_/__________________/   \__________________\_/__________ 7\\n\_/ * kEWl sTAFf! * dOCS''N''SOLVEs * _ * mODULEs * mEGa /x wAREHOUSe * \_/\n  \________________________________/ \________________________________/\n\n=============================================================================\n                         Mega Offer V0.1b (11-Dec-94)\n=============================================================================\n\n                              @{"    DESCRIPTION     " LINK "DESC"}\n                              @{"  COPYRIGHT NOTICE  " LINK "COPY"}\n                              @{"    REQUIREMENTS    " LINK "REQ"}\n                              @{"    INSTALLATION    " LINK "INSTALL"}\n                              @{"       USAGE        " LINK "USAGE"}\n                              @{" BUGS & SUGGESTIONS " LINK "BUGS"}\n                              @{"     GREETINGS      " LINK "GREETS"}\n                              @{"      HISTORY       " LINK "HIST"}\n                              @{"  FUTURE PROJECTS!  " LINK "PROJECTS"}\n\n=============================================================================\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "DESC" "Description"\n@NEXT "COPY"\n@PREV "MAIN"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\nDESCRIPTION:\n\n  Handles text offers that often occur as EALL msg''s on kewl boards!\n\n=============================================================================\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "COPY" "Copyright Notice"\n@NEXT "REQ"\n@PREV "DESC"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\nCOPYRIGHT NOTICE:\n\n                              (C) 1994 THE OMEN!\n                             All Rights Reserved\n                                  -CARDWARE-\n\n                                  Coded by :\n\n                                    Melody\n\n\n                                ASCII gfx by :\n\n                                 Spellbinder\n\n\n       If you like this door then please send me (Melody) a postcard to\n                                this address :\n\n                              Melody / The Omen\n                                Egelundsvej 35\n                                  4600 Køge\n                                   Denmark\n\n   The more postcards I get, the faster I''ll finish my @{"future projects!" LINK "PROJECTS"}\n\n=============================================================================\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "REQ" "Requirements"\n@NEXT "INSTALL"\n@PREV "COPY"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\nREQUIREMENTS:\n\n  It was made on an Amiga 2000 with 3meg ram, OS 2.1 and /X V4.7 but there\n    shouldn''t be any problems on other configs.\n\n=============================================================================\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "INSTALL" "Installation"\n@NEXT "USAGE"\n@PREV "REQ"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\nINSTALLATION:\n\n  Copy the "BBS" dir to your BBS: assign\n\n	Edit your ''BBS:NODE<x>/BULL.TXT(.GR)'' files and add the following line :\n\n  [--- CUT ---]\n  ~CC_OFFER|\n  [--- CUT ---]\n\n  All done! Go for it!\n\n=============================================================================\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "USAGE" "Usage"\n@NEXT "BUGS"\n@PREV "INSTALL"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\nUSAGE:\n\n  Type ''OFFER MENU'' at the /X main-prompt\n\n=============================================================================\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "BUGS" "Bugs''n''suggestions"\n@NEXT "GREETS"\n@PREV "USAGE"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\nBUGS & SUGGESTIONS:\n\n  Call the board on the top of the screen and leave mail for MELODY!\n\n=============================================================================\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "GREETS" "Greetings"\n@NEXT "HIST"\n@PREV "BUGS"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\nGREETINGS:\n\n  Thanx must go to ALL my BETA testers, ALL who replies on this door and\n    ofcourse everyone in THE OMEN. Especially :\n\n         Azlan, Eniac, Menace, N-GIN, Spellbinder and The Dancing Duck\n\n=============================================================================\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "HIST" "History"\n@NEXT "PROJECTS"\n@PREV "GREETS"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\nHISTORY:\n\n  04-Dec-94 (V0.1) : This project started...\n  11-Dec-94 (V0.1b): Released as BETA!\n\n=============================================================================\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "PROJECTS" "Future projects"\n@PREV "HIST"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n\nFUTURE PROJECTS:\n\n  Right now I''m working on a MUCH better version of Hacker! Here''s some of\n   the functions that SUPER HACKER has :\n\n   * Each player runs own board.\n   * Players can buy/sell to each other\n   * Buy/Sell :\n      Hardisks\n      Modems\n      Terminal Programs\n      BBS Programs\n      Virus\n      Virus killers\n   * Each playerboard has it''s own BBS Add which can be placed at other boards!\n   * Each playerboard has it''s own mail\n   * Each playerboard has an individual "last ten callers" bulletin\n   * At the "New Hacker HQ" there are :\n      An effective bank with rates on loan/account\n      A gambler with approx. 5 different games\n      Advertising for other boards\n      Sales section\n      External hacker section\n   *  At the external hacker section there will be functions like :\n       Hack some other users bank account, steal his money and change almost\n        everything\n       Hack the users REAL ulcredz and fuck them\n   * There are currently 6 different bulletins like :\n      Last 10 fights\n      Show all players\n      Show last 10 callers\n      Show your status\n      Top 10 current scores\n      Top 10 winners\n   * Hacking a BBS will not only cause damage to the HD. Also to the\n     different programs the user owns.\n   * There will be a lot of default logos for new boards.\n\n=============================================================================\n@ENDNODE\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,10138,2,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048657);
