 - Ezco - Vampire/PDY - The Ones I Forgot! -\n\n\n[EOF]\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',17730,12,0,NULL,NULL,'otl_aa10','scan',1780048664);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('otl_aa12','OTL-AA12.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/OTL-AA12.LHA','AquaAdder','XIM','AquaAdder',NULL,'Aquarius/OTL','OTL','/  \___\___   __/   /  _ \     /  _/  ___/ /    \  |  |   |/  _/\  |  \   /\  |____ \ /  Mb  \ |  |   /   |  \ _   \_     |   /  \',replace('   __    /\________________/\_______________\n  /  \___\___   __/   /  _ \     /  _/  ___/\n /    \  |  |   |/  _/\  |  \   /\  |____ \\n/  Mb  \ |  |   /   |  \ _   \_     |   /  \\n\______/    |___\_______\|____/ /\__|______/\n- ---`------''--------`---''----\/------- -- -\n- -->> AquaAdder v1.0 by Aquarius/OTL <<-- -\n- -- ------- ------------------ ------- -- -\n- -- -(- a fast ''n sexy text adder! -)- -- -\n- -- ------- ------------------ ------- -- -\n','\n',char(10)),'AquaAdder.doc',replace('\n       _ _ ___/\______/\__ ____/\___/\__ _ _/\____ _/\_ __ __/\______\n      __ ________   __   /   _   ___   / ______   \___/__/     _____/\n         bIS/   /   /   /   //   //   /___/ __¬   /  /  /  /\__   \\n           /   /   /   /   //   //   /   /  \    /  /  /  /   /   /\n    __  _ _\____  /\____  //_  //_____  /___/\  /\_____  /\ _/   /___\n     _  ___ _   \/  _  _\/_  \/____ __\/ ___ _\/_______\/____   /_ _/\n                                                            \  /\n                                  present                    \/\n\n                 >>> AquaAdder v1.0 by Aquarius/Outlaws <<<\n\n\n                          Copyright ©1994 Aquarius\n\n                 Permission is granted to freely distribute\n               this product for non-commercial purposes only,\n                  as long as all files remain unmodified.\n\n\n\nArchive (OTL-AA10.LHA) Contents\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nAquaAdder.doc                5085 bytes   This document file.\nAquaAdder.iff                2052 bytes   IFF picture of the output.\nBBS/FCheck/DOC.info           542 bytes   Icon for /X 3.x+.\nBBS/FCheck/DOK.info           542 bytes   Icon for /X 3.x+.\nBBS/FCheck/NFO.info           542 bytes   Icon for /X 3.x+.\nBBS/FCheck/TXT.info           542 bytes   Icon for /X 3.x+.\nC/AquaAdder                  3380 bytes   The executable.\nS/AquaAdder.Head              815 bytes   Sample header text.\nS/AquaAdder.Tail             1371 bytes   Sample tailer text.\n\n\nIntroduction\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\nAquaAdder is a text adder! It takes a text file and adds a header\n(S:AquaAdder.Head) and a tailer (S:AquaAdder.Tail) to it. It can be used both\nfrom shell and in BBS systems like AmiExpress.\n\n\nFeatures\n~~~~~~~~\nIt can insert time and date anywhere you like in the header and the tailer.\nThere are two time formats available (HH:MM and HH:MM:SS), and two date\nformats (DD-MMM-YY and MM-DD-YY).\n\nIt is very FAST - as fast as a text adder can be!! Maybe even faster...\n\nAquaAdder is completely system friendly and safe. No memory losses, Enforcer\nhits or any other crash risks.\n\nIf header + tailer + text file don''t fit in memory, the tool enters\n"low-memory mode"; it tries to load only the tailer, to append it. The header\nwon''t be inserted then.\n\nIt is "pure" and can therefore be made resident.\n\nThe output is extremely cool! :) (Look at the IFF picture..)\n\n\nRequirements\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\nAquaAdder requires an Amiga with OS 2.04 or higher.\n\n\nUsage\n~~~~~\nThe command syntax is:\n\nAquaAdder <TextFile>\n\n\nExample:\n\nAquaAdder dh3:tmp/god-bnbr.doc\n\n\nIf you are going to use this tool with AmiExpress 3.x or higher, copy the\nprovided icon ''TXT.info'' to BBS:FCheck/ and duplicate it for every other text\nfile extension: NFO.info, DOC.info, DOK.info etc.\n\nThere is just ONE error message that AmiExpress should recognize as an error\nthat should move the file to HOLD, and that string is "ERROR: Failed to\nwrite" or just "Failed to write". The other possible error messages, for\nexample "ERROR: Failed to open S:AquaAdder.Head!", should NOT cause the\nuploaded file to be put in HOLD.\n\n\nThe Header and Tailer\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nS:AquaAdder.Head is the file that will be put in front of the text file.\nS:AquaAdder.Tail will be put at the end. The header and the tailer may\ncontain codes that will be replaced by the current time and date\nrespectively. The possible codes are:\n\nCode        Format      Example\n---------   ---------   -------\n$TIME       HH:MM       14:52\n$TIMESEC    HH:MM:SS    14:52:45\n$DATE_DOS   DD-MMM-YY   29-Sep-94\n$DATE_US    MM-DD-YY    09-29-94\n\nFor example, if S:AquaAdder.Tail contains the string ''$DATE_DOS'', then that\nstring will be replaced by the current date formatted as ''DD-MMM-YY'', for\ninstance ''29-Sep-94''.\n\n\nContact Me!\n~~~~~~~~~~~\nIf you have any cool ideas for improvement of this tool, questions, bug\nreports or whatever, leave me a message on one of the following boards:\n\nNIGHTFALL ................ Whoosh ............ +46-90-120369  <---  Safest\nHALL OF FAME ............. Dansken ........... +46-910-26665      place to\nHYSTERIA ................. JAC ............... +46-21-842939     reach me!\nMASTURBATION STATION ..... Black Beard ....... +1-305-552-1192\nZION''S HIDEOUT ........... Zion .............. +1-614-876-0807\nDARK TOWER ............... Shadower .......... +1-801-476-9068\nMORTUARY ................. Bloodwolf ......... +1-312-284-7577\nBOONDOCKS ................ Sal-One! .......... +31-548-040-653\n\n\nHistory\n~~~~~~~\n1.0  (11-19-94) First release version.\n\n\nGreetings\n~~~~~~~~~\n                Greetings must go to (in no special order):\n\n           - Vegas/OTL - Biscrok/OTL - Toxic/OTL - AtomiX!/OTL -\n       - Whoosh/OTT^DVS^OTL^CLS - Snake/OTL - Nashua/OTL - SMS/OTL -\n   - Genghis Khan/OTL - Json/OTL - Jawlog/OTL - The Other OTL Members! -\n  - Dansken - CornFlake - Ace Caze - Firehawk! - fanta/THR - Static/THR -\n- JAz - FAX - Juan - Psychopath - Danzig - Sal-One - Metalbasher - BoneIdle -\n  - Wilsom/Obscene - Rize & Frosty - Norad - Doc Whoo - Zion! - MDR/OTT -\n     - WarDancer - Princip - Ezco - Vampire/PDY - The Ones I Forgot! -\n\n\n[EOF]\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',7242,2,0,NULL,NULL,'otl_aa12','scan',1780048664);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('otl_ab','OTL-AB.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/OTL-AB.LHA','AquaBulls','XIM','AquaBulls','2.0',NULL,'OTL','._________ ___ __ _/\______/  _/_ _/\__ ___. |               //____   __  ___/_/   /___ | | Update of the  /   /   /   /   /   /   / |',replace('[-aQUAbULLS v2.0-]          /\__[-aQUARIUS-]\n._________ ___ __ _/\______/  _/_ _/\__ ___.\n|               //____   __  ___/_/   /___ |\n| Update of the  /   /   /   /   /   /   / |\n| best bulletin _\___   /\___   /____   /__|\n| viewer for     _ ___ /__ ___ /_ ____ /__/|\n| AmiExpress!        \/      \/ -bIS!\/    |\n| More configurable! Can be made resident! |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'AquaBulls.guide',replace('@database AquaBulls\n@author Aquarius/Outlaws\n@$VER: AquaBulls.guide 2.0 (21.1.95)\n\n@node MAIN "AquaBulls v2.0 Documentation"\n\n       _ _ ___/\______/\__ ____/\___/\__ _ _/\____ _/\_ __ __/\______\n      __ ________   __   /   _   ___   / ______   \___/__/     _____/\n         bIS/   /   /   /   //   //   /___/ __¬   /  /  /  /\__   \\n           /   /   /   /   //   //   /   /  \    /  /  /  /   /   /\n    __  _ _\____  /\____  //_  //_____  /___/\  /\_____  /\ _/   /___\n     _  ___ _   \/  _  _\/_  \/____ __\/ ___ _\/_______\/____   /_ _/\n                                                            \  /\n                                  present:                   \/\n\n                 >>> AquaBulls v2.0 by Aquarius/Outlaws <<<\n\n                      [- Contents of Documentation -]\n\n                @{"   Copyright Note   " Link Copyright   }   @{"   Configuration    " Link Configuration}\n                @{"  Archive Contents  " Link Archive     }   @{"     Algorithms     " Link Algorithms}\n                @{"    Introduction    " Link Introduction}   @{"      History       " Link History}\n                @{"      Features      " Link Features    }   @{"  How to Reach Me   " Link ContactMe}\n                @{"    Requirements    " Link Requirements}   @{"    Other Tools     " Link AquaTools}\n                @{"    Installation    " Link Installation}   @{"     Greetings      " Link Greetings}\n@endnode\n\n@node Copyright "AquaBulls v2.0 Documentation"\n\n                          Copyright ©1995 Aquarius\n\n                 Permission is granted to freely distribute\n               this product for non-commercial purposes only,\n                  as long as all files remain unmodified.\n@endnode\n\n@node Archive "AquaBulls v2.0 Documentation"\n\nArchive (OTL-AB20.LHA) Contents\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nDoors/AquaBulls/\n   AquaBulls                 6020 bytes  The door itself!\n   AquaBulls.doc            19456 bytes  Ascii version of the doc.\n   AquaBulls.guide          24321 bytes  This AmigaGuide doc!\n   AquaBulls.config           655 bytes  Sample configuration text.\n   AquaBulls.info            1181 bytes  Sample configuration icon.\n\nCommands/BBSCmd/\n   B.info                    1275 bytes  Command icon for /X 3.0+.\n@endnode\n\n@node Introduction "AquaBulls v2.0 Documentation"\n\nIntroduction\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\nAquaBulls is a replacement for the AmiExpress ''B'' command (for viewing the\nnormal bulletins). It is written in highly optimized C code for great\nperformance, and it can be made resident which gives faster startups. Now,\ntake a look at all the @{"features" Link Features}...\n@endnode\n\n@node Features "AquaBulls v2.0 Documentation"\n\nFeatures\n~~~~~~~~\n- You can have both global bulletins (for all conferences) and conference\n  specific ones! If AquaBulls can''t find a bulletin in the current\n  conference, then it looks for it in the global directory ''Bulletins:''\n  (or whatever path you configure). But you can also have conferences\n  where the global bulletins can''t be accessed at all.\n\n- Just like the built-in ''B'' command, a bulletin can be specified on the\n  command line. Then only that bulletin will be shown, after which\n  AquaBulls exits. If the user writes NS after the bulletin number (even\n  on the bulletin prompt inside the door), and you''re running AmiExpress\n  3.19 or higher, the bulletin is shown non-stop.\n\n- It is flexible: @{"Configuration" Link Configuration} can be made in an icon or in a text file,\n  whatever you like best.\n\n- Two kinds of online updating are supported!\n\n   1. Updating of all/several bulletins: When the door is started, it\n      checks for a particular script file ''BullBatch.Script'' (both in the\n      conference and globally), and if it exists, the user gets the\n      question (if he has enough access) whether he wants the bulletins to\n      be updated or not, i.e. if the script should be executed.\n\n   2. Updating of specific bulletins: When a bulletin has been selected,\n      the door checks if the update script for that bulletin exists and if\n      it does, it is automatically executed. But the door can also be made\n      to ask the user if he wants the script to be executed or not.\n\n  Note that if you don''t want to use online updating, you don''t have to!!\n  Just don''t create any script files. But online updating can shorten your\n  logoff script drastically because you can remove much of the bulletin\n  updating stuff from it.\n\n- The screen types (different text formats or languages) in AmiExpress\n  3.0+ (configurable in BBS:ScreenTypes.info) are supported. The door\n  first looks for the bulletin of the screen type selected by the user and\n  if it doesn''t  exist it then tries the bulletin ending with ".TXT".\n\n- With AmiExpress 2.xx, bulletins ending with ".TXT.GR" are first looked\n  for (but only if ANSI is on), and if it can''t be found, the ".TXT"\n  bulletin is shown.\n\n- The screen is automatically cleared before each bulletin is shown.\n\n- ''Who'' doors show that the user is viewing bulletins when he''s using\n  AquaBulls. In fact, this was the thing that made me write this door. I\n  was going to install a bulletin viewer on Nightfall and I tested several\n  doors but all of them showed up in the who door as MODULE, not\n  VIEWING BULLETINS! Very annoying... :)\n\n- Whether a user has access to read bulletins or not is determined from\n  the access icons (/X 3.0+, tooltype ACS.READ_BULLETINS) or the CONFIG(x)\n  file (/X 2.xx). But the door doesn''t read those files. It still knows.\n  So it doesn''t matter if you set the door access "too low".\n\n- It allows you to write your own output (the BullHelp.txt)... Also, most\n  strings in the door are totally configurable, for example the bulletin\n  prompt. So you can choose colours yourself so that they match your\n  BullHelp.txt and bulletins.\n@endnode\n\n@node Requirements "AquaBulls v2.0 Documentation"\n\nRequirements\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\n- An Amiga with OS 2.0 or higher.\n\n- AmiExpress, SigmaExpress or any compatible program.\n@endnode\n\n@node Installation "AquaBulls v2.0 Documentation"\n\nInstallation\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\nFirst, copy the ''AquaBulls'' directory (the inner one) to ''Doors:''.\n\n\nFor AmiExpress 2.xx (and SigmaExpress?), add this to your ''BBS.CMD'' file:\n\n----Cut here------------------------------------\n*B        XM001Doors:AquaBulls/AquaBulls\n----Cut here------------------------------------\n\n\nFor AmiExpress 3.xx/4.xx, just copy ''B.info'' to your ''BBSCmd'' drawer.\n\nThe door is "pure" and is therefore perfectly safe to make resident. The\nchanges you have to make to ''B.info'' in that case are: Change the value of\nthe "LOCATION" tooltype to "AquaBulls", and add the tooltype "RESIDENT".\n\n\nThe conference specific bulletins are stored in the directory\n''<conf path>Bulletins/''. The global bulletins are stored in the path you\nconfigure with the @{"GLOBAL_DIR" Link GLOBAL_DIR} tooltype.\n\nIf you don''t want it to be possible to access the global bulletins from a\ncertain conference, then create ''<conf path>Bulletins/NoGlobalBulls''. The\ncontents don''t matter. An empty file will do fine.\n\n\nA script for online updating of all/several bulletins (the first kind\ndescribed in the @{"Features" Link Features} section) is called ''BullBatch.Script'' and is\nlocated in ''<conf path>Bulletins/'' or in ''<global path>''. If the\n''NoGlobalBulls'' file exists, then the script in ''<global path>'' won''t be\nexecuted, but otherwise BOTH scripts will be executed (if they both\nexist).\n\n\nA script that updates a _specific_ bulletin every time it is selected is\ncalled ''BULL<no>.script'' and is located in the same directory as the\nbulletin which it is supposed to create.\n\n\nNow it''s time to @{"configure" Link Configuration} the door...\n@endnode\n\n@node Configuration "AquaBulls v2.0 Documentation"\n\nConfiguration\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nSome people like icons, some don''t. The sysop configuration can be done\neither in an icon (''Doors:AquaBulls/AquaBulls.info''), or in a textfile if\nyou prefer that (''Doors:AquaBulls/AquaBulls.config''). AquaBulls first\nlooks for the icon so if you want to use the textfile you have to delete\nthe icon! The textfile should simply contain the tooltypes that would be\nin the icon otherwise.\n\nYou may well use ANSI codes in the string tooltypes. Note that the escape\ncharacter can be entered in a string gadget (in your tooltype editor if\nyou''re editing AquaBulls.info) using <LeftAmiga-Esc>,\n<LeftAmiga-Shift-Esc> or <LeftAmiga-Ctrl-Esc> etc.\n\nThese are the various tooltypes in AquaBulls.info/AquaBulls.config:\n\n@{" ALLQUE_ACS " Link ALLQUE_ACS}     @{" ONEQUE_ACS " Link ONEQUE_ACS}     @{" PROMPT_STR " Link PROMPT_STR}     @{" GLOBAL_DIR " Link GLOBAL_DIR}\n@{" ALLUPD_DEF " Link ALLUPD_DEF}     @{" ONEUPD_DEF " Link ONEUPD_DEF}     @{" NOBULL_STR " Link NOBULL_STR}\n@{" ALLANS_DEF " Link ALLANS_DEF}     @{" ONEANS_DEF " Link ONEANS_DEF}     @{" ERRINP_STR " Link ERRINP_STR}\n@{" ALLQUE_STR " Link ALLQUE_STR}     @{" ONEQUE_STR " Link ONEQUE_STR}     @{" NAVAIL_STR " Link NAVAIL_STR}\n@{" ALLUPD_STR " Link ALLUPD_STR}     @{" ONEUPD_STR " Link ONEUPD_STR}\n@endnode\n\n@node GLOBAL_DIR "AquaBulls v2.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: GLOBAL_DIR=<path>                                     Required.\nExample : GLOBAL_DIR=Bulletins:\n\nThis tooltype specifies <global path> - the directory for the global\nbulletins. It MUST end with ''/'' or '':''. Suitable location is for example\n''Bulletins:'' or ''BBS:Bulletins/''.\n@endnode\n\n@node ALLQUE_ACS "AquaBulls v2.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: ALLQUE_ACS=<access level>                             Required.\nExample : ALLQUE_ACS=1\n\nThis tooltype specifies the access level required to get the question "Do\nyou want to update the bulletins first?" at startup, or whatever string\nyou configure with @{"ALLQUE_STR" Link ALLQUE_STR}. (I will call it the "update-all" question\nfrom now on.) If the user answers Yes on that question, ''BullBatch.Script''\nwill be executed.\n@endnode\n\n@node ALLUPD_DEF "AquaBulls v2.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: ALLUPD_DEF=(YES|NO)                                   Required.\nExample : ALLUPD_DEF=YES\n\nThis tooltype determines what happens when the user hasn''t got enough\naccess to get the "update-all" question (see @{"ALLQUE_ACS" Link ALLQUE_ACS}). If the\n''BullBatch.Script'' SHOULD be executed then, set it to YES, else to NO.\n@endnode\n\n@node ALLANS_DEF "AquaBulls v2.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: ALLANS_DEF=(YES|NO)                                   Required.\nExample : ALLANS_DEF=YES\n\nThis tooltype determines what the default answer is to the "update-all"\nquestion, i.e. what the answer is if the user presses <Enter>. You have to\nmake sure that the question string (@{"ALLQUE_STR" Link ALLQUE_STR}) shows the correct default\n(''Y/n'' or ''y/N'' for example).\n@endnode\n\n@node ALLQUE_STR "AquaBulls v2.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: ALLQUE_STR=<string>                                   Required.\nExample : ALLQUE_STR=Do you want to update the bulletins first (y/N)?\n\nThis tooltype specifies the question if the user wants the bulletins to be\nupdated before any bulletins are shown (by executing ''BullBatch.Script'').\nThe default answer is determined by the tooltype @{"ALLANS_DEF" Link ALLANS_DEF}.\n@endnode\n\n@node ALLUPD_STR "AquaBulls v2.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: ALLUPD_STR=<string>                                   Required.\nExample : ALLUPD_STR=Updating bulletins...\n\nThis string will be shown when the ''BullBatch.Script'' is executed.\n@endnode\n\n@node ONEQUE_ACS "AquaBulls v2.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: ONEQUE_ACS=<access level>                             Required.\nExample : ONEQUE_ACS=300\n\nThis tooltype specifies the access level required to get the question "Do\nyou want to update this bulletin?" when a bulletin is selected, or\nwhatever string you configure with @{"ONEQUE_STR" Link ONEQUE_STR}. (I will call it the\n"update-one" question from now on.) If the user answers Yes on that\nquestion, ''Bull<no>.Script'' will be executed.\n@endnode\n\n@node ONEUPD_DEF "AquaBulls v2.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: ONEUPD_DEF=(YES|NO)                                   Required.\nExample : ONEUPD_DEF=YES\n\nThis tooltype determines what happens when the user hasn''t got enough\naccess to get the "update-one" question (see @{"ONEQUE_ACS" Link ONEQUE_ACS}). If the\n''BULL<no>.Script'' SHOULD be executed then, set it to YES, otherwise to NO.\n@endnode\n\n@node ONEANS_DEF "AquaBulls v2.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: ONEANS_DEF=(YES|NO)                                   Required.\nExample : ONEANS_DEF=YES\n\nThis tooltype determines what the default answer is to the "update-one"\nquestion, i.e. what the answer is if the user presses <Enter>. You have to\nmake sure that the question string (@{"ONEQUE_STR" Link ONEQUE_STR}) shows the correct default\n(''Y/n'' or ''y/N'' for example).\n@endnode\n\n@node ONEQUE_STR "AquaBulls v2.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: ONEQUE_STR=<string possibly containing ''%ld''>         Required.\nExample : ONEQUE_STR=Do you want to update this bulletin first (Y/n)?\n\nThis tooltype specifies the question if the user wants the bulletin to be\nupdated before it is shown (by executing ''BULL<no>.Script''). The default\nanswer is determined by the tooltype @{"ONEANS_DEF" Link ONEANS_DEF}. The tooltype can contain\nthe sequence ''%ld'' somewhere (but not more than one). The bulletin number\nwill be inserted there. No other ''%'' codes are allowed. But if you want a\n''%'' to be shown, enter ''%%'' in the tooltype.\n@endnode\n\n@node ONEUPD_STR "AquaBulls v2.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: ONEUPD_STR=<string possibly containing ''%ld''>         Required.\nExample : ONEUPD_STR=Updating bulletin %ld...\n\nThis tooltype specifies the string that will be shown when a single\nbulletin is updated (when BULL<no>.Script is executed). It can contain the\nsequence ''%ld'' somewhere (but not more than one). The bulletin number will\nbe inserted there. No other ''%'' codes are allowed. But if you want a ''%''\nto be shown, enter ''%%'' in the tooltype.\n@endnode\n\n@node PROMPT_STR "AquaBulls v2.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: PROMPT_STR=<string>                                   Required.\nExample : PROMPT_STR=Which bulletin (?)=List, (Enter)=None?\n\nThis string will be shown as the bulletin prompt inside the door.\n@endnode\n\n@node NOBULL_STR "AquaBulls v2.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: NOBULL_STR=<string possibly containing ''%ld''>         Required.\nExample : NOBULL_STR=Sorry, there is no bulletin %ld!\n\nThis tooltype specifies the string that will be shown when the user types\na valid number >= 0 and no bulletin ''BULL<no>.<suffix>'' with that number\nexists. The tooltype can contain the sequence ''%ld'' somewhere (but not\nmore than one). The bulletin number will be inserted there. No other ''%''\ncodes are allowed. But if you want a ''%'' to be shown, enter ''%%'' in the\ntooltype.\n@endnode\n\n@node ERRINP_STR "AquaBulls v2.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: ERRINP_STR=<string>                                   Required.\nExample : ERRINP_STR=Invalid input! No such bulletin!\n\nThis string will be shown when the user gives invalid input on the\nbulletin prompt.\n@endnode\n\n@node NAVAIL_STR "AquaBulls v2.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: NAVAIL_STR=<string>                                   Required.\nExample : NAVAIL_STR=No bulletins are available in this conference!\n\nThis string will be shown if no bulletins can be found. (Actually, if no\n''BullHelp.<suffix>'' can be found.)\n@endnode\n\n\n@node Algorithms "AquaBulls v2.0 Documentation"\n\nAlgorithms\n~~~~~~~~~~\nHere is an attempt to describe the way AquaBulls works. If you don''t\nunderstand a jot, use SnoopDos or some similar program to figure it out..\n\nWhen the door is started, it works like this (presuming that a BullHelp\nfile could be found):\n\n  If ''<conf path>Bulletins/BullBatch.Script'' exists,\n     or\n       ''<conf path>Bulletins/NoGlobalBulls'' doesn''t exist and\n       ''<global path>BullBatch.Script'' exists, then\n\n    Ask the user if the bulletins should be updated (provided he has the\n    access defined by @{"ALLQUE_ACS" Link ALLQUE_ACS}).\n    If YES then\n       If ''<conf path>Bulletins/BullBatch.Script'' exists then execute it.\n       If ''<conf path>Bulletins/NoGlobalBulls'' doesn''t exist, then\n          Try to execute ''<global path>BullBatch.Script''.\n\n  Show the BullHelp (plus screen type suffix or ''.TXT'').\n  Wait for the user to select a bulletin number.\n\n\nThe door works like this when the user has selected a bulletin to view:\n\n  If ''<conf path>Bulletins/BULL<no>.Script'' exists, ask if the user wants\n  it to be executed (provided he has the access defined by @{"ONEQUE_ACS" Link ONEQUE_ACS}).\n  If YES then execute it.\n\n  Try to show ''<conf path>Bulletins/BULL<no>.<screen type suffix>'' (/X 3).\n  If it failed, try to show ''<conf path>Bulletins/BULL<no>.TXT''.\n\n  If that failed too, and if ''<conf path>Bulletins/NoGlobalBulls'' doesn''t\n  exist then continue with:\n\n     If ''<global path>BULL<no>.Script'' exists, ask if the user wants it\n     to be executed (provided he has the access defined by @{"ONEQUE_ACS" Link ONEQUE_ACS}).\n     If YES then execute it.\n\n     Try to show ''<global path>BULL<no>.<screen type suffix>''.\n     If it failed, try to show ''<global path>BULL<no>.TXT''.\n\n\nThe BullHelp is searched for in a corresponding way (no script files for\nthat).\n@endnode\n\n@node History "AquaBulls v2.0 Documentation"\n\nHistory\n~~~~~~~\n1.0 (04-24-94) First release version.\n\n\n1.1 (01-11-95) For beta testers only.\n\n               Made it residentable and halved the size of the door!\n\n               It now shows the door version ([-AquaBulls vX.X-] instead\n               of just [-AquaBulls-]).\n\n               Made most strings configurable, using a bunch of tooltypes.\n\n               If the user starts the door with ''B <bull> NS'' (for example\n               ''B 18 NS''), the bulletin is displayed non-stop. You can\n               also write ''<bull> NS'' on the prompt inside the door...\n               /X 3.19 is required for this. In other versions the\n               bulletin will be displayed normally, with pauses.\n\n               Added tooltype GLOBAL_DIR=<dir for global bulletins>.\n\n               If the user gave a bulletin number as argument to the door,\n               it didn''t ask if he wanted to update the bulletins first.\n               Fixed that.\n\n\n2.0 (01-21-95) Second release version.\n\n               The S flag is no longer required on the script files.\n               Instead, the command EXECUTE must be in your C: directory\n               or be resident.\n\n               Revised the tooltypes. Changed a lot. ''ACS.UPDATE'' is no\n               longer in use.\n\n               Added support for a text file as configuration.\n               (''Doors:AquaBulls/AquaBulls.config''.) ''AquaBulls.info'' is\n               searched for first.\n@endnode\n\n@node ContactMe "AquaBulls v2.0 Documentation"\n\nContact Me!\n~~~~~~~~~~~\nIf you have any cool ideas for improvement of this tool, questions, bug\nreports or whatever, contact me on one of the following boards:\n\n@{"NIGHTFALL" Link NIGHTFALL} ................ Whoosh ............ +46-90-120369  <---  Safest\nHALL OF FAME ............. Dansken ........... +46-910-26665      place to\nACES HIGH ................ Norad ............. +46-410-44886     reach me!\nINTERCHANGE .............. Princip ........... +46-8-6082339\nZION''S HIDEOUT ........... Zion .............. +1-PRIVATE!!\nDEATH ROW ................ Shadower .......... +1-PRIVATE!!\nMORTUARY ................. Bloodwolf ......... +1-PRIVATE!!\nBOONDOCKS ................ Sal-One ........... +31-PRIVATE!!\n@endnode\n\n@node AquaTools "AquaBulls v2.0 Documentation"\n\nThe AquaTools Collection\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nHere is the complete list of my released tools (the latest versions):\n\nTool Name              File Name     Short Description\n---------------------- ------------- ------------------------------------------\nDisable v1.1           AQDSBL11.LHA  Payuser handling system.\nDisplayer v1.0         AQDSPL10.LHA  Text displayer. Perfect for door menu e.g.\nNetEdit v1.0           AQNETE10.LHA  Editor for certain netmail systems.\nConfReplace v1.0       OTL-CR10.LHA  Find and replace" area names in User.Data.\nListSpeeder v2.1       OTL-LS21.LHA  Filelist downloader.\nAnnounce v2.0          OTL-AN20.LHA  Notifies online users of logons/logoffs.\nAquaWho v2.0           OTL-AW20.LHA  Totally configurable WHO door!\nSpeedCheck v2.1        OTL-SC21.LHA  Disables download at too low connect rates.\nStripper v1.2          OTL-ST12.LHA  Strips log files to desired file sizes.\nAquaQuiet v1.0         OTL-AQ10.LHA  ''Q'' replacement. Toggles quiet node.\nAquaScan v1.0          OTL-AS10.LHA  File scanner! (F, N, CS, FR.)\nAquaCreateAcc v1.0     OTL-CA10.LHA  Door to create new accounts with.\nAquaMoveFiles v1.0     OTL-MF10.LHA  File and description mover, by date.\nAquaSafety v1.0        OTL-SA10.LHA  Anti-BBS-downtime utility.\nAquaAdder v1.0         OTL-AA10.LHA  Text adder.\nAquaBulls v2.0         OTL-AB20.LHA  Bulletin viewer.\nAquaQuick v1.0         OTL-QK10.LHA  Quick-logon door.\nRestoreQuietness v1.0  OTL-RQ10.LHA  Restores the nodes'' "quietness" at logoff.\nAquaSettings v1.0      OTL-SE10.LHA  ''W'' replacement. Menu of config commands.\n\n(...and more are coming!)\n\nYou can find them all on @{"Nightfall" Link NIGHTFALL} +46-90-120369 (free download)!\n@endnode\n\n@node Greetings "AquaBulls v2.0 Documentation"\n\nGreetings\n~~~~~~~~~\n                Greetings must go to (in no special order):\n\n           - Vegas/OTL - Biscrok/OTL - Toxic/OTL - Nashua/OTL -\n     - Snake/OTL - Whoosh/OTT^DVS^CLS^OTL^R2 - AtomiX!/OTL - SMS/OTL -\n   - Genghis Khan/OTL - The Other OTL Members - Ace Caze - Dansken/ACS -\n  - Princip! - Sandman - Rize & Frosty - Static & fanta - Marky & Power -\n  - Psychopath - Norad - Firehawk - Marwin - Danzig! - Lockjammer - MDR -\n   - HardHack! - Chig! - Wild Thing - Ezco - Enzo - FAX! - AXL - HiFly -\n    - Kid Curry - Juan - Wilsom - Gi Joe - Sal-One - Zion! - Shadower -\n     - Doc Whoo - JAz - Bowen/OTT - Json - WarDancer - MFM - Vileius -\n        - Bilbo Baggins - Biztro - Metalbasher - Kain - CornFlake -\n              - Karma - Dalamar - Wize - CountZero - Psyche -\n                         - The Friends I Forgot! -\n\n\n                         A few personal messages:\n\nWhoosh         - Whooopssss... Nice chatting with you every day. :)\n\nToxic/OTL      - Hard getting cards isn''t it? If you can, call Nightfall\n                 (new pwfail door hehe)!\n\nVegas/OTL      - Yeah let''s get the Swedish section rocking! I mean, MORE!\n                 Btw, Norrland is such a nice place, don''t you think? :)\n\nBiscrok/OTL    - The master of strange (tüffa) modules. ;)\n\nDansken        - Great friend and beta tester! Learn C soon!! hehe\n\nMarky & Power  - Hope you can find a new way to call...\n\nEzco           - Great Who designs!!\n\nAce Caze       - Funny dude and great beta tester! Hmmm why not\n                 topaz 8 on your WB?? ;)\n\nSnowman/Ex.OTL - Where did you disappear??? Get in touch, mate..\n@endnode\n\n@node NIGHTFALL "AquaBulls v2.0 Documentation"\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|         iNTO tOTAL dARKNESS, tHE uNKNOWN; cOME wALK wiTH mE...          |\n| a3ooo    ___/\       ___/\ ____/\__________/\ ___/   __/\ _________9ooMB|\n+----------\__  \______\__  \____  __________  \  /   \__  \   _____/-----+\n|         tS/    __    \/      /  /_____   /     /     /        /         |\n· /X 4.xx  /      /    /      /     /     /           /        /    r2 sHQ·\n          /      /    /      /     /     /     /     /        /    dVS sHQ\n   eNJOY /______/    /______/___________/_____/     /________/    oTT  sHQ\n   tHE         /____/                        /     /         oTL diST siTE\n sPEED!             ·3 uSR nODES riNGDOWN!· /     /\n    ___/\ _________/\ _________/\ ___   ___/     / sTAFF: wHOOSH, aQUARiUS,\n    \__  \ ________  \_________  \  /   \__     / riZE, mASTERmAN, nEMESiS\n·    /    _____/ /     __    /     /_____/     /_____                     ·\n:   /      /    /      /    /     /     /     /     /    mORE tHAN 1200   :\n|  /      /    /      /    /     /     /     /     / aMiX tOOLS oNLiNE!!  |\n+-/______/----/______/    /___________/___________/-----------------------+\n|                   /____/                                                |\n| nODE#1: +46-90-120369   nODE#2: +46-riNGDOWN!!  nODE#3: +46-riNGDOWN!!  |\n|      (14.4k DS)              (16.8k DS)              (28.8k DS)         |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n@endnode\n\n[EOF]\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',21665,1,0,NULL,NULL,'otl_ab10','scan',1780048664);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('otl_ab10','OTL-AB10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/OTL-AB10.LHA','AquaBulls','XIM','AquaBulls','1.0',NULL,'OTL','__ _/\______/\___/\_ _\  /_________________. __ ___  ___  ____  /_ \\//                 | /  /  / /  / /  /__  \/ A very powerful  |',replace('[-aQUAbULLS v1.0-]    ____  [-aQUARIUS/oTL-]\n__ _/\______/\___/\_ _\  /_________________.\n__ ___  ___  ____  /_ \\//                 |\n  /  /  / /  / /  /__  \/ A very powerful  |\n /  /  / /  / /  /  /    bulletin viewer   |\n_\__  /_/  /_/___  /  for /X! Supports two |\n____ /___ /__ ___ /     kinds of online    |\nbIS\/   \/      \/    updating. Global     |\n  bulls but also conference specific ones! |\n-- -  -    - -- -   ---- - ---- -----------''\n[THE]=--=] cS!-^-sAD-^-hJB-^-KLF! [=--=[PUB]\n','\n',char(10)),'AquaBulls.guide',replace('@database AquaBulls\n\nCopyright © 1994 Aquarius/Outlaws\n\n@Remark $VER: AquaBulls v1.0 AmigaGuide doc\n\n@node MAIN "AquaBulls v1.0 Documentation"\n\n       _ _ ___/\______/\__ ____/\___/\__ _ _/\____ _/\_ __ __/\______\n      __ ________   __   /   _   ___   / ______   \___/__/     _____/\n         bIS/   /   /   /   //   //   /___/ __¬   /  /  /  /\__   \\n           /   /   /   /   //   //   /   /  \    /  /  /  /   /   /\n    __  _ _\____  /\____  //_  //_____  /___/\  /\_____  /\ _/   /___\n     _  ___ _   \/  _  _\/_  \/____ __\/ ___ _\/_______\/____   /_ _/\n                                                            \  /\n                                  present                    \/\n                      a door for AmiExpress 2.xx/3.xx:\n\n                 >>> AquaBulls v1.0 by Aquarius/Outlaws <<<\n\n                      [- Contents of documentation -]\n\n                 @{"  Copyright Note  " Link Copyright   }    @{"   Installation   " Link Installation}\n                 @{" Archive Contents " Link Archive     }    @{"    Algorithms    " Link Algorithms}\n                 @{"   Introduction   " Link Introduction}    @{" How to Reach Me  " Link ContactMe}\n                 @{"     Features     " Link Features    }    @{"     History      " Link History}\n                 @{"   Requirements   " Link Requirements}    @{"    Greetings     " Link Greetings}\n@endnode\n\n@node Copyright "AquaBulls v1.0 Documentation"\n\n                          Copyright ©1994 Aquarius\n\n                 Permission is granted to freely distribute\n               this product for non-commercial purposes only,\n                  as long as all files remain unmodified.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Archive "AquaBulls v1.0 Documentation"\n\nArchive (OTL-AB10.LHA) Contents\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nDoors/AquaBulls/\n   AquaBulls                  11064 bytes  The door!\n   AquaBulls.info               473 bytes  Config icon.\n   AquaBulls.doc               8807 bytes  Ascii version of the doc.\n   AquaBulls.guide            14710 bytes  This document file!\n\nCommands/BBSCmd/\n   b.info                      1263 bytes  Command icon for /X 3.xx.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Introduction "AquaBulls v1.0 Documentation"\n\nIntroduction\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\nAquaBulls is a replacement for the AmiExpress ''b'' command (for viewing the\nnormal bulletins). It is written in highly optimized C code for great\nperformance.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Features "AquaBulls v1.0 Documentation"\n\nFeatures\n~~~~~~~~\n- You can have both global bulletins (for all conferences) and conference\n  specific ones! If AquaBulls can''t find a bulletin in the current\n  conference, then it looks for it in the global directory ''Bulletins:''.\n  But you can also have conferences where the global bulletins can''t be\n  accessed.\n\n- Just like the built-in command, a bulletin can be specified on the\n  command line. Then only that bulletin will be shown, after which\n  AquaBulls exits.\n\n- Two kinds of online updating are supported!\n\n   1. Updating of all/many bulletins: When the user starts the door\n      without giving a bulletin number on the command line, it checks for\n      a particular script file (both in the conference and globally) and\n      if that exists, the user gets the question whether he wants the\n      bulletins to be updated or not, that is if the script(s) should be\n      executed. But this can be access protected. In the config icon you\n      specify the access level that is required for starting this script.\n\n   2. Updating of specific bulletins: When a bulletin has been selected,\n      the door checks if the update script for that bulletin exists and if\n      it does, it is automatically executed.\n\n  Note that if you don''t want to use online updating you don''t have to!\n\n- The screen types (different text formats or languages) in AmiExpress\n  3.xx (configurable in BBS:ScreenTypes.info) are supported. The door\n  first looks for the bulletin of the screen type selected by the user and\n  if it doesn''t  exist it then tries the bulletin ending with ".TXT".\n\n- With AmiExpress 2.xx, bulletins ending with ".TXT.GR" are first looked\n  for (but only if ANSI is on), and if it can''t be found the ".TXT"\n  bulletin is shown.\n\n- The screen is automatically cleared before each bulletin is shown.\n\n- ''Who'' doors show that the user is viewing bulletins when he''s using\n  AquaBulls. In fact, this was the thing that made me write this door. I\n  was going to install a bulletin viewer on Nightfall and I tested several\n  doors but all of them showed up in the who door as MODULE and not\n  VIEWING BULLETINS! Very annoying... :-)\n\n- Whether a user has access to read bulletins or not is determined from\n  the access icons (/X 3.xx) or the CONFIG(x) file (/X 2.xx). But the door\n  doesn''t read those files. It still knows... So it doesn''t matter if you\n  set the door access too low. 10 is reasonable I guess...\n\n- It allows you to write your own output (the BullHelp.txt)...\n@endnode\n\n@node Requirements "AquaBulls v1.0 Documentation"\n\nRequirements\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\n- Any Amiga model with AmiExpress installed (v2.20-v3.38, possibly other\n  versions too).\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Installation "AquaBulls v1.0 Documentation"\n\nInstallation\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\nMake a directory in ''Doors:'' called ''AquaBulls'' and copy the door there,\nand perhaps this document as well.\n\n\nFor AmiExpress 2.xx, add this to your BBS.CMD:\n\n----Cut here------------------------------------\n*B        XM010Doors:AquaBulls/AquaBulls\n----Cut here------------------------------------\n               ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^- File name of the door with full path.\n            ^^^\n            Access required to use the door.\n\nFor AmiExpress 3.x, just copy ''b.info'' to your ''Commands/BBSCmd'' drawer\nand edit its tooltypes if they don''t suit you.\n\n\nAquaBulls requires ''Bulletins:'' to be assigned to the directory where you\nwill keep your global bulletins. So add this to ''S:User-Startup'' or\nwherever you want to keep your assigns:\n\n  assign Bulletins: <path to global bulletins>\n\n\nThe conference specific bulletins are stored in\n''<path to conf>Bulletins/''.\n\nIf you don''t want it to be possible to access the global bulletins from a\nconference, then create the file ''<conf path>Bulletins/NoGlobalBulls''. The\ncontents don''t matter. An empty file will do fine.\n\n\nA script for online updating of all/many bulletins (the first kind in the\n@{"Features" Link Features} section) is called ''BullBatch.script'' and is located in\n''<conf path>Bulletins/'' or in ''Bulletins:''. If the NoGlobalBulls file\nexists, then the script in ''Bulletins:'' won''t be executed, but otherwise,\nBOTH scripts will be executed (if they both exist). The scripts must have\nthe (s)cript flag to work. To set it, type in shell: ''protect <script\nfile> +s''.\n\nIf you want to use this kind of updating then you must specify an access\nlevel with the ACS.UPDATE tooltype in the configuration icon,\n''Doors:AquaBulls/AquaBulls.info''. If that icon contains ACS.UPDATE=200\nthen only users with access 200 or higher will be able to run the update\nscript.\n\n\nA script that updates a _specific_ bulletin every time it is shown is\ncalled ''BULL<nr>.script'' and is located in the same directory as the\nbulletin which it is supposed to create. The script file must have the\n(s)cript flag to work.\n@endnode\n\n@node Algorithms "AquaBulls v1.0 Documentation"\n\nAlgorithms\n~~~~~~~~~~\nWhen the door is started without any bulletin number as argument, it works\nlike this (presuming that a BullHelp file could be found):\n\n  If ''<conf path>Bulletins/BullBatch.script'' exists,\n     or\n     ''<conf path>Bulletins/NoGlobalBulls'' doesn''t exist and\n      ''Bulletins:BullBatch.script'' exists, THEN\n\n    Ask the user if the bulletins should be updated.\n    If YES then\n       Execute ''<conf path>Bulletins/BullBatch.script'' if it exists.\n       If ''<conf path>Bulletins/NoGlobalBulls'' doesn''t exist then\n          Try to execute ''Bulletins:BullBatch.script''.\n\n  Show the BullHelp (plus screen type suffix or ''.TXT'').\n  Wait for the user to select a bulletin number.\n\n\nThe door works like this when the user has selected a bulletin to view:\n\n  If ''<conf path>Bulletins/BULL<nr>.script'' exists then execute it.\n\n  Try to show ''<conf path>Bulletins/BULL<nr>.<screen type suffix>'' (/X 3).\n  If it failed, try to show ''<conf path>Bulletins/BULL<nr>.TXT''.\n\n  If that failed too, and if ''<conf path>Bulletins/NoGlobalBulls'' doesn''t\n  exist then continue with:\n\n     If ''Bulletins:BULL<nr>.script'' exists then execute it.\n\n     Try to show ''Bulletins:BULL<nr>.<screen type suffix>''.\n     If it failed, try to show ''Bulletins:BULL<nr>.TXT''.\n\n\nThe BullHelp is searched for in a corresponding way (no script files for\nthat).\n@endnode\n\n@node ContactMe "AquaBulls v1.0 Documentation"\n\nContact Me!\n~~~~~~~~~~~\nIf you have any cool ideas for improvement of this door, bug reports,\nquestions, or whatever, leave me a message on one of the following boards:\n\n@{"NIGHTFALL" Link Nightfall} ................ Prof Do Right ..... +46-90-120369\n@{"OVERLOAD" Link OverLoad} (OTL SHQ) ....... Vegas ............. +46-8-54063666\nHYSTERIA ................. JAC ............... +46-21-842939\nRAISING HELL ............. Psychopath ........ +46-23-26893\nINSIDE OUT ............... C/\TE¥E ........... +46-346-58697\n@{"SNAKE''S DEN" Link SnakesDen} (OTL WHQ) .... Snake ............. +1-513-683-2330\nTHE HOLE ................. Oldman ............ +1-419-899-2754\n\n@endnode\n\n@node History "AquaBulls v1.0 Documentation"\n\nHistory\n~~~~~~~\n1.0  (1994-04-24) First release version.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Greetings "AquaBulls v1.0 Documentation"\n\nGreetings\n~~~~~~~~~\n               Greetings must go to (in no special order):\n\n      - All Members of Outlaws!! - Prof Do Right/Classic - JAC/TDS -\n    - C/\TE¥E/Insane - Ace Caze/Obscene - Wilsom/Obscene - Kid Curry -\n   - Psychopath - Vinzi - Karma - Zin - Shapechanger - Rize - Seagull -\n    - Remix/Classic - RaJ-Ban - fanta/Therion - Static/Therion - CaT -\n     - Dansken - AXL/Attention - Rad!/LSD - Vileius! - Marwin/Duplo -\n      - Freddy Kreuger/GOD - Chig/TDS - The Silencer - Vampire/PDY -\n       - Crocodile/Obscene - Sal-One - Nojje - Zune/HCD - MadCap -\n           - Metalbasher - WarDancer/H&V - The Ones I Forgot! -\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Nightfall "AquaBulls v1.0 Documentation"\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|         iNTO tOTAL dARKNESS, tHE uNKNOWN; cOME wALK wiTH mE...          |\n| a3ooo    ___/\       ___/\ ____/\__________/\ ___/   __/\ _________9ooMB|\n+----------\__  \______\__  \____  __________  \  /   \__  \   _____/-----+\n|         tS/    __    \/      /  /_____   /     /     /        /         |\n·          /      /    /      /     /     /           /        /          ·\n rEG. /X! /      /    /      /     /     /     /     /        /ClAsSiC SHQ\n         /______/    /______/___________/_____/     /________/\n  lOTs oF      /____/                        /     /      2ooo AD (PC) WHQ\n /X uTiLS!          ·3 uSR nODES·aMiGa&pC!· /     /\n    ___/\ _________/\ _________/\ ___   ___/     / sTAFF : pROF dO riGHT,\n    \__  \ ________  \_________  \  /   \__     / aQUARiUS, riZE, rEMiX,\n·    /    _____/ /     __    /     /_____/     /_____ mASTERmAN, nEMESiS  ·\n:   /      /    /      /    /     /     /     /     /                     :\n|  /      /    /      /    /     /     /     /     /   eNJOY tHE sPEED!   |\n+-/______/----/______/    /___________/___________/-----------------------+\n|                   /____/                                                |\n| node#1: +46-90-120369   node#2: +46-90-178169   node#3: +46-90-142969   |\n|      (14.4k DS)              (16.8k DS)              (14.4k HST)        |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n@endnode\n\n@node OverLoad "AquaBulls v1.0 Documentation"\n                             .\n                             :\n                             |__       ___                   __\n        _____________________|  \_____/   \_________________/  \\n        \________     __     |     __      ________________     \_\n   .______/     U     \/     |     \/      __)____/      |/   ___/_____.\n   |:::::/ _ _         \     :      \_     |/     \      |       \:::::|\n   |:::  \___/_________/____   ______/_______      \_____A  _ _   \__::|\n   |:       / |            \___/       __   \______/      \/ _______/ :|\n   |  _____/  |   ____________________/  \________________/    \____  .|\n   |. \__     |___\__________      ________      _________       __/  :|\n   |:.  /     |    ___/     U      \/     |\     \/      |\      \   .:|\n   |::s/      :     \               \     _/      \_      /       \s.::|\n   |::c\_________    \______________/     A________/_________     /c:::|\n   °-----------\_____/-------\___________/------------------\____/-----°\n   ::::::                