INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('otl_mf10','OTL-MF10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/OTL-MF10.LHA','AquaMoveFiles','XIM','AquaMoveFiles','1.0',NULL,'OTL','__ _/\______/\___/\_ _\  /_________________. __ ___  ___  ____  /_ \\//                 | /  /  / /  / /  /__  \/ A utility for /X |',replace('[-aQUAmOVEfILES v1.0-]____  [-aQUARIUS/oTL-]\n__ _/\______/\___/\_ _\  /_________________.\n__ ___  ___  ____  /_ \\//                 |\n  /  /  / /  / /  /__  \/ A utility for /X |\n /  /  / /  / /  /  / that moves old files |\n_\__  /_/  /_/___  /  from one dir listing |\n____ /___ /__ ___ /  to another. Use it to |\nbIS\/   \/      \/keep your listings small.|\n-- -  -    - -- -   ---- - ---- -----------''\n','\n',char(10)),'AquaMoveFiles.doc',replace('\n       _ _ ___/\______/\__ ____/\___/\__ _ _/\____ _/\_ __ __/\______\n      __ ________   __   /   _   ___   / ______   \___/__/     _____/\n         bIS/   /   /   /   //   //   /___/ __¬   /  /  /  /\__   \\n           /   /   /   /   //   //   /   /  \    /  /  /  /   /   /\n    __  _ _\____  /\____  //_  //_____  /___/\  /\_____  /\ _/   /___\n     _  ___ _   \/  _  _\/_  \/____ __\/ ___ _\/_______\/____   /_ _/\n                                                            \  /\n                                  present                    \/\n\n                    a tool for AmiExpress/SigmaExpress:\n\n               >>> AquaMoveFiles v1.0 by Aquarius/Outlaws <<<\n\n\n                          Copyright ©1994 Aquarius\n\n                 Permission is granted to freely distribute\n               this product for non-commercial purposes only,\n                  as long as all files remain unmodified.\n\n\n\nArchive (OTL-MF10.LHA) Contents\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nAquaMoveFiles                8568 bytes   The executable.\nAquaMoveFiles.doc            5475 bytes   This document file.\nAquaMF.cfg.Amiga_2-1           95 bytes   A sample configuration file.\nAquaMF.cfg.Amiga_3-2           92 bytes   A sample configuration file.\nAquaMF.cfg.Console_2-1         84 bytes   A sample configuration file.\n\n\nIntroduction\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\nAquaMoveFiles is not a door. It is a utility that moves the descriptions\nfor files older than a certain number of days, from one AmiExpress-style\ndir listing to another. It can also move the files themself to another\ndirectory.\n\nWhy would you want to do that then? Well, you should keep your dir\nlistings rather small. For example, 200k for the upload dir and up to 600k\nfor the others could be suitable. But it depends on how much RAM memory\nyou have! Some doors (e.g. some zippy searchers and file scanners) load\nthe entire listing into memory (in order to speed it up). A large listing\ntakes much memory (and more time to load). A faker door would also benefit\nfrom smaller listings (especially the upload dir), because it will be much\nfaster.\n\nRecommended is that you use a cron program (like CyberCron) to run\nAquaMoveFiles once a day.\n\n\nRequirements\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\nAquaMoveFiles requires an Amiga with OS 2.04 or higher.\n\n\nUsage\n~~~~~\nThe command syntax is:\n\nAquaMoveFiles <ConfigFile1> <ConfigFile2> ...\n\n\nExamples:\n\nC:AquaMoveFiles S:AquaMF.cfg.Console_2-1\n\nC:AquaMoveFiles S:AquaMF.cfg.Amiga_3-2 S:AquaMF.cfg.Amiga_2-1\n\n\nThe configuration files\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nA config file for AquaMoveFiles has the following layout:\n\nLine 1: The number of days. Files uploaded this many days ago or earlier\n        will be moved.\n\nLine 2: The source dir listing. Full path to an AmiExpress DirX file.\n\nLine 3: The source directory. The directory where the files in the\n        source dir listing can be found. This line must end with a colon\n        (:) or a slash (/)!\n\nLine 4: The destination dir listing. Full path to an AmiExpress DirX file\n        (it doesn''t have to exist before this tool is used).\n\nLine 5: The destination directory. The directory where you want the old\n        files moved. If you don''t want to move them, write the same path\n        as the source directory. This line must end with a colon (:) or a\n        slash (/)!\n\n\nHere is an example:\n\n--- Cut here -----------------------------------------\n20\nBBS:CONF_Amiga/Dir3\nBBS:CONF_Amiga/Upload/\nBBS:CONF_Amiga/Dir2\nBBS:CONF_Amiga/OldUpload/\n--- Cut here -----------------------------------------\n\nThis means that files 20 or more days old according to BBS:CONF_Amiga/Dir3\nwill be moved from BBS:CONF_Amiga/Upload/ to BBS:CONF_Amiga/OldUpload/.\nThe descriptions for these files will be cut from BBS:CONF_Amiga/Dir3 and\nappended to BBS:CONF_Amiga/Dir2.\n\n\nContact Me!\n~~~~~~~~~~~\nIf you have any cool ideas for improvement of this tool, questions, bug\nreports or whatever, leave me a message on one of the following boards:\n\nNIGHTFALL ................ Whoosh ............ +46-90-120369  <---  Safest\nHALL OF FAME ............. Dansken ........... +46-910-26665      place to\nHYSTERIA ................. JAC ............... +46-21-842939     reach me!\nMASTURBATION STATION ..... Black Beard ....... +1-305-552-1192\nZION''S HIDEOUT ........... Zion .............. +1-614-876-0807\nDARK TOWER ............... Shadower .......... +1-801-476-9068\nMORTUARY ................. Bloodwolf ......... +1-312-284-7577\nBOONDOCKS ................ Sal-One! .......... +31-548-040-653\n\n\nHistory\n~~~~~~~\n1.0  (09-17-94) First release version.\n\n\nGreetings\n~~~~~~~~~\n                Greetings must go to (in no special order):\n\n           - Vegas/OTL - Biscrok/OTL - Toxic/OTL - AtomiX!/OTL -\n       - Whoosh/OTT^KRL^OTL^CLS - Snake/OTL - Nashua/OTL - SMS/OTL -\n    - Genghis Khan/OTL - The Other OTL Members! - Dansken - CornFlake -\n  - Ace Caze/Obscene - Firehawk! - fanta/THR - Static/THR - FAX! - Juan -\n - Psychopath - Danzig - Foss - Karma - Seagull - Marwin - CaT - Sal-One -\n - Metalbasher - No Limit - BoneIdle - Wilsom/Obscene - Stab - Kid Curry -\n - Chig/TDS - HardHack - Rize - Frosty - JAC/TDS - C/\TE¥E - AXL - Norad -\n - Crocodile - Freddy Kreuger/GOD - Doc Whoo - Zion! - Nocturne - Brutus -\n  - FireFlash/OTT - MDR/OTT - Neutralizer/OTT - Bytehunter/OTT - Remix! -\n    - WarDancer - Json/Kingdom - Slobo & Whale - [-HSR & MM-] - HiFly -\n      - Uffe - Gi Joe - Princip - The Silencer - Ezco - Vampire/PDY -\n          - Nero - Deltaforce! - Afterlife - The Ones I Forgot! -\n\n\n[EOF]\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',9279,2,0,NULL,NULL,'otl_mf10','scan',1780048664);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('otl_mrwf','OTL-MRWF.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/OTL-MRWF.LHA','MRW-File','XIM','MRW-File',NULL,'mRW/oTL','OTL','_| _ |_| | |_| |_| |  _| _ |_| Y |_| __|: __\_ | |\_ | |\_  __ |__\_ | |\_ | |\___ | _ ::Y  |  Y  |  Y   Y  |  Y  _  Y  ^  Y  |  Y:',replace('   .___. ._._. ._. ._.   .___. ._ _. .___..\n  _| _ |_| | |_| |_| |  _| _ |_| Y |_| __|:\n__\_ | |\_ | |\_  __ |__\_ | |\_ | |\___ | _\n::Y  |  Y  |  Y   Y  |  Y  _  Y  ^  Y  |  Y:\nsT|_ !  ._ !  ._  ._ !  ._ |  ._    ._ !  |:\n::::\___|:\___|:\_|:\___|:\|__|:\T__|:\___|:\n:·     oUTLAWS /X-iNNOVATION pRESENTS     ·:\n:   bbSfILErEMOVER tOOL v1.6 bY mRW/oTL    :\n:...(Usefull for SysOps with a small HD)...:\n','\n',char(10)),'MRW-File.Guide',replace('@DATABASE MRW-File Amiga Guide docs. \n@$VER: MRW-File 1.0\n@(C) Copyright Mr.Wishbone 1995-1996\n@AUTHOR Mr.Wishbone\n@NODE MAIN "  VISAS RULE - Mona Sahlin -95 (hehe :-)"\n - --------------------------------------------------------------- -\n\n                           bbSfILErEMOVER tOOL v1.6\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n                             Contents:\n\n           @{"[         o1. History                  ]" LINK HISTORY}\n           @{"[         o2. Installation             ]" LINK INSTALL}\n           @{"[         o3. Configuration            ]" LINK CONFIGU}\n           @{"[         o4. The credits              ]" LINK CREDITS}\n           @{"[         o5. Soon coming MRW-prods    ]" LINK SOONTOC}\n           @{"[         o6. MRW''s Greetings          ]" LINK GREETSI}\n           @{"[         o7. Where to reach me        ]" LINK REACHME}\n           @{"[         o8. Wanna join OTL?          ]" LINK JOINOTL}\n           @{"[         o9. Note to coders!          ]" LINK NOTETOO}\n           @{"[         1o. Comming in the future    ]" LINK UPDATES}\n           @{"[         11. Known bugs               ]" LINK KNOWNBUG}\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE HISTORY "History, hard to learn and completly useless!"\n\n                        \n                o1. History and what does it do\n\n Once upon a time there was a SysOp called ''nUP!'', he was suffering from\na major lack of HD-space(80MB for the BBS-files), so he accidently stumbled\nto this little wannabecoder(Mr.Wishbone),that was at the moment in Fanatic,\nsaid he could do anything with his computer..\n\n(At the moment I didn''t know that he meant coding=), well, okey, I did..),\nso, I asked if he could do me a prog. that would make all files\nolder than a specified date to be made 0kb long, so that they would take\nless room, but still they would be skipped if someone tried to upload them\nagain. Okey.. So he did that. Nice! But it wasn''t nice to trade when\nuploading all the files in the dir to another BBS(Yes, nUp! was very lazy).\nso I asked him to make an option to copy the files to another dir.\n\nThen Mr.Wishbone asked if nUP! knew a group with a powerful /X-section,\nand nUP! said: Outlaws is the world''s number one in the /X-business\n(Atleast almost), and Mr.Wishbone asked if I knew someone from OTL..\nThen I told the poor uninformed coder, that I was the OTL-finnish organizer,\nand because I had allways wanted a personal coder-slave, I took MRW to be\na Outlaws member.\n\nSo after that nUP! decided to slave the poor creature called Mr.Wishbone\nby telling him to code a door that would:\n\nA) Copy a file from the user specified dir/ to anotherdir/ older than a \n   certain date  (i.e 7 days or whatever) (note: this is optional\n   for the sysop, so if the sysop moonlights as a trader he can get the files\n   uploaded i.e today and then copy them to NComm:Trade/ or whatever and then\n   trade them until they get to old to delete them.)\n\nB) Set the file copied from dir/ to 0kB long. (Can be deleted to optional)\n\nC) Updates the users file list so that there is the text "DELETED!" over the \n   filesize so that users will se that a file has already been here.\n\nD) Format the HD hehe (Just kidding folks! =)\n\n(That story may be in some spots be quite fictious)\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE INSTALL "Installing is easy, using it ain''t!"\n\n                         o2. The installation\n\n For DD:\n\n1) Copy the DateTime.CFG.info to DOORS:MRW/MRW-File/ (Makedir u know :-)\n   *NOTE: Must be there! Otherwise the prog. won''t run!\n   (Lazy who me? - Ed''s Comment)\n\n2) Edit the config as you see suiteable for your purposes.\n\n3) Add this line to {CONF}/Data/Examine.DAT:\n   ''{YOURDIR}/MRW-File''\n\n..And that''s that!\n\n\n For /X:\n\n1) Copy the DateTime.CFG.info to DOORS:MRW/MRW-File/ (Makedir u know :-)\n   *NOTE: Must be there! Otherwise the prog. won''t run!\n   (Lazy who me? - Ed''s Comment)\n\n2) Edit the config as you see suiteable for your purposes.\n\n4) Add this line to your Filecheck/Examine.info\n   ''{YOURDIR}/MRW-File''\n\n..And that''s the end of that installation too!\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE CONFIGU "Now comes the fun part :^)"\n\n                         o3. Configuration\n\n And example configuration:\n\n               ---------- CUT HERE -----------\n DAYS=10\n ULDIRPATH=DAYDREAM:Elite/New/\n COPYDIRPATH=NCOMM:Trade/\n DELETEDAYS=10\n FLISTPATH=BBS:Elite/Data/Directory.002\n REMOVEDAYS=60\n PROGRAM=DD\n LONGMODE=NO\n\n               ---------- CUT HERE -----------\n\n "DAYS=10" - Delete all files older than 10 days.\n\n   This field in the icon tells the program that all of the files\n   in the upload dir older than 10 days will be set to the size of\n   0kB.\n\n "ULDIRPATH=DAYDREAM:Elite/New/" - Specifies the upload dir.\n\n   This field tells the program where to locate the upload dir.\n   In this dir all of the files older than 10 days (assuming that\n   DAYS was "DAYS=10") would be set to 0kB.\n\n "COPYDIRPATH=NCOMM:Trade/" - Specifies where to find the copydir.\n\n All files older [DAYS] will be set to 0kB will be copied to this \n directory before set to 0kB!.\n\n "DELETEDAYS=10" - Set how old a file can get in the copydir.\n\n If present then all files older than this will be deleted.\n (!NOT! set to 0kB!!!).\n\n "FLISTPATH=BBS:Elite/Data/Directory.002" - Filelist path.\n\n If this is in the config, then the sizeof of the file present in the\n file list will be replaced with ''MRWFILE''. Please note that the rest of\n the desc will remain intact. 2nd note: The default path is for daydream!\n so if you have /X use something like this:\n\n ''FLISTPATH=BBS:Elite/DIR2''\n\n "REMOVEDAYS=60" - Delete all files older than.\n\n Specifies how long a file can remain 0kb long, after it has reached this\n age it''ll be deleted (!NOT! set to 0kB!!!). This is mainly for speed\n reasons so that scanning the wdir will be faster (LESS TIME = LESS WASTE)\n\n "PROGRAM=DD" - Select mode for flist removal.\n\n If this is DD then it''ll use a diffrent offset for Filelist editing\n so that the filelist looks good :-) otherwise it''ll use the S!X/X standard\n so if you have /X then set this to whatever otherwise set it to DD\n This function has no effect if FLISTPATH isn''t present!\n\n "LONGMODE=NO" - Select between 12 & 18 chrs.\n\n This option only concernes DD users, if you have 18 chars long filenames\n in the filelist set this to YES otherwise you can set it to whatever..\n NOTE: this option has no effect if PROGRAM isn''t set to ''DD'' ...\n This function has no effect if FLISTPATH isn''t present!\n\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE CREDITS "Thank you, Thank you, Thank you very much!"\n\n\n                         o4. The credits\n\n\n             -  All bugs done by Mr.Wishbone/Outlaws  -\n\n                -  The main idea by nUP!/Outlaws  -\n\n         -  The little ideas by nUP!^Mr.Wishbone/Outlaws  -\n\n                    -  Design by nUP!/Outlaws  -\n\n          - The documentation by nUP!/Outlaws^mRW/Outlaws  -\n\n          -  All around pain in the ass mRW''s little bro  -\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE SOONTOC "Soon at a board near you!"\n\n                 o5. Soon coming mRW-Productions\n\n     mRW-Page       -a pager door for /X ^ DD\n     mRW-Join       -a joinconf door for DD    (And /X! (MRW''s Comment)\n     mRW-Who        -a 100% AquaWho copy :-) for /X (^DD?)\n     mRW-Stat       -a status door for /X ^ DD\n     mRW-KillIt!    -a doorremover for lame programmers :-) (/X only)\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE GREETSI "Greets to Mona Sahlin!"\n\n                         o6. MRW''s Greetings\n\n  dRUiD           - How''s life?\n  Akiro&dr.poop   - Are you busted or what?\n  tRAitOR         - I promise that I''ll finish it soon!\n  nUp!            - Hello :^)\n  Aquarius        - Feel like coding some doors with me?\n  POt-NooDlE      - I bet you moonlight as an askii artist!\n  EzCo            - You''re never around when I page you!\n  fUZZ            - Sorry I didn''t get into this months DC =(.\n  QuartZ          - Too bad I can''t be in MST too =)\n  Distler         - I''ll call you soon!\n  Hydra           - And you thought that I would code for DD :-) (kiddin)\n  Haka            - Smellin bad (KIDDING!) Hoppas du får ti''baks speeden\n  HotShots        - Värst vad du undviker mig... känner mig mobbad =)\n  Mona Sahlin     - Kanske du borde bli finans minister? hoho.\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE JOINOTL "Wanna join the best /X group? (Well almost :-)"\n\n                         o8. Wanna join Outlaws?\n\n    ________________________________ ___ __ _  _\n   _\\·\n   \\                  ______      ________        ·Mo!/(!·\n              _______|      |____|      _/ ___________         ______ _______\n   _________ _\\      /      |    |_     |      _     / ______ |      /      _|\n  /         \\\\      /|      |    _/     |      _      \\__    ||      \\      \\\n_//          \\_ __________._|    |      |      |______._/    /\\     _|\\      \\\n\\_____________/           |______|______|______|      |____  /\\_____\\________/\n                                                           \\/        \\\n                 · ouTLaWs ·                   _\\\n   _  _ __ ___ ________________________________\\\n\n\n We are searching for good\nCoders/Graphicians/Musicians/Traders/Boards/Crackers/Supliers/etc.\nSo if you think you''re one of the persons mentioned one line up,\nthen contact one of our organizers, or just a normal member for\nthe possible joining requests..\n\n\n\n Call our boards..\n\n    WHq  Wrath Of Khan.........................sYSOP:  GENGHiS KHAN\n    EHq  The Tribe.............................sYSOP:  sTERNONE\n    GHq  The Board.............................sYSOP:  BUD WEISER\n    GHq  Flying Dragon.........................sYSOP:  sAxOn!\n    GHq  Paradise Lost.........................sYSOP:  PICARD\n    BHq  SiN CiTY..............................sYSOP:  SiNTAX\n    LHq  Euro Trade Center.....................sYSOP:  tOXIC\n    IHq  Delta City............................sYSOP:  mODEM bOY\n    DHq  Megabyte..............................sYSOP:  nASHUA\n    SHq  Nightfall.............................sYSOP:  wHOOSH\n    DHq  Cool Corona...........................sYSOP:  Phantom\n    DHq  Mystery Land!.........................sYSOP:  fATE!\n   SFHq  Arctic Circle.........................sYSOP:  nUP!\n     Hq  Necronomicon..........................sYSOP:  Joo\n     Hq  Zillion Hours.........................sYSOP:  tRAiTOR\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE REACHME " Get a grip get a hold of a pro!"\n\n                      o7. Where to reachme\n\n        Reach me at theese boards across SWEDEN and FINLAND:\n\n   - ARCtiC CiRClE    1nd! - SYS0p:  nUp!       -  +358-PRiV-AtE   <- Safest place\n   - BERMUdA TRiANGlE ×ndz - SYS0p:  QuartZ     -  +358-HOlY-GRACE\n   - ZilliON hOURs    ×ndz - SYS0p:  tRAitOr    -  +358-MTR-FUKR\n\n   - INtOXiCAtiON     3ndz - SYS0p:  fUZZ       -  +46-tOP-SECREt  <- Fast response\n   - SERPENt hiLL     3ndz - SYS0p:  EzCo       -  +46-hYDRA-RULA  <- Here too.\n   - MELLOW iLLUSiONS 2ndz - SYS0p:  -zANOk!    -  +46-WhOLikES-U\n\n I also have an Email address: [email removed]\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE NOTETOO "HEY YOU THAT''s RIGHT! YOU!"\n\n                       o9. Note to coders\n\n Does anyone have have a HW ref. manual (3d ed.) for sale ? I am in a\n desperate need!!\n\n -MRW\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE UPDATES " Yet to come in the future"\n\n                    1o. Updates\n\n Soon you will be able to choose if you want the FILE_ID.DIZ stripped (Work\n in progress) However just so that I can see who is using my gr8t door\n you wont be able to remove the first line of the FILE_ID.DIZ which will\n contain stuff like version and stripped date.\n\n Logfile containning files set to 0kB (the names will be removed when the\n file is deleted i.e REMOVEDAYS=60...) so it wont set all files to 0kB!\n this should speed it up with 50% (atleast in big dirs :-).\n\n An option so that the prgrm will be loaded in to ram (or maybe an optional\n small prgrm which runs the main?) and then executed at a specefied time\n and date. this will speed up the logoff batch...\n\n If you have any suggestions (I don''t want any suggestions about a /T\\\n version :-) please let me know I can''t add it otherwise...\n\n Same for bug reports I can''t fix it until you tell me about it...\n\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE KNOWNBUG  "   --- ATTETION!! ---"\n\n                    11.   Bugs not fixed in this release!\n\n  MAJOR BUGS:\n\n          If year is a leap year my logorithms will foul up seriously\n          and kill files which are to young to die :-).\n\n          There is some c-function which handles this but I prefer to use\n          AmigaDOS functions, if I convert this src to asm oneday then\n          the c-functions will be little hard to translate :-)\n\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',26097,5,0,NULL,NULL,'otl_mrwf','scan',1780048664);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('otl_pw10','OTL-PW10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/OTL-PW10.LHA','AquaPWFail','XIM','AquaPWFail','1.0',NULL,'OTL','._________ ___ __ _/\______/  _/_ _/\__ ___. |               //____   __  ___/_/   /___ | | Great password /   /   /   /   /   /   / |',replace('[-aQUApWfAIL v1.0-]         /\__[-aQUARIUS-]\n._________ ___ __ _/\______/  _/_ _/\__ ___.\n|               //____   __  ___/_/   /___ |\n| Great password /   /   /   /   /   /   / |\n| failure door! _\___   /\___   /____   /__|\n| * Auto-mails   _ ___ /__ ___ /_ ____ /__/|\n|   sysop and user   \/      \/ -bIS!\/    |\n| * Special built-in pager with op. window |\n| * Creates last-password-failures bulletin|\n| Check it out! You won''t be disappointed! |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'AquaPWFail.guide',replace('@database AquaPWFail\n@author Aquarius/Outlaws\n@$VER: AquaPWFail.guide 1.0 (28.1.95)\n\n@node MAIN "AquaPWFail v1.0 Documentation"\n       _ _ ___/\______/\__ ____/\___/\__ _ _/\____ _/\_ __ __/\______\n      __ ________   __   /   _   ___   / ______   \___/__/     _____/\n         bIS/   /   /   /   //   //   /___/ __¬   /  /  /  /\__   \\n           /   /   /   /   //   //   /   /  \    /  /  /  /   /   /\n    __  _ _\____  /\____  //_  //_____  /___/\  /\_____  /\ _/   /___\n     _  ___ _   \/  _  _\/_  \/____ __\/ ___ _\/_______\/____   /_ _/\n                                                            \  /\n                                  present:                   \/\n\n                >>> AquaPWFail v1.0 by Aquarius/Outlaws <<<\n\n                      [- Contents of Documentation -]\n\n                @{"   Copyright Note   " Link Copyright   }   @{"   Configuration    " Link Configuration}\n                @{"  Archive Contents  " Link Archive     }   @{"      History       " Link History}\n                @{"    Introduction    " Link Introduction}   @{"  How to Reach Me   " Link ContactMe}\n                @{"      Features      " Link Features    }   @{"    Other Tools     " Link AquaTools}\n                @{"    Requirements    " Link Requirements}   @{"     Greetings      " Link Greetings}\n                @{"    Installation    " Link Installation}\n\n           @{" Comment on AQUA-FUQ.TXT " Link FuckText}   @{" Note about AquaSettings " Link AquaSettings}\n@endnode\n\n@node Copyright "AquaPWFail v1.0 Documentation"\n\n                          Copyright ©1995 Aquarius\n\n                 Permission is granted to freely distribute\n               this product for non-commercial purposes only,\n                  as long as all files remain unmodified.\n@endnode\n\n@node Archive "AquaPWFail v1.0 Documentation"\n\nArchive (OTL-PW10.LHA) Contents\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nDoors/AquaPWFail/\n   AquaPWFail         13928 bytes  The door itself.\n   AquaPWFail.guide   26401 bytes  This AmigaGuide doc!\n   AquaPWFail.info      960 bytes  A sample configuration icon.\n   BullText.txt         137 bytes  Will be inserted in last-pwfail bull.\n   Comment.txt          394 bytes  Will be shown when user leaves comment.\n\nCommands/SYSCmd/\n   PWFAIL.info         1277 bytes  Command icon for /X 3.0+.\n@endnode\n\n@node Introduction "AquaPWFail v1.0 Documentation"\n\nIntroduction\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\nAquaPWFail is a password failure door. You know, one that will be started\nwhen a user has failed 3 times in a row to enter his password correctly.\nIt has lots of nice and useful @{"features" Link Features}...\n@endnode\n\n@node Features "AquaPWFail v1.0 Documentation"\n\nFeatures\n~~~~~~~~\n* Auto-messages to sysop(s). It can automatically post a message to any\n  number of users, informing about the password failure - who, when,\n  where and the connect string. Why show the connect string then? Well you\n  might be able to conclude from that if it was someone who tried to hack\n  the account. For example, if it was an HST connect and you know that the\n  user owning the account has a pure V.32bis modem, then you should be\n  very suspicious...\n\n* Auto-message to user (optional of course). If it wasn''t the user owning\n  the account who made the password failure, it could be interesting for\n  him to be informed about it. You can configure what the ''from'' field in\n  the message header should read. If you let it be your handle, the user\n  can reply and explain to you about his password failure or tell you that\n  it wasn''t him...\n\n* Last-password-failures bulletin. The door can create a nice-looking\n  bulletin showing the last password failures (configurable number of\n  entries). Besides it being a funny thing to view, it is good for\n  users to check there now and then. If they are listed in the bulletin\n  but haven''t received any message from AquaPWFail (presuming that you\n  have ''Auto-message to user'' on) the hacker probably succeeded to hack\n  his account and deleted the message.\n\n* Special password failure log. If you want, the door can write to a log\n  (anywhere you like) about the password failure.\n\n* Page or leave comment. When the user has failed 3 times to enter his\n  password and then enters the door, he is given these options:\n\n        (1) Page Sysop\n        (2) Comment to Sysop\n        (Q) Hangup\n\n  This menu is shown repeatedly until Q is chosen.\n\n* Working comment function! Unlike in many other pwfail doors, the\n  ''Comment to Sysop'' function really works 100%. If you want several\n  users (for example yourself and some co-sysop) to receive the same\n  comments, that''s no problem.\n\n* Special built-in pager! When the user selects ''Page Sysop'' assuming\n  you''re "available" or you have configured that pwfail-users can override\n  the chatflag, the paging starts: A font-sensitive operator window opens\n  on the default public screen (which usually is Workbench). It has a\n  graphical progress bar which goes from 0% to 100% during the paging.\n  There is a progress bar on the user side as well. The window has three\n  buttons: ''Go into Chat'', ''Be Quiet'' and ''Deny Chat''. Pressing <Escape>\n  or clicking in the close gadget has the same function as pressing ''Be\n  Quiet''. Pressing <Enter> means ''Go into Chat''. There are also ordinary\n  hotkeys for every button.\n@endnode\n\n@node Requirements "AquaPWFail v1.0 Documentation"\n\nRequirements\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\n- An Amiga with OS 2.04 or higher.\n\n- AmiExpress, SigmaExpress or any compatible program.\n@endnode\n\n@node Installation "AquaPWFail v1.0 Documentation"\n\nInstallation\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\nJust copy the ''AquaPWFail'' directory (the inner one) to ''Doors:'', and\n(for /X 3.0+) put the provided command icon ''PWFAIL.info'' in your ''SYSCmd''\ndrawer.\n\nThe door is "pure" and is therefore safe to make resident.\n\nThe text ''Doors:AquaPWFail/Comment.txt'' will be displayed when the user\nchoses to leave a comment to the sysop. Edit it if you like.\n\nIf ''Doors:AquaPWFail/BullText.txt'' exists, it will be inserted in the\nlast-password-failures bulletin.\n\nNow you must @{"configure" Link Configuration} the door...\n@endnode\n\n@node Configuration "AquaPWFail v1.0 Documentation"\n\nTooltypes in ''Doors:AquaPWFail/AquaPWFail.info'':\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n       @{" SYSOP_MSGBASE   " Link SYSOP_MSGBASE}\n       @{" AUTOMAIL.x      " Link AUTOMAIL.x}\n       @{" COMMENT.x       " Link COMMENT.x}\n       @{" USER_MSGBASE    " Link USER_MSGBASE}\n       @{" TO_USER_FROM    " Link TO_USER_FROM}\n       @{" LOG_PATH        " Link LOG_PATH}\n       @{" BULL_PATH       " Link BULL_PATH}\n       @{" BULL_USERS      " Link BULL_USERS}\n       @{" CHATFLAG_IGNORE " Link CHATFLAG_IGNORE}\n       @{" PAGE_BEEP       " Link PAGE_BEEP}\n       @{" QUIETPOP        " Link QUIETPOP}\n       @{" PAGESTART_RUN   " Link PAGESTART_RUN}\n       @{" PAGESTOP_RUN    " Link PAGESTOP_RUN}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node SYSOP_MSGBASE "AquaPWFail v1.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: SYSOP_MSGBASE=<path>                                  [Required]\nExample : SYSOP_MSGBASE=BBS:CONF_Staff/MsgBase/\n\nThis tooltype specifies the message base directory where messages to\nsysops will be written (see @{"AUTOMAIL.<num>" Link AUTOMAIL.x} and @{"COMMENT.<num>" Link COMMENT.x}). It MUST end\nwith ''/'' or '':''.\n@endnode\n\n@node AUTOMAIL.x "AquaPWFail v1.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: AUTOMAIL.<num>=<name>                                 [Optional]\nExample : AUTOMAIL.1=Aquarius\n\nThese tooltypes specify the users who will be notified of every password\nfailure: a message will automatically be posted to them. No AUTOMAIL.<num>\ntooltypes means that no auto-messages will be posted.\n@endnode\n\n@node COMMENT.x "AquaPWFail v1.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: COMMENT.<num>=<name>                  [At least ONE is required]\nExample : COMMENT.1=Aquarius\n\nThese tooltypes specify the users who will receive the comments written by\nusers in the door (when they have chosen "Comment to Sysop").\n@endnode\n\n@node USER_MSGBASE "AquaPWFail v1.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: USER_MSGBASE=<path>                                   [Optional]\nExample : USER_MSGBASE=BBS:CONF_NewUsers/MsgBase/\n\nIf this tooltype is present, the door will write a message to the user\nhimself. The tooltype specifies the path to the message base where the\nmessage will be written. If it was someone who tried to hack his account\nit could be helpful for him to know that. The path MUST end with ''/'' or\n'':''.\n@endnode\n\n@node TO_USER_FROM "AquaPWFail v1.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: TO_USER_FROM=<string>       [Optional, default: AquaPWFail vX.X]\nExample : TO_USER_FROM=Aquarius\n\nThis tooltype specifies the user (or any other string) that will stand as\nsender in the auto-message to the user himself. If no @{"USER_MSGBASE" Link USER_MSGBASE}\ntooltype is present, that message won''t be posted, and this tooltype will\nbe ignored.\n@endnode\n\n@node LOG_PATH "AquaPWFail v1.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: LOG_PATH=<path>                                       [Optional]\nExample : LOG_PATH=Doors:AquaPWFail/AquaPWFail.Log\n\nThis tooltype specifies the path (including filename) where password\nfailures will be logged. If you leave this out, no log file will be\nmaintained.\n@endnode\n\n@node BULL_PATH "AquaPWFail v1.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: BULL_PATH=<path>                                      [Optional]\nExample : BULL_PATH=Doors:AquaPWFail/AquaPWFail.Bull\n\nThis tooltype specifies the path (including filename) where you want the\nlast-password-failures bulletin to be created. If you leave this out, no\nbulletin will be made.\n@endnode\n\n@node BULL_USERS "AquaPWFail v1.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: BULL_USERS=<number>                      [Optional, default: 10]\nExample : BULL_USERS=12\n\nThis tooltype specifies the number of users that will be displayed in the\nlast-password-failures bulletin.\n@endnode\n\n@node CHATFLAG_IGNORE "AquaPWFail v1.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: CHATFLAG_IGNORE=<YES|NO>                 [Optional, default: NO]\nExample : CHATFLAG_IGNORE=YES\n\nIf you set this to YES, the "available-for-chat flag" will be ignored and\nthe user in the door will always be able to page you.\n@endnode\n\n@node PAGE_BEEP "AquaPWFail v1.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: PAGE_BEEP=<YES|NO>                       [Optional, default: NO]\nExample : PAGE_BEEP=YES\n\nThis tooltype lets you decide if you want the door to make system beeps\nduring paging.\n@endnode\n\n@node QUIETPOP "AquaPWFail v1.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: QUIETPOP=<YES|NO>                        [Optional, default: NO]\nExample : QUIETPOP=NO\n\nThis tooltype determines what should happen when you press the ''Be Quiet''\nbutton in the operator window. If the AmiExpress screen should be popped\nto front, set the tooltype to YES. If it is NO then the previously\nfrontmost screen will be brought to front and the previously active window\nwill be activated.\n@endnode\n\n@node PAGESTART_RUN "AquaPWFail v1.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: PAGESTART_RUN=<CLI command>                           [Optional]\nExample : PAGESTART_RUN=C:Player mod.nice\n\nThe command you write here will be executed when the paging starts. (It is\nrun asyncronously so the door doesn''t wait for it to return.)\n@endnode\n\n@node PAGESTOP_RUN "AquaPWFail v1.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: PAGESTOP_RUN=<CLI command>                            [Optional]\nExample : PAGESTOP_RUN=C:KillPlayer\n\nThis command is executed when the operator window is closed (for any\nreason).\n@endnode\n\n@node History "AquaPWFail v1.0 Documentation"\n\nHistory\n~~~~~~~\n\n0.1 (12-26-94) First beta ready.\n\n\n0.2 (12-30-94) Built-in pager finished! Thanks to Sandman for inspiration.\n\n\n0.3 (12-30-94) It now works (can read connect string etc) if the\n               callerslog contains the attempted password instead of\n               "xxxx".\n\n               Added tooltypes PAGESTART_RUN and PAGESTOP_RUN.\n\n\n0.4 (01-09-95) If chat has been denied once, the user can''t page again.\n               Thanks to Ace Caze for the suggestion!\n\n               Restructured the tooltypes somewhat:\n                 Removed:\n                   SYSOP.<num>=<...>\n                 Added:\n                   AUTOMAIL.<num>=<receiver of automsg>\n                   COMMENT.<num>=<receiver of user comment>\n                   TO_USER_FROM=<sender of msg to user>\n\n               Time and date are now written in the body of the automsg\n               to sysop(s) and msg to user.\n               (I find it easier than having to look in the msg header.\n               And if the user replies to the msg, the time & date will\n               still be there, if he quotes.)\n\n               Made a better-looking door title..\n\n               Last pw failures bulletin!! Thanks to Dansken for bugging\n               me about it. :)\n\n               New tooltypes:\n                 BULL_PATH=<bulletin filename>\n                 BULL_USERS=<max # users in bulletin>\n\n               "Doors:AquaPWFail/BullText.txt" is inserted in the\n               bulletin...\n\n               If there was error reading callerslog, time and date will\n               be set to current, so no more "??:??:?? ??-??-??".\n\n               It now writes "Please hold a second..." at the start while\n               posting all messages, writing to the log and creating the\n               bulletin.\n\n               If BULL_USERS=1 then the bulletin title will be\n               "LAST PASSWORD FAILURE" instead of "LAST 1 PASSWORD\n               FAILURES".\n\n\n1.0 (01-11-95) Removed unused code and fixed a few strings.\n\n    (01-25-95) Fixed a gfx bug: The progress bar would grow a few pixels\n               too wide.\n\n    (01-28-95) First release!\n@endnode\n\n@node ContactMe "AquaPWFail v1.0 Documentation"\n\nContact Me!\n~~~~~~~~~~~\nIf you have any cool ideas for improvement of this tool, questions, bug\nreports or whatever, contact me on one of the following boards:\n\n@{"NIGHTFALL" Link NIGHTFALL} ................ Whoosh ............ +46-90120369  <---  Safest\nHALL OF FAME ............. Dansken ........... +46-91026665      place to\nACES HIGH ................ Norad ............. +46-41044886     reach me!\nINTERCHANGE .............. Princip ........... +46-86082339\nZION''S HIDEOUT ........... Zion .............. +1-PRIVATE!!\nDEATH ROW ................ Shadower .......... +1-PRIVATE!!\nBOONDOCKS ................ Sal-One ........... +31-PRIVATE!!\n@endnode\n\n@node AquaTools "AquaPWFail v1.0 Documentation"\n\nThe AquaTools Collection\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nHere is the complete list of my released tools (the latest versions):\n\nTool Name              File Name     Short Description\n---------------------- ------------- ------------------------------------------\nDisable v1.1           AQDSBL11.LHA  Payuser handling system.\nDisplayer v1.0         AQDSPL10.LHA  Text displayer. Perfect for door menu e.g.\nNetEdit v1.0           AQNETE10.LHA  Editor for certain netmail systems.\nConfReplace v1.0       OTL-CR10.LHA  Find and replace area names in User.Data.\nListSpeeder v2.1       OTL-LS21.LHA  Filelist downloader.\nAnnounce v2.0          OTL-AN20.LHA  Notifies online users of logons/logoffs.\nAquaWho v2.0           OTL-AW20.LHA  Totally configurable WHO door!\nSpeedCheck v2.1        OTL-SC21.LHA  Disables download at too low connect rates.\nStripper v1.2          OTL-ST12.LHA  Strips log files to desired file sizes.\nAquaScan v1.0          OTL-AS10.LHA  File scanner! (F, N, CS, FR.)\nAquaCreateAcc v1.0     OTL-CA10.LHA  Door to create new accounts with.\nAquaMoveFiles v1.0     OTL-MF10.LHA  File and description mover, by date.\nAquaSafety v1.0        OTL-SA10.LHA  Anti-BBS-downtime utility.\nAquaAdder v1.0         OTL-AA10.LHA  Text adder.\nAquaBulls v2.0         OTL-AB20.LHA  Bulletin viewer.\nAquaQuick v1.0         OTL-QK10.LHA  Quick-logon door.\nRestoreQuietness v1.0  OTL-RQ10.LHA  Restores the nodes'' "quietness" at logoff.\nAquaSettings v1.0      OTL-SE10.LHA  ''W'' replacement. Menu of config commands.\nAquaQuiet v1.1         OTL-AQ11.LHA  ''Q'' replacement. Toggles quiet node.\nAquaPWFail v1.0        OTL-PW10.LHA  Password failure door.\nAquaTopChat v1.0       OTL-TC10.LHA  Top-chat door.\n\n(...and more are coming!)\n\nYou can find them all on @{"Nightfall" Link NIGHTFALL} +46-90-120369 (free download)!\n@endnode\n\n@node BetaTesters "AquaPWFail v1.0 Documentation"\n\nBeta Testers\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThese are my beta testers. My tools wouldn''t have been as good as they\nare now if it hadn''t been for them. Many thanks dudes!\n\nACE CAZE ................. Dragon''s Lair ........ +46-16147118\nEZCO ..................... Serpent Hill ......... +46-8800293\nDANSKEN .................. Hall of Fame ......... +46-91026665\nFIREHAWK ................. Hardware Tower ....... +46-OFFLINE!\nKID CURRY ................ Pet Sematary ......... +46-PRIVATE!\nLOCKJAMMER ............... Substate ............. +46-OFFLINE!\nMARKY & POWER ............ Spread Draft ......... +49-PRIVATE!\nNASHUA ................... MegaByte ............. +45-42881885\nPLAYMATE ................. Northern Empire ...... +45-39619420\nPRINCIP .................. Interchange .......... +46-PRIVATE!\nPSYCHOPATH ............... Raising Hell ......... +46-243227029\nRIZE & FROSTY ............ Another World ........ +46-48088100\nSANDMAN .................. reference-board ............ +46-31918587\nSTATIC & FANTA ........... Frosen Assets ........ +46-322665225\nVEGAS & BISCROK .......... Overload ............. +46-OFFLINE!\nVITAL .................... Future Entrance ...... +46-60574467\nWHOOSH ................... @{"Nightfall" Link NIGHTFALL} ............ +46-90120369\nWIZE & HIFLY ............. Waterdeep ............ +46-PRIVATE!\n@endnode\n\n@node Greetings "AquaPWFail v1.0 Documentation"\n\nGreetings\n~~~~~~~~~\n                Greetings must go to (in no special order):\n\n           - Vegas/OTL - Biscrok/OTL - Toxic/OTL - Nashua/OTL -\n     - Snake/OTL - Whoosh/OTT^DVS^CLS^OTL^R2 - AtomiX!/OTL - SMS/OTL -\n   - Genghis Khan/OTL - The Other OTL Members - Ace Caze - Dansken/ACS -\n  - Princip! - Sandman - Rize & Frosty - Static & fanta - Marky & Power -\n  - Psychopath - Norad - Firehawk - Marwin - Danzig! - Lockjammer - MDR -\n  - HardHack - Chig - Kid Curry - Ezco - Enzo - Playmate - HiFly - Wize -\n   - Wild Thing - Juan! - Wilsom - Gi Joe - Sal-One - Zion! - Shadower -\n    - Doc Whoo - FAX - JAz - Bowen/OTT - Json - WarDancer - CornFlake -\n       - Bilbo Baggins - Sasha - Metalbasher - Psyche - CountZero! -\n               - Vital - Karma - Kain - Vileius - Nike/DLT -\n                       - And The Friends I Forgot! -\n\n\n                    Special thanks to my @{"beta testers" Link BetaTesters}!!\n\n\n                         A few personal messages:\n\nWhoosh         - Whooopssss... Nice chatting with you every day. :)\n\nToxic/OTL      - Hard getting cards isn''t it? If you can, call Nightfall\n                 (new pwfail door hehe)!\n\nVegas/OTL      - Yeah let''s get the Swedish section rocking! I mean, MORE!\n                 Btw, Norrland is such a nice place, don''t you think? :)\n\nBiscrok/OTL    - The master of strange (tüffa) modules. ;)\n\nDansken        - Great friend and beta tester! Learn C soon!! hehe\n\nMarky & Power  - Hope you can find a new way to call...\n\nEzco           - Great Who designs!!\n\nAce Caze       - Funny dude and great beta tester! Ok, nothing wrong with\n                 topaz 8! You just need a magnifying glass..\n\nSnowman/Ex.OTL - Where did you disappear??? Get in touch, mate..\n@endnode\n\n@node NIGHTFALL "AquaPWFail v1.0 Documentation"\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|         iNTO tOTAL dARKNESS, tHE uNKNOWN; cOME wALK wiTH mE...          |\n| a3ooo    ___/\       ___/\ ____/\__________/\ ___/   __/\ _________9ooMB|\n+----------\__  \______\__  \____  __________  \  /   \__  \   _____/-----+\n|         tS/    __    \/      /  /_____   /     /     /        /         |\n· /X 4.xx  /      /    /      /     /     /           /        /    r2 sHQ·\n          /      /    /      /     /     /     /     /        /    dVS sHQ\n   eNJOY /______/    /______/___________/_____/     /________/    oTT  sHQ\n   tHE         /____/                        /     /         oTL diST siTE\n sPEED!             ·3 uSR nODES riNGDOWN!· /     /\n    ___/\ _________/\ _________/\ ___   ___/     / sTAFF: wHOOSH, aQUARiUS,\n    \__  \ ________  \_________  \  /   \__     / riZE, mASTERmAN, nEMESiS\n·    /    _____/ /     __    /     /_____/     /_____                     ·\n:   /      /    /      /    /     /     /     /     /    mORE tHAN 1200   :\n|  /      /    /      /    /     /     /     /     / aMiX tOOLS oNLiNE!!  |\n+-/______/----/______/    /___________/___________/-----------------------+\n|                   /____/                                                |\n| nODE#1: +46-90-120369   nODE#2: +46-riNGDOWN!!  nODE#3: +46-riNGDOWN!!  |\n|      (14.4k DS)              (16.8k DS)              (28.8k DS)         |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n@endnode\n\n@node FuckText "AquaPWFail v1.0 Documentation"\n\nComment on AQUA-FUQ.TXT\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n--vv-vv----------------- START OF "AQUA-FUQ.TXT" ------------------vv-vv--\n\n@BEGIN_FILE_ID.DIZ\n--------------------------------------------\nPot-Noodle speaks: All of AQUARIUS /X doors\nare MY sources that HE edited! This is fuqn\nLAME! I bet he put alot of BACKDOORS in them\ntoo! DONT USE THEM! There''s PROOF in this\ntext that shows that I made all the doors!\n-------------------------[ P0t-N00dle/atx ]-\n@END_FILE_ID.DIZ\n\nI''m UPSET! About 1 year ago, Aquarius were a active user of my bbs, and he\ntold me he were an /X tool developer, so i gave him access to my /X tool/source\nconferance, and he leeched all of my unreleased utils in this conf.\nNow, 1 year later, i see more and more of them poppin up as ''quack-wa-scan''\nand whatever. I have no idea what he might have added more then just his\nname to my doors, but i would suggest you NOT to use them.\n\n                                                           >p0t-n00dle/anThrox<\n\n--^^-^^------------------ END OF "AQUA-FUQ.TXT" -------------------^^-^^--\n\nIf you''ve had the bad luck to have seen this text, you have probably\nfigured out that it is total bullshit. Then you''re absolutely right! It is\nplain lies! I haven''t even called P0T-NOoDLE''s BBS, EVER! This text is\njust another attempt from some lame "wanna-be" to destroy for a guy\nworking hard to supply the scene with backdoor-free, quality /X tools. It\nmakes me sad, whoever it is being attacked with lies like that. Can''t the\npitiful lamers producing such crap do something positive, instead of just\ntrying to destroy for others? I guess not... But then they should get the\nfuck out of the scene, at least until they''ve grown up!!\n\nThe lamer who wrote AQUA-FUQ.TXT is also abusing the highly respected name\nP0T-NOoDLE (great tools man!). Of course it''s not P0T-NOoDLE who wrote it.\nA few observations to make:\n\n* P0T-NOoDLE is English and I don''t think he would write "Aquarius were a\n  active user"... I''m sure the real writer has done his best to get it\n  right.\n\n* As far as I know, P0T-NOoDLE codes his tools in assembler (and some in\n  ARexx). I write mine in C, so how could I have stolen and edited his\n  sources??\n\n* P0T-NOoDLE has never used icons as config. I do it in most of my tools.\n\nAnd so on... If you still (!) have any doubts, take a look at the doc for\nP0T-NOoDLE''s excellent Super-DupeCheck v1.03 and the list of his\nunreleased tools. Then you''ll see that I haven''t made a single one like\nany of those.\n\nYou can also ask any of my @{"beta testers" Link BetaTesters}. They can assure you that my tools\nhave been DEVELOPED and weren''t just suddenly finished. For example\nAquaScan - it was rather simple in the beginning; no scroll-back, no\nflagging by number, no date/file separators etc. In this doc, I have\nincluded the @{"history" Link History} for the early beta versions of this tool. I usually\ndon''t do that. But just so that you can see that it is MY work! (sigh)\n\nAnd about the "accusation" of backdoors... Do you think I would spend most\nof my spare time writing lame backdoors?! Of course not! I code /X tools\nfor fun and for others to enjoy. And obviously people DO enjoy them. :)\nAs an example, Sasha (Datalus BBS, UK) just told me about AquaScan:\n"every (and i mean every) bbs in the uk uses it!"... That''s the only\nreward I want for my work; to hear that my tools are appreciated.\n\nSo if you see AQUA-FUQ.TXT somewhere, or any other text like that, nuke it\nto hell!\n\nOk, enough about this CRAP!\n@endnode\n\n@node AquaSettings "AquaPWFail v1.0 Documentation"\n\nNote about AquaSettings\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nFirst of all, I''m glad so many boards are using AquaSettings! Just a few\ndays after release and suddenly it''s installed on every other board! Cool!\n\nBut it seems I made a little mistake in the AquaSettings v1.0 archive..\nIn the provided configuration icon ''AquaSettings.info'', the ''CMD.1''\ntooltype was set to ''W''. It SHOULD have been ''W_INTERNAL''. This only goes\nfor AmiExpress 3.xx/4.xx. The icon was correct for SigmaExpress and\nAmiExpress 2.xx. I did write about that in the doc, but there I assumed\n''CMD.1'' was ''W_INTERNAL'' from the beginning.\n\nSo what''s the difference? Well, when you start AquaSettings you get a menu\nof different configuration stuff. The first entry is "Basic settings", or\nwhatever you name it, i.e. it starts the internal W command. But if\n''CMD.1=W'' then the door won''t be able to return to the menu again. That''s\nbecause of a limitation in AmiExpress/S-Express which doesn''t let any door\nrun an internal command (with the same name as a door), without quitting\nthe door first. But the W_INTERNAL command is a way around this. If you\nuse ''CMD.1=W_INTERNAL'' with AmiExpress 3.xx/4.xx, then "Basic settings"\nwill behave like all the other menu entries: you will be taken back to the\nAquaSettings menu afterwards.\n\nI haven''t seen it changed on any board, so what I have learnt from this is\nthat the contents of provided configuration files are very important, and\nthat most sysops don''t bother to read the doc entirely and check the\nconfiguration, which is a bit unfortunate.\n\n  .------------------------------------------------------------------.\n  | If you''re running AmiExpress 3.xx/4.xx, change ''CMD.1=W'' to      |\n  | ''CMD.1=W_INTERNAL'' in ''Doors:AquaSettings/AquaSettings.info'',    |\n  | and make sure you have copied ''W_INTERNAL.info'' from the archive |\n  | (OTL-SE10.LHA) to your ''BBSCmd'' drawer (NOT ''SYSCmd'').           |\n  `------------------------------------------------------------------''\n@endnode\n\n[EOF]\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',21736,3,0,NULL,NULL,'otl_pw10','scan',1780048664);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('otl_qk10','OTL-QK10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/OTL-QK10.LHA','AquaQuick','XIM','[-aQUAqUICK -]          /\__[-aQUARIUS-]','1.0',NULL,'OTL','._________ ___ __ _/\______/  _/_ _/\__ ___. |               //____   __  ___/_/   /___ | | Quick-logon    /   /   /   /   /   /   / |',replace('[-aQUAqUICK v1.0-]          /\__[-aQUARIUS-]\n._________ ___ __ _/\______/  _/_ _/\__ ___.\n|               //____   __  ___/_/   /___ |\n| Quick-logon    /   /   /   /   /   /   / |\n| door with up  _\___   /\___   /____   /__|\n| to 9 different _ ___ /__ ___ /_ ____ /__/|\n| logon modes.       \/      \/ -bIS!\/    |\n| Totally configurable prompt. Users who   |\n| don''t like to get the question when they |\n| logon can use the configuration door to  |\n| set a permanent logon mode. Residentable!|\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'AquaQuick.guide',replace('@database AquaQuick\n@author Aquarius/Outlaws\n@$VER: AquaQuick.guide 1.0 (21.1.95)\n\n@node MAIN "AquaQuick v1.0 Documentation"\n\n       _ _ ___/\______/\__ ____/\___/\__ _ _/\____ _/\_ __ __/\______\n      __ ________   __   /   _   ___   / ______   \___/__/     _____/\n         bIS/   /   /   /   //   //   /___/ __¬   /  /  /  /\__   \\n           /   /   /   /   //   //   /   /  \    /  /  /  /   /   /\n    __  _ _\____  /\____  //_  //_____  /___/\  /\_____  /\ _/   /___\n     _  ___ _   \/  _  _\/_  \/____ __\/ ___ _\/_______\/____   /_ _/\n                                                            \  /\n                                  present:                   \/\n\n                 >>> AquaQuick v1.0 by Aquarius/Outlaws <<<\n\n                      [- Contents of Documentation -]\n\n                @{"   Copyright Note   " Link Copyright   }   @{"   Configuration    " Link Configuration}\n                @{"  Archive Contents  " Link Archive     }   @{"      History       " Link History}\n                @{"    Introduction    " Link Introduction}   @{"  How to Reach Me   " Link ContactMe}\n                @{"    Requirements    " Link Requirements}   @{"    Other Tools     " Link AquaTools}\n                @{"    Installation    " Link Installation}   @{"     Greetings      " Link Greetings}\n@endnode\n\n@node Copyright "AquaQuick v1.0 Documentation"\n\n                          Copyright ©1995 Aquarius\n\n                 Permission is granted to freely distribute\n               this product for non-commercial purposes only,\n                  as long as all files remain unmodified.\n@endnode\n\n@node Archive "AquaQuick v1.0 Documentation"\n\nArchive (OTL-QK10.LHA) Contents\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nDoors/AquaQuick/\n   AquaQuick                 3780 bytes   The main door.\n   AquaQuickConfig           3768 bytes   Configuration door.\n   AquaQuick.doc            11922 bytes   Ascii version of the doc.\n   AquaQuick.guide          14892 bytes   This AmigaGuide doc!\n\nDoors/AquaQuick/Ex[1-3]/\n   AquaQuick.info                         Sample config icon.\n   AquaQuick.Prompt                       Sample "prompt" file.\n   Bull*                                  Sample bulletins.\n\nCommands/SYSCmd/\n   quick.info                1276 bytes   Command icon for /X 3.0+.\n   quickcfg.info             1362 bytes   Command icon for /X 3.0+.\n@endnode\n\n@node Introduction "AquaQuick v1.0 Documentation"\n\nIntroduction\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\nWhen a BBS user logs on, a various number of bulletins are displayed\nbefore him. The dilemma for you (the sysop) is that some people want to\nsee everything (WeekTop, TopUploaders, LastCallers etc) but some don''t\nwant anything of that. Well, AquaQuick is the solution! It lets you have\nup to 9 login modes to offer your users. For example, you can make it ask\n"(N)ormal, (S)hortened or (Q)uick Logon (N/s/q)?". Pressing N shows all\nthe screens, S gives a shorter logon (only WeekTop and LastCallers for\ninstance), and Q throws the user directly to mailscan.\n\nWhat''s wrong with the normal quick logons (''Y Q''/''N Q'' at the ANSI\nprompt)? you might ask yourself. Well, that only gives you 2 "modes", and\nif you always want to show something or run some particular MCI commands\nat every logon, AquaQuick is the solution! Then you should disable the\nnormal quick logons by putting DISABLE_QUICK_LOGONS in BBS:Node(x).info\n(for /X 3.0+).\n\nIf the user always want to use a particular mode he can configure that\neasily with the configuration door. Then he won''t get any question from\nthe main door at logon.\n@endnode\n\n@node Requirements "AquaQuick v1.0 Documentation"\n\nRequirements\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\n- An Amiga with OS 2.0 or higher.\n\n- AmiExpress, SigmaExpress or any compatible program.\n@endnode\n\n@node Installation "AquaQuick v1.0 Documentation"\n\nInstallation\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\nMake a directory ''Doors:AquaQuick''. It should contain ''AquaQuick'' (the\nmain door), ''AquaQuickConfig'' (configuration door), ''AquaQuick.info''\n(configuration icon) and ''AquaQuick.Prompt'' (text specifying the\n"prompt"). Then (for /X 3.0+) put the provided command icon ''quick.info''\nin your SYSCmd drawer and ''quickcfg.info'' in your BBSCmd drawer.\n\nAquaQuick is perfectly safe to make resident. The changes you have to make\nto the command icons in that case are: Change the value of "LOCATION" to\n"AquaQuick" and add the tooltype "RESIDENT". The configuration door\nAquaQuickConfig can also be made resident but there''s not much to gain\nwith that - it''s probably not run very often.\n\n\nYou must remove all bulletins that would normally be displayed at logon.\nThey are:\n\nBBS:BULL[<acs>].<suffix>\nBBS:Node<x>/BULL[<acs>].<suffix>\n\n\nLeave ''BBS:Node<x>/Logon[<acs>].<suffix>''. That is where AquaQuick is\nstarted from, using an MCI command:\n\n---------Cut-here------------------\n~\n~CC_QUICK|\n-----------Cut-here----------------\n\nIn case you didn''t know: Any MCI text must start with a ''~'', and every MCI\ncommand must end with a ''|'', a space ('' '') or a newline!\n\nIf you have other doors that must always be run at logon, you can put them\nthere too. For example if you''re using Announce (written by me), the text\nshould look something like this:\n\n---------Cut-here------------------\n~\n~CC_ANNLOGON|~CC_QUICK|\n-----------Cut-here----------------\n\nMaybe unvalidated users shouldn''t be able to use AquaQuick. Then make sure\nto have several Logon[<acs>].txt files, for example Logon100.txt (for\nnormal users) and Logon.txt (for unvalidated users), the last one without\n~CC_QUICK.\n\n\nThe file ''Doors:AquaQuick/AquaQuick.Prompt'' is what is shown to the user\nwhen he shall select login mode. You can write whatever you like there.\n\n\nYou should disable the normal quick logon way - ''Y Q''/''N Q'' at the ANSI\nprompt - at least if you have MCI commands which must be run at every\nlogon (for example Announce). For /X 3.0+, put the tooltype\n''DISABLE_QUICK_LOGONS'' in the BBS:Node(x).info icons.\n\n\nNow you must @{"configure" Link Configuration} the door...\n@endnode\n\n@node Configuration "AquaQuick v1.0 Documentation"\n\nTooltypes in ''Doors:AquaQuick/AquaQuick.info'':\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n @{" KEY.<num>        " Link ttKEY}\n @{" DESC.<num>       " Link ttDESC}\n @{" DISP.<num>.<num> " Link ttDISP}\n @{" DEFAULT          " Link ttDEFAULT}\n @{" CALLERSLOG       " Link ttCALLERSLOG}\n@endnode\n\n@node ttKEY "AquaQuick v1.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: KEY.<num>=<string>                    At least one required! :)\nExample : KEY.2=Yes\n\nThese tooltypes specify what choices the user can make. You can write\nstrings here but it is the *first character* that the user can type to\nchoose that alternative. But when the choice is made, the entire string\nwill be displayed. For example, let the KEY.x tooltypes in the icon be:\n\nKEY.1=Normal\nKEY.2=Quick\n\nWhat the user can press at the prompt is N and Q. If he presses N then\n"Normal" is written. If he types Q then "Quick" is written.\n@endnode\n\n@node ttDESC "AquaQuick v1.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: DESC.<num>=<string>               Optional, default: "" (ugly!)\nExample : DESC.2=Always quick logon\n\nThese strings will be shown in the configuration door as descriptions for\nthe logon modes.\n@endnode\n\n@node ttDISP "AquaQuick v1.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: DISP.<num>.<num>=<path pattern>                       Optional.\nExample : DISP.2.1=BBS:BullNotQuick%X.%S\n\nThese tooltypes specify what texts to display for the various login modes.\nThe first <num> says what @{"KEY.<num>" Link ttKEY} it belongs to. The second <num> is a\ncounter starting with 1. For example, if login mode number 2 is chosen,\nthe door first displays the textfile specified by DISP.2.1, then DISP.2.2,\nthen DISP.2.3, and so on until no more DISP.2.x tooltype can be found.\n\n<Path pattern> can be just a plain path to a textfile, or it can contain\none or more of the following codes:\n\n  "%N" - is replaced with the node number\n  "%X" - is replaced with an access level\n  "%S" - is replaced with a suffix ("TXT" for example)\n\nAn example.. Let''s say the node number is 3 and the user has access level\n100 and a screentype with the suffix "PCT". Then if a path pattern is\n"BBS:Node%N/BullFull%X.%S" the door will search for text files in this\norder and display the first one that it finds:\n\nBBS:Node3/BullFull100.PCT\nBBS:Node3/BullFull100.TXT\nBBS:Node3/BullFull95.PCT\nBBS:Node3/BullFull95.TXT\nBBS:Node3/BullFull90.PCT\nBBS:Node3/BullFull90.TXT\n...\nBBS:Node3/BullFull5.PCT\nBBS:Node3/BullFull5.TXT\nBBS:Node3/BullFull.PCT\nBBS:Node3/BullFull.TXT\n@endnode\n\n@node ttDEFAULT "AquaQuick v1.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: DEFAULT=<num>                                         Optional.\nExample : DEFAULT=1\n\nThis determines which logon mode should be the default. That is if the\nuser presses Return, that mode will be used. If you don''t want any mode to\nbe default, don''t use this tooltype.\n@endnode\n\n@node ttCALLERSLOG "AquaQuick v1.0 Documentation"\n\nTemplate: CALLERSLOG=<YES|NO>                       Optional. Default: NO\nExample : CALLERSLOG=NO\n\nIf "CALLERSLOG=YES" then the door will write to the callerslog what choice\nthe user made.\n@endnode\n\n@node History "AquaQuick v1.0 Documentation"\n\nHistory\n~~~~~~~\n1.0 (01-21-95)  First release version!\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ContactMe "AquaQuick v1.0 Documentation"\n\nContact Me!\n~~~~~~~~~~~\nIf you have any cool ideas for improvement of this tool, questions, bug\nreports or whatever, contact me on one of the following boards:\n\n@{"NIGHTFALL" Link NIGHTFALL} ................ Whoosh ............ +46-90-120369  <---  Safest\nHALL OF FAME ............. Dansken ........... +46-910-26665      place to\nACES HIGH ................ Norad ............. +46-410-44886     reach me!\nINTERCHANGE .............. Princip ........... +46-8-6082339\nZION''S HIDEOUT ........... Zion .............. +1-PRIVATE!!\nDEATH ROW ................ Shadower .......... +1-PRIVATE!!\nMORTUARY ................. Bloodwolf ......... +1-PRIVATE!!\nBOONDOCKS ................ Sal-One ........... +31-PRIVATE!!\n@endnode\n\n@node AquaTools "AquaQuick v1.0 Documentation"\n\nThe AquaTools Collection\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nHere is the complete list of my released tools (the latest versions):\n\nTool Name              File Name     Short Description\n---------------------- ------------- ------------------------------------------\nDisable v1.1           AQDSBL11.LHA  Payuser handling system.\nDisplayer v1.0         AQDSPL10.LHA  Text displayer. Perfect for door menu e.g.\nNetEdit v1.0           AQNETE10.LHA  Editor for certain netmail systems.\nConfReplace v1.0       OTL-CR10.LHA  Find and replace" area names in User.Data.\nListSpeeder v2.1       OTL-LS21.LHA  Filelist downloader.\nAnnounce v2.0          OTL-AN20.LHA  Notifies online users of logons/logoffs.\nAquaWho v2.0           OTL-AW20.LHA  Totally configurable WHO door!\nSpeedCheck v2.1        OTL-SC21.LHA  Disables download at too low connect rates.\nStripper v1.2          OTL-ST12.LHA  Strips log files to desired file sizes.\nAquaQuiet v1.0         OTL-AQ10.LHA  ''Q'' replacement. Toggles quiet node.\nAquaScan v1.0          OTL-AS10.LHA  File scanner! (F, N, CS, FR.)\nAquaCreateAcc v1.0     OTL-CA10.LHA  Door to create new accounts with.\nAquaMoveFiles v1.0     OTL-MF10.LHA  File and description mover, by date.\nAquaSafety v1.0        OTL-SA10.LHA  Anti-BBS-downtime utility.\nAquaAdder v1.0         OTL-AA10.LHA  Text adder.\nAquaBulls v2.0         OTL-AB20.LHA  Bulletin viewer.\nAquaQuick v1.0         OTL-QK10.LHA  Quick-logon door.\nRestoreQuietness v1.0  OTL-RQ10.LHA  Restores the nodes'' "quietness" at logoff.\nAquaSettings v1.0      OTL-SE10.LHA  ''W'' replacement. Menu of config commands.\n\n(...and more are coming!)\n\nYou can find them all on @{"Nightfall" Link NIGHTFALL} +46-90-120369 (free download)!\n@endnode\n\n@node Greetings "AquaQuick v1.0 Documentation"\n\nGreetings\n~~~~~~~~~\n                Greetings must go to (in no special order):\n\n           - Vegas/OTL - Biscrok/OTL - Toxic/OTL - Nashua/OTL -\n     - Snake/OTL - Whoosh/OTT^DVS^CLS^OTL^R2 - AtomiX!/OTL - SMS/OTL -\n   - Genghis Khan/OTL - The Other OTL Members - Ace Caze - Dansken/ACS -\n  - Princip! - Sandman - Rize & Frosty - Static & fanta - Marky & Power -\n  - Psychopath - Norad - Firehawk - Marwin - Danzig! - Lockjammer - MDR -\n   - HardHack! - Chig! - Wild Thing - Ezco - Enzo - FAX! - AXL - HiFly -\n    - Kid Curry - Juan - Wilsom - Gi Joe - Sal-One - Zion! - Shadower -\n     - Doc Whoo - JAz - Bowen/OTT - Json - WarDancer - MFM - Vileius -\n        - Bilbo Baggins - Biztro - Metalbasher - Kain - CornFlake -\n              - Karma - Dalamar - Wize - CountZero - Psyche -\n                         - The Friends I Forgot! -\n\n\n                         A few personal messages:\n\nWhoosh         - Whooopssss... Nice chatting with you every day. :)\n\nToxic/OTL      - Hard getting cards isn''t it? If you can, call Nightfall\n                 (new pwfail door hehe)!\n\nVegas/OTL      - Yeah let''s get the Swedish section rocking! I mean, MORE!\n                 Btw, Norrland is such a nice place, don''t you think? :)\n\nBiscrok/OTL    - The master of strange (tüffa) modules. ;)\n\nDansken        - Great friend and beta tester! Learn C soon!! hehe\n\nMarky & Power  - Hope you can find a new way to call...\n\nEzco           - Great Who designs!!\n\nAce Caze       - Funny dude and great beta tester! Hmmm why not\n                 topaz 8 on your WB?? ;)\n\nSnowman/Ex.OTL - Where did you disappear??? Get in touch, mate..\n@endnode\n\n@node NIGHTFALL "AquaQuick v1.0 Documentation"\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|         iNTO tOTAL dARKNESS, tHE uNKNOWN; cOME wALK wiTH mE...          |\n| a3ooo    ___/\       ___/\ ____/\__________/\ ___/   __/\ _________9ooMB|\n+----------\__  \______\__  \____  __________  \  /   \__  \   _____/-----+\n|         tS/    __    \/      /  /_____   /     /     /        /         |\n· /X 4.xx  /      /    /      /     /     /           /        /    r2 sHQ·\n          /      /    /      /     /     /     /     /        /    dVS sHQ\n   eNJOY /______/    /______/___________/_____/     /________/    oTT  sHQ\n   tHE         /____/                        /     /         oTL diST siTE\n sPEED!             ·3 uSR nODES riNGDOWN!· /     /\n    ___/\ _________/\ _________/\ ___   ___/     / sTAFF: wHOOSH, aQUARiUS,\n    \__  \ ________  \_________  \  /   \__     / riZE, mASTERmAN, nEMESiS\n·    /    _____/ /     __    /     /_____/     /_____                     ·\n:   /      /    /      /    /     /     /     /     /    mORE tHAN 1200   :\n|  /      /    /      /    /     /     /     /     / aMiX tOOLS oNLiNE!!  |\n+-/______/----/______/    /___________/___________/-----------------------+\n|                   /____/                                                |\n| nODE#1: +46-90-120369   nODE#2: +46-riNGDOWN!!  nODE#3: +46-riNGDOWN!!  |\n|      (14.4k DS)              (16.8k DS)              (28.8k DS)         |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n@endnode\n\n[EOF]\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,20829,2,0,NULL,NULL,'otl_qk10_aquaquick','scan',1780048664);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('otl_rq','OTL-RQ.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/OTL-RQ.LHA','Cls','XIM','[-REQUEST-]                 /\__   [--]','2.05','Neptune','OTL','._________ ___ __ _/\______/  _/_ _/\__ ___. |               //____   __  ___/_/   /___ | | REQUEST v2.05  /   /   /   /   /   /   / |',replace('[-REQUEST-]                 /\__   [-v2.05-]\n._________ ___ __ _/\______/  _/_ _/\__ ___.\n|               //____   __  ___/_/   /___ |\n| REQUEST v2.05  /   /   /   /   /   /   / |\n| [ RELEASE 2 ] _\___   /\___   /____   /__|\n|                _ ___ /__ ___ /_ ____ /__/|\n| We are proud to    \/      \/ -bIS!\/    |\n| present the best requester ever made for |\n| any /X. Lot''s of new features and bug-   |\n| fixes since the last release. CHECK IT!! |\n| Code by Neptune and Odyssey of Outlaws.  |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'Cls.doc',replace('\n\n                         .____.    .____.\n       ________._________|    |___ |    | ____________________________\n     ./   __   |    |    |  _____/_|    |_\____   |      /   |   ____/_.\n __  |     /   |    |    |   \     |    |    _    |     /    |\______  |  __\n-\/--|    /    |    |    |    \    |    |    /    |    /\    |    /    |--\/-\n-----|_________|_________|_________|____|_________|____/\____|_________|-p!--\n\n                            -  p r e s e n t s  -\n\n\n                                 *  C L S  *\n\n\nIntroduction / Features\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  This door is another production from outlaws/therion and it''s fully\n  programmed in c to accomplish some speed. If features a simle extra\n  command!!. REAL simple but nice!.. IT SIMPLY CLEARS THE SCREEN!!\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,25694,2,0,NULL,NULL,'otl_rq20_cls','scan',1780048664);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('otl_rq10','OTL-RQ10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/OTL-RQ10.LHA','RestoreQuietness','XIM','RestoreQuietness','1.0',NULL,'OTL','._________ ___ __ _/\______/  _/_ _/\__ ___. |               //____   __  ___/_/   /___ | | A utility for  /   /   /   /   /   /   / |',replace('[-rESTOREqUIETNESS v1.0-]   /\__[-aQUARIUS-]\n._________ ___ __ _/\______/  _/_ _/\__ ___.\n|               //____   __  ___/_/   /___ |\n| A utility for  /   /   /   /   /   /   / |\n| /X and clones _\___   /\___   /____   /__|\n| that fixes a   _ ___ /__ ___ /_ ____ /__/|\n| "bug": At logoff   \/      \/ -bIS!\/    |\n| it restores the node to its original     |\n| state, quiet or not quiet. Very small!   |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'RestoreQuietness.guide',replace('@database RestoreQuietness\n@author Aquarius/Outlaws\n@$VER: RestoreQuietness.guide 1.0 (21.1.95)\n\n@node MAIN "RestoreQuietness v1.0 Documentation"\n\n       _ _ ___/\______/\__ ____/\___/\__ _ _/\____ _/\_ __ __/\______\n      __ ________   __   /   _   ___   / ______   \___/__/     _____/\n         bIS/   /   /   /   //   //   /___/ __¬   /  /  /  /\__   \\n           /   /   /   /   //   //   /   /  \    /  /  /  /   /   /\n    __  _ _\____  /\____  //_  //_____  /___/\  /\_____  /\ _/   /___\n     _  ___ _   \/  _  _\/_  \/____ __\/ ___ _\/_______\/____   /_ _/\n                                                            \  /\n                                  present:                   \/\n\n              >>> RestoreQuietness v1.0 by Aquarius/Outlaws <<<\n\n                      [- Contents of Documentation -]\n\n                @{"   Copyright Note   " Link Copyright   }   @{"      History       " Link History}\n                @{"  Archive Contents  " Link Archive     }   @{"  How to Reach Me   " Link ContactMe}\n                @{"    Introduction    " Link Introduction}   @{"    Other Tools     " Link AquaTools}\n                @{"       Usage        " Link Usage       }   @{"     Greetings      " Link Greetings}\n@endnode\n\n@node Copyright "RestoreQuietness v1.0 Documentation"\n\n                          Copyright ©1995 Aquarius\n\n                 Permission is granted to freely distribute\n               this product for non-commercial purposes only,\n                  as long as all files remain unmodified.\n@endnode\n\n@node Archive "RestoreQuietness v1.0 Documentation"\n\nArchive (OTL-RQ10.LHA) Contents\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nRestoreQuietness               656 bytes   The executable.\nRestoreQuietness.doc          6288 bytes   Ascii version of the doc.\nRestoreQuietness.guide        8984 bytes   This AmigaGuide doc!\n@endnode\n\n@node Introduction "RestoreQuietness v1.0 Documentation"\n\nIntroduction\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThe Q command in AmiExpress and SigmaExpress is used to make a node quiet\n(invisible to other nodes). But these BBS programs (maybe not the latest\nSigmaExpress?) have a bug - they don''t restore the nodes'' "quietness" when\nthe user logs out, not even when the next user logs in! RestoreQuietness\nfixes this problem. It restores the node''s quietness to what it originally\nwas (when the node was started by ACP) - quiet or not quiet.\n@endnode\n\n@node Usage "RestoreQuietness v1.0 Documentation"\n\nUsage\n~~~~~\nRestoreQuietness is not a door. It is a utility that should be run from\nthe logoff scripts. It requires one argument: the node number.\n\nLet''s say you put the tool in your C: directory. Insert the following line\n*last* in the logoff scripts:\n\nC:RestoreQuietness <node>\n\nFor example, in the logoff script for node 3 the last line should look\nlike this:\n\nC:RestoreQuietness 3\n\nWhy the *last* line?! Well, if the user wants to be quiet (or not quiet)\nwhen he logs off he should remain so as long as possible during the\nlogoff.\n\nThis tool can be made resident even though I don''t see the point in doing\nso - it is very small and is loaded in no-time.\n@endnode\n\n@node History "RestoreQuietness v1.0 Documentation"\n\nHistory\n~~~~~~~\n1.0 (01-21-95)  First release version!\n@endnode\n\n@node ContactMe "RestoreQuietness v1.0 Documentation"\n\nContact Me!\n~~~~~~~~~~~\nIf you have any cool ideas for improvement of this tool, questions, bug\nreports or whatever, contact me on one of the following boards:\n\n@{"NIGHTFALL" Link NIGHTFALL} ................ Whoosh ............ +46-90-120369  <---  Safest\nHALL OF FAME ............. Dansken ........... +46-910-26665      place to\nACES HIGH ................ Norad ............. +46-410-44886     reach me!\nINTERCHANGE .............. Princip ........... +46-8-6082339\nZION''S HIDEOUT ........... Zion .............. +1-PRIVATE!!\nDEATH ROW ................ Shadower .......... +1-PRIVATE!!\nMORTUARY ................. Bloodwolf ......... +1-PRIVATE!!\nBOONDOCKS ................ Sal-One ........... +31-PRIVATE!!\n@endnode\n\n@node AquaTools "RestoreQuietness v1.0 Documentation"\n\nThe AquaTools Collection\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nHere is the complete list of my released tools (the latest versions):\n\nTool Name              File Name     Short Description\n---------------------- ------------- ------------------------------------------\nDisable v1.1           AQDSBL11.LHA  Payuser handling system.\nDisplayer v1.0         AQDSPL10.LHA  Text displayer. Perfect for door menu e.g.\nNetEdit v1.0           AQNETE10.LHA  Editor for certain netmail systems.\nConfReplace v1.0       OTL-CR10.LHA  Find and replace" area names in User.Data.\nListSpeeder v2.1       OTL-LS21.LHA  Filelist downloader.\nAnnounce v2.0          OTL-AN20.LHA  Notifies online users of logons/logoffs.\nAquaWho v2.0           OTL-AW20.LHA  Totally configurable WHO door!\nSpeedCheck v2.1        OTL-SC21.LHA  Disables download at too low connect rates.\nStripper v1.2          OTL-ST12.LHA  Strips log files to desired file sizes.\nAquaQuiet v1.0         OTL-AQ10.LHA  ''Q'' replacement. Toggles quiet node.\nAquaScan v1.0          OTL-AS10.LHA  File scanner! (F, N, CS, FR.)\nAquaCreateAcc v1.0     OTL-CA10.LHA  Door to create new accounts with.\nAquaMoveFiles v1.0     OTL-MF10.LHA  File and description mover, by date.\nAquaSafety v1.0        OTL-SA10.LHA  Anti-BBS-downtime utility.\nAquaAdder v1.0         OTL-AA10.LHA  Text adder.\nAquaBulls v2.0         OTL-AB20.LHA  Bulletin viewer.\nAquaQuick v1.0         OTL-QK10.LHA  Quick-logon door.\nRestoreQuietness v1.0  OTL-RQ10.LHA  Restores the nodes'' "quietness" at logoff.\nAquaSettings v1.0      OTL-SE10.LHA  ''W'' replacement. Menu of config commands.\n\n(...and more are coming!)\n\nYou can find them all on @{"Nightfall" Link NIGHTFALL} +46-90-120369 (free download)!\n@endnode\n\n@node Greetings "RestoreQuietness v1.0 Documentation"\n\nGreetings\n~~~~~~~~~\n                Greetings must go to (in no special order):\n\n           - Vegas/OTL - Biscrok/OTL - Toxic/OTL - Nashua/OTL -\n     - Snake/OTL - Whoosh/OTT^DVS^CLS^OTL^R2 - AtomiX!/OTL - SMS/OTL -\n   - Genghis Khan/OTL - The Other OTL Members - Ace Caze - Dansken/ACS -\n  - Princip! - Sandman - Rize & Frosty - Static & fanta - Marky & Power -\n  - Psychopath - Norad - Firehawk - Marwin - Danzig! - Lockjammer - MDR -\n   - HardHack! - Chig! - Wild Thing - Ezco - Enzo - FAX! - AXL - HiFly -\n    - Kid Curry - Juan - Wilsom - Gi Joe - Sal-One - Zion! - Shadower -\n     - Doc Whoo - JAz - Bowen/OTT - Json - WarDancer - MFM - Vileius -\n        - Bilbo Baggins - Biztro - Metalbasher - Kain - CornFlake -\n              - Karma - Dalamar - Wize - CountZero - Psyche -\n                         - The Friends I Forgot! -\n\n\n                         A few personal messages:\n\nWhoosh         - Whooopssss... Nice chatting with you every day. :)\n\nToxic/OTL      - Hard getting cards isn''t it? If you can, call Nightfall\n                 (new pwfail door hehe)!\n\nVegas/OTL      - Yeah let''s get the Swedish section rocking! I mean, MORE!\n                 Btw, Norrland is such a nice place, don''t you think? :)\n\nBiscrok/OTL    - The master of strange (tüffa) modules. ;)\n\nDansken        - Great friend and beta tester! Learn C soon!! hehe\n\nMarky & Power  - Hope you can find a new way to call...\n\nEzco           - Great Who designs!!\n\nAce Caze       - Funny dude and great beta tester! Hmmm why not\n                 topaz 8 on your WB?? ;)\n\nSnowman/Ex.OTL - Where did you disappear??? Get in touch, mate..\n@endnode\n\n@node NIGHTFALL "RestoreQuietness v1.0 Documentation"\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|         iNTO tOTAL dARKNESS, tHE uNKNOWN; cOME wALK wiTH mE...          |\n| a3ooo    ___/\       ___/\ ____/\__________/\ ___/   __/\ _________9ooMB|\n+----------\__  \______\__  \____  __________  \  /   \__  \   _____/-----+\n|         tS/    __    \/      /  /_____   /     /     /        /         |\n· /X 4.xx  /      /    /      /     /     /           /        /    r2 sHQ·\n          /      /    /      /     /     /     /     /        /    dVS sHQ\n   eNJOY /______/    /______/___________/_____/     /________/    oTT  sHQ\n   tHE         /____/                        /     /         oTL diST siTE\n sPEED!             ·3 uSR nODES riNGDOWN!· /     /\n    ___/\ _________/\ _________/\ ___   ___/     / sTAFF: wHOOSH, aQUARiUS,\n    \__  \ ________  \_________  \  /   \__     / riZE, mASTERmAN, nEMESiS\n·    /    _____/ /     __    /     /_____/     /_____                     ·\n:   /      /    /      /    /     /     /     /     /    mORE tHAN 1200   :\n|  /      /    /      /    /     /     /     /     / aMiX tOOLS oNLiNE!!  |\n+-/______/----/______/    /___________/___________/-----------------------+\n|                   /____/                                                |\n| nODE#1: +46-90-120369   nODE#2: +46-riNGDOWN!!  nODE#3: +46-riNGDOWN!!  |\n|      (14.4k DS)              (16.8k DS)              (28.8k DS)         |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n@endnode\n\n[EOF]\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',11912,3,0,NULL,NULL,'otl_rq10','scan',1780048664);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('otl_rq20','OTL-RQ20.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/OTL-RQ20.LHA','Cls','XIM','[-REQUEST-]                 /\__   [--]','2.05','Neptune','OTL','._________ ___ __ _/\______/  _/_ _/\__ ___. |               //____   __  ___/_/   /___ | | REQUEST v2.05  /   /   /   /   /   /   / |',replace('[-REQUEST-]                 /\__   [-v2.05-]\n._________ ___ __ _/\______/  _/_ _/\__ ___.\n|               //____   __  ___/_/   /___ |\n| REQUEST v2.05  /   /   /   /   /   /   / |\n| [ RELEASE 2 ] _\___   /\___   /____   /__|\n|                _ ___ /__ ___ /_ ____ /__/|\n| We are proud to    \/      \/ -bIS!\/    |\n| present the best requester ever made for |\n| any /X. Lot''s of new features and bug-   |\n| fixes since the last release. CHECK IT!! |\n| Code by Neptune and Odyssey of Outlaws.  |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'Request.doc',replace('\n\n                         .____.    .____.\n       ________._________|    |___ |    | ____________________________\n     ./   __   |    |    |  _____/_|    |_\____   |      /   |   ____/_.\n __  |     /   |    |    |   \     |    |    _    |     /    |\______  |  __\n-\/--|    /    |    |    |    \    |    |    /    |    /\    |    /    |--\/-\n-----|_________|_________|_________|____|_________|____/\____|_________|-p!--\n\n                            -  p r e s e n t s  -\n\n\n                         REQUEST v2.06 [RELEASE 2]\n                     COPYRIGHT 94-95, NEPTUNE & ODYSSEY\n\n\nIndex\n~~~~~\n  Contents of the archive\n  Introduction / Features\n  Requirements\n  Installation\n  Tooltypes (Configuration)\n  Copyrights\n  Greetings / Personal hellos\n  File_id.diz\n  Buggreports, Suggestions & How to contact!\n\n\nContents of the archive\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  BBS:Commands/BBSCmd/\n    REQ.info                1022 bytes - Provided command icon for /X 3.x+.\n\n  BBS:Doors/Request/\n    Request                24396 bytes - The door for any cpu.\n    Request.info            1240 bytes - Sample configuration icon.\n    Request.doc             6510 bytes - This documentation.\n\n\nIntroduction / Features\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  This door is another production from outlaws/therion and it''s fully\n  programmed in c to accomplish some speed.\n\n\nRequirements\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  - Any amiga with os2.0+.\n  - Amiexpress, S-Express or simular.\n\n\nInstallation\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  (CLI) : Copy Doors/Request to Doors:\n\n  2.x\n    (CLI) : Edit BBS:Commands/BBS.CMD\n      --- cut --- cut --- cut --- cut --- cut ---\n      *REQ       XM001Doors:Request/Request\n      --- cut --- cut --- cut --- cut --- cut ---\n\n  3.x, 4.x\n    (CLI) : Copy Commands/BBSCmd/REQ.info to BBS:Commands/BBSCmd/\n\n\nTooltypes (Configuration)\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  This door configures by tooltypes, (Doors:Request/Request.info):\n\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  Template: BULL.OUTPUT=<path:filename>\n  Example : BULL.OUTPUT=BBS:Conf.Requests/Bull.txt\n\n  Destination textfile for bulletin/list of requested files.\n\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  Template: BULL.HEADER=<path:filename>\n  Example : BULL.HEADER=Doors:Request/Header.txt\n\n  Headertext for the destination textfile.\n\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  Template: BULL.TAIL=<path:filename>\n  Example : BULL.TAIL=Doors:Request/Tailer.txt\n\n  Tailtext for the destination textfile.\n\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  Template: MSG.BASE_PATH=<path>\n  Example : MSG.BASE_PATH=BBS:Conf.Requests/Msgbase/\n\n  Messagebase path for conference to post messages in, note that it MUST\n  end with an "/" or an ":".\n\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  Template: MSG.MID_STRING=<string>\n  Example : MSG.MID_STRING=esc[34m|esc[0m\n\n  Separator string for destination textfile, Use Leftamiga+ctrl+esc to\n  get an escape character in a tooltype editor..\n\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  Template: MSG.PATTERN=<path:filename>\n  Example : MSG.PATTERN=Doors:Request/Message.dsg\n\n  Location of the design for the message output!. How to do some own\n  design will be explained later on!!\n\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  Template: MSG.SUBJECT=<string>\n  Example : MSG.SUBJECT=MOST WANTED!!\n\n  Simply the subject of the letter that will be created!\n\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  Template: MSG.POST_TO=<string>\n  Example : MSG.POST_TO=EALL\n\n  User to post the message to, "EALL" or "ALL" is recommended.\n\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  Template: ACS.DELETE_ALL=<access>\n  Example : ACS.DELETE_ALL=255\n\n  Minimum of access to delete any request (not just your own!!).\n\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  Template: DATAFILE_PATH=<path:filename>\n  Example : DATAFILE_PATH=Doors:Request/Request.data\n\n  Datafile path for the datafile!! NOT the same as the old Request data\n  so delete the old one or just don''t use the same!!\n\n  ----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\nMessage configuration\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n  These can be used anywhere in the text pattern:\n\n  %DT - Current Date\n  %UN - Username/Handle\n  %LT - Location/Group\n  %RQ - File Requested\n  %CM - Longer Description\n\n  If the user choose NOT to enter a longer comment the rows that starts with\n  an "°" character will be skipped. And if the user choose to enter a longer\n  comment these row''s will be shown, and the "°" char will be ignored!!\n\n  --- cut --- cut --- cut --- cut --- cut --- cut --- cut --- cut ---\n\n          Current Date: %DT\n       Username/Handle: %UN\n        Location/Group: %LT\n\n        Requested file: %RQ\n\n  ° Longer description..\n  ° : %CM\n  °\n  --- cut --- cut --- cut --- cut --- cut --- cut --- cut --- cut ---\n\n\nCopyrights\n~~~~~~~~~~\n  Permission is granted to freely distribute this product for non-commercial\n  purposes only, as long as all files remain unmodified. I take no charge\n  for the door but you could leave me a mail and tell me that you use it and\n  perhaps support my board.\n\n\nMega ultra hello to megaultramightyblastkillerboost.. (Greetings)\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n                Aquarius/Otl - Hijacker/Cls - Sandman/Flt\n            Dexter/Afl - Guardian/Ind - Juan/Trsi - Phase!/Frs\n         Kid Curry/Cls - Ezco/Dpl - Twister/Dcs? - Amigaspirit/Ind\n       B.B.King/Atm - Dalamar/Led - Nike/Crz - Whoosh/Otl - Nero/Pdx\n      Zcandaler/Ind - Karma/Acl? - Bobo/Mst - Vegas/Otl - Biscrok/Otl\n\n\nFile_id.diz\n~~~~~~~~~~~\n[-REQUEST-]                 /\__   [-v2.05-]\n._________ ___ __ _/\______/  _/_ _/\__ ___.\n|               //____   __  ___/_/   /___ |\n| REQUEST v2.05  /   /   /   /   /   /   / |\n| [ RELEASE 2 ] _\___   /\___   /____   /__|\n|                _ ___ /__ ___ /_ ____ /__/|\n| We are proud to    \/      \/ -bIS!\/    |\n| present the best requester ever made for |\n| any /X. Lot''s of new features and bug-   |\n| fixes since the last release. CHECK IT!! |\n| Code by Neptune and Odyssey of Outlaws.  |\n`------------------------------------------''\n\n\nBug reports, Suggestions & How to contact!\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  If you have any suggestions or bug-reports please contact us on..\n\n                  ---  FROZEN ASSETS  +46-322-665225  ---\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,43942,9,0,NULL,NULL,'otl_rq20_cls','scan',1780048664);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('otl_rq21','OTL-RQ21.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/OTL-RQ21.LHA',NULL,'XIM','Installer',NULL,NULL,'OTL',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'auto-added',96759,0,0,NULL,NULL,'otl_rq21','scan',1780048664);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('otl_sa10','OTL-SA10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/OTL-SA10.LHA','AquaSafety','XIM','AquaSafety','1.0',NULL,'OTL','__ _/\______/\___/\_ _\  /_________________. __ ___  ___  ____  /_ \\//                 | /  /  / /  / /  /__  \/  Anti-BBS-lockup |',replace('[-aQUAsAFETY v1.0-]   ____  [-aQUARIUS/oTL-]\n__ _/\______/\___/\_ _\  /_________________.\n__ ___  ___  ____  /_ \\//                 |\n  /  /  / /  / /  /__  \/  Anti-BBS-lockup |\n /  /  / /  / /  /  /   util! No more long |\n_\__  /_/  /_/___  /  annoying down-times! |\n____ /___ /__ ___ /  Every sysop with such |\nbIS\/   \/      \/ problems  should  check |\n  this out! It''s primarily intended for /X |\n but probably works with any other system. |\n-- -  -    - -- -   ---- - ---- -----------''\n','\n',char(10)),'AquaSafety.doc',replace('\n       _ _ ___/\______/\__ ____/\___/\__ _ _/\____ _/\_ __ __/\______\n      __ ________   __   /   _   ___   / ______   \___/__/     _____/\n         bIS/   /   /   /   //   //   /___/ __¬   /  /  /  /\__   \\n           /   /   /   /   //   //   /   /  \    /  /  /  /   /   /\n    __  _ _\____  /\____  //_  //_____  /___/\  /\_____  /\ _/   /___\n     _  ___ _   \/  _  _\/_  \/____ __\/ ___ _\/_______\/____   /_ _/\n                                                            \  /\n                                  present                    \/\n\n                >>> AquaSafety v1.0 by Aquarius/Outlaws <<<\n\n\n                          Copyright ©1994 Aquarius\n\n                 Permission is granted to freely distribute\n               this product for non-commercial purposes only,\n                  as long as all files remain unmodified.\n\n\n\nArchive (OTL-SA10.LHA) Contents\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nAquaSafety                14796 bytes   The executable.\nAquaSafety.doc             5937 bytes   This document.\nS/AquaSafety.config         290 bytes   A sample configuration file.\n\n\nIntroduction\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\nIf you have a BBS and it sometimes hangs, locks up, then AquaSafety might\nbe a very useful tool for you. What it does is that it watches certain\nfiles and if they haven''t been touched for a certain time (x minutes) it\nresets the computer! But before resetting, it opens a requester saying\n"Warning! Rebooting in y seconds!" (countdown). It has an abort button.\nYou can also press return or escape to abort. If you do, the program goes\nback to watching the files for another period of x minutes. So if you''re\nby the computer doing something, AquaSafety won''t make you angry by\nresetting all of a sudden...\n\nIt is especially intended for AmiExpress boards but will probably work\nwith many other systems. You determine.\n\n\nRequirements\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\nAquaSafety requires an Amiga with OS 2.04 or higher.\n\n\nInstallation\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\nPut AquaSafety anywhere you like, for example in C:.\n\nThe program requires is that the file ''S:AquaSafety.config'' exists and has\nthe following layout:\n\nLine 1: The number of minutes that the files may stay untouched.\n\nLine 2: The reboot warning time in seconds.\n\nLine 3: A command to be executed just before reboot. Leave this line empty\n        if you don''t want to run any command.\n\nLine 4: Keep log file (Y/N)? The name of the log file will be\n        S:AquaSafety.log.\n\nLine 5 and forwards: The files to be watched. Write one file on each line.\n\n\nHere is an example:\n\n--- Cut here -----------------------------------------\n80           ;The files are allowed to be untouched for 80 min.\n20           ;The warning requester will be shown for 20 s before reboot.\nC:Status >>S:AquaSafety.log\nY            ;Reboots will be logged.\nENV:STATS@1\nENV:STATS@2\nENV:STATS@3\nBBS:Node1/CallersLog\nBBS:Node2/CallersLog\nBBS:Node3/CallersLog\n--- Cut here -----------------------------------------\n\nThis example is meant for an AmiExpress BBS with nodes 1-3 open to call\non. Why should it watch those files then? Well, ENV:STATS@(x) will be\nchanged whenever the action code changes. The callerslogs are included\nbecause if a user is doing a huge transfer that will take more than 80\nminutes then the ENV:STATS@(x) file won''t change but the callerslog will\nbe written to for every file that he uploads/downloads. Presumably, no\nsingle file will take as much as 80 minutes to transfer...\n\nIn the example above, the command to execute before reboot, "C:Status\n>>S:AquaSafety.log", can be useful if you want to see what processes were\nloaded at the time of reset. Maybe one of them caused the BBS lockup...\n\nWhen you have made your configuration file, test it by executing\nAquaSafety. It tells you if the config file is correct. If it is, insert\nthis in your S:Startup-Sequence or S:User-Startup:\n\nrun >nil: C:AquaSafety\n\n\nQuitting\n~~~~~~~~\nYou can quit AquaSafety by sending it a CTRL-C signal. To do that, just\nopen a shell window and type "break `status com C:AquaSafety`".\n\n\nWarning!\n~~~~~~~~\nIf you are taking the board offline to make a backup of your harddiscs or\nto optimize them for example, remember to quit AquaSafety before! You\ndon''t want it to reset the computer then, do you?\n\n\nContact Me!\n~~~~~~~~~~~\nIf you have any cool ideas for improvement of this tool, questions, bug\nreports or whatever, leave me a message on one of the following boards:\n\nNIGHTFALL ................ Whoosh ............ +46-90-120369  <---  Safest\nHALL OF FAME ............. Dansken ........... +46-910-26665      place to\nHYSTERIA ................. JAC ............... +46-21-842939     reach me!\nMASTURBATION STATION ..... Black Beard ....... +1-305-552-1192\nZION''S HIDEOUT ........... Zion .............. +1-614-876-0807\nDARK TOWER ............... Shadower .......... +1-801-476-9068\nMORTUARY ................. Bloodwolf ......... +1-312-284-7577\nBOONDOCKS ................ Sal-One! .......... +31-548-040-653\n\n\nHistory\n~~~~~~~\n1.0  (09-17-94) First release version.\n\n\nGreetings\n~~~~~~~~~\n                Greetings must go to (in no special order):\n\n           - Vegas/OTL - Biscrok/OTL - Toxic/OTL - AtomiX!/OTL -\n       - Whoosh/OTT^KRL^OTL^CLS - Snake/OTL - Nashua/OTL - SMS/OTL -\n    - Genghis Khan/OTL - The Other OTL Members! - Dansken - CornFlake -\n  - Ace Caze/Obscene - Firehawk! - fanta/THR - Static/THR - FAX! - Juan -\n - Psychopath - Danzig - Foss - Karma - Seagull - Marwin - CaT - Sal-One -\n - Metalbasher - No Limit - BoneIdle - Wilsom/Obscene - Stab - Kid Curry -\n - Chig/TDS - HardHack - Rize - Frosty - JAC/TDS - C/\TE¥E - AXL - Norad -\n - Crocodile - Freddy Kreuger/GOD - Doc Whoo - Zion! - Nocturne - Brutus -\n  - FireFlash/OTT - MDR/OTT - Neutralizer/OTT - Bytehunter/OTT - Remix! -\n    - WarDancer - Json/Kingdom - Slobo & Whale - [-HSR & MM-] - HiFly -\n      - Uffe - Gi Joe - Princip - The Silencer - Ezco - Vampire/PDY -\n          - Nero - Deltaforce! - Afterlife - The Ones I Forgot! -\n\n\n[EOF]\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',18302,3,0,NULL,NULL,'otl_sa10','scan',1780048664);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('otl_sc20','OTL-SC20.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/OTL-SC20.LHA','SpeedCheck','XIM','SpeedCheck',NULL,'Aquarius','OTL','_____  __  / __   __  /_____  \__/ /   ____ :/  /  /  /  //  //  /__/  ¬  / / / /\_  \:: /  /  /  /  //  //  /  / _/  / / / /  /  /::',replace('_ _/\____/\_ ___/\__/\_ __/\__ _/\____/\__ _\n_____  __  / __   __  /_____  \__/ /   ____\n:/  /  /  /  //  //  /__/  ¬  / / / /\_  \::\n/  /  /  /  //  //  /  / _/  / / / /  /  /::\n\__  /\__  //  //___  /__\  /\__  /___  /:::\nbIS\/====\/==\/=====\/====\/====\/====\/===>\n   SpeedCheck v2.0 by Aquarius of Outlaws\n','\n',char(10)),'SpeedCheck.doc',replace('\n       _ _ ___/\______/\__ ____/\___/\__ _ _/\____ _/\_ __ __/\______\n      __ ________   __   /   _   ___   / ______   \___/__/     _____/\n         bIS/   /   /   /   //   //   /___/ __¬   /  /  /  /\__   \\n           /   /   /   /   //   //   /   /  \    /  /  /  /   /   /\n    __  _ _\____  /\____  //_  //_____  /___/\  /\_____  /\ _/   /___\n     _  ___ _   \/  _  _\/_  \/____ __\/ ___ _\/_______\/____   /_ _/\n                                                            \  /\n                                  present                    \/\n\n                      a door for AmiExpress 2.xx/3.xx:\n\n                >>> SpeedCheck v2.0 by Aquarius/Outlaws <<<\n\n\n                          Copyright ©1993 Aquarius\n\n                 Permission is granted to freely distribute\n               this product for non-commercial purposes only,\n                  as long as all files remain unmodified.\n\n\nArchive (OTL-SC20.LHA) contents\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nDoors/SpeedCheck/SpeedCheck       8344 bytes  The door.\nDoors/SpeedCheck/SpeedCheck.doc   5446 bytes  This document file!\nDoors/SpeedCheck/SpeedCheck.info   786 bytes  A sample configuration icon.\nCommands/BBSCmd/d.info            1248 bytes  Command icon for AmiExpress 3.xx.\n\n\nDescription\n~~~~~~~~~~~\nThis door protects from downloads below 9600 bps or whatever speed you decide.\nThis means you can have 2400 bps users (or V.32bis users calling an HST node),\nfor example, on your board but they will not be able to download, only read and\nwrite mail etc.\n\n\nFeatures\n~~~~~~~~\nThe door won''t disturb fast-modem users. It doesn''t write anything if a user\npasses speed check.\n\nYou may specify a time zone when the speed checks should be performed. This\nmeans you can allow slow-modem users to download, but only at times when the\nboard activity usually is low.\n\nIf there is a time zone and a user is prevented from downloading, the start and\nend times will be displayed, together with the current time.\n\nYou may specify an access level for overriding the speed checks. If you trust\nyour cosysops to be smart enough not to block the line with long downloads, you\ncould enter their access level in the config.\n\n\nInstallation\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\nCopy "SpeedCheck" and "SpeedCheck.info" to the "Doors:SpeedCheck/" directory.\n\nThe door is installed as the ''d'' command of course.\n\nAmiExpress 2.xx: Add the following line to your BBS.CMD file.\n\n*D        XM020Doors:SpeedCheck/SpeedCheck\n\nAmiExpress 3.xx: Copy the supplied icon "d.info" to "BBS:Commands/BBSCmd/" and\nedit its tooltypes if they don''t suit you.\n\nSet the access for the door low enough so that all users with download access\nwill be able to run it. It doesn''t really matter if you set too low, because if\na user passes the speed check, AmiExpress then checks that he has access to\ndownload.\n\n\nConfiguration\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThe configuration icon Doors:SpeedCheck/SpeedCheck.info can contain the\nfollowing tooltypes:\n\nLOWEST_SPEED=<baud rate>       - The lowest connect speed allowed for\n                                 downloading, for example 9600.\n\nACS.OVERRIDE=<access level>    - If a user has this access level or higher he\n                                 will always be able to download, even if his\n                                 bps is too low. This tooltype is optional.\n\nSTART=<time>                   - Start for the time zone when the speed should\n                                 be checked. Every user will be able to\n                                 download before and after this period. The\n                                 time must be in the format HH.MM.\n\nEND=<time>                     - End time for the period.\n\nThe bps will only be checked between START and END time. To never allow\ndownloads below the given speed, comment away the START or END tooltype.\nSTART=END means download is always allowed.\n\n\nContact me!\n~~~~~~~~~~~\nIf you have any cool ideas for improvement of this door, bug reports or\nwhatever, leave me a message on one of the following boards:\n\nNIGHTFALL ............... Prof Do Right ..... +46-90-120369\nOVERLOAD (Outlaws SHQ) .. Vegas ............. +46-8-54063666\nHYSTERIA ................ JAC ............... +46-21-842939\nINSIDE OUT .............. C/\TE¥E ........... +46-346-58697\nTRADERS NATION .......... RaJ-Ban ........... +46-176-55202\n\nYou can also mail me through AmiXnet (@SWE001) in the ChatterBox or AmiXnet\nInfo conference.\n\n\nGreetings\n~~~~~~~~~\nGreetings to: All members of Outlaws! And all my other friends.\n\nSpecial greetings to:\n\nJAC/ADDONIC            <<< Thanx for convincing me to write this door!\nPROF DO RIGHT/CLASSIC <<< Greetz, my favourite sysop!\nCHIG/INDEPENDENT     <<< No more quiz?\nFREDDY KREUGER/GOD  <<< Thanx for the feedback!\nC/\TE¥E/TAURUS     <<< A big greeting to you mate!\nVEGAS/OUTLAWS     <<< I rule don''t I no you think you rule I know hmm we rule..\nBISCROK/OUTLAWS  <<< I just love your asciis! I want more!\n\n\nDisclaimer\n~~~~~~~~~~\nNo responsibility is taken by the author for what effect this program might\nhave on your system.\n\n\nHistory\n~~~~~~~\n1.0  (931116) A version exclusivly for JAC/ADDONIC. It didn''t have any config\n     and it only stopped 2400 bps users from downloading.\n\n2.0  (931230) First public release. Config icon with tooltypes LOWEST_SPEED,\n     ACS.OVERRIDE, START and END, and all there''s to it... Nicer look.\n\n\n\nThat''s all for now. See ya in my next release!\n\n                                                   - Aquarius/OTL\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',10283,3,0,NULL,NULL,'otl_sc20','scan',1780048664);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('otl_sc21','OTL-SC21.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/OTL-SC21.LHA','SpeedCheck','XIM','SpeedCheck','2.1',NULL,'OTL','__ _/\______/\___/\_ _\  /_________________. __ ___  ___  ____  /_ \\//                 | /  /  / /  / /  /__  \/ An /X door which |',replace('[-sPEEDcHECK v2.1-]   ____  [-aQUARIUS/oTL-]\n__ _/\______/\___/\_ _\  /_________________.\n__ ___  ___  ____  /_ \\//                 |\n  /  /  / /  / /  /__  \/ An /X door which |\n /  /  / /  / /  /  /   protects from DL   |\n_\__  /_/  /_/___  /  below a certain bps  |\n____ /___ /__ ___ /  within a configurable |\nbIS\/   \/      \/ time zone. Now with     |\n  possibility to have a user-exclude list. |\n-- -  -    - -- -   ---- - ---- -----------''\n','\n',char(10)),'SpeedCheck.guide',replace('@database SpeedCheck\n\nCopyright © 1994 Aquarius/Outlaws\n\n@Remark $VER: SpeedCheck v2.1 AmigaGuide doc\n\n@node MAIN "SpeedCheck v2.1 Documentation"\n\n       _ _ ___/\______/\__ ____/\___/\__ _ _/\____ _/\_ __ __/\______\n      __ ________   __   /   _   ___   / ______   \___/__/     _____/\n         bIS/   /   /   /   //   //   /___/ __¬   /  /  /  /\__   \\n           /   /   /   /   //   //   /   /  \    /  /  /  /   /   /\n    __  _ _\____  /\____  //_  //_____  /___/\  /\_____  /\ _/   /___\n     _  ___ _   \/  _  _\/_  \/____ __\/ ___ _\/_______\/____   /_ _/\n                                                            \  /\n                                  present                    \/\n                      a door for AmiExpress 2.xx/3.xx:\n\n                >>> SpeedCheck v2.1 by Aquarius/Outlaws <<<\n\n                      [- Contents of documentation -]\n\n                @{"   Copyright Note   " Link Copyright   }   @{"   Configuration    " Link Configuration}\n                @{"  Archive Contents  " Link Archive     }   @{"  How to Reach Me   " Link ContactMe}\n                @{"    Introduction    " Link Introduction}   @{"      History       " Link History}\n                @{"      Features      " Link Features    }   @{"     Greetings      " Link Greetings}\n                @{"    Installation    " Link Installation}\n@endnode\n\n@node Copyright "SpeedCheck v2.1 Documentation"\n\n                          Copyright ©1994 Aquarius\n\n                 Permission is granted to freely distribute\n               this product for non-commercial purposes only,\n                  as long as all files remain unmodified.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Archive "SpeedCheck v2.1 Documentation"\n\nArchive (OTL-SC21.LHA) Contents\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nDoors/SpeedCheck/\n   SpeedCheck               8544 bytes  The door.\n   SpeedCheck.info           823 bytes  A sample configuration icon.\n   SpeedCheck.doc           6202 bytes  Ascii version of the doc.\n   SpeedCheck.guide        12011 bytes  This document file!\n\nCommands/BBSCmd/\n   d.info                   1248 bytes  Command icon for AmiExpress 3.xx.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Introduction "SpeedCheck v2.1 Documentation"\n\nIntroduction\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThis door protects from downloads below 9600 bps or whatever speed you\ndecide. This means for example that you can have 2400 bps users (or\nV.32bis users calling an HST node) on your board but they will not be able\nto download, only read and write mail etc.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Features "SpeedCheck v2.1 Documentation"\n\nFeatures\n~~~~~~~~\nThe door won''t disturb fast-modem users. It doesn''t write anything if a\nuser passes speed check.\n\nYou may specify a time zone when the speed checks should be performed.\nThis means you can allow slow-modem users to download, but only at times\nwhen the board activity usually is low.\n\nIf there is a time zone and a user is prevented from downloading, the\nstart and end times will be displayed, together with the current time.\n\nYou may specify an access level for overriding the speed checks. If you\ntrust your cosysops to be smart enough not to block the line with long\ndownloads, you could enter their access level in the config.\n\nAlso, you can configure a list of the users users who are always allowed\nto download.\n@endnode\n\n@node Installation "SpeedCheck v2.1 Documentation"\n\nInstallation\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\nMake the directory ''Doors:SpeedCheck'', and copy ''SpeedCheck'' and\n''SpeedCheck.info'' there.\n\nThe door is installed as the ''d'' command of course.\n\n\n/X 2.xx / SigmaExpress:\n\nAdd the following line to your BBS.CMD file:\n\n-----Cut-here---------------------------------\n*D        XM020Doors:SpeedCheck/SpeedCheck\n-------Cut-here-------------------------------\n\n\n/X 3.xx:\n\nCopy the supplied icon "d.info" to "BBS:Commands/BBSCmd/" and edit its\ntooltypes if they don''t suit you.\n\nSet the access for the door low enough so that all users with download\naccess will be able to run it. It doesn''t really matter if you set too\nlow, because if a user passes the speed check, AmiExpress then checks that\nhe has access to download.\n@endnode\n\n@node Configuration "SpeedCheck v2.1 Documentation"\n\nConfiguration\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThe configuration icon Doors:SpeedCheck/SpeedCheck.info can contain the\nfollowing tooltypes:\n\nLOWEST_SPEED=<baud rate>      - The lowest connect speed allowed for\n                                downloading, for example 9600.\n\nSTART=<time>                  - Start for the time zone when the speed\n                                should be checked. Every user will be able\n                                to download before and after this period.\n                                The time must be in the format HH:MM.\n\nEND=<time>                    - End time for the period.\n\nThe bps will only be checked between START and END time. To never allow\ndownloads below the given speed, comment away the START or END tooltype.\nSTART=END means download is always allowed.\n\nACS.OVERRIDE=<access level>   - If a user has this access level or higher\n                                he will always be able to download, even\n                                if his bps is too low. This tooltype is\n                                optional.\n\nNAME.x=<user name>            - The user written here will override the\n                                speed check. First, NAME.1 is looked for,\n                                then NAME.2, and so on, until it can''t be\n                                found.\n@endnode\n\n@node ContactMe "SpeedCheck v2.1 Documentation"\n\nContact Me!\n~~~~~~~~~~~\nIf you have any cool ideas for improvement of this door, bug reports,\nquestions, or whatever, leave me a message on one of the following boards:\n\n@{"NIGHTFALL" Link Nightfall} ................ Prof Do Right ..... +46-90-120369\n@{"OVERLOAD" Link OverLoad} (OTL SHQ) ....... Vegas ............. +46-8-54063666\nHYSTERIA ................. JAC ............... +46-21-842939\nRAISING HELL ............. Psychopath ........ +46-23-26893\nINSIDE OUT ............... C/\TE¥E ........... +46-346-58697\n@{"SNAKE''S DEN" Link SnakesDen} (OTL WHQ) .... Snake ............. +1-513-683-2330\nTHE HOLE ................. Oldman ............ +1-419-899-2754\n\n@endnode\n\n@node History "SpeedCheck v2.1 Documentation"\n\nHistory\n~~~~~~~\n1.0  (1993-11-16) A version exclusivly for JAC/ADDONIC. It didn''t have any\n     config and it only stopped 2400 bps users from downloading.\n\n2.0  (1993-12-30) First public release. Config icon with tooltypes\n     LOWEST_SPEED, START, END and ACS.OVERRIDE, and all there''s to it...\n     Nicer look.\n\n2.1  (1994-04-24) Second release version.\n     The time format was changed from HH.MM to HH:MM.\n     Certain users can now be excluded from the speed check. They are\n     listed in the config icon with the tooltype NAME.x where x >= 1.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Greetings "SpeedCheck v2.1 Documentation"\n\nGreetings\n~~~~~~~~~\n               Greetings must go to (in no special order):\n\n      - All Members of Outlaws!! - Prof Do Right/Classic - JAC/TDS -\n    - C/\TE¥E/Insane - Ace Caze/Obscene - Wilsom/Obscene - Kid Curry -\n   - Psychopath - Vinzi - Karma - Zin - Shapechanger - Rize - Seagull -\n    - Remix/Classic - RaJ-Ban - fanta/Therion - Static/Therion - CaT -\n     - Dansken - AXL/Attention - Rad!/LSD - Vileius! - Marwin/Duplo -\n      - Freddy Kreuger/GOD - Chig/TDS - The Silencer - Vampire/PDY -\n       - Crocodile/Obscene - Sal-One - Nojje - Zune/HCD - MadCap -\n           - Metalbasher - WarDancer/H&V - The Ones I Forgot! -\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Nightfall "SpeedCheck v2.1 Documentation"\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|         iNTO tOTAL dARKNESS, tHE uNKNOWN; cOME wALK wiTH mE...          |\n| a3ooo    ___/\       ___/\ ____/\__________/\ ___/   __/\ _________9ooMB|\n+----------\__  \______\__  \____  __________  \  /   \__  \   _____/-----+\n|         tS/    __    \/      /  /_____   /     /     /        /         |\n·          /      /    /      /     /     /           /        /          ·\n rEG. /X! /      /    /      /     /     /     /     /        /ClAsSiC SHQ\n         /______/    /______/___________/_____/     /________/\n  lOTs oF      /____/                        /     /      2ooo AD (PC) WHQ\n /X uTiLS!          ·3 uSR nODES·aMiGa&pC!· /     /\n    ___/\ _________/\ _________/\ ___   ___/     / sTAFF : pROF dO riGHT,\n    \__  \ ________  \_________  \  /   \__     / aQUARiUS, riZE, rEMiX,\n·    /    _____/ /     __    /     /_____/     /_____ mASTERmAN, nEMESiS  ·\n:   /      /    /      /    /     /     /     /     /                     :\n|  /      /    /      /    /     /     /     /     /   eNJOY tHE sPEED!   |\n+-/______/----/______/    /___________/___________/-----------------------+\n|                   /____/                                                |\n| node#1: +46-90-120369   node#2: +46-90-178169   node#3: +46-90-142969   |\n|      (14.4k DS)              (16.8k DS)              (14.4k HST)        |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n@endnode\n\n@node OverLoad "SpeedCheck v2.1 Documentation"\n                             .\n                             :\n                             |__       ___                   __\n        _____________________|  \_____/   \_________________/  \\n        \________     __     |     __      ________________     \_\n   .______/     U     \/     |     \/      __)____/      |/   ___/_____.\n   |:::::/ _ _         \     :      \_     |/     \      |       \:::::|\n   |:::  \___/_________/____   ______/_______      \_____A  _ _   \__::|\n   |:       / |            \___/       __   \______/      \/ _______/ :|\n   |  _____/  |   ____________________/  \________________/    \____  .|\n   |. \__     |___\__________      ________      _________       __/  :|\n   |:.  /     |    ___/     U      \/     |\     \/      |\      \   .:|\n   |::s/      :     \               \     _/      \_      /       \s.::|\n   |::c\_________    \______________/     A________/_________     /c:::|\n   °-----------\_____/-------\___________/------------------\____/-----°\n   ::::::                                                         ::::::\n   |::               »»»  O U T L A W S   S H Q  «««                 ::|\n   |:                                                                 :|\n   |SYSOPS: VEGAS/OTL, BiSCROK/OTL, PURE PAiN/DCS, CRUGER/SR, NATAS/HZ |\n   |:                 SUPPORTING: AMiGA & CONSOLE!                    :|\n   |::     CALL AND MAKE SOME TRANSFERS NOW AT: +46-8-540-63666      ::|\n   |::: CALL TO GET THE LATEST OUTLAWS RELEASES FOR FREEDOWNLOAD!   :::|\n   |:::::::.             .:::NO NUP NEEDED!:::.                .:::::::|\n   `-------------------------------------------------------------------''\n@endnode\n\n@node SnakesDen "SpeedCheck v2.1 Documentation"\n\n<----------------------------OUTLAWS--W-H-Q----------------------------->\n   ___________  ______    _______ _____  ______ _________   ___________\n   \     ____/__\  __ \  _\  ___ \     |/     /_\  ___   \_''\     ____/_\n   _\  ___     \_\/ /  \/  \/  /  \    /    _/   \/  /____/ _\  ___     \_\n  /  \/  /      /  /    \_   _     \_ _      \_    _____)__/  \/  /      /\n /             /  /      /   /      /  \      /    \      /             /\n/_____________/__/______/___/______/____\    /___________/_____________/\n<----------------------------------------\__/SyK!------------------------>\n       Sysop`s: Snake & Nazgul          _________  _________   ______\n   cosys`s: Rofoe/LGC & SIGMA 909/OTL  _\  ___   \_\  ___   \__\  __ \\n   _   __  __ ___ ____ _____ ________ /  \/  /    \_\/  /____/  \/ /  \\n  //  / / / //  //   //    //       //      /      /  _____)__    /    \_\n //  /_/ /_//__//___//____//_______//      /      /   \      /   /      /\n                                   /_____________/__________/___/______/\n\n<---------------wOrKiN` oN: A 4ooo/4o-1omb-54ombHD-2GigDat--------------->\n\n<--------DiAL:   + 1 - 5 1 3 - 6 8 3 - 2 3 3 0  -  3 NoDeZ RiNGdOwN!----->\n\n<----------------MoDeM`s: 21.6k & 16.8k DST`s + 14.4k HST---------------->\n@endnode\n\n[EOF]','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',18732,4,0,NULL,NULL,'otl_sc20','scan',1780048664);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('otl_se10','OTL-SE10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/OTL-SE10.LHA','AquaSettings','XIM','[-aQUAsETTINGS -]       /\__[-aQUARIUS-]','1.0',NULL,'OTL','._________ ___ __ _/\______/  _/_ _/\__ ___. |               //____   __  ___/_/   /___ | | A door to be   /   /   /   /   /   /   / |',replace('[-aQUAsETTINGS v1.0-]       /\__[-aQUARIUS-]\n._________ ___ __ _/\______/  _/_ _/\__ ___.\n|               //____   __  ___/_/   /___ |\n| A door to be   /   /   /   /   /   /   / |\n| installed on  _\___   /\___   /____   /__|\n| the W command. _ ___ /__ ___ /_ ____ /__/|\n| It lets you put    \/      \/ -bIS!\/    |\n| all configuration commands under one     |\n| roof, for example internal W, CF, SENT,  |\n| filescan configuration and "you name it"!|\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'AquaSettings.guide',replace('@database AquaSettings\n@author Aquarius/Outlaws\n@$VER: AquaSettings.guide 1.0 (21.1.95)\n\n@node MAIN "AquaSettings v1.0 Documentation"\n\n       _ _ ___/\______/\__ ____/\___/\__ _ _/\____ _/\_ __ __/\______\n      __ ________   __   /   _   ___   / ______   \___/__/     _____/\n         bIS/   /   /   /   //   //   /___/ __¬   /  /  /  /\__   \\n           /   /   /   /   //   //   /   /  \    /  /  /  /   /   /\n    __  _ _\____  /\____  //_  //_____  /___/\  /\_____  /\ _/   /___\n     _  ___ _   \/  _  _\/_  \/____ __\/ ___ _\/_______\/____   /_ _/\n                                                            \  /\n                                  present:                   \/\n\n                >>> AquaSettings v1.0 by Aquarius/Outlaws <<<\n\n                      [- Contents of Documentation -]\n\n                @{"   Copyright Note   " Link Copyright   }   @{"   Configuration    " Link Configuration}\n                @{"  Archive Contents  " Link Archive     }   @{"      History       " Link History}\n                @{"    Introduction    " Link Introduction}   @{"  How to Reach Me   " Link ContactMe}\n                @{"    Requirements    " Link Requirements}   @{"    Other Tools     " Link AquaTools}\n                @{"    Installation    " Link Installation}   @{"     Greetings      " Link Greetings}\n@endnode\n\n@node Copyright "AquaSettings v1.0 Documentation"\n\n                          Copyright ©1995 Aquarius\n\n                 Permission is granted to freely distribute\n               this product for non-commercial purposes only,\n                  as long as all files remain unmodified.\n@endnode\n\n@node Archive "AquaSettings v1.0 Documentation"\n\nArchive (OTL-SE10.LHA) Contents\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nDoors/AquaSettings/\n   AquaSettings              3068 bytes   The door itself.\n   AquaSettings.doc          9323 bytes   Ascii version of the doc.\n   AquaSettings.guide       12318 bytes   This AmigaGuide doc!\n   AquaSettings.info          680 bytes   Sample configuration icon.\n\nCommands/BBSCmd/\n   W.info                    1281 bytes   Command icon for /X 3.0+.\n   W_INTERNAL.info            969 bytes   Command icon for /X 3.0+.\n@endnode\n\n@node Introduction "AquaSettings v1.0 Documentation"\n\nIntroduction\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\nAquaSettings is meant to be used on the W command. You probably have lots\nof commands that the users can configure different things with, for\nexample AutoSent, the filescanner, CF (conference flags) and of course the\ninternal W command. AquaSettings will show a menu of all these commands,\nsomething like this:\n\n[ 1] Basic settings\n[ 2] Conference flags\n[ 3] AutoSent\n[ 4] Filescan options\netc.\n\nWhen you select one of these, that command is executed and then the menu\nis shown again, until you quit with a single <Enter>. Unfortunately, if\nyou''re running SigmaExpress or AmiExpress 2.xx and you choose "[ 1] Basic\nsettings" (which is the internal W command), you won''t be taken back to\nthe menu. That "bug" is because of a limitation in S!X and /X 2.xx that\ndoesn''t let you run an internal command (with the same name as a door)\nwithout quitting the door. In /X 3.0+ there is a way around this (see\n@{"installation" Link Installation} section).\n\nThe door can take a command number as argument. For example if you start\nthe door by typing ''W 3'', AutoSent is run (presuming we have the above\nmenu) just as if you had typed ''SENT'', and it quits immediately\nafterwards.\n\nWell, try it and I''m sure you will love this little door!\n@endnode\n\n@node Requirements "AquaSettings v1.0 Documentation"\n\nRequirements\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\n- An Amiga with OS 2.0 or higher.\n\n- AmiExpress, SigmaExpress or any compatible program.\n@endnode\n\n@node Installation "AquaSettings v1.0 Documentation"\n\nInstallation\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\nCopy the ''AquaSettings'' directory (the inner one) from the archive to your\n''Doors:'' directory. Then put the provided command icon ''W.info'' in your\n''BBSCmd'' drawer.\n\nThe access value in W.info can be set to 1 (the lowest possible) because\nthe door checks if the user has access to use the internal W command (in\n/X 3.0+ determined by the tooltype ''ACS.EDIT_USER_INFO'' in the user''s\naccess icon). If he doesn''t have access, the door just exits with the\nmessage "Command requires higher access." If you want some users to be\nable to use the internal W command but not the other commands that\nAquaSettings offer, you can use the tooltype @{"ACCESS" Link Configuration}) to set the access\nlevel below which the door will only run the internal W command.\n\nThe door is perfectly safe to be made resident. The changes you have to\nmake to the command icon in that case are: Change the value of "LOCATION"\nto "AquaSettings" and add the tooltype "RESIDENT".\n\nNow, for /X 3.0+, you must put the icon ''W_INTERNAL.info'' in your ''BBSCmd''\ndrawer! The only tooltype it contains is ''INTERNAL=W''. This icon makes it\npossible to run the internal W command without quitting the door. Note! It\nwill NOT work if you put ''W_INTERNAL.info'' in ''SYSCmd''!\n\nIf you''re running SigmaExpress or /X 2.xx you must change the value of the\n''DESC.1'' tooltype in ''AquaSettings.info'' from ''W_INTERNAL'' to ''W''. The\nside effect is that when you select "[ 1] Basic settings", the door exits\nto be able to start the internal W command, so you won''t be taken back to\nthe menu afterwards. (There is no better solution!)\n\nNow you must @{"configure" Link Configuration} the door...\n@endnode\n\n@node Configuration "AquaSettings v1.0 Documentation"\n\nTooltypes in ''Doors:AquaSettings/AquaSettings.info'':\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n-  ---  ------ ---------- -------------------------------- ------ ---  --\nTemplate: ACCESS=<access level>                                Optional.\nExample : ACCESS=20\n\nIf the user has a lower access level than this, only the internal W\ncommand is run. The user won''t even notice that a door is installed on W.\n\n-  ---  ------ ---------- -------------------------------- ------ ---  --\nTemplate: CMD.<num>=<command>\nExample : CMD.3=CS W\n\nThese tooltypes specify all the commands that the users should be able to\nstart from the AquaSettings menu.\n\n-  ---  ------ ---------- -------------------------------- ------ ---  --\nTemplate: DESC.<num>=<string>\nExample : DESC.3=Filescan options\n\nThese tooltypes are descriptions for every command. DESC.1 is the\ndescription for CMD.1, DESC.2 is for CMD.2, and so on.\n\n-  ---  ------ ---------- -------------------------------- ------ ---  --\n@endnode\n\n@node History "AquaSettings v1.0 Documentation"\n\nHistory\n~~~~~~~\n1.0 (01-21-95)  First release version!\n@endnode\n\n@node ContactMe "AquaSettings v1.0 Documentation"\n\nContact Me!\n~~~~~~~~~~~\nIf you have any cool ideas for improvement of this tool, questions, bug\nreports or whatever, contact me on one of the following boards:\n\n@{"NIGHTFALL" Link NIGHTFALL} ................ Whoosh ............ +46-90-120369  <---  Safest\nHALL OF FAME ............. Dansken ........... +46-910-26665      place to\nACES HIGH ................ Norad ............. +46-410-44886     reach me!\nINTERCHANGE .............. Princip ........... +46-8-6082339\nZION''S HIDEOUT ........... Zion .............. +1-PRIVATE!!\nDEATH ROW ................ Shadower .......... +1-PRIVATE!!\nMORTUARY ................. Bloodwolf ......... +1-PRIVATE!!\nBOONDOCKS ................ Sal-One ........... +31-PRIVATE!!\n@endnode\n\n@node AquaTools "AquaSettings v1.0 Documentation"\n\nThe AquaTools Collection\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nHere is the complete list of my released tools (the latest versions):\n\nTool Name              File Name     Short Description\n---------------------- ------------- ------------------------------------------\nDisable v1.1           AQDSBL11.LHA  Payuser handling system.\nDisplayer v1.0         AQDSPL10.LHA  Text displayer. Perfect for door menu e.g.\nNetEdit v1.0           AQNETE10.LHA  Editor for certain netmail systems.\nConfReplace v1.0       OTL-CR10.LHA  Find and replace" area names in User.Data.\nListSpeeder v2.1       OTL-LS21.LHA  Filelist downloader.\nAnnounce v2.0          OTL-AN20.LHA  Notifies online users of logons/logoffs.\nAquaWho v2.0           OTL-AW20.LHA  Totally configurable WHO door!\nSpeedCheck v2.1        OTL-SC21.LHA  Disables download at too low connect rates.\nStripper v1.2          OTL-ST12.LHA  Strips log files to desired file sizes.\nAquaQuiet v1.0         OTL-AQ10.LHA  ''Q'' replacement. Toggles quiet node.\nAquaScan v1.0          OTL-AS10.LHA  File scanner! (F, N, CS, FR.)\nAquaCreateAcc v1.0     OTL-CA10.LHA  Door to create new accounts with.\nAquaMoveFiles v1.0     OTL-MF10.LHA  File and description mover, by date.\nAquaSafety v1.0        OTL-SA10.LHA  Anti-BBS-downtime utility.\nAquaAdder v1.0         OTL-AA10.LHA  Text adder.\nAquaBulls v2.0         OTL-AB20.LHA  Bulletin viewer.\nAquaQuick v1.0         OTL-QK10.LHA  Quick-logon door.\nRestoreQuietness v1.0  OTL-RQ10.LHA  Restores the nodes'' "quietness" at logoff.\nAquaSettings v1.0      OTL-SE10.LHA  ''W'' replacement. Menu of config commands.\n\n(...and more are coming!)\n\nYou can find them all on @{"Nightfall" Link NIGHTFALL} +46-90-120369 (free download)!\n@endnode\n\n@node Greetings "AquaSettings v1.0 Documentation"\n\nGreetings\n~~~~~~~~~\n                Greetings must go to (in no special order):\n\n           - Vegas/OTL - Biscrok/OTL - Toxic/OTL - Nashua/OTL -\n     - Snake/OTL - Whoosh/OTT^DVS^CLS^OTL^R2 - AtomiX!/OTL - SMS/OTL -\n   - Genghis Khan/OTL - The Other OTL Members - Ace Caze - Dansken/ACS -\n  - Princip! - Sandman - Rize & Frosty - Static & fanta - Marky & Power -\n  - Psychopath - Norad - Firehawk - Marwin - Danzig! - Lockjammer - MDR -\n   - HardHack! - Chig! - Wild Thing - Ezco - Enzo - FAX! - AXL - HiFly -\n    - Kid Curry - Juan - Wilsom - Gi Joe - Sal-One - Zion! - Shadower -\n     - Doc Whoo - JAz - Bowen/OTT - Json - WarDancer - MFM - Vileius -\n        - Bilbo Baggins - Biztro - Metalbasher - Kain - CornFlake -\n              - Karma - Dalamar - Wize - CountZero - Psyche -\n                         - The Friends I Forgot! -\n\n\n                         A few personal messages:\n\nWhoosh         - Whooopssss... Nice chatting with you every day. :)\n\nToxic/OTL      - Hard getting cards isn''t it? If you can, call Nightfall\n                 (new pwfail door hehe)!\n\nVegas/OTL      - Yeah let''s get the Swedish section rocking! I mean, MORE!\n                 Btw, Norrland is such a nice place, don''t you think? :)\n\nBiscrok/OTL    - The master of strange (tüffa) modules. ;)\n\nDansken        - Great friend and beta tester! Learn C soon!! hehe\n\nMarky & Power  - Hope you can find a new way to call...\n\nEzco           - Great Who designs!!\n\nAce Caze       - Funny dude and great beta tester! Hmmm why not\n                 topaz 8 on your WB?? ;)\n\nSnowman/Ex.OTL - Where did you disappear??? Get in touch, mate..\n@endnode\n\n@node NIGHTFALL "AquaSettings v1.0 Documentation"\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|         iNTO tOTAL dARKNESS, tHE uNKNOWN; cOME wALK wiTH mE...          |\n| a3ooo    ___/\       ___/\ ____/\__________/\ ___/   __/\ _________9ooMB|\n+----------\__  \______\__  \____  __________  \  /   \__  \   _____/-----+\n|         tS/    __    \/      /  /_____   /     /     /        /         |\n· /X 4.xx  /      /    /      /     /     /           /        /    r2 sHQ·\n          /      /    /      /     /     /     /     /        /    dVS sHQ\n   eNJOY /______/    /______/___________/_____/     /________/    oTT  sHQ\n   tHE         /____/                        /     /         oTL diST siTE\n sPEED!             ·3 uSR nODES riNGDOWN!· /     /\n    ___/\ _________/\ _________/\ ___   ___/     / sTAFF: wHOOSH, aQUARiUS,\n    \__  \ ________  \_________  \  /   \__     / riZE, mASTERmAN, nEMESiS\n·    /    _____/ /     __    /     /_____/     /_____                     ·\n:   /      /    /      /    /     /     /     /     /    mORE tHAN 1200   :\n|  /      /    /      /    /     /     /     /     / aMiX tOOLS oNLiNE!!  |\n+-/______/----/______/    /___________/___________/-----------------------+\n|                   /____/                                                |\n| nODE#1: +46-90-120369   nODE#2: +46-riNGDOWN!!  nODE#3: +46-riNGDOWN!!  |\n|      (14.4k DS)              (16.8k DS)              (28.8k DS)         |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n@endnode\n\n[EOF]\n','\n',char(10)),'{"ACCESS":"<access"}',NULL,13507,2,0,NULL,NULL,'otl_se10_aquasettings','scan',1780048664);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('otl_st12','OTL-ST12.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/OTL-ST12.LHA','Strip','XIM','Strip','1.2',NULL,'OTL','__ _/\______/\___/\_ _\  /_________________. __ ___  ___  ____  /_ \\//                 | /  /  / /  / /  /__  \/   A useful tool  |',replace('[-sTRIPPER v1.2-]     ____  [-aQUARIUS/oTL-]\n__ _/\______/\___/\_ _\  /_________________.\n__ ___  ___  ____  /_ \\//                 |\n  /  /  / /  / /  /__  \/   A useful tool  |\n /  /  / /  / /  /  /    for keeping log   |\n_\__  /_/  /_/___  /  files at a constant  |\n____ /___ /__ ___ /   size, for example    |\nbIS\/   \/      \/ CallersLog and DoorLog. |\n-- -  -    - -- -   ---- - ---- -----------''\n','\n',char(10)),'Stripper.guide',replace('@database Stripper\n\nCopyright © 1994 Aquarius/Outlaws\n\n@Remark $VER: Stripper v1.2 AmigaGuide doc\n\n@node MAIN "Stripper v1.2 Documentation"\n\n       _ _ ___/\______/\__ ____/\___/\__ _ _/\____ _/\_ __ __/\______\n      __ ________   __   /   _   ___   / ______   \___/__/     _____/\n         bIS/   /   /   /   //   //   /___/ __¬   /  /  /  /\__   \\n           /   /   /   /   //   //   /   /  \    /  /  /  /   /   /\n    __  _ _\____  /\____  //_  //_____  /___/\  /\_____  /\ _/   /___\n     _  ___ _   \/  _  _\/_  \/____ __\/ ___ _\/_______\/____   /_ _/\n                          //                                \  /\n                          \\      present                    \/\n                          //\n                 >>> Stripper v1.2 by Aquarius/Outlaws <<<\n                        //\n                        \\\n                        //\n                      [- Contents of documentation -]\n\n                 @{"  Copyright Note  " Link Copyright   }    @{"      Usage       " Link Usage}\n                 @{" Archive Contents " Link Archive     }    @{" How to Reach Me  " Link ContactMe}\n                 @{"   Introduction   " Link Introduction}    @{"     History      " Link History}\n                 @{" Why It Is Useful " Link WhyUseful   }    @{"    Greetings     " Link Greetings}\n                 @{"   Requirements   " Link Requirements}\n@endnode\n\n@node Copyright "Stripper v1.2 Documentation"\n\n                          Copyright ©1994 Aquarius\n\n                 Permission is granted to freely distribute\n               this product for non-commercial purposes only,\n                  as long as all files remain unmodified.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Archive "Stripper v1.2 Documentation"\n\nArchive (OTL-ST12.LHA) Contents\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nStrip                  10408 bytes      The CLI command.\nStripper.doc            5381 bytes      Ascii version of the doc.\nStripper.guide         11078 bytes      This document file!\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Introduction "Stripper v1.2 Documentation"\n\nIntroduction\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\nStripper simply cuts off the beginning of a file, strips it. The cut off\npart can be moved to the end of another file, a "backup" file. You must\nspecify how many bytes you want the file you''re stripping to become.\nStripper won''t cut the file in the middle of a line though. It finds the\nnearest start of a line towards the beginning of the file and cuts there\ninstead. Hence, the stripped file will be bigger than, or equal to, the\nsize you specified.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node WhyUseful "Stripper v1.2 Documentation"\n\nWhy It Could Be Useful\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nIf you''re running an AmiExpress BBS, some files tend to grow quite large,\nfor example the CallersLog, UDLog and DoorLog. To keep them constantly at\na reasonable size, use Stripper! There are many doors that search through\nthese files, so they shouldn''t be too large, or else it could take a while\nfor the doors to handle them. Note that Stripper doesn''t check if it cuts\nthe files in the middle of a "user" (a call), it just makes sure it\ndoesn''t cut in the middle of a line. You could for example call it in your\nlogoff script, or run it once a day (with some Cron program) or once a\nweek. That''s up to you.\n\nThe terminal program TERM maintains (as default) a file called\nterm-action.log where all your actions are recorded, such as connects,\ndownloads, uploads and disconnects. That file can eventually grow very\nlarge, and that''s where Stripper comes into the picture...\n\nIt''s up to you to think of all the other possibilities.\n@endnode\n\n@node Requirements "Stripper v1.2 Documentation"\n\nRequirements\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\nStripper requires an Amiga with AmigaDOS 2.0 or higher to run.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Usage "Stripper v1.2 Documentation"\n\nHow to Use It\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThe command line syntax is as follows:\n\nstrip <stripfile> <size> [<backupfile>]\n\n<stripfile> is the name of the file that will get its beginning cut off.\n<size> is the desired size in bytes for the stripfile, which will be cut\nat the nearest beginning of a line, towards the beginning of the file. If\nyou specify a backup file, the cut off part will be appended to it.\n\nSome examples:\n\nstrip bbs:node0/CallersLog 100000\n\nThis call strips the file bbs:node0/CallersLog so that is becomes 100000\nbytes big, or perhaps a few bytes bigger so that it won''t be cut in the\nmiddle of a line.\n\nstrip bbs:node0/CallersLog 100000 bbs:node0/CLogBackup\n\nThis accomplishes the same as the previous call, but the cut-off part will\nbe appended to the file bbs:node0/CLogBackup.\n@endnode\n\n@node ContactMe "Stripper v1.2 Documentation"\n\nContact Me!\n~~~~~~~~~~~\nIf you have any cool ideas for improvement of this tool, bug reports,\nquestions, or whatever, leave me a message on one of the following boards:\n\n@{"NIGHTFALL" Link Nightfall} ................ Prof Do Right ..... +46-90-120369\n@{"OVERLOAD" Link OverLoad} (OTL SHQ) ....... Vegas ............. +46-8-54063666\nHYSTERIA ................. JAC ............... +46-21-842939\nRAISING HELL ............. Psychopath ........ +46-23-26893\nINSIDE OUT ............... C/\TE¥E ........... +46-346-58697\n@{"SNAKE''S DEN" Link SnakesDen} (OTL WHQ) .... Snake ............. +1-513-683-2330\nTHE HOLE ................. Oldman ............ +1-419-899-2754\n\n@endnode\n\n@node History\n\nHistory\n~~~~~~~\n1.0  (1993-06-29) First working version, made for Prof Do Right only.\n\n1.1  (1993-08-04) First public release.\n\n     Added CTRL-C disabling, a version string, and a check for OS V36.\n\n1.2  (1994-04-24) Second public release.\n\n     It doesn''t use a tempfile anymore. It reads to memory instead, which\n     makes it faster.\n\n     Usage syntax changed! The keyword BACKUP on command line should no\n     more be given. The third argument (optional) is taken as backup file.\n\n     The backup file isn''t opened unless something will be written to it.\n@endnode\n\n@node Greetings "Stripper v1.2 Documentation"\n\nGreetings\n~~~~~~~~~\n               Greetings must go to (in no special order):\n\n      - All Members of Outlaws!! - Prof Do Right/Classic - JAC/TDS -\n    - C/\TE¥E/Insane - Ace Caze/Obscene - Wilsom/Obscene - Kid Curry -\n   - Psychopath - Vinzi - Karma - Zin - Shapechanger - Rize - Seagull -\n    - Remix/Classic - RaJ-Ban - fanta/Therion - Static/Therion - CaT -\n     - Dansken - AXL/Attention - Rad!/LSD - Vileius! - Marwin/Duplo -\n      - Freddy Kreuger/GOD - Chig/TDS - The Silencer - Vampire/PDY -\n       - Crocodile/Obscene - Sal-One - Nojje - Zune/HCD - MadCap -\n           - Metalbasher - WarDancer/H&V - The Ones I Forgot! -\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Nightfall "Stripper v1.2 Documentation"\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n|         iNTO tOTAL dARKNESS, tHE uNKNOWN; cOME wALK wiTH mE...          |\n| a3ooo    ___/\       ___/\ ____/\__________/\ ___/   __/\ _________9ooMB|\n+----------\__  \______\__  \____  __________  \  /   \__  \   _____/-----+\n|         tS/    __    \/      /  /_____   /     /     /        /         |\n·          /      /    /      /     /     /           /        /          ·\n rEG. /X! /      /    /      /     /     /     /     /        /ClAsSiC SHQ\n         /______/    /______/___________/_____/     /________/\n  lOTs oF      /____/                        /     /      2ooo AD (PC) WHQ\n /X uTiLS!          ·3 uSR nODES·aMiGa&pC!· /     /\n    ___/\ _________/\ _________/\ ___   ___/     / sTAFF : pROF dO riGHT,\n    \__  \ ________  \_________  \  /   \__     / aQUARiUS, riZE, rEMiX,\n·    /    _____/ /     __    /     /_____/     /_____ mASTERmAN, nEMESiS  ·\n:   /      /    /      /    /     /     /     /     /                     :\n|  /      /    /      /    /     /     /     /     /   eNJOY tHE sPEED!   |\n+-/______/----/______/    /___________/___________/-----------------------+\n|                   /____/                                                |\n| node#1: +46-90-120369   node#2: +46-90-178169   node#3: +46-90-142969   |\n|      (14.4k DS)              (16.8k DS)              (14.4k HST)        |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n@endnode\n\n@node OverLoad "Stripper v1.2 Documentation"\n                             .\n                             :\n                             |__       ___                   __\n        _____________________|  \_____/   \_________________/  \\n        \________     __     |     __      ________________     \_\n   .______/     U     \/     |     \/      __)____/      |/   ___/_____.\n   |:::::/ _ _         \     :      \_     |/     \      |       \:::::|\n   |:::  \___/_________/____   ______/_______      \_____A  _ _   \__::|\n   |:       / |            \___/       __   \______/      \/ _______/ :|\n   |  _____/  |   ____________________/  \________________/    \____  .|\n   |. \__     |___\__________      ________      _________       __/  :|\n   |:.  /     |    ___/     U      \/     |\     \/      |\      \   .:|\n   |::s/      :     \               \     _/      \_      /       \s.::|\n   |::c\_________    \______________/     A________/_________     /c:::|\n   °-----------\_____/-------\___________/------------------\____/-----°\n   ::::::                                                         ::::::\n   |::               »»»  O U T L A W S   S H Q  «««                 ::|\n   |:                                                                 :|\n   |SYSOPS: VEGAS/OTL, BiSCROK/OTL, PURE PAiN/DCS, CRUGER/SR, NATAS/HZ |\n   |:                 SUPPORTING: AMiGA & CONSOLE!                    :|\n   |::     CALL AND MAKE SOME TRANSFERS NOW AT: +46-8-540-63666      ::|\n   |::: CALL TO GET THE LATEST OUTLAWS RELEASES FOR FREEDOWNLOAD!   :::|\n   |:::::::.             .:::NO NUP NEEDED!:::.                .:::::::|\n   `-------------------------------------------------------------------''\n@endnode\n\n@node SnakesDen "Stripper v1.2 Documentation"\n\n<----------------------------OUTLAWS--W-H-Q----------------------------->\n   ___________  ______    _______ _____  ______ _________   ___________\n   \     ____/__\  __ \  _\  ___ \     |/     /_\  ___   \_''\     ____/_\n   _\  ___     \_\/ /  \/  \/  /  \    /    _/   \/  /____/ _\  ___     \_\n  /  \/  /      /  /    \_   _     \_ _      \_    _____)__/  \/  /      /\n /             /  /      /   /      /  \      /    \      /             /\n/_____________/__/______/___/______/____\    /___________/_____________/\n<----------------------------------------\__/SyK!------------------------>\n       Sysop`s: Snake & Nazgul          _________  _________   ______\n   cosys`s: Rofoe/LGC & SIGMA 909/OTL  _\  ___   \_\  ___   \__\  __ \\n   _   __  __ ___ ____ _____ ________ /  \/  /    \_\/  /____/  \/ /  \\n  //  / / / //  //   //    //       //      /      /  _____)__    /    \_\n //  /_/ /_//__//___//____//_______//      /      /   \      /   /      /\n                                   /_____________/__________/___/______/\n\n<---------------wOrKiN` oN: A 4ooo/4o-1omb-54ombHD-2GigDat--------------->\n\n<--------DiAL:   + 1 - 5 1 3 - 6 8 3 - 2 3 3 0  -  3 NoDeZ RiNGdOwN!--