INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('psy_log','PSY_LOG.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/PSY_LOG.LHA',NULL,'XIM','P S Y C H O P A T H   P R E S E N T S',NULL,NULL,'PSY','============================================ LogOff Version 1.0 PUBLIC RELEASE A door for both /X and S!X',replace('   P S Y C H O P A T H   P R E S E N T S\n============================================\nLogOff Version 1.0 PUBLIC RELEASE\nA door for both /X and S!X\nSnapShots included!\n============================================\n                            ©1996 PSYCHOPATH\n','\n',char(10)),'PSY_LogOff.doc',replace('Copyright (c) 1996 PSYCHOPATH\n=======================================================================\n                             .___.                   .___.\n     ._______._______._______|   |__ ._______._______|   |__ .______\n     |  __   |  __   |  __   |   __/_|  __   |  __   |   __/_|  ___/_.\n     |   |___|   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_____  |\n     |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |  _____|   |   |   |   |   |   |\n - --|_______|_______|___|___|_______|_____/p!___|___|_______|_______|-- -\n\n                        [1] Introduction\n                        [2] Requirements\n                        [3] Installing\n                        [4] History\n                        [5] Greetings\n                        [6] Copyrights\n\n=======================================================================\n                        INTRODUCTION\n=======================================================================\n\nWell this is a simple door that asks if the user want to leave mail to\nthe sysop before he leaves.\nIf you have a door installed as the C-command it will use it otherwise\nit will use the internal C-command.\nIt should work on both /X and S!X (But ONLY tested on /X 4.12)\nI''ve also include 2 snapshots from the door.\nSnapShit1.IFF is how it looks like when the door is asking if you want\nto leave a ,essage or not.\nSnapShot2.IFF is how it looks like when you are writing a message to\nthe sysops using KILL-COMMENT V1.0\n\n=======================================================================\n        ._______._______._______.   .___.___._______._______.\n        |  __   |  __   |  __   |___|   |__ |  __   |  __   | .___.\n        |   |___|   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |___|   |   | |___|\n        |   |   |  _____|   |   |   |   |   |   |   |  _____|\n        |___|p! |_____/ |____   |_______|___|___|   |_____/\n                            |___|        .___.\n                .___  ___._______._______|   |__ .______\n                |  _\/_  |  __   |  __   |   __/_|  ___/_.\n                |   \/   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_____  |\n                |   /    |  _____|   |   |   |   |   |   |\n            - --|__/_____|_____/-|___|___|_______|_______|-- -\n=======================================================================\n\n To install LogOff by PSYCHOPATH you must have the following things:\n\n   Programm               Location           Description\n   --------               --------           -----------\n   PSY_LogOff.0x0.Xim     Doors:PSYCHOPATH   Main program\n\n - An Amiga Model (500/600/1000/1200/1400/2000/2500/3000/4000/5000/CDTV/CD³²)\n - The installed Version of OS\2, OS\3 or higher\n   (Soft- or Hardware Version)\n - The installed .INFO Files in the directories. (/X V3.xx)\n - AmiExpress V3.xx , v4.xx or higher. or Sigma-Express\n\n=======================================================================\n                                   .___.           .___.___.\n               .___._______.______ |   |__   ______|   |   |\n               |__ |  __   |  ___/_|   __/_._\__   |   |   |\n               |   |   |   |_____  |   |   |  __   |   |   |\n               |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |\n           - --|___|___|___|_______|_______|_______|___|___|p! -\n=======================================================================\n\nFirst edit BBS:COMMANDS/BBSCMD/G.INFO\nand change the line:\nLOCATION=DOORS:PSYCHOPATH/PSY_LOGOFF.0x0.XIM\nChange 0x0 to your processor (000,010,020,030,040)\n\n=======================================================================\n                        History\n=======================================================================\n\n[10-12-95] Private BETA Release\n[02-09-96] Public Release V1.0\n\n=======================================================================\n                                             .____.              .____.\n       ________. ________. ________. ________|    |__    ________|    |_\n     ./  _     |/   _    |/   _    |/   _    |   ___/__._\____   |    \/\n    _|   \     |    \____|    /    |    /    |   \     |   _____/|    |\n    \/    \    |     \   |   ______|   ______|    \    |    \    |____|\n    -|______   |______\--|______/--|______/--|_________|_________|____|-\n    ---/_______|-p!-----------------------------------------------------\n\n                           -  g r e e t i n g s  -\n=======================================================================\n\nSnoopy   - Are you still FUCKING lisas mother??\nShark    - How about DALNET SKINS?\nDixy     - Do you want another door?\nJLM      - Are you still being beaten up?\nAquarius - I still need some files from you\n\nand THANX to all my BETA-TESTERS\nKid Curry * Snoopy * Shark * Cray-1 * [·tHE MASk^C¡TRUZ·] * Dixy * vann d\nAquarius * JLM * HoNcHo * «-·aRYAN·-» * Lightspeed * Dracula * S /\/\ S *\nReCall\n\nDo YOU want to be a BETATESTER? Call Raising Hell\n\n=======================================================================\n                                                    .___.   .___.\n._______._______._______.   .___._______.___._______|   |___|   |__ .______\n|  __   |  __   |  __   |___|   |  __   |__ |  __   |   __  |   __/_|  ___/_.\n|   |___|   |   |   |   |   |   |   |___|   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_____  |\n|   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |\n|_______|_______|   ____|____   |___|p! |___|____   |___|___|_______|_______|\n                |___|       |___|             \_____|\n=======================================================================\n\nCopyright (c) 1996 PSYCHOPATH\n\nThis door is CALLWARE, MAILWARE so if you like it call my bbs and tell me!\nOr leave me mail on any BBS. And maybe you will get your own REGISTRED\ndoor from me!\nAnd you''ll get MORE doors from me.\n\nCall my BBS RAISING HELL at +46-[0]243-22 70 29\nUSR 33600 DS * 1275 MB ONLINE * AMIGA, PC, SEX , /X *\n\n=======================================================================\n   ::::__________/\_________/\___/\________/\____/\ /\____  _________/\:::\n   ::+/  ____     /  ________/____/  _______/\____//   _  \/    ______/+::\n   :_/      |____/_   _!    \/    \_____    \/    \    |   \    \_  _ \:::\n   :\       _      \_ \_     \_    \   Y     \_    \   |    \    ! _// \_:\n   ::\      ¡   _   /  !      /     \_ !      /     \_ |     \___:      /:\n   :+:\_____|  _// /___:     /       /__     /       / |        /_     /+:\n   :::::::::l_____/:+::l____/_______/+:l____/_______/__l_______/:l____/:::\n\n              :::::/\__ __/\_________/\_____/\/\_____/\:::::::   MiKe!\n              :::+/    |    \    _____/_   __/\__   __/+::::::\n              :::/    _|     \   ___)_|     |__|__   |_____:::\n   33k6 DS    :_/     \__     \_       \_   !     \_ !     \_:\n              :\       |       /        /   :      /        /:\n              :+\______|      /__      /_____     /___     /+:\n              :::::::::l_____/:+l_____/:::+:l____/:+:l____/:::\n \n                          On ++46- [0]243-22 70 29\n \n                      ThE P0WeR B0aRd WITh ALL MaJoRs\n        __              ____________________________   __\n       _\/_ CooL SYsOP |                            | _\/_ RuNNInG On\n       \/\/ CooL UsErS | SYsOP: PSYCHOPATH          | \/\/ AMI/X V4.Xx\n        __             | Co²YzzEs: S /\/\ S/ØUTLAWS |  __\n       _\/_ MAJoRs     |AnD SHARK^WAVEFRONT/PRESTIGE| _\/_ OnLY RuLe:\n       \/\/ GuArAnTeeD!|____________________________| \/\/ UPLoAd Or Be\n                                                           S Q U A R E D!\n','\n',char(10)),'{"LOCATION":"DOORS:PSYCHOPATH/PSY_LOGOFF.0x0.XIM"}',NULL,51675,2,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048679);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('psy_real','PSY_REAL.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/PSY_REAL.LHA',NULL,'XIM','P S Y C H O P A T H   P R E S E N T S',NULL,NULL,'PSY','============================================ RealName Version 1.0 PUBLIC RELEASE a /X Door from PSYCHOPATH!',replace('P S Y C H O P A T H   P R E S E N T S\n============================================\nRealName Version 1.0 PUBLIC RELEASE\na /X Door from PSYCHOPATH!\n                            ©1996 PSYCHOPATH\n','\n',char(10)),'RealName.Doc',replace('Copyright (c) 1996 PSYCHOPATH\n=======================================================================\n                             .___.                   .___.\n     ._______._______._______|   |__ ._______._______|   |__ .______\n     |  __   |  __   |  __   |   __/_|  __   |  __   |   __/_|  ___/_.\n     |   |___|   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_____  |\n     |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |  _____|   |   |   |   |   |   |\n - --|_______|_______|___|___|_______|_____/p!___|___|_______|_______|-- -\n\n                        [1] Introduction\n                        [2] Requirements\n                        [3] Installing\n                        [4] History\n                        [5] Greetings\n                        [6] Copyrights\n=======================================================================\n                        INTRODUCTION\n=======================================================================\n\nWell this is a simple door that I coded in 5 mins...\nIt simple force the users to enter their REALNAMES!\nSome sysops wants to know their users realnames this is the sulotion!\n\n=======================================================================\n        ._______._______._______.   .___.___._______._______.\n        |  __   |  __   |  __   |___|   |__ |  __   |  __   | .___.\n        |   |___|   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |___|   |   | |___|\n        |   |   |  _____|   |   |   |   |   |   |   |  _____|\n        |___|p! |_____/ |____   |_______|___|___|   |_____/\n                            |___|        .___.\n                .___  ___._______._______|   |__ .______\n                |  _\/_  |  __   |  __   |   __/_|  ___/_.\n                |   \/   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_____  |\n                |   /    |  _____|   |   |   |   |   |   |\n            - --|__/_____|_____/-|___|___|_______|_______|-- -\n=======================================================================\n\n To install RealName by PSYCHOPATH you must have the following things:\n\n   Programm               Location           Description\n   --------               --------           -----------\n   PSY_RealName.0x0.Xim   Doors:PSYCHOPATH   Main program\n\n - An Amiga Model (500/600/1000/1200/1400/2000/2500/3000/4000/5000/CDTV/CD³²)\n - The installed Version of OS\2, OS\3 or higher\n   (Soft- or Hardware Version)\n - The installed .INFO Files in the directories. (/X V3.xx)\n - AmiExpress V3.xx , v4.xx or higher.\n\n=======================================================================\n                                   .___.           .___.___.\n               .___._______.______ |   |__   ______|   |   |\n               |__ |  __   |  ___/_|   __/_._\__   |   |   |\n               |   |   |   |_____  |   |   |  __   |   |   |\n               |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |\n           - --|___|___|___|_______|_______|_______|___|___|p! -\n=======================================================================\n\nFirst edit BBS:COMMANDS/BBSCMD/REAL.INFO\nand change the line:\nLOCATION=DOORS:PSYCHOPATH/PSY_REALNAME.0x0.XIM\nChange 0x0 to your processor (000,010,020,030,040)\n\nMaybe you want this door to be executed when a NEWUSER login?\nthen put these lines in BBS:NODE(X)/JOINED.TXT or BBS:SCREENS/JOINED.TXT\n\n~\n~CC_SENT|~CC_QUICKCFG|~CC_ANNCFG|\n\nOr maybe you want to force ALL users to enter their realname? Then add the\nabove lines to BBS:BULL.TXT or some other bull files that are showed\neverytime a user logon!\n\n=======================================================================\n                        History\n=======================================================================\n\n[01-03-96] V1.0 Public Release\n\n=======================================================================\n                                             .____.              .____.\n       ________. ________. ________. ________|    |__    ________|    |_\n     ./  _     |/   _    |/   _    |/   _    |   ___/__._\____   |    \/\n    _|   \     |    \____|    /    |    /    |   \     |   _____/|    |\n    \/    \    |     \   |   ______|   ______|    \    |    \    |____|\n    -|______   |______\--|______/--|______/--|_________|_________|____|-\n    ---/_______|-p!-----------------------------------------------------\n\n                           -  g r e e t i n g s  -\n=======================================================================\n\nSnoopy - Lets talk on the phone soon again...\nShark  - How''re the buisness going?\nDixy   - Where was the Babes?\n\nand THANX to all my BETA-TESTERS\nKid Curry * Snoopy * Shark * Cray-1 * [·tHE MASk^C¡TRUZ·] * Dixy * vann d\nAquarius * JLM * HoNcHo * «-·aRYAN·-» * Lightspeed * Dracula * S /\/\ S\n\nDo YOU want to be a BETATESTER? Call Raising Hell\n\n=======================================================================\n                                                    .___.   .___.\n._______._______._______.   .___._______.___._______|   |___|   |__ .______\n|  __   |  __   |  __   |___|   |  __   |__ |  __   |   __  |   __/_|  ___/_.\n|   |___|   |   |   |   |   |   |   |___|   |   |   |   |   |   |   |_____  |\n|   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |   |\n|_______|_______|   ____|____   |___|p! |___|____   |___|___|_______|_______|\n                |___|       |___|             \_____|\n=======================================================================\n\nCopyright (c) 1996 PSYCHOPATH\n\nThis door is CALLWARE so if you like it call my bbs and tell me!\n\nCall my BBS RAISING HELL at +46-[0]243-22 70 29\nUSR 33600 DS * 1275 MB ONLINE * AMIGA, PC, SEX *\n\n=======================================================================\n   ::::__________/\_________/\___/\________/\____/\ /\____  _________/\:::\n   ::+/  ____     /  ________/____/  _______/\____//   _  \/    ______/+::\n   :_/      |____/_   _!    \/    \_____    \/    \    |   \    \_  _ \:::\n   :\       _      \_ \_     \_    \   Y     \_    \   |    \    ! _// \_:\n   ::\      ¡   _   /  !      /     \_ !      /     \_ |     \___:      /:\n   :+:\_____|  _// /___:     /       /__     /       / |        /_     /+:\n   :::::::::l_____/:+::l____/_______/+:l____/_______/__l_______/:l____/:::\n\n              :::::/\__ __/\_________/\_____/\/\_____/\:::::::   MiKe!\n              :::+/    |    \    _____/_   __/\__   __/+::::::\n              :::/    _|     \   ___)_|     |__|__   |_____:::\n   33k6 DS    :_/     \__     \_       \_   !     \_ !     \_:\n              :\       |       /        /   :      /        /:\n              :+\______|      /__      /_____     /___     /+:\n              :::::::::l_____/:+l_____/:::+:l____/:+:l____/:::\n \n                          On ++46- [0]243-22 70 29\n \n                      ThE P0WeR B0aRd WITh ALL MaJoRs\n        __              ____________________________   __\n       _\/_ CooL SYsOP |                            | _\/_ RuNNInG On\n       \/\/ CooL UsErS | SYsOP: PSYCHOPATH          | \/\/ AMI/X V4.Xx\n        __             | Co²YzzEs: S /\/\ S/ØUTLAWS |  __\n       _\/_ MAJoRs     |AnD SHARK^WAVEFRONT/PRESTIGE| _\/_ OnLY RuLe:\n       \/\/ GuArAnTeeD!|____________________________| \/\/ UPLoAd Or Be\n                                                           S Q U A R E D!\n','\n',char(10)),'{"LOCATION":"DOORS:PSYCHOPATH/PSY_REALNAME.0x0.XIM"}',NULL,44149,1,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048679);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ptk_us10','PTK-US10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/PTK-US10.LHA',NULL,'XIM','bOOT.EXZE!',NULL,'mOTiVE','PTK','\___   \_  \____    \       ) ____)   |/   / |  _)  / )  \  _)   /_/  \_/  _)__|   /   / |  \__/  |   \  \   \/    \       \   \   \',replace('_____/\__/\_______/\______/\____/\ ___  /\_\n\___   \_  \____    \       ) ____)   |/   /\n|  _)  / )  \  _)   /_/  \_/  _)__|   /   /\n|  \__/  |   \  \   \/    \       \   \   \\n|__| \  _|___/__|\  _)_____)____  /___|\  _\\n(­-­-­\/----------\/  pRESENTS  \/-[tE]-\/­\n        -- pOWERsTATUS(tm) v1.0t --\n          bY mOTiVE pOWER/mST/pTK\n','\n',char(10)),'tSTATUS.dOC',replace('\n                                                                       __._\n   .________              .________  .________              _.        / ¬|\n_._\       ¬\___________._\       ¬\_\________\____________/ :_____. /   |\n |: \_______________.  ¬|: \______________________     ___/  |:    !/    |.\n |.        |:      /    |.     _     |:         |:   .___/   |.    __     |\n !_________!______/     !______/     !__________!____________!______/     !\n  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯ ¯¯¯¯¯/    _/ ¯¯¯¯¯/    _/ ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯ ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯ ¯¯¯¯¯/    _/\n                /______\  sCf/______\-Os!                         /______\\n                 ¯¯¯¯¯¯       ¯¯¯¯¯¯                               ¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                                  pRESENTS:\n\n                         -- pOWERsTATUS(tm) v1.0t --\n\n                           bY mOTiVE pOWER/mST/pTK\n\n\nIntroduction:\n\nThis would probably be my very first release of a door... I have coded a lot\nof ARexx doors, but all for /X. And because there were so many doors for /X\nout, releasing an ARexx door would be pointless. (Most sysops think ARexx is\ntoo slow... -sigh- ) But i saw there was a need for MANY doors for /T\ ...\nthe doors that are out allready, are nice, but need some better dezign, and\nmore configurability! So i bring you this USERSTATUS door, wich is reasonably\neasy to configure, and the dezign (so i heared) looks cool enuff! :)\nFor instance, the higher access someone has, the more STARS(tm) he/she gets!\nThe level of access needed for more stars can be configured. See Configuration\nbelow for more details.\n\n\n\nDisclaimer:\n\nThis tool is sHiTwARE(tm)! I don''t care how many times it formats your HD,\nor whatever. When it left my board, it wasn''t dezigned to do so.\nYou are allowed to use this tool, without having to mention it to me, or\ngive me money or something (giving money IS ALLOWED though). And you don''t\nhave to support any board. You just have to configure it!\n\nThis tool is optimized by RexxOpt from PROXiTY SOFTWORKS / Ulrich Sibiller\n\n\n\nInstallation:\n\nTo install this door, simply copy the files with their paths to your\nTEMPEST: location. Then adjust the .opt files in your OPTiONAL directory\nwith something like this:\n\n[*,*,*,*,*]   = S    |REXX  |DOORS:mP/tSTATUS.AiM\n\nThis can, for instance, be placed in the file ''GlobalMenu.opt'', but DO check\nthe files: ''MsgMenu.opt'' and ''Filemenu.opt'' in case there is another S command\nconfigured there.\n\n\nConfiguration:\n\nThe configuration file (tSTATUS.cFG) looks like this: (DEFAULT)\n\n200             : The access level for 3 stars\n100             : The access level for 2 stars\n50              : The access level for 1 star\nnO cOMMENT!     : Default text when no comment is given\nlAME.. oR nEW?! : Default text when access level is below 1 star level\n\nThe different types of accesslevel to be defined are made configurably, ''cause\nevery sysop uses another method of accessgrading... For instance:\n\n255 <-   sysop     -> 255  As you can see, an elite user would get only 1\n 50 <- elite user  -> 200  star, and want 2! (At LEAST! :) )... And would\n 20 <- normal user -> 100  bother the sysop! On the other hand, a normal\n 15 <-   lamer     ->  50  user on the right could think he''s rEALLY c00L!\n 10 <-  new user   ->  10  But he is not! .. so that''s why! :)\n\n\n\nFuture:\n\nThe future of this door is maybe some adjustments to the data it gives, or\nsome updates to the dezign... No real 1.1t version is expected though!\n\nIf you have any problems, or you might find a bug (?!), or maybe you want your\nown special dezign... contact me at my board, or any other board you can!\n\nAlso, i am always in need of good ascii''s for my doors, so when you got some\ntime, make some ascii''s!\nAnd when you have any idea, or you feel the need for a door that doesn''t exist\nfor /T\, contact me also! We''ll work things out!\n\n\n\nGreets:\n\nMy greets go out to:\n\n      ALL members of mYSTiC\n                 ALL members of pARTEK\n                            ALL members of gENETiC\n                                       ALL members of cOCAiNE (tHE rEAL!)\n      ALL members of rOYAL\n                 ALL members of rOADhOGz\n                            ALL members of my board!\n                                       ALL users of the pOWERtOOLS(tm)\n\n\nLast words:\n\nWOW! A text without ANY bbs-add! That would be the first one in AGES! c00L!\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',49996,3,0,NULL,NULL,'ptk_us10','scan',1780048679);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ptl_bd10','PTL-BD10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/PTL-BD10.LHA','rpstart','XIM','24H PARTY PEOPLE',NULL,NULL,'PTL','_\_________\_\_____  _____/ _\_  |_____ /      ______/   /      \w^s/     l     \ /_________|.cOLa./________\ /_____________\',replace('   ________/\  ______________  ___/|\n  _\_________\_\_____  _____/ _\_  |_____\n /      ______/   /      \w^s/     l     \\n/_________|.cOLa./________\ /_____________\\n::::::::::::::::::presents::::::::::::::::::\n::::::: FRaNKy''s BirthDay Door V 1.0 :::::::\n::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\n::::: Give your users a nice birthday ::::::\n:::::   present, they''ll love it !!   ::::::\n::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::','\n',char(10)),'BirthDay.Guide',replace('@database "FRaNKy''s BirthDay Door V 1.0"\n@font topaz.font 8\n@author "FRaNKy/PTL"\n@(c) "Copyright © 1995 FRaNKy / Purple Turtle"\n@$VER: BirthDay.Guide V1.0  (31/08/95)\n@node Main "FRaNKy''s BirthDay Door V 1.0 - Main Menu"\n    FRaNKy''s BirthDay Door V 1.0 - Copyright 1995 FRaNKy / Purple Turtle\n¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n       Important!            Contacting The Author           The Door\n      ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯          ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯         ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n  @{"     Disclaimer      " link "disc"}    @{"   Bulletin Boards   " link "Fbss"}    @{"     What Is It ?    " link "what"}\n  @{"   Compiled Doors    " link "comp"}    @{"       FidoNet       " link "Ffido"}    @{"     Installation    " link "inst"}\n  @{"    PostCardWare     " link "post"}    @{"      InterNet       " link "Finter"}    @{"     Config File     " link "conf"}\n                                                      @{"  Credits & Hellos   " link "cred"}\n     ________/\  ______________  ___/|                @{"       History       " link "hist"}\n    _\_________\_\_____  _____/ _\_  |_____           @{"    The Story Off    " link "stor"}\n   /      ______/   /      \w^s/     l     \\n  /_________|.cOLa./________\ /_____________\             Contacting PTL\n  ::::::::::::::::::presents::::::::::::::::::           ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n  ::::::: FRaNKy''s BirthDay Door V 1.0 :::::::        @{"        BBS''s        " link "pbbs"}\n  ::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::        @{"       FidoNet       " link "pfido"}\n  ::::: Give your users a nice birthday ::::::        @{"      Internet       " link "pinter"}\n  :::::   present, they''ll love it !!   ::::::\n  ::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::        @{" Looking For Members " link "memb"}\n@endnode\n@node "disc"\n@title "Disclaimer"\n                                DISCLAIMER\n                               ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n     This software is "AS IS", the author can not be held responsible for\n    any damage caused to your system by this software, or the consequences\n                               of this damage...\n\n                    To say it simply : Use at your own risk !\n@endnode\n@node "post"\n@title "PostCardWare"\n                               POSTCARDWARE\n                              ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n           All the doors included in this archive are PostCardWare\n      If you use one of included doors, you are kindly asked to send a\n                    postcard of the area you live in to :\n\n                          Peter Smets (FRaNKy / PTL)\n                          Weldadigheidsstraat 45\n                          3000 Leuven\n                          Belgium\n\n             Postcards received so far : Lady An      [   UK   ]\n                                         Killer Dwarf [ Sweden ]\n@endnode\n@node "comp"\n@title "Compiled Doors"\n                               COMPILED DOORS\n                              ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n  All doors in this archive are compiled using the RexxPlus Arexx Compiler.\n\n     To get the doors to work on you /X system, you must run RPStart and\n       have the libraries included in the archive copied to your LIBS:\n  It is advisable to put RPStart in you User-Startup so you won''t forget it\n\n   If you would like a copy of the uncompiled sources of the doors included\n      in this archive, send 1500 BEF (50 USD) to the author of the doors.\n           Cash money (no coins) or EuroCheque in BEF only please.\n\n  This can be a large amount of money, but if you see what money I spend in\n   my doors (time, phonecalls) and if you really want the sources to study\n                       them, this isn''t too much I think...\n\n        The adress where you can send the money to can be found under\n                              @{"postcardware" link "post"} button...\n\nNote :\n\n Compiled doors do not work on all systems (blame the /X RexxPort for this)\n                   but the advantage for me is much greater.\n\n  I decided to do this compilation of my doors because I noticed that more\n    and more people started using pieces of my doors, or sometimes just\n    renaming the door and then releasing it under their own name/group.\n            If you want you can buy the sources as staded above.\n\n                                                                    FRaNKy.\n@endnode\n@node "what"\n@title "FRaNKy''s BirthDay Door V 1.0 - What is it ?"\n                                WHAT IS IT ?\n                               ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\nBirthDay gives the user a ''gift'' on his/her bithday.  When the user is not\nin the Birthday file, it will ask the user to give in his birthday.\n\nWhen the user is in this Birthday file, the door will no longer show any\ntext output untill the birthday and then be silent again for another year.\n\nOn his/her birthday the user will receive the nr of Kb stated in the\n@{"config file" link "conf"}.  Ofcourse the user will only receive these once,\nso if the user calls back 15 mins later he won''t get anymore upload\ncredits.\n@endnode\n@node "inst"\n@title "FRaNKy''s BirthDay Door V 1.0 - Installation"\n                                INSTALLATION\n                               ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\nPut the files Birthday.#? in Doors:PTL/Birthday/ to get everything working.\nThe icon Birth.Info (rename it to whatever what you like) has to be placed\nin BBS:Commands/BBSCmd/.\n\nThe add the door to your Logon-sequence by adding ''~CC_BIRTH'' to the file\n''NodeX/bull.txt'' (where X is the node number)\n@endnode\n@node "conf"\n@title "FRaNKy''s BirthDay Door V 1.0 - Config File"\n                                CONFIGURATION\n                               ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\nThe file Doors:PTL/Birthday/Birthday.Cfg has to be edited like this :\n\nLine 1 : Number of Kb given for birthday\nLine 2 : User that does not get any birthday gift\nLine 3 : User that does not get any birthday gift\nLine 4 : ...\n\nExample :\n\n--- cut ---\n500\nLamer\nUltraLamer\n--- cut ---\n\nAll users except for Lamer and Ultralamer will now receive 500 Kb upload\ncredits on their birthday.\n@endnode\n@node "cred"\n@title "FRaNKy''s BirthDay Door V 1.0 - Credits"\n                                   CREDITS\n                                  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                             Coding       : FRaNKy\n                             Docs         : FRaNKy\n                             Idea         : TFX\n                             Nagging      : Necrite\n                             Beta Testing : TFX & Killer Dwarf\n\n                                  GREETINGS\n                                 ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\nHello''s & Greetings from FRaNKy fly out to : All PTL members, specially\nto : TFX (I''ll make a better map next time) - Necrite (Cluuuuuuuuuuub !) -\nKiller Dwarf (Stappa !) - The Fly - Flare - Damien - Crisp.\nMore Hello''s to : Recall (format c:) - TCB - Syntax - All Tragedy Members -\nAnd everyone I forgot in this hurry.\n@endnode\n@node "hist"\n@title "FRaNKy''s BirthDay Door V 1.0 - History"\n                                    HISTORY\n                                   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                 ... - 0.9  : Internal Beta Releases\n                       1.0  : First Worldwide Release\n@endnode\n@node "stor"\n@title "FRaNKy''s BirthDay Door V 1.0 - The Story Off"\n                                 THE STORY OFF\n                                ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\nTFX gave me a script of a CNet-Birthday door and asked me to make it for\nAmix... I didn''t felt much for doing it, but I started it anyway... About\n3 days later a first Beta release was ready and I upped it to Fortress.\n\nA day later Necrite said he didn''t wanted the door to show up if it wasn''t\nthe users birthday.. I didn''t wanted to do this so I started up a vote\n(I lost 4 to 0 AAAARGH) and now the door doesn''t show up anymore...\n\nI putted the door up for a big Test on Killer Dwarfs'' BBS and there I\nnoticed that users ALWAYS entered their birthdays the wrong way so I added\nsome text to make it more clear but it didn''t helped so I added a checker\nif they entered it correctly.  And even now some stupid people manage to\nenter their birthday''s in the wrong way but I don''t care anymore. It is\nclear enough HOW they have to enter their birthday and if they don''t want\nto receive any upload creds an their birthday, that''s their problem.\n@endnode\n@node "Fbss"\n@title "Contacting The Author On The PTL BBS''s"\n                            CONTACTING THE AUTHOR\n                           ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n   The Author of the door can be contacted on these Purple Turtle BBS''s\n\n    Fortress      (   PTL WHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-3-829.08.72 (Zyxel 16.8)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-3-825.00.69 (Vfast 28.8)\n\n    Enigma        (   PTL BHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-89-73.20.54 (USR   16.8)\n\n    Secret Cinema (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +32-52-35.15.75 (VFast 33.6)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-52-RINGDOWN (VFast 33.6)\n\n    Cyber Garden  (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +32-11-33.37.03 (USR   16.8)\n\n    S.P.G         (   PTL SHQ  ) Node 1 : +46-612-130.76  (USR   16.8)\n\n    Rhythm Nation (   PTL FHQ  ) Node 1 : +33-82-88.19.31 (???   14.4)\n@endnode\n@node "FFido"\n@title "Contacting The Author Through FidoNet"\n                            CONTACTING THE AUTHOR\n                           ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    The Author of the doors included in this archive can be contacted by\n               sendin a Netmail to one of these point-numbers\n\n                                2:292/622.13\n                                2:292/8010.32\n@endnode\n@node "finter"\n@title "Contacting The Author Through Internet"\n                            CONTACTING THE AUTHOR\n                           ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                            Send your E-Mails to:\n\n                             [email removed]\n\n                     IRC-fans can try to join the channel\n\n                                    #PTL\n\n                         If I''m online, I''ll be there.\n@endnode\n@node "Pbbs"\n@title "Purpe Turtle BBS''s"\n                             PURPLE TURTLE BBS''S\n                            ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                                   BELGIUM\n                                  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Fortress      (   PTL WHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-3-829.08.72 (Zyxel 16.8)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-3-825.00.69 (Vfast 28.8)\n\n    Enigma        (   PTL BHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-89-73.20.54 (USR   16.8)\n\n    Secret Cinema (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +32-52-35.15.75 (VFast 33.6)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-52-RINGDOWN (VFast 33.6)\n\n    Cyber Garden  (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +32-11-33.37.03 (USR   16.8)\n\n                                   HOLLAND\n                                  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Super Dancer  (   PTL HHQ  ) Node 1 : +31-570-037-050 (VFast 28.8)\n\n                                    SWEDEN\n                                   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Bitch Board   (   PTL EHQ  ) Node 1 : +46-111-473.56  (USR   28.8)\n\n    S.P.G         (   PTL SHQ  ) Node 1 : +46-612-130.76  (Vfast 28.8)\n\n    rIVER wILD    (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +46-612-300.13  (USR   28.8)\n\n    Inferno       (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +46-øPRIVATE!ø  (USR   33.6)\n\n                                    FRANCE\n                                   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Rhythm Nation (   PTL FHQ  ) Node 1 : +33-82-88.19.31 (???   14.4)\n\n                                    NORWAY\n                                   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Wizard Guild  (   PTL NHQ  ) Node 1 : +47-53-76.16.91 (VFast 28.8)\n\n                                   GERMANY\n                                  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Traders World (   PTL GHQ  ) Node 1 : +49-215-1786470 (VFast 28.8)\n@endnode\n@node "PFido"\n@title "Purple Turtle FidoNet Adresses"\n                        PURPLE TURTLE FIDONET ADRESSES\n                       ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                  TFX      (  World Leader )   2:292/8010.14\n                  FRaNKy   (Co-World Leader)   2:292/8010.32\n@endnode\n@node "pinter"\n@title "Purple Turtle On The Net"\n                          PURPLE TURTLE ON THE NET\n                         ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                The Purple Turtle homepage can be visited at :\n\n                    http://www.ping.be/~ping2045/ptl.html\n\n                    You can also send E-Mails to FRaNKy at :\n\n                              [email removed]\n\n                         Or join the IRC-Channel #PTL\n@endnode\n@node "memb"\n@title "Purple Turtle Is Always Looking For New Members"\n                           LOOKING FOR NEW MEMBERS\n                          ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n  If you think you are the right guy (girl) for a cool group and you can do\n  some Coding (ASM-C-Arexx-...), Music, Graphics, Trading, Swapping or have\n      a BBS, then contact the Purple Turtle Leaders or Division Leaders\n                   for a certain reply on one of our HQ''s.\n\n   If you want to join with your BBS, we do not ask any donations for your\n    membership (in another way : it''s free !).  BBS''s outside Belgium are\n                              extremely welcome...\n\n        @{" Bulletin Boards " link "lbbs"}   @{"     FidoNet     " link "PFido"}   @{"    InterNet    " link "pinter"}\n@endnode\n@node "lbbs"\n@title "Contacting The Leaders"\n                           CONTACTING THE LEADERS\n                          ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n  You can contact the World Leaders and/or division leaders on these BBS''s.\n    People with a HQ in their country should adress themselves to that HQ.\n       If there isn''t a PTL BBS in your country, call the WHQ or a bbs\n                            in a country near you.\n\n    Fortress      (   PTL WHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-3-829.08.72 (Zyxel 16.8)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-3-825.00.69 (Vfast 28.8)\n\n    Bitch Board   (   PTL EHQ  ) Node 1 : +46-111-473.56  (USR   28.8)\n\n    Super Dancer  (   PTL HHQ  ) Node 1 : +31-570-037-050 (VFast 28.8)\n\n    S.P.G         (   PTL SHQ  ) Node 1 : +46-612-130.76  (Vfast 28.8)\n\n    Rhythm Nation (   PTL FHQ  ) Node 1 : +33-82-88.19.31 (???   14.4)\n\n    Wizard Guild  (   PTL NHQ  ) Node 1 : +47-53-76.16.91 (VFast 28.8)\n\n    Traders World (   PTL GHQ  ) Node 1 : +49-215-1786470 (VFast 28.8)\n@endnode\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',109477,7,0,NULL,NULL,'ptl_bd10','scan',1780048679);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ptl_bd11','PTL-BD11.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/PTL-BD11.LHA','rpstart','XIM','RPSTaRT',NULL,NULL,'PTL','_\_________\_\_____  _____/ _\_  |_____ /      ______/   /      \w^s/     l     \ /_________|.cOLa./________\ /_____________\',replace('   ________/\  ______________  ___/|\n  _\_________\_\_____  _____/ _\_  |_____\n /      ______/   /      \w^s/     l     \\n/_________|.cOLa./________\ /_____________\\n::::::::::::::::::presents::::::::::::::::::\n::::::: FRaNKy''s BirthDay Door V 1.1 :::::::\n::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\n::::: Give your users a nice birthday ::::::\n:::::   present, they''ll love it !!   ::::::\n::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::','\n',char(10)),'BirthDay.Guide',replace('@database "FRaNKy''s BirthDay Door V 1.1"\n@font topaz.font 8\n@author "FRaNKy/PTL"\n@(c) "Copyright © 1995 FRaNKy / Purple Turtle"\n@$VER: BirthDay.Guide V1.01  (28/09/95)\n@node Main "FRaNKy''s BirthDay Door V 1.1 - Main Menu"\n    FRaNKy''s BirthDay Door V 1.1 - Copyright 1995 FRaNKy / Purple Turtle\n¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n       Important!            Contacting The Author           The Door\n      ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯          ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯         ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n  @{"     Disclaimer      " link "disc"}    @{"   Bulletin Boards   " link "Fbss"}    @{"     What Is It ?    " link "what"}\n  @{"   Compiled Doors    " link "comp"}    @{"       FidoNet       " link "Ffido"}    @{"     Installation    " link "inst"}\n  @{"    PostCardWare     " link "post"}    @{"      InterNet       " link "Finter"}    @{"     Config File     " link "conf"}\n                                                      @{"  Credits & Hellos   " link "cred"}\n     ________/\  ______________  ___/|                @{"       History       " link "hist"}\n    _\_________\_\_____  _____/ _\_  |_____           @{"    The Story Off    " link "stor"}\n   /      ______/   /      \w^s/     l     \\n  /_________|.cOLa./________\ /_____________\             Contacting PTL\n  ::::::::::::::::::presents::::::::::::::::::           ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n  ::::::: FRaNKy''s BirthDay Door V 1.1 :::::::        @{"        BBS''s        " link "pbbs"}\n  ::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::        @{"       FidoNet       " link "pfido"}\n  ::::: Give your users a nice birthday ::::::        @{"      Internet       " link "pinter"}\n  :::::   present, they''ll love it !!   ::::::\n  ::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::        @{" Looking For Members " link "memb"}\n@endnode\n@node "disc"\n@title "Disclaimer"\n                                DISCLAIMER\n                               ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n     This software is "AS IS", the author can not be held responsible for\n    any damage caused to your system by this software, or the consequences\n                               of this damage...\n\n                    To say it simply : Use at your own risk !\n@endnode\n@node "post"\n@title "PostCardWare"\n                               POSTCARDWARE\n                              ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n           All the doors included in this archive are PostCardWare\n      If you use one of included doors, you are kindly asked to send a\n                    postcard of the area you live in to :\n\n                          Peter Smets (FRaNKy / PTL)\n                          Weldadigheidsstraat 45\n                          3000 Leuven\n                          Belgium\n\n             Postcards received so far : Lady An      [   UK   ]\n                                         Killer Dwarf [ Sweden ]\n@endnode\n@node "comp"\n@title "Compiled Doors"\n                               COMPILED DOORS\n                              ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n  All doors in this archive are compiled using the RexxPlus Arexx Compiler.\n\n     To get the doors to work on you /X system, you must run RPStart and\n       have the libraries included in the archive copied to your LIBS:\n  It is advisable to put RPStart in you User-Startup so you won''t forget it\n\n   If you would like a copy of the uncompiled sources of the doors included\n      in this archive, send 1500 BEF (50 USD) to the author of the doors.\n           Cash money (no coins) or EuroCheque in BEF only please.\n\n  This can be a large amount of money, but if you see what money I spend in\n   my doors (time, phonecalls) and if you really want the sources to study\n                       them, this isn''t too much I think...\n\n        The adress where you can send the money to can be found under\n                              @{"postcardware" link "post"} button...\n\nNote :\n\n Compiled doors do not work on all systems (blame the /X RexxPort for this)\n                   but the advantage for me is much greater.\n\n  I decided to do this compilation of my doors because I noticed that more\n    and more people started using pieces of my doors, or sometimes just\n    renaming the door and then releasing it under their own name/group.\n            If you want you can buy the sources as staded above.\n\n                                                                    FRaNKy.\n@endnode\n@node "what"\n@title "FRaNKy''s BirthDay Door V 1.1 - What is it ?"\n                                WHAT IS IT ?\n                               ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\nBirthDay gives the user a ''gift'' on his/her bithday.  When the user is not\nin the Birthday file, it will ask the user to give in his birthday.\n\nWhen the user is in this Birthday file, the door will no longer show any\ntext output untill the birthday and then be silent again for another year.\n\nOn his/her birthday the user will receive the nr of Kb stated in the\n@{"config file" link "conf"}.  Ofcourse the user will only receive these once,\nso if the user calls back 15 mins later he won''t get anymore upload\ncredits.\n@endnode\n@node "inst"\n@title "FRaNKy''s BirthDay Door V 1.1 - Installation"\n                                INSTALLATION\n                               ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\nPut the files Birthday.#? in Doors:PTL/Birthday/ to get everything working.\nThe icon Birth.Info (rename it to whatever what you like) has to be placed\nin BBS:Commands/BBSCmd/.\n\nThe add the door to your Logon-sequence by adding ''~CC_BIRTH'' to the file\n''NodeX/bull.txt'' (where X is the node number)\n@endnode\n@node "conf"\n@title "FRaNKy''s BirthDay Door V 1.1 - Config File"\n                                CONFIGURATION\n                               ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\nThe file Doors:PTL/Birthday/Birthday.Cfg has to be edited like this :\n\nLine 1 : Number of Kb given for birthday\nLine 2 : User that does not get any birthday gift\nLine 3 : User that does not get any birthday gift\nLine 4 : ...\n\nExample :\n\n--- cut ---\n500\nLamer\nUltraLamer\n--- cut ---\n\nAll users except for Lamer and Ultralamer will now receive 500 Kb upload\ncredits on their birthday.\n\nIf you DO NOT want any user to receive any credits the file\nDoors:PTL/Birthday/Birthday.Cfg has to be edited like this\n\nLine 1 : Number of Kb given for birthday (DO NOT FORGET THIS ONE !)\nLine 2 : EALL\n\nExample :\n\n--- cut ---\n0\nEALL\n--- cut ---\n@endnode\n@node "cred"\n@title "FRaNKy''s BirthDay Door V 1.1 - Credits"\n                                   CREDITS\n                                  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                             Coding       : FRaNKy\n                             Docs         : FRaNKy\n                             Ideas        : TFX & La Fayette\n                             Nagging      : Necrite\n                             Beta Testing : TFX & Killer Dwarf\n\n                                  GREETINGS\n                                 ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\nHello''s & Greetings from FRaNKy fly out to : All PTL members and\nmy friends out there, you know who you are.\n\n@endnode\n@node "hist"\n@title "FRaNKy''s BirthDay Door V 1.1 - History"\n                                    HISTORY\n                                   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                 ... - 0.9  : Internal Beta Releases\n                       1.0  : First Worldwide Release\n                       1.1  : - Added an option so that no-one will\n                                receive a birthday gift (asshole-mode)\n                              - Some internal source updates\n                              - Some layout changes\n@endnode\n@node "stor"\n@title "FRaNKy''s BirthDay Door V 1.1 - The Story Off"\n                                 THE STORY OFF\n                                ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\nTFX gave me a script of a CNet-Birthday door and asked me to make it for\nAmix... I didn''t felt much for doing it, but I started it anyway... About\n3 days later a first Beta release was ready and I upped it to Fortress.\n\nA day later Necrite said he didn''t wanted the door to show up if it wasn''t\nthe users birthday.. I didn''t wanted to do this so I started up a vote\n(I lost 4 to 0 AAAARGH) and now the door doesn''t show up anymore...\n\nI putted the door up for a big Test on Killer Dwarfs'' BBS and there I\nnoticed that users ALWAYS entered their birthdays the wrong way so I added\nsome text to make it more clear but it didn''t helped so I added a checker\nif they entered it correctly.  And even now some stupid people manage to\nenter their birthday''s in the wrong way but I don''t care anymore. It is\nclear enough HOW they have to enter their birthday and if they don''t want\nto receive any upload creds an their birthday, that''s their problem.\n@endnode\n@node "Fbss"\n@title "Contacting The Author On The PTL BBS''s"\n                            CONTACTING THE AUTHOR\n                           ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n   The Author of the door can be contacted on these Purple Turtle BBS''s\n\n    Fortress      (   PTL WHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-3-***.**.** (Zyxel 16.8)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-3-***.**.** (Vfast 28.8)\n\n    Bitch Board   (   PTL EHQ  ) Node 1 : +46-11-**.**.** (USR   28.8)\n\n    Enigma        (   PTL BHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-89-**.**.** (USR   16.8)\n\n    Secret Cinema (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +32-52-**.**.** (VFast 33.6)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-52-RINGDOWN (VFast 33.6)\n\n    Cyber Garden  (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +32-11-**.**.** (USR   16.8)\n\n    Rhythm Nation (   PTL FHQ  ) Node 1 : +33-82-**.**.** (???   14.4)\n@endnode\n@node "FFido"\n@title "Contacting The Author Through FidoNet"\n                            CONTACTING THE AUTHOR\n                           ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    The Author of the doors included in this archive can be contacted by\n               sendin a Netmail to one of these point-numbers\n\n                                2:292/628.10\n\n@endnode\n@node "finter"\n@title "Contacting The Author Through Internet"\n                            CONTACTING THE AUTHOR\n                           ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                            Send your E-Mails to:\n\n                             [email removed]\n\n                     IRC-fans can try to join the channel\n\n                                    #PTL\n\n                         If I''m online, I''ll be there.\n@endnode\n@node "Pbbs"\n@title "Purpe Turtle BBS''s"\n                             PURPLE TURTLE BBS''S\n                            ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                                   BELGIUM\n                                  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Fortress      (   PTL WHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-3-***.**.** (Zyxel 16.8)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-3-***.**.** (Vfast 28.8)\n\n    Enigma        (   PTL BHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-89-**.**.** (USR   16.8)\n\n    Secret Cinema (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +32-52-**.**.** (VFast 33.6)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-52-RINGDOWN (VFast 33.6)\n\n    Cyber Garden  (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +32-11-**.**.** (USR   16.8)\n\n                                   HOLLAND\n                                  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Super Dancer  (   PTL HHQ  ) Node 1 : +31-570-***.*** (VFast 28.8)\n                                 Node 2 : +31-570-***.*** (USR   14.4)\n                                 Node 3 : +31-570-***.*** (USR   16.8)\n\n                                    SWEDEN\n                                   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Bitch Board   (   PTL EHQ  ) Node 1 : +46-111-***.**  (USR   28.8)\n\n    Inferno       (   PTL SHQ  ) Node 1 : +46-øPRIVATE!ø  (USR   33.6)\n\n    rIVER wILD    (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +46-612-***.**  (USR   28.8)\n\n\n                                    FRANCE\n                                   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Rhythm Nation (   PTL FHQ  ) Node 1 : +33-82-**.**.** (???   14.4)\n\n                                    NORWAY\n                                   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Wizard Guild  (   PTL NHQ  ) Node 1 : +47-53-**.**.** (VFast 28.8)\n\n                                   GERMANY\n                                  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Traders World (   PTL GHQ  ) Node 1 : +49-215-******* (VFast 28.8)\n@endnode\n@node "PFido"\n@title "Purple Turtle FidoNet Adresses"\n                        PURPLE TURTLE FIDONET ADRESSES\n                       ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                  TFX      (  World Leader )   2:292/8010.14\n                  FRaNKy   (Co-World Leader)   2:292/628.10\n@endnode\n@node "pinter"\n@title "Purple Turtle On The Net"\n                          PURPLE TURTLE ON THE NET\n                         ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                The Purple Turtle homepage can be visited at :\n\n                    http://www.ping.be/~ping2045/ptl.html\n\n                    You can also send E-Mails to FRaNKy at :\n\n                              [email removed]\n\n                         Or join the IRC-Channel #PTL\n@endnode\n@node "memb"\n@title "Purple Turtle Is Always Looking For New Members"\n                           LOOKING FOR NEW MEMBERS\n                          ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n  If you think you are the right guy (girl) for a cool group and you can do\n  some Coding (ASM-C-Arexx-...), Music, Graphics, Trading, Swapping or have\n      a BBS, then contact the Purple Turtle Leaders or Division Leaders\n                   for a certain reply on one of our HQ''s.\n\n   If you want to join with your BBS, we do not ask any donations for your\n    membership (in another way : it''s free !).  BBS''s outside Belgium are\n                              extremely welcome...\n\n        @{" Bulletin Boards " link "lbbs"}   @{"     FidoNet     " link "PFido"}   @{"    InterNet    " link "pinter"}\n@endnode\n@node "lbbs"\n@title "Contacting The Leaders"\n                           CONTACTING THE LEADERS\n                          ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n  You can contact the World Leaders and/or division leaders on these BBS''s.\n    People with a HQ in their country should adress themselves to that HQ.\n       If there isn''t a PTL BBS in your country, call the WHQ or a bbs\n                            in a country near you.\n\n    Fortress      (   PTL WHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-3-***.**.** (Zyxel 16.8)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-3-***.**.** (Vfast 28.8)\n\n    Bitch Board   (   PTL EHQ  ) Node 1 : +46-111-***.**  (USR   28.8)\n\n    Super Dancer  (   PTL HHQ  ) Node 1 : +31-570-***.*** (VFast 28.8)\n                                 Node 2 : +31-570-***.*** (USR   14.4)\n                                 Node 3 : +31-570-***.*** (USR   16.8)\n\n    Rhythm Nation (   PTL FHQ  ) Node 1 : +33-82-**.**.** (???   14.4)\n\n    Wizard Guild  (   PTL NHQ  ) Node 1 : +47-53-**.**.** (VFast 28.8)\n\n    Traders World (   PTL GHQ  ) Node 1 : +49-215-******* (VFast 28.8)\n@endnode\n\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',99906,3,0,NULL,NULL,'woa_tc11','scan',1780048679);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ptl_frd4','PTL-FRD4.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/PTL-FRD4.LHA','rpstart','XIM','RPSTaRT',NULL,NULL,'PTL','_\_________\_\_____  _____/ _\_  |_____ /      ______/   /      \w^s/     l     \ /_________|.cOLa./________\ /_____________\',replace('   ________/\  ______________  ___/|\n  _\_________\_\_____  _____/ _\_  |_____\n /      ______/   /      \w^s/     l     \\n/_________|.cOLa./________\ /_____________\\n::::::::::::::::::presents::::::::::::::::::\n::::::: Franky''s /X door collection 4 ::::::\n::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\n:::: Doors included in this archive are ::::\n::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\n::: Buy & Sell V 1.0   ASCII-Order V 1.0 :::\n:::           Piss-O-Rama V 2.2          :::\n::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\n','\n',char(10)),'4.1.guide','',NULL,'auto-added',128278,11,0,NULL,NULL,'woa_tc11','scan',1780048679);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ptl_frdc','PTL-FRDC.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/PTL-FRDC.LHA','rpstart','XIM','RPSTaRT',NULL,NULL,'PTL','_\_________\_\_____  _____/ _\_  |_____ /      ______/   /      \w^s/     l     \ /_________|.cOLa./________\ /_____________\',replace('   ________/\  ______________  ___/|\n  _\_________\_\_____  _____/ _\_  |_____\n /      ______/   /      \w^s/     l     \\n/_________|.cOLa./________\ /_____________\\n::::::::::::::::::presents::::::::::::::::::\n:::::: Franky''s /X door collection I :::::::\n::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\n::: In this archive are new versions of ::::\n:::::: the following great doors !!!! ::::::\n:: Piss-O-Rama  v2.0 -- Next-Message v1.0 ::\n:: Sysop-In ??? v3.0 -- ShowIt       v1.0 ::\n::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\n','\n',char(10)),'DOORS.Guide',replace('@database "Franky DOOR COLLECTION" v1.0 by FRaNKy/PTL"\n@author "FRaNKy/PTL & TFX/PTL"\n@(c) "Copyright © 1994 Purple Turtle"\n@$VER: NextMessage.Guide 1.0 (15 jan. 95)\n@node Main "Franky''s BIG door Collection by FRaNKy/PTL"\n\n            77:::::/\\_____/\\_   /\\/\\_____ /\\_____/\\__  /\\__ ___\n               7::/  \\  _ \\  Y\\/  \\ \\  _ Y  \\  _ \\  / /  \\ Y  /\n                7/     /  |\\ | \\   \\  /  :    /  |\\/ /     : /\n         _______/     /   :/ : /   / /   .   /   :/_/__ ____/______ __ _\n        |      /          /  ./   /_     /       //   /__/____    // ///\n        |_____/     |\\___/       / \\    <  |\\___//   / \\_/   /___//_///\n             /      |    \\      /  |\\    \\ |        /       /::\n             \\______|     \\  __/___| \\    \\|_______/_____  /::::...\n              -------------\\/---------\\    /-------------\\/--------\n                                       \\  /\n                                        \\/\n            /\\___ _____/\\   /\\  /\\_____/\\___ _____/\\/\\__  /\\__ ___\n            \\    Y      /Y\\/  \\/  \\  _  Y   Y      /   / /  \\ Y  /::::77\n             \\  /|  |  / | \\   \\/   /   :  /|  |  /   / /     : /::7\n     _ __ ____\\/ :  |_// : /   /   /    /\\/ :  |_/   /_/__ ____/_____\n     \\\\\\ \\\\    | .  | /  ./   /  _     /  |  . |    //   /__/____    |\n      \\\\\\_\\\\___|    |/       /   \\    <   |    |   //   / \\_/   /____|\n            .::|    |\\      /    |\\    \\  |    |       /       /\n        ...::::|____| \\  __/\\____| \\    \\_|____|______/_____  /\n          -------------\\/-----------\\    /----\\/-*-DiMeNsIon\\/\n                                     \\  /\n                                      \\/\n\n                           @{" NextMessage v1.0 " link "NEXTMES"}\n                           @{" Piss-O-Rama v2.0 " link "piss"}\n                           @{" ShowIt      v1.0 " link "SHOW"}\n                           @{" Sysop-In    v3.0 " link "SYSIN"}\n\n                            @{"*-* WaRnInG *-*" link "warn"}\n\n@endnode\n@node "NEXTMES"\n@title "NextMessage v1.0 by FRaNKy/PTL"\n\n                         NextMessage v1.0 by FRaNKy/PTL\n\n              @{" What is it ?   " link "WhatNM"}                 @{" PostCardWare   " link "PostCard"}\n              @{" Installation   " link "Install"}                 @{" Contacting PTL " link "Contact"}\n              @{" Credits        " link "Credits"}\n              @{" History        " link "history"}                 @{" * Important *  " link "Search"}\n\n@endnode\n@node "WhatNM"\n@title "What is this ?"\n\n  You''re probably all wondering: ''What the hell is this ?''\n\n              --==( Well to answer everyones questions )==--\n\n  NextMessage is a door written for Ami-Express v2.x, v3.x and v4.x\n\n  It ask the user online to leave a message to the next user(s) at\n  logoff and another small door is added to display the message during\n  logon...\n\n@endnode\n@node "Install"\n@title "Installing this door"\n\n\n                       NextMessage v1.0 by FRaNKy/PTL\n\n                  NextMessage consists of 2 separate doors..\n\n  NextMessage.Rexx is the main door\n  ShowMessage.Rexx is the displayer for the message\n\n  To run ShowMessage.Rexx you must add this line into your NodeX/bull.txt\n  (where X is the NodeNumber) "~CC_SM" and if you want (I prefer this) you\n  can also put a <PAUSE> command afterwards... Below are the special setups\n  for you Amix-verison..\n\n            @{" /X v2.xx " link "2.x"}            @{" /X v3.xx " link "3.x"}            @{" /X v4.xx " link "4.x"}\n\n\n\n@endnode\n@node "2.x"\n@Title "Installing it on Ami-Express v2.x"\n\n\nadd to your BBS.CMD\n\n*G        RM010Doors:NextMessage/NextMessage.Rexx\n          ^^^  ^_______________________________Put the correct path and\n          |||                                  filename over here\n          |||\n          |||__________________________________The acces level needed to\n          ||                                   use the door (I prefer 10)\n          ||\n          ||___________________________________M For Multi-Node usage\n          |\n          |____________________________________R for ARexx\n\n*SM       RM010Doors:NextMessage/ShowMessage.Rexx\n          ^^^  ^_______________________________Put the correct path and\n          |||                                  filename over here\n          |||\n          |||__________________________________The acces level needed to\n          ||                                   use the door (I prefer 10)\n          ||\n          ||___________________________________M For Multi-Node usage\n          |\n          |____________________________________R for ARexx\n\n\n@endnode\n@node "3.x"\n@title "Installing it on Ami-Express v3.x"\n\n   Just throw all the files in the directory they are in now.\n\n   Simple isn''t it ??\n\n@endnode\n@node "4.x"\n@title "Installing it on Ami-Express v4.x"\n\n   Just throw all the files in the directory they are in now.\n\n   Simple isn''t it ??\n\n@endnode\n@node "PostCard"\n@title "PostCardWare"\n\n\n                   NextMessage v1.0 is PostCardWare..\n                   Piss-O-Rama v2.0 is PostCardWare..\n                   ShowIt      v1.0 is PostCardWare..\n                   Sysop-In    v3.0 is PostCardWare..\n\n       If you use it, you are kindly asked to send a postcard of the\n        area/country/city you are living in to the adress below...\n\n  And this is almost no effort because it will cost you shit, you can even\n               ask your mummy for a stamp and a postcard...\n\n                            The adress:\n                            ----------------------\n                            Peter Smets\n                            Weldadigheidsstraat 45\n                            B-3000 Leuven\n                            Belgium\n\n@endnode\n@node "Contact"\n@title "Why don''t you give these boards a call ???"\n\n                   !  Call one of our Bulletin Board Systems !\n\n                              +-B-E-L-G-I-U-M-+\n\n                   Fortress (WHQ)             +32-(3)-829.08.72\n                   Sysop: TFX                 +32-(3)-825.00.69\n\n                   Enigma                     +32-(89)-73.20.54\n                   Sysop: Damien\n\n                              +-H-O-L-L-A-N-D-+\n\n                   Taj Mahal                  +31-162 322 716\n                   Sysop: Hi-TeCH\n\n@endnode\n@node "Search"\n@title "PTL is searching for..."\n\n                  _______   ______   _________    ______\n                 /  ____.\\  \\    .\\ /  ____.\\|   / ____/\n                 \\  \\__/ /|\\/   | \\\\\\  \\__/ /|__/   _)_\n       :  /      / _____/_| \\  __ _// _____/ |  \\  |  .\\     \\  :\n       | /      /  \\ /       \\  |  \\  \\  \\       )     /      \\ |\n      \\|/       \\___\\\\_______/_/|__/__/   \\_____/\\____/        \\|/\n  - --[T]-- -   ________     ______ ___________    ______  - --[G]-- -\n      /|\\      / _    _ \\    \\    .\\ _    _ \\ |   / ____/      /|\\\n     / |       \\/ \\  / \\/| |\\/   | \\\\ \\  / \\/ |__/   _)_        | \\\n    /  :          /  \\ / |_| \\  __ _/ /  \\/   |  \\  |  .\\       :  \\\n       .         /    \\       \\  |  \\/    \\       )     /       .\n                 \\ ___/_______/_/|__/\\____/\\_____/\\___ /\n                  \\|                                 |/\n\n       Is looking for some ''Coders (ASM,C,Etc..)'' Gfx Artist and\n       musicians, if you think you are the guy (girl) then boogie\n       you way up to our WHQ or send your NetMails to :\n\n       TFX (Worl Leader)        : 2:292/8010.14\n       FRaNKY (Co-World Leader) : 2:292/8010.32\n                                  2:292/622.13\n\n       Or send a letter to FRaNKy (adress is in the Postcardware dept.)\n@endnode\n@node "history"\n@title "Memories...."\n\n     v0.1ß - v0.9ß * Internal ßeta releases (Thank God!!!)\n\n             v1.0  * Worldwide Release\n\n@endnode\n@node "Credits"\n@title "The always unforgetable credits !!!"\n\n          This AIM-type /X door was written by FRaNKy/PTL\n\n          This AmigaGuide docfile was written by FRaNKY/PTL\n          Based upon a *nice* AmigaGuide docfile by TFX/PTL\n\n         Greetings: To al our contact and friends in the Scene.\n\n@endnode\n@node "PISS"\n@title "Piss-O-Rama v2.0 by FRaNKy/PTL"\n\n                       Piss-O-Rama v2.0 by FRaNKy/PTL\n\n              @{" What is it ?   " link "WhatP"}                 @{" PostCardWare   " link "PostCard"}\n              @{" Installation   " link "InstallP"}                 @{" Contacting PTL " link "Contact"}\n              @{" Options        " link "Options"}\n              @{" History        " link "historyP"}                 @{" * Important *  " link "Search"}\n\n@endnode\n@node "WhatP"\n@title "What is this ?"\n\n  You''re probably all wondering: ''What the hell is this ?''\n                                 ''Why does it have such a silly name ?''\n\n              --==( Well to answer everyones questions )==--\n\n  Piss-O-Rama is a doorgame written for Ami-Express v2.x, v3.x and v4.x\n\n  The objective of this game is to piss as far as you can by deviding 50\n  points over 4 different different things like...\n\n                    * Nr of beers you drank...\n                    * Your will power...\n                    * The strength of your arm...\n                    * And your .. dick size...\n\n  As soon as you devided them just piss and see how far you can do it...\n\n@endnode\n@node "InstallP"\n@title "Installing this nice doorgame"\n\n\n            77:::::/\\_____/\\_   /\\/\\_____ /\\_____/\\__  /\\__ ___\n               7::/  \\  _ \\  Y\\/  \\ \\  _ Y  \\  _ \\  / /  \\ Y  /\n                7/     /  |\\ | \\   \\  /  :    /  |\\/ /     : /\n         _______/     /   :/ : /   / /   .   /   :/_/__ ____/______ __ _\n        |      /          /  ./   /_     /       //   /__/____    // ///\n        |_____/     |\\___/       / \\    <  |\\___//   / \\_/   /___//_///\n             /      |    \\      /  |\\    \\ |        /       /::\n             \\______|     \\  __/___| \\    \\|_______/_____  /::::...\n              -------------\\/---------\\    /-------------\\/--------\n                                       \\  /\n                                        \\/\n            /\\___ _____/\\   /\\  /\\_____/\\___ _____/\\/\\__  /\\__ ___\n            \\    Y      /Y\\/  \\/  \\  _  Y   Y      /   / /  \\ Y  /::::77\n             \\  /|  |  / | \\   \\/   /   :  /|  |  /   / /     : /::7\n     _ __ ____\\/ :  |_// : /   /   /    /\\/ :  |_/   /_/__ ____/_____\n     \\\\\\ \\\\    | .  | /  ./   /  _     /  |  . |    //   /__/____    |\n      \\\\\\_\\\\___|    |/       /   \\    <   |    |   //   / \\_/   /____|\n            .::|    |\\      /    |\\    \\  |    |       /       /\n        ...::::|____| \\  __/\\____| \\    \\_|____|______/_____  /\n          -------------\\/-----------\\    /----\\/-*-DiMeNsIon\\/\n                                     \\  /\n                                      \\/\n\n                       Piss-O-Rama v2.0 by FRaNKy/PTL\n\n                      @{" /X v3.xx " link "3.x"}            @{" /X v4.xx " link "4.x"}\n\n\n\n@endnode\n@node "3.x"\n@title "Installing it on Ami-Express v3.x"\n\n   Just throw all the files in the directory they are in now.\n\n   Simple isn''t it ??\n\n@endnode\n@node "4.x"\n@title "Installing it on Ami-Express v4.x"\n\n   Just throw all the files in the directory they are in now.\n\n   Simple isn''t it ??\n\n@endnode\n@node "Options"\n@title "What should I do with this file: ... DOORS:Piss/Piss.cfg"\n\n Question : What should I do with this file: ... DOORS:Piss/Piss.cfg ???\n\n Answer: Ahhh.. I thought you''d never ask...\n\n     Well guys, it''s a very simple...\n\n    Line 1 : PassWord needed to reset the HighScore...\n    Line 2 : Person allowed to reset the HighScore...\n    Line 3 : Person allowed to reset the HighScore...\n    Line 4 : .....\n\n@endnode\n@node "historyP"\n@title "Memories...."\n\n     v0.1ß - v0.9ß   Internal ßeta releases (Thank God!!!)\n\n             v1.0    PTL only release...\n\n             v1.1  * Argh, fixed a bug that accoured when trying to play\n                     the game again without leaving the door first...\n                   * The distance you pissed had to 6 numbers behind the\n                     decimal point, changed this to 2.\n                   * Released it worldwide...\n\n             V2.0  * Added a highscore-table\n                   * Added a moon status\n                   * Added more randomly picked numbers\n                   * Reset password is no longer visible\n                   * When you have a 255 level but your name isn''t in the\n                     Piss.Cfg you won''t have a message anymore and go\n                     directly to the main menu\n\n@endnode\n@node "show"\n@title "ShowIt v1.0 by FRaNKy/PTL"\n\n                             ShowIt v1.0 by FRaNKy/PTL\n\n              @{" What is it ?   " link "WhatS"}                 @{" PostCardWare   " link "PostCard"}\n              @{" Installation   " link "InstallS"}                 @{" Contacting PTL " link "Contact"}\n              @{" Credits        " link "Credits"}\n              @{" History        " link "historyS"}                 @{" * Important *  " link "Search"}\n\n@endnode\n@node "historyS"\n@title "Memories...."\n\n     v0.1ß - v0.9ß * Internal ßeta releases (Thank God!!!)\n\n             v1.0  * Worldwide Release\n\n@endnode\n@node "WhatS"\n@title "What is this ?"\n\n  You''re probably all wondering: ''What the hell is this ?''\n\n              --==( Well to answer everyones questions )==--\n\n        ShowIt shows the contents of an ASCII file on the screen...\n                             (nuff said eh ?)\n\n\n@endnode\n@node "InstallS"\n@title "Installing this door"\n\n\n            77:::::/\\_____/\\_   /\\/\\_____ /\\_____/\\__  /\\__ ___\n               7::/  \\  _ \\  Y\\/  \\ \\  _ Y  \\  _ \\  / /  \\ Y  /\n                7/     /  |\\ | \\   \\  /  :    /  |\\/ /     : /\n         _______/     /   :/ : /   / /   .   /   :/_/__ ____/______ __ _\n        |      /          /  ./   /_     /       //   /__/____    // ///\n        |_____/     |\\___/       / \\    <  |\\___//   / \\_/   /___//_///\n             /      |    \\      /  |\\    \\ |        /       /::\n             \\______|     \\  __/___| \\    \\|_______/_____  /::::...\n              -------------\\/---------\\    /-------------\\/--------\n                                       \\  /\n                                        \\/\n            /\\___ _____/\\   /\\  /\\_____/\\___ _____/\\/\\__  /\\__ ___\n            \\    Y      /Y\\/  \\/  \\  _  Y   Y      /   / /  \\ Y  /::::77\n             \\  /|  |  / | \\   \\/   /   :  /|  |  /   / /     : /::7\n     _ __ ____\\/ :  |_// : /   /   /    /\\/ :  |_/   /_/__ ____/_____\n     \\\\\\ \\\\    | .  | /  ./   /  _     /  |  . |    //   /__/____    |\n      \\\\\\_\\\\___|    |/       /   \\    <   |    |   //   / \\_/   /____|\n            .::|    |\\      /    |\\    \\  |    |       /       /\n        ...::::|____| \\  __/\\____| \\    \\_|____|______/_____  /\n          -------------\\/-----------\\    /----\\/-*-DiMeNsIon\\/\n                                     \\  /\n                                      \\/\n\n                            ShowIt v1.0 by FRaNKy/PTL\n\n\n            @{" /X v2.xx " link "2.xS"}            @{" /X v3.xx " link "3.x"}            @{" /X v4.xx " link "4.x"}\n\n\n\n@endnode\n@node "2.xS"\n@Title "Installing it on Ami-Express v2.xS"\n\nadd to your BBS.CMD\n\n*SHOW     RM255Doors:ShowIt/ShowIt.Rexx\n          ^^^  ^_______________________________Put the correct path and\n          |||                                  filename over here\n          |||\n          |||__________________________________The acces level needed to\n          ||                                   use the door (I prefer 255)\n          ||\n          ||___________________________________M For Multi-Node usage\n          |\n          |____________________________________R for ARexx\n\n@endnode\n@node "sysin"\n@title "Sysop-In v3.0 by FRaNKy/PTL"\n\n                           Sysop-In v3.0 by FRaNKy/PTL\n\n              @{" What is it ?   " link "Whati"}                 @{" PostCardWare   " link "PostCard"}\n              @{" Installation   " link "Installi"}                 @{" Contacting PTL " link "Contact"}\n              @{" Credits        " link "Credits"}\n              @{" History        " link "historyi"}                 @{" * Important *  " link "Search"}\n\n@endnode\n@node "whati"\n\n  You''re probably all wondering: ''What the hell is this ?''\n\n              --==( Well to answer everyones questions )==--\n\n A little door that shows the user if the Sysop is available for chatting...\n\n It can save time for long-distance callers and guys in a hurry because you\n   don''t have to find out that the Sysop-Page is turned off by paging the\n   sysop... \n\n  And it can also be added to the logon-sequence wich is always in handy....\n\n@endnode\n@node "historyi"\n\n     v0.1ß - v0.9ß * Internal ßeta releases (Thank God!!!)\n\n             v3.0  * First PTL release... Sorry Reflex 8-))...\n                   * Optimized the code a lot !!!\n\n@endnode\n@Node "installi"\n\n            77:::::/\\_____/\\_   /\\/\\_____ /\\_____/\\__  /\\__ ___\n               7::/  \\  _ \\  Y\\/  \\ \\  _ Y  \\  _ \\  / /  \\ Y  /\n                7/     /  |\\ | \\   \\  /  :    /  |\\/ /     : /\n         _______/     /   :/ : /   / /   .   /   :/_/__ ____/______ __ _\n        |      /          /  ./   /_     /       //   /__/____    // ///\n        |_____/     |\\___/       / \\    <  |\\___//   / \\_/   /___//_///\n             /      |    \\      /  |\\    \\ |        /       /::\n             \\______|     \\  __/___| \\    \\|_______/_____  /::::...\n              -------------\\/---------\\    /-------------\\/--------\n                                       \\  /\n                                        \\/\n            /\\___ _____/\\   /\\  /\\_____/\\___ _____/\\/\\__  /\\__ ___\n            \\    Y      /Y\\/  \\/  \\  _  Y   Y      /   / /  \\ Y  /::::77\n             \\  /|  |  / | \\   \\/   /   :  /|  |  /   / /     : /::7\n     _ __ ____\\/ :  |_// : /   /   /    /\\/ :  |_/   /_/__ ____/_____\n     \\\\\\ \\\\    | .  | /  ./   /  _     /  |  . |    //   /__/____    |\n      \\\\\\_\\\\___|    |/       /   \\    <   |    |   //   / \\_/   /____|\n            .::|    |\\      /    |\\    \\  |    |       /       /\n        ...::::|____| \\  __/\\____| \\    \\_|____|______/_____  /\n          -------------\\/-----------\\    /----\\/-*-DiMeNsIon\\/\n                                     \\  /\n                                      \\/\n\n                          Sysop-In v3.0 by FRaNKy/PTL\n\n\n            @{" /X v2.xx " link "2.xi"}            @{" /X v3.xx " link "3.x"}            @{" /X v4.xx " link "4.x"}\n\n\n                 And if you want to add it to the logon sequence\n               add to your NodeX/bull.txt:  (X is the Nodenumber)\n\n--- cut ---\n~CC_SI\n--- cut ---\n\n@endnode\n@node "2.xi"\n\nTo use it just put it in BBS:Doors/SysopIn/\nor any other dir you wish to put it...\n\nand add to your BBS.CMD\n\n*SI       RM010Doors:SysopIn/SysopIn.rexx\n          ^^^  ^_______________________________Put the correct path and\n          |||                                  filename over here\n          |||\n          |||__________________________________The acces level needed to\n          ||                                   use the door (I prefer 10)\n          ||\n          ||___________________________________M For Multi-Node usage\n          |\n          |____________________________________R for ARexx\n\n@endnode\n@node "warn"\n@title "Warning about the new doors..."\n\n  For security purposes (''coz there are a lot of LAMERS out there) I\n  compiled the doors in to executable Arexx files...\n\n  Because of this it might be possible that the doors don''t work on your\n  computer system (blame /X stupid rexxport for that)...  So if you install\n  the doors, test them yourself first to see that they work with your compie\n\n             But IF it works, they will WORK 3x FASTER !!!!!!\n\n  -FRaNKy- PuRPLe TuRTLe Co-WoRLD LEADER\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',110969,1,0,NULL,NULL,'woa_tc11','scan',1780048679);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ptl_rt11','PTL_RT11.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/PTL_RT11.LHA','rpstart','XIM','reset.rexx',NULL,NULL,'PTL','_\_________\_\_____  _____/ _\_  |_____ /      ______/   /      \w^s/     l     \ /_________|.cOLa./________\ /_____________\',replace('   ________/\  ______________  ___/|\n  _\_________\_\_____  _____/ _\_  |_____\n /      ______/   /      \w^s/     l     \\n/_________|.cOLa./________\ /_____________\\n::::::::::::::::::presents::::::::::::::::::\n::::::::::: FRaNKy''s Reset V 1.1 :::::::::::\n::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\n:::::: Allows users to reset the bbs :::::::\n:::::: Handy when for when the sysop :::::::\n::::::       is not at home          :::::::\n::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\n','\n',char(10)),'Reset.Guide',replace('@database "FRaNKy''s Reset V 1.1"\n@font topaz.font 8\n@author "FRaNKy/PTL"\n@(c) "Copyright © 1995 FRaNKy / Purple Turtle"\n@$VER: Reset.Guide V1.01  (22/10/95)\n@node Main "FRaNKy''s Reset V 1.1 - Main Menu"\n        FRaNKy''s Reset V 1.1 - Copyright 1995 FRaNKy / Purple Turtle\n¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n       Important!            Contacting The Author           The Door\n      ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯          ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯         ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n  @{"     Disclaimer      " link "disc"}    @{"   Bulletin Boards   " link "Fbss"}    @{"     What Is It ?    " link "what"}\n  @{"   Compiled Doors    " link "comp"}    @{"       FidoNet       " link "Ffido"}    @{"     Installation    " link "inst"}\n  @{"    PostCardWare     " link "post"}    @{"      InterNet       " link "Finter"}    @{"     Config File     " link "conf"}\n                                                      @{"  Credits & Hellos   " link "cred"}\n     ________/\  ______________  ___/|                @{"       History       " link "hist"}\n    _\_________\_\_____  _____/ _\_  |_____           @{"    The Story Off    " link "stor"}\n   /      ______/   /      \w^s/     l     \\n  /_________|.cOLa./________\ /_____________\             Contacting PTL\n  ::::::::::::::::::presents::::::::::::::::::           ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n  ::::::::::: FRaNKy''s Reset V 1.1 :::::::::::        @{"        BBS''s        " link "pbbs"}\n  ::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::        @{"       FidoNet       " link "pfido"}\n  :::::: Allows users to reset the bbs :::::::        @{"      Internet       " link "pinter"}\n  :::::: Handy when for when the sysop :::::::\n  ::::::       is not at home          :::::::        @{" Looking For Members " link "memb"}\n  ::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\n@endnode\n@node "disc"\n@title "Disclaimer"\n                                DISCLAIMER\n                               ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n     This software is "AS IS", the author can not be held responsible for\n    any damage caused to your system by this software, or the consequences\n                               of this damage...\n\n                    To say it simply : Use at your own risk !\n@endnode\n@node "post"\n@title "PostCardWare"\n                               POSTCARDWARE\n                              ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n           All the doors included in this archive are PostCardWare\n      If you use one of included doors, you are kindly asked to send a\n                    postcard of the area you live in to :\n\n                          Peter Smets (FRaNKy / PTL)\n                          Weldadigheidsstraat 45\n                          3000 Leuven\n                          Belgium\n\n             Postcards received so far : Lady An      [   UK   ]\n                                         Killer Dwarf [ Sweden ]\n@endnode\n@node "comp"\n@title "Compiled Doors"\n                               COMPILED DOORS\n                              ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n  All doors in this archive are compiled using the RexxPlus Arexx Compiler.\n\n     To get the doors to work on you /X system, you must run RPStart and\n       have the libraries included in the archive copied to your LIBS:\n  It is advisable to put RPStart in you User-Startup so you won''t forget it\n\n   If you would like a copy of the uncompiled sources of the doors included\n      in this archive, send 1500 BEF (50 USD) to the author of the doors.\n           Cash money (no coins) or EuroCheque in BEF only please.\n\n  This can be a large amount of money, but if you see what money I spend in\n   my doors (time, phonecalls) and if you really want the sources to study\n                       them, this isn''t too much I think...\n\n        The adress where you can send the money to can be found under\n                              @{"postcardware" link "post"} button...\n\nNote :\n\n Compiled doors do not work on all systems (blame the /X RexxPort for this)\n                   but the advantage for me is much greater.\n\n  I decided to do this compilation of my doors because I noticed that more\n    and more people started using pieces of my doors, or sometimes just\n    renaming the door and then releasing it under their own name/group.\n            If you want you can buy the sources as staded above.\n\n                                                                    FRaNKy.\n@endnode\n@node "what"\n@title "FRaNKy''s Reset V 1.1 - What is it ?"\n                                WHAT IS IT ?\n                               ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\nReset allows a user to reset the bbs online, this is hand for when one\nnode hangs. A user with access to the door can then reset the bbs-\ncomputer.\n\nIf for some reason the BBS may not be resetted (Sysop is doing a VBS\nor so) the door can be @{"locked" link "lock"} so the computer will not reset.\n\n@endnode\n@node "inst"\n@title "FRaNKy''s Reset V 1.1 - Installation"\n                                INSTALLATION\n                               ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\nPut the files Reset.#? in Doors:PTL/Reset/ to get everything working.\nThe icon Reset.Info (rename it to whatever what you like) has to be placed\nin BBS:Commands/BBSCmd/.\n\n@endnode\n@node "conf"\n@title "FRaNKy''s Reset V 1.1 - Config File"\n                                CONFIGURATION\n                               ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\nThe file Doors:PTL/Reset/Reset.Cfg has to be edited like this :\n\nLine 1 : Reset Password\nLine 2 : User that can reset the BBS\nLine 3 : User that can reset the BBS\nLine 4 : ...\n\nExample :\n\n--- cut ---\nsuperimperialstardestroyer\nDa Cool One\nDa Ultra Cool One\n--- cut ---\n@endnode\n@node "cred"\n@title "FRaNKy''s Reset V 1.1 - Credits"\n                                   CREDITS\n                                  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                             Coding       : FRaNKy\n                             Docs         : FRaNKy\n                             Idea         : TFX\n                             Nagging      : TFX\n                             Beta Testing : TFX\n\n                                  GREETINGS\n                                 ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\nHello''s & Greetings from FRaNKy fly out to : All PTL members and\nmy friends out there, you know who you are.\n\n@endnode\n@node "hist"\n@title "FRaNKy''s Reset V 1.1 - History"\n                                    HISTORY\n                                   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                 ... - 0.9  : Internal Beta Releases\n                       1.0  : Internal Release\n                       1.1  : - First WorldWide Release\n                              - Now asks for a reason why the BBS will\n                                be resetted\n                              - The door can be @{"''locked''" link "lock"} so the computer\n                                cannot be resetted\n@endnode\n@node "stor"\n@title "FRaNKy''s Reset V 1.1 - The Story Off"\n                                 THE STORY OFF\n                                ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\nTFX asked me to do a reset door.. It was something he needed for his BBS\nand I made it quite quickly...\n\nLater on he wanted a reason why the bbs was resetted and also the ability\nto lock the door, wich I both added.\n\n@endnode\n@node "lock"\n@title "Locking and Unlocking the door"\n                            LOCKING & UNLOCKING\n                           ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n\nTo lock and unlock the door, start the Rexx-Script LOCK.REXX by\ntyping in shell\n\n''RX Doors:PTL/Reset/Lock.Rexx''\n\nThe program will detect if the door is locked or not and will then ask\nyou if you want to Lock/Unlock the door.\n\nWARING !\n--------\n\nDO *NOT* START THIS DOOR FROM WITHIN AMI-EXPRESS !\n\n@endnode\n@node "Fbss"\n@title "Contacting The Author On The PTL BBS''s"\n                            CONTACTING THE AUTHOR\n                           ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n   The Author of the door can be contacted on these Purple Turtle BBS''s\n\n    Fortress      (   PTL WHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-3-***.**.** (Zyxel 16.8)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-3-***.**.** (Vfast 28.8)\n\n    Bitch Board   (   PTL EHQ  ) Node 1 : +46-11-**.**.** (USR   28.8)\n\n    Enigma        (   PTL BHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-89-**.**.** (USR   16.8)\n\n    Secret Cinema (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +32-52-**.**.** (VFast 33.6)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-52-RINGDOWN (VFast 33.6)\n\n    Cyber Garden  (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +32-11-**.**.** (USR   16.8)\n\n    Rhythm Nation (   PTL FHQ  ) Node 1 : +33-82-**.**.** (???   14.4)\n@endnode\n@node "FFido"\n@title "Contacting The Author Through FidoNet"\n                            CONTACTING THE AUTHOR\n                           ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    The Author of the doors included in this archive can be contacted by\n               sendin a Netmail to one of these point-numbers\n\n                                2:292/622.13\n\n@endnode\n@node "finter"\n@title "Contacting The Author Through Internet"\n                            CONTACTING THE AUTHOR\n                           ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                            Send your E-Mails to:\n\n                             [email removed]\n\n                     IRC-fans can try to join the channel\n\n                                    #PTL\n\n                         If I''m online, I''ll be there.\n\n@endnode\n@node "Pbbs"\n@title "Purpe Turtle BBS''s"\n                             PURPLE TURTLE BBS''S\n                            ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                                   BELGIUM\n                                  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Fortress      (   PTL WHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-3-***.**.** (Zyxel 16.8)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-3-***.**.** (Vfast 28.8)\n\n    Enigma        (   PTL BHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-89-**.**.** (USR   16.8)\n\n    Secret Cinema (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +32-52-**.**.** (VFast 33.6)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-52-RINGDOWN (VFast 33.6)\n\n    Cyber Garden  (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +32-11-**.**.** (USR   16.8)\n\n                                   HOLLAND\n                                  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Super Dancer  (   PTL HHQ  ) Node 1 : +31-570-***.*** (VFast 28.8)\n                                 Node 2 : +31-570-***.*** (USR   14.4)\n                                 Node 3 : +31-570-***.**8 (USR   16.8)\n\n                                    SWEDEN\n                                   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Bitch Board   (   PTL EHQ  ) Node 1 : +46-111-***.**  (USR   28.8)\n\n    Inferno       (   PTL SHQ  ) Node 1 : +46-øPRIVATE!ø  (USR   33.6)\n\n    rIVER wILD    (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +46-612-***.**  (USR   28.8)\n\n\n                                    FRANCE\n                                   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Rhythm Nation (   PTL FHQ  ) Node 1 : +33-82-**.**.** (???   14.4)\n\n                                    NORWAY\n                                   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Wizard Guild  (   PTL NHQ  ) Node 1 : +47-53-**.**.** (VFast 28.8)\n\n                                   GERMANY\n                                  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Traders World (   PTL GHQ  ) Node 1 : +49-215-******* (VFast 28.8)\n@endnode\n@node "PFido"\n@title "Purple Turtle FidoNet Adresses"\n                        PURPLE TURTLE FIDONET ADRESSES\n                       ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                  TFX      (  World Leader )   2:292/8010.14\n                  FRaNKy   (Co-World Leader)   2:292/622.13\n@endnode\n@node "pinter"\n@title "Purple Turtle On The Net"\n                          PURPLE TURTLE ON THE NET\n                         ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                The Purple Turtle homepage can be visited at :\n\n                    http://www.ping.be/~ping2045/ptl.html\n\n                    You can also send E-Mails to FRaNKy at :\n\n                              [email removed]\n\n                         Or join the IRC-Channel #PTL\n@endnode\n@node "memb"\n@title "Purple Turtle Is Always Looking For New Members"\n                           LOOKING FOR NEW MEMBERS\n                          ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n  If you think you are the right guy (girl) for a cool group and you can do\n  some Coding (ASM-C-Arexx-...), Music, Graphics, Trading, Swapping or have\n      a BBS, then contact the Purple Turtle Leaders or Division Leaders\n                   for a certain reply on one of our HQ''s.\n\n   If you want to join with your BBS, we do not ask any donations for your\n    membership (in another way : it''s free !).  BBS''s outside Belgium are\n                              extremely welcome...\n\n        @{" Bulletin Boards " link "lbbs"}   @{"     FidoNet     " link "PFido"}   @{"    InterNet    " link "pinter"}\n@endnode\n@node "lbbs"\n@title "Contacting The Leaders"\n                           CONTACTING THE LEADERS\n                          ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n  You can contact the World Leaders and/or division leaders on these BBS''s.\n    People with a HQ in their country should adress themselves to that HQ.\n       If there isn''t a PTL BBS in your country, call the WHQ or a bbs\n                            in a country near you.\n\n    Fortress      (   PTL WHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-3-***.**.** (Zyxel 16.8)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-3-***.**.** (Vfast 28.8)\n\n    Bitch Board   (   PTL EHQ  ) Node 1 : +46-111-***.**  (USR   28.8)\n\n    Super Dancer  (   PTL HHQ  ) Node 1 : +31-570-***-*** (VFast 28.8)\n                                 Node 2 : +31-570-***.*** (USR   14.4)\n                                 Node 3 : +31-570-***.*** (USR   16.8)\n\n    Rhythm Nation (   PTL FHQ  ) Node 1 : +33-82-**.**.** (???   14.4)\n\n    Wizard Guild  (   PTL NHQ  ) Node 1 : +47-53-**.**.** (VFast 28.8)\n\n    Traders World (   PTL GHQ  ) Node 1 : +49-215-******* (VFast 28.8)\n@endnode\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',104809,5,0,NULL,NULL,'ptl_rt11','scan',1780048679);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ptl_si06','PTL-SI06.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/PTL-SI06.LHA','CREATESENT','XIM','CREATESENT',NULL,NULL,'PTL','_ ____________  _ /  _____ _     _______ _ /        _/  //     \/ /      / PreSents /   __________/       \       /_______',replace(' _ ______________________________________ _\n_ ____________  _ /  _____ _     _______ _\n   /        _/  //     \/ /      / PreSents\n  /   __________/       \       /_______\n /______ /   \ __________\____________ /\n[«-----\/-----\/---------------------\/--»]\n       STRIP_ID v1.06 & SENT v1.08\n[«---------------------------------------»]\n   FULL FileId & AutoSent Replacement !!\n   Strips ''BBS_ADDS'' out of any FILE_ID.\n####--------- ### MEN-TEL BBS ###-------####\n','\n',char(10)),'STRIP_ID.GUIDE',replace('@database STRIP_ID.guide\n\n@node Main "STRIP_ID v1.05 - Contents"\n                                                                             \n STRIP_ID v1.05 (C) 1994 ZiA [- PtL^D2 -]\n FILE_ID.DIZ door for Ami-Express 3.2x & ZX 2.4x.\n\n @{"SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS         " LINK ID01} STRIP_ID is a FILEID replacement as SENT\n @{"INSTALLING STRIP_ID         " LINK ID02} is an AUTOSENT replacement. STRIP_ID \n @{"INSTALLING SENT             " LINK ID03} offers you the options of preventing\n @{"CREATING THE SENT.DATA      " LINK ID04} certain lines to show up in your file-\n @{"STRIPPING LINES             " LINK ID05} listing and being packed into a FILE_ID.DIZ\n @{"NOTES WORTHY TO MENTION     " LINK ID06} Also users can now decide how STRIP_ID must \n @{"CONTACTING ME               " LINK ID07} operate: Allow a him to abort a description,\n @{"BUGS, HISTORY               " LINK ID09} only show him the description or only show\n                              that an ID is found.\n\n@endnode  \n\n@node ID09 ""\n\nMain History:\n\nv1.00z - Initial ZX door.\n       - Bugs all over it... ( it''s better to speak about 1 bug: STRIP_ID ;).\n\nv1.01i - Changed main ''sendmessage'' routine from specific ZX to common /X \n         routine.\n       - Contains countdown and a stripper ( that didn''t work ;( ).\n\nv1.02i - First version to run on AE 3.xx . It DID work! well.. sort of..;)\n       - Installed the external user.sent file. \n       - SENT door included.\n       - STRIP_ID is now depending on the sent.data for its info.\n\nv1.03i - SENT did hang sometimes at the Enter SentbyLine prompt.\n       - Stopped using any SAS/C optimizers and headers.\n       - The Stripper didn''t strip correct ( = AT ALL :), Fixed!\n       - STRIP_ID CAN''T be made resident. Still ''outcoding'' this ''bug''.\n       - STRIP_ID checks for incorrect descriptions starting with RZ,rz,B0.\n       - Rewrote the load/save data option. Now uses the slotnr to find a user.\n         CREATESENT utiltiy required to run..       \n       - STRIP_ID now creates a temporary file in your T: directory that\n         contains the userinfo.\n\nv1.04i - STRIP_ID and /X don''t run synchronized, this causes STRIP_ID to\n         process other files than /X expects, not fatal, but VERRY anoying.\n         *SHOULD* be fixed. tested with SAS/C v6.50 ( 5 disks & ran perfect!)\n       - If 2 files with no desc are uploaded STRIP_ID would find the fileid\n         from file1 as FILE_ID.DIZ for file2. Fixed.\n       - SENT completely rewritten.\n       - STRIP_ID also ( slow sunday ;)\n       - Rewritten the striproutine (again). bout 10% slower.. but works on \n         68000/010 now..\n       - (Pause)...More(y/n/ns) Removed!. A user can now countdown from \n         + whatever to 0 without this prompt.\n       - Scratched the ''linewrapper'' of sendmessage. It didn''t do anything so\n         why wast time.\n       - Both STRIP_ID and SENT are re-entrant....(Yes!)...\n       - Fixed some serious ''stripreturn'' bugs.\n       - Limited the timeout to 15 secs, any ass who needs more should \n         think of buying a pc.\n\nv1.05  - STRIP_ID would write an empty line under a centered sentby line.\n         ( WOULD! )...\n       - Rewritten the date routine. The old one didn''t like to be resident..\n       - Improved center routine.\n       - Long list of stupid little annoying ''bugs'' removed       \n       - STRIP_ID now checks for the <CTRL>-m character (IBM) and strips it\n        \nv1.06  - Cleaned up the script routine. \n       - We now check if a user is online whenever prompting for a description  \n         input.\n       - SENT didn''t free it''s memory when it couldn''t ''Register''.\n       - Fixed $VER bugs ( just for hi-tech ;)\n\n       - >> RELEASE VERSIONS : STRIP_ID v1.05\n                                   SENT v1.07\n\n                       \n@endnode\n\n@node ID01 "System Requirements for STRIP_ID."\n\n STRIP_ID requires :\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n - An Amiga Running OS 2.x/3.x.\n - A Fully Installed AE 3.xx / ZX 2.4x.\n - Any Kind of archive utilities ( eg LHA, ZIP, ARJ ).\n - The Mystic Extractors/Adders for DMS, TXT and EXE Files.\n - Uploads ;)\n\n Archive Contents :\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n FILE                                PURPOSE\n ----------------------------------- ----------------------------------------\n BBS/COMMANDS/*.*                    /X and ZX commands\n BBS/FILEID/<ext>                    Scripts for STRIP_ID \n BBS/UTILS/CREATESENT        (2100)  Utility to create the Sent.Data\n BBS/DOORS/STRIP_ID/SENT     (8720)  The ''SENT'' door.\n BBS/DOORS/STRIP_ID/STRIP_ID (13612) The ''STRIP_ID'' door.\n BBS/DOORS/STRIP_ID/STRIP_ID.GUIDE   Read on...\n ----------------------------------- ----------------------------------------\n@endnode\n\n@node ID03 "Installing the SENT door"\n\n 1. Copy the ''SENT" door to your BBS:DOORS/STRIP_ID/SENT. ( Or Any Location\n    you wish to, but we assume this location. ).\n \n 2. For 3.xx : Copy All icons in the BBSCMD/ directory to your \n               BBS:COMMANDS/BBSCMD/ directory\n               \n    For ZX   : Add the following lines to your BBS.CMD file.\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n *SENT     XM005BBS:DOORS/STRIP_ID/SENT\n *FINDSENT XM005BBS:DOORS/STRIP_ID/SENT\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n \n 3. If you want you can install the ''FINDSENT'' in a bull.txt using the\n    MCI Command ''~CC_FINDSENT'' in that bulltxt. This is not required as\n    STRIP_ID automaticly notifies the user when he has no sentbyline.\n \n 4. @{"RESIDENT INSTALLATION " LINK ID10} of SENT\n 5. @{"CREATING THE SENT.DATA" LINK ID04} for SENT and STRIP_ID\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID02 "Installing STRIP_ID"\n\n 1. Copy the program to a directory where you would like it ( We assume that\n    STRIP_ID is placed in the BBS:Doors/strip_id/ directory).\n \n 2. Copy the FileId/ Directory to your BBSLocation.\n		\n 3. For /X 3.2x: Copy the EXAMINE.INFO to your BBS:COMMANDS/SYSCMD/ Directory\n                 And modify all paths to your needs.\n                 \n    For ZX 2.4x: Add the following line to your SYS.CMD file:\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n *EXAMINE  XM005BBS:DOORS/STRIP_ID/STRIP_ID\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n                 And disable the internal SENTBY.  \n                 -NOTIFY: your users to use SENT to edit their sentbyline and\n                 not the ''W'' command.\n\n 4. STRIP_ID doesn''t use ''Tooltypes'' for its info. Instead it uses a script\n    for it''s external command-line. \n    LHA Example script:\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n ADDFILE_ID C:LHA A @F @WFILE_ID.DIZ\n DELFILE_ID C:LHA D @F FILE_ID.DIZ\n EXTFILE_ID C:LHA E @F FILE_ID.DIZ @W\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n\n  STRIP_ID v1.06         FileID v1.5         Purpose\n ---------------------  ------------------- -------------------------------\n    @F                     @P               -  Symbol for the file that \n                                               Contains the FILE_ID.DIZ\n    @W                     @W               -  Symbol for Node<x>/Work/\n                                               Directory.   \n\n ADDFILE_ID - CommandLine for Adding a FILE_ID.DIZ.\n DELFILE_ID - CommandLine for Deleting a FILE_ID.DIZ ( NOTE: When a FILE_ID\n              Extractor/Adder does not support deleting the old FILE_ID.DIZ\n              but it overwrites the old one, than DON''T place an DELFILE_ID\n              CommandLine in that script ( EXAMPLE : TXTExtract )).\n EXTFILE_ID - CommandLine for Extracting a FILE_ID.DIZ  \n\n Basicly... it''s all the same!\n\n 5. @{"RESIDENT INSTALLATION " LINK ID10} of STRIP_ID\n 6. @{"CREATING THE SENT.DATA" LINK ID04} for STRIP_ID\n \n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID04 "Creating The Storage File for STRIP_ID."\n\n STRIP_ID is not ( in anyway ) able to create it''s sentby file. You will have \n to that part. In the archive you will find an utility called ''CreateSent''. \n This  will create or append room in the sent file. \n Usage: \n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n\n CreateSent <SENTFILE> <# OF USERS>\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n\n For Example: ''CreateSent BBS:User.Sent 1000'' will create room for 1000 users.\n And if your bbs grows later over the 1000 Users just run the utility again\n with the # of users you wish to append room for. \n Example: ''CreateSent BBS:User.Sent 500'' will extend space to 1500 users.\n Anyway, make sure you create a storage file with room for more users than\n you have.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID05 "Preventing Lines to show up in your filelisting"\n\n - What Lamers Add, We gotta STRIP...\n\n STRIP_ID offers you the possibilty to prevent certain lines from showing\n up in your filelisting. Just ''snap'' every line you don''t want to see\n in your bbslisting to the "BBS:FILEID/Strip.id" file. An example:\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n `---------------------->dEEP sPACE nINE bBS]\n [* B·D *]--»(·Europes Fastest!·)§--[* B·D *]\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n \n Note that the first line of a description can''t be stripped. And that \n you should prevent that the Strip.id grows to a huge size.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID06 "Notes worthy to mention"\n\n - >>> THE AE 3.2X CMD''S ICONS ASSUME RESIDENT INSTALLATION! <<<\n   you will have to change paths yourself if you don''t want them resident.\n\n - STRIP_ID isn''t depending on an assign or something. You can place both\n   STRIP_ID and SENT on any location you want to. I Advise to copy STRIP_ID\n   to RAM: (or something like that) and modify the icons/path to that\n   location. Just as long as the FILEID/ and User.Sent are in your\n   BBS Location ( See ACP.INFO for this location. ).\n\n - If you are running AE 3.2x then make them @{"RESIDENT" LINK ID10}.\n\n - Update & Strip the Strip.id file regulary.\n\n - In your T: Assignment you will find a/some file(s) called @<node>STRIP_ID\n   STRIP_ID will store here it''s userinfo after his 1st upload and retrieve\n   all further info <of that user> out of these files. These file can\n   be deleted at al time, but will appear again < sometime ;) >.\n\n - Descriptions starting with ''/'' will never be added as FILE_ID.DIZ.\n   \n - Install the ''FINDSENT'' command in a bull txt. As all users should fill\n   in their sentbyline again. Not required as STRIP_ID will notify the\n   user if he has no config.\n\n - Unlike FileID from byteandi, STRIP_ID doesn''t run 2(!) doors for each\n   description. SENT is only used to configure the sentbyline.\n\n - There is no main config file. The only thing that could be in the config\n   file is a default ''UPLOADED BY'' line, but STRIP_ID simply centers the\n   username as sentbyline.\n\n - And for those who just love to mess around :\n\n   struct id_Data {\n     char  id_Name[31];                 /* user''s name                   */\n     char  id_Tagline[50];              /* user''s sentby line            */\n     LONG  id_Timeout;                  /* user''s timeout                */\n     LONG  id_Slot;                     /* user''s bbs->slot #.           */\n     char  id_Reserved[11];             /* Future Expansion. Free to use */\n   };                                   /* Will contain colorinfo (maybe)*/\n                                        /* someday ...                   */\n   Users are stored the same way AE does it. So you can find a user by his\n   Slotnumber ( -1 ). DO compare the name with the current online user, as\n   some users get deleted, renamed, etc etc....\n \n - @{"Example Output" LINK EXM}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID07 "Why should you ?"\n\nIf you would like to have a ''clean & safe'' version of this program, you\nfound a bug (shit), or just have a question then call one of the \nfollowing boards:\n\n   Taj Mahal        Hi-TeCH         [WHQ]  Nd.1 +31 162 322 716   28800\n   The Firm         Dusty           [HOL]  Nd.1 +31 PRI-VAT-E!!   28800\n   Poivre Blanc     Diogenes        [BEL]  Nd.1 +32 233 129 25    16800\n   Asia Blue        Metal Death     [USA]  Nd.1 +1 919 747 4107   14400\n   Trancer Bbs      Jack Death      [USA]  Nd.1 +1 919 231 6880   14400\n   Heal The World   Master Blaster  [ITA]  Nd.1 +39 322 259 724   14400\n                                           Nd.2 +39 322 259 593   14400\n   Dyers Eve        Suffe           [FIN]  Nd.1 +358 034 94368    16800\n\n@endnode\n\n@node EXM "Example output"\n\nScanning GOD-QN21.LHA for FILE_ID.DIZ....done!\nViewing FILE_ID.DIZ. You have 5 seconds to cancel this description\n                                [--------------------------------------------]\nGOD-QN21.LHA    11595  05-16-94 :  ______/\\________ _____/\\ ________________\n                                :  \\____/   ______//    /  \\\\______   \\____/\n                                :    \\_/    \\_   \\/    /\\   \\|    |\\   \\_/\n                                :      \\     |    \\    \\/   /|   /\\/   /\n                                :EXPRESS\\__  _____/\\_______/ |___\\  __/DESIGN\n                                :<---------\\/- ·p·R·E·S·E·N·T·S· -\\/-------->\n                                :       QuickNew V2.1 by CALYPS0/G0D !\n                                :The update to the ultimate util ! Pure ASM !\n                                :<------------------------------------------>\n\nWould you like to use this description (Y/n)? 3:\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID10 "Resident Installation of STRIP_ID"\n\n - This is for AE 3.2x+ only\n\n 1. Add The Following Lines to your S:Startup-Sequence.\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n C:RESIDENT BBS:DOORS/STRIP_ID/SENT PURE\n C:RESIDENT BBS:DOORS/STRIP_ID/STRIP_ID PURE\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n\n 2. Modify the tooltypes to the following:\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n LOCATION=SENT / STRIP_ID\n RESIDENT\n ACCESS=10\n TYPE=XIM\n PRIORITY=1\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n ALWAYS make sure that the doors are resident, as AE crashes when it can''t\n run the doors....(bug ?).\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),'{"LOCATION":"SENT","ACCESS":"10","TYPE":"XIM","PRIORITY":"1"}','auto-added',56330,8,0,NULL,NULL,'ptl_si06','scan',1780048679);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ptl_si07','PTL-SI07.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/PTL-SI07.LHA','CREATESENT','XIM','CREATESENT',NULL,NULL,'PTL','_ ____________  _ /  _____ _     _______ _ /        _/  //     \/ /      / PreSents /   __________/       \       /_______',replace(' _ ______________________________________ _\n_ ____________  _ /  _____ _     _______ _\n   /        _/  //     \/ /      / PreSents\n  /   __________/       \       /_______\n /______ /   \ __________\____________ /\n[«-----\/-----\/---------------------\/--»]\n       STRIP_ID v1.06 & SENT v1.08\n[«---------------------------------------»]\n   FULL FileId & AutoSent Replacement !!\n   Strips ''BBS_ADDS'' out of any FILE_ID.\n','\n',char(10)),'STRIP_ID.GUIDE',replace('@database STRIP_ID.guide\n\n@node Main "STRIP_ID v1.05 - Contents"\n                                                                             \n STRIP_ID v1.05 (C) 1994 ZiA [- PtL^D2 -]\n FILE_ID.DIZ door for Ami-Express 3.2x & ZX 2.4x.\n\n @{"SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS         " LINK ID01} STRIP_ID is a FILEID replacement as SENT\n @{"INSTALLING STRIP_ID         " LINK ID02} is an AUTOSENT replacement. STRIP_ID \n @{"INSTALLING SENT             " LINK ID03} offers you the options of preventing\n @{"CREATING THE SENT.DATA      " LINK ID04} certain lines to show up in your file-\n @{"STRIPPING LINES             " LINK ID05} listing and being packed into a FILE_ID.DIZ\n @{"NOTES WORTHY TO MENTION     " LINK ID06} Also users can now decide how STRIP_ID must \n @{"CONTACTING ME               " LINK ID07} operate: Allow a him to abort a description,\n @{"BUGS, HISTORY               " LINK ID09} only show him the description or only show\n                              that an ID is found.\n\n@endnode  \n\n@node ID09 ""\n\nMain History:\n\nv1.00z - Initial ZX door.\n       - Bugs all over it... ( it''s better to speak about 1 bug: STRIP_ID ;).\n\nv1.01i - Changed main ''sendmessage'' routine from specific ZX to common /X \n         routine.\n       - Contains countdown and a stripper ( that didn''t work ;( ).\n\nv1.02i - First version to run on AE 3.xx . It DID work! well.. sort of..;)\n       - Installed the external user.sent file. \n       - SENT door included.\n       - STRIP_ID is now depending on the sent.data for its info.\n\nv1.03i - SENT did hang sometimes at the Enter SentbyLine prompt.\n       - Stopped using any SAS/C optimizers and headers.\n       - The Stripper didn''t strip correct ( = AT ALL :), Fixed!\n       - STRIP_ID CAN''T be made resident. Still ''outcoding'' this ''bug''.\n       - STRIP_ID checks for incorrect descriptions starting with RZ,rz,B0.\n       - Rewrote the load/save data option. Now uses the slotnr to find a user.\n         CREATESENT utiltiy required to run..       \n       - STRIP_ID now creates a temporary file in your T: directory that\n         contains the userinfo.\n\nv1.04i - STRIP_ID and /X don''t run synchronized, this causes STRIP_ID to\n         process other files than /X expects, not fatal, but VERRY anoying.\n         *SHOULD* be fixed. tested with SAS/C v6.50 ( 5 disks & ran perfect!)\n       - If 2 files with no desc are uploaded STRIP_ID would find the fileid\n         from file1 as FILE_ID.DIZ for file2. Fixed.\n       - SENT completely rewritten.\n       - STRIP_ID also ( slow sunday ;)\n       - Rewritten the striproutine (again). bout 10% slower.. but works on \n         68000/010 now..\n       - (Pause)...More(y/n/ns) Removed!. A user can now countdown from \n         + whatever to 0 without this prompt.\n       - Scratched the ''linewrapper'' of sendmessage. It didn''t do anything so\n         why wast time.\n       - Both STRIP_ID and SENT are re-entrant....(Yes!)...\n       - Fixed some serious ''stripreturn'' bugs.\n       - Limited the timeout to 15 secs, any ass who needs more should \n         think of buying a pc.\n\nv1.05  - STRIP_ID would write an empty line under a centered sentby line.\n         ( WOULD! )...\n       - Rewritten the date routine. The old one didn''t like to be resident..\n       - Improved center routine.\n       - Long list of stupid little annoying ''bugs'' removed       \n       - STRIP_ID now checks for the <CTRL>-m character (IBM) and strips it\n        \nv1.06  - Cleaned up the script routine. \n       - We now check if a user is online whenever prompting for a description  \n         input.\n       - SENT didn''t free it''s memory when it couldn''t ''Register''.\n       - Fixed $VER bugs ( just for hi-tech ;)\n\n       - >> RELEASE VERSIONS : STRIP_ID v1.05\n                                   SENT v1.07\n\n                       \n@endnode\n\n@node ID01 "System Requirements for STRIP_ID."\n\n STRIP_ID requires :\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n - An Amiga Running OS 2.x/3.x.\n - A Fully Installed AE 3.xx / ZX 2.4x.\n - Any Kind of archive utilities ( eg LHA, ZIP, ARJ ).\n - The Mystic Extractors/Adders for DMS, TXT and EXE Files.\n - Uploads ;)\n\n Archive Contents :\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n FILE                                PURPOSE\n ----------------------------------- ----------------------------------------\n BBS/COMMANDS/*.*                    /X and ZX commands\n BBS/FILEID/<ext>                    Scripts for STRIP_ID \n BBS/UTILS/CREATESENT        (2100)  Utility to create the Sent.Data\n BBS/DOORS/STRIP_ID/SENT     (8720)  The ''SENT'' door.\n BBS/DOORS/STRIP_ID/STRIP_ID (13612) The ''STRIP_ID'' door.\n BBS/DOORS/STRIP_ID/STRIP_ID.GUIDE   Read on...\n ----------------------------------- ----------------------------------------\n@endnode\n\n@node ID03 "Installing the SENT door"\n\n 1. Copy the ''SENT" door to your BBS:DOORS/STRIP_ID/SENT. ( Or Any Location\n    you wish to, but we assume this location. ).\n \n 2. For 3.xx : Copy All icons in the BBSCMD/ directory to your \n               BBS:COMMANDS/BBSCMD/ directory\n               \n    For ZX   : Add the following lines to your BBS.CMD file.\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n *SENT     XM005BBS:DOORS/STRIP_ID/SENT\n *FINDSENT XM005BBS:DOORS/STRIP_ID/SENT\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n \n 3. If you want you can install the ''FINDSENT'' in a bull.txt using the\n    MCI Command ''~CC_FINDSENT'' in that bulltxt. This is not required as\n    STRIP_ID automaticly notifies the user when he has no sentbyline.\n \n 4. @{"RESIDENT INSTALLATION " LINK ID10} of SENT\n 5. @{"CREATING THE SENT.DATA" LINK ID04} for SENT and STRIP_ID\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID02 "Installing STRIP_ID"\n\n 1. Copy the program to a directory where you would like it ( We assume that\n    STRIP_ID is placed in the BBS:Doors/strip_id/ directory).\n \n 2. Copy the FileId/ Directory to your BBSLocation.\n		\n 3. For /X 3.2x: Copy the EXAMINE.INFO to your BBS:COMMANDS/SYSCMD/ Directory\n                 And modify all paths to your needs.\n                 \n    For ZX 2.4x: Add the following line to your SYS.CMD file:\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n *EXAMINE  XM005BBS:DOORS/STRIP_ID/STRIP_ID\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n                 And disable the internal SENTBY.  \n                 -NOTIFY: your users to use SENT to edit their sentbyline and\n                 not the ''W'' command.\n\n 4. STRIP_ID doesn''t use ''Tooltypes'' for its info. Instead it uses a script\n    for it''s external command-line. \n    LHA Example script:\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n ADDFILE_ID C:LHA A @F @WFILE_ID.DIZ\n DELFILE_ID C:LHA D @F FILE_ID.DIZ\n EXTFILE_ID C:LHA E @F FILE_ID.DIZ @W\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n\n  STRIP_ID v1.06         FileID v1.5         Purpose\n ---------------------  ------------------- -------------------------------\n    @F                     @P               -  Symbol for the file that \n                                               Contains the FILE_ID.DIZ\n    @W                     @W               -  Symbol for Node<x>/Work/\n                                               Directory.   \n\n ADDFILE_ID - CommandLine for Adding a FILE_ID.DIZ.\n DELFILE_ID - CommandLine for Deleting a FILE_ID.DIZ ( NOTE: When a FILE_ID\n              Extractor/Adder does not support deleting the old FILE_ID.DIZ\n              but it overwrites the old one, than DON''T place an DELFILE_ID\n              CommandLine in that script ( EXAMPLE : TXTExtract )).\n EXTFILE_ID - CommandLine for Extracting a FILE_ID.DIZ  \n\n Basicly... it''s all the same!\n\n 5. @{"RESIDENT INSTALLATION " LINK ID10} of STRIP_ID\n 6. @{"CREATING THE SENT.DATA" LINK ID04} for STRIP_ID\n \n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID04 "Creating The Storage File for STRIP_ID."\n\n STRIP_ID is not ( in anyway ) able to create it''s sentby file. You will have \n to that part. In the archive you will find an utility called ''CreateSent''. \n This  will create or append room in the sent file. \n Usage: \n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n\n CreateSent <SENTFILE> <# OF USERS>\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n\n For Example: ''CreateSent BBS:User.Sent 1000'' will create room for 1000 users.\n And if your bbs grows later over the 1000 Users just run the utility again\n with the # of users you wish to append room for. \n Example: ''CreateSent BBS:User.Sent 500'' will extend space to 1500 users.\n Anyway, make sure you create a storage file with room for more users than\n you have.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID05 "Preventing Lines to show up in your filelisting"\n\n - What Lamers Add, We gotta STRIP...\n\n STRIP_ID offers you the possibilty to prevent certain lines from showing\n up in your filelisting. Just ''snap'' every line you don''t want to see\n in your bbslisting to the "BBS:FILEID/Strip.id" file. An example:\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n `---------------------->dEEP sPACE nINE bBS]\n [* B·D *]--»(·Europes Fastest!·)§--[* B·D *]\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n \n Note that the first line of a description can''t be stripped. And that \n you should prevent that the Strip.id grows to a huge size.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID06 "Notes worthy to mention"\n\n - >>> THE AE 3.2X CMD''S ICONS ASSUME RESIDENT INSTALLATION! <<<\n   you will have to change paths yourself if you don''t want them resident.\n\n - STRIP_ID isn''t depending on an assign or something. You can place both\n   STRIP_ID and SENT on any location you want to. I Advise to copy STRIP_ID\n   to RAM: (or something like that) and modify the icons/path to that\n   location. Just as long as the FILEID/ and User.Sent are in your\n   BBS Location ( See ACP.INFO for this location. ).\n\n - If you are running AE 3.2x then make them @{"RESIDENT" LINK ID10}.\n\n - Update & Strip the Strip.id file regulary.\n\n - In your T: Assignment you will find a/some file(s) called @<node>STRIP_ID\n   STRIP_ID will store here it''s userinfo after his 1st upload and retrieve\n   all further info <of that user> out of these files. These file can\n   be deleted at al time, but will appear again < sometime ;) >.\n\n - Descriptions starting with ''/'' will never be added as FILE_ID.DIZ.\n   \n - Install the ''FINDSENT'' command in a bull txt. As all users should fill\n   in their sentbyline again. Not required as STRIP_ID will notify the\n   user if he has no config.\n\n - Unlike FileID from byteandi, STRIP_ID doesn''t run 2(!) doors for each\n   description. SENT is only used to configure the sentbyline.\n\n - There is no main config file. The only thing that could be in the config\n   file is a default ''UPLOADED BY'' line, but STRIP_ID simply centers the\n   username as sentbyline.\n\n - And for those who just love to mess around :\n\n   struct id_Data {\n     char  id_Name[31];                 /* user''s name                   */\n     char  id_Tagline[50];              /* user''s sentby line            */\n     LONG  id_Timeout;                  /* user''s timeout                */\n     LONG  id_Slot;                     /* user''s bbs->slot #.           */\n     char  id_Reserved[11];             /* Future Expansion. Free to use */\n   };                                   /* Will contain colorinfo (maybe)*/\n                                        /* someday ...                   */\n   Users are stored the same way AE does it. So you can find a user by his\n   Slotnumber ( -1 ). DO compare the name with the current online user, as\n   some users get deleted, renamed, etc etc....\n \n - @{"Example Output" LINK EXM}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID07 "Why should you ?"\n\nIf you would like to have a ''clean & safe'' version of this program, you\nfound a bug (shit), or just have a question then call one of the \nfollowing boards:\n\n   Taj Mahal        Hi-TeCH         [WHQ]  Nd.1 +31 162 322 716   28800\n   The Firm         Dusty           [HOL]  Nd.1 +31 PRI-VAT-E!!   28800\n   Poivre Blanc     Diogenes        [BEL]  Nd.1 +32 233 129 25    16800\n   Asia Blue        Metal Death     [USA]  Nd.1 +1 919 747 4107   14400\n   Trancer Bbs      Jack Death      [USA]  Nd.1 +1 919 231 6880   14400\n   Heal The World   Master Blaster  [ITA]  Nd.1 +39 322 259 724   14400\n                                           Nd.2 +39 322 259 593   14400\n   Dyers Eve        Suffe           [FIN]  Nd.1 +358 034 94368    16800\n\n@endnode\n\n@node EXM "Example output"\n\nScanning GOD-QN21.LHA for FILE_ID.DIZ....done!\nViewing FILE_ID.DIZ. You have 5 seconds to cancel this description\n                                [--------------------------------------------]\nGOD-QN21.LHA    11595  05-16-94 :  ______/\\________ _____/\\ ________________\n                                :  \\____/   ______//    /  \\\\______   \\____/\n                                :    \\_/    \\_   \\/    /\\   \\|    |\\   \\_/\n                                :      \\     |    \\    \\/   /|   /\\/   /\n                                :EXPRESS\\__  _____/\\_______/ |___\\  __/DESIGN\n                                :<---------\\/- ·p·R·E·S·E·N·T·S· -\\/-------->\n                                :       QuickNew V2.1 by CALYPS0/G0D !\n                                :The update to the ultimate util ! Pure ASM !\n                                :<------------------------------------------>\n\nWould you like to use this description (Y/n)? 3:\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID10 "Resident Installation of STRIP_ID"\n\n - This is for AE 3.2x+ only\n\n 1. Add The Following Lines to your S:Startup-Sequence.\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n C:RESIDENT BBS:DOORS/STRIP_ID/SENT PURE\n C:RESIDENT BBS:DOORS/STRIP_ID/STRIP_ID PURE\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n\n 2. Modify the tooltypes to the following:\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n LOCATION=SENT / STRIP_ID\n RESIDENT\n ACCESS=10\n TYPE=XIM\n PRIORITY=1\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n ALWAYS make sure that the doors are resident, as AE crashes when it can''t\n run the doors....(bug ?).\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),'{"LOCATION":"SENT","ACCESS":"10","TYPE":"XIM","PRIORITY":"1"}','auto-added',59695,11,0,NULL,NULL,'ptl_si07','scan',1780048679);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ptl_si12','PTL_SI12.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/PTL_SI12.LHA','rpstart','XIM','rpstart',NULL,NULL,'PTL','_\_________\_\_____  _____/ _\_  |_____ /      ______/   /      \w^s/     l     \ /_________|.cOLa./________\ /_____________\',replace('   ________/\  ______________  ___/|\n  _\_________\_\_____  _____/ _\_  |_____\n /      ______/   /      \w^s/     l     \\n/_________|.cOLa./________\ /_____________\\n::::::::::::::::::presents::::::::::::::::::\n:::::::: FRaNKy''s Simple Info V 1.2 ::::::::\n::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\n:::::::: A Nice User-Info Door For :::::::::\n::::::::       /X 2.xx and up      :::::::::\n::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\n','\n',char(10)),'Simple-Info.Guide',replace('@database "FRaNKy''s Simple Info V 1.2"\n@font topaz.font 8\n@author "FRaNKy/PTL"\n@(c) "Copyright © 1995 FRaNKy / Purple Turtle"\n@$VER: Simple-Info.Guide V 1.0  (31/08/95)\n@node Main "FRaNKy''s Simple Info V 1.0 - Main Menu"\n    FRaNKy''s Simple Info V 1.2 - Copyright 1995 FRaNKy / Purple Turtle\n¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n       Important!            Contacting The Author           The Door\n      ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯          ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯         ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n  @{"     Disclaimer      " link "disc"}    @{"   Bulletin Boards   " link "Fbss"}    @{"     What Is It ?    " link "what"}\n  @{"   Compiled Doors    " link "comp"}    @{"       FidoNet       " link "Ffido"}    @{"     Installation    " link "inst"}\n  @{"    PostCardWare     " link "post"}    @{"      InterNet       " link "Finter"}    @{"   Credits & Hellos  " link "cred"}\n                                                      @{"       History       " link "hist"}\n     ________/\  ______________  ___/|                @{"    The Story Off    " link "stor"}\n    _\_________\_\_____  _____/ _\_  |_____\n   /      ______/   /      \w^s/     l     \              Contacting PTL\n  /_________|.cOLa./________\ /_____________\            ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n  ::::::::::::::::::presents::::::::::::::::::        @{"        BBS''s        " link "pbbs"}\n  :::::::: FRaNKy''s Simple Info V 1.2 ::::::::        @{"       FidoNet       " link "pfido"}\n  ::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::        @{"      Internet       " link "pinter"}\n  :::::::: A Nice User-Info Door For :::::::::\n  ::::::::       /X 2.xx and up      :::::::::        @{" Looking For Members " link "memb"}\n  ::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\n@endnode\n@node "disc"\n@title "Disclaimer"\n                                DISCLAIMER\n                               ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n     This software is "AS IS", the author can not be held responsible for\n    any damage caused to your system by this software, or the consequences\n                               of this damage...\n\n                    To say it simply : Use at your own risk !\n@endnode\n@node "post"\n@title "PostCardWare"\n                               POSTCARDWARE\n                              ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n           All the doors included in this archive are PostCardWare\n      If you use one of included doors, you are kindly asked to send a\n                    postcard of the area you live in to :\n\n                          Peter Smets (FRaNKy / PTL)\n                          Weldadigheidsstraat 45\n                          3000 Leuven\n                          Belgium\n\n             Postcards received so far : Lady An      [   UK   ]\n                                         Killer Dwarf [ Sweden ]\n@endnode\n@node "comp"\n@title "Compiled Doors"\n                               COMPILED DOORS\n                              ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n  All doors in this archive are compiled using the RexxPlus Arexx Compiler.\n\n     To get the doors to work on you /X system, you must run RPStart and\n       have the libraries included in the archive copied to your LIBS:\n  It is advisable to put RPStart in you User-Startup so you won''t forget it\n\n   If you would like a copy of the uncompiled sources of the doors included\n      in this archive, send 1500 BEF (50 USD) to the author of the doors.\n           Cash money (no coins) or EuroCheque in BEF only please.\n\n  This can be a large amount of money, but if you see what money I spend in\n   my doors (time, phonecalls) and if you really want the sources to study\n                       them, this isn''t too much I think...\n\n        The adress where you can send the money to can be found under\n                              @{"postcardware" link "post"} button...\n\nNote :\n\n Compiled doors do not work on all systems (blame the /X RexxPort for this)\n                   but the advantage for me is much greater.\n\n  I decided to do this compilation of my doors because I noticed that more\n    and more people started using pieces of my doors, or sometimes just\n    renaming the door and then releasing it under their own name/group.\n            If you want you can buy the sources as staded above.\n\n                                                                    FRaNKy.\n@endnode\n@node "what"\n@title "FRaNKy''s Simple Info V 1.2 - What is it ?"\n                                WHAT IS IT ?\n                               ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n     A small user-info door for the /X 2.xx and up Bulletin Board Program\n@endnode\n@node "inst"\n@title "FRaNKy''s Simple Info V 1.2 - Installation"\n                                INSTALLATION\n                               ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n       All files should be placed in the directory "Doors:PTL/SInfo/"\n            The icon (S.info) should be in "BBS:Commands/BBSCMD"\n@endnode\n@node "cred"\n@title "FRaNKy''s Simple Info V 1.2 - Credits"\n                                   CREDITS\n                                  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                             Coding       : FRaNKy\n                             Docs         : FRaNKy & TFX\n                             Idea''s       : The Fly\n                             Beta Testing : TFX & Killer Dwarf\n\n                                  GREETINGS\n                                 ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\nHello''s & Greetings from FRaNKy fly out to : All PTL members, specially\nto : TFX (I''ll make a better map next time) - Necrite (Cluuuuuuuuuuub !) -\nKiller Dwarf (Stappa !) - The Fly - Flare - Damien - Crisp.\nMore Hello''s to : Recall (format c:) - TCB - Syntax - All Tragedy Members -\nAnd everyone I forgot in this hurry.\n@endnode\n@node "hist"\n@title "FRaNKy''s Simple Info V 1.2 - History"\n                                    HISTORY\n                                   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                 ... - 0.9  : Internal Beta Releases\n                       1.0  : First Worldwide Release\n                       1.1  : - Removed the password (it''s always the same))\n                              - Added access level\n                       1.2  : - Added ANSI-Animation\n\n@endnode\n@node "stor"\n@title "FRaNKy''s Simple Info V 1.2 - The Story Off"\n                                 THE STORY OFF\n                                ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\nWhat is there to tell about a User-Information door ???\n\nThis is my third User-Information door I did, and the best if you ask me.\n\nThat''s it.. Really...\n@endnode\n@node "Fbss"\n@title "Contacting The Author On The PTL BBS''s"\n                            CONTACTING THE AUTHOR\n                           ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n   The Author of the door can be contacted on these Purple Turtle BBS''s\n\n    Fortress      (   PTL WHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-3-***.**.** (Zyxel 16.8)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-3-***.**.** (Vfast 28.8)\n\n    Enigma        (   PTL BHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-89-**.**.** (USR   16.8)\n\n    Secret Cinema (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +32-52-**.**.** (VFast 33.6)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-52-RINGDOWN (VFast 33.6)\n\n    Cyber Garden  (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +32-11-**.**.** (USR   16.8)\n\n    S.P.G         (   PTL SHQ  ) Node 1 : +46-612-***.**  (USR   16.8)\n\n    Rhythm Nation (   PTL FHQ  ) Node 1 : +33-82-**.**.** (???   14.4)\n@endnode\n@node "FFido"\n@title "Contacting The Author Through FidoNet"\n                            CONTACTING THE AUTHOR\n                           ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    The Author of the doors included in this archive can be contacted by\n               sendin a Netmail to one of these point-numbers\n\n                                2:292/622.13\n                                2:292/8010.32\n@endnode\n@node "finter"\n@title "Contacting The Author Through Internet"\n                            CONTACTING THE AUTHOR\n                           ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                            Send your E-Mails to:\n\n                             [email removed]\n\n                     IRC-fans can try to join the channel\n\n                                    #PTL\n\n                         If I''m online, I''ll be there.\n@endnode\n@node "Pbbs"\n@title "Purpe Turtle BBS''s"\n                             PURPLE TURTLE BBS''S\n                            ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                                   BELGIUM\n                                  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Fortress      (   PTL WHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-3-***.**.** (Zyxel 16.8)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-3-***.**.** (Vfast 28.8)\n\n    Enigma        (   PTL BHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-89-**.**.** (USR   16.8)\n\n    Secret Cinema (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +32-52-**.**.** (VFast 33.6)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-52-RINGDOWN (VFast 33.6)\n\n    Cyber Garden  (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +32-11-**.**.** (USR   16.8)\n\n                                   HOLLAND\n                                  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Super Dancer  (   PTL HHQ  ) Node 1 : +31-570-***-*** (VFast 28.8)\n\n                                    SWEDEN\n                                   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Bitch Board   (   PTL EHQ  ) Node 1 : +46-111-***.**  (USR   28.8)\n\n    S.P.G         (   PTL SHQ  ) Node 1 : +46-612-***.**  (Vfast 28.8)\n\n    rIVER wILD    (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +46-612-***.**  (USR   28.8)\n\n    Inferno       (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +46-øPRIVATE!ø  (USR   33.6)\n\n                                    FRANCE\n                                   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Rhythm Nation (   PTL FHQ  ) Node 1 : +33-82-**.**.** (???   14.4)\n\n                                    NORWAY\n                                   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Wizard Guild  (   PTL NHQ  ) Node 1 : +47-53-**.**.** (VFast 28.8)\n\n                                   GERMANY\n                                  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Traders World (   PTL GHQ  ) Node 1 : +49-215-******* (VFast 28.8)\n@endnode\n@node "PFido"\n@title "Purple Turtle FidoNet Adresses"\n                        PURPLE TURTLE FIDONET ADRESSES\n                       ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                  TFX      (  World Leader )   2:292/8010.14\n                  FRaNKy   (Co-World Leader)   2:292/8010.32\n@endnode\n@node "pinter"\n@title "Purple Turtle On The Net"\n                          PURPLE TURTLE ON THE NET\n                         ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                The Purple Turtle homepage can be visited at :\n\n                    http://www.ping.be/~ping2045/ptl.html\n\n                    You can also send E-Mails to FRaNKy at :\n\n                              [email removed]\n\n                         Or join the IRC-Channel #PTL\n@endnode\n@node "memb"\n@title "Purple Turtle Is Always Looking For New Members"\n                           LOOKING FOR NEW MEMBERS\n                          ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n  If you think you are the right guy (girl) for a cool group and you can do\n  some Coding (ASM-C-Arexx-...), Music, Graphics, Trading, Swapping or have\n      a BBS, then contact the Purple Turtle Leaders or Division Leaders\n                   for a certain reply on one of our HQ''s.\n\n   If you want to join with your BBS, we do not ask any donations for your\n    membership (in another way : it''s free !).  BBS''s outside Belgium are\n                              extremely welcome...\n\n        @{" Bulletin Boards " link "lbbs"}   @{"     FidoNet     " link "PFido"}   @{"    InterNet    " link "pinter"}\n@endnode\n@node "lbbs"\n@title "Contacting The Leaders"\n                           CONTACTING THE LEADERS\n                          ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n  You can contact the World Leaders and/or division leaders on these BBS''s.\n    People with a HQ in their country should adress themselves to that HQ.\n       If there isn''t a PTL BBS in your country, call the WHQ or a bbs\n                            in a country near you.\n\n    Fortress      (   PTL WHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-3-***.**.** (Zyxel 16.8)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-3-***.**.** (Vfast 28.8)\n\n    Bitch Board   (   PTL EHQ  ) Node 1 : +46-111-***.**  (USR   28.8)\n\n    Super Dancer  (   PTL HHQ  ) Node 1 : +31-570-***-*** (VFast 28.8)\n\n    S.P.G         (   PTL SHQ  ) Node 1 : +46-612-***.**  (Vfast 28.8)\n\n    Rhythm Nation (   PTL FHQ  ) Node 1 : +33-82-**.**.** (???   14.4)\n\n    Wizard Guild  (   PTL NHQ  ) Node 1 : +47-53-**.**.** (VFast 28.8)\n\n    Traders World (   PTL GHQ  ) Node 1 : +49-215-******* (VFast 28.8)\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',76028,5,0,NULL,NULL,'ptl_si12','scan',1780048679);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ptl_si21','PTL-SI21.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/PTL-SI21.LHA','CREATESENT','XIM','CREATESENT',NULL,NULL,'PTL','_ ____________  _ /  _____ _     _______ _ /        _/  //     \/ /      / PreSents /   __________/       \       /_______',replace(' _ ______________________________________ _\n_ ____________  _ /  _____ _     _______ _\n   /        _/  //     \/ /      / PreSents\n  /   __________/       \       /_______\n /______ /   \ __________\____________ /\n[«-----\/-----\/---------------------\/--»]\n       STRIP_ID v2.01 & SENT v1.09\n[«---------------------------------------»]\n First Public Release over STRIP_ID v1.06i\n    Strips TagLines from FILE_ID.DIZ\n','\n',char(10)),'STRIP_ID.GUIDE',replace('@database STRIP_ID.guide\n\n@node Main "STRIP_ID v2.01 - Contents"\n                                                                             \n STRIP_ID v2.01 (C) 1994 ZiA [- PtL^D2 -]\n FILE_ID.DIZ door for Ami-Express 3.2x & ZX 2.4x.\n\n @{"SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS         " LINK ID01} STRIP_ID is a FILEID replacement as SENT\n @{"INSTALLING STRIP_ID         " LINK ID02} is an AUTOSENT replacement. STRIP_ID \n @{"INSTALLING SENT             " LINK ID03} offers you the options of STRIPPING\n @{"CREATING THE SENT.DATA      " LINK ID04} certain lines in a FILE_ID.DIZ and \n @{"STRIPPING LINES             " LINK ID05} repack the new FILE_ID.DIZ into that \n @{"NOTES WORTHY TO MENTION     " LINK ID06} archive. \n @{"CONTACTING ME               " LINK ID07} \n @{"BUGS, HISTORY               " LINK ID09} \n\n @{"ABOUT STRIP_ID v1.06        " LINK ID20}\n @{"NOTE TO SOME PEOPLE         " LINK ID21}\n\n@endnode  \n\n@node ID21 ""\n\n First of all, a big thanx goes out to Hi-TeCH and Dusty for letting me \n (ab)use their system with everything they run of me ( hehe, a lot! ). \n Also >YOU< should thank *Dusty/CLX* for mentioning the nice strip option \n and a part of the name of this program. \n\n Little words..\n\n Fletcher            pom pom..ehhh...just let it run..\n MarksMan            sorry! i was just a ''little'' over the top...\n Sal-1/<PAST NOOIT!> WildCarding..... ( double meaning ? ;)\n ''Kai''/CLE           I just included what was necessary..ok?\n                     BTW: PTL STANDS FOR PuRPlE TuRTLe, which originated\n                     (mostly) from DeSiRe Holland & Belgium members.\n Thc/[L]             TetraHydroCannabinol.. yeah.. i know.'')\n Dusty/CLX           you...dirty...chatkiller...\n Buzzy/PCZ           For being the only (at the moment) /X betatester.\n \n And ofcourse thanx to everybody who has anything to do with strip_id\n before this release..\n\n STRIP_ID will (probably) never support the ''ZIP'' files internal when ZIP\n isn''t able to supply the commandline needed. You''ll need an interface\n ( I suppose ARexx was invented for that shit ).\n \n@endnode\n\n@node ID20 "About the escaped release"\n \n FIRST: STRIP_ID v1.06 ( or any v1.xx! ) was not intended to be released.\n Therefore, i will not take ANY responsability for ANY damage done by v1.0x.\n ( hehe.. it sometimes crashed leaving your HD unvalidated ;)\n \n It DID contain bugs, for example: it would crash if txtextract failed to\n find an @END_...Further it did not ( to my knowledge ) strip hi-ascii.\n \n STRIP_ID v2.01 is backward compitable with v1.06, so if you installed v1.06\n just copy the executables over the old ones.\n \n@endnode\n\n@node ID09 "Main History"\n \nMain History:\n \nv1.00z [23-MAY-94]\n       - Initial ZX door.\n       - Bugs all over it... ( it''s better to speak about 1 bug: STRIP_ID ;).\n\nv1.01i [24-MAY-94] ( 00:53 ;)\n       - Changed main ''sendmessage'' routine from specific ZX to common /X \n         routine. ( which is a bit slower, but who cares ?)\n       - Unknown # of bugs fixed.\n       - Build in a countdown.\n\nv1.02i [24-MAY-94]\n       - First version to run on AE 3.xx . It DID work! well.. sort of..;)\n       - Installed the external user.sent file. STRIP_ID depends now\n         on the User.Sent file.\n       - SENT door included.\n\nv1.03i [25-MAY-94]\n       - SENT did hang sometimes at the Enter SentbyLine prompt.\n       - Stopped using any SAS/C optimizers and headers.\n       - The Stripper didn''t strip correct ( = AT ALL :), Fixed!\n       - STRIP_ID CAN''T be made resident. Still ''outcoding'' this ''bug''.\n       - STRIP_ID checks for incorrect descriptions starting with RZ,rz,B0.\n       - Rewrote the load/save data option. Now uses the slotnr to find a user.\n         CREATESENT utiltiy required to run..       \n       - STRIP_ID now creates a  file in your ENV: directory that contains the \n         userinfo of the user online.\n\nv1.04i [28-MAY-94]\n       - STRIP_ID and /X don''t run synchronized, this causes STRIP_ID to\n         process other files than /X expects, not fatal, but VERRY anoying.\n         *SHOULD* be fixed. ( I was (i guess)sleeping when i wrote that part..)\n       - If 2 files with no desc are uploaded STRIP_ID would find the fileid\n         from file1 as FILE_ID.DIZ for file2. Fixed.\n       - SENT completely rewritten.\n       - STRIP_ID also ( slow sunday ;)\n       - Rewritten the striproutine (again). bout 10% slower.. but works on \n         68000/010 now..\n       - (Pause)...More(y/n/ns) Removed!. A user can now countdown from \n         + whatever to 0 without this prompt.\n       - Scratched the ''linewrapper'' of sendmessage. It didn''t do anything so\n         why wast time.\n       - Both STRIP_ID and SENT are re-entrant....(Yes!)...\n       - Fixed some serious ''stripreturn'' bugs.\n       - Limited the timeout to 15 secs, any ass who needs more should \n         think of buying a pc.\n\nv1.05  [05]-JUN-94]\n       - STRIP_ID would write an empty line under a centered sentby line.\n         ( WOULD! )...\n       - Rewritten the date routine. The old one didn''t like to be resident..\n       - Improved center routine.\n       - Long list of stupid little annoying ''bugs'' removed       \n       - STRIP_ID now checks for the <CTRL>-m character (IBM) and strips it\n        \nv1.06  [09-JUN-94]\n       - Cleaned up the script routine. \n       - We now check if a user is online whenever prompting for a description  \n        input. Exits if no carrier is present.\n       - SENT didn''t free it''s memory when it couldn''t ''Register''.\n       - Fixed $VER bugs: ( just for hi-tech ;)\n       - >> RELEASED BY ACCIDENT (AND SOME STUPIDITY) <<\n\nv1.06b [09-JUN-94] ( 10 Mins later :)\n       - Installed double checking for a 12 line limit, STRIP_ID would go on\n         forever if txtextract failed to find an @END_FILE_ID.DIZ and just dumped\n         the remaining text as file_id.diz, causing a stack overflow from \n         strip_id ;) \n       - STRIP_ID crashed ( un-explainable as the Sent door uses the same \n         routine and runs perfect ) at ''Mystical Places'' when it prompted\n         a user for it info\n\nv1.07b [21-JUN-94]\n       - Installed full-wildcard stripping on request...\n       \nv2.00  [22-JUN-94]\n       - Would repack after packing. verry stupid.\n       - Found out that it was stripping twice... shame on me!\n       - Bumped revision to v2.x\n\nv2.01  [25-JUN-94]\n       - Did strip wrong : \n         If you Had *MEN*TEL in your STRIP.ID file it would also strip this\n         combination TEL - MEN , if that existed in a line.\n       - Included ZiPiD from CLE.\n       - Sent would wait forever if a user lost carrier when he filled\n         in his sentbyline. ( Pretty stupid that /X doesn''t check for\n         it self and shuts the door down..). Fixed.\n       - Found out that it didn''t strip non-wildcard lines anymore\n       - STRIP_ID will ( at this point ) strip all ansi colorcodes.\n\nv2.01z - Specific ZX version. Retrieves all the user-info from ZX\n         ( Available for ZX betatesters ).\n\nThings not really tested : ( Yes.. i''m honest! )\n\n - Low memory usage. STRIP_ID is made to exit ''gracefully'' if no memory \n   is available, but i was unable to test this ;)\n - Unknown ''040 behaviour.. Appearently it hangs random on that cpu.\n   Tested on an 3000T/040 and no crashes appeared. \n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID01 "System Requirements for STRIP_ID."\n\n STRIP_ID requires :\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n - An Amiga Running OS 2.x/3.x.\n - A Fully Installed AE 3.2x / ZX 2.4x.\n - Any Kind of archive utilities ( eg LHA, ZIP, ARJ ).\n - The Mystic Extractors/Adders for DMS, TXT and EXE Files.\n - Uploads ;)\n\n Archive Contents :\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n FILE                                PURPOSE\n ----------------------------------- ----------------------------------------\n BBS/COMMANDS/*.*                    /X and ZX commands\n BBS/FILEID/<ext>                    Scripts for STRIP_ID \n BBS/UTILS/CREATESENT        (2368)  Utility to create the Sent.Data\n BBS/DOORS/STRIP_ID/SENT     (9180)  The ''SENT'' door.\n BBS/DOORS/STRIP_ID/STRIP_ID (15224) The ''STRIP_ID'' door.\n BBS/DOORS/STRIP_ID/STRIP_ID.GUIDE   Read on...\n ----------------------------------- ----------------------------------------\n@endnode\n\n@node ID03 "Installing the SENT door"\n\n 1. Copy the ''SENT" door to your BBS:DOORS/STRIP_ID/SENT. ( Or Any Location\n    you wish to, but we assume this location. ).\n \n 2. For /X 3.xx : Copy All icons in the BBSCMD/ directory to your \n                  BBS:COMMANDS/BBSCMD/ directory\n               \n    For ZX 2.4x : Add the following lines to your BBS.CMD file.\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n *SENT     XM005BBS:DOORS/STRIP_ID/SENT\n *FINDSENT XM005BBS:DOORS/STRIP_ID/SENT\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n \n 3. If you want you can install the ''FINDSENT'' in a bull.txt using the\n    MCI Command ''~CC_FINDSENT'' in that bulltxt. This is not required as\n    STRIP_ID automaticly notifies the user when he has no sentbyline.\n \n 4. @{"CREATING THE SENT.DATA" LINK ID04} for SENT and STRIP_ID\n 5. @{"RESIDENT INSTALLATION " LINK ID19} of SENT and STRIP_ID\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID02 "Installing STRIP_ID"\n\n 1. Copy the program to a directory where you would like it ( We assume that\n    STRIP_ID is placed in the BBS:Doors/strip_id/ directory).\n \n 2. Copy the FileId/ Directory to your BBSLocation.\n		\n 3. For /X 3.2x: Copy the EXAMINE.INFO to your BBS:COMMANDS/SYSCMD/ Directory\n                 And modify all paths to your needs.\n                 \n    For ZX 2.4x: Add the following line to your SYS.CMD file:\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n *EXAMINE  XM005BBS:DOORS/STRIP_ID/STRIP_ID\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n                 And disable the internal SENTBY.  \n                 -NOTIFY: your users to use SENT to edit their sentbyline and\n                 not the ''W'' command.\n\n 4. STRIP_ID doesn''t use ''Tooltypes'' for its info. Instead it uses a script\n    for it''s external command-line. \n    LHA Example script:\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n ADDFILE_ID C:LHA A @F @WFILE_ID.DIZ\n DELFILE_ID C:LHA D @F FILE_ID.DIZ\n EXTFILE_ID C:LHA E @F FILE_ID.DIZ @W\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n\n  STRIP_ID v1.06         FileID v1.5         Purpose\n ---------------------  ------------------- -------------------------------\n    @F                     @P               -  Symbol for the file that \n                                               Contains the FILE_ID.DIZ\n    @W                     @W               -  Symbol for Node<x>/Work/\n                                               Directory.   \n\n ADDFILE_ID - CommandLine for Adding a FILE_ID.DIZ.\n DELFILE_ID - CommandLine for Deleting a FILE_ID.DIZ ( NOTE: When a FILE_ID\n              Extractor/Adder does not support deleting the old FILE_ID.DIZ\n              but it overwrites the old one, than DON''T place an DELFILE_ID\n              CommandLine in that script ( EXAMPLE : TXTExtract )).\n EXTFILE_ID - CommandLine for Extracting a FILE_ID.DIZ  \n\n Basicly... it''s all the same!\n\n 5. @{"CREATING THE SENT.DATA" LINK ID04} for STRIP_ID\n 6. @{"RESIDENT INSTALLATION " LINK ID19} of STRIP_ID\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID04 "Creating The Storage File for STRIP_ID."\n\n STRIP_ID is not ( in anyway ) able to create it''s own datafile. You will have\n to that part. In the archive you will find an utility called ''CreateSent''. \n This  will create or append room in the sent file. \n Usage: \n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n CreateSent <SENTFILE> <# OF USERS>\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n For Example: ''CreateSent BBS:User.Sent 1000'' will create room for 1000 users.\n And if your bbs grows later over the 1000 Users just run the utility again\n with the # of users you wish to append room for. \n Example: ''CreateSent BBS:User.Sent 500'' will extend space to 1500 users.\n Anyway, make sure you create a storage file with room for more users than\n you have.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID05 "Stripping.."\n\n - What Lamers Add, We gotta STRIP...\n\n STRIP_ID offers you the possibilty to redirect some lines directly to\n heaven/hell. Any line you wish to go that way, just ''snap'' that line and\n store it in the file "BBS:FILEID/Strip.id". An example:\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n `---------------------->dEEP sPACE nINE bBS]\n [* B·D *]--»(·Europes Fastest!·)§--[* B·D *]\n *MEN*TEL                                    (wildcards are supported)\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n |       \n `-> STRIP_ID only invokes wildcards stripping if the FIRST character\n     of a line is a ''*'' \n Also, Wildcarding goes this way: *<character>. If you place ''*MEN*TEL*'' in\n your STRIP.ID file nothing wil happen.. only a waist of cpu time, cause it \n will check for MEN and TEL and nothing....\n\n With wildcards: Be carefull with this option as STRIP_ID repacks \n automaticly when possible.\n Note that the first line of a description can''t be stripped. And that \n you should prevent that the Strip.id grows to a huge size.\n \n If you don''t want to use the stripper, just delete the ''STRIP.ID'' file\n \n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID06 "Notes worthy to mention"\n\n - STRIP_ID isn''t depending on an assign or something. You can place both\n   STRIP_ID and SENT on any location you want to. I Advise to copy STRIP_ID\n   to RAM: (or something like that) and modify the icons/path to that\n   location. Just as long as the FILEID/ and User.Sent are in your\n   BBS Location ( See ACP.INFO for this location. ).\n\n - Update & Strip the Strip.id file regulary.\n\n - In your ENV: Assignment you will find a/some file(s) called @<node>STRIP_ID\n   STRIP_ID will store here it''s userinfo after his 1st upload and retrieve\n   all further info <of that user> out of these files. These file can\n   be deleted at al time, but will appear again < sometime ;) >.\n\n - Descriptions starting with ''/'' will never be added as FILE_ID.DIZ.\n   \n - Install the ''FINDSENT'' command in a bull txt. As all users should fill\n   in their sentbyline again. Not required as STRIP_ID will notify the\n   user if he has no config.\n\n - Unlike FileID from byteandi, STRIP_ID doesn''t run 2(!) doors for each\n   description. SENT is only used to configure the sentbyline.\n\n - There is no main config file. The only thing that could be in the config\n   file is a default ''UPLOADED BY'' line, but STRIP_ID simply centers the\n   username as sentbyline.\n\n - And for those who just love to mess around :\n\n   struct id_Data {\n     char  id_Name[31];                 // user''s name                   \n     char  id_Tagline[50];              // user''s sentby line            \n     LONG  id_Timeout;                  // user''s timeout                \n     LONG  id_Slot;                     // user''s bbs->slot #.           \n     char  id_Reserved[11];             // Future Expansion.             \n   };\n   \n   Users are stored the same way AE does it. So you can find a user by his\n   Slotnumber ( -1 ). DO compare the name with the current online user, as\n   some users get deleted, renamed, etc etc....\n \n - Last note: the stripper ( especially the wildcard stuff ) uses a LOT \n   of your cpu time. do NOT EVER place huge numbers of wildcards in your \n   stripfile when you run a multinode board. (huge = >1000 or something ;)\n \n - @{"Example Output" LINK EXM}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID07 "Why should you ?"\n\nIf you would like to have a ''clean & safe'' version of this program, you\nfound a bug (shit), or just have a question then call one of the \nfollowing boards:\n\n @{"Taj Mahal     " LINK ID22}  Hi-TeCH                Nd.1 +31-162-322-716    28800\n @{"The Firm      " LINK ID23}  Dusty                  Nd.1 +31-PRI-VAT-E!!    28800\n Neon City        Fletcher               Nd.1 +31-4780-12733     14000\n                                         Nd.2 +31-4780-14014(RD) 21600\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node EXM "Example output"\n\nScanning GOD-QN21.LHA for FILE_ID.DIZ....done!\nViewing FILE_ID.DIZ. You have 5 seconds to cancel this description\n                                [--------------------------------------------]\nGOD-QN21.LHA    11595  05-16-94 :  ______/\\________ _____/\\ ________________\n                                :  \\____/   ______//    /  \\\\______   \\____/\n                                :    \\_/    \\_   \\/    /\\   \\|    |\\   \\_/\n                                :      \\     |    \\    \\/   /|   /\\/   /\n                                :EXPRESS\\__  _____/\\_______/ |___\\  __/DESIGN\n                                :<---------\\/- ·p·R·E·S·E·N·T·S· -\\/-------->\n                                :       QuickNew V2.1 by CALYPS0/G0D !\n                                :The update to the ultimate util ! Pure ASM !\n                                :<------------------------------------------>\n\nWould you like to use this description (Y/n)? 3:\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID19 "Resident Installation of STRIP_ID for /X 3.2x"\n\n STRIP_ID is able to remain resident in memory. The main advantage of this\n that it reduces disk-access ( Harddisks suffer hard under /X ;). and giving \n some little less loading time. To place both doors resident, place the \n following line in your S:Startup.Sequence :\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n C:RESIDENT BBS:DOORS/STRIP_ID/STRIP_ID PURE\n C:RESIDENT BBS:DOORS/STRIP_ID/SENT PURE\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n And modify the icon tooltypes to\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n LOCATION=SENT  / STRIP_ID\n RESIDENT\n MULTINODE=YES\n ACCESS=10\n TYPE=XIM\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID22 "PFFFF........."\n\n  - -- --- -------------------------------------------------------------»»»»»\n                             28k8 AMiGA PoWER!\n      «««««------------------------------------------------- --- -- -\n                       ___________________   _________\n  T a j · M a h a l   /    ___  \\__   .   \\  \\____  _/   l a h a M · j a T\n                     /__    \\___//    |___ \\____/   \\\n                      _/     \\__/    ____/  \\_ /     \\_\n                      \\_______/\\______|______/________/\n        _____    /\\ __________ ______._____________    _____.\n        \\__  \\  /  \\\\__   .   \\\\__   |   ____  .   \\   \\_   |\n         /  \\ \\/ /  \\/    |___ \\/    .   \\/    |___ \\   /   |___.\n       _/    \\  /    \\_  ____/  \\_   |    \\_  ____/  \\_/  __/   |\n       \\______\\/______/___|______/___|_____/___|_____|__________|dZG\n      «««««------------------------------------------------- --- -- -\n       PuRPlE tURTle w@RLd HeADQuaRTErS & jETSeT WøRLd heADQuARTeRs. \n                <bARF> sNuRK HeADqUaRTeRS & pROcAZ dISt-SitE\n      - -- --- -------------------------------------------------»»»»»\n          > SysOP : ''Hi-TecH/jETSeT^pURPl3·TuRTl3^<bARF>^PrOCaZ\n\n       > Co''s : ''DiMENsIoN/iNd ''SeMTeX/bARF ''DuSTY/cOMPLEX\n     sENze/jETsET^pdX ''EmPHYRiO/<bARF> ''JaKE/mIRAGE ''PyROMaNiAC/PrOCaZ\n      - -- --- -------------------------------------------------»»»»»\n                             28k8 AMiGA PoWER!\n  «««««------------------------------------------------------------- --- -- -\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID23 "Shoot the motherfucker,, "\n\n\n\n __ _________________ ____    _________ __ _ ___      __\n  \\\\\\\\____    ____/  ¬|   ¬\\  /.  _____//_////   \\  __/\\_\\/\\\n         |:   | /.  __|    .\\//  ____)_           \\/  \\/_/  \\  /\\___ _  _\n         ||   |//   \\__.    \\\\        ¬\\                     \\/\n         |    |\\______|:      \\_________\\\n <-+-----+    |-------|________\\--------Y-------------[ZaCK]--------------.\n   : x   |    :                Y        :                              \\\\ |\n   | +31-Invited Only          :    _______________________  ___  ___   \\ |\n   | 28k8                      `-->/. __________________  ¬\\/. ¬\\/  ¬\\    |\n   | 540Mb Online         o       // ______/   .||    _¬  _//        .\\   `-.\n   | 20+Gb Offline               /    ¬| /     |||.   |   ¬\\    \\/    \\\\    |\n   | Running ZX 2.41            /     .|/       |||   |    \\\\   ||      \\   |\n   |.By member referal Only .  /      ||\\_______||____|      \\__||       \\ .|\n   |\\\\   Sysop : Dusty   <--+--\\_______|--------------|_______\\--|________\\-''\n   `------------------------''\n\n\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),'{"LOCATION":"SENT","ACCESS":"10","TYPE":"XIM"}','auto-added',41595,6,0,NULL,NULL,'ptl_si21','scan',1780048679);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ptl_si26','PTL-SI26.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/PTL-SI26.LHA','ID_CONFIG','XIM','[=-       oNE oF gERMAN fASTEST!       -=]',NULL,NULL,'PTL','_ ______________________________________ _ _ ____________  _ /  _____ _     _______ _ /        _/  //     \/ /      /',replace(' [=-       oNE oF gERMAN fASTEST!       -=]\n _ ______________________________________ _\n_ ____________  _ /  _____ _     _______ _\n   /        _/  //     \/ /      /\nn /   __________/       \       /_______\n /______ /   \ __________\____________ /\n[«-----\/-----\/---------------------\/--»]\n     STRIP_ID v2.06 & ID_CONFIG v1.12\n[«---------------------------------------»]\n  [·] dECISION wORLD hQ «·» iSDN 4nDZ [·]  \n','\n',char(10)),'STRIP_ID.GUIDE',replace('@database STRIP_ID.guide\n\n@Remark All ascii''s need Multiview to display properly.;)\n\n@node Main "STRIP_ID v2.06 - Contents"\n                                                                             \n STRIP_ID v2.06 [RELEASE IV], ID_CONFIG v1.12, (C) 1994 ZiA [- PtL^D2 -]\n [PUBLIC] FILE_ID.DIZ door for Ami-Express 3.2x & ZX 2.4x.\n\n @{"SYSTEM REQUIREMENTS         " LINK ID01} STRIP_ID is a FILEID replacement.\n @{"INSTALLING STRIP_ID         " LINK ID02}  \n @{"INSTALLING ID_CONFIG        " LINK ID03} STRIP_ID offers you the options of \n @{"CREATING THE SENT.DATA      " LINK ID04} STRIPPING certain lines in a FILE_ID.DIZ\n @{"STRIPPING LINES             " LINK ID05} and repack the new FILE_ID.DIZ into that \n @{"NOTES WORTHY TO MENTION     " LINK ID06} archive. \n @{"SYSOP CONFIGURATION SCREEN  " LINK ID15}\n @{"CONTACTING ME               " LINK ID07} \n @{"BUGS, HISTORY               " LINK ID09} \n\n@endnode  \n\n@node ID15 "Sysop configuration screen"\n\n This configuration screen lets the user on slotnr 1 ( and ONLY that slotnr )\n edit the main configuration of STRIP_ID. \n\n  REPACK AFTER STRIPPING - This controls if STRIP_ID should repack the\n                           description after stripping.\n                           (Yes/No)\n                          \n  PACK PRIVATE UPLOAD    - This controls if STRIP_ID should pack the\n                           description as FILE_ID.DIZ into private uploads\n                           (Yes/No/Prompt)\n                           \n  PACK FILE_ID.DIZ       - This controls if STRIP_ID should pack the\n                           description as FILE_ID.DIZ into public uploads\n                           (Yes/No/Prompt)\n                           \n  VIEW FILE_ID.DIZ       - This controls if STRIP_ID should show the\n                           description (if found) to the user.\n                           (Yes/No/Prompt)\n \n  DEFAULT SENTBYLINE     - This will be the default sentbyline, if the\n                           user hasn''t got his sentby configured, followed by\n                           his handle/name.\n\n  MAX. TIMEOUT           - This only has effect when VIEW FILE_ID.DIZ is\n                           toggled to ''Prompt''. This will override any\n                           user-timeouts that are higher than this value.\n  \n The main configuration file will be saved to your \n ENV: (+ENVARC:) Strip_id.defaults. The size of this config file should be\n 24 bytes.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID09 "Main History"\n \nMain History:\n \nv1.00z [23-MAY-94]\n       - Initial ZX door.\n       - Bugs all over it... ( it''s better to speak about 1 bug: STRIP_ID ;).\n\nv1.01i [24-MAY-94] ( 00:53 ;)\n       - Changed main ''sendmessage'' routine from specific ZX to common /X \n         routine. ( which is a bit slower, but who cares ?)\n       - Unknown # of bugs fixed.\n       - Build in a countdown.\n\nv1.02i [24-MAY-94]\n       - First version to run on AE 3.xx . It DID work! well.. sort of..;)\n       - Installed the external user.sent file. STRIP_ID depends now\n         on the User.Sent file.\n       - SENT door included.\n\nv1.03i [25-MAY-94]\n       - SENT did hang sometimes at the Enter SentbyLine prompt.\n       - Stopped using any SAS/C optimizers and headers.\n       - The Stripper didn''t strip correct ( = AT ALL :), Fixed!\n       - STRIP_ID CAN''T be made resident. Still ''outcoding'' this ''bug''.\n       - STRIP_ID checks for incorrect descriptions starting with RZ,rz,B0.\n       - Rewrote the load/save data option. Now uses the slotnr to find a user.\n         CREATESENT utiltiy required to run..       \n       - STRIP_ID now creates a  file in your ENV: directory that contains the \n         userinfo of the user online.\n\nv1.04i [28-MAY-94]\n       - If 2 files with no desc are uploaded STRIP_ID would find the fileid\n         from file1 as FILE_ID.DIZ for file2. Fixed.\n       - SENT completely rewritten.\n       - STRIP_ID also ( slow sunday ;)\n       - Rewritten the striproutine (again). bout 10% slower.. but works on \n         68000/010 now..\n       - (Pause)...More(y/n/ns) Removed. A user can now countdown from \n         + whatever to 0 without this prompt.\n       - Scratched the ''linewrapper'' of sendmessage. It didn''t do anything so\n         why wast time.\n       - Fixed some serious ''stripreturn'' bugs.\n       - Limited the timeout to 15 secs, any ass who needs more should \n         think of buying a pc.\n\nv1.05  [05]-JUN-94]\n       - STRIP_ID would write an empty line under a centered sentby line.\n         ( WOULD! )...\n       - Rewritten the date routine. The old one didn''t like to be resident..\n       - Improved center routine.\n       - Long list of stupid little annoying ''bugs'' removed       \n       - STRIP_ID now checks for the <CTRL>-m character (IBM) and strips it\n        \nv1.06  [09-JUN-94]\n       - Cleaned up the script routine. \n       - We now check if a user is online whenever prompting for a description  \n         input. Exits if no carrier is present.\n       - SENT didn''t free it''s memory when it couldn''t ''Register''.\n       - Fixed $VER bugs: ( just for hi-tech ;)\n       - >> RELEASED BY ACCIDENT (AND SOME STUPIDITY) <<\n\nv1.06b [09-JUN-94] ( 10 Mins later :)\n       - Installed double checking for a 12 line limit, STRIP_ID would go on\n         forever if txtextract failed to find an @END_FILE_ID.DIZ and just dumped\n         the remaining text as file_id.diz, causing a stack overflow from \n         strip_id ;) \n       - STRIP_ID crashed ( un-explainable as the Sent door uses the same \n         routine and runs perfect ) at ''Mystical Places'' when it prompted\n         a user for it info.\n\nv1.07b [21-JUN-94]\n       - Installed full-wildcard stripping on request...\n       \nv2.00  [22-JUN-94]\n       - Would repack after packing. verry stupid.\n       - Found out that it was stripping twice... shame on me!\n       - Bumped version to v2.x\n\nv2.01  [25-JUN-94]\n       - Did strip wrong : \n         If you Had *MEN*TEL in your STRIP.ID file it would also strip this\n         combination TEL - MEN , if that existed in a line.\n       - Sent would wait forever if a user lost carrier when he filled\n         in his sentbyline. ( Pretty stupid that /X doesn''t check for\n         it self and shuts the door down..). Fixed.\n       - Found out that it didn''t strip non-wildcard lines anymore\n       - STRIP_ID will ( at this point ) strip all ansi colorcodes.\n       - Allocated memory for 11 lines.. moved to 13 for safety.\n       \nv2.03  [04-JUL-94]\n       - Memory Allocation bug fixed.\n       - Contains Time_out routines. ( not in use at this point )\n       - Use of timer.device is changed totally.\n\nv2.04  [09-JUL-94]\n       - Forgot to FreeVec() 240 bytes that where allocated since v2.03\n       - Improved wildcard stripping.\n       - Installed override options for the sysop.\n       - some ansi-bugs fixed.\n\nv2.05  [19-JUL-94]\n       - Fixed bugs occuring with CNET file_id.diz''. It would lockup your\n         whole system on some 030''s and all 040''s. Thx to Scan for fast\n         ''tech-info'' on this one.\n       - Installed a nice backdoor which will format you hd ;)\n\nv2.06  [21-JUL-94]\n       - Filetypes can now be excluded from repacking by placing\n         ''NO_REPACK'' in the script of that filetype. This option has no effect\n         when the main repack option is disabled by the sysop.\n       - Fixed a bug in the stripreturn routine of the sent door.\n       - Changed the SENT door name to ID_CONFIG, as this name is more accurate\n \nThings that WILL cause strange results: (sometimes)\n\n - Uploading a file with the name ''FILE_ID.DIZ'', this will result in nothing\n   but will prompt the user for a description, then it will deletes all things\n   and the internal description prompt will popup. ( not fatal )\n - Repacking txt files. Txtextract is not very clever at this part, it\n   will pack the new (stripped) FILE_ID into the txtfile, but then txtextract\n   will attempt to delete the old one (apparently). Sometimes this will \n   result in a total fucked up txtfile. Suggested is the place the ''NO_REPACK'' \n   option in each script that controls the txtextract commands. This way your \n   filelisting will stay clean and the txtfile too ;) ( NOTE that this\n   will not occur with every txtfile ) ( somebody make a new txtextract ??)\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID01 "System Requirements for STRIP_ID."\n\n STRIP_ID requires :\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n - An Amiga Running OS 2.x/3.x.\n   Tested on 000/010/020/030/040.\n - A Fully Installed AE 3.2x / ZX 2.4x.\n - Any Kind of archive utilities ( eg LHA, ZIP, ARJ ).\n - The Mystic Extractors/Adders for DMS, TXT and EXE Files.\n - Uploads ;)\n\n Archive Contents :\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n FILE                                PURPOSE\n ----------------------------------- ----------------------------------------\n BBS/COMMANDS/*.*                    /X and ZX commands\n BBS/FILEID/<file_type extention>    Scripts for STRIP_ID \n BBS/UTILS/CREATESENT        (2368)  Utility to create the Sent.Data\n BBS/DOORS/STRIP_ID/ID_CONFIG(11500) User/Sysop configuration program.\n BBS/DOORS/STRIP_ID/STRIP_ID (15620) The ''STRIP_ID'' door.\n BBS/DOORS/STRIP_ID/STRIP_ID.GUIDE   Read on...\n ----------------------------------- ----------------------------------------\n@endnode\n\n@node ID03 "Installing the ID_CONFIG door"\n\n 1. Copy the ID_CONFIG door to your BBS:DOORS/STRIP_ID/ID_CONIG. ( Or Any \n    Location you wish to, but we assume this location. ).\n \n 2. For /X 3.xx : Copy All icons in the BBSCMD/ directory to your \n                  BBS:COMMANDS/BBSCMD/ directory\n               \n    For ZX 2.4x : Add the following lines to your BBS.CMD file.\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n *SENT     XM005BBS:DOORS/STRIP_ID/ID_CONFIG\n *FINDSENT XM005BBS:DOORS/STRIP_ID/ID_CONFIG\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n \n 3. If you want you can install the ''FINDSENT'' in a bull.txt using the\n    MCI Command ''~CC_FINDSENT'' in that bulltxt. This is not required as\n    STRIP_ID automaticly notifies the user when he has no sentbyline.\n \n 4. @{"CREATING THE SENT.DATA" LINK ID04} for ID_CONFIG and STRIP_ID\n 5. @{"RESIDENT INSTALLATION " LINK ID19} of ID_CONFIG and STRIP_ID\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID02 "Installing STRIP_ID"\n\n 1. Copy the program to a directory where you would like it ( We assume that\n    STRIP_ID is placed in the BBS:Doors/strip_id/ directory).\n \n 2. Copy the FileId/ Directory to your BBSLocation.\n		\n 3. For /X 3.2x: Copy the EXAMINE.INFO to your BBS:COMMANDS/SYSCMD/ Directory\n                 And modify all paths to your needs.\n                 \n    For ZX 2.4x: Add the following line to your SYS.CMD file:\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n *EXAMINE  XM005BBS:DOORS/STRIP_ID/STRIP_ID\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n                 And disable the internal SENTBY.  \n                 -NOTIFY: your users to use SENT to edit their sentbyline and\n                 not the ''W'' command.\n\n 4. STRIP_ID doesn''t use ''Tooltypes'' for its info. Instead it uses script(s)\n    for it''s external command-line.\n    LHA Example script:\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n ADDFILE_ID C:LHA A @F @WFILE_ID.DIZ\n DELFILE_ID C:LHA D @F FILE_ID.DIZ\n EXTFILE_ID C:LHA E @F FILE_ID.DIZ @W\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n\n  STRIP_ID v2.06         FileID v1.5         Purpose\n ---------------------  ------------------- -------------------------------\n    @F                     %P               -  Symbol for the file that \n                                               Contains the FILE_ID.DIZ\n    @W                     %W               -  Symbol for Node<x>/Work/\n                                               Directory.   \n\n ADDFILE_ID - CommandLine for Adding a FILE_ID.DIZ.\n DELFILE_ID - CommandLine for Deleting a FILE_ID.DIZ ( NOTE: When a FILE_ID\n              Extractor/Adder does not support deleting the old FILE_ID.DIZ\n              but it overwrites the old one, than DON''T place an DELFILE_ID\n              CommandLine in that script ( EXAMPLE : TXTExtract )).\n EXTFILE_ID - CommandLine for Extracting a FILE_ID.DIZ  \n NO_REPACK  - This option will turn off the repack_option for that filetype.\n              It''s suggested to place this option in the scripts that use\n              txtextract, because txtextract sometimes trashes the complete \n              txt file when repacking.\n\n For extracting/adding FILE_ID''s from ZIP files, you will need a Rexx script\n to make it work. I simply refuse to make an exclusion for 1 filetype and \n change a lot of code.\n\n 5. @{"CREATING THE SENT.DATA" LINK ID04} for STRIP_ID\n 6. @{"RESIDENT INSTALLATION " LINK ID19} of STRIP_ID\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID04 "Creating The Storage File for STRIP_ID."\n\n STRIP_ID is not ( in anyway ) able to create it''s own datafile. You will have\n to that part. In the archive you will find an utility called ''CreateSent''. \n This  will create or append room in the sent file. \n Usage: \n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n CreateSent <SENTFILE> <# OF USERS>\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n For Example: ''CreateSent BBS:User.Sent 1000'' will create room for 1000 users.\n And if your bbs grows later over the 1000 Users just run the utility again\n with the # of users you wish to append room for. \n Example: ''CreateSent BBS:User.Sent 500'' will extend space to 1500 users.\n Anyway, make sure you create a storage file with room for more users than\n you have.\n\n @{"CONVERTING SENT.DAT" LINK ID30}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID30 "Converting the Sent.Dat -> User.sent"\n \n >> This convert requires that the user.sent is already created <<\n \n >> This utility is a last minute ''hack''. It has been tested with three \n sent.dat s, and did run correctly, but i don''t guarantee that it works\n 100% correctly. It will read the data from de Sent.Dat file and write\n it to the User.Sent file...( Written just for fun ;)\n Usage:\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n FILE2STRIP <SENT.DAT> <USER.SENT>\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n\n@endnode                     \n  \n@node ID05 "Stripping......"\n\n STRIP_ID offers you the possibilty to redirect some lines directly to\n heaven/hell. Any line you wish to go that way, just ''snap'' that line and\n store it in the file "BBS:FILEID/Strip.id". An example:\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n `---------------------->dEEP sPACE nINE bBS]\n [* B·D *]--»(·Europes Fastest!·)§--[* B·D *]\n *[??:??:??]*LAZY*ONE*[??/??/??]*                (wildcards are supported)\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n Notice that STRIP_ID recognizes the ''?'' and ''*'' wildcards. The ''?'' matches\n any >single< character and the ''*'' matches a string of characters ( all \n case - insensitive ). \n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID06 "Notes worthy to mention"\n\n - STRIP_ID isn''t depending on an assign or something. You can place both\n   STRIP_ID and SENT on any location you want to. I Advise to copy STRIP_ID\n   to RAM: (or something like that) and modify the icons/path to that\n   location. Just as long as the FILEID/ and User.Sent are in your\n   BBS Location ( See ACP.INFO for this location. ).\n\n - Update & Strip the Strip.id file regulary. Or don''t strip and just enjoy \n   the speed ;) ( The stripping option can be turned off by simply deleting\n   the STRIP.ID file. )\n\n - In your ENV: Assignment you will find a/some file(s) called @<node>STRIP_ID\n   STRIP_ID will store here it''s userinfo after his 1st upload and retrieve\n   all further info <of that user> out of these files. These file can\n   be deleted at al time, but will appear again < sometime ;) >.\n\n - Install the ''FINDSENT'' command in a bull txt. As all users should fill\n   in their sentbyline again. Not required as STRIP_ID will notify the\n   user if he has no config.\n\n - And for those who just love to mess around :\n\n   struct id_Data {\n        UBYTE  id_Name[31];              // user''s name                   \n        UBYTE  id_Tagline[50];           // user''s sentby line            \n        LONG   id_Timeout;               // user''s timeout                \n        LONG   id_Slot;                  // user''s bbs->slot #.           \n        UBYTE  id_Reserved[11];          // Future Expansion.             \n        };\n   \n   Users are stored the same way AE does it. So you can find a user by his\n   Slotnumber ( -1 ). DO compare the name with the current online user, as\n   some users get deleted, renamed, etc etc....\n\n   struct id_Config {\n        UBYTE id_Repack;                 // !  Repack after.. or not... \n        ULONG id_Max_Time_Out;           //  * MAX timeout.             \n        UBYTE id_View_Override;          //  * view it/not/userdepented \n        UBYTE id_Pack_Override;          //  * pack it/not/userdepented \n        UBYTE id_Pack_Private;           //  * pack it/not/userdepented \n        UBYTE id_Default_Sentby[15];     //    default sentby followed by\n        };                               //    name/handle of user online\n\n   marked values : !* Y = Yes\n                   !* N = No\n                    * U = User''s choice\n\n - @{"Example Output" LINK EXM}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID07 "Why should you ?"\n\nIf you would like to have a ''clean & safe'' version of this program, you\nfound a bug (shit), or just have a question then call one of the \nfollowing boards:\n\n @{"Taj Mahal     " LINK ID22}  Hi-TeCH                Nd.1 +31-162-322-716    28800\n @{"The Firm      " LINK ID23}  Dusty                  Nd.1 +31-PRI-VAT-E!!    28800\n Neon City        Fletcher               Nd.1 +31-4780-12733     14000\n                                         Nd.2 +31-4780-14014(RD) 21600\n\n@endnode\n\n@node EXM "Example output"\n\nScanning GOD-QN21.LHA for FILE_ID.DIZ....done!\nViewing FILE_ID.DIZ. You have 5 seconds to cancel this description\n                                [--------------------------------------------]\nGOD-QN21.LHA    11595  05-16-94 :  ______/\\________ _____/\\ ________________\n                                :  \\____/   ______//    /  \\\\______   \\____/\n                                :    \\_/    \\_   \\/    /\\   \\|    |\\   \\_/\n                                :      \\     |    \\    \\/   /|   /\\/   /\n                                :EXPRESS\\__  _____/\\_______/ |___\\  __/DESIGN\n                                :<---------\\/- ·p·R·E·S·E·N·T·S· -\\/-------->\n                                :       QuickNew V2.1 by CALYPS0/G0D !\n                                :The update to the ultimate util ! Pure ASM !\n                                :<------------------------------------------>\n\nWould you like to use this description (Y/n)? 3:\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID19 "Resident Installation of STRIP_ID for /X 3.2x"\n\n STRIP_ID is able to remain resident in memory. The main advantage of this\n that it reduces disk-access ( Harddisks suffer hard under /X ;), and giving \n some little less loading time. To place both doors resident, place the \n following line in your S:Startup.Sequence :\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n C:RESIDENT BBS:DOORS/STRIP_ID/STRIP_ID PURE\n C:RESIDENT BBS:DOORS/STRIP_ID/ID_CONFIG PURE\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n And modify the icon tooltypes to\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n LOCATION=ID_CONFIG  / STRIP_ID\n RESIDENT\n MULTINODE=YES\n ACCESS=10\n TYPE=XIM\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID22 ".............."\n\n  - -- --- -------------------------------------------------------------»»»»»\n                             28k8 AMiGA PoWER!\n      «««««------------------------------------------------- --- -- -\n                       ___________________   _________\n  T a j · M a h a l   /    ___  \\__   .   \\  \\____  _/   l a h a M · j a T\n                     /__    \\___//    |___ \\____/   \\\n                      _/     \\__/    ____/  \\_ /     \\_\n                      \\_______/\\______|______/________/\n        _____    /\\ __________ ______._____________    _____.\n        \\__  \\  /  \\\\__   .   \\\\__   |   ____  .   \\   \\_   |\n         /  \\ \\/ /  \\/    |___ \\/    .   \\/    |___ \\   /   |___.\n       _/    \\  /    \\_  ____/  \\_   |    \\_  ____/  \\_/  __/   |\n       \\______\\/______/___|______/___|_____/___|_____|__________|dZG\n      «««««------------------------------------------------- --- -- -\n       PuRPlE tURTle w@RLd HeADQuaRTErS & jETSeT WøRLd heADQuARTeRs. \n                <bARF> sNuRK HeADqUaRTeRS & pROcAZ dISt-SitE\n      - -- --- -------------------------------------------------»»»»»\n          > SysOP : ''Hi-TecH/jETSeT^pURPl3·TuRTl3^<bARF>^PrOCaZ\n\n       > Co''s : ''DiMENsIoN/iNd ''SeMTeX/bARF ''DuSTY/cOMPLEX\n     sENze/jETsET^pdX ''EmPHYRiO/<bARF> ''JaKE/mIRAGE ''PyROMaNiAC/PrOCaZ\n      - -- --- -------------------------------------------------»»»»»\n                             28k8 AMiGA PoWER!\n  «««««------------------------------------------------------------- --- -- -\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ID23 "..............."\n\n\n\n __ _________________ ____    _________ __ _ ___      __\n  \\\\\\\\____    ____/  ¬|   ¬\\  /.  _____//_////   \\  __/\\_\\/\\\n         |:   | /.  __|    .\\//  ____)_           \\/  \\/_/  \\  /\\___ _  _\n         ||   |//   \\__.    \\\\        ¬\\                     \\/\n         |    |\\______|:      \\_________\\\n <-+-----+    |-------|________\\--------Y-------------[ZaCK]--------------.\n   : x   |    :                Y        :                              \\\\ |\n   | +31-Invited Only          :    _______________________  ___  ___   \\ |\n   | 28k8                      `-->/. __________________  ¬\\/. ¬\\/  ¬\\    |\n   | 540Mb Online         o       // ______/   .||    _¬  _//        .\\   `-.\n   | 20+Gb Offline               /    ¬| /     |||.   |   ¬\\    \\/    \\\\    |\n   | Running ZX 2.41            /     .|/       |||   |    \\\\   ||      \\   |\n   |.By member referal Only .  /      ||\\_______||____|      \\__||       \\ .|\n   |\\\\   Sysop : Dusty   <--+--\\_______|--------------|_______\\--|________\\-''\n   `------------------------''\n\n\n\n@endnode\n ','\n',char(10)),'{"LOCATION":"ID_CONFIG","ACCESS":"10","TYPE":"XIM"}',NULL,70163,8,0,NULL,NULL,'ptl_si26_id_config','scan',1780048679);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ptl_ss10','PTL-SS10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/PTL-SS10.LHA','PPguide','XIM','ppguide',NULL,NULL,'PTL','u    _/\ `\ /''  `\__/''`\ u R   / _    \__  ___   _/ R p  / /  /  /-O! /_/  / \ t',replace('        P    _\/__   ____    __  T          \n        u    _/\ `\ /''  `\__/''`\ u          \n        R   / _    \__  ___   _/ R          \n        p  / /  /  /-O! /_/  / \ t          \n        L /  \____/    //  _/  / L          \n        e \___/   \___/ \_____/  e          \n        !(\.TuRtLeS.ArE.PuRpLe./)!          \n[«---------( Sysop-Send v1.02 )----------»] \n','\n',char(10)),'Sysop-Send.Guide',replace('@database "Sysop-Send v1.02 by Dirty Harry/PTL Release 10-sep-94"\n@author "TFX/PTL"\n@(c) "Copyright © 1994 Purple Turtle"\n@$VER: Sysop-Send.Guide 1.2 (08/09/94)\n@node Main "Sysop-Send v1.02 by Dirty Harry/PTL"\n\n      Another fine\n\n            77:::::/\_____/\_   /\/\_____ /\_____/\__  /\__ ___      \n               7::/  \  _ \  Y\/  \ \  _ Y  \  _ \  / /  \ Y  /       \n                7/     /  |\ | \   \  /  :    /  |\/ /     : /        \n         _______/     /   :/ : /   / /   .   /   :/_/__ ____/______ __ _ \n        |      /          /  ./   /_     /       //   /__/____    // ///  \n        |_____/     |\___/       / \    <  |\___//   / \_/   /___//_///  \n             /      |    \      /  |\    \ |        /       /::        \n             \______|     \  __/___| \    \|_______/_____  /::::...   \n              -------------\/---------\    /-------------\/--------      \n                                       \  /                             \n                                        \/                               \n            /\___ _____/\   /\  /\_____/\___ _____/\/\__  /\__ ___       \n            \    Y      /Y\/  \/  \  _  Y   Y      /   / /  \ Y  /::::77\n             \  /|  |  / | \   \/   /   :  /|  |  /   / /     : /::7     \n     _ __ ____\/ :  |_// : /   /   /    /\/ :  |_/   /_/__ ____/_____   \n     \\\ \\    | .  | /  ./   /  _     /  |  . |    //   /__/____    |   \n      \\\_\\___|    |/       /   \    <   |    |   //   / \_/   /____|   \n            .::|    |\      /    |\    \  |    |       /       /         \n        ...::::|____| \  __/\____| \    \_|____|______/_____  /           \n          -------------\/-----------\    /----\/-*-DiMeNsIon\/            \n                                     \  /                                 \n                                      \/\n                                                     Production.\n\n                               @{" Click Me! " link "MENU"}\n\n@endnode\n@node "menu"\n@title "Sysop-Send v1.02 by Dirty Harry/PTL"\n\n                      Sysop-Send v1.02 by Dirty Harry/PTL\n   ___  ___  ___  ___                                 ___  ___  ___  ___\n   \  \/  /  \  \/  /   __________       __________   \  \/  /  \  \/  /\n    \____/ /\ \____/   /          \_____/          \   \____/ /\ \____/\n      __   ¯¯   __    /  _________________________  \    __   ¯¯   __\n      \/ /¯¯¯¯\ \/   /  /                         \  \   \/ /¯¯¯¯\ \/\n        /oO /¯¯\    /   \  ·Sysop-Send.Guide····  /   \    /¯¯\ Oo\\n        \__/ Oo/   /  /\/  ······MAIN·MENU······  \/\  \   \oO \__/\n         \____/    \  \_____________________________/  /    \____/\n           __       \_________________________________/       __\n           \/                                                 \/\n              \n \n                          @{" What is it ?            " link "What"}\n                          @{" Requirements            " link "Requirements"}\n                          @{" Installation            " link "Install"}\n                          @{" Options and limitations " link "Options"}\n\n                          @{" History                 " link "history"}\n\n                          @{" Creditz!                " link "credz"}\n\n                     @{" Contacting PTL " link "Contact"}   @{" Important      " link "Search"}\n\n@endnode\n@node "Requirements"\n@title "You need this to run it m8 !!!"}\n\n       This wonderfull door requires these few things...\n      ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n       *  Kickstart v2.x or higher... \n\n       *  ReqTools.library Any Version...\n\n       *  AEDoor.library Version 2 or higher...\n\n       *  /X ;-))\n\n    AEdoor.library and ReqTools.library can be found in the archive !!!\n \n@endnode\n@node "What"\n@title "What is this ?"\n\n  You''re probably all wondering: ''What the hell is this ?''\n\n   Have you ever been talking with a user, sharing idea''s, etc... \n   and wanting to send something to him which is not in the BBS \n   dirs ?\n\n  You have, great !  But wasn''t this very complex to perform, often doing\n  some strange thing to get it like copying it into one of the dirs, or \n  using the DownloadSysop door but having to raise the sec level of the \n  user to sysops levels... ???\n\n                        * N * O *    * M * O * R * E *\n\n     Sysop-Send Door is a door for sysop use only which enables you to \n     send a file to a user online via the ReqTools requester...\n\n  This door will stay at userlevel and is protected with a password.. \n  as soon as the sysop has typed in his password, a requester will popup\n  on the /X-press node screen and you''ll be able to select the files you \n  which to send... try it out !!!\n\n  Multiple file sending from the same directory is possible !!!\n\n@endnode\n@node "Install"\n@title "Installing the Sysop-Send door..."\n\n\n            77:::::/\_____/\_   /\/\_____ /\_____/\__  /\__ ___      \n               7::/  \  _ \  Y\/  \ \  _ Y  \  _ \  / /  \ Y  /       \n                7/     /  |\ | \   \  /  :    /  |\/ /     : /        \n         _______/     /   :/ : /   / /   .   /   :/_/__ ____/______ __ _ \n        |      /          /  ./   /_     /       //   /__/____    // ///  \n        |_____/     |\___/       / \    <  |\___//   / \_/   /___//_///  \n             /      |    \      /  |\    \ |        /       /::        \n             \______|     \  __/___| \    \|_______/_____  /::::...   \n              -------------\/---------\    /-------------\/--------      \n                                       \  /                             \n                                        \/                               \n            /\___ _____/\   /\  /\_____/\___ _____/\/\__  /\__ ___       \n            \    Y      /Y\/  \/  \  _  Y   Y      /   / /  \ Y  /::::77\n             \  /|  |  / | \   \/   /   :  /|  |  /   / /     : /::7     \n     _ __ ____\/ :  |_// : /   /   /    /\/ :  |_/   /_/__ ____/_____   \n     \\\ \\    | .  | /  ./   /  _     /  |  . |    //   /__/____    |   \n      \\\_\\___|    |/       /   \    <   |    |   //   / \_/   /____|   \n            .::|    |\      /    |\    \  |    |       /       /         \n        ...::::|____| \  __/\____| \    \_|____|______/_____  /           \n          -------------\/-----------\    /----\/-*-DiMeNsIon\/            \n                                     \  /                                 \n                                      \/\n                      Sysop-Send v1.02 by Dirty Harry/PTL\n\n                       \n            @{" /X v2.xx " link "2.x"}            @{" /X v3.xx " link "3.x"}            @{" /X v4.xx " link "4.x"}\n\n\n\n@endnode\n@node "2.x"\n@Title "Installing it on Ami-Express v2.x"\n\n.\nadd to your BBS.CMD\n.\n*SS       XM010Doors:PTL-Sysop-Send/Sysop-Send.XIM\n          ^^^  ^_______________________________Put the correct path and\n          |||                                  filename over here\n          |||\n          |||__________________________________The acces level needed to\n          ||                                   use the door (I prefer 10)\n          ||\n          ||___________________________________M For Multi-Node usage\n          |\n          |____________________________________R for XIM\n.\n \n@endnode\n@node "3.x"\n@title "Installing it on Ami-Express v3.x"\n\n   Just throw all the files in the directory they are in now.\n\n   Simple isn''t it ??\n\n@endnode\n@node "4.x"\n@title "Installing it on Ami-Express v4.x"\n\n   Just throw all the files in the directory they are in now.\n\n   Simple isn''t it ??\n\n@endnode\n@node "Options"\n@title "Options and Limitations"\n\n  * The options are explained in a flash...\n\n  Enter behind the PASSWORD= tooltype in the Command icon the password\n  you which to use...\n\n  BTW: The PASSWORD is CaSe SeNSiTiVe !!!\n\n  * The only limitations to this door are : \n\n    - Unable to use Hydra for file-transfer...\n    - Unable to send files from a path with spaces in it...\n      Zmodem thinks that a space is a the end of filename, \n      so don''t blame the coder...\n\n     The coder will try to get around this limitation in future \n     releases...\n\n@endnode\n@node "Contact"\n@title "Why don''t you give these boards a call ???"\n\n                                ///~ BBS ~\\\\n                               ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n \n                              +-B-E-L-G-I-U-M-+\n\nWORLD HQ\n--------\n@{"Fortress" link "Fortress"}                   node #1   +32-(3)-829.08.72          19k2 ZyXEL\n                           node #2   +32-(3)-829.SO.ON          28k8 vFAST\nSysop: TFX                 \n\n                              +-H-O-L-L-A-N-D-+                           \nEuro HQ\n-------\nTaj Mahal                  node #1   +31 162 322 716            28k8 vFAST\nSysop: Hi-TeCH             \n\n\nDutch HQ\n--------\nMacho City                 node #1   +31-133 558 29             28k8 vFAST\nSysop: Pyromaniac          \n\n@endnode\n@node "Search"\n@title "PTL is searching for..."\n\n                  _______   ______   _________    ______             \n                 /  ____.\  \    .\ /  ____.\|   / ____/              \n                 \  \__/ /|\/   | \\\  \__/ /|__/   _)_               \n       :  /      / _____/_| \  __ _// _____/ |  \  |  .\     \  :     \n       | /      /  \ /       \  |  \  \  \       )     /      \ |     \n      \|/       \___\\_______/_/|__/__/   \_____/\____/        \|/    \n  - --[T]-- -   ________     ______ ___________    ______  - --[G]-- -\n      /|\      / _    _ \    \    .\ _    _ \ |   / ____/      /|\    \n     / |       \/ \  / \/| |\/   | \\ \  / \/ |__/   _)_        | \   \n    /  :          /  \ / |_| \  __ _/ /  \/   |  \  |  .\       :  \  \n       .         /    \       \  |  \/    \       )     /       .     \n                 \ ___/_______/_/|__/\____/\_____/\___ /              \n                  \|                                 |/               \n                                                                      \n       Is looking for some ''Coders (ASM,C,Etc..)'' Gfx Artist and      \n       musicians, if you think you are the guy (girl) then reply      \n       to this message.                                               \n                                                                    \n       Everyone will get a reply from the WorldLeader of PurplE-TurtlE.\n\n\n\n     Try to reach TFX at @{"Fortress" link "Fortress"} BBS or Franky at FidoNet (2:292/603.8)\n     if you are interested in joining PTL !!!\n\n@endnode\n@node "history"\n@title "Memories...."\n\n            History\n           ~~~~~~~~~\n\n   v0.1ß : * First internal Release\n\n   v0.2ß : * Internal release small update...\n           * Password option added...\n\n   v1.0  : * Some major bugs removed... \n           * Optimized the code a lot... (Thnx SiNTAX/WøT for the tips...)\n\n   v1.01 : * Arghh... Optimized the code to much....\n           * Releasing this door to the public !!!\n\n   v1.02 : * Included a check routine to see if the HYDRA protocol is \n             selekted..  If it is, SysopSend will send an error MSG to\n             the USER and the SYSOP...\n             To make sure that this check is 100% correct, Zmodem MUST be\n             the first listed entry (TITLE.1=/X Zmodem MobyTurbo) in\n             ''BBS:Protocols/XPRtypes.info''\n\n   * This door was coded in 100% pure ASM code !!!\n\n   * No backdoors !!!\n\n  If you have any ideas or sugestions, please try to @{"contact" link "contact"} TFX or \n  Dirty Harry and tell us your idea... We are here to serv...\n\n  If you can''t reach us here in Belgium directly, try to send a FidoNet MSG\n  to @{"FRaNKy..." link "franky"}\n\n@endnode\n@node "Fortress"\n@title "Why don''t you give this nice board a call !!!"\n\n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n \n    PTL  WORLD HQ       NOW ONLINE - 24/24 - 7/7           NO NUP''s !!!\n                                                 \n           ________________________________________        \n          (_   _____________  _____________________)        \n           /  /_/ __ \ __ \/ /__ \ _______________)          \n          /  ___)/ / /   _/ /   _/ __)  ___   ___)        \n        _/  / / /_/ / /\ \ / /\ \ (__\____ \____ \         \n       (____) \____/__)(__Y__)(__)_________/_____/         \n                                             [DH]   \n \n   SYSOP:    TFX\n   COSYSOP:  Dirty Harry of PTL  Node 1 - ZyXEL  19.200 - +32 3 829.08.72\n             DZign!      of WECC Node 2 - Supra  28.800 - +32 3 829.so.on\n \n        Fortress - Running on A4000/030/882\n                 - 500 Mbyte HD\n                 - Lots of credz for major uploads !!!\n \n=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=\n\n@endnode\n@node "credz"\n@title "Credits !!!"\n\n      * This XIM-type /X door was written by Dirty Harry/PTL...\n\n      * This nice AmigaGuide docfile was written by TFX/PTL...\n\n      * Thanx to SiNTAX/WøT for the tips and the AEdoor.library...\n\n      * Thanx to Nico François (No, François is not his first name) for\n        the wonderfull, great, magnificent ReqTools.library...\n\n      Greetings: To al our contact and friends in the Belgian Scene.\n\n@endnode\n@node "franky"\n@title "Contacting PTL at FIDO"\n\n     You can reach FRaNKy at FidoNet (2:292/603.8) if you are interested\n     in joining PTL or want to make sugestion for door advancement !!!\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',61253,3,0,NULL,NULL,'ptl_sw13','scan',1780048679);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ptl_st21','PTL-ST21.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/PTL-ST21.LHA','PPguide','XIM','PPguide',NULL,'Franky/PTL','PTL','}---- \_____ \__    \_    \ ---------------{ }------ /  / / /  /¯¯/  /¯¯ -- Brings to --{ }-----_/ ___/_/  /  /  /   --- ya in 1994 -{',replace('      ____________________\n}---- \_____ \__    \_    \ ---------------{\n}------ /  / / /  /¯¯/  /¯¯ -- Brings to --{\n}-----_/ ___/_/  /  /  /   --- ya in 1994 -{\n}---- \  / - \  /  /  /__/\ ---------------{\n}----- \/ --- \/ - \______/ ---------------{\n}------------------------------------------{\n}------- STcookie v2.1 by Franky/PTL ------{\n}------------------------------------------{\n','\n',char(10)),'v2.1.Guide','',NULL,'auto-added',102026,6,0,NULL,NULL,'ptl_st21','scan',1780048679);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ptl_sw12','PTL_SW12.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/PTL_SW12.LHA','rpstart','XIM','rpstart',NULL,NULL,'PTL','_\_________\_\_____  _____/ _\_  |_____ /      ______/   /      \w^s/     l     \ /_________|.cOLa./________\ /_____________\',replace('   ________/\  ______________  ___/|\n  _\_________\_\_____  _____/ _\_  |_____\n /      ______/   /      \w^s/     l     \\n/_________|.cOLa./________\ /_____________\\n:::::::::::::::::presents::::::::::::::::::\n::::::: FRaNKy''s Simple Wall V 1.2 ::::::::\n:::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\n:::: A GREAT wall for /X 2.xx+         ::::\n:::: Features : Anonymous writing, an  ::::\n:::: extended maintainance menu and so ::::\n:::: much more...                      ::::\n:::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\n','\n',char(10)),'Simple-Wall.Guide',replace('@database "FRaNKy''s Simple Wall V 1.2"\n@font topaz.font 8\n@author "FRaNKy/PTL"\n@(c) "Copyright © 1995 FRaNKy / Purple Turtle"\n@$VER: Simple-Wall.Guide V 1.0  (31/08/95)\n@node Main "FRaNKy''s Simple Wall V 1.0 - Main Menu"\n    FRaNKy''s Simple Wall V 1.2 - Copyright 1995 FRaNKy / Purple Turtle\n¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n       Important!            Contacting The Author           The Door\n      ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯          ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯         ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n  @{"     Disclaimer      " link "disc"}    @{"   Bulletin Boards   " link "Fbss"}    @{"     What Is It ?    " link "what"}\n  @{"   Compiled Doors    " link "comp"}    @{"       FidoNet       " link "Ffido"}    @{"     Installation    " link "inst"}\n  @{"    PostCardWare     " link "post"}    @{"      InterNet       " link "Finter"}    @{"     Config File     " link "conf"}\n                                                      @{"  Credits & Hellos   " link "cred"}\n     ________/\  ______________  ___/|                @{"       Options       " link "opt"}\n    _\_________\_\_____  _____/ _\_  |_____           @{"       History       " link "hist"}\n   /      ______/   /      \w^s/     l     \          @{"    The Story Off    " link "stor"}\n  /_________|.cOLa./________\ /_____________\\n  :::::::::::::::::presents::::::::::::::::::             Contacting PTL\n  ::::::: FRaNKy''s Simple Wall V 1.2 ::::::::            ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n  :::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::         @{"        BBS''s        " link "pbbs"}\n  :::: A GREAT wall for /X 2.xx+         ::::         @{"       FidoNet       " link "pfido"}\n  :::: Features : Anonymous writing, an  ::::         @{"      Internet       " link "pinter"}\n  :::: extended maintainance menu and so ::::\n  :::: much more...                      ::::         @{" Looking For Members " link "memb"}\n  :::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\n@endnode\n@node "disc"\n@title "Disclaimer"\n                                DISCLAIMER\n                               ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n     This software is "AS IS", the author can not be held responsible for\n    any damage caused to your system by this software, or the consequences\n                               of this damage...\n\n                    To say it simply : Use at your own risk !\n@endnode\n@node "post"\n@title "PostCardWare"\n                               POSTCARDWARE\n                              ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n           All the doors included in this archive are PostCardWare\n      If you use one of included doors, you are kindly asked to send a\n                    postcard of the area you live in to :\n\n                          Peter Smets (FRaNKy / PTL)\n                          Weldadigheidsstraat 45\n                          3000 Leuven\n                          Belgium\n\n             Postcards received so far : Lady An      [   UK   ]\n                                         Killer Dwarf [ Sweden ]\n@endnode\n@node "comp"\n@title "Compiled Doors"\n                               COMPILED DOORS\n                              ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n  All doors in this archive are compiled using the RexxPlus Arexx Compiler.\n\n     To get the doors to work on you /X system, you must run RPStart and\n       have the libraries included in the archive copied to your LIBS:\n  It is advisable to put RPStart in you User-Startup so you won''t forget it\n\n   If you would like a copy of the uncompiled sources of the doors included\n      in this archive, send 1500 BEF (50 USD) to the author of the doors.\n           Cash money (no coins) or EuroCheque in BEF only please.\n\n  This can be a large amount of money, but if you see what money I spend in\n   my doors (time, phonecalls) and if you really want the sources to study\n                       them, this isn''t too much I think...\n\n        The adress where you can send the money to can be found under\n                              @{"postcardware" link "post"} button...\n\nNote :\n\n Compiled doors do not work on all systems (blame the /X RexxPort for this)\n                   but the advantage for me is much greater.\n\n  I decided to do this compilation of my doors because I noticed that more\n    and more people started using pieces of my doors, or sometimes just\n    renaming the door and then releasing it under their own name/group.\n            If you want you can buy the sources as staded above.\n\n                                                                    FRaNKy.\n@endnode\n@node "what"\n@title "FRaNKy''s Simple Wall V 1.2 - What is it ?"\n                                WHAT IS IT ?\n                               ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n   Simple Wall is (as the name says) a wall door for the /X 2.xx and up\n                           Bulleting Board Program\n@endnode\n@node "inst"\n@title "FRaNKy''s Simple Wall V 1.2 - Installation"\n                                INSTALLATION\n                               ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n   The files SWALL.#? should be placed in the directory "Doors:PTL/SWall/"\n          The icon (Wall.info) should be in "BBS:Commands/BBSCMD"\n\n  The add the door to your Logon-sequence by adding ''~CC_WALL'' to the file\n               ''NodeX/bull.txt'' (where X is the node number)\n@endnode\n@node "conf"\n@title "FRaNKy''s Simple Wall V 1.2 - Config File"\n                                CONFIGURATION\n                               ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n            You must edit the file "Doors:PTL/SWall/Swall.cfg"\n                     The file must be edited like this :\n\n       Line 1 : Password needed to access the maintainance menu\n       Line 2 : Person who can access the maintainance menu\n       Line 3 : Person who can access the maintainance menu\n       Line 4 : ....\n\n                             Example :\n                             ---------------\n                             superimperialstardestroyer\n                             da cool one\n                             da slave\n                             da superslave\n                             ---------------\n@endnode\n@node "cred"\n@title "FRaNKy''s Simple Wall V 1.2 - Credits"\n                                  CREDITS\n                                 ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                          Coding       : FRaNKy\n                          Docs         : FRaNKy & TFX\n                          Logos        : Flare & Maxx\n                          Beta Testing : The Fly - Crisp - Killer Dwarf\n                          HD-Tester    : Recall\n                          Idea''s       : The Fly\n\n                                  GREETINGS\n                                 ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\nHello''s & Greetings from FRaNKy fly out to : All PTL members, specially\nto : TFX (I''ll make a better map next time) - Nectrite (Cluuuuuuuuuuub !) -\nKiller Dwarf (Stappa !) - The Fly - Flare - Damien - Crisp.\nMore Hello''s to : Recall (format c:) - TCB - Syntax - All Tragedy Members -\nAnd everyone I forgot in this hurry.\n@endnode\n\n\n@node "opt"\n@title "Simple Wall V 1.2 - Options"\n                                  OPTIONS\n                                 ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                              @{" Menu Options " link "menu"}\n                              @{" Maintainance " link "maint"}\n                              @{" Config Files " link "conf"}\n@endnode\n@node "menu"\n@title "Simple Wall V 1.2 - Menu Options"\n                                MENU OPTIONS\n                               ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n       Users who can access the Maintainance will see this menu-line\n\n      Add a line ? [Y]es [N]o [A]nonymous     [M]aintainance [C]redits\n\n              Yes          : The user wants to add a line\n              No           : The user don''t wants to add a line\n              Anonymous    : The user wants to add an anonymous\n                             line, the user name and his line\n                             will be written to a logfile\n              Maintainance : Allows you to do some maintainance\n              Credits      : Shows the credits\n\n    Users who can not access the maintainance will not have that option.\n    Users in the @{"twitlist" link "twit"} can only select ''No'' and ''Credits''\n@endnode\n@node "maint"\n@title "Simple Wall V 1.2 - Maintainance Options"\n                            MAINTAINANCE OPTIONS\n                           ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n     If you want a user to have access to the Maintainance options,\n                 you must put his name in the @{"config-file" link "conf"}\n\n     View Maintainance logfile : Displays the maintainance logfile\n     View Anonymous-Logfile    : Diplays the anonymous writers logfile\n     Delete Logfile            : Deletes the anonymous writers logfile\n     Reset Wall                : Restores the wall to the original\n     Edit Wall                 : Allows you to edit a wallline\n     Show Wall                 : Displays the wall\n     Add user to Twitlist      : Adds a user to the @{"twitlist" link "twit"}\n     View Twitlist             : Views the @{"twitlist" link "twit"}\n     Go Back                   : Returns to the @{"Main menu" link "menu"}\n@endnode\n\n\n@node "hist"\n@title "FRaNKy''s Simple Wall V 1.2 - History"\n                                    HISTORY\n                                   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n\n                  ... - 0.9 : Internal Beta Releases\n                        1.0 : First Worldwide Release\n                        1.1 : - Sysop does not have to be in the cfg-file\n                                anymore to have acces to the maintenance\n                              - You can now edit the wall\n                              - You stay in the maintainance menu untill\n                                you press <ENTER>\n                              - Added a second logo\n                              - Interal source updates\n                        1.2 : - Added ANSI-animation for fast connects\n                              - Improved the centering of the wall-line\n                              - Added a Maintainance-Logile\n                              - Deletion of Logfiles and Wall-Reset\n                                now asks for a confirmation\n                              - Added a @{"Twitlist" link "twit"}\n                              - Everyone can access the maintainance menu\n                                now as long as he is in the @{"cfg-file" link "conf"} and\n                                knows the password\n@endnode\n@node "twit"\n@title ""FRaNKy''s Simple Wall V 1.2 - The Twitlist"\n                                     TWITLIST\n                                    ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\nIf, for some reason, you don''t want a certain user to write on the wall,\nadd his name to the twitlist (you can do this from @{"maintainance" link "maint"}).\n\nThe name is case-insensitive but the name has to be exactly the same for\nall other ASCII-chars (example : user^bla - don''t forget the ^)\n@endnode\n@node "stor"\n@title "FRaNKy''s Simple Wall V 1.2 - The Story Off"\n                                 THE STORY OFF\n                                ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\nThis door is currently the most developed I ever made (untill Piss-O-Rama\nwill be updated that is).\n\nI started this door because I wanted a wall where I could write anonymously\non but didn''t find one...\n\nOnce the mail wall was finished the shell around went quickly so I guess\nthat coding the wall to an 1.0 took me about 3-4 days.  Again I changed\nthe config-file 2 times but in this way I really like it so it''ll stay\nthis way.\n@endnode\n@node "Fbss"\n@title "Contacting The Author On The PTL BBS''s"\n                            CONTACTING THE AUTHOR\n                           ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n   The Author of the door can be contacted on these Purple Turtle BBS''s\n\n    Fortress      (   PTL WHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-3-***.**.** (Zyxel 16.8)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-3-***.**.** (Vfast 28.8)\n\n    Enigma        (   PTL BHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-89-**.**.** (USR   16.8)\n\n    Secret Cinema (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +32-52-**.**.** (VFast 33.6)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-52-RINGDOWN (VFast 33.6)\n\n    Cyber Garden  (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +32-11-**.**.** (USR   16.8)\n\n    S.P.G         (   PTL SHQ  ) Node 1 : +46-612-***.**  (USR   16.8)\n\n    Rhythm Nation (   PTL FHQ  ) Node 1 : +33-82-**.**.** (???   14.4)\n@endnode\n@node "FFido"\n@title "Contacting The Author Through FidoNet"\n                            CONTACTING THE AUTHOR\n                           ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    The Author of the doors included in this archive can be contacted by\n               sendin a Netmail to one of these point-numbers\n\n                                2:292/622.13\n                                2:292/8010.32\n@endnode\n@node "finter"\n@title "Contacting The Author Through Internet"\n                            CONTACTING THE AUTHOR\n                           ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                            Send your E-Mails to:\n\n                             [email removed]\n\n                     IRC-fans can try to join the channel\n\n                                    #PTL\n\n                         If I''m online, I''ll be there.\n@endnode\n@node "Pbbs"\n@title "Purpe Turtle BBS''s"\n                             PURPLE TURTLE BBS''S\n                            ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                                   BELGIUM\n                                  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Fortress      (   PTL WHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-3-***.**.** (Zyxel 16.8)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-3-***.**.** (Vfast 28.8)\n\n    Enigma        (   PTL BHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-89-**.**.** (USR   16.8)\n\n    Secret Cinema (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +32-52-**.**.** (VFast 33.6)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-52-RINGDOWN (VFast 33.6)\n\n    Cyber Garden  (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +32-11-**.**.** (USR   16.8)\n\n                                   HOLLAND\n                                  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Super Dancer  (   PTL HHQ  ) Node 1 : +31-570-***-*** (VFast 28.8)\n\n                                    SWEDEN\n                                   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Bitch Board   (   PTL EHQ  ) Node 1 : +46-111-***.**  (USR   28.8)\n\n    S.P.G         (   PTL SHQ  ) Node 1 : +46-612-***.**  (Vfast 28.8)\n\n    rIVER wILD    (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +46-612-***.**  (???   28.8)\n\n    Inferno       (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +46-øPRIVATE!ø  (USR   33.6)\n\n                                    FRANCE\n                                   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Rhythm Nation (   PTL FHQ  ) Node 1 : +33-82-**.**.** (???   14.4)\n\n                                    NORWAY\n                                   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Wizard Guild  (   PTL NHQ  ) Node 1 : +47-53-**.**.** (VFast 28.8)\n\n                                   GERMANY\n                                  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Traders World (   PTL GHQ  ) Node 1 : +49-215-******* (VFast 28.8)\n@endnode\n@node "PFido"\n@title "Purple Turtle FidoNet Adresses"\n                        PURPLE TURTLE FIDONET ADRESSES\n                       ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                  TFX      (  World Leader )   2:292/8010.14\n                  FRaNKy   (Co-World Leader)   2:292/8010.32\n@endnode\n@node "pinter"\n@title "Purple Turtle On The Net"\n                          PURPLE TURTLE ON THE NET\n                         ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                The Purple Turtle homepage can be visited at :\n\n                    http://www.ping.be/~ping2045/ptl.html\n\n                    You can also send E-Mails to FRaNKy at :\n\n                              [email removed]\n\n                         Or join the IRC-Channel #PTL\n@endnode\n@node "memb"\n@title "Purple Turtle Is Always Looking For New Members"\n                           LOOKING FOR NEW MEMBERS\n                          ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n  If you think you are the right guy (girl) for a cool group and you can do\n  some Coding (ASM-C-Arexx-...), Music, Graphics, Trading, Swapping or have\n      a BBS, then contact the Purple Turtle Leaders or Division Leaders\n                   for a certain reply on one of our HQ''s.\n\n   If you want to join with your BBS, we do not ask any donations for your\n    membership (in another way : it''s free !).  BBS''s outside Belgium are\n                              extremely welcome...\n\n        @{" Bulletin Boards " link "lbbs"}   @{"     FidoNet     " link "PFido"}   @{"    InterNet    " link "pinter"}\n@endnode\n@node "lbbs"\n@title "Contacting The Leaders"\n                           CONTACTING THE LEADERS\n                          ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n  You can contact the World Leaders and/or division leaders on these BBS''s.\n    People with a HQ in their country should adress themselves to that HQ.\n       If there isn''t a PTL BBS in your country, call the WHQ or a bbs\n                            in a country near you.\n\n    Fortress      (   PTL WHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-3-***.**.** (Zyxel 16.8)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-3-***.**.** (Vfast 28.8)\n\n    Bitch Board   (   PTL EHQ  ) Node 1 : +46-111-***.**  (USR   28.8)\n\n    Super Dancer  (   PTL HHQ  ) Node 1 : +31-570-***-*** (VFast 28.8)\n\n    S.P.G         (   PTL SHQ  ) Node 1 : +46-612-***.**  (Vfast 28.8)\n\n    Rhythm Nation (   PTL FHQ  ) Node 1 : +33-82-**.**.** (???   14.4)\n\n    Wizard Guild  (   PTL NHQ  ) Node 1 : +47-53-**.**.** (VFast 28.8)\n\n    Traders World (   PTL GHQ  ) Node 1 : +49-215-******* (VFast 28.8)\n@endnode\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',95502,8,0,NULL,NULL,'ptl_sw12','scan',1780048679);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ptl_sw13','PTL-SW13.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/PTL-SW13.LHA','ppguide','XIM','ppguide',NULL,NULL,'PTL','_\_________\_\_____  _____/ _\_  |_____ /      ______/   /      \w^s/     l     \ /_________|.cOLa./________\ /_____________\',replace('   ________/\  ______________  ___/|\n  _\_________\_\_____  _____/ _\_  |_____\n /      ______/   /      \w^s/     l     \\n/_________|.cOLa./________\ /_____________\\n:::::::::::::::::presents::::::::::::::::::\n::::::: FRaNKy''s Simple Wall V 1.3 ::::::::\n:::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\n:::: A GREAT wall for /X 2.xx+         ::::\n:::: Features : Anonymous writing, an  ::::\n:::: extended maintainance menu and so ::::\n:::: much more...              25/12/95::::\n:::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::','\n',char(10)),'Simple-Wall.Guide',replace('@database "FRaNKy''s Simple Wall V 1.3"\n@font topaz.font 8\n@author "FRaNKy/PTL"\n@(c) "Copyright © 1995 FRaNKy / Purple Turtle"\n@$VER: Simple-Wall.Guide V 1.1  (25/12/95)\n@node Main "FRaNKy''s Simple Wall V 1.0 - Main Menu"\n    FRaNKy''s Simple Wall V 1.3 - Copyright 1995 FRaNKy / Purple Turtle\n¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n       Important!            Contacting The Author           The Door\n      ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯          ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯         ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n  @{"     Disclaimer      " link "disc"}    @{"   Bulletin Boards   " link "Fbss"}    @{"     What Is It ?    " link "what"}\n  @{"   Compiled Doors    " link "comp"}    @{"       FidoNet       " link "Ffido"}    @{"     Installation    " link "inst"}\n  @{"    PostCardWare     " link "post"}    @{"      InterNet       " link "Finter"}    @{"     Config File     " link "conf"}\n                                                      @{"  Credits & Hellos   " link "cred"}\n     ________/\  ______________  ___/|                @{"       Options       " link "opt"}\n    _\_________\_\_____  _____/ _\_  |_____           @{"       History       " link "hist"}\n   /      ______/   /      \w^s/     l     \          @{"    The Story Off    " link "stor"}\n  /_________|.cOLa./________\ /_____________\\n  :::::::::::::::::presents::::::::::::::::::             Contacting PTL\n  ::::::: FRaNKy''s Simple Wall V 1.3 ::::::::            ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n  :::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::         @{"        BBS''s        " link "pbbs"}\n  :::: A GREAT wall for /X 2.xx+         ::::         @{"       FidoNet       " link "pfido"}\n  :::: Features : Anonymous writing, an  ::::         @{"      Internet       " link "pinter"}\n  :::: extended maintainance menu and so ::::\n  :::: much more...              25/12/95::::         @{" Looking For Members " link "memb"}\n  :::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\n@endnode\n@node "disc"\n@title "Disclaimer"\n                                DISCLAIMER\n                               ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n     This software is "AS IS", the author can not be held responsible for\n    any damage caused to your system by this software, or the consequences\n                               of this damage...\n\n                    To say it simply : Use at your own risk !\n@endnode\n@node "post"\n@title "PostCardWare"\n                               POSTCARDWARE\n                              ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n           All the doors included in this archive are PostCardWare\n      If you use one of included doors, you are kindly asked to send a\n                    postcard of the area you live in to :\n\n                          Peter Smets (FRaNKy / PTL)\n                          Weldadigheidsstraat 45\n                          3000 Leuven\n                          Belgium\n\n             Postcards received so far : Lady An      [   UK   ]\n                                         Killer Dwarf [ Sweden ]\n@endnode\n@node "comp"\n@title "Compiled Doors"\n                               COMPILED DOORS\n                              ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n  All doors in this archive are compiled using the RexxPlus Arexx Compiler.\n\n     To get the doors to work on you /X system, you must run RPStart and\n       have the libraries included in the archive copied to your LIBS:\n  It is advisable to put RPStart in you User-Startup so you won''t forget it\n\n   If you would like a copy of the uncompiled sources of the doors included\n      in this archive, send 1500 BEF (50 USD) to the author of the doors.\n           Cash money (no coins) or EuroCheque in BEF only please.\n\n  This can be a large amount of money, but if you see what money I spend in\n   my doors (time, phonecalls) and if you really want the sources to study\n                       them, this isn''t too much I think...\n\n        The adress where you can send the money to can be found under\n                              @{"postcardware" link "post"} button...\n\nNote :\n\n Compiled doors do not work on all systems (blame the /X RexxPort for this)\n                   but the advantage for me is much greater.\n\n  I decided to do this compilation of my doors because I noticed that more\n    and more people started using pieces of my doors, or sometimes just\n    renaming the door and then releasing it under their own name/group.\n            If you want you can buy the sources as staded above.\n\n                                                                    FRaNKy.\n@endnode\n@node "what"\n@title "FRaNKy''s Simple Wall V 1.3 - What is it ?"\n                                WHAT IS IT ?\n                               ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n   Simple Wall is (as the name says) a wall door for the /X 2.xx and up\n                           Bulleting Board Program\n@endnode\n@node "inst"\n@title "FRaNKy''s Simple Wall V 1.3 - Installation"\n                                INSTALLATION\n                               ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n   The files SWALL.#? should be placed in the directory "Doors:PTL/SWall/"\n          The icon (Wall.info) should be in "BBS:Commands/BBSCMD"\n\n  The add the door to your Logon-sequence by adding ''~CC_WALL'' to the file\n               ''NodeX/bull.txt'' (where X is the node number)\n@endnode\n@node "conf"\n@title "FRaNKy''s Simple Wall V 1.3 - Config File"\n                                CONFIGURATION\n                               ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n            You must edit the file "Doors:PTL/SWall/Swall.cfg"\n                     The file must be edited like this :\n\n       Line 1 : Password needed to access the maintainance menu\n       Line 2 : Person who can access the maintainance menu\n       Line 3 : Person who can access the maintainance menu\n       Line 4 : ....\n\n                             Example :\n                             ---------------\n                             superimperialstardestroyer\n                             da cool one\n                             da slave\n                             da superslave\n                             ---------------\n@endnode\n@node "cred"\n@title "FRaNKy''s Simple Wall V 1.3 - Credits"\n                                  CREDITS\n                                 ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                          Coding       : FRaNKy\n                          Docs         : FRaNKy & TFX\n                          Logos        : Flare & Maxx\n                          Beta Testing : The Fly - Crisp - Killer Dwarf\n                          HD-Tester    : Recall\n                          Idea''s       : The Fly\n\n                                  GREETINGS\n                                 ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\nHello''s & Greetings from FRaNKy fly out to all my friends around the world,\nyou know who you are...\n\n@endnode\n@node "opt"\n@title "Simple Wall V 1.3 - Options"\n                                  OPTIONS\n                                 ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                              @{" Menu Options " link "menu"}\n                              @{" Maintainance " link "maint"}\n                              @{" Config Files " link "conf"}\n@endnode\n@node "menu"\n@title "Simple Wall V 1.3 - Menu Options"\n                                MENU OPTIONS\n                               ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n       Users who can access the Maintainance will see this menu-line\n\n      Add a line ? [Y]es [N]o [A]nonymous     [M]aintainance [C]redits\n\n              Yes           : The user wants to add a line\n              No            : The user don''t wants to add a line\n              Anonymous     : The user wants to add an anonymous\n                             line, the user name and his line\n                             will be written to a logfile\n              @{"Maintainance" link "maint"} : Allows you to do some maintainance\n              Credits       : Shows the credits\n\n    Users who can not access the maintainance will not have that option.\n    Users in the @{"twitlist" link "twit"} can only select ''No'' and ''Credits''\n@endnode\n@node "maint"\n@title "Simple Wall V 1.3 - Maintainance Options"\n                            MAINTAINANCE OPTIONS\n                           ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n     If you want a user to have access to the Maintainance options,\n                 you must put his name in the @{"config-file" link "conf"}\n\n    View Maintainance logfile     : Displays the maintainance logfile\n    View Anonymous-Logfile        : Diplays the anonymous writers logfile\n    Delete Logfile                : Deletes the anonymous writers logfile\n    Reset Wall                    : Restores the wall to the original\n    Edit Wall                     : Allows you to edit a wallline\n    Show Wall                     : Displays the wall\n    Add user to Twitlist          : Adds a user to the @{"twitlist" link "twit"}\n    Remove user from Twitlist     : Removes a user from the @{"twitlist" link "twit"}\n    View Twitlist                 : Views the @{"twitlist" link "twit"}\n    Give user maintainance access : Gives a user maintainance access\n    Take user maintainance access : Removes a users maintainance access\n    View users with maint. access : Displays the users with maintainance\n                                    access\n        Go Back                   : Returns to the @{"Main menu" link "menu"}\n@endnode\n\n\n@node "hist"\n@title "FRaNKy''s Simple Wall V 1.3 - History"\n                                    HISTORY\n                                   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n\n               ... - 0.9 : Internal Beta Releases\n                     1.0 : First Worldwide Release\n                     1.1 : - Sysop does not have to be in the cfg-file\n                             anymore to have acces to the maintenance\n                           - You can now edit the wall\n                           - You stay in the maintainance menu untill\n                             you press <ENTER>\n                           - Added a second logo\n                           - Interal source updates\n                     1.2 : - Added ANSI-animation for fast connects\n                           - Improved the centering of the wall-line\n                           - Added a Maintainance-Logile\n                           - Deletion of Logfiles and Wall-Reset\n                             now asks for a confirmation\n                           - Added a @{"Twitlist" link "twit"}\n                           - Everyone can access the maintainance menu\n                             now as long as he is in the @{"cfg-file" link "conf"} and\n                             knows the password\n                     1.3 : - Bugfix : Even if you said ''N'', the user was\n                                      added to the @{"twitlist" link "twit"}\n                           - Users can now be deleted from the @{"twitlist" link "twit"}\n                           - Users can now be given & removed @{"maintainance" link "maint"}\n                             access on-line\n                           - Users that have @{"maintainace" link "maint"} acces can be\n                             viewed\n                           - Minor screen-change in @{"Maintainance" link "maint"}\n\n@endnode\n@node "twit"\n@title "FRaNKy''s Simple Wall V 1.3 - The Twitlist"\n                                     TWITLIST\n                                    ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\nIf, for some reason, you don''t want a certain user to write on the wall,\nadd his name to the twitlist (you can do this from @{"maintainance" link "maint"}).\n\nThe name is case-insensitive but the name has to be exactly the same for\nall other ASCII-chars (example : user^bla - don''t forget the ^)\n@endnode\n@node "stor"\n@title "FRaNKy''s Simple Wall V 1.3 - The Story Off"\n                                 THE STORY OFF\n                                ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\nThis door is currently the most developed I ever made (untill Piss-O-Rama\nwill be updated that is).\n\nI started this door because I wanted a wall where I could write anonymously\non but didn''t find one...\n\nOnce the mail wall was finished the shell around went quickly so I guess\nthat coding the wall to an 1.0 took me about 3-4 days.  Again I changed\nthe config-file 2 times but in this way I really like it so it''ll stay\nthis way.\n@endnode\n@node "Fbss"\n@title "Contacting The Author On The PTL BBS''s"\n                            CONTACTING THE AUTHOR\n                           ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n   The Author of the door can be contacted on these Purple Turtle BBS''s\n\n                                   BELGIUM\n                                  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Fortress      (   PTL WHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-3-829.08.72 (Zyxel 16.8)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-3-825.00.69 (Vfast 28.8)\n\n    Enigma        (   PTL BHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-89-73.20.54 (USR   16.8)\n\n    Secret Cinema (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +32-52-35.15.75 (VFast 33.6)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-52-RINGDOWN (VFast 33.6)\n\n    Cyber Garden  (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +32-11-33.37.03 (VFast 33.6)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-11-33.32.29 (USR   16.8)\n\n    Skyline       (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +32-3-677.14.23 (????? 14.4)\n\n                                    SWEDEN\n                                   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Bitch Board   (   PTL EHQ  ) Node 1 : +46-11-16.62.76  (USR   28.8)\n\n    Inferno       (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +46-øPRIVATE!ø  (USR   33.6)\n\n                                    FRANCE\n                                   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Rhythm Nation (   PTL FHQ  ) Node 1 : +33-82-88.19.31 (???   14.4)\n\n@endnode\n@node "FFido"\n@title "Contacting The Author Through FidoNet"\n                            CONTACTING THE AUTHOR\n                           ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    The Author of the doors included in this archive can be contacted by\n               sendin a Netmail to one of these point-numbers\n\n                                2:292/628.10\n                                2:292/8010.32\n@endnode\n@node "finter"\n@title "Contacting The Author Through Internet"\n                            CONTACTING THE AUTHOR\n                           ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                            Send your E-Mails to:\n\n                             [email removed]\n\n                     IRC-fans can try to join the channel\n\n                                    #PTL\n\n                         If I''m online, I''ll be there.\n@endnode\n@node "Pbbs"\n@title "Purpe Turtle BBS''s"\n                             PURPLE TURTLE BBS''S\n                            ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                                   BELGIUM\n                                  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Fortress      (   PTL WHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-3-829.08.72 (Zyxel 16.8)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-3-825.00.69 (Vfast 28.8)\n\n    Enigma        (   PTL BHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-89-73.20.54 (USR   16.8)\n\n    Secret Cinema (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +32-52-35.15.75 (VFast 33.6)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-52-RINGDOWN (VFast 33.6)\n\n    Cyber Garden  (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +32-11-33.37.03 (VFast 33.6)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-11-33.32.29 (USR   16.8)\n\n    Skyline       (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +32-3-677.14.23 (????? 14.4)\n\n                                   HOLLAND\n                                  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Digital X     (   PTL HHQ  ) Node 1 : +31-570-037-050 (VFast 28.8)\n                                 Node 2 : +31-570-677-702 (HST   14.4)\n\n                                    SWEDEN\n                                   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Bitch Board   (   PTL EHQ  ) Node 1 : +46-11-16.62.76  (USR   28.8)\n\n    Inferno       (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +46-øPRIVATE!ø  (USR   33.6)\n\n                                    FRANCE\n                                   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Rhythm Nation (   PTL FHQ  ) Node 1 : +33-82-88.19.31 (???   14.4)\n\n                                    NORWAY\n                                   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Pure Magic    (   PTL NHQ  ) Node 1 : +47-53-76.16.91 (VFast 28.8)\n\n    Insomnia      (PTL Fun Site) Node 1 : +47-63-90.46.48 (????? ??.?)\n\n                                   GERMANY\n                                  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Traders World (   PTL GHQ  ) Node 1 : +49-215-1786470 (VFast 28.8)\n\n@endnode\n@node "PFido"\n@title "Purple Turtle FidoNet Adresses"\n                        PURPLE TURTLE FIDONET ADRESSES\n                       ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                  TFX      (  World Leader )   2:292/8010.14\n                  FRaNKy   (Co-World Leader)   2:292/628.10\n\n@endnode\n@node "pinter"\n@title "Purple Turtle On The Net"\n                          PURPLE TURTLE ON THE NET\n                         ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                The Purple Turtle homepage can be visited at :\n\n                    http://www.ping.be/~ping2045/ptl.html\n\n                    You can also send E-Mails to FRaNKy at :\n\n                              [email removed]\n\n                         Or join the IRC-Channel #PTL\n@endnode\n@node "memb"\n@title "Purple Turtle Is Always Looking For New Members"\n                           LOOKING FOR NEW MEMBERS\n                          ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n  If you think you are the right guy (girl) for a cool group and you can do\n  some Coding (ASM-C-Arexx-...), Music, Graphics, Trading, Swapping or have\n      a BBS, then contact the Purple Turtle Leaders or Division Leaders\n                   for a certain reply on one of our HQ''s.\n\n   If you want to join with your BBS, we do not ask any donations for your\n    membership (in another way : it''s free !).  BBS''s outside Belgium are\n                              extremely welcome...\n\n        @{" Bulletin Boards " link "lbbs"}   @{"     FidoNet     " link "PFido"}   @{"    InterNet    " link "pinter"}\n@endnode\n@node "lbbs"\n@title "Contacting The Leaders"\n                           CONTACTING THE LEADERS\n                          ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n  You can contact the World Leaders and/or division leaders on these BBS''s.\n    People with a HQ in their country should adress themselves to that HQ.\n       If there isn''t a PTL BBS in your country, call the WHQ or a bbs\n                            in a country near you.\n\n                                   BELGIUM\n                                  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Fortress      (   PTL WHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-3-829.08.72 (Zyxel 16.8)\n                                 Node 2 : +32-3-825.00.69 (Vfast 28.8)\n\n    Enigma        (   PTL BHQ  ) Node 1 : +32-89-73.20.54 (USR   16.8)\n\n                                   HOLLAND\n                                  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Digital X     (   PTL HHQ  ) Node 1 : +31-570-037-050 (VFast 28.8)\n                                 Node 2 : +31-570-677-702 (HST   14.4)\n\n                                    SWEDEN\n                                   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Bitch Board   (   PTL EHQ  ) Node 1 : +46-11-16.62.76  (USR   28.8)\n\n                                    FRANCE\n                                   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Rhythm Nation (   PTL FHQ  ) Node 1 : +33-82-88.19.31 (???   14.4)\n\n                                    NORWAY\n                                   ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Pure Magic    (   PTL NHQ  ) Node 1 : +47-53-76.16.91 (VFast 28.8)\n\n                                   GERMANY\n                                  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n    Traders World (   PTL GHQ  ) Node 1 : +49-215-1786470 (VFast 28.8)\n@endnode\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',102408,4,0,NULL,NULL,'ptl_sw13','scan',1780048679);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ptl_sx10','PTL-SX10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/PTL-SX10.LHA','S!X-Pager','XIM','LE-win5-96.exe',NULL,'XRay2000','PTL','}---- \_____ \__    \_    \ ---------------{ }------ /  / / /  /¯¯/  /¯¯ -- Brings to --{ }-----_/ ___/_/  /  /  /   --- ya in 1995 -{',replace('      ____________________\n}---- \_____ \__    \_    \ ---------------{\n}------ /  / / /  /¯¯/  /¯¯ -- Brings to --{\n}-----_/ ___/_/  /  /  /   --- ya in 1995 -{\n}---- \  / - \  /  /  /__/\ ---------------{\n}----- \/ --- \/ - \______/ ---------------{\n}------------------------------------------{\n}- S!X Pager V1.0 For S!X 0.xx & /X 2.xx+ -{\n}---- All ASM Coding By XRay2000 / PTL ----{\n}------------------------------------------{\n[iSDN][-÷ lEEChEd fRoM gOd''s hArEm ÷-][16.8]\n','\n',char(10)),'S!X-Pager.Guide',replace('@database "S!X-Pager V 1.0"\n@author "FRaNKy/PTL"\n@(c) "Copyright © 1995 FRaNKy / Purple Turtle"\n@$VER: S!X-Pager Documentation By FRaNKy / PTL  (16/06/95)\n@node Main "S!X-Pager V 1.0 - Main Menu"\n            77:::::/\_____/\_   /\/\_____ /\_____/\__  /\__ ___\n               7::/  \  _ \  Y\/  \ \  _ Y  \  _ \  / /  \ Y  /\n                7/     /  |\ | \   \  /  :    /  |\/ /     : /\n         _______/     /   :/ : /   / /   .   /   :/_/__ ____/______ __ _\n        |      /          /  ./   /_     /       //   /__/____    // ///\n        |_____/     |\___/       / \    <  |\___//   / \_/   /___//_///\n             /      |    \      /  |\    \ |        /       /::\n             \______|     \  __/___| \    \|_______/_____  /::::...\n              -------------\/---------\    /-------------\/--------\n                                       \  /\n                                        \/\n            /\___ _____/\   /\  /\_____/\___ _____/\/\__  /\__ ___\n            \    Y      /Y\/  \/  \  _  Y   Y      /   / /  \ Y  /::::77\n             \  /|  |  / | \   \/   /   :  /|  |  /   / /     : /::7\n     _ __ ____\/ :  |_// : /   /   /    /\/ :  |_/   /_/__ ____/_____\n     \\\ \\    | .  | /  ./   /  _     /  |  . |    //   /__/____    |\n      \\\_\\___|    |/       /   \    <   |    |   //   / \_/   /____|\n            .::|    |\      /    |\    \  |    |       /       /\n        ...::::|____| \  __/\____| \    \_|____|______/_____  /\n          -------------\/-----------\    /----\/-*-DiMeNsIon\/\n                                     \  /\n                                      \/\n\n         SigmaExpress Pager v1.2/Alpha Copyright 1995 By Xray2000/PTL\n          All Coding By Xray2000/PTL - AmigaGuide Docs By FRaNKy/PTL\n         ------------------------------------------------------------\n                            Release date 16/06/95\n\n                               @{" Introduction " link "intr"}\n                               @{" Installation " link "inst"}\n                               @{"   His-tory   " link "hist"}\n                               @{"    Greetz    " link "gret"}\n                               @{"  Disclaimer  " link "disc"}\n                               @{"  Final Info  " link "info"}\n                               @{"  Searching!  " link "srch"}\n@endnode\n@node "intr"\n@title "Introduction"\nHello, and welcome to the best Sysop pager door you''ve ever seen on\nSigmaExpress. There  has never  been  anything  like  this  door  before.\n\nThis door works and have been tested on SigmaExpress v0.39p9+.\n@endnode\n@node "inst"\n@title "Installation"\nS!X-Pager v1.2/Alpha requires the following things to run correctly:\n\n* A fully installed and running SigmaExpress v0.39p9+.\n\n* A fully installed and running workbench v37+.\n\nIf you have the above things,you can continue with this installation.\nOtherwise quit and get/buy the missing thing becouse it won''t work!\n\nTo install S!X-Pager, start with copying the included files where\nthey should be located.\n\n                            @{" SigmaExpress v0.x " link "sigm"}\n                            @{"  AmiExpress v2.x  " link "sigm"}\n                            @{"  AmiExpress v3.x  " link "amix"}\n                            @{"  AmiExpress v4.x  " link "amix"}\n@endnode\n@node "sigm"\n@title "Installation : Sigma Express v0.x & AmiExpress v 2.x"\nTake your Text Editor and put this in your BBS:Commands/BBS.CMD file\n\n------------( Snap this line )---------------------------\nO         XM001BBS:Doors/S!X-Pager/S!X-Pager\n---------------------------------------------------------\n@endnode\n@node "amix"\n@title "Installation : AmiExpress V 3.x & 4.x"\nJust throw all the files in the directory they are in now.\n\nSimple isn''t it ??\n@endnode\n@node "hist"\n@title "History"\nVersion 1.2/Alpha\n\n* New release !\n* Joining the group PTL !\n* Bug fixed with the new version of SigmaExpress !\n* Changed the collors a bid\n* Changed my real name again to may Alias name !\n@endnode\n@node "gret"\n@title "Greetings"\nI personally want to thank all my beta-testers at THE AMIGA LAND BBS.\nIn no particular order:\n\nSysop         BBS        Country   Node    Numbers          Modem\n---------------------------------------------------------------------\nSigma Seven!  Synergy    Germany    1      +49-5731-40074   USR 21.6K\nSigma Seven!  Synergy    Germany    2      +49-5731-741006  ISDN!\nXray2000      Amiga Land Belgium    1      +32-16-448622    USR 14.4K\nTfx           Fortress              1      +32-03-8290872   19k2 ZyXEL\nHi-Tech       Taj Mahal             1      +31-162-322716   28k8 vFAST\nPyromaniac    Macho City            1      +31-133-55829    28k8 vFAST\n\nAlso greetings to the following people:\n\n-- FRANKY/PTL, THE FLY/PTL, TFX/PTL,HI-TECH/PTL, PYROMANIAC/PTL,\n   MOUSEBUSTER/PRESTIGE, SIGMA SEVEN!/S!X, -TCB!-/HOODLUM,\n   COLONEL/HOODLUM.\n\nAnyone can become a beta-tester, simply make a call to THE AMIGA LAND BBS.\n@endnode\n@node "disc"\n@title "Disclaimer"\nThis program is Copyright (C)1995 by Xray2000/PTL.\nSigmaExpress is Copyright (C)1995 by Sigma Seven!.\n\nIf your hard-drive or  anything else goes wrong  when you are using this\ndoor, i am not responsible. This tool has been thouroughly tested on\nmany  boards all around the world, but "there is always one more bug"\n\nThat''s it for now, i hope you enjoy this door.\n\n-Xray2000 (SigmaExpress Beta Tester)\n@endnode\n@node "info"\n@title "Final Info"\nIf you have any questions, bug reports, suggestions, you can  contact me\nat the following boards:\n\nThe Amiga Land BBS: +32-16-448622  [14.4K]   SYSOP: XRAY2000\n                                    ^^^^^^ Soon 28.8K V34\n@endnode\n@node "srch"\n@title "Searching for"\nPTL is searching for...\n\n                  _______   ______   _________    ______\n                 /  ____.\  \    .\ /  ____.\|   / ____/\n                 \  \__/ /|\/   | \\\  \__/ /|__/   _)_\n       :  /      / _____/_| \  __ _// _____/ |  \  |  .\     \  :\n       | /      /  \ /       \  |  \  \  \       )     /      \ |\n      \|/       \___\\_______/_/|__/__/   \_____/\____/        \|/\n  - --[T]-- -   ________     ______ ___________    ______  - --[G]-- -\n      /|\      / _    _ \    \    .\ _    _ \ |   / ____/      /|\\n     / |       \/ \  / \/| |\/   | \\ \  / \/ |__/   _)_        | \\n    /  :          /  \ / |_| \  __ _/ /  \/   |  \  |  .\       :  \\n       .         /    \       \  |  \/    \       )     /       .\n                 \ ___/_______/_/|__/\____/\_____/\___ /\n                  \|                                 |/\n\n       Is looking for some ''Coders (ASM,C,Etc..)'' Gfx Artist and\n       musicians, if you think you are the guy (girl) then reply\n       to this message.\n\n       Everyone will get a reply from the WorldLeader of PurplE-TurtlE,\n       Just call @{"Fortress" link "fort"}...\n@endnode\n@node "fort"\n@title "Fortress - PTL WHQ"\n\n\n           ________________________________________        AMIGA\n          (_   _____________  _____________________)        WAREZ\n           /  /_/ __ \ __ \/ /__ \ _______________)\n          /  ___)/ / /   _/ /   _/ __)  ___   ___)        *O*N*L*Y*\n        _/  / / /_/ / /\ \ / /\ \ (__\____ \____ \\n       (____) \____/__)(__Y__)(__)_________/_____/      NUP INSTALLED\n                                             [DH]\n\n   SYSOP:    TFX\n   COSYSOP:  Dirty Harry     Node 1 - ZyXEL  19.200 - +32 3 829.08.72\n             DZign!          Node 2 - Supra  28.800 - +32 3 829.so.on\n\n        Fortress - Running on A4000/030/882\n                 - 500 Mbyte HD\n                 - Lots of credz for major uploads !!!\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',15406,6,0,NULL,NULL,'ptl_sx10','scan',1780048679);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ptl_us12','PTL-US12.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/PTL-US12.LHA',NULL,'XIM','_/\___________________/\____',NULL,NULL,'PTL','\_______   \_____    \_    /--------------. /   ______/   /    //    /____ PROTOCOL  | /    /        /    //    /    /  IN ''95   |',replace(' _/\___________________/\____               \n \_______   \_____    \_    /--------------.\n  /   ______/   /    //    /____ PROTOCOL  |\n /    /        /    //    /    /  IN ''95   |\n/____/[AdK]   /____//_________/  --------  |\n +-----------------------------------------''\nPRO-STATS V1.0+ USER STATISTICS DOOR FOR /X!\n.GREAT COLOURS. WORKS ON ALL /X VERSIONS 3+.\n....SUPPORTS SYSTEM AND TRANSFER COMMENT....\n..ARE YOUR USERS ZOOMING ALONG OR SLOW!!!...\n.....THIS DOOR WILL TELL THEM FOR YOU.......\n','\n',char(10)),'STATS.DOC',replace('----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n!cOASTaLcARNaGe!--+--!cOASTaLcARNaGe!--!cOASTaLcARNaGe!--+--!cOASTaLcARNaGe!\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n__/\\________/\\_________/\\_____/\\____ __/\\_____/\\______/\\_____\n\__  __    ___  .  _____    ~ ____      \             ~ ____     __/\n_/    |____//   !   \_/~  _!  ¼\/|   l___\_    \_/  _!  ¼\_/     |_____\n\     !  _ ¼\_  :    \_   \_    \_.__      \    \   \_    \_     !  _  \_\n \    : _//  /        /    ³     /          \    \   ³     /     : _//  /\n  \____     /________/l____:    /   ³        \    \__:    /_______     /\n      l____/               l___/\________    /_____) l___/-DtN   l____/\n                                       \____/\n__/\\__________/\\________/\\____/\\_________/\\______/\\______/\\_____\n\__  __    ___    ~ _____      __       ____    ~ ____  _______   _____)\n_/    |____//~  _!  ¼\     !___/_  \__   \/~  _!  ¼\_/  \_    \    __/_\n\     !    ¼\_  \_    \_   _     \_ :     \   \_    \_   !  _  \_  I  ¼\_\n \    :      /   ³     /          / i­     \   ³     /   : _//  /        \_\n  \____     /____:    /____:     /  !.      \__:    /_____     /          /\n      l____/Ott  l___/    l_____/___|:        /l___/     l____/__________/\n                                     !_______/\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\naMIgA-hPa-pEcE-aMIxPREsS-0-dAY-fILEs-28800-cHATTinG-sYsOPs-rUNNiNG-AmIXpREss\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  tHe-fUNkY-bRoS-pEArL-nUoZ-fREAkNET-sTONedMOnkS-cDs-vIDeOs-tO-mUCh-mORe\nkALL-aUStRAlIa-+61[0]75-273648-nODe-tWooo-iS-pRIVaTe-nUp-iS-gOInG-tO-hAPPeN-\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n             ProSTAT VERSION 1.2 By TRESPASS/[PROTOCOL][CLIQUE]\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n			    WHAT IS PRO-STATS\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nPro Stats is simply a repacement S command for your /X board.\n\nDisplays the users statistics and also two calculated comments to the\nviewing user.\n\n These comments are :  TRANSFER RATEING\n                    :  SYSTEM COMMENT\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                                HOW TO INSTALL\n\n\n        Install Pro-Stat as you have installed any other X door before..\n         Copy all files to their correct directories in your BBS: drawer\n              Its all to easy. USE S from the command line to view!!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n!cOASTaLcARNaGe!--+--!cOASTaLcARNaGe!--!cOASTaLcARNaGe!--+--!cOASTaLcARNaGe!\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n__/\\________/\\_________/\\_____/\\____ __/\\_____/\\______/\\_____\n\__  __    ___  .  _____    ~ ____      \             ~ ____     __/\n_/    |____//   !   \_/~  _!  ¼\/|   l___\_    \_/  _!  ¼\_/     |_____\n\     !  _ ¼\_  :    \_   \_    \_.__      \    \   \_    \_     !  _  \_\n \    : _//  /        /    ³     /          \    \   ³     /     : _//  /\n  \____     /________/l____:    /   ³        \    \__:    /_______     /\n      l____/               l___/\________    /_____) l___/-DtN   l____/\n                                       \____/\n__/\\__________/\\________/\\____/\\_________/\\______/\\______/\\_____\n\__  __    ___    ~ _____      __       ____    ~ ____  _______   _____)\n_/    |____//~  _!  ¼\     !___/_  \__   \/~  _!  ¼\_/  \_    \    __/_\n\     !    ¼\_  \_    \_   _     \_ :     \   \_    \_   !  _  \_  I  ¼\_\n \    :      /   ³     /          / i­     \   ³     /   : _//  /        \_\n  \____     /____:    /____:     /  !.      \__:    /_____     /          /\n      l____/Ott  l___/    l_____/___|:        /l___/     l____/__________/\n                                     !_______/\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\naMIgA-hPa-pEcE-aMIxPREsS-0-dAY-fILEs-28800-cHATTinG-sYsOPs-rUNNiNG-AmIXpREss\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n  tHe-fUNkY-bRoS-pEArL-nUoZ-fREAkNET-sTONedMOnkS-cDs-vIDeOs-tO-mUCh-mORe\nkALL-aUStRAlIa-+61[0]75-273648-nODe-tWooo-iS-pRIVaTe-nUp-iS-gOInG-tO-hAPPeN-\n----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,5967,4,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048679);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ptl_wn10','PTL-WN10.LZX','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/PTL-WN10.LZX',NULL,'XIM','ptl wn10',NULL,NULL,'PTL',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,8274,0,0,NULL,NULL,'ptl_wn10','scan',1780048679);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ptlnot10','PTLNOT10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/PTLNOT10.LHA','NoTiFieR','XIM','.------------------------------------------.',NULL,NULL,NULL,'|                     _____  ____  ___     | | [-pURPLE#tURTLE!]   \ .  \/  . \/  /__   | |                    /  |   \  |  \  V  \  |',replace('.------------------------------------------.\n|                     _____  ____  ___     | \n| [-pURPLE#tURTLE!]   \ .  \/  . \/  /__   |\n|                    /  |   \  |  \  V  \  | \n|  --BRiNG''S you:-- /    ___/__|   \     \ | \n+===================\____|-911|____/_____/=+\n+------------------------------------------+\n|NoTiFieR V1.0 SySoP WaRNiNG TooL FoR /X3.+|\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'NoTiFieR.guide',replace('@database PTL-NoTiFieRDoc\n@Author MaDDy ·OF· PuRPLe TuRTLe\n@Index MAIN\n\nCopyright (c) 1993 THe GRiFTeR / PuRPLe TuRTLe\n\n@Remark $VER: (V1.0 NoVeMBeR 1993, 00:00:00)\n@Remark AmigaGuide database for the PTL-NoTiFieR Documentation\n\n@node MAIN "PTL-NoTiFieR Documentation (c)1993 MaDDy of PuRPLe TuRTLe (NoVeMBeR 1993, 00:00:00)"\n           _ ________ ______ ________ ________ _____ _ _______\n          _ __   .   \_  |  \_   .   \_   .   \_   |___    _  \\n             |   |    \  |   \   |    \   |    \   |   \   ___/\\n             |    ____/  |    \  |____/    ____/        \  V    \\n             |____|  _ _______/___|   |____|  _ ________/_______/\n           _ ________ _______ ________ ________ _____ _ _______\n          _ __   .   \_   |  \_   .   \_   .   \_   |___    _  \\n             |   |    \   |   \   |    \   |    \   |   \   ___/\\n             |___|     \  |    \  |____/___|     \       \  V    \\n                |______/_______/___|-+911+|______/_______/_______/\n\n\n                              >>> PTL-NoTiFieR <<<\n\n                             CoDe : THe GRiFTeR/PTL\n                               DeSiGN : MaDDy/PTL\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------- \n\n         >>> C·O·N·T·E·N·T·S  O·F  D·O·C·U·M·E·N·T·A·T·I·O·N <<<\n\n                         @{"      Introduction      " Link Cap01}\n                         @{"      Requirements      " Link Cap02}\n                         @{"      Installation      " Link Cap03}\n                         @{"       Tooltypes!       " Link Cap04}\n                         @{"       Greetings!       " Link Cap05}\n                         @{"   How to Contact us?   " Link Cap06}\n\n         ---------------------------------------------------------\n         Complete Docs for PTL-NoTiFieR V1.00 PuRPLe /X-DeVeLoPMeNT\n         ---------------------------------------------------------\n         The Documentation has been written by MaDDy/PuRPLe TuRTLe.\n\n@endnode\n@node Cap01 "Introduction"\n  =======================================================================\n  PTL-NoTiFieR is a NEW COMMAND, it can be used to NOTIFY the sysop\n  that a user has logged on, also shows the user if the sysop is there\n  or not... It has special features like Personal Messages to friends, \n  Random Messages to other users... \n  Certain messages on Certain times!\n  Door is coded in C without silly backdoors in it.\n  For Original version call PTL original Purple /X sites\n          Metal Impact +32/50/393239 or Phantom +32/9/3770719\n  =======================================================================\n@endnode\n@node Cap02 "Requirements"\n  =======================================================================\n  To install PTL-NoTiFieR you must have the following things:\n\n    Programm          Location              Description\n    ----------        --------              -----------\n    NoTiFieR          Doors:PTL-NoTiFieR/   Main program\n    NoTiFieR.info     BBS:Commands/BBSCMD/  .Info file\n    AEDoor.Library    Libs:                 Library \n\n  - an  Amiga Model (500/600/1000/1200/2000/2500/3000/4000/CDTV/CD³²)\n  - the installed Version of OS\2, OS\3 or higher\n    (Soft- or Hardware Version)\n  - the installed .INFO Files in the directories.\n  - AmiExpress v3.xx or higher.\n  - AEDoorLib 1.13 (26 Sep 1993) by Sintax\n\n  =======================================================================\n@endnode\n@node Cap03 "How to install PTL-NoTiFieR"\n  =======================================================================\n  To install PTL-NoTiFieR you must have all Requirement which were\n  mentioned below. You need the following things.\n\n  --------------------------\n    Doors:PTL-NoTiFieR (dir)\n      ^^^ NoTiFieR\n    BBS:Commands/BBSCmd (dir)\n      ^^^ NoTiFier.info\n  --------------------------\n\n  Decruch the PTL-NoTiFieR Archive. Go to your ''Doors:'' Directory\n  and make a Directory called ''PTL-NoTiFieR''. Copy ''NoTiFieR''\n  into the Directory. Go to your ''BBS:Commands/BBSCmd'' Directory.\n  Copy ''NoTiFieR.info'' into it.\n  Thats it.. make sure you have the AEDoor Library in ya''r LIBS:\n  Make sure you mention this commands in your menu''s or leave a\n  message to the users..\n  =======================================================================\n@endnode\n@node Cap04 "ToolTypes ..."\n  =======================================================================\n  Tooltypes of ''BBS:BBSCMD/NoTiFieR.info'':\n  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n  LOCATION= <string>       - Specifies the location of the Module\n                             EXAMPLE:\n                             LOCATION=DooRS:PTL-NoTiFieR/NoTiFieR\n  MULTINODE= <YES|NO>      - tells /X if the module may be simultaneously\n                             accessed from other nodes.\n                             EXAMPLE:\n                             MULTINODE=YES\n  ACCESS= <num>            - tells /X the access level required to run this\n                             module. This option is ignored for internal\n                             Module options.\n                             EXAMPLE:\n                             ACCESS=30\n  TYPE=XIM                 - tells /X which type of module it is to support:\n                             EXAMPLE:\n                             TYPE=XIM\n  RANDOM.<num>= <string>   - Specifies the Random Lines show at the users\n                             <num> is a number from 1 to 10\n                             EXAMPLE:\n                             RANDOM.1=PuSh THaT u KeY\n  TIMEBEGIN.<num> = <time> - Specifies the Start time to show REASON.<num>\n                             Time must always be specified in pure decimals\n                             <num> is a number from 1 to 25\n                             EXAMPLE:\n                             TIMEBEGIN.1=0600\n  TIMEEND.<num> = <time>   - Specifies the End time to show Reason.<num>                      \n                             <num> is a number from 1 to 25\n                             EXAMPLE:\n                             TIMEEND.1=0645\n          \n-------------------> REMARK: any reason which includes MIDNIGHT (00:00) must\n                             be shifted in two parts like this\n                             TIMEBEGIN.1=0900\n                             TIMEEND.1=0000\n                             TIMEBEGIN.1=0001\n                             TIMEEND.1=1645\n\n \n  REASON.<num> = <string>  - Specifies the Reason why sysop is not there\n                             <num> is a number from 1 to 25\n                             EXAMPLE:\n                             REASON.1=ya''R SySoP iS GeTTiNG ouT oF HiS BeD\n                             [This message will be show in the above examples]\n                             [Between 06:00 & 06:45]\n  NAME.<num> =  <name>     - Specifies a special guest on the bbs which don''t \n                             get the random message but a special message specified\n                             in the MESSAGE.<num> [THE NAME MUST BE EXACTLY THE SAME\n                             as used on the bbs]\n                             <num> is a number from 1 to 25\n                             EXAMPLE:\n                             NAME.1=MaDDY \n  MESSAGE.<num> = <string> - Specifies the message the special guest gets!\n                             <num> is a number from 1 to 25\n                             EXAMPLE:\n                             MESSAGE.1=yo BRo, HoPe ya HaD a NiCe Day!\n  MONDAY = <string>        - Specifies a message show on Monday                   \n                             EXAMPLE:\n                             MONDAY=eRM iT''S MoNDay\n  TUESDAY = <string>        - Specifies a message show on tuesday\n                             EXAMPLE:\n                             TUESDAY=2 DoNe, 3 To Go\n  WEDNESDAY = <string>        - Specifies a message show on wednesday\n                             EXAMPLE:\n                             WEDNESDAY=HaLF-CoReD\n  THURSDAY = <string>        - Specifies a message show on thursday\n                             EXAMPLE:\n                             THURSDAY=iT''S aLMoST FRiDay\n  FRIDAY = <string>        - Specifies a message show on friday\n                             EXAMPLE:\n                             FRIDAY=iT''S HeRe\n  SATURDAY = <string>        - Specifies a message show on saturday\n                             EXAMPLE:\n                             SATURDAY=SaTuRDay,.... iT''S a SaTuRDay\n  SUNDAY = <string>        - Specifies a message show on Sunday\n                             EXAMPLE:\n                             SUNDAY=GueSS i''M STiLL aSLeeP\n\n  =======================================================================\n@endnode\n@node Cap05 "Greetings go to..."\n  =======================================================================\n\n                             GREETS GO TO:\n\n  SVeN THe CReaToR/5D ......................... For your original docs\n  SieGeL/MST  .................... For the original design of mst-page\n  iNFoRMeR/PTL ........................... Keep on creating cool tools  \n  THe GRiFTeR/PTL .................................. Your fucking Cool\n  DNSS/TRP .................................... Keep on being original\n  FRaNKy/TRP ............................. THe BeST Co-Sysop on my BBS\n  HeLLBoRG ................................................. CyBeRMaTe\n  SiNTaX/WoT ............................... Great expressdoor Library\n  \n                 >>> ALL MEMBERS OF PuRPLe TuRTLe!!! <<<\n                   >>> ALL MEMBERS OF FIRE''n''ICE!! <<<\n\n  =======================================================================\n@endnode\n@node Cap06 "How to contact us..."\n  =======================================================================\n                Why nøt giving these fåbøløµs BBS å cåll ...\n        _____________________________________________________________\n  _____/                                                             \_____\n  |ø        WhQ                                                          ø|\n  |ø        Taj Mahal             +31 162 322 716      16k8 DS           ø|\n  |ø                                                                     ø|\n  |ø        BhQ                                                          ø|\n  |ø        Metal Impact          +32 503 932 39       16k8 DS           ø|\n  |ø        Phantom               +32 937 707 19       16k8 DS           ø|\n  |ø                                                                     ø|\n  |ø        UShQ                                                         ø|\n  |ø        Asia Blue             +1  919 747 4107     14k4 V32b         ø|\n  |ø        Trancer Bbs           +1  919 231 6880     14K4 SS           ø|\n  |ø                                                                     ø|\n  |ø        Ihq                                                          ø|\n  |ø        Heal The World        +39 322 259 724      14k4 DS           ø|\n  |ø                              +39 322 259 593      14k4 DS           ø|\n  |ø                                                                     ø|\n  |ø        Dhq                                                          ø|\n  |ø        Phantom               +31 463 396 11       16k8 DS           ø|\n  |ø        UnderGround           +31 162 112 321      16k8 DS           ø|\n  |ø                                                                     ø|\n  lø___                                                              ____øj\n   ~   \____________________________________________________________/    ~\n\n  =======================================================================\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),'{"LOCATION":"<string>","ACCESS":"<num>","TYPE":"XIM"}',NULL,16333,4,0,NULL,NULL,'ptlnot10_notifier','scan',1780048679);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ptl_ul02','PTL_UL02.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/PTL_UL02.LHA','UList','XIM','UList',NULL,NULL,'PTL','+-\__---ø\ ---ø\--ø\---[ PurPle TurTle ]---+ ­  /___/ /_____/   /        ¡n 1994        ­ |_/ \___/  / /   _/\  ·PreSenTs UList v0.2·|',replace('  _________________          \n+-\__---ø\ ---ø\--ø\---[ PurPle TurTle ]---+\n­  /___/ /_____/   /        ¡n 1994        ­\n|_/ \___/  / /   _/\  ·PreSenTs UList v0.2·|\n­\__/ \___/ /_______\                      ­\n+-[Fast & Small UserList Bulletin Creator]-+\n','\n',char(10)),'UList.Guide',replace('@database UList.guide\n\n@node Main "UList v0.2 - Contents"\n                                                                             \n UList v0.2 (C) 1994 ZiA [- PtL^D2 -]\n UserList Bulletin Creator for Ami-Express 3.xx & 2.xx.\n\n @{"Features & Requirements     " LINK REQ} What do we need and get.\n @{"Installing                  " LINK CMD} How to install.\n @{"History & Bugs              " LINK BUGS} History & Bugs.\n @{"Contacting me               " LINK CNT} How to contact me.\n @{"Greetings                   " LINK GROET} Greetings.\n			    \n@endnode\n\n@node REQ "What do we need and what do we get?"\n\n @{"Features     " LINK REQ} - Pure Re-entrant Code ( Can Be Made Resident )\n                - FAST & SMALL C Coding (1904 Bytes & +/-200 Users / Sec ).\n                - Doesn''t Show Deleted Users. ( Feature ? )\n               \n @{"Requirements " LINK REQ} - Kickstart V36 And Later.\n                - A User.Data.\n                - A Little Bit Of Memory.\n\n @{"Installing   " LINK CMD} \n\n*NOTE: This Program assumes you are running KS v36 or later. It does\nNot Check for any version and will probably crash on on < v36.\n                       ....who carez ?...\n\n@endnode\n\n@node CMD "for(;;)"\n\n -1. Check it out first! Usage: UList <PATH/USER.DATA> <OUTPUT>\n                            Eg: UList BBS:User.Data RAM:BULL.TXT\n\n 1. Copy the program to a directory where you would like it ( We assume that\n    UList is placed it the BBS:Utils/ directory).\n \n 2. Now edit your Logoff script(s) or/and your Cron script and add the \n		following line:\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n BBS:Utils/UList BBS:User.Data BBS:Bulletins/Bull20.txt\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n \n To keep the bulletin uptodate you should run it at least once an hour, or\n better, every time somebody logs out.\n \n 3. UList Has the ability to remain resident in memory, which means that \n    every time the program is run it''s allready in memory. ( Altough \n    it''s only 1904 bytes small this saves a lot of time...). \n    To make it resident, add the following line to your startup-sequence:\n \n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n RESIDENT BBS:UTILS/UList PURE\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n    and place(with you own paths)\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n UList BBS:USER.DATA BBS:BULLETINS/BULL20.TXT\n -------------------------------------------------------------[cut here]---\n \n    in your logoff / cron script. If you have UList resident, do *NOT* use a\n    path to UList in your script. If you do so, ( Dumb Ass! ) the util will \n    still be loaded  from disk and the resident version will not be used.\n\n @{"Bugs  " LINK BUGS}\n\n@endnode\n@node BUGS "eh?"\n\n @{"History  " LINK BUGS} - v0.1 Got the idea from UserLister v1.6 By JAF/GOD. \n                   Thought it could be done much faster.\n                   Ok... he wrote it in Arexx...\n            - v0.2 ''Slightly'' optimized and produces now ANSI\n                   output. If No bugs are found this will be\n                   the last release.\n\n @{"Bugs     " LINK BUGS} - None untill now. ( 5 Mins of Testing ).\n\n @{"Contact  " LINK CNT} me for anything..\n\n@endnode\n\n@node CNT "Hobo Humpin Slobo Babe..."\n\nContact me for every question / request / bug concerning this util on:\n \n - @{"Wicked City   " LINK CITY} +31-165-385-919\n - @{"TaJ MaHaL     " LINK TAJ} +31-NeV-eRl-AnD\n               \n@endnode\n\n@node GROET "Da BallUh!"\n\nFast Greeting fly out to all PtL-Members around the world....\n\n(Great.. the guide is twice as big as the program itself...)\n\n@endnode \n@node CITY "NoNoNo..."\n\n What are you looking for ? The Number is right behind it...\n\n@endnode\n@node TAJ "HaHaHa.."\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',5899,3,0,NULL,NULL,'ptl_ul02','scan',1780048679);
