        ]·-------------------------------------·\n        ·--------------------------------------·   Total Confs:[  17]                l\n        l         # HD''s:[  2]                 l   Total Nodes:[   5]                l\n        l   Type of HD''s:[ AT-BUS / SCSI      ]l  Active Nodes:[   4]                l\n        l  Free HD Space:[     662342144 Bytes]lInactive Nodes:[   1]                l\n        ·--------------------------------------·-------------------------------------·\n        !_ ____/\\  _ _ ___  100% C CODE, ©1998 [-JiM_bEAM / rEAL-]  ___ _ _  /\\____ _!\n                 \\/       )     Registered to: UNREGISTERED!!!     (       \\/\n\n\n\n                          __.___________ _/\\_.øØø._/\\_ __________.__\n        .øØø.__  /\\_ _ ___)     ,.:![  rEAL-sTATUs V2.0  ]!:.,     (___ _ _/\\  __.øØø.\n        l      \\/                                                            \\/      l\n        l           User Status Info                                                 l\n        ·----------------------------------------------------------------------------·\n        l    Name/Handle:[ Jim_Beam          ] l       Uploads:[                  59]l\n        l    Area Access:[ SYSOP             ] lUploaded Bytes:[            23889100]l\n        l Location/Group:[ [x] rEAL! [x]     ] l     Downloads:[                   0]l\n        l   Phone Number:[ NOTFORYOU!        ] l Leeched Bytes:[                   0]l\n        l  Computer Type:[  26]                l Today Leeched:[                   0]l\n        ·--------------------------------------·-------------------------------------·\n        l    Accesslevel:[ 255]                l    Byte Limit:[                  1] l\n        l   Current Slot:[   1]                l    Time Limit:[ 99998 mins]         l\n        l   Current Node:[   2]                l  Msg''s Posted:[                  1] l\n        l   Current Conf:[ aMIGA.dEMOS       ] l   Line Length:[  57]                l\n        l Current Conf #:[   2]                l         Calls:[               1175] l\n        l    Expert Mode:[ oFF]                ·-------------------------------------·\n        ·--------------------------------------· Last On:[ Sat May 30 17:33:56 1998 ]l\n        l  Current Ratio:[ dISABLED]           l  Online:[    32 mins/99999 mins]    l\n        l     Ratio Type:[ bYTE     ]          l    Baud:[ 19200 ]                   l\n        ·--------------------------------------·-------------------------------------·\n        !_ ____/\\  _ _ ___  100% C CODE, ©1998 [-JiM_bEAM / rEAL-]  ___ _ _  /\\____ _!\n                 \\/       )     Registered to: UNREGISTERED!!!     (       \\/\n\n\n@{b}      BBS Status Info@{ub}\n@{b}      ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~@{ub}\n\n                Name: The name of your BBS\n                      ( max.19 characters; BBSNAME-Tooltype )\n\n          /X Version: The versionnumber of AmiExpress\n                      ( max. 6 characters )\n\n            Location: The location of your BBS\n                      ( max.19 characters; BBSLOCATION-Tooltype )\n\n              # HD''s: The number of HD''s you use for your BBS\n                      ( max.2 characters; HDCOUNT-Tooltype )\n\n        Type of HD''s: The type of Harddiskdrive(s) you use for your BBS\n                      ( max.19 characters; HDTYPE-Tooltype )\n\n       Free HD Space: The free Harddiskdrive(s) space for uploads\n                      ( max.13 characters )\n\n               Sysop: The Name/Handle of the Sysop\n                      ( max.19 characters )\n\n           Chat Mode: ON/OFF ... shows if Sysop is available for chat on the\n                      current node\n                      ( max.3 characters )\n\n         Total Confs: The total number of conferences\n                      ( max.3 characters )\n\n         Total Nodes: The total number of nodes\n                      ( max.3 characters; NODES-Tooltype )\n\n        Active Nodes: The number of active Nodes\n                      ( max.3 characters )\n\n      Inactive Nodes: The number of inactive Nodes\n                      ( max.3 characters )\n\n\n@{b}      User Status Info@{ub}\n@{b}      ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~@{ub}\n\n         Name/Handle: The name/handle of the user\n                      ( max.18 characters )\n\n         Area Access: The area to which the user belongs to\n                      ( max.18 characters )\n\n      Location/Group: The location/group the user belongs to\n                      ( max.18 characters )\n\n        Phone Number: The phonenumber of the user\n                      ( max.18 characters )\n\n       Computer Type: The number of the Computer the user uses\n                      ( see ComputerList-Icon for complete )\n                      ( max.3 characters )\n\n         Accesslevel: The accesslevel of the user\n                      ( max.3 characters )\n\n        Current Slot: The current slot the user uses\n                      ( max.3 characters )\n\n        Current Node: The current node on which the user logged in\n                      ( max.3 characters )\n\n        Current Conf: The current joined conference of the user\n                      ( max.18 characters )\n\n      Current Conf #: The current joined conference number of the user\n                      ( max.3 characters )\n\n         Expert Mode: ON/OFF... shows the mode of the user...\n                      menue display ON or menue display OFF\n                      ( max.3 characters )\n\n       Current Ratio: The ratio of the user\n                      ( max.1 character )\n\n          Ratio Type: The ratio type of the user\n                      ( max.9 characters )\n\n             Uploads: The number of files the user uploaded in the current conference\n                      ( max.19 characters )\n\n      Uploaded Bytes: The number of bytes the user uploaded in the current conference\n                      ( max.19 characters )\n\n           Downloads: The number of files the user downloaded in the current conference\n                      ( max.19 characters )\n\n       Leeched Bytes: The number of bytes the user downloaded in the current conference\n                      ( max.19 characters )\n\n       Today Leeched: The number of bytes the user downloaded in the current conference\n                      today\n                      ( max.19 characters )\n\n          Byte Limit: The number of bytes the user may download\n                      ( max.18 characters )\n\n          Time Limit: How many minutes the user may use the BBS today\n                      ( max.5 characters )\n\n        Msg''s Posted: The number of messages the user has written\n                      in the current conference\n                      ( max.18 characters )\n\n         Line Length: How many lines are displayed in output\n                      ( max.3 characters )\n\n               Calls: The number of total calls the user has made\n                      ( max.18 characters )\n\n   Last Call/Last On: The date and time of user''s last call\n                      ( max.25 characters )\n\n    Time used/Online: How many minutes the user has used the BBS already\n                      ( max.5 characters )\n\n   Total Time/Online: How many minutes the user may use the BBS at total\n                      ( max.5 characters )\n\n   Connect Baud/Baud: The Baudrate of the user with that he connected to\n                      the BBS\n                      ( max.6 characters )\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "E_Mails_and_IRC_Node" "E_Mails_and_IRC"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n@{b}e-MAILs aND iRC@{ub}\n@{b}~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~@{ub}\n\n        e-MAILS:\n        --------\n        JiM_bEAM          e-mAIL tO: [email removed]\n                                     [email removed]\n        bUD               e-mAIL tO: [email removed]\n        hIGH-SPEEd        e-mAIL tO: [email removed]\n                                     [email removed]\n        iRON              e-mAIL tO: [email removed]\n                                     [email removed]\n                                     [email removed]\n        [-sAxOn-]         e-mAIL tO: [email removed]\n        sTEEL             e-mAIL tO: [email removed]\n        sTEVE             e-mAIL tO: [email removed]\n        dARKoNE           e-mAIL tO: [email removed]\n        hAZE              e-mAIL tO: [email removed]\n        jUNK              e-mAIL tO: [email removed]\n        kGB               e-mAIL tO: [email removed]\n\n\n\n        nICKS oN iRC (#amielite):\n        -------------------------\n        JiM_bEAM          nICKNAME oN iRC: JB^rEAL, jim_beam\n        bUD               nICKNAME oN iRC: Bud^rEAL, Bud\n        fLUX              nICKNAME oN iRC: fLUX, [fLUX]\n        hIGH-sPEED        nICKNAME oN iRC: High-Speed, HS\n        iRON              nICKNAME oN iRC: iRON, iRON^rEAL\n\n        ...tRY tO fIND oUT dA rEST yOURSELF oR aSK oN iRC!\n\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "Real_Node" "Real"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n@{b}rEAL@{ub}\n@{b}~~~~@{ub}\n\n@{b}                 .:::::.  .::::.      ..:::::.     ..:::::.\n               .::::::::.:::::::.   .:::··:::::   ::·:::::·\n             .:::::::::::::::::::  .:::·   ::::    .::::·\n         .:::::· :::::::·   :::::: ·::·    ::::   .:::·\n         :::::  ::::::::    ::::::    .... ::::  .:::·\n          :::.  :::::::;   ::::::; .::::::::::: .:::·          ...\n           :::. ·::::::...::::::· .::::··:::::: :::·          ::::.\n           ·:::. ··::::::::::··   ::::    ::::::::·            ::::\n            ·:::.  :::·        ..:::::    :::::::::.......:::::::::\n             ::::; :::    ...::::::::::..::::::::::::::::·····::::;\n              ···  ·::::::::::::· ·::::::::::·····b!d\n                    ·::::····\n\n                     [rEAL!] [tHE cHOICE oF qUALITY!]\n@{ub}\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "Contact_Node" "Contact"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n@{b}cONTACt@{ub}\n@{b}~~~~~~~@{ub}\n\n       tRY oUR wEBPAGE nOW...\n\n       rEAL hOMEPAGE: http://real.realworld.de\n\n       oR/aND...\n\n       JiM_bEAM''s hOMEPAGE: http://www.geocities.com/SunsetStrip/Club/8307/\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "Tools_released_Node" "Tools_released"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n@{b}tOOLz rELEASEd@{ub}\n@{b}~~~~~~~~~~~~~~@{ub}\n\n   pASSWORd sECURITy V1.0       iNTERNAL vERSION... nEVER rELEASED\n   pASSWORd sECURITy V1.1       nOW aVAILABLE...\n   pASSWORd sECURITy V1.2       nOW aVAILABLE...\n   pASSWORd sECURITy V1.3       nOW aVAILABLE... mAYbE iT''S tHE fINAL oNE\n   pASSWORd sECURITy V1.3.1     nOW aVAILABLE... (uPDATE fIX)\n   pASSWORd sECURITy V1.4       noW aVAILABLE...\n   rEAL-qUICKlOGON V1.0         nOW aVAILABLE...\n   rEAL-sTATUS V1.0             nOW aVAILABLE... (JiM_bEAM''s Version)\n   rEAL-sTATUS V2.0             nOW aVAILABLE... (JiM_bEAM''s Version)\n   sYS-DOWn V1.2                nOW aVAILABLE...\n   bAUD-cOUNTER V1.1            nOW aVAILABLE...\n   bAUD-cOUNTER V1.3            nOW aVAILABLE...\n   sEC-CHECk V1.3               nOW aVAILABLE...\n   rEAL-sTAT V1.1               nOW aVAILABLE...\n   cONF-MOVEr V1.1              nOW aVAILABLE...\n   rEAL-CALLERs V1.1            nOW aVAILABLE...\n   sYS-cOMMENT V1.1             nOW aVAILABLE...\n   rEAL-pAGE V1.1               nOW aVAILABLE...\n   rEAL-wALL V1.1               nOW aVAILABLE...\n   rEAL-wALL V1.2               nOW aVAILABLE...\n   rEAL-uPLOAD V1.0             nOW aVAILABLE...\n   rEAL-uPLOAD V1.1             nOW aVAILABLE...\n\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "emailware_Node" "emailware"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n@{b}E-mAILWARe ??@{ub}\n@{b}~~~~~~~~~~~~~@{ub}\n\n   You will ask yourself what''s meant by "E-mAILWARe".\n   Well, because i would like to know who is using my door for his BBS\n   i decided to release this door under "E-mAILWARe".\n   That means if you interested in this door and want to use it in your\n   BBS, you have to send me a e-mail with the Registerstring\n   (Handle or Handle & Group; up to 15 characters long)\n   you would like to have inserted into the Registertext "Registered to:"\n   in the Design.\n   Otherwise the Registertext will look like this:\n   Registered to: UNREGISTERED!!!\n\n   If you register the Registertext will look like this for example:\n\n   Registered to: JiM_bEAM^rEAL!\n\n   The door is fully functional without the Registerstring too.\n\n   My e-mail: [email removed]\n              [email removed]\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n','\n',char(10)),'{"ACCESS":"<num>","TYPE":"<","LOCATION":"<string>","STACK":"<Value>"}','auto-added',75535,2,0,NULL,NULL,'rea_st2','scan',1780048686);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('rea_st21','REA-ST21.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/REA-ST21.LHA',NULL,'XIM','rEAL-sTATUs00.exe',NULL,'JiM_bEAM','REA','_________/\  _ __ ____ _ ____/\ ___. REAL! \___.___  \\      ___/    .___\\   |______ |  /  _/___ ___)_____ ___/  \  l      \',replace('\n_________/\  _ __ ____ _ ____/\ ___. REAL!\n\___.___  \\      ___/    .___\\   |______\n    |  /  _/___ ___)_____ ___/  \  l      \\n yopl__\       \______  /_|      \______ //\n =======\_______\=====\/==l_______\=====\/=\n |                                        |\n |          * rEAL-sTATUs v2.1 *          |\n |  "S" cOMMANd rEPLACEMENt bY JiM_bEAM   |\n |                                        |\n `--[1/1]-----[ /X dOOR ]-----[05/31/98]--´\n','\n',char(10)),'rEAL-sTATUs.guide',replace('@DATABASE "rEAL-Status.guide"\n@NODE "Main" "rEAL-sTATUS V 1.0 bY JiM_bEAM / rEAL!"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n@{b}                _________/\\  _ __ _____ _ ____/\\ ___.@{ub}\n@{b}                \\___.___   \\\       ___/    .___ \\   |______@{ub}\n@{b}                    |  /  _/___  ___)_____ ___/  \\  l      \\@{ub}\n@{b}                     __\\       \\ ______  /_|      \\______ //@{ub}\n@{b}           <------ -----\\_______\\-- - -\\/--l_______\\yop -\\/- -- ->@{ub}\n\n@{b}          ... bRINGz yA ...@{ub}                    @{" iNTRODUCTIOn! " LINK "Introduction_Node"}\n@{b}                                       @{" rEQUIREMENTs! " LINK "Requirements_Node"}@{"tOOLz rELEASEd!" LINK "Tools_released_Node"}\n@{b}          rEAL-sTATUS V2.1!@{ub}            @{" iNSTALLATIOn! " LINK "Installation_Node"}@{" E-mAILWARe ?? " LINK "emailware_Node"}\n@{b}      tHE sTATUS /X dOOR bY rEAL@{ub}       @{" cONFIGURATIOn " LINK "Configuration_Node"}@{"   gREETINGs   " LINK "Greetings_Node"}\n@{b}                                       @{"    wORKINg    " LINK "Working_Node"}@{"    cONTACt    " LINK "Contact_Node"}\n@{b}      - cODED bY JiM_bEAM/rEAL -@{ub}       @{" dESIGn eXPLANATIOn! " LINK "DesignExplanation_Node"}@{"  rEAL!  " LINK "Real_Node"}\n@{b}    - dESIGN bY Trivial^JiM_bEAM -@{ub}            @{" e-mAILs aND iRC " LINK "E_Mails_and_IRC_Node"}\n\n\n@{b}     NOTE: THIS MIGHT BE MY LAST RELEASE UNDER THE "rEAL"-GROUPLABEL\n              BECAUSE THE GROUP "rEAL" IS OFFICIALLY DEAD NOW !!! @{ub}\n\n-===-===-===-===-===-===-===-===-===-===-===-===-===-===-===-===-===-===-===-\n                         this tool is E-MAILWARE\n                    copyright © 1998  JiM_bEAM / rEAL!\n-===-===-===-===-===-===-===-===-===-===-===-===-===-===-===-===-===-===-===-\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "Introduction_Node" "Introduction"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n@{b}iNTRODUCTIOn@{ub}\n@{b}~~~~~~~~~~~~@{ub}\n\n           ... here is the rEAL-sTATUS Door by JiM_bEAM / rEAL ...\n\n\n  Features:\n\n          - Download Option: the user can download his Status-Info\n          - TWO different Status-Infos in ONE door:\n            BBS-Status and User-Status\n          - all code written in pure C language\n          - 68000, 68020+ versions\n          - Because of @{b}NO BACKDOOR@{ub} NO RISK\n            Disassemble the code if ya don''t believe me !!!\n\n          To see all features just install the door and enter "S"\n          in the mainprompt of /X\n\n\n  NEW Features in V2.0:\n\n          - completly reorganised\n          - added a main menu\n          - 3 different Status-Infos in ONE door:\n            Complete Status (BBS + User; long output)\n            BBS Status\n            User Status\n          - view option for every status info\n          - download option for every status info\n          - Quit option\n          - all code written in pure C language\n          - 68000, 68020+ versions\n          - Because of @{b}NO BACKDOOR@{ub} NO RISK\n            Disassemble the code if ya don''t believe me !!!\n\n          To see all features just install the door and enter "S"\n          in the mainprompt of /X\n\n\n  NEW in V2.1:\n\n          - fixed a little bug in the "User-status only" design\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "Requirements_Node" "Requirements"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n@{b}rEQUIREMENTs@{ub}\n@{b}~~~~~~~~~~~~@{ub}\n\n                            Everyone can run it!!!\n\n          - you only need an AMIGA\n          - KS2.04 or higher\n          - the great AmiExpress V4.x\n          - the AEDoor.library V2.4+ in Libs:\n          - and rEALdOOR.library in Libs: (included in this archive)\n          - a assinged T: directory where "Status.log", "BBSStatus.log",\n            "USERStatus.log"-File will be stored for downloading\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "Installation_Node" "Installation"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n@{b}iNSTALLATIOn@{ub}\n@{b}~~~~~~~~~~~~@{ub}\n\n                      The installation is very simple...\n\n   - copy the rEALdOOR.library to Libs:\n   - copy the directory rEAL with all the files to DOORS:\n   - copy the directory COMMANDS with all the files to BBS:\n\n   ready...\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "Working_Node" "Working"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n@{b}wORKINg@{ub}\n@{b}~~~~~~~@{ub}\n\n   This Door is a replacement for the internal "S"-Command\n   in AmiExpress.\n   It shows the user info about his Status and about the\n   Status of the BBS.\n   There is a download option for the user so that he can\n   download the Status-Info if he need it.\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "Configuration_Node" "Configuration"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n@{b}cONFIGURATIOn@{ub}\n@{b}~~~~~~~~~~~~~@{ub}\n\n  You can configure the door. My door uses the standard /X-Tooltype-Configuration !\n\n  S.info ICON:\n\n  Tooltypes:\n     ACCESS\n     TYPE\n     LOCATION\n     STACK\n     NAME\n     MULTINODE\n     BBSNAME\n     BBSLOCATION\n     HDCOUNT\n     HDTYPE\n     HDSTORE\n     NODES\n\n\n  ACCESS:\n     Pattern : ACCESS= <num>\n     Function: Tells /X the access level required to run this module.\n               This option is ignored for internal Module options.\n     Example : ACCESS=10\n               Check for a level about 10 or higher.\n\n  TYPE:\n     Pattern : TYPE= < XIM | AIM | TIM | IIM | SIM | MCI >\n     Function: This is the type of door you use.\n     Example : TYPE=XIM\n               For my door the TYPE should be XIM !!!\n\n  LOCATION:\n     Pattern : LOCATION= <string>\n     Function: Specifies the location of the module\n     Example1: LOCATION=DOORS:rEAL/rEAL-sTATUS/rEAL-sTATUS00.exe\n               If you are using the version for 68000 CPUs !\n\n     Example2: LOCATION=DOORS:rEAL/rEAL-sTATUS/rEAL-sTATUS020.exe\n               If you are using the version for 68020 CPUs !\n\n     Example3: LOCATION=DOORS:rEAL/rEAL-sTATUS/rEAL-sTATUS030.exe\n               If you are using the version for 68030 CPUs !\n\n     Example4: LOCATION=DOORS:rEAL/rEAL-sTATUS/rEAL-sTATUS0x0.exe\n               If you are using the version for 68040/60 CPUs !\n\n  STACK:\n     Pattern : STACK= <Value>\n     Function: Specifies the Stack-value for the door and should be\n               set to 10000 !\n     Example : STACK = 10000\n               Sets stack to 10000\n\n  NAME:\n     Pattern : NAME= <Doorname>\n     Function: Specifies the name to display in the /X-Server window\n     Example : NAME = rEAL-sTATUS\n\n  MULTINODE:\n     Pattern : MULTINODE= <YES|NO>\n     Function: Tells /X if the module may be simultaneously accessed\n               from other nodes.\n\n  BBSNAME:\n     Pattern : BBSNAME= <Textstring>\n     Function: Here you must enter the name of your BBS which should\n               be displayed in the Status-Output\n     Example : BBSNAME=tHE dUNGEON\n\n  BBSLOCATION:\n     Pattern : BBSLOCATION= <Textstring>\n     Function: Here you must enter the location of your BBS which should\n               be displayed in the Status-Output\n     Example : BBSLOCATION=USA\n\n  HDCOUNT:\n     Pattern : HDCOUNT= <Number>\n     Function: Here you must enter the number of Harddiskdrives you use for\n               your BBS and should be displayed in the Status-Output\n     Example : HDCOUNT=2\n               You use 2 Harddiskdrives for your BBS\n\n  HDTYPE:\n     Pattern : HDTYPE= <Textstring>\n     Function: Here you must enter what type of Harddiskdrive(s) you use\n               for your BBS and should be displayed in the Status-Output\n     Example1: HDTYPE=AT-BUS\n               You use AT-BUS Harddiskdrive(s)\n     Example2: HDTYPE=SCSI\n               You use SCSI Harddiskdrive(s)\n     Example3: HDTYPE=AT-BUS / SCSI\n               You use AT-BUS and SCSI Harddiskdrives\n\n  HDSTORE:\n     Pattern : HDSTORE= <Path and filename to uploads-storage>\n     Function: Here you must enter the complete path to your\n               BBS-Harddiskdrives where uploads are stored\n               !! IT''S IMPORTANT FOR DISPLAYING THE "Free HD Space" !!\n     Example1: HDSTORE=BBS:\n               All uploads are stored in "BBS:"\n     Example2: HDSTORE=BBS:Uploads/\n               All uploads are stored in "BBS:Uploads"\n               !! DON''T FORGET THE "/" IF THE PATH IS A DIRECTORY !!\n\n  NODES:\n     Pattern : NODES= <Number>\n     Function: The number of total nodes your BBS supports\n     Example : NODES=5\n               Your BBS supports 5 Nodes (0,1,2,3,4)\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "Greetings_Node" "Greetings"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n@{b}gREETINGs!@{ub}\n@{b}~~~~~~~~~~@{ub}\n\n                           ... GReeTz fLYIng To ...\n\n\n      greETz fROM JiM_bEAM 2:\n\n      eXON, dIGIMAN, sHALLOW , cHUCK, TMN , hAMLET, lUCAS, lANCE,\n      sHADOW, zOD, dR.dRE, cOKE, wOober, pETRIEfIEd...\n      anD tO aLl mY cONTACTs oN #amielite anD dA rEST oF tHE cOOL sCENE...\n\n\n\n      sPECIAL gREETZ fROM JiM_bEAM :\n      ------------------------------\n\n      hIGH-SPEEd    nICHTs aLS dEN sERVEr iM kOPF wA ;)\n\n      jOULE         i''m sTILL w8ING fOR tHE rESt oF tHe aNSIs\n\n      iRON          nUR nOCH dEN rEAL-sERVER uND uNIx iM kOPf wA ;)\n                    "aMIGa iST tOD" ;)\n\n      jUDGE rAPID   wAR nEN eCHT cOOLEs gESPRÄCH aUF dER "cOMPUTER ''97"\n                    cOMPUtER ''98 ??\n\n      sLAPSHOt      "SLT" iS dEAD oDDA wAS ?\n                    mAN sIEHt, hÖRt nICHTs mEHr vON dIR... lEFT tHE sCENe ?\n      \n      sUNBEAM       iMMER fLEIßIG aM cODEn wAS ;)\n                    mAN tRIFFt sICH wIEDEr... aUF #amielite :)\n\n      bLUe          wO bISt dU ? sCHAU mAl wIEDEr aUF #amielite rEIn :)\n\n      sTEEl         sOSo... nUN tRSI... mAN bILDEt sICH wEITer wOll :)\n\n      wOober        tHNx fOR dOING aLL tHE aNSIs aND aSCIIs fOR mE\n                    aND fOR iNFORMING mE aBOUt tHE dESIGn bUG :)\n\n\n      \n      oKAY fOLKS nOTHING mORE... nEXT tIME i`ll sHOW tHE nEXT gREETINGS!\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE "DesignExplanation_Node" "DesignExplanation"\n@TOC "MAIN"\n@{b}dESIGn eXPLANATIOn!@{ub}\n@{b}~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~@{ub}\n\n                          __.___________ _/\\_.øØø._/\\_ __________.__\n        .øØø.__  /\\_ _ ___)     ,.:![  rEAL-sTATUs V2.1  ]!:.,     (___ _ _/\\  __.øØø.\n        l      \\/                                                            \\/      l\n        l           BBS Status Info            l           User Status Info          l\n        ·----------------------------------------------------------------------------·\n        l           Name:[ tHE dUNGEOn        ]l    Name/Handle:[ Jim_Beam          ]l\n        l     /X Version:[ v4.9  ]             l    Area Access:[ SYSOP             ]l\n        l       Location:[ USA                ]l Location/Group:[ [x] rEAL! [x]     ]l\n        ·--------------------------------------·   Phone Number:[ NOTFORYOU!        ]l\n        l         # HD''s:[  2]                 l  Computer Type:[  26]               l\n        l   Type of HD''s:[ AT-BUS / SCSI      ]·-------------------------------------·\n        l  Free HD Space:[     674433024 Bytes]l    Accesslevel:[ 255]               l\n        ·--------------------------------------l   Current Slot:[   1]               l\n        l          Sysop:[ Jim_Beam           ]l   Current Node:[   2]               l\n        l      Chat Mode:[ oN ]                l   Current Conf:[ aMIGA.dEM