INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('s_x39n2','S!X39N2.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/S!X39N2.LHA','config','XIM','CONFIG',NULL,'SIGMA',NULL,'| S!X Version 0.39n2 (Beta Release V0.1b)  | l__________________________________________| |                                          |',replace('.------------------------------------------.\n| S!X Version 0.39n2 (Beta Release V0.1b)  |\nl__________________________________________|\n|                                          |\n| Modular BBS Package written by SIGMA 7!  |\n|     /X Compatible , just *NO* Icons      |\n|     Easy to use and easy to install.     |\n|Takes advantage of OS2.1 LOCALE Feature!  |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'Announce.doc',replace('\n       _ _ ___/\______/\__ ____/\___/\__ _ _/\____ _/\_ __ __/\______\n      __ ________   __   /   _   ___   / ______   \___/__/     _____/\n         bIS/   /   /   /   //   //   /___/ __¬   /  /  /  /\__   \\n           /   /   /   /   //   //   /   /  \    /  /  /  /   /   /\n    __  _ _\____  /\____  //_  //_____  /___/\  /\_____  /\ _/   /___\n     _  ___ _   \/  _  _\/_  \/____ __\/ ___ _\/_______\/____   /_ _/\n                                                            \  /\n                                  present                    \/\n\n                      a tool for AmiExpress 2.xx/3.xx:\n\n                 >>> Announce v2.0 by Aquarius/Outlaws <<<\n\n\n                          Copyright ©1994 Aquarius\n\n                 Permission is granted to freely distribute\n               this product for non-commercial purposes only,\n                  as long as all files remain unmodified.\n\n\nArchive (OTL-AN20.LHA) Contents\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nDoors/Announce/\n   AnnLogon.10             9724 bytes  10-node version of the door.\n   AnnLogon.32             9812 bytes  32-node version (for /X 3.30+)..\n   AnnLogoff               7884 bytes  CLI util for logoff messages.\n   Announce.doc            6805 bytes  This document file.\n   Announce.guide         12578 bytes  AmigaGuide version of the doc.\n\nCommands/SYSCmd/\n   AnnLogon.info           1249 bytes  Command icon for /X 3.xx.\n\n\nIntroduction\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\nIf you are running a multi-node board, you just HAVE to try this tool!\nIt''s a really pleasant thing to have installed, for you and your users.\n\nWhat is does? Well, when a user logs on, it notifies the users who are\nalready online (on the other nodes) of the logon. You can also make it\nnotify them of logoffs (and loss carriers). If a message can''t be sent\nbecause the user is doing something (uploading, reading bulletins etc),\nthe message is queued. When he becomes idle again, he instantly gets all\nhis waiting logon/logoff messages. Here is an example of how that can\nlook:\n\n>>> Announce v2.0 by Aquarius/OTL <<<\n     ( Current time: 17:14:00 )\n\nHardHack logged in on node 3 at 17:07:37.\nErod logged off from node 1 at 17:09:13.\n\n>>>>\n\n\nRequirements\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\nAn Amiga with OS 2.0 or higher.\nAmiExpress/SigmaExpress.\n(The door works for sure on /X v2.20-3.38 and possibly on other versions\ntoo.)\n\n\nInstallation\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\nFirst create the directory ''Doors:Announce'', and copy the correct version\nof the door there. AnnLogon.10 is for AmiExpress versions below 3.30 and\nfor SigmaExpress. AnnLogon.32 is for AmiExpress 3.30 or higher.\n\n/X 2.xx, SigmaExpress:\n\nAdd the following line to your SYS.Cmd file:\n\n-----Cut-here-------------------------------\n*ANNLOGON XM005Doors:Announce/AnnLogon.10\n-------Cut-here-----------------------------\n\n/X 3.xx:\n\nCopy ''annlogon.info'' to your SYSCmd directory and check that its tooltype\nLOCATION is correct.\n\n\nRun the door with MCI in the Logon.txt. Don''t worry, the door is totally\ninvisible to the on-logging users. Every Logon.txt should start with the\nfollowing:\n\n-----Cut-here-------------\n~\n~CC_ANNLOGON|\n-------Cut-here-----------\n\n\nThe logoff notifier is not necessary to install (in contrast to the logon\nnotifier) but I really recommend that you do it (it''s nice!). Then copy\nAnnLogoff to Doors:Announce/. Run it in the logoff scripts, preferably\namong the first commands. You must supply two arguments: the node number\nand the node location (defined in ACP.info for /X 3.xx) which for most\nsysops is the same as the bbs location (bbs:). For example, in the logoff\nscript for node 2, write this line:\n\n-----Cut-here------------------------\nDoors:Announce/AnnLogoff 2 BBS:\n-------Cut-here----------------------\n\n(Provided that the location for the directory ''Node2'' is ''BBS:''.)\n\nPerhaps you shouldn''t put it in the script for your local node, since you\nprobably always logon with F1 and therefore by-pass Logon.txt and the\nlogon notifier. It would probably confuse your users if they only got the\nmessage that you logged off, and they hadn''t even noticed that you were\nonline.\n\n\nMiscellaneous Info\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThe first time the door (AnnLogon.xx) is used, it stays in memory as a\n''host task'' that will perform all the actual message sending to the nodes\nat the right times. Therefore, no logoff messages can be sent before the\nlogon notifier has been used. But the logon notifier is normally started\nfirst so this shouldn''t be any problem. If the logoff notifier is run\nfirst, nothing happens (no system crash if that''s what you thought).\n\nIf you want to change to another version of the door (from 10-node to\n32-node for example) or you want to reset Announce (clear all waiting\nmessages), you will first need to remove the door from memory.\n\nThat is accomplished by sending it a CTRL-C signal, for example by using\nthe AmigaDOS ''break'' command. If you don''t know how to do that I can tell\nyou... Open a shell and type ''status'', which shows all loaded processes.\nOne of them should be Doors:Announce/AnnLogon or something. Notice the\nprocess number for it. Then type ''break <process>'', for example ''break 8''\nif the process number was 8. Type ''status'' again and the process should be\ngone.\n\n\nContact Me!\n~~~~~~~~~~~\nIf you have any cool ideas for improvement of this tool, bug reports,\nquestions, or whatever, leave me a message on one of the following boards:\n\nNIGHTFALL ................ Prof Do Right ..... +46-90-120369\nOVERLOAD (OTL SHQ) ....... Vegas ............. +46-8-54063666\nHYSTERIA ................. JAC ............... +46-21-842939\nRAISING HELL ............. Psychopath ........ +46-23-26893\nINSIDE OUT ............... C/\TE¥E ........... +46-346-58697\nSNAKE''S DEN (OTL WHQ) .... Snake ............. +1-513-683-2330\nTHE HOLE ................. Oldman ............ +1-419-899-2754\n\n\nHistory\n~~~~~~~\n1.0  (1993-08-04) First release. It was then called ''AnnounceLogon''.\n\n2.0  (1994-04-24) Release version. The tool name was changed to just\n     ''Announce'' because I added logoff notification.\n\n     Messages are queued until the user becomes idle.\n\n     Messages are now sent without going via ARexx.\n\n     There are more news but I''m too lazy to describe them all.\n\n\nGreetings\n~~~~~~~~~\n               Greetings must go to (in no special order):\n\n      - All Members of Outlaws!! - Prof Do Right/Classic - JAC/TDS -\n    - C/\TE¥E/Insane - Ace Caze/Obscene - Wilsom/Obscene - Kid Curry -\n   - Psychopath - Vinzi - Karma - Zin - Shapechanger - Rize - Seagull -\n    - Remix/Classic - RaJ-Ban - fanta/Therion - Static/Therion - CaT -\n     - Dansken - AXL/Attention - Rad!/LSD - Vileius! - Marwin/Duplo -\n      - Freddy Kreuger/GOD - Chig/TDS - The Silencer - Vampire/PDY -\n       - Crocodile/Obscene - Sal-One - Nojje - Zune/HCD - MadCap -\n           - Metalbasher - WarDancer/H&V - The Ones I Forgot! -\n\n\n[EOF]','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',1156943,18,0,NULL,NULL,'exe_phr','scan',1780048704);
