INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('sad_al10','SAD-AL10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/SAD-AL10.LHA','gd-advertlog','XIM','LE-win5-96.exe',NULL,NULL,'SAD','\    _/   _//  __/__)  _    /  |_\(_/   _/ \   \    \/  _\   |  _/   /   _/ \\    \ ._\   \    \_._____|  \___.    |    \    \_.',replace('______ _____ _____  _________ _  __  _____  \n\    _/   _//  __/__)  _    /  |_\(_/   _/  \n \   \    \/  _\   |  _/   /   _/ \\    \   \n._\   \    \_._____|  \___.    |    \    \_.\n|_____/\_____|-Mo!-|___|--|____|_____\_____|\n| Sceptic! AmiExpress Design 1996 Presents |\n| SAD-AdvertLogger(TM) Version 1.0 Public! |\n| Idea: Marc Panther (Syncopation Bbs) And |\n| Code: GraveDancer/Sad                    |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'gd-advertlog.guide',replace('@database SAD-AdvertLog.guide\n@$VER: 1.0\n@author "GraveDancer/Sad ([email removed])"\n@(c) "(sCEPTIC /X dESIGN 1996)"\n@remark cREATED uSING cED 3.5\n@node "Main" "English Doc for SAD-AdvertLog"\n\n@{b}      .:::::::::::::::::::: .:::::::::::::::::::. ::::::::::::::::::.\n      `:::::::::..........  :::::::::: :::::::::: :::::::::: :::::::::.\n      .......... :::::::::: ::::::::::::::::::::: :::::::::: ::::::::::\n      ::::::::::.:::::::::: :::::::::: :::::::::: :::::::::: ::::::::::\n      `:::::::::::::::::::'' :::::::::: :::::::::: ::::::::::::::::::::''\n                            ::::::::::@{ub}\n                        .                            .\n                      .:::. sCEPTIC /X dESIGN 1996 .:::.\n\n                                 pRESENTS\n\n@{b}       Sceptic AdvertLog - Idea: Marc Panther - (C) GraveDancer/Sad@{ub}\n\n @{"Coypright Notes" link "CopyRight" 0}     @{"Introductions  " link "Introducti" 0}\n @{"Install to /X  " link "Install" 0}     @{"SAD Members    " link "members" 0}     @{"Contact SAD    " link "contact" 0}\n\n                   SAD - AmiExpress Doors And Beyond...\n\n@endnode\n@node "Copyright" "Copyright notes"\n.-=========================================================================-.\n|.:::::::::::::::::::::::::::] @{b}Copyright Notes@{ub} [:::::::::::::::::::::::::::.|\n`-=========================================================================-''\n\n @{b}Copyright@{ub}\n This program is written and copyright © 1996 by Sebastian Bergmann. No parts\n of  this  program  may  be  altered by any means (this includes editing,\n reprogramming, crunching, resourceing etc.), except archiving.\n\n This program, means several parts of it, takes use of the following programs:\n\n main idea @{b}............@{ub} (C) marc panther (syncopation bbs)\n rexxtricks.library @{b}...@{ub} (C) [email removed]\n\n @{b}Disclaimer@{ub}\n The  author  is in no way liable for any changes made to any part of the\n program,  or  consequences thereof as he is in no way liable for damages\n or loss of data directly or indirectly caused by this software.\n \n @{b}Distribution@{ub}\n Neither fees may be charged nor profits may be made by distributing this\n piece  of  software.  Only a nominal fee for costs of magnetic media may\n be  accepted,  the  amount  of  US  $5  shouldn''t be exceeded for a disk\n containing  Quick-Assign.  CD Manufactures are specifically granted the\n right to  include  this program on CD collections, as long as they are \n for the Public Domain. But the user still has to pay the registration fee!\n\n This software is provided @{b}as is@{ub} without warranty of any kind,\n either expressed or implied. By using this software package, you agree to\n accept the entire risk as to the quality and performance of this package.\n\n In no event (unless required by applicable law or agreed to in\n writing) will any copyright holder, or any other party who may\n redistribute this package as permitted above, be liable to you for\n damages, including any general, special, incidential or consequential\n damages arising out of the use or inability to use this package\n (including but not limited to loss of data or data being rendered\n inaccurate or losses sustained by you or third parties), even if such\n holder or other party has been advised of the possibility of such\n damages.\n\n @{b}The Author@{ub}\n Sebastian Bergmann a/k/a. GraveDancer/Sad\n ([email removed])\n Aulgasse 14\n 53721 Siegburg\n Germany\n\n Voice/Data: +49(0)2241-6238423\n\n                                    @{"Main Menu" link "Main" 0}\n@endnode\n@node "Introducti" "Introduction"\n.-=========================================================================-.\n|.::::::::::::::::::::::::::::] @{b}Introduction@{ub} [:::::::::::::::::::::::::::::.|\n`-=========================================================================-''\n\nYou canot imagine what a AdvertLogger (TM) is ??? Well, so did I until my\nregistered user marc panther told me his idea! Let''s quote him a bit...\n\n>I wonder is it possible to code a bbs adder that adds bbs adverts to 1 txt\n>file just like a .nfo or .txt adder but instead of a 40-60 line individual\n>bbs ascii files all the bbs ascii adder does is add 1 line 76 characters long\n>like this example...\n\n[ Sceptic Advert Logger (C) 1996 GraveDancer/Sad & Marc Panther ]----------- -\n\nDear dowloader of this file (SAD-AL10.LHA),\nto keep track on the way this file made its way to the bbs you leeched it from\nand to reduce the amount of adverts in an traded  file  the  following  boards\ndecided to install this fine door! It tells you on the one hand  were  it  was\ntraded first etc. and on the other hand the sysops can advert their  bbs  with\none single line.\n\nBulletin Board System  Groups/Location                    Node  Date/Time\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------- -\nTower·Of·Souls         Sceptic (DST) And Protest (WHQ)    00    25/04/96 13:32\n\nWell, i liked this idea so much and realised it in two hours of coding,\nincluding betatesting on some files...\n\nAt the moment it handles only .lha,.lzh and .lzx archives, but maybe i decide\nit at least to handle textfiles...\n\nBut! such doors like this gain only a real effect if many sysops use it, so\nthat the leecher can see from which bbs it was downloaded, uploaded then to\nthe next bbs, and so on!\n\nI also included this advert logger as a new feature to my filechecker, the\nregistered users among you get the update the usual way...\n\nThe executable files are pgp-signed so that you can check them if they are\nin their original state. My pgp public key follows...\n\nType Bits/KeyID    Date       User ID\npub  1024/4E990139 1996/03/29 Sebastian Bergmann <[email removed]>\n\n-----BEGIN PGP PUBLIC KEY BLOCK-----\nVersion: 2.6.3i\n\nmQCNAzFbKy8AAAEEAODlvHEfy2dWjvWynMVZtqG8T2eN+Wdz8+4gE3fPudS8tCtp\ni64EVDvoUpBt7U65HIJ6+idSf7hT3XuvTMMApvCuC/N05ntZ1gG1FdUZe4Fir01p\nU+FR/6tP+owKiX68S4HalyL4cMYiVbD8eV6nPPVnm6IXlK1tR943GHROmQE5AAUR\ntDFTZWJhc3RpYW4gQmVyZ21hbm4gPFNfQmVyZ21hbm5ATGFieXJpbnQuUmhlaW4u\nRGU+iQCVAwUQMVsrMN43GHROmQE5AQEt0AP/d801/5xYLEZBN4D7fQnlbucStufx\nynHoX8B4mpoBXUyk3KEpQQWs9wyQ/HITRkh5NapYKYKu3rs35hewKDm0kW95MR5b\nmZSKqaJYwPxy4LRtpS5ae3e/wUrdGJBfQwvgN6lVMP8RwNctbWFwyW940FLHhwHN\nlxSJCONYnzClKQ0=\n=SK+d\n-----END PGP PUBLIC KEY BLOCK-----\n\nIf you want to obtain your keyfile via electronic mail mail me first your\npgp public key.\n\n                                    @{"Main Menu" link "Main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "Install" "Installation to /X"\n.-=========================================================================-.\n|.::::::::::::::::::::::::::::] @{b}Installation@{ub} [:::::::::::::::::::::::::::::.|\n`-=========================================================================-''\n\n1) Make a dir  named: "DOORS:SCEPTIC" and copy the dir "GD-ADVERTLOF" to\n   this location.\n\n2) Copy the "EXAMINE<x>.info" to your SYSCMD/ and rename the icon for example\n   to Examine1.info as well as you have to do this rename in F!-START.info:\n   Examine1=doors:sceptic/gd-advertlog/gd-advertlog\n\n3) Copy the Dir "F!-START" + F!-Start.info to "DOORS:SCEPTIC"\n\n   If you have already installed F!-START then copy the Tooltypes from\n   this infofile to the previously installed one!\n\n4) Copy the REXXTRICKS.LIBRARY (v38.4) and the REXXSUPPORT.LIBRARY\n   to your LIBS:!\n\n.-=========================================================================-.\n|.::::::::::::::::::::::::::::] @{b}Configuration@{ub} [::::::::::::::::::::::::::::.|\n`-=========================================================================-''\n\nTooltype BBS_NAME=X\nTells the door to use X as bbsname in the bulletin.\n\nTooltype BBS_LOCATION = X\nTells the door to use X as location/group info in the bulletin.\n\n                                  @{"Main Menu" link "Main" 0}\n@ENDNODE\n\n@node "Contact" "Contact SAD"\n.-=========================================================================-.\n|.:::::::::::::::::::::::::::] @{b}How To Contact @{ub}[::::::::::::::::::::::::::::.|\n`-=========================================================================-''\n\n     @{b}Best way to reach me is my bbs Tower Of Souls (+49-2241-6238423)@{ub}\n           OnLine From 18:00 - 08:00 (Parent''s Line, you know!)\n\n   THE PUB             [WHQ]         +49-SAD      28k8/ISDN       fLI7e\n   EVIL MOON           [EHQ]         +49-SAD      28k8            FOX\n   RAVELAND            [GHQ]         +49-SAD      28k8            h2o!\n   @{b}TOWER OF SOULS      [DST]         +49-SAD      28k8/TELNET     graveDancer@{ub}\n   GOD`s HAREM         [DST]         +49-SAD      28k8/ISDN       LANCE\n   PLANET LOVE         [DST]         +49-SAD      28k8            MEPHISTO\n   TRADERS ASSAULT     [DST]         +49-SAD      28k8/ISDN       STARLIGHT\n   PARADISE LOST       [DST]         +49-SAD      28k8/ISDN       Picard\n   BUMBLE BEE LAND     [NHQ]         +47-SAD      28k8            Baffle!\n   THE TRIP            [DKHQ]        +45-SAD      33k6            JAWLOG\n   GREYHOUND           [IHQ]         +39-SAD      28k8            Gurgle\n   HIDDEN POWER        [IDIST]       +39-SAD      28k8            X/\\D\n   SILENT SERVICE      [OZHQ]       +616-SAD      28k8            Rudolf\n   FORBIDDEN PLANET    [IRLHQ]      +353-SAD      28k8            Green Beret\n\n                      !Still searching for more worldwide!\n\nsoon our hompage in http://users.aol.com will be open for you to get the\nlatest SAD releases 1 minute after release ...\n\n\n                                  @{"Main Menu" link "Main" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "members" "SAD Members"\n.-=========================================================================-.\n|.:::::::::::::::::::::::::::::] @{b}SAD Members@{ub} [:::::::::::::::::::::::::::::.|\n`-=========================================================================-''\n\n@{b}Sceptic /X Design members@{ub}\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n@{b}Fli7e             @{ub}Leader, Rexx Coder, Sysop(WHQ), @{b}Caustic Style Artist@{ub}\n@{b}GraveDancer       @{ub}Rexx Coder, @{b}Protest Artist@{ub}\n@{b}2fAST             @{ub}Rexx Coder, @{b}Contra Artist@{ub}\n@{b}H2o               @{ub}Sysop(GHQ), @{b}Contra@{ub} Artist@{ub}\n@{b}Wigwam            @{ub}Asm Coder\n@{b}Piwi              @{ub}C++ Coder\n@{b}Shadowmaster      @{ub}Arexx ^ Pascal Coder\n@{b}Bird              @{ub}Asm Coder\n@{b}Clyde Radcliffe   @{ub}Sysop(EHQ), Asm Coder\n@{b}Starlight         @{ub}Sysop(EDIST)\n@{b}Lance             @{ub}Sysop(GDIST), @{b}Pussy Posse Leader@{ub}\n@{b}X/\\D              @{ub}Sysop(IDIST), @{b}Nightfall Leader@{ub}\n@{b}Rudolf H.         @{ub}Sysop(OZDIST)\n@{b}Green Beret       @{ub}Sysop(IRL HQ)\n@{b}Mephisto          @{ub}Sysop(EGDIST), @{b}DG! Leader@{ub}\n@{b}Picard            @{ub}Sysop(GDIST)\n@{b}jAWLOG            @{ub}Sysop(DKHQ)\n@{b}Baffle!           @{ub}Sysop(NHQ)\n\n  18  Members  worldwide  and  NO ONE ELSE!  All who claim to be SAD are pure\n                 liers if they`re not listed in the one above!\n\n                                  @{"Main Menu" link "Main" 0}\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),'{"LOCATION":"X"}','auto-added',36278,8,0,NULL,NULL,'sad_al10','scan',1780048704);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('sad_ar10','SAD-AR10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/SAD-AR10.LHA',NULL,'XIM','exe.-l0S-eND0S-bBS-.exe',NULL,'!','SAD','_/ ___/_  _ /_ ___ \ SCEPTIC /X DESIGN / \_    /     /   / //- Presents in 95 /--. /_______/__/__/_____//  another AIM DOOR   |',replace('    _________________\n  _/ ___/_  _ /_ ___ \ SCEPTIC /X DESIGN\n / \_    /     /   / //- Presents in 95 /--.\n/_______/__/__/_____//  another AIM DOOR   |\n_                   Y                      |\n| Ansi Request v1.0 | Just a nice ANSI REQ |\n|        by         ! door! Just check it  |\n|   FLI7e of SAD    : out!                 |\n`-------------------'' Features REAL MSGBASE|\n|                     usage!               |\n`------------------------------------------''\n[iSDN][`] lEEChEd fRoM gOd''s hArEm [''][33.6]\n','\n',char(10)),'SAD-ARQ.doc',replace('     _________________________________  __________\n     \   __/_ ___/_ ___/_  __  /     /_/___/  ___/_\n.--- /\___  / /   /__/  /  ___/___/   /   /   /   / --------------------------.\n| A /______/_____/_____/___/    /____/___/_______/ /X Design Production 1995! |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n\n      .  .:.--¡!--------------------------------------------¡:----.\n:  : :: :::|  !: SAD-Ansi Request v1.0 by FLI7e/SAD^HJB^NJY !¡    |::: :: :  :\n      ·  ·:`--:---------------------------------------------:!----''\n                                                             :\n\n\n-  - -- ---------------------> (c)opyright notes <------------------- -- -  -\n\n                  Permission is granted to freely distribute\n                this product for non-commercial purposes only,\n                    as long as all files remain unmodified.\n\n- -- ------------------------------------------------------------------- --- --\n\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| Introduction                                                                |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n  SAD-Request is another kind of an REQUEST DOOR.  If anybody like to have an\n  old  ansi  he  could  specify everything like WHO should do it and for what\n  needs he would like to have it and so on.\n\n  This  door was mainly done for H2o/SAD and his BBS called RAVELAND!  But we\n  decided to make it public because it is just GREAT!\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| Requirements                                                                |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n  I  don`t  know If Mr.  J.  Hodge has changed the /X REXX PORT since /X $Ver\n  2.0!  But If he did so then you need at least /X 2.0+ to run this door!\n\n  Amiga  OS 2.04+ would also be very usefull because of the RexxMAST you need\n  to run this door!\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| Features                                                                    |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n  A user can request ansis and specify thinks like:\n\n  · Ansi Artist to do it\n  · The Name (IMPORTANT! 8^) ) the ansi should show\n  · For what the ansi should be used (DMS BANNER, LHA ADD, BBS INTERNAL etc.)\n  · The Style (PLAIN, COLORED, PERFECT, PERFECT / COLOR)\n  · The MAX. hight and widht of the Ansi\n\n  This  datas  will  be send as an MESSAGE to the MESSAGEBASE of an specified\n  conference  directly to the ANSI ARTIST or his representative if the artist\n  is NOT online!\n\n  At the moment the only way to give the finished ansi to the REQUESTER is to\n  write  a  msg  and  attach  the  file to it, but in the future versions the\n  finished ansis can be uploaded to the door directly to the REQUESTER!\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| Installation                                                                |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n  Copy the Dir "BBS/DOORS/SCEPTIC/F!-AnsiRequest" to your "DOORS:"\n\n  Copy  the given BBSCMD to your "BBSCMD" location or wherever you store your\n  BBS COMMANDS!\n\n  Now  load  the  config  file  and  edit  it to your needs:  Here`s a closer\n  information:\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCONFPATH	= "confs:asski/MSGBASE"\n                · Full path to the Conference where to store the ANSIREQUEST\n                  Messages\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAMOUNT		= 2\n                · How many ARTISTS to be able to request ansis on!\n                  -/-> MAX. 10 <-\-\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNAME		= "h2o"\n                · First name to be displayed in the MENU\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNAME		= "flI7e"\n                · Second name to be displayed in the MENU\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNAME		= "flI7e"\n                · ...\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUSERNAME	= "h2o"\n                · the 1st REAL USERNAME of the artists or his representative!\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUSERNAME	= "FLI7e"\n                · the 2nd REAL USERNAME of the artists or his representative!\n\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUSERNAME	= "FLI7e"\n                · ...\n\n\nFor a FULL configfile with 10 Artists it should look like this\n\n		CONFPATH	= "..."\n		AMOUNT		= 10\n		NAME		= "001"\n		NAME		= "002"\n		NAME		= "003"\n		NAME		= "004"\n		NAME		= "005"\n		NAME		= "006"\n		NAME		= "007"\n		NAME		= "008"\n		NAME		= "009"\n		NAME		= "010"\n		USERNAME	= "001"\n		USERNAME	= "002"\n		USERNAME	= "003"\n		USERNAME	= "004"\n		USERNAME	= "005"\n		USERNAME	= "006"\n		USERNAME	= "007"\n		USERNAME	= "008"\n		USERNAME	= "009"\n		USERNAME	= "010"\n\n\nCan`t be easier i think?!\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| Contact S/\D                                                                |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n  The Pub            (WHQ.  ) +49(0)5551-65139 - 1ND 28k8 (FLITE)\n  Silent Service     (OZ. HQ) +616   955 5119  - 1ND 28k8 (RUDOLF H.)\n  Forbidden Planet   (IRL-HQ) +353-1-820 8489  - 2ND 33k6 (Green-BERET)\n\n                     Or any BBS where your find FLI7e on!\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| History                                                                     |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n                  v1.0	-	First public release\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| Greetings                                                                   |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\nAquarius/Outlaws ................ -»> Still in Outlaws? Why don`t you come\n                                      over here!?\n\nFOX/AG!^REMEDY .................. -»> Hi Vince! Hope this one is running clean\n                                      and bugfree! Test it!\n\nSTC/TASK ........................ -»> Where are the NEW doors? Are you dead\n                                      or just sleeping?\n\nTHE PROPHET/NJY ................. -»> Hmmm! Same as above!\n\nPIWI GON/SAD .................... -»> Your /X CFG ED looks great! Letus work\n                                      fast to release it! MUI ROOLZ!\n\nCOUGAR/HOODLUM .................. -»> Lousiest BETA TESTER ever! Why don`t you\n                                      install the updates i pump to your system\n                                      so often?\n\nHITPOWER/PRODIGY ................ -»> Erm, Modem damaged? Or quitted scene? Why\n                                      don`t ya call?\n\nCASIO/SAD ....................... -»> Hey my dear ITALIAN ONE MEN DIVISION! How\n                                      are you?\n\n       and all slaved SYSOPS and /X-DOOR CODER worldwide! Keep /X going!\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| Greetings & Messages                                                        |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\nAquarius/Outlaws ................ -»> Still in Outlaws? Why don`t you come\n                                      over here!?\n\nFOX/AG!^REMEDY .................. -»> Hi Vince! Hope this one is running clean\n                                      and bugfree! Test it!\n\nSTC/TASK ........................ -»> Where are the NEW doors? Are you dead\n                                      or just sleeping?\n\nTHE PROPHET/NJY ................. -»> Hmmm! Same as above!\n\nPIWI GON/SAD .................... -»> You`r /X CFG ED looks great! Letus work\n                                      fast to release it! MUI ROOLZ!\n\nCOUGAR/HOODLUM .................. -»> Lousiest BETA TESTER ever! Why don`t you\n                                      install the updates i pump to your system\n                                      so often?\n\nHITPOWER/PRODIGY ................ -»> Erm, Modem damaged? Or quitted scene? Why\n                                      don`t ya call?\n\nCASIO/SAD ....................... -»> Hey my dear ITALIAN ONE MEN DIVISION! How\n                                      are you?\n\n       and all slaved SYSOPS and /X-DOOR CODER worldwide! Keep /X going!\n\n\n\nNO CARRIER\n\n+++ATH\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| ABOUT SAD                                                                   |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n\n    We in SAD are searching some good /X-Door and Tool coder (AIM, XIM etc.)\n\n        If you`re searching a NICE and "WANT-TO-BE-ACTIVE" group then we\n                       might be the right choice for YOU!\n\n      You`ve NOT to leave your actual Group, you can join us just for /X!\n\n       So if you`re a C, E, ASM, AREXX coder or an ANSI artist or a SYSOP\n     who like to open a DST SITE (BETA SITE) then just get in contact with\n\n                                     FLI7e\n\n                         EMail: [email removed]\n\n                                       or\n\n                           The Pub: +49(0)5551-65139\n\n\n                         Some closer Information on SAD\n                        +------------------------------+\n\n\n\n    SCEPTIC itself was founded in the early month of 1992! We released some\n             demos, intros, trainers, patches and ansi collections.\n\n      Our most famous production was CHIPMANIA (soon be released under the\n                 HAUJOBB label because I (fli7e) joined them!)\n\n      Then .. In summer 1994 I kicked all inactive members and decided to\n     change the way we go! DEMO-GROUP .. R.I.P .. /X + Toolgroup .. ALIVE!\n\n   From there on we worked a long time in the underground .. NO RELEASES ..!\n\n   But that should change NOW! With your help a famous group could be REBORN!\n\n                                Actual "MEMBERS"\n\n            FLi7e/HAUJOBB ^ N-JOY ^ SAD    (Leader, /X CODER, SYSOP)\n            H2o/SAD                                   (AZZKY LAYOUT)\n            PIWI/SAD                                      (/X CODER)\n            SLY/SAD                              (TRADER & /X CODER)\n            CASIO/SAD                                (ITALIAN CODER)\n            WIGWAM/SAD                                       (CODER)\n            SHADOWMASTER/IFT^SAD                          (/X CODER)\n            COUGAR/HOODLUM                             (BETA TESTER)\n            GREEN BERET                                  (IRL SYSOP)\n            RUDOLF H.                                    (OZ. SYSOP)\n\n  Well, not that much I think! And because of that we`ll try to strike again!\n\n                         ·W·I·T·H· ·Y·O·U·R· ·H·E·L·P·\n\n\n                             !KEEP THE CULT GOING!\n\n\n                               Fast greetings to\n\n            ZULU&GREY/REBELS, AEROSOUL/Ex. Shoot, ALL NJYs, ALL HJBs\n             FOX/AG!^RDY, STC/TASK, FASHION/STB, TOUCHSTONE/ESSENCE\n\n                    And all those bleeding noses out there!\n\n\n                 FUCK da Rotten Skunks called themselves NAZIS!\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| OUR PRODUCTIONS                                                             |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n\nAlready Released SAD Doors\n--------------------------\n\nBulletins           (AIM) -»> Great Bulletins Door with nice features\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRequest             (AIM) -»> A Request door with MSG BASE MAIL SEND\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWall                (AIM) -»> Two Walls in one! You can use PWs to switch\n                              between the PUBLIC and the "ELITE" wall!\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSecurity            (AIM) -»> Protect Special Conferences of Lamers!\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDLD                 (AIM) -»> Download Filedirs\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHelp                (AIM) -»> Multi Language Online Help for /X\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDoorsMenu           (AIM) -»> Displays Different DOORS menus depending on\n                              Users-access.\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCommentToSysop      (AIM) -»> As the Name states ... Another FINE Comment\n                              door!\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFrontend            (AIM) -»> Including: LASTCALLERS, WHO, PW, PWMENU, COOKIE!\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nStatus              (XIM) -»> Smashing FAST and sysop & user configurable\n                              status door!\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLogOff Deluxe       (AIM) -»> Logoff Door with BBS ADD option, LAST CALLER MSG\n                              with REPLY option\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAnsi Request        (AIM) -»> GREAT Ansi Request door! Nice features!\n\nand some other small ones!\n\n\nSoon to come SAD Doors/Tools\n----------------------------\n\n· /X Config Ed with MUI application and lotsa great features to easy\n  config ALL the /X 3.x+ Info files! The Tool comes with ALL available\n  /X INTERNAL Tooltypes for maximum configuration Power! Any tooltype\n  available on one Mousclick for any Standard and ANY Self Configured\n  BBS CMD and that stuff!\n\n  (XIM)\n\n· Keyboard Controlled MENU door! No more typing! Choose your command\n  by moving a BAR around! User-Chooseable if MENU or PROMPT mode!\n\n  (AIM or XIM)\n\n· GREAT Operator Pager with integrated LINECHAT (the first for /X ever!!\n  like in FastCall!), WB GUI with lotsa features .. A Must for SYSOPS ..\n\n  (AIM)\n\n· Ansi Request with incredible, never seen features! You can specify the\n  STYLE, the Width, the hight, colors, perfect style etc....\n\n  (AIM)\n\n· DoorChecker! Will check all BBSCMDs and SYSCMDs if the needed door is\n  still installed. DeInstall option for sure!\n\n  (AIM or XIM)\n\nand some more Ideas still in mind!\n\nIf you have any Idea .. just tell us!\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',13643,5,0,NULL,NULL,'sad_ar10','scan',1780048704);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('sad_ar20','SAD^AR20.LZX','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/SAD^AR20.LZX',NULL,'XIM','popel.exe',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'auto-added',16226,0,0,NULL,NULL,'sad_ar20','scan',1780048714);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('sad_bu11','SAD-BU11.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/SAD-BU11.LHA',NULL,'XIM','_________________',NULL,'Fli7e','SAD','_/ ___/_  _ /_ ___ \ SCEPTIC /X DESIGN / \_    /     /   / //- Presents in 95 /--. /_______/__/__/_____//  another AIM DOOR   |',replace('    _________________\n  _/ ___/_  _ /_ ___ \ SCEPTIC /X DESIGN\n / \_    /     /   / //- Presents in 95 /--.\n/_______/__/__/_____//  another AIM DOOR   |\n_                                          |\n|       SAD BULLETINS v1.1 by Fli7e        |\n|                                          |\n| A great BULLETINS replacement with nice  |\n|           output and handling            |\n|                                          |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'f!-bullsBULL.doc',replace('     _________________________________  __________\n     \   __/_ ___/_ ___/_  __  /     /_/___/  ___/_\n.--- /\___  / /   /__/  /  ___/___/   /   /   /   / --------------------------.\n| A /______/_____/_____/___/    /____/___/_______/ /X Design Production 1995! |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n\n      .  .:.--¡!---------------------------------------¡:----.              .\n:  : :: :::|  !: SAD-Bullets v1.1 by FLI7e/SAD^HJB^NJY !¡    |::: :: :  :   :\n      ·  ·:`--:----------------------------------------:!----''              ·\n                                                        :\n\n\n-  - -- ---------------------> (c)opyright notes <------------------- -- -  -\n\n                  Permission is granted to freely distribute\n                this product for non-commercial purposes only,\n                    as long as all files remain unmodified.\n\n- -- ------------------------------------------------------------------- --- --\n\n\n\n           AS THIS IS AN UPDATE READ -FEATURES- and HISTORY for news!\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| Introduction                                                                |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n  SAD-Bullets is a ~60 minutes AREXX coded /X door which, as the name states,\n  is  a  >>> Bulletin <<<  door.  You can choose a bull by keys.   That means\n  you can specify the keys with which the USER can scroll up/down a marker to\n  choose.\n\n  See FEATURES for the two or three features it has included!\n\n\n\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| Requirements                                                                |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n  I  don`t  know If Mr.  J.  Hodge has changed the /X REXX PORT since /X $Ver\n  2.0!  But If he did so then you need at least /X 2.0+ to run this door!\n\n  Amiga  OS 2.04+ would also be very usefull because of the RexxMAST you need\n  to run this door!\n\n\n\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| Features                                                                    |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n  Well,  as  stated  in  the Introduction SAD-COMMENTL did NOT offer any PLAY\n  AROUND options!  There are just TWO options:\n\n\n                                      -1-\n\n             Randomly chooseable header ansi (as much as you want!)\n\n\n\n                                      -2-\n\n  You can use keys to SCROLL around.  If I`ll get some informations on HOW to\n  do CURSOR KEY USING through AREXX then`ill include that for sure!\n\n  Thats`s all I think! If anybody will install this Door then please consider\n  contacting  me!  Not  for paying anything but as a notice for me that I did\n  well!\n\n\n\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| Installation                                                                |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n  1st step is to copy "BBS/DOORS/SCEPTIC/F!-Bulletins" to your "DOORS:"\n\n  2nd step  should  be to copy the given BBSCMD to your "BBSCMD" location or\n      wherever you store your BBS COMMANDS!\n\n  3rd step  (if  you  like  to)  is  to load the CONFIG-FILE and edit it to\n      your needs.\n\n\n             Maybe you can vary the steps? Just like a shuffle ...\n\n\n\n  YOU  CAN  HAVE  A MAXIMUM of 999 Bulletins in this VERSION!  But remember\n  that I don`t handle the MAXIMUM SCREEN HIGH of a users settings!  So try to\n  not use >10 or 15 Bulletins! But I think this should be more than enuff!\n\n\n\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| Contact the Author(s)                                                       |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n       To get in contact with FLI7E (Hi, that`s me) for any reason call:\n\n                                --- The Pub ---\n\n                               +49(0)5551-65139\n                                28k8 v34. vfast\n                                  A4000/33MHz\n                                   1.2GB HD\n\n                                  Sysop: ME!\n\n\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| History                                                                     |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n                  v0.5	-	First BBS-INTERNAL release\n -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n                  v0.8	-	Added Scroll up/down function\n -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n                  v1.0	-	First public release\n -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n                  v1.1  -	Second public release\n\n                                · Optimized the BAR SCROLLING!\n				· Removed a little Cursor OFF Bug which\n				  only appeared on the USER side!\n				· Optimized the CODE itself\n\n\n\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| Greetings                                                                   |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n     Aquarius/Outlaws /÷/ FOX/AG!^REMEDY \÷\ STC/TASK /÷/ THE PROPHET/NJY\n        PIWI/SAD \÷\ COUGAR/HOODLUM /÷/ HITPOWER/PRODIGY \÷\ CASIO/SAD\n\n       and all slaved SYSOPS and /X-DOOR CODER worldwide! Keep /X going!\n\n\n\nNO CARRIER\n\n+++ATH\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,8337,4,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048704);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('sad_bu12','SAD-BU12.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/SAD-BU12.LHA',NULL,'XIM','_________________',NULL,'Fli7e','SAD','_/ ___/_  _ /_ ___ \ SCEPTIC /X DESIGN / \_    /     /   / //- Presents in 95 /--. /_______/__/__/_____//  another AIM DOOR   |',replace('    _________________\n  _/ ___/_  _ /_ ___ \ SCEPTIC /X DESIGN\n / \_    /     /   / //- Presents in 95 /--.\n/_______/__/__/_____//  another AIM DOOR   |\n_                                          |\n|       SAD BULLETINS v1.2 by Fli7e        |\n|                                          |\n| A great BULLETINS replacement with nice  |\n| output and handling! Now just 1957bytes  |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'reference-board.txt',replace(replace('              W h e r e   t h e   w a r e z   c o m e   f r o m\r\n                                               __                /\_____:\r\n__/\__________________________________________|  \______________/  \    |__\r\n\_   ___________  _______ ________  \__   ___ |   _______  _______  \_  l  \\r\n__\____  \    _l   \    |  \     |___/     |  !    \   _l   \   _| __/\____ \_\r\n\_____    \___\     \___|   \___ !   \__   |_____   \__\     \__\    \____   /\r\n -mNT\_____/---\_____/--l____/-\______/\   |----\____/--\_____/--\____/--\__/\r\n                                        \__|\r\n\r\n- -- --> F A i R L i G H T   S W E D i S H   H E A D Q U A R T E R S <-- -- -\r\n\r\n           reference-board is back 2017 after more than 20 years in coma!\r\n\r\n                        Running on AmiExpress TelNet\r\n\r\n                    Connect to: reference-board.zapto.org:1541\r\n\r\n                    or: www.brysk.se/reference-board/index.htm\r\n               \n              UPLOAD DATE: 01-04-18  TIME: 20:05:11  ON NODE: 0\n','\r',char(13)),'\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,3887,2,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048704);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('sad_bu15','SAD-BU15.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/SAD-BU15.LHA',NULL,'XIM','popel.exe',NULL,NULL,'SAD','_\__:                                      : \  /:dOORNAME: bULLETINS v2.1              : \/ :  aUTHOR: fLI7e/sAD                   :',replace(' __,.-==========================- -=======-.\n_\__:                                      :\n\  /:dOORNAME: bULLETINS v2.1              :\n \/ :  aUTHOR: fLI7e/sAD                   :\n __ :fEATURES:-lIGHTBAR cHOOSING           :\n___|:         -nICE oUTPUT                 :\n\__l:         -eXECUTE sCRIPTS fOR oNLINE  :\n    :          uPDATING(s) added!          :\n___|·                                    __:\n\__|·                                    \/:\n-==-·-===========[sCEPTIC /X dESIGN |995]=-''\n[iSDN][°] lEEChEd fRoM gOd''s hArEm [°][33.6]\n[fOUND oN dA pROGRESS gHQ]-[dREAM pARK bBS!]\n','\n',char(10)),'BULL.doc',replace('\n             .----------------------------------------------------------------.\n             ¡ iT`s aNOTHER                                 ______            ¡\n_ ___________!_________ ___________ ____________ ___________\____/_ ________  |\n        ____/_    ____/____  ___  /___     __  /_______   _/_     /    ____/__|\n _ ___       /            /  \___/   /  ______/    |        /    /            |\n_ __________/____________/__________/ ____|        l_______/____/__________ _ |\n             !                                                                |\n             ! .                                         /X DESIGN Production !\n             : .                                         ·                    :\n      .  .:.--¡!-----------------------------------------¡:---.             . ·\n:  : :: :::|  !: SAD-Bulletins v1.5 by FLI7e/SAD^HJB^NJY !¡   |::: :: :  :  : :\n      ·  ·:`--:------------------------------------------:!---''             · ¡\n             !                                            :                   !\n             `----------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n\n\n===============================================================================\n                                (c)opyright notes\n===============================================================================\n\n                  Permission is granted to freely distribute\n                this product for non-commercial purposes only,\n                    as long as all files remain unmodified.\n\n     It`s not allowed to make any kind of PROFIT with this programm without\n           having a WRITTEN permission signed by the AUTHOR himself!\n\n                All © and Written 1995 Sceptic Amiexpress Design\n\n===============================================================================\n\n\n\n\n\n===============================================================================\n                                 Introduction\n===============================================================================\n\n  SAD-Bullets  is  an /X AREXX door which is just a NICE -B- replacement!  No\n  need  of  ONLINE updating and that crappy things!  I don`t know ANY ONE who\n  really use such a feature!\n\n  Now  it`s  SMALLER than 3k!  I think this is a SMASHING length if you think\n  of it`s features!  BarScrolling (FAKE CURSOR KEYS!) and Random Ansi Display\n  Option!\n\n  Now I optimized the bar scroll! The OLD position will now be remembered and\n  the bar will be placed on the last selected item after you viewed a bullet!\n\n\n\n\n\n===============================================================================\n                                 Requirements\n===============================================================================\n\n  I  don`t  know If Mr.  J.  Hodge has changed the /X REXX PORT since /X $Ver\n  2.0!  But If he did so then you need at least /X 2.0+ to run this door!\n\n  Amiga  OS 2.04+ would also be very usefull because of the RexxMAST you need\n  to run this door!\n\n\n\n\n\n===============================================================================\n                                 Installation\n===============================================================================\n\n    Copy all files from DOORS and COMMANDS to their matching places on your\n                          BBS: and load the cfg file.\n\n\n\n.x represents a number from 1-bulletins\n\nBulletins	= Number of bulletins\nScript.x	= Script to be executed! The result (file.1) will be shown\n                  after the script.1 has been executed! If the script is\n                  not found only the file will be shown!\n\n                  Scripts may be usefull to update WEEKTOPS or whatever\n                  online right before viewing them.\n\nFile.x		= "FILENAME of BULLETIN #1"\nBull.x		= "NAME OF THE BULLETIN ( for the SELECT MENU!)"\n\n\nHEADER		= Default Header Bodyname\n                  e.g. .../F!-Bulls/BULL.ansi\n\nRandom		= 0=No / 1=YES\nDefaultHeader	= DEFAULT ANSI NUMBER\n                  e.g. -1- will show .../F!-Bulls/BULL.ansi1\n\nFirstHeader	= Random FIRST NUMBER\nLastHeader	= Random LAST Number\n\n\n  YOU CAN HAVE A MAXIMUM of 999 Bulletins in this VERSION!  But remember that\n  I  don`t handle the MAXIMUM SCREEN HIGH of a users settings!  So try to not\n  use >10 or 15 Bulletins!  But I think this should be more than enuff!\n\n\n\n\n\n===============================================================================\n                                  Contact SAD\n===============================================================================\n                                                  __\n                                                 /\_\\n           -  - -- --- ---------------------.----\/_/---- --- -- -  -   -\n  __________       ________                 | __________   _____________\n  \         \_____/       /_________        !_\_  ___  /__/       / ___/_____\n   \____      /  /       / ____    /       /        / /  /       /  \__     /\n     /       /          /  \______/__     /        __/  /       /     /    /\n     \______/__/       /____________/F!   \________/ \_________/\_________/\n-  -= -=-==-==/_______/==-==-=- =-  -   -   ¡\n                                            !\n                            SAD WHQ - +49-5551-65139\n                                            :\n                                  SYSOP: fLI7e\n                                            |\n                                            |     _  _ __ ______ _\n                                            |     \ \\\\ \\   __\n           _ __ __ __ _                     |      \ \\\\_\\  /___ __ _  _\n   .-----------\\//-------------------------''               \//__//_//// /\n   |            \/\n   |________   ______ ___________         _______   ______   ______   ______\n  _!\ _____/__/     /_\____/    /___    __\ _ _  \__\_    \__\_    \__\___  \\n /   _/   /  /     /      /    /   /   /    / /  /   /    /   /    /     /  /\n/        /  /     /      /        /   /    / /  /   /    /   /    /     /  /\n\_______/\_______/\_____/\_______/    \___/_/__/\_______/\_______/\____/__/\n  _|_\n _\|_                       SAD EHQ - +49-3322-208768\n   \/\n   |                         SYSOP: cLYDE rADCLIFFE\n   |         __\n   `---------\/-----.----------------------------------------- --- -- -  -\n                    |\n                    |     _______ ____ __ ______ __ ____ _______\n                    |    /______//___//_//______\\_\\___\\______\\n                    |    \______\\___\\_\\______//_//___//______/\n     ________    ___!__     ____          _____     ______   ______   _____\n    _\_____ /____\__   \___/    \________/    /_____\__   \__\___  \__\___ \\n   /   __/    / ___    /  /     / ___   /    /   / ___    /     /  /     / /\n  /    \     /  \     /  /     /  \____/__      /  \     /     /  /       /\n  \_____\___/________/\_______/__________/_____/________/_____/__/_______/\n                    ¡\n                    |\n       - -- --------÷--> SAD GHQ - +49-7128-3511\n                    |\n                    |     SYSOP: H2o!\n                    |                 __\n                    |                _\/_\n                    `----.------------\/---------- --- -- -\n                         |\n       ________    ______!_____    ________  ________________\n    ___\    __/____\____/     /____\  ____/__\____   \       \__ ___\n    \   \___    /      /     /   /  __/    /     /   /\____    //  /__\n     \     /   /      /         /         /     /   /   /     //  // /_\n      \_______/\_____/\________/\________/_____/___/    \____//__//_///\n          ________   ____|___  ________      ____   ______ ________  ________\n   ___ ___\    __/___\  ____/__\_____ /_____/    \__\____/_\  ____/__\  ____/_\n __\  \\   \___    /  __/    /   __/    /  /     /      /     /    /  __/    /\n_\ \\  \\     /   /         /    \     /  /     /      /          /         /\n\\\_\\__\\_______/\________/\_____\___/\_______/\_____/\_________/\________/\n                         |\n                         |\n                         |  SAD OZHQ - +616-955-5119\n                         |   SYSOP: RUDOLF H.\n                         |\n- -- --- ----------------÷------------------------------------------- -- -\n                         |\n   ________ _____  ______!  _____    _____ ______   ______   ______   ______\n  _\  ____/_\__ /__\___ _/_/  __/____\___/_\___ /___\___ /___\ ___/___\___ /_\n /  ____/     /  /   _/   /   \__  /    /     /  /     /  /   _/   /     /  /\n/     //        /    \   /      / /    /     /  /     /  /        /     /  /\n\____/ \_______/\_____\__\_______/\___/\_______/\_______/\_______/\____/__/\n                    _____!________     _______  ________  ________________\n _______ _   ___ ___\_  ___  \   /_____\___   \_\____  /__\  ____/_       \__\n \   __ _  __\  \\      \____/  /   / ____    /     /   /  __/    /_____    /\n  \  /    _\ \\  \\      //        /  \      /     /   /         /  /      /\n   \/     \\\_\\__\\____/|\_______/\________/\____/___/\________/   \_____/\n                         |\n                         |\n                         |   SAD IRL HQ - +353-1-820 8489\n                         |      SYSOP: GREEN BERET\n                         |\n                         `-----------------÷----------------- --- -- -  -\n                                           |\n      ______  ______  ______  ____    ____ |  _____   ____    ______  ______\n   _ _\ ___/__\__  /__\ ___/_/   /___/   /_!__\_   \_/   /____\___  \_\___ /_\n        \_  / __/   /  _/   /__ /   /   /   /  /    /   /   /    /  /    /  /\n        /  /  \    /       /       /       /  /    /   /   /    /  /    /  /\n   __ ____/____\  /_______/_______/___/   /_______/_______/____/__/_______/\n               _\/_                  /___/ !\n             __\\//__\n             \ \\// /      SAD IHQ - +39-473-244-839\n              \ \/ /             SYSOP: GURGLE\n               \  /\n                \/                         ¡\n                                           !\n                                           :\n                                           .\n\n                                           .\n\n\n\n\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| History                                                                     |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n                  v0.5	-	First BBS-INTERNAL release\n -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n                  v0.8	-	Added Scroll up/down function\n -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n                  v1.0	-	First public release\n -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n                  v1.1  -	Second public release\n\n                                · Optimized the BAR SCROLLING!\n				· Removed a little Cursor OFF Bug which\n				  only appeared on the USER side!\n				· Optimized the CODE itself\n -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n                  v1.2  -	Third public release\n\n                                · Optimized Code: Gained 1547 bytes\n                                · Now about 20% faster!\n\n -----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n                  v1.5  -	Fourth public release\n\n                                · Enhanced the chooser\n                                · Nice new outfit!\n                                · aDDED uSING of Scripts for\n                                  online updating!\n\n\n\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| Greetings                                                                   |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n     Aquarius/Outlaws /÷/ FOX/AG!^REMEDY \÷\ STC/TASK /÷/ THE PROPHET/NJY\n        PIWI/SAD \÷\ COUGAR/HOODLUM /÷/ HITPOWER/PRODIGY \÷\ CASIO/SAD\n\n       and all slaved SYSOPS and /X-DOOR CODER worldwide! Keep /X going!\n\n\n\nNO CARRIER\n\n+++ATH\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',31474,9,0,NULL,NULL,'sad_bu15','scan',1780048704);
