 - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n- ADDLINE	= "[THE]=--=] cS!-^-sAD-^-hJB-^-KLF! [=--=[PUB]"\n\n  ø FILE ID line .. max 44 chars wide! (possible esc codes excluded!)\n  - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n- EALLUSER	= 3\n\n  ø NUMBER of users allowed to add an ADDITIONAL comment to the FREE DL eall!\n  - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n- EUSER		= "Fli7e"\n  EUSER		= "h2o"\n  EUSER		= "zaphod"\n\n  ø ALL USERNAMES allowed to add add. comments (3 in this example)\n  - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n- F4FCOMMAND	= "free"\n\n  ø COMMAND name of the "noc coupon" kinda door (free dl setter with\n    wilrdcards from the BBS mainline(build in the mainfile))\n  - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n- F4FUSER	= 3\n\n  ø NUMBER of users allowed to use the MAINLINE FREE DL (fuck 4 free)\n  - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n- FUSER		= "Fli7e"\n  FUSER		= "h2o"\n  FUSER		= "zaphod"\n\n  ø ALL USERNAMES allowed to use the FUCK FOR FREE (3 in this example)\n  - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n- PFXNUM	= 5\n\n  ø Number of prefixes to check for FREE DOWNLOAD on ...\n  - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -\n- PFX		= SAD\n  PFX		= HJB\n  PFX		= C!\n  PFX		= CS!\n  PFX		= KLF\n\n  ø ALL the prefixes matching files should be set to FREE DL ...\n    (5 in this example)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  Now commin` up the FREE DL MESSAGE LINE configfiles set for EACH prefix!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                           FREELINES/xxx (xxx=Prefix)\n                           ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n  Line1	  = # of following Free DL Lines\n  Line2-x = Free DL Line\n\n  IE:\n      3\n      >>>>> iT`s fOR fREE sO lEECH iT dUDEZ! <<<<<\n      >>>>>   i wANNA sEE yOU lEECH dUDEZ!   <<<<<\n      >>>>>   iT`s fREE bECAUSE iT`s !SAD!   <<<<<\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  Every file represents one of the given FREE DOWNLOAD PREFIXES given in the\n  CONFIG FILE ... Every file can store unlimited DIFFERENT FREE DOWNLOAD\n  lines from which you can choose ONE if a FREE DOWNLOAD for THIS PREFIX has\n  been recogniced by the door ... Just put the AMOUNT of LINES in the first\n  line of the file(s) and you`re finished ...\n\n  REMEMBER: Don`t use lines longer than 44 chars! If you use ESC CODES the\n            choose menu of FIDE 3.o will scramble up the layout! So beware\n            of it! This feature will be added in the NEXT version!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                               __________________\n                           _ __\_              _/__ _\n\n                                   cONTACT sAD\n                               _ ___        ___ _\n                                   \________/\n                       _ __ ___ ____ _    _ ____ ___ __ _\n                       \\\_\\__\\___\\\  ///___//__//_///\n                                      \\//\n                                       \/\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n    THE PUB             [WHQ]         +49-5551-911-SAD      28k8      fLI7e\n    EVIL MOON           [EHQ]         +49-3322-728-SAD      28k8      FOX\n    RAVELAND            [GHQ]         +49-7128-177-SAD      28k8      h2o!\n    SILENT MOON         [OZHQ]       +616-9555-119-SAD      28k8      Rudolf\n    FORBIDDEN PLANET    [IRLHQ]      +353-8208-489-SAD      28k8      Green Beret\n    GREYHOUND           [IHQ]         +39-4732-448-SAD      28k8      Gurgle\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                               __________________\n                           _ __\_              _/__ _\n\n                                     hISTORY\n                               _ ___        ___ _\n                                   \________/\n                       _ __ ___ ____ _    _ ____ ___ __ _\n                       \\\_\\__\\___\\\  ///___//__//_///\n                                      \\//\n                                       \/\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                          v1.o - ø fIRST pUBLIC rELEASE\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                          v2.o - ø tOTALY nEW cODED aND\n                                 · Added my OWN TXT ID ADDER\n                                   because TXTEXTRACT is full\n                                   of BUGS!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                          v3.o - ø Recoded 80%\n                                 · Fastened some routines\n                                 · Added RDZ Corrector\n                                 · Added ID Adverter\n                                 · Changed Layout\n                                 · FUCK 4 FREE is now\n                                   build in!\n                                 · Added LZX Type\n\n                                 · Ordered an ASM Version\n                                   of MY TXTADDER from\n                                   AVALON/SAD to speed up\n                                   TXT handling in the next\n                                   Version.\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                               __________________\n                           _ __\_              _/__ _\n\n                                    gREETINGS\n                               _ ___        ___ _\n                                   \________/\n                       _ __ ___ ____ _    _ ____ ___ __ _\n                       \\\_\\__\\___\\\  ///___//__//_///\n                                      \\//\n                                       \/\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                        aLL cAUSTIC sTYLE mEMBAz wORLDWIDE\n                           aLL hAUJOBB mEMBAz wORLDWIDe\n                            tHE eSSENTIAL eSSENCE cREW\n                                mY pC mATES iN kLF\n\n           All Manga Anime Fans (over 300 Videos orderable at THE PUB)\n\n mOGUE/Arclite                                                    (hijo nase!)\n Control/TRSI                                    (jaja, deine logos mach ich!)\n GrindCrusher/TRSI                                        (keep on your cd`s!)\n Mario/TRSI                                                          (wassup?)\n Capt.Crunch/TRSI                                                (was geht ..)\n Aquarius/Outlaws                                            (Still alive!???)\n Siegel/TRSI                            (Na das ARTORDER DOOR ueben wir noch!)\n BYTEANDI/TRSI                                         (Coolest FILE ID ever!)\n SVEN THE CREATOR/5D!                        (Sieht aus als ob du nachlaesst!)\n The Jailed Cougar Force                                  (keep on the drugs!)\n Treach/Contra                                     (Geiler Style mannnnnnnnn!)\n Starlight/Caustic Style                           (Welcome to uns my freund!)\n\n       And all who deserve and not mentioned ones! (what a lousy sentence!)\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                                   .\n                                ·.:.·\n                                .:··.             .   .\n                               ::               ·..:.·\n                             .:·     .......     .·::\n                             ::   .:··     ··:.     ·:\n                             :: .:      __    ·:.    ::\n                              :::     _ °° _    :. .::\n                               ::     `-^--''    ::::·\n                               ::               ::\n                                ·:.            .:·\n                                  :::........:··\n                                .::·  ·····::.\n                              . ·:.         ::    .\n                             :::..::        ·::..::: xCz\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  ................................                  ..............\n  :                              :                  :            :\n  :                              :                  :            :\n  :                              :                  :............:...........\n__:____                   ______ :    ____________._      _______:          :\n\   __/________ ______   / __  /_:___/  ___   ____|_______\_____/_  ______  :\n \______       / ____/__/_ \__/      \_ \_____\__      /           / ____/__:_\n..: \_________/  \        \___________/__:___|  |     /__________ /  \      : \_\n:            /_____________/(rLf):              |       |     -T!/__________:__/\n:                 ......         :              l_______|                   :\n:....             :    :.....    :                                  ........:\n:...:     ........:         :    :....                              :\n          :...:             :....:   :                              :\n              :                  :...:............                  :\n              :                                  :                  :\n                ........................         :        .....     :\n                :                      :         :........:   :.....:\n            a.M.I.E.X.P.R.E.S.s        :                  :...:\n                :                      :\n                :               d.E.S.I:G.n\n                :......................:\n\n\n\n\n\n          pLAN  : .. wE`LL rOOL tHE dOORsCENE fROM bEHIND tO tHE tOP!\n          rESULT: ................. wE mANAGED tO hIT tHE tOP 10 nOW!\n          fUTURE: ......................... wE`LL hIT 1ST pLACE sOON!\n\n\n\n\n\n                   ... tHE sTRONG oNEZ wILL sURF aND wIFE ...\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,28786,2,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048711);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('sad_fe10','SAD-FE10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/SAD-FE10.LHA',NULL,'XIM','MyCookie.exe',NULL,'Fli7e','SAD','_/ ___/_  _ /_ ___ \ SCEPTIC /X DESIGN / \_    /     /   / //- Presents in 95 /--. /_______/__/__/_____//  another AIM DOOR   |',replace('    _________________\n  _/ ___/_  _ /_ ___ \ SCEPTIC /X DESIGN\n / \_    /     /   / //- Presents in 95 /--.\n/_______/__/__/_____//  another AIM DOOR   |\n_                                          |\n|        SAD FRONTEND v1.0 by Fli7e        |\n|                                          |\n| MOST POWERFULL FRONTEND featuring: WHO,  |\n|        LASTCALLERS, PW and COOKIE        |\n|                                          |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'MyFrontEnd.cfg.doc',replace('\n                   ....... SAD-FRONT v1.0 by FLITE/SAD ......\n                   :             _                 _        :\n              ___, :____  ____ _|__.  _____      _|__. |    :_____\n             (_____(____)(    ) |  l_(____(  ---  |  l_l____(____/_\n                   :            |    ______)      |         :\n                   :........................................:\n\n/******************************************************************************/\n/* What you wanna use in your LOGIN                                           */\n/*                                                                            */\n/* 0=Disabled ÷ 1=Enabled                                                     */\n/******************************************************************************/\n\nUsePW           =0\nUsePWMENU	=0\nUseWHO          =1\nUseCookie       =1\nUseLastCaller   =1\n\n/******************************************************************************/\n/* SYSTEM PASSWORD                                                            */\n/******************************************************************************/\n\nPW              =The PW\nPrompt          =The prompt in front of the PW\nPWOK            =message to be sent if PW is OK\nPWWRONG         =message to be sent if PW is WRONG\nMSGTOSYSOPTXT   =file which`ll be shown if user failed 3 times and USEPWMENU\n                 is specified! This text will be shown if the HACKER will write\n                 a MSG to the sysop!\n\n/******************************************************************************/\n/* WHO                                                                        */\n/******************************************************************************/\n\nWhoDefaultBaud  =Default Baud amount\nWhoDefaultUser  =Default Username\nWhoDefaultLoca  =Default User Location\n\n/******************************************************************************/\n/* LASTCALLERS                                                                */\n/*                                                                            */\n/* 0=Disabled ÷ 1=Enabled                                                     */\n/******************************************************************************/\n\nTakeSysop       = Use sysop in lastcallers\nLeaveOutNode    = Mark out a node! This one will NOT be used for lastcallers\n\n>>> Now Comming up the KEYWORDS for the Lastcallers checker! I think you\n    can keep them as they are for 90% ... just some might NOT appear in\n    YOUR callerslog because they were sent by MY doors which are also out\n    to get! If you don`t have them installed ... Leave the keywords alone!!!\n\nPWFailKey       = "Password Failure"\nUploadKey       = "Uploading"\nDownldKey       = "Downloading"\nULFAILKey       = "Upload Failed"\nDLFAILKey       = "Download Failed"\nOpPageKey       = "Operator Page"\nChatOkKey       = "Cry-N-Chat"\nFileScKey       = "Directory Scan"\nConfScKey       = "Conference Scan"\nBulletKey       = "Bulletins"\nULResuKey       = "Resuming"\nAccEdiKey       = "Account editing"\nLocalLogon      = Bauf for LOCAL LOGIN\nOutput          = Outputfile of lastcallers\nAlltimeCaller	= Storgage file for ALL callers ever since you kill it!\n\n/******************************************************************************/\n/* MISCELLANEOUS                                                              */\n/******************************************************************************/\n\nTitleSlogan	="Short slogan for the FRONTEND titlebar"\nTopTextNoPW     =text been showed up if USEPW = 0\nTopTextPW       =text been showed up if USEPW = 1\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',54836,43,0,NULL,NULL,'sad_fe10','scan',1780048711);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('sad_fe15','SAD^FE15.LZX','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/SAD^FE15.LZX',NULL,'XIM','MyCookie.exe',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'auto-added',52869,0,0,NULL,NULL,'sad_fe15','scan',1780048714);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('sad_fe16','SAD-FE16.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/SAD-FE16.LHA','Warning!','XIM','MyCookie.exe',NULL,'WHO,','SAD','_/ ___/_  _ /_ ___ \ SCEPTIC /X DESIGN / \_    /     /   / /.- Presents in 95 /--. /_______/__/__/_____/ | another AIM DOOR   |',replace('    _________________\n  _/ ___/_  _ /_ ___ \ SCEPTIC /X DESIGN\n / \_    /     /   / /.- Presents in 95 /--.\n/_______/__/__/_____/ | another AIM DOOR   |\n- --- -- - -- - -- - -''                    |\n| SAD FRONT-END v1.6   Lastcallers, Cookie,|\n|         by           WHO, Password and   |\n|    FLI7e of SAD      Password Menu!      |\n|                      All these are also  |\n| >> MAJOR UPDATE <<   runable from Prompt!|\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'SAD-FrontEnd.guide',replace('@database SAD-FRONTEND\n@master doors:sceptic/F!-frontend/SAD-FrontEnd.guide\n@$VER: SAD-FRONTEND.guide v1.6 (21.06.1995)\n@author "FLI7e / SAD"\n@(c) "Sceptic /X Design 1995"\n@index Index\n@node "Main" "SAD-FRONTEND DOCUMENTATION MAIN PAGE"\n     _________________________________  __________\n     \\   __/_ ___/_ ___/_  __  /     /_/___/  ___/_\n.--- /\\___  / /   /__/  /  ___/___/   /   /   /   / --------------------------.\n| A /______/_____/_____/___/    /____/___/_______/ /X Design Production 1995! |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n\n      .  .:.--¡!-------------------------------------¡:---.              .    :\n:  : :: :::|  !: SAD-FRONT v1.6 by FLI7e/SAD^HJB^NJY !¡   |::: :: :  :   :    :\n      ·  ·:`--:--------------------------------------:!---''              ·    :\n                                                      :\n            @{fg highlight}.---------------------------------------------------@{fg text}.\n            @{fg highlight}|@{"·   (c)opyright Note   ·" link "01" 0}  @{"·     Introduction     ·" link "02" 0}@{fg text}|\n            @{fg highlight}|@{"·     Requirements     ·" link "03" 0}  @{"·       Features       ·" link "04" 0}@{fg text}|\n            @{fg highlight}|@{"·     Installation     ·" link "05" 0}  @{"·  Contact the Author  ·" link "06" 0}@{fg text}|\n            @{fg highlight}|@{"·     Door History     ·" link "07" 0}  @{"·  Greetings/Messages  ·" link "08" 0}@{fg text}|\n            @{fg highlight}|@{"·      About SAD!      ·" link "09" 0}  @{"·  SAD Tools & Doors!  ·" link "10" 0}@{fg text}|\n            @{fg highlight}`@{fg text}---------------------------------------------------''\n\n@endnode\n@node "01" "© 1995 SAD"\n\n\n\n\n-  - -- ---------------------> (c)opyright notes <------------------- -- -  -\n\n                         SAD-FRONTEND ©1995 FLI7e/SAD\n\n                  Permission is granted to freely distribute\n                this product for non-commercial purposes only,\n                    as long as all files remain unmodified.\n\n               Please Register so that I can see If you like this\n            hard piece of work! Registration did not cost any cent!\n                  I just want to see how my door`s are used!\n\n- -- ------------------------------------------------------------------- --- --\n\n                                @{"· MAIN MENU ·" link "MAIN" 0}\n@endnode\n@node "02" "INTRODUCTION"\n\n\n- -- ------------------------------------------------------------------- --- --\n               !!! - THIS IS AN UPDATED & BUGFIXED VERSION - !!!\n- -- ------------------------------------------------------------------- --- --\n\n  SAD-FRONTEND  v1.6  is  (in my opinion) the MOST-FEATURE frontend ever made\n  for AmiExpress.  Beside the STANDARD feature, the WHO it features:\n\n  ·LASTCALLERS\n  ·COOKIE\n  ·PASSWORD ROUTINE\n  ·Usage of /X INTERNAL or FULLED MSG Editor for the PW FAIL MSGs\n  ·All doors(WHO, PW & Cookie) are useable from the BBS-MAINLINE, TOO!\n\n  The lastcallers part features masses of infos and it`s running in an damned\n  fast speed (it`s AREXX ma friend!!!).\n\n  Read all about it in the FEATURES!\n\n                                @{"· MAIN MENU ·" link "MAIN" 0}\n\n- -- ------------------------------------------------------------------- --- --\n               !!! - THIS IS AN UPDATED & BUGFIXED VERSION - !!!\n- -- ------------------------------------------------------------------- --- --\n@endnode\n@node "03" "REQUIREMENTS"\n\n  I  don`t  know If Mr.  J.  Hodge has changed the /X REXX PORT since /X $Ver\n  2.0!  But If he did so then you need at least /X 2.0+ to run this door!\n\n  Amiga  OS 2.04+ would also be very usefull because of the RexxMAST you need\n  to run this door!\n\n                                @{"· MAIN MENU ·" link "MAIN" 0}\n@endnode\n@node "04" "Features"\n\n  · Lastcallers\n  · Who\n  · Password (better than internal SYSTEM PW)\n  · Random Cookie\n\n  LASTCALLERS\n  ===========\n\n  The  lastcallers  always were made as XIM because of speed in analyzing the\n  callerslog.   Hmm  ..   But  that`s  a  good reason to try it in arexx, eh?\n  Well,  I  did  so  and  the  result is a (I think so) powerfull lastcallers\n  featuring the following things:\n\n  · NICE looking output\n  · Daily status line\n  · New user detection\n  · Baud detection\n  · Node detection\n  · Logon Date\n  · Logon Time\n  · Logoff Time\n  · Chat/Pages Count\n  · UL+DL files & bytes\n  · an ALLTIME CALLER logfile\n  · 13 Different activities\n  · You can config the LOCAL logons (e.g fake baud)\n  · Take or take not SYSOP\n  · Mark out node(s) so they won`t be used for the last callers!\n\n  Since I released the 1.0 Version I improved many things and added some\n  new ones! See HISTORY for details\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n        _________________ ____                     ____ _________________\n        \________________\\___) I-M-P-O-R-T-A-N-T (___//________________/\n\n    IF YOU KNOW SOME /X INTERNAL MESSAGES SENT TO THE CALLERSLOG THEN PLEASE\n    LET ME KNOW SO THAT I CAN INCLUDE THEM TO PREVENT YOU OF POSSIBLE ERRORS\n    FORCED BY UNKNOWN LINES IN THE CALLERSLOG!\n        _________________ ____                     ____ _________________\n        \________________\\___) I-M-P-O-R-T-A-N-T (___//________________/\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  WHO\n  ===\n  Hmmm ...  Yes ...  This who is nothing special ..  Just that you can use it\n  IN  the  frontend AND from the mainprompt!  No need of a seperate WHO door!\n  I Think this is the only reason to install this as an BBSCMD, too!\n\n\n  PASSWORD\n  ========\n  This PW Protection is working like this:  If you Switch ON the USEPW option\n  a  different text will be shown and a Prompt will force the user to type in\n  the  PW!   If  he  fail  3 times he`ll be logged off.  If you switch on the\n  USEPWMENU he won`t be logged off but will be sent to the MENU where he can\n\n  · leave the sysop a message using build in MSG editor! and sent this to the\n    specified MSGBASE area of the Specified conference (new users seems to be\n\n  · Logoff\n\n    You can use this as BBSCMD, too to place it e.g. in SPECIAL areas or as a\n    protection for a command! But if you use it as an command-protection i\n    suggest to use it in a MULTISTART door like the one from STC or you put\n    it in a textfile as an MCI command (~CC_PW) for example!\n\n    See HISTORY for news and fixes!\n\n\n  COOKIE\n  ======\n\n  Well  ..   This is the ONLY part which use the help of an XIM part!  Thanxx\n  to  DRF/HJB  for giving this one to me!  It`s a damned fast cookie selector\n  and  I build in the option to display it to the /X Screen!  Nothing special\n  ...  Just damned fast!\n\n  You can use this as BBSCMD, too!\n\n  Thats`s  all  I  think  (isn`t that enough???) If anybody will install this\n  door  then  please consider contacting me!  Not for paying anything but as\n  a notice for me that I did well!\n\n                                @{"· MAIN MENU ·" link "MAIN" 0}\n\n@endnode\n@node "05" "Installation"\n\n   Copy all the files from this archive to the matching places on your BBS:\n\n            and load the config file and edit it to your needs!\n\n               Here is what you can config in the Config-file\n\nUsePW           = 0=NO ; 1=YES\nUsePWMENU       = 0=NO ; 1=YES\nUseWHO          = 0=NO ; 1=YES\nUseCookie       = 0=NO ; 1=YES\nUseLastCaller   = 0=NO ; 1=YES\n\nPW              ="<Password>"\nPWPrompt        ="<Password Prompt>"\nPWOK            ="<PW OK MSG>"\nPWWRONG         ="<PW WRONG MSG>"\nPWMSGPATH       ="<Path to the Conference where to send PWFAIL MSGs>"\n                  (e.g.: "bbs:ansi/MSGBASE/")\n\nPWMLINE         = "<MAINLINE Password>"\nPWPromptMLINE   = "<MAINLINE Password Prompt>"\nPWOKMLINE       = "<MAINLINE Password OK MSG>"\nPWWRONGMLINE    = "<MAINLINE Password Wrong MSG>"\n\nPWOVERRIDELEVEL = <Access level allowed to override pw procedure>\nPWSYSOPOVERRIDE = <0=NO, 1=YES to allow SYSOP to override pw procedure>\n\nWhoBaud.x       = "<Default Baud for node(x)>"\nWhoDefaultUser  = "<Username on AWAITING CONNECT nodes>"\nWhoDefaultLoca  = "<UserLocation on AWAITING CONNECT nodes>"\n\nTakeSysop       = 0=NO ; 1=YES\nPWFailKey       = "Password Failure"     <«- Keyword added to callerslog\nUploadKey       = "Uploading"            <«- Keyword added to callerslog\nULResuKey       = "Resuming"             <«- Keyword added to callerslog\nDownldKey       = "Downloading"          <«- Keyword added to callerslog\nULFAILKey       = "Upload Failed"        <«- Keyword added to callerslog\nDLFAILKey       = "Download Failed"      <«- Keyword added to callerslog\nOpPageKey       = "5D-DummyPage:"        <«- Keyword added to callerslog\nFileScKey       = "Directory Scan"       <«- Keyword added to callerslog\nConfScKey       = "Conference Scan"      <«- Keyword added to callerslog\nBulletKey       = "Bulletins"            <«- Keyword added to callerslog\nAccEdiKey       = "Account editing"      <«- Keyword added to callerslog\nLocalLogon      = "<FakeBaud for Local Login>"\nNoOFFTime	= "<5 Chars default>" if bbs crashed and no logofftime is\n                                      in the callerslog!\n\nLeaveOutNodes   = "<00,03,04 [...]>"\nOutput          = "<Outputpath/name> for the last ten!"\nAlltimeCaller   = "<Outputpath/name> for the HISTORY file"\n\nMLINEWHO        ="<the WHO header ansi>"\nMLINEPW         ="<the PW header ansi>"\nMLINECOOKIE     ="<the COOKIE header ansi>"\n\nTopTextNoPW     ="<normal logontext>"\nTopTextPW       ="<logontext if using PW>"\nTitleSlogan     ="<Slogan in the FRONTEND HEADERLINE>"\n\n            Look up the REAL configfile for further explanation!\n\n                                @{"· MAIN MENU ·" link "MAIN" 0}\n@endnode\n@node "06" "Contact SAD"\n\n   The Pub             (WHQ) +49-5551-65139  - 1ND 28k8 (sYSOP:       fLI7e)\n   Silent Service     (DIST) +616 955 5119   - 1ND 28k8 (sYSOP:   Rudolf H.)\n   RaveLand            (GHQ) +49-7128-3511   - 1ND 28k8 (sYSOP:        H2O!)\n   Forbidden Planet (IRL-HQ) +353-1-820 8489 - 2ND 33k6 (sYSOP: Green-Beret)\n\n   SWITCHBOARD          HLM GHQ.     5ND      MSG to "[]-> Fli7e & WTM <-[]"\n   EVIL MOON         RMD^AG! HQ.     1ND      MSG to "[]-> Fli7e & WTM <-[]"\n\n                                  oR wRITE tO\n\n                         EMail: [email removed]\n\n                                @{"· MAIN MENU ·" link "MAIN" 0}\n@endnode\n@node "07" "History"\n\n\n             _________________ ____        ____ _________________\n             \\________________\\\\___) v0.5 (___//________________/\n\n                          First BBS-INTERNAL release\n\n===============================================================================\n             _________________ ____        ____ _________________\n             \\________________\\\\___) v1.0 (___//________________/\n\n                             First public release\n\n===============================================================================\n             _________________ ____        ____ _________________\n             \\________________\\\\___) v1.1 (___//________________/\n\n                       Fixed some bugs - NEVER RELEASED -\n\n===============================================================================\n             _________________ ____        ____ _________________\n             \\________________\\\\___) v1.2 (___//________________/\n\n            Added some features & fixed some bugs - NEVER RELEASED -\n\n===============================================================================\n             _________________ ____        ____ _________________\n             \\________________\\\\___) v1.5 (___//________________/\n\n\n-»> Added different setup-feature for FRONTEND use and MAINLINE use! You can\n    now use different PWs, PROMPTs, FAIL & OK MSGs & DIFFERENT Mailsend CONFs\n\n-»> Now sending the PW FAIL message to the MESSAGE BASE area! No Fucking\n    textfile anymore where the sysop have to look up on his own! Just\n    specify a conference where to write the Message(s)!\n\n-»> Added Different PW COMMAND option! You can now have different BBSCOMMANDS\n    with different extensions! Let us say you use the PW-ROUTINE in a BULL\n    file and you like to use it it in differnt ones at different places you\n    can use it like this:\n\n    ~CC_PW		= This will use the MAINLINE PW from Config file\n    ~CC_PW-test		= This will use the word "test" as pw!\n\n    Just make sure you`ve the PW-TEST.info in your BBSCMD or NODE(x)CMD\n    drawer in BBS:COMMANDS/!!\n\n-»> Added ACCESS LEVEL override for MAINLINE use! If a user have a higher\n    level than the one you specified he will not forced to enter the PW!!\n\n-»> Added SYSOP override for MAINLINE use!\n\n-»> Dowloaded files/Day\n\n-»> Uploaded Bytes/Day\n\n-»> New smashing Ansi by H2o!/SAD\n\n-»> Added EXAMINE RESTRICTED FILES activitie\n\n-»> Recognizig FREE DOWNLOAD and NORMAL DOWNLOAD (Crashed in v1.0 because\n    I don`t use the STATUS line AFTER the download! I do it line by line\n    to become most accuracy! But If it was FREE DL then the bytes are\n    placed at another positing! RESULT=CRASH!)\n\n-»> If somebody logged in at 00:00:00 the door used this call as an\n    YESTERDAY CALL! What a fuck! Now fixed\n\n-»> If a user lost carrier because the BBS crashed no LOGOFF time and\n    LOGOFF STATUS were printed to the callerslog! But my Lastcallers\n    thought there MUST be such a line! It crashed! Now "(???)" will be\n    added as LOGOFFTIME (You can specify this!).\n\n-»> I REMOVED the differnt o + O activity because i recogniced that\n    nearly NO pager supports this Information in the callerslog. Just\n    MINE is supporting it! So if you use a Pager which is writing\n    different sentences to the callerslog (e.g. PAGED SYSOP, START CHATTING)\n    then tell me and I`ll include It for YOU again!.\n\n-»> You can now use unlimited LEAVE OUT NODES! e.g. you`ve a 9 node system\n    and you just want to have Node 4-9 in the lastcallers then you can\n    NOW leave out NODE 0-3! In 1.0 you were just able to leave out ONE node!\n    For this example the CONFIG line must look like this:\n\n    LEAVEOUTNODES	= "00,01,02,03"\n\n    This will force the LASTCALLERS to stay inactive if the NODE result\n    is one of 0-3!\n\n-»> You can now have ANSIS for the MAINLINE Usage of WHO, COOKIE and PW!\n\n-»> "Error Reading MsgBase Pointer" identification included! I missed this\n     because I never had this before! Now fixed!\n\n===============================================================================\n             _________________ ____        ____ _________________\n             \\________________\\\\___) v1.6 (___//________________/\n\n\n-»> Different BAUDRATES for WHO\n\n-»> Fixed CHAT COUNT bug made in v1.5!  Now PAGES will be counted, not chats!\n\n-»> Slightly optimized code\n\n-»> Added PW MENU usage for USER PW FAILURE in LOGON SEQUENCE\n\n-»> Added  USE of INTRNAL or FULLSCREEN editor of /X!  Best Way to write REAL\n    MSGs I think!!!\n\n-»> Now  Using  ACTUAL  CONFERENCE MSGBASE for PWFAIL MSGs!  So the Sysop can\n    see in which Conf the Failure occured!\n\n-»> Now need to specify the FULL PATH to LOGON PW FAIL MSGBASE!  In the other\n    version the CONFERENCE LOCATION itself fitted the needs!  Now you need to\n    specify it like this:  confpath/MSBASE/ That`s it!\n\n-»> Changed the MSG SEND TYPE! It was NOT a PRIVATE TO SYSOP msg!!\n\n                                @{"· MAIN MENU ·" link "MAIN" 0}\n@endnode\n@node "08" "Greetings"\n\nAquarius/Outlaws ................ -»> Still in Outlaws? Why don`t you come\n                                      over here!?\n\nFOX/AG!^REMEDY .................. -»> Hi Vince! Hope this one is running clean\n                                      and bugfree! Test it!\n\nSTC/TASK ........................ -»> Where are the NEW doors? Are you dead\n                                      or just sleeping?\n\nTHE PROPHET/NJY ................. -»> Hmmm! Same as above!\n\nPIWI GON/SAD .................... -»> You`r /X CFG ED looks great! Letus work\n                                      fast to release it! MUI ROOLZ!\n\nCOUGAR/HOODLUM .................. -»> Lousiest BETA TESTER ever! Why don`t you\n                                      install the updates i pump to your system\n                                      so often?\n\nHITPOWER/PRODIGY ................ -»> Erm, Modem damaged? Or quitted scene? Why\n                                      don`t ya call?\n\nCASIO/SAD ....................... -»> Hey my dear ITALIAN ONE MEN DIVISION! How\n                                      are you?\n\n       and all slaved SYSOPS and /X-DOOR CODER worldwide! Keep /X going!\n\n\n\nNO CARRIER\n\n+++ATH\n\n                                @{"· MAIN MENU ·" link "MAIN" 0}\n@endnode\n@node "09" "ABOUT SAD"\n\n    We in SAD are searching some good /X-Door and Tool coder (AIM, XIM etc.)\n\n        If you`re searching a NICE and "WANT-TO-BE-ACTIVE" group then we\n                       might be the right choice for YOU!\n\n      You`ve NOT to leave your actual Group, you can join us just for /X!\n\n       So if you`re a C, E, ASM, AREXX coder or an ANSI artist or a SYSOP\n     who like to open a DST SITE (BETA SITE) then just get in contact with\n\n                                     FLI7e\n\n                         Some closer Information on SAD\n                        +------------------------------+\n\n    SCEPTIC itself was founded in the early month of 1992! We released some\n             demos, intros, trainers, patches and ansi collections.\n\n      Our most famous production was CHIPMANIA (soon be released under the\n                 HAUJOBB label because I (fli7e) joined them!)\n\n      Then .. In summer 1994 I kicked all inactive members and decided to\n     change the way we go! DEMO-GROUP .. R.I.P .. /X + Toolgroup .. ALIVE!\n\n   From there on we worked a long time in the underground .. NO RELEASES ..!\n\n   But that should change NOW! With your help a famous group could be REBORN!\n\n                                Actual "MEMBERS"\n\n            FLi7e/HAUJOBB ^ N-JOY ^ SAD    (Leader, /X CODER, SYSOP)\n            H2o/SAD                                   (AZZKY Layout)\n            PIWI/SAD                                      (/X CODER)\n            SLY/SAD                              (TRADER & /X CODER)\n            CASIO/SAD                                        (CODER)\n            WIGWAM/SAD                                       (CODER)\n            SHADOWMASTER/IFT^SAD                          (/X CODER)\n            COUGAR/HOODLUM                             (BETA TESTER)\n\n  Well, not that much I think! And because of that we`ll try to strike again!\n\n                         ·W·I·T·H· ·Y·O·U·R· ·H·E·L·P·\n\n\n                             !KEEP THE CULT GOING!\n\n\n                               Fast greetings to\n\n            ZULU&GREY/REBELS, AEROSOUL/Ex. Shoot, ALL NJYs, ALL HJBs\n             FOX/AG!^RDY, STC/TASK, FASHION/STB, TOUCHSTONE/ESSENCE\n\n                    And all those bleeding noses out there!\n\n                 FUCK da Rotten Skunks called themselves NAZIS!\n\n                                @{"· MAIN MENU ·" link "MAIN" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "10" "SAD TOOLS/DOORS"\n\nAlready Released SAD Doors by FLI7e\n-----------------------------------\n\nBulletins           (AIM) -»> Great Bulletins Door with nice features\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nRequest             (AIM) -»> A Request door with MSG BASE MAIL SEND\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nWall                (AIM) -»> Two Walls in one! You can use PWs to switch\n                              between the PUBLIC and the "ELITE" wall!\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSecurity            (AIM) -»> Protect Special Conferences of Lamers!\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDLD                 (AIM) -»> Download Filedirs\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHelp                (AIM) -»> Multi Language Online Help for /X\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDoorsMenu           (AIM) -»> Displays Different DOORS menus depending on\n                              Users-access.\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCommentToSysop      (AIM) -»> As the Name states ... Another FINE Comment\n                              door!\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFrontend            (AIM) -»> Including: LASTCALLERS, WHO, PW, PWMENU, COOKIE!\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLogOff Deluxe       (AIM) -»> Logoff Door with BBS ADD option, LAST CALLER MSG\n                              with REPLY option\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nAnsi Request        (AIM) -»> GREAT Ansi Request door! Nice features!\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nFORCE ANSI ON       (AIM) -»> Override the MODE question in the login and\n                              the user can`t change the MODE itself online\n                              to NON ANSI! This is great for ANSI ONLY boards!\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nLOGOUT DOOR         (AIM) -»> Great LOGOFF Door with great features like:\n                              LAST CALLERS MSG, WRITE MSG TO SYSOP, RELOGON\n                              ADD BBS TO A LIST, VIEW BBS-LIST ...\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCD-ORDER            (AIM) -»> Written for a friend of mine who`s SELLING\n                              CD`s! But it`s also flexible so you can use\n                              it for any needs! Download catalogue lists of\n                              different subjects and more.\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nCHIPMANIA           (AIM) -»> The /X CHIPMANIA Vote Door! You can vote in\n                              unlimited Topics, Upload News, Interviews,\n                              Cliparts, Modules ... Download latest Issue!\n\n\n\nSoon to come SAD Doors/Tools\n----------------------------\n\n· /X Config Ed with MUI application and lotsa great features to easy\n  config ALL the /X 3.x+ Info files! The Tool comes with ALL available\n  /X INTERNAL Tooltypes for maximum configuration Power! Any tooltype\n  available on one Mousclick for any Standard and ANY Self Configured\n  BBS CMD and that stuff! YOU`re able to ADD/REMOVE tooltypes from\n  default lists and and and ...\n\n  (XIM) ---> STILL IN WORK and NEARLY FINISHED\n             ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n\n· Keyboard Controlled MENU door! No more typing! Choose your command\n  by moving a BAR around! User-Chooseable if MENU or PROMPT mode!\n\n  (AIM or XIM)\n\n\n· GREAT Operator Pager with integrated LINECHAT (the first for /X ever!!\n  like in FastCall!), WB GUI with lotsa features .. A Must for SYSOPS ..\n\n  (AIM)\n\n\n· DoorChecker! Will check all BBSCMDs and SYSCMDs if the needed door is\n  still installed. DeInstall option for sure!\n\n  (AIM or XIM)\n\n\n· SYSTEM SHELL with GREAT options like UPLOAD, DOWNLOAD directly to\n  system! REAL shell!! Batchdownload from anywhere! SYSOP can use\n  filerequester for Selecting files!\n\n  (AIM) ---> STILL IN WORK and NEARLY FINISHED\n             ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n\n\nand some more Ideas still in mind!\n\nIf you have any Idea .. just tell us!\n\n                                @{"· MAIN MENU ·" link "MAIN" 0}\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',63378,5,0,NULL,NULL,'sad_fe16','scan',1780048711);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('sad_fe21','SAD-FE21.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/SAD-FE21.LHA',NULL,'XIM','MyCookie.exe',NULL,'¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯','SAD','_/ ___/_  _ /_ ___ \ SCEPTIC /X DESIGN / \_    /     /   / /.- Presents in 95 /--. /_______/__/__/_____/ | another AIM DOOR   |',replace('    _________________\n  _/ ___/_  _ /_ ___ \ SCEPTIC /X DESIGN\n / \_    /     /   / /.- Presents in 95 /--.\n/_______/__/__/_____/ | another AIM DOOR   |\n- --- -- - -- - -- - -''                    |\n| SAD FRONT-END v2.1   REMOVED LASTCALLERS |\n|         by           ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯ |\n|    FLI7e of SAD      Other FUNCTIONS ARE |\n|                      STILL IN THERE!     |\n| >> MAJOR CHANGE <<   Check IT!           |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'SAD-FrontEnd.doc',replace('     _________________________________  __________\n     \   __/_ ___/_ ___/_  __  /     /_/___/  ___/_\n.--- /\___  / /   /__/  /  ___/___/   /   /   /   / --------------------------.\n| A /______/_____/_____/___/    /____/___/_______/ /X Design Production 1995! |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n\n      .  .:.--¡!-------------------------------------¡:---.              .    :\n:  : :: :::|  !: SAD-FRONT v2.1 by FLI7e/SAD^HJB^NJY !¡   |::: :: :  :   :    :\n      ·  ·:`--:--------------------------------------:!---''              ·    :\n                                                      :\n\n\n-  - -- ---------------------> (c)opyright notes <------------------- -- -  -\n\n                  Permission is granted to freely distribute\n                this product for non-commercial purposes only,\n                    as long as all files remain unmodified.\n\n- -- ------------------------------------------------------------------- --- --\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| Introduction                                                                |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n  SAD-FRONTEND  v2.1  is  (in my opinion) the MOST-FEATURE frontend ever made\n  for AmiExpress.  Beside the STANDARD feature, the WHO it features:\n\n  ·COOKIE\n  ·PASSWORD ROUTINE\n  ·Usage of /X INTERNAL or FULLED MSG Editor for the PW FAIL MSGs\n  ·All doors(WHO, PW & Cookie) are useable from the BBS-MAINLINE, TOO!\n  ·LAMER BAUD DETECT! Usefull to keep unwanted LOWBAUD caller offline!\n\n  I  REMOVED  the  LASTCALLERS  now  TOTALY!   It`s now a SEPERATE door to be\n  started   from   the  LOGOFF.BATCH!   I  did  this  because  of  some  more\n  flexibility!\n\n  But I think it`s a better way to do it like this!\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| Requirements                                                                |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n  I  don`t  know If Mr.  J.  Hodge has changed the /X REXX PORT since /X $Ver\n  2.0!  But If he did so then you need at least /X 2.0+ to run this door!\n\n  Amiga  OS 2.04+ would also be very usefull because of the RexxMAST you need\n  to run this door!\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| Features                                                                    |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n  · Who\n  · Password (better than internal SYSTEM PW)\n  · Random Cookie\n  · LAMER BAUD\n\n  WHO\n  ===\n  Hmmm ...  Yes ...  This who is nothing special ..  Just that you can use it\n  IN  the  frontend AND from the mainprompt!  No need of a seperate WHO door!\n  I Think this is the only reason to install this as an BBSCMD, too!\n\n\n  PASSWORD\n  ========\n  This PW Protection is working like this:  If you Switch ON the USEPW option\n  a  different text will be shown and a Prompt will force the user to type in\n  the  PW!   If  he  fail  3 times he`ll be logged off.  If you switch on the\n  USEPWMENU he won`t be logged off but will be sent to the MENU where he can\n\n  · leave the sysop a message using build in MSG editor! and sent this to the\n    specified MSGBASE area of the Specified conference (new users seems to be\n\n  · Logoff\n\n    You can use this as BBSCMD, too to place it e.g. in SPECIAL areas or as a\n    protection for a command! But if you use it as an command-protection i\n    suggest to use it in a MULTISTART door like the one from STC or you put\n    it in a textfile as an MCI command (~CC_PW) for example!\n\n    See HISTORY for news and fixes!\n\n\n  COOKIE\n  ======\n\n  Well  ..   This is the ONLY part which use the help of an XIM part!  Thanxx\n  to  DRF/HJB  for giving this one to me!  It`s a damned fast cookie selector\n  and  I build in the option to display it to the /X Screen!  Nothing special\n  ...  Just damned fast!\n\n  You can use this as BBSCMD, too!\n\n  Thats`s  all  I  think  (isn`t that enough???) If anybody will install this\n  door  then  please consider contacting me!  Not for paying anything but as\n  a notice for me that I did well!\n\n\n\n  BAUD DETECTION\n  ==============\n\n  LAMER BAUD DETECTION added!  Callers with a lower baud than the setted will\n  be  asked for a BAUD OVERRIDE PW!  This is usefull if you have some friends\n  calling  at  your bbs with a damned low baud but you don`t want NEW USER to\n  connect   on   these   baud   rate!    So   what  to  do?   Create  a  text\n  BBS:node(x)/nocallersat<baud>  ???  No you won`t because your friends can`t\n  login  anymore  ..   What  then?  Allow all low bauds?  No ..  Wrong again!\n  YOU  USE  THIS  DOOR!   It`ll prompt the LOW BAUD CALLER to enter the PW to\n  override this check!\n\n  If they fail ..  alike ..  they`ll be kicked off the line!  If they know it\n  ..  GREAT!  They`ll go on with the logon sequence!\n\n  Thanx to RUDOLF H. for the idea! It`s really great! I like it!\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| Installation                                                                |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n   Copy all the files from this archive to the matching places on your BBS:\n\n            and load the config file and edit it to your needs!\n\n               Here is what you can config in the Config-file\n\nUsePW           = 0=NO ; 1=YES\nUsePWMENU       = 0=NO ; 1=YES\nUseWHO          = 0=NO ; 1=YES\nUseCookie       = 0=NO ; 1=YES\nUseBaudCheck	= 0=NO ; 1=YES\n\nPW              ="<Password>"\nPWPrompt        ="<Password Prompt>"\nPWOK            ="<PW OK MSG>"\nPWWRONG         ="<PW WRONG MSG>"\nPWMSGPATH       ="<Path to the Conference where to send PWFAIL MSGs>"\n                  (e.g.: "bbs:ansi/MSGBASE/")\n\nPWMLINE         = "<MAINLINE Password>"\nPWPromptMLINE   = "<MAINLINE Password Prompt>"\nPWOKMLINE       = "<MAINLINE Password OK MSG>"\nPWWRONGMLINE    = "<MAINLINE Password Wrong MSG>"\n\nPWOVERRIDELEVEL = <Access level allowed to override pw procedure>\nPWSYSOPOVERRIDE = <0=NO, 1=YES to allow SYSOP to override pw procedure>\n\nWhoBaud.x       = "<Default Baud for node(x)>"\nWhoDefaultUser  = "<Username on AWAITING CONNECT nodes>"\nWhoDefaultLoca  = "<UserLocation on AWAITING CONNECT nodes>"\n\nBaudMin		= Lowest Baud accepted to log on\n                  e.g.: 2399 means 2400 connects are allowed!\n\nBaudPW		= "<BAUD OVERRIDE PW!>"\n                  If A User with a baudrate lower than the BAUDMIN knows\n                  this PW he`ll be accepted to logon! Others will get an\n                  kick ass!\n\nBaudPrompt	= "<BAUD PW PROMPT>"\nBaudPWOK	= "<PW OK MESSAGE>"\nBaudPWWRONG	= "<PW WRONG MESSAGE>"\nBaudDetectTXT	= "<text to be displayed if a LOW BAUD is detected>"\nBaudFailTXT	= "<text to be displayed if BAUD OVERRIDE PW fails 3 times>"\nBaudLogOfftxt   = "<A ONELINER which will be HIGHLIGHTED at the bottom on\n                   kick ass sequence>"\n\nMLINEWHO        ="<the WHO header ansi>"\nMLINEPW         ="<the PW header ansi>"\nMLINECOOKIE     ="<the COOKIE header ansi>"\n\nTopTextNoPW     ="<normal logontext>"\nTopTextPW       ="<logontext if using PW>"\nTitleSlogan     ="<Slogan in the FRONTEND HEADERLINE>"\n\n            Look up the REAL configfile for further explanation!\n\n  That`s it!!\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| Contact S/\D                                                                |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n   The Pub             (WHQ) +49-5551-65139  - 1ND 28k8 (sYSOP:       fLI7e)\n   Silent Service     (DIST) +616 955 5119   - 1ND 28k8 (sYSOP:   Rudolf H.)\n   RaveLand            (GHQ) +49-7128-3511   - 1ND 28k8 (sYSOP:        H2O!)\n   Forbidden Planet (IRL-HQ) +353-1-820 8489 - 2ND 33k6 (sYSOP: Green-Beret)\n\n   SWITCHBOARD          HLM GHQ.     5ND      MSG to "[]-> Fli7e & WTM <-[]"\n   EVIL MOON         RMD^AG! HQ.     1ND      MSG to "[]-> Fli7e & WTM <-[]"\n\n                                  oR wRITE tO\n\n                         EMail: [email removed]\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| Greetings & Messages                                                        |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\nAquarius/Outlaws ................ -»> Still in Outlaws? Why don`t you come\n                                      over here!?\n\nFOX/AG!^REMEDY .................. -»> Hi Vince! Hope this one is running clean\n                                      and bugfree! Test it!\n\nSTC/TASK ........................ -»> Where are the NEW doors? Are you dead\n                                      or just sleeping?\n\nTHE PROPHET/NJY ................. -»> Hmmm! Same as above!\n\nPIWI GON/SAD .................... -»> You`r /X CFG ED looks great! Letus work\n                                      fast to release it! MUI ROOLZ!\n\nCOUGAR/HOODLUM .................. -»> Lousiest BETA TESTER ever! Why don`t you\n                                      install the updates i pump to your system\n                                      so often?\n\nHITPOWER/PRODIGY ................ -»> Erm, Modem damaged? Or quitted scene? Why\n                                      don`t ya call?\n\nCASIO/SAD ....................... -»> Hey my dear ITALIAN ONE MEN DIVISION! How\n                                      are you?\n\n       and all slaved SYSOPS and /X-DOOR CODER worldwide! Keep /X going!\n\n\n\nNO CARRIER\n\n+++ATH\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| ABOUT SAD                                                                   |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n\n    We in SAD are searching some good /X-Door and Tool coder (AIM, XIM etc.)\n\n        If you`re searching a NICE and "WANT-TO-BE-ACTIVE" group then we\n                       might be the right choice for YOU!\n\n      You`ve NOT to leave your actual Group, you can join us just for /X!\n\n       So if you`re a C, E, ASM, AREXX coder or an ANSI artist or a SYSOP\n     who like to open a DST SITE (BETA SITE) then just get in contact with\n\n                                     FLI7e\n\n                         Some closer Information on SAD\n                        +------------------------------+\n\n    SCEPTIC itself was founded in the early month of 1992! We released some\n             demos, intros, trainers, patches and ansi collections.\n\n      Our most famous production was CHIPMANIA (soon be released under the\n                 HAUJOBB label because I (fli7e) joined them!)\n\n      Then .. In summer 1994 I kicked all inactive members and decided to\n     change the way we go! DEMO-GROUP .. R.I.P .. /X + Toolgroup .. ALIVE!\n\n   From there on we worked a long time in the underground .. NO RELEASES ..!\n\n   But that should change NOW! With your help a famous group could be REBORN!\n\n                                Actual "MEMBERS"\n\n            FLi7e/HAUJOBB ^ N-JOY ^ SAD    (Leader, /X CODER, SYSOP)\n            H2o/SAD                                   (AZZKY Layout)\n            PIWI/SAD                                      (/X CODER)\n            SLY/SAD                              (TRADER & /X CODER)\n            CASIO/SAD                                        (CODER)\n            WIGWAM/SAD                                       (CODER)\n            SHADOWMASTER/IFT^SAD                          (/X CODER)\n            COUGAR/HOODLUM                             (BETA TESTER)\n\n  Well, not that much I think! And because of that we`ll try to strike again!\n\n                         ·W·I·T·H· ·Y·O·U·R· ·H·E·L·P·\n\n\n                             !KEEP THE CULT GOING!\n\n\n                               Fast greetings to\n\n            ZULU&GREY/REBELS, AEROSOUL/Ex. Shoot, ALL NJYs, ALL HJBs\n             FOX/AG!^RDY, STC/TASK, FASHION/STB, TOUCHSTONE/ESSENCE\n\n                    And all those bleeding noses out there!\n\n                 FUCK da Rotten Skunks called themselves NAZIS!\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',40053,2,0,NULL,NULL,'sad_fe21','scan',1780048711);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('sad_filc','SAD-FILC.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/SAD-FILC.LHA',NULL,'XIM','DMSDescript',NULL,NULL,'SAD','__ _________  /___/_____________ _ _   ____//_/_  /      /  ____ _ of SCEPTIC __/ _/   / /__/   /  __/        HAUJOBB',replace('               ____\n__ _________  /___/_____________ _\n  _   ____//_/_  /      /  ____ _ of SCEPTIC\n     __/ _/   / /__/   /  __/        HAUJOBB\n __ _/_______/_/  /___/________ _  & N-JOY\n- -- ----------> Presents <------------ -- -\n________                            ________\n\      / FILE ID LIST CREATOR v1.0! \      /\n \    /                              \    /\n  \  / LHA/LZX/EXE/DMS/TXT and more!! \  /\n   \/                                  \/\n','\n',char(10)),'FILC.doc',replace('______________________________________________________________ _____ ___ _\n\_____________________________________________________________\\____\\__\\\\n\n\n                                     fLI7e\n\n                                       øf\n    ______     ______     ______     ________________     ______     ______\n_ __\  __/_____\ ___/_____\ ___/_____\   __ \_     _/_____\    /_____\ ___/_ _\n     \__    /    /     /   __/    /    ______/___      /   \  /   /    /\n       /   /          /          /      /     /       /     \/   /\n_ ________/__________/__________/______/÷F!÷ /_______/__________/_________ _\n\n                        __\n                       |_/__,____  ___ ____ ____ /_  ___\n                       |  \  \__/_`--. \__/_\  / \__`--.\n                       -  - ---------'' -  - -----------''\n\n                        FILE ID LIST CREATOR (FILC) v1.0\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nWHAT IS IT\n----------\n\nFILC  will  scan  a  given  dir for all\nfiles  and  then  extract, if possible,\nthe   FILE_ID.diz`s  out  of  them  and              ________\ncreate  a list like AmiExpress use them              \     _/__ _\n(not the same but close to it!)                       \  ___ _\n                                                       \  /\n                                                        \/\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                        __\n                                                       /\_\\ \  \    \\nSUPPORTET FILETYPES                              _____ \/_// /  /    /\n-------------------                             /\    \ ____\n                                                \ \    \\   \ ___\nLHA,LZH,LHZ,TXT,NFO,DOC,DOK,ANS,INF,DMS          \ \    \\   \\  \ __\nEXE,ZIP,LZX                                       \ \____\\___\\__\\_\\n                                                   \/____//___//__//_/\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nEXAMPLE OUTPUT\n--------------\n\nFILE ID LIST CREATOR v1.0                            (c) 1995 fLI7e/SAD^HJB^NJY\n\nFilename            Filelength     File Description\n===============================================================================\nSC_STATE.TXT            137438\n                                   .___________ _|_ ______ __|_ ___ ____  ___ _\n                                   |_\_.  \_ _   |________   |  ._/___  \|  sc/\n                                   :   l   / _}--:_\__   /   :  l_   /   \   /:\n                                   |______/______|   ___/____l______/   7___/ |\n                                   :             l______)          \____l     |\n                                   |     Author:               Title:         |\n                                   | ''sHAPECHANGER!''  .  ''a STATE oF mIND!''   |\n                                   l________________ _|_ _____________________|\n                                                      |\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\nREQUIREMENTS\n------------\n\n  OS 2.04+ by COMMODORE TECHNOLOGIES\n      TXTEXTRACT by SPY / MYSTIC\n     DMSDESCRIPT by REMO / MYSTIC\n     EXEDESCRIPT by REMO / MYSTIC\n         LHA by STEFAN BOBERG\n            UNZIP by anyone\n LZX by Data Compression Technologies.\n\n\n\n\n\n                                                 ____________________\n                                                 \ ______ __ ______ /\n                                                  _\     \\//     /_\n                                                  \\\     \/     ///\n                                                   __\          /__\nOTHER STUFF                                        \_\\        //_/\n-----------                                         ___\      /___\n                                                    \  \\    //  /\nThis  little  and ?LAME?  tool has been              \  \\  //  /\ndone in about 25minutes using the great               \__\\//__/\nAREXX language.                                         ______\n                                                        \    /\nIt`s   compiled   but  you  still  need                  \  /\nREXXMAST been active!                                     \/\n\nThis one is very usefull for ..  ehm ..\ni dunno ..  i use it to check all files\non  my  cd`s  for file id`s ..  but you\ncan use it for anything you like ..  to\neat, swim, sleep, smoke or just to have\nsex?\n\nOk  ...   out  of brain ...  have to go\nback to the army in 1 1/2 hours ...  so\ni`ll  be  back next weekend to maybe do\nanother little useless tool!\n\nFli7e ...\n\n______________________________________________________________ _____ ___ _\n\_____________________________________________________________\\____\\__\\\\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',34002,2,0,NULL,NULL,'sad_filc','scan',1780048711);
