INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('sad_wa11','SAD-WA11.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/SAD-WA11.LHA',NULL,'XIM','_________________',NULL,'Fli7e','SAD','_/ ___/_  _ /_ ___ \ SCEPTIC /X DESIGN / \_    /     /   / //- Presents in 95 /--. /_______/__/__/_____//  another AIM DOOR   |',replace('    _________________\n  _/ ___/_  _ /_ ___ \ SCEPTIC /X DESIGN\n / \_    /     /   / //- Presents in 95 /--.\n/_______/__/__/_____//  another AIM DOOR   |\n_                                          |\n|          SAD WALL v1.1 by Fli7e          |\n|                                          |\n| Great Wall with NICE output and USEFULL  |\n|      options like: STRIP and more        |\n|                                          |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'f!-wallSAD-WALL.doc',replace('     _________________________________  __________\n     \   __/_ ___/_ ___/_  __  /     /_/___/  ___/_\n.--- /\___  / /   /__/  /  ___/___/   /   /   /   / --------------------------.\n| A /______/_____/_____/___/    /____/___/_______/ /X Design Production 1995! |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n\n      .  .:.--¡!------------------------------------¡:----.              .    :\n:  : :: :::|  !: SAD-WALL v1.1 by FLI7e/SAD^HJB^NJY !¡    |::: :: :  :   :    :\n      ·  ·:`--:-------------------------------------:!----''              ·    :\n                                                     :\n\n\n-  - -- ---------------------> (c)opyright notes <------------------- -- -  -\n\n                  Permission is granted to freely distribute\n                this product for non-commercial purposes only,\n                    as long as all files remain unmodified.\n\n- -- ------------------------------------------------------------------- --- --\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| Introduction                                                                |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n  SAD-WALL  is  a 30minutes AREXX coded /X door which, as the name states, is\n  just  a  ?SIMPLE?   wall.   Well,  I haven`t inlcuded useless features like\n  other  doors have!  I`m not a big friend of useless USER-CONFIGURABLE LOGIN\n  DOORS,  because I don`t think that anyone who log on will first change some\n  options before writing (if he`s doing that) his one-liner!\n\n  SAD-WALL  is  just  a  "POP  UP  and  USE  door"  not a high end Message or\n  Database!   But it has been tested about 3 weeks and no errors occured!  So\n  it`s 100% save AND backdoor free!\n\n  See FEATURES for the two or three features it has included!\n\n\n\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| Requirements                                                                |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n  I  don`t  know If Mr.  J.  Hodge has changed the /X REXX PORT since /X $Ver\n  2.0!  But If he did so then you need at least /X 2.0+ to run this door!\n\n  Amiga  OS 2.04+ would also be very usefull because of the RexxMAST you need\n  to run this door!\n\n  A logintext where you can call (if you like, i do so) the WALL with the ~CC\n  command!\n\n\n\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| Features                                                                    |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n  Well,  as stated in the Introduction SAD-WALL did NOT offer any PLAY AROUND\n  options!  There are just TWO options:\n\n\n                                      -1-\n\n  You  can  specify  2 colors for the WALL-ENTRYS which will change by turns!\n  That means that entry 1 will get color one , entry 2 color 2, entry 3 color\n  1 and so on!\n\n  Colors: 1 = /X "WHITE", USER "RED"\n	  2 = Green\n	  3 = Yellow\n	  4 = Blue\n	  5 = Pink\n	  6 = Magenta\n	  7 = /X "RED, USER "WHITE"\n\n\n\n                                      -2-\n\n  It store ALL Wall-One-Liner in a seperate File so you can ( IF you like to)\n  use  the  best  of  them  for  a COOKIE file or just delete It!  I dunno if\n  someone else would use this FEATURE, but I like it!\n\n\n                                      -3-\n\n  You  can  change  the  HEADLINE  (Standard  says to NOT TAG BBS ADDS ON THE\n  WALL)...  just have a look on it!\n\n\n                                      -4-\n\n  You  can  change  the  sentence which will appear of the user did not write\n  anything!\n\n\n\n\n\n                              --- NEW in v1.1 ---\n\n\n                                      -5-\n\n  You  can  choose  If  you  want to Put the HANDLE of the user who wrote the\n  cookie on the wall in the STORAGE FILE, too!\n\n\n                                      -6-\n\n  You can PREVENT user writing some SPECIAL sentences/words on the wall.  For\n  example  I use this function to try to prevent my wall tagged with BBS ADDS\n  all over!  To get this feature active you must ADD the words/sentences to a\n  file which you can specify (see INSTALL for further Information)!\n\n  This  function  is just comparing the given INPUT with the RESTRICTED datas\n  in  the INVALIDFILE!  If it will find some matching patterns the INPUT will\n  not be printed to the wall or to the storagefile!\n\n\n\n\n\n  Thats`s  all  I  think!   If  anybody  will  install  this wall then please\n  consider  contacting  me!   Not  for paying anything but as a notice for me\n  that I did well!\n\n\n\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| Installation                                                                |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n  Copy the Dir "BBS/DOORS/SCEPTIC/F!-WALL" to your "DOORS:"\n\n  Copy  the given BBSCMD to your "BBSCMD" location or wherever you store your\n  BBS COMMANDS!\n\n  Include  an MCI Command in your login procedure to call the wall during the\n  Login session! (Just if you want to!)\n\n  Now  load  the  config  file  and  edit  it to your needs:  Here`s a closer\n  information:\n\n\nDatfile		= File to store the last 10 entrys\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nStorageFile	= File to store ALL wall-entries in...\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInvalidFile	= Datafile which contains all the FORBIDDEN keywords or\n		  sentences on which the WALL will react if this feature has\n                  been activated.\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nHeadline	= This line will be printed between wall and my header\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInvalid		= Slogan which will be shown if something RESTRICTED has been\n                  written to the wall (see feature -6- at FEATURES!)\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNoWriteCookie	= The Slogan which will be shown if the user has just pressed\n		  return!\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTraceInvalid	= Check for FORBIDDEN input! 0=no, 1=yes\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nStoreHandle	= Write USER-HANDLE to the STORAGEFILE, too. 0=no, 1=yes\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nColor1		= Color1 for the wall entrys\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nColor2		= Color1 for the wall entrys\n\n\n                 This is the Colortable for Color1 and Color2\n\n                       Sysop Side              Userside\n                       =================================\n                       1=White                 1=Red\n                       2=Green                 2=Green\n                       3=Yellow                3=Yellow\n                       4=Blue                  4=Blue\n                       5=Pink                  5=Pink\n                       6=Magenta               6=Magenta\n                       7=Red                   7=White\n\n\n\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| Contact the Author(s)                                                       |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n       To get in contact with FLI7E (Hi, that`s me) for any reason call:\n\n                                --- The Pub ---\n\n                               +49(0)5551-65139\n                                28k8 v34. vfast\n                                  A4000/33MHz\n                                   1.2GB HD\n\n                                  Sysop: ME!\n\n\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| History                                                                     |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n                  v0.5	-	First BBS-INTERNAL release\n  --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n                  v0.8	-	Added Alltime History File\n  --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n                  v1.0	-	First public release\n  --------------------------------------------------------------------------\n		  v1.1	-       Second public release\n\n				· Added TRACE command of INVALID inputs\n				· Added the ADD USERNAME function\n\n				· Fixed some little bugs\n\n				- If a user typed in extranous characters\n				  like CTRL-L, CTRL-X and so on, the wall\n			          output crashed! FIXED...\n\n				- If a user put SPACES in front or at the end\n                                  of his slogan the CENTERING seems 2 be very\n                                  UNCENTERED! FIXED ...\n\n                                - The NOTHING ENTERED prompt got scrambled\n                                  If user just typed in some SPACES! FIXED ...\n\n\n\n\n\n.-----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\n| Greetings                                                                   |\n`-----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\n\n     Aquarius/Outlaws /÷/ FOX/AG!^REMEDY \÷\ STC/TASK /÷/ THE PROPHET/NJY\n        PIWI/SAD \÷\ COUGAR/HOODLUM /÷/ HITPOWER/PRODIGY \÷\ CASIO/SAD\n\n       and all slaved SYSOPS and /X-DOOR CODER worldwide! Keep /X going!\n\n\n\nNO CARRIER\n\n+++ATH\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,16628,6,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048711);
