___/\n                       _ __ ___ ____ _    _ ____ ___ __ _\n                       \\\_\\__\\___\\\  ///___//__//_///\n                                      \\//\n                                       \/\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  Some  month  ago  (about  8 or more) I released an  FRONT END with included\n  lastcallers  ...   But that one was SOOOOO buggy, slow and lame allover!  I\n  put  the  idea  of  making  an  lastcallers  to  the big box under my table\n  fullfilled  with  ideas UNRELEASABLE in arexx ...  But after trying, coding\n  and imprroving my skill i grabbed it out again and it`s smashing!  I got an\n  Idea  to  find  out  the LAST CALLER without reading the callerslog line by\n  line  and  WITHOUT  taking  the same caller twice or more (most LASTCALLERS\n  don`t  care about the last caller still processed!  eg.  you call your last\n  callers  once  it`ll read out the data of the last caller and put it to the\n  bullfile!   if  you call it the second time same procedure ...  but why the\n  hell the same user should be put to the lastcallers bullfile?  I fixed this\n  neet bug by creating a 2nd datafile with the last callers dataline in it!)\n\n  I  also didn`t mind of the length of the callerslog ..  it`s always running\n  same speed ...  And it`s finding the LAST caller 100%\n\n  But  what do i`ve to say now ...  Just that you should install it and check\n  it  your  own!\n\n                       Signed : fLI7e oF sAD^HJB^KLF^CS!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                               __________________\n                           _ __\_              _/__ _\n\n                                  rEQUIREMENTS\n                               _ ___        ___ _\n                                   \________/\n                       _ __ ___ ____ _    _ ____ ___ __ _\n                       \\\_\\__\\___\\\  ///___//__//_///\n                                      \\//\n                                       \/\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                               /X 3.xx+, OS2.04+\n\n                           !!! REXX SERVER ACTIVE !!!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                               __________________\n                           _ __\_              _/__ _\n\n                                    fEATURES\n                               _ ___        ___ _\n                                   \________/\n                       _ __ ___ ____ _    _ ____ ___ __ _\n                       \\\_\\__\\___\\\  ///___//__//_///\n                                      \\//\n                                       \/\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n       Recognices Last user In LASTCALLER BULLFILE to prevent of double\n                              entrys in Bullfile\n\n      Can handle Connects up to 128000 (hahaha) (64000 is ISDN i guess!)\n\n                     Recognices F2 or SYSOP local logins!\n\n                Count upload/download time >or< ONLINE time!\n\n                             User Definable header\n\n    Daily Status: New Users/Day, Uploads & kbytes, Downloads & kbytes\n                      Pw Hacks/Day, Pages/Day and more\n\n                                  Nice layout\n\n                 Real fast if you remember it`s an arexx door!\n\n  You can decide if you want to have the ACTIVITIES legend displayed or not!\n\n  Now the SAD-KEY routine has been included! So if you have the SAD-KEY this\n    door will automatically be registered and all soon coming doors, too!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                               __________________\n                           _ __\_              _/__ _\n\n                                  iNSTALLATION\n                               _ ___        ___ _\n                                   \________/\n                       _ __ ___ ____ _    _ ____ ___ __ _\n                       \\\_\\__\\___\\\  ///___//__//_///\n                                      \\//\n                                       \/\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n  mAKE  A  DIR  named:   "DOORS:SCEPTIC" and copy the dir "F!-LAST" to it.\n\n  FNISHED ...\n\n\n\n\n\n  SAD-LAST.cfg\n  ~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n  BULLFILE	= Outputfile\n  HEADER	= Header (ascii???)\n  ENTRIES	= Number of last callers entrys in the bullfile\n  TIMEKIND	= WHICH TIME TO SHOW ... ONLINE or TRANSFER time used!\n  SHOWLEGEND    = Show ACTIVITIES description on(1)/off(0)\n  PAGERECOG	= "<key which your pager always print to callerslog>"\n  SCANRECOG	= "<key which your confscan always print to callerslog>"\n  ACCORECOG	= "<key /X writes to callerslog if account editing!>"\n                  Normaly it`s "Account Maintenance" but you may have\n                  a patched version? there are out some of them!\n\n  eg:	BULLFILE	= "doors:sceptic/F!-LAST/SAD-LAST.bull"\n  	HEADER		= "doors:Sceptic/F!-LAST/SAD-LAST.header"\n  	ENTRIES		= 10\n  	TIMEKIND	= T\n        SHOWLEGEND	= 1\n  	PAGERECOG	= "Operator Paged at"\n  	SCANRECOG	= "Directory Scan with AquaScan"\n  	ACCORECOG	= "Account Maintenance on"\n\n\n  Get your LOGOFF BATCH open and add the followng line:\n\n  -> cUT <-------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  doors:sceptic/sad-last.exe <node>\n\n  -------------------------------------------------------------------> cUT <-\n\n  eg: doors:sceptic/sad-last.exe 1    for node 1\n\n\n\n\n   Now load the "SAD-LAST.header" file and edit your personal header beeing\n                       placed right above the outputfile!\n\n                                  THAT`S ALL!\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                               __________________\n                           _ __\_              _/__ _\n\n                                   cONTACT sAD\n                               _ ___        ___ _\n                                   \________/\n                       _ __ ___ ____ _    _ ____ ___ __ _\n                       \\\_\\__\\___\\\  ///___//__//_///\n                                      \\//\n                                       \/\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n   -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n                          To Reach me FAST and DIRECT\n   -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   BBS   : THE PUB <«»> sAD WHQ <«»> +49-5551-911080 28k8 <«»> sYSgOD: fLI7e\n   EMAIL : [email removed] .................. once a week i get them\n   INET  : [email removed] ...................................... daily calling\n\n   -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n                                 To Contact SAD\n   -------------------------------------------------------------------------\n   EVIL MOON           [EHQ]         +49-SAD         28k8                fOX\n   RAVELAND            [GHQ]         +49-SAD         28k8               h2O!\n   SILENT MOON         [OZHQ]       +616-SAD         28k8             rUDOLF\n   FORBIDDEN PLANET    [IRLHQ]      +353-SAD         28k8        gREEN bERET\n   GREYHOUND           [IHQ]         +39-SAD         28k8             gURGLE\n   GOD`s HAREM         [DST]         +49-SAD         28k8/ISDN         lANCE\n   PLANET LOVE         [DST]         +49-SAD         28k8           mEPHISTO\n   TRADERS ASSAULT     [DST]         +49-SAD         28k8/ISDN     sTARLIGHT\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                               __________________\n                           _ __\_              _/__ _\n\n                                     hISTORY\n                               _ ___        ___ _\n                                   \________/\n                       _ __ ___ ____ _    _ ____ ___ __ _\n                       \\\_\\__\\___\\\  ///___//__//_///\n                                      \\//\n                                       \/\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n January 01st 1996        v1.0   > fIRST pUBLIC rELEASE\n\n\n ... internal ...         v1.1   > My    Baudchecker    fucked   up   if   no\n                                   MNP5,LAPM,V42BIS   or   whatever   connect\n                                   occured!    If  there  just  was  a  plain\n                                   connect  a wrong baudraute was shown!  ...\n                                   Now Fixed!\n\n January 21th 1996        v1.2   > sECOND pUBLIC rELEASE\n\n                                 > Added TIMECHOOSE . You can now decide what\n                                   time you want to have in the bullfile  for\n                                   each user! His time he needed to  TRANSFER\n                                   or the time he was ONLINE.\n\n                                 > Re-styled Outputfile\n                                 · Added many more DAILY stats to output.\n\n                                   See SAD-LAST.FEATURES for a complete  list\n                                   of FEATURES!\n\n                                 > Added ACTIVITIES DESCRIPTION on/off. So if\n                                   you don`t want the 2 lines  of  Activities\n                                   descriptions in the  output  bullfile  you\n                                   can switch them off!\n\n                                 > Added KEYFILE usage for automatic reg.!\n\nC YA ... Fli7e','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',25822,5,0,NULL,NULL,'sad_lc12','scan',1780048714);
