tc..\n==========================================================================\n                                  1.\n\n                 P.U.R.P.O.S.E.   &   D.E.S.C.R.I.P.T.I.O.N. \n\n      The purpose of this tool is simple.   It is an online BBS lister.\nThere have been a couple of similiar tools for /X for this purpose in the\npast but none to my knowledge supported many options besides viewing a\nspecified country.  We thought this was nice but why not add some nice\nfunctions like online editing of the list so users could update the list\nthemselves with thier own boards or other bbs''s they may have knowledge of\netc.  Of course this could be a drawback as well if a typical moron decided\nto add all his favorite local boards etc.. so of course this would be\nsolved by a simple configurable access level needed to use the edit\nfunctions..  Of course we have thought of this as well as often as BBS''s\nchange status different groups/changed numbers, etc..  All these functions\nand more are included in > T-LiST PRo < by S.R.H /X Design.  Read on...\n============================================================================\n                                  2.\n                  F.U.N.C.T.I.O.N.S.  O.F.  T.-.L.I.S.T.\n\n  If you have not allready installed T-LIST please skip this for now and\nmove down to section 3!!  :))    If you have read on..\n\n    Ok you have completed the simple install T-List Pro!  Now type TLIST\nand you will be presented with a nice looking ANSI of T-LIST :) and a menu\nwith a list of countries you can select to view and a command line below\nthe countries that looks a little like this line:\n\nCommand (#,S,C,E,A,D,?)\n\n The commands are as follows:\n\n #:  Type a number that corresponds with the country you wish to view the\nbbs on and T-List Pro will show you a list of the country selected!  :)\n\n S:  Search option.  T-List Pro will ask you for the string you wish to be\nsearched for.  After you enter your string hit return and it will ask you\nif you would like it to search ALL countries.  Hit return or ''y'' (default)\nand T-List Pro will start the search.  If you want a specific country to be\nsearched type ''n'' and T-List Pro will show you the country enu again and\nask you which country numbers you wish to be searched.\n\n C: Color On/Off\n\n E: Edit list.  When this is entered T-List Pro will ask you to give it the\nstring to search for that you wish to edit.  If it finds a matching text\nand the following command line: Edit (F,N,P,G,S,Q,?) [Continue]\n\n                                 F=Flag\n                                 N=Name\n                                 P=Phone\n                                 G=Group\n                                 S=Sysop\n                                 Q=Quit\n                                 ?=Expanded Help Line\n\n---------- F: FLAG\n    If the F function is selected from the edit menu as above it\nwill come up with this prompt:  Edit Flag (C,E,B,O,?) [Continue]\nJust select the type of flag to assign to the specifed BBS.\n                              C: Clear Flag.\n                              E: Mark as a newly edited BBS\n                              B: Mark as a Busted BBS.\n                              O: Mark as an Offline BBS.\n\n      ---------- N: NAME\n          Edit the Name of the BBS.\n      ---------- P: PHONE\n          Edit the phone number of the BBS.\n\n  NOTE:  When inputing the PHONE NUMBER be sure to add the appropriate\ndashes.. ie.... USA would be as follows:  1-###-###-#### :))\n*****IMPORTANT*****  Here is an example of what can happen if you do not\ndo this:   You add a new BBS in Finland and the number is something like\nthis:  +35867495325 without the hiphens (358-) T-List would read the ''35''\nbefore it could see the ''8'' afterwards and assume this is a Poland BBS\nbecause of the ''35'' country code of Poland.\n\n      ---------- G:\n          Edit the group of the BBS.\n      ---------- S:\n          Edit the sysop of the BBS.\n      ---------- Q:\n          Quit T-List Pro edit menu.\n      ---------- ?:\n          Expanded Help Prompt.\n\n                                    END OF EDIT FUNCTIONS\n\nA: Add a BBS to T-LIST.    T-List Pro will ask you for the needed\ninformation.   Simply follow online instructions.\n  NOTE:  When inputing the PHONE NUMBER be sure to add the appropriate\ndashes.. ie.... USA would be as follows:  1-###-###-#### :))\n*****IMPORTANT*****  Here is an example of what can happen if you do not\ndo this:   You add a new BBS in Finland and the number is something like\nthis:  +35867495325 without the hiphens (358-) T-List would read the ''35''\nbefore it could see the ''8'' afterwards and assume this is a Poland BBS\nbecause of the ''35'' country code of Poland.\n\nD: Delete a BBS from T-LIST.  T-List Pro will ask you for the text to find.\nWhen it finds a given string T-List will verify whether or not you wish the\nentry to be deleted.\n==========================================================================\n                                  3.\n                       I.N.S.T.A.L.L.A.T.I.O.N.\n\n    Un-Arc the T-List Pro archive into the drive that you store your bbs\non!  Or manually place the files where they need to go:\n\n         BBS:COMMANDS/BBSCMD/TLIST.INFO       (COMMAND ICON)\n         DOORS:SRH/TLIST/SRH-TLIST_PRO.INFO   (CONFIGURABLE ICON)\n         DOORS:SRH/TLIST/TLP2                 (T-LIST PRO 2 XIM MODULE)\n         DOORS:SRH/TLIST/SRH-TLIST_PRO2.DOC   (DOCS!!)\n         DOORS:SRH/TLIST/SRH-TLIST_PRO.GUIDE  (AMIGAGUIDE DOCS!!)\n\n             In addition to these files you will need an issue of S.R.H.''s\nT-LIST.TXT (SRH-TL#.TXT) which is released on a monthly basis.  This can\nbe located anywhere, but will have all adds stripped, so you might want\nto use a copy of your original.\n\n****IMPORTANT****\n    Please only use issues 10 and higher of the T-List.txt for proper BBS\nhighlight flagging operations!  \n****IMPORTANT****\n       The filename for the T-List txt is: SRH-TL#.TXT... the latest issue\nas of the release of this version of T-LIST PRO is SRH-TL8.TXT    If you \ncan not find a copy of T-LIST.TXT (doubtful) You can call these boards for \nthe latest issue:\n\n               Social Dizease  1-307-234-0580  T-LIST WHQ\n============================================================================\n                                  4.\n                          T.O.O.L.T.Y.P.E.S\n\n    The tooltypes of the icon\n\n\n                        LIST_PATH=<Path to TList.txt>\n                        COLUMNS=<Number of Columns>\n                        EDIT_AXS=<Access Level>\n                        ADD_AXS=<Access Level>\n                        KILL_AXS=<Access Level>\n\n    If the icon is not found or the tooltypes are commented '';'' they\ndefaults to 255.\n============================================================================\n                                  5.\n                           B.U.L.L.S.H.I.T.!.!\n \n      OK thaz all folks have fun with T-LIST PRO and please do not hesitate\nto send any bug reports on T-LIST or send in new infos you would like\npublished in future issues of T-LIST.TXT''s...  Greets to all our friends\netc.   Contact me (iNTRUdER) or fLASHbACK on any of these BBS''s:\n\n                             Social Dizease \n                             Lithium\n                             Skull Buggery\n                             The Void\n                             Snarf''s Pub\n\nNO CARRIER\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',22431,3,0,NULL,NULL,'srh_tlp2','scan',1780048749);
