INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('tic_dp1b','TIC-DP1B.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/TIC-DP1B.LHA','drewlpage','XIM','LE-win5-96.exe',NULL,NULL,'TIC','|  ______________   _______  |   |     THe | | /   ____   \___) /       \ | --O-- iNNeR | | \__/   .\__/  .|/    /___/ |   |    CoRe |',replace('.----------------------------.-------------.\n|  ______________   _______  |   |     THe |\n| /   ____   \___) /       \ | --O-- iNNeR |\n| \__/   .\__/  .|/    /___/ |   |    CoRe |\n|   |     || |  ||    /   /  | iNNoVaTioNS |\n|   |______| |___|_______/   |             |\n|                            |  PReSeNTS:  |\n)----------------------------^-------------(\n| DReWLPaGe V1.1B - /X FuLLSCReeN CHaTTeR! |\n|             THe BeST THeRe iS            |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'DrewlPage.Guide',replace('@DATABASE "Drewl-Page Release 1.1B Documentation"\012\012@NODE MAIN "Drewl-Page Release 1.1B Documentation"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                              Drewl-Page V1.1B                              |\012 |                  An Ami-Express V4.xx+ FullScreen-Chatter                  |\012 |                                                                            |\012 |                 CopyRight 1996 THe iNNeR CoRe iNNoVaTioNS!                 |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012\012             @{" Introduction      " Link INTRODUCTION} - Requirements, operation etc.\012             @{" Disclaimer        " Link DISCLAIMER} - Just read it\012             @{" Installation      " Link INSTALLATION} - How to install the system.\012             @{" Program Usage     " Link PROGRAM} - BBSCommand Installation\012             @{" Configuration     " Link CONFIG} - Example Configuration Files\012             @{" History           " Link HISTORY} - Version changes of Drewl-Page\012             @{" Future Versions   " Link FUTURE} - What will come in future versions?\012             @{" License           " Link LICENSE} - License agreement.\012             @{" Registration      " Link REG} - How to register.\012             @{" Special thanks    " Link THANX} - Thanks to these people...\012             @{" If there are bugs " Link BUGS} - Where to send your bugreports.\012\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE INTRODUCTION "Introduction"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                       Drewl-Page Introduction.                             |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012      Drewl-Page is an Ami-Express Full-Screen-Chatter Door.\012\012\012  Requirements:\012  -------------\012\012  o AmigaDOS 2.04 or higher.\012  o Ami-Express V4.x\012\012\012  Tested On:\012  -------------\012  Amiga  500/020/14      -  The iNNeR CoRe -  Sysop: Stingray\012  Amiga 2000/030/882/40  -  The iNNeR CoRe\012  Amiga 4000/030/882/25  -  The iNNeR CoRe\012\012  Operation:\012  -------------\012\012  o You can turn DrewlPage On/Off simply by toggling the internal\012    chat-control, or when you had installed ChatPage before, you can also\012    use the utils PageStat & PageEnv ((C) Ron Klinkien Used By CHATPAGE\012    (The FSC For Xenolink Pro) for turning the chat on/off. At this point\012    DrewlPage does nog recognize the several statustexts that these utils\012    write in env:chatstatus, but it will only see if the chat really is ON\012    or OFF (which should be more than enough anyway).\012  o DrewlPage uses Gadtools for it''s gui. The gui has an IGNORE button as\012    well as a FULLCHAT button. When the IGNORE button is pressed the gui will\012    disappear and sound will be turned off. The user won''t notice that\012    you''ve pressed the button since the socalled ''calling'' will continue on\012    his end. The user has 3 tries to call you in 1 session. When IGNORE has\012    been pressed at the first call, the gui will not even appear at the\012    second and/or third call.\012  o DrewlPage has been equiped with a fullscreen chatter which has a wordwrap\012    routine in it.\012  o DrewlPage is able to use the PREFS for it''s sampleplaying, but you can\012    also use your own sampleplayer if you wish. Please look at the\012    example-config in this guide how to use it.\012  o DrewlPage will create a directory in DOORS:DREWLPAGE. In that directory,\012    DrewlPage will place a logfile with info about who has paged you (and if\012    the chat was activated by you, it''ll also show the chatreason and HOW\012    long you''ve been chatting with the user). The log will have some\012    identification characters like |,#,[,],*,etcetc. So if you would like\012    to build a logscanner for who has been chatting the most with you, be\012    my guest. \012  o DrewlPage also keeps track of a capture-logfile so you can read back the\012    entire chatsession. If you wish to delete those files then just do so.\012    If DrewlPage sees (when chat is activated) that the current users logfile\012    doesn''t exist, it will simply create one.\012  o When sysop is unavailable (eg chat is OFF or sysop just hasn''t answered\012    it), a socalled TIMECOMMENT can be shown (look at the configuration\012    part). You are allowed to change the comments to your ''needs'' but\012    please don''t make them longer than 3 lines since cursorpositioning is\012    used in the chatter and it could screw up your entire screen. If you\012    don''t want to use these timecomments, then simply remove/rename the\012    config and they''re gone.\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE DISCLAIMER "Disclaimer"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                                 Disclaimer                                 |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012         No  warranty,  either express or implied, is made with respect\012                         to the fitness of Drewl-Page.\012\012  THe iNNeR CoRe iNNoVaTioNS (referred to as "the author"), reserves the right\012               to not develop any future versions of Drewl-Page.\012\012         The author will try to make a good faith attempt at correcting\012       any problems if any are discovered, but is in no way required, nor\012                             bound to correct them.\012\012         The author neither assumes nor accepts any responsibility for\012         the use or misuse of these programs. He also will not be held\012         liable for damages due to loss of profit or any other damages\012          arising out of the use, or inability to use these programs.\012\012  THe iNNeR CoRe iNNoVaTioNS will not be liable for any damage arising from\012         the  failure of these programs to perform as described, or any\012           destruction of other programs or data residing on a system\012          attempting to run the programs. While I know of no damaging\012       errors, the user of these programs uses it at his or her own risk.\012\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE INSTALLATION "Installation"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                       Drewl-Page Installation.                             |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012 Software Installation:\012 ------------------------\012\012 Doors (dir)\012       DrewlPage (dir)\012                 DrewlPage              40044 bytes\012                 Config (dir)\012                      DrewlPage.Cfg       613 Bytes\012                      Times.Cfg          2296 Bytes\012\012 Please do *NOT* change this directory structure since these paths are\012 hardcoded !!\012\012\012 BBSCommand Installation:\012 ------------------------\012 Use the following tooltypes:\012\012  ACCESS    = 010\012  LOCATION  = Doors:DrewlPage/DrewlPage\012  MULTINODE = YES\012  TYPE      = XIM\012  STACK     = 4096\012  NAME      = DReWLPaGe V1.1B\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE PROGRAM "Program Usage"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                               Program Usage                                |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012   To see the commandline just run the door in the CLI.. You should be shown\012                                this output....:\012\012   DReWLPaGe V1.1B (c)1996 THe iNNeR CoRe iNNoVaTioNS\012\012   This is a XIM door for Ami-Express V4.xx Professional BulletinBoard System\012\012   Use the following tooltypes in BBS:Commands/BBSCMD/O.info:\012\012   ACCESS    = 010\012   LOCATION  = Doors:DrewlPage/DrewlPage\012   MULTINODE = YES\012   TYPE      = XIM\012   STACK     = 4096\012   NAME      = DReWLPaGe V1.1B\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE CONFIG "External Configuration Files"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                      Drewl-Page Configuration Files.                       |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012 Doors:DrewlPage/Config/Drewlpage.Cfg\012 ---CUT---\012 BeepPause         20         ; The no. of ticks (50th of a sec) between Beeps\012 UserColor          3         ; Color of Text typed by User\012 SysOpColor         7         ; Color of Text typed by SysOp\012 Sample             Hear s:samples/sysop3.iff\012                              ; Which sample do you wish to use..\012                              ; PREFS - Use The WB/Prefs SOUND Util.\012                              ; OR use a commandline like:\012                              ; DSound -2 -m -w -o S:Samples/Sysop3.IFF\012 ---CUT---\012\012\012 Doors:DrewlPage/Config/Times.Cfg\012 ---CUT---\012 00 I''m Sorry!\012 00 The Sysop Can''t Be Reached Right Now.\012 00 Please Try Again Later This Morning.\012 01 Hmm, The Sysop Isn''t Replying...\012 01 Gee, Ya Know, Some People Have To Get To Work At 7:30AM\012 01 Please Do Not Disturb....\012 02 Jemig De Pemig, Mozes Kribbel!@$#!! It''s Two O''Clock!\012 02 I''ll Bet $100,- On It That The Sysop Is Laying In Bed,\012 02 ....Asleep! (Do YOU believe It ?? I Don''t..)\012 03 Are You Nuts?  Yelling At This Hour!\012 03\012 03 Wait For The Sunrise, And Try Again.\012 04 No, No, No, NO! I Will NOT Yell The Sysop For You!\012 04\012 04 Maybe It''s Time To Get Your Watch Repaired?!\012 05 U-Huh! It''s Too Early In The Morning.\012 05\012 05 I Can''t Reach Him Right Now.\012 06 The Sysop Is Delivering The Mail Now,\012 06 To Affort This BBS.. ;-((\012 06 Please Try Again Later Today.\012 07 Maybe The Sun Is Already Up....\012 07\012 07 But The Sysop Isn''t!\012 08 GoodMorning.\012 08 The Sysop Is In The BathRoom, I Guess..\012 08 Try Again Later Today...\012 09 Some People Have To Work You Know!\012 09\012 09 Please Try Again Later Today.\012 10 The Sysop Has Already Gone To Work.\012 10\012 10 Please Try Again Later Today.\012 11 The Sysop Is Watching A Movie On FilmNet+.\012 11\012 11 Please Try Again Later Today.\012 12 The Sysop Went Out For Lunch With His Girl.\012 12\012 12 Bon Appetit!\012 13 The Sysop Hasn''t Finished His Lunch Yet...\012 13 Please Try Again Later Today,\012 13 Or You Can Leave Him A Message.\012 14 The Sysop Went To Work.\012 14 That Is If He Hasn''t Been Fired Yet !\012 14 Please Try Again Later Today.\012 15 The Sysop Is Trying To Make Some Coffee...\012 15 If The BBS Is Down Soon, You''ll Know It Failed\012 15 Please Do Not Disturb And Let Him Die In Peace...\012 16 The Sysop Is Out With His FOUR Dogs.\012 16\012 16 Please Try Again Later Today.\012 17 The Sysop Is Currently In Bed...\012 17 His GIRLFRIEND Screams Too Loud! He Doesn''t Hear You!\012 17 Please Try Again Later Today.\012 18 The Sysop Is Throwing Up His Diner Above The Toilet.\012 18 His Mom Can''t Cook, You Know !!\012 18 Please Try Again Later Tonight...\012 19 The Sysop Is Probably Watching FilmNet(Plus)...\012 19 So, Why Don''t You Stroll Around A Bit,\012 19 You Can Try Again Later Tonight...\012 20 I Can''t Find Don Anywhere!!\012 20\012 20 Please Try Again Later Tonight.\012 21 Sorry, It Seems That Don Isn''t Home..\012 21\012 21 Please Try Again Later Tonight.\012 22 Sorry, The Sysop Went To Bed Early Today ;-))\012 22 (With His Girl Ofcourse)\012 22 Well, Ehr... You Know What''s Going On\012 23 The Sysop Is Sleeping Right Now!\012 23 He Probably Has To Get Up Early... (B^)\012 23 You Can Leave A Message If You Want.\012 ---CUT---\012\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE HISTORY "History"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                          Drewl-Page History                                |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012DrewlPage V1.1B:\012[Added]		- DrewlPage will now also log to the callerslog so that\012		  (for instance) SAmilog will know that someone has paged.\012[Fixed]		- Found a bug in the FSC. When a full line (no spaces in it)\012		  was entered, the line would not be written to the\012		  capturelog.\012[Added]		- It''s now possible to use your own samples through an\012		  external sampleplayer.\012\012DrewlPage V1.1A:\012		- Removed another error from the exitline. When answering\012		  NO at the exit request, the chatcolour turned to red\012		  instead of the configured chatcolour.\012		- Added a gui. Ignore & fullchat buttons available. No\012		  explanation needed I think.\012\012DrewlPage V1.0H:\012		- Changed the exitline (again). At first the ''/'' was displayed\012		  before the actual exitline was given. Now that ''/'' has been\012		  removed. A ''/'' will only be displayed now when it''s NOT\012		  the first character.\012		- Added CaptureLog. Now each user has his own logfile of\012		  the previous ( & ofcourse the current) chatsession. Easy\012		  to look back if you want to know what your last chat was\012		  all about.\012\012DrewlPage V1.0G:\012		- Added several nodestatus-functions. When Paging it will be\012		  "REQUESTING CHAT" and when chatting in the FSC it will be\012		  "CHATTING WITH THE SYSOP".\012\012DrewlPage V1.0F:\012		- Adjusted some routines (read Clean-Up). This caused the\012		  exe to be about 5k smaller.\012		- Removed a bug with reading the main config. The chatter\012		  would go crazy when one of the options was missing in the\012		  config ''cause it didn''t know what value to use. Now each\012		  option is DOUBLE checked if it''s available. If it''s not,\012		  it''ll get a default value.\012		- Changed The Time/Date loop. At First they were requested\012		  several times. Now that had changed to 2 times max.\012		- Bug removed when exiting FSC. When you were in the chat and\012		  midnight passed, the time-in-chat calculation failed. Gave\012		  a VERY negative number. Should be fixed now.\012		- Fixed a bug concerning the time.config. I forgot to check\012		  for a \n (newline) and so a Blank-line would never be\012		  printed if you only had a line with the hour-number.\012		- Added a callerlog. This log will contain info concerning\012		  if the chatstatus is ON/OFF, WHO paged the sysop and WHEN\012		  and when the fullchatter has been activated, it will also\012		  show in the logfile how long that chatsession took.\012\012DrewlPage V1.0E:\012		- Changed the routine for retrieving the time/date. Wasn''t\012		  done in the best way, so could result into a guru once in\012		  a while. Fixed !!\012		- Removed a bug in the exit-line of the FSC. When / was\012		  pressed and answer was NO, then the color in the FSC was\012		  changed to RED instead of the colors supplied in the\012		  config.\012		- Added a minor thing in the FSC exit-line. Now you can see\012		  how long you''ve been chatting with the current user.\012		- Changed the intro-logo when entering the FSC. The layout\012		  was too un-compatible with the rest of the pager.\012\012DrewlPage V1.0D:\012		- Bug Removed. It seems when running DrewlPage in ascii mode,\012		  /X would not remove ALL ansi-colors. Now I added a complete\012		  NEW routine for printing the ansi-colors in ascii mode.\012		  Should work fine.\012\012DrewlPage V1.0C:\012		- The UserColor and sysopcolor are now configurable. Colors\012		  are from 0-7 (0=ESC[30m, 3=ESC[33m 5=ESC[35m etcetc).\012		- Time between two beeps now configurable. Default is 20.\012		- Added a 2nd config which contains hourly comments. These\012		  comment can be changed into whatever you like, but MAXIMUM\012		  length is 74 characters. If you don''t want these comments,\012		  then simply rename or delete the config and they are gone.\012		  If you DO use the time-comments, make sure you do NOT use\012		  MORE than 6-7 Lines ''cause otherwise the time-comment-logo\012		  could get into a conflict with the return prompt (which is\012		  set at line 23).\012		- Added a cls-routine for when a user pages 1 second time in\012		  thesame session. Now the logo with the time-comment is\012		  cleared BEFORE paging the second/third time.\012		- Added a new variable to disable the cursorkeys. In earlier\012		  betaversions, they weren''t disabled, but they screwed up\012		  the FSC when they were used.\012\012DrewlPage V1.0B:\012		- Removed a bug. When a backspace was pressed at the first\012		  character, it was possible to erase the name of the person\012		  who was writing at the moment.\012		- Removed a bug concerning the wordwrap and (again) the\012		  backspace-key. It seems that when counting characters, the\012		  backspace was seen as a ADDED character instead of a\012		  substracted one. Therefor the wordwrap was invoked on an\012		  earlier moment when a backspace was pressed during the\012		  sentence.\012		- Added some information in the door. Now when you try to\012		  start the door from the shell, the ADVISEABLE menucommand\012		  will be printed. Please DO use this commandline (specificly\012		  the PATH) ''cause another door (WhoIsOn) checks for certain\012		  paths and it won''t recognize the door otherwise.\012		- Changed the exit line in the full screen chatter. At first\012		  when you pressed the ''/'' , the exitline appeared (as it''s\012		  supposed to), BUT when you pressed NO as an answer, the\012		  current writer switched to the other on (so user > sysop\012		  or the other way around). Now the name WON''T switch AND\012		  added a new CLS routine for clearing the exit-prompt.\012\012DrewlPage V1.0A:\012		- Added Chatstatus. DrewlPage now checks if chatmode is\012		  on/off. It checks the env: dir for a file called CHATSTATUS,\012		  so the util PAGESTAT ( (c) Ron Klinkien) CAN be used to\012		  control the status of this pager. It''s also possible to\012		  use the internal chat on/off from Xenolink. Just make sure\012		  that there''s no file called ENV:CHATSTATUS available.\012		- Added a full screen chatter.\012		- Added an intrologo when entering chatmode. The logo\012		  contains minor information like user''s location, time/date,\012		  accesslevel and xenolinknode.\012		- Added an option that a user can page MAXIMUM 3 times when\012		  the door has been started.\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE FUTURE "Future Versions"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                              Future Versions                               |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012    For now I''m not even sure if there will come another version. Depends if\012  there''s a use for it, BUT if there is, then there are some things that MIGHT\012                                be implemented.\012\012  o Macro-support\012  o Configurable screens\012  o A blacklist.\012  o An external util to display an own made text instead of a time-comment.\012\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE LICENSE "License"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                                  License                                   |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012       There is NO WARRANTY for the programs, to the extent permitted by\012     applicable law. Except when otherwise stated in writing the copyright\012   holders and/or other parties provide the programs "AS IS" without warranty\012    of any kind, either expressed or implied, including, but not limited to,\012     the implied warranties of merchantability and fitness for a particular\012   purpose. The entire risk as to the quality and performance of the programs\012    is with you. Should the programs prove defective, you assume the cost of\012                 all necessary servicing, repair or correction.\012\012   In no event unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing will\012   any copyright holder, or any other party who may redistribute the programs\012   as permitted above, be liable to you for ddamages, including any general,\012     special, incidental or consequential damages arising out of the use or\012    inability to use the programs (including but not limited to loss of data\012    or data being rendered inaccurate or losses sustained by you or a third\012   parties or a failure of the programs to operate with any other programs),\012   even if such holder or other party had been advised of the possibility of\012                                 such damages.\012\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE REG "Registration"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                             How To Register...                             |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012   Simple... There isn''t any.. We don''t ask for any fee whatsoever since Xeno\012         has already costed us a lot of money so this baby is for free.\012\012  HOWEVER !! If you decide to use this chatter, then please send me a message\012   that you do so. In that way I can see if there really is a use for further\012                           development on this door.\012\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE THANX "Special Thanx"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                  Special Thnx to the people listed below                   |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012    - Joseph Hodge for Ami-Express (Still works the best).\012    - Brian Kernighan & Dennis M. Ritchie for the C language!!\012    - Commodore Amiga for the computer.\012    - P0T-NooDLe for his ansi''s\012      Personal message to P0T: I know I didn''t ask ya if I could use your\012                               screens, but they really look great. Hope\012                               you don''t mind.....\012    - Alf for being somekind of a teacher to me.\012    - Roelof Jansen for sharing some tips & tricks.\012    - DJ. PiNSCHeR for his sometimes unusual ideas & betatesting.\012    - CRaM for his great help with the gui.\012    - XeNoN for sharing ideas & betatesting.\012\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE BUGS "If there are any bugs"\012\012                         __________  _____    _______/\_\012    :                   /   ____   \/  |  \  /  ____   /                   :\012  --+-------------------\__/   .\__/   |   \/  __/_\ //--------------------+--\012    |      SYSoP:         |     ||/   -+-  \\_      \/\      CoSYSoP:      |\012    |     STiNGRaY        |______|     |_____/________/     RoTeNTRaaG     |\012    |                           \______|                      DDaZZ        |\012   _|_  ______________________/\_______      _____________________  _______|/\\012  (___)/       \       \ ____   /____  \    /       \       \___  \/  ____   /\012  |  .|    /   /   /   /__/_\ // ___/   \  /    /___/   /   /__/   \ __/_\ //\012  |  ||   /   /   /   /      \/\ \_______)/    /   /   /   / \______)     \/\\012  |___|__/___/___/___/_________/    |   \ \_______/_______/    |   \________/\012  --+------------------------|______|    \_--------------|_____|    \_-----+--\012    :                               |_____/                    |_____/     :\012    .----------------------------------------------------------------------.\012    | RuNNiNG oN a2000/030/882 40MHZ 11MeGZ RaM  2.3GB HD aT YouR DiSPoSaL |\012    |      CoNNeCTRaTeS 2400 uPTo 28K8V34 uSiNG a TRoN DF 28K8 ToWeR       |\012    |                                                                      |\012    |                     oPeN 24HRZ/DaY - 7 DaYZ/WeeK                     |\012    `----[NoDe1: +31-10-420-0033 28K8]----[NoDe2: +31-10-RiNGDoWN 14K4]----''\012\012   .----------------.------------------.------------------.-----------------.\012   | THe iNNeR CoRe | NLa 14:101/202.9 | eRo 68:315/207.9 | Di 11:100/101.9 |\012   | +31-10-4200033 | FiDo 2:286/517.9 | LDY 69:100/101.9 )-----------------(\012   |  No NuP/SYSPW  | aMy 39:153/207.9 | e-MaiL [email removed]    |\012   `----------------^------------------^----^-------------------------------''\012\012   For bugreports and/or suggestions you can contact me at the above networks\012   or you can call the THe iNNeR CoRe SupportBBS directly at the above number\012\012@ENDNODE\012','\012',char(10)),'{"ACCESS":"010","LOCATION":"Doors:DrewlPage/DrewlPage","TYPE":"XIM","STACK":"4096"}','auto-added',61507,5,0,NULL,NULL,'tic_dp1b','scan',1780048780);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('tic_dp1c','TIC-DP1C.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/TIC-DP1C.LHA','DReWLPaGe','XIM','DReWLPaGe',NULL,NULL,'TIC','|  ______________   _______  |   |     THe | | /   ____   \___) /       \ | --O-- iNNeR | | \__/   .\__/  .|/    /___/ |   |    CoRe |',replace('.----------------------------.-------------.\n|  ______________   _______  |   |     THe |\n| /   ____   \___) /       \ | --O-- iNNeR |\n| \__/   .\__/  .|/    /___/ |   |    CoRe |\n|   |     || |  ||    /   /  | iNNoVaTioNS |\n|   |______| |___|_______/   |             |\n|                            |  PReSeNTS:  |\n)----------------------------^-------------(\n| DReWLPaGe V1.1C - /X FuLLSCReeN CHaTTeR! |\n|             THe BeST THeRe iS            |\n`------------------------------------------''\n     BUY A TICKET AND FLY WITH [31mTOPGUN[0m\n','\n',char(10)),'DrewlPage.Guide',replace('@DATABASE "Drewl-Page Release 1.1C Documentation"\012\012@NODE MAIN "Drewl-Page Release 1.1C Documentation"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                              Drewl-Page V1.1C                              |\012 |                  An Ami-Express V4.xx+ FullScreen-Chatter                  |\012 |                                                                            |\012 |                 CopyRight 1996 THe iNNeR CoRe iNNoVaTioNS!                 |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012\012             @{" Introduction      " Link INTRODUCTION} - Requirements, operation etc.\012             @{" Disclaimer        " Link DISCLAIMER} - Just read it\012             @{" Installation      " Link INSTALLATION} - How to install the system.\012             @{" Program Usage     " Link PROGRAM} - BBSCommand Installation\012             @{" Configuration     " Link CONFIG} - Example Configuration Files\012             @{" History           " Link HISTORY} - Version changes of Drewl-Page\012             @{" Future Versions   " Link FUTURE} - What will come in future versions?\012             @{" License           " Link LICENSE} - License agreement.\012             @{" Registration      " Link REG} - How to register.\012             @{" Special thanks    " Link THANX} - Thanks to these people...\012             @{" If there are bugs " Link BUGS} - Where to send your bugreports.\012\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE INTRODUCTION "Introduction"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                       Drewl-Page Introduction.                             |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012      Drewl-Page is an Ami-Express Full-Screen-Chatter Door.\012\012\012  Requirements:\012  -------------\012\012  o AmigaDOS 2.04 or higher.\012  o Ami-Express V4.x\012\012\012  Tested On:\012  -------------\012  Amiga  500/020/14      -  The iNNeR CoRe -  Sysop: Stingray\012  Amiga 2000/030/882/40  -  The iNNeR CoRe\012  Amiga 4000/030/882/25  -  The iNNeR CoRe\012\012  Operation:\012  -------------\012\012  o You can turn DrewlPage On/Off simply by toggling the internal\012    chat-control, or when you had installed ChatPage before, you can also\012    use the utils PageStat & PageEnv ((C) Ron Klinkien Used By CHATPAGE\012    (The FSC For Xenolink Pro) for turning the chat on/off. At this point\012    DrewlPage does nog recognize the several statustexts that these utils\012    write in env:chatstatus, but it will only see if the chat really is ON\012    or OFF (which should be more than enough anyway).\012  o DrewlPage uses Gadtools for it''s gui. The gui has an IGNORE button as\012    well as a FULLCHAT button. When the IGNORE button is pressed the gui will\012    disappear and sound will be turned off. The user won''t notice that\012    you''ve pressed the button since the socalled ''calling'' will continue on\012    his end. The user has 3 tries to call you in 1 session. When IGNORE has\012    been pressed at the first call, the gui will not even appear at the\012    second and/or third call.\012  o DrewlPage has been equiped with a fullscreen chatter which has a wordwrap\012    routine in it.\012  o DrewlPage is able to use the PREFS for it''s sampleplaying, but you can\012    also use your own sampleplayer if you wish. Please look at the\012    example-config in this guide how to use it.\012  o DrewlPage will create a directory in DOORS:DREWLPAGE. In that directory,\012    DrewlPage will place a logfile with info about who has paged you (and if\012    the chat was activated by you, it''ll also show the chatreason and HOW\012    long you''ve been chatting with the user). The log will have some\012    identification characters like |,#,[,],*,etcetc. So if you would like\012    to build a logscanner for who has been chatting the most with you, be\012    my guest. \012  o DrewlPage also keeps track of a capture-logfile so you can read back the\012    entire chatsession. If you wish to delete those files then just do so.\012    If DrewlPage sees (when chat is activated) that the current users logfile\012    doesn''t exist, it will simply create one.\012  o When sysop is unavailable (eg chat is OFF or sysop just hasn''t answered\012    it), a socalled TIMECOMMENT can be shown (look at the configuration\012    part). You are allowed to change the comments to your ''needs'' but\012    please don''t make them longer than 3 lines since cursorpositioning is\012    used in the chatter and it could screw up your entire screen. If you\012    don''t want to use these timecomments, then simply remove/rename the\012    config and they''re gone.\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE DISCLAIMER "Disclaimer"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                                 Disclaimer                                 |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012         No  warranty,  either express or implied, is made with respect\012                         to the fitness of Drewl-Page.\012\012  THe iNNeR CoRe iNNoVaTioNS (referred to as "the author"), reserves the right\012               to not develop any future versions of Drewl-Page.\012\012         The author will try to make a good faith attempt at correcting\012       any problems if any are discovered, but is in no way required, nor\012                             bound to correct them.\012\012         The author neither assumes nor accepts any responsibility for\012         the use or misuse of these programs. He also will not be held\012         liable for damages due to loss of profit or any other damages\012          arising out of the use, or inability to use these programs.\012\012  THe iNNeR CoRe iNNoVaTioNS will not be liable for any damage arising from\012         the  failure of these programs to perform as described, or any\012           destruction of other programs or data residing on a system\012          attempting to run the programs. While I know of no damaging\012       errors, the user of these programs uses it at his or her own risk.\012\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE INSTALLATION "Installation"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                       Drewl-Page Installation.                             |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012 Software Installation:\012 ------------------------\012\012 Doors (dir)\012       DrewlPage (dir)\012                 DrewlPage              40040 bytes\012                 Config (dir)\012                      DrewlPage.Cfg       613 Bytes\012                      Times.Cfg          2296 Bytes\012\012 Please do *NOT* change this directory structure since these paths are\012 hardcoded !!\012\012\012 BBSCommand Installation:\012 ------------------------\012 Use the following tooltypes:\012\012  ACCESS    = 010\012  LOCATION  = Doors:DrewlPage/DrewlPage\012  MULTINODE = YES\012  TYPE      = XIM\012  STACK     = 4096\012  NAME      = DReWLPaGe V1.1C\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE PROGRAM "Program Usage"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                               Program Usage                                |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012   To see the commandline just run the door in the CLI.. You should be shown\012                                this output....:\012\012   DReWLPaGe V1.1C (c)1996 THe iNNeR CoRe iNNoVaTioNS\012\012   This is a XIM door for Ami-Express V4.xx Professional BulletinBoard System\012\012   Use the following tooltypes in BBS:Commands/BBSCMD/O.info:\012\012   ACCESS    = 010\012   LOCATION  = Doors:DrewlPage/DrewlPage\012   MULTINODE = YES\012   TYPE      = XIM\012   STACK     = 4096\012   NAME      = DReWLPaGe V1.1C\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE CONFIG "External Configuration Files"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                      Drewl-Page Configuration Files.                       |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012 Doors:DrewlPage/Config/Drewlpage.Cfg\012 ---CUT---\012 BeepPause         20         ; The no. of ticks (50th of a sec) between Beeps\012 UserColor          3         ; Color of Text typed by User\012 SysOpColor         7         ; Color of Text typed by SysOp\012 Sample             Hear s:samples/sysop3.iff\012                              ; Which sample do you wish to use..\012                              ; PREFS - Use The WB/Prefs SOUND Util.\012                              ; OR use a commandline like:\012                              ; DSound -2 -m -w -o S:Samples/Sysop3.IFF\012 ---CUT---\012\012\012 Doors:DrewlPage/Config/Times.Cfg\012 ---CUT---\012 00 I''m Sorry!\012 00 The Sysop Can''t Be Reached Right Now.\012 00 Please Try Again Later This Morning.\012 01 Hmm, The Sysop Isn''t Replying...\012 01 Gee, Ya Know, Some People Have To Get To Work At 7:30AM\012 01 Please Do Not Disturb....\012 02 Jemig De Pemig, Mozes Kribbel!@$#!! It''s Two O''Clock!\012 02 I''ll Bet $100,- On It That The Sysop Is Laying In Bed,\012 02 ....Asleep! (Do YOU believe It ?? I Don''t..)\012 03 Are You Nuts?  Yelling At This Hour!\012 03\012 03 Wait For The Sunrise, And Try Again.\012 04 No, No, No, NO! I Will NOT Yell The Sysop For You!\012 04\012 04 Maybe It''s Time To Get Your Watch Repaired?!\012 05 U-Huh! It''s Too Early In The Morning.\012 05\012 05 I Can''t Reach Him Right Now.\012 06 The Sysop Is Delivering The Mail Now,\012 06 To Affort This BBS.. ;-((\012 06 Please Try Again Later Today.\012 07 Maybe The Sun Is Already Up....\012 07\012 07 But The Sysop Isn''t!\012 08 GoodMorning.\012 08 The Sysop Is In The BathRoom, I Guess..\012 08 Try Again Later Today...\012 09 Some People Have To Work You Know!\012 09\012 09 Please Try Again Later Today.\012 10 The Sysop Has Already Gone To Work.\012 10\012 10 Please Try Again Later Today.\012 11 The Sysop Is Watching A Movie On FilmNet+.\012 11\012 11 Please Try Again Later Today.\012 12 The Sysop Went Out For Lunch With His Girl.\012 12\012 12 Bon Appetit!\012 13 The Sysop Hasn''t Finished His Lunch Yet...\012 13 Please Try Again Later Today,\012 13 Or You Can Leave Him A Message.\012 14 The Sysop Went To Work.\012 14 That Is If He Hasn''t Been Fired Yet !\012 14 Please Try Again Later Today.\012 15 The Sysop Is Trying To Make Some Coffee...\012 15 If The BBS Is Down Soon, You''ll Know It Failed\012 15 Please Do Not Disturb And Let Him Die In Peace...\012 16 The Sysop Is Out With His FOUR Dogs.\012 16\012 16 Please Try Again Later Today.\012 17 The Sysop Is Currently In Bed...\012 17 His GIRLFRIEND Screams Too Loud! He Doesn''t Hear You!\012 17 Please Try Again Later Today.\012 18 The Sysop Is Throwing Up His Diner Above The Toilet.\012 18 His Mom Can''t Cook, You Know !!\012 18 Please Try Again Later Tonight...\012 19 The Sysop Is Probably Watching FilmNet(Plus)...\012 19 So, Why Don''t You Stroll Around A Bit,\012 19 You Can Try Again Later Tonight...\012 20 I Can''t Find Don Anywhere!!\012 20\012 20 Please Try Again Later Tonight.\012 21 Sorry, It Seems That Don Isn''t Home..\012 21\012 21 Please Try Again Later Tonight.\012 22 Sorry, The Sysop Went To Bed Early Today ;-))\012 22 (With His Girl Ofcourse)\012 22 Well, Ehr... You Know What''s Going On\012 23 The Sysop Is Sleeping Right Now!\012 23 He Probably Has To Get Up Early... (B^)\012 23 You Can Leave A Message If You Want.\012 ---CUT---\012\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE HISTORY "History"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                          Drewl-Page History                                |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012DrewlPage V1.1C:\012[Fixed]		- After adding the support to allow users with names starting\012		  with THE (etcetc), I encountered a bug when it was the\012		  other one''s turn.. Seems a part of the previous typed\012		  line would be removed on the screen (not in the log)..\012		  Changed some linefeeds & ansi-cursorcodes so now it''s\012		  gone.\012[Report][Fixed]	- Was informed that the comment option fucked up the entire\012		  screen. Added an ansi-cursor-code so the TO: etcetc will\012		  be placed UNDER the timecomment.\012[Report][Fixed]	- Report came in about some dudes who have a handle\012		  starting with ''THE'' .. so in the chatter his prompt would\012		  be THE> .. Now changed.. The chatter will scan the first\012		  four characters for a space.. if there''s one found, the\012		  entire username/handle will be printed. Otherwise only\012		  the first word (so until the space occures).\012\012DrewlPage V1.1B:\012[Added]		- DrewlPage will now also log to the callerslog so that\012		  (for instance) SAmilog will know that someone has paged.\012[Fixed]		- Found a bug in the FSC. When a full line (no spaces in it)\012		  was entered, the line would not be written to the\012		  capturelog.\012[Added]		- It''s now possible to use your own samples through an\012		  external sampleplayer.\012\012DrewlPage V1.1A:\012[Fixed]		- Removed another error from the exitline. When answering\012		  NO at the exit request, the chatcolour turned to red\012		  instead of the configured chatcolour.\012[Added]		- Added a gui. Ignore & fullchat buttons available. No\012		  explanation needed I think.\012\012DrewlPage V1.0H:\012[Added/Fixed]	- Changed the exitline (again). At first the ''/'' was displayed\012		  before the actual exitline was given. Now that ''/'' has been\012		  removed. A ''/'' will only be displayed now when it''s NOT\012		  the first character.\012[Added]		- Added CaptureLog. Now each user has his own logfile of\012		  the previous ( & ofcourse the current) chatsession. Easy\012		  to look back if you want to know what your last chat was\012		  all about.\012\012DrewlPage V1.0G:\012[Added]		- Added several nodestatus-functions. When Paging it will be\012		  "REQUESTING CHAT" and when chatting in the FSC it will be\012		  "CHATTING WITH THE SYSOP".\012\012DrewlPage V1.0F:\012[Added/Fixed]	- Adjusted some routines (read Clean-Up). This caused the\012		  exe to be about 5k smaller.\012[Fixed]		- Removed a bug with reading the main config. The chatter\012		  would go crazy when one of the options was missing in the\012		  config ''cause it didn''t know what value to use. Now each\012		  option is DOUBLE checked if it''s available. If it''s not,\012		  it''ll get a default value.\012[Added]Fixed]	- Changed The Time/Date loop. At First they were requested\012		  several times. Now that had changed to 2 times max.\012[Fixed]		- Bug removed when exiting FSC. When you were in the chat and\012		  midnight passed, the time-in-chat calculation failed. Gave\012		  a VERY negative number. Should be fixed now.\012[Fixed]		- Fixed a bug concerning the time.config. I forgot to check\012		  for a \n (newline) and so a Blank-line would never be\012		  printed if you only had a line with the hour-number.\012[Added]		- Added a callerlog. This log will contain info concerning\012		  if the chatstatus is ON/OFF, WHO paged the sysop and WHEN\012		  and when the fullchatter has been activated, it will also\012		  show in the logfile how long that chatsession took.\012\012DrewlPage V1.0E:\012[Fixed]		- Changed the routine for retrieving the time/date. Wasn''t\012		  done in the best way, so could result into a guru once in\012		  a while. Fixed !!\012[Fixed]		- Removed a bug in the exit-line of the FSC. When / was\012		  pressed and answer was NO, then the color in the FSC was\012		  changed to RED instead of the colors supplied in the\012		  config.\012[Added]		- Added a minor thing in the FSC exit-line. Now you can see\012		  how long you''ve been chatting with the current user.\012[Added/Fixed]	- Changed the intro-logo when entering the FSC. The layout\012		  was too un-compatible with the rest of the pager.\012\012DrewlPage V1.0D:\012[Fixed]		- Bug Removed. It seems when running DrewlPage in ascii mode,\012		  /X would not remove ALL ansi-colors. Now I added a complete\012		  NEW routine for printing the ansi-colors in ascii mode.\012		  Should work fine.\012\012DrewlPage V1.0C:\012[Added]		- The UserColor and sysopcolor are now configurable. Colors\012		  are from 0-7 (0=ESC[30m, 3=ESC[33m 5=ESC[35m etcetc).\012[Added]		- Time between two beeps now configurable. Default is 20.\012[Added]		- Added a 2nd config which contains hourly comments. These\012		  comment can be changed into whatever you like, but MAXIMUM\012		  length is 74 characters. If you don''t want these comments,\012		  then simply rename or delete the config and they are gone.\012		  If you DO use the time-comments, make sure you do NOT use\012		  MORE than 6-7 Lines ''cause otherwise the time-comment-logo\012		  could get into a conflict with the return prompt (which is\012		  set at line 23).\012[Added]		- Added a cls-routine for when a user pages 1 second time in\012		  thesame session. Now the logo with the time-comment is\012		  cleared BEFORE paging the second/third time.\012\012DrewlPage V1.0B:\012[Fixed]		- Removed a bug. When a backspace was pressed at the first\012		  character, it was possible to erase the name of the person\012		  who was writing at the moment.\012[Fixed]		- Removed a bug concerning the wordwrap and (again) the\012		  backspace-key. It seems that when counting characters, the\012		  backspace was seen as a ADDED character instead of a\012		  substracted one. Therefor the wordwrap was invoked on an\012		  earlier moment when a backspace was pressed during the\012		  sentence.\012[Added]		- Added some information in the door. Now when you try to\012		  start the door from the shell, the ADVISEABLE menucommand\012		  will be printed. Please DO use this commandline (specificly\012		  the PATH) ''cause another door (WhoIsOn) checks for certain\012		  paths and it won''t recognize the door otherwise.\012[Fixed]		- Changed the exit line in the full screen chatter. At first\012		  when you pressed the ''/'' , the exitline appeared (as it''s\012		  supposed to), BUT when you pressed NO as an answer, the\012		  current writer switched to the other on (so user > sysop\012		  or the other way around). Now the name WON''T switch AND\012		  added a new CLS routine for clearing the exit-prompt.\012\012DrewlPage V1.0A:\012[Added]		- Added Chatstatus. DrewlPage now checks if chatmode is\012		  on/off. It checks the env: dir for a file called CHATSTATUS,\012		  so the util PAGESTAT ( (c) Ron Klinkien) CAN be used to\012		  control the status of this pager. It''s also possible to\012		  use the internal chat on/off from Xenolink. Just make sure\012		  that there''s no file called ENV:CHATSTATUS available.\012[Added]		- Added a full screen chatter.\012[Added]		- Added an intrologo when entering chatmode. The logo\012		  contains minor information like user''s location, time/date,\012		  accesslevel and xenolinknode.\012[Added]		- Added an option that a user can page MAXIMUM 3 times when\012		  the door has been started.\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE FUTURE "Future Versions"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                              Future Versions                               |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012    For now I''m not even sure if there will come another version. Depends if\012  there''s a use for it, BUT if there is, then there are some things that MIGHT\012                                be implemented.\012\012  o Macro-support\012  o Configurable screens\012  o A blacklist.\012  o An external util to display an own made text instead of a time-comment.\012\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE LICENSE "License"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                                  License                                   |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012       There is NO WARRANTY for the programs, to the extent permitted by\012     applicable law. Except when otherwise stated in writing the copyright\012   holders and/or other parties provide the programs "AS IS" without warranty\012    of any kind, either expressed or implied, including, but not limited to,\012     the implied warranties of merchantability and fitness for a particular\012   purpose. The entire risk as to the quality and performance of the programs\012    is with you. Should the programs prove defective, you assume the cost of\012                 all necessary servicing, repair or correction.\012\012   In no event unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing will\012   any copyright holder, or any other party who may redistribute the programs\012   as permitted above, be liable to you for ddamages, including any general,\012     special, incidental or consequential damages arising out of the use or\012    inability to use the programs (including but not limited to loss of data\012    or data being rendered inaccurate or losses sustained by you or a third\012   parties or a failure of the programs to operate with any other programs),\012   even if such holder or other party had been advised of the possibility of\012                                 such damages.\012\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE REG "Registration"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                             How To Register...                             |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012   Simple... There isn''t any.. We don''t ask for any fee whatsoever since Xeno\012         has already costed us a lot of money so this baby is for free.\012\012  HOWEVER !! If you decide to use this chatter, then please send me a message\012   that you do so. In that way I can see if there really is a use for further\012                           development on this door.\012\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE THANX "Special Thanx"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                  Special Thnx to the people listed below                   |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012    - Joseph Hodge for Ami-Express (Still works the best).\012    - Brian Kernighan & Dennis M. Ritchie for the C language!!\012    - Commodore Amiga for the computer.\012    - P0T-NooDLe for his ansi''s\012      Personal message to P0T: I know I didn''t ask ya if I could use your\012                               screens, but they really look great. Hope\012                               you don''t mind.....\012    - Alf for being somekind of a teacher to me.\012    - Roelof Jansen for sharing some tips & tricks.\012    - DJ. PiNSCHeR for his sometimes unusual ideas & betatesting.\012    - CRaM for his great help with the gui.\012    - XeNoN for sharing ideas & betatesting.\012\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE BUGS "If there are any bugs"\012\012                         __________  _____    _______/\_\012    :                   /   ____   \/  |  \  /  ____   /                   :\012  --+-------------------\__/   .\__/   |   \/  __/_\ //--------------------+--\012    |      SYSoP:         |     ||/   -+-  \\_      \/\      CoSYSoP:      |\012    |     STiNGRaY        |______|     |_____/________/     RoTeNTRaaG     |\012    |                           \______|                      DDaZZ        |\012   _|_  ______________________/\_______      _____________________  _______|/\\012  (___)/       \       \ ____   /____  \    /       \       \___  \/  ____   /\012  |  .|    /   /   /   /__/_\ // ___/   \  /    /___/   /   /__/   \ __/_\ //\012  |  ||   /   /   /   /      \/\ \_______)/    /   /   /   / \______)     \/\\012  |___|__/___/___/___/_________/    |   \ \_______/_______/    |   \________/\012  --+------------------------|______|    \_--------------|_____|    \_-----+--\012    :                               |_____/                    |_____/     :\012    .----------------------------------------------------------------------.\012    | RuNNiNG oN a2000/030/882 40MHZ 11MeGZ RaM  2.3GB HD aT YouR DiSPoSaL |\012    |      CoNNeCTRaTeS 2400 uPTo 28K8V34 uSiNG a TRoN DF 28K8 ToWeR       |\012    |                                                                      |\012    |                     oPeN 24HRZ/DaY - 7 DaYZ/WeeK                     |\012    `----[NoDe1: +31-10-420-0033 28K8]----[NoDe2: +31-10-RiNGDoWN 14K4]----''\012\012   .----------------.------------------.------------------.-----------------.\012   | THe iNNeR CoRe | NLa 14:101/202.9 | eRo 68:315/207.9 | Di 11:100/101.9 |\012   | +31-10-4200033 | FiDo 2:286/517.9 | LDY 69:100/101.9 )-----------------(\012   |  No NuP/SYSPW  | aMy 39:153/207.9 | e-MaiL [email removed]    |\012   `----------------^------------------^----^-------------------------------''\012\012   For bugreports and/or suggestions you can contact me at the above networks\012   or you can call the THe iNNeR CoRe SupportBBS directly at the above number\012\012@ENDNODE\012','\012',char(10)),'{"ACCESS":"010","LOCATION":"Doors:DrewlPage/DrewlPage","TYPE":"XIM","STACK":"4096"}','auto-added',62474,5,0,NULL,NULL,'tic_dp1c','scan',1780048780);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('tic_dp1d','TIC-DP1D.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/TIC-DP1D.LHA','DReWLPaGe','XIM','DReWLPaGe',NULL,NULL,'TIC','|  ______________   _______  |   |     THe | | /   ____   \___) /       \ | --O-- iNNeR | | \__/   .\__/  .|/    /___/ |   |    CoRe |',replace('.----------------------------.-------------.\n|  ______________   _______  |   |     THe |\n| /   ____   \___) /       \ | --O-- iNNeR |\n| \__/   .\__/  .|/    /___/ |   |    CoRe |\n|   |     || |  ||    /   /  | iNNoVaTioNS |\n|   |______| |___|_______/   |             |\n|                            |  PReSeNTS:  |\n)----------------------------^-------------(\n| DReWLPaGe V1.1D - /X FuLLSCReeN CHaTTeR! |\n|             THe BeST THeRe iS            |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'DrewlPage.Guide',replace('@DATABASE "Drewl-Page Release 1.1C Documentation"\012\012@NODE MAIN "Drewl-Page Release 1.1C Documentation"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                              Drewl-Page V1.1C                              |\012 |                  An Ami-Express V4.xx+ FullScreen-Chatter                  |\012 |                                                                            |\012 |                 CopyRight 1996 THe iNNeR CoRe iNNoVaTioNS!                 |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012\012             @{" Introduction      " Link INTRODUCTION} - Requirements, operation etc.\012             @{" Disclaimer        " Link DISCLAIMER} - Just read it\012             @{" Installation      " Link INSTALLATION} - How to install the system.\012             @{" Program Usage     " Link PROGRAM} - BBSCommand Installation\012             @{" Configuration     " Link CONFIG} - Example Configuration Files\012             @{" History           " Link HISTORY} - Version changes of Drewl-Page\012             @{" Future Versions   " Link FUTURE} - What will come in future versions?\012             @{" License           " Link LICENSE} - License agreement.\012             @{" Registration      " Link REG} - How to register.\012             @{" Special thanks    " Link THANX} - Thanks to these people...\012             @{" If there are bugs " Link BUGS} - Where to send your bugreports.\012\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE INTRODUCTION "Introduction"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                       Drewl-Page Introduction.                             |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012      Drewl-Page is an Ami-Express Full-Screen-Chatter Door.\012\012\012  Requirements:\012  -------------\012\012  o AmigaDOS 2.04 or higher.\012  o Ami-Express V4.x\012\012\012  Tested On:\012  -------------\012  Amiga  500/020/14      -  The iNNeR CoRe -  Sysop: Stingray\012  Amiga 2000/030/882/40  -  The iNNeR CoRe\012  Amiga 4000/030/882/25  -  The iNNeR CoRe\012\012  Operation:\012  -------------\012\012  o You can turn DrewlPage On/Off simply by toggling the internal\012    chat-control, or when you had installed ChatPage before, you can also\012    use the utils PageStat & PageEnv ((C) Ron Klinkien Used By CHATPAGE\012    (The FSC For Xenolink Pro) for turning the chat on/off. At this point\012    DrewlPage does nog recognize the several statustexts that these utils\012    write in env:chatstatus, but it will only see if the chat really is ON\012    or OFF (which should be more than enough anyway).\012  o DrewlPage uses Gadtools for it''s gui. The gui has an IGNORE button as\012    well as a FULLCHAT button. When the IGNORE button is pressed the gui will\012    disappear and sound will be turned off. The user won''t notice that\012    you''ve pressed the button since the socalled ''calling'' will continue on\012    his end. The user has 3 tries to call you in 1 session. When IGNORE has\012    been pressed at the first call, the gui will not even appear at the\012    second and/or third call.\012  o DrewlPage has been equiped with a fullscreen chatter which has a wordwrap\012    routine in it.\012  o DrewlPage is able to use the PREFS for it''s sampleplaying, but you can\012    also use your own sampleplayer if you wish. Please look at the\012    example-config in this guide how to use it.\012  o DrewlPage will create a directory in DOORS:DREWLPAGE. In that directory,\012    DrewlPage will place a logfile with info about who has paged you (and if\012    the chat was activated by you, it''ll also show the chatreason and HOW\012    long you''ve been chatting with the user). The log will have some\012    identification characters like |,#,[,],*,etcetc. So if you would like\012    to build a logscanner for who has been chatting the most with you, be\012    my guest. \012  o DrewlPage also keeps track of a capture-logfile so you can read back the\012    entire chatsession. If you wish to delete those files then just do so.\012    If DrewlPage sees (when chat is activated) that the current users logfile\012    doesn''t exist, it will simply create one.\012  o When sysop is unavailable (eg chat is OFF or sysop just hasn''t answered\012    it), a socalled TIMECOMMENT can be shown (look at the configuration\012    part). You are allowed to change the comments to your ''needs'' but\012    please don''t make them longer than 3 lines since cursorpositioning is\012    used in the chatter and it could screw up your entire screen. If you\012    don''t want to use these timecomments, then simply remove/rename the\012    config and they''re gone.\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE DISCLAIMER "Disclaimer"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                                 Disclaimer                                 |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012         No  warranty,  either express or implied, is made with respect\012                         to the fitness of Drewl-Page.\012\012  THe iNNeR CoRe iNNoVaTioNS (referred to as "the author"), reserves the right\012               to not develop any future versions of Drewl-Page.\012\012         The author will try to make a good faith attempt at correcting\012       any problems if any are discovered, but is in no way required, nor\012                             bound to correct them.\012\012         The author neither assumes nor accepts any responsibility for\012         the use or misuse of these programs. He also will not be held\012         liable for damages due to loss of profit or any other damages\012          arising out of the use, or inability to use these programs.\012\012  THe iNNeR CoRe iNNoVaTioNS will not be liable for any damage arising from\012         the  failure of these programs to perform as described, or any\012           destruction of other programs or data residing on a system\012          attempting to run the programs. While I know of no damaging\012       errors, the user of these programs uses it at his or her own risk.\012\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE INSTALLATION "Installation"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                       Drewl-Page Installation.                             |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012 Software Installation:\012 ------------------------\012\012 Doors (dir)\012       DrewlPage (dir)\012                 DrewlPage              40040 bytes\012                 Config (dir)\012                      DrewlPage.Cfg       613 Bytes\012                      Times.Cfg          2296 Bytes\012\012 Please do *NOT* change this directory structure since these paths are\012 hardcoded !!\012\012\012 BBSCommand Installation:\012 ------------------------\012 Use the following tooltypes:\012\012  ACCESS    = 010\012  LOCATION  = Doors:DrewlPage/DrewlPage\012  MULTINODE = YES\012  TYPE      = XIM\012  STACK     = 4096\012  NAME      = DReWLPaGe V1.1C\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE PROGRAM "Program Usage"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                               Program Usage                                |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012   To see the commandline just run the door in the CLI.. You should be shown\012                                this output....:\012\012   DReWLPaGe V1.1C (c)1996 THe iNNeR CoRe iNNoVaTioNS\012\012   This is a XIM door for Ami-Express V4.xx Professional BulletinBoard System\012\012   Use the following tooltypes in BBS:Commands/BBSCMD/O.info:\012\012   ACCESS    = 010\012   LOCATION  = Doors:DrewlPage/DrewlPage\012   MULTINODE = YES\012   TYPE      = XIM\012   STACK     = 4096\012   NAME      = DReWLPaGe V1.1C\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE CONFIG "External Configuration Files"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                      Drewl-Page Configuration Files.                       |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012 Doors:DrewlPage/Config/Drewlpage.Cfg\012 ---CUT---\012 BeepPause         20         ; The no. of ticks (50th of a sec) between Beeps\012 UserColor          3         ; Color of Text typed by User\012 SysOpColor         7         ; Color of Text typed by SysOp\012 Sample             Hear s:samples/sysop3.iff\012                              ; Which sample do you wish to use..\012                              ; PREFS - Use The WB/Prefs SOUND Util.\012                              ; OR use a commandline like:\012                              ; DSound -2 -m -w -o S:Samples/Sysop3.IFF\012 ---CUT---\012\012\012 Doors:DrewlPage/Config/Times.Cfg\012 ---CUT---\012 00 I''m Sorry!\012 00 The Sysop Can''t Be Reached Right Now.\012 00 Please Try Again Later This Morning.\012 01 Hmm, The Sysop Isn''t Replying...\012 01 Gee, Ya Know, Some People Have To Get To Work At 7:30AM\012 01 Please Do Not Disturb....\012 02 Jemig De Pemig, Mozes Kribbel!@$#!! It''s Two O''Clock!\012 02 I''ll Bet $100,- On It That The Sysop Is Laying In Bed,\012 02 ....Asleep! (Do YOU believe It ?? I Don''t..)\012 03 Are You Nuts?  Yelling At This Hour!\012 03\012 03 Wait For The Sunrise, And Try Again.\012 04 No, No, No, NO! I Will NOT Yell The Sysop For You!\012 04\012 04 Maybe It''s Time To Get Your Watch Repaired?!\012 05 U-Huh! It''s Too Early In The Morning.\012 05\012 05 I Can''t Reach Him Right Now.\012 06 The Sysop Is Delivering The Mail Now,\012 06 To Affort This BBS.. ;-((\012 06 Please Try Again Later Today.\012 07 Maybe The Sun Is Already Up....\012 07\012 07 But The Sysop Isn''t!\012 08 GoodMorning.\012 08 The Sysop Is In The BathRoom, I Guess..\012 08 Try Again Later Today...\012 09 Some People Have To Work You Know!\012 09\012 09 Please Try Again Later Today.\012 10 The Sysop Has Already Gone To Work.\012 10\012 10 Please Try Again Later Today.\012 11 The Sysop Is Watching A Movie On FilmNet+.\012 11\012 11 Please Try Again Later Today.\012 12 The Sysop Went Out For Lunch With His Girl.\012 12\012 12 Bon Appetit!\012 13 The Sysop Hasn''t Finished His Lunch Yet...\012 13 Please Try Again Later Today,\012 13 Or You Can Leave Him A Message.\012 14 The Sysop Went To Work.\012 14 That Is If He Hasn''t Been Fired Yet !\012 14 Please Try Again Later Today.\012 15 The Sysop Is Trying To Make Some Coffee...\012 15 If The BBS Is Down Soon, You''ll Know It Failed\012 15 Please Do Not Disturb And Let Him Die In Peace...\012 16 The Sysop Is Out With His FOUR Dogs.\012 16\012 16 Please Try Again Later Today.\012 17 The Sysop Is Currently In Bed...\012 17 His GIRLFRIEND Screams Too Loud! He Doesn''t Hear You!\012 17 Please Try Again Later Today.\012 18 The Sysop Is Throwing Up His Diner Above The Toilet.\012 18 His Mom Can''t Cook, You Know !!\012 18 Please Try Again Later Tonight...\012 19 The Sysop Is Probably Watching FilmNet(Plus)...\012 19 So, Why Don''t You Stroll Around A Bit,\012 19 You Can Try Again Later Tonight...\012 20 I Can''t Find Don Anywhere!!\012 20\012 20 Please Try Again Later Tonight.\012 21 Sorry, It Seems That Don Isn''t Home..\012 21\012 21 Please Try Again Later Tonight.\012 22 Sorry, The Sysop Went To Bed Early Today ;-))\012 22 (With His Girl Ofcourse)\012 22 Well, Ehr... You Know What''s Going On\012 23 The Sysop Is Sleeping Right Now!\012 23 He Probably Has To Get Up Early... (B^)\012 23 You Can Leave A Message If You Want.\012 ---CUT---\012\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE HISTORY "History"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                          Drewl-Page History                                |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012DrewlPage V1.1D:\012[Added]		- Added another small feature.. Now everyone who has an\012		  equal/higher level than 250 can page you whenever he\012		  wants. When chatstatus is OFF, but his level is high\012		  enough, the door will automaticly activate the pager as\012		  if chatstatus was ON. You can adjust the level to\012		  whatever you want, but default setting is 250 (my cosys\012		  level).\012\012DrewlPage V1.1C:\012[Fixed]		- After adding the support to allow users with names starting\012		  with THE (etcetc), I encountered a bug when it was the\012		  other one''s turn.. Seems a part of the previous typed\012		  line would be removed on the screen (not in the log)..\012		  Changed some linefeeds & ansi-cursorcodes so now it''s\012		  gone.\012[Report][Fixed]	- Was informed that the comment option fucked up the entire\012		  screen. Added an ansi-cursor-code so the TO: etcetc will\012		  be placed UNDER the timecomment.\012[Report][Fixed]	- Report came in about some dudes who have a handle\012		  starting with ''THE'' .. so in the chatter his prompt would\012		  be THE> .. Now changed.. The chatter will scan the first\012		  four characters for a space.. if there''s one found, the\012		  entire username/handle will be printed. Otherwise only\012		  the first word (so until the space occures).\012\012DrewlPage V1.1B:\012[Added]		- DrewlPage will now also log to the callerslog so that\012		  (for instance) SAmilog will know that someone has paged.\012[Fixed]		- Found a bug in the FSC. When a full line (no spaces in it)\012		  was entered, the line would not be written to the\012		  capturelog.\012[Added]		- It''s now possible to use your own samples through an\012		  external sampleplayer.\012\012DrewlPage V1.1A:\012[Fixed]		- Removed another error from the exitline. When answering\012		  NO at the exit request, the chatcolour turned to red\012		  instead of the configured chatcolour.\012[Added]		- Added a gui. Ignore & fullchat buttons available. No\012		  explanation needed I think.\012\012DrewlPage V1.0H:\012[Added/Fixed]	- Changed the exitline (again). At first the ''/'' was displayed\012		  before the actual exitline was given. Now that ''/'' has been\012		  removed. A ''/'' will only be displayed now when it''s NOT\012		  the first character.\012[Added]		- Added CaptureLog. Now each user has his own logfile of\012		  the previous ( & ofcourse the current) chatsession. Easy\012		  to look back if you want to know what your last chat was\012		  all about.\012\012DrewlPage V1.0G:\012[Added]		- Added several nodestatus-functions. When Paging it will be\012		  "REQUESTING CHAT" and when chatting in the FSC it will be\012		  "CHATTING WITH THE SYSOP".\012\012DrewlPage V1.0F:\012[Added/Fixed]	- Adjusted some routines (read Clean-Up). This caused the\012		  exe to be about 5k smaller.\012[Fixed]		- Removed a bug with reading the main config. The chatter\012		  would go crazy when one of the options was missing in the\012		  config ''cause it didn''t know what value to use. Now each\012		  option is DOUBLE checked if it''s available. If it''s not,\012		  it''ll get a default value.\012[Added]Fixed]	- Changed The Time/Date loop. At First they were requested\012		  several times. Now that had changed to 2 times max.\012[Fixed]		- Bug removed when exiting FSC. When you were in the chat and\012		  midnight passed, the time-in-chat calculation failed. Gave\012		  a VERY negative number. Should be fixed now.\012[Fixed]		- Fixed a bug concerning the time.config. I forgot to check\012		  for a \n (newline) and so a Blank-line would never be\012		  printed if you only had a line with the hour-number.\012[Added]		- Added a callerlog. This log will contain info concerning\012		  if the chatstatus is ON/OFF, WHO paged the sysop and WHEN\012		  and when the fullchatter has been activated, it will also\012		  show in the logfile how long that chatsession took.\012\012DrewlPage V1.0E:\012[Fixed]		- Changed the routine for retrieving the time/date. Wasn''t\012		  done in the best way, so could result into a guru once in\012		  a while. Fixed !!\012[Fixed]		- Removed a bug in the exit-line of the FSC. When / was\012		  pressed and answer was NO, then the color in the FSC was\012		  changed to RED instead of the colors supplied in the\012		  config.\012[Added]		- Added a minor thing in the FSC exit-line. Now you can see\012		  how long you''ve been chatting with the current user.\012[Added/Fixed]	- Changed the intro-logo when entering the FSC. The layout\012		  was too un-compatible with the rest of the pager.\012\012DrewlPage V1.0D:\012[Fixed]		- Bug Removed. It seems when running DrewlPage in ascii mode,\012		  /X would not remove ALL ansi-colors. Now I added a complete\012		  NEW routine for printing the ansi-colors in ascii mode.\012		  Should work fine.\012\012DrewlPage V1.0C:\012[Added]		- The UserColor and sysopcolor are now configurable. Colors\012		  are from 0-7 (0=ESC[30m, 3=ESC[33m 5=ESC[35m etcetc).\012[Added]		- Time between two beeps now configurable. Default is 20.\012[Added]		- Added a 2nd config which contains hourly comments. These\012		  comment can be changed into whatever you like, but MAXIMUM\012		  length is 74 characters. If you don''t want these comments,\012		  then simply rename or delete the config and they are gone.\012		  If you DO use the time-comments, make sure you do NOT use\012		  MORE than 6-7 Lines ''cause otherwise the time-comment-logo\012		  could get into a conflict with the return prompt (which is\012		  set at line 23).\012[Added]		- Added a cls-routine for when a user pages 1 second time in\012		  thesame session. Now the logo with the time-comment is\012		  cleared BEFORE paging the second/third time.\012\012DrewlPage V1.0B:\012[Fixed]		- Removed a bug. When a backspace was pressed at the first\012		  character, it was possible to erase the name of the person\012		  who was writing at the moment.\012[Fixed]		- Removed a bug concerning the wordwrap and (again) the\012		  backspace-key. It seems that when counting characters, the\012		  backspace was seen as a ADDED character instead of a\012		  substracted one. Therefor the wordwrap was invoked on an\012		  earlier moment when a backspace was pressed during the\012		  sentence.\012[Added]		- Added some information in the door. Now when you try to\012		  start the door from the shell, the ADVISEABLE menucommand\012		  will be printed. Please DO use this commandline (specificly\012		  the PATH) ''cause another door (WhoIsOn) checks for certain\012		  paths and it won''t recognize the door otherwise.\012[Fixed]		- Changed the exit line in the full screen chatter. At first\012		  when you pressed the ''/'' , the exitline appeared (as it''s\012		  supposed to), BUT when you pressed NO as an answer, the\012		  current writer switched to the other on (so user > sysop\012		  or the other way around). Now the name WON''T switch AND\012		  added a new CLS routine for clearing the exit-prompt.\012\012DrewlPage V1.0A:\012[Added]		- Added Chatstatus. DrewlPage now checks if chatmode is\012		  on/off. It checks the env: dir for a file called CHATSTATUS,\012		  so the util PAGESTAT ( (c) Ron Klinkien) CAN be used to\012		  control the status of this pager. It''s also possible to\012		  use the internal chat on/off from Xenolink. Just make sure\012		  that there''s no file called ENV:CHATSTATUS available.\012[Added]		- Added a full screen chatter.\012[Added]		- Added an intrologo when entering chatmode. The logo\012		  contains minor information like user''s location, time/date,\012		  accesslevel and xenolinknode.\012[Added]		- Added an option that a user can page MAXIMUM 3 times when\012		  the door has been started.\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE FUTURE "Future Versions"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                              Future Versions                               |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012    For now I''m not even sure if there will come another version. Depends if\012  there''s a use for it, BUT if there is, then there are some things that MIGHT\012                                be implemented.\012\012  o Macro-support\012  o Configurable screens\012  o A blacklist.\012  o An external util to display an own made text instead of a time-comment.\012\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE LICENSE "License"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                                  License                                   |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012       There is NO WARRANTY for the programs, to the extent permitted by\012     applicable law. Except when otherwise stated in writing the copyright\012   holders and/or other parties provide the programs "AS IS" without warranty\012    of any kind, either expressed or implied, including, but not limited to,\012     the implied warranties of merchantability and fitness for a particular\012   purpose. The entire risk as to the quality and performance of the programs\012    is with you. Should the programs prove defective, you assume the cost of\012                 all necessary servicing, repair or correction.\012\012   In no event unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing will\012   any copyright holder, or any other party who may redistribute the programs\012   as permitted above, be liable to you for ddamages, including any general,\012     special, incidental or consequential damages arising out of the use or\012    inability to use the programs (including but not limited to loss of data\012    or data being rendered inaccurate or losses sustained by you or a third\012   parties or a failure of the programs to operate with any other programs),\012   even if such holder or other party had been advised of the possibility of\012                                 such damages.\012\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE REG "Registration"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                             How To Register...                             |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012   Simple... There isn''t any.. We don''t ask for any fee whatsoever since Xeno\012         has already costed us a lot of money so this baby is for free.\012\012  HOWEVER !! If you decide to use this chatter, then please send me a message\012   that you do so. In that way I can see if there really is a use for further\012                           development on this door.\012\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE THANX "Special Thanx"\012 .----------------------------------------------------------------------------.\012 |                  Special Thnx to the people listed below                   |\012 `----------------------------------------------------------------------------''\012\012    - Joseph Hodge for Ami-Express (Still works the best).\012    - Brian Kernighan & Dennis M. Ritchie for the C language!!\012    - Commodore Amiga for the computer.\012    - P0T-NooDLe for his ansi''s\012      Personal message to P0T: I know I didn''t ask ya if I could use your\012                               screens, but they really look great. Hope\012                               you don''t mind.....\012    - Alf for being somekind of a teacher to me.\012    - Roelof Jansen for sharing some tips & tricks.\012    - DJ. PiNSCHeR for his sometimes unusual ideas & betatesting.\012    - CRaM for his great help with the gui.\012    - XeNoN for sharing ideas & betatesting.\012\012@ENDNODE\012\012@NODE BUGS "If there are any bugs"\012\012                         __________  _____    _______/\_\012    :                   /   ____   \/  |  \  /  ____   /                   :\012  --+-------------------\__/   .\__/   |   \/  __/_\ //--------------------+--\012    |      SYSoP:         |     ||/   -+-  \\_      \/\      CoSYSoP:      |\012    |     STiNGRaY        |______|     |_____/________/     RoTeNTRaaG     |\012    |                           \______|                      DDaZZ        |\012   _|_  ______________________/\_______      _____________________  _______|/\\012  (___)/       \       \ ____   /____  \    /       \       \___  \/  ____   /\012  |  .|    /   /   /   /__/_\ // ___/   \  /    /___/   /   /__/   \ __/_\ //\012  |  ||   /   /   /   /      \/\ \_______)/    /   /   /   / \______)     \/\\012  |___|__/___/___/___/_________/    |   \ \_______/_______/    |   \________/\012  --+------------------------|______|    \_--------------|_____|    \_-----+--\012    :                               |_____/                    |_____/     :\012    .----------------------------------------------------------------------.\012    | RuNNiNG oN a2000/030/882 40MHZ 11MeGZ RaM  2.3GB HD aT YouR DiSPoSaL |\012    |      CoNNeCTRaTeS 2400 uPTo 28K8V34 uSiNG a TRoN DF 28K8 ToWeR       |\012    |                                                                      |\012    |                     oPeN 24HRZ/DaY - 7 DaYZ/WeeK                     |\012    `----[NoDe1: +31-10-420-0033 28K8]----[NoDe2: +31-10-RiNGDoWN 14K4]----''\012\012   .----------------.------------------.------------------.-----------------.\012   | THe iNNeR CoRe | NLa 14:101/202.9 | eRo 68:315/207.9 | Di 11:100/101.9 |\012   | +31-10-4200033 | FiDo 2:286/517.9 | LDY 69:100/101.9 )-----------------(\012   |  No NuP/SYSPW  | aMy 39:153/207.9 | e-MaiL [email removed]    |\012   `----------------^------------------^----^-------------------------------''\012\012   For bugreports and/or suggestions you can contact me at the above networks\012   or you can call the THe iNNeR CoRe SupportBBS directly at the above number\012\012@ENDNODE\012','\012',char(10)),'{"ACCESS":"010","LOCATION":"Doors:DrewlPage/DrewlPage","TYPE":"XIM","STACK":"4096"}','auto-added',59151,1,0,NULL,NULL,'tic_dp1c','scan',1780048780);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('tif101','TIF101.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/TIF101.LHA','TIF','XIM','TIF',NULL,NULL,NULL,'33.6 DigITal-X Prd/NirVana Dist Site! 33.6',replace('TrapDoor Intuition Frontend\n33.6 DigITal-X Prd/NirVana Dist Site! 33.6\n','\n',char(10)),'MAMBA_OK.TXT',replace('------------------------------------------------------------------------\n              CALL MAMBA BBS ! FOREIGN CALLERS DISABLED RATIO !\n         ____    ____   ____    ____    ____  _________      ____\n        |~  ~\  /~  ~|  \~~ \  |~  ~\  /~  ~||~   __  ~\     \~~ \\n        |:    \/    :|___\  \\ ||    \/    |||:  |__|  /   ___\  \\\n        ||  |    |  :/~ ~/\  \\||  |    |  ||||   ___ \\  /~ ~/\  \\\n        ||  |\  /|  //  /__\  \\:  |\  /|  ||||  |___| ||//  /__\  \\\n        |___| \/ |_/____________\__| \/ |___||__________/____________\       \n\n            * THE BIGGEST & FASTEST AMIGA BBS IN EAST EUROPE *\nPOLAND NOW !                                                  POLAND NOW !\n                             SysOp - EaSy RiDeR\n                Phone no. ++48-22-367443         24 hours/day\n                 USRobotics 14400/HST/V42.bis      HD 240 MB\n                            > >  U N I O N HQ < <\n                 __       __   __      __   __  ____           __ \n           |    |  |        |    |       | |       / |    |      |\n       -|- |__| |__| __   __|  __| __  __| |__  __/  |__| |__| __|\n              | |  |     |    |          | |  |  /      |    |   |\n              | |__|     |__  |__      __| |__| /       |    | __|\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',32745,10,0,NULL,NULL,'tif101','scan',1780048780);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('timeb','TIMEB.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/TIMEB.LHA',NULL,'XIM','..',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,replace('..\n','\n',char(10)),'TimeB.DOC',replace('\n                        TIME BATCH VERSION 1.0 \n                          by Jake of Silents\n\n NOTE: MAKE SURE YOU RUN THIS BATCH FROM AN INDEPENDENT SHELL WINDOW\n\n Introduction:\n ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n This little program is actually a batch file made from simple AmigaDOS\n commands. Of course anyone could have done it but no one bothered to\n make this. It started as a small batch file  customized for my system\n specificly. Later I added the .key command to get user input on the \n starting time and ending time. I see no reason for anyone to CODE \n what this little batch file does. It is fast the way it is and can''t \n be any faster as to improvements...well there can be many...\n You might ask yourseld what is the point of making FREE downloads? \n well few European boards have specific time when downloads are free;\n at a time where the least amount of callers calls. Instead of having\n for example no callers between 12:00 and 15:00 once you make \n freedownloads available people will call at that time. Of course you\n might think there is a draw back to this, that all loosers [if any]\n will call then and downloads everything for free, that is why I\n recommend you check the callerslog for abusers. I limit the free \n downloads to 2 mb a night. \n\n \n There is a similar program that executes commands at a specified time\n [I believe it was called Cron or something] but this little batch I\n made is especially for Ami Express. \n\n\n Set Up:\n ----------------------------------------------------------------------\n Copy files: FREE and TIMEB to your C: directory onto your SYS:\n Otherwise the Utility WILL NOT WORK\n \n\n How To Use This Util:\n ---------------------------------------------------------------------- \n YOU MUST ENTER THE SYNTAX EXACTLY ACCORDING TO THE MODEL BELOW, IF YOU\n ENTER THE FILE NAME ''TIMEB'' BY ITSELF YOU WILL GET AN ERROR MESSAGE.\n If the file cannot be executed without the EXECUTE command then do \n this: \n\n PROTECT TIMEB +S             --> This will make the file executable \n\n **********************************************************************\n \n Syntax:\n\n TIMEB [from] [to] [Conf]\n\n or \n \n EXECUTE TIMEB [from] [to] [Conf]\n \n FROM  - Put The Starting Time That you wish to make the free\n         downloads available FROM in this format 00:00 (hour:minutes)\n         You have to use the military time like: 13:23 for 1:23 PM,\n         and 00:10 for 10 past midnight.\n\n TO    - Put The Ending Time That You Wish to STOP free downloading.\n         Use the same time format as above.\n\n CONF  - Is The Conference PATH in which you want the files to be FREE\n         for the period of time you specified earlier. In a later\n         version I will add more than one conference option.\n         So here you would enter for example: bbs:node0/newstuff/\n\n Ok, here is what the whole syntax will look like:\n\n TIMEB 14:00 16:00 FH0:NEWSTUFF/\n\n or\n \n TIMEB 00:00 01:00 bbs:node0/conference/\n\n SIMPLE!\n\n The script copies the file c:free into conference:freedownloads\n thus making all files in that conference free. Then once the ending\n time is reached the script simply deletes that file and users once\n again have to use their credits to download.\n\n ======================================================================\n \n Future Additions:\n\n * FREE DOWNLOADS in Multiple Conferences\n\n * DISPLAYING a text file upon hitting the ''D'' key that tells you it is \n   FREE DOWNLOADING TIME [my custom version has this already]\n\n * TIME BATCH will open its own window thus no locking up the current\n   CLI or SHELL window \n\n * Whatever you people come up with...\n\n                                                     - JAKE\n\n              MAKE SURE TO CALL THESE SILENTS BOARDS!\n\n             WHQ!     TERMINAL DISASTER       215-739-2150   \n         EURO HQ!      THE CRIME ZONE!        +46-87178910   \n         EURO HQ!        !MOLDAVIA!           +32-13553962   \n         TSL GHQ!       DARK CENTURY!         +49-5113880447 \n         DUTCH HQ           CHAOS             +31-46339129   \n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,5543,8,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048780);
