INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('todup4','TODUP4.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/TODUP4.LHA',NULL,'XIM','todayup','4.0',NULL,NULL,'33.6 DigITal-X Prd/NirVana Dist Site! 33.6',replace('TODAYUPV4.0\n33.6 DigITal-X Prd/NirVana Dist Site! 33.6\n','\n',char(10)),'todayup.doc',replace('\n                               TODAYUPV4.0\n                              -------------\n\n\n\nDescription\n-----------\n\nThis Prog. generates a bulletin-text in wich all uploads of the day\nincl. name, bytes, baud, uploadtime, uploader and conference\nwill be written in. Now it is possible to generate texts where only the\nfilename will be showen.\n\nAll files who are no useruploads would be written as Sysopfiles.\nIf in the filelisting are newuploads with the date of this day,\nand they donn''t exists in the UDlog at the same day, than they would\nbe written as a sysopupload in den Bulletin-Text.\n\nIn this version the conference of the uploadfile will be named in the text.\nThats the reason why usernames will only displayed 15 chars long.\nNow a file who is send into the hold will no longer be displayed.\n\nNow U can let generate text''s who are conference-specific.\nIf in the config the option therefor is set, it will be generate in every\nin the config founded conference a Bull.txt .\nBut if U want U can let generate parallel the hole text, where all uploads\nof the day are written in.\n\nIn this version U can let TodayUp search in all U''r UDLogs.\n\nThe Outtext if there are no new uploads can now self definied.\n\nThe importend news is that the workspeed ist now 3x faster!\n\nThen there iss a new function wich let work todayup faster, but therefore\nit will be use more RAM. But this is no great problem, its not uch.\nLet the funktion on fast (S)...only if U as great memoryprobs, then switch\nit to slow (L), but this need a little bit more time to work.\nThe workspeed is different, if U''r UDLog''s are very long it''s uses more time\nthan with an not so long UDLog.\n\n\nThis Prog. can be started from a batch.\nExample: BBS:MULTX.\n\nThere are no parameters because it needs a configfile.\nNow for example a configfile:\n\nATTENTION! Form version 4.0 the configfile will be completly changed!!!\nWho tried to start TodayUp4.0 with the old config will have no chance.\nThen TodayUp will be quited without any work.\n\nI have the config new organised.\nThere are now keywords.\nEvery keyword is 10 Chars long.\nThe keyword follows directly an ''='' and them follows directly the parameter.\nIf TodayUp founds in the config a keyword, the parameter behind the ''=''\nwill be used.\nThis has many advantages.\nThe importend of this is that when it comes a new version of TodayUp with\nnew futures U must only write the new keyword everywhere in the configfile.\nAlso it''s more secure that nothing like the UDLog''s or Dir2''s can be\noverwritten.\nAlso the keywords can be found everywhere in the cofigfile when 2 rules\nare noted:\n1. The keyword must be located left at the beginning of a line.\n2. There is a maximum of 100 lines where the keyfiles are must be located,\n   if any keyword stands behind those 100 lines, it will not be found.\n   But 100 lines are enough.\n\nNow the example of a configfile...that''s the same wich must be found in\nthe Archiv of TodayUp.\n\n------------------------------CUT HERE-----------------------------------------\n-----------ToDayUp4.0 by Strider/Shades-----Keyworddescribtion-----------------\n\nKeyword: OUT_LANGUE -> Language for the Text  D=german  E=englisch\nKeyword: WORK_SPEED -> Speed                  L=slow    S=fast\nKeyword: OUTPTSTYLE -> Output                 L=long    K=small\nKeyword: TEXT_SPEZI -> ALLIN1=all uploads in the text, CONF=conference-specific\n                       BOTH=all/both\nKeyword: SYSOP_NAME -> Sysopname max. 15 chars. Dont''t use '' , '' !\nKeyword: NO_UP_TEXT -> Outline if there are no new uploads.\n                       Max. 76 chars. Dont''t use '' , '' !\nKeyword: PATHUDLOG1 -> Path incl. name for the N0 UDLog of /X\nKeyword: PATHUDLOG2 -> Path incl. name for the N1 UDLog of /X\nKeyword: PATHUDLOG3 -> Path incl. name for the N2 UDLog of /X\nKeyword: PATHUDLOG4 -> Path incl. name for the N3 UDLog of /X\nKeyword: PATHUDLOG5 -> Path incl. name for the N4 UDLog of /X\nKeyword: PATHUDLOG6 -> Path incl. name for the N5 UDLog of /X\nKeyword: PATHUDLOG7 -> Path incl. name for the N6 UDLog of /X\nKeyword: PATHUDLOG8 -> Path incl. name for the N7 UDLog of /X\nKeyword: PATHUDLOG9 -> Path incl. name for the N8 UDLog of /X\nKeyword: PATHFLIST1 -> Path incl. name for the 1.filelisting\nKeyword: PATHFLIST2 -> Path incl. name for the 2.filelisting\nKeyword: PATHFLIST3 -> Path incl. name for the 3.filelisting\nKeyword: PATHFLIST4 -> Path incl. name for the 4.filelisting\nKeyword: PATHFLIST5 -> Path incl. name for the 5.filelisting\nKeyword: PATHFLIST6 -> Path incl. name for the 6.filelisting\nKeyword: PATHFLIST7 -> Path incl. name for the 7.filelisting\nKeyword: PATHFLIST8 -> Path incl. name for the 8.filelisting\nKeyword: PATHFLIST9 -> Path incl. name for the 9.filelisting\nKeyword: PATH_BULL1 -> Path incl. name for the 1.bulletintext\nKeyword: PATH_BULL2 -> Path incl. name for the 2.bulletintext\nKeyword: PATH_BULL3 -> Path incl. name for the 3.bulletintext\nKeyword: PATH_BULL4 -> Path incl. name for the 4.bulletintext\nKeyword: PATH_BULL5 -> Path incl. name for the 5.bulletintext\nKeyword: PATH_BULL6 -> Path incl. name for the 6.bulletintext\nKeyword: PATH_BULL7 -> Path incl. name for the 7.bulletintext\nKeyword: PATH_BULL8 -> Path incl. name for the 8.bulletintext\nKeyword: PATH_BULL9 -> Path incl. name for the 9.bulletintext\n\n-----------ToDayUp4.0 by Strider/Shades-------configpart-----------------------\n\nOUT_LANGUE=D\nWORK_SPEED=S\nOUTPTSTYLE=L\nTEXT_SPEZI=BOTH\nSYSOP_NAME=Strider\nNO_UP_TEXT=              Nothing new today...   sorry no new uploads!!!\nPATHUDLOG1=BBS:Node0/UDLog\nPATHUDLOG2=BBS:Node1/UDLog\nPATHUDLOG3=\nPATHUDLOG4=\nPATHUDLOG5=\nPATHUDLOG6=\nPATHUDLOG7=\nPATHUDLOG8=\nPATHUDLOG9=\nPATHFLIST1=BBS:Doc/Dir2\nPATHFLIST2=BBS:AmigaPD/Dir2\nPATHFLIST3=BBS:Amiga/Dir2\nPATHFLIST4=BBS:AmigaDemo/Dir2\nPATHFLIST5=BBS:PCPD/Dir2\nPATHFLIST6=BBS:PC/Dir2\nPATHFLIST7=BBS:PCDemo/Dir2\nPATHFLIST8=BBS:Shades/Dir2\nPATHFLIST9=BBS:FRED/Dir2\nPATH_BULL1=BULL:Bull27.txt.gr\nPATH_BULL2=BULL:Bull27.txt\nPATH_BULL3=\nBBS:Amiga/Bull.txt <- cut for fast disabeling, maybe for tests etc..\nPATH_BULL4=\nBBS:PC/Bull.txt <- be sure to cut directly after the ''=''.\nPATH_BULL5=\nPATH_BULL6=\nPATH_BULL7=\nPATH_BULL8=\nPATH_BULL9=\n\n-----------ToDayUp4.0 by Strider/Shades-----------------ENDE-------------------\n------------------------------CUT HERE-----------------------------------------\n\nIf U want U can cut all the keyworddescribtions, but it''s better to let it in,\nfor fast describtion.\n\nThat all must be found in the S: Dir, under the name: "TodayUp.cfg"\n\n\nDescribtion:\n\nOUT_LANGUE -> Language for the date, D=german, E=englisch.\n              Set E or D.\nWORK_SPEED -> Speed,       L=slow, S=fast.\n              Let it set everytime to S , only U have problems with U''r memory,\n              than it can help, but it needs more time.\nOUTPTSTYLE -> Output,      L=Long, K=small.      \n              If U set L than the text will be generated as the earlier versions\n              of Todayup it has done.\n              If K is set than only the Filenames will be showed. 5 Files\n              in every line.\nTEXT_SPEZI -> ALLIN1=all uploads in the text, CONF=conference-specific.\n              BOTH=alles/beides.\n              If ALLIN1 is set the uploads of all conferences will be displayed\n              as the earlier versions of TodayUp it has done.\n              If CONF is set it would in all under PATHFLISTx showed conferences\n              the Bull.txt text''s generated witch AmiExpress will show if a\n              User change the conference, there will be only displayed the new\n              uploads of this conference.\n              If BOTH is set it will be do the both things (ALLIN1 & CONF).\n              ALLIN1 has the highest priority, if for example U have set on\n              PATH_BULLx a Bull.txt in one Conference.\nSYSOP_NAME -> Sysopname max. 15 chars will be used.  \n              This name will be showed if no user can be located, this must be\n              than an Sysopupload.\n              Please don''t use '' , '' in the name.\nNO_UP_TEXT -> Outline if there are no new uploads this text will be showed.\n              Max. 76 chars will be used.\n              Please don''t use '' , '' in the name.\nPATHUDLOG1 -> Path incl. name for the N0 UDLog of /X\n              Here U must show where the UDLog of the Node0 is located.\nPATHUDLOG2 -> Path incl. name for the N1 UDLog of /X\n              Here U must show where the UDLog of the Node1 is located.\nPATHUDLOG3 -> Path incl. name for the N2 UDLog of /X\n              Here U must show where the UDLog of the Node2 is located.\nPATHUDLOG4 -> Path incl. name for the N3 UDLog of /X\n              Here U must show where the UDLog of the Node3 is located.\nPATHUDLOG5 -> Path incl. name for the N4 UDLog of /X\n              Here U must show where the UDLog of the Node4 is located.\nPATHUDLOG6 -> Path incl. name for the N5 UDLog of /X\n              Here U must show where the UDLog of the Node5 is located.\nPATHUDLOG7 -> Path incl. name for the N6 UDLog of /X\n              Here U must show where the UDLog of the Node6 is located.\nPATHUDLOG8 -> Path incl. name for the N7 UDLog of /X\n              Here U must show where the UDLog of the Node7 is located.\nPATHUDLOG9 -> Path incl. name for the N8 UDLog of /X\n              Here U must show where the UDLog of the Node8 is located.\nPATHFLIST1 -> Path incl. name for the 1.filelisting  \n              Here U must show where the filelisting, the Dir2 or\n              Dir3 (the latest Dir) oft the 1. Conf. is located.\nPATHFLIST2 -> Path incl. name for the 2.filelisting  \n              Here U must show where the filelisting, the Dir2 or\n              Dir3 (the latest Dir) oft the 2. Conf. is located.\nPATHFLIST3 -> Path incl. name for the 3.filelisting  \n              Here U must show where the filelisting, the Dir2 or\n              Dir3 (the latest Dir) oft the 3. Conf. is located.\nPATHFLIST4 -> Path incl. name for the 4.filelisting  \n              Here U must show where the filelisting, the Dir2 or\n              Dir3 (the latest Dir) oft the 4. Conf. is located.\nPATHFLIST5 -> Path incl. name for the 5.filelisting  \n              Here U must show where the filelisting, the Dir2 or\n              Dir3 (the latest Dir) oft the 5. Conf. is located.\nPATHFLIST6 -> Path incl. name for the 6.filelisting  \n              Here U must show where the filelisting, the Dir2 or\n              Dir3 (the latest Dir) oft the 6. Conf. is located.\nPATHFLIST7 -> Path incl. name for the 7.filelisting  \n              Here U must show where the filelisting, the Dir2 or\n              Dir3 (the latest Dir) oft the 7. Conf. is located.\nPATHFLIST8 -> Path incl. name for the 8.filelisting  \n              Here U must show where the filelisting, the Dir2 or\n              Dir3 (the latest Dir) oft the 8. Conf. is located.\nPATHFLIST9 -> Path incl. name for the 9.filelisting  \n              Here U must show where the filelisting, the Dir2 or\n              Dir3 (the latest Dir) oft the 9. Conf. is located.\nPATH_BULL1 -> Path incl. name for the 1.bulletintext \n              Here U must show where the 1. text should be generated.\nPATH_BULL2 -> Path incl. name for the 2.bulletintext \n              Here U must show where the 2. text should be generated.\nPATH_BULL3 -> Path incl. name for the 3.bulletintext\n              Here U must show where the 3. text should be generated.\nPATH_BULL4 -> Path incl. name for the 4.bulletintext\n              Here U must show where the 4. text should be generated.\nPATH_BULL5 -> Path incl. name for the 5.bulletintext\n              Here U must show where the 5. text should be generated.\nPATH_BULL6 -> Path incl. name for the 6.bulletintext\n              Here U must show where the 6. text should be generated.\nPATH_BULL7 -> Path incl. name for the 7.bulletintext\n              Here U must show where the 7. text should be generated.\nPATH_BULL8 -> Path incl. name for the 8.bulletintext\n              Here U must show where the 8. text should be generated.\nPATH_BULL9 -> Path incl. name for the 9.bulletintext\n              Here U must show where the 9. text should be generated.\n\n\nIt could be searched in 9 filelistings for new uploads.\n9 are enough, because AmiEx has only 9 Conferences.\n\n\n\nKnown Bugs:\n- An '' , '' in the config will be recognized as an Return.\n\n\n1993 Shades Productions,\nby Strider of Shades.\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',55058,10,0,NULL,NULL,'todup4','scan',1780048780);
