INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('trapdoor','TRAPDOOR.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/TRAPDOOR.LHA','TrapPrefs','XIM','TrapPrefs',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,replace('CONFIG FOR TRAPDOORS\n','\n',char(10)),'TrapPrefs.guide',replace('@DATABASE "TrapPrefs v1.2 documentation"\n\n@NODE MAIN "TrapPrefs v1.2 documentation"\n\n                               TrapPrefs v1.2\n                   Preference editor for TrapDoor v1.84+\n\nTrapPrefs and this documentation are Copyright © 1994 by Michael Barsoom.\n\n@{" Copyright & Disclaimer " Link Copyright_&_Disclaimer}  --  Please read this first.\n@{" Features               " Link Features}  --  What exactly does TrapPrefs do?\n@{" Requirements           " Link Requirements}  --  What you need to run TrapPrefs.\n@{" Locale                 " Link Locale}  --  Using TrapPrefs in your own language.\n@{" Usage                  " Link Usage}  --  How do I get it to work?\n@{" Gadgets                " Link Gadgets}  --  What do all the gadget do?\n@{" CLI and ToolTypes      " Link CLI}  --  Other Options\n@{" Author''s Address       " Link Address}  --  How do I reach the author.\n@{" Shareware              " Link Shareware}  --  Shareware information.\n@{" History                " Link History}  --  What has changed.\n@{" Thanks To              " Link Thanks}  --  Who helped make TrapPrefs\n@{" ToDo                   " Link ToDo}  --  What''s in store for the future\n@{" Questions              " Link Questions}  --  These are not bugs\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@node Copyright_&_Disclaimer "Copyright & Disclaimer"\nTrapPrefs and this documentation are Copyright © 1994 by Michael\nBarsoom.\n\nTrapPrefs may be freely distributed as long as no charge is made other than\nto cover time and copying costs.  This should be no higher than what Fred\nFish charges from one of his freely redistributable disks.\n\nYou may not copy and/or distribute this program without the accompanying\ndocumentation unless you get permission from the author to do so.\n\nFred Fish and Walnut Creek have permission to include this program on their\nfreely redistributable disks/CDRoms.\n\nIf you write a freely redistributable program and would like to include\nTrapPrefs with it, feel free to do so only if you send me a fully\nregistered version of your program and keep all the files included in this\narchive.\n\nFinally if you wish to include TrapPrefs on a disk magazine you are\nREQUIRED to get the author''s permission FIRST.  Usually this will require\nyou to just send me a copy of the issue with TrapPrefs free of charge AND\nregister your copy of TrapPrefs.\n\nPlease see @{"Address" Link Address} for how to you can reach me.\n\n                           -+- Disclaimer -+-\n\nThis product is sold "as is" without representation or warranty of any\nkind, either expressed or implied.  The user assumes all risks and\nresponsibilities related to its use.\n@endnode\n\n@node Features\nTrapPrefs is an intition based preference editor for TrapDoor.\n\nFeatures:\n    o Supports all of the features of TrapDoor 1.84+\n    o All options can be set with simple cycle gadgets, and string\n      gadgets.\n    o Log and Stat window sizes can be set simply by adjusting their\n      size and location and clicking on a close gadget.\n    o ReqTools file and palette requesters.\n    o Full locale support.\n    o No anoying restrictions or requesters.\n    o Freely distributable @{"SHAREWARE" link shareware}.\n    o MUI interface.\n@endnode\n\n@node Thanks\nI''d like to thank the follow people for their help is creating TrapPrefs:\n\nMy loving wife.\n     For being herself.\n\nPiergiorgio Ghezzo\n     For reporting many bugs, and helping in beta testing.\n\nEveryone who has or will have registered TrapPrefs\n     For supporting shareware.\n\nNico Francois\n     For ReqTools.\n\nMaximilian Hantsch and Martin Laubach\n     For TrapDoor.\n\nStefan Stuntz\n     For MUI, and for answering my programming questions.\n@endnode\n\n@node Requirements\nTrapPrefs does not require much, you just need to have the following:\n\n1) Workbench 2.0+\n2) ReqTools library (© Nico Francois)\n3) @{"Magic User Interface" link MUI} v2.1 (will not work with 2.0 or before)\n4) TrapDoor v1.84 or v1.85 (© Maximilian Hantsch and Martin Laubach)\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Locale\n\nTrapPrefs can be run in you prefered language.  To do this you need to copy\nthe appropriate trapprefs.catalog to you locale directory.  If your language\nis not included, feel free to translate the included .ct file and send it to me\nand I will send back to you the .catalog file.\n\nNOTE: If you intend to translate TrapPrefs to your language, please read the\n      included TrapPrefs.cd as there are some special instructions needed for\n      proper translation.\n\nThanx to the following for their translations:\n\nPiergiorgio Ghezzo ([email removed])\n     for the Italian translation\n\nSteffen Salzmann (2:244/1544.2)\n	for the German translation\n	\nMichael Berg (2:238/24.28 | [email removed])\n    for the Danish translation\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Usage\nTrapPrefs\n\nAll of the buttons, cycle gadgets, and button gadgets set one of TrapDoor''s\nkeywords.  You just set the values as you want them they will automatically\nbe saved for you.  Please see TrapDoor.guide for a detailed explaination of\neach option.\n\nThe Menu:\n    Open    --  Loads a TrapDoor.cfg file into the prefs editor.\n    Open As --  Opens a filerequester so that you can specify the name\n                of the config to load.\n\n    Save    --  Save the current config with the current name or as\n                "Mail:TrapDoor.cfg" if none is specified\n    Save As --  Opens a filerequester so that you can specify the name\n                of the config to save.\n\n    About   --  duh :-)\n\n    Quit    --  Do I really need to tell you.\n\n    Reset to Defaults  --  set all options to TrapDoor''s default values.\n                           NOTE: the cycle gadgets have the default setting\n                                 in black, and the non default setting\n                                 in white or the style specified with the\n                                 COLOR tooltype\n\nLoading configurations:\n	When loading a configuration, if an error is discovered you will be notified\n	of the error.  The error requester has three gadgets on it:\n	     Abort:    Stop loading the config, and restore previous config.\n	               Note: in order to restore the previous config the directory\n                   T: must exist.\n	     Continue: Continue loading the config ignoring just this error\n	     Ignor:    Continue loading the config ignoring this and future errors\n\nThe Window sizes:\n    Clicking this gadget opens two windows, one representing the Log window and\n    the other the Status window.  Just adjust the position and size as you want\n    them and click either close gadget.\n\n    If you change your mind just select ''Cancel'' from the menu.\n\nThe Palette requester:\n    If your screen mode is not Workbench or Active, a screen will open up as\n    defined in your preferences with a palette requester on it.  Just adjust\n    palette and click on OK to save the new palette.\n\nThe Modem Mode:\n	This is were you set the default state for TrapDoor.  There are three options\n	Answer     put TrapDoor in answer mode)\n	Call BOSS  make TrapDoor call boss)\n	Call       with this option you need to fill in the ''Who'' string.  This can\n               be a node/point number or a phonenumber depending on if you\n               have a nodelist installed.\n\nOnline help:\n    Pressing ''HELP'' with the cursor over a gadget will automaticall open up the\n    appropriate page in TrapDoor.guide.  TrapDoor.guide must appear in your\n    AmigaGuide search path.\n    NOTE: As of MUI v2.2 this feature requires v39.x of AmigaGuide, and will\n          not work with v34.x.  At least it won''t on my system :-(\n\n@endnode\n\n@node Gadgets\nNOTE: This page requires that TrapDoor.guide be found in you AmigaGuide path.\n\nMain Pages\n\n    @{" System Settings  " Link System}\n    @{" General Settings " Link General}\n    @{" Modem Settings   " Link Modem}\n    @{" System Settings  " Link Session}\n    @{" Screen Settings  " Link Screen}\n    @{" Function Keys    " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.43}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node System "System Settings"\n\n    @{" Sysop Name  " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.111}\n    @{" BBS Name    " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.71}\n    @{" Node Number " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.72}\n    @{" AKA''s       " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.8}\n    @{" BOSS        " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.23}\n    @{" Password    " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.75}\n@endnode\n\n@node General "General Settings"\n\nLog File:   @{" LogFile          " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.58}\n            @{" LogCallerID      " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.57}\n            @{" MaxLogSecs       " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.63}\n            @{" MaxLogLines      " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.62}\n\n            @{" Log Groups       " Link TrapDoor.Guide/4.3.56}\n\nOther:      @{" Inbound          " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.49}\n            @{" OutBound         " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.74}\n            @{" NodeList         " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.73}\n\n            @{" ShowRexx         " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.97}\n            @{" ARexx Port       " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.83}\n            @{" TimeStamp        " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.114}\n            @{" Priority         " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.113}\n            @{" UseUserShell     " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.119}\n            @{" Esc Resets Modem " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.39}\n@endnode\n@node Modem "Modem Settings"\n\nSerial:         @{" Min Baud            " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.64}\n                @{" Baud                " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.16}\n                @{" Max Baud            " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.61}\n                @{" Lock                " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.55}\n                @{" FloatLock           " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.44}\n                @{" DSR                 " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.37}\n                @{" 7Wire               " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.1}\n                @{" Shared              " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.96}\n                @{" Serial Name         " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.94}\n                @{" Serial Flags        " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.93}\n                @{" Serial Unit         " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.95}\n                @{" Adjust              " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.6}\n                @{" SerialBufSize       " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.92}\n                @{" SlowModem           " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.99}\n\nDial Strings    @{" Modem Answer        " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.65}\n                @{" Modem HangUp        " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.68}\n                @{" Modem Dial Pre      " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.66}\n                @{" Modem Dial Post     " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.67}\n                @{" Modem Init          " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.69}\n                @{" Dialer              " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.31}\n                @{" Ring Command        " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.84}\n\nDial Misc:      @{" KiwiPulse           " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.53}\n                @{" SwePulse            " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.106}\n                @{" Strip Dashes        " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.107}\n\n                @{" Answer              " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.10}\n                @{" Call                " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.24}\n\n                @{" Rings               " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.86}\n                @{" Ringings            " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.85}\n                @{" Dial TimeOut        " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.32}\n                @{" ModemResetInterval  " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.70}\n                @{" Redial Delay        " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.80}\n                @{" Retries             " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.82}\n@endnode\n\n@node Session "Session settings"\n\nConnection:     @{" Emsi             " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.38}\n                @{" FastEmsi         " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.40}\n                @{" WaZoo            " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.122}\n                @{" DietIFNA         " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.33}\n                @{" ZedZip           " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.127}\n                @{" ZedZap           " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.126}\n                @{" DirectZap        " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.34}\n                @{" TrapZap          " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.115}\n                @{" Immediate        " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.48}\n                @{" SniffARQ         " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.101}\n\n                @{" ARQ String       " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.11}\n\nTransfer:       @{" PickUp           " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.76}\n                @{" Forbid XMail     " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.45}\n                @{" Forbid All       " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.45}\n                @{" ABS              " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.3}\n                @{" Keep All         " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.51}\n                @{" XMail            " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.125}\n                @{" Forbid Freq      " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.45}\n                @{" Allow Refusing   " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.9}\n                @{" Keep XMail       " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.52}\n\nBBS:            @{" BBS Mode         " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.21}\n                @{" BBS Message      " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.20}\n                @{" BBS Command      " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.18}\n                @{" BBS Char         " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.17}\n                @{" BBSInOut         " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.19}\n                @{" Drop BBS Seconds " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.36}\n                @{" Banner           " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.15}\n\nMisc:           @{" After Session    " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.7}\n                @{" File Request     " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.46}\n                @{" Fax String       " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.42}\n                @{" Fax Command      " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.41}\n                @{" Turn around      " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.116}\n                @{" Voice String     " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.121}\n                @{" Voice Command    " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.120}\n\nAccounting:     @{" Accounting       " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.4}\n                @{" Cost             " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.29}\n                @{" Account Limits   " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.5}\n@endnode\n@node Screen "Screen Settings"\n\n    @{" Quiet              " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.79}\n    @{" Auto Adjust        " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.12}\n    @{" Beep Display       " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.22}\n    @{" Wrap Lines         " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.123}\n    @{" Zoom Full Size     " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.128}\n    @{" Background         " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.14}\n    @{" Interlace          " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.50}\n    @{" Auto OverScan      " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.13}\n    @{" Use System Font    " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.118}\n    @{" Screen Mode        " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.89}\n    @{" Public Screen Name " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.77}\n    @{" DisplayID          " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.35}\n    @{" Window Sizes       " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.60}\n    @{" Palette            " Link TrapDoor.guide/4.3.26}\n@endnode\n\n@node CLI "Tooltypes and CLI options"\nTrapPrefs supports the following tooltypes / cli options\n\nTooltype and/or CLI option\n\n    CONFIG - name of TrapDoor config file to load at startup.  For example if\n             you want TrapPrefs to automatically load "Mail:TrapDoor.cfg"\n             when it is first run just add the following tooltype:\n             ''CONFIG=Mail:TrapDoor.cfg''\n\nTooltypes only\n\n    COLOR - color or style TrapPrefs should use to display non default options.\n            This option will be read even if TrapPrefs is started from the CLI.\n\n    		You can use any of the following:\n\n    		u    Set the soft style to underline.\n            b    Set the soft style to bold.\n            i    Set the soft style to italic\n            n    Set the soft style back to normal.\n           <n>   Use pen number n (2..9) as front pen. n must be a valid\n                 DrawInfo pen as specified in "intuition/screens.h".\n\n@endnode\n@node Address\nyou can reach me at:\n\nMichael Barsoom\n5524 Pine Street\nOmaha NE 68106\nUSA\n\nInternet:  [email removed]\nFidonet:   Mike Barsoom @ 1:285/11.9\nAmigaNet:  Mike Barsoom @ 40:200/10.9\n@endnode\n\n@node Shareware\nPLEASE SUPPORT SHAREWARE!\n\nTrapPrefs is shareware, however unlike most shareware authors I have not\ncrippled it any way.  You can use all of TrapPrefs''s functions without any\nrestrictions or anoying requesters.\n\nPlease, if you use TrapPrefs on a regular basis, concider sending me the\nregistration fee.  Once I receive your registration fee I will promptly\nsend you a key file which will personalize your copy of TrapPrefs and\nunlock TrapListPrefs.\n\nThe following is the current price list for TrapPrefs/TrapListPrefs:\nRegister with keyfile sent via e-mail:   		$10.00 US.\nRegister with keyfile send via regular mail:    $12.00 US.\n\nNOTE: Keyfiles will only be mailed on floppy disk to users how pay $12.00.\n\nSending in your registration fee will help ensure futhor developement of\nTrapPrefs.  Also I will give priority to suggestions and questions from\nregister users.\n\nPlease see @{"Address" Link Address} for how to you can reach me and where to send in your\nregistration fee.\n\nNOTE:  I have received e-mail from several people, and have attempted to\n       reply but the messages keep being returned by FidoNet as\n       undeliverable.  If you also have an internet or AmigaNet address\n       please include it in your message.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node History "History"\nWhat has changed - most recent version is first.\n\nv1.2 \n    o About requester said ''TrapListPrefs'' instead of ''TrapPrefs'' (fixed)\n      - reported by Steffen Salzmann\n    o ''Abort'' did not work correctly, requester would appear more than\n       once (fixed)\n      - reported by Steffen Salzmann\n    o If you click on ''Abort'', old config will be restored\n      - suggested by Steffen Salzmann\n\nv1.1\n    o Localized a few more strings.  You will need TrapPrefs catalog v1.1\n      for the new strings to be localized.\n    o Fixed a few spelling errors\n      - reported by Michael Berg\n    o Added keyfile support, now when you register you will receive a\n      keyfile to personalize your copy.  TrapPrefs itself still remains\n      completely non crippled, however the TrapListPrefs will require the\n      key file in order to work.\n    o Added Abort and Continue options to error requesters when loading\n      config.\n      - suggested by Steffen Salzmann\n    o Added hypertext link to TrapDoor.guide.  Now pressing HELP over a\n      gadget will bring up the appropriate page in TrapDoor.guide.  NOTE:\n      This feature requires that TrapDoor.guide be available in your\n      AmigaGuide path.\n      - requested by Piergiorgio Ghezzo\n    o Added NodeList support, now if you have a nodelist TrapPrefs will\n      read it and display the name and sysop of your boss.\n\nv1.0\n    o Fixed several enforcer hits when Resetting to Defaults\n      - reported by Andre Schenk\n    o Fixed an enforcer hit which magically appeared when I upgraded to\n      MUI 2.2.  I believe the problem is with MUI v2.2 not TrapPrefs.\n    o Dropped beta status.\n\nv0.99ß\n    o Was reporting error reading COLOURS (fixed)\n      - reported by Johan Billing\n    o Misspelled ''keyword'' in one requester\n      - reported by Johan Billing\n    o Small change in catalog.  Now LogLevels are preceeded with two spaces\n      rather than ''\0333'', Except for Discreet.\n\nv0.98ß\n    o Non default options in cycle gadgets were displayed in white,\n      this made them unreadable when MUI was used in its default\n      configuration as the background was also white, now\n      style/color is user selectable with the tooltype color.\n      - reported by Kai Bolay\n    o Had wrong default for BBSChar, should have been ''!'' (fixed)\n    o Split KiwiPulse and SwePulse into two gadgets\n    o Added ''Cancel'' menu item to adjust window sizes.\n    o When a screen is opened for setting windowsizes or palette and\n      UseSysFont is selected, the screen will also use the SysFont\n    o Moved some gadgets around in the ''Modem'' page\n    o Was saving BBSChar with doublw quotes rather than single\n      quotes (fixed)\n      - reported by Andy Wasserman\n\nv0.97ß\n    o Argument after keyword CALL will now be quoted\n      -suggested by Adam Dawes\n    o Changed how call works, added ''Call Boss'' to cycle gadget, now will\n      correctly save the node number rather than the word ''BOSS'' after\n      keyword call.\n    o Could not read palette if digits were in hex (fixed)\n      - reported by Piergiorgio Ghezzo\n    o Added quite a few more strings to the catalog, this\n      will require a new catalog (if you made one)\n\nv0.96ß\n    o Added error message if MUI could not be found, or if it is the wrong\n      version.\n    o Was not reading config specified in icon when started from CLI without\n      any options (fixed)\n\nv0.95ß\n    o Small bug in reading catalog for menus (fixed)\n      - reported by Piergiorgio Ghezzo\n    o Changed menu shortcuts to comply with style guide\n      - suggested by Piergiorgio Ghezzo\n    o Save As... and Save will now default to last loaded file.\n      - suggested by Piergiorgio Ghezzo\n    o If no file is specified when started from CLI, TrapPrefs will load\n      the config specified in the icon with the tooltype ''CONFIG''\n\nv0.94ß\n    o Added locale.\n    o If you left the Cost string empty, TrapPrefs would still write\n      the keyword ''COST'' in the config (fixed)\n      - reported by Piergiorgio Ghezzo\n\nv0.93ß\n    o Was reporting error when reading ACCTMAX (fixed)\n      - reported by Piergiorgio Ghezzo\n    o Was incorrectly parsing CALL keyword, added sting gadget to\n      specify number to call (fixed)\n      - reported by Piergiorgio Ghezzo\n    o Forget ending quote when saving ACCTMAX (fixed)\n    o Could not set ''ARQ String'' if you selected NOSNIFFARQ and FASTEMSI\n      Now ARQ String is disabled when both NOSNIFFARQ and NOFASTEMSI are\n      set (fixed)\n    o rearranged gadgets a bit.\n\nv0.92ß\n    o Clicking tab on the directory page was skipping the nodelist string\n      (fixed)\n    o Gadgets on the screen page were not being disabled properly (fixed)\n    o Added Open, and Open As... menu items\n    o If two or more keyword appeared on the same line in the config file\n      only the first was being read (fixed)\n      - reported by Piergiorgio Ghezzo\n    o Added cli option and tooltype CONFIG\n      - suggested by Piergiorgio Ghezzo\n    o Strings which contained a \" in the middle were not being read, instead\n      an error was reported (fixed)\n      - reported by Piergiorgio Ghezzo\n    o If a dial string contained a ''*'' it would be lost when reading\n      the config (fixed)\n\nv0.91ß\n    o Second beta release\n    o Added palette setting\n    o Fixed a few bugs when reading and writting config file.\n    o Forgot keyword COLOURS when reading config file (fixed).\n    o Removed keywords SWait, and STimeout\n    o Rearranged GUI a bit.\n    o Return now activats the next string gadget.\n    o Reset to defaults was not resetting ''DisplayID'' and ''PubScreenName''\n      (fixed).\n    o If file already exists, you will get an ''Are you sure?'' requester.\n    o TrapPrefs will now use its icon, if its there, when iconified.\n    o Save saving config with ''SerialBuffSize'' not ''SerialBufSize'' (fixed)\n\nv0.9ß\n    o First beta release.\n    o palette feature not there yet :-)\n@endnode\n\n@node ToDo\n\nThe following are some ideas I still have for TrapPrefs, many of them will\ndepend on the response I get:\n\n    o Make TrapPrefs have the ability to sence if the config has changed,\n      and warn you if you try to exist without saving your changes.\n\n    o Any good ideas you may have :-)\n\n@endnode\n\n@node MUI\n\n                          This application uses\n\n\n                        MUI - MagicUserInterface\n\n                (c) Copyright 1993/94 by Stefan Stuntz\n\n\nMUI is a system to generate and maintain graphical user interfaces. With\nthe  aid  of  a  preferences program, the user of an application has the\nability to customize the outfit according to his personal taste.\n\nMUI is distributed as shareware. To obtain a complete package containing\nlots of examples and more information about registration please look for\na  file  called  "muiXXusr.lha"  (XX means the latest version number) on\nyour local bulletin boards or on public domain disks.\n\n          If you want to register directly, feel free to send\n\n\n                         DM 30.-  or  US$ 20.-\n\n                                  to\n\n                             Stefan Stuntz\n                        Eduard-Spranger-Straße 7\n                             80935 München\n                                GERMANY\n\n@endnode\n@node Questions\n1. I get an error while reading the config if my dial strings\n   contain ''='' in it.\n\n   This is a fault of AmigaDos.  I use ReadArgs() calls in order to read\n   the config, and this function uses the ''='' as a separator between key\n   words and arguments.  The fix for this is very easy, enclose the string\n   in quotes.  This is the way the examples in TrapDoor.guide are shown, and\n   how TrapPrefs will save them.\n\n   As an example use MODEMANSWER "~~~ATS7=25A|"\n                 not MODEMANSWER ~~~ATS7=25A|   <- this will report an error.\n\n2. I am using a white background for the cycle gadgets and I cannot read some\n   of the options.\n\n   The default options are shown in black and the non default are shown in\n   white by TrapPrefs per default.  This can be changed by setting the\n   tooltype @{"COLOR" link CLI}.  With this tooltype you can change the color, or even make\n   the items bold or italic.\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',53218,2,0,NULL,NULL,'trapdoor','scan',1780048787);
