2 * cREDITZ fOR mAJORS! 3 * cREDITZ fOR mAJORS fROM yOUR oWN gROUP!\n    pROVIDING yOU: Amiga ECS/AGA, PC, AmiExpress, Sex Pic, Sex Stories\n\n          ---»> nO nEW uSER pASSWORD aND/oR sYSTEM pASSWORD! <«---\n\n- -- ---------------------------------------------------------------- -- -\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',161525,9,0,NULL,NULL,'nvx_rem5','scan',1780048787);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('trb_kwtf','TRB_KWTF.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/TRB_KWTF.LHA','rexxdoor','XIM','KingsWTF.rexx',NULL,'Tribe','TRB','|  |/  /      \ K I N G S  |     <|  |> _/  R A N S O M |  |\  \  |   \_',replace('               __  __ ______\n              |  |/  /      \    \n   K I N G S  |     <|  |> _/  R A N S O M \n              |  |\  \  |   \_  \n              |__| \__\_|\___/\n               1-305-247-7605\n      KingsWTF v1.0 / Released By Tribe\n     WHAT THE FUCK! BBS HACKER PROTECTOR\n33.6 DigITal-X Prd/NirVana Dist Site! 33.6\n','\n',char(10)),'KingsWTF.doc',replace('\n===============================\n     WHAT THE FUCK?! v1.0\n===============================\n    By King Conan of TRIBE\n===============================\nKings Ransom - 1-305-247-7605\n===============================\n\n\n*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*+*=*=*= IMPORTANT! =*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*\n \n It is very highly recommended that you follow the instructions for\nthis utility to the letter.  Even though you may have installed many\nREXX DOORS to your system already, this particular door sets up a bit\ndiffrently then the rest.  Especially the part that pertains to editing\nyour "BBS.CMD" file.\n\n*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*+*=*=*= IMPORTANT! =*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*\n\nINSTALLATION\n------------\nNEEDED TO RUN:\n--------------\n1st off let me state something:  Arexx utils are compatible with ALL AMIGAS!\nif an Arexx util is not working for you, then you have not properly set it\nup & probably forgot to install some of the libraries or spelled something\nwrong somewhere.  Follow these instructions to the letter, & all should be\nfine!  I have also heard that people with certain 69030 accelators have\nproblems running COMPILED AREXX DOORS.. If you fall into this catagory,\nsorry...\n\n>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\nYou need Arexx Installed in your System.\n>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\nAREXX is "NOT" included with this Util.\n>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \nalso:   copy the file RPSTART into your C: and then edit your \n        "startup-sequence" or "user-startup" to load this file\n        upon BBS bootup.   ex. C:RPSTART\n\n        copy RexxPlus.lib \n             rexxplslib.library   files to your LIBS: directory.\n\nalso IMPORTANT: make sure you have "rexxdoor" & "rexxport" in your\n                BBS:UTILS/ directory... They are standard AmiExpress\n                commands, amd allow AmiExpress to properly communicate\n                with Arexx doors & utils.\n\nSETUP:\n------\n\n Make sure you have "WAIT" in your C: directory. This is a standard WORKBENCH\n command that can be found in the C: directory of your WORKBENCH DISK.  It is\n needed by this door in order for it to properly work.\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------\n\n Make a directory called:  DOORS:KingsWTF/\n \nand put these files in it: KingsWTF.rexx\n                           KingsWTF.cfg\n\n>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\n\nNow Edit your BBS.CMD file as so:    (READ THIS PART CAREFULLY!)\n\n---------------------------------------------\nFORMAT   RM050Doors:KingsWTF/KingsWTF.rexx\n---------------------------------------------\n |       |||  |           \n |       |||  ` ''Doors:KingsWTF/KingsWTF.rexx  - Location Of Program!\n |       |||     Make sure not to change this!!\n |       |||\n |       ||` 050 Is the minimum access to use this door. Change it to what\n |       ||      you like.\n |       ||\n |       |` M For a mutilnode bbs (S For single)\n |       |\n |       ` R For an rexx type door which will use the ''Rexxdoor'' Util\n |\n `Letter to bring the door up on the board. In this case ''FORMAT''\n \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nNOTE:  "DO-NOT" USE THE RETARD OPTION WITH THIS DOOR!!!!!\n        ^^^^^^\n\n*FORMAT        RM050Doors:KingsInfo/KingsInfo.rexx\n|\n`-Retard Option. To Make Sure they only use ''FORMAT'' & only ''FORMAT'' to get\n the door to come up. If not used, things such as ''FORMAT HD0:''  and \n ''FORMAT DRIVE''  would still bring up the door (WHICH IS WHAT YOU WANT!)\n \n                   SO DONT USE THE RETARD OPTION!!!!\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\n\nWHAT DOES THIS DOOR DO?\n-----------------------\n \n  Every sysop, no matter how liked, always runs into a real jerk every\nnow & then.. And sometimes these jerks have mischevious attentions like\nbringing down your BBS for good.  Now most sysops are pretty smart, & take\nall precautions in assuring the safety of their BBS.  Things like making\nsure a user does not have access to damaging commands like "FORMAT" or\n"DELETE" is always at the top of a good sysops list.\n \n  But if a user does have the attention of damaging your BBS & actually\ntries to damage it, why should he be given a simple:\n \n             "YOU DONOT HAVE ACCESS TO THAT COMMAND"\n\n    when he should be punished for his damaging attentions?!!\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  This door is a SYSOP COMMAND/HACKER PROTECTOR. What this simply means\nis that if a user tries to access a command that he knows he has no right\nusing, he will be punished!\n \nFOR EXAMPLE:\n \nIf you wanted to protect the "FORMAT" command, you would put the following\nentry into your "BBS.CMD" file:\n\n               FORMAT   RM050Doors:KingsWTF/KingsWTF.rexx\n\nIf you wanted to protect the "DELETE" command, you would put the following\nentry into your "BBS.CMD" file:\n\n               DELETE   RM050Doors:KingsWTF/KingsWTF.rexx\n\netc, etc, etc....\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nYou can protect any command you want, (as long as the command in all\nreality is not really used on the BBS)..  What I mean by this is there\nreally is no "FORMAT" or "DELETE" command on any bbs, but alot of users\ndo-not relize this (or are just plain stupid), and try to access these\ncommands anyhow..\n \n---------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nNow, with the above entries placed into the "BBS.CMD" file, if a user\ntypes into the BBS :\n \n  Format\n  Format DF0:\n  Format HD0:\n  Format DH1:  etc, etc, etc... (SAME WITH DELETE)\n \n It will load up "WHAT THE FUCK?!" .....\n \nAs long as you donot insert a "*" (RETARD OPTION) into the "BBS.CMD" file\nfor a command, any FORM of that command typed out will load the door.\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nNow, Here is EXACTLY WHAT THE DOOR DOES:\n----------------------------------------\n  \n When a user has triggered the door to be loaded, the very 1st thing it\ndoes is:\n \n             1> Drops Users Access Level to 10  (NEW USER)\n             2> Changes Users Conference Access  X________\n                                                 123456789\n\nThen it displays the following message to the user:  (IN COLOR!)\n\n+===========================================================================+ \n|                                                                           |\n|                           WHAT THE FUCK!!  v1.0                           |\n|                                                                           |\n|   It would seem that you have made a very serious ACCESS LEVEL decision.  |\n|    In fact, Congradulations, you have just lowered your ACCESS LEVEL to   |\n|                              NEW-USER Status!                             |\n|                                                                           |\n|               New-Users are always REQUIRED to BEG for ACCESS.            |\n|                                                                           |\n|                         So Start Begging Asshole!                         |\n|                                                                           |\n+===========================================================================+\n|             A KINGS RANSOM/TRIBE Production.   1-305-247-7605             |\n+===========================================================================+\n\n>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\nNow the next thing it does depends on what you put into the CONFIG-FILE..\n\nBEFORE RUNNING THIS DOOR:\n-------------------------\n \n Before you run this door you need to edit the "KingsWTF.CFG" file.\n There is only "1" FLAG that needs to be edited in this file. \n \n       FLAG\n(LINE1)  N  ; KICK HACKER OFF BBS RIGHT-AWAY, OR SEND HIM TO CONF1? Y=KICKOFF\n                                                                    N=CONF1 \n\n                Y=KICK HIM OFF!!            \n\n                  Selecting this FLAG will DROP CARRIER on the user\n                  after the message (ABOVE IN LAST AREA) is displayed.\n                  When the user calls back, he will only be able to access\n                  CONFERENCE #1..(THE NEW-USERS AREA).. He will have \n                  New-Users Access & will not be able to do anything\n                  but leave you a COMMENT explaining his actions & begging\n                  for forgiveness.  This option is used by the "PISSED-OFF"\n                  sysop who never wants to see the stinking HACKER AGAIN.\n\n\n                N=THROW HIM INTO CONFERENCE #1\n                  in this mode, the user will "NOT" be thrown off the BBS\n                  immediately.  Instead, his access is lowered, and he is\n                  placed into CONFERENCE #1..(THE NEW-USERS AREA)..\n \n                  This option is used by the "NOT SO PISSED" sysop. hehe.\n                  It allows you to give the user an IMMEDIATE chance of\n                  leaving a COMMENT to the sysop & explain himself. That\n                  is, if he has the balls to do so..\n\n>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\n\nLOG INFORMATION\n---------------\n \n  This utility will write to your NODEx/CALLERSLOG after an illegal\nHACK attempt of a command.\n \n  THE "LOG ENTRY" will display the following information:\n\n        +------------------------------------------------------------+\n                 WHAT THE FUCK?  v1.0  STOPS ANOTHER HACKER!!\n        +------------------------------------------------------------+\n                SHAOLIN attempted to BRING DOWN THE BBS!!!\n \n                Access Level WAS: 100\n                Access Level NOW: 10  >>> NEW-USER STATUS! <<<\n \n                EXACT TIME OF MISHAP: Sun Apr 04 08:09:35 1993\n        +------------------------------------------------------------+\n           Send THANKS To: KING CONAN at KINGS RANSOM  305-247-7605 \n        +------------------------------------------------------------+\n\n>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\n\nSOME LAST THOUGHTS\n------------------\n \nRemember, you can use this door to protect as many commands as you wish,\nJust put a seperate entry for each command into your BBS.CMD file.\n \nAlso, it essential that the command is not actually used by the BBS.\n \nThings you might want to try is stuff like:\n \nIF YOU RUN "NOSNUKE" rename it to "NN" or something, for you & your Co''s,\nand then have entries in "BBS.CMD" for NOSNUKE & NUKE.. User tries to load\nNOSNUKE or NUKE he gets accessed lowered..\n \n In other words, protect your commands with some alternate names, & let the\nusers find out the hard way that you have been expecting their bullshit.\nAs far as im concerned, all users know that sysop commands are meant for\nuse ONLY by the sysops.. If he''s that stupid to try them, well then...\n\n---------\n \nAt any rate, you sould definately have this door protect:\n \nFORMAT , KILL ,  &  DELETE .....\n\n\n>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\nGREETS/THANX\n------------\n \nWhite Knight  -  Helping me look up stuff in Arexx Books.\n\nDenon         -  Actually logging in and REALLY TRYING to fuck-up bbs!\n                 Also staying up till 1:26am with me getting out all the\n                 kinks.. Thanx.. \n         \nTRIBE         -  To my fellow TRIBE mates!\n\nLSD           -  D-MAN, ZANDOR, MALACAR (or MALCAR?) hehe anyways glad you\n                 guys really enjoy my stuff!\n\n==========================================================================\n\nALL UPDATES TO MY UTILS CAN BE FOUND AT:\n----------------------------------------\nIf you have any questions or i forgot to mention some particulars about \nthis utility, then call me at:                                    _  _\n                                                                  \][/\n                     _      Hast La Vista Baby!                   / *\\n      _             (_)      ____        ____        ____        / __/\n     | \ __ __ __ __| |_____/ ___\______/ ___\______/ ___\______/ /____\n     |  |  |  |  |  | |____/ /_________/ /_________/ /_________/ /_____\\n     |  |__|__|__|__| |___/ /_________/ /_________/ /_________/ /______/\n     |_/            |_|  /_/      \____/      \____/      \____/\n                    (_)                 \n                         KINGS RANSOM  -  305-247-7605\n                           >> 16.8 DUAL STANDARD! <<\n\nAlso, call if you have any suggestions on updates to any of my present \nutils, or ideas for some new ones.. I donot claim to be the best, but if\ni think i can do it, Ill try!\n\n============================================================================\nFIXES AND UPDATES REPORT:\n-------------------------\n\n4-5-93   v1.0    First Completion of program.. Will release after a couple\n                 of days of major testing.. But all seems to be 100%\n\n============================================================================\n\nALSO CHECK OUT:\n===============\n \nKings Info v1.4  -  Replacement "W" command that allows for MANUAL or\n                    RANDOM password generation.. Nice FRESH look!!\n\nKings Help v1.0  -  The first ever HELP-DOOR for AmiExpress that allows \n                    users to get help on "ANY" command you have installed\n                    on the BBS!!\n\n===========================================================================\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',114228,15,0,NULL,NULL,'trb_kwtf','scan',1780048787);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('trb_vdt3','TRB_VDT3.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/TRB_VDT3.LHA','Copy','XIM','Copy',NULL,NULL,'TRB','+   </an /)amme Of Tr¡be Presents   | |                                   | +     VDTop v1.3 For AmiExpress     +',replace('    .+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+.\n    +   </an /)amme Of Tr¡be Presents   |\n    |                                   |\n    +     VDTop v1.3 For AmiExpress     +\n    + WeekTop For Different Conferences +\n    |                                   |\n    +  Final Arexx Version. All Fixed!  |\n    `+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+''\n','\n',char(10)),'VDTop.Doc',replace('\n                        VDTop v1.3 By </an /)amme                  \n                      ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~  \n              \n       For Any Comments Or Problems, You Can Reach Me On My Board... \n                                                                  \n         .:| DeATH RoW (416)548-8557/548-9558/548-6632/548-0240 |:.\n\n                                                                [05/03/93]\n\n First off.. lemma say sorry for not having the full C version ready yet.\nI''m still learning the language but have managed to convert most of the\nprogram already.  However, instead of making you wait anylong, I decided\nto release the 1.3 as the Final arexx full working version. This version\nhas been tested and all the bugs removed. Once again however - the messages\nhave been tested on 3.0 and 2.34, but if your not sure or just for safety,\ntest the message feature on a backup or test conference. You should do\nthis will all utils that use the message base anyway. It should work fine,\nbut you never know. :) Now on for the docs and changes...\n\n  Installing\n  ~~~~~~~~~~\n This utility, unlike most of my other ones is not to be run as a door but\ninstead from a cli/shell or in a logoff script for ami-express. Yes, please\ndon''t run this util if you don''t have ami-express installed. This door will \nalso work with any version of Ami-express you are running.\n \n First copy the VDTop program to your ''C:'' dir.  Next copy the rexxlib \nif you don''t have it already into your ''Libs:''. Also,if you don''t\nalready have the ''Delete'' and ''Copy'' files copy them to your ''C:'' dir as the\nprogram will need them to work properly. Copy The VDTop.Prefs file into\nyour ''S:'' directory as well as header files. You need the Prefs file for\nthe program to work, but you don''t need the headers, but more on this later.\nNow, edit your logoff batchs for your nodes to be like ''VDTop 1'' for node1,\n''VDTop 2'' for node 2, so when someone logs off node 2 it will run the VDTop\nprogram and look through the callerslog for node 2. It MUST be run in the\nlogoffs, as it needs to update the information after each caller.\n\n Now your ready to configure it to your board.\n\n  Other Utils\n  ~~~~~~~~~~~\n This weektop unlike some week or month tops works great with Nosnuke\nand AmiFaker. These two programs are about the only faker programs worth\nmentioning that I have seen. Big pat on the back to Spock and Nosferatu, \nand also thanks to both of them for writing callerslog entries that are\neasy to work with.  The VDTop will work perfectly with these utils, all\ngiven or subtracted credits by these utils will be updated for the VDTop\nfiles. So continue to NUKE away without worry.\n\n  Preferences\n  ~~~~~~~~~~~\n First off, if you would like to have custom header files for each conf,\nhere''s what you do. Make a file or files in ''S:'' called \n''VDTopHeader#/.Gr'' - Where # is the number of the conf to use this header\nand .Gr or no .Gr is for Ansi and no ansi respectivlely.  So A\n''VDTopHeader2'' Would be for conference 2 with no color, and \n''VDTopHeader2.Gr'' would be for conference 2 with color, and\n''VDTopHeader1.Gr'' would be for conference 1 with color, etc. There are a\nfew example files included in the ''S:'' directory for your viewing.\n\n NOTE: You need not use custom headers, but they do make the output files\n       look nicer. If you choose to not use any header files, then it\n       will default to a clear screen as the header. If you use a header,\n       you will have to include a clearscreen if you want it (Ctrl+L) at\n       the top, but you probably already knew that. :)\n\n Now the tough part, the preference file itself. I tried to make it as easy\nas I could, but due to the highly configurable nature of the program, you\nwill need to take some time to make sure all is in order.  Here''s an\nexample preference file and what every line does.  Configure each\nline to match your board. Beside the function will be a reference marker.\nSee that marker below the example for a full explanation.\n\n---------------------------------START-----------------------------------\nW                                   - Amount Of Time Before Reseting\nVan Damme - Sysop                   - Name Of Sysop\n1 Holding Cell                      - Conference Names\n2 The Chair      \n3 Cell Block     \n4 Gas Chamber    \n5 Warden''s Lounge\n6 The Shower     \n7 Courtyard      \n------------------                  - ******** First Divider ********\n2                                   - Conference Number\nAMIGA WARES                         - Name To Be Used For Conference\nY                                   - Use A Total Stat Bar In Output\nChair                               - Name Of Conference On Harddrive\nEALL                                - Receiver Of Message\nY                                   - Ansi Option For Top Records\nBBS:Chair/Bulletins/Bull3.Txt       - Output File For Top Records\n10                                  - Number Of Uploaders On Output\n0                                   - Number Of Downloaders On Output\nY                                   - Ansi Option For First Output\nBBS:Chair/Bull50.Txt.Gr             - Output File Name For First Output \nN                                   - Ansi Option For Second Ouput\nBBS:Chair/Bull50.Txt                - Output File Name For Second Output\n------------------                  - *********** Divider ***********\n3                                   - Conference Number\nCONSOLE WARES                       - Name To Be Used For Conference\nY                                   - Name To Be Used For Conference\nConsole                             - Name Of Conference On Harddrive\nVan Damme                           - Receiver Of Message\n                                    - Ansi Option For Top Records \n                                    - Output File For Top Records \n4                                   - Number Of Uploaders On Output\n3                                   - Number Of Downloaders On Output\nN                                   - Ansi Option For First Output  \nBBS:Console/Bull50.Txt              - Output File Name For Second Output\n------------------                  - *********** Divider ***********\n4                                   - Conference Number\nIBM WARES                           - Name To Be Used For Conference\nN                                   - Use A Total Stat Bar In Output\n                                    - Name Of Conference On Harddrive\n                                    - Receiver Of Message\nY                                   - Ansi Option For Top Records\nBBS:Chair/Bulletins/Bull3.Txt       - Output File For Top Records\n8                                   - Number Of Uploaders On Output\n2                                   - Number Of Downloaders On Output\nY                                   - Ansi Option For First Output\nBBS:Chair/Bull50.Txt.Gr             - Output File Name For First Output \nN                                   - Ansi Option For Second Ouput\nBBS:Chair/Bull50.Txt                - Output File Name For Second Output\nN                                   - Ansi Option For Third Ouput \nRam:Testing.Txt                     - Output File Name For Third Output \n----------------------------------END------------------------------------\n\n Yes.. quite a big preference file, but don''t lose all hope at once. It\njust looks big. It''s really easy to figure out if you take it step by step.\nThe first thing to notice is that between the first divider and the rest\nof the preference file the two parts are different. Before the first\ndivider, we have the conference outlines and other things - ONCE. After\nthe first divider comes the entries for EACH conference. You have one\nof this for each conference. So after the first divider, you can have\nas many entries as you want, but before it, you will always have one. \n\n * Before First Divider *\n\n - Amount Of Time Before Reseting\n\nThis is the first line in the program always. It is the length of time\nthat the program will run for before reseting.  Most people will use\nit as a Weektop, which is what it works best at, but you can set it for\nany number of days that you wish. On this line, Use a ''W'' for week, ''D'' for\na single Day, and ''M'' for a month.  After this time limit is reached, it\nwill post the message with the final results (optional) and also put\nout the top record bulletin(optional). You can also use a number like 3 or\n13 for a specific number of days instead of a day,week or month.  Note,\nthat if at any time you change this value after the program is working, it\nwill start over at day one of this new value, but the users stats will\nremain unchanged. (NOTE: For a true weektop, start the door or change to\na week on Monday.)\n\n - Name Of Sysop\n   \nStraigh forward, the name of the sysop or person that you wish to have\nthe message come from on the board.  It doesn''t have to be an active\naccount, it can be anyname, although the Sysop''s name works best in most\ncases. :)\n              \n - Conference Names\n\nThis program only supports 9 confs maximum now. If you have a problem with\nthis lemma know.  The conference name part contains a list of all the\nconferences on your board (1-9) and how they appear EXACTLY on your board -\nIt will use this name when searching through the callerslog to find\nwhat went to which conference. It is not case sensitive.  \n\n Changed - you now don''t have to have 9 conferencers listed. List only the\nones that you wish to keep track of, in anyorder. You can list 2 conferences\nhere, or all nine. It''s up to you. The only thing to remember is to put the\ndivider after the conferences, and to make sure the number that appears\nbefore the conf matches up with the first number of long entry for that \nconference. For example, if you list 1 in the confs as Amiga - like:\n\n1 Amiga\n--------(First divider)\n\nThen make sure that the entry that has 1 is this conf, so the long entry \n\n--------(First divider)\n1           \nAMIGA WARES \nY           \nBBS:Chair\nEtc..\n\nIs for the amiga conf, since they both have 1. Got it.. Good.. :)\n\n\nExample for the conf list (anyorder, anynumber up to 9 and at least 1):\n\n--------\n2 Amiga Crap - Unknowns World HQ\n5 Pc Wares\n6 Pornal pics\n7 Elite Files\n---------\n The reason for this conference part in the config is because of the\nrelative conference option on /X v2.37 or higher. Without doing it like\nthis, things get messed up badly. Just ask Kidlat! on the pit.. hehe.\n\n * After First Divider *\n\n NOTE: All this options are repeated over for each conference you wish \n       to have a record for.\n \n - Conference Number                 \n\nThis is the number of the conference as it appears on the Conference\nlists in the preference file beginning. So using the example in the\nConference listings, if I used 2 here it would be the \n''2 Amiga Crap - Unknowns World HQ'' conference that this preference entry\nwould be for. All other entries until the next divider will be for this\nconference.\n\n - Name To Be Used For Conference  \n\nThis is the name that you wish to appear for this conference on the\noutput bulletins. It doesn''t have to match anything, it can be whatever\nyou like. Like ''This bulletin''s for amiga'' or anything you want it to be.\nIf you can''t think of anything, you could always use the acutal conference\nname here. :)\n  \n - Use A Total Stat Bar In Output    \n\nA ''Y'' or ''N'' for this option here. If you use a Y, then the output \nbulletin for this conference will have a stat bar at the bottem with the\ntotal number of calls, ups, etc. If you have a no, no start bar will \nappear at the bottem of the output file. \n\n - Name Of Conference On Harddrive   \n\nGive the complete path to the location of the conference on your harddrive.\nIt''s like the one you have listed in your config or acp.startup for /X.\nSo if your amiga conf is in ''Dh2:BBS/Amiga'' then list it as this. I removed\nthe auto BBS: feature as although you should, more then 1 harddrive can\nlead to problems. (Thanks for the insight King Conan).\n\n NOTE: Leave this space BLANK for no message output.\n\n - Receiver Of Message               \n\n This is who the message will be written to at the end of the term. ''EALL''\nand ''ALL'' work nicely, but you can use any user name you wish.\n\n  NOTE: Leave this space BLANK for no message output.\n\n - Ansi Option For Top Records \n      \n ''Y'' or ''N'' , whether the Top record bulletin will be in ansi or not.\n\n  NOTE: Leave this space BLANK for no top record bulletin.\n\n - Output File For Top Records       \n\nThe output file for the top records of this conference goes here. It will\nkeep track of the 5 best uploaders and downloaders of all time in a \nseperate bulletin. This isn''t really something to show users when they\nlogon, but rather as a bulletin for them to view like a top cps one.\n\n  NOTE: Leave this space BLANK for no message output.\n\n - Number Of Uploaders On Output \n\n Simpley, any number (The more the slower, so no 100 users eh?) which will\nbe the number of uploaders that will be displayed on the output file.\n\n  NOTE: Use a 0 for no uploaders.    \n\n - Number Of Downloaders On Output   \n\n Simpley, any number (The more the slower, so no 100 users eh?) which will\nbe the number of downloaders that will be displayed on the output file.\n\n  NOTE: Use a 0 for no downloaders.\n\n - Ansi Option For First Output   \n\n''Y'' or ''N'' for whether or not the output file will have ansi or not.\n   \n - Output File Name For First Output \n\nThe output file for the list that will contain the top users for the week\nas outlined in the number of uploaders/downloaders. This is the file\nto display to the users when they log on to your board.\n    \n - Ansi Option For Etc..\n\n''Y'' or ''N''. You can have more then one output file (one ansi, one not, etc)\nfor each conference. Just remember for each output file you want, have\na Ansi option line and a Output filename line for each.\n\n - Output File Name For Etc..\n\nSee Above.\n\n\n Now here you would put a divider, and do the same thing above for\nthe next conference, until you have a complete entry with all the things\nabove (after the first divider) for each. And then another divider, and\nthe conference values, etc.\n\n\n And Remember, if all else fails, call me.. or go through my provided config\nand edit and change to suit your own instead of doing it from scratch. :)\n\n  Paths\n  ~~~~~\n If you a sysop, make sure that each conf has only 1 or two paths listed\nin the ''Paths'' file. For if they go to one conference and download all \nthe files from the board in there, they will all show up there and not\nwhere they should, in the conference they came from. Sysops and cosysops,\nmake sure to nuke the files while your in the conference that the file\nis in. I don''t see this as a problem at all, but you''ll always get the\non person that tries it and complains why the user lost credits in the \nwrong conf.\n\n HOWEVER - NOTE that if you like your users to download all their stuff\nfrom a single conf, you can still set it up properly. Just don''t use\nany downloaders in the output. Only list the top uploaders. Since a \nuser HAS to go to a conf to upload a file there (unlike downloading) the\nuploaded stats appear in the write spots.\n\n  Output Files\n  ~~~~~~~~~~~~\n The normal output files will have a Day(?/?) on it, which will list at\nwhat point your at so far. Like 2/5 would mean your on day 2 of 5. Once\nit hits 5/5 it will reset, or whatever you have it set at. This ''Day(?/?)''\nisn''t listed on the final top record bulletin, it''s replaced with the\nwords ''TOP USERS''. Also, only the final Bulletin and the messages have\nthe ''Updated On:'' now, as it wasn''t needed on the bulletins that are\nshown to the users when they log on, they get updated everytime someone\nlogs off. Ya.. 4 second diffence between updates.. hehe. gotta show that..\n\n Also note that the final top record bulletin will take only 1 user from\nthe term. So after the first week say, the top uploader and downloader\nwill be added to the top record bulletin.  ONLY the top users from that\nweek.  Next week, the top 2 users will be added, etc. It''s ONLY the top\nusers, not everybody.\n\n  Working Methods\n  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nDue to the complex nature of trying to keep seperate track of each file\ntransfer in seperate confs, I had to use a few output files that will\nbe created in ''S:''. You don''t need to touch them at all, they will update,\ndelete and be recreated as the program needs them. If you do for some\nreason need to know what they do and their purpose, they are:\n\nS:VDTop.Dates - Contains the Information about what day of the week it''s\n                currently on and how many more to go before reseting. If\n                This file is delete it will start over at the beginning of\n                the term.\n\nS:VDTop.Store - This is the major storage file, containing all the info\n                for every user. If deleted, all user stats will be lost for\n                the current term.\n\nS:VDTop.Stats - Contains the information needed for the stat bars - the\n                Total of all the calls, ups, etc for each conf. If deleted,\n                the stat bar information will all be reset to 0 for the term.\n\nS:VDTop.Final - Contains the top record information for each conf. If\n                Deleted, all the top records will be lost. Don''t delete it.\n\n  Options\n  ~~~~~~~\n\n One of the nicest options you''ll have noticed is the ability to keep\na SEPERATE record of the file transfers in each conference. No longer\nwill the amiga and console users have to try to compete against the mighty\nPC users, they can compete for the weektop in the confs with their own\nusers.  This utility isn''t meant to be a top uploader util, that would\nbe imposible to do for each conf, but it functions nicely as a week , day\nor month top.  I have set the limit of days to 99 max, cause after this\nthe storage files will probably become too big and slow the program down\ntoo much.. It''s only rexx you know. :)\n\n\n  Setup\n  ~~~~~\n The best way to set up the output files is as follows. Make the output\nfiles bulls in the Conference name directories, so every time they would\njoin the amiga conference, they would get the amiga list, or if they join\nthe PC section, they get the PC list. Output the top records to the \nbulletin section for each conf, so you''ll have a top pc records in the\nPC conf, and top amiga records in the amiga conference.  Use a nice big\nAmiga or PC header for the output lists, or mabey who''s HQ it is, etc.\nKinda like for the last caller (by pot-Noodle).  If you want to see\nthis method (and the method you should be using) call my board or the pit,\nas I know he has it setup properly.. hehe..  Also make the message go\nto the write conf! :)\n\n  Examples\n  ~~~~~~~~\n For some examples of the kind of output files you will be getting, look\nin the ExampleOutput directory in the archive.  The following example files\nare included:\n\nBull10.Txt       - Console Wares Section With 3 Up/3 Down And No Ansi\nBull10.Txt.Gr    - Console Wares Section With 3 Up/3 Down And Ansi\nBull50.Txt       - Amiga Wares Section With 10 Up/0 Down And No Ansi\nBull50.Txt.Gr    - Amiga Wares Section With 10 Up/0 Down And Ansi\nBull3.Txt        - Top Record Bulletin In Amiga Conf And Ansi\n\n  History\n  ~~~~~~~\n v1.0 : -No Known Bugs Or Problems. (Beta Release)\n v1.1 : -Public Release Under Tribe Label.\n        -Added Custom Headers For Each Conference.\n        -User Friendly To NosNuke And AmiFaker Now.\n        -Made To Work With /X''s Relative Conference Feature.\n        -Changed Preference Outline.\n        -Adjusted Output File Structure.\n        -Removed ''Updated On'' From Normal Output Files (Not Needed Here).\n        -Fixed Many Message Base Errors.\n        -Added Total Stat Bar (Optional).\n        -Many Other Small Bugs Fixed.\n        -Compiled Size (211824).\n v1.2 : -Found & Fixed Major Right After Releasing - Wouldn''t Read \n         Conference Joining Properly. Nobodys Perfect.\n        -Compiled Size (212584).\n v1.3 : -Found & Fixed Bug That Would Not Get The Users Name Correct If\n         It Was More Then One Word With NosNuke And AmiFaker.\n        -Removed Adding Of Credits Feature. Not Needed.\n        -No Longer Removed * Credits For Fakes. Only Original Byte Size\n         Of Faked File Is Removed. (*100 Off Would Removed All The Upload\n         Total Stats)\n        -Found Message Base Error That Could Corrupt Your Headfile.\n        -Amount Of Days Fixed In Final Bulletin.\n        -Full Path For Conference For Preferences Now Needed.\n        -Compiled Size (201580)\n\n  Greets\n  ~~~~~~\n A big big greet goes out to Akira of the pit bbs, for coming up with\nsuch a wonderful idea for a utility. I''ll tell ya, it was fucking hell \ntrying to figure out this one, but after a few days (hehe) I prevailed.\n\n Thanks to B.O.B, Danzig, and all other users on bytemasters BBS that\ntried the Beta version and let me know how to improve/fix the program up.\nAlso thanks that no one spreaded it out, I can trust you guys with other\nbeta versions of upcoming utilitys.\n\n Thanks to Akira and Kidlat of the Pit bbs again for helpful suggestions\non how to make it better.\n\n Thanks to PMF for explaining in english what Virtual Conferences were.\n Send hugs and kisses to Trixie for me.. hehe\n\n Thanks as always to Nzo for info and opinions on the door and how to make\nit better.\n\n Thanks to Spock and Nosferatu for great nuking utils, and writing\na callerslog good enough for me to extract what I needed.\n\n Thanks to the uploaders on my board that allowed me to see if it''s working.\nhehe.\n\n Great big Thanks to Illicit Trader who noticed a major bug just before\nthe file went public. Close one, thanks dude.\n\n Thanks to Tribe for giving me a group to release it under. \n\n I Hope to see this util being put to good use on boards everywhere. You \n amiga users always complained about getting shafted by the ibm users, well\n now do something about it. Tell your sysops to install VDTop now!\n\n Well I had a nice break, and had some fun. Im speading most of my time\n(few hours a week. hehe) in front of the computer on learning C, which is\ncoming along nicely. Also, to keep my utils updated, I''m working on an\nupdate of VDFree and VDRequest (v3.0) - Both loaded with so many nice\nnew features that will keep you satisfied for awhile at least. I really like\nhow the VDRequest is coming along, with features such as messages, long\nand short descriptions,awarding of credits, deletion of downloaded requests,\nand alot of other stuff. :)\n\n And a few greets to... \n\n Skol - I''m jeolous. You call Paradox''s board more then mine! :(\n Nzo - I talk to you more then I talk to myself when I''m lonely!\n       And where''s my damn dms checker for my board.. Arrggg!! \n PMF - So have you given Trixie The Big UK Sausage yet??\n /\KiRA - 300$ Phone bill from your board (and bytemasters hehe).. ARGGG!\n MAGNUS - Greets friend! How''s it been going? You still around?\n mUb - Greets to you too dude. Thanks for the support!\n Phideaux! - The AGA God lives and rules. :)\n Ceejay - Greets Mate. Save me a brewskie - make that whiskey, and alot.\n Rambo - New Blood. That''s What We Need. Where''s the Conference?\n Elf-Co - One day I''m going to mail you something!\n Ice Cube - Long time no talk dude. Call sometime!\n Zen - Always my best friend around! :) Never lose touch.\n Echo - Thank you for calling and talking your C disks. eheh\n Kidlat - I expect you to be using this door! :) Long Live VDEdit!!!\n Zandor - Speeded trader number one. Flames shoot off my modem when\n          you call. \n Squid - You have good taste since you run my utils. hehe\n Cragar - I shall talk with ya soon if you ever call back.\n Illicit Trader - Thanks for the console support. I really need it!\n Gilby - You should call me more! I may have PC one day.\n AxeL - Greets To My Newfound Friend. Where''s the asm examples?\n King Conan - Thanks for the update ideas. Keep the doors coming.\n Denon - Thanks for the update ideas as well. Really Appriciated.\n Eddie The Head - I''ll try to send some runners to your board then. \n                  Also, The Callback door went out in flames. I could\n                  find no way to do it. I''m not worthy. :)\n Robster - Thanks for the BBS support - Uploadwise!.\n Alberta - Good luck with the board. I''m sure it will work out.\n Esskayare - Did you get Your computer back out of your car when you found\n             out it was PMF and Nzo on the phone and not AT&T? hehe\n TsM - Greets to ya dude. Keep coding. Nice pretty dir util.\n Shen - Nice logon node door. I edited it abit though.. hehe. Thanks for it.\n        I''m running it now. (Remember to delete Temp Files In ram:)\n Sinatra - Thanks for the testing of VDEdit 2.5!\n Yankee Rose - Thanks for the VDColordir Idea. Glad to see the board back up!\n Kitaro - How''s the board doing m8? Call back.\n Shaggy - The Best Console Support I''ve seen yet. Where''d ya go?? :)\n Coca Cola Kid - What happened to that code? So quick eh?\n SkyLark - You really are the Number One Skull Brother. I bow to you! NOT\n The Biker - Kewl board.  Great name, can I take a drive?\n Blade - Long Live The Top Uploader! And Nzo will get ya next time!\n MetalBasher! - You really are the ascii Genius! Call for the /X help.\n Sir Garbagetruck - I hate to see someone crying. Here''s you mega kewl\n                    Greet. I will even make it three lines long, longer\n                    then any other one. Don''t you feel special now?? \n                    (Oops, make that 4. Eddie has a three liner.. hehe)\n Pazza - I''m gonna get that movie with the Hermaphodite! Yes, I''m a freak \n         and proud of it! I can''t wait to watch it. hehe\n Boomer - Your acsii is so kewl I have to greet you. I''m not worthy to use\n          them in my humble snap util.\n\n Greets To The Fellow Ami-Express Coders: \n\n Dr. G, Sigma Seven, Cool Falco, Maltese Falcon, Nosferatu, Pot-Noodle, \n Caffeine, Dux, Spock, GiapDJ, Trash, The Bird, Axeman, Shadow Man, Delusion.\n\n Your stuff is all top quality. Keep those utils coming guys.\n\n                 Send greets if you want them back!\n \n And those that I know but forgot, and also those users that still value\nfriendship over all else, and of course to all you other ami-express door\nwriters out there. Drop me a line on my board sometime, I''d be glad to help\ntest your utils or give you the latest updates on mine.\n\n Remember to call my board. I need some console users badly.. and amiga\nusers are always more then welcome!\n\n\n        Warm Greetings to all my friends in Tectron and Tribe.\n\n                       			           Later dudes.. Till then\n\n                   - Van Damme (TW,SA - U2 Is the Greatest Band Ever! Sure)\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',92735,3,0,NULL,NULL,'trb_vdt3','scan',1780048787);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('trb_vdtp','TRB_VDTP.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/TRB_VDTP.LHA','Copy','XIM','Copy',NULL,NULL,'TRB','+   </an /)amme Of Tr¡be Presents   | |                                   | +     VDTop v1.1 For AmiExpress     +',replace('    .+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+.\n    +   </an /)amme Of Tr¡be Presents   |\n    |                                   |\n    +     VDTop v1.1 For AmiExpress     +\n    + WeekTop For Different Conferences +\n    |                                   |\n    + The ONE For The Best Utils Around | \n    `+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+=+''\n33.6 DigITal-X Prd/NirVana Dist Site! 33.6\n','\n',char(10)),'VDTop.Doc',replace('\n                        VDTop v1.1 By </an /)amme                  \n                      ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~  \n              \n       For Any Comments Or Problems, You Can Reach Me On My Board... \n                                                                  \n         .:| DeATH RoW (416)548-8557/548-9558/548-6632/548-0240 |:.\n\n                                                                [04/19/93]\n\n  Installing\n  ~~~~~~~~~~\n This utility, unlike most of my other ones is not to be run as a door but\ninstead from a cli/shell or in a logoff script for ami-express. Yes, please\ndon''t run this util if you don''t have ami-express installed. This door will \nalso work with any version of Ami-express you are running.\n \n First copy the VDTop program to your ''C:'' dir.  Next copy the rexxlib \nif you don''t have it already into your ''Libs:''. Also,if you don''t\nalready have the ''Delete'' and ''Copy'' files copy them to your ''C:'' dir as the\nprogram will need them to work properly. Copy The VDTop.Prefs file into\nyour ''S:'' directory as well as header files. You need the Prefs file for\nthe program to work, but you don''t need the headers, but more on this later.\nNow, edit your logoff batchs for your nodes to be like ''VDTop 1'' for node1,\n''VDTop 2'' for node 2, so when someone logs off node 2 it will run the VDTop\nprogram and look through the callerslog for node 2. It MUST be run in the\nlogoffs, as it needs to update the information after each caller.\n\n Now your ready to configure it to your board.\n\n  Other Utils\n  ~~~~~~~~~~~\n This weektop unlike some week or month tops works great with Nosnuke\nand AmiFaker. These two programs are about the only faker programs worth\nmentioning that I have seen. Big pat on the back to Spock and Nosferatu, \nand also thanks to both of them for writing callerslog entries that are\neasy to work with.  The VDTop will work perfectly with these utils, all\ngiven or subtracted credits by these utils will be updated for the VDTop\nfiles. So continue to NUKE away without worry.\n\n  Preferences\n  ~~~~~~~~~~~\n First off, if you would like to have custom header files for each conf,\nhere''s what you do. Make a file or files in ''S:'' called \n''VDTopHeader#/.Gr'' - Where # is the number of the conf to use this header\nand .Gr or no .Gr is for Ansi and no ansi respectivlely.  So A\n''VDTopHeader2'' Would be for conference 2 with no color, and \n''VDTopHeader2.Gr'' would be for conference 2 with color, and\n''VDTopHeader1.Gr'' would be for conference 1 with color, etc. There are a\nfew example files included in the ''S:'' directory for your viewing.\n\n NOTE: You need not use custom headers, but they do make the output files\n       look nicer. If you choose to not use any header files, then it\n       will default to a clear screen as the header. If you use a header,\n       you will have to include a clearscreen if you want it (Ctrl+L) at\n       the top, but you probably already knew that. :)\n\n Now the tough part, the preference file itself. I tried to make it as easy\nas I could, but due to the highly configurable nature of the program, you\nwill need to take some time to make sure all is in order.  Here''s an\nexample preference file and what every line does.  Configure each\nline to match your board. Beside the function will be a reference marker.\nSee that marker below the example for a full explanation.\n\n---------------------------------START-----------------------------------\nW                                   - Amount Of Time Before Reseting\nVan Damme - Sysop                   - Name Of Sysop\n1 Holding Cell                      - Conference Names\n2 The Chair      \n3 Cell Block     \n4 Gas Chamber    \n5 Warden''s Lounge\n6 The Shower     \n7 Courtyard      \n8                \n9                                      \n------------------                  - ******** First Divider ********\n2                                   - Conference Number\nAMIGA WARES                         - Name To Be Used For Conference\nY                                   - Use A Total Stat Bar In Output\nChair                               - Name Of Conference On Harddrive\nEALL                                - Receiver Of Message\nY                                   - Ansi Option For Top Records\nBBS:Chair/Bulletins/Bull3.Txt       - Output File For Top Records\n10                                  - Number Of Uploaders On Output\n0                                   - Number Of Downloaders On Output\nY                                   - Ansi Option For First Output\nBBS:Chair/Bull50.Txt.Gr             - Output File Name For First Output \nN                                   - Ansi Option For Second Ouput\nBBS:Chair/Bull50.Txt                - Output File Name For Second Output\n------------------                  - *********** Divider ***********\n3                                   - Conference Number\nCONSOLE WARES                       - Name To Be Used For Conference\nY                                   - Name To Be Used For Conference\nConsole                             - Name Of Conference On Harddrive\nVan Damme                           - Receiver Of Message\n                                    - Ansi Option For Top Records \n                                    - Output File For Top Records \n4                                   - Number Of Uploaders On Output\n3                                   - Number Of Downloaders On Output\nN                                   - Ansi Option For First Output  \nBBS:Console/Bull50.Txt              - Output File Name For Second Output\n------------------                  - *********** Divider ***********\n4                                   - Conference Number\nIBM WARES                           - Name To Be Used For Conference\nN                                   - Use A Total Stat Bar In Output\n                                    - Name Of Conference On Harddrive\n                                    - Receiver Of Message\nY                                   - Ansi Option For Top Records\nBBS:Chair/Bulletins/Bull3.Txt       - Output File For Top Records\n8                                   - Number Of Uploaders On Output\n2                                   - Number Of Downloaders On Output\nY                                   - Ansi Option For First Output\nBBS:Chair/Bull50.Txt.Gr             - Output File Name For First Output \nN                                   - Ansi Option For Second Ouput\nBBS:Chair/Bull50.Txt                - Output File Name For Second Output\nN                                   - Ansi Option For Third Ouput \nRam:Testing.Txt                     - Output File Name For Third Output \n----------------------------------END------------------------------------\n\n Yes.. quite a big preference file, but don''t lose all hope at once. It\njust looks big. It''s really easy to figure out if you take it step by step.\nThe first thing to notice is that between the first divider and the rest\nof the preference file the two parts are different. Before the first\ndivider, we have the conference outlines and other things - ONCE. After\nthe first divider comes the entries for EACH conference. You have one\nof this for each conference. So after the first divider, you can have\nas many entries as you want, but before it, you will always have one. \n\n * Before First Divider *\n\n - Amount Of Time Before Reseting\n\nThis is the first line in the program always. It is the length of time\nthat the program will run for before reseting.  Most people will use\nit as a Weektop, which is what it works best at, but you can set it for\nany number of days that you wish. On this line, Use a ''W'' for week, ''D'' for\na single Day, and ''M'' for a month.  After this time limit is reached, it\nwill post the message with the final results (optional) and also put\nout the top record bulletin(optional). You can also use a number like 3 or\n13 for a specific number of days instead of a day,week or month.  Note,\nthat if at any time you change this value after the program is working, it\nwill start over at day one of this new value, but the users stats will\nremain unchanged. (NOTE: For a true weektop, start the door or change to\na week on Monday.)\n\n - Name Of Sysop\n   \nStraigh forward, the name of the sysop or person that you wish to have\nthe message come from on the board.  It doesn''t have to be an active\naccount, it can be anyname, although the Sysop''s name works best in most\ncases. :)\n              \n - Conference Names\n\nThis program only supports 9 confs maximum now. If you have a problem with\nthis lemma know.  The conference name part contains a list of all the\nconferences on your board (1-9) and how they appear EXACTLY on your board.\nIt will use this name when searching through the callerslog to find \nwhat went to which conference. It is not case sensitive.  If you have\nconferences you don''t wish to keep track of or that don''t have files, you\ncan leave the names blank, but you MUST, I repeat MUST have 9 entries here.\nAnd if it''s a vaild entry, it must have the conference number beside of it.\nExample:\n\n--------\n\n2 Amiga Crap - Unknowns World HQ\n\n4 Pc Wares\n5 Pornal pics\n\n7 Elite Files\n\n\n---------\n\nIf you don''t want to use a conf, leave it blank. But you MUST have nine\nentries here. It''s better and less confusing to just list all your confs\nwhether you use them or not, as I have in the example config file. And\nremember that they match up exactly as they appear on your board (save\nfor being case sensitive)\n\n The reason for this conference part in the config is because of the\nrelative conference option on /X v2.37 or higher. Without doing it like\nthis, things get messed up badly. Just ask Kidlat! on the pit.. hehe.\n\n * After First Divider *\n\n NOTE: All this options are repeated over for each conference you wish \n       to have a record for.\n \n - Conference Number                 \n\nThis is the number of the conference as it appears on the Conference\nlists in the preference file beginning. So using the example in the\nConference listings, if I used 2 here it would be the \n''2 Amiga Crap - Unknowns World HQ'' conference that this preference entry\nwould be for. All other entries until the next divider will be for this\nconference.\n\n - Name To Be Used For Conference  \n\nThis is the name that you wish to appear for this conference on the\noutput bulletins. It doesn''t have to match anything, it can be whatever\nyou like. Like ''This bulletin''s for amiga'' or anything you want it to be.\nIf you can''t think of anything, you could always use the acutal conference\nname here. :)\n  \n - Use A Total Stat Bar In Output    \n\nA ''Y'' or ''N'' for this option here. If you use a Y, then the output \nbulletin for this conference will have a stat bar at the bottem with the\ntotal number of calls, ups, etc. If you have a no, no start bar will \nappear at the bottem of the output file. \n\n - Name Of Conference On Harddrive   \n\nThis is the name of the directory of the conference EXACTLY as it appears\non your harddrive. It''s needed to find the message base to write a message.\nSo if your PC conf is BBS:PC - then you would use ''PC''. NO BBS: Needed here,\nit will be inserted. (If you can''t figure it out, look at your config\nfor /X or acp.start and look at the directory names for the confs and\nleave off the BBS:. \n\n NOTE: Leave this space BLANK for no message output.\n\n - Receiver Of Message               \n\n This is who the message will be written to at the end of the term. ''EALL''\nand ''ALL'' work nicely, but you can use any user name you wish.\n\n  NOTE: Leave this space BLANK for no message output.\n\n - Ansi Option For Top Records \n      \n ''Y'' or ''N'' , whether the Top record bulletin will be in ansi or not.\n\n  NOTE: Leave this space BLANK for no top record bulletin.\n\n - Output File For Top Records       \n\nThe output file for the top records of this conference goes here. It will\nkeep track of the 5 best uploaders and downloaders of all time in a \nseperate bulletin. This isn''t really something to show users when they\nlogon, but rather as a bulletin for them to view like a top cps one.\n\n  NOTE: Leave this space BLANK for no message output.\n\n - Number Of Uploaders On Output \n\n Simpley, any number (The more the slower, so no 100 users eh?) which will\nbe the number of uploaders that will be displayed on the output file.\n\n  NOTE: Use a 0 for no uploaders.    \n\n - Number Of Downloaders On Output   \n\n Simpley, any number (The more the slower, so no 100 users eh?) which will\nbe the number of downloaders that will be displayed on the output file.\n\n  NOTE: Use a 0 for no downloaders.\n\n - Ansi Option For First Output   \n\n''Y'' or ''N'' for whether or not the output file will have ansi or not.\n   \n - Output File Name For First Output \n\nThe output file for the list that will contain the top users for the week\nas outlined in the number of uploaders/downloaders. This is the file\nto display to the users when they log on to your board.\n    \n - Ansi Option For Etc..\n\n''Y'' or ''N''. You can have more then one output file (one ansi, one not, etc)\nfor each conference. Just remember for each output file you want, have\na Ansi option line and a Output filename line for each.\n\n - Output File Name For Etc..\n\nSee Above.\n\n\n Now here you would put a divider, and do the same thing above for\nthe next conference, until you have a complete entry with all the things\nabove (after the first divider) for each. And then another divider, and\nthe conference values, etc.\n\n\n And Remember, if all else fails, call me.. or go through my provided config\nand edit and change to suit your own instead of doing it from scratch. :)\n\n  Paths\n  ~~~~~\n If you a sysop, make sure that each conf has only 1 or two paths listed\nin the ''Paths'' file. For if they go to one conference and download all \nthe files from the board in there, they will all show up there and not\nwhere they should, in the conference they came from. Sysops and cosysops,\nmake sure to nuke the files while your in the conference that the file\nis in. I don''t see this as a problem at all, but you''ll always get the\non person that tries it and complains why the user lost credits in the \nwrong conf.\n\n  Output Files\n  ~~~~~~~~~~~~\n The normal output files will have a Day(?/?) on it, which will list at\nwhat point your at so far. Like 2/5 would mean your on day 2 of 5. Once\nit hits 5/5 it will reset, or whatever you have it set at. This ''Day(?/?)''\nisn''t listed on the final top record bulletin, it''s replaced with the\nwords ''TOP USERS''. Also, only the final Bulletin and the messages have\nthe ''Updated On:'' now, as it wasn''t needed on the bulletins that are\nshown to the users when they log on, they get updated everytime someone\nlogs off. Ya.. 4 second diffence between updates.. hehe. gotta show that..\n\n Also note that the final top record bulletin will take only 1 user from\nthe term. So after the first week say, the top uploader and downloader\nwill be added to the top record bulletin.  ONLY the top users from that\nweek.  Next week, the top 2 users will be added, etc. It''s ONLY the top\nusers, not everybody.\n\n  Working Methods\n  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nDue to the complex nature of trying to keep seperate track of each file\ntransfer in seperate confs, I had to use a few output files that will\nbe created in ''S:''. You don''t need to touch them at all, they will update,\ndelete and be recreated as the program needs them. If you do for some\nreason need to know what they do and their purpose, they are:\n\nS:VDTop.Dates - Contains the Information about what day of the week it''s\n                currently on and how many more to go before reseting. If\n                This file is delete it will start over at the beginning of\n                the term.\n\nS:VDTop.Store - This is the major storage file, containing all the info\n                for every user. If deleted, all user stats will be lost for\n                the current term.\n\nS:VDTop.Stats - Contains the information needed for the stat bars - the\n                Total of all the calls, ups, etc for each conf. If deleted,\n                the stat bar information will all be reset to 0 for the term.\n\nS:VDTop.Final - Contains the top record information for each conf. If\n                Deleted, all the top records will be lost. Don''t delete it.\n\n  Options\n  ~~~~~~~\n\n One of the nicest options you''ll have noticed is the ability to keep\na SEPERATE record of the file transfers in each conference. No longer\nwill the amiga and console users have to try to compete against the mighty\nPC users, they can compete for the weektop in the confs with their own\nusers.  This utility isn''t meant to be a top uploader util, that would\nbe imposible to do for each conf, but it functions nicely as a week , day\nor month top.  I have set the limit of days to 99 max, cause after this\nthe storage files will probably become too big and slow the program down\ntoo much.. It''s only rexx you know. :)\n\n\n  Setup\n  ~~~~~\n The best way to set up the output files is as follows. Make the output\nfiles bulls in the Conference name directories, so every time they would\njoin the amiga conference, they would get the amiga list, or if they join\nthe PC section, they get the PC list. Output the top records to the \nbulletin section for each conf, so you''ll have a top pc records in the\nPC conf, and top amiga records in the amiga conference.  Use a nice big\nAmiga or PC header for the output lists, or mabey who''s HQ it is, etc.\nKinda like for the last caller (by pot-Noodle).  If you want to see\nthis method (and the method you should be using) call my board or the pit,\nas I know he has it setup properly.. hehe..  Also make the message go\nto the write conf! :)\n \n  Examples\n  ~~~~~~~~\n For some examples of the kind of output files you will be getting, look\nin the ExampleOutput directory in the archive.  The following example files\nare included:\n\nBull10.Txt       - Console Wares Section With 3 Up/3 Down And No Ansi\nBull10.Txt.Gr    - Console Wares Section With 3 Up/3 Down And Ansi\nBull50.Txt       - Amiga Wares Section With 10 Up/0 Down And No Ansi\nBull50.Txt.Gr    - Amiga Wares Section With 10 Up/0 Down And Ansi\nBull3.Txt        - Top Record Bulletin In Amiga Conf And Ansi\n\n  History\n  ~~~~~~~\n v1.0 : -No Known Bugs Or Problems. (Beta Release)\n v1.1 : -Public Release Under Tribe Label.\n        -Added Custom Headers For Each Conference.\n        -User Friendly To NosNuke And AmiFaker Now.\n        -Made To Work With /X''s Relative Conference Feature.\n        -Changed Preference Outline.\n        -Adjusted Output File Structure.\n        -Removed ''Updated On'' From Normal Output Files (Not Needed Here).\n        -Fixed Many Message Base Errors.\n        -Added Total Stat Bar (Optional).\n        -Many Other Small Bugs Fixed.\n        -Compiled Size (211824).\n\n  Greets\n  ~~~~~~\n A big big greet goes out to Akira of the pit bbs, for coming up with\nsuch a wonderful idea for a utility. I''ll tell ya, it was fucking hell \ntrying to figure out this one, but after a few days (hehe) I prevailed.\n\n Thanks to B.O.B, Danzig, and all other users on bytemasters BBS that\ntried the Beta version and let me know how to improve/fix the program up.\nAlso thanks that no one spreaded it out, I can trust you guys with other\nbeta versions of upcoming utilitys.\n\n Thanks to Akira and Kidlat of the Pit bbs again for helpful suggestions\non how to make it better.\n\n Thanks to PMF for explaining in english what Virtual Conferences were.\n Send hugs and kisses to Trixie for me.. hehe\n\n Thanks as always to Nzo for info and opinions on the door and how to make\nit better.\n\n Thanks to Spock and Nosferatu for great nuking utils, and writing\na callerslog good enough for me to extract what I needed.\n\n Thanks to the uploaders on my board that allowed me to see if it''s working.\nhehe.\n\n Great big Thanks to Illicit Trader who noticed a major bug just before\nthe file went public. Close one, thanks dude.\n\n Thanks to Tribe for giving me a group to release it under. \n\n****************************************************************************\n\n I Hope to see this util being put to good use on boards everywhere. You \n amiga users always complained about getting shafted by the ibm users, well\n now do something about it. Tell your sysops to install VDTop now!\n\n |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n \n      THIS IS THE LAST MAJOR UTIL I AM DOING IN AREXX. IT''S TOO DAMN SLOW\n AND IT''S REALLY PISSING ME OFF. FROM NOW ON, I WILL BE DOING ALL MY UTILS\n IN C.. AND TO HELL WITH THE SLOW AND BULKYNESS OF REXX COMPILED FILES.\n I WILL ALSO BE DOING THE VDTOP, VDDATE AND VDEDIT OVER IN C AS THESE UTILS\n ARE ABOUT THE ONLY ONES THAT COULD USE A BOOST IN SPEED. STAY TUNED FOR\n MORE AND FASTER VD UTILS IN C.\n\n |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\n****************************************************************************\n\n Also, I''m taking a brake from writing utils for a week or so, so you \nprobably won''t seen another VD release until early may. A VDNuke was\nbrought to my attention, but I''m not sure. If you have any great ideas for\na door, lemma know please and I''m sure I''ll write it for ya. Write now,\nI''m going to settle back with a nice 40 ouncher of whiskey and wake up\nin a few days feeling good. Also remember to grab the first pack of\ngroup headers for VDEdit, released same time as this utility, Apr 19.\n\n And a few greets to... \n\n Skol/THG - Call again soon. Always nice to chat with ya.\n Nzo/Dual Crew - Ah.. I talk to you too much already. :)\n Nameless - Thanks for the greet in your NodeAct door.\n Nosferatu - Don''t Worry. VDTop works with Nosnuke.\n Pot-Noodle/Anthrox - Great Last caller util. \n PMF/Minstry - So have you given Trixie The Big UK Sausage yet??\n /\KiRA - I''m poor from calling your board! \n MAGNUS/LSD - Greets friend! How''s it been going?\n mUb/LSD - Greets to you too dude. Thanks for the support!\n Phideaux!/LSD - The AGA God lives and rules. :)\n Ceejay/WTi - Greets Mate. Save me a brewskie!\n Rambo/Fairlight - New Blood. That''s What We Need. Where''s the Conf?\n Elf-Co/Alpha Flight - One day I''m going to mail you something!\n Ice Cube/Anthrox - Long time no talk dude. Call sometime!\n Zen - Always my best friend around! :) Never lose touch.\n Echo/LSD - I put your C Disks up. You better call for them!\n Kidlat - I expect you to be using this door! :) Long Live VDEdit!!!\n Zandor/LSD - What A Trader You Are. Zoom zoom Boom! \n Squid/Prime - You have good taste since you run my utils. hehe\n Cragar/Prime - I shall talk with ya soon.\n Illicit Trader - Thanks for the console support. I really need it!\n Gilby/Minstry - You should call me more! I may have PC one day.\n AxeL - Greets To My Newfound Friend. Where''s the asm examples?\n King Conan/Tribe - Thanks for the update ideas. Keep the doors coming.\n Denon - Thanks for the update ideas as well. Really Appriciated.\n Eddie The Head/LSD - So your the sysop of the Carnival? Ahhh!.\n Robster - Thanks for the BBS support - Uploadwise!.\n Alberta - Good luck with the board. I''m sure it will work out.\n Esskayare - Did you get Your computer back out of your car when you found\n             out it was PMF and Nzo on the phone and not AT&T? hehe\n TsM/Tectron - Warm greets to ya dude. Keep coding. Nice pretty dir util.\n Shen/Tectron - When''s the next door. I shall release something under Tectron\n                very shortly. \n Sinatra/Tectron - Thanks for the testing of VDEdit 2.5!\n Yankee Rose - Thanks for the VDColordir Idea. Glad to see the board back up!\n Kitaro/FLT/SR - How''s the board doing m8? Call back.\n Shaggy - The Best Console Support I''ve seen yet. Where''d ya go?? :)\n Coca Cola Kid/Abuse - What happened to that code? So quick eh?\n SkyLark/LSD - You really are the Number One Skull Brother. \n The Biker/LSD - Kewl board.  Great name, can I take a drive?\n Blade/Tribe - Long Live The Top Uploader!\n MetalBasher! - You really are the ascii Genius! Call for the /X help.\n Dux/Tsl - Too bad about doc. Call me for the complete version of VDEdit.\n Caffeine/Eclipse - Nice FreeDownload door. VDFree still rules though. hehe\n\n                 Send greets if you want them back!\n \n And those that I know but forgot, and also those users that still value\nfriendship over all else, and of course to all you other ami-express door\nwriters out there. Drop me a line on my board sometime, I''d be glad to help\ntest your utils or give you the latest updates on mine.\n\n Remember to call my board. I need some console users badly.. and amiga\nusers are always more then welcome!\n\n\n        Warm Greetings to all my friends in Tectron and Tribe.\n\n                       			           Later dudes.. Till then!\n\n                   - Van Damme (TW,SA - U2 Is the Greatest Band Ever! Yup!)\n                                 ^\n                                 `- Haven''t you ever wondered what this is?\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',99108,9,0,NULL,NULL,'trb_vdtp','scan',1780048787);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('trb_wf11','TRB_WF11.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/TRB_WF11.LHA','rexxdoor','XIM','REXXDOOR',NULL,'Tribe','TRB','|  |/  /      \ K I N G S  |     <|  |> _/  R A N S O M |  |\  \  |   \_',replace('               __  __ ______\n              |  |/  /      \    \n   K I N G S  |     <|  |> _/  R A N S O M \n              |  |\  \  |   \_  \n              |__| \__\_|\___/\n               1-305-247-7605\n    Kings W.T.F. v1.1 / Released By Tribe\n33.6 DigITal-X Prd/NirVana Dist Site! 33.6\n','\n',char(10)),'KingsWTF.doc',replace('\n===============================\n     WHAT THE FUCK?! v1.1                     ANOTHER ONE THAT WILL\n===============================                     MAKE THE\n    By King Conan of TRIBE                  "BEST AMI-EXPRESS UTILITY"\n===============================                      CHARTS\nKings Ransom - 1-305-247-7605\n===============================\n\n\n*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*+*=*=*= IMPORTANT! =*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*\n \n It is very highly recommended that you follow the instructions for\nthis utility to the letter.  Even though you may have installed many\nREXX DOORS to your system already, this particular door sets up a bit\ndifferently then the rest.  Especially the part that pertains to editing\nyour "BBS.CMD" file.\n\n*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*+*=*=*= IMPORTANT! =*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*=*\n\nINSTALLATION\n------------\n\nNEEDED TO RUN:\n--------------\n1st off let me state something:  Arexx utils are compatible with ALL AMIGAS!\nif an Arexx util is not working for you, then you have not properly set it\nup & probably forgot to install some of the libraries or spelled something\nwrong somewhere.  Follow these instructions to the letter, & all should be\nfine!  I have also heard that people with certain 69030 accelators have\nproblems running COMPILED AREXX DOORS.. If you fall into this catagory,\nsorry...\n\n>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\nYou need Arexx Installed in your System.\n>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\nAREXX is "NOT" included with this Util.\n>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>> \nalso:   copy the file RPSTART into your C: and then edit your \n        "startup-sequence" or "user-startup" to load this file\n        upon BBS bootup.   ex. C:RPSTART\n\n        copy RexxPlus.lib \n             rexxplslib.library   files to your LIBS: directory.\n\nalso IMPORTANT: make sure you have "rexxdoor" & "rexxport" in your\n                BBS:UTILS/ directory... They are standard AmiExpress\n                commands, amd allow AmiExpress to properly communicate\n                with Arexx doors & utils.\n\nSETUP:\n------\n\n Make sure you have "WAIT" in your C: directory. This is a standard WORKBENCH\n command that can be found in the C: directory of your WORKBENCH DISK.  It is\n needed by this door in order for it to properly work.\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------\n\n Make a directory called:  DOORS:KingsWTF/\n \nand put these files in it: KingsWTF.rexx\n                           KingsWTF.cfg\n\n>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\n\nNow Edit your BBS.CMD file as so:    (READ THIS PART CAREFULLY!)\n\n---------------------------------------------\nFORMAT   RM010Doors:KingsWTF/KingsWTF.rexx\n---------------------------------------------\n |       |||  |           \n |       |||  ` ''Doors:KingsWTF/KingsWTF.rexx  - Location Of Program!\n |       |||     Make sure not to change this!!\n |       |||\n |       ||` 010 Is the minimum access to use this door. Change it to what\n |       ||      you like.\n |       ||\n |       |` M For a mutilnode bbs (S For single)\n |       |\n |       ` R For an rexx type door which will use the ''Rexxdoor'' Util\n |\n `Letter to bring the door up on the board. In this case ''FORMAT''\n \n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nNOTE:  "DO-NOT" USE THE RETARD OPTION WITH THIS DOOR!!!!!\n        ^^^^^^\n\n*FORMAT        RM050Doors:KingsInfo/KingsInfo.rexx\n|\n`-Retard Option. To Make Sure they only use ''FORMAT'' & only ''FORMAT'' to get\n the door to come up. If not used, things such as ''FORMAT HD0:''  and \n ''FORMAT DRIVE''  would still bring up the door (WHICH IS WHAT YOU WANT!)\n \n                   SO DONT USE THE RETARD OPTION!!!!\n-------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\n\nWHAT DOES THIS DOOR DO?\n-----------------------\n \n  Every sysop, no matter how liked, always runs into a real jerk every\nnow & then.. And sometimes these jerks have mischevious attentions like\nbringing down your BBS for good.  Now most sysops are pretty smart, & take\nall precautions in assuring the safety of their BBS.  Things like making\nsure a user does not have access to damaging commands like "FORMAT" or\n"DELETE" is always at the top of a good sysops list.\n \n  But if a user does have the attention of damaging your BBS & actually\ntries to damage it, why should he be given a simple:\n \n             "YOU DONOT HAVE ACCESS TO THAT COMMAND"\n\n    when he should be punished for his damaging attentions?!!\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n  This door is a SYSOP COMMAND/HACKER PROTECTOR. What this simply means\nis that if a user tries to access a command that he knows he has no right\nusing, he will be punished!\n \nFOR EXAMPLE:\n \nIf you wanted to protect the "FORMAT" command, you would put the following\nentry into your "BBS.CMD" file:\n\n               FORMAT   RM050Doors:KingsWTF/KingsWTF.rexx\n\nIf you wanted to protect the "DELETE" command, you would put the following\nentry into your "BBS.CMD" file:\n\n               DELETE   RM050Doors:KingsWTF/KingsWTF.rexx\n\netc, etc, etc....\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nYou can protect any command you want, (as long as the command in all\nreality is not really used on the BBS)..  What I mean by this is there\nreally is no "FORMAT" or "DELETE" command on any bbs, but alot of users\ndo-not relize this (or are just plain stupid), and try to access these\ncommands anyhow..\n \n---------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nNow, with the above entries placed into the "BBS.CMD" file, if a user\ntypes into the BBS :\n \n  Format\n  Format DF0:\n  Format HD0:\n  Format DH1:  etc, etc, etc... (SAME WITH DELETE)\n \n It will load up "WHAT THE FUCK?!" .....\n \nAs long as you donot insert a "*" (RETARD OPTION) into the "BBS.CMD" file\nfor a command, any FORM of that command typed out will load the door.\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nNow, Here is EXACTLY WHAT THE DOOR DOES:\n----------------------------------------\n  \n When a user has triggered the door to be loaded, the very 1st thing it\ndoes is:\n \n             1> Drops Users Access Level to 10  (NEW USER)\n             2> Changes Users Conference Access  X________\n                                                 123456789\n\nThen it displays the following message to the user:  (IN COLOR!)\n\n+===========================================================================+ \n|                                                                           |\n|                           WHAT THE FUCK!!  v1.1                           |\n|                                                                           |\n|   It would seem that you have made a very serious ACCESS LEVEL decision.  |\n|    In fact, Congratulations, you have just lowered your ACCESS LEVEL to   |\n|                              NEW-USER Status!                             |\n|                                                                           |\n|               New-Users are always REQUIRED to BEG for ACCESS.            |\n|                                                                           |\n|                         So Start Begging Asshole!                         |\n|                                                                           |\n+===========================================================================+\n|             A KINGS RANSOM/TRIBE Production.   1-305-247-7605             |\n+===========================================================================+\n\n>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\nNow the next thing it does depends on what you put into the CONFIG-FILE..\n\nBEFORE RUNNING THIS DOOR:\n-------------------------\n \n Before you run this door you need to edit the "KingsWTF.CFG" file.\n There are "4" FLAGS that need to be edited in this file. \n \n>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\n       FLAG\n(LINE1)  N  ; KICK HACKER OFF BBS RIGHT-AWAY, OR SEND HIM TO CONF1? Y=KICKOFF\n                                                                    N=CONF1 \n\n                Y=KICK HIM OFF!!            \n\n                  Selecting this FLAG will DROP CARRIER on the user\n                  after the message (ABOVE IN LAST AREA) is displayed.\n                  When the user calls back, he will only be able to access\n                  CONFERENCE #1..(THE NEW-USERS AREA).. He will have \n                  New-Users Access & will not be able to do anything\n                  but leave you a COMMENT explaining his actions & begging\n                  for forgiveness.  This option is used by the "PISSED-OFF"\n                  sysop who never wants to see the stinking HACKER AGAIN.\n\n\n                N=THROW HIM INTO CONFERENCE #1\n                  in this mode, the user will "NOT" be thrown off the BBS\n                  immediately.  Instead, his access is lowered, and he is\n                  placed into CONFERENCE #1..(THE NEW-USERS AREA)..\n \n                  This option is used by the "NOT SO PISSED" sysop. hehe.\n                  It allows you to give the user an IMMEDIATE chance of\n                  leaving a COMMENT to the sysop & explain himself. That\n                  is, if he has the balls to do so..\n\n>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\n\n(LINE2)  BBS:CONF3/    ; Full Path To Conference of where to send EALL\n                         message, if you answer "Y" to the SEND EALL\n                         flag.  \n \n                         NOTE:  You must type in the full PATH with either\n                                a ":" or a "/" at the end!!\n \n                      EXAMPLE: BBS:CONF1/  or  CONF1:   will both work!\n\n                         NOTE2: Even if you have the SEND-EALL flag turned\n                                off, please insert a path here.\n                                (JUST IN CASE)\n                                (RAM: will work nicely)\n>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\n\n(LINE3)  Y  ;      Write To Callerslog??  (Y or N)  (OBVIOUS USAGE)\n\n  THE "LOG ENTRY" will display the following information:\n\n        +------------------------------------------------------------+\n                 WHAT THE FUCK?  v1.1  STOPS ANOTHER HACKER!!\n        +------------------------------------------------------------+\n                SHAOLIN attempted to BRING DOWN THE BBS!!!\n \n                Access Level WAS: 100\n                Access Level NOW: 10  >>> NEW-USER STATUS! <<<\n \n                EXACT TIME OF MISHAP: Sun Apr 04 08:09:35 1993\n        +------------------------------------------------------------+\n           Send THANKS To: KING CONAN at KINGS RANSOM  305-247-7605 \n        +------------------------------------------------------------+\n\n>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\n\n\n(LINE4)  Y  ;      SEND A EALL message to all users DEGRADING the \n                   stupid Hacker??  (Y/N)\n \n                   SELECTING "N" will do nothing....\n \n                   SELECTING "Y" will read the PATH you inserted for \n                   (FLAG #2) & Insert the following message into \n                   YOUR CONF PATH/messagebase/\n\n        +------------------------------------------------------------+\n                 WHAT THE FUCK?  ''VER''  STOPS ANOTHER HACKER!!'')\n        +------------------------------------------------------------+\n               SHAOLIN attempted to BRING DOWN THE BBS!\n\n               Access Level WAS: 50\n               Access Level NOW: 10  >>> NEW-USER STATUS! <<<\n\n               EXACT TIME OF MISHAP: Fri Apr 23 12:08:43 1993\n        +------------------------------------------------------------+\n                        KILL THIS ASSHOLE IF POSSIBLE! \n        +------------------------------------------------------------+\n           Send THANKS To: KING CONAN at KINGS RANSOM  305-247-7605 \n        +------------------------------------------------------------+\n\n\n          >>>> THIS EALL MESSAGE WILL BE POSTED IN FULL COLOR!! <<<<\n\n>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\n\nSOME LAST THOUGHTS\n------------------\n \nRemember, you can use this door to protect as many commands as you wish,\nJust put a seperate entry for each command into your BBS.CMD file.\n \nAlso, it is essential that the command is not actually used by the BBS.\n \nThings you might want to try is stuff like:\n \nIF YOU RUN "NOSNUKE" rename it to "NN" or something, for you & your Co''s,\nand then have entries in "BBS.CMD" for NOSNUKE & NUKE.. User tries to load\nNOSNUKE or NUKE he gets accessed lowered..\n \n In other words, protect your commands with some alternate names, & let the\nusers find out the hard way that you have been expecting their bullshit.\nAs far as im concerned, all users know that sysop commands are meant for\nuse ONLY by the sysops.. If he''s that stupid to try them, well then...\n\n---------\n \nAt any rate, you sould definately have this door protect:\n \nFORMAT , KILL ,  &  DELETE .....\n\n\n>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>>\nGREETS/THANX\n------------\n \nWhite Knight  -  Helping me look up stuff in Arexx Books. Major Thoughts\n                 & Helpings under the 1.1 update.\n\nDenon         -  Actually logging in and REALLY TRYING to fuck-up bbs!\n                 Also staying up till 1:26am with me getting out all the\n                 kinks.. Thanx.. \n\nVan Damme     -  thanx for a working copy of the MESSAGE SENDING routine,\n                 (to bad your first version caused my BBS to loose 200+\n                  megs of files.. Oh the life of a programmer....)\n         \nTRIBE         -  To my fellow TRIBE mates!\n\nLSD           -  D-MAN, ZANDOR, MALACAR (or MALCAR?) hehe anyways glad you\n                 guys really enjoy my stuff!\n\n==========================================================================\n\nALL UPDATES TO MY UTILS CAN BE FOUND AT:\n----------------------------------------\nIf you have any questions or i forgot to mention some particulars about \nthis utility, then call me at:                                    _  _\n                                                                  \][/\n                     _      Hast La Vista Baby!                   / *\\n      _             (_)      ____        ____        ____        / __/\n     | \ __ __ __ __| |_____/ ___\______/ ___\______/ ___\______/ /____\n     |  |  |  |  |  | |____/ /_________/ /_________/ /_________/ /_____\\n     |  |__|__|__|__| |___/ /_________/ /_________/ /_________/ /______/\n     |_/            |_|  /_/      \____/      \____/      \____/\n                    (_)                 \n                         KINGS RANSOM  -  305-247-7605\n                           >> 16.8 DUAL STANDARD! <<\n\nAlso, call if you have any suggestions on updates to any of my present \nutils, or ideas for some new ones.. I donot claim to be the best, but if\ni think i can do it, Ill try!\n\n============================================================================\nFIXES AND UPDATES REPORT:\n-------------------------\n\n4-05-93   v1.0    First Completion of program.. Will release after a couple\n                  of days of major testing.. But all seems to be 100%\n\n\n4-23-93   v1.1  > Added CONFIG option for CALLERSLOG\n                > Added SEND EALL option\n                > Corrected Spelling error of CONGRATULATIONS from\n                  CONGRADULATIONS...  (THANX MR. WEBSTER)\n                \n============================================================================\n\nALSO CHECK OUT:\n===============\n \nKings Info v1.6  -  Replacement "W" command that allows for MANUAL or\n                    RANDOM password generation.. Nice FRESH look!!\n\nKings Help v1.0  -  The first ever HELP-DOOR for AmiExpress that allows \n                    users to get help on "ANY" command you have installed\n                    on the BBS!!\n\n===========================================================================\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',127321,15,0,NULL,NULL,'nvx_rem5','scan',1780048787);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('trd_chk2','TRD-CHK2.LZH','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/TRD-CHK2.LZH','check2','XIM','check2',NULL,NULL,'TRD','_______________  ___________________ ______ ____   \____    \/  ___  \____  _____Y_____ /   \   \      _/   !____/   .  /    Y.   \',replace('      - - --=> .t.R.A.D.E.R.''S. <=-- - -\n _______________  ___________________ ______\n____   \____    \/  ___  \____  _____Y_____\n/   \   \      _/   !____/   .  /    Y.   \\n\_______/__!    \________\___!  \____|!    \\n        EL?|_____/           `----'' \______/\n             Checker v2.0\nChecks between 2 filelist and tells you what\nis diffrent between them. Get all the files\nthat a bbs has not got that another one has.\nSysops can check other filelist against \nthere own and get the ones they missed....\n','\n',char(10)),'check2.doc',replace('                                Checker v2.0\n                                ------------\n\nOk I here you ask what is it?\n\nWell when I go round the BBS''s trading I get sick of looking throuh big \nfilelist and trying to find out what one BBS has that another one hasn''t\nand visa versa so I did a little bit of thinking and started writting this\nutill hope it help all you traders out there. Now here''s the scond version \nwhich is mouse driven.\n\nWhats in the Archive\n---------------------\nCheck2\nCheck2.docs\nPONTY.txt\nTD.TXT\nFile_id.diz\n\nHow it works.\n------------\n\nRight then a lot of changes from the first one I did to start it the same as \nbefore get your file list off 2 BBS''s lists goto a CLI or Shell\nand type in Check2 now then after you have pressed a key and got onto the main\nmenu everthing is mouse driven (as I like to be lazy) just click the\nselection that you wish to do.\n\nScreen/Printer\n--------------\n\n If you have told it screen or printer the up \ncomes a requester for you to click on the files that you wish to use \n(one at a time) it wil then tell you a bit about each file ( how many files)\nif your file is too big it will also tell you that as well so you can cut it\ndown to a better size.\nthen it will do its job.\n\nFiles\n-----\n\nIf you have selected that you wish to have the output to files then it will\ncheck to see what drives you have and ask you where you would like them put\nonce you have decided on the drive it will list it and tell you how much free\nspace you have on that drive. if you are happy with your selection then click\non the Y or you can if you wish hit the Y/N keys then it will give you a \nrequester for you to select the files that you wish to use. (same as in the\nabove screens or printer.) \nIt will then ask you if you wish to use the file for trading if you answer \nyes to this then it will only make a list of the names of the file and nothing\nelse. if you say no then it will add a few extra lines into the files it \nmakes. Then it will make the files I have named them FILE1 or File2 depending\nif you are making 1 or 2 files from the list.\nThen it will go off and do its job.\n\nMisc\n----\n\nWhile doing it job you can get back to workbench and carry on with something \nelse and toggle back it check if its done with the Left Amiga Key +A\n\nIf you do use the program more than once it will checkoto make sure that there\nis no file the same name as the one the program writes if there is then it\nwill ask you to rename the old file to somthing new. \n\nThings that it dose\n-------------------\nWill print out to printer,screen or to any drive.\nIt will give you 2 out puts telling you whats missing from one list to the \nother, or just the one that you wish.\nIt will take upto 8000 files names if more then you will have to split the\nlist.\nTakes files upto 500K each\n\n\nHow to use on a BBS.\n--------------------\n\nwell this part is easy the output from the check2 will be in ASCII form\n Then when you phone the bbs to get the files that are in the list go into\nthe download mode when it askes for the first file name do a ASCII SEND\nwith the comms package. Sending your list that this has made for you and it\nwill tag all the files in the list for you.\n\nThis will save you loads of time checking out the list for files what are\non one BBS and not on another.\n\nProbs and Creds\n---------------\n\nThis util was made by Tronic of The Ponty Express BBS\nif you have any probs then contact me on my BBS.\nyou can get the number from most of the BBS around.\nor if you have any comments then let me know.\nit has been tested on a 500 with 2 megs ram, a 1200 & a 4000\n\n\nFuture version ideas\n--------------------\n\nTo check the decriptions as well as file names.\nTo add menu commands.\nTo add some more keys if needed be.\n\nIf you think somthing is needed that I have not listed then let me know\n\nThank you for reading and using the utill. Hope it helps you as much as\nits helped me.\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',72105,4,0,NULL,NULL,'trd_chk2','scan',1780048787);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('trl_ds01','TRL-DS01.LZX','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/TRL-DS01.LZX',NULL,'XIM','DiskSpace.fim',NULL,NULL,'TRL',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'auto-added',21522,0,0,NULL,NULL,'trl_ds01','scan',1780048787);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('trs_bk22','TRS-BK22.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/TRS-BK22.LHA','ByteComment','XIM','ByteComment',NULL,NULL,'TRS','\___   _______    ¼\/   ___________/ TRiSTaR /     |    /    _/\____   ¼\     |  ReD /      |    \    \     V     \    | SeCToR',replace('___________________  _______________ _______\n\___   _______    ¼\/   ___________/ TRiSTaR\n  /     |    /    _/\____   ¼\     |  ReD  \n /      |    \    \     V     \    | SeCToR\n \_____ |____|\____\__________/____|________\n  \   /_____.__/  /  ______  \/    \___  \__\\n  / .   /  / _/ __/ ___/     /  /  /  /  /  /\n /_____/__   /__/_____/__/__/__/__/_____/__/\n    ________/of (tRSi/X-iNNOVATiON) \n                 PRESENTS       \n    ByteKiller V2.2 for /X3.+ and /X 4.+\n','\n',char(10)),'ByteKiller.eng.guide',replace('@database Bytekiller.guide\n@author "Byteandi/trsi"\n@$VER: Bytekiller.guide \n@node main "ByteKiller V2.2 Documentation (c) Byteandi/trsi"\n\n\n               _____         _____________  _____________\n               \   /_____.__/  /  ______  \/    \___  \__\\n               / .   /  / _/ __/ ___/     /  /  /  /  /  /\n              /_____/__   /__/_____/__/__/__/__/_____/__/ \n              ________/of (tRSi/X-iNNOVATiOn) presents:\n\n\n                           @{BG fill}@{"   ByteKiller V2.0    "   link Bytekiller}@{BG Background}\n                           @{BG fill}@{"   ByteComment V1.0   "   link ByteComment}@{BG Background}\n                           @{BG fill}@{" BytekillHandler V1.0 "   link Bytekillhandler}@{BG Background}\n                           @{BG fill}@{"     ByteLog V1.0     "   link ByteLog}@{BG Background}\n                           @{BG fill}@{"Registration & Updates" link updates}@{BG Background}\n                           @{BG fill}@{"      Greeting(s)     " link greetings}@{BG Background}\n                           @{BG fill}@{"      Other Tools     " link other_tools}@{BG Background}\n\n\n\n                           @{BG fill}@{"   Changes to  V2.2   "   link Changes}@{BG Background}\n\n\n@endnode\n@node Bytekiller "ByteKiller V2.0"\n\nByteKiller V2.0 is XIM Tool for /X 3.+ and /X 4.+\n\nWhat can Bytekiller :\n\nYou can start Bytekiller with "Nuke trsi* afl*.dms fake*.l*.txt"\n\nBytekiller search if the ToolType @{BG fill}@{"NUKER_ALL" link ToolTypes}@{BG Background}\nis installed or if there any Tooltypes looks like @{BG fill}@{"NUKER.<x>" link ToolTypes}@{BG Background} or @{BG fill}@{"PASSWORD.<x>" link ToolTypes}@{BG Background}\n\nIf there is NUKER_ALL, bytekiller starts for all who wanted to nuke and \nhave the right level,\nelse bytekiller search for the right name and if he have any PW-protection`s !\n\nBytekiller can write only one message to the Up-Downloader about all fakes\n\nIf bytekiller doesn`t can Lock Msgbase or Filelist, he wait a while and if \nthere is no chance for Lock, he aborted this routine..\n\nYou can Configure all Comments and Messages how ever you want..please \nsearch in @{BG fill}@{"Configuration" link mycfg}@{BG Background} for that\n\nBytekiller can search for hisself about Dl- and UlPathes or Path to Callerslog \nand any more, but it is important to install the Tooltype @{BG fill}@{"USER_DATA" link ToolTypes}@{BG Background}\nbecause I handle this for myself because some stupid changes in /X 4.+\n\nBytekiller can open an ASL-Requester if you have installed the Tooltype @{BG fill}@{"ASK_ASL" link ToolTypes}@{BG Background}\nbut this Option works only if you nuked from the Console..\n\nBytekiller have some extern Tools, if you use any of them you have the fastest\nNuker of the world...\n\nYou can set up All Options in Bytekiller !\n\n                           @{BG fill}@{"Start von Bytekiller"   link start_bytekiller}@{BG Background}\n\n@endnode\n@node start_bytekiller "ByteKiller V2.0"\n\nStart Bytekiller V2.0 :\n\nif you started bytekiller he ask (if exist) for the Password from the User,\nthan he shows, if there any UserComments about some fakes and ask if \nyou want to Nuke from List !\nYou can Insert so many Files you ever want with and without Wildcarts !\nNow Bytekiller Ask you if you want to nuke with Automodus and if you want to \nuse the same options for all Files.....\nif you use Automodus, you can set options for all files or options \nfrom file to file.\nnow Ask Bytekiller if you are interested to search for UpLoader and \nshow you his status if he have found the User..\nYou can take or give now so many Creditz you ever want..\nIf you have done this, bytekiller ask you to search for Downloader\nand do show you his status and ask if he can have some bytes back..\nIf that is Ok you can set up the comments for the Filelisting !\n\nNow Bytekiller changes the listing writes some messages to the \nUp-Downloader and ask you if you want to give some extra comments \nin that message (if you have install the Tooltype "EXTERN_COMMENT") !\n\n                              @{BG fill}@{"   ByteKiller V2.0    "   link Bytekiller}@{BG Background}\n                              @{BG fill}@{"ToolTypes" link ToolTypes}@{BG Background}\n@endnode\n\n@node ByteComment "ByteComment V1.0"\n\nByteComment V1.0 is XIM for /X 3+ \n\nThis Tool is for all User to add some comments in your Filelisting,\nthis comments are saved in your bytekiller/fakes/ dir and if you \nstarted Bytekiller and he found some Comments, he ask you to use this list !\n\n                              @{BG fill}@{"       Menue          "   link main}@{BG Background}\n                              @{BG fill}@{"   ByteKiller V2.0    "   link Bytekiller}@{BG Background}\n                              @{BG fill}@{"ToolTypes" link ToolTypes}@{BG Background}\n@endnode\n\n@node Bytekillhandler "Bytekillhandler V1.0"\n\nBytekillhandler is an external CLI-Tool to start in your logoff-batch, \nif you use this Tool, you doesn`t need to run ByteLog. \n\nthis Handler search in your Callerslog for any Uploads from the last user\nand saves his AccountNumber, this Handler doesn`t need DataFiles for that,\nso it doesn`t need any bytes from your HD`s\n\nmy tip : start bytekillhandler before all other in your Logoff-batch !\n\nexample for logoff-batch:\n----------------------------\n.key node\n\nDoors:Bytekilller/bytekillhandler BBS:node<node>/Callerslog\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n                           @{BG fill}@{"       Menue          "   link main}@{BG Background}\n                           @{BG fill}@{"   ByteKiller V2.0    "   link Bytekiller}@{BG Background}\n@endnode\n\n@node Bytelog "Bytelog V1.0"\n\nByteLog is XIM Tool for /X 3.+\n\nYou can start it with EXAMINE.INFO\n                      EXAMINE1.INFO .....  (/X 4.+)\n                      FILECHECK.INFO\n                      FILECHECK1.INFO .... (/X 4.+)\nin your SYSCMD/\n\nit saves the user and his Upload in one dataFile in your Conf,you can \nsay how many days you want to Log if you install @{BG fill}@{"LOG_DAYS=<tage>" link ToolTypes}@{BG Background}\nin your bytekiller.info, default is 7 days !\n\nByteLog doesn`t strip the UdLog, he search, if there is an Upload witch\nis older than your Log Days and overwrite this data !\n\nif you run this Door you doesn`t need Bytekillhandler !\n\n                              @{BG fill}@{"       Menue          "   link main}@{BG Background}\n                              @{BG fill}@{"   ByteKiller V2.0    "   link Bytekiller}@{BG Background}\n                              @{BG fill}@{"ToolTypes" link ToolTypes}@{BG Background}\n@endnode\n\n@node updates "Registration & Updates"\n\nUpdates :           !!!!! Only for Registered user from my Tools !!!!\n\nI want install the question if you like to see what Bytekiller \ndoes in autonukeModus, or if you want to do other nice thinks..\nHighscore List for Top nuked User\nRandom Comments for AutonukeModus...\nGive bytes to user who says any about fakes...\nall what you want....and what I can do\n\n IF YOU WANT TO BE REGISTERED FOR THAT OR NEXT COMMING TOOLS \n\n                PAY 20$ OR 30,-DM\n\n IF YOU WAS REGISTERED FOR FILEID AND TOOLS BEFORE, YOU GET THIS \n AND NEXT COMMING TOOLS FOR FREE\n\n                 # +49 (30) 7216071  4 Nodes Ringdown Dual 288er\n\n\n                              @{BG fill}@{"       Menue          "   link main}@{BG Background}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node greetings "Special Greeting(s)"\n\nSPEEDLOCK      for some tests in his BBS \nDeath Angel    because he installed all my Tools\n[-Amok-]       for his english changes in my Tool\nSpy/trsi       for his best Alloc() Routine...and some tips..\nByteAndi/trsi  for his very nice Tools\nsiegel/trsi    your Soft-Del is great, I like it and thx for your \n               configs\nTRSI           for the nice Group..\n\nMac LifeGuard  your TurboNews is Fast but Shit, I don`t like to hear \n               4MB ram is not enough or see my Listing in green or see\n               "can`t advange any furter..."\n\n\n                              @{BG fill}@{"       Menue          "   link main}@{BG Background}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node mycfg "All Informations about Configuration(s)"\n\nConfiguration from the messages :\n\n\n%L  ----->  List of all Fakes and Up-Download Day with \n            creditz taken/Given\n\n%N ------>  Name of the Nuker \n\n%F ------>  Name of the Faker or Downloader\n\n%T ------>  All bytes taken in this Session.......\n            (ONLY FOR UPLOADER.CFG)               \n          \n%G ------>  All bytes Given in this Session.......\n            (ONLY FOR UPLOADER.CFG)               \n\n%B ------>  All Dl-Bytes given back in this Session.......\n            (ONLY FOR DOWNLOADER.CFG)               \n\nexample :\n----------\n\n\nHey %F you are Lame ,\nI have taken you %T because some fakes.., here is a list of all\n\n%L\n\n             please Delete this Message !\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nmeans :\n\nHey byteandi/trsi you are lame,\nI have taken you 32228 bytes because some fakes.., here is the list of all\n\nOld UpLoad Bytes   :                         8738\nBytekiller V2.0    : Nuked *( -5)              71  Uploaded on (10-23-94)\nLamerDoc.txt       : Nuked *( -5)              71  Uploaded on (10-23-94)\n-------------------------------------------------\nNew UpLoad Bytes   :                            1\n\n             please Delete this Message !\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nConfiguration for your Comments in the Filelisting :\n\n%b  ---->  how many Creditz Taken/given\n%B  ---->  bytes from the Nuked File\n%N  ---->  Name of the Nuker\n\nExample :\n\nEnter FakeComment : ^^ %N Takes you %B Bytes * (%b) ^^\n\nmeans :\n\n                    ^^ Byteandi/trsi Takes you 32321 Bytes * (-5) ^^\n\n\n\n                              @{BG fill}@{"       Menue          "   link main}@{BG Background}\n                              @{BG fill}@{"   ByteKiller V2.0    "   link Bytekiller}@{BG Background}\n                              @{BG fill}@{"ToolTypes" link ToolTypes}@{BG Background}\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ToolTypes "All Informations about ToolTypes"\n\n\n\nUSER_DATA         -----> Path and Name from  UserData\n\nNUKER_ALL         -----> this means that there is no PW protection,\n                         All User with the right Level can nuke\n\nNUKER.<x>=<name>  -----> the name of the User who can Nuke \n                         x = Number from 1 to ..\n\nPASSWORD.<x>=<PW> -----> The Password from the User who can Nuke\n                         x = Number from 1 to ..\n\nANSI_MESSAGE      -----> if you doesn`t use this Tooltype, Bytekiller striped\n                         All Ansi-Codes in the messages...\n\nCOMMENT.x=<wieviel> ---> Comment for the Filelisting (default`s)\n                         x = Number from 1 to ..                 \n\nFAKE.<x>=<warum>  -----> Why you have Nuked the File (default`s)\n                         x = Number from 1 to ..                 \n\nSIZE.<x>=<shit!>  -----> Comments for the ByteSize in the Listing \n                         x = Number from 1 to ..                 \n\nFREE_COLOR=<36>   -----> Color for the Comment if you make the File to \n                         freedownload\n                         \nGIVE_COLOR=<32>   -----> Color for the Comment if you Give Creditz \n                         \n\nTAKE_COLOR=<44;39> ----> Color for the Comment if you Take Creditz \n                         \n\nEXTERN_COMMENT    -----> if you have this Toolstype, bytekiller ask\n                         if you want to write some lines to the \n                         Up-Downloader\n\nCREATE_FAKEFILE   -----> you can create Fakefiles if you want..\n\nASK_ASL           -----> Bytekiller ask you if you want to use an \n                         ASl-Requester to flag files\n\nSPY_LIST=<list>   -----> ONLY to use if you have installed SPY_LIST\n                         or you have the files and descriptions in more\n                         FileListings, than list = the last list of deleted\n                         Files..\nFREEDOWNLOAD=<text>  --> text = what ever you want to give as Comment in \n                         your Listing default is :\n                         "FREEDOWNLOAD FREEDOWNLOAD"\n\nLOG_DAYS=<days>   -----> for ByteLog, to say how many Days he must Log !\n                         \n\nCOM_COLOR=<44;39> -----> Color for ByteComment\n\n                              @{BG fill}@{"       Menue          "   link main}@{BG Background}\n                              @{BG fill}@{"   ByteKiller V2.0    "   link Bytekiller}@{BG Background}\n                              @{BG fill}@{"ToolTypes" link ToolTypes}@{BG Background}\n@endnode\n\n@node other_tools "All Informations about other Tools "\n\n\nSysopDownload V1.1     the best Tool for /X....\n\nNewFiles V2.1          with his funktions the first of his art...\n                       the last version was V2.5ß for any friends..\n                       I`m doesn`t interested this time to make some \n                       new versions of this Tool because there was \n                       to many out this moment ( Fuck TN or Task-NewScan)\n                       (Aqua-scan Rulez....I only can say..)\n\nBullView V1.5          one of the first Tools I have made\n                       1.5+ doesn`t from me it is shit...\n\nVereNaris V1.1         Cool work from re/Y\o and me \n\nFileId V1.5            Last FileId version I think to make some\n                       versions because I doesn`t like all other \n                       FileId Tools.....\n                       FileId V2.0 is in work and I think to bring \n                       this Tool January 95\n\nAutosent V1.6          Last Version for regidstered Sysops\n\nAutoCfg V1.0           only internal for some stupid User\n\nAFL-Quest V1.1         one of the first Tools I have made..\n                       \nFastDupe V1.0          nice programming of dre! and me hehe\n                       and nice to see how many lamer have made \n                       other versions\n\nByteMover V1.1         this Time Internal, but I think to release\n                       becuase all sysops like this Tool\n\nComment V1.2           Comment to Sysop, the first with Message-Upload\n                       \nFileDl V1.0            Download of All Filelistings from date \n                       \nRegister V1.5          Only Internal for (Mystic/X-Design)\n                       \nafl_Bull V1.0          The first Tool I have made, create 5 Bulls\n\n\n\n                              @{BG fill}@{"       Menue          "   link main}@{BG Background}\n                              @{BG fill}@{"   ByteKiller V2.0    "   link Bytekiller}@{BG Background}\n@endnode\n\n@node Changes "Changes to this Version V2.2 "\n\nSmall Bug in Memory-routines is now fixed..\n\nTooltype FREE_DOWNLOAD works now 100%\n\nI have added the "award.cfg", this txt is for Uploader if the sysop \nonly have Bytes given, if the sysop take and give Bytes he get the \nUploader.cfg !\n\nBytekiller is this Time by V2.3 (only for registered Sysops) and have \nmore new Futures, and I`m working to add some more Options\n\nKiloByte Option in Acp.Info works now 100%\n\n                              @{BG fill}@{"       Menue          "   link main}@{BG Background}\n                              @{BG fill}@{"   ByteKiller V2.0    "   link Bytekiller}@{BG Background}\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',85179,5,0,NULL,NULL,'trs_bk22','scan',1780048787);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('trs_bk23','TRS-BK23.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/TRS-BK23.LHA','ByteComment','XIM','ByteComment',NULL,NULL,'TRS','\___   _______    ¼\/   ___________/ TRiSTaR /     |    /    _/\____   ¼\     |  ReD /      |    \    \     V     \    | SeCToR',replace('___________________  _______________ _______\n\___   _______    ¼\/   ___________/ TRiSTaR\n  /     |    /    _/\____   ¼\     |  ReD  \n /      |    \    \     V     \    | SeCToR\n \_____ |____|\____\__________/____|________\n  \   /_____.__/  /  ______  \/    \___  \__\\n  / .   /  / _/ __/ ___/     /  /  /  /  /  /\n /_____/__   /__/_____/__/__/__/__/_____/__/\n    ________/of (tRSi/X-iNNOVATiON) \n                 PRESENTS       \n    ByteKiller V2.2 for /X3.+ and /X 4.+\n','\n',char(10)),'ByteKiller.eng.guide',replace('@database Bytekiller.guide\n@author "Byteandi/trsi"\n@$VER: Bytekiller.guide \n@node main "ByteKiller V2.2 Documentation (c) Byteandi/trsi"\n\n\n               _____         _____________  _____________\n               \   /_____.__/  /  ______  \/    \___  \__\\n               / .   /  / _/ __/ ___/     /  /  /  /  /  /\n              /_____/__   /__/_____/__/__/__/__/_____/__/ \n              ________/of (tRSi/X-iNNOVATiOn) presents:\n\n\n                           @{BG fill}@{"   ByteKiller V2.0    "   link Bytekiller}@{BG Background}\n                           @{BG fill}@{"   ByteComment V1.0   "   link ByteComment}@{BG Background}\n                           @{BG fill}@{" BytekillHandler V1.0 "   link Bytekillhandler}@{BG Background}\n                           @{BG fill}@{"     ByteLog V1.0     "   link ByteLog}@{BG Background}\n                           @{BG fill}@{"Registration & Updates" link updates}@{BG Background}\n                           @{BG fill}@{"      Greeting(s)     " link greetings}@{BG Background}\n                           @{BG fill}@{"      Other Tools     " link other_tools}@{BG Background}\n\n\n\n                           @{BG fill}@{"   Changes to  V2.2   "   link Changes}@{BG Background}\n\n\n@endnode\n@node Bytekiller "ByteKiller V2.0"\n\nByteKiller V2.0 is XIM Tool for /X 3.+ and /X 4.+\n\nWhat can Bytekiller :\n\nYou can start Bytekiller with "Nuke trsi* afl*.dms fake*.l*.txt"\n\nBytekiller search if the ToolType @{BG fill}@{"NUKER_ALL" link ToolTypes}@{BG Background}\nis installed or if there any Tooltypes looks like @{BG fill}@{"NUKER.<x>" link ToolTypes}@{BG Background} or @{BG fill}@{"PASSWORD.<x>" link ToolTypes}@{BG Background}\n\nIf there is NUKER_ALL, bytekiller starts for all who wanted to nuke and \nhave the right level,\nelse bytekiller search for the right name and if he have any PW-protection`s !\n\nBytekiller can write only one message to the Up-Downloader about all fakes\n\nIf bytekiller doesn`t can Lock Msgbase or Filelist, he wait a while and if \nthere is no chance for Lock, he aborted this routine..\n\nYou can Configure all Comments and Messages how ever you want..please \nsearch in @{BG fill}@{"Configuration" link mycfg}@{BG Background} for that\n\nBytekiller can search for hisself about Dl- and UlPathes or Path to Callerslog \nand any more, but it is important to install the Tooltype @{BG fill}@{"USER_DATA" link ToolTypes}@{BG Background}\nbecause I handle this for myself because some stupid changes in /X 4.+\n\nBytekiller can open an ASL-Requester if you have installed the Tooltype @{BG fill}@{"ASK_ASL" link ToolTypes}@{BG Background}\nbut this Option works only if you nuked from the Console..\n\nBytekiller have some extern Tools, if you use any of them you have the fastest\nNuker of the world...\n\nYou can set up All Options in Bytekiller !\n\n                           @{BG fill}@{"Start von Bytekiller"   link start_bytekiller}@{BG Background}\n\n@endnode\n@node start_bytekiller "ByteKiller V2.0"\n\nStart Bytekiller V2.0 :\n\nif you started bytekiller he ask (if exist) for the Password from the User,\nthan he shows, if there any UserComments about some fakes and ask if \nyou want to Nuke from List !\nYou can Insert so many Files you ever want with and without Wildcarts !\nNow Bytekiller Ask you if you want to nuke with Automodus and if you want to \nuse the same options for all Files.....\nif you use Automodus, you can set options for all files or options \nfrom file to file.\nnow Ask Bytekiller if you are interested to search for UpLoader and \nshow you his status if he have found the User..\nYou can take or give now so many Creditz you ever want..\nIf you have done this, bytekiller ask you to search for Downloader\nand do show you his status and ask if he can have some bytes back..\nIf that is Ok you can set up the comments for the Filelisting !\n\nNow Bytekiller changes the listing writes some messages to the \nUp-Downloader and ask you if you want to give some extra comments \nin that message (if you have install the Tooltype "EXTERN_COMMENT") !\n\n                              @{BG fill}@{"   ByteKiller V2.0    "   link Bytekiller}@{BG Background}\n                              @{BG fill}@{"ToolTypes" link ToolTypes}@{BG Background}\n@endnode\n\n@node ByteComment "ByteComment V1.0"\n\nByteComment V1.0 is XIM for /X 3+ \n\nThis Tool is for all User to add some comments in your Filelisting,\nthis comments are saved in your bytekiller/fakes/ dir and if you \nstarted Bytekiller and he found some Comments, he ask you to use this list !\n\n                              @{BG fill}@{"       Menue          "   link main}@{BG Background}\n                              @{BG fill}@{"   ByteKiller V2.0    "   link Bytekiller}@{BG Background}\n                              @{BG fill}@{"ToolTypes" link ToolTypes}@{BG Background}\n@endnode\n\n@node Bytekillhandler "Bytekillhandler V1.0"\n\nBytekillhandler is an external CLI-Tool to start in your logoff-batch, \nif you use this Tool, you doesn`t need to run ByteLog. \n\nthis Handler search in your Callerslog for any Uploads from the last user\nand saves his AccountNumber, this Handler doesn`t need DataFiles for that,\nso it doesn`t need any bytes from your HD`s\n\nmy tip : start bytekillhandler before all other in your Logoff-batch !\n\nexample for logoff-batch:\n----------------------------\n.key node\n\nDoors:Bytekilller/bytekillhandler BBS:node<node>/Callerslog\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n                           @{BG fill}@{"       Menue          "   link main}@{BG Background}\n                           @{BG fill}@{"   ByteKiller V2.0    "   link Bytekiller}@{BG Background}\n@endnode\n\n@node Bytelog "Bytelog V1.0"\n\nByteLog is XIM Tool for /X 3.+\n\nYou can start it with EXAMINE.INFO\n                      EXAMINE1.INFO .....  (/X 4.+)\n                      FILECHECK.INFO\n                      FILECHECK1.INFO .... (/X 4.+)\nin your SYSCMD/\n\nit saves the user and his Upload in one dataFile in your Conf,you can \nsay how many days you want to Log if you install @{BG fill}@{"LOG_DAYS=<tage>" link ToolTypes}@{BG Background}\nin your bytekiller.info, default is 7 days !\n\nByteLog doesn`t strip the UdLog, he search, if there is an Upload witch\nis older than your Log Days and overwrite this data !\n\nif you run this Door you doesn`t need Bytekillhandler !\n\n                              @{BG fill}@{"       Menue          "   link main}@{BG Background}\n                              @{BG fill}@{"   ByteKiller V2.0    "   link Bytekiller}@{BG Background}\n                              @{BG fill}@{"ToolTypes" link ToolTypes}@{BG Background}\n@endnode\n\n@node updates "Registration & Updates"\n\nUpdates :           !!!!! Only for Registered user from my Tools !!!!\n\nI want install the question if you like to see what Bytekiller \ndoes in autonukeModus, or if you want to do other nice thinks..\nHighscore List for Top nuked User\nRandom Comments for AutonukeModus...\nGive bytes to user who says any about fakes...\nall what you want....and what I can do\n\n IF YOU WANT TO BE REGISTERED FOR THAT OR NEXT COMMING TOOLS \n\n                PAY 20$ OR 30,-DM\n\n IF YOU WAS REGISTERED FOR FILEID AND TOOLS BEFORE, YOU GET THIS \n AND NEXT COMMING TOOLS FOR FREE\n\n                 # +49 (30) 7216071  4 Nodes Ringdown Dual 288er\n\n\n                              @{BG fill}@{"       Menue          "   link main}@{BG Background}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node greetings "Special Greeting(s)"\n\nSPEEDLOCK      for some tests in his BBS \nDeath Angel    because he installed all my Tools\n[-Amok-]       for his english changes in my Tool\nSpy/trsi       for his best Alloc() Routine...and some tips..\nByteAndi/trsi  for his very nice Tools\nsiegel/trsi    your Soft-Del is great, I like it and thx for your \n               configs\nTRSI           for the nice Group..\n\nMac LifeGuard  your TurboNews is Fast but Shit, I don`t like to hear \n               4MB ram is not enough or see my Listing in green or see\n               "can`t advange any furter..."\n\n\n                              @{BG fill}@{"       Menue          "   link main}@{BG Background}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node mycfg "All Informations about Configuration(s)"\n\nConfiguration from the messages :\n\n\n%L  ----->  List of all Fakes and Up-Download Day with \n            creditz taken/Given\n\n%N ------>  Name of the Nuker \n\n%F ------>  Name of the Faker or Downloader\n\n%T ------>  All bytes taken in this Session.......\n            (ONLY FOR UPLOADER.CFG)               \n          \n%G ------>  All bytes Given in this Session.......\n            (ONLY FOR UPLOADER.CFG)               \n\n%B ------>  All Dl-Bytes given back in this Session.......\n            (ONLY FOR DOWNLOADER.CFG)               \n\nexample :\n----------\n\n\nHey %F you are Lame ,\nI have taken you %T because some fakes.., here is a list of all\n\n%L\n\n             please Delete this Message !\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nmeans :\n\nHey byteandi/trsi you are lame,\nI have taken you 32228 bytes because some fakes.., here is the list of all\n\nOld UpLoad Bytes   :                         8738\nBytekiller V2.0    : Nuked *( -5)              71  Uploaded on (10-23-94)\nLamerDoc.txt       : Nuked *( -5)              71  Uploaded on (10-23-94)\n-------------------------------------------------\nNew UpLoad Bytes   :                            1\n\n             please Delete this Message !\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nConfiguration for your Comments in the Filelisting :\n\n%b  ---->  how many Creditz Taken/given\n%B  ---->  bytes from the Nuked File\n%N  ---->  Name of the Nuker\n\nExample :\n\nEnter FakeComment : ^^ %N Takes you %B Bytes * (%b) ^^\n\nmeans :\n\n                    ^^ Byteandi/trsi Takes you 32321 Bytes * (-5) ^^\n\n\n\n                              @{BG fill}@{"       Menue          "   link main}@{BG Background}\n                              @{BG fill}@{"   ByteKiller V2.0    "   link Bytekiller}@{BG Background}\n                              @{BG fill}@{"ToolTypes" link ToolTypes}@{BG Background}\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node ToolTypes "All Informations about ToolTypes"\n\n\n\nUSER_DATA         -----> Path and Name from  UserData\n\nNUKER_ALL         -----> this means that there is no PW protection,\n                         All User with the right Level can nuke\n\nNUKER.<x>=<name>  -----> the name of the User who can Nuke \n                         x = Number from 1 to ..\n\nPASSWORD.<x>=<PW> -----> The Password from the User who can Nuke\n                         x = Number from 1 to ..\n\nANSI_MESSAGE      -----> if you doesn`t use this Tooltype, Bytekiller striped\n                         All Ansi-Codes in the messages...\n\nCOMMENT.x=<wieviel> ---> Comment for the Filelisting (default`s)\n                         x = Number from 1 to ..                 \n\nFAKE.<x>=<warum>  -----> Why you have Nuked the File (default`s)\n                         x = Number from 1 to ..                 \n\nSIZE.<x>=<shit!>  -----> Comments for the ByteSize in the Listing \n                         x = Number from 1 to ..                 \n\nFREE_COLOR=<36>   -----> Color for the Comment if you make the File to \n                         freedownload\n                         \nGIVE_COLOR=<32>   -----> Color for the Comment if you Give Creditz \n                         \n\nTAKE_COLOR=<44;39> ----> Color for the Comment if you Take Creditz \n                         \n\nEXTERN_COMMENT    -----> if you have this Toolstype, bytekiller ask\n                         if you want to write some lines to the \n                         Up-Downloader\n\nCREATE_FAKEFILE   -----> you can create Fakefiles if you want..\n\nASK_ASL           -----> Bytekiller ask you if you want to use an \n                         ASl-Requester to flag files\n\nSPY_LIST=<list>   -----> ONLY to use if you have installed SPY_LIST\n                         or you have the files and descriptions in more\n                         FileListings, than list = the last list of deleted\n                         Files..\nFREEDOWNLOAD=<text>  --> text = what ever you want to give as Comment in \n                         your Listing default is :\n                         "FREEDOWNLOAD FREEDOWNLOAD"\n\nLOG_DAYS=<days>   -----> for ByteLog, to say how many Days he must Log !\n                         \n\nCOM_COLOR=<44;39> -----> Color for ByteComment\n\n                              @{BG fill}@{"       Menue          "   link main}@{BG Background}\n                              @{BG fill}@{"   ByteKiller V2.0    "   link Bytekiller}@{BG Background}\n                              @{BG fill}@{"ToolTypes" link ToolTypes}@{BG Background}\n@endnode\n\n@node other_tools "All Informations about other Tools "\n\n\nSysopDownload V1.1     the best Tool for /X....\n\nNewFiles V2.1          with his funktions the first of his art...\n                       the last version was V2.5ß for any friends..\n                       I`m doesn`t interested this time to make some \n                       new versions of this Tool because there was \n                       to many out this moment ( Fuck TN or Task-NewScan)\n                       (Aqua-scan Rulez....I only can say..)\n\nBullView V1.5          one of the first Tools I have made\n                       1.5+ doesn`t from me it is shit...\n\nVereNaris V1.1         Cool work from re/Y\o and me \n\nFileId V1.5            Last FileId version I think to make some\n                       versions because I doesn`t like all other \n                       FileId Tools.....\n                       FileId V2.0 is in work and I think to bring \n                       this Tool January 95\n\nAutosent V1.6          Last Version for regidstered Sysops\n\nAutoCfg V1.0           only internal for some stupid User\n\nAFL-Quest V1.1         one of the first Tools I have made..\n                       \nFastDupe V1.0          nice programming of dre! and me hehe\n                       and nice to see how many lamer have made \n                       other versions\n\nByteMover V1.1         this Time Internal, but I think to release\n                       becuase all sysops like this Tool\n\nComment V1.2           Comment to Sysop, the first with Message-Upload\n                       \nFileDl V1.0            Download of All Filelistings from date \n                       \nRegister V1.5          Only Internal for (Mystic/X-Design)\n                       \nafl_Bull V1.0          The first Tool I have made, create 5 Bulls\n\n\n\n                              @{BG fill}@{"       Menue          "   link main}@{BG Background}\n                              @{BG fill}@{"   ByteKiller V2.0    "   link Bytekiller}@{BG Background}\n@endnode\n\n@node Changes "Changes to this Version V2.2 "\n\nSmall Bug in Memory-routines is now fixed..\n\nTooltype FREE_DOWNLOAD works now 100%\n\nI have added the "award.cfg", this txt is for Uploader if the sysop \nonly have Bytes given, if the sysop take and give Bytes he get the \nUploader.cfg !\n\nBytekiller is this Time by V2.3 (only for registered Sysops) and have \nmore new Futures, and I`m working to add some more Options\n\nKiloByte Option in Acp.Info works now 100%\n\n                              @{BG fill}@{"       Menue          "   link main}@{BG Background}\n                              @{BG fill}@{"   ByteKiller V2.0    "   link Bytekiller}@{BG Background}\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',64259,7,0,NULL,NULL,'trs_bk23','scan',1780048787);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('trshconf','TRSHCONF.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/TRSHCONF.LHA',NULL,'XIM','exe.-l0S-eND0S-bBS-.exe',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,replace('CONFERENCE ACCESS LISTER FOR /X 2, 3+\n','\n',char(10)),'TConf2.Guide',replace('@database "TConf_V2.14_DOCS"\n@REMARK History at the end.\n@REMARK .-------------------------------------------------------------------.\n@REMARK |   ThrashConfV2.20, HyperText docs written by Thrash of ANTHROX.   |\n@REMARK `-------------------------------------------------------------------''\n@REMARK You need Multiview, AmigaGuide, or some other .Guide viewer.\n@REMARK Don''t be a fucking loser and view this with a standard ASCII viewer!!\n@REMARK $VER: Guide for TConf v2.20 (23rd Aug 1994)\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n@INDEX DIRECTORY\n@NODE MAIN "TConf: Contents."\n                    ___  _   _ _____ _   _ ____   _____  __     \n             __/\__/ _ \I \ I I_   _I I I I  _ \ / _ \ \/ /_/\__\n             \    / I_I I  \I I I I I I_I I I_) I I I \  /\    /\n             /_  _\  _  I I\  I I I I  _  I  _ <I I_I /  \/_  _\\n               \/ I_I I_I_I \_I I_I I_I I_I_I \_\\___/_/\_\ \/\n                              -*- PRESENTS -*-\n    .-------------------------------------------------------------------.\n    |          TCONF V2.20 RELEASE 2   (Conference Access Lister)       |\n    |         Written By THRASH Of ANTHR0X, ©1994/05 Gods''Gift.         |\n    |    (For ALL Versions And Variants Of Ami-Express BBS Software)    |\n    `-------------------------------------------------------------------''\n                              @{" What Is TConf? " Link WhatIs}\n                            @{" Noteable Features " Link Features}\n                      @{" Installation/Icon Requirements " LINK Installing}\n                           @{" Icon ToolTypes Used " LINK ToolTypes}\n                     @{" Running The Door From Ami-Express " LINK Running}\n                               @{" Main Index " LINK Directory}\n                            @{" Thanks And Greets " LINK Greets}\n                          @{" Other Gods''Gift Utils " LINK Others}\n@ENDNODE\n\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n@NODE WhatIs "TConf: What IS it?"\n\n	TConf Is Quite Simply A Conference Access Lister Door. I Know Your\nThinking That The Two or Three Already In Exsistence Are Slow So How The\nHell Can This Be A Door? Well, TConf Can Update In REALTIME in Under A\nSecond Due To It Being Written Entirely In Assembler. Try It Once And You''ll\nThrow Away The Others For Good! Just Take A Look At Some Of The @{"Features"Link Features}.\nTConf Is Compatable With All Versions Of Ami-Express Including S-Express By \nSigma-Seven.\n\n        A Quick Note To Chart-Loosers. If Your Gonna Vote On Any Sad,\nFake,Fixed Charts, At Least Make Sure You Get It Right!. Dont Vote For\nEither Myself Or P0T-N00dle As Individuals. We BOTH Do all The Work -\nTake A Look At The @{"Releases" LINK Others} We Have Both Done For You\nAll So Far!. Please Vote For Us As:\n\n                          GODS''GIFT/ANTHROX\n\nPS: If Somebody Else Asks P0T-N00Dle About "HIS" Tbar/TTop Etc, Ill Blow\n    A Fuckin Fuse! HeHe.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n@NODE Features "TConf: Features"\n\n     o - The GodsGift Seal Of Quality (Even More Rigorous Than Nintendo!)\n     o - 100% Assembly Language (As Always!).\n     o - 32 Node Compatable.(Actually 100!).\n     o - Compatable With ALL versions And Variants Of Ami-Express.\n     o - Can Be Run Resident.\n     o - RealTime Update Cause You Aint Never Seen One THIS Fast Before!\n     o - Using Nice And Easy Icon ToolTypes For ALL Command Options.\n     o - Can Display ANY Mixture Of conferences/Access "AREAS".\n     o - Optional HeaderFile Display.\n     o - Optional TailerFile Display.\n     o - Optional Statistics Bar.\n     o - Optional ClearScreen For Faster Ansi Displays & lazy Sysops.\n     o - Optional Password Protection (With Failure Comments To Callerslog).\n     o - Configurable Password Attempts.\n     o - One-Time-Passwords!!! (This one Is NICE for The Users!)\n     o - Fluffy Sheep Jumping On Pink Clouds All Over The Place.\n     o - I Was 100% Sober ThroughOut ALL coding.. (Well Almost!)\n     o - Not One Mention Of Fish-Fingers (SHIT!)\n     o - These Are Getting Silly.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n@NODE Installing "TConf: Installation"\n\n\n\n\n\nWhich Version Of Expess Are You Running?\n\n\n         @{" Version 2.x +/Variant " Link InstallingV2}  ........ Non-Icon Versions\n         @{" Version 3.x +/Variant " Link InstallingV3}  ........ Icon/ToolType Versions\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n@NODE InstallingV3 "TConf: Installation Express V3.x+"\nMake An Icon In Your Commands/BBSCMD (Or Commands/ConfX) Directory With\nThe Following ToolTypes:\n\nLOCATION=Path And Name Of This Util (Ie DOORS:TCONF2)\nMULTINODE=YES\nTYPE=XIM\nSTACK=4096\n\nNow Make An Icon (One Is Supplied In This Archive) For TConf2 Itself. You\nCan Rename The Util To Whatever You Wish So You Can Run Multiple Versions\nFor Different Conferences/Areas. Just Remember To Make The Icons For EVERY\nCopy You Want To Use. All Options Are Controlled By The Doors Icon \n@{"ToolTypes"Link ToolTypes} For Ease Of Use For Users Of Ami-Express V3+.\nAn Example Icon Is Supplied WIthin This Archive.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n@NODE InstallingV2 "TConf: Installation Express V2.x+ / Variant"\n\nCopy The Main Executable File To Your Doors Directory Or WhereEver You Want\nit. Make An Icon For The Util To Get Its Options From The @{"ToolTypes"Link ToolTypes}.\n\nYou Can Rename The Util To Whatever You Wish So You Can Run Multiple\nVersions For Different Conferences/Areas. Just Remember To Make An Icon And\nAn EXE For EVERY Different Copy You Want To Use. An Example Icon Is Supplied\nWIthin This Archive.\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n\n\n@NODE ToolTypes "TConf: Icon ToolTypes"\n\nThese Are All The ToolTypes Available To The Sysop:\n\n\n            @{" USER_DATA= " Link USER_DATA}  ........ Full Path/Name Of UserData.\n            @{" ACCESS_AREAS= " Link ACCESS_AREAS} ...... Area Names / Conference Numbers.\n            @{" HEADER_TEXT= " Link HEADER_TEXT} ....... Header Text To Be Displayed.\n            @{" TAILER_TEXT= " Link TAILER_TEXT} ....... Bottom Text To Be Displayed.\n            @{" CLEAR_SCREEN= " Link CLEAR_SCREEN} ...... Clear Sceen Before Any Output.\n            @{" STATS_BAR= " Link STATS_BAR} ......... Small Stats Bar Underneath Users.\n            @{" CONF_NAME= " Link CONF_NAME} ......... Name Of Conference To Be Displayed.\n            @{" PASSWORD= " Link PASSWORD} .......... Password Required To Continue.\n            @{" PASSWORD_TRIES= " Link PASSWORD_TRIES} .... Allowed Password Attempts.\n            @{" HACK_TEXT= " Link HACK_TEXT} ......... HangUp Text To Be Displayed.\n            @{" ONE_TIME_PASSWORD= " Link ONE_TIME_PASSWORD} . Special Type Of PassWord.\n            @{" EXPRESS_VERSION= " Link VERSION} ... Version/Variant Number Of Ami-Express.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n@NODE USER_DATA "TConf: ToolTypes - USER_DATA"\n\nUSER_DATA=X\n\nThis ToolType MUST Exist. "X" Is Simply The FULL Path AND Name Of Your\nUserData File ie:\n\nUSER_DATA=BBS:USER.DATA\n@ENDNODE\n\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n@NODE ACCESS_AREAS "TConf: ToolTypes - ACCESS_AREAS"\n\n\nWhich Version Of Expess Are You Running?\n\n\n         @{" Version 2.x +/Variant " Link ACCESS_AREAS_V2}  ........ Non-Icon Versions\n         @{" Version 3.x +/Variant " Link ACCESS_AREAS_V3}  ........ Icon/ToolType Versions\n@ENDNODE\n\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n@NODE ACCESS_AREAS_V3 "TConf: ToolTypes - ACCESS_AREAS /X3+"\n\nACCESS_AREAS=AREANAME1;AREANAME2 Etc..\n\nThis Is The Name Of The Area Used In Your "Access" Drawer. Multiple Areas\nCan Be Used But Each Area MUST Be Seperated By a Semi-Colon ";". Ie..\n\nACCESS_AREAS=SYSOP;NEWUSERS        - Show Users Whose "AREA" Is SYSOP Or\n                                     NEWUSERS.\n\nOr\n\nACCESS_AREAS=SYSOP;SPECIAL_USERS;AMIGA;CONSOLE\n@ENDNODE\n\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n@NODE ACCESS_AREAS_V2 "TConf: ToolTypes - ACCESS_AREAS /X2+"\n\nACCESS_AREAS=X;X;X Etc......\n\n\nWhere "X" Is The NUMBER Of the COnference You Want TConf To Display. You\nCan Use Multiple Conferences But Each Must Be Seperated By A Semi-Colon (;).\nIe:\n\nACCESS_AREAS=5          - Show Users With Access To Conf 5.\n\nOr\n\nACCESS_AREAS=5;9;1      - Show Users With Access To Confs 5;9 And 1.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n@NODE HEADER_TEXT "TConf: ToolTypes - HEADER_TEXT"\n\nHEADER_TEXT=X\n\nWhere "X" Is The FULL Path AND Name Of A Header/Logo Text You Wish To Be \nDisplayed BEFORE Any User Information Is Shown.Ie\n\nHEADER_TEXT=BBS:SCREENS/AMIGA/ACCESS_LOGO1.TXT\n@ENDNODE\n\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n@NODE TAILER_TEXT "TConf: ToolTypes - TAILER_TEXT"\n\nTAILER_TEXT=X\n\nWhere "X" Is The FULL Path AND Name Of A Tailer/Logo Text You Wish To Be \nDisplayed AFTER Any User Information Has Been Shown.Ie\n\nHEADER_TEXT=BBS:SCREENS/AMIGA/ACCESS_BOTTOM.TXT\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE CLEAR_SCREEN "TConf: ToolTypes - CLEAR_SCREEN"\n\nCLEAR_SCREEN=YES/NO\n\nIf You Wish The Screen To Be Cleared BEFORE Any Text Is Shown Then Make\nThis YES. It Just Saves Lazy Sysops From Including A Screen Clear On Logos.\nAnd Of Course Will Mean The Screen Update Will Be Slightly Faster Due To\nNo "Scroll-Up" By Ami-Express.\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n@NODE STATS_BAR "TConf: ToolTypes - STATS_BAR"\n\nSTATS_BAR=YES/NO\n\nIf You Wish The One Line Of Quick-Stats To Be Displayed At The Bottom Then\nSet This To YES. It Will Take The Util NO LONGER To Execute So You May As\nWell Leave It In, Unless You Simply Dont Like The Idea.\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE CONF_NAME "TConf: ToolTypes - CONF_NAME"\n\nCONF_NAME=YES/NO\n\nAfter The Logo/ClearScreen But BEFORE The Users Are Displayed To The Screen,\nYou Can Have The Conference Name From Which The Util Was Run Displayed At The\nTop Of The Ansi Output. Simply A Yes/No Option. NOTE: I said The Name Of\nThe Conference TConf Was Run FROM. *NOT* The Conference/s You Have Put Into\nThe @{" ACCESS_AREAS= " Link ACCESS_AREAS} ToolType.\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n@NODE PASSWORD "TConf: ToolTypes - PASSWORD"\n\nPASSWORD=XXXX....\n\nIf TConf Finds This ToolType Present With A Valid Password It Will Ask\nThe User To Input The Correct Password Before It Will Let Him Exit The\nUtil And Proceed Within The Conference. This Is Mainly Here For Those\nSysops Who Wish To Run This Door As Soon As A User Has Joined A Private\nConference. The Password Can be ANY combination Of Numbers/Letters Etc,\nUpto A Maximum Limit Of 59 Characters. The Check Made Is NOT Case Sensitive\nCause That Only Would Piss Legitimate Users Off! The User Will Be Given\n3 Attempts To Enter The Correct Password Followed By Return. If They\nFail All 3 Attempts TConf Will Legally Drop Carrier On The User And Notify\nThe Sysop By Leaving A Suitable Comment Attached To The Nodes CallersLog.\nAmi-Express Will Then Reset The Node And Await The Next Caller.\n\n\n\nSee Also: \n\n@{" PASSWORD_TRIES= " Link PASSWORD_TRIES},@{" ONE_TIME_PASSWORD= " Link ONE_TIME_PASSWORD},@{" HACK_TEXT= " Link HACK_TEXT}\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n@NODE PASSWORD_TRIES "TConf: ToolTypes - PASSWORD_TRIES"\n\nPASSWORD_TRIES=X\n\nWhere X Is A Number Between 1 And 9. This Tells TConf How Many Attempts\nAt Getting The Correct PassWord Are Allowed Before The User Is Kicked\nOff The Board. If This ToolType Is NOT Found Then TConf Will Default To\n3 Attempts If PassWords Are Required.\n\n\nSee Also: \n\n@{" ONE_TIME_PASSWORD= " Link ONE_TIME_PASSWORD},@{" HACK_TEXT= " Link HACK_TEXT},@{" PASSWORD= " Link PASSWORD}\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n@NODE HACK_TEXT "TConf: ToolTypes - HACK_TEXT"\n\nHACK_TEXT=X\n\nWhere X Is The FULL Name And Path Of A Text File The Sysop Wants To Be\nDisplayed Just Before A User/Hacker Is To Be Kicked Off The BBS. Ie\n\nHACK_TEXT=BBS:DOORS/TCONF/FUCK_OFF.TXT\n\n\n\nSee Also: \n\n@{" PASSWORD_TRIES= " Link PASSWORD_TRIES},@{" ONE_TIME_PASSWORD= " Link ONE_TIME_PASSWORD},@{" PASSWORD= " Link PASSWORD}\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n@NODE ONE_TIME_PASSWORD "TConf: ToolTypes - ONE_TIME_PASSWORD"\n\nONE_TIME_PASSWORD=YES/NO\n\nThis Is A Special PassWord Option. In Order For This To Run Correctly\nYou Will Need To Have An Assigned T: Directory. When A User Logs On\nAnd Correctly Gets The PassWord To A Particular Conference A SMALL File\nIn Your T: Dieectory Will Be Created By TConf. If He Rejoins This Same\nConf He Will NOT Need To Type In The PassWord Again. TConf Will Keep \nTrack Of ALL Conference PassWords Correctly Accessed By The User And \nNot Ask For Them A Second Time. This Even Tracks If The User Uses "RL" \nTo Re-Logon Or Simply Calls The Same Node Again Before Any Other Users.\n\n           Although A Good Idea (Thanks T.G.R!), This Way Of Doing\nThings Does Have A slight Problem. If A Hacking User Logs OnTo The Board\nStraight After The Legitimate User Has Called He Would Have Access\nTo The Protected Conference (DUMB!!). A Simple Way Of Stopping This \nProblem Is To Delete The File Created In The T: Directory In That \nParticular Nodes Logoff-Script. So Simply Add To Each Nodes Logoff-Script\nThe Following Line:\n\nDELETE T:TConfUser_NodeX     << "X" Is The Node Of The Logoff-Script!!\n\nThis Will Mean The User WOULD Be required To Insert The Correct PassWord\nIf He Re-Logs On Or Is The Next Person To Call The SAME Node, And Gets\nRid Of The Hacker Problem. I could Have Built This In But It Would Mean\nYou Would Have To Run A Second Util As Your "G" Or "RL" Commands And\nThis Was Thought To Be NOT A Good Idea. (Even If "G" Doors Do Suk In My\nBooks!)\n\n          Its A Little Hard To Explain How It Works So Try It Out And \nSee For YourSelf. A Nice Idea, But ,Of Course, Its Only Optional!\n\n   If This ToolType Does NOT Exist, Then TConf Will Default To NO.\n\nSee Also: \n\n@{" PASSWORD_TRIES= " Link PASSWORD_TRIES},@{" HACK_TEXT= " Link HACK_TEXT},@{" PASSWORD= " Link PASSWORD}\n@ENDNODE\n\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n@NODE VERSION "TConf: ToolTypes - EXPRESS_VERSION"\n\nEXPRESS_VERSION=X\n\nWhere "X" Is the MAIN Version Number Of The Express/Express Variant You Are \nUsing. TConf Of Course CAN Find The Internal Version By Itself (Which It \nDoes By Default If This ToolType Does NOT Exist), However This Will Allow\nThe Variant Programmers Who Are Using The OLD! Version 2 Release To Upgrade\nTheir Version To Number To 3 Without This Util Screwing Up On Them. \nIe If your Version Of Express Uses Icon ToolTypes For Everything Then:\n\nEXPRESS_VERSION=3\n\nEXPRESS_VERSION=4\n\nIf,However You Are Using S-Express 3 (If There Ever Is One), But It DOESNT\nUse Icon ToolTypes Then You Should Have:\n\nEXPRESS_VERSION=2\n\n\nWas That Simple Enough For You???.. Now You Can Upgrade The Version Number\nProperly Stefan!\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n@NODE RUNNING "TConf: Running From Ami-Express."\n\nYou Have Two Choices For Running TConf. Any Sysop Should Know What They Are.\nSimply Have The User Type In Whatever You Have Setup For The Door TO Run. Ie\nIn This Archive They Would Type In "ACCESS" And Be Told What Users Have \nAccess To The Confs Desribed In The ToolTypes. Or You Can Set It Up To Run\nIn An MCI script. For Instance Your NewUsers/Bull100.Txt May Say...\n\n~\n~CC_ACCESS\n\nWhich In MCI-Script Language Tells Ami-Express To Run The Door Called\nACCESS Rather Than Display This As A text File. Simple Stuff Eh?\n\nAlso See Notes On @{"Installation "Link Installing}.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n@NODE DIRECTORY "TConf: Main Index."\n\nHelpful Index Aint I???\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n@NODE Greets "TConf: Thanks And Greetings."\n                            ____.___.                               \n       _________._________I    I_  I____.________ _______ ____ ____ \n       \____    _   __   \    __/ _I    I_  _    \   _   \    I  _/ \n       /        I    I    \    I  \.    I  _/   _/   I    \_      \ \n       \___I    I    I____/    I___I    I___\    \________/   I____\\n           `----''----''    `----''   `----''    \____/      /____Ie  \n\nThanks To My Beta-Testers Who This Time Were: \n\n                    Ice D / Sysop BURGERBAR ATX-UKHQ.\n                 Picard / Sysop USS ENTERPRISE ATX-WHQ.\n\nGreetings To ALL The Following (And Many Forgotten) For Their FriendShip\nAnd Work (No Firkin Order!!) :-\n\n                   ALL MEMBERS Of ANTHROX WORLDWIDE\n\n             PRESTiGE, PARADOX, DELiRiUM, FAiRLiGHT, GOD\n\n\nIf You Feel The Need To Get Sommit Off Your Chest Or Wish To Bore Me\nShitless With Your "AMAZING" Ideas For A New Util Hehe. Then Call One Of\nThe WorldWide Anthrox Boards. If You Are Further Interested In GODSGiFT\nUtils Then A Special Conference Has Been Set Up On Our EHQ (BURGERBAR!),\nWhere You Can Chat To Myself And Pot-Noodle About Them.\n\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n| USS ENTERPRiSE ... +1-412-233-2611   USS ENTERPRiSE ... +1-RiNG-D0WN!!! |\n| USS ENTERPRiSE ... +1-RiNG-D0WN!!!   USS ENTERPRiSE ... +1-RiNG-D0WN!!! |\n| USS ENTERPRiSE ... +1-RiNG-D0WN!!!   USS ENTERPRiSE ... +1-RiNG-D0WN!!! |\n| BURGER BAR ....... +44-PRi-VATE!!!   BURGER BAR ....... +44-RiNG-D0WN!! |\n| CONSOLiA ......... +32-11-234-523!   CONSOLiA ......... +32-11-234-872! |\n| SYNERGY .......... +49-PRi-VATE!!!   SYNERGY .......... +49-PRi-VATE!!! |\n| SYNERGY .......... +49-***-ISDN!!!   SYNERGY .......... +49-***-ISDN!!! |\n| METROPOLIS ....... +34-XXXX-XXXX!!   METROPOLIS ....... +34-XXXX-XXXX!! |\n| TRADE LINE ....... +1-XXXX-XXXX!!!   TRADE LINE ....... +1-XXXX-XXXX!!! |\n| THE WALL ......... +44-PRI_VATE!!!       ***** SPACE F0R RENT!! *****   |\n+-------------------------------------------------------------------------+\n                         -* SPECiAL REGARDS TO -*-\n              PRESTiGE, PARADOX, REDNEX, DELiRiUM, FAiRLiGHT.\n\n\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\n@NODE Others "TConf: Other Gods''Gift Releases"\nThere should be a directory that came with this archive containing lots of\nexample outputs from a selection of the utils featured below.\n\nContents: G''G Release History.\n=============================================================================\n:::::::::::::::::::::::::  GODS''GIFT/ATX RELEASES  ::::::::::::::::::::::::::\n=============================================================================\nDates are the release/completion dates of the latest update.\nLatest releases at the top!...\n=============================================================================\nATX-TC22.LHA | 16-Feb-95 | ThrashConf V2.20 (68000) Thrash of Anthrox\n-------------+-----------+---------------------------------------------------\n Release [2] | Purpose:  | Small bug fixed.\n             |           | \n=============================================================================\nATX-TC2.LHA  | 09-Sep-94 | ThrashConf V2.14 (68000) Thrash of Anthrox\n-------------+-----------+---------------------------------------------------\n Release [1] | Purpose:  | Conference Access Lister Door For ALL /X Versions\n-------------+-----------+---------------------------------------------------\n             | Extras:   | FAST code. Can be made RESIDENT.\n             |           | 32 Node/Multi-Node Compatable (Upto 100 nodes!!)\n             |           | Compatable With ALL Versions Of Ami-Express.\n             |           | Optional Header/Tailer TEXTS.\n             |           | Any Number Of Single/Mixed "Areas"/Conferences.\n             |           | REALTIME Updated Cause This One Is FAST!.\n             |           | Using Icon TOOLTYPES As Standard For The 1st Time.\n             |           | Optional User STATISTICS Bar At Bottom.\n             |           | Option To Display COnference Name.\n             |           | Optional SCREENCLEAR For Lazy Text Makers/Sysops.\n             |           | Optional PASSWORD Protection.\n             |           | PassWord HACK Attempts Logged To CallersLog.\n             |           | Optional Text Displayed On Drop Carrier.\n             |           | Configuarable Amount Of PassWord Attempts.\n             |           | One-Time-PassWords. User Has To Only Enter Pass-\n             |           | Word Once, Including Re-logons Etc! Till Node Is\n             |           | Used By Different User.\n=============================================================================\nATX-SDC1.LHA | 04-Apr-94 | Super-DupeCheck v1.0 (68000) P0T-NOoDLE of Anthrox\n-------------+-----------+---------------------------------------------------\n Release [1] | Purpose:  | Dupe-Checker & FileCheck Handler Door.\n-------------+-----------+---------------------------------------------------\n             | Extras:   | FAST code. Can be made resident.\n             |           | Can run infinite other filechecker-type doors.\n             |           | Can display infinite text files. (Global & Conf)\n             |           | Cool percentage-done progress bar!\n             |           | 32-Node compatable. (Actually, upto 100nodes)\n             |           | "Script"-style config file for versatility\n             |           | Skips archive-checking if file is duped.\n             |           | Allows for DupeChecking to be skipped for Named\n             |           | Allows for DupeChecking to be skipped for Access\n             |           | Allows for a special Dupe-Checker filelisting\n             |           |    that is checked by not viewable by users.\n             |           | Allows for DupeChecking only on selected DirFiles\n             |           | Allows for a special Global-Dupe-Dir listing that\n             |           |    is seached for uploads in ALL conferences.\n             |           | Actual DupeChecking does NOT have to be performed.\n             |           |    Can be used to display messages and run doors.\n             |           | Can check for Dupes where *.LHA = *.ZOO etc.\n             |           | Skips DupeCheck on private uploads.\n=============================================================================\nATX-TCOM.LHA | 01-Oct-93 | ThrashComment v1.00  (68000)     Thrash of Anthrox\n-------------+-----------+---------------------------------------------------\n             | Purpose:  | Sysop Comment Door.\n-------------+-----------+---------------------------------------------------\n             | Extras:   | Will use any number of sysops between 1 and 99.\n             |           | Header/Tailer texts. Special External file option\n             |           | to display your own ansi instead of the built-in\n             |           | defaults to make it look how YOU want it.\n=============================================================================\nATX-SAL5.LHA | 20-Aug-93 | Super-AmiLog v2.00   (68000) P0T-NOoDLE of Anthrox\n-------------+-----------+---------------------------------------------------\n Release [5] | Purpose:  | Create a list of the last callers.\n-------------+-----------+---------------------------------------------------\n             | Extras:   | Keeps records of best number of callers etc in\n             |           | one day. Outputs a list of weekly statistics with\n             |           | info on the last 7 days, and the weekly averages.\n             |           | MULTI-NODE compatable. 0 to 20 callers shown.\n             |           | Non-ANSI mode. Header/Tailer texts. Random 1 line\n             |           | messages. Can be made Resident. Docs built into\n             |           | the util. Mini-Callerslog made with compact info\n             |           | about each call. For each user, can show Baud,\n             |           | Node,Name,Location,Connect Time,Logoff Time,\n             |           | Time Spent Online, Up/Down KBytes,Actions.\n             |           | Actions include: Up/Download,Up/Download Failed,\n             |           | Password Hack,Lost Carrier,Paged Sysop,Sysop Cmds.\n             |           | Shows: Calls Today/Yesterday,Up/Down Files/Bytes\n             |           | today, and finally Hours used today.\n=============================================================================\nATX-NEWL.LHA | 12-Jun-93 | Super-NewLst v1.00   (68000) P0T-NOoDLE of Anthrox\n-------------+-----------+---------------------------------------------------\n             | Purpose:  | Make a list of all new users waiting for access.\n-------------+-----------+---------------------------------------------------\n             | Extras:   | Lists 3 users per line for compact output.\n             |           | Put it as a bulletin on your BBS and your users\n             |           | can let you know if any of the new guys are OK...\n=============================================================================\nATXTBAR1.LHA | 23-May-93 | ThrashBar    v1.01   (68000)     Thrash of Anthrox\n-------------+-----------+---------------------------------------------------\n             | Purpose:  | BarCharts of Top Up/Down Bytes, Up/Down Files,\n             |           | Callers, Message Writters. \n-------------+-----------+---------------------------------------------------\n             | Extras:   | Exclude users (by number or sec level).\n             |           | 0 to ALL users shown on Chart. User Ratings.\n             |           | Non-ANSI Mode. Header file. Random 1 Line Msgs.\n             |           | Shows overall BBS statistics: megs/files up/down,\n             |           | number of leeches/elites/normals. Built in Docs.\n             |           | Archive contains .GUIDE (hypertext) docs.\n=============================================================================\nATX-TT15.LHA | 23-May-93 | ThrashTop    v1.05   (68000)     Thrash of Anthrox\n-------------+-----------+---------------------------------------------------\n             | Purpose:  | Normal Chart of Top Up/Down Loaders.\n-------------+-----------+---------------------------------------------------\n             | Extras:   | Unlimited Header/Tailer texts.\n             |           | 0 to ALL users shown on Chart. User Ratings.\n             |           | Also shows users'' Location,Messages,Calls,Files up\n             |           | Shows overall BBS statistics: megs/files up/down,\n             |           | number of leeches/elites/normals. Built in Docs.\n=============================================================================\nATX-STAT.LHA | 23-May-93 | ThrashStat   v1.03   (68000)     Thrash of Anthrox\n-------------+-----------+---------------------------------------------------\n             | Purpose:  | Create a list of all users and their statistics.\n-------------+-----------+---------------------------------------------------\n             | Extras:   | Shows users'' Number,Name,Location,Up/Down Bytes,\n             |           | Up Files,Calls,Messages Written.\n             |           | Shows total number of Users,Uploads,Msgs, etc.\n=============================================================================\nATX-STC3.LHA | 18-Jan-93 | Super-TopCPS v1.06   (68000) P0T-NOoDLE of Anthrox\n-------------+-----------+---------------------------------------------------\n Release [3] | Purpose:  | Create a list of the best CPS rates.\n-------------+-----------+---------------------------------------------------\n             | Extras:   | Never "forgets" CPS rates because it stores then\n             |           | in it''s file! Shows 0 to 20 users. Head/Tail file.\n             |           | Shows: Username,Date of CPS rate,Filename used,\n             |           | wether it was an Up/Download,Baud Rate,CPS rate.\n=============================================================================\nATX-TCON.LHA | 02-Oct-92 | ThrashConf   v1.00   (68000)     Thrash of Anthrox\n-------------+-----------+---------------------------------------------------\n             | Purpose:  | Create a list of all users with access to a conf.\n-------------+-----------+---------------------------------------------------\n             | Extras:   | Shows 3 users per line for compact output.\n             |           | Great for those private conferences!\n=============================================================================\n:::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\n=============================================================================\n@ENDNODE\n\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n@REMARK -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n','\n',char(10)),'{"LOCATION":"Path","TYPE":"XIM","STACK":"4096"}','auto-added',31340,6,0,NULL,NULL,'trshconf','scan',1780048787);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('trsi_add','TRSI-ADD.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/TRSI-ADD.LHA','DRE!ADVERTISE','XIM','.....................    .................',NULL,'DR.DRE!','TRSI','.::::::: ..........:  ::::::.....  :::::: ::::::::: :::::: ::::: ...... ::::: :::::: .::::::::: :::::: :::::.::::::.::::: ::::::.',replace('.....................    .................\n  .::::::: ..........:  ::::::.....  ::::::\n ::::::::: :::::: ::::: ...... ::::: ::::::\n.::::::::: :::::: :::::.::::::.::::: ::::::.\n<-rS!/aRt-.::::::- /X iNNoVATiON pRESENTs ->\n      DRE!ADVERTISE v2.o [RELEASE 2]\n BEST BBS ADD MANAGER AROUND - CRSR SUPPORT\n   WRITTEN BY DR.DRE!  TRSI /X-iNNoVATioN\n','\n',char(10)),'DRE!ADVERTISE.Guide',replace('@DATABASE\n@Remark $VER: Version 2.o [RELEASE 2] (Monday 12-Sep-94 17:48:18)\n@Remark AmigaGuide DataBase for dRE!ADVERtiSE 2.o\n\n@Node MAIN "dRE!ADVERtiSE v2.o - [RELEASE 2] for AMiEXPRESS 3.xx - 4.xx"\n\n                   ._________________  ______        .\n                   l___       /      \\/    _/_______.:\n                     /       /   /  _/\\___      /    :\n                    /_______/-rS!\\_____\\  _____/     |\n                          /_______|     \\/`94/_______|\n                   «««          dR.dRE! oF         »»»\n                   »»» tRISTAr aNd rEd^sECTOr iNc! «««\n                   «««    aMiEXPRESs iNNoVATioN    »»»\n\n                 iS pROUd tO pRESENt: dRE!aDVERtiSE v2.o\n\n                 @{"             iNtRoDUCtiON!            " LINK Introduction}\n                 @{"             iNStALLATiON!            " LINK Installation}\n                 @{"               tOOLtYPES!             " LINK Tooltypes}\n                 @{"                OPtiONS!              " LINK Options}\n                 @{"                CREDitS!              " LINK Credits}\n                 @{"         OtHER dRE!dOORS/tOOlS        " LINK Other}\n                 @{"               GREETINGS!             " LINK Greetings}\n                 @{"           tRSi /X-iNNoVATioN         " LINK Innovation}\n                 @{"           REGiStER DRE!DooRS         " LINK Register}\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Introduction "dRE!ADVERtiSE iNtRoDUCtiON"\n\n                            ABOUT DRE!ADVERtiSE\n                          - ------------------- -\n\nDRE!ADVERtiSE v2.o is a powerfull DataBase Manager for BBS Adverts.\nUntil now your MsgBase will be clean from all BBS Add`s.\n\nFeatures: Full Level Configurable\n          Enter,View,Download,Remove BBS Adverts.\n          CURSOR Key Support\n          and more...\n\nAll what you need is any Model of the great AMIGA, OS2.x or higher.\nRegistered (or not) Version of AmiExpress 3.xx - 4.xx.\nAssigned Doors:\nThats all... have Fun with this powerfull Door.\n\n\n@{"  MAIN  " LINK MAIN}\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Installation "dRE!ADVERtiSE iNStALLAtiON"\n\n                           INSTALL DRE!ADVERtiSE\n                         - --------------------- -\n\nCopy the complete DRE Directory to your Doors.\n\nNOTE: Until now all my Doors are placed in this DOORS:DRE/ Directory,\n      so may you need them for other Doors/Utils again.\n\nThen Copy the Add.Info to your BBS:COMMANDS/BBSCMD/ .\nNow the rough Install is done, open now the \nDOORS:DRE/DRE!ADVERT/DRE!ADVERTISE.INFO to Edit the @{" ToolTypes " LINK Tooltypes}\n\nIf you have configured the DRE!ADVERTISE.INFO the Install is done.\nEnjoy it...\n\n\n@{"  MAIN  " LINK MAIN}\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Tooltypes "AVAiLAVLE TOOLtYPES"\n\n                        TOOLtYPES FOR DRE!ADVERtiSE\n                      - --------------------------- -\n\nVIEW_ADD=<LEVEL>  - This allows a User with this Level or higher to view the\n                    posted BBS Adverts.\n\nENTER_ADD=<LEVEL> - This allows a User with this Level or higher to Add a\n                    BBS Advert to the Door.\n\nREMOVE_ADD=<LEVEL> - This allows a User with this Level or higher to remove\n                     BBS Adverts from DRE!ADVERTISE.\n\nDL_ADDS=<LEVEL>    - This allows a User with this Level or higher to Down-\n                     load the Adverts from DRE!ADVERTISE.\n\nPACK_PATH=<PATH>   - Here yo can specify the Path where the Adverts where\n                     packed before a User can Download it.\n                     Default Path is RAM:\n                     NOTE: The Path must end with a '':'' or ''/'' !!!\n\n@{"  MAIN  " LINK MAIN}\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Options "DRE!ADVERTISE MENU OPTIONS"\n\n                        DRE!ADVERTISE MENU OPTIONS\n                      - -------------------------- -\n\nMENU(0) - VIEW BBS ADVERT(S) [·] Here the User can view a List with all\n          available Advertisments, and choose between it!\n          \nMENU(1) - ENTER BBS ADVERT(S) [·] Here the User can add a own Advert to\n          the DataBase. He will be asked if he like to use the normal\n          Editor or Upload the Advert, (NO ASCII SEND, real binaer (U/L))\n          The Door looks if may any special signs in the Advert Name, and\n          replace them against normal Signs.\n\nMENU(2) - DOWNLOAD BBS ADVERT(S) [·] Here the User can Download all Addis\n          which are available. DRE!ADVERTISE will pack all Adverts to an\n          LHA Archive (So may your LHA should be placed in your C: Dir.\n          The Path where DRE!ADVERTISE Pack the LHA Archive, can you con-\n          figure in the DRE!ADVERTISE.INFO\n          NOTE: Path must end with an `:` or `/` !!!\n\nMENU(3) - REMOVE BBS ADVERT(S) [·] Here the User is able to remove Adverts\n          from the Door. He will see a List with all available Addi`s and\n          can then choose which he will delete.\n          Better you set the REMOVE_ADD Level high so thats only you and\n          your CoSysops can Access them.\n\nMENU(4) - QUIT DRE!ADVERTISE [·] Explained his self i think.\n\n\n@{"  MAIN  " LINK MAIN}\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE Credits "Noteable Credits"\n\n                             NOTEABLE CREDITS\n                           - ---------------- -\n\n DRE!ADVERTISE v2.o [RELEASE 2] was written by Dr.Dre!/tRSi /X-iNNoVATioN\n\n     The AmigaGuide DataBase was written by Dr.Dre!/tRSi /X-iNNoVATioN\n\n        AMIEXPRESS PROFESSIONAL (C) - LIGHTSPEED TECHNOLOGIES INC.\n\n      MUSICAL SUPPORT: ANTHRAX [·] NIRVANA [·] THERAPY [·] PHILIP BOA\n\n     FOOD SUPPORT : MC`DONALD`S [·] CITY GRILL [·] PIZERIA PULCINELLA\n\n\n@{"  MAIN  " LINK MAIN}\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Other "Other already released DRE!DOORS/TOOLS"\n\n                           OTHER DRE!DOORS/TOOLS\n                         - --------------------- -\n\n NAME                  TYPE   VERSION\n---------------------+------+---------------------------------------------\nDRE!WHO              | XiM  |  V1.1  PUBLIC\nDRE!FRONT            | XiM  |  V1.O  PUBLIC\nCHAT!ACCESS          | XiM  |  v1.2  PUBLIC\nDRE!COMMENT          | XiM  |  V1.3  PRiVATE RELEASE FOR REG. USERS ONLY\nDOORMENU             | XiM  |  v1.o  PUBLIC\nDRE!WALL             | XiM  |  v1.2  PRiVATE RELEASE FOR REG. USERS ONLY\nFAST!DUPE            | XiM  |  v1.11 PRIVATE COOP DR.DRE!^BYTEANDI\nMOST WANTED          | XiM  |  v1.52 PRiVATE RELEASE FOR REG. USERS ONLY\nLHA CHEKKO           | DOS  |  v2.o  PRiVATE RELEASE FOR REG. USERS ONLY\nSPEEDADD (TXT)       | DOS  |  v1.09 PRiVATE RELEASE FOR REG. USERS ONLY\nSPEEDZIP (ZIP)       | DOS  |  v1.o  BETA\nBULL!VIEW            | XiM  |  v1.02 PUPLIC\nDRE!FREE             | XiM  |  v1.ß  PRIVATE RELEASE FOR REG. USERS ONLY\nLAST!JUNKZ           | AiM  |  v1.0  PRIVATE RELEASE FOR REG. USERS ONLY\nPWFAILURE            | XiM  |  v1.1  PUPLIC\nBETA!REPORT          | XiM  |  v0.92 BETATESTER(S) ONLY\nDRE!NODECHECK        | XiM  |  c0.ß  PUBLIC\nCARD DISTRIBUTOR     | XiM  |  v1.oa BETA (PRIVATE^PUBLIC VERSION SOON)\nDRE!SENDLIST         | XiM  |  v1.2  PUBLIC\nNUP^SYSPW COMMNTER   | XiM  |  v1.2  PUBLIC\nNEWUSER SCRIPT       | XiM  |  v1.21 PUBLIC\nGLOBAL USER STATUS   | XiM  |  v1.9  PUBLIC\nSPEEDLIST (USERLIST) | XiM  |  v1.ß  PRIVATE RELEASE FOR REG. USERS ONLY\nDESCRIPTION!SNAP     | AiM  |  v1.o  PUPLIC\n---------------------+------+---------------------------------------------\nTHERE ARE ALSO SOME OLDER (AiM) DOORS AVAILABLE WHERE I CANT REMEMBER\nWHAT WAS IT EXACTLY ... SEARCH ONLY FOR DR.DRE!\nIF YOU LIKE MY DOORS/UTILS AND WANT BE @{" REGISTERED " LINK Register} USER OF IT\n@{"  MAIN  " LINK MAIN}\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Register "REGISTER DRE!DOORS"\n\n                            REGISTER DRE!DOORS\n                          - ------------------ -\n\nTHE REGISTRATION FEE IS 2O$, SHURE YOU THINK PHEW! A LOT OF MONEY, BUT READ\nWHAT I WILL BET FOR YOUR MONEY.\n\n1. YOU WANNA BE SHURE YOU GET ONLY DOORS WITHOUT ANY BACKDOOR ? OF COURSE\n   THE REGISTERED USER(S) ARE GETTING ONLY PRIVATE VERSIONS, ALL PUBLIC\n   VERSIONS HAVE A TIMELIMIT OR I REMOVE SOME MENU POINTS. ONLY!!! THE REG.\n   USERS HAVE THE FULL VERSION.\n\n2. YOU FOUND A BUG ? -> REPORT HIM TO ME AND YOU GET SOON AS POSSIBLE A\n   FIXED VERSION, NO LONG NEED TO WAIT FOR A NEWER RELEASE VERSION.\n\n3. YOU HAVE SOME GOOD IMPROVEMENTS, TALK WITH ME, AND I WILL SEE IF I CAN\n   REALISE IT.\n\n4. YOU NEED A PRIVATE DOOR ONLY FOR YOUR BBS, I WILL CODE THEM.\n\n5. PRIVATE SUPPORT CONFERENCE IN A FUCKEN FAST TRSI BOARD IN NEDERLAND.\n\n6. ALL DOORS/UTILS ARE INCLUDING YOUR REGISTER STRING.\n\n7. YOU`LL GET ALL LATER VERSIONS OR NEW DOORS FOR THIS PRICE.\n\n                  SIMPLY YOU GET THE BEST SUPPORT AROUND.\n          THINK ABOUT IT AND KEEP THE PROGRAMMERS PROGRAMMING !!!\n\nIF YOU ARE INTERESTED SO CONTACT ME AT ANY TRSI BOARD OR SIMPLY AT THE\n                           TRSI EHQ - BOONDOCKS\n\n@{"  MAIN  " LINK MAIN}\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Greetings "GREETINGS"\n\n                            SOME FAST GREETINGS\n                          - ------------------- -\n                               TO THIS DUDES\n\n   [·] MCLOUD/TRSI [·] MARIO [·] ECS [·] SIEGEL [·] BYTEANDI [·] SPY [·]\n    [·] VALSHARE [·] REDSKIN! [·] EMPIRE/MST [·] RICHI/FLT [·] NICK [·]\n    [·] SAL-1/TRSI [·] TRITON [·] VAMPIRE/PDY [·] XTREME [·] BJOERN [·]\n     [·] LINEBACKER [·] BLOODWOLF [·] JUAN/TRSI [·] BLIND GUARDIAN [·]\n           [·] THE CHARGE [·] SPEEDLOCK [·] AND ALL I FORGOT...\n\n@{"  MAIN  " LINK MAIN}\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Innovation "TRSI /X-iNNoVATioN"\n\n\n\n                      TRSI /X-iNNoVATioN MEMBERS ARE:\n                    - ------------------------------- -\n\n\n                               DR.DRE!/TRSI\n                               BYTEANDI/TRSI\n                                SIEGEL/TRSI\n                                 SPY/TRSI\n\n   IF YOU WANNA JOIN US, SO GET IN TOUCH WITH ONE OF THE DUDES ABOUVE...\n@ENDNODE\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,47985,11,0,NULL,NULL,'trsi_add_dre_advertise','scan',1780048787);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('trsi_ar','TRSI-AR.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/TRSI-AR.LHA','ASKII-REQUEST','XIM','ASKII-REQUEST',NULL,'SieGeL/tRSi','TRSI','\    ____    )  /___/\_| & rED sECTOR ¡NC | .-\___\ | \___\__   /   |  /X ¡NNOVATION   | `---|___|___|______/____|---[ [RESENTS ]---''',replace(' _____________ ___Mo! __.<---[ tRISTAR ]---.\n \    ____    )  /___/\_| & rED sECTOR ¡NC |\n.-\___\ | \___\__   /   |  /X ¡NNOVATION   |\n`---|___|___|______/____|---[ [RESENTS ]---''\n.------------------------------------------.\n|    aSKII-rEQUEST V1.oo bY SieGeL/tRSi    |\n`------------------------------------------''\ngREAT rEQUEST-dOOR wITH fREELY cONFIGURABLE\n dEZIGN, pSEUDO-eALL mESSAGES, oUTPUT-bULL\n--------------------------------------------\n','\n',char(10)),'aSKII-rEQUEST.guide',replace('@database aSKII-rEQUEST V1.0 - English DataBase\n@author "SieGeL/tRSi"\n@(c) "Copyright © 1995 (tRSi/X-iNNOVATiON)"\n@$VER: aSKII-rEQUEST.guide 1.00 (06-04-95)\n\n@index Main\n\n@node Main "aSKII-rEQUEST - BBS uTIL wRITTEN bY SieGeL oF (tRSi/X-iNNOVATiON)"\n@{b}                                                                     ______\n .-----------[ TRSI (/X·INNOVATION) ]------------.       _  ________/     /\n | _________________________________       ______`-------\\//  __    \\    /---.\n | \\       _____________     /     /______(______)  _     /    \\     \\  /    |\n |  \\______\\    |    __/   _/\\______       /     | (/)   /     /\\     \\/ Mo! |\n | \\     |      |    \\      \\       |     /      |  ¯   /     / /\\     \\_    |\n | \\\\    l______|_____\\      \\___________/_______|    _/     /_/  \\_____/    |\n `---------------------\\______/-----------------------\\_____/-\\_____/--------''@{ub}\n\n                           iS pROUD tO pRESENT:\n\n@{APEN 2}                   aSKII-rEQUEST V1.0 written by SieGeL@{APEN 1}\n\n                      @{" COPYRIGHT! " LINK COPYRIGHT}     @{"DISTRIBUTION" LINK DISTRIBUTION}\n                      @{"INTRODUCTION" LINK INTRODUCTION}     @{"INSTALLATION" LINK INSTALLATION}\n                      @{" HOW TO USE " LINK HOW2USE}     @{" -CREDITZ!- " LINK GREETINGS}\n\n        aNOTHER tOOL cOMMIN'' fROM tHE "rEAL" (tRSi/X-iNNOVATiON) tEAM\n@endnode\n\n@NODE COPYRIGHT "Copyright-Information of this Production"\n\n     @{u}Copyright@{uu}\n\n   This Program is `FreeWare''.\n\n   It can be freely copied and distributed for non-commercial purposes,\n  provided that no file is added to or removed from the distribution\n  archive and no charge, beside a nominal fee, is requested.\n\n  The whole Copyright is reserved by the Author (myself!), and without\n  written Permission it''s not allowed to distribute this Program in any\n  comercial way.\n\n  This Version is the only one which will be released, all following\n  updates and bugfixings are only available for registered Users. To\n  become registered User, you have to pay a registration Fee (30,- DM / $20).\n\n  You don''t have to pay for every new BBS-Tool I wrote, this Fee has to\n  be paid only one time. To become registered User, call my @{"BBS" LINK ADDY1} and leave\n  a mail to SieGeL/tRSi about a Registration.\n\n  @{"Click here for a list of all available programs written by SieGeL" LINK PRGLIST}\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE DISTRIBUTION "Distribution of this Production"\n\n     @{u}Distribution@{uu}\n\n  It is allowed to put this archive on any PD-Magazine/-Pool (i.e. AMINET),\n  as long as no charge, beside a nominal fee, is requested and no file is\n  added to or removed from the distribution archive.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE INTRODUCTION "Introduction...."\n\n@{u}Introduction@{uu}\n\nThis door is written during the fact that aRTcORE! decided to make my BBS\nto their German Headquarter. To let Users request something, they gave me\nAsciiOrder written by Duplo...well I don''t like this door, coz'' it''s a\nlittle bit to simple....and therefor I decided to write my own aSKII-request\ndoor....it has some nice features, like:\n\n - is able to simulate EALL messages to all painters\n\n - Additional Comment (3 Lines) possible, to give further infos ''bout the\n   request...\n\n - Hole design is freely configurable during external ANSI-Pictures\n\n - Every Painter gets his own Datafile, reg. Users got l8er an Auto-Answer\n   Mode, allowing aSKII-rEQUEST to automatically delete uploaded requests.\n\n - Creates a nice Bulletin about all Requests.\n\n...etc. etc. etc...:) If you need such a program, look in the @{"Installation" LINK INSTALLATION}\nchapter on how to install it...\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE INSTALLATION "How to install it to your BBS-System"\n\n@{u}Installation@{uu}\n\nThis door runs under Fame and Amiex BBS-Systems, but was mainly written for\nusage on Amiex, therefor special functions available under FAME aren''t\nsupported!\n\nThe easiest way for installing is the Usage of the Installer-Script found\nin this archive. This will install aSKII-rEQUEST and all needed files to\nyour system. If you want to install it by hand read now :\n\n@{b}Installation to Amiex@{ub}\n\n1. Copy aSKII-rEQUEST + aSKII-rEQUEST.info to your Doors: directory, I\n   recommend to create an own drawer for this Program, as it creates Data-\n   Files in the Program-Directory!\n\n2. Copy the supplied ''ASCII.INFO'' to your BBS:COMMANDS/BBSCMD/ drawer and\n   adjust the path to the drawer you have put in aSKII-rEQUEST.\n\n3. Now edit the ToolTypes. For more Informations take a look to chapter\n   @{"ToolTypes" LINK TOOLTYPES}.\n\n4. That''s it..:)\n\n\n@{b}Installation to FAME@{ub}\n\n1. Copy aSKII-rEQUEST + aSKII-rEQUEST.info to your FAME:Doors directory, I\n   recommend to create an own drawer for this Program, as it creates Data-\n   Files in the Program-Directory!\n\n2. Start the SystemEditor, go into the Doors-Menu and load in the supplied\n   ANSI Command (aSKII-rEQUEST/FAME/SETTINGS/DOORS/BBSMCMD/ANSI). Adjust\n   the Path to the Drawer where aSKII-reQUEST could be found.\n\n3. Now edit the ToolTypes. For more Informations take a look to chapter\n   @{"ToolTypes" LINK TOOLTYPES}.\n\n4. That''s it..:)\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE TOOLTYPES "Tooltype-Informations for aSKII-rEQUEST"\n\n@{u}ToolTypes@{uu}\n\naSKII-rEQUEST needs some Tooltypes to work correctly. Here''s a list :\n\nSLOT.(x)=<SLOTNR.>    -> Here you define the painters available on your BBS.\n                         You have to define here the Slot-Numbers to allow\n                         aSKII-rEQUEST to write to the correct persons.\n                         You need at least ONE painter to let the prg working.\n                         Of course you could have as many painters as you like.\n\n                         @{b}Example:@{ub}\n\n                                 SLOT.1=17\n                                 SLOT.2=82\n                                 SLOT.3=444\n\n\nSHOW_AS.(x)=<STRING>  -> Here you could define alternate Names for the\n                         painters. If you don''t define this Tooltype, the\n                         current Username is used. If you defined it, the\n                         Name you entered here will be displayed when showing\n                         the artists instead of the Painter''s real Username.\n\n                         @{b}Example:@{ub}\n\n                               SHOWN_AS.1=2fAST/aRTCORE\n                               SHOWN_AS.2=sTYLeZ/^nEON^aRTCORE\n                               SHOWN_AS.3=(-rAPiD-)/sCOOPeX^aRTCORE\n\n\nOUTPUT_BULL=<PATH>    -> Here you could enter an alternate Path for creating\n                         the Output-Bulletin containing the requests. If this\n                         Tooltype isn''t present, aSKII-rEQUEST uses his own\n                         Path-Location as path, and creates in it a Bull called\n                         ORDER.TXT. If you wish to create it in another path,\n                         you *MUST* enter here a complete path including the\n                         filename, otherwise aSKII-rEQUEST won''t create the\n                         BULL!\n\n                         @{b}Example:@{ub}\n\n                         You don''t defined this Tooltype. aSKII-rEQUEST is\n                         located in DOORS:ASKII-REQUEST/, then the Bull will\n                         be created in ''DOORS:ASKII-REQUEST/ORDER.TXT'' .\n\nCurrently no more Tooltypes available, but for registered Users will be a\nmajor update in the next month...so get registered!\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE HOW2USE "How to use this Program"\n\n@{u}How it works@{uu}\n\nTo allow Sysops to design this Door to their own needings, I have decided to\nread in all screens from HD...so if you want to change the Style of this \nDoor, simply edit the following files found in the drawer of aSKII-rEQUEST:\n\n        ASKII-MAIN.TXT     --> ANSI for MainMenu\n        ASKII-ENTER.TXT    --> ANSI for Menu ENTER REQUESTS\n        ASKII-LIST.TXT     --> ANSI for Menu SHOW ARTISTS\n        ASKII-DELETE.TXT   --> ANSI for Menu DELETE REQUESTS\n\nIncluded in this archive are the Ansis painted by sTYLeZ of da famous \naRT-cORE! posse...i think everyone will love them..:) You could of course\nalternately use this door without any ANSI-Pictures, but who wants this..:)\n\n@{u}Main-Usage of aSKII-rEQUEST@{uu}\n\nWhen starting aSKII-rEQUEST, you have the following choices :\n\n                    @{" 1 " LINK HELP_1} ->  rEQUEST aN aSCII\n                    @{" 2 " LINK HELP_2} ->  deLETE rEQUESTS\n                    @{" 3 " LINK HELP_3} ->  vIEW rEQUESTS\n                    @{" 4 " LINK HELP_4} ->  sHOW aRTISTS\n                    @{" 5 " LINK HELP_5} ->  qUIT pROGRAM\n\nClick on number (1-5) you want more informations about...\n\nThe Output-Bulletin will be created each time the user exits the program.\nSo if you want to see the Bull, simply start and exit immediatly the door ;)\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE HELP_1 "Help on ''REQUEST AN ASCII''"\n\n@{u}REQUEST AN ASCII@{uu}\n\nHere you request ansis..:) when selected, you were first prompted if you want\nto write a Pseudo-EALL Message to all available painters. If you answer here\nNo, you could choose the Painter you wish to request something. By pressing\nonly Enter, you got back to the main menu. \nAfter choosing the Painter, you were now asked about the Type of logo you \nwant to request. So you could enter here i.e. DMS-Banner, BBSTitle, etc... \nso the painter sees which type he should paint for you...:) Again only \npressing Enter brings yar back to the main prompt...\nNow you were asked for the Name on the Banner, here you should enter now the\nName you want to have painted...i.e. SieGeL etc..\nAt least, you could enter an additional comment to the painter(s) containing \nmax. 3 lines with 78 chars each line. Only pressing enter exits the comment-\neditor. Of course you could use this Comment-Editor as a real Line-Editor \nwith CRSR-Left/Right support, DEL/BACKSPACe etc...\n\nAfter all parameters are entered, aSKII-rEQUEST displays the complete\nmessage to you and asks you if you really want to save this Message. Select\nNo to abort saving...if you have selected to write to ALL Painters, aSKII-\nrEQUEST will now write a couple number of messages, depending on how many\npainters are available. After successful saving, you will kicked back to\nmain menu.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE HELP_2 "Help on ''DELETE REQUESTS''"\n\n@{u}DELETE REQUESTS@{uu}\n\nThis Menu-Entry is only accessable for the Sysop and the Painters defined\nin the aSKII-rEQUEST.info. Here you could delete old requests. For registered\nUsers a new tool will be written, which deletes requests automatically. In\nthis FreeVersion all painters have to delete their Requests for themself.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE HELP_3 "Help on ''VIEW REQUESTS''"\n\n@{u}VIEW REQUESTS@{uu}\n\nWith this point you could take a look to all available requests. When \nselecting this point, you where asked if you want to view the Requests from\nALL painters or from a single Painter. Depending on your choice you see the\nrequests.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE HELP_4 "Help on ''SHOW ARTISTS''"\n\n@{u}SHOW ARTISTS@{uu}\n\nThis point allows you to see which painters are available on this BBS. I \nthink nothing more has to say about this point I think.......\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE HELP_5 "Help on ''QUIT PROGRAM''"\n\n@{u}QUIT PROGRAM@{uu}\n\nThis exits aSKII-rEQUEST.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GREETINGS "Da famous Greetings...what else :)"\n\nGreetings fly to :\n\naRGON/PDY       - for having now 336oo BPS Connects :(\nsTYLEZ/aC!      - for painting me the Pictures for this Door\n(-rAPiD-)/aC!   - for giving me the Idea to do this Door\n2fAST/aC!       - fOR painting me such nice cewl pictures\nmOGUE!/aC!      - I''m sorry that you leave the scene...suxx man!\nByteAndi/tRSi   - fOR his GREAT Edit-Routine...\nsPY/tRSi        - hope you run FAME sometime.:)\nsTRIDER/sDC     - tHE bEST BBS iS FAME, nothing else.......\nfLASHBACK!/SCX  - fOR the nice chat last time :) Hope to hear from U..\nbYSiS/iNDY      - Yeah, cODIN'' iS thE BEST, you will get them all...:)\nBloodRock/sDC   - full-chat roolez oldae ;)\ndEATH aNGEL/sDC - for beeing such a nice Beta-Tester & Friend\nBeatnik/sDC     - v34 roolez oda ?\n\nand all others I''ve forgot to list here...take it easy & don''t worry :-)\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PRGLIST "List of all Programs written by SieGeL/tRSi"\n\n@{u}Program-List@{uu}\n\nTo give you an overview what you got if you are registered user, here''s a\nlist of all my programs I have made until now...\n\n@{b}Currently available for reg. Users:@{ub}\n\nCD-Server V1.00     - CD-Server for @{"FAME" LINK FAME}/AMIEX\nwORLD-cLOCK V1.18   - Great Worldtime-Door for @{"FAME" LINK FAME}/AMIEX\nmEGA-vIEW V2.08+    - Best TXT-Viewer ever written for @{"FAME" LINK FAME}/AMIEX\nlASTCALLERS V0.051  - Lastcaller-Util for @{"FAME" LINK FAME}, faster than SAMILOG!\nsOFT-dEL V1.01      - Fast Online-Softdeleter for @{"FAME" LINK FAME} & AMIEX\nU-sTAT V1.31        - User-Statistics Door, freely configurable (@{"FAME" LINK FAME} & /X)\nASKII-REQUEST V1.00 - Very cewl askii-requester @{"FAME" LINK FAME}/AMIEX\n\n@{b}Still in work or needs to be updated:@{ub}\n\nPage-Master V0.05   - A CEWL Page-Door for @{"FAME" LINK FAME} with Gadtools-driven Window\noRDER V.02          - Door for Ordering sites, i.e. sell hardware via BBS..\nBBS-VIEW V1.1       - CLI-Util for displaying ANSI-Pics, 100% ASM!\nU-Convert V0.3      - CLI-Util to convert /X user.data -> @{"FAME" LINK FAME} user.data\nBullcreator V1.0    - Highscore-Util for ByteKiller V1.0, will be updated\n\nI think 30,- DM (btw. $20) is not too much for such a list, eh ? And of\ncourse,if possible, I try to realize all your wishes/needs for any problem\nyou have with this doors...To get in contact, take a look to Chapter @{"BBS" LINK ADDY1}.\n@endnode\n\n@node FAME "WHAT THE HELL IS FAME ?????"\n\n@{u}Some informations about FAME@{uu}\n\nWhat is FAME, you may ask. FAME is a new BBS-System written by Strider of\nSyndicate, which is about 90% compatible to Amiex-Doors, but has also an\nown Message-Port to use more than 1000 (!) commands. The whole BBS is\ncompletly hardware-depend, meaning that the only limit this system has is\nyour computer-equipment !\nThe configuration and the control of the BBS is realized with a System-Editor\n(fully Gadtoolsdriven, NO ICONS ANYMORE!), and a very comfortable Server\n(Commodity- & Gadtools-driven).\n\nDuring the fact that this BBS is currently in Beta-Stage, it''s not avail-\nable until now, but if you want more informations, contact us and we will\ngive you all informations needed.\n@endnode\n\n@node ADDY1 "(tRSi/X-iNNOVATiON) WHQ & Beta Site"\n\n@{APEN 2}                           hOW tO cONTACT uS : @{aPEN 1}\n\n   _____________  __________               /\\\n  |     __     /__\\__      /___________   /  \\             _____\n  |   ________/    /      /_\\____      \\_//   \\___________|_____|_______\n  |     |  \\      /      /      /      _//     \\    ______________      \\_\n  l_____|   \\___________/______/       \\_______/\\______   \\_    l/       /\n                              \\________/      /____________/____/       /\n                                       _________________       \\_______/\n     ______ /\\____ ____________ _______\\______   ______/\n    /      /_      \\    __    /_\\_____      \\_    |\n  _/      \\/______/   _______/\\      /       /    |    · PUN¡sHMeNT ¡NC. ·\n  \\________\\    _/_____________\\____/  Mo!  /_____|\n                /                  \\_______/\n                                           /\\  ______________  ___________\n     1oo% LeGaL sTUFF oN aM¡Ga^PC         /  \\_\\_______      \\_\\    _____/___\n                                         //   \\       /       /     /       /\n     RUNN¡NG oN a4ooo/4o · V.FasT      _//     \\_____/       /_____________/\n                                       \\________/   \\_______/\n\n TR¡sTaR & ReD seCToR ¡NC. (/X·¡NNoVaT¡oN) WHQ, aRTcORE! GHQ & eTH¡C D¡sT s¡Te\n\n   [> +49-(o)-3o-694-84-7o <]  sYsoP: s¡eGeL/TRs¡  [> +49-(o)-3o-694-sOON! <]\n\n                     @{"> pARALYSIS BBS - dISTRIBUTION sITE <" LINK ADDY2}\n@endnode\n\n@node ADDY2 "(tRSi/X-iNNOVATiON) bETA & dIST SITE"\n       ____\n    ___\\  /______________________________________________________________\n   /   \\\\//                                                              \\\n  /     \\/ -[ THe BeST eQUiPPeD PuBLIC DoMAIN BoaRD IN BeRLIN ]-          \\\n /   -[ WiTH 4 GReaT U.S.ROBOTICS V.FAST CLASS MoDeMS WiTH FLaSH-RoMS ]-   \\\n/                                                                           \\\n\\                        -- -[ SYNDIC/\\TE WHQ ]- --                         /\n \\   _____  _____    _____   _____  __      ___ __  _____   ___ _____      /\n  \\ /  _  \\/  _  \\  /  _  \\ /  _  \\/  |___ /   |  \\/   __)_/ __|   __)_   /\n   /   |   \\  _   \\/   |  //   _   \\  |   \\\\_____  \\___    \\¯  |___    \\ /\n  /   _____/  |    \\_ __   \\_  |    \\ |    \\   |    \\|      \\  | |    