his is .REALLY. a must for every Boardsystems!! so their users can\n   see what doors they can use!\n   Off course with seperate menus for SYSOPs and normal Users!!!\n\n. [ Requirements: ] . \n---------------------\n\n   All what you need is any Model of an Amiga OS2.0 or higher!\n   AmiExpress 2.xx - 3.xx\n   Thats all folks....\n\n. [ INSTALLATION ] .\n--------------------\n   Copy the files in the archive to your directories,\n   they are :                                        \n                                                  \n   BBS:Doors/ShowDoors/ShowDoors.XiM\n   BBS:Doors/ShowDoors/SysopMenu.txt              \n   BBS:Doors/ShowDoors/UserMenu.txt\n   BBS:Doors/ShowDoors/ShowDoors.txt\n   LIBS:AEDoor.library ( © Sintax/WOT )\n\n\n   All Users under SecLevel=250 will see the UserDoors.txt and of course\n   the Rest (over 250) will see the SysopDoors.txt!\n   thats it..... have fun!!!\n\n. [HISTORY: ] .\n---------------\n                     V0.1    -  First release\n                     V0.2    -  Some Bug removed\n                     V0.3    -  New feature implanted\n                                (Users over 250 can select between\n                                 UserMenu and SysopMenu)\n. [Other RELEASES] .\n--------------------\n                     Security Guide v0.1\n\n. [ Thx to: ] .\n---------------\n           DJAX/Sigma7 for some rumour Reports and for Beta testing\n\n. [ Greetings: ] .\n------------------\n           Djax - Rico - DreamWarrior - Tekkno - Saito - Samir - McLoud \n         Dr.Dre - Prayer - Lion - PeeWee - Blitter - Steve - RasterBlaster \n                           - AND ALL TRSI Members -\n  \n. [ Last words: ] .\n-------------------\n\n        for a registered version of my doors call +43 512 365302!!\n\n --[·»«·-[·tRISTAr & rEd^sECTOr iNc.·]-·»«·]::[·»»««·-[---------------------\n\n          __________        __ __     ___________    __    /\__\n          \   __    \      /  |  \   |  /  __    \  /  \  //  /\n\ s¡g/X\a  \_/  \_  \\    //     \\  |\/  | //   / //   \//  /    aHQ    /\n:\   7      //  | \  \\  //   :   \\ |  __://   ( // ___/   (           /:\n::\    /\_ //   |  \  \\//  __|_ _ \\:  \___    \\_  \____   \_ _/\    /::\n:::\  /::::\\   |__/   \\   \_ _    \\    |:\\_   /    /\    //::::\  /:::\n::::\/::::::\___________/_____|_______)___|::\_\//____/::\_ //::::::\/::::\n:::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\/::::::::::\/:::::::::::::\n::::::___:::___::::::___:::::__:__:::::_________:::::::::::::__:::__::::::\n\::::|\ /|:|\  |::::|\  |:::/  |  \:::/   __   /:/\:::_/\:::|  \ |  |:::::\n \:::| Y |:| \/|/\::| \/|/\/   :  \\::\\    \//:_\/::/\  \::||  \| ||::::/\n  \::| : |:|   : \\:|   : \\   |   \\::\\   \\:|  /|// \ \\:|:   \ :|:::/ \n   \:| . |:|   .  \\:   .  \\  l    \\:/\    \\:\/ |/ / \ \\:. \   .|::/  \n     |   | |        \        \        // \__   \   |  \_/   \  |\   |[CTX]\n     |__ | |_______ /_______ /________\ :______/___|_______ /__| \  |     \n        Y          Y        Y          \!                  Y      \ |     \n        :          :        :           :    s¡G/X\a 7 aHQ :       \|\n        .    _    _._ ___   :___  ___  ___  ___  ____  ___ .        !\n        : __//_  //// _//   ._// //__ //_   _// // // __// :        :\n        :  //     //__// ø __// //_// __//__// //_// //__  | :      .\n        |                                                · :_.      \n        |                sYsOp: CøRteX/tRS¿              :_:/       :\n        |          cOsYsOpS: FeLoN - DJAX/sIgMa 7         \/        .\n        | ·                                                |        °\n      · :_:· rUnNiNg oN A1200 - 68882/33Mhz with /X v3.X   |\n      :/\_\:        24h a DaY - keWl Ansi Dezigns          |  _/\_\n       \/_/ __ _______________________________________ __  |  \__/\n        |                                                  |  (__)\n        :         aMiGa - /X sUpPoRt - mUzAx - aSm         :    \n    - --+--------------------------------------------------+-- -\n        .                                                  . \n\n--[·»«·-[·tRISTAr & rEd^sECTOr iNc.·]-·»«·]::[·»»««·-[---------------------\n\n\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',20215,4,0,NULL,NULL,'trsi_sd3','scan',1780048798);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('trsi_sdl','TRSI_SDL.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/TRSI_SDL.LHA','SysOpDL','XIM','SysOpDL',NULL,'SieGeL/tRSi','TRSI','\    ____    )  /___/\_| & rED sECTOR ¡NC | .-\___\ | \___\__   /   |  /X-¡NNOVATION   | `---|___|___|______/____|---[ PRESENTS ]---''',replace(' _____________ ___Mo! __.<---[ tRISTAR ]---.\n \    ____    )  /___/\_| & rED sECTOR ¡NC |\n.-\___\ | \___\__   /   |  /X-¡NNOVATION   |\n`---|___|___|______/____|---[ PRESENTS ]---''\n    SysOp-Download V1.33p by SieGeL/tRSi\n.------------------------------------------.\n|   rEMAKE oF tHE oRIGINAL fROM bYTEANDI   |\n| sUPPORTS fULL CRSR-kEY cONTROL, tAB-kEY, |\n|     hYDRA, lHA, lZX & zIP sUPPORTED      |\n| iNSTALLERSCRIPT iNCLUDED, cHECK iT oUT ! |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'SysOpDL.guide',replace('@database SysOpDL.guide\n@$VER: 1.0\n@author "SieGeL/tRSi ([email removed])"\n@(c) "(tRSi/X-iNNOVATiON)"\n@index HeddleyAutoIndex\n@remark Created with Heddley v1.1 (c) Edd Dumbill 1994\n\n@node "Main" "English documentation for SysOp-DownLoad"\n     @{b}@{fg shine} ............................... ...............................\n     :::::::::: ...........:::::::::'' `:::::::::..........  ..........\n     :::::::::: :::::::::: :::::::::: .......... :::::::::: ::::::::::\n     :::::::::: :::::::::: :::::::::: ::::::::::.:::::::::'' ::::::::::@{ub}@{fg text}\n    @{b}--[@{ub} Mo! @{b}]--------.----@{ub} @{b}@{fg shine}::::::::::@{ub}@{fg text} @{b}---------------------@{ub} @{b}@{fg shine}::::::::::@{ub}@{fg text} @{b}--.@{ub}\n                     @{b}|@{ub}                  ( /X·INNOVATION )                @{b}|@{ub}\n                     @{b}`---------------------------------------------------''@{ub}\n\n                             pROUDLY pRESENTS:\n\n             SysOp-Download V1.33 by SieGeL (tRSi/X-iNNOVATiON)\n\n                  DS Replacement for FAME & Amiex Systems\n\n                    @{" · " link "FEATURES" 0} Introduction & Features of this Tool\n                    @{" · " link "AUTHOR" 0} Distribution & Technical informations\n                    @{" · " link "REGISTER" 0} Registration of Tools/Doors\n                    @{" · " link "INSTALLATION" 0} Installation of SysOp-Download\n                    @{" · " link "TOOLTYPES" 0} ToolType-informations\n                    @{" · " link "USAGE" 0} How to use SysOp-Download\n                    @{" · " link "CREDITZ" 0} Credits & Copyright Notes\n                    @{" · " link "TRSI" 0} (tRSi/X-/F-/T-iNNOVATiON)\n                    @{" · " link "GREETINGS" 0} The famous Greetings\n\n          aNOTHER tOOL cOMMIN'' fROM tHE rEAL (tRSi/X-iNNOVATiON)\n@endnode\n\n@node "FEATURES" "Introduction and Features"\n@{b}INTRODUCTION@{ub}\n\n Some people knows the good old SysopDownload from @{"ByteAndi/tRSi" link "TRSI" 0}, which was\n released a long time ago...personally i think that this was the best DS\n Replacement ever written for Amiex-Systems, but it has some disadvantages\n I don''t like very much, like the Problems with Hydra, hardcoded archive-\n names, missing CRSR-Key Support etc. The biggest problem was the fact that\n ByteAndi looses all his sources during a Bust of his BBS, so there was no\n chance to update the old sourcecode. Anyway, I want an update, so I asked\n Byti if I could write a new DS Door with all new enhancements a door should\n have now...he agrees and I made this new Update of SysOp-Download with the\n following features:\n\n@{b}FEATURES@{ub}\n\n @{b}·@{ub} Uses only @{b}AmigaDOS@{ub} routines instead of ANSI-C, makes it very faast!\n\n @{b}·@{ub} Supports @{b}LZX@{ub}, @{b}LHA@{ub} & @{b}ZIP@{ub} for packing files/directories.\n\n @{b}·@{ub} @{b}CRSR-Keys controlled Line-Edit prompt@{ub}, allowing you to edit the whole\n   path without typing anytime the same. Also @{b}CTRL-X@{ub} to kill the line is\n   supported, @{b}TAB-Key@{ub} for Pathname-Completition etc. For a complete\n   overview take a look to Chapter @{"Usage of SysOp-Download" link "USAGE" 0}.\n\n @{b}·@{ub} @{b}Integrated History-buffer@{ub}, which buffers up to 20 entries, so you could\n   easily repeat the last command by using @{b}CRSR-UP/DOWN@{ub}.\n\n @{b}·@{ub} Supports @{b}all AmigaDOS Wildcards and Patterns@{ub}, also an @{b}Device-Detection@{ub}\n   is built in, so it''s impossible that an user could flag i.e. DH0: , but\n   he could flag C: for example! SysOp-Download is able to detect assigns\n   and devices automatically.\n\n @{b}·@{ub} Flaglist is only limited by your Memory, not any longer by the door !\n   Also all Error-Requesters are disabled for more security.\n\n @{b}·@{ub} @{b}Archivename@{ub} is now @{b}freely selectable@{ub}!! After packing, you could choose\n   your own filename for this archive.\n\n @{b}·@{ub} @{b}Correct BatchDownloading@{ub}. If you select many files at once and don''t\n   pack them, SysOp-Download sends all files at once, not any longer in\n   the way: Send File, close ZModem-Requester, send next file, etc. Also the\n   @{b}Hydra@{ub} Transfer works now perfect!\n@endnode\n\n@node "AUTHOR" "Author & technical Informations"\n@{b}DISTRIBUTION:@{ub}\n\n Following notice applies to product called "SysOpDownload" and everything \n in its original distribution archive.\n\n * Program is published by SieGeL/tRSi under concept of @{"RegisterWare" link "REGISTER" 0}.\n   No warranties are given. I take no responsibility of any possible\n   harm this product could do to your amiga system (not that it would but..).\n\n * You may NOT sell this product without permission from me.\n\n * Program must not be altered in any way.\n\n * Package must always be kept intact when spreading.\n\n * It is OK to include this on CD-ROM & disk collections and distribute\n   it through aminet and other such ftp''s and file nets.\n\n Above mentioned rules apply to SysOpDownload and other texts/libraries\n within the original package versions 1.33 and newer unless otherwise stated.\n\n@{b}TECHNICAL INFORMATION:@{ub}\n\n @{b}Program:@{ub}       SysOp-Download Door for FAME & Amiex Systems.\n @{b}Version:@{ub}       V1.33 \n @{b}Released:@{ub}      09-18-95\n @{b}Written by:@{ub}    SieGeL/tRSi\n @{b}Machine used:@{ub}  A4ooo, 68o4o/4o, 14MB,AmigaOS 3.1\n @{b}Required:@{ub}      AmigaDOS 2.o or above, installed Amiex or FAME BBS,\n                PIPE: already mounted.\n @{b}Special Note:@{ub}  Original Program by ByteAndi/tRSi,completly new coded and \n                enhanced by SieGeL/tRSi. I rewrote this Tool from ByteAndi\n                during the fact that the original program had the big\n                disadvantage that it won''t support Hydra, was very slow etc.\n                In this new Version, Hydra will be no longer any problem and\n                the speed is the same like any other Tool with Pathname-\n                completition.\n@endnode\n\n@node "REGISTER" "Registration of Tools/Doors"\n@{b}REGISTER DOORS/TOOLS@{ub}\n\n All tools I''ve made in the past are released under the @{b}RegisterWare@{ub} concept.\n This means, that I release all my doors only one time as full working Public\n Versions, all updates/bugfixings are only available for registered Users.\n\n The Registration costs @{b}30.- DM@{ub} and has to be paid only @{b}*ONE*@{ub} time for @{b}*ALL*@{ub} \n bbs-doors I have made until now. Of course all new doors are included in \n this registration fee, too.\n\n To become registered user, contact one of the following Boards and leave a\n mail to SieGeL/tRSi about Registration:\n\n @{b}pUNISHMENT iNC:@{ub} +49(0) 30 694 8470\n                 +49(0) 30 694 8570\n\n @{b}Paralysis:@{ub}      +49(0) 30 721 6071\n                 +49(0) 30 721 6072\n                 +49(0) 30 721 6073\n                 +49(0) 30 721 6065\n\n @{b}Spirit of Soul:@{ub} Absolute Private\n\n              @{fg shine}These Boards are supporting only 100% Public Domain.@{fg text}\n\n       You could also use E-Mail to contact me: [email removed]\n@endnode\n\n@node "INSTALLATION" "Installation of SysOp-DL"\n@{b}INSTALLATION@{ub}\n\n Just click on the supplied Install Icon to Install SysOp-Download via the\n Installer. This script will set everything for you including the Tooltypes.\n\n If you want to install it by yourself, follow these steps:\n\n 1. Copy the SysOpDL/ Drawer to your DOORS: drawer or wherever you have\n    stored your BBS-Tools.\n\n 2. Edit the ToolTypes from the SysOp-Download Icon to your needs.\n\n 3. Depending on your BBS-System follow this step now:\n\n    @{u}For AMIEX-Users:@{uu}\n\n    Copy the Icon @{b}COMMANDS/BBSCMD/DS.INFO@{ub} to your @{b}BBS:COMMANDS/BBSCMD/@{ub}\n    drawer and adjust (if needed) the @{b}LOCATION@{ub} Tooltype to the path\n    were SysOp-Download could be found.\n\n    -------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    @{u}For FAME-Users:@{uu}\n\n    Copy the Door-Definition from @{b}SETTINGS/DOORS/BBSCMD/DS@{ub} to your\n    @{b}FAME:SETTINGS/DOORS/BBSCMD/@{ub} drawer. Now start SystemEditor, load in\n    the BBSCMD "@{b}DS@{ub}" and adjust the path to SysOp-Download. Don''t forget\n    to save back the definition!\n\n 4. If you have installed SysOp-Download with the Installer-Script, you\n    should now read the Chapter @{"Usage of SysOp-Download" link "USAGE" 0}, all others should\n    take a look to the @{"ToolTypes" link "TOOLTYPES" 0} to setup the Program correctly!\n@endnode\n\n@node "TOOLTYPES" "All Tooltypes from SysOp-DL"\n @{b}ALL TOOLTYPE-INFORMATIONS@{ub}\n\nNow following a list of all currently supported Tooltypes:\n\n  @{fg shine}TOOLTYPE:@{fg text} @{b}|@{ub}@{fg shine} DESCRIPTION:@{fg text} \n @{b}-----------+---------------------------------------------------------------@{ub}\n PASSWORD   @{b}|@{ub} This is the only Tooltype which is absolutly needed for\n            @{b}|@{ub} SysOp-Download. If you don''t specify it, it won''t work ! Enter\n            @{b}|@{ub} here a Password (max. 40 Chars, not case-sensitive!) which\n            @{b}|@{ub} will be used as Securitycheck every time the Door starts. \n @{b}-----------+---------------------------------------------------------------@{ub} \n TEMP_PATH  @{b}|@{ub} When you plan to use the Pack-Option of SysOpDL, you MUST (!)\n            @{b}|@{ub} enter here a valid ADOS-Path. This path is used to pack all\n            @{b}|@{ub} selected files into an archive  which will be created into\n            @{b}|@{ub} this path, so make sure that enough Bytes are free! If this\n            @{b}|@{ub} Tooltype isn''t present, it''s impossible to download complete\n            @{b}|@{ub} dirs,  as directories are always packed by SysOpDL ! \n @{b}-----------+---------------------------------------------------------------@{ub}\n LHA        @{b}|@{ub} Here you should enter the full path of the packers you want to \n LZX        @{b}|@{ub} use with SysOpDL, i.e. LHA=PACKERS:LHA. If some of this Tool- \n ZIP        @{b}|@{ub} types are not available, the according packers won''t be shown\n            @{b}|@{ub} in the ''Choose-Packer'' List.\n@endnode\n\n@node "USAGE" "How to use SysOp-DL"\n@{b}USAGE OF SYSOP-DOWNLOAD@{ub}\n\n         Please select chapter for which you need more informations:\n\n@{b}FLAGGING:@{ub}\n\n @{" · " link "FLAGFILES" 0} Flagging of files\n @{" · " link "TAB-KEY" 0} File-Completition\n @{" · " link "HELPFILE" 0} Online-Help\n @{" · " link "RESTRICTIONS" 0} Restrictions\n\n@{b}FLAG-MENU:@{ub}\n\n @{" · " link "PACKING" 0} Packing\n @{" · " link "DOWNLOADING" 0} Downloading\n @{" · " link "SHOW_FLAGS" 0} Show flagged files\n @{" · " link "HELPFILE" 0} Online-Help\n @{" · " link "QUIT" 0} Quit\n@endnode\n\n@node "FLAGFILES" "Flagging files with SysOp-Download"\n@{b}FLAGGING OF FILES@{ub}\n\n When you are in the flagging Prompt, you could enter here the pathnames of\n the files you want to flag for downloading. Also inside this prompt some\n special Keyshortcuts are available:\n\n       ?         -> Display the external @{"Helpfile" link "HELPFILE" 0}.\n      TAB        -> Allows @{"Pathname-Completition" link "TAB-KEY" 0}.\n    CTRL-X       -> Clear whole line.\n  CRSR UP/DOWN   -> Forward/Backward scrolling through the History-Buffer.\n CRSR LEFT/RIGHT -> One char left/right allowing you to edit the line.\n     ENTER       -> Switch to @{"Flagmenu" link "Flagmenu" 0}.\n\n When flagging files, you could also use @{b}ALL@{ub} valid AmigaDOS patterns to find\n the files, but it''s not allowed to flag patterns! So if you enter i.e.\n @{b}dh0:c/pic*@{ub} and simply press return, it won''t work ! But if you press first\n @{"TAB" link "TAB-KEY" 0} to complete this pattern and after this press Return, it will work :)\n\n Flagging of dirs is also possible, but SysOp-Download takes care about\n Devices, and if found one, won''t flag it, i.e. an user flags the device:\n\n                                   @{b}DH0:@{ub}\n\n and enters return, the screen flashes and the flagging won''t be made! \n But of course you could enter i.e.\n\n                        @{b}DH0:DEVS/MONITORS/ or DEVS:@{ub}\n\n to flag the whole dir. As you can see, it''s allowed to flag @{b}ASSIGNS@{ub} only !\n SysOp-Download takes care about this difference, of course the device\n "@{b}SYS:@{ub}" is also disabled. See chapter @{"Restrictions" link "RESTRICTIONS" 0} for a complete list of\n all restrictions. As a special security, SysOp-Download will expand the\n path from assigns to their real path, i.e. the logical assign ''C:'' may be\n expanded to ''Workbench:C''. This was neccessary in fact of a bug in the\n Evulation Version of LZX V1.20, which always append an Slash (/) to every \n path,no matter if this pathname ends with a double-quote (:) or a slash!\n So if you flagged i.e. ENV: and decides to pack with LZX, it will result in\n packing first ENV:/ (on my configuration in RAM:) and then all files found\n in ENV: ! In fact of expanding the files you could be sure that everything\n will be packed correctly.\n\n When you flag directories/assigns, it results in packing first all entries\n before downloading them! See chapter @{"Packing" link "PACKING" 0} for more informations.\n This step had to be done because directories could grow in their size \n extremly and to avoid problems, all directories would be packed.\n If the SysOp decides to disable the Packing-Procedure, you where not able\n to download Directories ! So I recommend to supply at least one packer to\n support this feature of SysOp-Download.\n\n All files that should be flagged are also checked for the Restricted File-\n comment and if found, won''t flag those files.\n\n When you flag files, which are already found in the Flaglist, those files\n were skipped. You could see this if the Number of flagged files won''t grow.\n@endnode\n\n@node "TAB-KEY" "Tab-Key Support from SysOp-Download"\n@{b}USING THE PATHNAME-COMPLETITION VIA THE TAB-KEY@{ub}\n\n The Pathname-Completition is 100% the same like the wellknown @{"C-Shell" link "CREDITZ" 0}, but\n it handles the scanning a little bit different from other programs which\n support Path-completition. So it''s possible to expand Wildcards to whole \n pathes, i.e. the following Wildcard:\n\n             @{fg fill}dh0:*/*/*/*/*@{fg text}\n\n could be expanded i.e. to:\n\n             @{fg fill}dh0:Tools/Monitor-Tuning/MonEd3a/thinpaz/8@{fg text}\n\n or something similar found on your HD :) Check out the speed SysOp-DL found\n this pattern vs. C-Shell, and you will notice an increadible difference!\n\n You could of course write down only a part of a file and let SysOp-DL\n complete the path. If a path won''t be completed, it won''t exist or is marked\n as @{"restricted" link "RESTRICTIONS" 0} File/Dir ! If this happens, a screenflash appears to inform\n you about the failure.\n\n The length of the Pathes is currently limited to ca. @{b}70 chars@{ub}, that should\n be enough. If not, please @{"register" link "REGISTER" 0} and you will get more chars to enter! If\n the selected path is longer than the max. amount of chars, it won''t be\n completed via TAB-Key!\n\n All unknown devices (i.e. SIEGEL:) were skipped and answered with a Screen-\n flashing. This means, that @{b}ALL@{ub} AmigaDOS-Requesters are disabled, so it''s\n not possible to hang up a node by typing the wrong device etc.\n@endnode\n\n@node "HELPFILE" "Online-Help from SysOp-Download"\n@{b}THE ONLINE-HELP@{ub}\n\n The Online-Help could be found in the Program-Dir of SysOpDL and is called\n ''@{b}SysOpDL.hlp@{ub}''. You may change this file to your own needs, it is not \n neccessary to install it, but if you want online-help, you should install\n it or create your own help-file.\n\n Here is an ASCII Output of the Help-File:\n\n @{fg fill}-------------------------------[CUT HERE]-----------------------------------@{fg text}\n\n                      Sysop-Download - Online Help\n                      ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n (P)ack........Pack flagged files with your favourite packer and dl'' them\n (D)ownload....Download all flagged files without packing (NO DIRS/ASSIGNS!)\n (S)how Flags..Show all currently flagged files \n (?) Show Help.Display this Page here \n (Q)uit........Exits Sysop-Download\n\n ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n NOTES: If you are in Flag-Mode, you could use the TAB-Key for pathname-\n        completition, the CRSR-Keys left/right to edit the line, CRSR-Up and\n        down for History-Buffer-Usage and wildcards are also supported. When\n        you flag Assigns or dirs, Sysop-Download expands them to the complete\n        pathname to avoid problems with the packers! Also the Packoption is\n        turned on, as it makes no sense to download dirs without packing them\n        first!\n ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n @{fg fill}-------------------------------[CUT HERE]-----------------------------------@{fg text}\n\n This file is only an example, you could of course paint your own one..:)\n@endnode\n\n@node "RESTRICTIONS" "What''s allowed and what''s forbidden..."\n@{b}RESTRICTIONS WHEN USING SYSOP-DOWNLOAD@{ub}\n\n During the flagging of files, there are some restrictions on which SysOpDL\n keeps an eye to avoid "problems"...here''s a list of all restrictions from\n SysOpDL:\n\n · Checks out the Device-List if you enter i.e. an assign. If this assign\n   is locked as Device, you are not able to flag this! Also the Devicename\n   "SYS:" is forbidden.\n\n · Checks the FileComment for restricted Files, and if found, won''t complete\n   the filename or flag it.\n\n · Checks if given Filename contains AmigaDOS patterns. If found some, skips\n   the flagging. So please use always @{b}FULL@{ub} filenames/pathes. This should be\n   no problem when using the @{"TAB-Key" link "TAB-KEY" 0}.\n\n · Flagging Directories/Assigns results in @{"Packing" link "PACKING" 0} the Files before down-\n   loading them.\n\n · Double Filenames are skipped, i.e. you''ve flagged "ARQ" and after some\n   files again "ARQ", it won''t be copied to the flaglist anymore!\n\n\n This methods should give enough security I think...if you need more, feel\n free to @{"register" link "REGISTER" 0} yourself and you''ve got your additional security-checks\n ASAP!\n@endnode\n\n@node "Flagmenu" "Flagmenu of SysOp-Download"\n@{b}THE FLAGMENU@{ub}\n\n This menu appears if you press ENTER only in the Fileprompt. The following\n menu would be displayed:\n\n (@{"P" link "PACKING" 0})ack, (@{"D" link "DOWNLOADING" 0})ownload, (@{"S" link "SHOW_FLAGS" 0})how Flags, (@{"?" link "HELPFILE" 0})=Display Online Help, (@{"Q" link "QUIT" 0})uit Program\n\n Select the desired menuentry or @{"CLICK HERE" link "Main" 0} to go to main menu section.\n@endnode\n\n@node "PACKING" "Packing Support from SysOp-Download"\n@{b}PACKING OF FILES@{ub}\n\n Here you could pack your files before @{"downloading" link "DOWNLOADING" 0} them. To let this work,\n you must supply at least one of the Packer-Tooltypes. All packers, for which\n @{"Tooltypes" link "TOOLTYPES" 0} exists, where shown and you could choose which one should be used.\n The packing works in "Realtime", meaning that you could view the whole\n packing process directly.\n\n After packing, you where prompted for a filename to use for downloading.\n The default filename is SysOpDL<node>.<packer>. If you want to abort the\n downloading, simply delete the line and press enter, this aborts and exits\n SysOp-Download without downloading.\n\n @{u}NOTE:@{uu} Of course you have the same options to edit the line like in the\n       Fileflagging prompt, but of course the @{"TAB-Key" link "TAB-KEY" 0} is disabled :)\n\n @{fg fill}If you''ve flagged directories/assigns, you MUST pack the files before down-\n loading them, otherwise it''s not possible to download the flagged list!@{fg text}\n\n After downloading, SysOp-Download writes a comment in the node callerslog \n and exits.\n@endnode\n\n@node "DOWNLOADING" "Downloading of Files..."\n@{b}DOWNLOADING ALL FLAGGED FILES@{ub}\n\n When you''ve selected this option, SysOp-Download starts with the BatchDown-\n load procedure. After downloading the files, SysOp-Download writes a comment\n in node''s callerslog and exists.\n\n @{u}NOTE:@{uu} It''s not possible to download directories/assigns, without packing\n       them first!!! So if you have flagged directories and press ''D'' for\n       downloading, SysOp-Download will first pack your files before sending\n       them to you!\n@endnode\n\n@node "SHOW_FLAGS" "Show flagged files..."\n@{b}SHOW FLAGGED FILES@{ub}\n\n This gives you an overview of all currently flagged files. The output looks\n like :\n\n\n  001 BarClock                                                     6364 Bytes\n  002 BarClock.info                                                1751 Bytes\n  003 Workbench:C                                                  Directory\n  004 MagicSelector.info                                           1581 Bytes\n  005 devs:MountList.ParNET.Client                                 446 Bytes\n  006 ram:T                                                        Directory\n  ...\n  ...\n  ...\n\n If you have no files flagged, an information text appears and you return\n to @{"Flag Menu" link "Flagmenu" 0}.\n@endnode\n\n@node "QUIT" "Quit SysOp-Download"\n@{b}QUIT SYSOP-DOWNLOAD@{ub}\n\nThis exits SysOp-Download...what else...:)\n@endnode\n\n@node "GREETINGS" "The wellknown Greetings :)"\n@{b}THE GREETINGS@{ub}\n\n ByteAndi/tRSi  -  Und gefaellt dir das nu so wie es is oder wat ?\n dR.dRE!/tRSi   -  Ich musste mal deinen Guide-Style klauen, sorry..:)))\n Strider/tRSi   -  Mach hinne mit der FAME, alles schreit danach...\n Bloodrock/tRSi -  Wo zum Teufel bleibt der chat ????????????? :)\n Beatnik/tRSi   -  Und wo bleibt das Join Conference fuer FAME ? :)\n Mario/tRSi     -  Welcome as new Dist Site ! :)\n Argon          -  Nu sollten die Probs mit Hydra wech sein..:)\n dEATH aNGEL    -  Gib dir ALLES beim Testen, nur weiter so!\n\n        ...and of course all my registered users and Beta-Testers...\n@endnode\n\n@node "CREDITZ" "Credits and Copyright Notes"\n@{b}CREDITS AND COPYRIGHT NOTICES@{ub}\n\n@{u}SysopDL v1-v1.20@{uu}   Copyright © & distributed 1991-1994 by Andreas "ByteAndi"\n                   Petermann. All rights reserved.\n\n@{u}SysOpDL v1.30++@{uu}    Copyright © & distributed 1995 by Sascha "SieGeL" Pfalz.\n                   All rights reserved.\n\n@{u}SysOpDL.guide@{uu}      Copyright © & distributed 1995 by Sascha "SieGeL" Pfalz.\n                   written with Heddley V1.18\n\n@{u}SysOpDL.install@{uu}    Copyright © & distributed 1995 by Sascha "SieGeL" Pfalz.\n                   written for Usage with Installer licensed under CBM.\n\n@{u}FAME BBS@{uu}           Copyright © 1993-95 by David "Strider" Wettig.\n                   All rights reserved.\n\n@{u}AMIEX BBS@{uu}          Copyright © 1993-95 by Lightspeed Technologies Inc.\n                   All rights reserved.\n\n@{u}Heddley@{uu}            v1.18 Copyright 1994 Edd Dumbill. All rights reserved.\n\n@{u}AmigaGuide@{uu}         v40.4 (c) Copyright 1991-93 Commodore-Amiga, Inc.\n                   All rights reserved.\n\n@{u}Installer@{uu}          (C) Copyright 1991-93 Commodore-Amiga Inc.\n                   All rights reserved.\n\n@{u}LZX@{uu}                v1.20 Copyright © 1995 Data Compression Technologies.\n                   Evaluation Version. All rights reserved.\n\n@{u}LHA@{uu}                v1.50 Copyright (c) 1991,92 Stefan Boberg.\n\n@{u}ZIP@{uu}                v2.0.1 Copyright (C) 1990-93 Mark Adler, Richard B. Wales,\n                   Jean-loup Gailly, John Bush and Paul Kienitz.\n\n@{u}AMIGA@{uu}              is a registered Trademark of ESCOM AG.\n@endnode\n\n@node "TRSI" "All members of (tRSi/X-iNNOVATiON)"\n\n                    @{fg fill}(tRSi/X-/F-/T-iNNOVATiON) mEMBERS:@{fg text}\n\n                 ByteAndi   <->  AMIEX & FAME Coder, Leader\n                 SieGeL     <->  AMIEX & FAME Coder\n                 Spy        <->  AMIEX Coder\n                 dR.dRE!    <->  AMIEX, FAME & /T\empest Coder\n                 Cørtex     <->  AMIEX Coder\n                 Fuzzy      <->  /T\empest Coder\n                 Beatnik    <->  FAME Coder\n                 Strider    <->  Coder of FAME BBS\n                 Bloodrock  <->  FAME Coder\n\n\n               @{fg fill}You could reach us mainly on these boards:@{fg text}\n\n\n pARALYSIS BBS         GERMAN HQ (SYSOP SPY)        Node 1. +49-30-721 6071\n                                                    Node 2. +49-30-721 6072\n                                                    Node 3. +49-30-721 6073\n                                                    Node 4. +49-30-721 6065\n\n pUNISHMENT iNC.       GERMAN HQ (SYSOP SieGeL)     Node 1. +49-30-694 8470\n                                                    Node 2. +49-30-694 8570\n\n\n sPIRIT oF sOULS       DIST SITE (SYSOP MARIO)      -> ABSOLUTE PRIVATE! <-\n@endnode\n\n@node HeddleyAutoIndex "Index"\n@remark Index auto-generated by Heddley\nIndex of database SysOpDL.guide\n\nDocuments\n\n@{"All members of (tRSi/X-iNNOVATiON)" link "TRSI"}\n@{"All Tooltypes from SysOp-DL" link "TOOLTYPES"}\n@{"Author & technical Informations" link "AUTHOR"}\n@{"Credits and Copyright Notes" link "CREDITZ"}\n@{"Downloading of Files..." link "DOWNLOADING"}\n@{"English documentation for SysOp-DownLoad" link "Main"}\n@{"Flagging files with SysOp-Download" link "FLAGFILES"}\n@{"Flagmenu of SysOp-Download" link "Flagmenu"}\n@{"How to use SysOp-DL" link "USAGE"}\n@{"Installation of SysOp-DL" link "INSTALLATION"}\n@{"Introduction and Features" link "FEATURES"}\n@{"Online-Help from SysOp-Download" link "HELPFILE"}\n@{"Packing Support from SysOp-Download" link "PACKING"}\n@{"Quit SysOp-Download" link "QUIT"}\n@{"Registration of Tools/Doors" link "REGISTER"}\n@{"Show flagged files..." link "SHOW_FLAGS"}\n@{"Tab-Key Support from SysOp-Download" link "TAB-KEY"}\n@{"The wellknown Greetings :)" link "GREETINGS"}\n@{"What''s allowed and what''s forbidden..." link "RESTRICTIONS"}\n\nButtons\n\n@{"?" link "HELPFILE" 0}\n@{"ByteAndi/tRSi" link "TRSI" 0}\n@{"C-Shell" link "CREDITZ" 0}\n@{"CLICK HERE" link "Main" 0}\n@{"D" link "DOWNLOADING" 0}\n@{"downloading" link "DOWNLOADING" 0}\n@{"Flag Menu" link "Flagmenu" 0}\n@{"Flagmenu" link "Flagmenu" 0}\n@{"Helpfile" link "HELPFILE" 0}\n@{"P" link "PACKING" 0}\n@{"Packing" link "PACKING" 0}\n@{"Pathname-Completition" link "TAB-KEY" 0}\n@{"Q" link "QUIT" 0}\n@{"register" link "REGISTER" 0}\n@{"RegisterWare" link "REGISTER" 0}\n@{"restricted" link "RESTRICTIONS" 0}\n@{"Restrictions" link "RESTRICTIONS" 0}\n@{"S" link "SHOW_FLAGS" 0}\n@{"TAB" link "TAB-KEY" 0}\n@{"TAB-Key" link "TAB-KEY" 0}\n@{"ToolTypes" link "TOOLTYPES" 0}\n@{"Usage of SysOp-Download" link "USAGE" 0}\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',32595,2,0,NULL,NULL,'trsi_sdl','scan',1780048806);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('trsi_sg','TRSI-SG.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/TRSI-SG.LHA',NULL,'XIM','_ ___________',NULL,'CøRteX/tRS¿!','TRSI','___________ ___  \_________/\ \  _   _  /  |/  /    ____/  \  /X rulez! / \_/   |_/  _/   \____  \_____)  ________/',replace('    _ ___________              \n___________ ___  \_________/\  \n\  _   _  /  |/  /    ____/  \  /X rulez! / \n \_/   |_/  _/   \____  \_____)  ________/ \nMb/    |____\_____/  /   \   |  / \n (_____|        (________/---'' / presents:\n \n Security Guide v0.1 coded by CøRteX/tRS¿!\n         for Ami or S-Express\n','\n',char(10)),'SecurityGuide.Doc',replace('\n --[·»«·-[·tRISTAr & rEd^sECTOr iNc.·]-·»«·]::[·»»««·-[---------------------\n\n   .  .           .          .                  .           .      .     .\n   :   ______/\___:______/\_____________ /\_________/\______:_/\__ :   * .\n   .   \________________/  \_______    //  \_____________________/   .   :\n   :  :   _/      .   _/     .   | \  /\__ ______      \_   .    \_    .\n      .  \\`      :   \`     :   |  \/  //      |      ''/   :    ''// : . :\n   *  .   \\  _________\  _______|____ //____________  /_______  //\n      .  . \\/____:_____\/___.________\/________.____\/_____:__\// CONtR0L\n   .  .  .  \/    :     \/   :        \/   :    :    \/     :  \/    .\n   .  .  .        .          .             .    .           .      . .   .\n\n --[·»«·-[·tRISTAr & rEd^sECTOr iNc.·]-·»«·]::[·»»««·-[---------------------\n      \n<------------------------------------------------------------------        \n                                    pReSenTs\n        ------------------------------------------------------------------->\n \n                    Security GUIDE v0.1 coded by CøRteX/tRS¿\n                   -========================================-\n\n. [ INTRUDUCTION: ] .\n---------------------\n\n   I have seen many of Security Doors last times but this is one of the\n   BEST and of course one of the FASTEST Security Doors for Ami-Express.\n\n   For some good ideas for another Doors or an registered Version of this\n   Door call my BBS under +43 512 365302. \n\n   But now enjoy this really fine door .... \n\n. [ Requirements: ] . \n---------------------\n\n   All what you need is any Model of an Amiga OS2.0 or higher!\n   AmiExpress 2.xx - 3.xx\n   Thats all folks....\n\n. [ INSTALLATION ] .\n--------------------\n   Copy the files in the archive to your directories,\n   they are :                                        \n                                                  \n   BBS:Doors/SecurityGuide/SGFront.XiM\n   BBS:Doors/SecurityGuide/SGMain.XiM              \n   BBS:Doors/SecurityGuide/SecurityGuide.cfg\n   BBS:Doors/SecurityGuide/SecurityGuide.Doc\n   LIBS:AEDoor.library ( © Sintax/WOT )\n\n   Start the SGfront.Xim door in your Logon.txt or Bull.txt\n\n   Example of an Logon.txt:\n\n------- Cut -------\n\n    ~CC_SGFront\n\n------- Cut -------\n\nExample of an Config File:\n\n  ;Security Guide v0.1 by CøRteX/tRSi!\n#\n250                        ;All Users over this SecLevel would be freezed down\n100                        ;to this SecLevel!!!\n#\nCoRteX                     ;1. (Co)SYSOPS Name\n255                        ;= SecLevel, after he typed in his right Password\npass                       ;password for this (Co)Sysop\n#\nDJAX                       ;2.Sysop\n250                        ;......\nHeidi                      ;.....\n#\nFelon                      :3. ....\n250\nbeer\n##			   ;End Command\n\n\n\n. [HISTORY: ] .\n---------------\n                     V0.1    -  First release\n\n. [ Thx to: ] .\n---------------\n           DJAX/Sigma7 for some rumour Reports and for Beta testing\n\n. [ Greetings: ] .\n------------------\n           Djax - Rico - DreamWarrior - Tekkno - Saito - Samir - McLoud \n         Dr.Dre - Prayer - Lion - PeeWee - Blitter - Steve - RasterBlaster \n                           - AND ALL TRSI Members -\n  \n --[·»«·-[·tRISTAr & rEd^sECTOr iNc.·]-·»«·]::[·»»««·-[---------------------\n\n          __________        __ __     ___________    __    /\__\n          \   __    \      /  |  \   |  /  __    \  /  \  //  /\n\ s¡g/X\a  \_/  \_  \\    //     \\  |\/  | //   / //   \//  /    aHQ    /\n:\   7      //  | \  \\  //   :   \\ |  __://   ( // ___/   (           /:\n::\    /\_ //   |  \  \\//  __|_ _ \\:  \___    \\_  \____   \_ _/\    /::\n:::\  /::::\\   |__/   \\   \_ _    \\    |:\\_   /    /\    //::::\  /:::\n::::\/::::::\___________/_____|_______)___|::\_\//____/::\_ //::::::\/::::\n:::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\/::::::::::\/:::::::::::::\n::::::___:::___::::::___:::::__:__:::::_________:::::::::::::__:::__::::::\n\::::|\ /|:|\  |::::|\  |:::/  |  \:::/   __   /:/\:::_/\:::|  \ |  |:::::\n \:::| Y |:| \/|/\::| \/|/\/   :  \\::\\    \//:_\/::/\  \::||  \| ||::::/\n  \::| : |:|   : \\:|   : \\   |   \\::\\   \\:|  /|// \ \\:|:   \ :|:::/ \n   \:| . |:|   .  \\:   .  \\  l    \\:/\    \\:\/ |/ / \ \\:. \   .|::/  \n     |   | |        \        \        // \__   \   |  \_/   \  |\   |[CTX]\n     |__ | |_______ /_______ /________\ :______/___|_______ /__| \  |     \n        Y          Y        Y          \!                  Y      \ |     \n        :          :        :           :    s¡G/X\a 7 aHQ :       \|\n        .    _    _._ ___   :___  ___  ___  ___  ____  ___ .        !\n        : __//_  //// _//   ._// //__ //_   _// // // __// :        :\n        :  //     //__// ø __// //_// __//__// //_// //__  | :      .\n        |                                                · :_.      \n        |                sYsOp: CøRteX/tRS¿              :_:/       :\n        |          cOsYsOpS: FeLoN - DJAX/sIgMa 7         \/        .\n        | ·                                                |        °\n      · :_:· rUnNiNg oN A1200 - 68882/33Mhz with /X v3.X   |\n      :/\_\:        24h a DaY - keWl Ansi Dezigns          |  _/\_\n       \/_/ __ _______________________________________ __  