INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ult_stp_','ULT^STP!.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ULT^STP!.LHA',NULL,'XIM','___.---. ____________________________',NULL,'gIZMO','ULT^STP','/   |    \                            | \  .---. / u.L.T.i.M.A  p.R.E.S.E.N.T | \:|   |/__                           |',replace('   ___.---. ____________________________\n  /   |    \                            |\n  \  .---. / u.L.T.i.M.A  p.R.E.S.E.N.T |\n   \:|   |/__                           |\n  :  |  ____7___         sTOP!          |\n  :: |:/       7 /X dOOR tO sTOP uP oR  .\n  ::.  `-.   .-'' dOWNLOADS to cERTAiN .::\n  :::::. |:. |   cONFS.    bY gIZMO .::::\n  ::::::.`---'' ------------------ .::::::\n','\n',char(10)),'STOP.guide',replace('@DataBase uLTiMA sTOP! v1.0 bY gIZMO/uLTiMA\n@Author rINCEWiND/uLT^dAT\n\n@node MAIN \n@TITLE "uLTiMA sTOP © 1996 gIZMO/uLTiMA.  mAIN dOCUMENTATiON"\n\n\n   _____        ____.        ______               ___  ___     ________\n._\\   /____ ._\\   |____ ._\\    /_  ._\\ ___ ._\\  \/   \ ._\\____   \-T!\n|     |    .\|      |   .\|      __/__|   \\ .\|     \/   .\|  ____/   .\\n|    /|     \\      |    \\      \    \       \\______\    \\           \\\n|____________/____________/____________\_______/ tGø/_______/____________/\n                                    96\n\n\n                       BELIEVE -+- BEWARE -+- BEHOLD\n                         \n                                sTOP! v 1.o\n \n                            @{" iNTRODUCTiON " Link iNTRODUCTiON}\n                            @{" iNSTALLATiON " Link iNSTALLATiON}\n                            @{" rEGiSTRATION " Link rEGiSTRATION}                            \n                            @{" cREDS n tHAT " Link gREETS}\n                \n@endnode\n@node iNTRODUCTiON\n@TITLE "iNTRODUCTION"\n\n\nI coded this little door becoz I have a free download conference on my \nBBS where all warez over a certain age are moved to,  to keep the main \no-3 day conf speedy.  Occasionally,  though,  I get the odd jerk \nuploading to this conference by mistake or coz there thick-  coz the\nfiles don''t stay long,  and are deleted after a few weeks-  also coz\nI''m too lazy to move the files by myself.\n\nThis door simply sTOPS (hence the name =) users from upping to a selected\nconference,  additionally is a tool to stop downloading,  I don''t need\nthis door myself,  but peeps who run collection points for,  say, discmags,\ncharts,  etc. may want people uploading  to a conference,  but not leeching\nfrom it.\n\n\n                            @{"  mAIN  mENU  " Link mAiN}\n                            @{" iNSTALLATiON " Link iNSTALLATION}\n\n@endnode\n@node iNSTALLATiON\n@TITLE "iNSTALLiNG tHE dOOR"\n\npREPARiNG fOR iNSTALLATiON\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nInstallation is real simple..\n\ncopy all files as they are in the archive into u''re BBS directory,  in\nthe cOMMANDS dir there is a dir called `cONFxcMD''  and the x should be\nreplaced with the conference that you don''t want upping/downing to.\nyou can clone this dir so the door can be used in as many conferences as\nyou like.  also,  don''t forget to remove the icons u don''t need (Ie. in\na free download conference you will need to remove...\n                   BBS:cOMMANDS/cONFxcMD/d.iNFO\n                                                  ... right?\nIf you don''t understand check your /X documentation,  that''ll see you\nthrough,  or you could call my BBS.\n\n\nwHAT eACH iCON dOES.\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nCONFXCMD/\n         RZ.INFO  Stops upload without starting the full upload sequence\n          U.INFO  Stops upload with full upload sequence                \n          D.INFO  Stops downloads                                       \n\n\n                            @{"  mAiN  mENU  " Link main}\n                            @{" rEGiSTRATION " Link rEGiSTRATiON}\n \n\n@endnode\n@node rEGiSTRATION\n@TITLE "sUPPORT fUTURE dOORS"\n\n\nThis file is `Call my BBS coz I need some users'' ware.  This means that\nmy BBS is a bit thin on the ground,  so give me a call!  Registered users\nwill get the words `Registered to whoever'' on their door,  see,  its\nworth it!\n\n\n                            @{"  mAiN  mENU  " Link main}\n                            @{" aBOUT & tHAT "Link gREETS}\n\n@endnode\n@node gREETS\n@TITLE "sTUPiD bIT"\n\nThis door was compiled by gIZMO / uLTIMA.\nThis cewl Amiga Guide by rINCEWiND / uLTiMA^dATA dIViSiON.\nKewl uLTIMA logo by tANGO/tWiSTED ..   cHEERS n bEERS m8ee!\n\nmUSiC sUPPORT (For rINCWiND,  not gIZMO,  coz he only likes eLViS)\n\nsMASHiNG pUMPKiNS,  gARBAGE,  fLAMiNG lIPS,  gREEN dAY,  oASiS,\nvERUCA sALT,  tHE lEVELLERS,  hOLE,  pJ hARVEY,  eCHOBELLY,  \ntHE bLUETONES,  fLUFFY,  hEAVY sTEREO, tHE cARDIGANS..  \n                                             ..bRAT bUS tOUR rULEZ!\n\ncONTACT\n~~~~~~~\n\nTo get in touch with the best Amiga guide writer in the world,  or\nGizmo,  try these Ultima BBS''s.\n\ngIZMO is sysop of Poohs corner,  call there to get registered.\n\nrINCEWiND is sysop of sUBhUMAN,  and is always on dIGiTAL cANDY,\n          so you may wanna try them.\n\n            _:\n            \|_                [36mULTIMA 96             .\n             |/                                           ¦\n             |                 ____.    /\                |\n           ._:__  _______.    /    |__ (__) ______  ____  :_________\n    |      |    \/       |___/     __/_/  \/      \/    \/    __    \\n    |      |     \       |   \     |   \   \      \/     \    \_     \\n    |      ______/     ______/     ____/___/     _/\_____/     |_____/\n    `------'' tGø`------''-T! `------''      `------''      `------''\n             .                                            |\n             |       dIGITAL cANDY    o1912 325527        |\n             |        (5 nODE rINGDOWN - uLT wHQ)         |\n             |       sUBhUMAN         o1952 4o57o5       _|\n             |       cORN oN tHE cOB  o1743 358493       \|_\n             |       fAWLTY tOWERS    o1813 867123        |/\n             |       dIGITAL pLEASURE oH! i fORGOT        :\n             |       tHE sTABLE       o1554 891246        .\n             |       pOOHS cORNER     o1952 276374        :\n             !       dROP zONE        o1633 877657        ¦\n             ¦       nODDYS iSLAND    o1934 645734        |\n             :       lEVI''s 5o1       o13o5 822843        |\n                     vOYAGER          o12o5 357272\n                     dISCLOSURE nD1.  o1914 783149        .\n                     dISCLOSURE nD2.  o1914 783154\n\n                b e l i e v e ÷ b e w a r e ÷ b e h o l d\n\ngREETS..\n~~~~~~~~\n(gIZMO)\n\nCreds go to RINCEWIND for writing the guide and beta testing.and of coz you for\ninstalling this door.\nFuckings go to Freeman who sold his amiga and bought a pc ehehehehehehe !!!!\nmega greets go to all the ULTIMA crew out there\n\n(rINCEWiND)\n\nWell,  Hi to all the deserving guys out there,  Including..\n\naww,  fuck,  can''t be arsed..  all I know..\n\n\nbut mostly to sHAiTAN for helping the group whilst I take time out..  \nOh!  major `wHAT tHE fUCK iS gOING oN''s to jULiE..  \n\n                           \n                            @{"  mAiN  mENU  " Link main}\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,13431,5,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048813);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ult','ULT.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ULT.LHA',NULL,'XIM','__ .--. __     __         _   .----. ____',NULL,NULL,NULL,'|  ||  ||  |__ |  `-.  __ |  \/     |:__  : |  `''  ||  :  ||  .-''.:  :|     /|  |.--'' | :___   |:   __;:   __;|  ||  |\/ :__;| o  |',replace('  __ .--. __     __         _   .----. ____\n |  ||  ||  |__ |  `-.  __ |  \/     |:__  :\n |  `''  ||  :  ||  .-''.:  :|     /|  |.--'' |\n :___   |:   __;:   __;|  ||  |\/ :__;| o  |\n     `--''`--''   `--''   :__;`--''       `----''\n  /\/\         uLTIMa''s pRESENTS      /\_/\\n ( oO )         + /X   aEhYDRA        {o^O}\n-:  . :-  hACKER (BETA)  fOR /X 4.+   /( )\\n.|_||_|.gIVE tHEM hACKERS A mESSAGE   I_:_I\n~~~  ~~~     bEFORE tHEY gET IN\n        wRITES A nICE EALL tO uSERS\ntHANX tO: [Melone] aT aTLANTIC\n','\n',char(10)),'HACKER.DOC',replace('          :______.                                             /\\n    ._____¡      ¡____________________________________________/  \\n    |     |      |      |            |      |                 |  .\\n    |    .|     .|     .|           .|     .|                .|   \\\n    |    ¡|     ¡|     ¡|______     ¡|     ¦|          ,     ¡| |  \\\n    |    ~|     ¦|     ``     |     ||     ||      \  ø/     || |   ~\\n    |           `|            |     `|     `|      |\_/|     ||       \\n    |____________|____________|      |______|______|   |     `|_|      \\n                              `------''                 |______| `-------''\n===============================================================================\n1995 Gizmo/ULTIMA Hack Attempt v0.01\n===============================================================================\nHack attempt is a flexible hack door that came about from Lame peeps trying to \nuse commands that they where not supposed to use,So this door reminds them that\nits no use them even trying to use the command.\nIts rather a stupid door but it does give the lamer a nasty hint that the sysop\nis a miffed of them trying to use say the shell command when they are not \nsupposed to.I know that you can set the acces level of some doors so that to use \nthem the user will need a higher access, but on some occasions a user may just\nhave that access.\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSIMPLE TO INSTALL..... just drag the draw into your doors Dir. and put the \nbbs command Icon in bbs commands.\nFirst rename your command that you dont want to be used to somthing else that \nyou will remeber,BUT let you user (who you want to use that command) know what \nits now called eg rename shell. info say to enter.info or whatever\nin the bbs command dir  in this arcive rename the icon there to say shell\nSO whwn a hacker trys to use shell he gets the new door insted of the shell he \nwanted easy ehhh .You can use this for any command you choose.\nSO the hacker gets the new door, and it writes an eall message to all users,\nthat he (whoever he may be) tried to hack the bbs.SO now every one knows he \ntried to hack your bbs\nOK you will have to alter the arexx script a bit too, you must set the path for\nyour eall message eg.\nCONFNAME =''BBS:CONF3/''\nand the sysop name eg\nSYSOPNAME = FRED\nthats about it.I hope you enjoy theis silly door\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nIf you have trouble installing this door the close ya bbs down as its simple enough\nThere is no need to regester for this door as it is Nutt werze ,That means you know \na monkey does with his Nutts well thats where ya stick it when youve finnished with\nit.\n____________________________________________________________________________________\n\nTHIS IS A INTERNAL ULTIMA DOOR SO DONT SPRED IT OUTSIDE ULTIMA UNTILL FULL BETA TESTED\n\n>>>>>>>>>> bBS nUMBERS...to call\n.----------------+------------------------------------+----------------:\n|                |                                    |                ¡\n|  sUB hUMAN     | uLTIMa^uFORIa wHQ            28.8  |  o1952 4o57o5  |\n|    vOYAGEr     | uLTIMa^uFORIa hQ             28.8  |  o12o5 357272  |\n| cORn oN tHe cOb| uLTIMa^uFr^aQs hQ            28.8  |  o1743 358493  |\n|   tHE sTABLE   | uLTIMa hQ                    28.8  |  o1554 891246  |\n|  pOOHs  cORNEr | uLTIMa^uFORIa hQ             28.8  |  o1952 276374  |\n|  fAWLTy tOWERs | uLTIMa^uFORIa hQ             28.8  |  o1813 867123  |\n|    dROP zONE   | uLTIMA^rMC hQ                28.8  |  o1633 877657  |\n|dIGITAL pLEASURE| uLTIMA hQ                    28.8  |  o1            |\n| nOODYS iSLAND  | uLTiMA^dATA dIVISION hQ      14.4  |  o1934 645734  |\n| fIRST eDiTiON  | uLTiMA^rMC hQ                28.8  |  o13o5 822843  |\n|   dISCLOSURE   | uLTIMA^dATA dIVISION hQ      28.8  |  o1914 783149  |\n|   (2 nODES!)   | nUP; rEM   sPW; sTiPE              |  o1914 783154  |\n|                |                                    |                |\n:----------------[ uLTIMa &  \/FO-RI/\  SUPPORT BBS''s ]----------------''\n\n\n                 Somebody Stop me !!!!,  I''m Gona Call\n\n                   ThE HoUsE At PooH''s CoRnEr BBS on\n \n                          +44 01952 276374 \n\n                            It''s Smokin''  \n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,11186,5,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048813);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ulthack','ULTHACK.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/ULTHACK.LHA','aehydra','XIM','aehydra',NULL,NULL,NULL,'|  ||  ||  |__ |  `-.  __ |  \/     |:__  : |  `''  ||  :  ||  .-''.:  :|     /|  |.--'' | :___   |:   __;:   __;|  ||  |\/ :__;| o  |',replace('  __ .--. __     __         _   .----. ____\n |  ||  ||  |__ |  `-.  __ |  \/     |:__  :\n |  `''  ||  :  ||  .-''.:  :|     /|  |.--'' |\n :___   |:   __;:   __;|  ||  |\/ :__;| o  |\n     `--''`--''   `--''   :__;`--''       `----''\n  /\/\         uLTIMa''s pRESENTS      /\_/\\n ( oO )         + /X   aEhYDRA        {o^O}\n-:  . :-  hACKER (BETA)  fOR /X 4.+   /( )\\n.|_||_|.gIVE tHEM hACKERS A mESSAGE   I_:_I\n~~~  ~~~     bEFORE tHEY gET IN\n        wRITES A nICE EALL tO uSERS\n','\n',char(10)),'reference-board.txt',replace(replace('              W h e r e   t h e   w a r e z   c o m e   f r o m\r\n                                               __                /\_____:\r\n__/\__________________________________________|  \______________/  \    |__\r\n\_   ___________  _______ ________  \__   ___ |   _______  _______  \_  l  \\r\n__\____  \    _l   \    |  \     |___/     |  !    \   _l   \   _| __/\____ \_\r\n\_____    \___\     \___|   \___ !   \__   |_____   \__\     \__\    \____   /\r\n -mNT\_____/---\_____/--l____/-\______/\   |----\____/--\_____/--\____/--\__/\r\n                                        \__|\r\n\r\n- -- --> F A i R L i G H T   S W E D i S H   H E A D Q U A R T E R S <-- -- -\r\n\r\n           reference-board is back 2017 after more than 20 years in coma!\r\n\r\n                        Running on AmiExpress TelNet\r\n\r\n                    Connect to: reference-board.zapto.org:1541\r\n\r\n                    or: www.brysk.se/reference-board/index.htm\r\n               \n              UPLOAD DATE: 01-04-18  TIME: 20:40:00  ON NODE: 0\n','\r',char(13)),'\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',37297,2,0,NULL,NULL,'ulthack','scan',1780048813);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('unarj241','UNARJ241.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/UNARJ241.LHA','unarj','XIM','sonnencreme.exe',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,replace('UNARJ V 2.41\n','\n',char(10)),'UNARJ.DOC',replace('\n     UNARJ.DOC, UNARJ 2.41                                   April 1993\n\n\n        UNARJ software and manual copyright (c) 1991-93 by Robert K Jung.\n	All rights reserved.\n\n        UNARJ version 2.41 release\n\n\n     This documents new or updated information since UNARJ 2.10.\n\n\n     ** IMPORTANT NEWS ****************************************************\n\n     The ARJ archive format at 2.39 and above supports an archive\n     date-time modified field.\n\n     A new data check has been added to make_table() in DECODE.C to\n     account for badly corrupted data.\n\n     There is a newly defined flag bit in the ARJ flags.  See TECHNOTE.DOC\n     for details.  UNARJ only supports this flag bit with the "l" command.\n\n     There is an extended header bug in older versions of ARJ, AV.C and\n     UNARJ.C.  The extended header processing in read_header() should skip\n     4 bytes for the extended header CRC and not 2 bytes.  This is NOT a\n     current problem as no versions of ARJ use the extended header.\n\n     The following source line in DECODE.C is AMBIGUOUS and has been\n     corrected.\n\n	weight[i++] = 1 << (16 - i);\n\n     **********************************************************************\n\n     Here is the C source code for a simple UNARJ extractor program.  It\n     has been portabilized courtesy of Mark Adler for platforms that do not\n     support ANSI C.  This UNARJ is NOT meant for use as a production\n     quality ARJ extractor.  It is meant for the use of 3rd party\n     developers who want to build file readers, etc, for ARJ.  The UNARJ\n     source code has been built and tested under Turbo C++ 1.0, Quick C\n     2.5, and Coherent 3.2.0.\n\n     It has none of the program protection and other fancy features of\n     ARJ 2.41.  It is also VERY SLOW compared to ARJ!!!  In ARJ, all of\n     the critical routines are written in assembly language.\n\n\n     COMMAND SYNTAX:\n\n     UNARJ has been modified to support the four commands: "e", "l", "t",\n     and "x".  These are similar to the ARJ version of these commands.\n     However, UNARJ does not create directories when using the "x" command.\n\n     Usage:  UNARJ archive[.arj]    (list archive)\n	     UNARJ e archive	    (extract archive)\n	     UNARJ l archive	    (list archive)\n	     UNARJ t archive	    (test archive)\n	     UNARJ x archive	    (extract with pathnames)\n\n     UNARJ does not accept any other commands or options.  You cannot\n     specify a base directory or select individual files to extract.  UNARJ\n     does not support empty directories or volume labels.  UNARJ is much\n     slower than ARJ because ARJ is highly optimized using assembly\n     language.\n\n\n     "e" extract command\n\n     This command extracts the contents of the ARJ archive to the current\n     directory.  Files in the archive that already exist in the current\n     directory will not be extracted.\n\n\n     "l" list command\n\n     This command lists the contents of the archive to the screen.  The\n     UNARJ l command replaces the old AV.EXE program.\n\n     The last field on the display BTPMGVX stands for:\n	 B -> file has been marked as a backup\n	 T -> text/binary/directory/volume label type\n	 P -> path information available in "V" listing\n	 M -> compression method used\n	 G -> file has been garbled (encrypted)\n	 V -> archive has been continued to another volume\n	 X -> this file is an extended portion of a larger file\n\n\n     "t" test command\n\n     This command tests the contents of the archive by extracting the files\n     to the NUL device (no data will be written to disk).  If the contents\n     of a file is corrupted, UNARJ will display "CRC error!".  If the\n     contents are valid, UNARJ will display "CRC OK".\n\n     You can use this command to see if an archive contains pathnames.\n\n\n     "x" extract with pathnames command\n\n     This command extracts the contents of the ARJ archive to the pathnames\n     stored in the archive.  If only filespecs are stored in the archive,\n     then the files will be extracted to the current directory.  UNARJ will\n     not create missing directories in the pathnames.  You must create them\n     manually.	Use the UNARJ t command to see the full pathnames stored in\n     the archive.\n\n\n     PROGRESS INDICATOR\n\n     UNARJ uses a small spinning bar to indicate extraction/testing\n     progress.  For some systems that have buffered output, the progress\n     indicator may not work.\n\n\n     BUILDING THE UNARJ PROGRAM\n\n     Source files:  UNARJ.C, DECODE.C, ENVIRON.C, UNARJ.H, UNARJ.DEF,\n		    TCCUNARJ.MAK, QCLUNARJ.MAK, OS2UNARJ.MAK.\n\n     For Turbo C/C++, type MAKE /ftccunarj.mak\n\n     For QuickC,      type NMAKE /F qclunarj.mak\n\n     For OS/2,	      type NMAKE /F os2unarj.mak\n\n     For Coherent,    type\n	 cc -DUNIX -DCOHERENT -o unarj unarj.c decode.c environ.c\n\n     For UNIX	      type cc -DUNIX -o unarj unarj.c decode.c environ.c\n\n     If you use a compiler other than listed above, the resulting UNARJ.EXE\n     will not support restoring file date-time stamps.	You can modify the\n     ENVIRON.C file to add these functions for your particular\n     implementation environment.\n\n     If you send me your implementations, I will try to incorporate them\n     into the next version of UNARJ.\n\n\n     ACKNOWLEDGEMENTS:\n\n     I wish to thank Haruhiko Okumura for providing the ideas for ARJ and\n     UNARJ.  His AR001 and AR002 provided the basic compression algorithms\n     for ARJ 1.0.  At ARJ 2.0, ARJ uses only the secondary Huffman\n     compressor from AR002.\n\n     I wish to thank Mark Adler for helping make UNARJ more portable.\n\n     I also wish to acknowledge the use of the file date-time stamping\n     routines in Rahul Dhesi''s ZOO archiver.\n\n     And to those who have contributed bug reports and porting information,\n     I extend my thanks.\n\n\n     UNARJ LICENSE POLICY FOR ALL USERS:\n\n     The UNARJ program, source code, and the associated documentation\n     are copyright (c) 1990-93 Robert K Jung, all rights reserved.\n\n     If you distribute this software to others, you are required to\n     distribute the ENTIRE package consisting of the following files:\n\n     README.DOC\n     UNARJ.EXE\n     UNARJ.DOC\n     UNARJ.C\n     DECODE.C\n     ENVIRON.C\n     UNARJ.H\n     UNARJ.DEF\n     TCCUNARJ.MAK\n     QCLUNARJ.MAK\n     OS2UNARJ.MAK\n     TECHNOTE.DOC\n\n     I strongly prefer that the files be distributed in the format\n     originally released:  UNARJ241.EXE with the ARJ-SECURITY envelope as\n     created by the author.  If you must distribute the UNARJ archive in\n     another archive format, please archive the UNARJ241.EXE as one file\n     inside the other archive.	Re-archival of the software as separate\n     files means losing the ARJ security envelope.\n\n     You may freely use the UNARJ C source code provided the end product is\n     NOT an ARJ archiver (both compress and extract ARJ files).  If you\n     wish to distribute a modified version of UNARJ.EXE, you MUST indicate\n     that it is a modified version both in the program and source code.\n\n     I am holding the copyright on the source code, so please do not delete\n     my name from the program files or the documentation.\n\n     The UNARJ.EXE program is built from this source using Turbo C++ 1.0.\n\n     You may freely use, copy, and distribute UNARJ.EXE, provided that no\n     fee is charged for such use, copying or distribution.\n\n     You may use UNARJ.EXE in a commercial software package provided that\n     no additional fee is charged for using UNARJ.EXE and provided that\n     the user fully understands that NO warranty or support is provided\n     for UNARJ.EXE by ARJ Software.  Moreover, the user must fully\n     understand that UNARJ does not have the long usage history that ARJ\n     does.\n\n     This source code is intended to promote the building of utilities to\n     support the use of ARJ and ARJ archives.\n\n\n     TECHNICAL SUPPORT:\n\n     Please report any bugs.  I will TRY to fix them.  If you have\n     portability improvements, I would appreciate receiving a copy of them.\n\n     I can be reached at:\n\n     Robert Jung at Channel One BBS   (617) 354-8873\n\n     Robert Jung at Bay State BBS     (617) 598-6646\n\n     Robert Jung at FIDONET address:  1:16/390.7\n\n     Robert Jung in the ARJ (RIME/RELAYNET), COMPRESS (ILINK), LHARC /\n     COMPRESSIONS (SMARTNET), or ARCHIVERS (RIME/RELAYNET) echo\n     conferences.\n\n     ARJ Software\n     Robert and Susan Jung\n     2606 Village Road West\n     Norwood, Massachusetts 02062  USA\n\n     Internet address:  [email removed]\n\n     CompuServe userid: 72077,445\n\n\n     DISCLAIMER:\n\n     This software UNARJ is provided on an "as is" basis without warranty\n     of any kind, expressed or implied, including but not limited to the\n     implied warranties of merchantability and fitness for a particular\n     purpose.  The person using the software bears all risk as to the\n     quality and performance of the software. Should the software prove\n     defective, the user assumes the entire cost of all necessary repair,\n     servicing, or correction.	The author will not be liable for any\n     special, incidental, consequential, indirect or similar damages due to\n     loss of data or any other reason, even if the author or an agent of\n     the author has been advised of the possibility of such damages.\n\n\n     HISTORY:\n\n     UNARJ 2.41 - Added ARCHIMEDES support.  Added archive date-time\n                  modified field support.  Added data check to\n                  make_table().  Updated ARJ header descriptions.\n\n     UNARJ 2.30 - Added new header arj flag (BACKUP_FLAG).\n		  Updated information in TECHNOTE.DOC.\n\n     UNARJ 2.22 - Added missing semicolon to unarj.c for THINK_C.\n		  Modified text mode processing to include test for\n		  host_os in fwrite_txt_crc().\n		  Added more error checking to unarj.c.\n\n     UNARJ 2.21 - Changed uint ratio() to static uint ratio().\n		  Added #ifdef VMS to unarj.c.\n		  Tested unarj on COHERENT (UNIX clone).\n		  Fixed use of _chmod to handle directories.\n		  Modified unarj.c to support the MAC THINK_C compiler.\n		  Added #include <stdlib.h> to vanilla section of environ.c.\n		  Added file date-time stamping to UNIX section of environ.c.\n\n     UNARJ 2.20 - Changed arguments in get_mode_str() and set_ftime_mode() to\n		  at least int size.\n\n		  Added default_case_path() for convenience in UNIX.\n\n		  Added two missing %c from printf statement in list_arc().\n\n   end document\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',48188,5,0,NULL,NULL,'unarj241','scan',1780048813);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('uni_dl','UNI-DL.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/UNI-DL.LHA','Download','XIM','.          xx',NULL,'ZORRo/lINK','UNI','U   ___|\  _  __  __  ___  _  __    U N   \_ ! \/ \/  \/  \/   \/ \/  \   N I   /  !  \  \   \  \\ !  \  \   \  I',replace('          .          xx\n   U   ___|\  _  __  __  ___  _  __    U\n   N   \_ ! \/ \/  \/  \/   \/ \/  \   N\n   I   /  !  \  \   \  \\ !  \  \   \  I\n   O  //      \ \   /   \\·   ) \   /  O\n   N (_________)/\_/______)__/\_/\_/   N \n               P·R·E·S·E·N·T             \n +---------------------------------------+\n |dOWNlOAD COUNtER v1.0 bY ZORRo/lINK    |\n |      wORKS oN /X v.!! aND S!X         |\n `---------------------------------------´\n','\n',char(10)),'DOWNLOADMSG.TXT',replace('~\n~CC_DOWN\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,42149,2,0,NULL,NULL,'uni_dl_download','scan',1780048813);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('uni_nb10','UNI-NB10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/UNI-NB10.LHA','NuBroadCaster','XIM','NuBroadCaster',NULL,'CRiMSON!/UNiVERSAL','UNI','.-/ / /  \/ / / /_ \__ \  ____ \/ /--------. |/ / / / / / / / / /  _/\  /   / /_:TEMPEST| / / / / / / / / __/ / / / / / / / /+DESIGNS|',replace('   ______  ____/\______________  /\\n.-/ / /  \/ / / /_ \__ \  ____ \/ /--------.\n|/ / / / / / / / / /  _/\  /   / /_:TEMPEST|\n/ / / / / / / / __/ / / / / / / / /+DESIGNS|\n\__/\/ /\/\__/\__/\/\/\  /\__/\__/:PRESENTS|\n|----\/----------------\/------------------|\n|: ->....NEW-USER BROADCASTER! V1.0....<- :|\n|:Announces new-users with massmail msg''s!:|\n|:      Coded By CRiMSON!/UNiVERSAL       :|\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'NuBroadCaster.Guide',replace('@database UNIVERSAL DOCUMENTS\n\n@node MAIN "-->>  UNiVERSAL iNC.! TEMPEST DESiGNS <<--"\n\n                       ______  ____/\\______________  /\\\n                      / / /  \\/ / / /_ \\__ \\  ____ \\/ /\n                     / / / / / / / / / /  _/\\  /   / /_\n                    / / / / / / / / __/ / / / / / / / /\n                    \\__/\\/ /\\/\\__/\\__/\\/\\/\\  /\\__/\\__/\n                         \\/                \\/              \n                                                     \n                      -//-    P R E S E N T S   -//- \n\n        ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n               NEW-USER BROADCASTER V1.0 BY CRiMSON!/UNiVERSAL\n\n        ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n\n                        @{" -->>  Introduction  <<-- " Link Introduction}\n                        @{" -->>  Installation  <<-- " Link Installation}\n                        @{" -->>    Plannings   <<-- " Link Plannings}\n                        @{" -->>    Greetings   <<-- " Link Greetings}\n@endnode\n@node Introduction "Introduction"\n\n  New-User BroadCaster is a door wich announces new-users!\n\n   Features:\n   ~~~~~~~~~\n    - Writes a Mass-Mail message into the E-Mail Area (conf. 0)!\n\n    - 100% C Code!\n\n\n   -->> If you find any bugs or have suggestions, please leave a mail to\n        ''CRiMSON!'' at Dawn of Eternity, The Tribe!, or Traders Paradise!\n\n\n                          @{"  Main  " Link MAIN}\n@endnode\n@node Installation "Installation"\n\n - Unpack the archive with the full paths!\n\n - Or copy NuBroadCaster to DOORS:UNIVERSAL/NUBROADCASTER/\n   copy Text-NewUserQuestions to TEMPEST:TEXT/ENGLISH/\n\n   -->> I used Text-NewuserQuestions to start this door from, since\n        there was no text-joined or something like /X ...\n\n\n                          @{"  Main  " Link MAIN}\n@endnode\n@node Plannings "Plannings"\n\n - Dunno, Tell me!\n\n\n                               @{"  Main  " Link MAIN}\n@endnode\n@node Greetings "Greetings"\n\n - Skeleton.....: Hope you like this?\n - DAMiEN.......: The BoomBoom man :)\n - LeatherFace..: Nice board m8!\n\n\n                       ...and all the rest I forgot!\n\n\n                               @{"  Main  " Link MAIN}\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',19853,5,0,NULL,NULL,'uni_nb10','scan',1780048813);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('uni_sr10','UNI-SR10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/UNI-SR10.LHA','Super-Request','XIM','Super-Request',NULL,'CRiMSON!/UNiVERSAL','UNI','.-/ / /  \/ / / /_ \__ \  ____ \/ /--------. |/ / / / / / / / / /  _/\  /   / /_:TEMPEST| / / / / / / / / __/ / / / / / / / /+DESIGNS|',replace('   ______  ____/\______________  /\\n.-/ / /  \/ / / /_ \__ \  ____ \/ /--------.\n|/ / / / / / / / / /  _/\  /   / /_:TEMPEST|\n/ / / / / / / / __/ / / / / / / / /+DESIGNS|\n\__/\/ /\/\__/\__/\/\/\  /\__/\__/:PRESENTS|\n|----\/----------------\/------------------|\n|: ->........SUPER REQUEST V1.0........<- :|\n|:                                        :|\n|:      Coded By CRiMSON!/UNiVERSAL       :|\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'Super-Request.Guide',replace('@database UNIVERSAL DOCUMENTS\n\n@node MAIN "-->>  UNiVERSAL iNC.! TEMPEST DESiGNS <<--"\n\n                       ______  ____/\\______________  /\\\n                      / / /  \\/ / / /_ \\__ \\  ____ \\/ /\n                     / / / / / / / / / /  _/\\  /   / /_\n                    / / / / / / / / __/ / / / / / / / /\n                    \\__/\\/ /\\/\\__/\\__/\\/\\/\\  /\\__/\\__/\n                         \\/                \\/              \n                                                     \n                      -//-    P R E S E N T S   -//- \n\n        ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n                  SUPER-REQUEST V1.0 BY CRiMSON!/UNiVERSAL\n\n        ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n\n                        @{" -->>  Introduction  <<-- " Link Introduction}\n                        @{" -->>  Installation  <<-- " Link Installation}\n                        @{" -->>    ToolTypes   <<-- " Link ToolTypes}\n                        @{" -->>    Plannings   <<-- " Link Plannings}\n                        @{" -->>    Greetings   <<-- " Link Greetings}\n@endnode\n@node Introduction "Introduction"\n\n  Super-Request is a normal request door!\n\n   Features:\n   ~~~~~~~~~\n    - Writes an Eall message in the conference you have specified!\n\n    - All config can be set in the @{" Tooltypes " Link Tooltypes}\n\n    - 100% C Code!\n\n\n   -->> If you find any bugs or have suggestions, please leave a mail to\n        ''CRiMSON!'' at Dawn of Eternity, The Tribe!, or Traders Paradise!\n\n   -->> At the moment I run on a B/W moni, so if the output is ugly,\n        gimme a mail!\n\n\n                          @{"  Main  " Link MAIN}\n@endnode\n@node Installation "Installation"\n\n - Unpack the archive with the full paths!\n\n - Or copy Super-Request & Super-Request.info to DOORS:UNIVERSAL/SUPER-REQUEST/\n\n - Add this to your globalmenu.opt file:\n\n-------------------------> Cut Here <-------------------------\n[20-,*,*,*,*]  = REQUEST  |T-DOOR|DOORS:UNIVERSAL/SUPER-REQUEST/SUPER-REQUEST\n[20-,*,*,*,*]  = REQ      |T-DOOR|DOORS:UNIVERSAL/SUPER-REQUEST/SUPER-REQUEST\n-------------------------> Cut Here <-------------------------\n\n - Now edit the @{" Tooltypes " Link Tooltypes}... That''s all!\n\n\n                          @{"  Main  " Link MAIN}\n@endnode\n@node ToolTypes "ToolTypes"\n\n Conference=<x>        <<----- Number of the conference where the messages\n                                must be written!\n\n\n                          @{"  Main  " Link MAIN}\n@endnode\n@node Plannings "Plannings"\n\n - Dunno, Tell me!\n\n\n                               @{"  Main  " Link MAIN}\n@endnode\n@node Greetings "Greetings"\n\n - Skeleton.....: thnx for the sort routines!\n - DAMiEN.......: Versterker kopen hehe?\n - LeatherFace..: Nice board m8!\n\n\n                       ...and all the rest I forgot!\n\n\n                               @{"  Main  " Link MAIN}\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',20344,5,0,NULL,NULL,'uni_sr10','scan',1780048813);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('unilist','UNILIST.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/UNILIST.LHA','uni-userlist','XIM','uni-userlist','2.2',NULL,NULL,'userlister capable of outputting to a file. C-Net Amiga v3.05+ [MetalSoft]',replace('Uni-UserList v2.2 - a configurable\nuserlister capable of outputting to\na file. C-Net Amiga v3.05+ [MetalSoft]\n','\n',char(10)),'UniList_22.doc',replace('INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('uniquest','UNIQUEST.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/UNIQUEST.LHA','UniQuest','XIM','UniQuest',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,replace('A very universal request door for AmBoS     \n','\n',char(10)),'UniQuest.guide',replace('@database Default\n@master df0:uniquest/UniQuest.guide\n@$VER: 1.01\n@author "Lars Maschmann"\n@(c) ""\n@remark ""\n\n@node "Main" "UniQuest"\n@next "Einführung"\n\n      @{b}UniQuest Version 1.01@{ub}\n      ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n      Ein externes Programm für AmBoS\n      \n\n     @{" Was ist UniQuest? " link "Einführung" 0}\n      \n     @{" Wie wird UniQuest installiert? " link "Installation" 0}\n      \n     @{" Wie wird UniQuest konfiguriert? " link "Konfiguration" 0}\n      \n     @{" Wer hat UniQuest programmiert? " link "Autor" 0}\n      \n     @{" Wer darf UniQuest benutzen? " link "Copyright" 0}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "Einführung" "Einführung"\n@next "Installation"\n@prev "Main"\n UniQuest - Einführung \n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n Was ist UniQuest?\n\n UniQuest ist ein externes Programm für das Mailboxsystem AmBoS. UniQuest \n ist ein einfaches Hilfsmittel, wenn z.B. der SysOp den Usern (z.B. \n nach dem Antrag) noch einige Fragen stellen möchte. Nachdem der Benutzer \n alle Fragen beantwortet hat, wird in ein bestimmtes Postfach oder in das\n SystemInfo-Brett ein UniQuest-Report erzeugt.\n \n    @{" Installation " link "Installation" 0}    @{" Hauptmenü " link "Main" 0}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "Installation" "Installation"\n@next "Konfiguration"\n@prev "Einführung"\n @{b}UniQuest - Installation@{ub} \n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n 1. So wird das Verzeichnis "UniQuest" im Verzeichnis "BBS:Externe" mit\n    Hilfe der AmigaShell angelegt:\n    \n    1> makedir BBS:Externe/UniQuest\n    \n 2. Nun werden alle benötigten Dateien in dieses Verzeichnis kopiert:\n \n    1> copy <quellpfad>/UniQuest#? BBS:Externe/UniQuest\n\n    Für den Betrieb nötig sind mind. die Dateien UniQuest und UniQuest.cmd.\n    \n 3. Das Programm wird im AmBoS-Setup / Doors als externer Befehl einge-\n    tragen. Soll jeder Benutzer UniQuest zu jeder Zeit aufrufen können,\n    muß der Schalter "Eingeschaltet" aktiviert sein. Bei ausschließlicher\n    Verwendung von UniQuest in den Batchdateien sollte dieser Schalter\n    ausgeschaltet sein. Aufruf in einer Batchdatei: Execute UniQuest.\n    \n 4. Nun sollte die Steuerdatei an die eigenen Bedürfnisse angepaßt werden.\n    Dies geschieht mit einem Texteditor, z.B. dem ED der Workbench:\n    \n    1> ED BBS:Externe/UniQuest/UniQuest.cmd\n    \n\n    @{" Konfiguration " link "Konfiguration" 0}    @{" Hauptmenü " link "Main" 0}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "Konfiguration" "Konfiguration"\n@next "Autor"\n@prev "Installation"\n @{b}UniQuest - Konfiguration@{ub} \n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n UniQuest wird über eine Steuerdatei konfiguriert. Dies ist eine Textdatei,\n die mit jedem normalen Texteditor (z.B. ED von der Workbench) verändert\n werden kann.\n\n    @{b}Befehle:@{ub}\n\n             @{" ansifile " link "ansifile" 0}    - Ausgabe einer ANSI-Datei\n             @{" textfile " link "textfile" 0}    - Ausgabe einer Textdatei\n             @{" mailtouser " link "mailtouser" 0}  - Empfänger des Reports (User)\n             @{" mailtoboard " link "mailtoboard" 0} - Brett, in das der Report abgelegt wird\n             @{" text " link "text" 0}        - Ausgabe einer Zeichenkette\n             @{" ask " link "ask" 0}         - Abfrage einer Zeichenkette\n             @{" wait " link "wait" 0}        - auf einen Tastendruck warten\n\n             @{" ;  " link "comment" 0}          - Kennzeichnung einer Kommentarzeile\n             \n\n    @{" Hauptmenü " link "Main" 0}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "mailtouser" "Befehl: mailtouser"\n @{b}Befehle der Steuerdatei ''UniQuest.cmd''@{ub}\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n Befehl: @{b}mailtouser@{ub}\n\n hiermit wird der Empfänger des UniQuest-Reports angegeben\n\n Syntax:    cmd=mailtouser topic=<username>\n Beispiel:  cmd=mailto topic=SysOp\n \n Wird weder mailtouser noch mailtoboard angegeben, so wird der Report \n in das Brett ''/SystemInfo/Box'' gestellt.\n\n\n \n    @{" Befehlsübersicht " link "Konfiguration" 0}   @{" Hauptmenü " link "Main" 0}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "mailtoboard" "Befehl: mailtoboard"\n@{b} Befehle der Steuerdatei ''UniQuest.cmd''@{ub}\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n Befehl: @{b}mailtoboard@{ub}\n \n Hiermit wird angegeben, in welches Brett der Mailbox der Report ge-\n schrieben werden soll.\n \n Syntax:     cmd=mailtoboard topic=<boardname>\n \n Beispiel:   cmd=mailtoboard topic=/SysOp-Bereich/NeueUser\n \n Die Angabe des Brettnamens erfolgt immer mit einem ''/'' am Anfang, \n dieser Schrägstrich stellt symbolisch das Root-Verzeichnis dar.\n \n Wird weder mailtoboard noch mailtouser angegeben, so schreibt UniQuest\n den Report in das Brett ''/SystemInfo/Box''.\n \n \n   @{" Befehlsübersicht " link "Konfiguration" 0}      @{" Hauptmenü " link "Main" 0}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "textfile" "Befehl: textfile"\n @{b}Befehle der Steuerdatei ''UniQuest.cmd''@{ub}\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n Befehl: @{b}textfile@{ub}\n\n Ausgabe einer Textdatei\n\n Optionale Parameter: Positionierung des Cursors (x,y)\n                      Löschen des Bildschirms (cls)\n\n Syntax:    cmd=textfile topic=<textfile> [x=<spalte> y=<zeile>] [cls]\n\n Beispiel:  cmd=textfile topic=BBS:Texte/UniquestMaske.txt x=1 y=1 cls\n\n\n   @{" Befehlsübersicht " link "Konfiguration" 0}    @{" Hauptmenü " link "Main" 0}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "ask" "Befehl: ask"\n @{b}Befehle der Steuerdatei ''UniQuest.cmd''@{ub}\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n Befehl: @{b}ask@{ub}\n\n Eingabe einer Zeichenkette in eine Variable\n\n Optionale Parameter: Unterdrückung des Hintergrundes (noback)\n                      Positionierung des Feldes (x,y)\n                      Löschen des Bildschirms (cls)\n                      Länge des Eingabefeldes (len)\n\n Syntax:    cmd=ask topic=<variable> [x=<spalte> y=<zeile>] [noback]\n                                     [len=<länge>]\n\n Beispiel:  cmd=ask topic=Mailboxnummer x=10 y=5 len=20 noback\n \n Hinweis:   Wird der Parameter ''len'' nicht angegeben, dann wird die\n            Defaultlänge von 40 Zeichen benutzt.\n\n\n    @{" Befehlsübersicht " link "Konfiguration" 0}    @{" Hauptmenü " link "Main" 0}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "text" "Befehl: text"\n @{b}Befehle der Steuerdatei ''UniQuest.cmd''@{ub}\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n Befehl: @{b}text@{ub}\n\n Ausgabe einer Zeichenkette\n\n Optionale Parameter: Positionierung des Cursors (x,y)\n                      Unterdrückung des Zeilenvorschubs (noline)\n                      Löschen des Bildschirms (cls)\n\n Syntax:    cmd=text topic="<zeichenkette>" [x=<spalte> y=<zeile>] [cls]\n\n Beispiel:  cmd=text topic="Das ist ein Text." x=10 y=7\n\n            cmd=text x=1 y=1 cls (Löscht den ganzen Bildschirm)\n\n\n   @{" Befehlsübersicht " link "Konfiguration" 0}    @{" Hauptmenü " link "Main" 0}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "ansifile" "Befehl: ansifile"\n @{b}Befehle der Steuerdatei ''UniQuest.cmd''@{ub}\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n Befehl: @{b}ansifile@{ub}\n\n Ausgabe einer ANSI-Datei\n\n Optionale Parameter: Positionierung des Cursors (x,y)\n                      Löschen des Bildschirms (cls)\n\n Syntax:    cmd=ansifile topic=<ansidatei> [x=<spalte> y=<zeile>] [cls]\n\n Beispiel:  cmd=ansifile topic=BBS:Texte/UniquestMaske.ansi x=1 y=1\n\n\n    @{" Befehlsübersicht " link "Konfiguration" 0}    @{" Hauptmenü " link "Main" 0}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "wait" "wait"\n @{b}Befehle der Steuerdatei ''UniQuest.cmd''@{ub}\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n Befehl: @{b}wait@{ub}\n \n wartet auf einen Tastendruck\n \n Optionale Parameter: Positionierung des Cursors (x,y)\n                      Unterdrückung des Zeilenvorschubs (noline)\n                      Löschen des Bildschirms (cls)\n\n Syntax:    cmd=wait topic="<zeichenkette>" [x=<spalte> y=<zeile>] [cls]\n\n Beispiel:  cmd=wait topic="Taste drücken, wenn bereit." x=10 y=7\n\n\n   @{" Befehlsübersicht " link "Konfiguration" 0}     @{" Hauptmenü " link "Main" 0}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "comment" "Befehl: Kommentar"\n @{b}Befehle der Steuerdatei ''UniQuest.cmd''@{ub}\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n Befehl: @{b}; (Kommentar)@{ub}\n\n Stellt einen Kommentar dar\n\n Syntax:    ; \n\n Beispiel:  ; Das ist ein Kommentar.\n\n Alle Zeichen nach dem Kommentar-Zeichen werden vom internen Interpreter\n von UniQuest ignoriert.\n\n\n   @{" Befehlsübersicht " link "Konfiguration" 0}    @{" Hauptmenü " link "Main" 0}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "Autor" "Autor"\n@next "Copyright"\n@prev "Konfiguration"\n @{b}Der Autor von UniQuest@{ub}\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n Geschrieben wurde dieses AmBoS-Tool von\n \n          Torsten Kramer, eMail: [email removed]\n          \n mit dem SAS/C-Compiler (Version 6.56).\n \n\n @{b}Der Autor dieser Anleitung / Betatesting@{ub}\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n Betatester und Autor dieser Anleitung ist\n \n         Lars Maschmann, eMail:   [email removed]\n                                  [email removed]\n                         Mailbox: ExecBase 0421-242966\n         \n Getestet wurde UniQuest mit der AmBoS-Version 1.23, 2.24 bis 2.81.\n \n Version 1.00 (26.01.96) \n Version 1.01 (05.01.97) - Fehler behoben (x,y-Koordinaten)\n\n\n\n    @{" Hauptmenü " link "Main" 0}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "Copyright" "Copyright"\n@next "Main"\n@prev "Autor"\n @{b}Copyright, Haftung und so weiter...@{ub}\n ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n \n Der Autor übernimmt für das Programm ''UniQuest'' keinerlei Haftung.\n \n ''UniQuest'' wird als FREEWARE publiziert, d.h. jeder darf das Programm\n beliebig oft kopieren, benutzen und weitergeben. Softwaremodifikationen\n jeglicher Art (ausgenommen der Steuerdatei) sind ausdrücklich unter-\n sagt, das Copyright bleibt dem Autor vorbehalten.\n \n Die Software darf nicht zweckentfremdet eingesetzt werden, es darf zwar\n kommerziell eingesetzt werden, der Verkauf ist jedoch verboten.\n \n Es ist untersagt, diese Software zu kriegerischen oder rassistischen\n Maßnahmen einzusetzen oder es zur Herstellung von Waffen oder Garten-\n zwergen einzusetzen. \n \n \n    @{" Hauptmenü " link "Main" 0}\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',12497,4,0,NULL,NULL,'uniquest','scan',1780048813);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('unzip5_2','UNZIP5_2.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/UNZIP5_2.LHA','unzip','XIM','unzip','5.0',NULL,'UNZIP5',NULL,replace('New Unzip V5.0/5.2 Før da /X Checker !!\n','\n',char(10)),'unzip.doc',replace('\012UNZIP(1)                 USER COMMANDS                   UNZIP(1)\012\012NAME\012     unzip - list/test/extract from a ZIP archive file\012\012SYNOPSIS\012     unzip [ -cflptuvxz[ajnoqUV] ] file[.zip] [filespec ...]\012\012ARGUMENTS\012     file[.zip]  Path of the ZIP archive.  The suffix ``.zip'''' is\012                 applied  if  the  file specified does not exist.\012                 Note that self-extracting  ZIP  files  are  sup-\012                 ported;  just  specify the ``.exe'''' suffix your-\012                 self.\012\012     [filespec]  An optional list of archive members to  be  pro-\012                 cessed.  Expressions may be used to match multi-\012                 ple members; be sure to quote  expressions  that\012                 contain  characters interpreted by the operating\012                 system.  See  DESCRIPTION   (below)   for   more\012                 details.\012\012OPTIONS\012     -c  extract files to stdout/screen (``CRT'''')\012     -f  freshen existing files (replace if newer); create none\012     -l  list archive files (short format)\012     -p  extract files to pipe; no informational messages\012     -t  test archive files\012     -u  update existing files; create new ones if needed\012     -v  list archive files (verbose format)\012     -x  extract files in archive (default)\012     -z  display only the archive comment\012\012MODIFIERS\012     -a  convert to MS-DOS textfile format (CR  LF),  Mac  format\012         (CR),  Unix/VMS  format  (LF),  OR from ASCII to EBCDIC,\012         depending on your system (only use for TEXT files!)\012     -j  junk paths (don''t recreate  archive''s  directory  struc-\012         ture)\012     -n  never overwrite existing files; don''t prompt\012     -o  OK to overwrite files without prompting\012     -q  perform operations quietly (-qq => even quieter)\012     -s  [OS/2,  MS-DOS]  allow  spaces   in   filenames   (e.g.,\012         ``EA DATA. SF'''')\012     -U  leave filenames uppercase if created under MS-DOS,  VMS,\012         etc.\012     -V  retain (VMS) file version numbers\012     -X  [VMS]  restore  owner/protection   info   (may   require\012         privileges)\012\012DESCRIPTION\012     UnZip will list, test, or extract from a ZIP  archive,  com-\012     monly  found on MSDOS systems.  Archive member extraction is\012     implied by the absence of the -c,  -p,  -t,  -l,  -v  or  -z\012\012Info-ZIP          Last change: 22 Aug 92 (v5.0)                 1\012\012UNZIP(1)                 USER COMMANDS                   UNZIP(1)\012\012     options.    All  archive  members  are  processed  unless  a\012     filespec is provided to specify  a  subset  of  the  archive\012     members.   The  filespec  is similar to an egrep expression,\012     and may contain:\012\012     *      matches a sequence of 0 or more characters\012     ?      matches exactly 1 character\012     \nnn   matches the character having octal code nnn\012     [...]  matches any single character found inside the  brack-\012            ets; ranges are specified by a beginning character, a\012            hyphen, and an ending character.  If  an  exclamation\012            point  or  a  carat  (`!''  or  `^'')  follows the left\012            bracket, then the range of characters matched is com-\012            plemented  with  respect  to  the ASCII character set\012            (that is, anything except the characters  inside  the\012            brackets is considered a match).\012\012ENVIRONMENT OPTIONS\012     UnZip''s default behavior may be modified via options  placed\012     in  an  environment  variable.   This  can  be done with any\012     option, but it is probably most useful with the -q,  -o,  or\012     -n modifiers:  in order to make UnZip quieter by default, or\012     to make it always overwrite or never overwrite files  as  it\012     extracts them.  For example, to make UnZip act as quietly as\012     possible, only reporting errors, one would use  one  of  the\012     following commands:\012\012           setenv UNZIP -qq           Unix C shell\012\012           UNZIP=-qq; export UNZIP    Unix Bourne shell\012\012           set UNZIP=-qq              OS/2 or MS-DOS\012\012           define UNZIP_OPTS "-qq"    VMS (quotes for LOWERCASE)\012\012     Environment options are, in effect, considered  to  be  just\012     like  any  other  command-line options, except that they are\012     effectively the first options on the command line.  To over-\012     ride  an  environment option, one may use the ``minus opera-\012     tor'''' to remove it.  For instance, to override  one  of  the\012     quiet-flags in the example above, use the command\012\012           unzip --q[other options] zipfile\012\012     The first hyphen is the normal  switch  character,  and  the\012     second  is  a  minus sign, acting on the q option.  Thus the\012     effect here is to cancel a single quantum of quietness.   To\012     cancel both quiet flags, two (or more) minuses may be used:\012\012           unzip -x--q zipfile\012\012Info-ZIP          Last change: 22 Aug 92 (v5.0)                 2\012\012UNZIP(1)                 USER COMMANDS                   UNZIP(1)\012\012     or\012\012           unzip ---qx zipfile\012\012     (the two are equivalent).  This may seem awkward or  confus-\012     ing,  but it is reasonably intuitive:  just ignore the first\012     hyphen and go from there.  It is also  consistent  with  the\012     behavior of Unix nice(1).\012\012EXAMPLES\012     To  use  UnZip  to  extract  all  members  of  the   archive\012     letters.zip, creating any directories as necessary:\012\012           unzip letters\012\012     To extract all members of letters.zip to the current  direc-\012     tory:\012\012           unzip -j letters\012\012     To test letters.zip, printing only a summary  message  indi-\012     cating whether the archive is OK or not:\012\012           unzip -tq letters\012\012     To extract to standard output  all  members  of  letters.zip\012     whose  names  end  in ``.tex'''', converting to the local end-\012     of-line convention and piping the output into more(1):\012\012           unzip -ca letters \*.tex | more\012\012     (The backslash before the asterisk is only required  if  the\012     shell  expands  wildcards,  as  in Unix; double quotes could\012     have been used instead, as in the source example below.)  To\012     extract  the  binary  file paper1.dvi to standard output and\012     pipe it to a printing program:\012\012           unzip -p articles paper1.dvi | dvips\012\012     To extract all FORTRAN and C source  files--*.f,  *.c,  *.h,\012     Makefile  (the  double quotes are necessary only in Unix and\012     only if globbing is turned on):\012\012           unzip source.zip "*.[fch]" Makefile\012\012     To extract only newer versions of the files already  in  the\012     current  directory,  without  querying (NOTE:  be careful of\012     unzipping in one timezone a zipfile created in  another--ZIP\012     archives  contain  no  timezone information, and a ``newer''''\012     file from an eastern timezone may, in fact, be older):\012\012Info-ZIP          Last change: 22 Aug 92 (v5.0)                 3\012\012UNZIP(1)                 USER COMMANDS                   UNZIP(1)\012\012           unzip -fo sources\012\012     To extract newer  versions  of  the  files  already  in  the\012     current  directory and to create any files not already there\012     (same caveat as previous example):\012\012           unzip -uo sources\012\012     In the last five examples, assume that UNZIP  or  UNZIP_OPTS\012     is set to -q.  To do a singly quiet listing:\012\012           unzip -l file\012\012     To do a doubly quiet listing:\012\012           unzip -ql file\012\012     To do a standard listing:\012\012           unzip --ql file\012\012     or\012\012           unzip -l-q file\012\012     or\012\012           unzip -l--q file\012\012     (extra minuses don''t hurt).\012\012TIPS\012     The current maintainer, being a lazy  sort,  finds  it  very\012     useful to define an alias ``tt'''' for ``unzip -tq''''.  One may\012     then simply type ``tt zipfile'''' to test the  archive,  some-\012     thing  which  one  ought  make  a habit of doing.  With luck\012     UnZip will report ``No  errors  detected  in  zipfile.zip,''''\012     after which one may breathe a sigh of relief.\012\012SEE ALSO\012     funzip(1),  zip(1),  zipcloak(1),  zipinfo(1),   zipnote(1),\012     zipsplit(1)\012\012AUTHORS\012     Samuel H. Smith, Carl Mascott, David P. Kirschbaum, Greg  R.\012     Roelofs,  Mark  Adler,  Kai  Uwe  Rommel, Igor Mandrichenko,\012     Johnny Lee, Jean-loup Gailly; Glenn  Andrews,  Joel  Aycock,\012     Allan  Bjorklund,  James  Birdsall,  Wim Bonner, John Cowan,\012     Frank da Cruz, Bill Davidsen, Arjan de Vet, James Dugal, Jim\012     Dumser,  Mark  Edwards, David Feinleib, Mike Freeman, Hunter\012     Goatley, Robert Heath, Dave  Heiland,  Larry  Jones,  Kjetil\012     J(o)rgenson,  Bob Kemp, J. Kercheval, Alvin Koh, Bo Kullmar,\012\012Info-ZIP          Last change: 22 Aug 92 (v5.0)                 4\012\012UNZIP(1)                 USER COMMANDS                   UNZIP(1)\012\012     Johnny Lee, Warner Losh, Fulvio Marino,  Gene  McManus,  Joe\012     Meadows,  Mike  O''Carroll,  Humberto  Ortiz-Zuazaga, Piet W.\012     Plomp, Antonio Querubin Jr., Steve Salisbury, Georg  Sassen,\012     Jon  Saxton,  Hugh Schmidt, Martin Schulz, Charles Scripter,\012     Chris Seaman, Richard Seay, Alex Sergejew,  Cliff  Stanford,\012     Onno  van der Linden, Jim Van Zandt, Antoine Verheijen, Paul\012     Wells.\012\012VERSIONS\012     v1.2  15 Mar 89  Samuel H. Smith\012     v2.0   9 Sep 89  Samuel H. Smith\012     v2.x  fall 1989  many Usenet contributors\012     v3.0   1 May 90  Info-ZIP (DPK, consolidator)\012     v3.1  15 Aug 90  Info-ZIP (DPK, consolidator)\012     v4.0   1 Dec 90  Info-ZIP (GRR, maintainer)\012     v4.1  12 May 91  Info-ZIP\012     v4.2  20 Mar 92  Info-ZIP (zip-bugs subgroup; GRR, maint.)\012     v5.0  21 Aug 92  Info-ZIP (zip-bugs subgroup; GRR, maint.)\012\012Info-ZIP          Last change: 22 Aug 92 (v5.0)                 5\012\012','\012',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',72762,5,0,NULL,NULL,'unzip5_2','scan',1780048813);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('upd10','UPD10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/UPD10.LHA','UPDATER','XIM','UPDATER','1.0','REbEL/QTX',NULL,'Written by REbEL/QTX A little /X tool to prevent your users from losing their creds if there is a',replace('           User Data Updater v1.0\n \n            Written by REbEL/QTX\n \n   A little /X tool to prevent your users\n   from losing their creds if there is a\n   bbs crash after uploading/downloading\n','\n',char(10)),'dESiGN.TXT',replace(' \n \n \n               _______  ___.___  __.____  ________________\n              (_  .___)(_  |  _)(_ |__ _)(_  ____)__  ____)\n              _/  |  \__/  |  \__/ l__ \__/  ;--\__/  _  \_\n              \_______/\___.   /\_______/\_______/\___7___/\n                    [sTORM]|__/\n           _______  _______  _______  _______  _______  _______\n          (_ __  _)(_  ____)(_ .____)(_______)(_  ____)(_  .  _)\n          _/  ¬\ \__/  ;--\__/---. \__/     \__/  \_ \__/  |  \_\n          \_______/\_______/\_______/\_______/\_______/\___|___/\n \n      .--[ aMiGA «·» /X uTiLs «·» dRUGS «·» h/P/a «·» aScII ]-- -     -\n   -  | -  - - ---->  [+] mASTER : sTORM / sHOXX -  [+]  <-- -    -     -\n      `------[ fRiEND sHiP rULEZ! ]-[ oNLiNE aSCII oRDERIN'' ]----------.\n  -   -  - - --[ +46-320-611-11 ]---[ nON-SWEDES = fREE lEECH! ]-------''\n \n \n \n \n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',13856,13,0,NULL,NULL,'upd10','scan',1780048813);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('upl10','UPL10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/UPL10.LHA','dfree','XIM','LE-win5-96.exe',NULL,NULL,NULL,'v1.0 - (c) S.Gillibrand 1996 Digital Design Production! You won''t believe how much this',replace('Upl - Uploading Software For TransAmiga\n      v1.0 - (c) S.Gillibrand 1996\n       Digital Design Production!\n    You won''t believe how much this\n improves TA''s standard upload feature\n Xfer and be amazed is all I can say :)\n','\n',char(10)),'Upl.Guide',replace('@database Upl.guide\n@author "Stuart Gillibrand"\n@(c) "Copyright © 1996 S.Gillibrand - Digital Design Production"\n@$VER: Upl.guide 1.0 (03.02.95)\n\n@Node Main "Upl v1.0 - Main - (C) S.Gillibrand 1996 - Digital Design"\n                          .µ¸ µ. jµµµµ_  µµµ\n                          ¶Ø¹ ¶# ¬ØØ@¶#L ]Ø#\n                          #Ø  ##  ØØÞ ØØÞJØ#\n                          #Ø  ##  ØØÞ ØØ1JØ#\n                          #Ø  ##  ØØKµØØÞJØ#\n                          #Ø  ##  ØØØÑÑ° JØ#   _\n                          #Øx_Æ#  ØØ1    jØQ__µ#\n                          ¯0ØØØ¯ JØØÑ    ØØØØØØ\n\n                                   Upl\n\n          Upload Processing Software For TransAmiga BBS Systems\n\n                                Version 1.0\n             (C) Copyright 1996 S.Gillibrand - Digital Design\n\n                               * FREEWARE *\n\n                      @{"         What Is Upl?        " Link "WHATIS_UPL"}\n                      @{"     System Requirements     " Link "REQUIR_UPL"}\n                      @{"    How Do I Install Upl?    " Link "INSTAL_UPL"}\n                      @{"            Usage            " Link "USAGE!_UPL"}\n                      @{"          Varibles!          " Link "VARIABLES_UPL"}\n\n                      @{"       Upl DATA File!!       " Link "TUPLDATA_UPL"}\n\n                      @{"          Known Bugs         " Link "BUGS!!_UPL"}\n                      @{"            History          " Link "HISTOR_UPL"}\n\n                      @{"  How To Contact The Author  " Link "AUTHOR_UPL"}\n                      @{" What/Who Is Digital Design? " Link "DESIGN_UPL"}\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "WHATIS_UPL" "Upl - What Is Upl? - (C) S.Gillibrand 1996 - Digital Design"\n\nWhat Is Upl?\n+------------+\n\nUPL is a replacement for the standard TransAmiga upload command.. Mainly\nwritten becuase I was sick of the standard one and how it worked.\n\no This does ALL the jobs the original did plus a few extras which you should\n  like if I''m correct (Respect Mystic Meg ;!).\n\no You can have more than 1 line of description per file (Definable by you\n  the SysOp).\n\no Possible to limit number of lines allowed to be taken from a FILE_ID.DIZ.\n\no It will inform the user of how much byte credit is being added each time\n  (s)he has uploaded a file.\n\no Looks a lot nicer :).\n\no Will Switch to the upload area automatically (So no more pressing A and\n  selecting 1/etc.).\n\no Will scan for File_Id.diz''s in files using standard file.cfg faster\n  than TransAmiga.\n\no Will look for afterul.trans in BBS:REXX which will be executed _AFTER_\n  all the file description entering has taken place, if it exists.\n\no Will detect a local logon and use C:Requestfile or String entering\n  for local file uploads (multiple/single).\n\no Spews out loads of nice statistics after upload(s) :-).\n\no SysOp definable time bonus.\n\no Creates a tempfile in T: containing parsable data for external\n  programmes.\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "REQUIR_UPL" "Upl - System Requirements - (C) S.Gillibrand 1996 - Digital Design"\n\nSystem Requirements\n+-----------------+\n\n1) An Amiga ;-)    <Why is it EVERY guide has this in - It''s not funny ;0>\n\n2) TransAmiga BBS Software v2.x ->\n\n4) ARexx Server Running\n\n5) The Following Commands In Your Search Path:\n\nCommand Executable         Comment\n\nRequestfile                Issued With WB\nCopy                       Issued With WB\nWait                       Issued With WB\nDelete                     Issued With WB\nExecute                    Issued With WB (Auto-Resident With KS 2.0+)\nInfo                       Issued With WB (Auto-Resident With KS 2.0+)\nDFree                      Inside The FList Archive (Free From Copyright)\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "INSTAL_UPL" "Upl - How To Install Upl - (C) S.Gillibrand 1996 - Digital Design"\n\nHow Do I Install Upl?\n+---------------------+\n\nFollow these easy steps and you''ll have no problems.\n\n1) Enter a CLI and do the following:\n\n[.]-AmigaShell                                                     [ ][ ]\n\nSYS:> Cd <Where you unarced Upl to>\nRam:> Cd UPL\nRam:Upl> Copy rexx/#? bbs:rexx\n	Upl.trans..copied\nRam:Upl> Copy docs/#? bbs:docs\n	Upl.guide..copied\nRam:FList> Copy c/#? C:\n	DFree..copied\n\n                                                                      [ ]\n\n2) Edit BBS:CONFIGS/File.RX to include\n   an entry for Upl something like this:\n\n   U Upload Files          10 -------X Upl.Trans\n\n\n   **Important: Don''t forget to replace the old ''u'' with a ''.'' and to put the\n     access level up to 256!**\n\n   Read the TransAmiga manual for more info.\n\n3) Edit Upl.Trans and change the variables to suite your own\n   needs.\n\n   See @{"Variables" Link "VARIABLES_UPL"}\n\n4) Finished :-)\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "USAGE!_UPL" "Upl - Usage - (C) S.Gillibrand 1996 - Digital Design"\n\nUsage\n+---+\n\nSelf explanatory really!\n\nWhen a user is online, if they select to run Upl then it will run and\nfunction as it was made to, which is to replace the standard upload function\nof TransAmiga.\n\nYou could of course locally logon and try out it''s extensive local upload\nfeatures :-)\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "BUGS!!_UPL" "Upl - Known Bugs - (C) S.Gillibrand 1996 - Digital Design"\n\nKnown Bugs\n+--------+\n\nNone.\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "HISTOR_UPL" "Upl - History - (C) S.Gillibrand 1996 - Digital Design"\n\nHistory\n+-----+\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\nUpl - S.Gillibrand 1996 - Digital Design\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n01-Nov-95\nv0.00  -+- ** STARTED PROGRAMMING ** -+-\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n...Endless Beta''s :-) <Hello Tom :-)>\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n03-Feb-96\nv1.0  -+- ** First Public Release ** -+-\n\n-----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n	---Eof.\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "AUTHOR_UPL" "Upl - How To Contact The Author - (C) S.Gillibrand 1996 - Digital Design"\n\nHow To Contact The Author\n+-----------------------+\n\nPlease do contact me for @{"Bug Reports" Link "BUGS!!_UPL"} or @{"Improvement" Link "HISTOR_UPL"} ideas that you have.\n\nYou can contact me via the following methods:\n\n\nBBS:\n Digital Dreams Amiga BBS UK - 44-1772-454995 - 24 Hours\n\nNETMAIL:\n 2:250/602.0\n\nE-MAIL:\n [email removed]\n    [email removed]\n\nSNAIL MAIL:\n Stuart Gillibrand,\n 8, Thornton Drive,\n Farington Moss,\n Leyland,\n Preston,\n Lancashire.\n PR5 3QH\n ENGLAND\n\n\nDon''t hesitate to contact me no matter how trivial the matter.\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "DESIGN_UPL" "Upl - The Famous Digital Design! - (C) S.Gillibrand 1996 - Digital Design"\n\nWhat/Who is Digital Design\n+------------------------+\n\nDigital Design is a group of people who code all types of programmes for BBSs\naround the world, TransAmiga, DLG, Xeno, ANY Basically.\n\nIt was founded by @{"Stuart Gillibrand" Link "AUTHOR_UPL"} in February 1996.\n\n\n         President: Stuart Gillibrand - [email removed]\n         Vice President: Jamie Prince - [email removed]\n\nProgrammers:                                       ANSI Artists:\n Stuart Gillibrand                                  Stuart Gillibrand\n Jamie Prince                                       Jamie Prince\n\n\nDocumentation writers:                             Ideas:\n Stuart Gillibrand                                  Stuart Gillibrand\n Jamie Prince                                       Jamie Prince\n\n\nIf you would like to join Digital Design as a Programmer, Doc Writer, Artist\nor Idea Conceptor (?!) then contact @{"ME" Link "AUTHOR_UPL"}.\n\nWe ONLY accept programming in the languages:\n\nArexx, C, E and ASM (:-)).\n\nYou will need to show us an example of your skill if you wish to join, which\nboth Jamie and I will look over before contacting you.\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "VARIABLES_UPL" "Upl - Varibles Rundown - (C) S.Gillibrand 1996 - Digital Design"\n\nListed here are the variables at the top of the Upl.Trans file and how to use them:\n\n---[Unarcd]--\n\nTemplate: unarcd=<path>\nExample : unarcd="T:"\nUsage   : FULL Path of temporary directory for Upl.\n\n---[Descln]---\n\nTemplate: descln=<integer>\nExample : descln=10\nUsage   : Maximum number of lines a user can enter for 1 file description.\n\n---[MaxDiz]---\n\nTemplate: maxdiz=<integer>\nExample : maxdiz=15\nUsage   : Maximum number of lines taken from FILE_ID.DIZ as description.\n\n---[UplDev]---\n\nTemplate: upldev=<device>\nExample : upldev="BBS:"\nUsage   : Actual DEVICE of upload drive (BBS:Uploads/Line0/ would be "BBS:").\n\n---[Switch]---\n\nTemplate: switch=<integer>\nExample : switch=1\nUsage   : Area number to switch to if user doesn''t have access to current.\n\n--[Logging]---\n\nTemplate: logging=<boolean>\nExample : logging=1\nUsage   : Log to TransAmiga.Log? - Boolean [True/False] 0=No, 1=Yes.\n\n--[UlBonus]---\n\nTemplate: ulbonus=<integer>\nExample : ulbonus=2\nUsage   : Amount to multiply time taken to upload by;\n          Time taken to upload gets modified by this then this value\n          is ''refunded'' to the current time left online.\n          >0 = Bonus, 0 = No Bonus (Straight Refund), -1 = No Refund!\n\n@EndNode\n\n@Node "TUPLDATA_UPL" "Upl - Upl Data File Format - (C) S.Gillibrand 1996 - Digital Design"\n\nWhenever Upl is invoked and processes uploads it creates a file in T: under the\nfollowing filename:\n\nT:Upl_<BBS Line Number>.Dat\n\nThis file may be put to good use in the "AfterUl.Trans" file.\nThe format follows:\n\n(All lines preceded with a ";" aren''t in the produced file!)\n\n; Upl signature purely for authenticity.\n@-UplData\n<Files Uploaded>\n; Then for each file uploaded the following lines:\n<Filename>\n<Filepath>\n<Filesize>\n; #desc to define beginning of file description\n#desc\n<Description....>\n<Description....>\n<etc.>\n; #endesc to define end of file description\n#endesc\n<Big Description (1=Yes 0=No)>\n<File Credit Given>\n<Bytes Credit Given>\n; After the files data the following is listed:\n<Total Bytes Uploaded>\n<Total File Credit Given>\n<Total Byte Credit Given>\n<Files Available Before Next Upload>\n<Bytes Available Before Next Upload>\n<Time Taken By Upload(s) And Description Entering>\n<Time Awarded For Upload(s)>\n<Time Left On-Line Today>\n\n\nAn example of the above file follows from a local upload on my BBS:\n\nT:Upl_0.Dat\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n@-UplData\n5\nA8filecfgspam.rexx\nBBS:BBSUploads/A8filecfgspam.rexx\n756\n#desc\nAminet8 CDRom File.Cfg Spammer For TA   \n#endesc\n0\n255\n0\nA8Spam.rexx\nBBS:BBSUploads/A8Spam.rexx\n733\n#desc\nAminet8 CDRom Files.BBS/DIr Spammer For \nTA v1.2+                                \n#endesc\n0\n255\n0\nagony.gif\nBBS:BBSUploads/agony.gif\n36875\n#desc\nHand draw picture from the Party 95''    \n                                        \n                      Randall/Subs      \n#endesc\n0\n255\n0\nInstaller.doc\nBBS:BBSUploads/Installer.doc\n63788\n#desc\nCommodore Installer Documentation       \n#endesc\n0\n255\n0\nTAED.Functions\nBBS:BBSUploads/TAED.Functions\n770\n#desc\nASCII List                              \n                                        \nList of TAEd (Issued with TA) functions \nfor use by some programme somewhere :)  \n#endesc\n0\n255\n0\n102922\n1275\n0\nInfinite\nInfinite\n3\n6\n74\n\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n@EndNode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',30101,5,0,NULL,NULL,'upl10','scan',1780048813);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('upstatsr','UPSTATSR.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/UPSTATSR.LHA','upstats','XIM','upstats',NULL,NULL,NULL,'::::: > TMS < A New /X-Designer  ::::: ::     ________ _  _   _______      :: ::     \__  __// \/ \  \  ___/      ::',replace('::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\n::::: > TMS < A New /X-Designer  :::::\n::     ________ _  _   _______      ::\n::     \__  __// \/ \  \  ___/      ::\n::       /  \ /   _  \ /___  \      ::\n::       \__/ \__/ \_/ \_____/      ::\n::                                  ::\n::: UpLoad Status V1.00 RELEAS VER. ::\n::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\n','\n',char(10)),'upstats.doc',replace('                      Easy Install Doc.\n\nYou Cant Copy The Dirs To You BBS\n\nLittle Script:\n\nCopy BBS:DOORS/TMS TO YOU BBS:DOORS/\nCopy BBS:COMMANDS/BBSCMD/US.INFO TO YOU BBS:COMMANDS/BBSCMD/\n                                                AND /SYSCMD/\n\n\n          ----------------------------------------------------\n               Conding By T-SPOON/TMS FORM SUPER DANCER CDHQ\n\n      There Wil Be Soon A Releast Version  From The TMS-UPLOAD-STATS\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------\n                          TNX/GREET. To\n           ----------------------------------------------------\n\n      KLATSCH/TMS  : For Calling And For Beta Testing On The A1200\n\n\n           ----------------------------------------------------\n\n              Cal Me For Some Other Tools For All Versions Of /X..\n\n                Super Dancer CDHQ Node [1] +31-570-037-050 28k8 V34\n                Super Dancer CDHQ Node [2] +31-570-077-702 14k4 HST\n\nEnd.......\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',4013,4,0,NULL,NULL,'upstatsr','scan',1780048813);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('uptime13','UPTIME13.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/UPTIME13.LHA',NULL,'XIM','Displays uptime information',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Good For bbs''s etc',replace('Displays uptime information                 \nGood For bbs''s etc                          \n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,8072,5,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048813);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('usehydra','USEHYDRA.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/USEHYDRA.LHA','hydracom','XIM','hydracom',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,replace(' \n','\n',char(10)),'HYDRACOM.DOC',replace(replace('\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n                         HydraCom Version 1.00\r\n\r\n                    A sample implementation of the\r\n              HYDRA Bi-Directional File Transfer Protocol\r\n\r\n                        HydraCom was written by\r\n              Arjen G. Lentz, LENTZ SOFTWARE-DEVELOPMENT\r\n             COPYRIGHT (C) 1991-1993; ALL RIGHTS RESERVED\r\n\r\n                  The HYDRA protocol was designed by\r\n            Arjen G. Lentz, LENTZ SOFTWARE-DEVELOPMENT and\r\n                       Joaquim H. Homrighausen\r\n             COPYRIGHT (C) 1991-1993; ALL RIGHTS RESERVEDINSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('usgd_105','USGD_105.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/USGD_105.LHA','INSTALL','XIM','INSTALL',NULL,NULL,'USGD','\_____ USG DESCRIPTION STANDARD v1.05 _____/ A description standard with several MAJOR enhancements over the FILE_ID.DIZ standard.',replace('====== Users Standards Group Presents ======\n\_____ USG DESCRIPTION STANDARD v1.05 _____/\n\n A description standard with several MAJOR\nenhancements over the FILE_ID.DIZ standard.\nFeatures among many other things support for\nmultiple languages in the same description.\nAlso sports a keyword system for checking\nuseful information such as version, author,\nlanguages supported (nice to know if it is\na german only ware or not) and much more...\n IF YOU WANT TO STAY AHEAD, USE THIS NOW!!!\n','\n',char(10)),'USG_Desc.doc',replace('\n\n\n\n\n\n                           - Users Standards Group -\n\n\n                         Standard for file description\n\n\n\n                           Version 1.05, Release 1.0\n                               Updated: 16/08/94\n\n\n\n\n\n                                 Public Release\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n                     Copyright ©1994, Users Standards Group\n                              All rights reserved\nINSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('usmsg203','USMSG203.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/USMSG203.LHA',NULL,'XIM','sonnencreme.exe','2.03','P0T-NOoDLE',NULL,'-------------------------------------------- User-Message door. (NOT a wall -> Displays one large, editable message).',replace('UserMsg v2.03 by P0T-NOoDLE\n--------------------------------------------\nUser-Message door. (NOT a wall -> Displays \none large, editable message).\n* Pseudo Full-screen editor (sizes by users \n  # lines/screen)\n* Optionally Auto-Centre or rainbow-colour \n  each line.\n* Good for announcements or just for users \n  to leave fun message.\n','\n',char(10)),'usermsg.doc',replace('Usermsg door for AmiExpress!!  "OH NO NOT ANOTHER ONE" well when I\nfirst wrote and release it there was only a lame WALL door out so shut\nup!! Anyhow mine doesn''t have the problem a lot of reacent doors have of\nlooking like dog shit!...\n\nInstallation is simple as shit. Edit the top of USERMSG.REXX to alter\nthe output file. The rest is as normal and I''m not explaining how\nto run a BBS, you should know that!.\n\nIf you wanna see what the output looks like before you waste that time\ninstalling it, look in ATX_UTILS and type USERMSG.DOOR or whatever...\n\nSorry that the ARexx is unreadble but its easier to update when its\nmade modular (Well sort of modular!). IF your some paranoid idiot, search\nfor the words FORMAT or DELETE or USERDATA or whatever, you wont find any\nshit in there... Or replace every ";" with a CR... Uptoyou!\n\n\n\nHistory:-\n\nv2 (I think) Released with P0T-TRIX.DMS\nv2.03 - this one - No works out the size of the user''s screen using what\n        they''ve set their lines/screen to.\n        Also fixed something... FUck I dont remember... Who cares???\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',7883,5,0,NULL,NULL,'usmsg203','scan',1780048821);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('usrsdl','USRSDL.LZX','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/USRSDL.LZX',NULL,'XIM','!Kurwa·Fuck!',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,'auto-added',318626,0,0,NULL,NULL,'usrsdl','scan',1780048821);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('usx_qus1','USX-QUS1.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/USX-QUS1.LHA',NULL,'XIM','_______ _____________ _______________ _ ___.',NULL,'tESTAMENT/uSX!','USX','\_ | | |__ | _ | _ _/ \_ __| _ | _ | | | _/| || | | | | | __| _ | __|__ | | | | | |_| |1| || | | | | | _ | | |/_/| | | | | | | | __|9|',replace('_______ _____________ _______________ _ ___.\n\_ | | |__ | _ | _ _/ \_ __| _ | _ | | | _/|\n|| | | | | | __| _ | __|__ | | | | | |_| |1|\n|| | | | | | _ | | |/_/| | | | | | | | __|9|\n|| | | | | | | | | |   | | | | | | | | | |9|\n|| __| __|_| |_| |_|   |__ |__ |_| |_|_| |5|\n||_| |_|   |_| |_|       |_| |_| |_|-Ra!_| |\n`---------------( Presents )---------------:\n:     uSX!-qUEST v1.0 bY tESTAMENT/uSX!    |\n|  New User Quest Door For Ami/S!-Express  |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'uSX!-qUEST.doc',replace('\n                    ___     __     ______ _____  ____\n                  _/ l \  _/ l     \_ __//  _  \/  _ \\n                  \_ |  \ \_ |___  /  l_/    __/   l_ \\n                  /  |   \/  |   \/     \   _  \   _/  \\n                 /   |    \  |    \      \  l   \  l    \\n                 \________/_______/______/__|___/__|____/\n\n                    ____    ___     _.      __ ____.____\n                  _/ ___) _/ _ \  _/ l__  _(__)\   |   /\n                  \___  \ \_ l  \ \_ __ \ \_  \ \_   _/\n                  /  l   \/  |   \/  l   \/    \/  _  \\n                 /   |    \  |    \  |    \     \  l   \\n                 \________/_______/__|____/_____/__|___/\n                                                   -Ra \n\n                              P R E S E N T S \n \n \n   A new production that will change the face of computing. A tool that \n   will revolutionise the world of bbs''ing. Never again shall we all be\n   victims to the creatures we refer to as ''new user'' or to be put more\n   formally ''lamers''. The world has found a solution and the path to it\n   can be found with the simple installation of a new tool.....\n \n   First there was the television set. Then the television set begat the\n   Simpsons (tm). The Simpsons (tm) then begat the X-Files (©1993 Fox TV)\n   and later on ,with the addition of many intense hours of hard work and\n   sweat (NOT!.. the fuckin door is coded in ARexx so I''ll spare you all\n   the bullshit :)), came a new user quest door called:\n \n                   .-----------------------------------.\n                   | uSX!-qUEST v1.0 bY tESTAMENT/uSX! |\n                   `-------------------------.  ©1995  |\n                                             `---------''\n \nFeatures:\n---------\n*  Config file to enter New User Questions and number of lines you wish\n   each question to be answered in...\n \n*  Saves user''s answers in a text file for sysop reference...\n \n*  Checks to see if an answer file for a new user already exists and if \n   it finds it (meaning the user was deleted on their first application)\n   it will then display a text file to them (Deleted.txt) telling them to\n   piss off and then drop carrier on them.. The text file is optional.\n \n*  Optional choice of using a header file to make the door look sweet and\n   sexy.. This is optional..\n \n*  Forces a new user to write a message to the sysop once they have finished\n   filling out the questions...\n \n \nRequirements:\n-------------\n*  Ummm.. An AMiGA is a good start...\n \n*  AmiExpress v2.0 and above or the mega-lame S!-Express (sorry sysops)\n \n*  WorkBench 2.0 and above (if ya using any earlier version of Workbench\n   you wont have much fun installing a door ie. most WONT work...\n \n*  A brain and the intelligence level needed in order to successfully \n   install a door.. (this is the most important i think!)\n \n*  RexxMast being run in your startup-sequence or user-startup...(duh!)\n \n*  Umm.. If I''ve forgotten something then sue me.. You should have no \n   need to read doc''s... you are a sysop for christ''s sake :)\n \n \nInstallation:\n-------------\n1. Copy the icon from the Commands/BBSCmd directory in this archive into \n   your BBS:Commands/BBSCmd directory...\n \n2. Copy the uSX!-qUEST directory thats in the Doors directory of the archive\n   into your DOORS: directory and ya set... \n \n3. Configure the uSX-qUEST.cfg file to your needs.. this wil be explained in\n   detail below so be patient!\n \n4. Edit your Node<x>/Join.txt file and stick in the following MCI sequence:\n\n   ~\n   ~CC_Quest\n   \n   And that should do it.. so now it gets called and all.... you should \n   know this shit by now... if not.. get rid of your amiga and buy a PC!\n\n5. Hit your head REALLY HARD on the nearest wall and go learn how to use a\n   computer.. you shouldn''t need to read this shit if your a sysop!\n \n6. You want more info??? well the fucker should be working.. if it aint its\n   something YOU have done wrong so dont blame the door...\n \n7. After installing and using the door... if you find ANY bugs or problems \n   in this door OR even an idea to make it even better then mail me on any \n   DECENT oz bbs or call pERPETUAL dECAY on +61-2-509-552 and mail me there.\n \n8. You also have the option of including a header file to smarten up the \n   door''s look.. this header file MUST be placed in the DOORS:uSX!-qUEST\n   directory and called Header.txt\n \n9. Another option is a text/ansi file to be displayed to a user if they\n   are found to be deleted with an answer file existing.. this file should\n   be placed in the same place as discussed above but named Deleted.txt. It\n   is of course optional and if the file ''Deleted.txt'' is not found the door\n   will display its own message telling the user to piss off etc etc....\n \n                      \n \nConfiguration File (uSX!-qUEST.cfg):\n------------------------------------\n \nIts all pretty simple really... you MUST have the file named as\nuSX!-qUEST.cfg and its gotta be located in the DOORS:uSX!-qUEST directory\notherwise you wont have any luck in getting this door to work....\nAnyways.. have a look at the 2 example configuration files supplied called\nuSX!-qUEST.cfg1 and uSX!-qUEST.cfg2 and just edit them to your liking..\nThe first config file is the same as the second just the second has ansi\ncodes in the questions in order to make the door look sexy.. experiment and\nyou''ll get it looking real nice...\nAnyways.. heres how the config file should be configured:\n \n1. First few lines in the config file are just plain numbers that represent\n   the number of lines you wish each question to be answered in.. Like 2\n   will give the user two lines to answer the question in...\n \n2. After that you MUST end the line number settings with the line\n   [SETTINGS_END] otherwise everything will shit itself...\n \n3. Then comes the main bit.. the questions.. each line after [SETTINGS_END] \n   will be the questions the door asks the user.. here you may put in ansi\n   codes or whateva ya like.. it''ll all work.. as the door simply reads in\n   the lines string by string and spits it out at the user one at a time...\n \n4. When you have done all this simply end it all of with the line\n   [QUEST_END] .. and thats about it for the config file... Just look at the\n   sample configuration files supplied with this archive to get an idea of\n   what the door expects....Remember that the config file must be names\n   uSX!-qUEST.cfg (it aint case-sensitive!).....\n  \n\nFuture Enhancements:\n--------------------\n* Door will be FULLY coded in either SAS/C or AmigaE once i get the time to\n  bother with it all...\n \n* Totally icon driven with the use of tooltypes etc etc...\n \n* The option to FORCE questions to be answered so a user cannot just hit\n  enter and skip answering a certain question (already working on this).\n \n* Automatic mailing to Sysops of choice notifying them of the new user and\n  telling them to check the new user''s answers instead of the user having\n  to write mail to the sysop...\n\n* If ya got any more ideas for me or find the usual fuckup in the door then\n  mail me on any DECENT Australia board and i''ll get back to you or call my\n  board pERPETUAL-dECAY on +61-2-509-552....\n \n \nGreets And Other Goodies:\n-------------------------\nJaguar Speed/uSX!   -    Great Co-Sysop and buddie.. Stay cool man...\ncARCASS!            -    A man of GREAT wisdom (NOT!)..  \nbuttkikker          -    Where the fuck ya been? Enjoying the QLD sun?!?!\nSmaSh!/uSX!         -    We all know how Telstra sux man... take it easy\n                         on the STD calls then :)\ndEMOLiTiON/dVS      -    One or OZ''s greatest sysops.. stay cool and dont\n                         become like a lot of other fuckwit sysops that \n                         come and go all the time...\naCID kID/HNY       -     Thanx for the ascii''s... your a great artist...\n\nAnd thanx to all the thousands of others i forgot to thank above.. you know\nwho you all are (fuck.. this sounds worse than a CD thank you list)...\n\n\nMusic Support:\n--------------\nMachine Head, Smashing Pumpkins, Pearl Jam, Obituary, Napalm Death, Carcass,\nFear Factory, Slayer, TumbleWeed, Iron Maiden, Alice In Chains, Cannibal\nCorpse, Nirvana (RIP), MegaDeth, My Dying Bride, Morbid Angel, Metallica, \nPantera, Sepultura, SoundGarden, Testament..... any more?\n\nAnyways here comes the add:\n\n    |-------| pERPETUAL dECAY |-----------------| +61-2-509-552 |-------|\n                                                                     \n                          -÷[ uLTRa-sONiX! hQ ]÷-                   ___\n    ______________________  __________________________.---_______  /  l\n  _/ ____  \_ __________  \/ ____  \_ ________  ____  |   \_ ___ \/   |\n  l  \______/ _)--._ __/  /  \______/ _)--._/    \/   |   l   \/  \   |___\n  |       l        / \    \_      l        /      \   |   |  _/    \  :   \\n  |_______|_______/___\    /______|_______/\______/_______|__\     /______/\n                       \  /                                   \___/\n                        \/  m!^dG         _________                        \n     _______  ____________________________\       /  \n    _\____  \/   _______ ________ ___ \    \_    / sYSOP: tESTAMENT/uSX!\n  _/    l/   \_  _)--.l   l/  \_   \/  \   _/  _/                          \n  \    _/     /       /   |    /  _/    \  l   l   sTAFF: jAGUAR sPEED/uSX!\n   \___\     /_______/\_______/___\     /______|          dEMOLiTiON/dVS\n        \___/                      \___/                  SmaSh!/uSX!\n \n             aMiGA · aMi-eXPRESS · hPAC · rEQUESTS · uSX!-diSTRO\n           rUNNiNG /X v4.12r oN aN a3000 wiTH oVER 1.3 giGS oNLiNE\n                                                                       \n    |-------| pERPETUAL dECAY |-----------------| +61-2-509-552 |-------|\n  \n\nSeeya''s!!!!\n\n                                                      -tESTAMENT/uSX!\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,8608,2,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048821);
