INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('vdstat11','VDSTAT11.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/VDSTAT11.LHA','RPStart','REXX','VDFree By </an /)amme [ REALEASE 3 ]','1.1','</an',NULL,'·<>· cOCKTAILS BBS  -  /X Tools Support ·<>·',replace('VDFree v1.1 By </an /)amme [ REALEASE 3 ]\n·<>· cOCKTAILS BBS  -  /X Tools Support ·<>·\n','\n',char(10)),'VDStat.Doc',replace('\n                       VDStat v1.1b By </an /)amme                  \n                      ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~  \n              \n       For Any Comments Or Problems, You Can Reach Me On My Board... \n                                                                  \n         .:| DeATH RoW (416)548-8557/548-9558/548-6632/548-0240 |:.\n\n                                                                [02/27/93]\n\n  Installing\n  ~~~~~~~~~~\n First off, /X means Ami-Express for those that don''t know already. Now,\nto install the door load up the Customcommands (/X v2.2x or below) or\nBBS.CMD (/X v2.3x). Now load up the file in a text editor and all the\nfollowing:\n\n          11 Spaces In         \n          |\n----------------------------          \n*S        RM010Doors:VDStat\n----------------------------\n||        |||  |           \n||        |||  ` ''Doors:VDStat'' is the actually location of the file.\n||        |||     Make sure not to change this.\n||        |||\n||        ||` 010 Is the minimum access to use this door. Change it to what\n||        ||      you like.\n||        ||\n||        |` M For a mutilnode bbs (S For single)\n||        |\n||        ` R For an rexx type door which will use the ''Rexxdoor'' Util\n||\n|`Letter to bring the door up on the board. In this case ''S''\n|\n`-Retard Option. To Make Sure they only use ''S'' & only ''S'' to get the \ndoor to come up. If not used, things such as ''Stimpy'' and ''SA'' would\nstill bring up the door.\n\n Use the line between the lines only. The other parts are just an \nexplanation to make sure you know what each part is doing (Since no one\nwould tell me back in the days where I didn''t know what was going on!)\n\n Now copy the ''VDStat'' file to the doors: dir. You should also copy and\nuse the prefs file ''VDStat.Prefs'', but it''s not needed. More on this later.\n\n Copy the 2 rexxplus libs into your libs: dir, because the compiled doors\nneed these libraries in order to work.\n\n Also Make sure if not already to copy the ''RPStart'' file to your C dir\nand make sure your running it in the background. A good place to run it from\nis your startup so it will always be running.\n\n At this point if all things so far are in order and exist, you should be\nready to run the door.\n\n  Passwords\n  ~~~~~~~~~\n Due to some points made in security problems, you can make sure the user''s\npassword isn''t displayed. There are two ways to do this. First, by using\nthe config file and tuning it off (See Preferences & Ratings). The second\nis by way of stacking. At the menu, instead of typing ''S'', you can type\n''S N'' or ''S n'' and this will prevent your password from coming up. If you\nchoose this way, make sure you tell your users how to use it.\n\n  Preferences & Ratings\n  ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n A new option added is the rating system and the preference file. An \nexplaination of each line is as follows:\n\n The First line will allow you to keep the users password from coming up.\nA simple ''Y'' or ''N'' will do, ''Y'' will make the password come up (can prevent\nwith stacking - See Passwords) and vice versa.\n\n The Second line will allow you to select bytes or files to be used when\ndetermining the upload to download ratio for the users. ''B'' will use bytes\nand ''F'' will use files.\n\n The next 3 sections should each be seperated with a ''='' character.\n\n The first section will allow you to set the upload to download ratio \nmessages for the users. The number you use will be the number of\ndownloads against 1 and then after the number will come the message to\nbe used if that quota is met. For example:\n\n10 Total Leech\n\nIf the user is found to have 10 downloads for every 1 upload this message\nwill be used (Total Leech).\n\n3 Could Be Worse\n\nIf the user is found to have 3 downloads for every 1 upload this message\nwill be used (Could Be Worse). Etc.\n If an exact match isn''t found, the door will always round down, so if\nthe door has only up to 5, and the user has a 1/10 ratio then it will use\nthe entry for 5.\n\n NOTE: The door can compare either files or bytes. (See above)\n\n The second section deals with access. Users will be matched up with \nthe access listed and the respective message will be used. If an exact\nmatch isn''t found, it will round down in the same manner as the\nRatio (See Above). Some examples are:\n\n100 Special User \n\nUsers with access of 100 will have the message ''Special User''\n\n The third section deals with conferences. This time an EXACT match \nmust be found or a ''?'' will be used.  The users current conference\nlevel will be matched with the ones listed in the prefs file. Note that\nif you use ''_''s in the accounts, use them in the door as it needs an\nexact match to use the message for it. Example:\n\nXXXX_____ Normal Areas\n\nUsers with this access in their account will have a Normal Areas Message.\n\n NOTE: Make sure you seperate each different part with a ''='' character so\n       it will know what to use for what.  This is no limit as to how many\n       entries are used for the ratio,access and conf sections.\n\n See the included Prefs File for an example of how to set it up.\n\n If you decide not to use the prefs file, the door will default to using\nthe following setup:\n\nY    (Y/N) Show Password\nB    (B/F) Bytes Or Files For Ratio\n=======1 Up For Every Down=========\n10 Total Leech\n5 See The U Key?\n4 Try An Upload\n3 Could Be Worse\n2 Not Too Bad\n1 Nice And Even\n0 Awesome Work\n==============Access===============\n10 New User\n50 Normal User\n100 Special User \n200 CoSysop       \n255 Sysop \n============Conferences============\nX________ Holding  Only  \nXXXX_____ Normal Areas  \nXXXXX____ Special Areas \nXXXXXX___ Group Member\nXXXXXXXXX You Got It All\n\n  Statistics\n  ~~~~~~~~~~\n At this point I''ll give a brief explanation of what each of the stat means \nso they''re will be no confusion as to what they are for.\n\n --Board Statistics---------------------------------------------------------\n\n BBS   : The name of the BBS.\n Sysop : The name of the sysop.\n Nodes : The current number of nodes running on the BBS. Inactive nodes\n         will not count, only currently active nodes. So if you were\n         to have a 5 node BBS, but 2 of the nodes are inactive at the\n         time then it would say you have 3 nodes.\n /X    : Current version of ami-express the board is being run on.\n     \n --User Statistics---------------------------------------------------------\n\n User        : Name of the user.\n Location    : Location/Group of the user.\n Slot        : Slot number of the user (The number he has in the accounts)\n Conferences : The conferences that the user has access to. They will be\n               matched up with the ''X''s below the numbers of them. Eg.\n \n               123456789\n               X_X__XX__  This user would have access to conferences 1,3,6,7\n\n Downloads   : Number of downloads the user has done.\n Bytes       : Amount of bytes the user has downloaded.\n Uploads     : Number of uploads the user has done.\n Bytes       : Amount of bytes the user has uploaded.\n\n NOTE: The Bytes to the right of the downloads is the amount of bytes he\n       has downloaded, and likewise for the uploads. This amount will be\n       rounded off in K (1k = 1024 bytes).\n\n Expert Mode : If the user has the expert mode on or off. A Y or N will be\n               used in each case respectivly.\n Time Limit  : Daily time limit for the user.\n Time Used   : How much time the user has already used today.\n Time Left   : Daily time limit left for the day.\n\n NOTE: Time limits will be in minutes.\n\n Access      : Access level of the user.\n Password    : Password for the user.\n Messages    : Number of messages the user has written.\n Ratio       : The ratio of the user. A ''DIS'' means the user has a \n               disabled ratio (0). \n Phone       : The users phone number.\n Calls       : The total number of calls the user has made to the board.\n Last On     : The date that the user was last on. \n Node        : The current node that the user is calling on.\n Baud        : The online baud rate of the user.\n Length      : The screen length of the user (The number of lines to be\n               displayed before a [Pause] prompt is displayed).\n Conf. In    : The number of the conference the user is currently in.\n\n --System Statistics--------------------------------------------------------\n\n Total System Calls   : The total number of calls the board has ever had.\n Percent Of All Calls : The percent of total system calls that the user has\n                        made.\n Time                 : The Current Time Of Day.\n\n  --Ratings-----------------------------------------------------------------\n\n Ratio  : Displays ratio rating matching the users \n Access : Displays access rating matching the users \n Confs  : Displays conference rating matching the users\n\n  Callerslog\n  ~~~~~~~~~~\n As with all my doors, the callerslog is used in this door. A simple line\nwill be added to the callerslog showing at that time the user used the\nstat door. The line is as follows:\n\nVan Damme Used VDStat v1.1b At 1:29PM\n\n  History\n  ~~~~~~~\n v1.0  : -First Public Release. No Known Bugs Or Problems.\n v1.1b : -Fixed Bug That Forgot To Round Off Byte Sizes Lower Then 1 \n         -Added Seperate Perference File\n         -Added Option To Not Display Password (In Prefs)\n         -Added Stacking Option To Not Display Password\n         -Add A Rating System (Configurable From Prefs File)\n         -Changed Colors Of BBS Stat And Ratings\n\n  Greets\n  ~~~~~~\n Well that''s the end of another of my doors. I made this door cause I didn''t\nreally like the ones that were around the boards.  As always I update my\nutils frequently so stay tuned for more and better updates of this program.\nTill then....\n\n Special thanks for Denon for the idea to add the password protection, and\nfor the rating system.  \n\n And thanks to everyone that called my board to say they liked my VDEdit\nprogram.  You guys make it worthwhile :). Stay tuned for a further update\nlater this week. And also stay tuned for the Public release of VDDate once\nI finish Beta Testing it (Thanks Robster & Denon For The Help). \n\n And a few greets to...\n\n Skol/THG - Call again soon. Always nice to chat with ya.\n Nzo/Dual Crew - Ah.. I talk to you too much already. :)\n Nameless - Thanks for the greet in your NodeAct door.\n Nosferatu - Will we see a NosNuke to work with VDColorDir ever???\n Pot-Noodle/Anthrox - Great Last caller util. \n PMF/Minstry - You and Nzo should get married. You act like you already are!\n /\KiRA/Minstry - I''d call ya more if I could afford it! \n Iron Eagle/Tarkus Team - Still waiting for that call dude.\n MAGNUS/LSD - Greets friend! Everyone is going to LSD nowadays!\n mUb/LSD - Greets to you too dude. Thanks for the support!\n Phideaux!/LSD - Mabey someone will crack Perfect General one day!\n Ceejay/WTi - Greets Mate. Save me a brewskie!\n Rambo/Fairlight - You liked your last greet eh? Here''s another. \n Elf-Co/Alpha Flight - One day I''m going to mail you something!\n Defcon - Seen any good cars blow up lately?!?\n Ice Cube/Anthrox - Long time no talk dude. Call sometime!\n PhARAOh - Hiya dude. See the board''s getting better all the time!\n Zen - Always my best friend around! :)\n Echo/LSD - Hope all that midi stuff works for ya.\n Kidlat - I expect you to be using this door! :)\n Esskayare - You just love to chat with everyone don''t ya.\n Blade/Prime - I take it your following Nzo with that 2400. :)\n Zandor/LSD - See, just to prove my point. Another one joins LSD. About\n              me next dudes.\n Squid/Prime - You have good taste since you run my utils.\n Cragar/Prime - A greet for my new found friend. I shall talk with ya soon.\n Illicit Trader - Thanks for the console support. I really need it!\n Gilby/Minstry - You should call me more!\n AxeL - Greets To My Newfound Friend. \n\n                 Send greets if you want them back!\n \n And those that I know but forgot, and also those users that still value\nfriendship over all else, and of course to all you other ami-express door\nwriters out there. Drop me a line on my board sometime, I''d be glad to help\ntest your utils or give you the latest updates on mine.\n\n Remember to call my board. I need some console users badly.. and amiga\nusers are always more then welcome!\n\n And I''m still groupless.. Any group willing to take me on please get ahold\nof me. I like releasing my doors under a group name. They get spread faster!\n\n                                   Later dudes.. Till then!\n\n                                                    -Van Damme (TW,SA)\n','\n',char(10)),'{"ACCESS":"=============="}',NULL,106687,2,0,NULL,NULL,'vdstat11','scan',1780048821);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ves_b_s1','VES-B&S1.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/VES-B&S1.LHA',NULL,'XIM','_ ___ ___ ___ _   _   _ ___ _  _',NULL,'VesuVius:::|','VES','.______/_\\ _\\ _\\ _\\\ _\\ _\\\ _\\\_\\Æ§. |::::://///////////////_\ //_ ////////·//::| |::::/_ // _/////////////////////////·//:::|',replace('        _ ___ ___ ___ _   _   _ ___ _  _\n.______/_\\ _\\ _\\ _\\\ _\\ _\\\ _\\\_\\Æ§.\n|::::://///////////////_\ //_ ////////·//::|\n|::::/_ // _/////////////////////////·//:::|\n|::://////))/////_ ////////////_ /·\\//::::|\n|::/__//////__//////__//____/////··/_/:::::|\n|:PRESENTS:::::Buy&Sale v1.0 by VesuVius:::|\n·-----[ /X AIM Module +bonus release ]-----·\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,22561,5,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048821);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ves_fac1','VES-FAC1.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/VES-FAC1.LHA','REXXDOOR','XIM','REXXDOOR',NULL,'VesuVius','VES','|::::\°  __   \°  __   \°    __ \°  __   \|A |::::/   //   /  /_/   /    /  \/  /_/   /|m |:::/   //   /   _    /\___    /   _    /:|i',replace('|::::____________________________________:| \n|::::\°  __   \°  __   \°    __ \°  __   \|A\n|::::/   //   /  /_/   /    /  \/  /_/   /|m\n|:::/   //   /   _    /\___    /   _    /:|i\n|::/   //   /   //   /    /   /   //   /::|E\n|::\__//___/\__//___/\_______/\__//___/:::|x\n|::/X 3.x --[ P R E S E N T S ]-- /X 3.x::|.\n`--[Face v1.0 by VesuVius /X Shell Door]--''\n','\n',char(10)),'FACE.guide',replace('@DATABASE "Face.guide"\n@NODE MAIN "N.A.S.A : Federation of free Programmers"\n\n==============================================================================\n:::::::::::::::::::::##::##::::####::::#####::::####::::::::::::::::::::::::::\n::::AtomiX:::::::::::###:##:::##::##:::##::::::##::##:::::::::::::AtomiX::::::\n:::::::::::::::::::::######:::######:::#####:::######:::::::::::::::::::::::::\n:::::::::::::::::::::##:###:::##::##::::::##:::##::##:::::::::::::::::::::::::\n:::::::::::::::::::::##::##:::##::##:::#####:::##::##:::::::::::::::::::::::::\n==============================================================================\n\n                      Federation of free Programmers\n\n                           /X FACE  Version 1.0\n                    -----------------------------------\n                   Shell interface for AmiExpress v3.++\n   \n                         @{"    Copyright Note    " LINK COPRIGHT}\n                         @{"    Introducing       " LINK Anleitung}\n                         @{"    Installation      " LINK INSTALL }\n                         @{"    History & Changes " LINK History }\n                         @{"    Bug Report        " LINK BUG     }\n                         @{"    Greetings         " LINK DANKE   }\n                         @{"    New tools         " LINK FEATURE }\n                         @{"    Released Tools    " LINK SCHONDA\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n\n@NODE COPRIGHT\n@TITLE "Copyrighted"\n\n - All N.A.S.A Team products are FreeWare \n\n - What is the N.A.S.A Team ?! \n   it''s a Federation of free Programmers in the whole World.\n\n - AmiExpress is Copyrighted by LightSpeed Technologies\n\n - MultView is Copyrighted by Commodore\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE Anleitung\n@TITLE "INTRODUCING"\n\nConfig!\n~~~~~~~\n\n***USERNAMES_ALLOWED:\n\n        In the first part there are all users specified who have\n            axxess to the door (CASE SENSITIVE).\n\n\n***PASSWORD_COMMANDS:\n\n        In the second part there are all DOS Commands you like to\n            include. Program checks only in C: for commands.\n        You can specify a password for every command \n            you like to use. (CASE SENSITIVE)\n        Notice the '','' char between command and password.\n          Type "pass" instead a password,\n            to disable password protection for a command.\n\n        Internal zmodem commands are also optional\n\n\n***NAMES_NOT_ALLOWED:\n\n        In the last part there are all Files/Commands/Directories\n             who are not allowed to be touched in any way!(UPPERCASE)\n\n\n\ni.e.\n-----cut here --------------------\n***USERNAMES_ALLOWED:\nVesuVius\nAtomiX\nSpaceman\nStormBreaker\n***PASSWORD_COMMANDS:\n/XDOWNLOAD,pass\n/XUPLOAD,upload\n/XCLIUPLOAD,cliup\nC:LHA,lha\nC:DELETE,delete\nC:INFO,info\nC:RENAME,rename\nC:COPY,copy\nC:MOVE,move\n***NAMES_NOT_ALLOWED:\n#?\nS\nACCESS\nCOMMANDS\nVESUTILS\nSYQUEST1\nFORMAT\nDRIVE\nALL\nFORCE\nQUIET\nACP\nEXPRESS\nUSER.DATA\nUSER.KEYS\nUSER.DATA{1}\nUSER.KEYS{1}\nSTARTUP-SEQUENCE\nUSER-STARTUP\nFACE.CFG\nCALLERSLOG\n-----cut here --------------------\n\n\nZMODEM\n~~~~~~\n\nFor the time the programm runs, all used DOS commands (LIST,\n    DIR, INFO, AVAIL, DELETE) are protected.\n   Maybe that someone try to upload a customcommand \n    named as internal command.In this case zmodem skip file.\n\nThe configfile is also protected.\n\n\n\nNOTE:   To validate the devicename in the commandstring I use the\n        rexxsupport function SHOWLIST(). But this returns only the\n        volumenames (Workbench:, Program:, ...), and not the name of\n        the units. (DH0:, DH1:, DH2:, ...) So ''CD'' volumes by name.\n        Assigns can ''CD'' normally.\n        Because invalid volumename will pop up requester on WorkBench:\n                 "PLEASE INSERT VOLUME ... IN ANY DRIVE."\n                  ... and noboby at home to cancel ...iihh)\n\n  The advantage is, if you use other device names than the unit names\n        just protect ''INFO'' with password to make strange ''CD'' handle more difficult.\n  Also you can add volumenames without ":" extension and other directorynames\n       to NAMES_NOT_ALLOWED to restrict ''CD'' handle.\n\n\nWhat?\n~~~~~\n    Face opens a door to your DOS. There are several commands available.\n\n        Syntax commands:\n        CD      -   CD <dir>, CD /, CD :\n        TYPE    -   TYPE <path|name>\n        LIST    -   List [<dir>] [FILES|DIRS] \n        DIR     -   Dir [<dir>] [FILES|DIRS] \n        MAKEDIR -   MAKEDIR <path|name>\n        DELETE* -   DELETE <path|name>\n        INFO*   -   Info [<dev>] \n        AVAIL   -   Avail [CHIP|FAST]\n        DATE    -   Date\n\n\n        Zmodem commands:\n        D*   - Download from Shell\n        U*   - Upload\n        UP*  - Upload to Shell\n      \n      XTra*  - Extract LHA file to RAM:\n               (need ''C:Lha'')\n\n  NOTE: Commands with ''*'' are available for password protection\n\n\n        Other DOS commands available in config\n\n	Writing shell sessions in callerslog\n\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE HISTORY\n@TITLE "History"\n\n  History\n  ~~~~~~~\n  Version 1.0    - First Release\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE INSTALL\n@TITLE "N.A.S.A Tools - Installation"\n\n * INSTALLATION *\nHow?\n~~~~\n	- Copy Face.rexx to Doors:VESUtils/    \n	- Copy Face.cfg to Doors:VESUtils/\n        - Copy Face.info to BBS:Commands/BBSCmd/\n        - Specify password in module icon.\n        - Copy rexxplus.lib to LIBS:\n        - Copy rexxplslib.library to LIBS:\n        - Copy RPStart to C:\n          (Modify Startup-Sequence "C:RPStart")\n        - Copy Rexxdoor to BBS:Utils/\n\n        - Type ''?'' on prompt for commands\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE BUG\n@TITLE "Bug Reports"\n\n BUG REPORT & SUGGESTIONS\n ------------------------\n\n   It''s possible that a mistake will occur.... nobody is perfect.\n   If you have any suggestions or comments please leave a message\n   to the programmer or Sysop on the N.A.S.A Headquarter\n\n   For Bug Reports or Suggestion''s call our BBS\n\n     N.A.S.A HQ  +49-5723-74340  United Germany\n     ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯  ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯\n\n   Traders are Welcome !!\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE FEATURE\n@TITILE "In the next time"\n\n  New Tools in the next Time.\n  \n  1. User Information V 1.05\n\n             written totally in C , complete new\n             styling .\n             coded by AtomiX / N.A.S.A Team Leader\n\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n\n@NODE DANKE\n@TITLE "Greetings to the following guy''s"\n\n      Written and tested on A2000c/030 and AmiExpress v3.12\n       (Maybe running on /X v2.xx too, but its not tested) \n\n                 //\n     Thanks to \X/ Amiga for being the best computer ever !\n\n\nThat''s all folks ...something forgotten ?!\n                      ...any GOOD ideas ??\n                        Lets talk about !!\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE SCHONDA\n@NODE TITLE "Released Tools"\n\n  Already released Tools from the N.A.S.A Team\n\n  PW Fail            V 1.0\n  Free Download Door V 1.0 , V 1.1\n  Logon Watchdog     V 1.0\n  User Information   V.1.03 , V 1.04\n  Door Menu          V 1.0 , V 1.1\n  Bulletin Viewer    V 1.1 , V 1.2\n  Face               V 1.0\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',118298,5,0,NULL,NULL,'nvx_rem5','scan',1780048821);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ves_dg11','VES_DG11.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/VES_DG11.LHA',NULL,'XIM','Danish_Bacon.exe',NULL,'VesuVius','VES','|::::\°  __   \°  __   \°    __ \°  __   \|A |::::/   //   /  /_/   /    /  \/  /_/   /|m |:::/   //   /   _    /\___    /   _    /:|i',replace('|::::____________________________________:| \n|::::\°  __   \°  __   \°    __ \°  __   \|A\n|::::/   //   /  /_/   /    /  \/  /_/   /|m\n|:::/   //   /   _    /\___    /   _    /:|i\n|::/   //   /   //   /    /   /   //   /::|E\n|::\__//___/\__//___/\_______/\__//___/:::|x\n|::/X 3.x --[ P R E S E N T S ]-- /X 3.x::|.\n`---[ WatchDog v1.0 by VesuVius /XDoor]---''\n','\n',char(10)),'WatchDog.DOC',replace('                  ____________________________________\n                  \**********************************/\n                   \*  ._    /_ __   _   ·/   __.  */\n                    \*   \  |_ |_ | | \  || ||_   */\n                     \*   \/|____||_|  \/||_|__| */\n                      \**************************/\n                       \*                      */\n                        \*      release       */\n                         \********************/ \n                          \*                */\n                           \*  AmiExpress  */\n                            \*    DOOR    */\n                             \*          */\n                              \*  v3.x  */\n                               \*      */\n                                \******/\n                                 \****/\n                                  \**/\n                                   \/\n\n                    LOGON WATCHDOG  Version 1.0  DOCS\n                 ---------------------------------------\n \n\nWhat?\n~~~~~\n\nLOGON WATCHDOG is a packet of three ARexx scripts handle NewUser\n               and PWfail activities on node.\n\n	PWFail.rexx    - Password fail door. Force the user to\n                         write some text about his password fail.\n\n	NoNewUser.rexx - No new user door. New users can write and\n                         receive messages, without an account.\n\n	WatchDog.rexx  - Partly a tiny message base to receive and send\n                         messages to new users.\n                       - Shows also all PWFail messages\n\n\nRequirements:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n	AmiExpress v3.x\n\n        Assigned ENV: and ENVARC:\n\n        ECHO, DELETE, TYPE and COPY command in C:\n\n\nHow to install?\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n- You need a Bull to launch the WatchDog. The Bull number should\n  be the same as the SysOp security level. i.e. Bull255.txt\n  If this Bull still in use then add the following MCI command in front\n  of your own : \n\n~CC_WatchDog\n\n\n- Copy NONEWUSERS to your speciefied screen directory or to every Node\n  directory you like to use it. The file included another MCI command\n  to launch NoNewUser every time a new user is online.\n\n\nHow to use?\n~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nAfter install, make a SysOp logon and you receive :\n\nNo password failed.....\n\nNo new User.....       \n\nThis is the normal message tells you, there is no event on logon.\n\n\nTo test the WatchDog, make a local logon and enter your BBS\nas a new user. You will prompt to write a text before /X\ndrop carrier. The text was saved to "BBS:NodeX/CallersWatchDog"\nin the node directory and also to a temp file \n"ENV:NoNewUser.msg"\n\nThen make another local logon and fail three times on password.\n(Do not use your SysOp handle)\nAll needed datas from the user saved to ENV:nnu/<username>\nThe account will drop to lower level, and then\nyou will also prompt to write a text before /X drop carrier.\nThis text will be added to the callerslog and to a temp file\n"ENV:PWFail.msg"\n\nMake a SysOp logon or type WatchDog on the main prompt to receive \nthe message from the NoNewUser door.\nUse option to delete this message, cause its only the temp file.\nThe whole message transfer is documented in "BBS:NodeX/CallersWatchDog".\nNow take the ability to write a message to the new user. He will\nreceived it on next logon. But he get no account !!\nUse the NewUser delete option to remove a specified user from the env\n\nThen you see the message from the PWFail door with the option to delete\nthe temp file.\n\n\nTo clean up from testing or for any reset, just delete the directories\n"nnu" and "nu" in ENV: and ENVARC:\n\n\n\nThis door is written and tested on A2000/030 and AmiExpress v3.12\n\n                 //\n     Thanks to \X/ Amiga for being the best computer ever !\n\n\nThat''s all folks. For questions reach me on\n\n                           NASA BBS +49 5723-74340\n\n\nGreetz to all\nsign VesuVius\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',27769,8,0,NULL,NULL,'ves_dg11','scan',1780048821);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('vlabpicx','VLABPICX.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/VLABPICX.LHA',NULL,'XIM','VLAB /X DOOR',NULL,'Eurobyte/Cocaine',NULL,'Tranfer Live Pic''s to /X Made by Eurobyte/Cocaine VERsion V0.91',replace('VLAB /X DOOR\nTranfer Live Pic''s to /X\nMade by Eurobyte/Cocaine\nVERsion V0.91\n','\n',char(10)),'VLAB.PREFS.DOC',replace('HOWDIE DUDE\n\n\nPut the Vlab-prefs file in your prefs:env-archive/Vlab\n\nBackup first Your Vlab-prefs\n\ncya      Eurobyte/Cocaine\n\n\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,3825,2,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048821);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('vn_fdup','VN_FDUP.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/VN_FDUP.LHA','dmstestutrk','XIM','ExeChecker',NULL,NULL,'VN',': _____.__/\:____   ____  ____   )/ideo    : | \__  | / \\__  \ /  _ \/ _  \  (--oo)    | :   \  | \__/  \  \  ___/ //  /   \_-/     :',replace('.------------------------------------------.\n: _____.__/\:____   ____  ____   )/ideo    :\n| \__  | / \\__  \ /  _ \/ _  \  (--oo)    |\n:   \  | \__/  \  \  ___/ //  /   \_-/     :\n|    \ : /  |  /  / /  /  /  /    /\/asty  |\n:     \_/|__|____/____/\____/ -[Presents]- :\n|__________________________________________|\n:NastyDUP DupeCheckr Replacment 100% Faster|\n|  Than ANY DUPECHECKER Complete FCHECK    |\n: Replacement  UKNOWUWANTIT  /\/asty Style |\n`------------------------------------------''\nTHi§ FIle WaS DowNLoaded aT DreAM-PHASE','\n',char(10)),'NastyDupCheck.guide',replace('@database Unnamed_Database\n@master NastyDupCheck.guide\n@remark Created with Heddley v1.1 (c) Edd Dumbill 1994\n\n@node "Main" "Main Document"\n             Another Alternative to The standard........\n\n               VideoNasty Presents @{"NastyDupCheck" link "DupCheck" 0}\n\n  No Tricks no MadAsFuk Config files just simple easy to folow\n  |)os Scripts....... DONT STOP READING What u get is.......\n\n  @{b}@{bg shine}INSTANT DupFileCheck@{ub}@{bg back} No scanning DIR(x) files\n  @{b}@{fg shadow}@{bg shine}CHECK AS UPLOAD@{ub}@{fg text}@{bg back} Not After so saves USERS @{fg shine}@{bg fill}TIME & MONEY@{fg text}@{bg back}\n\n  Requirez you TURN on 1 OPTION in the NODE(x) Icons\n\n  @{"WHY USE THIS" link "WHY" 0}----- Obvious!\n@endnode\n\n@node "DupCheck" "NastyDupCheck"\nTo use this Instead of your own Method simply RENAME (As you may not\nwant to keep my setup) your BBS:FCheck directory to sumting else Copy\nthe FCHECK directory includided in this archive into your BBS:\nDirectory replacing your old FCHECK, Thats it NastyDupCheck is\ninstalled.\n\n Now Edit the ToolTypes in your NODE(x) Directory Icons and ADD\n FILESNOTALLOWED=BBS:Fcheck/Checkers/UpLoadList\n Now when you upload a file it will be added to above filelist\n\n Adding your Dir(x) listings to UpLoadList @{"AddDirs.cli" link "AddDirs" 0} Utility\n@endnode\n\n@node "AddDirs" "AddDirs.cli"\nCD into @{b}BBS:Fcheck/Checkers/@{ub} directory\n\nin this Dir are all the Scripts & files needed to use NastyDupCheck\nalso you will find 2 Rexx programs @{b}@{u}AddDirs.rex@{ub}@{uu}x & @{b}@{u}AddFile.rex@{ub}@{uu}x\n\n@{b}@{u}AddFile.rexx@{ub}@{uu} is the rexx program that adds all new uploads into the\nuploadlist.\n\n@{b}@{u}AddDirs.rexx@{ub}@{uu} is the rexx program that adds your dir(x) files to the\nuploadlist.\n\n USAGE for AddDirs.Rexx \n Rx @{b}AddDirs.Rexx@{ub} BBS:{conference}/{Dir(X)}\n Example.. \n Rx @{b}AddDirs.Rexx BBS:Conferences/Amiga/Dir1@{ub}\n Would Add ALL files uploaded in Dir1 list into the Uploadlist BUT\n using the supplied @{b}AddDirs.CLI@{ub} Dos script to do this is easier.\n\n @{b}AddDirs.Cli@{ub} can be started like any other dos script file and should\n have its S bit set so you can start it like anyother command/program\n@endnode\n\n@node "WHY" "WHY USE THIS"\nThe number of advantages for using this are vast here i list the most\nimportant...........\n\n Because it checks AS the upload Starts or as the name of the upload\n is recieved.\n\n What will it STOP------ User list first\n\n 1-Nuked for Uploading A dup file\n 2-Time Wasted online uploding files already recieved\n 3-MONEY on length of call\n 4-Time waiting for DUPCHECKER to finish checking Dir(x) files\n\n Whys it better for sysop------\n\n 1-Never have to delete a Dup file\n 2-No dupe files in your holds saving HardDrive room\n 3-Users online for shorter periods & NO NODES recieving files\n   already recieved, some files can be as big as 2Meg and take\n   quite a long time to transfer.  My method keeps this sort of\n   wasted BBS time down to an absolute mininimum 99% of Uploads\n   will be NEW and not Old Duplicated files. RENAMES still get\n   through, SoRRY cant stop this but i have a method that im\n   working on but again this will be a DupChecker type of utility\n   that needs to scan the dir(x) files after an upload...\n 4-Users will notice that your bbs has virtualy no Duplicates and so\n   will prefer to call your bbs.\n\nSo as you can see there are lots of reasons for using this method hope\nyou find it as usefull as MySelf & Various other sysops in and around\nthe Manchester Area.\n\n I Created this Utility pack for our EXCLUSIVE Use and never intended\nto release it into the public but sysops have asked us for it as there\nusers have said that our bbs is better than theres in this area and\nwere all complaing about the time dupChecker was taking on there BBS.\n\nSo Use it if you like and dont if you dont it was created for our use\nand if you dont like it then let your users suffer DupChecks for\neternity sooner or later your users will get fed up with it no matter\nhow FAST you CPU is, then they will either STOP calling your bbs or\nNever upload many files........ CAN you AFFORD NOT To USE IT...\n@endnode\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',119795,7,0,NULL,NULL,'vn_fdup','scan',1780048821);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('vn_rexx','VN_REXX.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/VN_REXX.LHA',NULL,'XIM','Install.exe',NULL,NULL,'VN','/  |_/\/  |/  \ |/  \/   \  /\__. \ /   |   \  :   / :   /  \   / /  |  \ \_______/\____/\____/\__/\_/  \_____/',replace('The  / | <T>/ __ \/ __ \\_  \/   /  ___/\n    /  |_/\/  |/  \ |/  \/   \  /\__. \\n   /   |   \  :   / :   /  \   / /  |  \\n   \_______/\____/\____/\__/\_/  \_____/\nNastyNode NastyEdit & NastyFlist Updates\n/X Replacement utilities for Who & F.\n   Nothing Compares with these now!','\n',char(10)),'VN_Edit.doc',replace('                   NASTYEDIT V1.1 by )/ideo /\/asty\n\nInstalling:- \n Stick one finger in left ear (any finger on right arm) and shout i''m\nnasty and i''m going to eat your cat.\n\n after spitting out all the fur, look at the file VN_EDIT.rexx, check\nit out fully once you are sure there are no hacked bits install it and\nhave mega loads of fun, well your users with access will.. i know i do\non the boards i have got using it...\n\nRite install it and use it.........\n EDit the main .rexx file and modify the variables to suit your needs.\n\nKeepBackup="YES" if this is on then an origanal of the msg will be kept\nSHOWUSER="YES"   if on the editor will be shown\nBLAME=access     set this to a access level so that users can blame\n                 someone else for there edit, if you dont want this set \n                 it to OFF.\n\n\n-----( BLAME )-----\nTo activate the BLAME option just press the * key u will be prompted for\nthe rest of the stuff, however if you dont enter a name and showuser is\non then showuser will be turned off.\n\n-----( CALL FOR FUN )-----\nanyways if you want a BUG FREE unedited version of this then call my\nbbs Low-Life II (where LoONs hangout!) +44(0)61 499 3786\n\nRite im off now so pull that finger out and install this mother,.\n\nother info. this util is much better to use when the full screen editor\nis in use. so use any full screen editor.\n\nSetup for use with /X 3.x but should work on any /X version i think?\n\n...........\n\nPUT VN_Edit.rexx in DOORS:AREXX/\nAND MED.info in     BBS:commands/BBSCmd/\n\n. SYSOPS DONT EDIT BIG FILES WITH THE ALL OPTION . i included that\noption so that i can edit my logoff scripts from freinds houses, ever\nbeen away from your bbs and needed to edit your bbs scripts, then this\nis how to do it..\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',12375,2,0,NULL,NULL,'vn_rexx','scan',1780048821);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('vn_top11','VN_TOP11.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/VN_TOP11.LHA',NULL,'XIM','Install.exe',NULL,'Read/Write','VN','/  |_/\/  |/  \ |/  \/   \  /\__. \ /   |   \  :   / :   /  \   / /  |  \ \_______/\____/\____/\__/\_/  \_____/',replace('The  / | <T>/ __ \/ __ \\_  \/   /  ___/\n    /  |_/\/  |/  \ |/  \/   \  /\__. \\n   /   |   \  :   / :   /  \   / /  |  \\n   \_______/\____/\____/\__/\_/  \_____/\nVN_TOP Read/Write Private Mail Door v1.1\n\n','\n',char(10)),'TopSecret.doc',replace('      .---------------------------------------------------------.\n      | TopSecret Message Writer v1.1 Release by )/ideo /\/asty |\n      `---------------------------------------------------------''\n\nNEW IN v1.1......\nSYSOP STORE READ...\nthe sysop doesnt have a Download option instead there is a SYSOP store\noption, for the sysop to read STORED mail then he must logon and type\n\nTOPREAD SYSOP\n  ^       ^\n  |       |\n  |       `-OPTION\n  `-COMMAND\n\nREMEMBER TO EDIT the VARIABLES in the .REXX files to point to your DATA\nfiles Examples below\n\nTopSecretDir="DOORS:TopSecret/MailDir/"\nkeyfile="bbs:user.keys"  to find the users slot numbers\n^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^\n\nAlot of other bits have been updated bit nothing that will need to be\ndocumented in here. Run the Door try it out and let me know of any\nbugs.\n\nQUARANTEED 100% BACKDOOR FREE, leave me mail on ANY of the boards i\ncall with a number i can reach you on DATA!<-- and i will upload the\n100% version to you.\n\n------------------------ TOP READ/WRITE iNFO --------------------------\nWhat is It?.\n TopSecret Mail Reader/Writer/Replyer is a neat utility that will allow\nyou to read and write true private mail to any user.\n\nHow To Install?.\n Simple copy all Supplied 3.x icons to the commands directory and copy\nthe supplied doors to the doors directory.\n\nIcons: TopRead.info  < this is the icon for the reader\n       TopWrite.info < this is a SPARE icon for the writer\n       E.info        < this is to replace the standard E command\n\nWriting Mail:\nAs you can see i have replaced the standard E command this is because\nTopSecret can be used as a doorway to the normal mail routines within\nAmiExpress, so EALL ALL and wildcard expansion is still possible. When\nin use there will be no visable difference between TopSecret & the\nnormal method. This helps as users are very silly people and are very\neasy to confuse.\n\nReading Mail:\n This works much better as a MCI command added to any autoshow text\nfile on logon, Remember you CAN have multiple MCI commands in any MCI\ntext file. This too looks and works in much the same way as the normal\nread command, with a few differences.\n\nDownload Mail:\ninstead of Delete, the D command has been made into a Download command.\nAnd Delete has been moved to the exit from mail routine so on exit you\nare prompted to delete the mail, NOTE if a user doent delete the mail\nhe will be forced to read it next time he/she logs on.\n\n If the sysop selects this option then a SYSOP msg will be created for\nreading later, with the SYSOP FUNCTION this allows the sysop to keep\nthe more important messages.\n\nQuit:\nQuit is disabled as this type of mail is suppose to be force read.\n\nBackwards:\n- = Go back one message.\nNormally the - is used to go in reverse but in this to go all the way\nback u will have to repeat the process.\n\nExample MCI\n-------CUT------------\n~CC_Wall ~CC_TopRead \n-------CUT----------^-\n                    +-Leave a Space after the command\n\nNote Commands can be stacked on the same line always remember to leave\na trailing space after any MCI command EVEN the LAST MCI command will\nstill require a Space or a Newline.\n\nThe above example would first do the Wall door then it would do the\nTopRead door.\n\nNow install it and let your users decide if they like it or not...\n\nAs with all my doors/utils i refuse to add AUTO SHOW BBS plugging on my\nBBS i WILL NOT use doors/ utils that auto plug another bbs, and i hope\nto get everyone out of this LAME habbit. if your BBS is good enuff then\nit will not need to be pluged in ever little door/util you write.\n\nHellos go to:\n Python        - Even tho he is a Scouser\n Bill          - For Testing all my utilities out\n All the LoOnS - Dont know em all and cant be arsed reading a LoONs Doc\n Mark Kidd     - For Archive Tapes, Very handy to backup with\n Captain Blood - No reason just thourght i would say hello\n Ace           - Cos it was his 40th birthday not long ago\n Venom         - For Rexx Routine''s (if i ever get em?)\n Tango         - Ill think of a reason later\n DWAiN DiBLEY  - The duke of Dork, for having a fuking Ace handle\n Mad Turnip    - The strangest cabbage i have ever met\n BlackHawk     - For DMSTest even tho i still cant use it.\n PoleCat       - For the Modem\n [PRIVATE]     - He knows why, hahahahahahaha, but u dont!\n PooR BaBy     - For putting up with my weirdness\n Hitman        - For mad mail\n FireBlade     - I''ll think of why later (much later)\n Zealot        - For cheep drive\n Proteus       - For taking a joke Badly hahaha\n ALL PersPeX   - Cos i do take the piss out ove em, Only Joking Guys?\n               - Seems they can take a Joke now Unlike at First!\n ALL MY CALLERS- For calling and supporting the BBS\n New Order     - The BEST Group Ever to release a Record\n The Prodigy   - For some of the Best weirdness tunes ever\n D-Man         - Or should he be in the next bit? hahaha\n\nHates to:\n Trevor             - The FaT Cunt, for being full of SHIT\n Andrew Loyd Webber - i dunno why but i saw it written somewhere\n Spots              - Why cant they Taste like Salard Cream too\n Bogies up my Nose  - For being there\n Two Unlimited      - For thinking they write/sing Tekno Records\n Me                 - For being a Lazy bastard\n\nIf i missed anyone out then it was intentional so shut the fuk up.\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',10388,2,0,NULL,NULL,'vn_top11','scan',1780048821);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('vn_tops','VN_TOPS.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/VN_TOPS.LHA',NULL,'XIM','Install.exe',NULL,'Reader/Writer','VN','/  |_/\/  |/  \ |/  \/   \  /\__. \ /   |   \  :   / :   /  \   / /  |  \ \_______/\____/\____/\__/\_/  \_____/',replace('The  / | <T>/ __ \/ __ \\_  \/   /  ___/\n    /  |_/\/  |/  \ |/  \/   \  /\__. \\n   /   |   \  :   / :   /  \   / /  |  \\n   \_______/\____/\____/\__/\_/  \_____/\nNastyTopSecret Message Reader/Writer\n Another AmiExpress Quality Utility','\n',char(10)),'TopSecret.doc',replace('      .---------------------------------------------------------.\n      | TopSecret Message Writer v1.0 Release by )/ideo /\/asty |\n      `---------------------------------------------------------''\n\nWhat is It?.\n TopSecret Mail Reader/Writer/Replyer is a neat utility that will allow\nyou to read and write true private mail to any user.\n\nHow To Install?.\n Simple copy all Supplied 3.x icons to the commands directory and copy\nthe supplied doors to the doors directory.\n\nIcons: TopRead.info  < this is the icon for the reader\n       TopWrite.info < this is a SPARE icon for the writer\n       E.info        < this is to replace the standard E command\n\nWriting Mail:\nAs you can see i have replaced the standard E command this is because\nTopSecret can be used as a doorway to the normal mail routines within\nAmiExpress, so EALL ALL and wildcard expansion is still possible. When\nin use there will be no visable difference between TopSecret & the\nnormal method. This helps as users are very silly people and are very\neasy to confuse.\n\nReading Mail:\n This works much better as a MCI command added to any autoshow text\nfile on logon, Remember you CAN have multiple MCI commands in any MCI\ntext file. This too looks and works in much the same way as the normal\nread command, with a few differences.\n\nDownload Mail:\ninstead of Delete, the D command has bee made into a Download command\nas All Private mail will be deleted on exit, also saves your msg base\nbeing cluttered up with old mail.\n\n If the sysop selects this option then a Stored msg file will be\ncreated for reading later, this allows the sysop to keep the more\nimportant messages. I will be writing a Sysop read option into the Read\nrexx, but u will have to wait for the next version for that.\n\nQuit:\nQuit is disabled as this type of mail is suppose to be force read.\n\nBackwards:\n- = Go back one message.\nNormally the - is used to go in reverse but in this to go all the way\nback u will have to repeat the process.\n\nExample MCI\n-------CUT------------\n~CC_Wall ~CC_TopRead \n-------CUT----------^-\n                    +-Leave a Space after the command\n\nNote Commands can be stacked on the same line always remember to leve a\ntrailing space after any MCI command EVEN the LAST MCI command will\nstill require a Space or a Newline.\n\nThe above example would first do the Wall door then it would do the\nTopRead door.\n\nNow install it and let your users decide if they like it or not...\n\nAs with all my doors/utils i refuse to add AUTO SHOW BBS plugging on my\nBBS i WILL NOT use doors/ utils that auto plug another bbs, and i hope\nto get everyone out of this LAME habbit. if your BBS is good enuff then\nit will not need to be pluged in ever little door/util you write.\n\nHellos go to:\n Python        - Even tho he is a Scouser\n Bill          - For Testing all my utilities out\n All the LoOnS - Dont know em all and cant be arsed reading a LoONs Doc\n Mark Kidd     - For Archive Tapes, Very handy to backup with\n Captain Blood - No reason just thourght i would say hello\n Ace           - Cos it was his 40th birthday not long ago\n Venom         - For Rexx Routine''s (if i ever get em?)\n Tango         - Ill think of a reason later\n DWAiN DiBLEY  - The duke of Dork, for having a fuking Ace handle\n Mad Turnip    - The strangest cabbage i have ever met\n BlackHawk     - For DMSTest even tho i still cant use it.\n PoleCat       - For the Modem\n [PRIVATE]     - He knows why, hahahahahahaha, but u dont!\n PooR BaBy     - For putting up with my weirdness\n Hitman        - For mad mail\n FireBlade     - I''ll think of why later (much later)\n Zealot        - For cheep drive\n Proteus       - For taking a joke Badly hahaha\n ALL PersPeX   - Cos i do take the piss out ove em, Only Joking Guys?\n               - Seems they can take a Joke now Unlike at First!\n ALL MY CALLERS- For calling and supporting the BBS\n New Order     - The BEST Group Ever to release a Record\n The Prodigy   - For some of the Best weirdness tunes ever\n D-Man         - Or should he be in the next bit? hahaha\n\nHates to:\n Trevor             - The FaT Cunt, for being full of SHIT\n Andrew Loyd Webber - i dunno why but i saw it written somewhere\n Spots              - Why cant they Taste like Salard Cream too\n Bogies up my Nose  - For being there\n Two Unlimited      - For thinking they write/sing Tekno Records\n Me                 - For being a Lazy bastard\n\nIf i missed anyone out then it was intentional so shut the fuk up.\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',10499,2,0,NULL,NULL,'vn_tops','scan',1780048821);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('vn_wal13','VN_WAL13.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/VN_WAL13.LHA',NULL,'XIM','Install.exe',NULL,')/ideo','VN','T \_     / ______  ___________ |   __/______ H /     /\/   _  \/   _  \    \|   \   ____/ E/     /  \   |   \   |   \    \   /\___  \',replace('  ________                      ______      \nT \_     / ______  ___________ |   __/______\nH /     /\/   _  \/   _  \    \|   \   ____/\nE/     /  \   |   \   |   \    \   /\___  \ \n/     /    \_ |    \  |    \      /    |   \\n\___________/______/_______/ \___/_________/\no- by )/ideo /\/asty ---|____|----------Mb->\n| NastyWall v1.3 Now MultiNode & FiXED!    |\n| New Options NEVER used before on a WALL  |\n| Optional Spray Cans & anonomous Entries  |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'VN_Wall.doc',replace('                     NastyWall v1.3 by )/ideo /\/asty LOONs\nCall the Nasty Doors Test site.  G.B.H.  +44(0)61 945 8603 3 Nodes *RiNGDoWN*\n\nOK!  i said no BBS pluging will be done in my doors, however as this version\nwas bourght by the sysop on G.B.H.  he requested that as he paid for it he\nwanted his BBS pluging done on the bottom banner.\n\nIf anyone else wants to buy 1 of my doors feel free to contact me.\n\nHistory :\nNastyWall 1.3 - Added optional anonymous option,anonymous entries will be\n                added to the callers log so the sysop can see who written\n                what.\n                Added optional colour cans\n                Removed the internal cans text and Added a new file\n                "VN_Wall.Cans" so you can draw your own cans if anyone can\n                do better spray cans than the ones i have done then please\n                call G.B.H. and upload them to me -Thanks-\n                Made the display area work ok for PC users with only 23 lines\n                now screens with ONLY 200 pixels will display ok.\n                PC''s suck!  & ST''s Suck even more.\n                Now Multinode Freindly.  Will not allow a user to start to\n                write on the wall if somebody else is writing.\n#---------------------------------------------------------------------------#\nNastyWall 1.3a- Test version, Pre-Release used on G.B.H. BBS only\n                No way is runner getting a grip of this one yet!\n\nNastyWall 1.2 - Whole new type of wall. Release version\n\nNastyWall 1.2a- Spread (While i was ill) and it wasnt finished, i had a few\n                things left to do, but Runner decided to spread it\n                unfinished! Without my permission.\n                to find if you had the wrong version check the users screen\n                lengths.  as this version had a bug, it sets the users screen\n                length to 200 lines.  Both version carry the 1.2 Version\n                string as i never planned to release it until it was\n                finished.\n\nNastyWall 1.1 - Never released, Was only used on G.B.H. BBS\n              - Was a complete re-write.\n\nNastyWall 1.0 - Looked like every other wall (Boring!)\n\nFuture :\nI keep getting asked about adding other colours to the output text I think\nthat type of look is scruffy, but as some of you want it I may add it as a\ntoggle feature.\n\nHandles :\nI''ve been told that some users WONT write abuse or daft MSG''s on the wall\nbecause of the handle being shown.  I may change this so u can blame another\nuser (access dependant) or be anonymous.\n\n             -----------Docs for NastyWall---------------\nI''m a bit sick of the wall programs on boards at the mo they all seem to look\nand act the same way.  So I have added a few changes to Nastywall.\n\n I have tried to gain interest in using the program you have all logged onto\na BBs and been prompted to scribble something on a wall if the wall program\nlooks messy and boring chances are your not gonna bother to write on it.\nThis is where NastyWall comes in its different and so make the users\ninterested in it.\n\nALL users on G.B.H.  have studied it and most have scribbled on it where as\nbefore with a standard wall installed noone but the LoONs were using it, All\nLoONs use the wall to slag each other off, our way of having a bit of a\nlaugh.\n\nMost hated walls have 1 or more of the following.\n1 - BackDoors (Why be a 16 sandwich eating fat fucking LAMER)\n2 - Random Colours for the text (VERY VERY scruffy)\n3 - BBS Plugs Before or After the Wall has shown (LAME)\n4 - NO Bricks. (Shit that wouldn''t hold the house up)\n\nAs I believe in user editability this wall will remain in Arexx format, it\nwill have to anyway as I know nowt about C or ASM, if anyone wants to write\nthis wall in C and send it to me along witha C compiler I would be very\ninterested in learning it.  Arexx may be a little slow but at least even the\nstupidest sysop can check for backdoors.\n\nYou can now use Number characters on the wall (0-9) in the previous version I\ndecided that all (0-9) characters were a possible BBS PLUG and redirected\nfrom the wall to a definable BBS Adder.  This can still be done in this\nversion but you get asked this time.\n\nAll files needed are in the archive for this.  install it like any other\nAREXX door if you cant do that then get out of the BBS game as its lamers\nlike you that give us a BAD name.\n\nEditable option in the Arexx program.\n\nNastypath="DOORS:Arexx/"   <-Set this to the path you install Wall into\nRXCommand="SYS:RexxC/Rx"   <-where dos can find RX\nBBSPLUG="BBS Lister/Adder" <-The name of the BBS lister/adder\nBBSACC=200                 <-Access level needed to use BBS lister/adder\nBBSREXX="DOORS:ADDBBS/Addbbstologoff.Rexx" <location of BBSAdder\n\nVN_Wall.hdr <-this is for you to add your Brick effects or anything else you\n              may want to put in before the main wall is displayed.\n\nFormat of VN_Hdr=21 Lines 80 Columns.\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',11898,2,0,NULL,NULL,'vn_wal13','scan',1780048821);
