t allow a user to start to\n                write on the wall if somebody else is writing.\n#---------------------------------------------------------------------------#\nNastyWall 1.3a- Test version, Pre-Release used on G.B.H. BBS only\n                No way is runner getting a grip of this one yet!\n\nNastyWall 1.2 - Whole new type of wall. Release version\n\nNastyWall 1.2a- Spread (While i was ill) and it wasnt finished, i had a few\n                things left to do, but Runner decided to spread it\n                unfinished! Without my permission.\n                to find if you had the wrong version check the users screen\n                lengths.  as this version had a bug, it sets the users screen\n                length to 200 lines.  Both version carry the 1.2 Version\n                string as i never planned to release it until it was\n                finished.\n\nNastyWall 1.1 - Never released, Was only used on G.B.H. BBS\n              - Was a complete re-write.\n\nNastyWall 1.0 - Looked like every other wall (Boring!)\n\nFuture :\nI keep getting asked about adding other colours to the output text I think\nthat type of look is scruffy, but as some of you want it I may add it as a\ntoggle feature.\n\nHandles :\nI''ve been told that some users WONT write abuse or daft MSG''s on the wall\nbecause of the handle being shown.  I may change this so u can blame another\nuser (access dependant) or be anonymous.\n\n             -----------Docs for NastyWall---------------\nI''m a bit sick of the wall programs on boards at the mo they all seem to look\nand act the same way.  So I have added a few changes to Nastywall.\n\n I have tried to gain interest in using the program you have all logged onto\na BBs and been prompted to scribble something on a wall if the wall program\nlooks messy and boring chances are your not gonna bother to write on it.\nThis is where NastyWall comes in its different and so make the users\ninterested in it.\n\nALL users on G.B.H.  have studied it and most have scribbled on it where as\nbefore with a standard wall installed noone but the LoONs were using it, All\nLoONs use the wall to slag each other off, our way of having a bit of a\nlaugh.\n\nMost hated walls have 1 or more of the following.\n1 - BackDoors (Why be a 16 sandwich eating fat fucking LAMER)\n2 - Random Colours for the text (VERY VERY scruffy)\n3 - BBS Plugs Before or After the Wall has shown (LAME)\n4 - NO Bricks. (Shit that wouldn''t hold the house up)\n\nAs I believe in user editability this wall will remain in Arexx format, it\nwill have to anyway as I know nowt about C or ASM, if anyone wants to write\nthis wall in C and send it to me along witha C compiler I would be very\ninterested in learning it.  Arexx may be a little slow but at least even the\nstupidest sysop can check for backdoors.\n\nYou can now use Number characters on the wall (0-9) in the previous version I\ndecided that all (0-9) characters were a possible BBS PLUG and redirected\nfrom the wall to a definable BBS Adder.  This can still be done in this\nversion but you get asked this time.\n\nAll files needed are in the archive for this.  install it like any other\nAREXX door if you cant do that then get out of the BBS game as its lamers\nlike you that give us a BAD name.\n\nEditable option in the Arexx program.\n\nNastypath="DOORS:Arexx/"   <-Set this to the path you install Wall into\nRXCommand="SYS:RexxC/Rx"   <-where dos can find RX\nBBSPLUG="BBS Lister/Adder" <-The name of the BBS lister/adder\nBBSACC=200                 <-Access level needed to use BBS lister/adder\nBBSREXX="DOORS:ADDBBS/Addbbstologoff.Rexx" <location of BBSAdder\n\nVN_Wall.hdr <-this is for you to add your Brick effects or anything else you\n              may want to put in before the main wall is displayed.\n\nFormat of VN_Hdr=21 Lines 80 Columns.\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,7757,2,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048821);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('vn_wall','VN_WALL.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/VN_WALL.LHA',NULL,'XIM','Install.exe',NULL,')/ideo','VN','T \_     / ______  ___________ |   __/______ H /     /\/   _  \/   _  \    \|   \   ____/ E/     /  \   |   \   |   \    \   /\___  \',replace('  ________                      ______\nT \_     / ______  ___________ |   __/______\nH /     /\/   _  \/   _  \    \|   \   ____/\nE/     /  \   |   \   |   \    \   /\___  \\n/     /    \_ |    \  |    \      /    |   \\n\___________/______/_______/ \___/_________/\no-----[PRESENT]---------|____|----------Mb->\n| NastyWall 1.2 - by )/ideo /\/asty LøONS! |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'VN_Wall.doc',replace('                NastyWall v1.2 by )/ideo /\/asty LOONs\n\nHistory :\nNastyWall 1.2 - This version\n\nNastyWall 1.1 - Never released, Was only used on G.B.H. BBS\n              - Was a complete re-write.\n\nNastyWall 1.0 - Looked like every other wall (Boring!)\n\nFuture :\nI keep getting asked about adding other colours to the output text I\nthink that type of look is scruffy, but as some of you want it I may\nadd it as a toggle feature.\n\nHandles :\nI''ve been told that some users WONT write abuse or daft MSG''s on the\nwall because of the handle being shown.  I may change this so u can\nblame another user (access dependant) or be anonymous.\n\n             -----------Docs for NastyWall---------------\nI''m a bit sick of the wall programs on boards at the mo they all seem\nto look and act the same way. So I have added a few changes to\nNastywall.\n I have tried to gain interest in using the program you have all logged\nonto a BBs and been prompted to scribble something on a wall if the wall\nprogram looks messy and boring chances are your not gonna bother to\nwrite on it. This is where NastyWall comes in its different and so\nmake the users interested in it.\n\nALL users on G.B.H. have studied it and most have scribbled on it where\nas before with a standard wall installed noone but the LoONs were\nusing it, All LoONs use the wall to slag each other off, our way of\nhaving a bit of a laugh.\n\nMost hated walls have 1 or more of the following.\n1 - BackDoors (Why be a 16 sandwich eating fat fucking LAMER)\n2 - Random Colours for the text (VERY VERY scruffy)\n3 - BBS Plugs Before or After the Wall has shown (LAME)\n4 - NO Bricks. (Shit that wouldn''t hold the house up)\n\nAs I believe in user editability this wall will remain in Arexx format,\nit will have to anyway as I know nowt about C or ASM, if anyone wants\nto write this wall in C and send it to me along witha C compiler I\nwould be very interested in learning it.\nArexx may be a little slow but at least even the stupidest sysop can\ncheck for backdoors.\n\nU can now use Number characters on the wall (0-9) in the previous\nversion I decided that all (0-9) characters were a possible BBS PLUG\nand redirected from the wall to a definable BBS Adder. This can still\nbe done in this version but you get asked this time.\n\nAll files needed are in the archive for this. install it like any other\nAREXX door if you cant do that then get out of the BBS game as its\nlamers like you that give us a BAD name.\n\nEditable option in the Arexx program.\n\nNastypath="DOORS:Arexx/"   <-Set this to the path you install Wall into\nRXCommand="SYS:RexxC/Rx"   <-where dos can find RX\nBBSPLUG="BBS Lister/Adder" <-The name of the BBS lister/adder\nBBSACC=200                 <-Access level needed to use BBS lister/adder\nBBSREXX="DOORS:ADDBBS/Addbbstologoff.Rexx" <location of BBSAdder\n\nVN_Wall.hdr <-this is for you to add your Brick effects or anything\n              else you may want to put in before the main wall is\n              displayed.\n\nFormat of VN_Hdr=21 Lines 80 Columns.\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',6783,3,0,NULL,NULL,'vn_wall','scan',1780048821);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('vn_wallg','VN_WALLG.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/VN_WALLG.LHA',NULL,'XIM','.------------------------------------------.',NULL,NULL,'VN',': _____.__/\:____   ____  ____   )/ideo    : | \__  | / \\__  \ /  _ \/ _  \  (--oo)    | :   \  | \__/  \  \  ___/ //  /   \_-/     :',replace('.------------------------------------------.\n: _____.__/\:____   ____  ____   )/ideo    :\n| \__  | / \\__  \ /  _ \/ _  \  (--oo)    |\n:   \  | \__/  \  \  ___/ //  /   \_-/     :\n|    \ : /  |  /  / /  /  /  /    /\/asty  |\n:     \_/|__|____/____/\____/ -[Presents]- :\n|__________________________________________|\n: NastyWall v3.0 Major Update lots of new  :\n: Stuff, including Config,Edit Lines +more :\n: *#> AmigaGuide Doc for new WALL      <#* :\n: *#>      Release Soon......          <#* :\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'VN_Wall_User.guide',replace('@database NastyWall\n@master VN_Wall_User.guide\n@$VER: 3.0\n@author ")/ideo /\/asty"\n@(c) "NastySoft (NOT)"\n@help "Help"\n@wordwrap\n@font cedfont.font 0\n@index History\n@remark Created with Heddley v1.1 (c) Edd Dumbill 1994\n\n@node "Main" "NastyWall v3.0 by )/ideo /\/asty & Venom"\n\n                   NastyWall v3.0 by )/ideo /\\/asty\n\n     Call the Nasty Doors Test site. LowLife3 The Final Conflict\n \n                       @{" Installing    " link "Instalation" 0}\n                       @{" Wall Options  " link "options" 0}\n\n                       @{" Configuration " link "config" 0}\n                       @{" User Config   " link "USRCFG" 0}\n\n                       @{" Main Docs     " link "MainDocs" 0}\n\n                       @{" History       " link "history" 0}\n                       @{" Future        " link "future" 0} Shit can only get to 87 MPH\n                       @{" Greetings     " link "Greets" 0}\n                       @{" BUGS          " link "Bugs" 0} Taste nice on a butty\n\n                       @{" Serious Dudes " link "Serious" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "Instalation" "How to Install"\n\n Auto Install:-\n                    @{"Click Me To Install" system "VN_Wall.INSTALL"}\n\nManualy:-\n                1 - UnArc to an Empty directory\n                2 - You will now see the following\n\nBBS/Doors/NastyWall/@{"VN_Wall.guide" link "Guide" 0}\n                    @{"VN_Wall.bricks" link "Bricks" 0}\n                    @{"VN_Wall.log" link "Log" 0}\n                    @{"VN_Wall.XIM" link "XIM" 0}\n                    @{"VN_Wall.grafiti" link "Grafiti" 0}\n                    @{"VN_Wall.cfg" link "Config" 0}\n                    @{"VN_Wall.Install" link "AutoInstall" 0}\n\nBBS/Commands/BBSCmd/@{"Wall.info" link "Info" 0}\n\nSimply copy the BBS Directory to your BBS: Directory/Path \n (WoW! Fuking easy door to install)\n\nLogIn to your bbs and Type WALL, Thats it The wall Creates its own config when it is first run.\n You can Edit the config and change its default settings you will find the config files in ENV:VN_Wall.cfg & ENVARC:VN_Wall.cfg Read the TXT in the Config for information on what each line is for.\n\nyou may want to add this wall to an Auto show file on login simply add the command ~CC_WALL <-to any MCI auto show file.\n@endnode\n\n@node "Options" "Main Options Avaiable"\n                               Options:\n Y = Yes Write @{"Grafiti" link "Grafiti" 0} \n N = No Do somthing else\n R = Reverse Read Previous Grafiti lines\n F = Forward Read Previous Grafiti lines\n L = Last Page shows grafiti lines shown on startup\n I = Information about things not that interesting but there because\n     everyone else has one.\n V = View @{"Wall log" link "Log" 0} (NOTE#) there was no room to add this\n     to the option line but its mainly for Sysop & Co-Sysop''s ect.. so\n     that wont matter.\n E = Edit Any line of Grafiti Entered by any user (Also not on Option line\n     Can set access to any but i suggest only sysops & Co-Sysops get access\n     to this option.  I''ll be using it to Remove BBS plugs from the\n     Grafiti.\n\n                         Edit Line Options:-\n\n E = Start to Edit *any line* will be prompted for line Number & new text\n S = Save Modified Line (Only if line has been modified)\n Q = Quit Edit options & return to normal wall usage\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "Config" "Configuration"\n\n                         Config file layout:-\n\n Line 1 = Path to @{"Grafiti" link "Grafiti" 0},@{"Bricks" link "Bricks" 0},& @{"WallLog" link "Log" 0} Files\n Line 2 = Maximum number of lines to store in Grafiti file\n Line 3 = Maximum Lines to store in Wall log file\n\n NEXT line is one of those options that may cause problems so ive\n     provided a fix for those users that may experience problems.\n\n Line 4 = Maximum Lines to show at 1 time = 18-MaxLines\n         Some users may experience problems with this so its best to fix\n         it low at 18 so that banners fit the screen. i''ve added it only\n         because i was asked to do so by alot of sysops. youv''e got it now\n         Check with your users that they see the grafiti between the top &\n         bottom banners, if any lines overwrite the banners then there\n         screen length is over the maximum visible. Get them to change it.\n         Or do what ive done in the config and limit it to 18 lines.\n\n Line 5 = View Log Access level, access level required to view log\n         the log stores ALL anonomous & blame options.  This is best\n         set to Sysop/Co-Sysop access level, most users will not be\n         aware that this option exists.\n\n Line 6 = Access for Blame option, access level required to blame\n         another user Best left so everyone can use it!  More Phun!\n Line 7 = Access for Anonomous option, Same as above\n Line 8 = Access for Edit Line, Access required to beable to edit any\n         grafiti line entered by any user. Best set to sysop/Co-Sysop\n         access level, again most users will not know this exists.\n@endnode\n\n@node "MainDocs" "SucKER-Reading-DøCS"\n\n     ---------Docs for NastyWall----SucKER-Reading-DøCS---------\n\nI''m a bit sick of the wall programs on boards at the mo they all seem to look and act the same way.  So I have added a few changes to Nastywall.\n\n I have tried to gain interest in using the program you have all logged onto a BBs and been prompted to scribble something on a wall if the wall program looks messy and boring chances are your not gon na bother to write on it.  This is where NastyWall comes in its different and so make the users interested in it.\n\nALL users on G.B.H.  have studied it and most have scribbled on it where as before with a standard wall installed noone but the regular callers were using it.\n\n          Most hated walls have 1 or more of the following.\n\n\n 1 - BackDoors (Why be a 16 sandwich eating fat fucking LAMER)\n 2 - Random Colours for the text (VERY VERY scruffy)\n 3 - BBS Plugs Before or After the Wall has shown (LAME)\n 4 - NO Bricks.  (Shit that wouldn''t hold the house up)\n\nAs I believe in user editability even tho Now NastyWall is in XIM it is still possible to modify it by using the External configuration.\n\n\nYou can now use Number characters on the wall (0-9) in the previous version I decid ed that al l (0-9) characters were a possible BBS PLUG and redirected from the wall to a definable BBS Adder. This can still be done in this version but you get asked this time.\n\nAll files needed are in the archive for this. install it like any other AREXX door if you cant do that then get out of the BBS game as its lamers like you that give us a BAD name.\n\nEditable option in the Arexx program.  none Cos its not going to be released in Arexx\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "Future" "Things left to do"\n\n                         Back to the Future:\n\n               o Make internal config editor\n               o Write AmigaGuide Doc file. (Oh! Must have done this)\n               o Brew up Smoke Splif then Format DH0:\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "Greets" "Greetings to a few Peeps"\n\n              Greetings:- in a Very Specific order...\n\n Aint it a load of shite when everyone puts Greets in no specific order\n theres an order alright they just dont want to offend (haha) but i''m\n not bothered.  ive put em in in the order i thourght of em.\n\n )/ideo /\\/asty   o Someone has to think of me first\n R$-Jøhn          o Hows the Diet Going Fatty\n Runner           o Hows my Monitor? is it Missing me? :(\n                    Probably would have forgoten you but just been\n                    talking to you outside shops.\n Venom            o Got a headace YET?\n ACE              o Wot u upto these days?\n Icon             o Mad as you like Chat sessions\n Borg             o Pissed without us on Thursday.\n CoolSpot         o Soz Bout Thursday but John had to BABY Sit for his\n                    Girlfriend because her mummy & daddy wer e going out &\n                    she is too young to be left on her own. hahahahahaha.\n Tango            o ERm did you ever marry that Animal you were caught with?\n Mad Turnip       o Eaten any mouldy socks latly (your 1 seriously SiCK cunt)\n MasterDrive      o Pay your phone bill NOW (you know its good to Talk)\n The Duke of DorK o Dwain Dibley (the Real one) how about 2hours for dinner\n Zealot           o Got any cheap drives?\n Proteus          o You still around Spotty\n Trader           o Get off my T-Shit and stop breathing that bad breath\n                    1 Person who said he was gonna Thump me, So i went\n                    and met him, He didnt punch me though.\n BiG W            o for comments & ideas\n Randy Rabbit     o Wheres my Fiver, Spent on Beer i hope?\n FireFlash        o Fat cunt 16st 6ft SO do i look like i''m Shaking (NOT!)\n                    Dont threaten me, you may Never wake from a CoMA.\n                    Chill out and get a life Beyond SAD Computers.\n                    After All its all a load of BolloX and Games.\n BilL9ives        o So you dont Trust ME? (Apologize or FUCKOFF)\n Python           o Got summat to Say then Say it?\n                    How long have i know you (Do you realy think that?)\n NitA             o Got anymore UFB''s (unidentified low flying Birdies)\n DualCrew&Shining o For Taking over Amiga Conference on R$-Johns BBS\n                    Have any of your guys called there yet tho?!\n FLASH            o GroveRider? Been swimming in Sale waterpark l8tly?\n                  o Why not change your Computer Handel to G roveRider?\n And not Forgetting...\n Bernard Sumner   o (NewOrder) Not BBS Dude. Get a Haircut\n                    like your Sons.\n PiNK FloyD       o For there Wall (Much better than mine)\n BBS TV           o For Excelent Programs like Red Dwarf.\n\n ERm.... theres prob more but im tired now so bye bye.......\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "History" "Not to be confused with Boring Subject at School"\n\n                              History : \n\n                        @{" NastyWall v3.0   " link "v3.0" 0} Alpha Version new stuff\n                        @{" NastyWall v2.0   " link "v2.0" 0}\n                        @{" NastyWall v1.3   " link "v1.3" 0}\n                        @{" NastyWall v1.3a  " link "v1.3a" 0}\n                        @{" NastyWall v1.2   " link "v1.2" 0}\n                        @{" NastyWall v1.2a  " link "v1.2a" 0}\n                        @{" NastyWall v1.1   " link "v1.1" 0}\n                        @{" NastyWall v1.0   " link "v1.0" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "v1.0" "v1.0"\n\n                Looked like every other wall (Boring!)\n@endnode\n\n@node "v1.1" "v1.1"\n\n               Never released, Was only used on G.B.H.  BBS Was a complete re-write.\n@endnode\n\n@node "v1.2a" "v1.2a"\n\n Spread (While i was ill) and it wasnt finished, i had a few things left to do, but Runner decided to spread it unfinished! Without my permission. to  find if you had the wrong version check the users screen lengths. as this version had a bug, it sets the users screen length to 200 lines. Both version carry the 1.2 Version string as i never planned to release it until it was finished.\n@endnode\n\n@node "v1.2" "v1.2"\n\n Whole new type of wall. Release version\n@endnode\n\n@node "v1.3a" "v1.3a"\n\n Test version, Pre-Release used on G.B.H. BBS only No way is runner getting a grip of this one yet!\n@endnode\n\n@node "v1.3" "v1.3"\n\n         Added optional anonymous option,anonymous entries will be\n         added to the callers log so the sysop can see who written\n         what.\n         Added optional colour cans\n         Removed the internal cans text and Added a new file\n         "VN_Wall.Cans" so you can draw your own cans if anyone can\n         do better spray cans than the ones i have done then please\n         call G.B.H. and upload them to me -Thanks-\n         Made the display area work ok for PC users with only 23\n         lines\n         now screens with ONLY 200 pixels will display ok.\n         PC''s suck!  & ST''s Suck even more.\n         Now Multinode Freindly.  Will not allow a user to start to\n         write on the wall if somebody else is writing.\n@endnode\n\n@node "v2.0" "v2.0"\n\n         Added Option Screen, You now have the choice of being\n         anonymous,New Handle,or your own handle.\n         Thats all thats NEW. Except for 1 Major part. The new\n         Phone Numbers for the BBS See Top of this Doc.\n         ALL Handles Changed Will be in White.\n@endnode\n\n@node "v3.0" "NastyWall v3.0 Alpha Version"\n                          @{" Whats 2 do b4 Release " link "V3.0update" 0}\n\n                          Stuff already done\n\n        o Added option to have more than 22 lines of Grafiti\n        o Added Reverse,Forward View to show more lines\n        o Added External CFG as now NastyWall is Released ONLY\n          as an Executable Zuper Fast XIM Module instead of Rexx\n          Thanks to Venom for Re-Sourcing it into C for me. Nice 1.\n        o Added LogFile Only Anonomous & Blame Options will be\n          Recorded into it.\n        o Fixed Columns to 79 Characters, was gonna put this in\n          the cfg but changed my mind.\n        o Made Anonomous,Blame and View Log Access dependant\n        o Made Wall Auto Adapt to the users Screen len,\n        o Added the Edit Grafiti mode\n        o Fixed some Cosmetic problems\n        o Removed External Spraycans, Now Fixed Internal only\n        o Probably added more but forgot about em for now.\n        o Removed ADDBBS doorway\n        o Added an Info Page and Removed BBS Plug from BANNER\n          Yeah bout time Hate BBS Plugs.\n        o Added a Greetings Section to this Doc......\n        o Didnt Fix Any bugs cos there wasnt any, But did fix\n          a few screen glitches found due to new code.\n@endnode\n\n@node "V3.0update" "Stuff added during Development"\n@next "History"\n@prev "v3.0"\nAS Previous Version was an Alpha (BUT Working) it was never released cos i wanted to release it with all the options avaiable ready to use, If i do it this way then Version wont spring up with slight modifications This way you get 1 Major release and any Releases Between V3.0-V4.0 will NOT be needed as im going to use Version numbers between them for Bug fixes Cosmetic changes ect.\n\nONLY when there are several new options will V4.0 arrive\n\n        o Added user configuration\n        o Added Sysop Mode, Allows editing of user configs\n        o modified Sysop mode so the sysop can access sysop mode on users node\n          this makes setting up usr configs for a user online easy.\n@endnode\n\n@node "Guide" "Guide"\n\n                           Your Reading it.\n@endnode\n\n@node "Bricks" "Bricks"\n\n This is used to show some background bricks/ layout is 79 chrs 18 lines\n@endnode\n\n@node "Log" "Log"\n\n This is the file used to store *anonomous* & Blame options See the cfg file for more info.\n@endnode\n\n@node "XIM" "XIM"\n\n From now NastyWall will only ever be released in C its of no use in Rexx format as a door this size (its got Bigger) is extreamly slow in Rexx format, as weve noticed when 4 users are all on the bbs\n\nI''d like to thank Venom again for Re-Sourcing this Wall into XIM if it was not possible for it to be released in XIM then NastyWall Would not have been updated so much. Rexx is Slow FireFlash is Slower\n@endnode\n\n@node "Grafiti" "Grafiti"\n\n This file stores all the grafiti written by the users. its possible to have any amount of lines stored in this file from 18-{whatever} definable in the configuration file.\n@endnode\n\n@node "Info" "Info"\n\n This is the Wall.info file for the BBSCmds directory if you move the wall to another directory then edit the information in this icon.\n@endnode\n\n@node "Bugs" "Bugs"\n\n                     What No Spiders................\n\n If any users spot any spiders or creepy crawlies please Slam them with a heavy object. and send them to me for further investigation.\n\n If however you decide its not really a bug i would be interested in, then Eat it yourself, you know you want to.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "Serious" "Serious"\nIf you are offended by anything i have written then its you i wanted to offend, i really hate all the serious side of this wank scene, there are plenty of guys/girls that dont take this crap seriously. Those are the people i want to know.\n\nIve NO TIME for WannaBe''s There ARE NO GODS in the scene just Wankers who think they are GODS\n\n I could name lots of you, and believe me im not afraid to do so its just not worth the thospur burn on the screen\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "AutoInstall" "Auto Install Information"\n\n This is a AutoInstall.script just type "VN_Wall.Install" at a CLI prompt to install this version of the wall\n\nThis will install into a Directory in Doors: called NastyWall also created in this directory will be a USRCFGS directory for storing user configs the user CFG stores the number of lines to show for that user as some users have screen lengths that are over the maximum visible, that type of setting is not compatable with NastyWall as banners will be overwritten, also stored will be access to certain options.\n\n                                    User Config\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "USRCFG" "USRCFG"\n\n                  User Configuration file...........\n\n Line 1 = the USERS name this allows new users who take over a (SLOT)\n          to have there own CFG and not just inherit the old users\n          configs.\n Line 2 = Number of Lines to show at 1 time = 18-MaxLines\n          Some users may experience problems with banners this is the\n          best way to fix it.\n Line 3 = ON/OFF/IGNORE\n          if ON Access to view log enabled\n Line 4 = ON/OFF/IGNORE\n          if ON Access to Blame option enabled\n Line 5 = ON/OFF/IGNORE\n          if ON Access to Anonomous option enabled\n Line 6 = ON/OFF/IGNORE\n          if on Access to Edit Line option enabled\n\n If any option is turned OFF then access to that option will be disabled\n if any option is set to IGNORE then access will depend on the settings in the VN_WALL.cfg configuration file\n when a user creates his/her config from within NastyWall all options will be set to IGNORE and the user will be prompted for a screen length\n\nAll options in the User configs overide the access levels set in the VN_WAll.cfg\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "Help" "Help for Dumies"\n\n\n                         Help for DickBrains\n\nClick a BUTTON like this one ---> @{"CLICK ME" link "Help" 0} to read the bits you want\n@endnode\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,9969,3,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048821);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('vn_wallr','VN_WALLR.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/VN_WALLR.LHA',NULL,'XIM','.------------------------------------------.',NULL,NULL,'VN',': _____.__/\:____   ____  ____   )/ideo    : | \__  | / \\__  \ /  _ \/ _  \  (--oo)    | :   \  | \__/  \  \  ___/ //  /   \_-/     :',replace('.------------------------------------------.\n: _____.__/\:____   ____  ____   )/ideo    :\n| \__  | / \\__  \ /  _ \/ _  \  (--oo)    |\n:   \  | \__/  \  \  ___/ //  /   \_-/     :\n|    \ : /  |  /  / /  /  /  /    /\/asty  |\n:     \_/|__|____/____/\____/ -[Presents]- :\n|__________________________________________|\n: NastyWall v3 Rexx Version Major Update   :\n: lots of new Stuff, including Config,Edit :\n: Edit Lines +more : The ONLY WALL Needed  :\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'VN_Wall_User.guide',replace('@database NastyWall\n@master VN_Wall_User.guide\n@$VER: 3.0\n@author ")/ideo /\/asty"\n@(c) "NastySoft (NOT)"\n@help "Help"\n@wordwrap\n@font cedfont.font 0\n@index History\n@remark Created with Heddley v1.1 (c) Edd Dumbill 1994\n\n@node "Main" "NastyWall v3.0 by )/ideo /\/asty & Venom"\n\n                     NastyWall v3.0 by Video Nasty Rexx Version.\n\n     Call the Nasty Doors Test site. LowLife3 The Final Conflict\n\nNot got Time to Complete this as yet and lots of you want it so here it is, Full Release Soon as i get time. Planned 68020,30,40 versions in XIM format.\n \n                       @{" Installing    " link "Instalation" 0}\n                       @{" Requirements  " link "Require" 0}\n                       @{" Wall Options  " link "options" 0}\n\n                       @{" Configuration " link "config" 0}\n                       @{" User Config   " link "USRCFG" 0}\n\n                       @{" Main Docs     " link "MainDocs" 0}\n\n                       @{" History       " link "history" 0}\n                       @{" Future        " link "future" 0} Shit can only get to 87 MPH\n                       @{" Greetings     " link "Greets" 0}\n                       @{" BUGS          " link "Bugs" 0} Taste nice on a butty\n\n                       @{" Serious Dudes " link "Serious" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "Instalation" "How to Install"\n\n Auto Install:-\n                    @{"Click Me To Install" system "VN_Wall.INSTALL"}\n\nManualy:-\n                1 - UnArc to an Empty directory\n                2 - You will now see the following\n\nBBS/Doors/NastyWall/@{"VN_Wall.guide" link "Guide" 0}\n                    @{"VN_Wall.bricks" link "Bricks" 0}\n                    @{"VN_Wall.log" link "Log" 0}\n                    @{"VN_Wall.XIM" link "XIM" 0}\n                    @{"VN_Wall.grafiti" link "Grafiti" 0}\n                    @{"VN_Wall.cfg" link "Config" 0}\n                    @{"VN_Wall.Install" link "AutoInstall" 0}\n\nBBS/Commands/BBSCmd/@{"Wall.info" link "Info" 0}\n\nSimply copy the BBS Directory to your BBS: Directory/Path \n (WoW! Fuking easy door to install)\n\nLogIn to your bbs and Type WALL, Thats it The wall Creates its own config when it is first run.\n You can Edit the config and change its default settings you will find the config files in ENV:VN_Wall.cfg & ENVARC:VN_Wall.cfg Read the TXT in the Config for information on what each line is for.\n\nyou may want to add this wall to an Auto show file on login simply add the command ~CC_WALL <-to any MCI auto show file.\n@endnode\n\n@node "Options" "Main Options Avaiable"\n                               Options:\n Y = Yes Write @{"Grafiti" link "Grafiti" 0} \n N = No Do somthing else\n R = Reverse Read Previous Grafiti lines\n F = Forward Read Previous Grafiti lines\n L = Last Page shows grafiti lines shown on startup\n I = Information about things not that interesting but there because\n     everyone else has one.\n V = View @{"Wall log" link "Log" 0} (NOTE#) there was no room to add this\n     to the option line but its mainly for Sysop & Co-Sysop''s ect.. so\n     that wont matter.\n E = Edit Any line of Grafiti Entered by any user (Also not on Option line\n     Can set access to any but i suggest only sysops & Co-Sysops get access\n     to this option.  I''ll be using it to Remove BBS plugs from the\n     Grafiti.\n\n                         Edit Line Options:-\n\n E = Start to Edit *any line* will be prompted for line Number & new text\n S = Save Modified Line (Only if line has been modified)\n Q = Quit Edit options & return to normal wall usage\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "Config" "Configuration"\n\n                         Config file layout:-\n\n Line 1 = Path to @{"Grafiti" link "Grafiti" 0},@{"Bricks" link "Bricks" 0},& @{"WallLog" link "Log" 0} Files\n Line 2 = Maximum number of lines to store in Grafiti file\n Line 3 = Maximum Lines to store in Wall log file\n\n NEXT line is one of those options that may cause problems so ive\n     provided a fix for those users that may experience problems.\n\n Line 4 = Maximum Lines to show at 1 time = 18-MaxLines\n         Some users may experience problems with this so its best to fix\n         it low at 18 so that banners fit the screen. i''ve added it only\n         because i was asked to do so by alot of sysops. youv''e got it now\n         Check with your users that they see the grafiti between the top &\n         bottom banners, if any lines overwrite the banners then there\n         screen length is over the maximum visible. Get them to change it.\n         Or do what ive done in the config and limit it to 18 lines.\n\n Line 5 = View Log Access level, access level required to view log\n         the log stores ALL anonomous & blame options.  This is best\n         set to Sysop/Co-Sysop access level, most users will not be\n         aware that this option exists.\n\n Line 6 = Access for Blame option, access level required to blame\n         another user Best left so everyone can use it!  More Phun!\n Line 7 = Access for Anonomous option, Same as above\n Line 8 = Access for Edit Line, Access required to beable to edit any\n         grafiti line entered by any user. Best set to sysop/Co-Sysop\n         access level, again most users will not know this exists.\n@endnode\n\n@node "MainDocs" "SucKER-Reading-DøCS"\n\n     ---------Docs for NastyWall----SucKER-Reading-DøCS---------\n\nI''m a bit sick of the wall programs on boards at the mo they all seem to look and act the same way.  So I have added a few changes to Nastywall.\n\n I have tried to gain interest in using the program you have all logged onto a BBs and been prompted to scribble something on a wall if the wall program looks messy and boring chances are your not gon na bother to write on it.  This is where NastyWall comes in its different and so make the users interested in it.\n\nALL users on G.B.H.  have studied it and most have scribbled on it where as before with a standard wall installed noone but the regular callers were using it.\n\n          Most hated walls have 1 or more of the following.\n\n\n 1 - BackDoors (Why be a 16 sandwich eating fat fucking LAMER)\n 2 - Random Colours for the text (VERY VERY scruffy)\n 3 - BBS Plugs Before or After the Wall has shown (LAME)\n 4 - NO Bricks.  (Shit that wouldn''t hold the house up)\n\nAs I believe in user editability even tho Now NastyWall is in XIM it is still possible to modify it by using the External configuration.\n\n\nYou can now use Number characters on the wall (0-9) in the previous version I decid ed that al l (0-9) characters were a possible BBS PLUG and redirected from the wall to a definable BBS Adder. This can still be done in this version but you get asked this time.\n\nAll files needed are in the archive for this. install it like any other AREXX door if you cant do that then get out of the BBS game as its lamers like you that give us a BAD name.\n\nEditable option in the Arexx program.  none Cos its not going to be released in Arexx\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "Future" "Things left to do"\n\n                         Back to the Future:\n\n               o Make internal config editor\n               o Write AmigaGuide Doc file. (Oh! Must have done this)\n               o Brew up Smoke Splif then Format DH0:\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "Greets" "Greetings to a few Peeps"\n\n              Greetings:- in a Very Specific order...\n\n Aint it a load of shite when everyone puts Greets in no specific order\n theres an order alright they just dont want to offend (haha) but i''m\n not bothered.  ive put em in in the order i thourght of em.\n\n )/ideo /\\/asty   o Someone has to think of me first\n R$-Jøhn          o Hows the Diet Going Fatty\n Runner           o Hows my Monitor? is it Missing me? :(\n                    Probably would have forgoten you but just been\n                    talking to you outside shops.\n Venom            o Got a headace YET?\n ACE              o Wot u upto these days?\n Icon             o Mad as you like Chat sessions\n Borg             o Pissed without us on Thursday.\n CoolSpot         o Soz Bout Thursday but John had to BABY Sit for his\n                    Girlfriend because her mummy & daddy wer e going out &\n                    she is too young to be left on her own. hahahahahaha.\n Mad Turnip       o Eaten any mouldy socks latly (your 1 seriously SiCK cunt)\n MasterDrive      o Pay your phone bill NOW (you know its good to Talk)\n The Duke of DorK o Dwain Dibley (the Real one) how about 2hours for dinner\n Zealot           o Hahaha Had any Female Visitors????? :)\n Proteus          o You still around Spotty\n Trader           o Get off my T-Shit and stop breathing that bad breath\n                    1 Person who said he was gonna Thump me, So i went\n                    and met him, He didnt punch me though.\n BiG W            o for comments & ideas\n Randy Rabbit     o Wheres my Fiver, Spent on Beer i hope?\n FireFlash        o Fat cunt 16st 6ft SO do i look like i''m Shaking (NOT!)\n                    Dont threaten me, you may Never wake from a CoMA.\n                    Chill out and get a life Beyond SAD Computers.\n                    After All its all a load of BolloX and Games.\n BilL9ives        o So you dont Trust ME? (Apologize or FUCKOFF)\n Python           o Got summat to Say then Say it?\n                    How long have i know you (Do you realy think that?)\n NitA             o Got anymore UFB''s (unidentified low flying Birdies)\n DualCrew&Shining o For Taking over Amiga Conference on R$-Johns BBS\n                    Have any of your guys called there yet tho?!\n FLASH            o GroveRider? Been swimming in Sale waterpark l8tly?\n                  o Why not change your Computer Handel to G roveRider?\n GreenGrass & Co  o Forgot the other Guys Handle?, Get a Real Modem.. :)\n\n And not Forgetting...\n Bernard Sumner   o (NewOrder) Not BBS Dude. Get a Haircut\n                    like your Sons.\n PiNK FloyD       o For there Wall (Much better than mine)\n BBS TV           o For Excelent Programs like Red Dwarf.\n\n ERm.... theres prob more but im tired now so bye bye.......\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "History" "Not to be confused with Boring Subject at School"\n\n                              History : \n\n                        @{" NastyWall v3.0   " link "v3.0" 0} Alpha Version new stuff\n                        @{" NastyWall v2.0   " link "v2.0" 0}\n                        @{" NastyWall v1.3   " link "v1.3" 0}\n                        @{" NastyWall v1.3a  " link "v1.3a" 0}\n                        @{" NastyWall v1.2   " link "v1.2" 0}\n                        @{" NastyWall v1.2a  " link "v1.2a" 0}\n                        @{" NastyWall v1.1   " link "v1.1" 0}\n                        @{" NastyWall v1.0   " link "v1.0" 0}\n@endnode\n\n@node "v1.0" "v1.0"\n\n                Looked like every other wall (Boring!)\n@endnode\n\n@node "v1.1" "v1.1"\n\n               Never released, Was only used on G.B.H.  BBS Was a complete re-write.\n@endnode\n\n@node "v1.2a" "v1.2a"\n\n Spread (While i was ill) and it wasnt finished, i had a few things left to do, but Runner decided to spread it unfinished! Without my permission. to  find if you had the wrong version check the users screen lengths. as this version had a bug, it sets the users screen length to 200 lines. Both version carry the 1.2 Version string as i never planned to release it until it was finished.\n@endnode\n\n@node "v1.2" "v1.2"\n\n Whole new type of wall. Release version\n@endnode\n\n@node "v1.3a" "v1.3a"\n\n Test version, Pre-Release used on G.B.H. BBS only No way is runner getting a grip of this one yet!\n@endnode\n\n@node "v1.3" "v1.3"\n\n         Added optional anonymous option,anonymous entries will be\n         added to the callers log so the sysop can see who written\n         what.\n         Added optional colour cans\n         Removed the internal cans text and Added a new file\n         "VN_Wall.Cans" so you can draw your own cans if anyone can\n         do better spray cans than the ones i have done then please\n         call G.B.H. and upload them to me -Thanks-\n         Made the display area work ok for PC users with only 23\n         lines\n         now screens with ONLY 200 pixels will display ok.\n         PC''s suck!  & ST''s Suck even more.\n         Now Multinode Freindly.  Will not allow a user to start to\n         write on the wall if somebody else is writing.\n@endnode\n\n@node "v2.0" "v2.0"\n\n         Added Option Screen, You now have the choice of being\n         anonymous,New Handle,or your own handle.\n         Thats all thats NEW. Except for 1 Major part. The new\n         Phone Numbers for the BBS See Top of this Doc.\n         ALL Handles Changed Will be in White.\n@endnode\n\n@node "v3.0" "NastyWall v3.0 Alpha Version"\n                          @{" Whats 2 do b4 Release " link "V3.0update" 0}\n\n                          Stuff already done\n\n        o Added option to have more than 22 lines of Grafiti\n        o Added Reverse,Forward View to show more lines\n        o Added External CFG as now NastyWall is Released ONLY\n          as an Executable Zuper Fast XIM Module instead of Rexx\n          Thanks to Venom for Re-Sourcing it into C for me. Nice 1.\n        o Added LogFile Only Anonomous & Blame Options will be\n          Recorded into it.\n        o Fixed Columns to 79 Characters, was gonna put this in\n          the cfg but changed my mind.\n        o Made Anonomous,Blame and View Log Access dependant\n        o Made Wall Auto Adapt to the users Screen len,\n        o Added the Edit Grafiti mode\n        o Fixed some Cosmetic problems\n        o Removed External Spraycans, Now Fixed Internal only\n        o Probably added more but forgot about em for now.\n        o Removed ADDBBS doorway\n        o Added an Info Page and Removed BBS Plug from BANNER\n          Yeah bout time Hate BBS Plugs.\n        o Added a Greetings Section to this Doc......\n        o Didnt Fix Any bugs cos there wasnt any, But did fix\n          a few screen glitches found due to new code.\n@endnode\n\n@node "V3.0update" "Stuff added during Development"\n@next "History"\n@prev "v3.0"\nAS Previous Version was an Alpha (BUT Working) it was never released cos i wanted to release it with all the options avaiable ready to use, If i do it this way then Version wont spring up with slight modifications This way you get 1 Major release and any Releases Between V3.0-V4.0 will NOT be needed as im going to use Version numbers between them for Bug fixes Cosmetic changes ect.\n\nONLY when there are several new options will V4.0 arrive\n\n        o Added user configuration\n        o Added Sysop Mode, Allows editing of user configs, The user\n          will have to have built a Config before the sysop can edit\n          it.  Also the sysop can only access a User Config from the\n          Node the user is on with NastyWall. If a Sysop wants to\n          edit a user config then use a Text Editor. Look in the Wall\n          Directory you will find a Directory Called USRCFGS/ this is\n          Where all user configs are stored.\n@endnode\n\n@node "Guide" "Guide"\n\n                           Your Reading it.\n@endnode\n\n@node "Bricks" "Bricks"\n\n This is used to show some background bricks/ layout is 79 chrs 18 lines\n@endnode\n\n@node "Log" "Log"\n\n This is the file used to store *anonomous* & Blame options See the cfg file for more info.\n@endnode\n\n@node "XIM" "XIM"\n\n From now NastyWall will only ever be released in C its of no use in Rexx format as a door this size (its got Bigger) is extreamly slow in Rexx format, as weve noticed when 4 users are all on the bbs\n\nI''d like to thank Venom again for Re-Sourcing this Wall into XIM if it was not possible for it to be released in XIM then NastyWall Would not have been updated so much. Rexx is Slow FireFlash is Slower\n@endnode\n\n@node "Grafiti" "Grafiti"\n\n This file stores all the grafiti written by the users. its possible to have any amount of lines stored in this file from 18-{whatever} definable in the configuration file.\n@endnode\n\n@node "Info" "Info"\n\n This is the Wall.info file for the BBSCmds directory if you move the wall to another directory then edit the information in this icon.\n@endnode\n\n@node "Bugs" "Bugs"\n\n                     What No Spiders................\n\n If any users spot any spiders or creepy crawlies please Slam them with a heavy object. and send them to me for further investigation.\n\n If however you decide its not really a bug i would be interested in, then Eat it yourself, you know you want to.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "Serious" "Serious"\nIf you are offended by anything i have written then its you i wanted to offend, i really hate all the serious side of this wank scene, there are plenty of guys/girls that dont take this crap seriously. Those are the people i want to know.\n\nIve NO TIME for WannaBe''s There ARE NO GODS in the scene just Wankers who think they are GODS\n\n I could name lots of you, and believe me im not afraid to do so its just not worth the thospur burn on the screen\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "AutoInstall" "Auto Install Information"\n\n This is a AutoInstall.script just type "VN_Wall.Install" at a CLI prompt to install this version of the wall\n\nThis will install into a Directory in Doors: called NastyWall also created in this directory will be a USRCFGS directory for storing user configs the user CFG stores the number of lines to show for that user as some users have screen lengths that are over the maximum visible, that type of setting is not compatable with NastyWall as banners will be overwritten, also stored will be access to certain options.\n\n                                    User Config\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "USRCFG" "USRCFG"\n\n                  User Configuration file...........\n\n Line 1 = the USERS name this allows new users who take over a (SLOT)\n          to have there own CFG and not just inherit the old users\n          configs.\n Line 2 = Number of Lines to show at 1 time = 18-MaxLines\n          Some users may experience problems with banners this is the\n          best way to fix it.\n Line 3 = ON/OFF/IGNORE\n          if ON Access to view log enabled\n Line 4 = ON/OFF/IGNORE\n          if ON Access to Blame option enabled\n Line 5 = ON/OFF/IGNORE\n          if ON Access to Anonomous option enabled\n Line 6 = ON/OFF/IGNORE\n          if on Access to Edit Line option enabled\n\n If any option is turned OFF then access to that option will be disabled\n if any option is set to IGNORE then access will depend on the settings in the VN_WALL.cfg configuration file\n when a user creates his/her config from within NastyWall all options will be set to IGNORE and the user will be prompted for a screen length\n\nAll options in the User configs overide the access levels set in the VN_WAll.cfg\n\n@endnode\n\n@node "Help" "Help for Dumies"\n\n\n                         Help for DickBrains\n\nClick a BUTTON like this one ---> @{"CLICK ME" link "Help" 0} to read the bits you want\n@endnode\n\n@node "Require" "Requirements  "\n               To use this Wall you will Require......\n\nA Computer Preferably an Amiga 4000 with WarpEngine Mega, But any will do for now\n\nAn AmiXpress BBS setup v4.x is good for now. Should work with S-Express tho!\n\n1 packet of Crispy pancakes. 16 cans Bavaria 2oz BushWeed\n@endnode\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,22392,1,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048821);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('vote3_0','VOTE3_0.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/VOTE3_0.LHA',NULL,'XIM','\>/<\>/<\>/<\/<\>/<\/<\>/<\/<\>/<\/<\>/<\>/<',NULL,NULL,'VOTE3','<                      _                   / /                     /_\                  < >      ____/\ _________  ____________      \',replace('\>/<\>/<\>/<\/<\>/<\/<\>/<\/<\>/<\/<\>/<\>/<\n<                      _                   /\n/                     /_\                  <\n>      ____/\ _________  ____________      \\n/      \  .  \\  . _/  \/ .__ /\  .  \     >\n<      /\//. //\/ //.  /\_  \/ /\//  /     /\n\    _// // ///  ///  // /   \//  __/_     <\n>    \______\___/\___/\______/_______/     \\n/ Vote, Du Schwein! V3.0 The one and only  >\n<     Voting Door for »»» /X 3.X «««       /\n/<\>/<\>/<\>/<\/<\>/<\/<\>/<\/<\>/<\/<\>/<\>','\n',char(10)),'Vote.Guide',replace('@DATABASE Vote.guide\n@NODE MAIN "Contents"\n\n                       »»» VOTE,DU SCHWEIN V3.0 «««\n\n                      »» Contents of Documentation ««\n\n\n                              @{" Introduction " LINK int}\n                              @{" Requirements " LINK req}\n                              @{" Installation " LINK ins}\n                              @{"Configuration " LINK Con}\n                              @{"  The Menus   " LINK Menu}\n                              @{"   Credits    " LINK Credz}\n			      @{"  Greetings   " LINK Greets}\n                              @{"   History    " LINK Hist}\n                              @{"Other /X doors" LINK doors}\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Credz "Credits"\n@{b}\n                               \  \                  \\n                              \ \  \                   \\n                   ________   ______\_    ________   _\__\___\n                  \\   /  /  \\      /   \\      /  \\   ___/\n         _____    //\ /  /   //\ /\ / \  //\  /\/   //\ __/  _____\n        /____/__ //  /  /   //  /  /    //   /     //     / /____/__\n          /____/..\__  /   ..\__  /  \ ..\  /      .\__  / \  /____/\n                    .\/        .\/  \   ..\/          .\/ \    \\n                                   \ \  \   \              \ \ \\n     ______ ________   _______________\____\______________\___\ _\____\n    .\     \\   /  /  .\   __/\      \   /  \   //  \   ___\ \ \\ \   \\n    //\ /  //\ /  /   //\_  \ /\ /__//\    //\ //  //\ __/ /\  //\ /\ /\n   //  /  //  /  /   //     //  /  //  /  //    \ //     //   //  /\ /\n   .\__  /.\__  /    .\__  /.\__  /.\_/  /.\___\ /.\__  / \  /.\_/  /flc\n      .\/    .\/        .\/    .\/    .\/  \  .\/    .\/  .\/    .\/\\n                                          \ \    \                 \  \\n                                             \ \  \                  \\n                                            \  \                       \\n                                                  \\n\n@{ub}\n                            V·E·R·S·I·O·N  3.0\n\n                          released on 25/01/1994\n\n                          Coding by : Kyle/ARÏSE\n                         Ansis by :  Falcon/ARÏSE\n\n                 It was done for Pater Pink''s Power Board.\n                           Call +49-(0)7244-2199\n\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Int "Introduction"\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n\nVote,Du Schwein! is a door,which allows the users to vote in chartmags on\nYOUR BBS and give them U/L credits for their votings.\nIt is possible to include 9 different "Votingforms".\nThe door will generate an ASCII Texts with the votes of the users for each\nmag.\nSince Version 3.0 it is also possible to U/L adverts (or articles) to the\nvarious mags and the Editor is able to download them.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Req "Requirements"\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n\nTo run "Vote,Du Schwein! V3.0" you need:\n\n-An Amiga model (500/600/1000/1200/2000/2500/3000/4000/CDTV/CD³²)\n-AmiExpress (V3.xx or higher)\n-The following commands in your C: directory:\n  -Copy\n  -Delete\n  -Lha\n  -List\n  -Makedir\n  -Rename\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Ins "Installation"\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n\nTo install "Vote,Du Schwein! V3.0",just do the following things:\n\n-Decrunch the archive\n-Copy the the <Commands> and the <Doors> directories to your BBS directory\n-@{"Configurate" LINK Con} it to your desires.\n-Copy the following commands in your C: directory:\n  -Copy\n  -Delete\n  -Lha\n  -List\n  -Makedir\n  -Rename\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Con "Configuration"\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n\nVote,Du Schwein V3.0 allows you to include the votingforms of up to nine\ndifferent chartmags. To configurate it you have to use these files:\n\n    @{"  Vote.cfg  " LINK voteconf} - The main configuratin file\n    @{" VoteInfo.X " LINK VoteInf} - The info files about the mags\n    @{"VoteHeader.X" LINK VoteHead} - The header files for the mags\n    @{"Questions.X " LINK Quest} - The questions for the mags\n    @{" Editors.X  " LINK Editors} - The names of the editors\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE VoteConf "Vote.cfg"\n@TOC con\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n\nIn the <Vote.cfg> you define the Filenames for your other config files and\nthe amount of different charts and their names.\nYou can edit this files with any editor like ED or CygnusEd.\n\nIt has to look like this:\n\nLine			Function\n1			Filename of the @{" results.X  " LINK result} files\n2                       Filename of the @{"  voters.X  " LINK voters} files\n3                       Filename of the @{" VoteInfo.X " LINK VoteInf} files\n4			Filename of the @{"VoteHeader.X" LINK VoteHead} files\n5			Filename of the @{"Questions.X " LINK Quest} files\n6                       Filename of the @{" Editors.X  " LINK Editors} files\n7                       Filename of the @{"IssueInfo.X " LINK Issue} files\n8                       Path for the    @{"   Ads.X    " LINK Ads} dirs\n9			Filename of the @{"  Log file  " LINK Log}\n10			Amount of mags you want to include\n11/13/15/...		Names of the mags\n12/14/16/...		Amount of U/L credits you want to give the\n			users for voting in this chart.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE result "result.X"\n@TOC con\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n\nIn these files, the door will store the votes of the users.\nWhen the editor selects @{"New Issue" LINK Issue} in the editors menu\nthis file will be deleted.\nThe <.X> will be replaced by the number of the mag.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE voters "voters.X"\n@TOC con\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n\nIn these files, the door will store the slotnumbers of the voters and what\nthey typed at <Filled out by>, to check if a user already voted for this\nissue.\nWhen the editor selects @{"New Issue" LINK Issue} in the editors menu\nthis file will be deleted.\nThe <.X> will be replaced by the number of the mag.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE voteInf "VoteInfo.X"\n@TOC con\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n\nThese files have to be edited by you. Here you can write a small infotext,\nwhich will be displayed, when the user selects Information in the menu.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE voteHead "VoteHeader.X"\n@TOC con\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n\nThese files have to be edited by you. It will be displayed, when a user\nstarts voting. Here you should write the name of the mag and maybe the\nrulez for voting.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Quest "Questions.X"\n@TOC con\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n\nIn these files, you edit the questions. It is really easy to do:\n-To display normal text just type it. If you want the user to edit something\n in the the textline, the line has to start with a "~".\n-To ask the user for any amount of places of any category just type the\n category in one line and a questionmark ("?") followed by the number of\n places (no space) in the next line.\n The have a default answer, just type a space after the amount of places\n and then the default answer.\n-To write simple text, just type it. THE LINE MUST NOT START WITH "~" OR\n "?"!!\nThe door will automatically ask the user, to enter his name.\nIf you do not understand it, just take a look at the examples in the\npresets directory...\nThe answers will be stored in the @{"Results.X" LINK result} files.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE editors "Editors.X"\n@TOC con\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n\nIn these files, you have to enter the names of the editors for the mags.\nOnly an editor is able to enter the @{"Editor Menu" LINK Edit}\nThe <.X> will be replaced by the number of the mag.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE issue "IssueInfo.X"\n@TOC con\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n\nWhen you select New Issue in the @{"Editor Menu" LINK Edit}, this file will\nbe rewritten. It contains the actual issue number and the planned release\ndate.\nIf it does not exist, the door will use "1" as issueno. and "when it''s\nfinished" as release date.\nThe <.X> will be replaced by the number of the mag.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Ads "Ads.X"\n@TOC con\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n\nIn these directories, the door will save the uploaded adverts.\nYou do not need to create these dirs, the door will do it for you.\nThe <.X> will be replaced by the number of the mag.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Log "Log File"\n@TOC con\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n\nIn the Log file the door will store, when a user enters VOTE,DU SCHWEIN\nV3.0 and which Submenus he enters. Also the errormessages will be stored in\nthis file, except when the name of the configfile is wrong, because the\ndoor does not know where the log is. The errormessage will then be stored\nin the Callerslog.\nThe information,what the user does in\nthe submenus will now also be stored in the LOG file, no more in the\n<results.X> files.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Menu "The Menus"\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n\n                             @{" The Main Menu " LINK MainMenu}\n                             @{"  Chart Menus  " LINK Chart}\n                             @{"The Sysop Menu " LINK Sysop}\n                             @{" Editor Menus  " LINK Edit}\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE MainMenu "The Main Menu"\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n\nThe Main Menu is the menu, which you can see, when you start VOTE,DU\nSCHWEIN.\nHere you have the following choices:\n\n1..9 - Enter one of the @{"Chart Menus" LINK Chart}\nI    - View General Information\nQ    - Quit\nS    - Enter the @{"Sysop Menu" LINK Sysop} (of course only if the sysop\n       entered VOTE,DU SCHWEIN.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Chart "The Chart Menus"\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n\nIf you choose a number in the Main Menu, you will enter one of the Chart\nMenus. Here you have the following choices:\n\nV - Vote or, if you already voted, view your vote.\nI - Information about the mag\nU - Upload an advert\nR - Return to the @{"Main Menu" LINK MainMenu}\nIf your name is included in the @{"Editors.X" LINK Editors} file for\nthis mag, you can also enter the @{"Editor Menu" LINK Edit}\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Sysop "The Sysop Menu"\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n\nIf you choose ''S'' in the  @{"Main Menu" LINK MainMenu}, you will enter the Sysop Menu.\nHere you have the following choices:\n\nV - View Configuration\n    View no. of voters and adverts for all mags\nL - Log View\n    View the mainlog\nD - Delete Mainlog\nT - Truncate Mainlog\nR - Return to the @{"Main Menu" LINK MainMenu}\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Edit "Editor Menus"\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n\nIf you choose ''E'' in the Chart Menu, you will enter one the Editor menu\nfor this chart, if you name is included in the @{"Editors.X" LINK Editors} file.\nHere you have the following choices:\n\nL - View/Download list of voters\nV - View votes of user, you can select\nD - Download the @{"results.X" LINK result} file\nN - Begin a new issue and rewrite the @{"IssueInfo.X" LINK Issue} file\nS - View the list of ads for this chart\nT - View an advert\nA - Download adverts as LHA file\nR - Return to @{"Chart Menu" LINK Chart}\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Greets "Greetings"\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n\nGreetings fly to:\n\n@{"      SLAM/ESSENCE    " LINK Slam}\n@{"         KiWi         " LINK CALL}\n@{"       Gandalf        " LINK CALL}\n@{"        Ronny         " LINK CALL}\n@{"     Buster & Fuzz    " LINK CALL}\n@{"         Nose         " LINK CALL}\n@{"        Pencl         " LINK CALL}\n@{"    SMC & Skindiver   " LINK CALL}\n@{"all other cool Freaks!" LINK CALL}\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Slam "Hallo Slam"\n@TOC Greets\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n\nPater Pink meint,warum man hier den Slam Button anklickt,wenn man gar nicht\nSlam ist, und ueberhapt!\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE call "Vote for my BBS!"\n@TOC Greets\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n\n                  Call Pater Pink''s Power Board\n\n                     the official ARÏSE WHQ\n\n                    ask ELITE for the NUMBA!!\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE Hist "History"\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n\nV1.0    First Version\n        It was only possible to vote in "THE OFFICIAL EUROCHARTS,TOO".\nV1.5    Now included config file, so that it is possible to use it for\n        other mags.\nV2.0    Now included the option of 9 different charts in one door\nV2.1    Included the "~" command in the question files\n        First public release\n        Tested for 3 months.\nV2.11	Included the option to choose the number of places for each\n	question.\nV2.12	Changed the Log output to one file. So only real reults will\n	be in the <results.X> files.\nV3.0    Changed Log output\n        Added "Upload Advert" function\n        Added "View your vote" function\n        Added "Default" option in the config file\n        Added Sysop Menu with the following functions:\n         -View Configuration\n         -Log View\n         -Delete Log\n         -Truncate Log\n        Added Editors menu with the following functions:\n         -List of voters\n         -View votes\n         -Download votes\n         -New issue\n         -Show adverts\n         -Type adverts\n         -Advert leeching\n\nKnown bugs:\n-none-\n\nTo be included:\n-Variable amount of mags\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n@ENDNODE\n@NODE doors "Other /X Doors by the ARÏSE /X Power Team"\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n\nReleased:\n\nPower Rulez V1.0        Displays a variable amount of Rulez out of\n                        a rulez file.\nPower Page V1.0         Chat, even is the Sysop is not at home.\n                        (is being beta tested at the moment)\n\nPlanned:\n\nPower Status            hmm...The only cool Power Status\nPower Request           Request door\nPower Partner           Find your Dream Guy on the Board.\n                        (Spaetere Hochzeit nicht ausgeschlossen)\nPower Quest             Question Door for NEWUSER Questions.\nPower Security          Security Door for LogIn. Will support the answers\n                        the user gave in Power Quest.\n\n----------------------------------------------------------------{VOTE!}----\n@ENDNODE\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,76593,14,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048821);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('vsg_me10','VSG-ME10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/VSG-ME10.LHA','*','XIM','mental_v1.0.exe','1.0',NULL,'VSG',NULL,replace('an bug fixed version of MENTAL STATUS V1.0\n','\n',char(10)),'mastrb8.txt',replace(replace('STILL GOING STRONG in 2014!\r\n\r\n                ___         ._            _______             ·\r\n   /\  _________)  \________| \___________)__   /_________:__ :________\r\n  /  \/\  __  \    ____ ___/|  \______  \_  / _/___  \_ ____/ ¦__ \___ \\r\n /   /  \ \__  \___  \  |   |   \  _/  __/ /    /\__  \  |¦   | /  \_|  \\r\n/  \/    \_ \   \ !   \_|   !    \_\    \_     /   \   \ ||   |·    /|   \_\r\n\___|     ___\  /__    /l________ /_\    /__  /_____\  / |¦   |    /_|    /\r\n    l____/-A×E\/  \___/_!       \/   \  /   \/       \/__|:   ¦__ /  l___/\r\n       ______            _____        \/      :    ____   ·   : \/\r\n    ___)     \___________)    \__________:___ ¦____)   \__________\r\n    \    _______     _______    \___    ____/ |\_____   \______   \\r\n   /\___   \/        |    _)    \/       ¦    |/    |    \    |    \\r\n _/    !    \        |    \      \_      |    |     !     \   |     \\r\n \______     \___    |_____\      /___   |    ¦            \  |      \_\r\n       \______/ \____!      \    /   \___|    :________     \_|       /\r\n                             \  /        ¦    ·       \______/|      /\r\n   YOUVE HEARD ABOUT IT!      \/         :    ·               l_____/\r\n       \r\n         MASTURBATiON STATiON AMIGA/PC/CONSOLE/ASCII-ANSI/C64        \r\n               Telnet: bbs.masturbationstationbbs.com\r\n\r\n           UPLOAD DATE: 04-26-16  TIME: 11:18:16  ON NODE: 1\r\n\r\n  UPLOADER: Black Beard            LOCATION: mSTATION.servebbs.com    \r\n\r\n','\r',char(13)),'\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',6317,5,0,NULL,NULL,'vsg_me10','scan',1780048821);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('vsg_me20','VSG-ME20.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/VSG-ME20.LHA',NULL,'XIM','.___.__.______________________________',NULL,NULL,'VSG','____|   (__)  ________  /   ____/   _____/ \   |  _/  \___  \   _  \   \   \   _____)_ \  !  \   /  /   \  \   \   \   \   \    /',replace('    .___.__.______________________________  \n____|   (__)  ________  /   ____/   _____/  \n\   |  _/  \___  \   _  \   \   \   _____)_ \n \  !  \   /  /   \  \   \   \   \   \    / \n  \_____\__\______/______ \___    \______/  \n                         \/   \___/^X×L!    \n               PRESENTS :                   \n                                            \n           MENTAL-STATUS v2.0               \n                                            \n','\n',char(10)),'Mental_V2.0.Guide',replace('@database "GlobalDupe.Guide"\n@WIDTH 77\n@NODE Main "MAIN" "Welcome to Mental-Status Documentation"\n\n  \n                           Mental Status 2.0 (15/06-95)\n     \n                              By Mr.orion / ViSaGe\n                                         \n                          @{"What is Mental Status ?   " LINK "ABOUT"}   \n                          @{"Requirements.             " LINK "REQ"}                \n                          @{"Installation.             " LINK "INSTA"}              \n                          @{"Credits                   " LINK "CREDS"}\n                          @{"Greetings.                " LINK "GREET"}                 \n                          @{"How to contact Me         " LINK "HOWTOCONTACT"}\n              \n@ENDNODE\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n@NODE "ABOUT" "What is Mental Status ?"\n\n\nMental Status V2.0 is an STATUS door to Amiexpress V4.xx+\nwell.. i wanted to make an STATUS door becourze all \n( ALLmost all STATUS doors ) is not so userfriendly like\nthiz door.. i my self thing that tiz door is VERY userfri-\nendly to look at.. there for i deside to make THIZ...\n  \n\n\n\n                   Filesize 