D ·   ·   ·\n          -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-    -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n \n·                  ONE OF DK''S MOST ELiTE AMiGA SySTEMS!                 ·\n·                 SUPPORTiN''  pACMAG · hYDRA · dREAMcHART                ·\n· AFL DKHQ                                                   VANiTY DKHQ ·\n·                      · 3 × uSR V34+ 33600 dUALS ·                      ·\n            ···-········           ···-········           ···-········\n·   NoDE 1: +45-44946208 · NoDE 2: +45-RiNGDOwN · NoDE 3: +45-RiNGDOwN   ·\n            ···^········           ···^········           ···^········\n· SySOP: GiLTHANAS!  ·  DATE: 31-Aug-95 TiME: 09:16:02  ·  A4040, 2.2gB! ·\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',13223,4,0,NULL,NULL,'vty_ad10','scan',1780048821);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('vty_ad12','VTY-AD12.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/VTY-AD12.LHA','Adder','XIM','Adder',NULL,'Wardancer','VTY','_/  |__________   __ __________________|¬\ |   |   _/  _ ¬\_/ ¬\|   _/_\__   __/  |: \_ |:  |   |  __   |    \  :|   ||  :|\__   __/',replace('  ___                                  __\n_/  |__________   __ __________________|¬\\n|   |   _/  _ ¬\_/ ¬\|   _/_\__   __/  |: \_\n|:  |   |  __   |    \  :|   ||  :|\__   __/\n|_______|  :|___|   \____|___||  _|øo|_  |\n ---Y--\____|--\____|----Stz--|_/------\_|\n             Mr. Sinister V1.25\n         Made By Wardancer OfCoz :)\nA Very Kinky .lha Adder For Use With Any /X\nAnd Other Bbs Systems. New in stuff in V1.25\n Includes Two New Types Of Adding, A Couple\n   Of Bug Fixes, Some Optimizing And Some\n        Slight Changes In The Design       \n','\n',char(10)),'reference-board.txt',replace(replace('              W h e r e   t h e   w a r e z   c o m e   f r o m\r\n                                               __                /\_____:\r\n__/\__________________________________________|  \______________/  \    |__\r\n\_   ___________  _______ ________  \__   ___ |   _______  _______  \_  l  \\r\n__\____  \    _l   \    |  \     |___/     |  !    \   _l   \   _| __/\____ \_\r\n\_____    \___\     \___|   \___ !   \__   |_____   \__\     \__\    \____   /\r\n -mNT\_____/---\_____/--l____/-\______/\   |----\____/--\_____/--\____/--\__/\r\n                                        \__|\r\n\r\n- -- --> F A i R L i G H T   S W E D i S H   H E A D Q U A R T E R S <-- -- -\r\n\r\n           reference-board is back 2017 after more than 20 years in coma!\r\n\r\n                        Running on AmiExpress TelNet\r\n\r\n                    Connect to: reference-board.zapto.org:1541\r\n\r\n                    or: www.brysk.se/reference-board/index.htm\r\n               \n              UPLOAD DATE: 01-04-18  TIME: 20:39:05  ON NODE: 0\n','\r',char(13)),'\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',19595,3,0,NULL,NULL,'vty_ad12','scan',1780048821);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('vty_cm11','VTY-CM11.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/VTY-CM11.LHA',NULL,'XIM','___                                  __',NULL,'Dux/VTY','VTY','_/  |__________   __ __________________|¬\ |   |   _/  _ ¬\_/ ¬\|   _/_\__   __/  |: \_ |:  |   |  __   |    \  :|   ||  :|\__   __/',replace('  ___                                  __\n_/  |__________   __ __________________|¬\\n|   |   _/  _ ¬\_/ ¬\|   _/_\__   __/  |: \_\n|:  |   |  __   |    \  :|   ||  :|\__   __/\n|_______|  :|___|   \____|___||  _|øo|_  |\n ---Y--\____|--\____|----Stz--|_/------\_|\n--------------------------------------------\nChat-O-Mater V1.1 For /X V3.x     By Dux/VTY\n             New and Improved...\n--------------------------------------------\n','\n',char(10)),'Meter.doc',replace('.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.\no                                                                           o\n.                             Chat-O-Meter v1.1                             .\no                                                                           o\n.                               by Dux/Vanity                               .\no                                                                           o\n.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.\n\n\n\n                                 Introduction\n                                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~\nChat-O-Meter will tell you exactly how long you''ve been chatting, and will\nalso make a top-bulletin with your top-chatters.\n\n\n                                 Installation\n                                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~\nJust copy the contents of the archive to your BBS: directory or install in\nmanually as an XIM door.\n\nRemember that you need T: assigned somewhere, since Chat-O-Meter uses it for\nsome temporary files.\n\nThen you need to configure Chat-O-Meter with these tooltypes:\n\n"OUTPUT=" will define where you want a top-bull created. If you don''t want\na top-bull just remove the "OUTPUT=" tooltype.\n\n"SHOW_CHATTIME" will define whether you want to show how long the chat took\nafter each chat. If you don''t want to show it just remove it.\n\n"SHOW_TOP" will define whether you want to show the top-chats after each chat.\n\n"NUMBER_OF_USERS=" will define how many entries you want on your\ntop-chat-bull. Default is 10.\n\n\nNow you need to add these lines to your Node{x}/StartChat.txt and\nNode{x}/EndChat.txt:\n\n--CUT--\n~\n~CC_METER\n--CUT--\n\nAnd that''s it for the installation.\n\n\n                                   History\n                                   ~~~~~~~\nv1.0\nFirst release - No known bugs\n\nv1.1\nSecond public release - still no know bugs\nAdded tooltypes to configure\nAdded top-chat-bull\nImproved the speed of the code a bit\n\n\n                                How to contact\n                                ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nYou can reach me on my own board Mainline; +45-9815 3062/+45-9815 3562 or\nthrough /Xnet at Dux@DK0001 or on any major board in Denmark.\n\nIf you use this tool please contact me, as I''d like to know who''s using it.\n\n\n                                    Greets\n                                    ~~~~~~\nWardancer - Tarzan - Ramirez - Devilstar - Lector - Scratch - Van Damme - JSon\nEmpire\n\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,60035,6,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048821);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('vty_cs11','VTY-CS11.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/VTY-CS11.LHA',NULL,'XIM','Z1.EXE',NULL,'pARANOID/vTY','VTY','_/  |__________   __ __________________|¬\ |   |   _/  _ ¬\_/ ¬\|   _/_\__   __/  |: \_ |:  |   |  __   |    \  :|   ||  :|\__   __/',replace('  ___                                  __\n_/  |__________   __ __________________|¬\\n|   |   _/  _ ¬\_/ ¬\|   _/_\__   __/  |: \_\n|:  |   |  __   |    \  :|   ||  :|\__   __/\n|_______|  :|___|   \____|___||  _|øo|_  |\n ---Y--\____|--\____|----Stz--|_/------\_|\n--------------------------------------------\n  cRAZY sTATS v1.1 /X dOOR bY pARANOID/vTY\n--------------------------------------------','\n',char(10)),'crazystats11.doc',replace('                                                           ____       ._.\n   ________.________.________.________.________.________._(____)______| |\n __\_    _ |\_    _ |\_    _ |\_    _ |\_    _ |\_    _ |\_    |\_    _ | __\n.::Y     !  Y     !  Y     |  Y     !  Y     |  Y     |  Y      Y     |  Y::.\n.::|     ___|     _  |     |__|     _  |     |  |     !  |      |     !  |sT.\n¯\:|     |::|     |  |     |::|     |  |     |  |        |      |        |:/¯\n  ¯`-----''¯¯`-----^--^-----''¯¯`-----^--^-----^--^--------^------^--------''¯\n                                 () F\n              __        __         __             __        __\n         ____/ l___   _/ l___   __ | \_   __   ___l \_   ___l \_\n         \_    |   \_/       \_/  \l   \_/  \_/       \_/   |   \__\n          :|.   |    Y.   |    Y. _ \_   Y   .Y    _   .Y_____   ._%\n          ÷||   l    l|   _    l|  \     l   |l____l   |l    |   ||÷\n          :l         |    |    |    \    |    l_Stz|    |    l    l:\n          :¯\_  .___/¯\_  |___/¯\_  |\__/¯\_  _/   |  _/¯\___.  _/¯:\n          `---\_l-------\_l-------\_l-------\_l----l_/-------l_/---''\n\n            P R E S E N T S   -  C R A Z Y  S T A T S   V 1 . 1\n\nCRAZYSTATS V1.1 is a nice n'' cool replacement for the normal S command.\nIt displays a nice big list of infos to the user.. The usual stuff and\nalso some more.. The first screen shown in CRAZYSTATS is the normal info\nthat most users would want to view.. HANDLE/UPLOADS/CALLS etc. The user\nis then asked if he/she would like to view more info.. If this is done\nthen there is some really neat things... The user is shown extra infos,\nand is asked if he/she would like to download a BBS AD! Yep.. If yes then\nthe program will send your ad, if no then it will return to the BBS..\n \nI didn''t feel there was enuff need to facilitate an option for the sysop\nto specify the name and directory of the BBS ad, why bother including a\nconfig file with just one line? So for this reason you must call your\nBBS ad "BOARD.AD" and it must be located in the S: directory! To install\nthe door simply copy the various files across from the archive into the\nidentical directories on your HD.. eg. copy:\n \n        BBS/DOORS/PARANOID/crazystats11.rexx\n\nTo your hard drive, in the same directories.. If you dont have a PARANOID\ndirectory in your doors dir then make one, so my name can be on everyone''s\nhard drive!! heheh.. \n\nThats all for now dudes, enjoy the door, install it.. tell me if ya like it!\n\nSOME GREETS NOW! - IN ALPHABETICAL ORDER!\n\n			BREN/AFL\n			BUGBYTE/TRZ\n			CAFFEINE/AFL\n			DEL & KICK/IND\n			FURY/TRZ\n			GAZZER/IND\n			GILTHANAS/2kAD\n			GREEN-BERET/VTY\n			HELLHOUND/VTY\n			HIGHLANDER/GOD\n			HOGSTER/FLT\n			JAY/VTY\n			KILLERETTE/SR\n			KRONION/VTY\n			LEGEND/DLM?\n			MR.VAIN/$CP?\n			NORSKE/PDY\n			O.B.1./VTY\n			RECYCLER/HMN\n			SHOCK/CSL\n			SILIKON/IND\n			SPLATT/FLT\n			SUPERTOUCH/HMN\n			TANGO/OGN\n			TARZAN/CSL\n			THE FREAK/VTY\n			TIN MAN/VTY\n			ULTRAMARINE\n                        VOYAGER+SNOWQUEEN/IND\n			WARDANCER/VTY\n			ZANY/VTY\n			ZOLDAN/SCL\n\nAnd all those guys who I think I have on the list.. But dont.. sorry dudes,\nI''m damn forgetful.. just remind me next time we chat! And all at H&V who\nI dont really know... L8erz! And call H&V boards... Contact me on these,\nfind the numbers and NUP''s yaself!\n \nDARK DOMAIN - FORBIDDEN PLANET - SUSPERIA - ROAD TO NOWHERE - FASTRAX\n  HOUSE OF PAIN - PRIORITY 1 - USS ENTERPRISE - PLASTIC PASSION \nWARES UNLIMITED - AND MANY MANY MORE COOL BOARDS EVERYWHERE! LATER BROS!\n\n[PARANOID/VTY]\n\n           __ _   _         _  _ __ _____ __ _  _          _  _ __\n          /                                                       \\n   .-/\--/---------------------------------------------------------\--/\-.\n   |/  \/ ______      ______      _____     ______ ______     _____ \/  \|\n  _/  ___/_____/_____/_____/_ ___/____/_ __/_____//_____/_ __/____/_     \_\n ¡ |  \_______     _/_____   \\______   \\__    \¯______  \\______  \    ¡ ¡\n : |   /     /     /     /   \\     /    \/    //     /    \    /    \   | |\n : :   \\   /    //          //    //    /     /    _/_____/____     /   | :\n . :    \___     /_____/     /____/     /_____/     /         /     /    : :\n_  . /\_   \____/     /¯____/    /¯____/     /¯____/         /_____/ _/\ : ._\n \  /                                                                   \. /\n  \/----------------------> V · A · N · I · T · Y <----------------------\/\n\n  . _ __ _________  /\________________________  /\__________________ __ _ .\n -÷---[ NAME ]----\/---[ NDZ ]-----[ NUMBER ]-\/--[ BAUD ]---[ SYSOP ]---÷\n  |                                                                      |\n  |  DARK DOMAIN          4   +1 30 5989 0718  WHQ  16.8D   TIN MAN      |\n  ·  SUSPERIA             2   +45   4343 4236  SCHQ 14.4d   ZANY         |\n  |  SOMEWHERE ONLINE     2   +45   5965 3801  DKHQ 16.8d   HELLHOUND    |\n  |  FORBiDDEN-PLANET     2   +353  1820 8489  IRHQ 16.8D   GREEN BERET  |\n  |                                                                      |\n -¦---[ NAME ]----/\---[ NDZ ]-----[ NUMBER ]-/\--[ BAUD ]---[ SYSOP ]---¦-\n  : ¯ ¯¯ ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯  \/¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯  \/¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯ ¯¯ ¯ :\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',25008,11,0,NULL,NULL,'vty_cs11','scan',1780048830);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('vty_li13','VTY-LI13.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/VTY-LI13.LHA','WarList','XIM','WarList',NULL,'WarDancer/VTY','VTY','_/  |__________   __ __________________|¬\ |   |   _/  _ ¬\_/ ¬\|   _/_\__   __/  |: \_ |:  |   |  __   |    \  :|   ||  :|\__   __/',replace('  ___                                  __\n_/  |__________   __ __________________|¬\\n|   |   _/  _ ¬\_/ ¬\|   _/_\__   __/  |: \_\n|:  |   |  __   |    \  :|   ||  :|\__   __/\n|_______|  :|___|   \____|___||  _|øo|_  |\n ---Y--\____|--\____|----Stz--|_/------\_|\n--------------------------------------------\nWarList V1.3 For /X V3.xx   By WarDancer/VTY\n   BoardList Program, New Fields Added...\n--------------------------------------------\n<<<<------------[ MEN-TEL BBS ]--------->>>>\n','\n',char(10)),'WarList.guide',replace('@database WarListDoc\n@Author Wardancer/Vanity\n@Index MAIN\n\nCopyright 1994 Wardancer/Vanity\n\n@node MAIN "WarPage V1.0 Documentation."\n\n                  ___                                  __\n                _/  |__________   __ __________________|¬\\n                |   |   _/  _ ¬\_/ ¬\|   _/_\__   __/  |: \_\n                |:  |   |  __   |    \  :|   ||  :|\__   __/\n                |_______|  :|___|   \____|___||  _|øo|_  |\n                 ---Y--\____|--\____|----Stz--|_/------\_|\n                ------------------(Presents)----------------\n                                 WarList V1.3\n                --------------------------------------------\n\n                         Made by : Wardancer/Vanity\n\n\n\n                             Table of contents :\n\n                           @{"     Whats this ?     " Link 01}\n                           @{"     Installation     " Link 02}\n                           @{"        Greets        " Link 03}\n                           @{"   Bug report/ideas   " Link 04}\n                           @{"       History        " Link 05}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node 01 "Whats this ?"\n\n  ========================================================================\n\n  WarList is a boardlist  program where  users can enter thier fav. board.\n  The  programs  supports  the  following  fields : Name,  Number,  Nodes,\n  Syspop,  Status,  Modem, NUP, Syspw, and an  optional note. Please  note\n  that users with 250 and above in security level can reset the list.\n\n  ========================================================================\n\n@endnode\n\n@node 02 "Installation"\n\n  ========================================================================\n\n  Installing  this program is really  quite simple, the  only things you\n  have to is to make sure the following is right :\n\n  Program      Location          Description\n  -------      --------          -----------\n  WarList      Doors:WarList     The main program\n  List         Doors:WarList     The list of baords that will\n                                 be displayed\n  Templist     Doors:WarList     File containing board data\n  Front        Doors:WarList     Front banner that is copied to\n                                 list\n  End          Doors:WarList     End banner that is copied to\n                                 list\n\n  Also make sure that list.info is in the commands/bbscmd drawer.\n\n  ========================================================================\n\n@endnode\n\n@node 03 "Greets"\n\n  ========================================================================\n\n  I would like to greet the following in no order :\n\n  Kronion, Dux, The Freak, Ramirez, Omar, Striker, Playmate, Calvin,\n  Plexer, Gilthanas, Energy, Shamer, Tactica, Zany, Zeke, Spike,\n  Delirium&Kickface, Mike&Tofke, Norske, Chock, Paranoid, OB1, Curmit,\n  Tin Man, Mandrake, Mr. Orion, Mr. Beer, Marty, Nookman, Poison, Json,\n  Conan&Newton, Tarzan, Jake, HAL 9000, D-Day, Cracy Creep, Mr. Vain,\n  Overlord, Stezotehic, Tango, Json, Deature, Spacebrain, Enzo,\n  G0blin, Aquarius, Cockroach, Bugbyte, Hoffi, Triple B, Curt Cool,\n  G.O.D, Lector, Nashua, Paxdei, Tas, Caesar, Nero, Undertaker, Zinko,\n  Laxity, Devilstar, Carebear, Wolfman, Ozone&Rob, Janitor, NSL,\n  Mr. Hyde, Relief, Kreon, Fozzi, Green-Beret, Jay, O.B.1.\n\n      And all other Vanity members and people I forgot.\n\n  Specials go to :\n\n  Kronion .......................... For being a great leader\n  Dux .............................. For helping me with AmiExpress\n  Ramirez .......................... For letting me test at your board\n  Omar ............................. For all sorts of crazy conversation\n  Json ............................. Also for letting me test at your BBS\n  Aquarius ......................... For helping me with /X at TG94\n  Nero ............................. Cool board\n\n  ========================================================================\n\n@endnode\n\n@node 04 "Bug report/ideas"\n\n  ========================================================================\n\n  Send your bug reports or ideas to the following boards :\n\n  Dark Domain ............ +1   305-989-0718 (Vanity WHQ)\n  Susperia ............... +45  434-342-36   (Vanity SCHQ)\n  Somewhere Online ....... +45  597-538-01   (Vanity DKHQ)\n  Forbidden Planet ....... +353 182-084-89   (Vanity IRHQ)\n  Suffocation ............ +45  491-807-60   (The board where I test my doors)\n  Mainline ............... +45  981-530-62   (Also supports netmail)\n  Static Chaos ........... +45  864-395-14   (Another testsite)\n\n  You can also leave a msg to ''WarDancer@DK0001''\n\n  ======================================================================== \n\n@endnode\n\n@node 05 "History"\n\n  ========================================================================\n\n  V1.0 - Not released to anybody else than Suffocation.\n\n  V1.1 - Changed layout completly.\n       - Allowed more data to be entered.\n\n  V1.2 - Minor changes (not released).\n\n  V1.3 - New fields added.\n\n  ========================================================================\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',19054,8,0,NULL,NULL,'vty_li13','scan',1780048830);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('vty_ol03','VTY-OL03.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/VTY-OL03.LHA','WarOLM','XIM','WarOLM',NULL,'Wardancer/Vanity','VTY','_/  |__________   __ __________________|¬\ |   |   _/  _ ¬\_/ ¬\|   _/_\__   __/  |: \_ |:  |   |  __   |    \  :|   ||  :|\__   __/',replace('  ___                                  __\n_/  |__________   __ __________________|¬\\n|   |   _/  _ ¬\_/ ¬\|   _/_\__   __/  |: \_\n|:  |   |  __   |    \  :|   ||  :|\__   __/\n|_______|  :|___|   \____|___||  _|øo|_  |\n ---Y--\____|--\____|----Stz--|_/------\_|\n------------------(Presents)----------------\n   WarOLM V0.3 Coded By: Wardancer/Vanity\nAnother ''Online Message'' Door, Just Better..\n Supports ''blacklisting'', ''colors'', ''cursor\n   keys'' and LOADS of other neat stuff...\n--------------------------------------------\n','\n',char(10)),'WarOLM.Guide',replace('@database WarOLMDoc\n@Author Wardancer/Vanity\n@Index MAIN\n\nCopyright 1995 Wardancer/Vanity\n\n@node MAIN "WarOLM V0.3 Documentation."\n\n    THe PHuCKiNG /X DuDeS FRoM VANi7Y iS PRouD To BRiNG you aNoTHeR DooR\n                  ___                                  __\n                _/  |__________   __ __________________|¬\\n                |   |   _/  _ ¬\_/ ¬\|   _/_\__   __/  |: \_\n                |:  |   |  __   |    \  :|   ||  :|\__   __/\n                |_______|  :|___|   \____|___||  _|øo|_  |\n                 ---Y--\____|--\____|----Stz--|_/------\_|\n                ------------------(Presents)----------------\n                @{BG FILL}                 WarOLM  V0.3               @{BG BACKGROUND}\n                --------------------------------------------\n\n                aND THiS TiMe iT iS MaDe By Wardancer/Vanity\n\n                             Table of contents :\n\n                           @{".....Whats This ?....." link 01}\n                           @{".....Installation....." link 02}\n                           @{"........Greets........" link 03}\n                           @{"...Bug report/ideas..." link 04}\n                           @{".......History........" link 05}\n                           @{"...R_E_G_I_S_T_E_R...." link 06}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node 01 "Whats This ?..."\n\n  =========================[   Whats This ?   ]===========================\n\n  WarOLM is an ''OnLine Message'' program that allows users to send messages\n  to other nodes, so that they can deliver brief messages to each other in\n  a relatively quick way.\n\n  So, what makes WarOLM special compared to the countless number of other\n  OLM doors already available, I will tell you... WarOLM supports the\n  following features: Cursor Keys Select...\n                      Neat Blacklisting Module...\n                      Color Support In OLM Message...\n                      Icon Config FIle...\n                      Cool Ascii By Zany/Vty...\n                      Reciever Does Not Have To Be Idle...\n                      Mainline supports (eg. ''OLM 1'')...\n\n  But you just wait and see, more stuff will be added in later version,\n  which should be reason enough for you to register your version.\n\n  To use WarOLM just install it as described and enter ''olm'' at the\n  prompt, a fanzy menu should appear. To access the blacklisting module,\n  you should type ''olm blacklist'' at the prompt. Furthermore, you can\n  also type specify which node you wish to send to at the prompt by typing\n  ''olm x'' where x is the nodenumber.\n\n  =========================[   Whats This ?   ]===========================\n\n@endnode\n\n@node 02 "Installation..."\n\n  =========================[   Installation   ]===========================\n\n  Installing this program is really quite simple, the only things you have\n  to is to make sure the following is right :\n\n  Program      Location                      Description\n  -------      --------                      -----------\n  WarOLM       Doors:!!!WAR!!!/WarOLM/       The main program...\n               (It doesn''t have to be there\n               exactly, put remember to\n               update in olm.info if you\n               change the path)\n  Config.info  Doors:!!!WAR!!!/WarOLM/       Config file...\n\n  The Config file is quite simple, so anybody should be able to alter it\n  as they please, here are the tooltypes:\n\n  LOWNODE=xx              Where ''xx'' is the lowest nodenumber which\n                          WarOLM will display, this tooltype is optional,\n                          it will default to 0 if it is not set.\n\n  HIGNNODE=xx             Where ''xx'' is the highest nodenumber which\n                          WarOLM will display, this tooltype is NOT\n                          optional.\n\n  ASK_BEFORE_SENDING=xxx  Where ''xxx'' is either ''YES'' or ''NO'', if it is a\n                          ''YES'' then WarOLM will ask the user if he/she\n                          is sure that he/she wants to send the message\n                          he/she just typed. This tooltype is optional,\n                          and it will default to ''NO'' if not set.\n\n  NOTE: The HIGHNODE value must always be higher or equal the LOWNODE\n        value.\n\n  Furthermore, to enable blacklisting, you hve to create a drawer called\n  ''DOORS:!!!WAR!!!/WAROLM/LISTS''\n\n  Also make sure that olm.info is in the commands/bbscmd drawer. To use\n  this door most effectively, the command icon must be named olm.info,\n  this is because of the mainline support that wont work if the command\n  name is anything else than ''olm'' (case insensitive).\n\n  =========================[   Installation   ]===========================\n\n@endnode\n\n@node 03 "Greets..."\n\n  =========================[      Greets      ]===========================\n\n  @{BG FILL}                 GReeTZ Go ouT To THe FoLLoWiNG DuDeS:                  @{BG BACKGROUND}\n\n  Dux, Kronion, Zeke, Mickey, Tactica, Mandrake, Nookman, Sorcerer,\n  The Freak, Melomaniac, Marty, Morph, Deature, Json, D-Tron, Webster,\n  Gilthanas, Striker, Hellhound, Devilstar, Zinko, Lector, Playmate,\n  Paranoid, Enzo, Menace, Ironman, Nashua, Ramirez, Omar, Nero, Janitor,\n  Conan, Newton, Relief, The Priest\n\n   Mega Super Special Fantastic Thanks To ZANY/VTY At Susperia For Making\n  All That Great Ascii For Me, Thanks Dude, It Made It Look So Much Better\n\n  =========================[      Greets      ]===========================\n\n@endnode\n\n@node 04 "Bug Report/Ideas..."\n\n  =========================[ Bug Report/Ideas ]===========================\n\n  Send your bug reports or ideas to the following boards :\n\n  Susperia ............... +45  434-342-36   (VANiTY SCHQ)\n  Somewhere Online ....... +45  597-538-01   (VANiTY DKHQ)\n\n  You can also leave a msg on the InterNet to me at [email removed]\n\n  If you would like to betatest for me, then just contact me at Susperia.\n\n  =========================[ Bug Report/Ideas ]===========================\n\n@endnode\n\n@node 05 "History..."\n\n  =========================[      History     ]===========================\n\n  V0.1 - First version, never went beyond Susperia...\n\n  V0.2 - Made a nice menu system, incorporated Ascii from Zany, and\n         finally added the blacklisting module...\n\n  V0.3 - Added color support...\n\n  =========================[      History     ]===========================\n\n@endnode\n\n@node 06 "Registration Info..."\n\n  =========================[   Registration   ]===========================\n\n  So, why should you register your Wardancer doors, here is a couple of\n  reasons...\n\n  1)     You will get a registered version with your handle & board name\n         in it.\n\n  2)     You will get all future versions some time before they are\n         released.\n\n  3)     If you desperately need a special door for your board, then the\n         chance that I will actually get around to programming it is much\n         larger if you show that you are serious by registering.\n\n  4)     You will get access to a lot of my source-code (Information\n         Wants To Be Free).\n\n  So how fo you register your Wardancer doors, there are 2 ways...\n\n  1)     Drop a message to me on any Vanity board.\n\n  2)     Drop a message to my email account ([email removed]).\n\n  The message should comtain the following information:\n\n                          ... The Names Of The War Doors You Are\n                              Currently Using\n                          ... The Name AND Number Of Your Board\n                              (Includinf, Ofcoz, Any Nups or Syspw''s)\n                          ... Why You Want To Register\n                          ... If You Have Email, Your Email Address,\n                              So That I Can UUEncode And Email You\n                              The Future Versions\n\n  Believe it or not, that is all it takes to register. Since I dont charge\n  you $$$, you will have to be the one who has to pick up the updates at\n  one of our boards, which is also why I would prefer if you have an email\n  address where I can mail your updates to.\n\n  =========================[   Registering   ]============================\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',20285,6,0,NULL,NULL,'vty_ol03','scan',1780048830);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('vty_os10','VTY-OS10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/VTY-OS10.LHA','OStat','XIM','___                                  __',NULL,'Dux/Vanity','VTY','_/  |__________   __ __________________|¬\ |   |   _/  _ ¬\_/ ¬\|   _/_\__   __/  |: \_ |:  |   |  __   |    \  :|   ||  :|\__   __/',replace('  ___                                  __\n_/  |__________   __ __________________|¬\\n|   |   _/  _ ¬\_/ ¬\|   _/_\__   __/  |: \_\n|:  |   |  __   |    \  :|   ||  :|\__   __/\n|_______|  :|___|   \____|___||  _|øo|_  |\n ---Y--\____|--\____|----Stz--|_/------\_|\n--------------------------------------------\n         OStat v1.00 for AmiExpress\n      Allow users to view others stats      \n               By Dux/Vanity\n--------------------------------------------\n','\n',char(10)),'OStat.doc',replace('.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.\no                                                                           o\n.                                OStat v1.00                                .\no                                                                           o\n.                               by Dux/Vanity                               .\no                                                                           o\n.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.\n\n\n\n                                 Introduction\n                                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThis is a AmiExpress door that will let your users view other users stats, eg.\nup/dn bytes/files, number of calls, when he/she last called etc.\n\n\n                                 Installation\n                                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~\nJust copy the supplied files to your BBS: directory or install it manually as\nan XIM door.\n\n\n                                   History\n                                   ~~~~~~~\nv1.00\nFirst release - no known bugs\n\n\n                                How to contact\n                                ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nYou can reach me on my own board Mainline; +45-9815 3062/+45-9815 3562 or\nthrough /Xnet at Dux@DK0001 or on any major board in Denmark.\n\nIf you use this tool please contact me, as I''d like to know who''s using it.\n\n\n                                    Greets\n                                    ~~~~~~\nWardancer - Tarzan - Ramirez - Devilstar - Lector - Scratch - Van Damme - JSon\nEmpire\n\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,28769,3,0,NULL,NULL,'vty_os10_ostat','scan',1780048830);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('vty_pc10','VTY-PC10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/VTY-PC10.LHA','PowerComment','XIM','____           ____   ____',NULL,NULL,'VTY','____ /   /_/\  _____(____)__\_  \ ____ ---\   Y   / ._ \/     \   (_   _)  Y   /--M \     /  _/  \  |   \   |   |\_   _/   A',replace('         ____           ____   ____\n   ____ /   /_/\  _____(____)__\_  \ ____\n---\   Y   / ._ \/     \   (_   _)  Y   /--M\n    \     /  _/  \  |   \   |   |\_   _/   A\n-----\___/___|    \_|    \__|   |-|   |----!\n             |____/ |____/  |___| `---''\n      MeNaCe/Vanity & Opaque presents:\n             POWERCOMMENT v1.00\n Multiple Designs, Argument Support, Online\n Configuration, Arrow Support, Diff. Setups\n         For Each Conference ect..\n            Released: 27-sep-95\n','\n',char(10)),'PowerComment.doc',replace('\n                            Power Comment V1.00\n\n                              Coded By MeNaCe\n\nDescription:\n============\n\nPowerComment is a powerfull multicomment door which many features like:\n\n-> Nice design using 16-colours!\n-> Online configuation - NO ICONS!\n-> Possible to make bar''s between entries.\n-> Each conference can have a diffrent setup (local config)\n-> Arrow key support\n-> Argument support\n-> Multiple designs available.\n\nInstallation:\n=============\n\nJust  install  this  door  as  any other XIM doors.  PowerComment have been\ntested  ok on both AmiExpress and Sigma so there should be no problems.  If\nthere is - please contact me right away!\n\nConfiguation:\n=============\n\n(Access 250+ needed)\nTo configuate the door - press ''c'' to start the door, then press ''c'' (again)\nwhich will bring up the configuation-screen. From here you can modify the door\nsuit your needs. Try it, it''s really easy.\n\nLast Words:\n===========\n\nSorry for this quite bad doc - but i *hate* writing ''em :(\n\nIf you have some designs for the door please don''t hesitate to contact me; Call\niMPERiAL  - +45 58286107 leave a comment or page me.  Or you can leave me a\nmessage on most danish boards. (Handle: MeNaCe).\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,16644,2,0,NULL,NULL,'vty_pc10_powercomment','scan',1780048830);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('vty_ql11','VTY-QL11.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/VTY-QL11.LHA',NULL,'XIM','___                                  __',NULL,'Dux/Vanity','VTY','_/  |__________   __ __________________|¬\ |   |   _/  _ ¬\_/ ¬\|   _/_\__   __/  |: \_ |:  |   |  __   |    \  :|   ||  :|\__   __/',replace('  ___                                  __\n_/  |__________   __ __________________|¬\\n|   |   _/  _ ¬\_/ ¬\|   _/_\__   __/  |: \_\n|:  |   |  __   |    \  :|   ||  :|\__   __/\n|_______|  :|___|   \____|___||  _|øo|_  |\n ---Y--\____|--\____|----Stz--|_/------\_|\n--------------------------------------------\n      Quick Logon v1.1 for AmiExpress\n   Allows users to choose their logontype\n              By Dux/Vanity\n--------------------------------------------','\n',char(10)),'QLogon.doc',replace('.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.\no                                                                           o\n.                              Quick Logon v1.1                             .\no                                                                           o\n.                               by Dux/Vanity                               .\no                                                                           o\n.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.\n\n\n\n                                 Introduction\n                                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~\nHave you ever wanted to give your users a choice between viewing a lot of\nbulls(hit) at login or just loggin in fast? If yes, then this is the door\nyou''ve been looking for.\n\n\n                                 Installation\n                                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~\nJust copy the contents of the archive to your BBS: directory or install the\ndoor manually as an XIM.\n\nThen you need to modify your BBS:Bull.txt to look something like this:\n\n--CUT--\n~\n~CC_QLOGON\n--CUT--\n\nNow you just need to configure the QuickLogon with these tooltypes:\n"QUICK" this is the path of the loginscript used when choosing a quicklogon.\n\n"NOQUICK" this is the path when choosing a normal logon.\n\n"SHOW_ALL" this is the path of the loginscript that will be showed to\neveryone. Use this for stuff that should otherwise have been in both the\nQUICK-text and the NOQUICK-text. Leave out this tooltype if you don''t want to\nuse it.\n\n"FORCE.{baud}" this is the path of the loginscripts that will be forced upon a\ncertain baudrate, so you can eg. have large ansi-logins for your 14400+ users\nand a normal ascii-login for your 2400 users. Leave out this tooltype if you\ndon''t want to use it.\n\n\nAnd that''s about it for the installation. Look at the supplied files if you\nneed more info.\n\n\n                                   History\n                                   ~~~~~~~\nv1.0\nFirst release - no known bugs\n\nv1.1\nSecond public release - still no known bugs\nAdded SHOW_ALL tooltype\nAdded FORCE.{baud} tooltype\n\n\n                                How to contact\n                                ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nYou can reach me on my own board Mainline; +45-9815 3062/+45-9815 3562 or\nthrough /Xnet at Dux@DK0001 or on any major board in Denmark.\n\nIf you use this tool please contact me, as I''d like to know who''s using it.\n\n\n                                    Greets\n                                    ~~~~~~\nWardancer - Tarzan - Ramirez - Devilstar - Lector - Scratch - Van Damme - JSon\nEmpire\n\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,30928,5,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048830);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('vty_rw10','VTY-RW10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/VTY-RW10.LHA',NULL,'XIM','___                                  __',NULL,'Dux/Vanity','VTY','_/  |__________   __ __________________|¬\ |   |   _/  _ ¬\_/ ¬\|   _/_\__   __/  |: \_ |:  |   |  __   |    \  :|   ||  :|\__   __/',replace('  ___                                  __\n_/  |__________   __ __________________|¬\\n|   |   _/  _ ¬\_/ ¬\|   _/_\__   __/  |: \_\n|:  |   |  __   |    \  :|   ||  :|\__   __/\n|_______|  :|___|   \____|___||  _|øo|_  |\n ---Y--\____|--\____|----Stz--|_/------\_|\n--------------------------------------------\n      Realtime Who v1.0 for /X v3.35+       \n         Realtime updating Who door\n              By Dux/Vanity\n--------------------------------------------','\n',char(10)),'RealtimeWho.doc',replace('.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.\no                                                                           o\n.                             Realtime Who v1.0                             .\n.                                                                           .\no                                                                           o\n.                               by Dux/Vanity                               .\no                                                                           o\n.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.o.\n\n\n\n                                 Introduction\n                                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~\nThe Realtime Who (RW) is almost like any other who-door for /X, BUT with one\nexception; RW will keep running''n''updating until you quit it. This means that\nthe users don''t have to run the who-door 1.000 times to see if another user is\nready for a multichat. They can just start RW and then watch and wait.\n\n\n                                 Installation\n                                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~\nTo install it, just copy the contents of the archive to your BBS: directory or\ninstall it manually as an XIM door.\n\nThen you need to configure RW. The tooltypes are like this:\n\nNODE.{x}= Is used to define the phonenumber for each of the nodes. Eg.\nNODE.1=+45-9815 3062. If you don''t want the number to appear, just leave out\nthe tooltype for that node.\n\n\n                                   History\n                                   ~~~~~~~\nv0.6\nOnly worked on the 9 node version of /X.\n\nv1.0\nThis version works on the 32 node version of /X.\nAlso uses semaphores so unneccesary disk-activity is avoided.\n\n\n                                How to contact\n                                ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\nYou can reach me on my own board Mainline; +45-9815 3062/+45-9815 3562 or\nthrough /Xnet at Dux@DK0001 or on any major board in Denmark.\n\nIf you use this tool please contact me, as I''d like to know who''s using it.\n\n\n                                    Greets\n                                    ~~~~~~\nWardancer - Tarzan - Ramirez - Devilstar - Lector - Scratch - Van Damme - JSon\nEmpire\n\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,35010,6,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048830);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('vty_sm10','VTY-SM10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/VTY-SM10.LHA',NULL,'XIM','___                                  __',NULL,'pARANOID/vTY','VTY','_/  |__________   __ __________________|¬\ |   |   _/  _ ¬\_/ ¬\|   _/_\__   __/  |: \_ |:  |   |  __   |    \  :|   ||  :|\__   __/',replace('  ___                                  __\n_/  |__________   __ __________________|¬\\n|   |   _/  _ ¬\_/ ¬\|   _/_\__   __/  |: \_\n|:  |   |  __   |    \  :|   ||  :|\__   __/\n|_______|  :|___|   \____|___||  _|øo|_  |\n ---Y--\____|--\____|----Stz--|_/------\_|\n--------------------------------------------\n  sTAT mASTER v1.o /X dOOR bY pARANOID/vTY\n--------------------------------------------\n<<<<------------[ MEN-TEL BBS ]--------->>>>\n','\n',char(10)),'smaster.doc',replace('                                                           ____       ._.\n   ________.________.________.________.________.________._(____)______| |\n __\_    _ |\_    _ |\_    _ |\_    _ |\_    _ |\_    _ |\_    |\_    _ | __\n.::Y     !  Y     !  Y     |  Y     !  Y     |  Y     |  Y      Y     |  Y::.\n.::|     ___|     _  |     |__|     _  |     |  |     !  |      |     !  |sT.\n¯\:|     |::|     |  |     |::|     |  |     |  |        |      |        |:/¯\n  ¯`-----''¯¯`-----^--^-----''¯¯`-----^--^-----^--^--------^------^--------''¯\n                                 () F\n              __        __         __             __        __\n         ____/ l___   _/ l___   __ | \_   __   ___l \_   ___l \_\n         \_    |   \_/       \_/  \l   \_/  \_/       \_/   |   \__\n          :|.   |    Y.   |    Y. _ \_   Y   .Y    _   .Y_____   ._%\n          ÷||   l    l|   _    l|  \     l   |l____l   |l    |   ||÷\n          :l         |    |    |    \    |    l_Stz|    |    l    l:\n          :¯\_  .___/¯\_  |___/¯\_  |\__/¯\_  _/   |  _/¯\___.  _/¯:\n          `---\_l-------\_l-------\_l-------\_l----l_/-------l_/---''\n\n\n\n            P R E S E N T S   -  S T A T M A S T E R   V 1 . 0\n\nSTATMASTER V1.0 is a small, nice looking /X door.. It has been tested on\n/X 3.37 and /X 3.38.. should be oki on other older versions! Hmm, the\ndoor is just a little info displayer for users who are about to file\ntransfer to or from your board... It will show them the amount they have\nuploaded and downloaded in KBYTES and also the amount of files.. And will\ndisplay a small comment also.. I''ve also tested this on a board which\nincorporates conference accounting (seperate statistics for seperate\nconfs..) and it works fine.. There shouldn''t be any problems with this,\nit''s simple, small and straightforward.. Completely backdoor free, and\nhopefully bug free too! (There might be some problems when a user has\nuploaded or downloaded about 1 million files... HEHE :) ) Use it if you\nwant... Dont use it if you dont want... But it looks nice, and better\nthan displaying goddamn STATS doors everytime you type U or.. D! Who\nwants to see their name,location,time etc. when they press U?? Nobody!\nJust the facts baby!!\n\nInstallation is simple.. copy the files in this archive to the dirs they\nappear in .. eg. BBS/COMMANDS/sm.info goes into your BBS/COMMANDS/ dir!\nThe file SMASTER.rexx must be located in a directory called PARANOID/\nlocated in your DOORS directory.. If ya dont have one then make one.. \nTo run the program you should either have this as your upload/download\nmessys.. \n-----CUT HERE!---------\n~\n~CC_sm\n----CUT HERE!---------\n\nOr if you wanna have a text file before it, then just put ~ at the very\nbeginning of the text file and ~CC_sm at the end.. simple stuff...\n\nSOME GREETS NOW! - IN ALPHABETICAL ORDER!\n\n			BREN/AFL\n			BUGBYTE/TRZ\n			CAFFEINE/AFL\n			DEL & KICK/IND\n			FURY/TRZ\n			GAZZER/PDY\n			GILTHANAS/2kAD\n			GREEN-BERET/VTY\n			HELLHOUND/VTY\n			HIGHLANDER/GOD\n			HOGSTER/FLT\n			JAY/VTY\n			KILLERETTE/SR\n			KRONION/VTY\n			LEGEND/DLM?\n			MR.VAIN/SCP?\n			NORSKE/PDY\n			O.B.1./VTY\n			RECYCLER/HMN\n			SHOCK/CSL\n			SILIKON/IND\n			SPLATT/FLT\n			SUPERTOUCH/HMN\n			TANGO/GOD\n			TARZAN/CSL\n			THE FREAK/VTY\n			TIN MAN/VTY\n			ULTRAMARINE\n                        VOYAGER+SNOWQUEEN/IND\n			WARDANCER/VTY\n			ZANY/VTY\n			ZOLDAN/SCL\n\nAnd all those guys who I think I have on the list.. But dont.. sorry dudes,\nI''m damn forgetful.. just remind me next time we chat! And all at H&V who\nI dont really know... L8erz! And call H&V boards... Contact me on these,\nfind the numbers and NUP''s yaself!\n \nDARK DOMAIN - FORBIDDEN PLANET - SUSPERIA - ROAD TO NOWHERE - FASTRAX\n  HOUSE OF PAIN - PRIORITY 1 - USS ENTERPRISE - PLASTIC PASSION \nWARES UNLIMITED - AND MANY MANY MORE COOL BOARDS EVERYWHERE! LATER BROS!\n\n[PARANOID/VTY]\n\n           __ _   _         _  _ __ _____ __ _  _          _  _ __\n          /                                                       \\n   .-/\--/---------------------------------------------------------\--/\-.\n   |/  \/ ______      ______      _____     ______ ______     _____ \/  \|\n  _/  ___/_____/_____/_____/_ ___/____/_ __/_____//_____/_ __/____/_     \_\n ¡ |  \_______     _/_____   \\______   \\__    \¯______  \\______  \    ¡ ¡\n : |   /     /     /     /   \\     /    \/    //     /    \    /    \   | |\n : :   \\   /    //          //    //    /     /    _/_____/____     /   | :\n . :    \___     /_____/     /____/     /_____/     /         /     /    : :\n_  . /\_   \____/     /¯____/    /¯____/     /¯____/         /_____/ _/\ : ._\n \  /                                                                   \. /\n  \/----------------------> V · A · N · I · T · Y <----------------------\/\n\n  . _ __ _________  /\________________________  /\__________________ __ _ .\n -÷---[ NAME ]----\/---[ NDZ ]-----[ NUMBER ]-\/--[ BAUD ]---[ SYSOP ]---÷\n  |                                                                      |\n  |  DARK DOMAIN          4   +1 30 5989 0718  WHQ  16.8D   TIN MAN      |\n  ·  SUSPERIA             2   +45   4343 4236  SCHQ 14.4d   ZANY         |\n  |  SOMEWHERE ONLINE     2   +45   5965 3801  DKHQ 16.8d   HELLHOUND    |\n  |  FORBiDDEN-PLANET     2   +353  1820 8489  IRHQ 16.8D   GREEN BERET  |\n  |                                                                      |\n -¦---[ NAME ]----/\---[ NDZ ]-----[ NUMBER ]-/\--[ BAUD ]---[ SYSOP ]---¦-\n  : ¯ ¯¯ ¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯  \/¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯  \/¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯¯ ¯¯ ¯ :\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,11654,9,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048830);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('vty_wa10','VTY-WA10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/VTY-WA10.LHA','WarAccess','XIM','___                                  __',NULL,'Wardancer/Vanity','VTY','_/  |__________   __ __________________|¬\ |   |   _/  _ ¬\_/ ¬\|   _/_\__   __/  |: \_ |:  |   |  __   |    \  :|   ||  :|\__   __/',replace('  ___                                  __\n_/  |__________   __ __________________|¬\\n|   |   _/  _ ¬\_/ ¬\|   _/_\__   __/  |: \_\n|:  |   |  __   |    \  :|   ||  :|\__   __/\n|_______|  :|___|   \____|___||  _|øo|_  |\n ---Y--\____|--\____|----Stz--|_/------\_|\n------------------(Presents)----------------\n WarAccess v1.0  Coded By  Wardancer/Vanity\nAn ''InstantAccess'' door that will allow\nusers that  know the ''secret'' command to get\naccess instantly, ofcoz  with some nice sec.\n  built into  it to avoid hack situations.\n--------------------------------------------\n','\n',char(10)),'WarAccess.Guide',replace('@database WarAccess Documantation\n@Author Wardancer/Vanity\n@Index MAIN\n\nCopyright 1995 Wardancer/Vanity\n\n@node MAIN "WarAccess V1.0 Documentation."\n\n    THe PHuCKiNG /X DuDeS FRoM VANi7Y iS PRouD To BRiNG you aNoTHeR DooR\n                  ___                                  __\n                _/  |__________   __ __________________|¬\\n                |   |   _/  _ ¬\_/ ¬\|   _/_\__   __/  |: \_\n                |:  |   |  __   |    \  :|   ||  :|\__   __/\n                |_______|  :|___|   \____|___||  _|øo|_  |\n                 ---Y--\____|--\____|----Stz--|_/------\_|\n                ------------------(Presents)----------------\n                @{BG FILL}               WarAccess  V1.0              @{BG BACKGROUND}\n                --------------------------------------------\n\n                aND THiS TiMe iT iS MaDe By Wardancer/Vanity\n\n                             Table of contents :\n\n                           @{".....Whats This ?....." link 01}\n                           @{".....Installation....." link 02}\n                           @{"........Greets........" link 03}\n                           @{"...Bug report/ideas..." link 04}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node 01 "Whats This ?..."\n\n  =========================[   Whats This ?   ]===========================\n\n  Now, this one is going to be difficult (at best), to describe. ''Instant\n  Access'' is the first thing that springs to my mind really. Imagine this\n  you write a msg to some dude in a foreign country telling him to give\n  your board a call, ok, great, he says he will do so, but he isn''t sure\n  when, and he would like to have fully access from the first time he logs\n  on, so you give him a ''secret'' command that will upgrade his account\n  unto an account with full access, this exactly what this door does.\n\n  Is it complicated ??? No not at all really, in a subdir of the doors dir\n  you just create some icons where you specify what the particular setting\n  does to the users account. So far the following things can be set: Area,\n  Access, Time, Bytes Uploaded, Uploads, Ration, and finally Ratio Type.\n\n  How, since I know that many sysop''s are a bit paranoid when it comes to\n  hacked, you can also equip each profile with a password, and if the user\n  fails to enter the correct password, it will be recorded into the\n  callerslog, actually, succeeding at the password check will also be\n  noted at the callerlog.\n\n  =========================[   Whats This ?   ]===========================\n\n@endnode\n\n@node 02 "Installation..."\n\n  =========================[   Installation   ]===========================\n\n  Installing this program is really quite simple, the only things you have\n  to is to make sure the following is right :\n\n  Program      Location                      Description\n  -------      --------                      -----------\n  WarAccess    Doors:!!!War!!!/WarAccess/    The main program...\n\n  The settings should be placed in a seperate dir with the following name:\n\n                    ''Doors:!!!War!!!/WarAccess/Settings/''\n\n  Lets take a look at the different tooltypes:\n\n  PASSWORD=xxx\n\n  Enables password protection on the setting, where ''xxx'' is the password\n  (max. 16 chars)\n\n  ACCESS=xxx\n\n  Defines what access the user should get, where ''xxx'' is the access\n  level.\n\n  AREA=xxx\n\n  Defines what ''AREA'' the user belongs to (eg. what conferences the user\n  will have access to), where ''xxx'' is the ''AREA'' name.\n\n  TIMELIMIT=xxx\n\n  Defines how much time the user has, where ''xxx'' is the time in seconds.\n\n  UPLOADS=xxx\n\n  Defines how many uploads the user is to get, where ''xxx'' is, you guessed\n  it.\n\n  BYTESUL=xxx\n\n  Defines how many bytes the user is to get.\n\n  RATIO=xxx\n\n  Defines the users ration, where ''xxx'' is going to be the ration\n  (eg. 1:xxx).\n\n  RATIOTYPE=xxx\n\n  Defines the users type of ration, where ''xxx'' may either be ''BYTES'' for\n  a byte only ratio, ''BYTES/FILES'' for a byte/file ration or ''FILES'' for a\n  file only ratio.\n\n  If you are still in doubt then try and take a quick look at the included\n  settings files.\n\n  Since the ''secret'' command word is variable that also mean that the\n  .info file for the door in bbscmd/ can not be set to a default name,\n  so if your secret command is ''ulveunge'' then you would have to have an\n  icon named ''smoelf.info'' in bbscmd/ and a setting also named\n  ''ulveunge.info'' in the settings dir.\n\n  =========================[   Installation   ]===========================\n\n@endnode\n\n@node 03 "Greets..."\n\n  =========================[      Greets      ]===========================\n\n  @{BG FILL}                 GReeTZ Go ouT To THe FoLLoWiNG DuDeS:                  @{BG BACKGROUND}\n\n  Dux, Kronion, Zeke, Mickey, Tactica, Mandrake, Nookman, Sorcerer,\n  The Freak, Melomaniac, Marty, Morph, Deature, Json, D-Tron, Webster,\n  Gilthanas, Striker, Hellhound, Devilstar, Zinko, Lector, Playmate,\n  Paranoid, Enzo, Menace, Ironman, Nashua, Ramirez, Omar, Nero, Janitor,\n  Conan, Newton, Relief, The Priest, Dizy, Darkwing, Gandalf\n\n  =========================[      Greets      ]===========================\n\n@endnode\n\n@node 04 "Bug Report/Ideas..."\n\n  =========================[ Bug Report/Ideas ]===========================\n\n  Send your bug reports or ideas to the following boards :\n\n  Susperia ............... +45  4343-4236   (VANi7Y SCHQ)\n  Warez Unlimited ........ +45  4494-6208   (VANi7Y DKHQ)\n\n  If you would like to betatest for me, then just contact me at Susperia.\n\n  =========================[ Bug Report/Ideas ]===========================\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),'{"ACCESS":"xxx","TYPE":"xxx"}',NULL,16492,2,0,NULL,NULL,'vty_wa10_waraccess','scan',1780048830);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('vty_wk10','VTY-WK10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/VTY-WK10.LHA','WarKick''Em','XIM','WarKick''Em',NULL,'Wardancer/Vanity','VTY','_/  |__________   __ __________________|¬\ |   |   _/  _ ¬\_/ ¬\|   _/_\__   __/  |: \_ |:  |   |  __   |    \  :|   ||  :|\__   __/',replace('  ___                                  __\n_/  |__________   __ __________________|¬\\n|   |   _/  _ ¬\_/ ¬\|   _/_\__   __/  |: \_\n|:  |   |  __   |    \  :|   ||  :|\__   __/\n|_______|  :|___|   \____|___||  _|øo|_  |\n ---Y--\____|--\____|----Stz--|_/------\_|\n------------------(Presents)----------------\n     WarKick''Em V1.0 By Wardancer/Vanity\n\nA Nifty Tool For Kicking Lame Users Of Their\n  Nodes, So Your ELI7E Traders Can Get To\n   Work, With Some Nifty Security Ofcoz.\n--------------------------------------------\n','\n',char(10)),'WarKick''Em.Guide',replace('@database WarKick''Em Documantation\n@Author Wardancer/Vanity\n@Index MAIN\n\nCopyright 1995 Wardancer/Vanity\n\n@node MAIN "WarKick''Em V1.0 Documentation."\n\n    THe PHuCKiNG /X DuDeS FRoM VANi7Y iS PRouD To BRiNG you aNoTHeR DooR\n                  ___                                  __\n                _/  |__________   __ __________________|¬\\n                |   |   _/  _ ¬\_/ ¬\|   _/_\__   __/  |: \_\n                |:  |   |  __   |    \  :|   ||  :|\__   __/\n                |_______|  :|___|   \____|___||  _|øo|_  |\n                 ---Y--\____|--\____|----Stz--|_/------\_|\n                ------------------(Presents)----------------\n                @{BG FILL}               WarKick''Em  V2.0             @{BG BACKGROUND}\n                --------------------------------------------\n\n                aND THiS TiMe iT iS MaDe By Wardancer/Vanity\n\n                             Table of contents :\n\n                           @{".....Whats This ?....." link 01}\n                           @{".....Installation....." link 02}\n                           @{"........Greets........" link 03}\n                           @{"...Bug report/ideas..." link 04}\n\n             Truth, Tell Me The Truth, The Truth, Motherfucker,\n          Tell Me The Truth, Tell Me The Truth, Tell Me The Truth,\n                           The Truth, You Sucker.\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node 01 "Whats This ?..."\n\n  =========================[   Whats This ?   ]===========================\n\n  WarKick''Em is a tool that will allow selected users to kick users from\n  other nodes, that is naturally a VERY powerful weapon to put into a\n  users hand, an so some kind of security is needed, suffice to say that\n  the door asks the user of a reason why is about to kick another user,\n  and logs the data the user writes in the callerslog together with a\n  datestamp, handle of user about to be kicked and the node # of the user\n  about to be kicked. Also, if the user being kicked is idle then the door\n  will post a warning to him saying that he will be kicked of in 30 secs.,\n  which will aloow the user to log out normally.\n\n  *** Danger *** If the users being kicked is using a door that has a\n  poorly written emergency exit code, then it is possible that his node\n  will be locked up until the next reboot of the board.\n\n  So why should you install this door, well, just imagine this, some lame\n  14.4K user is bugging down your nice and shiny V.34 line, and one of\n  super ELI7E trader have just gotten hands on an 1 hour release, wouldn''t\n  it be nice if the super ELI7E trader could kick the lamer so we would\n  be able to get hold of the V.34 line ???\n\n  =========================[   Whats This ?   ]===========================\n\n@endnode\n\n@node 02 "Installation..."\n\n  =========================[   Installation   ]===========================\n\n  Installing this program is really quite simple, the only things you have\n  to is to make sure the following is right :\n\n  Program      Location                      Description\n  -------      --------                      -----------\n  WarKick''Em   Doors:!!!War!!!/WarKick''Em/   Main Program.\n  SecList      Doors:!!!War!!!/WarKick''Em/   List Of Users Allowed To Use\n                                             The Door Seperated By Cr''s.\n\n  Also make sure that kick.info is in the ''Commands/BBSCmd/'' drawer.\n\n  =========================[   Installation   ]===========================\n\n@endnode\n\n@node 03 "Greets..."\n\n  =========================[      Greets      ]===========================\n\n  @{BG FILL}                 GReeTZ Go ouT To THe FoLLoWiNG DuDeS:                  @{BG BACKGROUND}\n\n  Dux, Kronion, Zeke, Mickey, Tactica, Mandrake, Nookman, Sorcerer,\n  The Freak, Melomaniac, Marty, Morph, Deature, Json, D-Tron, Webster,\n  Gilthanas, Striker, Hellhound, Devilstar, Zinko, Lector, Playmate,\n  Paranoid, Enzo, Menace, Ironman, Nashua, Ramirez, Omar, Nero, Janitor,\n  Conan, Newton, Relief, The Priest, Dizy, Darkwing\n\n  =========================[      Greets      ]===========================\n\n@endnode\n\n@node 04 "Bug Report/Ideas..."\n\n  =========================[ Bug Report/Ideas ]===========================\n\n  Send your bug reports or ideas to the following boards :\n\n  Susperia ............... +45  4343-4236   (VANi7Y SCHQ)\n  Warez Unlimited ........ +45  4494-6208   (VANi7Y DKHQ)\n\n  If you would like to betatest for me, then just contact me at Susperia.\n\n  =========================[ Bug Report/Ideas ]===========================\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',14148,6,0,NULL,NULL,'vty_wk10','scan',1780048830);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('vty_wl20','VTY-WL20.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/VTY-WL20.LHA','WarLogoff','XIM','WarLogoff',NULL,'Wardancer/Vanity','VTY','_/  |__________   __ __________________|¬\ |   |   _/  _ ¬\_/ ¬\|   _/_\__   __/  |: \_ |:  |   |  __   |    \  :|   ||  :|\__   __/',replace('  ___                                  __\n_/  |__________   __ __________________|¬\\n|   |   _/  _ ¬\_/ ¬\|   _/_\__   __/  |: \_\n|:  |   |  __   |    \  :|   ||  :|\__   __/\n|_______|  :|___|   \____|___||  _|øo|_  |\n ---Y--\____|--\____|----Stz--|_/------\_|\n------------------(Presents)----------------\n  WarLogoff V2.0 Coded By Wardancer/Vanity\n  Code Is Once Again Completly Redone From\nScratch, This Time With Color Support Added,\n  And A Lot Of Other Nice''N''Cute Features.\n--------------------------------------------\n','\n',char(10)),'WarLogoff.Guide',replace('@database WarLogoff Documantation\n@Author Wardancer/Vanity\n@Index MAIN\n\nCopyright 1995 Wardancer/Vanity\n\n@node MAIN "WarLogoff V2.0 Documentation."\n\n    THe PHuCKiNG /X DuDeS FRoM VANi7Y iS PRouD To BRiNG you aNoTHeR DooR\n                  ___                                  __\n                _/  |__________   __ __________________|¬\\n                |   |   _/  _ ¬\_/ ¬\|   _/_\__   __/  |: \_\n                |:  |   |  __   |    \  :|   ||  :|\__   __/\n                |_______|  :|___|   \____|___||  _|øo|_  |\n                 ---Y--\____|--\____|----Stz--|_/------\_|\n                ------------------(Presents)----------------\n                @{BG FILL}               WarLogoff  V2.0              @{BG BACKGROUND}\n                --------------------------------------------\n\n                aND THiS TiMe iT iS MaDe By Wardancer/Vanity\n\n                             Table of contents :\n\n                           @{".....Whats This ?....." link 01}\n                           @{".....Installation....." link 02}\n                           @{"........Greets........" link 03}\n                           @{"...Bug report/ideas..." link 04}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node 01 "Whats This ?..."\n\n  =========================[   Whats This ?   ]===========================\n\n  WarLogoff is a door that will show a message to the user just before he\n  logs off your system, and it will also allow him/her to enter a new\n  message for the following users to see, quite useful for witty remarks,\n  or comments.\n\n  Well, this is the third time this door has been released and it is also\n  the second time it has been completly rewritten from scratch. This new\n  and improved version also features some nice color support.\n\n  =========================[   Whats This ?   ]===========================\n\n@endnode\n\n@node 02 "Installation..."\n\n  =========================[   Installation   ]===========================\n\n  Installing this program is really quite simple, the only things you have\n  to is to make sure the following is right :\n\n  Program      Location                      Description\n  -------      --------                      -----------\n  WarLogoff    Doors:!!!WAR!!!/WarLogoff/    The main program...\n\n  ---[ The Following Files Are Not Nesc.]---\n\n  Banner.txt   Doors:!!!War!!!/WarLogoff/    Banner to be displayed...\n  Ignore       Doors:!!!War!!!/WarLogoff/    List of users that doesn''t\n                                             want to be bothered with\n                                             WarLogoff...\n  Twits        Doors:!!!War!!!/WarLogoff/    List of users that are not\n                                             allowed to enter anything\n                                             into the door...\n  Anon         Doors:!!!War!!!/WarLogoff/    List of users that are\n                                             allowed to remain anonymous...\n\n  Ok, as you can see, there are a couple of lists that do different\n  things, please note that the lists uses SLOTNUMBERS and not usernames.\n\n  If a user whshes to be listed in the ''ignore'' list, all he has to do is\n  enter ''g ignore'' which will either add his name to the list, or if his\n  name is already there, will remove it from the list.\n\n  The two other lists are not intended for the users to tamper with (guess\n  why), so those you have to maintain yourself.\n\n  Also make sure that g.info is in the commands/bbscmd drawer.\n\n  =========================[   Installation   ]===========================\n\n@endnode\n\n@node 03 "Greets..."\n\n  =========================[      Greets      ]===========================\n\n  @{BG FILL}                 GReeTZ Go ouT To THe FoLLoWiNG DuDeS:                  @{BG BACKGROUND}\n\n  Dux, Kronion, Zeke, Mickey, Tactica, Mandrake, Nookman, Sorcerer,\n  The Freak, Melomaniac, Marty, Morph, Deature, Json, D-Tron, Webster,\n  Gilthanas, Striker, Hellhound, Devilstar, Zinko, Lector, Playmate,\n  Paranoid, Enzo, Menace, Ironman, Nashua, Ramirez, Omar, Nero, Janitor,\n  Conan, Newton, Relief, The Priest, Dizy, Darkwing\n\n  =========================[      Greets      ]===========================\n\n@endnode\n\n@node 04 "Bug Report/Ideas..."\n\n  =========================[ Bug Report/Ideas ]===========================\n\n  Send your bug reports or ideas to the following boards :\n\n  Susperia ............... +45  4343-4236   (VANi7Y SCHQ)\n  Warez Unlimited ........ +45  4494-6208   (VANi7Y DKHQ)\n\n  If you would like to betatest for me, then just contact me at Susperia.\n\n  =========================[ Bug Report/Ideas ]===========================\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',14097,1,0,NULL,NULL,'h_v_wlog_3','scan',1780048830);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('war_cm10','WAR-CM10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/WAR-CM10.LHA','WarComment','XIM','WarComment',NULL,NULL,'WAR','A              O f              U N            VTY^HMS            M I           Presents:           A',replace('     V           Wardancer           H\n     A              O f              U\n     N            VTY^HMS            M\n     I           Presents:           A\n     T        WarComment V1.0        N\n     Y  (THE GROUPS HAVEN''T MERGED)  S\n Another XiM Door For The /X System, With A\n Real Nice  Dezign, Just Ready To Be Popped\n Into Your Doors Drawer.','\n',char(10)),'WarComment.Guide',replace('@database WarCommentDoc\n@Author Wardancer/VANiTY^HUMANS\n@Index MAIN\n\nCopyright 1994 Wardancer/VANiTY^HUMANS\n\n@node MAIN "WarComment V1.0 Documentation."\n\n                  ___                                  __\n                _/  |__________   __ __________________|¬\\n                |   |   _/  _ ¬\_/ ¬\|   _/_\__   __/  |: \_\n                |:  |   |  __   |    \  :|   ||  :|\__   __/\n                |_______|  :|___|   \____|___||  _|øo|_  |\n                 ---Y--\____|--\____|----Stz--|_/------\_|\n                ------------------(Presents)----------------\n                                WarLogoff V1.3\n                --------------------------------------------\n                     .___:_._____  _______ ___ :   _____\n                 __ _|   | :    /\/ \_ __ \   \|   \  _/___\n                 \//_|   | |   /.  / \ \_  \   \  ._\___   \\n                  / \_   | |  /  \/   \ |   \ \   |   l/  ø/\n                 /ø  |___|___/___|l____\|    \|\__l_______//\n                /____|---( presents )---l_____\--------mAZ-»\n\n                     NOTE: THE GROUPS ARE !NOT! UNITED\n\n\n                     Made by : Wardancer/VANiTY^HUMANS\n\n\n\n                             Table of contents :\n\n                           @{"     Whats this ?     " Link 01}\n                           @{"     Installation     " Link 02}\n                           @{"        Greets        " Link 03}\n                           @{"   Bug report/ideas   " Link 04}\n                           @{"       History        " Link 05}\n                           @("         NOTE         " Link 06}\n\n@endnode\n\n@node 01 "Whats this ?"\n\n  ========================================================================\n\n  WarCommet Is Another One Of Those Pesky Comment To The Staff Doors, Only\n  This One Should be Better Than Those Already Out, It Has A REAL Nice\n  Hotkey Support, And An Easy To Use Config Icon File To Make Your Life A\n  Bit Easier, It Is All 100% Failsafe...\n\n  ========================================================================\n\n@endnode\n\n@node 02 "Installation"\n\n  ========================================================================\n\n  Installing  this program is really  quite simple, the  only things you\n  have to is to make sure the following is right :\n\n  Program      Location                      Description\n  -------      --------                      -----------\n  WarComment   Doors:!!!WAR!!!/WarComment    The main program\n  Congif.Info  Doors:!!!WAR!!!/WarComment    The Config File\n  Banner.txt   Doors:!!!WAR!!!/WarComment    An Optional banner To Be\n                                             Displayed\n\n  Also make sure that c.info is in the commands/bbscmd drawer.\n\n  ========================================================================\n\n@endnode\n\n@node 03 "Greets"\n\n  ========================================================================\n\n  I would like to greet the following in no order :\n\n  Kronion, Dux, The Freak, Ramirez, Omar, Striker, Playmate, Calvin,\n  Plexer, Gilthanas, Energy, Shamer, Tactica, Zany, Zeke, Spike,\n  Delirium&Kickface, Mike&Tofke, Norske, Chock, Paranoid, OB1, Curmit,\n  Tin Man, Mandrake, Mr. Orion, Mr. Beer, Marty, Nookman, Poison, Json,\n  Conan&Newton, Tarzan, Jake, HAL 9000, D-Day, Cracy Creep, Mr. Vain,\n  Overlord, Stezotehic, Tango, Json, Deature, Spacebrain, Enzo,\n  G0blin, Aquarius, Cockroach, Bugbyte, Hoffi, Triple B, Curt Cool,\n  G.O.D, Lector, Nashua, Paxdei, Tas, Caesar, Nero, Undertaker, Zinko,\n  Laxity, Devilstar, Carebear, Wolfman, Ozone&Rob, Janitor, NSL,\n  Mr. Hyde, Relief, Kreon, Fozzi, Green-Beret, Jay, O.B.1., IZI,\n  Zanthor, The Priest\n\n      And all other Vanity members and people I forgot.\n\n  Specials go to :\n\n  Kronion .......................... For being a great leader\n  Dux .............................. For helping me with AmiExpress\n  Ramirez .......................... For letting me test at your board\n  Omar ............................. For all sorts of crazy conversation\n  Json ............................. Also for letting me test at your BBS\n  Aquarius ......................... For helping me with /X at TG94\n  Nero ............................. Cool board\n\n  ========================================================================\n\n@endnode\n\n@node 04 "Bug report/ideas"\n\n  ========================================================================\n\n  Send your bug reports or ideas to the following boards :\n\n  X-Factor ............... +1 XXX-XXXX-XXX   (VANiTY WHQ)\n  Susperia ............... +45  434-342-36   (VANiTY SCHQ)\n  Somewhere Online ....... +45  597-538-01   (VANiTY DKHQ)\n  Forbidden Planet ....... +353 182-084-89   (VANiTY IRHQ & HUMANS IRHQ)\n  Suffocation ............ +45  491-807-60   (The board where I test my doors)\n  Mainline ............... +45  981-530-62   (Also supports netmail)\n  Static Chaos ........... +45  864-395-14   (Another testsite)\n\n  You can also leave a msg to:   /X-Net ''WarDancer@DK0001''\n                                FidoNet 2:236/19.66\n                               InterNet [email removed]\n\n  ======================================================================== \n\n@endnode\n\n@node 05 "History"\n\n  ========================================================================\n\n  V1.0 - First Release Ever Of This Door\n\n  ========================================================================\n\n@endnode\n\n@node 06 "NOTE"\n\n  =======================================================================\n\n  Just to Lets  You All Know, I Have Also Joined  Forces With Humans, But\n  I''m Still Also A Vanity  Member. The Two Groups Havent Joined Together.\n\n  =======================================================================\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',10228,3,0,NULL,NULL,'war_cm10','scan',1780048830);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('warjab','WARJAB.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/WARJAB.LHA','JABChat','XIM','JABChat',NULL,NULL,NULL,'/. | \/    \____  \___   \| \_ \/   \ //  |  \  |  \  _ _/ _____/|  /  \  _ \ /   /¯\  \ _   \ |  \  |/   _  \   \ |  |',replace('[33m   /¬|_  _____________________(__) ___\n  /. | \/    \____  \___   \| \_ \/   \\n //  |  \  |  \  _ _/ _____/|  /  \  _ \\n/   /¯\  \ _   \ |  \  |/   _  \   \ |  |\n\________/_|___/_|   \ |\___|   \__/_|  | \n =[ \X/arph¡ns ]=l____):====l____)===l__|\n==[  PRESENTS  ]=========================[0m\nSplit screen chat for the /X..Really works\nDownload it and try it on your Amiexpress\nbbs...  THIS FILE IS VIRUS FREE..........\n','\n',char(10)),'reference-board.txt',replace(replace('              W h e r e   t h e   w a r e z   c o m e   f r o m\r\n                                               __                /\_____:\r\n__/\__________________________________________|  \______________/  \    |__\r\n\_   ___________  _______ ________  \__   ___ |   _______  _______  \_  l  \\r\n__\____  \    _l   \    |  \     |___/     |  !    \   _l   \   _| __/\____ \_\r\n\_____    \___\     \___|   \___ !   \__   |_____   \__\     \__\    \____   /\r\n -mNT\_____/---\_____/--l____/-\______/\   |----\____/--\_____/--\____/--\__/\r\n                                        \__|\r\n\r\n- -- --> F A i R L i G H T   S W E D i S H   H E A D Q U A R T E R S <-- -- -\r\n\r\n           reference-board is back 2017 after more than 20 years in coma!\r\n\r\n                        Running on AmiExpress TelNet\r\n\r\n                    Connect to: reference-board.zapto.org:1541\r\n\r\n                    or: www.brysk.se/reference-board/index.htm\r\n               \n              UPLOAD DATE: 01-04-18  TIME: 20:38:50  ON NODE: 0\n','\r',char(13)),'\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',29375,1,0,NULL,NULL,'warjab','scan',1780048830);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('warpsear','WARPSEAR.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/WARPSEAR.LHA','WarpSearch','XIM','WarpSearch',NULL,'Dres',NULL,'|  _________________           __          | |  \________________|)____.---''--`---.____ | |               ||    \----.________.----/ |',replace('.------------------------------------------.\n|  _________________           __          |\n|  \________________|)____.---''--`---.____ |\n|               ||    \----.________.----/ |\n| /X WarpSearch ||     / /    `--''         |\n|    V1.0     __||____/ /_    by Dres      |\n|            |___         \   & Crayor     |\n|                `--------''                |\n|This is the /X version of our boyer-moore |\n|  double buffered async I/O search code.  |\n|  It`s a "z" door that unifies all known  |\n|   speedup concepts of the AMiGA system.  |\n|On 040/060 the bottleneck is our baracuda |\n| fast-scsi2 drive 7MB/s. Go on Warp now!  |\n|The search routine is 100% pure assembler.|\n`------------------------------------------''\n{ISDN} dAiLY FrEsH FrUiTbOaRd STuFF {28k8}\n','\n',char(10)),'lOSeNDOS.guide',replace('                   \n                     __  _ __  /\__ _  _ __/\  __ _  __\n                    _\/___   \/              \/   ___\/_\n              ......\/\  /........................\  /\/......\n             :         \/                          \/         :\n             :      .___             .___         .___        :\n             :   _ _|   \      ______|   \  ______|   \       :\n             :   \\\__   7___  \______   /  \__   ____/       :\n             :      /.   |   \__/.  l/   \___/_____   \__ _   :\n             :     /::.  |    _/::.       _/::.  l/    _///   :\n             :     \___________\___________\____________\     :\n             :___        .___        .___        .___         :___\n     _ ______|   \ ______|   \ ______|   \ ______|   \  ______|   \\n     \\\__   ____/ \______   / \______   / \______   /  \__   ____/\n        /.   ___|___/.   |   \__/.  _|   \__/.  l/   \___/_____   \__ _\n       /::.  l/   _/::.  |    _/::. \___  _/::.       _/::.  l/    _///\n       \_ _________\_____|_____\___________\___________\___________ \\n         Y   :                                                :[nM$]Y\n      .------''                                                `------.\n      :eXON/rIOT^jORMAS · gHANDY/gODS · rAHIEM/eSSENCE · cELIC/rEKTUM: \n      `------.                                                .------''\n             `------------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',17422,5,0,NULL,NULL,'wrpser10','scan',1780048830);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('warpsrch','WARPSRCH.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/WARPSRCH.LHA','WarpSearch','XIM','WarpSearch',NULL,'Dres',NULL,'|  _________________           __          | |  \________________|)____.---''--`---.____ | |               ||    \----.________.----/ |',replace('.------------------------------------------.\n|  _________________           __          |\n|  \________________|)____.---''--`---.____ |\n|               ||    \----.________.----/ |\n| /X WarpSearch ||     / /    `--''         |\n|    V1.0     __||____/ /_    by Dres      |\n|            |___         \   & Crayor     |\n|                `--------''                |\n|This is the /X version of our boyer-moore |\n|  double buffered async I/O search code.  |\n|  It`s a "z" door that unifies all known  |\n|   speedup concepts of the AMiGA system.  |\n|On 040/060 the bottleneck is our baracuda |\n| fast-scsi2 drive 7MB/s. Go on Warp now!  |\n|The search routine is 100% pure assembler.|\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'WarpSearch.doc',replace('WarpSearch V1.0\n\nIntroduction\n------------\nThis is the AmiExpress version of WarpSearch.\nIt uses the boyer-moore search algorithm implemented in assembler code.\nThis algorithm is the fastest available.\n\nFeatures\n--------\nV1.0:\n-pattern matching\n-double buffered asynchonous I/O\n-backwards/forwards counting of filelists\n-highlightning\n\nInstallation\n------------\nCopy "z.info" to "bbs:commands/bbscmd/".\nChange LOCATION to your full path of the WarpSearch executable.\n\nUsage\n-----\nz <pattern> <filelist#> <+/->\n\nExample usage: "z foo" (searches from ul dir down for "foo").\nWildcards in pattern are allowed, like "z foo*bar" or "z bm_zearch*V1.0*"\nUse "z foo*bar 2 +" to search from dir2 upwards. Default is downwards search.\nThe pattern must match an expression in one line.\nPatterns are not case sensitive. Only "*" is accepted as a wildcard and no other\nconstructions like "#?","?" , which noone needs anyway in this application.\n\nInfo\n----\nThe complete filedescription including filename etc. is searched through.\nWe, the authors, think that this magic code is the fastest search routine ever\nmade for an /X like filelist, because the 100% assembler boyer-moore search\nroutine with pattern matching and highlightning is optimized for cpu cycles by\nhand, some magic is done for splitted filedescriptions, asychronous I/O.\nWe concidered speedup concepts for every line of code.\nOn our system the bottleneck is the Fast-SCSI-II Baracuda drive with a\nFast-SCSI-II CyberSCSI Controller that does 7MB/s, and the code is 3 times\nfaster if the filelist is in RAM with 50MB/s burst.\n\nThe maximum length of a description line allowed is 1000 chars. Since /X\nallows 80 chars/line as maximum we think this is no bug. If a line is longer\nthan 1000 chars enforcer hits may occur. A check for line length would slow\ndown the code significantly. That`s why we don`t do it.\n\nFor those who are interested, a short explanation of what "double buffered\nasync I/O" means:\nDue to the coolness of the Amiga, SCSI is the most accepted standard on this\nplatform (..well if we dont consider 4000 desktops..). SCSI has the ability\nto transfer data per DMA, thus meaning without using the processor. This is were\nasync I/O comes in. A program using double buffered async I/O lets the File-\nSystem first fill up one buffer, then sends the request to fill up the second\nbuffer, and while the HD is busy transfering data to the 2nd buffer the processor\nis free to do its work on the first one. As you can imagine this technique\ndramatically speeds up the whole process.\n\nIf you are keen on a shell version, just ask.\n\nSend your suggestions or bug reports to [email removed].\n\nGreetz\n------\nSome hellos to the following guys:\n\n"Ibo"  - with his always busy or down BBS, so that we weren`t able to abuse\n         his BBS for beta testing ;)\nHijack - thx for the cool name of this door m8. (yep! "WarpSearch" actually was\n         his idea)\nSCSI   - for his help on using iwan.device\nAmok   - for the address of Mr.F\nSTC    - for the competition of coding the fastest search code for /X filelists\nHydra  - for his try to code a better /X (hbbs)\nDave Haynie\n       - for answering my email on the Surfer Package\n\nRevision History\n----------------\nV1.0 - first public release\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',16321,6,0,NULL,NULL,'warpsrch','scan',1780048830);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('warps_10','WARPS_10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/WARPS_10.LHA','WarpSearch','XIM','LE-win5-96.exe',NULL,'Dres','WARPS','|  _________________           __          | |  \________________|)____.---''--`---.____ | |               ||    \----.________.----/ |',replace('.------------------------------------------.\n|  _________________           __          |\n|  \________________|)____.---''--`---.____ |\n|               ||    \----.________.----/ |\n| /X WarpSearch ||     / /    `--''         |\n|    V1.0     __||____/ /_    by Dres      |\n|            |___         \   & Crayor     |\n|                `--------''                |\n|This is the /X version of our boyer-moore |\n|  double buffered async I/O search code.  |\n|  It`s a "z" door that unifies all known  |\n|   speedup concepts of the AMiGA system.  |\n|On 040/060 the bottleneck is our baracuda |\n| fast-scsi2 drive 7MB/s. Go on Warp now!  |\n|The search routine is 100% pure assembler.|\n`------------------------------------------''\n\n','\n',char(10)),'lOSeNDOS.guide',replace('                   \n                     __  _ __  /\__ _  _ __/\  __ _  __\n                    _\/___   \/              \/   ___\/_\n              ......\/\  /........................\  /\/......\n             :         \/                          \/         :\n             :      .___             .___         .___        :\n             :   _ _|   \      ______|   \  ______|   \       :\n             :   \\\__   7___  \______   /  \__   ____/       :\n             :      /.   |   \__/.  l/   \___/_____   \__ _   :\n             :     /::.  |    _/::.       _/::.  l/    _///   :\n             :     \___________\___________\____________\     :\n             :___        .___        .___        .___         :___\n     _ ______|   \ ______|   \ ______|   \ ______|   \  ______|   \\n     \\\__   ____/ \______   / \______   / \______   /  \__   ____/\n        /.   ___|___/.   |   \__/.  _|   \__/.  l/   \___/_____   \__ _\n       /::.  l/   _/::.  |    _/::. \___  _/::.       _/::.  l/    _///\n       \_ _________\_____|_____\___________\___________\___________ \\n         Y   :                                                :[nM$]Y\n      .------''                                                `------.\n      :eXON/rIOT^jORMAS · gHANDY/gODS · rAHIEM/eSSENCE · cELIC/rEKTUM: \n      `------.                                                .------''\n             `------------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',19088,5,0,NULL,NULL,'warps_10','scan',1780048830);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('warps_20','WARPS_20.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/WARPS_20.LHA','WarpSearch','XIM','WarpSearch',NULL,'Dres','WARPS','|  _________________           __          | |  \________________|)____.---''--`---.____ | |               ||    \----.________.----/ |',replace('.------------------------------------------.\n|  _________________           __          |\n|  \________________|)____.---''--`---.____ |\n|               ||    \----.________.----/ |\n| /X WarpSearch ||     / /    `--''         |\n|    V2.0     __||____/ /_    by Dres      |\n|            |___         \   & Crayor     |\n|                `--------''                |\n|  Second release of our famous program.   |\n|  AmiExpress and shell version included.  |\n|  New features: -real reverse search      |\n|  -residentable, DMA optimized            |\n|  -color output, completely configurable  |\n|  -prompts always behind complete descs   |\n|  -flagging, s-express compatibility      |\n`------------------------------------------''\n','\n',char(10)),'mastrb8.txt',replace(replace('STILL GOING STRONG in 2014!\r\n\r\n                ___         ._            _______             ·\r\n   /\  _________)  \________| \___________)__   /_________:__ :________\r\n  /  \/\  __  \    ____ ___/|  \______  \_  / _/___  \_ ____/ ¦__ \___ \\r\n /   /  \ \__  \___  \  |   |   \  _/  __/ /    /\__  \  |¦   | /  \_|  \\r\n/  \/    \_ \   \ !   \_|   !    \_\    \_     /   \   \ ||   |·    /|   \_\r\n\___|     ___\  /__    /l________ /_\    /__  /_____\  / |¦   |    /_|    /\r\n    l____/-A×E\/  \___/_!       \/   \  /   \/       \/__|:   ¦__ /  l___/\r\n       ______            _____        \/      :    ____   ·   : \/\r\n    ___)     \___________)    \__________:___ ¦____)   \__________\r\n    \    _______     _______    \___    ____/ |\_____   \______   \\r\n   /\___   \/        |    _)    \/       ¦    |/    |    \    |    \\r\n _/    !    \        |    \      \_      |    |     !     \   |     \\r\n \______     \___    |_____\      /___   |    ¦            \  |      \_\r\n       \______/ \____!      \    /   \___|    :________     \_|       /\r\n                             \  /        ¦    ·       \______/|      /\r\n   YOUVE HEARD ABOUT IT!      \/         :    ·               l_____/\r\n       \r\n         MASTURBATiON STATiON AMIGA/PC/CONSOLE/ASCII-ANSI/C64        \r\n               Telnet: bbs.masturbationstationbbs.com\r\n\r\n           UPLOAD DATE: 04-01-15  TIME: 15:23:38  ON NODE: 1\r\n\r\n  UPLOADER: Black Beard            LOCATION: mASTURBATIONSTATIONBBS.COM\r\n\r\n','\r',char(13)),'\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',34469,6,0,NULL,NULL,'warps_20','scan',1780048830);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('warps_21','WARPS_21.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/WARPS_21.LHA','WarpSearch','XIM','WarpSearch',NULL,'Dres','WARPS','|  _________________           __          | |  \________________|)____.---''--`---.____ | |               ||    \----.________.----/ |',replace('.------------------------------------------.\n|  _________________           __          |\n|  \________________|)____.---''--`---.____ |\n|               ||    \----.________.----/ |\n| /X WarpSearch ||     / /    `--''         |\n|    V2.1     __||____/ /_    by Dres      |\n|            |___         \   & Crayor     |\n|                `--------''                |\n|  Fastest zippy door for an /X filelist.  |\n|  AmiExpress and shell version included.  |\n|                                          |\n|  Harmless bug was fixed, read doc for    |\n|  precise information.                    |\n`------------------------------------------''\n[07-20-96]Call SeCrEt CiNemA BBS !!![12:50]\n','\n',char(10)),'WarpSearch.doc',replace('WarpSearch V2.1\n\n\nIntroduction\n------------\nThis is the AmiExpress version of WarpSearch.\nIt uses the boyer-moore search algorithm implemented in assembler code.\nThis algorithm is the fastest available.\n\n\nFeatures\n--------\nV1.0:\n-pattern matching\n-asynchonous I/O\n-backwards/forwards counting of filelists\n-highlightning\n\nV2.0:\n-now real reverse search (search code / buffer loading / dir counting)\n-residentable\n-DMA optimized\n-prompts always behind complete descriptions\n-simple flagging, also "f file1.lha f file2.lha"\n-ndirs file is used to be s-express compatible if no ndirs tooltype exists\n-colors for the description output\n-configurable via tooltypes (of the WarpSearch executable) or WarpSearch.config file\n tooltypes override file config\n\nV2.1:\n-bugfixed V2.0\n If there were escape codes in the text of a file description the line was\n repeated in an infinite loop but you were able to quit the program at the\n prompt. No memory trashes or similar occured. This is fixed now. A harmless\n byte read from adress 0 in the shell version was wiped out too.\n \n\nInstallation\n------------\nCopy "z.info" to "bbs:commands/bbscmd/".\nChange LOCATION to your full path of the WarpSearch executable.\nAdjust configuration if you like.\n\n\nUsage\n-----\ncompatible to /X z door\n\nz <pattern> <filelist#> <+/-/r>\n\nExample usage:\n"z foo"      (searches in upload dir for "foo" forwards).\n"z foo r"    (searches in upload dir reverse).\n\n"z foo 3 r"  (searches in dir3 reverse).\n"z foo a +"  (searches from dir1 up for "foo").\n\n"z foo a -"  (searches from upload dir down for "foo").\n"z foo 2 +"  (searches from dir2 up for "foo").\n"z foo 1"    (searches dir1 only for "foo").\n\nWildcards in pattern are allowed, like "z foo*bar" or "z warp*V1.0*"\nUse "z foo*bar 2 +" to search from dir2 upwards. Default is downwards search.\nThe pattern must match an expression in one line.\nPatterns are not case sensitive. Only "*" is accepted as a wildcard and no\nother constructions like "#?","?" , which noone needs anyway in this application.\n\n\nInfo\n----\nDue to the boyer-moore algorithm the longer the pattern (w/o wildcards)\nthe shorter the search time.\n\nThe complete filedescription including filename etc. is searched through.\nWe, the authors, think that this magic code is the fastest search routine ever\nmade for an /X like filelist, because the 100% assembler boyer-moore search\nroutine with pattern matching and highlightning is optimized for cpu cycles by\nhand, some magic is done for splitted filedescriptions, asychronous I/O\noptimized even for 68040. (cache flushing problem)\n\nOn our system the bottleneck is the Fast-SCSI-II Baracuda drive with a\nFast-SCSI-II CyberSCSI Controller that does 7MB/s, and the code is 3 times\nfaster if the filelist is in RAM with 50MB/s burst.\n\nThe maximum length of a description line allowed is 1000 chars. Since /X\nallows 80 chars/line as maximum we think this is no bug. If a line is longer\nthan 1000 chars enforcer hits may occur. A check for line length would slow\ndown the code significantly. That`s why we don`t do it.\n\nFor those who are interested, a short explanation of what "double buffered\nasync I/O" means:\nDue to the coolness of the Amiga, SCSI is the most accepted standard on this\nplatform (..well if we dont consider 4000 desktops..). SCSI has the ability\nto transfer data per DMA, thus meaning without using the processor. This is\nwere async I/O comes in. A program using double buffered async I/O lets the\nfilesystem first fill up one buffer, then sends the request to fill up the\nsecond buffer, and while the HD is busy transfering data to the 2nd buffer the\nprocessor is free to do its work on the first one. As you can imagine this\ntechnique dramatically speeds up the whole process.\n\nShell version now included.\n\nA pseudo door that calls the door to be debugged is now developed. This way you\ncan use SAS/C`s debugger cpr easily. If you need it just ask.\n\nSend your suggestions or bug reports to [email removed] or\[email removed].\n\nReverse search is quite slow, because the seeking in the filelist (which is\neven asynchronous) takes 87% of the execution time on Crayor`s system (060&\nCyberScsi). Use a cache program like DynamiCache V1.02 by Christopher A. Wolf\nwith big memory values to make reverse search as fast as forwards search.\nMaybe a scsi RAID system could be a good solution for reverse searching too,\nif you have one please contact Crayor!\n\n\nMemory Requirements\n-------------------\nApprox. 2*blocksize*100 bytes which is about 100k for load buffers plus 20k\nfor print buffer plus code size\n(blocksize is usually 512 bytes)\n\nAmiExpress3.38 needs approx. 200k to run it.\n\n\nShell Version\n-------------\nThe shell version needs a config file with the name\nprogdir:<executable_name>.config\n\nThis way you can have several instances of WarpSearch_shell with different\nnames for your filelist collections.\n\nLook at the example file "WarpSearch_shell.config" for the construction.\nRemember that characters like ´+´ have special meanings in the shell.\nIf you hit return while not beeing at a prompt the output will be trashed\nofcoz.\n\n\nGreetz\n------\nSome hellos to the following guys:\n\n"Ibo"  - with his always busy or down BBS, so that we weren`t able to abuse\n         his BBS for beta testing ;)\nHijack - thx for the cool name of this door m8. (yep! "WarpSearch" actually was\n         his idea)\nSCSI   - for his help on using iwan.device and other help\nAmok   - for the address of Mr.F\nSTC    - for the competition of coding the fastest search code for /X filelists\nHydra  - for still developing hbbs\nDave Haynie\n       - for answering my several emails\n\nRevision History\n----------------\nV1.0 - first public release\nV2.0 - second public release\nV2.1 - bugfixed V2.0\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',32646,1,0,NULL,NULL,'warps_21','scan',1780048830);
