INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('xtrude12','XTRUDE12.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/XTRUDE12.LHA','Xtruder','XIM','Xtruder','1.2',NULL,NULL,'with BBS''s in mind. Checks lha archives for vira, Arexx and Locale support.',replace('Xtruder v1.2! A new virus killer\nwith BBS''s in mind. Checks lha\narchives for vira, Arexx and\nLocale support.\n','\n',char(10)),'Xtruder.guide',replace('@DATABASE "Xtruder.guide"\n@AUTHOR "Martin Wulffeld"\n\n* $VER: Xtruder.guide 1.2 (5.12.94)\n* Copyright © 1994 Martin Wulffeld\n\n@WIDTH 80\n@HEIGHT 255\n\n@NODE Main "Xtruder guide"\n\n Xtruder\n *******\n\n @{" About Xtruder " LINK AboutXtruder}\n @{" About SHI " LINK AboutSHI}\n @{" Disclaimer " LINK Legal}\n\n @{" Features " LINK Features}\n\n @{" CLI usage " LINK CLI_Usage}\n @{" Menus " LINK Menus}\n @{" Gadgets " LINK Gadgets}\n @{" ARexx commands " LINK ARexxCmds}\n\n @{" Trouble shooting " LINK TroubleShooting}\n\n @{" History " LINK History}\n @{" Future " LINK Future}\n\n @{" How to register " LINK Register}\n @{" Contacting the author "LINK Author}\n @{" Credits " LINK Credits}\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE AboutXtruder "About Xtruder"\n\n Xtruder is copyright © 1994 Martin Wulffeld - All Rights Reserved.\n\n\n This program is SHAREWARE and you''re only allowed a 2 week evaluation\n period. If you want to use Xtruder beyond that period you must register.\n\n                         @{" How to register " LINK Register}\n\n This is yet another viruskiller but in quite a different vein than\n the majority. The main aim with Xtruder is to stop the spreading of\n vira through bulletin boards.\n\n Xtruder requires Kickstart 2.04 or higher.\n\n It needs the following versions of libraries:\n \n reqtools.library      v38+  -  ReqTools is Copyright (c) Nico François\n unpack.library        v39+  -  Library made by Thomas Neumann/SHI\n removelink.library    v32+  -  Library made by Johan Öhman/SHI\n Bootblock.library     v3+   -  Library made by Johan Eliasson/SHI\n FileID.library        v6+   -  Made by BLOODROCK of SYNDICATE\n \n and the following must be placed in L:\n \n Bootblock.brainfile        -  Used by Bootblock.library\n\n\n When you start Xtruder you will either see the GUI or nothing! If you\n don''t see anything it''s because you have configured it not to popup at\n start. See @{" General preferences " LINK MENU_General} for more information.\n\n It will of course load the preferences, paths and rexx prefs files if\n they are available. \n\n When Xtruder "sleeps" it will still be aware of the time check and\n ARexx scripts can also still be executed.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE AboutSHI "About SHI"\n\n If  you   know  a  virus  programmer  you  can  get  a reward of $ 1000 for\n supplying  his  name  and  address.  The fact is that the law punishes data \n crime very severely. (5 years in jail in most countries).\n \n We  are an international group with more than 250 members  who have started \n trying to stop the spreading of vira. Let me give you some examples:\n\n\n        1. Our motto is: "Safe Hex", who dares do anything else today?".\n        2. A virus bank containing all well known virus killer programmes.\n        3. We help people to get money back lost by virus infection.\n        4. We write articles about virus problems for 8 magazines.\n        5. We release the newest and the best virus killers around.\n        6. We have more than 20 "Virus Centers" worldwide  where you \n           can get free virus help by phoning our "Hotline", and the\n           newest killers translated in your own language at very little\n           cost.\n        7. We hope that you can see how important your support is too,\n           if you are using one of the following  programs, which are\n           actually using our anti virus libraries:\n\n \n                     * Virus Checker by Johan Veldthuis\n \n                     * Virus Scanner by Gabriele Greco\n\n                     * Fides Professional by John Lohmeyer\n\n                     * Fides Checker by John Lohmeyer\n \n                     * D-Copy by Stefan Bernbo\n \n                     * X-Copy APRIL ''93 by Cachet Software (commercial)\n\n                     * Disk Ute Copy by Alchemy Software.\n \n                     * MT-Copy by Gert-Jan Strik, is doing a file- and \n                       boot virus check while you are copying disks and \n                       is extremly fast too... supprised?\n\n\n Please send new viruses because without YOUR SUPPORT TOO, \n we can''t stop the future virus spreading!\n\n\n For more information contact:\n\n        SAFE HEX INTERNATIONAL           (Please  send  a "Coupon-Response \n        Erik Loevendahl Soerensen        International" and a self addres-\n        Snaphanevej 10                   sed  envelope, if you want infor-\n        4720 Praestoe                    mation about SHI by letter).\n        Denmark                             \n\n        Phone: +45 55 99 25 12\n        Fax:   +45 55 99 34 98\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE Legal "Legal stuff"\n\n When there in the following is refered to Xtruder it implies the files\n listed in the Contents file.\n\n Xtruder is Copyright © 1994 Martin Wulffeld. All rights reserved.\n\n Xtruder may not be modified nor disassembled in any way! Doing so is\n illegal.\n\n Xtruder may not be used for commercial purposes without a written\n permission from me. Ie distributing Xtruder on a coverdisk is strictly\n forbidden.\n\n You may distribute Xtruder as long as all files are accompanied it and\n no more than a reasonable copying fee is charged, but no more than US $5.\n Xtruder may be packed with lha or similar archiver as long as the files\n are not modified by it.\n\n Xtruder has been tested on several machine configurations and has proven\n to run fine on those, but I the author, Martin Wulffeld, cannot be held\n responsible for ANY damage the Xtruder package might have inflicted to\n your system due to bugs or misuse!\n\n If you want to see future development on Xtruder you have to register.\n\n @{" How to register " LINK Register}\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE Register "How to register"\n\n To register, send me an errorfree doubledensity disk and US $15, DM 25,\n £10 or 100 DKr. Cash is prefered.\n\n Fill out the registrationform which is included in the Xtruder archive as\n ''Xtruder.regform'' and mail it to me.\n \n Version 1.0 of Xtruder has not been crippled but future versions might\n be if the donations are few. Therefore I might make a key file.\n If I do so all those who registered before the key file was made will\n of course be able to get their key file. Just send a disk to me and\n I''ll forward a keyfile with the newest version of Xtruder back to you.\n\n NOTE NEW EMAIL NUMBERS:\n\n * Snail mail:    Martin Wulffeld\n                  Fredensvej 14\n                  4720 Præstø\n                  Denmark\n                  \n * Fidonet:       2:236/12.1 (Preferably use this one)\n                  2:236/116.14\n\n * Amynet:        39:141/12.1\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE Features "Features"\n\n   * A commodity\n   * Supports newlook menus\n   * Able to unpack almost any cruncher type\n   * Check for vira within archives\n   * Check specified paths every n minutes and handle vira without\n     any user interaction at all\n   * Save bootblocks as binary for later use\n   * ARexx port\n   * 99% keyboard controllable\n   * Configurable to skip already checked files\n   * Time check\n   * Locale support (WB 2.1 or higher)\n   * Works with MultiUserFileSystem (AFAIK ;)\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE CLI_Usage "CLI Usage"\n\n Xtruder has a small but efficient CLI interface. The template is:\n \n P=PATH/K,F=FILE/K,Q=QUIT/S\n \n The arguments have the following meaning \n \n P/PATH        - The path to check\n F/FILE        - The file to check. File is treated as uncrunched.\n Q/QUIT        - Quit Xtruder after checking path/file\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE Menus "Menus in Xtruder"\n\n  @{" About... " LINK MENU_About}\n  @{" Hide     " LINK MENU_Hide}\n  @{" Quit     " LINK MENU_Quit}\n\n  @{" Load ARexx scripts...   " LINK MENU_LoadCmds}\n  @{" Save ARexx scripts...   " LINK MENU_SaveCmds}\n  @{" Install ARexx script... " LINK MENU_InstallCmd}\n  @{" <script names>          " LINK MENU_ChooseCmd}\n\n  @{" Clear... " LINK MENU_LogClear}\n  @{" Show...  " LINK MENU_LogShow}\n  @{" Save...  " LINK MENU_LogSave}\n\n  @{" Paths...   " LINK MENU_Paths}\n  @{" General... " LINK MENU_General}\n  @{" Check...   " LINK MENU_Check}\n  @{" Save...    " LINK MENU_Save}\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE MENU_About "Project menu - About..."\n\n Well... surprise, surprise! Information on Xtruder will be shown.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE MENU_Hide "Hide"\n\n Choosing Hide will hide the graphical appearance of Xtruder. You can then\n press the defined popkey and it will reopen it''s GUI.\n \n NOTE: When the GUI is hidden the timed check is still active and ARexx\n       script can still be executed.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE MENU_Quit "Quit"\n\n I just don''t feel like explaining this right now :-)\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE MENU_LoadCmds "Load ARexx scripts"\n\n Choosing this will pop up a file requester with the default name for the\n ARexx script file. But you can of course choose an earlier saved script\n file.\n\n After having loaded the commands they will appear in the ARexx menu.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE MENU_SaveCmds "Save ARexx scripts"\n\n Choosing this will pop up a file requester with the default name for the\n ARexx script file. You can of course choose another name for the scripts\n but upon startup ONLY the ARexx script file ''S:Xtruder.rexxcmds'' will be\n loaded.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE MENU_InstallCmd "Install ARexx script"\n\n First a little requester will appear asking you to enter a number  which\n corresponds to the item in the ARexx menu where this script will appear.\n Upon pressing return or ''Okay'' yet another requester appears. Here you can\n have to write the filename of the rexx script. Fx ''xtruder/chkpaths.rexx''.\n\n The filename will appear in the menu and when you select the script it\n will be executed.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE MENU_ChooseCmd "Execute ARexx script"\n\n Executes the ARexx script installed in the chosen menu.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE MENU_LogClear "Clearing log"\n\n Clears the log buffer.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE MENU_LogShow "Show log"\n\n Shows the contents of the log buffer.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE MENU_LogSave "Save log"\n\n Saves the contents of the log buffer. Pops up a file requester where you\n must choose a filename.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE MENU_Paths "Paths preferences"\n\n Here you will see a list of the paths which you check with  @{" All Paths " LINK GADGET_Check_ALLPATHS}\n or then again maybe nothing at all. Anyway choose ''Add Path'' and a path\n requester pops up. Choose Okay and the path you selected will be shown in\n the list.\n\n To remove a path just select one and press ''Remove Path''. Easy? Yep!\n\n To save the paths (instead of choosing them over and over again) press\n ''Save paths'' and they will be saved to ''S:Xtruder.paths''.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE MENU_General "General preferences"\n\n @{" Log file " LINK PREFS_LOGFILE }\n @{" Write to log buffer " LINK PREFS_WRITETOLOG }\n @{" Cx Popkey " LINK PREFS_CXPOPKEY }\n @{" Popup at start " LINK PREFS_POPUPATSTART }\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_LOGFILE "General preferences - Log file"\n\n A filename for the log buffer. When you first select @{" Save... " LINK MENU_LogSave} this\n name will be used to save the log! If a file with that name exist a\n filerequester will request you for a new name.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_WRITETOLOG "General preferences - Write to log buffer"\n\n Whether you want to write to the log buffer or not!\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_CXPOPKEY "General preferences - Popkey"\n\n Your popkey! Default popkey is ''control lamiga x''.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_POPUPATSTART "General preferences - Pop up at start"\n\n If you want to hide Xtruder when it is started just deselect this check\n box gadget. Ideal for BBS users who doesn''t want Xtruder to pop up but\n just stay in the background.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE MENU_Check "Check preferences"\n\n @{" Unpack path " LINK PREFS_UNPACKPATH }\n @{" Virus path  " LINK PREFS_VIRUSPATH }\n @{" Virus comment " LINK PREFS_VIRUSCOMMENT }\n @{" Virus rename extension " LINK PREFS_VIRUSRENAMEEXT }\n @{" Custom BB " LINK PREFS_CUSTOMBB }\n @{" Do if virus found " LINK PREFS_IFFOUND }\n @{" Do if virus copied " LINK PREFS_IFCOPIED }\n @{" Time check " LINK PREFS_TIMECHECK }\n @{" CPB flags " LINK PREFS_CPBFLAGS }\n @{" Set CPB Flags " LINK PREFS_SETCPBFLAGS }\n @{" Check files with CPB " LINK PREFS_CHECKCPBFILES }\n @{" Auto deprotect " LINK PREFS_AUTODEPROTECT }\n @{" Decrunch files " LINK PREFS_DECRUNCHFILES }\n @{" Extract archives " LINK PREFS_EXTRACTARCHIVES }\n @{" Check dirs recursively " LINK PREFS_CHECKRECURSE }\n @{" Safe delete " LINK PREFS_SAFEDELETE }\n @{" Auto check disks " LINK PREFS_AUTOCHECKDISKS }\n @{" Auto read bootblock " LINK PREFS_AUTOREADBOOTBLOCK }\n @{" Show bootblock " LINK PREFS_SHOWBOOTBLOCK }\n @{" Quiet time check " LINK PREFS_QUIETTIMECHECK }\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_UNPACKPATH "Check preferences - Unpack path"\n\n By default this string gadget contains ''RAM:Unpack''. This path must be\n present for Xtruder if you will be able to decrunch files or extract\n archives.\n \n Upon startup Xtruder will try to find this path and if it doesn''t exist\n Xtruder will ask you if it should be created.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_VIRUSPATH "Check preferences - Virus path"\n\n By default this string gadget contains ''RAM:Virus''. This path must be\n present for Xtruder being able to store infected files.\n\n Upon startup Xtruder will try to find this path and if it doesn''t exist\n Xtruder will ask you if it should be created.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_VIRUSCOMMENT "Check preferences - Virus comment"\n\n By default this string gadget contains ''This file is a virus or has a\n virus linked to it''.\n\n This is the comment that automatically will be used when Xtruder finds a\n virus and  @{" Do if virus found " LINK PREFS_IFFOUND } or @{" Do if virus copied " LINK PREFS_IFCOPIED } has been set \n to ''Comment''.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_VIRUSRENAMEEXT "Check preferences - Virus rename extension"\n\n By default this string gadget contains ''_VIRUS''.\n\n If you have set @{" Do if virus found " LINK PREFS_IFFOUND } or @{" Do if virus copied " LINK PREFS_IFCOPIED } to ''Rename''\n this is what will be appended to the virus:\n \n Example:\n \n A file ''BadBoy'' would then be renamed to ''BadBoy_VIRUS''.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_CUSTOMBB "Check preferences - Custom BB"\n\n By default this string gadget contains nothing.\n\n The filename of a custom bootblock.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_IFFOUND "Check preferences - Do if virus found"\n\n You have the choice between the following:\n \n  @{" Enfeeble " LINK PREFS_IF_VIRENFEEBLE}\n  @{" Delete " LINK PREFS_IF_VIRDELETE}\n  @{" Rename " LINK PREFS_IF_VIRRENAME}\n  @{" Comment " LINK PREFS_IF_VIRCOMMENT}\n  @{" Copy " LINK PREFS_IF_VIRCOPY}\n  @{" Move " LINK PREFS_IF_VIRMOVE}\n  @{" Request - Enfeeble " LINK PREFS_IF_VIRENFEEBLE}\n  @{" Request - Delete " LINK PREFS_IF_VIRDELETE}\n  @{" Request - Rename " LINK PREFS_IF_RQVIRRENAME}\n  @{" Request - Comment " LINK PREFS_IF_RQVIRCOMMENT}\n  @{" Request - Copy " LINK PREFS_IF_VIRCOPY}\n  @{" Request - Move " LINK PREFS_IF_VIRMOVE}\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_IF_VIRENFEEBLE "Do if virus found/copied - Enfeeble"\n\n Simply removes the executable bit from the protection flags of the\n infected file so it can''t be started.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_IF_VIRDELETE "Do if virus found - Delete"\n\n Deletes the infected file/archive.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_IF_VIRRENAME "Do if virus found/copied - Rename"\n\n Appends the @{" Virus rename extension " LINK PREFS_VIRUSRENAMEEXT} to the infected file/archive.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_IF_VIRCOMMENT "Do if virus found/copied - Comment"\n\n Comments the infected file/archive with @{" Virus comment " LINK PREFS_VIRUSCOMMENT}\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_IF_VIRCOPY "Do if virus found - Copy"\n\n Copies the infected file/archive to the @{" Virus path " LINK PREFS_VIRUSPATH}.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_IF_VIRMOVE "Do if virus found - Move"\n\n Copies the infected file/archive to the @{" Virus path " LINK PREFS_VIRUSPATH} and then\n deletes the original!\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_IF_VIRNOTHING "Do if virus found/copied - Nothing"\n\n Quite tricky this one .-) Does absolutely NOTHING!\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_IF_RQVIRENFEEBLE "Do if virus found/copied - Request -> Enfeeble"\n\n Simply removes the executable bit from the protection flags of the\n infected file so it can''t be started.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_IF_RQVIRDELETE "Do if virus found/copied - Request -> Delete"\n\n Deletes the infected file/archive.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_IF_RQVIRRENAME "Do if virus found/copied - Request -> Rename"\n\n A request for a name for the infected file pops up. This name will NOT\n be appended to the old name!\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_IF_RQVIRCOMMENT "Do if virus found/copied - Request -> Comment"\n\n A request for a comment pops up where you can write a string of max 80\n characters.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_IF_RQVIRCOPY "Do if virus found - Request -> Copy"\n\n Copies the infected file/archive to the @{" Virus path " LINK PREFS_VIRUSPATH}.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_IF_RQVIRMOVE "Do if virus found - Request -> Move"\n\n Copies the infected file/archive to the @{" Virus path " LINK PREFS_VIRUSPATH} and then\n deletes the original!\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_IFCOPIED "Check preferences - Do if virus copied"\n\n You have the choice between the following:\n \n  @{" Enfeeble " LINK PREFS_IF_VIRENFEEBLE}\n  @{" Rename " LINK PREFS_IF_VIRRENAME}\n  @{" Comment " LINK PREFS_IF_VIRCOMMENT}\n  @{" Nothing " LINK PREFS_IF_VIRNOTHING}\n  @{" Request - Enfeeble " LINK PREFS_IF_VIRENFEEBLE}\n  @{" Request - Rename " LINK PREFS_IF_RQVIRRENAME}\n  @{" Request - Comment " LINK PREFS_IF_RQVIRCOMMENT}\n  @{" Request - Nothing " LINK PREFS_IF_VIRNOTHING}\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_TIMECHECK "Check preferences - Time check"\n\n If set to 0 minutes there will not be an active time check but as soon as\n you change this value to something higher than 0 and leave preferences\n Xtruder will try to set up a time request and notify you if it succeded\n in doing so. Every time you change the value Xtruder will abort the current\n time request and set up a new one.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_CPBFLAGS "Check preferences - CPB flags"\n\n CPB stands for ''Checked Protection Bits''. These flags are used for\n identifying files which have already been checked. Put in another way: If\n a file has the flags specified here and  @{" Check files with CPB " LINK PREFS_CHECKCPBFILES} is\n off, that file will be skipped! Ideal if you have a lot of lha archives\n which has been checked before.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_SETCPBFLAGS "Check preferences - Set CPB flags"\n\n CPB stands for ''Checked Protection Bits''. Will set the @{" CPB flags " LINK PREFS_CPBFLAGS}\n specified if a file was succesfully checked.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_CHECKCPBFILES "Check preferences - Check files with CPB"\n\n If set, files with the Checked Protection Bits flags will also be checked.\n Ideal when you get a new version of removelink.library which knows more\n vira.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_AUTODEPROTECT "Check preferences - Auto deprotect"\n\n If a file is protected from reading you can set this option and it will be\n deprotected.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_DECRUNCHFILES "Check preferences - Decrunch files"\n\n Set this to decrunch files. Very handy indeed :-)\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_EXTRACTARCHIVES "Check preferences - Extract archives"\n\n Set this to extract lha archives. Remember that ALL files within the\n archive will be decrunched or extracted if they can be!\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_CHECKRECURSE "Check preferences - Check dirs recursively"\n\n Set this if you want to enter sub-directories.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_SAFEDELETE "Check preferences - Safe delete"\n\n When an archive has been extracted it either takes up memory or HD space.\n Therefore the extracted files in the @{" Unpack path " LINK PREFS_UNPACKPATH} will be deleted.\n This can be done without user interaction at all but if you set this\n option you will be asked before Xtruder starts deleting!\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_AUTOCHECKDISKS "Check preferences - Auto check disks"\n\n If set, Xtruder will check any inserted disk as a normal path. Ie no need\n to fumble with the gadgets if you need to check your whole disk collection\n for vira.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_AUTOREADBOOTBLOCK "Check preferences - Auto read bootblock"\n\n If set, Xtruder will check any inserted disks bootblocks.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_SHOWBOOTBLOCK "Check preferences - Show bootblock"\n\n If set, Xtruder will show the checked bootblock on the screen.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PREFS_QUIETTIMECHECK "Check preferences - Quiet time check"\n\n If set, Xtruder will not ask you if it should commence checking\n specified paths. Ideal if you run a BBS and want to check your uploads\n every hour or so.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE MENU_Save "Save preferences"\n\n Save preferences to ''S:Xtruder.prefs''.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE Gadgets "Gadgets in the main window of Xtruder"\n\n @{" Check         " LINK GADGET_Check}\n @{" Bootblock     " LINK GADGET_Bootblock}\n @{" System        " LINK GADGET_System}\n @{" Miscellaneous " LINK GADGET_Miscellaneous}\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GADGET_Check "Check menu"\n\n @{" All Paths   " LINK GADGET_Check_ALLPATHS}\n @{" Single path " LINK GADGET_Check_SINGLEPATH}\n @{" Bootblock   " LINK GADGET_Check_BOOTBLOCK}\n @{" Memory      " LINK GADGET_Check_MEMORY}\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GADGET_Check_ALLPATHS "Check All Paths"\n\n This function is mainly for BBS use but can of course also be used by the\n general user. To use this function you must first specify some paths which\n you want to check regularly. This is done in @{" Paths... " LINK MENU_Paths }. Pressing All Paths\n will then automatically check all the paths you have specified.\n\n During a scan of a directory a little window pops up in the right side of\n the screen with 4 gadgets named:\n\n @{" Stop     " LINK GADGET_CONTROL_STOP}\n @{" Pause    " LINK GADGET_CONTROL_PAUSE}\n @{" Next     " LINK GADGET_CONTROL_NEXT}\n @{" Skip     " LINK GADGET_CONTROL_SKIP}\n\n E.g.: If a file is being decrunched and you press ''Stop'' Xtruder will\n       first stop when this file has decrunched and checked.\n\n Pressing  ''Pause''  will  pause  the  scanning  and wait until you press it\n again.\n\n If you have set @{" Check dirs recursively " LINK PREFS_CHECKRECURSE} Xtruder will enter sub-directories\n and check them as well. Otherwise only the files in this directory will be\n checked.\n\n If Xtruder finds a virus there is a number of different actions which can\n be carried out. These actions are discussed in @{" Do if virus found " LINK PREFS_IFFOUND }.\n\n If a lha archive is encountered and you have lha in C: this file will be\n extracted to the @{" Unpack path " LINK PREFS_UNPACKPATH }, and all files within\n this archive (crunched programs/other archives) will be unpacked/extracted\n too. When the archive has been extracted succesfully or unsuccesfully the\n unpack path will be checked.\n \n It''s a good idea to make lha resident. This will reduce the time spent\n checking archives.\n\n When a scanning of a directory is performed the number of files encountered\n will be written in the action window. Files in an archive are not counted\n though (they will be soon :-)\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GADGET_CONTROL_STOP "Control menu - Stop"\n\n Aborts the whole scan.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GADGET_CONTROL_PAUSE "Control menu - Pause"\n\n Pops up a requester informing you of your pausing and waits for you to\n continue.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GADGET_CONTROL_NEXT "Control menu - Next"\n\n ''Next'' will jump to the next path you specified in @{" Paths... " LINK MENU_Paths}.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GADGET_CONTROL_SKIP "Control menu - Skip"\n\n If you have entered a sub-directory with hundreds of sources and wish to\n skip it press Skip!\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GADGET_Check_SINGLEPATH "Check a single path"\n\n Does what it says actually. Pops up a requester where you select the path\n you want to check, and then checks it.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GADGET_Check_BOOTBLOCK "Check a bootblock"\n\n A window will pop up with 4 gadgets containing the possible drives (DF0 -\n DF3). Those which you do not have are ghosted eg disabled. Choose a drive\n and another window will pop up with 9 choices of bootblocks to install. The\n first 8 are from the bootblock library and represents the standard types of\n bootblocks. The last one (Custom BB) is a custom bootblock taken from the\n the @{" Custom BB " LINK PREFS_CUSTOMBB } in preferences.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GADGET_Check_MEMORY "Check the memory"\n\n Checks the memory via the removelink library and kills any vira it might\n have found.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GADGET_Bootblock "Bootblock gadgets"\n\n  @{"   Install   " LINK GADGET_Bootblock_INSTALL}\n  @{"  Save  bin  " LINK GADGET_Bootblock_SAVEBIN}\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GADGET_Bootblock_INSTALL "Install a bootblock"\n\n A window will pop up with 4 gadgets containing the possible drives (DF0 -\n DF3). Those which you do not have are ghosted eg disabled. Choose a drive\n and another window will pop up with 9 choices of bootblocks to install. The\n first 8 are from the bootblock library and represents the standard types of\n bootblocks. The last one (Custom BB) is a custom bootblock taken from a\n file. You can set the filename of the custom bootblock in check\n preferences.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GADGET_Bootblock_SAVEBIN "Save a bootblock as binary"\n\n A window will pop up with 4 gadgets containing the possible drives (DF0 -\n DF3). Those which you do not have are ghosted eg disabled. Choose a drive\n and the bootblock of the drive will be read. If everything wen''t okay a\n filerequester pops up. Choose a file or write a name in the filename gadget\n and the bootblock will be saved.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GADGET_System "System gadgets"\n\n  @{"  Libraries  " LINK GADGET_System_LIBRARIES}\n  @{"   Devices   " LINK GADGET_System_DEVICES}\n  @{"  Resources  " LINK GADGET_System_RESOURCES}\n  @{"    Tasks    " LINK GADGET_System_TASKS}\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GADGET_System_LIBRARIES "List of libraries"\n\n A window pops up showing all the libraries currently loaded to memory.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GADGET_System_DEVICES "List of devices"\n\n A window pops up showing all the devices currently loaded to memory.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GADGET_System_RESOURCES "List of resources"\n\n A window pops up showing all the resources currently loaded to memory.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GADGET_System_TASKS "List of tasks"\n\n A window pops up showing all the waiting tasks.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GADGET_Miscellaneous "Miscellaneous gadgets"\n\n  @{" Delete  " LINK GADGET_Miscellaneous_DELETE}\n  @{" Rename  " LINK GADGET_Miscellaneous_RENAME}\n  @{" Makedir " LINK GADGET_Miscellaneous_MAKEDIR}\n  @{" Comment " LINK GADGET_Miscellaneous_COMMENT}\n  @{" Execute " LINK GADGET_Miscellaneous_EXECUTE}\n\n  @{" Type " LINK GADGET_Miscellaneous_PATHTYPE}\n\n  @{" Type   " LINK GADGET_Miscellaneous_FILETYPE}\n  @{" Unpack " LINK GADGET_Miscellaneous_UNPACK}\n  @{" Check  " LINK GADGET_Miscellaneous_CHECK}\n\n  @{" Bootblock " LINK GADGET_Miscellaneous_BOOTBLOCK}\n  @{" File/Link " LINK GADGET_Miscellaneous_FILELINK}\n  @{" Crunchers " LINK GADGET_Miscellaneous_CRUNCHERS}\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GADGET_Miscellaneous_DELETE "Delete a file"\n\n You might want to delete a file once in a while ( I do :) so just use this\n function.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GADGET_Miscellaneous_RENAME "Rename a file"\n\n In case you want to rename a file to something completely different.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GADGET_Miscellaneous_MAKEDIR "Create a directory"\n\n Want a new unpack path? Just create one with this function.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GADGET_Miscellaneous_COMMENT "Comment a file"\n\n You just found an archive with a virus, and want to comment it! Well then\n this function will come in handy! If a file already has a comment it will\n be in the string gadget.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GADGET_Miscellaneous_EXECUTE "Execute a command"\n\n Well, if you want to execute something like an external memory checker you\n could use this function.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GADGET_Miscellaneous_PATHTYPE "Identify files in a path"\n\n Identify files in a path! Their filetypes will be written to the window\n but if you have set @{" Write to log buffer " LINK PREFS_WRITETOLOG} they\n will also be written to the log buffer!\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GADGET_Miscellaneous_FILETYPE "Identify a file"\n\n Have you always wondered what that darn certain file was? Well, then you\n can use this function to identify it.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GADGET_Miscellaneous_UNPACK "Unpack a file"\n\n Unpacks the file you select to the @{" Unpack path " LINK PREFS_UNPACKPATH}.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GADGET_Miscellaneous_CHECK "Check a file"\n\n Checks the file you select for file/link virus.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GADGET_Miscellaneous_BOOTBLOCK "List of known bootblock vira"\n\n Will simply show those bootblock vira which are known to the bootblock\n library''s brainfile!\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GADGET_Miscellaneous_FILELINK "List of known file/link vira"\n\n Will show those file/link vira which are known to the current version of\n removelink library!\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE GADGET_Miscellaneous_CRUNCHERS "List of known crunchers"\n\n Will show the types of crunchers which are known to the unpack library!\n@ENDNODE\n\n::::::::::::::::::::::::::: ARexx commands ::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\n\n@NODE ARexxCmds "ARexx commands"\n\n As you probably know Xtruder has an ARexx interface. The address of the\n Xtruder ARexx port is ''XTRUDER''.\n\n These are the commands:\n\n @{" GETFILE          " LINK AREXX_GETFILE }\n @{" GETPATH          " LINK AREXX_GETPATH }\n @{" CHECKALLPATHS    " LINK AREXX_CHECKALLPATHS }\n @{" CHECKPATH        " LINK AREXX_CHECKPATH }\n @{" CHECKCLEANUP     " LINK AREXX_CHECKCLEANUP }\n @{" CHECKFILE        " LINK AREXX_CHECKFILE }\n @{" CHECKMEMORY      " LINK AREXX_CHECKMEMORY }\n @{" CHECKBOOTBLOCK   " LINK AREXX_CHECKBOOTBLOCK }\n @{" INSTALLBOOTBLOCK " LINK AREXX_INSTALLBOOTBLOCK }\n @{" UNPACKFILE       " LINK AREXX_UNPACKFILE }\n @{" CLEANUP          " LINK AREXX_CLEANUP }\n @{" SHOWGUI          " LINK AREXX_SHOWGUI }\n @{" HIDEGUI          " LINK AREXX_HIDEGUI }\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE AREXX_GETFILE "ARexx command - GETFILE"\n\n  NAME\n        GETFILE - Get a filename\n  \n  SYNOPSIS\n        GETFILE <pathname>\n\n  FUNCTION\n        Request the user to select a filename from the filerequester.\n\n  INPUTS\n        pathname    - NOT required but if pathname is present it will\n                      be set in the filerequester.\n\n  RESULT\n        name        - Will return whatever that was in the path gadget with\n                      the filename appended to it.\n\n        0          - If the user selected ''Cancel''.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE AREXX_GETPATH "ARexx command - GETPATH"\n\n  NAME\n        GETPATH - Get a path from the filerequester\n\n  SYNOPSIS\n        GETPATH <pathname>\n  \n  FUNCTION\n        Request the user to select a path from the pathrequester.\n        \n  INPUTS\n        pathname    - NOT required but if pathname is present it will\n                      be set in the filerequester.\n\n  RESULT\n        name        - Whatever in the path string gadget.\n        \n        0           - If the user selected ''Cancel''.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE AREXX_CHECKALLPATHS "ARexx command - CHECKALLPATHS"\n \n  NAME\n        CHECKALLPATHS - Check spefied paths for vira\n  \n  SYNOPSIS\n        CHECKALLPATHS\n  \n  FUNCTION\n        Checks the paths you have set in @{" Paths... " LINK MENU_PATHS } for vira.\n\n  RESULT\n        0 - n       - How many vira that were found.\n\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE AREXX_CHECKPATH "ARexx command - CHECKPATH"\n \n  NAME\n        CHECKPATH - Check a path for vira\n  \n  SYNOPSIS\n        CHECKPATH pathname\n  \n  FUNCTION\n        Checks a path like @{" All Paths " LINK GADGET_Check_ALLPATHS}.\n\n  INPUTS\n        pathname    - A fully qualified pathname.\n\n  RESULT\n        0 - n       - How many vira that were found.\n        \n        -1          - If it couldn''t find ''pathname''.\n@ENDNODE\n \n@NODE AREXX_CHECKCLEANUP "ARexx command - CHECKCLEANUP"\n \n  NAME\n        CHECKCLEANUP - Check unpack path and delete afterwards\n  \n  SYNOPSIS\n        CHECKCLEANUP\n  \n  FUNCTION\n        Checks the unpack path and then deletes all files within afterwards.\n\n  INPUTS\n        pathname    - A fully qualified pathname.\n\n  RESULT\n        0 - n       - How many vira that were found.\n        \n        -1          - If it couldn''t find ''pathname''.\n@ENDNODE\n \n@NODE AREXX_CHECKFILE "ARexx command - CHECKFILE"\n\n  NAME\n        CHECKFILE - Check a file\n  \n  SYNOPSIS\n        CHECKFILE filename\n  \n  FUNCTION\n        Checks a file to see if it is a virus or has one linked up to it.\n  \n  INPUTS\n        filename    - A fully qualified filename.\n\n  RESULT\n        1           - If it is infected.\n        2           - If it is clean.\n\n        0           - If it couldn''t find ''filename'' or load the file perhaps\n                      due to low memory.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE AREXX_CHECKMEMORY "ARexx command - CHECKMEMORY"\n\n  NAME\n        CHECKMEMORY - Check memory for vira\n  \n  SYNOPSIS\n        CHECKMEMORY\n  \n  FUNCTION\n        Checks your memory for vira and kills those that were found.\n \n  RESULT\n        1           - If your memory was infected.\n        2           - If your memory was clean.\n@ENDNODE\n\n\n@NODE AREXX_CHECKBOOTBLOCK "ARexx command - CHECKBOOTBLOCK"\n\n  NAME\n        CHECKBOOTBLOCK - Check a disk bootblock\n\n  SYNOPSIS\n        CHECKBOOTBLOCK unit\n\n  FUNCTION\n        Checks a bootblock and determines via the Bootblock.brainfile if\n        it''s a known virus or not.\n\n  INPUT\n        unit        - The drive unit ranging from 0 to 3 (DFx:).\n\n  RESULT\n        0           - Not a virus\n        1           - If it''s a virus.\n        2           - If the bootblock wasn''t bootable.\n\n        -1          - If failed to read the bootblock.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE AREXX_INSTALLBOOTBLOCK "ARexx command - INSTALLBOOTBLOCK"\n\n  NAME\n        INSTALLBOOTBLOCK - Install a bootblock on a disk\n\n  SYNOPSIS\n        INSTALLBOOTBLOCK unit type\n\n  FUNCTION\n        Will try to install a bootblock on a disk.\n\n  INPUT\n        unit        - The drive unit ranging from 0 to 3 (DFx:).\n        type        - The type of bootblock:\n\n                      0  - 1.x OFS\n                      1  - 1.3 FFS\n                      2  - 2.0 OFS\n                      3  - 2.0 FFS\n                      4  - 2.0 OFS International\n                      5  - 2.0 FFS International\n                      6  - 3.0 OFS DirCache\n                      7  - 3.0 FFS DirCache     \n\n  RESULT\n        0           - Installed succesfully.\n        n           - Error code returned by either IoErr() or trackdisk\n                      device.\n        -99         - Illegal type of bootblock.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE AREXX_UNPACKFILE "ARexx command - UNPACKFILE"\n\n  NAME\n        UNPACKFILE - Unpack a file\n\n  SYNOPSIS\n        UNPACKFILE filename\n\n  FUNCTION\n        Unpacks/extracts a file to the unpack directory.\n\n  INPUTS\n        filename    - A fully qualified filename. Must be with path or else\n                      it will naturally try to load the file from the current\n                      directory.\n\n  RESULT\n        1           - Succes\n\n        0           - In case of error\n        \n  NOTES\n        The unpack library unpacks/extracts all files in an archive, so if\n        you have 2 archives within another archive they will be extracted\n        too.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE AREXX_CLEANUP "ARexx command - CLEANUP"\n\n  NAME\n        CLEANUP - Delete all files in the unpack path\n\n  SYNOPSIS\n        CLEANUP\n\n  FUNCTION\n        Deletes all files in the unpack path. You could use this command in\n        conjunction with UNPACKFILE, CHECKPATH.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE AREXX_SHOWGUI "ARexx command - SHOWGUI"\n\n  NAME\n        SHOWGUI - Shows Xtruder\n\n  SYNOPSIS\n        SHOWGUI\n\n  FUNCTION\n        If Xtruder was asleep it will open it''s GUI (graphical user\n        interface). Otherwise it will pop it''s screen to the front.\n\n  NOTES\n        If memory is VERY low there may not be enough memory to open  \n        the GUI and you will then informed about that with a requester.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE AREXX_HIDEGUI "ARexx command - HIDEGUI"\n\n  NAME\n        HIDEGUI - Hides Xtruder\n  \n  SYNOPSIS\n        HIDEGUI\n\n  FUNCTION\n        Hides the graphical user interface of Xtruder. You can then show it\n        again with @{" SHOWGUI " LINK AREXX_SHOWGUI}.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE TroubleShooting "Problems with Xtruder"\n\n When unpacking a file an error might occur and if so it will be written\n like this:\n \n UNPACK ERROR <errornumber>: Problem with <filename>\n\n With version 39.53 of the unpack library you can encounter the following\n errors:\n \n   1      - Can''t open file\n   2      - Read/Write error\n   3      - Not enough memory\n   4      - Can''t determine file\n   5      - Illegal password\n   6      - Hunk error\n   7      - Extern file error\n   8      - File is corrupt\n   9      - Illegal device\n   10     - Couldn''t open device or create port\n   11     - CRC Checksum error\n   12     - Checksum error\n   13     - Decruncher in library to old\n   14     - Error from device\n   15     - Couldn''t set protection bits\n   16     - Output file error\n\n The most common error is probably error 3! You can then try to clear the log\n buffer to free up some memory!\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE History "The history of Xtruder"\n\n @{" 1.0 " LINK VERS_10 }\n @{" 1.1 " LINK VERS_11 }\n @{" 1.2 " LINK VERS_12 }\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE VERS_10 "Version 1.0  :  18.10.1994"\n\n First release.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE VERS_11 "Version 1.1  :  14.11.1994"\n\n Bug fixes:    Whenever a file with the name ''*'' were encountered Xtruder\n               would hang. Now it simply skips it! This is only a temporary\n               solution though.\n            \n               Wouldn''t delete files in the unpack path after extracting an\n               Lha archive.\n            \n               Showing bootblock could cause a crash on 68000 machines.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE VERS_12 "Version 1.2  :  5.12.1994"\n\n Bug fixes:    ''Miscellaneous/Check file'' didn''t write anything if a data\n               file weren''t infected.\n \n Enhancements: When commenting a file the file''s original comment will be\n               placed in the string gadget.\n               \n               Swedish catalog by Tauno Pinni included.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE Future "Future improvements"\n\n Here are some things I intend to add to Xtruder:\n \n  * Screen mode adaptive\n  * Font sensitive\n  * Palette requester\n  * Check sectors on a drive\n  * Remove vira from files and sectors\n  * Memory info\n  * Hardware info\n  * Unpack track crunched files (DMS)\n  * Scroll window\n  * Public screen\n  * Vector/LVO check\n  * Knowing patches\n  * Check statistics\n  * Improved CLI interface\n  * Custom bootblock brainfile\n  * Custom file brainfile\n  * Integration of the VIB package (Information on virus can be shown)\n  * Bootblock analyzer\n  * More ARexx commands\n  * Zip/other archivers extract routine\n  * Full support for multiple BBS lines\n  * Make coffee :-D\n\n  * Most important! What do YOU want?\n\n All suggestions will be taken into consideration from ALL users.\n\n Of course whether these future improvements will be implemented or not\n depends on how many registered users there are. The more the greater\n enhancements.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE Author "How to contact the author"\n\n If you happen to find a bug please contact me. Remember to state exactly\n the circumstances under which the bug occured and state what computer\n and equipment you have. I can''t do much if you say you have an A500+ so\n you will also have to state your Workbench and Kickstart version.\n\n If you have translated Xtruder into a non supported language please mail\n the CT file to me so I can include it in future versions. Thank you.\n\n You can find my (Email) address in @{" How to register " LINK Register}.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE Credits "Credits"\n\n I would like to thank the following people for their great suggestions and\n sometimes annoying bug reports (Kasper) ;-)\n\n In alphabetical order...\n\n   @{" Jan Bo Andersen " LINK JAC}\n   @{" Paul Browne " LINK PBC}\n   @{" Stefan Daugaard " LINK SDC}\n   @{" Kasper B. Graversen " LINK KBG}\n   @{" Peter Klein " LINK PKC}\n   @{" Henrik Lauridsen " LINK HL}\n   @{" Flemming Lindeblad " LINK FLC}\n   @{" Thomas Neumann " LINK TNC}\n   @{" Erik Løvendahl Sørensen " LINK ELS}\n\n Not to forget Bjørn Moritz and Trucker/Tauno Pinni for the catalog\n translations.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE JAC "Jan Bo Andersen"\n\n ßetatester and all in all a great guy :)\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PBC "Paul Browne"\n\n Leader of SHI UK Division. VERY funny guy :))) Corrected grammar in a\n previous documentation but unfortunately that was lost in cyberspace\n during a HD crash :-( But maybe next time :)\n \n And BTW: I rule Kick Off II  ;-)\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE KBG "Kasper B. Graversen"\n\n Bughunter SUPREME!! Mega thanx dude :) What can I say. Found "some"\n undocumented features once in a while. He''s like ''A helping hand\n when needed'' ;*)\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE SDC "Stefan Daugaard"\n\n YAß (Yet another ßetatester :) Found some well hidden bugs. Geez a whole\n paper actually.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE HL "Henrik Lauridsen"\n\n Thanks for the great (Internet) support. Keep up the excellent work :)\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE PKC "Peter Klein"\n\n Also a ßetatester. And responsible for suggestions leading to Xtruder\n being a commodity and having Arexx support. (And thereby delaying the\n release some months ;)\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE FLC "Flemming Lindeblad"\n\n ßetatester. Suggested Xtruder should have locale support. Made the\n danish translation catalog.\n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE TNC "Thomas Neumann alias Tax of Access"\n\n Creator of the brilliant unpack library. Also reported a couple of bugs :) \n@ENDNODE\n\n@NODE ELS "Erik Løvendahl Sørensen"\n\n SHI leader. Great support!\n@ENDNODE\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',165567,6,0,NULL,NULL,'xtrude12','scan',1780048843);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('xvc_v14','XVC_V14.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/XVC_V14.LHA',NULL,'XIM','LE-window6.12','1.4',NULL,'XVC',NULL,replace('V1.4 XVirusCheck, Check uploaded files for Virii\n','\n',char(10)),'CLASS.README',replace('                      ·\n     .:::::··   ·     : ·\n   .::''  _______    .:::.   _________     rIOT..: - WHQ  JORMAS..: - GHQ\n  .:''  ._\_    /__ .:   :.__\  _____/___. ABYSS.: - GHQ  NUANCE..: - EHQ\n  :·   |     _/   ::     ::  \----.     | GODS..: - GHQ  SYNDROME: - GHQ\n  :    :--.________:.   .:''_____________| mONO..: - GHQ  sUKMAS..: - GHQ\n  :                 :. .:                         ·\n  :               .  ::: .· >>LOS·ENDOS·BBS<<     :\n  :    ____________   :       _____   ________  .:::.    _________\n  :  ._\_____     /___·_____ |     |__\____   \.:    :.__\  _____/___.\n  :  |    _/_____/    |     \|     |      /   ::     ::  \----.     |\n  :  :--._____________|____\ \     |-.________/:.   .:''--.__________|\n  :                  cDr/e^d\______|            :. .:\n                                                 :::      _ _ __  _\nnODE0: +49-(0)-02103-lOCAL   -   33.6k v.34 sOON! :    __/\\__ _ __  _\nnODE1: +49-(0)-02103-52440   -   33.6k v.34 sPEED      \ Oo¯//_ _   _\nnODE2: TELNET 194.163.210.xx -   19.2k !vARIABLE!      / ø _\\__ _  __\nnODE3: TELNET 194.163.210.xx -   19.2k !vARIABLE!      ¯¯\//¯¯_    __\n                                                          ¯\n   - t H I S   i S   d A   b O A R D   f O R   t H E   d E M O S C E N E -','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',11209,7,0,NULL,NULL,'xvc_v14','scan',1780048843);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('xzn_dscp','XZN-DSCP.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/XZN-DSCP.LHA',NULL,'XIM','dreamsweeper.xim',NULL,'hORATiUZ^X-ZonE','XZN','___|   / /(______________/   /_)__/ \_ '' _/__\--___/  ,  \   \  / ___)__ .--/  T__\¯¬(_____\_____/  |__/________\---.',replace('      .____  _               ____ ____\n   ___|   / /(______________/   /_)__/\n   \_ '' _/__\--___/  ,  \   \  / ___)__\n.--/  T__\¯¬(_____\_____/  |__/________\---.\n| /___|                ''---''               |\n|                                          |\n|   dREAMSWEEPER 1.1 bY hORATiUZ^X-ZonE    |\n|   ·StATE OF tHE ARt MiNESWEEPER GAME·    |\n|                                          |\n|    cONVERTEd tO /X (XIM) bY CiNDY/XZN    |\n`-[CiNDY]-------------------------[X-ZoNE]-''\n','\n',char(10)),'dreamsweeper.doc',replace('          ............................................................\n        __:__    _____    _____    _____    _____                    :\n     ___\ | /_ __\_  /__ _) _ /_ __\ _ /_ __\ __/___                 :\n     \    .   \_  __/   \_  (   \    /   \  __)    /   X - Z O N E   :\n      \___|    /__\______/______/___/     \_\_____/                  :\n          |___/ -gdm^lkr           /_______\                         :\n          :                                                          :\n          :..........................................................:\n\n                           IS PROUD TO GIVE YOU\n\n                 -=[÷]=- DREAMSWEEPER XIM VERSION -=[÷]=-\n\n-- Introduction --\n\nDreamsweeper was origionally coded by Horatiuz / X-ZoNe for use in CLI and\nstdio supporting BBS''es.\n\nIt was converted to XIM by Cindy / X-ZoNe.\n\n-- Features --\n\n* Configuration file, explained later.\n* Uses cursorkeys and/or number pad.\n* Highscore file\n* Fast\n\n-- Installation --\n\nJust copy the icon and ''dreamsweeper.xim'' to wherever you want it, see if\nyou need to change anything in the icon.\nCopy the ''dreamsweeper.cfg'' file to S: and edit it, if you dont have any\n''dreamsweeper.cfg'', dreamsweeper will create one by itself, or, just make\na new one, with this information:\n                         ------- CUT HERE -------\n5\n5\ns:Highscores.dat\n\n1st line: Amount of mines\n2nd line: Amount of flags\n3rd line: Highscores file.\n                         ------- CUT HERE -------\nOnly the 3 first lines are necessary, the rest is ignored by the program\nanyway, but you might want that info there sometime in the future ;)\n\n-- Playing --\n\nMoving up        : Cursor up    or 8\nMoving down      : Cursor down  or 2\nMoving right     : Cursor right or 6\nMoving left      : Cursor left  or 4\nMoving right-up  : 9\nMoving right-down: 3\nMoving left-up   : 7\nMoving left-down : 1\nSelecting a cell : RETURN or 5\nFlagging a cell  : F\nExit             : Q\n\nThe rest should be pretty self-explaining.\n\n-- Platforms --\n\nDreamsweeper XIM version has been tested on:\nAmi-Express\nDaydream with the XIM extensional program by Darkelf/Insane.\n\n-- Contacting --\n\nFor any bugs or questions concerning the XIM version, please contact Cindy.\n\nHoratiuz: Tobias Gustaffson\n          Utmarksbacken 1\n          50760 Borås\n          Sweden\n\n          E-Mail: [email removed]\n\nCindy   : Martin Fredricsson\n          3:e Västralundsg. 9\n          59337 Västervik\n          Sweden\n\n          E-Mail: [email removed]\n\nYou might see us on IRCNET, either #amigascne, #amielite or #scene.se.\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',9114,1,0,NULL,NULL,'xzn_dscp','scan',1780048843);
