INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('xzn_lgon','XZN-LGON.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/XZN-LGON.LHA','mAStERlOGON','XIM','.______________________________.',NULL,NULL,'XZN','|:::· ·    ____          · ·:::| |::   \_/ _  // __  _    __  ·:| |:    / \\  //_(__)( \_)(_/_  :|',replace('.______________________________.\n|:::· ·    ____          · ·:::|\n|::   \_/ _  // __  _    __  ·:|\n|:    / \\  //_(__)( \_)(_/_  :|\n|.       \\                   .|\n|       mAStER-lOGON V.1.0     |\n|      /X-Support from XZN!    |\n|Get this Logon-door for Amiex.|\n`------------------------------''','\n',char(10)),'MLogon.Doc',replace('\n\n                         A X-ZoNe Product in 1996!\n\n           ............................................................\n         __:__    _____    _____    _____    _____                    :\n      ___\ | /_ __\_  /__ _) _ /_ __\ _ /_ __\ __/___                 :\n      \    .   \_  __/   \_  (   \    /   \  __)    /   X - Z O N E   :\n       \___|    /__\______/______/___/     \_\_____/                  :\n           |___/ -gdm^lkr           /_______\                         :\n           :                                                          :\n           :..........................................................:\n\n\n                            World Release from:\n           \n\n          ##   ##    ###   ###                                   ##    \n       #####        ## ## ## ##  ####   ######   ####   #####   #####  \n      ##  ##  ###   ##    ##    ##  ##  ##   ## ##  ##  ##  ##   ##    \n     ##   ##   ##   ####  ####  ######  ##      ######  ##   ##  ##    \n     ##   ##   ##   ##    ##    ##      ##      ##      ##   ##  ##    \n     ##   ##   ##   ##    ##    ##   ## ##      ##   ## ##   ##  ##  # \n      ###### ###### ##    ##     #####  ## ©npt  #####  ##   ##   ###  \n        ._____.\n    ____|_    |     _____   _______        ______  _____  _____     ______  \n  ./    _/    |_____\    \./    __/___.____\_    \_\    \/    /_____\    /_. \n  |     \     |     /    /|    _|     |     /     |     \/     |    |\     |\n  |___________|_____\_____|___________|___________|_____||_____|___________|\n                                                                            \n                                                                          \n                        RUNNiNG /X 4.9 a12oo/020/6\n                           1.3 gb ONLiNE sPACE!\n                                X-ZoNe SHQ!\n                     AMiGA,pC,sCNE and *LOTS* of MODS\n                                JUSt cAll!\n                             +46(0)33-412-990!\n\n                    .-------------------------------.\n                    |        ZAblER pRESENTs:       |\n                    |       MasterLogon v1.0        |\n                    |   Nice Looking /X-LogonDoor   |\n                    `-------------------------------''\n\n                                  cREDS:\n                                Code: ZAblER\n                               Debug: Jägarn\n\nIndex:\n~~~~~~\n	Contents\n	Requirements\n	Installation\n	CopyRight\n	Bugreports\n	Greeting\n	Important\n\n\nContents:\n~~~~~~~~~\n\n* BBS:Commands/SYSCmd\n	Quick.Info		.Info to da door\n\n* BBS:DOORS/MasterDoors/MasterLogon/\n	Masterlogon		Da door\n\n* BBS:Doors/MasterDoors/MasterLogon/\n	Normal.TXT		Config for NORMAL logon\n\n* BBS:Doors/MasterDoors/MasterLogon/\n	Shortened.TXT		Config for SHORTENED logon\n\n* BBS:DOORS/MasterDoors/MasterLogon/\n	Quick.TXT		Config for QUICK logon\n\n* BBS:\n	MLogon.DOC		Some shit.\n\n\nRequirements:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nPC586 200MHZ on your 10th birthday!\n33k6 Modem on your 11th birthday!\nFUCK OFF!!!!!!!!!!!!!!\n\nRealy needed:\n\nPURE AMIGA POWER!\nAMIEXPRESS\n\n\nInstallation:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nJust put the Info in SYSCmd.\nCopy all other things to DOORS:MasterDoors/MasterLogon/\nEdit the files for your logon. Example:\n~SS_BULLETINS:XZN.TXT|~SP|~SS_BULLETINS:BULL2.TXT|~SP|~CC_WALL|~CC_WEEK|~SP\nThis is my Normal Logon.\nIt''s not hard.. Give it a try.. ;))\nEdit the files Normal, Shortened, Quick after your own mind.\n\n\nCopyright:\n~~~~~~~~~~\n\nIf u use this doors. Please call my board:\n\nDiFFERENt dREAMs +46-33-412-990\n\n\nBugreports:\n~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nFirst realese. No bugs known. If u notice one. Please contact me.\n\n\nGreeting time:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n                   Aeroba - bOiNG - GUffAW - zUG - a!DS\n               bELZEbUb - sTORM - ORCHiS - StRiDER - rACOON\n         Neptune - iCE - rATmAN - rEtARd - fISh - VAldi - Avenger\n          lEOpARd - Executor - _VoDkA_ - Infant - creon - MATHEWS\n                  _eCs_ - Louie - nEWT - ORiGO - typhoon\n                  And to all scneers all over the world!\n\nGreater greetz to:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\n                 m7g^FLW - Thanx for your coding help man!\n\n                    X-ZoNe cREW - You are the greatest!\n\n\nDisclaimer:\n~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nI take NO response if u use this door. But it will work nice. No Backdoors\nor shit like that. I use all my doors by myself. And nothing has happend. ;)\n\nWhats X-ZoNe?\n~~~~~~~~~~~~~\n\nA nice amiga group! Wanna join!?\nWe still need some demo coders!!\nCu all at Tp!\n\n\nJust call:\n\n\n        __________________________________________________   _______\n     _._)                                                `---''     (_._\n      |                                                              |\n   ____    ___    _____________________ ______   ________  ____    ____\n   \___\  (__/_  /      /      \_     / \____ \  \_     / / _\ \  /   /_\n  /  |/ \/     \/  /___/  /___/ /____/_/   _/  \/ /____/_/   \\ \/  ___/_\n_/   /  /      /   __//   __//  __/_  /    \   /  __/_   \_   \  \_  \   \_\n\_______\______\___/  \___/  \________\_____\  \__________/____\__/_______/\n      .                                      \__/                    .-d!\n      : _______   _______   __________ _______    __  __    _______  :\n      | \_____ \  \____  \  \_       / \____  \  /  \/  \  /  ____/  |\n      ./    |/  \/   _/   \/ /______/_/   _/   \/        \_\______ \ :\n     _/     /   /    \    /   __/_   /    \    /    \/    \_     /  \_\n     \__________\_____\   \__________\_____\___\____/______/_________/\n      .     __   __    \___/                                         .\n      :    /\_\ /\_\      sTAFF: ZAblER^XZN - PAiN^FLW - m7g^FLW     :\n      :    \/_// / /          rUNNiNG /X 4.9 oN a12oo/6/1.3Gb        :\n     _!_       \/_/\                 +46-33-412-990                 _!_\n        )___________\\_____________________________________________(\n                     \\\n                       \\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,10948,5,0,NULL,NULL,'xzn_lgon_masterlogon','scan',1780048843);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('y_cu04','Y-CU04.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/Y-CU04.LHA','CheckUP','XIM','CheckUP',NULL,'Hi-TeCH/YoNI',NULL,'|       CheckUP v0.4 by Hi-TeCH/YoNI       | |       ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~       ! ! The ultimate Upload-Checker for all you  |',replace('o- -- --- ---- ----- ------ ------- - - - -o\n|       CheckUP v0.4 by Hi-TeCH/YoNI       |\n|       ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~       !\n! The ultimate Upload-Checker for all you  |\n|  sysops out there! Also a YONI-first!!!! !\n!      For /X, Daydream, S!X, ZX etc...    |\n|        Ofcourse fully documented.        |\nO- - - - - ------ ----- ---- --- -- - - - -O\n','\n',char(10)),'CheckUP.doc',replace('\n                               CheckUP v0.4\n                               ============\n\nRequirements:\n=============\n-       Amiga OS2.04 or better.\n-       A running Rexxmast.\n-       Any BBS system which uses logoffscripts.\n-       512kb of memory (not much).\n-       rexxsupport.library in your LIBS:\n\n\nIs this for free ???\n====================\nSure it is! Ofcourse if you want to you can write me a note on my BBS\nto say you like it (or not), so it makes my ego feel good.\n\n\nWhat is this for ???\n====================\nThis is actually a very simple gadget! It''s used for checking if there\nare files in a certain directory (mostly the upload-directory of a BBS)\nand based upon the result it will run a certain scriptfile.\nI use this in my logoffscript of /X, but ofcourse you can also use this\non other BBS programmes too, I guess.\n\n\nSyntaxis:\n=========\nCheckUP <uldir> <ulscript> <noscript> [W] [M] [Mdir]\n\n<uldir>    :    Pathname (Must end with ":" or "/") to search for Files.\n                (for example: -> bbs:amiga/uploads/ <-)\n\n<ulscript> :    Scriptfile which will be run when there are found files\n                in the selected <Uldir>.\n                (for example: -> bbs:node1/logoff.uploads <-)\n\n<noscript> :    Scriptfile which will be run when there are not found\n                any files in the selected <Uldir>.\n                (for example: -> bbs:node1/logoff.none <-)\n\n[W]        :    If you use this optional flag, the scriptfiles will be run\n                in an open window. This way you can see the output of all\n                tools you run in your script. BUT, the Node will go online\n                immediately when the script is being started. If you leave\n                this option out, the scripts will just be executed like any\n                normal logoffscript and the node will be held busy while\n                doing so.\n\n[M]        :    If you use this optional flag, all files in the <uldir> will\n                be moved to [Mdir]. BUT (!!!), this will only work when\n                you DON''T use the [W]-flag.\n\n[Mdir]     :    Pathname to where all files in the <uldir> will be moved\n                after either the <ulscript> or <noscript> has been run.\n\nN.B.\n----    You don''t NEED to use the optional flags, they''re just here for those\n        who feel like they need it.\n\n\n\nExamples:\n=========\n\nCheckUP U: BBS:logoff.uploads BBS:logoff.none M U2:\n\nCheckUP U: BBS:logoff.uploads BBS:logoff.none W\n\nCheckUP U: BBS:logoff.uploads BBS:logoff.none\n\n\n\nIMPORTANT!!!\n============\nSince this tool checks a certain <uldir>, it is mandatory that you move the\nuploaded files after each RUN of CheckUP to a secundary directory so the\n<uldir> will be empty each time a user logs on to your BBS.\nYou can do this yourself by adding a simple line to your <ulscript> like:\nmove dir1:#? dir2:\n(Where ''dir1'' and ''dir2'' are the directory names, any fool can see that*8).)\nYou can also let CheckUP do the work if you want, but only when you don''t use\nthe [W]-flag.\n\nIf you enter ''CheckUP ?'' it will show you a full description of the syntaxis\nto use.\n\n\n            CheckUP was coded by Hi-TeCH / Jetset^NO^Barf!^Yoni\n               Dox written by Hi-TeCH / Jetset^NO^Barf!^Yoni\n\nContact me on these *REAL* Yoni-Boards:\n                         ___________________   _________              \n       «««««------------/    ___  \__   .   \--\____  _/----- --- -- -\n                       /__    \___//    |___ \____/   \               \n                        _/     \__/    ____/  \_ /     \_             \n                        \_______/\______|______/________/             \n          _____    /\ __________ ______._____________    _____.       \n          \__  \  /  \\__   .   \\__   |   ____  .   \   \_   |       \n       - --/  \ \/ /  \/    |___ \/    .   \/    |___ \---/   |----»»»\n         _/    \  /    \_  ____/  \_   |    \_  ____/  \_/  __/¯¯¯|   \n         \______\/______/___|______/___|_____/___|_____|__________|\n                                                               \n                               rEiNCARNATED\n \n \n              Jetset WHQ ^ New Order HQ ^ Official Yoni-Site\n \n       «««««------------------------------------------------- --- -- -\n                 Maharadja''s : Hi-TeCH , SeMTeX , DJ HoPPA\n       - -- --- -------------------------------------------------»»»»»\n \n                  tERUG vAN wEG gEWEEST -> t''IS fEEST!!!!\n \n                              +31-162-322-716\n\n\n          /   /                                  _________             /   /  \n  _______/___/____ ________ ________ _____  _____\F@nK!  /________ ___/___/__\n |       |    |_  |        |______  |     \/    | \_____/|        |  ___    /\n |__  |  |_____/  |__  |   |  ___   |           |_       |___   __|  \_____/   \n   ''-------''--------''--|---''--------''''---\__/----''---------''-----`---------   \n     /   / __________                                             /   /       \n   _/___/__\     ___/______ _________ _________ _______ _________/ __/________\n  |       | \____|    _____|________ |    _____|       |    ____  |    ___   /\n  |__  |  |__    |_______  |   ____  |_______  |___   _|__  \_____|__ |  ___/\n /  ''------''-------`----/--`-----------`----/----''----/  ''----------''-|-----`\n/   /                                                        /   /\n******************************************************************************\n            Online since 22-01-96 at 22:22:22 Together with TAJ MAHAL           \n                                                                              \n           NEW ORDER - DIST SITE ; A BIZARRE - INFO SITE ; YONI - SITE\n                                                                              \n24Hrs*A1200*SYSOP*SeMTeX*COSYSOPS*HI-TECH*ANDABATA*DAIL*0765134991*ANDGETALIFE\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',85872,3,0,NULL,NULL,'y_cu04','scan',1780048843);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('y_tw00i','Y-TW00I.LZX','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/Y-TW00I.LZX',NULL,'XIM','y tw00i',NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,NULL,8951,0,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048843);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ydl_cd01','YDL-CD01.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/YDL-CD01.LHA','cdrom','XIM','cdrom','0.1','WiLD','YDL','|    ______                     _ __ ____  | ¦    \_   /_________________________\\_ ¬\ : :    /   / ¬\_  _  ¬\____  ¬\_ ___ ¬\/   / ¦',replace('+--[ CD-ROM v0.1    by WiLD THiNG/YoDeL ]--+\n|    ______                     _ __ ____  |\n¦    \_   /_________________________\\_ ¬\ :\n:    /   / ¬\_  _  ¬\____  ¬\_ ___ ¬\/   / ¦\n¦   /   /  _/   /  _/   /  _/  \____/   /  |\n|  _\___   \_______\_______\_______\___/   |\n+--\______/--------------------------------+\n| PReZeNTZ FRoM Da FaMouS WiLDTooLZ SeRieS |\n:        aN /X 3.x & 4.x XIM DooR          :\n¦        CD-ROM v0.1   (07/12/94)          ¦\n|          online CD-ROM server            |\n+------------------------------------------+\n','\n',char(10)),'CD-ROM.DOC',replace('                      [---> -P- ¥·O·Ð·E·L -P- <---]\n                              presents the\n     ____  ____  ___ __ _______ _____________________   _____________\n    /    /\    \/   \  :       \        /     :      : /    /       /\n   //           \___/  :___     \   ___/ ____ : ____ :/    /___    /____\n   \            /   \      \ /  /    /:       :      :        /   /    /\n    \____/\____/\___/______/___/____/ :_______:______:_______/________/\n                                 SeRieS\n   +==================================================================+\n   :                    WiLD THiNG''s CD-ROM Server                    :\n   :                 (c) 12/94 by WiLD THiNG/YoDeL                    :\n   +==================================================================+\n\nThis  is  an  /X  XIM  door,  written in Amiga E for best speed results, it\nrequires the AEDOOR.LIBRARY by Sintax/WoT (included).\n\nWhat  does  it  ?  Well this door makes it possible to access CD-ROM''s from\n/X.\n\nInstallation: \ncreate this dirs:         \n                        doors:wildtools/\n                        doors:wildtools/CD-ROM/\n                        doors:wildtools/CD-ROM/CD-DATA/\n\ncopy  the file CDROM to doors:wildtools/CD-ROM/ and create and icon for it.\nNow  You  must  create  some data files concerning the CD-ROM''s You want to\nuse:  create for each CD-ROM a directory with the name of the CD-ROM (e.g.:\ndoors:wildtools/CD-ROM/CD-DATA/AMINET_0794/  for  Aminet  3 (AMINET_0794 is\nthe volume name of it))\n\nnow You need to create two files:       - paths\n                                        - names\nnames will contain the names of the directories and paths will contain the\nfull path to the dirs so an example:\nYou have a CD with the volume name PICS:\nwrite in the names file:\nRAY_TRACING\nX-RATED\nCLIPARTS\n\nin the paths file you must write then:\nPICS:RAYTRACING\nPICS:X-RATED\nPICS:CLIPARTS\n\nthe  names must fit to the path files, now you need to create filelists for\nthe dirs, name them EXACTLY as the dir-names:\n\nRAY_TRACING     <- contains the filelist for ray tracing pics\nX-RATED         <-    "      "     "      "  x-rated pics\nCLIPARTS        <-    "      "     "      "  cliparts\nand so on....\n\nIncluded in this arc is the complete setup for the Aminet 3 CD.\n\nOh  yes,  I  forgot,  the CD is supposed to be in CD0:  (have a look at the\nplanned improvements below)\n\nIf  ye  got  any questions or suggestions drop a mail to me (WiLD THiNG) at\nthese boards:\n\n        Dixie           +48-71-575825\n        Boondocks       +31-ASKFORIT\n        Edge of Sanity  +46-346-81852\n\n\nPLANNED IMPROVEMENTS:   - selectable device names for CD-ROMs\n                        - multiple CD-ROM support\n                        - filetagging by numba\n                        - viewing of arc''s\n\nand  anything  YOU  suggest,  by  the  way  if  there''s anybody who has got\nmultiple  CD-ROM''s,  pleeze contact me, coz I don''t have the possibility to\ncheck this feature.\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',112753,6,0,NULL,NULL,'ydl_cd01','scan',1780048843);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ydl_cd02','YDL-CD02.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/YDL-CD02.LHA','cdlist','XIM','+--[ WiLD HeLP by WiLD THiNG/YoDeL ]--+','0.2','WiLD','YDL','|    ______  /X >3.x XiM DooR   _ __ ____  | ¦    \_   /_________________________\\_ ¬\ : :    /   / ¬\_  _  ¬\____  ¬\_ ___ ¬\/   / ¦',replace('+--[ WiLD HeLP v0.2 by WiLD THiNG/YoDeL ]--+\n|    ______  /X >3.x XiM DooR   _ __ ____  |\n¦    \_   /_________________________\\_ ¬\ :\n:    /   / ¬\_  _  ¬\____  ¬\_ ___ ¬\/   / ¦\n¦   /   /  _/   /  _/   /  _/  \____/   /  |\n|  _\___   \_______\_______\_______\___/   |\n+--\______/--------------------------------+\n| PReZeNTZ FRoM Da FaMouS WiLDTooLZ SeRieS |\n¦        CD-ROM v0.2   (10/12/94)          ¦\n:    Removable Media FileBase Handler      :\n|       supports CDs, SyQuests etc         |\n+------------------------------------------+\n','\n',char(10)),'CD-ROM.DOC',replace('                      [---> -P- ¥·O·Ð·E·L -P- <---]\n                              presents the\n     ____  ____  ___ __ _______ _____________________   _____________\n    /    /\    \/   \  :       \        /     :      : /    /       /\n   //           \___/  :___     \   ___/ ____ : ____ :/    /___    /____\n   \            /   \      \ /  /    /:       :      :        /   /    /\n    \____/\____/\___/______/___/____/ :_______:______:_______/________/\n                                 SeRieS\n   +==================================================================+\n   :                  WiLD THiNG''s CD-ROM Server v0.2                 :\n   :                   (c) 12/94 by WiLD THiNG/YoDeL                  :\n   +==================================================================+\n\n                            -=- DISCLAIMER -=-\nTHIS DOOR IS CALL-WARE, IF YOU USE IT, CALL MY BOARD (SEE BELOW FOR NUMBA)\n                                -=-  +  -=-\n\nHell,  it''s  the  10th  of December, 02:56 am and I have birthday and don''t\nhave anything better to do than to write this stupid docs, by the way, does\nanybody read this shit ?\n\nThis  is  an  /X  XIM  door,  written in Amiga E for best speed results, it\nrequires the AEDOOR.LIBRARY by Sintax/WoT (included).\n\nWhat  does  it  ?  Well this door makes it possible to access CD-ROM''s from\n/X.\n\nREQUIREMENTS: any Amiga, some RAM (if using indexed CD''s it''ll be lots more\n              coz those are read to mem in whole), Kick >2.x, a CD-ROM\n              would be useful, thou You can use this also to access any\n              removable media, some net shit etc, to say it clear, any\n              media that is not always available or to build more complex \n              filebases.\n\n- Thou  any  removable  media is supported it is not further mentioned below,\n  but the usage for CDs or other removable media is the same.\n- Files are NOT buffered but sent directly from their paths\n- automatic detection of medium inserted in drive\n- I forgot something, I know it, w8 for the next update \n\nCD-TYPES:   There  are  to  possibilities  to handle CD''s, the one way is a\nnormal  CD  as  the AmiNet ones (look at the example) where the files for a\nDIR  are  in  the path defined by the paths file or indexed files, then You\nhave to create an index file with the full paths to all files that shall be\naccessible  on  a CD (useful for Fish CD''s or CD''s where there''s other junk\nor just for a clearer outlook)\nNOTE: The index files should begin with a CR, otherwise the first file will\n      never be found.\n\nInstallation: \ncreate this dirs:         \n                        doors:wildtools/\n                        doors:wildtools/CD-ROM/\n                        doors:wildtools/CD-ROM/CD-DATA/\n\ncopy  the file CDROM to doors:wildtools/CD-ROM/ and create and icon for it.\nNow  You  must  create  some data files concerning the CD-ROM''s You want to\nuse:  create for each CD-ROM a directory with the volume-name of the CD-ROM\n(e.g.:     doors:wildtools/CD-ROM/CD-DATA/AMINET_0794/    for    Aminet   3\n(AMINET_0794 is the volume name of it))\n\nnow You need to create two files:       - paths (not for indexed CD''s)\n                                        - names\nnames will contain the names of the directories and paths will contain the\nfull path to the dirs so an example:\nYou have a CD with the volume name PICS:\nwrite in the names file:\nRAY_TRACING\nX-RATED\nCLIPARTS\n\nin the paths file you must write then:\n(NOTE: no paths file is needed when using an file-index)\nPICS:RAYTRACING\nPICS:X-RATED\nPICS:CLIPARTS\n\nthe  names must fit to the path files, now you need to create filelists for\nthe dirs, name them EXACTLY as the dir-names:\n\nRAY_TRACING     <- contains the filelist for ray tracing pics\nX-RATED         <-    "      "     "      "  x-rated pics\nCLIPARTS        <-    "      "     "      "  cliparts\nand so on....\n\nIncluded  in  this arc is the complete setup for the Aminet 3 CD, Pandora''s\nCD (as example for a normal CD) and for FrozenFish-Apr94 (as example for an\nindexed CD).\n\nTOOLTYPES: edit the tooltypes in doors:wildtools/cd-rom/cdrom.info\n\nTYPE.NAME       If this is set to INDEX, an index file will be used for\n                finding the file paths, eg.: TYPE.FrozenFish-Apr94=INDEX,\n                if you want a normal NOT indexed CD just leave this out.\n                No paths file is needed when u use an index.\n\nINDEX.NAME      This contains the full path to the index-file,\n                e.g.:\n        INDEX.FrozenFish-Apr94=wt:cd-rom/cd-data/frozenfish-apr94/INDEX\n\nCD.X            device names of the CD-ROM''s, the number of CD-ROM''s\n                supported has no logical limits (wanna say it''s only \n                limited by Your mem)\n                e.g.:   CD.1=CD0:\n                        CD.2=CD1:\n                        CD.3=SYQ:\n                (This makes it also possible to use CD-ROM via nets like\n                 ParNet or someting similar, to do this assign the \n                 full path thru the net to anything You want and put this\n                 in here)\n                 \nThere are also two utils included:\n                                 -CDLIST-\nSYNTAX: CDLIST DEVICENAME\nDEVICENAME  is  the volume-name without colon (:), after creating the PATHS\nand  the  NAMES  files  You  can  run this util to automatically create all\nfilelists  with  filenames and sizes of the files, but without descriptions\nofcoz.\ne.g.: CDLIST AMINET_0794\n\n                                -MAKEINDEX-\nSYNTAX: MAKEINDEX DEVICENAME\nMAKEINDEX  is  a script file which creates an file-index file for a CD-ROM.\nDEVICENAME  is the volume-name of the CD.  The index file will be placed in\nthe data dir for the CD (the dir must exist).\ne.g.: MAKEINDEX AMINET_0794\n\nIf  ye  got  any questions or suggestions drop a mail to me (WiLD THiNG) at\nthese boards:\n\n        Dixie           +48-71-575825   <- my board, fastest answers\n        Boondocks       +31-ASKFORIT\n        Edge of Sanity  +46-346-81852\n\n\nPLANNED IMPROVEMENTS:   - byte/file accounting\n                        - filetagging by numba\n                        - viewing of arc''s\n                        - anything  YOU  suggest\n\n             :::::::::::::::::::::HISTORY:::::::::::::::::::::\nv0.1 06-12-94   - first version\n\nv0.2 09-12-94   - Index file support -> any CD is useable \n                - fast search option added\n                - added the two utils for creating indexes, filelists\n\n     10-12-94   - multi-CD support added\n             :::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::::\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,304643,4,0,NULL,NULL,NULL,'scan',1780048843);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ydl_lc05','YDL-LC05.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/YDL-LC05.LHA','wlast','XIM','wlast','0.5',NULL,'YDL','¦_ _______               ___          _____¦ \\__   /______________|_  |________|   | /   /  \    _  \   __///______   /   |',replace('+--[  yODEl pREzENTz : lASt cALLEr v0.5 ]--+\n¦_ _______               ___          _____¦\n  \\__   /______________|_  |________|   | \n    /   /  \    _  \   __///______   /   |  \n.--/   /|   \   \   \   \   |   /___/.   |-.\n| /______   |\______/\______|\____   |___| |\n|       |___|      pReSeNTz      |___|     |\n| __/\__       WiLD Last v0.5b             |\n| \ oO /     aN /X > 2.x XiM uTIl          |\n`-/_\/_\-. fASTeSt & bESt lASTcALlEr  .----''\n    \/   `----------------------------'' >vNZ\n','\n',char(10)),'Wildlast.doc',replace('                      [---> -P- ¥·O·Ð·E·L -P- <---]\n                              presents the\n     ____  ____  ___ __ _______ _____________________   _____________\n    /    /\    \/   \  :       \        /     :      : /    /       /\n   //           \___/  :___     \   ___/ ____ : ____ :/    /___    /____\n   \            /   \      \ /  /    /:       :      :        /   /    /\n    \____/\____/\___/______/___/____/ :_______:______:_______/________/\n                                 SeRieS\n\n     - --÷======================================================÷-- -\n                              WiLD Last v0.5b\n                        (c) ''95 by WiLD THiNG^yODEl\n     - --÷======================================================÷-- -\n             cODe: WiLD THiNG^yODEl        dEZIGn: Vinzi^yODEl\n     - --÷======================================================÷-- -\n\nWhat shall I write ?  Dunno, just wanted to write down the history before I\nforget it, shit, v0.4 contained a little bug which caused random crashes.\n\na Yes, WiLDlASt i an util which creates an bull with the last x callers,\ncommand line template is:\n\nNODE/N,CALLERS/N,FILENAME/A\n |        |        |\n |        |        +----------------- full path for bulletin        \n |        +-------------------------- number of callers to be in the bull\n +----------------------------------- node number to process\n\n\nSo  why is it the fastest around You''ll ask, well Wlast doesn''t read & scan\nthe  whole  filelist,  it  just  scans  as much as is needed, so u can have\nfilelists  of  5MB and it''ll be the same fast as on a filelist of 10k.  The\nother point is that it''s written in AmigaE.\n\nPut the bulletin wherever u like, eg to BULL.TXT, use\n~SS_<filename>\n\n     - --÷======================================================÷-- -\n                       F - E - A - T - U - R - E - S\n     - --÷======================================================÷-- -\n- it''s fast\n- it looks great\n\n\n     - --÷======================================================÷-- -\n                        H - I - S - T  - O - R - Y\n     - --÷======================================================÷-- -\n\nv0.3                    complete new dezign by Vinzi^yODEl (yEAh)\nv0.4                    Data handling/storing changed/rewritten\nv0.4b   31-01-95 beta   Bugfixes\nv0.5    01-02-95 beta   now reads only last 35k of the callerslog for \n                        better speed\nv0.5b   04-02-95 beta   was wondering  why there  were crashes, though it\n                        wlast  didn''t hang itself it caused the system to \n                        be "damaged", fixed  that, ouch it hurts to write\n                        some  data  somewhere  into  mem where it doesn''t\n                        belong\n        28-02-95        PUBLIC RELEASE\n\n\n                 ----÷÷÷÷::::::::fUTURe::::::::÷÷÷÷÷÷----\n- records by month/eternal \n- weekly stats\n- sum more thingys\n\n\n                        -----÷ gREETz gO tO ÷-----\n               ÷ Aquarius/OTL  ÷  Sebax/OBS  ÷  ToYo/Fate ÷\n         ÷ Sal-One/TRSi etc. ÷  ByteAndi/TRSi ÷ J-23 ÷ Yasiu/OBS ÷\n       ÷ Easy Rider/TRSi & MST ÷ UFoK/MST  ÷  Dalamar ÷ GOT & GRYC ÷ \n    ÷ Franklin ÷ Dansken  ÷ Vinzi/yDL ÷  Skrubier/YDL  ÷ AmigaSpirit ÷ \n  ÷ Demonic  ÷  Zielu ÷ Fenix  ÷  tHe Mask/DD Style  ÷ Citruz/DD Style ÷\n    ÷ Bionic/yDL ÷ Rabocost ÷  Damage ÷  Halloween ÷  The Trader/Fear ÷\n         ÷ Kula ÷ Ziutek ÷ R19 ÷ Krasnal ÷ Artie/TAU ÷ CatEye/INS\n           ---------÷ gROUP gREETz & aCKNoLeDGMENTS  ÷---------\n             ÷ aLL fORMEr TAURUS MEMBERS ÷ Mannassas ÷ Yodel ÷\n               ÷ TRSi /X Innovation ÷ MST /X Dezign ÷ DAF ÷\n                            ÷ Fear ÷ Outlaws ÷ \n\n\n\n- Y O D E L  I Z  A  M E M B E R  O F  D A F - dEMOgROUPs aGAINSt fASCISM -\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',37105,6,0,NULL,NULL,'ydl_lc05','scan',1780048843);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ydl_mens','YDL-MENS.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/YDL-MENS.LHA','cmg','XIM','cmg',NULL,'WT','YDL','|    YoDeL BriNGZ yOU tODaY [02-01-95     | :       fRoM tHE WiLDTooLZ sERiES         : : A set of utils to create custom menus   :',replace('+-[ The Complete Menu creation set by WT ]+\n|    YoDeL BriNGZ yOU tODaY [02-01-95     |\n:       fRoM tHE WiLDTooLZ sERiES         :\n: A set of utils to create custom menus   :\n: CONTAINS: Custom Menu Generator v0.1    :\n:           COMLIST v0.1 : /X util        :\n|           WiLDMenus II v0.1: /X XIM     |\n+-----------------------------------------+\n','\n',char(10)),'CMG.DOC',replace('                                                                    _\n          ¡                                                      _(_)_\n      - --O---- - .-                                          . (_(_)_)\n          |  _____|\_________________________________________/|   (_)\n          |  \_   |   __     ____________   __     ______     |____!_ _\n          |  /    |   ¬\     |   ¬\     |   ¬\     __) ¬\     |   ¬\\\\\n          ! /     |     \    |     \    |     \    |     \    |     \\n        _ _ \______      \___       \___       \___       \___       \\n        ////_____________/   \______/   \______/   \______/   \______/\n                       [---> -P- ¥·O·Ð·E·L -P- <---]                                                                  :\n\n                              presents the\n     ____  ____  ___ __ _______ _____________________   _____________\n    /    /\    \/   \  :       \        /     :      : /    /       /\n   //           \___/  :___     \   ___/ ____ : ____ :/    /___    /____\n   \            /   \      \ /  /    /:       :      :        /   /    /\n    \____/\____/\___/______/___/____/ :_______:______:_______/________/\n                                 SeRieS\n   +==================================================================+\n   :              WiLD THiNG''s Custom Menu Generator v0.1             :\n   :                   (c) 12/94 by WiLD THiNG/YoDeL                  :\n   +==================================================================+\n\n                            -=- DISCLAIMER -=-\nTHIS UTIL IS CALL-WARE, IF YOU USE IT, CALL MY BOARD (SEE BELOW FOR NUMBA)\n                                -=-  +  -=-\n\n\n\n                           -=- INTRODUCTION -=-\n\nCMG is an util to create custom ANSI menus. They are maybe not very pretty\nbut quickly created and easy to overview. The use is easy:\n\nCreate a source file which has to look like that:\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=- CuT HeRe -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n; CMG source for MENU.MAIL\n\n                         [36m<-[34m[ [33mM A I L [34m-[33m M E N U [34m][36m->[0m\n\n~E  [000] Enter message\n~R  [000] Read message\n~C  [000] Comment to Sysop\n~EA [200] Enter Anonymous\n~UM [000] U/L message\n~Q  [010] Quick Message Scan\n\n~ZOOM [100] QWK download\n~SQWK [100] QWK upload\n\n-=-=-=-=-=-=-=- CuT HeRe -=-=-=-=-=-=-=-\n\nJust  type  ~  and the name of the command, then in brackets [,] the access\nlevel  and  after  that  the  description.  The menus will be output in two\ncolumns, enter comments with a colon (;) at the beginning of the line.\nAny other line will be put to the menu file as is.\n\nSYNTAX: CMG SOURCE DESTINATION ACCESSLEVEL\n               \nSOURCE: name of the source file\n\nDESTINATION: name of the menu file to be created\n\nACCESSLEVEL: the menu file will include commands equal or below this one\n\n              \nIf  ye  got  any  questions  or  suggestions  or  if  U  want  to  become a\nbeta-tester, drop a mail to me (WiLD THiNG) at these boards:\n\n        Dixie           +48-71-575825   <- my board, fastest answers\n        Boondocks       +31-ASKFORIT\n        Edge of Sanity  +46-346-81852\n\n\n                  ___,,,____\n             _,-æÆNÆN®#MNÆWØÐ-,,                   ........................\n          _gÑMN®#MØ**¤¤²¢**WÑÆNÆNm,_         ....  :                    :::\n        _æÑÆWW¤°"           ¯¨°¢MWØW,_       :  :..:                    :::\n      _ÆØØØØ~                   ¯°#ÑÆN_  . ..:                          :::\n     aNÆWØÑ®#_¸qm   ææææææææææææææj°#MN#,                               :::\n    ÁNÆW¹¯¢ØØØW_°   Ñ®MWÑÆN®MN®###1 ¬0MWØ_          ¸®ÑW                :::\n   ÁNÆN´   ,\®###,  ###MNÆNÆN®MN®M]   ¶ÑÆW   __,,   ®WØF   mEMBER oF    .·:\n  ,ØØÑF    ®ð_\WØÑÆ,°0®#MP°°°°°°°°"    #WÑ#  °ÆWØØ_JÑ®Ø     __            ·\n  Ø##M     WØØQ¬¢®#MN,°0MQ________¸    `®MW   0ØÑ¯¢N®#¹     ¬¤0æ,_   ,æøø>\n  ÑÆNF     ÆWØÑ®À¬¢®MNÆ­¨4WÑ®MNÆWØÍ     Ñ®#1   MNÐ MN®  ææøææ­ÆÑÆV  ®®#/°ÑÐ\n  NÆN1     ÆN®MN®#b,¢####_°¶Ñ®#MWØÍ     ØÑ®I   `®#L#MN  0ÆN  Æ®#@ ²dMW# ..\n  #ØØ#     *********ð,¢N®MN,~4Ñ®##I     WØØ¹    ¶ØÑÆWÑ   #ÆÐJØØØ   ØÑ®À, ·:\n  ¶MNÆ              N®þ,°®MWØ_°4##1    óMWÑ      ÆWØÑÆ    WØÑ®M''  d#M@°°´.:\n   ®MWÀ    øææøæøæød®MNÆþ,¢MNÆN_°0]   ,ÑÆNF      0®#ÑW    0##MN   ÆNÆ   :::\n   ¬Ñ®#þ   WÑÆWÑÆWØØÑ®MN®I  \WÑÆW\"  ,ØØÑ@        °°''     ÌÆWØV  ÆÑ®P   :::\n    ¯WØÑ&_ WÑÆN®#MWÑ®MWÑ®1   _¹®MWÑ_,®MWP  dEMOGROUPS      ¤²¤³  WÑÆ    :::\n     ¬0WØÑö¬~¨~¬¨~¨~¨~¨"~"   ¨  ¢®#MN®M/                        jWÑM    :::\n       °W®##æ__                __Æ#MNP              aGAiNST     0MN¹    :::\n         °0ÆN®#h­_,________,-øÑ®MNÑ¤´                                   :::\n           ¬°*ØWØØØÑÆN®MNÆWÑÆWØ@³¨           ....         fASCiSM!!!    :::\n               "°°^²²***»¤²^°"      . .....  :  :                       :::\n                                          :..:  :  .....................:::\n                                                :..:   \n-> ZonderLamando or similar group members aRe NoT aLLoWeD To uZe THiZ Door <-\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',54797,6,0,NULL,NULL,'ydl_mens','scan',1780048843);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ydl_mu10','YDL-MU10.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/YDL-MU10.LHA','multi','XIM','+---[ yODEl pREzENTz : WiLD MuLTi ]---+','1.0',NULL,'YDL','¦_ _______               ___          _____¦ \\__   /______________|_  |________|   | /   /  \    _  \   __///______   /   |',replace('+---[ yODEl pREzENTz : WiLD MuLTi v1.0 ]---+\n¦_ _______               ___          _____¦  \n  \\__   /______________|_  |________|   |  \n    /   /  \    _  \   __///______   /   |  \n.--/   /|   \   \   \   \   |   /___/.   |-.\n| /______   |\______/\______|\____   |___| |\n|       |___|      pReSeNTz      |___|     |\n| WiLD MuLTi v1.0 - tHe bESt /X dUPe cHkEr |\n| - mULTi dOOR sTaRT  - aUTo fREe & mSG    |\n|  - qUiCKnEw  - fULLy cONFiGurable & mOre |\n`------------------------------------------''\n-[I pASSEd tHRU SoCiAL DiZeASE OTT USHQ ]-','\n',char(10)),'WiLDMuLTi.GUiDe',replace('@database WiLDMuLTi.guide\n\n@node MAIN "WiLD MuLTi DuPe v1.0 (c) 02/95  WiLD THiNG/YoDeL"\n                      [---> -P- ¥·O·Ð·E·L -P- <---]\n                              presents the\n     ____  ____  ___ __ _______ _____________________   _____________\n    /    /\    \/   \  :       \        /     :      : /    /       /\n   //           \___/  :___     \   ___/ ____ : ____ :/    /___    /____\n   \            /   \      \ /  /    /:       :      :        /   /    /\n    \____/\____/\___/______/___/____/ :_______:______:_______/________/\n                                 SeRieS\n   +==================================================================+\n   :                        WiLD MuLTi DuPe v1.0                      :\n   :                 (c) 02/95 by WiLD THiNG/YoDeL                    :\n   +==================================================================+\n   : cODe : WiLD THiNG^yODEl       dEZIGn : bIONIc & WiLD THiNG^yODEl :\n   +==================================================================+\n\n              @{" Introduction        " link "introduction"} @{" Greetings         " link "greets"}\n              @{" Installation        " link "installation"} @{" Contact           " link "contact"}\n              @{" Configuration       " link "config"} @{" History           " link "history"} \n              @{" Other WiLDTooLS     " link "tools"} \n\n\n           - READ THIZ DOCS BEFORE ASKING ME STUPID QUESTIONS -\n@endnode\n\n@node introduction "Introduction"\n\nWiLD  MuLTi  DuPe  is  a  LightningFast  Dupe  Checker, a MultiDoorStarter,\nAutoFree  maker  and  a  dirstyle clone all in one.  Sure all of these have\nalready been here, but not in one door and not this fast.\n\nFEATURES:       - SPEEEEEEEEED\n                - multidoor starter\n                - auto free of group releases\n                - config by conf\n                - checking of external dirs\n                - ONLINE creation of daily upload stats with files upped\n                  that day\n                - fully configurable by tooltypes\n                - adding of uploader, time & node info\n                - selectable upload dir checking\n                - daily upload statistics\n                - automatically writes messages to inform \n                  about group releases\n                - and many more...\n\nSOME  WORDS ''BOUT SPEED:  A dupe checker has to be fast, MuLTi DuPe iz damn\nfast, ofcoz it depends mosty on Your HD, coz reading a 500k filelist take a\nwhile,  the  searching  time  You  won''t  even notice (compared to the time\nrequired  to  read  it),  but  the  speed  will  be even improved in future\nreleases.\n\nThis  door  has been tested for several month on different systems, only on\nan  A4000/30  have  occurred  troubles  which  I couldn''t cope with yet, on\nothers like A2000/30, A1200, A500 ''030, A3000  etc no probs are known.\n\nTAKE MY WORD: NO WILDTOOLZ CONTAIN ANY BACKDOORS -> ONLY GAYS &\n              LAMERS MAKE IT FROM BEHIND :-)\n\n                have fun and a horny day\n                                         WiLD THiNG/YoDeL\n\n\nDISCLAIMER: THIS DOOR IS CALL-WARE, IF YOU USE CALL ONE THESE @{" BOARDS "\nlink "contact"} AND DROP ME A MAIL AND YOUR OPINION\n\n          >> DESTROY FASCISM ! FUN IS FUN NAZI''S ARE A PLAGUE <<\n@endnode\n\n@node history\n                 -======================================-\n                               H I S T O R Y\n                 -======================================-\n\n-VeR----ReL.DaTe-----------------------CHaNGeD/uPDaTeD--------------------\n 0.1    13/10/94 beta   First working version, only ßeta release\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\n 0.2    13/10/94 beta   Added Override Tooltype\n                        added capital option\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\n 0.3    15-10-94 beta   - added ANSI selection\n                        - fixed to more than 9 nodes\n                        - fixed bug in override routine\n                        - fixed ANSI chars\n                        - added CHECKUPLOAD tooltype\n                        - individual config for each conf\n                        (ALL BUGS FIXED IN THIS VERSION WERE \n                         REPORTED BY AQUARIUS/OUTLAWS)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\n 0.4    16-10-94 beta   - fixed bug in override routine\n                        - checks now if upload is private\n                        - forgot to free some mem -> fixed that\n                        - added checking of external dirs\n                        (BUGS/SUGGESTIONS BY AQUARIUS/OUTLAWS)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\n 0.5    16-10-94 beta   - removed some unneccesary tooltypes\n                        - changed the dezign a bit\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\n 0.6    17-10-94 beta   - again changed dezign -> now a progress bar\n                          is shown\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\n 0.7    09-11-94 beta   - once more a different dezign -> changed the \n                          progress bar\n                        - included showtext option\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\n 0.8    14-11-94 beta   - quicknew included\n        15-11-94 beta   - heavy memory optimization done:needs less memory\n                        - dezign of quicknew output improved\n                        - finally made dupe identification more secure\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\n 0.9    16-11-94 beta   - added ADDRESTRICTED option\n                          (sug. by Toyo/Fate)\n                        - new dezign for the quicknew bull by Vinzi/YoDeL\n                        - fixed that bug if no door was started that MDupe\n                          didn''t start the /X filechecking\n                          (Big Thanx to Aquarius/Outlaws)\n                        - fixed a bug with private file checking\n                          (when no dir was dupe check it was LUCK\n                           if the file was private or not, oooops)\n\n        18-11-94 beta   - now quicknew is possible by conf:\n                          added tooltypes: QUICKTITLE, QUICKDATA, QUICKFILES,\n                        - added HUGE option\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\n 0.10                   - minor bugfixes\n                        - LOCAL feature added\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\n 1.0                    - changed dezign, first public beta release \n        19-02-95        - added message option\n        28-02-95        - PUBLIC RELEASE\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node installation "Installation"\n\n                             _________________  \n                            |~ |___________| ~|\n                            |  |___________|  |\n                            |  |___________|  |\n                            |  |___________|  |\n                            |  |___________|  |\n                            |    _________    |\n                            |   |~_    ~| |   |\n                            |   || |    | |   |\n                            l   || |    | |   |\n                             \_,||_|____|_|___|\n\nFirst copy the AEDoor.library to Your libs:\n\nType COPY bbs/* all bbs: and the files are where they should be :-) it''s\nalmost installed, now there are only the tooltypes left:\n\nBETA NOTE: CREATE A DIR CALLED doors:wildtools/wildmulti/\n           COPY THE FILES multi#?  and copy FILECHECK.INFO\n           TO BBS:COMMANDS/SYSCMD\n           \n\n\nPlace the FILECHECK.INFO icon in bbs:commands/syscmd/           \nThe  executable  multi and the config files multiX.info should be placed in\ndoors:wildtools/wildmulti/\n\nNow @{" configure " link "config"} Multi Dupe to yer needs.\n@endnode\n\n@node config "CONFIGURATION"\n===========================================================================\n                                 TOOLTYPES\n===========================================================================\n\n                        @{" START.X & ASTART.X  " link startx}\n                        @{" FREE file options   " link free}\n                        @{" RESTRICTED files    " link restricted}\n                        @{" QUICKNEW options    " link quicknew}\n                        @{" SHOWTEXT            " link showtext}\n                        @{" EXTERNAL            " link external}\n                        @{" CHECKPRIVATE        " link checkprivate}\n                        @{" ADDINFO             " link addinfo}\n                        @{" OVERRIDE            " link override}\n                        @{" CAPITAL             " link capital}\n                        @{" ANSI                " link ansi}\n                        @{" HUGE                " link huge}\n                        @{" CHECKUPLOAD         " link checkupload}\n                        @{" auto-MESSAGE        " link automessage}\n\nYou  can have for each conf an individual configuration, for that create an\nicon   called   multiX.info,   where   X  is  the  conference  number(e.g.:\nmulti2.info for conference numba two), default config file for all confs if\nmultiX.info  doesn''t  exist  is  multi.info,  these icons must be placed in\ndoors:wildtools/wildmulti\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node automessage "Automatical messages"\n\nThis  option gives You the possibility to let MultiDupe automatically write\nand  EALL  message  to  inform the users about a group release.  To disable\nmessage writing just delete the MSGPATH tooltype.\n\n\nMSGPATH         path of the conference where the message should be written\ne.g.: MSGPATH=bbs:conf4/        <- DON''T FORGET THE SLASH \n\nMSG.X           Group identifier \ne.g.: MSG.1=YDL-\n      MSG.2=OBS-\n       .\n       .\n\nSUBJECT.X       Subject for the message when a release from group X is found,\ne.g.: SUBJECT.1=yODEl rELEASe\n      SUBJECT.2=oBSESSIOn reLEASe\n\n@endnode\n\n\n@node huge "HUGE"\n\nHUGE=filesize in KB, if the real filesize is bigger than the size You set\nhere file checking will be skipped, this is usefull if You are low on\nmemory coz files of sizes >2 or 3 megs MAY need quite a ot to check\n\ne.g.: HUGE=2048         <- files bigger than 2 megs won''t be fiechecked,\n                           they WILL be dupe checked and so on...\n\n@endnode\n\n@node addinfo "ADDINFO"\nADDINFO  :  If this is =YES then one line will be added with the user name,\nnode no, and upload time\ne.g.: ADDINFO=YES\n\nNOTE: IF ANSI is ON the info will contain ANSI chars if ANSI is OFF guess\nwhat happens :)\n@endnode\n\n@node override "OVERRIDE"\nOVERRIDE  :   Level  from  which on no dupe files will be moved, to disable\noverride set OVERRIDE=-1 OR remove this tooltype\ne.g.: OVERRIDE=200\n@endnode\n\n@node capital "CAPITAL"\nCAPITAL  :   let  /X  make  Your filenames uppercase (put the CAPITOL_FILES\ntooltype in your NodeX.info), then put CAPITAL=YES and the scanning will be\neven faster\ne.g.: CAPITAL=YES\n@endnode\n\n@node ansi "ANSI"\nANSI  :   IF this is off no ANSI characters will be added, to switch it off\nput ANSI=NO or remove this tooltype\ne.g.: ANSI=YES\n@endnode\n\n@node checkupload "CHECKUPLOAD"\nCHECKUPLOAD :  If CHECKUPLOAD = NO then dupechecking on upload dirs will be\nskipped,  DEFAULT  if  NO,  coz  if  a file is in the upload dir it will be\nprobably skipped anyway\nNOTE:   IF  CHECKUPLOAD=NO  and  there''s only one dir and no external dirs\n        have been defined dupechecking will be skipped at all\ne.g.: CHECKUPLOAD=NO\n@endnode\n\n@node checkprivate "CHECKPRIVATE"\nCHECKPRIVATE : If this set on yes, private files will also be filechecked,\ndefault is NO -> do not check private files.\ne.g.: CHECKPRIVATE=YES\n@endnode\n\n@node external "EXTERNAL.X"\nEXTERNAL.X  :   let''s  you  define  dirs  to be checked that are not in the\ncurrent  conference.   Number is unlimited (well it IS limited, but only by\nyour  memory).   Enter  the  full  path  to  the  dir to be checked.  e.g.:\nEXTERNAL.1=bbs:conf4/dir1\n@endnode \n\n@node showtext "SHOWTEXT"\nSHOWTEXT  :   show a text file after dupechecking etc & before filechecking\ne.g.:  SHOWTEXT=dh0:texts/bla.txt\n@endnode\n\n@NODE free "FREE files options"\nFREE.X  :  files starting with this will be free (make files beginning with\nYDL- free leech,eg:  YDL-WS06,LHA, YDL-3&4.LHA etc) The number of different\npossibilities is unlimited\ne.g.: FREE.1=YDL-\n\nFREESTR.X   :    String  to  be  displayed  if  there''s  a  free  file  eg:\nFREESTR.1=YoDeL  ReLeaSe,  so this will be displayed and the file made free\ndownload\n\nFREESTR :  String under the filedescription , may be up to 200 chars though\nthere  is  a nice default free string, if You leave this out a nice default\nstring will be added\ne.g.: FREESTR=<< FREE LEECH >>\n\n\nNOTE:  The info and free string adding WILL NOT BE ADDED to the filelist if\nthere  are  too  many lines in the description, this is sad, but /X somehow\ncuts them off :-(\n\nNOTE2:   If  You  are  using  ByteKillerhandler  or  something similar, the\nfilenote (FREE DOWNLOAD) will be overwriten by @ and the usernumber and the\nfiles won''t be free download anymore.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node restricted "ADDRESTRICTED"\nADDRESTRICTED : adds the filename to the file You defined by the tooltype\nFILESNOTALLOWED in the bbs:nodeX.info icon, so files will be skipped BEFORE\nuploading.\ne.g.: ADDRESTRICTED=YES\n@endnode\n\n\n@node startx "START.X & ATART.X"\nSTART.X  : name of module to be started, the number of these is unlimited,\nTHESE DOORS WILL NOT BE STARTED IF THE UPLOADED FILE IS A DUPE OR IF THE\nUPLOAD IS PRIVATE\ne.g.: START.1=CONFTOP\n\nASTART.X  :same  as  START.X  just that these doors will always be started,\neven  before the dupechecking (dont no what for anybody could need this but\nit was requested by Aquarius)\ne.g.: ASTART.1=DUNNOWHAT\n@endnode\n\n@node quicknew "Quicknew options"\nQUICKNEW :  creates a bulletin with the today uploaded filenames, kb, no of\nfiles and yesterdays no of files & kb, to disable remove this tooltype\ne.g.: QUICKNEW=bulletins:quicknew.txt\n\n            This ones have only effect if quicknew is enabled:\n\nQUICKDATA  :   full path to the global/conf quicknew data file, if you want\nto  have  quicknew  by  conf, enter another path/filename in the mutix.info\nicon\ne.g.: QUICKDATA=doors:wildtools/wildmuti/quickdata.12   \nIf You leave this tooltype out, a defaut one is used for all confs\n\nQUICKFILES  :  as above, just the path to the file where filenames of today\nuploaded files are stored, if left out a default path is used\ne.g.: QUICKFILE=doors:wildtools/wildmulti/quickfiles.12\n\nQUICKTITLE  :   defines  the title line for the bulletin, %s may be a place\nholder for the date\ne.g.: QUICKTITLE= AMIGA WAREZ <-> fReSH fiLeS fOR %s\nwill give     =>  AMIGA WAREZ <-> fReSH fiLeS fOR 11-11-94\n\nWith  the  possibility  of  having  a  config  for each conf You can create\nquicknew  files  for  only ONE conf, all confs together or just two or more\nconfs.\n@endnode\n\n\n\n\n                                           \n@node greets "Greetings & Fuckings"\n                 -======================================-\n                       Greetings go to(in no order)\n                 -======================================-\n\nREAL  BIG  THANKS  MUST  GO  TO AQUARIUS/OUTLAWS FOR HIS NEVER ENDING GREAT\nIDEAS,  TECHNICAL  SUPPORT  AND  HIS  BUG REPORTS, WHITHOUT WHICH THIS DOOR\nWOULDN''T BE WHAT IT IS.\n\nall   Ex-Mannassas   &  FeaR  members,  Tic.,  R19,  Dragon/Motion,  Vince,\nAndy/Motion,  Sunset, Donald/Motion, Vince, The Generat, Wild Child/Taurus,\nEaZy-E/Taurus,  Zielu/Mad  Elks, uNReaL/Surprise Prod., Easy Rider/Mystic &\nTRSi,uFoK/Mystic  EMPiRE/Mystic,  ByteAndi/TRSi,  Selz/Nova  Acies(?),  The\nTrader/FeaR,  Chipsi/Taurus,  SAL-ONE/TRSi,  Crazy  Squaw, Calypso/GOD, KC,\nC/\Te¥e/Insane, all my Beta-Testers, and all others I forgot ....\n                                    ____\n ___________________________________\  /________________________________\n(__________________________________ \\// _______________________________)     \n \_________________________________\ \/ /______________________________/\n                                   \\  //\n                                    \\//\n                                     \/\n              \nA BIG BIG THANX TO THIS DUDES FOR GIVING ME SUGGESTIONS/BUG REPORTS TO MY\nDOORS:\n\n- Aquarius/Outlaws              all of them\n- Vinzi/YoDeL                   WiLDWall,PeWeFail and all the dezigns\n- Bionic/YoDeL                  All of them :-)\n- Jarri/Union                   WiLDList & some others\n- Dansken/Hall Of Fame BBS      WiLDWall, WiLDStat\n- DPJSoft/Opus BBS              WiLDBBS\n- BOGGAN                        WiLDWall\n- Toyo/Fate                     Multi Dupe\n\n\n    ToYo : czesc maly ;)      \n        CiTRuZ : gonna call ye soooon\n           SAL-ONE/TRSi : hi, I''m workin'' on that styler\n      /\      Aquarius/OTL : thx for all yer help\n ____/  \____ Dalamar/LED  : g8 to be yer distro ;)\n \   /\/\   / Bionic/Yodel : yODEl mEETINg 95 at DiXiE BBS, u know ;)\n  \  \/\/  /  GOT/Termos   : hehe my top uploader :-)\n  /        \  Yodel        : hello bros... nice to be in YoDeL now\n /___ () ___\ SiNTAX/WøT   : ...your examples in E and your AEDoor.library\n     \  /  Wouter van Oortmerssen : ... Amiga E compiler, it''s the BEST\n      \/  Big C & Amiga   : ... the best toy for bored programmers ;-)\n\n        \n             Life is NOT to short... it''s just that you are DEAD for so long.\n        \n        \n@endnode\n\n@node contact "Contact me ..."\n\nCall  these  WiLDToolz Beta-Test and Release Sites for the newest WiLDToolz\nand to drop some suggestions or bug reports:\n\n- Country -------- Board Name ------ Board Numba ----- Write to -----------\n\n  Sweden           Edge Of Sanity    +46-346-81852     WiLD THiNG\n> Poland           Dixie             +48-71-575825     WiLD THiNG <\n  Sweden           Hall Of Fame      +46-910-26665     WiLD THiNG\n  Poland           Opus              +48-22-188465     WiLD THiNG\n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n    TYPE ''SUG'' AT THESE BOARDS FOR LEAVING YOUR BUG REPORT/SUGGESTIONS\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    > For the quickest answers call Dixie BBS, The Home Of WiLDToolz <\n\nIf  You  want  to  become a beta-tester, call one of these boards above and\nleave detailed information ''bout Your board, system configuration etc.\n\n@endnode\n\n@node tools "Other WiLDToolz"\n                          LooK ouT FoR THe oTHeR \n      ____  ____  ___ __ _______ _____________________   _____________\n     /    /\    \/   \  :       \        /     :      : /    /       /\n    //           \___/  :___     \   ___/ ____ : ____ :/    /___    /____\n    \            /   \      \ /  /    /:       :      :        /   /    /\n     \____/\____/\___/______/___/____/ :_______:______:_______/________/\n\n[----- NAME ------|------ DESCRIPTION -------|------- FEATURES ---------------]\n WiLDRead v0.13   | file/archive/log viewer  | text search\n                  | AIM door                 | file/arc info\n                  |                          | next/prev. page\n                  |                          | page selection\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDNeW v0.5     | new user questionaire    | multilanguage\n                  | AIM door                 | baud checking for questions\n                  |                          | multiple answers\n                  |                          | text comments (internal ed)\n                  |                          | sysop review of new users\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDBull v0.2    | global bulletins         | scroll bar selection\n                  | AIM door                 | all bulls in one dir\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDMenu v0.1    | multi level menus        | all menus in one file\n                  | AIM door                 |\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDKick v0.1    | unwanted users kick out  | show  msg to user & hang up\n                  | AIM door                 |\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDVote v0.10   | vote door                | configurable user add/delete\n                  | AIM door                 | of topics and itemz\n                  |                          | download of result file\n                  |                          | result output with graph bars\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDLiST v0.9    | file LIST dl             | download all filelists from\n                  | XIM door                 | conferences the user has \n                  |                          |  access TO in one file\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n DOS Join v0.2    | J command for DOS        | changes current dir to conf\n                  | tool                     | location; works as /X j just\n                  |                          | for the shell\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDStat v0.4    | Stats door               | replacement the syscmd/s door\n                  | XIM                      | mega-cool access-o-meter\n                  |                          | cookie file\n                  |                          | configurable which part ye want\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n Spar Wall v0.6   | Nice & easy to use wall  | nothing special, select string\n                  | XIM                      | & color\n                  |                          | adds username or anonymous\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n Important v0.1   | forces to read a text    | displays a text for 10 secs \n                  | XIM                      | without the possibility to abort\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLD BBS v0.5    | BBS data base            | handles BBS list, download, add\n                  | XiM                      | handles logoff screen\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDNeW v0.11    | new user questionaire    | multilanguage\n                  | XIM door now             | check answers \n                  | ^^^                      | multiple answers\n                  |                          | text comments (internal ed)\n                  |                          | comfortabel answer viewer\n                  |                          | new user checker, let''s users \n                  |                          |   write a one line comment bout\n                  |                          |   the new ones\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLD MoVeR v0.1  | File/Desc MoVeR          | da best file mover ever\n                  | XiM                      | move files/descs anywhere\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n Stat-X v0.1      | Dir-File Statistics      | show statistics for a dir file\n                  | DOS util                 |\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n Dkiller v0.1     | Strip descriptions       | Stips descriptions and leaves\n                  | DOS util                 | only the first line \n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLD Menu v0.1   | Expansion for W command  | Create different door menus \n                  | XiM                      | (more than one possible, eg\n                  |                          |  for all status doors, all\n                  |                          |  settings doors)\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLD Multi v0.9  | Fastest Dupechecker      | Dupechecker, AutoFree, DirStyle\n                  | XIM, what else ?         | MultiDoorStart &  more\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,145414,19,0,NULL,NULL,'ydl_mu10_multi','scan',1780048843);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ydl_wh01','YDL-WH01.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/YDL-WH01.LHA','h','XIM','______                     _ __ ____',NULL,NULL,'YDL',':  \_   /_________________________\\_ ¬\ : .-''  /   / ¬\_  _  ¬\____  ¬\_ ___ ¬\/   / ¦ `-. /   /  _/   /  _/   /  _/  \____/   /.-''',replace('     ______                     _ __ ____   \n  :  \_   /_________________________\\_ ¬\ :\n.-''  /   / ¬\_  _  ¬\____  ¬\_ ___ ¬\/   / ¦\n`-. /   /  _/   /  _/   /  _/  \____/   /.-''\n.-''_\___   \_______\_______\_______\___/ `-.\n`--\______/--------------------------------''\n+------------------------------------------+                                           \n| PReZeNTZ FRoM Da FaMouS WiLDTooLZ SeRieS |\n:        aN /X 3.x & 4.x XIM DooR          :\n:        WiLD HeLP v0.1 (27/09/94)         :\n. Simple to use & install & expand online  .\n.               Help system                .\n............................................\n','\n',char(10)),'WiLDHeLP.GUiDe',replace('@database WiLDHeLP.guide\n\n@node MAIN "WiLD HeLP v0.1 (c) 09/94  WiLD THiNG/YoDeL"\n\n                      [---> -P- ¥·O·Ð·E·L -P- <---]\n                              presents the\n     ____  ____  ___ __ _______ _____________________   _____________\n    /    /\    \/   \  :       \        /     :      : /    /       /\n   //           \___/  :___     \   ___/ ____ : ____ :/    /___    /____\n   \            /   \      \ /  /    /:       :      :        /   /    /\n    \____/\____/\___/______/___/____/ :_______:______:_______/________/\n                                 SeRieS\n   ====================================================================\n                              WiLD HeLP v0.1\n                     (c) 09/94 by WiLD THiNG/YoDeL\n   ====================================================================\n              @{" Introduction        " link "introduction"} @{" Greetings         " link "greets"}\n              @{" Installation        " link "installation"} @{" Contact           " link "contact"}\n              @{" Other WiLDTooLS     " link "tools"} @{" History           " link "history"}\n\n\n           - READ THIZ DOCS BEFORE ASKING ME STUPID QUESTIONS -\n@endnode\n\n@node introduction "Introduction"\n\nWiLD HeLP is an /X 3.xx & 4.xx XiM door, it''s purpose is to display online\nhelp for any main prompt command, You can expand it at wish.\n\n                have fun and a horny day\n                                         WiLD THiNG/YoDeL\n\n@endnode\n\n@node history\n                 -======================================-\n                               H I S T O R Y\n                 -======================================-\n\n-VeR----ReL.DaTe-----------------------CHaNGeD/uPDaTeD--------------------\n 0.1    27-09-94        first version\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node installation "Installation"\n\n                             _________________  \n                            |~ |___________| ~|\n                            |  |___________|  |\n                            |  |___________|  |\n                            |  |___________|  |\n                            |  |___________|  |\n                            |    _________    |\n                            |   |~_    ~| |   |\n                            |   || |    | |   |\n                            l   || |    | |   |\n                             \_,||_|____|_|___|\n\nWhen You have unpacked this little shit just copy the aedoor.library to yer\nlibs:  and then type copy bbs/* all bbs:  and WoP WiLD HeLP is installed.\n\nThe   dir   doors:wildtools/wildhelp/data/   contains  all  help  files  in\nASCII/ANSI format -> have a look at it and you''ll know what''s up\n\n@endnode\n\n                                           \n@node greets "Greetings & Fuckings"\n                 -======================================-\n                       Greetings go to(in no order)\n                 -======================================-\n\nall   Ex-Mannassas   &  FeaR  members,  Tic.,  R19,  Dragon/Motion,  Vince,\nAndy/Motion,  Sunset, Donald/Motion, Vince, The Generat, Wild Child/Taurus,\nEaZy-E/Taurus,  Zielu/Mad  Elks, uNReaL/Surprise Prod., Easy Rider/Mystic &\nTRSi,  EMPiRE/Mystic,  ByteAndi/TRSi,  Selz/Nova Acies(?), The Trader/FeaR,\nChipsi/Taurus,   Crazy  Squaw,  Calypso/GOD,  KC,  C/\Te¥e/Insane,  all  my\nBeta-Testers, and all others I forgot ....\n                                    ____\n ___________________________________\  /________________________________\n(__________________________________ \\// _______________________________)     \n \_________________________________\ \/ /______________________________/\n                                   \\  //\n                                    \\//\n                                     \/\n\n                     aND  LaZT  BuT  OF CoZ N°T LeaST\n              a BiG, FaT & HaiR¥ GReeT¥ T° a££ M¥ HoRNeD BRoS\n\n                  \n\nFranklin/Termos : YO, (I hate this RAP & similar shit), keep smilin'' & thx\n                  for da fonts\nuFoK/MySTiC     : thx FøR äLL THøZë µPPZ\nDune/FeaR       : YeP that''s ¥ouR ASCii STuFF, ThX aN¥Wa¥\n      /\      Artie/Taurus : hi hope to chat to ye as soon as possible,\n ____/  \____                what about that new stuff ??\n \   /\/\   / Bionic/Yodel : w8in'' for another all-thru-the-night chat\n  \  \/\/  /  Fazer/Razor 1911: I''ll call as soon as I can, promised\n  /        \  Vinzi/Yodel     : Nice  txt in that intro (YC3+4)\n /___ () ___\ SiNTAX/WøT      : ...your examples in E and your AEDoor.library\n     \  /  Wouter van Oortmerssen : ... Amiga E compiler, it''s the BEST\n      \/  Big C & Amiga   : ... the best toy for bored programmers ;-)\n\nRage against ZK : Go on like this\nLogic           : hey yer checkers  are da best \nMystic PL       : Czesc maluchy\nYodel           : hello to all of you, nice intro\n\n                 -======================================-\n                              Fuckings go to\n                 -======================================-\nPolish telecom (TPSA): fucked up assholes\nall you stupid lamers here that even can''t do a simple file description\nZonder Lamando       : fuck yerself\nMcDonald''s           : this McChampion is BuLLSHiT\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node contact "Contact me ..."\n\nCall  these  WiLDToolz Beta-Test and Release Sites for the newest WiLDToolz\nand to drop some suggestions or bug reports:\n\n- Country -------- Board Name ------ Board Numba ----- Write to -----------\n\n  Sweden           Edge Of Sanity    +46-346-81852     WiLD THiNG\n> Poland           Dixie             +48-71-575825     WiLD THiNG <\n  Poland           Opus              +48-22-188465     WiLD THiNG\n  Australia        Nirvana           +61-654-11672     Halloween \n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    > For the quickest answers call Dixie BBS, The Home Of WiLDToolz <\n\n@endnode\n\n@node tools "Other WiLDToolz"\n                          LooK ouT FoR THe oTHeR \n      ____  ____  ___ __ _______ _____________________   _____________\n     /    /\    \/   \  :       \        /     :      : /    /       /\n    //           \___/  :___     \   ___/ ____ : ____ :/    /___    /____\n    \            /   \      \ /  /    /:       :      :        /   /    /\n     \____/\____/\___/______/___/____/ :_______:______:_______/________/\n\n\n[----- NAME ------|------ DESCRIPTION -------|------- FEATURES ---------------]\n WiLDRead v0.13   | file/archive/log viewer  | text search\n                  | AIM door                 | file/arc info\n                  |                          | next/prev. page\n                  |                          | page selection\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDNeW v0.5     | new user questionaire    | multilanguage\n                  | AIM door                 | baud checking for questions\n                  |                          | multiple answers\n                  |                          | text comments (internal ed)\n                  |                          | sysop review of new users\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDBull v0.2    | global bulletins         | scroll bar selection\n                  | AIM door                 | all bulls in one dir\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDMenu v0.1    | multi level menus        | all menus in one file\n                  | AIM door                 |\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDKick v0.1    | unwanted users kick out  | show  msg to user & hang up\n                  | AIM door                 |\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDVote v0.10   | vote door                | configurable user add/delete\n                  | AIM door                 | of topics and itemz\n                  |                          | download of result file\n                  |                          | result output with graph bars\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDLiST v0.9    | file LIST dl             | download all filelists from\n                  | XIM door                 | conferences the user has \n                  |                          |  access TO in one file\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n DOS Join v0.2    | J command for DOS        | changes current dir to conf\n                  | tool                     | location; works as /X j just\n                  |                          | for the shell\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDStat v0.4    | Stats door               | replacement the syscmd/s door\n                  | XIM                      | mega-cool access-o-meter\n                  |                          | cookie file\n                  |                          | configurable which part ye want\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n Spar Wall v0.4   | Nice & easy to use wall  | nothing special, select string\n                  | XIM                      | & color\n                  |                          | adds username \n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n Important v0.1   | forces to read a text    | displays a text for 10 secs \n                  | XIM                      | without the possibility to abort\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLD BBS v0.1    | BBS data base            | handles BBS list, download, add\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDNeW v0.8     | new user questionaire    | multilanguage\n                  | XIM door now             | check answers \n                  | ^^^                      | multiple answers\n                  |                          | text comments (internal ed)\n                  |                          | comfortabel answer viewer\n                  |                          | new user checker, let''s users \n                  |                          |   write a one line comment bout\n                  |                          |   the new ones\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLD MoVeR v0.1  | File/Desc MoVeR          | da best file mover ever\n                  | XiM                      | move files/descs anywhere\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,17667,4,0,NULL,NULL,'ydl_wh01','scan',1780048843);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ydl_wn11','YDL-WN11.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/YDL-WN11.LHA','wildnew','XIM',':::: ::::  .......   ....::::  .......  ::::',NULL,NULL,'YDL',':::: :::: :::: :::: :::: :::: :::: :::: :::: ·:::.:::: :::: :::: :::: :::: ::::.:::: :::: .....:::· ·:::.:::· ·:::.:::: ·:::..... ::::',replace(':::: ::::  .......   ....::::  .......  ::::\n:::: :::: :::: :::: :::: :::: :::: :::: ::::\n·:::.:::: :::: :::: :::: :::: ::::.:::: ::::\n.....:::· ·:::.:::· ·:::.:::: ·:::..... ::::\n+------------------------------------------+                                           \n| PReZeNTZ FRoM Da FaMouS WiLDTooLZ SeRieS |\n:        aN /X 3.x & 4.x XIM DooR          :\n:        WiLD NeW v0.11 (11/09/94)          :\n.   The best New User Checking System ever .\n.User comments on new users, answer viewer,.\n              Many NeW FeaTurES\n............................................\n','\n',char(10)),'WiLDNeW.doc',replace('                            [---> Taurus <---]\n\n                             presents from da\n     ____  ____  ___ __ _______ _____________________   _____________\n    /    /\    \/   \  :       \        /     :      : /    /       /\n   //           \___/  :___     \   ___/ ____ : ____ :/    /___    /____\n   \            /   \      \ /  /    /:       :      :        /   /    /\n    \____/\____/\___/______/___/____/ :_______:______:_______/________/\n                                 SeRieS\n \n===========================================================================\n                               WiLDNeW v0.8\n                          written by WiLD THiNG\n===========================================================================\nThis  is a new questionaire door for new users, it can give some answers or\ncomments on the questions and you can have your questinairs in ANSI and you\ncan have different questions for different baud-rates.  Furthermore you can\nask  new  questions on specified answers (you should now say WOW, no ?  na,\nmaybe   next   time). \n\n Now  you  can  have  your  questions in whatever language you want, i have\nsupplied  with  this  release  an English, Polish and German one, but don''t\nforget that the user will probably answer in the language he has been asked\nif you don''t tell him otherwise.\n\nThe  filled in questionaires will be saved in the WiLDTools/WiLDNew/answers\ndirectory with the user name as filename.\n\nuse  the  BBS  command  ''NEW'' to enter sysop mode and review new user apps,\ndon''t forget to set up the security level for the command.  With a security\nlevel higher than 2oo you will be also able to delete the apps.\n\nConfig file:\n~~~~~~~~~~~~\n(doors:WiLDTools//WiLDNeW/WiLDNew.cfg)\nYes here you must declare which languages you want to have, and the names\nof the quest files \neg.: \n==== cut here ====\nEnglish quest.eng\nPolski quest.pol\nDeutsch quest.ger \n==== cut here ====\nand whatever you want...\n\nWiLDNew will ask which language the user prefers.\n\nThe first two lines are fixed, the rest You can do as You want,\n\neg.:\nEnglish Question File For WiLDNew v0.8 (10/07/94)\n[36mYou [35mMUST[36m answer this question[0m\n\nThe first line is a comment, put here anything you want,\nthe second one is the string which will be printed when a user won''t answer\na question which he MUST answer.\n\n\n\nhere  are the recognition chars for the quest file, they have to be at the\nbeginning of every line:\n\n- print out line\n? Ask question\n§ Ask question which user MUST Answer \n^ Check answer \n+ Call the editor and let the user write you a comment, that \n        comment will be saved in .../answers/username.ext\n=xxxxx ask user with specified baud rate where xxxxx is the rate\n%xxxxx show line only to user calling at xxxxx baud\n\nYou can combine the answer checking with a new question:\n\n?Have you ever heard of WiLDTools ?             - ask question\n^yes                                            - if entered "yes" then\n§Why not ?                                      - user must answer why\n?Is there anything you want to tell me ?\n^yes\n+ext                                            - if the answer is\n                                                  yes - start the\n                                                  editor\n\nLook at the example config file to see some possibilities :)\n\nHaVe PHµN aNÐ Ma¥ Ða Wa®eZ Be WiTH ¥øµ\n\nFor  any  bug reports, improvements or if you''d like me to write a door for\nyou  contact  me  at my board Dixie ++48-71-575825.\n\n\nHistory:\n~~~~~~~~\nv0.1            First Version\nv0.2            added Multilanguage option\nv0.3            some fixes and edit option\nv0.4            sysop mode was added\nv0.4b 25-06-94  fixed sysop mode option, ''NEW'' command works now,  \n                uses now custom ''V'' command TO view apps FOR more \n                convenience\nv0.5  10-07-94  Bugfixes over bugfixes , added ''View By Name'' TO sysop mode,\n                new look\n\n@endnode\n\n                          LooK ouT FoR THe oTHeR \n      ____  ____  ___ __ _______ _____________________   _____________\n     /    /\    \/   \  :       \        /     :      : /    /       /\n    //           \___/  :___     \   ___/ ____ : ____ :/    /___    /____\n    \            /   \      \ /  /    /:       :      :        /   /    /\n     \____/\____/\___/______/___/____/ :_______:______:_______/________/\n\n\n[----- NAME ------|------ DESCRIPTION -------|------- FEATURES ---------------]\n WiLDRead v0.13   | file/archive/log viewer  | text search\n                  | AIM door                 | file/arc info\n                  |                          | next/prev. page\n                  |                          | page selection\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDNeW v0.5     | new user questionaire    | multilanguage\n                  | AIM door                 | baud checking for questions\n                  |                          | multiple answers\n                  |                          | text comments (internal ed)\n                  |                          | sysop review of new users\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDBull v0.2    | global bulletins         | scroll bar selection\n                  | AIM door                 | all bulls in one dir\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDMenu v0.1    | multi level menus        | all menus in one file\n                  | AIM door                 |\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDKick v0.1    | unwanted users kick out  | show  msg to user & hang up\n                  | AIM door                 |\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDVote v0.9    | vote door                | configurable user add/delete\n                  | AIM door                 | of topics and itemz\n                  |                          | download of result file\n                  |                          | result output with graph bars\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDLiST v0.7    | file LIST dl             | download all filelists from\n                  | XIM door                 | conferences the user has \n                  |                          |  access TO in one file\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n Global Zippy     | Zippy command FOR all    | searches all confs for search\n                  | confs                    | string\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n\n\n                 -======================================-\n                           Special thanx for ...\n                 -======================================-\n\nEmpire/Mystic   : well you see, finally got away from that arexx stuff, and\n                  removed the old config and you can select the confs you\n                  want\nByteAndi/MST    : for da kewl stuff, ich hab ne liste mit einigen vielen\n                  bugs und Vorschlaegenn fuer Dich :-)\nGollum          : Thx for da reeeeeaall fast text converison proc\nZiPPER/Yodel    : THX for all\nZielu/Mad Elks  : thx for yer loooooooooong bug reports\nuNReaL/FeaR     : ...all the KeWL ASCII''s\nEasy Rider/MST  : ...beta-testing & fast ''distribution''\n                  and yer beta-testing\nWouter van Oortmerssen : ... Amiga E compiler, it''s the BEST\nSiNTAX/WøT      : ...your examples in E and your AEDoor.library\nBig C & Amiga   : ... the best toy for bored programmers ;-)\n\n                  \n\n\n                 -======================================-\n                       Greetings go to(in no order)\n                 -======================================-\n\n                      all Ex-Mannassas & FeaR members\nTic.,   R19,  Dragon/Motion,  Vince,  Andy/Motion,  Sunset,  Donald/Motion,\nVince,The  Generat, Wild Child/Taurus,EaZy-E/Taurus(ruf mal an, hab was mit\nDir zu schwätze), CatEye/Taurus, Artie/Taurus and all others who want to be\ngreeted...\n\nLogic           : hey yer checkers  are da best \nRage against ZK : Go on like this\n\n                 -======================================-\n                              Fuckings go to\n                 -======================================-\nPolish telecom (TPSA): fucked up assholes\nall you stupid lamers here that even can''t do a simple file description\nZonder Lamando       : fuck yerself ye bloody nazis\n\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,NULL,34632,15,0,NULL,NULL,'ydl_wn11_wildnew','scan',1780048843);
INSERT INTO door_catalog VALUES('ydl_ws04','YDL-WS04.LHA','~/Code/amiexpress_doors/Archives/AmiExpress/YDL-WS04.LHA','ws','XIM','ws',NULL,NULL,'YDL',':  \_   /_________________________\\_ ¬\ : .-''  /   / ¬\_  _  ¬\____  ¬\_ ___ ¬\/   / ¦ `-. /   /  _/   /  _/   /  _/  \____/   /.-''',replace('     ______                     _ __ ____   \n  :  \_   /_________________________\\_ ¬\ :\n.-''  /   / ¬\_  _  ¬\____  ¬\_ ___ ¬\/   / ¦\n`-. /   /  _/   /  _/   /  _/  \____/   /.-''\n.-''_\___   \_______\_______\_______\___/ `-.\n`--\______/--------------------------------''\n+------------------------------------------+\n| PReZeNTZ FRoM Da FaMouS WiLDTooLZ SeRieS |\n:        aN /X 3.x & 4.x XIM DooR          :\n               WiLD STaT v0.4\n  NiCe LooKiN RePLaCeMeNT FoR Da /X STaT \n      NoW FuLLY CoNFiGuRaBle, with cool\n         access-o-meter & cookie file \n','\n',char(10)),'WiLDSTaT.GUiDe',replace('@database WiLDSTaT.guide\n\n@node MAIN "WiLD STaT v0.4 (c) 09/94  WiLD THiNG/YoDeL"\n\n                      [---> -P- ¥·O·Ð·E·L -P- <---]\n                              presents the\n     ____  ____  ___ __ _______ _____________________   _____________\n    /    /\    \/   \  :       \        /     :      : /    /       /\n   //           \___/  :___     \   ___/ ____ : ____ :/    /___    /____\n   \            /   \      \ /  /    /:       :      :        /   /    /\n    \____/\____/\___/______/___/____/ :_______:______:_______/________/\n                                 SeRieS\n   ====================================================================\n                              WiLD STaT v0.4\n                     (c) 09/94 by WiLD THiNG/YoDeL\n   ====================================================================\n              @{" Introduction        " link "introduction"} @{" Greetings         " link "greets"}\n              @{" Installation        " link "installation"} @{" Contact           " link "contact"}\n              @{" Other WiLDTooLS     " link "tools"} @{" History           " link "history"}\n\n\n           - READ THIZ DOCS BEFORE ASKING ME STUPID QUESTIONS -\n@endnode\n\n@node introduction "Introduction"\n\nWiLD  STaT is meant to replace the /X S command.  After logging in /X shows\nsum  statistics  etc.,  but  the outlook of it is quite ugly, so here comes\nWiLD  Stat  and  gives  ya da infos a user needs when he is ready to start,\nmost  import  of  ''coz if the Sysop is chattable or not :-), and as special\nYou have the possibility of using an cookie file.\n\nDISTRIBUTION NOTE: WILDSTAT (c) ToDaY BY WiLD THiNG, IZ FUNWARE, IF YOU\n                   LIKE IT THEN USE IT\n\n                have fun and a horny day\n                                         WiLD THiNG/YoDeL\n\n@endnode\n\n@node history\n                 -======================================-\n                               H I S T O R Y\n                 -======================================-\n\n-VeR----ReL.DaTe-----------------------CHaNGeD/uPDaTeD--------------------\n 0.1    26/05/94        First working version, only ßeta release\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\n 0.2    09/08/94 beta   added da mega-cool ACCESS-O-METER\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\n 0.3    08/09/94 beta   bug fixes, improved error handling\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------\n 0.4    17/09/94 beta   added cookie file, *** CHANGED HOME DIRECTORY ***\n                        configurable via tooltypes\n\n@endnode\n\n@node installation "Installation"\n\n                             _________________  \n                            |~ |___________| ~|\n                            |  |___________|  |\n                            |  |___________|  |\n                            |  |___________|  |\n                            |  |___________|  |\n                            |    _________    |\n                            |   |~_    ~| |   |\n                            |   || |    | |   |\n                            l   || |    | |   |\n                             \_,||_|____|_|___|\n\nWhen You have unpacked this little shit just copy the aedoor.library to yer\nlibs:  and then type copy bbs/* all bbs:  and WoP WiLD STaT is installed.\n(You must be ofcoz in the dir where you unpacked WiLDStat to)\n\nYes, now da config file, easy thing, \nexample:\n---= cut here =--- (doors:wildtools/wildstat/wildstat.cfg)\nSysop\n255\nCosysop\n200\nElite\n100\nLamer\n50\n---= cut here =---\nSo one line the title for the access level, next line the access level, and\nthat are the settings for the ACCESS-O-METER, just check it out.\n\nTHE TOOLTYPES:\nEasy  thing, there are only three, they let u choose which part of WiLDStat\nshall be active, which not, here we go:\n\nAVAIL=YES       Show if Sysop is at home or not\nMETER=YES       Use Access-o-meter\nCOOKIE=YES      Show random line from cookie file\n\nYep, if You want any of them disabled, just kill da line or write anything\nelse then YES, NOTE: ''YES'' MUST BE WRITTEN IN CAPITAL LETTERS\n\nTHE COOKIE FILE (doors:wildtools/wildstat/cookie)\nWiLDStat  will display randomly any line contained in this file (if anyones\ninterested,  WS  gets  the  random  number  from the actual numba of ticks,\nshould be good enough for this purpose)\n\n\n\n\n\n@endnode\n\n                                           \n@node greets "Greetings & Fuckings"\n                 -======================================-\n                       Greetings go to(in no order)\n                 -======================================-\n\nall   Ex-Mannassas   &  FeaR  members,  Tic.,  R19,  Dragon/Motion,  Vince,\nAndy/Motion,  Sunset, Donald/Motion, Vince, The Generat, Wild Child/Taurus,\nEaZy-E/Taurus,  Zielu/Mad  Elks, uNReaL/Surprise Prod., Easy Rider/Mystic &\nTRSi,  EMPiRE/Mystic,  ByteAndi/TRSi,  Selz/Nova Acies(?), The Trader/FeaR,\nChipsi/Taurus,   Crazy  Squaw,  Calypso/GOD,  KC,  C/\Te¥e/Insane,  all  my\nBeta-Testers, and all others I forgot ....\n                                    ____\n ___________________________________\  /________________________________\n(__________________________________ \\// _______________________________)     \n \_________________________________\ \/ /______________________________/\n                                   \\  //\n                                    \\//\n                                     \/\n\n                     aND  LaZT  BuT  OF CoZ N°T LeaST\n              a BiG, FaT & HaiR¥ GReeT¥ T° a££ M¥ HoRNeD BRoS\n\n                  \n\nFranklin/Termos : YO, (I hate this RAP & similar shit), keep smilin'' & thx\n                  for da fonts\nuFoK/MySTiC     : thx FøR äLL THøZë µPPZ\nDune/FeaR       : YeP that''s ¥ouR ASCii STuFF, ThX aN¥Wa¥\n      /\      Artie/Taurus : hi hope to chat to ye as soon as possible,\n ____/  \____                what about that new stuff ??\n \   /\/\   / Bionic/Yodel : w8in'' for another all-thru-the-night chat\n  \  \/\/  /  Fazer/Razor 1911: I''ll call as soon as I can, promised\n  /        \  Vinzi/Yodel     : Nice  txt in that intro (YC3+4)\n /___ () ___\ SiNTAX/WøT      : ...your examples in E and your AEDoor.library\n     \  /  Wouter van Oortmerssen : ... Amiga E compiler, it''s the BEST\n      \/  Big C & Amiga   : ... the best toy for bored programmers ;-)\n\nRage against ZK : Go on like this\nLogic           : hey yer checkers  are da best \nMystic PL       : Czesc maluchy\nYodel           : hello to all of you, nice intro\n\n                 -======================================-\n                              Fuckings go to\n                 -======================================-\nPolish telecom (TPSA): fucked up assholes\nall you stupid lamers here that even can''t do a simple file description\nZonder Lamando       : fuck yerself\nMcDonald''s           : this McChampion is BuLLSHiT\n\n\n@endnode\n\n@node contact "Contact me ..."\n\nCall  these  WiLDToolz Beta-Test and Release Sites for the newest WiLDToolz\nand to drop some suggestions or bug reports:\n\n- Country -------- Board Name ------ Board Numba ----- Write to -----------\n\n  Sweden           Edge Of Sanity    +46-346-81852     WiLD THiNG\n> Poland           Dixie             +48-71-575825     WiLD THiNG <\n  Poland           Opus              +48-22-188465     WiLD THiNG\n  Australia        Nirvana           +61-654-11672     Halloween \n\n---------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n    > For the quickest answers call Dixie BBS, The Home Of WiLDToolz <\n\n@endnode\n\n@node tools "Other WiLDToolz"\n                          LooK ouT FoR THe oTHeR \n      ____  ____  ___ __ _______ _____________________   _____________\n     /    /\    \/   \  :       \        /     :      : /    /       /\n    //           \___/  :___     \   ___/ ____ : ____ :/    /___    /____\n    \            /   \      \ /  /    /:       :      :        /   /    /\n     \____/\____/\___/______/___/____/ :_______:______:_______/________/\n\n\n[----- NAME ------|------ DESCRIPTION -------|------- FEATURES ---------------]\n WiLDRead v0.13   | file/archive/log viewer  | text search\n                  | AIM door                 | file/arc info\n                  |                          | next/prev. page\n                  |                          | page selection\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDNeW v0.5     | new user questionaire    | multilanguage\n                  | AIM door                 | baud checking for questions\n                  |                          | multiple answers\n                  |                          | text comments (internal ed)\n                  |                          | sysop review of new users\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDBull v0.2    | global bulletins         | scroll bar selection\n                  | AIM door                 | all bulls in one dir\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDMenu v0.1    | multi level menus        | all menus in one file\n                  | AIM door                 |\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDKick v0.1    | unwanted users kick out  | show  msg to user & hang up\n                  | AIM door                 |\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDVote v0.10   | vote door                | configurable user add/delete\n                  | AIM door                 | of topics and itemz\n                  |                          | download of result file\n                  |                          | result output with graph bars\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDLiST v0.8    | file LIST dl             | download all filelists from\n                  | XIM door                 | conferences the user has \n                  |                          |  access TO in one file\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n WiLDStat v0.3    | Stats door               | replacement the syscmd/s door\n                  |                          | with mega cool access-o-meter\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n Spar Wall v0.2   | Nice & easy to use wall  | nothing special, select string\n                  | XIM                      | & color\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n Important v0.1   | forces to read a text    | displays a text for 10 secs \n                  | XIM                      | without the possibility to abort\n[-----------------|--------------------------|--------------------------------]\n@endnode\n','\n',char(10)),NULL,'auto-added',21739,7,0,NULL,NULL,'ydl_ws04','scan',1780048843);
