\n[32mTodays Uploads in [33m>> Amiga Elite ! <<[34m :     [0m([35mFiles[33m: [36m@N[0m, [35mFakes[33m: [36m@F, [35mMegs[33m: [36m@M.0[0m)\n[35mYesterdays Statistics [0m: [32m@Y [36mFiles[33m, [32m@Z [36mFakes[33m, [32m@B.0 [36mMegs [33m!\n#\nBBS:Elite/Dir2\n[32mTodays Uploads in [33m>> SNES Only ! <<[34m :       [0m([35mFiles[33m: [36m@N[0m, [35mFakes[33m: [36m@F, [35mMegs[33m: [36m@M.0[0m)\n[35mYesterdays Statistics [0m: [32m@Y [36mFiles[33m, [32m@Z [36mFakes[33m, [32m@B.0 [36mMegs [33m!\n#\nBBS:Consoles/Dir2\n----------------------------(cut here)--------\n\n        \n        You can run the tool from CLI for testing. The output\n        will be sent to your CLI-Window. Install it in your\n        Logoff-Batch using ''>'' to redirect the output to a file !\n\n        E.g. :\n\n        ----------------------------(cut here)--------\n        QuickNew S:QuickNew.Config >BBS:Screens/QuickNew.txt.gr\n        ----------------------------(cut here)--------\n        \n\n        If you call it with different config-files you can make\n        different outputs, e.g. for every conference !\n\n        Example-Outputs are included in the archive !\n\n\n        Now some hints how you can display it in your BBS !\n\n        This is my Node(x)/Bull(x).txt(.gr) :\n\n        ----------------------------(cut here)--------\n        ~SS_BBS:Screens/LastCallers.txt.gr\n        ~SP                               \n        ~SS_BBS:Screens/QuickNew.txt.gr\n        ----------------------------(cut here)--------\n\n        So you can display the Lastcallers and the QuickNew right\n        after each other...        \n\n\nLAST WORDS :\n------------\n        \n        Now have fun with this great tool !\n\n        For Bugs (there are none), Ideas (yeah !) or just for fun\n        call my BBS :\n\n                   bLACK m00N       G·O·D EXPRESS DESIGN WHQ !        \n                  ~~~~~~~~~~~~      L^O^G^I^C wORLDHEADQUARTERS !     \n   